// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — TOEIC Themed Vocabulary
window.TC_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Accident 意外事故","cards":[{"w":"collision","p":"n.","d":"a crash in which two things hit each other","c":"碰撞；相撞","s":"A: Why are all the delivery trucks so late this morning, and why hasn't the warehouse manager answered any of my calls yet? B: There was a collision between two buses on the highway near the factory, so traffic is blocked for miles, and the manager is busy calling customers to explain the delay.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上所有的送貨卡車都這麼晚，而且倉庫經理到現在都還沒接我的電話？ B：工廠附近的高速公路上兩輛公車發生了【碰撞】，所以車流堵塞了好幾英里，經理正忙著打電話向客戶解釋延誤的原因。"},{"w":"crash","p":"n.","d":"an accident in which a vehicle hits something hard","c":"撞車；車禍；墜毀","s":"A: Did the sales manager make it to the conference in Chicago on time, or did someone else have to give his presentation to the clients? B: No, he missed the morning session because a car crash closed the main road to the airport, so he had to take a longer route and catch a later flight.","t":"A：業務經理有準時趕到芝加哥的研討會嗎？還是有別人必須代替他向客戶做簡報？ B：沒有，他錯過了上午的場次，因為一場【車禍】封閉了通往機場的主要道路，所以他只好繞遠路並改搭較晚的班機。"},{"w":"incident","p":"n.","d":"something unusual or bad that happens","c":"事件；事故","s":"A: Should I tell the supervisor that a heavy box fell from the top shelf in the warehouse this afternoon, even though it didn't hit anyone? B: Yes, you should, because every incident must be written down in the safety log, and the supervisor uses those notes to decide which shelves need to be repaired or replaced.","t":"A：今天下午倉庫最上層的架子掉下一個很重的箱子，雖然沒有砸到任何人，我還是應該告訴主管嗎？ B：對，你應該說，因為每一起【事件】都必須記錄在安全日誌裡，主管會根據這些紀錄決定哪些架子需要修理或更換。"},{"w":"mishap","p":"n.","d":"a small accident or piece of bad luck","c":"小意外；小差錯","s":"A: How did the product launch go yesterday, and were the new customers happy with the demonstration of our latest software? B: It went well overall, and most guests were impressed, but there was a small mishap when the projector suddenly stopped working, so we had to present the last part without any slides.","t":"A：昨天的產品發表會進行得如何？新客戶對我們最新軟體的展示滿意嗎？ B：整體很順利，大部分來賓都印象深刻，但投影機突然故障時出了個小【意外】，所以最後一部分我們只好在沒有投影片的情況下報告。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"harm done to a person's body","c":"傷害；受傷","s":"A: Why is Tom working from home this week, and will he still be able to join the client meeting on Thursday afternoon? B: He got a back injury while he was lifting heavy boxes in the storeroom, so his doctor told him to rest for a few days, but he can still join the meeting by video call.","t":"A：湯姆這週為什麼在家工作？他還能參加星期四下午的客戶會議嗎？ B：他在儲藏室搬重箱子時背部【受傷】了，所以醫生要他休息幾天，不過他還是可以透過視訊參加會議。"},{"w":"damage","p":"n.","d":"harm done to a thing so it is broken or worth less","c":"損壞；損害","s":"A: Has the insurance company checked the delivery van yet, and do they know how much the repairs are going to cost us? B: Yes, an agent came this morning to take photos, and he said the damage to the front door and the side mirror will cost about two thousand dollars, which our policy should cover.","t":"A：保險公司檢查過那輛送貨車了嗎？他們知道修理費用大概要花我們多少錢嗎？ B：檢查過了，今天早上有位專員來拍照，他說前門和側後照鏡的【損壞】大約要花兩千元修理，我們的保單應該會理賠。"},{"w":"wound","p":"n.","d":"a cut or hurt place on the body","c":"傷口","s":"A: The new worker on the night shift cut his hand on a sharp metal sheet at the factory. Was it serious, and did anyone help him? B: The company nurse cleaned the wound carefully and covered it with a clean bandage, and then she reminded him to wear protective gloves every time he handles metal parts.","t":"A：夜班的新員工在工廠被一片鋒利的金屬板割傷了手。嚴重嗎？有人幫他處理嗎？ B：公司護士仔細清潔了【傷口】，並用乾淨的繃帶包紮，然後提醒他每次處理金屬零件時都要戴上防護手套。"},{"w":"emergency","p":"n.","d":"a sudden, dangerous situation that needs fast action","c":"緊急情況","s":"A: What should all the visitors and staff do if the fire alarm rings during the board meeting on the twelfth floor this afternoon? B: In an emergency, everyone should stay calm, leave the building by the nearest stairway, and meet in the parking lot, but please do not use the elevators under any circumstances.","t":"A：如果今天下午十二樓開董事會時火災警報響了，所有訪客和員工應該怎麼做？ B：遇到【緊急情況】時，每個人都應該保持冷靜，從最近的樓梯離開大樓，並到停車場集合，但無論如何都請不要搭電梯。"},{"w":"ambulance","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle that takes sick or hurt people to hospital","c":"救護車","s":"A: One of the visitors at the front desk suddenly fainted in the lobby, and she still isn't waking up. What should we do right now? B: Call an ambulance right away, and then ask the security guard to keep the area clear and open the main entrance so the medical team can get in quickly when they arrive.","t":"A：櫃台有位訪客突然在大廳昏倒了，到現在還沒有醒來。我們現在該怎麼辦？ B：馬上叫【救護車】，然後請警衛淨空該區域並打開正門，這樣醫療團隊抵達時就能快速進來。"},{"w":"rescue","p":"v.","d":"to save someone from danger","c":"救援；營救","s":"A: Was anyone trapped inside when the old storage building near the train station caught fire late last night? B: Two security workers were still inside checking the doors, but the firefighters arrived within ten minutes and managed to rescue them before the roof fell down, so both of them are safe now.","t":"A：昨天深夜火車站附近的舊倉庫失火時，有人被困在裡面嗎？ B：有兩名保全人員還在裡面檢查門窗，但消防員在十分鐘內趕到，並在屋頂塌下來之前成功把他們【救出】，所以兩人現在都很安全。"},{"w":"survive","p":"v.","d":"to stay alive or keep going after something bad","c":"倖存；存活；撐過","s":"A: I read in the news about the passenger plane that made an emergency landing near the coast during the storm. Was anyone badly hurt? B: It was a frightening experience for everyone on board, but thanks to the pilot's skill, all the passengers managed to survive, and only a few of them needed to stay in the hospital overnight.","t":"A：我在新聞上看到那架客機在暴風雨中於海岸附近緊急降落。有人受重傷嗎？ B：對機上每個人來說都是很可怕的經歷，但多虧了機長的技術，所有乘客都【倖存】了，只有少數幾人需要在醫院住一晚。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"to fall down suddenly","c":"倒塌；崩塌","s":"A: Why is the parking garage behind our office closed to all employees today, and where are we supposed to park our cars? B: Engineers are worried that part of the second floor could collapse after the heavy rain last weekend, so they are checking the structure today, and staff can use the public parking lot across the street.","t":"A：我們辦公室後面的停車場今天為什麼不開放給所有員工？我們應該把車停在哪裡？ B：工程師擔心上週末大雨過後二樓有一部分可能會【倒塌】，所以他們今天正在檢查結構，員工可以使用對街的公共停車場。"},{"w":"slip","p":"v.","d":"to slide by accident and lose your balance","c":"滑倒；滑跤","s":"A: Why is there a large yellow warning sign in front of the restroom on the third floor, right next to the meeting rooms? B: The cleaner just mopped the floor, and it is still very wet, so the sign warns people that they might slip and fall if they walk too quickly or carry heavy things past the area.","t":"A：三樓洗手間前面、就在會議室旁邊，為什麼放了一個大大的黃色警告標誌？ B：清潔人員剛拖完地，地板還很濕，所以這個標誌是提醒大家，如果走太快或搬重物經過這裡，可能會【滑倒】摔跤。"},{"w":"fall","p":"v.","d":"to drop down to the ground by accident","c":"跌落；掉落；跌倒","s":"A: Why do all the visitors and workers need to wear hard hats as soon as they enter the construction site, even for a short tour? B: Workers on the upper floors sometimes drop small tools, and these tools can fall from a great height, so a helmet protects your head from serious harm, even if you only stay for a few minutes.","t":"A：為什麼所有訪客和工人一進入工地就必須戴安全帽，即使只是短暫參觀也一樣？ B：上層樓的工人有時會掉落小工具，這些工具可能從很高的地方【掉落】，所以即使你只待幾分鐘，安全帽也能保護你的頭部免受嚴重傷害。"},{"w":"trip","p":"v.","d":"to hit your foot on something and almost fall","c":"絆倒；絆到","s":"A: Could you please move these long computer cables away from the walkway before the visitors from the head office arrive this afternoon? B: Sure, I'll do it right now, because someone could easily trip over them and get hurt, and the safety inspector is also coming at three o'clock to check every department on this floor.","t":"A：總公司的訪客今天下午抵達之前，能請你把這些長長的電腦線從走道移開嗎？ B：當然，我馬上處理，因為很容易有人被它們【絆倒】而受傷，而且安全檢查員三點也會來檢查這層樓的每個部門。"},{"w":"careless","p":"adj.","d":"not paying enough attention; not careful","c":"粗心的；不小心的","s":"A: How did the forklift hit the metal shelf in the warehouse, and were any of the boxes of new phones damaged? B: The driver was careless and kept looking at his phone while he was driving, so he hit the shelf and broke six boxes, and the manager gave him a written warning this morning.","t":"A：堆高機怎麼會撞上倉庫的金屬貨架？有任何一箱新手機受損嗎？ B：司機很【粗心】，開車時一直看手機，所以撞上了貨架並弄壞了六箱貨，經理今天早上給了他書面警告。"},{"w":"dangerous","p":"adj.","d":"likely to hurt someone or cause harm","c":"危險的","s":"A: Is it okay to store these boxes of cleaning chemicals next to the heater in the back room until the supplier picks them up next week? B: No, that is very dangerous because those chemicals can catch fire easily when they get hot, so please move them to the cool storage room downstairs and keep the door locked.","t":"A：在供應商下週來取貨之前，可以把這幾箱清潔化學藥品放在後面房間的暖氣旁邊嗎？ B：不行，那非常【危險】，因為那些化學藥品變熱時很容易起火，所以請把它們移到樓下陰涼的儲藏室，並把門鎖好。"},{"w":"serious","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and worrying","c":"嚴重的","s":"A: I heard there was an accident at the factory last week. Was it serious, and will production be stopped for a long time? B: Fortunately not, because the two workers only had small cuts on their hands, but the machine was badly damaged, so the production line will be closed until a new one arrives next Monday.","t":"A：我聽說上週工廠發生了事故。情況【嚴重】嗎？生產線會停工很久嗎？ B：幸好不嚴重，那兩名員工手上只有小割傷，但機器嚴重損壞，所以生產線會關閉，直到下週一新機器送達為止。"},{"w":"minor","p":"adj.","d":"small and not very serious","c":"輕微的；次要的","s":"A: Do we need to cancel the company trip to the mountains because of the bus accident this morning, or can we still go? B: No, it was only a minor accident in the parking lot and nobody was hurt, and the bus company is sending another vehicle, so we can still leave on time after lunch.","t":"A：因為今天早上遊覽車發生事故，我們需要取消公司的山區旅遊嗎？還是仍然可以去？ B：不用，那只是停車場裡一起【輕微的】事故，沒有人受傷，而且客運公司會另派一輛車，所以我們午餐後還是可以準時出發。"},{"w":"unexpected","p":"adj.","d":"not expected; surprising","c":"意外的；出乎意料的","s":"A: Why did the shipment of electronic parts from Japan arrive three days late, and did our customers complain about the delay? B: There was an unexpected storm along the coast, so the ship had to wait in the port until the weather improved, and we sent an email to every customer to explain the situation.","t":"A：從日本來的那批電子零件為什麼晚了三天才到？我們的客戶有抱怨延誤嗎？ B：沿海出現了一場【出乎意料的】暴風雨，所以船只好在港口等到天氣好轉，我們也寄了電子郵件給每位客戶說明情況。"},{"w":"suddenly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without any warning","c":"突然地","s":"A: What happened during the sales presentation this morning? Some people said the meeting room became very dark. B: The lights suddenly went out in the whole building because of a power problem, so we had to finish the meeting with only the light from our laptops, and the clients thought it was quite funny.","t":"A：今天早上的業務簡報發生了什麼事？有些人說會議室變得很暗。 B：因為電力問題，整棟大樓的燈【突然】熄滅了，所以我們只好靠筆電的光把會議開完，客戶們覺得還蠻好笑的。"},{"w":"fortunately","p":"adv.","d":"luckily; used before good news","c":"幸運地；幸好","s":"A: I heard that a delivery truck hit the front gate of our office building early this morning. Was anyone hurt in the accident? B: Yes, the gate was badly damaged, but fortunately, nobody was standing near it at that time, and the driver was not hurt either, so we only need to call a repair company today.","t":"A：我聽說今天一大早有輛送貨卡車撞上了我們辦公大樓的大門。有人在事故中受傷嗎？ B：有，大門嚴重損壞，但【幸好】當時沒有人站在附近，司機也沒有受傷，所以我們今天只需要打電話找維修公司就好。"},{"w":"unfortunately","p":"adv.","d":"sadly; used before bad news","c":"不幸地；遺憾地","s":"A: Will Ms. Lin still be able to give her speech at the marketing conference tomorrow morning, or should we change the schedule? B: unfortunately, she hurt her ankle while she was jogging in the park last night, so her assistant will speak in her place, and we don't need to change the schedule at all.","t":"A：林小姐明天早上還能在行銷研討會上演講嗎？還是我們應該更改議程？ B：【很遺憾】，她昨晚在公園慢跑時扭傷了腳踝，所以會由她的助理代替她發言，我們完全不需要更改議程。"},{"w":"carefully","p":"adv.","d":"with close attention so you don't make mistakes or get hurt","c":"小心地；仔細地","s":"A: Is there anything important I should know before I start using the new cutting machine in the workshop for the first time? B: Yes, read the instructions carefully before you turn it on, and always wear safety glasses and gloves, because small pieces of metal can fly out and hurt your eyes or hands.","t":"A：我第一次使用工作坊裡那台新的切割機之前，有什麼重要的事情是我應該知道的嗎？ B：有，開機前要【仔細地】閱讀說明書，而且一定要戴上護目鏡和手套，因為小金屬碎片可能會飛出來傷到你的眼睛或手。"},{"w":"witness","p":"n.","d":"a person who sees something happen","c":"目擊者；證人","s":"A: Did anyone see the car hit the bicycle outside our store this afternoon? The police officer wants to speak to someone who was there. B: Yes, one of our cashiers was a witness because she was standing by the window, and she has already told the police officer exactly what she saw before the ambulance came.","t":"A：今天下午有人看到那輛車在我們店外撞上腳踏車嗎？警察想找當時在場的人談一談。 B：有，我們的一位收銀員是【目擊者】，因為她當時站在窗邊，她已經在救護車來之前把看到的情況詳細告訴警察了。"},{"w":"report","p":"v.","d":"to tell a person in charge about something that happened","c":"報告；通報","s":"A: What should I do if I see broken equipment in the laboratory, especially if other people are planning to use it later in the day? B: You should report the problem to the safety officer immediately, and you should also put a \"Do Not Use\" sign on the equipment so that nobody touches it before it is repaired.","t":"A：如果我在實驗室看到損壞的設備，尤其是其他人當天稍後還打算使用時，我該怎麼做？ B：你應該立刻向安全負責人【通報】這個問題，並在設備上貼上「請勿使用」的標示，這樣在修好之前就不會有人碰它。"},{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the facts about something","c":"調查","s":"A: Does anyone know why the machine on Line 3 caught fire yesterday, and is it safe for the workers to go back to that area? B: Not yet, but the safety team will investigate the problem this week, and they will share their findings with all staff, so please keep Line 3 closed until they finish their report.","t":"A：有人知道昨天三號生產線的機器為什麼起火嗎？工人回到那個區域安全嗎？ B：還不知道，但安全小組本週會【調查】這個問題，並將結果告知全體員工，所以在他們完成報告之前，請讓三號生產線保持關閉。"},{"w":"cause","p":"n.","d":"the reason why something happens","c":"原因；起因","s":"A: Have the engineers found out why the elevator stopped between the fifth and sixth floors yesterday with six people inside? B: Yes, they said the cause was an electrical problem in the control box, and the elevator will be fixed by Friday, so please use the stairs or the other elevator until then.","t":"A：工程師查出昨天電梯為什麼載著六個人卡在五樓和六樓之間了嗎？ B：查出來了，他們說【原因】是控制箱的電力問題，電梯會在星期五前修好，所以在那之前請走樓梯或使用另一部電梯。"},{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"預防；防止","s":"A: Why are we putting new rubber mats at the main entrance and in front of the elevators on the first floor this week? B: The mats will help prevent accidents on rainy days, because the floor near the doors gets very wet and slippery, and last month two customers almost fell while they were walking in.","t":"A：我們這週為什麼要在一樓正門和電梯前面鋪新的橡膠地墊？ B：這些地墊有助於【預防】雨天發生意外，因為門口附近的地板會變得又濕又滑，上個月就有兩位客戶走進來時差點跌倒。"},{"w":"safety","p":"n.","d":"the state of being safe from danger or harm","c":"安全","s":"A: Do new employees have to attend any training before they start working on the production floor, or can they begin right away? B: Everyone must attend a safety workshop on the first day, where they learn how to use the fire extinguishers, where the emergency exits are, and what to do if someone gets hurt.","t":"A：新進員工在生產線開始工作之前必須參加任何訓練嗎？還是可以馬上開始？ B：每個人第一天都必須參加【安全】研習，學習如何使用滅火器、緊急出口在哪裡，以及有人受傷時該怎麼做。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to get well again after being sick or hurt","c":"康復；恢復","s":"A: When will Mr. Chen come back to the office after his car accident, and who is taking care of his projects right now? B: His doctor says he needs about two weeks to recover, so the three of us on his team will share his projects until he returns, and he will answer emails from home when he feels better.","t":"A：陳先生出車禍後什麼時候會回辦公室？現在由誰負責他的專案？ B：他的醫生說他大約需要兩週時間【康復】，所以在他回來之前，我們團隊三個人會分擔他的專案，等他感覺好一點時會在家回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"shock","p":"n.","d":"a sudden, strong feeling of surprise or fear after something bad","c":"震驚；驚嚇","s":"A: How is the delivery driver who was in the accident on Main Street this morning? I heard his truck was badly damaged. B: He was not badly hurt, but he was in shock for a while and could not answer questions clearly, so the paramedics kept him in the ambulance until he felt calm enough to talk.","t":"A：今天早上在緬因街出車禍的那位送貨司機還好嗎？我聽說他的卡車嚴重損壞。 B：他沒有受重傷，但有一段時間處於【驚嚇】狀態，無法清楚回答問題，所以急救人員讓他待在救護車上，直到他冷靜到可以說話為止。"},{"w":"treatment","p":"n.","d":"medical care for an illness or injury","c":"治療","s":"A: Does our company insurance pay for hospital costs if an employee gets hurt in an accident while working at the factory? B: Yes, it covers all medical treatment for injuries at work, including doctor visits and medicine, but you must fill out the claim forms and submit them to the HR office within thirty days.","t":"A：如果員工在工廠工作時發生意外受傷，公司的保險會支付醫療費用嗎？ B：會，它涵蓋所有工作傷害的醫療【治療】費用，包括看診和藥品，但你必須填寫理賠表格，並在三十天內交給人資辦公室。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars and other vehicles on a road","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: Should we leave for the airport now to meet the clients from Singapore, or can we finish this report first? B: We should leave right away, because there was an accident on the bridge an hour ago, so the traffic will be heavy all the way to the airport, and we don't want the clients to wait for us.","t":"A：我們現在該出發去機場接新加坡來的客戶了嗎？還是可以先把這份報告完成？ B：我們應該馬上出發，因為一小時前橋上發生了事故，所以到機場一路上【交通】都會很擁擠，我們可不想讓客戶等我們。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Accommodation 住宿","cards":[{"w":"currently","p":"adv.","d":"at the present time","c":"目前；現在","s":"A: Is the company still looking for a new office in the city center, or has the manager decided to stay in this old building for another year? B: We are currently renting a small floor near the train station while the agents search for a larger space with better parking for our staff and visitors.","t":"A：公司還在市中心找新辦公室嗎？還是經理已經決定在這棟舊大樓再待一年？ B：我們【目前】在火車站附近租了一個小樓層，同時仲介正在幫我們找一個更大、讓員工和訪客停車更方便的空間。"},{"w":"afford","p":"v.","d":"to have enough money to pay for something","c":"負擔得起；買得起","s":"A: Are you going to buy that two-bedroom flat near your office, since you said last month that the rent you pay now is far too high? B: I would love to, but I can't afford such a large down payment this year, so I plan to save more money and look again next spring.","t":"A：你要買你辦公室附近那間兩房公寓嗎？你上個月說現在付的房租太高了。 B：我很想買，但今年我無法【負擔】這麼高的頭期款，所以我打算多存點錢，明年春天再看看。"},{"w":"yard","p":"n.","d":"an area of land next to a house, often with grass","c":"院子；庭院","s":"A: Why did your family choose the older house on Maple Street instead of the new apartment downtown, even though the drive to work is much longer? B: The house has a large yard where our children can play safely after school, and there is enough room for a small vegetable garden and our dog.","t":"A：為什麼你們家選擇楓樹街那間比較舊的房子，而不是市中心的新公寓，即使開車上班要久得多？ B：那間房子有一個大【院子】，孩子們放學後可以在那裡安全地玩耍，而且還有足夠的空間弄一個小菜園和養我們的狗。"},{"w":"veranda","p":"n.","d":"a covered area with a roof along the outside of a house","c":"有頂的走廊；陽台","s":"A: Where should we serve coffee to the guests after the hotel tour this afternoon, since the weather report says it might rain a little later? B: Let's use the veranda at the front of the main building, because it has a roof to keep everyone dry, comfortable chairs, and a lovely view of the lake.","t":"A：今天下午飯店導覽結束後，我們應該在哪裡請客人喝咖啡？氣象報告說晚一點可能會下點雨。 B：我們就用主建築前面的【有頂走廊】吧，因為它有屋頂可以讓大家不被淋濕，有舒服的椅子，還能看到湖的美景。"},{"w":"spot","p":"n.","d":"a particular place","c":"地點；場所","s":"A: Have you found a good place to stay for the sales conference next month, or are all the hotels near the convention center already fully booked? B: I found a quiet spot just ten minutes away by subway, and it has a free breakfast, fast internet, and a small meeting room we can use.","t":"A：你找到下個月業務會議期間的好住處了嗎？還是會展中心附近的飯店都已經訂滿了？ B：我找到一個安靜的【地點】，搭地鐵只要十分鐘，而且有免費早餐、快速網路，還有一間我們可以使用的小會議室。"},{"w":"outskirts","p":"n.","d":"the outer areas of a town or city","c":"郊區；市郊","s":"A: Why is the new factory so far from the city center, when most of the workers live downtown and have to take two buses every morning? B: Land on the outskirts of town is much cheaper, so the company could build a bigger site, and it will run a free shuttle bus for staff starting next month.","t":"A：為什麼新工廠離市中心這麼遠？大部分工人都住在市區，每天早上得搭兩班公車。 B：城鎮【郊區】的土地便宜很多，所以公司能蓋更大的廠區，而且從下個月開始會為員工提供免費接駁車。"},{"w":"uniquely","p":"adv.","d":"in a special way that is unlike any other","c":"獨特地；獨一無二地","s":"A: What makes this boutique hotel so popular with business travelers, even though its room prices are higher than the chain hotels nearby? B: Each room is uniquely designed by a local artist, and guests also enjoy free laundry service, a quiet work area, and a personal welcome from the friendly owner.","t":"A：為什麼這間精品飯店這麼受商務旅客歡迎，雖然它的房價比附近的連鎖飯店還貴？ B：每間房間都是由當地藝術家【獨特地】設計的，而且客人還能享受免費洗衣服務、安靜的工作區，以及友善老闆的親自歡迎。"},{"w":"patio","p":"n.","d":"a flat paved area outside a building for sitting or eating","c":"露台；戶外平台","s":"A: Where are we having the team lunch on Friday, since the cafeteria is closed for repairs and the conference room is too small for everyone? B: The manager booked a restaurant with a large patio behind the building, so we can eat outdoors under umbrellas and enjoy the warm weather together.","t":"A：星期五的團隊午餐我們要在哪裡吃？員工餐廳因為維修關閉，會議室又太小，容納不下所有人。 B：經理訂了一家餐廳，建築後面有一個大【露台】，所以我們可以在陽傘下戶外用餐，一起享受溫暖的天氣。"},{"w":"port","p":"n.","d":"a town or place with a harbor where ships load and unload","c":"港口；港市","s":"A: Why did the shipping company move its main office out of the capital last year, when most of its clients are still based there? B: The managers wanted to be close to the busy port where our cargo ships arrive, so they can check deliveries quickly and solve problems with customs officers in person.","t":"A：為什麼那家航運公司去年把總部搬出首都？它大部分的客戶都還在那裡。 B：經理們想靠近我們貨船抵達的繁忙【港口】，這樣他們就能快速檢查貨物，並親自和海關人員解決問題。"},{"w":"barbeque","p":"n.","d":"an outdoor meal where food is cooked over a fire","c":"烤肉；烤肉聚會","s":"A: How are we going to welcome the new employees who joined the sales department this month, since many of them have not met the rest of the staff yet? B: We are planning a barbeque in the park next Saturday afternoon, and the company will pay for the meat, drinks, and games for everyone's families.","t":"A：我們要怎麼歡迎這個月加入業務部的新員工？他們很多人都還沒見過其他同事。 B：我們計劃下星期六下午在公園辦一場【烤肉聚會】，公司會出錢買肉、飲料，還會為大家的家人準備遊戲。"},{"w":"apartment block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large building divided into many flats","c":"公寓大樓","s":"A: Where will the new engineers from overseas live when they arrive next month, since the hotels near the office are very expensive for long stays? B: The company rented ten units in a new apartment block across the street, so they can walk to work, share a gym, and get help from the building manager.","t":"A：海外來的新工程師下個月抵達後要住在哪裡？辦公室附近的飯店長期住宿非常貴。 B：公司在對街一棟新的【公寓大樓】租了十個單位，這樣他們可以走路上班、共用健身房，還能得到大樓管理員的協助。"},{"w":"back garden","p":"n.phr.","d":"the garden behind a house","c":"後花園；後院","s":"A: Why are you working from home every Friday now, when you used to come into the office five days a week without any problems? B: My manager agreed that I could use the quiet office I built in my back garden, so I can focus on reports without noise and save two hours of driving.","t":"A：為什麼你現在每個星期五都在家工作？你以前一週五天進辦公室都沒問題啊。 B：我的主管同意我使用我在【後花園】蓋的安靜辦公室，這樣我可以在沒有噪音的情況下專心寫報告，還能省下兩小時的開車時間。"},{"w":"detached house","p":"n.phr.","d":"a house that stands alone and is not joined to another","c":"獨棟房屋","s":"A: Are you and your wife still looking at small flats in the city, or have you changed your plans since the baby was born last spring? B: We now want a detached house with three bedrooms, because we need more space and privacy, and we don't want to share walls with noisy neighbors anymore.","t":"A：你和太太還在看城裡的小公寓嗎？還是去年春天寶寶出生後你們改變計畫了？ B：我們現在想要一間有三個房間的【獨棟房屋】，因為我們需要更多空間和隱私，也不想再和吵鬧的鄰居共用牆壁了。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區；近郊住宅區","s":"A: Why does Ms. Chen take the early train every morning, even though our meetings usually don't start until ten o'clock? B: She lives in a quiet suburb about forty minutes from the city, so she leaves early to avoid crowded trains and uses the extra time to answer her emails.","t":"A：為什麼陳小姐每天早上都搭早班火車？我們的會議通常十點才開始。 B：她住在離城市大約四十分鐘車程的安靜【郊區】，所以她提早出門以避開擁擠的列車，並利用多出來的時間回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"terraced house","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of a row of houses that are joined together","c":"連棟房屋；排屋","s":"A: What kind of home did you finally choose when you moved to London for your new job at the bank last autumn? B: I rented a small terraced house in a row of old brick homes, and although the walls are shared, it is cheaper than a flat and close to the underground station.","t":"A：你去年秋天為了銀行的新工作搬到倫敦時，最後選了什麼樣的住處？ B：我在一排老舊的磚造房子中租了一間小【連棟房屋】，雖然牆壁是共用的，但比公寓便宜，而且離地鐵站很近。"},{"w":"dream home","p":"n.phr.","d":"the perfect house that someone has always wanted","c":"夢想中的家","s":"A: Why have you been working so much overtime and saving almost all of your salary since the beginning of the year? B: My husband and I found our dream home near the beach, with big windows and a sunny kitchen, and we need a larger down payment before the bank will approve our loan.","t":"A：為什麼你從年初開始就一直加班，還把幾乎所有薪水都存起來？ B：我先生和我在海邊附近找到了我們【夢想中的家】，有大窗戶和陽光充足的廚房，在銀行核准貸款前我們需要更多頭期款。"},{"w":"layout","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of a place are arranged","c":"格局；佈局；配置","s":"A: Did the clients like the new office building they visited yesterday, or do they still want to look at other places before signing the lease? B: They loved the open layout, because the desks, meeting rooms, and kitchen are arranged so that teams can easily talk, share ideas, and work together.","t":"A：客戶喜歡他們昨天參觀的新辦公大樓嗎？還是他們在簽租約前還想看看其他地方？ B：他們很喜歡那個開放式的【格局】，因為辦公桌、會議室和廚房的配置讓各團隊可以輕鬆交談、分享想法並一起工作。"},{"w":"troublesome","p":"adj.","d":"causing problems or worry","c":"麻煩的；棘手的","s":"A: Why did you decide to move out of your old flat downtown before your lease ended, even though the rent was very reasonable? B: The heating system was troublesome all winter, and the landlord took weeks to send someone to fix it, so I often had to work at home in my coat.","t":"A：為什麼你在租約到期前就決定搬離市區的舊公寓？雖然房租很合理。 B：暖氣系統整個冬天都很【麻煩】，房東要好幾週才派人來修，所以我在家工作時常常得穿著外套。"},{"w":"fully-furnished","p":"adj.","d":"having all the furniture that is needed","c":"家具齊全的","s":"A: What should I bring when I move to Singapore for the six-month project, since I don't want to ship too many heavy boxes? B: Don't worry, the company has booked you a fully-furnished apartment with a bed, sofa, desk, and kitchen tools, so you only need your clothes and your laptop.","t":"A：我搬去新加坡做六個月的專案時該帶什麼？我不想運太多很重的箱子。 B：別擔心，公司已經幫你訂了一間【家具齊全的】公寓，有床、沙發、書桌和廚房用具，所以你只需要帶衣服和筆電。"},{"w":"hall of residence","p":"n.phr.","d":"a building where university students live","c":"大學宿舍；學生宿舍","s":"A: Where did the summer interns from the local university stay while they worked at our head office for eight weeks this year? B: They lived in a hall of residence on campus, which was cheap and near the bus line, and they shared meals there with students working at other companies too.","t":"A：今年在我們總公司工作八週的當地大學暑期實習生住在哪裡？ B：他們住在校園內的【學生宿舍】，價格便宜又靠近公車路線，而且他們也在那裡和在其他公司工作的學生一起吃飯。"},{"w":"home comforts","p":"n.phr.","d":"things that make life at home easy and pleasant","c":"居家的舒適；家中的便利","s":"A: Do you enjoy staying in hotels during your long business trips, or do you get tired of living out of a suitcase for weeks? B: I usually miss my home comforts, like my own soft pillow, my coffee machine, and cooking my own dinner, so I try to book serviced apartments instead.","t":"A：你長期出差時喜歡住飯店嗎？還是連續好幾週靠一只行李箱過活會讓你感到疲倦？ B：我通常會想念【居家的舒適】，像是我自己的軟枕頭、咖啡機，還有自己煮晚餐，所以我會盡量改訂服務式公寓。"},{"w":"house-warming party","p":"n.phr.","d":"a party to celebrate moving into a new home","c":"喬遷派對；暖屋派對","s":"A: What are you doing this Saturday evening, since several of us from the marketing team are going out for dinner after the trade show? B: I can't join you because Kevin from accounting just bought a new flat, and he invited the whole department to his house-warming party to see the place.","t":"A：你這個星期六晚上要做什麼？我們行銷團隊幾個人在商展結束後要出去吃晚餐。 B：我沒辦法跟你們去，因為會計部的凱文剛買了新公寓，他邀請整個部門去參加他的【喬遷派對】看看新家。"},{"w":"exhausting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel very tired","c":"令人筋疲力盡的","s":"A: How was your move to the new office building last weekend, and did the moving company arrive on time with enough workers? B: It was exhausting, because the elevator broke in the morning, so we had to carry dozens of boxes up five floors, and I slept for twelve hours afterward.","t":"A：你們上週末搬到新辦公大樓的情況如何？搬家公司有準時帶足夠的工人來嗎？ B：真是【令人筋疲力盡】，因為電梯早上壞了，我們只好把幾十個箱子搬上五樓，之後我睡了十二個小時。"},{"w":"move into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start living or working in a new place","c":"搬進；遷入","s":"A: When can the accounting team start using the new office space on the third floor, since they are working in the crowded meeting room right now? B: The painters will finish on Thursday, so the team can move into the new space next Monday, after the IT staff set up the phones and computers.","t":"A：會計團隊什麼時候可以開始使用三樓的新辦公空間？他們現在正在擁擠的會議室裡工作。 B：油漆工星期四會完工，所以在資訊人員裝好電話和電腦之後，團隊下星期一就可以【搬進】新空間。"},{"w":"chill out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to relax and rest","c":"放鬆；休息","s":"A: What do you usually do after a long week of meetings and deadlines, since you always look so calm and fresh on Monday mornings? B: I like to chill out on my balcony with a good book and some music, and I turn off my work phone so nobody can bother me all weekend.","t":"A：在經歷了一整週的會議和截止期限後，你通常會做什麼？你每個星期一早上看起來總是很冷靜又有精神。 B：我喜歡在陽台上看本好書、聽點音樂來【放鬆】，而且我會關掉工作手機，這樣整個週末就沒人能打擾我。"},{"w":"permanent address","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place where you live long-term, used on official forms","c":"永久地址；戶籍地址","s":"A: Which address should I write on this job application form, since I am staying in a hotel until I find a flat in the city? B: Please give your permanent address, such as your family home, so the human resources office can send your contract and tax documents to a place that won't change.","t":"A：在這張求職申請表上我應該寫哪個地址？我在城裡找到公寓之前都住在飯店。 B：請填寫你的【永久地址】，例如你的老家，這樣人資部才能把你的合約和稅務文件寄到一個不會變動的地方。"},{"w":"ideal home","p":"n.phr.","d":"the best possible home for someone","c":"理想的家","s":"A: What is the main goal of the new housing project that our construction company is building near the river next year? B: We want to create the ideal home for young families, with safe parks, good schools nearby, energy-saving windows, and prices that most local workers can really pay each month.","t":"A：我們建設公司明年要在河邊蓋的新住宅案，主要目標是什麼？ B：我們想為年輕家庭打造【理想的家】，有安全的公園、附近有好學校、節能窗戶，而且價格是大部分當地上班族每個月真的付得起的。"},{"w":"single room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room for one person","c":"單人房","s":"A: Should I book a double room for the training course in Tokyo, or will I be sharing with someone else from our branch office? B: The company only pays for a single room for each employee, so you will have your own space, but it is quite small and has just one bed and a desk.","t":"A：東京的培訓課程我該訂雙人房嗎？還是我會和分公司的其他人同住？ B：公司只為每位員工支付一間【單人房】的費用，所以你會有自己的空間，但房間很小，只有一張床和一張書桌。"},{"w":"spacious room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room with a lot of space","c":"寬敞的房間","s":"A: Why did the managers choose this hotel for the annual training workshop instead of the cheaper one near the airport? B: This hotel offered a spacious room that can hold eighty people with tables, a large screen, and good lighting, while the other one only had small meeting areas for groups of ten.","t":"A：為什麼主管們選這間飯店舉辦年度培訓工作坊，而不是機場附近比較便宜的那間？ B：這間飯店提供了一間能容納八十人、配有桌子、大螢幕和良好照明的【寬敞房間】，而另一間只有供十人小組使用的小型會議區。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and pleasant","c":"舒適溫暖的；溫馨的","s":"A: How do you like the small café the company opened on the ground floor for staff who want a break from their desks? B: It feels very cozy, with soft chairs, warm lights, and a small bookshelf, so many of us go there to relax or have quiet meetings in the afternoon.","t":"A：你覺得公司在一樓為想離開辦公桌休息的員工開的小咖啡館怎麼樣？ B：感覺非常【溫馨舒適】，有柔軟的椅子、溫暖的燈光和一個小書架，所以我們很多人下午都會去那裡放鬆或開安靜的會議。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Achievement 成就","cards":[{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"the good result of doing what you planned to do","c":"成功","s":"A: Why did the director invite the whole sales team to a dinner at the hotel restaurant last Friday evening? B: She wanted to celebrate the success of our new product launch, because we sold twice as many units as we expected in the first month, and she believed everyone deserved a reward for their hard work.","t":"A：主管為什麼上週五晚上邀請整個業務團隊到飯店餐廳吃晚餐？ B：她想慶祝我們新產品上市的【成功】，因為第一個月的銷量是我們預期的兩倍，而且她認為每個人的努力都值得獎勵。"},{"w":"accomplish","p":"v.","d":"to finish something successfully","c":"完成；達成","s":"A: Do you think our small team can finish the whole website redesign before the client meeting next Thursday afternoon? B: If we divide the work carefully, stay focused, and avoid long meetings this week, I believe we can accomplish the task on time, even though two designers are still on vacation until Monday.","t":"A：你覺得我們這個小團隊能在下週四下午的客戶會議前完成整個網站改版嗎？ B：如果我們仔細分工、保持專注，並且這週避免開冗長的會議，我相信我們能準時【完成】這項任務，雖然有兩位設計師休假到星期一。"},{"w":"attain","p":"v.","d":"to reach a goal or level after a lot of effort","c":"達到；獲得","s":"A: Why is the factory manager asking every worker to attend extra safety training on Saturday mornings this month? B: The company wants to attain an international quality certificate by the end of the year, and the inspectors will check whether every employee understands the new safety rules before they visit the factory.","t":"A：為什麼工廠經理這個月要求每位工人星期六早上參加額外的安全訓練？ B：公司想在年底前【取得】一張國際品質認證，而檢查人員來工廠前會確認每位員工是否了解新的安全規定。"},{"w":"milestone","p":"n.","d":"an important event or stage in the development of something","c":"里程碑；重要階段","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office wearing party hats and eating cake in the meeting room this afternoon? B: Our online store just reached one million customers, which is an important milestone for a company that started in a tiny garage only five years ago, so the boss ordered snacks for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午辦公室裡每個人都戴著派對帽、在會議室吃蛋糕？ B：我們的網路商店剛達到一百萬名顧客，對一家五年前才在小車庫創立的公司來說，這是一個重要的【里程碑】，所以老闆幫大家訂了點心。"},{"w":"fulfillment","p":"n.","d":"a happy feeling that comes from doing something useful or important","c":"成就感；滿足感","s":"A: Why did you leave your well-paid job at the bank to become a teacher at a small community center last year? B: The salary was great, but I never felt any real fulfillment there, and now I feel happy every day because I can see my students improving and using English confidently at work.","t":"A：你去年為什麼辭掉銀行的高薪工作，去一間小社區中心當老師？ B：那裡薪水很好，但我從沒感到真正的【成就感】，現在我每天都很快樂，因為我能看到學生進步，並在工作上自信地使用英文。"},{"w":"triumph","p":"n.","d":"a great success or victory","c":"勝利；巨大成功","s":"A: How did the new marketing manager react when she heard that the company had signed the contract with the Japanese buyer? B: She called it a real triumph for the whole department, because three other companies had also wanted the deal, and our team worked late every night for two months to prepare the proposal.","t":"A：新任行銷經理聽到公司和日本買家簽約時有什麼反應？ B：她說這是整個部門的一大【勝利】，因為另外三家公司也想拿到這筆生意，而我們團隊連續兩個月每晚加班準備提案。"},{"w":"excel","p":"v.","d":"to be very good at something","c":"擅長；表現出色","s":"A: Why did the human resources department choose Kevin to lead the customer service training program for new employees this year? B: He has always been able to excel at solving difficult problems with angry customers, and he explains things in a calm, friendly way that helps new staff feel relaxed and confident.","t":"A：人資部門今年為什麼選凱文來負責新進員工的客服訓練課程？ B：他一向【擅長】處理憤怒顧客的棘手問題，而且他會用冷靜友善的方式解釋事情，讓新員工感到放鬆又有自信。"},{"w":"progress","p":"n.","d":"movement toward finishing or improving something","c":"進展；進步","s":"A: The construction company promised that the new office building would be ready in March, so why are we still working from the old one? B: Heavy rain stopped the workers for several weeks, so progress has been slower than planned, but the manager says we should be able to move in by early summer.","t":"A：建設公司承諾新辦公大樓三月就會完工，為什麼我們還在舊大樓上班？ B：大雨讓工人停工好幾週，所以【進度】比計畫慢，不過經理說我們應該能在初夏前搬進去。"},{"w":"mastery","p":"n.","d":"great skill or knowledge in a subject or activity","c":"精通；熟練","s":"A: Why did the company hire a young engineer from Germany instead of choosing someone from the local office for the new project? B: Her mastery of the latest design software is impressive, and the project needs someone who can solve technical problems quickly and also train our local team to use the same programs.","t":"A：公司為什麼從德國聘請一位年輕工程師，而不是從本地辦公室挑人負責新專案？ B：她對最新設計軟體的【精通】令人佩服，而這個專案需要一個能快速解決技術問題、又能訓練本地團隊使用同樣程式的人。"},{"w":"distinction","p":"n.","d":"a special honor given for excellent work or results","c":"優異成績；殊榮；卓越","s":"A: Have you heard anything about the new accountant who is joining our finance team next Monday morning? B: Yes, she graduated with distinction from a famous business school in London, and after that she worked for an international bank for six years, so I think she will bring a lot of useful experience.","t":"A：你有聽說下週一早上要加入我們財務團隊的新會計嗎？ B：有，她以【優異成績】從倫敦一所知名商學院畢業，之後在一家國際銀行工作了六年，所以我想她會帶來很多有用的經驗。"},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"public praise or thanks for something good someone has done","c":"認可；表揚","s":"A: Why does the company hold a special lunch for staff members at the end of every quarter? B: The managers want to give public recognition to employees who worked hard or helped customers in special ways, because they believe that thanking people in front of their coworkers makes everyone feel more motivated.","t":"A：為什麼公司每季末都會為員工舉辦特別午餐？ B：主管們想公開【表揚】那些努力工作或用特別方式幫助顧客的員工，因為他們相信在同事面前感謝別人，會讓大家更有動力。"},{"w":"realize","p":"v.","d":"to make a hope or plan really happen","c":"實現（夢想、計畫）","s":"A: Why did your sister quit her office job and open a small bakery near the train station last spring? B: She had always dreamed of running her own business, and after saving money for ten years, she finally decided it was time to realize that dream before she got too busy with other responsibilities.","t":"A：你姊姊去年春天為什麼辭掉辦公室工作，在火車站附近開了一家小麵包店？ B：她一直夢想經營自己的事業，存了十年的錢之後，她終於決定是時候【實現】這個夢想了，免得之後被其他責任綁住而太忙。"},{"w":"victory","p":"n.","d":"success in a game, competition, or fight","c":"勝利","s":"A: Why is the sports shop on Main Street offering a thirty percent discount on all football shirts this weekend? B: The local team won the national championship last night, and the owner wants to celebrate the victory with the fans, so he expects the store to be very crowded until Sunday evening.","t":"A：為什麼大街上的運動用品店這個週末所有足球衫都打七折？ B：當地球隊昨晚贏得全國冠軍，老闆想和球迷一起慶祝這場【勝利】，所以他預計店裡到星期日晚上都會很擁擠。"},{"w":"breakthrough","p":"n.","d":"an important new discovery or development","c":"突破；重大進展","s":"A: Why are the scientists in the research lab so excited, and why did the company cancel this afternoon's regular meeting? B: They finally made a major breakthrough in developing a cheaper battery for electric cars, so the director called an urgent meeting with the investors to discuss how quickly the product can reach the market.","t":"A：研究實驗室的科學家為什麼這麼興奮？公司又為什麼取消今天下午的例行會議？ B：他們終於在開發更便宜的電動車電池上有了重大【突破】，所以主管召開緊急會議，和投資人討論產品能多快上市。"},{"w":"accolade","p":"n.","d":"praise or an award given for excellent work","c":"讚揚；榮譽；獎項","s":"A: Have you seen the article in this morning's newspaper about the small Italian restaurant across the street from our office? B: Yes, a famous food critic gave it the highest accolade of the year, so now it is almost impossible to book a table there for our team lunch next Friday.","t":"A：你看了今天早報上那篇關於我們辦公室對面那家小義大利餐廳的報導嗎？ B：看了，一位知名美食評論家給了它今年最高的【讚譽】，所以現在要訂那裡的位子給我們下週五的團隊午餐幾乎不可能了。"},{"w":"honor","p":"n.","d":"something that makes you feel proud and respected","c":"榮幸；榮譽","s":"A: How did you feel when the president of the company asked you to give the opening speech at the annual conference in Singapore? B: It was a great honor for me, because I have only worked here for two years, but I was also very nervous about speaking in front of five hundred people.","t":"A：公司總裁請你在新加坡年會上致開幕詞時，你有什麼感覺？ B：這對我來說是莫大的【榮幸】，因為我在這裡才工作兩年，但要在五百人面前演講也讓我非常緊張。"},{"w":"advance","p":"v.","d":"to move forward or get a higher position at work","c":"晉升；前進","s":"A: Why are so many junior staff members signing up for the evening management courses that the company offers this semester? B: They know that employees who complete the courses usually advance to senior positions more quickly, and the company also pays for the classes, so it is a great opportunity for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼這學期有這麼多基層員工報名公司開設的晚間管理課程？ B：他們知道完成課程的員工通常能更快【晉升】到高階職位，而且公司也負擔學費，所以對大家來說是很好的機會。"},{"w":"gain","p":"v.","d":"to get something useful, such as skills or experience","c":"獲得；增加","s":"A: Why did you accept a summer internship at a small trading company instead of taking a longer vacation with your family? B: I wanted to gain some practical experience before I graduate, and the manager there promised that I could work directly with overseas clients, which will look great on my resume.","t":"A：你為什麼接受一家小貿易公司的暑期實習，而不是和家人去度個較長的假？ B：我想在畢業前【獲得】一些實務經驗，而且那裡的經理承諾我可以直接和海外客戶合作，這會讓我的履歷很加分。"},{"w":"prosperity","p":"n.","d":"a situation of having money and success","c":"繁榮；興旺","s":"A: Why has the city government spent so much money on building a new port and highway near the coast? B: The mayor believes that better transportation will attract foreign companies and bring long-term prosperity to the region, creating thousands of new jobs for young people who usually move away to find work.","t":"A：市政府為什麼花那麼多錢在海岸附近興建新港口和高速公路？ B：市長相信更好的交通能吸引外國企業，為這個地區帶來長期的【繁榮】，替那些通常得外移找工作的年輕人創造數千個新工作機會。"},{"w":"completion","p":"n.","d":"the act of finishing something","c":"完成；結束","s":"A: When will the contractor receive the final payment for renovating our office on the third floor? B: According to the contract, we will pay the last part of the money after the completion of all the work, including painting the walls, installing the new lights, and cleaning the whole area.","t":"A：承包商什麼時候會收到我們三樓辦公室翻修的尾款？ B：根據合約，我們會在所有工程【完成】後支付最後一筆款項，包括粉刷牆壁、安裝新燈具以及清潔整個區域。"},{"w":"reward","p":"n.","d":"something given to thank someone for good work or effort","c":"獎勵；報酬","s":"A: Why did the store manager give each cashier a gift card and an extra day off at the end of the holiday season? B: It was a reward for their hard work during the busiest weeks of the year, when they served long lines of customers and stayed late almost every night without complaining.","t":"A：店經理為什麼在假期旺季結束時給每位收銀員一張禮物卡和一天額外的假？ B：那是對他們在一年中最忙碌幾週辛勤工作的【獎勵】，當時他們服務大排長龍的顧客，幾乎每晚都留下來加班卻毫無怨言。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to be successful or to do something","c":"抱負；雄心","s":"A: What did the young sales assistant say during her interview when the manager asked about her plans for the future? B: She said her biggest ambition is to open her own fashion company one day, and she wants to learn everything about buying, marketing, and managing a store while she works with us.","t":"A：主管在面試時問那位年輕的銷售助理對未來的規劃，她怎麼回答？ B：她說她最大的【抱負】是有一天開自己的服裝公司，所以她想在跟我們工作時，學習所有關於採購、行銷和管理商店的知識。"},{"w":"merit","p":"n.","d":"good quality or ability that deserves praise or reward","c":"優點；功績；實力","s":"A: How does the company decide which employees receive a pay raise at the end of each year? B: Raises are based on merit, not on how long people have worked here, so managers look carefully at each person's results, teamwork, and customer feedback before they make any final decisions.","t":"A：公司每年年底如何決定哪些員工可以加薪？ B：加薪是根據【實力與表現】，而不是看在這裡工作多久，所以主管在做最後決定前，會仔細檢視每個人的成果、團隊合作和顧客回饋。"},{"w":"earn","p":"v.","d":"to get money or respect because of your work","c":"賺取；贏得","s":"A: Why does Daniel work as a tour guide on weekends even though he already has a full-time job at the bank? B: He wants to earn some extra money to pay for his master's degree next year, and he also enjoys meeting tourists from different countries and practicing his foreign languages.","t":"A：丹尼爾已經在銀行有全職工作，為什麼週末還要當導遊？ B：他想【賺】一些外快來支付明年的碩士學費，而且他也喜歡認識來自不同國家的觀光客並練習外語。"},{"w":"win","p":"v.","d":"to be the best in a competition or to get a prize or contract","c":"贏得；獲勝","s":"A: Why is the design team working so late every evening this week, even though their normal projects are almost finished? B: They are preparing a special presentation because they really hope to win the contract for the new airport terminal, which would be the biggest project in the company's history.","t":"A：設計團隊這週為什麼每晚都加班到很晚，即使他們的一般專案都快完成了？ B：他們正在準備一份特別簡報，因為他們非常希望【贏得】新機場航廈的合約，那將是公司史上最大的專案。"},{"w":"outcome","p":"n.","d":"the final result of an action or event","c":"結果；成果","s":"A: Have the managers decided whether we will move our main office to the new business park outside the city? B: Not yet, they are still discussing the costs with the landlord, and they said they will tell all the staff about the final outcome of the negotiations at the meeting next Wednesday.","t":"A：主管們決定好是否要把總公司搬到市郊新的商業園區了嗎？ B：還沒，他們還在和房東討論費用，並說會在下週三的會議上告訴所有員工談判的最終【結果】。"},{"w":"acquire","p":"v.","d":"to get or learn something, such as a skill or a company","c":"習得；取得；收購","s":"A: Why does the company send new engineers to work in the Tokyo office for six months during their first year? B: It helps them acquire useful skills and learn how our partners in Japan work, so they can communicate better with overseas clients when they return to the head office.","t":"A：公司為什麼在新工程師的第一年派他們到東京辦公室工作六個月？ B：這能幫助他們【習得】實用的技能，並了解我們日本夥伴的工作方式，讓他們回到總公司後能和海外客戶更順利地溝通。"},{"w":"status","p":"n.","d":"a person's position or importance compared with others","c":"地位；身分","s":"A: Why do so many of our clients insist on staying at the expensive five-star hotel downtown when they visit for business meetings? B: For many of them, staying there shows their high status in the company, and they also like the quiet meeting rooms and the excellent restaurant on the top floor.","t":"A：為什麼我們很多客戶來開商務會議時，堅持要住市中心那家昂貴的五星級飯店？ B：對他們很多人來說，住在那裡能彰顯他們在公司裡的崇高【地位】，而且他們也喜歡那裡安靜的會議室和頂樓的高級餐廳。"},{"w":"self-made","p":"adj.","d":"successful or rich because of your own hard work, not help from others","c":"白手起家的","s":"A: What do you know about the woman who will give the main speech at the small business conference next month? B: She is a self-made businesswoman who started selling handmade bags at a night market twenty years ago, and today her company has more than fifty shops across Asia and Europe.","t":"A：你對下個月在小企業研討會上發表主題演講的那位女士了解多少？ B：她是一位【白手起家的】女企業家，二十年前從夜市賣手工包包起家，如今她的公司在亞洲和歐洲擁有超過五十家店。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Activity 活動","cards":[{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"something important or special that happens, often planned","c":"活動；大型活動；事件","s":"A: Why is the hotel lobby so crowded today, and why are there so many people in suits carrying name badges and brochures? B: A large technology company has rented the main hall for a special event to celebrate its twentieth anniversary, so hundreds of guests, partners, and reporters have arrived from different cities this morning.","t":"A：為什麼今天飯店大廳這麼擁擠，而且有這麼多穿西裝的人拿著名牌和手冊？ B：一家大型科技公司租下了主廳舉辦一場特別的【活動】來慶祝二十週年，所以今天早上有數百位賓客、合作夥伴和記者從不同城市來到這裡。"},{"w":"occasion","p":"n.","d":"a special time or event","c":"場合；特殊時刻","s":"A: Should I wear my usual work clothes to the retirement dinner for Mr. Lin on Friday night, or do you think something more formal would be better? B: Since it is an important occasion and the president will give a speech, most of the staff are planning to wear suits or nice dresses, so I would dress up a little.","t":"A：週五晚上林先生的退休晚宴，我應該穿平常的上班服裝，還是你覺得穿正式一點比較好？ B：因為這是一個重要的【場合】，而且總裁會致詞，大部分員工都打算穿西裝或漂亮的洋裝，所以我會稍微打扮一下。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people for a social or work purpose","c":"聚會；集會","s":"A: Are you going to the small gathering in the staff lounge after work today, or do you have to leave early to pick up your children from school? B: I will stay for about an hour because the team wants to say goodbye to Emma, who is moving to our Tokyo office next week, and I helped buy her gift.","t":"A：你今天下班後會去員工休息室的小型【聚會】嗎？還是你得早點離開去學校接小孩？ B：我會待大約一個小時，因為團隊想跟下週要調到東京辦公室的艾瑪道別，而且我有幫忙買她的禮物。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a party or special event to show you are happy about something","c":"慶祝；慶祝活動","s":"A: Why did the manager order so many cakes and balloons for the office this afternoon, and is it someone's birthday today? B: No, it is a celebration for our sales team, because they reached their yearly target two months early, and the director wants to thank everyone for working so hard during the busy season.","t":"A：為什麼經理今天下午幫辦公室訂了這麼多蛋糕和氣球？今天是誰生日嗎？ B：不是，這是為我們業務團隊舉辦的【慶祝活動】，因為他們提早兩個月達成年度目標，主管想感謝大家在旺季這麼努力工作。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special time when people enjoy music, food, or culture, often for several days","c":"節慶；（藝術、音樂等）節","s":"A: Why are all the hotels near the river fully booked next weekend, and where should our visiting clients stay during their trip? B: The city is holding its yearly food and music festival by the river, so thousands of tourists are coming, and we should book rooms in a business hotel near the train station instead.","t":"A：為什麼下週末河邊附近的飯店都客滿了？來訪的客戶出差期間應該住在哪裡？ B：市政府要在河邊舉辦一年一度的美食音樂【節】，所以會有數千名遊客湧入，我們應該改訂火車站附近的商務旅館。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal public event with special traditions or actions","c":"典禮；儀式","s":"A: What time should the guests arrive at the new factory on Monday morning, and will there be enough chairs for the local reporters? B: The opening ceremony starts at ten o'clock, when the mayor will cut the ribbon, so guests should arrive by nine-thirty, and I have already asked the staff to set up fifty extra seats.","t":"A：週一早上賓客應該幾點到達新工廠？給當地記者的椅子夠嗎？ B：開幕【典禮】十點開始，屆時市長會剪綵，所以賓客應該在九點半前抵達，而且我已經請員工多擺五十個座位。"},{"w":"function","p":"n.","d":"a formal social event, such as a party or dinner","c":"宴會；正式聚會","s":"A: Is the large dining room on the top floor of the hotel available on Saturday evening, or has another company already reserved it? B: I'm sorry, but a bank is holding a private function for its most important customers that night, so the room is closed to the public, but our garden restaurant still has space.","t":"A：飯店頂樓的大型餐廳週六晚上可以使用嗎？還是已經被其他公司預訂了？ B：很抱歉，那天晚上一家銀行要為最重要的客戶舉辦私人【宴會】，所以那個廳不對外開放，不過我們的花園餐廳還有位子。"},{"w":"program","p":"n.","d":"a planned series of activities or events","c":"計畫；課程方案；節目","s":"A: How can new employees learn about the company's products and safety rules before they start working in the warehouse next month? B: The human resources department has created a two-week training program with short classes, factory tours, and practice tests, so every new worker will understand the main rules before their first real shift.","t":"A：新進員工下個月開始在倉庫工作前，要怎麼了解公司的產品和安全規定？ B：人資部門設計了一個為期兩週的訓練【計畫】，包括短期課程、工廠參觀和練習測驗，所以每位新員工在第一次正式上班前都會了解主要規定。"},{"w":"session","p":"n.","d":"a period of time used for a particular activity","c":"（活動的）一段時間；場次；講習","s":"A: I couldn't get to the conference until lunchtime because my flight was delayed, so did I miss anything really important this morning? B: You missed the first session about online marketing, but the speaker uploaded her slides to the website, and the afternoon talks about customer service are probably more useful for your team anyway.","t":"A：我的班機延誤，所以到中午才趕到研討會，我今天早上有錯過什麼很重要的內容嗎？ B：你錯過了第一【場】關於網路行銷的講座，不過講者已經把投影片上傳到網站，而且下午關於客服的演講對你的團隊可能反而更有用。"},{"w":"meeting","p":"n.","d":"an event when people come together to discuss something","c":"會議","s":"A: Why isn't Mr. Chen answering his phone this morning, when the client from Singapore has called him three times already? B: He is in a long meeting with the board of directors to discuss next year's budget, and he asked his assistant not to disturb him until it finishes at about eleven-thirty.","t":"A：為什麼陳先生今天早上都不接電話？新加坡的客戶已經打給他三次了。 B：他正在和董事會開一場很長的【會議】討論明年的預算，他請助理在大約十一點半結束前不要打擾他。"},{"w":"workshop","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where people learn a skill by doing practical activities","c":"研習會；工作坊","s":"A: Do you know any good way for our sales staff to improve their speaking skills before they meet the overseas buyers next month? B: Yes, a local business school is offering a one-day workshop on presentation skills, where each person practices speaking in small groups and gets helpful feedback from an experienced trainer.","t":"A：你知道有什麼好方法可以讓我們的業務人員在下個月見國外買家之前提升口說能力嗎？ B：有，當地一所商學院開設了為期一天的簡報技巧【工作坊】，每個人都會在小組中練習說話，並得到經驗豐富的講師給予的實用回饋。"},{"w":"seminar","p":"n.","d":"a class or meeting where a small group discusses a subject with an expert","c":"研討會；專題討論會","s":"A: Why are so many accountants from our department leaving the office early this Thursday afternoon, and who will answer client calls? B: They are going to a seminar at the city hall about the new tax laws, which will start next year, and two staff members from the front desk will answer the phones while they are away.","t":"A：為什麼我們部門這週四下午有這麼多會計師提早離開辦公室？誰來接客戶的電話？ B：他們要去市政廳參加一場關於明年開始實施的新稅法的【研討會】，他們不在時，櫃台的兩位員工會負責接電話。"},{"w":"conference","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting where many people discuss a subject, often for several days","c":"（大型）會議；大會","s":"A: Have you booked your flight to Singapore for next month yet, and are you going to give a speech there this year? B: Yes, I booked it yesterday, because I'm speaking at the international conference on green energy, where about two thousand engineers and business leaders will share ideas for three days.","t":"A：你訂好下個月飛新加坡的機票了嗎？你今年會在那裡演講嗎？ B：訂好了，我昨天訂的，因為我要在國際綠能【大會】上演講，屆時大約兩千名工程師和企業領袖會在三天內交流想法。"},{"w":"competition","p":"n.","d":"an event in which people try to win a prize by being the best","c":"比賽；競賽","s":"A: Why is everyone in the design department working so late every night this week, even though our big project is already finished? B: They entered a national competition for the best new product packaging, and the winning team will receive a large cash prize, so they want their design to be perfect before Friday's deadline.","t":"A：為什麼設計部的每個人這週每天晚上都工作到這麼晚？我們的大案子明明已經完成了。 B：他們報名了一場全國最佳新產品包裝【比賽】，獲勝的團隊會得到一大筆獎金，所以他們希望在週五截止前讓設計完美無缺。"},{"w":"tournament","p":"n.","d":"a sports or game competition with many players or teams and several rounds","c":"錦標賽；聯賽","s":"A: Why is the company gym booked every evening this month, when I usually go there after work to exercise? B: Our office is holding a basketball tournament between eight departments, and teams practice there every night, but the games will end next Friday, so you can use the gym again after that.","t":"A：為什麼公司健身房這個月每天晚上都被預約滿了？我平常下班後都會去那裡運動。 B：我們辦公室正在舉辦一場八個部門之間的籃球【錦標賽】，各隊每天晚上都在那裡練習，不過比賽下週五就會結束，之後你就可以再使用健身房了。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of playing music, dancing, or acting in front of people","c":"演出；表演","s":"A: Did you enjoy the company's year-end party at the hotel last night, or did you leave early because you were so tired? B: I stayed until the end, because the most exciting part was a live performance by a famous jazz band, and the guests kept dancing and clapping until almost midnight.","t":"A：你昨晚喜歡公司在飯店舉辦的尾牙嗎？還是因為太累提早離開了？ B：我待到最後，因為最精彩的部分是一個知名爵士樂團的現場【演出】，賓客一直跳舞拍手到快午夜。"},{"w":"show","p":"n.","d":"an event where people look at products or watch entertainment","c":"展覽；表演；節目","s":"A: Why did the marketing team pack so many boxes of brochures and product samples into the van this morning? B: They are driving to the convention center for a three-day trade show, where hundreds of companies display their newest products, and they hope to meet many new buyers from Japan and Korea there.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊今天早上把這麼多箱手冊和產品樣品搬上廂型車？ B：他們要開車到會展中心參加為期三天的貿易【展】，數百家公司會在那裡展示最新產品，他們希望能在那裡認識許多來自日本和韓國的新買家。"},{"w":"exhibition","p":"n.","d":"a public event where art or products are shown to people","c":"展覽；展覽會","s":"A: What are you planning to do with the visiting clients on Saturday afternoon after the factory tour is over? B: I'm going to take them to the city museum, because there is a special exhibition of old Taiwanese photographs and paintings, and they told me they are very interested in local history and art.","t":"A：週六下午工廠參觀結束後，你打算帶來訪的客戶做什麼？ B：我要帶他們去市立博物館，因為那裡有一個台灣老照片和畫作的特別【展覽】，他們跟我說對當地歷史和藝術很有興趣。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk that gives information about something to a group of people","c":"簡報；報告","s":"A: You look very nervous this morning, so is something wrong with the new project, or did you not sleep well last night? B: I have to give a presentation to the senior managers about our sales results at ten o'clock, and I'm worried that the projector might not work, so I printed copies of every slide.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來很緊張，是新專案出了什麼問題，還是昨晚沒睡好？ B：我十點要向高階主管做一場關於業績結果的【簡報】，我擔心投影機可能會故障，所以把每張投影片都印出來了。"},{"w":"demonstration","p":"n.","d":"an act of showing how something works or how to do something","c":"示範；展示","s":"A: How will the store staff learn to use the new coffee machines before the café opens to customers next Monday? B: A technician from the supplier is coming on Friday afternoon to give a demonstration, so she will show everyone step by step how to clean the machine and make each type of drink.","t":"A：門市員工要怎麼在下週一咖啡廳開幕前學會使用新的咖啡機？ B：供應商的技術人員週五下午會來做【示範】，她會一步一步教大家如何清潔機器以及製作每一種飲料。"},{"w":"activity-based","p":"adj.","d":"using practical activities to help people learn or work","c":"以活動為主的；活動式的","s":"A: The new employees seemed bored during last month's training, so how can we make the lessons more interesting for the next group? B: We should try an activity-based approach, where trainees solve real problems in small teams and play short role-play games instead of listening to long lectures all day.","t":"A：新進員工在上個月的訓練中似乎很無聊，我們要怎麼讓下一梯次的課程更有趣？ B：我們應該試試【以活動為主的】方式，讓學員以小組解決真實問題並玩簡短的角色扮演遊戲，而不是整天聽冗長的講課。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing people to take part and communicate, not just watch or listen","c":"互動的；互動式的","s":"A: Why do so many children and parents visit the science museum downtown on weekends, even though the tickets are quite expensive? B: The museum has many interactive displays, where visitors can touch screens, build simple machines, and try small experiments, so families have fun and learn something at the same time.","t":"A：為什麼週末有這麼多孩子和家長去市中心的科學博物館，即使門票相當貴？ B：博物館有很多【互動式的】展示，參觀者可以觸碰螢幕、組裝簡單的機器並嘗試小實驗，所以家庭可以同時玩得開心又學到東西。"},{"w":"recreational","p":"adj.","d":"relating to activities that people do for fun when they are not working","c":"娛樂的；休閒的","s":"A: What kind of benefits does the new company offer its staff, apart from a good salary and health insurance? B: It has a large recreational center next to the office with a swimming pool, a game room, and tennis courts, so employees can relax and exercise after work without paying any extra fees.","t":"A：除了優渥的薪水和健康保險，新公司還提供員工哪些福利？ B：公司在辦公室旁邊有一座大型【休閒】中心，裡面有游泳池、遊戲室和網球場，所以員工下班後可以放鬆和運動，不需要另外付費。"},{"w":"scheduled","p":"adj.","d":"planned for a particular time","c":"預定的；排定的","s":"A: Is the shipment of new office furniture still going to arrive on Tuesday, or has the delivery company changed the date again? B: The scheduled delivery time is still Tuesday at two o'clock, but the driver said heavy rain might cause a short delay, so someone should wait at the loading area that afternoon.","t":"A：新辦公家具還是會在週二送到嗎？還是貨運公司又改日期了？ B：【預定的】送貨時間還是週二下午兩點，不過司機說大雨可能會造成短暫延誤，所以那天下午應該要有人在卸貨區等。"},{"w":"organized","p":"adj.","d":"planned carefully and arranged well","c":"有組織的；安排好的","s":"A: Are you going on the weekend trip to the mountains with the rest of the accounting team, or do you prefer to rest at home? B: I'm going, because it's an organized tour with a bus, a local guide, and all the meals included, so I don't need to plan anything or worry about getting lost.","t":"A：你會跟會計團隊的其他人一起去山上的週末旅行嗎？還是你比較想在家休息？ B：我會去，因為那是一個【安排好的】團體行程，包含巴士、當地導遊和所有餐點，所以我不需要計畫任何事情，也不用擔心迷路。"},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity or event","c":"參加；參與","s":"A: Do all employees have to join the company's charity run in the park next Sunday morning, even if they are not very good at running? B: No, nobody is required to participate, but the manager hopes many people will join, because the money we raise will help buy books for children at a local school.","t":"A：所有員工都必須參加下週日早上在公園舉辦的公司慈善路跑嗎？即使不太擅長跑步也一樣？ B：不，沒有人被要求一定要【參加】，但經理希望很多人會加入，因為我們募到的錢會用來幫當地一所學校的孩子買書。"},{"w":"host","p":"v.","d":"to organize an event and invite people to it","c":"主辦；舉辦","s":"A: Which city did the board of directors finally choose for next year's sales meeting, and when will they tell the regional managers? B: They decided that our Taichung office will host the meeting, because it has a large new conference room and is close to the high-speed rail station, and they will announce it on Monday.","t":"A：董事會最後選了哪個城市辦明年的業務會議？他們什麼時候會告知各區經理？ B：他們決定由我們台中辦公室【主辦】這場會議，因為那裡有一間新的大型會議室，而且離高鐵站很近，他們會在週一宣布。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event, such as a meeting or class","c":"出席；參加","s":"A: Will you be able to attend the training workshop on customer service tomorrow afternoon, or are you still busy preparing the monthly report? B: I'll be there, because my supervisor said it is very important for everyone who works at the front desk, and I finished most of the report last night anyway.","t":"A：你明天下午能【出席】客服訓練工作坊嗎？還是你還在忙著準備月報？ B：我會到，因為主管說這對所有在櫃台工作的人都非常重要，而且反正我昨晚已經把報告大部分完成了。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"v.","d":"to organize and do a particular activity","c":"進行；實施","s":"A: How will the company find out whether customers are happy with the new mobile app that we released last month? B: The marketing department plans to conduct an online survey next week, asking about five hundred users to answer ten short questions, and the results will help the designers decide what to improve.","t":"A：公司要怎麼了解顧客是否滿意我們上個月推出的新手機應用程式？ B：行銷部打算下週【進行】一項線上調查，請大約五百位使用者回答十個簡短的問題，結果會幫助設計師決定要改善哪些地方。"},{"w":"launch","p":"v.","d":"to start something new, or to make a new product available","c":"推出；發起","s":"A: Why has the marketing team been working so hard on weekends recently, and when will they finally get some rest? B: The company is going to launch its new line of energy drinks at a big event next month, so they are busy preparing the advertisements, the website, and the free samples for customers.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊最近週末都這麼努力工作？他們什麼時候才能休息？ B：公司下個月要在一場大型活動中【推出】新系列的能量飲料，所以他們正忙著準備廣告、網站和給顧客的免費樣品。"},{"w":"engage","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity, or to get someone interested","c":"參與；吸引（注意）","s":"A: Why does the new manager always ask so many questions and give small prizes during her training classes for the sales staff? B: She wants everyone to engage in the discussion instead of just sitting quietly, because she believes people remember more information when they share their own ideas and experiences with the group.","t":"A：為什麼新經理在業務人員訓練課上總是問很多問題又發小獎品？ B：她希望大家都能【參與】討論，而不是只是安靜地坐著，因為她相信當人們和團隊分享自己的想法和經驗時，會記得更多資訊。"},{"w":"occur","p":"v.","d":"to happen","c":"發生","s":"A: Why did the factory manager suddenly call an emergency meeting this afternoon, and should the office staff join it too? B: He wants to explain the new safety rules, because two small accidents happened in the warehouse last week, and he wants to make sure that problems like that never occur again in any part of the building.","t":"A：為什麼工廠經理今天下午突然召開緊急會議？辦公室員工也要參加嗎？ B：他想說明新的安全規定，因為上週倉庫發生了兩起小意外，他要確保這類問題不會在大樓的任何地方再次【發生】。"},{"w":"wrap-up","p":"n.","d":"the final part of an event that sums up what happened","c":"總結；收尾","s":"A: Do I need to stay until the very end of the three-day conference on Friday, or can I leave after the last afternoon talk? B: Please stay for the wrap-up at four o'clock, because the organizers will summarize the main ideas from every session, give out certificates, and explain how to download all of the speakers' slides.","t":"A：週五這場為期三天的研討會，我需要待到最後嗎？還是可以在下午最後一場演講後離開？ B：請留下來參加四點的【總結】，因為主辦單位會歸納每一場的重點、頒發證書，並說明如何下載所有講者的投影片。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Actor 演員","cards":[{"w":"actress","p":"n.","d":"a woman whose job is acting in plays, films, or TV shows","c":"女演員","s":"A: Who is going to appear in the new television commercial for our skin care products, and has the marketing team already signed the contract with her agent? B: We hired a young actress from Taipei who has starred in two popular dramas, and her agent signed the contract yesterday, so filming will start next Monday at the studio downtown.","t":"A：誰要出演我們護膚產品的新電視廣告？行銷團隊已經和她的經紀人簽約了嗎？ B：我們聘請了一位來自台北、主演過兩部熱門連續劇的年輕【女演員】，她的經紀人昨天已經簽約了，所以下週一將在市中心的攝影棚開始拍攝。"},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to act, sing, or dance in front of an audience","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: What kind of entertainment have you planned for the company's annual dinner, and will it be finished before the awards ceremony begins? B: A local theater group will perform a short comedy about office life for about twenty minutes, and then the managers will hand out the awards right after the actors leave the stage.","t":"A：你為公司年度晚宴安排了什麼樣的娛樂節目？會在頒獎典禮開始前結束嗎？ B：一個當地劇團將【表演】一齣大約二十分鐘、關於辦公室生活的短篇喜劇，演員們一離開舞台，經理們就會立刻頒發獎項。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"an event when people act, sing, or dance for an audience","c":"演出；表演","s":"A: Did you enjoy the play that the sales department took our overseas clients to see at the National Theater last Friday evening? B: Yes, the performance was excellent, and the clients were so impressed by the actors and the music that they asked our manager to book tickets for another show before they fly home.","t":"A：上週五晚上業務部帶海外客戶去國家戲劇院看的那齣戲，你喜歡嗎？ B：喜歡，那場【演出】非常精彩，客戶們對演員和音樂印象深刻，還請我們經理在他們回國前再訂另一場表演的票。"},{"w":"role","p":"n.","d":"the part that an actor plays in a film or play","c":"角色","s":"A: Why has the famous actor agreed to appear in such a small training video for our bank, even though he usually only makes big movies? B: His sister works in our customer service department, and he liked the role of a friendly bank teller who helps an elderly customer, so he agreed to take a much lower fee than usual.","t":"A：為什麼那位知名演員願意出演我們銀行這麼小的培訓影片，他平常不是只拍大型電影嗎？ B：他的妹妹在我們客服部工作，而且他喜歡那個幫助年長顧客的親切銀行櫃員【角色】，所以他同意收取比平常低很多的酬勞。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal in a story, film, or play","c":"角色；人物","s":"A: What do you think about the new animated advertisement that the design team created for our online shopping app last week? B: I really like the main character, a cheerful delivery cat who brings packages to customers' doors, because it is cute and easy to remember, and many young shoppers have already shared the video on social media.","t":"A：你覺得設計團隊上週為我們的網購應用程式製作的新動畫廣告怎麼樣？ B：我很喜歡那個主要【角色】，一隻把包裹送到顧客家門口的開心送貨貓，因為牠很可愛又好記，許多年輕購物者已經在社群媒體上分享這支影片了。"},{"w":"cast","p":"n.","d":"all the actors in a film, play, or show","c":"全體演員；演員陣容","s":"A: How many people will be in the short film that the human resources department is making about workplace safety this spring? B: The whole cast includes eight employees from different departments, and they will practice their parts together every Wednesday afternoon in the meeting room until filming begins at the factory in April.","t":"A：人資部今年春天要拍的職場安全短片會有多少人參與演出？ B：【全體演員】包括來自不同部門的八名員工，他們每週三下午會在會議室一起排練各自的部分，直到四月在工廠開拍為止。"},{"w":"script","p":"n.","d":"the written words that actors say in a film, play, or ad","c":"劇本；腳本","s":"A: Have you finished writing the words for the product video, or do you still need more time to check the technical details with the engineers? B: I finished the script last night and emailed it to the engineers this morning, so once they confirm the information is correct, the actors can start learning their parts tomorrow.","t":"A：你寫完產品影片的台詞了嗎？還是你還需要更多時間跟工程師確認技術細節？ B：我昨晚完成了【劇本】，今天早上已經寄給工程師了，所以只要他們確認資訊正確，演員明天就能開始背自己的部分。"},{"w":"rehearse","p":"v.","d":"to practice a play, speech, or show before the real event","c":"排練；預演","s":"A: Why are the sales team members staying so late in the conference room every evening this week, even though their reports are already finished? B: They want to rehearse the short play they are presenting at the trade show on Saturday, because they will perform in front of hundreds of visitors and don't want to forget anything.","t":"A：為什麼業務團隊成員這週每天晚上都在會議室待到這麼晚，他們的報告不是已經完成了嗎？ B：他們想【排練】週六要在商展上演出的短劇，因為他們將在數百名參觀者面前表演，不想忘記任何東西。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"the words that characters say to each other in a film or play","c":"對話；對白","s":"A: Why did the director stop filming the scene in the hotel lobby so many times this afternoon, and is there a problem with the actors? B: The dialogue between the receptionist and the guest sounded too formal and unnatural, so the writer is changing some of the words to make the conversation sound more like real people talking.","t":"A：為什麼導演今天下午在飯店大廳拍那場戲時喊停了那麼多次？演員有什麼問題嗎？ B：櫃台人員和客人之間的【對白】聽起來太正式、不自然，所以編劇正在修改一些用字，讓這段對話聽起來更像真人在交談。"},{"w":"monologue","p":"n.","d":"a long speech by one actor alone","c":"獨白","s":"A: What will the actor do at the start of our product launch event, before the CEO walks out to introduce the new smartphone? B: He will deliver a two-minute monologue alone on the stage about how much a phone changes our daily lives, and then the lights will go down and the CEO will appear.","t":"A：在執行長走出來介紹新智慧型手機之前，那位演員會在我們產品發表會一開始做什麼？ B：他會獨自在舞台上發表一段兩分鐘的【獨白】，講述手機如何改變我們的日常生活，然後燈光會暗下來，執行長就會登場。"},{"w":"stage","p":"n.","d":"the raised area in a theater or hall where people perform","c":"舞台","s":"A: Is the main hall ready for tomorrow's awards ceremony, or are the workers still setting up the lights and the sound system? B: The workers finished building the stage this afternoon, but they are still testing the microphones and the lights, so I think everything will be ready by about ten o'clock tonight.","t":"A：大廳已經準備好明天的頒獎典禮了嗎？還是工作人員還在架設燈光和音響系統？ B：工作人員今天下午已經搭好【舞台】，但他們還在測試麥克風和燈光，所以我想今晚十點左右一切都會準備就緒。"},{"w":"screen","p":"n.","d":"the surface where films or TV shows are seen; films and TV in general","c":"螢幕；銀幕","s":"A: Why did the company choose that young actor for our new coffee commercial when there are so many experienced people available? B: He looks very warm and friendly on screen, and when we tested his video with customers in three cities, most of them said they trusted him more than the other actors.","t":"A：為什麼公司選了那位年輕演員拍我們新的咖啡廣告，明明有那麼多有經驗的人可以選？ B：他在【螢幕】上看起來非常溫暖親切，而且我們在三個城市拿他的影片給顧客測試時，大多數人都說比起其他演員更信任他。"},{"w":"audition","p":"n.","d":"a short test where an actor shows if they are right for a part","c":"試鏡","s":"A: How did you choose the actors for the training videos, and how many people came to try out for the parts last weekend? B: We held an audition at our office on Saturday morning, and more than forty people came to read the script, so it took us the whole day to choose the final six actors.","t":"A：你們是怎麼挑選培訓影片的演員的？上週末有多少人來爭取角色？ B：我們週六早上在辦公室舉辦了一場【試鏡】，有四十多人來讀劇本，所以我們花了一整天才選出最後的六位演員。"},{"w":"director","p":"n.","d":"the person who tells the actors and crew what to do when making a film or play","c":"導演","s":"A: Who is in charge of telling the actors where to stand and how to say their words during the filming of our new advertisement? B: The director we hired from a film company will guide the actors and the camera crew, and she will also decide which scenes we keep after filming is finished next week.","t":"A：在拍攝我們的新廣告時，誰負責告訴演員站在哪裡以及如何說台詞？ B：我們從一家電影公司請來的【導演】會指導演員和攝影團隊，下週拍攝結束後，她也會決定保留哪些場景。"},{"w":"producer","p":"n.","d":"the person who controls the money and plans for a film, show, or play","c":"製作人","s":"A: Who is responsible for the budget of the company documentary, and who should I talk to if we need to rent more equipment? B: You should speak to the producer, because he controls the money, hires the staff, and makes sure the project finishes on time, so he will decide whether we can rent more equipment.","t":"A：誰負責公司紀錄片的預算？如果我們需要租更多設備，我應該找誰談？ B：你應該和【製作人】談，因為他掌控資金、聘請工作人員，並確保專案準時完成，所以要不要多租設備由他決定。"},{"w":"talent","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability to do something well","c":"天賦；才能","s":"A: Why did the manager ask Lisa from accounting to speak in the new recruiting video instead of hiring a professional actor? B: Lisa has a natural talent for speaking in front of a camera, and she is relaxed and friendly, so the manager believes job seekers will find her more honest than a paid actor.","t":"A：為什麼經理請會計部的Lisa在新的招募影片中說話，而不是聘請專業演員？ B：Lisa天生有面對鏡頭說話的【天賦】，而且她輕鬆又親切，所以經理認為求職者會覺得她比付費請來的演員更真誠。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"showing feelings clearly, often with the face or voice","c":"富有表情的；善於表達的","s":"A: Why did the advertising agency choose that actor for our silent video, which has no words, only music and pictures? B: He has a very expressive face, so he can show surprise, joy, and worry clearly without saying anything, which is perfect for a video that will play on screens in busy train stations.","t":"A：為什麼廣告公司為我們那支沒有台詞、只有音樂和畫面的無聲影片挑選了那位演員？ B：他的臉非常【富有表情】，不用說話就能清楚地表現驚訝、喜悅和擔憂，非常適合在繁忙火車站的螢幕上播放的影片。"},{"w":"dramatic","p":"adj.","d":"exciting, sudden, or full of strong feeling","c":"戲劇性的；激動人心的","s":"A: How did the audience react at the end of the play that our company sponsored at the city theater last weekend? B: The ending was very dramatic, with loud music and the main character running into the rain, so many people in the audience stood up and clapped for several minutes after the lights came back on.","t":"A：我們公司上週末在市立劇院贊助的那齣戲，結尾時觀眾有什麼反應？ B：結局非常【戲劇性】，配上響亮的音樂和主角衝進雨中的畫面，所以燈光重新亮起後，許多觀眾起立鼓掌了好幾分鐘。"},{"w":"convincing","p":"adj.","d":"making people believe that something is true or real","c":"令人信服的；逼真的","s":"A: Did the customers believe the actor in our new advertisement was a real doctor, or did they think he was just reading a script? B: His acting was so convincing that many viewers called our office to ask which hospital he worked at, so we had to add a small note saying that he is an actor.","t":"A：顧客相信我們新廣告裡的演員是真正的醫生嗎？還是他們覺得他只是在念劇本？ B：他的演技非常【逼真】，許多觀眾打電話到我們辦公室詢問他在哪家醫院工作，所以我們只好加上一個小註記，說明他是演員。"},{"w":"versatile","p":"adj.","d":"able to do many different things well","c":"多才多藝的；多用途的","s":"A: Why do you want to hire the same actor for all three of our commercials, when each one is so different in style and mood? B: She is very versatile, so she can play a serious business owner in one commercial, a funny mother in another, and a sporty student in the third without any problem.","t":"A：我們的三支廣告風格和氛圍都很不一樣，為什麼你想讓同一位演員拍全部三支？ B：她非常【多才多藝】，所以她可以在一支廣告中飾演嚴肅的企業主，在另一支中飾演風趣的媽媽，在第三支中飾演愛運動的學生，完全沒問題。"},{"w":"famous","p":"adj.","d":"known by many people","c":"有名的；著名的","s":"A: Why are there so many reporters and photographers waiting outside the hotel entrance this morning, blocking the guests' cars? B: A famous movie star is staying here while she films a new action movie in the city, and the reporters are hoping to take her picture when she leaves for the studio.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有那麼多記者和攝影師在飯店門口等候，還擋住了客人的車？ B：一位【有名的】電影明星在本市拍攝新動作片期間住在這裡，記者們希望在她出發去攝影棚時拍到她的照片。"},{"w":"celebrity","p":"n.","d":"a famous person, especially in entertainment","c":"名人","s":"A: How can we attract more visitors to the opening of our new shopping mall next month, since the advertising budget is limited? B: We could invite a local celebrity, such as a popular TV host or singer, to cut the ribbon, because fans will come to see them and then stay to shop in the stores.","t":"A：既然廣告預算有限，我們下個月新購物中心開幕時要怎麼吸引更多遊客？ B：我們可以邀請一位當地【名人】，例如受歡迎的電視主持人或歌手來剪綵，因為粉絲會來看他們，然後留下來在店裡購物。"},{"w":"spotlight","p":"n.","d":"a strong light on a performer; public attention","c":"聚光燈；眾人注目的焦點","s":"A: Why did the new manager look so nervous at the award ceremony, even though she won the prize for the best sales results? B: She is a quiet person who doesn't enjoy being in the spotlight, so standing on the stage in front of five hundred coworkers with everyone looking at her made her very uncomfortable.","t":"A：為什麼新經理在頒獎典禮上看起來那麼緊張，她明明拿到了最佳業績獎？ B：她是個安靜的人，不喜歡成為【眾人注目的焦點】，所以站在五百名同事面前的舞台上、被大家盯著看，讓她非常不自在。"},{"w":"emotion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling, such as love, fear, or sadness","c":"情感；情緒","s":"A: Why did so many people at the charity event start crying while they were watching the short film about the children's hospital? B: The young actors showed real emotion when they played sick children waiting for help, and the story was so touching that the guests donated twice as much money as we expected.","t":"A：為什麼慈善活動上那麼多人在看那部關於兒童醫院的短片時哭了？ B：年輕演員們在飾演等待幫助的生病孩子時流露出真實的【情感】，故事非常感人，所以賓客捐出的錢是我們預期的兩倍。"},{"w":"improvise","p":"v.","d":"to act or speak without planning or practicing first","c":"即興表演；即興發揮","s":"A: What happened during the live product show yesterday when the projector suddenly stopped working in the middle of the presentation? B: The host had to improvise for about five minutes, so he told funny stories and asked the audience questions until the technicians fixed the problem, and nobody even noticed that anything was wrong.","t":"A：昨天的現場產品展示會上，投影機在簡報進行到一半時突然故障，發生了什麼事？ B：主持人只好【即興發揮】了大約五分鐘，他講了好笑的故事並向觀眾提問，直到技術人員解決問題，根本沒有人察覺出了狀況。"},{"w":"line","p":"n.","d":"words that an actor says in a play or film","c":"台詞","s":"A: Why did the filming of the bank commercial take so much longer than planned yesterday afternoon? B: The actor kept forgetting his last line, \"Your money is safe with us,\" because he was nervous, so the director had to film the same short scene about fifteen times before it was perfect.","t":"A：為什麼昨天下午銀行廣告的拍攝時間比計畫中長那麼多？ B：那位演員因為緊張，一直忘記他的最後一句【台詞】「您的錢交給我們很安全」，所以導演只好把同一個短場景拍了大約十五次才完美。"},{"w":"backstage","p":"adv.","d":"in the area behind the stage that the audience cannot see","c":"在後台","s":"A: Where should the speakers wait before they give their presentations at the conference, and can they bring their own laptops? B: They should wait backstage in the small room behind the main hall, where there are chairs, water, and power outlets, so they can check their slides on their laptops before they go on.","t":"A：講者在研討會上簡報之前應該在哪裡等候？他們可以帶自己的筆電嗎？ B：他們應該在【後台】、也就是大廳後方的小房間等候，那裡有椅子、水和電源插座，所以他們上台前可以先用筆電檢查投影片。"},{"w":"costume","p":"n.","d":"special clothes an actor wears to look like a character","c":"戲服；服裝","s":"A: Why is the marketing team spending so much money on clothes for the history video about our company's first factory? B: Each actor needs a costume that looks like the clothes workers wore in the 1960s, because the video should look real, and the old photos show exactly what everyone was wearing back then.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊為了那支關於我們公司第一間工廠的歷史影片，花那麼多錢在服裝上？ B：每位演員都需要一套看起來像1960年代工人穿著的【戲服】，因為影片要看起來真實，而舊照片清楚顯示了當時每個人穿的衣服。"},{"w":"makeup","p":"n.","d":"colors and creams put on the face to change how it looks","c":"化妝；彩妝","s":"A: Why do the managers have to arrive at the studio an hour before the filming of the company interview video starts? B: The makeup artist needs time to prepare their faces, because the bright studio lights can make people look pale or shiny on camera, and she wants everyone to look healthy and natural.","t":"A：為什麼經理們必須在公司訪談影片開拍前一小時抵達攝影棚？ B：【化妝】師需要時間幫他們的臉做準備，因為攝影棚明亮的燈光會讓人在鏡頭前看起來蒼白或油亮，她希望每個人看起來都健康自然。"},{"w":"scene","p":"n.","d":"one part of a film or play that happens in one place","c":"場景；一場戲","s":"A: Which part of the new commercial do you think the customers will remember most after they see it on television? B: I think they will remember the final scene, where the whole family sits around the table and shares our frozen dumplings, because it is warm, simple, and shows the product clearly.","t":"A：你覺得顧客在電視上看到新廣告後，會對哪個部分印象最深？ B：我想他們會記得最後一【場戲】，全家人圍坐在餐桌旁分享我們的冷凍水餃，因為那一幕溫馨、簡單，又能清楚呈現產品。"},{"w":"lead","p":"n.","d":"the main part in a play or film, or the actor who plays it","c":"主角","s":"A: Who is going to play the main part in the musical that our company is sponsoring at the arts festival this summer? B: A young singer from Kaohsiung got the lead after a long competition with many other performers, and the director says her strong voice will help the show sell lots of tickets.","t":"A：誰要在我們公司今年夏天於藝術節贊助的音樂劇中擔任主要角色？ B：一位來自高雄的年輕歌手在和許多其他表演者激烈競爭後拿到了【主角】，導演說她渾厚的嗓音將幫助這齣戲賣出很多票。"},{"w":"supporting","p":"adj.","d":"(of an actor or part) less important than the main part","c":"配角的；輔助的","s":"A: Did the actor from our company's training video win any prizes at the short film festival last month? B: Yes, he won the award for best supporting actor, because even though he only appeared in a few scenes as the helpful coworker, his acting made the whole story feel more real.","t":"A：我們公司培訓影片中的那位演員，上個月在短片影展有得到任何獎項嗎？ B：有，他獲得了最佳【男配角】獎，因為雖然他只在幾場戲中飾演樂於助人的同事，但他的演技讓整個故事感覺更真實。"},{"w":"career","p":"n.","d":"the job or series of jobs a person does for a long time","c":"職業生涯；事業","s":"A: Why did the well-known TV actor agree to teach a public speaking workshop for our sales staff next month? B: He started his career as a salesperson before he became an actor, so he understands how hard it is to talk to customers, and he wants to share his speaking skills with young employees.","t":"A：為什麼那位知名電視演員同意下個月為我們的業務人員教授公眾演說工作坊？ B：他在成為演員之前，是以業務員開始他的【職業生涯】的，所以他了解和顧客交談有多難，也想和年輕員工分享他的說話技巧。"},{"w":"applause","p":"n.","d":"the sound of people clapping their hands to show they liked something","c":"掌聲","s":"A: How did the employees respond when the CEO announced the year-end bonuses at the end of the company party last night? B: There was loud applause that lasted for almost a minute, and some people even stood on their chairs and cheered, because the bonuses were much bigger than everyone had expected this year.","t":"A：昨晚公司派對結束時執行長宣布年終獎金，員工們有什麼反應？ B：現場響起了幾乎持續一分鐘的熱烈【掌聲】，有些人甚至站到椅子上歡呼，因為今年的獎金比大家預期的多很多。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Ad 廣告","cards":[{"w":"advertise","p":"v.","d":"to tell people about a product, service, or job in public so they will want it","c":"做廣告；刊登廣告","s":"A: Our new bakery opened last week, but very few customers have come in, so what do you think we should do to bring in more people from the neighborhood? B: I think we should advertise on the local radio station and in the community newspaper, because many older residents still listen and read them every morning before work.","t":"A：我們的新麵包店上週開幕了，但很少有客人上門，你覺得我們該怎麼做才能吸引更多附近的居民？ B：我認為我們應該在地方廣播電台和社區報紙上【刊登廣告】，因為許多年長的居民每天早上上班前仍然會收聽和閱讀它們。"},{"w":"advertising","p":"n.","d":"the business or activity of making and showing ads","c":"廣告業；廣告活動","s":"A: Why did the marketing director ask for a much larger budget at yesterday's meeting with the finance team? B: She explained that our competitors spend twice as much on advertising as we do, and if we don't increase our spending on television and online ads, we will lose customers to them this year.","t":"A：為什麼行銷總監在昨天和財務團隊的會議上要求大幅增加預算？ B：她解釋說，我們的競爭對手在【廣告】上的花費是我們的兩倍，如果我們不增加電視和網路廣告的支出，今年就會把客戶輸給他們。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"an activity, such as a special price, that helps sell a product","c":"促銷；宣傳活動","s":"A: Have you seen all the customers waiting outside the electronics store this morning, even before the doors opened? B: Yes, the store is running a special promotion this weekend, so anyone who buys a new laptop gets a free printer and a two-year warranty, and many people want to take advantage of it.","t":"A：你有看到今天早上電子產品店外面等候的那些客人嗎？甚至在開門之前就在排了。 B：有啊，這家店這個週末在舉辦特別【促銷活動】，任何購買新筆電的人都能獲得一台免費印表機和兩年保固，所以很多人想好好把握。"},{"w":"promote","p":"v.","d":"to help sell something by telling people about it","c":"推廣；促銷；宣傳","s":"A: The company is launching a new line of healthy snacks next month, so how are we going to tell people about them? B: We plan to promote the snacks at gyms and sports events, where we will hand out free samples and discount coupons to customers who care about eating well.","t":"A：公司下個月要推出新的健康零食系列，我們要怎麼讓大家知道呢？ B：我們打算在健身房和運動賽事上【推廣】這些零食，在那裡發送免費試吃品和折價券給重視飲食健康的顧客。"},{"w":"campaign","p":"n.","d":"a planned series of activities to sell a product or reach a goal","c":"（廣告）宣傳活動","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department staying late at the office every evening this week? B: They are preparing a big campaign for our new phone, which includes TV ads, posters in train stations, and online videos, and everything has to be ready before the product goes on sale next Monday.","t":"A：為什麼行銷部的每個人這週每天晚上都在辦公室待到很晚？ B：他們正在為我們的新手機準備一個大型【宣傳活動】，包括電視廣告、火車站的海報和網路影片，而且一切都必須在產品下週一開賣前準備好。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"the name of a product made by a particular company","c":"品牌；商標","s":"A: Why do so many shoppers pay more for this coffee when the supermarket's own coffee looks almost the same? B: Most people trust this brand because it has been popular for over fifty years, and they believe the quality is always good, so they are happy to spend a little extra money for it.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多購物者願意花更多錢買這款咖啡，而超市自有的咖啡看起來幾乎一樣？ B：大多數人信任這個【品牌】，因為它已經流行了五十多年，而且他們相信品質一直都很好，所以他們很樂意為它多花一點錢。"},{"w":"branding","p":"n.","d":"the design, name, and image a company uses so people recognize it","c":"品牌形象；品牌塑造","s":"A: Our small tea shop has good products, so why did the owner hire a design company to change our logo and cups? B: She thinks our branding looks old-fashioned, and a fresh logo, modern colors, and matching packaging will help young customers remember us and recognize our shop from across the street.","t":"A：我們的小茶店產品很好，為什麼老闆要請設計公司更換我們的標誌和杯子？ B：她認為我們的【品牌形象】看起來很過時，而新的標誌、現代的顏色和搭配的包裝能幫助年輕顧客記住我們，並且從對街就認出我們的店。"},{"w":"commercial","p":"n.","d":"an ad on television or radio","c":"（電視或廣播）廣告","s":"A: How did you first hear about the new sports drink that everyone in the office is talking about? B: I saw a funny thirty-second commercial on TV during the basketball game last night, and it showed famous players drinking it after a hard practice, so I bought a bottle on my way to work.","t":"A：你最初是怎麼聽說辦公室裡大家都在談論的那款新運動飲料的？ B：我昨晚看籃球比賽時在電視上看到一支有趣的三十秒【廣告】，畫面中知名球員在辛苦練習後喝它，所以我在上班途中買了一瓶。"},{"w":"slogan","p":"n.","d":"a short, easy-to-remember phrase used in ads","c":"標語；口號","s":"A: The design team has finished the new poster for our airline, but do you think the words at the bottom are good enough? B: I think the slogan is too long, because customers only look at a poster for a few seconds, so we need a short and simple phrase that people can remember easily.","t":"A：設計團隊已經完成了我們航空公司的新海報，但你覺得底部的文字夠好嗎？ B：我認為那句【標語】太長了，因為顧客只會看海報幾秒鐘，所以我們需要一句簡短又容易讓人記住的話。"},{"w":"headline","p":"n.","d":"the title in large letters at the top of an article or ad","c":"標題；大標","s":"A: Why did the editor ask us to rewrite the top of the advertisement for the newspaper before it goes to print tomorrow? B: She said the headline was not exciting enough, and since most readers only see the large words at the top of the page, they must be strong enough to make people stop and read more.","t":"A：為什麼編輯要求我們在明天付印前重寫報紙廣告的頂端部分？ B：她說那個【標題】不夠吸引人，而因為大部分讀者只會看到頁面頂端的大字，所以它們必須夠有力，才能讓人停下來繼續閱讀。"},{"w":"copy","p":"n.","d":"the written words used in an ad","c":"廣告文案；廣告文字","s":"A: The pictures for our new hotel brochure look beautiful, but who is going to write the text that goes next to them? B: We hired a freelance writer to prepare the copy, and she will describe the rooms, the pool, and the restaurant in a friendly way that makes families want to book a holiday with us.","t":"A：我們新飯店手冊的照片看起來很漂亮，但誰要撰寫旁邊的文字呢？ B：我們聘請了一位自由撰稿人來準備【廣告文案】，她會以親切的方式描述客房、游泳池和餐廳，讓家庭想要向我們預訂假期。"},{"w":"target","p":"v.","d":"to aim a product or ad at a particular group of people","c":"以…為目標；鎖定","s":"A: Our new video game is selling well in Japan, but why are sales so low in Europe and North America? B: The marketing team decided to target teenagers in those regions with ads on social media apps, but most of our real players are adults in their thirties who rarely use those apps at all.","t":"A：我們的新電玩遊戲在日本賣得很好，但為什麼在歐洲和北美的銷量這麼低？ B：行銷團隊決定在那些地區透過社群媒體應用程式的廣告來【鎖定】青少年，但我們真正的玩家大多是三十多歲的成年人，他們很少使用那些應用程式。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch, read, or listen to something","c":"觀眾；聽眾；受眾","s":"A: Should we show our new advertisement during the late-night news or during the morning cartoons on Saturday? B: Since our product is a toy for young children, the morning time is better, because the audience at that hour is mostly kids and their parents, who are exactly the people we want to sell to.","t":"A：我們應該在深夜新聞時段還是週六早上的卡通時段播放我們的新廣告？ B：既然我們的產品是給幼童的玩具，早上的時段比較好，因為那個時間的【觀眾】大多是孩子和他們的父母，正是我們想要銷售的對象。"},{"w":"reach","p":"v.","d":"to be seen or heard by a group of people","c":"觸及；接觸到（受眾）","s":"A: Why did the company decide to put its ads on a popular music app instead of in printed magazines this year? B: The manager believes we can reach millions of young listeners every day through the app, while magazine sales have fallen a lot, so fewer people would see our ads in print.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年決定把廣告放在熱門音樂應用程式上，而不是印刷雜誌上？ B：經理相信透過這個應用程式，我們每天可以【觸及】數百萬年輕聽眾，而雜誌銷量已經大幅下滑，所以在紙本上看到我們廣告的人會比較少。"},{"w":"impression","p":"n.","d":"one time that an online ad is shown to a person","c":"（廣告）曝光次數；印象","s":"A: The report says our online banner ad was shown two million times last month, but why are the managers still unhappy? B: Each impression only means the ad appeared on someone's screen, so although the number looks big, very few people actually opened it or bought anything from our website.","t":"A：報告說我們的網路橫幅廣告上個月被顯示了兩百萬次，但為什麼經理們還是不滿意？ B：每一次【曝光】只代表廣告出現在某人的螢幕上，所以雖然數字看起來很大，但實際上打開它或在我們網站上購買東西的人非常少。"},{"w":"engagement","p":"n.","d":"how much people react to and take part in content, such as liking or sharing","c":"互動；參與度","s":"A: Our posts on social media get thousands of views, so why does the marketing manager want to change our strategy? B: She is worried about low engagement, because people see the posts but rarely like, share, or comment on them, which means they are not really interested in our products or our company.","t":"A：我們在社群媒體上的貼文有數千次瀏覽，為什麼行銷經理想要改變我們的策略？ B：她擔心【互動】程度偏低，因為人們看到貼文，卻很少按讚、分享或留言，這表示他們對我們的產品或公司並不是真的感興趣。"},{"w":"click","p":"n.","d":"the act of pressing a mouse button or tapping a link on a screen","c":"點擊","s":"A: How do we know whether people are interested in the new online ad for our cooking classes? B: Every click on the ad takes a visitor to our sign-up page, so the system counts how many people want more information, and so far more than five hundred people have visited the page this week.","t":"A：我們怎麼知道大家是否對我們烹飪課的新網路廣告感興趣？ B：廣告上的每一次【點擊】都會把訪客帶到我們的報名頁面，所以系統會計算有多少人想要更多資訊，到目前為止，這週已經有超過五百人造訪了該頁面。"},{"w":"conversion","p":"n.","d":"the act of a visitor or viewer becoming a paying customer","c":"轉換（指訪客變成顧客）","s":"A: Thousands of people visited our online shoe store after the holiday ads started, so why are sales still disappointing? B: Our conversion rate is very low, which means most visitors look at the shoes but leave without buying, so we need to make the checkout page faster and offer free delivery to change their minds.","t":"A：假期廣告開始後，有數千人造訪我們的網路鞋店，為什麼銷量還是令人失望？ B：我們的【轉換】率非常低，這表示大部分訪客看了鞋子卻沒買就離開了，所以我們需要讓結帳頁面更快，並提供免運來改變他們的想法。"},{"w":"endorsement","p":"n.","d":"public support for a product by a famous person, often for money","c":"代言；背書","s":"A: Sales of our running shoes doubled in only two months, so what was the main reason for this sudden success? B: We got an endorsement from a famous Olympic runner, and after she said in interviews that she wears our shoes every day, many sports fans started trusting our products and buying them.","t":"A：我們的跑鞋銷量在短短兩個月內翻倍，這突然成功的主要原因是什麼？ B：我們獲得了一位知名奧運跑者的【代言】，在她於訪談中說她每天都穿我們的鞋之後，許多運動迷開始信任並購買我們的產品。"},{"w":"testimonial","p":"n.","d":"a statement from a customer saying a product or service is good","c":"推薦；（顧客）見證","s":"A: Our website explains all the features of the language software, but how can we make new visitors trust us more? B: We could add a testimonial from a happy customer, such as a nurse who passed her English test after using our program for three months, because people believe real users more than companies.","t":"A：我們的網站說明了這款語言軟體的所有功能，但我們要怎麼讓新訪客更信任我們？ B：我們可以加入一位滿意顧客的【推薦見證】，例如一位使用我們的程式三個月後就通過英文考試的護理師，因為人們比較相信真正的使用者，而不是公司。"},{"w":"influencer","p":"n.","d":"a person who affects what others buy, often through social media","c":"網紅；有影響力的人","s":"A: Why is our cosmetics company paying a young woman to post videos about our new lipstick on her social media account? B: She is a popular influencer with over a million followers, and when she shows a product in her videos, many of her fans go online and buy it within a few days.","t":"A：為什麼我們的化妝品公司要付錢給一位年輕女性，請她在社群媒體帳號上發布關於我們新口紅的影片？ B：她是一位擁有超過一百萬名追蹤者的熱門【網紅】，當她在影片中展示一項產品時，她的許多粉絲會在幾天內上網購買。"},{"w":"placement","p":"n.","d":"the position where a product or ad is put so people will see it","c":"（商品或廣告的）擺放位置；置入","s":"A: The supermarket has agreed to sell our new cereal, but why are we paying an extra fee to the store? B: The fee is for better placement, so our boxes will sit at eye level near the entrance instead of on the bottom shelf, where busy shoppers might walk past without noticing them.","t":"A：超市已經同意販售我們的新穀片，但為什麼我們還要付額外的費用給店家？ B：那筆費用是為了取得更好的【陳列位置】，這樣我們的盒子就會擺在入口附近、與視線同高的地方，而不是在最底層的架子上，因為忙碌的購物者可能會走過去而沒注意到。"},{"w":"display","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement of products for people to look at in a store","c":"陳列；展示","s":"A: The new perfume arrives at our department store on Friday, so how should we show it to customers in the busy holiday season? B: Let's set up a large display near the main entrance with bright lights, flowers, and free samples, so everyone who walks into the store will notice the perfume right away.","t":"A：新香水週五會到我們百貨公司，在繁忙的假期季節中，我們該如何展示給顧客看？ B：我們在主要入口附近布置一個大型【展示區】，搭配明亮的燈光、花卉和免費試用品，讓每個走進店裡的人都能馬上注意到這款香水。"},{"w":"broadcast","p":"v.","d":"to send out a program or ad on TV or radio","c":"播放；廣播","s":"A: Our company paid a lot of money for a two-minute ad, so when will people actually be able to watch it on television? B: The TV station will broadcast it during the final match of the football championship next Sunday evening, when millions of fans across the country will be sitting in front of their screens.","t":"A：我們公司為一支兩分鐘的廣告付了很多錢，那麼大家到底什麼時候能在電視上看到它？ B：電視台將在下週日晚上的足球錦標賽決賽期間【播放】它，屆時全國數百萬名球迷都會坐在螢幕前。"},{"w":"sponsor","p":"v.","d":"to pay for an event or team in return for advertising","c":"贊助","s":"A: Why does our bank's logo appear on the shirts of the local basketball team this season? B: Our bank decided to sponsor the team, which means we pay for their uniforms and travel costs, and in return our name is shown at every game, so thousands of local families see it each week.","t":"A：為什麼這一季我們銀行的標誌出現在本地籃球隊的球衣上？ B：我們銀行決定【贊助】這支球隊，也就是說我們支付他們的制服和交通費用，作為回報，我們的名字會在每場比賽中出現，所以每週都有數千個本地家庭看到它。"},{"w":"persuasive","p":"adj.","d":"able to make people believe or do something","c":"有說服力的","s":"A: Your sales presentation to the hotel group went very well, so how did you convince them to sign a three-year contract? B: I think my argument was persuasive because I showed them clear numbers proving that our cleaning service saves money, and I also shared positive comments from other hotels we work with.","t":"A：你對飯店集團的銷售簡報非常成功，你是怎麼說服他們簽下三年合約的？ B：我想我的論點很有【說服力】，因為我向他們展示了明確的數據，證明我們的清潔服務能省錢，而且我也分享了其他合作飯店的正面評價。"},{"w":"promotional","p":"adj.","d":"used to advertise a product or company","c":"促銷的；宣傳的","s":"A: We have a lot of extra pens, bags, and T-shirts with our company logo, so what should we do with them? B: Let's give them away at the trade fair next month as promotional gifts, because visitors love free items, and every time they use them, they will be reminded of our company and our services.","t":"A：我們有很多印有公司標誌的多餘筆、袋子和T恤，該怎麼處理它們？ B：我們下個月在商展上把它們當作【宣傳】贈品送出去吧，因為參觀者喜歡免費物品，而且每次使用時，都會讓他們想起我們公司和我們的服務。"},{"w":"viral","p":"adj.","d":"spreading very quickly to many people on the internet","c":"（網路上）迅速傳播的；爆紅的","s":"A: I heard that our small restaurant suddenly became busy last week, so what happened to bring in all those new customers? B: A customer filmed our chef making noodles by hand and posted it online, and the video went viral, so millions of people watched it in just three days and many came to try our food.","t":"A：我聽說我們的小餐廳上週突然變得很忙，到底發生什麼事，帶來了這麼多新客人？ B：一位顧客拍下我們的主廚手工製作麵條的影片並上傳到網路上，結果那支影片【爆紅】，短短三天內就有數百萬人觀看，很多人都來品嚐我們的食物。"},{"w":"catchy","p":"adj.","d":"easy to remember and pleasant to hear","c":"易記的；朗朗上口的","s":"A: Why do so many people in the office keep singing the same little song while they work this week? B: It's from the new ice cream ad on the radio, and the music is so catchy that once you hear it, you cannot stop humming it all day, which is exactly what the company wanted.","t":"A：為什麼這週辦公室裡這麼多人一邊工作一邊哼著同一首小歌？ B：那是電台新冰淇淋廣告裡的歌，旋律非常【朗朗上口】，你一聽到就會一整天停不下來地哼，這正是那家公司想要的效果。"},{"w":"compelling","p":"adj.","d":"so interesting or strong that you pay attention or are convinced","c":"引人入勝的；令人信服的","s":"A: Many companies made short films for the charity competition, so why did the judges choose our video as the winner? B: They said our story about the old fisherman and his daughter was very compelling, and it made viewers feel strong emotions, so they wanted to keep watching until the very end.","t":"A：很多公司都為慈善比賽拍攝了短片，為什麼評審選擇我們的影片為冠軍？ B：他們說我們關於老漁夫和他女兒的故事非常【引人入勝】，讓觀眾產生強烈的情感，所以他們想一直看到最後。"},{"w":"strategically","p":"adv.","d":"in a carefully planned way to reach a goal","c":"策略性地；戰略上","s":"A: Why did the coffee chain open its new branches next to train stations and large office buildings instead of in quiet neighborhoods? B: The company placed them strategically, because thousands of busy workers pass those places every morning, and many of them want a quick cup of coffee on their way to work.","t":"A：為什麼那家咖啡連鎖店把新分店開在火車站和大型辦公大樓旁邊，而不是安靜的住宅區？ B：公司是【策略性地】安排它們的位置，因為每天早上都有數千名忙碌的上班族經過那些地方，其中很多人在上班途中想要一杯快速取得的咖啡。"},{"w":"creatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a new and imaginative way","c":"有創意地；創造性地","s":"A: Our marketing budget is very small this year, so how can we compete with the big companies that spend millions on TV? B: We have to think creatively, for example by making funny short videos with our own staff, running online contests, and working with local shops to share customers at no extra cost.","t":"A：我們今年的行銷預算很少，要怎麼和那些在電視上花數百萬的大公司競爭？ B：我們必須【有創意地】思考，例如用自己的員工拍攝有趣的短片、舉辦網路競賽，並和本地商店合作互相分享顧客，而且不需額外費用。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Adventure 冒險","cards":[{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it","c":"探索；探險；考察","s":"A: We have a free afternoon after the sales conference in Lisbon, so what would you like to do before our flight leaves tomorrow morning? B: I'd love to explore the old part of the city on foot, because the hotel receptionist said there are small cafés, markets, and museums hidden in every narrow street.","t":"A：我們在里斯本的業務研討會結束後有一個空閒的下午，所以在明天早上班機起飛前你想做什麼？ B：我很想步行【探索】這座城市的舊城區，因為飯店櫃檯人員說每條窄巷裡都藏著小咖啡館、市場和博物館。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"the act of traveling through a place to find out about it","c":"探索；探勘；考察","s":"A: Why did the travel company decide to add a new tour to its catalog this year, even though most of its customers prefer beach holidays? B: More young professionals are asking for trips that include exploration of caves and mountain villages, so the managers believe this kind of tour will sell well next summer.","t":"A：為什麼這家旅行社今年決定在型錄裡增加新的行程，雖然大部分客人比較喜歡海灘度假？ B：越來越多年輕上班族要求包含洞穴和山村【探索】的旅程，所以經理們相信這類行程明年夏天會賣得很好。"},{"w":"journey","p":"n.","d":"a trip from one place to another, often a long one","c":"旅程；旅行","s":"A: How was your trip to the factory in the north last week, and did you manage to finish the safety inspection before the weekend? B: The journey took nearly nine hours by train and bus because of heavy snow, but I arrived in time and finished the inspection on Friday afternoon.","t":"A：你上週去北部工廠的行程怎麼樣，有在週末前完成安全檢查嗎？ B：因為大雪，這趟【旅程】搭火車和巴士花了將近九個小時，不過我及時抵達，並在週五下午完成了檢查。"},{"w":"expedition","p":"n.","d":"an organized trip made for a special purpose, such as science or exploring","c":"遠征；探險；考察旅行","s":"A: I heard our outdoor equipment company is sponsoring a group of climbers this spring, so where exactly are they planning to go? B: They are joining an expedition to the Himalayas for six weeks, and they will test our new tents and jackets in very cold and windy conditions.","t":"A：我聽說我們戶外用品公司今年春天要贊助一群登山客，他們究竟打算去哪裡？ B：他們要參加為期六週的喜馬拉雅山【遠征】，並會在非常寒冷且強風的環境中測試我們的新帳篷和外套。"},{"w":"quest","p":"n.","d":"a long search for something important or difficult to find","c":"追求；探索；尋找","s":"A: Why has the hotel group sent its chef to visit small farms in three different countries during the past two months? B: The chef is on a quest for the freshest local ingredients, because the company wants every restaurant menu to feature special dishes that guests cannot find anywhere else.","t":"A：為什麼這家飯店集團在過去兩個月內派主廚去拜訪三個不同國家的小農場？ B：主廚正在【尋找】最新鮮的在地食材，因為公司希望每間餐廳的菜單都能推出客人在其他地方吃不到的特色料理。"},{"w":"venture","p":"n.","d":"a new business or activity that involves some risk","c":"（有風險的）事業；冒險","s":"A: Is it true that Mr. Tanaka is leaving the bank next month after working there for more than fifteen years? B: Yes, he and his sister are starting a new business venture together, a small travel agency that plans hiking and camping trips for families who live in big cities.","t":"A：田中先生在銀行工作了十五年以上，下個月要離職是真的嗎？ B：是的，他和他姊姊要一起展開一項新的商業【冒險事業】，開一間小型旅行社，為住在大城市的家庭規劃健行和露營旅程。"},{"w":"discovery","p":"n.","d":"the act of finding something that was not known before","c":"發現；發現的事物","s":"A: Why are so many reporters waiting outside the museum this morning, and why has the director canceled all of her afternoon meetings? B: A team of researchers made an exciting discovery of ancient coins near the river last week, and the director will present them to the public at noon today.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有這麼多記者在博物館外面等候，館長又為什麼取消了她下午所有的會議？ B：一組研究人員上週在河邊有了令人振奮的古錢幣【發現】，館長今天中午將向大眾展示這些錢幣。"},{"w":"trail","p":"n.","d":"a path through the countryside, forest, or mountains","c":"小徑；步道","s":"A: Our team-building weekend is next month, so do you know a good place where twenty employees can walk together safely? B: The national park has a wide forest trail that takes about three hours to complete, and there are rest areas, clean toilets, and a small café near the end.","t":"A：我們的團隊建立週末活動在下個月，你知道哪裡有適合二十名員工安全地一起健行的好地方嗎？ B：國家公園有一條寬敞的森林【步道】，大約三個小時可以走完，沿途有休息區、乾淨的廁所，終點附近還有一間小咖啡館。"},{"w":"voyage","p":"n.","d":"a long trip, especially by sea or in space","c":"航行；航程","s":"A: Why did the cruise company hire so many extra kitchen staff and entertainers for the trip that starts next Monday? B: It is a three-week voyage across the Pacific Ocean with more than two thousand passengers, so the ship needs extra workers to prepare meals and keep guests busy every evening.","t":"A：為什麼郵輪公司為下週一出發的旅程額外雇用了這麼多廚房人員和表演者？ B：那是一趟橫越太平洋、為期三週的【航行】，船上有兩千多名乘客，所以需要更多員工來準備餐點，並讓客人每晚都有活動可以參加。"},{"w":"escape","p":"n.","d":"a way of forgetting about daily problems or a stressful situation for a short time","c":"逃離；逃避；解脫","s":"A: You always look so relaxed when you come back to the office on Monday, so what do you usually do on weekends? B: My husband and I drive to a quiet cabin in the mountains, and it is the perfect escape from the noise of the city and the pressure of our busy jobs.","t":"A：你每週一回到辦公室時看起來總是很放鬆，你週末通常都做些什麼？ B：我和我先生會開車到山上一間安靜的小木屋，那是【逃離】城市喧囂和繁忙工作壓力的完美去處。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the possibility that something bad or dangerous may happen","c":"風險；危險","s":"A: Should we let our guests go kayaking on the lake tomorrow afternoon if the weather report says there might be strong winds? B: I don't think so, because there is a serious risk that the boats could turn over, and our insurance does not cover water activities in bad weather.","t":"A：如果氣象預報說明天下午可能有強風，我們還應該讓客人去湖上划獨木舟嗎？ B：我認為不應該，因為船有翻覆的嚴重【風險】，而且我們的保險不涵蓋惡劣天氣下的水上活動。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"n.","d":"something new and difficult that tests your skill or ability","c":"挑戰；難題","s":"A: Why did you accept the job in Singapore when you already had a good position and a comfortable life here in Taipei? B: I wanted a new challenge, and managing a team of people from five different countries will help me improve my leadership and communication skills much faster.","t":"A：你在台北已經有不錯的職位和舒適的生活，為什麼還接受新加坡的工作？ B：我想要一個新的【挑戰】，管理來自五個不同國家的團隊會幫助我更快提升領導和溝通能力。"},{"w":"thrill","p":"n.","d":"a sudden strong feeling of excitement and pleasure","c":"興奮；激動；刺激","s":"A: Why do you think the zip-line tour is the most popular activity at the resort, even though the ticket is quite expensive? B: Most guests love the thrill of flying over the jungle at high speed, and they also enjoy the beautiful view of the waterfalls and the ocean from above.","t":"A：雖然票價相當貴，你為什麼認為高空滑索行程是度假村最受歡迎的活動？ B：大部分客人都喜歡在叢林上空高速飛越的【刺激】感，也很享受從上方看到瀑布和海洋的美麗景色。"},{"w":"excitement","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being very happy and eager about something","c":"興奮；激動","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department talking so loudly and smiling so much this morning? B: There is a lot of excitement because the manager just told us that our team won the annual sales award, and the prize is a four-day trip to Bali for everyone in the department.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上行銷部的每個人都說話這麼大聲、笑得這麼開心？ B：大家都很【興奮】，因為經理剛告訴我們，我們團隊贏得了年度業績獎，獎品是全部門同仁四天的峇里島之旅。"},{"w":"wilderness","p":"n.","d":"a large natural area where nobody lives and nature has not been changed","c":"荒野；未開發地區","s":"A: Should I bring my laptop and phone charger on the company's survival training trip next week? B: You can bring them, but they won't be very useful, because we will spend three days in the wilderness, far from any towns, roads, or electricity, and there is no phone signal there.","t":"A：下週公司的野外求生訓練之旅，我應該帶筆電和手機充電器嗎？ B：你可以帶，但用處不大，因為我們會在【荒野】中待三天，遠離任何城鎮、道路和電力，那裡也沒有手機訊號。"},{"w":"survival","p":"n.","d":"the state of continuing to live or exist, especially after danger or difficulty","c":"生存；存活","s":"A: Why did the hiking club ask every new member to attend a two-day training course before joining the mountain trips? B: The course teaches basic survival skills, such as how to find clean water, build a simple shelter, and stay warm if someone gets lost in bad weather.","t":"A：為什麼登山社要求每位新成員在參加登山活動前，先上兩天的訓練課程？ B：這門課教基本的【求生】技巧，例如如何找到乾淨的水、搭建簡單的避難所，以及有人在惡劣天氣中迷路時如何保暖。"},{"w":"brave","p":"adj.","d":"willing to do things that are dangerous or difficult without showing fear","c":"勇敢的","s":"A: Did you hear what happened at the hotel pool yesterday afternoon when a small child fell into the deep water? B: Yes, a brave young lifeguard jumped in immediately and pulled the child out, and the hotel manager has decided to give him a special award at next week's staff meeting.","t":"A：你有聽說昨天下午飯店泳池發生的事嗎？有個小孩掉進了深水區。 B：有，一位【勇敢的】年輕救生員立刻跳下水把孩子救上來，飯店經理決定在下週的員工會議上頒給他特別獎。"},{"w":"daring","p":"adj.","d":"brave enough to do something dangerous, new, or unusual","c":"大膽的；勇於冒險的","s":"A: What did the investors think about the plan to open our first restaurant on a boat that travels along the river every evening? B: They said it was a daring idea that nobody in the city had tried before, but they agreed to fund it because tourists would probably love the experience.","t":"A：投資人對於我們把第一間餐廳開在每晚沿河航行的船上這個計畫有什麼看法？ B：他們說這是一個城裡從未有人嘗試過的【大膽的】構想，但他們同意出資，因為觀光客很可能會喜愛這種體驗。"},{"w":"fearless","p":"adj.","d":"not afraid of anything","c":"無畏的；大無畏的","s":"A: Who do you think should guide the group of guests on the rock-climbing tour this Saturday morning? B: Maria would be perfect, because she is fearless on steep cliffs, she has ten years of experience, and she always explains the safety rules clearly so that nervous beginners feel calm.","t":"A：你認為這週六早上應該由誰帶領客人參加攀岩行程？ B：瑪麗亞再適合不過了，因為她在陡峭的懸崖上【毫無畏懼】，有十年的經驗，而且總是把安全規則解釋得很清楚，讓緊張的初學者感到安心。"},{"w":"wild","p":"adj.","d":"living or growing in nature, not kept or controlled by people","c":"野生的；未經馴化的","s":"A: Is it safe for our tour group to leave food outside the tents at the campsite tonight after dinner? B: No, the park ranger warned us that wild animals such as bears and foxes often come close to the camp at night, so we must lock all the food in the cars.","t":"A：今晚晚餐後，我們旅行團把食物留在營地帳篷外面安全嗎？ B：不安全，公園管理員警告我們，熊和狐狸等【野生】動物晚上常會靠近營地，所以我們必須把所有食物鎖在車裡。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"far away from towns, cities, and other people","c":"偏遠的；遙遠的","s":"A: Why does it take so long to deliver our products to the new customer in the mountains, even when we use express shipping? B: The village is in a very remote area with only one narrow road, so the delivery trucks can go there just twice a week when the weather is good.","t":"A：為什麼即使用快遞，把產品送到山區的新客戶那裡還是要花這麼久？ B：那個村莊位於非常【偏遠的】地區，只有一條狹窄的道路，所以貨車只有在天氣好的時候，每週才能去兩次。"},{"w":"unpredictable","p":"adj.","d":"changing so often that you cannot know what will happen","c":"無法預測的；難以預料的","s":"A: Should we hold the company picnic by the sea in early October, or is it better to plan an indoor event this year? B: I prefer an indoor event, because the weather near the coast is very unpredictable in autumn, and a sudden storm could ruin all the food and games we prepare.","t":"A：我們應該在十月初到海邊辦公司野餐，還是今年最好規劃室內活動？ B：我比較喜歡室內活動，因為秋天海岸附近的天氣非常【難以預測】，一場突來的暴風雨可能會毀了我們準備的所有食物和遊戲。"},{"w":"dangerous","p":"adj.","d":"able to hurt or harm people","c":"危險的","s":"A: Why did the tour company cancel the boat trip to the small island this afternoon, even though most passengers had already paid? B: The captain said the waves were too high and it was dangerous to sail, so the company is offering everyone a full refund or a free ticket for another day.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社今天下午取消了去小島的船程，即使大部分乘客都已經付款了？ B：船長說浪太高，出航很【危險】，所以公司提供每個人全額退款，或改天使用的免費船票。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"something that happens to you and affects how you feel","c":"經歷；體驗","s":"A: How was your weekend trip to the desert with the new clients from Dubai, and did they enjoy the activities you planned? B: It was an amazing experience for all of us, because we rode camels, watched the sunset from the sand dunes, and ate a traditional dinner under the stars.","t":"A：你和杜拜的新客戶去沙漠的週末之旅怎麼樣？他們喜歡你安排的活動嗎？ B：對我們所有人來說都是一次很棒的【經歷】，因為我們騎了駱駝、在沙丘上看日落，還在星空下吃了傳統晚餐。"},{"w":"wander","p":"v.","d":"to walk slowly around a place without a clear direction or purpose","c":"閒逛；漫步","s":"A: What did you do during the long break between your two meetings in Kyoto yesterday? B: I decided to wander through the quiet streets near the old temples for about two hours, and I found a lovely tea shop where I bought some gifts for my coworkers back home.","t":"A：昨天你在京都兩場會議之間的長時間空檔做了什麼？ B：我決定在古寺附近安靜的街道上【漫步】大約兩個小時，還發現了一間很棒的茶舖，在那裡幫家鄉的同事買了一些禮物。"},{"w":"roam","p":"v.","d":"to move or travel freely around a large area","c":"漫遊；閒逛；徜徉","s":"A: What makes the safari park different from an ordinary zoo, and why are the tickets so popular with families? B: In the safari park, the animals can roam across large open fields instead of living in small cages, and visitors watch them safely from special buses with big windows.","t":"A：野生動物園和一般動物園有什麼不同？為什麼門票這麼受家庭歡迎？ B：在野生動物園裡，動物可以在廣大的開放草原上自由【漫遊】，而不是住在小籠子裡，遊客則從有大窗戶的特殊巴士上安全地觀賞牠們。"},{"w":"navigate","p":"v.","d":"to find the right way to go from one place to another","c":"導航；找路；駕駛（船、飛機等）","s":"A: How will we find the hotel if our phones lose signal while we are driving through the mountains tonight? B: Don't worry, Ken brought a paper map and a compass, and he learned how to navigate without GPS when he worked as a tour guide in Canada for five years.","t":"A：如果今晚我們開車穿越山區時手機沒有訊號，要怎麼找到飯店？ B：別擔心，肯帶了紙本地圖和指南針，他在加拿大當了五年導遊，學會了如何在沒有衛星導航的情況下【找路】。"},{"w":"trek","p":"v.","d":"to make a long, difficult journey, usually on foot","c":"長途跋涉；徒步旅行","s":"A: Why are the new hiking boots selling so quickly in our store this month, even though they cost more than the old model? B: Many customers plan to trek across the mountains during the holiday season, and they want strong, waterproof boots that will keep their feet dry and comfortable.","t":"A：為什麼新款登山靴這個月在我們店裡賣得這麼快，雖然它比舊款貴？ B：許多顧客計畫在假期期間徒步【長途跋涉】穿越山區，他們想要堅固又防水的靴子，讓雙腳保持乾燥舒適。"},{"w":"boldly","p":"adv.","d":"in a brave and confident way, without fear","c":"大膽地；勇敢地","s":"A: How did our small company manage to win the contract when three much larger firms were also competing for it? B: Our director spoke boldly at the final meeting, promised a faster delivery schedule, and showed the clients a creative plan that none of the other companies had thought of.","t":"A：當另外三家大得多的公司也在競爭時，我們這家小公司是怎麼贏得合約的？ B：我們的總監在最後一次會議上【大膽地】發言，承諾更快的交貨時程，還向客戶展示了其他公司都沒想到的創意企畫。"},{"w":"freely","p":"adv.","d":"without being controlled or limited","c":"自由地；無拘束地","s":"A: Do the guests on the island tour have to stay with the guide all day, or can they choose their own activities? B: After lunch, they can move around the island freely, so some people go swimming, others visit the local market, and a few just relax on the beach until the boat leaves.","t":"A：參加島嶼行程的客人必須整天跟著導遊，還是可以自己選擇活動？ B：午餐後他們可以在島上【自由地】活動，所以有些人去游泳，有些人逛當地市場，還有幾個人就在沙灘上放鬆到船開為止。"},{"w":"unexpectedly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that surprises you because you did not think it would happen","c":"出乎意料地；意外地","s":"A: Why didn't the hiking group reach the top of the mountain on Saturday, when they had planned the trip for months? B: The weather changed unexpectedly in the early afternoon, and the guide decided to turn back because thick clouds and strong rain made the path too slippery to continue.","t":"A：為什麼登山隊週六沒有登上山頂？他們可是計畫了好幾個月。 B：天氣在午後【出乎意料地】變了，因為濃厚的雲層和大雨讓山路太滑無法繼續，嚮導決定折返。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Advice 建議","cards":[{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone what you think they should do","c":"建議；勸告；忠告","s":"A: I'm thinking about buying a used delivery van for my flower shop, but I don't know much about cars, so what should I do first? B: I would advise you to ask a trusted mechanic to check the engine and brakes carefully before you sign anything, because repairs on old vans can be very expensive.","t":"A：我在考慮為我的花店買一輛二手送貨車，但我不太懂車，我應該先做什麼？ B：我會【建議】你在簽任何文件之前，先請一位信得過的技師仔細檢查引擎和煞車，因為舊貨車的維修費用可能非常高。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about how to do something","c":"指導；引導","s":"A: How are the new interns doing in their first month at the accounting firm, and have they made many mistakes with the reports? B: They are doing well, mostly because each intern works under the guidance of a senior accountant who checks their work every afternoon and answers their questions patiently.","t":"A：新來的實習生在會計師事務所的第一個月表現如何？他們的報告出了很多錯嗎？ B：他們表現得很好，主要是因為每位實習生都在一位資深會計師的【指導】下工作，那位會計師每天下午都會檢查他們的工作並耐心回答問題。"},{"w":"suggestion","p":"n.","d":"an idea or plan that you offer for someone to think about","c":"建議；提議","s":"A: The staff kitchen is always messy at the end of the day, and people keep complaining about it, so what can we do? B: I have a suggestion: let's make a simple weekly cleaning schedule and put it on the fridge, so each team takes care of the kitchen for one day.","t":"A：員工廚房每天下班時總是很亂，大家一直抱怨，我們能怎麼做？ B：我有一個【建議】：我們來做一張簡單的每週清潔值日表貼在冰箱上，讓每個小組各負責一天的廚房清潔。"},{"w":"recommendation","p":"n.","d":"advice about what is best to do or buy, often from an expert","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: Why did the company suddenly change its supplier of office chairs after using the same one for almost ten years? B: The safety committee made a recommendation after many employees complained about back pain, so the managers chose a new supplier that sells chairs with much better support.","t":"A：為什麼公司在用了同一家辦公椅供應商將近十年後突然換掉？ B：在許多員工抱怨背痛之後，安全委員會提出了一項【建議】，所以主管們選擇了一家販售支撐性好得多的椅子的新供應商。"},{"w":"counsel","p":"n.","d":"advice, especially from an older or more experienced person or a professional","c":"忠告；勸告；法律顧問","s":"A: You seemed so calm during the difficult contract talks with the Japanese company last month, so how did you prepare for them? B: Before the talks, I asked for counsel from our former director, who has negotiated with many Asian firms, and her advice helped me stay patient and polite.","t":"A：上個月和那家日本公司進行艱難的合約談判時，你看起來很冷靜，你是怎麼準備的？ B：在談判前，我向我們的前任總監尋求【忠告】，她和許多亞洲公司談判過，她的建議幫助我保持耐心和禮貌。"},{"w":"instruction","p":"n.","d":"information that tells you how to do or use something","c":"指示；說明；用法說明","s":"A: The new printer in the meeting room keeps showing an error message, so do you know how to fix it before the clients arrive? B: Read the instruction printed on the inside of the front cover, because it explains step by step how to remove stuck paper and restart the machine safely.","t":"A：會議室的新印表機一直出現錯誤訊息，你知道在客戶到之前要怎麼修好嗎？ B：去看印在前蓋內側的【說明】，上面一步一步解釋如何取出卡紙並安全地重新啟動機器。"},{"w":"tip","p":"n.","d":"a small but useful piece of practical advice","c":"訣竅；小建議；提示","s":"A: I have to give a speech in English at the international sales meeting next week, and I'm already very nervous about it, so can you help? B: Here's a useful tip that always works for me: practice in front of a mirror every night, and speak a little more slowly than you normally do.","t":"A：下週我必須在國際業務會議上用英文演講，我已經非常緊張了，你能幫幫我嗎？ B：這是一個對我總是很有用的【訣竅】：每天晚上對著鏡子練習，並且說話比平常稍微慢一點。"},{"w":"warning","p":"n.","d":"a statement telling someone about a possible danger or problem","c":"警告；預告","s":"A: Why did all the ships stay in the harbor this morning, even though the sky looked clear and the sea was calm? B: The weather office issued a storm warning late last night, saying that strong winds and heavy rain would reach the coast by noon, so the captains decided not to sail.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上所有船隻都留在港口，即使天空看起來很晴朗、海面也很平靜？ B：氣象局昨晚深夜發布了暴風雨【警報】，說強風和大雨中午前會抵達沿岸，所以船長們決定不出航。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give someone confidence or hope","c":"鼓勵；激勵","s":"A: How did Daniel manage to pass the difficult accounting exam on his third try, after failing it twice last year? B: His manager gave him a lot of encouragement, let him leave work early twice a week to study, and kept telling him that he had the skills to succeed.","t":"A：丹尼爾去年考了兩次都沒過，他是怎麼在第三次通過那個困難的會計考試的？ B：他的主管給了他很多【鼓勵】，讓他每週兩次提早下班去讀書，還不斷告訴他，他有成功的能力。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"comments about how well someone did something, given so they can improve","c":"回饋；意見","s":"A: How will we know whether guests are happy with the changes we made to the hotel restaurant last month? B: We can send them a short online survey after they check out, and their feedback will show us which dishes they liked and what we still need to improve.","t":"A：我們要怎麼知道客人對上個月飯店餐廳的改變是否滿意？ B：我們可以在他們退房後寄一份簡短的線上問卷，他們的【回饋】會讓我們知道他們喜歡哪些菜，以及我們還需要改進什麼。"},{"w":"consult","p":"v.","d":"to go to a person or a book for information or advice","c":"諮詢；請教；查閱","s":"A: The pain in my wrist has become much worse since I started typing for eight hours a day on the new project, so what should I do? B: You should consult a doctor this week, and you might also ask the office manager for a better keyboard and a soft wrist pad.","t":"A：自從我開始在新專案每天打字八個小時後，手腕就痛得更厲害了，我該怎麼辦？ B：你這週應該去【請教】醫生，也可以向辦公室經理要一個比較好的鍵盤和柔軟的護腕墊。"},{"w":"consultation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting with an expert to get advice","c":"諮詢；商議；會診","s":"A: I'd like to make my small restaurant more energy-efficient, but I have no idea where to start, so can you help me? B: The city offers a free consultation with an energy expert, who will visit your restaurant, check your kitchen equipment, and suggest simple ways to cut your electricity bills.","t":"A：我想讓我的小餐廳更節能，但完全不知道從何開始，你能幫我嗎？ B：市政府提供和能源專家的免費【諮詢】，專家會到你的餐廳檢查廚房設備，並建議簡單的方法來降低電費。"},{"w":"opinion","p":"n.","d":"what you think or believe about something","c":"意見；看法；見解","s":"A: The marketing team has prepared two different designs for the new product package, and we need to choose one by Friday. B: In my opinion, the blue design looks more modern and professional, but we should also show both designs to a few customers before we make the final decision.","t":"A：行銷團隊為新產品包裝準備了兩種不同的設計，我們必須在週五前選出一個。 B：依我的【看法】，藍色的設計看起來比較現代、專業，但在做最後決定前，我們也應該把兩種設計拿給幾位顧客看看。"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of thinking about something","c":"觀點；看法；角度","s":"A: Why did the director invite three young employees to join the planning meeting for next year's advertising campaign? B: She wanted a fresh perspective from people in their twenties, because the campaign is aimed at young customers, and the older managers may not understand what they really want.","t":"A：為什麼總監邀請三位年輕員工參加明年廣告活動的企畫會議？ B：她想要聽聽二十幾歲年輕人的新【觀點】，因為這次活動的對象是年輕顧客，而年長的主管們可能不了解他們真正想要什麼。"},{"w":"direction","p":"n.","d":"instructions or control that help someone know what to do","c":"指導；指揮；方向","s":"A: The new branch had very poor sales last year, so why are the numbers so much better this year? B: Under the direction of the new branch manager, the staff set clear monthly goals, improved their customer service, and started selling products online as well as in the store.","t":"A：新分店去年的業績很差，為什麼今年的數字好了這麼多？ B：在新分店經理的【指導】下，員工訂定了明確的每月目標、改善了顧客服務，並且除了店面之外也開始在網路上銷售產品。"},{"w":"input","p":"n.","d":"ideas, advice, or information that you give to help with a project","c":"意見；建議；投入","s":"A: Should we finish the budget plan ourselves this afternoon, or do we need to talk to anyone else in the company first? B: We need some input from the sales department before we finish, because they know which products will need more money for advertising during the holiday season.","t":"A：我們應該今天下午自己完成預算計畫，還是需要先和公司裡的其他人談談？ B：在完成之前，我們需要業務部的一些【意見】，因為他們知道哪些產品在假期期間需要更多的廣告經費。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is good and suitable","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: Our Korean clients are arriving on Thursday evening, and I want to take them somewhere nice for dinner after their long flight. B: I recommend the seafood restaurant near the harbor, because it is quiet enough for conversation, the service is excellent, and it has a beautiful view of the city lights.","t":"A：我們的韓國客戶週四晚上抵達，他們長途飛行後，我想帶他們去不錯的地方吃晚餐。 B：我【推薦】港口附近的那間海鮮餐廳，因為那裡夠安靜可以聊天，服務很好，還能欣賞美麗的城市夜景。"},{"w":"urge","p":"v.","d":"to strongly advise or try hard to persuade someone to do something","c":"力勸；敦促；催促","s":"A: Why did the IT department send another email to all staff this morning, when we already received one yesterday? B: They want to urge everyone to change their passwords before Friday, because several employees received fake emails last week that tried to steal their account information.","t":"A：為什麼資訊部今天早上又寄了一封信給全體員工？我們昨天已經收到一封了。 B：他們想【敦促】大家在週五前更改密碼，因為上週有幾位員工收到企圖竊取帳號資料的假電子郵件。"},{"w":"proposal","p":"n.","d":"a plan or idea that is formally suggested for people to consider","c":"提案；建議；計畫書","s":"A: What happened at the board meeting this morning, and did the directors agree to open a new office in Vietnam? B: They read the proposal carefully and liked most of it, but they asked us to add more details about costs and local hiring before they make a final decision next month.","t":"A：今天早上的董事會發生了什麼事？董事們同意在越南設立新辦公室了嗎？ B：他們仔細閱讀了【提案】，大部分都很喜歡，但要求我們補充更多關於成本和當地招聘的細節，下個月才會做最後決定。"},{"w":"hint","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of advice or a clue that helps you do or guess something","c":"提示；暗示；小訣竅","s":"A: I've tried three times to set up the new video meeting software on my laptop, but it still won't connect to the camera. B: Here's a hint: close all your other programs first, then restart the software, because the camera often stops working when another app is already using it.","t":"A：我已經試了三次在筆電上安裝新的視訊會議軟體，但它還是連不上攝影機。 B：給你一個【提示】：先關掉其他所有程式，再重新啟動軟體，因為當其他應用程式正在使用攝影機時，它常常會無法運作。"},{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"something you learn from a bad experience that helps you in the future","c":"教訓；課程","s":"A: Last year we lost a big order because we promised a delivery date that our factory could not meet, didn't we? B: Yes, and that was an important lesson for all of us, so now we always check with the factory before we promise any dates to customers.","t":"A：去年我們因為承諾了工廠無法達到的交貨日期而失去一筆大訂單，對吧？ B：對，那是給我們所有人的重要【教訓】，所以現在我們在向客戶承諾任何日期之前，一定會先和工廠確認。"},{"w":"reminder","p":"n.","d":"something that helps you remember something you must do","c":"提醒；提示通知","s":"A: How can we stop so many patients from missing their appointments at the dental clinic every week? B: We could send each patient a text message reminder the day before the visit, because most people forget appointments that they made several weeks earlier, especially when they are busy at work.","t":"A：我們要怎麼做，才能讓牙科診所每週不再有這麼多病人錯過預約？ B：我們可以在看診前一天傳簡訊【提醒】每位病人，因為大部分人會忘記幾週前預約的時間，尤其是工作忙碌的時候。"},{"w":"coaching","p":"n.","d":"the process of training and helping someone to improve a skill","c":"指導；訓練；輔導","s":"A: Our sales staff are friendly, but many of them find it hard to close deals with difficult customers, so what can we do? B: We could hire an expert to provide weekly coaching for the team, because practicing real situations with a professional usually builds confidence and improves results quickly.","t":"A：我們的業務人員很友善，但很多人都很難和難搞的顧客成交，我們能怎麼做？ B：我們可以聘請專家每週為團隊提供【指導訓練】，因為和專業人士一起演練真實情境，通常能很快建立信心並提升成果。"},{"w":"mentorship","p":"n.","d":"help and advice given over time by an experienced person to a less experienced one","c":"師徒指導；導師制度","s":"A: Why do so many young engineers want to work at your company, even though other firms offer slightly higher salaries? B: We have an excellent mentorship program, in which every new engineer is paired with a senior colleague who meets them each week and helps them plan their careers.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多年輕工程師想到你們公司工作，即使其他公司提供稍高的薪水？ B：我們有一個很棒的【導師指導】計畫，每位新進工程師都會和一位資深同事配對，對方每週和他們見面，並幫助他們規劃職涯。"},{"w":"directive","p":"n.","d":"an official order or instruction from someone in authority","c":"指令；命令；指示","s":"A: Why are all the managers working from the office again this week when they were allowed to work from home last month? B: The head office sent a new directive on Monday saying that all managers must be in the office at least four days a week to meet with their teams.","t":"A：為什麼這週所有經理又回辦公室上班了？上個月他們不是可以在家工作嗎？ B：總公司週一發布了一項新的【指令】，規定所有經理每週至少要有四天在辦公室與團隊開會。"},{"w":"guiding","p":"adj.","d":"giving direction or advice that helps someone decide what to do","c":"指導性的；引導的","s":"A: Our company is growing very fast, so how do you make sure that all the new branches treat customers in the same way? B: We have one guiding principle that every employee learns on the first day, which is that the customer's comfort and safety always come before quick profits.","t":"A：我們公司成長得很快，你們要怎麼確保所有新分店都用同樣的方式對待顧客？ B：我們有一個每位員工第一天就要學習的【指導】原則，就是顧客的舒適與安全永遠優先於快速獲利。"},{"w":"advisory","p":"adj.","d":"having the job of giving advice, usually without making the final decisions","c":"顧問的；諮詢的","s":"A: Will the university professors decide how the city spends the money for the new public transportation system? B: No, they only have an advisory role, so they will study the plans and share their ideas, but the city council will make the final decisions about the budget.","t":"A：大學教授們會決定市政府如何使用新大眾運輸系統的經費嗎？ B：不會，他們只擔任【顧問】角色，所以他們會研究計畫並提供想法，但預算的最後決定權在市議會。"},{"w":"wisdom","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make good decisions based on knowledge and experience","c":"智慧；明智","s":"A: Why does the young owner of the bakery still ask her grandfather for advice, even though he retired many years ago? B: He ran the shop successfully for forty years, and she values his wisdom about handling customers, choosing suppliers, and keeping costs low during difficult times.","t":"A：為什麼那間麵包店的年輕老闆仍然向祖父請教，即使他多年前就退休了？ B：他成功經營那家店四十年，她很重視他在應對顧客、挑選供應商，以及在困難時期控制成本方面的【智慧】。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Age 年齡","cards":[{"w":"reality","p":"n.","d":"the true situation, not what you hope or imagine","c":"現實；真實情況","s":"A: When I was a student, I thought that working at a big company would be exciting every day, so how does it feel after five years? B: The reality is quite different, because most days are full of emails and meetings, but I've learned to enjoy the small successes and the friendly people around me.","t":"A：我當學生時，以為在大公司工作每天都會很刺激，你工作五年後感覺如何？ B：【現實】很不一樣，因為大部分的日子都塞滿了電子郵件和會議，但我已經學會享受小小的成就和身邊友善的人們。"},{"w":"quite","p":"adv.","d":"fairly or very, but not extremely","c":"相當；頗","s":"A: Your father retired from the bank last spring, so how is he spending his time now that he doesn't go to the office every day? B: He is quite busy, actually, because he volunteers at the library twice a week, takes cooking classes, and helps my sister look after her two young children.","t":"A：你爸爸去年春天從銀行退休了，他現在不用每天進辦公室，都怎麼打發時間？ B：其實他【相當】忙，因為他每週去圖書館當兩次志工、上烹飪課，還幫我姊姊照顧她的兩個小孩。"},{"w":"enjoy","p":"v.","d":"to get pleasure from something","c":"享受；喜愛","s":"A: Many of our older customers have stopped coming to the gym in the evenings, so do you know why they changed their routine? B: They told me they enjoy the morning yoga classes much more, because the gym is quieter, the music is softer, and they can have coffee together afterward.","t":"A：我們很多年長的顧客晚上不再來健身房了，你知道他們為什麼改變作息嗎？ B：他們告訴我，他們更【喜歡】早上的瑜伽課，因為健身房比較安靜、音樂比較柔和，而且課後他們可以一起喝咖啡。"},{"w":"relive","p":"v.","d":"to remember something so clearly that you feel you are experiencing it again","c":"重溫；再經歷","s":"A: Why did so many retired employees come to the company's fiftieth anniversary party last Saturday night? B: The organizers showed old photos and videos from the 1980s, so everyone had a chance to relive their younger days and meet colleagues they had not seen for many years.","t":"A：為什麼上週六晚上有這麼多退休員工來參加公司五十週年派對？ B：主辦單位播放了1980年代的老照片和影片，所以大家都有機會【重溫】年輕時光，並見到許多年沒見的同事。"},{"w":"appear","p":"v.","d":"to seem; to give a particular impression","c":"顯得；看起來；似乎","s":"A: Did you know that Mr. Wilson, the new head of the design team, is already sixty-two years old? B: Really? He doesn't appear to be that old at all, maybe because he exercises every morning, rides his bike to work, and is always full of new ideas in meetings.","t":"A：你知道設計團隊的新主管威爾森先生已經六十二歲了嗎？ B：真的嗎？他完全【看起來】不像那個年紀，可能是因為他每天早上運動、騎腳踏車上班，而且開會時總是充滿新點子。"},{"w":"near","p":"adj.","d":"close in time or distance","c":"接近的；不久的","s":"A: Our team is getting older, and three senior engineers will retire within two years, so what is the company planning to do? B: In the near future, the company will hire several young engineers and ask the senior staff to train them before they leave.","t":"A：我們團隊的年紀越來越大，有三位資深工程師兩年內就要退休，公司打算怎麼做？ B：在【不久的】將來，公司會雇用幾位年輕工程師，並請資深員工在離職前訓練他們。"},{"w":"adulthood","p":"n.","d":"the time of life when you are an adult","c":"成年；成年期","s":"A: Why does the bank run free money-management workshops for university students every summer? B: Many young people enter adulthood without knowing how to save money, pay bills, or avoid debt, so the bank wants to teach them these skills before they start their first full-time jobs.","t":"A：為什麼銀行每年夏天都為大學生舉辦免費的理財工作坊？ B：許多年輕人步入【成年】時還不知道如何存錢、繳帳單或避免負債，所以銀行想在他們開始第一份全職工作前教他們這些技能。"},{"w":"experienced","p":"adj.","d":"having knowledge or skill from doing something for a long time","c":"有經驗的；經驗豐富的","s":"A: The client wants the new shopping center designed in only six months, so who should we put in charge of the project? B: We need an experienced architect who has handled large projects before, because a tight schedule like this leaves no time for beginners to learn from their mistakes.","t":"A：客戶希望新購物中心在短短六個月內設計完成，我們應該讓誰負責這個專案？ B：我們需要一位以前處理過大型專案、【經驗豐富的】建築師，因為這麼緊湊的時程，沒有時間讓新手從錯誤中學習。"},{"w":"recognize","p":"v.","d":"to know who someone is because you have seen them before","c":"認出；認得","s":"A: Did you meet anyone interesting at the high school reunion dinner at the hotel last weekend? B: It was a bit funny, because after twenty-five years many of my classmates had gray hair, and I couldn't recognize some of them until they told me their names.","t":"A：上週末在飯店舉辦的高中同學會晚餐，你有遇到什麼有趣的人嗎？ B：有點好笑，因為過了二十五年，很多同學都有白頭髮了，有些人直到他們告訴我名字，我才【認出】他們來。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and new ideas","c":"充滿活力的；有幹勁的","s":"A: Why do you think the new manager has become so popular with the staff in only three months? B: She is very dynamic, always full of energy and fresh ideas, and she encourages both younger and older employees to share their opinions in every meeting.","t":"A：你認為新經理為什麼在短短三個月內就這麼受員工歡迎？ B：她非常【有活力】，總是充滿幹勁和新點子，而且她在每次會議上都鼓勵年輕和年長的員工分享意見。"},{"w":"personality","p":"n.","d":"the kind of person someone is, shown by the way they behave and feel","c":"個性；性格","s":"A: Both candidates for the receptionist job have similar experience, so how will we choose the right person? B: I think we should choose the one with the warmer personality, because the receptionist is the first person every visitor meets, and a friendly attitude makes a strong first impression.","t":"A：兩位應徵接待員工作的人經驗差不多，我們要怎麼選出合適的人？ B：我認為我們應該選【個性】比較溫暖的那一位，因為接待員是每位訪客見到的第一個人，友善的態度能留下深刻的第一印象。"},{"w":"relaxed","p":"adj.","d":"calm and not worried","c":"放鬆的；輕鬆自在的","s":"A: You looked very tired and stressed last month, but you seem much happier now, so what changed? B: I started leaving work on time and walking in the park every evening, and now I feel much more relaxed, even when we have busy weeks with lots of deadlines.","t":"A：你上個月看起來很疲倦、壓力很大，但現在似乎開心多了，有什麼改變嗎？ B：我開始準時下班，每天傍晚去公園散步，現在即使遇到截止期限很多的忙碌週，我也覺得【放鬆】多了。"},{"w":"predict","p":"v.","d":"to say what will happen in the future","c":"預測；預言","s":"A: Why is the company building so many new apartments for older people in the suburbs this year? B: Experts predict that the number of residents over sixty-five will grow quickly in the next ten years, so the company expects strong demand for safe, comfortable homes near hospitals and parks.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年在郊區興建這麼多給年長者的新公寓？ B：專家【預測】未來十年六十五歲以上的居民人數會快速增加，所以公司預期靠近醫院和公園、安全又舒適的住宅會有強勁需求。"},{"w":"intriguing","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting because it is unusual or mysterious","c":"引人入勝的；耐人尋味的","s":"A: What did you think of the presentation about the island where many people live past one hundred years old? B: I found it very intriguing, especially the part about their simple diet and close family ties, and I'd like to read the full research report when it is published next month.","t":"A：你覺得那場關於許多人活過一百歲的島嶼的簡報怎麼樣？ B：我覺得非常【引人入勝】，尤其是關於他們簡單飲食和緊密家庭關係的部分，等下個月完整的研究報告出版時，我想讀一讀。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure that you can do something well","c":"有信心的；自信的","s":"A: How did your daughter feel about her first job interview at the travel agency yesterday afternoon? B: She felt quite confident, because she had practiced her answers with me several times, researched the company carefully, and prepared some good questions to ask the manager at the end.","t":"A：你女兒對她昨天下午在旅行社的第一次工作面試感覺如何？ B：她覺得很有【自信】，因為她跟我練習了好幾次回答、仔細研究了公司，還準備了幾個好問題在最後問經理。"},{"w":"vastly","p":"adv.","d":"very much; to a very great degree","c":"極大地；大大地","s":"A: Do you think the way young people shop today is similar to how your parents shopped thirty years ago? B: Not at all, it is vastly different, because most young people now compare prices on their phones and buy online, while my parents always went to local stores and paid in cash.","t":"A：你覺得現在年輕人購物的方式和你父母三十年前的方式相似嗎？ B：完全不同，是【大大地】不一樣，因為現在大部分年輕人都用手機比價並在網路上購買，而我父母總是去當地商店並用現金付款。"},{"w":"ponder","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something for a long time","c":"沉思；仔細考慮","s":"A: Is your uncle still planning to sell his restaurant and retire next year, or has he changed his mind? B: He is still trying to decide, so he will ponder the offer from the buyer over the holiday, because the restaurant has been his whole life for over thirty years.","t":"A：你叔叔還打算明年把餐廳賣掉然後退休嗎？還是他改變心意了？ B：他還在考慮，所以他會在假期期間【仔細思考】買家的出價，因為三十多年來，那間餐廳就是他的全部生活。"},{"w":"mature","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in a sensible way, like an adult","c":"成熟的；穩重的","s":"A: The new intern is only twenty years old, so are you sure we should let her speak with our most important client? B: Yes, she is very mature for her age, because she listens carefully, stays calm under pressure, and always asks for help when she isn't sure about something.","t":"A：新來的實習生才二十歲，你確定我們應該讓她和我們最重要的客戶談話嗎？ B：確定，以她的年紀來說她非常【成熟】，因為她會仔細聆聽、在壓力下保持冷靜，而且不確定的時候總會尋求協助。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"able to live or work without help from others","c":"獨立的；自主的","s":"A: Why did your grandmother decide to stay in her own apartment instead of moving in with your family? B: She wants to stay independent as long as possible, so she cooks for herself, takes the bus to the market, and only asks us for help with heavy cleaning once a month.","t":"A：你奶奶為什麼決定住在自己的公寓，而不搬去和你們家同住？ B：她想盡可能保持【獨立】，所以她自己煮飯、搭公車去市場，只有每個月一次的大掃除才會請我們幫忙。"},{"w":"insecure","p":"adj.","d":"not confident about yourself or your abilities","c":"沒有安全感的；缺乏自信的","s":"A: Why does Tom always stay quiet in meetings, even when he clearly knows the answer to the manager's questions? B: He feels insecure because he is the youngest person on the team, so he worries that the older engineers will laugh at his ideas or think they are too simple.","t":"A：為什麼湯姆開會時總是保持沉默，即使他顯然知道經理問題的答案？ B：他覺得【沒有自信】，因為他是團隊裡最年輕的人，所以擔心年長的工程師會嘲笑他的想法，或覺得太簡單。"},{"w":"embrace","p":"v.","d":"to accept new ideas, changes, or opportunities with enthusiasm","c":"欣然接受；擁抱","s":"A: Were the older staff members unhappy when the company replaced all the paper forms with a new computer system? B: Surprisingly, most of them were happy to embrace the change, because the training was clear and patient, and the new system saves them about an hour of work every day.","t":"A：公司用新的電腦系統取代所有紙本表格時，年長的員工不高興嗎？ B：令人驚訝的是，他們大多數人都樂於【接受】這項改變，因為訓練清楚又有耐心，而且新系統每天幫他們省下大約一個小時的工作。"},{"w":"ageless","p":"adj.","d":"never seeming to grow old; not affected by time","c":"永不顯老的；永恆的","s":"A: Why did the fashion company choose a famous sixty-year-old actress for its new advertising campaign this autumn? B: The company wanted to show that style is ageless, and its research found that many older women feel ignored by advertisements that only use very young models.","t":"A：為什麼這家時尚公司今年秋天的新廣告活動選了一位六十歲的知名女演員？ B：公司想表達時尚是【不受年齡限制的】，而且它的研究發現，許多年長女性覺得只用年輕模特兒的廣告忽略了她們。"},{"w":"mindset","p":"n.","d":"a way of thinking or set of attitudes","c":"心態；思維模式","s":"A: How has your sixty-five-year-old father managed to learn computer programming so quickly after he retired? B: He has a great mindset, because he believes people can learn new skills at any age, so he practices every day and isn't afraid of making mistakes.","t":"A：你六十五歲的父親退休後，是怎麼這麼快學會電腦程式設計的？ B：他有很棒的【心態】，因為他相信人在任何年紀都能學習新技能，所以他每天練習，而且不怕犯錯。"},{"w":"re-energize","p":"v.","d":"to give someone new energy and enthusiasm","c":"使恢復活力；重新振作","s":"A: Our sales team seems tired and bored after such a long and difficult year, so what can we do to help them? B: A short trip to the beach for team activities might re-energize everyone, and the managers could also announce some exciting new goals and rewards for next year.","t":"A：經過這麼漫長又艱難的一年，我們的業務團隊似乎又累又無精打采，我們能做些什麼來幫助他們？ B：去海邊進行短程的團隊活動或許能讓大家【重新振作】，主管們也可以宣布一些令人振奮的明年新目標和獎勵。"},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"full of life, energy, and color","c":"充滿活力的；鮮明的","s":"A: Why did the company choose this neighborhood for its new office, when the rent is higher than in other parts of the city? B: The area is very vibrant, with busy cafés, art galleries, and street markets, and the managers believe young employees will enjoy working in such a lively place.","t":"A：為什麼公司把新辦公室選在這個社區？這裡的租金比城裡其他地方都高。 B：這個地區非常【有活力】，有熱鬧的咖啡館、藝廊和街頭市集，主管們相信年輕員工會喜歡在這麼熱鬧的地方工作。"},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen and impossible to avoid","c":"不可避免的；必然的","s":"A: Do you think our company will need to raise the price of our products next year because of higher costs? B: I'm afraid it's inevitable, because the price of raw materials and shipping has gone up by twenty percent, and we cannot keep paying for the difference ourselves.","t":"A：你認為我們公司明年會因為成本上升而需要調漲產品價格嗎？ B：恐怕這是【不可避免的】，因為原物料和運費已經上漲了百分之二十，我們沒辦法一直自己吸收差額。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"something that is more important than other things and must be done first","c":"優先事項；優先考慮","s":"A: Now that your children are in elementary school, have you thought about going back to full-time work at the hospital? B: Yes, but my main priority is still my family, so I'm looking for a part-time job that lets me finish work before the children come home in the afternoon.","t":"A：既然你的孩子都上小學了，你有考慮回醫院做全職工作嗎？ B：有，但我的首要【優先事項】仍然是家庭，所以我在找一份兼職工作，讓我能在孩子下午回家前下班。"},{"w":"behave","p":"v.","d":"to act or do things in a particular way","c":"表現；舉止","s":"A: Why are we giving the new store staff a full day of customer service training before the shop opens next week? B: We want them to know how to behave politely with all customers, including elderly people who may need extra time and patience when they pay or ask questions.","t":"A：為什麼要在下週新店開幕前，給新店員一整天的顧客服務訓練？ B：我們希望他們知道如何對所有顧客禮貌地【應對】，包括在付款或詢問時可能需要更多時間和耐心的長者。"},{"w":"physically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way related to the body","c":"身體上；體力上","s":"A: Your father is eighty years old, but he still works in his garden every morning, so how does he stay so healthy? B: He stays physically active by walking for an hour every day, lifting light weights, and doing simple stretching exercises, and he also eats lots of fresh vegetables from his garden.","t":"A：你父親八十歲了，但每天早上還在花園裡工作，他是怎麼保持這麼健康的？ B：他每天走路一小時、舉輕量啞鈴、做簡單的伸展運動來保持【身體】活躍，還吃很多自家花園種的新鮮蔬菜。"},{"w":"mentally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way related to the mind","c":"心理上；精神上；智力上","s":"A: How does your grandmother keep her memory so sharp, even though she is now over ninety years old? B: She stays mentally active by doing crossword puzzles every morning, reading the newspaper, and playing card games with her friends at the community center three afternoons a week.","t":"A：你奶奶已經九十多歲了，她是怎麼讓記憶力保持這麼好的？ B：她每天早上玩填字遊戲、看報紙，每週有三個下午在社區中心和朋友玩紙牌，藉此保持【頭腦】活躍。"},{"w":"obsessed","p":"adj.","d":"thinking about something or someone all the time in a way that is not normal","c":"著迷的；執著的","s":"A: Why does our sales manager check the sales numbers on his phone every ten minutes, even during lunch? B: He is obsessed with reaching the yearly target before December, but I think he should relax a little, because the team is already doing better than last year.","t":"A：為什麼我們的業務經理連吃午餐時都每十分鐘就用手機查一次業績數字？ B：他對在十二月前達成年度目標很【執著】，但我覺得他應該稍微放鬆一點，因為團隊的表現已經比去年好了。"},{"w":"relevant","p":"adj.","d":"connected with what is being discussed or done","c":"相關的；切題的","s":"A: Should I include my summer job at the ice cream shop on my résumé when I apply for the marketing position? B: Only if it is relevant to the job, so you could mention that you designed the shop's social media posts, because that shows you already have some marketing experience.","t":"A：我應徵行銷職位時，應該在履歷上寫我暑假在冰淇淋店打工的經歷嗎？ B：只有在和這份工作【相關】時才寫，所以你可以提到你設計過店裡的社群媒體貼文，因為那顯示你已經有一些行銷經驗。"},{"w":"inclination","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that makes you want to do something","c":"傾向；意願；愛好","s":"A: Your father has worked as a lawyer for forty years, so does he plan to keep working, or will he retire soon? B: He has no inclination to stop working yet, because he still loves helping his clients, and he says that a busy schedule keeps him young and healthy.","t":"A：你父親當了四十年律師，他打算繼續工作，還是很快就會退休？ B：他目前還沒有停止工作的【意願】，因為他仍然很喜歡幫助客戶，而且他說忙碌的行程讓他保持年輕和健康。"},{"w":"interact","p":"v.","d":"to communicate with and spend time with other people","c":"互動；交流","s":"A: Why did the nursing home start inviting students from the nearby high school to visit every Friday afternoon? B: The staff want the elderly residents to interact with young people more often, because talking, playing games, and sharing stories helps everyone feel happier and less lonely.","t":"A：為什麼安養院開始邀請附近高中的學生每週五下午來拜訪？ B：工作人員希望長者住民能更常和年輕人【互動】，因為聊天、玩遊戲和分享故事能讓每個人更快樂、更不孤單。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Airport 機場","cards":[{"w":"terminal","p":"n.","d":"a large building at an airport where passengers arrive and leave","c":"航廈；航站","s":"A: I'm picking up our clients from Seoul at the airport tomorrow afternoon, but I'm not sure where I should wait for them. B: Their airline uses terminal 2, so wait near the arrivals hall on the first floor, and send them a message so they know where to find you after they collect their bags.","t":"A：我明天下午要去機場接首爾來的客戶，但不確定該在哪裡等他們。 B：他們的航空公司使用第二【航廈】，所以在一樓入境大廳附近等，並傳訊息給他們，讓他們領完行李後知道去哪裡找你。"},{"w":"runway","p":"n.","d":"a long, flat road where airplanes take off and land","c":"跑道","s":"A: Why has our plane been waiting on the ground for forty minutes when it was supposed to leave at nine o'clock? B: The captain just announced that workers are clearing snow from the runway, and he thinks we will be able to take off in about fifteen minutes once they have finished.","t":"A：為什麼我們的飛機已經在地面等了四十分鐘？它原本應該九點起飛的。 B：機長剛剛廣播說，工作人員正在清除【跑道】上的積雪，他認為等他們清完，我們大約十五分鐘後就能起飛。"},{"w":"gate","p":"n.","d":"the place in an airport where passengers get on a plane","c":"登機門","s":"A: Excuse me, my flight to Bangkok leaves in thirty minutes, but the screen doesn't show where I should go to get on the plane. B: Your flight has just been moved to gate 15 because of a technical problem, so please walk quickly to the end of this hall and turn left.","t":"A：不好意思，我飛往曼谷的班機三十分鐘後起飛，但螢幕沒有顯示我該去哪裡登機。 B：因為技術問題，您的班機剛剛改到15號【登機門】，所以請快步走到這個大廳的盡頭再左轉。"},{"w":"check-in","p":"n.","d":"the place or process where you show your ticket and give your bags before a flight","c":"報到；登機手續；報到櫃台","s":"A: Our flight to Tokyo leaves at seven in the morning, so what time do you think we should leave the hotel? B: Let's leave at four thirty, because the check-in counter closes one hour before departure, and there are often long lines of tour groups at the airport early in the morning.","t":"A：我們飛往東京的班機早上七點起飛，你覺得我們應該幾點離開飯店？ B：我們四點半出發吧，因為【報到】櫃台在起飛前一小時就關閉了，而且清晨的機場常常有旅行團排長長的隊伍。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"the area at an airport where bags and passengers are checked for dangerous items","c":"安檢；安全檢查處；安全","s":"A: Why did it take you so long to get to the gate, when you arrived at the airport two hours before the flight? B: The line at security was huge, and then the officers opened my bag because I forgot to take my laptop out and put it in a separate tray.","t":"A：你在班機起飛前兩小時就到機場了，為什麼花了這麼久才到登機門？ B：【安檢】的隊伍超長，然後安檢人員打開了我的包包，因為我忘了把筆電拿出來放在另一個托盤裡。"},{"w":"customs","p":"n.","d":"the place at an airport where officers check what you bring into a country","c":"海關","s":"A: I bought some expensive watches during my business trip to Switzerland, so do I need to do anything special when I land? B: Yes, you need to go to the red line at customs and tell the officers what you bought, because you may have to pay tax on goods over a certain value.","t":"A：我在瑞士出差時買了幾支昂貴的手錶，降落時需要做什麼特別的事嗎？ B：需要，你必須到【海關】的紅線通道向關員申報你買的東西，因為超過一定金額的物品可能要繳稅。"},{"w":"immigration","p":"n.","d":"the place at an airport where officers check passports and visas","c":"入境檢查；移民局","s":"A: How long will it take us to leave the airport after we land in New York on Monday evening? B: It could take an hour or more, because the lines at immigration are usually very long in the evening, and the officers ask every visitor several questions before stamping their passports.","t":"A：我們週一晚上在紐約降落後，要花多久時間才能離開機場？ B：可能要一個小時以上，因為晚上【入境審查】的隊伍通常很長，而且官員在護照蓋章前會問每位訪客好幾個問題。"},{"w":"baggage","p":"n.","d":"the bags and suitcases you take with you when you travel","c":"行李","s":"A: I'm flying to Singapore for a two-week training course, and I need to bring a lot of documents and clothes. B: Check the airline's website before you pack, because your ticket only includes twenty kilograms of baggage, and the fee for extra weight at the airport is very expensive.","t":"A：我要飛去新加坡參加兩週的培訓課程，需要帶很多文件和衣服。 B：打包前先查一下航空公司的網站，因為你的機票只含二十公斤的【行李】，在機場付超重費非常貴。"},{"w":"luggage","p":"n.","d":"suitcases and bags used for carrying things when traveling","c":"行李","s":"A: Do you know where I can leave my bags for a few hours, because my hotel room won't be ready until three o'clock this afternoon? B: There is a luggage storage office on the ground floor of the train station, and it only costs about five dollars for each bag per day.","t":"A：你知道我可以把包包寄放在哪裡幾個小時嗎？因為我的飯店房間要到下午三點才準備好。 B：火車站一樓有一個【行李】寄放處，每件每天大約只要五美元。"},{"w":"carousel","p":"n.","d":"a moving belt at an airport from which passengers collect their bags","c":"行李轉盤","s":"A: We've been waiting for our suitcases for nearly thirty minutes, so are you sure we're standing in the right place? B: The screen says that bags from our flight will come out on carousel 4, but there was a problem with the machine, so the airport staff are fixing it now.","t":"A：我們已經等行李將近三十分鐘了，你確定我們站對地方了嗎？ B：螢幕顯示我們班機的行李會從4號【行李轉盤】出來，但機器出了問題，所以機場人員正在修理。"},{"w":"boarding","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting on a plane, ship, or train","c":"登機；上船；上車","s":"A: I still need to buy a gift for my client at the duty-free shop, so do I have enough time before our flight? B: You'll have to hurry, because boarding starts in fifteen minutes, and passengers with small children and business class tickets will get on the plane first.","t":"A：我還需要在免稅店買份禮物給客戶，我們班機起飛前我時間夠嗎？ B：你得快一點，因為十五分鐘後就開始【登機】了，帶小孩的乘客和商務艙旅客會先上飛機。"},{"w":"departure","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a place, especially at the start of a journey","c":"出發；離開；起飛","s":"A: Our flight to Hong Kong was supposed to leave at eleven, but it's already eleven thirty, so what's happening? B: The airline just sent a text saying that the departure has been moved to twelve fifteen because the plane arrived late from Manila after bad weather this morning.","t":"A：我們飛往香港的班機原定十一點起飛，但現在已經十一點半了，怎麼回事？ B：航空公司剛剛傳簡訊說，因為飛機今天早上遇到壞天氣從馬尼拉晚到，【起飛】時間改到十二點十五分。"},{"w":"arrival","p":"n.","d":"the act of reaching a place","c":"抵達；到達","s":"A: When should the hotel driver go to the airport to pick up our guest speaker from London? B: Her arrival is planned for six forty in the evening, but the driver should check the flight information online before he leaves, because flights from Europe are sometimes early or late.","t":"A：飯店司機應該什麼時候去機場接從倫敦來的演講嘉賓？ B：她預計晚上六點四十分【抵達】，但司機出發前應該先上網查航班資訊，因為來自歐洲的班機有時會提早或延誤。"},{"w":"delay","p":"n.","d":"a time when someone or something has to wait or is late","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: Why didn't Mr. Lopez join the morning meeting at our office in Taipei as he had planned? B: His flight had a four-hour delay because of a typhoon near Hong Kong, so he landed after lunch and joined the afternoon session by video call from the airport.","t":"A：為什麼羅培茲先生沒有如原本計畫參加我們台北辦公室的早上會議？ B：他的班機因為香港附近的颱風【延誤】了四個小時，所以他午餐後才降落，並在機場用視訊參加了下午的會議。"},{"w":"cancellation","p":"n.","d":"a decision that something planned will not happen","c":"取消","s":"A: The airline just told us that our flight to Osaka won't leave tonight because of the snowstorm, so what should we do? B: Go to the service desk right away, because after a cancellation like this, the airline must offer you a seat on the next flight and a free hotel room.","t":"A：航空公司剛告訴我們，因為暴風雪，我們飛往大阪的班機今晚不會起飛，我們該怎麼辦？ B：馬上去服務櫃台，因為發生像這樣的【取消】後，航空公司必須提供你下一班飛機的座位和免費的飯店房間。"},{"w":"passport","p":"n.","d":"an official document that shows who you are and allows you to travel to other countries","c":"護照","s":"A: The company wants me to attend a trade fair in Germany next month, but I haven't traveled abroad for over ten years. B: Then check your passport today, because it may have expired, and getting a new one can take two or three weeks during the busy summer season.","t":"A：公司要我下個月去德國參加商展，但我已經十多年沒出國了。 B：那你今天就檢查一下你的【護照】，因為它可能已經過期了，而在忙碌的夏季，申請新的可能要兩、三個星期。"},{"w":"visa","p":"n.","d":"an official document or stamp that allows you to enter or stay in a country","c":"簽證","s":"A: Our new engineer from India is starting work at the Taipei office in March, so has everything been prepared for him? B: Almost everything, but he is still waiting for his work visa, and the human resources department says it should be ready about two weeks before he flies here.","t":"A：我們從印度來的新工程師三月要在台北辦公室上班，所有事情都替他準備好了嗎？ B：幾乎都好了，但他還在等工作【簽證】，人資部說大約在他飛來前兩週就會辦好。"},{"w":"ticket","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper or electronic document that shows you have paid to travel","c":"票；機票","s":"A: I need to fly to Kaohsiung for a client meeting next Thursday, so should I book the flight myself or ask someone else to do it? B: Please ask the travel coordinator to buy your ticket, because the company gets a special discount, and she also keeps all the receipts for the accounting department.","t":"A：我下週四要飛去高雄和客戶開會，我應該自己訂機票，還是請別人幫忙？ B：請差旅專員幫你買【機票】，因為公司有特別折扣，而且她也會為會計部保留所有收據。"},{"w":"boarding pass","p":"n.phr.","d":"a card or electronic document that allows you to get on a plane","c":"登機證","s":"A: The airline staff at the gate won't let me get on the plane, but I already showed them my passport. B: You also need to show your boarding pass, so open the airline app on your phone, find your trip, and show them the code with your seat number on it.","t":"A：登機門的航空公司人員不讓我上飛機，但我已經給他們看過護照了。 B：你還需要出示你的【登機證】，所以打開手機上的航空公司應用程式，找到你的行程，給他們看有座位號碼的條碼。"},{"w":"aisle","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow space between rows of seats on a plane","c":"走道","s":"A: Would you like me to book a window seat for your long flight to Los Angeles next week? B: No, please get me a seat on the aisle, because I usually drink lots of water on long trips and need to stand up and walk around without asking the other passengers to move.","t":"A：下週你飛洛杉磯的長途航班，要我幫你訂靠窗的座位嗎？ B：不用，請幫我訂靠【走道】的座位，因為我長途旅行時通常會喝很多水，需要站起來走動，不想一直請其他乘客讓開。"},{"w":"overhead","p":"adj.","d":"above your head","c":"頭頂上的；上方的","s":"A: Where should I put my laptop bag and coat after I find my seat on the plane? B: You can put the coat in the overhead bin, but keep the laptop bag under the seat in front of you, because the flight attendants want the space above the seats for larger suitcases.","t":"A：我在飛機上找到座位後，筆電包和外套應該放在哪裡？ B：外套可以放在【頭頂上方的】置物櫃，但筆電包要放在前方座位底下，因為空服員希望座位上方的空間留給較大的行李箱。"},{"w":"carry-on","p":"n.","d":"a small bag that you are allowed to take onto a plane with you","c":"隨身行李","s":"A: Can I bring my large camera bag onto the plane, or do I need to check it at the counter with my suitcase? B: Each passenger can take one carry-on that weighs less than seven kilograms, so you can bring the camera bag if it is light enough to fit those airline rules.","t":"A：我可以把大相機包帶上飛機嗎？還是需要和行李箱一起在櫃台託運？ B：每位乘客可以攜帶一件七公斤以下的【隨身行李】，所以如果相機包夠輕、符合航空公司的規定，你就可以帶上去。"},{"w":"jet lag","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tired feeling after a long flight across different time zones","c":"時差；時差反應","s":"A: You flew back from New York only yesterday, so how are you feeling this morning, and are you ready for the meeting? B: I'm suffering from jet lag, because I woke up at three in the morning and couldn't sleep again, so I'll need lots of coffee to stay awake during the meeting.","t":"A：你昨天才從紐約飛回來，今天早上感覺怎麼樣？準備好開會了嗎？ B：我有【時差】，因為我凌晨三點就醒了，再也睡不著，所以開會時我需要很多咖啡才能保持清醒。"},{"w":"announcement","p":"n.","d":"a public statement giving people information","c":"宣布；廣播；公告","s":"A: Did you hear what the voice just said through the speakers in the waiting area? It was too noisy for me. B: It was an announcement that our flight to Hanoi is ready for boarding, and passengers sitting in rows thirty to forty-five should go to the gate first.","t":"A：你有聽到剛才候機區喇叭說了什麼嗎？太吵了我沒聽清楚。 B：那是一則【廣播】，說我們飛往河內的班機準備登機了，坐在第三十到四十五排的乘客要先到登機門。"},{"w":"queue","p":"n.","d":"a line of people waiting for something","c":"隊伍；行列","s":"A: Why are so many passengers standing near the information desk, and why does everyone look so angry? B: There is a long queue of travelers waiting to change their tickets, because three flights were canceled this morning due to fog, and only two staff members are working at the desk.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多乘客站在服務台附近，而且大家看起來都那麼生氣？ B：有一長串旅客在【排隊】等著換票，因為今天早上有三個航班因大霧取消，而服務台只有兩名工作人員。"},{"w":"transfer","p":"n.","d":"moving from one plane or vehicle to another during a trip","c":"轉機；轉乘；接駁","s":"A: I have to fly from Taipei to Toronto for the conference next month, but there is no direct flight. B: You can take the flight with a transfer in Vancouver, because you only wait two hours there, and your suitcase will go directly to Toronto without you collecting it.","t":"A：下個月我要從台北飛多倫多參加研討會，但沒有直飛班機。 B：你可以搭在溫哥華【轉機】的班機，因為在那裡只要等兩個小時，而且你的行李箱會直接送到多倫多，不用自己領取。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"a plane, train, or bus that you take after getting off another one","c":"轉乘班機；銜接的交通工具","s":"A: Our first flight from Taipei is already thirty minutes late, so will we still be able to catch the flight to Paris in Dubai? B: I'm worried that we might miss our connection, because there is only one hour between the two flights, and the airport in Dubai is very large.","t":"A：我們從台北起飛的第一班飛機已經誤點三十分鐘了，我們還趕得上在杜拜飛往巴黎的班機嗎？ B：我擔心我們會錯過【轉機班機】，因為兩個航班之間只有一個小時，而杜拜機場又非常大。"},{"w":"screening","p":"n.","d":"the process of checking people or bags for dangerous items","c":"篩檢；檢查；安全檢查","s":"A: Why did the airport ask all international passengers to arrive three hours early this week? B: The government added extra screening of passengers and bags after some new safety rules started on Monday, so every person now goes through two machines before reaching the gates.","t":"A：為什麼機場這週要求所有國際線旅客提早三個小時到？ B：週一開始實施一些新的安全規定後，政府對旅客和行李增加了額外的【檢查】，所以現在每個人到登機門前都要通過兩台機器。"},{"w":"taxi","p":"v.","d":"(of a plane) to move slowly along the ground before taking off or after landing","c":"（飛機）滑行","s":"A: We landed ten minutes ago, so why are we still sitting on the plane and not at the gate yet? B: The airport is very busy this morning, so the plane has to taxi slowly across the airfield and wait for another aircraft to leave our gate before we can get off.","t":"A：我們十分鐘前就降落了，為什麼還坐在飛機上、還沒到登機門？ B：今天早上機場很忙，所以飛機必須在機坪上緩慢【滑行】，並等另一架飛機離開我們的登機門後，我們才能下機。"},{"w":"depart","p":"v.","d":"to leave a place, especially to start a journey","c":"出發；離開；起飛","s":"A: Is the last flight to Hualien tonight still on schedule, or has it been affected by the strong winds along the coast? B: It is scheduled to depart at eight forty-five, but the airline says it will send passengers a message within the next hour if the weather becomes too dangerous.","t":"A：今晚飛往花蓮的最後一班飛機還照常嗎？還是受到沿海強風的影響？ B：預定八點四十五分【起飛】，但航空公司說如果天氣變得太危險，會在接下來一小時內傳訊息通知乘客。"},{"w":"arrive","p":"v.","d":"to reach a place at the end of a journey","c":"到達；抵達","s":"A: How early should international passengers get to Taoyuan Airport before their flights during the holiday season? B: The airport suggests that they arrive at least three hours before their flight, because the check-in lines and security checks are much slower when so many families are traveling.","t":"A：在假期期間，國際線旅客應該在班機起飛前多早到桃園機場？ B：機場建議他們至少在起飛前三小時【抵達】，因為有這麼多家庭出遊時，報到的隊伍和安檢都會慢很多。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is firmly fixed or safely protected","c":"牢固地；安全地","s":"A: The plane is shaking a lot, and the seatbelt sign just came on, so is there anything I should do right now? B: Make sure your seatbelt is fastened securely around your waist, and put your hot coffee on the floor so that it doesn't spill on you or the passenger next to you.","t":"A：飛機晃得很厲害，安全帶指示燈剛剛亮了，我現在有什麼該做的嗎？ B：確定你的安全帶有【牢牢地】繫在腰上，並把熱咖啡放到地上，以免灑到你或你旁邊的乘客。"},{"w":"onboard","p":"adj.","d":"available or happening on a plane, ship, or train","c":"機上的；船上的；車上的","s":"A: It's a twelve-hour flight to Amsterdam, so how will you keep busy during the trip if you don't want to work? B: The airline has a great onboard entertainment system with hundreds of films and music albums, so I plan to watch a few movies and then sleep for several hours.","t":"A：飛阿姆斯特丹要十二個小時，如果你不想工作，旅途中要怎麼打發時間？ B：這家航空公司有很棒的【機上】娛樂系統，有數百部電影和音樂專輯，所以我打算看幾部電影，然後睡幾個小時。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Alone 獨處","cards":[{"w":"socialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend time with other people in a friendly way","c":"交際；社交；與人往來","s":"A: Why does the company organize a dinner party for all the staff every three months, even though it costs quite a lot of money? B: The managers want employees from different departments to socialize outside the office, because people who know each other well usually communicate better and solve problems faster at work.","t":"A：為什麼公司每三個月都為全體員工舉辦晚餐派對，即使花費相當多？ B：主管們希望不同部門的員工能在辦公室以外【交流往來】，因為彼此熟悉的人在工作上通常溝通得更好，解決問題也更快。"},{"w":"social life","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time you spend with friends and doing activities for fun","c":"社交生活","s":"A: You've been working until ten o'clock every night since you got promoted, so do you still have time to see your friends? B: Not really, my social life has almost disappeared, so I've decided to leave the office by seven at least three days a week and join my friends for dinner.","t":"A：你升職後每天都工作到晚上十點，還有時間見朋友嗎？ B：其實沒有，我的【社交生活】幾乎消失了，所以我決定每週至少三天七點前下班，和朋友一起吃晚餐。"},{"w":"solitude","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone, especially when you enjoy it","c":"獨處；孤獨（多指享受的）","s":"A: Why does the writer rent a small cabin in the mountains every winter instead of working from her apartment in the city? B: She needs complete solitude to finish her novels, because there are no phone calls, visitors, or traffic noise there, so she can focus on writing for ten hours a day.","t":"A：為什麼那位作家每年冬天都在山上租一間小木屋，而不在城裡的公寓工作？ B：她需要完全的【獨處】才能完成小說，因為那裡沒有電話、訪客或車聲，她可以一天專心寫作十個小時。"},{"w":"solitary","p":"adj.","d":"done alone or existing alone","c":"單獨的；獨自的；孤獨的","s":"A: You used to love working with large teams, so why did you accept a job as a night guard at the museum? B: I actually enjoy solitary work at this stage of my life, because I can read during quiet hours, and I don't have to attend long meetings or deal with office politics.","t":"A：你以前很喜歡和大團隊一起工作，為什麼接受了博物館夜間警衛的工作？ B：在人生的這個階段，我其實很享受【獨自一人的】工作，因為安靜的時候我可以看書，而且不用參加冗長的會議或應付辦公室政治。"},{"w":"self-reliant","p":"adj.","d":"able to do things and make decisions without help from others","c":"自立的；依靠自己的","s":"A: Your son moved to Australia for university last year, so how is he managing without his family nearby? B: He has become very self-reliant, because he cooks his own meals, works part-time at a café to pay his rent, and solves most of his problems without calling us for help.","t":"A：你兒子去年去澳洲念大學，家人不在身邊，他過得怎麼樣？ B：他變得非常【自立】，因為他自己煮飯、在咖啡館兼職付房租，大部分的問題都自己解決，不會打電話向我們求助。"},{"w":"recharge","p":"v.","d":"to rest so that you get your energy back","c":"恢復精力；充電","s":"A: Why do you always spend your lunch break walking alone in the park instead of eating with the team? B: I talk to customers on the phone all morning, so I need some quiet time to recharge, and a short walk helps me feel fresh and focused for the busy afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼你午休總是獨自在公園散步，而不和團隊一起吃飯？ B：我整個早上都在和顧客講電話，所以需要一些安靜的時間來【恢復精力】，短暫的散步能讓我在忙碌的下午感到清新又專注。"},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully and seriously about something","c":"反思；深思","s":"A: Why did the manager give everyone a notebook at the end of the long project and ask us to write in it? B: She wants each of us to reflect on what went well and what went wrong, so that we can avoid the same problems when we start the next project in January.","t":"A：為什麼經理在漫長的專案結束時發給每個人一本筆記本，要我們在上面寫東西？ B：她希望我們每個人【反思】哪些地方做得好、哪些地方出了錯，好讓我們一月開始下一個專案時，能避免同樣的問題。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and become calm, especially after work","c":"放鬆；休息","s":"A: You look really tired after such a busy week at the trade fair, so what are your plans for the weekend? B: I'm going to stay home, turn off my phone, and just relax with a good book and some music, because I need to rest before the next sales trip on Monday.","t":"A：在商展忙了這麼一整週，你看起來好累，週末有什麼計畫？ B：我要待在家、關掉手機，就看本好書、聽點音樂【放鬆】一下，因為在週一下一趟業務出差前，我需要休息。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of happiness because something unpleasant has ended or not happened","c":"寬慰；鬆了一口氣","s":"A: How did you feel when the client finally called and said they had approved our design, after making us change it five times? B: It was a huge relief, because the whole team had worked every weekend for a month, and we were worried that we might lose the contract.","t":"A：在客戶要我們修改五次設計後，終於打電話來說核准了，你有什麼感覺？ B：真是大大【鬆了一口氣】，因為整個團隊一個月來每個週末都在工作，我們很擔心可能會失去這份合約。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and calm, without noise or trouble","c":"寧靜的；平和的","s":"A: Why did you choose that small hotel by the lake instead of the big one near the conference center? B: The big hotel is always full of noisy tour groups, but the lake hotel is so peaceful that I can sleep well and prepare for my presentations without any distractions.","t":"A：為什麼你選擇湖邊那間小飯店，而不選會議中心附近的大飯店？ B：大飯店總是擠滿吵鬧的旅行團，但湖邊的飯店非常【寧靜】，我可以睡得很好，並在沒有任何干擾的情況下準備簡報。"},{"w":"release","p":"v.","d":"to let a feeling or energy go so that you feel better","c":"釋放；發洩","s":"A: Why does the company now offer free boxing classes in the gym after work on Tuesdays and Thursdays? B: Many employees said they feel tense after long days at their desks, and hitting a punching bag helps them release stress in a healthy way before they go home.","t":"A：為什麼公司現在每週二和週四下班後在健身房提供免費拳擊課？ B：許多員工說，在辦公桌前坐了一整天後感覺很緊繃，打沙包能幫助他們在回家前用健康的方式【釋放】壓力。"},{"w":"pressure","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult demands or too much work","c":"壓力","s":"A: Why has Kevin been so quiet and tired lately, when he used to be the most cheerful person in the office? B: He is under a lot of pressure because he has to finish three big reports before the end of the month, and his manager keeps adding new tasks to his list.","t":"A：凱文以前是辦公室裡最開朗的人，為什麼最近這麼安靜又疲倦？ B：他承受很大的【壓力】，因為他必須在月底前完成三份大型報告，而他的主管還不斷在他的清單上增加新任務。"},{"w":"belong to somebody","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel that you are an important part of someone's life or a group","c":"歸屬於某人；有歸屬感","s":"A: Why did your elderly neighbor start volunteering at the animal shelter after her husband passed away last year? B: She said that caring for the dogs makes her feel that she still has a purpose and can belong to somebody, because the animals are always so happy to see her each morning.","t":"A：為什麼你年長的鄰居在她先生去年過世後，開始到動物收容所當志工？ B：她說照顧狗狗讓她覺得自己仍有生活目標，並且能【有所歸屬】，因為每天早上動物們見到她總是非常開心。"},{"w":"introvert","p":"n.","d":"a quiet person who prefers to spend time alone or with a few people","c":"內向的人","s":"A: Lisa is one of our best programmers, but she never joins the team lunches or the after-work parties, so is something wrong? B: Nothing is wrong, she's just an introvert, so she prefers to eat quietly at her desk and recharge her energy before the afternoon meetings.","t":"A：麗莎是我們最優秀的程式設計師之一，但她從不參加團隊午餐或下班後的聚會，是出了什麼問題嗎？ B：沒什麼問題，她只是個【內向的人】，所以比較喜歡安靜地在座位上吃飯，在下午的會議前恢復精力。"},{"w":"attractive","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant or interesting, so that people want it","c":"有吸引力的；誘人的","s":"A: Why are so many young professionals choosing to live alone in small studio apartments in the city center? B: Living alone is very attractive to them, because they can decide their own schedules, keep the space exactly how they like it, and walk to work in just ten minutes.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多年輕上班族選擇獨自住在市中心的小套房？ B：獨居對他們來說非常【有吸引力】，因為他們可以自己決定作息、把空間維持成自己喜歡的樣子，而且走路十分鐘就能到公司。"},{"w":"regulate","p":"v.","d":"to control something so that it stays at the right level","c":"調節；控制；管理","s":"A: The new office building has a smart system that turns the heating on and off by itself, so how does it work? B: Sensors in every room regulate the temperature throughout the day, so the building stays comfortable for workers while using about thirty percent less energy than our old office.","t":"A：新辦公大樓有一套會自動開關暖氣的智慧系統，它是怎麼運作的？ B：每個房間的感測器整天都在【調節】溫度，所以大樓能讓員工保持舒適，同時比我們的舊辦公室少用約百分之三十的能源。"},{"w":"emotion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling such as love, anger, fear, or joy","c":"情緒；情感","s":"A: How did the staff react when the director announced that the company was closing the factory where many of them had worked for years? B: There was a lot of emotion in the room, because some people cried, others were angry, and everyone was worried about finding new jobs.","t":"A：當總監宣布公司要關閉許多員工工作多年的工廠時，員工有什麼反應？ B：會議室裡充滿了【情緒】，因為有些人哭了，有些人很生氣，而且每個人都擔心要找新工作。"},{"w":"avoid","p":"v.","d":"to stay away from someone or something, or to stop something from happening","c":"避免；避開；迴避","s":"A: Why do you always take the earliest train to the office, even though our working day doesn't start until nine? B: I like to avoid the crowds at rush hour, because the trains after eight o'clock are so full that I can't sit down, read, or even think clearly.","t":"A：為什麼你總是搭最早的火車去辦公室，即使我們九點才開始上班？ B：我喜歡【避開】尖峰時段的人潮，因為八點以後的火車擠到我沒辦法坐下、看書，甚至無法好好思考。"},{"w":"scary","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel afraid","c":"可怕的；嚇人的","s":"A: How did you feel when you moved to Berlin alone for your first overseas job, without knowing anyone there? B: It was really scary at first, because I didn't speak German and got lost often, but after a few months I made friends at work and started to enjoy the city.","t":"A：你獨自搬去柏林做第一份海外工作、在那裡一個人都不認識時，有什麼感覺？ B：一開始真的很【可怕】，因為我不會說德語，又常常迷路，但幾個月後我在工作上交了朋友，開始喜歡這座城市了。"},{"w":"wonder","p":"v.","d":"to think about something and want to know more about it","c":"想知道；納悶；好奇","s":"A: The new employee from Canada always eats lunch by herself in the break room and doesn't say much to anyone. B: I wonder whether she feels lonely, so let's invite her to join us for lunch tomorrow and ask her some questions about her life back home.","t":"A：那位從加拿大來的新員工總是自己一個人在休息室吃午餐，也不太和任何人說話。 B：我【想知道】她是否覺得孤單，所以我們明天邀請她和我們一起吃午餐，並問問她在家鄉生活的事吧。"},{"w":"stressful","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried and nervous","c":"壓力大的；令人緊張的","s":"A: How was your first month as a manager at the call center, and do you still enjoy the job? B: It has been very stressful, because I have to deal with angry customers, train new staff, and meet sales targets, but I'm learning a lot and starting to feel more confident.","t":"A：你在客服中心當經理的第一個月怎麼樣？你還喜歡這份工作嗎？ B：一直都【壓力很大】，因為我必須應付生氣的顧客、訓練新員工並達成業績目標，但我學到很多，也開始比較有自信了。"},{"w":"triggering","p":"adj.","d":"causing someone to have strong, upsetting feelings or memories","c":"引發情緒反應的；觸發的","s":"A: Why did the company add a short warning before the online safety training video about factory accidents? B: Some scenes in the video show serious injuries, and they could be triggering for workers who have been in accidents before, so the warning allows them to prepare or ask for another format.","t":"A：為什麼公司在關於工廠事故的線上安全訓練影片前加了一段簡短的警語？ B：影片中有些畫面顯示嚴重的傷害，對曾經發生過事故的員工來說可能會【引發強烈情緒】，所以警語讓他們可以做好準備或要求其他形式。"},{"w":"burnout","p":"n.","d":"a state of feeling extremely tired and unable to work because of too much stress","c":"倦怠；身心俱疲","s":"A: Why did the company decide to give all employees an extra week of paid holiday this year? B: Many staff members were working more than sixty hours a week, and the managers wanted to prevent burnout before people became sick or decided to quit their jobs.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定今年給所有員工多一週的帶薪假？ B：許多員工每週工作超過六十小時，主管們想在大家生病或決定辭職之前，預防【過勞倦怠】。"},{"w":"quietly","p":"adv.","d":"without making much noise","c":"安靜地；輕聲地","s":"A: The library on the third floor is the only place in our building where I can concentrate, but people keep chatting there. B: Let's put up a sign asking everyone to talk quietly or go to the café downstairs, because many employees use that room to read and prepare important reports.","t":"A：三樓的圖書室是我們大樓裡唯一能讓我專心的地方，但大家一直在那裡聊天。 B：我們貼一張告示，請大家【輕聲】說話或去樓下咖啡廳，因為很多員工會用那個房間閱讀和準備重要報告。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something that you do often and regularly, often without thinking about it","c":"習慣","s":"A: How do you stay so calm and organized, even when we have five deadlines in the same week? B: I have a habit of spending fifteen minutes alone every morning, planning my tasks with a cup of tea before I open any emails or answer any phone calls.","t":"A：即使我們同一週有五個截止期限，你是怎麼保持這麼冷靜又有條理的？ B：我有一個【習慣】，每天早上會獨自花十五分鐘，在打開任何電子郵件或接任何電話之前，邊喝茶邊規劃我的工作。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤；烤","s":"A: What do you usually do on Sunday afternoons when you live alone and your family is so far away? B: I like to bake bread and cookies in my small kitchen, because it calms me down after a busy week, and I often bring the extra cookies to the office on Monday.","t":"A：你一個人住、家人又離得那麼遠，週日下午通常都做什麼？ B：我喜歡在我的小廚房裡【烤】麵包和餅乾，因為這能讓我在忙碌的一週後平靜下來，我也常在週一把多的餅乾帶到辦公室。"},{"w":"disturb","p":"v.","d":"to interrupt someone when they are trying to work, sleep, or rest","c":"打擾；干擾","s":"A: I need to finish the budget report for the director by four o'clock, but people keep coming to my desk with questions. B: Book the small meeting room for two hours and put a sign on the door asking people not to disturb you, and I'll answer any questions for you.","t":"A：我必須在四點前完成給總監的預算報告，但一直有人到我座位問問題。 B：預約小會議室兩個小時，在門上貼個告示請大家不要【打擾】你，有任何問題我會幫你回答。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to look around a new place, or to try new activities, to learn about them","c":"探索；嘗試；探究","s":"A: You moved to Tainan alone for this new job two months ago, so how do you spend your free time when you're not working? B: I explore a different neighborhood every weekend, and I've found some wonderful temples, old streets, and food stalls that most tourists never see.","t":"A：你兩個月前為了這份新工作獨自搬到台南，不工作的時候都怎麼打發空閒時間？ B：我每個週末都去【探索】一個不同的街區，已經發現了一些很棒的廟宇、老街和大多數觀光客從沒見過的小吃攤。"},{"w":"bookworm","p":"n.","d":"a person who loves reading and spends a lot of time reading","c":"書蟲；愛看書的人","s":"A: Do you know what we should buy as a farewell gift for Ms. Kim, who is retiring from the accounting department next week? B: She is a real bookworm who reads several novels every month, so a gift card for the big bookstore near her apartment would probably make her very happy.","t":"A：你知道下週從會計部退休的金小姐，我們該買什麼當作送別禮物嗎？ B：她是個真正的【書蟲】，每個月會讀好幾本小說，所以送她公寓附近大型書店的禮券，她大概會很開心。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Ambition 抱負","cards":[{"w":"desire","p":"v.","d":"to want something very much","c":"渴望；想要","s":"A: Why did Mr. Lee leave his well-paid job at the bank last month, even though his manager offered him a promotion and a bigger office? B: He told me he had always wanted to run his own café, and he did not desire a higher position at a company where he felt bored every day.","t":"A：為什麼李先生上個月離開銀行那份高薪工作，即使他的經理提供他升遷和更大的辦公室？ B：他告訴我他一直想經營自己的咖啡店，而且他並不【渴望】在一家每天都讓他覺得無聊的公司裡得到更高的職位。"},{"w":"determination","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to keep trying until you succeed","c":"決心；毅力","s":"A: How did Sarah finish her MBA while working full-time at the marketing agency and taking care of her two young children? B: She studied late every night after the kids went to bed, and her determination to get a management role helped her pass every exam, even when she felt very tired.","t":"A：莎拉是怎麼在行銷公司全職工作、還要照顧兩個年幼孩子的同時完成企管碩士學位的？ B：她每天晚上等孩子睡了之後讀書讀到很晚，而她想取得管理職位的【決心】幫助她通過了每一場考試，即使她覺得非常疲累。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make something better","c":"改善；提升","s":"A: Our team leader said the customer survey results were disappointing this quarter, so what is the plan for the next three months? B: We are going to give all the call center staff extra training, because we really need to improve our service quality before the important contract with the hotel chain is renewed.","t":"A：我們的組長說這一季的顧客調查結果令人失望，那接下來三個月的計畫是什麼？ B：我們要給所有客服中心的員工額外的訓練，因為在和連鎖飯店的重要合約續約之前，我們真的需要【改善】我們的服務品質。"},{"w":"achieve","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in reaching a goal","c":"達成；實現","s":"A: Do you think the sales department can reach its target of one million dollars by the end of the year, even with the new competitor in town? B: I think we can achieve it if everyone keeps visiting new clients and the marketing team launches the holiday campaign on time next month.","t":"A：你覺得即使鎮上出現了新的競爭對手，業務部門還是能在年底前達到一百萬美元的目標嗎？ B：我認為如果每個人都持續拜訪新客戶，而且行銷團隊下個月準時推出節慶活動，我們就能【達成】它。"},{"w":"realize","p":"v.","d":"to make a hope or plan really happen","c":"實現（夢想、計畫）；了解","s":"A: I heard you finally opened your own design studio downtown, so how does it feel after dreaming about it for so many years? B: It feels wonderful, because I saved money for ten years and took business classes at night, and now I can finally realize my dream of working for myself.","t":"A：我聽說你終於在市中心開了自己的設計工作室，夢想了這麼多年，現在感覺如何？ B：感覺很棒，因為我存了十年的錢，晚上還去上商業課程，現在我終於可以【實現】自己當老闆的夢想了。"},{"w":"skip","p":"v.","d":"to not do something you usually do","c":"略過；不做","s":"A: You look exhausted this morning, so did you stay at the office late again to prepare the slides for the investors' meeting? B: Yes, I worked until midnight, and I had to skip lunch and dinner yesterday because I want this project to succeed and help me get promoted next year.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來累壞了，你昨天又為了準備投資人會議的簡報留在辦公室到很晚嗎？ B：對，我工作到半夜，昨天還不得不【略過】午餐和晚餐，因為我希望這個專案成功，幫助我明年獲得升遷。"},{"w":"distracted","p":"adj.","d":"not able to pay attention to what you are doing","c":"分心的","s":"A: Why did James make so many mistakes in the monthly budget report that he sent to the finance director on Friday afternoon? B: He was distracted because his phone kept ringing with calls about his new apartment, and he could not focus on the numbers while he was worrying about moving.","t":"A：為什麼詹姆士週五下午寄給財務長的月度預算報告裡有那麼多錯誤？ B：他【分心】了，因為他的手機一直響，都是關於他新公寓的電話，而他在擔心搬家的時候沒辦法專注在數字上。"},{"w":"dull","p":"adj.","d":"boring; not interesting","c":"乏味的；單調的","s":"A: Why did Kevin decide to leave the accounting department and apply for a position on the sales team last month? B: He said his daily work was dull because he entered the same kind of data every day, and he wanted a more exciting job where he could travel and meet new people.","t":"A：為什麼凱文上個月決定離開會計部門，去應徵業務團隊的職位？ B：他說他每天的工作很【乏味】，因為他每天都在輸入同一類的資料，而他想要一份更刺激、可以出差和認識新朋友的工作。"},{"w":"standstill","p":"n.","d":"a situation where nothing moves or makes progress","c":"停頓；停滯","s":"A: What happened with the plan to build the new shopping mall next to the train station, which was supposed to open next spring? B: The project has come to a standstill because the city has not approved the final design yet, so the builders are waiting and nobody knows when work will start again.","t":"A：原本預計明年春天開幕、蓋在火車站旁的新購物中心，計畫後來怎麼樣了？ B：這個專案已經陷入【停頓】，因為市政府還沒有核准最終設計，所以營建商都在等待，也沒有人知道工程什麼時候會再開始。"},{"w":"ignore","p":"v.","d":"to pay no attention to someone or something","c":"忽視；不理會","s":"A: Did the manager listen to your suggestions about the new schedule, or did she decide to keep the old system for the warehouse staff? B: Unfortunately, she decided to ignore my ideas at the meeting, but I will write a detailed report with numbers so she can see how much time we could save.","t":"A：經理有聽你對新班表的建議嗎？還是她決定讓倉庫員工維持舊制度？ B：很可惜，她在會議上決定【忽視】我的想法，但我會寫一份附有數據的詳細報告，讓她看看我們可以節省多少時間。"},{"w":"arrange","p":"v.","d":"to plan or organize something","c":"安排","s":"A: I am interested in learning more about the leadership training program, but I am not sure whom I should contact about it. B: You should talk to Ms. Chen in Human Resources, because she can arrange a meeting with the program director for you next week and explain how to apply before the deadline.","t":"A：我有興趣多了解領導力培訓課程，但我不確定該聯絡誰。 B：你應該去找人資部的陳小姐，因為她可以幫你【安排】下週和課程主任開會，並向你說明如何在截止日期前申請。"},{"w":"uncertain","p":"adj.","d":"not sure about something","c":"不確定的","s":"A: Are you going to accept the job offer from the company in Singapore, or will you stay here in Taipei with your current team? B: I am still uncertain about it, because the salary is much higher, but I would have to move far away from my family and learn a whole new market.","t":"A：你會接受新加坡那家公司的工作邀約，還是會留在台北和你現在的團隊一起？ B：我對這件事還【不確定】，因為薪水高很多，但我必須搬到離家人很遠的地方，還要學習一個全新的市場。"},{"w":"unpredictable","p":"adj.","d":"changing in a way that is hard to know before","c":"難以預測的","s":"A: Why does the restaurant need so many part-time workers on the weekend schedule when some evenings are very quiet? B: The number of customers is very unpredictable on Saturdays and Sundays, so the manager prefers to have extra staff ready in case a large tour group suddenly walks in.","t":"A：為什麼有些晚上很冷清，餐廳週末的班表卻需要那麼多兼職人員？ B：週六和週日的客人數量非常【難以預測】，所以經理寧願多準備一些人手，以防大型旅行團突然上門。"},{"w":"involvement","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something","c":"參與；涉入","s":"A: Why did the company choose Linda to lead the new community project instead of someone with more experience in marketing? B: Her involvement in several charity events over the past three years showed the directors that she works well with volunteers and really cares about helping local families.","t":"A：為什麼公司選琳達帶領新的社區專案，而不是選一個行銷經驗更豐富的人？ B：她過去三年【參與】了好幾場慈善活動，讓董事們看到她很擅長和志工合作，而且真心在乎幫助當地家庭。"},{"w":"mandatory","p":"adj.","d":"required by a rule","c":"強制的；義務的","s":"A: Do all the new employees have to attend the safety workshop on Monday morning, or can some of them join the online version later? B: The workshop is mandatory for everyone who works in the factory, so please tell your team to arrive at eight o'clock and bring their ID cards with them.","t":"A：所有新進員工都必須參加週一早上的安全講習嗎？還是有些人可以之後再參加線上版？ B：這場講習對所有在工廠工作的人來說都是【強制性的】，所以請告訴你的團隊八點到場，並帶上他們的識別證。"},{"w":"path","p":"n.","d":"a way of living or a direction in your career","c":"道路；途徑","s":"A: My younger brother just graduated from university, and he cannot decide whether to work in finance or become a teacher. B: Tell him to try a few internships first, because it takes time to find the right career path, and real work experience will show him what he enjoys doing every day.","t":"A：我弟弟剛從大學畢業，他無法決定要從事金融業還是當老師。 B：告訴他先試試幾份實習，因為要找到對的職涯【道路】需要時間，而真正的工作經驗會讓他知道自己每天喜歡做什麼。"},{"w":"renowned","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected","c":"著名的；有名望的","s":"A: Why is the hotel ballroom so full tonight, when the business dinner usually has only about fifty guests? B: A renowned chef from Paris is cooking the main course this evening, so many local business owners bought tickets because they wanted to taste his food and meet him in person.","t":"A：為什麼今晚飯店宴會廳這麼滿，而商務晚宴平常只有大約五十位賓客？ B：今晚有一位來自巴黎的【知名】主廚料理主菜，所以很多當地企業老闆都買了票，因為他們想品嚐他的料理並親自見到他。"},{"w":"initiation","p":"n.","d":"the start of a plan or process","c":"開始；啟動；入會","s":"A: When did the new training program for junior managers officially begin, and has it helped the staff so far? B: Since its initiation in January, more than forty employees have joined the program, and many of them say they now feel more confident when they lead meetings and give feedback.","t":"A：給初階主管的新培訓計畫是什麼時候正式開始的？到目前為止對員工有幫助嗎？ B：自從一月【開始實施】以來，已經有四十多名員工參加了這個計畫，其中許多人說他們現在主持會議和給予回饋時更有自信了。"},{"w":"fulfilling","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel happy and satisfied","c":"令人有成就感的；令人滿足的","s":"A: You used to earn a lot more at the law firm, so why did you decide to work for a small charity that helps older people? B: The pay is lower, but the work is much more fulfilling because I can see how my daily efforts make a real difference in people's lives.","t":"A：你以前在律師事務所賺得多很多，為什麼決定到一個幫助長者的小型慈善機構工作？ B：薪水是比較低，但這份工作讓人更有【成就感】，因為我可以看到自己每天的努力真正改變了人們的生活。"},{"w":"frustrated","p":"adj.","d":"upset because you cannot do or change something","c":"挫折的；沮喪的","s":"A: Why did Tom look so upset when he left the meeting with the IT department this afternoon? B: He feels frustrated because he has asked them three times to fix the computer system, but they keep saying they are too busy, so his team still cannot process customer orders quickly.","t":"A：為什麼湯姆今天下午和資訊部開完會離開時看起來那麼不高興？ B：他覺得很【挫折】，因為他已經要求他們修電腦系統三次了，但他們一直說太忙，所以他的團隊還是沒辦法快速處理顧客的訂單。"},{"w":"immense","p":"adj.","d":"very large","c":"巨大的；極大的","s":"A: How did the new product launch go last weekend, and were there many visitors at the company's booth at the trade fair? B: It was an immense success, because thousands of people visited our booth over two days, and we received more orders than we had expected for the whole month.","t":"A：上週末的新產品發表會進行得怎麼樣？公司在商展的攤位有很多訪客嗎？ B：那是一次【巨大的】成功，因為兩天內有數千人參觀我們的攤位，而我們收到的訂單比原本預期整個月的還要多。"},{"w":"possibility","p":"n.","d":"something that might happen or be true","c":"可能性","s":"A: Do you think the company will open a branch office in Tokyo next year, since our sales in Japan have grown so quickly? B: There is a strong possibility that it will happen, because the board discussed it last week, but they still need to find the right location and hire local staff.","t":"A：既然我們在日本的銷售成長得這麼快，你覺得公司明年會在東京開設分公司嗎？ B：這件事很有【可能】發生，因為董事會上週討論過了，但他們還需要找到合適的地點並僱用當地員工。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"so good that people admire it","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"A: Did you read the résumé from the woman who applied for the marketing manager position, and what did you think of her experience? B: Yes, her background is very impressive, since she has worked for two international companies and led a team that doubled online sales in only one year.","t":"A：你讀過那位應徵行銷經理職位女士的履歷了嗎？你覺得她的經歷如何？ B：讀過了，她的背景非常【令人印象深刻】，因為她曾在兩家跨國公司工作，還帶領團隊在短短一年內讓線上銷售翻倍。"},{"w":"decent","p":"adj.","d":"good enough; acceptable","c":"還不錯的；像樣的","s":"A: Are you happy with the new job at the logistics company, or are you still looking for something better in the city? B: I am quite happy, because the company pays a decent salary and gives good benefits, and my manager has promised to send me to training courses next year.","t":"A：你對物流公司的新工作滿意嗎？還是你還在城裡找更好的工作？ B：我蠻滿意的，因為公司給的薪水【還不錯】，福利也很好，而且我的主管答應明年會送我去上培訓課程。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"hard work and loyalty to a job or goal","c":"奉獻；投入","s":"A: Why is the CEO giving Ms. Wang a special award at the annual dinner, when she is not a manager or a director? B: She has worked here for twenty-five years and never missed a deadline, so the award is to thank her for her dedication to the company and its customers.","t":"A：為什麼執行長要在年度晚宴上頒特別獎給王小姐，而她既不是經理也不是主管？ B：她在這裡工作了二十五年，從來沒錯過任何截止期限，所以這個獎是為了感謝她對公司和顧客的【奉獻】。"},{"w":"vital","p":"adj.","d":"very important; necessary","c":"極為重要的；必要的","s":"A: Should I spend more time on the slides or on practicing my speech before tomorrow's presentation to the new clients from Korea? B: Practicing is vital, because the clients will judge you by how clearly and confidently you speak, and nice slides will not help if you cannot answer their questions.","t":"A：明天要向來自韓國的新客戶做簡報，在那之前我應該多花時間做投影片還是練習演講？ B：練習是【極為重要的】，因為客戶會根據你說話有多清楚、多有自信來評價你，如果你回答不了他們的問題，漂亮的投影片也沒有用。"},{"w":"fascination","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest in something","c":"著迷；強烈的興趣","s":"A: How did Maria end up working as an engineer for an airline company after studying history at university? B: She has had a fascination with airplanes since she was a little girl, so after graduation she took night classes in engineering and finally got the job she always dreamed of.","t":"A：瑪莉亞大學念的是歷史，最後怎麼會在航空公司當工程師？ B：她從小就對飛機非常【著迷】，所以畢業後她去上工程的夜間課程，終於得到了她一直夢想的工作。"},{"w":"prospect","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something good will happen in the future","c":"前景；可能性","s":"A: Why are so many young people applying for jobs at the new electric car factory outside the city this year? B: The company offers good training, and the prospect of getting promoted quickly is attractive to graduates who want to build a long career in a growing industry.","t":"A：為什麼今年有這麼多年輕人去應徵城外那間新電動車工廠的工作？ B：這家公司提供很好的訓練，而且快速升遷的【前景】對想在成長產業中長久發展的畢業生很有吸引力。"},{"w":"astonishing","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising","c":"驚人的；令人驚訝的","s":"A: Did you hear that the small startup down the street was bought by a huge technology company for fifty million dollars? B: Yes, it is astonishing news, because the company only started two years ago in a tiny office with three employees, and now everyone in the industry is talking about it.","t":"A：你聽說街上那家小型新創公司被一家大型科技公司以五千萬美元收購了嗎？ B：聽說了，這真是【驚人的】消息，因為那家公司兩年前才在一間小辦公室裡由三名員工創立，現在業界每個人都在談論它。"},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"a building or place used for a special purpose","c":"設施；場所","s":"A: Where will the new employees from the overseas office receive their technical training when they arrive next month? B: They will stay at the company's training facility in Hsinchu, which has modern classrooms, a lab, and a small hotel, so they will not need to travel every day.","t":"A：海外辦公室的新進員工下個月抵達後，會在哪裡接受技術訓練？ B：他們會待在公司位於新竹的訓練【設施】，那裡有現代化的教室、實驗室和一間小旅館，所以他們不需要每天通勤。"},{"w":"aspiration","p":"n.","d":"a strong hope to achieve something","c":"抱負；志向","s":"A: During your job interview, what did you tell the manager when she asked about your goals for the next five years? B: I told her that my aspiration is to become a team leader, so I plan to take management courses and learn as much as I can from experienced colleagues.","t":"A：在你的工作面試中，當經理問你未來五年的目標時，你怎麼回答？ B：我告訴她我的【抱負】是成為團隊領導人，所以我打算去上管理課程，並盡可能向有經驗的同事學習。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give money, help, or ideas","c":"貢獻；捐助","s":"A: Our department is collecting money for the new library at the children's hospital, so would you like to join us this month? B: Of course, I would be glad to contribute some money, and I can also ask my friends at the bank if they want to help with books and toys.","t":"A：我們部門正在為兒童醫院的新圖書室募款，你這個月想加入我們嗎？ B：當然，我很樂意【捐】一些錢，我也可以問問我在銀行的朋友，看他們是否想幫忙提供書籍和玩具。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Animal 動物","cards":[{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to understand the value of something and be thankful for it","c":"欣賞；感激","s":"A: How did the volunteers from our office feel after spending the whole Saturday cleaning up the city animal shelter last weekend? B: They were tired but happy, and the shelter manager said she really wanted to appreciate their hard work, so she sent each of them a thank-you card with a photo of the dogs.","t":"A：我們辦公室的志工上週末花了整個星期六打掃市立動物收容所，之後他們感覺如何？ B：他們很累但很開心，收容所經理說她非常想【感謝】他們的辛勞，所以她寄給每個人一張附有狗狗照片的感謝卡。"},{"w":"stand out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be easy to see or notice because it is different or better","c":"突出；脫穎而出","s":"A: Why did the pet food company choose that small design agency for its new advertising campaign instead of the big firm in the city? B: The agency's poster showed a sleepy cat sitting inside a coffee cup, and the bright, funny picture made their idea stand out from all the other proposals the marketing team received.","t":"A：為什麼那家寵物食品公司的新廣告活動選了那間小型設計公司，而不是城裡的大公司？ B：那間公司的海報畫了一隻坐在咖啡杯裡打瞌睡的貓，這張明亮又有趣的圖讓他們的點子在行銷團隊收到的所有提案中【脫穎而出】。"},{"w":"creation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something new, or the new thing that is made","c":"創造；創建；作品","s":"A: What is the main goal of the new project that the city council and the local zoo announced at the press conference yesterday afternoon? B: They are planning the creation of a large wildlife park outside town, which will protect rare birds, provide about two hundred jobs, and attract more tourists to the area.","t":"A：市議會和當地動物園昨天下午在記者會上宣布的新計畫，主要目標是什麼？ B：他們正在規劃在城外【創建】一座大型野生動物園，它將保護稀有鳥類、提供大約兩百個工作機會，並吸引更多觀光客來到這個地區。"},{"w":"special","p":"adj.","d":"different from usual and better or more important","c":"特別的；特殊的","s":"A: Is it true that the hotel downtown now allows guests to bring their dogs, even though pets were not permitted there in the past? B: Yes, they opened a special floor for pet owners last month, with wooden floors, dog beds, and a small garden, and the rooms are fully booked every weekend.","t":"A：市中心那家飯店現在真的允許房客帶狗入住嗎？過去那裡是不准帶寵物的。 B：是的，他們上個月為飼主開放了一個【特別的】樓層，有木頭地板、狗床和一座小花園，而且每個週末房間都被訂滿。"},{"w":"emotional","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing strong feelings","c":"情感的；情緒激動的","s":"A: Why did Mr. Lin leave the meeting early, and why did he look so upset when he returned to his desk this afternoon? B: His family's old dog died this morning after fifteen years together, so he felt very emotional and needed a few minutes alone before he could talk to the clients again.","t":"A：林先生為什麼提早離開會議？他今天下午回到座位時為什麼看起來那麼難過？ B：他家那隻陪伴了十五年的老狗今天早上過世了，所以他的情緒非常【激動】，需要獨處幾分鐘才能再和客戶談話。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"a relationship or link between people, animals or things","c":"連結；關係","s":"A: Why does the hospital let trained dogs visit the patients in the children's ward every Wednesday afternoon? B: The doctors found that the kids feel calmer and less lonely when they build a connection with a friendly animal, and many of them also eat better and sleep longer after the visits.","t":"A：為什麼醫院每週三下午讓受過訓練的狗去探訪兒童病房的病人？ B：醫生們發現，孩子們和友善的動物建立【連結】時，會覺得比較平靜、比較不孤單，而且很多孩子在探訪後也吃得更好、睡得更久。"},{"w":"dedicated to something","p":"adj.phr.","d":"giving a lot of time and energy to one thing because you care about it","c":"致力於某事；全心投入某事","s":"A: What kind of person are you looking for to manage the new animal rescue center that the company is sponsoring next year? B: We need someone who is dedicated to something they truly believe in, because the job has long hours and low pay, and the manager must keep working hard even on difficult days.","t":"A：你們在找什麼樣的人來管理公司明年要贊助的新動物救援中心？ B：我們需要一個【全心投入】自己真心相信之事的人，因為這份工作工時長、薪水低，即使在辛苦的日子，管理者也必須持續努力。"},{"w":"come across somebody","p":"v.phr.","d":"to meet or find someone by chance","c":"偶然遇見某人","s":"A: How did you find such an experienced dog trainer for the security team at the warehouse so quickly last month? B: I was walking in the park on Sunday morning when I happened to come across somebody who was training three police dogs, so I asked for her business card and invited her for an interview.","t":"A：上個月你是怎麼這麼快就為倉庫保全團隊找到一位經驗這麼豐富的訓犬師？ B：星期天早上我在公園散步時，碰巧【遇見一個人】正在訓練三隻警犬，所以我向她要了名片，並邀請她來面試。"},{"w":"husky","p":"n.","d":"a strong dog with thick fur that can pull sleds over snow","c":"哈士奇；雪橇犬","s":"A: Have you decided which photo to use on the front page of our winter travel brochure for the trip to northern Canada? B: Yes, the design team picked a picture of a beautiful husky pulling a sled across the snow, because it shows the adventure and excitement that our customers are looking for.","t":"A：你決定好我們加拿大北部旅遊行程的冬季旅遊手冊封面要用哪張照片了嗎？ B：決定了，設計團隊選了一張美麗的【哈士奇】拉著雪橇穿越雪地的照片，因為它呈現出顧客想要的冒險與刺激感。"},{"w":"infeasible","p":"adj.","d":"not possible to do in practice","c":"不可行的","s":"A: Why did the board reject the plan to build a large pet hotel on the empty land next to our shopping mall? B: The engineers reported that the land is too wet and the building costs would be far too high, so the whole project was judged infeasible and the board voted against it.","t":"A：董事會為什麼否決在我們購物中心旁邊空地蓋一間大型寵物旅館的計畫？ B：工程師報告說那塊地太潮濕，建築成本也會高出太多，所以整個計畫被判定為【不可行】，董事會因此投票反對。"},{"w":"child-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"suitable and safe for children","c":"適合兒童的；對兒童友善的","s":"A: Which restaurant should we book for the company family day, since many employees are bringing their young kids this year? B: Let's choose the farm café near the river, because it is very child-friendly, with a small petting zoo, a safe play area, and a special menu for kids under ten.","t":"A：今年很多員工會帶小孩來，公司家庭日我們應該訂哪家餐廳？ B：我們選河邊那家農場咖啡廳吧，因為它非常【適合兒童】，有一個小型動物觸摸區、安全的遊戲區，還有給十歲以下孩子的特別菜單。"},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"causing death","c":"致命的","s":"A: Why did the farm owner call the vet so early this morning, and why are all the workers wearing masks and gloves today? B: A few of the chickens became sick overnight, and the vet warned that the disease can be fatal to birds if it spreads, so everyone must follow strict safety rules.","t":"A：農場主人今天一大早為什麼打電話給獸醫？為什麼今天所有工人都戴著口罩和手套？ B：有幾隻雞一夜之間生病了，獸醫警告說這種疾病如果擴散，對鳥類可能是【致命的】，所以大家都必須遵守嚴格的安全規定。"},{"w":"dread to think","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be afraid to imagine something bad that might happen","c":"不敢想像","s":"A: Did you hear that the security guard found a large snake in the storage room just before the school children arrived for their factory tour? B: Yes, luckily he caught it and called the animal control office, but I dread to think what might have happened if one of the kids had opened that door first.","t":"A：你有沒有聽說，就在學童抵達工廠參觀前，保全在儲藏室裡發現了一條大蛇？ B：有，幸好他抓住了牠並打電話給動物管制單位，但我真【不敢想像】如果有個孩子先打開那扇門會發生什麼事。"},{"w":"improvement","p":"n.","d":"a change that makes something better","c":"改善；進步","s":"A: Has the new diet that the zoo started last spring made any difference to the health of the older elephants? B: Yes, the keepers have seen a clear improvement in their weight and energy, and the vet said the animals are now walking longer distances and eating more fresh fruit every day.","t":"A：動物園去年春天開始的新飲食，對年長大象的健康有任何影響嗎？ B：有，飼育員看到牠們的體重和活力都有明顯的【改善】，獸醫也說這些動物現在每天走更遠的距離，也吃更多新鮮水果。"},{"w":"vertical","p":"adj.","d":"standing or pointing straight up","c":"垂直的；直立的","s":"A: How can the pet store fit so many fish tanks and bird houses into such a small shop on the main street? B: The owner installed tall vertical shelves along every wall, so the tanks are stacked from the floor to the ceiling, which saves space and still leaves room for customers to walk around.","t":"A：大街上那間寵物店那麼小，怎麼放得下那麼多魚缸和鳥屋？ B：老闆沿著每面牆裝了高大的【垂直】層架，所以魚缸從地板一路疊到天花板，既節省空間，又還留有讓顧客走動的空間。"},{"w":"beloved","p":"adj.","d":"loved very much","c":"心愛的；深受喜愛的","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office signing that large card on the reception desk, and who is it for? B: Our manager's beloved cat, which used to visit the office every Friday and sleep on the printer, passed away last night, so we want to show her that we care about her.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室裡每個人都在簽櫃台上那張大卡片？是要給誰的？ B：我們經理【心愛的】貓昨晚過世了，牠以前每個星期五都會來辦公室，睡在印表機上，所以我們想讓她知道我們很關心她。"},{"w":"rear","p":"v.","d":"to care for young animals or children until they are fully grown","c":"飼養；養育","s":"A: What does your cousin do on that large farm in the mountains, since she moved away from the city three years ago? B: She and her husband rear sheep and goats for wool and cheese, and they also sell their products online to customers and restaurants all over the country.","t":"A：你表姊三年前搬離城市後，在山上那座大農場做什麼？ B：她和她先生【飼養】綿羊和山羊來生產羊毛和起司，他們也在網路上把產品賣給全國各地的顧客和餐廳。"},{"w":"adopt","p":"v.","d":"to take an animal or child into your home and care for it as your own","c":"領養；收養","s":"A: Are you still planning to buy a puppy from the pet shop near the train station after you move into your new apartment? B: No, I changed my mind after visiting the animal shelter last weekend, and I decided to adopt an older dog that needs a home instead of paying a lot of money.","t":"A：你搬進新公寓後，還打算從火車站附近那家寵物店買一隻小狗嗎？ B：不了，上週末我去過動物收容所後改變主意，我決定【領養】一隻需要家的老狗，而不是花很多錢去買。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"嗜好；業餘愛好","s":"A: What do you usually do on weekends to relax, since your job at the bank is so stressful during the week? B: My favorite hobby is bird watching, so I often drive to the wetlands with my camera early on Saturday morning and spend a few quiet hours taking photos of the birds.","t":"A：你在銀行的工作平日壓力那麼大，週末通常做什麼來放鬆？ B：我最喜歡的【嗜好】是賞鳥，所以我常在星期六一大早帶著相機開車去濕地，花幾個安靜的小時拍鳥的照片。"},{"w":"immense","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large or great","c":"巨大的；極大的","s":"A: Was the charity event for the wildlife protection group a success, and how much money did your team finally raise? B: It was an immense success, because more than two thousand people attended, and we raised enough money to build a new hospital for injured sea turtles on the coast.","t":"A：為野生動物保護團體舉辦的慈善活動成功嗎？你們團隊最後募到多少錢？ B：那是一次【巨大的】成功，因為有超過兩千人參加，而且我們募到的錢足夠在海岸邊蓋一間新的受傷海龜醫院。"},{"w":"naughty","p":"adj.","d":"behaving badly; used about children or pets","c":"頑皮的；淘氣的","s":"A: Why are you late for the morning meeting, and why is there mud all over the bottom of your trousers? B: Sorry, my naughty puppy ran out of the gate while I was taking out the trash, and I had to chase him through the neighbor's wet garden for almost twenty minutes.","t":"A：你為什麼晨會遲到？褲管下面為什麼全都是泥巴？ B：抱歉，我在倒垃圾的時候，我那隻【頑皮的】小狗從大門跑出去，我只好在鄰居濕答答的花園裡追了牠將近二十分鐘。"},{"w":"relatively","p":"adv.","d":"when compared with other things or people","c":"相對地；比較而言","s":"A: Do you think a rabbit would be a good pet for my daughter, since we live in a small apartment and both work long hours? B: Yes, rabbits are relatively quiet and clean compared with dogs, and they don't need daily walks, but you will still have to clean their space every few days.","t":"A：你覺得兔子適合給我女兒當寵物嗎？我們住在小公寓，而且兩個人工時都很長。 B：適合，和狗相比，兔子【相對】安靜又乾淨，也不需要每天散步，不過你們還是得每隔幾天清理牠們的空間。"},{"w":"absolutely","p":"adv.","d":"completely; totally","c":"絕對地；完全地","s":"A: Is it really all right to bring my guide dog into your restaurant, since I saw a sign at the door that says no animals are allowed? B: Yes, it is absolutely fine, because that rule doesn't apply to working dogs, and our staff will happily find you a quiet table near the window.","t":"A：帶我的導盲犬進你們餐廳真的沒問題嗎？我在門口看到一個寫著禁止動物進入的告示。 B：是的，【完全】沒問題，因為那條規定不適用於工作犬，我們的員工也很樂意為您安排靠窗的安靜座位。"},{"w":"definitely","p":"adv.","d":"certainly; without any doubt","c":"一定；肯定地","s":"A: Should we include the visit to the panda center in the schedule for the overseas clients, or will they be too tired after the long flight? B: We should definitely keep it, because several of the clients said in their emails that seeing the pandas was the thing they were most excited about.","t":"A：我們應該把參觀熊貓中心排進海外客戶的行程嗎？還是他們長途飛行後會太累？ B：我們【一定】要保留這個行程，因為有好幾位客戶在電子郵件中說，看熊貓是他們最期待的事。"},{"w":"cage","p":"n.","d":"a box made of metal bars or wire for keeping birds or animals","c":"籠子","s":"A: How should we send the two parrots that the customer ordered, since they are traveling by plane to another city tomorrow? B: The airline requires each bird to travel in a strong cage with water, food, and holes for fresh air, so please check the size rules on their website before you buy one.","t":"A：客戶訂的兩隻鸚鵡明天要搭飛機去另一個城市，我們應該怎麼寄送？ B：航空公司規定每隻鳥都必須裝在堅固的【籠子】裡運送，要附上水、食物和通風孔，所以你買之前請先到他們網站查看尺寸規定。"},{"w":"dump","p":"v.","d":"to leave something or someone somewhere because you do not want it","c":"丟棄；拋棄","s":"A: Why has the animal shelter asked the city to put more cameras along the country road behind the industrial park? B: Some people drive there at night to dump pets they no longer want, and the shelter hopes the cameras will stop them and help the police find the owners.","t":"A：為什麼動物收容所要求市政府在工業區後方的鄉間道路多裝一些攝影機？ B：有些人晚上開車到那裡【丟棄】他們不想再養的寵物，收容所希望攝影機能阻止他們，並幫助警方找到飼主。"},{"w":"stroke","p":"v.","d":"to move your hand gently over something, such as an animal's fur","c":"撫摸","s":"A: Is it all right for the children on the school tour to touch the animals at your farm, or is that too dangerous for them? B: They can gently stroke the baby goats and the rabbits in the small yard, but they must wash their hands afterward and stay away from the horses.","t":"A：參加校外教學的孩子們可以摸你們農場的動物嗎？還是那對他們來說太危險了？ B：他們可以在小院子裡輕輕【撫摸】小山羊和兔子，但之後一定要洗手，而且要遠離那些馬。"},{"w":"depressed","p":"adj.","d":"very sad and without hope, often for a long time","c":"沮喪的；憂鬱的","s":"A: Why did your sister decide to get a dog after she moved to Taipei for her new job at the advertising company? B: She felt lonely and a little depressed living alone in a new city, so her doctor suggested a pet, and now she walks in the park every evening and has made new friends.","t":"A：你妹妹搬到台北去廣告公司做新工作後，為什麼決定養狗？ B：她一個人住在陌生的城市覺得孤單，也有點【沮喪】，所以她的醫生建議她養寵物，現在她每天傍晚都去公園散步，還交了新朋友。"},{"w":"hesitate","p":"v.","d":"to stop or wait before doing something because you are not sure","c":"猶豫","s":"A: What will you do if my dog gets sick while I am away on my business trip and you are looking after him? B: I will take him to the vet right away, but please don't hesitate to send me his medical records and the clinic's phone number before you leave, so I have everything ready.","t":"A：我出差期間由你照顧我的狗，如果牠生病了你會怎麼做？ B：我會立刻帶牠去看獸醫，不過請你出發前不要【猶豫】，把牠的病歷和診所電話傳給我，這樣我就能把一切準備好。"},{"w":"chores","p":"n.","d":"small regular jobs that you do at home, such as cleaning","c":"家務；雜事","s":"A: How do you manage to keep your house clean while working full-time and taking care of two cats and a large dog? B: My husband and I share the chores every weekend, so he vacuums the pet hair and washes the floors while I clean the litter boxes and do the laundry.","t":"A：你全職工作，還要照顧兩隻貓和一隻大狗，是怎麼保持家裡乾淨的？ B：我先生和我每個週末分擔【家務】，他用吸塵器吸寵物毛並拖地，我則清理貓砂盆和洗衣服。"},{"w":"companion","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal you spend a lot of time with","c":"同伴；伴侶","s":"A: Why does the retirement home in our neighborhood keep a cat in the main lounge, even though some visitors are worried about allergies? B: The staff said the cat is a wonderful companion for the older residents, who feel happier and less lonely when it sits on their laps during the afternoon.","t":"A：我們社區的養老院為什麼在主要交誼廳養了一隻貓，即使有些訪客擔心過敏問題？ B：工作人員說，那隻貓是年長住戶很棒的【同伴】，下午牠坐在他們腿上時，他們會覺得更快樂、比較不孤單。"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to make pain, worry or stress less","c":"減輕；緩解","s":"A: Why did the tech company bring several puppies into the office during the final week of the busy product launch? B: The managers wanted to relieve stress among the engineers, who were working late every night, and playing with the puppies for a few minutes really helped everyone feel calmer.","t":"A：為什麼那家科技公司在忙碌的產品發表最後一週把幾隻小狗帶進辦公室？ B：主管們想【減輕】每天晚上都工作到很晚的工程師們的壓力，和小狗玩幾分鐘真的讓大家感覺平靜許多。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Apologize 道歉","cards":[{"w":"sorry","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sad about something you did wrong","c":"抱歉的；難過的","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager call you so early this morning, and is there a problem with the room we booked for the visiting clients? B: She called to say she was very sorry because the air conditioner in their suite broke last night, so she has moved them to a bigger room for free.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理今天一大早就打電話給你？我們幫來訪客戶訂的房間有問題嗎？ B：她打來說她非常【抱歉】，因為他們套房的冷氣昨晚壞了，所以她已經免費把他們換到更大的房間。"},{"w":"regret","p":"n.","d":"a sad feeling about something you wish you had not done","c":"遺憾；懊悔","s":"A: Have you heard back from the customer whose order was sent to the wrong address last week, and is she still angry with us? B: Yes, our director wrote to her personally to express deep regret for the mistake, and she was pleased that we also offered her a discount on her next purchase.","t":"A：上週訂單被寄錯地址的那位顧客有回覆了嗎？她還在生我們的氣嗎？ B：有，我們的主管親自寫信給她，對這個錯誤表達深深的【遺憾】，而且她很高興我們還提供她下次購物的折扣。"},{"w":"remorse","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of being sorry for doing something wrong","c":"懊悔；自責","s":"A: Why did Kevin stay so late at the office yesterday, even though his shift finished at five and his family was waiting for dinner? B: He felt real remorse after he deleted the shared sales report by accident, so he stayed until midnight to rebuild every page before the morning meeting.","t":"A：為什麼凱文昨天在辦公室待到那麼晚？他的班明明五點就結束了，家人還在等他吃晚餐。 B：他不小心刪掉了共用的業績報告之後感到非常【懊悔】，所以他一直待到半夜，在早上開會前把每一頁都重新做好。"},{"w":"forgive","p":"v.","d":"to stop being angry with someone who did something wrong","c":"原諒；寬恕","s":"A: Do you think the restaurant owner will keep working with our catering company after we delivered the wrong cakes to her wedding event on Saturday? B: I hope she will forgive us, because we have already returned her money, sent fresh flowers to her shop, and promised a free dessert table next month.","t":"A：我們星期六把錯的蛋糕送到那位餐廳老闆的婚禮活動上，你覺得她還會繼續跟我們的外燴公司合作嗎？ B：我希望她會【原諒】我們，因為我們已經退錢給她、送了鮮花到她店裡，還承諾下個月免費提供甜點桌。"},{"w":"forgiveness","p":"n.","d":"the act of forgiving someone","c":"原諒；寬恕","s":"A: What did the airline say in the email after our flight to Tokyo was cancelled without any warning and we missed the trade show? B: The customer service team asked for our forgiveness, explained that a storm had closed the airport, and gave each passenger a travel voucher worth three hundred dollars.","t":"A：我們飛往東京的班機在毫無預警下被取消，害我們錯過了商展，航空公司在電子郵件裡怎麼說？ B：客服團隊請求我們的【原諒】，解釋是暴風雨導致機場關閉，並給每位乘客一張價值三百美元的旅遊抵用券。"},{"w":"excuse","p":"v.","d":"to forgive someone for something small, such as being rude or late","c":"原諒（小過失）；請見諒","s":"A: Why did the new trainee leave the meeting room so suddenly while the manager was still explaining the safety rules to everyone? B: She got an urgent call from her daughter's school, so she said, 'Please excuse me,' and promised to read the meeting notes carefully later in the afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼經理還在向大家說明安全規定時，那位新來的實習生突然離開會議室？ B：她接到女兒學校打來的緊急電話，所以她說「請【原諒】我」，並承諾下午稍晚會仔細閱讀會議紀錄。"},{"w":"admit","p":"v.","d":"to say that something bad is true, often that you did it","c":"承認","s":"A: Did anyone find out why the shipment of printers left the warehouse two days late and caused so many complaints from our stores? B: Yes, the new supervisor had the courage to admit that he had forgotten to sign the delivery form, and he has already created a checklist so it won't happen again.","t":"A：有人查出那批印表機為什麼晚了兩天才離開倉庫，讓我們的門市收到那麼多抱怨嗎？ B：有，新來的主管有勇氣【承認】他忘了簽出貨單，而且他已經做了一份檢查清單，以免再發生這種事。"},{"w":"acknowledge","p":"v.","d":"to accept or say that something is true or exists","c":"承認；確認","s":"A: How did the bank respond when you called about the extra charge on your credit card statement this month? B: The manager was very helpful; she was quick to acknowledge that their system had made an error, and she said the money would be returned to my account within three working days.","t":"A：你這個月打電話去問信用卡帳單上多出來的費用時，銀行怎麼回應？ B：經理非常幫忙，她很快就【承認】是他們的系統出錯，並說這筆錢會在三個工作天內退回我的帳戶。"},{"w":"confess","p":"v.","d":"to admit that you did something wrong, often something you kept secret","c":"坦白；招認","s":"A: Why did Mr. Lin look so nervous when he walked into the director's office after lunch today? B: He had to confess that he lost the company laptop on the train last Friday, and he was worried because it contained important files about our new product launch in Singapore.","t":"A：林先生今天午餐後走進主管辦公室時，為什麼看起來那麼緊張？ B：他必須【坦白】他上週五在火車上弄丟了公司的筆電，他很擔心，因為裡面有關於我們在新加坡推出新產品的重要檔案。"},{"w":"fault","p":"n.","d":"responsibility for a mistake or problem","c":"過錯；責任","s":"A: Should we ask the customer to pay for the broken glass table, since it was damaged during the delivery to her new apartment? B: No, it was our driver's fault because he did not tie it down properly in the truck, so we will replace the table and pay for the shipping ourselves.","t":"A：那張玻璃桌在送到她新公寓的途中損壞了，我們應該請顧客付錢嗎？ B：不行，那是我們司機的【過錯】，因為他沒有在貨車上把它綁牢，所以我們會換一張新桌子，運費也由我們自己負擔。"},{"w":"blame","p":"n.","d":"responsibility for something bad that happened","c":"責備；過錯責任","s":"A: Why is the project manager so upset after the client cancelled the contract, when most of the problems came from the design team? B: He feels that he must take the blame as the leader of the project, so he is preparing an apology letter and a plan to win back the client's trust.","t":"A：大部分的問題都出在設計團隊，為什麼客戶取消合約後專案經理會那麼難過？ B：他覺得身為專案的負責人，他必須承擔【過錯責任】，所以他正在準備一封道歉信和一份贏回客戶信任的計畫。"},{"w":"responsibility","p":"n.","d":"the duty to deal with something, or being the one who caused a problem","c":"責任","s":"A: What did the company president say at the press conference after customers found mistakes in the new phone's instruction booklet? B: She accepted full responsibility for the problem, thanked the customers who reported it, and announced that corrected booklets would be mailed to every buyer by the end of the month.","t":"A：顧客發現新手機的說明書有錯誤後，公司總裁在記者會上說了什麼？ B：她為這個問題承擔全部【責任】，感謝回報問題的顧客，並宣布會在月底前把更正後的說明書寄給每位買家。"},{"w":"make amends","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something good to show you are sorry for something bad you did","c":"彌補；賠罪","s":"A: Why is the café giving free coffee to everyone in our office building this morning, even to people who have never been there before? B: The owner wants to make amends for the loud construction noise last week, which bothered many workers, so she is also handing out discount cards for next month.","t":"A：為什麼那家咖啡店今天早上要送免費咖啡給我們辦公大樓裡的每個人，連從沒去過的人也有？ B：老闆想為上週吵鬧的施工噪音向大家【彌補】，那些噪音打擾了很多上班族，所以她也在發放下個月的折扣卡。"},{"w":"reconcile","p":"v.","d":"to become friendly again after an argument","c":"和解；和好","s":"A: Are the two sales directors still refusing to speak to each other after their argument about the bonus system last month? B: No, the general manager invited them to lunch, listened to both sides, and helped them reconcile, so now they are planning the new marketing campaign together without any problems.","t":"A：那兩位業務主管上個月為了獎金制度吵架之後，現在還是拒絕跟彼此說話嗎？ B：沒有了，總經理請他們吃午餐，聽了雙方的說法，並幫助他們【和解】，所以現在他們正一起順利地規劃新的行銷活動。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken or damaged, such as a relationship","c":"修補；修復","s":"A: What is the hotel doing now that the online reviews about its rude front desk staff have spread so quickly across social media? B: The new manager is trying to repair the hotel's reputation by training every employee in customer service and personally answering each negative review with a polite apology.","t":"A：關於飯店櫃檯人員態度無禮的網路評論在社群媒體上迅速擴散，飯店現在打算怎麼做？ B：新經理正努力【修補】飯店的名聲，他訓練每位員工的客服能力，並親自以禮貌的道歉回覆每一則負評。"},{"w":"sincere","p":"adj.","d":"honest and really meaning what you say","c":"真誠的；誠懇的","s":"A: How did the customer react when our team leader called her to talk about the missing items in her online order? B: She was angry at first, but she calmed down because his apology sounded sincere, and he also arranged for a courier to bring the missing items to her home that same evening.","t":"A：我們的組長打電話給那位顧客，談她網購訂單裡缺少的商品時，她有什麼反應？ B：她一開始很生氣，但後來冷靜下來了，因為他的道歉聽起來很【真誠】，而且他還安排快遞員當天晚上就把缺少的商品送到她家。"},{"w":"heartfelt","p":"adj.","d":"felt very deeply and honestly","c":"衷心的；真摯的","s":"A: What did the staff do for Mrs. Chen after the office party, when someone accidentally broke the vase her late mother had given her? B: Everyone signed a card with a heartfelt message saying how sorry they were, and the team also bought her a beautiful new vase from her favorite shop.","t":"A：辦公室派對上有人不小心打破陳太太已故母親送她的花瓶後，同事們為她做了什麼？ B：大家在一張卡片上簽名，寫下【衷心的】話語表達他們有多抱歉，團隊也從她最喜歡的店買了一個漂亮的新花瓶送她。"},{"w":"humble","p":"adj.","d":"not proud; not thinking you are better than others","c":"謙虛的；謙卑的","s":"A: Why do so many employees respect the new CEO, even though she has only worked at our company for three months? B: She is very humble; when her plan to change the work schedule failed, she apologized to the whole staff in an email and asked for their ideas to improve it.","t":"A：新任執行長才在我們公司工作三個月，為什麼有那麼多員工尊敬她？ B：她非常【謙虛】；當她更改工作時間表的計畫失敗時，她寫電子郵件向全體員工道歉，並請大家提供改善的想法。"},{"w":"ashamed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling bad or guilty about something you did","c":"羞愧的；慚愧的","s":"A: Did you talk to the new assistant who shouted at a customer on the phone yesterday because the system kept crashing? B: Yes, she said she felt deeply ashamed of her behavior, so she called the customer back this morning to apologize and offered to process his order for him herself.","t":"A：昨天因為系統一直當機而在電話裡對顧客大吼的那位新助理，你跟她談過了嗎？ B：談過了，她說她對自己的行為感到非常【羞愧】，所以今天早上她回電向那位顧客道歉，並主動親自幫他處理訂單。"},{"w":"embarrassed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling shy or uncomfortable because of something you did in front of others","c":"尷尬的；難為情的","s":"A: Why did Tom's face turn so red during the presentation to the investors this afternoon? B: He felt really embarrassed when he noticed that his slides had the wrong company name on them, so he stopped, apologized to everyone in the room, and quickly explained the correct sales figures.","t":"A：今天下午向投資人做簡報時，湯姆的臉為什麼變得那麼紅？ B：他發現投影片上的公司名稱寫錯時感到非常【尷尬】，所以他停下來向會議室裡的每個人道歉，並迅速說明正確的銷售數字。"},{"w":"polite","p":"adj.","d":"speaking and acting in a kind way that shows respect for others","c":"有禮貌的","s":"A: What should I write in the reply to the guest who complained that his room was not cleaned during his three-day stay? B: Keep your email short and polite, say that you are sorry for the trouble, and offer him a free breakfast or a discount the next time he visits our hotel.","t":"A：有位客人抱怨他住宿三天期間房間都沒有打掃，我回信時該寫些什麼？ B：信要寫得簡短又【有禮貌】，說你對造成的麻煩感到抱歉，並在他下次來我們飯店時提供免費早餐或折扣。"},{"w":"respectfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows respect","c":"恭敬地；尊重地","s":"A: How should I tell the client that we cannot finish the website by Friday without making her feel that we don't care about her project? B: Speak to her respectfully, apologize for the change, explain clearly why the testing needs more time, and give her a new date that you are sure the team can meet.","t":"A：我該怎麼告訴客戶我們無法在星期五前完成網站，又不讓她覺得我們不在乎她的專案？ B：【恭敬地】跟她說話，為這個變動道歉，清楚說明為什麼測試需要更多時間，並給她一個你確定團隊能趕上的新日期。"},{"w":"honestly","p":"adv.","d":"in a truthful way, without hiding anything","c":"誠實地；坦白地","s":"A: What happened when the shop manager found out that the new cashier had given a customer the wrong change on Monday? B: The cashier explained honestly what had happened, so the manager did not get angry; instead, they called the customer together, apologized, and returned the money that same afternoon.","t":"A：店長發現新來的收銀員星期一找錯錢給顧客時，發生了什麼事？ B：收銀員【誠實地】說明了事情經過，所以店長沒有生氣；他們反而一起打電話給那位顧客道歉，並在當天下午就把錢退還給他。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in front of other people or in a way that everyone can see","c":"公開地","s":"A: Why did the food company post a video message on its website and social media accounts last night? B: The president wanted to apologize publicly for the wrong labels on its cookie boxes, because many customers were worried, and she promised that all the boxes in stores would be replaced this week.","t":"A：那家食品公司昨晚為什麼在官網和社群媒體帳號上發布一段影片訊息？ B：總裁想要【公開地】為餅乾盒上的錯誤標示道歉，因為很多顧客都很擔心，她並承諾本週內會更換店裡所有的盒子。"},{"w":"formally","p":"adv.","d":"in an official and serious way","c":"正式地","s":"A: Is a phone call enough to say sorry to our biggest client for the shipping delay that cost them a week of sales? B: I don't think so; we should apologize formally in a signed letter from the director, and then arrange a meeting to discuss how we will prevent similar delays in the future.","t":"A：運送延誤讓我們最大的客戶損失了一週的銷售，只打一通電話道歉夠嗎？ B：我覺得不夠；我們應該用一封主管簽名的信【正式地】道歉，然後安排一場會議，討論我們將來要如何避免類似的延誤。"},{"w":"personally","p":"adv.","d":"by yourself, not by sending someone else","c":"親自地","s":"A: Did the regional manager send an assistant to visit the customer whose washing machine flooded her kitchen after our technician fixed it? B: No, he went personally to her house yesterday afternoon to apologize, check the damage, and promise that our company would pay for the new floor.","t":"A：我們技師修好那位顧客的洗衣機後卻淹了她的廚房，區經理有派助理去拜訪她嗎？ B：沒有，他昨天下午【親自】去她家道歉、查看損壞情況，並承諾我們公司會支付新地板的費用。"},{"w":"promptly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without delay","c":"迅速地；立即地","s":"A: What is the most important thing to do when a guest complains about the service in our restaurant during a busy dinner? B: You should respond promptly, listen carefully without interrupting, apologize for the problem, and then ask the kitchen to prepare a new dish so the guest does not have to wait too long.","t":"A：在忙碌的晚餐時段，客人抱怨我們餐廳的服務時，最重要的是做什麼？ B：你應該【迅速地】回應，仔細聆聽不要打斷，為問題道歉，然後請廚房準備一道新菜，讓客人不用等太久。"},{"w":"graciously","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind, polite and generous way","c":"親切地；寬厚地","s":"A: How did the guest speaker react when our team forgot to prepare a microphone for her talk at the annual conference? B: She graciously accepted our apology, smiled at the audience, and spoke loudly for the first ten minutes while our technician brought a new microphone from the hotel's storage room.","t":"A：我們團隊在年會上忘了幫演講嘉賓準備麥克風，她有什麼反應？ B：她【寬厚地】接受了我們的道歉，對觀眾微笑，並在前十分鐘大聲演講，同時我們的技術人員從飯店的儲藏室拿來一支新的麥克風。"},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"to agree to take something that is offered, such as an apology","c":"接受","s":"A: Has the supplier answered the letter we sent after our accountant paid their invoice two months late by mistake? B: Yes, they wrote back to say that they accept our apology and understand that the delay was caused by the new software, so they are happy to continue our partnership next year.","t":"A：我們的會計誤將供應商的發票晚了兩個月才付款後，我們寄了一封信，他們回覆了嗎？ B：回了，他們回信說他們【接受】我們的道歉，也理解延誤是新軟體造成的，所以很樂意明年繼續我們的合作關係。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Apology Letter 道歉信","cards":[{"w":"regret","p":"v.","d":"to feel sorry about something you did or that happened","c":"後悔；遺憾","s":"A: Have you finished the letter to the hotel guests whose wedding party was moved to a smaller room at the last minute? B: Almost, and I want the first line to say that we deeply regret the change, because the couple had planned the decorations for months and were very upset.","t":"A：你寫完給那些婚宴在最後一刻被移到較小廳的飯店客人的信了嗎？ B：快寫完了，我希望第一行就說明我們對這次的更動深感【遺憾】，因為那對新人花了好幾個月規劃佈置，他們非常難過。"},{"w":"mistake","p":"n.","d":"something done wrong because of bad judgment or not paying attention","c":"錯誤；失誤","s":"A: Why did the customer in Kaohsiung receive twenty boxes of printer paper when she only ordered two boxes for her small office? B: A new clerk in the warehouse made a mistake when he typed the order, so we are sending a driver to collect the extra boxes this afternoon at no cost to her.","t":"A：為什麼高雄那位客戶的小辦公室只訂了兩箱影印紙，卻收到二十箱？ B：倉庫一位新來的職員在輸入訂單時犯了【錯誤】，所以我們今天下午會派司機去把多出來的箱子收回，她不需要負擔任何費用。"},{"w":"error","p":"n.","d":"a mistake, especially in numbers, writing or a system","c":"錯誤；差錯","s":"A: I just noticed that our monthly electricity bill is three times higher than usual, even though the office was closed for a week. Should we call the power company? B: Yes, please call them today, because it is probably a billing error, and they usually send a corrected bill within a few business days.","t":"A：我剛注意到我們這個月的電費帳單比平常高了三倍，可是辦公室明明關了一個星期。我們要打電話給電力公司嗎？ B：要，請今天就打給他們，因為這很可能是帳單【錯誤】，他們通常會在幾個工作天內寄來更正後的帳單。"},{"w":"fault","p":"n.","d":"responsibility for a mistake or problem","c":"過錯；責任","s":"A: The client is angry that the brochures arrived with the wrong phone number printed on the back cover. Did our design team cause the problem? B: No, it wasn't our fault, because the client sent us the old number in their email, but we will still reprint the brochures quickly to keep a good relationship.","t":"A：客戶很生氣，因為送到的宣傳手冊封底印錯了電話號碼。是我們設計團隊造成的問題嗎？ B：不是，這不是我們的【過錯】，因為客戶在電子郵件裡給我們的是舊號碼，但為了維持良好的關係，我們還是會盡快重印手冊。"},{"w":"responsibility","p":"n.","d":"the duty of dealing with something, or being the cause of a problem","c":"責任","s":"A: The online store sent the wrong size of jackets to more than fifty customers last weekend. What should our apology email say to them? B: It should say clearly that we take full responsibility for the problem, and then offer each customer a free exchange and a discount code for their next order.","t":"A：上週末網路商店寄錯了五十多位顧客的夾克尺寸。我們的道歉信應該怎麼寫？ B：信中應該清楚說明我們對這個問題負起全部【責任】，然後提供每位顧客免費換貨，以及下次訂購可用的折扣碼。"},{"w":"inconvenience","p":"n.","d":"a problem that causes trouble or makes things less easy","c":"不便；麻煩","s":"A: The elevators in our building will be closed for repairs all day on Friday, and many visitors will have to use the stairs. Should we tell our clients ahead of time? B: Yes, let's send them a short notice today and apologize for any inconvenience, especially to the older clients who have meetings on the tenth floor.","t":"A：我們大樓的電梯星期五整天都要停用維修，很多訪客將必須走樓梯。我們應該事先通知客戶嗎？ B：要，我們今天就寄一封簡短的通知給他們，並為造成的任何【不便】致歉，尤其是要在十樓開會的年長客戶。"},{"w":"trouble","p":"n.","d":"problems, difficulty or extra work","c":"麻煩；困難","s":"A: The supplier drove all the way from Taichung to replace the broken coffee machine in our break room this morning. Should we thank him in some way? B: Yes, I think we should write him a short note, because he went to a lot of trouble to help us, even though his company was already busy with other orders.","t":"A：供應商今天早上大老遠從台中開車過來，替我們更換休息室裡壞掉的咖啡機。我們應該用某種方式謝謝他嗎？ B：應該，我覺得我們該寫張簡短的謝卡給他，因為他不怕【麻煩】、特地來幫我們，即使他們公司已經在忙其他訂單了。"},{"w":"delay","p":"n.","d":"a time when something happens later than planned","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: The new laptops for the sales team were supposed to arrive on Monday, but they still haven't come. Did the shipping company give you any reason? B: They said the delay was caused by a typhoon that closed the port in Keelung for two days, and they expect the laptops to arrive by Thursday afternoon.","t":"A：業務團隊的新筆電原本應該星期一送到，但到現在還沒來。貨運公司有給你任何理由嗎？ B：他們說這次【延誤】是因為颱風讓基隆港關閉了兩天，他們預計筆電會在星期四下午前送達。"},{"w":"late","p":"adj.","d":"happening or arriving after the expected time","c":"遲的；晚的","s":"A: I'm writing an apology to the client because our monthly report reached her two days after the deadline. What else should I mention in the email? B: Explain that the report was late because two team members were sick, and promise that next month's report will be sent at least one day early.","t":"A：我在寫道歉信給客戶，因為我們的月報比截止日期晚了兩天才送到她手上。電子郵件裡我還應該提到什麼？ B：說明報告之所以【遲交】是因為有兩位組員生病，並承諾下個月的報告至少會提早一天寄出。"},{"w":"misunderstanding","p":"n.","d":"a situation where people do not understand each other correctly","c":"誤會；誤解","s":"A: Mr. Wang thought our meeting was at ten in the morning, but the rest of us arrived at two in the afternoon. How did that happen? B: There was a misunderstanding about the time because the invitation used a twenty-four-hour clock, so I will call him today and set up a new meeting that suits his schedule.","t":"A：王先生以為我們的會議是早上十點，但我們其他人卻是下午兩點才到。怎麼會這樣？ B：因為邀請函使用二十四小時制，大家對時間產生了【誤會】，所以我今天會打電話給他，另外安排一個適合他行程的會議。"},{"w":"careless","p":"adj.","d":"not paying enough attention, so mistakes happen","c":"粗心的","s":"A: How did the hotel booking for our visitors from Japan get the dates wrong when they had already sent us all the details by email? B: I'm afraid I was careless when I copied the dates into the booking system, so I will contact the hotel right away and write a short apology to the visitors myself.","t":"A：日本訪客早就用電子郵件把所有細節寄給我們了，為什麼他們的飯店訂房日期還會弄錯？ B：恐怕是我把日期輸入訂房系統時太【粗心】了，所以我會馬上聯絡飯店，並親自寫一封簡短的道歉信給訪客。"},{"w":"unintentional","p":"adj.","d":"not done on purpose","c":"無心的；非故意的","s":"A: One of our customers says our newsletter shared her phone number with everyone on the mailing list. Is that true, and what should we tell her? B: Sadly, it is true, but the mistake was completely unintentional, because the software added a wrong column, so we should apologize and explain how we fixed the system.","t":"A：有位顧客說我們的電子報把她的電話號碼分享給了郵寄名單上的所有人。這是真的嗎？我們該怎麼跟她說？ B：很遺憾，這是真的，但這個錯誤完全是【無心的】，因為軟體多加了一個錯誤的欄位，所以我們應該向她道歉，並說明我們如何修正了系統。"},{"w":"sincere","p":"adj.","d":"honest and really meant","c":"真誠的；誠摯的","s":"A: Our regional manager wants to send flowers to the customer who fell on the wet floor in our store last week. Is that enough, or should we do more? B: Flowers are nice, but I think she would value a sincere letter from the manager more, because it shows that someone really cares about what happened to her.","t":"A：我們的區經理想送花給上週在我們店裡濕滑地板上跌倒的那位顧客。這樣夠嗎？還是我們應該做更多？ B：送花很好，但我覺得她會更看重經理寫的一封【真誠的】信，因為那代表有人真正關心她發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"deeply","p":"adv.","d":"very much; strongly","c":"深深地；非常","s":"A: The restaurant served the wrong dish to one of our guests at the company dinner last night, and she had to wait almost an hour for her meal. Is she all right now? B: She is fine, but the owner was deeply sorry, so he called her this morning and promised to give her a free dinner next week.","t":"A：昨晚公司聚餐時，餐廳把錯的菜端給我們一位客人，她等了將近一小時才吃到她的餐點。她現在還好嗎？ B：她沒事，但老闆【深深地】感到抱歉，所以他今天早上打電話給她，並承諾下週請她免費吃一頓晚餐。"},{"w":"truly","p":"adv.","d":"really; in a real and honest way","c":"真心地；確實","s":"A: Do you think the client will believe our apology after we missed the delivery date for the third time this year? B: She will only believe us if we are truly sorry and show it with action, so let's offer her free delivery for six months and give her a direct phone number for our manager.","t":"A：今年我們已經第三次錯過交貨日期了，你覺得客戶還會相信我們的道歉嗎？ B：只有我們【真心】感到抱歉並用行動證明，她才會相信我們，所以我們就提供她六個月的免運，並給她經理的直撥電話號碼吧。"},{"w":"wholeheartedly","p":"adv.","d":"completely and with all your feelings","c":"全心全意地；由衷地","s":"A: The staff at the branch office worked all weekend to fix the problem our mistake caused in their computer system. How should we thank them? B: Our director will visit them on Monday and wholeheartedly apologize for the extra work, and she will also bring lunch for the whole team to show how grateful we are.","t":"A：分公司的員工整個週末都在加班，修復我們的錯誤在他們電腦系統中造成的問題。我們該如何感謝他們？ B：我們的主管星期一會去拜訪他們，【由衷地】為額外的工作致歉，她也會為整個團隊帶午餐過去，表達我們有多感激。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear by giving details or reasons","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Several passengers missed their connecting flights because our airport shuttle broke down on the highway this morning. What should I write in the email to them? B: First, explain what happened to the shuttle and why it took so long to send another bus, and then tell them how we will pay for their new tickets.","t":"A：今天早上我們的機場接駁車在高速公路上拋錨，好幾位乘客錯過了轉機班機。我應該在給他們的電子郵件裡寫些什麼？ B：首先，【說明】接駁車發生了什麼事，以及為什麼花了那麼久才派另一輛巴士過去，然後告訴他們我們將如何支付他們的新機票。"},{"w":"reason","p":"n.","d":"a cause or explanation for something","c":"原因；理由","s":"A: Our biggest customer canceled the contract renewal meeting this morning without saying much. Do you know why she did that? B: She told me the main reason was our slow customer service last month, so I'm writing her a letter today to apologize and to show her the changes we have already made.","t":"A：我們最大的客戶今天早上取消了續約會議，也沒多說什麼。你知道她為什麼這麼做嗎？ B：她告訴我主要的【原因】是我們上個月的客服太慢，所以我今天會寫一封信給她，向她道歉，並讓她看看我們已經做出的改變。"},{"w":"situation","p":"n.","d":"the things that are happening at a certain time and place","c":"情況；處境","s":"A: The air conditioning in the conference hall stopped working during the product launch, and many guests left early because it was so hot. How should we handle this? B: Let's call each guest personally to explain the situation, apologize for the uncomfortable afternoon, and invite them to a private product demonstration next month.","t":"A：產品發表會期間會議廳的冷氣停止運轉，很多賓客因為太熱而提早離開。我們該怎麼處理？ B：我們親自打電話給每位賓客說明【情況】，為那個不舒服的下午道歉，並邀請他們參加下個月的私人產品展示會。"},{"w":"circumstance","p":"n.","d":"a fact or condition that affects what happens","c":"情況；狀況","s":"A: Why did the training workshop for new employees start an hour late this morning, and why did nobody tell us about the change? B: Because of a circumstance beyond our control, the trainer's train from Hsinchu was stopped for an hour, and the message to staff failed to send, so we will apologize to everyone today.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上的新進員工訓練課程晚了一小時才開始？為什麼都沒人通知我們這個變動？ B：由於我們無法控制的【狀況】，講師從新竹搭的火車停駛了一小時，而且發給員工的通知沒有成功寄出，所以我們今天會向大家道歉。"},{"w":"promise","p":"v.","d":"to say that you will certainly do something","c":"承諾；答應","s":"A: The customer who waited three weeks for her new sofa wants to know if her next order will also take that long. What should I tell her? B: Apologize again and promise that her next delivery will arrive within five days, but only say it if the warehouse manager agrees that it is possible.","t":"A：那位等了三週才收到新沙發的顧客想知道，她下一次訂購是否也要等那麼久。我該怎麼告訴她？ B：再次向她道歉，並【承諾】她下一次的貨會在五天內送達，但前提是倉庫經理同意這是做得到的才說。"},{"w":"assure","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone something firmly so they feel less worried","c":"向…保證；使放心","s":"A: The guests are worried after the fire alarm went off twice in the hotel last night, and some want to check out early. What should the front desk say? B: The staff should apologize for the noise and assure the guests that the building is safe, because the technician found that a faulty sensor caused both alarms.","t":"A：昨晚飯店的火災警報響了兩次，客人們都很擔心，有些人想提早退房。櫃台應該怎麼說？ B：員工應該為噪音道歉，並向客人【保證】大樓是安全的，因為技師發現兩次警報都是一個故障的感應器造成的。"},{"w":"guarantee","p":"v.","d":"to promise firmly that something will happen or be done","c":"保證；擔保","s":"A: Our client is upset because the posters for her concert were printed in the wrong colors. Can we print new ones in time for the event next Saturday? B: Yes, our print shop can work overtime, so we can guarantee that the new posters will be ready by Wednesday, and we won't charge her anything extra for them.","t":"A：我們的客戶很不高興，因為她音樂會的海報印錯了顏色。我們能在下星期六活動前及時印好新的嗎？ B：可以，我們的印刷廠可以加班，所以我們可以【保證】新海報會在星期三前完成，而且不會向她收取任何額外費用。"},{"w":"correct","p":"v.","d":"to make something right or remove the mistakes from it","c":"改正；更正","s":"A: The price list on our website still shows last year's prices, and three customers have already complained that they were charged more at checkout. What should we do? B: Ask the web team to correct the prices before noon today, and then send those three customers an apology and a refund for the difference.","t":"A：我們網站上的價目表還是去年的價格，已經有三位顧客抱怨結帳時被收了比較多錢。我們該怎麼做？ B：請網站團隊今天中午前【更正】價格，然後寄給那三位顧客道歉信，並退還差額。"},{"w":"fix","p":"v.","d":"to repair something or solve a problem","c":"修理；解決","s":"A: Customers keep calling because the payment page on our app shows an error message every time they try to pay by credit card. How long will it take? B: Our technicians think they can fix the problem by tonight, so let's post an apology on our homepage and tell customers to pay by bank transfer until then.","t":"A：顧客一直打電話來，因為他們每次想用信用卡付款時，我們應用程式的付款頁面都會出現錯誤訊息。要多久才能處理好？ B：我們的技術人員認為今晚就能【解決】這個問題，所以我們先在首頁公告致歉，並告訴顧客在那之前改用銀行轉帳付款。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to find a solution to a problem or disagreement","c":"解決","s":"A: The tenants on the fifth floor have complained for two weeks about the noise from the construction work next door. Has the building manager done anything yet? B: She met the construction company yesterday to resolve the issue, and they agreed to start work after nine in the morning, so she is writing an apology letter to the tenants now.","t":"A：五樓的房客已經抱怨隔壁施工的噪音兩個星期了。大樓管理員做了什麼處理嗎？ B：她昨天和建設公司見面來【解決】這個問題，他們同意早上九點以後才開工，所以她現在正在寫道歉信給房客。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make something better","c":"改善；改進","s":"A: Our survey shows that many hotel guests were unhappy with the long wait at the front desk during the busy holiday season. What are we going to do about it? B: We plan to improve the check-in process by adding two more staff in the evenings and letting guests check in on our mobile app before they arrive.","t":"A：我們的調查顯示，許多住客對假期旺季時櫃台要等很久感到不滿。我們打算怎麼處理？ B：我們計劃在晚上增加兩名員工，並讓住客抵達前就能用我們的手機應用程式辦理入住，藉此【改善】入住流程。"},{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"防止；預防","s":"A: The client was angry when she found that her private files had been sent to the wrong company by email last Friday. What steps are we taking now? B: We have apologized to her, and we added a new check to our email system to prevent the same thing from happening again in the future.","t":"A：那位客戶發現她的私人檔案上星期五被用電子郵件寄到錯誤的公司時非常生氣。我們現在採取了哪些措施？ B：我們已經向她道歉，並在電子郵件系統中新增了一道檢查程序，以【防止】同樣的事情將來再度發生。"},{"w":"ensure","p":"v.","d":"to make certain that something happens","c":"確保","s":"A: The conference organizers apologized because there weren't enough seats for all the guests at last year's event. Will this year be any different? B: Yes, they have booked a much larger hall and hired extra staff to ensure that every guest has a seat and gets a copy of the program at the door.","t":"A：研討會主辦單位曾為去年活動座位不夠所有來賓坐而道歉。今年會有所不同嗎？ B：會，他們訂了一個大得多的會場，並多請了工作人員，以【確保】每位來賓都有座位，並在門口拿到一份議程表。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be grateful for something","c":"感激；感謝","s":"A: How should I end the letter to the customer whose package was lost during our office move last month? She was very calm on the phone with me. B: You should say that we really appreciate her patience while we searched for the package, and that a replacement has already been sent by express mail.","t":"A：上個月我們辦公室搬遷時弄丟了一位顧客的包裹，給她的信我該怎麼結尾？她在電話中對我非常冷靜。 B：你應該說，我們在尋找包裹期間非常【感謝】她的耐心，而且替代品已經用快遞寄出了。"},{"w":"understanding","p":"n.","d":"kindness and patience shown when someone accepts a problem","c":"體諒；諒解","s":"A: The main road to our factory will be closed for a week, so all deliveries to our customers will be one or two days slower than usual. How should I finish the notice? B: End it by thanking customers for their understanding and giving them the phone number of our service desk in case they have any urgent orders.","t":"A：通往我們工廠的主要道路將封閉一週，所以所有送給客戶的貨都會比平常慢一兩天。這份通知我該怎麼結尾？ B：最後感謝客戶的【體諒】，並提供我們服務台的電話號碼，以防他們有任何緊急訂單。"},{"w":"patience","p":"n.","d":"the ability to wait calmly without getting angry","c":"耐心","s":"A: Many passengers at the station have been waiting more than an hour for the train to Tainan because of a signal problem. What should we announce next? B: Announce that the trains will start running again in twenty minutes, apologize for the long wait, and thank the passengers for their patience during this difficult morning.","t":"A：因為號誌問題，車站裡很多旅客已經等前往台南的火車等了一個多小時。我們接下來該廣播什麼？ B：廣播說火車將在二十分鐘後恢復行駛，為長時間的等候致歉，並感謝旅客在這個辛苦的早上所展現的【耐心】。"},{"w":"forgive","p":"v.","d":"to stop being angry with someone for something they did","c":"原諒","s":"A: I accidentally sent the meeting notes with the private salary details to the entire department this morning. Do you think my manager will be angry with me? B: She might be upset at first, but if you tell her the truth right away and help her deal with the problem, I'm sure she will forgive you quickly.","t":"A：我今天早上不小心把附有私人薪資明細的會議紀錄寄給了整個部門。你覺得我的經理會對我生氣嗎？ B：她一開始可能會不高興，但如果你馬上跟她說實話，並幫她處理這個問題，我相信她很快就會【原諒】你。"},{"w":"forgiveness","p":"n.","d":"the act of forgiving someone","c":"原諒；寬恕","s":"A: Our team leader shouted at the new assistant in front of everyone during the busy sales meeting yesterday, and the assistant was very upset. Has he said anything since then? B: Yes, he went to her desk this morning, asked for her forgiveness, and promised to talk to staff more calmly and privately when there is a problem.","t":"A：昨天在忙碌的業務會議上，我們組長當著大家的面對新來的助理大吼，助理非常難過。他之後有說什麼嗎？ B：有，他今天早上走到她的座位，請求她的【原諒】，並承諾以後有問題時會更冷靜、私下地和員工談。"},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"to agree to take something that is offered","c":"接受","s":"A: The hotel offered the guest a free night and dinner for two after the cleaning staff entered his room by mistake while he was sleeping. Did he say yes? B: At first he wanted a full refund, but after the manager called him personally, he decided to accept the apology and the free night.","t":"A：清潔人員在一位客人睡覺時誤闖他的房間，飯店事後招待他免費住一晚和兩人晚餐。他答應了嗎？ B：他一開始想要全額退款，但經理親自打電話給他之後，他決定【接受】道歉和免費住宿。"},{"w":"once again","p":"adv.phr.","d":"one more time","c":"再一次；再次","s":"A: I have finished the letter to the customers whose orders were canceled because of our computer system problem last week. How should I close it? B: Close it by saying that we apologize once again for the trouble, and remind them that their discount code can be used until the end of next month.","t":"A：給上週因電腦系統問題被取消訂單的顧客的信我寫完了。我該怎麼結尾？ B：最後說我們【再一次】為造成的麻煩致歉，並提醒他們折扣碼可以使用到下個月月底。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"in an honest and real way; also used to end a formal letter","c":"真誠地；誠摯地","s":"A: The airline canceled our flight to Singapore because of a technical problem, and we missed the first day of the trade fair. Has the airline said anything to us? B: Yes, they sent an email this morning saying they sincerely apologize, and they are offering each of us a voucher worth three hundred dollars for our next trip.","t":"A：航空公司因為技術問題取消了我們飛往新加坡的班機，我們錯過了商展的第一天。航空公司有跟我們說什麼嗎？ B：有，他們今天早上寄了一封電子郵件，說他們【誠摯地】致歉，並且提供我們每人一張價值三百美元的抵用券，供下次旅行使用。"},{"w":"immediately","p":"adv.","d":"at once; without waiting","c":"立即；馬上","s":"A: A customer just called to say that the milk she bought at our supermarket this morning had already gone bad when she opened it at home. What should we do? B: Ask her to come back with the receipt so we can refund her immediately, and please also check every carton on that shelf before more customers buy it.","t":"A：一位顧客剛打電話來說，她今天早上在我們超市買的牛奶，回家打開時就已經壞了。我們該怎麼做？ B：請她帶收據回來，好讓我們【立即】退款給她，也請你在更多顧客購買之前檢查那個貨架上的每一盒牛奶。"},{"w":"soon","p":"adv.","d":"in a short time from now","c":"很快；不久","s":"A: The online shop told me that my printer would be shipped on Monday, but it still hasn't left their warehouse after four days. Did they reply to my email? B: Yes, they apologized for the slow service and said the printer will be sent out very soon, probably tomorrow morning, along with a free box of ink cartridges.","t":"A：網路商店告訴我印表機會在星期一出貨，但四天過去了還沒離開他們的倉庫。他們回覆我的電子郵件了嗎？ B：回了，他們為服務太慢道歉，並說印表機【很快】就會寄出，大概明天早上，還會附送一盒免費的墨水匣。"},{"w":"attention","p":"n.","d":"the act of noticing or dealing with something","c":"注意；關注","s":"A: Who first noticed that the wrong delivery address was printed on all the shipping labels for our biggest customer's order? B: One of the drivers brought the problem to our attention before he left the warehouse, so we stopped the trucks in time and sent the customer an apology for the small delay.","t":"A：是誰最先發現我們最大客戶訂單的所有出貨標籤都印錯了送貨地址？ B：一位司機在離開倉庫前讓我們【注意】到了這個問題，所以我們及時攔下了卡車，並為小小的延誤向客戶道歉。"},{"w":"matter","p":"n.","d":"a subject or situation that you must deal with","c":"事情；問題","s":"A: A customer wrote to our head office to say that a store clerk was rude to her when she tried to return a broken lamp. Who is handling the complaint? B: The regional manager is looking into the matter personally, and she plans to call the customer this afternoon to apologize and offer her a full refund.","t":"A：一位顧客寫信到我們總公司，說她想退回一盞壞掉的檯燈時，店員對她很無禮。誰在處理這件客訴？ B：區經理正親自調查這件【事情】，她打算今天下午打電話給這位顧客道歉，並提供全額退款。"},{"w":"response","p":"n.","d":"an answer or reaction","c":"回應；回覆","s":"A: Mr. Lin wrote to us last week to complain about the noise from our night deliveries, but nobody has answered him yet. Is that a problem? B: Yes, it is, because a slow response can make an angry customer even angrier, so please send him a short apology and explain our new delivery hours today.","t":"A：林先生上週寫信給我們，抱怨我們夜間送貨的噪音，但到現在都還沒人回覆他。這會有問題嗎？ B：會，因為【回應】太慢會讓生氣的顧客更生氣，所以請你今天寄給他一封簡短的道歉信，並說明我們新的送貨時間。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"App 應用程式","cards":[{"w":"app","p":"n.","d":"a program you use on a phone or computer","c":"應用程式；App","s":"A: I keep forgetting which meeting rooms are free, and the front desk is always busy when I call, so is there an easier way to book one? B: Yes, the company has a new app on our phones, so you can check which rooms are open and reserve one in a few seconds before you leave your desk.","t":"A：我老是忘記哪些會議室有空，而且我打電話時櫃台總是很忙，有沒有比較簡單的預約方法？ B：有，公司在我們的手機上推出了一個新的【應用程式】，你離開座位前只要幾秒鐘就能查看哪些會議室有空並預約。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a computer program designed for a particular job","c":"應用軟體；應用程式","s":"A: Our accounting team spends hours every week typing sales numbers into spreadsheets by hand, and they often make small mistakes, so what can we do about it? B: The IT manager suggested a new software application that collects the numbers from every store automatically, which should save time and reduce errors before the monthly report is due.","t":"A：我們的會計團隊每週都花好幾個小時手動把銷售數字輸入試算表，而且常常出小錯，我們能怎麼辦？ B：資訊部經理建議用一套新的【應用軟體】，它能自動收集每家門市的數字，這應該能在月報截止前節省時間並減少錯誤。"},{"w":"app store","p":"n.phr.","d":"an online shop where you get programs for your phone","c":"應用程式商店","s":"A: Our customers keep asking where they can get our new shopping program for their phones, and the marketing team hasn't sent out any instructions yet, so what should I tell them? B: Tell them to open the app store on their phone and type our company name, and they can get it for free in less than a minute.","t":"A：顧客一直問哪裡可以取得我們新的手機購物程式，行銷團隊還沒發出任何說明，我該怎麼告訴他們？ B：請他們打開手機上的【應用程式商店】，輸入我們的公司名稱，不到一分鐘就能免費取得。"},{"w":"download","p":"v.","d":"to copy files or programs from the internet to your device","c":"下載","s":"A: I'm flying to Tokyo for the trade show tomorrow, and I heard the internet on the plane is very slow and expensive, so how can I read the reports during the flight? B: You should download all the files onto your laptop tonight while you're still at the office, so you can open them later without any connection.","t":"A：我明天要飛去東京參加商展，我聽說飛機上的網路很慢又很貴，飛行途中我要怎麼看報告？ B：你應該今晚還在辦公室時就把所有檔案【下載】到筆電裡，這樣之後沒有網路也能打開。"},{"w":"install","p":"v.","d":"to put a program on a computer or phone so it is ready to use","c":"安裝","s":"A: The new security program that the head office sent us last week still isn't working on my computer, and I have a client meeting in an hour, so can you help me? B: Of course, I'll come to your desk and install it for you now, but you'll need to restart your computer afterward, which takes about five minutes.","t":"A：總公司上週寄給我們的新安全程式在我的電腦上還是不能用，而我一小時後要和客戶開會，你能幫我嗎？ B：當然，我現在就到你座位幫你【安裝】，不過之後你需要重新開機，大概要五分鐘。"},{"w":"update","p":"v.","d":"to add the newest information to something","c":"更新","s":"A: Customers have been complaining that our online menu still shows last month's prices, and some of them were surprised when they paid more at the counter, so who's responsible for that? B: That's my job, actually, and I'm sorry because I forgot to update the menu after the price change, but I'll fix it this afternoon.","t":"A：顧客一直抱怨我們的線上菜單還是顯示上個月的價格，有些人在櫃台付了比較多錢時很驚訝，這是誰負責的？ B：其實那是我的工作，很抱歉我在價格調整後忘了【更新】菜單，我今天下午會修正。"},{"w":"interface","p":"n.","d":"the screens and buttons that let a person use a program","c":"介面；操作介面","s":"A: The older employees in the warehouse said the new inventory system is too difficult, and some of them still write everything on paper instead, so what's the main problem? B: Most of them told me the interface is confusing because the buttons are tiny and the menus are hidden, so we're asking the designers to make the screens simpler.","t":"A：倉庫裡年紀較大的員工說新的庫存系統太難用，有些人甚至還是全部寫在紙上，主要的問題是什麼？ B：他們大部分告訴我【介面】很令人困惑，因為按鈕很小、選單又藏起來，所以我們正請設計師把畫面做得更簡單。"},{"w":"feature","p":"n.","d":"an important or interesting part of a product","c":"功能；特色","s":"A: Why did the sales team choose this new phone for all the staff when it's more expensive than the one we used before? B: They liked one special feature that turns spoken words into written notes during meetings, so salespeople can listen to clients carefully instead of writing everything down by hand.","t":"A：這款新手機比我們以前用的貴，為什麼業務團隊還幫所有員工選它？ B：他們喜歡其中一項特別的【功能】，可以在會議中把口說內容轉成文字筆記，這樣業務員就能專心聽客戶說話，而不用全部手寫下來。"},{"w":"functionality","p":"n.","d":"the range of things a program or machine can do","c":"功能性；功能","s":"A: The free version of the design program looks almost the same as the expensive one, so why does the art department want us to pay for the full package this year? B: The free version has limited functionality, which means designers can't share files with clients or work on large projects together, so it slows the whole team down.","t":"A：這套設計程式的免費版看起來跟昂貴的版本幾乎一樣，為什麼美術部今年要我們付費買完整版？ B：免費版的【功能】有限，也就是說設計師不能和客戶分享檔案，也不能一起做大型專案，所以會拖慢整個團隊。"},{"w":"user","p":"n.","d":"a person who uses a product or service","c":"使用者；用戶","s":"A: Before we spend more money on advertising the new booking website, shouldn't we find out whether people actually enjoy it? B: Good idea, so let's send a short survey to every user who booked a hotel room through it last month, and we can ask them what they liked and what confused them.","t":"A：在我們花更多錢宣傳新的訂房網站之前，不是應該先了解大家是否真的喜歡它嗎？ B：好主意，那我們寄一份簡短的問卷給上個月透過網站訂飯店房間的每一位【使用者】，問問他們喜歡什麼、哪裡讓他們感到困惑。"},{"w":"account","p":"n.","d":"a personal record that lets you use a website or service","c":"帳號；帳戶","s":"A: I'd like to see my order history and change my delivery address on your website, but the page keeps asking me for a password, so what should I do? B: First you need to create an account with your email address and a password, and after that you can manage all your orders and addresses in one place.","t":"A：我想在你們的網站上查看訂單紀錄並更改送貨地址，但頁面一直要我輸入密碼，我該怎麼辦？ B：你需要先用電子郵件地址和密碼建立一個【帳號】，之後就能在同一個地方管理所有訂單和地址。"},{"w":"login","p":"n.","d":"the name and password you use to enter a system","c":"登入帳號；登入","s":"A: I'm starting at the Taipei branch on Monday, and I'll need to check the team schedule and my email from my first morning, so what do I need from the office? B: The IT department will give you a login and a temporary password on your first day, and you should change the password as soon as you sign in.","t":"A：我週一要開始在台北分公司上班，第一天早上就需要查看團隊行程和電子郵件，我需要辦公室提供什麼？ B：資訊部會在你上班第一天給你【登入帳號】和臨時密碼，你一登入就應該馬上更改密碼。"},{"w":"subscribe","p":"v.","d":"to sign up to get something regularly, often by paying","c":"訂閱","s":"A: I really enjoy the business news podcast that you recommended, but I keep forgetting to check when a new episode comes out, so is there an easier way? B: You can subscribe to the program on your phone, and then every new episode will appear automatically each Monday morning, so you can listen on your way to work.","t":"A：我很喜歡你推薦的商業新聞播客，但我老是忘記看新的一集什麼時候出來，有更簡單的方法嗎？ B：你可以在手機上【訂閱】這個節目，之後每週一早上新的一集就會自動出現，你就能在上班途中收聽。"},{"w":"subscription","p":"n.","d":"money you pay regularly to receive a product or service","c":"訂閱；訂閱費","s":"A: Why are we paying the music company every single month, when nobody in the office remembers signing any long contract with them? B: That's for the background music in our shops, and the subscription costs thirty dollars a month, but we can cancel it any time if we find a cheaper service.","t":"A：為什麼我們每個月都要付錢給那家音樂公司？辦公室裡沒有人記得和他們簽過什麼長期合約啊。 B：那是我們店裡的背景音樂，這項【訂閱】每月三十美元，但如果找到更便宜的服務，我們隨時可以取消。"},{"w":"free","p":"adj.","d":"costing no money","c":"免費的","s":"A: Our small café can't afford expensive advertising this year, so how can we let more people in the neighborhood know about our new breakfast menu? B: We could post photos on social media, which is completely free, and ask our regular customers to share them with their friends, so it won't cost us anything at all.","t":"A：我們的小咖啡館今年負擔不起昂貴的廣告，要怎麼讓附近更多人知道我們的新早餐菜單？ B：我們可以在社群媒體上貼照片，那是完全【免費的】，再請常客分享給朋友，這樣一毛錢都不用花。"},{"w":"paid","p":"adj.","d":"that you must pay money to use","c":"付費的","s":"A: Is it true that the language-learning program the company offers has two versions, and why do the managers in our department all use the more expensive one? B: Yes, the paid version has no advertisements and lets you practice speaking with a teacher online, so the company covers the cost for managers who travel abroad.","t":"A：公司提供的語言學習程式真的有兩種版本嗎？為什麼我們部門的經理們都用比較貴的那個？ B：是的，【付費】版沒有廣告，還能和老師線上練習口說，所以公司幫要出國的經理們支付費用。"},{"w":"in-app purchase","p":"n.phr.","d":"something you buy inside a program after you download it","c":"應用程式內購買；內購","s":"A: My son played a game on my work phone during the weekend, and now my credit card bill shows a strange charge of fifty dollars, so what do you think happened? B: He probably made an in-app purchase, like buying extra coins inside the game, so you should turn on a password for payments to stop it from happening again.","t":"A：我兒子週末用我的公務手機玩遊戲，現在我的信用卡帳單上出現一筆奇怪的五十美元費用，你覺得發生了什麼事？ B：他可能做了一筆【應用程式內購買】，例如在遊戲裡買額外的金幣，所以你應該開啟付款密碼，避免再次發生。"},{"w":"rating","p":"n.","d":"a score that shows how good something is","c":"評分；評等","s":"A: Our new delivery service has been running for three months now, so how do customers feel about it compared with the other companies in the city? B: It has an average rating of four and a half stars out of five, which is higher than our competitors, although some people said the drivers sometimes arrive late.","t":"A：我們新的外送服務已經營運三個月了，跟市內其他公司相比，顧客覺得如何？ B：它的平均【評分】是五顆星中的四顆半，比我們的競爭對手高，不過有些人說司機有時候會遲到。"},{"w":"review","p":"n.","d":"a written opinion about how good a product or service is","c":"評論；評價","s":"A: Before we choose a caterer for the company's annual dinner, how can we know which one actually serves good food and arrives on time? B: Let's read what other customers wrote online, because one bad review might be unfair, but if many people complain about cold dishes, we should pick a different company.","t":"A：在替公司年度晚宴挑選外燴業者前，我們要怎麼知道哪一家真的餐點好吃又準時抵達？ B：我們來看看其他顧客在網路上寫了什麼，因為一則負面的【評論】可能不公平，但如果很多人抱怨菜是冷的，我們就該換一家公司。"},{"w":"category","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that are similar in some way","c":"類別；種類","s":"A: Our online shop sells hundreds of office products now, and customers say they can't find what they need quickly, so how can we make the website easier to use? B: We could put every item into a clear category, such as paper, furniture, or printers, so shoppers can click on one group and see only the products they want.","t":"A：我們的網路商店現在賣好幾百種辦公用品，顧客說他們沒辦法快速找到需要的東西，我們要怎麼讓網站更好用？ B：我們可以把每件商品放進清楚的【類別】，例如紙類、家具或印表機，讓購物者點一個分類就只看到想要的商品。"},{"w":"developer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that creates computer programs","c":"開發人員；開發商","s":"A: The hotel wants a new mobile program that lets guests check in and open their room doors with their phones, so who's going to build it for us? B: We've hired a software developer from a company in Hsinchu, and she'll meet our managers next week to discuss the design, the budget, and the schedule.","t":"A：飯店想要一個新的手機程式，讓房客能用手機辦理入住並打開房門，誰要幫我們做？ B：我們請了一位新竹公司的軟體【開發人員】，她下週會和我們的經理們見面，討論設計、預算和時程。"},{"w":"bug","p":"n.","d":"a mistake in a computer program that stops it working correctly","c":"程式錯誤；漏洞","s":"A: Several customers called this morning to say they were charged twice when they paid for their tickets online, so do we know what caused the problem? B: The technical team found a bug in the payment system that sent each order two times, and they're fixing it now and will return the extra money by Friday.","t":"A：今天早上有好幾位顧客打電話來說，他們在線上購票時被重複扣款，我們知道問題的原因嗎？ B：技術團隊在付款系統裡發現一個【程式錯誤】，會把每筆訂單送出兩次，他們正在修正，並會在週五前退還多收的錢。"},{"w":"crash","p":"v.","d":"(of a computer or program) to suddenly stop working","c":"當機；故障","s":"A: Why didn't you send me the sales presentation last night as you promised, when I needed to review it before this morning's meeting with the clients? B: I'm really sorry, but my laptop started to crash every time I opened the file, so I had to ask the IT team to repair it this morning.","t":"A：你為什麼沒有照答應的昨晚把業務簡報寄給我？我需要在今天早上和客戶開會前先看過。 B：真的很抱歉，但我的筆電每次打開那個檔案就【當機】，所以我今天早上只好請資訊團隊修理。"},{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"working well and not likely to fail or change suddenly","c":"穩定的","s":"A: Our online store had serious problems during the holiday sale last year, so are you confident the website will work well when thousands of shoppers visit at the same time? B: Yes, we moved to a stronger server in the summer, and the system has been very stable since then, without a single breakdown in four months.","t":"A：我們的網路商店去年假期特賣時出了嚴重的問題，你有把握網站在幾千名購物者同時上線時能正常運作嗎？ B：有，我們夏天換了一台更強的伺服器，從那以後系統一直很【穩定】，四個月來沒有故障過一次。"},{"w":"compatible","p":"adj.","d":"able to work together with another machine or system","c":"相容的","s":"A: I just bought a new tablet for my business trips, but will I be able to use our company's sales software on it while I'm visiting clients in Japan? B: You should check with the IT team first, because the program is only compatible with certain systems, and some older tablets can't run it at all.","t":"A：我剛為出差買了一台新平板，在日本拜訪客戶時能在上面使用公司的業務軟體嗎？ B：你應該先跟資訊團隊確認，因為那個程式只和特定系統【相容】，有些較舊的平板完全無法執行。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the right to keep your personal information secret","c":"隱私","s":"A: Some customers are worried about giving us their phone numbers and home addresses when they join our membership program, so what should our staff tell them? B: Explain that we protect their privacy carefully, and we never sell personal information to other companies, so their details are only used for deliveries and special offers.","t":"A：有些顧客在加入我們的會員計畫時，擔心要提供電話號碼和住家地址，我們的員工該怎麼跟他們說？ B：向他們說明我們會謹慎保護他們的【隱私】，而且絕不會把個人資料賣給其他公司，他們的資料只會用於送貨和特別優惠。"},{"w":"permission","p":"n.","d":"the right to do something that someone allows you to have","c":"權限；許可","s":"A: When I opened the new expense program on my phone, it asked whether it could use my camera, so is it safe to say yes? B: Yes, you should give it permission, because the program needs the camera to take photos of your receipts, and then it sends them straight to the accounting department.","t":"A：我在手機上打開新的報帳程式時，它問我能不能使用相機，答應安全嗎？ B：安全，你應該給它【權限】，因為程式需要用相機拍你的收據，然後直接傳給會計部。"},{"w":"notification","p":"n.","d":"a short message on a phone or computer that tells you about something new","c":"通知","s":"A: I missed the urgent meeting about the client's complaint yesterday because nobody told me it had moved to two o'clock, so how can I avoid that next time? B: Turn on the calendar alerts on your phone, and you'll get a notification every time a meeting is changed or canceled, even when you're away from your desk.","t":"A：昨天我錯過了關於客戶投訴的緊急會議，因為沒有人告訴我會議改到兩點，下次要怎麼避免？ B：打開手機上的行事曆提醒，這樣每次會議變更或取消時，就算你不在座位上也會收到【通知】。"},{"w":"launch","p":"v.","d":"to make a new product available to the public for the first time","c":"推出；發表","s":"A: The marketing team has been working on the new ordering program for almost a year, so when will customers finally be able to use it? B: We plan to launch it at the trade show in March, and we'll offer a ten percent discount to everyone who places an order with it during the first week.","t":"A：行銷團隊已經為新的訂購程式努力了將近一年，顧客到底什麼時候才能使用？ B：我們打算在三月的商展上【推出】它，並在第一週給所有用它下單的人九折優惠。"},{"w":"browse","p":"v.","d":"to look at things casually, especially on the internet","c":"瀏覽","s":"A: I don't know what to buy for my manager's farewell gift, and I don't have time to visit the department store after work this week, so do you have any suggestions? B: You could browse a few online gift shops during your lunch break, because many of them have useful ideas and can deliver to the office by Friday.","t":"A：我不知道該買什麼當經理的歡送禮物，而且這週下班後也沒時間去百貨公司，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：你可以在午休時【瀏覽】幾家網路禮品店，因為很多家都有不錯的點子，而且能在週五前送到辦公室。"},{"w":"search","p":"v.","d":"to look carefully for something, often by typing words into a computer","c":"搜尋；查找","s":"A: The customer called again about the missing order, but I can't find her name anywhere in this long list of deliveries, so what should I do? B: Don't read the whole list line by line, but search the database for her order number instead, which will show you the delivery details in a few seconds.","t":"A：那位顧客又打電話來詢問遺失的訂單，但我在這份很長的送貨清單裡怎麼都找不到她的名字，我該怎麼辦？ B：別一行一行看整份清單，改用她的訂單編號【搜尋】資料庫，幾秒鐘就會顯示送貨細節。"},{"w":"optimize","p":"v.","d":"to make something work as well or as quickly as possible","c":"最佳化；優化","s":"A: Our website takes almost ten seconds to open on mobile phones, and the sales manager thinks many shoppers leave before they see any products, so what can we do? B: The developers can optimize the photos and the code so the pages load faster, which should keep more visitors on the site and increase our sales.","t":"A：我們的網站在手機上要將近十秒才打開，業務經理認為很多購物者還沒看到商品就離開了，我們能怎麼做？ B：開發人員可以【優化】照片和程式碼讓網頁載入更快，這應該能留住更多訪客並提高我們的銷售額。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"in a safe way that protects something from being stolen or seen","c":"安全地","s":"A: I need to send the new employees' salary details to the accountant at our Kaohsiung office today, so can I just attach the file to a normal email? B: No, please upload it securely through the company's protected file system, because personal information like that must never be sent in an ordinary message.","t":"A：我今天需要把新進員工的薪資資料寄給高雄辦公室的會計師，我可以直接把檔案附在一般的電子郵件裡嗎？ B：不行，請透過公司受保護的檔案系統【安全地】上傳，因為那類個人資料絕不能用一般訊息寄送。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"Application Letter 求職信","cards":[{"w":"position","p":"n.","d":"a job in a company","c":"職位；職缺","s":"A: I saw on the company website that the marketing department is hiring again this month, so do you know what kind of person they are looking for? B: Yes, the position is for a sales assistant who can speak English and Japanese, and they want someone who can start working in early March.","t":"A：我在公司網站上看到行銷部這個月又在徵人，你知道他們在找什麼樣的人嗎？ B：知道，這個【職位】是業務助理，要會說英文和日文，而且他們希望對方能在三月初開始上班。"},{"w":"vacancy","p":"n.","d":"a job that is open and needs someone to fill it","c":"職缺；空缺","s":"A: Our receptionist is moving to Kaohsiung next month, and the front desk will be very busy without her, so what should we do now? B: I will ask the human resources office to post the vacancy online today, so we can start interviewing new people before she leaves the company.","t":"A：我們的櫃台接待員下個月要搬去高雄，沒有她櫃台會非常忙，我們現在該怎麼辦？ B：我會請人資部今天就把這個【職缺】公告在網路上，這樣我們就能在她離職前開始面試新人。"},{"w":"candidate","p":"n.","d":"a person who is being considered for a job","c":"候選人；應徵者","s":"A: We have interviewed six people for the office manager job this week, and all of them seemed friendly and well prepared, so who do you think we should choose? B: In my opinion, the best candidate is Ms. Chen, because she has managed a busy office before and she answered every question clearly.","t":"A：這週我們為辦公室經理一職面試了六個人，他們看起來都很友善也準備充分，你覺得我們該選誰？ B：我認為最好的【候選人】是陳小姐，因為她以前管理過忙碌的辦公室，而且每個問題都回答得很清楚。"},{"w":"applicant","p":"n.","d":"a person who formally asks for a job","c":"申請人；求職者","s":"A: The deadline for the designer job closed yesterday, and my inbox is completely full of emails from people who want the job, so how many did we receive? B: We got more than eighty letters, so each applicant will first take a short online test before we invite the top ten for an interview.","t":"A：設計師職缺的截止日是昨天，我的收件匣塞滿了想要這份工作的人寄來的信，我們總共收到多少封？ B：我們收到八十多封信，所以每位【求職者】都會先做一個簡短的線上測驗，之後我們再邀請前十名來面試。"},{"w":"employer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays people to work for them","c":"雇主","s":"A: I am writing my first job letter, and I am not sure whether I should talk about my part-time job at the coffee shop, so what do you think? B: You should mention it, because any future employer will be glad to know that you served customers politely and handled money carefully during busy weekends.","t":"A：我正在寫我的第一封求職信，不確定該不該提到我在咖啡店的兼職工作，你覺得呢？ B：你應該提，因為任何未來的【雇主】都會很高興知道你在忙碌的週末能禮貌地服務顧客並謹慎處理金錢。"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an official record, like a degree, showing you have finished training","c":"資格；學歷證明","s":"A: The job advertisement says the company wants an accountant, but I studied business, not accounting, at university, so should I still send my letter? B: You can try, but they will probably ask for a professional qualification, so you might need to finish an accounting course first and then apply next year.","t":"A：這則徵才廣告說公司要找會計人員，但我大學念的是商業而不是會計，我還要寄求職信嗎？ B：你可以試試看，不過他們可能會要求專業【資格】，所以你也許需要先完成會計課程，明年再申請。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or skill you get from doing a job for some time","c":"經驗","s":"A: This hotel is looking for a front desk supervisor, and I have worked at a hotel reception for five years, so how should I start my letter? B: Start by explaining your experience at the reception desk, because the manager will want to know that you have already handled guests, bookings, and complaints for many years.","t":"A：這家飯店在找櫃台主管，而我在飯店櫃台工作了五年，我的求職信該怎麼開頭？ B：先說明你在櫃台的【經驗】，因為經理會想知道你多年來已經處理過客人、訂房和客訴。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something well because you have practiced it","c":"技能；技巧","s":"A: The new travel agency needs someone who can answer calls from foreign tourists, so is it a good idea to say that I speak three languages? B: Of course, because language is a very useful skill in that kind of job, and you should also mention that you can use booking software quickly.","t":"A：那家新的旅行社需要能接聽外國觀光客電話的人，在信裡說我會說三種語言是好主意嗎？ B：當然，因為語言在那種工作中是非常有用的【技能】，而且你也應該提到你能快速使用訂位軟體。"},{"w":"ability","p":"n.","d":"the power or talent to do something","c":"能力","s":"A: The manager of the call center told me she needs a new team leader before the busy holiday season, so what is the most important thing for her? B: She told me she wants someone with the ability to stay calm under pressure, because the team often handles hundreds of angry calls on a single day.","t":"A：客服中心經理告訴我，她需要在忙碌的假期旺季前找到新的組長，對她來說最重要的是什麼？ B：她跟我說她想找一個有【能力】在壓力下保持冷靜的人，因為這個團隊常常一天就要處理好幾百通憤怒的電話。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"a good quality or skill that someone has","c":"優點；長處","s":"A: In the interview tomorrow, they will probably ask me to describe myself, and I always get nervous about that question, so how should I answer it? B: Talk about one real strength, such as your careful planning, and then give an example of a project where your planning helped your team finish early.","t":"A：明天面試他們可能會要我描述自己，我每次遇到這個問題都很緊張，我該怎麼回答？ B：談一個真實的【優點】，例如你做事規劃仔細，然後舉一個你的規劃幫助團隊提早完成的專案例子。"},{"w":"education","p":"n.","d":"the learning you get at school, college, or university","c":"教育；學歷","s":"A: I finished high school in Tainan and then studied hotel management at a college in Taipei for four years, so where should I put this information? B: Put it in a short education section under your work history, and list the name of each school, your main subject, and the year you finished.","t":"A：我在台南念完高中，之後在台北一所學院念了四年的飯店管理，這些資料該放在哪裡？ B：把它放在你工作經歷下面一個簡短的【學歷】欄位，列出每所學校的名稱、你的主修科目和畢業年份。"},{"w":"degree","p":"n.","d":"the title a university gives you when you finish your studies","c":"學位","s":"A: This engineering company only hires people who have finished university, and I will graduate this June, so can I apply for the job now? B: Yes, you can, but you should explain in your letter that you will receive your degree in June, and that you can start working right after that.","t":"A：這家工程公司只錄用大學畢業的人，而我今年六月才畢業，我現在可以應徵嗎？ B：可以，但你應該在信中說明你會在六月拿到【學位】，而且之後就能馬上開始上班。"},{"w":"certificate","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that shows you have passed a test or finished a course","c":"證書；證照","s":"A: The job post says that all tour guides must pass the national guide test, and I passed it last spring, so how can I show that to them? B: You should scan your certificate and include it with your email, so the manager can see your test result and the date immediately.","t":"A：這則職缺公告說所有導遊都必須通過國家導遊考試，而我去年春天考過了，我要怎麼向他們證明？ B：你應該把你的【證書】掃描起來，隨電子郵件一起寄出，這樣經理就能馬上看到你的考試結果和日期。"},{"w":"resume","p":"n.","d":"a short document listing your education and work history","c":"履歷","s":"A: My cousin wants to apply for a job at a bank, and she has only written a cover letter, so what else does she need to send? B: She also needs a one-page resume that shows her education, past jobs, and skills, because banks usually check that document before they read anything else.","t":"A：我表妹想應徵銀行的工作，她只寫了一封求職信，她還需要寄什麼？ B：她還需要一份一頁的【履歷】，列出她的學歷、過去的工作和技能，因為銀行通常會先看那份文件再看其他東西。"},{"w":"CV","p":"n.","d":"a document listing your education, work, and skills (curriculum vitae)","c":"履歷（CV）","s":"A: The British company I am applying to asked for a detailed list of my studies, research, and work history, so is that different from a normal job letter? B: Yes, that is your CV, and in the UK it is often two pages long, so you can include your research projects and conference talks there.","t":"A：我要應徵的那家英國公司要求一份詳細列出我的學業、研究和工作經歷的清單，這和一般的求職信不一樣嗎？ B：對，那是你的【履歷（CV）】，在英國通常有兩頁長，所以你可以把你的研究計畫和研討會發表都列在裡面。"},{"w":"attach","p":"v.","d":"to add a file to an email","c":"附加（檔案）","s":"A: I have finished my letter for the assistant manager job, and I am ready to send the email to the hotel, but what about my resume and photo? B: Before you click send, please attach both files and check that they open correctly, because many managers will not read an email without them.","t":"A：我已經寫好應徵副理職位的信，準備把電子郵件寄給飯店了，那我的履歷和照片呢？ B：按下寄出之前，請把兩個檔案都【附加】上去並確認能正常開啟，因為很多經理不會看缺少這些檔案的郵件。"},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"a person who can tell an employer about your work and character","c":"推薦人；介紹人","s":"A: The company has asked me for the name of someone who can talk about my work, and I am not sure who I should choose, so can you help? B: Your old supervisor at the bookstore would be a good reference, because she worked with you for three years and knows how hard you work.","t":"A：公司要我提供一個能談論我工作表現的人，我不確定該選誰，你能幫忙嗎？ B：你以前在書店的主管會是很好的【推薦人】，因為她和你共事了三年，知道你工作多努力。"},{"w":"recommendation","p":"n.","d":"a statement that someone is good for a job","c":"推薦；推薦信","s":"A: I am applying for a teaching job at an international school, and they want a letter from someone who has seen me teach, so who should I ask? B: Ask the head teacher at your current school for a recommendation, because a letter from a senior teacher will make your application much stronger.","t":"A：我正在應徵一所國際學校的教職，他們要一封看過我教學的人寫的信，我該找誰？ B：請你目前學校的主任幫你寫一封【推薦信】，因為資深老師寫的信會讓你的申請更有說服力。"},{"w":"interest","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of wanting to know about or do something","c":"興趣；關注","s":"A: I really want to work for this green energy company, but I do not have much experience yet, so what should I say in the first paragraph? B: Explain your strong interest in solar power, and mention the volunteer project where you helped install solar panels at a school last summer.","t":"A：我真的很想在這家綠能公司工作，但我還沒有太多經驗，第一段該寫什麼？ B：說明你對太陽能有濃厚的【興趣】，並提到去年夏天你在一所學校幫忙安裝太陽能板的志工計畫。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of excitement and interest","c":"熱情的；熱衷的","s":"A: My letter lists all my skills, but my friend said it sounds a little cold and boring, so how can I make it sound more friendly and positive? B: Add a sentence saying you are enthusiastic about the chance to work with their team, and explain why their products really excite you.","t":"A：我的信列出了我所有的技能，但我朋友說聽起來有點冷淡又無聊，我要怎麼讓它聽起來更友善、更正面？ B：加一句話說你對能和他們團隊共事的機會感到很【熱衷】，並說明為什麼他們的產品真的讓你很興奮。"},{"w":"motivated","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to do something and willing to work hard for it","c":"有動力的；積極的","s":"A: Our sales team lost two people last month, and the new targets for next year are much higher, so what kind of person should we hire now? B: We need a highly motivated person who wants to meet targets, who does not give up easily, and who is happy to visit customers every day.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊上個月走了兩個人，而明年的新目標高很多，我們現在該聘請什麼樣的人？ B：我們需要一個非常【積極】的人，想要達成目標、不輕易放棄，而且樂意每天拜訪客戶。"},{"w":"responsible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted to do the right thing","c":"負責任的；可靠的","s":"A: The restaurant manager is going on vacation next month and needs someone to open the shop and count the money every morning, so who should do it? B: I think Kevin is the most responsible worker here, because he always arrives early, locks the doors carefully, and never makes mistakes with the cash.","t":"A：餐廳經理下個月要去度假，需要有人每天早上開店並清點現金，該由誰來做？ B：我覺得凱文是這裡最【負責任】的員工，因為他總是早到、仔細鎖門，而且處理現金從不出錯。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted to do something well every time","c":"可靠的；可信賴的","s":"A: I want to show the shipping company that I can be trusted, but I have only had one job, so what is a good example to use in my letter? B: Write that you were a reliable driver at the bakery for two years, and that you delivered every order on time, even during typhoons.","t":"A：我想向那家貨運公司證明我值得信任，但我只做過一份工作，信裡用什麼例子比較好？ B：寫你在麵包店當了兩年【可靠】的司機，每一張訂單都準時送達，連颱風天也一樣。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"showing the skills and polite manner expected at work","c":"專業的","s":"A: I usually write emails to my friends in a very casual way, with lots of short words and emojis, so is that fine for my job letter? B: No, you should use a more professional style, with complete sentences, a polite greeting, and a clear closing, because the manager will judge you by your writing.","t":"A：我平常寫信給朋友都很隨性，用很多簡短的字和表情符號，這種寫法用在求職信可以嗎？ B：不行，你應該用比較【專業】的風格，句子要完整、問候要禮貌、結尾要清楚，因為經理會從你的文字來評斷你。"},{"w":"teamwork","p":"n.","d":"working well together with other people","c":"團隊合作","s":"A: The job post says the company builds websites in small groups of four or five people, so what should I write about my last job? B: Describe how you planned the company trade show with three coworkers, because that example shows your teamwork and your ability to share tasks fairly.","t":"A：這則職缺公告說那家公司以四、五個人的小組來架設網站，我該怎麼寫我上一份工作？ B：描述你和三位同事一起籌劃公司商展的經過，因為這個例子展現你的【團隊合作】以及公平分工的能力。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the sharing of information with other people","c":"溝通","s":"A: This customer service job means talking to clients on the phone and writing emails all day, so what should I show them in my letter? B: Show them your strong communication skills, for example by explaining how you answered more than fifty customer questions a day in your last job.","t":"A：這份客服工作就是整天和客戶講電話、寫電子郵件，我該在信中向他們展現什麼？ B：展現你很強的【溝通】能力，例如說明你在上一份工作中一天回答超過五十個客戶的問題。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something good","c":"機會","s":"A: I just finished my letter for the internship at the airline, and I want my last sentence to sound polite and thankful, so what can I write? B: You could write that you would welcome the opportunity to meet them in person, and that you hope to hear from them soon.","t":"A：我剛寫完應徵航空公司實習的信，希望最後一句聽起來有禮貌又帶著感謝，我可以怎麼寫？ B：你可以寫你很希望有【機會】和他們當面見面，並希望很快收到他們的消息。"},{"w":"career","p":"n.","d":"the jobs you do in your working life","c":"職涯；事業","s":"A: I have worked as a bank teller for three years, but now I want to move into marketing, so how can I explain this change in my letter? B: Explain that you want to build a long-term career in marketing, and show how your customer service at the bank taught you what clients really need.","t":"A：我當了三年的銀行櫃員，但現在想轉往行銷，我要怎麼在信中解釋這個轉變？ B：說明你想在行銷領域建立長期的【職涯】，並說明你在銀行的客服經驗如何讓你了解客戶真正的需求。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give your ideas, time, or work to help something succeed","c":"貢獻","s":"A: The manager asked in the advertisement what new people can bring to the team, but I am not sure how to answer that, so do you have any ideas? B: Write that you can contribute your experience with social media, since their online sales are growing and they will need someone to manage their accounts.","t":"A：經理在廣告中問新人能為團隊帶來什麼，但我不確定該怎麼回答，你有什麼想法嗎？ B：寫你能【貢獻】你的社群媒體經驗，因為他們的網路銷售正在成長，會需要有人管理他們的帳號。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to make something grow or become better","c":"發展；培養","s":"A: Why do you want to leave your job at the small shop and work for a large international company, even though you would earn almost the same salary? B: I want to develop my management skills, and a big company offers training courses and chances to lead larger teams in different countries.","t":"A：雖然薪水幾乎一樣，你為什麼想離開小店的工作，去大型國際公司上班？ B：我想【培養】我的管理能力，而大公司會提供培訓課程，也有機會在不同國家帶領更大的團隊。"},{"w":"learn","p":"v.","d":"to get knowledge or a skill by studying or practicing","c":"學習","s":"A: I have never used the design software that this company uses, and I am worried that they will not hire me because of it, so what should I say? B: Tell them honestly that you are ready to learn new programs quickly, and mention that you taught yourself video editing in only two months.","t":"A：我從來沒用過這家公司使用的設計軟體，我擔心他們會因此不錄用我，我該怎麼說？ B：老實告訴他們你準備好快速【學習】新程式，並提到你只花兩個月就自學會了影片剪輯。"},{"w":"grow","p":"v.","d":"to become bigger, better, or more skilled","c":"成長","s":"A: The last question on the application form asks where I see myself in five years, and I do not want to sound too proud, so how should I answer? B: Say that you hope to grow with the company, take on more responsibility, and maybe lead a small team after a few years of hard work.","t":"A：申請表上最後一個問題問我五年後的自己在哪裡，我不想聽起來太驕傲，該怎麼回答？ B：說你希望能和公司一起【成長】，承擔更多責任，經過幾年努力後也許能帶領一個小團隊。"},{"w":"suitable","p":"adj.","d":"right or good for a particular job or purpose","c":"合適的；適合的","s":"A: We received a letter from a young man who has a law degree, but this job is for a graphic designer, so should we call him for an interview? B: I do not think he is suitable for this job, but we can keep his letter, because our legal department may need an assistant next year.","t":"A：我們收到一位擁有法律學位的年輕人的信，但這個職缺是平面設計師，我們該打電話請他來面試嗎？ B：我不認為他【適合】這份工作，但我們可以留著他的信，因為我們的法務部明年可能需要助理。"},{"w":"qualified","p":"adj.","d":"having the right training or exams for a job","c":"合格的；具備資格的","s":"A: The hospital needs a new nurse for the night shift, and three people have applied this week, so can all of them start working right away? B: Only two of them are fully qualified, because the third person has not passed the national nursing exam yet and cannot work alone at night.","t":"A：醫院需要一位新的夜班護理師，這週有三個人應徵，他們都能馬上開始上班嗎？ B：只有兩位完全【具備資格】，因為第三位還沒通過國家護理考試，不能獨自值夜班。"},{"w":"available","p":"adj.","d":"free to do something, such as start a job or meet someone","c":"有空的；可到職的","s":"A: The manager wants to know when I can come in for the interview, but I am still working at my old job during the day, so what should I say? B: Tell her you are available on weekday evenings after six o'clock or any time on Saturday, and ask which time is best for her.","t":"A：經理想知道我什麼時候能來面試，但我白天還在原本的公司上班，我該怎麼說？ B：告訴她你平日晚上六點以後或星期六任何時間都【有空】，並問她哪個時間最方便。"},{"w":"interview","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting where someone asks you questions to decide if you get a job","c":"面試","s":"A: I just received an email from the hotel saying they liked my letter and my resume, so what is the next step in their hiring process? B: They will probably invite you to an interview next week, so you should prepare answers about your experience and practice speaking clearly in English.","t":"A：我剛收到飯店的電子郵件，說他們喜歡我的信和履歷，他們招聘流程的下一步是什麼？ B：他們下週可能會邀請你去【面試】，所以你應該準備好關於你經驗的回答，並練習清楚地用英文表達。"},{"w":"discuss","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something with someone","c":"討論","s":"A: How should I end my letter so the manager feels that I really want to meet her, without sounding too pushy or impatient? B: Write that you would be happy to discuss your experience and ideas in more detail at a meeting, and give your phone number so she can call you easily.","t":"A：我的信該怎麼結尾，才能讓經理覺得我真的想見她，又不會顯得太強勢或沒耐心？ B：寫你很樂意在會面時更詳細地【討論】你的經驗和想法，並附上你的電話號碼，讓她方便打給你。"},{"w":"consider","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something before deciding","c":"考慮","s":"A: I think my letter is almost ready, but the closing sentence feels too short, so what polite words can I use to thank the company? B: You can write \"Thank you for taking the time to consider my application,\" because it is polite and shows that you respect the manager's busy schedule.","t":"A：我覺得我的信快寫好了，但結尾那句感覺太短，我可以用什麼禮貌的話來感謝公司？ B：你可以寫「感謝您撥冗【考慮】我的申請」，因為這句話很有禮貌，也顯示你尊重經理忙碌的行程。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be thankful for something","c":"感謝；感激","s":"A: The manager of the design studio replied to my letter within one day and gave me some helpful advice about my portfolio, so should I write back? B: Yes, write a short email saying you really appreciate her quick reply and her advice, and tell her you will send the new portfolio by Friday.","t":"A：設計工作室的經理一天內就回了我的信，還給我一些關於作品集的有用建議，我該回信嗎？ B：要，寫一封簡短的電子郵件說你很【感謝】她迅速回覆和她的建議，並告訴她你會在星期五前寄出新的作品集。"},{"w":"response","p":"n.","d":"an answer to a letter, email, or question","c":"回覆；回應","s":"A: I sent my letter to the trading company two weeks ago, and nobody has called or emailed me since then, so is it rude to contact them again? B: It is not rude at all, so send a polite email asking about your application, because a quick response is not always possible when they have many applicants.","t":"A：我兩週前把信寄給那家貿易公司，到現在都沒人打電話或寄信給我，再聯絡他們會不禮貌嗎？ B：一點也不會，寄一封有禮貌的信詢問你的申請狀況吧，因為應徵者很多時，他們不一定能很快【回覆】。"},{"w":"contact","p":"v.","d":"to call, email, or write to someone","c":"聯絡","s":"A: At the end of my letter, I want the manager to know how she can reach me quickly if she wants to set up a meeting, so what should I write? B: Write \"Please contact me at 0912-345-678 or by email at any time,\" and make sure the number and the address are correct.","t":"A：在信的最後，我想讓經理知道如果她想安排面談，要怎樣快速找到我，我該寫什麼？ B：寫「歡迎隨時撥打0912-345-678或以電子郵件與我【聯絡】」，並確認電話號碼和地址正確無誤。"},{"w":"soon","p":"adv.","d":"in a short time from now","c":"很快；不久","s":"A: My letter is finished, but my teacher says the last line should sound hopeful and friendly, not like a demand, so how should I end it? B: You can write \"I look forward to hearing from you soon,\" because almost every business letter in English uses this kind of hopeful closing sentence.","t":"A：我的信寫完了，但老師說最後一句應該聽起來充滿期待又友善，而不是像在要求，我該怎麼結尾？ B：你可以寫「期待【很快】收到您的消息」，因為幾乎每一封英文商業書信都會用這種帶著期待的結尾句。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"used before your name at the end of a formal letter","c":"敬上（正式信件結尾用語）","s":"A: I started my letter with \"Dear Ms. Wang\" because I know the manager's name from the website, so which closing phrase should I write before my name? B: Since you know her name, you should write \"Yours sincerely,\" which is the most common polite ending for formal business letters in English.","t":"A：我的信是以「親愛的王小姐」開頭，因為我從網站上知道經理的名字，在我的名字前該用哪個結尾語？ B：既然你知道她的名字，就應該寫「Yours 【sincerely（謹啟）】」，這是英文正式商業書信最常見的禮貌結尾。"},{"w":"faithfully","p":"adv.","d":"used at the end of a formal British letter when you do not know the person's name","c":"敬上（英式正式信件，不知收件人姓名時用）","s":"A: The British company did not give the name of the hiring manager, so I started my letter with \"Dear Sir or Madam,\" and now I need an ending. B: In British English, when you do not know the person's name, you should finish with \"Yours faithfully,\" and then sign your full name below it.","t":"A：那家英國公司沒有提供招聘經理的姓名，所以我的信以「敬啟者」開頭，現在我需要一個結尾。 B：在英式英文中，當你不知道對方姓名時，應該以「Yours 【faithfully（謹上）】」結尾，然後在下方簽上你的全名。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"Appointment 預約","cards":[{"w":"schedule","p":"v.","d":"to plan something for a certain time","c":"安排（時間）；排定","s":"A: The new client from Tokyo wants to visit our factory and see the production line next week, so what should I do first? B: Please schedule a visit for Tuesday morning, because the machines run all day then, and send him the address and a map before the weekend.","t":"A：東京來的新客戶下週想來參觀我們的工廠和生產線，我該先做什麼？ B：請把參觀【安排】在星期二早上，因為那天機器整天運轉，並在週末前把地址和地圖寄給他。"},{"w":"booking","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to have a seat, room, or service at a certain time","c":"預訂；預約","s":"A: Our team dinner for the sales award is on Friday night, and that Italian restaurant is always full on weekends, so did anyone call them? B: Yes, I made a booking for twelve people at seven o'clock, and the restaurant also promised to give us a private room in the back.","t":"A：我們慶祝業績獎的團隊晚餐在星期五晚上，那家義大利餐廳週末總是客滿，有人打電話給他們了嗎？ B：有，我做了七點十二個人的【預訂】，餐廳還答應給我們後面的一間包廂。"},{"w":"reserve","p":"v.","d":"to ask for a room, seat, or table to be kept for you","c":"預訂；保留","s":"A: More than forty people from different branches will come to the training day next month, and our meeting rooms are too small, so where can we hold it? B: I will reserve the large conference hall at the hotel across the street, because it has a projector, good sound, and enough chairs for everyone.","t":"A：下個月有四十多位來自不同分公司的人要來參加訓練日，我們的會議室太小了，可以在哪裡舉辦？ B：我會【預訂】對街飯店的大型會議廳，因為那裡有投影機、良好的音響，也有足夠的椅子給每個人。"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to keep a room, table, or ticket for someone","c":"預約；訂位","s":"A: I arrived at the hotel in Singapore after a long flight, but the front desk says they cannot find my name in their system, so what can I do? B: Show them the email with your reservation number, and if they still have a problem, call our travel agent, who booked the room for you last month.","t":"A：我長途飛行後抵達新加坡的飯店，但櫃台說系統裡找不到我的名字，我該怎麼辦？ B：給他們看有你【訂房】編號的電子郵件，如果還有問題，就打給上個月幫你訂房的旅行社人員。"},{"w":"meeting","p":"n.","d":"an event where people come together to discuss something","c":"會議","s":"A: The marketing manager wants to talk with everyone about the new product launch, but half of the team works from home on Mondays, so when should we do it? B: Let's hold the meeting on Wednesday afternoon in Room 5, and we can also share a video link for anyone who cannot come in person.","t":"A：行銷經理想跟大家談新產品上市的事，但星期一有一半的團隊在家工作，我們該什麼時候進行？ B：我們星期三下午在五號會議室開【會議】吧，也可以分享視訊連結給無法親自出席的人。"},{"w":"consultation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting to get advice from an expert","c":"諮詢；諮商","s":"A: Our company wants to open a store in Japan next year, but none of us understand the local tax rules very well, so who can help us? B: I have booked a consultation with a tax expert in Osaka next Thursday, and she will explain the rules and the forms we need to prepare.","t":"A：我們公司明年想在日本開店，但我們沒有人很了解當地的稅務規定，誰能幫我們？ B：我已經預約了下週四和大阪一位稅務專家的【諮詢】，她會說明相關規定和我們需要準備的表格。"},{"w":"interview","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting where someone is asked questions, for example for a job","c":"面試","s":"A: The human resources office called me this morning about the assistant job I applied for last week, and they sounded very friendly, so what did they say? B: They invited me to an interview at ten o'clock on Monday, and they asked me to bring my diploma and two copies of my resume.","t":"A：人資部今天早上打電話給我，談我上週應徵的助理工作，他們聽起來很友善，他們說了什麼？ B：他們邀請我星期一十點去【面試】，還要我帶畢業證書和兩份履歷影本。"},{"w":"session","p":"n.","d":"a period of time used for a particular activity","c":"（一段）時間；場次","s":"A: The new accounting software is quite difficult, and many staff members have asked for help using it, so how are we going to train everyone? B: We will hold a two-hour training session every Friday afternoon this month, and each person can choose the week that fits their work schedule best.","t":"A：新的會計軟體相當難用，很多員工都要求協助，我們要怎麼訓練每個人？ B：這個月每週五下午我們會舉辦兩小時的訓練【場次】，每個人可以選擇最符合自己工作時間的那一週。"},{"w":"time slot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short period of time that is kept for one appointment or activity","c":"時段","s":"A: I need to see the eye doctor before my business trip next week, but the clinic's website says almost every day is full, so is there any chance? B: There is only one free time slot left on Thursday at 4:30, so you should book it online right now before someone else takes it.","t":"A：我下週出差前需要看眼科醫生，但診所網站說幾乎每天都額滿了，還有機會嗎？ B：星期四四點半只剩下一個空的【時段】，你應該現在就上網預約，免得被別人搶走。"},{"w":"availability","p":"n.","d":"the times when someone is free to meet or do something","c":"有空的時間；可用性","s":"A: The director wants to meet all five department heads before the budget is finished, but they all have very different schedules, so how can we find a time? B: I will send everyone an online form today to check their availability for next week, and then I will choose the time that works for most people.","t":"A：主任想在預算定案前和五位部門主管見面，但他們的行程都很不一樣，我們要怎麼找到時間？ B：我今天會寄一份線上表單給每個人，確認他們下週【有空的時間】，然後選一個大多數人都可以的時間。"},{"w":"calendar","p":"n.","d":"a list of dates or a digital tool showing your plans and appointments","c":"行事曆","s":"A: I keep forgetting my meetings with clients because I write them on small pieces of paper that I often lose, so do you have any advice? B: Put every appointment in the shared online calendar, because it sends you alerts on your phone and your assistant can see your plans too.","t":"A：我老是忘記和客戶的會面，因為我把它們寫在常常弄丟的小紙條上，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：把每個約會都記在共用的線上【行事曆】，因為它會在你手機上發出提醒，你的助理也能看到你的安排。"},{"w":"confirm","p":"v.","d":"to say or show that something is definite or correct","c":"確認","s":"A: The visitors from the German supplier are flying in on Sunday night, and they plan to come to our office on Monday, but I am not sure about the time. B: Please call their assistant this afternoon to confirm the meeting time, so we can prepare the room and order lunch for everyone.","t":"A：德國供應商的訪客星期天晚上搭機抵達，他們打算星期一來我們辦公室，但我不確定時間。 B：請你今天下午打電話給他們的助理【確認】會議時間，這樣我們才能準備會議室並幫大家訂午餐。"},{"w":"confirmation","p":"n.","d":"a message or document that says something is definite","c":"確認（函）","s":"A: I booked the train tickets for our trip to the trade show in Taichung online last night, but I have not received anything yet, so is something wrong? B: Check your spam folder, because the website usually sends a confirmation email within ten minutes, and you will need its code to pick up the tickets.","t":"A：我昨晚在網路上訂了去台中參加商展的火車票，但到現在什麼都還沒收到，是出了什麼問題嗎？ B：檢查一下你的垃圾郵件匣，因為網站通常會在十分鐘內寄出【確認】信，你取票時需要信裡的代碼。"},{"w":"reminder","p":"n.","d":"a message that helps you remember something","c":"提醒（通知）","s":"A: Many patients forget their appointments at our clinic, and the doctors end up waiting with nothing to do, so how can we fix this problem? B: We can send each patient a text reminder one day before the visit, and they can reply to it if they need to change the time.","t":"A：我們診所很多病人忘記約診，醫生最後只能空等，我們要怎麼解決這個問題？ B：我們可以在看診前一天傳簡訊【提醒】每位病人，如果他們需要改時間也可以直接回覆。"},{"w":"reschedule","p":"v.","d":"to change the time or date of a planned event","c":"改期；重新安排時間","s":"A: My flight back from Hong Kong was delayed, so I will not be in the office on Thursday, but I have a meeting with the bank that morning. B: Then you should call the bank today and reschedule the meeting for Friday or next Monday, because they need you to sign the loan papers in person.","t":"A：我從香港回來的班機延誤了，所以星期四不會進辦公室，但那天早上我和銀行有會議。 B：那你今天應該打電話給銀行，把會議【改期】到星期五或下週一，因為他們需要你親自簽貸款文件。"},{"w":"postpone","p":"v.","d":"to move an event to a later time","c":"延後；延期","s":"A: A strong typhoon is expected to hit northern Taiwan on Saturday, and our company picnic is planned for that day in the park, so what should we do? B: We should postpone the picnic until the following weekend, and I will send an email to all staff members this afternoon to let them know.","t":"A：預計星期六會有強烈颱風侵襲北台灣，而我們的公司野餐就安排在那天在公園舉行，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該把野餐【延後】到下個週末，我今天下午會寄電子郵件通知所有員工。"},{"w":"cancel","p":"v.","d":"to say that a planned event will not happen","c":"取消","s":"A: The client from Seoul just emailed to say she is sick and cannot travel this week, but we booked a hotel room and a car for her. B: Please cancel the hotel room and the car service right away, because we can still get our money back if we tell them before noon today.","t":"A：首爾的客戶剛寄信說她生病了，這週不能出差，但我們已經幫她訂了飯店房間和車子。 B：請馬上【取消】飯店房間和派車服務，因為如果我們今天中午前通知，還能拿回退款。"},{"w":"cancellation","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping a planned event or order","c":"取消","s":"A: Our hotel has many guests who book rooms and then simply do not arrive, which costs us a lot of money during the busy season, so what can we do? B: We could charge a cancellation fee of fifty percent if guests do not tell us at least two days before their arrival date.","t":"A：我們飯店有很多客人訂了房卻沒來，在旺季讓我們損失很多錢，我們能怎麼做？ B：如果客人沒有在入住日前至少兩天告知我們，我們可以收取百分之五十的【取消】費用。"},{"w":"delay","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen later than planned","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: The heavy rain this morning has caused terrible traffic on the highway, and the delivery truck is still stuck near Taoyuan, so will the client meeting still start on time? B: I think we must delay the start of the meeting by thirty minutes, because the samples we want to show the client are on that truck.","t":"A：今天早上的大雨造成高速公路嚴重塞車，送貨卡車還卡在桃園附近，客戶會議還能準時開始嗎？ B：我想我們必須把會議開始時間【延後】三十分鐘，因為我們要給客戶看的樣品就在那輛卡車上。"},{"w":"punctual","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or doing something at the right time, not late","c":"準時的；守時的","s":"A: Our new client from Switzerland is coming at nine o'clock tomorrow, and I heard that people in her company care a lot about time, so is that true? B: Yes, she is always very punctual, so please be in the lobby by 8:50, and make sure the meeting room is ready before she arrives.","t":"A：我們瑞士的新客戶明天九點要來，我聽說她公司的人很重視時間，是真的嗎？ B：是的，她總是非常【守時】，所以請你八點五十分前到大廳，並確保她到達前會議室已經準備好。"},{"w":"late","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or happening after the expected time","c":"遲到的；晚的","s":"A: I am stuck in a long line of cars because of an accident on the bridge, and my appointment with the lawyer starts in ten minutes, so what should I do? B: Call her office now and tell them you will be about twenty minutes late, because it is polite to let people know before the meeting begins.","t":"A：因為橋上發生車禍，我被困在長長的車陣裡，而我和律師的約再十分鐘就開始了，我該怎麼辦？ B：現在就打電話到她的事務所，告訴他們你大約會【遲到】二十分鐘，因為在會面開始前通知對方是禮貌。"},{"w":"early","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or happening before the expected time","c":"提早的；早的","s":"A: This is my first time visiting the government office to renew my business license, and I heard there are always long lines, so when should I go? B: You should be early and arrive before they open at eight thirty, because by ten o'clock the waiting room is usually completely full.","t":"A：這是我第一次去政府機關更新營業執照，聽說那裡總是大排長龍，我該什麼時候去？ B：你應該【提早】，在他們八點半開門前就到，因為到了十點，等候室通常就完全坐滿了。"},{"w":"urgent","p":"adj.","d":"very important and needing action immediately","c":"緊急的","s":"A: The computer system in the accounting office stopped working an hour ago, and the staff cannot send any invoices to clients, so what is the plan? B: I have asked the IT company for an urgent visit this afternoon, because we must send all the monthly invoices before the end of today.","t":"A：會計室的電腦系統一小時前當機了，員工沒辦法寄任何發票給客戶，計畫是什麼？ B：我已經請資訊公司今天下午【緊急】到場，因為我們必須在今天結束前寄出所有月結發票。"},{"w":"fixed","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be changed","c":"固定的","s":"A: Can we move the presentation for the investors to Thursday, because two people on our team are still finishing the sales charts and need more time? B: I am afraid the date is fixed, since the investors are flying in from Hong Kong only for Wednesday, so we must finish the charts tonight.","t":"A：我們可以把對投資人的簡報改到星期四嗎？因為我們團隊有兩個人還在完成銷售圖表，需要更多時間。 B：恐怕日期是【固定的】，因為投資人只為了星期三從香港飛來，所以我們今晚必須完成圖表。"},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"able to change easily","c":"有彈性的；可變通的","s":"A: The supplier wants to visit us next week to show their new packaging, but my schedule is full of meetings, so can you meet them for me? B: Sure, my schedule is quite flexible next week, so I can see them any morning or afternoon, and I will tell you what they show me.","t":"A：供應商下週想來展示他們的新包裝，但我的行程排滿了會議，你可以替我和他們見面嗎？ B：當然，我下週的行程很【有彈性】，所以早上或下午都能見他們，我會告訴你他們展示了什麼。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event such as a meeting or class","c":"出席；參加","s":"A: The headquarters in Singapore is holding a sales conference next month, and the manager wants two people from our office to go, so who will it be? B: She has asked Emily and me to attend the conference, because we handled the biggest accounts this year and can share our results with the other teams.","t":"A：新加坡總部下個月要舉辦業務會議，經理希望我們辦公室派兩個人去，會是誰？ B：她請艾蜜莉和我去【參加】這場會議，因為我們今年負責最大的客戶，可以和其他團隊分享我們的成果。"},{"w":"miss","p":"v.","d":"to not go to something or not be there at the right time","c":"錯過；缺席","s":"A: I overslept this morning because my phone battery died, and I did not hear the alarm, so what happened at the eight o'clock meeting? B: Do not worry too much, because you only had to miss the first part, and I took notes on the new sales targets, so I can share them with you now.","t":"A：我今天早上因為手機沒電沒聽到鬧鐘而睡過頭，八點的會議發生了什麼事？ B：別太擔心，因為你只是【錯過】了前半段，我有記下新的業績目標筆記，現在可以和你分享。"},{"w":"arrange","p":"v.","d":"to plan and organize something","c":"安排","s":"A: The new manager from our Tokyo office is visiting Taipei next week, and she has never been to Taiwan before, so how can we help her? B: I will arrange a car to pick her up at the airport, and I will also plan a short tour of our three stores on her first afternoon.","t":"A：東京辦公室的新經理下週要來台北，她以前從沒來過台灣，我們能怎麼幫她？ B：我會【安排】一輛車去機場接她，也會規劃在她第一天下午簡短參觀我們的三家門市。"},{"w":"booked","p":"adj.","d":"already reserved, so no more places are available","c":"（被）預訂的；客滿的","s":"A: My boss asked me to find a hotel near the convention center for the trade show next weekend, but I have already called three places, so is there a problem? B: Most hotels in that area are fully booked because of the show, so you should try the hotels near the train station, which are only fifteen minutes away.","t":"A：老闆要我找一家下週末商展時會展中心附近的飯店，我已經打了三家，是有什麼問題嗎？ B：因為商展的關係，那一帶大部分飯店都已經【被訂滿了】，你應該試試火車站附近的飯店，離那裡只有十五分鐘。"},{"w":"officially","p":"adv.","d":"in a formal way that is accepted by people in charge","c":"正式地","s":"A: Everyone in the office is talking about the new branch manager, but I have not received any email or notice about it, so is it really true? B: It is true, but she will start her job officially on the first of next month, and the director will introduce her at the staff meeting on Monday.","t":"A：辦公室裡大家都在談論新的分店經理，但我沒收到任何電子郵件或通知，這是真的嗎？ B：是真的，但她要到下個月一號才【正式】上任，主任會在星期一的員工會議上介紹她。"},{"w":"promptly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without delay; exactly at the right time","c":"準時地；迅速地","s":"A: Last week, the training started almost twenty minutes late because some people were still getting coffee, and the trainer was quite unhappy, so what should we do this time? B: Please remind everyone that the session will begin promptly at nine o'clock, and ask them to take their seats five minutes before that.","t":"A：上週訓練幾乎晚了二十分鐘才開始，因為有些人還在拿咖啡，講師很不高興，這次我們該怎麼做？ B：請提醒大家課程將在九點【準時】開始，並請他們提前五分鐘入座。"}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"Argument 爭論","cards":[{"w":"dispute","p":"n.","d":"a serious disagreement, often between groups or companies","c":"糾紛；爭議","s":"A: Why hasn't the shipping company delivered our new office furniture yet, even though we paid for it two months ago and they promised it last week? B: There is a dispute between them and the factory about the final price, and the lawyers say it may take another month before they agree on anything.","t":"A：我們兩個月前就付了錢，他們也承諾上週送達，為什麼貨運公司到現在還沒送來新的辦公家具？ B：他們和工廠之間對最終價格有【糾紛】，律師說可能還要一個月他們才能達成任何共識。"},{"w":"quarrel","p":"n.","d":"an angry argument between people who know each other","c":"爭吵；口角","s":"A: Why are Tom and Kevin sitting so far apart in the meeting room today, when they usually work together on every project and eat lunch together? B: They had a small quarrel yesterday about who should present the report to the director, and now they are both too proud to say sorry first.","t":"A：湯姆和凱文平常每個專案都一起做、也一起吃午餐，為什麼今天在會議室坐得那麼遠？ B：他們昨天為了誰該向主任報告而起了小【口角】，現在兩個人都太驕傲，不肯先道歉。"},{"w":"conflict","p":"n.","d":"a situation where people strongly disagree or want different things","c":"衝突","s":"A: The sales team wants to lower our prices to win more customers, but the finance team says we will lose money, so what is the manager going to do? B: She will meet both teams on Friday to solve this conflict, because the company cannot plan next year's budget until everyone agrees on the prices.","t":"A：業務團隊想降價來爭取更多客戶，但財務團隊說我們會賠錢，經理打算怎麼做？ B：她星期五會和兩個團隊開會解決這個【衝突】，因為在大家對價格達成共識之前，公司沒辦法規劃明年的預算。"},{"w":"debate","p":"n.","d":"a discussion in which people give different opinions on a subject","c":"辯論；討論","s":"A: The board members spent almost three hours yesterday talking about whether we should open a new factory in Vietnam, so did they decide anything at last? B: Not yet, because the debate is still going on, and some members think the costs are too high while others believe the cheaper workers will help us grow.","t":"A：董事會成員昨天花了將近三個小時談論我們是否該在越南開新工廠，他們最後有做出決定嗎？ B：還沒有，因為這場【辯論】還在進行中，有些成員認為成本太高，有些則相信較便宜的人力能幫助我們成長。"},{"w":"clash","p":"n.","d":"a short, strong disagreement or fight","c":"衝突；交鋒","s":"A: I heard there was a lot of shouting in the warehouse this morning, and some workers stopped working for almost an hour, so what happened down there? B: There was a clash between the night shift and the morning shift about who left the loading area so messy, but the supervisor calmed everyone down.","t":"A：我聽說今天早上倉庫裡吵得很兇，有些工人停工了將近一個小時，那裡發生了什麼事？ B：夜班和早班為了誰把裝貨區弄得那麼亂起了【衝突】，不過主管讓大家都冷靜下來了。"},{"w":"disagree","p":"v.","d":"to have a different opinion from someone","c":"不同意；意見不合","s":"A: The manager suggested moving our weekly team meeting from Monday morning to Friday afternoon, so what do you think about her new plan? B: I disagree with her, because many people leave early on Fridays to visit their families, and they would probably miss important news about the week ahead.","t":"A：經理建議把每週的團隊會議從星期一早上改到星期五下午，你覺得她的新計畫怎麼樣？ B：我【不同意】她的看法，因為很多人星期五會提早離開去探望家人，他們可能會錯過下週的重要消息。"},{"w":"argue","p":"v.","d":"to speak angrily with someone because you disagree","c":"爭論；爭吵","s":"A: The two designers were talking very loudly in the meeting room after lunch, and I could hear them from my desk, so is everything all right? B: They often argue about colors and fonts when a deadline is close, but they always find a good solution and stay friends after the project is finished.","t":"A：兩位設計師午餐後在會議室裡講話很大聲，我在座位上都聽得到，一切都還好嗎？ B：截止日快到時，他們常常為了顏色和字體【爭論】，但他們總能找到好的解決方法，專案結束後也依然是朋友。"},{"w":"contest","p":"v.","d":"to formally say that a decision or result is wrong","c":"對…提出異議；爭辯","s":"A: The city government fined our restaurant for putting tables on the sidewalk, but we have a permit that allows us to do that, so what should we do? B: We should contest the fine by sending a copy of our permit to the city office, and our lawyer can help us write a formal letter.","t":"A：市政府因為我們餐廳在人行道上擺桌子而開罰，但我們有允許這麼做的許可證，該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該把許可證影本寄到市政府來對罰單【提出異議】，我們的律師可以幫忙寫正式的信函。"},{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"to disagree with a plan and try to stop it","c":"反對","s":"A: The company wants to build a large parking lot behind our office, but that would mean cutting down all the old trees there, so how do people feel about it? B: Many staff members oppose the plan, because they enjoy eating lunch under those trees, and they have already signed a letter to the director.","t":"A：公司想在我們辦公室後面蓋一座大型停車場，但這表示要砍掉那裡所有的老樹，大家覺得怎麼樣？ B：很多員工【反對】這個計畫，因為他們喜歡在那些樹下吃午餐，而且已經聯名寫信給主任了。"},{"w":"complaint","p":"n.","d":"a statement that you are unhappy about something","c":"抱怨；客訴","s":"A: A customer called this morning and said that her new washing machine was delivered with a broken door, and she sounded very upset, so what did you do? B: I wrote down her complaint in our system and promised that a technician would visit her home tomorrow to replace the door for free.","t":"A：今天早上有位顧客打電話說她的新洗衣機送到時門是壞的，她聽起來很不高興，你怎麼處理？ B：我把她的【客訴】記錄在系統裡，並承諾明天會有技術人員到她家免費更換洗衣機門。"},{"w":"accusation","p":"n.","d":"a statement saying that someone has done something wrong","c":"指控；指責","s":"A: Our new supplier says that our company copied their product design, and they have sent an angry email to our president, so is this a serious problem? B: It is serious, but the accusation is not true, because we have drawings that show our designers finished the design two years before theirs.","t":"A：我們的新供應商說我們公司抄襲他們的產品設計，還寄了一封很生氣的信給我們總裁，這是嚴重的問題嗎？ B：是很嚴重，但這項【指控】不是真的，因為我們有設計圖可以證明我們的設計師比他們早兩年完成設計。"},{"w":"blame","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone is responsible for something bad","c":"責怪；歸咎","s":"A: The project was finished three weeks late, and the client is very unhappy with us, so whose fault was it in the end? B: It is not fair to blame only one person, because the supplier was late, the designs changed twice, and our team was also too small.","t":"A：這個專案晚了三週才完成，客戶對我們非常不滿，最後到底是誰的錯？ B：只【責怪】一個人並不公平，因為供應商延誤、設計改了兩次，我們的團隊人手也太少。"},{"w":"criticism","p":"n.","d":"words that say what is bad or wrong about something","c":"批評","s":"A: The director said many negative things about my marketing plan in front of everyone at the meeting today, and I felt quite embarrassed. B: Try not to take the criticism personally, because she wants the plan to succeed, and her comments about the budget could make your next version much stronger.","t":"A：主任今天在會議上當著大家的面對我的行銷計畫說了很多負面的話，我覺得很難堪。 B：試著不要把這些【批評】當成針對你個人，因為她希望這個計畫成功，她對預算的意見可能會讓你的下一版更有力。"},{"w":"tension","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry and anger between people","c":"緊張（關係）","s":"A: Since the company announced it might close one of the two branches, the people in our office seem very quiet and nervous, so have you noticed it too? B: Yes, there is a lot of tension between the two branches now, because everyone is worried about losing their job and nobody wants to share information.","t":"A：自從公司宣布可能要關閉兩間分公司中的一間，我們辦公室的人似乎都很安靜又緊張，你也注意到了嗎？ B：有，現在兩間分公司之間的【緊張關係】很嚴重，因為大家都擔心丟了工作，沒有人願意分享資訊。"},{"w":"hostility","p":"n.","d":"unfriendly and angry feelings or behavior","c":"敵意","s":"A: When the new manager from headquarters came to visit our factory, many workers would not even say hello to her, so why were they so unfriendly? B: There is some hostility toward headquarters because they cut everyone's bonus last year, and the workers still feel that nobody listened to them.","t":"A：總部的新經理來參觀我們工廠時，很多工人連招呼都不跟她打，他們為什麼那麼不友善？ B：大家對總部有些【敵意】，因為他們去年削減了每個人的獎金，工人們到現在仍覺得沒有人聽他們的意見。"},{"w":"anger","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling you have when something is unfair or wrong","c":"憤怒；怒氣","s":"A: The passengers at Gate 12 have been waiting for over four hours because of the delay, and some of them are now shouting at the airline staff, so what should we do? B: We should offer them free meals and a clear update right away, because that will help reduce their anger while the engineers fix the plane.","t":"A：12號登機門的乘客因為班機延誤已經等了四個多小時，有些人現在正對航空公司人員大吼，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該馬上提供免費餐點和清楚的最新消息，因為在工程師修理飛機時，這能幫助緩和他們的【怒氣】。"},{"w":"frustration","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being upset because you cannot do what you want","c":"挫折感；沮喪","s":"A: The new computer system crashes almost every afternoon, and our team cannot finish the orders on time, so what did people say at the meeting? B: Many people talked about their frustration with the system, and the manager promised to ask the IT company to fix the problem by the end of the week.","t":"A：新的電腦系統幾乎每天下午都當機，我們團隊沒辦法準時完成訂單，會議上大家說了什麼？ B：很多人談到他們對這套系統的【挫折感】，經理承諾會請資訊公司在這週結束前解決問題。"},{"w":"escalate","p":"v.","d":"to become more serious or worse","c":"升級；惡化","s":"A: The customer who complained about the late delivery is now threatening to post bad reviews online and call a lawyer, so how should we deal with him? B: We must act quickly before the situation can escalate any further, so please call him today, say sorry, and offer him a full refund.","t":"A：那位抱怨送貨延誤的客戶現在威脅要上網留負評並找律師，我們該怎麼處理他？ B：我們必須在情況進一步【惡化】之前趕快行動，所以請你今天打給他、向他道歉，並提供全額退款。"},{"w":"provoke","p":"v.","d":"to cause a strong, often angry reaction","c":"激起；挑釁","s":"A: The company is planning to send an email that says all workers must work on Saturdays next month without extra pay, so do you think that is a good idea? B: No, that email will surely provoke a lot of anger among the staff, so the managers should explain the reason and offer extra days off instead.","t":"A：公司打算寄一封電子郵件，說所有員工下個月星期六都得上班而且沒有加班費，你覺得這是好主意嗎？ B：不是，那封信一定會【激起】員工很大的怒氣，所以主管們應該說明原因，並改為提供額外的休假。"},{"w":"defend","p":"v.","d":"to speak in support of someone or something that is criticized","c":"為…辯護；捍衛","s":"A: At the meeting yesterday, the director said our new advertisement was too expensive and not very creative, so did anyone say anything about it? B: Yes, Linda stood up to defend the advertisement, and she showed charts proving that it brought in twice as many new customers as last year's one.","t":"A：昨天會議上主任說我們的新廣告太貴又不夠有創意，有人對此表示什麼嗎？ B：有，琳達站起來為這支廣告【辯護】，並拿出圖表證明它帶來的新客戶是去年那支的兩倍。"},{"w":"justify","p":"v.","d":"to give a good reason for something","c":"證明…有理；為…辯解","s":"A: The finance manager wants to know why our department spent so much money on taxis and hotels last month, so what should I tell her? B: You need to justify each cost with receipts and a short note, for example that the client meetings in Taichung ended late and there were no trains.","t":"A：財務經理想知道我們部門上個月為什麼花了那麼多錢在計程車和飯店上，我該怎麼跟她說？ B：你需要用收據和簡短說明來【證明】每一筆費用是合理的，例如在台中的客戶會議結束得很晚，已經沒有火車了。"},{"w":"assert","p":"v.","d":"to say something firmly and with confidence","c":"斷言；堅稱","s":"A: The client says our team made a mistake in the contract and wants us to pay for the extra costs, but our lawyer read it carefully, so what does she think? B: She continues to assert that the contract is completely correct, and she has prepared a letter that explains each section clearly for the client.","t":"A：客戶說我們團隊在合約中犯了錯，要我們負擔額外費用，但我們的律師仔細讀過了，她怎麼看？ B：她依然【堅稱】合約完全正確，並準備了一封信，為客戶清楚說明每一個條款。"},{"w":"counter","p":"v.","d":"to answer an argument by giving a different opinion","c":"反駁；回應","s":"A: During the negotiation, the buyer said our prices were much higher than the prices of other suppliers in Asia, so how did our sales manager respond to that? B: She was able to counter his point by showing that our products last twice as long and come with a free five-year service plan.","t":"A：談判時，買方說我們的價格比亞洲其他供應商高出許多，我們的業務經理是怎麼回應的？ B：她拿出證據說明我們的產品耐用度是兩倍，還附贈五年免費維修方案，成功【反駁】了他的論點。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which each side gives up something it wants","c":"妥協；折衷","s":"A: The workers want a ten percent pay raise, but the company says it can only afford three percent this year, so is there any way to end this disagreement? B: I think a compromise is possible, such as a six percent raise with two extra days off, because both sides really want to avoid a strike.","t":"A：工人想加薪百分之十，但公司說今年只負擔得起百分之三，有沒有辦法結束這個分歧？ B：我認為可能找到【折衷】方案，例如加薪百分之六再多兩天假，因為雙方都真的想避免罷工。"},{"w":"resolution","p":"n.","d":"the act of solving a problem or ending a disagreement","c":"解決（方法）","s":"A: The two companies have been arguing about the unpaid bill for almost six months, and the lawyers' fees are getting very expensive, so is there any good news yet? B: Yes, they finally found a resolution yesterday, and they agreed to share the cost equally and continue working together on the new project.","t":"A：兩家公司為了這筆未付帳款爭執將近六個月，律師費越來越貴，有任何好消息了嗎？ B：有，他們昨天終於找到了【解決方法】，同意平均分擔費用並繼續合作新專案。"},{"w":"reconcile","p":"v.","d":"to become friendly with someone again after an argument","c":"和解；使和好","s":"A: The two founders of the company stopped speaking to each other last year after a big argument about money, so is it true that they are working together again? B: Yes, a close friend helped them reconcile last month, and now they are planning to open a new store in Taichung together next spring.","t":"A：公司的兩位創辦人去年為了錢大吵一架後就不跟對方說話了，聽說他們又一起合作了，是真的嗎？ B：是的，上個月一位好友幫他們【和解】，現在他們正計畫明年春天一起在台中開一家新店。"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something in order to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"A: The rent for our office will go up by twenty percent next year, and our budget is already very tight, so do we have to accept the new price? B: Not necessarily, because the manager plans to negotiate with the owner next week and ask for a smaller increase if we sign a five-year contract.","t":"A：我們辦公室的租金明年要漲百分之二十，我們的預算已經很緊了，我們一定要接受新價格嗎？ B：不一定，因為經理打算下週和房東【協商】，如果我們簽五年約，就請他少漲一點。"},{"w":"calm","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and not angry or nervous","c":"冷靜的；平靜的","s":"A: A very angry customer is standing at the front desk and shouting about his missing package, and the new receptionist looks scared, so what should she do? B: She should stay calm, speak slowly and politely, and then call the delivery company to find out where the package is right now.","t":"A：一位非常生氣的顧客站在櫃台大吼他遺失的包裹，新來的接待員看起來很害怕，她該怎麼做？ B：她應該保持【冷靜】，慢慢地、有禮貌地說話，然後打電話給貨運公司查出包裹現在在哪裡。"},{"w":"heated","p":"adj.","d":"full of angry and excited feelings","c":"激烈的；激動的","s":"A: The meeting about the new working hours went on for three hours yesterday, and I heard people were shouting, so was it really that bad? B: It was a very heated discussion, because many parents on the team cannot start work at seven, but in the end, the manager agreed to change the plan.","t":"A：昨天關於新工作時間的會議開了三個小時，我聽說有人在大吼，真的那麼糟嗎？ B：那是一場非常【激烈】的討論，因為團隊裡很多家長沒辦法七點開始上班，不過最後經理同意修改計畫。"},{"w":"verbal","p":"adj.","d":"spoken, not written","c":"口頭的；言語的","s":"A: The supplier says we agreed to pay a higher price on the phone last month, but I cannot find that agreement in any of our emails, so is it real? B: It was only a verbal agreement, so we should ask them to send everything in writing before we pay any extra money.","t":"A：供應商說我們上個月在電話中同意支付更高的價格，但我在任何電子郵件中都找不到這項協議，這是真的嗎？ B：那只是【口頭】協議，所以在我們支付任何額外款項之前，應該請他們把所有內容以書面寄來。"},{"w":"hostile","p":"adj.","d":"very unfriendly and ready to argue","c":"有敵意的；不友善的","s":"A: The local people at the town meeting did not seem to like our plan for the new shopping mall, and some of them were shouting, so how did it go? B: The crowd was quite hostile at first, but after we explained the new jobs and the free parking, many of them started to listen.","t":"A：鎮民大會上當地居民似乎不喜歡我們新購物中心的計畫，有些人還在大吼，結果怎麼樣？ B：一開始群眾相當【有敵意】，但在我們說明會有新工作和免費停車之後，很多人開始願意聽了。"},{"w":"peacefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a calm way without fighting or arguing","c":"和平地；平靜地","s":"A: Our two neighbors in the office building have argued about the shared parking spaces for months, and the building manager is tired of it, so what happened today? B: They finally sat down together and solved the problem peacefully, and now each company has five spaces with its name painted on the ground.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓的兩個鄰居為了共用停車位吵了好幾個月，大樓管理員也受夠了，今天發生了什麼事？ B：他們終於坐下來，【和平地】解決了問題，現在每家公司都有五個地上漆著公司名稱的車位。"},{"w":"openly","p":"adv.","d":"in an honest way, without hiding anything","c":"公開地；坦率地","s":"A: Many people on our team are unhappy about the new schedule, but nobody says anything at meetings because they are worried about the boss, so what can we do? B: The boss should invite everyone to talk openly about their concerns, and promise that no one will get into trouble for sharing an honest opinion.","t":"A：我們團隊很多人對新的排班不滿，但開會時沒人敢說話，因為他們擔心老闆，我們能怎麼辦？ B：老闆應該邀請大家【坦率地】說出他們的顧慮，並承諾沒有人會因為說出真心話而惹上麻煩。"}]},{"unit":20,"theme":"Art 藝術","cards":[{"w":"aesthetic","p":"n.","d":"a particular style or idea of what is beautiful","c":"美感；美學風格","s":"A: The new café near our office is always full, even though its coffee costs more than the shops around it, so why do so many people go there? B: Customers love its simple Japanese aesthetic, with wooden tables, soft lights, and plants everywhere, so they enjoy taking photos and sharing them online.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家新咖啡廳總是客滿，雖然咖啡比附近店家貴，為什麼那麼多人去？ B：顧客很喜歡它簡約的日式【美學風格】，有木頭桌、柔和的燈光，到處都是植物，所以他們喜歡拍照並上傳網路分享。"},{"w":"composition","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of a picture or piece of music are arranged","c":"構圖；（作品的）組成","s":"A: The photographer took hundreds of pictures of our new product yesterday, but the marketing manager only chose three of them for the brochure, so why did she pick those? B: She said their composition was the best, because the product is in the center, the background is simple, and the light falls nicely on the logo.","t":"A：攝影師昨天幫我們的新產品拍了好幾百張照片，但行銷經理只選了三張放進手冊，她為什麼選那幾張？ B：她說那幾張的【構圖】最好，因為產品位於中央、背景簡單，光線也很好地打在商標上。"},{"w":"harmony","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant mix of colors, sounds, or parts that go well together","c":"和諧；協調","s":"A: The interior designer used blue, green, and light gray in our new meeting rooms, and everyone says the rooms feel very relaxing, so how did she choose those colors? B: She said these colors work in harmony with each other and with the view of the park, so people feel calm during long meetings.","t":"A：室內設計師在我們新會議室用了藍色、綠色和淺灰色，大家都說房間感覺很放鬆，她是怎麼選這些顏色的？ B：她說這些顏色彼此之間以及和公園景色都很【和諧】，所以大家在長時間開會時會覺得平靜。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way a surface feels when you touch it","c":"質地；紋理","s":"A: The furniture company sent us two kinds of fabric for the new sofas in the hotel lobby, and both are the same color, so which one should we choose? B: I prefer the one with the soft texture, because guests will sit on these sofas for a long time while they wait, and it feels warm and comfortable.","t":"A：家具公司寄給我們兩種用在飯店大廳新沙發的布料，顏色都一樣，我們該選哪一種？ B：我比較喜歡【質地】柔軟的那一種，因為客人等候時會在沙發上坐很久，而那種布摸起來溫暖又舒服。"},{"w":"palette","p":"n.","d":"the range of colors an artist or designer uses","c":"色調；調色盤","s":"A: The new logo for our tea company looks very bright and modern, but some older customers say it does not feel like our brand anymore, so what can we do? B: The designer can try a softer color palette, such as light green and warm brown, which reminds people of fresh tea leaves and our long history.","t":"A：我們茶葉公司的新商標看起來非常鮮豔又現代，但有些老顧客說感覺不像我們的品牌了，我們能怎麼做？ B：設計師可以試試比較柔和的【色調】，例如淺綠和暖棕色，讓人聯想到新鮮茶葉和我們悠久的歷史。"},{"w":"rhythm","p":"n.","d":"a regular, repeated pattern of sounds or movements","c":"節奏","s":"A: The video for our new running shoes looks great, but the manager says it feels a little slow and boring, so how can we make it more exciting? B: We can add music with a strong rhythm, and then cut the video so that each step of the runners matches the beat of the drums.","t":"A：我們新跑鞋的影片看起來很棒，但經理說感覺有點慢又無聊，我們要怎麼讓它更刺激？ B：我們可以加上【節奏】強烈的音樂，然後剪輯影片，讓跑者的每一步都配合鼓聲的節拍。"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference between two things, such as colors","c":"對比","s":"A: Many customers say they cannot read the price tags in our store from far away, especially older people, so what is wrong with the design? B: The problem is the low contrast between the light yellow letters and the white background, so we should print the prices in dark blue instead.","t":"A：很多顧客說他們從遠處看不清楚我們店裡的價格標籤，尤其是年長者，設計出了什麼問題？ B：問題在於淡黃色字和白色背景之間的【對比】太低，所以我們應該改用深藍色印價格。"},{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"the showing of a feeling or idea through words, art, or the face","c":"表達；表現","s":"A: Our company is paying for an art class for staff every Friday evening, but some people say they cannot draw at all, so should they still join? B: Yes, they should, because the teacher says the class is about personal expression, not perfect drawing, and it is a great way to relax after work.","t":"A：公司每週五晚上出錢讓員工上美術課，但有些人說他們完全不會畫畫，他們還該參加嗎？ B：應該，因為老師說這堂課重點在於個人的【表達】，不是畫得完美，而且這是下班後放鬆的好方法。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the idea or wish to do something","c":"啟發；激勵","s":"A: Why did the design team visit the old temples and night markets in Tainan last week, when they are supposed to be designing our new packaging? B: The manager hoped the trip would inspire them with new ideas, because she wants the packaging to show the colors and culture of southern Taiwan.","t":"A：設計團隊應該在設計我們的新包裝，為什麼上週跑去台南參觀老廟和夜市？ B：經理希望這趟旅程能【啟發】他們新的點子，因為她想讓包裝呈現南台灣的色彩和文化。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"not showing people or things in a realistic way, but using shapes and colors","c":"抽象的","s":"A: The bank bought a large painting for the main lobby, but it only has circles and lines in red and black, and some customers ask what it means. B: It is an abstract painting, so it does not show any real objects, and the artist says each person can find their own meaning in the shapes.","t":"A：銀行買了一幅大畫掛在主大廳，但畫裡只有紅色和黑色的圓圈和線條，有些顧客問那是什麼意思。 B：那是一幅【抽象】畫，所以不呈現任何真實的物體，畫家說每個人都可以在這些形狀中找到自己的意義。"},{"w":"melody","p":"n.","d":"the main tune in a piece of music","c":"旋律","s":"A: Our new TV advertisement is finished, but the manager wants people to remember our brand after they hear the music only once, so what should we do? B: We should use a short and simple melody that people can easily hum, and play it again at the end when our logo appears.","t":"A：我們的新電視廣告完成了，但經理希望人們只聽過一次音樂就能記住我們的品牌，我們該怎麼做？ B：我們應該使用簡短好記、讓人容易哼唱的【旋律】，並在最後商標出現時再播放一次。"},{"w":"tone","p":"n.","d":"the general feeling or style of something, such as writing or music","c":"基調；語氣","s":"A: The poster for our charity concert looks very dark, and the music group thinks it may scare away families with children, so how should we change it? B: Let's use brighter colors and a happier photo, so the poster has a warm and friendly tone that matches the cheerful music of the concert.","t":"A：我們慈善音樂會的海報看起來很陰暗，樂團認為可能會嚇跑有小孩的家庭，我們該怎麼修改？ B：我們用比較明亮的顏色和比較歡樂的照片吧，讓海報有溫暖友善的【基調】，搭配音樂會歡快的音樂。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"a pleasing arrangement in which no part looks too strong or heavy","c":"平衡","s":"A: The new website for our hotel has many large pictures on the left side and only a small block of text on the right, so does it look good to you? B: Not really, because the page has no balance, so we should make the pictures smaller and give the text more space on the right side.","t":"A：我們飯店的新網站左邊有很多大張圖片，右邊只有一小塊文字，你覺得好看嗎？ B：不太好看，因為頁面缺乏【平衡】，我們應該把圖片縮小，讓右邊的文字有更多空間。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and movement","c":"充滿活力的；動感的","s":"A: The sports company wants its new advertisement to look exciting and powerful, but our first version shows the athletes just standing and smiling, so what should we change? B: We need more dynamic shots of the athletes jumping and running, with fast camera movement and bright lights, so the advertisement feels full of energy.","t":"A：那家運動公司希望新廣告看起來刺激又有力量，但我們的第一版只拍運動員站著微笑，我們該改什麼？ B：我們需要更多運動員跳躍和奔跑的【動感】鏡頭，加上快速的鏡頭移動和明亮的燈光，讓廣告充滿活力。"},{"w":"form","p":"n.","d":"the shape of something, or a type of art","c":"形式；形狀","s":"A: Our company wants to add some art to the garden in front of the new office building, but we cannot decide between paintings, photographs, and other ideas, so what do you suggest? B: I think a large metal sculpture is the best form of art for a garden, because it can stay outside in the rain and the sun.","t":"A：我們公司想在新辦公大樓前的花園增添一些藝術品，但我們在畫作、攝影和其他點子之間猶豫不決，你有什麼建議？ B：我認為大型金屬雕塑是最適合花園的藝術【形式】，因為它可以在雨天和大太陽下放在戶外。"},{"w":"improvise","p":"v.","d":"to make up music, words, or actions without planning","c":"即興演出；臨時發揮","s":"A: The band at our company dinner lost their song sheets in the taxi, and they are supposed to start playing in ten minutes, so are they going to cancel the show? B: No, the band leader says they will improvise for the first part of the evening, and their manager is bringing new copies from the studio.","t":"A：公司晚宴的樂團把樂譜掉在計程車上了，他們再十分鐘就要開始演奏，表演會取消嗎？ B：不會，樂團團長說晚會前半段他們會【即興演奏】，他們的經理正從錄音室帶新的樂譜過來。"},{"w":"mood","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that a place, picture, or piece of music gives you","c":"氛圍；情緒","s":"A: The owner of the new restaurant wants guests to feel relaxed and stay longer at dinner, but the room still feels cold and too bright, so what can we change? B: We can create a warm mood with soft yellow lights, quiet jazz music, and a few paintings of the countryside on the walls.","t":"A：新餐廳的老闆希望客人用晚餐時感到放鬆並待久一點，但空間還是感覺冰冷又太亮，我們能改什麼？ B：我們可以用柔和的黃色燈光、輕柔的爵士樂，再加上幾幅鄉村風景畫掛在牆上，營造溫暖的【氛圍】。"},{"w":"motif","p":"n.","d":"a shape or idea that is repeated in a design or work of art","c":"圖案；主題（重複出現的元素）","s":"A: The new uniforms for our hotel staff look nice, but the manager feels they do not show anything special about our hotel, so how can we improve them? B: We could add a small flower motif from our hotel logo on the collar and the pockets, so every uniform clearly matches the style of the building.","t":"A：我們飯店員工的新制服看起來不錯，但經理覺得無法展現我們飯店的特色，我們要怎麼改進？ B：我們可以在領口和口袋加上飯店商標中的小花【圖案】，讓每件制服都明顯和建築風格相配。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to explain or understand the meaning of something","c":"詮釋；解讀","s":"A: Our art gallery is showing modern paintings this month, and many visitors say they do not understand them at all, so how can we help them? B: We can hire a guide to help visitors interpret each painting, and we can also put short notes beside the paintings in both Chinese and English.","t":"A：我們美術館這個月展出現代畫作，很多參觀者說完全看不懂，我們要怎麼幫助他們？ B：我們可以聘請導覽員幫助參觀者【解讀】每一幅畫，也可以在畫作旁放上中英文的簡短說明。"},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"a strong cloth that artists paint on, or a painting on it","c":"畫布；油畫","s":"A: The artist we hired is going to paint a large picture of the city for our new office lobby, so how big will the finished painting be? B: She is using a canvas that is three meters wide, so we will need to clear the wall near the entrance and ask the building manager for a special light.","t":"A：我們聘請的畫家要為新辦公室大廳畫一幅大型城市畫作，完成的畫會有多大？ B：她用的【畫布】有三公尺寬，所以我們需要清空入口附近的牆面，並請大樓管理員裝一盞特別的燈。"},{"w":"lyrical","p":"adj.","d":"expressing feelings in a beautiful, song-like way","c":"抒情的；如詩般的","s":"A: The hotel wants to play some music in the lobby in the evening, but the guests did not like the loud pop songs we tried last week, so what should we play now? B: Try some soft and lyrical piano music, because it sounds beautiful and emotional, and guests can still talk quietly while they wait.","t":"A：飯店想在晚上的大廳播放一些音樂，但客人不喜歡我們上週試的大聲流行歌曲，現在該播什麼？ B：試試輕柔又【抒情】的鋼琴音樂，因為它聽起來優美又感人，客人等候時也還能小聲交談。"},{"w":"vivid","p":"adj.","d":"very bright and strong (colors) or very clear (descriptions)","c":"鮮豔的；生動的","s":"A: Our travel agency's brochure for Hualien uses gray and pale photos, and very few customers have booked that tour, so how can we make it more attractive? B: We should use vivid pictures of the blue sea and the green mountains, because bright colors make people want to visit a place right away.","t":"A：我們旅行社的花蓮手冊用的是灰暗又淡的照片，很少顧客報名那個行程，要怎麼讓它更吸引人？ B：我們應該使用藍色大海和翠綠山脈的【鮮豔】照片，因為明亮的色彩會讓人想立刻去那個地方。"},{"w":"craft","p":"n.","d":"a skill of making things by hand, or the things made","c":"工藝；手藝","s":"A: Our company wants to give special gifts to our overseas clients this year, but we do not want to buy the usual cheap souvenirs from the airport, so do you have ideas? B: We could buy local bamboo craft from a small workshop in Nantou, because each piece is handmade and shows a traditional skill from Taiwan.","t":"A：公司今年想送特別的禮物給海外客戶，但不想買機場那種常見的便宜紀念品，你有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們可以向南投一間小工坊購買當地的竹【工藝】品，因為每件都是手工製作，展現台灣的傳統技藝。"},{"w":"symbolism","p":"n.","d":"the use of images or objects to represent ideas","c":"象徵手法；象徵意義","s":"A: The new poster for our bank shows a small tree growing out of a pile of coins, and some customers are asking why it looks like that, so what does it mean? B: The symbolism is simple, because the tree shows that your savings can grow slowly but strongly over time if you keep them in our bank.","t":"A：我們銀行的新海報畫著一棵從一堆硬幣中長出來的小樹，有些顧客在問為什麼長那樣，那是什麼意思？ B：它的【象徵意義】很簡單，那棵樹代表只要把存款放在我們銀行，你的儲蓄就能隨著時間慢慢穩健地成長。"},{"w":"tempo","p":"n.","d":"the speed of a piece of music","c":"（音樂的）速度；節拍","s":"A: The fitness center wants new music for its morning exercise class, but the members say the current songs are too slow to keep them moving, so what should we choose? B: Choose songs with a faster tempo, about one hundred and thirty beats per minute, because quick music helps people move and work harder.","t":"A：健身中心想為早上的運動課換新音樂，但會員說目前的歌太慢，沒辦法讓他們一直動，該選什麼？ B：選擇【速度】較快的歌，大約每分鐘一百三十拍，因為快節奏的音樂能幫助人們動起來、更賣力運動。"},{"w":"gesture","p":"n.","d":"a movement of the hands or body that shows a meaning or feeling","c":"手勢；姿態","s":"A: The dancer in our new advertisement only moves her hands slowly at the end, but the client says that last moment is the most important part, so why is that? B: Her final gesture looks like she is opening a door, and it shows that our company opens new chances for young people.","t":"A：我們新廣告裡的舞者在最後只是慢慢地移動雙手，但客戶說最後那一刻是最重要的部分，為什麼？ B：她最後的【手勢】看起來像是在打開一扇門，表示我們公司為年輕人開啟新的機會。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and original things or ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: Our sales of the new juice are lower than we expected, and the old advertisements have not worked well with young people, so who should we ask for help? B: We should hire a more creative advertising team, because they can make fun short videos and new ideas that young people want to share online.","t":"A：我們新果汁的銷量比預期低，以前的廣告對年輕人效果不好，我們該找誰幫忙？ B：我們應該聘請一個更有【創意】的廣告團隊，因為他們能做出有趣的短影片和年輕人想上網分享的新點子。"},{"w":"nuance","p":"n.","d":"a very small difference in color, meaning, or feeling","c":"細微差別","s":"A: The translation of our English advertisement into Japanese is finished, but the manager in Tokyo says it sounds a little strange, so what is the problem? B: The translator missed a small nuance in the slogan, because the Japanese word sounds too serious, while the English one sounds friendly and light.","t":"A：我們英文廣告的日文翻譯完成了，但東京的經理說聽起來有點奇怪，問題在哪裡？ B：譯者漏掉了標語中一個【細微差別】，因為日文用字聽起來太嚴肅，而英文的則聽起來親切又輕鬆。"},{"w":"visual","p":"adj.","d":"relating to seeing or things that you can see","c":"視覺的","s":"A: Our sales presentation has twenty slides full of long sentences and numbers, and the clients looked bored last time, so how can we make it better? B: Let's add more visual information, such as charts, photos, and simple icons, because people understand and remember pictures much faster than long text.","t":"A：我們的業務簡報有二十張投影片，都塞滿長句和數字，上次客戶看起來很無聊，我們要怎麼改善？ B：我們多加一些【視覺】資訊吧，像是圖表、照片和簡單的圖示，因為人們理解和記住圖片的速度比長篇文字快得多。"},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to play music, dance, or act in front of an audience","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: The company's year-end party is in three weeks, and the manager wants some entertainment after dinner, so has anyone offered to do something? B: Yes, five people from the accounting department will perform a traditional dance, and they have been practicing every evening after work in the meeting room.","t":"A：公司尾牙再三週就到了，經理希望晚餐後有些表演節目，有人自願要做什麼嗎？ B：有，會計部的五個人要【表演】一支傳統舞蹈，他們每天下班後都在會議室裡練習。"}]},{"unit":21,"theme":"Athlete 運動員","cards":[{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to keep doing something hard for a long time","c":"耐力","s":"A: Our company is sponsoring a runner in the Taipei Marathon this year, and the marketing team wants to make a short video about her, so what makes her special? B: She has amazing endurance, because she can run for more than three hours without slowing down, and she trains every morning before she goes to work.","t":"A：我們公司今年贊助一位參加台北馬拉松的跑者，行銷團隊想幫她拍一支短片，她有什麼特別之處？ B：她有驚人的【耐力】，可以跑三個多小時都不減速，而且她每天早上上班前都會練習。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"the physical power of the body","c":"力量；體力","s":"A: The moving company wants to hire three new workers to carry furniture up and down stairs in old apartment buildings, so what should they look for? B: They need people with good physical strength, because the workers often have to carry heavy sofas and refrigerators up five floors without an elevator.","t":"A：搬家公司想再雇三名工人，在老公寓裡上下樓梯搬家具，他們應該找什麼樣的人？ B：他們需要體能【力量】好的人，因為工人常常得在沒有電梯的情況下把沉重的沙發和冰箱搬上五樓。"},{"w":"speed","p":"n.","d":"how fast someone or something moves","c":"速度","s":"A: The sports shoe company says its new running shoes are much lighter than last year's model, so why do professional runners like them so much? B: The lighter shoes help runners increase their speed in short races, and several athletes broke their personal records while wearing them at the national games.","t":"A：那家運動鞋公司說他們的新跑鞋比去年的款式輕很多，職業跑者為什麼這麼喜歡？ B：比較輕的鞋子能幫跑者在短跑比賽中提升【速度】，好幾位運動員穿著它在全國運動會上打破了個人紀錄。"},{"w":"agility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to move quickly and change direction easily","c":"敏捷","s":"A: The basketball coach at our company team keeps asking the players to run between small cones on the floor, and some of them think it is boring, so why does he do it? B: That exercise improves their agility, so they can turn quickly, move around other players, and react faster during real games.","t":"A：我們公司籃球隊的教練一直要球員在地上的小三角錐之間跑，有些人覺得很無聊，他為什麼要這樣做？ B：那個練習能提升他們的【敏捷度】，讓他們在真正比賽時能迅速轉身、繞過其他球員並更快反應。"},{"w":"stamina","p":"n.","d":"the energy to keep doing physical or mental work for a long time","c":"體力；精力","s":"A: The tour guides at our travel agency often walk with groups for eight hours a day in the mountains, and some new guides feel very tired by lunchtime, so what can help them? B: They should go swimming or jogging a few times a week to build up their stamina, so they will not feel so tired on long tours.","t":"A：我們旅行社的導遊常常一天帶團在山裡走八個小時，有些新導遊到午餐時間就覺得很累，有什麼辦法能幫助他們？ B：他們應該每週游泳或慢跑幾次來增強【體力】，這樣帶長途行程就不會那麼累了。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control yourself and follow rules or plans","c":"自律；紀律","s":"A: How does that young tennis player manage to study at university and still train for four hours every day, when most students can barely finish their homework? B: She has very strong discipline, because she follows a strict schedule, goes to bed early, and never skips a training session, even on weekends.","t":"A：大部分學生連作業都快寫不完，那位年輕網球選手是怎麼一邊念大學、一邊每天練球四個小時的？ B：她非常【自律】，因為她遵守嚴格的時間表、早早上床睡覺，就算週末也從不缺席任何一次訓練。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"working hard because you care a lot about something","c":"投入的；專注的","s":"A: Our company wants to choose one local athlete to be the face of our new sports drink, and we have three names on the list, so who do you suggest? B: I suggest the swimmer from Kaohsiung, because she is very dedicated to her sport and also spends her free time teaching poor children to swim.","t":"A：我們公司想挑一位本地運動員擔任新運動飲料的代言人，名單上有三個人，你建議誰？ B：我建議那位高雄的游泳選手，因為她對這項運動非常【投入】，空閒時還會教弱勢孩童游泳。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to win or be better than others","c":"好勝的；有競爭力的","s":"A: When we play basketball after work on Fridays, Jason always gets angry when his team loses, even though it is only a friendly game, so why is he like that? B: He is very competitive, because he played on the national team in college, and he still hates losing at anything, even card games.","t":"A：我們週五下班後打籃球時，傑森的隊伍一輸他就生氣，雖然那只是友誼賽，他為什麼會這樣？ B：他非常【好勝】，因為他大學時是國家隊的，到現在還是很討厭輸，連玩牌都一樣。"},{"w":"training","p":"n.","d":"the process of preparing for a sport through exercise and practice","c":"訓練","s":"A: The baseball team that our bank sponsors will play in an important tournament in Japan next month, so how are the players getting ready for it? B: They have started a special training program that includes running, weight lifting, and batting practice six days a week, and they will rest only on Sundays.","t":"A：我們銀行贊助的棒球隊下個月要去日本參加重要的錦標賽，球員們怎麼準備？ B：他們開始了一套特別的【訓練】計畫，包含跑步、重量訓練和打擊練習，每週六天，只有星期天休息。"},{"w":"coach","p":"n.","d":"a person who trains athletes or a sports team","c":"教練","s":"A: Our company volleyball team has lost every game this season, and the players are starting to feel unhappy, so what does the manager plan to do? B: She wants to hire a professional coach who can train the team twice a week and teach them better ways to play together.","t":"A：我們公司的排球隊這一季每場比賽都輸，球員開始覺得不開心，經理打算怎麼做？ B：她想聘請一位專業【教練】，每週訓練球隊兩次，教他們更好的團隊打法。"},{"w":"technique","p":"n.","d":"a special way of doing something that needs skill","c":"技巧；技術","s":"A: The golf club is offering lessons for our sales team because many of our clients like to play golf, but none of us are good at it, so is it worth it? B: Yes, because the lessons will teach you the correct technique for holding the club and swinging it, so you can play with clients without feeling embarrassed.","t":"A：高爾夫球俱樂部要為我們業務團隊開課，因為很多客戶喜歡打高爾夫，但我們都打得不好，值得去上嗎？ B：值得，因為課程會教你握桿和揮桿的正確【技巧】，這樣你和客戶打球時就不會覺得難為情。"},{"w":"flexibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to bend and stretch your body easily","c":"柔軟度","s":"A: Many people in our office complain about back pain after sitting at their desks all day, so the company wants to offer an exercise class, but which one? B: I think a yoga class is the best choice, because it improves flexibility and helps people stretch the muscles that become tight after long hours at the computer.","t":"A：我們辦公室很多人抱怨整天坐在辦公桌前造成背痛，公司想開一堂運動課，要開哪一種？ B：我認為瑜伽課是最好的選擇，因為它能改善【柔軟度】，幫助大家伸展長時間使用電腦後變緊繃的肌肉。"},{"w":"focus","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving all your attention to one thing","c":"專注；焦點","s":"A: The archer we interviewed for our sports magazine said she does not listen to music or look at her phone on the day of a competition, so why does she do that? B: She wants to keep her focus completely on the target, because even a small distraction can cause her to miss by a few centimeters.","t":"A：我們運動雜誌採訪的那位射箭選手說，比賽當天她不聽音樂也不看手機，她為什麼這樣做？ B：她想讓自己的【專注力】完全放在箭靶上，因為即使一點小小的分心都可能讓她偏差幾公分。"},{"w":"mental","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the mind","c":"心理的；精神的","s":"A: Our company now offers free talks with a sports psychologist for staff who play in the city tennis league, so why would players need that kind of help? B: Many players say that mental strength is just as important as physical skill, because staying calm under pressure often decides who wins a close game.","t":"A：我們公司現在為參加市立網球聯賽的員工提供和運動心理師免費談話的機會，球員為什麼需要那種協助？ B：很多球員說【心理】素質和體能技巧一樣重要，因為在壓力下保持冷靜往往決定誰能贏得勢均力敵的比賽。"},{"w":"resilient","p":"adj.","d":"able to recover quickly after something bad happens","c":"有韌性的；能迅速恢復的","s":"A: That baseball player hurt his shoulder badly last year, and many people thought his career was over, so how is he playing so well this season? B: He is very resilient, because he worked hard with doctors for months, never gave up, and came back even stronger than before.","t":"A：那位棒球選手去年肩膀受了重傷，很多人以為他的職業生涯結束了，他這一季怎麼打得這麼好？ B：他非常【有韌性】，因為他和醫生努力了好幾個月，從不放棄，回來後甚至比以前更強。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the reason or energy that makes you want to do something","c":"動力；動機","s":"A: Our company started a walking challenge last month, but many people stopped joining after the first two weeks, so how can we get them interested again? B: We can give small prizes every week, because rewards often increase people's motivation, and we can show each team's steps on a big screen in the lobby.","t":"A：公司上個月開始了健走挑戰，但很多人在前兩週後就不參加了，我們要怎麼讓他們重新感興趣？ B：我們可以每週發小獎品，因為獎勵常常能提高人們的【動力】，也可以在大廳的大螢幕上顯示每一隊的步數。"},{"w":"practice","p":"n.","d":"the regular activity of doing something again and again to improve","c":"練習","s":"A: Why does our company soccer team meet in the park at six thirty every Tuesday and Thursday morning, before the office opens? B: They have practice twice a week before work, because many players have family duties in the evening and the park is quiet and cool early in the morning.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司的足球隊每週二和週四早上六點半，在辦公室開門前就到公園集合？ B：他們每週上班前有兩次【練習】，因為很多球員晚上要照顧家庭，而且公園一大早既安靜又涼爽。"},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of getting healthy again after an injury or hard exercise","c":"恢復；康復","s":"A: Our star runner hurt her knee during training last month, and the big race is in eight weeks, so can she still compete in it? B: The doctor says her recovery is going well, and if she continues her treatment and rests properly, she should be ready to race in about six weeks.","t":"A：我們的明星跑者上個月訓練時傷了膝蓋，而大型比賽在八週後，她還能參賽嗎？ B：醫生說她的【康復】狀況良好，只要繼續治療並適當休息，大約六週後就能準備好比賽。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"how well someone does in a game or activity","c":"表現","s":"A: The sports drink company wants to know if their new product really helps athletes, so how are they going to test it this summer? B: They will measure each runner's performance in races with and without the drink, and then they will compare the results to see if there is a real difference.","t":"A：運動飲料公司想知道他們的新產品是否真的對運動員有幫助，今年夏天他們打算怎麼測試？ B：他們會測量每位跑者在有喝和沒喝飲料時比賽的【表現】，然後比較結果，看看是否真的有差異。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a plan for achieving a goal","c":"策略；戰術","s":"A: Our company team is playing against the bank's team in the final of the basketball tournament next week, and they are much taller than us, so how can we win? B: We need a smart strategy, such as passing the ball quickly and shooting from far away, so their tall players cannot block us easily.","t":"A：我們公司隊下週要在籃球錦標賽決賽中對上銀行隊，他們比我們高很多，我們要怎麼贏？ B：我們需要聰明的【戰術】，例如快速傳球和遠距離投籃，讓他們的高個子球員沒辦法輕易阻擋我們。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"harm done to the body, for example in an accident or sport","c":"受傷；傷害","s":"A: Our best soccer player could not play in yesterday's game, and the team lost by three goals, so what happened to him? B: He has a knee injury from a fall during practice last week, and the doctor told him to rest for at least a month before he plays again.","t":"A：我們最好的足球員沒辦法參加昨天的比賽，球隊輸了三球，他發生了什麼事？ B：他上週練習時跌倒造成膝蓋【受傷】，醫生要他至少休息一個月才能再上場。"},{"w":"conditioning","p":"n.","d":"exercise that makes the body fit and strong for a sport","c":"體能訓練；體能狀況","s":"A: The new fitness coach at our company gym makes the volleyball players run up and down the stairs for twenty minutes before each practice, so what is the point of that? B: It is part of their conditioning program, because it builds the strong legs and heart they need to jump and play hard for the whole match.","t":"A：我們公司健身房的新體能教練每次練習前都要排球員在樓梯上下跑二十分鐘，這樣做有什麼用意？ B：那是他們【體能訓練】計畫的一部分，因為它能鍛鍊出整場比賽跳躍和全力打球所需的強壯雙腿和心臟。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to stay steady without falling","c":"平衡（感）","s":"A: The sports equipment store wants to sell more of its new surfboards this summer, but many beginners are afraid to try surfing, so what can the store do? B: The store can offer free lessons on the beach, where teachers show beginners how to keep their balance on the board before they go into the deeper water.","t":"A：運動用品店今年夏天想多賣一些新的衝浪板，但很多初學者不敢嘗試衝浪，店家能怎麼做？ B：店家可以在海灘上提供免費課程，讓老師在初學者下到深水區之前，教他們如何在板子上保持【平衡】。"},{"w":"coordination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make different parts of the body work well together","c":"協調性","s":"A: The video game company wants to test whether its new dance game is good exercise for children, so what will the researchers measure during the study? B: They will check the children's coordination before and after two months of playing, because the game asks players to move their hands and feet together to the music.","t":"A：電玩公司想測試他們的新跳舞遊戲對孩子來說是否是好的運動，研究人員在研究期間會測量什麼？ B：他們會在孩子玩兩個月前後檢查他們的【協調性】，因為這個遊戲要求玩家隨著音樂同時移動手腳。"},{"w":"power","p":"n.","d":"physical strength and force","c":"力量；爆發力","s":"A: The sports company is making an advertisement for its new tennis racket, and it wants to show how strong the racket is, so what kind of scene should we film? B: We should film a famous player hitting a serve with great power, and then show the ball flying past the other player at more than two hundred kilometers an hour.","t":"A：運動公司在為新網球拍拍廣告，想展現球拍有多強，我們該拍什麼樣的畫面？ B：我們應該拍一位知名選手以強大【力量】發球，然後呈現球以時速超過兩百公里飛過對手身邊。"},{"w":"goal-oriented","p":"adj.","d":"focused on reaching a clear aim","c":"目標導向的","s":"A: The sales manager said that she likes to hire former athletes for her team, but she did not explain why, so what do you think her reason is? B: Former athletes are usually very goal-oriented, so they set clear targets, plan each step carefully, and keep working hard until they reach them.","t":"A：業務經理說她喜歡雇用前運動員加入團隊，但她沒解釋原因，你覺得她的理由是什麼？ B：前運動員通常非常【目標導向】，所以他們會設定明確的目標、仔細規劃每一步，並且持續努力直到達成。"},{"w":"compete","p":"v.","d":"to take part in a race or contest in order to win","c":"比賽；競爭","s":"A: Our company has sent five of its staff members to the city's half-marathon every year, and they always enjoy it, so who is joining this year? B: This year, ten people want to compete in the race, so we will order matching shirts with our company logo and arrange a bus to the starting line.","t":"A：我們公司每年都派五名員工參加市區半程馬拉松，他們總是玩得很開心，今年有誰參加？ B：今年有十個人想【參加】這場比賽，所以我們會訂製印有公司商標的同款上衣，並安排巴士送大家到起點。"},{"w":"teamwork","p":"n.","d":"the ability of a group to work well together","c":"團隊合作","s":"A: Our company volleyball team does not have any very tall or famous players, but they won the city tournament this year, so how did they do it? B: Their teamwork was excellent, because they talked to each other on every point, trusted each other, and always covered for a teammate who made a mistake.","t":"A：我們公司排球隊沒有很高或很有名的球員，但今年卻贏得了市錦標賽，他們是怎麼做到的？ B：他們的【團隊合作】非常出色，因為每一分他們都互相溝通、彼此信任，而且總是幫犯錯的隊友補位。"},{"w":"victory","p":"n.","d":"a win in a game, competition, or fight","c":"勝利","s":"A: The baseball team that our company sponsors won the national championship last night, and the whole office is talking about it, so how should we celebrate? B: Let's hold a small party for the team on Friday to celebrate their victory, and we can put a big photo of them holding the trophy in the lobby.","t":"A：我們公司贊助的棒球隊昨晚贏得全國冠軍，整個辦公室都在討論，我們該怎麼慶祝？ B：我們星期五為球隊辦個小派對慶祝他們的【勝利】吧，還可以在大廳放一張他們捧著獎盃的大照片。"}]},{"unit":22,"theme":"Bags 包包","cards":[{"w":"backpack","p":"n.","d":"a bag you carry on your back with two straps","c":"背包；後背包","s":"A: I have to walk from the train station to the client's office every morning this week, and my laptop and files are getting heavy, so what kind of bag should I buy? B: You should get a backpack with padded straps, because it spreads the weight across both shoulders and leaves your hands free for your phone and umbrella.","t":"A：這週我每天早上都得從火車站走到客戶辦公室，筆電和文件越來越重，我該買什麼樣的包包？ B：你應該買一個肩帶有襯墊的【後背包】，因為它能把重量分散在兩邊肩膀上，讓你的雙手可以拿手機和雨傘。"},{"w":"handbag","p":"n.","d":"a small bag that women often use to carry money, keys, and other things","c":"手提包","s":"A: The department store wants to put a new display near the main entrance before Mother's Day, so which products should we show there to attract shoppers? B: We should display our new leather handbag in red and cream, because many customers buy them as gifts for their mothers and they look great in the window.","t":"A：百貨公司想在母親節前於大門口附近擺一個新的展示區，我們該展示哪些商品來吸引顧客？ B：我們應該展示紅色和米色的新款皮革【手提包】，因為很多顧客會買來當作送給媽媽的禮物，而且放在櫥窗裡很好看。"},{"w":"tote","p":"n.","d":"a large open bag with two handles, used for carrying many things","c":"托特包；大手提袋","s":"A: Our company is giving away free gifts at the trade show next month, and the manager wants something useful that people will keep, so what do you suggest? B: Let's give each visitor a cotton tote with our logo on it, because people can use it for shopping, and our name will be seen all over the city.","t":"A：我們公司下個月要在商展上贈送免費禮物，經理想要大家會留著用的實用東西，你有什麼建議？ B：我們送每位參觀者一個印有公司商標的棉布【托特包】吧，因為大家可以拿來購物，我們的名字就會出現在城市各處。"},{"w":"satchel","p":"n.","d":"a bag with a long strap and a flap, often used for books or papers","c":"側背書包；公事包","s":"A: My new job is at a law office, and I need to carry a lot of papers and a small laptop to court, but I do not like backpacks, so what is a good choice? B: A brown leather satchel would look professional, because it has a long shoulder strap, a flap that closes tightly, and enough room for your documents.","t":"A：我的新工作在律師事務所，需要帶很多文件和一台小筆電去法院，但我不喜歡後背包，有什麼好選擇？ B：一個棕色皮革【側背公事包】看起來會很專業，因為它有長肩帶、可以緊緊扣住的掀蓋，空間也夠放你的文件。"},{"w":"clutch","p":"n.","d":"a small, flat bag without a handle, held in the hand, usually for formal events","c":"手拿包","s":"A: The company's year-end party is at a fancy hotel this year, and everyone has to dress formally, but my everyday bag is far too big, so what should I bring? B: You could carry a small silver clutch, because it holds your phone, keys, and a lipstick, and it looks elegant with an evening dress.","t":"A：今年公司尾牙在高級飯店舉行，大家都要穿正式服裝，但我平常的包包太大了，我該帶什麼？ B：你可以拿一個小小的銀色【手拿包】，因為它能裝手機、鑰匙和口紅，搭配晚禮服也很優雅。"},{"w":"duffel","p":"n.","d":"a large soft bag shaped like a tube, used for sports clothes or travel","c":"圓筒旅行袋；行李袋","s":"A: I am going on a three-day team-building trip in the mountains with my coworkers, and we have to carry our things from the bus to the cabin, so is a suitcase okay? B: A suitcase is hard to roll on the mountain path, so take a soft duffel instead, because you can carry it on your shoulder and squeeze it into small spaces.","t":"A：我要和同事去山上參加三天的團隊建立活動，我們得自己把東西從巴士搬到小木屋，帶行李箱可以嗎？ B：行李箱在山路上很難拉，所以改帶軟的【圓筒行李袋】吧，因為你可以把它扛在肩上，也能塞進狹小的空間。"},{"w":"pouch","p":"n.","d":"a small soft bag for keeping small things","c":"小袋子；收納包","s":"A: Every time I travel for work, my phone charger, earphones, and cables get mixed up at the bottom of my bag, and it takes forever to find them. B: Put them all in a small zip pouch, and then you can take everything out at once when you get to the hotel or the meeting room.","t":"A：每次出差，我的手機充電器、耳機和傳輸線都混在包包底部，要找很久才找得到。 B：把它們全部放進一個有拉鍊的小【收納包】，這樣到了飯店或會議室時，你就能一次把所有東西拿出來。"},{"w":"zipper","p":"n.","d":"a metal or plastic device with two rows of teeth that closes a bag or clothes","c":"拉鍊","s":"A: A customer brought back the suitcase she bought from our shop two weeks ago, and she seems quite upset, so what is wrong with it? B: The zipper on the front pocket broke on her first trip, so we should replace the suitcase for free and tell the factory to check that part more carefully.","t":"A：有位顧客把兩週前在我們店裡買的行李箱拿回來，她看起來很不高興，是出了什麼問題？ B：前面口袋的【拉鍊】在她第一次旅行時就壞了，所以我們應該免費幫她換一個行李箱，並請工廠更仔細檢查那個零件。"},{"w":"strap","p":"n.","d":"a narrow piece of leather or cloth used to carry a bag","c":"背帶；肩帶","s":"A: Many customers like the design of our new laptop bag, but some of them say it hurts their shoulder after they walk for a while, so how can we improve it? B: We can make the strap wider and add a soft pad, so the weight of the laptop does not press so hard on one small area of the shoulder.","t":"A：很多顧客喜歡我們新筆電包的設計，但有些人說走一陣子後肩膀會痛，我們要怎麼改進？ B：我們可以把【背帶】加寬並加上軟墊，這樣筆電的重量就不會集中壓在肩膀的一小塊地方。"},{"w":"compartment","p":"n.","d":"a separate section inside a bag for keeping things apart","c":"隔層；夾層","s":"A: I often carry my laptop and my lunch box in the same bag on my way to the office, and I am worried that the soup might leak onto the computer. B: Choose a bag with a separate padded compartment for the laptop, so your computer stays safe and dry even if something spills in the main part.","t":"A：我上班途中常把筆電和便當盒放在同一個包包裡，擔心湯會漏到電腦上。 B：選一個有獨立襯墊筆電【隔層】的包包，這樣即使主袋裡有東西灑出來，你的電腦也能保持安全乾燥。"},{"w":"pocket","p":"n.","d":"a small bag sewn onto or into a larger bag or clothes","c":"口袋","s":"A: At the airport, I always have to look through my whole bag to find my passport and boarding pass, and the people behind me in line get impatient. B: Keep them in the small outside pocket of your backpack, because you can reach it quickly without opening the main part of the bag.","t":"A：在機場我總是得翻遍整個包包才找得到護照和登機證，排在我後面的人都不耐煩了。 B：把它們放在後背包外側的小【口袋】裡，因為你不用打開包包主袋就能很快拿到。"},{"w":"lining","p":"n.","d":"a layer of material covering the inside of a bag","c":"內襯；襯裡","s":"A: The outside of this handbag is made of beautiful leather, but the price is much higher than the other bags on the shelf, so why does it cost so much? B: It has a silk lining inside, which protects your things and makes the bag look elegant every time you open it, and it is all sewn by hand.","t":"A：這個手提包外層是用漂亮的皮革做的，但價格比架上其他包包高很多，為什麼這麼貴？ B：它裡面有絲質【內襯】，能保護你的物品，每次打開包包時看起來都很優雅，而且全部都是手工縫製。"},{"w":"leather","p":"n.","d":"animal skin that is treated and used to make bags, shoes, and clothes","c":"皮革","s":"A: Our company wants to give the top salespeople a special gift at the end of the year, something that lasts for many years and looks professional, so what would be good? B: A briefcase made of real leather would be a great choice, because it becomes softer and more beautiful with age and can last more than ten years.","t":"A：公司想在年底送一份特別的禮物給頂尖業務員，要能用很多年又看起來專業的東西，什麼比較好？ B：真【皮】製的公事包會是很好的選擇，因為它會隨著時間變得更柔軟、更漂亮，而且可以用十年以上。"},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"a strong, heavy cloth used for bags, shoes, and tents","c":"帆布","s":"A: The bookstore wants to sell its own shopping bags, but the manager does not want plastic because many customers care about the environment, so which material should we use? B: We should use thick cotton canvas, because it is strong enough to carry heavy books, easy to print a logo on, and can be washed many times.","t":"A：書店想販售自己的購物袋，但經理不想用塑膠，因為很多顧客在意環保，我們該用什麼材質？ B：我們應該用厚棉【帆布】，因為它夠堅固能裝重的書、容易印上商標，而且可以洗很多次。"},{"w":"waterproof","p":"adj.","d":"not letting water go through","c":"防水的","s":"A: I will be visiting construction sites in Keelung all next week, and the weather report says it will rain almost every day, so how can I keep my documents dry? B: Use a waterproof bag with a roll-top opening, because even heavy rain cannot get inside, and your plans and contracts will stay completely dry.","t":"A：下週我整週都要去基隆的工地，氣象報告說幾乎每天都會下雨，我要怎麼讓文件保持乾燥？ B：用一個捲口式開口的【防水】包，因為就算大雨也進不去，你的設計圖和合約都能保持完全乾燥。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"able to last a long time without breaking","c":"耐用的","s":"A: Our delivery workers carry heavy packages in their bags all day, and the cheap bags we bought last year all fell apart within a few months, so what should we buy now? B: We need more durable bags made of thick nylon with strong stitching, even if they cost more, because they will last for several years and save money.","t":"A：我們的送貨員整天用包包背重物，去年買的便宜包包幾個月內就都壞了，我們現在該買什麼？ B：我們需要更【耐用】的包包，用厚尼龍和堅固的縫線製成，即使比較貴，因為它們能用好幾年，反而省錢。"},{"w":"lightweight","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy","c":"輕量的；輕便的","s":"A: The flight attendants at our airline walk through long airports every day with their bags, and many of them have complained about sore backs, so what can we do? B: We can give them new lightweight bags that weigh less than one kilogram when empty, so they will carry much less weight during long workdays.","t":"A：我們航空公司的空服員每天都要提著包包走過很長的機場，很多人抱怨背痛，我們能怎麼做？ B：我們可以發給他們空包重量不到一公斤的新款【輕量】包包，這樣他們在漫長的工作日中就能少背很多重量。"},{"w":"spacious","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of room inside","c":"寬敞的；容量大的","s":"A: I am going to Singapore for a week-long sales conference, and I need to bring business suits, product samples, and a laptop, so will my small bag be enough? B: No, you will need a more spacious suitcase, because the samples take up a lot of room, and you may also bring back gifts from the clients.","t":"A：我要去新加坡參加為期一週的業務會議，需要帶西裝、產品樣品和筆電，我的小包包夠用嗎？ B：不夠，你需要一個更【寬敞】的行李箱，因為樣品很佔空間，而且你可能還會帶客戶送的禮物回來。"},{"w":"compact","p":"adj.","d":"small and using little space","c":"小巧的；輕巧的","s":"A: Many young office workers in Taipei ride scooters to work, and they say large bags are hard to store under the seat, so what product should we design for them? B: We should design a compact bag that fits easily under a scooter seat but still holds a tablet, a wallet, and a raincoat.","t":"A：台北很多年輕上班族騎機車通勤，他們說大包包很難放進座墊下，我們該為他們設計什麼產品？ B：我們應該設計一款【小巧】的包包，能輕鬆放進機車座墊下，但還是能裝平板、皮夾和雨衣。"},{"w":"fashionable","p":"adj.","d":"popular and in a style that many people like now","c":"時髦的；流行的","s":"A: Our bags are well made and practical, but sales to young customers have been falling this year, so what do you think is the main problem? B: Young people want bags that look fashionable, so we should work with a popular designer and add brighter colors and modern shapes to our collection.","t":"A：我們的包包做工好又實用，但今年賣給年輕顧客的銷量一直下滑，你覺得主要問題是什麼？ B：年輕人想要看起來【時髦】的包包，所以我們應該和受歡迎的設計師合作，在產品系列中加入更亮的顏色和現代的造型。"},{"w":"functional","p":"adj.","d":"practical and useful, made to do a job well","c":"實用的；功能性的","s":"A: The customer survey shows that business travelers do not care much about the color of a bag, so what do they want most when they choose one? B: They want a functional bag with many pockets, a laptop section, and a charging port, because they need to work in airports and hotels.","t":"A：顧客調查顯示商務旅客不太在意包包的顏色，那他們挑選時最想要的是什麼？ B：他們想要一個【實用】的包包，有很多口袋、筆電夾層和充電孔，因為他們需要在機場和飯店工作。"},{"w":"capacity","p":"n.","d":"the amount that something can hold","c":"容量","s":"A: The hiking company wants to know which backpack it should rent to customers for the two-day mountain tour, because some customers carry a lot of clothes. B: Choose the one with a forty-liter capacity, because it holds clothes, food, and water for two days, but it is still light enough for most people.","t":"A：登山公司想知道兩天山區行程該出租哪一款背包給客人，因為有些客人會帶很多衣服。 B：選四十公升【容量】的那一款，因為它能裝兩天份的衣服、食物和水，而且對大多數人來說還是夠輕。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in a neat and useful way","c":"整理；收納","s":"A: My bag is always so messy that I cannot find my pens, business cards, or keys when a client is waiting, and it makes me look unprofessional. B: You should organize your things with small pouches, putting each type of item in its own place, so you can find anything in a few seconds.","t":"A：我的包包總是很亂，客戶在等的時候我都找不到筆、名片或鑰匙，讓我看起來很不專業。 B：你應該用小收納袋來【整理】你的東西，把每一類物品放在固定的位置，這樣幾秒鐘就能找到任何東西。"},{"w":"carry","p":"v.","d":"to hold something and take it with you","c":"攜帶；拿","s":"A: The new rules at the factory say that workers cannot bring large bags onto the production floor, so where should they keep their personal things? B: They can only carry a small clear bag with their phone and water bottle, and everything else must stay in the lockers near the main entrance.","t":"A：工廠的新規定說工人不能帶大包包進入生產區，那他們的私人物品要放哪裡？ B：他們只能【攜帶】一個裝手機和水壺的小透明袋，其他東西都必須放在大門附近的置物櫃裡。"},{"w":"pack","p":"v.","d":"to put things into a bag or suitcase for a trip","c":"打包；收拾（行李）","s":"A: My flight to Tokyo leaves at seven tomorrow morning, and I still have a lot of work to finish at the office tonight, so when will I have time to get ready? B: You should pack your suitcase as soon as you get home, before you do anything else, so you can sleep early and not forget anything important.","t":"A：我飛東京的班機明天早上七點起飛，今晚在辦公室還有很多工作要做，我什麼時候才有時間準備？ B：你一到家就應該先【打包】行李，再做其他事，這樣你才能早點睡，也不會忘記任何重要的東西。"},{"w":"travel","p":"v.","d":"to go from one place to another, especially far away","c":"旅行；出差","s":"A: Our sales manager is going to Japan, Korea, and Thailand in two weeks, and she will only have one bag, so what kind should she take? B: She will travel light with a carry-on suitcase, because she can take it on the plane and avoid waiting at baggage claim in every airport.","t":"A：我們業務經理兩週後要去日本、韓國和泰國，她只會帶一個包包，她該帶哪一種？ B：她會帶一個登機箱輕裝【出差】，因為可以帶上飛機，在每個機場都不必等行李。"},{"w":"reusable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used again and again","c":"可重複使用的","s":"A: The supermarket wants to stop giving out plastic bags next year, but some shoppers may be unhappy about it, so how can we help them change their habits? B: We can sell cheap reusable bags near the checkout and give a small discount to customers who bring their own bags from home.","t":"A：超市明年想停止提供塑膠袋，但有些購物者可能會不高興，我們要怎麼幫助他們改變習慣？ B：我們可以在結帳處附近販售便宜的【可重複使用】購物袋，並給自己從家裡帶袋子的顧客小折扣。"},{"w":"handle","p":"n.","d":"the part of a bag that you hold in your hand","c":"提把；把手","s":"A: The new shopping bags for our bakery look beautiful, but several customers said they broke when they carried heavy cakes home, so what went wrong? B: The paper handle is too thin for heavy boxes, so we should ask the printing company to use stronger rope instead.","t":"A：我們麵包店的新購物袋看起來很漂亮，但有幾位顧客說提重蛋糕回家時袋子壞了，問題出在哪裡？ B：紙製【提把】對重的盒子來說太薄了，所以我們應該請印刷公司改用比較堅固的繩子。"},{"w":"secure","p":"adj.","d":"safe and protected from being opened or stolen","c":"安全的；牢固的","s":"A: Many tourists in our city have complained about pickpockets in crowded night markets, so what kind of bag should our travel shop recommend to them? B: We should recommend a secure bag with hidden zippers and a lock, so thieves cannot open it easily while people are walking through crowds.","t":"A：我們城市很多觀光客抱怨在擁擠的夜市遇到扒手，我們旅行用品店應該推薦他們什麼樣的包包？ B：我們應該推薦有隱藏式拉鍊和鎖的【安全】包包，這樣人們走在人群中時，小偷就不容易打開。"}]},{"unit":23,"theme":"Baking 烘焙","cards":[{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤；烘焙","s":"A: Our café has been buying cakes from a big factory, but customers say they do not taste fresh, so what can we do to improve them? B: We could hire a pastry chef to bake cakes in our own kitchen every morning, so customers can enjoy fresh cakes and smell them as soon as they walk in.","t":"A：我們咖啡廳一直向大工廠買蛋糕，但顧客說吃起來不新鮮，我們能怎麼改善？ B：我們可以聘請一位甜點師每天早上在自己的廚房【烘烤】蛋糕，讓顧客能吃到新鮮的蛋糕，一走進來就聞得到香味。"},{"w":"oven","p":"n.","d":"a box-shaped machine that heats and cooks food inside","c":"烤箱","s":"A: The bakery is getting more and more orders for birthday cakes, but the bakers can only make ten cakes at a time, so how can we increase production? B: We should buy a second large oven, because then the bakers can cook twenty cakes at the same time and finish all the orders before noon.","t":"A：麵包店接到的生日蛋糕訂單越來越多，但烘焙師一次只能做十個，我們要怎麼提高產量？ B：我們應該再買一台大型【烤箱】，這樣烘焙師就能同時烤二十個蛋糕，在中午前完成所有訂單。"},{"w":"dough","p":"n.","d":"a thick mix of flour and water used to make bread","c":"麵團","s":"A: The new pizza restaurant near our office is always full at lunchtime, and people say the pizza base is soft but crispy, so what is their secret? B: The owner told me they make the dough by hand every night and let it rest in the fridge for twenty-four hours before they use it.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近的新披薩店午餐時總是客滿，大家都說餅皮又軟又脆，他們的秘訣是什麼？ B：老闆告訴我，他們每天晚上手工製作【麵團】，並讓它在冰箱裡靜置二十四小時後才使用。"},{"w":"batter","p":"n.","d":"a liquid mix of flour, eggs, and milk used for cakes or pancakes","c":"麵糊","s":"A: The breakfast shop is going to start selling pancakes next month, but the cooks are worried that they will be too slow during the morning rush, so what can they do? B: They can prepare the batter the night before and keep it in the fridge, so in the morning they only need to pour it onto the hot pan.","t":"A：早餐店下個月要開始賣鬆餅，但廚師擔心早上尖峰時段會做得太慢，他們能怎麼辦？ B：他們可以前一天晚上先準備好【麵糊】放在冰箱，這樣早上只要倒在熱鍋上就好。"},{"w":"flour","p":"n.","d":"a powder made from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","c":"麵粉","s":"A: The price of our bread has gone up twice this year, and some customers have started to complain, so why are our costs rising so fast? B: The price of flour has risen because of the bad wheat harvest in several countries, and it is the main ingredient in almost everything we bake.","t":"A：我們的麵包今年漲價兩次了，有些顧客開始抱怨，為什麼我們的成本漲得這麼快？ B：因為好幾個國家小麥歉收，【麵粉】的價格上漲了，而它幾乎是我們所有烘焙產品的主要原料。"},{"w":"yeast","p":"n.","d":"a substance used to make bread rise and become soft","c":"酵母","s":"A: The new baker's bread came out flat and hard this morning, and we had to throw away three trays of rolls, so what went wrong in the kitchen? B: He used old yeast that had been open for months, so the dough could not grow, and we need to check the dates on everything in the storeroom.","t":"A：新烘焙師今天早上烤出來的麵包又扁又硬，我們只好丟掉三盤餐包，廚房裡出了什麼問題？ B：他用了開封好幾個月的舊【酵母】，所以麵團發不起來，我們需要檢查儲藏室裡所有東西的日期。"},{"w":"sugar","p":"n.","d":"a sweet substance used in food and drinks","c":"糖","s":"A: Many of our customers have asked for healthier cakes because they are trying to eat better, but they still want them to taste good, so what should we change? B: We can use less sugar in our recipes and add fresh fruit instead, because the fruit makes the cakes sweet in a more natural way.","t":"A：很多顧客要求更健康的蛋糕，因為他們想吃得更好，但還是希望好吃，我們該改什麼？ B：我們可以在食譜中少用一點【糖】，改加新鮮水果，因為水果能讓蛋糕以更自然的方式變甜。"},{"w":"butter","p":"n.","d":"a soft yellow food made from cream","c":"奶油","s":"A: Our croissants are much more expensive than the ones at the supermarket, and some customers ask why they should pay more, so what should we tell them? B: Tell them we use real French butter, which gives our croissants their rich taste and many light, flaky layers that cheap ones do not have.","t":"A：我們的可頌比超市的貴很多，有些顧客問為什麼要多付錢，我們該怎麼告訴他們？ B：告訴他們我們用的是真正的法國【奶油】，讓我們的可頌有濃郁的風味和許多輕盈酥脆的層次，這是便宜可頌沒有的。"},{"w":"mix","p":"v.","d":"to put different things together and stir them","c":"混合；攪拌","s":"A: The new kitchen helper is making cookies for the first time, and she is not sure what to do after measuring all the ingredients, so can you help her? B: Tell her to mix the butter and sugar first until they are soft and smooth, and then slowly add the eggs and the flour.","t":"A：新來的廚房助手第一次做餅乾，她量好所有材料後不確定接下來要做什麼，你能幫她嗎？ B：告訴她先把奶油和糖【攪拌】到柔軟滑順，然後再慢慢加入蛋和麵粉。"},{"w":"knead","p":"v.","d":"to press and fold dough again and again with your hands","c":"揉（麵團）","s":"A: The bakery is thinking about buying a large machine for making bread dough, but it costs a lot of money, so is it really worth it? B: Yes, because our bakers spend almost two hours every morning trying to knead the dough by hand, and the machine can do the same job in fifteen minutes.","t":"A：麵包店考慮買一台製作麵團的大型機器，但要花很多錢，真的值得嗎？ B：值得，因為我們的烘焙師每天早上要花將近兩小時用手【揉】麵團，而機器只要十五分鐘就能做好同樣的工作。"},{"w":"rise","p":"v.","d":"(of bread dough) to get bigger because of yeast","c":"（麵團）發酵膨脹","s":"A: Why do the bakers come to work at four o'clock in the morning, when the shop does not open until seven thirty? B: The bread dough needs about two hours to rise before it goes into the oven, so they must start very early to have fresh bread ready when customers arrive.","t":"A：店裡七點半才開門，為什麼烘焙師凌晨四點就要來上班？ B：麵團進烤箱前大約需要兩個小時【發酵膨脹】，所以他們必須很早開始，才能在顧客到來時準備好新鮮麵包。"},{"w":"proof","p":"v.","d":"to let bread dough rest so it can grow before baking","c":"（使麵團）醒發；發酵","s":"A: Our kitchen is very cold in winter, and the bread has been coming out smaller and heavier than usual, so how can we fix this problem? B: We can buy a warm cabinet to proof the dough at the right temperature, so it grows properly before baking even on the coldest mornings.","t":"A：我們的廚房冬天很冷，烤出來的麵包比平常小又重，要怎麼解決這個問題？ B：我們可以買一個保溫櫃，讓麵團在適當溫度下【醒發】，這樣即使在最冷的早晨，它也能在烘烤前好好膨脹。"},{"w":"preheat","p":"v.","d":"to heat an oven to the right temperature before cooking","c":"預熱","s":"A: The cookies from the new baker's first tray were pale and soft in the middle, but the second tray was perfect, so why did that happen? B: He forgot to preheat the oven before he put in the first tray, so the cookies started baking at a low temperature and did not cook evenly.","t":"A：新烘焙師第一盤餅乾顏色很淡、中間軟軟的，但第二盤卻很完美，為什麼會這樣？ B：他放第一盤之前忘了【預熱】烤箱，所以餅乾一開始是在低溫下烤，沒有烤得均勻。"},{"w":"pan","p":"n.","d":"a metal container used for baking or cooking","c":"烤盤；平底鍋","s":"A: Customers say our cakes sometimes break into pieces when we take them out for decorating, and we have wasted a lot of cakes this month, so what is the problem? B: We should put baking paper in each pan before we pour in the batter, so the cakes come out easily without sticking.","t":"A：顧客說我們的蛋糕在取出來裝飾時有時會碎掉，這個月我們浪費了很多蛋糕，問題出在哪？ B：我們應該在倒入麵糊前在每個【烤盤】裡鋪烘焙紙，這樣蛋糕就能輕鬆取出而不會沾黏。"},{"w":"measure","p":"v.","d":"to find the exact amount or size of something","c":"測量；量","s":"A: Our cakes taste a little different every day, and some customers have noticed it, so how can we make sure they always taste the same? B: Every baker must measure each ingredient with a digital scale instead of using cups or spoons, because even small differences can change the taste.","t":"A：我們的蛋糕每天吃起來都有點不一樣，有些顧客也注意到了，要怎麼確保味道始終如一？ B：每位烘焙師都必須用電子秤來【量】每一樣材料，而不是用量杯或湯匙，因為即使是小小的差異也會改變味道。"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"a set of instructions for making a type of food","c":"食譜；配方","s":"A: Our pineapple cakes have been the most popular gift in the shop for twenty years, and a large company wants to buy our business, so what do they really want? B: They mainly want our secret recipe, because it was created by the owner's grandmother, and no other bakery knows exactly how to make the filling.","t":"A：我們的鳳梨酥二十年來都是店裡最受歡迎的伴手禮，有家大公司想收購我們，他們真正想要的是什麼？ B：他們主要是想要我們的秘密【配方】，因為那是老闆的祖母創造的，沒有其他麵包店知道內餡確切的做法。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way food feels in your mouth","c":"口感；質地","s":"A: The test group liked the taste of our new rice bread, but some people said it was a little too sticky, so what should we change? B: We can add a little more wheat flour to make the texture lighter and softer, and then we will ask the group to try it again next week.","t":"A：試吃小組喜歡我們新米麵包的味道，但有些人說有點太黏，我們該改什麼？ B：我們可以多加一點小麥麵粉，讓【口感】更輕盈柔軟，然後下週再請試吃小組試一次。"},{"w":"crust","p":"n.","d":"the hard outside part of bread or a pie","c":"（麵包或派的）外皮","s":"A: The French customer who comes in every morning said our baguettes are good, but not quite like the ones in Paris, so what is different? B: She wants a harder and crispier crust, so we should bake the bread a little longer at a higher temperature and add steam at the beginning.","t":"A：每天早上來的那位法國顧客說我們的法國長棍不錯，但不太像巴黎的，有什麼不一樣？ B：她想要更硬更脆的【外皮】，所以我們應該用稍高的溫度烤久一點，並在一開始加入蒸氣。"},{"w":"crumb","p":"n.","d":"a very small piece of bread or cake; also the soft inside of bread","c":"麵包屑；麵包內部組織","s":"A: The cleaning staff say there is a lot of mess under the tables in our café every evening, and it takes them a long time to clean, so what is causing it? B: Every small crumb from the croissants falls on the floor, so we should serve them on larger plates and give customers more napkins.","t":"A：清潔人員說每天晚上咖啡廳桌子底下都很髒亂，要花很多時間清理，是什麼造成的？ B：可頌的每一小片【碎屑】都會掉到地上，所以我們應該用比較大的盤子盛裝，並給顧客多一點餐巾紙。"},{"w":"golden","p":"adj.","d":"having a warm yellow-brown color, like gold","c":"金黃色的","s":"A: How do the bakers know exactly when the egg tarts are ready to come out of the oven, because they do not use a timer? B: They watch the tops carefully, and when the pastry turns golden brown and the filling stops moving, they take the tray out right away.","t":"A：烘焙師沒有用計時器，他們怎麼知道蛋塔什麼時候可以出爐？ B：他們會仔細看塔的表面，當酥皮變成【金黃】褐色、內餡不再晃動時，就立刻把烤盤拿出來。"},{"w":"moist","p":"adj.","d":"slightly wet in a pleasant way, not dry","c":"濕潤的","s":"A: Several customers wrote online that our chocolate cake was too dry last week, and our rating dropped a little, so what should we do about it? B: We can add more butter and a little yogurt to keep the cake moist, and we should also store it in a sealed box instead of on the open shelf.","t":"A：上週有好幾位顧客在網路上留言說我們的巧克力蛋糕太乾，我們的評分也下降了一點，該怎麼辦？ B：我們可以多加點奶油和一些優格讓蛋糕保持【濕潤】，也應該把它存放在密封盒裡，而不是放在開放的架子上。"},{"w":"fluffy","p":"adj.","d":"soft, light, and full of air","c":"鬆軟的；蓬鬆的","s":"A: The Japanese pancakes at the new café are so popular that people wait in line for an hour, so what makes them so special? B: They are very tall and fluffy, because the cooks beat the egg whites until they are full of air, and the pancakes almost shake on the plate.","t":"A：新咖啡廳的日式鬆餅超受歡迎，大家要排一個小時，它們有什麼特別之處？ B：它們又高又【蓬鬆】，因為廚師把蛋白打到充滿空氣，鬆餅放在盤子上幾乎會晃動。"},{"w":"dense","p":"adj.","d":"heavy and thick, with little air inside","c":"紮實的；密實的","s":"A: Our new whole wheat bread is healthy, but some customers say it feels too heavy, and they do not buy it again, so how can we improve it? B: The bread is too dense because whole wheat flour is heavy, so we can mix in some white flour and let the dough rise a little longer.","t":"A：我們新的全麥麵包很健康，但有些顧客說感覺太重，不會再買，我們要怎麼改善？ B：因為全麥麵粉比較重，麵包太【紮實】了，所以我們可以混入一些白麵粉，並讓麵團發酵久一點。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"having the taste of sugar","c":"甜的","s":"A: Our cakes sell very well in Japan, but the sales team in Korea says customers there think they taste too strong, so what should we change for that market? B: We can make them less sweet for Korean customers by using half the sugar, and we can add more fresh cream and fruit instead.","t":"A：我們的蛋糕在日本賣得很好，但韓國的業務團隊說當地顧客覺得味道太重，我們該為那個市場改什麼？ B：我們可以只用一半的糖，讓蛋糕對韓國顧客來說不那麼【甜】，再改加更多鮮奶油和水果。"},{"w":"savory","p":"adj.","d":"salty or spicy rather than sweet","c":"鹹的；鹹香的","s":"A: Many office workers buy breakfast at our bakery, but some of them say they get tired of sweet buns every morning, so what new products could we offer? B: We could add more savory items, such as cheese and ham rolls or tuna sandwiches, because many people prefer salty food in the morning.","t":"A：很多上班族在我們麵包店買早餐，但有些人說每天早上吃甜麵包吃膩了，我們可以推出什麼新產品？ B：我們可以增加更多【鹹的】品項，例如起司火腿捲或鮪魚三明治，因為很多人早上比較喜歡吃鹹的。"},{"w":"cool","p":"v.","d":"to become or make something less hot","c":"冷卻；放涼","s":"A: The new staff member tried to put cream on the cakes as soon as they came out of the oven, and the cream melted everywhere, so what should she do next time? B: She should let the cakes cool on a rack for at least an hour first, because cream only stays firm on a cake that is completely cold.","t":"A：新員工在蛋糕一出爐時就想抹上奶油，結果奶油融得到處都是，她下次該怎麼做？ B：她應該先讓蛋糕在架子上【放涼】至少一小時，因為奶油只有在完全冷卻的蛋糕上才能保持定型。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look nicer by adding things to it","c":"裝飾","s":"A: A large company ordered fifty cakes for its twentieth anniversary party next Friday, and they want each cake to look special, so how much time will we need? B: We need two full days to decorate the cakes with the company's logo, flowers made of sugar, and the words \"Happy 20th Anniversary\" on each one.","t":"A：一家大公司為下週五的二十週年派對訂了五十個蛋糕，他們希望每個蛋糕看起來都很特別，我們需要多少時間？ B：我們需要整整兩天，在每個蛋糕上用公司商標、糖做的花朵和「二十週年快樂」的字樣來【裝飾】。"},{"w":"icing","p":"n.","d":"a sweet mix of sugar and liquid used to cover cakes","c":"糖霜","s":"A: Children love the cupcakes at our shop, but their parents say they have too much sugar on top, so how can we make them healthier but still pretty? B: We can use a thinner layer of icing and add colorful fresh fruit on top, so the cupcakes still look fun but contain less sugar.","t":"A：小朋友很愛我們店裡的杯子蛋糕，但家長說上面的糖太多，我們要怎麼讓它更健康又一樣漂亮？ B：我們可以用薄一點的【糖霜】，再在上面放色彩繽紛的新鮮水果，這樣杯子蛋糕看起來還是很有趣，但含糖量比較少。"},{"w":"batch","p":"n.","d":"an amount of food made at one time","c":"一批","s":"A: The hotel has ordered two hundred cookies for the conference coffee break tomorrow, but our oven can only bake fifty at once, so can we finish them in time? B: Yes, each batch takes about fifteen minutes, so we can make all four in about one hour and still have time to pack them.","t":"A：飯店為明天的會議茶敘訂了兩百片餅乾，但我們的烤箱一次只能烤五十片，來得及做完嗎？ B：可以，每【一批】大約十五分鐘，所以四批大約一個小時就能做完，還有時間包裝。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong pleasant smell, especially of food","c":"香氣；香味","s":"A: Our bakery is on a busy street, but many people walk past without coming in, so how can we attract more customers without spending a lot of money on advertising? B: We can open the front door when the bread comes out of the oven, because the warm aroma of fresh bread often makes people stop and walk inside.","t":"A：我們麵包店在熱鬧的街上，但很多人經過卻沒進來，要怎麼在不花大錢打廣告的情況下吸引更多顧客？ B：我們可以在麵包出爐時打開前門，因為新鮮麵包溫暖的【香氣】常常會讓人停下腳步走進來。"}]},{"unit":24,"theme":"Bar Chart 長條圖","cards":[{"w":"axis","p":"n.","d":"a line at the side or bottom of a chart used to show values","c":"座標軸","s":"A: I am making a bar chart of our monthly sales for tomorrow's meeting, but I am not sure where to put the names of the months and the sales numbers. B: Put the months along the bottom and the sales amounts on the vertical axis, so everyone can see how high each month's bar goes.","t":"A：我正在為明天的會議做每月銷售的長條圖，但不確定月份名稱和銷售數字該放在哪裡。 B：把月份放在底部，銷售金額放在垂直【座標軸】上，這樣大家就能看出每個月的長條有多高。"},{"w":"category","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that have similar features","c":"類別；種類","s":"A: The store manager wants a chart that shows which kinds of products sold best last quarter, but we sell more than five hundred different items, so how can I make it simple? B: Put the items into groups like drinks, snacks, and frozen food, and then draw one bar for each category so the chart stays clear and easy to read.","t":"A：店長想要一張圖表顯示上一季哪些種類的商品賣得最好，但我們賣五百多種商品，要怎麼讓它簡單一點？ B：把商品分成飲料、零食和冷凍食品等組別，然後每個【類別】畫一根長條，這樣圖表就會清楚易讀。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"a number or amount shown on a chart","c":"數值","s":"A: When I showed my chart to the director, she said she could not tell the exact sales for each region just by looking at the bars, so how can I fix that? B: Write the value at the top of each bar, such as \"2.5 million,\" so she can read the exact number without guessing from the lines on the side.","t":"A：我給主任看圖表時，她說光看長條沒辦法知道每個地區確切的銷售額，我要怎麼修正？ B：在每根長條頂端寫上【數值】，例如「250萬」，這樣她不必從旁邊的格線猜，就能讀到確切的數字。"},{"w":"scale","p":"n.","d":"the set of numbers used to measure the size of things on a chart","c":"刻度；比例尺","s":"A: In my chart, the small differences between our three stores look huge, and the manager thinks the Tainan store is doing terribly, but that is not true. B: The scale on your chart starts at ninety instead of zero, so you should change it to start at zero, and the differences will look as small as they really are.","t":"A：在我的圖表裡，我們三家門市之間的小差距看起來很大，經理以為台南店表現很差，但其實不是。 B：你圖表上的【刻度】從九十開始而不是從零，你應該改成從零開始，這樣差距看起來就會和實際一樣小。"},{"w":"frequency","p":"n.","d":"how often something happens","c":"頻率；次數","s":"A: The customer service team wants to know which problems customers call about most often, so that they can train new staff better, so what chart should I make? B: Make a bar chart that shows the frequency of each type of complaint last month, so the team can see that late delivery calls happen three times more than any other.","t":"A：客服團隊想知道顧客最常為了哪些問題打電話，好更有效地訓練新員工，我該做什麼圖表？ B：做一張長條圖，顯示上個月每一種客訴的【次數】，讓團隊看到送貨延遲的電話比其他任何問題多三倍。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"A: The board wants to see whether our new advertisement worked, but they only have ten minutes for our report at the meeting, so what should I show them? B: Use one bar chart to compare sales in the three months before and after the advertisement, because the difference will be easy to see in a few seconds.","t":"A：董事會想知道我們的新廣告有沒有效，但會議上只給我們十分鐘報告，我該給他們看什麼？ B：用一張長條圖來【比較】廣告前後三個月的銷售，因為幾秒鐘內就能輕鬆看出差異。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking at things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較；對照","s":"A: Our manager asked me to show how our prices are different from those of our three main competitors, but I only have the numbers in a long table. B: Turn the table into a bar chart, because a visual comparison of prices is much easier for people to understand than a page full of numbers.","t":"A：經理要我呈現我們的價格和三家主要競爭對手有什麼不同，但我只有一張很長的數字表格。 B：把表格轉成長條圖，因為價格的視覺化【比較】比整頁數字更容易讓人理解。"},{"w":"distribution","p":"n.","d":"the way something is spread out among different groups","c":"分布","s":"A: Human resources wants to know the ages of our employees, because many senior workers may retire soon, so how should I present this information? B: Make a bar chart showing the age distribution of all staff in five-year groups, so managers can quickly see how many people are over fifty-five.","t":"A：人資部想知道員工的年齡，因為很多資深員工可能快退休了，我該怎麼呈現這些資訊？ B：做一張長條圖，以每五歲為一組顯示全體員工的年齡【分布】，讓主管能很快看出有多少人超過五十五歲。"},{"w":"label","p":"n.","d":"a word or short phrase that names part of a chart","c":"標籤；標示","s":"A: I showed my sales chart to the new interns, and none of them understood what the bars meant, even though the colors looked nice. B: You forgot to add a label under each bar, so people cannot tell which bar is for which store, and you should also give the chart a title.","t":"A：我把銷售圖表給新來的實習生看，雖然顏色很好看，但沒人看得懂那些長條代表什麼。 B：你忘了在每根長條下面加上【標籤】，所以大家分不出哪根長條是哪家門市的，你也應該幫圖表加個標題。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"a small box on a chart that explains what each color or symbol means","c":"圖例","s":"A: My chart uses blue bars for this year and gray bars for last year, but the manager asked me which color was which during the meeting, and I felt embarrassed. B: Add a small legend in the top right corner that explains each color, so people can understand the chart without asking you.","t":"A：我的圖表用藍色長條代表今年、灰色長條代表去年，但經理在會議中問我哪個顏色是哪個，讓我很難為情。 B：在右上角加一個小【圖例】說明每個顏色，這樣大家不必問你也能看懂圖表。"},{"w":"dataset","p":"n.","d":"a collection of related information, usually stored on a computer","c":"資料集","s":"A: The marketing team wants charts about customer spending for the last five years, but our sales numbers are stored in many different files, so where should I start? B: First, combine all the files into one clean dataset in a spreadsheet, and check for missing numbers before you make any charts from it.","t":"A：行銷團隊想要過去五年顧客消費的圖表，但我們的銷售數字存放在很多不同的檔案裡，我該從哪裡開始？ B：先把所有檔案整合成試算表裡一個乾淨的【資料集】，在用它做任何圖表之前，先檢查有沒有缺漏的數字。"},{"w":"variable","p":"n.","d":"a factor or quantity that can change","c":"變數；變項","s":"A: Our ice cream sales went up a lot in July, and the manager thinks it was because of our new advertisement, but I am not so sure about that. B: Temperature is another important variable, so you should show the weather data in the chart as well, because hot days usually increase ice cream sales.","t":"A：我們的冰淇淋銷量在七月大幅上升，經理認為是新廣告的關係，但我不太確定。 B：氣溫是另一個重要的【變數】，所以你也應該在圖表中呈現天氣資料，因為炎熱的天氣通常會讓冰淇淋銷量增加。"},{"w":"horizontal","p":"adj.","d":"going from side to side, flat like the ground","c":"水平的；橫向的","s":"A: The names of our product lines are very long, such as \"premium organic green tea,\" and they do not fit under the bars in my chart, so what can I do? B: Turn the chart into a horizontal bar chart, with the bars going from left to right, so the long names fit easily on the left side.","t":"A：我們的產品線名稱很長，例如「頂級有機綠茶」，在我的圖表長條下面放不下，我該怎麼辦？ B：把圖表改成【橫向】長條圖，讓長條從左往右延伸，這樣長名稱就能輕鬆放在左側。"},{"w":"vertical","p":"adj.","d":"going straight up and down","c":"垂直的；直立的","s":"A: Our designer made the sales chart with bars going up from the bottom of the page, but the director said she prefers bars that go across, so should we change it? B: For monthly sales, vertical bars are usually easier to read because time goes from left to right, so I would explain that and keep the original design.","t":"A：我們的設計師把銷售圖表做成從頁面底部往上的長條，但主任說她比較喜歡橫向的長條，我們該改嗎？ B：對每月銷售來說，【垂直】長條通常比較容易閱讀，因為時間是從左往右排列的，所以我會向她說明並保留原本的設計。"},{"w":"discrete","p":"adj.","d":"separate and different from each other","c":"離散的；個別的","s":"A: Why did you use a bar chart instead of a line chart to show sales in our five different stores, when the manager usually likes line charts? B: Because the stores are discrete groups that are not connected to each other, a line would suggest a change over time, which is not what the data shows.","t":"A：經理通常喜歡折線圖，你為什麼用長條圖而不是折線圖來呈現五家不同門市的銷售？ B：因為這些門市是彼此不相連的【個別】群組，用折線會讓人以為是隨時間的變化，但資料呈現的並不是這個。"},{"w":"magnitude","p":"n.","d":"the great size or importance of something","c":"規模；大小","s":"A: The bar for online sales is three times taller than the bar for store sales this year, and some managers were very surprised, so what does it mean? B: It shows the magnitude of the change in how customers shop, because online sales have grown much faster than anyone expected in just two years.","t":"A：今年網路銷售的長條比門市銷售高了三倍，有些經理非常驚訝，這代表什麼？ B：這顯示了顧客購物方式改變的【規模】，因為網路銷售在短短兩年內的成長速度遠超出任何人的預期。"},{"w":"proportion","p":"n.","d":"a part of a whole, often shown as a percentage","c":"比例","s":"A: The director wants to know how much of our total income comes from overseas customers, because she is planning a trip to Japan and Korea next month. B: My chart shows that a large proportion of our income, about forty percent, comes from overseas, and most of it is from Japanese customers.","t":"A：主任想知道我們總收入中有多少來自海外顧客，因為她下個月打算去日本和韓國。 B：我的圖表顯示我們收入中很大的【比例】，大約百分之四十，來自海外，其中大多數是日本顧客。"},{"w":"trend","p":"n.","d":"a general direction in which something is changing","c":"趨勢","s":"A: Our sales went up in some months and down in others this year, so the board is confused about whether the business is doing well or not. B: If you look at all five years together in one chart, the overall trend is clearly upward, even though a few months were weaker than others.","t":"A：我們今年的銷售有幾個月上升、有幾個月下降，所以董事會搞不清楚業務到底好不好。 B：如果你把五年的資料放在一張圖表裡一起看，整體【趨勢】顯然是向上的，即使有幾個月比較弱。"},{"w":"gap","p":"n.","d":"a large difference between two things","c":"差距","s":"A: The chart shows that the Taipei store sold far more than the Hualien store last year, and the manager wants to understand why the difference is so large. B: Part of the gap comes from the size of the city, but the Hualien store also has fewer staff and much shorter opening hours.","t":"A：圖表顯示台北店去年的銷量遠高於花蓮店，經理想了解為什麼差異這麼大。 B：部分【差距】來自城市的規模，但花蓮店的員工也比較少，營業時間也短得多。"},{"w":"interval","p":"n.","d":"the space between two numbers or points on a scale","c":"間隔；區間","s":"A: My chart has numbers on the side going 0, 7, 14, 21, and 28, and the manager said they are hard to read, so what numbers should I use instead? B: Use an interval of ten, with numbers like 0, 10, 20, and 30, because round numbers make it much easier to estimate the height of each bar.","t":"A：我的圖表側邊數字是0、7、14、21、28，經理說很難閱讀，我該改用什麼數字？ B：用十為一個【間隔】，像是0、10、20、30，因為整數能讓人更容易估計每根長條的高度。"},{"w":"rank","p":"v.","d":"to put things in order from highest to lowest","c":"排名；排序","s":"A: The sales director wants to see which of our twenty salespeople did best this year, but my chart puts them in alphabetical order, so is that a problem? B: Yes, it is, so you should rank them from the highest sales to the lowest, because then the top performers will appear right at the top of the chart.","t":"A：業務總監想看我們二十位業務員中今年誰表現最好，但我的圖表是按字母順序排列，這樣有問題嗎？ B：有，你應該把他們從銷售最高到最低【排序】，這樣表現最好的人就會出現在圖表最上方。"},{"w":"highlight","p":"v.","d":"to make something easy to notice","c":"突顯；強調","s":"A: My chart shows sales for all twelve products, but I really want the board to notice that our new green tea drink sold the most, so how can I do that? B: You can highlight that bar in bright orange and make all the other bars light gray, so their eyes will go straight to the green tea.","t":"A：我的圖表呈現了全部十二項產品的銷售，但我真的希望董事會注意到我們新的綠茶飲料賣得最多，要怎麼做？ B：你可以用亮橘色【突顯】那根長條，把其他長條都改成淺灰色，這樣他們的目光就會直接落在綠茶上。"},{"w":"summary","p":"n.","d":"a short statement of the main points","c":"摘要；總結","s":"A: The president will only look at my report for a few minutes before her flight to Singapore this afternoon, so what should I put on the first page? B: Put a short summary of the main results with one simple bar chart, so she can understand the key points even if she does not read the rest.","t":"A：總裁今天下午搭機去新加坡前只會看我的報告幾分鐘，我第一頁該放什麼？ B：放一段主要結果的簡短【摘要】，再搭配一張簡單的長條圖，這樣即使她沒讀其他部分，也能了解重點。"},{"w":"baseline","p":"n.","d":"a starting point used to compare later changes","c":"基準；基線","s":"A: We started a new training program for the sales team in March, and the manager wants to know if it really made a difference to their results. B: Use the sales in February as the baseline, and then show each month after that in the chart, so everyone can see how much sales grew after the training.","t":"A：我們三月為業務團隊開辦了新的培訓課程，經理想知道它是否真的對業績有影響。 B：以二月的銷售作為【基準】，然後在圖表中呈現之後的每個月，讓大家看出培訓後銷售成長了多少。"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference that is easy to see","c":"對比；差異","s":"A: The bars for 2025 and 2026 in my chart are light blue and slightly darker blue, and people say they look almost the same on the projector screen. B: Use colors with more contrast, such as dark blue and orange, so the two years are easy to tell apart, even in a bright meeting room.","t":"A：我圖表中2025年和2026年的長條是淺藍色和稍深的藍色，大家說在投影幕上看起來幾乎一樣。 B：用【對比】更強的顏色，例如深藍和橘色，這樣即使在明亮的會議室裡也很容易分辨這兩年。"},{"w":"clarity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand","c":"清晰；清楚","s":"A: My chart has a 3D design, shadows, and many different colors, and I think it looks very modern, but the director did not seem to like it. B: She cares more about clarity than style, so you should use a simple flat design with only two colors, so the numbers are easy to understand.","t":"A：我的圖表有立體設計、陰影和很多不同顏色，我覺得看起來很現代，但主任似乎不喜歡。 B：她比較在意【清晰度】而不是風格，所以你應該用只有兩種顏色的簡單平面設計，讓數字容易理解。"},{"w":"color","p":"n.","d":"red, blue, green, and so on","c":"顏色","s":"A: The marketing report has five charts, and each one uses different colors for the same three products, so the readers keep getting confused. B: Give each product one color and use it in every chart, for example green for tea and brown for coffee, so readers recognize them right away.","t":"A：行銷報告有五張圖表，每張都用不同顏色代表同樣的三項產品，讓讀者一直搞混。 B：每項產品都給一種【顏色】，並在每張圖表中使用，例如綠色代表茶、棕色代表咖啡，讓讀者馬上就能認出來。"},{"w":"measure","p":"v.","d":"to find out the size or amount of something","c":"衡量；測量","s":"A: The manager wants a chart to show whether our customers are happier with our service this year, but happiness is not a number, so how can we show it? B: We can measure customer satisfaction with a short online survey that asks people to score our service from one to ten after each visit.","t":"A：經理想要一張圖表顯示今年顧客是否對我們的服務更滿意，但滿意度不是數字，要怎麼呈現？ B：我們可以用簡短的線上問卷來【衡量】顧客滿意度，請顧客在每次光顧後為我們的服務打一到十分。"},{"w":"insight","p":"n.","d":"a clear, deep understanding of something","c":"洞察；深入了解","s":"A: The chart shows that most of our customers shop late at night, which nobody in the company expected, so how can this help our business? B: It gives us a useful insight into our customers' habits, so we can send special offers in the evening and keep our online help desk open later.","t":"A：圖表顯示我們大多數顧客都在深夜購物，公司裡沒人預料到，這對我們的業務有什麼幫助？ B：它讓我們對顧客的習慣有了有用的【深入了解】，所以我們可以在晚上發送特別優惠，並延長線上客服的服務時間。"}]},{"unit":25,"theme":"Barbecue 烤肉","cards":[{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to cook food on metal bars over strong heat","c":"燒烤；炙烤","s":"A: Our company is holding a Moon Festival party on the rooftop this year, and the manager wants everyone to cook together, so what food should we prepare? B: Let's buy plenty of meat, corn, and mushrooms so everyone can grill their own food, and we can also order some mooncakes and fruit for dessert.","t":"A：公司今年要在頂樓舉辦中秋派對，經理希望大家一起烤肉，我們該準備什麼食物？ B：我們買很多肉、玉米和香菇，讓大家可以自己【燒烤】食物，也可以訂些月餅和水果當甜點。"},{"w":"smoke","p":"n.","d":"the gray cloud that comes from something burning","c":"煙","s":"A: The neighbors in the apartment building next to our restaurant have complained to the city about our outdoor grill, so what exactly is the problem? B: Too much smoke from the grill is blowing into their windows in the evening, so we need to install a better fan and move the grill to the other side.","t":"A：我們餐廳隔壁公寓大樓的住戶向市政府投訴我們的戶外烤爐，問題到底是什麼？ B：晚上烤爐冒出太多【煙】吹進他們的窗戶，所以我們需要裝一台更好的抽風機，並把烤爐移到另一邊。"},{"w":"charcoal","p":"n.","d":"black material made from burnt wood, used as fuel for grilling","c":"木炭","s":"A: We are planning a barbecue at the beach for our clients next Saturday, but the beach has no electricity, so how are we going to cook all the food? B: We will use charcoal in three large grills, so please buy about ten bags, some lighters, and a few buckets of water for safety.","t":"A：我們計畫下週六在海邊為客戶舉辦烤肉，但海灘沒有電，我們要怎麼煮那麼多食物？ B：我們會在三個大烤爐裡用【木炭】，所以請你買大約十袋，再準備一些打火機和幾桶水以策安全。"},{"w":"flame","p":"n.","d":"the hot, bright light that comes from a fire","c":"火焰","s":"A: The steaks at the staff barbecue were black on the outside but raw in the middle, and some people did not want to eat them, so what went wrong? B: The flame was too high and touched the meat directly, so next time we should wait until the fire burns down and the coals turn white.","t":"A：員工烤肉時牛排外面焦黑、裡面卻是生的，有些人都不想吃，出了什麼問題？ B：【火焰】太高，直接碰到了肉，所以下次我們應該等火勢變小、炭變白之後再烤。"},{"w":"marinate","p":"v.","d":"to leave meat or fish in a mix of oil, spices, and sauce before cooking","c":"醃製；浸泡","s":"A: The chicken we grilled at last year's company barbecue was dry and did not have much taste, and many people left it on their plates. B: This year we should marinate the chicken in soy sauce, garlic, and honey the night before, so it will be soft and full of flavor.","t":"A：去年公司烤肉時我們烤的雞肉又乾又沒什麼味道，很多人都剩在盤子上。 B：今年我們應該前一晚用醬油、大蒜和蜂蜜【醃】雞肉，這樣它就會柔軟又充滿風味。"},{"w":"seasoning","p":"n.","d":"salt, pepper, herbs, or spices added to food for flavor","c":"調味料","s":"A: The new barbecue restaurant wants its meat to taste special, so that customers will remember it and come back again, but it does not want to use heavy sauces. B: The chef created a secret seasoning of sea salt, black pepper, and dried herbs from Hualien, which he puts on the meat just before grilling.","t":"A：那家新的燒烤餐廳想讓肉吃起來很特別，讓顧客記住並再次光臨，但又不想用很重的醬汁。 B：主廚調配了一款秘製【調味料】，有海鹽、黑胡椒和花蓮的乾燥香草，他會在燒烤前才撒在肉上。"},{"w":"rub","p":"n.","d":"a dry mix of spices pressed onto meat before cooking","c":"乾醃料；香料粉","s":"A: The American customers who visited our restaurant last week said our ribs tasted good, but they missed the strong flavor of barbecue from their home in Texas. B: We could try a spicy rub made of brown sugar, paprika, and garlic powder, which we press into the meat several hours before we cook it.","t":"A：上週來我們餐廳的美國顧客說我們的肋排好吃，但他們想念家鄉德州烤肉的濃郁風味。 B：我們可以試試用紅糖、紅椒粉和蒜粉做成的辣味【乾醃料】，在烹調前幾小時把它抹進肉裡。"},{"w":"sauce","p":"n.","d":"a thick liquid served with or on food","c":"醬汁；烤肉醬","s":"A: We are selling grilled meat at the night market for our company's charity event, and many visitors have asked whether we have anything to add more taste. B: We should put bottles of sweet barbecue sauce on every table, because in Taiwan most people like to brush it on grilled meat and corn.","t":"A：我們在夜市為公司慈善活動賣烤肉，很多遊客問有沒有可以增添風味的東西。 B：我們應該在每張桌子上放幾瓶甜的烤肉【醬】，因為在台灣大多數人喜歡把它刷在烤肉和玉米上。"},{"w":"slow-cook","p":"v.","d":"to cook food for a long time at a low temperature","c":"慢燉；低溫慢煮","s":"A: The beef at the new barbecue restaurant is so soft that you can cut it with a spoon, and customers wait over an hour for a table, so how do they do it? B: The chefs slow-cook the beef for twelve hours at a low temperature, so the meat becomes very soft and takes in all the smoky flavor.","t":"A：那家新烤肉餐廳的牛肉軟到可以用湯匙切開，顧客要等一個多小時才有位子，他們是怎麼做到的？ B：廚師用低溫把牛肉【慢煮】十二個小時，讓肉變得非常軟嫩，並吸收所有煙燻風味。"},{"w":"tender","p":"adj.","d":"soft and easy to cut and chew","c":"軟嫩的","s":"A: Several customers wrote online that our steak was too tough and hard to chew, and our restaurant's rating dropped this month, so what should we do? B: We should buy better beef and let it rest for a few minutes after grilling, because that keeps the meat tender and easy to cut.","t":"A：好幾位顧客在網路上留言說我們的牛排太硬、很難咀嚼，餐廳這個月的評分也下降了，我們該怎麼做？ B：我們應該買品質更好的牛肉，並在烤好後讓它靜置幾分鐘，因為這能讓肉保持【軟嫩】又容易切。"},{"w":"juicy","p":"adj.","d":"containing a lot of liquid in a way that tastes good","c":"多汁的","s":"A: Our new burger is selling very well, and a food blogger even wrote that it was the best in Taipei, so what makes it so popular with customers? B: The meat stays juicy because we grill it quickly over high heat, and people love the way the flavor fills their mouths with every bite.","t":"A：我們的新漢堡賣得很好，有位美食部落客甚至寫說那是台北最好吃的，是什麼讓它這麼受顧客歡迎？ B：肉能保持【多汁】是因為我們用大火快速燒烤，大家都很喜歡每一口都滿嘴風味的感覺。"},{"w":"smoky","p":"adj.","d":"tasting or smelling of smoke","c":"煙燻味的","s":"A: Our sausages taste fine, but the customers at the food fair said they wanted something that really tastes like a real outdoor barbecue, so how can we do that? B: We can cook them over apple wood for an hour, which gives them a rich, smoky flavor that people usually only get from cooking outside.","t":"A：我們的香腸味道還不錯，但美食展的顧客說想要真正像戶外烤肉那樣的味道，我們要怎麼做？ B：我們可以用蘋果木烤一個小時，讓它們有濃郁的【煙燻】風味，這通常只有在戶外烹調才吃得到。"},{"w":"grill marks","p":"n.phr.","d":"dark lines left on food by the hot metal bars of a grill","c":"烤痕；烤紋","s":"A: The photographer for our restaurant's new menu says the grilled chicken in the photos looks pale and not very attractive, so how can we make it look better? B: The chef can press the chicken onto a very hot grill for one minute to make dark grill marks, because those lines show customers that the meat is freshly grilled.","t":"A：我們餐廳新菜單的攝影師說照片裡的烤雞看起來很蒼白、不太吸引人，我們要怎麼讓它更好看？ B：主廚可以把雞肉壓在很燙的烤架上一分鐘，烤出深色的【烤痕】，因為這些紋路能讓顧客知道肉是現烤的。"},{"w":"skewer","p":"n.","d":"a long thin stick used to hold pieces of food for cooking","c":"烤肉串籤；串燒","s":"A: About two hundred guests are coming to our company's outdoor party, and we do not have enough plates or forks, so what kind of food should we serve? B: Let's serve meat and vegetables on a bamboo skewer, because guests can hold the stick and eat while they walk around and talk to each other.","t":"A：公司的戶外派對大約有兩百位賓客，我們的盤子和叉子不夠，該提供什麼樣的食物？ B：我們把肉和蔬菜串在竹【籤】上吧，因為賓客可以拿著竹籤邊走邊吃，同時和彼此聊天。"},{"w":"patty","p":"n.","d":"a flat round piece of chopped meat, often used in burgers","c":"肉餅；漢堡肉","s":"A: Our fast-food restaurant wants to add a vegetarian burger to the menu next month, because more and more young customers are asking for one. B: We can make a patty from beans, mushrooms, and rice, and grill it just like a beef one, so it looks and feels like a normal burger.","t":"A：我們速食店下個月想在菜單上加一款素食漢堡，因為越來越多年輕顧客在要求。 B：我們可以用豆子、香菇和米做成【肉餅】，然後像牛肉餅一樣燒烤，讓它看起來、吃起來都像一般的漢堡。"},{"w":"sausage","p":"n.","d":"chopped meat with spices inside a long thin skin","c":"香腸","s":"A: Many foreign visitors to our night market tour want to try a typical Taiwanese barbecue snack, so what is the best thing for our guides to recommend? B: They should try the sweet grilled pork sausage with a piece of raw garlic, because it is cheap, popular, and very different from the ones in Europe.","t":"A：參加我們夜市導覽的很多外國遊客都想嚐嚐典型的台灣烤肉小吃，導遊最適合推薦什麼？ B：他們應該試試甜甜的烤豬肉【香腸】配一瓣生蒜，因為它便宜、受歡迎，而且和歐洲的很不一樣。"},{"w":"brisket","p":"n.","d":"meat from the lower chest of a cow, often cooked slowly","c":"牛胸肉","s":"A: The new Texas-style restaurant only serves one main meat dish, but it sells out by two o'clock every afternoon, so what is so special about it? B: It serves smoked brisket, which is a cut of beef from the chest that the cooks smoke for fifteen hours until it becomes very soft.","t":"A：那家新的德州風味餐廳只賣一道主菜肉類，但每天下午兩點就賣完了，到底有什麼特別？ B：它賣的是煙燻【牛胸肉】，這是來自胸部的牛肉部位，廚師要煙燻十五個小時直到它變得非常軟嫩。"},{"w":"rib","p":"n.","d":"one of the curved bones of the chest; meat cut with this bone","c":"肋排；肋骨","s":"A: Our restaurant's barbecue platter is the most expensive item on the menu, so customers sometimes ask what they will get if they order it. B: Tell them it includes chicken wings, sausages, and a large pork rib with honey sauce, which is enough for three or four people to share.","t":"A：我們餐廳的烤肉拼盤是菜單上最貴的品項，所以顧客有時會問點了會吃到什麼。 B：告訴他們有雞翅、香腸和一大份蜂蜜醬豬【肋排】，夠三、四個人分享。"},{"w":"baste","p":"v.","d":"to pour or brush liquid over meat while it is cooking","c":"（烹調時）塗油；淋汁","s":"A: The roast chicken at our company's Christmas dinner was very dry last year, and the hotel chef wants to make sure it does not happen again. B: He plans to baste the chickens with melted butter and their own juices every twenty minutes while they cook, so the meat stays soft.","t":"A：去年公司聖誕晚宴的烤雞非常乾，飯店主廚想確保這種事不會再發生。 B：他打算在烤雞時每二十分鐘用融化的奶油和雞肉本身的肉汁幫雞【淋汁】，讓肉保持軟嫩。"},{"w":"flip","p":"v.","d":"to turn something over quickly","c":"翻面；翻動","s":"A: I am cooking the burgers at our team barbecue this afternoon, but I have never done it before, and I am worried that I will burn them in front of everyone. B: Do not worry, just flip each burger once after about four minutes, and do not press it down, so the juice stays inside the meat.","t":"A：今天下午團隊烤肉由我負責烤漢堡肉，但我從來沒烤過，擔心會在大家面前烤焦。 B：別擔心，大約四分鐘後把每片漢堡肉【翻面】一次就好，也不要往下壓，這樣肉汁才會留在肉裡。"},{"w":"coal","p":"n.","d":"a hard black material that is burned for heat","c":"煤炭；炭火","s":"A: How do the cooks at the barbecue restaurant know when the grill is hot enough to start cooking the meat, because they do not use a thermometer? B: They wait until every piece of coal is covered with white ash and glowing red underneath, which usually takes about twenty minutes after they light it.","t":"A：燒烤餐廳的廚師不用溫度計，他們怎麼知道烤爐熱到可以開始烤肉了？ B：他們會等到每一塊【炭】都覆蓋白色灰燼、底下發出紅光，點火後通常大約需要二十分鐘。"},{"w":"outdoor","p":"adj.","d":"happening or used outside, not in a building","c":"戶外的","s":"A: Our staff have been working hard all year, and the manager wants to plan a fun event in the spring where people can relax and enjoy the fresh air. B: Let's hold an outdoor barbecue at the riverside park, where there are tables, grills, and plenty of space for games and music.","t":"A：我們員工一整年都很努力工作，經理想在春天規劃一個有趣的活動，讓大家放鬆並享受新鮮空氣。 B：我們在河濱公園辦一場【戶外】烤肉吧，那裡有桌子、烤爐，還有很多空間可以玩遊戲和放音樂。"},{"w":"picnic","p":"n.","d":"a meal eaten outside, often in a park","c":"野餐","s":"A: The weather is going to be warm and sunny this Saturday, and our team has finished the big project early, so how should we celebrate together? B: Let's have a picnic in Daan Park, where everyone can bring some food, sit on blankets under the trees, and play games.","t":"A：這週六天氣會很溫暖晴朗，我們團隊也提早完成了大專案，我們該怎麼一起慶祝？ B：我們去大安森林公園【野餐】吧，大家可以帶些食物，在樹下鋪墊子坐著玩遊戲。"},{"w":"platter","p":"n.","d":"a large plate used for serving food","c":"大淺盤；拼盤","s":"A: Our sales team is meeting a group of clients at the barbecue restaurant tonight, and there will be ten people, so should each person order a separate dish? B: It is easier to order a large mixed platter for the table, because it comes with beef, pork, chicken, and vegetables, and everyone can share.","t":"A：我們業務團隊今晚要在燒烤餐廳和一群客戶見面，總共十個人，每個人應該各點一道菜嗎？ B：幫整桌點一份大的綜合【拼盤】比較簡單，因為裡面有牛肉、豬肉、雞肉和蔬菜，大家都可以分享。"},{"w":"sizzle","p":"v.","d":"to make a hissing sound like food cooking in hot oil","c":"（煎炸時）發出嘶嘶聲","s":"A: The advertising agency wants our new TV commercial for the barbecue restaurant to make people feel hungry right away, so what should it show? B: It should show steaks as they sizzle on a hot grill, because the sound and the smoke make people imagine the smell and taste of the meat.","t":"A：廣告公司希望我們燒烤餐廳的新電視廣告能讓人立刻覺得餓，廣告應該呈現什麼？ B：應該呈現牛排在熱烤架上【滋滋作響】的畫面，因為那聲音和煙會讓人想像到肉的香味和滋味。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong pleasant smell, especially of food","c":"香氣；香味","s":"A: Our barbecue stall is hidden at the back of the night market, and many visitors do not see it, so how can we attract more customers to our stall? B: We can place the grill near the walkway, because the aroma of grilled meat and garlic will reach people walking by and make them follow it.","t":"A：我們的烤肉攤藏在夜市後方，很多遊客看不到，要怎麼吸引更多顧客到我們攤位？ B：我們可以把烤爐放在走道旁，因為烤肉和大蒜的【香氣】會飄到路過的人那裡，讓他們循著香味過來。"},{"w":"glaze","p":"n.","d":"a shiny coating of sauce brushed on food","c":"亮面醬汁；糖漿塗層","s":"A: The ribs at our restaurant taste great, but they do not look as attractive as the ones in the photos on the menu, so what is missing? B: The cooks should brush a sweet honey glaze on the ribs during the last five minutes, so the meat looks shiny and brown when it reaches the table.","t":"A：我們餐廳的肋排很好吃，但看起來沒有菜單照片上那麼誘人，少了什麼？ B：廚師應該在最後五分鐘刷上甜甜的蜂蜜【亮面醬汁】，讓肉送上桌時看起來閃亮又金黃。"},{"w":"well-done","p":"adj.","d":"(of meat) cooked completely, with no pink inside","c":"全熟的","s":"A: One of our clients from the Middle East is joining the barbecue dinner tonight, and he told me he does not like any pink color in his meat. B: Then please ask the chef to cook his steak well-done, and make sure it is grilled on a separate part of the grill from the pork.","t":"A：今晚有一位來自中東的客戶要參加烤肉晚宴，他跟我說他不喜歡肉裡有任何粉紅色。 B：那就請主廚把他的牛排烤到【全熟】，並確保是在烤架上和豬肉分開的地方烤。"},{"w":"feast","p":"n.","d":"a large special meal for many people","c":"盛宴；大餐","s":"A: Our company had a record year, and the president wants to thank all two hundred staff members with something more exciting than a normal dinner. B: Let's plan a barbecue feast at the beach resort, with whole roast pigs, fresh seafood, and live music, so everyone can celebrate together.","t":"A：公司創下紀錄的一年，總裁想用比一般晚餐更精彩的方式感謝全體兩百名員工。 B：我們在海灘度假村規劃一場燒烤【盛宴】吧，有烤全豬、新鮮海鮮和現場音樂，讓大家一起慶祝。"}]},{"unit":26,"theme":"Bargain 划算交易","cards":[{"w":"deal","p":"n.","d":"something bought for a good price; a business agreement","c":"划算的交易；協議","s":"A: The electronics store is selling last year's laptop model for half price this weekend, and our office needs five new computers, so should we buy them there? B: Yes, that is a great deal, because last year's model is still fast enough for our work, and we can save almost fifty thousand dollars.","t":"A：電器行這個週末用半價賣去年的筆電款式，我們辦公室需要五台新電腦，應該去那裡買嗎？ B：應該，那是很划算的【交易】，因為去年的款式對我們的工作來說還是夠快，而且能省下將近五萬元。"},{"w":"discount","p":"n.","d":"an amount taken off the usual price","c":"折扣","s":"A: Our company orders a lot of paper and ink from the same supplier every month, but we always pay the normal price, so is there a way to pay less? B: We should ask the supplier for a ten percent discount, because we are one of their biggest customers and we have ordered from them for five years.","t":"A：我們公司每個月都向同一家供應商訂很多紙張和墨水，但總是付原價，有沒有辦法少付一點？ B：我們應該向供應商要求打九折的【折扣】，因為我們是他們最大的客戶之一，而且已經跟他們訂貨五年了。"},{"w":"sale","p":"n.","d":"a time when a store sells things at lower prices","c":"特價；拍賣","s":"A: My suit is getting old, and I have an important job interview next month, but new suits are very expensive at the department store, so what should I do? B: Wait until next weekend, because the department store is having its big anniversary sale, and most clothes will be thirty to fifty percent off.","t":"A：我的西裝舊了，下個月有個重要的工作面試，但百貨公司的新西裝很貴，我該怎麼辦？ B：等到下個週末吧，因為百貨公司要舉辦週年慶【特賣】，大部分衣服都會打五到七折。"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something to reach an agreement, often about price","c":"談判；議價","s":"A: The office we want to rent costs eighty thousand dollars a month, which is more than our budget allows, but the location is perfect for our business. B: We should negotiate with the owner, because the office has been empty for six months, and he may accept a lower rent if we sign a long contract.","t":"A：我們想租的辦公室每個月八萬元，超出了預算，但地點對我們的業務來說很完美。 B：我們應該和房東【議價】，因為那間辦公室已經空了六個月，如果我們簽長約，他可能會接受較低的租金。"},{"w":"haggle","p":"v.","d":"to argue about the price of something, especially at a market","c":"討價還價；殺價","s":"A: I am taking a group of clients to a traditional market in Bangkok tomorrow, and they want to buy some silk scarves, but they are not sure about the prices. B: Tell them it is normal to haggle with the sellers there, so they should start at about half the price the seller asks and slowly go up.","t":"A：我明天要帶一群客戶去曼谷的傳統市場，他們想買絲巾，但不確定價格。 B：告訴他們在那裡跟賣家【討價還價】是很正常的，所以他們應該從賣家開價的一半左右開始，再慢慢往上加。"},{"w":"cheap","p":"adj.","d":"low in price","c":"便宜的","s":"A: The new printer we bought for the office last month already stopped working, and the shop says it is not worth fixing, so what went wrong? B: It was very cheap, but it was also badly made, so this time we should spend a little more and buy a better brand with a three-year warranty.","t":"A：我們上個月為辦公室買的新印表機已經壞了，店家說不值得修，是哪裡出了問題？ B：它很【便宜】，但做工也很差，所以這次我們應該多花一點錢，買有三年保固的好品牌。"},{"w":"affordable","p":"adj.","d":"not too expensive, so most people can pay for it","c":"價格實惠的；負擔得起的","s":"A: Many young workers in our company say they cannot pay the high rents in Taipei, and some of them are leaving for jobs in other cities, so what can we do? B: The company could build staff apartments with affordable rents, so young workers can live near the office without spending most of their salary.","t":"A：我們公司很多年輕員工說付不起台北的高房租，有些人因此離職去其他城市工作，我們能怎麼辦？ B：公司可以興建租金【負擔得起】的員工宿舍，讓年輕員工能住在辦公室附近，又不必花掉大部分薪水。"},{"w":"price","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you need to pay for something","c":"價格","s":"A: Our coffee shop has been losing customers since a new chain store opened across the street, and they sell coffee for much less than we do. B: We could lower the price of our basic coffee, but I think we should also offer better service and free Wi-Fi, so customers have more reasons to stay.","t":"A：自從對街開了一家新的連鎖店後，我們咖啡店的顧客一直流失，他們賣的咖啡比我們便宜很多。 B：我們可以降低基本款咖啡的【價格】，但我認為也應該提供更好的服務和免費無線網路，讓顧客有更多理由留下來。"},{"w":"worth","p":"adj.","d":"having a certain value; good enough to deserve the money or time spent","c":"值得的；有…價值的","s":"A: The new office chairs cost three times as much as the ones we usually buy, and the finance manager is not happy about it, so should we still order them? B: I think they are worth the money, because they last ten years and help prevent the back pain that has caused so many sick days.","t":"A：新的辦公椅價格是我們平常買的三倍，財務經理不太高興，我們還要訂嗎？ B：我認為它們【值得】這個價錢，因為它們可以用十年，還能預防造成那麼多病假的背痛。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how useful or important something is compared with its price","c":"價值；划算程度","s":"A: The hotel near the airport costs a little more than the others, but the manager still wants our staff to stay there on business trips, so why is that? B: The room price includes breakfast, free airport transfers, and a gym, so it gives us better value than the cheaper hotels with no extra services.","t":"A：機場附近那家飯店比其他家貴一點，但經理還是希望員工出差時住那裡，為什麼？ B：房價包含早餐、免費機場接送和健身房，所以比起沒有額外服務的便宜飯店，它對我們更【划算】。"},{"w":"save","p":"v.","d":"to keep money instead of spending it","c":"節省；存（錢）","s":"A: Our electricity bill has gone up a lot this year, and the manager wants every department to find ways to reduce costs, so what can our team do? B: We can save money by turning off the lights and computers every evening and setting the air conditioner two degrees higher in summer.","t":"A：我們今年的電費漲了很多，經理希望每個部門都想辦法降低成本，我們團隊能做什麼？ B：我們可以每天晚上關燈和電腦，夏天把冷氣調高兩度來【節省】開支。"},{"w":"cost","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money needed to buy, make, or do something","c":"成本；費用","s":"A: The marketing team wants to hold a large product launch at a five-star hotel next month, but the director is worried about spending too much money. B: The total cost of the event will be about five hundred thousand dollars, including the room, food, and decorations, so we need her approval before we book.","t":"A：行銷團隊想在下個月於五星級飯店舉辦大型產品發表會，但主任擔心花太多錢。 B：活動總【費用】大約五十萬元，包含場地、餐點和佈置，所以我們在預訂前需要她核准。"},{"w":"reasonable","p":"adj.","d":"fair and not too expensive","c":"合理的；價格公道的","s":"A: We need a printing company to make two thousand brochures for the trade show, and I have received prices from four different companies, so which one should we choose? B: The company in Banqiao gave us the most reasonable price, and their quality is good, so I think we should give the order to them.","t":"A：我們需要一家印刷公司為商展印兩千份手冊，我收到了四家公司的報價，該選哪一家？ B：板橋那家給我們的價格最【合理】，品質也很好，所以我認為應該把訂單交給他們。"},{"w":"overpriced","p":"adj.","d":"more expensive than it should be","c":"定價過高的；太貴的","s":"A: The sandwiches at the café in our office building cost two hundred dollars each, and many people now go to the convenience store instead, so what is the problem? B: Most staff think the food there is overpriced, because the same sandwich costs less than half that price at the shop just across the street.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓裡咖啡廳的三明治一個要兩百元，很多人現在改去便利商店，問題在哪裡？ B：大多數員工認為那裡的食物【太貴了】，因為同樣的三明治在對街的店裡價格不到一半。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you plan to spend on something","c":"預算","s":"A: The team wants to buy new laptops, chairs, and a coffee machine for the office this year, but we cannot afford everything at once, so what should we do? B: Our budget for equipment is only two hundred thousand dollars, so we should buy the laptops first and wait until next year for the other things.","t":"A：團隊今年想為辦公室買新筆電、椅子和咖啡機，但我們沒辦法一次買齊，該怎麼辦？ B：我們的設備【預算】只有二十萬元，所以應該先買筆電，其他東西等明年再說。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at two or more things to see how they are different","c":"比較","s":"A: I need to book flights to Tokyo for five people from our sales team next month, and the prices on different websites are very different, so where should I start? B: First, compare the prices on three or four travel websites and the airline's own site, because the same seat can sometimes cost much less on one of them.","t":"A：我下個月要幫業務團隊五個人訂飛東京的機票，不同網站的價格差很多，我該從哪裡開始？ B：先【比較】三、四個旅遊網站和航空公司官網的價格，因為同一個座位有時在其中一個網站上便宜很多。"},{"w":"offer","p":"n.","d":"a special lower price or deal for a short time","c":"優惠；特價","s":"A: Our gym has fewer members this year than last year, and many people say the monthly fee is too high, so how can we attract new customers quickly? B: We can create a special offer for new members, such as three months for the price of two, which starts on the first day of next month.","t":"A：我們健身房今年的會員比去年少，很多人說月費太高，我們要怎麼快速吸引新顧客？ B：我們可以為新會員推出特別【優惠】，例如三個月只收兩個月的費用，從下個月第一天開始。"},{"w":"coupon","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper or code that lets you pay less for something","c":"優惠券；折價券","s":"A: Our pizza restaurant wants more customers to order online on weekday evenings, because the kitchen is not very busy then, so what can we try first? B: We can send every customer a coupon by email that gives one hundred dollars off any order placed from Monday to Thursday.","t":"A：我們披薩店希望平日晚上有更多顧客線上訂餐，因為那時廚房不太忙，我們可以先試什麼？ B：我們可以用電子郵件寄給每位顧客一張【優惠券】，週一到週四下的任何訂單都可折抵一百元。"},{"w":"clearance","p":"n.","d":"a sale to sell old products quickly and cheaply","c":"清倉拍賣","s":"A: The warehouse is full of last season's winter jackets, and we need the space for the new summer clothes arriving next month, so what should we do with them? B: Let's hold a clearance sale this weekend with prices up to seventy percent off, because it is better to sell them cheaply than keep them for another year.","t":"A：倉庫堆滿了上一季的冬季外套，而下個月到貨的新夏裝需要空間，我們該怎麼處理？ B：我們這個週末辦一場【清倉】拍賣吧，價格最低打三折，因為便宜賣掉總比再留一年好。"},{"w":"secondhand","p":"adj.","d":"owned or used by someone else before","c":"二手的","s":"A: Our small company is opening a new branch office, but we do not have much money for furniture this year, so where can we find desks and cabinets? B: We can buy secondhand furniture from a company that is moving out of our building, because it is in good condition and costs much less than new furniture.","t":"A：我們這家小公司要開新的分公司，但今年沒有太多錢買家具，在哪裡可以找到辦公桌和櫃子？ B：我們可以向一家要搬離我們大樓的公司買【二手】家具，因為它們狀況良好，價格也比新家具便宜很多。"},{"w":"markdown","p":"n.","d":"a reduction in the price of something in a store","c":"降價；減價","s":"A: The new phone cases are not selling well, even though we put them right next to the cash register, so how can we sell them before the new models come out? B: We can give them a thirty percent markdown and put red stickers with the new price on each one, so customers can see the lower price easily.","t":"A：新手機殼就算放在收銀台旁邊也賣得不好，我們要怎麼在新款推出前把它們賣掉？ B：我們可以將它們【降價】百分之三十，並在每個上面貼上標示新價格的紅色貼紙，讓顧客容易看到較低的價格。"},{"w":"shop","p":"v.","d":"to go to stores to look at and buy things","c":"購物；逛街","s":"A: My manager wants me to buy small gifts for twenty clients before the Lunar New Year, but I do not have much time during the day, so what should I do? B: You can shop online tonight, because many websites offer free gift wrapping and can deliver all twenty gifts to the office by Friday.","t":"A：經理要我在農曆新年前買小禮物送給二十位客戶，但我白天沒什麼時間，該怎麼辦？ B：你今晚可以上網【購物】，因為很多網站提供免費禮品包裝，還能在星期五前把二十份禮物全送到辦公室。"},{"w":"splurge","p":"v.","d":"to spend a lot of money on something special that you do not really need","c":"揮霍；大手筆花錢","s":"A: Our team finally finished the biggest project of the year, and the manager says we can use the extra money in our budget to celebrate together. B: Let's splurge on a dinner at that famous steak restaurant, because everyone worked late every night for three months and deserves something special.","t":"A：我們團隊終於完成今年最大的專案，經理說可以用預算中多出來的錢一起慶祝。 B：我們就【大手筆】去那家知名牛排館吃一頓晚餐吧，因為大家三個月來每晚都加班，值得享受一點特別的。"},{"w":"thrifty","p":"adj.","d":"careful about spending money and not wasting it","c":"節儉的","s":"A: Our new accountant always brings lunch from home, uses both sides of the paper, and finds the cheapest train tickets for every business trip. B: She is very thrifty, and that is good for our small company, because her careful habits saved us almost two hundred thousand dollars last year.","t":"A：我們的新會計總是從家裡帶午餐、紙張雙面使用，每次出差都會找到最便宜的火車票。 B：她非常【節儉】，這對我們這家小公司是好事，因為她謹慎的習慣去年幫我們省下了將近二十萬元。"},{"w":"economical","p":"adj.","d":"using little money, fuel, or energy","c":"經濟的；省錢的","s":"A: Our delivery company needs to buy ten new vans this year, and fuel prices keep going up, so what kind of vans should we choose? B: We should choose electric or hybrid vans, because they are more economical to run and will save us a lot of money on fuel over the next ten years.","t":"A：我們的貨運公司今年需要買十輛新廂型車，油價又一直上漲，我們該選哪一種車？ B：我們應該選電動車或油電混合車，因為它們運作起來更【省錢】，未來十年能幫我們省下很多油錢。"},{"w":"steal","p":"n.","d":"something that costs much less than it is really worth","c":"非常便宜的東西；超值品","s":"A: I found a used projector online for only three thousand dollars, and it is the same model that costs twenty thousand dollars new, so should I buy it for the meeting room? B: At that price, it is a steal, but please ask the seller to show you that it works before you pay, just to be safe.","t":"A：我在網路上找到一台二手投影機只要三千元，和新的要兩萬元的是同一款，我該買來放會議室嗎？ B：以那個價格來說，簡直是【超值】，不過付錢前為了安全起見，請賣家先證明它能正常運作。"},{"w":"fair","p":"adj.","d":"reasonable and right for both sides","c":"公平的；合理的","s":"A: Our long-time supplier wants to raise the price of rice by five percent next year, and the restaurant owner is not sure whether he should agree. B: I think it is a fair price, because the cost of rice has gone up much more than that this year, and the supplier has always been reliable.","t":"A：我們長期合作的供應商明年想把米價調漲百分之五，餐廳老闆不確定是否該同意。 B：我認為那是【合理】的價格，因為今年米的成本漲得比那還多，而且這家供應商一直都很可靠。"},{"w":"retail","p":"n.","d":"the sale of goods to the public in stores","c":"零售","s":"A: Our company makes kitchen tools and has only sold them to hotels and restaurants until now, but the director wants to grow our business next year. B: We could start selling in retail, through department stores and online shops, so ordinary families can also buy our products for their homes.","t":"A：我們公司生產廚房用具，到目前為止只賣給飯店和餐廳，但主任想在明年擴大業務。 B：我們可以開始做【零售】，透過百貨公司和網路商店販售，讓一般家庭也能買我們的產品回家用。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"money you earn after paying all your costs","c":"利潤；獲利","s":"A: Our store sold more items during the big sale last month than in any other month this year, but the manager does not seem very happy, so why is that? B: Because the prices were so low, our profit on each item was very small, and after paying the staff for extra hours, we earned almost nothing.","t":"A：我們店上個月大特賣賣出的商品數量是今年最多的，但經理似乎不太高興，為什麼？ B：因為價格太低，我們每件商品的【利潤】非常少，付完員工加班費之後幾乎沒賺到錢。"}]},{"unit":27,"theme":"Believing 信念","cards":[{"w":"belief","p":"n.","d":"an idea that you accept as true","c":"信念；相信","s":"A: Why did the new manager spend so much time talking with the team before she changed the weekly schedule at the office? B: It is her strong belief that workers do better when they understand the reasons for a change, so she always explains her plans clearly and listens to their questions first.","t":"A：為什麼新經理在更改辦公室的每週班表之前，花了那麼多時間和團隊談話？ B：她堅定的【信念】是，員工了解改變的原因時會表現得更好，所以她總是先清楚說明計畫並聽取他們的問題。"},{"w":"believer","p":"n.","d":"a person who strongly thinks that something is good or true","c":"信奉者；深信…的人","s":"A: Are you surprised that the head of the sales department now rides her bicycle to work every day, even when it rains in the morning? B: Not at all, because she has been a firm believer in healthy habits for years, and she often tells new staff that regular exercise helps her stay focused at meetings.","t":"A：業務部主管現在每天騎腳踏車上班，即使早上下雨也一樣，你會感到驚訝嗎？ B：一點也不，因為她多年來一直是健康習慣的堅定【信奉者】，她也常告訴新員工規律運動能幫助她在開會時保持專注。"},{"w":"trust","p":"v.","d":"to believe that someone is honest or will do the right thing","c":"信任；信賴","s":"A: Why did the director let the new assistant handle the important client meeting in Singapore by himself last week? B: She has worked with him on several difficult projects, and he always finishes his tasks carefully and on time, so she knows she can trust him with serious responsibilities.","t":"A：為什麼主任上週讓新助理獨自負責在新加坡的重要客戶會議？ B：她和他合作過好幾個困難的專案，他總是仔細又準時完成任務，所以她知道可以【信任】他、交付重大的責任。"},{"w":"faith","p":"n.","d":"strong trust in someone or something","c":"信心；信任；信仰","s":"A: The company lost money for two years in a row, so why are the investors still giving it more support this year? B: They have great faith in the new CEO because she turned around two other businesses before, and her plan to cut costs and open online stores looks very practical.","t":"A：這家公司連續兩年虧損，為什麼投資人今年還繼續給予更多支持？ B：他們對新任執行長很有【信心】，因為她之前曾讓另外兩家企業轉虧為盈，而且她削減成本和開設網路商店的計畫看起來非常務實。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you can do something well","c":"信心；自信","s":"A: How did the new intern manage to give such a clear presentation to the board of directors without looking nervous at all? B: Her supervisor practiced with her several times during the week and gave her helpful advice, which built up her confidence and helped her speak calmly in front of everyone.","t":"A：新來的實習生是怎麼在董事會面前做出這麼清楚的簡報，而且一點都不緊張？ B：她的主管那週陪她練習了好幾次，並給她有用的建議，這建立了她的【信心】，讓她能在大家面前冷靜地發言。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe that something is true","c":"說服；使相信","s":"A: The finance team was against the idea at first, so how did you get approval to buy new computers for the design department? B: I showed them a report on how much time the old machines were wasting every day, and that was enough to convince them that the purchase would save money.","t":"A：財務團隊起初反對這個想法，你是怎麼取得核准，為設計部門購買新電腦的？ B：我給他們看了一份報告，說明舊電腦每天浪費多少時間，這就足以【說服】他們相信這筆採購會省錢。"},{"w":"convinced","p":"adj.","d":"completely sure that something is true","c":"確信的；深信的","s":"A: Why does the marketing manager want to move most of our advertising money from newspapers to social media next year? B: After studying last year's sales numbers carefully, she is convinced that younger customers find our products online, so she believes the change will bring in many more orders.","t":"A：為什麼行銷經理明年想把大部分廣告預算從報紙轉到社群媒體？ B：仔細研究去年的銷售數字後，她【確信】年輕顧客是在網路上找到我們的產品，所以她認為這項改變會帶來更多訂單。"},{"w":"convincing","p":"adj.","d":"able to make people believe something is true","c":"令人信服的","s":"A: Did the hotel manager accept the guest's complaint about the noisy air conditioner, or did she refuse to give him a refund? B: He recorded the loud noise on his phone and showed her the video at the front desk, so his story was convincing enough for her to return half of his payment.","t":"A：飯店經理有接受那位房客對冷氣噪音的投訴嗎？還是她拒絕退款給他？ B：他用手機錄下了很大的噪音，並在櫃台給她看影片，所以他的說法夠【令人信服】，她便退還了一半的費用。"},{"w":"doubt","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of not being sure about something","c":"懷疑；疑慮","s":"A: Why hasn't the manager signed the agreement with the new supplier yet, since their prices are much lower than our current ones? B: She has some doubt about whether such a small company can deliver large orders on time, so she wants to visit their factory before she makes a final decision.","t":"A：新供應商的價格比我們目前的低很多，為什麼經理還沒和他們簽約？ B：她對這麼小的公司能否準時交付大量訂單有些【疑慮】，所以她想在做最後決定之前先參觀他們的工廠。"},{"w":"uncertain","p":"adj.","d":"not sure or not clearly known","c":"不確定的","s":"A: Has the travel agency told you yet when your group can fly to Tokyo for the trade show next month? B: Not yet, because a big storm is moving toward Japan, and the schedule for flights out of Taipei is still uncertain, so they promised to call me as soon as they hear any news.","t":"A：旅行社告訴你了嗎？你們這團下個月什麼時候可以飛去東京參加商展？ B：還沒，因為一個大型暴風正往日本移動，從台北出發的航班時刻仍然【不確定】，所以他們答應一有消息就打電話給我。"},{"w":"certain","p":"adj.","d":"completely sure","c":"確定的；肯定的","s":"A: Should we order extra chairs for the company's annual dinner, or do you think the hall already has enough for all our guests? B: I called the event center this morning and checked the numbers twice, so I am certain they have two hundred chairs, which is more than enough for everyone we invited.","t":"A：我們應該為公司年度晚宴多訂一些椅子嗎？還是你覺得會場已經有足夠的椅子給所有賓客了？ B：我今天早上打電話給活動中心，也核對了兩次數字，所以我【確定】他們有兩百張椅子，對所有受邀的人來說綽綽有餘。"},{"w":"certainty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being completely sure","c":"確定；確信","s":"A: Can you tell the customer exactly when the repair team will arrive to fix the broken elevator in her office building? B: I can't say with certainty, because the team is still working at another site downtown, but they usually finish by noon, so they should reach her building early in the afternoon.","t":"A：你能明確告訴客戶維修團隊何時會到她的辦公大樓修理故障的電梯嗎？ B：我無法【確定】地說，因為團隊還在市中心的另一個地點施工，但他們通常中午前會完成，所以應該在下午早些時候抵達她的大樓。"},{"w":"assume","p":"v.","d":"to think something is true without checking it","c":"假定；以為","s":"A: Why did so many people arrive at the wrong meeting room on the third floor this morning? B: The room was changed late last night, and most of the staff didn't read the new email, so it was natural for them to assume that the meeting was still in the usual place, and they went there out of habit.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有這麼多人跑錯到三樓的會議室？ B：會議室昨晚很晚才更改，大部分員工沒看到新的電子郵件，所以他們很自然地【以為】會議還在平常的地點，就習慣性地去了那裡。"},{"w":"assumption","p":"n.","d":"something you believe is true without proof","c":"假設；設想","s":"A: Why is the sales report for the new store so different from the numbers the planning team expected last spring? B: Their plan was based on the assumption that many tourists would visit the area, but the new train station opened late, so far fewer shoppers came than they had hoped.","t":"A：為什麼新門市的銷售報告和規劃團隊去年春天預期的數字差這麼多？ B：他們的計畫是基於很多觀光客會來這個地區的【假設】，但新的火車站延後開通，所以來的購物者比他們希望的少很多。"},{"w":"opinion","p":"n.","d":"what you think or feel about something","c":"意見；看法","s":"A: Before we choose a design for the new company logo, should we ask the staff in the other branches what they think? B: Yes, I'd like to hear everyone's opinion because they meet our customers every day, so I'll send a short online survey to all of our offices this afternoon.","t":"A：在我們選定公司新標誌的設計之前，應該問問其他分公司員工的想法嗎？ B：是的，我想聽聽每個人的【意見】，因為他們每天都接觸我們的顧客，所以我今天下午會寄一份簡短的線上問卷給我們所有的辦公室。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something by giving reasons","c":"說服；勸說","s":"A: Our best engineer said she was going to leave for a job in Singapore, so is she really staying with us now? B: Yes, the director met her for lunch and offered her a team of her own and more flexible hours, which helped persuade her to stay for at least another two years.","t":"A：我們最優秀的工程師說她要去新加坡工作，那她現在真的會留下來嗎？ B：是的，主任和她共進午餐，提供她一個自己的團隊和更彈性的工時，這幫助【說服】她至少再留兩年。"},{"w":"persuasion","p":"n.","d":"the act of making someone agree with you","c":"說服；勸說","s":"A: How did the hotel finally agree to give us a lower price for the conference rooms during the busy holiday season? B: It took a lot of persuasion, but our manager explained that we would book fifty guest rooms every year, so the hotel decided a long-term customer was worth the discount.","t":"A：飯店最後怎麼會同意在忙碌的假期旺季給我們會議室較低的價格？ B：花了很多【說服】的功夫，但我們經理說明我們每年都會訂五十間客房，所以飯店認為一位長期客戶值得這個折扣。"},{"w":"credible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be believed or trusted","c":"可信的；可靠的","s":"A: Why did the reporter call so many different people before she wrote her story about the factory closing next year? B: She wanted to make sure her information came from credible sources, such as company managers and city officials, because readers would complain if the news turned out to be wrong.","t":"A：為什麼那位記者在寫工廠明年關閉的報導之前，打電話給這麼多不同的人？ B：她想確保她的資訊來自【可靠的】消息來源，例如公司經理和市府官員，因為如果新聞內容錯誤，讀者會抱怨。"},{"w":"credibility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being trusted and believed","c":"可信度；信譽","s":"A: Why is the company so worried about a small mistake in the price list it sent to customers last week? B: Several clients already noticed the wrong numbers, and if we don't correct them quickly and apologize, we could lose our credibility with buyers who have trusted us for many years.","t":"A：為什麼公司這麼擔心上週寄給客戶的價目表裡的一個小錯誤？ B：好幾位客戶已經注意到錯誤的數字，如果我們不快點更正並道歉，可能會失去在多年來信任我們的買家心中的【信譽】。"},{"w":"skeptical","p":"adj.","d":"having doubts that something is true or useful","c":"懷疑的；持懷疑態度的","s":"A: Did the board members like the idea of letting all the staff work from home three days a week? B: Most of them were skeptical at first because they worried that people would work less, but the results from a small test group last month changed their minds completely.","t":"A：董事會成員喜歡讓所有員工每週在家工作三天的想法嗎？ B：他們大多數起初都抱持【懷疑】態度，因為擔心大家工作量會減少，但上個月一個小型測試小組的結果完全改變了他們的想法。"},{"w":"skepticism","p":"n.","d":"an attitude of doubting that something is true","c":"懷疑態度；質疑","s":"A: How did the customers react when the company said its new phone battery could last a full week without charging? B: Many people reacted with skepticism because other brands had made similar promises before, so the company invited reporters to test the phones themselves for seven days.","t":"A：公司宣稱新手機電池不用充電就能用整整一週時，顧客有什麼反應？ B：很多人以【懷疑】的態度回應，因為其他品牌以前也做過類似的承諾，所以公司邀請記者親自測試手機七天。"},{"w":"devotion","p":"n.","d":"great love, care, or loyalty to someone or something","c":"奉獻；忠誠；熱愛","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner give the head chef a special award at the staff party on Friday night? B: He has worked there for twenty years, often staying late to train young cooks and test new dishes, so the owner wanted to thank him for his devotion to the business.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳老闆在週五晚上的員工派對上頒給主廚一個特別獎？ B：他在那裡工作了二十年，常常留到很晚訓練年輕廚師和試做新菜，所以老闆想感謝他對這家店的【奉獻】。"},{"w":"loyal","p":"adj.","d":"always supporting a person, company, or idea","c":"忠誠的；忠實的","s":"A: Why does the small coffee shop near our office give free drinks to some customers on their birthdays? B: The owner wants to thank the people who come in almost every morning, because loyal customers like them keep the shop busy even when the big chain store across the street has a sale.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近那家小咖啡店會在某些顧客生日時送免費飲料？ B：老闆想感謝那些幾乎每天早上都來的人，因為像他們這樣的【忠實】顧客，即使在對街的大型連鎖店打折時也讓店裡生意興隆。"},{"w":"loyalty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of always supporting someone or something","c":"忠誠；忠誠度","s":"A: Why did the supermarket start giving points to shoppers every time they buy groceries with their membership card? B: The managers hope the program will build customer loyalty, because people who collect points usually come back every week instead of trying the new store that opened nearby.","t":"A：為什麼超市開始在顧客每次用會員卡買雜貨時給他們點數？ B：經理們希望這個計畫能建立顧客【忠誠度】，因為收集點數的人通常每週都會回來，而不是去試試附近新開的商店。"},{"w":"commit","p":"v.","d":"to promise to give your time or effort to something","c":"承諾；致力於","s":"A: Is the new partner company really serious about working with us on the hospital building project next year? B: Yes, they are ready to commit to the full three-year plan, and they have already agreed to send ten engineers and share half of the costs for the design work.","t":"A：新的合作公司真的認真要在明年和我們合作醫院大樓專案嗎？ B：是的，他們準備好【承諾】投入完整的三年計畫，而且已經同意派十位工程師並分擔一半的設計費用。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"a promise or strong decision to do something","c":"承諾；投入","s":"A: Why did the customers choose our cleaning company again this year, even though another company offered them lower prices? B: They told us they valued our commitment to quality, since our team always arrives on time, uses safe products, and fixes any problem within one day of a complaint.","t":"A：為什麼客戶今年又選擇了我們的清潔公司，即使另一家公司提供更低的價格？ B：他們告訴我們，他們重視我們對品質的【承諾】，因為我們的團隊總是準時抵達、使用安全的產品，並在接到投訴一天內解決任何問題。"},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"to agree to take or receive something","c":"接受","s":"A: Did the young designer decide to take the job offer from the advertising agency in Taichung, or is she still thinking about it? B: She plans to accept it tomorrow morning, because the salary is good, the office is close to her parents' home, and the team works on interesting international projects.","t":"A：那位年輕設計師決定要去台中那家廣告公司工作了嗎？還是她還在考慮？ B：她打算明天早上【接受】這份工作，因為薪水不錯、辦公室離她父母家很近，而且團隊做的都是有趣的國際專案。"},{"w":"acceptance","p":"n.","d":"the act of agreeing to take or approve something","c":"接受；錄取；認可","s":"A: Have we heard back from the conference organizers about the research paper our team sent them in September? B: Yes, we received a letter of acceptance this morning, so two of our engineers will fly to Berlin in March to present the results to experts from around the world.","t":"A：我們有收到研討會主辦單位關於我們團隊九月寄去的研究論文的回覆嗎？ B：有，我們今天早上收到了【接受】通知函，所以我們的兩位工程師三月會飛往柏林，向世界各地的專家發表研究成果。"},{"w":"conviction","p":"n.","d":"a strong belief or opinion","c":"堅定的信念；確信","s":"A: Why did the director spend so much of the company's budget on training programs during such a difficult year? B: It is her deep conviction that skilled workers are the key to long-term success, so she would rather cut office costs than stop helping employees learn new skills.","t":"A：為什麼主任在這麼艱難的一年裡，把公司這麼多預算花在培訓課程上？ B：她深深【確信】，有技能的員工是長期成功的關鍵，所以她寧願削減辦公室開支，也不願停止幫助員工學習新技能。"},{"w":"devout","p":"adj.","d":"believing strongly in a religion and following its rules","c":"虔誠的","s":"A: Why did the hotel staff prepare a quiet prayer room and special meals for the group of visitors arriving from Indonesia next week? B: The travel agent told us that many of the guests are devout Muslims who pray several times a day, so we want them to feel comfortable and respected during their stay.","t":"A：為什麼飯店員工為下週從印尼來的旅客團準備了一間安靜的祈禱室和特別餐點？ B：旅行社告訴我們，許多客人是一天祈禱好幾次的【虔誠】穆斯林，所以我們希望他們在住宿期間感到舒適並受到尊重。"},{"w":"ideology","p":"n.","d":"a set of ideas and beliefs that guide a group or a system","c":"意識形態；思想體系；理念","s":"A: Why did the two business partners decide to end their company after working together successfully for more than ten years? B: Their management ideology became very different, because one wanted fast growth and big profits while the other cared more about small shops, fair pay, and protecting the environment.","t":"A：為什麼那兩位事業夥伴在成功合作十多年後決定結束他們的公司？ B：他們的經營【理念】變得非常不同，因為一個想要快速成長和高利潤，另一個則更在意小商店、公平的薪資和保護環境。"}]},{"unit":28,"theme":"Bicycle 自行車","cards":[{"w":"pedal","p":"v.","d":"to push the pedals of a bike with your feet to make it move","c":"踩踏板；騎（腳踏車）","s":"A: Why are you so tired this morning, and did you have to come to the office by bike again because your car is still at the repair shop? B: Yes, and the route from my apartment goes up a long, steep hill, so I had to pedal very hard for twenty minutes before I finally reached the building.","t":"A：你今天早上為什麼這麼累？是不是因為你的車還在修車廠，所以又得騎腳踏車來辦公室？ B：對，而且從我公寓出發的路線要爬一段又長又陡的坡，所以我得用力【踩踏板】整整二十分鐘才終於到達大樓。"},{"w":"wheel","p":"n.","d":"a round object that turns to let a bike or car move","c":"輪子；車輪","s":"A: Can you tell me why the delivery bike didn't arrive at the customer's address on time yesterday afternoon? B: The rider hit a deep hole near the train station, and the front wheel got badly bent, so he had to push the bike to the nearest shop and wait an hour for repairs.","t":"A：你能告訴我為什麼昨天下午送貨腳踏車沒有準時抵達客戶地址嗎？ B：騎士在火車站附近撞到一個很深的坑洞，前【輪】嚴重變形，所以他必須把車推到最近的店，等了一個小時修理。"},{"w":"tire","p":"n.","d":"the rubber ring filled with air around a wheel","c":"輪胎","s":"A: Before we lend these company bikes to the visitors for the city tour this weekend, is there anything we should check first? B: Please make sure each tire has enough air in it, because the bikes have been sitting in the storage room for months, and a flat one could ruin the whole trip.","t":"A：這個週末我們把公司腳踏車借給訪客做城市導覽之前，有什麼需要先檢查的嗎？ B：請確認每個【輪胎】的氣都夠，因為這些腳踏車已經在儲藏室放了好幾個月，一個洩了氣的就可能毀了整趟行程。"},{"w":"handlebar","p":"n.","d":"the bar at the front of a bike that you hold to steer","c":"（腳踏車的）把手；車把","s":"A: Do you think this used bike is a good choice for my daily trip to the office, or should I spend more money on a new one? B: It looks fine overall, but the handlebar is a little loose, so you should tighten it before you ride in heavy traffic, or you might lose control when you turn.","t":"A：你覺得這台二手腳踏車適合我每天上班騎嗎？還是我應該多花點錢買台新的？ B：整體看起來不錯，但【車把手】有點鬆，所以你在車流量大的地方騎之前應該先鎖緊，否則轉彎時可能會失控。"},{"w":"seat","p":"n.","d":"the part of a bike or vehicle that you sit on","c":"座位；座椅","s":"A: My back hurts after riding to work every day this week, so what do you think the problem could be? B: I noticed that your seat is too low for someone as tall as you, so you should raise it a few centimeters, and your knees and back will feel much better after a few days.","t":"A：這週我每天騎車上班後背都很痛，你覺得可能是什麼問題？ B：我注意到你的【座椅】對像你這麼高的人來說太低了，所以你應該把它調高幾公分，幾天後你的膝蓋和背就會舒服很多。"},{"w":"frame","p":"n.","d":"the main metal or carbon structure of a bike","c":"車架；框架","s":"A: Why is this bike in the shop window so much more expensive than the others, even though it looks almost the same? B: Its frame is made of carbon instead of steel, so the whole bike is lighter and stronger, which is why professional racers and serious riders are willing to pay the higher price.","t":"A：櫥窗裡這台腳踏車看起來和其他的幾乎一樣，為什麼貴這麼多？ B：它的【車架】是用碳纖維而不是鋼做的，所以整台車更輕更堅固，這就是為什麼職業選手和認真的車友願意付較高的價錢。"},{"w":"chain","p":"n.","d":"a line of metal rings that turns the back wheel when you pedal","c":"（腳踏車）鏈條","s":"A: I heard a strange noise from my bike all the way to the meeting this morning, so do you know what might be wrong with it? B: It is probably the chain, because it looks dry and a little rusty, so you should clean it and add some oil before you ride home this evening.","t":"A：今天早上我一路騎去開會，腳踏車都發出奇怪的聲音，你知道可能是哪裡出問題嗎？ B：可能是【鏈條】，因為它看起來很乾又有點生鏽，所以你今晚騎回家前應該先清理並上點油。"},{"w":"gear","p":"n.","d":"a part that controls how hard or easy it is to pedal","c":"排檔；齒輪","s":"A: How did you manage to ride all the way up that steep hill to the conference center without stopping even once? B: I changed to a lower gear at the bottom of the hill, so pedaling became much easier, and I could keep a steady pace even though I was carrying a heavy laptop bag.","t":"A：你是怎麼一路騎上那個陡坡到會議中心，中間一次都沒停下來的？ B：我在坡底就換到較低的【檔位】，所以踩起來輕鬆多了，即使背著很重的筆電包也能保持穩定的速度。"},{"w":"brake","p":"n.","d":"the part you use to slow down or stop a bike","c":"煞車；制動器","s":"A: Why did the bike rental shop give you a discount when you returned the bike yesterday afternoon? B: The back brake didn't work well when I was riding down the hill near the river, so I almost hit a car, and the manager apologized and gave me half my money back.","t":"A：你昨天下午還車時，腳踏車租借店為什麼給你折扣？ B：我在河邊附近騎下坡時，後【煞車】不太靈，所以我差點撞到一台車，經理向我道歉並退還一半的錢。"},{"w":"helmet","p":"n.","d":"a hard hat that protects your head","c":"安全帽；頭盔","s":"A: Does the company require us to wear any special safety equipment if we join the charity bike race next month? B: Yes, every rider must wear a helmet during the whole race, and the organizers will check each person at the starting line, so please remember to bring yours or rent one.","t":"A：如果我們參加下個月的慈善單車賽，公司要求我們穿戴特別的安全裝備嗎？ B：要，每位騎士整場比賽都必須戴【安全帽】，主辦單位會在起跑線檢查每個人，所以請記得帶你自己的或租一頂。"},{"w":"saddle","p":"n.","d":"the seat on a bicycle or on a horse","c":"（腳踏車）坐墊；鞍座","s":"A: After the long weekend bike tour along the coast, which part of the trip was the most uncomfortable for you? B: Honestly, sitting for six hours was hard because the saddle on my rental bike was narrow and very hard, so next time I will bring a soft cover or rent a better model.","t":"A：沿著海岸騎了漫長的週末單車之旅後，對你來說行程中哪個部分最不舒服？ B：說實話，坐六個小時很辛苦，因為我租的腳踏車【坐墊】又窄又硬，所以下次我會帶個軟墊套或租個比較好的車款。"},{"w":"spoke","p":"n.","d":"one of the thin metal bars that join the center of a wheel to its edge","c":"（車輪的）輻條","s":"A: The repair technician said my back wheel is not perfectly round anymore, so what exactly caused that problem? B: One thin metal spoke broke when you rode over the curb last week, so the wheel lost its shape, and he will need to replace it and adjust the others before you ride again.","t":"A：維修技師說我的後輪已經不再是完美的圓形，到底是什麼造成這個問題？ B：上週你騎過路緣石時，一根細細的金屬【輻條】斷了，所以車輪變形，他在你再騎之前需要更換它並調整其他的輻條。"},{"w":"hub","p":"n.","d":"the center part of a wheel that turns around the axle; also a central place","c":"（車輪的）輪轂；花鼓；中心","s":"A: Why does my front wheel make a grinding sound and turn so slowly, even after I pumped up the tires this morning? B: The hub in the center of the wheel probably needs new bearings, so take the bike to the shop downtown, and they can usually fix it within one day.","t":"A：為什麼我的前輪會發出摩擦聲而且轉得那麼慢，即使今天早上已經把輪胎打飽氣了？ B：車輪中心的【花鼓】可能需要換新的軸承，所以把車牽去市中心的店，他們通常一天內就能修好。"},{"w":"ride","p":"v.","d":"to sit on and control a bike, motorbike or horse as it moves","c":"騎（腳踏車、馬等）","s":"A: Since the subway is closed for repairs all next week, how are you planning to get to the office downtown every morning? B: I will ride my bike along the river path, because it only takes about twenty-five minutes, and I can avoid the crowded buses and the heavy traffic on the main streets.","t":"A：既然下週地鐵整週都因維修而關閉，你打算每天早上怎麼去市中心的辦公室？ B：我會沿著河濱步道【騎】腳踏車，因為只要大約二十五分鐘，而且可以避開擁擠的公車和主要街道上的車潮。"},{"w":"cycle","p":"v.","d":"to ride a bicycle","c":"騎自行車","s":"A: What did your team decide to do for the company's health month, since many people wanted an outdoor activity this year? B: We decided to cycle together around the lake every Saturday morning, and the company will pay for bike rentals and breakfast for everyone who joins at least three times.","t":"A：既然今年很多人想要戶外活動，你們團隊決定在公司健康月做什麼？ B：我們決定每週六早上一起繞湖【騎單車】，而且公司會替參加至少三次的每個人支付租車費和早餐。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to stay steady without falling","c":"平衡","s":"A: Why did the new delivery worker fall off his bike in front of the restaurant this afternoon? Was anyone hurt? B: He was carrying too many boxes on the back, so he lost his balance when he turned the corner too quickly, but luckily he only hurt his arm a little and the food was fine.","t":"A：新來的外送員今天下午為什麼在餐廳前從腳踏車上摔下來？有人受傷嗎？ B：他後座載了太多箱子，所以轉彎太快時失去了【平衡】，但幸好他只是手臂受了點輕傷，餐點也沒事。"},{"w":"speed","p":"n.","d":"how fast something moves","c":"速度","s":"A: Are there any special rules for riding company bikes inside the factory area that new employees should know about? B: Yes, you must keep your speed under ten kilometers per hour near the loading area, because forklifts and workers move around there all day and accidents can happen very easily.","t":"A：在工廠區內騎公司腳踏車，有沒有什麼新員工應該知道的特別規定？ B：有，在裝卸區附近你必須把【速度】保持在每小時十公里以下，因為堆高機和工人整天都在那裡來來去去，很容易發生意外。"},{"w":"trail","p":"n.","d":"a path through the countryside, a forest, or mountains","c":"小徑；步道","s":"A: Do you know a good place where our department could go cycling for the team-building day next month? B: There is a beautiful trail through the forest just outside the city, and it is wide and flat enough for beginners, so even colleagues who rarely ride could enjoy it safely.","t":"A：你知道下個月團隊建立日我們部門可以去哪裡騎單車嗎？ B：城外有一條穿過森林的美麗【小徑】，夠寬也夠平坦，適合初學者，所以就算是很少騎車的同事也能安全地享受。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work","c":"通勤","s":"A: Why did you decide to move to an apartment so close to the office, even though the rent there is much higher? B: I used to commute by bus for almost two hours every day, which made me very tired, so now I save time and can simply bike to work in ten minutes.","t":"A：你為什麼決定搬到離公司這麼近的公寓，即使那裡的房租貴很多？ B：我以前每天搭公車【通勤】將近兩個小時，讓我非常疲累，所以現在我省下時間，只要騎十分鐘腳踏車就能上班。"},{"w":"mountain","p":"n.","d":"a very high hill","c":"山；山岳","s":"A: What are your plans for the long holiday weekend, since the weather report says it will be sunny and cool? B: A few friends from the marketing team and I are going to ride our bikes up a mountain near the national park, and we plan to camp at the top and watch the sunrise.","t":"A：氣象預報說天氣會晴朗涼爽，你連假週末有什麼計畫？ B：我和行銷團隊的幾個朋友要騎腳踏車登上國家公園附近的一座【山】，我們打算在山頂露營看日出。"},{"w":"road","p":"n.","d":"a wide way for cars and bikes to travel on","c":"道路；馬路","s":"A: Is it safe to ride a bike from the hotel to the convention center, or should our guests take a taxi instead? B: It is fairly safe, but the main road has no bike lane and lots of trucks, so guests should use the quieter side streets and follow the green signs.","t":"A：從飯店騎腳踏車到會展中心安全嗎？還是我們的客人應該改搭計程車？ B：還算安全，但主要【道路】沒有自行車道而且卡車很多，所以客人應該走比較安靜的小巷並跟著綠色標誌走。"},{"w":"grip","p":"n.","d":"a firm hold on something","c":"緊握；抓握力；抓地力","s":"A: It rained heavily during my ride to work this morning, so why did I feel like my hands kept sliding while I was steering? B: The rubber covers on your handlebars are old and smooth, so you have a poor grip, and you should buy new ones before riding in wet weather again.","t":"A：今天早上我騎車上班時下大雨，為什麼我在控制方向時一直覺得手在打滑？ B：你把手上的橡膠套又舊又光滑，所以【抓握力】很差，你在下次雨天騎車之前應該買新的。"},{"w":"reflector","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of plastic or glass that shines when light hits it","c":"反光片；反光鏡","s":"A: The police stopped me on my way home last night and warned me about my bike, but what did I do wrong? B: Your bike has no light or reflector on the back, so drivers can't see you in the dark, and the law requires every bike to have one for riding safely at night.","t":"A：昨晚我回家路上被警察攔下來，警告我腳踏車的問題，我到底做錯了什麼？ B：你的腳踏車後面沒有車燈或【反光片】，所以駕駛在黑暗中看不到你，法律規定每台腳踏車都要裝一個才能在夜間安全騎乘。"},{"w":"lightweight","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy","c":"輕量的；重量輕的","s":"A: Which bike would you recommend for our sales staff, who often need to carry their bikes up the stairs to the train platform? B: I suggest this lightweight folding model, because it weighs less than ten kilos, and it fits easily under a desk when they arrive at the office.","t":"A：我們的業務員常常需要把腳踏車扛上樓梯到火車月台，你會推薦哪一款腳踏車？ B：我建議這款【輕量】摺疊車，因為它重量不到十公斤，而且他們抵達辦公室時可以輕鬆地放在桌子底下。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"able to last a long time without breaking","c":"耐用的；持久的","s":"A: Why did the delivery company choose these bikes even though they cost more than the cheaper models from other suppliers? B: They are very durable, so they can be used every day in rain and heat for many years, and in the end the company actually saves money on repairs and replacements.","t":"A：外送公司為什麼選這些腳踏車，即使它們比其他供應商的便宜款式還貴？ B：它們非常【耐用】，可以在雨天和高溫下每天使用好幾年，所以最後公司其實在維修和更換上省了錢。"},{"w":"maintenance","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping something in good condition","c":"保養；維修","s":"A: How often should the office send the shared bikes to the repair shop to make sure they stay in good condition? B: They should get regular maintenance every three months, including cleaning, oiling the chains, and checking the brakes, so small problems don't turn into expensive repairs later.","t":"A：辦公室應該多久把共用腳踏車送去修車店一次，以確保它們維持良好狀態？ B：它們應該每三個月做一次定期【保養】，包括清潔、替鏈條上油和檢查煞車，這樣小問題才不會在之後變成昂貴的維修。"},{"w":"fitness","p":"n.","d":"the condition of being healthy and strong","c":"健康；體能","s":"A: Have you noticed that Daniel seems much healthier and more energetic at work since the beginning of this year? B: Yes, he started cycling thirty kilometers every weekend to improve his fitness, and he told me he has lost five kilos and sleeps much better than before.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到，從今年年初開始，丹尼爾在工作時看起來健康許多、也更有活力？ B：有，他開始每個週末騎三十公里來提升【體能】，他告訴我他瘦了五公斤，而且睡得比以前好多了。"},{"w":"eco-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"not harmful to the environment","c":"環保的；對環境友善的","s":"A: Why is the city government giving free bike passes to office workers in the downtown area this year? B: It wants people to choose a more eco-friendly way to get to work, because fewer cars mean cleaner air, less noise, and lower carbon emissions for everyone living in the city.","t":"A：市政府今年為什麼要發免費的腳踏車通行證給市中心的上班族？ B：它希望大家選擇更【環保】的方式上班，因為汽車少了，代表城市裡的每個人都能享有更乾淨的空氣、更少的噪音和更低的碳排放。"}]},{"unit":29,"theme":"Birds 鳥類","cards":[{"w":"keen","p":"adj.","d":"very interested in something and eager to do it","c":"熱衷的；渴望的","s":"A: Why did the marketing director ask Linda to plan the company's weekend trip to the wetlands park this year instead of hiring a travel agency? B: Linda is very keen on bird watching, so she already knows the best walking paths, the quietest viewing spots, and the time when most of the birds come out to feed.","t":"A：為什麼行銷總監今年要琳達規劃公司週末去濕地公園的旅遊，而不是請旅行社？ B：琳達非常【熱衷於】賞鳥，所以她早就知道最好的步道、最安靜的觀賞地點，以及大部分鳥類出來覓食的時間。"},{"w":"fond","p":"adj.","d":"liking someone or something very much","c":"喜愛的","s":"A: Why does Mr. Chen always eat his lunch on the bench beside the pond instead of joining the rest of the team in the staff cafeteria? B: He has always been fond of the ducks and small birds that live there, and he says that watching them for twenty minutes helps him relax before his busy afternoon meetings.","t":"A：為什麼陳先生總是在池塘邊的長椅上吃午餐，而不是和團隊其他人一起去員工餐廳？ B：他一直都很【喜愛】住在那裡的鴨子和小鳥，他說看牠們二十分鐘能幫助他在忙碌的下午會議前放鬆。"},{"w":"attract","p":"v.","d":"to make a person or animal come to a place","c":"吸引","s":"A: The hotel garden looks so quiet these days, so what is the manager planning to do before the spring tourist season begins next month? B: She has ordered several wooden feeders and some colorful flowering plants to attract more birds, because many of our guests enjoy taking photos of wildlife while they have breakfast on the terrace.","t":"A：飯店花園最近看起來好冷清，經理打算在下個月春季旅遊旺季開始前做些什麼？ B：她訂購了幾個木製餵食器和一些色彩鮮豔的開花植物，來【吸引】更多鳥類，因為我們許多客人喜歡在露台吃早餐時拍野生動物的照片。"},{"w":"creature","p":"n.","d":"a living animal, especially a small or unusual one","c":"生物；動物","s":"A: What did the children in the after-school nature class find most exciting about yesterday's field trip to the forest center? B: They loved the guided walk, but the best moment was when the guide showed them a tiny creature with bright blue feathers sitting quietly on a branch just above the visitors' path.","t":"A：課後自然課的孩子們覺得昨天去森林中心的校外教學中最令人興奮的是什麼？ B：他們很喜歡導覽步行，但最精彩的時刻是導遊讓他們看到一隻有著亮藍色羽毛的小【生物】，靜靜地停在遊客步道正上方的樹枝上。"},{"w":"vertebrate","p":"n.","d":"an animal that has a backbone","c":"脊椎動物","s":"A: Our new exhibition sign at the science museum needs a simple explanation, so how should we describe birds for the young visitors? B: We could say that a bird is a vertebrate, which means it has a backbone just like fish, frogs, snakes, and people, and then add a colorful picture of a bird's skeleton next to the text.","t":"A：我們科學博物館的新展覽告示牌需要簡單的說明，那我們要如何向年輕參觀者描述鳥類？ B：我們可以說鳥是一種【脊椎動物】，意思是牠和魚、青蛙、蛇以及人一樣有脊椎，然後在文字旁邊加上一張彩色的鳥類骨骼圖。"},{"w":"feather","p":"n.","d":"one of the soft, light parts that cover a bird's body","c":"羽毛","s":"A: Why did the furniture company decide to stop selling the expensive pillows that were so popular in last year's winter catalog? B: Several customers complained that a feather kept coming out through the cotton cover every night, so the product team is now testing a stronger cover and a different filling.","t":"A：為什麼家具公司決定停賣那款在去年冬季型錄中很受歡迎的昂貴枕頭？ B：好幾位顧客抱怨每天晚上都有【羽毛】從棉質枕套裡跑出來，所以產品團隊現在正在測試更牢固的枕套和不同的填充物。"},{"w":"beak","p":"n.","d":"the hard, pointed mouth of a bird","c":"鳥喙","s":"A: How did the zoo's animal doctor know that the old parrot was sick, even though it still looked active and noisy in the bird house? B: She noticed that its beak had a small crack near the tip, so the bird could not break open its seeds properly and had been eating much less food than usual.","t":"A：雖然那隻老鸚鵡在鳥舍裡看起來仍然很活潑又吵鬧，動物園的獸醫怎麼知道牠生病了？ B：她注意到牠的【鳥喙】靠近尖端處有一道小裂縫，所以這隻鳥無法好好啄開種子，吃的食物也比平常少了很多。"},{"w":"Aves","p":"n.","d":"the scientific name for the class of all birds","c":"鳥綱（鳥類的學名）","s":"A: The publisher wants the new animal guidebook to look more professional, so what should we print at the top of the chapter about birds? B: Let's print the scientific class name Aves under the main title, and then explain in a short note that every bird, from the tiny hummingbird to the huge ostrich, belongs to this group.","t":"A：出版社希望新的動物圖鑑看起來更專業，那我們應該在鳥類那一章的頂端印些什麼？ B：我們在主標題下方印上科學分類名稱【鳥綱】，然後用一段簡短說明解釋每一種鳥，從小小的蜂鳥到巨大的鴕鳥，都屬於這一類。"},{"w":"distinctive","p":"adj.","d":"special or different, so it is easy to recognize","c":"獨特的；與眾不同的","s":"A: Why did the design team choose a small red bird for the new logo instead of the blue circle that the director first suggested? B: They wanted something distinctive that customers would remember after seeing it only once, and the red bird stands out clearly on our product boxes, website, and delivery trucks.","t":"A：為什麼設計團隊為新標誌選了一隻小紅鳥，而不是總監一開始建議的藍色圓圈？ B：他們想要一個【獨特的】東西，讓顧客只看一次就記得，而且這隻紅鳥在我們的產品盒子、網站和送貨卡車上都非常顯眼。"},{"w":"flora","p":"n.","d":"all the plants that grow in a particular area","c":"植物群；（某地區的）植物","s":"A: What will the tour guide talk about during the first part of the afternoon nature walk around the island for our company group? B: She will first introduce the local flora, such as the tall palm trees and wild orchids, and explain how these plants give the island's birds both food and safe places to rest.","t":"A：導遊在下午為我們公司團體安排的環島自然步行前半段會介紹什麼？ B：她會先介紹當地的【植物】，例如高大的棕櫚樹和野生蘭花，並說明這些植物如何為島上的鳥類提供食物和安全的休息處。"},{"w":"fauna","p":"n.","d":"all the animals that live in a particular area","c":"動物群；（某地區的）動物","s":"A: Why is the environmental group asking our construction company to delay the new factory project near the river until next year? B: They are worried that the noise and dust will harm the local fauna, especially the rare birds, frogs, and fish that depend on the quiet riverbanks during their breeding season.","t":"A：為什麼環保團體要求我們的營建公司把河邊的新工廠案延到明年？ B：他們擔心噪音和灰塵會傷害當地的【動物】，尤其是在繁殖季節依賴安靜河岸的珍稀鳥類、青蛙和魚類。"},{"w":"rare","p":"adj.","d":"not seen or found very often","c":"稀有的；罕見的","s":"A: Why were so many photographers waiting outside the city park with their big cameras when I walked past this morning on my way to the office? B: A birdwatcher posted online that a rare owl from the mountains had been seen there, so people came early hoping to get a picture before it flew away.","t":"A：今天早上我走路去辦公室經過時，為什麼有那麼多攝影師帶著大相機在市立公園外等？ B：一位賞鳥人士在網路上發文說，有人在那裡看見一隻來自山區的【稀有】貓頭鷹，所以大家一早就來，希望在牠飛走前拍到照片。"},{"w":"shiny","p":"adj.","d":"bright and reflecting light","c":"發亮的；閃亮的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant staff put plastic covers over the outdoor tables after the lunch rush ended yesterday afternoon? B: A group of crows kept landing on the patio and stealing the shiny spoons and forks, so the manager decided to protect the silverware until the birds stop visiting.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳員工昨天下午午餐尖峰過後，要在戶外餐桌上蓋上塑膠罩？ B：有一群烏鴉一直降落在露台上偷走【亮晶晶的】湯匙和叉子，所以經理決定在那些鳥不再來之前先保護好餐具。"},{"w":"breed","p":"v.","d":"to keep animals so that they produce young animals","c":"繁殖；飼養","s":"A: How does the small family farm outside the city make enough money now that fewer people are buying their fresh vegetables at the market? B: The owners started to breed chickens and ducks for local restaurants, and they also sell the eggs online, which has become their most successful product this year.","t":"A：現在在市場買新鮮蔬菜的人變少了，城外那座小型家庭農場要如何賺足夠的錢？ B：農場主人開始【繁殖飼養】雞和鴨供應給當地餐廳，他們也在網路上賣雞蛋，這已成為他們今年最成功的產品。"},{"w":"pigeon","p":"n.","d":"a gray bird often seen in cities and parks","c":"鴿子","s":"A: Why is the building manager putting thin metal spikes along the edges of the roof and above all the office windows this week? B: Every pigeon from the train station seems to land on our roof, and the birds leave such a mess on the windows that the cleaning company says washing them every day costs too much.","t":"A：為什麼大樓管理員這週要在屋頂邊緣和所有辦公室窗戶上方裝上細細的金屬尖刺？ B：火車站那邊的每一隻【鴿子】似乎都會降落在我們的屋頂上，而且這些鳥把窗戶弄得好髒，清潔公司說每天清洗的費用太高了。"},{"w":"sparrow","p":"n.","d":"a small, common brown bird","c":"麻雀","s":"A: What was that small brown bird that flew into the café this morning and made all the customers laugh while they were waiting in line? B: It was just a sparrow looking for bread crumbs, and after one of our servers opened the back door, it hopped outside and flew up into the tree by the parking lot.","t":"A：今天早上飛進咖啡廳、讓排隊的客人都笑出來的那隻棕色小鳥是什麼？ B：那只是一隻在找麵包屑的【麻雀】，我們一位服務生打開後門後，牠就跳到外面，飛上停車場旁的那棵樹。"},{"w":"finch","p":"n.","d":"a small singing bird with a short, thick beak","c":"雀鳥（雀科鳴禽）","s":"A: My manager wants a small pet for the reception area that is quiet, cheerful, and easy to care for, so what would you recommend from your shop? B: I would suggest a finch, because it is a small, colorful songbird that eats simple seeds, does not need much space, and sings softly enough not to disturb your visitors.","t":"A：我的經理想為接待區找一隻安靜、討喜又好照顧的小寵物，你會推薦你們店裡的哪一種？ B：我建議養一隻【雀鳥】，因為牠是一種色彩繽紛的小型鳴禽，吃簡單的種子、不需要太多空間，而且歌聲輕柔，不會打擾你們的訪客。"},{"w":"exotic","p":"adj.","d":"coming from a faraway country and unusual","c":"異國的；外來的；奇特的","s":"A: Why has the number of visitors to the botanical garden increased so much since the new section opened in the summer? B: The garden built a warm glass house full of exotic birds from South America and Africa, and many families now visit on weekends to see their bright colors and listen to their unusual songs.","t":"A：為什麼植物園從夏天新區開放後，遊客人數增加了那麼多？ B：植物園蓋了一座溫暖的玻璃屋，裡面滿是來自南美洲和非洲的【異國】鳥類，現在很多家庭週末都會來看牠們鮮豔的色彩、聽牠們奇特的歌聲。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"far away from towns and cities","c":"偏遠的","s":"A: Why does the research team need a helicopter for their bird study next month instead of driving there in the company vans? B: The birds they want to study only live on a remote island about two hundred kilometers from the coast, and there are no roads, ferries, or hotels anywhere near it.","t":"A：為什麼研究團隊下個月的鳥類研究需要直升機，而不是開公司的廂型車去？ B：他們想研究的鳥只住在離海岸約兩百公里的一座【偏遠的】島上，而且附近完全沒有道路、渡輪或旅館。"},{"w":"hunt","p":"v.","d":"to chase and catch animals for food or sport","c":"狩獵；獵捕","s":"A: Why did the national park office put up so many new signs near the lake entrance before the autumn holiday weekend? B: The signs tell visitors that it is against the law to hunt the ducks and geese in the park, because the number of these birds has dropped sharply over the past few years.","t":"A：為什麼國家公園管理處在秋季連假前，在湖畔入口附近豎立了那麼多新告示牌？ B：告示牌告訴遊客，在園內【獵捕】鴨子和鵝是違法的，因為這些鳥的數量在過去幾年大幅減少。"},{"w":"roast","p":"v.","d":"to cook meat in an oven or over a fire","c":"烤；烘烤","s":"A: The hotel is hosting a large holiday dinner for our clients next Friday, so how will the kitchen prepare the main dish for so many guests? B: The head chef plans to roast twenty turkeys slowly in the big ovens for several hours, and then serve them with potatoes, fresh vegetables, and a special fruit sauce.","t":"A：飯店下週五要為我們的客戶舉辦大型節日晚宴，廚房要如何為這麼多客人準備主菜？ B：主廚打算用大烤箱慢慢地【烤】二十隻火雞好幾個小時，然後搭配馬鈴薯、新鮮蔬菜和特製水果醬一起上菜。"},{"w":"game birds","p":"n.phr.","d":"wild birds that people hunt for sport or food","c":"獵禽（可狩獵食用的野鳥）","s":"A: Why does the new restaurant near the old castle have such a short menu and change it every few weeks during the autumn and winter? B: The chef only cooks game birds, such as wild duck, pheasant, and quail, that local hunters bring in each week, so the dishes depend on what is available during the season.","t":"A：為什麼古堡附近那家新餐廳的菜單那麼短，而且在秋冬期間每幾週就換一次？ B：主廚只烹調當地獵人每週送來的【獵禽】，像是野鴨、雉雞和鵪鶉，所以菜色取決於當季能取得的食材。"},{"w":"delicacy","p":"n.","d":"a rare or expensive food that people think is special","c":"珍饈；美味佳餚","s":"A: What dish should we order for the visiting Japanese clients at tonight's business dinner if we want them to try something truly local? B: Let's order the roast pigeon, which is a famous delicacy in this region, and the restaurant only serves a few plates each night, so I will call now to reserve two.","t":"A：如果我們想讓來訪的日本客戶嚐嚐道地的料理，今晚的商務晚宴該點什麼菜？ B：我們點烤乳鴿吧，那是這個地區有名的【美味佳餚】，而且餐廳每晚只供應幾盤，所以我現在就打電話預訂兩份。"},{"w":"cage","p":"n.","d":"a box made of wire or bars for keeping birds or animals","c":"籠子","s":"A: The pet shop customer said her parrot keeps trying to escape, so what advice did you give her before she left the store? B: I told her to buy a bigger cage with a stronger lock on the door, because a bird that has too little space often gets bored and looks for ways to get out.","t":"A：那位寵物店顧客說她的鸚鵡一直想逃跑，她離開店之前你給了她什麼建議？ B：我告訴她買一個更大、門鎖更牢固的【籠子】，因為空間太小的鳥常常會覺得無聊，並想辦法跑出來。"},{"w":"nest","p":"n.","d":"a place a bird builds to lay its eggs and keep its babies","c":"鳥巢","s":"A: Why haven't the workers started painting the outside of the office building yet, even though the job was supposed to begin on Monday? B: They found a nest with four small eggs under the roof near the main entrance, so the manager decided to wait until the young birds can fly before the painting begins.","t":"A：為什麼工人還沒開始粉刷辦公大樓外牆，明明工程應該在星期一開始？ B：他們在主要入口附近的屋簷下發現一個有四顆小蛋的【鳥巢】，所以經理決定等到幼鳥會飛之後再開始粉刷。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural place where an animal or plant lives","c":"棲息地","s":"A: Why is our company giving money to the wetland project this year instead of sponsoring the city marathon like we did before? B: The CEO believes we should help protect the natural habitat of the water birds, since the new housing developments near the coast have already destroyed many of the places where they feed and rest.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司今年要捐錢給濕地計畫，而不是像以前那樣贊助城市馬拉松？ B：執行長認為我們應該幫忙保護水鳥的自然【棲息地】，因為沿海附近的新住宅開發已經破壞了許多牠們覓食和休息的地方。"},{"w":"perch","p":"v.","d":"(of a bird) to sit on a branch or an edge","c":"（鳥）棲息；停歇","s":"A: Why did the café owner put a small wooden bar outside the front window when she redecorated the shop last month? B: She noticed that birds like to perch near the window in the morning, so she gave them a safe place to sit, and now customers enjoy watching them while they drink their coffee.","t":"A：為什麼咖啡廳老闆上個月重新裝潢店面時，在前窗外放了一根小木桿？ B：她注意到鳥兒喜歡在早上【停歇】在窗戶附近，所以她給牠們一個安全的地方坐，現在客人都喜歡一邊喝咖啡一邊看牠們。"},{"w":"amuse","p":"v.","d":"to make someone laugh or smile","c":"逗樂；使開心","s":"A: The children in the hospital waiting room looked bored and tired this morning, so what did the nurses do to make them feel better? B: A volunteer brought a friendly talking parrot to amuse them, and the kids laughed loudly every time the bird said hello or copied the sound of a ringing phone.","t":"A：今天早上醫院候診室的孩子們看起來又無聊又疲倦，護理師們做了什麼讓他們感覺好一點？ B：一位志工帶來一隻友善、會說話的鸚鵡來【逗樂】他們，每次那隻鳥說哈囉或模仿電話鈴聲時，孩子們都大聲笑出來。"}]},{"unit":30,"theme":"Birthday 生日","cards":[{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable for a special day or success","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Our department finally reached its sales target for the year, so what are we planning to do for the team before the holiday break starts next week? B: The director wants to celebrate the success with a dinner at the Italian restaurant downtown on Friday evening, and she has already booked a private room for everyone.","t":"A：我們部門終於達成了今年的業績目標，那在下週假期開始前，我們打算為團隊做些什麼？ B：主任想在週五晚上到市中心的義大利餐廳【慶祝】這次的成功，而且她已經為大家訂好了包廂。"},{"w":"party","p":"n.","d":"a social event where people meet to eat, drink and have fun","c":"派對；聚會","s":"A: Do you know why the conference room on the third floor is closed this afternoon, because I wanted to use it for a quick meeting with a supplier? B: The human resources team is holding a birthday party there for Mr. Chen at three o'clock, so you could book the small meeting room near the elevator instead.","t":"A：你知道為什麼三樓的會議室今天下午不開放嗎？因為我想用它和供應商開個簡短的會議。 B：人資團隊三點要在那裡為陳先生舉辦生日【派對】，所以你可以改訂電梯旁邊的小會議室。"},{"w":"cake","p":"n.","d":"a sweet baked food, often eaten at birthdays","c":"蛋糕","s":"A: I'm going to the bakery on Main Street during my lunch break, so is there anything special you would like me to order for Linda's birthday tomorrow? B: Could you please order a chocolate cake large enough for twenty people, and ask them to write her name on top, because the whole office will be celebrating together after the morning meeting?","t":"A：我午休時要去大街上的麵包店，明天琳達生日，你有什麼特別想要我訂的嗎？ B：可以請你訂一個夠二十個人吃的巧克力【蛋糕】，並請他們在上面寫她的名字嗎？因為早上開完會後全辦公室要一起慶祝。"},{"w":"candle","p":"n.","d":"a stick of wax that gives light when it burns","c":"蠟燭","s":"A: The hotel manager said we have to follow strict safety rules at the banquet hall, so are we still allowed to have a real fire on the birthday cake tonight? B: Yes, but only one small candle is permitted, and a staff member must stand nearby with a fire extinguisher until the guest of honor blows it out.","t":"A：飯店經理說我們在宴會廳必須遵守嚴格的安全規定，那今晚生日蛋糕上還可以點真的火嗎？ B：可以，但只允許一根小【蠟燭】，而且在壽星吹熄之前，必須有一位工作人員拿著滅火器站在旁邊。"},{"w":"gift","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone without asking for payment","c":"禮物；贈品","s":"A: Our most important client from Japan is turning sixty next month, so what should our company send him to show our appreciation for his long business relationship with us? B: I think a high-quality tea set would be a thoughtful gift, and we should include a handwritten note from the president thanking him for twenty years of cooperation.","t":"A：我們最重要的日本客戶下個月滿六十歲，我們公司應該送他什麼來感謝他與我們長久的業務往來？ B：我覺得一套高品質的茶具會是很貼心的【禮物】，而且我們應該附上一張總裁的親筆短箋，感謝他二十年來的合作。"},{"w":"present","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone on a special day","c":"禮物","s":"A: Everyone in the accounting department is giving fifty dollars for Peter's birthday this Friday, but have we decided what to buy him with the money yet? B: Sarah suggested a new pair of wireless headphones as a present, since he often complains about the noise in the office while he is working on the monthly reports.","t":"A：會計部的每個人都為彼得這週五的生日出了五十美元，但我們決定好要用這筆錢買什麼給他了嗎？ B：莎拉建議買一副新的無線耳機當作【禮物】，因為他在做每月報表時常常抱怨辦公室很吵。"},{"w":"wish","p":"v.","d":"to say that you hope someone will have something good","c":"祝；祝福","s":"A: I heard that the vice president is leaving for a business trip to London on the same day as his birthday, so how can the team show that we remember it? B: We could all sign a card and give it to him at the airport, so we can wish him a happy birthday and a safe flight before he boards the plane.","t":"A：我聽說副總裁生日當天要出發去倫敦出差，那團隊要怎麼表示我們記得他的生日？ B：我們可以大家一起在卡片上簽名，然後在機場交給他，這樣就能在他登機前【祝】他生日快樂、一路平安。"},{"w":"balloon","p":"n.","d":"a small colorful rubber bag filled with air or gas","c":"氣球","s":"A: The children's birthday event at the shopping mall starts at ten o'clock on Saturday morning, so what still needs to be done to get the stage ready? B: We still need to tie a big red balloon to every chair in the front row, and then the sound technician has to test the microphones before the families begin to arrive.","t":"A：購物中心的兒童生日活動星期六早上十點開始，那要把舞台準備好還有什麼事要做？ B：我們還需要在第一排的每張椅子上綁一顆大紅【氣球】，然後音響技師要在各個家庭開始抵達前測試麥克風。"},{"w":"card","p":"n.","d":"a folded piece of thick paper with a picture and a message","c":"卡片","s":"A: Ms. Wang from the marketing team is celebrating her fortieth birthday on Monday, but she is working at our branch office in Kaohsiung all week, so what can we do? B: Let's buy a large birthday card, ask everyone here to write a short message in it, and send it by express mail so it arrives before the weekend.","t":"A：行銷部的王小姐星期一要過四十歲生日，但她整週都在我們高雄的分公司工作，那我們能做些什麼？ B：我們去買一張大的生日【卡片】，請這裡的每個人在上面寫一段簡短的話，然後用快遞寄出，這樣週末前就能送到。"},{"w":"surprise","p":"n.","d":"something that happens that you did not expect","c":"驚喜；意外","s":"A: Why did the manager ask all of us to hide in the meeting room and turn off the lights at exactly five o'clock this afternoon? B: It's Kevin's birthday today, and she wants it to be a complete surprise, so please stay quiet and don't send him any messages until he walks through the door.","t":"A：為什麼經理要我們全部的人在今天下午五點整躲進會議室並把燈關掉？ B：今天是凱文的生日，她希望這是一個完全的【驚喜】，所以請保持安靜，而且在他走進門之前不要傳任何訊息給他。"},{"w":"invite","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone to come to an event","c":"邀請","s":"A: The restaurant can only hold thirty people for the company's tenth birthday dinner next month, so how are we going to choose who can attend? B: The general manager has decided to invite our top ten clients and their partners first, and then the remaining seats will be offered to employees who have worked here the longest.","t":"A：下個月公司十週年的晚宴，餐廳只能容納三十人，那我們要怎麼決定誰可以參加？ B：總經理決定先【邀請】我們前十大客戶及其伴侶，然後剩下的座位會提供給在這裡服務最久的員工。"},{"w":"guest","p":"n.","d":"a person who is invited to an event or a home","c":"賓客；客人","s":"A: Have you finished the seating plan for Mr. Lin's birthday banquet at the Grand Hotel, because the event coordinator needs it by tomorrow morning? B: Almost, but one more guest confirmed this afternoon that she is coming from Singapore, so I need to add another chair at the table near the stage.","t":"A：你完成林先生在格蘭大飯店生日晚宴的座位安排了嗎？因為活動協調人明天早上就要。 B：快好了，但今天下午又有一位【賓客】確認她會從新加坡過來，所以我需要在靠近舞台的那桌再加一張椅子。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make a place look nicer by adding pretty things","c":"裝飾；佈置","s":"A: The office looks really plain for tomorrow's birthday lunch, and the guests from head office will arrive at noon, so what should we do tonight? B: A few of us will stay after work to decorate the break room with paper flowers, colorful lights, and a banner, so it will look cheerful when everyone walks in.","t":"A：明天的生日午餐，辦公室看起來真的很單調，而且總公司的客人中午就會到，那我們今晚該做什麼？ B：我們幾個人下班後會留下來，用紙花、彩色燈串和一條布條【裝飾】休息室，這樣大家走進來時就會覺得很歡樂。"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"a thing used to make a place look attractive","c":"裝飾；裝飾品","s":"A: The event company sent us a bill for the hotel birthday celebration, but why is the total so much higher than the price we agreed on last month? B: They charged us extra for the decoration on every table, including the flowers and gold ribbons, which the client asked for at the last minute without telling our department.","t":"A：活動公司寄來了飯店生日慶祝會的帳單，但為什麼總金額比我們上個月談好的價格高出這麼多？ B：他們為每張桌子上的【裝飾】額外收費，包括花和金色緞帶，那是客戶在最後一刻要求的，卻沒有告訴我們部門。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a special event to enjoy an important day or success","c":"慶祝活動；慶典","s":"A: Our company is turning fifty years old this spring, so is the board planning any special events for the employees and their families? B: Yes, there will be a big celebration at the city park on the last Saturday of April, with live music, food stands, and games for children, and every worker can bring three guests.","t":"A：我們公司今年春天滿五十週年，董事會有計劃為員工和家屬舉辦什麼特別活動嗎？ B：有，四月最後一個星期六會在市立公園舉辦盛大的【慶祝活動】，有現場音樂、食物攤位和兒童遊戲，每位員工可以帶三位賓客。"},{"w":"song","p":"n.","d":"a short piece of music with words that you sing","c":"歌；歌曲","s":"A: When the waiters bring out the cake for Mr. Huang's birthday at the end of dinner tonight, what should the rest of us at the table do? B: We'll all stand up and sing the birthday song together, and then the president will give a short speech to thank him for his hard work this year.","t":"A：今晚晚餐結束時，服務生端出黃先生的生日蛋糕，我們桌上其他人該做什麼？ B：我們會全部站起來一起唱生日【歌】，然後總裁會發表簡短的致詞，感謝他今年的辛勞。"},{"w":"age","p":"n.","d":"the number of years a person has lived","c":"年齡","s":"A: The new gym near our office is offering a free birthday membership this month, but can anyone in the company sign up for it? B: No, there is a minimum age of eighteen, so the summer interns cannot join, but all full-time staff can register at the front desk with their employee cards.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近新開的健身房這個月提供免費的生日會員資格，但公司裡的任何人都可以報名嗎？ B：不行，最低【年齡】是十八歲，所以暑期實習生不能加入，但所有全職員工都可以拿員工證到櫃台登記。"},{"w":"special","p":"adj.","d":"better or more important than usual","c":"特別的","s":"A: Our sales director is celebrating his birthday during the trade show in Berlin, so is there anything we can arrange for him after the busy exhibition day? B: I've booked a special dinner at a famous German restaurant near the hotel, and the chef will prepare a dessert with his name written on the plate.","t":"A：我們的業務總監在柏林商展期間過生日，那在忙碌的展覽日結束後，我們有什麼可以為他安排的嗎？ B：我在飯店附近一家有名的德國餐廳訂了一頓【特別的】晚餐，主廚會準備一道在盤子上寫著他名字的甜點。"},{"w":"happy","p":"adj.","d":"feeling pleased and glad","c":"快樂的；高興的","s":"A: How did Ms. Lee react when she saw that the whole department had stayed late to prepare a birthday surprise for her yesterday evening? B: She was so happy that she almost cried, and she told us it was the best birthday she has had since she joined the company five years ago.","t":"A：昨天傍晚李小姐看到整個部門留下來為她準備生日驚喜時，她有什麼反應？ B：她【高興】到差點哭出來，還告訴我們這是她五年前進公司以來最棒的一次生日。"},{"w":"treat","p":"n.","d":"something nice that you buy or do for someone","c":"請客；招待（的東西）","s":"A: Why is there a big box of chocolates and fresh fruit on the reception desk this morning, and who brought it into the office? B: It's Daniel's birthday, so he bought it as a treat for everyone, and he said we can take as much as we like during our coffee break.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上接待櫃台上有一大盒巧克力和新鮮水果，是誰帶進辦公室的？ B：今天是丹尼爾的生日，所以他買來當作給大家的【招待點心】，他說我們在喝咖啡休息時間想拿多少都可以。"},{"w":"family","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who are related, such as parents and children","c":"家人；家庭","s":"A: Are you going to join the team at the karaoke bar after work on Friday to celebrate Tom's promotion and his birthday at the same time? B: I'm sorry, but I can't come, because my whole family is coming up from Tainan by high-speed train that evening for my grandmother's eightieth birthday dinner, and I promised to pick them up.","t":"A：你週五下班後要和團隊一起去KTV同時慶祝湯姆升職和生日嗎？ B：很抱歉我不能去，因為那天晚上我全【家】人要坐高鐵從台南上來參加我奶奶的八十歲生日晚餐，而我答應要去接他們。"},{"w":"friend","p":"n.","d":"a person you know well and like","c":"朋友","s":"A: Who is the woman talking with the CEO near the window, because I don't think she works in our building or for any of our partners? B: She is an old friend of his from university, and she flew in from Canada to surprise him at his birthday reception, so they haven't stopped talking all evening.","t":"A：在窗邊和執行長說話的那位女士是誰？因為我不覺得她在我們大樓工作，也不像是我們合作夥伴的人。 B：她是他大學時代的老【朋友】，特地從加拿大飛過來在他的生日酒會上給他驚喜，所以他們整晚都聊個不停。"},{"w":"photo","p":"n.","d":"a picture taken with a camera","c":"照片","s":"A: The marketing department wants to post something on the company website about yesterday's birthday celebration for our founder, so do we have any good pictures? B: Yes, the photographer took a great group photo of all the employees standing in front of the building, and I'll email it to you before lunch.","t":"A：行銷部想在公司網站上發布關於昨天創辦人生日慶祝會的內容，那我們有好的照片嗎？ B：有，攝影師拍了一張很棒的全體員工站在大樓前的團體【照】，我會在午餐前用電子郵件寄給你。"},{"w":"memory","p":"n.","d":"something from the past that you remember","c":"回憶；記憶","s":"A: You have worked at this company for over thirty years, so what is your favorite moment from all the events and parties you have attended here? B: My best memory is the surprise birthday dinner my team organized during my first year, when everyone secretly saved money for weeks to buy me a watch.","t":"A：你在這家公司工作超過三十年了，在這裡參加過的所有活動和派對中，你最喜歡的時刻是什麼？ B：我最美好的【回憶】是我第一年時團隊為我籌辦的驚喜生日晚餐，那時大家偷偷存了好幾週的錢買了一支手錶給我。"},{"w":"greeting","p":"n.","d":"words or actions used to say hello or send good wishes","c":"問候；祝賀","s":"A: Our online store wants to keep loyal customers coming back, so what new idea did the marketing team suggest at this morning's meeting? B: They plan to send every member a personal birthday greeting by email, together with a coupon for fifteen percent off any item purchased during their birthday month.","t":"A：我們的網路商店想讓忠實顧客持續回購，那行銷團隊在今天早上的會議中提出了什麼新點子？ B：他們打算透過電子郵件寄給每位會員一封個人化的生日【祝福】，並附上一張在生日當月購買任何商品都可享八五折的優惠券。"},{"w":"fun","p":"adj.","d":"enjoyable and pleasant","c":"好玩的；有趣的","s":"A: How was the team-building trip to the beach that the company organized for the manager's fiftieth birthday last weekend? B: It was really fun, because we played volleyball, had a barbecue by the sea, and sang songs around a campfire, and even the quiet engineers from the research department joined in.","t":"A：上週末公司為經理五十歲生日舉辦的海灘團隊建立旅行怎麼樣？ B：真的很【好玩】，因為我們打了排球、在海邊烤肉，還圍著營火唱歌，連研發部那些安靜的工程師也都加入了。"},{"w":"party hat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a colorful paper hat worn at a party","c":"派對帽","s":"A: The photographer for the children's birthday event at the toy store wants a cute picture for the advertisement, so what should each kid wear? B: Please give every child a colorful paper party hat and a small flag with our store logo, and ask them to stand together in front of the big window display.","t":"A：玩具店兒童生日活動的攝影師想要一張可愛的照片用在廣告上，那每個小孩應該戴什麼？ B：請給每個小孩一頂彩色紙製【派對帽】和一面印有我們商店標誌的小旗子，並請他們一起站在大型櫥窗展示前面。"},{"w":"celebratory","p":"adj.","d":"done to celebrate a happy event","c":"慶祝的","s":"A: The CEO just announced that we won the government contract, and it's also her birthday today, so what has the office manager arranged for this evening? B: She has ordered a celebratory dinner with champagne at the rooftop restaurant, and everyone in the project team is invited to join after work.","t":"A：執行長剛宣布我們拿到了政府合約，而今天剛好也是她的生日，那辦公室經理為今晚安排了什麼？ B：她在頂樓餐廳訂了一頓有香檳的【慶祝】晚餐，專案團隊的每個人下班後都受邀參加。"}]},{"unit":31,"theme":"Book 書籍","cards":[{"w":"author","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes a book","c":"作者；作家","s":"A: Who is going to speak at the bookstore event next Friday evening, and do we need to prepare extra chairs for the guests? B: The author of the new business guide will talk about her career, so please set up about fifty chairs and ask the café staff to serve coffee after her speech.","t":"A：下週五晚上誰要在書店活動上演講？我們需要為來賓準備額外的椅子嗎？ B：那本新商業指南的【作者】會談談她的職涯，所以請擺大約五十張椅子，並請咖啡廳員工在她演講後供應咖啡。"},{"w":"title","p":"n.","d":"the name of a book or other piece of writing","c":"書名；標題","s":"A: Have you decided what to call the new guide for small business owners, or is the marketing team still arguing about it? B: We finally agreed on a short and simple title, so the designer can start working on the front of the book, and we can send it to the printer next week.","t":"A：你們決定好那本給小企業主的新指南要叫什麼名字了嗎？還是行銷團隊還在爭論？ B：我們終於同意採用一個簡短的【書名】，所以設計師可以開始設計書的封面，我們下週就能把它送去印刷廠。"},{"w":"chapter","p":"n.","d":"one of the main parts of a book","c":"章；章節","s":"A: How much of the training manual have you finished translating, because the Tokyo office needs it before the workshop starts? B: I have completed the first chapter about customer service, and I will finish the part on handling complaints by Thursday if nobody gives me extra work this week.","t":"A：那本訓練手冊你翻譯完多少了？因為東京辦公室在研習開始前就需要它。 B：我已經完成了關於客戶服務的第一【章】，如果這週沒有人給我額外工作，我會在星期四前完成處理客訴的部分。"},{"w":"page","p":"n.","d":"one side of a sheet of paper in a book","c":"頁；頁面","s":"A: Why did the printer call us this morning, and is there a problem with the catalog we sent them yesterday? B: Yes, one page near the end is missing the product prices, so they have stopped printing until we send them a corrected file before noon today.","t":"A：印刷廠今天早上為什麼打電話給我們？我們昨天寄給他們的型錄有問題嗎？ B：是的，接近最後的一【頁】少了產品價格，所以他們暫停印刷，直到我們今天中午前寄給他們修正過的檔案。"},{"w":"cover","p":"n.","d":"the outside front and back of a book","c":"封面；書皮","s":"A: What do customers usually notice first when they walk past the new books table at the front of our store? B: Most people look at the cover, so we chose bright colors and a large photo of the city to make the travel guide stand out from the others.","t":"A：顧客走過我們店門口的新書桌時，通常最先注意到什麼？ B：大多數人會看【封面】，所以我們選了鮮豔的顏色和一張大幅城市照片，讓這本旅遊指南在其他書中脫穎而出。"},{"w":"genre","p":"n.","d":"a type of book, film, or music","c":"類型；體裁","s":"A: Which kind of books should we put on the main display this month, since sales have been slow since the holidays? B: Mystery is the most popular genre with our customers right now, so let's choose ten crime stories and add a small sign that offers a twenty percent discount.","t":"A：既然假期後銷售一直很慢，我們這個月應該在主要展示區放哪一類書？ B：推理是目前我們顧客最喜歡的【類型】，所以我們選十本犯罪小說，再加一個提供八折優惠的小標示。"},{"w":"novel","p":"n.","d":"a long story about imaginary people and events","c":"小說","s":"A: What is the new book by the famous journalist about, and should we order more copies for the store before the weekend? B: It is her first novel, a long story about a family running a small hotel, and early reviews are so good that we should order at least two hundred copies.","t":"A：那位知名記者的新書是關於什麼的？我們週末前應該為店裡多訂一些嗎？ B：這是她的第一本【小說】，一個關於一家人經營小旅館的長篇故事，早期書評非常好，我們應該至少訂兩百本。"},{"w":"fiction","p":"n.","d":"stories about imaginary people and events","c":"小說；虛構作品","s":"A: Why are you moving all those books to the second floor, and where will customers find the travel guides now? B: The manager wants all the fiction together upstairs, so stories about imaginary people will be on the second floor, while travel guides and cookbooks will stay near the entrance.","t":"A：你為什麼要把那些書都搬到二樓？顧客現在要去哪裡找旅遊指南？ B：經理希望把所有【小說類書籍】集中放在樓上，所以關於虛構人物的故事會放在二樓，而旅遊指南和食譜會留在入口附近。"},{"w":"nonfiction","p":"n.","d":"writing about real facts, people, and events","c":"非小說類作品；紀實文學","s":"A: What kind of books do the employees in our company book club prefer, and should we choose a mystery for next month? B: Most members prefer nonfiction, such as true stories about successful business leaders, so I suggest choosing a biography instead of a mystery for our next meeting.","t":"A：我們公司讀書會的員工喜歡哪一類書？下個月我們應該選一本推理小說嗎？ B：大多數成員比較喜歡【非小說類書籍】，例如成功企業領袖的真實故事，所以我建議下次聚會選一本傳記而不是推理小說。"},{"w":"plot","p":"n.","d":"the series of events in a story","c":"情節；故事梗概","s":"A: Did you enjoy the mystery novel that the book club chose for this month, or did you stop halfway through it? B: I finished it in two days because the plot was full of surprises, and I never guessed who stole the money from the bank until the last chapter.","t":"A：你喜歡讀書會這個月選的那本推理小說嗎？還是讀到一半就放棄了？ B：我兩天就讀完了，因為【情節】充滿驚喜，直到最後一章我都沒猜到是誰偷了銀行的錢。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"a person in a story, film, or play","c":"角色；人物","s":"A: What did the readers at the library discussion say about the new novel, and did they like the ending? B: Most of them loved the main character, a hard-working young nurse who opens her own clinic, but several people thought the ending was too sad and too sudden.","t":"A：圖書館討論會的讀者對那本新小說有什麼看法？他們喜歡結局嗎？ B：他們大多數人都很喜歡主要【角色】，一位開設自己診所的勤奮年輕護士，但有幾個人覺得結局太悲傷也太突然。"},{"w":"setting","p":"n.","d":"the place and time in which a story happens","c":"背景；場景","s":"A: Why does the publisher want the writer to make changes to the story before it is printed next spring? B: They think the setting should be modern Taipei instead of a small village in the past, because young readers will connect more easily with a busy city they know.","t":"A：出版社為什麼要作者在明年春天印刷前修改故事？ B：他們認為故事【背景】應該是現代的台北，而不是過去的小村莊，因為年輕讀者會更容易對他們熟悉的繁忙城市產生共鳴。"},{"w":"theme","p":"n.","d":"the main subject or idea in a piece of writing","c":"主題","s":"A: What is the main idea of the business novel we are discussing at lunch, since I only finished half of it? B: The central theme is teamwork, because the story shows how a small group of workers saves their failing company by listening to each other and sharing ideas.","t":"A：我們午餐時要討論的那本商業小說主要想法是什麼？我只讀完了一半。 B：核心【主題】是團隊合作，因為故事描述一小群員工如何透過互相傾聽和分享想法，拯救了他們快倒閉的公司。"},{"w":"narrative","p":"n.","d":"a story or a description of events","c":"敘述；故事","s":"A: Why did the editor ask you to rewrite the company history book, when you already spent six months on it? B: She said the narrative jumped between different years too often, so readers got confused, and she wants the story told in order from the founding of the company.","t":"A：既然你已經花了六個月寫那本公司歷史書，編輯為什麼還要你重寫？ B：她說【敘述】太常在不同年份之間跳來跳去，讓讀者感到混亂，她希望故事從公司創立開始依序講述。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"a conversation between people in a book, play, or film","c":"對話","s":"A: What do you think of the new English textbook for our staff training, and is it useful for beginners? B: I like it because each lesson has a short dialogue between a hotel clerk and a guest, so the trainees can practice speaking in pairs before they talk to real customers.","t":"A：你覺得我們員工訓練用的新英文課本怎麼樣？對初學者有用嗎？ B：我喜歡它，因為每一課都有一段飯店櫃台人員和客人之間的簡短【對話】，所以受訓者可以在和真正的顧客交談前兩人一組練習口說。"},{"w":"description","p":"n.","d":"words that tell what something is like","c":"描述；說明","s":"A: Has the online bookstore added the new cookbook to its website yet, because several customers have asked when they can order it? B: Not yet, they are still waiting for a short description of the book, so I need to send them a paragraph about the recipes and the chef by tomorrow morning.","t":"A：網路書店把新食譜書放上網站了嗎？因為有好幾位顧客問什麼時候可以訂購。 B：還沒有，他們還在等這本書的簡短【介紹】，所以我需要在明天早上前寄給他們一段關於食譜和主廚的文字。"},{"w":"edition","p":"n.","d":"one version of a book printed at a particular time","c":"版本；版次","s":"A: Why are some customers returning the accounting textbook they bought from us last month, and is something wrong with it? B: The publisher released a new edition with updated tax rules last week, so the professors told their students to buy the latest version instead of the old one.","t":"A：為什麼有些顧客要退回上個月向我們買的會計課本？書有什麼問題嗎？ B：出版社上週發行了更新稅法的新【版本】，所以教授們要學生改買最新版而不是舊版。"},{"w":"publisher","p":"n.","d":"a company that prepares and sells books","c":"出版社；出版商","s":"A: Have you heard back from anyone about the business guide you wrote last year, or are you still waiting for an answer? B: Yes, a large publisher in Taipei called me yesterday and offered to print five thousand copies, so I am meeting their editor next Tuesday to sign the contract.","t":"A：你去年寫的那本商業指南有收到任何回音嗎？還是你還在等回覆？ B：有，台北一家大型【出版社】昨天打電話給我，提議印五千本，所以我下週二要和他們的編輯見面簽約。"},{"w":"hardcover","p":"n.","d":"a book with a stiff, strong cover","c":"精裝本","s":"A: Should we order the cheaper version of the art book for the store, or will customers pay more for a better one? B: For art books, many customers prefer the hardcover because it is strong and looks beautiful on a shelf, so let's order mostly that version even though it costs more.","t":"A：我們店裡應該訂那本藝術書比較便宜的版本，還是顧客會願意多付錢買比較好的？ B：對藝術書來說，很多顧客偏好【精裝本】，因為它很堅固，放在書架上也很好看，所以即使比較貴，我們還是大多訂那個版本吧。"},{"w":"paperback","p":"n.","d":"a book with a soft paper cover","c":"平裝本","s":"A: Which version of the novel should I take on my business trip to Singapore, since my suitcase is already quite heavy? B: You should take the paperback, because it is light and small enough to fit in your jacket pocket, and it costs only half the price of the other one.","t":"A：我去新加坡出差應該帶哪個版本的小說？我的行李箱已經很重了。 B：你應該帶【平裝本】，因為它又輕又小，可以放進外套口袋，而且價格只有另一種的一半。"},{"w":"illustration","p":"n.","d":"a picture in a book","c":"插圖；圖解","s":"A: Why is the children's book about saving energy taking so long to finish, when the writer sent us the story in May? B: The artist is still drawing the last illustration for the final page, and she wants every picture to be bright and clear so young readers can understand the ideas.","t":"A：既然作者五月就把故事寄給我們了，那本關於節約能源的童書為什麼要花這麼久才完成？ B：畫家還在畫最後一頁的最後一張【插圖】，她希望每張圖都鮮明清楚，讓年輕讀者能理解其中的概念。"},{"w":"read","p":"v.","d":"to look at words and understand them","c":"閱讀；讀","s":"A: Have you had time to look at the new safety manual before the training session with the factory workers this afternoon? B: Yes, I managed to read the whole thing on the train this morning, and I wrote down three questions about the fire exits that I want to ask the manager.","t":"A：今天下午和工廠員工的訓練課程之前，你有時間看新的安全手冊嗎？ B：有，我今天早上在火車上把整本【讀】完了，還寫下了三個關於逃生出口的問題要問經理。"},{"w":"review","p":"n.","d":"a written report that gives an opinion about a book, film, etc.","c":"評論；書評","s":"A: How did the newspaper describe our company's new travel guide, and will it help us sell more copies this month? B: The review in Sunday's newspaper said it was clear, useful, and full of great photos, so I expect sales to rise quickly over the next few weeks.","t":"A：報紙怎麼描述我們公司的新旅遊指南？這會幫助我們這個月多賣一些嗎？ B：週日報紙上的【書評】說它內容清楚、實用，而且有很多很棒的照片，所以我預期接下來幾週銷售會快速上升。"},{"w":"bookmark","p":"n.","d":"a thin strip put in a book to mark a page","c":"書籤","s":"A: Are we giving customers anything free with their purchases during the book fair this weekend, like we did last year? B: Yes, every customer will get a paper bookmark with our store's logo and website on it, so they can keep their place in a book and remember to shop with us again.","t":"A：這週末書展期間，我們會像去年一樣隨購買贈送顧客任何東西嗎？ B：會，每位顧客都會拿到一張印有我們店標誌和網址的紙製【書籤】，這樣他們可以標記閱讀的位置，也會記得再來我們店購物。"},{"w":"library","p":"n.","d":"a place where books are kept for people to read or borrow","c":"圖書館；圖書室","s":"A: Where can I find old reports about the market in Southeast Asia, since I need them for my presentation on Monday? B: The company library on the third floor keeps copies of all reports from the past ten years, and you can borrow them for two weeks if you show your staff card.","t":"A：我可以在哪裡找到東南亞市場的舊報告？我星期一的簡報需要用到。 B：三樓的公司【圖書室】保存了過去十年所有報告的副本，只要出示員工證，你就可以借兩個星期。"},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"books, poems, and plays that are thought to be important art","c":"文學","s":"A: Why did the bookstore hire a new staff member for the second floor, and what will she be responsible for? B: She studied English literature at university and knows a lot about famous poems and plays, so she will help customers choose good books and organize our monthly reading events.","t":"A：書店為什麼為二樓僱用了一位新員工？她會負責什麼？ B：她大學念英國【文學】，對著名的詩和劇本很了解，所以她會幫顧客挑選好書，並籌辦我們每月的讀書活動。"},{"w":"classic","p":"n.","d":"a famous book that people have admired for a long time","c":"經典作品；名著","s":"A: Which books should we include in the gift box for our loyal customers this holiday season, since we want something that lasts? B: Let's include a famous classic that people have loved for over a hundred years, along with a new bestseller, so the box appeals to both older and younger readers.","t":"A：這個假期我們要在送給忠實顧客的禮盒裡放哪些書？我們想要有長久價值的東西。 B：我們放一本人們喜愛了一百多年的著名【經典作品】，再加一本新的暢銷書，讓禮盒同時吸引年長和年輕的讀者。"},{"w":"bestseller","p":"n.","d":"a book that sells a very large number of copies","c":"暢銷書","s":"A: Why did the publishing company decide to print another twenty thousand copies of the cookbook this month? B: It became a bestseller just two weeks after it came out, because a famous TV chef recommended it on her show, and many bookstores have already sold all their copies.","t":"A：出版公司為什麼決定這個月再加印兩萬本那本食譜書？ B：它出版短短兩週就成為【暢銷書】，因為一位知名電視主廚在節目中推薦了它，許多書店都已經賣光了。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making people feel excited and want to do something","c":"激勵人心的；鼓舞人的","s":"A: Why are so many employees talking about the speaker at yesterday's training event, and what did she talk about? B: Her speech was very inspiring, because she described how she started her bookstore with almost no money, and now many of us feel ready to try new ideas at work.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多員工在談論昨天訓練活動的講者？她講了什麼？ B：她的演講非常【激勵人心】，因為她描述了自己如何在幾乎沒有錢的情況下開了書店，現在我們很多人都覺得準備好在工作上嘗試新點子了。"}]},{"unit":32,"theme":"Bookstore 書店","cards":[{"w":"bookshelf","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture with shelves for books","c":"書架","s":"A: The new store manager wants the travel guides to be easier for visitors to find, so where should we put the boxes that arrived from the publisher this morning? B: Let's move them to the tall bookshelf next to the front window, because tourists usually walk in from the street and look there first before they explore the rest of the shop.","t":"A：新店長希望旅遊指南能讓客人更容易找到，那今天早上出版社送來的那幾箱書我們該放在哪裡？ B：我們把它們移到前窗旁邊那個高高的【書架】上吧，因為觀光客通常從街上走進來，會先看那裡，再逛店裡其他地方。"},{"w":"aisle","p":"n.","d":"a long, narrow path between rows of shelves or seats","c":"走道","s":"A: A woman just called to ask where she can find our cookbooks, but I only started working here yesterday, so do you know where they are? B: Tell her to walk past the cashier and turn left into the third aisle, where the cookbooks are on the lower shelves right beside the gardening magazines.","t":"A：有位女士剛打電話來問我們的食譜書在哪裡，但我昨天才開始在這裡上班，你知道在哪嗎？ B：告訴她走過收銀員後左轉進入第三條【走道】，食譜書就在園藝雜誌旁邊的下層架子上。"},{"w":"section","p":"n.","d":"one part or area of a store, book, or place","c":"區；部分","s":"A: Our sales report shows that more parents are buying learning materials for young kids this year, so how should we change the layout of the second floor? B: I think we should make the children's section bigger and add some small chairs and tables, so families can sit together and read before they decide what to buy.","t":"A：我們的銷售報告顯示今年有更多家長購買幼兒學習教材，那我們應該怎麼調整二樓的配置？ B：我認為我們應該把兒童【區】擴大，並增加一些小椅子和小桌子，讓家人可以先坐在一起閱讀，再決定要買什麼。"},{"w":"genre","p":"n.","d":"a type or style of book, film, or music","c":"類型；體裁","s":"A: Since the store is planning a summer promotion for adult readers, which kind of story do you think we should feature on the big table near the entrance? B: Mystery is the most popular genre among our regular shoppers, especially office workers who like exciting stories during their long train rides home, so let's choose that.","t":"A：既然書店計畫為成人讀者舉辦夏季促銷，你覺得我們應該在入口附近的大桌子上主打哪一類故事？ B：推理小說是我們常客最喜歡的【類型】，尤其是喜歡在漫長回家火車上看刺激故事的上班族，所以就選這個吧。"},{"w":"display","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement of things put out for people to see","c":"陳列；展示","s":"A: The publisher is sending us fifty copies of the new cookbook next Monday, so how can we make sure people notice it as soon as they come in? B: We could build a colorful display near the front door with a few sample dishes, some posters, and a sign showing the special opening price for the first week.","t":"A：出版社下週一會寄五十本新食譜書給我們，我們要怎麼確保客人一進門就注意到它？ B：我們可以在前門附近佈置一個色彩繽紛的【陳列】，擺上幾道範例菜餚、一些海報，以及標示第一週特別開幕價的牌子。"},{"w":"counter","p":"n.","d":"a long, flat surface where customers are served","c":"櫃檯","s":"A: Where should customers pick up the books they ordered online, since many of them complain that they can't find anyone to help them when they arrive? B: From next week, they can go straight to the service counter beside the entrance, where one employee will check their order number and hand them their package.","t":"A：顧客應該在哪裡領取他們網路訂購的書？很多人抱怨到店時找不到人幫忙。 B：從下週開始，他們可以直接到入口旁的服務【櫃檯】，會有一位員工核對訂單編號並把包裹交給他們。"},{"w":"cashier","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to take payments in a store","c":"收銀員","s":"A: The lines at the front of the store were really long on Saturday afternoon, and several shoppers left without buying anything, so what can we do about it? B: The manager has decided to hire another part-time cashier for weekends, so two people can take payments at the same time when the store gets busy.","t":"A：星期六下午店門口排隊的人潮很長，好幾位客人什麼都沒買就走了，我們能怎麼辦？ B：經理決定在週末再雇用一位兼職【收銀員】，這樣店裡忙碌時就能有兩個人同時收款。"},{"w":"customer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys things from a store or business","c":"顧客","s":"A: Why does the store manager want everyone to learn the names of the people who come in every week, even though we are always so busy? B: She believes that when a regular customer feels welcome and remembered, he or she will keep coming back and will probably tell friends about our shop too.","t":"A：為什麼店長要大家記住每週都來的人的名字，即使我們總是這麼忙？ B：她相信當一位常來的【顧客】覺得受到歡迎、被記住時，就會一直回來，而且很可能也會跟朋友介紹我們的店。"},{"w":"browse","p":"v.","d":"to look at things in a store without a clear plan to buy","c":"瀏覽；隨意看看","s":"A: Do you think it is a good idea to put some comfortable chairs near the travel section, even though people might sit there for hours without buying anything? B: Yes, because many visitors like to browse for a while before they choose something, and if they feel relaxed, they usually end up buying more than one item.","t":"A：你覺得在旅遊區附近放幾張舒適的椅子是個好主意嗎？即使有人可能在那裡坐上好幾個小時卻什麼都不買。 B：是的，因為很多客人喜歡先【瀏覽】一會兒再做選擇，而且如果他們感到放鬆，最後通常會買不只一樣東西。"},{"w":"purchase","p":"v.","d":"to buy something","c":"購買","s":"A: The school librarian called this morning and said she has a budget for new English readers, but she isn't sure how many copies she can afford this year. B: If she decides to purchase more than thirty copies at once, we can give her a fifteen percent discount and deliver the boxes to her school for free.","t":"A：學校圖書館員今天早上打電話來說她有預算買新的英文讀本，但她不確定今年能負擔幾本。 B：如果她決定一次【購買】超過三十本，我們可以給她八五折，並免費把書送到她的學校。"},{"w":"checkout","p":"n.","d":"the place in a store where you pay for things; the act of paying","c":"結帳處；結帳","s":"A: Several shoppers wrote online that paying at our store takes too long, especially in the evening after work, so what is the company planning to do? B: Head office is installing a self-service checkout machine next month, so people with only one or two items can pay by card quickly without waiting in line.","t":"A：好幾位顧客在網路上寫說在我們店裡付款太久，尤其是下班後的晚上，公司打算怎麼做？ B：總公司下個月會安裝一台自助【結帳】機，這樣只買一兩樣東西的人就能快速刷卡付款，不用排隊。"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper that shows you paid for something","c":"收據","s":"A: A woman wants to return a cookbook she bought as a gift last week because her friend already has a copy, so can we give her the money back? B: Yes, as long as she shows the receipt and the book is still in good condition, we can return the money to her credit card or give her store credit.","t":"A：有位女士想退回她上週買來送人的食譜，因為她朋友已經有一本了，我們可以退錢給她嗎？ B：可以，只要她出示【收據】而且書的狀況仍然良好，我們就可以把錢退到她的信用卡，或給她店內購物金。"},{"w":"bestseller","p":"n.","d":"a book that sells a very large number of copies","c":"暢銷書","s":"A: Why did the store order so many extra copies of that new business book, even though most new titles only sell a few copies each week? B: The author was interviewed on a popular TV program last night, and the book has become a bestseller in just a few days, so we expect lots of people to ask for it.","t":"A：為什麼書店多訂了那麼多本那本新的商業書？大部分新書每週只賣出幾本而已。 B：作者昨晚上了一個熱門電視節目接受訪問，這本書短短幾天就成了【暢銷書】，所以我們預期會有很多人來問。"},{"w":"staff","p":"n.","d":"the people who work for a business","c":"員工；職員","s":"A: The holiday season is our busiest time of the year, so what is the manager doing to make sure customers get help quickly when they come in? B: She is hiring extra staff for December, and every new employee will get two days of training on the cash register and our online ordering system.","t":"A：假期是一年中最忙的時候，經理打算怎麼確保顧客一進來就能很快得到協助？ B：她正在為十二月招募額外的【員工】，每位新進人員都會接受兩天的收銀機和線上訂購系統訓練。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is good and suggest it to someone","c":"推薦","s":"A: A businessman just asked me for a good book to read on his long flight to London tomorrow, but I don't know much about his interests at all. B: Ask him what kinds of stories he enjoyed in the past, and then recommend two or three titles from our staff favorites table near the cashier.","t":"A：一位商人剛問我有沒有好書可以在他明天飛往倫敦的長途航班上看，但我完全不了解他的興趣。 B：問問他以前喜歡哪類故事，然後從收銀台附近的員工推薦桌上【推薦】兩三本書給他。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making little or no noise","c":"安靜的","s":"A: Why do so many university students come to our café on the second floor in the afternoon, even though there is a larger coffee shop across the street? B: They say our place is much more quiet than other cafés nearby, so they can study for their exams and read without being disturbed by loud music or noisy groups.","t":"A：為什麼下午有那麼多大學生來我們二樓的咖啡廳，即使對街就有一家更大的咖啡店？ B：他們說我們這裡比附近其他咖啡廳【安靜】多了，所以他們可以準備考試、看書，不會被大聲的音樂或吵鬧的團體打擾。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and relaxing","c":"溫暖舒適的","s":"A: The designer has shown us the plans for the new reading corner, but what kind of feeling does the owner want customers to have when they sit down there? B: She wants it to feel warm and cozy, like a living room at home, with soft lamps, a thick carpet, and comfortable armchairs where people can relax for hours.","t":"A：設計師已經給我們看了新閱讀角的規劃，但老闆希望顧客坐在那裡時有什麼樣的感覺？ B：她希望那裡感覺溫暖又【舒適】，就像家裡的客廳一樣，有柔和的檯燈、厚地毯和舒服的扶手椅，讓人可以放鬆好幾個小時。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"not owned or controlled by a larger company","c":"獨立的","s":"A: How is your small shop able to survive when the big online companies sell most books at much lower prices than you can offer? B: As an independent store that is not owned by a large company, we can choose unusual titles, hold local events, and give personal advice that people cannot get from a website.","t":"A：當大型網路公司賣的書大多比你們便宜很多時，你們這家小店要怎麼生存？ B：身為一家不屬於大公司的【獨立】書店，我們可以挑選特別的書、舉辦地方活動，並提供網站無法給的個人化建議。"},{"w":"chain","p":"n.","d":"a group of shops owned by the same company","c":"連鎖店","s":"A: I heard the old bookshop on Main Street was sold last month, so do you know whether the new owners are going to keep the same name and employees? B: It was bought by a national chain with more than two hundred stores, so they will probably change the sign and use the same design as their other branches.","t":"A：我聽說主街上那家老書店上個月被賣掉了，你知道新老闆會保留原來的店名和員工嗎？ B：它被一家擁有兩百多家門市的全國【連鎖店】買下了，所以他們可能會換招牌，並採用和其他分店一樣的設計。"},{"w":"inventory","p":"n.","d":"all the goods a store has; a list of these goods","c":"存貨；庫存清單","s":"A: Why is the store closing early this Sunday afternoon, since weekends are usually when we make most of our sales? B: All employees need to count every book and magazine on the shelves and in the storeroom, because the accountant needs an exact record of our inventory before the end of the financial year.","t":"A：為什麼書店這週日下午要提早打烊？週末通常是我們銷售最多的時候。 B：所有員工都需要清點架上和倉庫裡的每一本書和雜誌，因為會計師需要在會計年度結束前取得我們【存貨】的精確紀錄。"},{"w":"hardcover","p":"n.","d":"a book with a strong, stiff cover","c":"精裝本","s":"A: A customer wants to buy the new history book as a birthday gift for her grandfather, so which version should I suggest to her? B: Suggest the hardcover, because it has a strong, beautiful cover that will last for many years, even though it costs about ten dollars more than the soft version.","t":"A：有位顧客想買那本新的歷史書當作送給祖父的生日禮物，我該建議她哪一個版本？ B：建議她買【精裝本】，因為它有堅固又漂亮的封面，可以保存很多年，雖然比軟皮版貴大約十元。"},{"w":"paperback","p":"n.","d":"a book with a soft paper cover","c":"平裝本","s":"A: Many students say our textbooks and novels are too heavy to carry around in their school bags every day, so is there anything cheaper and lighter we can offer? B: Yes, most of those titles are also available in paperback, which is much lighter and usually costs about half the price of the hard version.","t":"A：很多學生說我們的教科書和小說太重，不適合每天放在書包裡帶著走，有沒有更便宜、更輕的選擇？ B：有，那些書大多也有【平裝本】，輕很多，價格通常只有精裝版的一半左右。"},{"w":"magazine","p":"n.","d":"a thin publication with articles and photos that comes out regularly","c":"雜誌","s":"A: The owner wants to attract more young office workers who stop by during their lunch break, so what kind of products should we add near the entrance? B: Let's add a rack with a monthly business magazine, some fashion titles, and a few travel guides, because people can read them quickly while they wait for their coffee.","t":"A：老闆想吸引更多午休時間順道進來的年輕上班族，我們應該在入口附近加哪類商品？ B：我們加一個架子，擺放每月出刊的商業【雜誌】、一些時尚刊物和幾本旅遊指南吧，因為大家等咖啡時可以快速翻閱。"},{"w":"stationery","p":"n.","d":"paper, pens, envelopes, and other writing materials","c":"文具","s":"A: Sales of books have been slow this spring, so is there anything else we can sell to bring more students and office workers into the shop? B: The manager plans to add a stationery corner with notebooks, pens, envelopes, and greeting cards, since people often need these items for school, work, and special occasions.","t":"A：今年春天書籍銷售一直很慢，我們有沒有其他東西可以賣，吸引更多學生和上班族來店裡？ B：經理打算增設一個【文具】區，販售筆記本、筆、信封和賀卡，因為大家上學、上班和特殊場合常常需要這些東西。"},{"w":"signing","p":"n.","d":"an event where an author signs copies of a book","c":"簽書會；簽名活動","s":"A: Why are there so many people waiting outside the store with copies of that new novel this morning, even though we don't open until ten o'clock? B: The famous author is coming at eleven for a book signing, so fans want to be first in line to meet her and get their copies autographed.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有這麼多人拿著那本新小說在店外等？我們十點才開門。 B：那位知名作家十一點會來舉辦新書【簽書會】，所以書迷們想排在最前面跟她見面並取得簽名書。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"a planned public or social occasion","c":"活動","s":"A: The owner wants to bring more families into the shop on weekends, so do you have any ideas that won't cost the company too much money? B: We could hold a free storytelling event for children every Saturday morning, and parents could look around and buy books while their kids listen to the stories.","t":"A：老闆想在週末吸引更多家庭來店裡，你有沒有不會讓公司花太多錢的點子？ B：我們可以每週六早上為孩子舉辦免費的說故事【活動】，家長可以在孩子聽故事時四處逛逛、買書。"},{"w":"reading","p":"n.","d":"an event where a writer reads his or her work aloud to an audience","c":"朗讀會；閱讀","s":"A: The poet who wrote that new collection is visiting our city next week, so is the store planning anything special for her visit? B: Yes, she will give a public reading of her poems in the café on Thursday evening, and afterwards guests can ask her questions about her work and her writing habits.","t":"A：寫那本新詩集的詩人下週要來我們城市，書店有計畫為她的來訪安排什麼特別活動嗎？ B：有，她星期四晚上會在咖啡廳舉行公開詩作【朗讀會】，之後來賓可以問她有關作品和寫作習慣的問題。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"the people who live in one area","c":"社區；社群","s":"A: Why does our store offer its meeting room for free to local book clubs and parent groups, even though we could rent it out to companies instead? B: The owner believes a bookstore should be an important part of the neighborhood community, and when local people feel connected to the shop, they support it for many years.","t":"A：為什麼我們書店免費提供會議室給當地讀書會和家長團體使用，明明可以租給公司？ B：老闆相信書店應該成為鄰近【社區】重要的一部分，而當地居民對書店有歸屬感時，他們會支持它很多年。"},{"w":"literary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with literature or serious writing","c":"文學的","s":"A: The store has been asked to organize a weekend festival with famous writers, poets, and university professors, so what should we call it on the posters? B: Let's call it a literary festival, because the program focuses on novels, poetry, and serious writing, and that name will attract readers who love good books.","t":"A：書店受邀籌辦一場有知名作家、詩人和大學教授參加的週末節慶，我們在海報上該怎麼稱呼它？ B：就叫它【文學】節吧，因為節目重點是小說、詩和嚴肅寫作，這個名稱會吸引喜愛好書的讀者。"}]},{"unit":33,"theme":"Bored 感到無聊","cards":[{"w":"boredom","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being tired and unhappy because nothing is interesting","c":"無聊；厭倦","s":"A: Why did so many workers in the packing department ask to change jobs last month, even though the pay there is quite good? B: The HR survey showed that doing the same simple task for eight hours every day caused great boredom, so the manager is now planning to rotate staff between different stations each week.","t":"A：雖然包裝部門的薪水相當不錯，為什麼上個月有那麼多員工要求調職？ B：人資的調查顯示，每天八小時重複同樣簡單的工作讓人感到非常【無聊】，所以經理現在打算每週讓員工在不同的工作站之間輪調。"},{"w":"weary","p":"adj.","d":"very tired, especially after working hard for a long time","c":"疲倦的；厭倦的","s":"A: How did the sales team look when they finally came back from the trade show in Singapore after five long days? B: They all looked weary because they had been standing at the booth from early morning until late evening, so the director told them to take Monday off and rest at home.","t":"A：業務團隊在新加坡參加了漫長的五天商展終於回來時，看起來怎麼樣？ B：他們看起來都很【疲憊】，因為他們從清晨到深夜一直站在攤位前，所以主管要他們星期一休假，在家好好休息。"},{"w":"restless","p":"adj.","d":"unable to stay still or relaxed, often because you are bored or worried","c":"坐立不安的；焦躁的","s":"A: Why did the trainer suddenly stop her presentation and give everyone a fifteen-minute coffee break in the middle of the afternoon? B: She noticed that the new employees were becoming restless, moving in their chairs and checking their phones, after sitting and listening to her for nearly three hours without a pause.","t":"A：為什麼訓練講師在下午中途突然停止簡報，讓大家休息十五分鐘喝咖啡？ B：她注意到新進員工在沒有休息的情況下坐著聽她講了將近三個小時後，變得【坐立不安】，在椅子上動來動去，還一直看手機。"},{"w":"listless","p":"adj.","d":"having no energy or interest in doing anything","c":"無精打采的","s":"A: Is something wrong with Kevin from the accounting department, because he hardly said a word during the budget meeting this morning? B: He has seemed listless ever since his big project was cancelled last week, so his supervisor is going to talk with him and maybe give him a new task that he will enjoy more.","t":"A：會計部的凱文是不是怎麼了？他今天早上的預算會議中幾乎一句話也沒說。 B：自從他的大專案上週被取消後，他看起來一直【無精打采】，所以他的主管打算跟他談談，或許會給他一個他會更喜歡的新任務。"},{"w":"apathetic","p":"adj.","d":"showing no interest or concern about something","c":"冷漠的；漠不關心的","s":"A: Why did only twelve people vote in the election for the new staff committee, when the company has more than three hundred employees? B: Many workers have become apathetic because they believe the committee never changes anything, so the managers want to show some real results this year to win back their trust.","t":"A：公司有三百多名員工，為什麼新員工委員會的選舉只有十二個人投票？ B：許多員工變得【漠不關心】，因為他們認為委員會從來沒有改變任何事情，所以經理們希望今年能展現一些實際成果，以贏回大家的信任。"},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adj.","d":"not caring about or interested in something","c":"不在乎的；冷淡的","s":"A: Did the customers in the survey care much about the new color of our coffee cups, or were they more interested in something else? B: Most of them were completely indifferent to the color, but they complained a lot about the high prices and the long lines in the morning, so we should fix those problems first.","t":"A：調查中的顧客很在意我們咖啡杯的新顏色嗎？還是他們對別的事更感興趣？ B：他們大多對顏色完全【不在乎】，但對高價格和早上大排長龍抱怨很多，所以我們應該先解決那些問題。"},{"w":"disengaged","p":"adj.","d":"not feeling involved in or interested in your work or activity","c":"不投入的；疏離的","s":"A: What did the consultant say about the results of the employee satisfaction survey that we did across all our branches in March? B: She said that almost a third of our staff feel disengaged from their work because they rarely get feedback from managers, so she suggested holding short monthly meetings with every team member.","t":"A：顧問對我們三月在所有分店進行的員工滿意度調查結果怎麼說？ B：她說我們將近三分之一的員工對工作感到【不投入】，因為他們很少得到主管的回饋，所以她建議每個月和每位團隊成員舉行簡短的面談。"},{"w":"uninvolved","p":"adj.","d":"not taking part in something","c":"未參與的；置身事外的","s":"A: Should we ask the designers from the marketing department to join our planning meeting for the new product launch next week? B: No, they have been uninvolved in this project from the start, so it would be better to send them a short summary later instead of asking them to sit through a two-hour discussion.","t":"A：我們要不要請行銷部的設計師參加下週新產品發表的企劃會議？ B：不用，他們從一開始就【沒有參與】這個專案，所以與其要他們坐著聽兩個小時的討論，不如之後寄一份簡短的摘要給他們。"},{"w":"lethargic","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sleepy and having very little energy","c":"昏昏欲睡的；懶洋洋的","s":"A: Why does the office manager want to open the windows and turn up the lights in the meeting room every afternoon now? B: Many staff members said they felt lethargic after lunch in the warm, dark room, so she hopes that fresh air and brighter lights will help everyone stay awake and focused during the long meetings.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理現在每天下午都要打開會議室的窗戶並把燈開亮一點？ B：很多員工說午餐後在溫暖又昏暗的房間裡會感到【昏昏欲睡、提不起勁】，所以她希望新鮮空氣和明亮的燈光能幫助大家在冗長的會議中保持清醒和專注。"},{"w":"unmotivated","p":"adj.","d":"not having any reason or wish to work hard","c":"缺乏動力的","s":"A: Why are the new sales assistants making so few calls to customers, even though the manager has asked them several times to try harder? B: They feel unmotivated because there is no bonus for reaching their targets this year, so the director is thinking about bringing back a small reward for the top three sellers each month.","t":"A：雖然經理已經多次要求新的業務助理更努力，為什麼他們打給客戶的電話還是那麼少？ B：他們覺得【缺乏動力】，因為今年達成目標沒有獎金，所以主管正在考慮恢復每月給前三名業績最好的人一份小獎勵。"},{"w":"ennui","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being bored and unhappy because life seems dull","c":"倦怠；百無聊賴","s":"A: Why did Laura decide to leave her well-paid office job at the bank and open a small bakery near the train station? B: After ten years of the same reports and the same meetings, she felt a deep ennui every morning, so she decided to follow her dream and do something creative that would make her happy.","t":"A：蘿拉為什麼決定辭掉銀行裡高薪的辦公室工作，在火車站附近開一間小烘焙坊？ B：做了十年同樣的報告、開同樣的會議之後，她每天早上都感到深深的【倦怠】，所以她決定追隨夢想，做些能讓她快樂的創意工作。"},{"w":"fed up","p":"adj.phr.","d":"annoyed and tired of something that has continued for too long","c":"受夠了的；厭煩的","s":"A: Why is the receptionist asking the building manager for a new air conditioner for the lobby again this week? B: She is fed up with the old machine because it breaks down almost every day in summer, and visitors keep complaining about the heat while they wait for their appointments.","t":"A：為什麼接待員這週又在向大樓管理員要求為大廳換新冷氣？ B：她已經【受夠了】那台舊機器，因為它夏天幾乎每天都故障，而訪客在等候約會時一直抱怨很熱。"},{"w":"tired","p":"adj.","d":"needing rest or sleep","c":"疲倦的；累的","s":"A: Why did the project manager decide to postpone the client presentation from this morning until tomorrow afternoon? B: The whole team worked until two o'clock last night to finish the slides, so they were too tired to explain the plan clearly, and she thought a good night's sleep would help them do much better.","t":"A：專案經理為什麼決定把客戶簡報從今天早上延到明天下午？ B：整個團隊昨晚工作到凌晨兩點才把投影片做完，所以他們太【累】了，沒辦法把計畫解釋清楚，她認為好好睡一晚會讓他們表現得好很多。"},{"w":"jaded","p":"adj.","d":"no longer interested or excited because you have seen or done something too often","c":"厭倦的；麻木的（因經歷太多）","s":"A: Why didn't the senior engineers get excited about the new software system that the IT department showed them yesterday? B: They have become jaded after watching so many \"amazing\" systems fail over the past twenty years, so they want to see real test results before they believe this one will work.","t":"A：昨天資訊部門展示新軟體系統時，資深工程師們為什麼一點都不興奮？ B：過去二十年看過太多「了不起」的系統失敗後，他們已經變得【麻木厭倦】，所以他們要先看到真正的測試結果，才會相信這套系統行得通。"},{"w":"unenthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"not showing excitement or interest","c":"不熱衷的；冷淡的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the manager announced that the annual company trip would be a hiking tour in the mountains this year? B: Most of them were quite unenthusiastic because they had hoped for a beach resort, so the manager promised to send out a survey and let everyone vote on next year's destination.","t":"A：經理宣布今年的員工旅遊是山區健行之旅時，員工們有什麼反應？ B：他們大多相當【不熱衷】，因為他們原本希望去海灘度假村，所以經理答應會發問卷，讓大家投票決定明年的目的地。"},{"w":"detached","p":"adj.","d":"not emotionally involved; showing little interest or feeling","c":"冷漠疏離的；超然的","s":"A: Why did the customers give the new call center workers such low scores in last month's service survey? B: Many callers said the workers sounded detached and read from a script without really listening to their problems, so the manager is planning extra training on how to show care and understanding on the phone.","t":"A：上個月的服務調查中，顧客為什麼給新的客服中心人員這麼低的分數？ B：很多來電者說那些人員聽起來很【冷漠疏離】，只照著稿子念，沒有真正傾聽他們的問題，所以經理打算額外培訓他們如何在電話中表現關心和理解。"},{"w":"blank","p":"adj.","d":"showing no feeling, understanding, or interest","c":"茫然的；無表情的","s":"A: How did the audience react when the speaker started explaining the complicated tax rules at the end of the long conference yesterday? B: Most people just had blank looks on their faces because they were exhausted and did not understand the details, so the organizer decided to email everyone a simple summary the next day.","t":"A：昨天漫長的研討會快結束時，講者開始解釋複雜的稅務規定，聽眾有什麼反應？ B：大多數人臉上只是一臉【茫然】，因為他們已經筋疲力盡又聽不懂細節，所以主辦單位決定隔天寄一份簡單的摘要給大家。"},{"w":"passive","p":"adj.","d":"accepting what happens without trying to take action or change things","c":"被動的；消極的","s":"A: Why does the training manager want to change the format of the new employee workshops starting next month? B: She thinks that sitting and listening to long lectures makes trainees too passive, so she wants to add group tasks and role-plays that will get everyone talking and working together actively.","t":"A：訓練經理為什麼想從下個月開始改變新進員工研習的形式？ B：她認為坐著聽冗長的講課會讓學員太過【被動】，所以她想加入小組任務和角色扮演，讓每個人都積極地發言和合作。"},{"w":"uninterested","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to learn more about something or take part in it","c":"不感興趣的","s":"A: Did the visitors from the hotel group want to hear more about our new cleaning service after the short demonstration this morning? B: Sadly, they seemed uninterested and kept looking at their watches, so I think we should prepare a cheaper package and contact them again when their current contract ends next spring.","t":"A：今天早上簡短的示範之後，飯店集團的訪客有想進一步了解我們的新清潔服務嗎？ B：可惜他們似乎【不感興趣】，一直看手錶，所以我想我們應該準備一個更便宜的方案，等他們目前的合約明年春天到期時再聯絡他們。"},{"w":"monotony","p":"n.","d":"a boring lack of change in something","c":"單調；千篇一律","s":"A: Why does the factory now play music and give workers a short break every two hours on the production line? B: The manager wanted to reduce the monotony of checking thousands of identical bottles all day long, because tired, bored workers were missing more mistakes and the number of customer complaints was rising.","t":"A：為什麼工廠現在在生產線上播放音樂，而且每兩小時讓工人短暫休息？ B：經理想減少整天檢查成千上萬個一模一樣的瓶子所帶來的【單調】，因為疲倦又無聊的工人漏掉更多錯誤，顧客投訴的數量也一直在增加。"},{"w":"drowsy","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sleepy","c":"昏昏欲睡的","s":"A: Why did the safety officer tell the delivery drivers not to take that cold medicine before their long trips? B: The medicine can make people feel drowsy, and falling asleep for even a second on the highway could cause a serious accident, so drivers should ask a doctor for a different kind that is safe to take.","t":"A：安全主管為什麼告訴送貨司機在長途行車前不要吃那種感冒藥？ B：那種藥會讓人感到【昏昏欲睡】，而在高速公路上即使只睡著一秒鐘也可能造成嚴重事故，所以司機應該請醫生開另一種可以安全服用的藥。"},{"w":"vacant","p":"adj.","d":"showing no interest, thought, or feeling","c":"茫然的；空洞的（表情）","s":"A: Did the interns understand the new filing system after Mr. Chen explained it to them for over an hour yesterday afternoon? B: I don't think so, because they just stared at him with vacant expressions the whole time, so I am going to make a simple step-by-step guide with pictures for them this morning.","t":"A：陳先生昨天下午花了一個多小時向實習生解釋新的歸檔系統，他們聽懂了嗎？ B：我覺得沒有，因為他們整個過程都用【茫然空洞】的表情盯著他，所以我今天早上要為他們做一份有圖片的簡單步驟說明。"},{"w":"resigned","p":"adj.","d":"accepting something unpleasant because you feel you cannot change it","c":"認命的；無奈接受的","s":"A: Are the staff still angry that the office will move to the industrial park outside the city at the end of this year? B: Not really anymore; they seem resigned to the change now because the decision is final, and the company has promised a free shuttle bus from the main train station every morning.","t":"A：員工們還在為辦公室今年年底要搬到市郊的工業區生氣嗎？ B：其實已經不太會了；他們現在似乎已經【無奈接受】這個改變，因為決定已成定局，而且公司答應每天早上提供從火車總站出發的免費接駁車。"},{"w":"numb","p":"adj.","d":"unable to feel emotions, often after a shock","c":"麻木的；失去感覺的","s":"A: How did the employees at the branch office feel when they heard that the company would close it after thirty years? B: At first, many of them just felt numb and could not react at all, but after a few days they started asking HR about job openings at the other branches in the city.","t":"A：分公司的員工聽到公司要在三十年後關閉分公司時，有什麼感受？ B：一開始他們很多人只是感到【麻木】，完全無法反應，但幾天後他們開始向人資詢問市內其他分店的職缺。"},{"w":"dispirited","p":"adj.","d":"having lost hope or enthusiasm","c":"灰心的；沮喪的","s":"A: Why does the sales team look so unhappy this morning, even though they worked very hard on the proposal for the airport project? B: They feel dispirited because the client chose a cheaper company yesterday, so the director is taking them out for lunch to thank them and talk about the next big opportunity.","t":"A：雖然業務團隊為機場專案的提案非常努力，為什麼他們今天早上看起來那麼不開心？ B：他們感到【灰心沮喪】，因為客戶昨天選擇了一家較便宜的公司，所以主管要請他們吃午餐表達謝意，並討論下一個大好機會。"},{"w":"unresponsive","p":"adj.","d":"not reacting or answering","c":"無回應的；反應遲鈍的","s":"A: Has the supplier in Vietnam replied to our emails about the late shipment of fabric that should have arrived last Friday? B: No, they have been completely unresponsive for over a week, so the purchasing manager plans to call their head office directly this afternoon and look for a backup supplier just in case.","t":"A：越南的供應商回覆我們關於上週五就該送達的布料延遲出貨的電子郵件了嗎？ B：沒有，他們已經一個多星期完全【沒有回應】，所以採購經理打算今天下午直接打電話到他們總公司，並且找一家備用供應商以防萬一。"},{"w":"drained","p":"adj.","d":"very tired, with no energy left","c":"精疲力竭的","s":"A: How do you feel after spending the whole day answering angry customers' calls about yesterday's system problem? B: I feel completely drained, because I talked to more than eighty people and had to stay calm and polite with every single one of them, so I am going straight home to rest tonight.","t":"A：花了一整天接聽顧客因為昨天系統問題打來的憤怒電話後，你感覺怎麼樣？ B：我覺得完全【精疲力竭】，因為我跟八十多個人通話，每一個都得保持冷靜和禮貌，所以我今晚要直接回家休息。"},{"w":"stagnant","p":"adj.","d":"not growing, changing, or developing","c":"停滯的；不景氣的","s":"A: Why is the board of directors so worried about the results of the company's clothing business in Asia this year? B: Sales have been stagnant for three years in a row while our competitors keep growing, so the board wants a new marketing plan that will attract younger customers and bring fresh energy to the brand.","t":"A：董事會為什麼對公司今年在亞洲的服飾業務成果這麼擔心？ B：我們的銷售已經連續三年【停滯不前】，而競爭對手卻持續成長，所以董事會想要一個能吸引年輕顧客、為品牌注入新活力的新行銷計畫。"},{"w":"burned out","p":"adj.phr.","d":"extremely tired and unable to work well because of too much work or stress","c":"身心俱疲的；職業倦怠的","s":"A: Why did the head nurse ask the hospital director to hire three more nurses for the night shift as soon as possible? B: Her team has been working twelve-hour shifts six days a week for months, and many of them are burned out, so she is afraid that some of them will quit or make serious mistakes.","t":"A：護理長為什麼要求醫院院長盡快為夜班多聘請三名護理師？ B：她的團隊好幾個月來每週工作六天、每班十二小時，很多人都已經【身心俱疲】，所以她擔心有些人會辭職或犯下嚴重錯誤。"}]},{"unit":34,"theme":"Boring 乏味的","cards":[{"w":"tedious","p":"adj.","d":"long and boring, making you tired","c":"冗長乏味的","s":"A: Why did Mark stay so late at the office last night when he usually leaves at six? B: He had to check five hundred customer addresses one by one in the old database, which is a really tedious job, but the manager needs the mailing list ready before the holiday sale begins next week.","t":"A：Mark平常六點就下班，為什麼他昨晚在辦公室待到那麼晚？ B：他必須在舊資料庫裡逐一核對五百個客戶地址，這是非常【冗長乏味的】工作，但經理需要在下週假期特賣開始前把郵寄名單準備好。"},{"w":"monotonous","p":"adj.","d":"always the same and boring, with no change","c":"單調的","s":"A: How was the training webinar about the new accounting software that the finance team attended yesterday afternoon? B: The software itself looks useful, but the speaker talked in a slow, monotonous voice for two hours without any slides or examples, so several people fell asleep before it ended.","t":"A：財務團隊昨天下午參加的新會計軟體培訓網路研討會怎麼樣？ B：軟體本身看起來很有用，但講者用緩慢、【單調的】聲音講了兩個小時，沒有任何投影片或例子，所以好幾個人在結束前就睡著了。"},{"w":"dull","p":"adj.","d":"not interesting or exciting; (of a blade) not sharp","c":"枯燥的；無聊的；鈍的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the company's annual dinner at the hotel on Friday night, or did you leave early like last year? B: I left early again, because the speeches were very dull and long, the music was too quiet, and most of my friends from the sales department had already gone home.","t":"A：你喜歡週五晚上在飯店舉行的公司年度晚宴嗎？還是你又像去年一樣提早離開了？ B：我又提早離開了，因為致詞非常【枯燥】又冗長，音樂太小聲，而且我業務部的大多數朋友都已經回家了。"},{"w":"repetitive","p":"adj.","d":"doing or saying the same thing many times","c":"重複的；反覆的","s":"A: Why does the factory want to buy those expensive new robots for the packaging line next year? B: The workers there do the same repetitive movements all day long, putting bottles into boxes, so many of them get sore arms, and the robots can do that work faster and more safely.","t":"A：工廠為什麼明年要為包裝線購買那些昂貴的新機器人？ B：那裡的工人整天都在做相同的【重複】動作，把瓶子裝進箱子裡，所以很多人手臂痠痛，而機器人可以更快、更安全地完成這項工作。"},{"w":"uninteresting","p":"adj.","d":"not able to hold your attention","c":"無趣的；引不起興趣的","s":"A: Why did so few visitors stop at our booth at the trade fair, even though we had the best location near the entrance? B: I think our display looked plain and uninteresting compared with the other companies, which had bright lights, free samples, and video screens that attracted crowds all day.","t":"A：雖然我們的攤位在入口附近位置最好，為什麼在商展上停下來的訪客這麼少？ B：我覺得和其他公司比起來，我們的展示看起來單調又【無趣】，他們有明亮的燈光、免費樣品和影片螢幕，整天都吸引人潮。"},{"w":"tiresome","p":"adj.","d":"annoying and boring, making you feel tired","c":"令人厭煩的","s":"A: Why do you look so annoyed after the phone call from that customer in Osaka this morning? B: He called for the fifth time this week to complain about the same small delay, and answering the same questions again and again is becoming very tiresome, even though I try to stay polite.","t":"A：今天早上大阪那位客戶打電話來之後，你為什麼看起來這麼不高興？ B：他這週已經第五次打來抱怨同一個小延誤，一再回答同樣的問題變得非常【令人厭煩】，雖然我還是努力保持禮貌。"},{"w":"dreary","p":"adj.","d":"dull, dark, and making you feel sad","c":"沉悶陰鬱的","s":"A: Why is the human resources team planning to repaint the staff room and buy new furniture this spring? B: The room is small, gray, and dreary, with no windows and old chairs, so employees don't want to spend their lunch break there, and the manager hopes brighter colors will improve everyone's mood.","t":"A：人資團隊為什麼打算今年春天重新粉刷員工休息室並購買新家具？ B：那個房間又小又灰、【沉悶陰鬱】，沒有窗戶，椅子也很舊，所以員工都不想在那裡度過午休，經理希望明亮的顏色能改善大家的心情。"},{"w":"mind-numbing","p":"adj.","d":"so boring that you cannot think clearly","c":"極其無聊的；令人麻木的","s":"A: How is your summer internship at the bank going, and are they giving you any interesting projects yet? B: Not really, I spend eight hours a day typing numbers from paper forms into a computer, which is mind-numbing work, but my supervisor promised that I can join a client meeting next month.","t":"A：你在銀行的暑期實習進行得如何？他們有給你任何有趣的專案了嗎？ B：還沒有，我每天花八小時把紙本表格上的數字輸入電腦，這是【極其無聊的】工作，不過我的主管答應下個月讓我參加一場客戶會議。"},{"w":"pointless","p":"adj.","d":"having no purpose or use","c":"毫無意義的","s":"A: Should we hold another meeting tomorrow to discuss the new office layout with the design team? B: I think it would be pointless, because the director already made the final decision yesterday, and the furniture has been ordered, so we should spend our time preparing for the move instead.","t":"A：我們明天要不要再開一次會，和設計團隊討論新辦公室的配置？ B：我覺得那會【毫無意義】，因為主任昨天已經做了最後決定，家具也已經訂了，所以我們應該把時間花在準備搬遷上。"},{"w":"uninspiring","p":"adj.","d":"not making people feel excited or interested","c":"平淡無奇的；無法激勵人心的","s":"A: What did the marketing director think of the first design for our new summer advertising campaign? B: She said the design was uninspiring because it used the same old colors and slogans as last year, and she asked us to create something fresh that would make young customers notice our products.","t":"A：行銷主任對我們新夏季廣告活動的初版設計有什麼看法？ B：她說那個設計【平淡無奇】，因為用的是和去年一樣的老顏色和標語，她要我們創造一些新鮮的東西，讓年輕顧客注意到我們的產品。"},{"w":"stale","p":"adj.","d":"no longer fresh; old and not interesting","c":"不新鮮的；陳腐的","s":"A: Why didn't anyone eat the cookies that were left on the table in the break room after the client visit? B: They had been sitting there without a cover since Monday, so they were hard and stale, and someone finally threw them away and bought fresh fruit for the afternoon meeting instead.","t":"A：客戶來訪後留在休息室桌上的餅乾，為什麼都沒人吃？ B：它們從週一開始就沒蓋著一直放在那裡，所以變得又硬又【不新鮮】，最後有人把它們丟掉，改買新鮮水果給下午的會議。"},{"w":"lifeless","p":"adj.","d":"without energy or excitement; dead-looking","c":"死氣沉沉的；缺乏生氣的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner decide to change the music and lighting in the dining area last month? B: Customers said the place felt cold and lifeless on weekday evenings, so she added warm lights, soft jazz, and some plants, and now more couples come in for dinner after work.","t":"A：餐廳老闆上個月為什麼決定改變用餐區的音樂和燈光？ B：顧客說平日晚上那裡感覺冷冰冰又【死氣沉沉】，所以她加了溫暖的燈光、輕柔的爵士樂和一些植物，現在有更多情侶下班後來吃晚餐。"},{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual things you do regularly in the same order","c":"例行公事；慣例","s":"A: How do you stay so organized when you have to manage three different projects at the same time? B: I follow the same daily routine: I check my email at eight, plan my tasks before nine, and review the progress of each project at four, so nothing important gets forgotten.","t":"A：你同時要管理三個不同的專案，怎麼還能保持這麼有條理？ B：我每天都遵循相同的【例行公事】：八點查看電子郵件，九點前規劃工作，四點檢查每個專案的進度，這樣就不會忘記任何重要的事。"},{"w":"drag","p":"n.","d":"something boring or annoying (informal)","c":"令人厭煩的事；累贅","s":"A: Are you looking forward to the three-hour train ride to the branch office in Kaohsiung tomorrow morning? B: Not really, the trip is a real drag because the train is always crowded and the internet is slow, but at least I can read the sales report before I meet the branch manager.","t":"A：你期待明天早上搭三小時火車去高雄分公司嗎？ B：不太期待，這趟路程真是件【令人厭煩的事】，因為火車總是很擠、網路又慢，但至少我可以在見分公司經理前把銷售報告讀完。"},{"w":"chore","p":"n.","d":"a boring job that you have to do regularly","c":"雜務；乏味的工作","s":"A: Who is responsible for cleaning the coffee machine and emptying the recycling bins in our office every Friday? B: We take turns, so each person on the team does the chore once a month, and the schedule is posted on the kitchen wall so that nobody can forget their turn.","t":"A：每週五誰負責清理咖啡機和清空我們辦公室的回收桶？ B：我們輪流做，所以團隊中每個人每個月做一次這項【雜務】，值日表貼在茶水間的牆上，這樣就沒人會忘記輪到自己。"},{"w":"tedium","p":"n.","d":"the state of being long and boring","c":"單調乏味；沉悶","s":"A: How do the night security guards at the warehouse stay awake during their long twelve-hour shifts? B: They walk around the building every hour and listen to the radio between rounds, which helps them break the tedium of watching the same quiet cameras all night when nothing usually happens.","t":"A：倉庫的夜班保全在十二小時的長班中怎麼保持清醒？ B：他們每小時繞大樓巡邏一次，在巡邏之間聽收音機，這能幫助他們打破整晚盯著通常什麼事都沒發生的安靜監視器的【單調乏味】。"},{"w":"ennui","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being bored and not satisfied with life","c":"倦怠；無聊感","s":"A: Why did your manager suddenly decide to take a six-month break from her job after working at the company for fifteen years? B: She told me she felt a deep ennui because every year looked exactly the same, so she wants to travel, study design, and find new energy before she returns.","t":"A：你的經理在公司工作了十五年之後，為什麼突然決定休假六個月？ B：她告訴我，她感到一種深深的【倦怠】，因為每一年看起來都一模一樣，所以她想去旅行、學設計，並在回來之前找到新的活力。"},{"w":"plodding","p":"adj.","d":"slow and boring, without excitement","c":"緩慢乏味的；拖沓的","s":"A: Why did the publisher ask the author to rewrite the first three chapters of her new mystery novel? B: The editor said the story moved at a slow, plodding pace at the beginning, so readers might stop reading before the exciting murder scene finally happens in chapter four.","t":"A：出版社為什麼要求作者重寫她新推理小說的前三章？ B：編輯說故事開頭的節奏緩慢又【拖沓】，所以讀者可能在第四章終於出現精彩的謀殺場景之前就不想讀了。"},{"w":"predictable","p":"adj.","d":"happening in a way that you expected","c":"可預料的；老套的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the action movie that the team watched together after the company dinner on Friday? B: The special effects were great, but the story was so predictable that I knew exactly how it would end after twenty minutes, so I spent most of the time checking my phone.","t":"A：你喜歡週五公司晚餐後團隊一起看的那部動作片嗎？ B：特效很棒，但劇情太【老套】了，二十分鐘後我就完全知道會怎麼結束，所以我大部分時間都在看手機。"},{"w":"uneventful","p":"adj.","d":"with nothing interesting or unusual happening","c":"平靜無事的；平淡的","s":"A: How was your first week at the new branch, and did anything exciting happen while the manager was away? B: It was quite uneventful, to be honest, because there were only a few customers, no problems with the computers, and I spent most of my time reading training manuals.","t":"A：你在新分行的第一週過得怎麼樣？經理不在的時候有發生什麼令人興奮的事嗎？ B：老實說相當【平靜無事】，因為只有少數幾位顧客，電腦也沒有出問題，我大部分時間都在讀培訓手冊。"},{"w":"bland","p":"adj.","d":"without a strong taste or interest","c":"淡而無味的；平淡的","s":"A: Why did the hotel restaurant get so many bad reviews from guests on the travel website last month? B: Many guests said the food was too bland, with almost no salt or spices, so the new chef is now changing the menu and adding more local flavors to every dish.","t":"A：飯店餐廳上個月為什麼在旅遊網站上收到那麼多房客的負評？ B：很多房客說食物太【淡而無味】，幾乎沒有鹽或香料，所以新主廚正在更改菜單，並在每道菜中加入更多在地風味。"},{"w":"dry","p":"adj.","d":"boring because it is serious and has no humor or pictures","c":"枯燥的；乏味的","s":"A: Why do so many new employees skip the online course about company rules and safety laws? B: The course is very dry because it only has long pages of legal text with no pictures or examples, so the training team is planning to add short videos and quizzes next year.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多新進員工都跳過關於公司規定和安全法規的線上課程？ B：那門課程非常【枯燥】，因為只有一頁頁冗長的法律文字，沒有圖片或例子，所以培訓團隊打算明年加入短片和小測驗。"},{"w":"unvaried","p":"adj.","d":"always the same, with no change","c":"一成不變的","s":"A: Why are the staff complaining about the lunch boxes that the company provides in the cafeteria? B: The menu has been completely unvaried for six months, with the same chicken, rice, and cabbage every single day, so many workers now buy their lunch from shops near the office.","t":"A：員工為什麼在抱怨公司餐廳提供的便當？ B：六個月來菜單完全【一成不變】，每天都是一樣的雞肉、米飯和高麗菜，所以現在很多員工都去辦公室附近的店買午餐。"},{"w":"wearisome","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel tired and bored","c":"令人疲倦厭煩的","s":"A: How did the negotiations with the supplier go after you spent the whole week at their head office? B: It was a long and wearisome process, because we argued about the same prices every day, but in the end we signed a two-year contract that saves us ten percent.","t":"A：你在供應商總部待了一整週之後，和他們的談判進行得如何？ B：那是一個冗長又【令人疲倦厭煩的】過程，因為我們每天都在爭論同樣的價格，但最後我們簽了一份兩年合約，為我們省下了百分之十。"},{"w":"flat","p":"adj.","d":"without energy or growth; not changing","c":"平淡的；停滯的","s":"A: How were the sales of our new sports drink during the first quarter of this year? B: Sales were quite flat, with almost no growth from January to March, so the marketing team plans to give out free samples at gyms and running events to attract more customers.","t":"A：我們的新運動飲料今年第一季的銷售如何？ B：銷售相當【停滯】，從一月到三月幾乎沒有成長，所以行銷團隊打算在健身房和路跑活動發送免費樣品來吸引更多顧客。"},{"w":"humdrum","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and boring","c":"平凡乏味的","s":"A: Why did Kevin leave his comfortable job at the insurance office to become a tour guide in Europe? B: He said his life felt too humdrum, with the same desk, the same forms, and the same bus ride every day, and he wanted a job where he could meet new people.","t":"A：Kevin 為什麼離開保險公司舒適的工作，去歐洲當導遊？ B：他說他的生活感覺太【平凡乏味】，每天都是同樣的辦公桌、同樣的表格和同樣的公車路程，他想要一份能認識新朋友的工作。"},{"w":"dreariness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being dull, dark, and sad","c":"沉悶；陰鬱","s":"A: What made you decide to move your small design company out of that old building near the train station? B: The dreariness of the place was affecting our creativity, with dark hallways and gray walls everywhere, so we rented a bright studio with large windows near the river.","t":"A：是什麼讓你決定把你的小設計公司搬出火車站附近那棟舊大樓？ B：那個地方的【陰鬱沉悶】正在影響我們的創意，到處都是昏暗的走廊和灰色牆壁，所以我們在河邊租了一間有大窗戶的明亮工作室。"},{"w":"unstimulating","p":"adj.","d":"not making you think or feel interested","c":"缺乏刺激的；無法激發興趣的","s":"A: Why did the young engineer quit after only three months, even though the salary was very good? B: She found the work unstimulating because she only copied old drawings and never solved any real problems, so she accepted an offer from a smaller company with more challenging projects.","t":"A：那位年輕工程師為什麼才三個月就辭職了，即使薪水很好？ B：她覺得工作【缺乏刺激】，因為她只是複製舊圖紙，從來沒有解決過任何真正的問題，所以她接受了一家有更多挑戰性專案的小公司的錄取。"},{"w":"mechanical","p":"adj.","d":"done without thinking or feeling, like a machine","c":"機械式的；呆板的","s":"A: Why did the customer service manager change the way the staff answer phone calls last month? B: Customers said the staff sounded mechanical because they read the same script word for word, so now employees are trained to listen carefully and answer in a more natural and friendly way.","t":"A：客服經理上個月為什麼改變了員工接電話的方式？ B：顧客說員工聽起來很【機械式】，因為他們逐字照讀同一份稿子，所以現在員工都接受訓練，要仔細聆聽，並用更自然友善的方式回答。"},{"w":"lacklustre","p":"adj.","d":"lacking energy, excitement, or success","c":"平淡無奇的；表現不佳的","s":"A: Why is the board of directors meeting again this afternoon after the meeting they had on Monday? B: The company announced lacklustre results for the third quarter, with profits much lower than expected, so the directors need to discuss a new plan to reduce costs and win back investors.","t":"A：董事會週一才開過會，為什麼今天下午又要開會？ B：公司公布了第三季【表現不佳的】業績，利潤比預期低很多，所以董事們需要討論一個降低成本、贏回投資人的新計畫。"}]},{"unit":35,"theme":"Borrow 借用","cards":[{"w":"avid","p":"adj.","d":"very keen and interested in something","c":"熱衷的；熱心的","s":"A: Why does the library want to invite Mr. Chen to speak at next month's reading event, even though he is not a famous author or a teacher? B: He is an avid reader who borrows about ten books every week, so the staff believe his stories and advice will encourage more local families to visit.","t":"A：為什麼圖書館想邀請陳先生在下個月的閱讀活動上演講，即使他不是知名作家也不是老師？ B：他是一位【熱衷的】讀者，每週借大約十本書，所以館員相信他的故事和建議會鼓勵更多當地家庭來館。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is good or that someone should do something","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: I need to borrow a projector for the sales presentation on Friday, but our department's one is broken, so do you know where I can get another one quickly? B: I would recommend asking the IT office on the third floor, because they usually lend equipment to staff for a few days without any charge.","t":"A：我週五的業務簡報需要借一台投影機，但我們部門的那台壞了，你知道我可以去哪裡很快借到另一台嗎？ B：我會【建議】你去問三樓的資訊部辦公室，因為他們通常會免費把設備借給員工使用幾天。"},{"w":"awkward","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel uncomfortable or embarrassed","c":"尷尬的；令人不自在的","s":"A: Why didn't you ask your manager if you could borrow her laptop while yours was being repaired at the service center last week? B: It felt a little awkward to ask her, because she had just lent me her car the week before, so I used an old computer in the meeting room instead.","t":"A：上週你的筆電在維修中心修理時，你為什麼不問經理能不能借她的筆電？ B：向她開口讓我覺得有點【尷尬】，因為她前一週才剛借我車，所以我改用了會議室裡的一台舊電腦。"},{"w":"seldom","p":"adv.","d":"not often; rarely","c":"很少；不常","s":"A: Do you think we should buy our own ladder for the shop, or should we keep borrowing one from the hardware store next door whenever we need it? B: Let's keep borrowing, because we seldom need a ladder more than twice a year, and a new one would take up too much space in our small storage room.","t":"A：你覺得我們應該替店裡買一把自己的梯子，還是每次需要時繼續向隔壁五金行借？ B：繼續借吧，因為我們一年【很少】需要用到梯子超過兩次，而且買新的會占用我們小儲藏室太多空間。"},{"w":"innumerable","p":"adj.","d":"too many to be counted","c":"數不清的；無數的","s":"A: Why is the public library planning to move its old newspapers and magazines into a digital system next year? B: Because there are innumerable paper copies in the basement, and the staff spend hours finding the right one whenever a visitor wants to borrow an article for research.","t":"A：公立圖書館為什麼打算明年把舊報紙和雜誌移到數位系統？ B：因為地下室裡有【數不清的】紙本，每當有訪客想借閱某篇文章做研究時，館員都要花好幾個小時才找得到。"},{"w":"make ends meet","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have just enough money to pay for the things you need","c":"維持收支平衡；勉強維持生計","s":"A: Why did the young designer decide to borrow money from his parents instead of applying for a bank loan last month? B: His rent went up sharply in January, and he could barely make ends meet with his small salary, so his parents offered him a loan without any interest until he finds a better job.","t":"A：那位年輕設計師上個月為什麼決定向父母借錢，而不是去申請銀行貸款？ B：他的房租在一月大幅上漲，靠著微薄的薪水他幾乎無法【維持收支平衡】，所以他父母提供他無息借款，直到他找到更好的工作。"},{"w":"wear and tear","p":"n.phr.","d":"damage that happens to things through normal use over time","c":"（正常使用造成的）磨損；耗損","s":"A: The customer returned the camera that she rented from us for two weeks, so do we need to charge her extra for the small scratches on the lens cover? B: No, those marks are just normal wear and tear, and our rental agreement clearly says that customers only pay for serious damage or missing parts.","t":"A：那位客戶歸還了她向我們租了兩週的相機，我們需要因為鏡頭蓋上的小刮痕向她額外收費嗎？ B：不用，那些痕跡只是正常的【磨損】，而且我們的租賃合約寫得很清楚，客戶只需為嚴重損壞或遺失零件付費。"},{"w":"on time","p":"phr.","d":"at the correct time; not late","c":"準時","s":"A: Will the bank give us a lower interest rate if we ask for a second loan to open another branch of our restaurant next spring? B: There is a good chance, because we have made every monthly payment on time for the last three years, and the bank manager said they value reliable customers like us.","t":"A：如果我們申請第二筆貸款，在明年春天開餐廳的另一家分店，銀行會給我們較低的利率嗎？ B：很有可能，因為過去三年我們每一期月付款都【準時】繳納，而且銀行經理說他們很重視像我們這樣可靠的客戶。"},{"w":"fragile","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged","c":"易碎的；脆弱的","s":"A: Can I borrow the glass display stands from your shop for our product launch at the hotel this weekend? B: Sure, but please pack them carefully in the boxes with plenty of paper, because they are very fragile and could break easily if the delivery van hits a bump on the way.","t":"A：這週末我們在飯店舉辦產品發表會，我可以向你的店借那些玻璃展示架嗎？ B：當然可以，但請用大量紙張仔細把它們裝進箱子裡，因為它們非常【易碎】，如果貨車在途中顛簸，很容易就會破掉。"},{"w":"persist","p":"v.","d":"to continue to exist or happen for a long time","c":"持續；持續存在","s":"A: What should I do about the printer that we borrowed from the head office, since it keeps showing an error message even though I have restarted it several times this morning? B: If the problems persist after lunch, please call the technician, because we must print two hundred brochures for the trade fair by tomorrow morning.","t":"A：我們向總公司借來的印表機一直出現錯誤訊息，雖然我今天早上已經重新啟動好幾次了，我該怎麼辦？ B：如果午餐後問題【持續存在】，請打電話給技術人員，因為我們明天早上前必須印好兩百份商展用的手冊。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which each side accepts less than it wanted","c":"妥協；折衷","s":"A: Did you and the landlord finally agree on how much rent you have to pay while the office building is being repaired? B: Yes, we reached a compromise yesterday afternoon, so we will pay only half the normal rent for three months, and he will lend us some extra desks for the temporary rooms.","t":"A：大樓整修期間你們要付多少租金，你和房東終於談好了嗎？ B：是的，我們昨天下午達成了【妥協】，所以這三個月我們只付一半的正常租金，而且他還會借我們一些額外的桌子放在臨時辦公室。"},{"w":"write off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide that a debt will never be paid and remove it from the accounts","c":"註銷（債務）；勾銷","s":"A: What did the finance department decide about the money that a small customer borrowed from us two years ago and never paid back? B: Since the customer's company has closed and nobody can contact the owner, the director agreed to write off the debt and remove it from this year's accounts.","t":"A：關於一位小客戶兩年前向我們借了卻一直沒還的錢，財務部決定怎麼處理？ B：由於那位客戶的公司已經倒閉，也沒有人聯絡得上老闆，主管同意把這筆債務【註銷】，並從今年的帳目中移除。"},{"w":"assume","p":"v.","d":"to think something is true without being sure","c":"以為；假定；猜想","s":"A: Why didn't Ms. Lin bring back the meeting room keys that she borrowed from the reception desk yesterday afternoon? B: I assume that she simply forgot about them, because she left for the airport in a hurry, so I'll send her a text message and ask her to drop them off tomorrow morning.","t":"A：林小姐為什麼沒有把她昨天下午向櫃檯借的會議室鑰匙還回來？ B：我【猜想】她只是忘了，因為她匆忙趕去機場，所以我會傳簡訊給她，請她明天早上把鑰匙送回來。"},{"w":"reasonable","p":"adj.","d":"fair and not too expensive or too much","c":"合理的；價格公道的","s":"A: Is the interest rate on the small business loan from the local bank too high for our new bakery, or should we accept their offer? B: I think the rate is quite reasonable compared with the other banks that we visited, and the payment plan gives us five years to pay back the full amount.","t":"A：當地銀行提供的小型企業貸款利率對我們新開的麵包店來說會太高嗎？還是我們應該接受他們的條件？ B：和我們拜訪過的其他銀行相比，我覺得這個利率相當【合理】，而且還款計畫給我們五年時間償還全部金額。"},{"w":"tiny","p":"adj.","d":"very small","c":"極小的；很小的","s":"A: Can you lend me your storage room for a few days, because I need somewhere to keep the extra chairs for the company party? B: I'm sorry, but my storage room is really tiny, and it is already full of boxes, so maybe you should ask the building manager whether the basement is free.","t":"A：你可以把你的儲藏室借我幾天嗎？因為我需要地方放公司派對多出來的椅子。 B：抱歉，我的儲藏室真的很【小】，而且已經堆滿箱子了，也許你應該問問大樓管理員地下室是否有空。"},{"w":"let go","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop holding or keeping something (often with \"of\")","c":"放手；放開","s":"A: Why did your brother finally agree to lend his old car to his cousin, since he loved it so much and never allowed anyone else to drive it? B: He realized that he hardly ever drove it anymore, so he decided to let go of it for a while, and his cousin can now use it for her new job in the city.","t":"A：你哥哥那麼愛他的舊車，從不讓別人開，為什麼最後同意把它借給他的表妹？ B：他發現自己幾乎不再開那台車了，所以決定暫時【放手】，現在他表妹可以開它去城裡上新工作。"},{"w":"give in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finally agree to something after first refusing","c":"讓步；屈服","s":"A: Did the store manager agree to lend the customer a free phone while her broken one was being repaired? B: At first he said no, but the customer complained for twenty minutes in front of other shoppers, so he finally decided to give in and offered her an older model for one week.","t":"A：店經理有同意在顧客壞掉的手機維修期間借她一支免費手機嗎？ B：一開始他拒絕了，但那位顧客在其他購物者面前抱怨了二十分鐘，所以他最後決定【讓步】，借她一支舊型號手機使用一週。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed because you cannot do what you want","c":"令人沮喪的；令人洩氣的","s":"A: How was your experience applying for a student loan at the bank downtown last week? B: It was really frustrating, because I waited in line for two hours, and then the clerk told me that I had to fill out the same forms again on the bank's website.","t":"A：你上週在市區那家銀行申請學生貸款的經驗如何？ B：真的很【令人沮喪】，因為我排隊等了兩個小時，然後行員告訴我必須在銀行網站上重新填一次同樣的表格。"},{"w":"upset","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy and worried or angry","c":"不高興的；心煩的","s":"A: Why does Mr. Wang look so unhappy this morning, and why isn't he talking to anyone in the design team? B: He is upset because someone borrowed his expensive drawing tablet without asking, and when it came back yesterday, the screen had a long crack across the middle.","t":"A：王先生今天早上為什麼看起來這麼不開心，而且都不跟設計團隊的任何人說話？ B：他很【不高興】，因為有人沒問過他就借走了他昂貴的繪圖板，昨天還回來時，螢幕中間多了一道長長的裂痕。"},{"w":"repay","p":"v.","d":"to pay back money that you borrowed","c":"償還；還（錢）","s":"A: How long will it take our company to pay off the loan that we used to buy the new delivery trucks last year? B: If sales keep growing like this, we should be able to repay the full amount by next summer, which is almost two years earlier than the bank expected.","t":"A：我們公司去年用來買新貨車的那筆貸款，要多久才能還清？ B：如果銷售持續這樣成長，我們應該能在明年夏天前【償還】全部金額，比銀行預期的提早了將近兩年。"},{"w":"give back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to return something to the person who owns it","c":"歸還；還給","s":"A: Have you finished using the tools that you borrowed from the maintenance department for the shelves in the new meeting room? B: Almost, I just need to fix the last shelf, and then I'll give back the drill and the ladder before the department closes at five o'clock this afternoon.","t":"A：你向維修部借來裝新會議室架子的工具用完了嗎？ B：快好了，我只要再裝好最後一個架子，然後我會在維修部今天下午五點下班前把電鑽和梯子【歸還】。"}]},{"unit":36,"theme":"Break 休息","cards":[{"w":"rest","p":"n.","d":"a period of relaxing or sleeping to get back your energy","c":"休息","s":"A: You look exhausted after flying back from the trade show in Singapore, so are you planning to come to the sales meeting this afternoon? B: No, my manager told me to go home and get some rest first, because I barely slept on the plane and I need a clear head for tomorrow's client visit.","t":"A：你從新加坡的商展飛回來看起來累壞了，你打算來參加今天下午的業務會議嗎？ B：不，我的經理叫我先回家好好【休息】，因為我在飛機上幾乎沒睡，而且明天拜訪客戶需要頭腦清醒。"},{"w":"pause","p":"n.","d":"a short stop in speaking or doing something","c":"暫停；停頓","s":"A: The speaker at this morning's training session talked very fast, so how did the new employees manage to take notes on all the safety rules? B: She made a short pause after each important point, which gave everyone a few seconds to write things down and ask questions before she moved on to the next slide.","t":"A：今天早上訓練課程的講者講得很快，新員工是怎麼把所有安全規定都記下來的？ B：她在每個重點之後都會短暫【停頓】一下，讓大家有幾秒鐘可以寫下來並發問，然後才進到下一張投影片。"},{"w":"interval","p":"n.","d":"the time between two events","c":"間隔；間隔時間","s":"A: How often does the shuttle bus run between the train station and the convention center during the international technology fair next week? B: The organizers said there will be a fifteen-minute interval between buses from seven in the morning until nine at night, so visitors should never have to wait very long in the cold.","t":"A：下週國際科技展期間，火車站和會展中心之間的接駁車多久一班？ B：主辦單位說從早上七點到晚上九點，每班車之間【間隔】十五分鐘，所以參觀者不必在寒冷中等太久。"},{"w":"time off","p":"n.phr.","d":"time when you are not at work","c":"休假；不上班的時間","s":"A: Have you decided what you're going to do after the big product launch is finished at the end of this month? B: I've asked my supervisor for some time off in early December, because I have been working overtime for weeks and I really want to visit my parents in the countryside.","t":"A：你決定這個月底大型產品發表會結束後要做什麼了嗎？ B：我已經向主管申請十二月初【休假】幾天，因為我已經連續加班好幾週了，真的很想回鄉下看看我爸媽。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and become calm","c":"放鬆","s":"A: The hotel guests in room 512 just complained that the meeting next door was too noisy, so what should we offer them? B: Let's give them free tickets to the spa on the top floor, where they can relax in the hot pool and enjoy a massage while we move the conference to a different room.","t":"A：512號房的房客剛剛抱怨隔壁的會議太吵，我們應該提供他們什麼？ B：我們送他們頂樓水療中心的免費券吧，他們可以在溫水池裡【放鬆】、享受按摩，同時我們把會議移到別的房間。"},{"w":"unwind","p":"v.","d":"to relax after work or a stressful time","c":"放鬆心情；紓壓","s":"A: Most of the accountants have been staying in the office until midnight to finish the annual report, so how can we help them feel better? B: I'm planning a casual dinner at the Italian restaurant across the street on Friday night, so everyone can unwind together and forget about numbers for a few hours.","t":"A：大部分會計師為了完成年度報告都待在辦公室到半夜，我們要怎麼讓他們好過一點？ B：我打算週五晚上在對街的義大利餐廳辦個輕鬆的晚餐，讓大家可以一起【放鬆心情】，暫時忘掉數字幾個小時。"},{"w":"recharge","p":"v.","d":"to get your energy back by resting","c":"恢復精力；充電","s":"A: Why did the company decide to give every employee an extra day off after the busy holiday shopping season? B: The managers believe that people need time to rest and recharge after working long hours, so they come back to work with more energy and new ideas for the coming year.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定在忙碌的假期購物季後給每位員工多放一天假？ B：主管們認為大家在長時間工作後需要休息、【恢復精力】，這樣回來上班時才會更有活力，並為新的一年帶來新點子。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to get well again after being sick, hurt or in trouble","c":"康復；恢復","s":"A: Is the warehouse manager coming back to work on Monday, or should we ask someone else to check the deliveries next week? B: He called this morning and said he needs a few more days at home to recover from the flu, so please ask Linda to handle the deliveries until he returns.","t":"A：倉庫經理星期一會回來上班嗎？還是我們下週應該請別人檢查送貨？ B：他今天早上打電話來說還需要在家幾天從流感中【康復】，所以在他回來之前請琳達處理送貨的事。"},{"w":"refresh","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less tired and more lively","c":"使恢復精神；使清爽","s":"A: The workshop has been going on for three hours, and some of the participants look like they are falling asleep in their chairs. B: Let's stop for fifteen minutes so people can get a cup of coffee and some fresh air outside, which should refresh everyone before we start the final group activity.","t":"A：研習已經進行三個小時了，有些參加者看起來快在椅子上睡著了。 B：我們停十五分鐘，讓大家去喝杯咖啡、到外面呼吸新鮮空氣，這應該能讓大家【恢復精神】，再開始最後的小組活動。"},{"w":"breather","p":"n.","d":"a short rest from work or effort","c":"短暫休息；喘口氣","s":"A: We have been answering customer emails nonstop since eight o'clock, and I can't even think clearly anymore. B: Why don't we take a quick breather and walk to the bakery around the corner, because a short walk will help us focus better when we come back to finish the rest of the messages.","t":"A：我們從八點開始就不停地回覆客戶的電子郵件，我已經沒辦法清楚思考了。 B：我們何不【稍作喘息】，走到轉角的麵包店，因為短暫散步能幫助我們回來處理剩下的訊息時更專心。"},{"w":"respite","p":"n.","d":"a short time of relief from something unpleasant","c":"暫緩；喘息","s":"A: The construction work outside our office has been extremely loud every day this month, so has anything changed? B: Yes, the workers are stopping for the national holiday this weekend, so we will finally get a short respite from the noise, although they will start drilling again on Monday morning.","t":"A：這個月我們辦公室外面的工程每天都非常吵，有什麼改變嗎？ B：有，工人們這個週末因國定假日停工，所以我們終於可以從噪音中得到短暫的【喘息】，不過他們星期一早上又會開始鑽地了。"},{"w":"timeout","p":"n.","d":"a short stop in a game so a team can rest or plan","c":"（比賽中的）暫停","s":"A: The basketball team that our company sponsors was losing badly at halftime, so what happened in the second half of the game? B: The coach called a timeout in the third quarter and gave the players a new plan, and after that they scored twenty points in a row and won the match.","t":"A：我們公司贊助的籃球隊上半場輸得很慘，下半場發生了什麼事？ B：教練在第三節喊了【暫停】，給球員們一個新戰術，之後他們連得二十分，贏了比賽。"},{"w":"intermission","p":"n.","d":"a short break between the parts of a show or concert","c":"中場休息","s":"A: The clients we invited to the concert tonight might want something to eat, so is there a good time to visit the snack bar? B: Yes, there is a twenty-minute intermission between the first and second parts of the show, so we can take them to the lobby for drinks and sandwiches then.","t":"A：我們今晚邀去聽音樂會的客戶可能會想吃點東西，有沒有適合去點心吧的時間？ B：有，表演上下半場之間有二十分鐘的【中場休息】，我們可以那時帶他們去大廳喝飲料、吃三明治。"},{"w":"downtime","p":"n.","d":"time when a machine or system is not working","c":"停機時間；（系統）無法運作的時間","s":"A: Why couldn't our customers place any online orders last night between midnight and three in the morning? B: The IT department planned some downtime to update the website's payment system, and they sent an email to all customers last week to explain that the site would be unavailable for a few hours.","t":"A：為什麼我們的顧客昨晚午夜到凌晨三點之間無法在線上下單？ B：資訊部門安排了一段【停機時間】來更新網站的付款系統，他們上週也寄了電子郵件給所有顧客，說明網站會有幾個小時無法使用。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"free time when you are not working","c":"閒暇；空閒時間","s":"A: What kinds of facilities will the new apartment building near our head office offer to the people who live there? B: Besides a swimming pool and a gym, there will be a large garden and a reading room, so residents can enjoy their leisure without leaving the building on weekends.","t":"A：我們總公司附近的新公寓大樓會提供住戶哪些設施？ B：除了游泳池和健身房，還會有大花園和閱讀室，所以住戶週末不必離開大樓就能享受【閒暇時光】。"},{"w":"vacation","p":"n.","d":"a period of time away from work or school for rest or travel","c":"假期；度假","s":"A: I noticed that Mr. Chen's desk has been empty all week, so is he working from home or visiting a client overseas? B: Neither, he is on a two-week vacation with his family in Japan, and he asked me to answer his phone calls and forward any urgent emails until he gets back.","t":"A：我注意到陳先生的座位整個禮拜都空著，他是在家工作還是去國外拜訪客戶？ B：都不是，他和家人在日本【度假】兩週，他請我在他回來之前幫他接電話並轉寄緊急郵件。"},{"w":"holiday","p":"n.","d":"a day when most people do not have to work","c":"假日；節日","s":"A: Will the bank downtown be open on Monday, because I need to deposit the payments we received from our customers? B: No, Monday is a national holiday, so all the banks and government offices will be closed, but you can use the machine in the lobby or wait until Tuesday.","t":"A：市中心的銀行星期一會開嗎？我需要把客戶付的款項存進去。 B：不會，星期一是國定【假日】，所有銀行和政府機關都不上班，不過你可以使用大廳的機器，或等到星期二。"},{"w":"nap","p":"n.","d":"a short sleep during the day","c":"小睡；午睡","s":"A: You seem much more cheerful this afternoon than you were this morning, so did you drink another cup of strong coffee? B: Actually, I took a short nap in the staff lounge during my lunch hour, and twenty minutes of sleep made me feel much more awake for the rest of the day.","t":"A：你今天下午看起來比早上開心多了，是又喝了一杯濃咖啡嗎？ B：其實我午休時間在員工休息室【小睡】了一下，睡二十分鐘讓我接下來一整天都清醒多了。"},{"w":"step back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop and think about a situation from a distance","c":"退一步（思考）","s":"A: Our team has been arguing about the new advertising plan for two hours, and nobody wants to change their opinion. B: I think we should step back and look at the bigger picture, because the main goal is to attract younger customers, not to prove who has the best idea.","t":"A：我們團隊為了新的廣告企劃已經吵了兩個小時，沒有人想改變意見。 B：我想我們應該【退一步】看看大局，因為主要目標是吸引年輕顧客，而不是證明誰的點子最好。"},{"w":"slow down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do things less quickly or work less hard","c":"放慢腳步；減速","s":"A: The doctor at the company health check said my blood pressure is too high, and I'm worried because I work twelve hours a day. B: Maybe it's time to slow down a little and let your assistant handle some of the smaller tasks, because your health is more important than any project deadline.","t":"A：公司健康檢查的醫生說我的血壓太高，我很擔心，因為我一天工作十二個小時。 B：或許是時候【放慢腳步】，讓你的助理處理一些比較小的工作了，因為你的健康比任何專案截止日都重要。"},{"w":"switch off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop thinking about work and relax","c":"放空；不再想工作","s":"A: Even when you're at home in the evening, you keep checking your work messages, so don't you ever feel tired? B: You're right, and my wife says I need to switch off after dinner, so from now on I will leave my work phone in my bag and spend time with my children instead.","t":"A：即使晚上在家，你也一直在看工作訊息，你都不會覺得累嗎？ B：你說得對，我太太說我晚餐後需要【放空】，所以從現在起我會把工作手機放在包包裡，改成陪孩子。"},{"w":"take it easy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to rest and not work too hard","c":"放輕鬆；別太勞累","s":"A: I just got back from the hospital after my knee operation, but I'm thinking about returning to the office on Wednesday. B: Please take it easy for at least another week and work from home if you need to, because the doctor said walking too much could make your knee worse.","t":"A：我膝蓋開完刀剛出院，但我在考慮星期三就回辦公室。 B：請至少再【放輕鬆、別太勞累】一個禮拜，有需要的話就在家工作，因為醫生說走太多路會讓你的膝蓋更糟。"},{"w":"wind down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to slowly relax after a busy or stressful time","c":"（逐漸）放鬆下來","s":"A: What do you usually do in the evening after a stressful day of meetings with difficult customers? B: I like to wind down by taking a warm bath and listening to soft music, and I try not to look at any screens for an hour before I go to bed.","t":"A：和難搞的客戶開了一整天壓力很大的會之後，你晚上通常做什麼？ B：我喜歡泡個熱水澡、聽輕柔的音樂來【放鬆下來】，而且睡前一小時我會盡量不看任何螢幕。"},{"w":"retreat","p":"n.","d":"a quiet place or trip where people go to rest, think or plan","c":"休養處；靜修（會議）","s":"A: Where is the management team going for their two-day planning meeting next month, since the conference room here is being repainted? B: They booked a quiet mountain retreat about two hours from the city, where they can discuss next year's goals, go hiking together, and stay away from daily office problems.","t":"A：會議室在重新粉刷，管理團隊下個月兩天的規劃會議要去哪裡開？ B：他們預訂了距離市區大約兩小時、一處安靜的山中【休養所】，可以在那裡討論明年的目標、一起健行，並遠離日常辦公室的問題。"},{"w":"escape","p":"n.","d":"a way to get away from a stressful situation for a while","c":"逃離；解脫","s":"A: Why are so many office workers from the city booking rooms at that small beach hotel every weekend this summer? B: The hotel advertises itself as the perfect escape from busy city life, and its quiet rooms, fresh seafood, and beautiful sunsets make guests feel calm after a stressful week.","t":"A：為什麼今年夏天有那麼多城市上班族每週末都去訂那家小海濱飯店？ B：那家飯店宣傳自己是【逃離】忙碌都市生活的完美去處，安靜的房間、新鮮海鮮和美麗的夕陽，讓客人在壓力大的一週後感到平靜。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities people do for fun in their free time","c":"休閒娛樂；消遣","s":"A: The city government wants to turn the old factory near the river into something useful for local families, so what is the plan? B: They are going to build a park with tennis courts, bicycle paths, and a children's playground, so people will have more space for recreation on evenings and weekends.","t":"A：市政府想把河邊的舊工廠改造成對當地家庭有用的地方，計畫是什麼？ B：他們要蓋一座公園，有網球場、自行車道和兒童遊樂場，讓大家在晚上和週末有更多空間從事【休閒娛樂】。"},{"w":"refreshment","p":"n.","d":"light food and drinks","c":"茶點；點心飲料","s":"A: Our seminar for new clients will last from nine in the morning until four in the afternoon, so will the guests get anything to eat or drink? B: Yes, the hotel will set up a refreshment table with coffee, tea, cookies, and fresh fruit during each break, and a full lunch will be served in the restaurant at noon.","t":"A：我們的新客戶研討會從早上九點到下午四點，來賓會有東西吃喝嗎？ B：有，飯店會在每次休息時擺設一張放有咖啡、茶、餅乾和新鮮水果的【茶點】桌，中午也會在餐廳供應完整的午餐。"},{"w":"reset","p":"v.","d":"to start again in a fresh way; to set again","c":"重新設定；重整","s":"A: I came back from my week at the beach feeling great, but I'm worried that the stress will return as soon as I open my email. B: A good vacation can really help you reset your mind, so try to keep some of those calm habits, like taking a walk at lunch, now that you're back at work.","t":"A：我在海邊待了一週回來感覺很棒，但我擔心一打開電子郵件壓力就會回來。 B：一個好的假期真的能幫你【重新整理】心情，所以既然回來上班了，試著保留一些平靜的習慣，例如午餐時去散步。"},{"w":"disconnect","p":"v.","d":"to stop being connected to work, people or the internet","c":"斷開；中斷聯繫","s":"A: Are you going to bring your laptop on your camping trip next weekend in case the office needs to contact you? B: No, I want to completely disconnect from work and the internet for three days, so I told my team to call my manager if any serious problems happen while I'm away.","t":"A：你下週末去露營會帶筆電嗎？以防辦公室需要聯絡你。 B：不會，我想完全【斷開】工作和網路三天，所以我已經告訴團隊，如果我不在時發生任何嚴重問題就打給我的經理。"}]},{"unit":37,"theme":"Building 建築","cards":[{"w":"architect","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to design buildings","c":"建築師","s":"A: The new head office downtown looks amazing with all that glass and natural light, so who was in charge of the design? B: Our company hired a young architect from Taipei who won an award last year, and she spent months meeting staff to understand how we actually work before drawing anything.","t":"A：市中心的新總部有那麼多玻璃和自然光，看起來太棒了，是誰負責設計的？ B：我們公司聘請了一位來自台北、去年得過獎的年輕【建築師】，她在動手畫圖之前，花了好幾個月和員工見面，了解我們實際上如何工作。"},{"w":"planner","p":"n.","d":"a person who decides how land and buildings in a town should be used","c":"都市規劃師；規劃者","s":"A: Why hasn't the shopping mall project started yet, even though the builders were ready to begin work last month? B: The city planner asked us to change the parking area and add more trees along the road, so our team is still updating the drawings before we can get final approval.","t":"A：為什麼購物中心的工程還沒開始？建商上個月就已經準備好要動工了。 B：市政府的【都市規劃師】要求我們修改停車區，並在道路旁加種更多樹木，所以我們團隊還在更新設計圖，之後才能取得最後核准。"},{"w":"delay","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen later than planned","c":"延誤；延後","s":"A: Do you think the new factory will still open in March as the manager promised at the shareholders' meeting? B: Probably not, because the heavy rain this winter has flooded the site twice, and the builders say the bad weather will delay the opening by at least two months.","t":"A：你認為新工廠還會像經理在股東大會上承諾的那樣在三月開幕嗎？ B：大概不會，因為今年冬天的大雨已經淹了工地兩次，建商說惡劣的天氣會讓開幕【延後】至少兩個月。"},{"w":"detection","p":"n.","d":"the act of noticing or discovering something, often with a machine","c":"偵測；發現","s":"A: Why did the hotel spend so much money on new equipment for every guest room and hallway this year? B: After a small kitchen fire last spring, the owners decided to install a modern smoke detection system, so the staff can find any danger quickly and guide guests out safely.","t":"A：為什麼飯店今年在每間客房和走廊都花那麼多錢買新設備？ B：去年春天廚房發生小火災後，業主決定安裝現代化的煙霧【偵測】系統，讓員工能快速發現任何危險，並安全地引導房客離開。"},{"w":"faulty","p":"adj.","d":"not working correctly because something is wrong with it","c":"有缺陷的；故障的","s":"A: The lights on the third floor keep turning off during our afternoon meetings, and it's really annoying everyone in the department. B: The building manager checked it this morning and found some faulty wiring behind the ceiling, so an electrician is coming tomorrow to replace it before anyone gets hurt.","t":"A：三樓的燈在我們下午開會時一直熄掉，讓部門裡每個人都很困擾。 B：大樓管理員今天早上檢查過了，發現天花板後面有一些【有缺陷的】電線，所以明天會有電工來更換，以免有人受傷。"},{"w":"inspection","p":"n.","d":"a careful check of something to make sure it is safe or correct","c":"檢查；視察","s":"A: Are we allowed to move our office furniture into the new building on Monday, or do we need to wait longer? B: We have to wait until Thursday, because a safety officer from the city government is coming for a final inspection of the fire exits, elevators and electrical systems on Wednesday afternoon.","t":"A：我們星期一可以把辦公家具搬進新大樓嗎？還是要再等久一點？ B：我們要等到星期四，因為市政府的安全人員星期三下午會來對逃生出口、電梯和電力系統做最後的【檢查】。"},{"w":"hype","p":"v.","d":"to advertise something a lot so that it seems better than it really is","c":"大肆宣傳；炒作","s":"A: Everyone in the marketing team seems excited about the new apartment tower by the river, but is it really that special? B: Not really, because the developer paid a lot of famous bloggers to hype it online, but when I visited last weekend, the rooms were small and the views were ordinary.","t":"A：行銷部的每個人好像都對河邊那棟新公寓大樓很興奮，它真的那麼特別嗎？ B：其實沒有，建商花錢請了很多知名部落客在網路上【大肆宣傳】，但我上週末去參觀時，房間很小，景觀也很普通。"},{"w":"amenity","p":"n.","d":"something in a building or area that makes life more comfortable or useful","c":"便利設施","s":"A: The rent at the new business center is higher than our current office, so why are you recommending that we move there? B: The price includes a gym, free parking and a rooftop café, and I think the most useful amenity for our team is the twenty-four-hour meeting room that clients can book online.","t":"A：新商務中心的租金比我們目前的辦公室高，你為什麼還建議我們搬過去？ B：價格包含健身房、免費停車和頂樓咖啡廳，而我認為對我們團隊最有用的【設施】是客戶可以上網預約的二十四小時會議室。"},{"w":"wander","p":"v.","d":"to walk slowly around a place without a clear purpose","c":"閒逛；漫步","s":"A: What did you do while you were waiting for the property agent at the old train station building yesterday afternoon? B: She was forty minutes late because of traffic, so I decided to wander around the empty halls and take photos of the beautiful windows and wooden ceilings for our report.","t":"A：昨天下午你在舊火車站大樓等房仲的時候做了什麼？ B：她因為塞車晚了四十分鐘，所以我決定在空蕩蕩的大廳裡隨意【閒逛】，並替我們的報告拍下美麗的窗戶和木頭天花板。"},{"w":"run-down","p":"adj.","d":"in very poor condition because nobody has taken care of it","c":"破舊的；失修的","s":"A: Why did the company choose such an old warehouse near the harbor for its new design studio? B: The building was very run-down when we bought it, with broken windows and peeling paint, but the price was low, and we had enough money left to repair everything and make it bright and modern.","t":"A：公司為什麼為新的設計工作室選了港口附近那麼舊的倉庫？ B：我們買下時那棟建築非常【破舊】，窗戶破了、油漆剝落，但價格很低，我們剩下的錢足夠把一切修好，讓它變得明亮又現代。"},{"w":"donkey's years","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very long time (informal)","c":"很長一段時間；好多年","s":"A: Do you know when the convention center across the street was last repainted, because the outside looks really dirty now? B: Nobody in our office remembers exactly, but my manager says it hasn't been painted for donkey's years, probably since before she joined the company over twenty years ago.","t":"A：你知道對街的會議中心上次重新粉刷是什麼時候嗎？外觀現在看起來真的很髒。 B：我們辦公室沒人記得確切時間，但我的經理說它已經【好多年】沒粉刷了，可能是在她二十多年前進公司之前。"},{"w":"laughing stock","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person or thing that everyone laughs at","c":"笑柄","s":"A: Why is the mayor so worried about the design of the new city library that was shown in the newspaper today? B: Many people online say it looks like a giant shoebox, and he's afraid the town will become a laughing stock if the builders finish it without making any changes to the plan.","t":"A：為什麼市長對今天報上刊登的新市立圖書館設計那麼擔心？ B：網路上很多人說它看起來像一個巨大的鞋盒，他擔心如果建商不修改計畫就完工，整個城鎮會成為大家的【笑柄】。"},{"w":"run-of-the-mill","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and not special in any way","c":"普通的；平凡的","s":"A: The client said our first design for their new hotel lobby was nice, so why do they want us to start again? B: They felt it was too run-of-the-mill and looked like every other hotel in the city, so they're asking for something more creative that guests will remember and share on social media.","t":"A：客戶說我們為他們新飯店大廳做的第一版設計還不錯，為什麼還要我們重新開始？ B：他們覺得太【普通】了，看起來就跟城裡其他飯店一樣，所以他們想要更有創意、讓房客會記住並分享到社群媒體的設計。"},{"w":"pass the time","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something so that a period of waiting does not feel long","c":"打發時間","s":"A: How did the visitors keep busy while the elevator in the tower was being repaired for nearly two hours yesterday? B: Our receptionist offered them coffee in the lobby, and many of them chose to pass the time by reading magazines, chatting with each other or looking at the photos of the building's history on the walls.","t":"A：昨天大樓電梯維修了將近兩個小時，訪客們是怎麼打發時間的？ B：我們的接待員在大廳請他們喝咖啡，許多人選擇看雜誌、彼此聊天或欣賞牆上大樓歷史照片來【打發時間】。"},{"w":"stack up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to compare with something else in quality or value","c":"比得上；與……相比","s":"A: Our team must choose between two office buildings by Friday, so how does the new one near the station compare? B: When you look at the rent, the parking and the distance to the metro, it doesn't really stack up well against the older building on Main Street, which is cheaper and has much bigger rooms.","t":"A：我們團隊必須在星期五前從兩棟辦公大樓中選一棟，車站附近那棟新的比起來怎麼樣？ B：從租金、停車和到捷運的距離來看，它跟主街上那棟較舊的大樓相比並不怎麼【比得上】，那棟比較便宜，房間也大得多。"},{"w":"density","p":"n.","d":"how many people or things there are in a certain area","c":"密度","s":"A: Why does the government want to build so many tall apartment towers near the new metro line this year? B: The area already has a high population density, and officials think more homes close to the trains will help reduce traffic, since thousands of people can walk to the station instead of driving.","t":"A：為什麼政府今年要在新捷運線附近蓋那麼多高樓公寓？ B：這個區域的人口【密度】已經很高，官員認為在車站附近多蓋住宅可以幫助減少交通量，因為成千上萬的人可以走路去車站而不用開車。"},{"w":"skyrocket","p":"v.","d":"to rise very quickly and suddenly","c":"飆漲；急速上升","s":"A: Why are so many young families moving out of the city center and into the suburbs this year? B: Since the new high-speed rail station opened downtown, house prices have started to skyrocket, and most couples who work nearby can no longer afford even a small apartment close to their offices.","t":"A：為什麼今年有那麼多年輕家庭搬離市中心、搬到郊區？ B：自從市中心的新高鐵站啟用後，房價開始【飆漲】，大多數在附近上班的夫妻甚至買不起離辦公室近的小公寓了。"},{"w":"torn","p":"adj.","d":"unable to decide between two choices","c":"左右為難的；猶豫不決的","s":"A: Have the managers decided whether to repair the old headquarters or build a completely new one outside the city? B: Not yet, because they're torn between saving the historic building that the founder loved and moving to a modern space that would be much cheaper to heat, cool and maintain.","t":"A：經理們決定好要修繕舊總部，還是在城外蓋全新的總部了嗎？ B：還沒，因為他們在保留創辦人喜愛的歷史建築和搬到冷暖氣與維護都便宜許多的現代空間之間【左右為難】。"},{"w":"monstrosity","p":"n.","d":"a large building or object that is very ugly","c":"龐大醜陋的建築；怪物","s":"A: What do local residents think about the huge parking garage the company built next to the old temple last year? B: Most of them hate it and call it a concrete monstrosity, because it blocks the view of the mountains and looks completely out of place among the small traditional shops.","t":"A：當地居民對公司去年在老廟旁蓋的那座巨大停車場有什麼看法？ B：大多數人很討厭它，稱它為水泥【怪物】，因為它擋住了山景，而且和周圍的小型傳統商店完全格格不入。"},{"w":"justification","p":"n.","d":"a good reason for doing something","c":"正當理由","s":"A: The board wants to spend millions on a new glass entrance for the head office, but do we really need it? B: I asked the same question at the meeting, and nobody could give a clear justification for the cost, especially when our factory roofs are leaking and need urgent repairs before the rainy season.","t":"A：董事會想花幾百萬元替總部建一個新的玻璃入口，但我們真的需要嗎？ B：我在會議上問了同樣的問題，沒有人能為這筆花費給出明確的【理由】，尤其是我們工廠的屋頂在漏水，需要在雨季前緊急修理。"},{"w":"renovate","p":"v.","d":"to repair and improve an old building or room","c":"翻修；整修","s":"A: Why is the restaurant on the ground floor of our building closed for the whole summer this year? B: The owner plans to renovate the kitchen and dining area, adding new lights, larger windows and an outdoor terrace, so they can serve more customers when they reopen in September.","t":"A：為什麼我們大樓一樓的餐廳今年整個夏天都關門？ B：老闆打算【翻修】廚房和用餐區，加裝新燈具、更大的窗戶和戶外露台，好讓九月重新開幕時能服務更多客人。"},{"w":"castle","p":"n.","d":"a large strong building with thick walls, built long ago to protect people","c":"城堡","s":"A: Where are we holding the company's anniversary dinner next month, since the usual hotel ballroom is fully booked? B: The event team found a beautiful stone castle on a hill outside the city that was built three hundred years ago, and it now rents out its great hall for weddings and business events.","t":"A：既然平常用的飯店宴會廳都訂滿了，下個月的公司週年晚宴要在哪裡舉辦？ B：活動團隊在城外的山丘上找到一座三百年前建造的美麗石造【城堡】，它現在把大廳出租給婚禮和商務活動使用。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to damage or spoil something completely","c":"破壞；毀掉","s":"A: Why are the people who live near the beach so angry about the new hotel the developer wants to build there? B: They believe a twenty-floor tower would ruin the natural beauty of the coastline, and they worry that tourists will stop coming if the quiet little fishing village disappears.","t":"A：為什麼住在海灘附近的人對開發商想在那裡蓋新飯店那麼生氣？ B：他們認為一棟二十層樓的大樓會【破壞】海岸線的自然美景，而且擔心如果寧靜的小漁村消失，遊客就不會再來了。"},{"w":"quaint","p":"adj.","d":"attractive in an unusual or old-fashioned way","c":"古色古香的；別緻的","s":"A: Where did you stay during the business trip to the countryside last week, since there are no big hotels there? B: The client booked us into a quaint little guesthouse with old wooden doors, flower boxes on every window and a garden, and the owner cooked us a delicious breakfast every morning.","t":"A：上週你去鄉下出差時住在哪裡？那裡沒有大飯店。 B：客戶幫我們訂了一間【古色古香】的小民宿，有老木門、每扇窗都有花箱，還有一座花園，老闆每天早上都替我們煮美味的早餐。"},{"w":"attraction","p":"n.","d":"a place or thing that people visit for interest or fun","c":"景點；吸引人的事物","s":"A: Why does the city want to spend so much money restoring the old sugar factory by the river? B: The tourism office hopes it will become a major attraction for visitors, with shops, a museum and restaurants inside, which would bring more jobs and money to the local businesses nearby.","t":"A：為什麼市政府要花那麼多錢修復河邊的舊糖廠？ B：觀光局希望它能成為吸引遊客的主要【景點】，裡面有商店、博物館和餐廳，能為附近的在地商家帶來更多工作機會和收入。"},{"w":"hassle","p":"n.","d":"something annoying that causes trouble or takes a lot of effort","c":"麻煩事","s":"A: Why did your team decide to rent a furnished office instead of buying your own desks, chairs and cabinets? B: Buying, delivering and setting up all that furniture would be a real hassle for a small company like ours, and we'd rather spend our time and energy finding new clients and growing the business.","t":"A：為什麼你們團隊決定租附家具的辦公室，而不是自己買桌椅和櫃子？ B：對我們這樣的小公司來說，購買、運送和組裝所有家具真的很【麻煩】，我們寧願把時間和精力花在開發新客戶和拓展業務上。"},{"w":"irrelevant","p":"adj.","d":"not connected with or important to the subject","c":"無關的；無關緊要的","s":"A: The buyer keeps asking about the color of the curtains in the empty office, but shouldn't we focus on more important things? B: Yes, those details are completely irrelevant right now, because we still need to agree on the price, the length of the lease and who will pay for the roof repairs.","t":"A：買方一直問空辦公室窗簾的顏色，但我們不是應該專注在更重要的事情上嗎？ B：對，那些細節現在完全【無關緊要】，因為我們還需要談妥價格、租約期限，以及誰要支付屋頂維修費用。"},{"w":"aesthetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with beauty and how something looks","c":"在美學上；外觀上","s":"A: The new art museum downtown cost a lot of money, so are people happy with the final result? B: Most visitors say it is aesthetically pleasing, with its curved white walls and huge windows, but some staff complain that the building is hard to clean and difficult to heat in winter.","t":"A：市中心的新美術館花了很多錢，大家對最後的成果滿意嗎？ B：大多數參觀者說它在【美學上】令人賞心悅目，有彎曲的白牆和巨大的窗戶，但有些員工抱怨這棟建築很難清潔，冬天也很難保暖。"},{"w":"outskirts","p":"n.","d":"the outer areas of a city or town","c":"郊區；市郊","s":"A: Why is the furniture company building its new warehouse so far away from the city center? B: Land on the outskirts of the city is much cheaper, and the location is close to the highway, so trucks can deliver products quickly without getting stuck in downtown traffic every morning.","t":"A：家具公司為什麼要把新倉庫蓋在離市中心那麼遠的地方？ B：城市【郊區】的土地便宜得多，而且位置靠近高速公路，所以卡車可以快速送貨，不會每天早上卡在市中心的車陣裡。"},{"w":"handful","p":"n.","d":"a small number of people or things","c":"少數；一把","s":"A: How many people actually came to see the model apartments at the open house last Saturday? B: Only a handful of visitors showed up in the morning because of the typhoon warning, but more families arrived after lunch when the rain stopped, and we sold three units by evening.","t":"A：上週六的開放參觀日到底有多少人來看樣品屋？ B：因為颱風警報，早上只有【少數幾位】訪客到場，但雨停後、午餐過後來了更多家庭，到晚上我們賣出了三戶。"},{"w":"façade","p":"n.","d":"the front wall of a building","c":"建築物正面；外牆","s":"A: The old bank building on the corner looks completely different now, so what exactly did the new owners change? B: They kept the inside almost the same, but they cleaned and repaired the stone façade facing the street, so the front of the building looks bright and elegant again.","t":"A：轉角那棟舊銀行大樓現在看起來完全不一樣，新屋主到底改了什麼？ B：他們內部幾乎沒變，但清洗並修復了面向街道的石造【外牆】，所以建築正面看起來再度明亮又優雅。"},{"w":"blight","p":"n.","d":"something ugly or harmful that spoils a place","c":"損害景觀的事物；禍害","s":"A: Why does the city council want to tear down those empty factories near the train station? B: Residents say the buildings have become a blight on the neighborhood, because they're covered in graffiti, attract rats and make visitors think the whole area is unsafe at night.","t":"A：為什麼市議會想拆掉火車站附近那些空置的工廠？ B：居民說這些建築已成為社區的【禍害】，因為上面滿是塗鴉、會招來老鼠，還讓訪客覺得整個地區晚上不安全。"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"everything you can see when you look across a large area of land","c":"景觀；風景","s":"A: Why did the designers plan the new hotel with only three floors when the land is big enough for a tower? B: The owners wanted the building to fit naturally into the green hills and rice fields, so they kept it low to protect the beautiful landscape that guests come here to enjoy.","t":"A：既然土地大到可以蓋高樓，為什麼設計師把新飯店只規劃成三層樓？ B：業主希望建築能自然地融入綠色山丘和稻田中，所以把樓層壓低，以保護房客來這裡欣賞的美麗【景觀】。"},{"w":"inclination","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that you want to do something","c":"意願；傾向","s":"A: Are you going to apply for the facilities manager position at our new headquarters next year? B: To be honest, I have no inclination to deal with builders and repair problems every day, so I'd rather stay in the finance department, where I can focus on numbers, budgets and long-term planning.","t":"A：你明年會申請我們新總部的設施經理職位嗎？ B：老實說，我沒有每天處理建商和維修問題的【意願】，所以我寧願待在財務部，專心處理數字、預算和長期規劃。"},{"w":"erect","p":"v.","d":"to build or put up a structure","c":"建造；豎立；搭建","s":"A: How long will it take to get the temporary stage ready for the outdoor product launch next weekend? B: The event company says their workers can erect the main structure in just one day, but they'll need another afternoon to set up the lights, speakers and the large video screen.","t":"A：下週末戶外產品發表會的臨時舞台要多久才能準備好？ B：活動公司說他們的工人只要一天就能【搭建】主結構，但還需要再一個下午來架設燈光、喇叭和大型螢幕。"}]},{"unit":38,"theme":"Business 商業","cards":[{"w":"company","p":"n.","d":"a business that makes or sells goods or services","c":"公司","s":"A: I heard you're leaving the bank after eight years, so where are you going to work from next month? B: I'm joining a small software company in Neihu that builds booking apps for hotels, and although the salary is a little lower, the team is friendly and I can work from home on Fridays.","t":"A：聽說你在銀行工作八年後要離職了，下個月你要去哪裡上班？ B：我要加入內湖一家小型軟體【公司】，他們為飯店開發訂房應用程式，雖然薪水低一點，但團隊很友善，而且我週五可以在家工作。"},{"w":"enterprise","p":"n.","d":"a business or company, often one that someone starts and runs","c":"企業；事業","s":"A: Our bank is launching a new loan program next quarter, so which business owners are we hoping to reach with it? B: We want to help people who run a small family enterprise, such as a local bakery or a repair shop, because those owners often struggle to borrow money from large lenders when they need new equipment.","t":"A：我們銀行下一季要推出新的貸款方案，我們希望接觸到哪些業主？ B：我們想幫助經營小型家族【企業】的人，例如當地的麵包店或修理店，因為這些老闆需要新設備時，常常很難向大型貸方借到錢。"},{"w":"firm","p":"n.","d":"a business, especially one that gives professional services like law or accounting","c":"公司；事務所","s":"A: The new office lease looks quite complicated, and I don't understand several of the clauses, so who should we ask to check it before we sign? B: Let's contact the law firm that helped us last year, because their lawyers are careful, they reply quickly, and they already know our business well.","t":"A：新辦公室的租約看起來相當複雜，有好幾條條款我看不懂，簽約前我們應該請誰檢查？ B：我們聯絡去年幫過我們的那家律師【事務所】吧，因為他們的律師很細心、回覆很快，而且已經很了解我們的業務。"},{"w":"corporation","p":"n.","d":"a large company or group of companies that acts as one legal unit","c":"大公司；股份有限公司","s":"A: Why are there so many security guards and reporters in the lobby downstairs this morning? B: A huge international corporation from Japan is signing an agreement with our CEO today, and because the deal is worth millions of dollars, everyone wants photos of the meeting before the official press conference at noon.","t":"A：今天早上樓下大廳為什麼有那麼多警衛和記者？ B：一家來自日本的大型跨國【公司】今天要和我們的執行長簽協議，因為這筆交易價值數百萬美元，大家都想在中午正式記者會前拍到會議的照片。"},{"w":"startup","p":"n.","d":"a new, small company, often in technology, that is just beginning","c":"新創公司","s":"A: You used to work at a big bank downtown, so why did you decide to quit such a stable job last spring? B: Two friends and I opened a small startup that makes a phone app for booking dog walkers, and although we work long hours, it is exciting to build something new from nothing.","t":"A：你以前在市中心的大銀行上班，為什麼去年春天決定辭掉這麼穩定的工作？ B：我和兩個朋友開了一家小型【新創公司】，開發預約遛狗員的手機應用程式，雖然我們工作時間很長，但從無到有打造新東西很令人興奮。"},{"w":"industry","p":"n.","d":"all the businesses that make or sell a particular kind of product or service","c":"產業；工業","s":"A: You have worked in hotels for over ten years, so how has your job changed since the pandemic ended? B: The whole tourism industry has changed a lot, because travelers now book everything online at the last minute, so hotels must use new software and train staff to answer guests quickly through chat apps.","t":"A：你在飯店工作超過十年了，疫情結束後你的工作有什麼改變？ B：整個觀光【產業】改變很多，因為旅客現在都在最後一刻上網預訂一切，所以飯店必須使用新軟體，並訓練員工透過聊天應用程式迅速回覆客人。"},{"w":"commerce","p":"n.","d":"the activity of buying and selling goods, especially on a large scale","c":"商業；貿易","s":"A: Why is our team spending so much time improving the website instead of opening another shop at the mall? B: Online commerce is growing much faster than store shopping, because busy people prefer ordering from their phones at night, so the director believes a better website will bring us more buyers than a new shop.","t":"A：為什麼我們團隊花這麼多時間改善網站，而不是在購物中心再開一家店？ B：線上【商務】的成長比實體店購物快得多，因為忙碌的人喜歡晚上用手機下單，所以主管認為更好的網站會比新店帶來更多買家。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"an area or group of people where a product can be sold","c":"市場","s":"A: Our new energy drink sold very well in Taiwan this year, so what is the next step for the product? B: The board wants to enter the Japanese market next spring, so we are hiring a local research team to learn what young people there like to drink and how much they usually pay.","t":"A：我們的新能量飲料今年在台灣賣得很好，這項產品下一步是什麼？ B：董事會希望明年春天打入日本【市場】，所以我們正在聘請當地的研究團隊，了解那裡的年輕人喜歡喝什麼，以及他們通常願意付多少錢。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"money you earn from business after paying all costs","c":"利潤；盈利","s":"A: The café on the corner always seems full, so is the owner making good money from it? B: Not really, because rent in this area is very high and coffee beans have become more expensive, so after paying staff and bills, she only made a small profit last year and is thinking about moving.","t":"A：轉角那家咖啡店好像總是客滿，老闆賺很多錢嗎？ B：其實沒有，因為這一區的租金很高，咖啡豆也變貴了，所以付完員工薪水和帳單後，她去年只賺到一點【利潤】，正在考慮搬家。"},{"w":"revenue","p":"n.","d":"the total money a business receives from selling goods or services","c":"營收；收入","s":"A: The finance team looked very happy at the meeting this morning, so did the quarterly report bring good news? B: Yes, our total revenue rose by fifteen percent compared to last year, mostly because the new online store attracted many overseas buyers, so the managers are planning to give everyone a bonus.","t":"A：財務團隊今天早上開會時看起來很開心，季報帶來好消息了嗎？ B：是的，我們的總【營收】比去年成長了百分之十五，主要是因為新的網路商店吸引了許多海外買家，所以經理們打算發獎金給大家。"},{"w":"investment","p":"n.","d":"money or time you put into something to get a benefit later","c":"投資","s":"A: Our old printers break down almost every week, so should we just keep repairing them to save money? B: I think buying new machines would be a smart investment, because although they are expensive at first, they will save us repair fees and many hours of waiting, which helps the whole office work faster.","t":"A：我們的舊印表機幾乎每週都故障，我們是不是應該繼續修理來省錢？ B：我認為買新機器會是明智的【投資】，因為雖然一開始很貴，但能省下維修費和許多等待的時間，讓整個辦公室工作更快。"},{"w":"capital","p":"n.","d":"money used to start or grow a business","c":"資本；資金","s":"A: You have wanted to open your own bakery for years, so what is stopping you from doing it now? B: I still don't have enough capital to rent a shop and buy ovens, so I am saving part of my salary every month and also talking to the bank about a small loan.","t":"A：你想開自己的麵包店已經很多年了，現在是什麼阻止你去做？ B：我還沒有足夠的【資金】租店面和買烤箱，所以我每個月存一部分薪水，也正在和銀行洽談一筆小額貸款。"},{"w":"expense","p":"n.","d":"money spent on something, especially for work","c":"費用；開支","s":"A: The hotel in Osaka was quite expensive, so will the company pay for my room during the trade fair? B: Yes, the hotel is a business expense, so just keep every receipt, fill in the online form when you return, and the accounting department will pay the money back into your account within two weeks.","t":"A：大阪那家飯店相當貴，商展期間公司會幫我付房費嗎？ B：會的，住宿屬於出差【費用】，所以只要保留每張收據，回來後填寫線上表單，會計部門會在兩週內把錢退到你的帳戶。"},{"w":"cost","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money needed to buy, make, or do something","c":"成本；費用","s":"A: Why did management decide to move the factory from the city to a small town in the south? B: The main reason is that the cost of land and labor there is much lower, so the company can save money every year and still deliver products to its customers on time.","t":"A：管理階層為什麼決定把工廠從城市搬到南部的小鎮？ B：主要原因是那裡的土地和勞工【成本】低很多，所以公司每年都能省錢，還能準時把產品交給顧客。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"a plan of how much money can be spent on something","c":"預算","s":"A: The marketing team wants to hire a famous singer for our new advertisement, so can we afford it? B: I'm afraid not, because our budget for this campaign is only two million dollars, and that singer usually asks for more than that, so we should look for a less expensive option.","t":"A：行銷團隊想請一位知名歌手拍我們的新廣告，我們負擔得起嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為這次活動的【預算】只有兩百萬元，而那位歌手通常要價更高，所以我們應該找比較便宜的選擇。"},{"w":"management","p":"n.","d":"the people who control a company, or the work of controlling it","c":"管理；管理階層","s":"A: The staff seem much happier this year, so what changed in the office after the new director arrived? B: The management started listening to employees' ideas at monthly meetings and allowed flexible working hours, so people feel more respected, and fewer workers have quit compared to last year.","t":"A：員工今年似乎開心多了，新主管上任後辦公室有什麼改變？ B：【管理階層】開始在每月會議上聽取員工的想法，並允許彈性工時，所以大家覺得更受尊重，離職的員工也比去年少。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a careful plan to reach a goal","c":"策略；戰略","s":"A: Sales of our phones dropped again this quarter, so what is the director planning to do about it? B: She is working on a new strategy that focuses on students, because they buy new phones often, and she wants to offer cheaper models with good cameras and special discounts during the school holidays.","t":"A：我們手機的銷量這一季又下滑了，主管打算怎麼處理？ B：她正在擬定一個以學生為主的新【策略】，因為學生常常換新手機，她想推出相機不錯的平價機型，並在學校假期提供特別折扣。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"the work or activity of a business, or a part of it","c":"營運；業務","s":"A: Why are so many engineers flying to Vietnam next month instead of staying at the main office here? B: Our company is moving part of its manufacturing operation to Hanoi, so the engineers need to set up the machines, train the local workers, and make sure everything runs smoothly before production begins.","t":"A：為什麼下個月有這麼多工程師要飛去越南，而不是留在這裡的總部？ B：我們公司要把部分製造【業務】移到河內，所以工程師需要安裝機器、訓練當地員工，並確保生產開始前一切運作順利。"},{"w":"productivity","p":"n.","d":"how much work a person or company produces in a certain time","c":"生產力","s":"A: Since we started working from home two days a week, have you noticed any change in how much the team gets done? B: Actually, our productivity has gone up, because people spend less time on crowded trains and fewer meetings interrupt them, so they finish reports faster and make fewer mistakes.","t":"A：自從我們開始每週在家工作兩天，你有注意到團隊完成的工作量有什麼變化嗎？ B：其實我們的【生產力】提升了，因為大家花在擁擠火車上的時間變少，被會議打斷的次數也減少，所以他們更快完成報告，錯誤也更少。"},{"w":"efficiency","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something well without wasting time, money, or energy","c":"效率","s":"A: The new delivery software looks complicated, so why did the manager insist that every driver must use it? B: It plans the shortest routes and shows traffic jams in real time, which improves the efficiency of our deliveries, so drivers use less fuel and customers get their packages much sooner.","t":"A：新的配送軟體看起來很複雜，經理為什麼堅持每位司機都要用？ B：它會規劃最短路線並即時顯示塞車狀況，提升我們配送的【效率】，所以司機用油更少，顧客也能更快收到包裹。"},{"w":"competition","p":"n.","d":"the situation when businesses try to be more successful than others","c":"競爭","s":"A: Why did our coffee chain suddenly lower prices and start offering free cookies this month? B: Two new cafés opened on the same street last week, so the competition is much stronger now, and we need to give people a good reason to keep coming to us instead of trying the new places.","t":"A：為什麼我們的連鎖咖啡店這個月突然降價，還開始送免費餅乾？ B：上週同一條街開了兩家新咖啡店，所以現在【競爭】激烈得多，我們需要給大家一個好理由，讓他們繼續光顧我們，而不是去試新的店。"},{"w":"client","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays for a professional service","c":"客戶；委託人","s":"A: You look nervous, and you've checked your slides three times, so what is happening this afternoon? B: I'm meeting an important client from a large hotel group who wants to redesign all their websites, and if she likes my presentation, our agency could win a contract worth over a million dollars.","t":"A：你看起來很緊張，投影片已經檢查三次了，今天下午有什麼事？ B：我要和一家大型飯店集團的重要【客戶】見面，她想重新設計他們所有的網站，如果她喜歡我的簡報，我們公司可能會拿到價值超過一百萬元的合約。"},{"w":"customer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys goods or services from a shop or business","c":"顧客","s":"A: Why is the store manager standing at the counter and talking to that woman for so long? B: A customer bought a coffee machine here last week, but it stopped working after two days, so he is apologizing, checking her receipt, and offering her a new one or a full refund.","t":"A：為什麼店經理站在櫃檯跟那位女士談了那麼久？ B：一位【顧客】上週在這裡買了咖啡機，但兩天後就壞了，所以他正在道歉、核對她的收據，並提供她換一台新的或全額退款。"},{"w":"supplier","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that provides goods to other businesses","c":"供應商","s":"A: Our restaurant ran out of fresh vegetables twice last week, so what went wrong with the deliveries? B: Our usual supplier had problems with his trucks because of the typhoon, so I have already contacted another farm near Taoyuan that can deliver every morning before we open.","t":"A：我們餐廳上週兩次沒有新鮮蔬菜可用，送貨出了什麼問題？ B：我們平常的【供應商】因為颱風，貨車出了問題，所以我已經聯絡桃園附近另一家農場，他們每天早上開店前可以送貨。"},{"w":"contract","p":"n.","d":"a written legal agreement between two or more people or companies","c":"合約；契約","s":"A: The design agency agreed to all our requests on the phone yesterday, so can we start the project on Monday? B: Not yet, because both sides still need to sign the contract, and our lawyer wants to check the payment terms and deadlines carefully before anyone puts their name on it.","t":"A：設計公司昨天在電話中同意了我們所有的要求，我們星期一可以開始這個專案嗎？ B：還不行，因為雙方還需要簽【合約】，而我們的律師想在任何人簽名之前仔細檢查付款條件和截止日期。"},{"w":"negotiation","p":"n.","d":"formal discussion between people who are trying to reach an agreement","c":"協商；談判","s":"A: The supplier asked for a ten percent price increase, so did we finally accept their new offer? B: Not completely, because after three hours of negotiation yesterday, they agreed to raise prices by only five percent if we promise to keep buying from them for two more years.","t":"A：供應商要求漲價百分之十，我們最後接受他們的新報價了嗎？ B：沒有完全接受，因為昨天經過三個小時的【協商】，他們同意只要我們承諾再向他們採購兩年，就只漲價百分之五。"},{"w":"marketing","p":"n.","d":"the work of advertising and promoting products so people buy them","c":"行銷","s":"A: We have a great new product, but hardly anyone has heard of it, so what should we do next? B: We need to spend more on marketing, such as short videos on social media and free samples at train stations, because people will not buy something if they don't even know it exists.","t":"A：我們有很棒的新產品，但幾乎沒人聽過，接下來該怎麼做？ B：我們需要在【行銷】上投入更多，例如社群媒體上的短影片和在火車站發送免費試用品，因為如果大家連它存在都不知道，就不會買。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a name of a product or company that people know","c":"品牌","s":"A: These two pairs of running shoes look almost the same, so why does one cost twice as much as the other? B: The expensive pair is from a famous sports brand that many athletes wear, so people are happy to pay more for the name and the feeling that the quality is better.","t":"A：這兩雙跑鞋看起來幾乎一樣，為什麼其中一雙貴了一倍？ B：比較貴的那雙來自一個許多運動員都穿的知名運動【品牌】，所以大家很樂意為了這個名字，以及品質更好的感覺多付錢。"},{"w":"sales","p":"n.","d":"the number of products sold, or the money received from selling them","c":"銷售額；銷售","s":"A: You stayed at the office very late every night last December, so why was that month so busy for you? B: Our sales always increase sharply before Christmas, because many families buy our toys as gifts, so the whole team had to pack and ship hundreds of extra orders every day.","t":"A：你去年十二月每天晚上都在辦公室待到很晚，為什麼那個月那麼忙？ B：我們的【銷售額】在聖誕節前總是大幅增加，因為許多家庭會買我們的玩具當禮物，所以整個團隊每天都要多包裝和寄送數百筆訂單。"},{"w":"growth","p":"n.","d":"an increase in size, amount, or success","c":"成長；增長","s":"A: Your small online shop only had two workers three years ago, so how many people work there now? B: We have thirty employees today, because the fast growth of our business came from selling healthy snacks during the pandemic, and many of those customers still order from us every month.","t":"A：你的小網店三年前只有兩名員工，現在有多少人在那裡工作？ B：我們現在有三十名員工，我們生意的快速【成長】來自疫情期間販售健康零食，而且許多顧客至今每個月仍向我們訂購。"},{"w":"expansion","p":"n.","d":"the act of becoming larger, such as opening new branches","c":"擴張；擴展","s":"A: Why is the company hiring so many new staff and looking at office buildings in Kaohsiung? B: The board approved an expansion into southern Taiwan, so we are opening a second office there next year, and they need people who know the local customers and can speak Taiwanese with them.","t":"A：公司為什麼要招聘這麼多新員工，還在高雄看辦公大樓？ B：董事會批准了向南台灣【擴展】的計畫，所以我們明年要在那裡開設第二個辦公室，他們需要了解當地顧客、能用台語和他們溝通的人。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something bad, like losing money, may happen","c":"風險","s":"A: My brother wants to put all his savings into his friend's new restaurant, so do you think that's a good idea? B: It's a big risk, because many new restaurants close within the first year, so he should only invest money he can afford to lose and ask to see a clear business plan first.","t":"A：我哥哥想把所有積蓄投入他朋友的新餐廳，你覺得這是好主意嗎？ B：這是很大的【風險】，因為許多新餐廳在第一年內就倒閉，所以他應該只投資輸得起的錢，並先要求看清楚的營運計畫。"},{"w":"sustainability","p":"n.","d":"using resources in a way that does not harm the environment in the future","c":"永續性；永續發展","s":"A: Why did our company stop using plastic bags and start buying electricity from solar farms this year? B: The new CEO cares a lot about sustainability, and many young customers now choose brands that protect the environment, so going green helps the planet and also improves our image.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司今年停止使用塑膠袋，並開始向太陽能電廠購電？ B：新任執行長非常重視【永續發展】，而且許多年輕顧客現在會選擇保護環境的品牌，所以走向環保既能幫助地球，也能提升我們的形象。"}]},{"unit":39,"theme":"Busy 忙碌","cards":[{"w":"occupied","p":"adj.","d":"busy doing something, or being used by someone","c":"忙碌的；（座位、房間）有人使用的","s":"A: I wanted to ask the director about the new budget plan this morning, but is she available to talk for a few minutes before lunch? B: I'm afraid she will be occupied with job interviews until two o'clock, so you should send her an email now and she can reply after the last candidate leaves.","t":"A：我今天早上想問主任有關新預算計畫的事，她午餐前有空談幾分鐘嗎？ B：恐怕她到兩點前都會【忙著】面試應徵者，所以你現在應該寄電子郵件給她，等最後一位應徵者離開後她就可以回覆你。"},{"w":"overworked","p":"adj.","d":"having too much work to do","c":"工作過度的；過勞的","s":"A: Why did three people from the customer service team quit last month, even though the company had just raised everyone's salary in January? B: Most of them felt overworked because they had to answer hundreds of calls every day without enough breaks, and the manager never hired anyone new to help them.","t":"A：為什麼客服團隊上個月有三個人離職，即使公司一月才剛幫大家加薪？ B：他們大多覺得【工作過度】，因為每天必須接數百通電話又沒有足夠的休息時間，而經理也從沒僱用新人來幫忙。"},{"w":"swamped","p":"adj.","d":"having so much work that you can hardly deal with it","c":"忙得不可開交的；應接不暇的","s":"A: Could you help me check these sales figures before the meeting with our partners from Tokyo tomorrow morning? B: I'd love to, but I'm completely swamped with customer orders since the holiday promotion started, so maybe you could ask Kevin in the finance department, who usually has more free time on Thursdays.","t":"A：你可以幫我在明天早上和東京合作夥伴開會前檢查這些銷售數字嗎？ B：我很樂意，但自從假期促銷開始後，我就完全被顧客訂單【淹沒】了，所以也許你可以問財務部的凱文，他星期四通常比較有空。"},{"w":"loaded","p":"adj.","d":"carrying or having a large amount of something","c":"裝滿的；堆滿的","s":"A: Are you sure you can take on the hotel booking for the sales conference as well as the monthly report? B: To be honest, my desk is already loaded with files from the new clients, but if you give me until Friday afternoon, I can finish the report first and then book the rooms.","t":"A：你確定你能在處理月報之外，也負責業務研討會的飯店訂房嗎？ B：老實說，我的桌上已經【堆滿】了新客戶的檔案，但如果你給我到星期五下午的時間，我可以先完成報告再訂房間。"},{"w":"stretched","p":"adj.","d":"having hardly enough time, money or people for what is needed","c":"（人力、資源）吃緊的","s":"A: Can our design team start working on the new website for the restaurant chain next week, as the client requested? B: I'm not sure, because the team is already stretched with two other big projects, and two designers are on vacation, so we might need to ask the client for an extra month.","t":"A：我們的設計團隊可以照客戶要求，下週開始製作連鎖餐廳的新網站嗎？ B：我不確定，因為團隊已經因為另外兩個大案子而【人手吃緊】，而且有兩位設計師在休假，所以我們可能需要請客戶多給一個月。"},{"w":"hectic","p":"adj.","d":"very busy and full of activity","c":"忙亂的；繁忙的","s":"A: How was your first week at the airport information desk, now that the summer travel season has begun? B: It was really hectic, because thousands of passengers kept asking about delayed flights and lost bags, but my supervisor was very kind and showed me how to stay calm and handle each problem one by one.","t":"A：既然夏季旅遊旺季已經開始，你在機場服務台的第一週過得如何？ B：真的很【忙亂】，因為成千上萬的旅客一直詢問延誤的航班和遺失的行李，但我的主管人很好，教我如何保持冷靜，一一處理每個問題。"},{"w":"frantic","p":"adj.","d":"done in a hurried and worried way, without control","c":"慌亂的；瘋狂的","s":"A: Why was everyone in the marketing office running around and shouting this morning before the product launch? B: They were in a frantic search for the USB drive with the presentation slides, because the CEO was arriving in twenty minutes and nobody could remember where the intern had put it last night.","t":"A：今天早上產品發表前，行銷辦公室的每個人為什麼都跑來跑去還大聲喊叫？ B：他們在【慌亂地】尋找存有簡報投影片的隨身碟，因為執行長二十分鐘後就要到了，卻沒人記得實習生昨晚把它放在哪裡。"},{"w":"rushed","p":"adj.","d":"done too quickly, or having to hurry","c":"匆忙的；倉促的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the business lunch with the new suppliers from Vietnam at the hotel yesterday? B: Not really, because it felt very rushed, since we only had forty minutes before their train left, so we had to eat quickly and couldn't discuss the delivery prices in much detail.","t":"A：你昨天在飯店和越南新供應商的商務午餐吃得愉快嗎？ B：不太愉快，感覺很【匆忙】，因為他們的火車開之前我們只有四十分鐘，所以我們得吃很快，也沒辦法詳細討論運費價格。"},{"w":"pressed","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough of something, especially time","c":"（時間、金錢）緊迫的；不足的","s":"A: Would you like to join us for a coffee and a quick chat about the training program in the lobby café? B: I'm a little pressed for time today, because I have to prepare a sales presentation for an important client by four o'clock, but I'd be happy to meet you tomorrow morning instead.","t":"A：你要不要和我們一起去大廳的咖啡廳喝杯咖啡，簡短聊一下培訓課程？ B：我今天時間有點【緊迫】，因為我得在四點前為一位重要客戶準備銷售簡報，但我很樂意改成明天早上和你碰面。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, energy or skill","c":"費力的；要求高的","s":"A: Why did Linda decide to leave her well-paid position at the international bank after only one year? B: She said the job was too demanding, since she often worked late into the night and traveled abroad twice a month, so she hardly saw her family and felt tired all the time.","t":"A：為什麼琳達在國際銀行待了才一年就決定離開她高薪的職位？ B：她說那份工作太【吃力】了，因為她常常工作到深夜，而且每個月出國兩次，所以她幾乎見不到家人，總是覺得很累。"},{"w":"time-consuming","p":"adj.","d":"taking a lot of time","c":"耗時的；費時的","s":"A: Should we check every customer survey by hand, or is there a faster way to find the most common complaints? B: Reading them one by one would be very time-consuming, because we received more than five thousand forms last month, so I suggest we use the new software that sorts the comments automatically.","t":"A：我們應該人工檢查每份顧客問卷，還是有更快的方法找出最常見的抱怨？ B：一份一份看會非常【耗時】，因為我們上個月收到超過五千份表格，所以我建議用那套能自動分類意見的新軟體。"},{"w":"engaged","p":"adj.","d":"busy; (of a phone line) being used","c":"忙碌的；（電話）佔線的","s":"A: I've been trying to call the shipping company all morning to ask about our missing boxes, but why can't I get through? B: Their line is probably engaged because many customers are calling after the storm delayed deliveries, so why don't you send them a message through their website instead?","t":"A：我整個早上一直打電話給貨運公司詢問我們遺失的箱子，但為什麼都打不通？ B：他們的電話大概【佔線中】，因為暴風雨延誤了送貨，很多顧客都在打電話，所以你何不改成透過他們的網站傳訊息？"},{"w":"active","p":"adj.","d":"busy doing many things; full of energy","c":"活躍的；積極的","s":"A: Your grandfather is almost eighty, so does he still spend most of his time at home since he retired from the factory? B: Not at all, he's still very active, because he volunteers at the local library three mornings a week, plays tennis on weekends, and even takes an English class at the community center.","t":"A：你祖父快八十歲了，他從工廠退休後是不是大部分時間都待在家裡？ B：完全不是，他還是非常【活躍】，因為他每週有三個早上在當地圖書館當志工，週末打網球，甚至還在社區中心上英文課。"},{"w":"on the go","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very busy and moving around all the time","c":"忙個不停的","s":"A: How does your sister manage to run her own bakery and take care of three young children at the same time? B: She's always on the go from six in the morning until late at night, but she says she enjoys it, and her husband helps with the kids after he finishes work at the hospital.","t":"A：你姊姊是怎麼同時經營自己的麵包店又照顧三個小孩的？ B：她從早上六點到深夜總是【忙個不停】，但她說她很享受，而且她先生在醫院下班後也會幫忙照顧孩子。"},{"w":"full","p":"adj.","d":"having no free space or time left","c":"滿的；排滿的","s":"A: Can I book an appointment with Dr. Chen this Friday afternoon to talk about the results of my health check? B: I'm sorry, but her calendar is completely full on Friday because of the medical conference, so the earliest time I can offer you is next Monday at ten o'clock in the morning.","t":"A：我可以預約陳醫師這個星期五下午，談一下我的健康檢查結果嗎？ B：很抱歉，因為醫學研討會，她星期五的行事曆完全【排滿】了，所以我能提供給您最早的時間是下星期一早上十點。"},{"w":"packed","p":"adj.","d":"very crowded; full of people or things","c":"擠滿的；塞滿的","s":"A: Do you think we can find seats on the train to Kaohsiung if we arrive at the station around five o'clock on Friday? B: I doubt it, because the trains are always packed with office workers going home for the long weekend, so we should buy our tickets online tonight to be safe.","t":"A：如果我們星期五五點左右到車站，你覺得我們找得到往高雄火車的座位嗎？ B：我很懷疑，因為火車上總是【擠滿】了要回家過連假的上班族，所以為了保險起見，我們今晚應該在網路上買票。"},{"w":"jam-packed","p":"adj.","d":"extremely full or crowded","c":"擠得水洩不通的；塞得滿滿的","s":"A: What did you think of the trade fair in Taipei, and did your company get many new business contacts? B: The exhibition hall was jam-packed with visitors from all over Asia, so it was hard to move around, but we collected more than two hundred business cards and received several large orders.","t":"A：你覺得台北的商展怎麼樣，你們公司有得到很多新的商業人脈嗎？ B：展覽館裡【擠得水洩不通】，都是來自亞洲各地的訪客，所以很難走動，但我們收集了兩百多張名片，還接到好幾筆大訂單。"},{"w":"tight","p":"adj.","d":"with very little free time or money","c":"緊湊的；拮据的","s":"A: Is it possible to add a visit to the new factory during the clients' trip to Taichung next week? B: The program is already very tight, since they have meetings from nine to six both days and fly back on Wednesday night, but I'll ask whether they'd like to skip the city tour instead.","t":"A：下週客戶到台中的行程中，有可能加入參觀新工廠嗎？ B：行程已經非常【緊湊】，因為他們兩天都從九點開會到六點，而且星期三晚上就要飛回去，但我會問他們是否願意改為取消市區觀光。"},{"w":"burdened","p":"adj.","d":"having a heavy load of work, duties or problems","c":"負擔沉重的","s":"A: Why does the new accountant look so stressed during our team meetings these days? B: She feels burdened with too many responsibilities, because she has to handle the annual tax report, train two interns, and cover for a colleague who is on maternity leave until the end of next month.","t":"A：為什麼新來的會計師最近在我們的團隊會議上看起來壓力那麼大？ B：她覺得被太多責任【壓得喘不過氣】，因為她必須處理年度稅務報告、訓練兩位實習生，還要代理一位休產假到下個月底的同事。"},{"w":"workload","p":"n.","d":"the amount of work a person has to do","c":"工作量","s":"A: Since two people left the accounting team last month, how are the rest of you dealing with all the extra work? B: Our workload has nearly doubled, so we've asked the manager to hire a temporary assistant, and in the meantime we've agreed to share the urgent jobs and work one extra hour each evening.","t":"A：自從會計團隊上個月有兩個人離職後，你們其他人怎麼應付那些額外的工作？ B：我們的【工作量】幾乎加倍了，所以我們已經請經理僱用一位臨時助理，同時我們也同意分擔緊急的工作，每天晚上多工作一小時。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists when things will happen","c":"時間表；行程表","s":"A: Have you planned the visit for the Japanese buyers who are coming to see our showroom on Tuesday? B: Yes, I've prepared a detailed schedule for their visit, starting with a factory tour at nine, followed by a product demonstration and lunch, and I'll email a copy to everyone on the sales team this afternoon.","t":"A：你安排好星期二要來參觀我們展示間的日本買家的行程了嗎？ B：是的，我已經為他們的參訪準備了一份詳細的【行程表】，九點從工廠參觀開始，接著是產品示範和午餐，我今天下午會把副本寄給業務團隊的每個人。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the latest time by which something must be done","c":"截止期限","s":"A: When does the marketing department need the final version of the brochure for the new hotel? B: The deadline is next Monday at noon, because the printing company needs three days to print five thousand copies before the grand opening, so we must not make any more changes after this weekend.","t":"A：行銷部什麼時候需要新飯店宣傳手冊的最終版本？ B：【截止期限】是下星期一中午，因為印刷公司需要三天在盛大開幕前印好五千份，所以這個週末之後我們不能再做任何修改了。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"something you have promised to do, which takes your time","c":"承諾；應盡的責任","s":"A: Would you like to lead the planning team for the company's twentieth anniversary party in December? B: I'd love to help, but I have a family commitment on weekends, since I travel to Tainan to take care of my elderly parents, so I wouldn't be able to attend the planning meetings held on Saturday mornings.","t":"A：你願意帶領十二月公司二十週年派對的籌備小組嗎？ B：我很樂意幫忙，但我週末有家庭【責任】，因為我要去台南照顧年邁的父母，所以我沒辦法參加星期六早上舉行的籌備會議。"},{"w":"task","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work that must be done","c":"任務；工作","s":"A: What should I do first on my first day as a receptionist at the hotel, since everything here seems so new to me? B: Your first task is to learn how to use the booking system, and after lunch Sarah will show you how to welcome guests, check their passports, and give them their room keys.","t":"A：我第一天在飯店當櫃檯人員應該先做什麼呢？這裡的一切對我來說都好新。 B：你的第一項【任務】是學會使用訂房系統，午餐後莎拉會教你如何接待客人、檢查他們的護照，並把房間鑰匙交給他們。"},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work or job that someone is given to do","c":"（分派的）任務；派任工作","s":"A: Why is Mark flying to Jakarta next month when he only joined the engineering department in March? B: The company gave him a six-month assignment at our new factory there, because he speaks Indonesian and can help the local staff learn how to use the machines we bought from Germany.","t":"A：馬克三月才加入工程部，為什麼下個月就要飛去雅加達？ B：公司給了他一項在那裡新工廠為期六個月的【派任工作】，因為他會說印尼語，可以幫助當地員工學會使用我們從德國買來的機器。"},{"w":"multitask","p":"v.","d":"to do several things at the same time","c":"同時處理多項工作","s":"A: What kind of skills are you looking for in the new office assistant you plan to hire next month? B: We need someone who can multitask well, because the assistant will answer phone calls, greet visitors, and update the sales records at the same time, especially during our busy morning hours.","t":"A：你們下個月打算僱用的新辦公室助理，需要具備什麼樣的技能？ B：我們需要一個很能【同時處理多項工作】的人，因為助理要同時接電話、招呼訪客和更新銷售紀錄，特別是在早上忙碌的時段。"},{"w":"juggle","p":"v.","d":"to try to deal with several jobs or duties at the same time","c":"兼顧；同時應付","s":"A: How do you manage to study for your MBA while working full-time at the advertising agency in the city center? B: It's hard to juggle work and school, but I study on the train every morning, attend classes online on weekends, and my manager kindly lets me leave early on exam days.","t":"A：你怎麼能在市中心的廣告公司全職工作的同時，又讀企管碩士？ B：要【兼顧】工作和學業很難，但我每天早上在火車上讀書，週末上線上課程，而且考試那天我的經理會好心讓我提早下班。"},{"w":"rush","p":"v.","d":"to move or do something very quickly","c":"趕；匆忙行事","s":"A: The meeting with the bank doesn't start until three o'clock, so should we leave the office right now? B: There's no need to rush, because the bank is only a ten-minute walk from here, so let's finish checking the loan documents carefully first and then leave at around half past two.","t":"A：和銀行的會議三點才開始，所以我們應該現在就離開辦公室嗎？ B：不需要【趕】，因為銀行從這裡走路只要十分鐘，所以我們先把貸款文件仔細檢查完，大約兩點半再出發。"},{"w":"prioritise","p":"v.","d":"to decide which things are most important and do them first","c":"排定優先順序","s":"A: I have to finish the sales report, answer twenty customer emails, and prepare for tomorrow's training session, so where should I start? B: You need to prioritise your work, so start with the sales report, because the director needs it by noon, and then reply to the customers who have complained about late deliveries.","t":"A：我得完成銷售報告、回覆二十封顧客郵件，還要準備明天的訓練課程，我應該從哪裡開始？ B：你需要把工作【排定優先順序】，所以先從銷售報告開始，因為主任中午前要，然後再回覆那些抱怨送貨延遲的顧客。"},{"w":"crammed","p":"adj.","d":"too full of people, things or activities","c":"塞滿的；擠滿的","s":"A: Why didn't you enjoy the guided tour of Europe that your company gave you as a reward for being the top salesperson? B: The tour was crammed with too many activities, so we visited six cities in seven days and spent most of our time on the bus instead of relaxing and enjoying the local food.","t":"A：公司為了獎勵你成為頂尖業務員而送你的歐洲導覽旅遊，你為什麼玩得不開心？ B：那趟旅遊【塞滿】了太多活動，所以我們七天去了六個城市，大部分時間都在巴士上，而不是放鬆享受當地美食。"},{"w":"nonstop","p":"adj.","d":"continuing without stopping or resting","c":"不停的；直達的","s":"A: You look really tired today, so did you have a difficult day at the call center? B: Yes, it was nonstop work from the moment I arrived, because our internet service went down across the whole city, and hundreds of angry customers called, so I couldn't eat lunch until three o'clock.","t":"A：你今天看起來真的很累，你在客服中心度過了辛苦的一天嗎？ B：是的，從我一到就是【不停歇的】工作，因為我們的網路服務在全市都斷線了，數百位生氣的顧客打電話來，所以我到三點才能吃午餐。"},{"w":"overloaded","p":"adj.","d":"given too much work or too much to carry or handle","c":"超載的；負擔過重的","s":"A: Why did the company's online shopping website crash during the big sale last Friday night? B: The system was overloaded with too many visitors at the same time, because over two hundred thousand people tried to buy the discounted phones in the first ten minutes, so the technical team is now upgrading the servers.","t":"A：上週五晚上大特賣時，為什麼公司的網路購物網站當機了？ B：系統因為同時有太多訪客而【超載】，因為前十分鐘就有超過二十萬人想搶購打折手機，所以技術團隊現在正在升級伺服器。"},{"w":"snowed under","p":"adj.phr.","d":"having so much work that you cannot deal with it all","c":"忙得不可開交的","s":"A: Can you come to the farewell dinner for Mr. Lin at the Italian restaurant on Thursday evening? B: I'd really like to, but I'm snowed under with end-of-year reports right now, so I might have to stay in the office until nine, though I'll try to join you for dessert if I can.","t":"A：你星期四晚上能來義大利餐廳參加林先生的歡送晚宴嗎？ B：我真的很想去，但我現在被年終報告弄得【忙得不可開交】，所以我可能得在辦公室待到九點，不過如果可以的話，我會盡量趕去和你們一起吃甜點。"},{"w":"flat out","p":"adj.phr.","d":"working as hard or as fast as possible","c":"全力以赴的；忙到極點的","s":"A: Has the factory been able to produce enough air conditioners for all the stores during this extremely hot summer? B: The workers have been flat out for weeks, running the machines day and night, but the demand is still higher than we expected, so we're planning to open a second production line in August.","t":"A：在這個極度炎熱的夏天，工廠有辦法為所有門市生產足夠的冷氣機嗎？ B：工人們好幾週來一直【全力以赴】，機器日夜運轉，但需求還是比我們預期的高，所以我們打算八月開設第二條生產線。"}]},{"unit":40,"theme":"Buy 購買","cards":[{"w":"purchase","p":"v.","d":"to buy something, especially for a business","c":"購買；採購","s":"A: Our team needs six new laptops before the training program starts next month, so who should I talk to about getting them quickly? B: You should email Mr. Chen in the finance office, because every department must get his approval before it can purchase any equipment that is worth more than five thousand dollars.","t":"A：我們團隊在下個月培訓計畫開始前需要六台新筆電，我該找誰才能快點拿到？ B：你應該寄電子郵件給財務室的陳先生，因為每個部門在【購買】任何價值超過五千元的設備之前，都必須先得到他的核准。"},{"w":"pay","p":"v.","d":"to give money for something you buy or a service","c":"付款；支付","s":"A: The hotel front desk just told me that the conference room charge was not included in our package, so what should I do now? B: Don't worry, just pay with the company credit card, keep the receipt, and send it to accounting when we get back to the office on Monday.","t":"A：飯店櫃台剛剛告訴我，會議室的費用不包含在我們的套裝方案裡，我現在該怎麼辦？ B：別擔心，就用公司信用卡【付款】，把收據留著，等我們星期一回辦公室再交給會計部。"},{"w":"price","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you must pay to buy something","c":"價格","s":"A: I found a printer online that has all the features we need, but the shop near our office sells the same model, so which one should we choose? B: Let's check the price at both places first, because the website also charges a shipping fee, and the local shop might give us free setup.","t":"A：我在網路上找到一台功能完全符合我們需求的印表機，但辦公室附近的店也賣同一款，我們該選哪一個？ B：我們先查一下兩邊的【價格】吧，因為網站還要收運費，而附近的店可能會免費幫我們安裝。"},{"w":"cost","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money needed to buy, do, or make something","c":"費用；成本","s":"A: The manager wants to send all twenty sales staff to the trade fair in Tokyo next spring, but is there enough money in our travel budget? B: I'm not sure yet, because the total cost of flights, hotels, and meals for that many people could be much higher than what we spent on last year's event.","t":"A：經理想在明年春天派全部二十位業務人員去東京參加商展，但我們的差旅預算夠嗎？ B：我還不確定，因為那麼多人的機票、飯店和餐費的總【費用】，可能會比我們去年活動花的錢高出許多。"},{"w":"afford","p":"v.","d":"to have enough money to pay for something","c":"負擔得起","s":"A: The new office building downtown looks amazing, and it is very close to the subway station, so why didn't the company decide to move there? B: The rent is almost twice what we pay now, and with sales falling this year, we simply cannot afford such a large expense until business improves again.","t":"A：市中心那棟新辦公大樓看起來很棒，而且離捷運站很近，公司為什麼沒決定搬過去？ B：那裡的租金幾乎是我們現在的兩倍，而且今年業績下滑，在生意好轉之前我們根本【負擔不起】這麼大的開銷。"},{"w":"spend","p":"v.","d":"to use money to buy or pay for things","c":"花費（金錢）","s":"A: Our department received an extra two thousand dollars at the end of the year, and the director said we must use it by December, right? B: Yes, so I suggest we spend most of it on comfortable new chairs for the meeting room, since everyone has been complaining that the old ones hurt their backs.","t":"A：我們部門年底多拿到兩千元，主任說我們必須在十二月前用掉，對吧？ B：對，所以我建議我們把大部分的錢【花】在會議室的舒適新椅子上，因為大家一直抱怨舊椅子坐得背痛。"},{"w":"sale","p":"n.","d":"a time when a shop sells things at lower prices than usual","c":"特價；拍賣","s":"A: Are you going to the department store after work tonight, because I heard many people are lining up outside even though it's a Tuesday? B: Yes, they are having a huge end-of-season sale this week, and winter coats are fifty percent off, so I want to buy one before the popular sizes are gone.","t":"A：你今晚下班後要去百貨公司嗎？我聽說雖然今天才星期二，外面就已經大排長龍了。 B：對，他們這週在辦換季大【拍賣】，冬季外套打五折，所以我想在熱門尺寸賣完之前買一件。"},{"w":"discount","p":"n.","d":"an amount taken off the usual price","c":"折扣","s":"A: We want to order two hundred company T-shirts for the charity run next month, but the price on the website seems quite high for our small budget. B: Call the supplier directly and explain that it's a large order, because they usually give a ten percent discount to businesses that buy more than one hundred items.","t":"A：我們想為下個月的慈善路跑訂兩百件公司T恤，但網站上的價格對我們的小預算來說似乎太高了。 B：直接打電話給供應商，說明這是大量訂單，因為他們通常會給購買超過一百件的公司九折的【折扣】。"},{"w":"bargain","p":"n.","d":"something bought for much less than its usual price","c":"便宜貨；划算的東西","s":"A: I can't believe you bought that leather briefcase for only fifty dollars, because it looks exactly like the ones they sell in the luxury shops downtown. B: I know, it was a real bargain, since the shop was closing down and selling everything at very low prices, so I went there during my lunch break and got it.","t":"A：真不敢相信你只花五十元就買到那個皮革公事包，它看起來跟市中心精品店賣的一模一樣。 B：我知道，真的很【划算】，因為那家店要結束營業，所有東西都超低價出清，所以我趁午休去把它買下來了。"},{"w":"cheap","p":"adj.","d":"costing little money","c":"便宜的","s":"A: Should we book the hotel next to the convention center for the sales team, or look for somewhere farther away to save money? B: The hotels near the center are full and expensive, but there's a clean, cheap guesthouse two stops away by train, so we could save a lot and still arrive on time.","t":"A：我們該幫業務團隊訂會展中心旁邊的飯店，還是找遠一點的地方來省錢？ B：中心附近的飯店都客滿又貴，但搭火車兩站外有一間乾淨又【便宜】的民宿，所以我們可以省很多錢，而且還是能準時抵達。"},{"w":"expensive","p":"adj.","d":"costing a lot of money","c":"昂貴的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team decide to cancel the TV commercial they were planning for the new energy drink launch in the spring? B: Advertising on television turned out to be far too expensive for a small company like ours, so we are going to promote the drink on social media and at local events instead.","t":"A：行銷團隊為什麼決定取消原本為春季新能量飲料上市規劃的電視廣告？ B：在電視上打廣告對我們這樣的小公司來說實在太【昂貴】了，所以我們改在社群媒體和地方活動上宣傳這款飲料。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how useful or important something is compared with its price","c":"價值；划算程度","s":"A: Do you think it's worth paying more for the premium coffee machine for our office kitchen, or should we just buy the basic model? B: The premium one is pricier at first, but it lasts much longer and uses less costly coffee pods, so I think it offers better value for money over the next few years.","t":"A：你覺得辦公室茶水間值得多花錢買高級咖啡機嗎？還是我們就買基本款就好？ B：高級款一開始比較貴，但它耐用得多，而且用的咖啡膠囊比較便宜，所以我認為接下來幾年它更【物超所值】。"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper that shows you have paid for something","c":"收據","s":"A: I took two clients out for dinner last night after we signed the contract, so can the company pay me back for the meal? B: Yes, but you'll need to attach the original receipt to your expense form and submit it to the accounting department before Friday, or they won't be able to process your claim this month.","t":"A：我昨晚簽完合約後請兩位客戶吃晚餐，公司可以幫我報帳嗎？ B：可以，但你需要把【收據】正本附在費用申請單上，並在星期五前交給會計部，否則他們這個月就無法處理你的申請。"},{"w":"refund","p":"n.","d":"money that is given back to you when you return something","c":"退款","s":"A: The projector we bought last week stopped working after only two presentations, and the technician says it can't be repaired easily. B: Take it back to the electronics shop with the box and paperwork, and ask for a full refund, because their policy says shoppers can return faulty items within thirty days of buying them.","t":"A：我們上週買的投影機只用了兩次簡報就壞了，技術人員說不容易修好。 B：把它連同盒子和文件一起拿回電器行，要求全額【退款】，因為他們的規定是顧客在購買後三十天內可以退回有瑕疵的商品。"},{"w":"checkout","p":"n.","d":"the place or final step where you pay for what you buy","c":"結帳（處）","s":"A: I've been trying to buy the plane tickets for our business trip, but the website keeps showing an error message, and I don't know why. B: That often happens at the checkout page when your session times out, so log in again, add the tickets to your basket, and finish the payment within ten minutes this time.","t":"A：我一直想買我們出差的機票，但網站一直跳出錯誤訊息，我不知道為什麼。 B：當你的登入逾時，【結帳】頁面常常會這樣，所以重新登入，把機票加進購物籃，這次要在十分鐘內完成付款。"},{"w":"cart","p":"n.","d":"a list of items you plan to buy on a website; a shopping trolley","c":"購物車","s":"A: I'm ordering office supplies on the website right now, and I've already chosen paper, pens, and ink, but is there anything else we need? B: Please add two boxes of staples and some sticky notes to the shopping cart before you pay, because we're almost out and the next supply run won't be until next month.","t":"A：我現在正在網站上訂辦公用品，已經選了紙、筆和墨水，我們還需要什麼嗎？ B：付款前請把兩盒訂書針和一些便利貼加進【購物車】，因為快用完了，而下一次補貨要等到下個月。"},{"w":"customer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys things from a shop or business","c":"顧客","s":"A: Why does the manager want all the shop assistants to attend a training session on Saturday morning, when that's usually our busiest time? B: She received several complaints last month, so she wants us to learn how to stay polite and patient when a customer is angry about a late delivery or a damaged product.","t":"A：經理為什麼要所有店員星期六早上參加培訓？那通常是我們最忙的時候。 B：她上個月收到好幾件客訴，所以她希望我們學會當【顧客】因為送貨延誤或商品損壞而生氣時，如何保持禮貌和耐心。"},{"w":"seller","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that sells something","c":"賣家；賣方","s":"A: I want to buy a used van for our flower business, and I found one online that looks good, but how can I be sure it's safe? B: Arrange to meet the seller in person, ask to see the service records, and bring a mechanic friend to check the engine before you agree to pay any money.","t":"A：我想為我們的花店買一台二手廂型車，在網路上找到一台看起來不錯，但我怎麼確定它安全？ B：約【賣家】當面見面，要求看保養紀錄，並帶一位當技師的朋友檢查引擎，然後再同意付錢。"},{"w":"order","p":"v.","d":"to ask for goods to be made, supplied, or delivered","c":"訂購；點（餐）","s":"A: We're expecting forty guests at the product launch on Friday evening, so how much food should we get from the catering company? B: Let's order enough sandwiches and drinks for fifty people, just in case some guests bring colleagues, because running out of food at an important event would make our company look bad.","t":"A：星期五晚上的產品發表會預計有四十位來賓，我們該向外燴公司訂多少食物？ B：我們就【訂】夠五十人份的三明治和飲料吧，以防有些來賓帶同事來，因為在重要活動上食物不夠會讓公司很沒面子。"},{"w":"delivery","p":"n.","d":"the act of bringing goods to a place","c":"送貨；運送","s":"A: The new furniture for the reception area was supposed to arrive this morning, but nothing has come yet, and the visitors arrive tomorrow. B: I just called the supplier, and they said the delivery was delayed because of heavy traffic on the highway, but the truck should reach our building before four o'clock this afternoon.","t":"A：接待區的新家具本來應該今天早上送到，但到現在什麼都還沒來，而訪客明天就到了。 B：我剛打給供應商，他們說因為高速公路塞車，【送貨】延誤了，但卡車應該會在今天下午四點前抵達我們大樓。"},{"w":"online","p":"adj.","d":"using the internet","c":"線上的；網路的","s":"A: Our small bakery has been getting fewer customers since the new supermarket opened across the street, so what do you think we should do? B: We could open an online shop on our website, so people can order cakes and bread from home and pick them up, or even have them delivered to their door.","t":"A：自從對面新超市開幕後，我們的小麵包店客人越來越少，你覺得我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們可以在網站上開一家【網路】商店，讓大家在家就能訂蛋糕和麵包，再來店取貨，甚至直接送到家門口。"},{"w":"store","p":"n.","d":"a shop, especially a large one","c":"商店","s":"A: Excuse me, I'm visiting from Taipei for a business meeting and forgot my phone charger, so where can I buy a new one near this hotel? B: There's a large electronics store just around the corner, next to the bank, and it stays open until ten o'clock at night, so you still have plenty of time.","t":"A：不好意思，我從台北來這裡開商務會議，忘了帶手機充電器，這間飯店附近哪裡可以買到新的？ B：轉角就有一家大型電器【商店】，就在銀行旁邊，營業到晚上十點，所以你還有很多時間。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"an area or group of people where products can be sold","c":"市場","s":"A: Our company wants to start selling its tea products overseas next year, but which country do you think we should try first? B: Japan could be a good market for us, because many young people there enjoy Taiwanese bubble tea, and our research shows that demand for healthy drinks is growing quickly in big cities.","t":"A：我們公司明年想開始在海外銷售茶類產品，你覺得我們應該先試哪個國家？ B：日本可能是很好的【市場】，因為那裡很多年輕人喜歡台灣珍珠奶茶，而且我們的研究顯示大城市對健康飲品的需求成長很快。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a type of product made by a particular company with its own name","c":"品牌","s":"A: Why are you buying this printer paper when there's a cheaper one on the shelf right next to it that looks almost the same? B: I prefer this brand because the paper never jams in our office machines, and I'd rather pay a little more than waste time fixing the printer every week.","t":"A：架上旁邊就有一款更便宜、看起來幾乎一樣的影印紙，你為什麼還要買這款？ B：我比較喜歡這個【品牌】，因為它的紙從來不會卡在我們辦公室的機器裡，我寧願多付一點錢，也不想每週浪費時間修印表機。"},{"w":"quality","p":"n.","d":"how good or bad something is","c":"品質","s":"A: The supplier from overseas offered us shirts at half the price of our current factory, so why didn't the manager accept the deal? B: She ordered some samples first, and the quality was very poor, because the stitching came apart after one wash, and our customers would definitely complain about that.","t":"A：海外供應商開給我們的襯衫價格只有現在工廠的一半，經理為什麼不接受這筆交易？ B：她先訂了一些樣品，結果【品質】非常差，洗一次縫線就裂開了，我們的顧客一定會抱怨。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at two or more things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"A: I need to choose a new mobile phone plan for the whole sales team, but there are so many companies offering different deals. B: Make a simple chart and compare the monthly fees, data limits, and contract lengths of the three biggest providers, and then show it to the manager so she can decide by Friday.","t":"A：我需要為整個業務團隊選一個新的手機方案，但有好多公司提供不同的優惠。 B：做一張簡單的表格，【比較】三大電信業者的月租費、數據上限和合約長度，然後拿給經理看，讓她在星期五前做決定。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you have to spend on something","c":"預算","s":"A: The design team wants to hire a famous photographer for the new catalog, but do we have enough money for that this quarter? B: Unfortunately, our marketing budget was cut by twenty percent this year, so we will probably need to use our own staff photographer and save the extra money for internet advertising.","t":"A：設計團隊想為新型錄請一位知名攝影師，但我們這一季有足夠的錢嗎？ B：很遺憾，我們今年的行銷【預算】被砍了百分之二十，所以我們可能得用自己公司的攝影師，把多出來的錢留給網路廣告。"},{"w":"installment","p":"n.","d":"one of several payments made over a period of time","c":"分期付款（的一期）","s":"A: The new accounting software costs twelve thousand dollars, and that's a lot of money for a small company like ours to pay all at once. B: The software company allows small businesses to pay the first installment of one thousand dollars this month, and then pay the same amount every month for the rest of the year.","t":"A：新的會計軟體要一萬兩千元，對我們這樣的小公司來說，一次付清是一大筆錢。 B：軟體公司允許小企業這個月先付第一期一千元的【分期款】，然後在今年剩下的每個月都付同樣的金額。"},{"w":"warranty","p":"n.","d":"a written promise that a company will repair or replace a product if it breaks","c":"保固；保證書","s":"A: My office laptop suddenly stopped charging this morning, and I have an important presentation to finish by tomorrow afternoon, so what can I do? B: Check the paperwork in the IT office, because I think that laptop is still under a two-year warranty, which means the manufacturer will repair or replace it for free.","t":"A：我的辦公室筆電今天早上突然無法充電，而我有一份重要的簡報要在明天下午前完成，我該怎麼辦？ B：去資訊室查一下文件，因為我記得那台筆電還在兩年【保固】期內，這表示製造商會免費維修或更換。"}]},{"unit":41,"theme":"Cafe 咖啡館","cards":[{"w":"coffeehouse","p":"n.","d":"a café where people drink coffee and meet","c":"咖啡館","s":"A: Our team needs a relaxed place to meet the new designer from Osaka on Friday morning, so do you have any suggestions near the office? B: There is a charming old coffeehouse on Maple Street that opened in the 1950s, and it has large wooden tables where we can spread out the drawings and talk for hours.","t":"A：週五早上我們團隊需要一個輕鬆的地方和來自大阪的新設計師見面，你在辦公室附近有什麼建議嗎？ B：楓樹街上有一家1950年代開業的迷人老【咖啡館】，裡面有大木桌，我們可以把圖稿攤開，聊上好幾個小時。"},{"w":"barista","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is making coffee drinks in a café","c":"咖啡師","s":"A: The coffee at the new branch tastes much better than it did last month, so did the owner change suppliers or buy a new machine? B: Actually, she hired an experienced barista who won a national competition last year, and he has been training the other staff to prepare every drink more carefully.","t":"A：新分店的咖啡比上個月好喝多了，老闆是換了供應商還是買了新機器？ B：其實她聘請了一位去年贏得全國比賽的資深【咖啡師】，他一直在訓練其他員工更用心地準備每一杯飲料。"},{"w":"espresso","p":"n.","d":"a small cup of very strong black coffee","c":"濃縮咖啡","s":"A: You have to finish the quarterly report before the board meeting at nine tomorrow, so are you going to stay late at the office tonight? B: Yes, I probably will, so I'm going downstairs to get a double espresso first, because I need something strong to keep me awake while I check all the figures.","t":"A：你必須在明天九點董事會前完成季報，所以你今晚要在辦公室待到很晚嗎？ B：是的，大概會，所以我要先下樓買一杯雙份【濃縮咖啡】，因為我需要喝點濃的東西，讓我在核對所有數字時保持清醒。"},{"w":"latte","p":"n.","d":"a coffee drink made with espresso and a lot of hot milk","c":"拿鐵咖啡","s":"A: I'm going to the café across the street to pick up drinks for the visitors from the head office, so what would you like? B: Please get me a large latte with oat milk, because normal milk upsets my stomach, and I'd like something warm and creamy on a cold, rainy afternoon like this.","t":"A：我要去對街的咖啡店幫總公司來的訪客買飲料，你想喝什麼？ B：請幫我買一杯加燕麥奶的大杯【拿鐵】，因為一般牛奶會讓我胃不舒服，而且在這樣寒冷下雨的下午，我想喝點溫暖又綿密的東西。"},{"w":"cappuccino","p":"n.","d":"a coffee drink made with espresso, hot milk and milk foam","c":"卡布奇諾","s":"A: The client from Milan will arrive at the office around ten, so what should we prepare for her while she waits for the director? B: Let's offer her a fresh cappuccino with a little chocolate powder on top, since her assistant told me she drinks one every morning and doesn't like tea or juice at all.","t":"A：米蘭來的客戶大約十點會到辦公室，她等主任的時候我們該為她準備什麼？ B：我們給她一杯上面撒點巧克力粉的新鮮【卡布奇諾】吧，因為她的助理告訴我她每天早上都喝一杯，而且完全不喜歡茶或果汁。"},{"w":"menu","p":"n.","d":"a list of the food and drinks you can order and their prices","c":"菜單","s":"A: Sales at our café have dropped since the new bakery opened next door, so what do you think we should change first? B: I think we should update the menu with more healthy options like salads and fruit bowls, because many office workers nearby told us they want lighter lunches that don't cost too much.","t":"A：自從隔壁新麵包店開幕後，我們咖啡店的業績就下滑了，你認為我們應該先改變什麼？ B：我認為我們應該更新【菜單】，加入更多像沙拉和水果碗之類的健康選擇，因為附近很多上班族告訴我們，他們想要清淡又不會太貴的午餐。"},{"w":"counter","p":"n.","d":"a long table in a shop or café where customers order and pay","c":"櫃台","s":"A: I've been waiting for my sandwich for almost twenty minutes, and my lunch break ends soon, so should I ask a waiter about it? B: Here they don't bring food to the tables, so you need to pick it up at the counter near the entrance when the staff calls your number on the screen.","t":"A：我的三明治已經等了將近二十分鐘，我的午休快結束了，我應該問服務生嗎？ B：這裡不會把餐點送到桌上，所以當員工在螢幕上叫你的號碼時，你需要到入口附近的【櫃台】取餐。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the feeling or mood that a place gives you","c":"氣氛","s":"A: Why do you always hold your team meetings at that little café on the corner instead of in the conference room upstairs? B: The atmosphere there is relaxed and friendly, with soft lights and comfortable chairs, so my staff feel free to share new ideas without worrying about what the managers might think.","t":"A：你為什麼總是在轉角那間小咖啡店開團隊會議，而不是在樓上的會議室？ B：那裡的【氣氛】輕鬆友善，有柔和的燈光和舒服的椅子，所以我的員工可以自由地分享新點子，不用擔心主管會怎麼想。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable and pleasant, like a small home","c":"溫馨舒適的","s":"A: We need a place to interview the two job candidates on Thursday afternoon, but the meeting rooms are all booked, so where should we go? B: There's a small, cozy café behind the train station with soft sofas and a fireplace, so the candidates will feel comfortable and probably speak more naturally about their experience.","t":"A：週四下午我們需要找個地方面試兩位應徵者，但會議室都被預訂了，我們該去哪裡？ B：火車站後面有一間小而【溫馨舒適】的咖啡館，有柔軟的沙發和壁爐，所以應徵者會覺得自在，可能會更自然地談論他們的經驗。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong, pleasant smell, especially of food or coffee","c":"香氣","s":"A: Why did the café owner decide to roast the coffee beans by the front window every morning instead of in the back kitchen? B: She noticed that the rich aroma of fresh coffee spreads into the street, and it attracts many people on their way to work, so her morning sales have nearly doubled.","t":"A：咖啡店老闆為什麼決定每天早上在前窗邊烘咖啡豆，而不是在後面的廚房？ B：她發現新鮮咖啡濃郁的【香氣】會飄到街上，吸引許多上班途中的人，所以她早上的營業額幾乎翻倍了。"},{"w":"brew","p":"v.","d":"to make a hot drink such as coffee or tea","c":"沖泡；釀造","s":"A: The coffee machine in the staff kitchen broke again this morning, so what are we going to do for the clients' meeting at eleven? B: Don't worry, I brought a French press from home, so I can brew a large pot of coffee for everyone in about ten minutes before they arrive.","t":"A：員工廚房的咖啡機今天早上又壞了，那十一點的客戶會議我們要怎麼辦？ B：別擔心，我從家裡帶了一個法式濾壓壺，所以我可以在他們到之前，用大約十分鐘為大家【沖泡】一大壺咖啡。"},{"w":"pastry","p":"n.","d":"a small sweet baked food made with butter and flour","c":"酥皮點心；糕點","s":"A: The training session tomorrow starts at eight, and most of the new staff will come straight from the train station, so should we provide breakfast? B: Yes, let's order coffee and a fresh pastry for each person from the bakery downstairs, because people learn better when they aren't hungry or tired.","t":"A：明天的訓練課程八點開始，大部分新員工會直接從火車站過來，我們應該提供早餐嗎？ B：好，我們從樓下的麵包店幫每個人訂咖啡和一份新鮮的【糕點】吧，因為人不餓也不累的時候學習效果比較好。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food you eat at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: The dinner with our Japanese partners went very well, but should we order anything else before we ask for the bill? B: Let's ask the waiter to bring a dessert for everyone, like the chocolate cake or the mango pudding, because sharing something sweet is a nice way to end a successful evening together.","t":"A：和日本夥伴的晚餐很順利，但我們在結帳前還要點些什麼嗎？ B：我們請服務生為大家送上一份【甜點】吧，像是巧克力蛋糕或芒果布丁，因為一起分享甜食是結束一個成功夜晚的好方式。"},{"w":"takeaway","p":"n.","d":"food or a drink that you buy in a shop and take away to eat or drink","c":"外帶餐點","s":"A: I have a conference call with the London office in fifteen minutes, so do you think I have enough time to eat lunch at the café downstairs? B: Probably not, so you should get a takeaway instead and eat it at your desk, because the café is always very busy and slow at this time of day.","t":"A：我十五分鐘後要和倫敦辦公室開電話會議，你覺得我有足夠時間在樓下咖啡店吃午餐嗎？ B：大概沒有，所以你應該改買【外帶餐點】在座位上吃，因為這個時段咖啡店總是很忙，出餐很慢。"},{"w":"dine","p":"v.","d":"to eat a meal, especially dinner, often at a restaurant","c":"用餐","s":"A: The visitors from our Singapore branch arrive on Friday evening, so where would be a good place to take them after the factory tour? B: I think we should dine at the Italian restaurant by the river, because it has a quiet private room and the chef can prepare vegetarian dishes for the manager.","t":"A：新加坡分公司的訪客週五晚上抵達，參觀工廠之後帶他們去哪裡好？ B：我想我們應該在河邊那家義大利餐廳【用餐】，因為它有安靜的包廂，而且主廚可以為經理準備素食料理。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drinks to people","c":"供應；上（菜）","s":"A: We expect over a hundred guests at the product launch on Saturday, so how many staff will the café need to send to help us? B: They will send six people, and they will serve coffee, tea and sandwiches in the lobby from two o'clock until the presentations finish around five.","t":"A：週六的產品發表會預計會有超過一百位賓客，咖啡店需要派多少員工來幫忙？ B：他們會派六個人，從兩點到大約五點簡報結束，他們會在大廳【供應】咖啡、茶和三明治。"},{"w":"seat","p":"n.","d":"a place where you can sit, such as a chair","c":"座位","s":"A: The café near the station is always crowded at lunchtime, so how can we make sure we have somewhere to sit with the client on Monday? B: I'll call them this afternoon and ask them to save a seat for each of us by the window, because they let regular customers book tables before noon.","t":"A：車站附近那家咖啡店午餐時間總是很擁擠，我們要怎麼確定週一和客戶有地方坐？ B：我今天下午會打電話給他們，請他們在窗邊為我們每人保留一個【座位】，因為他們讓常客在中午前訂位。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of too many people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: Why did you leave the café so quickly this morning when you had planned to finish your sales report there before work? B: It was too crowded because a tour group had just arrived, and there were people everywhere, so I couldn't find a table or think clearly about my numbers.","t":"A：你原本計畫上班前在咖啡店完成業務報告，為什麼今天早上那麼快就離開了？ B：因為有個旅行團剛到，裡面太【擁擠】了，到處都是人，所以我找不到桌子，也沒辦法好好思考我的數字。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making very little noise; peaceful","c":"安靜的","s":"A: I need to prepare for an important phone interview with a bank this afternoon, but the office is noisy because of the renovation, so where should I go? B: You could use the small room upstairs, because it's usually quiet after lunch and nobody will disturb you while you practice your answers.","t":"A：我今天下午要準備一場銀行的重要電話面試，但辦公室因為裝修很吵，我該去哪裡？ B：你可以用樓上的小房間，因為午餐後那裡通常很【安靜】，你練習回答時不會有人打擾。"},{"w":"wifi","p":"n.","d":"a way of connecting to the internet without wires","c":"無線網路","s":"A: I'm planning to work from the café near my apartment tomorrow because the office air conditioning is being repaired, but will I be able to join the video meeting? B: Yes, they offer free wifi for customers, and the connection is fast enough for video calls, though you should ask the staff for the password first.","t":"A：明天因為辦公室冷氣在維修，我打算在我公寓附近的咖啡店工作，但我能參加視訊會議嗎？ B：可以，他們為顧客提供免費【無線網路】，連線速度足以進行視訊通話，不過你應該先向店員要密碼。"},{"w":"regular","p":"n.","d":"a customer who often goes to the same shop, café or restaurant","c":"常客","s":"A: The waiter at the corner café knew exactly what you wanted before you even said anything this morning, so how does he know you so well? B: I've been a regular there for almost three years, because I stop by every morning on my way to the office and always order the same thing.","t":"A：今天早上轉角咖啡店的服務生在你開口前就知道你要什麼，他怎麼會那麼了解你？ B：我在那裡當【常客】快三年了，因為我每天早上上班途中都會順道過去，而且總是點一樣的東西。"},{"w":"refreshment","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of food or drink that makes you feel less tired or thirsty","c":"茶點；提神飲食","s":"A: The workshop for the new sales team will last about four hours on Wednesday, so do you think the attendees will need a break in the middle? B: Yes, and the café downstairs can deliver juice, tea and cookies at three, which will be a welcome refreshment for everyone after hours of training.","t":"A：週三新業務團隊的研習大約會持續四個小時，你覺得參加者中間需要休息嗎？ B：需要，樓下的咖啡店可以在三點送果汁、茶和餅乾來，對受訓好幾個小時的大家來說會是很受歡迎的【茶點】。"},{"w":"specialty","p":"n.","d":"a food or product that a place is famous for or does very well","c":"招牌菜；特色商品","s":"A: We are taking the visitors from Korea to the café on the top floor of the shopping mall, so is there anything we must try there? B: Their specialty is a honey cake made with fruit from local farms, and it has won several awards, so the visitors will probably enjoy it with their coffee.","t":"A：我們要帶韓國訪客去購物中心頂樓的咖啡店，那裡有什麼我們一定要嚐嚐的嗎？ B：他們的【招牌】是用當地農場水果做的蜂蜜蛋糕，得過好幾個獎，所以訪客們大概會很喜歡配著咖啡吃。"},{"w":"order","p":"v.","d":"to ask for food, drinks or goods that you want to buy","c":"點（餐）；訂購","s":"A: The meeting with the investors might go past lunchtime, and nobody wants to leave the room while we're discussing the contract, so what should we do? B: I'll order sandwiches and salads from the café across the street at half past eleven, and they can deliver everything to the conference room by noon.","t":"A：和投資人的會議可能會超過午餐時間，而且討論合約時沒人想離開會議室，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我會在十一點半向對街的咖啡店【訂購】三明治和沙拉，他們可以在中午前把所有東西送到會議室。"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper that shows you have paid for something","c":"收據","s":"A: I bought coffee and cakes for the whole team after the client meeting, so how can I get the money back from the company? B: Just give the receipt to Linda in the accounting department before Friday, and she will add the amount to your salary at the end of the month.","t":"A：客戶會議之後我替整個團隊買了咖啡和蛋糕，我要怎麼向公司拿回這筆錢？ B：只要在週五前把【收據】交給會計部的琳達，她會在月底把金額加到你的薪水裡。"},{"w":"tip","p":"n.","d":"extra money you give to a waiter or driver to thank them","c":"小費","s":"A: The service at the restaurant last night was excellent, and the waiter even helped our guests call a taxi, so how much extra should we pay? B: In this country people usually leave a tip of about fifteen percent of the bill, but since he was so helpful, I think twenty percent would be fair.","t":"A：昨晚餐廳的服務非常好，服務生甚至幫我們的客人叫計程車，我們應該多付多少錢？ B：在這個國家，人們通常會留下帳單約百分之十五的【小費】，不過既然他那麼熱心幫忙，我想百分之二十比較合理。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"sounds such as songs that people play or sing","c":"音樂","s":"A: Some customers have complained that it's hard to have a conversation in our café during the afternoon, so do you know what the problem is? B: I think the background music is too loud, especially the rock songs the new staff like to play, so we should choose softer jazz and turn the volume down.","t":"A：有些顧客抱怨下午在我們咖啡店很難交談，你知道問題出在哪裡嗎？ B：我覺得背景【音樂】太大聲了，尤其是新員工喜歡放的搖滾歌曲，所以我們應該選擇比較柔和的爵士樂，並把音量調低。"},{"w":"interior","p":"n.","d":"the inside part of a building or room and its design","c":"內部；室內裝潢","s":"A: The new café on Park Road has become very popular on social media in just a few weeks, so what makes it so special? B: The interior was designed by a famous architect, with green plants, wooden walls and large windows, so customers love taking photos and sharing them online with their friends.","t":"A：公園路上那家新咖啡店短短幾週就在社群媒體上大受歡迎，它有什麼特別之處？ B：它的【室內裝潢】是由一位知名建築師設計的，有綠色植物、木頭牆面和大窗戶，所以顧客很喜歡拍照並上網分享給朋友。"},{"w":"local","p":"adj.","d":"from or in the area near you","c":"在地的；當地的","s":"A: Our company wants to choose a coffee supplier for the new office kitchen, so should we use the big international brand we had before? B: I'd prefer a local roaster from our own neighborhood, because the beans are fresher, the prices are similar, and we can support small businesses in our community.","t":"A：公司想為新辦公室的茶水間挑選咖啡供應商，我們應該用之前那個國際大品牌嗎？ B：我比較想選我們附近社區的【在地】烘豆商，因為咖啡豆比較新鮮、價格差不多，而且我們還能支持社區裡的小型企業。"}]},{"unit":42,"theme":"Cake 蛋糕","cards":[{"w":"slice","p":"n.","d":"a thin flat piece cut from something like cake or bread","c":"一片；一塊","s":"A: The client meeting starts at three, and Mr. Lee asked for some light refreshments, so how much of the lemon cake should I bring to the conference room? B: Please cut it so that each of the twelve visitors can have one small slice, and put the rest in the staff kitchen for our team to enjoy later.","t":"A：客戶會議三點開始，李先生要求準備一些簡單的茶點，所以我該帶多少檸檬蛋糕到會議室？ B：請把它切好，讓十二位訪客每人都能拿到一小【片】，剩下的放到員工廚房，讓我們團隊晚點享用。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤","s":"A: Our café has received an order for fifty cupcakes for a company party on Saturday morning, so do you think we can finish them in time? B: If we start early on Friday afternoon and bake them in two batches, they will be ready, cooled, and packed before the delivery driver arrives.","t":"A：我們咖啡館接到一筆訂單，要為週六早上的公司派對準備五十個杯子蛋糕，你覺得我們來得及完成嗎？ B：如果我們週五下午早點開始，分兩批【烘烤】，它們就能在送貨司機抵達前烤好、放涼並包裝完成。"},{"w":"oven","p":"n.","d":"a box-shaped machine that heats food so you can bake or cook it","c":"烤箱","s":"A: The cakes in the bakery came out burned on one side again this morning, and two customers complained, so what do you think is causing the problem? B: I believe the old oven is not heating evenly anymore, so I have already asked the manager to call a technician and get a quote for a new one.","t":"A：今天早上麵包店的蛋糕又有一邊烤焦了，還有兩位客人抱怨，你覺得是什麼原因造成的？ B：我認為那台舊【烤箱】已經無法均勻加熱了，所以我已經請經理打電話找技師來，並請他們報價換一台新的。"},{"w":"flour","p":"n.","d":"a white powder made from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","c":"麵粉","s":"A: The supplier just called to say that our delivery of baking ingredients will be two days late because of the storm, so can we still make the wedding cake? B: We only have half a bag of flour left in the storeroom, so I will buy a few more kilograms from the supermarket on my way back from lunch.","t":"A：供應商剛打電話來說，因為暴風雨，我們的烘焙材料要晚兩天才會送到，那我們還能做婚禮蛋糕嗎？ B：儲藏室裡只剩下半袋【麵粉】了，所以我午餐回來的路上會去超市再多買幾公斤。"},{"w":"sugar","p":"n.","d":"a sweet white or brown substance added to food and drinks","c":"糖","s":"A: Several of our older customers have asked whether we could offer healthier desserts, so do you have any ideas for changing our popular carrot cake? B: We could use less sugar and add more fresh fruit and nuts instead, which would keep the flavor pleasant while making the cake better for people who watch their diet.","t":"A：好幾位年長的顧客問我們能不能提供更健康的甜點，你對改良我們那款熱賣的胡蘿蔔蛋糕有什麼想法嗎？ B：我們可以少放一點【糖】，改加更多新鮮水果和堅果，這樣既能保持好吃的味道，也讓蛋糕更適合注重飲食的人。"},{"w":"butter","p":"n.","d":"a soft yellow food made from milk, used in cooking and baking","c":"奶油；牛油","s":"A: The head baker said the new pound cakes taste a little dry and plain compared with last month's, so did something change in the kitchen? B: Yes, the purchasing department switched to a cheaper brand of butter to save money, but I think we should go back to the old one because quality matters more to our customers.","t":"A：首席烘焙師說新的磅蛋糕吃起來比上個月的稍微乾又平淡，廚房裡有什麼改變嗎？ B：是的，採購部門為了省錢改用比較便宜的【奶油】品牌，但我認為我們應該換回原來的，因為品質對顧客來說更重要。"},{"w":"egg","p":"n.","d":"a round object laid by a hen, used as food and in baking","c":"蛋；雞蛋","s":"A: I am preparing the shopping list for tomorrow's baking class at the community center, so how many ingredients will each of the twenty students need? B: Every student needs one fresh egg, two cups of flour, and a small bowl of milk, so please buy a few extra in case someone drops something on the floor.","t":"A：我正在為明天社區中心的烘焙課準備購物清單，二十位學員每人需要多少材料？ B：每位學員需要一顆新鮮的【蛋】、兩杯麵粉和一小碗牛奶，所以請多買一些，以防有人把東西掉到地上。"},{"w":"icing","p":"n.","d":"a sweet mixture of sugar and water or butter used to cover or decorate cakes","c":"糖霜","s":"A: The marketing team wants the company logo to appear on top of the anniversary cake for Friday's event, so is that something your bakery can do? B: Certainly, our designer can draw the logo in blue and white icing on a smooth surface, but we need the image file by Wednesday so that we have time to practice.","t":"A：行銷團隊希望週五活動的週年蛋糕上能有公司標誌，你們麵包店做得到嗎？ B：當然可以，我們的設計師可以在平滑的表面上用藍白兩色的【糖霜】畫出標誌，不過我們需要在週三前拿到圖檔，才有時間練習。"},{"w":"frosting","p":"n.","d":"a thick, soft, sweet mixture spread on cakes and cupcakes","c":"（蛋糕上的）糖霜；奶油霜","s":"A: The children's hospital asked us to provide cupcakes for their holiday party next week, so what kind of decoration do you think the kids would like? B: I suggest a thick layer of pink and green frosting with colorful sprinkles on top, because it looks cheerful and is easy for young children to eat with their hands.","t":"A：兒童醫院請我們為下週的節日派對提供杯子蛋糕，你覺得孩子們會喜歡什麼樣的裝飾？ B：我建議塗上一層厚厚的粉紅色和綠色【糖霜】，上面撒上彩色糖粒，因為看起來很歡樂，而且小孩用手拿著吃也很方便。"},{"w":"cream","p":"n.","d":"the thick fatty part of milk, often whipped and put on desserts","c":"鮮奶油","s":"A: The strawberry cakes we sent to the hotel yesterday were not as fresh as usual, and the event planner was quite unhappy, so what went wrong? B: The delivery van's cooling system broke down during the trip, so the whipped cream melted in the heat, and we have offered the hotel a full refund and a free replacement.","t":"A：我們昨天送到飯店的草莓蛋糕不像平常那麼新鮮，活動策劃人相當不滿，到底出了什麼問題？ B：送貨車的冷藏系統在途中故障了，所以打發的【鮮奶油】在高溫下融化了，我們已經向飯店提出全額退款並免費補送。"},{"w":"chocolate","p":"n.","d":"a sweet brown food made from cocoa beans","c":"巧克力","s":"A: We are choosing a cake for the sales department's farewell party for Ms. Chen, so do you know what flavor she likes best? B: Her assistant told me that she loves dark chocolate more than anything else, so let's order a rich, bitter cake with fresh berries from the bakery near the train station.","t":"A：我們正在為業務部替陳小姐舉辦的歡送會挑選蛋糕，你知道她最喜歡什麼口味嗎？ B：她的助理告訴我，她最愛黑【巧克力】，所以我們就向火車站附近的麵包店訂一個濃郁微苦、配上新鮮莓果的蛋糕吧。"},{"w":"vanilla","p":"n.","d":"a sweet flavor that comes from the seeds of a tropical plant","c":"香草","s":"A: A customer is planning a small office party for forty people and cannot decide which flavor will please everyone, so what should I recommend to her? B: Tell her that classic vanilla is the safest choice because almost everyone enjoys it, and she can add fresh fruit on top if she wants something more colorful.","t":"A：一位顧客正在籌劃一場四十人的小型辦公室派對，無法決定哪種口味能讓大家都滿意，我該推薦她什麼？ B：告訴她經典的【香草】口味是最保險的選擇，因為幾乎每個人都喜歡，如果她想要更繽紛一點，也可以在上面加些新鮮水果。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: The restaurant manager wants to attract more business lunch customers on weekdays, so do you have any suggestions for the new set menu? B: We could include a small dessert, such as a piece of cheesecake or a fruit tart, with every main course, because office workers love having something sweet after a busy morning.","t":"A：餐廳經理想在平日吸引更多商務午餐客人，你對新的套餐菜單有什麼建議嗎？ B：我們可以在每份主餐附上一份小【甜點】，例如一塊起司蛋糕或水果塔，因為上班族在忙碌的早上之後很喜歡吃點甜的。"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"a set of instructions for cooking a dish, with a list of ingredients","c":"食譜","s":"A: Our new pastry chef from Paris will start next Monday, so should we ask her to follow the instructions we have always used for our famous apple cake? B: Yes, please give her a printed copy of the recipe on her first day, because customers expect the taste to stay exactly the same as it has been for years.","t":"A：我們從巴黎來的新甜點師下週一開始上班，我們要請她照著我們一直以來做招牌蘋果蛋糕的做法嗎？ B：是的，請在她上班第一天給她一份印好的【食譜】，因為顧客期待味道和多年來完全一樣。"},{"w":"layer","p":"n.","d":"one level of something that lies on top of another","c":"層","s":"A: The bride and groom want a tall, impressive wedding cake for their reception at the hotel, so how big do you think it should be for two hundred guests? B: I recommend four round levels stacked on top of each other, and each layer can have a different flavor so that guests with different tastes will all find something they enjoy.","t":"A：新郎新娘想在飯店喜宴上擺一個高大氣派的結婚蛋糕，你覺得兩百位賓客需要多大的蛋糕？ B：我建議堆疊四層圓形蛋糕，每一【層】可以有不同口味，這樣口味不同的賓客都能找到喜歡的。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to add things to something to make it look more attractive","c":"裝飾","s":"A: The office manager wants to surprise the team with a cake for reaching our sales target this quarter, so could your shop add something special to it? B: Of course, our staff can decorate it with fresh flowers, gold letters, and small sugar stars, and we can deliver it to your building before the afternoon meeting starts.","t":"A：辦公室經理想用蛋糕給達成本季業績目標的團隊一個驚喜，你們店能在上面加點特別的東西嗎？ B：當然可以，我們的員工可以用鮮花、金色字母和小糖星星來【裝飾】它，還能在下午會議開始前送到你們大樓。"},{"w":"topping","p":"n.","d":"food put on top of a dish, such as fruit, nuts or sauce","c":"（食物上的）配料","s":"A: Our café is creating a new cheesecake for the summer menu, and the owner wants it to look bright and fresh in photos, so what do you suggest? B: We could add a topping of mango, kiwi, and blueberries, because the colorful fruit will look great on social media and taste refreshing on hot days.","t":"A：我們咖啡館正在為夏季菜單研發新的起司蛋糕，老闆希望它拍照時看起來明亮清新，你有什麼建議？ B：我們可以加上芒果、奇異果和藍莓的【配料】，因為色彩繽紛的水果在社群媒體上看起來很棒，而且在炎熱的日子吃起來也很清爽。"},{"w":"candle","p":"n.","d":"a stick of wax with a string in the middle that you burn for light","c":"蠟燭","s":"A: Everything is ready for Mr. Wang's retirement party in the meeting room, but the lights are still on, so when should we bring in the cake? B: Turn off the lights first, and then I will carry it in slowly with one tall candle burning in the middle while everyone starts to sing and clap.","t":"A：王先生退休派對在會議室都準備好了，但燈還亮著，我們應該什麼時候把蛋糕拿進來？ B：先把燈關掉，然後我會端著中間點著一根高【蠟燭】的蛋糕慢慢走進來，同時大家開始唱歌拍手。"},{"w":"birthday","p":"n.","d":"the day each year when a person was born","c":"生日","s":"A: I noticed that Ms. Park from the accounting department has been working late every night this month, so is there anything special happening next week? B: Yes, her birthday is next Thursday, so the team is planning to order a small cake and have a short party in the break room during lunch.","t":"A：我注意到會計部的朴小姐這個月每晚都加班，下週有什麼特別的事嗎？ B：有啊，下週四是她的【生日】，所以團隊打算訂一個小蛋糕，午餐時間在休息室辦個簡短的派對。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"tasting of sugar or honey","c":"甜的","s":"A: Some guests at yesterday's conference said the chocolate cake was delicious, but a few others left most of it on their plates, so did they say why? B: They felt it was too sweet for them after a heavy lunch, so next time we should choose a lighter dessert with less sugar and more fruit.","t":"A：昨天研討會上有些來賓說巧克力蛋糕很好吃，但也有幾位把大部分都剩在盤子裡，他們有說為什麼嗎？ B：他們覺得吃完豐盛的午餐後，那個蛋糕對他們來說太【甜】了，所以下次我們應該選擇少糖、多水果的清爽甜點。"},{"w":"moist","p":"adj.","d":"slightly wet in a pleasant way; not dry","c":"濕潤的","s":"A: Our online reviews have improved a lot since we hired the new baker in March, so what do customers say they like most about our cakes now? B: Many people write that the cakes are soft and moist inside, not dry like before, because she adds yogurt to the batter and never leaves them in the oven too long.","t":"A：自從三月聘請新烘焙師之後，我們的網路評價改善很多，顧客現在說他們最喜歡我們蛋糕的哪一點？ B：很多人寫說蛋糕裡面鬆軟又【濕潤】，不像以前那樣乾，因為她在麵糊裡加了優格，而且從不讓蛋糕在烤箱裡烤太久。"},{"w":"fluffy","p":"adj.","d":"soft and light, with a lot of air inside","c":"蓬鬆的","s":"A: The Japanese cheesecake we sell is one of our best products, and a reporter wants to know what makes it so popular, so what should I tell her? B: Tell her that the cake is light and fluffy, almost like a cloud, because our bakers beat the egg whites carefully by hand for more than ten minutes.","t":"A：我們賣的日式起司蛋糕是最暢銷的產品之一，有位記者想知道它為什麼這麼受歡迎，我該怎麼告訴她？ B：告訴她這款蛋糕輕盈又【蓬鬆】，幾乎像雲朵一樣，因為我們的烘焙師會用手仔細打發蛋白超過十分鐘。"},{"w":"rich","p":"adj.","d":"(of food) containing a lot of butter, cream, sugar or chocolate, with a strong taste","c":"（食物）濃郁的","s":"A: The hotel's head chef wants a dessert for the formal dinner that will impress the company directors, so which cake do you recommend? B: I recommend our dark chocolate cake because it has a deep, rich flavor, and a small piece is enough to satisfy guests after a large meal of several courses.","t":"A：飯店主廚想為正式晚宴準備一道能讓公司董事們印象深刻的甜點，你推薦哪款蛋糕？ B：我推薦我們的黑巧克力蛋糕，因為它的味道深沉又【濃郁】，在吃完好幾道菜的豐盛晚餐後，一小塊就足以讓客人滿足。"},{"w":"sponge","p":"n.","d":"a light, soft cake made with eggs, sugar and flour","c":"海綿蛋糕","s":"A: A customer would like a simple, light cake for her grandmother, who does not enjoy heavy cream or chocolate, so what can we offer her? B: We can make a plain sponge with a little lemon juice and powdered sugar on top, which is soft, easy to eat, and not too heavy for older people.","t":"A：一位顧客想為不喜歡厚重鮮奶油或巧克力的奶奶買一個簡單清爽的蛋糕，我們可以提供什麼？ B：我們可以做一個原味【海綿蛋糕】，上面淋一點檸檬汁、撒上糖粉，口感柔軟、容易入口，對長輩來說也不會太膩。"},{"w":"fill","p":"v.","d":"to put something inside until it is full","c":"填滿；填入","s":"A: The new cream puffs on our menu look beautiful, but some customers said the inside was almost empty, so how can we fix this problem quickly? B: From now on, the kitchen staff should fill each one completely with custard before it goes on display, and a supervisor will check a few every morning.","t":"A：菜單上新推出的泡芙看起來很漂亮，但有些顧客說裡面幾乎是空的，我們要怎麼迅速解決這個問題？ B：從現在起，廚房員工應該在陳列前把每一個都用卡士達醬完全【填滿】，而且主管每天早上會抽查幾個。"},{"w":"mix","p":"v.","d":"to combine two or more things so they become one","c":"混合；攪拌","s":"A: This is my first week working in the bakery, and I want to make sure I do everything correctly, so what is the most important step for making the muffins? B: You should mix the dry ingredients and the wet ingredients gently for only about one minute, because if you stir too much, the muffins will become hard and heavy.","t":"A：這是我在麵包店工作的第一週，我想確保每件事都做對，做馬芬最重要的步驟是什麼？ B：你應該把乾性材料和濕性材料輕輕【混合】大約一分鐘就好，因為攪拌太久的話，馬芬會變得又硬又紮實。"},{"w":"batter","p":"n.","d":"a liquid mixture of flour, eggs and milk used to make cakes","c":"麵糊","s":"A: The cakes from this morning did not rise properly in the oven, and they look flat and heavy, so do you know what might have happened? B: I think the new assistant forgot to add baking powder when he prepared the batter, so I will show him the correct steps again before the lunch rush begins.","t":"A：今天早上的蛋糕在烤箱裡沒有好好膨脹，看起來又扁又紮實，你知道可能發生了什麼事嗎？ B：我想新來的助手在準備【麵糊】時忘了加泡打粉，所以我會在午餐尖峰時段開始前再教他一次正確步驟。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drinks to people at a meal","c":"供應；端上（食物）","s":"A: The guests at the awards dinner have almost finished their main course, and the speeches will begin in twenty minutes, so when should the waiters bring out the cake? B: Please ask them to serve it right after the last speech, together with coffee and tea, so that people can relax and chat while they eat.","t":"A：頒獎晚宴的來賓主餐快吃完了，致詞將在二十分鐘後開始，服務生應該什麼時候把蛋糕端出來？ B：請他們在最後一位致詞結束後馬上【端上】蛋糕，搭配咖啡和茶，讓大家可以邊吃邊放鬆聊天。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a special event or party held because something good has happened","c":"慶祝；慶祝活動","s":"A: Our company has just won the biggest contract in its history, and the CEO wants to thank everyone who worked so hard on it, so what is the plan? B: She is organizing a big celebration in the hotel ballroom next Friday evening, with a buffet dinner, live music, and a huge cake with the client's logo on it.","t":"A：我們公司剛贏得史上最大的合約，執行長想感謝所有為此努力的人，有什麼計畫？ B：她下週五晚上要在飯店宴會廳舉辦一場盛大的【慶祝活動】，有自助晚餐、現場音樂，還有一個印著客戶標誌的巨型蛋糕。"}]},{"unit":43,"theme":"Cancellation 取消","cards":[{"w":"cancel","p":"v.","d":"to decide that a planned event or booking will not happen","c":"取消","s":"A: The airline just sent a message saying that heavy snow is expected in Chicago tomorrow morning, so what should we do about our sales trip? B: I think we should cancel the flights today and book a video call with the clients instead, because the roads will probably be dangerous anyway.","t":"A：航空公司剛傳訊息說明天早上芝加哥預計會下大雪，那我們的業務出差該怎麼辦？ B：我覺得我們今天就應該【取消】航班，改和客戶約視訊會議，因為路況可能也會很危險。"},{"w":"postpone","p":"v.","d":"to move an event to a later time","c":"延後；延期","s":"A: Half of the marketing team is still sick with the flu this week, so are we going to hold the product launch meeting on Thursday as planned? B: No, the manager decided to postpone it until next Monday, when everyone should be back in the office and ready to share their ideas.","t":"A：行銷團隊有一半的人這週還在感冒生病，我們還要照原計畫在星期四開產品發表會議嗎？ B：不，經理決定把它【延後】到下週一，到時候大家應該都回到辦公室，準備好分享想法了。"},{"w":"delay","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen later than planned","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: The new office furniture was supposed to arrive this morning, but the warehouse is still empty, so did the supplier explain what happened? B: Yes, they said a problem at the port will delay the shipment by about three days, so we will have to use the old desks until Friday.","t":"A：新的辦公家具原本應該今天早上送到，但倉庫還是空的，供應商有解釋發生什麼事嗎？ B：有，他們說港口的問題會使貨運【延誤】大約三天，所以我們得用舊桌子用到星期五。"},{"w":"reschedule","p":"v.","d":"to change the time or date of a planned event","c":"重新安排時間","s":"A: I just realized that my dentist appointment on Wednesday afternoon is at the same time as the budget review with the finance department, so what should I do? B: Just call the clinic and ask them to reschedule it for another day, because the budget review is much more important for your project.","t":"A：我剛發現我星期三下午的牙醫預約和財務部的預算審查撞期了，我該怎麼辦？ B：打電話給診所，請他們把預約【重新安排】到別天就好，因為預算審查對你的專案重要得多。"},{"w":"call off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide that a planned event will not take place","c":"取消（活動等）","s":"A: The weather report says a strong typhoon will hit the coast on Saturday, so is the company still having its annual beach picnic for employees and their families? B: Unfortunately, the organizers had to call off the whole event this afternoon, but they promised to choose a new date in November when the weather is better.","t":"A：氣象報告說週六會有強颱登陸沿海，公司還要為員工和家屬舉辦年度海灘野餐嗎？ B：很遺憾，主辦人今天下午不得不【取消】整個活動，但他們承諾會在天氣比較好的十一月另選日期。"},{"w":"withdraw","p":"v.","d":"to stop taking part in something; to take back an offer","c":"退出；撤回","s":"A: I heard that one of the biggest companies in the city was planning to join our trade fair next month, so is that still true? B: Sadly, they decided to withdraw from the fair yesterday because their new products will not be ready in time, so we now have an empty booth near the entrance.","t":"A：我聽說市內一家大公司下個月打算參加我們的商展，現在還是這樣嗎？ B：很可惜，他們昨天決定【退出】商展，因為他們的新產品來不及準備好，所以入口附近現在空出一個攤位。"},{"w":"termination","p":"n.","d":"the act of ending something, such as a contract or a job","c":"終止；結束","s":"A: Our cleaning company has been missing several visits every month, and the office looks terrible, so can we simply stop working with them? B: Yes, but the contract says we must send a written letter of termination at least thirty days in advance, so I will prepare it and ask the director to sign it today.","t":"A：我們的清潔公司每個月都缺好幾次，辦公室看起來很糟，我們可以直接不跟他們合作嗎？ B：可以，但合約規定我們必須至少提前三十天寄出書面的【終止】合作通知信，所以我會準備好，今天請主任簽名。"},{"w":"suspension","p":"n.","d":"a short stop of a service or activity","c":"暫停；中止","s":"A: Why are so many passengers standing outside the train station looking at their phones and trying to find taxis this morning? B: There was a power failure on the main line, so the railway company announced a suspension of all services until noon, and many people are worried about being late for work.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上這麼多乘客站在火車站外面看手機、想找計程車？ B：主線發生停電，所以鐵路公司宣布所有班次【暫停】到中午，很多人擔心上班會遲到。"},{"w":"abandon","p":"v.","d":"to stop doing a plan or activity before it is finished","c":"放棄；中止","s":"A: The research team spent almost two years developing that new smartphone app, so why did it never appear in the online store? B: After testing it with customers, the company found that very few people wanted it, so they decided to abandon the project and spend the money on improving their popular products.","t":"A：研發團隊花了將近兩年開發那個新手機應用程式，為什麼它從來沒有出現在線上商店？ B：用客戶測試後，公司發現很少人想要它，所以他們決定【放棄】這個專案，把錢花在改進熱賣商品上。"},{"w":"revocation","p":"n.","d":"the official act of taking away a right or permit","c":"撤銷；吊銷","s":"A: I read in the newspaper that the restaurant near our office has suddenly closed, even though it was always busy at lunchtime, so what happened? B: Health inspectors found serious problems in the kitchen, which led to the revocation of its business license, and the owner cannot reopen until everything is fixed.","t":"A：我在報紙上看到我們辦公室附近那家餐廳突然關門了，雖然它午餐時間總是客滿，發生什麼事了？ B：衛生稽查員在廚房發現嚴重問題，導致它的營業執照被【撤銷】，老闆在一切改善之前都不能重新開業。"},{"w":"annul","p":"v.","d":"to officially say that an agreement or marriage is not legal","c":"宣告無效；廢除","s":"A: The two companies signed an agreement last spring, but now they are arguing about it in court, so what does the smaller company want? B: Its lawyers are asking the judge to annul the agreement completely, because they believe the other side gave them false information about the sales numbers before they signed it.","t":"A：這兩家公司去年春天簽了協議，但現在他們在法庭上爭執，比較小的那家公司想要什麼？ B：它的律師要求法官將這份協議完全【宣告無效】，因為他們認為對方在簽約前提供了不實的銷售數據。"},{"w":"void","p":"adj.","d":"not legal or not valid any more","c":"無效的","s":"A: I bought a ticket for the concert from a stranger on the internet, but the staff at the gate would not let me enter last night, so why not? B: They said the ticket was void because it had already been reported as stolen, so you should contact your bank and ask for help getting your money back.","t":"A：我在網路上跟陌生人買了一張演唱會門票，但昨晚門口的工作人員不讓我進去，為什麼？ B：他們說那張票是【無效的】，因為已經被通報為失竊票，所以你應該聯絡銀行，請他們幫忙把錢拿回來。"},{"w":"nullify","p":"v.","d":"to make something have no effect or value","c":"使無效；抵銷","s":"A: Our team worked very hard to reduce costs in the factory this year, so why are our total profits still lower than last year? B: The sharp rise in fuel prices this summer managed to nullify most of our savings, so the management is now looking for cheaper energy suppliers for next year.","t":"A：我們團隊今年很努力降低工廠成本，為什麼總利潤還是比去年低？ B：今年夏天燃料價格急遽上漲，【抵銷】了我們大部分節省下來的錢，所以管理層正在為明年尋找比較便宜的能源供應商。"},{"w":"refund","p":"n.","d":"money that is paid back to a customer","c":"退款","s":"A: The printer I ordered online for the office arrived with a broken screen, and it will not even turn on, so what should I do? B: Take some photos of the damage and send them to the store's customer service team, and they should give you a full refund within a week or send a new printer.","t":"A：我在網路上幫辦公室訂的印表機送來時螢幕是壞的，甚至開不了機，我該怎麼辦？ B：拍幾張損壞的照片寄給那家店的客服團隊，他們應該會在一週內給你全額【退款】或寄一台新的印表機。"},{"w":"charge","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you must pay for something","c":"費用；收費","s":"A: I want to change my hotel booking from Friday to Saturday because my meeting in Tokyo was moved, so is that going to be a problem? B: The hotel allows changes, but there is an extra charge of twenty dollars if you do it less than forty-eight hours before arrival, so you should call them right away.","t":"A：我的東京會議改期了，我想把飯店訂房從星期五改到星期六，會有問題嗎？ B：飯店允許更改，但如果在抵達前四十八小時內更改，要額外收二十美元的【費用】，所以你應該馬上打電話給他們。"},{"w":"policy","p":"n.","d":"a set of rules that a company or group follows","c":"政策；規定","s":"A: A customer bought a jacket from our shop three months ago, and today she brought it back without a receipt, asking for her money, so can I accept it? B: I am sorry, but our store policy only allows returns within thirty days with a receipt, so please explain that politely and offer her a discount on something new.","t":"A：有位顧客三個月前在我們店裡買了一件外套，今天她沒帶收據拿回來要求退錢，我可以接受嗎？ B：很抱歉，我們店的【政策】只允許三十天內持收據退貨，所以請禮貌地向她解釋，並提供她購買新商品的折扣。"},{"w":"notice","p":"n.","d":"information or a warning given before something happens","c":"通知；預先通知","s":"A: The landlord told us yesterday that we have to move out of this office because he plans to sell the whole building, so how much time do we have? B: According to our rental agreement, he must give us at least two months' notice, so we have enough time to find a new place near the station.","t":"A：房東昨天告訴我們必須搬離這間辦公室，因為他打算賣掉整棟大樓，我們還有多少時間？ B：根據我們的租約，他必須至少提前兩個月【通知】我們，所以我們有足夠時間在車站附近找新地方。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the latest time by which something must be done","c":"截止期限","s":"A: If our guests want to stay at the conference hotel but change their plans later, when do they need to tell the hotel so they do not lose money? B: The deadline for free changes is next Friday at five o'clock, so please remind everyone in your department to check their travel plans before then.","t":"A：如果我們的客人想住會議飯店但之後改變計畫，他們需要什麼時候告訴飯店才不會損失金錢？ B：免費更改的【截止期限】是下週五五點，所以請提醒你部門的每個人在那之前確認行程。"},{"w":"penalty","p":"n.","d":"money you must pay for breaking a rule or agreement","c":"罰金；違約金","s":"A: I need to end my phone contract six months early because the company is giving me a new work phone with free service, so is that expensive? B: Yes, the phone company asks for a penalty of about one hundred dollars for leaving early, but the free work phone will save you more than that by the end of the year.","t":"A：公司要給我一支免費通話的新公務手機，所以我得提前六個月終止手機合約，這樣會很貴嗎？ B：會，電信公司對提前解約會收大約一百美元的【違約金】，但到年底時，這支免費的公務手機幫你省下的錢會更多。"},{"w":"fee","p":"n.","d":"money paid for a service or to join something","c":"費用","s":"A: Our department wants to join the international business conference in Singapore next spring, but we have not decided yet, so when should we register? B: If we sign up before the end of this month, the registration fee is only two hundred dollars per person, but it will double in January, so we should decide soon.","t":"A：我們部門想參加明年春天在新加坡舉辦的國際商務會議，但還沒決定，應該什麼時候報名？ B：如果在這個月底前報名，每人報名【費】只要兩百美元，但一月起會翻倍，所以我們應該盡快決定。"},{"w":"unexpected","p":"adj.","d":"not expected; surprising","c":"意料之外的；意外的","s":"A: The sales report looked great on Monday, so why did the manager call an emergency meeting this morning and look so worried? B: There was a completely unexpected problem with our biggest customer, who suddenly said they could not pay their bill this month, and nobody in the company had seen it coming.","t":"A：星期一的銷售報告看起來很好，為什麼經理今天早上召開緊急會議，而且看起來那麼擔心？ B：我們最大的客戶出了一個完全【意料之外的】問題，他們突然說這個月付不出帳款，公司裡沒有人預料到。"},{"w":"sudden","p":"adj.","d":"happening very quickly and without warning","c":"突然的","s":"A: Why did the outdoor concert in the city park end so early last night, when the band had only played three songs? B: A sudden storm with strong wind and heavy rain arrived without any warning, so the organizers stopped the show and asked everyone to go to the nearby shopping mall for safety.","t":"A：昨晚市立公園的戶外音樂會為什麼那麼早就結束了，樂團才唱了三首歌？ B：一場夾帶強風豪雨的【突如其來的】暴風雨毫無預警地來襲，所以主辦單位停止演出，請大家到附近的購物中心避難。"},{"w":"official","p":"adj.","d":"approved by or coming from a government or organization","c":"正式的；官方的","s":"A: Everyone is saying that the summer music festival will not happen this year because of the new road construction, so is it really true? B: I have heard the same thing from friends, but we should wait for the official announcement from the city government before we cancel our hotel rooms and train tickets.","t":"A：大家都在說今年的夏季音樂節因為新的道路工程不會舉辦，這是真的嗎？ B：我也從朋友那裡聽說了，但我們應該等市政府的【正式】公告，再取消飯店房間和火車票。"},{"w":"notify","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone officially about something","c":"通知","s":"A: The water company plans to repair the pipes in our building next Tuesday, and there will be no water from nine to three, so what should we do? B: Please send an email to notify all the staff today, so they can bring bottled water and plan their lunch breaks outside the office.","t":"A：自來水公司下週二要修理我們大樓的水管，九點到三點會停水，我們該怎麼做？ B：請今天寄電子郵件【通知】全體員工，這樣他們可以帶瓶裝水，並計畫到辦公室外面吃午餐。"},{"w":"confirm","p":"v.","d":"to say or show that a plan or booking is definite","c":"確認","s":"A: I booked a table for twelve people at the Italian restaurant for our team dinner on Friday night, so is there anything else I need to do? B: Yes, the restaurant asked us to call on Thursday to confirm the reservation, or they may give the table to other customers because Friday nights are very busy.","t":"A：我在義大利餐廳為週五晚上的團隊晚餐訂了十二人的位子，還有什麼需要做的嗎？ B：有，餐廳要求我們星期四打電話【確認】訂位，否則他們可能會把桌子給其他客人，因為週五晚上很忙。"},{"w":"disruption","p":"n.","d":"a problem that stops something from working normally","c":"中斷；干擾","s":"A: The city is going to repair the main bridge downtown for the next three weeks, so how will that affect our delivery drivers? B: There will be some disruption to traffic during rush hour, so the drivers should leave earlier in the morning and take the highway to reach our customers on time.","t":"A：市政府接下來三週要修理市中心的主要橋梁，這會對我們的送貨司機有什麼影響？ B：尖峰時段交通會受到一些【干擾】，所以司機早上應該早點出發，走高速公路才能準時送達客戶。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n.","d":"another choice you can use instead","c":"替代方案；其他選擇","s":"A: Our flight to Hong Kong was cancelled because of the typhoon, and the airline says the next available seats are on Thursday, so what can we do? B: One good alternative is to take the high-speed train to another city and fly from there tomorrow, which means we can still attend the meeting.","t":"A：我們飛往香港的班機因颱風取消了，航空公司說下一個有位子的是星期四，我們能怎麼辦？ B：一個不錯的【替代方案】是搭高鐵到另一個城市，明天從那裡起飛，這樣我們還是能參加會議。"},{"w":"compensation","p":"n.","d":"money paid to someone because of a loss or problem","c":"賠償；補償","s":"A: The airline kept us waiting at the gate for more than seven hours without any food, and we missed an important business dinner, so can we ask for something? B: Yes, under the new travel rules you can apply for compensation on their website, and they may pay you up to three hundred dollars for the long wait.","t":"A：航空公司讓我們在登機門等了七個多小時，而且沒有提供任何食物，我們也錯過了重要的商務晚餐，我們可以要求什麼嗎？ B：可以，根據新的旅遊規定，你可以在他們的網站上申請【賠償】，他們可能會因為長時間等候付你最多三百美元。"},{"w":"reinstate","p":"v.","d":"to bring back a service, rule or person to an earlier position","c":"恢復；使復職","s":"A: Many customers complained after the bus company stopped the late-night service from the airport last year, so has anything changed since then? B: Yes, the company has agreed to reinstate the service starting next month, so travelers arriving on evening flights will be able to get home cheaply again.","t":"A：去年公車公司停駛機場深夜班次後，很多乘客抱怨，從那之後有任何改變嗎？ B：有，公司已同意從下個月起【恢復】這項服務，所以搭晚班飛機抵達的旅客又能便宜地回家了。"}]},{"unit":44,"theme":"Car 汽車","cards":[{"w":"vehicle","p":"n.","d":"a machine such as a car, bus or truck that carries people or goods","c":"車輛","s":"A: Our sales team will visit five clients in the countryside next week, and the roads there are narrow and muddy, so which company car should we book? B: I suggest the large vehicle with four-wheel drive, because it can carry all six of us and our sample boxes without any trouble on those rough mountain roads.","t":"A：我們業務團隊下週要拜訪鄉下的五位客戶，那裡的道路又窄又泥濘，我們該預訂哪一輛公司車？ B：我建議那台四輪驅動的大型【車輛】，因為它可以載我們六個人和樣品箱，在崎嶇的山路上也不會有任何問題。"},{"w":"engine","p":"n.","d":"the part of a car that makes the power to move it","c":"引擎","s":"A: The delivery van made a loud knocking noise this morning when I started it, and then it stopped twice on the highway, so what do you think is wrong? B: The mechanic checked it at lunchtime and said the engine is overheating because it has not had fresh oil for almost a year.","t":"A：今天早上我發動送貨車時它發出很大的敲擊聲，接著在高速公路上熄火了兩次，你覺得是哪裡出了問題？ B：技師午餐時間檢查過了，他說【引擎】過熱，因為它將近一年沒換新機油了。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"n.","d":"something such as gas or oil that is burned to give power","c":"燃料","s":"A: The trip to the trade fair in Kaohsiung is about four hours by car, so how often do you think we will need to stop on the way? B: The tank holds enough fuel for around six hundred kilometers, so we should only need one short stop, and we can buy coffee and snacks at the same time.","t":"A：開車去高雄的商展大約要四個小時，你覺得我們路上需要停幾次？ B：油箱裡的【燃料】足夠跑大約六百公里，所以我們應該只需要短暫停一次，同時還可以買咖啡和點心。"},{"w":"petrol","p":"n.","d":"the British word for gasoline, the liquid fuel for cars","c":"汽油","s":"A: The company is paying for our travel expenses during the sales tour around the island, so do I need to keep every receipt from the gas station? B: Yes, please keep them all, because the accounting department will only pay you back for the petrol if you attach the original receipts to your expense report.","t":"A：公司會支付我們環島業務之旅的差旅費，那我需要保留加油站的每一張收據嗎？ B：是的，請全部保留，因為只有你在費用報告上附上收據正本，會計部才會退還你的【汽油】費用。"},{"w":"diesel","p":"n.","d":"a heavy fuel used in many trucks, buses and some cars","c":"柴油","s":"A: Our moving company is planning to replace the old trucks next year, so are you going to choose the same type of fuel as before or try something different? B: We will probably stay with diesel for the heavy trucks because it gives them more power on long trips, but the small vans may become fully electric.","t":"A：我們搬家公司打算明年汰換舊卡車，你們會選擇和以前一樣的燃料，還是嘗試不同的？ B：重型卡車我們可能會繼續用【柴油】，因為它在長途行駛時提供更大的動力，但小型廂型車可能會全面改為電動。"},{"w":"electric","p":"adj.","d":"using electricity for power","c":"電動的","s":"A: The city government is offering money to companies that reduce air pollution this year, so should we think about changing the vehicles we use for deliveries? B: That is a great idea, because an electric van does not need gasoline, it is much quieter in busy streets, and charging it overnight at the warehouse is quite cheap.","t":"A：市政府今年提供補助給減少空氣汙染的公司，我們是否該考慮更換送貨用的車輛？ B：這是個好主意，因為【電動】廂型車不需要汽油，在繁忙的街道上安靜得多，而且晚上在倉庫充電也相當便宜。"},{"w":"battery","p":"n.","d":"an object that stores electricity to start a car or run a machine","c":"電瓶；電池","s":"A: I tried to start my car in the parking lot after the late meeting last night, but nothing happened at all, even though the lights had been switched off. B: That usually means the battery is dead, so you should ask a coworker to help you with jump leads or call the roadside assistance number.","t":"A：昨晚開完很晚的會後，我在停車場想發動車子，但完全沒反應，雖然車燈都已經關掉了。 B：那通常表示【電瓶】沒電了，你應該請同事用救車線幫忙，或打道路救援電話。"},{"w":"brake","p":"v.","d":"to make a vehicle slow down or stop","c":"煞車","s":"A: When you were driving the company van down that steep hill in the rain yesterday afternoon, did you notice anything strange about how it handled the road? B: Yes, I had to brake much harder than usual to slow down before the traffic lights, so I think the pedals need to be checked as soon as possible.","t":"A：昨天下午你在雨中開公司廂型車下那個陡坡時，有沒有注意到車子的操控有什麼奇怪的地方？ B：有，我必須比平常更用力【煞車】才能在紅綠燈前減速，所以我認為踏板需要盡快檢查。"},{"w":"accelerate","p":"v.","d":"to make a vehicle go faster","c":"加速","s":"A: I am a little nervous about driving on the highway for the first time with my new job, so do you have any advice for joining the fast lane? B: When you enter from the ramp, you need to accelerate smoothly until you match the speed of the other cars, and always check your mirrors before you change lanes.","t":"A：新工作讓我第一次要開上高速公路，我有點緊張，你對切入快車道有什麼建議嗎？ B：從匝道進入時，你需要平穩地【加速】直到跟上其他車的速度，而且變換車道前一定要看後照鏡。"},{"w":"steer","p":"v.","d":"to control the direction a vehicle goes","c":"駕駛；操控方向","s":"A: The rental company gave us a very large van for moving the office furniture this weekend, and I have only ever driven small cars, so is it difficult? B: It is not too bad, but you must steer slowly and carefully around corners, because the back of the van needs much more space than you might expect.","t":"A：租車公司給了我們一台很大的廂型車，這週末用來搬辦公室家具，而我只開過小車，這會很難嗎？ B：還好，但轉彎時你必須慢慢地、小心地【操控方向】，因為廂型車的後半部需要的空間比你想像的多得多。"},{"w":"wheel","p":"n.","d":"one of the round parts under a car that turn so it can move","c":"車輪","s":"A: Why did the delivery driver arrive almost two hours late this afternoon when the customer had been waiting since lunch? B: He said a nail went through one of the front tires on the highway, so he had to stop at the side of the road and change the wheel by himself before he could continue.","t":"A：客戶從午餐時間就在等，為什麼送貨司機今天下午遲到將近兩個小時？ B：他說在高速公路上有根釘子刺穿了一個前輪胎，所以他得停在路邊自己換【車輪】才能繼續上路。"},{"w":"tire","p":"n.","d":"the rubber ring around a wheel that is filled with air","c":"輪胎","s":"A: The company minibus feels a bit unsteady when I drive it at high speed on the highway, and it seems to pull to the left, so what should I do? B: One tire probably does not have enough air in it, so stop at the next gas station and check the pressure on all four before you drive any further.","t":"A：我在高速公路上高速駕駛公司的小巴時感覺有點不穩，而且好像會往左偏，我該怎麼辦？ B：可能有一個【輪胎】氣不足，所以在下一個加油站停下來，四個都檢查胎壓後再繼續開。"},{"w":"seat","p":"n.","d":"a place where a person sits in a vehicle","c":"座位","s":"A: I am driving three clients from the airport to the hotel tonight, and one of them is quite tall, so how can I make the trip more pleasant for him? B: Offer him the front passenger seat, because it has the most room for his legs, and he can enjoy the view of the city lights on the way.","t":"A：我今晚要開車載三位客戶從機場到飯店，其中一位個子很高，我該怎麼讓他的車程更舒服？ B：讓他坐前面的副駕駛【座位】，因為那裡的腿部空間最大，而且他可以沿途欣賞城市的燈光。"},{"w":"seatbelt","p":"n.","d":"a belt in a car that holds you in your seat for safety","c":"安全帶","s":"A: Our new driving rules for staff say that everyone in a company car must follow certain safety steps, so what is the most important one? B: Before the car moves, the driver must make sure that every passenger, including those in the back, has fastened their seatbelt, because it can save lives in an accident.","t":"A：我們新的員工駕駛規定說，每個坐公司車的人都必須遵守某些安全步驟，最重要的是哪一個？ B：車子開動前，司機必須確認每位乘客，包括後座的人，都已經繫好【安全帶】，因為發生事故時它能救命。"},{"w":"dashboard","p":"n.","d":"the panel in front of the driver that shows speed, fuel and other information","c":"儀表板","s":"A: While I was driving to the branch office this morning, a small orange light suddenly came on in front of me, and I wasn't sure whether it was serious. B: If a warning light appears on the dashboard, you should check the owner's manual right away, because it might mean the engine oil is low.","t":"A：今天早上我開車去分公司時，面前突然亮起一個橘色小燈，我不確定是否嚴重。 B：如果【儀表板】上出現警示燈，你應該立刻查看車主手冊，因為那可能表示引擎機油不足。"},{"w":"mirror","p":"n.","d":"a piece of glass in a car that lets the driver see behind or beside","c":"後照鏡","s":"A: I almost hit a motorcycle when I was turning right into the hotel entrance yesterday, and I still feel shaken about it, so what went wrong? B: Before you turn or change lanes, always look in the side mirror and also turn your head, because motorcycles can hide in places you cannot easily see.","t":"A：我昨天右轉進飯店入口時差點撞到一台機車，到現在還心有餘悸，是哪裡出了錯？ B：轉彎或變換車道前，一定要看側邊【後照鏡】，也要轉頭確認，因為機車可能躲在你不容易看到的地方。"},{"w":"headlight","p":"n.","d":"one of the large lights at the front of a car","c":"車頭燈","s":"A: I have to drive back from the factory late tonight after the inspection, and the country road there has no street lamps at all, so is that dangerous? B: Just drive slowly, and before you leave, ask the security guard to check that each headlight is working, because you will need strong light to see the road clearly.","t":"A：今晚檢查完後我得很晚才從工廠開車回來，那裡的鄉間道路完全沒有路燈，這樣危險嗎？ B：慢慢開就好，出發前請警衛幫你確認每一個【車頭燈】都正常運作，因為你需要強光才能看清楚路面。"},{"w":"license","p":"n.","d":"an official card that shows you are allowed to drive","c":"執照；駕照","s":"A: We are hiring a new sales assistant who will often visit customers by car, so what documents should we ask the candidates to bring to the interview? B: Besides their résumé, they must bring a valid driver's license, and we should also ask how many years of driving experience they have on busy city roads.","t":"A：我們要招聘一位常需要開車拜訪客戶的新業務助理，應該請應徵者帶哪些文件來面試？ B：除了履歷，他們還必須帶有效的駕駛【執照】，我們也應該問他們在繁忙市區道路有幾年的駕駛經驗。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars, buses and other vehicles moving on a road","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: The meeting with the investors starts at nine o'clock tomorrow morning in the city center, so what time should we leave the office to get there? B: Let's leave by seven thirty, because the traffic on the main road is always heavy during rush hour, and we don't want to arrive late and stressed.","t":"A：明天早上九點在市中心和投資人開會，我們該幾點離開辦公室才能到？ B：我們七點半前出發吧，因為尖峰時段主要道路上的【車流】總是很多，我們不想遲到又緊張兮兮地抵達。"},{"w":"parking","p":"n.","d":"space for leaving cars; the act of leaving a car somewhere for a time","c":"停車；停車位","s":"A: Many visitors are coming to our product launch at the convention center on Saturday, so how will they find a place to leave their cars? B: The center has free parking for up to three hundred cars behind the main hall, and we will put clear signs at the entrance to guide drivers there.","t":"A：週六會有很多訪客來會展中心參加我們的產品發表會，他們要怎麼找到地方放車？ B：會展中心主廳後方有可容納三百輛車的免費【停車位】，我們會在入口放置清楚的指標引導駕駛人過去。"},{"w":"garage","p":"n.","d":"a building where cars are kept or repaired","c":"車庫；修車廠","s":"A: The weather report says there will be a strong typhoon this weekend with heavy rain and wind, so where should we keep the company cars? B: Please move all of them into the underground garage below the office building on Friday evening, because branches and flying objects could easily damage them outside.","t":"A：氣象報告說這週末會有強烈颱風，伴隨大雨和強風，我們該把公司車放在哪裡？ B：請在週五傍晚把所有車都移到辦公大樓下方的地下【車庫】，因為在外面樹枝和飛落物很容易把它們弄壞。"},{"w":"service","p":"v.","d":"to check and fix a vehicle or machine regularly so it keeps working well","c":"保養；檢修","s":"A: Our delivery vans have traveled more than ten thousand kilometers since January, and two drivers say the brakes feel soft, so what should we do? B: We should service all of them at the dealer next week, so the mechanics can check the oil, the brakes and the tires before any real problems appear.","t":"A：我們的送貨車從一月以來已經跑了一萬多公里，有兩位司機說煞車感覺很軟，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們下週應該把它們全部送到經銷商那裡【保養】，讓技師在真正出問題之前檢查機油、煞車和輪胎。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken or damaged","c":"修理","s":"A: Someone backed into my car in the shopping mall parking lot on Sunday and broke the back door, so how long will it take to fix? B: The body shop told me they can repair the damage in about three days, and the insurance company will pay for most of the cost because the other driver admitted it.","t":"A：週日有人在購物中心停車場倒車撞到我的車，撞壞了後車門，要多久才能修好？ B：鈑金廠告訴我他們大約三天就能【修理】好損壞的地方，而且因為對方駕駛承認了，保險公司會支付大部分費用。"},{"w":"speed","p":"n.","d":"how fast something moves","c":"速度","s":"A: I got a ticket in the mail this morning for driving too fast near the school on my way to the office last month, and I'm very surprised. B: The speed limit on that street is only thirty kilometers per hour during school hours, and there is a camera hidden near the crossing.","t":"A：今天早上我收到一張罰單，是上個月上班途中在學校附近開太快，我非常驚訝。 B：那條街在上學時段的【速度】限制只有每小時三十公里，而且斑馬線附近藏了一台測速相機。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a particular type or version of a product","c":"車款；型號","s":"A: The sales manager wants to replace her old company car with something more modern this year, so which car is she thinking about buying? B: She likes the latest model from the Japanese maker, because it has a bigger trunk for her samples, better fuel economy, and a smart system that connects to her phone.","t":"A：業務經理今年想把她的舊公司車換成更現代化的車，她考慮買哪一台？ B：她喜歡那家日本車廠的最新【車款】，因為它的後車廂更大可以放樣品、更省油，還有能連接手機的智慧系統。"},{"w":"used","p":"adj.","d":"owned by someone before; not new","c":"二手的","s":"A: Our small catering business needs a second van for weekend events, but we don't have a large budget this year, so what are our choices? B: We could buy a used van from a trusted dealer, because it costs about half the price of a brand-new one, and many come with a one-year warranty.","t":"A：我們的小型外燴公司週末活動需要第二台廂型車，但今年預算不多，我們有哪些選擇？ B：我們可以向信譽良好的車商買一台【二手】廂型車，因為價格大約是全新車的一半，而且很多附有一年保固。"},{"w":"new","p":"adj.","d":"recently made or bought; not used before","c":"新的","s":"A: I heard that the company finally replaced the old delivery trucks that kept breaking down last winter, so how do the drivers feel about it? B: They are very happy with the new trucks, which arrived straight from the factory last week, because they are quieter, cleaner and much more reliable on long trips.","t":"A：我聽說公司終於汰換了去年冬天一直故障的舊送貨卡車，司機們覺得怎麼樣？ B：他們對上週直接從工廠送來的【新】卡車非常滿意，因為它們更安靜、更乾淨，長途行駛也可靠得多。"},{"w":"safe","p":"adj.","d":"not likely to cause harm or danger","c":"安全的","s":"A: My elderly parents want to buy a car for their weekend trips to the countryside, and they asked me for advice, so what should they look for? B: They should choose a safe car with good airbags, automatic emergency braking and high test scores, because protecting the people inside matters more than style or speed.","t":"A：我年邁的父母想買一台車週末去鄉下玩，他們問我的意見，他們應該注意什麼？ B：他們應該選擇一台有良好安全氣囊、自動緊急煞車和高測試分數的【安全】車款，因為保護車內的人比外型或速度更重要。"},{"w":"comfortable","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel relaxed and physically pleasant","c":"舒適的","s":"A: The marketing team will drive six hours to the exhibition in Taichung and back on Friday, so which car should I reserve from the rental company? B: Please book the large sedan with soft leather seats and plenty of leg room, because it is much more comfortable for long trips than the small city car.","t":"A：行銷團隊週五要開六個小時的車往返台中的展覽，我該向租車公司預訂哪一台車？ B：請預訂那台有柔軟皮椅和寬敞腿部空間的大型轎車，因為長途旅行時它比小型城市車【舒適】得多。"}]},{"unit":45,"theme":"Career 職涯","cards":[{"w":"profession","p":"n.","d":"a type of job that needs special training or education","c":"職業；專業","s":"A: My niece is finishing her degree in health sciences next spring, but she still seems unsure about her future, so what advice did you give her at dinner last night? B: I told her that nursing is a respected profession with many chances to work abroad, and that hospitals in Taipei are always looking for caring, well-trained staff.","t":"A：我外甥女明年春天就要拿到健康科學學位了，但她似乎對未來還不確定，你昨晚吃飯時給了她什麼建議？ B：我告訴她護理是一個受人尊敬、有很多出國工作機會的【職業】，而且台北的醫院一直在找有愛心、受過良好訓練的人員。"},{"w":"occupation","p":"n.","d":"a person's job or regular work","c":"職業","s":"A: The bank's loan application asks for a lot of personal details, so what should I write in the box near the bottom of the second page? B: That box is for your occupation, so just write \"accountant,\" and then add the name of your company and how many years you have worked there.","t":"A：銀行的貸款申請表要填很多個人資料，第二頁底部附近的那一格我該寫什麼？ B：那一格是填你的【職業】，就寫「會計師」，然後再加上你公司的名稱以及你在那裡工作了幾年。"},{"w":"job","p":"n.","d":"work that you do regularly to earn money","c":"工作","s":"A: You looked really tired at the team meeting this morning, so is everything all right with your new role in the marketing department? B: I'm fine, but the job keeps me busier than I expected, because I have to write reports, answer client emails, and plan two product launches before the end of the month.","t":"A：你今天早上開團隊會議時看起來很累，你在行銷部的新職務一切都還好嗎？ B：我很好，只是這份【工作】比我預期的還要忙，因為我得寫報告、回覆客戶郵件，還要在月底前規劃兩場產品發表會。"},{"w":"position","p":"n.","d":"a job in a company or organization","c":"職位","s":"A: I saw that the hotel downtown is hiring again this month, so are you thinking about sending them your application before the deadline on Friday? B: Yes, they have an open position at the front desk, and since I speak English and Japanese well, I think I have a good chance of getting it.","t":"A：我看到市中心那家飯店這個月又在徵人了，你打算在星期五截止前寄申請給他們嗎？ B：是的，他們櫃檯有一個空缺的【職位】，而且我英文和日文都說得不錯，我覺得我很有機會錄取。"},{"w":"employment","p":"n.","d":"the state of having paid work","c":"就業；受雇","s":"A: Many students in my evening class will graduate this summer, so do you know what kind of support the city government offers to young people looking for work? B: The local employment center runs free workshops every Saturday, where career advisers help graduates write cover letters, practice answering questions, and search for suitable openings online.","t":"A：我夜間班的很多學生今年夏天就要畢業了，你知道市政府為找工作的年輕人提供哪些協助嗎？ B：當地的【就業】服務中心每週六都有免費工作坊，職涯顧問會協助畢業生寫求職信、練習回答問題，並在網路上搜尋合適的職缺。"},{"w":"employer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays people to work for them","c":"雇主","s":"A: You have worked at the same electronics company for almost twelve years now, so what makes you stay there when so many other firms offer higher pay? B: My employer treats people fairly, provides excellent health insurance, and even pays for evening classes, so I feel valued and have never wanted to leave.","t":"A：你在同一家電子公司已經工作快十二年了，有那麼多公司開出更高的薪水，是什麼讓你留下來？ B：我的【雇主】待人公平，提供很好的健康保險，甚至幫我們付夜間課程的學費，所以我覺得被重視，從來沒想過要離開。"},{"w":"employee","p":"n.","d":"a person who is paid to work for a company","c":"員工","s":"A: The manager gave a special award at the year-end party last night, so who received it, and why did everyone clap so loudly? B: It went to a quiet employee from the shipping department who worked extra hours during the busy season and helped train three new team members without being asked.","t":"A：經理昨晚在尾牙上頒了一個特別獎，是誰得獎了？為什麼大家拍手拍得那麼大聲？ B：得獎的是出貨部一位安靜的【員工】，他在旺季時加班，而且主動幫忙訓練了三位新同事。"},{"w":"salary","p":"n.","d":"fixed money paid to a worker, usually every month","c":"薪水（月薪；年薪）","s":"A: The software company in Hsinchu offered you the job yesterday, so are you going to accept it, or are you still comparing it with the other offer? B: I'm probably going to accept, because the monthly salary is twenty percent higher than what I earn now, and they also give a bonus at the end of the year.","t":"A：新竹那家軟體公司昨天錄取你了，你要接受嗎？還是還在跟另一個工作機會比較？ B：我大概會接受，因為每個月的【薪水】比我現在多百分之二十，而且年底還有獎金。"},{"w":"wage","p":"n.","d":"money paid per hour or day for work","c":"工資（時薪；日薪）","s":"A: Many part-time workers at the supermarket have been complaining recently, so what exactly are they unhappy about? B: They say their hourly wage hasn't gone up in three years, even though rent and food prices have risen, so they want the owner to discuss a fair increase with them next week.","t":"A：超市很多兼職員工最近一直在抱怨，他們到底在不滿什麼？ B：他們說雖然房租和食物都漲價了，但他們的時薪【工資】三年來都沒調漲，所以希望老闆下週和他們討論合理的加薪。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"a move to a higher, more important job","c":"升遷；晉升","s":"A: Jessica has been working late almost every night and taking extra training courses, so is she preparing for something special at work? B: Yes, she hopes to get a promotion to sales manager next spring, because the current manager is moving to the Singapore office and the director wants someone from inside the team.","t":"A：Jessica幾乎每晚都加班，還額外上培訓課程，她是在為工作上什麼特別的事做準備嗎？ B：是的，她希望明年春天能【升遷】為業務經理，因為現任經理要調到新加坡辦公室，而主管希望從團隊內部找人接任。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or skill you get from doing a job","c":"經驗","s":"A: We received over fifty applications for the accounting role, so how are we going to choose the five people to interview next week? B: Let's first look for candidates with at least three years of experience in a large firm, and then compare their language ability and the software they can use.","t":"A：會計職缺我們收到超過五十份申請，要怎麼選出下週面試的五個人？ B：我們先找在大公司有至少三年【經驗】的應徵者，然後再比較他們的語言能力和會用的軟體。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"an ability to do something well because you have practiced it","c":"技能","s":"A: The new customer service team will start answering calls on Monday, so what is the most important thing they should learn during training this week? B: Listening carefully is the key skill, because angry customers calm down quickly when they feel understood, and then our staff can solve the problem much more easily.","t":"A：新的客服團隊星期一就要開始接電話了，這週培訓期間他們最該學的是什麼？ B：仔細聆聽是關鍵【技能】，因為生氣的顧客覺得被理解時會很快冷靜下來，這樣我們的員工就能更輕鬆地解決問題。"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an exam or course result that shows you can do a job","c":"資格；證照","s":"A: I'd love to teach English at a public high school after I move back to Taiwan, so what do I need to prepare before applying? B: You'll need a teaching qualification from a recognized university, a good English test score, and some classroom practice, so start collecting your documents as early as possible.","t":"A：我搬回台灣後很想在公立高中教英文，申請之前我需要準備什麼？ B：你需要一所認可大學核發的教師【資格】、不錯的英文檢定成績，以及一些實際教學經驗，所以盡早開始準備文件吧。"},{"w":"training","p":"n.","d":"teaching people the skills for a job","c":"培訓；訓練","s":"A: The factory is installing new machines next month, so how will the workers learn to use them safely without slowing down production? B: The supplier will send two engineers to give every shift three days of hands-on training, and they will also leave a detailed manual in Chinese for later reference.","t":"A：工廠下個月要安裝新機器，工人要怎麼在不拖慢生產的情況下學會安全操作？ B：供應商會派兩位工程師為每個班次提供三天的實作【培訓】，還會留下一份詳細的中文手冊供日後參考。"},{"w":"resume","p":"n.","d":"a document listing your education and work history","c":"履歷","s":"A: I'm applying for a design job at an advertising agency next week, so could you look at my documents and tell me what to improve? B: Your resume is too long, so cut it down to one page, put your best projects at the top, and remove the part-time jobs you had in high school.","t":"A：我下週要應徵一家廣告公司的設計工作，你可以看看我的資料，告訴我哪裡要改進嗎？ B：你的【履歷】太長了，刪減到一頁，把最好的作品放在最上面，並拿掉你高中時做過的打工。"},{"w":"interview","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting where an employer asks a job seeker questions","c":"面試","s":"A: You're wearing a suit today, and you keep checking your watch, so do you have an important meeting with a client this afternoon? B: Not exactly, I have a job interview with a bank at two o'clock, and I'm nervous because they will ask me questions in English in front of three managers.","t":"A：你今天穿西裝，又一直看手錶，下午是要跟客戶開重要的會嗎？ B：不完全是，我兩點要去一家銀行【面試】，我很緊張，因為他們會在三位經理面前用英文問我問題。"},{"w":"hire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job","c":"雇用","s":"A: Our online orders have doubled since the holiday sale started, and the warehouse staff are exhausted, so what is the boss planning to do about it? B: She has decided to hire five temporary workers until the end of January, so the regular team can rest and customers can still receive their packages on time.","t":"A：假期特賣開始後我們的網路訂單翻倍了，倉庫員工都累壞了，老闆打算怎麼處理？ B：她決定【雇用】五名臨時工到一月底，這樣正職團隊可以休息，顧客也能準時收到包裹。"},{"w":"fire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone leave their job, usually as a punishment","c":"開除；解雇","s":"A: I heard that the new cashier at the downtown branch suddenly stopped coming to work, so did she quit, or did something happen? B: The manager had to fire her after she was caught taking money from the register twice, even though he had given her a clear warning the first time.","t":"A：聽說市區分店的新收銀員突然不來上班了，她是辭職了，還是發生了什麼事？ B：她被抓到兩次從收銀機拿錢，經理只好【開除】她，即使第一次他已經明確警告過她了。"},{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"achieving what you planned or wanted","c":"成功","s":"A: Your bakery has opened three new shops in the past two years, so what do you think is the main reason customers keep coming back? B: Much of our success comes from using fresh local ingredients and listening to feedback, because we change the menu whenever regular customers suggest something new and interesting.","t":"A：你的麵包店過去兩年開了三家新店，你覺得顧客一再回訪的主要原因是什麼？ B：我們的【成功】大多來自使用新鮮的在地食材並傾聽意見，因為只要熟客提出新奇有趣的建議，我們就會調整菜單。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to achieve something","c":"抱負；雄心","s":"A: Your younger brother just started his first job as a sales assistant, so what kind of future does he hope to have in the company? B: His biggest ambition is to open his own sporting goods store one day, so he is learning everything he can about buying, pricing, and managing staff while he works there.","t":"A：你弟弟剛開始他的第一份工作當銷售助理，他希望在公司裡有什麼樣的未來？ B：他最大的【抱負】是有一天開自己的運動用品店，所以他在那裡工作時盡可能學習採購、定價和管理員工的一切。"},{"w":"goal","p":"n.","d":"something you are trying to achieve","c":"目標","s":"A: The sales team had a difficult first half of the year, so what did the director say at the planning meeting this morning? B: She set a clear goal of winning ten new corporate clients by December, and she promised a team trip to Japan if we reach it before the holidays.","t":"A：業務團隊上半年很辛苦，主管今天早上在規劃會議上說了什麼？ B：她訂了一個明確的【目標】，要在十二月前爭取到十家新的企業客戶，還承諾如果我們在假期前達成，就招待團隊去日本旅遊。"},{"w":"path","p":"n.","d":"a series of steps or choices that lead somewhere, such as in a career","c":"道路；（職涯）路線","s":"A: You studied engineering at university, but now you work in human resources, so how did you end up in such a different field? B: My career path changed after I organized training events at my first company, because I discovered that I enjoyed helping people grow much more than designing machines.","t":"A：你大學念工程，現在卻在人資部門工作，你怎麼會走進這麼不同的領域？ B：我在第一家公司籌辦培訓活動後，職涯【道路】就改變了，因為我發現比起設計機器，我更喜歡幫助別人成長。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something good","c":"機會","s":"A: The head office in London has invited two staff members from our branch to work there for six months, so are you going to apply? B: Definitely, because it's a great opportunity to improve my English, learn how a global team works, and build connections that could help my career later.","t":"A：倫敦總公司邀請我們分公司兩位員工去那裡工作六個月，你要申請嗎？ B：當然，因為這是提升英文、了解國際團隊如何運作，以及建立日後對職涯有幫助的人脈的好【機會】。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"a healthy mix of different parts, such as work and private life","c":"平衡","s":"A: You used to stay at the office until ten every night, but lately you leave at six, so what made you change your routine? B: I realized I needed a better balance between work and family, so now I finish my tasks earlier, have dinner with my kids, and go jogging on weekends.","t":"A：你以前每晚都在辦公室待到十點，最近卻六點就下班，是什麼讓你改變作息？ B：我發現我需要在工作和家庭之間取得更好的【平衡】，所以現在我提早完成工作，和孩子一起吃晚餐，週末去慢跑。"},{"w":"retire","p":"v.","d":"to stop working, usually because you are older","c":"退休","s":"A: Mr. Lin has managed the accounting department for almost thirty years, so is it true that the company is planning a big farewell party for him? B: Yes, he will retire at the end of March so he can travel around Europe with his wife, and the staff are collecting money to buy him a nice camera.","t":"A：林先生管理會計部將近三十年了，公司真的要為他辦一場盛大的歡送會嗎？ B：是的，他三月底就要【退休】了，好和太太去歐洲旅行，員工們正在集資買一台好相機送他。"},{"w":"long-term","p":"adj.","d":"lasting or planned for a long time","c":"長期的","s":"A: The startup offered me a higher salary than my current company, but I'm worried because it's so new, so what do you think I should do? B: Think about your long-term plans first, because if you want to stay in one place for many years and buy a home, a stable company might be the safer choice.","t":"A：那家新創公司開的薪水比我現在的公司高，但我擔心它太新了，你覺得我該怎麼做？ B：先想想你的【長期】計畫，因為如果你想在一個地方待很多年並買房子，穩定的公司可能是比較安全的選擇。"},{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"not likely to change; steady","c":"穩定的","s":"A: Your sister left her exciting job at a travel startup to work for the city government, so why did she make such a big change? B: After her son was born, she wanted a stable income with regular hours, so she chose a government office where the pay is lower but she never worries about losing her job.","t":"A：你姊姊離開了旅遊新創公司那份刺激的工作，去市政府上班，她為什麼要做這麼大的改變？ B：她兒子出生後，她想要有【穩定的】收入和規律的工時，所以選擇了政府機關，雖然薪水較低，但她從不擔心失業。"},{"w":"rewarding","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel satisfied and happy","c":"有意義的；有成就感的","s":"A: You gave up a well-paid position at a bank to teach science at a rural elementary school, so do you ever regret that decision? B: Not at all, because the work is very rewarding, and seeing my students get excited about experiments every week makes me happier than any bonus I received at the bank.","t":"A：你放棄銀行的高薪職位，去鄉下的小學教自然科學，你曾後悔過這個決定嗎？ B：一點也不，因為這份工作很【有成就感】，每週看到學生對實驗感到興奮，比我在銀行領過的任何獎金都讓我開心。"}]},{"unit":46,"theme":"Celebration 慶祝","cards":[{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable because of a special event","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Our sales team finally reached its yearly target last Friday, so how is the manager planning to thank everyone for all the extra hours? B: She has booked a private room at an Italian restaurant downtown, and we will celebrate the success with dinner and a short speech next Thursday evening.","t":"A：我們銷售團隊上週五終於達成年度目標，經理打算怎麼感謝大家加了那麼多班？ B：她在市中心一家義大利餐廳訂了包廂，下週四晚上我們會用晚餐和簡短致詞來【慶祝】這次的成功。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special event or time with performances, food, or celebrations","c":"節慶；節日活動","s":"A: The hotels in the city center are almost fully booked for the second week of October, so do you know why so many visitors are coming? B: The annual food festival is taking place along the river that week, and thousands of tourists usually arrive to try dishes from over fifty local restaurants.","t":"A：市中心的飯店十月第二週幾乎都客滿了，你知道為什麼有這麼多遊客要來嗎？ B：那週河岸邊會舉辦一年一度的美食【節】，通常有成千上萬的遊客前來品嚐五十多家在地餐廳的料理。"},{"w":"party","p":"n.","d":"a social event where people meet to eat, drink, and have fun","c":"派對","s":"A: Mr. Chen is retiring at the end of this month after working here for thirty years, so is the department doing anything special for him? B: Yes, we are organizing a surprise farewell party in the staff lounge on his last afternoon, and his family has secretly agreed to join us.","t":"A：陳先生在這裡工作了三十年，這個月底就要退休了，部門有沒有為他準備什麼特別的活動？ B：有，我們正在籌辦一場驚喜歡送【派對】，就在他最後一天下午於員工休息室舉行，他的家人也已經偷偷答應要參加。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal public event held for a special purpose","c":"典禮；儀式","s":"A: The new factory in Taichung is ready to start production next month, so will the company hold any official event to mark the opening? B: The CEO will cut a red ribbon at the opening ceremony on Monday morning, and several local officials and reporters have been invited to watch.","t":"A：台中的新工廠下個月就要開始生產了，公司會舉辦任何正式活動來紀念開幕嗎？ B：執行長星期一早上會在開幕【典禮】上剪綵，也邀請了幾位地方官員和記者到場觀禮。"},{"w":"occasion","p":"n.","d":"a special event or an important time","c":"場合；特殊時刻","s":"A: I want to buy a nice pen for my boss because she just got promoted to regional director, but do you think a present like that is too expensive? B: Not at all, because a promotion is an important occasion, and a quality pen is something she will use at meetings every day.","t":"A：我想買一支好筆送老闆，因為她剛升任區域總監，但你覺得這樣的禮物會不會太貴？ B：一點也不會，因為升遷是很重要的【時刻】，而且一支好筆是她每天開會都會用到的東西。"},{"w":"anniversary","p":"n.","d":"the date each year when an important event happened in the past","c":"週年紀念","s":"A: Why is the lobby full of balloons and old photographs of the original office building this morning? B: Our company was founded exactly twenty years ago today, so management is marking the anniversary with a photo exhibition and a free lunch for every employee in the building.","t":"A：今天早上大廳為什麼擺滿了氣球和原本辦公大樓的老照片？ B：我們公司正好是二十年前的今天成立的，所以管理階層用攝影展和為大樓裡每位員工準備的免費午餐來紀念這個【週年紀念日】。"},{"w":"birthday","p":"n.","d":"the day each year when someone was born","c":"生日","s":"A: Everyone in the accounting office signed a big card this morning, so what is the reason for it? B: It is Linda's fortieth birthday today, and while she is at a meeting with the auditors, we are going to hide a chocolate cake in the kitchen to surprise her later.","t":"A：今天早上會計辦公室每個人都在一張大卡片上簽名，是什麼原因呢？ B：今天是琳達的四十歲【生日】，趁她在和查帳人員開會時，我們要把一個巧克力蛋糕藏在茶水間，晚點給她驚喜。"},{"w":"wedding","p":"n.","d":"a ceremony at which two people get married","c":"婚禮","s":"A: Could you cover my shifts at the front desk next Friday and Saturday, because I need to fly to Kaohsiung for a family event? B: Sure, I remember you mentioned that your younger sister is getting married, so please have a great time at the wedding and send my congratulations to the happy couple.","t":"A：你下週五和週六可以幫我代櫃檯的班嗎？因為我要飛去高雄參加家族活動。 B：當然，我記得你提過你妹妹要結婚了，祝你在【婚禮】上玩得開心，也幫我向這對新人道賀。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people for a social purpose","c":"聚會","s":"A: The new employees from our overseas branches seem a little lonely in the city, so how can we help them make friends quickly? B: The HR department is planning a casual gathering on the rooftop next Friday evening, with snacks, drinks, and simple games so that people can talk freely.","t":"A：海外分公司來的新員工在這城市好像有點孤單，我們要怎麼幫他們快點交到朋友？ B：人資部正計畫下週五晚上在頂樓辦一場輕鬆的【聚會】，有點心、飲料和簡單遊戲，讓大家可以自在聊天。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom or belief passed down over many years","c":"傳統","s":"A: Why does everyone in your office eat a big lunch in the meeting room on the last working day of every year? B: It is a long tradition that started when the founder ran the company, and even though we now have three hundred staff, we still keep it to thank everyone.","t":"A：為什麼你們辦公室每年最後一個上班日大家都在會議室吃大餐？ B：這是創辦人經營公司時就開始的悠久【傳統】，雖然我們現在有三百名員工，還是保留下來感謝大家。"},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"a usual way of behaving in a society or group","c":"習俗；風俗","s":"A: I am visiting our partners in Seoul next week for the first time, so is there anything I should know before the business dinner? B: It is a local custom to wait until the oldest person at the table starts eating, so be patient and follow what the others do during the meal.","t":"A：我下週第一次去首爾拜訪合作夥伴，商務晚宴之前有什麼該知道的嗎？ B：當地的【習俗】是要等桌上最年長的人先開動，所以用餐時要有耐心，跟著其他人的做法就對了。"},{"w":"toast","p":"n.","d":"the act of raising glasses and drinking to wish someone success or happiness","c":"敬酒；祝酒","s":"A: The managing director just stood up and lifted her glass at the end of the annual dinner, so what is she going to do? B: She is about to propose a toast to the whole sales team for their excellent results, so pick up your glass and get ready to drink with everyone.","t":"A：常務董事在年度晚宴尾聲站起來舉起酒杯，她要做什麼？ B：她要為整個業務團隊的優異成績提議【敬酒】，所以拿起你的杯子，準備和大家一起乾杯。"},{"w":"cheer","p":"v.","d":"to shout loudly to show you are happy or to support someone","c":"歡呼；喝采","s":"A: What was all that noise coming from the conference room during the lunch break today? B: The whole marketing department gathered to watch the live announcement of the design awards, and everyone started to cheer loudly when our team's poster won first prize.","t":"A：今天午休時會議室傳來的那些吵鬧聲是什麼？ B：整個行銷部聚在一起看設計獎的直播頒獎，當我們團隊的海報拿下首獎時，大家都大聲【歡呼】起來。"},{"w":"joyful","p":"adj.","d":"very happy; full of joy","c":"歡樂的；喜悅的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the CEO announced that everyone would get an extra week of paid holiday this year? B: The atmosphere in the hall was very joyful, with people laughing, hugging their coworkers, and immediately talking about where they wanted to travel in the summer.","t":"A：執行長宣布今年大家都多一週帶薪假時，員工反應如何？ B：大廳裡的氣氛非常【歡樂】，大家笑著擁抱同事，馬上就聊起夏天想去哪裡旅行。"},{"w":"festive","p":"adj.","d":"bright and cheerful because of a holiday or celebration","c":"節慶的；喜氣洋洋的","s":"A: The department store downtown looks completely different this December, so what has the management changed? B: They hung red lanterns and thousands of small lights across the entrance, and they play holiday songs all day, so the whole building feels really festive for shoppers.","t":"A：市中心那家百貨公司今年十二月看起來完全不一樣，管理部門改了什麼？ B：他們在入口處掛了紅燈籠和成千上萬顆小燈，還整天播放節日歌曲，讓整棟建築對購物者來說充滿【節慶氣氛】。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make a place look nicer by adding pretty things to it","c":"裝飾；布置","s":"A: The holiday party starts at six o'clock in the main hall, so what should the volunteers do after lunch? B: Please decorate the walls with paper stars and balloons, set up the tables near the windows, and check that the speakers work before the guests arrive.","t":"A：節日派對六點在大廳開始，志工們午餐後該做什麼？ B：請用紙星星和氣球【裝飾】牆面，把桌子擺在窗邊，並在賓客抵達前確認喇叭正常運作。"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"a thing used to make something look more attractive","c":"裝飾品","s":"A: The cleaning staff asked me what to do with all the paper lanterns and lights from last night's company party, so do you have any idea? B: Please put every decoration back into the large boxes in the storage room, because we plan to use them again at next year's event.","t":"A：清潔人員問我昨晚公司派對留下的紙燈籠和燈飾要怎麼處理，你有什麼想法嗎？ B：請把每一件【裝飾品】放回儲藏室的大箱子裡，因為我們打算明年的活動再用。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"pleasant sounds made by voices or instruments","c":"音樂","s":"A: The guests at the hotel's anniversary dinner seemed bored during the first hour, so how can we make the evening more lively? B: Let's ask the jazz band to start playing some cheerful music near the dance floor, because people usually relax and talk more once they hear a good rhythm.","t":"A：飯店週年晚宴前一小時賓客似乎很無聊，我們怎麼讓晚上更熱鬧？ B：請爵士樂團在舞池附近開始演奏一些歡快的【音樂】吧，因為人們聽到好節奏通常就會放鬆、聊得更多。"},{"w":"dance","p":"v.","d":"to move your body to music","c":"跳舞","s":"A: Is the year-end banquet just a formal dinner, or will there be some activities after the speeches are finished? B: After dessert, the lights will go down and a DJ will play popular songs, so anyone who wants to dance can join their coworkers on the floor until midnight.","t":"A：尾牙只是正式晚餐嗎？還是致詞結束後會有些活動？ B：甜點之後燈光會調暗，DJ會播放流行歌曲，想【跳舞】的人可以和同事一起到舞池直到午夜。"},{"w":"gift","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone, often on a special day","c":"禮物","s":"A: Our biggest client, Ms. Tanaka, is celebrating her company's tenth year in business, so what should we send to her office? B: I think a basket of high-quality Taiwanese tea would be a thoughtful gift, and we can attach a handwritten card from our president as well.","t":"A：我們最大的客戶田中女士的公司正在慶祝創立十週年，我們該送什麼到她辦公室？ B：我覺得一籃高品質的台灣茶會是一份貼心的【禮物】，我們也可以附上總裁的親筆卡片。"},{"w":"cake","p":"n.","d":"a sweet baked food made from flour, sugar, and eggs","c":"蛋糕","s":"A: We are holding a small celebration for the team's tenth project this afternoon, so have you ordered something sweet for everyone? B: Yes, the bakery across the street is making a large strawberry cake with our company logo on top, and they will deliver it at three o'clock.","t":"A：今天下午我們要為團隊第十個專案辦個小慶祝，你有幫大家訂甜點嗎？ B：有，對街的麵包店正在做一個上面有公司標誌的大草莓【蛋糕】，三點會送來。"},{"w":"fireworks","p":"n.","d":"colorful explosions in the sky used for celebrations","c":"煙火","s":"A: Why are so many people waiting outside the office buildings near Taipei 101 at almost midnight on December 31st? B: They are hoping to get a good view of the famous New Year's fireworks, which light up the sky for several minutes and are shown live on TV around the world.","t":"A：為什麼十二月三十一日快午夜時，台北101附近的辦公大樓外面有這麼多人在等？ B：他們希望能清楚看到著名的跨年【煙火】，煙火會照亮天空好幾分鐘，並在全世界的電視上現場直播。"},{"w":"crowd","p":"n.","d":"a large number of people together in one place","c":"人群","s":"A: Should we drive to the stadium for the city's victory parade tomorrow, or will it be difficult to find a parking space? B: The news says a huge crowd of about fifty thousand fans is expected, so taking the subway early in the morning is definitely the safer and faster choice.","t":"A：明天市區的勝利遊行我們要開車去體育場嗎？還是會很難找到停車位？ B：新聞說預計會有約五萬名球迷的龐大【人群】，所以一早搭捷運絕對是比較安全又快速的選擇。"},{"w":"invite","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone to come to an event","c":"邀請","s":"A: The company is opening its new branch in Hsinchu next month, so who should we ask to attend the opening event? B: We should invite our main suppliers, a few important customers, and the local reporters, and we need to mail the cards at least three weeks in advance.","t":"A：公司下個月要在新竹開新分店，開幕活動我們該請誰出席？ B：我們應該【邀請】主要供應商、幾位重要客戶和地方記者，而且至少要提前三週寄出卡片。"},{"w":"guest","p":"n.","d":"a person who is invited to an event or a home","c":"客人；賓客","s":"A: How many chairs should I set up in the ballroom for the award dinner on Saturday night? B: According to the final list from the events team, two hundred and twenty people have replied, and every guest will receive a name card, so please prepare ten extra seats for any last-minute visitors as well.","t":"A：週六晚上的頒獎晚宴，我在宴會廳要擺多少張椅子？ B：根據活動團隊的最終名單，共有兩百二十人回覆，每位【賓客】都會拿到名牌，所以也請多準備十個座位給臨時來的訪客。"},{"w":"host","p":"v.","d":"to organize an event and welcome the people who come","c":"主辦；招待","s":"A: Our department won the best customer service award this year, so where will the celebration dinner take place? B: The general manager has offered to host the dinner at her house in Yangmingshan, and she will even hire a chef to cook for the whole team that night.","t":"A：我們部門今年拿到最佳客服獎，慶功晚宴會在哪裡舉行？ B：總經理主動提議在她陽明山的家裡【主辦】晚宴，她甚至會請一位廚師當晚為整個團隊下廚。"},{"w":"enjoy","p":"v.","d":"to get pleasure from something","c":"享受；喜愛","s":"A: You took the new interns to the night market after their first week at work, so how did they like it? B: They seemed to enjoy the evening very much, because they tried a lot of local snacks, played some games, and kept taking photos until nearly eleven o'clock.","t":"A：實習生第一週上班後你帶他們去夜市，他們覺得怎麼樣？ B：他們似乎非常【享受】那個晚上，因為吃了很多在地小吃、玩了一些遊戲，還一直拍照到快十一點。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"special and easy to remember","c":"難忘的","s":"A: The customers who joined our boat tour for the company's anniversary sent many thank-you emails, so what did they like most? B: Many of them said it was a memorable trip, because the sunset over the harbor was beautiful and the staff served fresh seafood on the deck.","t":"A：參加我們公司週年遊船行程的客戶寄來很多感謝信，他們最喜歡什麼？ B：很多人說那是一趟【難忘的】旅程，因為港口的夕陽很美，員工還在甲板上提供新鮮海鮮。"},{"w":"together","p":"adv.","d":"with each other; in the same place","c":"一起；在一起","s":"A: The team has been working remotely for almost a year, so how can we improve communication between the members? B: I suggest that we bring everyone together for a weekend trip to Hualien, where they can share meals, go hiking, and get to know each other better.","t":"A：團隊遠距工作快一年了，我們要怎麼改善成員之間的溝通？ B：我建議把大家聚集【在一起】去花蓮週末旅遊，讓他們可以共享餐點、健行，彼此更加了解。"}]},{"unit":47,"theme":"Celebrity 名人","cards":[{"w":"impressed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling admiration because of what someone did","c":"印象深刻的","s":"A: How did the film director react when the young actress performed her scene in the rehearsal yesterday afternoon? B: He was so impressed by her natural performance and clear voice that he offered her a bigger role in the movie, and he even called her agent before lunch.","t":"A：昨天下午排練時，那位年輕女演員演出她的那場戲，電影導演有什麼反應？ B：他對她自然的表演和清晰的聲音感到非常【印象深刻】，所以給了她電影中更重要的角色，甚至在午餐前就打電話給她的經紀人。"},{"w":"renowned","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected by many people","c":"著名的；有名望的","s":"A: Who is giving the opening speech at the international food festival that our company is sponsoring next month in the convention center? B: A renowned chef from Paris will speak about healthy cooking, and many restaurant owners have already bought tickets because they want to hear her advice in person.","t":"A：下個月我們公司在會議中心贊助的國際美食節，開幕演講由誰負責？ B：一位來自巴黎的【著名】主廚會談健康烹飪，很多餐廳老闆已經買了票，因為他們想親耳聽她的建議。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give money, time, or ideas to help something","c":"貢獻；捐助","s":"A: The famous singer visited the children's hospital last weekend, but did she just take photos with the patients and leave quickly? B: No, she promised to contribute part of the money from her next concert tour to build a new playroom, and she also stayed for three hours to sing with the kids.","t":"A：那位知名歌手上週末去兒童醫院探訪，她是不是只和病人拍照就很快離開了？ B：不是，她承諾要把下一次巡迴演唱會的部分收入【捐助】出來蓋一間新的遊戲室，而且她還待了三個小時和孩子們一起唱歌。"},{"w":"prominent","p":"adj.","d":"important and well known","c":"重要的；著名的","s":"A: Why are so many reporters and photographers waiting outside the hotel lobby this morning, and should we warn our guests about the noise? B: A prominent business leader from Singapore is staying here during the trade conference, so yes, please tell guests that the main entrance may be busy until noon.","t":"A：今天早上為什麼有這麼多記者和攝影師在飯店大廳外面等，我們要提醒客人會有噪音嗎？ B：一位來自新加坡的【知名】企業領袖在貿易會議期間住在這裡，所以是的，請告訴客人正門到中午之前可能都會很擁擠。"},{"w":"ingenuity","p":"n.","d":"skill at thinking of new and clever ideas","c":"獨創力；巧思","s":"A: The cooking show host only had a small kitchen and very few ingredients on today's episode, so how did she make such a beautiful dinner? B: Her ingenuity really surprised everyone, because she turned leftover rice and a few vegetables into a colorful dish, and the audience clapped loudly when she finished.","t":"A：那位烹飪節目主持人今天這集只有一個小廚房和很少的食材，她怎麼做出這麼漂亮的晚餐？ B：她的【巧思】真的讓大家很驚訝，因為她把剩飯和幾樣蔬菜變成了一道色彩繽紛的菜，她做完時觀眾都大聲鼓掌。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"hard work and strong commitment to a goal","c":"奉獻；專注投入","s":"A: That famous tennis player has won so many tournaments over the past ten years, so what do you think is the secret of her long success? B: I think it is her dedication to training, because she practices six hours every day, follows a strict diet, and never skips her morning run, even on holidays.","t":"A：那位知名網球選手過去十年贏了這麼多錦標賽，你覺得她長久成功的秘訣是什麼？ B：我認為是她對訓練的【投入】，因為她每天練習六小時、遵守嚴格的飲食，而且即使在假日也從不跳過晨跑。"},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"strong excitement and interest","c":"熱情；熱忱","s":"A: The new host of our company's podcast has never worked in radio before, so are you worried about how listeners will react to her? B: Not at all, because her enthusiasm for technology is easy to hear in every episode, and the number of listeners has already doubled since she joined us in March.","t":"A：我們公司播客的新主持人以前從沒在廣播界工作過，你擔心聽眾對她的反應嗎？ B：一點也不，因為每一集都很容易聽出她對科技的【熱情】，而且自從她三月加入以來，聽眾人數已經增加了一倍。"},{"w":"lauded","p":"adj.","d":"highly praised in public","c":"備受讚揚的","s":"A: Is the new museum downtown worth visiting this weekend, or should I take my parents somewhere else when they come to Taipei? B: You should definitely go, because the museum was designed by a widely lauded architect from Japan, and newspapers have praised its bright galleries and peaceful rooftop garden.","t":"A：市中心的新博物館這週末值得去嗎？還是我爸媽來台北時應該帶他們去別的地方？ B：你一定要去，因為那座博物館是由一位來自日本、廣受【讚揚】的建築師設計的，報紙都稱讚它明亮的展廳和寧靜的屋頂花園。"},{"w":"demeanor","p":"n.","d":"the way a person looks and behaves","c":"舉止；態度","s":"A: The actor was asked many difficult questions about his private life at the press conference, so did he become angry with the journalists? B: No, his calm and polite demeanor impressed everyone in the room, and he simply smiled and said he would rather talk about his new film.","t":"A：那位演員在記者會上被問了很多關於他私生活的困難問題，他有對記者發脾氣嗎？ B：沒有，他冷靜又有禮貌的【舉止】讓在場的每個人都印象深刻，他只是微笑著說他比較想談談他的新電影。"},{"w":"integrity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being honest and having strong morals","c":"正直；誠信","s":"A: Why did the sports drink company choose that particular basketball player as the face of their new advertising campaign this year? B: They chose him mainly because of his integrity, since he has always been honest with fans, refused money to lose games, and treated his teammates with respect.","t":"A：那家運動飲料公司今年為什麼選那位籃球員當新廣告活動的代言人？ B：他們主要是因為他的【正直】才選他，因為他一向對球迷誠實、拒絕收錢打假球，而且尊重他的隊友。"},{"w":"pursuit","p":"n.","d":"the act of trying to get or achieve something","c":"追求","s":"A: The famous pianist left her comfortable job at a bank when she was twenty-five, so wasn't her family worried about that decision? B: They were nervous at first, but they supported her pursuit of a music career, and now they travel with her to concerts in Europe every summer.","t":"A：那位知名鋼琴家二十五歲時辭去了銀行的安穩工作，她的家人不擔心那個決定嗎？ B：他們一開始很緊張，但他們支持她對音樂事業的【追求】，現在他們每年夏天都陪她到歐洲參加音樂會。"},{"w":"converted","p":"adj.","d":"changed so it can be used for a different purpose","c":"改建的；改裝的","s":"A: Where is the TV star planning to hold the launch party for her new clothing brand, since the hotels downtown are all fully booked? B: She rented a converted factory near the river that is now a stylish event space, and it has enough room for two hundred guests and a small stage.","t":"A：那位電視明星打算在哪裡舉辦她新服裝品牌的發表派對？市中心的飯店都已經被訂滿了。 B：她租了河邊一間【改建的】工廠，現在是一個時尚的活動場地，有足夠的空間容納兩百位賓客和一個小舞台。"},{"w":"representative","p":"n.","d":"a person who speaks or acts for another person or group","c":"代表；代理人","s":"A: The famous actor can't come to the charity dinner tonight because his flight from Los Angeles was delayed, so who will accept the award for him? B: His representative from the agency will come instead, and she will read a short thank-you message that he wrote on the plane this morning.","t":"A：那位知名演員因為從洛杉磯來的班機延誤，今晚無法出席慈善晚宴，誰會替他領獎？ B：他經紀公司的【代表】會代替他出席，她會朗讀一段他今天早上在飛機上寫的簡短感謝詞。"},{"w":"professionalism","p":"n.","d":"the high skill and good behavior expected of a worker","c":"專業精神；專業素養","s":"A: The singer's concert was delayed for an hour because of the heavy rain last night, so were the fans angry when she finally walked on stage? B: Some were upset, but her professionalism helped a lot, because she apologized sincerely, explained the safety problem clearly, and then sang three extra songs for free.","t":"A：昨晚因為大雨，那位歌手的演唱會延遲了一個小時，她最後上台時歌迷生氣嗎？ B：有些人不高興，但她的【專業精神】幫了很大的忙，因為她真誠地道歉、清楚說明安全問題，然後還免費多唱了三首歌。"},{"w":"outstanding","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; much better than others","c":"傑出的；出色的","s":"A: Which employee is going to receive the special prize at the year-end party, since the managers met for a long time yesterday afternoon? B: They chose Linda from customer service, because her work this year was truly outstanding, and three of our biggest clients wrote letters to thank her personally.","t":"A：誰會在尾牙上拿到特別獎？經理們昨天下午開了很久的會。 B：他們選了客服部的琳達，因為她今年的工作表現真的很【傑出】，我們三位最大的客戶還親自寫信感謝她。"},{"w":"bias","p":"n.","d":"an unfair preference for or against someone or something","c":"偏見；偏袒","s":"A: Why did the TV station change the judges for the singing competition before the final round next Saturday night? B: Viewers complained about bias, because one judge was a close friend of a contestant, so the station replaced him to make sure every singer would be treated fairly.","t":"A：電視台為什麼在下週六晚上決賽前更換了歌唱比賽的評審？ B：觀眾抱怨有【偏袒】，因為其中一位評審是某位參賽者的好朋友，所以電視台換掉他，確保每位歌手都能被公平對待。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making people want to do or achieve something","c":"鼓舞人心的","s":"A: What did you think of the talk by that famous mountain climber at the leadership workshop yesterday afternoon in the main hall? B: It was really inspiring, because she described how she reached the top after failing twice, and many of my coworkers said they now want to set bigger goals.","t":"A：你覺得昨天下午在大禮堂領導力工作坊上那位知名登山家的演講怎麼樣？ B：真的很【鼓舞人心】，因為她講述了自己失敗兩次後如何登頂，我很多同事都說他們現在想設定更遠大的目標。"},{"w":"stardom","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a very famous performer","c":"明星地位；成名","s":"A: That young actor worked as a waiter in a small restaurant only two years ago, so how did his life change so quickly? B: He rose to stardom after his first movie became a huge hit online, and now fans follow him everywhere and companies pay him to advertise their products.","t":"A：那位年輕演員兩年前還在一家小餐廳當服務生，他的人生怎麼變化得這麼快？ B：他的第一部電影在網路上爆紅之後，他就一躍【成名】，現在粉絲到處跟著他，還有公司付錢請他代言產品。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be thankful for something; to value something","c":"感激；欣賞","s":"A: The famous author spent two hours signing books for our customers on Saturday, so should we send her something to say thank you? B: Yes, let's send flowers and a card, because I'm sure she will appreciate the gesture, and we hope she will visit our bookstore again when her next novel comes out.","t":"A：那位知名作家星期六花了兩個小時幫我們的顧客簽書，我們要送她什麼東西表示感謝嗎？ B：好啊，我們送花和卡片吧，我相信她會【感激】這份心意，而且希望她下一本小說出版時能再來我們書店。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: Why are there so many people standing outside the shopping mall entrance this afternoon, and is something wrong with the building? B: Nothing is wrong, but people are curious because a popular movie star is filming a scene inside, and everyone wants to see who it is before the security guards close the doors.","t":"A：今天下午為什麼有這麼多人站在購物中心門口？大樓出了什麼問題嗎？ B：沒有問題，只是大家都很【好奇】，因為一位當紅電影明星正在裡面拍戲，每個人都想在保全關門前看看是誰。"},{"w":"determined","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong wish to do something and not giving up","c":"下定決心的；堅決的","s":"A: The famous swimmer hurt her shoulder badly last year, so does she really plan to compete in the national games again this summer? B: Yes, she is determined to win another gold medal, so she has been doing physical therapy every morning and training in the pool every evening for months.","t":"A：那位知名游泳選手去年肩膀受了重傷，她今年夏天真的打算再參加全國運動會嗎？ B：是的，她【下定決心】要再拿一面金牌，所以好幾個月來她每天早上做物理治療，每天晚上在泳池訓練。"},{"w":"overcome","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in dealing with a problem or difficulty","c":"克服","s":"A: Our new spokesperson used to be very shy when she was young, so how did she become such a confident speaker on television? B: She worked hard to overcome her fear by joining a drama club in college, and she practiced speaking in front of small groups until she felt comfortable with large audiences.","t":"A：我們的新發言人小時候很害羞，她是怎麼變成在電視上這麼有自信的講者的？ B：她大學時參加戲劇社，努力【克服】她的恐懼，她練習在小團體面前說話，直到她面對大批觀眾也能感到自在。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that make a person who they are","c":"品格；性格","s":"A: The hotel manager said the famous guest in room 801 was very kind to the cleaning staff, so is he always like that? B: Yes, people who know him say he has strong character, because he treats everyone with the same respect, whether they are company presidents or waiters in a small café.","t":"A：飯店經理說801號房那位知名房客對清潔人員很友善，他一直都是這樣嗎？ B：是的，認識他的人都說他【品格】很好，因為不管對方是公司總裁還是小咖啡館的服務生，他都一樣尊重。"},{"w":"iconic","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and seen as a symbol of something","c":"標誌性的；具代表性的","s":"A: The tour group from Korea only has one free afternoon in Taipei next week, so which place should we take them to see? B: I think we should take them to Taipei 101, because it is the city's most iconic building, and they can enjoy the view from the top and shop in the mall below.","t":"A：韓國旅行團下週在台北只有一個自由的下午，我們應該帶他們去看哪裡？ B：我覺得應該帶他們去台北101，因為那是這座城市最具【代表性】的建築，他們可以在頂樓欣賞風景，再到樓下的購物中心逛街。"},{"w":"adore","p":"v.","d":"to love and admire someone very much","c":"非常喜愛；崇拜","s":"A: Why is the toy company paying so much money to put that cartoon voice actor in its new television commercial this winter? B: Young children adore her because she voices their favorite rabbit character, so the marketing team believes parents will buy more toys when kids hear her voice.","t":"A：那家玩具公司為什麼要花這麼多錢，請那位卡通配音員拍今年冬天的新電視廣告？ B：小孩子都很【喜愛】她，因為她為他們最喜歡的兔子角色配音，所以行銷團隊相信孩子聽到她的聲音時，父母就會買更多玩具。"},{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to respect and approve of someone or something","c":"欽佩；讚賞","s":"A: You have read every book written by that famous business leader, so what do you like most about him as a person? B: I really admire the way he started his company with almost no money, and even after becoming rich, he still spends weekends teaching free classes to young people.","t":"A：那位知名企業領袖寫的每本書你都讀過了，你最喜歡他這個人哪一點？ B：我真的很【欽佩】他幾乎沒有錢就創立了公司，而且即使變得富有之後，他週末仍然為年輕人免費上課。"},{"w":"ordeal","p":"n.","d":"a very difficult and unpleasant experience","c":"苦難；痛苦的經歷","s":"A: The famous travel blogger was stuck at the airport for two days because of the typhoon, so how is she feeling now that she is home? B: She is tired but fine, and she wrote a long post about the ordeal, describing how she slept on the floor and shared snacks with other passengers.","t":"A：那位知名旅遊部落客因為颱風被困在機場兩天，她現在回到家了，感覺怎麼樣？ B：她很累但還好，她寫了一篇長文描述這段【痛苦的經歷】，說她怎麼睡在地板上，還和其他旅客分享零食。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to wear clothes in photos or fashion shows; a good example to copy","c":"模特兒；模範","s":"A: The clothing company needs someone to wear the new winter jackets in next month's catalog, so have you found anyone yet? B: Yes, we hired a young model from Tainan who has worked for several big brands, and the photo shoot will take place at the beach next Tuesday if the weather is good.","t":"A：服裝公司需要有人穿新款冬季夾克拍下個月的型錄，你們找到人了嗎？ B：找到了，我們聘請了一位來自台南的年輕【模特兒】，她曾為好幾個大品牌工作過，如果天氣好，下週二會在海邊拍照。"},{"w":"awesome","p":"adj.","d":"very good or impressive","c":"很棒的；令人驚嘆的","s":"A: How was the concert you went to with your coworkers on Friday night at the new stadium near the train station? B: It was absolutely awesome, because the band played all their famous songs, the light show was amazing, and we even got a chance to take a photo with the drummer afterward.","t":"A：你星期五晚上和同事去火車站附近新體育館看的演唱會怎麼樣？ B：真的太【棒了】，因為樂團唱了所有的經典歌曲，燈光秀很精彩，我們之後甚至還有機會和鼓手合照。"}]},{"unit":48,"theme":"Challenge 挑戰","cards":[{"w":"difficulty","p":"n.","d":"a problem that makes something hard to do","c":"困難","s":"A: Why did the new accounting software take three weeks to install when the vendor promised it would only need a few days? B: Our technicians had real difficulty connecting it to the old customer database, because the two systems store dates in different formats, so they had to rewrite several files by hand.","t":"A：廠商保證只要幾天，為什麼新的會計軟體花了三週才安裝好？ B：我們的技術人員在把它連接到舊的客戶資料庫時遇到很大的【困難】，因為兩個系統儲存日期的格式不同，所以他們必須手動改寫好幾個檔案。"},{"w":"obstacle","p":"n.","d":"something that blocks you or makes progress hard","c":"障礙","s":"A: The board likes your plan to open a second store in Tainan, but what do you think could stop the project from moving forward this year? B: The biggest obstacle is the shortage of trained staff in that area, so we will need to start recruiting and training people at least six months before opening.","t":"A：董事會喜歡你在台南開第二家店的計畫，但你認為今年有什麼可能讓這個專案無法推進？ B：最大的【障礙】是那個地區缺乏受過訓練的員工，所以我們至少要在開幕前六個月開始招募和培訓人員。"},{"w":"problem","p":"n.","d":"a situation that causes trouble and needs to be fixed","c":"問題","s":"A: Several customers called this morning to say they could not log in to their online accounts, so do you know what is going on with the website? B: The IT team found a problem with the main server after last night's update, and they expect to fix it and restore full service before lunch.","t":"A：今天早上有好幾位顧客打電話來說他們無法登入線上帳戶，你知道網站怎麼了嗎？ B：IT團隊發現昨晚更新後主伺服器出了【問題】，他們預計在午餐前修好並恢復全部服務。"},{"w":"pressure","p":"n.","d":"a worried feeling caused by too much work or by demands from others","c":"壓力","s":"A: You have been staying at the office until ten o'clock every night this month, so is the new product launch really that difficult? B: Yes, the managers are under a lot of pressure from the head office to finish before the trade show, so everyone on the team is working extra hours.","t":"A：你這個月每天晚上都待在辦公室到十點，新產品上市真的那麼困難嗎？ B：是的，經理們承受總公司很大的【壓力】，必須在商展前完成，所以團隊裡每個人都在加班。"},{"w":"stressful","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried and tense","c":"有壓力的；令人緊張的","s":"A: How was your first week as the new customer service supervisor at the airport branch? B: It was very stressful because two flights were canceled during a typhoon, hundreds of angry passengers came to our desk at once, and I had to organize hotel rooms for all of them before midnight.","t":"A：你在機場分店擔任新的客服主管，第一週過得怎麼樣？ B：非常【有壓力】，因為颱風期間有兩班航班取消，數百名憤怒的乘客同時湧到我們的櫃檯，而我必須在午夜前幫他們全部安排好飯店房間。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, energy or skill","c":"要求高的；費力的","s":"A: I heard that you turned down the offer from the consulting firm last week, so may I ask why you decided not to take it? B: The salary was attractive, but the job was too demanding for me right now, since it required traveling abroad every week and answering clients' emails late at night.","t":"A：我聽說你上週拒絕了那家顧問公司的工作邀約，可以問你為什麼決定不接受嗎？ B：薪水很吸引人，但那份工作對我現在來說太【費力】了，因為它要求每週出國出差，還要在深夜回覆客戶的電子郵件。"},{"w":"tough","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to do or deal with","c":"艱難的；棘手的","s":"A: Our sales dropped by almost twenty percent in the last quarter, so how is the company going to explain this to the shareholders at next month's meeting? B: The CEO will admit it was a tough year for the whole industry, and then she will present her plan to cut costs and reach new markets in Asia.","t":"A：我們上一季的銷售額下滑了將近百分之二十，公司要怎麼在下個月的會議上向股東解釋？ B：執行長會承認這對整個產業來說是【艱難】的一年，然後她會提出削減成本並開拓亞洲新市場的計畫。"},{"w":"struggle","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to do something that is difficult","c":"努力；吃力應付","s":"A: Why does the new intern stay late every evening and ask so many questions during team meetings? B: She is a hard worker, but she seems to struggle with our complicated ordering system, so I have asked one of the senior clerks to sit with her for an hour each afternoon this week.","t":"A：為什麼新來的實習生每天晚上都留得很晚，而且在團隊會議中問這麼多問題？ B：她很認真，但她似乎在我們複雜的訂購系統上【很吃力】，所以我請了一位資深職員這週每天下午陪她一個小時。"},{"w":"setback","p":"n.","d":"something that delays progress or makes a situation worse","c":"挫折；阻礙","s":"A: Is the new shopping center near the train station still going to open in March as the developer announced last year? B: Unfortunately, there has been a serious setback, because heavy rain flooded the underground parking area last month, and the builders now think the opening will be delayed until summer.","t":"A：火車站附近的新購物中心還會像開發商去年宣布的那樣在三月開幕嗎？ B：很遺憾，出現了嚴重的【挫折】，因為上個月大雨淹沒了地下停車場，建商現在認為開幕會延到夏天。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something bad may happen","c":"風險","s":"A: Our competitor is selling a cheaper version of our printer, so should we lower our prices right away to keep our customers? B: That might help in the short term, but there is a real risk that we will lose money on every unit, so let's study the numbers carefully with the finance team first.","t":"A：我們的競爭對手在賣我們印表機的較便宜版本，我們該立刻降價來留住顧客嗎？ B：短期內可能有幫助，但真的有每台都虧錢的【風險】，所以我們先和財務團隊仔細研究數字吧。"},{"w":"overcome","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in dealing with a difficulty","c":"克服","s":"A: Your presentation to the investors was excellent, but I remember you used to feel very nervous about speaking in front of large groups, didn't you? B: Yes, I joined a public speaking club two years ago, and practicing every week with friendly members really helped me overcome my fear of talking to an audience.","t":"A：你對投資人的簡報非常出色，但我記得你以前在大群人面前說話會很緊張，不是嗎？ B：是的，我兩年前參加了一個演講社，每週和友善的社員一起練習，真的幫助我【克服】了對觀眾說話的恐懼。"},{"w":"cope","p":"v.","d":"to deal successfully with a difficult situation","c":"應付；處理","s":"A: Since the factory received that huge order from Germany, how are the workers on the production line handling the extra work? B: They are managing to cope with the heavy workload for now, but the manager plans to hire twenty temporary workers next month so that nobody has to work weekends.","t":"A：自從工廠接到德國那筆大訂單後，生產線上的工人如何處理額外的工作？ B：他們目前還能【應付】繁重的工作量，但經理打算下個月聘請二十名臨時工，這樣就沒有人必須週末上班。"},{"w":"effort","p":"n.","d":"the energy or hard work used to do something","c":"努力","s":"A: The client from Singapore just signed the contract for three more years, so what do you think finally convinced him to stay with us? B: I think he noticed the extra effort our team made to deliver every order on time, even during the busy holiday season when other suppliers were often late.","t":"A：新加坡的客戶剛簽了再延三年的合約，你認為最後是什麼說服他繼續和我們合作？ B：我想他注意到我們團隊為了準時交付每一筆訂單所付出的額外【努力】，即使在其他供應商常常延遲的忙碌假期季節也是如此。"},{"w":"persistence","p":"n.","d":"continuing to try even when something is difficult","c":"毅力；堅持不懈","s":"A: How did you finally get that big hotel chain to become our customer after they rejected our offer twice last year? B: It took a lot of persistence, because I kept calling their purchasing manager every few months, sent her samples of our new towels, and finally she agreed to meet me in person.","t":"A：去年那家大型連鎖飯店兩度拒絕我們的提案，你最後是怎麼讓他們成為我們的客戶的？ B：這需要很大的【毅力】，因為我每隔幾個月就打電話給他們的採購經理，寄給她我們新毛巾的樣品，最後她終於同意和我見面。"},{"w":"resilience","p":"n.","d":"the ability to recover quickly after something bad happens","c":"韌性；恢復力","s":"A: Many small restaurants in this neighborhood closed during the economic crisis, so how did your family's noodle shop manage to stay open? B: I think it was our resilience, because we quickly started a delivery service, changed the menu to cheaper dishes, and kept our loyal customers coming back every week.","t":"A：經濟危機期間這附近許多小餐廳都倒閉了，你們家的麵店是怎麼撐下來的？ B：我想是靠我們的【韌性】，因為我們很快就開始提供外送服務，把菜單換成較便宜的菜色，並讓忠實顧客每週持續回來光顧。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change in order to suit a new situation","c":"適應；調整","s":"A: You moved from the Taipei office to our branch in Toronto six months ago, so how are you finding life and work in Canada? B: At first the cold weather and the different working style were hard, but I am slowly learning to adapt to the new environment, and my colleagues have been very helpful.","t":"A：你六個月前從台北辦公室調到我們多倫多的分公司，你覺得在加拿大的生活和工作如何？ B：一開始寒冷的天氣和不同的工作方式很辛苦，但我正慢慢學著【適應】新環境，而且我的同事們一直很幫忙。"},{"w":"solution","p":"n.","d":"a way to solve a problem","c":"解決辦法","s":"A: Our meeting rooms are always fully booked, and teams keep arguing about who can use them, so what should we do about it? B: One possible solution is to install an online booking system, so every team can reserve a room in advance and see clearly which rooms are free each day.","t":"A：我們的會議室總是被訂滿，各團隊一直為了誰可以使用而爭吵，我們該怎麼辦？ B：一個可行的【解決辦法】是安裝線上預約系統，這樣每個團隊都能事先預約會議室，並清楚看到每天哪些會議室是空的。"},{"w":"failure","p":"n.","d":"a lack of success","c":"失敗","s":"A: Last year's online advertising campaign cost a lot of money, so why are we not using the same agency again this year? B: The campaign was a complete failure, because it attracted very few new customers, and the agency never sent us the reports they promised, so the director decided to look for a new partner.","t":"A：去年的網路廣告活動花了很多錢，為什麼我們今年不再找同一家廣告公司？ B：那次活動完全【失敗】，因為它吸引到的新顧客非常少，而且那家公司從來沒有寄給我們他們承諾的報告，所以主任決定另找新的合作夥伴。"},{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"something useful you learn from an experience","c":"教訓","s":"A: Last month the shipment to our biggest customer arrived a week late because nobody checked the address, so what did the team decide after that mistake? B: We all learned an important lesson from it, and now two people must check every shipping document carefully before any package leaves the warehouse.","t":"A：上個月寄給我們最大客戶的貨晚了一週才到，因為沒有人檢查地址，那次錯誤之後團隊決定了什麼？ B：我們都從中學到了重要的【教訓】，現在每個包裹離開倉庫前，都必須由兩個人仔細檢查所有運送文件。"},{"w":"growth","p":"n.","d":"an increase in size, amount or importance","c":"成長","s":"A: The figures in this report look very good, so which part of the business did best during the past twelve months? B: Our online store showed the strongest growth, with sales rising by thirty-five percent, mainly because more young customers started ordering our skincare products through their phones.","t":"A：這份報告的數字看起來非常好，過去十二個月哪個部分的業務表現最好？ B：我們的網路商店【成長】最強勁，銷售額上升了百分之三十五，主要是因為更多年輕顧客開始用手機訂購我們的保養品。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something good or useful","c":"機會","s":"A: The head office is looking for someone to manage the new branch in Vietnam for two years, so are you going to apply for the position? B: Yes, I think it is a great opportunity to gain international experience, learn a new language, and show the directors that I am ready for a bigger role.","t":"A：總公司正在找人管理越南的新分公司兩年，你會申請這個職位嗎？ B：會，我認為這是一個累積國際經驗、學習新語言，並向董事們證明我準備好擔任更重要角色的好【機會】。"},{"w":"brave","p":"adj.","d":"willing to do something difficult or frightening","c":"勇敢的","s":"A: I heard that Mr. Lin told the board directly that their plan to close the factory was a mistake, so how did they react? B: Everyone agreed it was a brave thing to do, because he could have lost his job, but in the end the directors listened and found a way to keep most of the workers.","t":"A：我聽說林先生直接告訴董事會他們關閉工廠的計畫是個錯誤，他們有什麼反應？ B：大家都認為這是很【勇敢】的舉動，因為他可能會因此丟掉工作，但最後董事們聽進去了，並找到辦法保留大部分的工人。"},{"w":"determined","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong wish to do something and not letting anything stop you","c":"有決心的；堅決的","s":"A: The new manager has only been here for two months, but the store already looks cleaner and sales are much higher, so how did she do it? B: She is very determined to make this branch the best in the city, so she meets the staff every morning and checks every shelf herself before the doors open.","t":"A：新經理才來兩個月，店裡就已經看起來更乾淨，銷售額也高了很多，她是怎麼做到的？ B：她非常【有決心】要讓這家分店成為全市最好的，所以她每天早上都和員工開會，並在開門前親自檢查每一個貨架。"},{"w":"positive","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful and confident; thinking about the good side","c":"正面的；積極的","s":"A: Our team lost the government contract that we worked on for six months, so how is everyone feeling in the office today? B: People are disappointed, of course, but the director told us to stay positive, because the client praised our proposal and promised to invite us to bid again next year.","t":"A：我們團隊失去了花了六個月爭取的政府合約，今天辦公室裡大家的心情如何？ B：大家當然很失望，但主任要我們保持【積極】，因為客戶稱讚了我們的提案，並答應明年會再邀請我們投標。"},{"w":"mentally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with the mind","c":"在心理上；精神上","s":"A: You have a job interview with the airline tomorrow morning, and you said there will be five people asking questions, so how are you getting ready? B: I have practiced my answers many times, and tonight I will go to bed early so that I feel mentally prepared and calm when I walk into the room.","t":"A：你明天早上要去航空公司面試，你說會有五個人問你問題，你怎麼準備？ B：我已經練習回答很多次了，今晚我會早點睡，這樣走進面試室時我就會覺得【心理上】已準備好而且很冷靜。"},{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"the achievement of something you planned or wanted","c":"成功","s":"A: The charity concert last weekend raised more money than any event we have organized before, so what do you think made it work so well? B: Its success came from careful planning, a popular local band that performed for free, and dozens of volunteers who sold tickets in shopping malls for a whole month.","t":"A：上週末的慈善音樂會募到的錢比我們以前辦的任何活動都多，你認為它為什麼這麼順利？ B：它的【成功】來自周詳的規劃、一個免費演出的當地人氣樂團，以及數十位志工整整一個月在購物中心賣票。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you can do something well","c":"信心；自信","s":"A: The new sales assistant seemed very shy when she started, but yesterday she gave an excellent product demonstration to a large group of buyers, didn't she? B: Yes, after three months of training and good feedback from customers, she has gained a lot of confidence, and now she enjoys speaking to people.","t":"A：新的銷售助理剛開始時看起來很害羞，但昨天她為一大群買家做了很出色的產品示範，不是嗎？ B：是的，經過三個月的訓練和顧客的好評，她增加了很多【自信】，現在她很喜歡和人說話。"}]},{"unit":49,"theme":"Change 改變","cards":[{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual order in which you do things every day","c":"例行公事；慣例","s":"A: Since the company moved our start time from nine to eight o'clock last month, how have you managed to get your children ready for school every morning? B: It was difficult at first, but we created a new morning routine where everyone packs their bags the night before and eats breakfast together at seven.","t":"A：自從公司上個月把上班時間從九點改到八點，你每天早上是怎麼讓孩子準備好上學的？ B：一開始很困難，但我們建立了一套新的早晨【例行程序】，每個人前一晚就把書包整理好，七點一起吃早餐。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something you do often, almost without thinking","c":"習慣","s":"A: I noticed you stopped buying coffee from the shop downstairs every afternoon, so did the doctor tell you to cut down on caffeine? B: No, I just wanted to save money for my trip to Japan, so I replaced that expensive habit with drinking tea that I bring from home in a bottle.","t":"A：我注意到你不再每天下午到樓下店裡買咖啡了，是醫生叫你少喝咖啡因嗎？ B：不是，我只是想為日本之旅存錢，所以我把那個昂貴的【習慣】換成喝我用瓶子從家裡帶來的茶。"},{"w":"challenging","p":"adj.","d":"difficult in a way that tests your ability","c":"具挑戰性的","s":"A: How do you feel about moving from the sales team to the new project management position that the director offered you last week? B: I think the job will be quite challenging because I have to lead twelve people and manage a tight budget, but I am excited to learn new skills and grow.","t":"A：你對於從業務團隊轉到主任上週提供給你的新專案管理職位感覺如何？ B：我覺得這份工作會相當【具挑戰性】，因為我必須帶領十二個人並管理緊縮的預算，但我很期待學習新技能並成長。"},{"w":"afraid","p":"adj.","d":"feeling fear or worry about something","c":"害怕的；擔心的","s":"A: Why didn't Tom say anything during the meeting when the manager asked for opinions about the new working schedule? B: He told me later that he was afraid that his ideas would sound silly, because he only joined the company two weeks ago and does not know everyone yet.","t":"A：經理在會議中詢問大家對新工作時間表的意見時，湯姆為什麼什麼都沒說？ B：他後來告訴我，他【害怕】自己的想法聽起來很蠢，因為他兩週前才進公司，還不認識每個人。"},{"w":"resist","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to accept something or try to stop it","c":"抗拒；抵抗","s":"A: Several older workers in the warehouse are unhappy about the new scanning system, so what is the best way to help them accept it? B: People often resist changes when they do not understand the reasons, so let's hold a short training session and show them how the system will save them time.","t":"A：倉庫裡好幾位年長員工對新的掃描系統不滿，幫助他們接受它最好的方法是什麼？ B：人們不了解原因時常常會【抗拒】改變，所以我們來辦一場簡短的訓練課程，讓他們看看這套系統如何幫他們節省時間。"},{"w":"frequently","p":"adv.","d":"often; many times","c":"頻繁地；經常","s":"A: Do you know why the printer on the third floor keeps breaking down, even though the technician repaired it last month? B: The marketing team uses it very frequently to print large posters and brochures, so I think we should buy a stronger machine instead of fixing this old one again.","t":"A：你知道為什麼三樓的印表機一直故障嗎？明明技術人員上個月才修好。 B：行銷團隊非常【頻繁地】用它來印大型海報和手冊，所以我認為我們應該買一台更耐用的機器，而不是再修這台舊的。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time or forever","c":"永久的；長期的","s":"A: You have been working at the front desk as a temporary staff member for six months, so has the hotel offered you a contract yet? B: Yes, the manager called me yesterday and said they want to give me a permanent position starting in January, with health insurance and paid holidays.","t":"A：你在櫃檯當臨時員工已經六個月了，飯店給你合約了嗎？ B：有，經理昨天打電話給我，說他們想從一月開始給我一個【長期正式的】職位，有健康保險和帶薪假。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"a move to a higher job or rank","c":"升職；晉升","s":"A: Congratulations, I heard you will be the new head of the customer service department next month, so how did you hear the news? B: Thank you, my boss invited me to lunch on Friday and told me about the promotion, and she also said my salary will increase by fifteen percent.","t":"A：恭喜，我聽說你下個月要成為客服部門的新主管，你是怎麼得知消息的？ B：謝謝，我老闆週五請我吃午餐，告訴我【升職】的事，她還說我的薪水會增加百分之十五。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change your behavior to fit a new situation","c":"適應","s":"A: The company is moving our office from Taipei to Kaohsiung next spring, so are you worried about living in a new city? B: A little, but I have moved several times before, and I usually adapt quickly to new places by joining local clubs and exploring the neighborhood on weekends.","t":"A：公司明年春天要把辦公室從台北搬到高雄，你擔心住在新城市嗎？ B：有一點，但我以前搬過好幾次家，我通常會參加當地社團、週末探索街坊，很快就【適應】新的地方。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to create something new or make it better over time","c":"開發；發展","s":"A: Our online shop is getting more orders from customers in Japan and Korea, so what should the IT team focus on this year? B: I think they should develop a mobile app in Japanese and Korean, because most of these customers shop on their phones during their train rides to work.","t":"A：我們的網路商店接到越來越多日本和韓國顧客的訂單，IT團隊今年應該把重點放在哪裡？ B：我認為他們應該【開發】一個日文和韓文的手機應用程式，因為這些顧客大多在搭火車上班時用手機購物。"},{"w":"decade","p":"n.","d":"a period of ten years","c":"十年","s":"A: The town looks so different from the photos in the lobby, so how long has this hotel been here? B: It opened in the 1980s, and during the last decade the area has changed a lot, with new shopping malls, office towers, and a subway station built right across the street.","t":"A：這個小鎮和大廳裡的照片看起來差好多，這間飯店在這裡多久了？ B：它在1980年代開幕，在過去【十年】裡，這一帶改變了很多，蓋了新的購物中心、辦公大樓，對街還蓋了一座地鐵站。"},{"w":"metamorphosis","p":"n.","d":"a complete change into something very different","c":"蛻變；徹底轉變","s":"A: I visited your restaurant again last night, and I could hardly believe it was the same place after the renovation, so who designed the new interior? B: A young designer from Tainan planned the whole metamorphosis, turning our dark old dining room into a bright, modern space with plants, large windows, and an open kitchen.","t":"A：我昨晚又去了你的餐廳，裝修後我幾乎不敢相信是同一個地方，新的室內是誰設計的？ B：一位台南的年輕設計師規劃了整個【蛻變】，把我們陰暗的老用餐區變成一個有植物、大窗戶和開放式廚房的明亮現代空間。"},{"w":"secure","p":"v.","d":"to get something important after a lot of effort","c":"獲得；爭取到","s":"A: The factory almost closed last year because of falling orders, so how did it manage to stay open and keep all its workers? B: The new sales director worked very hard to secure a three-year contract with a large car company, which brought in enough money to buy new machines.","t":"A：去年工廠因為訂單下滑差點關門，它是怎麼撐下去並保住所有員工的？ B：新的業務總監非常努力地【爭取到】一份與大型汽車公司簽的三年合約，帶進了足夠的錢買新機器。"},{"w":"incumbent","p":"n.","d":"the person who holds an official position now","c":"現任者","s":"A: Do you think the city will finally build the new bike lanes after the mayor election next month? B: It depends on who wins, because the incumbent has promised to finish the project, but the other candidate says the money should go to repairing old roads and public schools instead.","t":"A：你認為下個月市長選舉後，市政府終於會蓋新的自行車道嗎？ B：要看誰贏，因為【現任者】承諾要完成這個計畫，但另一位候選人說這筆錢應該改用來修舊道路和公立學校。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make something better","c":"改善；提升","s":"A: Our customers have complained that the website is slow and confusing, so what are we going to do about it this quarter? B: We have hired an outside company to improve the design, and they promise that people will be able to find products and pay in less than two minutes.","t":"A：顧客抱怨網站又慢又難用，這一季我們打算怎麼處理？ B：我們請了一家外部公司來【改善】設計，他們保證大家能在兩分鐘內找到產品並付款。"},{"w":"lazy","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to work or make an effort","c":"懶惰的","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to change the cleaning company that looks after our office building? B: Some of the old staff were quite lazy and often left the kitchen dirty and the trash bins full, so many employees complained, and the manager found a more reliable company last week.","t":"A：經理為什麼決定更換負責我們辦公大樓的清潔公司？ B：之前有些員工相當【懶惰】，常常讓廚房髒亂、垃圾桶滿出來，所以很多員工抱怨，經理上週就找了一家更可靠的公司。"},{"w":"awkward","p":"adj.","d":"uncomfortable or embarrassing","c":"尷尬的；不自在的","s":"A: How was your first day at the new branch after you transferred from the head office? B: It felt a little awkward in the morning because nobody knew my name and I sat alone at lunch, but in the afternoon my team leader introduced me to everyone, and things became much easier.","t":"A：你從總公司調到新分店後的第一天怎麼樣？ B：早上感覺有點【尷尬】，因為沒人知道我的名字，午餐時我一個人坐，但下午組長把我介紹給大家，事情就輕鬆多了。"},{"w":"struggle","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to do something difficult","c":"努力掙扎；奮鬥","s":"A: Many small bookstores in this neighborhood have closed in the past few years, so how is your shop doing? B: We still struggle to pay the rent some months because more people buy books online, but we have started holding reading events and selling coffee, which brings in new customers.","t":"A：這一帶很多小書店在過去幾年關門了，你的店經營得如何？ B：有些月份我們還是【很吃力地】付房租，因為越來越多人在網路上買書，但我們開始舉辦讀書活動和賣咖啡，吸引了新顧客。"},{"w":"boost","p":"v.","d":"to increase or improve something","c":"提升；促進","s":"A: Sales of our winter jackets have been lower than expected this year, so what can we do before the season ends? B: The marketing team suggests a weekend discount and a social media contest, which should boost sales quickly and help us clear the stock before the spring collection arrives.","t":"A：我們的冬季外套今年銷售比預期差，在季節結束前我們能做什麼？ B：行銷團隊建議週末打折和社群媒體比賽，應該能迅速【提升】銷售量，幫我們在春季新品到貨前清掉庫存。"},{"w":"recognize","p":"v.","d":"to know someone or something because you have seen it before","c":"認出；辨認","s":"A: You have not been back to your hometown for fifteen years, so did it still look the same when you visited last weekend? B: Not at all, I could hardly recognize the main street because the old market was replaced by a shopping center and most of the small shops had new names.","t":"A：你已經十五年沒回家鄉了，上週末回去時還是一樣嗎？ B：完全不一樣，我幾乎無法【認出】大街，因為舊市場被購物中心取代，大多數小店也都換了新名字。"},{"w":"catch","p":"v.","d":"to get on a bus, train, or plane in time","c":"趕上；搭上","s":"A: Since the bus company changed its timetable last week, how have you been getting to the office on time? B: I now leave home twenty minutes earlier to catch the 7:15 bus, because the next one does not come until 7:50, and that would make me late for the morning meeting.","t":"A：自從公車公司上週更改時刻表後，你都怎麼準時到公司？ B：我現在提早二十分鐘出門去【趕上】7點15分的公車，因為下一班要到7點50分才來，那會讓我晨會遲到。"},{"w":"positive","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful and confident; showing approval","c":"積極的；正面的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the CEO announced that everyone could work from home two days a week? B: Most people were very positive about it, because they will save time on commuting, but a few team leaders worried that it might be harder to hold meetings and share ideas.","t":"A：執行長宣布每個人每週可以在家工作兩天時，員工的反應如何？ B：大多數人對此非常【正面】，因為能節省通勤時間，但有幾位組長擔心開會和交流想法可能會變得比較困難。"},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen and impossible to stop","c":"不可避免的","s":"A: Do you think the bank will close more of its small branches now that so many customers use the mobile app? B: I am afraid it is inevitable, because fewer people visit the branches each year, and the company says it needs to cut costs and invest more money in online services.","t":"A：既然這麼多顧客使用手機應用程式，你認為銀行會關閉更多小分行嗎？ B：恐怕這是【無可避免的】，因為每年去分行的人越來越少，而公司說需要削減成本，把更多錢投入線上服務。"},{"w":"transformation","p":"n.","d":"a complete change in form or character","c":"轉變；轉型","s":"A: The old textile factory near the river has been empty for years, so what is the city planning to do with it? B: The city has hired an architect to lead its transformation into a cultural center with art studios, a small theater, and a market where local farmers can sell vegetables on weekends.","t":"A：河邊那間舊紡織廠已經空了好幾年，市政府打算怎麼處理？ B：市政府聘請了一位建築師主導它的【轉型】，把它變成一個有藝術工作室、小劇場和週末讓當地農民賣菜的市集的文化中心。"},{"w":"favorable","p":"adj.","d":"good and likely to help something succeed","c":"有利的；良好的","s":"A: The weather has been terrible this month, so do you think the outdoor company sports day can still happen on Saturday? B: The forecast looks favorable for the weekend, with sunny skies and light wind, so we will go ahead with the plan, but we will also book the gym in case it rains.","t":"A：這個月天氣很糟，你覺得公司戶外運動會週六還能舉行嗎？ B：週末的天氣預報看起來很【有利】，晴天又微風，所以我們會照計畫進行，但也會預訂體育館以防下雨。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed because you cannot do what you want","c":"令人沮喪的","s":"A: You look tired today, so did something happen with the new accounting software that the company installed on Monday? B: Yes, it has been really frustrating because the program keeps freezing whenever I try to save a report, and I had to type the same numbers three times this morning.","t":"A：你今天看起來很累，週一公司安裝的新會計軟體出了什麼事嗎？ B：對，真的很【令人沮喪】，因為每次我要儲存報表程式就當掉，我今天早上同樣的數字打了三次。"},{"w":"transitional","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a change from one state to another","c":"過渡的","s":"A: The new manager starts in March, but our current manager leaves at the end of January, so who will lead the team in February? B: During this transitional period, the senior supervisor will take care of daily decisions, and both managers will also hold a video call every week to share important information.","t":"A：新經理三月上任，但現任經理一月底就離職，那二月誰來帶領團隊？ B：在這段【過渡】期間，資深主管會處理日常決策，兩位經理也會每週開一次視訊會議交接重要資訊。"},{"w":"inquisitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to learn and asking many questions","c":"好奇的；愛發問的","s":"A: The new intern asks so many questions about every department, so do you think it bothers the other staff members? B: Not at all, most people like how inquisitive she is, because her questions show that she really wants to learn how the company works, and some of them even helped us find problems.","t":"A：新來的實習生對每個部門都問好多問題，你覺得會打擾到其他員工嗎？ B：一點也不，大多數人都喜歡她這麼【好奇好問】，因為她的問題顯示她真的想了解公司如何運作，有些問題甚至幫我們發現了問題。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"極有趣的；引人入勝的","s":"A: How was the conference in Singapore that you attended last week with the research team? B: It was really fascinating, especially a talk about how robots are changing hospitals, and I took so many notes that I want to share them with everyone at our team meeting on Thursday afternoon.","t":"A：你上週和研究團隊去參加的新加坡會議怎麼樣？ B：真的非常【引人入勝】，尤其是一場關於機器人如何改變醫院的演講，我做了好多筆記，想在星期四下午的團隊會議上跟大家分享。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making people feel excited and want to do something good","c":"鼓舞人心的","s":"A: Why did so many employees sign up for the volunteer program after the company's annual meeting? B: The guest speaker gave a very inspiring talk about how she changed her life by helping children in poor villages, and many people said they wanted to do something meaningful too.","t":"A：公司年會後，為什麼這麼多員工報名志工計畫？ B：特別來賓發表了一場非常【鼓舞人心】的演講，講她如何透過幫助貧困村莊的孩子改變自己的人生，很多人說他們也想做些有意義的事。"},{"w":"regrettable","p":"adj.","d":"that you feel sorry about; unfortunate","c":"令人遺憾的","s":"A: The online store sent hundreds of customers the wrong items during the holiday sale, so what did the company say about the problem? B: The CEO called the mistake very regrettable and promised that every customer will receive a full refund, free shipping, and a discount code for their next order.","t":"A：網路商店在假期特賣期間寄錯了幾百位顧客的商品，公司對這個問題怎麼說？ B：執行長稱這個錯誤非常【令人遺憾】，並承諾每位顧客都會獲得全額退款、免運費和下次訂購的折扣碼。"}]},{"unit":50,"theme":"Changing Room 更衣室","cards":[{"w":"fitting room","p":"n.","d":"a small room in a shop where you try on clothes","c":"試衣間","s":"A: I want to check whether these dark blue trousers suit me before I pay, but I can't see anywhere private in this busy department store, so where should I go? B: The fitting room is just behind the shoe section on the second floor, and a staff member there will give you a number card for each item you take in.","t":"A：我想在付款前看看這條深藍色褲子適不適合我，但在這間繁忙的百貨公司裡我看不到任何隱密的地方，我該去哪裡？ B：【試衣間】就在二樓鞋區的後面，那裡的工作人員會為你帶進去的每件衣物發一張號碼牌。"},{"w":"locker room","p":"n.","d":"a room where people change clothes before or after sports","c":"（運動場所的）更衣室","s":"A: After the company football match on Saturday afternoon, where can the players take a shower and get dressed before we all go out for dinner together? B: The sports center has a large locker room next to the main field, with hot showers and plenty of space, so everyone can get ready there in about twenty minutes.","t":"A：週六下午公司足球賽結束後，球員們可以在哪裡沖澡換衣服，然後大家再一起去吃晚餐？ B：運動中心主球場旁邊有一間很大的【更衣室】，有熱水淋浴和充足的空間，所以大家大約二十分鐘就能在那裡準備好。"},{"w":"locker","p":"n.","d":"a small cupboard with a lock for keeping your things safe","c":"置物櫃","s":"A: I'm going to the gym straight from the office tonight, but I'm worried about leaving my laptop and wallet somewhere unsafe while I exercise, so what do you suggest? B: Each member can rent a small locker with a key for just fifty dollars a month, and it is large enough for a laptop bag and a jacket.","t":"A：我今晚要從辦公室直接去健身房，但我擔心運動時把筆電和錢包放在不安全的地方，你有什麼建議？ B：每位會員每個月只要五十元就可以租一個附鑰匙的小【置物櫃】，空間大到可以放下筆電包和一件外套。"},{"w":"mirror","p":"n.","d":"a piece of glass in which you can see yourself","c":"鏡子","s":"A: The customers keep complaining that they cannot see how the clothes look from behind after they try them on, so how can we solve this problem cheaply? B: Let's put a tall mirror on the back wall of each changing area, so people can turn around and check the whole outfit without asking a salesperson for help.","t":"A：顧客一直抱怨試穿後看不到衣服背面的樣子，我們要怎麼便宜地解決這個問題？ B：我們在每個更衣區的後牆裝一面高的【鏡子】，這樣大家可以轉身檢查整套服裝，不必請店員幫忙。"},{"w":"bench","p":"n.","d":"a long seat for two or more people","c":"長凳","s":"A: Some older customers have told us that they feel tired while they wait for their family members outside the changing rooms, so is there anything simple we can do? B: We could place a long wooden bench along the wall near the entrance, so they can sit down comfortably and keep an eye on the shopping bags.","t":"A：有些年長顧客告訴我們，他們在更衣室外等家人時覺得很累，有什麼簡單的方法可以改善嗎？ B：我們可以在入口附近沿著牆放一張長的木製【長凳】，讓他們可以舒服地坐著，同時看顧購物袋。"},{"w":"curtain","p":"n.","d":"a piece of cloth that hangs down to cover a window or an opening","c":"簾子；窗簾","s":"A: One of the changing rooms in the women's section doesn't close properly anymore, and a customer felt uncomfortable using it this morning, so what exactly is wrong with it? B: The thick curtain that covers the entrance is too short and keeps sliding open, so I have already ordered a longer one that should arrive on Thursday.","t":"A：女裝區有一間更衣室關不好了，今天早上有位顧客用起來覺得很不自在，到底是哪裡出了問題？ B：遮住入口的那條厚【簾子】太短，而且一直滑開，所以我已經訂了一條更長的，應該週四會到。"},{"w":"door","p":"n.","d":"the thing you open and close to go into a room","c":"門","s":"A: The new changing rooms look really modern, but I noticed that several customers had trouble locking themselves in while they were trying things on, so what is the issue? B: The lock on each door is placed too high for shorter people to reach easily, so the builder will come back next week and move them lower.","t":"A：新的更衣室看起來很現代，但我注意到有好幾位顧客試穿時很難把自己鎖在裡面，問題出在哪裡？ B：每扇【門】上的鎖裝得太高，個子較矮的人不容易搆到，所以施工人員下週會回來把鎖裝低一點。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone and not seen by other people","c":"隱私","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to replace all the old plastic panels in the changing area with solid wooden walls, even though it cost the store a lot of money? B: Many shoppers complained that people walking by could see inside, and she believes every customer deserves complete privacy while trying on clothes.","t":"A：為什麼經理決定把更衣區所有的舊塑膠隔板換成實心木牆，即使這花了店裡很多錢？ B：許多顧客抱怨路過的人看得到裡面，而她認為每位顧客在試穿衣服時都應該享有完全的【隱私】。"},{"w":"clothes","p":"n.","d":"things you wear, such as shirts and trousers","c":"衣服","s":"A: The hotel staff change into their work uniforms when they arrive every morning, so where should they leave the things they wore on the way to work? B: There is a staff room on the basement level where everyone can hang their own clothes on a rail and pick them up again at the end of the shift.","t":"A：飯店員工每天早上到班後會換上工作制服，那他們上班途中穿的東西要放在哪裡？ B：地下室有一間員工休息室，每個人都可以把自己的【衣服】掛在衣架桿上，下班時再拿回來。"},{"w":"outfit","p":"n.","d":"a set of clothes worn together","c":"一套服裝","s":"A: I have an important job interview at a bank next Tuesday, but I'm not sure what to wear, so could you come shopping with me this weekend? B: Of course, I think a dark jacket with matching trousers and simple shoes would make a smart and professional outfit, and the mall downtown is having a sale.","t":"A：我下週二在一家銀行有個重要的面試，但我不確定要穿什麼，你這個週末可以陪我去逛街嗎？ B：當然，我覺得深色外套配上同色系長褲和簡單的鞋子，會是一套俐落又專業的【服裝】，而且市中心的購物中心正在特價。"},{"w":"try on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put on clothes to see if they fit or look good","c":"試穿","s":"A: I really like the gray coat in the window, but this brand often makes its clothes a little small, so should I just buy it online to save time? B: I think you should try on the coat in the store first, because the changing rooms are free right now and you can return it easily if it feels wrong.","t":"A：我很喜歡櫥窗裡那件灰色大衣，但這個牌子的衣服常常偏小，我是不是直接在網路上買比較省時間？ B：我覺得你應該先在店裡【試穿】那件大衣，因為現在更衣室剛好沒人，而且如果覺得不對也很容易退貨。"},{"w":"change","p":"v.","d":"to take off your clothes and put on different ones","c":"換（衣服）","s":"A: Our client meeting finishes at five, and the charity dinner starts at six on the other side of the city, so will we have enough time to get ready? B: Yes, the hotel has agreed to give us a small room near the lobby, so we can quickly change into our evening clothes there and take a taxi straight to the event.","t":"A：我們的客戶會議五點結束，而慈善晚宴六點在城市的另一頭開始，我們有足夠的時間準備嗎？ B：有，飯店同意在大廳附近給我們一間小房間，我們可以在那裡迅速【換】上晚禮服，然後直接搭計程車去會場。"},{"w":"size","p":"n.","d":"how big or small something is, such as clothes or shoes","c":"尺寸","s":"A: The blue shirt I ordered for the team photo is much too small around the shoulders, so do you think the store will let me exchange it? B: Yes, as long as you keep the receipt and the label, they will happily give you a larger size, and they usually have extra stock in the back room.","t":"A：我為團體照訂的藍色襯衫肩膀太小了，你覺得店家會讓我換嗎？ B：會的，只要你保留收據和標籤，他們會很樂意給你大一號的【尺寸】，而且他們後面的倉庫通常有額外庫存。"},{"w":"fit","p":"v.","d":"to be the right size and shape for someone","c":"合身","s":"A: You bought those black trousers for the company dinner last month, so why haven't you worn them to the office yet? B: Unfortunately, they don't fit me well anymore because I've been eating so many snacks at my desk during busy weeks, so I'll take them to a tailor this weekend to have them made bigger.","t":"A：你上個月為了公司晚宴買了那條黑色長褲，為什麼還沒穿來辦公室？ B：可惜它已經不太【合身】了，因為忙碌的那幾週我在座位上吃了太多零食，所以這個週末我會拿去給裁縫改大一點。"},{"w":"tight","p":"adj.","d":"fitting your body very closely, often too closely","c":"緊的","s":"A: You look a little uncomfortable in that new suit, so is something wrong with it, or are you just nervous about giving the presentation this afternoon? B: To be honest, the jacket feels quite tight around my arms, so I can hardly lift them, and I should have tried a bigger one before I bought it.","t":"A：你穿那套新西裝看起來有點不自在，是衣服有問題，還是你只是對今天下午的簡報感到緊張？ B：老實說，這件外套的手臂部分感覺很【緊】，我幾乎舉不起手臂，我買之前應該先試穿大一號的。"},{"w":"loose","p":"adj.","d":"too big and not fitting closely","c":"寬鬆的；鬆的","s":"A: The new warehouse uniforms arrived this morning, but several workers say they are uncomfortable, so what seems to be the main problem with them? B: The trousers are so loose around the waist that people keep pulling them up while they carry boxes, which could be dangerous near the heavy machines.","t":"A：新的倉庫制服今天早上送到了，但有好幾位工人說穿起來不舒服，主要問題是什麼？ B：褲子腰部太【鬆】了，大家搬箱子時一直要把褲子往上拉，在重型機器附近可能很危險。"},{"w":"comfortable","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel relaxed, with no pain","c":"舒適的","s":"A: Our team will be walking around the trade fair for about eight hours tomorrow, meeting suppliers and visiting booths, so what kind of shoes should I wear? B: Choose something soft and comfortable instead of your new leather shoes, because the halls are huge and your feet will hurt badly by lunchtime otherwise.","t":"A：我們團隊明天要在商展裡走大約八個小時，和供應商見面並參觀攤位，我該穿什麼鞋子？ B：選一雙柔軟又【舒適】的鞋，不要穿你的新皮鞋，因為展館很大，不然到午餐時間你的腳就會很痛。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: I'd like to buy a few shirts for my business trip, so do you think Saturday afternoon is a good time to visit the shopping mall near the station? B: I wouldn't go then, because the stores are always crowded on weekends and you might wait twenty minutes for a changing room, so try a weekday evening instead.","t":"A：我想為出差買幾件襯衫，你覺得週六下午去車站附近的購物中心是好時機嗎？ B：我不會那時候去，因為週末店裡總是很【擁擠】，你可能要等二十分鐘才有更衣室，改在平日晚上去吧。"},{"w":"empty","p":"adj.","d":"with no people or things inside","c":"空的","s":"A: The staff changing room downstairs is usually full of people at eight in the morning, so when is the best time for me to use it before my shift? B: It is almost always empty around seven thirty, because most of the early workers have already gone upstairs and the others don't arrive until later.","t":"A：樓下的員工更衣室早上八點通常擠滿了人，我上班前什麼時候使用最好？ B：七點半左右那裡幾乎都是【空的】，因為大部分早班員工已經上樓了，其他人則要晚一點才會到。"},{"w":"clean","p":"adj.","d":"not dirty","c":"乾淨的","s":"A: A gym member wrote an angry online review saying that the shower area smelled bad last weekend, so how should we respond to make customers trust us again? B: Let's hire an extra cleaner for the weekends and promise that the changing area will be kept clean and dry at all times, then reply politely to the review.","t":"A：一位健身房會員在網路上寫了一則憤怒的評論，說上週末淋浴區很臭，我們該如何回應才能讓顧客重新信任我們？ B：我們週末多請一位清潔人員，並承諾更衣區隨時保持【乾淨】和乾燥，然後禮貌地回覆那則評論。"},{"w":"messy","p":"adj.","d":"untidy, with things in the wrong places","c":"凌亂的","s":"A: The store manager looked very unhappy after she checked the changing rooms at closing time yesterday, so did something go wrong during the evening shift? B: Yes, the rooms were really messy, with shirts and jeans lying on the floor everywhere, because nobody had time to collect them during the busy sale.","t":"A：店長昨天打烊時檢查完更衣室後看起來很不高興，晚班是不是出了什麼問題？ B：是的，那些房間真的很【凌亂】，到處都是丟在地上的襯衫和牛仔褲，因為在忙碌的特賣期間沒有人有時間收。"},{"w":"hook","p":"n.","d":"a curved piece of metal or plastic for hanging things on","c":"掛鉤","s":"A: Customers keep putting their coats and handbags on the floor of the changing rooms, which makes the area look dirty, so how can we improve this? B: We should fix a metal hook on the wall inside each room, so people have a proper place to hang their things while they are trying on clothes.","t":"A：顧客一直把外套和手提包放在更衣室地上，讓那裡看起來很髒，我們該如何改善？ B：我們應該在每間更衣室的牆上裝一個金屬【掛鉤】，讓大家試穿衣服時有適當的地方掛東西。"},{"w":"bag","p":"n.","d":"a container for carrying things","c":"袋子；包包","s":"A: I'm flying to Singapore for a two-day conference next week, and I don't want to wait at the airport for my luggage, so what should I bring? B: Just pack one small bag that fits in the overhead space, with two shirts, a pair of trousers, and your laptop, and you can walk straight out after landing.","t":"A：我下週要飛去新加坡參加為期兩天的會議，我不想在機場等行李，我該帶什麼？ B：只要帶一個能放進頭頂置物櫃的小【包包】，裝兩件襯衫、一條長褲和你的筆電，降落後就可以直接走出去。"},{"w":"shoes","p":"n.","d":"things you wear on your feet","c":"鞋子","s":"A: The office is installing new carpet throughout the meeting rooms this month, so is there any new rule that the staff should follow during that time? B: Yes, everyone must take off their outdoor shoes at the entrance and wear the slippers provided, so the carpet will stay clean and won't get damaged.","t":"A：辦公室這個月要在所有會議室鋪新地毯，這段期間員工有什麼新規定要遵守嗎？ B：有，每個人在入口都必須脫掉外面穿的【鞋子】並換上提供的拖鞋，這樣地毯才能保持乾淨、不會損壞。"},{"w":"uniform","p":"n.","d":"special clothes that all workers or students of a group wear","c":"制服","s":"A: I start my new job at the hotel reception desk on Monday morning, but nobody has told me what I'm supposed to wear on the first day, so do you know? B: The hotel will give you a dark green uniform with your name badge, and you can pick it up from the staff office before your shift begins.","t":"A：我週一早上要開始在飯店櫃檯的新工作，但沒有人告訴我第一天應該穿什麼，你知道嗎？ B：飯店會給你一套深綠色的【制服】和名牌，你可以在上班前到員工辦公室領取。"},{"w":"sportswear","p":"n.","d":"clothes and shoes made for doing sports","c":"運動服裝","s":"A: Our company is organizing a team hiking day in the mountains next month, so should I wear my usual office clothes or something else? B: You'd better wear light sportswear and running shoes, because the trail is long and hot, and you'll want clothes that dry quickly when you sweat.","t":"A：我們公司下個月要在山上舉辦團隊健行日，我該穿平常的上班服裝還是別的？ B：你最好穿輕便的【運動服裝】和跑鞋，因為步道又長又熱，你會需要流汗時能快乾的衣服。"},{"w":"queue","p":"v.","d":"to wait in a line of people for your turn","c":"排隊","s":"A: The department store is having its biggest sale of the year this weekend, so how early should we arrive if we want to try on the discounted coats? B: We'll probably have to queue for at least half an hour outside the changing rooms, so let's get there right when the doors open at ten.","t":"A：百貨公司這個週末舉辦年度最大的特賣，如果我們想試穿打折的大衣，應該多早到？ B：我們可能得在更衣室外【排隊】至少半小時，所以我們十點一開門就到吧。"},{"w":"available","p":"adj.","d":"free to be used","c":"可用的；空出來的","s":"A: There are only three changing rooms in this small shop, and all of them seem to have people inside right now, so how will I know when it's my turn? B: The assistant will call you as soon as a room is available, and in the meantime you can look at the new scarves near the front counter.","t":"A：這間小店只有三間更衣室，現在好像都有人在裡面，我怎麼知道什麼時候輪到我？ B：一有房間【空出來】，店員就會馬上叫你，在這期間你可以看看櫃檯附近的新圍巾。"},{"w":"sign","p":"n.","d":"a board with words or pictures that gives information","c":"標示；告示牌","s":"A: Some customers walked right past the changing rooms yesterday because they didn't know where they were, so how can we make them easier to find? B: Let's put a large sign with an arrow above the hallway near the escalator, so shoppers can see the way to the changing area from anywhere on the floor.","t":"A：昨天有些顧客直接走過了更衣室，因為他們不知道在哪裡，我們要怎麼讓它更容易被找到？ B：我們在手扶梯附近的走廊上方放一個大的箭頭【標示】，讓顧客在樓層任何地方都能看到往更衣區的路。"}]},{"unit":51,"theme":"Charity 慈善","cards":[{"w":"donation","p":"n.","d":"money or goods given to help people or a group","c":"捐款；捐贈物","s":"A: The hospital's children's ward needs new beds and toys before the winter holidays, so how can our company help them without spending too much time on planning? B: We could ask every department to make a small donation this month, and the finance team will collect the money and send it to the hospital together.","t":"A：醫院的兒童病房在寒假前需要新的病床和玩具，我們公司要怎麼幫忙又不必花太多時間規劃？ B：我們可以請每個部門這個月做一筆小額【捐款】，由財務團隊收齊後一起送到醫院。"},{"w":"donate","p":"v.","d":"to give money or things to help others","c":"捐贈；捐款","s":"A: Our office is moving to the new building downtown next month, and we have dozens of old desks, chairs, and computers that still work well, so what should we do with them? B: I called a local school yesterday, and they would be very happy if we donate the furniture and computers to their new library.","t":"A：我們辦公室下個月要搬到市中心的新大樓，我們有好幾十張還能用的舊桌椅和電腦，該怎麼處理？ B：我昨天打電話給一所當地學校，如果我們把家具和電腦【捐贈】給他們的新圖書館，他們會非常開心。"},{"w":"volunteer","p":"v.","d":"to offer to do work without being paid","c":"自願做；當志工","s":"A: The community center is organizing a beach clean-up on Saturday morning, but they still need about twenty more people to pick up trash and carry bags, so are you free that day? B: Yes, my sister and I both want to volunteer, because we often swim there and are worried about all the plastic on the sand.","t":"A：社區中心週六早上要舉辦淨灘活動，但他們還需要大約二十個人撿垃圾和搬袋子，你那天有空嗎？ B：有，我和我姊姊都想去【當志工】，因為我們常在那裡游泳，很擔心沙灘上那些塑膠垃圾。"},{"w":"fundraising","p":"n.","d":"the activity of collecting money for a cause","c":"募款","s":"A: The school orchestra wants to travel to Japan for an international music competition next spring, but the trip will cost a lot of money, so how will the parents pay for it? B: They are planning a big fundraising effort, including a bake sale, a concert, and an online page where friends and relatives can give money.","t":"A：學校管弦樂團明年春天想去日本參加國際音樂比賽，但這趟旅程要花很多錢，家長們要怎麼負擔？ B：他們正在規劃一場大型【募款】活動，包括義賣烘焙點心、一場音樂會，還有一個讓親友可以捐錢的網頁。"},{"w":"fundraiser","p":"n.","d":"an event held to collect money for a cause","c":"募款活動","s":"A: I saw on the company website that the marketing team rented the hotel ballroom next Friday evening, so is it for a product launch or a party? B: Neither, it is a fundraiser for the children's hospital, and tickets cost two thousand dollars each, with all the money going to buy medical equipment.","t":"A：我在公司網站上看到行銷團隊租了下週五晚上的飯店宴會廳，是要辦產品發表會還是派對？ B：都不是，那是為兒童醫院舉辦的【募款活動】，每張票兩千元，所有收入都會用來購買醫療設備。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help someone, often by giving money or encouragement","c":"支持；援助","s":"A: Many small farms in the mountains lost most of their fruit after the typhoon last week, and the farmers are worried about paying their bills, so is there anything our supermarket chain can do? B: We could support them by buying their remaining fruit at a fair price and selling it in our stores with a special sign.","t":"A：上週颱風過後，山區許多小農場損失了大部分的水果，農民們擔心付不出帳單，我們連鎖超市能做些什麼嗎？ B：我們可以用合理的價格收購他們剩下的水果，並在店裡放上特別標示販售，以此來【支持】他們。"},{"w":"aid","p":"n.","d":"help such as food, money, or medicine given to people in need","c":"援助；救援物資","s":"A: After the earthquake destroyed several villages in the south, many families had no food, clean water, or blankets, so how did the government respond so quickly? B: It sent trucks full of emergency aid within twenty-four hours, and the army helped deliver everything to the areas that were hardest to reach.","t":"A：地震摧毀了南部幾個村莊後，許多家庭沒有食物、乾淨的水或毯子，政府怎麼能那麼快回應？ B：它在二十四小時內派出滿載緊急【援助物資】的卡車，軍隊也協助把物資送到最難抵達的地區。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"food, money, or help given to people after a disaster","c":"救濟；救援","s":"A: The flood last weekend left hundreds of people in the river town without homes, and many of them are staying in schools, so what is our bank doing to help? B: We have started a disaster relief fund, and for every dollar that customers give, the bank will add another dollar until we reach one million.","t":"A：上週末的水災讓河邊小鎮數百人無家可歸，很多人暫住在學校裡，我們銀行在做什麼幫忙？ B：我們成立了災害【救濟】基金，客戶每捐一元，銀行就再加一元，直到達到一百萬元為止。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"the people who live in one area","c":"社區；社群","s":"A: Why did the company decide to build a small park and playground next to the new factory instead of using the land for more parking spaces? B: The managers wanted to give something back to the local community, because many of our workers live nearby and their children had no safe place to play.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定在新工廠旁邊蓋一座小公園和遊樂場，而不是把那塊地拿來做更多停車位？ B：主管們想回饋當地【社區】，因為我們很多員工住在附近，他們的孩子之前沒有安全的地方可以玩。"},{"w":"nonprofit","p":"adj.","d":"not set up to make money for its owners","c":"非營利的","s":"A: My cousin left her well-paid job at an investment bank last year, so where is she working now, and does she still enjoy her career? B: She joined a small nonprofit group that teaches computer skills to older people, and although she earns less money, she says the work makes her feel useful every day.","t":"A：我表姊去年辭掉了投資銀行的高薪工作，她現在在哪裡工作？還喜歡她的職涯嗎？ B：她加入了一個教長者電腦技能的小型【非營利】團體，雖然賺得比較少，但她說這份工作讓她每天都覺得自己有用。"},{"w":"organization","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together for a purpose","c":"組織；機構","s":"A: I would like to give some of my year-end bonus to help stray animals, but I am worried that the money will not be used properly, so do you have any advice? B: Choose an organization that publishes clear reports every year showing how much it spends on food, medical care, and staff.","t":"A：我想把部分年終獎金拿來幫助流浪動物，但我擔心錢沒被妥善使用，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：選擇一個每年公開清楚報告、說明在食物、醫療和人事上花了多少錢的【組織】。"},{"w":"cause","p":"n.","d":"an aim or idea that people support or work for","c":"理想；公益目標","s":"A: Every year our department chooses one social issue to focus on during the holiday season, so which one should we pick this December? B: I think clean drinking water in poor villages is a good cause, because a small amount of money can build a well that helps hundreds of people for many years.","t":"A：我們部門每年都會在假期選一個社會議題來關注，今年十二月我們該選哪一個？ B：我覺得貧困村莊的乾淨飲用水是個很好的【公益目標】，因為一小筆錢就能蓋一口井，幫助數百人許多年。"},{"w":"campaign","p":"n.","d":"a planned set of activities to reach a goal","c":"（有組織的）活動；宣傳運動","s":"A: The posters about recycling old phones are everywhere in the subway stations this month, so who is paying for all of them? B: A large electronics company started the campaign in October, and it plans to collect fifty thousand phones by the end of the year and give the profits to schools.","t":"A：這個月捷運站到處都是回收舊手機的海報，是誰出錢做的？ B：一家大型電子公司在十月發起了這項【活動】，計畫在年底前收集五萬支手機，並把收益捐給學校。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"a planned social occasion or activity","c":"活動；大型聚會","s":"A: The hotel manager asked me how many guests will attend our charity dinner, but I have not finished counting the replies yet, so what should I tell her? B: Tell her that about three hundred people will come to the event, and we will send the final number by Wednesday afternoon at the latest.","t":"A：飯店經理問我有多少賓客會參加我們的慈善晚宴，但我還沒算完回覆，我該怎麼跟她說？ B：告訴她大約三百人會來參加這場【活動】，最晚週三下午我們會提供最終人數。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"n.","d":"an event held to raise money for people in need","c":"義演；慈善活動","s":"A: I heard that several famous singers will perform at the stadium on Sunday night, but the tickets seem very cheap, so why is that? B: It is a benefit concert for families who lost their homes in the fire, and the singers agreed to perform for free so that more money can go to the victims.","t":"A：我聽說幾位知名歌手週日晚上會在體育場表演，但票價看起來很便宜，為什麼？ B：那是一場為火災中失去家園的家庭舉辦的【慈善義演】音樂會，歌手們同意免費演出，好讓更多錢能送到災民手中。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"willing to help; useful","c":"有幫助的；樂於助人的","s":"A: This was the first time our team organized a book drive for the rural schools, so how did everything go when you delivered the boxes on Thursday? B: The teachers there were very helpful, because they carried the boxes into the library with us and showed us which books the students needed most.","t":"A：這是我們團隊第一次為偏鄉學校辦募書活動，你週四送箱子過去時一切順利嗎？ B：那裡的老師們很【樂於幫忙】，他們跟我們一起把箱子搬進圖書館，還告訴我們學生最需要哪些書。"},{"w":"generous","p":"adj.","d":"happy to give money, time, or help","c":"慷慨的；大方的","s":"A: The animal shelter finally has enough money to repair its roof before the rainy season, so where did the money come from? B: A generous businessman who adopted a dog there last year gave half a million dollars, and he also promised to pay for food for the next three years.","t":"A：動物收容所終於有足夠的錢在雨季前修好屋頂了，錢是從哪裡來的？ B：一位去年在那裡領養了狗的【慷慨】商人捐了五十萬元，他還答應未來三年負擔飼料費。"},{"w":"kindness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being friendly and helpful to others","c":"仁慈；善意","s":"A: Why did you buy a big box of chocolates for the woman who works at the reception desk downstairs? B: When I lost my wallet last Monday, she paid for my taxi home and called the police for me, so I wanted to thank her for her kindness and let her know how much it meant to me.","t":"A：你為什麼買了一大盒巧克力送給樓下櫃檯的那位女士？ B：上週一我掉了錢包，她幫我付了回家的計程車錢，還幫我打電話報警，所以我想謝謝她的【善意】，讓她知道這對我意義有多大。"},{"w":"care","p":"n.","d":"the work of looking after people who need help","c":"照顧；照護","s":"A: The new center for elderly people opened near our office last month, so what kind of services does it offer to the families in this neighborhood? B: It provides daily care for older people who cannot live alone, with nurses who check their health, cook healthy meals, and take them for short walks.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近上個月開了新的長者中心，它提供這一帶家庭什麼樣的服務？ B：它為無法獨居的長者提供日間【照護】，有護理師幫他們檢查健康、煮健康的餐點，還會帶他們去散步。"},{"w":"poor","p":"adj.","d":"having very little money","c":"貧窮的","s":"A: The volunteers from our company are going to the mountain villages again next weekend, so what will they bring to the families there this time? B: They will bring warm jackets and school supplies, because many families in that area are poor and cannot afford new clothes before the cold winter arrives.","t":"A：我們公司的志工下週末又要去山區村落了，這次他們要帶什麼給那裡的家庭？ B：他們會帶保暖外套和文具，因為那一帶很多家庭很【貧窮】，在寒冬來臨前買不起新衣服。"},{"w":"needy","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough money, food, or clothes","c":"貧困的；有需要的","s":"A: Our restaurant always has a lot of fresh bread and soup left at closing time, and it feels terrible to throw it away, so do you have a better idea? B: We could work with the local food bank, which picks up extra food every night and gives it to needy families in the neighborhood.","t":"A：我們餐廳打烊時總是剩很多新鮮麵包和湯，丟掉感覺很糟，你有更好的主意嗎？ B：我們可以跟當地的食物銀行合作，他們每晚會來收多餘的食物，再送給附近【有需要的】家庭。"},{"w":"homeless","p":"adj.","d":"having no place to live","c":"無家可歸的","s":"A: Why are so many staff members bringing sleeping bags and thick blankets to the office lobby this week? B: The human resources team is collecting them for homeless people who sleep in the train station, because the weather report says the temperature will drop below ten degrees this weekend.","t":"A：為什麼這週有這麼多員工把睡袋和厚毯子帶到辦公室大廳？ B：人資團隊正在為睡在火車站的【無家可歸的】人收集這些物品，因為氣象預報說這個週末氣溫會降到十度以下。"},{"w":"shelter","p":"n.","d":"a place where people or animals in need can stay","c":"收容所；庇護所","s":"A: My neighbor found three small kittens in a box behind the supermarket yesterday, but she cannot keep them in her apartment, so where should she take them? B: She can bring them to the animal shelter on Green Road, where the staff will give them medical checks and help them find new families.","t":"A：我鄰居昨天在超市後面的箱子裡發現三隻小貓，但她的公寓不能養，她該把牠們送去哪裡？ B：她可以帶去綠園路上的動物【收容所】，那裡的工作人員會幫牠們做健康檢查，並協助牠們找到新家庭。"},{"w":"mission","p":"n.","d":"the main purpose of a group or organization","c":"使命；任務","s":"A: The new director of the charity gave a long speech at the meeting this morning, but I arrived late, so what was the main point? B: She explained that the group's mission is to make sure every child in the city has three healthy meals a day, and all future projects must follow that goal.","t":"A：慈善團體的新主任今天早上在會議上發表了長篇演講，但我遲到了，重點是什麼？ B：她說明了這個團體的【使命】是確保市內每個孩子每天都有三頓健康的餐點，未來所有計畫都必須遵循這個目標。"},{"w":"impact","p":"n.","d":"a strong effect on someone or something","c":"影響；衝擊","s":"A: The board members want to know whether the reading program we paid for last year really helped the students, so what results can we show them? B: The program had a clear impact on the children, because their test scores went up by twenty percent and more of them now borrow books every week.","t":"A：董事會想知道我們去年出資的閱讀計畫是否真的幫助了學生，我們能給他們看什麼成果？ B：這個計畫對孩子們有明顯的【影響】，他們的考試成績提高了百分之二十，而且現在有更多人每週借書。"},{"w":"awareness","p":"n.","d":"knowing about something and understanding that it is important","c":"意識；認識","s":"A: Why is the hospital putting up colorful boards in the shopping mall and giving free health checks to everyone this weekend? B: They want to raise public awareness of heart disease, because many people do not know the early warning signs and only see a doctor when it is too late.","t":"A：醫院為什麼這個週末在購物中心擺放彩色看板，並幫每個人做免費健康檢查？ B：他們想提高大眾對心臟病的【意識】，因為很多人不知道早期警訊，等到看醫生時已經太晚了。"},{"w":"fair","p":"n.","d":"an outdoor event where people sell goods, often to raise money","c":"市集；園遊會","s":"A: Our department made a lot of handmade soap and candles in the workshop last month, so where are we going to sell them? B: We will rent a table at the charity fair in the city park on Saturday, where many companies and schools will sell goods and give the money to the children's hospital.","t":"A：我們部門上個月在工作坊做了很多手工皂和蠟燭，要拿去哪裡賣？ B：我們會在週六市立公園的慈善【市集】租一張桌子，那裡會有很多公司和學校販售物品，並把收入捐給兒童醫院。"},{"w":"hope","p":"v.","d":"to want something to happen and think it is possible","c":"希望","s":"A: The team has collected almost four hundred thousand dollars for the new children's library, but the building will cost half a million, so what will happen next? B: We hope to reach our goal by the end of next month, because two large companies have promised to match the money that employees give.","t":"A：團隊已經為新的兒童圖書館募到將近四十萬元，但建築需要五十萬元，接下來會怎樣？ B：我們【希望】在下個月底前達成目標，因為有兩家大公司承諾會配合員工捐款金額捐出同等的錢。"}]},{"unit":52,"theme":"Chatting 聊天","cards":[{"w":"chat","p":"v.","d":"to talk in a friendly, informal way","c":"聊天、閒聊","s":"A: I noticed that you spent almost an hour in the break room with the new intern this afternoon, so was there a problem with her first project? B: No, everything is fine, we just wanted to chat about her hometown and her favorite restaurants, because I want her to feel welcome on the team.","t":"A：我注意到你今天下午和新實習生在休息室待了快一個小時，她的第一個專案有問題嗎？ B：沒有，一切都很好，我們只是想【聊聊】她的家鄉和她最喜歡的餐廳，因為我希望她在團隊裡感到受歡迎。"},{"w":"chatter","p":"n.","d":"quick, continuous talk about unimportant things","c":"喋喋不休、閒聊聲","s":"A: Why did you move your desk from the open area to the small room next to the storage closet last Monday? B: The loud chatter from the sales team near the coffee machine made it hard for me to concentrate on the monthly budget report, so my manager kindly let me work somewhere quieter.","t":"A：你上週一為什麼把辦公桌從開放區搬到儲藏室旁邊的小房間？ B：咖啡機附近業務團隊吵雜的【閒聊聲】讓我很難專心做每月預算報告，所以經理好心讓我到比較安靜的地方工作。"},{"w":"conversation","p":"n.","d":"a talk between two or more people","c":"對話、交談","s":"A: How did you find out that the client in Singapore was unhappy with our delivery schedule before the official complaint arrived? B: I had a long phone conversation with their purchasing manager yesterday evening, and she told me openly that the last two shipments were late and that her boss was worried.","t":"A：在正式投訴送到之前，你是怎麼發現新加坡的客戶對我們的交貨時程不滿意的？ B：我昨天傍晚和他們的採購經理進行了很長的電話【交談】，她坦白告訴我最近兩批貨都遲到了，而且她的老闆很擔心。"},{"w":"talk","p":"n.","d":"a short speech to a group of people about a subject","c":"演講、談話","s":"A: Are you going to the marketing conference in Taichung next month, or are you too busy with the new product launch? B: I'm definitely going, because our director asked me to give a short talk about how we used social media to attract younger customers, and I've already started preparing my slides.","t":"A：你下個月要去台中的行銷研討會嗎？還是你忙著新產品上市太忙了？ B：我一定會去，因為我們的主管請我做一場簡短的【演講】，談談我們如何利用社群媒體吸引年輕顧客，我已經開始準備投影片了。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a talk in which people share ideas and opinions about something","c":"討論","s":"A: Did the managers finally decide whether the company will allow employees to work from home two days a week? B: Not yet, they had a long discussion about it during this morning's meeting, but they still disagree about how to measure productivity, so they will meet again next Thursday.","t":"A：經理們最後決定公司是否允許員工每週在家工作兩天了嗎？ B：還沒，他們在今天早上的會議中對此進行了很長的【討論】，但對於如何衡量生產力仍有分歧，所以下週四會再開會。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"a serious talk between groups to solve a problem or understand each other","c":"對話、溝通","s":"A: The two departments have been arguing about the shared budget for weeks, so what is the new manager planning to do about it? B: She wants to start an open dialogue between the team leaders, so every Friday they will sit down together, explain their needs honestly, and try to find a fair solution.","t":"A：兩個部門為了共用預算已經爭吵好幾週了，新經理打算怎麼處理？ B：她想在團隊主管之間展開開放的【對話】，所以每週五他們會坐下來一起坦誠說明各自的需求，並試著找出公平的解決辦法。"},{"w":"gossip","p":"n.","d":"talk about other people's private lives, often not true","c":"八卦、閒話","s":"A: Is it true that our branch office in Kaohsiung is going to close at the end of the year? B: I don't think so, that is probably just gossip from the staff lounge, because the regional manager told me yesterday that sales there have actually increased and they are hiring more people.","t":"A：我們高雄分公司年底要關閉是真的嗎？ B：我不這麼認為，那大概只是員工休息室流傳的【八卦】，因為區域經理昨天告訴我那裡的業績其實有成長，而且他們正在招募更多人。"},{"w":"small talk","p":"n.phr.","d":"polite talk about unimportant topics, often with people you don't know well","c":"寒暄、閒聊","s":"A: I always feel nervous at networking events because I never know what to say to people I have just met. B: Start with some easy small talk about the weather, the food, or the traffic on the way there, and after a few minutes the conversation usually becomes more natural and relaxed.","t":"A：我在交流活動上總是很緊張，因為我從來不知道要對剛認識的人說什麼。 B：先從一些輕鬆的【寒暄】開始，例如天氣、食物或來的路上的交通，幾分鐘後對話通常就會變得比較自然和放鬆。"},{"w":"banter","p":"n.","d":"friendly joking talk between people","c":"打趣、玩笑話","s":"A: The new designers seem to get along really well, don't they, even though they only joined the company two weeks ago? B: Yes, there is always friendly banter between them during lunch, and they joke about each other's favorite sports teams, which makes the whole office feel more cheerful.","t":"A：新來的設計師們似乎相處得很好，對吧？雖然他們兩週前才進公司。 B：是啊，午餐時他們之間總是有友善的【玩笑話】，還會互相開對方最喜歡的運動隊伍的玩笑，讓整個辦公室感覺更愉快。"},{"w":"exchange","p":"v.","d":"to give something to someone and receive something from them","c":"交換","s":"A: The conference in Tokyo was very busy, so did you have any chance to meet people from other companies in our industry? B: Yes, during the coffee breaks I was able to exchange business cards with several suppliers, and two of them have already emailed me about possible partnerships next year.","t":"A：東京的研討會很忙，你有機會認識我們產業其他公司的人嗎？ B：有，在咖啡休息時間我和幾家供應商【交換】了名片，其中兩家已經寄電子郵件給我，談明年可能的合作。"},{"w":"message","p":"n.","d":"a short piece of information you send or leave for someone","c":"訊息、留言","s":"A: I called the accounting department twice this morning to ask about my travel refund, but nobody answered the phone. B: Most of them are attending a training session until noon, so you should leave a message with the receptionist, and someone will call you back as soon as the session ends.","t":"A：我今天早上打了兩次電話給會計部詢問我的差旅退款，但沒有人接電話。 B：他們大部分人在參加訓練課程到中午，所以你應該請櫃檯人員幫你留個【訊息】，課程一結束就會有人回電給你。"},{"w":"text","p":"v.","d":"to send a written message by mobile phone","c":"傳簡訊","s":"A: The shuttle bus from the hotel to the exhibition center might be late tomorrow morning because of the road repairs. B: In that case, please text me as soon as you leave the hotel, and I will tell the organizers to keep a seat for you near the front of the main hall.","t":"A：因為道路施工，明天早上從飯店到展覽中心的接駁車可能會遲到。 B：這樣的話，你一離開飯店就請【傳簡訊】給我，我會告訴主辦單位幫你在主廳前面保留一個座位。"},{"w":"reply","p":"v.","d":"to answer someone in speech or writing","c":"回覆、回答","s":"A: The customer from Melbourne has sent us three emails about the missing package since Monday, and she sounds very upset now. B: I know, I promised to reply to her before lunch today, as soon as the warehouse manager confirms where the package is and when it can be delivered.","t":"A：墨爾本的那位顧客從週一起已經寄了三封關於遺失包裹的電子郵件給我們，她現在聽起來很不高興。 B：我知道，我答應今天午餐前【回覆】她，只要倉庫經理確認包裹在哪裡以及何時可以送達。"},{"w":"respond","p":"v.","d":"to say or do something as an answer or reaction","c":"回應","s":"A: Our online store received a lot of negative reviews after the website crashed during the holiday sale last weekend. B: The marketing team will respond to each review personally this week, apologize for the problem, and offer every unhappy customer a discount code for their next purchase.","t":"A：上週末假期特賣期間網站當機後，我們的網路商店收到很多負評。 B：行銷團隊這週會親自【回應】每一則評論，為問題道歉，並提供每位不滿意的顧客下次購物的折扣碼。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information or ideas with others","c":"溝通、傳達","s":"A: Since half of our project team works in Vietnam and the other half is here in Taipei, how do you keep everyone informed? B: We communicate mainly through a shared online platform, and we also hold a video meeting every Tuesday morning so that everyone can ask questions and report problems.","t":"A：既然我們專案團隊一半在越南、一半在台北，你們怎麼讓大家掌握最新消息？ B：我們主要透過共用的線上平台【溝通】，每週二早上也會開視訊會議，讓大家可以提問並回報問題。"},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"the act of talking or doing things with other people","c":"互動","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager want the front desk staff to take a customer service course next month? B: Because guests said in the survey that their interaction with the staff at check-in felt cold and rushed, and she believes a warmer welcome will bring more guests back.","t":"A：飯店經理為什麼要櫃檯人員下個月上客戶服務課程？ B：因為房客在問卷中表示，他們入住時與員工的【互動】感覺冷淡又匆忙，而她相信更溫暖的接待會讓更多客人回流。"},{"w":"socialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend time with other people in a friendly way","c":"交際、社交","s":"A: The company has planned a barbecue by the river on Saturday afternoon, but I'm not sure if I should go because I don't know many people. B: You should come, because it's a great chance to socialize with colleagues from other departments outside the office, and the food is always delicious.","t":"A：公司星期六下午在河邊辦了烤肉活動，但我不確定要不要去，因為我認識的人不多。 B：你應該來，因為那是在辦公室以外和其他部門同事【交際】的好機會，而且食物總是很好吃。"},{"w":"catch up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to talk with someone you have not seen for a while about recent news","c":"敘舊、了解近況","s":"A: You and your old university roommate haven't seen each other for almost five years, right? B: That's right, but she is visiting Taipei for a business trip next week, so we are going to have dinner at a night market on Wednesday and catch up on everything that has happened in our lives.","t":"A：你和你大學時的老室友快五年沒見面了，對吧？ B：沒錯，但她下週來台北出差，所以我們週三要去夜市吃晚餐，好好【敘敘舊】，聊聊我們生活中發生的一切。"},{"w":"ramble","p":"v.","d":"to talk for a long time in a confused way, without staying on the topic","c":"漫談、東拉西扯","s":"A: The presentation by the new consultant was supposed to last twenty minutes, so why did it take over an hour? B: He started to ramble about his own travels and past clients instead of focusing on our sales data, and several people in the audience began checking their phones.","t":"A：新顧問的簡報應該只有二十分鐘，為什麼花了一個多小時？ B：他開始【東拉西扯】地講自己的旅行和以前的客戶，而不是專注在我們的銷售數據上，台下好幾個人都開始看手機了。"},{"w":"interrupt","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone while they are speaking or doing something","c":"打斷、打擾","s":"A: The director is still on a video call with the investors from Hong Kong, but the delivery company is waiting for her signature downstairs. B: Please don't interrupt her right now, because the meeting is very important, so ask the driver to wait ten more minutes or come back after lunch.","t":"A：主管還在和香港投資人進行視訊會議，但快遞公司在樓下等她簽名。 B：現在請不要【打斷】她，因為這場會議非常重要，請司機再等十分鐘，或午餐後再來。"},{"w":"listen","p":"v.","d":"to pay attention to what someone says","c":"聆聽、傾聽","s":"A: Several employees complained that the new manager makes decisions without asking anyone for their opinions. B: I heard about that too, so the HR director advised him to listen carefully to his team during weekly meetings and to take notes on their ideas before he decides anything important.","t":"A：好幾位員工抱怨新經理做決定時都不問任何人的意見。 B：我也聽說了，所以人資主管建議他在每週會議中仔細【聆聽】團隊的意見，並在做任何重要決定之前記下大家的想法。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to tell others about your ideas, feelings or experiences","c":"分享","s":"A: What should we do during the first fifteen minutes of the workshop to help the participants relax? B: Let's ask everyone to share one interesting story about their first job, because it is a fun way to break the ice and helps people remember each other's names.","t":"A：工作坊的前十五分鐘我們該做什麼，讓參加者放鬆一點？ B：我們請每個人【分享】一個關於自己第一份工作的有趣故事，因為這是打破僵局的有趣方式，也能幫助大家記住彼此的名字。"},{"w":"debate","p":"n.","d":"a discussion in which people give different opinions on a topic","c":"辯論、爭論","s":"A: Did the city council make a final decision about building the new shopping mall near the train station? B: Not yet, there was a heated debate at last night's public meeting, because local shop owners worry about losing customers while residents hope for more jobs and better parking.","t":"A：市議會對於在火車站附近興建新購物中心做出最後決定了嗎？ B：還沒，昨晚的公聽會上有一場激烈的【辯論】，因為當地店家擔心失去顧客，而居民則希望有更多工作機會和更好的停車空間。"},{"w":"comment","p":"n.","d":"something you say or write that gives an opinion","c":"評論、意見","s":"A: Have you read the feedback forms that the trainees filled out after yesterday's safety workshop? B: Yes, and one comment was especially useful, because a trainee suggested adding more real examples from our factory, so I'm going to update the slides before the next session in December.","t":"A：你看過受訓人員在昨天安全工作坊後填寫的意見回饋表嗎？ B：看過了，其中一則【評論】特別有用，有位受訓人員建議加入更多我們工廠的真實案例，所以我會在十二月的下一堂課之前更新投影片。"}]},{"unit":53,"theme":"Child 兒童","cards":[{"w":"children","p":"n.","d":"young people who are not yet adults","c":"兒童；孩子們（複數）","s":"A: Our hotel is planning a family weekend package for the summer holidays, so what should we include to attract more parents? B: We should offer a supervised play area and a special menu for children under twelve, because parents can relax at the pool while their kids have fun safely nearby.","t":"A：我們飯店正在規劃暑假的家庭週末套裝行程，應該包含什麼才能吸引更多家長？ B：我們應該提供有人看顧的遊戲區，以及給十二歲以下【兒童】的特別菜單，因為家長可以在泳池邊放鬆，而孩子就在附近安全地玩樂。"},{"w":"kid","p":"n.","d":"a child (informal)","c":"小孩（口語）","s":"A: You look tired this morning, and you usually arrive at the office before everyone else, so did something happen at home last night? B: My youngest kid had a high fever, so my wife and I took turns staying awake with him until the doctor's office opened at eight.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來很累，而且你通常比大家早到辦公室，昨晚家裡發生什麼事了嗎？ B：我最小的【孩子】發高燒，所以我和太太輪流熬夜照顧他，直到早上八點診所開門。"},{"w":"infant","p":"n.","d":"a very young baby","c":"嬰兒","s":"A: The airline called to confirm our flight to Tokyo next month, and they asked whether anyone in our group is traveling with a baby, so what did you tell them? B: I said my sister is bringing her six-month-old infant, so they will reserve a front-row seat with a special bed attached to the wall.","t":"A：航空公司打電話來確認我們下個月飛東京的班機，他們問我們團體中是否有人帶嬰兒同行，你怎麼回答？ B：我說我姊姊會帶她六個月大的【嬰兒】，所以他們會保留一個前排座位，並在牆上加裝一個特別的嬰兒床。"},{"w":"toddler","p":"n.","d":"a young child who is learning to walk","c":"學步的幼兒","s":"A: The new daycare center near our office is opening next week, so do you know what age groups they accept and how much it costs? B: They accept any toddler between one and three years old, and the monthly fee includes lunch, afternoon snacks, and a short music class every Friday.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近新的托兒中心下週開幕，你知道他們收哪些年齡層、費用多少嗎？ B：他們收一到三歲的任何【幼兒】，月費包含午餐、下午點心，以及每週五的簡短音樂課。"},{"w":"baby","p":"n.","d":"a very young child","c":"嬰兒；寶寶","s":"A: Linda has not been in the office for two weeks, and her desk is completely empty, so did she leave the company? B: No, she is on maternity leave because she just had a baby girl last Tuesday, and she plans to return to work in about three months.","t":"A：琳達已經兩週沒來辦公室了，而且她的桌子完全清空，她離職了嗎？ B：沒有，她在請產假，因為她上週二剛生了一個女【寶寶】，她打算大約三個月後回來上班。"},{"w":"youth","p":"n.","d":"young people as a group; the time of being young","c":"青少年；青年；青春時期","s":"A: The city government gave our company a grant this year, so how are we going to use the money to help the local community? B: We are starting a summer training program for youth from low-income families, where teenagers can learn computer skills and get real work experience in our offices.","t":"A：今年市政府給了我們公司一筆補助金，我們要怎麼用這筆錢來幫助當地社區？ B：我們要為低收入家庭的【青少年】開辦暑期訓練計畫，讓他們可以學習電腦技能，並在我們的辦公室獲得實際工作經驗。"},{"w":"teenager","p":"n.","d":"a person aged 13 to 19","c":"青少年（13–19歲）","s":"A: Our new smartphone sold well with office workers, but the marketing team wants to reach younger customers, so what do you suggest? B: Since almost every teenager spends hours on video apps after school, we should hire popular online creators to show the phone's camera features in short, funny clips.","t":"A：我們的新智慧型手機在上班族之間賣得很好，但行銷團隊想觸及更年輕的顧客，你有什麼建議？ B：既然幾乎每個【青少年】放學後都花好幾個小時在影音應用程式上，我們應該聘請受歡迎的網路創作者，用簡短有趣的影片展示手機的相機功能。"},{"w":"minor","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not yet an adult by law","c":"未成年人","s":"A: A customer at the front desk wants to rent one of our scooters for his sixteen-year-old son this afternoon, so is that allowed? B: I'm afraid company rules say we cannot rent vehicles to a minor, even when a parent is present and is willing to sign all the forms.","t":"A：櫃檯有位顧客想在今天下午幫他十六歲的兒子租一台我們的機車，這樣可以嗎？ B：恐怕公司規定我們不能把車輛租給【未成年人】，即使有家長在場而且願意簽署所有文件也不行。"},{"w":"juvenile","p":"adj.","d":"related to young people, especially young people who break the law","c":"青少年的；少年的","s":"A: I read that the city is building a new center near the train station, so do you know what it will be used for? B: It will be a juvenile support center where young people who have gotten into trouble can receive counseling, finish their studies, and learn job skills.","t":"A：我看到市政府在火車站附近蓋一座新中心，你知道它要做什麼用嗎？ B：那會是一座【青少年】輔導中心，讓惹上麻煩的年輕人可以接受諮商、完成學業，並學習工作技能。"},{"w":"youngster","p":"n.","d":"a young person or child","c":"年輕人；小孩","s":"A: The weekend art workshop at the museum was fully booked again, so why do you think it has become so popular with local families? B: Every youngster who joins gets to paint a real canvas with a professional artist, and the parents love taking photos of the finished work at the end.","t":"A：博物館的週末藝術工作坊又額滿了，你覺得為什麼它在本地家庭之間這麼受歡迎？ B：每個參加的【小朋友】都能和專業藝術家一起在真正的畫布上作畫，而家長們很喜歡在最後幫完成的作品拍照。"},{"w":"offspring","p":"n.","d":"a person's or animal's children or young","c":"子女；後代（動物的幼崽）","s":"A: The documentary team wants to film the sea turtles on the island this summer, so when is the best time for them to visit? B: They should come in August, because that is when the mother turtles' offspring hatch on the beach at night and crawl toward the ocean for the first time.","t":"A：紀錄片團隊今年夏天想去島上拍攝海龜，他們什麼時候去最好？ B：他們應該八月去，因為那是海龜媽媽的【後代】在夜裡於沙灘上孵化、第一次爬向大海的時候。"},{"w":"descendant","p":"n.","d":"a person in a later generation of the same family","c":"後裔；子孫","s":"A: The hotel's new brochure says the building has a long history, so who owns it now and how did they get it? B: The current owner is a descendant of the merchant who built it in 1890, and the property has passed down through five generations of the same family.","t":"A：飯店的新簡介說這棟建築歷史悠久，現在是誰擁有它，他們又是怎麼得到的？ B：現任屋主是1890年建造它的那位商人的【後裔】，這份產業在同一個家族中傳了五代。"},{"w":"pupil","p":"n.","d":"a child who goes to school","c":"學童；小學生","s":"A: The elementary school down the street asked our bank to help with its financial education day, so what are we planning to do? B: Our staff will visit each class and teach every pupil how to save money with a simple piggy bank game that takes about forty minutes.","t":"A：街上那間小學請我們銀行協助他們的理財教育日，我們打算做什麼？ B：我們的員工會到每個班級，用一個大約四十分鐘的簡單撲滿遊戲，教每位【學童】如何存錢。"},{"w":"student","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies at a school or university","c":"學生","s":"A: We need extra help at the shop during the busy holiday season, but our budget is tight, so who should we hire? B: Let's hire a university student for part-time weekend shifts, because many young people want flexible work and some extra money during their winter break.","t":"A：假期旺季時店裡需要額外人手，但我們預算很緊，應該雇用誰？ B：我們雇一位大學【學生】來上週末兼職班吧，因為很多年輕人在寒假期間想要彈性的工作和額外的收入。"},{"w":"playmate","p":"n.","d":"a friend that a child plays with","c":"玩伴","s":"A: Your daughter seems much happier since you moved into the new apartment last month, so what changed for her? B: The family next door has a girl the same age, so now she has a playmate to ride bikes with in the courtyard every afternoon after school.","t":"A：你女兒自從上個月搬進新公寓後好像快樂多了，她有什麼改變？ B：隔壁那家有個同年齡的女孩，所以現在她每天放學後都有【玩伴】可以一起在中庭騎腳踏車。"},{"w":"classmate","p":"n.","d":"a person in the same class as you","c":"同學","s":"A: How did you find out about the job opening at the design company, since they never posted it online? B: An old classmate from my university marketing course works there now, and she told me about the position and recommended me to the manager before the interview.","t":"A：你怎麼知道那間設計公司有職缺的？他們從來沒有在網路上公布。 B：我大學行銷課的一位老【同學】現在在那裡工作，她告訴我這個職位，還在面試前把我推薦給經理。"},{"w":"dependent","p":"n.","d":"a person, such as a child, who needs someone else for money and care","c":"受撫養人；家屬","s":"A: I'm filling out the new health insurance form from human resources, but I'm not sure about one question, so can you help me? B: Sure, they want to know whether you have a dependent, such as a child or an elderly parent who relies on your income, because that changes your monthly payment.","t":"A：我在填人資部新的健康保險表格，但有一題不太確定，你可以幫我嗎？ B：當然，他們想知道你是否有【受撫養人】，例如依靠你收入生活的孩子或年長父母，因為這會影響你每月的保費。"},{"w":"young","p":"adj.","d":"not old; in an early part of life","c":"年輕的；年幼的","s":"A: The new manager seems very confident in meetings, but some staff members think she lacks experience, so how old is she? B: She is quite young, only twenty-eight, but she has already led three successful projects overseas and speaks four languages fluently, so the directors trust her completely.","t":"A：新經理在會議上看起來很有自信，但有些員工覺得她經驗不足，她幾歲？ B：她相當【年輕】，只有二十八歲，但她已經在海外帶領過三個成功的專案，還能流利說四種語言，所以董事們完全信任她。"},{"w":"childish","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in a silly way, like a small child (negative)","c":"幼稚的","s":"A: Did the meeting between the two department heads go well this morning, or are they still arguing about the budget? B: It went badly, because they refused to look at each other and kept blaming each other loudly, which was really childish behavior for two experienced managers in their fifties.","t":"A：今天早上兩位部門主管的會議順利嗎？還是他們仍在為預算爭吵？ B：很糟糕，因為他們拒絕看對方，還一直大聲互相指責，對兩位五十多歲的資深經理來說，這種行為真的很【幼稚】。"},{"w":"childlike","p":"adj.","d":"having the good qualities of a child, such as trust and wonder","c":"孩子般（天真）的","s":"A: Why do so many visitors love the old toy designer who runs the workshop at the craft fair every year? B: Even at eighty, he still has a childlike sense of wonder, and he gets excited about every new idea, which makes both kids and adults smile when they talk with him.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多遊客喜歡那位每年在手工藝市集經營工作坊的老玩具設計師？ B：即使八十歲了，他仍保有【孩子般】的好奇心，對每個新點子都很興奮，讓小孩和大人跟他聊天時都會微笑。"},{"w":"playful","p":"adj.","d":"full of fun and liking to play","c":"愛玩的；頑皮可愛的","s":"A: We need a new mascot for the pet food brand, so what kind of character do you think customers would like best? B: I suggest a playful puppy that jumps around and chases balls in the commercials, because cheerful and energetic animals usually make shoppers feel happy and remember the product.","t":"A：我們的寵物食品品牌需要一個新吉祥物，你覺得顧客會最喜歡什麼樣的角色？ B：我建議在廣告裡用一隻跳來跳去、追著球跑的【愛玩的】小狗，因為開朗又有活力的動物通常會讓消費者感到快樂並記住產品。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: The science museum wants more families to visit on weekends, so what kind of exhibition should they design next? B: They should build a hands-on space where curious children can touch robots, try simple experiments, and ask staff questions, because kids learn best when they can explore by themselves.","t":"A：科學博物館希望週末有更多家庭來參觀，他們接下來應該設計什麼樣的展覽？ B：他們應該建造一個動手做的空間，讓【好奇的】孩子可以摸機器人、試做簡單實驗並向員工提問，因為孩子能自己探索時學得最好。"},{"w":"innocent","p":"adj.","d":"not guilty of a crime; not knowing about bad things","c":"無辜的；清白的；天真的","s":"A: The security camera showed someone taking money from the cash register last night, so did the police find out who did it? B: Yes, and luckily the new cashier was completely innocent, because the video clearly showed a delivery driver opening the drawer after she had already gone home.","t":"A：監視器顯示昨晚有人從收銀機拿錢，警方查出是誰做的嗎？ B：查出來了，幸好新來的收銀員完全是【清白的】，因為影片清楚顯示，在她已經回家後，是一名送貨司機打開了抽屜。"},{"w":"naughty","p":"adj.","d":"behaving badly; not doing what adults say","c":"頑皮的；不聽話的","s":"A: The restaurant manager looked upset during lunch today, so did something go wrong in the dining room? B: A naughty boy kept running between the tables and knocked over a tray of drinks, and his parents just laughed instead of asking him to sit down and behave.","t":"A：餐廳經理今天午餐時看起來很不高興，用餐區出了什麼問題嗎？ B：一個【頑皮的】男孩一直在桌子之間跑來跑去，還撞翻了一盤飲料，他的父母只是笑，而沒有叫他坐下守規矩。"},{"w":"obedient","p":"adj.","d":"doing what you are told to do","c":"聽話的；順從的","s":"A: You said your team is training dogs for the hotel's new pet-friendly program, so how long does the training usually take? B: It takes about six weeks before each dog is calm and obedient enough to sit quietly in the lobby, follow simple commands, and greet guests without jumping on them.","t":"A：你說你們團隊在為飯店新的寵物友善計畫訓練狗，訓練通常要多久？ B：大約要六週，每隻狗才會冷靜、【聽話】到能安靜地坐在大廳、遵守簡單指令，並在不撲向客人的情況下迎接他們。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to grow or make something grow stronger or better","c":"發展；培養","s":"A: The kindergarten across the street wants to buy new toys for its classrooms, so what kind should they choose? B: They should choose building blocks and puzzles, because these toys help young children develop problem-solving skills and learn to work together while they are having fun.","t":"A：對街的幼兒園想為教室買新玩具，他們應該選哪一種？ B：他們應該選積木和拼圖，因為這些玩具能幫助幼童在玩樂中【培養】解決問題的能力，並學會互相合作。"},{"w":"grow up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change from a child into an adult","c":"長大；成長","s":"A: You know so much about farming and fresh vegetables, and our restaurant buyers always ask for your opinion, so where did you learn all this? B: I was lucky to grow up on my grandparents' farm in the south of Taiwan, so I spent every summer picking fruit and helping them sell it at the market.","t":"A：你對農業和新鮮蔬菜懂這麼多，我們餐廳的採購總是問你的意見，你是在哪裡學到這些的？ B：我很幸運能在台灣南部祖父母的農場【長大】，所以每年夏天我都在摘水果，並幫他們在市場上販賣。"},{"w":"educate","p":"v.","d":"to teach someone, especially in a school or about an issue","c":"教育","s":"A: Many customers still throw plastic bottles into the regular trash bins at our supermarket, so how can we change this? B: We should put clear signs and short videos near the entrance to educate shoppers about recycling, and we can give small discounts to people who bring back empty bottles.","t":"A：很多顧客還是把塑膠瓶丟進我們超市的一般垃圾桶，我們要怎麼改變這種情況？ B：我們應該在入口附近放清楚的標示和短片來【教育】顧客關於回收的事，並且可以給帶回空瓶的人小額折扣。"},{"w":"raise","p":"v.","d":"to take care of a child until he or she is an adult","c":"養育；撫養","s":"A: Why did Mr. Chen decide to move his family from the city center to a small town after his promotion last year? B: He wanted to raise his two sons in a quieter place with clean air, good schools, and large parks, even though it means a longer drive to the office.","t":"A：陳先生去年升職後，為什麼決定把家人從市中心搬到一個小鎮？ B：他想在空氣乾淨、學校好、公園大的安靜地方【養育】他的兩個兒子，即使那表示要開更久的車去上班。"},{"w":"nurture","p":"v.","d":"to care for and help someone or something grow","c":"培育；養育","s":"A: Our company keeps losing talented young engineers to bigger competitors, so what can we do to keep them? B: We need to nurture their talent by giving each new engineer an experienced mentor, regular training courses, and clear chances for promotion during their first three years.","t":"A：我們公司一直流失有才華的年輕工程師給大型競爭對手，我們能做什麼來留住他們？ B：我們需要【培育】他們的才能，在他們最初三年給每位新工程師安排一位資深導師、定期訓練課程和明確的升遷機會。"},{"w":"protect","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something safe from harm","c":"保護","s":"A: Parents have been complaining that the playground in our shopping mall is not safe enough, so what are we going to do about it? B: We will install soft rubber floors and higher fences to protect small children from falls, and a security guard will watch the area during busy weekend hours.","t":"A：家長一直抱怨我們購物中心的遊樂場不夠安全，我們要怎麼處理？ B：我們會鋪設柔軟的橡膠地板和加高圍欄來【保護】幼童免於跌倒，而且在週末熱門時段會有一名警衛看守這個區域。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"v.","d":"to punish someone for breaking rules so they behave better","c":"懲處；管教","s":"A: One of the new sales assistants keeps arriving late and leaving early without telling anyone, so what should the store manager do? B: She needs to discipline him fairly by giving him a written warning first, and if the problem continues next month, she may have to reduce his shifts.","t":"A：其中一位新銷售助理一直遲到早退又不告訴任何人，店長應該怎麼做？ B：她需要公平地【懲處】他，先給他一份書面警告，如果下個月問題持續，她可能必須減少他的班次。"},{"w":"mature","p":"v.","d":"to become more adult in behavior; to become fully developed","c":"成熟；長成","s":"A: Our youngest team member made a lot of mistakes when he first joined, but his recent reports are excellent, so what changed? B: He has really started to mature over the past year, because he now plans his work carefully, listens to feedback, and stays calm when clients are difficult.","t":"A：我們團隊最年輕的成員剛加入時犯了很多錯，但他最近的報告非常出色，有什麼改變？ B：他過去一年真的開始【成熟】了，因為他現在會仔細規劃工作、聽取回饋，並在客戶難搞時保持冷靜。"}]},{"unit":54,"theme":"Childhood Activities 童年活動","cards":[{"w":"play","p":"v.","d":"to do things for fun, especially as a child","c":"玩耍","s":"A: The new apartment complex near our office has a large green yard, so do you think families with young kids will like living there? B: Definitely, because parents can watch their children play safely outside while they cook dinner, and the security guard checks the gate every evening.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近的新公寓社區有一大片綠色庭院，你覺得有小孩的家庭會喜歡住在那裡嗎？ B：當然，因為父母煮晚餐時可以看著孩子在外面安全地【玩耍】，而且保全每天晚上都會檢查大門。"},{"w":"game","p":"n.","d":"an activity with rules that people play for fun","c":"遊戲","s":"A: We need an activity for the children at the company family day next Saturday, but the weather might be rainy, so what should we prepare? B: Let's set up a simple board game in the meeting room, because it only needs a table and some chairs, and kids of different ages can join in together.","t":"A：下週六公司家庭日我們需要為孩子準備一個活動，但天氣可能會下雨，我們該準備什麼？ B：我們在會議室擺一個簡單的桌上【遊戲】吧，因為只需要一張桌子和幾把椅子，不同年齡的孩子都能一起參加。"},{"w":"hide-and-seek","p":"n.","d":"a game in which one child looks for the others who are hiding","c":"捉迷藏","s":"A: The kindergarten teachers want a cheap activity for the open house that keeps the children busy in the garden, so do you have any ideas? B: They could organize a round of hide-and-seek, where one child closes their eyes and counts to twenty while the others find secret places behind the trees and bushes.","t":"A：幼兒園老師想在開放日辦一個便宜的活動，讓孩子們在花園裡玩得忙不停，你有什麼點子嗎？ B：他們可以辦一輪【捉迷藏】，一個孩子閉上眼睛數到二十，其他孩子則在樹木和灌木叢後面找祕密的地方躲起來。"},{"w":"tag","p":"n.","d":"a children's game in which one player chases and touches the others","c":"鬼抓人","s":"A: Why were the children at the summer camp so tired and hungry when they came back to the hotel lobby this afternoon? B: They spent almost an hour playing tag on the beach, so whoever was 'it' had to chase the others and touch them before they reached the big umbrella.","t":"A：夏令營的孩子們今天下午回到飯店大廳時，為什麼又累又餓？ B：他們在海灘上玩了將近一小時的【鬼抓人】，當鬼的人必須追其他人，並在他們跑到大陽傘之前碰到他們。"},{"w":"outdoor play","p":"n.phr.","d":"games and activities that children do outside","c":"戶外遊戲","s":"A: The new daycare center downtown charges more than the one near the station, so why are so many working parents choosing it? B: It has a large garden, and the staff plan two hours of outdoor play every day, which helps the children stay healthy, sleep better at night, and make new friends.","t":"A：市中心的新托兒所收費比車站附近那家貴，為什麼還有這麼多上班族父母選擇它？ B：它有一個大花園，而且工作人員每天安排兩小時的【戶外遊戲】，能幫助孩子保持健康、晚上睡得更好，還能交到新朋友。"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to form new pictures and ideas in your mind","c":"想像力","s":"A: The toy company's new advertisement shows only a cardboard box and a little girl, so why did the marketing team choose such a simple idea? B: They wanted to show that a child's imagination can turn an empty box into a spaceship or a castle, and parents responded very positively to that message online.","t":"A：玩具公司的新廣告只有一個紙箱和一個小女孩，行銷團隊為什麼選這麼簡單的點子？ B：他們想表達孩子的【想像力】可以把空箱子變成太空船或城堡，而家長們在網路上對這個訊息的反應非常正面。"},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing new and creative ideas","c":"富有想像力的","s":"A: The publisher received over two hundred stories for its children's writing contest this year, so how did the judges choose the winner? B: They picked a ten-year-old boy's very imaginative story about a talking bicycle that travels around Taiwan, because it was original, funny, and full of surprising ideas.","t":"A：出版社今年的兒童寫作比賽收到超過兩百篇故事，評審是怎麼選出優勝者的？ B：他們選了一個十歲男孩非常【富有想像力】的故事，講一輛會說話的腳踏車環遊台灣，因為它很有原創性、很有趣，而且充滿令人驚喜的點子。"},{"w":"pretend","p":"v.","d":"to act as if something is true when it is not, often in play","c":"假裝","s":"A: Your daughter was talking to her stuffed animals in the waiting room for twenty minutes, so was she bored while you were seeing the bank manager? B: Not at all, she loves to pretend that she owns a small restaurant, so she was taking their orders and serving them imaginary noodles.","t":"A：你女兒在等候室跟她的絨毛玩具說了二十分鐘的話，你和銀行經理談事情時她覺得無聊嗎？ B：一點也不，她很喜歡【假裝】自己開了一家小餐廳，所以她在幫它們點餐，還端上想像出來的麵。"},{"w":"role-play","p":"n.","d":"an activity in which people act as different characters","c":"角色扮演","s":"A: How did the English teacher help the young students feel less nervous about speaking at the school's international day? B: She set up a short role-play in which the children acted as shop owners and customers, so they practiced asking prices and saying thank you before they met the foreign visitors.","t":"A：英文老師是怎麼幫助年幼的學生在學校國際日時說話不那麼緊張的？ B：她安排了一段簡短的【角色扮演】，讓孩子們扮成店主和顧客，所以他們在見到外國訪客之前就練習了問價錢和說謝謝。"},{"w":"drawing","p":"n.","d":"a picture made with a pencil, pen, or crayon","c":"圖畫；素描","s":"A: I noticed a colorful picture of a house and a big sun on your office wall, so did you buy it at the art fair last weekend? B: No, it is a drawing my five-year-old son made with crayons for my birthday, and I put it there because it makes me smile during long meetings.","t":"A：我注意到你辦公室牆上有一幅色彩鮮豔、畫著房子和大太陽的畫，是你上週末在藝術市集買的嗎？ B：不是，那是我五歲兒子用蠟筆為我生日畫的【圖畫】，我把它掛在那裡，因為在冗長的會議中它會讓我微笑。"},{"w":"coloring","p":"n.","d":"the activity of adding color to pictures, often with crayons","c":"著色；塗色","s":"A: The family restaurant on the corner gets very busy on Sunday afternoons, so how do the waiters keep the young customers quiet while they wait for food? B: They give every child a box of crayons and some coloring pages with animals and cartoon cars, so the kids stay at the table and the parents can relax.","t":"A：轉角那家家庭餐廳週日下午很忙，服務生是怎麼讓小客人在等餐時保持安靜的？ B：他們給每個孩子一盒蠟筆和幾張畫有動物和卡通汽車的【著色】頁，這樣孩子就會待在餐桌旁，父母也能放鬆。"},{"w":"painting","p":"n.","d":"the activity of making pictures with paint","c":"繪畫","s":"A: The community center is offering several weekend classes for kids this spring, so which one do you think your daughter will choose? B: She will probably sign up for painting, because she loves mixing bright colors with a brush and wants to make a picture of our cat for her grandmother.","t":"A：社區中心今年春天開了幾堂週末兒童課程，你覺得你女兒會選哪一堂？ B：她大概會報名【繪畫】課，因為她喜歡用畫筆調出鮮豔的顏色，還想畫一張我們家貓咪的畫送給奶奶。"},{"w":"craft","p":"n.","d":"something made by hand with skill, or the activity of making it","c":"手工藝","s":"A: What will the children do during the holiday workshop at the department store while their parents are shopping on the upper floors? B: The staff will help them make a simple paper craft, such as a lantern or a card, using glue, scissors, and colored paper that the store provides for free.","t":"A：家長在百貨公司樓上購物時，孩子們在假日工作坊裡會做什麼？ B：工作人員會幫他們做一個簡單的紙【手工藝品】，例如燈籠或卡片，用的是百貨公司免費提供的膠水、剪刀和色紙。"},{"w":"sing","p":"v.","d":"to make music with your voice","c":"唱歌","s":"A: The kindergarten is holding a small concert for parents at the end of the term, so what will your son's class perform on stage? B: The children will sing three short songs in English while their teacher plays the piano, and they have been practicing every morning after breakfast for two weeks.","t":"A：幼兒園學期末要為家長辦一場小型音樂會，你兒子的班上要表演什麼？ B：孩子們會在老師彈鋼琴時用英文【唱】三首短歌，他們已經每天早餐後練習兩個星期了。"},{"w":"dance","p":"v.","d":"to move your body to music","c":"跳舞","s":"A: Why was the hotel ballroom so noisy during the wedding reception last night, even though the band had already finished? B: The DJ played some popular children's songs, and all the little guests hurried to the middle of the room to dance and spin around until almost eleven o'clock.","t":"A：昨晚的婚宴上樂團已經演奏完了，為什麼飯店宴會廳還這麼吵？ B：DJ放了一些熱門兒歌，所有的小賓客都趕到廳中央【跳舞】、轉圈圈，一直到快十一點。"},{"w":"nursery rhyme","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short traditional poem or song for young children","c":"童謠","s":"A: The children's bookstore wants to attract more young families on weekday mornings, so what new event are the managers planning? B: They will hold a free music hour where a teacher leads parents and babies in singing a classic nursery rhyme like 'Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star' with simple hand movements.","t":"A：童書店想在平日早上吸引更多年輕家庭，經理們在規劃什麼新活動？ B：他們會辦一個免費的音樂時段，由一位老師帶領家長和寶寶一起唱經典【童謠】，例如〈一閃一閃亮晶晶〉，並搭配簡單的手部動作。"},{"w":"storytelling","p":"n.","d":"the activity of telling or reading stories to people","c":"說故事","s":"A: The public library has many visitors on Saturday afternoons, so which event do the young children enjoy most there? B: They love the storytelling hour, when a volunteer reads a picture book aloud with funny voices and asks the kids questions about what might happen next in the plot.","t":"A：公共圖書館週六下午有很多訪客，小朋友在那裡最喜歡哪個活動？ B：他們最喜歡【說故事】時間，一位志工會用逗趣的聲音朗讀繪本，還會問孩子接下來的情節可能會怎麼發展。"},{"w":"reading","p":"n.","d":"the activity of looking at and understanding written words","c":"閱讀","s":"A: The school asked parents to limit screen time at home, so how are you keeping your kids busy in the evenings now? B: We have made thirty minutes of reading part of their bedtime routine, and every Friday we visit the library so they can choose new books about animals and space.","t":"A：學校請家長在家限制孩子使用螢幕的時間，你現在晚上都怎麼讓孩子有事做？ B：我們把三十分鐘的【閱讀】變成他們睡前的固定習慣，而且每週五都去圖書館，讓他們挑選關於動物和太空的新書。"},{"w":"listen","p":"v.","d":"to pay attention to sounds or to what someone says","c":"聆聽","s":"A: The training company is running a weekend program that teaches young children how to behave well during group activities, so what is the first skill they practice? B: The coaches first teach them to listen carefully when someone else is speaking, so they wait for their turn instead of shouting out answers.","t":"A：那家培訓公司正在辦一個週末課程，教小朋友在團體活動中守規矩，他們第一個練習的技能是什麼？ B：教練們會先教他們在別人說話時仔細【聆聽】，讓他們等輪到自己再說，而不是大聲喊出答案。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it","c":"探索","s":"A: Our family is staying at a farm resort in Yilan next month, so what activities does the resort offer for young guests? B: The kids can explore the forest trail with a guide, look for insects under the leaves, and visit a small river where they can see fish and frogs.","t":"A：我們家下個月要住宜蘭的一間農場度假村，那裡有什麼給小房客的活動？ B：孩子們可以跟著導覽員【探索】森林步道、在樹葉底下找昆蟲，還可以去一條小河看魚和青蛙。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking around a place or thing to discover more","c":"探索","s":"A: Why does the new science museum let children touch almost everything instead of keeping the exhibits behind glass? B: The designers believe that hands-on exploration helps kids remember what they learn, so visitors can build bridges, test magnets, and dig for model dinosaur bones in a large sand pit.","t":"A：新的科學博物館為什麼讓孩子幾乎什麼都能摸，而不是把展品放在玻璃後面？ B：設計師相信親自動手的【探索】能幫助孩子記住所學，所以參觀者可以搭橋、測試磁鐵，還能在大沙坑裡挖恐龍骨頭模型。"},{"w":"climb","p":"v.","d":"to go up something using your hands and feet","c":"爬；攀爬","s":"A: The building manager asked us to check the new play area in the lobby before it opens on Monday, so is everything safe for the children? B: Mostly, but the rope wall is too high, and kids could climb over the top and fall onto the hard floor, so we need thicker mats.","t":"A：大樓管理員請我們在週一開放前檢查大廳新的遊戲區，對孩子來說一切都安全嗎？ B：大致上是，但繩網牆太高了，孩子可能會【爬】過頂端掉到堅硬的地板上，所以我們需要更厚的墊子。"},{"w":"run","p":"v.","d":"to move quickly on your feet","c":"跑","s":"A: Why did the school decide to remove some of the old benches from the sports field during the summer holiday? B: The children needed more open space to run around safely at lunchtime, and the teachers were worried that someone would trip over the benches and get hurt.","t":"A：學校為什麼決定在暑假期間移走運動場上一些舊長椅？ B：孩子們午餐時間需要更多空地可以安全地【跑】來跑去，而且老師們擔心有人會被長椅絆倒受傷。"},{"w":"jump","p":"v.","d":"to push yourself off the ground into the air with your legs","c":"跳","s":"A: The trampoline park near the shopping mall is offering a discount for company groups, so should we take our team's children there next month? B: Good idea, the kids can jump as high as they want on the soft surfaces, and there is a café where the parents can sit and chat.","t":"A：購物中心附近的彈跳床樂園有公司團體優惠，我們下個月要不要帶團隊同事的孩子去？ B：好主意，孩子們可以在柔軟的彈跳床上盡情地【跳】，那裡還有一間咖啡館讓家長坐著聊天。"},{"w":"ride","p":"v.","d":"to sit on and control a bicycle, horse, etc.","c":"騎","s":"A: The city just finished building a new riverside park with wide paths, so what will families be able to do there on weekends? B: Children can ride their bicycles along the river without worrying about cars, and there is a rental shop near the entrance for families who don't have their own.","t":"A：市政府剛蓋好一座有寬敞步道的河濱公園，週末家庭可以在那裡做什麼？ B：孩子們可以沿著河邊【騎】腳踏車，不用擔心汽車，而且入口附近有一家出租店，給沒有自己車子的家庭使用。"},{"w":"bike riding","p":"n.phr.","d":"the activity of riding a bicycle for fun or exercise","c":"騎腳踏車","s":"A: Your son seems much more confident and active than he was last year, so has he joined any new after-school clubs recently? B: Yes, he has taken up bike riding with his father every weekend, and they usually travel about ten kilometers along the coast before stopping for breakfast at a small café.","t":"A：你兒子看起來比去年更有自信、更活潑了，他最近有參加什麼新的課後社團嗎？ B：有，他每個週末都跟爸爸去【騎腳踏車】，他們通常沿著海岸騎大約十公里，再停在一家小咖啡館吃早餐。"},{"w":"sports","p":"n.","d":"games or activities in which people use their bodies and often compete","c":"運動","s":"A: The company is planning a family fun day at the stadium in October, so what kind of activities should we include for employees' children? B: We should offer several team sports like soccer and relay races, because they are easy to organize, and the kids will learn to cooperate with new friends.","t":"A：公司打算十月在體育場辦家庭同樂日，我們應該為員工的孩子安排哪些活動？ B：我們應該提供幾項團隊【運動】，例如足球和接力賽，因為它們容易安排，孩子們也能學著和新朋友合作。"},{"w":"swimming","p":"n.","d":"the activity of moving through water using your arms and legs","c":"游泳","s":"A: The hotel we booked for our business trip to Kenting has a large pool, so do you think your kids will enjoy staying there? B: Absolutely, they love swimming more than any other summer activity, and they took lessons at the sports center for three months, so they can now float and kick without help.","t":"A：我們出差去墾丁訂的飯店有一個大泳池，你覺得你的孩子會喜歡住那裡嗎？ B：當然，他們最愛【游泳】，勝過任何其他夏日活動，而且他們在運動中心上了三個月的課，現在不用別人幫忙就能漂浮和踢水了。"},{"w":"playground","p":"n.","d":"an outdoor area with equipment for children to play on","c":"遊樂場","s":"A: The property developer says the new housing project will attract young families, so what facilities are they adding to the site? B: They are building a large playground with slides, swings, and a sandbox in the center of the complex, so parents can watch their children from the windows of their apartments.","t":"A：建商說新的住宅案會吸引年輕家庭，他們在基地上增加了哪些設施？ B：他們正在社區中央蓋一座有溜滑梯、鞦韆和沙坑的大型【遊樂場】，讓父母可以從公寓窗戶看著孩子。"},{"w":"picnic","p":"n.","d":"a meal eaten outdoors, often in a park","c":"野餐","s":"A: The weather forecast says it will be sunny and warm on Sunday, so do you have any plans with your family this weekend? B: We are going to have a picnic by the lake in Daan Park, and the kids will help me make sandwiches and pack fruit and cold drinks in the morning.","t":"A：天氣預報說週日會晴朗溫暖，這個週末你和家人有什麼計畫嗎？ B：我們要去大安公園的湖邊【野餐】，孩子們早上會幫我做三明治，並把水果和冷飲打包好。"},{"w":"collect","p":"v.","d":"to get and keep things of the same type as a hobby","c":"收集","s":"A: Why is your son so excited about the new convenience store promotion that started at the beginning of this month? B: He likes to collect the small cartoon stickers that come with each purchase, and he wants to fill the whole album before the event ends in December.","t":"A：你兒子為什麼對這個月初開始的便利商店新促銷活動這麼興奮？ B：他喜歡【收集】每次購物附贈的小卡通貼紙，而且想在活動十二月結束前把整本集點冊貼滿。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of similar things that someone has gathered","c":"收藏品","s":"A: The toy museum is asking local residents to lend items for its new exhibition about childhood in the 1980s, so are you going to help? B: Yes, my father still has his collection of old metal cars from his school days, and he is happy to let the museum display them for three months.","t":"A：玩具博物館正在請當地居民出借物品，舉辦一個關於1980年代童年的新展覽，你會幫忙嗎？ B：會，我父親還留著他學生時代的舊金屬小汽車【收藏】，他很樂意讓博物館展出三個月。"},{"w":"help out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help someone, especially by doing a share of the work","c":"幫忙","s":"A: The children at your neighbor's house seem very busy in the garden every Saturday morning, so what are they doing out there? B: Their grandparents grow vegetables, and the kids help out by watering the plants and picking tomatoes, which teaches them responsibility and earns them a little pocket money.","t":"A：你鄰居家的孩子每週六早上在花園裡看起來都很忙，他們在那裡做什麼？ B：他們的祖父母種菜，孩子們會【幫忙】澆水和摘番茄，這能培養他們的責任感，還能賺一點零用錢。"},{"w":"chores","p":"n.","d":"small regular jobs at home, like cleaning or washing dishes","c":"家務；雜事","s":"A: How do you get your kids to stop watching cartoons and do something useful on weekend mornings at home? B: We made a simple chart of household chores, such as feeding the dog and folding laundry, and they earn a sticker for each task they finish before lunch.","t":"A：週末早上在家，你是怎麼讓孩子不再看卡通、做點有用的事？ B：我們做了一張簡單的【家務】表，例如餵狗和摺衣服，他們每在午餐前完成一項就能得到一張貼紙。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"嗜好","s":"A: The manager asked about your childhood during the job interview this morning, so what did you tell her? B: I said that my favorite hobby was building model airplanes, because it taught me patience and attention to detail, which are useful skills for an engineering position like this one.","t":"A：今天早上面試時經理問了你的童年，你怎麼回答她？ B：我說我最喜歡的【嗜好】是做模型飛機，因為它教會我耐心和注重細節，這些對像這樣的工程職位都是很有用的技能。"}]},{"unit":56,"theme":"Children's Education 兒童教育","cards":[{"w":"education","p":"n.","d":"the process of teaching and learning, especially at school","c":"教育","s":"A: Our company is thinking about opening a training center for the children of our factory workers, so what do you think parents care about most? B: Most of them want their kids to get a good education, because they believe that strong schooling will help their children find better jobs than they had.","t":"A：我們公司正考慮為工廠員工的孩子開設一個培訓中心，你覺得家長最在乎的是什麼？ B：他們大多數希望孩子能受到良好的【教育】，因為他們相信紮實的學校教育能幫助孩子找到比自己更好的工作。"},{"w":"schooling","p":"n.","d":"the education a child receives at school","c":"學校教育","s":"A: The new manager from Singapore said she moved here with her two sons last month, so where are the boys studying now? B: They are attending an international school near the station, and she told me that their schooling costs a lot but the small classes are worth the money.","t":"A：新來的新加坡經理說她上個月帶著兩個兒子搬來這裡，那兩個男孩現在在哪裡讀書？ B：他們在車站附近的一所國際學校上學，她告訴我他們的【學校教育】花費很高，但小班制是值得的。"},{"w":"learning","p":"n.","d":"the process of gaining knowledge or skills","c":"學習","s":"A: Why did the library decide to buy so many tablets and educational games for the children's corner this year? B: The director believes that learning should be fun, so she wants young visitors to explore science and language through games instead of just sitting quietly with heavy books.","t":"A：圖書館今年為什麼決定為兒童區購買這麼多平板電腦和教育遊戲？ B：館長認為【學習】應該是有趣的，所以她希望年幼的訪客能透過遊戲探索科學和語言，而不只是安靜地坐著看厚重的書。"},{"w":"teach","p":"v.","d":"to show or explain to someone how to do something","c":"教；教導","s":"A: I heard you are volunteering at the community center on Saturday mornings, so what exactly do you do there with the kids? B: I teach a group of ten-year-olds how to use simple computer programs, and afterward we usually play board games together until their parents arrive.","t":"A：我聽說你週六早上在社區中心當志工，你在那裡和孩子們具體做些什麼？ B：我【教】一群十歲的孩子如何使用簡單的電腦程式，之後我們通常會一起玩桌遊，直到他們的父母來接。"},{"w":"teacher","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to help students learn","c":"老師","s":"A: Your daughter seems much more confident about speaking English than she was last year, so what made the biggest difference for her? B: Her new teacher at the language school is very patient, and she always gives every child a chance to speak in front of the class without feeling nervous.","t":"A：你女兒說英文似乎比去年有自信多了，對她來說最大的改變是什麼？ B：她在語言學校的新【老師】非常有耐心，總是給每個孩子在全班面前說話的機會，而不會讓他們感到緊張。"},{"w":"student","p":"n.","d":"a person who is studying at a school or university","c":"學生","s":"A: The science museum is offering free tickets next month, but does the offer include everyone or only certain groups of visitors? B: Any student under eighteen can get in for free if they show a school ID card at the front desk, so it is a great chance for families.","t":"A：科學博物館下個月提供免費門票，但這個優惠是適用所有人還是只限特定族群的訪客？ B：任何未滿十八歲的【學生】只要在櫃台出示學生證就能免費入場，所以這對家庭來說是個很好的機會。"},{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"all the subjects that are taught in a school","c":"課程","s":"A: The board of education announced some major changes for elementary schools starting next September, so what will be different for the kids? B: The new curriculum will include coding classes and more outdoor science projects, and schools will reduce the number of tests that students take each term.","t":"A：教育局宣布從明年九月起國小將有一些重大改變，對孩子來說會有什麼不同？ B：新的【課程】將包含程式設計課和更多戶外科學專題，而且學校會減少學生每學期的考試次數。"},{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"a period of time in which someone is taught something","c":"一堂課；課程","s":"A: Is your son still taking swimming classes at the sports center near your apartment, or did he stop after the summer vacation? B: He still goes every Wednesday, and each lesson lasts about forty-five minutes, so I can finish my shopping at the supermarket before I pick him up.","t":"A：你兒子還在你公寓附近的運動中心上游泳課嗎？還是暑假後就停了？ B：他還是每週三去，每一【堂課】大約四十五分鐘，所以我可以在接他之前先在超市買完東西。"},{"w":"classroom","p":"n.","d":"a room where students have lessons","c":"教室","s":"A: The parents' association raised a lot of money at the spring fair, so how is the school planning to spend it? B: They will repaint every classroom on the second floor and buy new desks and chairs, because the old furniture is broken and too small for the older children.","t":"A：家長會在春季園遊會上募得了不少錢，學校打算怎麼使用這筆錢？ B：他們會重新粉刷二樓的每一間【教室】，並購買新的桌椅，因為舊家具已經壞了，對年紀較大的孩子來說也太小了。"},{"w":"homework","p":"n.","d":"school work that students do at home","c":"回家作業","s":"A: You usually leave the office right at five o'clock these days, so do you have a new class or appointment in the evening? B: Not really, but my twins have a lot of homework now that they are in third grade, and I like to sit with them while they do it after dinner.","t":"A：你最近通常五點一到就下班，晚上是有新的課程還是約會嗎？ B：其實沒有，只是我的雙胞胎升上三年級後有很多【回家作業】，我喜歡晚餐後坐在旁邊陪他們寫。"},{"w":"literacy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to read and write","c":"讀寫能力","s":"A: Why is the publishing company donating thousands of picture books to schools in the mountain areas this year? B: The company wants to improve literacy among young children there, because many of them do not have libraries nearby and some still cannot read simple sentences by the age of eight.","t":"A：出版社今年為什麼要捐贈數千本繪本給山區的學校？ B：公司希望提升當地幼童的【讀寫能力】，因為許多孩子附近沒有圖書館，有些到了八歲還看不懂簡單的句子。"},{"w":"numeracy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand and work with numbers","c":"算術能力","s":"A: The after-school program uses a lot of cooking activities, but how does making cookies actually help the kids with their studies? B: Measuring flour, counting eggs, and dividing the cookies equally all build numeracy, so children practice basic math skills without even noticing that they are learning something.","t":"A：課後輔導班使用很多烹飪活動，但做餅乾到底對孩子的課業有什麼幫助？ B：量麵粉、數雞蛋和平均分配餅乾都能培養【算術能力】，所以孩子們在不知不覺中就練習了基本的數學技巧。"},{"w":"reading","p":"n.","d":"the activity of looking at and understanding written words","c":"閱讀","s":"A: My nephew spends almost every evening playing games on his phone, so how can his parents get him interested in books? B: They could make reading part of the family routine, for example by spending twenty minutes together with stories before bed and visiting the library every weekend.","t":"A：我姪子幾乎每天晚上都在手機上玩遊戲，他父母要怎麼讓他對書產生興趣？ B：他們可以把【閱讀】變成家庭作息的一部分，例如睡前一起花二十分鐘看故事，並且每個週末去圖書館。"},{"w":"writing","p":"n.","d":"the activity or skill of putting words on paper or a screen","c":"寫作","s":"A: The judges for the children's story competition have finished reading all the entries, so did any of them stand out? B: One girl's writing was especially impressive, because she described her grandmother's farm with such clear details that we could almost smell the fresh rice fields.","t":"A：兒童故事比賽的評審已經看完所有參賽作品了，有沒有哪一篇特別突出？ B：有一個女孩的【寫作】特別令人印象深刻，因為她把祖母的農場描寫得非常細膩，我們幾乎能聞到新鮮稻田的味道。"},{"w":"assessment","p":"n.","d":"a way of judging how much someone has learned","c":"評量；評估","s":"A: Before the kids join the advanced English class, does the school check their level, or can parents just sign them up? B: Every child takes a short assessment with a teacher first, which includes a few listening questions and a simple conversation, so the school can place them in the right group.","t":"A：孩子加入英文進階班之前，學校會檢查他們的程度嗎？還是家長直接報名就可以？ B：每個孩子都會先和老師進行一個簡短的【評量】，包括幾題聽力和簡單的對話，這樣學校才能把他們分到合適的組別。"},{"w":"exam","p":"n.","d":"an official test of knowledge or skill","c":"考試","s":"A: Your son looked really tired when I saw him at the bus stop this morning, so is something wrong at school? B: He has been studying late every night because he has an important exam next Monday, and the results will decide whether he can enter the senior high school he wants.","t":"A：我今天早上在公車站看到你兒子，他看起來真的很累，學校發生什麼事了嗎？ B：他每天晚上都讀書到很晚，因為下週一有一場重要的【考試】，結果將決定他能不能進入想讀的高中。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"training people to obey rules and control their behavior","c":"紀律","s":"A: The new kindergarten seems very popular with parents in our neighborhood, so what makes it different from the others? B: The teachers there believe that gentle but firm discipline is important, so they set clear rules about sharing toys and cleaning up, and the children learn to follow them happily.","t":"A：新開的幼兒園似乎很受我們社區家長歡迎，它和其他幼兒園有什麼不同？ B：那裡的老師認為溫和但堅定的【紀律】很重要，所以他們訂下分享玩具和收拾整理的明確規則，孩子們也學會開心地遵守。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about how to do something","c":"指導；輔導","s":"A: My daughter cannot decide whether she should study art or engineering in college, and she is getting really stressed about it. B: Maybe she should ask the school counselor for some guidance, because counselors know a lot about different careers and can help students think about their strengths and interests.","t":"A：我女兒無法決定大學要讀藝術還是工程，她為此感到壓力很大。 B：也許她應該向學校的輔導老師尋求一些【指導】，因為輔導老師很了解各種職業，也能幫助學生思考自己的長處和興趣。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help someone or something, especially when help is needed","c":"支持；幫助","s":"A: Our firm wants to do something useful for the local community this year, so do you have any ideas for a project? B: We could support the reading program at the public library by giving books and sending volunteers twice a month to help children who are falling behind at school.","t":"A：我們公司今年想為當地社區做些有意義的事，你對專案有什麼想法嗎？ B：我們可以透過捐書和每個月派兩次志工，幫助課業落後的孩子，來【支持】公立圖書館的閱讀計畫。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone confidence or hope to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: Your son used to be so shy, but yesterday he sang a song in front of the whole school at the concert, didn't he? B: Yes, his music teacher worked hard to encourage him, and she kept telling him that his voice was beautiful until he finally believed it himself.","t":"A：你兒子以前很害羞，但他昨天在音樂會上當著全校的面唱了一首歌，對吧？ B：是啊，他的音樂老師很努力地【鼓勵】他，一直告訴他他的聲音很好聽，直到他自己終於相信了。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something","c":"激勵；激發動機","s":"A: The kids in the after-school club used to complain about doing math, but now they seem excited about it, so what changed? B: The coordinator found a smart way to motivate them by giving small prizes and points for every finished worksheet, and the class with the most points wins a pizza party.","t":"A：課後社團的孩子們以前抱怨做數學，現在卻似乎很興奮，是什麼改變了？ B：協調員找到一個聰明的方法來【激勵】他們，每完成一張學習單就給小獎品和積分，積分最多的班級可以贏得披薩派對。"},{"w":"educate","p":"v.","d":"to teach someone, especially over a period of time","c":"教育","s":"A: Why is the city hospital sending nurses to visit elementary schools all through the month of October? B: They want to educate children about healthy eating and washing their hands properly, because doctors have seen more kids getting sick from poor habits during the cold season.","t":"A：市立醫院為什麼整個十月都派護理師去拜訪國小？ B：他們想【教育】孩子有關健康飲食和正確洗手的知識，因為醫生發現在寒冷的季節有越來越多孩子因為不良習慣而生病。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to grow or make something grow stronger or better","c":"培養；發展","s":"A: Do you really think the weekend robot club is worth the high fee that the center charges for each term? B: I think so, because it helps kids develop problem-solving skills and teamwork, and my daughter now plans her projects carefully and explains her ideas clearly to her teammates.","t":"A：你真的認為週末機器人社團值得中心每學期收的高額費用嗎？ B：我認為值得，因為它能幫助孩子【培養】解決問題的能力和團隊合作，我女兒現在會仔細規劃她的專案，並清楚地向隊友解釋自己的想法。"},{"w":"practice","p":"v.","d":"to do something again and again to get better at it","c":"練習","s":"A: Your daughter played the violin so beautifully at the company's year-end party, so how long has she been learning? B: Only about two years, but she has to practice for at least an hour every day after school, even on weekends when her friends invite her to go out and play.","t":"A：你女兒在公司尾牙上小提琴拉得真好聽，她學多久了？ B：只有大約兩年，但她每天放學後至少要【練習】一個小時，即使週末朋友找她出去玩也一樣。"},{"w":"focus","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to something","c":"專注","s":"A: The noise from the construction site next to the school has been terrible this month, so how are the students managing in class? B: Many of them find it hard to focus on their lessons, so the principal has asked the builders to do the loudest work only after three o'clock.","t":"A：學校隔壁工地的噪音這個月非常嚴重，學生們上課時怎麼應付？ B：很多學生覺得很難【專注】在課業上，所以校長已經要求建商只在三點以後才進行最吵的工程。"},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"welcoming and including all kinds of people","c":"包容的；融合的","s":"A: The father of a boy who uses a wheelchair asked whether the new private school would accept his son, so what did the school say? B: The principal told him that they run an inclusive program, so the building has ramps and elevators, and every class welcomes children with different needs.","t":"A：一位坐輪椅男孩的父親詢問新的私立學校是否會接受他的兒子，學校怎麼說？ B：校長告訴他學校實施【融合】課程，所以建築物有斜坡和電梯，每個班級都歡迎有不同需求的孩子。"},{"w":"effective","p":"adj.","d":"working well and producing the result you want","c":"有效的","s":"A: We tried several ways to help the new staff's children with their summer homework, so which one worked the best? B: Small study groups were the most effective, because older kids helped younger ones and everyone finished their tasks faster than when they studied alone at home.","t":"A：我們試了幾種方法幫助新進員工的孩子完成暑假作業，哪一種效果最好？ B：小型讀書會最【有效】，因為大孩子會幫助小孩子，每個人都比獨自在家讀書時更快完成任務。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and interesting things or ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: The marketing team was really impressed by the drawings the employees' kids made for our calendar, weren't they? B: Yes, the children were so creative that one boy turned our company logo into a flying dragon, and the design team now wants to use his idea in our next advertisement.","t":"A：行銷團隊對員工的孩子為我們月曆畫的圖真的印象深刻，對吧？ B：是啊，孩子們非常【有創意】，有一個男孩把我們公司的標誌變成了一條飛龍，設計團隊現在想在下一支廣告中使用他的點子。"},{"w":"academic","p":"adj.","d":"related to school, study, and learning","c":"學業的；學術的","s":"A: Why did the private high school offer that girl from the countryside a full scholarship for all three years? B: Her academic results were excellent in every subject, especially science and mathematics, and she also volunteered at the local clinic every weekend to help elderly patients.","t":"A：那所私立高中為什麼提供那位鄉下女孩三年的全額獎學金？ B：她每一科的【學業】成績都很優秀，尤其是自然科學和數學，而且她每個週末還在當地診所當志工幫助年長的病患。"},{"w":"basic","p":"adj.","d":"simple and necessary as a first step","c":"基本的","s":"A: The summer camp is only two weeks long, so can the kids really learn anything useful about computers in such a short time? B: They will not become experts, of course, but they will learn basic skills like typing, saving files, and searching online safely, which will help them a lot at school.","t":"A：夏令營只有兩週，孩子們真的能在這麼短的時間內學到有用的電腦知識嗎？ B：當然他們不會成為專家，但他們會學到【基本】技能，像是打字、儲存檔案和安全地上網搜尋，這對他們在學校會有很大的幫助。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"official, and following the usual system of schools or training","c":"正規的；正式的","s":"A: The new receptionist speaks four languages very well, so did she study them at a university abroad? B: Actually, she had very little formal schooling as a child because her family traveled a lot, but she picked up languages by talking with people in every country they lived in.","t":"A：新來的接待員能說流利的四種語言，她是在國外大學學的嗎？ B：其實她小時候因為家人經常旅行，很少接受【正規】學校教育，但她在他們住過的每個國家透過和當地人交談學會了語言。"},{"w":"early","p":"adj.","d":"happening near the beginning of a period of time","c":"早期的；幼年的","s":"A: Why is the government spending so much money on preschools and training for kindergarten teachers this year? B: Studies show that the early years of a child's life are very important for the brain, so good care before age six can help children do better later at school.","t":"A：政府今年為什麼要花這麼多錢在幼兒園和幼教老師的培訓上？ B：研究顯示孩子生命中的【早期】幾年對大腦非常重要，所以六歲前的良好照顧能幫助孩子日後在學校表現更好。"},{"w":"lifelong","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for the whole of a person's life","c":"終身的","s":"A: Your father retired from the bank last year, but I heard he is taking Japanese and painting classes now, isn't he? B: Yes, he believes in lifelong learning, and he says that studying new things keeps his mind sharp and gives him a reason to meet new friends every week.","t":"A：你父親去年從銀行退休了，但我聽說他現在在上日文課和繪畫課，對嗎？ B：是的，他相信【終身】學習，他說學習新事物能讓頭腦保持敏銳，也讓他每週都有理由認識新朋友。"},{"w":"quality","p":"adj.","d":"of a high standard; very good","c":"優質的","s":"A: Many young families are moving to the new town near the science park, so what is attracting them there? B: Besides the cheaper apartments, the town offers quality education, with modern schools, well-trained teachers, and free after-school activities for every child who lives in the area.","t":"A：很多年輕家庭搬到科學園區附近的新市鎮，是什麼吸引他們去那裡？ B：除了比較便宜的公寓之外，那個市鎮還提供【優質】教育，有現代化的學校、訓練有素的老師，以及給區內每個孩子的免費課後活動。"},{"w":"well-rounded","p":"adj.","d":"having many different skills and interests","c":"全面發展的","s":"A: Why do so many parents in this neighborhood send their children to music, sports, and art classes on weekends? B: They want their kids to become well-rounded people who are good at many things, not just test scores, because companies today look for people with a wide range of skills.","t":"A：為什麼這個社區有這麼多家長在週末送孩子去上音樂、運動和美術課？ B：他們希望孩子成為【全面發展】的人，擅長很多事情，而不只是考試成績，因為現在的公司都在尋找具備多種技能的人。"}]},{"unit":57,"theme":"Chocolate 巧克力","cards":[{"w":"cocoa","p":"n.","d":"powder made from roasted cacao beans, used in drinks and baking","c":"可可（粉）","s":"A: The café wants to add a warm winter drink to the menu before the holiday season, so what ingredients should we order from the supplier this week? B: Let's order a large bag of good-quality cocoa powder, because customers love hot chocolate on cold evenings and we can also use it in our brownies.","t":"A：咖啡館想在節慶季節前在菜單上新增一款冬季熱飲，我們這週該向供應商訂哪些材料？ B：我們訂一大袋優質的【可可】粉吧，因為顧客在寒冷的晚上很喜歡熱巧克力，我們也可以把它用在布朗尼裡。"},{"w":"cacao","p":"n.","d":"the tree or raw beans that chocolate is made from","c":"可可樹；可可豆","s":"A: Our marketing team wants to explain where our chocolate comes from on the new website, so do you have any photos from the farm visit last spring? B: Yes, I took dozens of pictures of the farmers in Ghana picking cacao pods and drying the beans in the sun before shipping them to our factory.","t":"A：我們的行銷團隊想在新網站上說明我們的巧克力來自哪裡，你有去年春天參訪農場的照片嗎？ B：有，我拍了幾十張迦納農民採摘【可可】果莢、並在運往我們工廠前把豆子放在陽光下曬乾的照片。"},{"w":"bar","p":"n.","d":"a small flat block of chocolate or other food","c":"條；塊","s":"A: I want to buy something small for each member of my team to thank them for working late during the busy season, but I don't have much money left. What do you suggest? B: You could give everyone a bar of dark chocolate from the shop downstairs, because it is cheap, nicely wrapped, and easy to leave on their desks.","t":"A：我想買點小東西送給團隊的每位成員，感謝他們在旺季加班，但我剩的錢不多了。你有什麼建議？ B：你可以從樓下的店買一【條】黑巧克力送給每個人，因為它便宜、包裝漂亮，又方便放在他們的桌上。"},{"w":"truffle","p":"n.","d":"a soft, round chocolate candy, often with a creamy center","c":"松露巧克力","s":"A: The hotel manager asked us to choose a small sweet to leave on each guest's pillow at night, so which option did the kitchen staff recommend? B: They suggested a handmade chocolate truffle rolled in cocoa powder, because it looks elegant, tastes wonderful, and guests often mention it in their online reviews.","t":"A：飯店經理請我們選一款晚上放在每位客人枕頭上的小甜點，廚房員工推薦哪一種？ B：他們建議裹上可可粉的手工【松露巧克力】，因為它看起來高雅、味道很棒，而且客人常在網路評論中提到它。"},{"w":"bonbon","p":"n.","d":"a small sweet candy, often covered in chocolate","c":"夾心糖；糖果","s":"A: The front desk wants to put a bowl of candy in the lobby for visitors who wait for their appointments, so what kind should we order? B: Let's order a large box from the local chocolate maker, because each bonbon is wrapped in colorful paper, easy to share, and won't melt in the air-conditioned waiting area.","t":"A：櫃檯想在大廳放一碗糖果給等候預約的訪客，我們該訂哪一種？ B：我們向本地巧克力商訂一大盒吧，因為每顆【夾心糖】都包著彩色糖紙，方便分享，而且在有空調的等候區也不會融化。"},{"w":"filling","p":"n.","d":"the soft food inside a cake, candy, or pastry","c":"餡料；內餡","s":"A: Several customers said our new chocolate pastries were too dry last week, so has the bakery team found a way to improve the recipe before the weekend? B: Yes, they added a soft orange filling inside each pastry, and the testers in the office said it tastes fresher and much more interesting now.","t":"A：上週有幾位顧客說我們新的巧克力酥皮點心太乾，烘焙團隊在週末前找到改良食譜的方法了嗎？ B：有，他們在每個點心裡加了柔軟的柳橙【內餡】，辦公室的試吃人員說現在吃起來更清爽，也有趣多了。"},{"w":"cocoa butter","p":"n.phr.","d":"the natural fat from cacao beans, used in chocolate and skin creams","c":"可可脂","s":"A: Why does the expensive chocolate from the Swiss supplier feel so much smoother than the cheaper brand we sold last year? B: The Swiss company uses pure cocoa butter instead of vegetable oil, so the chocolate melts slowly on your tongue, and that is why many customers are happy to pay a higher price.","t":"A：為什麼瑞士供應商的高價巧克力吃起來比我們去年賣的便宜品牌滑順這麼多？ B：那家瑞士公司使用純【可可脂】而不是植物油，所以巧克力會在舌頭上慢慢融化，這就是很多顧客樂意付更高價格的原因。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"tasting of sugar","c":"甜的","s":"A: The new energy bar we are testing is popular with the younger staff, but why did the older managers give it such low scores in the survey? B: Most of them said it was far too sweet for their taste, so the product team plans to reduce the sugar and add more nuts before the official launch in March.","t":"A：我們正在測試的新能量棒很受年輕員工歡迎，但為什麼年長的主管在調查中給它這麼低的分數？ B：他們大多說它對他們來說太【甜】了，所以產品團隊打算在三月正式上市前減少糖分，並加入更多堅果。"},{"w":"bitter","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, sharp taste that is not sweet","c":"苦的","s":"A: I tried the ninety-percent chocolate that the sales representative left in the meeting room this morning, but I could only finish one small piece. Did you like it? B: Not really, because it was much too bitter for me, although our director said it tastes perfect with a strong cup of black coffee after lunch.","t":"A：我試了業務代表今天早上留在會議室的百分之九十巧克力，但我只吃得完一小塊。你喜歡嗎？ B：不太喜歡，因為對我來說太【苦】了，不過我們主任說它午餐後配一杯濃黑咖啡吃剛剛好。"},{"w":"rich","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, full flavor, often with a lot of butter, cream, or chocolate","c":"濃郁的","s":"A: We need a dessert for the client dinner on Thursday night, but some guests may feel full after the main course, so should we serve the chocolate cake? B: I'd choose something lighter, because that cake is very rich and heavy, and people usually prefer fresh fruit or sorbet after a big meal.","t":"A：週四晚上的客戶晚宴我們需要一道甜點，但有些客人吃完主菜可能會很飽，我們該上巧克力蛋糕嗎？ B：我會選清淡一點的，因為那個蛋糕非常【濃郁】又厚重，大家大餐後通常比較喜歡新鮮水果或雪酪。"},{"w":"smooth","p":"adj.","d":"having an even texture without lumps","c":"滑順的","s":"A: The chocolate sauce in our new dessert looked lumpy in the photos for the menu, so did the kitchen staff find out what went wrong yesterday? B: They heated it too quickly, so today the chef stirred it slowly over low heat until it became completely smooth and shiny, and the new photos look excellent.","t":"A：菜單照片中我們新甜點的巧克力醬看起來結塊了，廚房員工昨天找出問題出在哪裡了嗎？ B：他們加熱得太快了，所以今天主廚用小火慢慢攪拌，直到它變得完全【滑順】又有光澤，新照片看起來很棒。"},{"w":"creamy","p":"adj.","d":"soft and thick like cream","c":"綿密的；含奶油的","s":"A: Our café is planning a new cold drink for the summer months, and the owner wants something that feels special, so what did the test group prefer? B: Most people chose the chocolate milkshake made with fresh ice cream, because it was thick and creamy, and it reminded them of the drinks they had as children.","t":"A：我們咖啡館正在規劃夏季的新冷飲，老闆想要一款感覺特別的，試飲小組比較喜歡哪一款？ B：大多數人選了用新鮮冰淇淋做的巧克力奶昔，因為它濃稠又【綿密】，讓他們想起小時候喝的飲料。"},{"w":"dark","p":"adj.","d":"(of chocolate) containing a lot of cocoa and little or no milk","c":"黑的；深色的","s":"A: The health company wants to give its members a small chocolate gift, but it should match its healthy image, so which type do you think fits best? B: I'd recommend dark chocolate with at least seventy percent cocoa, because it has less sugar than other kinds, and many people believe it is better for the heart.","t":"A：那家健康公司想送會員一份小巧克力禮物，但要符合它健康的形象，你覺得哪一種最合適？ B：我會推薦可可含量至少百分之七十的【黑】巧克力，因為它的糖比其他種類少，而且很多人認為它對心臟比較好。"},{"w":"milk","p":"n.","d":"the white liquid from cows; \"milk chocolate\" is chocolate made with milk","c":"牛奶","s":"A: The children's hospital asked us to donate chocolate for its holiday party next Saturday, so which kind should we send to make the kids happy? B: Most young children find dark chocolate too strong, so let's send milk chocolate in small fun shapes, because it is softer, sweeter, and much more popular with kids.","t":"A：兒童醫院請我們為下週六的節日派對捐贈巧克力，我們該送哪一種才能讓孩子們開心？ B：大多數小孩覺得黑巧克力太濃烈，所以我們送造型有趣的小塊【牛奶】巧克力吧，因為它更軟、更甜，也更受孩子歡迎。"},{"w":"white","p":"adj.","d":"(of chocolate) made from cocoa butter, sugar, and milk, without dark cocoa solids","c":"白的","s":"A: The bakery wants to decorate the wedding cookies for Saturday's big order with a different color, because the brown chocolate looks too plain. Any ideas? B: We could melt some white chocolate and draw thin lines on top, because it stands out nicely against the brown, and the bride said she wants an elegant look.","t":"A：麵包店想用不同的顏色裝飾週六那筆大訂單的婚禮餅乾，因為咖啡色巧克力看起來太單調了。有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們可以融化一些【白】巧克力在上面畫細線，因為它在咖啡色上很顯眼，而且新娘說她想要高雅的感覺。"},{"w":"melt","p":"v.","d":"to change from solid to liquid because of heat","c":"融化","s":"A: We are shipping two hundred boxes of chocolate to our client in Kaohsiung next week, but the weather forecast says it will be very hot. How can we protect them? B: We should use the refrigerated delivery service, because the chocolates will quickly melt in a normal truck, and the client would definitely ask for a refund.","t":"A：我們下週要運兩百盒巧克力給高雄的客戶，但氣象預報說天氣會很熱。我們要怎麼保護它們？ B：我們應該用冷藏配送服務，因為巧克力在一般貨車裡很快就會【融化】，客戶一定會要求退款。"},{"w":"temper","p":"v.","d":"to heat and cool chocolate carefully so it becomes shiny and firm","c":"為（巧克力）調溫","s":"A: The chocolates from the new trainee look dull and gray instead of shiny, and some of them break too easily. What do you think the problem is? B: He probably didn't temper the chocolate correctly, so I will show him how to heat and cool it to the right temperatures during tomorrow's training session.","t":"A：新實習生做的巧克力看起來暗沉灰白而不是有光澤，有些還很容易斷裂。你覺得問題出在哪裡？ B：他可能沒有正確地為巧克力【調溫】，所以我明天培訓時會教他如何把它加熱和冷卻到正確的溫度。"},{"w":"coat","p":"v.","d":"to cover something with a thin layer","c":"裹上；覆蓋","s":"A: The strawberries we bought for the company's anniversary party look fresh, but they seem a little plain for such a special event. Any suggestions? B: We could coat them in melted dark chocolate and add some nuts on top, because guests usually love dipped fruit, and it looks very attractive on the dessert table.","t":"A：我們為公司週年派對買的草莓看起來很新鮮，但對這麼特別的活動來說似乎有點單調。有什麼建議嗎？ B：我們可以把它們【裹上】融化的黑巧克力，再在上面撒些堅果，因為客人通常很喜歡沾醬水果，而且放在甜點桌上看起來很吸引人。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤","s":"A: Our team wants to raise money for the local animal shelter next Friday, but we have a very small budget for the event. Do you have any ideas? B: Several of us could bake chocolate brownies at home on Thursday night and sell them in the lobby, because people always buy homemade treats for a good cause.","t":"A：我們團隊想在下週五為本地動物收容所募款，但活動預算非常少。你有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們幾個人可以週四晚上在家【烤】巧克力布朗尼，然後在大廳販售，因為大家總是會為了好的目的買自製點心。"},{"w":"flavor","p":"n.","d":"the particular taste of a food or drink","c":"口味；風味","s":"A: The marketing department wants to launch a limited chocolate product for the summer, so what did customers ask for in last month's online survey? B: Many of them asked for a new flavor like mango or passion fruit, because they think tropical tastes feel more refreshing during the hot months in Taiwan.","t":"A：行銷部想在夏天推出一款限定巧克力產品，顧客在上個月的線上調查中提出了什麼要求？ B：很多人希望有像芒果或百香果這樣的新【口味】，因為他們覺得熱帶風味在台灣炎熱的月份裡感覺更清爽。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong, pleasant smell","c":"香氣","s":"A: Why do so many people walk into the chocolate shop near the train station, even when they are in a hurry to catch the morning train? B: The owner makes hot chocolate near the front door every morning, so the sweet aroma fills the whole street, and commuters find it hard to walk past without buying something.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多人走進火車站附近的巧克力店，即使他們正趕著搭早班火車？ B：老闆每天早上都在門口附近做熱巧克力，所以甜甜的【香氣】瀰漫整條街，通勤族很難不買點東西就走過去。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: The restaurant is preparing the set menu for the company's year-end banquet, and the manager wants to know what we would like to serve after the main course. B: Let's choose a warm chocolate cake with vanilla ice cream for dessert, because almost everyone likes it, and it is the chef's most famous dish.","t":"A：餐廳正在準備公司尾牙的套餐菜單，經理想知道主菜之後我們想上什麼。 B：我們選溫熱的巧克力蛋糕配香草冰淇淋當【甜點】吧，因為幾乎每個人都喜歡，而且這是主廚最有名的料理。"},{"w":"treat","p":"n.","d":"something special and pleasant, such as food, that you give or enjoy","c":"犒賞；點心","s":"A: Our sales team finally reached its yearly target this afternoon after months of hard work, so how should the manager thank everyone before the weekend? B: She is planning to bring a box of fancy Belgian chocolates as a special treat for the team, and she will also let everyone leave an hour early on Friday.","t":"A：我們業務團隊經過幾個月的努力，今天下午終於達成年度目標，經理在週末前該怎麼感謝大家？ B：她打算帶一盒精緻的比利時巧克力作為團隊的特別【犒賞】，而且週五還會讓大家提早一小時下班。"},{"w":"indulgence","p":"n.","d":"something you enjoy that is not really necessary, often a little unhealthy","c":"放縱；享受","s":"A: You usually eat a very healthy lunch every day, so why did you buy that expensive chocolate cake at the café downstairs this afternoon? B: I finished a difficult project report after working late all week, so this cake is my small indulgence, and I will go back to salads and fruit on Monday.","t":"A：你平常每天午餐都吃得很健康，那為什麼今天下午在樓下咖啡館買了那個昂貴的巧克力蛋糕？ B：我整週加班，終於完成了一份困難的專案報告，所以這塊蛋糕是我的小小【放縱】，週一我就會回去吃沙拉和水果。"},{"w":"craving","p":"n.","d":"a very strong wish to eat or have something","c":"渴望；嘴饞","s":"A: Why do you always keep a few pieces of chocolate in your desk drawer, even though you say you are trying to eat less sugar this year? B: I often get a strong craving for something sweet around three o'clock, so one small piece helps me stay focused until the end of the working day.","t":"A：你說今年想少吃糖，為什麼總是在桌子抽屜裡放幾塊巧克力？ B：我常在三點左右非常【渴望】吃點甜的，所以吃一小塊能幫我保持專注到下班。"},{"w":"snack","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of food eaten between meals","c":"點心；零食","s":"A: The training session on Wednesday will last from nine to five, and the trainer is worried that people will get tired after lunch. What should we prepare? B: Let's put a basket of chocolate cookies and fruit at the back of the room, so everyone can grab a quick snack during the short afternoon break.","t":"A：週三的培訓從九點持續到五點，講師擔心大家午餐後會累。我們該準備什麼？ B：我們在教室後面放一籃巧克力餅乾和水果吧，這樣大家在下午短暫休息時可以快速拿點【點心】吃。"},{"w":"luxury","p":"n.","d":"something expensive and enjoyable that you do not really need","c":"奢侈品；奢華","s":"A: Why does the department store charge almost two thousand dollars for that small box of chocolates, when the supermarket sells similar ones for much less? B: That brand sells itself as a luxury, so every piece is handmade in France, wrapped in gold paper, and packed in a beautiful wooden box.","t":"A：為什麼百貨公司那一小盒巧克力要價將近兩千元，超市類似的卻便宜得多？ B：那個品牌把自己定位為【奢侈品】，所以每一顆都是在法國手工製作，用金色紙包裝，再裝進漂亮的木盒裡。"},{"w":"handmade","p":"adj.","d":"made by hand, not by machine","c":"手工製的","s":"A: The small shop on Lin Street sells chocolates at twice the price of the big brands, but it always has a long line on weekends. Why is that? B: Everything there is handmade by the owner and two assistants in the kitchen behind the shop, so customers know each piece is fresh and made with care.","t":"A：林街那家小店的巧克力價格是大品牌的兩倍，但週末總是大排長龍。為什麼會這樣？ B：那裡的每樣東西都是老闆和兩位助手在店後面的廚房【手工製作】的，所以顧客知道每一顆都新鮮又用心。"},{"w":"organic","p":"adj.","d":"grown without chemical fertilizers or pesticides","c":"有機的","s":"A: Our supermarket chain wants to attract more health-conscious shoppers this year, so which new chocolate products should we put on the shelves first? B: Let's start with bars made from organic cocoa grown without chemicals, because younger customers check labels carefully, and they are willing to pay more for natural products.","t":"A：我們的連鎖超市今年想吸引更多注重健康的顧客，我們該先把哪些新的巧克力產品上架？ B：我們先從用不含化學物質種植的【有機】可可做成的巧克力條開始吧，因為年輕顧客會仔細看標籤，而且願意為天然產品多付錢。"},{"w":"packaging","p":"n.","d":"the boxes, paper, or plastic used to wrap and sell a product","c":"包裝","s":"A: Sales of our chocolate gift boxes dropped last quarter, even though customers still say the taste is excellent. What do you think went wrong? B: The design team believes the packaging looks old-fashioned compared with our competitors' products, so they are creating a brighter box with a modern logo for the holiday season.","t":"A：雖然顧客仍然說味道很棒，但我們巧克力禮盒上一季的銷量下滑了。你覺得哪裡出了問題？ B：設計團隊認為和競爭對手的產品相比，我們的【包裝】看起來很過時，所以他們正在為節慶季節設計一款有現代標誌、更明亮的盒子。"},{"w":"gift","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone, often on a special occasion","c":"禮物","s":"A: Our most important client in Tokyo is retiring at the end of this month after thirty years, so what should we send to thank her for her support? B: Let's send a beautiful box of local chocolates with a handwritten card as a farewell gift, because she always enjoyed tasting Taiwanese sweets during her visits.","t":"A：我們在東京最重要的客戶做了三十年，這個月底就要退休了，我們該送什麼感謝她的支持？ B：我們送一盒漂亮的在地巧克力配上手寫卡片作為臨別【禮物】吧，因為她每次來訪時都很喜歡品嚐台灣甜點。"},{"w":"satisfying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel pleased because it gives you what you need or want","c":"令人滿足的","s":"A: I usually feel hungry again an hour after eating a regular candy bar, so why do you choose the chocolate with nuts for your afternoon break? B: The nuts give it more protein and fiber, so it is much more satisfying and keeps me full until dinner, especially on days when I have long meetings.","t":"A：我平常吃完一般的糖果棒一小時後又會餓，為什麼你下午休息時都選有堅果的巧克力？ B：堅果讓它有更多蛋白質和纖維，所以更【令人滿足】，能讓我一直飽到晚餐，尤其是在我有長時間會議的日子。"},{"w":"decadent","p":"adj.","d":"very rich and enjoyable, in a way that feels like a bit too much","c":"極致奢華的；濃郁享受的","s":"A: The hotel's new chocolate dessert costs almost five hundred dollars, so why are so many guests posting photos of it on social media this month? B: It is a truly decadent creation with three layers of chocolate, gold leaf, and a warm sauce poured at the table, so people feel it is worth the price.","t":"A：飯店新推出的巧克力甜點要價將近五百元，為什麼這個月有這麼多客人在社群媒體上貼它的照片？ B：它是一道真正【極致奢華】的作品，有三層巧克力、金箔，還有在桌邊淋上的熱醬汁，所以大家覺得物有所值。"}]},{"unit":58,"theme":"City 城市","cards":[{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a city or town","c":"城市的；都市的","s":"A: Our company is planning to open three new fitness centers next year, so should we choose locations in small towns or in big cities? B: I think we should focus on urban areas first, because young office workers who live near the city center have more money and less free time to drive far away for exercise.","t":"A：我們公司計畫明年開三家新的健身中心，我們應該選在小鎮還是大城市？ B：我認為我們應該先把重點放在【都市】地區，因為住在市中心附近的年輕上班族比較有錢，也比較沒有空閒時間開車到遠處運動。"},{"w":"downtown","p":"n.","d":"the main business area in the center of a city","c":"市中心；商業區","s":"A: The client from Singapore wants to meet us on Thursday afternoon, but she is staying at a hotel near the airport, so where should we hold the meeting? B: Let's book a quiet meeting room near downtown, because it is only twenty minutes away by train and there are many good restaurants nearby for lunch afterward.","t":"A：新加坡的客戶想在星期四下午和我們見面，但她住在機場附近的飯店，我們應該在哪裡開會？ B：我們在【市中心】附近訂一間安靜的會議室吧，因為搭火車只要二十分鐘，而且附近有很多不錯的餐廳可以在會後吃午餐。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區","s":"A: You used to live in a small apartment right next to the office, so why did you decide to move so far away last spring? B: After our second child was born, we bought a house with a garden in a quiet suburb, and although my trip to work is longer now, my kids have much more space to play outside.","t":"A：你以前住在辦公室旁邊的小公寓，為什麼去年春天決定搬到那麼遠的地方？ B：我們第二個孩子出生後，在一個安靜的【郊區】買了一間有花園的房子，雖然我現在上班的路程比較長，但孩子們有更多空間可以在戶外玩。"},{"w":"neighborhood","p":"n.","d":"a small area of a town and the people who live there","c":"社區；街坊","s":"A: The real estate agent showed me two apartments today, and they are almost the same price, so how should I decide between them? B: You should walk around each neighborhood in the evening, because it will help you see whether the area feels safe, whether there are shops nearby, and how noisy it becomes at night.","t":"A：房仲今天帶我看了兩間公寓，價格幾乎一樣，我該怎麼在兩者之間做決定？ B：你應該在傍晚到每個【社區】附近走走，因為這能幫你看出那一帶是否讓人覺得安全、附近有沒有商店，以及晚上會變得多吵。"},{"w":"street","p":"n.","d":"a public road in a city or town with buildings along it","c":"街道","s":"A: I am driving to the new client's office for the first time this afternoon, but my GPS keeps showing two different addresses, so can you help me? B: Their building is on Elm street, right across from the big department store, and you can park in the public lot behind the post office.","t":"A：我今天下午要第一次開車去新客戶的辦公室，但我的導航一直顯示兩個不同的地址，你可以幫我嗎？ B：他們的大樓在榆樹【街】上，就在那家大百貨公司正對面，你可以把車停在郵局後面的公共停車場。"},{"w":"avenue","p":"n.","d":"a wide street in a city, often with trees","c":"大街；大道","s":"A: The marketing team wants our new store to be seen by as many shoppers as possible, so which location do you prefer? B: I prefer the empty shop on Fifth avenue, because the wide road is lined with famous brand stores and thousands of tourists walk past it every weekend, even though the rent is quite high.","t":"A：行銷團隊希望我們的新店能被越多購物者看到越好，你比較喜歡哪個地點？ B：我比較喜歡第五【大道】上那間空店面，因為那條寬闊的路兩旁都是知名品牌商店，每個週末有數千名觀光客經過，雖然租金相當高。"},{"w":"boulevard","p":"n.","d":"a wide city road, often with trees on both sides","c":"林蔭大道","s":"A: The city government plans to hold the international marathon next month, so which roads will be closed on the morning of the race? B: The main boulevard that runs from the train station to the river will be closed from five to eleven, so employees who drive to work should leave home early or take the subway.","t":"A：市政府計畫下個月舉辦國際馬拉松，比賽當天早上哪些道路會封閉？ B：從火車站延伸到河邊的那條主要【林蔭大道】會從五點封到十一點，所以開車上班的員工應該提早出門或改搭捷運。"},{"w":"district","p":"n.","d":"a particular area of a city or country","c":"區；地區","s":"A: Our bank is looking for a place to open a new branch for small business owners, so do you have any recommendations in the city? B: The financial district near City Hall would be ideal, because many companies have their offices there and the area is easy to reach by both bus and train.","t":"A：我們銀行正在找地點，要為小型企業主開一家新分行，你對市區有什麼建議嗎？ B：市政府附近的金融【區】會很理想，因為很多公司的辦公室都在那裡，而且搭公車和火車都很容易到達。"},{"w":"skyscraper","p":"n.","d":"a very tall modern building in a city","c":"摩天大樓","s":"A: The architecture firm has invited us to visit their newest project downtown, so what exactly have they been building for the past three years? B: They have just finished a sixty-floor skyscraper with offices, a hotel, and a shopping center inside, and visitors can enjoy an amazing view of the whole city from the top floor.","t":"A：那家建築事務所邀請我們去參觀他們在市中心的最新案子，他們過去三年到底在蓋什麼？ B：他們剛完成一棟六十層樓的【摩天大樓】，裡面有辦公室、飯店和購物中心，訪客可以從頂樓欣賞整座城市的壯觀景色。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"a famous building or place that is easy to recognize","c":"地標","s":"A: Our overseas guests will arrive on Saturday, and they only have one free afternoon before the conference starts, so where should we take them? B: We should take them to Taipei 101, because it is the city's most famous landmark, and they can also visit the shopping mall and the food court on the lower floors.","t":"A：我們的海外貴賓星期六抵達，會議開始前他們只有一個空閒的下午，我們應該帶他們去哪裡？ B：我們應該帶他們去台北101，因為那是這座城市最有名的【地標】，他們還可以逛逛低樓層的購物中心和美食街。"},{"w":"square","p":"n.","d":"an open public area in a city with buildings around it","c":"廣場","s":"A: The company wants to hold a free outdoor concert to celebrate its twentieth anniversary, so where can thousands of people gather at once? B: The main square in front of the old city hall is large enough, and the city government usually gives permission for public events there as long as we apply two months early.","t":"A：公司想舉辦一場免費戶外音樂會慶祝二十週年，哪裡可以一次容納數千人聚集？ B：舊市政廳前的主【廣場】夠大，而且只要我們提早兩個月申請，市政府通常會核准在那裡舉辦公開活動。"},{"w":"plaza","p":"n.","d":"an open public space, often with shops around it","c":"廣場；購物廣場","s":"A: The new office building has a large open space on the ground floor, so how is the management company planning to use it? B: They are turning it into a shopping plaza with cafés, a bookstore, and benches under the trees, so that employees and local residents can relax there during lunch breaks and on weekends.","t":"A：新辦公大樓的一樓有一大片開放空間，管理公司打算怎麼使用它？ B：他們要把它改成一個購物【廣場】，裡面有咖啡館、書店和樹下的長椅，讓員工和當地居民可以在午休時間和週末在那裡放鬆。"},{"w":"park","p":"n.","d":"a large public area with grass and trees","c":"公園","s":"A: Many of our employees have said that they feel stressed and tired after sitting in front of their computers all day, so what can we do? B: We could organize a short walking group at lunchtime, because there is a beautiful park with a lake and shady trees only five minutes from our office building.","t":"A：很多員工反映整天坐在電腦前讓他們覺得壓力大又疲累，我們能做些什麼？ B：我們可以在午餐時間組織一個簡短的健走小組，因為離我們辦公大樓只要五分鐘就有一座有湖和樹蔭的漂亮【公園】。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars and other vehicles moving on roads","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: You are usually the first person in the office every morning, so why did you arrive almost an hour late today? B: There was a serious accident on the highway near the bridge, and the traffic was so heavy that my car barely moved for forty minutes, so next time I will probably take the train instead.","t":"A：你通常每天早上都是第一個到辦公室的人，今天為什麼遲到將近一個小時？ B：橋附近的高速公路發生嚴重車禍，【交通】非常壅塞，我的車有四十分鐘幾乎動不了，所以下次我可能會改搭火車。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work","c":"通勤","s":"A: Since you moved to Taoyuan last year, how long does it take you to get to our Taipei office every morning? B: I commute by high-speed rail and then take the subway for two stops, so the whole trip takes about fifty minutes, which gives me enough time to read the news and answer emails.","t":"A：你去年搬到桃園之後，每天早上到我們台北辦公室要花多久時間？ B：我搭高鐵【通勤】，然後再坐兩站捷運，所以整趟路程大約五十分鐘，讓我有足夠的時間看新聞和回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of too many people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: I need to buy a birthday present for my manager after work today, so do you think I should go to the night market or the department store? B: I would avoid the night market tonight, because it is always extremely crowded on Friday evenings, and you will spend more time waiting in lines than actually shopping.","t":"A：我今天下班後需要幫經理買生日禮物，你覺得我該去夜市還是百貨公司？ B：我今晚會避開夜市，因為星期五晚上那裡總是非常【擁擠】，你排隊等候的時間會比真正逛街的時間還多。"},{"w":"busy","p":"adj.","d":"full of people, vehicles or activity","c":"繁忙的；熱鬧的","s":"A: The owner wants to move our small bakery to a new location next year, so what kind of place is she looking for? B: She wants a shop on a busy corner near the train station, because thousands of commuters walk past there every morning and many of them would happily buy fresh bread on the way to work.","t":"A：老闆想在明年把我們的小麵包店搬到新地點，她在找什麼樣的地方？ B：她想要一間在火車站附近【熱鬧】街角的店面，因為每天早上有數千名通勤族從那裡經過，很多人會很樂意在上班途中買新鮮麵包。"},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy, life and excitement","c":"充滿活力的","s":"A: Our travel agency is creating a new tour package for young travelers, so what kind of city do you think they would enjoy most? B: Young people usually love a vibrant city with colorful street art, live music, and lively night markets, so I suggest that we include Kaohsiung and Tainan in the trip.","t":"A：我們旅行社正在為年輕旅客設計新的套裝行程，你覺得他們最喜歡哪一種城市？ B：年輕人通常喜愛有繽紛街頭藝術、現場音樂和熱鬧夜市、【充滿活力】的城市，所以我建議把高雄和台南排進行程。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"new and using the latest ideas or designs","c":"現代的","s":"A: The old train station looks very different from the photos I saw last year, so did the city government rebuild it? B: Yes, they kept the historic front wall but replaced the inside with a bright and modern hall that has glass roofs, digital signs, and comfortable waiting areas for passengers.","t":"A：舊火車站看起來和我去年看到的照片很不一樣，市政府重建了它嗎？ B：是的，他們保留了具歷史意義的正面牆，但把內部換成一個明亮又【現代】的大廳，有玻璃屋頂、數位看板和舒適的旅客候車區。"},{"w":"historic","p":"adj.","d":"important in history","c":"有歷史意義的；歷史悠久的","s":"A: The developer wants to tear down the old tea factory near the river and build apartments, so why are so many residents against the plan? B: The building is more than a hundred years old and is considered a historic site, so local people believe it should be protected and turned into a museum instead.","t":"A：開發商想拆除河邊的老茶廠蓋公寓，為什麼這麼多居民反對這項計畫？ B：那棟建築已經超過一百年，被視為【具歷史意義的】古蹟，所以當地人認為應該保護它，改建成博物館。"},{"w":"population","p":"n.","d":"the number of people living in a place","c":"人口","s":"A: The supermarket chain is thinking about opening a store in Hsinchu, so what information does the planning team need before making a final decision? B: They need to know how quickly the population of the city is growing, because more people moving there for technology jobs means more families who will shop for groceries every week.","t":"A：那家連鎖超市正在考慮在新竹開店，規劃團隊在做最後決定之前需要哪些資訊？ B：他們需要知道這座城市的【人口】成長得有多快，因為越多人為了科技業工作搬到那裡，就代表每週會有越多家庭來採買食品雜貨。"},{"w":"resident","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a particular place","c":"居民","s":"A: The building manager sent an email saying that the elevator will be repaired next week, so what should people living on the top floors do? B: Every resident who has difficulty using the stairs can contact the front desk, and the staff will help carry their shopping bags and heavy packages up to their apartments.","t":"A：大樓管理員寄電子郵件說下週要修電梯，住在頂樓的人該怎麼辦？ B：每位爬樓梯有困難的【居民】都可以聯絡櫃檯，工作人員會幫忙把購物袋和重的包裹搬到他們的公寓。"},{"w":"tourist","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels to a place for fun","c":"觀光客","s":"A: Sales at our gift shop have increased by thirty percent this summer, so what do you think is the main reason for this success? B: Since the new airline started direct flights from Japan, many more tourist groups visit the old street every day, and they love buying our handmade tea cups as souvenirs.","t":"A：我們禮品店今年夏天的業績成長了百分之三十，你覺得成功的主要原因是什麼？ B：自從新的航空公司開了從日本出發的直飛航班，每天有更多【觀光客】團體來逛老街，他們很喜歡買我們手工做的茶杯當紀念品。"},{"w":"transport","p":"n.","d":"a system for carrying people or goods from place to place","c":"交通運輸","s":"A: Many new employees have asked whether they really need to buy a car after moving to the city for this job, so what should we tell them? B: Tell them that public transport here is cheap and reliable, because buses and trains run every few minutes and can take them almost anywhere in the city.","t":"A：很多新員工問，為了這份工作搬到這座城市後，他們是否真的需要買車，我們該怎麼告訴他們？ B：告訴他們這裡的大眾【運輸】既便宜又可靠，因為公車和火車每幾分鐘就有一班，幾乎可以載他們到市區任何地方。"},{"w":"subway","p":"n.","d":"an underground train system in a city","c":"地鐵；捷運","s":"A: The conference center is on the other side of the city, and the taxi drivers say the roads will be very busy tomorrow morning, so how should we get there? B: Let's take the subway, because the underground trains are not affected by road traffic, and the station is right next to the main entrance of the center.","t":"A：會議中心在城市的另一邊，計程車司機說明天早上路上會很塞，我們該怎麼去？ B：我們搭【捷運】吧，因為地下列車不受道路交通影響，而且車站就在會議中心主要入口旁邊。"},{"w":"bus","p":"n.","d":"a large vehicle that carries many passengers on a fixed route","c":"公車","s":"A: The company is moving to a new office in the science park next month, and many employees are worried about how they will get there without a car, so what is the plan? B: Management has arranged a free shuttle bus that will leave the main train station every fifteen minutes during rush hour in the morning and evening.","t":"A：公司下個月要搬到科學園區的新辦公室，很多員工擔心沒有車要怎麼去，計畫是什麼？ B：管理階層安排了免費接駁【公車】，早晚尖峰時段每十五分鐘從火車總站發車一次。"},{"w":"intersection","p":"n.","d":"a place where two or more roads cross","c":"十字路口","s":"A: The delivery driver called again and said he cannot find our warehouse, even though he is very close, so how should I explain the way? B: Tell him to turn left at the next intersection with the big traffic lights and the gas station, and our gray building will be the third one on the right side.","t":"A：送貨司機又打電話來說他找不到我們的倉庫，雖然他已經很近了，我該怎麼跟他說明路線？ B：告訴他在下一個有大紅綠燈和加油站的【十字路口】左轉，我們的灰色建築就是右手邊的第三棟。"},{"w":"crosswalk","p":"n.","d":"a marked place where people can walk across a road","c":"斑馬線；行人穿越道","s":"A: Parents at the school next to our office are worried about their children's safety in the morning, so what has the city decided to do? B: The city is painting a new crosswalk in front of the school gate and adding a traffic light, so that students can cross the road safely when cars are coming.","t":"A：我們辦公室隔壁學校的家長擔心孩子早上的安全，市政府決定怎麼做？ B：市政府要在校門前漆一條新的【斑馬線】並增設紅綠燈，讓學生在有車來的時候也能安全過馬路。"},{"w":"sidewalk","p":"n.","d":"a path at the side of a road for people to walk on","c":"人行道","s":"A: The restaurant manager wants to put a few tables outside so that customers can enjoy the warm spring weather, so is that allowed in this area? B: Yes, but we must apply for a permit first, and we have to leave enough space on the sidewalk so that people with strollers and wheelchairs can still pass by easily.","t":"A：餐廳經理想在外面擺幾張桌子，讓客人享受溫暖的春天天氣，這一區允許這樣做嗎？ B：可以，但我們必須先申請許可，而且要在【人行道】上留下足夠的空間，讓推嬰兒車和坐輪椅的人仍然可以輕鬆通過。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"a place where people buy and sell food and goods","c":"市場","s":"A: The chef at our hotel restaurant always says that his vegetables taste much fresher than the ones in supermarkets, so where does he buy them? B: He goes to the traditional market near the river at six o'clock every morning, where local farmers sell fruit, vegetables, and fish that were picked or caught only a few hours earlier.","t":"A：我們飯店餐廳的主廚總是說他的蔬菜比超市的新鮮多了，他都在哪裡買？ B：他每天早上六點去河邊的傳統【市場】，當地農民在那裡賣幾個小時前才摘下或捕到的水果、蔬菜和魚。"},{"w":"mall","p":"n.","d":"a large building with many shops inside","c":"購物中心","s":"A: The weather forecast says it will rain all weekend, so where can we take the visiting sales team to relax after the training sessions finish? B: We could take them to the new shopping mall next to the station, because it has hundreds of stores, a cinema, and a large food court, so nobody will get wet.","t":"A：天氣預報說整個週末都會下雨，訓練課程結束後，我們可以帶來訪的業務團隊去哪裡放鬆？ B：我們可以帶他們去車站旁邊新開的【購物中心】，因為那裡有數百家店、一間電影院和一個大型美食街，沒有人會淋濕。"},{"w":"restaurant","p":"n.","d":"a place where people pay to sit and eat meals","c":"餐廳","s":"A: We need to take the visiting directors out for dinner after the board meeting on Wednesday, so have you made a reservation anywhere yet? B: I booked a private room at a seafood restaurant on the twentieth floor, because the food there is excellent and the guests can enjoy a wonderful night view of the river.","t":"A：星期三董事會開完後，我們需要帶來訪的董事們去吃晚餐，你已經在哪裡訂位了嗎？ B：我在二十樓的一家海鮮【餐廳】訂了包廂，因為那裡的菜很棒，客人還能欣賞美麗的河岸夜景。"},{"w":"cafe","p":"n.","d":"a small place that sells coffee, drinks and light meals","c":"咖啡館","s":"A: I have an online job interview at ten tomorrow morning, but the internet at my apartment has been very slow this week, so where can I go? B: There is a quiet cafe around the corner with fast WiFi and private booths, so you can order a coffee and do the interview there without any noise.","t":"A：我明天早上十點有一場線上工作面試，但這週我公寓的網路一直很慢，我可以去哪裡？ B：轉角有一家安靜的【咖啡館】，有快速的無線網路和私人座位區，你可以點杯咖啡，在那裡安靜地面試。"},{"w":"nightlife","p":"n.","d":"entertainment such as bars, music and clubs at night","c":"夜生活","s":"A: Our company is sending three young engineers to work in Bangkok for six months, so what do you think they will enjoy most about living there? B: They will probably love the nightlife, because the city has rooftop bars, live music, and night markets that stay open until very late, even after a long day at work.","t":"A：我們公司要派三位年輕工程師到曼谷工作六個月，你覺得他們最喜歡那裡生活的哪一點？ B：他們大概會很愛那裡的【夜生活】，因為那座城市有屋頂酒吧、現場音樂和營業到很晚的夜市，即使上班一整天後也能去玩。"},{"w":"skyline","p":"n.","d":"the shape of buildings against the sky","c":"天際線","s":"A: The photographer for our company's annual report wants to take a picture that shows how much the city has grown, so where should he stand? B: He should go to the top of the hill behind the university at sunset, because from there he can capture the whole skyline with all the tall office towers lit up.","t":"A：為公司年報拍照的攝影師想拍一張能呈現這座城市成長多少的照片，他應該站在哪裡？ B：他應該在日落時到大學後面的山頂，因為從那裡他可以拍到所有高聳辦公大樓都亮燈的整片【天際線】。"}]},{"unit":59,"theme":"Classmates 同學","cards":[{"w":"peer","p":"n.","d":"a person of the same age, class or level as you","c":"同儕；同輩","s":"A: The new interns seem nervous about giving feedback to the senior designers, so how can we help them feel more confident during their first month? B: Let's pair each intern with a peer from last year's program, because people usually ask questions more freely when the person helping them is at the same level.","t":"A：新來的實習生似乎不太敢給資深設計師意見，我們要怎麼幫助他們在第一個月更有自信？ B：我們讓每位實習生搭配一位去年計畫的【同儕】吧，因為當幫忙的人和自己程度相同時，大家通常會更放心地發問。"},{"w":"schoolmate","p":"n.","d":"a person who goes or went to the same school as you","c":"同校同學；校友","s":"A: I heard you already knew the new marketing manager before she joined our company last week, so where did you two first meet? B: She was my schoolmate at a high school in Tainan, and although we were in different classes, we often took the same bus home every afternoon.","t":"A：聽說新來的行銷經理上週加入公司前你就認識她了，你們兩個最初是在哪裡認識的？ B：她是我在台南念高中時的【同校同學】，雖然我們不同班，但每天下午常搭同一班公車回家。"},{"w":"friend","p":"n.","d":"a person you know well and like","c":"朋友","s":"A: You look really happy today, and you keep smiling at your phone, so did you get some good news from the head office this morning? B: Not exactly, but my closest friend from university just told me she is moving to Taipei next month and will work in the building across the street.","t":"A：你今天看起來好開心，一直對著手機微笑，是今天早上收到總公司的好消息嗎？ B：不完全是，是我大學時最要好的【朋友】剛告訴我，她下個月要搬到台北，而且會在對街的大樓上班。"},{"w":"teammate","p":"n.","d":"a person who is on the same team as you","c":"隊友","s":"A: Our department won the company basketball tournament on Saturday, so who scored the winning points in the last few seconds of the game? B: Kevin from accounting threw the final shot, but he said he could not have done it without his teammate, who passed him the ball at exactly the right moment.","t":"A：我們部門星期六贏得了公司籃球賽，最後幾秒是誰得到致勝分的？ B：會計部的 Kevin 投進最後一球，但他說如果沒有他的【隊友】在最恰當的時刻把球傳給他，他不可能做到。"},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"a person you work or do an activity with","c":"夥伴；搭檔","s":"A: The training course next week includes several role-play exercises about handling customer complaints, so do we need to prepare anything before the first session? B: Yes, the trainer asked everyone to choose a partner from another department and practice a short conversation together, so you should contact someone by Thursday.","t":"A：下週的培訓課程有好幾個處理客訴的角色扮演練習，第一堂課前我們需要準備什麼嗎？ B：需要，講師要求每個人從其他部門選一位【搭檔】，一起練習一段簡短的對話，所以你應該在星期四前聯絡好人選。"},{"w":"group","p":"n.","d":"a number of people who do something together","c":"小組；群體","s":"A: There are almost forty new employees at the orientation today, so how will the trainers manage such a large number of people in one room? B: They plan to divide everyone into a small group of five or six people, and each one will have its own table, leader, and set of tasks.","t":"A：今天的新人訓練有將近四十位新員工，訓練師要怎麼在一個房間裡帶這麼多人？ B：他們打算把大家分成五、六人一組的【小組】，每組都有自己的桌子、組長和一套任務。"},{"w":"class","p":"n.","d":"a group of students taught together; a course of lessons","c":"班級；課程","s":"A: You have been leaving the office early every Tuesday and Thursday this month, so are you taking care of something important for your family? B: No, I signed up for an evening Japanese class near the train station, because our company is going to open a new branch in Osaka next spring.","t":"A：你這個月每週二和週四都提早下班，是在處理家裡重要的事嗎？ B：不是，我報名了火車站附近的晚間日文【課程】，因為我們公司明年春天要在大阪開新分公司。"},{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others to reach the same goal","c":"合作；配合","s":"A: The building manager says the fire drill will take about thirty minutes on Friday afternoon, so what does he expect from all the tenants? B: He hopes every company will cooperate with the safety team by leaving quickly through the stairs, because last year many workers ignored the alarm and stayed at their desks.","t":"A：大樓管理員說星期五下午的消防演習大約要三十分鐘，他希望所有租戶怎麼做？ B：他希望每家公司都能【配合】安全小組，迅速從樓梯離開，因為去年很多員工不理會警報，一直待在座位上。"},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with someone to create or achieve something","c":"協作；共同合作","s":"A: The new advertising campaign for the sports drink looks amazing, so did our design team create all the videos and posters by themselves? B: No, they decided to collaborate with a young film studio from Kaohsiung, and the two teams spent three months sharing ideas, writing scripts, and filming together.","t":"A：那款運動飲料的新廣告看起來好棒，所有影片和海報都是我們設計團隊自己做的嗎？ B：不是，他們決定和一家來自高雄的年輕影像工作室【共同合作】，兩個團隊花了三個月一起交流想法、寫腳本和拍攝。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to have or use something together with others","c":"分享；共用","s":"A: The office is getting very crowded since the sales team moved to our floor, so where will the two new assistants sit next week? B: Until the renovation upstairs is finished, they will have to share the long desk by the window, and they can keep their files in the cabinet behind it.","t":"A：自從業務團隊搬到我們這層後辦公室變得好擠，下週兩位新助理要坐哪裡？ B：在樓上整修完成之前，他們得【共用】窗邊那張長桌，文件可以放在後面的櫃子裡。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help and encourage someone","c":"支持；支援","s":"A: Linda seems worried about leading her first big project while the director is away on a business trip, so is there anything we can do? B: Let's support her by answering her questions quickly and offering to check her reports, because she will feel much calmer if she knows the team is behind her.","t":"A：主任出差期間，Linda 要帶她的第一個大型專案，她似乎很擔心，我們能做些什麼嗎？ B：我們就盡快回答她的問題、主動幫她檢查報告來【支持】她，因為只要知道團隊站在她這邊，她會安心很多。"},{"w":"discuss","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something with other people","c":"討論","s":"A: The customer survey shows that many people are unhappy with our delivery times, so when will the managers decide how to solve this problem? B: They are meeting on Monday morning to discuss several possible plans, including hiring more drivers and opening a small warehouse in the southern part of the city.","t":"A：顧客調查顯示很多人不滿意我們的送貨時間，經理們什麼時候會決定怎麼解決這個問題？ B：他們星期一早上會開會【討論】幾個可能的方案，包括多雇幾位司機和在市區南邊開一個小倉庫。"},{"w":"interact","p":"v.","d":"to talk and do things with other people","c":"互動","s":"A: Why did the hotel ask its front desk staff to stand beside the counter instead of sitting behind the computer screens all day? B: The manager believes that guests feel more welcome when employees interact with them face to face, smile often, and offer useful advice about restaurants and places to visit nearby.","t":"A：為什麼飯店要求櫃檯人員站在櫃檯旁邊，而不是整天坐在電腦螢幕後面？ B：經理認為當員工面對面和客人【互動】、常常微笑，並提供附近餐廳和景點的實用建議時，客人會覺得更受歡迎。"},{"w":"respect","p":"v.","d":"to treat someone or something with care because you think they are important","c":"尊重","s":"A: Our new team includes people from five different countries, so how can we avoid misunderstandings when we plan meetings and company events? B: We should respect everyone's holidays and customs, ask politely when we are not sure about something, and choose times and foods that work for the whole team.","t":"A：我們的新團隊有來自五個不同國家的人，規劃會議和公司活動時要怎麼避免誤會？ B：我們應該【尊重】每個人的節日和習俗，不確定時禮貌地詢問，並選擇適合整個團隊的時間和食物。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"useful; willing to help","c":"有幫助的；樂於助人的","s":"A: How was your first week at the new branch, and did you have any trouble learning the computer system the company uses for orders? B: It was great, because the staff there were very helpful and showed me every step slowly, so I could process orders by myself by Wednesday afternoon.","t":"A：你在新分店的第一週怎麼樣？學公司的訂單電腦系統有遇到困難嗎？ B：很棒，因為那裡的員工都非常【樂於助人】，慢慢地教我每個步驟，所以到星期三下午我就能自己處理訂單了。"},{"w":"friendly","p":"adj.","d":"kind and pleasant to other people","c":"友善的","s":"A: We are looking for a café where we can hold a relaxed meeting with our new clients from Singapore next Friday, so do you know a good place? B: There is a quiet café on Fifth Street where the owner is very friendly, remembers every guest's name, and often brings free cookies to the table.","t":"A：我們在找一家咖啡館，下週五要和新加坡的新客戶輕鬆開個會，你知道哪裡不錯嗎？ B：第五街有一家安靜的咖啡館，老闆非常【友善】，記得每位客人的名字，還常常送免費餅乾到桌上。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to win or be better than others","c":"好勝的；競爭激烈的","s":"A: The sales contest only started on Monday, but Jason has already called over a hundred customers, so why is he working so hard this week? B: He is a very competitive person who always wants to finish first, and the winner of this contest will also get a free trip to Japan.","t":"A：業績競賽星期一才開始，Jason 已經打給超過一百位客戶了，他這週為什麼這麼拚？ B：他是個非常【好勝】的人，總是想拿第一，而且這次比賽的優勝者還能免費去日本旅行。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help and encouragement","c":"支持的；給予鼓勵的","s":"A: You decided to take evening classes for your master's degree while working full-time, so how does your manager feel about your busy schedule? B: She has been very supportive about it, and she even lets me leave thirty minutes early on exam days so that I can get to campus on time.","t":"A：你決定一邊全職工作一邊上夜間碩士課程，你的主管對你這麼忙的行程有什麼看法？ B：她一直非常【支持】，甚至讓我在考試那天提早三十分鐘下班，好讓我準時到學校。"},{"w":"cooperative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to work with others and help them","c":"合作的；配合的","s":"A: The software company in Hsinchu finally agreed to fix the problems with our new booking system, so how was the meeting with their engineers yesterday? B: It went smoothly, because their team was very cooperative, answered all our questions, and promised to send us an updated version before the end of the month.","t":"A：新竹那家軟體公司終於同意修正我們新訂位系統的問題，昨天和他們工程師的會議怎麼樣？ B：很順利，因為他們的團隊非常【配合】，回答了我們所有的問題，還答應在月底前寄給我們更新版本。"},{"w":"active","p":"adj.","d":"doing a lot of things; taking part","c":"積極的；活躍的","s":"A: The company wants to choose one employee to represent our office at the regional leadership program next spring, so who do you think should go? B: I would recommend Grace, because she is very active in team meetings, often shares new ideas, and volunteers to organize events for the whole department.","t":"A：公司想選一位員工代表我們辦公室參加明年春天的區域領導力課程，你覺得誰該去？ B：我推薦 Grace，因為她在團隊會議中非常【積極】，常常提出新點子，還自願幫整個部門籌辦活動。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making little noise; not talking much","c":"安靜的；文靜的","s":"A: The new accountant does not say much during our weekly meetings, so do you think she is unhappy with her job or with the team? B: I don't think so, because she is just a quiet person who prefers listening, and her reports are always the most careful and detailed ones in the office.","t":"A：新來的會計在每週會議中話不多，你覺得她是對工作或團隊不滿意嗎？ B：我不這麼認為，她只是個【文靜】的人，比較喜歡傾聽，而且她的報告一直是辦公室裡最仔細、最詳盡的。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的","s":"A: Why is there always such a long line at the small noodle shop next to our office building every day around twelve o'clock? B: It is very popular with office workers in this area because the prices are low, the portions are big, and the owner can prepare an order in less than five minutes.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公大樓旁邊那家小麵店每天中午十二點左右都大排長龍？ B：它在這一帶的上班族之間非常【受歡迎】，因為價格便宜、份量大，而且老闆不到五分鐘就能做好一份餐點。"},{"w":"familiar","p":"adj.","d":"known to you because you have seen or used it before","c":"熟悉的","s":"A: We need someone to help the visitors from our German partner find their way around the factory tomorrow, so who should we ask to guide them? B: Let's ask Peter, because he has worked in every section of the factory for ten years and is familiar with all the machines and safety rules.","t":"A：明天需要有人幫德國合作夥伴的訪客認識工廠環境，我們該請誰帶他們？ B：請 Peter 吧，因為他在工廠每個部門都待過，做了十年，對所有機器和安全規定都很【熟悉】。"},{"w":"diverse","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other; including many types","c":"多元的；多樣的","s":"A: The new international school near the science park has been hiring a lot of teachers this year, so what kind of students do they have? B: Their student body is very diverse, with children from more than twenty countries, so the school also offers language support classes and cultural events every month.","t":"A：科學園區附近那所新的國際學校今年聘了很多老師，他們的學生是什麼樣的？ B：他們的學生非常【多元】，有來自二十多個國家的孩子，所以學校每個月也會提供語言輔導課和文化活動。"},{"w":"attentive","p":"adj.","d":"listening or watching carefully; noticing what others need","c":"專心的；體貼周到的","s":"A: The hotel received excellent reviews on the travel website last month, so what did the guests like most about their stay there? B: Many of them said the staff were very attentive, because they noticed small things like extra pillows or birthday plans and took care of them before guests even asked.","t":"A：那家飯店上個月在旅遊網站上得到很好的評價，客人最喜歡住宿的哪一點？ B：很多人說員工非常【體貼周到】，因為他們會注意到額外枕頭或生日安排這類小事，甚至在客人開口之前就處理好了。"},{"w":"respectful","p":"adj.","d":"showing politeness and care for others","c":"尊重人的；有禮貌的","s":"A: Some customers become very angry on the phone when their packages arrive late, so how should new call center staff deal with them? B: They should stay calm and respectful, listen without interrupting, apologize for the delay, and explain clearly when the customer can expect to receive the package.","t":"A：包裹延遲送達時，有些客人在電話裡會非常生氣，新來的客服人員該怎麼應對？ B：他們應該保持冷靜和【有禮貌】，不打斷對方地傾聽，為延誤道歉，並清楚說明客人預計何時能收到包裹。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a talk about something between people","c":"討論","s":"A: The meeting about the new holiday schedule lasted almost three hours yesterday afternoon, so why did it take so long to make a decision? B: There was a long discussion about whether the factory should close for a whole week in February or only for three days, because both choices have problems.","t":"A：昨天下午關於新假期安排的會議開了將近三個小時，為什麼這麼久才做出決定？ B：大家針對工廠二月該停工整整一週還是只停三天進行了很長的【討論】，因為兩種選擇都有問題。"},{"w":"activity","p":"n.","d":"something people do for fun or to reach a goal","c":"活動","s":"A: The human resources department wants to plan something special for the staff before the busy season starts in October, so do you have any ideas? B: A team-building activity like a cooking contest or a mountain hike would be fun, because people from different departments could get to know each other better.","t":"A：人資部想在十月旺季開始前為員工安排一些特別的事，你有什麼想法嗎？ B：像烹飪比賽或爬山這類團隊建立【活動】會很有趣，因為不同部門的人可以更了解彼此。"},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work given to someone as part of a job or course","c":"任務；作業","s":"A: You look very busy this week, and I saw you stay at the office until nine last night, so what are you working on now? B: My manager gave me a special assignment to compare the prices of five suppliers, and she needs my report before the budget meeting on Friday morning.","t":"A：你這週看起來好忙，我看到你昨晚待在辦公室到九點，你現在在忙什麼？ B：主管交給我一項特別【任務】，要比較五家供應商的價格，她需要在星期五早上預算會議前拿到我的報告。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk that gives information to a group of people","c":"簡報；發表","s":"A: The clients from Tokyo are arriving at ten tomorrow morning, so is everything ready for the meeting in the large conference room? B: Almost, but I still need to check the projector and practice my presentation about our new products one more time, because I want to finish it in twenty minutes.","t":"A：東京的客戶明天早上十點到，大會議室的會議都準備好了嗎？ B：差不多了，但我還要檢查投影機，並再練習一次介紹新產品的【簡報】，因為我想在二十分鐘內講完。"},{"w":"study","p":"v.","d":"to spend time learning about a subject","c":"研讀；學習","s":"A: You told me you are planning to apply for the position at our London office next year, so how are you preparing for the interview? B: I study business English for an hour every night after dinner, and on weekends I join an online group where we practice speaking about our jobs.","t":"A：你跟我說你打算明年申請倫敦辦公室的職位，你怎麼準備面試？ B：我每天晚餐後花一小時【研讀】商用英文，週末則參加一個線上社團，一起練習談論我們的工作。"},{"w":"review","p":"v.","d":"to look at or check something again carefully","c":"審閱；複習","s":"A: The contract with the new cleaning company is almost ready, so can we sign it this afternoon and let them start working next Monday? B: Not yet, because our lawyer wants to review every page carefully first, especially the part about the price increases and what happens if they miss a cleaning day.","t":"A：和新清潔公司的合約快好了，我們今天下午可以簽約，讓他們下週一開始工作嗎？ B：還不行，因為我們的律師想先仔細【審閱】每一頁，尤其是漲價的部分，以及如果他們漏掉一天清潔會怎樣。"},{"w":"get along","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a friendly relationship with someone","c":"相處融洽","s":"A: The two new engineers will share an office and travel together to the factory in Vietnam every month, so do you think that will cause any problems? B: I don't think so, because they already get along very well, often eat lunch together, and even went hiking with their families last weekend.","t":"A：兩位新工程師要共用一間辦公室，每個月還要一起去越南的工廠，你覺得會有問題嗎？ B：我不這麼認為，因為他們已經【相處融洽】，常一起吃午餐，上週末甚至帶著家人一起去爬山。"}]},{"unit":60,"theme":"Climate 氣候","cards":[{"w":"climate","p":"n.","d":"the usual weather conditions in a place over a long time","c":"氣候","s":"A: Our company is thinking about opening a new factory in the south of the country next year, so what do managers need to consider before they choose the location? B: They should study the local climate carefully, because hot and wet conditions all year round can damage machines and raise cooling costs.","t":"A：我們公司正考慮明年在國家南部開設一間新工廠，經理們在選擇地點前需要考慮什麼？ B：他們應該仔細研究當地的【氣候】，因為全年炎熱潮濕的環境會損壞機器並提高冷卻成本。"},{"w":"weather","p":"n.","d":"the conditions in the air at a particular time, such as rain, sun or wind","c":"天氣","s":"A: The outdoor product launch is planned for Saturday afternoon in the park, but I heard it might rain, so should we prepare a backup plan just in case? B: Yes, let's check the weather report again on Thursday, and if it looks bad, we can move the event into the hotel ballroom.","t":"A：戶外產品發表會預定在週六下午於公園舉行，但我聽說可能會下雨，我們要不要準備一個備案以防萬一？ B：要，我們週四再查一次【天氣】預報，如果看起來不好，就把活動移到飯店宴會廳。"},{"w":"temperature","p":"n.","d":"how hot or cold something is","c":"溫度；氣溫","s":"A: Several employees on the third floor have complained that the office feels too cold in the afternoons, so is there anything the building manager can do? B: He said he will raise the temperature on the air conditioner by two degrees and also check whether any windows near the meeting rooms are leaking.","t":"A：三樓有好幾位員工抱怨下午辦公室太冷，大樓管理員能做些什麼嗎？ B：他說會把冷氣的【溫度】調高兩度，也會檢查會議室附近是否有窗戶漏風。"},{"w":"rainfall","p":"n.","d":"the amount of rain that falls in an area","c":"降雨量","s":"A: The farmers who supply vegetables to our restaurant chain say prices may go up this autumn, so do you know why that is happening? B: The total rainfall this summer was much lower than usual, so many fields were too dry and the harvest will be smaller than last year's.","t":"A：供應我們連鎖餐廳蔬菜的農民說今年秋天價格可能會上漲，你知道為什麼嗎？ B：今年夏天的總【降雨量】比平常少很多，所以許多田地太乾，收成會比去年少。"},{"w":"humidity","p":"n.","d":"the amount of water in the air","c":"濕度","s":"A: The paper in our storage room keeps getting soft and wavy before we can use it in the printers, so what do you think the problem is? B: The humidity in that room is very high during the rainy season, so we should buy a dehumidifier and keep the door closed.","t":"A：我們儲藏室裡的紙在放進印表機前總是變軟變皺，你覺得問題出在哪裡？ B：那個房間在雨季時【濕度】很高，所以我們應該買一台除濕機，並且把門關好。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the mixture of gases around the earth","c":"大氣（層）","s":"A: I'm preparing a short presentation for our environmental training next week, so could you help me explain why factory smoke is such a serious problem? B: Sure, you can say that the smoke releases harmful gases into the atmosphere, where they trap heat and make the air dirtier for everyone who lives nearby.","t":"A：我正在為下週的環保訓練準備一個簡短報告，你能幫我解釋為什麼工廠排煙是這麼嚴重的問題嗎？ B：當然，你可以說煙會把有害氣體排放到【大氣】中，這些氣體會留住熱量，並讓附近居民呼吸的空氣更髒。"},{"w":"season","p":"n.","d":"one of the four periods of the year, such as spring or winter","c":"季節","s":"A: Our travel agency is planning special tour packages to Japan, so which time of year do you think will attract the most customers from Taiwan? B: I think spring is the best season because the cherry blossoms are beautiful, the temperature is comfortable, and many families take vacations in early April.","t":"A：我們旅行社正在規劃前往日本的特別旅遊行程，你認為一年中哪個時候最能吸引台灣客人？ B：我認為春天是最好的【季節】，因為櫻花很美、氣溫舒適，而且許多家庭在四月初會去度假。"},{"w":"seasonal","p":"adj.","d":"happening or needed only at a certain time of year","c":"季節性的","s":"A: Our ice cream shop always gets very busy from June to August, but we don't need as many workers in winter, so how should we handle staffing? B: We could hire seasonal workers, such as university students on summer break, who are happy to work for three months and then return to school.","t":"A：我們的冰淇淋店每年六月到八月都很忙，但冬天不需要那麼多員工，我們該如何安排人力？ B：我們可以雇用【季節性的】工作人員，例如放暑假的大學生，他們很樂意工作三個月然後回學校。"},{"w":"tropical","p":"adj.","d":"from or like the hot, wet areas near the equator","c":"熱帶的","s":"A: The marketing team wants to hold next year's sales conference somewhere warm and relaxing, so do you have any ideas for a good place? B: How about a tropical island in Southeast Asia, where the weather is hot, the beaches are beautiful, and the resort hotels have large meeting rooms?","t":"A：行銷團隊希望明年的業務會議在溫暖又放鬆的地方舉行，你有什麼好地點的建議嗎？ B：東南亞的【熱帶】島嶼怎麼樣？那裡天氣炎熱、海灘漂亮，而且度假飯店有大型會議室。"},{"w":"temperate","p":"adj.","d":"not very hot and not very cold","c":"溫帶的；溫和的","s":"A: Our company is choosing between two cities for its new European office, so why did the director say that the weather was an important factor? B: She prefers the city with a temperate climate, because staff will not suffer from extreme heat in summer or heavy snow that stops trains in winter.","t":"A：公司正在兩個城市中為新的歐洲辦公室做選擇，為什麼主管說天氣是重要因素？ B：她偏好【溫帶】氣候的城市，因為員工夏天不會受酷熱之苦，冬天也不會遇到讓火車停駛的大雪。"},{"w":"arid","p":"adj.","d":"very dry, with little or no rain","c":"乾旱的","s":"A: The engineers are designing a new water system for the factory we are building in the desert region, so why does it cost so much more than usual? B: The land there is extremely arid, with almost no rain for most of the year, so they must pipe water in from a river eighty kilometers away.","t":"A：工程師正在為我們在沙漠地區興建的工廠設計新的供水系統，為什麼費用比平常高這麼多？ B：那裡的土地極度【乾旱】，一年中大部分時間幾乎不下雨，所以他們必須從八十公里外的河流引水過來。"},{"w":"polar","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the very cold areas around the North or South Pole","c":"極地的","s":"A: I saw that the science museum downtown has a new exhibition this month, so do you think it would be a good trip for our staff family day? B: Yes, the polar exhibition is perfect for kids, because they can learn about penguins, ice, and how animals survive in the coldest places on earth.","t":"A：我看到市中心的科學博物館這個月有新展覽，你覺得那適合當作我們員工家庭日的行程嗎？ B：適合，那個【極地】展覽很適合小孩，因為他們可以認識企鵝、冰，以及動物如何在地球上最冷的地方生存。"},{"w":"forecast","p":"n.","d":"a statement about what will probably happen, especially with the weather","c":"預報；預測","s":"A: We are supposed to fly to Okinawa for the client meeting on Monday morning, but I'm worried about the typhoon, so what did the news say? B: The latest forecast says the storm will arrive on Sunday night, so the airline may cancel our flight and we should call the client today.","t":"A：我們預定週一早上飛到沖繩和客戶開會，但我擔心颱風，新聞怎麼說？ B：最新的【預報】說暴風會在週日晚上抵達，所以航空公司可能會取消我們的航班，我們今天應該打電話給客戶。"},{"w":"drought","p":"n.","d":"a long period with little or no rain","c":"乾旱","s":"A: The coffee supplier just told us that bean prices will rise by twenty percent next quarter, so did they explain the reason for such a big increase? B: Yes, a long drought in Brazil lasted for almost six months, and many coffee farms lost a large part of their crop because there was no water.","t":"A：咖啡供應商剛告訴我們下一季咖啡豆價格會上漲百分之二十，他們有解釋漲這麼多的原因嗎？ B：有，巴西一場長期【乾旱】持續了將近六個月，許多咖啡農場因為缺水損失了大部分作物。"},{"w":"flood","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of water covering land that is usually dry","c":"洪水；水災","s":"A: Why is the warehouse team moving all the boxes from the ground floor up to the second floor this afternoon? B: The river next to the building rose quickly after three days of heavy rain, and the city warned that a flood could reach our area tonight, so we want to protect the products.","t":"A：倉庫團隊今天下午為什麼要把一樓的箱子全部搬到二樓？ B：連續下了三天大雨後，大樓旁邊的河水迅速上漲，市政府警告今晚【洪水】可能淹到我們這一區，所以我們想保護產品。"},{"w":"storm","p":"n.","d":"very bad weather with strong winds and heavy rain","c":"暴風雨","s":"A: The power went off in the whole office building around two o'clock, and my computer shut down before I saved my report, so what happened? B: A strong storm with heavy rain and lightning passed over the city, and it damaged some power lines near the train station.","t":"A：兩點左右整棟辦公大樓停電了，我的電腦在我存檔報告前就關機了，發生了什麼事？ B：一場夾帶大雨和閃電的強烈【暴風雨】經過市區，損壞了火車站附近的一些電線。"},{"w":"heatwave","p":"n.","d":"a period of unusually hot weather","c":"熱浪","s":"A: Sales of fans and air conditioners at our electronics stores have doubled this week, so did the marketing team start a special promotion? B: No, the main reason is the heatwave, because temperatures have stayed above thirty-seven degrees for six days and many people cannot sleep at night.","t":"A：我們電器行的電風扇和冷氣銷量這週翻倍了，是行銷團隊開始了特別促銷嗎？ B：不是，主要原因是【熱浪】，因為氣溫已經連續六天超過三十七度，很多人晚上都睡不著。"},{"w":"cold spell","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short period of very cold weather","c":"寒流；一段寒冷期","s":"A: The vegetable prices at the market went up suddenly this week, and our restaurant's food costs are much higher, so what caused the change? B: A sudden cold spell last weekend brought freezing temperatures to the farms in central Taiwan, and many leafy vegetables were damaged by the frost.","t":"A：這週市場的菜價突然上漲，我們餐廳的食材成本高了很多，是什麼造成的？ B：上週末一波突如其來的【寒流】讓中台灣的農場出現低溫，許多葉菜都被霜凍壞了。"},{"w":"wind","p":"n.","d":"air that moves quickly across the land","c":"風","s":"A: Why did the construction company stop using the tall crane on the new office tower this afternoon? B: The wind became too strong after lunch, and the safety manager decided it was dangerous to lift heavy steel beams that high, so the workers will continue tomorrow morning if it is calmer.","t":"A：建設公司今天下午為什麼停止使用新辦公大樓上的高塔吊車？ B：午餐後【風】變得太強，安全經理認為把沉重的鋼樑吊到那麼高很危險，所以如果明天早上比較平靜，工人會繼續施工。"},{"w":"cloud cover","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of the sky that is covered by clouds","c":"雲層覆蓋；雲量","s":"A: The photography team wants to take pictures of the new hotel from the air using a drone, so is tomorrow a good day to do it? B: Probably not, because thick cloud cover is expected all morning, so the sky will look gray and the building will not stand out in the photos.","t":"A：攝影團隊想用無人機從空中拍新飯店的照片，明天是適合拍攝的日子嗎？ B：可能不是，因為預計整個早上都會有厚厚的【雲層覆蓋】，天空看起來會灰灰的，建築物在照片中不會突出。"},{"w":"sunlight","p":"n.","d":"the light that comes from the sun","c":"陽光","s":"A: The interior designer is planning the layout of our new office, so where does she suggest we put the main work area for the staff? B: She wants it next to the large windows on the east side, because the room gets plenty of natural sunlight in the morning and people will feel more awake.","t":"A：室內設計師正在規劃我們新辦公室的配置，她建議把員工的主要工作區放在哪裡？ B：她想把它放在東側的大窗戶旁邊，因為那個房間早上有充足的自然【陽光】，大家會覺得比較有精神。"},{"w":"greenhouse effect","p":"n.phr.","d":"the warming of the earth because gases in the air trap the sun's heat","c":"溫室效應","s":"A: Our company is making a short environmental video for customers, and I need to explain why the earth is getting warmer, so can you help me with the script? B: You could start with the greenhouse effect, which happens when gases like carbon dioxide trap heat from the sun and stop it from escaping into space.","t":"A：我們公司正在為客戶製作一支簡短的環保影片，我需要解釋地球為什麼越來越暖，你可以幫我寫腳本嗎？ B：你可以從【溫室效應】開始講，它是指像二氧化碳這類氣體留住太陽的熱，使熱無法散逸到太空中。"},{"w":"global warming","p":"n.phr.","d":"the slow rise in the earth's average temperature","c":"全球暖化","s":"A: The insurance company sent us a letter saying our business insurance will cost more next year, so did they explain why the price is going up? B: They said global warming is causing more typhoons and floods every year, so they must pay for more damage and are raising prices for all customers.","t":"A：保險公司寄信給我們說明年的商業保險費會變貴，他們有解釋為什麼漲價嗎？ B：他們說【全球暖化】每年造成更多颱風和水災，所以他們必須支付更多損失，因此對所有客戶調漲價格。"},{"w":"climate change","p":"n.phr.","d":"long-term changes in the earth's weather patterns, mainly caused by people","c":"氣候變遷","s":"A: Our board of directors asked every department to suggest ways to cut energy use this year, so why are they suddenly so interested in this issue? B: Many investors now worry about climate change, and they want companies to show clear plans for reducing pollution and protecting the environment in the future.","t":"A：董事會要求每個部門今年提出減少能源使用的方法，他們為什麼突然這麼關心這個議題？ B：現在許多投資人擔心【氣候變遷】，他們希望公司提出明確的計畫來減少污染並保護未來的環境。"},{"w":"emissions","p":"n.","d":"gases or other substances sent out into the air","c":"排放物；排放量","s":"A: The government announced new environmental rules for factories last month, so what does our plant need to change before the deadline in December? B: We must reduce our carbon emissions by fifteen percent, so the engineers are replacing the old boilers and adding filters to the chimneys.","t":"A：政府上個月公布了新的工廠環保規定，我們工廠在十二月截止日前需要做哪些改變？ B：我們必須把碳【排放量】減少百分之十五，所以工程師正在更換舊鍋爐，並在煙囪加裝濾網。"},{"w":"carbon","p":"n.","d":"a chemical element; often used to mean the carbon dioxide released into the air","c":"碳","s":"A: Our customers keep asking whether our delivery service is environmentally friendly, so what should I tell them when they call the hotline? B: Tell them we switched to electric vans last year, which cut the amount of carbon our trucks release by almost half, and we plan to replace the rest by 2028.","t":"A：客戶一直問我們的配送服務是否環保，他們打客服專線時我該怎麼回答？ B：告訴他們我們去年改用電動貨車，讓車隊排放的【碳】減少了將近一半，而且我們計畫在2028年前汰換其餘車輛。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to continue for a long time without harming the environment","c":"永續的；可持續的","s":"A: The new hotel owner wants to attract younger travelers who care about the environment, so what changes is she planning for the building? B: She wants to make the hotel more sustainable by installing solar panels, collecting rainwater for the gardens, and serving food from local farms instead of imported products.","t":"A：新的飯店老闆想吸引重視環保的年輕旅客，她打算對建築物做哪些改變？ B：她想透過安裝太陽能板、收集雨水澆花園，以及供應當地農場的食物而非進口產品，讓飯店更加【永續】。"},{"w":"extreme","p":"adj.","d":"very great or severe; much more than usual","c":"極端的","s":"A: Why did the airport cancel so many flights yesterday, even though the sky looked clear here in the city? B: The problem was at the other end, because extreme weather in northern Japan, including heavy snow and freezing winds, closed three airports there for most of the day.","t":"A：昨天這裡市區的天空看起來很晴朗，機場為什麼還取消了這麼多航班？ B：問題出在另一端，因為日本北部的【極端】天氣，包括大雪和冰冷的強風，讓那裡三座機場大半天都關閉了。"},{"w":"variable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change often","c":"多變的；易變的","s":"A: I'm going to London for a week of meetings with our British partners next month, so what kind of clothes do you think I should pack? B: The weather there is very variable in spring, so it might be sunny in the morning and rainy in the afternoon, and you should bring a light jacket and an umbrella.","t":"A：我下個月要去倫敦和英國夥伴開一週的會，你覺得我該帶什麼樣的衣服？ B：那裡春天的天氣非常【多變】，可能早上晴天、下午下雨，你應該帶一件薄外套和一把雨傘。"},{"w":"mild","p":"adj.","d":"not too hot and not too cold; pleasant","c":"溫和的；暖和的","s":"A: Our company is choosing a place for the annual staff trip in January, so why did the planning committee choose southern Taiwan instead of the mountains? B: The winter weather in the south is usually mild, around twenty-three degrees, so people can enjoy outdoor activities without thick coats or the risk of icy roads.","t":"A：公司正在為一月的年度員工旅遊選地點，為什麼籌備委員會選擇南台灣而不是山區？ B：南部冬天的天氣通常很【溫和】，大約二十三度，大家不用穿厚外套，也不必擔心路面結冰，就能享受戶外活動。"},{"w":"predictable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be known or expected before it happens","c":"可預測的","s":"A: Why do the managers at the beach resort plan their busy summer schedule so early, even in February? B: The weather there is quite predictable, with sunny days from June to September almost every year, so they can confidently hire extra staff and book tour groups many months ahead.","t":"A：海灘度假村的經理們為什麼這麼早，甚至在二月就規劃夏季旺季的排班？ B：那裡的天氣相當【可預測】，幾乎每年六月到九月都是晴天，所以他們可以放心地提前好幾個月加聘人手和預訂旅行團。"},{"w":"unstable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change suddenly; not steady","c":"不穩定的","s":"A: The hiking club from our company planned to climb Jade Mountain this weekend, so why did the leader suddenly postpone the trip? B: The weather in the mountains has been very unstable this week, with sudden thunderstorms in the afternoons, so she thought it was too risky for the group.","t":"A：公司的登山社原本計畫這週末去爬玉山，為什麼領隊突然延期了？ B：這週山上的天氣非常【不穩定】，下午常有突如其來的雷陣雨，所以她認為對團體來說太危險了。"},{"w":"long-term","p":"adj.","d":"continuing for a long time into the future","c":"長期的","s":"A: Why did the city council decide to build a new seawall along the harbor, when it will take ten years to finish? B: They are thinking about the long-term risk of rising sea levels, because experts say that many shops and homes near the port could be under water in fifty years.","t":"A：市議會為什麼決定沿著港口興建新的海堤，明明要花十年才能完工？ B：他們考量的是海平面上升的【長期】風險，因為專家說港口附近的許多商店和住家五十年後可能會被淹沒。"},{"w":"average","p":"adj.","d":"usual or typical; found by adding amounts and dividing by the number of them","c":"平均的","s":"A: The new branch manager is moving from Taipei to Hualien next month, so is she worried about how the weather there will be different? B: Not really, because the average temperature in Hualien is only about one degree lower than in Taipei, although she says it rains more in the winter months.","t":"A：新的分店經理下個月要從台北搬到花蓮，她會擔心那裡的天氣不一樣嗎？ B：不太會，因為花蓮的【平均】氣溫只比台北低大約一度，不過她說冬季月份那裡比較常下雨。"}]},{"unit":61,"theme":"Clothes 服裝","cards":[{"w":"fashionable","p":"adj.","d":"following the latest style; popular now","c":"時髦的；流行的","s":"A: I'm meeting an important client from Milan for lunch tomorrow, and I'm worried my old gray jacket looks a bit boring, so what do you think I should wear? B: You could try that navy blazer you bought last month, because it looks very fashionable but still professional enough for a business meal.","t":"A：我明天要和一位來自米蘭的重要客戶吃午餐，我擔心我那件舊灰色外套看起來有點無聊，你覺得我該穿什麼？ B：你可以試試上個月買的那件海軍藍西裝外套，因為它看起來很【時髦】，但對商務餐敘來說也夠正式。"},{"w":"fashion house","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company that designs and sells expensive clothes","c":"時裝公司；服裝品牌","s":"A: Our marketing team has been asked to design the online campaign for a luxury brand next season, but do you know much about the company? B: Yes, it is a famous French fashion house that has made elegant dresses and handbags since 1920, so we should keep the style simple and classic.","t":"A：我們行銷團隊被要求為一個奢侈品牌設計下一季的線上活動，你對這家公司了解多少？ B：知道，它是一家有名的法國【時裝公司】，從1920年起就製作優雅的洋裝和手提包，所以我們應該讓風格保持簡單經典。"},{"w":"fashion icon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a famous person whose style many people copy","c":"時尚偶像；時尚指標人物","s":"A: Why did the department store decide to put a large photo of that famous actress at the main entrance of the new shop? B: She is a real fashion icon whom many young shoppers admire, so the managers believe her picture will attract more customers to the new clothing section this winter.","t":"A：為什麼百貨公司決定在新店的正門口放那位知名女演員的大照片？ B：她是許多年輕購物者崇拜的真正【時尚偶像】，所以經理們相信她的照片會在今年冬天吸引更多顧客到新的服飾區。"},{"w":"fashion show","p":"n.phr.","d":"an event where models wear new clothes for an audience","c":"時裝秀","s":"A: The hotel ballroom looks very busy this afternoon, with workers carrying lights and a long stage, so what event is happening tonight? B: A local designer is holding a fashion show to present her spring collection, and about three hundred buyers and reporters have already registered to attend.","t":"A：今天下午飯店宴會廳看起來很忙，工人們搬著燈光和一座長舞台，今晚有什麼活動？ B：一位本地設計師要舉辦一場【時裝秀】來發表她的春季系列，已經有大約三百位買家和記者報名參加。"},{"w":"old fashioned","p":"adj.phr.","d":"no longer modern or popular","c":"過時的；老式的","s":"A: Should we keep using the brown uniforms for the front desk staff, or is it time to order new ones before the hotel reopens in March? B: I think we should replace them, because several guests said the design looks old fashioned and does not match our modern lobby.","t":"A：我們應該繼續讓櫃檯人員穿那套咖啡色制服，還是該在飯店三月重新開幕前訂新的？ B：我覺得應該換掉，因為好幾位客人說那個設計看起來很【過時】，和我們現代化的大廳不搭。"},{"w":"tie","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow piece of cloth worn around the neck with a shirt","c":"領帶","s":"A: I have a job interview at the bank tomorrow morning, and I already ironed my white shirt, but do you think I need anything else? B: Yes, you should wear a dark blue tie with that shirt, because most managers at the bank dress formally and will notice small details.","t":"A：我明天早上在銀行有工作面試，我已經燙好白襯衫了，你覺得我還需要什麼嗎？ B：需要，你應該搭配一條深藍色【領帶】，因為銀行大部分主管都穿著正式，會注意到小細節。"},{"w":"suit","p":"n.","d":"a jacket and trousers or skirt made of the same cloth","c":"西裝；套裝","s":"A: The sales director is flying to Singapore next week to sign a large contract with a new partner, so has he prepared everything? B: Almost, but he still needs to pick up his gray suit from the dry cleaner, since he wants to look professional at the signing ceremony.","t":"A：業務總監下週要飛去新加坡和新合作夥伴簽一份大合約，他都準備好了嗎？ B：差不多了，但他還要去乾洗店拿他的灰色【西裝】，因為他想在簽約儀式上看起來很專業。"},{"w":"shorts","p":"n.","d":"short trousers that end above the knee","c":"短褲","s":"A: The company picnic is at the beach on Saturday, and the weather report says it will be very hot, so what should employees wear? B: The organizers said comfortable shorts and sandals are fine, but everyone should bring a hat and sunscreen because we will be outdoors all afternoon.","t":"A：公司野餐週六在海邊，氣象預報說會很熱，員工應該穿什麼？ B：主辦人說穿舒適的【短褲】和涼鞋就可以，但大家都應該帶帽子和防曬乳，因為我們整個下午都會在戶外。"},{"w":"T-shirt","p":"n.","d":"a simple cotton shirt with short sleeves and no collar","c":"T恤","s":"A: We are planning a charity run for our staff next month, and many people want something to remember the event, so do you have any ideas? B: We could print our company logo on a bright orange T-shirt for every runner, because it is cheap, useful, and easy to see in photos.","t":"A：我們正在計畫下個月為員工舉辦慈善路跑，很多人想要紀念這次活動的東西，你有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們可以在每位跑者的亮橘色【T恤】上印公司標誌，因為它便宜、實用，在照片裡也很顯眼。"},{"w":"trousers","p":"n.","d":"a piece of clothing that covers each leg separately","c":"長褲","s":"A: You ordered a new uniform from the online store last week, but you looked unhappy when the package arrived this morning, so was something wrong with it? B: Yes, the jacket fits perfectly, but the trousers are about five centimeters too long, so I need to send them back and ask for a shorter pair.","t":"A：你上週在網路商店訂了一套新制服，但今天早上包裹到的時候你看起來不太高興，是有什麼問題嗎？ B：對，外套非常合身，但【長褲】長了大約五公分，所以我得退回去，請他們換一條短一點的。"},{"w":"suitcase","p":"n.","d":"a large case with a handle for carrying clothes when traveling","c":"行李箱","s":"A: You are leaving for the trade fair in Frankfurt early tomorrow morning, so have you finished packing all your clothes and product samples yet? B: Not yet, because my old suitcase broke last month, so I need to buy a new one with strong wheels at the mall after work today.","t":"A：你明天一早要出發去法蘭克福參加商展，你的衣服和產品樣品都打包好了嗎？ B：還沒，因為我那個舊【行李箱】上個月壞了，所以我今天下班後得去購物中心買一個輪子堅固的新的。"},{"w":"dress","p":"n.","d":"a piece of women's clothing that covers the body and legs","c":"洋裝；連身裙","s":"A: My sister is getting married in a garden in May, and I want to look nice without spending too much money, so where should I shop? B: The new boutique near our office is having a sale this week, and I saw a lovely light blue dress there for only half the usual price.","t":"A：我姊姊五月要在花園裡結婚，我想穿得好看但又不想花太多錢，我該去哪裡買？ B：我們辦公室附近那家新精品店這週在特價，我在那裡看到一件很漂亮的淺藍色【洋裝】，只要平常價格的一半。"},{"w":"flip flop","p":"n.","d":"a light open sandal held on by a strap between the toes","c":"夾腳拖鞋","s":"A: Why are you walking with only one shoe on after the team-building trip to the beach this afternoon? B: A big wave took my left flip flop away while we were playing volleyball near the water, so I have to buy a new pair at the hotel shop before dinner.","t":"A：今天下午去海邊參加團隊建立活動後，你為什麼只穿一隻鞋走路？ B：我們在水邊打排球的時候，一個大浪把我左腳的【夾腳拖】捲走了，所以我晚餐前得去飯店商店買一雙新的。"},{"w":"waistcoat","p":"n.","d":"a sleeveless jacket with buttons worn over a shirt","c":"背心（西裝背心）","s":"A: The restaurant manager wants all the waiters to look more elegant at the wedding dinner on Sunday, so what will they wear? B: Each waiter will wear a white shirt, black trousers, and a dark red waistcoat over the shirt, which matches the colors of the wedding decorations.","t":"A：餐廳經理希望週日婚宴上所有服務生看起來更優雅，他們會穿什麼？ B：每位服務生都會穿白襯衫、黑長褲，再在襯衫外加一件深紅色【西裝背心】，和婚禮佈置的顏色相配。"},{"w":"backpack","p":"n.","d":"a bag carried on your back with two straps","c":"背包","s":"A: You ride your bicycle to the office every day, so how do you carry your laptop, lunch box, and documents without dropping anything? B: I put everything in a large waterproof backpack, which keeps my hands free and protects my computer when it suddenly starts raining on the way.","t":"A：你每天騎腳踏車上班，你是怎麼帶筆電、便當和文件而不掉東西的？ B：我把所有東西都放進一個大的防水【背包】，這樣雙手可以空出來，在路上突然下雨時也能保護我的電腦。"},{"w":"briefcase","p":"n.","d":"a flat case for carrying papers to work","c":"公事包","s":"A: The new lawyer seems very organized, and she always arrives at meetings with every contract ready, so how does she keep her papers so neat? B: She carries a brown leather briefcase with several sections inside, so each client's documents stay separate and she can find them quickly.","t":"A：新來的律師看起來很有條理，每次開會都把所有合約準備好，她是怎麼讓文件保持這麼整齊的？ B：她帶著一個裡面分好幾格的咖啡色皮革【公事包】，所以每位客戶的文件都分開放，她能很快找到。"},{"w":"casual clothes","p":"n.phr.","d":"comfortable, informal clothes such as jeans","c":"便服；休閒服","s":"A: The company has announced a new rule about what we can wear on Fridays, but I missed the meeting this morning, so what did they say? B: From next week, employees may wear casual clothes such as jeans and polo shirts on Fridays, unless they have meetings with important customers.","t":"A：公司宣布了一項關於星期五可以穿什麼的新規定，但我錯過了今天早上的會議，他們說了什麼？ B：從下週開始，員工星期五可以穿牛仔褲和Polo衫之類的【便服】，除非他們要和重要客戶開會。"},{"w":"vintage clothes","p":"n.phr.","d":"good-quality old clothes from an earlier time","c":"復古服裝；古著","s":"A: That small shop on Second Avenue always has a long line of young people outside on weekends, so what does it sell? B: It sells vintage clothes from the 1970s and 1980s, such as old leather jackets and colorful shirts, which have become very popular with university students recently.","t":"A：第二大道上那家小店週末外面總是排著一長串年輕人，它賣什麼？ B：它賣1970和1980年代的【復古服裝】，像是舊皮夾克和色彩鮮豔的襯衫，最近在大學生之間變得非常受歡迎。"},{"w":"smart clothes","p":"n.phr.","d":"neat, formal clothes for special or business events","c":"體面的服裝；正式服裝","s":"A: I've been invited to the annual awards dinner at the Grand Hotel next Friday, but the invitation does not mention a dress code, so what should I do? B: You should wear smart clothes, like a jacket and nice shoes, because the CEO and many important guests will give speeches there.","t":"A：我受邀參加下週五在大飯店舉辦的年度頒獎晚宴，但邀請函沒提到服裝規定，我該怎麼辦？ B：你應該穿【體面的服裝】，像是西裝外套和好看的鞋子，因為執行長和許多重要來賓都會在那裡致詞。"},{"w":"second-hand","p":"adj.","d":"already used or owned by someone else","c":"二手的","s":"A: Our small startup needs desks and chairs for the five new employees, but the budget is very limited this year, so how can we save money? B: We could buy second-hand furniture from the office that is closing downstairs, because the owner is selling everything in good condition at low prices.","t":"A：我們小新創公司需要為五位新員工準備桌椅，但今年預算很有限，我們要怎麼省錢？ B：我們可以向樓下要歇業的辦公室買【二手】家具，因為老闆正以低價出售所有狀況良好的東西。"},{"w":"keen on","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very interested in something or liking it a lot","c":"熱衷於；很喜歡","s":"A: We need someone to help choose the new uniforms for our hotel staff, and the deadline is next Monday, so who should we ask? B: Lisa from reception is very keen on fashion and often reads design magazines, so I'm sure she would be happy to join the project.","t":"A：我們需要有人幫忙挑選飯店員工的新制服，截止日是下週一，我們該問誰？ B：櫃檯的Lisa非常【熱衷於】時尚，常常看設計雜誌，所以我相信她會很樂意加入這個專案。"},{"w":"stylish","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and fashionable in appearance","c":"有型的；時尚的","s":"A: The interior designer showed us three ideas for the new reception area yesterday, so which one do you think the visitors will like best? B: I prefer the second design, because the gray sofas and gold lamps look modern and stylish, and they will give clients a good first impression.","t":"A：室內設計師昨天給我們看了新接待區的三個構想，你覺得訪客會最喜歡哪一個？ B：我比較喜歡第二個設計，因為灰色沙發和金色燈具看起來既現代又【有型】，會給客戶好的第一印象。"},{"w":"abandon","p":"v.","d":"to stop doing or planning something before it is finished","c":"放棄；中止","s":"A: The clothing company spent two years developing a line of paper jackets, so why did they stop selling them so suddenly last month? B: Customers complained that the jackets tore easily in the rain, so the managers decided to abandon the project and focus on cotton products instead.","t":"A：那家服飾公司花了兩年開發一系列紙製外套，為什麼上個月突然停止販售？ B：顧客抱怨外套在雨中很容易破，所以經理們決定【放棄】這個計畫，改為專注於棉製產品。"},{"w":"fancy","p":"adj.","d":"expensive and of high quality, often with decoration","c":"高級的；花俏的","s":"A: The sales team reached its yearly target in only ten months, so how is the manager planning to thank everyone for their hard work? B: She has booked a fancy restaurant on the top floor of a hotel downtown, where we will enjoy a seven-course dinner and a view of the city.","t":"A：業務團隊只用了十個月就達成年度目標，經理打算怎麼感謝大家的辛勞？ B：她在市中心一家飯店頂樓訂了一間【高級】餐廳，我們會在那裡享用七道菜的晚餐，還能欣賞城市景色。"},{"w":"mix and match","p":"v.phr.","d":"to combine different pieces of clothing in different ways","c":"混搭","s":"A: I'm going on a ten-day business trip to three countries, but my suitcase is small, so how can I bring enough outfits for every meeting? B: Pack a few pieces in simple colors like black, white, and navy, so you can mix and match them easily and create a different look each day.","t":"A：我要去三個國家出差十天，但我的行李箱很小，要怎麼帶足夠每場會議穿的衣服？ B：帶幾件黑色、白色和海軍藍等簡單顏色的單品，這樣你就能輕鬆【混搭】它們，每天打造不同的造型。"},{"w":"heap","p":"n.","d":"an untidy pile of things","c":"一堆","s":"A: The storeroom behind the clothing shop is such a mess, and the new manager is visiting tomorrow, so what happened in there? B: The delivery company dropped all the winter coats in a big heap on the floor this morning, and nobody has had time to hang them up yet.","t":"A：服飾店後面的倉庫好亂，新經理明天就要來了，裡面發生什麼事了？ B：貨運公司今天早上把所有冬季大衣在地上丟成一大【堆】，到現在還沒有人有時間把它們掛起來。"},{"w":"ridiculous","p":"adj.","d":"very silly or unreasonable","c":"荒謬的；離譜的","s":"A: Did you see the price of the plain white T-shirt in the new designer shop at the airport while we were waiting for our flight? B: Yes, it cost almost two hundred dollars, which is a ridiculous amount for a simple cotton shirt that you can buy anywhere for much less.","t":"A：我們等班機的時候，你有看到機場那家新設計師商店裡素白T恤的價格嗎？ B：有，要價將近兩百美元，對一件到處都能用便宜得多的價格買到的簡單棉衫來說，真是【離譜的】金額。"},{"w":"denim","p":"n.","d":"a strong cotton cloth, usually blue, used to make jeans","c":"丹寧布；牛仔布","s":"A: Our factory received a large order from a jeans company in Europe, so what kind of material do we need to buy in the next few weeks? B: We need about five thousand meters of strong blue denim, and the supplier promised to deliver it before the end of the month.","t":"A：我們工廠接到歐洲一家牛仔褲公司的大訂單，接下來幾週我們需要買什麼布料？ B：我們需要大約五千公尺耐用的藍色【丹寧布】，供應商答應會在月底前送到。"},{"w":"trendy","p":"adj.","d":"very fashionable and modern at the moment","c":"新潮的；流行的","s":"A: The café on the corner has completely changed its look since it reopened last week, so why is it suddenly so crowded with young customers? B: The new owner turned it into a trendy place with bright lights, colorful chairs, and pretty desserts that people love to share online.","t":"A：轉角那家咖啡館上週重新開幕後外觀完全變了，為什麼突然擠滿了年輕顧客？ B：新老闆把它改造成一個【新潮的】地方，有明亮的燈光、彩色椅子和漂亮的甜點，大家都很喜歡在網路上分享。"}]},{"unit":62,"theme":"Coffee 咖啡","cards":[{"w":"espresso","p":"n.","d":"a small cup of very strong coffee","c":"濃縮咖啡","s":"A: The sales team has a long presentation to prepare before tomorrow's client meeting, so should I order some drinks to help everyone stay awake tonight? B: Yes, please get a few strong cups of espresso from the café downstairs, because most of us prefer something small and powerful rather than a large sweet drink.","t":"A：業務團隊在明天的客戶會議前有一份很長的簡報要準備，所以我應該訂些飲料幫大家今晚保持清醒嗎？ B：好，請從樓下的咖啡館買幾杯【濃縮咖啡】，因為我們大多數人比較喜歡小杯又夠力的，而不是大杯的甜飲料。"},{"w":"beverage","p":"n.","d":"a drink of any kind except water","c":"飲料","s":"A: We are planning the refreshments for the training workshop next Monday, and about sixty employees will attend, so what should we serve during the morning break? B: Let's offer a choice of hot and cold beverage options, such as coffee, juice and sparkling water, along with some light snacks from the bakery.","t":"A：我們正在規劃下週一培訓研習的茶點，大約有六十位員工會參加，上午休息時間要提供什麼呢？ B：我們提供冷熱【飲料】選擇吧，例如咖啡、果汁和氣泡水，再搭配一些麵包店的輕食點心。"},{"w":"iced","p":"adj.","d":"made cold by adding ice","c":"加冰的；冰的","s":"A: It's going to be over thirty-five degrees during the outdoor product launch on Saturday afternoon, so how can we keep our visitors comfortable while they wait? B: We could set up a small stand near the entrance that gives out free iced coffee and lemonade, and we should also put up some large umbrellas for shade.","t":"A：週六下午的戶外產品發表會氣溫會超過三十五度，我們要怎麼讓來賓在等待時感到舒適？ B：我們可以在入口附近設個小攤位，免費發送【冰】咖啡和檸檬水，也應該架起幾把大傘遮陽。"},{"w":"caffeinated","p":"adj.","d":"containing caffeine, which keeps you awake","c":"含咖啡因的","s":"A: I've noticed that you stopped drinking coffee after lunch, so is there a special reason for the change in your daily routine at the office? B: My doctor told me that caffeinated drinks in the afternoon were making it hard for me to fall asleep at night, so now I only have one cup in the morning.","t":"A：我注意到你午餐後就不再喝咖啡了，你在辦公室的日常習慣改變有什麼特別原因嗎？ B：醫生告訴我，下午喝【含咖啡因的】飲料讓我晚上很難入睡，所以現在我只在早上喝一杯。"},{"w":"milky","p":"adj.","d":"containing a lot of milk; pale white like milk","c":"含大量牛奶的；乳白色的","s":"A: The new coffee shop near our branch office has so many choices on its menu, and I never know what to order, so which drink would you recommend for someone who doesn't like bitter flavors? B: Try their milky coffee with extra foam, because it's soft, sweet and much gentler than the black coffee most of us drink.","t":"A：我們分公司附近那家新咖啡店菜單上選擇好多，我總是不知道要點什麼，你會推薦不喜歡苦味的人喝哪一種？ B：試試他們加了額外奶泡的【奶味濃的】咖啡，因為它口感柔順香甜，比我們大多數人喝的黑咖啡溫和多了。"},{"w":"hospitality","p":"n.","d":"friendly and generous treatment of guests; the hotel and restaurant business","c":"款待；好客；餐旅業","s":"A: Our Japanese partners are visiting the factory next week for the first time, and I want them to feel welcome, so what should we prepare for their arrival? B: Let's show them our best hospitality by greeting them at the airport, serving local coffee and snacks in the meeting room, and booking a nice dinner on the first evening.","t":"A：我們的日本合作夥伴下週第一次來參觀工廠，我希望他們感到賓至如歸，我們應該為他們的到來準備什麼？ B：我們就展現最好的【款待】吧：到機場迎接他們、在會議室提供在地咖啡和點心，並在第一天晚上訂一頓好晚餐。"},{"w":"thirst-quenching","p":"adj.","d":"making you stop feeling thirsty","c":"解渴的","s":"A: The runners will finish the charity race at around noon, when the sun is strongest, so what kind of drinks should the volunteers hand out at the finish line? B: We need something cold and thirst-quenching, like water with fresh lemon or a light sports drink, because heavy milk drinks would make the tired runners feel sick.","t":"A：跑者們大約會在中午太陽最大的時候跑完慈善路跑，志工們應該在終點線發什麼樣的飲料？ B：我們需要冰涼又【解渴的】東西，像是加了新鮮檸檬的水或清淡的運動飲料，因為濃厚的奶類飲品會讓疲累的跑者不舒服。"},{"w":"green tea","p":"n.","d":"a light tea made from leaves that are not fermented","c":"綠茶","s":"A: You used to drink three cups of coffee every day at your desk, but recently I've seen you with a different cup, so what are you drinking now? B: I switched to green tea last month because it has less caffeine, it tastes fresh and light, and my colleague from Taichung gave me a large box from her family's farm.","t":"A：你以前每天在座位上喝三杯咖啡，但最近我看到你拿著不同的杯子，你現在喝什麼？ B：我上個月改喝【綠茶】了，因為它咖啡因比較少、味道清爽，而且我台中的同事送了我一大盒她家農場的茶。"},{"w":"top-up","p":"n.","d":"an extra amount added to fill something again, such as a cup","c":"續杯；加值","s":"A: I'm working at the café for the whole afternoon to finish this report, and my cup is almost empty, so do you know if I have to pay for another full coffee? B: No, this shop offers a free top-up of regular filter coffee to customers who stay, so just show your receipt to the barista at the counter.","t":"A：我整個下午都要在咖啡館把這份報告寫完，我的杯子快空了，你知道我需要再付一整杯咖啡的錢嗎？ B：不用，這家店為留下來的客人提供一般濾泡咖啡的免費【續杯】，只要到櫃檯把收據給咖啡師看就好。"},{"w":"make a habit","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start doing something regularly (make a habit of + V-ing)","c":"養成…的習慣","s":"A: You always seem so calm and organized when the busy season starts, even when the rest of the department is stressed, so what's your secret? B: I make a habit of arriving fifteen minutes early, pouring a cup of coffee, and writing a short list of my most important tasks before I open my email each morning.","t":"A：每到旺季開始，即使部門其他人都壓力很大，你總是顯得冷靜又有條理，你的秘訣是什麼？ B：我【養成習慣】每天早上提早十五分鐘到、倒一杯咖啡，並在打開電子郵件前寫下最重要工作的簡短清單。"},{"w":"preference","p":"n.","d":"a liking for one thing more than another","c":"偏好","s":"A: The catering company needs our final order for the annual meeting by Thursday, so should I just choose the standard coffee package for all two hundred guests? B: I think we should first send a short online survey to ask about each guest's preference, because some people want decaf, some need plant milk, and others only drink juice.","t":"A：外燴公司星期四前需要我們年會的最終訂單，我是不是直接幫兩百位來賓都選標準咖啡方案就好？ B：我覺得我們應該先寄一份簡短的線上問卷，詢問每位來賓的【偏好】，因為有人要低咖啡因、有人需要植物奶，還有人只喝果汁。"},{"w":"emphasize","p":"v.","d":"to show that something is especially important","c":"強調","s":"A: The new café manager is meeting all the part-time staff on Friday morning before the weekend rush, so what will be the main point of her talk? B: She plans to emphasize how important it is to greet every customer with a smile and to serve each drink quickly, because the shop recently received several complaints about slow service.","t":"A：新來的咖啡館經理週五早上、週末人潮湧入前要和所有兼職員工開會，她談話的重點會是什麼？ B：她打算【強調】面帶微笑招呼每位客人並快速送上每杯飲料有多重要，因為店裡最近收到好幾則服務太慢的客訴。"},{"w":"dull","p":"adj.","d":"boring; not bright; not sharp","c":"單調乏味的；暗淡的；鈍的","s":"A: Many guests left the afternoon seminar early yesterday, even though the topic was useful for their business, so what do you think went wrong? B: The speaker read every slide in a slow, dull voice for almost two hours, and the organizers didn't even provide coffee during the break to help people stay awake.","t":"A：昨天下午的研討會雖然主題對來賓的生意很有用，但很多人還是提早離開了，你覺得哪裡出了問題？ B：講者用緩慢又【單調乏味的】聲音念了每一張投影片將近兩個小時，而且主辦單位休息時間連咖啡都沒提供，讓大家保持清醒。"}]},{"unit":63,"theme":"Coins 硬幣","cards":[{"w":"currency","p":"n.","d":"the money used in a particular country","c":"貨幣","s":"A: I'm flying to Tokyo for the trade fair next Monday, and I won't have time to visit a bank after I land, so what should I do about money? B: You should exchange some local currency at the airport counter here before you leave, because taxis and small restaurants in Japan often prefer cash.","t":"A：我下週一要飛去東京參加貿易展，落地後沒時間去銀行，錢的部分該怎麼辦？ B：你應該出發前在這裡的機場櫃檯換一些當地【貨幣】，因為日本的計程車和小餐廳常常比較喜歡收現金。"},{"w":"change","p":"n.","d":"coins or small amounts of money","c":"零錢","s":"A: The vending machine on the third floor keeps rejecting my five-hundred-dollar bill, and I really need a coffee before the client meeting starts at ten, so can you help me? B: Sure, I have some small change in my desk drawer, so take a few coins and pay me back after lunch.","t":"A：三樓的自動販賣機一直不收我的五百元鈔票，客戶會議十點開始前我真的需要一杯咖啡，你可以幫我嗎？ B：當然，我書桌抽屜裡有一些【零錢】，拿幾個硬幣去用，午餐後再還我就好。"},{"w":"denomination","p":"n.","d":"the value printed on a coin or bill","c":"面額","s":"A: The bank teller asked how I wanted the cash for the staff party prizes, but I wasn't sure what to say, so what would you suggest? B: Ask for a mix of every denomination, from ten-dollar coins to thousand-dollar bills, so that we can prepare envelopes with different amounts for each winner.","t":"A：銀行行員問我員工派對獎金的現金要怎麼領，但我不確定該怎麼回答，你有什麼建議？ B：每種【面額】都換一些，從十元硬幣到千元鈔票都要，這樣我們就能為每位得獎者準備不同金額的紅包。"},{"w":"mint","p":"v.","d":"to make coins from metal","c":"鑄造（硬幣）","s":"A: Our museum shop wants to sell special coins to celebrate the city's two-hundredth anniversary next spring, but who can actually produce them for us? B: The national coin factory will mint a limited number of silver pieces for us, but we must send them the final drawings before the end of this month.","t":"A：我們博物館商店想販售特別的硬幣，慶祝明年春天城市兩百週年，但誰真的能幫我們製作？ B：國家造幣廠會為我們【鑄造】限量的銀幣，但我們必須在這個月底前把最終設計圖寄給他們。"},{"w":"metal","p":"n.","d":"a hard material such as gold, copper, or iron","c":"金屬","s":"A: Why does the new one-dollar coin feel so much lighter than the old one when I hold it in my hand? B: The government decided to use a cheaper metal to lower production costs, so the coin is thinner and weighs less, although it still looks very similar to the previous version.","t":"A：為什麼新的一元硬幣拿在手上感覺比舊的輕這麼多？ B：政府為了降低生產成本，決定使用比較便宜的【金屬】，所以硬幣變得更薄更輕，不過外觀還是和之前的版本很像。"},{"w":"alloy","p":"n.","d":"a metal made by mixing two or more metals","c":"合金","s":"A: The supplier says the souvenir coins for our hotel guests will not turn green or rust, even after many years, so what are they made of? B: They use a strong alloy of copper and nickel, which is cheaper than pure silver but stays bright and resists damage from water and air.","t":"A：供應商說我們給飯店客人的紀念幣即使過了很多年也不會變綠或生鏽，它們是用什麼做的？ B：他們使用銅和鎳的堅固【合金】，比純銀便宜，但能保持光亮，並且不受水和空氣損害。"},{"w":"design","p":"n.","d":"the pattern or picture on something","c":"圖案設計","s":"A: The marketing team voted on three ideas for the company's tenth-anniversary coin yesterday afternoon, so which one did they finally choose? B: They picked the design with our first office building on one side and a small tree on the other, because it shows how the business has grown since 2016.","t":"A：行銷團隊昨天下午針對公司十週年紀念幣的三個點子投票，他們最後選了哪一個？ B：他們選了一面是我們第一棟辦公大樓、另一面是一棵小樹的【圖案設計】，因為它展現了公司自2016年以來的成長。"},{"w":"engraving","p":"n.","d":"a picture or words cut into metal or stone","c":"雕刻圖案","s":"A: This old coin from my grandfather's drawer looks quite ordinary, so why did the dealer at the antique market offer me such a high price for it? B: Look closely at the tiny engraving of a ship near the bottom, because only a few hundred coins were made with that detail before the factory changed it.","t":"A：這枚從我祖父抽屜找到的舊硬幣看起來很普通，為什麼古董市場的商人出這麼高的價錢？ B：仔細看底部附近那個小小的船隻【雕刻圖案】，因為在工廠改版之前，只有幾百枚硬幣有這個細節。"},{"w":"edge","p":"n.","d":"the outer side or rim of a flat object","c":"邊緣","s":"A: Visitors with poor eyesight sometimes find it hard to tell the fifty-dollar coin from the ten-dollar coin, so how can they separate them quickly? B: They can feel the edge with their fingers, because the larger coin has small lines around it while the smaller one is completely smooth.","t":"A：視力不好的訪客有時很難分辨五十元和十元硬幣，他們要怎麼快速區分？ B：他們可以用手指摸硬幣的【邊緣】，因為較大的硬幣周圍有細紋，而較小的那枚則完全光滑。"},{"w":"face","p":"n.","d":"the front side of a coin, usually with a picture of a person","c":"（硬幣的）正面","s":"A: The new trainee at the bank wants to know which side of each coin should point up in the visitors' display case, so what should I tell him? B: Put the face with the president's portrait on top, because customers usually want to see the famous picture first and the number on the back second.","t":"A：銀行的新進實習生想知道訪客展示櫃裡每枚硬幣該哪一面朝上，我該怎麼告訴他？ B：把印有總統肖像的【正面】朝上，因為顧客通常想先看到有名的人像，再看背面的數字。"},{"w":"reverse","p":"n.","d":"the back side of a coin","c":"（硬幣的）背面","s":"A: The catalog photo only shows the portrait of the queen, so how can our buyers tell which year this coin was made before they place an order? B: Ask the seller to send another picture of the reverse, because the year and the name of the factory are printed on that side beneath the eagle.","t":"A：目錄照片只顯示女王的肖像，我們的買家下單前要怎麼知道這枚硬幣是哪一年鑄造的？ B：請賣家再寄一張【背面】的照片，因為年份和造幣廠名稱就印在那一面的老鷹下方。"},{"w":"circulation","p":"n.","d":"the movement of money from person to person in daily use","c":"流通","s":"A: I found a strange two-dollar coin in my change at the supermarket this morning, and the cashier had never seen one before, so is it still valid? B: Yes, but very few people use it, because the government took most of them out of circulation in 2010 after shoppers complained that they looked too similar to other coins.","t":"A：今天早上我在超市找的零錢裡發現一枚奇怪的兩元硬幣，收銀員也從沒見過，它還能用嗎？ B：可以，但很少人使用，因為2010年購物者抱怨它和其他硬幣太像之後，政府就把大部分收回、不再【流通】。"},{"w":"legal tender","p":"n.phr.","d":"money that must be accepted by law for payments","c":"法定貨幣","s":"A: A tourist at our gift shop wants to pay with old coins from the 1980s that she found at home, so should we accept them or not? B: Please check the list from the central bank first, because those coins are no longer legal tender, and we cannot deposit them into our business account.","t":"A：禮品店有位觀光客想用她在家裡找到的1980年代舊硬幣付款，我們該不該收？ B：請先查看中央銀行的清單，因為那些硬幣已經不是【法定貨幣】，我們也無法把它們存進公司帳戶。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how much money something is worth","c":"價值","s":"A: My uncle left me a box of foreign coins when he moved overseas last year, so how can I find out whether they are worth anything? B: Take them to the coin dealer near the train station, because she can check their condition and age and tell you the real value of each piece for free.","t":"A：我叔叔去年搬到國外時留給我一盒外國硬幣，我要怎麼知道它們值不值錢？ B：拿去火車站附近的錢幣商那裡，她可以檢查它們的狀況和年代，並免費告訴你每一枚的真正【價值】。"},{"w":"worth","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something that a sum of money equals or buys","c":"價值；等值的量","s":"A: The children's charity asked our office to collect spare coins for three months, so how much money did the staff finally give to them yesterday? B: We handed over about five thousand dollars' worth of coins in two heavy glass jars, and the bank needed nearly an hour to count everything by machine.","t":"A：兒童慈善機構請我們辦公室收集零錢三個月，員工們昨天最後給了他們多少錢？ B：我們交出了兩個沉重玻璃罐、大約【價值】五千元的硬幣，銀行用機器數了將近一個小時才數完。"},{"w":"rare","p":"adj.","d":"not common; hard to find","c":"稀有的","s":"A: Why is everyone at the collectors' fair crowding around that small table in the corner instead of visiting the other booths this afternoon? B: The man there is selling an extremely rare coin from 1933, and experts believe fewer than twenty of them still exist anywhere in the world today.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午收藏展上大家都擠在角落那張小桌子旁，而不去逛其他攤位？ B：那裡的男士正在賣一枚1933年極為【稀有的】硬幣，專家認為現今全世界剩下不到二十枚。"},{"w":"ancient","p":"adj.","d":"very old; from a long time ago","c":"古代的","s":"A: The history museum downtown is planning a new exhibition for the summer holidays, so what kind of objects will visitors be able to see there? B: They will show ancient coins from Greece and Rome that are more than two thousand years old, along with tools that people used to make money back then.","t":"A：市中心的歷史博物館正在規劃暑假的新展覽，訪客會在那裡看到什麼樣的展品？ B：他們會展出來自希臘和羅馬、超過兩千年歷史的【古代】硬幣，還有當時人們用來製作錢幣的工具。"},{"w":"collectible","p":"adj.","d":"worth collecting because it is special or limited","c":"具收藏價值的","s":"A: The post office is selling a set of coins with pictures of Taiwan's national parks, so do you think they are just for tourists or for serious buyers? B: They are highly collectible because only five thousand sets were produced, so many people buy them as gifts or as a long-term investment.","t":"A：郵局在賣一組印有台灣國家公園圖案的硬幣，你覺得它們只是給觀光客的，還是給認真的買家？ B：它們非常【具收藏價值】，因為只生產了五千組，所以很多人買來當禮物或長期投資。"},{"w":"shiny","p":"adj.","d":"bright and reflecting light","c":"閃亮的","s":"A: The jewelry store wants to give each customer a lucky coin during the Lunar New Year sale next week, so what should the coins look like? B: They should be bright and shiny, like new gold, because customers believe clean coins bring good fortune, so please ask the bank for freshly made ones.","t":"A：珠寶店下週農曆新年特賣時想送每位客人一枚幸運硬幣，硬幣應該是什麼樣子？ B：應該要明亮又【閃亮】，像新的金子一樣，因為客人相信乾淨的硬幣會帶來好運，所以請向銀行要剛鑄好的硬幣。"},{"w":"worn","p":"adj.","d":"damaged or thin from long use","c":"磨損的","s":"A: The ticket machine at the parking garage keeps returning one of my coins, even though it looks normal, so what could be wrong with it? B: It is probably too worn after many years of use, because the machine checks the weight and thickness, and old coins slowly become lighter as people handle them.","t":"A：停車場的售票機一直退回我的一枚硬幣，雖然它看起來很正常，可能是哪裡出了問題？ B：它大概用了很多年、太【磨損】了，因為機器會檢查重量和厚度，而舊硬幣經過人們經手後會慢慢變輕。"},{"w":"counterfeit","p":"adj.","d":"fake; made to look real in order to cheat people","c":"偽造的","s":"A: The cashier at our convenience store noticed that several fifty-dollar coins in the drawer felt lighter than usual today, so what should she do? B: She should put them aside and call the police, because they might be counterfeit coins, and a gang was caught making fake money in this area last month.","t":"A：我們便利商店的收銀員今天發現抽屜裡好幾枚五十元硬幣比平常輕，她該怎麼辦？ B：她應該把它們放在一旁並報警，因為它們可能是【偽造的】硬幣，上個月這一帶才抓到一個製造假錢的集團。"},{"w":"authentic","p":"adj.","d":"real, not a copy","c":"真品的；真正的","s":"A: An online seller is offering a silver coin from the eighteenth century for only three thousand dollars, so should our gallery buy it for the new display? B: Not yet, because we must first ask an expert to confirm that it is authentic, since many cheap copies of old coins are sold on the internet.","t":"A：有位網路賣家只要三千元就賣一枚十八世紀的銀幣，我們畫廊要買來放新展區嗎？ B：先不要，因為我們必須先請專家確認它是【真品】，網路上有很多便宜的舊硬幣仿製品。"},{"w":"collect","p":"v.","d":"to get and keep things of one kind as a hobby","c":"收集","s":"A: Your desk is always full of small plastic bags and boxes, so what are you doing with all those coins from different countries? B: I collect coins from every place I visit on business trips, and so far I have pieces from twenty-three countries, which I plan to show my children someday.","t":"A：你的桌上總是放滿小塑膠袋和盒子，你拿那些來自不同國家的硬幣做什麼？ B：我出差到每個地方都會【收集】當地的硬幣，到目前為止已經有二十三個國家的硬幣，打算有一天給我的孩子看。"},{"w":"trade","p":"v.","d":"to exchange one thing for another","c":"交換","s":"A: You and Mr. Lin from accounting seem to spend every lunch break looking at coins together, so what exactly are you two doing? B: We trade coins with each other, because he has extra pieces from Europe that I need, and I have several Japanese ones that are missing from his set.","t":"A：你和會計部的林先生好像每天午休都一起看硬幣，你們兩個到底在做什麼？ B：我們彼此【交換】硬幣，因為他有我需要的多餘歐洲硬幣，而我有幾枚他那套收藏缺少的日本硬幣。"},{"w":"spend","p":"v.","d":"to use money to buy things","c":"花（錢）","s":"A: I still have a lot of euro coins left over from the conference in Paris, and banks here will not exchange them, so what can I do? B: Try to spend them at the airport shops before your next flight to Europe, because coins are usually impossible to change back into Taiwan dollars.","t":"A：我在巴黎開會後還剩很多歐元硬幣，這裡的銀行不收，我該怎麼辦？ B：下次飛歐洲時試著在機場商店把它們【花掉】，因為硬幣通常沒辦法換回台幣。"},{"w":"save","p":"v.","d":"to keep money instead of spending it","c":"存（錢）","s":"A: Your daughter told me she wants to buy a new bicycle before the summer vacation starts, so how is she planning to pay for it? B: She has decided to save all the coins she receives as pocket money in a large piggy bank, and I promised to pay half if she reaches her goal.","t":"A：你女兒跟我說她想在暑假開始前買一台新腳踏車，她打算怎麼付錢？ B：她決定把收到的零用錢硬幣全部【存】進一個大撲滿裡，我答應她如果達到目標就幫她出一半。"},{"w":"flip","p":"v.","d":"to throw a coin into the air so that it turns over","c":"擲（硬幣）","s":"A: Both teams want to present first at tomorrow's sales competition, and the manager doesn't want to treat either side unfairly, so how will she decide? B: She will flip a coin in front of both team leaders before the meeting starts, and the winner of the toss can choose to go first or second.","t":"A：明天的業務比賽兩隊都想先報告，經理又不想對任何一方不公平，她會怎麼決定？ B：她會在會議開始前當著兩位隊長的面【擲】硬幣，猜贏的一方可以選擇先報告或後報告。"},{"w":"deposit","p":"v.","d":"to put money into a bank account","c":"存入","s":"A: Our café collects a huge bag of coins from the tip jar every week, and it is getting too heavy to keep in the office, so what do you suggest? B: You can deposit them at the bank's coin machine on Friday mornings, and the money goes straight into the café account without any extra fee.","t":"A：我們咖啡館每週從小費罐收到一大袋硬幣，重到不適合放在辦公室，你有什麼建議？ B：你可以在週五早上用銀行的硬幣機把它們【存入】，錢會直接進到咖啡館的帳戶，不收額外手續費。"},{"w":"count","p":"v.","d":"to find the total number of something","c":"數；計算","s":"A: The night manager says the cash register was short by about two hundred dollars yesterday, so what will we do differently from now on? B: Two staff members will count all the coins and bills together at the end of every shift, and then both of them will sign the report before going home.","t":"A：夜班經理說昨天收銀機短少了大約兩百元，從現在起我們要怎麼做？ B：每班結束時會由兩位員工一起【數】所有硬幣和鈔票，然後兩人都在報告上簽名才下班。"},{"w":"collector","p":"n.","d":"a person who collects things as a hobby","c":"收藏家","s":"A: Who was that elderly gentleman asking so many questions at the information desk about the coin exhibition this morning? B: He is a famous collector from Tainan who owns more than ten thousand old coins, and he offered to lend us some of his best pieces for next year's show.","t":"A：今天早上在服務台問了很多硬幣展覽問題的那位老先生是誰？ B：他是來自台南的知名【收藏家】，擁有超過一萬枚舊硬幣，還主動借我們幾枚他最好的硬幣參加明年的展覽。"},{"w":"numismatics","p":"n.","d":"the study or collecting of coins and money","c":"錢幣學","s":"A: The university is offering evening courses for adults next semester, and I am interested in history and money, so which class would you recommend? B: You should try the class on numismatics, because the professor teaches how to study old coins and what they tell us about trade and daily life in the past.","t":"A：大學下學期開設成人夜間課程，我對歷史和金錢有興趣，你推薦哪一門課？ B：你應該試試【錢幣學】這門課，因為教授會教大家如何研究舊硬幣，以及它們能告訴我們過去的貿易和日常生活。"},{"w":"treasure","p":"n.","d":"a collection of valuable things such as gold or coins","c":"寶藏","s":"A: I read in the news that workers building the new subway station downtown found something unusual underground last week, so what was it? B: They discovered a hidden treasure of about three hundred gold coins inside an old clay pot, and historians think a rich family buried it during a war.","t":"A：我在新聞上看到，在市中心興建新捷運站的工人上週在地底發現不尋常的東西，那是什麼？ B：他們在一個舊陶罐裡發現了大約三百枚金幣的隱藏【寶藏】，歷史學家認為是某個富有家族在戰爭時埋下的。"}]},{"unit":64,"theme":"Colleague 同事","cards":[{"w":"colleague","p":"n.","d":"a person you work with in the same company or profession","c":"同事","s":"A: I heard you are leaving early on Friday afternoon to catch a flight to Tokyo, so who will answer your clients' calls while you are away? B: I asked a colleague from the marketing department to cover for me, and she already knows most of my customers because we worked on several accounts together last year.","t":"A：我聽說你週五下午要提早離開去搭飛往東京的班機，你不在的時候誰來接你客戶的電話？ B：我請了行銷部的一位【同事】幫我代班，她已經認識我大部分的客戶，因為我們去年一起負責過好幾個客戶帳戶。"},{"w":"coworker","p":"n.","d":"a person who works with you at the same place","c":"同事、同僚","s":"A: You look much happier at the office these days, so did something change after you moved to the new branch downtown? B: Yes, my new coworker at the next desk showed me how to use the booking system on my first day, and now we often eat lunch together near the station.","t":"A：你最近在辦公室看起來開心多了，搬到市中心的新分店後有什麼改變嗎？ B：有啊，坐我隔壁的新【同事】在我第一天就教我怎麼用訂位系統，現在我們常常一起在車站附近吃午餐。"},{"w":"teammate","p":"n.","d":"a person who is on the same team as you","c":"隊友、團隊夥伴","s":"A: The sales competition between the branches ends next Monday, so how is your group doing compared with the other offices? B: We are in second place right now, but my teammate Kevin just signed a big contract with a hotel chain this morning, so we may finally move into first place.","t":"A：各分店之間的業績競賽下週一結束，你們這組和其他辦公室比起來表現如何？ B：我們目前排第二，但我的【隊友】凱文今天早上剛和一家連鎖飯店簽下一份大合約，所以我們也許終於能衝上第一名。"},{"w":"associate","p":"n.","d":"a person you work or do business with","c":"夥伴、合夥人、同事","s":"A: Our law firm needs someone to meet the client from Singapore at the airport tomorrow, but I have to be in court all day, so can you help? B: I will send my business associate, Ms. Huang, because she has handled this client's contracts before and speaks both English and Mandarin very well.","t":"A：我們事務所明天需要有人去機場接來自新加坡的客戶，但我整天都要出庭，你能幫忙嗎？ B：我會派我的事業【夥伴】黃小姐去，因為她以前處理過這位客戶的合約，而且英語和中文都說得很好。"},{"w":"staff","p":"n.","d":"all the people who work for an organization","c":"全體員工、職員","s":"A: The hotel is going to be completely full during the international trade fair next week, so do we have enough people to work at the front desk? B: Not really, so the manager has hired five extra staff members for the busy period, and they will start training with us this Thursday morning.","t":"A：下週國際貿易展期間飯店會完全客滿，我們有足夠的人手在櫃台工作嗎？ B：其實不太夠，所以經理為忙碌期間多聘了五名【工作人員】，他們這週四早上就會開始跟我們一起受訓。"},{"w":"employee","p":"n.","d":"a person who is paid to work for a company","c":"員工、雇員","s":"A: The new factory near Taichung is opening in March, so how many people will the company need to hire before then? B: The plan is to hire about two hundred, and every new employee will receive two weeks of safety training before they are allowed to operate any of the machines on the production line.","t":"A：台中附近的新工廠三月就要開幕了，公司在那之前需要雇用多少人？ B：計畫是雇用大約兩百人，每位新【員工】在被允許操作生產線上的任何機器之前，都會接受兩週的安全訓練。"},{"w":"manager","p":"n.","d":"a person who controls or runs a department or business","c":"經理、主管","s":"A: A customer just called to complain that her order arrived damaged for the second time this month, and she wants to speak to someone in charge. B: Please put her through to the store manager, because only he can approve a full refund and offer her free delivery on her next purchase.","t":"A：一位顧客剛打來抱怨她的訂單這個月第二次送到時已經損壞，她想跟負責人說話。 B：請把電話轉給店【經理】，因為只有他能核准全額退款，並提供她下次購物免運費。"},{"w":"supervisor","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches and directs workers","c":"主管、督導","s":"A: I made a mistake on the delivery schedule yesterday, and now two trucks are going to arrive at the warehouse at the same time, so what should I do? B: Tell your supervisor right away, because she can change the loading times and ask the night shift workers to help unload the extra boxes.","t":"A：我昨天把送貨時程表弄錯了，現在兩輛卡車會同時抵達倉庫，我該怎麼辦？ B：馬上告訴你的【主管】，因為她可以更改裝貨時間，並請夜班工人幫忙卸下多出來的箱子。"},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns or runs a business with another person","c":"合夥人、夥伴","s":"A: Your new bakery has become very popular in the neighborhood, so how did you manage to open it so quickly after leaving your office job? B: My old university classmate became my partner, and she paid half of the rent and equipment costs while I focused on creating the recipes and training the staff.","t":"A：你的新麵包店在附近變得很受歡迎，你離開辦公室工作後怎麼能這麼快就開店？ B：我的大學老同學成了我的【合夥人】，她負擔了一半的租金和設備費用，而我專心研發食譜和訓練員工。"},{"w":"professional","p":"n.","d":"a person who is trained and skilled in a job","c":"專業人士","s":"A: The pipes in the office kitchen are leaking again, and water is spreading across the floor, so should we try to fix them ourselves this afternoon? B: No, it is better to call a trained professional who has the right tools, because if we make the problem worse, the repair will cost much more.","t":"A：辦公室茶水間的水管又漏水了，水正蔓延到整個地板上，我們今天下午要不要自己試著修理？ B：不，最好打電話找一位有合適工具、受過訓練的【專業人士】，因為如果我們把問題弄得更糟，修理費會貴很多。"},{"w":"team","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together","c":"團隊","s":"A: The client wants the new website finished by the end of the month, which is much sooner than we expected, so can one designer do it alone? B: No, it is too much work for one person, so I am putting together a small team of three designers and two programmers to share the job.","t":"A：客戶希望新網站在月底前完成，比我們預期的早很多，一個設計師能獨自完成嗎？ B：不行，對一個人來說工作量太大了，所以我要組一個由三位設計師和兩位程式設計師組成的小【團隊】來分擔工作。"},{"w":"workplace","p":"n.","d":"the place where people work","c":"工作場所、職場","s":"A: Many of our younger staff members say they feel tired and stressed by the end of the week, so what can the company do to help them? B: We should make the workplace more comfortable by adding plants, quiet rooms and better lighting, and we could also let people work from home on Fridays.","t":"A：我們許多年輕員工說他們到週末時感到疲累又有壓力，公司能做些什麼來幫助他們？ B：我們應該增加植物、安靜室和更好的照明，讓【工作場所】更舒適，也可以讓大家週五在家工作。"},{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others to reach a goal","c":"合作、配合","s":"A: The two departments have been arguing about the budget for weeks, and now the product launch is in danger of being delayed, so what should we do? B: The director called a meeting this morning and told both sides that they must cooperate with each other if they want the launch to happen on time.","t":"A：兩個部門為了預算已經爭執好幾週，現在產品發表可能會延後，我們該怎麼辦？ B：主任今天早上召開會議，告訴雙方如果想讓發表會準時舉行，就必須彼此【合作】。"},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with someone to create or produce something","c":"合作、協作","s":"A: Our company wants to design a new line of sports shoes for young runners, but we do not have much experience with that market, right? B: That is true, so we plan to collaborate with a famous local athlete and a design school in Taipei to create shoes that teenagers will really want to buy.","t":"A：我們公司想為年輕跑者設計一系列新的運動鞋，但我們對那個市場沒有太多經驗，對吧？ B：沒錯，所以我們打算與一位知名的本地運動員和台北一所設計學校【協作】，打造青少年真正想買的鞋子。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information or ideas with other people","c":"溝通、傳達","s":"A: Since half of our department started working from home three days a week, people often miss important updates, so how can we fix this? B: We should communicate more clearly by sending a short email summary every morning and holding a fifteen-minute video call before lunch on Mondays and Thursdays.","t":"A：自從我們部門有一半的人開始每週在家工作三天，大家常常錯過重要的最新消息，我們要怎麼解決？ B：我們應該更清楚地【溝通】，每天早上寄一份簡短的電子郵件摘要，並在週一和週四午餐前舉行十五分鐘的視訊會議。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help and encourage someone","c":"支持、支援","s":"A: I am worried about giving my first presentation to the board of directors next Tuesday, because my English is still not very fluent. B: Don't worry, the whole department will support you, and I can help you practice your speech during our lunch breaks every day this week.","t":"A：我很擔心下週二第一次向董事會做簡報，因為我的英文還不是很流利。 B：別擔心，整個部門都會【支持】你，而且這週每天午休時間我都可以幫你練習你的演講。"},{"w":"respect","p":"v.","d":"to admire someone and treat them well","c":"尊重、敬重","s":"A: The new team leader is much younger than most of the engineers in our group, so do you think they will listen to her instructions? B: I think they will, because people quickly learn to respect someone who works hard, listens carefully and always explains her decisions in a calm and fair way.","t":"A：新的組長比我們組裡大部分工程師都年輕得多，你覺得他們會聽她的指示嗎？ B：我想會的，因為人們很快就會【尊重】一個努力工作、仔細傾聽，而且總是冷靜公平地解釋自己決定的人。"},{"w":"assist","p":"v.","d":"to help someone do something","c":"協助、幫助","s":"A: The conference room needs to be ready for sixty guests by nine o'clock tomorrow, but I still have to print all the name tags and handouts. B: I will ask two interns to assist you with setting up the chairs, the projector and the coffee table, so you can focus on the printing.","t":"A：會議室明天九點前要準備好接待六十位來賓，但我還得印出所有的名牌和講義。 B：我會請兩位實習生【協助】你擺放椅子、投影機和咖啡桌，這樣你就能專心印東西了。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted to do something well","c":"可靠的","s":"A: We need someone to collect the payments from our stores every evening and take the money to the bank, so who would you recommend? B: I would choose Mr. Chen, because he is very reliable; in ten years he has never been late, and he always checks every receipt twice before he leaves.","t":"A：我們需要有人每天傍晚向各店收款，再把錢送到銀行，你會推薦誰？ B：我會選陳先生，因為他非常【可靠】；十年來他從沒遲到過，而且離開前總是把每張收據檢查兩次。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help and encouragement to others","c":"支持的、給予鼓勵的","s":"A: How did you feel during your first month at the accounting firm, since you had never worked in an office before? B: It was easier than I expected, because my coworkers were very supportive, and they always answered my questions patiently and invited me to join them for lunch.","t":"A：你在會計事務所的第一個月感覺如何？畢竟你以前從沒在辦公室工作過。 B：比我預期的輕鬆，因為我的同事們都非常【支持、照顧人】，總是耐心回答我的問題，還邀請我一起吃午餐。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"useful, or willing to help","c":"有幫助的","s":"A: I need to find out how to change the shipping address on a customer's order, but the instructions in the computer system are really confusing. B: The video guide that the IT department made last month is very helpful, because it shows every step slowly and clearly in less than five minutes.","t":"A：我需要知道怎麼更改顧客訂單上的寄送地址，但電腦系統裡的說明真的很令人困惑。 B：資訊部上個月做的影片教學非常【有幫助】，因為它在五分鐘內就把每個步驟慢慢且清楚地示範出來。"},{"w":"experienced","p":"adj.","d":"having knowledge or skill from doing something for a long time","c":"有經驗的、經驗豐富的","s":"A: The new branch in Kaohsiung is losing money, and the staff there seem to have no clear plan, so what does head office want to do? B: They are sending an experienced manager who has run three successful stores before, and she will stay there for six months to train the local team.","t":"A：高雄的新分店在虧錢，那邊的員工似乎沒有明確的計畫，總公司打算怎麼做？ B：他們要派一位以前經營過三家成功門市、【經驗豐富的】經理，她會在那裡待六個月來訓練當地團隊。"},{"w":"skilled","p":"adj.","d":"having the ability and training to do something well","c":"熟練的、有技術的","s":"A: The furniture factory has received a large order of handmade tables from a hotel in Japan, but the deadline is very tight, isn't it? B: Yes, so we are hiring several skilled workers who can cut and shape wood quickly and accurately without wasting too much expensive material.","t":"A：家具工廠接到日本一家飯店的大量手工桌子訂單，但期限很緊，不是嗎？ B：是的，所以我們正在雇用幾位能夠快速準確地切割和塑形木材、又不會浪費太多昂貴材料的【熟練】工人。"},{"w":"friendly","p":"adj.","d":"kind and pleasant to other people","c":"友善的","s":"A: What do our hotel guests usually say about their stay when they write reviews on the booking website after they check out? B: Most of them say the rooms are a little small, but the front desk staff are very friendly and always greet them with a warm smile and useful tips about the city.","t":"A：我們飯店的房客退房後在訂房網站寫評論時，通常怎麼評價他們的住宿？ B：他們大多說房間有點小，但櫃台人員非常【友善】，總是帶著溫暖的笑容迎接他們，還提供實用的城市旅遊建議。"},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"working well without wasting time or money","c":"有效率的","s":"A: Last year it took our office almost a week to process each customer's insurance claim, so why is it so much faster now? B: We started using new software that is far more efficient, so most claims are checked and approved within two days without any extra paperwork.","t":"A：去年我們辦公室處理每位客戶的保險理賠幾乎要花一週，為什麼現在快這麼多？ B：我們開始使用一套更【有效率】的新軟體，所以大部分理賠在兩天內就能審核並通過，不需要額外的文書作業。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"working hard and caring a lot about something","c":"盡心盡力的、專注投入的","s":"A: Why did the company choose Ms. Lin as Employee of the Year, since there are so many hard-working people in the sales department? B: She is extremely dedicated to her customers; she often stays late to solve their problems and even visited a sick client in the hospital last winter.","t":"A：銷售部有那麼多努力工作的人，公司為什麼選林小姐為年度最佳員工？ B：她對客戶極為【盡心盡力】；她常常加班到很晚幫他們解決問題，去年冬天甚至去醫院探望一位生病的客戶。"},{"w":"trustworthy","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted; honest","c":"值得信賴的","s":"A: We need someone to manage the key to the safe where we keep the company's important documents and cash, so who should we choose? B: Mrs. Wang has worked here for fifteen years and has never broken a rule, so I think she is the most trustworthy person in the whole office.","t":"A：我們需要有人管理存放公司重要文件和現金的保險箱鑰匙，該選誰呢？ B：王太太在這裡工作了十五年，從沒違反過任何規定，所以我認為她是整個辦公室最【值得信賴】的人。"},{"w":"busy","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of things to do","c":"忙碌的","s":"A: Could we get together this week to talk about the new advertising plan for the summer sale, maybe on Wednesday afternoon? B: I am sorry, but I will be very busy until Thursday because I have to visit three clients and finish the monthly sales report, so how about Friday morning instead?","t":"A：我們這週可以見個面討論夏季特賣的新廣告計畫嗎？也許週三下午？ B：抱歉，我到週四前都會非常【忙碌】，因為我要拜訪三位客戶並完成每月銷售報告，改成週五早上如何？"},{"w":"meeting","p":"n.","d":"an event where people come together to discuss something","c":"會議","s":"A: Everyone in the marketing department seems to be in a hurry this morning, so is something important happening today? B: Yes, there is a meeting with our biggest client at ten o'clock, and we need to show them the new advertising plan, the budget and the results of last month's survey.","t":"A：今天早上行銷部每個人看起來都很匆忙，今天有什麼重要的事嗎？ B：是的，十點要和我們最大的客戶開【會議】，我們需要向他們展示新的廣告計畫、預算以及上個月的調查結果。"},{"w":"project","p":"n.","d":"a planned piece of work with a clear goal","c":"專案、計畫","s":"A: You have been working late every night this month, so what are you and the engineers busy with? B: We are working on a big project to build a new solar power system for a shopping mall in Tainan, and the first stage must be finished before the end of December.","t":"A：你這個月每晚都工作到很晚，你和工程師們在忙什麼？ B：我們正在進行一項大型【專案】，要為台南一家購物中心建造新的太陽能發電系統，第一階段必須在十二月底前完成。"},{"w":"task","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work that must be done","c":"任務、工作","s":"A: Now that you are the new office assistant, what will you have to do first every morning when you arrive at work? B: My first task is to check the email inbox and answer customer questions, and after that I need to order office supplies and update the meeting calendar.","t":"A：既然你是新的辦公室助理，你每天早上到公司首先要做什麼？ B：我的第一項【任務】是檢查電子郵件收件匣並回覆顧客的問題，之後我需要訂購辦公用品並更新會議行事曆。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"comments about how good or bad something is","c":"回饋、意見","s":"A: We tested the new mobile app with fifty customers last week, so what did they think about the design and the payment process? B: Most of the feedback was positive, but several users said the buttons were too small, so the designers are making them bigger before the official launch next month.","t":"A：我們上週讓五十位顧客試用了新的手機應用程式，他們對設計和付款流程有什麼看法？ B：大部分的【意見回饋】都是正面的，但有幾位使用者說按鈕太小，所以設計師正在下個月正式上線前把它們改大。"},{"w":"network","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who know and help each other","c":"人脈網絡","s":"A: You found your new job at the bank so quickly after you moved back to Taipei, so how did you do it? B: I have built a strong network of contacts by going to business events and staying in touch with former colleagues, and one of them told me about the opening.","t":"A：你搬回台北後這麼快就在銀行找到新工作，你是怎麼辦到的？ B：我透過參加商務活動並和以前的同事保持聯絡，建立了強大的人脈【網絡】，其中一位告訴了我這個職缺。"}]},{"unit":65,"theme":"Collection 收藏","cards":[{"w":"collector","p":"n.","d":"a person who collects things as a hobby or business","c":"收藏家","s":"A: The auction house is expecting a big crowd on Saturday, so who do you think will bid on the old Japanese stamps from the 1920s? B: A wealthy collector from Singapore has already called twice to ask about them, and she said she is willing to pay much more than the starting price.","t":"A：拍賣行預計週六會有很多人來，你覺得誰會競標那些1920年代的日本舊郵票？ B：一位來自新加坡的富有【收藏家】已經打了兩次電話來詢問，她說她願意出比起標價高很多的價錢。"},{"w":"collectible","p":"n.","d":"an object that people collect because it is valuable or interesting","c":"收藏品","s":"A: I noticed that the toy company is producing only five thousand of the new robot figures this year, so why are customers lining up outside the shop before it even opens? B: Many fans see each figure as a collectible that will become more valuable over time, so they want to buy one before they sell out.","t":"A：我注意到那家玩具公司今年新的機器人公仔只生產五千個，為什麼顧客在店還沒開門前就在外面排隊？ B：很多粉絲把每個公仔都看成一件會隨著時間越來越值錢的【收藏品】，所以想在賣完之前買一個。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you enjoy doing in your free time","c":"嗜好","s":"A: You always look so relaxed when you come back to the office on Monday mornings, so what do you usually do on the weekends? B: My favorite hobby is collecting old vinyl records, so I spend most Saturdays visiting second-hand shops and markets around the city to look for rare albums.","t":"A：你每週一早上回到辦公室時總是看起來很放鬆，你週末通常都做些什麼？ B：我最喜歡的【嗜好】是收集舊黑膠唱片，所以大部分的週六我都會去城市各處的二手店和市集尋找稀有的專輯。"},{"w":"rare","p":"adj.","d":"not common; not found or seen very often","c":"稀有的","s":"A: Why did the museum decide to put extra security guards in the new exhibition hall when the show opened last week? B: The hall contains several rare coins from ancient Rome, and since only a few of them exist anywhere in the world, the museum cannot risk losing even one.","t":"A：上週展覽開幕時，博物館為什麼決定在新展廳增派保全人員？ B：展廳裡有幾枚來自古羅馬的【稀有】硬幣，而且全世界僅存幾枚，所以博物館連一枚都不能冒險遺失。"},{"w":"valuable","p":"adj.","d":"worth a lot of money","c":"貴重的；值錢的","s":"A: My grandfather left me a box of old watches when he moved into the care home, but I have no idea whether they are worth anything at all. B: You should take them to a professional dealer, because some of those older Swiss models can be very valuable if they still work properly.","t":"A：我祖父搬進安養院時留給我一盒舊手錶，但我完全不知道它們值不值錢。 B：你應該把它們拿給專業的經銷商看，因為有些較舊的瑞士錶款如果還能正常運作，可能非常【貴重】。"},{"w":"unique","p":"adj.","d":"being the only one of its kind","c":"獨一無二的","s":"A: Why is the gallery asking such a high price for that small painted plate in the corner of the front window? B: The artist made it by hand for a royal wedding in 1890, and because there is no other piece like it, the owner says it is completely unique.","t":"A：為什麼畫廊對櫥窗角落那個小彩繪盤子開那麼高的價錢？ B：那是藝術家在1890年為一場皇室婚禮手工製作的，因為沒有其他作品和它一樣，老闆說它完全是【獨一無二的】。"},{"w":"antique","p":"adj.","d":"old and valuable, usually more than 100 years old","c":"古董的","s":"A: The new hotel lobby looks very elegant, so did the designer buy all of this furniture from a modern store in Taipei? B: No, she found most of the antique chairs and tables at a market in France, and some of them were made more than a hundred and fifty years ago.","t":"A：新飯店的大廳看起來非常優雅，設計師是在台北的現代家具店買這些家具的嗎？ B：不是，她大部分的【古董】桌椅都是在法國的市集找到的，有些甚至是一百五十多年前做的。"},{"w":"souvenir","p":"n.","d":"something you buy or keep to remember a place or event","c":"紀念品","s":"A: Did you have enough free time to look around Kyoto after the sales conference finished on Thursday afternoon? B: Yes, I walked through the old streets for two hours and bought a small paper fan as a souvenir for my daughter, who loves anything traditional from Japan.","t":"A：週四下午業務會議結束後，你有足夠的空閒時間逛逛京都嗎？ B：有，我在古老的街道上走了兩個小時，還買了一把小紙扇當作【紀念品】送給我女兒，她很喜歡日本的傳統東西。"},{"w":"album","p":"n.","d":"a book with empty pages for keeping photos or stamps","c":"相簿；集郵冊","s":"A: Where should we keep all the photos from the company's twentieth anniversary party so that visitors can look at them? B: Let's print the best ones and put them in a large leather album on the table in the reception area, so guests can enjoy them while they wait.","t":"A：公司二十週年派對的照片應該放在哪裡，讓訪客可以看？ B：我們把最好的照片印出來，放進接待區桌上的一本大皮革【相簿】裡，這樣客人等候時就可以欣賞。"},{"w":"display","p":"v.","d":"to put something where people can see it","c":"展示；陳列","s":"A: The shop owner just received a large box of hand-painted model trains from Germany, so where is she planning to put them? B: She wants to display them in the big glass cabinet near the entrance, because customers walking past on the street will notice them right away.","t":"A：店主剛收到一大箱來自德國的手繪模型火車，她打算把它們放在哪裡？ B：她想把它們【展示】在入口附近的大玻璃櫃裡，因為走在街上的顧客馬上就會注意到。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in a clear order","c":"整理；安排","s":"A: Your stamp collection has grown so much since last year, but how do you find a particular stamp when you need it? B: Every Sunday evening I organize the new ones by country and year in separate folders, so I can find anything within a minute or two.","t":"A：你的郵票收藏從去年到現在增加了好多，你需要某張郵票時要怎麼找到它？ B：每個週日晚上，我都會把新的郵票依國家和年份【整理】到不同的資料夾裡，所以我一兩分鐘內就能找到任何一張。"},{"w":"sort","p":"v.","d":"to put things into groups by type, size, date, etc.","c":"分類","s":"A: The library received hundreds of old postcards from a local family last week, so what are the volunteers doing with them now? B: They are helping the staff sort the cards into different boxes by city and decade before the library scans them and puts them online.","t":"A：圖書館上週收到當地一戶人家捐的數百張舊明信片，志工們現在在做什麼？ B：他們正在幫工作人員把明信片按城市和年代【分類】到不同的箱子裡，之後圖書館會掃描並放上網。"},{"w":"series","p":"n.","d":"a group of similar things that come one after another","c":"系列","s":"A: Why do so many people come to the bookstore early on the first Friday of every month? B: That is the day the publisher releases the next comic in a popular series about a young detective, and fans want to complete their sets as quickly as possible.","t":"A：為什麼每個月第一個週五都有那麼多人一早就來書店？ B：那天出版社會發行一套熱門少年偵探【系列】漫畫的下一集，粉絲們想盡快把整套收齊。"},{"w":"edition","p":"n.","d":"one form or printing of a book, coin, etc.","c":"版本","s":"A: That old copy of the novel on your office shelf looks quite ordinary, so why are you so careful when anyone touches it? B: It is a first edition that was printed in 1952, and a book dealer told me it could be worth about three thousand dollars today.","t":"A：你辦公室書架上那本舊小說看起來很普通，為什麼有人碰它時你都那麼小心？ B：那是1952年印刷的初【版】，一位書商告訴我它今天可能值三千美元左右。"},{"w":"limited","p":"adj.","d":"small in number or amount","c":"限量的；有限的","s":"A: Should we order the new anniversary mugs for our clients now, or can we wait until the end of the month? B: We should order them today, because the company is producing only a limited number of them, and the sales manager said they will probably sell out by next week.","t":"A：我們應該現在就為客戶訂購新的週年紀念馬克杯，還是可以等到月底？ B：我們今天就該訂，因為公司只生產【有限】的數量，業務經理說下週大概就會賣完。"},{"w":"trade","p":"v.","d":"to give something and receive something else in return","c":"交換；交易","s":"A: My son has two copies of the same baseball card, but he is still missing the famous pitcher from Tainan. B: He could bring the extra card to the club meeting on Saturday and trade it with another member who might have the pitcher card he wants.","t":"A：我兒子有兩張一樣的棒球卡，但他還缺那位來自台南的知名投手。 B：他可以把多的那張卡帶去週六的社團聚會，跟另一位可能有他想要的投手卡的成員【交換】。"},{"w":"swap","p":"v.","d":"to exchange one thing for another","c":"交換；調換","s":"A: I bought a blue team scarf at the stadium, but my wife says she really prefers the red one that you got. B: That's no problem, because I actually like blue better, so we can swap scarves tomorrow when we meet for lunch near the office.","t":"A：我在體育場買了一條藍色球隊圍巾，但我太太說她其實比較喜歡你買的那條紅色的。 B：沒問題，因為我其實比較喜歡藍色，所以明天我們在辦公室附近吃午餐時可以【交換】圍巾。"},{"w":"duplicate","p":"n.","d":"an exact copy of something","c":"複本；重複品","s":"A: When we checked the shipment of old coins this morning, why did you put two of them aside in a separate envelope? B: Each of those coins was a duplicate of one that we already have in the museum, so we plan to sell them to raise money for repairs.","t":"A：今天早上我們檢查那批舊硬幣時，你為什麼把其中兩枚另外放進一個信封裡？ B：那兩枚都是博物館已經有的硬幣的【重複品】，所以我們打算把它們賣掉來籌措修繕經費。"},{"w":"complete","p":"adj.","d":"having all the parts; with nothing missing","c":"完整的","s":"A: Your uncle has been buying those small model cars for almost thirty years, so is he still looking for more of them? B: He finally has a complete set of all the racing cars made in the 1960s, so now he only wants to keep them in good shape.","t":"A：你叔叔買那些小模型車已經將近三十年了，他還在找更多嗎？ B：他終於擁有1960年代所有賽車的【完整】一套，所以現在他只想把它們保持在良好狀態。"},{"w":"set","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that belong together","c":"一套；一組","s":"A: What gift should we give the retiring manager, since she loves drinking tea with her friends every afternoon? B: I saw a beautiful set of hand-painted teacups and a matching pot at the department store, and I think she would really enjoy using them.","t":"A：我們應該送即將退休的經理什麼禮物？她每天下午都喜歡和朋友喝茶。 B：我在百貨公司看到一【套】漂亮的手繪茶杯和配套茶壺，我想她一定會很喜歡用。"},{"w":"theme","p":"n.","d":"the main subject or idea of something","c":"主題","s":"A: There are so many different stamps on the market, so how did you decide which ones to start collecting? B: I chose birds as my main theme, because I love nature, and now I have stamps showing birds from more than sixty different countries around the world.","t":"A：市面上有那麼多不同的郵票，你是怎麼決定要開始收集哪些的？ B：我選了鳥類當作我的主要【主題】，因為我熱愛大自然，現在我有來自全世界六十多個國家、印有鳥類的郵票。"},{"w":"catalog","p":"n.","d":"a list of items for sale, often with pictures and prices","c":"目錄","s":"A: How can customers check which antique maps are available before they travel all the way to our shop? B: We send them an online catalog every month that shows a photo, a short description, and the price of each map that we currently have in the store.","t":"A：顧客要怎麼在大老遠來我們店之前，先查看有哪些古地圖可以買？ B：我們每個月會寄給他們一份線上【目錄】，裡面有店內目前每張地圖的照片、簡短描述和價格。"},{"w":"preserve","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in good condition","c":"保存","s":"A: Why does the museum keep the lights so dim in the room where the old letters and newspapers are shown? B: Strong light damages old paper very quickly, so the staff use soft lighting to preserve the documents for the many future visitors and researchers who will come.","t":"A：為什麼博物館展示舊信件和報紙的展間燈光那麼暗？ B：強光會很快損壞舊紙張，所以工作人員用柔和的燈光來【保存】這些文件，留給未來許多會來的參觀者和研究人員。"},{"w":"condition","p":"n.","d":"the state that something is in","c":"狀況；狀態","s":"A: The seller is asking eight hundred dollars for that old comic book, which seems like a lot of money to me. B: The price is high because the book is in excellent condition, with no torn pages or stains, even though it was printed more than sixty years ago.","t":"A：賣家那本舊漫畫開價八百美元，我覺得這好像很貴。 B：價格高是因為那本書的【狀況】極佳，沒有任何撕破的頁面或汙漬，儘管它是六十多年前印的。"},{"w":"storage","p":"n.","d":"the keeping of things in a special place until they are needed","c":"儲藏；存放","s":"A: Our office is moving to a smaller building next month, so what will we do with all the old files and sample products? B: The company has rented a storage unit near the airport, so we can keep everything there safely until we decide what to throw away.","t":"A：我們辦公室下個月要搬到比較小的大樓，那些舊檔案和樣品要怎麼處理？ B：公司在機場附近租了一個【儲藏】空間，所以在我們決定要丟掉什麼之前，可以把所有東西安全地放在那裡。"},{"w":"case","p":"n.","d":"a box or container for keeping or protecting things","c":"盒子；箱子","s":"A: I'm worried that the old silver coins will get scratched when we carry them to the trade show in Kaohsiung next week. B: Don't worry, because I bought a hard plastic case with soft padding inside, so each coin will stay safe during the trip.","t":"A：我擔心下週把那些舊銀幣帶去高雄商展時會被刮傷。 B：別擔心，我買了一個內有柔軟襯墊的硬塑膠【盒子】，所以每枚硬幣在路上都會很安全。"},{"w":"exhibit","p":"v.","d":"to show something to the public, especially in a museum or gallery","c":"展出","s":"A: The city art museum has been closed for two months, so do you know when it will open again to the public? B: It reopens next Monday, and it will exhibit more than two hundred old toys from a famous private collection for the first time ever.","t":"A：市立美術館已經關閉兩個月了，你知道什麼時候會重新對外開放嗎？ B：下週一重新開放，而且會首次【展出】來自一個知名私人收藏的兩百多件古老玩具。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: Why did so many visitors stop at the small table in the corner of the exhibition hall this morning? B: The old machine on that table makes a strange sound when you turn the handle, so people were curious and wanted to find out what it was used for.","t":"A：今天早上為什麼那麼多參觀者在展覽廳角落的小桌子前停下來？ B：那張桌上的舊機器在你轉動把手時會發出奇怪的聲音，所以大家都很【好奇】，想知道它是用來做什麼的。"},{"w":"passion","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest in or love for something","c":"熱愛；熱情","s":"A: Your manager seems to know a lot about old cameras, so has she always been interested in photography? B: Yes, her passion for cameras started when her father gave her one for her tenth birthday, and now she owns more than three hundred of them.","t":"A：你的經理似乎很懂舊相機，她一直都對攝影有興趣嗎？ B：是的，她對相機的【熱愛】始於她十歲生日時父親送她一台相機，現在她擁有三百多台。"},{"w":"expand","p":"v.","d":"to become larger or make something larger","c":"擴大；擴展","s":"A: The small shop that sells old records has become very popular with young people over the past year, hasn't it? B: Yes, and the owner plans to expand the store next spring by renting the empty space next door, so she can add a listening area.","t":"A：那家賣舊唱片的小店在過去一年很受年輕人歡迎，不是嗎？ B：是的，老闆打算明年春天租下隔壁的空店面來【擴大】店面，這樣她就能增加一個試聽區。"},{"w":"search","p":"v.","d":"to look carefully for something","c":"搜尋；尋找","s":"A: How did you finally find that rare postcard of the old train station that you had wanted for so many years? B: I used to search online auction sites every night after work, and last month someone in Canada listed exactly the card I needed.","t":"A：你最後是怎麼找到那張你想要了好多年的舊火車站稀有明信片的？ B：我以前每天下班後都會【搜尋】網路拍賣網站，上個月加拿大有人剛好刊登了我需要的那張明信片。"},{"w":"discover","p":"v.","d":"to find something for the first time","c":"發現","s":"A: Is it true that the workers found something interesting while they were repairing the roof of the old bank building? B: Yes, they were surprised to discover a metal box full of old coins and letters hidden under the floor of the attic last Tuesday.","t":"A：工人們在修理舊銀行大樓屋頂時找到了有趣的東西，是真的嗎？ B：是的，上週二他們驚訝地在閣樓地板下【發現】一個裝滿舊硬幣和信件的金屬盒。"},{"w":"treasure","p":"n.","d":"something that is very valuable or special to someone","c":"珍寶；寶物","s":"A: Why does your grandmother keep that old wooden box on the top shelf where nobody else can reach it? B: Inside it are letters my grandfather wrote to her during the war, and for her, they are the greatest treasure she owns, more precious than any jewelry.","t":"A：你祖母為什麼把那個舊木盒放在沒人搆得到的最上層架子上？ B：裡面是我祖父在戰爭期間寫給她的信，對她來說，那是她擁有最珍貴的【珍寶】，比任何珠寶都寶貴。"},{"w":"enthusiast","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very interested in a particular activity","c":"愛好者；熱衷者","s":"A: Who is the man in the green jacket talking to the museum guide about the old steam engines? B: He is a railway enthusiast from Australia who travels around the world every year to visit train museums and take photos of historic locomotives.","t":"A：那個穿綠色夾克、正在和博物館導覽員談論舊蒸汽火車頭的男子是誰？ B：他是一位來自澳洲的鐵道【愛好者】，每年都環遊世界參觀火車博物館，並拍攝歷史悠久的火車頭。"}]},{"unit":66,"theme":"Color 顏色","cards":[{"w":"hue","p":"n.","d":"a color or a type of color","c":"色調；色彩","s":"A: The client from the hotel chain said the lobby design looks a little cold, so what changes should we make before Thursday's presentation? B: I suggest we choose a warmer hue for the walls, maybe a soft orange, because guests usually feel more relaxed when the space looks friendly and inviting.","t":"A：連鎖飯店的客戶說大廳設計看起來有點冷冰冰，我們在週四簡報前應該做哪些修改？ B：我建議牆面選擇比較溫暖的【色調】，也許是柔和的橘色，因為空間看起來友善又吸引人時，客人通常會覺得比較放鬆。"},{"w":"shade","p":"n.","d":"a lighter or darker form of a color","c":"（顏色的）深淺；色度","s":"A: The printer delivered our new brochures this morning, but the logo looks different from the one on our website, doesn't it? B: You're right, the blue is a slightly darker shade than our official color, so I'll call the printing company and ask them to correct it before the trade fair next week.","t":"A：印刷廠今天早上送來我們的新手冊，但標誌看起來跟網站上的不一樣，對吧？ B：你說得對，這個藍色的【深淺】比我們的官方顏色稍微深一點，所以我會打電話給印刷公司，請他們在下週商展前修正。"},{"w":"tint","p":"n.","d":"a light amount of color added to something","c":"淡色；（玻璃的）色膜","s":"A: Our sales team often drives clients around the city in the summer, so is there anything we can do to keep the company cars from getting so hot? B: The garage on Fifth Street can add a light gray tint to the windows, which blocks much of the strong sunlight but still lets the driver see clearly.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊夏天常開車載客戶在市區跑，有什麼辦法能讓公司車不要那麼熱嗎？ B：第五街的修車廠可以在車窗加上淡灰色的【色膜】，能擋掉大部分強烈的陽光，但駕駛仍然看得很清楚。"},{"w":"tone","p":"n.","d":"the general quality of a color, such as how warm or dark it is","c":"色調","s":"A: The photographer sent us the pictures for the new catalog, but the manager thinks they look too cold and serious, so what can we do? B: We can ask the designer to adjust the overall tone of the photos so the colors feel softer, because our furniture should look friendly and welcoming to families.","t":"A：攝影師把新型錄的照片寄來了，但經理覺得看起來太冷、太嚴肅，我們能怎麼做？ B：我們可以請設計師調整照片的整體【色調】，讓顏色感覺柔和一點，因為我們的家具應該讓家庭覺得親切又溫馨。"},{"w":"pigment","p":"n.","d":"a substance that gives color to paint, ink, or skin","c":"色素；顏料","s":"A: Why are the art supplies from the new factory so much more expensive than the ones we sold last year? B: The company now uses a natural pigment made from plants and minerals in all its paints, which is safer for children, and many schools are happy to pay a little more for that.","t":"A：為什麼新工廠的美術用品比我們去年賣的貴那麼多？ B：這家公司現在所有的顏料都使用由植物和礦物製成的天然【色素】，對孩子比較安全，很多學校也願意為此多付一點錢。"},{"w":"dye","p":"n.","d":"a substance used to change the color of cloth or hair","c":"染料","s":"A: The fashion company wants to promote its new T-shirts as environmentally friendly, but what makes them different from the ones other brands sell? B: Each shirt is colored with a plant-based dye that uses less water and no harmful chemicals, so the factory doesn't pollute the river near the village.","t":"A：這家服飾公司想把新款T恤宣傳成環保產品，但它們和其他品牌賣的有什麼不同？ B：每件衣服都是用植物性的【染料】染色，用水較少也沒有有害化學物質，所以工廠不會污染村子附近的河川。"},{"w":"palette","p":"n.","d":"a set of colors chosen for a design; a board for mixing paint","c":"配色；調色盤","s":"A: The marketing director wants all of our posters, websites, and shopping bags to look like they belong to the same brand, so how should we plan the design? B: Let's choose a simple palette of four or five colors and use only those everywhere, so customers will recognize our products immediately.","t":"A：行銷總監希望我們所有的海報、網站和購物袋看起來都屬於同一個品牌，那我們該怎麼規劃設計？ B：我們挑一組四到五種顏色的簡單【配色】，並且到處都只用這些顏色，這樣顧客就能立刻認出我們的產品。"},{"w":"vivid","p":"adj.","d":"very bright and strong (of colors)","c":"鮮豔的","s":"A: Our new restaurant is on a busy street with many other shops, so how can we make sure people notice it when they walk past? B: We should paint the front door and the sign in vivid red and yellow, because strong colors catch people's attention even from across the road.","t":"A：我們的新餐廳在一條有很多其他店家的熱鬧街上，要怎樣確保路人經過時會注意到它？ B：我們應該把大門和招牌漆成【鮮豔的】紅色和黃色，因為強烈的顏色即使隔著馬路也能吸引人們注意。"},{"w":"bright","p":"adj.","d":"strong, full of light, and easy to see","c":"明亮的；鮮亮的","s":"A: The children's hospital asked us to redesign the waiting room on the second floor, so what kind of colors do you think would work best? B: I'd use cheerful, bright colors like sunny yellow and sky blue, since young patients often feel nervous and a happy space can help them calm down.","t":"A：兒童醫院請我們重新設計二樓的候診室，你覺得哪種顏色最適合？ B：我會用開朗、【明亮的】顏色，像陽光黃和天空藍，因為小病人常會緊張，一個快樂的空間能幫助他們平靜下來。"},{"w":"pale","p":"adj.","d":"light in color; not strong","c":"淡的；淺的；蒼白的","s":"A: The new meeting room feels very small and crowded, even though only eight people usually sit in there, so what can we do without moving any walls? B: Painting the walls a pale green or light gray would make the room look bigger, especially if we also add a large mirror near the window.","t":"A：新的會議室感覺很小又很擠，雖然通常只有八個人坐在裡面，不拆牆的話我們能怎麼做？ B：把牆漆成【淺】綠色或淺灰色會讓房間看起來比較大，尤其是如果我們也在窗戶旁加一面大鏡子的話。"},{"w":"dark","p":"adj.","d":"close to black in color","c":"深色的；暗的","s":"A: The uniforms for our delivery drivers get dirty very quickly because they spend all day carrying boxes, so should we order different ones? B: Yes, I think dark blue or black uniforms would be more practical, because they hide dust and stains much better than the white shirts we have now.","t":"A：我們送貨司機的制服很快就髒了，因為他們整天都在搬箱子，我們應該訂不同的嗎？ B：是的，我覺得【深】藍色或黑色的制服比較實用，因為它們比我們現在的白襯衫更能遮住灰塵和污漬。"},{"w":"pastel","p":"adj.","d":"soft and light (of colors)","c":"粉彩的；柔和淡色的","s":"A: The bakery owner wants the packaging for her spring cookie collection to look gentle and sweet, so what do you recommend for the boxes? B: Soft pastel colors such as light pink, mint green, and baby blue would be perfect, because they remind customers of flowers and the warm spring weather.","t":"A：烘焙坊老闆希望她春季餅乾系列的包裝看起來溫柔又甜美，你建議盒子用什麼？ B：柔和的【粉彩】色，例如淺粉紅、薄荷綠和嬰兒藍會很完美，因為它們會讓顧客聯想到花朵和溫暖的春天天氣。"},{"w":"neon","p":"adj.","d":"extremely bright, as if giving off light","c":"螢光的；霓虹的","s":"A: Our cycling club is going to ride along the coast road early in the morning, so what should members wear to stay safe in the traffic? B: Everyone should wear a neon yellow or orange vest, because drivers can see those very bright colors from far away, even when it's foggy.","t":"A：我們的自行車社要一大早沿著海岸公路騎車，社員該穿什麼才能在車流中保持安全？ B：每個人都應該穿【螢光】黃或橘色的背心，因為駕駛即使在起霧時也能從很遠的地方看到那些非常亮的顏色。"},{"w":"bold","p":"adj.","d":"strong and easy to notice","c":"醒目的；大膽的","s":"A: The sports drink company wants its new advertisement to feel exciting and full of energy, so which design should we show them first? B: Let's start with the version that uses bold red and black stripes, because those strong, confident colors match the young athletes in the photos very well.","t":"A：那家運動飲料公司希望新廣告感覺刺激又充滿活力，我們應該先給他們看哪個設計？ B：我們先從使用【醒目的】紅黑條紋的版本開始，因為那些強烈又有自信的顏色和照片中的年輕運動員非常搭。"},{"w":"muted","p":"adj.","d":"soft and not bright","c":"柔和的；不鮮豔的","s":"A: The law firm on the tenth floor wants its new office to look calm and serious for clients, so what kind of colors should we suggest? B: I'd recommend muted colors like soft gray, beige, and dusty blue, because bright colors might seem too playful for a professional legal office.","t":"A：十樓的律師事務所希望新辦公室給客戶沉穩、正式的感覺，我們該建議哪種顏色？ B：我會推薦【柔和的】顏色，像淺灰、米色和灰藍色，因為鮮豔的顏色對專業的法律事務所來說可能顯得太活潑。"},{"w":"warm","p":"adj.","d":"(of colors) like red, orange, or yellow","c":"暖色的","s":"A: Customers say our café feels a bit cold and empty in the evening, even though the food is good, so how can we change that feeling? B: We could use warm colors like orange and soft red on the walls and change the lights, so the space feels cozy and inviting at night.","t":"A：客人說我們咖啡館晚上感覺有點冷清，雖然食物很好吃，我們該怎麼改變這種感覺？ B：我們可以在牆上用橘色和柔和的紅色等【暖】色，並更換燈光，讓空間在晚上感覺舒適又吸引人。"},{"w":"cool","p":"adj.","d":"(of colors) like blue or green","c":"冷色的","s":"A: Our spa is opening a new relaxation room next month, and the owner wants guests to feel calm and peaceful the moment they enter, so what colors should we use? B: I'd choose cool colors such as light blue and soft green, because they remind people of water and nature.","t":"A：我們的水療中心下個月要開一間新的放鬆室，老闆希望客人一進門就感到平靜祥和，我們該用什麼顏色？ B：我會選擇淺藍和柔和的綠色等【冷】色系，因為它們會讓人聯想到水和大自然。"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference between two colors or things","c":"對比","s":"A: Some older customers have complained that the text on our website is hard to read, especially on their phones, so what should we fix first? B: We need more contrast between the words and the background, so let's change the light gray text to black and keep the background white.","t":"A：有些年長的客人抱怨我們網站上的文字很難閱讀，尤其是在手機上，我們應該先修正什麼？ B：我們需要讓文字和背景之間有更多【對比】，所以把淺灰色的文字改成黑色，背景維持白色。"},{"w":"blend","p":"v.","d":"to mix together smoothly; to look like part of the surroundings","c":"混合；融合","s":"A: The new warehouse is next to a forest park, and some neighbors worried that it would look ugly from the walking trails, so what did the architects do? B: They painted the outside walls green and brown so the building would blend in with the trees, and now most visitors hardly notice it.","t":"A：新倉庫就在森林公園旁邊，有些鄰居擔心從步道看過去會很醜，建築師怎麼處理的？ B：他們把外牆漆成綠色和棕色，讓建築【融入】樹林中，現在大部分遊客幾乎不會注意到它。"},{"w":"fade","p":"v.","d":"to slowly lose color or brightness","c":"褪色；變淡","s":"A: The large banner outside our shop looked great when we hung it last spring, so why does it look so old and pale now? B: It has been in strong sunlight every afternoon for months, and cheap materials tend to fade quickly, so next time we should pay a little more for a sun-resistant one.","t":"A：我們店外面的大型布條去年春天掛上去時看起來很棒，為什麼現在看起來又舊又淡？ B：它好幾個月每天下午都曬在強烈的陽光下，而便宜的材料往往很快就會【褪色】，所以下次我們應該多花一點錢買抗曬的。"},{"w":"glow","p":"v.","d":"to give out a soft, steady light","c":"發光；發亮","s":"A: The hotel wants guests to find the emergency exits easily if the power suddenly goes off during the night, so what kind of signs should we install? B: We should buy special signs that glow in the dark for several hours, because they still work even when there is no electricity at all.","t":"A：飯店希望如果晚上突然停電，客人也能輕鬆找到緊急出口，我們應該安裝哪種標誌？ B：我們應該買能在黑暗中【發光】好幾個小時的特殊標誌，因為就算完全沒電也還能發揮作用。"},{"w":"sparkle","p":"v.","d":"to shine with many small flashes of light","c":"閃閃發光","s":"A: The jewelry store manager thinks the new diamond rings don't look as attractive in the window display as they did in the catalog, so what should we change? B: Let's add some small spotlights above the display, because diamonds sparkle much more when strong light hits them from different directions.","t":"A：珠寶店經理覺得新款鑽戒在櫥窗展示中不像在型錄裡那麼吸引人，我們該改什麼？ B：我們在展示櫃上方加一些小聚光燈吧，因為強光從不同方向照射時，鑽石會更加【閃閃發光】。"},{"w":"transparent","p":"adj.","d":"clear enough to see through","c":"透明的","s":"A: Customers keep asking whether our salads are fresh before they buy them, so how can we show them the quality more clearly at the counter? B: Let's switch to transparent plastic boxes, so people can see the fresh vegetables inside without opening the lid, and they will feel more confident about buying them.","t":"A：客人在買沙拉前一直問是不是新鮮的，我們要怎麼在櫃檯更清楚地展現品質？ B：我們改用【透明的】塑膠盒吧，這樣大家不用打開蓋子就能看到裡面的新鮮蔬菜，買的時候也會更放心。"},{"w":"translucent","p":"adj.","d":"letting some light through but not clear","c":"半透明的","s":"A: The new office has glass walls around every meeting room, but some managers feel uncomfortable because everyone walking past can see exactly what they are doing, so any ideas? B: We could cover the glass with a translucent film that still lets daylight in but makes the people inside look blurry from the hallway.","t":"A：新辦公室每間會議室周圍都是玻璃牆，但有些經理覺得不自在，因為每個經過的人都能清楚看到他們在做什麼，有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們可以在玻璃上貼一層【半透明的】膜，仍然能讓日光進來，但從走廊看裡面的人會變得模糊。"},{"w":"opaque","p":"adj.","d":"not letting light through; impossible to see through","c":"不透明的","s":"A: Our medicine bottles are currently made of clear plastic, but the lab report says sunlight can damage the pills inside, so what should we do about the packaging? B: We should switch to opaque white bottles that block the light completely, even though they will cost the company a little more to produce.","t":"A：我們的藥瓶目前是用透明塑膠做的，但實驗室報告說陽光可能會損害裡面的藥丸，包裝該怎麼處理？ B：我們應該改用能完全阻擋光線的【不透明】白色瓶子，雖然公司的生產成本會稍微增加。"},{"w":"monochrome","p":"adj.","d":"using only one color, or only black and white","c":"單色的；黑白的","s":"A: The photography exhibition at the city gallery has received excellent reviews, so what makes it different from the other shows this year? B: All the photos are monochrome, using only black, white, and gray, and many visitors say the lack of color makes the faces and emotions in the pictures feel much stronger.","t":"A：市立美術館的攝影展得到極佳的評價，它和今年其他展覽有什麼不同？ B：所有照片都是【黑白單色的】，只用黑、白、灰，很多參觀者說缺少色彩反而讓照片中的臉孔和情感更加強烈。"},{"w":"multicolored","p":"adj.","d":"having many different colors","c":"多色的；五顏六色的","s":"A: The toy company asked us to design a new set of building blocks for young children, so what do you think will attract parents in the stores? B: A box of multicolored blocks in red, yellow, green, and blue would look fun on the shelf, and the different colors can also help kids learn while they play.","t":"A：玩具公司請我們為幼童設計一套新的積木，你覺得什麼會在店裡吸引家長？ B：一盒紅、黃、綠、藍的【五顏六色】積木放在架上看起來會很有趣，不同的顏色也能幫助孩子邊玩邊學習。"},{"w":"colorful","p":"adj.","d":"full of bright colors","c":"色彩繽紛的","s":"A: The night market downtown has become very popular with tourists from Japan and Korea, so what do visitors enjoy most when they walk around there? B: Most of them love the colorful food stalls with their bright lights and signs, and they take hundreds of photos before they even start eating.","t":"A：市中心的夜市在日本和韓國遊客之間變得非常受歡迎，遊客在那裡逛的時候最喜歡什麼？ B：他們大多喜歡那些燈光和招牌明亮、【色彩繽紛的】小吃攤，甚至在開始吃之前就拍了好幾百張照片。"},{"w":"colorless","p":"adj.","d":"having no color","c":"無色的","s":"A: Some customers worry that our new cleaning spray might leave marks on their light carpets and white sofas, so what should we tell them? B: Please explain that the liquid is completely colorless and has no dye in it, so it won't stain any fabric, even after many uses.","t":"A：有些客人擔心我們新的清潔噴霧可能會在他們的淺色地毯和白沙發上留下痕跡，我們該怎麼跟他們說？ B：請解釋這種液體完全【無色】，裡面也沒有染料，所以即使用了很多次也不會弄髒任何布料。"},{"w":"saturated","p":"adj.","d":"(of colors) very strong and full","c":"飽和的；濃烈的","s":"A: The photos for our travel brochure look a bit dull compared to the real beaches we visited, so can the designer improve them before we print? B: Yes, she can make the blues and greens more saturated so the sea and trees look rich and deep, but she shouldn't go too far or they'll look fake.","t":"A：我們旅遊手冊的照片跟我們實際去過的海灘比起來有點黯淡，設計師能在印刷前改善嗎？ B：可以，她可以讓藍色和綠色更【飽和】，讓海和樹看起來濃郁深沉，但不能調過頭，不然會看起來很假。"},{"w":"gradient","p":"n.","d":"a slow change from one color to another","c":"漸層","s":"A: The new app's start screen looks too flat and boring compared with our competitors' apps, so what could the design team try this week? B: They could use a smooth gradient that changes from deep purple at the top to light pink at the bottom, which would make the screen feel modern and lively.","t":"A：新應用程式的開始畫面和競爭對手的比起來太平淡無趣了，設計團隊這週可以試試什麼？ B：他們可以用一個從頂部深紫色到底部淺粉紅色的平順【漸層】，會讓畫面感覺現代又活潑。"},{"w":"iridescent","p":"adj.","d":"showing changing rainbow colors as the light moves","c":"隨光變色的；彩虹色的","s":"A: The cosmetics company wants its new perfume bottle to look special on the shelf next to dozens of other brands, so what material are they thinking about? B: They're testing an iridescent glass that shows different rainbow colors when customers turn it in the light, just like a soap bubble or a seashell.","t":"A：化妝品公司希望新的香水瓶在架上和幾十個其他品牌並列時看起來很特別，他們在考慮什麼材質？ B：他們在測試一種【隨光變幻彩虹色的】玻璃，當顧客在光線下轉動它時會呈現不同的顏色，就像肥皂泡或貝殼一樣。"},{"w":"neutral","p":"adj.","d":"(of colors) not strong, such as beige, gray, or cream","c":"中性色的","s":"A: We're furnishing twenty apartments for business travelers who usually stay for one or two months, so what color should we choose for the sofas and curtains? B: I think neutral colors like beige, cream, and gray are the safest choice, because they match almost any style and most guests feel comfortable with them.","t":"A：我們要為通常停留一兩個月的商務旅客佈置二十間公寓，沙發和窗簾該選什麼顏色？ B：我認為米色、奶油色和灰色等【中性】色是最安全的選擇，因為它們幾乎能搭配任何風格，大部分客人也覺得很舒服。"},{"w":"pigmented","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of strong color","c":"顯色的；色素飽滿的","s":"A: Our makeup customers often complain that cheap lipsticks need to be put on again and again during a long workday, so what should we say about the new product line? B: Tell them the new lipsticks are highly pigmented, so just one layer gives a rich color that lasts for eight hours without fading.","t":"A：我們的彩妝客人常抱怨便宜的口紅在漫長的工作日裡要一直補擦，關於新產品線我們該怎麼介紹？ B：告訴他們新口紅非常【顯色】，只要擦一層就能呈現濃郁的色彩，而且能持續八小時不褪色。"}]},{"unit":67,"theme":"Comedy 喜劇","cards":[{"w":"humor","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being funny; the ability to see what is funny","c":"幽默；幽默感","s":"A: Why did the hotel choose Daniel to lead the welcome talk for the new staff instead of the training manager this year? B: He explains the rules clearly, but he also uses a lot of gentle humor in his talks, so nervous new workers relax quickly and remember the important points much better.","t":"A：為什麼今年飯店選擇丹尼爾、而不是訓練經理，來主持新進員工的歡迎講話？ B：他把規定解釋得很清楚，但他的講話中也用了很多溫和的【幽默】，所以緊張的新員工很快就放鬆下來，也更能記住重要的重點。"},{"w":"joke","p":"n.","d":"a short funny story or remark told to make people laugh","c":"笑話；玩笑","s":"A: How did you start your speech at the sales conference in Kaohsiung when everyone looked so tired after lunch? B: I opened with a short joke about my first day as a salesperson, when I got lost in the client's building, and the whole room woke up and started paying attention.","t":"A：午餐後大家看起來都很累，你在高雄的業務會議上是怎麼開始演講的？ B：我用一個關於我當業務員第一天的簡短【笑話】開場，那天我在客戶的大樓裡迷路了，結果整個會場都醒了過來，開始專心聽講。"},{"w":"punchline","p":"n.","d":"the last, funniest line of a joke or story","c":"笑點；（笑話的）妙語結尾","s":"A: Why didn't anyone smile at the end of Kevin's story during the team dinner last Friday night? B: He was so nervous that he forgot the punchline and had to check his phone to remember it, so by the time he finally said it, everyone had already lost interest.","t":"A：上週五晚上的團隊聚餐，凱文講完故事時為什麼沒有人笑？ B：他太緊張了，忘了【笑點】，還得看手機才想起來，所以等他終於說出來時，大家早就沒興趣了。"},{"w":"wit","p":"n.","d":"the ability to say clever and funny things quickly","c":"機智；風趣","s":"A: What do the customers like most about the new host of the morning radio program that our company sponsors? B: They love her quick wit, because she answers callers' questions in clever and funny ways, and the station says the number of listeners has grown by twenty percent since she started.","t":"A：顧客最喜歡我們公司贊助的晨間廣播節目新主持人哪一點？ B：他們很喜歡她敏捷的【機智】，因為她總能用聰明又有趣的方式回答聽眾的問題，電台說自從她開始主持以來，聽眾人數增加了百分之二十。"},{"w":"satire","p":"n.","d":"humor that shows how foolish people, ideas or organizations are","c":"諷刺（作品）","s":"A: Why is the new online show about office life getting so much attention from business magazines this month? B: It is a clever satire of big companies that hold too many useless meetings, and many managers say they recognize their own bad habits, even though the show makes them feel a little embarrassed.","t":"A：為什麼這個關於職場生活的新網路節目這個月受到商業雜誌這麼多關注？ B：它是一部巧妙【諷刺】大公司開太多無用會議的作品，許多主管說他們從中看到了自己的壞習慣，雖然這個節目讓他們覺得有點難為情。"},{"w":"parody","p":"n.","d":"a funny copy of a famous song, film or style","c":"模仿作品；惡搞","s":"A: What did the marketing team show at the company's year-end party that made the general manager smile so much? B: They made a short video parody of a famous movie trailer, using our own products and staff as the actors, and it was so popular that we later posted it on our social media page.","t":"A：行銷團隊在公司尾牙上播放了什麼，讓總經理笑得那麼開心？ B：他們拍了一支知名電影預告片的【模仿】短片，用我們自己的產品和員工當演員，因為太受歡迎了，我們後來還把它放上公司的社群網頁。"},{"w":"skit","p":"n.","d":"a short funny performance, often by amateurs","c":"短劇；幽默小品","s":"A: How is the customer service department preparing for the training day for new employees next Monday morning? B: Two senior staff members will act out a short skit about a very angry customer and a calm assistant, so the new workers can see the right way to handle difficult situations.","t":"A：客服部門如何準備下週一早上的新進員工訓練日？ B：兩位資深員工會表演一齣關於一位非常生氣的客人和一位冷靜店員的【短劇】，讓新員工能看到處理困難狀況的正確方法。"},{"w":"slapstick","p":"n.","d":"comedy based on silly actions, such as people falling over","c":"打鬧喜劇；鬧劇","s":"A: Which kind of show do you think we should book for the family day at the factory next month, since many workers are bringing young children? B: Let's choose a slapstick performance, because kids love clowns who fall over, slip on banana skins and throw pies, and they don't need to understand difficult words.","t":"A：既然很多員工會帶小孩來，你覺得下個月工廠家庭日我們該訂哪一種表演？ B：我們選一場【打鬧喜劇】表演吧，因為小孩子很喜歡會跌倒、踩到香蕉皮滑倒和丟派的小丑，而且他們不需要聽懂困難的字。"},{"w":"stand-up","p":"n.","d":"comedy in which one person stands on stage and tells jokes","c":"單口喜劇；脫口秀","s":"A: Is it true that your colleague in the accounting department has a second job on the weekends, and what does he do? B: Yes, he performs stand-up at a small bar near Taipei Main Station every Saturday night, telling funny stories about numbers, tax forms and his strict boss to a crowd of young office workers.","t":"A：你那位會計部門的同事週末真的有第二份工作嗎？他做什麼？ B：是的，他每個星期六晚上在台北車站附近的一間小酒吧表演【單口喜劇】，對著一群年輕上班族講關於數字、稅表和他嚴格老闆的好笑故事。"},{"w":"comedian","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to make people laugh","c":"喜劇演員","s":"A: Who is going to host the charity dinner that our bank is organizing at the Grand Hotel next month? B: We hired a well-known comedian from a popular TV show, because we hope his funny stories will keep the guests in a good mood and encourage them to give more money to the children's hospital.","t":"A：我們銀行下個月在大飯店舉辦的慈善晚宴由誰主持？ B：我們請了一位知名電視節目的【喜劇演員】，因為我們希望他的趣事能讓賓客保持好心情，並鼓勵他們捐更多錢給兒童醫院。"},{"w":"comic","p":"adj.","d":"funny; connected with comedy","c":"滑稽的；喜劇的","s":"A: Why did the director of the training video ask the shy new receptionist to take a part in it? B: He thought her natural comic style would make the safety rules more interesting to watch, and in the end, her funny face when the fire alarm rang became everyone's favorite scene.","t":"A：為什麼訓練影片的導演請那位害羞的新接待員參與演出？ B：他認為她自然的【滑稽】風格會讓安全規定看起來更有趣，結果最後，她在火災警報響起時的好笑表情成了大家最喜歡的一幕。"},{"w":"funny","p":"adj.","d":"making you laugh or smile; also strange","c":"好笑的；有趣的；奇怪的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the guest speaker at the marketing seminar this afternoon, or was it as boring as last year's talk? B: It was much better, because she told a really funny story about losing her luggage in Tokyo before an important meeting, and then she explained what that experience taught her about planning.","t":"A：你喜歡今天下午行銷研討會的客座講者嗎？還是跟去年的演講一樣無聊？ B：好多了，因為她講了一個真的很【好笑】的故事，說她在一場重要會議前在東京弄丟了行李，然後她解釋了那次經驗教她的規劃之道。"},{"w":"hilarious","p":"adj.","d":"extremely funny","c":"極好笑的；爆笑的","s":"A: Why was everyone in the meeting room crying with laughter when I walked past the glass door this morning? B: The new translation software turned our product name into something hilarious in the Japanese version of the brochure, and we were all very lucky that we noticed it before it was printed.","t":"A：今天早上我經過玻璃門時，為什麼會議室裡的大家都笑到流眼淚？ B：新的翻譯軟體把我們的產品名稱在日文版手冊裡翻成了很【爆笑】的東西，幸好我們在印刷前就發現了。"},{"w":"amusing","p":"adj.","d":"funny and enjoyable","c":"有趣的；逗趣的","s":"A: What did you think of the short film that the training department showed at the beginning of the workshop on customer service? B: I found it quite amusing, because it showed a waiter making every possible mistake in one evening, and it was a light way to introduce a serious topic before lunch.","t":"A：你覺得訓練部門在客服工作坊一開始播放的短片如何？ B：我覺得相當【有趣】，因為它呈現了一位服務生在一個晚上犯下所有可能的錯誤，在午餐前用輕鬆的方式介紹一個嚴肅的主題。"},{"w":"witty","p":"adj.","d":"clever and funny in the way you speak or write","c":"機智風趣的；妙語如珠的","s":"A: Why do so many people follow the online account of that small coffee shop near our office building? B: The owner writes short, witty posts about daily life behind the counter, such as customers who order very strange drinks, and many readers come in to try the coffee after reading them.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多人追蹤我們辦公大樓附近那間小咖啡店的網路帳號？ B：老闆會寫一些簡短又【機智風趣】的貼文，描述櫃台後的日常生活，例如點了非常奇怪飲料的客人，很多讀者看完之後就會進店試喝咖啡。"},{"w":"sarcastic","p":"adj.","d":"saying the opposite of what you mean, to criticize or joke","c":"諷刺的；挖苦的","s":"A: Why did the sales manager ask Tom to come to her office after the team meeting this afternoon? B: When she announced the new weekend schedule, he said, 'Great, I love working on Sundays,' in a very sarcastic voice, and some customers waiting outside the room heard him and looked surprised.","t":"A：為什麼業務經理在今天下午的團隊會議後叫湯姆去她辦公室？ B：她宣布新的週末班表時，他用非常【挖苦】的語氣說：「太好了，我最愛星期天上班了。」幾位在會議室外等候的客人聽到了，看起來很驚訝。"},{"w":"ridiculous","p":"adj.","d":"very silly or unreasonable","c":"荒謬的；可笑的","s":"A: Are you going to accept the offer from the moving company to carry our office furniture to the new building? B: No, they asked for a ridiculous amount of money, almost three times what other companies charge, so I am going to call two more movers this afternoon and compare prices.","t":"A：你要接受搬家公司把我們的辦公家具搬到新大樓的報價嗎？ B：不要，他們開了一個【荒謬】的價格，幾乎是其他公司收費的三倍，所以我今天下午要再打給兩家搬家公司比價。"},{"w":"absurd","p":"adj.","d":"completely unreasonable or silly","c":"荒唐的；不合理的","s":"A: What do you think about the new rule that every employee must fill out a form before using the office printer? B: It seems completely absurd to me, because we print hundreds of pages every day, and filling out so many forms will waste more paper and time than it saves.","t":"A：你覺得每位員工使用辦公室印表機前都要填表格的新規定怎麼樣？ B：我覺得完全【荒唐】，因為我們每天要印好幾百頁，填這麼多表格浪費的紙和時間比省下來的還多。"},{"w":"playful","p":"adj.","d":"light-hearted and fun; not serious","c":"俏皮的；愛玩的；開玩笑的","s":"A: Why did the toy company decide to change the logo and colors on all its packages this year? B: Their old design looked too serious and formal, so they wanted a more playful style with bright colors and cartoon animals that would attract young children and their parents in busy shops.","t":"A：為什麼這家玩具公司今年決定更換所有包裝上的商標和顏色？ B：他們舊的設計看起來太嚴肅、太正式了，所以他們想要一種更【俏皮】的風格，用鮮豔的色彩和卡通動物，在熱鬧的商店裡吸引小孩和家長。"},{"w":"laugh","p":"v.","d":"to make sounds that show you think something is funny","c":"笑；大笑","s":"A: How did the new manager make such a good first impression on the staff at yesterday's welcome lunch? B: She told an honest story about her own mistakes in her first job, and it made everyone laugh, so people felt comfortable talking to her and asking questions for the rest of the afternoon.","t":"A：新經理是如何在昨天的歡迎午餐上給員工留下這麼好的第一印象？ B：她誠實地講了自己第一份工作犯錯的故事，讓大家都【笑】了，所以整個下午大家都很自在地跟她聊天、問問題。"},{"w":"giggle","p":"v.","d":"to laugh in a quiet, silly way","c":"咯咯地笑；傻笑","s":"A: Why did the photographer have so much trouble taking the group picture of the sales team for the company website? B: Two of the younger staff members kept starting to giggle every time he asked them to look serious, so it took nearly forty minutes to get one good photo.","t":"A：為什麼攝影師幫業務團隊拍公司網站用的團體照這麼困難？ B：每次他要大家表情嚴肅一點，兩位比較年輕的員工就忍不住【咯咯地笑】起來，所以花了將近四十分鐘才拍到一張好照片。"},{"w":"chuckle","p":"v.","d":"to laugh quietly","c":"輕聲笑；暗自發笑","s":"A: How did the chairman react when the intern accidentally showed a picture of her cat during the financial presentation? B: Luckily, he just began to chuckle softly and said that the cat looked smarter than some of our competitors, so the intern relaxed and finished her talk without any problems.","t":"A：實習生在財務簡報中不小心秀出她家貓咪的照片時，董事長有什麼反應？ B：幸好他只是輕聲地【笑了笑】，說那隻貓看起來比我們的一些競爭對手還聰明，於是實習生放鬆下來，順利完成了報告。"},{"w":"snicker","p":"v.","d":"to laugh quietly in an unkind way","c":"竊笑；暗笑","s":"A: Why did the trainer stop the workshop for a moment and speak to the group in such a serious voice? B: When a new employee gave a wrong answer, some people in the back row began to snicker, so the trainer reminded everyone that the session was a safe place to make mistakes and learn.","t":"A：為什麼講師暫停工作坊，用那麼嚴肅的語氣跟大家說話？ B：有位新員工答錯時，後排有些人開始【竊笑】，所以講師提醒大家，這堂課是一個可以安心犯錯和學習的地方。"},{"w":"tease","p":"v.","d":"to make jokes about someone, in a friendly or unkind way","c":"取笑；逗弄","s":"A: Why does Mark look so embarrassed whenever someone mentions the word 'coffee' in the office kitchen? B: Last month he spilled a whole cup on the CEO's shirt during a meeting, and his colleagues still tease him about it in a friendly way, although the CEO forgave him the same day.","t":"A：為什麼每次有人在辦公室茶水間提到「咖啡」這個字，馬克就看起來很難為情？ B：上個月他在會議中把一整杯咖啡潑到執行長的襯衫上，同事們到現在還會善意地拿這件事【取笑】他，雖然執行長當天就原諒他了。"},{"w":"entertain","p":"v.","d":"to keep people interested and amused; to welcome guests","c":"娛樂；招待","s":"A: What are we going to do with the visiting clients from Singapore after the factory tour ends on Thursday afternoon? B: We plan to entertain them at a traditional restaurant in Tamsui, where they can enjoy local food, watch the sunset by the river and listen to a live band before going back to their hotel.","t":"A：週四下午工廠參觀結束後，我們要怎麼安排來自新加坡的訪問客戶？ B：我們打算在淡水的一間傳統餐廳【招待】他們，讓他們享用在地美食、在河邊看夕陽、聽現場樂團演奏，然後再回飯店。"},{"w":"improvise","p":"v.","d":"to do or say something without preparing it first","c":"即興表演；臨場發揮","s":"A: What happened when the projector stopped working in the middle of your presentation to the investors yesterday? B: I had to improvise and draw the main charts on the whiteboard by hand, and the investors said they actually understood the numbers better because I explained each step slowly.","t":"A：昨天你向投資人做簡報時，投影機在中途壞掉，結果怎麼樣？ B：我只好【臨場發揮】，用手在白板上畫出主要圖表，投資人說因為我一步一步慢慢解釋，他們反而更了解那些數字。"},{"w":"timing","p":"n.","d":"the skill of doing or saying something at exactly the right moment","c":"時機掌握；節奏","s":"A: Why do you think Jessica's toast at the retirement party got such a warm reaction from the guests? B: Her timing was excellent, because she paused at exactly the right moments before each funny line, and she finished her speech just as the waiters were bringing out the cake.","t":"A：你覺得為什麼潔西卡在退休派對上的祝酒詞得到賓客這麼熱烈的反應？ B：她的【時機掌握】非常好，每句好笑的話之前都在恰到好處的時刻停頓，而且她剛好在服務生端出蛋糕時結束了致詞。"},{"w":"delivery","p":"n.","d":"the way someone speaks when giving a speech or performance","c":"表達方式；講述方式","s":"A: Your report on the new market had great information, so why did the director say it still needs more practice? B: She said my delivery was too fast and too quiet, so people at the back of the room couldn't follow me, and she wants me to speak more slowly and look at the listeners.","t":"A：你的新市場報告內容很好，為什麼主管說還需要多練習？ B：她說我的【表達方式】太快又太小聲，會議室後面的人跟不上，她希望我講慢一點並看著聽眾。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch or listen to a performance or talk","c":"觀眾；聽眾","s":"A: How many people came to the product launch at the exhibition center in Nangang last Saturday afternoon? B: We had an audience of about five hundred, including reporters, store owners and online influencers, which was much bigger than we expected, so we ran out of free samples in an hour.","t":"A：上週六下午在南港展覽館的產品發表會來了多少人？ B：我們大約有五百位【觀眾】，包括記者、店家老闆和網紅，比我們預期的多很多，所以免費試用品一個小時就發完了。"},{"w":"sketch","p":"n.","d":"a short funny scene that is part of a comedy show","c":"幽默短劇；小品","s":"A: What is the most popular part of the weekly comedy show that our company advertises on during prime time? B: Viewers love the short sketch at the end of each episode, in which two actors play a confused boss and a lazy assistant, and clips of it often get millions of views online.","t":"A：我們公司在黃金時段打廣告的那個每週喜劇節目，最受歡迎的部分是什麼？ B：觀眾很喜歡每集最後的【短劇】，兩位演員分別扮演搞不清楚狀況的老闆和懶惰的助理，片段常常在網路上獲得數百萬次觀看。"},{"w":"spoof","p":"n.","d":"a funny copy of something that makes fun of it","c":"惡搞；諷刺模仿","s":"A: Why did our competitor's new advertisement get so many comments on social media this week? B: It is a spoof of a famous sports commercial, but instead of a star athlete, it shows an office worker running to catch the last bus home, and many people say it reminds them of their own lives.","t":"A：為什麼競爭對手的新廣告這週在社群媒體上得到這麼多留言？ B：那是一支知名運動廣告的【惡搞】版，但影片中不是明星運動員，而是一位上班族為了趕末班公車回家而狂奔，許多人說這讓他們想起自己的生活。"},{"w":"banter","p":"n.","d":"friendly, joking conversation","c":"打趣；玩笑話","s":"A: Do the two hosts of the business podcast really get along, or is their friendly attitude just for the listeners? B: They have been close friends since university, so the easy banter between them is completely natural, and that relaxed style is the main reason the show has so many loyal fans.","t":"A：那個商業播客的兩位主持人真的處得很好嗎？還是他們友好的態度只是做給聽眾看的？ B：他們從大學時就是好朋友，所以兩人之間輕鬆的【打趣】完全是自然的，而這種輕鬆的風格正是節目有這麼多忠實粉絲的主要原因。"},{"w":"gag","p":"n.","d":"a joke or funny trick","c":"笑話；噱頭","s":"A: Why is there a rubber chicken sitting on the reception desk in the marketing department this week? B: It's a silly gag from the team's birthday party for the manager, and now everyone moves it to a new place every morning to see who will find it first.","t":"A：為什麼這週行銷部的接待櫃台上放著一隻橡膠雞？ B：那是團隊幫經理辦生日派對時留下的一個傻氣【噱頭】，現在大家每天早上都會把它移到新的地方，看誰會先找到它。"},{"w":"farce","p":"n.","d":"a comedy with silly situations; an event so badly organized that it is ridiculous","c":"鬧劇；荒唐的事","s":"A: How did the meeting with the new supplier go yesterday, since you were waiting for it all week? B: It was a complete farce, because they brought the wrong samples, their laptop wouldn't connect to our screen, and their sales manager got our company name wrong three times.","t":"A：你等了一整個星期，昨天跟新供應商的會議進行得怎麼樣？ B：那完全是一場【鬧劇】，他們帶錯了樣品，筆電連不上我們的螢幕，他們的業務經理還把我們公司名字說錯了三次。"}]},{"unit":68,"theme":"Communication 溝通","cards":[{"w":"message","p":"n.","d":"words you send or leave for someone when you cannot talk to them","c":"訊息；留言","s":"A: Did the client from Singapore call back while I was in the budget meeting with the finance team this afternoon? B: Yes, she called around three o'clock, and she left a message asking you to send the updated price list before Friday, because her manager needs it for a board meeting.","t":"A：我下午和財務團隊開預算會議時，新加坡的客戶有回電嗎？ B：有，她大約三點打來，留了一則【訊息】請你在星期五前寄出更新的價目表，因為她的經理開董事會時需要用到。"},{"w":"conversation","p":"n.","d":"a talk between two or more people","c":"對話；談話","s":"A: How did you find out that the marketing department is planning to move to the new building next spring? B: I had a long conversation with their team leader during the lunch break yesterday, and she told me that they need more space because they are hiring ten new designers.","t":"A：你怎麼知道行銷部門計畫明年春天搬到新大樓？ B：我昨天午休時和他們的組長有一段很長的【談話】，她告訴我因為他們要聘請十位新設計師，所以需要更多空間。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a talk in which people share ideas about a subject","c":"討論","s":"A: Has the management team decided whether employees can work from home two days a week starting next month? B: Not yet, because there was a long discussion about it in this morning's meeting, and some managers worry that teamwork will suffer if people are not in the office together.","t":"A：管理團隊決定員工從下個月起是否可以每週在家工作兩天了嗎？ B：還沒，因為今天早上的會議對此進行了很長的【討論】，有些經理擔心如果大家不一起在辦公室，團隊合作會受到影響。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"a serious talk between two groups to solve problems or understand each other","c":"對話；交流","s":"A: Why did the factory managers agree to meet the workers' representatives every month from now on? B: After the strike last year, both sides realized that open dialogue is the best way to solve problems early, before small complaints about pay or safety turn into serious conflicts.","t":"A：工廠經理為什麼同意從現在起每個月與工人代表開會？ B：去年罷工之後，雙方都明白開放的【對話】是及早解決問題的最好方法，免得關於薪資或安全的小抱怨演變成嚴重的衝突。"},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"the act of talking or working with someone","c":"互動；交流","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager want all new receptionists to attend a three-day training course before they start work? B: Because every interaction with a guest at the front desk affects the hotel's online reviews, so she wants the staff to be friendly, patient, and helpful from their very first day.","t":"A：飯店經理為什麼要所有新的櫃檯人員在上班前參加三天的訓練課程？ B：因為櫃檯和客人的每一次【互動】都會影響飯店的網路評價，所以她希望員工從第一天起就友善、有耐心且樂於助人。"},{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"a look on someone's face that shows a feeling","c":"表情；表達","s":"A: Did the new sales assistant seem happy when the manager announced the changes to the work schedule this morning? B: Not really, because I could see from the worried expression on her face that she was upset about working on Saturdays, but she didn't say anything during the meeting.","t":"A：今天早上經理宣布班表變動時，新來的銷售助理看起來開心嗎？ B：不太開心，我從她臉上擔憂的【表情】看得出來她對週六要上班感到不高興，但她在會議中什麼也沒說。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"comments about how well someone did something, used to make it better","c":"回饋；意見","s":"A: How do you know whether the new training program for customer service staff is actually working well? B: After every session, we ask the trainees to fill out a short online form and give honest feedback, and then we use their comments to improve the next course.","t":"A：你怎麼知道客服人員的新訓練課程是否真的有效？ B：每堂課結束後，我們會請學員填寫一份簡短的線上表單並給予誠實的【意見回饋】，然後我們用他們的意見來改善下一期課程。"},{"w":"response","p":"n.","d":"an answer or reaction to something","c":"回應；回覆","s":"A: Have we heard anything from the hotel in Tokyo about the meeting rooms we asked to book for the conference? B: Yes, I sent them an email on Monday, and I received a quick response the next morning saying that two large rooms are available on the dates we need.","t":"A：東京那家飯店有回覆我們要為研討會預訂會議室的事嗎？ B：有，我星期一寄了電子郵件給他們，隔天早上就收到快速的【回覆】，說我們需要的日期有兩間大會議室可以使用。"},{"w":"statement","p":"n.","d":"something said or written officially to give information","c":"聲明；陳述","s":"A: What did the airline say about the cancelled flights after the storm closed the airport last night? B: The company released an official statement this morning saying that all passengers will get a full refund or a free seat on another flight within the next three days.","t":"A：昨晚暴風雨導致機場關閉後，航空公司對取消的航班怎麼說？ B：公司今天早上發布了正式【聲明】，表示所有乘客都可以獲得全額退款，或在接下來三天內免費改搭其他航班。"},{"w":"tone","p":"n.","d":"the way a voice sounds that shows how someone feels","c":"語氣；口吻","s":"A: Why did the customer get so angry on the phone, even though you gave him the right information about his order? B: My manager said that my tone of voice sounded impatient and a little rude, so next time I will speak more slowly and try to sound calm and friendly.","t":"A：雖然你給了那位客人正確的訂單資訊，他為什麼在電話裡那麼生氣？ B：我的經理說我說話的【語氣】聽起來不耐煩又有點無禮，所以下次我會說慢一點，並試著讓自己聽起來冷靜又友善。"},{"w":"gesture","p":"n.","d":"a movement of the hands or head that shows meaning","c":"手勢；姿態","s":"A: How did you communicate with the factory workers in Vietnam when you visited last month, since you don't speak Vietnamese? B: Usually a translator helped us, but when she was busy, I just made a simple gesture with my hands, such as pointing at a machine or giving a thumbs-up, and the workers understood me quite well.","t":"A：你上個月去越南時不會說越南話，是怎麼和工廠工人溝通的？ B：通常有翻譯員幫忙，但她忙的時候，我就用手做個簡單的【手勢】，像是指著機器或比個讚，工人們都相當能理解我的意思。"},{"w":"signal","p":"n.","d":"a sound, action, or sign that gives information","c":"信號；暗號","s":"A: How will the tour guide let our group know when it is time to return to the bus at the crowded market? B: She told us that she will raise a yellow flag as a signal, and then everyone should walk back to the parking lot within ten minutes so we can leave on time.","t":"A：在擁擠的市場裡，導遊要怎麼讓我們這團知道該回巴士了？ B：她告訴我們她會舉起一面黃旗作為【信號】，然後大家應該在十分鐘內走回停車場，這樣我們才能準時出發。"},{"w":"clarify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to understand","c":"闡明；釐清","s":"A: The new travel policy is very confusing, so will we get money back for taxi rides to the airport or not? B: I'm not sure either, so I have asked the human resources manager to clarify the rules at Friday's staff meeting, because many employees have asked the same question this week.","t":"A：新的差旅政策很令人困惑，那我們搭計程車去機場的費用到底能不能報銷？ B：我也不確定，所以我已經請人資經理在星期五的員工會議上【釐清】規定，因為這週有很多員工問了同樣的問題。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear by giving details","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Why are so many customers calling the help desk about the new online banking app this week? B: The app changed a lot after the update, so our team will make a short video to explain how to log in and pay bills, and we will post it on our website tomorrow.","t":"A：為什麼這週有這麼多顧客打電話到服務台詢問新的網路銀行應用程式？ B：更新後應用程式改變很多，所以我們團隊會製作一支短片來【說明】如何登入和繳費，明天會放上我們的網站。"},{"w":"inform","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone facts, often in an official way","c":"通知；告知","s":"A: What should I do if I need to leave work early on Friday for my daughter's school concert? B: You should inform your supervisor at least two days before, and then ask a colleague to cover your phone calls in the afternoon so that customers are not left waiting.","t":"A：如果我星期五要提早下班去參加女兒學校的音樂會，我該怎麼做？ B：你應該至少提前兩天【告知】你的主管，然後請一位同事幫你接下午的電話，這樣顧客才不會一直等。"},{"w":"notify","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone officially about something","c":"通知；告知","s":"A: The shipment of printer paper will arrive two days later than planned, so what should we do about the customers who ordered it? B: Please notify each customer by email this afternoon, apologize for the delay, and offer them free delivery on their next order so that they stay happy with our service.","t":"A：印表機紙的貨會比預定晚兩天到，那些訂購的顧客我們該怎麼處理？ B：請在今天下午以電子郵件【通知】每位顧客，為延誤道歉，並提供他們下次訂購免運費，讓他們對我們的服務保持滿意。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something by giving good reasons","c":"說服；勸服","s":"A: How did you get the hotel to give us a discount on the rooms for the sales conference in March? B: I managed to persuade the hotel manager by promising that we would book fifty rooms for three nights and hold our dinner party in their restaurant as well.","t":"A：你是怎麼讓飯店給我們三月業務研討會的房間折扣的？ B：我承諾我們會訂五十間房住三晚，而且也會在他們的餐廳舉辦晚宴，就這樣成功【說服】了飯店經理。"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to talk with others in order to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"A: The supplier wants to raise the price of the plastic boxes by fifteen percent next year, so what is our plan? B: Our purchasing manager will fly to Shanghai next week to negotiate a better deal, and she hopes to keep the increase below five percent by ordering more boxes each month.","t":"A：供應商明年想把塑膠盒的價格調漲百分之十五，我們有什麼打算？ B：我們的採購經理下週會飛去上海【協商】出更好的條件，她希望藉由每月訂購更多盒子，把漲幅控制在百分之五以下。"},{"w":"translate","p":"v.","d":"to change words from one language into another","c":"翻譯","s":"A: We are sending the new product brochure to customers in Japan and Korea, so is it ready to go yet? B: Not yet, because we hired a language company to translate the brochure into both languages, and they need another week to finish and check all the technical words.","t":"A：我們要把新產品手冊寄給日本和韓國的客戶，準備好了嗎？ B：還沒，因為我們請了一家語言公司把手冊【翻譯】成這兩種語言，他們還需要一週來完成並檢查所有的專業用語。"},{"w":"verbal","p":"adj.","d":"spoken, not written","c":"口頭的；言語的","s":"A: Did the landlord give you a written contract when you agreed to rent the small office above the bakery? B: No, we only made a verbal agreement over the phone, so my lawyer told me to ask for a signed document before I pay the deposit next week.","t":"A：你同意租麵包店樓上那間小辦公室時，房東有給你書面合約嗎？ B：沒有，我們只在電話裡達成【口頭】協議，所以我的律師叫我在下週付押金之前要求一份簽好的文件。"},{"w":"nonverbal","p":"adj.","d":"without using words","c":"非語言的","s":"A: Why does the sales trainer spend so much time talking about how we stand and smile during meetings with clients? B: She believes that nonverbal communication, such as eye contact and body language, often tells customers more than our words, so it can help us win their trust.","t":"A：業務培訓師為什麼花這麼多時間講我們和客戶開會時怎麼站、怎麼微笑？ B：她認為【非語言的】溝通，像是眼神接觸和肢體語言，常常比我們說的話更能傳達訊息給顧客，所以能幫助我們贏得他們的信任。"},{"w":"written","p":"adj.","d":"put down on paper or in a document","c":"書面的","s":"A: Can I just tell my manager on the phone that I want to take three weeks of vacation in August? B: You can call her first, but the company also needs a written request through the online system at least one month before, or human resources cannot approve your leave.","t":"A：我可以直接打電話告訴經理我八月想休三週假嗎？ B：你可以先打給她，但公司也需要你至少提前一個月透過線上系統提出【書面】申請，否則人資部門無法核准你的假。"},{"w":"oral","p":"adj.","d":"spoken, not written","c":"口頭的；口說的","s":"A: What do candidates have to do in the second part of the job interview for the flight attendant position? B: After the written test, each person takes an oral exam in English and Japanese, in which they answer questions from passengers and explain safety rules out loud to the interviewers.","t":"A：空服員職位的面試第二部分，應徵者要做什麼？ B：筆試結束後，每個人都要參加英文和日文的【口說】測驗，要回答乘客的問題，並大聲向面試官說明安全規定。"},{"w":"effective","p":"adj.","d":"working well and giving the result you want","c":"有效的","s":"A: Our team keeps missing deadlines because people don't share updates, so what do you suggest we change? B: I think a short meeting every morning would be very effective, because everyone could explain what they are working on and ask for help before small problems become big ones.","t":"A：我們團隊因為大家不分享最新進度而一直趕不上期限，你建議我們改變什麼？ B：我覺得每天早上開個簡短的會議會非常【有效】，因為每個人都可以說明自己正在做什麼，並在小問題變成大問題之前尋求協助。"},{"w":"clear","p":"adj.","d":"easy to understand","c":"清楚的；明確的","s":"A: I read the new safety instructions for the warehouse twice, but I still don't understand what to do in a fire. B: I agree that they aren't very clear, so I will ask the safety officer to rewrite them with simple steps and pictures and post them next to every exit.","t":"A：倉庫新的安全須知我讀了兩遍，但還是不懂發生火災時該怎麼做。 B：我同意內容不太【清楚】，所以我會請安全專員用簡單的步驟和圖片重寫，並貼在每個出口旁邊。"},{"w":"concise","p":"adj.","d":"short and clear, using only the words that are needed","c":"簡潔的","s":"A: The director only has ten minutes for our presentation tomorrow, so how should we prepare our slides? B: We should keep each slide short and concise, with only three key points and one chart, so that she can quickly understand the sales results and make a decision before her next meeting.","t":"A：主管明天只有十分鐘聽我們簡報，我們該怎麼準備投影片？ B：我們應該讓每張投影片簡短又【簡潔】，只放三個重點和一張圖表，這樣她就能很快了解銷售成果，並在下一個會議前做出決定。"},{"w":"direct","p":"adj.","d":"saying what you think in an honest and clear way","c":"直率的；直接的","s":"A: What kind of manager is the new head of the finance department, and is she easy to work with? B: She is very direct, so if she doesn't like your report, she will tell you exactly what is wrong, but she also praises good work, and most of the team respects her honesty.","t":"A：財務部的新主管是什麼樣的經理？和她共事容易嗎？ B：她非常【直率】，如果她不喜歡你的報告，她會明確告訴你哪裡有問題，但她也會稱讚好的表現，所以大部分組員都很尊重她的坦誠。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"serious and official, following the correct rules","c":"正式的","s":"A: What should I wear to the awards dinner at the Grand Hotel next Saturday, since this is my first company event? B: The invitation says the dinner is formal, so men should wear a dark suit and tie, and women usually wear an evening dress, because the company president and important clients will attend.","t":"A：下週六在君悅飯店的頒獎晚宴我該穿什麼？這是我第一次參加公司活動。 B：邀請函上說晚宴是【正式的】，所以男士應該穿深色西裝打領帶，女士通常穿晚禮服，因為公司總裁和重要客戶都會出席。"},{"w":"informal","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and friendly, not official","c":"非正式的；輕鬆的","s":"A: Do I need to prepare slides for the meeting with the new interns on Thursday afternoon? B: No, it's just an informal chat over coffee in the break room, so you can simply introduce yourself, talk about your job, and answer any questions they have about working here.","t":"A：星期四下午和新實習生的會議我需要準備投影片嗎？ B：不用，那只是在休息室邊喝咖啡邊進行的【非正式】閒聊，你只要簡單自我介紹、談談你的工作，並回答他們對在這裡工作的任何問題就好。"},{"w":"actively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that takes part and does things with energy","c":"積極地；主動地","s":"A: Why did the manager choose Tom to lead the new customer service project instead of someone with more experience? B: During every meeting, Tom listens actively, asks useful questions, and writes down what customers say, so the manager believes he understands their problems better than anyone else on the team.","t":"A：經理為什麼選Tom帶領新的客服專案，而不是選更有經驗的人？ B：每次開會Tom都會【積極地】傾聽、提出有用的問題，並記下顧客說的話，所以經理相信他比團隊裡任何人都更了解顧客的問題。"},{"w":"clearly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easy to see, hear, or understand","c":"清楚地","s":"A: The conference room is very large, so how can we make sure everyone in the back row hears the speaker? B: We will set up two extra speakers and give the presenter a wireless microphone, so she can speak clearly without shouting, and the guests at the back won't miss anything important.","t":"A：會議廳很大，我們要怎麼確保最後一排的人都聽得到講者？ B：我們會多架兩個喇叭，並給講者一支無線麥克風，這樣她不用大喊也能【清楚地】說話，後排的來賓就不會錯過任何重要內容。"},{"w":"politely","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind and respectful way","c":"有禮貌地","s":"A: What did you say to the customer who wanted a refund for a jacket he had already worn for two months? B: I politely explained that our store only gives refunds within thirty days, but I offered him a discount coupon for his next purchase, and he seemed satisfied when he left.","t":"A：那位外套已經穿了兩個月卻要退款的顧客，你跟他說了什麼？ B：我【有禮貌地】解釋本店只在三十天內提供退款，但我給了他一張下次購物的折價券，他離開時看起來很滿意。"},{"w":"openly","p":"adv.","d":"honestly, without hiding anything","c":"公開地；坦率地","s":"A: Why do you think the new team leader is so popular with the staff after only three months in the job? B: She talks openly about the department's problems and goals at every meeting, and she encourages everyone to share their honest opinions without worrying about getting into trouble.","t":"A：你覺得新組長為什麼上任才三個月就這麼受員工歡迎？ B：她在每次會議上都【坦率地】談論部門的問題和目標，並鼓勵每個人分享真實的想法，不必擔心惹上麻煩。"}]},{"unit":69,"theme":"Company 公司","cards":[{"w":"innovator","p":"n.","d":"a person who introduces new ideas, methods or products","c":"創新者；革新者","s":"A: Why did the board choose Ms. Lin to lead the new research department instead of hiring someone from outside the company? B: She is a true innovator who designed our best-selling smart lamp, and the directors believe she can bring fresh ideas to every product we develop next year.","t":"A：董事會為什麼選林小姐來帶領新的研發部門，而不是從公司外部聘請人？ B：她是一位真正的【創新者】，設計了我們最暢銷的智慧檯燈，董事們相信她能為我們明年開發的每項產品帶來新點子。"},{"w":"disruptor","p":"n.","d":"a company or person that changes an industry with a completely new way of doing things","c":"顛覆者；破壞式創新者","s":"A: Why are the big taxi companies in the city so worried about the new ride-sharing app that launched last spring? B: The app has become a real disruptor in the transport market, because customers can book cheaper rides in seconds, and many drivers have already left their old employers to join it.","t":"A：為什麼市內的大型計程車公司這麼擔心去年春天推出的新共乘應用程式？ B：這個應用程式已經成為交通市場上真正的【顛覆者】，因為顧客可以在幾秒內預訂更便宜的車程，而且許多司機已經離開原本的雇主加入它。"},{"w":"entrepreneur","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts and runs their own business","c":"企業家；創業者","s":"A: How did your cousin manage to open three coffee shops in Taipei before she turned thirty? B: She is a hard-working entrepreneur who saved money for years, borrowed a small loan from the bank, and spent every weekend learning about marketing, rent and hiring staff before opening her first shop.","t":"A：你表姊是怎麼在三十歲之前就在台北開了三家咖啡店的？ B：她是一位勤奮的【創業者】，存了好幾年的錢，向銀行借了一筆小額貸款，並在開第一家店之前每個週末都在學習行銷、租金和聘僱員工的知識。"},{"w":"entrepreneurship","p":"n.","d":"the skills and activity of starting and running new businesses","c":"創業精神；創業","s":"A: Why is the university inviting so many business owners to give talks on campus this semester? B: The school wants to encourage entrepreneurship among its students, so local company founders will explain how they found investors, dealt with failure and turned simple ideas into profitable businesses.","t":"A：為什麼大學這學期邀請這麼多企業主到校園演講？ B：學校想要在學生之間鼓勵【創業精神】，所以當地的公司創辦人會說明他們如何找到投資者、面對失敗，以及把簡單的點子變成能獲利的事業。"},{"w":"start-up","p":"n.","d":"a new, small company, often in technology","c":"新創公司","s":"A: Why did Kevin leave his well-paid job at the bank after working there for almost ten years? B: He joined a small start-up that is developing an online payment app, and although the salary is lower, he gets shares in the company and the chance to learn something new every day.","t":"A：凱文在銀行工作了將近十年，為什麼要離開那份高薪工作？ B：他加入了一家正在開發線上支付應用程式的小型【新創公司】，雖然薪水比較低，但他能獲得公司股份，而且每天都有機會學到新東西。"},{"w":"founder","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts a company or organization","c":"創辦人","s":"A: Who is going to give the opening speech at the company's twentieth anniversary dinner next Friday evening? B: The founder of the company, Mr. Chen, will fly back from Singapore to tell the story of how he started the business in a tiny garage with only two employees.","t":"A：下週五晚上公司二十週年晚宴上，誰要致開幕詞？ B：公司的【創辦人】陳先生會從新加坡飛回來，講述他如何只帶著兩名員工在一間小車庫裡創業的故事。"},{"w":"manpower","p":"n.","d":"the number of workers available to do a job","c":"人力","s":"A: Can the factory finish the large order for the hotel chain before the end of next month? B: I'm afraid we don't have enough manpower right now, because several workers are on holiday, so we will need to hire temporary staff or ask the customer for an extra two weeks.","t":"A：工廠能在下個月底之前完成連鎖飯店的大訂單嗎？ B：恐怕我們現在沒有足夠的【人力】，因為有好幾位員工在休假，所以我們需要聘請臨時員工，或者請客戶多給兩週時間。"},{"w":"mentor","p":"n.","d":"an experienced person who advises and helps someone with less experience","c":"導師；指導者","s":"A: How are the new trainees in the sales department settling in during their first month with us? B: Each of them has a mentor from the senior team who meets them every week, answers their questions about clients and gives them helpful advice on how to reach their monthly targets.","t":"A：業務部的新進受訓人員在第一個月適應得如何？ B：他們每個人都有一位來自資深團隊的【導師】，每週和他們見面，回答他們關於客戶的問題，並針對如何達成每月目標給予實用的建議。"},{"w":"net worth","p":"n.phr.","d":"the total value of what a person or company owns, minus what they owe","c":"淨資產；身價","s":"A: Why was the owner of that small electronics firm suddenly in all the business newspapers this week? B: After his company went public on Monday, his net worth rose to over two billion dollars, which made him one of the richest people in the country almost overnight.","t":"A：那家小型電子公司的老闆這週為什麼突然登上所有的商業報紙？ B：他的公司週一上市之後，他的【淨資產】增加到超過二十億美元，幾乎一夜之間讓他成為全國最富有的人之一。"},{"w":"perk","p":"n.","d":"an extra benefit you get from your job in addition to your pay","c":"額外福利","s":"A: Why do so many young designers want to work for that software company even though its salaries are not the highest? B: One popular perk is free lunch every day in the staff cafeteria, and employees can also work from home on Fridays and use the gym downstairs for free.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多年輕設計師想在那家軟體公司工作，即使它的薪水不是最高的？ B：一項很受歡迎的【額外福利】是每天在員工餐廳免費供應午餐，員工週五也可以在家工作，還能免費使用樓下的健身房。"},{"w":"stake","p":"n.","d":"a share in a business or its profits","c":"股份；投資額","s":"A: Why are the directors of the Japanese car maker visiting our factory in Kaohsiung next Thursday morning? B: They are planning to buy a twenty percent stake in our company, so they want to see the production lines and meet the managers before they sign the final agreement.","t":"A：那家日本汽車製造商的董事們為什麼下週四早上要參觀我們在高雄的工廠？ B：他們打算買下我們公司百分之二十的【股份】，所以想在簽署最終協議前看看生產線並和經理們見面。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to work hard or do something","c":"激勵；促使","s":"A: Sales have been slow for three months, so what is the new manager going to do about the team's low energy? B: She plans to motivate everyone by offering a weekend trip to the top seller each month, and she will also share positive comments from customers at every Monday meeting.","t":"A：銷售已經疲軟三個月了，新經理打算怎麼處理團隊士氣低落的問題？ B：她打算每月提供週末旅遊給業績最好的人來【激勵】大家，她也會在每週一的會議上分享顧客的正面評價。"},{"w":"savvy","p":"adj.","d":"having practical knowledge and good judgment about something","c":"精明的；在行的","s":"A: Why did the marketing director hire such a young assistant to manage the company's online advertising? B: He is very savvy about social media, so he knows which videos customers will share, and last month his short ads brought in twice as many orders as our television commercials.","t":"A：行銷總監為什麼聘請這麼年輕的助理來管理公司的線上廣告？ B：他對社群媒體非常【在行】，所以知道顧客會分享哪些影片，上個月他的短廣告帶來的訂單是我們電視廣告的兩倍。"},{"w":"contravene","p":"v.","d":"to break a law or rule","c":"違反；觸犯","s":"A: Why did the city government order the new restaurant on Park Road to close for a whole week? B: Inspectors found that the kitchen and the fire exits contravene several local safety rules, so the owners must fix every problem and pass another check before they can serve customers again.","t":"A：市政府為什麼下令公園路上那家新餐廳停業整整一週？ B：檢查人員發現廚房和逃生出口【違反】了好幾條地方安全規定，所以業主必須修正每個問題並通過另一次檢查，才能再次營業接待顧客。"},{"w":"scale something up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make something larger in size or amount","c":"擴大（某事物的）規模","s":"A: Our new plant-based snacks sold out in all twenty test stores, so when will we start selling them nationwide? B: Before we scale something up, we need a bigger factory and more suppliers, so the plan is to increase production step by step and reach every supermarket by next summer.","t":"A：我們新的植物性零食在二十家試賣店都賣光了，什麼時候開始全國販售？ B：在我們【擴大規模】之前，需要更大的工廠和更多供應商，所以計畫是逐步增加產量，在明年夏天前進入每一家超市。"},{"w":"wilfully","p":"adv.","d":"deliberately, while knowing that it is wrong","c":"故意地；蓄意地","s":"A: Why did the company fire the warehouse supervisor so suddenly last Friday afternoon? B: An investigation showed that he had wilfully ignored the safety rules for months to save time, even though two workers were injured and his manager had warned him several times in writing.","t":"A：公司上週五下午為什麼這麼突然開除倉庫主管？ B：調查顯示他好幾個月來為了節省時間而【故意】忽視安全規定，即使有兩名員工受傷，而且他的經理也曾多次以書面警告他。"},{"w":"rapidly","p":"adv.","d":"very quickly","c":"迅速地","s":"A: Why does the online shop need to rent a second warehouse in Taoyuan so soon after moving into the first one? B: Orders are growing rapidly because of our new mobile app, and we are now shipping three times more boxes every day than we did at the beginning of the year.","t":"A：那家網路商店才剛搬進第一間倉庫不久，為什麼就需要在桃園租第二間倉庫？ B：因為我們新的手機應用程式，訂單正【迅速地】成長，我們現在每天出貨的箱數是年初的三倍。"},{"w":"corporation","p":"n.","d":"a large company or group of companies","c":"大公司；企業","s":"A: Is it true that you are leaving the small design studio to work somewhere much bigger next year? B: Yes, I accepted an offer from a large corporation with offices in twelve countries, so I will have more chances to travel, although I will probably miss the friendly atmosphere at the studio.","t":"A：聽說你明年要離開那家小設計工作室，到規模大很多的地方工作，是真的嗎？ B：是的，我接受了一家在十二個國家設有辦公室的大【企業】的工作邀約，所以會有更多出差機會，不過我大概會想念工作室友善的氣氛。"},{"w":"multinational","p":"adj.","d":"operating in several countries","c":"跨國的","s":"A: Why does the company need so many staff who can speak English, Japanese and Vietnamese? B: We have become a multinational company with factories in three countries, so our managers must communicate with suppliers, customers and colleagues abroad every day, often during long video meetings.","t":"A：公司為什麼需要那麼多會說英文、日文和越南文的員工？ B：我們已經成為一家在三個國家設有工廠的【跨國】公司，所以經理們每天都必須和國外的供應商、客戶及同事溝通，常常要開很長的視訊會議。"},{"w":"subsidiary","p":"n.","d":"a company that is owned and controlled by a larger company","c":"子公司","s":"A: Who will be in charge of the new office in Ho Chi Minh City when it opens in March? B: It will be run as a subsidiary of our Taipei head office, so the local manager will make daily decisions, but the budget and major plans still need approval from our board.","t":"A：三月胡志明市的新辦公室開幕後，由誰負責？ B：它會以台北總公司的【子公司】形式營運，所以當地經理會做日常決策，但預算和重大計畫仍需經過我們董事會的核准。"},{"w":"consultancy","p":"n.","d":"a company that gives expert advice to other businesses","c":"顧問公司","s":"A: How did the hospital find ways to reduce patients' waiting times so quickly this year? B: They hired a consultancy that specializes in healthcare, and its experts spent two months studying the reception area before suggesting a new booking system that cut the average wait by half.","t":"A：醫院今年是怎麼這麼快就找到縮短病患候診時間的方法？ B：他們聘請了一家專門從事醫療保健的【顧問公司】，該公司的專家花了兩個月研究掛號區，然後建議了一套新的預約系統，把平均等候時間減少一半。"},{"w":"venture","p":"n.","d":"a new business activity that involves risk","c":"（有風險的）新事業；投資事業","s":"A: Why did the two hotel owners decide to work together after competing with each other for years? B: They started a joint venture to build a luxury resort by the lake, because neither of them had enough money to pay for such a large and risky project alone.","t":"A：那兩位飯店老闆競爭了好幾年，為什麼決定合作？ B：他們展開了一項合資【事業】，要在湖邊興建豪華度假村，因為他們兩人都沒有足夠的錢獨自負擔這麼大型又有風險的計畫。"},{"w":"global","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the whole world","c":"全球的","s":"A: Why have the prices of our laptops gone up so much since the beginning of the summer? B: There is a global shortage of computer chips, so factories in many countries are waiting for parts, and we have had to pay our suppliers much more to keep our production running.","t":"A：從夏天一開始，我們筆電的價格為什麼漲這麼多？ B：電腦晶片出現【全球性的】短缺，所以許多國家的工廠都在等零件，我們必須付給供應商更多錢才能維持生產。"},{"w":"takeover","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting control of a company by buying most of its shares","c":"收購；接管","s":"A: Why are so many employees at the bookstore chain worried about their jobs this month? B: A large online retailer has announced a takeover of the company, and staff are afraid that the new owners will close some stores and move most of the business online.","t":"A：這個月連鎖書店的許多員工為什麼都在擔心自己的工作？ B：一家大型網路零售商宣布了對該公司的【收購】，員工擔心新老闆會關閉一些門市，並把大部分業務移到線上。"},{"w":"convert","p":"v.","d":"to change something into a different form or use","c":"轉換；改建","s":"A: What is the company going to do with the empty storage rooms on the fifth floor of our building? B: The managers have decided to convert them into a quiet lounge and two small meeting rooms, because staff often complain that there is nowhere to relax or make private phone calls.","t":"A：公司打算怎麼處理我們大樓五樓那些空著的儲藏室？ B：經理們決定把它們【改建】成一間安靜的休息室和兩間小會議室，因為員工常抱怨沒有地方可以放鬆或打私人電話。"},{"w":"admittedly","p":"adv.","d":"used when you agree that something is true, although it does not help your argument","c":"誠然；不可否認地","s":"A: Do you think we should still choose the supplier from Tainan, even though its prices are higher? B: admittedly, their products cost about ten percent more than the others, but they always deliver on time and their quality is excellent, so I believe they are worth the extra money.","t":"A：即使台南那家供應商價格比較高，你認為我們還是應該選它嗎？ B：【不可否認地】，他們的產品比其他家貴大約百分之十，但他們總是準時交貨，品質也非常好，所以我相信多花的錢是值得的。"},{"w":"commercially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to business and making money","c":"商業上；在商業方面","s":"A: Why did the company stop making the electric bicycle that won a design award two years ago? B: It was very popular with critics but was never commercially successful, because it cost too much to produce, and most customers chose cheaper models from other brands instead.","t":"A：公司為什麼停產兩年前得過設計獎的那款電動腳踏車？ B：它很受評論家歡迎，但在【商業上】從未成功，因為生產成本太高，大部分顧客反而選擇其他品牌較便宜的車款。"},{"w":"welfare","p":"n.","d":"the health, happiness and safety of a person or group","c":"福利；福祉","s":"A: Why has the factory started offering free health checks and a counseling service for its workers? B: The new owners care a lot about employee welfare, and they believe that staff who feel healthy and supported will stay longer, make fewer mistakes and work more efficiently.","t":"A：工廠為什麼開始為員工提供免費健康檢查和諮商服務？ B：新老闆非常重視員工【福利】，他們相信感到健康並受到支持的員工會待得更久、犯更少錯，工作也更有效率。"},{"w":"donate","p":"v.","d":"to give money or goods to help a person or organization","c":"捐贈；捐款","s":"A: What is the company planning to do for the local community during the holiday season this year? B: We will donate one percent of our December sales to a children's hospital, and many employees have also volunteered to collect toys and books for young patients.","t":"A：公司今年假期期間打算為當地社區做什麼？ B：我們會把十二月銷售額的百分之一【捐贈】給一家兒童醫院，許多員工也自願為年幼的病童收集玩具和書籍。"},{"w":"forbidden","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed","c":"被禁止的","s":"A: Can visitors take photos of the new production line when they tour the factory next week? B: No, photography is forbidden inside the building because our machines use secret technology, so guests must leave their phones at the reception desk before the tour begins.","t":"A：下週訪客參觀工廠時可以拍攝新的生產線嗎？ B：不行，大樓內【禁止】拍照，因為我們的機器使用機密技術，所以來賓必須在參觀開始前把手機寄放在接待櫃台。"},{"w":"bonus","p":"n.","d":"extra money added to your pay, usually as a reward","c":"獎金；紅利","s":"A: Why does everyone in the sales department look so cheerful this morning? B: The manager announced that every member of the team will receive a year-end bonus equal to two months' salary, because we beat our sales target by thirty percent this year.","t":"A：業務部的每個人今天早上為什麼看起來這麼開心？ B：經理宣布團隊每位成員都會獲得相當於兩個月薪水的年終【獎金】，因為我們今年超越銷售目標百分之三十。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a plan for achieving a goal over a long period","c":"策略；戰略","s":"A: Our sales in Europe dropped again last quarter, so what will the directors discuss at tomorrow's meeting? B: They will present a new marketing strategy that focuses on online advertising and partnerships with local shops, and they hope it will win back young customers within a year.","t":"A：我們上一季在歐洲的銷售又下滑了，董事們明天的會議會討論什麼？ B：他們會提出一項新的行銷【策略】，重點放在線上廣告和與當地商店的合作，希望能在一年內贏回年輕顧客。"}]},{"unit":70,"theme":"Competition 競爭；比賽","cards":[{"w":"contest","p":"n.","d":"a competition in which people try to win something","c":"比賽；競賽","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department staying late and taking so many photos of the new products this week? B: The company is holding a photo contest for staff, and the person who takes the best picture for our next catalog will receive two free plane tickets to Tokyo.","t":"A：為什麼行銷部門的每個人這週都留到很晚，還拍了那麼多新產品的照片？ B：公司正在為員工舉辦攝影【比賽】，替我們下一期型錄拍出最佳照片的人將獲得兩張飛往東京的免費機票。"},{"w":"tournament","p":"n.","d":"a series of games between many players or teams to find one winner","c":"錦標賽；聯賽","s":"A: Why did the sales team leave the office so early on Friday afternoon, and who is answering their phones today? B: They are playing in the annual company golf tournament at the country club, so the receptionist is taking messages until they come back on Monday morning.","t":"A：業務團隊為什麼星期五下午那麼早就離開辦公室？今天誰幫他們接電話？ B：他們去鄉村俱樂部參加公司年度高爾夫【錦標賽】了，所以在他們星期一早上回來之前，由櫃檯人員幫忙留言。"},{"w":"race","p":"n.","d":"a competition to see who is the fastest","c":"賽跑；競速比賽","s":"A: Why are the streets around the city hall closed this Sunday, and how will our delivery drivers reach the shops downtown? B: A charity race is taking place there in the morning, with thousands of runners, so the drivers should use the highway and wait until the roads open again after noon.","t":"A：為什麼市政府附近的街道這個星期天要封閉？我們的送貨司機要怎麼到市中心的商店？ B：那天早上那裡有一場慈善【賽跑】，有數千名跑者參加，所以司機們應該走高速公路，等到中午過後道路重新開放再進去。"},{"w":"match","p":"n.","d":"a game in which two people or teams play against each other","c":"比賽；競賽","s":"A: Do you want to join us at the sports bar after work tonight, or do you have to finish the budget report first? B: I would love to come, because the national football match starts at eight, but I need to send this report to my manager before I leave the office.","t":"A：今晚下班後你要和我們一起去運動酒吧嗎？還是你得先完成預算報告？ B：我很想去，因為國家隊的足球【比賽】八點開始，但我離開辦公室前必須先把這份報告寄給經理。"},{"w":"rivalry","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which two people or groups compete with each other for a long time","c":"競爭；敵對","s":"A: Why do the two coffee chains on Main Street keep lowering their prices and giving away free cakes every month? B: There has been a strong rivalry between them for years, and each company wants to attract more office workers in the area, so customers enjoy cheaper drinks.","t":"A：為什麼大街上的兩家連鎖咖啡店每個月都一直降價又送免費蛋糕？ B：它們之間多年來一直存在激烈的【競爭】，兩家公司都想吸引這一帶更多上班族，所以顧客就享受到比較便宜的飲料。"},{"w":"opponent","p":"n.","d":"a person or team you play or compete against","c":"對手；敵手","s":"A: How did your presentation go at the debate competition for young managers in Singapore last weekend? B: I was nervous at first because my opponent had more experience and spoke very confidently, but the judges liked my clear examples, so I made it to the final round.","t":"A：上週末你在新加坡年輕經理人辯論賽的表現怎麼樣？ B：一開始我很緊張，因為我的【對手】經驗比較豐富，說話也非常有自信，但評審喜歡我清楚的例子，所以我晉級到最後一輪了。"},{"w":"challenger","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that tries to win against the leader or champion","c":"挑戰者","s":"A: Should we still worry about that small online shop that started selling office furniture last year? B: Yes, because it has become a serious challenger to our business, offering lower prices and faster delivery, and several of our regular customers have already placed orders with them.","t":"A：我們還需要擔心去年開始販售辦公家具的那家小型網路商店嗎？ B：需要，因為它已經成為我們生意的強勁【挑戰者】，價格更低、送貨更快，我們有幾個老客戶已經向他們下單了。"},{"w":"competitor","p":"n.","d":"a company or person trying to be more successful than others","c":"競爭對手；參賽者","s":"A: Why did the manager call an emergency meeting this morning instead of having the usual coffee break with the team? B: Our biggest competitor has just released a cheaper smartphone with a better camera, so we need to discuss how to protect our sales before the holiday season begins.","t":"A：為什麼經理今天早上召開緊急會議，而不是像平常一樣和團隊喝咖啡休息？ B：我們最大的【競爭對手】剛推出一款更便宜、相機更好的智慧型手機，所以我們需要在假期旺季開始前討論如何保住我們的銷售量。"},{"w":"participant","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in an activity or event","c":"參加者；參與者","s":"A: How many people have signed up for the leadership workshop that the training department is organizing next month? B: So far we have forty, and each participant will receive a workbook, lunch on both days, and a certificate at the end, so we still need to order more materials.","t":"A：訓練部門下個月舉辦的領導力工作坊目前有多少人報名了？ B：目前有四十人，每位【參加者】都會拿到一本練習手冊、兩天的午餐，並在結束時獲得一張證書，所以我們還需要訂購更多資料。"},{"w":"victory","p":"n.","d":"the success of winning a game, fight or competition","c":"勝利","s":"A: Why is the whole IT department wearing the same blue shirts and eating pizza in the meeting room today? B: They are celebrating their victory in the city's software design competition, where their team beat twenty other companies and won a prize of ten thousand dollars.","t":"A：為什麼整個資訊部門今天都穿著一樣的藍色上衣，還在會議室吃披薩？ B：他們在慶祝在全市軟體設計比賽中獲得【勝利】，他們的團隊打敗了其他二十家公司，贏得了一萬美元的獎金。"},{"w":"defeat","p":"n.","d":"the fact of losing a game, fight or competition","c":"失敗；挫敗","s":"A: Is the sales director still upset about losing the hospital contract to that company from Osaka last month? B: She was disappointed at first, but she says the defeat taught us an important lesson about our prices, so now we are preparing a much stronger offer for the next project.","t":"A：業務總監還在為上個月輸給那家大阪公司、失去醫院合約的事情難過嗎？ B：她一開始很失望，但她說這次【失敗】讓我們學到了關於價格的重要一課，所以我們現在正在為下一個案子準備更有競爭力的提案。"},{"w":"prize","p":"n.","d":"something valuable given to the winner","c":"獎品；獎項","s":"A: What do the staff members get if they come up with the best idea for saving energy in the factory this year? B: The winner will receive a prize of a new laptop and an extra day off, and the manager will also share the idea in the company newsletter.","t":"A：如果員工今年想出工廠最佳的節能點子，可以得到什麼？ B：獲勝者將得到一台新筆電作為【獎品】，外加一天額外休假，經理也會在公司電子報中分享這個點子。"},{"w":"trophy","p":"n.","d":"a cup or other object given to the winner of a competition","c":"獎盃","s":"A: What is that large gold cup on the shelf next to the reception desk, and when did the company get it? B: That is the trophy we received last year for the best customer service in the region, and the CEO likes visitors to see it as soon as they walk in.","t":"A：櫃檯旁邊架子上那個大金杯是什麼？公司是什麼時候得到的？ B：那是我們去年因地區最佳客戶服務而獲得的【獎盃】，執行長喜歡讓訪客一走進來就看到它。"},{"w":"medal","p":"n.","d":"a round flat piece of metal given as a prize","c":"獎牌","s":"A: Why is your neighbor's daughter on the front page of the local newspaper this morning? B: She won a gold medal in swimming at the national games last weekend, and now a sports company has asked her to appear in its new advertisement for summer swimwear.","t":"A：為什麼你鄰居的女兒今天早上登上了地方報紙的頭版？ B：她上週末在全國運動會的游泳項目中贏得了一面金色【獎牌】，現在有一家運動用品公司請她拍攝新的夏季泳裝廣告。"},{"w":"rank","p":"v.","d":"to give or have a position in a list based on quality or success","c":"排名；位居","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager look so pleased while she reads the travel magazine at the front desk? B: The magazine has decided to rank our hotel third among all the business hotels in the city, so she expects many more bookings from companies sending staff here next year.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理在櫃檯看旅遊雜誌時看起來那麼高興？ B：那本雜誌把我們飯店【排名】為全市所有商務飯店中的第三名，所以她預期明年會有更多派員工來這裡的公司向我們訂房。"},{"w":"score","p":"n.","d":"the number of points a person or team gets","c":"分數；得分","s":"A: Did you pass the English test that the company requires before you can move to the overseas office? B: Yes, I got a score of 850, which is much higher than the minimum, so the human resources department says I can start working in London next spring.","t":"A：你通過公司規定調到海外辦公室之前必須考的英文測驗了嗎？ B：通過了，我拿到850的【分數】，比最低標準高出許多，所以人資部門說我明年春天就可以開始在倫敦工作。"},{"w":"compete","p":"v.","d":"to try to be more successful than others","c":"競爭；參賽","s":"A: Why is the small bakery on our street offering free coffee with every sandwich this month? B: A large supermarket opened nearby in October, and the owner says it is hard to compete with its low prices, so he hopes the free drinks will keep his regular customers coming back.","t":"A：為什麼我們街上那家小麵包店這個月每份三明治都送免費咖啡？ B：十月時附近開了一家大型超市，老闆說很難和它的低價【競爭】，所以他希望免費飲料能讓老顧客繼續回來光顧。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"v.","d":"to invite someone to compete or fight against you","c":"向…挑戰","s":"A: Why are the engineers practicing table tennis in the break room every lunchtime this week? B: The design team decided to challenge them to a friendly match on Friday, and the losing team has to buy coffee for the whole floor, so everyone is taking it very seriously.","t":"A：為什麼工程師們這週每天午休都在休息室練習桌球？ B：設計團隊決定【挑戰】他們，星期五來一場友誼賽，輸的隊伍要請整層樓的人喝咖啡，所以大家都非常認真。"},{"w":"strive","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to achieve something","c":"努力；奮鬥","s":"A: What makes your restaurant different from the many other Italian places in this busy shopping area? B: Our staff always strive to give every guest friendly service and fresh food made with local ingredients, and that is why so many office workers come back for lunch every week.","t":"A：你們的餐廳和這個熱鬧購物區裡其他許多義大利餐廳有什麼不同？ B：我們的員工總是【努力】為每位客人提供親切的服務，以及用在地食材製作的新鮮料理，這就是為什麼有那麼多上班族每週都回來吃午餐。"},{"w":"win","p":"v.","d":"to be the best or first in a competition","c":"贏；獲勝","s":"A: Do you think our team has a real chance in the national sales competition next month in Taipei? B: I think we can win if we prepare carefully, because our numbers this year are better than last year, and the judges usually care most about customer feedback and teamwork.","t":"A：你覺得我們團隊在下個月於台北舉行的全國業務競賽中真的有機會嗎？ B：我認為只要我們仔細準備就能【贏】，因為我們今年的業績比去年好，而且評審通常最重視顧客回饋和團隊合作。"},{"w":"lose","p":"v.","d":"to not win; to stop having something you had","c":"輸；失去","s":"A: Why does the manager want us to answer every customer email within two hours from now on? B: She is worried that we will lose our biggest clients to the new company across the street, because they reply very quickly and offer free delivery on all orders.","t":"A：為什麼經理要我們從現在起在兩小時內回覆每封顧客電子郵件？ B：她擔心我們會【失去】最大的客戶，被對街那家新公司搶走，因為他們回信很快，所有訂單還免運費。"},{"w":"dominate","p":"v.","d":"to be the most powerful or important in a place or market","c":"主導；稱霸","s":"A: Why is our company so interested in buying that small tech firm in Seoul for such a high price? B: The board believes that with its new battery technology, we could dominate the electric scooter market in Asia within five years and leave our competitors far behind.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司那麼想用這麼高的價格收購首爾那家小型科技公司？ B：董事會認為有了它的新電池技術，我們可以在五年內【稱霸】亞洲電動機車市場，把競爭對手遠遠拋在後面。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"trying hard to be better than others; (of prices) low enough to attract buyers","c":"競爭激烈的；有競爭力的","s":"A: Why did the hotel decide to lower its room rates for business travelers this autumn? B: The market here has become very competitive since three new hotels opened near the convention center, so we need lower prices and a better breakfast to keep our corporate guests.","t":"A：為什麼飯店決定今年秋天降低商務旅客的房價？ B：自從會展中心附近開了三家新飯店以後，這裡的市場變得非常【競爭激烈】，所以我們需要更低的價格和更好的早餐來留住企業客戶。"},{"w":"intense","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or extreme","c":"強烈的；激烈的","s":"A: How was your first month as a salesperson at the car dealership near the airport? B: It was harder than I expected, because the pressure to reach our monthly targets is intense, and everyone works long hours, but I have learned a lot from my experienced colleagues.","t":"A：你在機場附近汽車經銷商當業務員的第一個月怎麼樣？ B：比我預期的辛苦，因為達成每月目標的壓力非常【強烈】，大家都工作很長時間，不過我從經驗豐富的同事身上學到很多。"},{"w":"fierce","p":"adj.","d":"very strong and determined, sometimes in an angry way","c":"激烈的；猛烈的","s":"A: Why did the online bookstore shut down its office in Hong Kong after only two years? B: There was fierce competition from bigger shopping websites that sold the same books for less money, and the company could not make enough profit to pay the high rent there.","t":"A：為什麼那家網路書店只營運兩年就關閉了香港的辦公室？ B：較大的購物網站用更低的價格賣同樣的書，帶來【激烈的】競爭，公司賺不到足夠的利潤來支付那裡高昂的租金。"},{"w":"close","p":"adj.","d":"(of a competition) won or lost by only a small amount","c":"勢均力敵的；差距很小的","s":"A: Who won the vote for the new company logo at the staff meeting yesterday afternoon? B: It was very close, because the blue design got forty-one votes and the green one got thirty-nine, so the director asked the designers to combine the best parts of both.","t":"A：昨天下午員工會議上新公司標誌的投票是誰贏了？ B：票數非常【接近】，藍色設計得到四十一票，綠色設計得到三十九票，所以主管請設計師結合兩者最好的部分。"},{"w":"fair","p":"adj.","d":"treating everyone in the same way and following the rules","c":"公平的","s":"A: Why did the manager ask someone from another department to choose the winner of our sales contest? B: She wanted the results to be completely fair, because some people complained last year that she gave the prize to her own team members, so now an outside judge decides.","t":"A：為什麼經理請其他部門的人來選出我們業務競賽的贏家？ B：她希望結果完全【公平】，因為去年有些人抱怨她把獎項給了自己組裡的人，所以現在由外部評審來決定。"},{"w":"equal","p":"adj.","d":"the same in size, number, value or level","c":"相等的；平等的","s":"A: How will the two branches share the money from the new government contract they won together this month? B: The directors agreed that each branch will get an equal share of the profits, because both teams worked just as hard on the proposal and the final presentation.","t":"A：這兩間分公司要怎麼分配這個月共同贏得的新政府合約的錢？ B：主管們同意每間分公司都會得到【相等的】利潤，因為兩個團隊在提案和最後簡報上都一樣努力。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"doing something as a paid job, not as a hobby","c":"職業的；專業的","s":"A: Why did the company hire a coach to train our basketball team before the charity game next month? B: The manager wants us to look good in front of our clients, so she invited a former professional player who played in the national league for ten years to help us practice twice a week.","t":"A：為什麼公司在下個月的慈善比賽之前請了一位教練來訓練我們的籃球隊？ B：經理希望我們在客戶面前表現得好一點，所以她請來一位曾在全國聯賽打了十年的前【職業】球員，每週幫我們練習兩次。"},{"w":"amateur","p":"adj.","d":"doing something for fun, not as a paid job","c":"業餘的","s":"A: Are the singers performing at the company's year-end party this Friday famous musicians from a record company? B: No, they are an amateur band made up of three accountants and an engineer from our office, and they practice every Wednesday evening after work in a small studio downtown.","t":"A：這個星期五在公司尾牙表演的歌手是唱片公司的知名音樂人嗎？ B：不是，他們是由我們辦公室三位會計師和一位工程師組成的【業餘】樂團，每週三晚上下班後在市中心的一間小錄音室練習。"},{"w":"actively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that involves doing things and taking part","c":"積極地；主動地","s":"A: What qualities is the hiring team looking for in the new marketing assistant who will join us in January? B: We need someone who will actively share ideas in meetings and look for new customers online, instead of just waiting for the manager to give instructions every day.","t":"A：招募小組在找即將於一月加入的新行銷助理時，看重哪些特質？ B：我們需要一個會在會議中【積極地】分享想法、並在網路上尋找新客戶的人，而不是每天只等經理下指示。"},{"w":"successfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that achieves the result you wanted","c":"成功地","s":"A: How did the small company manage to get its new tea drinks into so many convenience stores across the country? B: The marketing team successfully competed against several larger brands in a national taste test, and after their drinks took first place, the stores were eager to sell them.","t":"A：那家小公司是怎麼讓它的新茶飲進入全國這麼多便利商店的？ B：行銷團隊在全國試飲評比中【成功地】擊敗了幾個較大的品牌，他們的飲料拿下第一名後，商店都很想販售。"},{"w":"closely","p":"adv.","d":"carefully and with attention","c":"密切地；仔細地","s":"A: Why does the sales director check the websites of the other phone companies every morning before work? B: She likes to watch their prices and special offers closely, so that our team can react quickly and change our own deals before customers decide to buy from someone else.","t":"A：為什麼業務總監每天上班前都要查看其他電信公司的網站？ B：她喜歡【密切地】觀察他們的價格和優惠方案，這樣我們團隊就能快速反應，在顧客決定向別人購買之前調整我們自己的方案。"}]},{"unit":71,"theme":"Complaining 抱怨","cards":[{"w":"complaint","p":"n.","d":"a statement that something is wrong or not good enough","c":"抱怨；投訴","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager look so worried this morning, and why did she cancel her meeting with the new suppliers? B: A guest on the fifth floor made a serious complaint about the noise from the kitchen last night, so she is checking the problem herself before the guest checks out at noon.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理今天早上看起來這麼擔心，而且她為什麼取消了和新供應商的會議？ B：五樓的一位房客昨晚針對廚房傳來的噪音提出了嚴重的【投訴】，所以她要在房客中午退房前親自檢查這個問題。"},{"w":"grumble","p":"v.","d":"to complain in a quiet, unhappy way","c":"發牢騷；抱怨","s":"A: How did the staff react when the company announced that the office would move to the new building outside the city? B: Some people began to grumble about the longer journey to work, but most of them stopped complaining after they saw the bright rooms and the free parking spaces.","t":"A：公司宣布辦公室要搬到市郊的新大樓時，員工有什麼反應？ B：有些人開始【發牢騷】，抱怨通勤路程變長，但大多數人看到明亮的房間和免費停車位後就不再抱怨了。"},{"w":"moan","p":"v.","d":"to complain in an annoying way about something","c":"抱怨；嘟囔","s":"A: Is it true that the sales team is unhappy with the new travel policy that the finance department introduced last month? B: Yes, they often moan about the cheap hotels they have to book now, but the manager says the company must cut costs until sales improve next year.","t":"A：聽說業務團隊對財務部上個月推出的新差旅政策不滿意，是真的嗎？ B：是的，他們常常【抱怨】現在必須訂的便宜飯店，但經理說在明年業績好轉之前，公司必須削減開支。"},{"w":"whine","p":"v.","d":"to complain in a weak, childish voice","c":"哀訴；發牢騷","s":"A: Why did the trainer look so tired after the team-building trip to the mountains with the new interns last weekend? B: Several of the interns continued to whine about the cold weather and the long hike all day, so she had to keep encouraging them until they finally reached the camp.","t":"A：上週末和新實習生去山上參加團隊建立活動後，訓練員為什麼看起來那麼累？ B：好幾個實習生一整天不停地【發牢騷】，抱怨寒冷的天氣和漫長的健行，所以她得一直鼓勵他們，直到他們終於抵達營地。"},{"w":"protest","p":"v.","d":"to show strongly in public that you do not agree with something","c":"抗議","s":"A: Why were so many workers standing outside the factory gate with signs when I drove past early this morning? B: They gathered there to protest against the plan to close the night shift, because about two hundred people could lose their jobs if the owners decide to go ahead with it.","t":"A：我今天一大早開車經過時，為什麼有那麼多工人拿著標語站在工廠大門外？ B：他們聚集在那裡【抗議】關閉夜班的計畫，因為如果老闆決定執行，大約兩百人可能會失去工作。"},{"w":"object","p":"v.","d":"to say that you do not agree with or do not like something","c":"反對","s":"A: Did everyone at the board meeting agree with the proposal to build a second warehouse near the airport? B: Not exactly, two directors decided to object to the plan because they think the land is too expensive, so the final vote has been delayed until next month.","t":"A：董事會上每個人都同意在機場附近蓋第二座倉庫的提案嗎？ B：不完全是，有兩位董事決定【反對】這個計畫，因為他們認為土地太貴，所以最後的表決延到下個月。"},{"w":"criticize","p":"v.","d":"to say what is bad or wrong about someone or something","c":"批評","s":"A: Why did the marketing director look so upset when she came out of the meeting with the company president? B: The president began to criticize her team's new advertising campaign in front of everyone, saying the photos were too dark and the message was confusing for younger customers.","t":"A：行銷總監和公司總裁開完會出來時，為什麼看起來那麼沮喪？ B：總裁當著所有人的面開始【批評】她團隊的新廣告活動，說照片太暗，而且訊息讓年輕顧客感到困惑。"},{"w":"blame","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone is responsible for something bad","c":"責怪；歸咎","s":"A: Who is responsible for the shipping mistake that sent two hundred boxes to the wrong store in Kaohsiung last week? B: It's hard to say, but you shouldn't blame the drivers, because the address in our computer system was wrong before the orders even left the warehouse.","t":"A：上週把兩百箱貨送錯到高雄門市的運送錯誤，該由誰負責？ B：很難說，但你不應該【責怪】司機，因為在訂單離開倉庫之前，我們電腦系統裡的地址就已經錯了。"},{"w":"accuse","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone has done something wrong","c":"指控；控告","s":"A: Why is the store manager meeting with the security team and a lawyer this afternoon? B: A customer plans to accuse one of our cashiers of taking money from her wallet, so the manager wants to check the camera recordings carefully before anyone says anything to the police.","t":"A：店長今天下午為什麼要和保全團隊及一位律師開會？ B：一位顧客打算【指控】我們的一名收銀員從她的皮夾拿錢，所以經理想在任何人向警方說明之前，先仔細檢查監視器錄影。"},{"w":"dissatisfaction","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of not being pleased with something","c":"不滿","s":"A: Why did the airline decide to give every passenger on the delayed flight a free meal and a travel voucher? B: The managers noticed growing dissatisfaction among customers on social media after many long delays this summer, and they want to win back their trust before the busy holiday season.","t":"A：為什麼航空公司決定給延誤班機上的每位乘客一份免費餐點和旅遊抵用券？ B：經理們注意到，今年夏天多次長時間延誤後，顧客在社群媒體上的【不滿】越來越多，他們想在忙碌的假期旺季前贏回顧客的信任。"},{"w":"frustration","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being upset because you cannot do or change something","c":"挫折感；沮喪","s":"A: How is the IT team dealing with the computer problems that have slowed down the whole accounting department this week? B: They are working late every night, and I can understand their frustration, because each time they fix one error, another one appears and the accountants keep calling them for help.","t":"A：IT團隊如何處理這週拖慢整個會計部門的電腦問題？ B：他們每天晚上都加班，我能理解他們的【挫折感】，因為每次修好一個錯誤，就會出現另一個，而會計人員一直打電話向他們求助。"},{"w":"annoyance","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being a little angry","c":"惱怒；煩惱","s":"A: Did the passengers complain when the train stopped for almost an hour between two stations yesterday evening? B: Yes, many of them showed their annoyance by sighing and checking their watches, especially because nobody explained the reason for the delay over the speakers until much later.","t":"A：昨晚火車在兩站之間停了將近一小時，乘客有抱怨嗎？ B：有，很多人嘆氣、一直看手錶來表現他們的【惱怒】，尤其是因為直到很久之後才有人透過廣播說明延誤的原因。"},{"w":"issue","p":"n.","d":"a problem that people need to deal with","c":"問題；議題","s":"A: Why did the customer service team call a special meeting before the store opened this morning? B: Several shoppers wrote to us about the same issue with our online payment system, so the team wants to find out what went wrong and fix it before the weekend sale begins.","t":"A：客服團隊為什麼在今天早上開店前召開特別會議？ B：好幾位顧客寫信給我們反映網路付款系統的同一個【問題】，所以團隊想找出哪裡出錯，並在週末特賣開始前修好。"},{"w":"concern","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry about something","c":"擔憂；關切的事","s":"A: What did the parents say at the meeting with the school about the new bus company? B: Their main concern was safety, because the buses often arrive late and the drivers seem to drive too fast, so the principal promised to discuss the problem with the company director.","t":"A：家長們在跟學校開會時，對新的巴士公司說了什麼？ B：他們主要的【擔憂】是安全，因為公車常常遲到，而且司機似乎開得太快，所以校長答應會和公司主管討論這個問題。"},{"w":"negative","p":"adj.","d":"bad or harmful; showing a bad opinion","c":"負面的；消極的","s":"A: How did customers respond to the new menu that the restaurant introduced at the beginning of the month? B: We received a lot of negative comments online, because many people felt the dishes were smaller and more expensive, so the chef is already planning to bring back some old favorites.","t":"A：餐廳月初推出的新菜單，顧客的反應如何？ B：我們在網路上收到很多【負面的】評論，因為很多人覺得菜變少了又變貴，所以主廚已經打算把一些老招牌菜加回來。"},{"w":"critical","p":"adj.","d":"saying that someone or something is bad or wrong","c":"批評的；挑剔的","s":"A: Why did the hotel owner decide to repaint all the rooms and replace the old carpets so suddenly? B: A famous travel writer stayed here last month and wrote a very critical article about the poor condition of the rooms, and after that our online bookings dropped quite a lot.","t":"A：飯店老闆為什麼這麼突然決定重新粉刷所有房間並更換舊地毯？ B：一位知名的旅遊作家上個月住過這裡，寫了一篇非常【批評性的】文章，指出房間狀況很差，之後我們的網路訂房就減少了很多。"},{"w":"unhappy","p":"adj.","d":"not pleased or satisfied","c":"不滿意的；不高興的","s":"A: Why is the receptionist calling the cleaning company again, even though they came to the office yesterday? B: She is unhappy with their work, because the meeting rooms still look dirty and the trash in the kitchen was not taken out, so she wants them to come back today.","t":"A：清潔公司昨天已經來過辦公室了，為什麼接待員又打電話給他們？ B：她對他們的工作【不滿意】，因為會議室看起來還是很髒，廚房的垃圾也沒倒，所以她要他們今天再來一次。"},{"w":"dissatisfied","p":"adj.","d":"not pleased with something because it is not good enough","c":"不滿意的","s":"A: Why did the online shop decide to offer free returns on all items starting from next month? B: Too many dissatisfied customers were leaving bad reviews because they had to pay shipping fees to send back clothes that did not fit, so the owners decided to change the policy.","t":"A：網路商店為什麼決定從下個月起所有商品都提供免費退貨？ B：太多【不滿意的】顧客留下差評，因為他們得付運費退回不合身的衣服，所以老闆決定改變政策。"},{"w":"irritated","p":"adj.","d":"feeling annoyed or a little angry","c":"惱火的；不耐煩的","s":"A: Why did the manager speak so sharply to the new assistant during the meeting this morning? B: He was irritated because the assistant had forgotten to print the sales reports again, and the clients from Japan had to wait while someone ran to the printer on the third floor.","t":"A：經理今天早上開會時為什麼對新助理說話那麼嚴厲？ B：他很【惱火】，因為助理又忘了印業務報告，日本客戶只好等著有人跑到三樓的印表機去印。"},{"w":"outraged","p":"adj.","d":"extremely angry and shocked","c":"極為憤怒的","s":"A: What happened after the bank suddenly raised its fees without telling its customers in advance? B: Many customers were outraged and wrote angry letters to the local newspaper, so the bank finally apologized and promised to return the extra money to everyone by the end of the month.","t":"A：銀行在沒有事先告知客戶的情況下突然調高手續費，之後發生了什麼事？ B：許多客戶【極為憤怒】，寫了憤怒的信給當地報紙，所以銀行最後道歉，並承諾在月底前把多收的錢退還給每個人。"},{"w":"formally","p":"adv.","d":"in an official way","c":"正式地","s":"A: What should I do if my landlord still refuses to repair the broken heater in my apartment after three weeks? B: You should complain formally by writing a letter to the housing office, and keep a copy for yourself, because they usually act faster when they receive a written complaint.","t":"A：如果房東過了三週還是不肯修我公寓裡壞掉的暖氣，我該怎麼辦？ B：你應該寫信給住房管理處【正式地】投訴，並自己留一份副本，因為他們收到書面投訴時通常處理得比較快。"},{"w":"repeatedly","p":"adv.","d":"many times, again and again","c":"一再地；反覆地","s":"A: Why did the company finally replace the old coffee machine in the staff kitchen on the second floor? B: Employees had repeatedly asked for a new one because it broke down almost every week, and last Monday it leaked water all over the floor and damaged some boxes of paper.","t":"A：公司為什麼終於更換了二樓員工廚房裡的舊咖啡機？ B：員工們【一再地】要求換新的，因為它幾乎每週都故障，上週一還漏水流得滿地都是，弄壞了幾箱紙。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that many people can see or hear","c":"公開地","s":"A: Why is the restaurant owner so worried about the review that the food blogger posted last night? B: The blogger publicly complained about the slow service and cold soup on her website, and more than fifty thousand people follow her, so many of them might decide not to visit us.","t":"A：餐廳老闆為什麼這麼擔心那位美食部落客昨晚發布的評論？ B：那位部落客在她的網站上【公開地】抱怨服務很慢、湯是冷的，而她有超過五萬名追蹤者，所以其中很多人可能會決定不來我們店。"},{"w":"loudly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that makes a lot of noise","c":"大聲地","s":"A: Why did the security guard have to come to the front desk of the bank this morning? B: A customer was complaining very loudly about the long line and shouting at the tellers, so the other customers felt uncomfortable and the manager asked the guard to calm him down.","t":"A：今天早上保全為什麼必須到銀行櫃台來？ B：一位顧客非常【大聲地】抱怨排隊太久，還對著行員大吼，讓其他客人覺得不舒服，所以經理請保全讓他冷靜下來。"},{"w":"privately","p":"adv.","d":"without other people being present","c":"私下地","s":"A: Should I tell my team leader in the meeting that her schedule for the project is not realistic? B: It's better to speak to her privately after the meeting, because she may feel embarrassed if you point out the problem in front of the whole team and the new clients.","t":"A：我應該在會議上跟組長說她的專案時程不切實際嗎？ B：最好在會後【私下】跟她說，因為如果你在全組和新客戶面前指出這個問題，她可能會覺得難堪。"},{"w":"voice","p":"v.","d":"to say what you think or feel about something","c":"表達；說出","s":"A: How can employees share their opinions about the new working hours if they don't want to speak in the big meeting? B: They can voice their concerns through the online survey that human resources sent out yesterday, and all the answers will be anonymous, so nobody needs to worry.","t":"A：如果員工不想在大型會議上發言，他們要怎麼分享對新工作時間的看法？ B：他們可以透過人資部昨天寄出的線上問卷【表達】他們的疑慮，而且所有回答都是匿名的，所以大家不用擔心。"},{"w":"raise","p":"v.","d":"to bring up a subject so people can talk about it","c":"提出（問題、議題）","s":"A: When is the best time to talk about the problems with our software supplier, who keeps missing deadlines? B: You can raise the matter at Thursday's management meeting, because the director will be there and she has the power to change suppliers if the problems continue.","t":"A：我們的軟體供應商一直延誤期限，什麼時候是談這個問題的最好時機？ B：你可以在週四的管理會議上【提出】這件事，因為主管會出席，而且如果問題持續，她有權更換供應商。"},{"w":"report","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone in charge about something that happened","c":"報告；通報","s":"A: What should I do if the air conditioner in the meeting room starts making that strange noise again? B: Please report the problem to the building maintenance office on the ground floor right away, and they will send a technician to check it before the afternoon training session starts.","t":"A：如果會議室的冷氣又開始發出那種怪聲，我該怎麼辦？ B：請立刻向一樓的大樓維修辦公室【通報】這個問題，他們會在下午的訓練課程開始前派技術人員來檢查。"},{"w":"escalate","p":"v.","d":"to pass a problem to a higher level or more senior person","c":"上報；使升級","s":"A: The customer has called five times about her missing package, so what should I do if she phones again? B: If you cannot solve the problem yourself, you should escalate it to the supervisor, who can contact the delivery company directly and offer the customer a full refund if necessary.","t":"A：那位顧客已經為了遺失的包裹打來五次了，如果她再打來我該怎麼辦？ B：如果你自己無法解決，就應該把問題【上報】給主管，主管可以直接聯絡貨運公司，必要時提供顧客全額退款。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to find an answer to a problem","c":"解決","s":"A: How long does it usually take your team to deal with a customer complaint about a broken product? B: We try to resolve most problems within forty-eight hours, either by sending a replacement or giving a refund, because we know that quick service keeps our customers loyal.","t":"A：你們團隊處理顧客對瑕疵產品的投訴通常需要多久？ B：我們盡量在四十八小時內【解決】大部分的問題，不是寄送替換品就是退款，因為我們知道快速的服務能留住忠實顧客。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"opinions about how good or bad something is","c":"意見回饋","s":"A: Why is the hotel asking every guest to fill out a short survey when they check out this month? B: The manager wants honest feedback about the rooms, the breakfast and the staff, so she can find out what guests really think and decide which areas need improvement first.","t":"A：飯店這個月為什麼請每位房客退房時填一份簡短的問卷？ B：經理想得到有關房間、早餐和員工的真實【意見回饋】，這樣她就能了解房客真正的想法，並決定哪些部分要優先改善。"},{"w":"petition","p":"n.","d":"a written request signed by many people asking for a change","c":"請願書","s":"A: How are the residents trying to stop the city from building a large parking lot in the park near our office? B: They started a petition last week, and more than three thousand people have already signed it, so they plan to give it to the mayor at the next council meeting.","t":"A：居民們如何試著阻止市政府在我們辦公室附近的公園蓋大型停車場？ B：他們上週發起了一份【請願書】，已經有超過三千人簽名，所以他們打算在下次市議會開會時交給市長。"},{"w":"dispute","p":"n.","d":"a serious disagreement between people or groups","c":"爭端；糾紛","s":"A: Why hasn't the construction company finished the new shopping mall, even though it was supposed to open in May? B: There is a dispute between the builders and the owners about the extra costs, and work has stopped until both sides agree on who should pay for the changes.","t":"A：建設公司為什麼還沒蓋完新購物中心？它原本應該在五月開幕。 B：建商和業主之間對於額外費用有【糾紛】，在雙方對誰該支付變更費用達成共識之前，工程已經停止。"}]},{"unit":72,"theme":"Complaint Letter 投訴信","cards":[{"w":"dissatisfied","p":"adj.","d":"not happy with something","c":"不滿意的","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager call a meeting with all the front desk staff early this morning before the guests came down for breakfast? B: Several guests wrote online reviews saying they were dissatisfied with the slow check-in last weekend, so she wants everyone to learn the new computer system before the holiday rush.","t":"A：飯店經理為什麼今天一大早、在房客下樓吃早餐前，就召集所有櫃檯人員開會？ B：好幾位房客在網路上留下評論，說他們對上週末緩慢的入住手續感到【不滿意】，所以她希望大家在假期旺季前學會新的電腦系統。"},{"w":"issue","p":"n.","d":"a problem that people need to deal with","c":"問題；議題","s":"A: Have you heard back from the software company about the problem with our online booking page that keeps crashing? B: Yes, their technician called this morning and said the issue was caused by an old update, and he promised to fix it before our busy weekend sale begins on Friday.","t":"A：你有收到軟體公司的回覆嗎？關於我們線上訂位頁面一直當機的問題。 B：有，他們的技術人員今天早上打電話來，說這個【問題】是一次舊的更新造成的，並承諾會在星期五週末大特賣開始前修好。"},{"w":"problem","p":"n.","d":"something that is wrong and needs to be fixed","c":"問題","s":"A: Why are so many customers calling the help desk today instead of using the mobile app to pay their bills? B: There is a problem with the payment page, so people cannot finish their transactions, and our IT team has been working on it since eight o'clock this morning.","t":"A：為什麼今天這麼多顧客打電話到服務台，而不是用手機應用程式繳費？ B：付款頁面出了【問題】，所以大家無法完成交易，我們的資訊團隊從今天早上八點就一直在處理。"},{"w":"defective","p":"adj.","d":"not made correctly; not working properly","c":"有瑕疵的；有缺陷的","s":"A: Why did the electronics store take all the new coffee machines off the shelves just two days after they arrived? B: The manufacturer discovered that some of the heating parts were defective and could get too hot, so every store was told to send the machines back for safety checks.","t":"A：電器行為什麼在新咖啡機到貨才兩天，就把它們全部下架？ B：製造商發現部分加熱零件有【瑕疵】，可能會過熱，所以每家店都被要求把機器送回去做安全檢查。"},{"w":"damage","p":"v.","d":"to harm or break something","c":"損壞；損害","s":"A: Why does the moving company want us to pack all the computers in special boxes before Saturday? B: They said the trucks often shake on the mountain roads to the new office, and the heavy movement could damage the screens, so the extra protection will save us money on repairs.","t":"A：搬家公司為什麼要我們在星期六前把所有電腦裝進特殊的箱子裡？ B：他們說卡車在通往新辦公室的山路上常常晃動，劇烈的震動可能會【損壞】螢幕，所以多一層保護能幫我們省下維修費。"},{"w":"damaged","p":"adj.","d":"harmed or broken","c":"受損的；損壞的","s":"A: Why is the receptionist taking photos of the boxes that just arrived from our supplier in Vietnam? B: Two of the boxes look damaged on the corners, and some of the glass cups inside might be broken, so she needs pictures to send to the supplier along with our complaint.","t":"A：接待員為什麼在拍剛從越南供應商送來的箱子？ B：其中兩個箱子的邊角看起來【受損】了，裡面有些玻璃杯可能破了，所以她需要照片，連同我們的投訴一起寄給供應商。"},{"w":"delay","p":"n.","d":"a time when something happens later than planned","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: Why did the manager send an email to all the customers who ordered the new office chairs last month? B: There was a long delay at the port because of a storm, so the chairs will arrive two weeks later than planned, and she wanted to explain it before people started calling.","t":"A：經理為什麼寄電子郵件給上個月訂購新辦公椅的所有顧客？ B：港口因為暴風雨出現長時間【延誤】，所以椅子會比原定時間晚兩週到貨，她想在大家開始打電話來之前先說明。"},{"w":"late","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or happening after the expected time","c":"遲的；晚的","s":"A: Why does the customer at the counter look so angry, and why does he keep showing everyone his phone? B: His furniture order was supposed to arrive last Monday, but the truck came four days late, and he had to take another day off work to wait at home for the drivers.","t":"A：櫃檯那位顧客為什麼看起來這麼生氣，還一直給大家看他的手機？ B：他訂的家具原本上週一就該送到，但貨車【晚】了四天才來，他還得再請一天假在家等司機。"},{"w":"incorrect","p":"adj.","d":"not right; wrong","c":"不正確的；錯誤的","s":"A: Why did the accounting department send the monthly bill back to the cleaning company this afternoon? B: The bill showed the wrong number of hours, and the total was incorrect by almost three hundred dollars, so they asked the company to check its records and send a new one.","t":"A：會計部門今天下午為什麼把月帳單退回給清潔公司？ B：帳單上的時數錯了，總金額【不正確】，差了將近三百美元，所以他們請公司核對紀錄並重寄一份。"},{"w":"error","p":"n.","d":"a mistake","c":"錯誤","s":"A: Why did hundreds of customers receive two copies of the same bill from the phone company this month? B: A computer error in the billing system sent every message twice, and the company has already posted an apology on its website and promised that no one will pay extra.","t":"A：為什麼這個月有好幾百位顧客收到電信公司寄來兩份相同的帳單？ B：帳務系統的電腦【錯誤】讓每封訊息都寄了兩次，公司已經在網站上公告道歉，並承諾不會有人多付錢。"},{"w":"poor service","p":"n.phr.","d":"service that is slow, rude or of low quality","c":"服務差；服務不佳","s":"A: Why did the company decide to stop holding its annual dinner at that famous hotel downtown this year? B: Last year the waiters were rude, the food came out cold, and many guests complained about the poor service, so the planning team chose a smaller restaurant with much better reviews.","t":"A：公司今年為什麼決定不再在市中心那家知名飯店舉辦年度晚宴？ B：去年服務生很沒禮貌，餐點上桌時都是冷的，許多賓客抱怨【服務很差】，所以籌備小組選了一家評價好得多的小餐廳。"},{"w":"customer service","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of a company that helps customers with questions and problems","c":"客戶服務；客服","s":"A: My new laptop keeps turning off by itself, and I bought it only last week, so what should I do now? B: You should call the store's customer service number on the back of your receipt, because they usually offer free checks and can tell you whether you need to return it.","t":"A：我的新筆電一直自己關機，而且上週才買的，我現在該怎麼辦？ B：你應該打收據背面那家店的【客服】電話，因為他們通常提供免費檢測，也能告訴你是否需要退貨。"},{"w":"refund","p":"n.","d":"money that is paid back to you","c":"退款","s":"A: Did the airline do anything for you after it cancelled your flight to Tokyo at the last minute? B: Yes, after I filled out a form online, they gave me a full refund for the ticket, and they also paid for my hotel room near the airport that night.","t":"A：航空公司在最後一刻取消你飛東京的班機後，有為你做些什麼嗎？ B：有，我在網路上填完表格後，他們全額【退款】機票錢，還支付我那晚機場附近的飯店房間費用。"},{"w":"replace","p":"v.","d":"to put a new thing in the place of an old or broken one","c":"更換；替換","s":"A: The printer in the sales office has broken down three times this month, so what are we going to do about it? B: The office manager has decided to replace it with a faster model next week, because paying for repairs again and again costs more than buying a new one.","t":"A：業務辦公室的印表機這個月已經壞了三次，我們打算怎麼處理？ B：辦公室經理決定下週把它【換成】速度更快的機型，因為一再付維修費比買新的還貴。"},{"w":"replacement","p":"n.","d":"a new thing that takes the place of an old or broken one","c":"替換品；更換","s":"A: What happened when you told the online shop that the blender you received had a broken glass jar? B: They said sorry and sent me a replacement by express mail the next day, and they told me I could keep the broken one because returning it would be too much trouble.","t":"A：你告訴網路商店收到的果汁機玻璃杯破了之後，結果怎樣？ B：他們道了歉，隔天就用快遞寄來一台【替換品】，還說壞掉那台我可以留著，因為寄回去太麻煩了。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken","c":"修理；修復","s":"A: Why are there workers on the roof of the office building, and why is part of the parking lot closed today? B: The heavy rain last week caused a leak above the meeting room, so the building owner hired a team to repair the roof before the next storm arrives.","t":"A：辦公大樓屋頂上為什麼有工人，而且今天部分停車場也封閉了？ B：上週的大雨讓會議室上方漏水，所以大樓業主請了一組人在下一場暴風雨來之前【修理】屋頂。"},{"w":"compensation","p":"n.","d":"money paid to someone because of a loss or problem","c":"賠償；補償","s":"A: Did the travel agency do anything after your tour group waited at the airport for six hours with no bus? B: After many of us wrote letters, the agency offered each traveler two hundred dollars as compensation and a free day trip on our next holiday with them.","t":"A：你們旅行團在機場等了六個小時都沒有巴士，旅行社後來有做什麼嗎？ B：在我們很多人寫信之後，旅行社給每位旅客兩百美元作為【賠償】，並在下次跟他們出遊時免費招待一日遊。"},{"w":"solution","p":"n.","d":"a way to solve a problem","c":"解決辦法","s":"A: Our customers keep complaining that they wait too long on the phone, so has the team found any way to help? B: Yes, the best solution we found is to add an online chat service, so simple questions can be answered quickly while staff on the phones handle the harder problems.","t":"A：顧客一直抱怨電話等太久，團隊有找到任何改善方法嗎？ B：有，我們找到最好的【解決辦法】是增加線上聊天服務，這樣簡單的問題能很快回覆，電話客服人員則處理較困難的問題。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to find an answer to a problem or end a disagreement","c":"解決","s":"A: How long does your team usually need to deal with a customer's complaint after it comes in by email? B: Our goal is to resolve most complaints within forty-eight hours, but if a case needs a visit from a technician, it can take up to a week to finish.","t":"A：顧客的投訴透過電子郵件進來後，你們團隊通常需要多久處理？ B：我們的目標是在四十八小時內【解決】大部分的投訴，但如果需要技術人員到府，可能要花一週才能完成。"},{"w":"request","p":"n.","d":"the act of politely asking for something","c":"要求；請求","s":"A: Why did the hotel move the businessman in room 512 to a different floor this afternoon? B: He made a request for a quieter room because of the construction noise next door, and since he stays with us every month, the manager wanted to keep him happy.","t":"A：飯店今天下午為什麼把512號房的商務客換到別的樓層？ B：因為隔壁施工噪音，他提出換到較安靜房間的【要求】，而且他每個月都住我們這裡，經理想讓他滿意。"},{"w":"regret","p":"v.","d":"to feel sorry about something","c":"遺憾；後悔","s":"A: How did the furniture company answer the angry letter you sent about the broken table they delivered? B: The manager wrote that they regret the trouble it caused us, and she promised that a new table would be delivered by Friday along with a gift card for our next purchase.","t":"A：家具公司怎麼回覆你寄去抱怨他們送來的桌子壞掉的那封信？ B：經理寫說他們對造成我們的困擾深感【遺憾】，並承諾星期五前會送來一張新桌子，還附上下次購物可用的禮物卡。"},{"w":"disappointed","p":"adj.","d":"sad because something was not as good as you hoped","c":"失望的","s":"A: How did the guests feel about the resort after the long trip to the island last weekend? B: Many of them were disappointed because the swimming pool was closed for cleaning and the sea view rooms they booked were not ready, so the manager offered them free dinners.","t":"A：上週末長途跋涉到島上後，賓客們對度假村感覺如何？ B：很多人都很【失望】，因為游泳池關閉清潔，而他們訂的海景房也還沒準備好，所以經理請他們免費吃晚餐。"},{"w":"unsatisfactory","p":"adj.","d":"not good enough","c":"不令人滿意的；不夠好的","s":"A: Why did the company decide not to sign a new contract with the cleaning service this year? B: The quality of their work was unsatisfactory for several months, with dirty floors and empty soap bottles in the restrooms, so the office manager found a more reliable team.","t":"A：公司今年為什麼決定不和清潔公司續約？ B：他們好幾個月的工作品質都【不令人滿意】，地板髒、廁所的洗手乳瓶也是空的，所以辦公室經理找了更可靠的團隊。"},{"w":"inconvenience","p":"n.","d":"trouble or difficulty that makes things less easy","c":"不便；麻煩","s":"A: Why is the elevator closed today, and what should visitors who can't use the stairs do? B: It is being checked for safety until four o'clock, and the building manager has put up a sign to say sorry for the inconvenience and to tell visitors to use the service elevator at the back.","t":"A：電梯今天為什麼停用？無法走樓梯的訪客該怎麼辦？ B：電梯在做安全檢查到四點，大樓管理員貼了告示，為造成的【不便】致歉，並請訪客使用後面的貨梯。"},{"w":"apology","p":"n.","d":"words that say you are sorry","c":"道歉","s":"A: Did the restaurant do anything after the waiter dropped a bowl of soup on your new suit last night? B: The manager came to our table right away, gave me a sincere apology, paid for the dry cleaning, and also took the cost of our whole dinner off the bill.","t":"A：昨晚服務生把一碗湯打翻在你的新西裝上，餐廳有做什麼嗎？ B：經理馬上來到我們桌邊，誠懇地向我【道歉】，支付了乾洗費，還把我們整頓晚餐的費用從帳單上扣掉。"},{"w":"apologize","p":"v.","d":"to say that you are sorry","c":"道歉","s":"A: What should I say to the customer whose package was sent to the wrong address twice this month? B: First, you should apologize for our mistake and listen to her carefully, and then offer her free shipping on her next purchase, because we really don't want to lose a loyal customer.","t":"A：這位顧客的包裹這個月兩度被送錯地址，我該怎麼跟她說？ B：首先，你應該為我們的錯誤【道歉】並仔細聆聽她說的話，然後提供她下次購物免運費，因為我們真的不想失去一位忠實顧客。"},{"w":"contact","p":"v.","d":"to call, write to or email someone","c":"聯絡","s":"A: I've been waiting for the online store to send my office supplies for almost two weeks now, so what should I do? B: You should contact them by email and include your receipt number, because they usually answer within one working day and can check where the package is.","t":"A：我等網路商店寄辦公用品已經快兩週了，我該怎麼辦？ B：你應該寫電子郵件【聯絡】他們並附上收據編號，因為他們通常一個工作天內會回覆，也能查詢包裹在哪裡。"},{"w":"respond","p":"v.","d":"to answer or reply","c":"回覆；回應","s":"A: How quickly does our company expect the support team to answer complaints that come in through the website? B: The rule is that staff must respond to every message within twenty-four hours, even on weekends, because customers become angrier when they feel that nobody is listening to them.","t":"A：公司希望支援團隊多快回覆網站上收到的投訴？ B：規定是員工必須在二十四小時內【回覆】每一則訊息，即使是週末也一樣，因為顧客覺得沒人理會時會更生氣。"},{"w":"prompt","p":"adj.","d":"done quickly, without waiting","c":"迅速的；及時的","s":"A: Why did that customer write such a nice review about our repair center on the website last night? B: She was happy with our prompt reply, because her washing machine broke on Sunday morning and our technician fixed it in her home before dinner the same day.","t":"A：那位顧客昨晚為什麼在網站上給我們維修中心那麼好的評論？ B：她很滿意我們【迅速】的回應，因為她的洗衣機星期天早上壞了，我們的技術人員當天晚餐前就到她家修好了。"},{"w":"immediately","p":"adv.","d":"at once; right now","c":"立刻；馬上","s":"A: What happened when the guest in room 304 called the front desk to say that the water in his bathroom was leaking onto the floor? B: The manager sent a plumber immediately, and she also moved the guest to a bigger room with a city view so that he could get some sleep.","t":"A：304號房的房客打電話到櫃檯說浴室的水漏到地板上，結果怎樣？ B：經理【立刻】派了水電工過去，還把房客換到一間有市景的較大房間，讓他能好好睡覺。"},{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the facts about something","c":"調查","s":"A: Several customers say they were charged twice for the same meal at our downtown branch, so what is the head office doing about it? B: They have asked the finance team to investigate the payment records from last month, and anyone who paid too much will get their money back.","t":"A：好幾位顧客說他們在我們市中心分店同一餐被扣款兩次，總公司打算怎麼處理？ B：他們已經請財務團隊【調查】上個月的付款紀錄，任何多付錢的人都會拿回退款。"},{"w":"clarify","p":"v.","d":"to make something clearer or easier to understand","c":"釐清；澄清","s":"A: Why did the sales manager call the customer again after she had already answered his long email this morning? B: Some parts of his message were confusing, so she wanted to clarify exactly which items were missing from the box before sending the new ones by express delivery.","t":"A：業務經理今天早上已經回覆那位顧客的長篇郵件了，為什麼又打電話給他？ B：他的訊息有些部分讓人困惑，所以她想在用快遞寄出新品前，【釐清】箱子裡到底少了哪些品項。"},{"w":"evidence","p":"n.","d":"facts or things that show something is true","c":"證據；證明","s":"A: The insurance company says it needs more information before it pays for our broken shop window, so what should we send them? B: We should give them some evidence, such as the photos from the security camera and the police report, to show that the window was broken during the storm.","t":"A：保險公司說在理賠我們店破掉的櫥窗之前需要更多資料，我們該寄什麼給他們？ B：我們應該提供一些【證據】，例如監視器的照片和報案紀錄，證明窗戶是在暴風雨期間破掉的。"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper that shows you have paid for something","c":"收據","s":"A: I want to take this jacket back to the department store because the zipper broke after only one week, but what will they ask me for? B: They will want to see your receipt, so look for it in your wallet or email, because without it they may only give you store credit.","t":"A：這件夾克才穿一週拉鍊就壞了，我想拿回百貨公司退，但他們會要求我出示什麼？ B：他們會想看你的【收據】，所以找找你的皮夾或電子郵件，因為沒有它的話，他們可能只會給你購物抵用金。"},{"w":"invoice","p":"n.","d":"a list of goods or services that shows how much you must pay","c":"發票；請款單","s":"A: Why hasn't the accounting team paid the printing company for the brochures they made for the trade show? B: The invoice they sent us listed five thousand copies, but we only received three thousand, so we asked them to correct it before we make the payment.","t":"A：會計團隊為什麼還沒付錢給幫我們印商展手冊的印刷公司？ B：他們寄來的【請款單】列了五千份，但我們只收到三千份，所以我們請他們先更正再付款。"},{"w":"order","p":"n.","d":"a request to buy goods","c":"訂單；訂購","s":"A: Why does the customer on line two sound so upset, and why does she keep asking for the manager? B: She placed an order for twenty office desks a month ago, but only ten have arrived, and her new employees start work on Monday with nowhere to sit.","t":"A：二線的顧客聽起來為什麼這麼不高興，還一直要求找經理？ B：她一個月前下了二十張辦公桌的【訂單】，但只到了十張，而她的新員工星期一就要上班，卻沒有地方坐。"},{"w":"delivery","p":"n.","d":"the act of bringing goods to a place","c":"送貨；遞送","s":"A: Why is the restaurant owner so worried about tonight's big wedding party? B: The delivery of fresh fish and vegetables did not arrive this morning because the truck broke down on the highway, and she is now calling other suppliers to find enough food for two hundred guests.","t":"A：餐廳老闆為什麼這麼擔心今晚的大型婚宴？ B：今天早上新鮮魚貨和蔬菜的【送貨】沒有到，因為卡車在高速公路上拋錨了，她現在正打電話給其他供應商，想找到足夠兩百位賓客吃的食材。"},{"w":"shipment","p":"n.","d":"a load of goods that is sent together","c":"一批貨；運送的貨物","s":"A: Why did the warehouse staff refuse to sign for the boxes from the paper supplier this morning? B: The whole shipment was wet from the rain because the driver left the truck door open, so they took photos and asked the supplier to send new boxes as soon as possible.","t":"A：倉庫人員今天早上為什麼拒絕簽收紙品供應商送來的箱子？ B：整批【貨】都被雨淋濕了，因為司機沒關卡車門，所以他們拍了照，並要求供應商盡快重新送貨。"},{"w":"policy","p":"n.","d":"a set of rules a company follows","c":"政策；規定","s":"A: Can I return these running shoes even though I've already worn them outside a few times? B: According to the store's return policy, you can bring back any shoes within thirty days if they hurt your feet, but you must show your receipt and the original box.","t":"A：這雙跑鞋我已經穿出去幾次了，還能退貨嗎？ B：根據店家的退貨【政策】，只要鞋子讓你腳痛，三十天內都能退回，但你必須出示收據和原本的鞋盒。"},{"w":"guarantee","p":"n.","d":"a promise that something will be done or will work","c":"保證","s":"A: Why did you choose this cleaning company for the office when there are cheaper ones in the neighborhood? B: They offer a money-back guarantee, so if we are not happy with their work after the first month, we can get all our money back without any questions.","t":"A：附近有更便宜的清潔公司，你為什麼選這家來打掃辦公室？ B：他們提供退款【保證】，如果第一個月後我們不滿意他們的工作，可以無條件拿回全部的錢。"},{"w":"warranty","p":"n.","d":"a written promise to repair a product for free for a period of time","c":"保固；保證書","s":"A: The screen on my office laptop suddenly went black this morning, so do I have to pay for the repair myself? B: No, the computer is still under warranty for another six months, so the manufacturer will fix it for free if you bring it to their service center downtown.","t":"A：我辦公室的筆電螢幕今天早上突然變黑，維修費要我自己付嗎？ B：不用，這台電腦還有六個月的【保固】，只要你拿到市中心的維修中心，製造商會免費修理。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you really mean it","c":"誠摯地；真誠地","s":"A: How should I end the letter to the customer whose wedding cake arrived three hours after the party started? B: Tell her that we sincerely hope she will give us another chance, sign it with your full name and title, and include a gift card for a free cake on her first anniversary.","t":"A：那位顧客的結婚蛋糕在派對開始三小時後才送到，我寫給她的信該怎麼結尾？ B：告訴她我們【誠摯地】希望她能再給我們一次機會，署上你的全名和職稱，並附上一張她結婚一週年可兌換免費蛋糕的禮物卡。"},{"w":"faithfully","p":"adv.","d":"used in \"Yours faithfully\" to end a formal letter when you don't know the person's name","c":"謹上（正式書信結尾）；忠實地","s":"A: I am writing a formal complaint letter to a hotel, but I don't know the manager's name, so how should I finish it? B: When you begin with \"Dear Sir or Madam,\" you should end the letter with \"Yours faithfully,\" and then sign your full name clearly below it.","t":"A：我正在寫一封給飯店的正式投訴信，但我不知道經理的名字，該怎麼結尾？ B：當你用「敬啟者」開頭時，信的結尾應該寫「【謹上】」，然後在下面清楚簽上你的全名。"},{"w":"concern","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry about something","c":"擔憂；關切","s":"A: Why did the parents ask for a meeting with the manager of the after-school program last Friday? B: They raised a concern about the old playground equipment, because two children were hurt last month, and they want the program to replace the swings before summer.","t":"A：家長們上週五為什麼要求和課後班的負責人開會？ B：他們對老舊的遊樂設施提出【擔憂】，因為上個月有兩個孩子受傷，他們希望課後班在夏天前更換鞦韆。"},{"w":"attention","p":"n.","d":"the act of noticing or dealing with something","c":"注意；處理","s":"A: I have written to the airline three times about my lost suitcase, but nobody has answered, so what else can I do? B: Try sending your letter for the attention of the customer relations manager, because it will go directly to her desk instead of to the busy general mailbox.","t":"A：我已經寫信給航空公司三次詢問遺失的行李箱，但都沒人回覆，我還能怎麼做？ B：試著在信上註明「客戶關係經理【親啟】」，這樣信會直接送到她的桌上，而不是進到繁忙的一般信箱。"},{"w":"action","p":"n.","d":"something you do to deal with a problem","c":"行動；措施","s":"A: What did the restaurant owner say after the newspaper wrote about the dirty kitchen and the angry diners? B: She promised to take action right away, so she closed the restaurant for three days, hired a new cleaning team, and trained all the cooks again.","t":"A：報紙報導了廚房髒亂和顧客生氣的事之後，餐廳老闆怎麼說？ B：她承諾立刻採取【行動】，所以關店三天，請了新的清潔團隊，並重新訓練所有廚師。"},{"w":"situation","p":"n.","d":"what is happening at a particular time","c":"情況；處境","s":"A: Why did the manager call an emergency meeting with the customer service staff this afternoon? B: Hundreds of people are angry because their flights were cancelled by the storm, so she wants to explain how the team should handle the situation and which passengers should get hotel rooms first.","t":"A：經理今天下午為什麼和客服人員召開緊急會議？ B：好幾百人因為班機被暴風雨取消而很生氣，所以她想說明團隊該如何處理這個【情況】，以及哪些乘客應該優先安排飯店房間。"},{"w":"matter","p":"n.","d":"a subject or problem that you deal with","c":"事情；問題","s":"A: Thank you for listening to my complaint about the noisy air conditioner in my hotel room, but when will someone fix it? B: I will report this matter to our maintenance team right now, and a technician will come to your room within thirty minutes, or we can move you to another room.","t":"A：謝謝你聽我抱怨飯店房間的冷氣很吵，但什麼時候會有人來修？ B：我現在就會把這件【事】回報給維修團隊，技術人員會在三十分鐘內到您房間，或者我們也可以幫您換房。"}]},{"unit":73,"theme":"Computer 電腦","cards":[{"w":"hardware","p":"n.","d":"the physical parts of a computer, such as the screen and keyboard","c":"硬體","s":"A: Why can't the design team start using the new video editing program that the company bought last month? B: The program needs much more power than our old laptops have, so we are waiting for new hardware, such as faster computers and bigger monitors, which should arrive next Tuesday.","t":"A：為什麼設計團隊還不能開始使用公司上個月買的新影片剪輯軟體？ B：那個軟體需要的效能比我們的舊筆電高很多，所以我們在等新的【硬體】，例如更快的電腦和更大的螢幕，應該下週二會送到。"},{"w":"software","p":"n.","d":"programs that tell a computer what to do","c":"軟體","s":"A: How are the accountants going to handle the extra work now that two of them have left the company? B: The manager has bought new accounting software that can prepare reports and send invoices by itself, so the remaining staff will save several hours of work every week.","t":"A：既然有兩位會計離職了，剩下的會計要怎麼處理多出來的工作？ B：經理買了新的會計【軟體】，可以自動準備報表和寄送發票，所以留下來的員工每週能省下好幾個小時的工作。"},{"w":"program","p":"n.","d":"a set of instructions that makes a computer do a task","c":"程式","s":"A: Why is Kevin still sitting at his desk so late when everyone else from the IT team went home hours ago? B: He is writing a small computer program that will check our stock levels every night and email a list of low items to the warehouse manager before the morning shift begins.","t":"A：IT團隊其他人幾個小時前就回家了，為什麼凱文這麼晚還坐在桌前？ B：他正在寫一個小型電腦【程式】，每晚會檢查我們的庫存量，並在早班開始前把缺貨品項清單寄給倉庫經理。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a program made for one particular job, especially on a phone","c":"應用程式","s":"A: Is there an easier way for our sales staff to record their travel costs while they are visiting clients in other cities? B: Yes, the finance department has just introduced a mobile application, so staff can take a photo of each receipt with their phone and send it for approval right away.","t":"A：我們的業務員在其他城市拜訪客戶時，有沒有更簡單的方式記錄差旅費用？ B：有，財務部剛推出一款手機【應用程式】，員工可以用手機拍下每張收據，並立刻送出申請核准。"},{"w":"system","p":"n.","d":"a group of computer programs and equipment that work together","c":"系統","s":"A: Why did it take so long to check in at the hotel last night when there were only a few guests in the lobby? B: The booking system stopped working for almost an hour, so the receptionists had to write every guest's details by hand and call the manager to confirm the room numbers.","t":"A：昨晚大廳只有幾位客人，為什麼辦理入住還花了那麼久？ B：訂房【系統】停擺了將近一小時，所以櫃檯人員必須手寫每位客人的資料，還要打電話給經理確認房號。"},{"w":"processor","p":"n.","d":"the main part of a computer that carries out instructions","c":"處理器","s":"A: Why does the marketing team want to replace their laptops when they are only two years old? B: They now edit large video files every day, and the processor in their current machines is too slow, so each video takes hours to finish and they often miss deadlines.","t":"A：行銷團隊的筆電才用兩年，為什麼想要換掉？ B：他們現在每天都要剪輯大型影片檔，而現有電腦的【處理器】太慢，所以每支影片都要花好幾個小時才完成，他們常常趕不上截止期限。"},{"w":"memory","p":"n.","d":"the part of a computer that holds information while it is working","c":"記憶體","s":"A: Why does my computer freeze every time I open the sales spreadsheet and join a video call at the same time? B: Your laptop only has a small amount of memory, so it cannot run several large programs together; I will order an upgrade for you, and it should be ready by Friday.","t":"A：為什麼我每次同時打開銷售試算表和加入視訊會議時，電腦就會當機？ B：你的筆電只有很小的【記憶體】，所以無法同時執行好幾個大型程式；我會幫你訂購升級，星期五前應該就會弄好。"},{"w":"storage","p":"n.","d":"space for keeping computer data","c":"儲存（空間）","s":"A: Where should we keep all the photos and videos from the company's annual trade show so that everyone can find them later? B: Let's put them in the cloud storage account that the IT department set up last year, because it has plenty of space and staff in every branch can access it.","t":"A：公司年度商展的所有照片和影片要存在哪裡，大家以後才找得到？ B：我們放到IT部門去年設立的雲端【儲存】帳號吧，因為空間很充足，而且每家分公司的員工都能存取。"},{"w":"file","p":"n.","d":"a set of information stored on a computer under one name","c":"檔案","s":"A: Could you send me the latest version of the price list before my meeting with the new client this afternoon? B: Sure, I'll attach the file to an email right now, but please check the prices on page two carefully, because the supplier changed some of them yesterday morning.","t":"A：今天下午我和新客戶開會前，你可以把最新版的價目表寄給我嗎？ B：當然，我現在就把【檔案】附在電子郵件裡寄給你，不過請仔細確認第二頁的價格，因為供應商昨天早上改了一些。"},{"w":"folder","p":"n.","d":"a place on a computer where you keep files together","c":"資料夾","s":"A: I can't find the training documents for the new employees who are starting next Monday; where did you put them? B: They are all in a shared folder called \"New Staff\" on the company drive, and I have already given the department managers permission to open and edit them.","t":"A：我找不到下週一要報到的新員工訓練文件，你放在哪裡？ B：全部都在公司雲端硬碟上一個叫「新進員工」的共用【資料夾】裡，我已經授權各部門主管開啟和編輯了。"},{"w":"keyboard","p":"n.","d":"the set of keys you press to type on a computer","c":"鍵盤","s":"A: Why did you ask the office manager for new equipment when your computer is working perfectly well? B: Some of the letters on my keyboard have worn off after years of typing reports, and the space bar often sticks, so I make a lot of spelling mistakes in my emails.","t":"A：你的電腦運作得很正常，為什麼還向辦公室經理申請新設備？ B：打了好幾年報告，我的【鍵盤】上有些字母已經磨掉了，空白鍵也常卡住，所以我寫電子郵件時常打錯字。"},{"w":"mouse","p":"n.","d":"a small device you move by hand to control the cursor on a screen","c":"滑鼠","s":"A: Do you need anything else for your home office now that you are working from home three days a week? B: A new mouse would be helpful, because my old one doesn't move the cursor smoothly, and it takes me a long time to select and drag items when I design presentation slides.","t":"A：既然你現在每週有三天在家工作，你的居家辦公室還需要什麼嗎？ B：一個新的【滑鼠】會很有幫助，因為我的舊滑鼠游標移動不順，我設計簡報投影片時要花很久才能選取和拖曳物件。"},{"w":"screen","p":"n.","d":"the flat surface of a computer or phone where you see pictures and words","c":"螢幕","s":"A: Why are you sitting so close to your laptop when you are just reading a simple report? B: The screen is very small, and the letters are hard to see in this bright room, so I'm going to ask the IT department for a larger monitor before I start working on the budget.","t":"A：你只是在讀一份簡單的報告，為什麼坐得離筆電這麼近？ B：【螢幕】很小，在這麼亮的房間裡字很難看清楚，所以我開始做預算之前，要先向IT部門要一台比較大的顯示器。"},{"w":"monitor","p":"n.","d":"a separate screen that shows information from a computer","c":"顯示器；螢幕","s":"A: How can I work faster when I have to compare two long contracts and write a summary for my manager every day? B: You should ask for a second monitor, so you can open one contract on each side of your desk and type your notes without switching between windows all the time.","t":"A：我每天都要比對兩份很長的合約並幫主管寫摘要，要怎麼做才能更快？ B：你應該申請第二台【顯示器】，這樣你可以在桌子兩邊各開一份合約，不用一直切換視窗就能打筆記。"},{"w":"network","p":"n.","d":"a group of computers that are connected so they can share information","c":"網路；網絡","s":"A: Why couldn't anyone in the office print documents or open shared files this morning? B: The company's computer network went down after a storm damaged some cables near the building, so none of our machines could connect to each other until the technicians fixed it at noon.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上辦公室裡沒有人能列印文件或打開共用檔案？ B：暴風雨損壞了大樓附近的一些電纜，公司的電腦【網路】因此中斷，所以在技術人員中午修好之前，我們所有的電腦都無法互相連線。"},{"w":"internet","p":"n.","d":"the worldwide system that connects computers so people can share information","c":"網際網路；網路","s":"A: Is it a good idea to hold the training workshop at the hotel near the airport next month? B: The rooms are comfortable, but the internet connection there is very slow, so our trainers won't be able to show online videos or let participants join from other offices.","t":"A：下個月在機場附近的飯店舉辦培訓工作坊是好主意嗎？ B：那裡的房間很舒適，但【網路】連線很慢，所以我們的講師無法播放線上影片，也不能讓學員從其他辦公室遠端參加。"},{"w":"browser","p":"n.","d":"a program used to look at websites","c":"瀏覽器","s":"A: Why can't I open the new booking website that the travel agency sent us for the sales trip? B: You are still using a very old web browser that doesn't support the site, so please download the latest version of Chrome or Edge and then try the link again.","t":"A：為什麼我打不開旅行社寄給我們、為出差準備的新訂位網站？ B：你還在用很舊的網頁【瀏覽器】，它不支援這個網站，所以請下載最新版的Chrome或Edge，然後再點一次連結。"},{"w":"download","p":"v.","d":"to copy information from the internet to your computer or phone","c":"下載","s":"A: How can the new staff read the company handbook before their first day if we don't mail them a printed copy? B: We'll email them a link this afternoon, so they can download the handbook to their laptop or phone and read it at home over the weekend.","t":"A：如果我們不寄紙本給新進員工，他們要怎麼在第一天上班前讀到員工手冊？ B：我們今天下午會寄連結給他們，這樣他們就能把手冊【下載】到筆電或手機上，週末在家閱讀。"},{"w":"upload","p":"v.","d":"to send information from your computer to the internet","c":"上傳","s":"A: How should the designers send their final drawings to the client in Tokyo, since the files are too large for email? B: They should upload the drawings to the project website before six o'clock tonight, and then the client's team can review them first thing tomorrow morning in Japan.","t":"A：設計師的最終設計圖檔案太大，無法用電子郵件寄送，要怎麼交給東京的客戶？ B：他們應該在今晚六點前把設計圖【上傳】到專案網站，這樣客戶團隊明天早上一上班就能在日本審閱。"},{"w":"install","p":"v.","d":"to put a program or piece of equipment in place so it is ready to use","c":"安裝","s":"A: When will the new security cameras in the parking garage be ready to use? B: The technicians will install them this weekend while the building is closed, and after they test the recording equipment on Monday, the guards will be able to watch the garage from the front desk.","t":"A：停車場的新監視器什麼時候可以使用？ B：技術人員會在本週末大樓關閉時【安裝】，週一測試錄影設備之後，警衛就能從櫃檯監看停車場。"},{"w":"update","p":"v.","d":"to add the newest information or make something more modern","c":"更新","s":"A: The address on our website still shows our old office, and several customers went there by mistake yesterday; who can fix it? B: I'll ask Tina from the web team to update the contact page this morning, and she can also add a map that shows how to get here from the station.","t":"A：我們網站上的地址還是舊辦公室的，昨天有好幾位顧客走錯地方，誰能修正？ B：我今天早上會請網站團隊的蒂娜【更新】聯絡頁面，她也可以加一張從車站到這裡的地圖。"},{"w":"save","p":"v.","d":"to store work on a computer so you do not lose it","c":"儲存；存檔","s":"A: What happened to the sales report that you spent the whole afternoon writing yesterday? B: The power went off suddenly at five o'clock, and I had forgotten to save my work, so I lost almost everything and had to start again early this morning before my manager arrived.","t":"A：你昨天花了整個下午寫的銷售報告怎麼了？ B：五點時突然停電，而我忘了【存檔】，所以幾乎全部都不見了，今天一大早只好在主管到之前重新開始。"},{"w":"delete","p":"v.","d":"to remove something from a computer","c":"刪除","s":"A: Why is the shared drive so full that nobody in the department can add new documents this week? B: People have kept old photos and copies of the same reports for years, so the manager has asked everyone to delete any files they no longer need before Friday.","t":"A：為什麼共用硬碟滿到這週部門裡沒人能新增文件？ B：大家多年來一直保留舊照片和同樣報告的副本，所以經理要求每個人在星期五前【刪除】不再需要的檔案。"},{"w":"digital","p":"adj.","d":"using computer technology instead of paper","c":"數位的","s":"A: Are we still going to print the restaurant's new menu on paper, like we did last year? B: No, we are switching to a digital menu that customers can read on their phones by scanning a code on the table, which saves printing costs and lets us change prices easily.","t":"A：我們還要像去年一樣把餐廳的新菜單印在紙上嗎？ B：不，我們要改用【數位】菜單，客人掃描桌上的條碼就能在手機上閱讀，這樣可以省下印刷費，也能輕鬆更改價格。"},{"w":"online","p":"adj.","d":"connected to or available through the internet","c":"線上的；網路上的","s":"A: Why have the bookstore's sales improved so much this year even though fewer people are visiting the shop? B: The owner opened an online store last spring, so customers can now order books from home at any time, and many of them also choose next-day delivery.","t":"A：為什麼今年書店的來客變少，銷售額卻大幅提升？ B：老闆去年春天開了一家【線上】商店，現在顧客隨時都能在家訂書，而且很多人還選擇隔日到貨。"},{"w":"wireless","p":"adj.","d":"working without cables or wires","c":"無線的","s":"A: Why are there no more cables lying on the floor of the meeting room since the renovation last month? B: The company replaced the old equipment with wireless speakers, keyboards and projectors, so everything now connects through the air, and people no longer trip over wires during presentations.","t":"A：自從上個月整修後，會議室地板上為什麼再也沒有電線了？ B：公司把舊設備換成了【無線】喇叭、鍵盤和投影機，現在所有設備都不用接線就能連接，大家在簡報時不會再被電線絆倒。"},{"w":"virtual","p":"adj.","d":"done or seen on a computer instead of in person","c":"虛擬的；線上的","s":"A: Will the managers from our overseas branches fly to Taipei for the planning meeting in December? B: No, travel costs are too high this year, so we will hold a virtual meeting instead, and everyone will join by video from their own offices in Singapore, Seoul and Sydney.","t":"A：海外分公司的經理們會飛來台北參加十二月的規劃會議嗎？ B：不會，今年差旅費太高了，所以我們會改開【虛擬】會議，大家從新加坡、首爾和雪梨各自的辦公室用視訊參加。"},{"w":"automatic","p":"adj.","d":"working by itself without a person controlling it","c":"自動的","s":"A: Do I need to remember to back up my work files every evening before I leave the office? B: No, the IT department set up an automatic backup last month, so the system copies all your documents to the server at midnight without anyone having to press a button.","t":"A：我每天傍晚離開辦公室前，需要記得備份工作檔案嗎？ B：不用，IT部門上個月設定了【自動】備份，系統每天午夜會把你所有的文件複製到伺服器，不需要任何人按按鈕。"},{"w":"secure","p":"adj.","d":"safe and protected from danger or attack","c":"安全的","s":"A: Is it safe for our staff to check their work email on the free Wi-Fi at the airport or in coffee shops? B: Not really, because public networks are often not very secure, so please always turn on the company's VPN first to protect customer information from hackers.","t":"A：我們的員工在機場或咖啡店用免費Wi-Fi查看公司郵件安全嗎？ B：不太安全，因為公共網路通常不太【安全】，所以請一定先開啟公司的VPN，保護客戶資料不被駭客竊取。"},{"w":"quickly","p":"adv.","d":"fast; in a short time","c":"快速地；迅速地","s":"A: How did you finish entering all the customer orders before the deadline when the office was so busy yesterday? B: I used the new shortcut keys that the trainer showed us, which helped me type much more quickly, and I finished the whole list an hour before the warehouse closed.","t":"A：昨天辦公室那麼忙，你是怎麼在截止前輸入完所有顧客訂單的？ B：我用了講師教我們的新快捷鍵，讓我能更【快速地】打字，在倉庫關門前一小時就完成了整份清單。"},{"w":"efficiently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that uses time and energy well","c":"有效率地","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to buy new scanners for the reception desk this year? B: The old machines kept jamming, and the new ones can scan fifty pages a minute, so the receptionists can work more efficiently and spend more time helping visitors instead of fixing paper problems.","t":"A：經理今年為什麼決定為接待櫃檯買新的掃描器？ B：舊機器一直卡紙，新機器每分鐘能掃描五十頁，所以接待人員能更【有效率地】工作，花更多時間協助訪客，而不是處理卡紙問題。"},{"w":"remotely","p":"adv.","d":"from a distance, not in the same place","c":"遠端地；遠距地","s":"A: How did the technician fix my computer problem yesterday when he was working from home because of the typhoon? B: He connected to your laptop remotely through a special program, so he could control your screen from his house and repair the settings without coming into the office.","t":"A：昨天因為颱風技術人員在家工作，他是怎麼修好我的電腦問題的？ B：他透過一個特殊程式【遠端】連上你的筆電，所以能從家裡控制你的螢幕並修正設定，不用進辦公室。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often, at the same times each day, week, month, etc.","c":"定期地；經常地","s":"A: What can our team do to protect the company's data after the attack on our competitor's computers last month? B: Everyone should change their passwords regularly, about every three months, and the IT staff will also check the system every Friday to find any weak points before hackers do.","t":"A：上個月競爭對手的電腦遭到攻擊後，我們團隊可以做什麼來保護公司資料？ B：每個人都應該【定期】更換密碼，大約每三個月一次，IT人員每週五也會檢查系統，在駭客之前找出任何弱點。"}]},{"unit":74,"theme":"Concentration 專注","cards":[{"w":"focus","p":"n.","d":"the main thing that you pay attention to","c":"焦點；重點；專注","s":"A: Why did the manager cancel the two new projects that the design team had been planning since the spring? B: She wants the department to keep its focus on finishing the mobile app before the December launch, because the client will pay a large bonus if everything is delivered on time.","t":"A：為什麼經理取消了設計團隊從春天就開始規劃的兩個新專案？ B：她希望部門把【焦點】放在十二月上市前完成手機應用程式，因為如果一切準時交付，客戶會支付一大筆獎金。"},{"w":"attention","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching, listening to or thinking about something carefully","c":"注意力；注意","s":"A: Why do the trainers always start their afternoon workshops with a short game instead of going straight to the slides? B: After a big lunch, most employees feel sleepy, so a quick activity helps everyone get their attention back before the trainers explain the new safety rules for the factory.","t":"A：為什麼講師下午的工作坊總是先玩個小遊戲，而不是直接看投影片？ B：吃完豐盛的午餐後，大多數員工都會想睡，所以一個簡短的活動能幫大家在講師說明工廠新的安全規定之前找回【注意力】。"},{"w":"absorption","p":"n.","d":"the state of being so interested in something that you notice nothing else","c":"全神貫注；專心","s":"A: Why didn't Kevin answer when the receptionist called his name three times in the waiting room this morning? B: He was reading the contract for his new apartment with such complete absorption that he didn't hear anything around him, so she finally had to walk over and tap him on the shoulder.","t":"A：今天早上接待員在候診室叫了凱文的名字三次，他為什麼都沒回應？ B：他閱讀新公寓的合約時完全【全神貫注】，絲毫沒聽到周圍的聲音，所以她最後只好走過去拍拍他的肩膀。"},{"w":"awareness","p":"n.","d":"knowing about something or understanding that it is important","c":"意識；認識","s":"A: Why is the hotel putting small signs about saving water and electricity in every guest room this year? B: The owners want to raise awareness of environmental problems among travelers, and they hope guests will reuse their towels and turn off the lights when they leave the room.","t":"A：為什麼飯店今年要在每間客房放置節約用水和用電的小告示？ B：業主希望提高旅客對環境問題的【意識】，也希望房客重複使用毛巾，並在離開房間時關燈。"},{"w":"distraction","p":"n.","d":"something that takes your attention away from what you are doing","c":"使人分心的事物；干擾","s":"A: Why did the office manager ask everyone to turn off their phone notifications during the monthly planning meeting? B: She said the constant beeping was a big distraction for the speakers, and last month the meeting ran almost an hour longer because people kept checking their messages instead of listening.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理要求大家在每月規劃會議期間關閉手機通知？ B：她說不斷的嗶嗶聲對講者來說是很大的【干擾】，而且上個月的會議延長了將近一小時，因為大家一直查看訊息而沒有專心聽。"},{"w":"interruption","p":"n.","d":"a short time when something stops before it continues again","c":"打斷；中斷","s":"A: How did the online training session for the new accounting software go yesterday afternoon? B: Not very well, because there was an interruption in the internet service halfway through, so we lost the connection for twenty minutes and had to repeat the most important part today.","t":"A：昨天下午新會計軟體的線上訓練課程進行得如何？ B：不太順利，因為課程進行到一半網路服務【中斷】，我們斷線了二十分鐘，今天只好重上最重要的部分。"},{"w":"mindfulness","p":"n.","d":"the practice of calmly paying attention to the present moment","c":"正念；留心當下","s":"A: What is the new program that the human resources department started for staff who feel stressed at work? B: Every Wednesday morning, a coach leads a short mindfulness class in the meeting room, where employees learn to breathe slowly and pay attention to the present moment before they start their busy day.","t":"A：人資部門為工作壓力大的員工推出的新課程是什麼？ B：每週三早上，一位教練會在會議室帶領簡短的【正念】課程，員工在開始忙碌的一天之前，學習慢慢呼吸並專注於當下。"},{"w":"engagement","p":"n.","d":"the state of being interested and involved in something","c":"投入；參與","s":"A: Why does the company send a short survey to every employee at the end of each year? B: The managers want to measure staff engagement, because they have found that workers who feel involved and valued usually stay longer, work harder and give better service to customers.","t":"A：為什麼公司每年年底都會寄一份簡短的問卷給每位員工？ B：主管們想要衡量員工的【投入程度】，因為他們發現覺得自己有參與感且受到重視的員工，通常會待得更久、工作更努力，也給顧客更好的服務。"},{"w":"immersion","p":"n.","d":"being completely involved in an activity or surrounded by a language or culture","c":"沉浸；投入","s":"A: How did the sales director learn to speak Japanese so well in only one year before moving to the Tokyo office? B: She took a three-month immersion course in Osaka, where she lived with a local family and was only allowed to use Japanese in class, in shops and at dinner every day.","t":"A：業務總監在調到東京辦公室之前，怎麼能在短短一年內把日文說得這麼好？ B：她在大阪上了三個月的【沉浸式】課程，在那裡和當地家庭同住，每天在課堂上、商店裡和晚餐時都只能說日文。"},{"w":"concentrate","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to one thing","c":"專心；集中注意力","s":"A: Why have you started coming to the office at seven in the morning, two hours before everyone else arrives? B: It is the only time of day when I can really concentrate on the monthly sales reports, because after nine the phones ring constantly and people keep stopping by my desk with questions.","t":"A：你為什麼開始早上七點就來辦公室，比其他人早兩個小時？ B：那是一天當中我唯一能真正【專心】處理每月銷售報告的時間，因為九點以後電話一直響，而且大家不斷來我桌前問問題。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to deal with or take care of someone or something (usually attend to)","c":"處理；照顧（attend to）","s":"A: Why isn't the store manager at the meeting with the new suppliers this afternoon? B: She had to attend to an angry customer who wanted a refund for a broken coffee machine, but she said she would join us as soon as the problem was solved at the front desk.","t":"A：店經理為什麼沒參加今天下午和新供應商的會議？ B：她必須【處理】一位要求為壞掉的咖啡機退款的生氣顧客，但她說等櫃台的問題解決後就會馬上加入我們。"},{"w":"absorb","p":"v.","d":"to take in and understand information","c":"吸收；理解","s":"A: Why did the trainer give the new bank tellers a whole week to read the customer service handbook? B: The handbook contains a lot of rules and procedures, and it is difficult to absorb so much information in one or two days, especially when you are also learning the computer system.","t":"A：為什麼講師給新進銀行行員一整週的時間閱讀客服手冊？ B：手冊裡有很多規定和流程，要在一兩天內【吸收】這麼多資訊很困難，特別是同時還要學習電腦系統。"},{"w":"ignore","p":"v.","d":"to pay no attention to something or someone","c":"忽略；不理會","s":"A: How do you manage to finish so much work at your desk when the open-plan office is so noisy all day? B: I wear headphones and try to ignore the conversations around me, and I only check my email twice a day so that I don't keep stopping in the middle of a task.","t":"A：開放式辦公室整天都那麼吵，你是怎麼在座位上完成這麼多工作的？ B：我戴上耳機，試著【忽略】周圍的談話聲，而且一天只查看兩次電子郵件，這樣就不會在做事做到一半時一直停下來。"},{"w":"refocus","p":"v.","d":"to give your attention or effort to something again or to something new","c":"重新集中；重新聚焦","s":"A: Our sales have dropped for three months in a row, so what is the new plan from the marketing director? B: She wants us to refocus our efforts on our loyal customers in Taipei and Kaohsiung, because many of them have stopped buying from us since our main competitor lowered its prices last spring.","t":"A：我們的銷售額已連續三個月下滑，行銷總監的新計畫是什麼？ B：她希望我們把心力【重新集中】在台北和高雄的忠實顧客上，因為自從我們的主要競爭對手去年春天降價後，他們很多人都不再向我們購買了。"},{"w":"attentive","p":"adj.","d":"listening or watching carefully; helpful and caring toward others","c":"專心的；體貼周到的","s":"A: Why do so many business travelers choose that small hotel near the convention center instead of the bigger ones? B: The rooms are simple, but the staff are very attentive, and they remember each guest's name, arrange taxis early in the morning and even prepare breakfast boxes for people who leave before seven.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多商務旅客選擇會議中心附近那間小飯店，而不是比較大的飯店？ B：房間雖然簡單，但員工非常【體貼周到】，他們記得每位房客的名字，一大早幫忙叫計程車，甚至為七點前就出門的人準備早餐盒。"},{"w":"focused","p":"adj.","d":"paying full attention to one aim or task","c":"專注的；集中的","s":"A: How did the new project leader finish the website redesign two weeks earlier than the deadline? B: She stayed focused on the most important features, held very short daily meetings, and politely said no whenever other departments asked her team to add extra pages that were not in the plan.","t":"A：新的專案負責人是怎麼比截止日期提早兩週完成網站改版的？ B：她始終【專注】於最重要的功能，每天只開很短的會議，而且只要其他部門要求她的團隊加入計畫外的頁面，她都會禮貌地拒絕。"},{"w":"alert","p":"adj.","d":"awake and quick to notice things","c":"警覺的；機靈的","s":"A: Why does the warehouse supervisor insist that forklift drivers take a fifteen-minute break every two hours? B: Driving those heavy machines for a long time makes people tired, and drivers must stay alert at all times because one small mistake could hurt a coworker or damage expensive goods.","t":"A：為什麼倉庫主管堅持堆高機駕駛每兩小時要休息十五分鐘？ B：長時間駕駛那些重型機具會讓人疲倦，而駕駛必須隨時保持【警覺】，因為一個小錯誤就可能傷到同事或損壞昂貴的貨物。"},{"w":"absorbed","p":"adj.","d":"so interested in something that you notice nothing else","c":"全神貫注的；專心的","s":"A: Did you notice that the lights went off on the third floor while you were working late last night? B: No, I was so absorbed in the budget report for next year that I didn't notice anything until the security guard knocked on my door and told me the building was closing.","t":"A：你昨晚加班時，有注意到三樓的燈熄了嗎？ B：沒有，我太【專心】於明年的預算報告，完全沒注意到任何事，直到警衛來敲門告訴我大樓要關門了。"},{"w":"distracted","p":"adj.","d":"unable to pay attention because you are thinking about something else","c":"分心的","s":"A: Why did Linda make so many mistakes in the shipping orders she entered on Friday afternoon? B: She was distracted because her son was sick at home and she kept checking her phone for messages from the babysitter, so the manager has given her a day off to take care of him.","t":"A：琳達週五下午輸入的出貨訂單為什麼錯這麼多？ B：她當時【分心】了，因為兒子在家生病，她一直查看手機看保母有沒有傳訊息，所以經理讓她休假一天去照顧他。"},{"w":"engaged","p":"adj.","d":"interested and taking an active part in something","c":"投入的；參與的","s":"A: What did you think of the guest speaker who talked about online marketing at the conference yesterday? B: She was excellent, because she asked the audience questions and used funny examples, so everyone stayed engaged for the whole hour, and many people wanted to talk to her after the session.","t":"A：你覺得昨天研討會上談網路行銷的客座講者怎麼樣？ B：她很棒，因為她會問聽眾問題，還舉了有趣的例子，所以大家整整一小時都很【投入】，很多人在講座結束後還想跟她聊聊。"},{"w":"mindful","p":"adj.","d":"remembering something and thinking about it carefully","c":"留意的；注意的","s":"A: Is there anything I should remember before I give the presentation to our new partners from Saudi Arabia next week? B: Be mindful of their cultural customs, so avoid scheduling the meeting during prayer times, and don't be surprised if they want to build a friendly relationship before they talk about business.","t":"A：下週我要向來自沙烏地阿拉伯的新夥伴做簡報，有什麼需要記住的事嗎？ B：要【留意】他們的文化習俗，所以避免把會議安排在禱告時間，而且如果他們想先建立友好關係再談生意，也不要感到驚訝。"},{"w":"steady","p":"adj.","d":"continuing or developing in a regular way without big changes","c":"穩定的；平穩的","s":"A: How is the new coffee shop on the ground floor of our office building doing after its first three months? B: The owner told me business has been steady, with about two hundred customers every weekday, and she plans to add sandwiches and salads to the menu so that office workers can buy lunch there too.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓一樓新開的咖啡店開幕三個月後經營得如何？ B：老闆告訴我生意一直很【穩定】，每個平日約有兩百位顧客，她打算在菜單上加入三明治和沙拉，讓上班族也能在那裡買午餐。"},{"w":"deeply","p":"adv.","d":"very much; strongly","c":"深深地；非常","s":"A: How did the staff react when the factory manager announced that he would retire at the end of the year? B: Many workers were deeply moved, because he had worked there for thirty-five years, and he always remembered everyone's birthday and helped families when they were having difficult times.","t":"A：工廠經理宣布他將在年底退休時，員工有什麼反應？ B：許多員工都【深深地】受到感動，因為他在那裡工作了三十五年，總是記得每個人的生日，並在大家遇到困難時幫助他們的家人。"},{"w":"carefully","p":"adv.","d":"with great attention so that you avoid mistakes","c":"仔細地；小心地","s":"A: Is there anything special I should do before I sign the lease for the new branch office downtown? B: Yes, read every page carefully, especially the part about repairs and rent increases, because last time we missed a small sentence and had to pay for a new air conditioner ourselves.","t":"A：簽下市中心新分公司的租約前，有什麼特別需要做的嗎？ B：有，要【仔細地】閱讀每一頁，特別是有關維修和調漲租金的部分，因為上次我們漏看了一個小句子，結果只好自己出錢買新冷氣。"},{"w":"closely","p":"adv.","d":"with careful attention; in a way that involves working together a lot","c":"密切地；仔細地","s":"A: Why does the quality control team check every tenth bottle on the production line so often these days? B: After a customer found a crack in one of our bottles last month, the director asked us to watch the machines closely and report even the smallest problem immediately to the engineering department.","t":"A：品管團隊最近為什麼這麼頻繁地檢查生產線上每第十瓶產品？ B：上個月有位顧客在我們的一個瓶子上發現裂痕後，主管要我們【密切地】監看機器，即使是最小的問題也要立刻回報工程部。"},{"w":"fully","p":"adv.","d":"completely","c":"完全地；充分地","s":"A: Can the new employees start working at the front desk of the hotel on Monday morning? B: Not yet, because they will not be fully trained until the end of next week, and they still need to learn how to use the booking system and deal with guests who want to change their rooms.","t":"A：新員工星期一早上可以開始在飯店櫃台工作嗎？ B：還不行，因為他們要到下週末才會【完全】受訓完成，還需要學會使用訂房系統，以及處理想要換房間的房客。"},{"w":"intently","p":"adv.","d":"with great attention and interest","c":"專注地；專心地","s":"A: Why was everyone so quiet during the meeting when the chief financial officer explained the new budget? B: People listened intently because she was talking about which departments would lose money next year, and many managers were worried that their teams might become smaller after the changes.","t":"A：財務長說明新預算時，會議中為什麼大家都那麼安靜？ B：大家都【專注地】聆聽，因為她在講明年哪些部門會被刪減經費，許多經理擔心改變之後他們的團隊可能會縮編。"},{"w":"calmly","p":"adv.","d":"in a quiet way, without getting upset or excited","c":"冷靜地；平靜地","s":"A: What happened at the airport check-in counter when the flight to Singapore was canceled this morning? B: Many passengers were angry, but the airline agent explained the situation calmly, offered everyone a hotel room and a meal ticket, and booked them on the first flight tomorrow morning.","t":"A：今天早上飛往新加坡的班機取消時，機場報到櫃台發生了什麼事？ B：許多乘客很生氣，但航空公司人員【冷靜地】說明情況，提供每個人飯店房間和餐券，並幫他們訂了明天早上的第一班飛機。"},{"w":"consistently","p":"adv.","d":"always in the same way, especially in a good way","c":"一貫地；始終如一地","s":"A: Why did the company choose Maria as the Employee of the Year instead of someone from the sales team? B: She has consistently delivered excellent work for five years, she has never missed a deadline, and customers often send emails to thank her for solving their problems quickly and politely.","t":"A：公司為什麼選瑪莉亞當年度最佳員工，而不是業務團隊的人？ B：她五年來【始終如一地】交出優秀的成果，從未錯過任何截止期限，而且顧客常寄電子郵件感謝她迅速又有禮貌地解決問題。"},{"w":"briefly","p":"adv.","d":"for a short time; in a few words","c":"簡短地；短暫地","s":"A: The board meeting starts in ten minutes, so do I have time to explain the whole marketing plan? B: No, please describe it briefly in two or three minutes, and then send the full report by email afterward, because the directors have a long list of other topics to discuss this morning.","t":"A：董事會十分鐘後就要開始了，我有時間解釋整個行銷計畫嗎？ B：沒有，請用兩三分鐘【簡短地】說明，之後再用電子郵件寄送完整報告，因為董事們今天早上還有一長串其他議題要討論。"},{"w":"mentally","p":"adv.","d":"in the mind; relating to thinking and feelings","c":"心理上；精神上","s":"A: Why does the airline give its pilots so much rest time between long international flights? B: Flying for twelve hours is very tiring, and pilots need to be mentally prepared to make quick decisions in bad weather, so the company makes sure they sleep well before every trip.","t":"A：為什麼航空公司在長途國際航班之間給機師這麼多休息時間？ B：飛行十二小時非常累人，而機師需要在【心理上】做好準備，才能在惡劣天氣中迅速做決定，所以公司會確保他們每趟飛行前都睡得好。"},{"w":"actively","p":"adv.","d":"in a busy, energetic way; by taking action","c":"積極地；主動地","s":"A: How is your team preparing for the new branch opening in Singapore next spring? B: We are actively looking for local staff who speak English and Chinese, and next month two of our managers will fly there to meet possible partners and visit several office buildings.","t":"A：你們團隊如何為明年春天在新加坡開設新分公司做準備？ B：我們正【積極地】尋找會說英文和中文的當地員工，下個月我們有兩位經理會飛過去和潛在合作夥伴見面，並參觀幾棟辦公大樓。"}]},{"unit":75,"theme":"Conference 會議","cards":[{"w":"seminar","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where a small group learns about or discusses a subject with an expert","c":"研討會；專題討論會","s":"A: Why are half of the accountants leaving the office early this Thursday afternoon, when the quarterly report is due on Friday? B: The finance director signed them up for a free seminar on the new tax rules, and she wants them to learn the changes before they prepare next year's budget.","t":"A：為什麼一半的會計師這週四下午要提早離開辦公室，季報不是星期五就要交了嗎？ B：財務長幫他們報名了一場關於新稅法的免費【研討會】，她希望他們在準備明年預算之前先了解這些變動。"},{"w":"workshop","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where people learn a skill by doing practical activities together","c":"工作坊；研習會","s":"A: How did the new sales staff learn to answer difficult questions from customers so quickly? B: Last month they spent two full days in a hands-on workshop, where they practiced real phone calls in small groups and received useful advice from an experienced trainer after each round.","t":"A：新進業務人員怎麼這麼快就學會回答客戶的刁鑽問題？ B：上個月他們花了整整兩天參加一場實作【工作坊】，在小組中練習真實的電話對話，並在每一輪結束後得到資深講師的實用建議。"},{"w":"symposium","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting where experts give talks on one subject","c":"專題研討會；學術討論會","s":"A: Why has the hospital asked so many doctors from Japan and Korea to visit Taipei next spring? B: It is holding a three-day symposium on new heart treatments, and experts from several countries will give short talks and then answer questions from local doctors and nurses.","t":"A：為什麼醫院邀請這麼多日本和韓國的醫生明年春天來台北？ B：醫院將舉辦為期三天、主題是心臟新療法的【專題研討會】，來自多國的專家會發表簡短演講，然後回答本地醫師和護理師的問題。"},{"w":"summit","p":"n.","d":"an important meeting between leaders of governments or organizations","c":"高峰會","s":"A: Why are all the hotels near the exhibition center fully booked during the second week of May? B: Leaders from twenty countries will meet there for an economic summit about trade and energy, so thousands of reporters, guards and assistants need rooms close to the meeting halls.","t":"A：為什麼展覽中心附近的飯店在五月第二週全部客滿？ B：二十個國家的領袖將在那裡召開一場關於貿易和能源的經濟【高峰會】，所以上千名記者、警衛和助理都需要靠近會議廳的房間。"},{"w":"convention","p":"n.","d":"a large meeting of people from the same job or interest group","c":"大會；大型會議","s":"A: Why did you order so many extra brochures and samples for the booth this month? B: The yearly toy industry convention opens in Las Vegas next week, and more than ten thousand buyers usually visit, so we need enough materials to give to everyone who stops at our stand.","t":"A：你這個月為什麼為攤位多訂了這麼多手冊和樣品？ B：一年一度的玩具業【大會】下週在拉斯維加斯開幕，通常有超過一萬名買家參觀，所以我們需要足夠的資料，發給每一位在我們攤位停留的人。"},{"w":"forum","p":"n.","d":"a meeting or place where people discuss a topic and share ideas","c":"論壇；討論會","s":"A: How will the city government decide where to build the new bus station in our neighborhood? B: It is holding an open public forum at the community center on Saturday, where residents and shop owners can share their opinions before the mayor makes a final decision next month.","t":"A：市政府要怎麼決定在我們社區哪裡蓋新的公車站？ B：市府星期六會在社區中心舉辦一場公開【論壇】，居民和店家老闆可以在市長下個月做出最後決定之前，發表他們的意見。"},{"w":"session","p":"n.","d":"a period of time used for one activity, such as a meeting or class","c":"場次；一段時間；會議","s":"A: I arrived late because my train was delayed, so did I miss anything important at the training this morning? B: You only missed the first session about safety rules, but the trainer said she will email the slides to everyone, and the hands-on part begins after the coffee break.","t":"A：我因為火車誤點遲到了，今天早上的訓練我有錯過什麼重要的內容嗎？ B：你只錯過了關於安全規定的第一個【場次】，不過講師說她會把投影片寄給每個人，而實作部分在咖啡休息後才開始。"},{"w":"agenda","p":"n.","d":"a list of topics to be discussed at a meeting","c":"議程","s":"A: Should I prepare anything before the board meeting tomorrow, since this is my first time joining it? B: Yes, please read the agenda I sent you last night, because the budget and the new office lease are the first two topics, and the chairman may ask for your opinion on both.","t":"A：明天的董事會我是第一次參加，需要事先準備什麼嗎？ B：需要，請先看我昨晚寄給你的【議程】，因為預算和新辦公室租約是頭兩個議題，主席可能會詢問你對這兩件事的意見。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists the times when things will happen","c":"時間表；行程表","s":"A: Do you know what time the keynote speaker will start, because I have a client call at ten? B: According to the printed schedule at the front desk, her talk begins at nine thirty and lasts forty-five minutes, so you should be able to leave the hall in time.","t":"A：你知道主講人幾點開始嗎？因為我十點要跟客戶通電話。 B：根據服務台印好的【時間表】，她的演講九點半開始，持續四十五分鐘，所以你應該來得及離開會場。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk that gives information about a new product, idea or piece of work","c":"簡報；報告","s":"A: Why were you still in the office so late last night when everyone else had already gone home? B: I had to finish the slides for my presentation to the new client from Singapore, because the meeting starts at nine this morning and my manager wanted to check them first.","t":"A：昨晚其他人都回家了，你為什麼還那麼晚待在辦公室？ B：我得完成要給新加坡新客戶的【簡報】投影片，因為會議今天早上九點開始，而且經理想先檢查一遍。"},{"w":"lecture","p":"n.","d":"a long talk on a subject, especially to students or a group","c":"演講；講座","s":"A: Are you going to the library this evening, or are you joining us for dinner after the meeting? B: Neither, because a famous economist from London is giving a free lecture on online shopping trends at the university tonight, and I want to take notes for our marketing plan.","t":"A：你今晚要去圖書館，還是開完會跟我們去吃晚餐？ B：都不是，今晚有位倫敦的知名經濟學家在大學舉辦一場關於網路購物趨勢的免費【講座】，我想去做筆記，用在我們的行銷計畫上。"},{"w":"speech","p":"n.","d":"a formal talk given to an audience","c":"演說；致詞","s":"A: Why does the CEO look so nervous today, even though she usually seems very calm at company events? B: She has to give a speech at the opening dinner tonight in front of five hundred guests, including the mayor and several major investors, and she is worried about forgetting her lines.","t":"A：執行長平常在公司活動都很冷靜，今天為什麼看起來這麼緊張？ B：她今晚要在開幕晚宴上，對包括市長和幾位大投資人在內的五百位來賓發表【演說】，她很擔心會忘詞。"},{"w":"panel","p":"n.","d":"a small group of experts who discuss a topic or make decisions in front of others","c":"專題小組；座談小組","s":"A: Who will answer questions about the new travel rules at the tourism meeting this afternoon? B: A panel of four experts, including an airline manager and a hotel owner, will discuss the changes on stage, and then the audience can ask them questions for about thirty minutes.","t":"A：今天下午的觀光會議上，誰會回答關於新旅遊規定的問題？ B：一個由四位專家組成的【座談小組】，包括一位航空公司經理和一位飯店老闆，會在台上討論這些變動，之後觀眾可以向他們提問約三十分鐘。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a talk between people about a subject, in which ideas are shared","c":"討論","s":"A: Did the managers agree on how to reduce costs at the meeting yesterday afternoon? B: Not yet, because after a long discussion about cutting staff or closing the small branch, they decided to collect more information and meet again next Tuesday before making any final choice.","t":"A：昨天下午的會議上，經理們對於如何降低成本達成共識了嗎？ B：還沒有，在針對裁員或關閉小分行進行一番冗長的【討論】之後，他們決定再收集更多資料，下週二再開會，然後才做最後決定。"},{"w":"networking","p":"n.","d":"meeting people at events to make useful business contacts","c":"建立人脈；交流","s":"A: Why did you stay at the reception so long after the last talk ended yesterday evening? B: It was a great chance for networking, because many buyers from Europe were there, and I exchanged business cards with six people who might become important clients for our company next year.","t":"A：昨晚最後一場演講結束後，你為什麼在招待會待那麼久？ B：那是個【建立人脈】的好機會，因為很多歐洲買家都在場，我跟六個明年可能成為我們公司重要客戶的人交換了名片。"},{"w":"delegate","p":"n.","d":"a person chosen to represent a group at a meeting","c":"代表","s":"A: Who is going to speak for our branch at the company's global meeting in Tokyo this summer? B: The staff voted for Ms. Lin as our delegate, because she knows the local market well, and she will share our ideas and report back to us when she returns.","t":"A：今年夏天在東京舉行的公司全球會議，誰會代表我們分公司發言？ B：員工投票選出林小姐擔任我們的【代表】，因為她很了解本地市場，她會分享我們的想法，回來後再向我們報告。"},{"w":"attendee","p":"n.","d":"a person who goes to a meeting or event","c":"出席者；與會者","s":"A: What should we put in the welcome bags for the trade show next week? B: Every attendee should get a name badge, a map of the hall, a bottle of water and a list of restaurants nearby, because many visitors are coming from abroad and don't know the area.","t":"A：下週商展的迎賓袋裡應該放什麼？ B：每位【與會者】都應該拿到一張名牌、一份會場地圖、一瓶水和一份附近餐廳的清單，因為很多訪客來自國外，不熟悉這一帶。"},{"w":"organizer","p":"n.","d":"a person who plans and arranges an event","c":"主辦人；籌辦者","s":"A: Who should I call if the projector in Room B stops working during my talk tomorrow? B: Call the event organizer, Mr. Chen, because he is in charge of the rooms and equipment, and his phone number is printed on the back of your name badge.","t":"A：如果明天我演講時B會議室的投影機壞了，我該打電話給誰？ B：打給活動【主辦人】陳先生，因為他負責場地和設備，他的電話號碼印在你名牌的背面。"},{"w":"host","p":"v.","d":"to organize an event and welcome the guests who come to it","c":"主辦；舉辦","s":"A: Why is our hotel hiring so many part-time waiters and cleaners for the first week of October? B: We will host a large medical conference with almost two thousand guests, so we need extra staff to serve meals, clean the rooms and help visitors find their meeting halls.","t":"A：為什麼我們飯店十月第一週要招募這麼多兼職服務生和清潔人員？ B：我們將【主辦】一場將近兩千名賓客的大型醫學會議，所以需要額外人手供餐、打掃房間，並幫助訪客找到他們的會議廳。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event such as a meeting or class","c":"出席；參加","s":"A: Can you meet the supplier from Vietnam on Wednesday morning, or are you busy that day? B: I'm sorry, but I have to attend a training course on the new accounting software all day Wednesday, so could we move the meeting to Thursday afternoon instead?","t":"A：你星期三早上可以跟越南供應商見面嗎，還是那天很忙？ B：抱歉，我星期三一整天都要【參加】新會計軟體的訓練課程，可以改成星期四下午開會嗎？"},{"w":"present","p":"v.","d":"to show or explain information to a group of people","c":"報告；提出；呈現","s":"A: What will happen at the meeting with the bank on Monday morning? B: Our finance manager will present the new business plan to the bank's loan officers, and if they like our sales figures and the timeline, they may lend us the money for the second factory.","t":"A：星期一早上和銀行的會議會進行什麼？ B：我們的財務經理會向銀行的放款專員【報告】新的營運計畫，如果他們滿意我們的銷售數字和時程，他們可能會借我們錢蓋第二座工廠。"},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity or event","c":"參與；參加","s":"A: Is the volunteer beach cleanup on Saturday only for the marketing team? B: No, every employee is welcome to participate, and the company will provide gloves, bags and lunch, so please sign the list at reception by Thursday if you'd like to join us.","t":"A：星期六的志工淨灘活動只限行銷團隊嗎？ B：不是，歡迎每位員工【參加】，公司會提供手套、袋子和午餐，所以如果你想加入，請在星期四前到櫃台簽名。"},{"w":"register","p":"v.","d":"to put your name on an official list to take part in something","c":"登記；報名；註冊","s":"A: Is it too late to join the marketing conference in Kaohsiung next month? B: No, you can still register online until Friday, but the early-bird price has ended, so the ticket now costs three thousand dollars, which includes lunch on both days.","t":"A：現在參加下個月在高雄的行銷研討會會太晚嗎？ B：不會，你到星期五前都還可以在網路上【報名】，不過早鳥價已經結束了，所以門票現在要三千元，包含兩天的午餐。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to plan and arrange an event or activity","c":"籌劃；組織；安排","s":"A: Who is responsible for the company's year-end party this December? B: The human resources team will organize it this year, so they are already booking a restaurant, planning the games and choosing the prizes, and they want everyone's ideas by the end of the month.","t":"A：今年十二月公司尾牙由誰負責？ B：今年由人資團隊【籌劃】，所以他們已經在訂餐廳、規劃遊戲和挑選獎品，並希望在月底前收集到大家的點子。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"serious and following official rules, not relaxed","c":"正式的","s":"A: What should I wear to the awards dinner at the Grand Hotel on Friday evening? B: It is a formal event with government officials and company presidents, so men should wear a dark suit and tie, and women should wear an evening dress or a business suit.","t":"A：星期五晚上在大飯店的頒獎晚宴，我該穿什麼？ B：那是有政府官員和公司總裁出席的【正式】場合，所以男士應穿深色西裝打領帶，女士應穿晚禮服或套裝。"},{"w":"annual","p":"adj.","d":"happening once every year","c":"每年的；年度的","s":"A: Why is everyone in the sales department working so hard to finish their reports this week? B: Our annual sales meeting is next Monday, where the managers review the whole year's results, and the best team will win a trip to Okinawa next spring.","t":"A：為什麼業務部的每個人這週都這麼努力趕報告？ B：我們的【年度】業務會議在下週一，經理們會在會中檢視整年的成果，表現最好的團隊將贏得明年春天的沖繩之旅。"},{"w":"international","p":"adj.","d":"involving two or more countries","c":"國際的","s":"A: Why do we need so many interpreters at the trade fair in Taichung this year? B: It has become a truly international event, with companies from Japan, Germany, Brazil and India showing their machines, so visitors need help talking with sellers who don't speak Chinese.","t":"A：為什麼今年台中的商展需要這麼多口譯員？ B：它已經成為一個真正的【國際】活動，有日本、德國、巴西和印度的公司展示機器，所以參觀者需要協助才能和不會說中文的賣家溝通。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"showing the skills and high standards expected from a trained worker","c":"專業的；職業的","s":"A: Why do you think the new hotel won the contract for the medical conference instead of our hotel? B: Their staff gave a very professional tour of the meeting rooms, answered every question clearly, and sent a detailed price list the same day, which really impressed the organizers.","t":"A：你認為為什麼新飯店拿下了醫學會議的合約，而不是我們飯店？ B：他們的員工帶領大家參觀會議室時非常【專業】，清楚回答每個問題，還在同一天寄出詳細的價目表，這讓主辦單位印象深刻。"},{"w":"academic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to schools, universities, research and study","c":"學術的","s":"A: Why is the university hiring extra security guards and drivers for next weekend? B: It is holding a large academic conference on artificial intelligence, and over three hundred professors and researchers from Asia and Europe will come to share their latest studies.","t":"A：為什麼大學要為下週末加聘保全和司機？ B：學校將舉辦一場關於人工智慧的大型【學術】研討會，超過三百位來自亞洲和歐洲的教授和研究人員會來分享最新的研究。"},{"w":"successfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that achieves what you wanted","c":"成功地","s":"A: How did the launch of the new smartwatch go in Singapore last week? B: The team successfully finished all three product demonstrations without any technical problems, and several large electronics stores have already placed orders for the holiday season, so the boss is very pleased.","t":"A：上週新智慧手錶在新加坡的發表會進行得如何？ B：團隊【成功地】完成了三場產品展示，沒有任何技術問題，而且好幾家大型電子賣場已經為假期旺季下訂單了，所以老闆非常滿意。"},{"w":"formally","p":"adv.","d":"in an official way","c":"正式地","s":"A: Has the new branch manager in Kaohsiung started her job yet, or is she still in training? B: She has been learning the system for two weeks, but the president will formally introduce her to all the staff at the monthly meeting on Friday, and she will take full charge next Monday.","t":"A：高雄的新任分店經理開始上任了嗎，還是還在受訓？ B：她已經學習系統兩週了，不過總裁會在星期五的月會上向全體員工【正式】介紹她，下週一她就會全面接手。"},{"w":"actively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that involves doing things, not just watching","c":"積極地；主動地","s":"A: Why do you think Kevin was chosen to lead the new customer service project? B: He always actively shares ideas in team meetings, asks useful questions and helps others solve problems, so the managers believe he has the energy and skills to guide a group.","t":"A：你覺得為什麼凱文被選為新客服專案的負責人？ B：他在團隊會議中總是【積極地】分享想法、提出有用的問題並幫助別人解決問題，所以經理們相信他有帶領團隊的活力和能力。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often, or at the same time each day, week, etc.","c":"定期地；經常","s":"A: How does your team keep track of all the tasks when everyone works from home three days a week? B: We regularly hold short video meetings every Monday and Thursday morning, where each person reports progress and problems, so the manager always knows what is happening.","t":"A：每個人一週有三天在家工作，你們團隊怎麼掌握所有任務？ B：我們每週一和週四早上都會【定期】舉行簡短的視訊會議，每個人報告進度和問題，所以經理總能掌握狀況。"}]},{"unit":76,"theme":"Confident 自信","cards":[{"w":"self-esteem","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you have value and are good enough","c":"自尊心；自我價值感","s":"A: Why did the HR department decide to start a mentoring program for new employees in the customer service center this year? B: Many young staff members lost their self-esteem after dealing with rude callers every day, so the program helps them feel valued and keeps them from quitting too soon.","t":"A：人資部門今年為什麼決定為客服中心的新進員工開辦導師計畫？ B：許多年輕員工每天應付無禮的來電者後失去了【自尊心】，所以這個計畫幫助他們感到被重視，避免他們太早離職。"},{"w":"assurance","p":"n.","d":"a promise that something will happen or is true","c":"保證；擔保","s":"A: Are you sure the furniture supplier will deliver the new desks before our staff move into the office on Monday morning? B: Yes, the sales manager gave me his personal assurance that the truck will arrive on Friday afternoon, and he even offered a discount if it is late.","t":"A：你確定家具供應商會在員工週一早上搬進辦公室前送來新書桌嗎？ B：是的，業務經理親自給了我【保證】，說卡車會在週五下午抵達，他甚至表示如果遲到就給折扣。"},{"w":"self-belief","p":"n.","d":"trust in your own abilities","c":"自信；對自己的信心","s":"A: How did the new sales assistant manage to close such a big deal with the hotel chain after working here for only three months? B: She prepared very carefully and had strong self-belief, so even when the hotel's buyer asked difficult questions about price, she answered clearly and never gave up.","t":"A：新來的業務助理才在這裡工作三個月，怎麼能和那家連鎖飯店談成這麼大的生意？ B：她準備得非常仔細，而且有強烈的【自信心】，所以即使飯店採購人員問了關於價格的難題，她也回答得很清楚，從不放棄。"},{"w":"poise","p":"n.","d":"a calm, confident and graceful way of behaving","c":"沉著；鎮定；從容自信的舉止","s":"A: What impressed the interview panel most about the candidate for the receptionist position at the hotel last week? B: Even when the phone kept ringing and a guest started shouting during the role-play test, she handled everything with great poise and kept a warm smile on her face.","t":"A：上週飯店櫃檯接待職位的應徵者，最讓面試小組印象深刻的是什麼？ B：即使在角色扮演測驗中電話一直響，又有客人開始大吼，她依然非常【沉著】地處理一切，臉上始終保持溫暖的微笑。"},{"w":"certainty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being completely sure","c":"確定；把握","s":"A: Can you tell the clients exactly when the new shopping mall will open, since they want to rent two shops there? B: Not with any certainty, because the builders are still waiting for the city to approve the fire safety plan, so the opening could be delayed by several months.","t":"A：既然客戶想在那裡租兩間店面，你能告訴他們新購物中心確切何時開幕嗎？ B：沒辦法有任何【把握】，因為建商還在等市政府核准消防安全計畫，所以開幕可能會延後好幾個月。"},{"w":"trust","p":"n.","d":"the belief that someone is honest and reliable","c":"信任","s":"A: Why does the bank spend so much money training its staff to explain fees clearly to every customer? B: Customers will only keep their savings here if they have trust in us, and once people feel they have been cheated, they quickly move their money to another bank.","t":"A：銀行為什麼花那麼多錢訓練員工向每位顧客清楚說明各項費用？ B：顧客只有在對我們有【信任】時才會把存款留在這裡，一旦人們覺得被騙了，就會很快把錢轉到另一家銀行。"},{"w":"confidence-building","p":"adj.","d":"helping people feel more sure of themselves","c":"建立自信的；增強信心的","s":"A: What will the new interns do during their first week before they start working with real customers in the call center? B: They will join several confidence-building activities, such as short speaking games and practice calls with friendly managers, so they feel less nervous when the real phone calls begin.","t":"A：新實習生在客服中心開始接觸真正的顧客之前，第一週要做什麼？ B：他們會參加幾項【建立自信的】活動，例如簡短的口說遊戲以及和友善的主管練習通話，這樣真正的電話開始時他們就比較不會緊張。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure about yourself or sure that something will happen","c":"有信心的；自信的","s":"A: Do you think our team can finish the new website for the travel agency before the holiday season starts next month? B: I'm quite confident that we can, because the designers have already finished most of the pages, and the programmers only need two more weeks to test the booking system.","t":"A：你覺得我們團隊能在下個月假期旺季開始前完成旅行社的新網站嗎？ B：我相當【有信心】我們可以，因為設計師已經完成了大部分的頁面，而程式設計師只需要再兩週來測試訂位系統。"},{"w":"self-confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure of your own abilities and value","c":"有自信的","s":"A: Why did the manager choose Kevin to lead the product launch even though he only joined the company last year? B: He is very self-confident when he speaks in front of large groups, and the manager believes that customers will trust a speaker who looks relaxed and sure of himself.","t":"A：凱文去年才進公司，為什麼經理還選他主導產品發表會？ B：他在一大群人面前說話時非常【有自信】，而經理相信顧客會信任一位看起來輕鬆又對自己有把握的講者。"},{"w":"assured","p":"adj.","d":"confident and showing skill","c":"從容自信的；有把握的","s":"A: How was the new pilot's first flight with passengers from Taipei to Tokyo yesterday afternoon? B: The captain said her landing in strong wind was smooth and assured, and several passengers even clapped when the plane stopped, so she will probably fly the route again next week.","t":"A：新機師昨天下午第一次載客從台北飛東京的情況如何？ B：機長說她在強風中的降落平穩又【從容自信】，有幾位乘客甚至在飛機停下時鼓掌，所以她下週可能會再飛這條航線。"},{"w":"bold","p":"adj.","d":"brave and willing to take risks","c":"大膽的；勇敢的","s":"A: Why are the shareholders so excited about the company's plan for next year? B: The CEO made a bold decision to open twenty new stores in Southeast Asia at the same time, and although it is risky, many experts think it could double our profits within three years.","t":"A：股東們為什麼對公司明年的計畫那麼興奮？ B：執行長做了一個【大膽的】決定，要同時在東南亞開設二十家新店，雖然有風險，但許多專家認為三年內可能讓我們的利潤加倍。"},{"w":"secure","p":"adj.","d":"feeling safe and confident, without worry","c":"有安全感的；安心的","s":"A: Why do you think so many workers have stayed at this small printing company for more than ten years? B: The owner offers long contracts and fair pay, so the staff feel secure about their future, and they don't need to worry about losing their jobs when business is slow.","t":"A：你覺得為什麼有那麼多員工在這家小印刷公司待了十年以上？ B：老闆提供長期合約和合理的薪水，所以員工對未來感到【安心】，生意清淡時也不必擔心會失去工作。"},{"w":"optimistic","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful that good things will happen","c":"樂觀的","s":"A: How does the sales director feel about our chances of winning the contract with the airline next month? B: She is fairly optimistic, because our price is lower than the other companies' offers, and the airline's manager said he was very happy with our sample uniforms.","t":"A：業務總監對我們下個月拿下航空公司合約的機會有什麼看法？ B：她相當【樂觀】，因為我們的價格比其他公司的報價低，而且航空公司的經理說他對我們的制服樣品非常滿意。"},{"w":"fearless","p":"adj.","d":"not afraid of anything","c":"無所畏懼的","s":"A: Why did the news company send Maria to report on the floods in the south instead of a more experienced journalist? B: She is completely fearless in difficult situations, and last year she stayed calm while reporting from a forest fire, so the editor trusts her to work safely in dangerous places.","t":"A：新聞公司為什麼派瑪麗亞去報導南部的水災，而不是派更有經驗的記者？ B：她在困難的情況下完全【無所畏懼】，去年她在森林大火現場報導時也保持冷靜，所以總編輯信任她能在危險的地方安全地工作。"},{"w":"assertive","p":"adj.","d":"stating your opinions and needs clearly and firmly","c":"堅定自信的；敢於表達主張的","s":"A: What advice did the trainer give the new team leaders about dealing with suppliers who often deliver goods late? B: She told them to be polite but assertive, which means they should explain clearly what they need, set a firm deadline, and not simply accept another excuse.","t":"A：訓練師給新任組長什麼建議，來應付經常延遲交貨的供應商？ B：她要他們保持禮貌但要【堅定表達主張】，也就是應該清楚說明自己的需求、訂下明確的期限，而不是單純接受另一個藉口。"},{"w":"decisive","p":"adj.","d":"able to make decisions quickly and clearly","c":"果斷的；決定性的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant group promote Mr. Lin to regional manager instead of someone who has worked there longer? B: When the kitchen caught fire last year, he was very decisive, and he moved all the guests outside and called the fire department within two minutes, so nobody was hurt.","t":"A：餐飲集團為什麼升林先生為區域經理，而不是在那裡工作更久的人？ B：去年廚房失火時，他非常【果斷】，在兩分鐘內就把所有客人移到外面並打電話給消防隊，所以沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"positive","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful and confident; thinking about the good side","c":"正面的；積極的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the manager announced that the office would move to a smaller building next year? B: Most people stayed positive about the change, because the new office is close to the train station, and the company promised to buy new computers and comfortable chairs for everyone.","t":"A：經理宣布辦公室明年要搬到較小的大樓時，員工有什麼反應？ B：大多數人對這個改變保持【正面】的態度，因為新辦公室靠近火車站，而且公司承諾要為每個人買新電腦和舒適的椅子。"},{"w":"proud","p":"adj.","d":"feeling pleased about something you or others have done","c":"驕傲的；自豪的","s":"A: Why did the factory manager invite all the workers to a special dinner at the hotel last Friday night? B: He was very proud of them, because they had worked for a whole year without a single accident, and they also produced more machine parts than in any previous year.","t":"A：工廠經理上週五晚上為什麼邀請所有員工到飯店參加特別晚宴？ B：他為他們感到非常【驕傲】，因為他們整整一年工作都沒有發生任何意外，而且生產的機械零件比以往任何一年都多。"},{"w":"calm","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not worried, excited or angry","c":"冷靜的；平靜的","s":"A: How did the flight attendants handle the situation when the plane hit strong turbulence over the ocean last night? B: They stayed calm and walked through the cabin to check every seat belt, and their relaxed voices helped the nervous passengers feel much safer until the shaking stopped.","t":"A：昨晚飛機在海上遇到強烈亂流時，空服員是怎麼處理的？ B：他們保持【冷靜】，走過機艙檢查每一條安全帶，他們從容的聲音讓緊張的乘客感到安全許多，直到搖晃停止。"},{"w":"believe","p":"v.","d":"to feel sure that something is true or that someone can do something","c":"相信","s":"A: Why did the director give such an important project to a young designer who has never managed a team before? B: She has seen his work for two years and really seems to believe in his talent, so she thinks he only needs the chance to show what he can do.","t":"A：總監為什麼把這麼重要的專案交給一位從未管理過團隊的年輕設計師？ B：她看了他兩年的作品，似乎真的【相信】他的才華，所以她認為他只需要一個機會來展現自己的能力。"},{"w":"reassure","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less worried","c":"使安心；使放心","s":"A: What did you say to the customer who called because her package hadn't arrived after ten days? B: I tried to reassure her by explaining that the delay was caused by the typhoon, and I promised to send her a tracking number and a small gift card for her trouble.","t":"A：那位因為包裹十天都沒送到而打電話來的顧客，你跟她說了什麼？ B：我試著讓她【安心】，向她解釋延誤是颱風造成的，並承諾會寄給她追蹤號碼以及一張小禮物卡作為補償。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone support or confidence to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: Why does the company pay for English classes for all its office staff on Tuesday evenings? B: The managers want to encourage everyone to speak with foreign clients more often, because the company is planning to sell its products in Europe and Australia starting next year.","t":"A：公司為什麼為所有辦公室員工支付週二晚上的英文課費用？ B：主管們想【鼓勵】每個人更常和外國客戶交談，因為公司正計畫從明年開始在歐洲和澳洲銷售產品。"},{"w":"affirm","p":"v.","d":"to state strongly and publicly that something is true","c":"明確表示；確認；重申","s":"A: What did the CEO say at the press conference after the rumors that the company might close its factory in Taichung? B: She stood in front of the reporters to affirm that the factory would stay open, and she added that the company plans to hire fifty more workers there next year.","t":"A：在傳出公司可能關閉台中工廠的謠言後，執行長在記者會上說了什麼？ B：她站在記者面前【明確表示】工廠會繼續營運，還補充說公司計畫明年在那裡再雇用五十名員工。"},{"w":"project","p":"v.","d":"to show a quality or feeling to other people","c":"展現；表現出（形象、特質）","s":"A: Why does the training course spend so much time on how we stand and use our hands during sales presentations? B: Our body language helps us project confidence to customers, so if we stand straight and look people in the eye, they are more likely to trust what we say about our products.","t":"A：為什麼訓練課程花那麼多時間在我們做銷售簡報時的站姿和手勢上？ B：肢體語言能幫助我們向顧客【展現】自信，所以如果我們站直並直視對方的眼睛，他們就比較可能相信我們對產品的介紹。"},{"w":"confidently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are sure","c":"自信地；有把握地","s":"A: How did the new accountant do when the auditors asked her questions about last year's travel expenses? B: She answered every question confidently and showed them the receipts for each trip, so the auditors finished their check in one day instead of the three days they had planned.","t":"A：審計人員問新會計關於去年差旅費用的問題時，她表現得如何？ B：她【自信地】回答了每個問題，並向他們出示每趟出差的收據，所以審計人員一天就完成了檢查，而不是原本計畫的三天。"},{"w":"boldly","p":"adv.","d":"in a brave and confident way","c":"大膽地","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department talking about the new advertisement for our sports drinks? B: The designers boldly used bright pink and black instead of our usual blue, and although some managers were worried at first, sales went up by twenty percent in the first month.","t":"A：行銷部的每個人為什麼都在談論我們運動飲料的新廣告？ B：設計師【大膽地】使用亮粉紅色和黑色，而不是我們平常的藍色，雖然有些主管一開始很擔心，但第一個月的銷售量就上升了百分之二十。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is firmly fixed or safe","c":"牢固地；安全地","s":"A: What should the warehouse staff check before the trucks leave for the department stores early tomorrow morning? B: They need to make sure every box is tied securely to the floor of the truck, because last month several boxes of glasses fell over on the highway and broke into pieces.","t":"A：明天一早卡車出發前往百貨公司之前，倉庫員工應該檢查什麼？ B：他們必須確認每個箱子都【牢固地】綁在卡車的底板上，因為上個月有好幾箱玻璃杯在高速公路上倒下摔碎了。"},{"w":"assuredly","p":"adv.","d":"in a confident way; certainly","c":"從容自信地；確實地","s":"A: How did the young violinist perform at the company's anniversary concert in the hotel ballroom on Saturday? B: Although she was only fifteen, she played assuredly in front of five hundred guests, and the president was so impressed that he offered to sponsor her music studies abroad next year.","t":"A：那位年輕小提琴手週六在飯店宴會廳的公司週年音樂會上表現如何？ B：雖然她只有十五歲，卻在五百位賓客面前【從容自信地】演奏，總裁印象非常深刻，提議明年贊助她出國學音樂。"},{"w":"calmly","p":"adv.","d":"in a relaxed and quiet way, without getting upset","c":"冷靜地；平靜地","s":"A: What should we do if a customer starts shouting at the front desk because the hotel lost his reservation? B: Listen to him calmly without interrupting, apologize for the problem, and then offer him another room or a free breakfast, because getting angry back will only make the situation worse.","t":"A：如果有顧客因為飯店弄丟他的訂房而在櫃檯大吼，我們該怎麼辦？ B：【冷靜地】聽他說，不要打斷他，為這個問題道歉，然後提供他另一間房間或免費早餐，因為以生氣回應只會讓情況更糟。"},{"w":"positively","p":"adv.","d":"in a hopeful or approving way","c":"正面地；積極地","s":"A: How did the customers respond to the free samples of our new low-sugar cookies at the supermarket last weekend? B: Most shoppers reacted very positively, and many said the cookies tasted just as good as the regular ones, so the supermarket has already ordered three hundred boxes for next month.","t":"A：上週末顧客對我們在超市發送的新款低糖餅乾試吃品有什麼反應？ B：大多數購物者反應非常【正面】，很多人說這款餅乾和一般的一樣好吃，所以超市已經訂了三百盒準備下個月販售。"},{"w":"firmly","p":"adv.","d":"in a strong, clear way that shows you will not change your mind","c":"堅定地；牢固地","s":"A: Did the supplier agree to lower the price of the steel after our long meeting with them yesterday? B: No, their sales manager firmly said that the price could not change because of higher shipping costs, so we will have to look for another company that can offer a better deal.","t":"A：昨天和供應商開了很久的會之後，他們同意降低鋼材價格了嗎？ B：沒有，他們的業務經理【堅定地】表示，因為運費提高，價格無法調整，所以我們必須找另一家能提供更好條件的公司。"},{"w":"fearlessly","p":"adv.","d":"without fear; bravely","c":"無畏地；勇敢地","s":"A: Why did the city give an award to the young bus driver at the ceremony in the town hall yesterday? B: When a fire started at the back of her bus, she acted fearlessly and helped every passenger get out safely before the fire department arrived, even though the smoke was very thick.","t":"A：市政府昨天為什麼在市政廳的典禮上頒獎給那位年輕的公車司機？ B：她的公車後方起火時，她【無畏地】行動，在消防隊抵達前幫助每位乘客安全下車，即使當時煙霧非常濃。"},{"w":"proudly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are pleased with what you or others have done","c":"自豪地；驕傲地","s":"A: What did the restaurant owner do after her small café won the best breakfast award in the city? B: She proudly hung the certificate on the wall next to the front door, and she also posted a photo of her whole kitchen team on social media to thank them for their hard work.","t":"A：那家小咖啡館的老闆在店裡贏得全市最佳早餐獎後做了什麼？ B：她【自豪地】把證書掛在前門旁的牆上，還在社群媒體上貼出整個廚房團隊的照片，感謝他們的辛勞。"}]},{"unit":77,"theme":"Construction 建築工程","cards":[{"w":"building","p":"n.","d":"a structure with walls and a roof, such as an office or house","c":"建築物；大樓","s":"A: Why are so many workers standing outside the office this morning instead of going up to their desks on time? B: The fire alarm went off at eight o'clock, so security asked everyone to leave the building until the fire department checks every floor and says it is safe to return.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上這麼多員工站在辦公室外面，而不是準時上樓到座位上？ B：八點時火災警報響了，所以保全請大家離開【大樓】，直到消防隊檢查完每一層樓並確認可以安全回去為止。"},{"w":"site","p":"n.","d":"a place where something is built or happens","c":"地點；工地","s":"A: Do visitors need to wear anything special when they come to see the new hospital that your company is building near the river? B: Yes, everyone who enters the construction site must wear a hard hat and safety boots, and they have to sign in at the gate before the guide shows them around.","t":"A：參觀者來看你們公司在河邊興建的新醫院時，需要穿戴什麼特別的東西嗎？ B：需要，每個進入施工【工地】的人都必須戴安全帽、穿安全靴，而且在導覽員帶他們參觀之前要先在大門登記。"},{"w":"project","p":"n.","d":"a planned piece of work with a clear goal","c":"專案；工程計畫","s":"A: How long will it take to finish the new shopping center beside the train station, and when can the shops start moving in? B: The whole project should take about eighteen months, but the builders hope to open the first floor early so that a few stores can start doing business before the holidays.","t":"A：車站旁的新購物中心要多久才能完工？商店什麼時候可以開始進駐？ B：整個【工程案】大約需要十八個月，但建商希望提早開放一樓，讓幾家店能在假期前開始營業。"},{"w":"foundation","p":"n.","d":"the solid base under a building that supports it","c":"地基","s":"A: Why did the workers spend so many weeks digging a deep hole before they started putting up the walls of the new hotel? B: They needed to build a strong foundation under the ground first, because the hotel will have twenty floors and the soil in this area is quite soft after heavy rain.","t":"A：為什麼工人們在開始蓋新飯店的牆之前，花了好幾個星期挖一個深坑？ B：他們必須先在地下打好堅固的【地基】，因為飯店將有二十層樓，而且這一帶的土壤在大雨後相當鬆軟。"},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"something that has been built, such as a bridge or building","c":"結構；建築物","s":"A: What did the safety inspector say after she checked the old bridge that connects our factory to the main road last Friday? B: She said the whole structure is still strong enough for cars, but heavy trucks should use the other road until the city replaces some of the rusty metal parts next spring.","t":"A：上週五安全檢查員檢查完連接我們工廠和主要道路的舊橋後，她說了什麼？ B：她說整個【結構】仍然足以承受汽車通行，但在市政府明年春天更換一些生鏽的金屬零件之前，重型卡車應該改走另一條路。"},{"w":"framework","p":"n.","d":"the main frame that supports a building or object","c":"框架；骨架","s":"A: The new warehouse already looks quite tall, but why can I still see right through it from the parking lot? B: So far the workers have only put up the metal framework that holds everything together, and they will add the walls, windows and roof over the next two months if the weather stays dry.","t":"A：新倉庫看起來已經很高了，但為什麼我從停車場還能直接看穿過去？ B：到目前為止，工人只搭好了支撐整體的金屬【骨架】，如果天氣持續乾燥，他們會在接下來兩個月加上牆壁、窗戶和屋頂。"},{"w":"material","p":"n.","d":"a substance used to make or build things","c":"材料","s":"A: Why has the price of the new office building gone up so much since we signed the contract with the builder in January? B: The cost of almost every building material, such as wood, glass and metal, has risen sharply this year, so the builder asked us to pay an extra eight percent.","t":"A：自從我們一月和建商簽約以來，新辦公大樓的價格為什麼漲了這麼多？ B：今年幾乎每一種建築【材料】，像是木材、玻璃和金屬，價格都大幅上漲，所以建商要求我們多付百分之八。"},{"w":"cement","p":"n.","d":"a gray powder mixed with water and sand that becomes hard when dry","c":"水泥","s":"A: Why are the builders covering the new sidewalk in front of our store with plastic sheets this afternoon? B: They just poured fresh cement this morning, and it needs at least two days to dry completely, so they don't want customers or dogs to walk on it and leave footprints.","t":"A：為什麼建築工人今天下午用塑膠布蓋住我們店門口的新人行道？ B：他們今天早上剛倒了新的【水泥】，至少需要兩天才能完全乾，所以他們不希望顧客或狗走在上面留下腳印。"},{"w":"concrete","p":"n.","d":"a hard building material made from cement, sand, small stones and water","c":"混凝土","s":"A: Why did the city decide to replace the old wooden parking garage behind the train station instead of fixing it? B: The engineers said that wood is not safe enough for so many cars, so the new garage will be made of concrete, which is much stronger and will last for at least fifty years.","t":"A：市政府為什麼決定拆換火車站後面的舊木造停車場，而不是修理它？ B：工程師說木頭對於這麼多車輛來說不夠安全，所以新的停車場會用【混凝土】建造，它堅固得多，而且至少可以用五十年。"},{"w":"brick","p":"n.","d":"a small hard block of baked clay used for building walls","c":"磚塊","s":"A: What kind of walls are you planning for the new café that you are opening near the university next year? B: We want warm red brick walls inside and outside, because students like a cozy, old-fashioned look, and the walls also keep the room cool during the hot summer months.","t":"A：你們明年要在大學附近開的新咖啡館，打算用什麼樣的牆？ B：我們想要內外都是溫暖的紅【磚】牆，因為學生喜歡溫馨、復古的風格，而且這種牆在炎熱的夏季月份也能讓室內保持涼爽。"},{"w":"steel","p":"n.","d":"a very strong metal made from iron","c":"鋼；鋼鐵","s":"A: Why is the new sports stadium so much more expensive than the one the city built about twenty years ago? B: The designers chose a roof made of strong steel beams that can cover the whole field without any columns, and that metal is very expensive to buy and to bring here by ship.","t":"A：為什麼新的體育場比市政府大約二十年前蓋的那座貴這麼多？ B：設計師選擇了用堅固的【鋼】樑做成的屋頂，可以不用任何柱子就覆蓋整個場地，而這種金屬的購買和用船運來的費用都非常昂貴。"},{"w":"crane","p":"n.","d":"a tall machine used for lifting and moving heavy things","c":"起重機；吊車","s":"A: How do the workers get those huge glass windows all the way up to the thirtieth floor of the new tower? B: They use a tall crane that lifts each window slowly from the truck, and two workers on the top floor guide it into place with ropes while talking to the driver by radio.","t":"A：工人們是怎麼把那些巨大的玻璃窗一路送到新大樓的三十樓的？ B：他們用一台高大的【起重機】把每片窗戶從卡車上慢慢吊起來，頂樓的兩名工人一邊用無線電和操作員通話，一邊用繩子把窗戶引導到定位。"},{"w":"scaffold","p":"n.","d":"a frame of poles and boards that workers stand on when working on a building","c":"鷹架","s":"A: Why is the front of the bank covered with metal poles and wooden boards this week? B: The painters put up a scaffold so they can stand safely while they clean and paint the outside walls, and they expect to take it down by Friday if it doesn't rain.","t":"A：為什麼這週銀行正面被金屬桿和木板包圍住？ B：油漆工搭了【鷹架】，這樣他們在清洗和粉刷外牆時可以安全地站在上面，如果不下雨，他們預計週五前拆掉。"},{"w":"blueprint","p":"n.","d":"a detailed plan or drawing of a building","c":"藍圖；設計圖","s":"A: Before we sign the contract, can we see exactly where the meeting rooms and the kitchen will be in our new office? B: Of course, the architect will bring the blueprint to our meeting on Tuesday, and she can explain every room and make small changes if you want more space.","t":"A：在我們簽約之前，可以先看看新辦公室裡會議室和茶水間的確切位置嗎？ B：當然可以，建築師週二開會時會帶【藍圖】來，她可以說明每個房間，如果你們想要更多空間，她也可以做些小修改。"},{"w":"contractor","p":"n.","d":"a person or company paid to do building work","c":"承包商","s":"A: Who will be responsible for hiring the workers and buying the materials for the new factory in Taichung? B: We chose a local contractor with thirty years of experience, so his company will manage the whole job, and we only need to check the progress once a month.","t":"A：誰會負責雇用工人並購買台中新工廠的材料？ B：我們選了一家有三十年經驗的當地【承包商】，所以他的公司會管理整個工作，我們只需要每個月檢查一次進度。"},{"w":"architect","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to design buildings","c":"建築師","s":"A: The new library looks so modern, with all that glass and the green garden on the roof, but who came up with the idea? B: A young architect from Kaohsiung won the design competition last year, and she wanted the building to use natural light and save as much energy as possible.","t":"A：新圖書館看起來好現代，有那麼多玻璃，屋頂上還有綠色花園，這是誰想出來的點子？ B：一位來自高雄的年輕【建築師】去年贏得設計比賽，她希望這棟建築能利用自然光並盡可能節省能源。"},{"w":"engineer","p":"n.","d":"a person who designs or builds machines, roads, bridges, etc.","c":"工程師","s":"A: Why did the builders stop working on the tenth floor of the apartment tower for a whole week? B: A structural engineer found a small crack in one of the main columns, so she ordered extra tests to make sure the tower is strong enough before anyone continues.","t":"A：建築工人為什麼整整一個星期停止在公寓大樓十樓施工？ B：一位結構【工程師】在其中一根主柱上發現了一道小裂縫，所以她下令進行額外的測試，在任何人繼續施工前確保大樓夠堅固。"},{"w":"laborer","p":"n.","d":"a worker who does hard physical work","c":"勞工；工人","s":"A: Why does the construction company give its workers such long breaks in the middle of the afternoon during the summer? B: Every laborer on the team spends hours carrying heavy materials and digging under the hot sun, so the manager wants to protect their health and prevent accidents caused by tiredness.","t":"A：為什麼營造公司在夏天的下午給工人這麼長的休息時間？ B：團隊中的每個【工人】都要在烈日下花好幾個小時搬運重物和挖土，所以經理想要保護他們的健康，並防止因疲勞造成的意外。"},{"w":"permit","p":"n.","d":"an official document that allows you to do something","c":"許可證","s":"A: Why haven't the builders started work on your new restaurant yet, even though you signed the contract two months ago? B: We are still waiting for a building permit from the city government, and without that official paper we are not allowed to break any walls or add a second floor.","t":"A：你兩個月前就簽約了，為什麼建築工人還沒開始動工蓋你的新餐廳？ B：我們還在等市政府核發建築【許可證】，沒有那份正式文件，我們不准打掉任何牆或加蓋二樓。"},{"w":"build","p":"v.","d":"to make something by putting parts or materials together","c":"建造","s":"A: Our company has grown so fast this year, so where are we going to put all the new staff next spring? B: The board has decided to build a five-story office next to the factory, and the work will start in March so that everyone can move in before the end of the year.","t":"A：我們公司今年成長得這麼快，明年春天要把新員工安置在哪裡？ B：董事會決定在工廠旁邊【建造】一棟五層樓的辦公室，工程將在三月開始，好讓大家在年底前搬進去。"},{"w":"construct","p":"v.","d":"to build something such as a road, bridge or building","c":"建造；建設","s":"A: How is the city going to handle all the traffic when the new science park opens near the highway? B: The government plans to construct two new bridges and a wider road over the next three years, so drivers will be able to reach the park without waiting in long lines.","t":"A：新的科學園區在高速公路附近開幕時，市政府要如何處理所有交通？ B：政府計畫在未來三年內【興建】兩座新橋和一條更寬的道路，這樣駕駛人就能不必大排長龍抵達園區。"},{"w":"install","p":"v.","d":"to put equipment into place so it is ready to use","c":"安裝","s":"A: The new office looks almost ready, but why is it still so hot inside when the staff are moving in next Monday? B: The technicians will come on Thursday to install the air conditioners in every room, and they promised that everything will be working before the weekend.","t":"A：新辦公室看起來差不多好了，但員工下週一就要搬進來，為什麼裡面還這麼熱？ B：技術人員星期四會來在每個房間【安裝】冷氣，他們保證週末前一切都會正常運作。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken or damaged","c":"修理；修補","s":"A: Why is part of the parking lot behind our office closed off with orange cones today? B: Heavy rain last week made several deep holes in the ground, so the building manager hired a team to repair the surface before someone damages a car or falls and gets hurt.","t":"A：為什麼今天我們辦公室後面停車場有一部分用橘色三角錐圍起來？ B：上週的大雨在地面上造成好幾個深坑，所以大樓管理員請了一組人來【修補】路面，以免有人的車子受損或有人跌倒受傷。"},{"w":"demolish","p":"v.","d":"to completely destroy a building","c":"拆除","s":"A: What is going to happen to the old cinema on Main Street now that it has been closed for so many years? B: The new owner plans to demolish it next month and build a modern apartment complex, because the old building is unsafe and would cost too much to fix.","t":"A：主街上那家關閉多年的老電影院會怎麼樣？ B：新屋主計畫下個月把它【拆除】，然後蓋一座現代化的公寓大樓，因為那棟舊建築不安全，修理的費用也太高。"},{"w":"residential","p":"adj.","d":"(of an area) where people live, not where they work","c":"住宅的","s":"A: Why can't the factory owner build a new warehouse on that empty land beside the park? B: That area is a quiet residential zone with houses and schools, so the city does not allow big trucks or noisy businesses there, and he will have to look for land in the industrial park instead.","t":"A：為什麼工廠老闆不能在公園旁那塊空地上蓋新倉庫？ B：那一區是有房屋和學校的安靜【住宅】區，市政府不允許大型卡車或吵雜的商家在那裡，所以他必須改在工業區找地。"},{"w":"commercial","p":"adj.","d":"related to business and making money","c":"商業的","s":"A: Why is the rent for the ground floor so much higher than the rent for the apartments upstairs? B: The ground floor is used as commercial space for shops and restaurants, and businesses are willing to pay more because thousands of people walk past the building every day.","t":"A：為什麼一樓的租金比樓上的公寓高這麼多？ B：一樓是作為商店和餐廳的【商業】空間，因為每天有數千人經過這棟大樓，所以商家願意付更多錢。"},{"w":"industrial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with factories and the production of goods","c":"工業的","s":"A: Why did your company decide to move its factory out of the city center last year? B: The government created a new industrial park near the port with cheaper land and better roads for trucks, so moving there saved us money and made shipping our products overseas much easier.","t":"A：為什麼你們公司去年決定把工廠搬出市中心？ B：政府在港口附近設立了新的【工業】園區，土地更便宜，卡車用的道路也更好，所以搬到那裡為我們省了錢，也讓產品運往海外變得容易許多。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only for a short time","c":"暫時的；臨時的","s":"A: Where will the staff work while the builders are fixing the roof and the walls of the main office this summer? B: The company has rented a temporary office on the other side of the street for three months, and everyone will move back once the work is finished in September.","t":"A：今年夏天建築工人修理總公司屋頂和牆壁時，員工要在哪裡上班？ B：公司在對街租了一間為期三個月的【臨時】辦公室，等九月工程完成後，大家就會搬回去。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a very long time or forever","c":"永久的","s":"A: Will the outdoor market behind the train station stay open after the summer festival is over? B: Yes, the city liked it so much that it will become a permanent market, and workers will build a proper roof and toilets so that it can stay open all year round.","t":"A：夏季節慶結束後，火車站後面的戶外市集還會繼續開嗎？ B：會，市政府非常喜歡它，所以它會成為【永久性】的市集，工人會蓋一個正式的屋頂和廁所，讓它全年都能營業。"},{"w":"safely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that avoids danger or harm","c":"安全地","s":"A: Why does every new worker have to attend a two-day training course before they are allowed onto the building site? B: The company wants everyone to learn how to use the machines and climb ladders safely, because even one small mistake on a busy site can cause a serious accident.","t":"A：為什麼每個新工人在獲准進入工地之前，都必須參加兩天的訓練課程？ B：公司希望每個人都學會如何【安全地】使用機器和爬梯子，因為在忙碌的工地上，即使一個小錯誤也可能造成嚴重意外。"},{"w":"carefully","p":"adv.","d":"with great attention to avoid mistakes or damage","c":"小心地；仔細地","s":"A: Why did the workers spend so much time moving the old paintings out of the museum before the renovation started? B: The paintings are very valuable and easy to damage, so the team packed each one carefully in soft boxes and drove them slowly to a storage room across town.","t":"A：為什麼工人在翻修開始前，花了那麼多時間把舊畫作搬出博物館？ B：那些畫非常珍貴而且容易損壞，所以團隊把每一幅都【小心地】包裝在柔軟的箱子裡，然後慢慢開車送到城市另一頭的儲藏室。"},{"w":"efficiently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that works well without wasting time or money","c":"有效率地","s":"A: How did the builders manage to finish the new train station three months earlier than everyone expected? B: The manager planned every step and made sure the teams worked efficiently, so nobody wasted time waiting for materials and the machines were busy from early morning until late evening.","t":"A：建築工人是怎麼做到比大家預期早三個月完成新火車站的？ B：經理規劃了每一個步驟，並確保各組都【有效率地】工作，所以沒有人浪費時間等材料，機器從清晨一直忙到深夜。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"again and again at the same time or interval","c":"定期地","s":"A: How do you make sure the old office tower stays safe for the hundreds of people who work there every day? B: We hire inspectors to check the elevators, the fire doors and the walls regularly, usually every three months, and we fix any problem they find right away.","t":"A：你們如何確保這棟老舊辦公大樓對每天在那裡工作的數百人來說是安全的？ B：我們聘請檢查員【定期】檢查電梯、防火門和牆壁，通常每三個月一次，發現任何問題就立刻修理。"}]},{"unit":78,"theme":"Consultation Letter 諮詢信","cards":[{"w":"advice","p":"n.","d":"an opinion about what someone should do","c":"建議；勸告","s":"A: You look worried about the new office lease, so what are you going to do before you sign the contract next Monday? B: I'm going to ask our company lawyer for some advice, because the contract is twenty pages long and I don't fully understand the rules about repairs and early cancellation.","t":"A：你看起來很擔心新辦公室的租約，下週一簽約前你打算怎麼做？ B：我要向公司的律師尋求一些【建議】，因為合約有二十頁長，我不完全了解有關維修和提前解約的規定。"},{"w":"suggest","p":"v.","d":"to give an idea for someone to think about","c":"建議；提議","s":"A: The customers keep complaining that our online store is too slow during the holiday season, so what should we tell the manager at today's meeting? B: I would suggest that we move the website to a faster server before December, since a short delay can make shoppers leave and buy from our competitors instead.","t":"A：顧客一直抱怨我們的網路商店在假期旺季太慢，今天開會時我們該跟經理說什麼？ B：我會【建議】我們在十二月前把網站移到更快的伺服器，因為短暫的延遲就可能讓購物者離開，轉而向競爭對手購買。"},{"w":"suggestion","p":"n.","d":"an idea or plan that someone offers","c":"建議；提議","s":"A: Did anyone come up with a good way to cut our printing costs before the end of the financial year? B: Yes, Maria from accounting made a useful suggestion at the staff meeting: we should print reports on both sides of the paper and send most documents by email instead.","t":"A：有人想出在會計年度結束前降低印刷成本的好方法嗎？ B：有，會計部的瑪麗亞在員工會議上提出了一個實用的【建議】：我們應該雙面列印報告，而且大部分文件改用電子郵件寄送。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is good or suitable","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: I need to book a hotel near the convention center for three clients who are flying in from Tokyo next week, but I've never stayed in that area. B: I can recommend the Harbor View Hotel, because it is only five minutes away on foot, the rooms are quiet, and breakfast is included in the price.","t":"A：我需要為下週從東京飛來的三位客戶在會議中心附近訂飯店，但我從沒住過那一區。 B：我可以【推薦】港景飯店，因為走路只要五分鐘，房間很安靜，而且價格包含早餐。"},{"w":"recommendation","p":"n.","d":"advice about what is best to do or choose","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: Why did the company decide to hire an outside firm to manage its computer security this year? B: The board followed the recommendation of the IT consultant, who found several weak points in our network last spring and said a specialist team could protect our customer data much better.","t":"A：公司今年為什麼決定聘請外部公司來管理電腦安全？ B：董事會採納了資訊顧問的【建議】，他去年春天在我們的網路中發現了幾個弱點，並表示專業團隊能更妥善地保護我們的客戶資料。"},{"w":"opinion","p":"n.","d":"what a person thinks about something","c":"意見；看法","s":"A: The design team has finished two different logos for our new coffee brand, and we have to choose one by Friday afternoon. B: Before we decide, let's ask a few regular customers for their opinion, because they are the people who will see the logo on every cup they buy.","t":"A：設計團隊已經完成兩個不同的新咖啡品牌標誌，我們必須在週五下午前選出一個。 B：在決定之前，我們先問問幾位常客的【意見】吧，因為他們是每買一杯都會看到這個標誌的人。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about how to do something","c":"指導；輔導","s":"A: How are the new sales assistants getting on in their first month at the downtown branch? B: They're doing well, mainly because each of them works with a senior colleague who gives them guidance on how to handle difficult customers and use the new payment system.","t":"A：新來的銷售助理在市中心分店的第一個月表現如何？ B：他們表現不錯，主要是因為每個人都跟著一位資深同事，由他提供如何應對難搞顧客以及使用新付款系統的【指導】。"},{"w":"assistance","p":"n.","d":"help or support","c":"協助；幫助","s":"A: The airline lost my suitcase on the flight from Singapore, and my important presentation notes were inside it. B: Go to the service desk next to baggage claim right away, because the staff there can give you assistance with the lost-luggage form and send the bag to your hotel once they find it.","t":"A：航空公司在新加坡飛來的航班上弄丟了我的行李箱，我重要的簡報筆記就在裡面。 B：馬上去行李提領區旁的服務台，那裡的員工可以【協助】你填寫遺失行李表格，找到後也會把行李送到你的飯店。"},{"w":"request","p":"n.","d":"an act of politely asking for something","c":"請求；要求","s":"A: Have you heard back from the head office about the extra staff we need for the busy summer season? B: Yes, they approved our request for two part-time workers this morning, so we can start interviewing college students next week and train them before July.","t":"A：總公司有回覆我們在夏季旺季需要額外人手的事嗎？ B：有，他們今天早上批准了我們招募兩名兼職人員的【請求】，所以下週我們就能開始面試大學生，並在七月前訓練他們。"},{"w":"concern","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry about something","c":"擔憂；關切","s":"A: Why did the residents call a meeting with the construction company last night? B: They wanted to express their concern about the noise and dust from the new shopping center, because the workers start at six in the morning and many families have small children who can't sleep.","t":"A：居民昨晚為什麼要求跟建設公司開會？ B：他們想表達對新購物中心噪音和灰塵的【擔憂】，因為工人早上六點就開工，很多家庭有睡不著的小孩。"},{"w":"issue","p":"n.","d":"a problem or subject that people talk about","c":"問題；議題","s":"A: Why hasn't the online payment page worked since this morning, even though the website itself is still running? B: There's a technical issue with the bank's system, and our IT staff are working with them to fix it, so customers will have to pay by phone for a few hours.","t":"A：為什麼網站本身還在運作，但線上付款頁面從今天早上就無法使用？ B：銀行的系統出了技術【問題】，我們的資訊人員正在和他們一起修復，所以顧客在接下來幾小時必須用電話付款。"},{"w":"matter","p":"n.","d":"a subject or situation that you must deal with","c":"事情；問題","s":"A: Should I tell my team leader that two of our suppliers have sent the wrong products three times this month? B: Yes, this is a serious matter, so you should report it to her today, and she will probably want to discuss it with the purchasing manager before we place any more orders.","t":"A：我該告訴組長我們有兩家供應商這個月已經三次送錯貨嗎？ B：該，這是件嚴重的【事情】，你今天就應該向她報告，她很可能會想在我們再下訂單前和採購經理討論。"},{"w":"situation","p":"n.","d":"the things that are happening at a certain time and place","c":"情況；處境","s":"A: How is the hotel dealing with the power cut that started during the wedding dinner last night? B: The manager explained the situation to all the guests, moved the party to the garden with candles, and gave everyone a free breakfast, so most people were actually quite happy in the end.","t":"A：飯店怎麼處理昨晚婚宴晚餐期間開始的停電？ B：經理向所有賓客說明了【情況】，把派對移到點著蠟燭的花園，並招待大家免費早餐，所以到最後多數人其實都相當開心。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear or easy to understand","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Many of our older customers say the new banking app is confusing, and some of them have stopped using it completely. B: Then let's make a short video that can explain each step slowly, from logging in to paying bills, and post it on our website and in every branch.","t":"A：許多年長的顧客說新的銀行應用程式很難懂，有些人已經完全不用了。 B：那我們來做一支短片，從登入到繳費，慢慢【解釋】每個步驟，並放在我們的網站和每家分行。"},{"w":"clarify","p":"v.","d":"to make something clearer by giving more details","c":"釐清；闡明","s":"A: The client's email says they want the brochures 'as soon as possible,' but I'm not sure whether that means this week or next month. B: You should call them this afternoon to clarify the delivery date, because we need to know how many workers to put on the printing machines.","t":"A：客戶的電子郵件說要「盡快」拿到小冊子，但我不確定那是指這週還是下個月。 B：你今天下午應該打電話給他們【釐清】交貨日期，因為我們需要知道要安排多少工人操作印刷機。"},{"w":"discuss","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something with other people","c":"討論","s":"A: Why are the department heads meeting in the large conference room this afternoon instead of their usual office? B: They need to discuss next year's budget with the finance director, and since about fifteen people are coming, the small room simply doesn't have enough chairs for everyone.","t":"A：各部門主管今天下午為什麼在大會議室開會，而不是平常的辦公室？ B：他們需要和財務長【討論】明年的預算，而且約有十五人會來，小會議室根本沒有足夠的椅子。"},{"w":"consider","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something before deciding","c":"考慮","s":"A: The software company in Taichung offered me a higher salary, but it would mean moving away from my family. B: You should consider all the costs before you say yes, because rent, travel and time away from home can be more important than the extra money you earn each month.","t":"A：台中那家軟體公司開給我更高的薪水，但那代表我得離開家人。 B：你答應之前應該【考慮】所有代價，因為房租、交通和離家的時間可能比你每個月多賺的錢更重要。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n.","d":"another thing you can choose instead","c":"替代方案；其他選擇","s":"A: The train workers are on strike tomorrow, so how will our staff get to the trade fair in Kaohsiung on time? B: The best alternative is to rent a large bus for the whole team, which costs a little more but lets us leave from the office together at seven o'clock.","t":"A：鐵路員工明天罷工，我們的員工要怎麼準時到高雄參加商展？ B：最好的【替代方案】是為整個團隊租一輛大巴士，雖然貴一點，但我們可以七點一起從辦公室出發。"},{"w":"option","p":"n.","d":"something you can choose","c":"選項；選擇","s":"A: Our customers want faster delivery, but we can't afford to open another warehouse this year, so what can we do? B: One option is to work with a local delivery company in each city, which would let us send most orders within one day without buying new trucks.","t":"A：顧客想要更快的配送，但我們今年負擔不起再開一間倉庫，那能怎麼辦？ B：一個【選項】是在每個城市和當地的快遞公司合作，這樣不用買新卡車，就能在一天內寄出大部分訂單。"},{"w":"decision","p":"n.","d":"a choice that you make after thinking","c":"決定","s":"A: Has the manager chosen which of the two candidates will lead the new marketing team in Hong Kong? B: Not yet, she says she will make a final decision after the second interviews on Thursday, because both people have strong skills and she wants to see how they work with the team.","t":"A：經理選好兩位應徵者中誰要帶領香港的新行銷團隊了嗎？ B：還沒，她說會在週四第二次面試後做出最後【決定】，因為兩人能力都很強，她想看看他們和團隊合作的情形。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"comments about how good or useful something is","c":"回饋；意見","s":"A: How do you know whether the new training course for sales staff is actually working? B: At the end of every class, we ask the trainees to fill out a short online form and give us honest feedback, and then we change the lessons that they found boring or hard to follow.","t":"A：你怎麼知道銷售人員的新訓練課程到底有沒有效？ B：每堂課結束時，我們都請學員填寫一份簡短的線上表單並給我們誠實的【回饋】，然後我們會修改他們覺得無聊或難以理解的課程。"},{"w":"expert","p":"n.","d":"a person who knows a lot about a subject","c":"專家","s":"A: Our factory uses too much electricity, and the monthly bills have nearly doubled since last winter. B: Let's invite an energy expert to visit the factory next week, because someone with special knowledge can show us which machines waste the most power and how to save money.","t":"A：我們工廠用電太多，每月電費從去年冬天以來幾乎翻倍了。 B：我們邀請一位能源【專家】下週來參觀工廠吧，因為有專業知識的人可以告訴我們哪些機器最耗電，以及如何省錢。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or skill you get from doing something","c":"經驗","s":"A: Why did you choose Mr. Chen to manage the new restaurant, even though he is younger than the other applicants? B: He has ten years of experience in busy hotel kitchens, and he has already trained many young cooks, so I believe he can lead the team well from the first day.","t":"A：為什麼你選陳先生管理新餐廳，即使他比其他應徵者年輕？ B：他有十年在忙碌飯店廚房工作的【經驗】，也已經訓練過許多年輕廚師，所以我相信他從第一天起就能把團隊帶好。"},{"w":"qualified","p":"adj.","d":"having the right training or skills for a job","c":"合格的；有資格的","s":"A: The hospital needs to hire three new nurses for the night shift, but only a few people have applied so far. B: We should keep the job ad online for another month, because we must find qualified staff who hold a nursing license and can safely care for patients on their own.","t":"A：醫院需要為夜班招聘三名新護理師，但目前只有少數人應徵。 B：我們應該讓徵才廣告再刊登一個月，因為我們必須找到持有護理執照、能獨立安全照顧病人的【合格】人員。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something","c":"機會","s":"A: Are you going to apply for the six-month job in our London office that the manager mentioned this morning? B: Definitely, because it's a great opportunity to improve my English, meet international clients, and learn how the European market works before I return to Taipei next year.","t":"A：你要申請經理今天早上提到的倫敦辦公室六個月職缺嗎？ B：一定會，因為這是一個提升英文、認識國際客戶、並在明年回台北前了解歐洲市場運作的好【機會】。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"useful or ready to help","c":"有幫助的；樂於助人的","s":"A: How was your first week at the new branch, and did you have any trouble learning the computer system? B: It went well, because my coworkers were very helpful; they showed me how to enter orders, answered all my questions, and even invited me to lunch on my first day.","t":"A：你在新分店的第一週如何？學電腦系統有遇到困難嗎？ B：很順利，因為我的同事都很【樂於助人】，他們教我怎麼輸入訂單、回答我所有問題，第一天甚至還邀我一起吃午餐。"},{"w":"useful","p":"adj.","d":"helping you to do or get something","c":"有用的；實用的","s":"A: Do you think the time-management workshop last Saturday was worth the money the company paid for it? B: Yes, it was really useful, because the trainer showed us simple ways to plan our week, and I have already finished two reports early by following her ideas.","t":"A：你覺得上週六的時間管理工作坊值得公司付的錢嗎？ B：值得，真的很【實用】，因為講師教我們簡單規劃一週的方法，我照著她的點子已經提早完成兩份報告了。"},{"w":"beneficial","p":"adj.","d":"having a good effect","c":"有益的；有利的","s":"A: Why is the company giving everyone a free gym membership starting next month? B: The managers believe that regular exercise is beneficial for both health and work, because staff who feel fit usually take fewer sick days and have more energy in the afternoon.","t":"A：公司為什麼從下個月開始給每個人免費的健身房會員？ B：主管們認為規律運動對健康和工作都【有益】，因為覺得身體健康的員工通常請病假較少，下午也更有精神。"},{"w":"appropriate","p":"adj.","d":"suitable or right for a situation","c":"適當的；合適的","s":"A: I've been invited to a formal dinner with our Japanese partners next Friday, but I'm not sure what to wear. B: A dark suit and a simple tie would be appropriate, because the dinner is at an expensive restaurant and the partners will probably be dressed quite formally too.","t":"A：我受邀參加下週五和日本合作夥伴的正式晚宴，但不確定要穿什麼。 B：深色西裝配簡單的領帶會很【合適】，因為晚宴在一家昂貴的餐廳，合作夥伴很可能也會穿得相當正式。"},{"w":"effective","p":"adj.","d":"producing the result that you want","c":"有效的","s":"A: Sales of our new juice were very low in the first month, so what changed after that? B: We started giving free samples in supermarkets on weekends, and it was a very effective way to attract shoppers, because sales doubled within three weeks without any TV advertising.","t":"A：我們的新果汁第一個月銷量很差，之後有什麼改變？ B：我們開始在週末於超市提供免費試喝，這是吸引購物者非常【有效】的方法，因為不靠任何電視廣告，銷量在三週內就翻倍了。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to find an answer to a problem","c":"解決","s":"A: Two of our designers have been arguing for days about the colors for the new catalog, and the work has stopped. B: I'll meet with both of them tomorrow morning to resolve the disagreement, because the catalog must go to the printer by Friday and we can't lose any more time.","t":"A：我們兩位設計師為了新型錄的配色已經爭論好幾天，工作都停擺了。 B：我明天早上會和他們兩人見面來【解決】這個分歧，因為型錄週五前一定要送印，我們不能再浪費時間了。"},{"w":"problem","p":"n.","d":"something difficult that needs to be dealt with","c":"問題；難題","s":"A: Why are so many passengers waiting at the gate when the flight to Seoul was supposed to leave an hour ago? B: There is a problem with one of the engines, so the mechanics are checking it carefully, and the airline is giving everyone meal coupons while they wait.","t":"A：飛首爾的班機一小時前就該起飛了，為什麼還有這麼多乘客在登機門等候？ B：其中一具引擎有【問題】，所以技師正在仔細檢查，航空公司也在乘客等待時發放餐券給大家。"},{"w":"difficulty","p":"n.","d":"something that makes it hard to do something","c":"困難","s":"A: Why is the new branch in Bangkok opening two months later than we planned in the spring? B: The managers had great difficulty finding a building in a good location at a fair price, and after that the local government took several weeks to approve the business license.","t":"A：曼谷新分店為什麼比我們春天計畫的晚了兩個月開幕？ B：主管們在尋找地點好、價格合理的建築物時遇到很大的【困難】，之後當地政府又花了好幾週才核准營業執照。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"n.","d":"something new and difficult that tests your ability","c":"挑戰","s":"A: How do you feel about leading the project to open our first store in Vietnam next year? B: It will be a big challenge for me, because I don't speak the language and the market is new to us, but I'm excited and I've already started taking Vietnamese lessons.","t":"A：你對明年帶領在越南開設第一家店的專案有什麼感想？ B：這對我來說會是一大【挑戰】，因為我不會說當地語言，市場對我們也很陌生，但我很興奮，而且已經開始上越南語課了。"},{"w":"inquiry","p":"n.","d":"a question asking for information","c":"詢問；查詢","s":"A: Did anyone reply to the customer who emailed yesterday about our prices for large group tours to Hualien? B: Yes, I answered her inquiry this morning and sent a full price list, and she said she will book a tour for forty employees from her company in October.","t":"A：昨天寄電子郵件詢問花蓮大型團體旅遊價格的那位顧客，有人回覆她嗎？ B：有，我今天早上回覆了她的【詢問】並寄了完整價目表，她說十月會幫公司四十位員工預訂行程。"},{"w":"thank you in advance","p":"phr.","d":"a polite phrase to thank someone before they help you","c":"先謝謝您；預先致謝","s":"A: How should I end my email to the hotel manager asking whether we can use their meeting room for free next month? B: Write that you would be very grateful for their help, then finish with 'thank you in advance for your time,' because it sounds polite and shows that you expect a kind reply.","t":"A：我寫給飯店經理、詢問下個月能否免費使用他們會議室的電子郵件該怎麼結尾？ B：寫上你會非常感謝他們的協助，然後用「【先謝謝您】撥冗回覆」結尾，因為這聽起來很有禮貌，也表示你期待友善的回覆。"}]},{"unit":79,"theme":"Consume 消費；消耗","cards":[{"w":"consumption","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something that is used","c":"消耗；消費量","s":"A: Why did the factory manager ask everyone to turn off their computers and the lights before leaving the office every evening this month? B: Our electricity bill rose by almost twenty percent last quarter, so the company wants to reduce energy consumption and save money before the new budget starts in January.","t":"A：為什麼工廠經理這個月要求大家每天晚上離開辦公室前都關掉電腦和電燈？ B：我們上一季的電費上漲了將近百分之二十，所以公司希望在一月新預算開始前減少能源【消耗】並省錢。"},{"w":"consumer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys goods or services","c":"消費者","s":"A: What did the marketing team learn from the online survey that they sent to our customers after the summer sale? B: They found that the average consumer now compares prices on at least three websites before buying anything, so we need to make our online store faster and our prices clearer.","t":"A：行銷團隊從暑期特賣後寄給顧客的線上問卷中得到了什麼結論？ B：他們發現一般【消費者】現在買任何東西前都會在至少三個網站比價，所以我們需要讓線上商店更快、價格更清楚。"},{"w":"consumable","p":"adj.","d":"used up and needing to be bought again","c":"消耗性的","s":"A: Why does the office manager check the supply room every Friday afternoon before she goes home? B: She makes a list of consumable items such as printer ink, paper, coffee and cleaning products, because the department runs out of them quickly and she must order more before Monday morning.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理每週五下午回家前都要檢查儲藏室？ B：她會列出【消耗性】物品的清單，例如印表機墨水、紙張、咖啡和清潔用品，因為部門很快就會用完，她必須在週一早上前訂購更多。"},{"w":"ingest","p":"v.","d":"to take food, drink or another substance into the body","c":"攝入；吞下","s":"A: Why are the workers in the chemical plant required to wear masks and gloves all day, even when the weather is very hot? B: The safety officer explained that some of the powders are dangerous, and workers could accidentally ingest small amounts if they touch their mouths or breathe the dust.","t":"A：為什麼化學工廠的工人整天都必須戴口罩和手套，即使天氣非常炎熱？ B：安全主管解釋說，有些粉末很危險，如果工人碰到嘴巴或吸入粉塵，可能會不小心【攝入】少量。"},{"w":"devour","p":"v.","d":"to eat something quickly because you are very hungry","c":"狼吞虎嚥","s":"A: How was the lunch meeting with the new sales team at the Italian restaurant near the station yesterday? B: It went well, although everyone was so hungry after the long morning training that they started to devour the pizzas as soon as the waiter put them on the table.","t":"A：昨天和新業務團隊在車站附近義大利餐廳的午餐會議如何？ B：很順利，不過經過一整個早上的長時間訓練大家都很餓，服務生一把披薩放上桌，他們就開始【狼吞虎嚥】。"},{"w":"eat","p":"v.","d":"to put food in your mouth and swallow it","c":"吃；用餐","s":"A: Why do so many staff members leave the building at noon instead of having lunch in the company cafeteria on the third floor? B: Most of them prefer to eat at the small noodle shop across the street, because the food is cheaper, the portions are bigger, and they can relax away from their desks for an hour.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多員工中午都離開大樓，而不在三樓的公司餐廳吃午餐？ B：他們大多數比較喜歡在對街的小麵店【吃飯】，因為食物比較便宜、份量比較大，而且可以離開辦公桌放鬆一個小時。"},{"w":"drink","p":"v.","d":"to take liquid into your mouth and swallow it","c":"喝；飲用","s":"A: Why did the doctor at the company health check tell you to change your habits at work? B: She said I should drink more water during the day instead of so much coffee, because I often feel tired and get headaches in the afternoon while I am sitting at my computer.","t":"A：為什麼公司健康檢查的醫生要你改變工作時的習慣？ B：她說我白天應該【喝】更多水，而不是喝那麼多咖啡，因為我下午坐在電腦前時常覺得疲倦和頭痛。"},{"w":"absorb","p":"v.","d":"to take in liquid, sound, heat or information","c":"吸收","s":"A: Why did the hotel decide to replace all the old carpets in the conference rooms on the second floor last month? B: The new carpets absorb noise much better, so guests in the nearby rooms are no longer disturbed when large groups hold meetings or parties in the evening.","t":"A：為什麼飯店上個月決定更換二樓會議室所有的舊地毯？ B：新地毯【吸收】噪音的效果好得多，所以當大型團體晚上舉行會議或派對時，附近房間的客人不會再被打擾。"},{"w":"utilize","p":"v.","d":"to use something in a practical and useful way","c":"利用；使用","s":"A: How is the new manager planning to improve the warehouse without hiring more workers or buying more machines this year? B: She wants to utilize the empty space at the back of the building more effectively, so she is adding tall shelves and a better labeling system to store more products.","t":"A：新經理打算如何在今年不增聘工人、不添購機器的情況下改善倉庫？ B：她想更有效地【利用】大樓後方的空間，所以正在增加高的貨架和更好的標籤系統，以存放更多產品。"},{"w":"use","p":"v.","d":"to do something with an object or method for a purpose","c":"使用；用","s":"A: Our printer on the fifth floor stopped working again this morning, so what should I do with the contract that the client needs by noon? B: You can use the new color printer in the meeting room next to the elevator, but remember to enter your staff code first so the system can record the copies.","t":"A：五樓的印表機今天早上又壞了，客戶中午前需要的合約我該怎麼辦？ B：你可以【使用】電梯旁會議室裡的新彩色印表機，但記得先輸入你的員工代碼，這樣系統才能記錄影印張數。"},{"w":"expend","p":"v.","d":"to use time, money or effort to do something","c":"耗費；花費","s":"A: Why does the sales director look so tired after the trade fair in Singapore last week? B: She had to expend a great deal of time and effort meeting more than sixty possible buyers in three days, and she also gave two long presentations about our new products.","t":"A：為什麼業務總監上週參加新加坡貿易展後看起來那麼疲倦？ B：她必須在三天內【耗費】大量時間和精力與六十多位潛在買家會面，而且還做了兩場關於我們新產品的長篇簡報。"},{"w":"exhaust","p":"v.","d":"to use all of something so that none is left","c":"用盡；耗盡","s":"A: Why did the project team ask the finance department for extra money only two months after the project started? B: The unexpected repairs to the old building will exhaust most of the original budget by next month, so they need more funds to finish the work on time and pay the contractors.","t":"A：為什麼專案團隊在專案開始僅兩個月後就向財務部要求額外資金？ B：舊大樓意外的維修費用到下個月就會【用光】大部分的原始預算，所以他們需要更多資金來準時完工並支付承包商。"},{"w":"deplete","p":"v.","d":"to reduce the amount of something until little is left","c":"耗盡；大量減少","s":"A: Why has the hotel restaurant stopped serving fresh tuna on its dinner menu this season? B: The chef read a report that overfishing could deplete the tuna population in the Pacific within a few years, so he decided to offer local fish that are easier to find and protect.","t":"A：為什麼飯店餐廳這一季的晚餐菜單停止供應新鮮鮪魚？ B：主廚讀到一份報告指出，過度捕撈可能在幾年內【耗盡】太平洋的鮪魚數量，所以他決定改供應較容易取得、也較能保護的當地魚類。"},{"w":"waste","p":"v.","d":"to use something badly or more than you need","c":"浪費","s":"A: Why did the manager cancel the weekly meeting that usually takes place every Monday morning at nine? B: He said we waste too much time discussing the same small problems every week, so now each team will send a short written report by email instead.","t":"A：為什麼經理取消了通常每週一早上九點舉行的週會？ B：他說我們每週都【浪費】太多時間討論同樣的小問題，所以現在每個團隊改為用電子郵件寄一份簡短的書面報告。"},{"w":"spend","p":"v.","d":"to use money to pay for things; to pass time","c":"花費（金錢、時間）","s":"A: How much does the company plan to invest in the new training program for the customer service staff next year? B: The board agreed to spend about fifty thousand dollars on online courses and workshops, because they believe better training will reduce complaints and help us keep more customers.","t":"A：公司明年打算在客服人員的新訓練計畫上投資多少錢？ B：董事會同意在線上課程和工作坊上【花費】大約五萬美元，因為他們相信更好的訓練能減少客訴，並幫助我們留住更多顧客。"},{"w":"purchase","p":"v.","d":"to buy something","c":"購買","s":"A: Why are so many people waiting outside the electronics store at seven o'clock on a Saturday morning? B: The store is offering half price on laptops for the first hundred customers, so people want to purchase a new computer before the sale ends and the prices go back up.","t":"A：為什麼週六早上七點會有那麼多人在電子產品店外等候？ B：這家店對前一百名顧客提供筆電半價優惠，所以大家想在特價結束、價格回升前【購買】一台新電腦。"},{"w":"acquire","p":"v.","d":"to get or buy something, such as a company","c":"取得；收購","s":"A: Why did the small software company suddenly hire twenty new engineers and move to a bigger office downtown? B: A large international firm plans to acquire the company next spring, so it is growing quickly and preparing to develop more products for customers in Europe and Asia.","t":"A：為什麼那家小型軟體公司突然雇用二十名新工程師，並搬到市中心更大的辦公室？ B：一家大型國際企業計畫明年春天【收購】這家公司，所以它正在快速成長，並準備為歐洲和亞洲的客戶開發更多產品。"},{"w":"intake","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food or drink that you take in","c":"攝取量","s":"A: Why did the company nurse suggest changes to the snacks that are sold in the vending machines on every floor? B: Many employees sit at their desks all day, and she wants to help them lower their daily sugar intake by offering fruit, nuts and yogurt instead of candy and soda.","t":"A：為什麼公司護理師建議更改每層樓自動販賣機裡販售的零食？ B：許多員工整天坐在辦公桌前，她希望提供水果、堅果和優格來取代糖果和汽水，幫助他們降低每日的糖分【攝取量】。"},{"w":"digestion","p":"n.","d":"the process of breaking down food in the body","c":"消化","s":"A: Why does your manager always take a short walk around the park after lunch, even when he is very busy? B: He says that walking for fifteen minutes helps his digestion, so he does not feel heavy and sleepy during the long meetings that usually start at two o'clock.","t":"A：為什麼你的經理午餐後總是在公園散步一下，即使他很忙？ B：他說散步十五分鐘有助於他的【消化】，所以在通常兩點開始的冗長會議中，他不會覺得肚子脹、昏昏欲睡。"},{"w":"appetite","p":"n.","d":"the wish to eat; a strong wish for something","c":"食慾；胃口；渴望","s":"A: How did the new marketing campaign for our frozen meals perform in the first three months? B: It was very successful, because the colorful photos of hot food really increased customers' appetite for our products, and our sales in supermarkets went up by thirty percent.","t":"A：我們冷凍餐點的新行銷活動在前三個月表現如何？ B：非常成功，因為熱騰騰食物的繽紛照片真的提升了顧客對我們產品的【胃口】，我們在超市的銷售量增加了百分之三十。"},{"w":"gluttony","p":"n.","d":"the habit of eating and drinking too much","c":"暴飲暴食；貪吃","s":"A: Why did the restaurant critic give the new all-you-can-eat buffet such a negative review in the magazine? B: She wrote that the place encourages gluttony rather than good taste, because guests pile huge amounts of food on their plates and then throw much of it away.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳評論家在雜誌上給新開的吃到飽自助餐這麼負面的評價？ B：她寫道那個地方鼓勵的是【暴飲暴食】而不是好品味，因為客人把大量食物堆在盤子上，然後又丟掉很多。"},{"w":"voracious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting a lot of food or a lot of something","c":"貪婪的；求知若渴的","s":"A: Why is the new intern always the first person to finish the reports and manuals that the manager hands out? B: She is a voracious reader who often reads two or three business books every week, so she can understand long documents quickly and remember the important details.","t":"A：為什麼新來的實習生總是第一個讀完經理發下來的報告和手冊？ B：她是個【求知若渴的】讀者，常常每週讀兩三本商業書籍，所以能快速理解長篇文件並記住重要細節。"},{"w":"edible","p":"adj.","d":"safe or good enough to eat","c":"可食用的","s":"A: What did the catering company use to decorate the cake for the director's retirement party last Friday? B: They covered it with edible flowers made from sugar and colored chocolate, so the guests could enjoy every part of the cake and nothing had to be thrown away.","t":"A：外燴公司上週五用什麼來裝飾總監退休派對的蛋糕？ B：他們用糖和彩色巧克力做成的【可食用的】花朵覆蓋蛋糕，所以客人可以享用蛋糕的每一部分，沒有任何東西需要丟掉。"},{"w":"potable","p":"adj.","d":"(of water) clean and safe to drink","c":"可飲用的","s":"A: Why does the construction company need to bring large water tanks to the new building site outside the city? B: There is no potable water in the area yet, so the workers need clean water for drinking and cooking until the local government connects the site to the main pipes.","t":"A：為什麼建設公司需要把大型水箱運到城外的新工地？ B：那個地區還沒有【可飲用的】水，所以在地方政府把工地接上主要水管之前，工人需要乾淨的水來飲用和煮飯。"},{"w":"disposable","p":"adj.","d":"made to be used once and then thrown away","c":"用完即丟的；一次性的","s":"A: Why did the café near our office start charging customers ten dollars extra for each cup this month? B: The city introduced a new rule to reduce plastic waste, so shops must charge for disposable cups, and customers who bring their own mugs now get a small discount.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近的咖啡館這個月開始每杯向顧客多收十元？ B：市政府推出減少塑膠垃圾的新規定，所以商店必須對【一次性】杯子收費，而自備杯子的顧客現在可以享有小折扣。"},{"w":"recyclable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be processed and used again","c":"可回收的","s":"A: Why did our company change the packaging for all of its skin care products this year? B: Many customers complained that the old boxes were too heavy and full of plastic, so we switched to recyclable paper packaging that people can put in the blue bins at home.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司今年更換了所有護膚產品的包裝？ B：許多顧客抱怨舊盒子太重而且充滿塑膠，所以我們改用【可回收的】紙製包裝，讓大家可以在家丟進藍色回收桶。"},{"w":"overuse","p":"v.","d":"to use something too much","c":"過度使用","s":"A: Why did the IT department send everyone an email about the shared online storage system yesterday afternoon? B: Some teams overuse the system by saving large video files there every day, so it has become very slow, and the department now asks staff to delete old files.","t":"A：為什麼資訊部門昨天下午寄電子郵件給大家，說明共用線上儲存系統的事？ B：有些團隊每天在那裡存放大型影片檔，【過度使用】這個系統，導致它變得很慢，所以部門現在要求員工刪除舊檔案。"},{"w":"misuse","p":"v.","d":"to use something in a wrong or dishonest way","c":"濫用；誤用","s":"A: Why was the regional manager asked to leave the company after the annual audit last month? B: The auditors discovered that he continued to misuse the company credit card for personal trips and expensive dinners with friends, even after he had been warned twice by the finance director.","t":"A：為什麼區域經理在上個月的年度稽核後被要求離開公司？ B：稽核人員發現他持續【濫用】公司信用卡支付私人旅行和與朋友的昂貴晚餐，即使財務總監已經警告過他兩次。"},{"w":"depletion","p":"n.","d":"a big reduction in the amount of something","c":"耗盡；枯竭","s":"A: Why is the fishing company investing so much money in fish farms along the coast instead of buying new boats? B: The managers are worried about the depletion of wild fish in the ocean, and they believe farming will give them a more stable supply for many years.","t":"A：為什麼漁業公司把那麼多錢投資在沿海的養殖場，而不是購買新船？ B：經理們擔心海洋中野生魚類的【枯竭】，他們相信養殖能在未來多年提供更穩定的供應。"},{"w":"energy","p":"n.","d":"power from electricity, fuel, the sun, etc. used to run machines","c":"能源；精力","s":"A: Why did the company install solar panels on the roof of the main factory last summer? B: The managers wanted to produce clean energy for the machines and lights, and they expect the panels to cut the monthly electricity bill by almost a third over the next ten years.","t":"A：為什麼公司去年夏天在主工廠屋頂安裝太陽能板？ B：經理們想為機器和照明生產乾淨的【能源】，他們預期這些太陽能板在未來十年能把每月電費減少將近三分之一。"},{"w":"resource","p":"n.","d":"something useful that a person or company can use","c":"資源","s":"A: Why does the training manager always tell new employees to talk to Ms. Chen in the accounting department? B: She has worked here for twenty years and knows every system and client, so she is a valuable resource for anyone who has questions about company rules or old projects.","t":"A：為什麼訓練經理總是叫新員工去找會計部的陳小姐談談？ B：她在這裡工作了二十年，熟悉每個系統和客戶，所以對任何有公司規定或舊專案問題的人來說，她都是寶貴的【資源】。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"n.","d":"something such as gas or oil that is burned to make power","c":"燃料","s":"A: Why did the delivery company decide to replace half of its old trucks with electric vans this year? B: The price of fuel has risen sharply over the past two years, and electric vans are cheaper to run, so the company expects to save money while also reducing pollution in the city.","t":"A：為什麼快遞公司今年決定把一半的舊卡車換成電動廂型車？ B：過去兩年【燃料】價格大幅上漲，而電動廂型車的營運成本較低，所以公司預期能省錢，同時減少城市的污染。"},{"w":"calorie","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring the energy in food","c":"卡路里；熱量","s":"A: What kind of lunch boxes is the company cafeteria going to offer for staff who want to eat more healthily? B: The chef is creating a new low-calorie menu with grilled chicken, brown rice and fresh vegetables, and each box will show nutrition information so people can choose wisely.","t":"A：公司餐廳打算為想吃得更健康的員工提供什麼樣的便當？ B：主廚正在設計一份新的低【熱量】菜單，有烤雞、糙米和新鮮蔬菜，而且每個便當都會標示營養資訊，讓大家能聰明地選擇。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to continue without harming the environment","c":"永續的；可持續的","s":"A: Why did the hotel group stop buying cheap furniture from its old supplier in Southeast Asia? B: Investors asked the company to become more sustainable, so it now buys tables and chairs made from wood that comes from carefully managed forests, even though they cost a little more.","t":"A：為什麼這家飯店集團停止向東南亞的舊供應商購買便宜家具？ B：投資人要求公司變得更具【永續性】，所以現在改買來自妥善管理森林的木材製成的桌椅，即使價格稍微貴一點。"}]},{"unit":80,"theme":"Contribute 貢獻","cards":[{"w":"contribution","p":"n.","d":"something you give or do to help something succeed","c":"貢獻；捐款","s":"A: Why did the director mention Linda by name during the end-of-year party at the hotel last night? B: She wanted to thank her for her important contribution to the new online store, because Linda designed the payment system that helped us double our sales in only six months.","t":"A：昨晚在飯店的年終派對上，主任為什麼特別點名琳達？ B：她想感謝琳達對新網路商店的重要【貢獻】，因為琳達設計了付款系統，幫助我們在短短六個月內讓銷售額翻倍。"},{"w":"contributor","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives money, work or ideas to something","c":"貢獻者；撰稿人","s":"A: Who wrote the article about saving energy in the office that appeared in this month's company newsletter? B: It was written by Mr. Tanaka from the engineering team, and he is now a regular contributor to the newsletter, so he will send us a new article every two months.","t":"A：這個月公司通訊裡那篇關於辦公室節能的文章是誰寫的？ B：是工程團隊的田中先生寫的，他現在是通訊的固定【撰稿人】，所以他每兩個月會寄一篇新文章給我們。"},{"w":"donate","p":"v.","d":"to give money or goods to help a person or group","c":"捐贈；捐款","s":"A: What are we going to do with all the old laptops and office chairs after we move to the new building next month? B: The manager has decided to donate them to a local school, since they still work well and the students there really need more computers for their classes.","t":"A：下個月搬到新大樓後，我們要怎麼處理那些舊筆電和辦公椅？ B：經理決定把它們【捐贈】給當地一所學校，因為它們還很好用，而那裡的學生上課很需要更多電腦。"},{"w":"donation","p":"n.","d":"money or goods that you give to help a person or group","c":"捐款；捐贈物","s":"A: How much money did our staff raise at the charity bake sale in the lobby last Friday afternoon? B: We collected almost two thousand dollars, and the company agreed to match every donation, so the children's hospital will receive four thousand dollars for new equipment.","t":"A：上週五下午我們員工在大廳舉辦的慈善烘焙義賣籌到多少錢？ B：我們募到將近兩千美元，而且公司同意對每一筆【捐款】提供相同金額，所以兒童醫院將收到四千美元購買新設備。"},{"w":"donor","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that gives money or goods to help","c":"捐贈者","s":"A: Why is there a new name on the wall next to the entrance of the city library this week? B: That is the name of the largest donor, a local businessman who gave half a million dollars to build the new reading room and buy hundreds of children's books.","t":"A：這週市立圖書館入口旁的牆上為什麼多了一個新名字？ B：那是最大【捐贈者】的名字，他是一位本地商人，捐了五十萬美元興建新閱覽室，並購買了數百本童書。"},{"w":"support","p":"n.","d":"help or encouragement that you give to someone","c":"支持；支援","s":"A: How did your small team finish the huge marketing report before the deadline, even though two people were sick last week? B: We could not have done it without the support of the sales department, because they sent us three extra people to collect data and check the numbers.","t":"A：雖然上週有兩個人生病，你們的小團隊是怎麼在截止日前完成那份龐大的行銷報告的？ B：沒有業務部的【支援】我們不可能做到，因為他們派了三個額外人手來幫我們蒐集資料和核對數字。"},{"w":"assistance","p":"n.","d":"help","c":"協助；幫助","s":"A: I'm having trouble with the new booking system, and three customers are waiting at the front desk right now. B: Don't worry, just call the IT office on extension 205, and someone will give you assistance within a few minutes, because they are on duty all morning to deal with problems like this.","t":"A：我在新的訂位系統上遇到問題，而且現在有三位客人在櫃台等著。 B：別擔心，只要打分機205給資訊室，幾分鐘內就會有人給你【協助】，因為他們整個早上都在值班處理這類問題。"},{"w":"aid","p":"n.","d":"help such as money, food or supplies for people in need","c":"援助；救助","s":"A: Why are so many boxes of food, water, and blankets stacked near the loading area of our warehouse today? B: Our company is sending emergency aid to the towns that were hit by the flood last weekend, and the trucks will leave for the south early tomorrow morning.","t":"A：今天我們倉庫的裝卸區附近為什麼堆了那麼多箱食物、水和毛毯？ B：我們公司要將緊急【援助】物資送到上週末遭受水災的城鎮，卡車明天一早就會出發前往南部。"},{"w":"help","p":"v.","d":"to make it easier for someone to do something","c":"幫助；幫忙","s":"A: The new intern looks a bit lost at her desk, and she has been staring at that spreadsheet for almost an hour. B: Could you go over and help her with the formulas for a while, since you know the program better than anyone else in this office?","t":"A：新來的實習生坐在座位上看起來有點不知所措，她盯著那張試算表快一個小時了。 B：你可以過去【幫】她弄一下公式嗎？畢竟你比辦公室裡任何人都熟悉這個程式。"},{"w":"volunteer","p":"v.","d":"to offer to do something without being asked or paid","c":"自願；當志工","s":"A: Who is going to stay late on Friday to welcome the visitors from our partner company in Germany? B: Kevin and Mia decided to volunteer for the job, because they both speak some German and they thought it would be a good chance to practice and meet new people.","t":"A：週五誰會留晚一點迎接我們德國合作公司的訪客？ B：凱文和米亞決定【自願】擔任這份工作，因為他們都會說一點德語，而且他們覺得這是練習和認識新朋友的好機會。"},{"w":"voluntary","p":"adj.","d":"done because you want to, not because you must","c":"自願的；義務的","s":"A: Do all employees have to join the English training class that starts every Wednesday evening next month? B: No, the class is completely voluntary, so you can decide for yourself, but the manager hopes that people who often talk with foreign clients will try to attend.","t":"A：下個月每週三晚上開始的英語訓練課，所有員工都必須參加嗎？ B：不用，這門課完全是【自願參加的】，所以你可以自己決定，不過經理希望常和外國客戶交談的人能盡量出席。"},{"w":"sponsor","p":"v.","d":"to pay for an event or activity, often to advertise your company","c":"贊助","s":"A: Why is our company logo printed on all the T-shirts for the city marathon this year? B: The board agreed to sponsor the race for three years, because thousands of runners and their families will see our name, and it shows that we care about health in the community.","t":"A：為什麼今年城市馬拉松的所有T恤上都印著我們公司的標誌？ B：董事會同意【贊助】這場比賽三年，因為成千上萬的跑者和他們的家人都會看到我們的名字，而且這顯示我們關心社區的健康。"},{"w":"sponsorship","p":"n.","d":"money or support given to pay for an event or activity","c":"贊助","s":"A: How can the drama club pay for the costumes and the theater for its big show in December? B: The club leader is asking several banks and restaurants downtown for sponsorship, and in return their names will appear on the posters and in the program for the show.","t":"A：戲劇社要怎麼支付十二月大型演出的服裝和劇場費用？ B：社長正在向市中心幾家銀行和餐廳尋求【贊助】，作為回報，他們的名字會出現在海報和演出節目單上。"},{"w":"fund","p":"v.","d":"to provide money for something","c":"資助；提供資金","s":"A: Is the government going to pay for the new bus line between the airport and the business park? B: Yes, the city will fund most of the project, but two large companies in the park will also pay part of the cost, because their workers will use the buses every day.","t":"A：政府會出錢興建機場和商業園區之間的新公車路線嗎？ B：會，市政府將【資助】這項計畫的大部分費用，不過園區裡的兩家大公司也會負擔部分成本，因為他們的員工每天都會搭這些公車。"},{"w":"funding","p":"n.","d":"money that is given for a particular purpose","c":"資金；經費","s":"A: Why did the science team stop working on the new battery project after only one year? B: They lost their funding when the main investor pulled out last spring, and without money they could not pay for the expensive machines and the salaries of the researchers.","t":"A：為什麼科學團隊才做了一年就停止新電池計畫？ B：去年春天主要投資者退出後，他們就失去了【資金】，沒有錢就付不起昂貴的機器和研究人員的薪水。"},{"w":"subsidize","p":"v.","d":"to pay part of the cost of something","c":"補助；補貼","s":"A: How can the factory workers afford such nice lunches in the staff cafeteria when food prices are rising so fast? B: The company has decided to subsidize the meals, so each worker only pays half the real price, and the rest comes out of the welfare budget.","t":"A：食物價格漲得這麼快，工廠員工怎麼吃得起員工餐廳那麼好的午餐？ B：公司決定【補貼】餐費，所以每位員工只需付實際價格的一半，其餘由福利預算支付。"},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity or event","c":"參加；參與","s":"A: Are you going to join the sales training in Taichung next week, or do you have too many meetings with clients? B: I plan to participate in the first two days, but I have to come back on Wednesday to meet an important customer from Japan at our main office.","t":"A：你下週會去參加台中的業務訓練嗎？還是你和客戶的會議太多了？ B：我打算【參加】前兩天，但週三我必須回來，在總公司和一位重要的日本客戶見面。"},{"w":"participation","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something","c":"參與；參加","s":"A: Why did the HR manager look so pleased at the end of the staff meeting this afternoon? B: She was happy about the high level of participation in the health survey, because almost ninety percent of the employees answered all the questions before the deadline.","t":"A：今天下午員工會議結束時，人資經理為什麼看起來那麼滿意？ B：她很高興健康調查的【參與】度很高，因為將近百分之九十的員工都在截止日前回答了所有問題。"},{"w":"engage","p":"v.","d":"to get someone interested and involved in something","c":"吸引…參與；參與","s":"A: What is the main goal of the new social media plan that the marketing team presented this morning? B: They want to engage young customers by posting short videos and asking questions, so that people will comment, share their ideas, and feel closer to our brand.","t":"A：行銷團隊今天早上提出的新社群媒體計畫，主要目標是什麼？ B：他們想藉由發布短片和提問來【吸引】年輕顧客參與，讓大家留言、分享想法，並覺得和我們的品牌更親近。"},{"w":"involvement","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something","c":"參與；牽涉","s":"A: Why does the director want the store managers to attend the planning meetings for next year's products? B: She believes their involvement is very important, because they talk to customers every day and know which items sell well and which ones stay on the shelves.","t":"A：為什麼主任希望門市經理參加明年產品的規劃會議？ B：她認為他們的【參與】非常重要，因為他們每天和顧客交談，知道哪些商品賣得好、哪些一直擺在架上。"},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others to make or do something","c":"合作；協作","s":"A: How will the design team in Taipei and the engineers in Singapore finish the new phone app by March? B: They will collaborate closely through video meetings every morning, and they will share all their files online so that both teams can see the latest changes at any time.","t":"A：台北的設計團隊和新加坡的工程師要怎麼在三月前完成新的手機應用程式？ B：他們每天早上會透過視訊會議密切【合作】，並把所有檔案放在網路上共享，讓兩個團隊隨時都能看到最新的修改。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together with others","c":"合作","s":"A: Did you hear that our coffee shop chain is going to sell cakes from that famous French bakery next month? B: Yes, the new menu is the result of a collaboration between the two companies, and both sides hope it will bring more customers into the shops in the afternoon.","t":"A：你有沒有聽說我們的咖啡連鎖店下個月要販售那家知名法式麵包店的蛋糕？ B：有啊，新菜單是兩家公司【合作】的成果，雙方都希望這能在下午吸引更多顧客進店。"},{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together or do what someone asks","c":"合作；配合","s":"A: The fire safety inspectors are coming to check the whole building on Thursday morning, aren't they? B: Yes, and the manager has asked all of us to cooperate with them fully, so please open every storage room and answer their questions honestly when they visit our floor.","t":"A：消防安全檢查員週四早上要來檢查整棟大樓，對吧？ B：對，經理要求我們全力【配合】他們，所以當他們來到我們這層樓時，請打開每一間儲藏室，並誠實回答他們的問題。"},{"w":"cooperation","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together to get something done","c":"合作；配合","s":"A: Why did the train company send an email to all passengers about the station repairs this weekend? B: They wanted to explain the changes to the timetable and thank everyone for their cooperation, because some trains will be slower and the main entrance will be closed for two days.","t":"A：火車公司為什麼寄電子郵件給所有乘客，說明本週末的車站維修？ B：他們想說明時刻表的變動，並感謝大家的【配合】，因為有些列車會比較慢，主要入口也會關閉兩天。"},{"w":"assist","p":"v.","d":"to help someone","c":"協助；幫助","s":"A: The new cashier is starting work on Monday, but nobody has shown her how to use the cash register yet. B: Don't worry, Linda will stay with her for the first week to assist her with difficult customers and show her how to handle returns and credit card problems.","t":"A：新收銀員週一開始上班，但還沒有人教她怎麼使用收銀機。 B：別擔心，第一週琳達會陪著她，【協助】她應付難搞的顧客，並教她如何處理退貨和信用卡的問題。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to use something together with others; to tell others something","c":"分享；共用","s":"A: Why are you moving all your things out of your office this afternoon? Is something wrong? B: Nothing is wrong, but our department is getting two new managers, so I have to share a room with Peter until the renovation on the fifth floor is finished in June.","t":"A：你今天下午為什麼要把東西全部搬出辦公室？發生什麼事了嗎？ B：沒什麼事，只是我們部門要來兩位新經理，所以在五樓的整修六月完工之前，我得和彼得【共用】一間辦公室。"},{"w":"provide","p":"v.","d":"to give someone something they need","c":"提供","s":"A: Do we need to bring our own lunch to the training workshop at the hotel on Saturday? B: No, the organizers will provide lunch and coffee for everyone, but you should bring a notebook and a pen, because the trainer will ask us to write down a lot of ideas.","t":"A：週六在飯店舉辦的培訓工作坊，我們需要自備午餐嗎？ B：不用，主辦單位會為每個人【提供】午餐和咖啡，但你應該帶筆記本和筆，因為講師會要我們寫下很多想法。"},{"w":"offer","p":"v.","d":"to say you are willing to give or do something","c":"提供；主動提出","s":"A: The hotel was fully booked when we arrived last night, so what did the receptionist do for us? B: She apologized many times and decided to offer us a free room at their sister hotel nearby, and she also called a taxi to take us there with our luggage.","t":"A：我們昨晚抵達時飯店已經客滿了，那櫃台人員幫我們做了什麼？ B：她道歉了好多次，並決定【提供】我們附近姊妹飯店的一間免費房間，還叫了計程車載我們和行李過去。"},{"w":"give","p":"v.","d":"to let someone have something","c":"給；給予","s":"A: What should I do with the extra tickets for the company concert, since my family can't come on Saturday? B: You could give them to the new staff in the accounting department, because they just moved to the city and probably don't have many plans for the weekend yet.","t":"A：我家人週六不能來，公司音樂會多出來的票我該怎麼處理？ B：你可以把票【給】會計部的新同事，因為他們剛搬到這個城市，週末可能還沒有什麼安排。"},{"w":"input","p":"n.","d":"ideas, advice or information that you give to help with something","c":"意見；投入","s":"A: Why did the manager invite the delivery drivers to the meeting about the new warehouse layout? B: She wanted their input before making a final decision, because the drivers load and unload the trucks every day and know exactly where the shelves and doors should go.","t":"A：經理為什麼邀請送貨司機參加新倉庫配置的會議？ B：她想在做最後決定之前聽聽他們的【意見】，因為司機每天都在裝卸貨車，非常清楚貨架和門應該放在哪裡。"},{"w":"back","p":"v.","d":"to support a person, plan or idea","c":"支持；支援","s":"A: Do you think the board will agree to open a new branch in Kaohsiung next year? B: I think so, because the two biggest shareholders have already said they will back the plan, and the market research shows strong demand for our products in southern Taiwan.","t":"A：你覺得董事會會同意明年在高雄開設新分公司嗎？ B：我想會，因為兩位最大股東已經表示會【支持】這個計畫，而且市場調查顯示台灣南部對我們的產品需求強勁。"},{"w":"endorse","p":"v.","d":"to say publicly that you support a person, product or idea","c":"支持；背書；代言","s":"A: Why did sales of our new running shoes go up so quickly after the first week? B: A famous Olympic runner agreed to endorse them on her social media, and after she posted a video of her training in our shoes, thousands of young people ordered a pair online.","t":"A：我們的新款跑鞋為什麼在第一週後銷量就迅速上升？ B：一位知名奧運跑者同意在她的社群媒體上為這款鞋【代言】，她發布穿著我們的鞋訓練的影片後，成千上萬的年輕人上網訂購了一雙。"},{"w":"pitch in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to join others and help with work","c":"出一份力；幫忙","s":"A: How will we get all these boxes packed before the moving company arrives at eight tomorrow morning? B: If everyone in the department can pitch in for an hour after work today, we should finish in time, and the manager has promised to buy pizza for all of us.","t":"A：搬家公司明天早上八點就要到了，我們要怎麼在那之前把這些箱子全部打包好？ B：如果部門裡每個人今天下班後都能【幫忙】一個小時，我們應該能及時完成，而且經理答應請大家吃披薩。"},{"w":"play a part","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help cause something; to be one of the reasons for it","c":"起作用；扮演角色","s":"A: Our team won the customer service award this year, but why did the director thank the cleaning staff in her speech? B: She said that everyone in the building helps us, and that the cleaners also play a part in our success, because a clean and comfortable lobby makes visitors feel welcome before they even talk to us.","t":"A：我們團隊今年贏得了客服獎，但主任為什麼在致詞中感謝清潔人員？ B：她說大樓裡的每個人都在幫助我們，清潔人員也在我們的成功中【發揮了作用】，因為乾淨舒適的大廳能讓訪客在和我們交談之前就感到賓至如歸。"}]},{"unit":81,"theme":"Conversation 對話","cards":[{"w":"lecturer","p":"n.","d":"a person who teaches at a university or gives talks","c":"講師","s":"A: Who will lead the two-day training course on business writing that the human resources department has organized for new employees next month? B: A lecturer from the local university will teach it, because she has taught report writing to adults for many years and also worked as an editor for a newspaper.","t":"A：人資部門為新進員工安排了下個月為期兩天的商業寫作訓練課程，由誰來帶？ B：當地大學的一位【講師】會來教，因為她多年來一直教成人寫報告，也曾在報社擔任編輯。"},{"w":"impress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone admire or respect you","c":"使印象深刻；使欽佩","s":"A: Why did the sales director invite you to join the meeting with the new clients from Singapore this afternoon? B: She wants me to impress them with the short video I made about our factory, because she thinks it shows our quality control better than any long report could.","t":"A：業務總監為什麼邀請你參加今天下午和新加坡新客戶的會議？ B：她希望我用我製作的那支關於我們工廠的短片讓他們【留下深刻印象】，因為她認為那支影片比任何冗長的報告都更能展現我們的品質管控。"},{"w":"admit","p":"v.","d":"to agree that something is true, often something bad","c":"承認","s":"A: How did the project manager react when the client asked why the new website was still not working last Friday? B: He decided to admit that our team had made a mistake in the payment system, and then he promised to fix the problem before the end of the weekend.","t":"A：上週五客戶問為什麼新網站還不能用時，專案經理有什麼反應？ B：他決定【承認】我們團隊在付款系統上出了錯，接著承諾在週末結束前修好問題。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something or work harder","c":"激勵；激發","s":"A: What do you usually say to the new sales staff when they feel tired after a long week of phone calls without many results? B: I try to motivate them by sharing stories of my own first year, when I also failed often but slowly learned how to win customers' trust.","t":"A：新進業務人員打了一整週電話卻沒什麼成果、感到疲累時，你通常會對他們說什麼？ B：我會試著分享我自己第一年的故事來【激勵】他們，那時我也常常失敗，但慢慢學會了如何贏得客戶的信任。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new and interesting ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team choose Lisa to plan the opening event for our new café downtown? B: She always has creative ideas, such as the free coffee tasting she organized last year, and her events usually attract many young customers who share photos online.","t":"A：行銷團隊為什麼選擇麗莎來籌劃我們市中心新咖啡店的開幕活動？ B：她總是有很【有創意的】點子，像是她去年舉辦的免費咖啡品嚐會，而且她的活動通常會吸引很多會在網路上分享照片的年輕顧客。"},{"w":"effective","p":"adj.","d":"working well and producing the result you want","c":"有效的","s":"A: Have you found a good way to keep the weekly team meeting short now that so many people join it online from different offices? B: The most effective method has been sending the agenda one day early, so everyone comes prepared and we usually finish in under thirty minutes.","t":"A：現在有那麼多人從不同辦公室線上參加，你有找到讓每週團隊會議保持簡短的好方法嗎？ B：最【有效的】方法是提前一天寄出議程，這樣大家都有備而來，我們通常不到三十分鐘就能結束。"},{"w":"monopolize","p":"v.","d":"to take all of something, such as a conversation, so others cannot share it","c":"獨占；壟斷","s":"A: Why did the chairperson set a two-minute time limit for each speaker at the residents' meeting last night? B: At the last meeting, one man tried to monopolize the discussion for almost an hour, so many other neighbors never had a chance to share their opinions about the parking problem.","t":"A：主席昨晚為什麼在住戶會議上給每位發言者設兩分鐘的時間限制？ B：上次開會時有一位男士幾乎花了一個小時想【獨占】討論，所以很多其他鄰居根本沒有機會分享他們對停車問題的意見。"},{"w":"anxiety","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry or nervousness","c":"焦慮；不安","s":"A: Why does Tom always practice his presentations so many times in the empty meeting room before he talks to the board? B: He feels a lot of anxiety when he speaks in front of senior managers, so repeating the slides again and again helps him stay calm and remember the numbers.","t":"A：湯姆為什麼在向董事會報告前，總是在空會議室裡練習那麼多次？ B：他在高階主管面前說話時會感到很【焦慮】，所以一遍又一遍地練習投影片能幫助他保持冷靜並記住數字。"},{"w":"nearly","p":"adv.","d":"almost; not quite","c":"幾乎；將近","s":"A: How long did the phone call with the angry customer from the hotel chain last this morning? B: It went on for nearly two hours, because he wanted to discuss every single problem with the last delivery, and I could not end the call politely until he felt satisfied.","t":"A：今天早上和那位飯店連鎖集團的憤怒客戶通電話，講了多久？ B：講了【將近】兩個小時，因為他想討論上一批貨的每一個問題，在他滿意之前我無法禮貌地結束通話。"},{"w":"utmost","p":"adj.","d":"greatest; most important","c":"最大的；極度的","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager spend so much time training the front desk staff on how to speak with guests? B: She believes that every guest deserves the utmost respect, even when they are tired or rude after a long flight, because a kind conversation can change their whole stay.","t":"A：飯店經理為什麼花那麼多時間訓練櫃檯人員如何和客人說話？ B：她相信每位客人都應該得到【最大的】尊重，即使他們在長途飛行後很疲累或無禮也一樣，因為一段親切的對話可以改變他們整個住宿的體驗。"},{"w":"enhance","p":"v.","d":"to make something better or improve its quality","c":"提高；增強","s":"A: Why did the company pay for all customer service staff to take a weekend course on telephone skills? B: The managers want to enhance the way we speak with callers, because last year's survey showed that many customers felt our replies were too short and not very friendly.","t":"A：公司為什麼出錢讓所有客服人員參加週末的電話技巧課程？ B：主管們想【提升】我們和來電者說話的方式，因為去年的調查顯示，很多客戶覺得我們的回覆太簡短，也不太友善。"},{"w":"captivating","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting and holding your attention","c":"迷人的；引人入勝的","s":"A: What did you think of the speaker who opened the marketing conference in the main hall this morning? B: She was truly captivating, because she told funny stories about her first failed business, and the whole crowd stayed quiet and listened carefully for the full forty minutes.","t":"A：你覺得今天早上在主廳為行銷研討會開場的講者怎麼樣？ B：她真的很【引人入勝】，因為她講了自己第一次創業失敗的有趣故事，全場群眾在整整四十分鐘裡都安靜專心地聆聽。"},{"w":"suffer","p":"v.","d":"to become worse or be hurt by something","c":"受損；受苦","s":"A: Why did the director decide to stop sending so many emails and hold short face-to-face meetings every Monday instead? B: She noticed that teamwork began to suffer when people only wrote messages, because small problems became big arguments that could have been solved in a quick talk.","t":"A：主任為什麼決定不再寄那麼多電子郵件，改成每週一開簡短的面對面會議？ B：她注意到大家只用寫訊息溝通時，團隊合作開始【受到影響】，因為小問題變成了大爭吵，而這些本來只要簡單談一下就能解決。"},{"w":"judgmental","p":"adj.","d":"too quick to criticize or form opinions about people","c":"愛評斷人的；武斷的","s":"A: Why do so many junior staff members feel comfortable sharing their problems with the new team leader? B: She listens carefully and is never judgmental, so people can explain their mistakes honestly without worrying that she will think they are lazy or not smart enough.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多資淺員工都願意跟新的組長分享他們的問題？ B：她會仔細聆聽，而且從不【愛評斷人】，所以大家可以誠實說出自己的錯誤，不用擔心她會認為他們懶惰或不夠聰明。"},{"w":"aspersion","p":"n.","d":"an unkind remark that attacks someone's character","c":"誹謗；中傷","s":"A: Why was the accountant so upset after the budget meeting with the finance director yesterday afternoon? B: When she asked about the missing receipts, he made a rude aspersion on her honesty in front of the whole team, even though she had done nothing wrong and had reported the problem herself.","t":"A：會計師昨天下午和財務長開完預算會議後，為什麼那麼生氣？ B：她詢問遺失的收據時，他當著整個團隊的面無禮地【中傷】她的誠信，即使她什麼都沒做錯，而且問題還是她自己報告的。"},{"w":"devote","p":"v.","d":"to give time or energy to something","c":"投入；奉獻","s":"A: How will the new manager improve communication between the sales team and the warehouse staff this year? B: She plans to devote the first hour of every Wednesday to a joint meeting, so both groups can talk about orders, delays and customer complaints before small problems grow.","t":"A：新經理今年要如何改善業務團隊和倉庫人員之間的溝通？ B：她打算把每週三的第一個小時【專門用於】聯合會議，讓兩邊可以在小問題擴大之前討論訂單、延誤和客戶抱怨。"},{"w":"prepare","p":"v.","d":"to get ready or make something ready","c":"準備","s":"A: Do you have any advice before my first phone interview with the airline company tomorrow morning? B: You should prepare short answers to common questions about your experience, and keep your notes next to the phone, because it is easy to forget important details when you feel nervous.","t":"A：明天早上我第一次跟航空公司進行電話面試，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：你應該針對常見的經歷問題【準備】簡短的回答，並把筆記放在電話旁邊，因為緊張時很容易忘記重要的細節。"},{"w":"material","p":"n.","d":"information or documents used for a purpose","c":"資料；材料","s":"A: What will we give the visitors from the Japanese bank when they arrive for the product presentation on Thursday? B: Each guest will receive a folder with printed material about our services, including price lists and contact details, so they can read it again on the train home.","t":"A：週四日本銀行的訪客來參加產品簡報時，我們要給他們什麼？ B：每位客人會收到一個資料夾，裡面有關於我們服務的印刷【資料】，包括價目表和聯絡方式，讓他們可以在回程的火車上再看一遍。"},{"w":"critique","p":"n.","d":"a careful judgment of the good and bad parts of something","c":"評論；評析","s":"A: Why did the design team ask the senior architect to look at their plans for the new library before the meeting with the city? B: They wanted an honest critique of their ideas, because she has built many public buildings and can quickly see weak points that the city officials might question.","t":"A：設計團隊為什麼在和市政府開會前，請資深建築師看他們的新圖書館設計圖？ B：他們想要聽到對自己構想的誠實【評論】，因為她蓋過許多公共建築，能很快看出市府官員可能會質疑的弱點。"},{"w":"intend","p":"v.","d":"to plan or mean to do something","c":"打算；意圖","s":"A: Are you going to tell the client about the shipping delay today, or will you wait until the goods arrive at the port? B: I intend to call him this afternoon, because hearing bad news early is always better than finding out at the last minute when nothing can be changed.","t":"A：你今天要告訴客戶出貨延誤的事，還是要等貨到港口再說？ B：我【打算】今天下午打電話給他，因為提早聽到壞消息總比在最後一刻、什麼都無法改變時才知道要好。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the group of people who watch or listen to a talk or show","c":"觀眾；聽眾","s":"A: How many people are expected to attend the CEO's speech at the annual meeting in the convention center next week? B: The audience will be about five hundred people, including investors and reporters, so the IT team is testing the microphones and the big screen several times before the event.","t":"A：下週在會議中心的年度大會上，預計有多少人會來聽執行長的演講？ B：【聽眾】大約有五百人，包括投資人和記者，所以資訊團隊在活動前會測試麥克風和大螢幕好幾次。"},{"w":"grab","p":"v.","d":"to quickly get or take something, such as attention","c":"抓住；吸引","s":"A: How did the speaker get everyone to listen so quickly at the start of the sales training this morning? B: She began with a surprising fact about lost customers to grab our attention, and after that nobody looked at their phones until the coffee break at ten thirty.","t":"A：今天早上業務訓練一開始，講者是怎麼讓大家那麼快就專心聽講的？ B：她一開始先講了一個關於流失客戶的驚人事實來【抓住】我們的注意力，之後直到十點半咖啡休息前都沒有人看手機。"},{"w":"maintain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something at the same level or in good condition","c":"維持；保持","s":"A: What is the secret to keeping a good relationship with clients who live in other countries and rarely visit our office? B: We try to maintain regular contact through video calls every month, and we also send short updates by email, so they always know what is happening with their orders.","t":"A：和住在其他國家、很少來我們辦公室的客戶保持良好關係的祕訣是什麼？ B：我們每個月透過視訊通話盡量【維持】固定聯繫，也會用電子郵件寄簡短的最新消息，讓他們隨時知道訂單的狀況。"},{"w":"entirely","p":"adv.","d":"completely","c":"完全地","s":"A: Do you agree with the new plan to move all customer support calls to the office in Manila next year? B: I am not entirely sure it is a good idea, because our customers here like talking to staff who know the local market, but I understand that it will save money.","t":"A：你同意明年把所有客服電話移到馬尼拉辦公室的新計畫嗎？ B：我不【完全】確定這是個好主意，因為這裡的客戶喜歡和了解在地市場的員工說話，但我明白這樣可以省錢。"},{"w":"ignoring","p":"v.","d":"not paying attention to someone or something on purpose (the -ing form of ignore)","c":"忽視；不理會","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner have a long talk with the new waiter after the lunch rush yesterday? B: Several customers said he kept ignoring them when they raised their hands, so the owner explained that guests must always feel noticed, even when the dining room is very busy.","t":"A：餐廳老闆昨天午餐尖峰過後為什麼和新來的服務生談了很久？ B：好幾位客人說他們舉手時他一直【不理會】他們，所以老闆向他說明，即使用餐區非常忙碌，也一定要讓客人覺得自己有被注意到。"},{"w":"pretend","p":"v.","d":"to act as if something is true when it is not","c":"假裝","s":"A: What should I do if a customer asks me a technical question about the software that I really cannot answer? B: Never pretend to know the answer, because giving wrong information causes bigger problems later; just say you will check with the engineers and call the customer back within an hour.","t":"A：如果客戶問我一個我真的答不出來的軟體技術問題，我該怎麼辦？ B：絕對不要【假裝】知道答案，因為給錯誤的資訊之後會造成更大的問題；只要說你會向工程師確認，並在一小時內回電給客戶就好。"},{"w":"attentive","p":"adj.","d":"listening or watching carefully; caring about others' needs","c":"專心的；體貼周到的","s":"A: Why do so many business travelers choose to stay at that small hotel near the train station instead of the bigger ones? B: The staff are very attentive, so they remember each guest's name and needs, and they always notice when someone needs a taxi or an early breakfast before a meeting.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多商務旅客選擇住在火車站附近那家小飯店，而不是大飯店？ B：那裡的員工非常【體貼周到】，會記得每位客人的名字和需求，也總是能注意到誰需要計程車，或在開會前需要提早吃早餐。"},{"w":"empathic","p":"adj.","d":"able to understand and share other people's feelings","c":"有同理心的","s":"A: What kind of person are you looking for to answer calls on the new customer care hotline next month? B: We need someone who is calm and empathic, because many callers will be worried about their bills, and they need to feel that the person on the phone understands their situation.","t":"A：下個月新的客戶關懷專線，你們想找什麼樣的人來接電話？ B：我們需要冷靜又【有同理心的】人，因為很多來電者會擔心他們的帳單，他們需要覺得電話那頭的人理解他們的處境。"},{"w":"emotionally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to feelings","c":"情緒上地；感情上","s":"A: Why did the HR manager take a short break during the meeting with the employee who was leaving the company? B: The conversation became quite emotionally difficult, because the employee had worked here for twenty years and started crying while talking about her friends in the accounting team.","t":"A：人資經理和那位即將離職的員工開會時，為什麼中途休息了一下？ B：那次談話在【情緒上】變得相當難受，因為那位員工在這裡工作了二十年，談到會計組的朋友時哭了起來。"},{"w":"rephrase","p":"v.","d":"to say something again using different words","c":"換句話說；改述","s":"A: What did you do when the visitors from Brazil did not understand your explanation of the new return policy? B: I tried to rephrase it using shorter sentences and simpler words, and I also drew a small chart on the whiteboard, so they finally understood how the process works.","t":"A：巴西來的訪客聽不懂你對新退貨政策的說明時，你怎麼做？ B：我試著用比較短的句子和比較簡單的字【換個方式說】，還在白板上畫了一張小圖表，他們終於了解流程是怎麼運作的。"},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something","c":"反思；深思","s":"A: Why does our team leader always ask us to wait a day before replying to difficult emails from clients? B: She wants us to reflect on what the client really needs, because a quick reply written when we feel angry often makes the situation worse instead of solving it.","t":"A：我們組長為什麼總是要我們等一天再回覆客戶的棘手郵件？ B：她希望我們先【仔細思考】客戶真正需要的是什麼，因為生氣時匆忙寫的回覆，常常會讓情況更糟而不是解決問題。"},{"w":"mimic","p":"v.","d":"to copy the way someone speaks or acts","c":"模仿","s":"A: How did you learn to speak so naturally on the phone with clients from London when you first joined the company? B: I used to listen to recorded calls of our best sales staff and mimic their tone and polite phrases, and after a few months it felt completely natural to me.","t":"A：你剛進公司時，是怎麼學會跟倫敦客戶講電話講得那麼自然的？ B：我以前會聽我們最優秀業務人員的通話錄音，並【模仿】他們的語氣和禮貌用語，幾個月後就覺得完全自然了。"}]},{"unit":82,"theme":"Cooking 烹飪","cards":[{"w":"cook","p":"v.","d":"to make food ready to eat by heating it","c":"烹調；煮","s":"A: Who is going to prepare the food for the welcome party for our new interns on Friday afternoon? B: Our team leader offered to cook a big pot of curry at home on Thursday night, and two volunteers will bring salad, bread and drinks to the meeting room before three o'clock.","t":"A：誰要為週五下午歡迎新實習生的派對準備食物？ B：我們的組長願意週四晚上在家【煮】一大鍋咖哩，另外兩位志工會在三點前把沙拉、麵包和飲料帶到會議室。"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"a list of foods and steps for making a dish","c":"食譜","s":"A: The soup at the company cafeteria tasted completely different today, so did the kitchen hire a new cook? B: No, the same staff are working there, but the manager asked them to try a new recipe from a famous Thai restaurant because many employees said the old soup was too salty.","t":"A：今天公司餐廳的湯味道完全不一樣，廚房是換了新廚師嗎？ B：沒有，還是同樣的員工，但經理請他們試做一家知名泰式餐廳的新【食譜】，因為很多員工說舊的湯太鹹了。"},{"w":"ingredient","p":"n.","d":"one of the foods used to make a dish","c":"材料；食材","s":"A: Why did the bakery near our office stop selling its famous strawberry cakes last month? B: The owner told me that the price of fresh strawberries went up sharply after the heavy rain, and she refuses to use a cheaper ingredient because she believes customers will notice the lower quality immediately.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近的麵包店上個月為什麼不再賣招牌草莓蛋糕了？ B：老闆告訴我，大雨過後新鮮草莓的價格大漲，而她拒絕使用較便宜的【食材】，因為她相信客人會馬上察覺品質變差。"},{"w":"kitchen","p":"n.","d":"a room where food is prepared and cooked","c":"廚房","s":"A: Is there anywhere on this floor where I can heat up my lunch, or do I have to go down to the cafeteria? B: There is a small staff kitchen next to the photocopy room with a microwave, a fridge and a kettle, but please wash your dishes afterward because everyone shares it.","t":"A：這層樓有地方可以加熱午餐嗎？還是我得下樓到員工餐廳？ B：影印室旁邊有一間小小的員工【廚房】，裡面有微波爐、冰箱和熱水壺，但用完請洗碗，因為大家共用。"},{"w":"chef","p":"n.","d":"a skilled cook who works in a restaurant or hotel","c":"廚師；主廚","s":"A: Why is the hotel restaurant so popular with business travelers even though its prices are quite high? B: The head chef trained in Paris for ten years, and he creates a new seasonal menu every month, so guests know they will always enjoy creative dishes made with local ingredients.","t":"A：為什麼那家飯店餐廳雖然價格很高，卻還是很受商務旅客歡迎？ B：那位【主廚】在巴黎受訓了十年，而且每個月都推出新的季節菜單，所以客人知道一定能吃到用在地食材做的創意料理。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘焙；烤","s":"A: What are you planning to bring to the charity sale at the community center this weekend? B: My sister and I will bake about fifty chocolate muffins on Saturday morning, and all the money we raise will go to the children's hospital that is building a new playroom.","t":"A：這個週末你打算帶什麼去社區中心的義賣會？ B：我和我姊姊週六早上會【烤】大約五十個巧克力瑪芬，募到的錢會全部捐給正在蓋新遊戲室的兒童醫院。"},{"w":"boil","p":"v.","d":"to heat a liquid until it bubbles","c":"煮沸；燒開","s":"A: The water in this old office building tastes a little strange, so is it safe to drink from the tap? B: The building manager says it is clean, but she still suggests that we boil it in the kettle first until the new filters are installed in the pipes next week.","t":"A：這棟老舊辦公大樓的水喝起來有點怪，直接喝水龍頭的水安全嗎？ B：大樓管理員說水是乾淨的，但她還是建議我們先用熱水壺把水【煮沸】，等下週水管裝好新的濾水器再說。"},{"w":"fry","p":"v.","d":"to cook food in hot oil","c":"油炸；煎","s":"A: Why does the new fast-food restaurant near the station advertise that its chicken is healthier than other places? B: The manager explained that they fry the chicken in fresh vegetable oil that they change every day, and they also offer a baked version for customers who want fewer calories.","t":"A：車站附近新開的速食店為什麼宣傳他們的雞肉比別家健康？ B：經理解釋說，他們用每天更換的新鮮植物油來【炸】雞肉，而且也提供烤的版本給想少攝取熱量的客人。"},{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to cook food over or under direct strong heat","c":"燒烤","s":"A: What kind of food will the catering company serve at our outdoor sales event in the park next Saturday? B: They will bring two large barbecues and grill burgers, sausages and corn for about two hundred guests, and they will also prepare vegetarian options for people who do not eat meat.","t":"A：下週六我們在公園舉辦的戶外銷售活動，外燴公司會提供什麼食物？ B：他們會帶兩台大型烤肉架，為大約兩百位客人【烤】漢堡、香腸和玉米，也會為不吃肉的人準備素食選擇。"},{"w":"roast","p":"v.","d":"to cook meat or vegetables in an oven or over a fire","c":"烘烤","s":"A: What is the special dish on the hotel's holiday menu for our department's year-end dinner? B: The chef will roast a whole turkey slowly in the oven for about five hours and serve it with potatoes, vegetables and a rich sauce that guests can add at their tables.","t":"A：我們部門尾牙飯店節慶菜單上的特色菜是什麼？ B：主廚會把一整隻火雞放進烤箱慢慢【烘烤】大約五個小時，搭配馬鈴薯、蔬菜和濃郁的醬汁，客人可以在桌上自行添加。"},{"w":"steam","p":"v.","d":"to cook food using the hot air from boiling water","c":"蒸","s":"A: Our new cafeteria menu offers fish twice a week, but how is it prepared, because I am trying to eat less oil? B: The cooks usually steam the fish with ginger and green onions instead of frying it, so it stays soft and healthy, and many office workers choose it for lunch.","t":"A：我們新的員工餐廳菜單每週提供兩次魚，但是怎麼料理的？因為我正在試著少吃油。 B：廚師通常會用薑和蔥來【蒸】魚，而不是油炸，所以魚肉保持軟嫩又健康，很多上班族午餐都選它。"},{"w":"simmer","p":"v.","d":"to cook something slowly just below boiling","c":"用小火慢燉","s":"A: How does the small noodle shop on Elm Street make its beef soup taste so rich and full? B: The owner told me that he lets the bones simmer over low heat for twelve hours every night after the shop closes, so the soup is ready when the first customers arrive in the morning.","t":"A：榆樹街那家小麵店的牛肉湯為什麼喝起來這麼濃郁？ B：老闆告訴我，他每天晚上打烊後都讓骨頭用小火【慢燉】十二個小時，所以早上第一批客人到的時候，湯就準備好了。"},{"w":"saute","p":"v.","d":"to cook food quickly in a little hot oil or butter","c":"嫩煎；快炒","s":"A: The cooking class at the community center sounds fun, so what did you learn in the first lesson last night? B: The instructor showed us how to saute mushrooms and onions quickly in a little butter over high heat, and then we used them to make a simple pasta for dinner.","t":"A：社區中心的烹飪課聽起來很好玩，你昨晚第一堂課學了什麼？ B：老師教我們怎麼用少許奶油大火快速【嫩煎】蘑菇和洋蔥，然後我們用它們做了簡單的義大利麵當晚餐。"},{"w":"mix","p":"v.","d":"to put two or more things together and combine them","c":"混合；攪拌","s":"A: Can you help me prepare the drinks for the client meeting, because the guests will arrive in twenty minutes? B: Sure, I will mix the orange juice with sparkling water in these two large glass jugs, and then we can add some ice and fresh lemon slices just before they come in.","t":"A：你可以幫我準備客戶會議的飲料嗎？客人再二十分鐘就到了。 B：沒問題，我會在這兩個大玻璃壺裡把柳橙汁和氣泡水【混合】，然後在他們進來前加點冰塊和新鮮檸檬片。"},{"w":"stir","p":"v.","d":"to move a spoon around in food or liquid","c":"攪拌","s":"A: The tomato sauce for tonight's staff dinner smells wonderful, but is there anything I can do to help you in the kitchen? B: Could you stir the sauce slowly with this wooden spoon every few minutes, because it can burn easily at the bottom while I cut the vegetables for the salad?","t":"A：今晚員工晚餐的番茄醬聞起來好香，廚房裡有什麼我可以幫忙的嗎？ B：你可以每隔幾分鐘用這支木湯匙慢慢【攪拌】醬汁嗎？因為我切沙拉蔬菜的時候，醬汁底部很容易燒焦。"},{"w":"whisk","p":"v.","d":"to beat eggs or cream very fast to add air","c":"攪打；打發","s":"A: Why are the pancakes at the hotel breakfast buffet so light and soft compared with the ones I make at home? B: The cook told me that he uses fresh eggs and he will whisk them for several minutes until they are full of air before he adds the flour and milk.","t":"A：飯店早餐自助吧的鬆餅為什麼比我在家做的鬆軟這麼多？ B：廚師告訴我，他用新鮮雞蛋，而且會把蛋【攪打】好幾分鐘，直到充滿空氣，才加入麵粉和牛奶。"},{"w":"slice","p":"v.","d":"to cut food into thin flat pieces","c":"切成薄片","s":"A: How should I prepare the bread for the sandwiches at tomorrow's training workshop for the new sales staff? B: Please slice the loaves thinly with the sharp knife in the top drawer, and then keep the bread in plastic bags overnight so it stays fresh until the lunch break starts.","t":"A：明天新業務人員的訓練工作坊要做三明治，麵包要怎麼準備？ B：請用最上層抽屜裡那把利刀把麵包【切成薄片】，然後整晚放在塑膠袋裡，讓麵包保持新鮮直到午休時間。"},{"w":"chop","p":"v.","d":"to cut food into small pieces with a knife","c":"切碎；剁","s":"A: The salad bar at the new restaurant downtown looks amazing, so how do they prepare so many vegetables every day? B: Three kitchen assistants arrive at six in the morning to wash and chop carrots, cabbage and peppers, so everything is fresh and ready before the lunch crowd arrives at noon.","t":"A：市中心新餐廳的沙拉吧看起來好棒，他們每天怎麼準備這麼多蔬菜？ B：三位廚房助理早上六點就到，清洗並【切碎】紅蘿蔔、高麗菜和甜椒，所以中午用餐人潮到之前，一切都新鮮備妥。"},{"w":"dice","p":"v.","d":"to cut food into small square pieces","c":"切丁","s":"A: What should I do with these potatoes and carrots for the beef stew we are making for the office potluck? B: Please peel them first and then dice them into small, even cubes about two centimeters wide, so they cook at the same speed and are easy for guests to eat.","t":"A：我們要為辦公室百樂餐做燉牛肉，這些馬鈴薯和紅蘿蔔要怎麼處理？ B：請先削皮，然後把它們【切丁】成大約兩公分寬、大小均勻的小塊，這樣熟的速度一樣，客人也方便吃。"},{"w":"peel","p":"v.","d":"to take the skin off fruit or vegetables","c":"剝皮；削皮","s":"A: Why does the fruit tray from the catering company cost more than buying the fruit at the supermarket ourselves? B: Their staff wash, peel and cut every orange, mango and kiwi by hand, so our guests can eat the fruit right away without making a mess in the meeting room.","t":"A：外燴公司的水果盤為什麼比我們自己去超市買水果還貴？ B：他們的員工會用手清洗、【剝皮】並切好每一顆柳橙、芒果和奇異果，所以客人可以馬上吃，不會把會議室弄得一團亂。"},{"w":"season","p":"v.","d":"to add salt, pepper or spices to food","c":"調味","s":"A: The grilled chicken at the company picnic last year was a little tasteless, so what will you do differently this time? B: I will season the meat with salt, pepper, garlic and lemon the night before, so the flavor has time to go deep into the chicken before we cook it.","t":"A：去年公司野餐的烤雞有點沒味道，這次你會怎麼改進？ B：我會在前一晚用鹽、胡椒、大蒜和檸檬幫肉【調味】，讓味道在烹煮前有時間深入雞肉。"},{"w":"spice","p":"n.","d":"a dried plant part used to give food a strong taste","c":"香料","s":"A: Why are you buying so many small bags at the market when you are only cooking dinner for four colleagues tonight? B: The Indian curry I am making needs more than one kind of spice, such as cumin, turmeric and chili, and the shop near my home does not sell any of them.","t":"A：今晚你只為四位同事煮晚餐，為什麼要在市場買這麼多小包裝？ B：我要做的印度咖哩需要不只一種【香料】，例如孜然、薑黃和辣椒，而我家附近的店都沒有賣。"},{"w":"flavor","p":"n.","d":"the particular taste of a food or drink","c":"口味；風味","s":"A: Which of the three new ice creams did the customers prefer during the product test at the shopping mall? B: Most people chose the green tea flavor because it was not too sweet, so the marketing team plans to sell it in convenience stores across Asia starting next spring.","t":"A：在購物中心的產品試吃中，顧客比較喜歡三種新冰淇淋中的哪一種？ B：大多數人選了綠茶【口味】，因為它不會太甜，所以行銷團隊計畫從明年春天開始在亞洲各地的便利商店販售。"},{"w":"taste","p":"n.","d":"the feeling food or drink gives in your mouth","c":"味道","s":"A: Did you enjoy the lunch at the new Korean restaurant that the manager recommended for our team meeting? B: Yes, the beef soup had a wonderful taste, but it was a bit too hot for me, so next time I will ask the waiter for a milder version before I order.","t":"A：你喜歡經理推薦我們開團隊會議的那家新韓式餐廳的午餐嗎？ B：喜歡，牛肉湯的【味道】很棒，但對我來說有點太辣，所以下次點餐前我會請服務生做比較不辣的。"},{"w":"portion","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food served to one person","c":"（食物的）一份；份量","s":"A: Why do so many customers leave food on their plates at the hotel restaurant during the conference lunch? B: The portion of rice that the kitchen serves is far too large for most office workers, so the manager plans to make it smaller and lower the price slightly next month.","t":"A：會議午餐時，為什麼飯店餐廳有那麼多客人把食物剩在盤子裡？ B：廚房供應的白飯【份量】對大多數上班族來說太多了，所以經理打算下個月減量，並稍微降價。"},{"w":"utensil","p":"n.","d":"a tool used for cooking or eating, such as a spoon","c":"器具；餐具","s":"A: What else do we need to buy for the new staff kitchen before the office opens on Monday morning? B: We already have plates and cups, but we still need a basic utensil set with knives, forks, spoons and a few large serving spoons for the shared lunches on Fridays.","t":"A：辦公室週一早上開幕前，新的員工廚房還需要買什麼？ B：我們已經有盤子和杯子，但還需要一組基本的【餐具】，包括刀子、叉子、湯匙，以及週五共餐用的幾支大湯匙。"},{"w":"pan","p":"n.","d":"a flat metal container with a handle used for cooking","c":"平底鍋；鍋","s":"A: Why are you buying new cookware at the department store when your kitchen at home already has so much? B: My old frying pan has a broken handle, and the eggs always stick to the bottom, so I want a light, non-stick one that is easy to wash after breakfast.","t":"A：你家廚房已經有很多廚具了，為什麼還要在百貨公司買新的？ B：我那支舊的【平底鍋】把手壞了，雞蛋總是黏在鍋底，所以我想買一支輕巧、不沾、早餐後好洗的。"},{"w":"pot","p":"n.","d":"a deep round container used for cooking soup or stew","c":"鍋子","s":"A: How are we going to serve hot soup to all fifty volunteers at the beach cleanup event on Saturday? B: The restaurant owner next door will lend us a huge metal pot, and we can keep the soup warm on a gas burner under the tent until everyone finishes working.","t":"A：週六淨灘活動時，我們要怎麼為五十位志工提供熱湯？ B：隔壁餐廳老闆會借我們一個超大的金屬【鍋子】，我們可以把湯放在帳篷下的瓦斯爐上保溫，直到大家工作結束。"},{"w":"oven","p":"n.","d":"a box-shaped machine that bakes or roasts food","c":"烤箱","s":"A: Why did the bakery downtown close for two days last week, even though it was a busy holiday period? B: Its main oven broke down on Monday morning, so the bakers could not make any bread or cakes until a technician arrived from the factory with a replacement part.","t":"A：市中心那家麵包店為什麼上週在忙碌的假期關門兩天？ B：店裡的主要【烤箱】週一早上故障了，所以麵包師傅無法做任何麵包或蛋糕，直到技師從工廠帶來替換零件。"},{"w":"stove","p":"n.","d":"a piece of kitchen equipment with burners for cooking","c":"爐子；爐灶","s":"A: Is it safe to leave the soup cooking while we go to the meeting downstairs for an hour? B: No, please turn off the stove before you leave, because the building rules say nobody may leave a gas flame burning in the staff kitchen without someone there to watch it.","t":"A：我們去樓下開一小時的會時，把湯留著繼續煮安全嗎？ B：不安全，離開前請把【爐子】關掉，因為大樓規定沒有人看著的時候，任何人都不可以讓員工廚房的瓦斯火繼續燒。"},{"w":"apron","p":"n.","d":"a piece of cloth worn over clothes to keep them clean","c":"圍裙","s":"A: Do I need to bring anything special to the cooking class that the company is offering as a team-building activity? B: You should bring an old apron to keep your shirt clean, because we will be working with tomato sauce and oil, and the school does not provide one for every student.","t":"A：公司舉辦的團隊建立烹飪課，我需要帶什麼特別的東西嗎？ B：你應該帶一件舊【圍裙】保持襯衫乾淨，因為我們會用到番茄醬和油，而學校不會為每位學員提供。"},{"w":"delicious","p":"adj.","d":"having a very good taste","c":"美味的","s":"A: How was the dinner at the seafood restaurant where you took the visitors from the head office last night? B: The grilled fish was absolutely delicious, and the visitors enjoyed it so much that they asked for the restaurant's address so they could return before flying home on Friday.","t":"A：昨晚你帶總公司來的訪客去那家海鮮餐廳，晚餐怎麼樣？ B：烤魚真的非常【美味】，訪客們吃得很開心，還問了餐廳地址，好在週五搭機回去前再來一次。"},{"w":"savory","p":"adj.","d":"salty or spicy, not sweet","c":"鹹味的；鹹香的","s":"A: The client from Japan does not like sweet food, so what should we order for the afternoon break during the long meeting? B: Let's choose some savory snacks such as cheese crackers, mini sandwiches and chicken pies instead of cakes, and we can also offer green tea and coffee.","t":"A：那位日本客戶不喜歡甜食，長時間會議的下午休息時間我們該點什麼？ B：我們選一些【鹹味的】點心吧，像是起司餅乾、迷你三明治和雞肉派，而不是蛋糕，另外也可以提供綠茶和咖啡。"},{"w":"homemade","p":"adj.","d":"made at home, not bought from a shop or factory","c":"自製的；家常的","s":"A: Why is the little café across from our office always full of customers at lunchtime, even though it is quite small? B: The owner serves homemade soup and bread that her mother prepares every morning, and office workers say it tastes much better than food from the chain restaurants nearby.","t":"A：我們辦公室對面那家小咖啡館雖然很小，為什麼午餐時間總是客滿？ B：老闆提供她媽媽每天早上準備的【自製】湯和麵包，上班族都說比附近連鎖餐廳的食物好吃多了。"}]},{"unit":83,"theme":"Cooperation 合作","cards":[{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others to reach the same goal","c":"合作；配合","s":"A: How did the two delivery companies manage to finish moving all the hospital equipment before the new building opened on Monday? B: Their managers agreed to cooperate closely for the whole weekend, so one company packed the machines while the other drove the trucks and set everything up in the new rooms.","t":"A：這兩家貨運公司是怎麼在新大樓週一啟用前把所有醫院設備搬完的？ B：他們的經理同意整個週末密切【合作】，所以一家公司負責打包機器，另一家負責開卡車並在新房間裡把所有東西裝設好。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together to make or create something","c":"合作；協作","s":"A: Who designed the new reusable coffee cups that the café near our office started selling last month? B: They were made in collaboration with a local art school, and the students created the colorful patterns while the café paid for the materials and gave part of the profits to the school.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家咖啡廳上個月開始販售的新環保咖啡杯是誰設計的？ B：那是與當地一所藝術學校【合作】製作的，學生們設計了繽紛的圖案，咖啡廳則支付材料費並把部分利潤捐給學校。"},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work with another person or group on a project","c":"合作；協作","s":"A: Why are the engineers from our Taipei office flying to Munich next week instead of holding another video call? B: They need to collaborate with the German design team on the new electric bike, and it is much easier to test the parts together in the same workshop.","t":"A：為什麼我們台北辦公室的工程師下週要飛去慕尼黑，而不是再開一次視訊會議？ B：他們需要和德國設計團隊【合作】開發新的電動自行車，而在同一個工作室裡一起測試零件容易多了。"},{"w":"teamwork","p":"n.","d":"the way people work well together as a group","c":"團隊合作","s":"A: How did the restaurant staff serve three hundred guests at the wedding party without any serious problems last Saturday? B: It was excellent teamwork, because the chefs, waiters and dishwashers all knew their jobs, helped each other when it got busy, and kept talking to each other all night.","t":"A：上週六餐廳員工是怎麼在婚宴上服務三百位賓客卻沒出任何大問題的？ B：那是絕佳的【團隊合作】，因為廚師、服務生和洗碗工都清楚自己的工作，忙的時候互相幫忙，而且整晚都持續互相溝通。"},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that works or runs a business with another","c":"合夥人；合作夥伴","s":"A: Who is going to run the bakery while you are away visiting your family in Canada for three weeks this summer? B: My business partner, Lisa, will manage the shop, order the flour and pay the staff, because we started the bakery together five years ago and she knows everything about it.","t":"A：今年夏天你回加拿大探親三週期間，誰來經營麵包店？ B：我的事業【合夥人】麗莎會管理店面、訂購麵粉並支付員工薪水，因為我們五年前一起創立這家麵包店，她對店裡的一切都很清楚。"},{"w":"partnership","p":"n.","d":"a relationship in which people or companies work together","c":"合作關係；合夥","s":"A: Why does our hotel now offer free tickets to the science museum for every guest who stays more than two nights? B: We formed a partnership with the museum last spring, so they send visitors to us for rooms, and we send our guests to them for tours and special exhibitions.","t":"A：為什麼我們飯店現在提供科學博物館免費門票給每位住宿超過兩晚的客人？ B：我們去年春天和博物館建立了【合作關係】，所以他們把需要住宿的遊客介紹給我們，我們則把客人介紹給他們參加導覽和特展。"},{"w":"ally","p":"n.","d":"a person, group or country that helps and supports another","c":"盟友；支持者","s":"A: How did you get the board to approve your plan for a new staff gym when most directors thought it cost too much? B: The finance director became my strongest ally, because she showed everyone that healthier workers take fewer sick days, and that changed their minds.","t":"A：大多數董事都認為新員工健身房太花錢，你是怎麼讓董事會通過這個計畫的？ B：財務長成了我最有力的【盟友】，因為她向大家證明，比較健康的員工請病假的天數較少，這改變了他們的想法。"},{"w":"alliance","p":"n.","d":"an agreement between groups or companies to work together","c":"聯盟；結盟","s":"A: Why are three small airlines in Asia suddenly selling tickets for each other's flights on their websites? B: They joined an alliance earlier this year, so passengers can book one trip across several countries, collect points with any member, and change planes more easily at busy airports.","t":"A：為什麼亞洲三家小型航空公司突然在各自網站上互售對方航班的機票？ B：他們今年稍早加入了一個【聯盟】，所以乘客可以預訂橫跨數國的單一行程、在任何成員公司累積點數，並在繁忙的機場更方便地轉機。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help someone by giving encouragement, money or practical help","c":"支持；資助","s":"A: Are you sure the manager will agree to let you study part-time for a master's degree while you keep working here? B: Yes, she promised to support my plan, and the company will even pay half of the fees if I stay with the firm for two more years after I graduate.","t":"A：你確定經理會同意你一邊在這裡工作一邊兼讀碩士學位嗎？ B：確定，她承諾會【支持】我的計畫，而且如果我畢業後再留在公司兩年，公司甚至會負擔一半的學費。"},{"w":"assist","p":"v.","d":"to help someone do a job or task","c":"協助；幫助","s":"A: Who will show the new interns how to use the cash register and the stock system during their first week at the store? B: Our most experienced cashier will assist them at the counter every morning, and in the afternoons they will learn how to check the shelves with the floor manager.","t":"A：新實習生在店裡的第一週，誰要教他們使用收銀機和庫存系統？ B：我們最資深的收銀員每天早上會在櫃台【協助】他們，下午他們則會跟著樓面經理學習如何檢查貨架。"},{"w":"help","p":"v.","d":"to make it easier for someone to do something","c":"幫助；幫忙","s":"A: The printer on the third floor is broken again, and I have to print forty copies of the sales report before the meeting at ten. B: Don't worry, I can help you carry your files down to the second floor, where the large color printer is working fine this morning.","t":"A：三樓的印表機又壞了，而我必須在十點開會前印出四十份銷售報告。 B：別擔心，我可以【幫】你把文件搬到二樓，那裡的大型彩色印表機今天早上運作得很正常。"},{"w":"coordinate","p":"v.","d":"to organize different people or activities so they work well together","c":"協調；統籌","s":"A: With so many speakers, hotels and buses involved, who is in charge of the international sales conference in Bangkok next month? B: Mr. Chen will coordinate all the travel plans, so he will book the rooms, arrange the airport buses and make sure every speaker knows the schedule.","t":"A：下個月在曼谷的國際業務會議牽涉這麼多講者、飯店和巴士，誰負責呢？ B：陳先生會【統籌】所有的行程安排，他會預訂房間、安排機場接駁巴士，並確保每位講者都知道時間表。"},{"w":"coordination","p":"n.","d":"the act of making people or groups work well together","c":"協調；配合","s":"A: Why did the shopping mall's fire drill take almost an hour when it was supposed to last only twenty minutes? B: There was poor coordination between the security guards and the shop managers, so some stores closed their doors too late and several groups used the wrong exits.","t":"A：購物中心的消防演習原本預計只要二十分鐘，為什麼花了將近一小時？ B：保全人員和店長之間的【協調】很差，所以有些店太晚關門，好幾組人也走錯了出口。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give money, time or ideas to help something succeed","c":"貢獻；捐助；出一份力","s":"A: Is everyone in the department giving money for Mr. Lin's retirement gift, or only the people who worked with him for many years? B: Everyone is welcome to contribute, even the new staff, and we plan to buy him a good camera because he wants to travel around Japan next year.","t":"A：部門裡每個人都要出錢買林先生的退休禮物嗎？還是只有跟他共事多年的人？ B：歡迎每個人【出一份力】，連新員工也可以，我們打算買一台好相機給他，因為他明年想去日本各地旅行。"},{"w":"contribution","p":"n.","d":"something you give or do to help make something successful","c":"貢獻；捐款","s":"A: Why did the CEO mention the night-shift workers by name during the year-end party last Friday evening? B: She wanted to thank them for their huge contribution to the company, because they worked extra hours for three months to finish the big order from our Canadian customer on time.","t":"A：上週五晚上的尾牙，執行長為什麼點名提到大夜班的員工？ B：她想感謝他們對公司的巨大【貢獻】，因為他們連續三個月加班，準時完成了加拿大客戶的大訂單。"},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity or event","c":"參加；參與","s":"A: Do all the sales staff have to join the two-day training course on customer service at the hotel next weekend? B: Only the new staff must participate, but experienced workers can also sign up if they want to learn the latest ways to handle difficult customers on the phone.","t":"A：所有業務人員都必須參加下週末在飯店舉辦、為期兩天的客服訓練課程嗎？ B：只有新進人員必須【參加】，不過資深員工如果想學習在電話中應對難纏顧客的最新方法，也可以報名。"},{"w":"participation","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something","c":"參與；參加","s":"A: Why did the human resources team decide to give free movie tickets to everyone who filled out the staff survey this year? B: Last year participation was very low, with only a quarter of the workers answering, so the team hoped a small gift would encourage more people to share their opinions.","t":"A：為什麼人資團隊今年決定送電影票給每位填寫員工問卷的人？ B：去年的【參與】率很低，只有四分之一的員工作答，所以團隊希望一份小禮物能鼓勵更多人分享意見。"},{"w":"engage","p":"v.","d":"to attract someone's interest and get them involved","c":"吸引（參與）；使投入","s":"A: What can we do to make the online training videos more interesting for the factory workers, who often stop watching after five minutes? B: We could add short quizzes and real stories from the factory floor to engage the viewers, so they stay interested and remember the safety rules much better.","t":"A：工廠員工常常看五分鐘就不看了，我們可以怎麼讓線上訓練影片更有趣？ B：我們可以加入簡短測驗和來自工廠現場的真實故事來【吸引】觀眾，讓他們保持興趣，也能把安全規定記得更牢。"},{"w":"involvement","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something or being connected with it","c":"參與；涉入","s":"A: Why does the company give an extra day off to employees who join the beach clean-up every spring? B: The managers believe that staff involvement in local community projects builds team spirit and improves our image, so they want to reward people who give up their weekend to help.","t":"A：為什麼公司會多給參加每年春季淨灘活動的員工一天假？ B：主管們相信員工【參與】在地社區活動能凝聚團隊精神並提升公司形象，所以想獎勵那些犧牲週末去幫忙的人。"},{"w":"unite","p":"v.","d":"to join together as a group for a shared purpose","c":"團結；聯合","s":"A: The two offices have argued about the budget for months, so how can we make them work together on the new product launch? B: We should give them one clear goal, such as beating our biggest rival in sales, because a common target can unite people who usually disagree.","t":"A：兩個辦公室為了預算爭吵了好幾個月，我們要怎麼讓他們一起合作推出新產品？ B：我們應該給他們一個明確的目標，例如在銷售上打敗最大的對手，因為共同的目標能讓平常意見不合的人【團結】起來。"},{"w":"unity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being joined together and agreeing","c":"團結；統一","s":"A: Why did the sports company ask all its staff to wear the same blue shirts at the trade fair in Singapore? B: The marketing director wanted to show unity and team spirit, so visitors would see that everyone at the booth belonged to one strong company with the same goals.","t":"A：為什麼那家運動用品公司要全體員工在新加坡商展上穿同樣的藍色襯衫？ B：行銷總監想展現【團結】和團隊精神，讓參觀者看到攤位上的每個人都屬於同一家有共同目標的強大公司。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to let others use or have part of something","c":"分享；共用","s":"A: There aren't enough desks for all the new designers who start on Monday, so what should we do until the extra furniture arrives? B: Two people can share each large desk by the window for a week, and the others can work in the meeting room, which is free most afternoons.","t":"A：週一報到的新設計師沒有足夠的辦公桌，在額外家具送來前我們該怎麼辦？ B：靠窗的每張大桌子可以讓兩個人【共用】一週，其他人可以在會議室工作，那裡大部分下午都沒人用。"},{"w":"joint","p":"adj.","d":"done or owned by two or more people together","c":"共同的；聯合的","s":"A: Are the two banks planning to merge, or are they just working together on that new mobile payment app? B: They are not merging, but they started a joint project last year, so both banks paid for the app and will split the profits from the service equally.","t":"A：那兩家銀行打算合併，還是只是一起開發那個新的行動支付應用程式？ B：他們沒有要合併，不過去年啟動了一個【聯合】專案，所以兩家銀行都出資開發這個應用程式，並會平分這項服務的利潤。"},{"w":"collective","p":"adj.","d":"shared or done by all members of a group","c":"集體的；共同的","s":"A: Who should get the credit for winning the biggest contract in the company's history after so many months of hard work? B: It was a collective effort, because the sales team found the client, the engineers built the sample and the lawyers checked every line of the long contract.","t":"A：經過這麼多個月的努力，贏得公司史上最大合約的功勞應該歸誰？ B：這是【集體的】努力，因為業務團隊找到客戶、工程師做出樣品，律師則檢查了冗長合約中的每一行。"},{"w":"mutual","p":"adj.","d":"felt or done by two or more people toward each other","c":"相互的；共同的","s":"A: Why did the factory and the trucking company agree to sign a five-year contract instead of a shorter one this time? B: The deal brings mutual benefits, because the factory gets lower delivery prices, and the trucking company knows it will have steady work for many years.","t":"A：為什麼這次工廠和貨運公司同意簽五年合約，而不是較短的合約？ B：這筆交易帶來【互惠的】好處，因為工廠能取得較低的運費，而貨運公司也知道未來多年都會有穩定的工作。"},{"w":"consensus","p":"n.","d":"an agreement that most or all people in a group accept","c":"共識","s":"A: Did the managers finally decide where to hold the company trip this year, or are they still arguing about it? B: After a long meeting, they reached a consensus to go to Hualien, because most people wanted beaches and mountains, and the hotel there offered a good group price.","t":"A：經理們終於決定今年員工旅遊的地點了嗎？還是仍在爭論？ B：經過一場冗長的會議，他們達成去花蓮的【共識】，因為大多數人想要海灘和山景，而且那裡的飯店提供了不錯的團體價格。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which each side gives up part of what it wants","c":"妥協；折衷","s":"A: The designers wanted a bright red logo, and the sales team wanted a dark blue one, so what did they finally choose? B: They agreed on a compromise, using dark blue letters with a small red circle, so both teams got part of what they wanted for the new brand.","t":"A：設計師想要亮紅色的標誌，業務團隊想要深藍色的，他們最後選了什麼？ B：他們達成了【折衷方案】，採用深藍色字母搭配一個紅色小圓圈，所以兩個團隊都在新品牌上得到了部分想要的東西。"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something in order to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"A: The supplier wants to raise the price of paper cups by fifteen percent next month, so should we just accept it? B: No, I will meet their sales manager on Thursday to negotiate a better deal, perhaps a smaller increase if we promise to order more cups every month.","t":"A：供應商下個月想把紙杯價格調漲百分之十五，我們就直接接受嗎？ B：不，我週四會和他們的業務經理見面，【談判】出更好的條件，如果我們承諾每個月訂購更多紙杯，也許漲幅可以小一點。"},{"w":"negotiation","p":"n.","d":"formal discussion between people trying to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"A: Has the company signed the new rental agreement for the warehouse near the port yet? B: Not yet, because the negotiation with the landlord is still going on, and both sides are arguing about who should pay for repairing the old roof before we move in next month.","t":"A：公司已經簽下港口附近倉庫的新租約了嗎？ B：還沒，因為和房東的【談判】仍在進行中，雙方還在爭論下個月我們搬進去前該由誰支付修理舊屋頂的費用。"},{"w":"facilitate","p":"v.","d":"to make an action or process easier","c":"促進；使便利","s":"A: Why did the company buy that expensive new video system for every meeting room in all of its offices? B: The managers hope it will facilitate communication between our teams in Taipei, Tokyo and Seoul, so people can solve problems quickly without traveling so often.","t":"A：公司為什麼要幫所有辦公室的每間會議室都買那套昂貴的新視訊系統？ B：主管們希望它能【促進】我們台北、東京和首爾團隊之間的溝通，讓大家不必經常出差就能迅速解決問題。"},{"w":"synchronize","p":"v.","d":"to make things happen at the same time or show the same information","c":"同步；使一致","s":"A: Why did my phone show a different meeting time from the calendar on my office computer this morning? B: You probably forgot to synchronize the two devices after you changed the time yesterday, so open the app, press the update button, and both calendars should match again.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上我手機上顯示的會議時間和辦公室電腦行事曆上的不一樣？ B：你昨天改時間後可能忘了讓這兩台裝置【同步】，打開應用程式按下更新按鈕，兩個行事曆應該就會再次一致。"},{"w":"harmonious","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and peaceful, without arguments","c":"和諧的；融洽的","s":"A: Why do so few people leave the accounting department, even though the pay there is not higher than in other teams? B: The manager has created a very harmonious working environment, where people respect each other, solve problems calmly and often have lunch together on Fridays.","t":"A：會計部的薪水並沒有比其他團隊高，為什麼很少有人離職？ B：經理營造了一個非常【和諧的】工作環境，大家互相尊重、冷靜解決問題，而且週五常常一起吃午餐。"},{"w":"together","p":"adv.","d":"with each other; as a group","c":"一起；共同","s":"A: Should each department plan its own end-of-year party, or would one big event for the whole company be better this time? B: I think we should celebrate together in one hall, because staff from different floors rarely meet, and a big party is a good chance to make new friends.","t":"A：今年每個部門應該各自籌辦年終派對，還是全公司辦一場大型活動比較好？ B：我認為我們應該在同一個大廳【一起】慶祝，因為不同樓層的員工很少見面，大型派對是結交新朋友的好機會。"}]},{"unit":84,"theme":"Country 國家","cards":[{"w":"nation","p":"n.","d":"a country and its people","c":"國家；民族","s":"A: Why is the hotel chain spending so much money on advertising in Vietnam this year instead of in its home market? B: The managers believe it is a young and fast-growing nation, so they expect millions of new travelers there to need clean, affordable rooms over the next ten years.","t":"A：為什麼這家連鎖飯店今年在越南花這麼多錢打廣告，而不是在本國市場？ B：經理們認為那是一個年輕且快速成長的【國家】，所以預期未來十年那裡會有數百萬名新旅客需要乾淨又平價的房間。"},{"w":"state","p":"n.","d":"a part of a country, such as the US, with its own local government","c":"州","s":"A: Why does the company want to move its main warehouse from California to Texas next spring? B: Taxes and land prices are much lower in that state, and the new location is closer to our biggest customers, so we can save money and deliver orders a day faster.","t":"A：為什麼公司想在明年春天把主要倉庫從加州搬到德州？ B：那個【州】的稅金和土地價格低很多，而且新地點離我們最大的客戶比較近，所以我們可以省錢，而且出貨能快一天。"},{"w":"republic","p":"n.","d":"a country with an elected leader and no king or queen","c":"共和國","s":"A: What did you learn about the country before you went there to open our new sales office last month? B: I read that it became a republic in 1960, so its leader is chosen by voters every five years, and the government has worked hard to attract foreign companies like ours.","t":"A：上個月你去那裡開設我們的新業務辦公室之前，對那個國家有什麼了解？ B：我讀到它在1960年成為【共和國】，所以領導人每五年由選民選出，而且政府一直很努力吸引像我們這樣的外國公司。"},{"w":"kingdom","p":"n.","d":"a country ruled by a king or queen","c":"王國","s":"A: Why are so many tourists booking our tour package to Bhutan, even though the flights are expensive? B: The small mountain kingdom has a royal family, beautiful old temples and very few visitors, so travelers feel they are discovering a special place that most people never see.","t":"A：為什麼即使機票很貴，還是有那麼多遊客預訂我們的不丹旅遊套裝行程？ B：這個小小的山中【王國】有王室、美麗的古老寺廟，而且遊客很少，所以旅客覺得他們正在發現一個大多數人從沒見過的特別地方。"},{"w":"government","p":"n.","d":"the group of people who control and manage a country","c":"政府","s":"A: Why are so many small restaurants in our neighborhood hiring young workers again this summer? B: The government started a new program that pays part of the salary for anyone under twenty-five, so owners can train new staff without spending too much of their own money.","t":"A：為什麼我們社區有這麼多小餐廳今年夏天又開始僱用年輕員工？ B：【政府】推出了一項新計畫，替二十五歲以下的人支付部分薪水，所以老闆們可以培訓新員工，而不用花太多自己的錢。"},{"w":"capital","p":"n.","d":"the city where a country's government is","c":"首都","s":"A: Where will the international trade fair be held next year, and should we book our hotel rooms now? B: It will take place in the capital, near the president's office and the main train station, so I suggest booking early because hotels there fill up quickly during big events.","t":"A：明年的國際商展會在哪裡舉辦？我們應該現在就訂飯店房間嗎？ B：會在【首都】舉行，靠近總統府和主要火車站，所以我建議提早預訂，因為那裡的飯店在大型活動期間很快就會客滿。"},{"w":"border","p":"n.","d":"the line between two countries","c":"邊界；國界","s":"A: Why did the delivery of the machine parts from Germany arrive two days late this week? B: The trucks had to wait for many hours at the border because customs officers were checking every vehicle carefully, so the driver could not enter the country until Wednesday afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼這週從德國運來的機器零件晚了兩天才到？ B：卡車必須在【邊界】等好幾個小時，因為海關人員正在仔細檢查每一輛車，所以司機直到星期三下午才能入境。"},{"w":"territory","p":"n.","d":"an area of land controlled by a country, or an area a person is responsible for","c":"領土；（業務）轄區","s":"A: Why are you traveling so much more this year than you did last year? B: My boss made me responsible for a much larger sales territory that includes three countries in Southeast Asia, so I visit clients in a different city almost every week.","t":"A：為什麼你今年出差的次數比去年多那麼多？ B：老闆讓我負責一個大得多的銷售【轄區】，包含東南亞三個國家，所以我幾乎每週都要去不同城市拜訪客戶。"},{"w":"citizen","p":"n.","d":"a person who legally belongs to a country","c":"公民；國民","s":"A: Can our new engineer from Canada start working at the Tokyo office next month, or does she need a special visa? B: She is actually a Japanese citizen because her mother was born in Osaka, so she does not need a work visa and can start as soon as she finds an apartment.","t":"A：我們從加拿大來的新工程師下個月可以開始在東京辦公室上班嗎？還是她需要特別的簽證？ B：她其實是日本【公民】，因為她母親在大阪出生，所以她不需要工作簽證，只要找到公寓就可以開始上班。"},{"w":"citizenship","p":"n.","d":"the legal right to belong to a country","c":"公民身分；國籍","s":"A: Why did the human resources manager ask for a copy of your passport during the interview yesterday? B: For this government project, every employee must have local citizenship, so she needed to check that I was born here and have the right to work on secret documents.","t":"A：為什麼人資經理昨天面試時要你的護照影本？ B：這個政府專案的每位員工都必須具備本國【公民身分】，所以她需要確認我是在這裡出生，而且有權處理機密文件。"},{"w":"population","p":"n.","d":"the number of people living in a place","c":"人口","s":"A: Why did the supermarket chain decide to open three new stores in the northern part of the city? B: The population there has grown quickly since the new train line opened, and many young families have moved into the apartments, so the company expects strong sales of fresh food.","t":"A：為什麼這家連鎖超市決定在城市北區開三家新店？ B：自從新的火車路線開通後，那裡的【人口】快速成長，許多年輕家庭搬進了公寓，所以公司預期生鮮食品的銷售會很強勁。"},{"w":"democracy","p":"n.","d":"a system in which people vote to choose their government","c":"民主；民主國家","s":"A: Why is the news channel planning so many special programs for next weekend? B: The country is holding its first free election since it became a democracy, so reporters will interview voters all day and explain the results live as soon as the votes are counted.","t":"A：為什麼新聞台下週末規劃了那麼多特別節目？ B：這個國家自從成為【民主國家】以來首次舉行自由選舉，所以記者們會整天採訪選民，並在計票完成後立刻現場解說結果。"},{"w":"economy","p":"n.","d":"the system of money, trade and jobs in a country","c":"經濟","s":"A: Why are fewer customers buying new cars at our showroom this year compared with last year? B: The economy has been weak since prices for food and gas went up, so many families are worried about their jobs and prefer to keep their old cars a little longer.","t":"A：為什麼今年來我們展示中心買新車的顧客比去年少？ B：自從食物和油價上漲後，【經濟】一直很疲弱，所以許多家庭擔心工作不保，寧願把舊車多開一陣子。"},{"w":"culture","p":"n.","d":"the customs, art and way of life of a group of people","c":"文化","s":"A: Why does the company give a two-day training course to every manager before they move to the Seoul office? B: Business culture in Korea is quite different from ours, so the course teaches managers how to greet clients, exchange business cards and behave politely at company dinners.","t":"A：為什麼公司要讓每位經理在調到首爾辦公室之前上兩天的訓練課程？ B：韓國的商業【文化】和我們的很不一樣，所以課程會教經理如何問候客戶、交換名片，以及在公司聚餐時表現得有禮貌。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom or belief passed down over many years","c":"傳統","s":"A: Why does everyone in the office bring a dish of food to the meeting room on the last Friday of December? B: It is a tradition that our founder started thirty years ago, so each department cooks something special and we all eat lunch together before the holiday break.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室的每個人在十二月的最後一個星期五都帶一道菜到會議室？ B：這是我們創辦人三十年前開始的【傳統】，所以每個部門都會煮一道特別的菜，我們在放假前一起吃午餐。"},{"w":"heritage","p":"n.","d":"the history, buildings and customs that a country or group values","c":"遺產；文化資產","s":"A: Why did the city council reject the plan to build a shopping mall on the old harbor site? B: The old warehouses there are an important part of the city's heritage, so the council wants to protect them and turn them into a museum and small shops for tourists.","t":"A：為什麼市議會否決了在舊港口用地蓋購物中心的計畫？ B：那裡的舊倉庫是這座城市【文化資產】的重要部分，所以議會想保護它們，並把它們改建成博物館和給遊客的小店。"},{"w":"language","p":"n.","d":"the words and grammar people use to speak and write","c":"語言","s":"A: Why did the hotel hire two new receptionists even though business has been slow this autumn? B: Many of our guests now come from Spain and Brazil, so the manager wanted staff who speak a second language well enough to help visitors check in and answer their questions.","t":"A：為什麼飯店今年秋天生意清淡，還是僱用了兩位新的櫃台人員？ B：我們現在有很多客人來自西班牙和巴西，所以經理想要第二種【語言】說得夠好的員工，來幫助旅客辦理入住並回答他們的問題。"},{"w":"religion","p":"n.","d":"a belief in God or gods and the activities connected with it","c":"宗教","s":"A: Why did the restaurant add so many new vegetarian dishes to its menu this year? B: Many of our customers follow a religion that does not allow them to eat meat, so the chef created more choices to make sure every guest can enjoy a full meal here.","t":"A：為什麼這家餐廳今年在菜單上加了那麼多新的素食料理？ B：我們有很多顧客信奉不允許吃肉的【宗教】，所以主廚設計了更多選擇，確保每位客人都能在這裡享用完整的一餐。"},{"w":"flag","p":"n.","d":"a piece of cloth with a special design that is the symbol of a country or group","c":"國旗；旗子","s":"A: What should we put on the stage for the welcome ceremony when the Japanese partners arrive on Monday? B: Please place their national flag next to ours behind the speaker's desk, because it shows respect for our guests and will look good in the photos for the newsletter.","t":"A：日本合作夥伴星期一抵達時，歡迎儀式的舞台上應該放什麼？ B：請把他們的【國旗】放在講台後方我們的國旗旁邊，因為這表示對貴賓的尊重，而且在電子報的照片裡也會很好看。"},{"w":"anthem","p":"n.","d":"a country's official song","c":"國歌","s":"A: Why did everyone in the stadium stand up before the football match started last night? B: The band played the national anthem before the opening kick, so all the players and fans stood quietly to show respect, and then the crowd cheered loudly when the game finally began.","t":"A：昨晚足球賽開始前，為什麼體育場裡的每個人都站起來？ B：樂隊在開球前演奏【國歌】，所以所有球員和球迷都安靜地站著表示敬意，比賽終於開始時，觀眾才大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"independence","p":"n.","d":"freedom from control by another country","c":"獨立","s":"A: Why will the bank and the post office be closed next Thursday? B: It is the day the country celebrates its independence from Britain, so it is a public holiday, and there will be a big parade with music and fireworks along the main street in the evening.","t":"A：為什麼銀行和郵局下週四不營業？ B：那天是國家慶祝脫離英國【獨立】的日子，所以是國定假日，晚上主要街道上還會有盛大的遊行，有音樂和煙火。"},{"w":"colony","p":"n.","d":"a country or area controlled by another country","c":"殖民地","s":"A: Why do so many street signs and old buildings in this city look so European? B: The city was a Portuguese colony for more than four hundred years, so the old churches, squares and even some of the food still show the influence of that long period.","t":"A：為什麼這座城市有那麼多路標和老建築看起來很有歐洲風格？ B：這座城市曾經是葡萄牙【殖民地】超過四百年，所以老教堂、廣場，甚至一些食物至今仍顯示出那段漫長時期的影響。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"connected with towns and cities","c":"都市的；城市的","s":"A: Why is the car-sharing company only offering its service in large cities and not in small towns? B: In urban areas, many people live close together, parking is expensive and fewer people own cars, so the service is used much more often and makes a bigger profit.","t":"A：為什麼這家共享汽車公司只在大城市提供服務，而不在小鎮？ B：在【都市】地區，很多人住得很近，停車費很貴，而且擁有汽車的人比較少，所以服務的使用率高得多，利潤也比較大。"},{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the countryside","c":"鄉村的","s":"A: Why is the internet company building so many new towers in the mountains this year? B: The government wants families in rural villages to have fast internet too, so it is paying the company to bring service to farms and small schools far away from the cities.","t":"A：為什麼網路公司今年在山區蓋了那麼多新的基地台？ B：政府希望【鄉村】地區村落的家庭也能有快速網路，所以付錢讓公司把服務帶到遠離城市的農場和小學校。"},{"w":"developed","p":"adj.","d":"having many industries and a high standard of living","c":"已開發的","s":"A: Why are the company's sales of luxury watches so strong in Europe and North America? B: People in highly developed countries usually have higher incomes and more free time, so they are more willing to spend money on expensive gifts and quality products that last for many years.","t":"A：為什麼公司的高級手錶在歐洲和北美賣得那麼好？ B：高度【已開發】國家的人通常收入較高、空閒時間較多，所以比較願意花錢買昂貴的禮物和能用很多年的優質產品。"},{"w":"developing","p":"adj.","d":"becoming richer and building more industries","c":"開發中的","s":"A: Why is our company making a cheaper version of its smartphone this year? B: Many customers in developing countries want a reliable phone but cannot pay high prices yet, so a simpler model with a good camera could help us sell millions more units in Africa and Asia.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司今年要推出比較便宜的智慧型手機版本？ B：許多【開發中】國家的顧客想要可靠的手機，但目前還付不起高價，所以一款相機不錯的簡化機型能幫我們在非洲和亞洲多賣出數百萬支。"},{"w":"coastal","p":"adj.","d":"on or near the coast","c":"沿海的","s":"A: Where is the new hotel resort going to be built, and when will it be ready for guests? B: It will be in a quiet coastal town about two hours south of the airport, right next to the beach, and the owners hope to welcome the first guests before next summer.","t":"A：新的度假飯店要蓋在哪裡？什麼時候可以接待客人？ B：會蓋在機場南邊大約兩小時車程的一個安靜【沿海】小鎮，就在海灘旁邊，業主希望在明年夏天前迎接第一批客人。"},{"w":"inland","p":"adj.","d":"away from the sea, in the middle of a country","c":"內陸的","s":"A: Why does it take so long to ship our products to the customer in Chengdu? B: It is a large inland city far from the ocean, so the containers arrive at the port in Shanghai first and then travel by train for several more days before they reach the warehouse.","t":"A：為什麼把我們的產品運到成都的客戶那裡要花那麼久？ B：那是一座遠離海洋的大型【內陸】城市，所以貨櫃會先抵達上海的港口，再搭火車走好幾天才到倉庫。"},{"w":"diverse","p":"adj.","d":"including many different types of people or things","c":"多元的；各式各樣的","s":"A: Why does the marketing team want to show people of different ages and backgrounds in the new advertisement? B: Our customers are a very diverse group, from students to retired teachers, so the team wants everyone who watches the ad to feel that the product is also made for them.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊想在新廣告裡呈現不同年齡和背景的人？ B：我們的顧客群非常【多元】，從學生到退休老師都有，所以團隊希望每個看廣告的人都覺得這個產品也是為他們設計的。"},{"w":"patriotic","p":"adj.","d":"loving and supporting your country","c":"愛國的","s":"A: Why did the sports drink company use so many red and white colors in its new commercial? B: The ad will be shown during the national team's World Cup games, so the company wanted a patriotic message that makes viewers feel proud and connected to the players.","t":"A：為什麼那家運動飲料公司在新廣告裡用了那麼多紅色和白色？ B：這支廣告會在國家隊的世界盃比賽期間播出，所以公司想傳達【愛國】的訊息，讓觀眾感到驕傲並與球員產生連結。"},{"w":"national","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a whole country","c":"全國的；國家的","s":"A: Why are all the shops downtown so busy with customers buying gifts this week? B: Monday is a national holiday, so most people have a long weekend off work, and many of them are buying presents and food before they travel home to visit their families.","t":"A：為什麼這週市中心的商店都擠滿了買禮物的顧客？ B：星期一是【國定】假日，所以大部分人都有連假，很多人在回家探望家人之前購買禮物和食物。"},{"w":"foreign","p":"adj.","d":"from or connected with another country","c":"外國的","s":"A: Why does the bank have such a long line of travelers at the counter near the entrance today? B: That counter changes foreign money, and many people are getting dollars and euros before the summer holidays, so the staff are busy serving customers all morning.","t":"A：為什麼今天銀行入口附近的櫃台排了那麼長的旅客隊伍？ B：那個櫃台負責兌換【外國】貨幣，很多人在暑假前換美元和歐元，所以員工整個上午都忙著服務顧客。"},{"w":"overseas","p":"adj.","d":"in or from another country across the sea","c":"海外的","s":"A: Why did the furniture company hire three new sales staff who speak both English and Japanese? B: Most of its overseas customers live in the United States and Japan, so the company needs people who can answer emails and phone calls from those markets quickly and politely.","t":"A：為什麼那家家具公司僱用了三位會說英文和日文的新業務人員？ B：它大部分的【海外】顧客住在美國和日本，所以公司需要能快速且有禮貌地回覆來自那些市場的電子郵件和電話的人。"},{"w":"abroad","p":"adv.","d":"in or to a foreign country","c":"在國外；到國外","s":"A: Why is Mr. Chen leaving his job at the bank after working there for fifteen years? B: He has accepted an offer to work abroad for two years at a company in London, and he wants his children to learn English and experience life in another country while they are young.","t":"A：陳先生為什麼在銀行工作十五年後要離職？ B：他接受了一份到【國外】倫敦一家公司工作兩年的機會，他希望孩子們趁年紀還小時學英文，並體驗在另一個國家的生活。"}]},{"unit":85,"theme":"Countryside 鄉村","cards":[{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"in or relating to the countryside","c":"鄉村的；農村的","s":"A: Why is the bank planning to open three small branches outside the city next spring, when most customers now use the mobile app? B: Many older people in rural areas still prefer to talk to a real person about loans and savings, and the nearest branch for them is more than an hour away by bus.","t":"A：大部分顧客現在都用手機應用程式，為什麼銀行還打算明年春天在城外開三家小分行？ B：許多住在【鄉村】地區的年長者仍然比較喜歡和真人討論貸款和存款的事，而且對他們來說最近的分行搭公車要一個多小時。"},{"w":"village","p":"n.","d":"a small group of houses and other buildings in the countryside","c":"村莊","s":"A: Where is the film crew going to shoot the new television commercial for our organic tea, since the city studio is fully booked this month? B: They found a quiet mountain village with old stone houses and narrow streets about two hours south of here, and the local people have agreed to appear in some scenes.","t":"A：既然市區的攝影棚這個月都被訂滿了，拍攝團隊要去哪裡拍我們有機茶的新電視廣告？ B：他們在這裡往南大約兩小時車程的地方找到一個寧靜的山間【村莊】，那裡有古老的石屋和狹窄的街道，而且當地居民也同意在一些場景中入鏡。"},{"w":"farm","p":"n.","d":"land and buildings used for growing crops or keeping animals","c":"農場","s":"A: Why does the restaurant manager drive out of the city every Tuesday morning instead of ordering vegetables from the usual supplier? B: She buys eggs, cheese and vegetables directly from a family farm near the mountains, because the food is fresher, the price is fair, and customers love reading about it on the menu.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳經理每週二早上都開車出城，而不是向平常的供應商訂購蔬菜？ B：她直接向山區附近一座家庭【農場】購買雞蛋、起司和蔬菜，因為食物比較新鮮、價格公道，而且顧客很喜歡在菜單上讀到這些介紹。"},{"w":"farmland","p":"n.","d":"land that is used for farming","c":"農地","s":"A: Why are so many people in the town upset about the plan to build a new shopping center next to the highway? B: The developer wants to cover about fifty hectares of rich farmland with concrete and parking lots, and local families worry that rice growers will lose their jobs and the area will flood more easily.","t":"A：為什麼鎮上這麼多人對在高速公路旁蓋新購物中心的計畫感到不滿？ B：開發商想把大約五十公頃肥沃的【農地】鋪上水泥、蓋成停車場，當地家庭擔心稻農會失去工作，而且這個地區會更容易淹水。"},{"w":"field","p":"n.","d":"an area of open land used for growing crops or keeping animals","c":"田地；原野","s":"A: Why did the photographer ask the bus driver to stop on the country road for a few minutes during the company trip? B: She saw a huge field of yellow sunflowers shining in the afternoon light, and she wanted to take a group photo of all of us for the cover of the annual report.","t":"A：員工旅遊途中，攝影師為什麼請司機在鄉間小路上停幾分鐘？ B：她看到一大片向日葵【田】在午後的陽光下閃閃發亮，想幫我們所有人拍一張團體照，用來當年度報告的封面。"},{"w":"pasture","p":"n.","d":"land covered with grass where cows, sheep or horses eat","c":"牧場；牧草地","s":"A: How does the dairy company keep the quality of its milk so high, even though its prices are lower than most competitors? B: The cows spend most of the day eating grass on open pasture instead of staying inside crowded buildings, so they are healthier and the farmers spend less money on medicine and feed.","t":"A：這家乳品公司的價格比大多數競爭對手低，為什麼還能讓牛奶品質維持這麼高？ B：乳牛一天大部分時間都在開闊的【牧場】上吃草，而不是待在擁擠的建築裡，所以牠們比較健康，農民花在藥品和飼料上的錢也比較少。"},{"w":"barn","p":"n.","d":"a large farm building for storing crops or keeping animals","c":"穀倉；畜棚","s":"A: Have you found a special place for the company's twentieth anniversary party, or are we going to use the hotel ballroom again this year? B: I booked an old wooden barn on a horse farm outside town that has been turned into an event space, with long tables, warm lights and room for two hundred guests.","t":"A：你找到適合公司二十週年派對的特別場地了嗎？還是我們今年又要用飯店的宴會廳？ B：我訂了城外一座馬場上的老舊木造【穀倉】，它已經改建成活動場地，有長桌、溫暖的燈光，可以容納兩百位賓客。"},{"w":"cottage","p":"n.","d":"a small house, usually in the countryside","c":"小屋；村舍","s":"A: Where are you planning to stay during your two-week holiday in the north of England after the busy sales season ends? B: My husband and I rented a small stone cottage beside a quiet lake, with a fireplace and a little garden, because we just want to read, walk and sleep without any phone calls from work.","t":"A：忙碌的銷售旺季結束後，你們去英格蘭北部度假兩週時打算住在哪裡？ B：我先生和我在一座寧靜的湖邊租了一間石造【小屋】，有壁爐和一座小花園，因為我們只想看書、散步和睡覺，不想接到任何工作電話。"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"everything you can see when you look across a large area of land","c":"風景；景觀","s":"A: Why did the tourism board choose that particular region for its new advertising campaign aimed at visitors from Japan and Korea? B: The landscape there changes so much with the seasons, from green rice terraces in summer to golden hills in autumn, that the photographers can create beautiful pictures all year round.","t":"A：觀光局為什麼選擇那個地區來做針對日本和韓國遊客的新廣告活動？ B：那裡的【景觀】隨著季節變化很大，從夏天翠綠的梯田到秋天金黃的山丘，攝影師一整年都能拍出美麗的照片。"},{"w":"scenery","p":"n.","d":"the natural features of an area, such as mountains and trees, especially when beautiful","c":"風景；景色","s":"A: Why do you always take the slow train to the branch office in Hualien instead of flying there in less than an hour? B: The railway runs between the mountains and the ocean, and the scenery is so beautiful that I can relax, prepare for my meetings and arrive feeling much calmer than after a flight.","t":"A：你去花蓮分公司時為什麼總是搭慢車，而不是搭不到一小時的飛機？ B：鐵路穿梭在山與海之間，沿途【風景】非常美，讓我可以放鬆並準備會議，抵達時也比搭飛機平靜許多。"},{"w":"meadow","p":"n.","d":"a field with grass and wild flowers","c":"草地；草原","s":"A: What kind of activities have you planned for the team-building weekend at the mountain resort next month? B: On Saturday afternoon we will have a picnic and some outdoor games in a large meadow full of wild flowers behind the hotel, and in the evening everyone can watch the stars around a campfire.","t":"A：下個月在山區度假村的團隊建立週末，你安排了哪些活動？ B：星期六下午我們會在飯店後面一片開滿野花的大【草地】上野餐並玩一些戶外遊戲，晚上大家可以圍著營火看星星。"},{"w":"valley","p":"n.","d":"an area of low land between hills or mountains","c":"山谷；溪谷","s":"A: Why does the wine company want to open a visitor center so far away from the main cities and highways? B: Its vineyards are in a green valley between two mountain ranges, where the weather is perfect for grapes, and tourists enjoy driving down there to taste the wine and take photos.","t":"A：為什麼這家葡萄酒公司想把遊客中心設在離主要城市和高速公路那麼遠的地方？ B：它的葡萄園位於兩座山脈之間一個翠綠的【山谷】裡，那裡的天氣非常適合種葡萄，遊客也喜歡開車去那裡品酒和拍照。"},{"w":"hill","p":"n.","d":"an area of land higher than the land around it, but smaller than a mountain","c":"小山；丘陵","s":"A: Is the new hotel really worth the extra cost for our conference guests, or should we choose the cheaper one near the train station? B: I think it is worth it, because it sits on top of a hill with a wide view of the bay, and guests can walk down to the beach in ten minutes.","t":"A：新飯店對我們的會議來賓來說真的值得多花錢嗎？還是我們應該選火車站附近比較便宜的那家？ B：我覺得值得，因為它位在一座【小山】的山頂上，可以看到海灣的廣闊景色，來賓走十分鐘就能下到海灘。"},{"w":"forest","p":"n.","d":"a large area of land covered with trees","c":"森林","s":"A: Why did the paper company decide to plant one million trees over the next five years, even though it will cost a lot of money? B: Customers want products that are good for the environment, and the new forest will replace the trees we cut down, protect animals and clean the air for nearby towns.","t":"A：雖然要花很多錢，為什麼這家造紙公司還決定在未來五年種植一百萬棵樹？ B：顧客想要對環境友善的產品，而這片新【森林】可以取代我們砍掉的樹木、保護動物，並為附近的城鎮淨化空氣。"},{"w":"woods","p":"n.","d":"an area of land covered with trees, smaller than a forest","c":"樹林","s":"A: How do you manage to stay so calm and focused during the busy end-of-year period at the accounting firm? B: Every Sunday morning I take my dog for a long walk in the woods behind our apartment building, where it is cool and quiet, and I come back feeling ready for another week of deadlines.","t":"A：會計事務所年底這麼忙，你怎麼還能保持冷靜和專注？ B：每個星期天早上我都會帶狗到我們公寓後面的【樹林】裡散步很久，那裡涼爽又安靜，回來後我就準備好再迎接一週的截止期限了。"},{"w":"stream","p":"n.","d":"a small, narrow river","c":"小溪；溪流","s":"A: Why did the campsite owner tell us not to drink the water from the tap in the cabin without boiling it first? B: The water comes from a small mountain stream that runs past the farms above the camp, so it might contain dirt or bacteria, but there is free bottled water at the front desk.","t":"A：營地老闆為什麼告訴我們，小木屋水龍頭的水要先煮沸才能喝？ B：那些水來自一條流經營地上方農場的山間【小溪】，所以可能含有泥土或細菌，不過櫃檯有免費的瓶裝水。"},{"w":"river","p":"n.","d":"a large natural flow of water that goes into the sea or a lake","c":"河流","s":"A: Why were all the trucks from the northern warehouse delayed by almost three hours yesterday afternoon? B: After two days of heavy rain, the river rose so high that the police closed the main bridge into town, so every vehicle had to take a long route through the mountains.","t":"A：北部倉庫的所有卡車昨天下午為什麼延誤了將近三個小時？ B：連續下了兩天大雨後，【河】水漲得太高，警方封閉了進城的主要橋樑，所以每輛車都得繞遠路穿過山區。"},{"w":"lake","p":"n.","d":"a large area of water surrounded by land","c":"湖；湖泊","s":"A: What makes the new resort different from the other hotels that our travel agency usually recommends to its customers? B: Every room has a balcony that looks out over a clear blue lake, and guests can rent small boats, go fishing or simply sit outside and enjoy the mountain air with a cup of coffee.","t":"A：新的度假村和我們旅行社平常推薦給顧客的其他飯店有什麼不同？ B：每個房間都有可以眺望清澈藍色【湖泊】的陽台，房客可以租小船、去釣魚，或只是坐在外面喝杯咖啡、享受山上的空氣。"},{"w":"wildlife","p":"n.","d":"wild animals and birds living in natural conditions","c":"野生動物","s":"A: Why does the eco-tour company limit each group to only ten people, even though many more customers want to join? B: Large, noisy groups scare the birds, deer and monkeys in the national park, and the guides want visitors to see the wildlife without disturbing the animals or damaging their homes.","t":"A：明明還有更多顧客想參加，為什麼這家生態旅遊公司每團只收十個人？ B：吵鬧的大團體會嚇到國家公園裡的鳥、鹿和猴子，導遊希望遊客能看到【野生動物】，又不打擾牠們或破壞牠們的棲息地。"},{"w":"livestock","p":"n.","d":"animals kept on a farm, such as cows, pigs and sheep","c":"家畜；牲畜","s":"A: Why did the farmers in the area ask the government for financial help after last summer's long drought? B: There was not enough grass or water for their livestock, so they had to buy expensive feed and sell many cows and sheep at low prices, and some families are now in serious debt.","t":"A：去年夏天長期乾旱之後，當地農民為什麼向政府請求經濟援助？ B：他們的【家畜】沒有足夠的草和水，所以他們必須購買昂貴的飼料，並以低價賣掉許多牛羊，有些家庭現在負債很嚴重。"},{"w":"harvest","p":"n.","d":"the time when crops are collected, or the crops that are collected","c":"收成；收穫","s":"A: Why are apple prices at the supermarket so much higher this month than they were at the same time last year? B: A strong storm hit the main growing region just before the harvest, so farmers lost almost half of their fruit, and the stores now have to import apples from overseas.","t":"A：為什麼超市這個月的蘋果價格比去年同期高那麼多？ B：就在【收成】之前，一場強烈的暴風雨襲擊了主要產區，農民損失了將近一半的果實，現在商店只好從國外進口蘋果。"},{"w":"agriculture","p":"n.","d":"farming; growing crops and keeping animals","c":"農業","s":"A: Why is the university offering new courses on drones and computer programs for students in the farming department? B: Modern agriculture uses technology to check soil, water crops and count animals, so graduates who understand these tools can find better jobs and help farms produce more food with fewer workers.","t":"A：為什麼大學要為農學系的學生開設無人機和電腦程式的新課程？ B：現代【農業】會利用科技來檢測土壤、灌溉作物和清點動物，所以懂得這些工具的畢業生能找到更好的工作，並幫助農場用更少的人力生產更多糧食。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and calm, without noise or trouble","c":"寧靜的；平靜的","s":"A: Why did the software company move its design team from the downtown office to a small building outside the city? B: The new location is surrounded by trees and has a very peaceful atmosphere, so the designers can think clearly without traffic noise, and their work has actually improved since the move.","t":"A：為什麼這家軟體公司把設計團隊從市中心的辦公室搬到城外的一棟小建築？ B：新地點被樹木環繞，氣氛非常【寧靜】，設計師可以在沒有車聲的情況下清楚思考，而且搬過去之後他們的作品其實變得更好了。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"far away from towns and cities","c":"偏遠的；遙遠的","s":"A: Why does it take so long for online orders to reach customers who live in the eastern mountains? B: Many of those homes are in remote areas with narrow roads and no nearby post office, so our delivery partner can only send a truck up there twice a week.","t":"A：為什麼住在東部山區的顧客要等那麼久才能收到網路訂單？ B：那些住家很多都在【偏遠】地區，道路狹窄，附近也沒有郵局，所以我們的物流合作夥伴一週只能派兩次卡車上山。"},{"w":"isolated","p":"adj.","d":"far from other places or people; alone","c":"孤立的；偏僻的","s":"A: Why did the new manager of the mountain hotel quit after only three months, even though the salary was very good? B: The hotel is so isolated that the nearest town is two hours away, and he felt lonely because he could rarely see his friends or family on his days off.","t":"A：山上那家飯店的新經理薪水明明很好，為什麼才三個月就辭職了？ B：那家飯店非常【偏僻】，最近的城鎮也要兩個小時車程，他休假時很少能見到朋友或家人，所以覺得很寂寞。"},{"w":"spacious","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of space; large inside","c":"寬敞的","s":"A: Why did you and your wife decide to buy a house in the countryside instead of another apartment in the city? B: For the same price, we got a spacious home with four bedrooms and a big garden, so the children have room to play and I can finally have a proper office for working from home.","t":"A：你和你太太為什麼決定在鄉下買房子，而不是在城市裡再買一間公寓？ B：用同樣的價錢，我們買到一間有四個房間和大花園的【寬敞】住宅，孩子們有空間玩，我也終於能有一間像樣的在家工作辦公室。"},{"w":"natural","p":"adj.","d":"existing in nature; not made or caused by people","c":"天然的；自然的","s":"A: Why are so many visitors choosing the small hot spring town instead of the large resorts near the airport this winter? B: The town has protected its natural beauty, with forests, waterfalls and hot springs that come straight from the ground, and travelers prefer that to big hotels and shopping malls.","t":"A：今年冬天為什麼這麼多遊客選擇那個小溫泉鎮，而不是機場附近的大型度假村？ B：這個小鎮保存了它的【自然】美景，有森林、瀑布和直接從地底湧出的溫泉，比起大飯店和購物中心，旅客更喜歡這些。"},{"w":"fresh","p":"adj.","d":"recently picked or made; (of air) clean and cool","c":"新鮮的；清新的","s":"A: Why do you look so much healthier since you started working at the company's new office in the mountains last spring? B: I walk to work through the trees every morning, breathe clean fresh air all day instead of city smog, and I sleep much better than I did downtown.","t":"A：自從你去年春天開始在公司山上的新辦公室上班後，為什麼看起來健康多了？ B：我每天早上穿過樹林走路上班，整天呼吸乾淨【清新】的空氣，而不是城市的霧霾，睡得也比住在市中心時好多了。"},{"w":"rustic","p":"adj.","d":"simple and typical of the countryside, often in an attractive way","c":"鄉村風格的；質樸的","s":"A: How should we decorate the new café so that it feels different from all the modern coffee chains on this street? B: Let's choose a rustic style with wooden tables, old farm tools on the walls and baskets of vegetables near the counter, so customers feel like they are visiting a country kitchen.","t":"A：我們應該怎麼裝潢新咖啡店，讓它和這條街上所有現代連鎖咖啡店感覺不一樣？ B：我們選擇【鄉村】風格吧，用木頭桌子、在牆上掛舊農具，在櫃檯旁放幾籃蔬菜，讓顧客覺得好像來到鄉下的廚房。"},{"w":"tranquil","p":"adj.","d":"calm, quiet and peaceful","c":"寧靜的；安寧的","s":"A: Why did the yoga company choose a small island for its staff training retreat instead of a conference hotel in the city? B: The island is so tranquil, with soft waves, quiet beaches and no cars at all, that the instructors can rest their minds and practice without any noise or interruptions.","t":"A：為什麼這家瑜伽公司選擇一座小島辦員工訓練營，而不是城市裡的會議飯店？ B：那座島非常【寧靜】，有輕柔的海浪、安靜的海灘，而且完全沒有車子，教練們可以讓心靈休息，在沒有噪音和干擾的情況下練習。"},{"w":"fertile","p":"adj.","d":"(of land) able to grow a lot of good crops","c":"肥沃的","s":"A: Why did the food company buy land in that river area instead of somewhere closer to its factory in the north? B: The soil there is very fertile because the river brings rich mud every year, so the vegetables grow quickly, and the company can produce more crops while using fewer chemicals.","t":"A：為什麼這家食品公司在那片河流地區買地，而不是在比較靠近北部工廠的地方買？ B：那裡的土壤非常【肥沃】，因為河流每年都會帶來營養豐富的泥土，所以蔬菜長得很快，公司能用更少的化學藥劑生產更多作物。"},{"w":"quietly","p":"adv.","d":"making very little noise; in a calm way","c":"安靜地","s":"A: What did you enjoy most about the weekend you spent at your grandparents' farm after the stressful product launch? B: Early each morning I sat quietly on the porch with a cup of tea, listening to the birds and watching the fog lift from the fields, and I didn't check my email even once.","t":"A：在壓力很大的產品發表會之後，你在祖父母的農場度過的那個週末，最喜歡的是什麼？ B：每天一大早，我都【安靜地】坐在門廊喝杯茶，聽鳥叫、看著霧從田野上散去，而且我連一次電子郵件都沒有檢查。"},{"w":"outdoors","p":"adv.","d":"outside, not in a building","c":"在戶外","s":"A: Why does the summer camp for our employees' children have so few computer games and indoor classes this year? B: The organizers want the kids to spend most of the day outdoors, hiking, swimming in the lake and learning about plants and insects, because they think children already spend too much time looking at screens.","t":"A：今年為我們員工小孩辦的夏令營，為什麼電腦遊戲和室內課程這麼少？ B：主辦單位希望孩子們一天大部分時間都待【在戶外】，去健行、在湖裡游泳、認識植物和昆蟲，因為他們認為孩子們花太多時間看螢幕了。"},{"w":"away","p":"adv.","d":"not at home or at work; at a distance","c":"不在；離開；在遠處","s":"A: Why can't anyone reach the sales director this week, even though there is an important contract that needs his signature? B: He is away on a hiking holiday in the mountains where there is no phone signal, but his assistant has permission to sign the contract for him until he returns on Monday.","t":"A：明明有一份重要合約需要業務總監簽名，為什麼這週沒人聯絡得上他？ B：他【不在】公司，去山上健行度假了，那裡沒有手機訊號，不過在他星期一回來之前，他的助理有權代他簽約。"}]},{"unit":86,"theme":"Course 課程","cards":[{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"all the subjects and topics taught in a school or training program","c":"（整體）課程；全部課程","s":"A: Why is the training department hiring two new staff members before the new employees start in September? B: The director wants to update the whole curriculum for new hires, adding topics like data safety and customer care, so they need people who can design materials and plan each week.","t":"A：為什麼訓練部門要在新進員工九月報到前再聘請兩名新員工？ B：主任想要更新新進人員的整套【課程】，加入資料安全和顧客服務等主題，所以他們需要能設計教材並規劃每週內容的人。"},{"w":"syllabus","p":"n.","d":"a list of the topics, readings and dates for a course","c":"課程大綱；教學大綱","s":"A: How will I know which chapters to read before each meeting of the marketing course that the company is paying for? B: The teacher will email everyone the syllabus on Monday, and it shows the topics, reading pages and due dates for all twelve weeks, so you can plan your time.","t":"A：我要怎麼知道公司出錢讓我上的行銷課，每次上課前該讀哪些章節？ B：老師星期一會把【課程大綱】寄給大家，上面列出全部十二週的主題、閱讀頁數和繳交期限，所以你可以規劃時間。"},{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"a period of time when someone is taught something","c":"一堂課；課程","s":"A: Are you free to join us for dinner after work on Thursday, since the whole team is celebrating the new contract? B: I'd love to, but I have a Spanish lesson with a private tutor from six to seven, so I can meet you at the restaurant a little later.","t":"A：既然全隊要慶祝新合約，你星期四下班後有空跟我們一起吃晚餐嗎？ B：我很想去，但我六點到七點要和家教上一堂西班牙文【課】，所以我可以晚一點到餐廳跟你們會合。"},{"w":"class","p":"n.","d":"a group of students taught together; a period of teaching","c":"班級；一堂課","s":"A: Why do you always leave the office so quickly on Wednesday evenings, even when we still have reports to finish? B: I'm taking an accounting class at the community college near my apartment, and it starts at half past six, so I can't be late.","t":"A：為什麼你每週三晚上總是那麼快離開辦公室，即使我們還有報告要完成？ B：我在公寓附近的社區大學上一門會計【課】，六點半開始，所以我不能遲到。"},{"w":"lecture","p":"n.","d":"a talk given to a group of people to teach them about a subject","c":"講座；演講","s":"A: Did you find the talk by the famous economist at the business school useful for our planning meeting next week? B: Yes, her lecture on global trade lasted two hours, and she explained clearly why shipping costs will rise next year, so I took a lot of notes for our team.","t":"A：你覺得那位知名經濟學家在商學院的演說對我們下週的規劃會議有幫助嗎？ B：有，她關於全球貿易的【講座】長達兩小時，清楚解釋了明年運費為何會上漲，所以我替我們團隊做了很多筆記。"},{"w":"seminar","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where a small group discusses a subject with a teacher or expert","c":"研討會；研討課","s":"A: Why is the small meeting room on the third floor booked for the whole afternoon on Friday? B: Our lawyer is leading a seminar for the managers about the new privacy laws, and there will only be twelve people, so everyone can ask questions and discuss real cases.","t":"A：為什麼三樓的小會議室星期五整個下午都被預訂了？ B：我們的律師要為經理們主持一場關於新隱私法的【研討會】，只有十二個人參加，所以每個人都可以提問並討論實際案例。"},{"w":"workshop","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where people learn a skill by doing practical activities","c":"工作坊；研習會","s":"A: What should the new sales staff bring to the training on Saturday morning? B: They should bring their laptops, because the afternoon workshop is very hands-on, and they will practice writing real emails and making short sales calls in small groups while the trainer gives them advice.","t":"A：新進業務人員星期六早上的培訓應該帶什麼？ B：他們應該帶筆電，因為下午的【工作坊】非常著重實作，他們會分成小組練習寫真正的電子郵件和打簡短的銷售電話，同時培訓師會給他們建議。"},{"w":"module","p":"n.","d":"one separate part of a course","c":"（課程的）單元；模組","s":"A: How much of the online safety training have you finished, since the deadline is the end of this month? B: I've completed three out of five parts, and the next module is about fire safety, which takes about forty minutes, so I'll do it during my lunch break tomorrow.","t":"A：既然期限是這個月底，你的線上安全培訓完成多少了？ B：五個部分我已經完成三個，下一個【單元】是關於消防安全，大約需要四十分鐘，所以我明天午休時會完成它。"},{"w":"unit","p":"n.","d":"one part of a textbook or course, usually about one topic","c":"單元；課","s":"A: Which part of the English textbook should we cover before the overseas clients visit our factory next month? B: Let's focus on the unit about giving directions and describing products, because our staff will need those skills most when they show the visitors around the production lines.","t":"A：下個月海外客戶參觀我們工廠前，我們應該上英文課本的哪一部分？ B：我們把重點放在關於指路和描述產品的那一個【單元】，因為員工帶訪客參觀生產線時最需要這些技能。"},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work given to someone as part of a course or job","c":"作業；任務","s":"A: Why are you staying at your desk so late tonight when the office is almost empty? B: I have to finish a written assignment for my business management course, which is a ten-page report on a local company, and I must hand it in to my professor by midnight.","t":"A：辦公室幾乎沒人了，你今晚為什麼還這麼晚坐在位子上？ B：我得完成企業管理課的書面【作業】，是一份關於本地公司的十頁報告，而且我必須在午夜前交給教授。"},{"w":"homework","p":"n.","d":"work that a student is asked to do at home","c":"家庭作業；功課","s":"A: How is your son doing at his new school since your family moved to Taipei for your job in the spring? B: He likes his teachers, but he gets a lot of homework every night, so I usually help him with math after dinner before I check my work emails.","t":"A：自從你春天因為工作全家搬到台北後，你兒子在新學校適應得如何？ B：他喜歡他的老師，但他每天晚上都有很多【功課】，所以我通常在晚餐後先幫他做數學，再查看工作郵件。"},{"w":"project","p":"n.","d":"a planned piece of work that has a clear goal","c":"專題；計畫；企畫","s":"A: What do students in the evening marketing program have to do to pass at the end of the term? B: Each group must complete a final project, in which they create a full advertising plan for a real local business and then present it to the owner and the teacher.","t":"A：夜間行銷課程的學生在學期末要做什麼才能及格？ B：每一組都必須完成一個期末【專題】，為一家真實的本地商家制定完整的廣告計畫，然後向老闆和老師報告。"},{"w":"assessment","p":"n.","d":"the process of judging how well someone has learned or done something","c":"評量；評估","s":"A: How does the language school decide which level new students should join when they first arrive? B: Everyone takes a short assessment on the first day, including a reading test and a ten-minute talk with a teacher, and then the school puts them in the right group.","t":"A：新生剛到時，語言學校如何決定他們應該加入哪個程度？ B：每個人第一天都要做一個簡短的【評量】，包括閱讀測驗和與老師十分鐘的對話，然後學校會把他們分到合適的組別。"},{"w":"exam","p":"n.","d":"a formal test of knowledge or skill","c":"考試","s":"A: Why have you been reading that thick accounting book on the train every morning for the past month? B: I'm preparing for an important professional exam in December, and if I pass it, I can get a promotion and a higher salary at the bank next year.","t":"A：過去一個月，你為什麼每天早上都在火車上讀那本厚厚的會計書？ B：我在準備十二月一場重要的專業【考試】，如果通過，明年我就可以在銀行升職並拿到更高的薪水。"},{"w":"quiz","p":"n.","d":"a short test","c":"小考；測驗","s":"A: Is there anything we have to do after watching the safety video that the human resources department sent us this morning? B: Yes, there is a short quiz with ten questions at the end, and you need to get at least eight right before the system marks your training as complete.","t":"A：看完人資部今天早上寄給我們的安全影片後，還有什麼要做的嗎？ B：有，最後有一個十題的簡短【測驗】，你至少要答對八題，系統才會把你的培訓標記為完成。"},{"w":"grade","p":"n.","d":"a mark or score that shows how good a student's work is","c":"成績；分數","s":"A: Why does the company want to see my school records when I'm applying for the trainee program? B: They only accept people with a good grade in math and English, because trainees have to read financial reports and write to overseas customers from their very first week.","t":"A：我申請儲備幹部計畫時，公司為什麼要看我的在校紀錄？ B：他們只接受數學和英文【成績】好的人，因為儲備幹部從第一週就必須閱讀財務報告並寫信給海外客戶。"},{"w":"credit","p":"n.","d":"a unit that shows a student has finished part of a course","c":"學分","s":"A: Why did you choose the weekend program at the university instead of the cheaper online one? B: The university gives each student a credit for every course they finish, and I need twelve more of them to complete my degree before I apply for a manager position.","t":"A：你為什麼選擇大學的週末課程，而不是較便宜的線上課程？ B：大學每完成一門課就給學生一個【學分】，而我在申請經理職位前，還需要再修十二個學分才能完成學位。"},{"w":"certificate","p":"n.","d":"an official document that shows you have finished a course or passed a test","c":"證書；結業證明","s":"A: What will the staff receive after they finish the six-week first aid training at the hospital? B: Each person will get an official certificate with their name on it, which they should give to the office manager, because the company must keep a copy for the safety inspectors.","t":"A：員工在醫院完成六週急救訓練後會得到什麼？ B：每個人都會拿到一張印有自己名字的正式【證書】，他們應該交給辦公室經理，因為公司必須留一份影本給安全檢查員。"},{"w":"enroll","p":"v.","d":"to officially join a course or school","c":"註冊；報名入學","s":"A: I want to improve my presentation skills before the big conference in March, so do you know any good courses? B: You could enroll in the public speaking course at the training center downtown, and if you sign up before Friday, the company will pay half of the fee.","t":"A：我想在三月的大型研討會前提升簡報技巧，你知道有什麼好課程嗎？ B：你可以【報名】市中心培訓中心的公眾演說課程，如果你在星期五前登記，公司會支付一半的費用。"},{"w":"register","p":"v.","d":"to put your name on an official list for a course or event","c":"登記；註冊","s":"A: How can I get a seat at the free computer training that the city library is offering next month? B: You need to register on the library website by the end of this week, because there are only twenty places and they usually fill up within two or three days.","t":"A：我要怎麼才能在市立圖書館下個月提供的免費電腦訓練中拿到名額？ B：你必須在這週結束前在圖書館網站上【登記】，因為只有二十個名額，而且通常兩三天內就會額滿。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event, class or meeting","c":"參加；出席；上（課）","s":"A: Why is Michael working from home on Tuesday and Thursday mornings this month? B: He has to attend a leadership course at the main office across the city, and the classes start at eight, so the manager agreed to let him work from home afterward.","t":"A：麥可這個月為什麼星期二和星期四早上在家工作？ B：他必須去城市另一頭的總公司【上】領導力課程，課程八點開始，所以經理同意讓他上完課後在家工作。"},{"w":"study","p":"v.","d":"to spend time learning about a subject","c":"學習；讀書；研讀","s":"A: Where do you usually go after work on weekdays, since you never join us at the gym anymore? B: I go to the quiet café near the station to study for my accounting test, because it's hard to focus at home with my two young children running around.","t":"A：你平日下班後通常去哪裡？你都不再跟我們去健身房了。 B：我會去車站附近那家安靜的咖啡店【讀書】準備會計考試，因為家裡有兩個小孩跑來跑去，很難專心。"},{"w":"learn","p":"v.","d":"to get new knowledge or a new skill","c":"學習；學會","s":"A: Why did the company send you to Japan for three months last year when you were still quite new? B: They wanted me to learn how their partner factory controls quality, so I could teach the same methods to our team when I came back to Taiwan.","t":"A：去年你還算是新人，公司為什麼派你去日本三個月？ B：他們希望我【學習】合作工廠如何控管品質，這樣我回台灣後就可以把同樣的方法教給我們的團隊。"},{"w":"teach","p":"v.","d":"to give lessons or show someone how to do something","c":"教；教導","s":"A: Who is going to train the new cashiers before the second store opens in the shopping mall next week? B: Linda will teach them how to use the new payment system, because she has worked at the counter for five years and she explains things very patiently.","t":"A：第二間店下週在購物中心開幕前，誰要訓練新收銀員？ B：琳達會【教】他們如何使用新的付款系統，因為她在櫃台工作了五年，而且解釋事情非常有耐心。"},{"w":"instructor","p":"n.","d":"a person who teaches a practical skill or a course","c":"講師；教練","s":"A: How was the first day of the driving course that the delivery company asked you to take? B: It went well, because the instructor was very calm and patient, and he showed us how to drive the large trucks safely on narrow roads before we practiced by ourselves.","t":"A：快遞公司要你上的駕駛課第一天怎麼樣？ B：很順利，因為【教練】非常冷靜有耐心，他先示範如何在狹窄道路上安全駕駛大卡車，然後我們才自己練習。"},{"w":"trainer","p":"n.","d":"a person who teaches people skills for a job or sport","c":"培訓師；訓練員","s":"A: Our customer service team keeps getting complaints about rude phone calls, so what should we do about it? B: I think we should hire a professional trainer to run a two-day program on handling angry customers, because our staff have never had any proper training in that area.","t":"A：我們客服團隊一直收到關於電話態度不佳的投訴，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我認為我們應該聘請一位專業【培訓師】來舉辦為期兩天的應對憤怒顧客課程，因為我們的員工從未在這方面接受過正式訓練。"},{"w":"beginner","p":"n.","d":"a person who has just started learning something","c":"初學者","s":"A: Should I join the advanced Excel class with the rest of the finance team, or is it too difficult for me? B: Since you've only used spreadsheets for a few weeks, you're still a beginner, so you should start with the basic course and move up next term.","t":"A：我應該跟財務團隊的其他人一起上進階Excel課，還是那對我來說太難了？ B：既然你才用試算表幾週，你還是個【初學者】，所以你應該先從基礎課程開始，下學期再往上升級。"},{"w":"intermediate","p":"adj.","d":"at a middle level, between beginner and advanced","c":"中級的","s":"A: Which Japanese class did the language school put you in after the test you took last Saturday? B: They put me in the intermediate group, because I can already have simple conversations, but I still make many grammar mistakes when I write emails to our clients in Osaka.","t":"A：你上週六考完試後，語言學校把你分到哪一班日文課？ B：他們把我分到【中級】組，因為我已經能進行簡單的對話，但寫電子郵件給大阪客戶時仍然會犯很多文法錯誤。"},{"w":"advanced","p":"adj.","d":"at a high level; for people who already know a lot","c":"高級的；進階的","s":"A: Why is Kevin always the person who fixes the problems with our sales data and reports? B: He took an advanced course in data analysis last year, so he understands complex formulas and charts much better than the rest of us, who only know the basics.","t":"A：為什麼總是凱文在處理我們銷售數據和報表的問題？ B：他去年上過資料分析的【進階】課程，所以他對複雜公式和圖表的理解比我們其他只懂基礎的人好得多。"},{"w":"online","p":"adj.","d":"done over the internet","c":"線上的","s":"A: How can our staff in the Kaohsiung branch join the training if they can't travel to Taipei next month? B: We'll offer an online version of the course, so they can watch the lessons on their laptops at home and send their questions to the teacher by email.","t":"A：如果高雄分公司的員工下個月不能來台北，他們要怎麼參加培訓？ B：我們會提供這門課的【線上】版本，讓他們可以在家用筆電觀看課程，並用電子郵件把問題寄給老師。"},{"w":"intensive","p":"adj.","d":"involving a lot of work in a short time","c":"密集的；強化的","s":"A: How did your new assistant improve her English so quickly before starting the job in our export department? B: She took an intensive two-week course, with six hours of classes every day, and she also practiced speaking with a tutor every evening after dinner.","t":"A：你的新助理在進入我們出口部門工作前，英文怎麼進步得這麼快？ B：她上了一個為期兩週的【密集】課程，每天上六個小時，而且每天晚餐後還和家教練習口說。"},{"w":"elective","p":"adj.","d":"chosen by the student, not required","c":"選修的","s":"A: Do all the students in the hotel management program have to take the wine course in their second year? B: No, it's an elective subject, so students can choose it if they're interested, but many people take it because it helps them find jobs in fine restaurants.","t":"A：飯店管理學程的所有學生第二年都必須修葡萄酒課嗎？ B：不，那是一門【選修】科目，學生有興趣的話可以選，但很多人會修，因為這有助於他們在高級餐廳找到工作。"},{"w":"compulsory","p":"adj.","d":"required by a rule; you must do it","c":"必修的；強制的","s":"A: Can I skip the fire safety training next Tuesday, since I already have a meeting with an important client that afternoon? B: I'm afraid not, because the training is compulsory for every employee in this building, so you'll need to move your client meeting to another day.","t":"A：我下週二下午已經和一位重要客戶有約，可以不參加消防安全訓練嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為這項訓練對這棟大樓的每位員工都是【強制性】的，所以你得把客戶會議改到別天。"},{"w":"practical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with doing things, not ideas; useful in real situations","c":"實用的；實作的","s":"A: What did you think of the business writing course that the company paid for last month? B: It was very practical, because instead of just talking about theory, the teacher had us write real emails, reports and meeting notes that we could use at work the next day.","t":"A：你覺得公司上個月出錢讓你上的商業寫作課怎麼樣？ B：非常【實用】，因為老師不只是講理論，而是讓我們寫真正的電子郵件、報告和會議紀錄，隔天就能用在工作上。"}]},{"unit":87,"theme":"COVID-19 新冠肺炎","cards":[{"w":"virus","p":"n.","d":"a very small living thing that causes illness","c":"病毒","s":"A: Why did the clinic ask all the staff to wear masks again in the waiting room this week? B: A new flu virus is spreading quickly through the city, and the doctors want to protect older patients, so everyone must also wash their hands often and stay home if they feel unwell.","t":"A：診所這週為什麼又要求所有員工在候診室戴口罩？ B：一種新的流感【病毒】正在城裡迅速傳播，醫生們想保護年長的病人，所以每個人也必須常洗手，覺得不舒服就待在家裡。"},{"w":"disease","p":"n.","d":"an illness that affects people, animals or plants","c":"疾病","s":"A: Why is the company offering free health checks to all employees in the main office next month? B: The HR team learned that heart disease is a serious problem for people who sit at desks all day, so they invited nurses from the local hospital to check everyone's blood pressure and give advice.","t":"A：公司為什麼下個月要為總公司所有員工提供免費健康檢查？ B：人資團隊得知心臟【疾病】對整天坐在辦公桌前的人來說是個嚴重問題，所以邀請了當地醫院的護士來為每個人量血壓並提供建議。"},{"w":"coronaviruses","p":"n.","d":"a group of viruses that can cause illnesses such as colds and COVID-19","c":"冠狀病毒（複數）","s":"A: What was the guest speaker from the university talking about at the health and safety seminar yesterday afternoon? B: She explained that coronaviruses are a large family of germs, and some of them only cause a mild cold, while others, like the one behind the global crisis in 2020, can be very dangerous.","t":"A：昨天下午健康安全研討會上，那位大學來的客座講者在談什麼？ B：她解釋說【冠狀病毒】是一個龐大的病菌家族，其中有些只會引起輕微感冒，而另一些，像是造成2020年全球危機的那一種，可能非常危險。"},{"w":"outbreak","p":"n.","d":"a sudden start of a disease that affects many people","c":"（疾病的）爆發","s":"A: Why did the cruise company cancel next week's trip to the islands and offer every passenger a full refund? B: There was an outbreak of stomach flu on the ship last week, and more than two hundred people got sick, so the whole ship has to be cleaned carefully before it can sail again.","t":"A：郵輪公司為什麼取消下週前往群島的行程，並提供每位乘客全額退款？ B：上週船上【爆發】了腸胃型流感，超過兩百人生病，所以整艘船必須徹底清潔後才能再次出航。"},{"w":"transmission","p":"n.","d":"the passing of a disease from one person to another","c":"傳播；傳染","s":"A: Why did the office manager put plastic screens between all the desks in the customer service area this morning? B: The health department says the screens can reduce the transmission of the flu from one worker to another, especially in busy rooms where people talk on the phone all day.","t":"A：辦公室經理今天早上為什麼在客服區的所有辦公桌之間裝了塑膠隔板？ B：衛生局說隔板可以減少流感在員工之間的【傳播】，尤其是在大家整天講電話的忙碌空間裡。"},{"w":"symptom","p":"n.","d":"a sign that you have an illness","c":"症狀","s":"A: When should employees stay at home instead of coming into the office during the flu season this winter? B: If you have even one symptom, such as a high fever, a sore throat or a bad cough, you should call your supervisor, work from home and see a doctor as soon as possible.","t":"A：今年冬天流感季期間，員工什麼時候應該待在家而不是進辦公室？ B：只要你有任何一種【症狀】，例如發高燒、喉嚨痛或嚴重咳嗽，就應該打電話給主管、在家工作，並儘快去看醫生。"},{"w":"respiratory","p":"adj.","d":"connected with breathing","c":"呼吸的；呼吸道的","s":"A: Why does the factory require all workers in the paint room to wear special masks during every shift? B: Breathing in the chemicals every day can cause serious respiratory problems, such as coughing and difficulty breathing, so the masks protect their lungs while they work with the paint.","t":"A：工廠為什麼要求噴漆室的所有工人每個班次都要戴特殊口罩？ B：每天吸入化學物質可能造成嚴重的【呼吸道】問題，例如咳嗽和呼吸困難，所以口罩能在他們處理油漆時保護肺部。"},{"w":"asthma","p":"n.","d":"an illness that makes it difficult to breathe","c":"氣喘；哮喘","s":"A: Why did Mr. Chen ask to move his desk away from the window near the busy road outside? B: He has asthma, and the dust and smoke from the traffic sometimes make it hard for him to breathe, so he feels much better sitting in the quieter area near the meeting rooms.","t":"A：陳先生為什麼要求把他的辦公桌從靠近外面繁忙馬路的窗邊移開？ B：他有【氣喘】，車流造成的灰塵和廢氣有時讓他呼吸困難，所以他坐在靠近會議室較安靜的區域會舒服很多。"},{"w":"acute","p":"adj.","d":"very serious or severe, and starting suddenly","c":"急性的；劇烈的","s":"A: Why was the sales director taken to the hospital in the middle of the client meeting this afternoon? B: He suddenly felt acute pain in his stomach and could not stand up, so his assistant called an ambulance, and the doctors are now checking whether he needs an operation tonight.","t":"A：業務總監今天下午為什麼在客戶會議進行到一半時被送到醫院？ B：他突然感到胃部【劇烈的】疼痛，站不起來，所以他的助理叫了救護車，醫生們正在檢查他今晚是否需要動手術。"},{"w":"pneumonia","p":"n.","d":"a serious illness of the lungs","c":"肺炎","s":"A: Why has Ms. Lin been away from the office for almost three weeks, and when will she return to work? B: Her cold got much worse and turned into pneumonia, so she had to stay in the hospital for several days, and her doctor says she needs another week of rest at home.","t":"A：林小姐為什麼已經快三個星期沒來辦公室？她什麼時候會回來上班？ B：她的感冒變得嚴重很多，轉成了【肺炎】，所以她必須住院好幾天，醫生說她還需要在家休息一個星期。"},{"w":"syndrome","p":"n.","d":"a group of signs that together show a particular illness","c":"症候群；綜合症","s":"A: Why did the airline start showing a short video about leg exercises on all of its long international flights? B: Sitting still for many hours can cause a health problem sometimes called economy class syndrome, so the video teaches passengers simple ways to move their legs and keep their blood flowing.","t":"A：航空公司為什麼開始在所有長程國際航班上播放關於腿部運動的短片？ B：長時間坐著不動可能引起一種有時被稱為經濟艙【症候群】的健康問題，所以影片教乘客用簡單的方法活動雙腿、保持血液循環。"},{"w":"epidemic","p":"n.","d":"a disease that spreads quickly among many people in one area","c":"（區域性）流行病；疫情","s":"A: Why did the government ask all large companies to let their staff work from home for the next two weeks? B: A flu epidemic has moved across several cities in the north, and hospitals are already full, so officials want fewer people on crowded trains and buses until the number of cases goes down.","t":"A：政府為什麼要求所有大公司讓員工在接下來兩週在家工作？ B：一場流感【疫情】已經擴散到北部好幾個城市，醫院已經爆滿，所以官員希望在病例數下降之前減少搭乘擁擠火車和公車的人。"},{"w":"pandemic","p":"n.","d":"a disease that spreads over many countries at the same time","c":"全球大流行病","s":"A: How did your travel agency survive when almost nobody could fly overseas a few years ago? B: During the pandemic, we stopped selling international tours and started offering local hiking trips and online cooking classes, which helped us keep most of our staff until people could travel abroad again.","t":"A：幾年前幾乎沒人能搭機出國時，你們的旅行社是怎麼撐過去的？ B：在【全球大流行】期間，我們停止銷售國際旅遊行程，改推當地健行之旅和線上烹飪課，這幫助我們留住大部分員工，直到大家能再次出國旅行。"},{"w":"epicentre","p":"n.","d":"the central place where something bad is happening most strongly","c":"中心；重災區","s":"A: Why did the company move its Asian sales meeting from the capital to a hotel on the coast at the last minute? B: The capital had become the epicentre of a serious flu outbreak, with thousands of new cases every day, so the managers decided it was safer to hold the meeting somewhere else.","t":"A：公司為什麼在最後一刻把亞洲業務會議從首都移到海邊的一家飯店？ B：首都成了一場嚴重流感疫情的【中心】，每天都有數千個新病例，所以經理們決定在別的地方開會比較安全。"},{"w":"infect","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a disease","c":"傳染；感染","s":"A: Why does the hospital ask every visitor to clean their hands at the front door before going upstairs? B: Germs on your hands can easily infect patients whose bodies are already weak, so washing or cleaning your hands is one of the simplest ways to keep everyone in the building safe.","t":"A：醫院為什麼要求每位訪客上樓前在正門清潔雙手？ B：手上的病菌很容易【感染】本來身體就虛弱的病人，所以洗手或清潔雙手是讓大樓裡每個人保持安全最簡單的方法之一。"},{"w":"infection","p":"n.","d":"an illness caused by germs entering the body","c":"感染","s":"A: Why did the dentist give you medicine after your appointment, even though the treatment didn't hurt at all? B: She took out a broken tooth, and she wants to prevent an infection in my mouth, so I have to take the pills twice a day for a week and avoid very hot drinks.","t":"A：牙醫為什麼在看診後給你藥，即使治療一點都不痛？ B：她拔掉了一顆斷掉的牙齒，想防止我嘴裡【感染】，所以我必須一天吃兩次藥，連吃一週，並避免喝太燙的飲料。"},{"w":"disinfect","p":"v.","d":"to clean something with chemicals to kill germs","c":"消毒","s":"A: What do the cleaners do every evening after the last customers leave the fitness center? B: They disinfect all the machines, door handles and changing rooms with a strong cleaning spray, so that the gym is safe and fresh for the early members who arrive at six the next morning.","t":"A：健身中心最後一批客人離開後，清潔人員每天晚上做什麼？ B：他們用強效清潔噴霧為所有器材、門把和更衣室【消毒】，讓健身房對隔天早上六點來的早鳥會員來說安全又清新。"},{"w":"contagious","p":"adj.","d":"easily passed from one person to another","c":"傳染性的；會傳染的","s":"A: Should I come to the team meeting tomorrow morning if I still have a slight cough and a runny nose? B: Please stay home, because the doctor said this kind of flu is very contagious for at least five days, and we don't want the whole team to get sick before the big product launch.","t":"A：如果我明天早上還有點咳嗽和流鼻水，還應該來參加團隊會議嗎？ B：請待在家裡，因為醫生說這種流感至少五天內都很容易【傳染】，我們不希望整個團隊在大型產品發表會前全都生病。"},{"w":"contaminate","p":"v.","d":"to make something dirty or harmful by adding germs or chemicals","c":"污染","s":"A: Why did the restaurant throw away all the salad and chicken in the kitchen this morning? B: The fridge stopped working overnight, and the manager was worried that bacteria could contaminate the food, so she decided it was safer to throw everything away than to risk making customers sick.","t":"A：餐廳今天早上為什麼把廚房裡所有的沙拉和雞肉都丟掉了？ B：冰箱整晚故障，經理擔心細菌會【污染】食物，所以她決定把東西全丟掉比冒著讓客人生病的風險更安全。"},{"w":"expose","p":"v.","d":"to put someone in a situation where they could be harmed","c":"使暴露於","s":"A: Why do all the lab workers have to wear gloves, glasses and long coats, even for simple tests? B: Some of the samples carry harmful germs, and the company doesn't want to expose its staff to any danger, so everyone must follow the safety rules carefully from the moment they enter the lab.","t":"A：為什麼所有實驗室人員即使做簡單的檢驗也要戴手套、護目鏡和穿長袍？ B：有些樣本帶有有害病菌，公司不想讓員工【暴露】在任何危險中，所以每個人從進入實驗室的那一刻起都必須仔細遵守安全規定。"},{"w":"droplet","p":"n.","d":"a very small drop of liquid","c":"小滴；飛沫","s":"A: Why is the hotel asking guests to cover their mouths with a tissue or their arm when they cough in the lobby? B: Every time a sick person coughs, each tiny droplet of water from the mouth can carry germs through the air, and it may land on tables, door handles or other guests nearby.","t":"A：飯店為什麼要求客人在大廳咳嗽時用紙巾或手臂遮住嘴巴？ B：生病的人每次咳嗽，嘴巴噴出的每一個微小【飛沫】都可能把病菌帶到空氣中，並落在附近的桌子、門把或其他客人身上。"},{"w":"respiratory droplet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tiny drop of liquid that comes out when people cough, sneeze or talk","c":"呼吸道飛沫","s":"A: The new office has a fresh air system, but why do we still need to keep two meters apart in the meeting room? B: The system helps, but a single respiratory droplet from someone who is talking or sneezing can still travel quite far, so staying apart lowers the chance of passing the flu to a colleague.","t":"A：新辦公室有新鮮空氣系統，但為什麼我們在會議室裡仍需保持兩公尺距離？ B：系統有幫助，但一個人說話或打噴嚏時的一顆【呼吸道飛沫】仍可能傳得相當遠，所以保持距離能降低把流感傳給同事的機會。"},{"w":"ventilator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that helps a sick person breathe","c":"呼吸器","s":"A: Why did the hospital spend so much of its budget on new equipment for the intensive care unit this year? B: It bought ten more machines, because each ventilator helps patients breathe when their lungs are too weak, and during last winter's flu season the hospital did not have enough of them.","t":"A：醫院今年為什麼把那麼多預算花在加護病房的新設備上？ B：它多買了十台機器，因為每一台【呼吸器】都能在病人肺部太虛弱時幫助他們呼吸，而去年冬天流感季時醫院的數量不夠。"},{"w":"asymptomatic","p":"adj.","d":"having an illness but showing no signs of it","c":"無症狀的","s":"A: Why did the company test every employee before the overseas trip, even people who felt completely healthy? B: Some people who carry the virus are asymptomatic, which means they feel fine and have no fever or cough, but they can still pass it to others on the plane or at the trade fair.","t":"A：公司為什麼在出國前替每位員工做檢測，甚至包括覺得完全健康的人？ B：有些帶有病毒的人是【無症狀的】，也就是說他們感覺很好，沒有發燒或咳嗽，但仍可能在飛機上或商展時傳染給別人。"},{"w":"target","p":"v.","d":"to aim help or action at a particular group or place","c":"以…為目標；針對","s":"A: Why is the city sending free health vans only to a few neighborhoods instead of to every part of town? B: Officials decided to target the areas with the highest number of cases and the most elderly residents, so the limited number of nurses and test kits can help the people who need them most.","t":"A：市政府為什麼只派免費健康巡迴車到少數幾個社區，而不是城裡每個地方？ B：官員決定把【目標鎖定】在病例數最多、年長居民最多的地區，讓有限的護理師和檢測試劑能幫助最需要的人。"},{"w":"zoonotic","p":"adj.","d":"able to pass from animals to humans","c":"人畜共通的","s":"A: Why are the farm workers at the poultry company getting special health training this month? B: The trainers are teaching them about zoonotic diseases, which can pass from chickens and other animals to humans, so the workers learn how to wear protective clothing and wash properly after each shift.","t":"A：家禽公司的農場工人這個月為什麼要接受特別的健康訓練？ B：訓練人員正在教他們有關【人畜共通的】疾病，這類疾病可能從雞和其他動物傳染給人，所以工人們要學習如何穿防護衣，以及每個班次後如何正確清洗。"},{"w":"widespread","p":"adj.","d":"happening in many places or among many people","c":"廣泛的；普遍的","s":"A: Why did the company decide to make the online shopping app its top priority for the next two years? B: Our research showed widespread changes in how people shop since the health crisis, with many customers in every age group now ordering food and clothes on their phones instead of visiting stores.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定把線上購物應用程式列為未來兩年的首要任務？ B：我們的研究顯示，自從健康危機以來，人們的購物方式出現了【廣泛的】改變，各年齡層的許多顧客現在都用手機訂購食物和衣服，而不是去實體店。"},{"w":"super-spreader","p":"n.","d":"a person who passes a disease to an unusually large number of people","c":"超級傳播者","s":"A: Why did the health department contact everyone who attended the company's annual dinner last Friday? B: One guest turned out to be a super-spreader who passed the flu to more than forty people at the party, so officials want everyone who was there to watch their health closely for a week.","t":"A：衛生局為什麼聯絡了上週五參加公司年度晚宴的每個人？ B：其中一位賓客原來是【超級傳播者】，在派對上把流感傳給了四十多人，所以官員希望在場的每個人在一週內密切注意自己的健康。"},{"w":"epidemiologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies how diseases spread","c":"流行病學家","s":"A: Who did the city council invite to speak at the public meeting about the new flu rules next week? B: They invited an epidemiologist from the national university, who studies how diseases move through large groups of people, so she can explain why the rules are needed and answer questions from local business owners.","t":"A：市議會邀請誰在下週關於新流感規定的公開會議上演講？ B：他們邀請了國立大學的一位【流行病學家】，她研究疾病如何在大群人之間傳播，可以解釋為什麼需要這些規定，並回答當地企業主的問題。"},{"w":"telehealth","p":"n.","d":"medical advice or care given by phone or video","c":"遠距醫療","s":"A: How can our employees in the small branch offices see a doctor without traveling to the city? B: The new insurance plan includes a telehealth service, so staff can talk to a doctor through a video call on their phone or laptop and even get a prescription sent to a nearby pharmacy.","t":"A：我們在小分公司的員工如何不用進城就能看醫生？ B：新的保險方案包含【遠距醫療】服務，所以員工可以用手機或筆電透過視訊通話和醫生談話，甚至可以讓處方箋送到附近的藥局。"},{"w":"precaution","p":"n.","d":"something you do to stop a bad thing from happening","c":"預防；防範","s":"A: Why are all the staff at the bank wearing masks today when nobody in the office is sick? B: It's just a precaution, because several customers came in with bad colds yesterday, and the manager doesn't want anyone at the counter to get ill during the busiest week of the month.","t":"A：今天銀行所有員工為什麼都戴著口罩，明明辦公室沒人生病？ B：這只是一種【防範】，因為昨天有好幾位客人重感冒來辦事，經理不希望櫃檯的任何人在一個月中最忙的那週生病。"},{"w":"precautionary measures","p":"n.phr.","d":"actions taken in advance to prevent danger or harm","c":"預防措施","s":"A: What steps will the organizers take to protect the guests at next month's trade show in the convention center? B: They will introduce several precautionary measures, such as checking temperatures at the entrance, placing hand gel at every booth and limiting the number of people in each hall at one time.","t":"A：主辦單位將採取哪些步驟，在下個月會展中心的商展中保護來賓？ B：他們將實施幾項【預防措施】，例如在入口量體溫、在每個攤位放置乾洗手，以及限制每個展廳同時入場的人數。"},{"w":"severity","p":"n.","d":"how serious or bad something is","c":"嚴重程度","s":"A: Why are the doctors at the clinic asking every patient so many questions about their fever and cough? B: They need to understand the severity of each illness before deciding on treatment, because some patients only need rest at home, while others must go straight to the hospital for more tests.","t":"A：診所的醫生為什麼要問每位病人那麼多關於發燒和咳嗽的問題？ B：他們在決定治療方式前，需要了解每種病的【嚴重程度】，因為有些病人只需在家休息，而另一些必須直接到醫院做更多檢查。"},{"w":"vaccine","p":"n.","d":"a substance put into the body to protect it from a disease","c":"疫苗","s":"A: Why is the company setting up a small clinic in the staff cafeteria every Friday this month? B: Nurses from the local hospital will give the flu vaccine to any employee who wants it, which is free and fast, so nobody has to take time off work to visit a doctor.","t":"A：公司這個月為什麼每週五都在員工餐廳設置一個小診所？ B：當地醫院的護士會為任何想接種的員工施打流感【疫苗】，免費又快速，所以沒有人需要請假去看醫生。"},{"w":"immune","p":"adj.","d":"protected from a disease and unable to catch it","c":"免疫的","s":"A: Why did you get the flu shot this year when you said you never get sick in winter? B: My doctor explained that nobody is fully immune to new types of flu, and since I travel to trade fairs every month and meet hundreds of people, I decided it was better to be safe.","t":"A：你說你冬天從不生病，為什麼今年還去打流感疫苗？ B：醫生跟我解釋，沒有人對新型流感是完全【免疫的】，而且因為我每個月都去參加商展、接觸數百人，我決定還是安全一點比較好。"},{"w":"immune systems","p":"n.phr.","d":"the parts of the body that fight illness","c":"免疫系統（複數）","s":"A: Why does the nursing home ask visitors with even a mild cold to stay away for a few days? B: Many of the elderly residents have weak immune systems, so an illness that seems small to a healthy adult can become very dangerous for them and move quickly through the building.","t":"A：為什麼養老院要求即使只有輕微感冒的訪客也要幾天內不要來？ B：許多年長住民的【免疫系統】很弱，所以對健康成人來說似乎很小的病，對他們可能變得非常危險，並在整棟樓迅速傳開。"},{"w":"new strains","p":"n.phr.","d":"new types of a virus or germ","c":"新病毒株","s":"A: Why do scientists have to update the flu vaccine every single year instead of using the same one? B: The virus keeps changing, and new strains appear each season in different parts of the world, so the medicine companies must study them and change the vaccine to give people the best protection.","t":"A：為什麼科學家每年都要更新流感疫苗，而不是一直用同一種？ B：病毒不斷變化，每一季世界各地都會出現【新病毒株】，所以藥廠必須研究它們並調整疫苗，給人們最好的保護。"},{"w":"life-threatening","p":"adj.","d":"so serious that it could cause death","c":"危及生命的","s":"A: Why did the flight attendant ask whether there was a doctor on board during our flight to Tokyo? B: A passenger had a life-threatening reaction to some nuts in his meal and could hardly breathe, so a nurse sitting in row twelve helped him until the plane landed and an ambulance arrived.","t":"A：我們飛往東京的航班上，空服員為什麼詢問機上是否有醫生？ B：一位乘客對餐點中的堅果產生了【危及生命的】過敏反應，幾乎無法呼吸，所以坐在第十二排的一位護士幫助他，直到飛機降落、救護車抵達。"},{"w":"self-isolate","p":"v.","d":"to stay away from other people so you do not spread a disease","c":"自我隔離","s":"A: What should I do if someone in my family tests positive for the flu while I'm working on the team project? B: Company rules say you must self-isolate at home for five days, so you can't come to the office, but you can still join our meetings online and send your reports by email.","t":"A：如果我在做團隊專案期間，家人流感檢測呈陽性，我該怎麼辦？ B：公司規定你必須在家【自我隔離】五天，所以你不能進辦公室，但你仍可以線上參加會議，並用電子郵件寄報告。"},{"w":"quarantine","p":"n.","d":"a period when people must stay apart to stop a disease from spreading","c":"隔離；檢疫","s":"A: Why couldn't the new engineer from Germany start work at our Taipei office on the first of the month? B: When he arrived, the government rules required a week of hotel quarantine for all travelers from overseas, so he worked online from his hotel room until he was allowed to leave.","t":"A：那位從德國來的新工程師為什麼無法在月初到我們台北辦公室上班？ B：他抵達時，政府規定所有海外旅客都要在飯店【隔離】一週，所以他在飯店房間線上工作，直到獲准離開。"},{"w":"hand sanitizer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a liquid or gel used to clean hands without water","c":"乾洗手；手部消毒液","s":"A: What did the hotel do to make guests feel safer after the flu season began this year? B: They placed bottles of hand sanitizer at the front desk, beside every elevator and outside the restaurant, so guests can clean their hands quickly whenever they touch buttons or door handles.","t":"A：今年流感季開始後，飯店做了什麼讓客人感覺更安全？ B：他們在櫃檯、每部電梯旁和餐廳外放置了一瓶瓶【乾洗手】，讓客人每次碰觸按鈕或門把後都能快速清潔雙手。"},{"w":"antimicrobial","p":"adj.","d":"able to kill germs or stop them from growing","c":"抗菌的","s":"A: Why did the hospital choose the more expensive material for the new beds and curtains in the patient rooms? B: The fabric is antimicrobial, which means it stops many germs from growing on its surface, so it helps reduce illness among patients and makes the cleaners' work a little easier.","t":"A：醫院為什麼為病房的新病床和簾子選擇比較貴的材料？ B：這種布料是【抗菌的】，也就是能阻止許多病菌在表面生長，所以有助於減少病人生病，也讓清潔人員的工作輕鬆一點。"},{"w":"contain","p":"v.","d":"to stop something harmful from spreading","c":"控制；遏止","s":"A: Why did the factory close only one production line instead of shutting down the whole building last week? B: Three workers on that line got sick with the flu, and the managers wanted to contain the illness quickly, so they sent that team home while the other lines kept working safely.","t":"A：工廠上週為什麼只關閉一條生產線，而不是整棟建築停工？ B：那條生產線上有三名工人得了流感，經理們想迅速【控制】疫情，所以讓那組人回家，其他生產線則安全地繼續運作。"},{"w":"social distancing","p":"n.phr.","d":"keeping a safe space between yourself and other people","c":"社交距離","s":"A: Why are there yellow lines on the floor in front of every cashier in the supermarket? B: The store started social distancing during the flu season, so the lines show customers where to stand and help them keep enough space between each other while they wait to pay.","t":"A：為什麼超市每個收銀台前的地板上都有黃線？ B：商店在流感季期間開始實施【社交距離】，所以這些線告訴顧客該站在哪裡，幫助他們排隊等結帳時彼此保持足夠空間。"},{"w":"community spread","p":"n.phr.","d":"the passing of a disease among people in a local area without a known source","c":"社區傳播","s":"A: Why did the city close the public libraries and sports centers even though there were only a few cases at first? B: Officials found community spread, which means people were catching the virus in shops and on buses without traveling anywhere, so they knew the number of cases could rise very quickly.","t":"A：雖然一開始只有少數病例，市政府為什麼關閉了公立圖書館和運動中心？ B：官員發現了【社區傳播】，意思是人們沒有去過任何地方，卻在商店和公車上感染病毒，所以他們知道病例數可能迅速上升。"},{"w":"vulnerable","p":"adj.","d":"easily hurt or harmed","c":"易受傷害的；脆弱的","s":"A: Why does the pharmacy open one hour early every Tuesday morning just for older customers? B: Elderly people are more vulnerable to serious illness during the winter, so the owner wants them to shop safely before the store gets crowded with office workers on their way to work.","t":"A：藥局為什麼每週二早上提早一小時只為年長顧客開門？ B：年長者在冬天更【容易受到】重病侵襲，所以老闆希望他們在店裡擠滿趕著上班的上班族之前安全地購物。"},{"w":"incubation period","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time between catching a disease and showing signs of it","c":"潛伏期","s":"A: Why must the travelers who were on the same flight as the sick passenger watch their health for two weeks? B: This flu has an incubation period of up to ten days, so people may feel fine at first even though they are already carrying the illness and could become sick later.","t":"A：為什麼和那位生病乘客同班機的旅客必須觀察自己的健康兩週？ B：這種流感的【潛伏期】長達十天，所以人們一開始可能感覺沒事，即使他們已經帶有病毒，之後也可能發病。"},{"w":"medical care","p":"n.phr.","d":"help and treatment from doctors and nurses","c":"醫療照護","s":"A: Why did the company add a doctor and two nurses to the team at its new mine in the mountains? B: The mine is three hours from the nearest town, so workers need quick medical care if someone gets hurt or sick, and the company wants to make sure help is always close by.","t":"A：公司為什麼在山區的新礦場團隊增加了一位醫生和兩位護理師？ B：礦場離最近的城鎮有三個小時路程，所以如果有人受傷或生病，工人需要即時的【醫療照護】，公司想確保隨時都有援助在身邊。"},{"w":"PPE","p":"n.","d":"personal protective equipment, such as masks, gloves and gowns","c":"個人防護裝備","s":"A: Why did the hospital order so many boxes of gloves, masks and gowns from the supplier this month? B: The nurses use a lot of PPE every day when they care for sick patients, and the manager wants to make sure the hospital never runs out during the busy winter season.","t":"A：醫院這個月為什麼向供應商訂購了那麼多箱手套、口罩和隔離衣？ B：護理師照顧病人時每天要用大量的【個人防護裝備】，經理想確保醫院在忙碌的冬季絕不會缺貨。"},{"w":"spread","p":"v.","d":"to pass from one person or place to others","c":"傳播；擴散","s":"A: Why does the manager want everyone to stay home when they have a fever, even during the busiest weeks? B: When sick people come to work, they can easily spread germs to everyone in the office, and then half the team might be absent at the same time, which is much worse for business.","t":"A：經理為什麼要大家發燒時待在家，即使是在最忙的幾週？ B：生病的人來上班時，很容易把病菌【傳播】給辦公室裡的每個人，然後可能一半的團隊同時缺勤，這對生意更糟。"},{"w":"face mask","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cover worn over the nose and mouth","c":"口罩","s":"A: Do visitors need to bring anything special when they tour the food factory next Thursday? B: Everyone must wear a face mask and a hair cap inside the production area, but we will give them to you at the entrance, so you only need comfortable shoes and your visitor pass.","t":"A：訪客下週四參觀食品工廠時需要帶什麼特別的東西嗎？ B：每個人在生產區內都必須戴【口罩】和髮帽，不過我們會在入口發給你們，所以你們只需要穿舒適的鞋子並帶訪客證。"},{"w":"stockpile","p":"v.","d":"to collect and keep a large amount of something for later","c":"囤積；儲備","s":"A: Why are the shelves for rice, toilet paper and canned food almost empty at the supermarket today? B: After the news report about the new flu, many shoppers started to stockpile basic goods at home, even though the government said there was no need, so the store is waiting for new deliveries.","t":"A：為什麼今天超市裡米、衛生紙和罐頭的貨架幾乎都空了？ B：新流感的新聞報導出來後，許多購物者開始在家【囤積】基本物資，儘管政府說沒有必要，所以店家正在等新的貨送到。"},{"w":"lockdown","p":"n.","d":"a time when people must stay at home and most places are closed","c":"封城；封鎖","s":"A: How did your restaurant manage to keep earning money when the city was closed for a month? B: During the lockdown, nobody could eat inside restaurants, so we started a delivery service and sold meal boxes online, and now those orders make up almost a third of our income.","t":"A：城市封閉一個月的時候，你的餐廳是怎麼維持收入的？ B：在【封城】期間，沒有人能在餐廳內用餐，所以我們開始外送服務並在網上賣餐盒，現在那些訂單幾乎佔我們收入的三分之一。"},{"w":"curfew","p":"n.","d":"a rule that people must stay indoors after a certain time","c":"宵禁","s":"A: Why did the restaurants downtown close so early during the health crisis, even on Friday nights? B: The city set a ten o'clock curfew, so people had to be at home by then, and the owners closed their kitchens at nine to give staff enough time to clean and travel home.","t":"A：在健康危機期間，市中心的餐廳為什麼那麼早關門，連週五晚上也是？ B：市政府實施了晚上十點的【宵禁】，人們必須在那之前回到家，所以老闆們九點就關廚房，讓員工有足夠時間清潔和回家。"}]},{"unit":88,"theme":"Creative Person 有創意的人","cards":[{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and interesting ideas or things","c":"有創意的；創造性的","s":"A: Why did the hotel chain hire a new advertising agency instead of keeping the old one that worked with them for ten years? B: The managers felt the old ads looked the same every year, and they wanted a more creative team that could think of fresh ideas to attract younger travelers.","t":"A：為什麼這家連鎖飯店要聘請新的廣告公司，而不繼續和合作了十年的舊公司合作？ B：經理們覺得舊的廣告每年看起來都一樣，他們想要一個更有【創意】的團隊，能想出新點子來吸引年輕旅客。"},{"w":"creativity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make new ideas or things","c":"創造力；創意","s":"A: What did the trainer say about the long meetings we have every Monday morning in the main conference room? B: She said that sitting in the same room for three hours kills creativity, so she suggested short walking meetings outside, where people feel relaxed and share new ideas more easily.","t":"A：訓練師對我們每週一早上在主會議室開的冗長會議有什麼看法？ B：她說在同一個房間坐三個小時會扼殺【創造力】，所以她建議改在戶外舉行簡短的步行會議，讓大家感到放鬆，也更容易分享新點子。"},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing new and unusual ideas","c":"富有想像力的","s":"A: How did the small bakery near the station become so popular on social media in only a few months? B: The owner came up with an imaginative idea to bake cakes that look like famous buildings, and customers love taking photos of them before they eat them.","t":"A：車站附近那家小麵包店怎麼在短短幾個月內就在社群媒體上爆紅？ B：老闆想出一個很有【想像力】的點子，把蛋糕做成知名建築的樣子，顧客很喜歡在吃之前先拍照。"},{"w":"innovative","p":"adj.","d":"using new methods or ideas","c":"創新的","s":"A: Why are so many investors interested in that young technology company from Taichung this year? B: It has developed an innovative app that helps restaurants reduce food waste by predicting how many customers will come each day, and several large hotel groups have already signed contracts.","t":"A：為什麼今年有這麼多投資人對那家來自台中的年輕科技公司感興趣？ B：它開發了一款【創新的】應用程式，能預測每天會有多少顧客上門，幫助餐廳減少食物浪費，而且好幾家大型飯店集團已經簽約了。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"new and different from others","c":"原創的；新穎的","s":"A: Did the marketing director like the slogans that the summer interns wrote for the new juice drink? B: She liked most of them, but she said one slogan was too similar to a competitor's, so she asked the interns to come up with something more original by Friday.","t":"A：行銷總監喜歡暑期實習生為新果汁飲料寫的標語嗎？ B：她大部分都喜歡，但她說有一句標語和競爭對手的太像了，所以她要求實習生在星期五前想出更【有原創性】的內容。"},{"w":"inventive","p":"adj.","d":"able to think of new and clever ways to do things","c":"有發明才能的；善於創新的","s":"A: How did the warehouse staff solve the problem of boxes falling off the high shelves last month? B: One inventive worker built a simple wooden barrier from leftover materials, and it worked so well that the manager decided to install the same design in all three warehouses.","t":"A：上個月倉庫員工怎麼解決箱子從高架子上掉下來的問題？ B：一位很【有發明才能】的員工用剩下的材料做了一個簡單的木製擋板，效果好到經理決定在三間倉庫都安裝同樣的設計。"},{"w":"visionary","p":"adj.","d":"able to imagine how the future could be","c":"有遠見的；有眼光的","s":"A: Why do so many employees still talk about the woman who started this company thirty years ago? B: She was a visionary leader who believed people would shop online long before most companies did, and her plans helped us grow from a tiny office into an international business.","t":"A：為什麼還有那麼多員工在談論三十年前創辦這家公司的那位女士？ B：她是一位很有【遠見的】領導者，早在大多數公司之前就相信人們會在網路上購物，她的規劃幫助我們從一間小辦公室成長為國際企業。"},{"w":"artist","p":"n.","d":"a person who paints, draws or makes other art","c":"藝術家；畫家","s":"A: Who painted the colorful picture of the harbor that hangs on the wall behind the reception desk? B: A local artist from Keelung made it for us last year, and many guests ask the receptionist where they can buy her other paintings of the city.","t":"A：掛在接待櫃台後面牆上那幅色彩繽紛的港口畫是誰畫的？ B：是去年一位基隆在地的【藝術家】為我們畫的，很多客人都會問接待人員在哪裡可以買到她其他描繪這座城市的畫作。"},{"w":"designer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to plan how things will look","c":"設計師","s":"A: Have you decided who will plan the new look of our restaurant before it opens again in March? B: Yes, we hired a young interior designer who has worked on several popular cafés downtown, and she will show us her drawings and color samples next Tuesday.","t":"A：你決定好由誰在三月重新開幕前規劃我們餐廳的新風格了嗎？ B：決定了，我們聘請了一位年輕的室內【設計師】，她曾經參與市中心好幾家熱門咖啡館的設計，下週二會給我們看她的草圖和色樣。"},{"w":"writer","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes books, articles or other texts","c":"作家；撰稿人","s":"A: Who is going to prepare the English text for our new company website and the product brochures? B: We found a freelance writer who used to work for a travel magazine, and she promised to send us the first draft of every page within two weeks.","t":"A：誰要負責準備我們新公司網站和產品手冊的英文內容？ B：我們找到一位以前在旅遊雜誌工作過的自由【撰稿人】，她答應在兩週內把每一頁的初稿寄給我們。"},{"w":"musician","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays or writes music","c":"音樂家","s":"A: Are we going to play recorded music at the company's year-end party at the hotel again this time? B: No, the planning team booked a musician who plays the piano and sings, so guests can enjoy live performances while they have dinner and wait for the awards.","t":"A：這次公司在飯店舉辦的尾牙，我們還是要播放錄好的音樂嗎？ B：不是，籌備小組請了一位會彈鋼琴又會唱歌的【音樂家】，讓賓客在吃晚餐和等待頒獎時能欣賞現場表演。"},{"w":"inventor","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes something new that did not exist before","c":"發明家","s":"A: Why is there a small museum on the first floor of the factory that visitors can walk through? B: It tells the story of the inventor who designed our first electric fan in 1965, and it shows his early drawings, tools and the machines he built in his garage.","t":"A：為什麼工廠一樓有一間訪客可以參觀的小型博物館？ B：它講述了在1965年設計出我們第一台電風扇的那位【發明家】的故事，並展示了他早期的草圖、工具，以及他在車庫裡做出來的機器。"},{"w":"creator","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes something new","c":"創作者；創造者","s":"A: Why did the bank invite that young woman with the popular cooking videos to its financial planning event? B: She is the creator of a well-known online channel with over a million followers, and the bank hopes she can help explain saving money to younger customers.","t":"A：為什麼銀行邀請那位拍熱門烹飪影片的年輕女生參加理財規劃活動？ B：她是一個擁有超過一百萬追蹤者的知名網路頻道的【創作者】，銀行希望她能幫忙向年輕顧客解釋存錢的觀念。"},{"w":"talented","p":"adj.","d":"having a natural ability to do something well","c":"有才華的；有天分的","s":"A: Why did the sales department decide to send Kevin to the international trade fair in Singapore next month? B: He is a very talented speaker who can explain our products clearly in three languages, and customers always remember him after his short presentations at the booth.","t":"A：為什麼業務部決定下個月派Kevin去新加坡參加國際商展？ B：他是一位非常【有才華的】講者，能用三種語言清楚介紹我們的產品，而且顧客在攤位上聽完他簡短的介紹後總是對他印象深刻。"},{"w":"gifted","p":"adj.","d":"having a special natural ability","c":"有天賦的；資優的","s":"A: Is it true that the new accountant also plays the violin in a city orchestra on weekends? B: Yes, she is a gifted violinist who started playing when she was four, and she will perform a short piece at the opening of our charity concert next month.","t":"A：新來的會計師週末也在市立管弦樂團拉小提琴，是真的嗎？ B：是的，她是一位很有【天賦的】小提琴手，四歲就開始拉琴，下個月她會在我們慈善音樂會的開場演奏一首短曲。"},{"w":"skilled","p":"adj.","d":"having the training and experience to do a job well","c":"熟練的；有技能的","s":"A: Why is the furniture factory offering such high salaries in its job advertisements this spring? B: It is very hard to find skilled workers who can build wooden tables and chairs by hand, so the company must pay more to attract experienced people from other cities.","t":"A：為什麼這家家具工廠今年春天在徵人廣告上開出這麼高的薪水？ B：要找到能手工製作木桌和木椅的【熟練】工人非常困難，所以公司必須付更多薪水，才能吸引其他城市有經驗的人。"},{"w":"resourceful","p":"adj.","d":"good at finding quick and clever ways to solve problems","c":"足智多謀的；善於應變的","s":"A: How did the tour guide handle the problem when the bus broke down on the mountain road last weekend? B: She was very resourceful; she called a local taxi company, found a small café where everyone could wait, and still got the group to the hotel before dinner.","t":"A：上週末巴士在山路上拋錨時，導遊是怎麼處理的？ B：她非常【足智多謀】；她打電話給當地計程車行，找了一家小咖啡館讓大家等候，最後還是在晚餐前把團員送到飯店。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"showing feelings or ideas clearly","c":"富有表現力的；表情豐富的","s":"A: Why did the director choose that actor for our new television commercial instead of a more famous star? B: He has a very expressive face, so he can show surprise, joy and worry without saying a word, which is perfect for a short ad with no dialogue.","t":"A：為什麼導演選那位演員拍我們新的電視廣告，而不是找更有名的明星？ B：他的臉部表情非常【豐富】，不用說一句話就能表現出驚訝、喜悅和擔憂，非常適合沒有對白的短廣告。"},{"w":"inspired","p":"adj.","d":"filled with new ideas and a strong wish to do something","c":"受到啟發的；有靈感的","s":"A: What made the chef add so many new Thai dishes to the restaurant's menu this autumn? B: She felt inspired after spending two weeks at a cooking school in Bangkok, and she wanted to share the fresh flavors she discovered at the night markets with her customers.","t":"A：是什麼讓主廚今年秋天在餐廳菜單上加了這麼多新的泰式料理？ B：她在曼谷的烹飪學校待了兩週後深受【啟發】，想把她在夜市發現的新鮮風味分享給顧客。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"something that gives you new ideas","c":"靈感；鼓舞","s":"A: Where did the designer get the idea for the blue and white pattern on our new coffee cups? B: She said the old tiles in her grandmother's kitchen in Tainan were her main inspiration, and she wanted the cups to feel warm and familiar to local customers.","t":"A：設計師是從哪裡得到我們新咖啡杯上藍白圖案的點子？ B：她說她外婆在台南廚房裡的舊磁磚是她主要的【靈感來源】，她希望這些杯子讓在地顧客感到溫暖又熟悉。"},{"w":"brainstorm","p":"v.","d":"to share many ideas quickly in a group","c":"腦力激盪；集思廣益","s":"A: How are we going to choose a name for the new snack product before the launch in December? B: The manager wants the whole team to brainstorm together on Thursday afternoon, and everyone should write down at least five ideas before we vote on the best one.","t":"A：在十二月上市前，我們要怎麼為新的零食產品取名字？ B：經理希望整個團隊星期四下午一起【腦力激盪】，每個人在投票選出最好的名字之前，至少要寫下五個點子。"},{"w":"imagine","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture of something in your mind","c":"想像","s":"A: Why did the architect bring virtual reality glasses to the meeting with the hotel owners yesterday? B: She wanted to help them imagine what the new lobby will look like, because it is hard for most people to understand a building just from flat drawings on paper.","t":"A：為什麼建築師昨天和飯店業主開會時帶了虛擬實境眼鏡？ B：她想幫助他們【想像】新大廳會是什麼樣子，因為大多數人很難只靠紙上的平面圖就理解一棟建築。"},{"w":"create","p":"v.","d":"to make something new or cause something to exist","c":"創造；建立","s":"A: What is the main goal of the new training program that the human resources department started this month? B: It aims to create a friendly working environment where new employees feel comfortable asking questions, so they can learn faster and stay with the company longer.","t":"A：人資部這個月開始的新訓練計畫，主要目標是什麼？ B：它的目的是【營造】一個友善的工作環境，讓新進員工能自在地發問，這樣他們能學得更快，也會在公司待得更久。"},{"w":"design","p":"v.","d":"to plan and draw how something will look or work","c":"設計","s":"A: Who is responsible for the new uniforms that the airline's flight attendants will start wearing next year? B: A famous fashion company was asked to design them, and it chose light fabric and soft colors so the staff can stay comfortable on long international flights.","t":"A：航空公司空服員明年開始穿的新制服是由誰負責的？ B：一家知名時裝公司受邀【設計】制服，他們選用輕薄的布料和柔和的顏色，讓員工在長途國際航班上也能保持舒適。"},{"w":"compose","p":"v.","d":"to write music, a poem or a letter","c":"作曲；創作；撰寫","s":"A: Did the marketing team buy the background music for our new television commercial from an online library? B: No, we paid a young musician to compose a short, cheerful song just for us, so no other company can use the same music in their ads.","t":"A：行銷團隊是從線上音樂庫購買新電視廣告的背景音樂嗎？ B：不是，我們付錢請了一位年輕音樂家專門為我們【創作】一首輕快的短曲，這樣其他公司就不能在廣告中使用同樣的音樂。"},{"w":"craft","p":"v.","d":"to make something carefully and with skill","c":"精心製作；手工製作","s":"A: Why are the leather bags from that small shop in Taipei so much more expensive than the ones in department stores? B: The owner and her two assistants craft every bag by hand in their workshop, so each one takes about three days to make, and they use only the best leather from Italy.","t":"A：為什麼台北那家小店的皮包比百貨公司的貴那麼多？ B：老闆和她的兩位助理在工作室裡用手工【精心製作】每一個包包，所以每個大約要花三天才能完成，而且他們只用來自義大利的最好皮革。"},{"w":"experiment","p":"v.","d":"to try new ways of doing something to see what happens","c":"實驗；嘗試","s":"A: Why does the new coffee shop downstairs change its menu almost every week? B: The young owner likes to experiment with different flavors, such as oolong tea lattes and honey cold brew, and she asks regular customers to give feedback before she adds a drink permanently.","t":"A：為什麼樓下新開的咖啡店幾乎每週都換菜單？ B：年輕的老闆喜歡【嘗試】不同的口味，例如烏龍茶拿鐵和蜂蜜冷萃，而且她在正式加入一款飲料之前，會請常客提供意見。"},{"w":"express","p":"v.","d":"to show a feeling or idea in words or actions","c":"表達；表示","s":"A: Why did the manager ask everyone to fill out an anonymous survey after the office moved to the new building? B: She wanted to give employees a safe way to express their opinions about the new space, because some people feel nervous about complaining in front of their team.","t":"A：為什麼經理在辦公室搬到新大樓後，要求大家填寫一份匿名問卷？ B：她想讓員工有一個安全的方式來【表達】對新空間的意見，因為有些人不敢在團隊面前抱怨。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: Why did so many people stop at our booth at the technology fair even though we are a small company? B: They were curious about the robot arm that was making coffee in front of the booth, so they came closer to watch, and then our staff explained our products.","t":"A：我們只是一家小公司，為什麼在科技展上有那麼多人在我們的攤位停下來？ B：他們對攤位前那隻正在煮咖啡的機器手臂感到很【好奇】，所以走近來看，然後我們的員工就向他們介紹產品。"},{"w":"open-minded","p":"adj.","d":"willing to accept new and different ideas","c":"思想開明的；心胸開闊的","s":"A: What kind of person are you looking for to lead the new team that will work with partners in Japan and Vietnam? B: We need someone who is open-minded and willing to listen to different ideas, because people from each country have their own ways of doing business.","t":"A：你們在找什麼樣的人來帶領這個要和日本及越南夥伴合作的新團隊？ B：我們需要一個【思想開明】、願意聆聽不同想法的人，因為每個國家的人都有自己做生意的方式。"},{"w":"bold","p":"adj.","d":"brave and willing to take risks","c":"大膽的；勇敢的","s":"A: Why are people in the industry so surprised by the new advertising campaign from that small phone company? B: It made a very bold decision to compare its phones directly with the market leader's on huge billboards downtown, and the campaign has already doubled its online sales.","t":"A：為什麼業界對那家小手機公司的新廣告活動這麼驚訝？ B：它做了一個非常【大膽的】決定，在市中心的巨型看板上直接把自家手機和市場龍頭的手機做比較，而這個活動已經讓它的網路銷售翻倍了。"},{"w":"playful","p":"adj.","d":"full of fun; not serious","c":"愛玩的；俏皮的；活潑的","s":"A: Why does the new children's clothing brand use cartoon animals in all of its shop windows and online ads? B: The company wants a playful image that makes parents smile and children want to come inside, so even the price tags have small drawings of rabbits and bears.","t":"A：為什麼新的童裝品牌在所有櫥窗和網路廣告中都使用卡通動物？ B：公司想要一個【活潑有趣的】形象，讓家長會心一笑、孩子想走進店裡，所以連價格標籤上都畫有小兔子和小熊。"},{"w":"unique","p":"adj.","d":"being the only one of its kind","c":"獨特的；獨一無二的","s":"A: Why do so many tourists visit that small hotel in the mountains even though it is far from the train station? B: Every room has a unique theme based on a local legend, and guests enjoy staying in a different room each time they come back with their friends.","t":"A：那家山上的小旅館離火車站很遠，為什麼還有那麼多觀光客去住？ B：每個房間都有一個以當地傳說為基礎的【獨特】主題，客人很喜歡每次和朋友回來時都住不同的房間。"},{"w":"distinctive","p":"adj.","d":"easy to notice because it is different from others","c":"有特色的；與眾不同的","s":"A: How can customers recognize our company's delivery trucks so easily, even from far away on the highway? B: All of the trucks are painted a distinctive bright orange with a large green leaf on the side, so people notice them immediately, and it works like free advertising.","t":"A：為什麼顧客即使在高速公路上離很遠，也能輕易認出我們公司的送貨卡車？ B：所有卡車都漆成【很有特色的】亮橘色，側面還有一片大大的綠葉，所以大家馬上就會注意到，這就像免費廣告一樣。"},{"w":"creatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that uses new and original ideas","c":"有創意地","s":"A: Our department's budget for the year-end party was cut in half, so how are we going to make it fun this time? B: We'll have to think creatively, for example, by holding the party in the office garden, asking colleagues to bring homemade food, and organizing simple games instead of hiring performers.","t":"A：我們部門的尾牙預算被砍了一半，這次要怎麼辦得好玩？ B：我們得【發揮創意】思考，例如在辦公室花園辦派對、請同事帶自製料理，以及安排簡單的遊戲，而不是請表演者。"}]},{"unit":89,"theme":"Crime 犯罪","cards":[{"w":"criminal","p":"n.","d":"a person who has broken the law","c":"罪犯","s":"A: Why did the bank hire an extra security guard for the main branch downtown last month? B: The police warned the manager that a criminal had been using stolen cards at several ATMs in the area, so the bank wanted someone to watch the machines during busy hours.","t":"A：為什麼銀行上個月要為市中心的總行多聘一位保全？ B：警方警告經理，有一名【罪犯】一直在該地區好幾台提款機使用偷來的卡片，所以銀行希望在尖峰時段有人看守這些機器。"},{"w":"theft","p":"n.","d":"the crime of stealing something","c":"竊盜；偷竊","s":"A: Why does everyone now need a key card to enter the storage room on the third floor? B: After the theft of six new laptops last month, the office manager decided that only staff from the IT department should be allowed inside, and she also put a camera above the door.","t":"A：為什麼現在大家都需要門禁卡才能進入三樓的儲藏室？ B：上個月發生六台新筆電的【竊盜】事件後，辦公室經理決定只有資訊部的員工可以進入，她還在門上方裝了一台攝影機。"},{"w":"robbery","p":"n.","d":"the crime of taking money or things from a person or place, often by force","c":"搶劫","s":"A: Why is the convenience store on the corner closing at ten o'clock instead of staying open all night? B: There was a robbery there last week when two men took all the money from the cash register, so the owner feels it is too dangerous for his staff to work late.","t":"A：為什麼轉角那家便利商店十點就關門，不再整夜營業了？ B：上週那裡發生了一起【搶劫】案，兩名男子拿走了收銀機裡所有的錢，所以老闆覺得讓員工上晚班太危險了。"},{"w":"burglary","p":"n.","d":"the crime of entering a building to steal things","c":"入室竊盜","s":"A: Why are you calling the insurance company during your lunch break today? B: Someone broke into our apartment while we were on vacation in Japan, and I need to report the burglary so that they can pay for the stolen television, the jewelry and my husband's camera.","t":"A：你今天午休時間為什麼在打電話給保險公司？ B：我們去日本度假時有人闖入我們的公寓，我需要通報這起【入室竊盜】案，讓他們理賠被偷的電視、珠寶和我先生的相機。"},{"w":"fraud","p":"n.","d":"the crime of tricking people to get money","c":"詐欺","s":"A: Why did the accounting department call a meeting with the bank this morning? B: They noticed that several payments had been sent to a supplier that does not exist, and they believe someone inside the company may be committing fraud to steal money from our accounts.","t":"A：會計部今天早上為什麼和銀行開會？ B：他們發現有幾筆款項被匯給一家根本不存在的供應商，他們認為公司內部可能有人在進行【詐欺】，從我們的帳戶偷錢。"},{"w":"assault","p":"n.","d":"a physical attack on a person","c":"襲擊；人身攻擊","s":"A: Why has the shopping mall added more security guards near the parking area at night? B: Last month there was an assault on a cleaner who was walking to her car after her shift, and although she was not badly hurt, the managers want every worker to feel safe.","t":"A：為什麼購物中心晚上在停車區附近增加了更多保全？ B：上個月有一名清潔人員下班走去開車時遭到【襲擊】，雖然她沒有受重傷，但經理們希望每位員工都能感到安全。"},{"w":"violence","p":"n.","d":"actions that use force to hurt people","c":"暴力","s":"A: Why did the city council decide to put more lights and cameras in the old park near the train station? B: Residents complained about fights late at night, and the council hopes that better lighting will reduce violence and make families feel comfortable using the park again.","t":"A：為什麼市議會決定在火車站附近的老公園裝設更多路燈和監視器？ B：居民抱怨深夜常有人打架，議會希望更好的照明能減少【暴力】事件，讓家庭再次安心使用公園。"},{"w":"victim","p":"n.","d":"a person who is hurt or cheated by a crime","c":"受害者","s":"A: Why is the bank sending emails to customers about fake phone calls this week? B: An elderly customer became the victim of a scam last Friday when someone pretending to be a bank officer asked for her password, and she lost almost all of her savings.","t":"A：銀行這週為什麼寄電子郵件提醒客戶注意假冒電話？ B：上週五一位年長客戶成了詐騙的【受害者】，有人假裝是銀行行員向她要密碼，她幾乎失去了所有積蓄。"},{"w":"suspect","p":"n.","d":"a person who the police think may have done a crime","c":"嫌疑犯","s":"A: Have the police found out who took the money from the safe in the hotel office? B: Not yet, but they showed the manager a video from the lobby camera, and the main suspect is a man who checked in under a false name and left early the next morning.","t":"A：警方查出是誰從飯店辦公室的保險箱拿走錢了嗎？ B：還沒有，不過他們給經理看了大廳監視器的影片，主要【嫌疑犯】是一名用假名入住、隔天一早就離開的男子。"},{"w":"evidence","p":"n.","d":"facts or objects that show something is true","c":"證據","s":"A: Why did the store manager save all the security videos from last weekend on a separate hard drive? B: The police asked her to keep them as evidence, because one of the cameras clearly shows the person who broke the front window and took several expensive watches.","t":"A：店長為什麼把上週末所有的監視器影片存在另一個硬碟裡？ B：警方請她把影片留作【證據】，因為其中一台攝影機清楚拍到打破前窗、拿走好幾支名錶的人。"},{"w":"arrest","p":"v.","d":"(of the police) to take someone away because they may have broken the law","c":"逮捕","s":"A: Did you read the news about the man who was stealing packages from doorsteps in our neighborhood? B: Yes, the police were able to arrest him yesterday afternoon because a neighbor's doorbell camera recorded his face and the number plate of the van he was driving.","t":"A：你看到我們社區有個男子偷門口包裹的新聞了嗎？ B：看到了，警方昨天下午得以【逮捕】他，因為一位鄰居的門鈴攝影機拍到了他的臉和他開的廂型車車牌。"},{"w":"trial","p":"n.","d":"a meeting in a court to decide if someone is guilty","c":"審判","s":"A: Why will the finance director be away from the office for most of next week? B: She has to give evidence at the trial of a former employee who is accused of stealing company money, and the lawyers expect it to last at least four days.","t":"A：財務長為什麼下週大部分時間不在辦公室？ B：她必須在一名前員工的【審判】中出庭作證，那人被控盜用公司資金，律師預計至少會持續四天。"},{"w":"court","p":"n.","d":"the place where legal cases are decided","c":"法院；法庭","s":"A: Why is the landlord of our office building not answering our emails about the broken elevator? B: We stopped paying rent until it is repaired, so now he is taking us to court, and our company lawyer is preparing documents to show that the building is unsafe.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓的房東為什麼都不回覆我們關於電梯故障的電子郵件？ B：我們在電梯修好前停付房租，所以他現在要把我們告上【法院】，我們公司的律師正在準備文件，證明大樓不安全。"},{"w":"judge","p":"n.","d":"the person who controls a court and decides punishments","c":"法官","s":"A: How did the case between our company and the former supplier end yesterday? B: After listening to both sides for three hours, the judge decided that the supplier had broken the contract, so they must pay us back for the damaged goods and the delivery costs.","t":"A：我們公司和前供應商的官司昨天結果如何？ B：聽完雙方三個小時的陳述後，【法官】判定供應商違約，所以他們必須賠償我們受損的貨物和運費。"},{"w":"jury","p":"n.","d":"a group of ordinary people who decide in court if someone is guilty","c":"陪審團","s":"A: Why did your manager let you take two weeks off in the middle of the busy season? B: I was chosen to serve on a jury for a big fraud case, and in this country every company must give workers paid time off when the court calls them.","t":"A：為什麼你的主管讓你在旺季中間請兩週假？ B：我被選為一宗大型詐欺案的【陪審團】成員，在這個國家，法院傳喚時每家公司都必須給員工帶薪假。"},{"w":"sentence","p":"n.","d":"the punishment a judge gives to a criminal","c":"判決；刑罰","s":"A: What happened to the former manager who took money from the charity's bank account? B: The judge gave him a sentence of three years in prison, and he must also pay back all the money that he stole from the organization over the past five years.","t":"A：那位從慈善機構銀行帳戶挪用款項的前經理後來怎麼了？ B：法官判他三年徒刑的【刑罰】，他還必須歸還過去五年從該機構偷走的所有錢。"},{"w":"prison","p":"n.","d":"a building where criminals are kept as punishment","c":"監獄","s":"A: Why is the company giving a job to someone who was in trouble with the law years ago? B: He spent two years in prison when he was young, but since then he has studied hard, earned a business degree, and every manager who has worked with him says he is reliable.","t":"A：公司為什麼要給一個多年前犯過法的人工作機會？ B：他年輕時在【監獄】待過兩年，但從那之後他努力讀書，拿到了商學學位，每位和他共事過的主管都說他很可靠。"},{"w":"jail","p":"n.","d":"a place where people are kept by the police, often for a short time","c":"拘留所；監獄","s":"A: Why didn't the delivery driver arrive for his shift on Saturday morning? B: He spent the night in jail after the police stopped him for driving too fast without a license, and his brother had to pay money before he could go home on Sunday.","t":"A：那位送貨司機星期六早上為什麼沒來上班？ B：他因為無照超速被警察攔下，在【拘留所】待了一晚，他哥哥得先付錢，他星期天才能回家。"},{"w":"fine","p":"n.","d":"money you must pay as a punishment","c":"罰款","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner look so upset after the city inspector left this afternoon? B: The inspector found that the kitchen did not meet the new safety rules, so the owner has to pay a fine of two thousand dollars and fix the problems within one month.","t":"A：市府稽查員今天下午離開後，餐廳老闆為什麼看起來那麼沮喪？ B：稽查員發現廚房不符合新的安全規定，所以老闆必須繳交兩千元的【罰款】，並在一個月內改善問題。"},{"w":"illegal","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by law","c":"違法的","s":"A: Why did the manager tell everyone to delete the music software from their office computers? B: The IT team discovered that it was an illegal copy downloaded from the internet, and the company could face serious legal problems if the software maker found out about it.","t":"A：經理為什麼要大家刪除辦公室電腦裡的音樂軟體？ B：資訊團隊發現那是從網路下載的【違法】拷貝，如果軟體公司發現，公司可能會面臨嚴重的法律問題。"},{"w":"law","p":"n.","d":"a rule made by the government that everyone must follow","c":"法律","s":"A: Why are all the employees taking an online course about customer information this month? B: A new law says that companies must protect people's personal data carefully, and if we make a mistake, the government can charge us a very large amount of money.","t":"A：為什麼所有員工這個月都在上關於客戶資料的線上課程？ B：一項新【法律】規定企業必須謹慎保護個人資料，如果我們出錯，政府可以向我們收取非常高額的罰金。"},{"w":"police","p":"n.","d":"the people whose job is to stop crime and keep people safe","c":"警察","s":"A: What should I do if I see someone trying to open the back door of the warehouse late at night? B: Don't try to stop the person yourself; call the police right away, then phone the security manager and wait in a safe place until help arrives.","t":"A：如果我深夜看到有人想打開倉庫後門，我該怎麼辦？ B：不要自己試圖阻止對方；立刻打電話給【警察】，再打給保全經理，然後在安全的地方等待支援到來。"},{"w":"detective","p":"n.","d":"a police officer whose job is to find out who did a crime","c":"偵探；刑警","s":"A: Who was the woman asking questions at the front desk this morning? B: She is a detective from the city police, and she is trying to find out who has been stealing guests' wallets from the hotel gym, so she wants to see our list of visitors.","t":"A：今天早上在櫃台問問題的那位女士是誰？ B：她是市警局的【刑警】，正在調查是誰一直在飯店健身房偷房客的皮夾，所以她想看我們的訪客名單。"},{"w":"witness","p":"n.","d":"a person who sees a crime or accident happen","c":"目擊者；證人","s":"A: Why does the security manager want to talk to you before you go home tonight? B: I was the only witness when a man took a laptop bag from the reception area this afternoon, so she needs me to describe what he looked like and which way he went.","t":"A：為什麼保全經理要你今晚回家前找你談話？ B：今天下午有個男子從接待區拿走一個筆電包時，我是唯一的【目擊者】，所以她需要我描述他的長相和他往哪個方向走。"},{"w":"motive","p":"n.","d":"the reason why someone does something, especially a crime","c":"動機","s":"A: Why would an experienced accountant with a good salary steal money from the company? B: The investigators think his motive was a large gambling debt, because they found that he had borrowed money from several people and could not pay any of it back.","t":"A：一位薪水不錯、經驗豐富的會計師為什麼會偷公司的錢？ B：調查人員認為他的【動機】是一大筆賭債，因為他們發現他向好幾個人借錢，卻一毛都還不出來。"},{"w":"alibi","p":"n.","d":"proof that you were somewhere else when a crime happened","c":"不在場證明","s":"A: Did the police think the night guard was involved in the warehouse theft last weekend? B: At first they did, but he had a strong alibi, because the hospital records show he was in the emergency room with his son from ten at night until six the next morning.","t":"A：警方認為上週末倉庫竊案和夜班警衛有關嗎？ B：一開始是這樣認為，但他有很有力的【不在場證明】，因為醫院紀錄顯示他從晚上十點到隔天早上六點都和兒子在急診室。"},{"w":"guilty","p":"adj.","d":"having done a crime","c":"有罪的","s":"A: What was the result of the trial of the sales manager who sold fake products to customers? B: After two days of discussion, the jury found him guilty of cheating more than fifty buyers, and the judge will decide his punishment at the end of this month.","t":"A：那位賣假貨給客戶的業務經理，審判結果如何？ B：經過兩天討論，陪審團裁定他詐騙超過五十名買家【有罪】，法官將在本月底決定他的刑罰。"},{"w":"innocent","p":"adj.","d":"not having done a crime","c":"無辜的；清白的","s":"A: Why did the company apologize to the cashier who was accused of taking money from the register? B: The security video later proved that she was completely innocent, because it showed a customer reaching over the counter and taking the cash while she was helping someone else.","t":"A：公司為什麼向那位被指控從收銀機拿錢的收銀員道歉？ B：監視器影片後來證明她完全是【清白的】，因為影片顯示是一名顧客在她幫忙別人時從櫃台伸手拿走現金。"},{"w":"felony","p":"n.","d":"a serious crime","c":"重罪","s":"A: Why is the human resources department checking the background of every new driver so carefully? B: Under our insurance contract, we cannot hire anyone who has been found guilty of a felony, such as robbery or selling drugs, during the past ten years.","t":"A：人資部為什麼這麼仔細地審查每位新司機的背景？ B：根據我們的保險合約，我們不能雇用過去十年內曾被判犯下【重罪】的人，例如搶劫或販毒。"},{"w":"misdemeanor","p":"n.","d":"a crime that is not very serious","c":"輕罪","s":"A: Will the minor charge on our new driver's record from when he was a teenager stop us from hiring him? B: No, it was only a misdemeanor, which is a small offense, so it is not a serious problem, but the insurance company still wants a copy of his record before he starts next Monday.","t":"A：我們新司機紀錄上那條青少年時期的小罪名，會讓我們無法雇用他嗎？ B：不會，那只是一項【輕罪】，屬於小型違法行為，所以不是嚴重的問題，但保險公司仍希望在他下週一上班前拿到一份他的紀錄。"},{"w":"vandalism","p":"n.","d":"damaging public or private property on purpose","c":"蓄意破壞（公物）","s":"A: Why are the walls of the parking garage being painted again so soon after the last repair? B: Some teenagers sprayed paint all over them on Saturday night, and the building manager says this kind of vandalism has cost the company more than five thousand dollars this year.","t":"A：停車場的牆壁才剛修好不久，為什麼又在重新粉刷？ B：星期六晚上有幾個青少年在牆上到處噴漆，大樓經理說今年這種【蓄意破壞】已經讓公司花了五千多元。"},{"w":"smuggling","p":"n.","d":"taking goods into or out of a country secretly and against the law","c":"走私","s":"A: Why are the customs officers checking every container from that shipping company so slowly this month? B: They discovered that some workers were hiding expensive phones inside boxes of toys, so the government is trying to stop the smuggling before more goods enter the country without tax.","t":"A：海關人員這個月為什麼檢查那家船運公司的每個貨櫃都那麼慢？ B：他們發現有些員工把昂貴的手機藏在玩具箱裡，所以政府想在更多貨物逃稅入境之前阻止這種【走私】行為。"},{"w":"corruption","p":"n.","d":"dishonest behavior by people in power, such as taking secret money","c":"貪污；腐敗","s":"A: Why did the city cancel the contract for the new bridge just before construction began? B: Reporters found that an official had accepted secret payments from the building company, and the mayor promised that there would be no corruption in any public project during her time in office.","t":"A：市政府為什麼在新橋開工前取消了合約？ B：記者發現一名官員收受了營建公司的秘密款項，市長承諾在她任內任何公共工程都不會有【貪污】情事。"},{"w":"cybercrime","p":"n.","d":"crime done using computers or the internet","c":"網路犯罪","s":"A: Why does the IT department make us change our passwords every two months and take security training? B: The number of cybercrime cases is growing quickly, and last year hackers stole customer data from a company just like ours, so we need to protect our systems and train every employee carefully.","t":"A：資訊部為什麼要我們每兩個月更換密碼並接受資安訓練？ B：【網路犯罪】案件正在快速增加，去年駭客從一家和我們很像的公司竊取了客戶資料，所以我們需要保護系統並仔細訓練每位員工。"}]},{"unit":90,"theme":"Crop 農作物","cards":[{"w":"harvest","p":"n.","d":"the time or act of gathering crops from the fields","c":"收成；收割","s":"A: Why is the food company asking all its drivers to work extra hours in the countryside next month? B: The rice harvest starts in early October, so the trucks must collect the crops from local farms quickly and bring them to our factory before the rainy season begins.","t":"A：為什麼食品公司要求所有司機下個月在鄉下加班？ B：稻米的【收成】十月初開始，所以卡車必須盡快從當地農場收集作物，並在雨季開始前送到我們的工廠。"},{"w":"plant","p":"v.","d":"to put seeds or young plants in the ground so they grow","c":"種植","s":"A: What is the hotel going to do with the empty land behind the parking lot now that the old storage building has been removed? B: The manager wants to plant tomatoes, herbs and lettuce there, so the chefs can pick fresh ingredients every morning for the restaurant's breakfast menu.","t":"A：舊倉庫拆除後，飯店打算怎麼處理停車場後面的空地？ B：經理想在那裡【種植】番茄、香草和萵苣，這樣廚師每天早上都能為餐廳的早餐菜單採摘新鮮食材。"},{"w":"seed","p":"n.","d":"a small part of a plant from which a new plant grows","c":"種子","s":"A: Why did the garden center order so many packets from the supplier in Japan this spring? B: Customers have been asking for a special kind of pumpkin seed that grows well on small balconies, and we expect sales to be very strong before the planting season starts in April.","t":"A：園藝中心今年春天為什麼向日本供應商訂了這麼多包貨？ B：顧客一直在詢問一種適合在小陽台生長的特殊南瓜【種子】，我們預計在四月種植季開始前銷量會非常好。"},{"w":"soil","p":"n.","d":"the top layer of the earth in which plants grow","c":"土壤","s":"A: Why did the farm manager hire a scientist from the university before buying the new land near the river? B: She wanted someone to test the soil first, because if it contains too much salt or chemicals, the vegetables will not grow well and the company could lose a lot of money.","t":"A：農場經理為什麼在買下河邊那塊新地之前，先從大學請了一位科學家？ B：她想先請人檢測【土壤】，因為如果裡面含有太多鹽分或化學物質，蔬菜就長不好，公司可能會損失很多錢。"},{"w":"fertilizer","p":"n.","d":"a substance added to the ground to help plants grow","c":"肥料","s":"A: Why have our sales to farmers in the south increased so much during the last three months? B: Our new natural fertilizer, which is made from food waste collected from local restaurants, helps crops grow faster without harming the environment, so many farmers have switched from more expensive chemical products.","t":"A：為什麼過去三個月我們賣給南部農民的銷售量增加這麼多？ B：我們新的天然【肥料】是用從當地餐廳收集的廚餘製成的，能幫助作物長得更快又不傷害環境，所以許多農民已經從較貴的化學產品改用它。"},{"w":"irrigation","p":"n.","d":"supplying water to land or crops through pipes or channels","c":"灌溉","s":"A: How did the farm manage to keep growing vegetables last summer when it hardly rained for two months? B: The owners had installed a modern irrigation system the year before, which sends water through underground pipes directly to the roots, so they used less water and still had a good harvest.","t":"A：去年夏天兩個月幾乎沒下雨，那座農場怎麼還能持續種蔬菜？ B：農場主人前一年就安裝了現代化的【灌溉】系統，透過地下管線把水直接送到根部，所以他們用水更少，仍然有很好的收成。"},{"w":"pesticide","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used to kill insects that damage crops","c":"殺蟲劑；農藥","s":"A: Why did the supermarket remove all the strawberries from that supplier from its shelves this week? B: A government test found that the fruit contained too much pesticide, which farmers had sprayed to kill insects, so the company decided to stop selling them until the supplier passes a new safety inspection.","t":"A：超市這週為什麼把那家供應商的草莓全部下架？ B：政府檢驗發現那些水果含有過多的【農藥】，是農民為了殺蟲而噴灑的，所以公司決定在供應商通過新的安全檢查之前暫停販售。"},{"w":"herbicide","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used to kill unwanted plants","c":"除草劑","s":"A: Why are the gardeners at the business park pulling out the unwanted plants by hand instead of using machines? B: The management decided to stop using herbicide on the lawns last year, because many employees eat lunch on the grass and were worried that the chemicals might be bad for their health.","t":"A：商業園區的園丁為什麼用手拔除不要的植物，而不是用機器？ B：管理部門去年決定停止在草坪上使用【除草劑】，因為許多員工在草地上吃午餐，擔心那些化學物質可能對健康有害。"},{"w":"weed","p":"n.","d":"a wild plant that grows where it is not wanted","c":"雜草","s":"A: Why does the vegetable garden on the roof of our office building look so messy these days? B: The volunteer who usually takes care of it has been on vacation for three weeks, so every weed has grown tall between the tomatoes, and nobody else in the office has had time to pull them out.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓屋頂上的菜園最近為什麼看起來這麼凌亂？ B：平常照顧它的志工已經休假三週了，所以每一株【雜草】都在番茄之間長得很高，辦公室裡其他人都沒有時間把它們拔掉。"},{"w":"yield","p":"n.","d":"the amount of crops that a piece of land produces","c":"產量","s":"A: Why is the farming company planning to buy new machines and hire more workers for its fields next year? B: Last year the yield per hectare was twenty percent higher than expected thanks to better seeds and careful watering, so the company wants to grow more corn and sell it overseas.","t":"A：那家農業公司為什麼計畫明年替田地購買新機器並雇用更多工人？ B：去年因為種子更好、澆水更仔細，每公頃的【產量】比預期高出百分之二十，所以公司想種更多玉米並賣到海外。"},{"w":"farmland","p":"n.","d":"land that is used for farming","c":"農地","s":"A: Why are so many local residents attending the city council meeting about the new shopping mall tonight? B: The developer wants to build it on a large area of farmland outside town, and many people are worried that we will lose the fields where farmers have grown rice for more than a hundred years.","t":"A：為什麼今晚有那麼多當地居民參加關於新購物中心的市議會會議？ B：開發商想把它蓋在城外一大片【農地】上，許多人擔心我們會失去農民種植稻米超過一百年的田地。"},{"w":"field","p":"n.","d":"an area of land used for growing crops","c":"田地","s":"A: Where are the new interns going to spend their first week, since the main office is being painted? B: They will join our team in the countryside and visit a large corn field owned by one of our suppliers, so they can see how the raw materials for our snacks are grown and collected.","t":"A：主辦公室正在油漆，新實習生第一週要去哪裡？ B：他們會跟我們團隊一起去鄉下，參觀一家供應商擁有的一大片玉米【田】，讓他們了解我們零食的原料是如何種植和採收的。"},{"w":"plow","p":"v.","d":"to turn over the soil with a machine or tool before planting","c":"犁（田）；耕地","s":"A: Why did the farm rent two large tractors from the equipment company at the end of February? B: The workers need to plow all the fields before the spring planting begins, and the old machines broke down last year, so the manager wanted to make sure the job would be finished on time.","t":"A：農場為什麼在二月底向設備公司租了兩台大型拖拉機？ B：工人們必須在春季播種開始前【犁】完所有田地，而舊機器去年壞了，所以經理想確保工作能準時完成。"},{"w":"sow","p":"v.","d":"to put seeds in the ground so that they grow","c":"播種","s":"A: When should our garden center start advertising the new flower collection to customers in the north? B: Most people in that area sow their flower seeds in late March, after the cold weather ends, so we should send out the online advertisements and email discounts by the beginning of the month.","t":"A：我們園藝中心應該什麼時候開始向北部顧客宣傳新的花卉系列？ B：那一帶大多數人在三月下旬寒冷天氣結束後【播】下花卉種子，所以我們應該在月初前發出網路廣告和電子郵件折扣。"},{"w":"sprout","p":"v.","d":"to begin to grow and produce new leaves","c":"發芽","s":"A: How long will it take before the children in our company's weekend gardening class can see their beans growing? B: If they water the pots every day and keep them in a warm, sunny place, the beans should sprout in about five days, and the children can measure the little plants each week.","t":"A：我們公司週末園藝課的孩子們要多久才能看到他們種的豆子長出來？ B：如果他們每天替花盆澆水，並放在溫暖、陽光充足的地方，豆子大約五天就會【發芽】，孩子們可以每週測量小植物的高度。"},{"w":"ripen","p":"v.","d":"to become ready to be picked or eaten","c":"成熟","s":"A: Why does the fruit company pick its bananas while they are still green instead of waiting? B: The trip to Europe by ship takes about three weeks, so the bananas slowly ripen during the journey and arrive yellow and ready to eat when they reach the supermarkets in Germany and France.","t":"A：那家水果公司為什麼在香蕉還是綠色時就採收，而不是等待？ B：坐船到歐洲大約需要三週，所以香蕉在運送途中慢慢【成熟】，到達德國和法國的超市時已經變黃可以吃了。"},{"w":"grain","p":"n.","d":"the seeds of plants such as wheat and rice used as food","c":"穀物","s":"A: Why did the price of bread at our bakery chain go up again at the beginning of this month? B: Bad weather in several countries reduced the amount of grain that farmers could produce, so the cost of flour increased by almost fifteen percent, and we had to raise our prices to cover it.","t":"A：我們連鎖麵包店的麵包價格為什麼這個月初又漲了？ B：幾個國家的惡劣天氣減少了農民能生產的【穀物】數量，所以麵粉成本上漲了將近百分之十五，我們只好提高價格來因應。"},{"w":"wheat","p":"n.","d":"a plant whose grain is used to make flour and bread","c":"小麥","s":"A: Where does the company get the flour for its popular noodles that are sold in convenience stores across Asia? B: We buy high-quality wheat from farmers in Australia and Canada, and then our factory in Taichung turns it into flour, which is mixed with water and salt to make the noodles every day.","t":"A：公司那款在亞洲便利商店熱賣的麵條，麵粉是從哪裡來的？ B：我們向澳洲和加拿大的農民購買高品質的【小麥】，然後由台中工廠磨成麵粉，每天和水、鹽混合製成麵條。"},{"w":"corn","p":"n.","d":"a tall plant with yellow seeds that grow on a cob","c":"玉米","s":"A: What new snack is the marketing team planning to introduce at the food fair in Taipei next month? B: They are going to sell sweet corn soup and grilled cobs with butter, because the recipe uses fresh crops from local farmers, and visitors at last year's fair loved healthy snacks.","t":"A：行銷團隊打算在下個月台北的食品展推出什麼新點心？ B：他們要賣甜【玉米】濃湯和奶油烤玉米棒，因為食譜使用當地農民的新鮮作物，而去年展覽的訪客很喜歡健康點心。"},{"w":"rice","p":"n.","d":"small white or brown grains eaten as a main food in Asia","c":"稻米；米飯","s":"A: Why did the restaurant chain decide to sign a long contract with the farmers' group in Hualien? B: The farmers there grow excellent rice without chemicals, and the agreement means we will get a steady supply for our lunch boxes at a fixed cost for the next five years, even if the market changes.","t":"A：那家連鎖餐廳為什麼決定和花蓮的農民團體簽長期合約？ B：那裡的農民不用化學物質種出優質的【稻米】，這份協議表示未來五年即使市場變動，我們的便當也能以固定成本獲得穩定供應。"},{"w":"barley","p":"n.","d":"a grain used for food, drinks and animal feed","c":"大麥","s":"A: What is the main ingredient in the new drink that our beverage company will launch in convenience stores this summer? B: It is made from roasted barley, which gives it a light, nutty flavor, and our research shows that many office workers want a healthy drink with no sugar and no caffeine.","t":"A：我們飲料公司今年夏天要在便利商店推出的新飲料，主要成分是什麼？ B：它是用烘焙過的【大麥】製成，帶有淡淡的堅果風味，我們的研究顯示許多上班族想要無糖、無咖啡因的健康飲料。"},{"w":"oats","p":"n.","d":"a grain often cooked with milk or water for breakfast","c":"燕麥","s":"A: Why has the hotel added a new section to its breakfast buffet next to the fresh fruit and yogurt? B: Many business guests asked for a healthier option, so the kitchen now cooks warm oats with milk and honey every morning, and guests can add nuts, berries or cinnamon on top.","t":"A：飯店為什麼在早餐自助餐的新鮮水果和優格旁邊新增了一區？ B：許多商務客人要求更健康的選擇，所以廚房現在每天早上用牛奶和蜂蜜煮溫熱的【燕麥】，客人可以在上面加堅果、莓果或肉桂。"},{"w":"soybean","p":"n.","d":"a bean used to make tofu, soy milk and oil","c":"黃豆；大豆","s":"A: Why is the food factory in Tainan building a new production line next to the tofu section? B: Demand for plant-based milk has grown quickly, so the company will use the same soybean supply from its partner farms to make soy milk and sell it to coffee shops around the island.","t":"A：台南的食品工廠為什麼在豆腐區旁邊建新的生產線？ B：植物奶的需求成長很快，所以公司會用合作農場相同的【黃豆】供應來製作豆漿，並賣給全島的咖啡店。"},{"w":"vegetable","p":"n.","d":"a plant or part of a plant eaten as food, such as carrots or spinach","c":"蔬菜","s":"A: Why did the company cafeteria change its lunch menu after the health survey last month? B: The survey showed that many employees were not eating enough fresh food, so now every meal comes with at least one green vegetable, such as spinach or broccoli, and the price has not changed.","t":"A：員工餐廳上個月健康調查後為什麼改變了午餐菜單？ B：調查顯示許多員工沒吃到足夠的新鮮食物，所以現在每份餐點都至少附一種綠色【蔬菜】，例如菠菜或花椰菜，而且價格沒有改變。"},{"w":"fruit","p":"n.","d":"the sweet part of a plant that contains seeds, such as apples","c":"水果","s":"A: What gifts is the sales team going to send to our most important customers before the Lunar New Year holiday? B: We ordered beautiful boxes of seasonal fruit, such as oranges and apples from local orchards, because they are healthy, look attractive and represent good luck in Taiwanese culture.","t":"A：業務團隊在農曆新年假期前要送什麼禮物給最重要的客戶？ B：我們訂了精美的當季【水果】禮盒，例如當地果園的柳丁和蘋果，因為它們健康、外觀漂亮，而且在台灣文化中象徵好運。"},{"w":"orchard","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land where fruit trees are grown","c":"果園","s":"A: Where is the company holding its family day this year, since the beach resort is fully booked? B: We rented an apple orchard in the mountains near Taichung, where employees and their children can pick fruit from the trees, enjoy a picnic lunch and join a short tour about how the farm works.","t":"A：海灘度假村客滿了，公司今年的家庭日要在哪裡舉辦？ B：我們租了台中附近山區的一座蘋果【園】，員工和孩子可以從樹上摘水果、享用野餐午餐，並參加一個介紹農場運作的簡短導覽。"},{"w":"greenhouse","p":"n.","d":"a glass building where plants are grown in warm conditions","c":"溫室","s":"A: How can the farm sell fresh strawberries to hotels even during the cold winter months? B: They grow them inside a large greenhouse made of glass, where the temperature and light are controlled by computers, so the plants stay warm and produce sweet fruit all year round.","t":"A：那座農場怎麼能在寒冷的冬季也賣新鮮草莓給飯店？ B：他們在一座玻璃製的大型【溫室】裡種植，溫度和光線都由電腦控制，所以植物保持溫暖，一年四季都能結出甜美的果實。"},{"w":"drought","p":"n.","d":"a long period of time with little or no rain","c":"乾旱","s":"A: Why did the coffee company warn its customers that prices might rise later this year? B: A long drought in Brazil has lasted almost six months, and without rain many coffee plants have died, so the supply of beans will be much smaller and the cost of buying them will go up.","t":"A：咖啡公司為什麼警告顧客今年稍晚價格可能上漲？ B：巴西一場長期的【乾旱】已經持續將近六個月，沒有雨水，許多咖啡樹都死了，所以咖啡豆供應會少很多，購買成本也會上升。"},{"w":"flood","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of water covering land that is usually dry","c":"洪水；水災","s":"A: Why were the deliveries of fresh vegetables to our restaurants so late and so small last week? B: Heavy rain caused a serious flood in the farming area along the river, and many fields were under water for days, so the farmers could not harvest their crops or reach the main roads.","t":"A：上週送到我們餐廳的新鮮蔬菜為什麼這麼晚又這麼少？ B：大雨在沿河的農業區造成嚴重【水災】，許多田地被水淹了好幾天，所以農民無法收成作物，也無法到達主要道路。"},{"w":"climate","p":"n.","d":"the usual weather conditions in a place","c":"氣候","s":"A: Why did the tea company decide to open a new farm in the mountains instead of near the coast? B: The cool, wet climate at high altitudes is perfect for growing tea leaves with a rich flavor, and the experts believe the plants there will produce better quality tea than our older farm.","t":"A：茶葉公司為什麼決定在山區而不是海邊開新的茶園？ B：高海拔涼爽潮濕的【氣候】非常適合種出風味濃郁的茶葉，專家認為那裡的茶樹會比我們舊茶園產出品質更好的茶。"},{"w":"organic","p":"adj.","d":"grown without artificial chemicals","c":"有機的","s":"A: Why is the new supermarket near our office always so busy on weekday evenings? B: It sells organic vegetables and fruit grown without any chemicals, and many young office workers are willing to pay a little more because they believe this kind of food is healthier for their families.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近的新超市為什麼平日晚上總是那麼忙？ B：它販售不使用任何化學物質種植的【有機】蔬菜和水果，許多年輕上班族願意多付一點錢，因為他們相信這類食物對家人更健康。"},{"w":"rotation","p":"n.","d":"changing the crops grown in a field from season to season","c":"輪作；輪換","s":"A: How does the farm keep its soil healthy without using a lot of expensive chemicals every year? B: The manager follows a careful crop rotation plan, so the same field grows rice one year, beans the next year and vegetables the year after that, which helps the land stay rich and productive.","t":"A：那座農場如何在不每年使用大量昂貴化學物質的情況下保持土壤健康？ B：經理遵循仔細的作物【輪作】計畫，同一塊田第一年種稻米、第二年種豆類、第三年種蔬菜，這樣有助於土地保持肥沃和高產。"},{"w":"agriculture","p":"n.","d":"the work of farming and growing crops","c":"農業","s":"A: Why is the bank offering special low-interest loans to young people in the countryside this year? B: The government wants to support agriculture, because many farmers are getting old and few young people want to grow crops, so the loans help new farmers buy land, machines and seeds.","t":"A：銀行今年為什麼提供特別的低利貸款給鄉下的年輕人？ B：政府想要扶持【農業】，因為許多農民年紀漸長，很少年輕人願意種植作物，所以這些貸款幫助新農民購買土地、機器和種子。"},{"w":"cultivate","p":"v.","d":"to prepare land and grow crops on it","c":"耕種；栽培","s":"A: What will the company do with the large piece of land it bought near the lake last autumn? B: We plan to cultivate herbs and flowers there for our natural skin care products, and we will hire local workers to look after the plants and collect them by hand during the busy summer season.","t":"A：公司去年秋天在湖邊買的那一大片土地要做什麼用？ B：我們打算在那裡【栽種】香草和花卉，用於我們的天然保養品，並雇用當地工人照顧植物，在忙碌的夏季用手採收。"}]},{"unit":91,"theme":"Crowded Place 擁擠的地方","cards":[{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: Why did you leave the company's year-end party so early last Friday, when everyone else stayed until midnight? B: The restaurant was so crowded that I could hardly move between the tables, and I also had to catch the last bus home because my car was at the repair shop.","t":"A：上週五公司尾牙，大家都待到午夜，你為什麼那麼早離開？ B：餐廳太【擁擠】了，我幾乎無法在桌子之間走動，而且我的車在修車廠，所以我還得趕最後一班公車回家。"},{"w":"packed","p":"adj.","d":"completely full of people","c":"擠滿人的；爆滿的","s":"A: Did you manage to find a seat at the product launch in the hotel ballroom yesterday afternoon? B: No, the room was packed with reporters, buyers and fans of the brand, so I stood near the back door for two hours and took notes on my phone instead.","t":"A：你昨天下午在飯店宴會廳的產品發表會有找到座位嗎？ B：沒有，會場【擠滿】了記者、採購和品牌粉絲，所以我在後門附近站了兩個小時，改用手機做筆記。"},{"w":"busy","p":"adj.","d":"full of people or activity","c":"繁忙的；熱鬧的","s":"A: Should we hold the client lunch at the café across from the train station or somewhere quieter? B: That café is always very busy at noon because office workers from the nearby towers go there, so I think the hotel restaurant would be better for a serious business talk.","t":"A：我們要在火車站對面的咖啡廳還是比較安靜的地方請客戶吃午餐？ B：那家咖啡廳中午總是非常【繁忙】，因為附近大樓的上班族都去那裡，所以我覺得飯店餐廳比較適合談正式的生意。"},{"w":"jammed","p":"adj.","d":"so full that people or cars cannot move","c":"擠得水洩不通的；塞滿的","s":"A: Why didn't the delivery van arrive at the warehouse by ten o'clock as the driver promised this morning? B: The roads near the stadium were completely jammed with cars because of the football final, so the driver waited in the same spot for almost an hour before he could turn around.","t":"A：送貨車為什麼沒有像司機今天早上答應的那樣在十點前抵達倉庫？ B：因為足球決賽，體育場附近的道路完全被車子【擠得水洩不通】，司機在同一個地方等了將近一個小時才能掉頭。"},{"w":"congested","p":"adj.","d":"too full of traffic or people","c":"壅塞的；擁擠的","s":"A: Why is the city planning to build a new subway line to the industrial park in the north? B: The main highway to the park is heavily congested every morning and evening, so workers waste a lot of time in their cars, and many companies say they are losing good employees because of it.","t":"A：市政府為什麼計畫興建一條通往北部工業區的新捷運線？ B：通往工業區的主要公路每天早晚都嚴重【壅塞】，工人在車上浪費很多時間，許多公司說他們因此流失了優秀的員工。"},{"w":"overcrowded","p":"adj.","d":"having too many people inside","c":"過度擁擠的","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to rent a second floor in the building next door for the design team? B: Our office became overcrowded after we hired twenty new staff this year, and people were sharing desks and fighting over meeting rooms, so it was hard for anyone to work properly.","t":"A：經理為什麼決定在隔壁大樓多租一層樓給設計團隊？ B：我們今年雇用了二十名新員工後，辦公室變得【過度擁擠】，大家共用桌子、搶會議室，所以任何人都很難好好工作。"},{"w":"bustling","p":"adj.","d":"full of busy, noisy activity","c":"熙熙攘攘的；熱鬧的","s":"A: What did the visiting buyers from Germany enjoy most during their business trip to Taipei last week? B: They loved walking through the bustling night market near their hotel, where hundreds of people were buying snacks and clothes, and they said it was much more exciting than the quiet streets at home.","t":"A：上週來台北出差的德國買家最喜歡什麼？ B：他們很喜歡逛飯店附近【熙熙攘攘】的夜市，那裡有好幾百人在買小吃和衣服，他們說那比家鄉安靜的街道刺激多了。"},{"w":"lively","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and activity","c":"熱鬧的；充滿活力的","s":"A: Which area would you recommend for our team dinner after the sales conference on Thursday evening? B: I'd suggest the old harbor district, because it has a lively atmosphere with street musicians and outdoor restaurants, and the staff will enjoy relaxing there after three long days of meetings.","t":"A：週四晚上業務大會結束後，你推薦哪個區域讓我們團隊聚餐？ B：我建議舊港區，因為那裡有街頭音樂家和露天餐廳，氣氛很【熱鬧】，員工開了三天的長會後會很喜歡在那裡放鬆。"},{"w":"noisy","p":"adj.","d":"making a lot of loud sound","c":"吵鬧的","s":"A: Why did you ask the hotel to move you to a different room on your first night in Bangkok? B: My first room faced a noisy street full of motorbikes, buses and food stalls, and I couldn't sleep at all, so I was worried I would be too tired for my meeting the next morning.","t":"A：你在曼谷第一晚為什麼要求飯店幫你換房間？ B：我第一間房間面對一條擠滿機車、公車和小吃攤的【吵鬧】街道，我完全睡不著，所以很擔心隔天早上開會時會太累。"},{"w":"queue","p":"n.","d":"a line of people waiting for something","c":"排隊的隊伍；行列","s":"A: How long did it take you to get through passport control at the airport after your flight from Seoul? B: There was a long queue of tourists at every counter because three international flights landed at the same time, so I waited almost forty minutes before an officer checked my documents.","t":"A：你從首爾搭機抵達後，在機場通過護照查驗花了多久？ B：因為三班國際航班同時降落，每個櫃台前都有遊客排成長長的【隊伍】，所以我等了將近四十分鐘，才有官員檢查我的證件。"},{"w":"crowd","p":"n.","d":"a large group of people in one place","c":"人群；群眾","s":"A: Why did the store open its doors thirty minutes earlier than usual on the first day of the holiday sale? B: A huge crowd of shoppers was already waiting outside at seven o'clock, so the manager opened early to keep people safe and to stop the line from blocking the main road.","t":"A：假日特賣第一天，那家店為什麼比平常提早三十分鐘開門？ B：七點時外面已經有大批購物【人群】在等候，所以經理提早開門以確保民眾安全，也避免隊伍擋住大馬路。"},{"w":"throng","p":"n.","d":"a very large crowd of people","c":"一大群人；人潮","s":"A: Was it difficult to reach the company's booth at the international travel fair in the convention center? B: Yes, a throng of visitors filled the main hall all afternoon, so our sales staff had to guide clients through a side entrance near the loading area to reach our stand.","t":"A：要到國際旅展會場中的公司攤位困難嗎？ B：是的，整個下午大批【人潮】擠滿主展廳，所以我們的業務人員只好帶客戶從靠近卸貨區的側門進來到我們的攤位。"},{"w":"rush","p":"n.","d":"a time when many people hurry to do the same thing","c":"(人潮的)湧入；匆忙","s":"A: Why does the coffee shop on the ground floor hire two extra baristas every weekday morning? B: There is a big rush of office workers between eight and nine o'clock, when everyone wants a drink before work, and the owner doesn't want customers to wait too long and leave.","t":"A：一樓的咖啡店為什麼每個平日早上都多請兩名咖啡師？ B：八點到九點之間會有大批上班族【湧入】，大家都想在上班前買杯飲料，老闆不希望客人等太久而離開。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars and other vehicles moving on a road","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: Why are you leaving the office so early to meet the client at the airport this afternoon? B: The traffic on the expressway is usually terrible on Friday afternoons, especially near the toll station, and I don't want our most important customer to wait alone in the arrival hall.","t":"A：你今天下午為什麼這麼早離開辦公室去機場接客戶？ B：週五下午快速道路上的【車流】通常很糟，尤其是收費站附近，我不想讓我們最重要的客戶獨自在入境大廳等待。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work","c":"通勤","s":"A: How does your new assistant get to the office now that she has moved to a town outside the city? B: She has to commute by train for about ninety minutes each way, so we agreed that she can work from home on Fridays to save time and energy.","t":"A：你的新助理搬到市區外的小鎮後，現在怎麼來上班？ B：她每趟要搭大約九十分鐘的火車【通勤】，所以我們同意她週五可以在家工作，以節省時間和體力。"},{"w":"shoulder","p":"v.","d":"to push through people using your shoulder","c":"用肩膀擠開；擠過","s":"A: How did the reporter get close enough to ask the CEO a question after the press conference ended? B: She had to shoulder her way through dozens of photographers who were standing in front of the stage, and she finally reached him just before he got into his car.","t":"A：記者會結束後，那位記者是怎麼靠近到能向執行長提問的？ B：她必須【用肩膀擠】過站在舞台前的幾十位攝影師，終於在他上車前一刻追上他。"},{"w":"squeeze","p":"v.","d":"to force yourself into a small space","c":"擠進；硬塞","s":"A: Were you able to take the elevator up to the meeting on the twentieth floor this morning? B: Yes, but I had to squeeze into a tiny space next to a delivery man with a large box, because everyone in the building was trying to get to work before nine o'clock.","t":"A：你今天早上有搭到電梯上二十樓開會嗎？ B：有，但我得【擠進】一個抱著大箱子的送貨員旁邊的小小空間，因為大樓裡每個人都想在九點前趕到公司。"},{"w":"jostle","p":"v.","d":"to push against other people in a crowd","c":"推擠","s":"A: Why did the museum decide to sell tickets online for the new exhibition with fixed entry times? B: On the opening weekend, visitors started to jostle each other in front of the famous paintings, and a few people almost fell, so the director wanted to control the number of guests.","t":"A：博物館為什麼決定新展覽改為網路售票並固定入場時間？ B：開幕週末時，參觀者在名畫前開始互相【推擠】，有幾個人差點跌倒，所以館長想控制參觀人數。"},{"w":"gather","p":"v.","d":"to come together in one place","c":"聚集","s":"A: Why are so many people standing outside the bank on Main Street this morning? B: Customers started to gather there before opening time because the bank is offering a special savings account with a high interest rate, but only to the first two hundred people.","t":"A：今天早上為什麼有那麼多人站在主街的銀行外面？ B：顧客在開門前就開始在那裡【聚集】，因為銀行推出一種高利率的特別儲蓄帳戶，但只限前兩百人。"},{"w":"assemble","p":"v.","d":"to meet together as a group for a purpose","c":"集合","s":"A: What should all employees do if the fire alarm goes off during the safety drill next Tuesday? B: Everyone must leave by the nearest stairs and assemble in the parking lot behind the building, where each team leader will count their staff and report to the security manager.","t":"A：如果下週二安全演練時火災警報響了，所有員工應該怎麼做？ B：每個人都必須從最近的樓梯離開，並到大樓後面的停車場【集合】，各組組長會在那裡清點人數並向保全經理回報。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special event with music, food or celebrations","c":"節慶；藝術節；音樂節","s":"A: Why are all the hotels in the city fully booked for the second weekend of next month? B: A famous music festival takes place in the riverside park that weekend, and thousands of fans from all over Asia are coming, so you should book your business trip for a different date.","t":"A：為什麼市內所有飯店下個月第二個週末都客滿了？ B：那個週末河濱公園會舉辦一場知名的音樂【節】，成千上萬來自亞洲各地的樂迷都會來，所以你應該把出差安排在其他日期。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"a place where people buy and sell goods","c":"市場","s":"A: Where does the restaurant buy such fresh fish and vegetables for its lunch menu every day? B: The chef goes to the local market at five o'clock every morning, before it gets too crowded, so he can choose the best products and talk directly with the farmers and fishermen.","t":"A：那家餐廳每天的午餐菜單哪來這麼新鮮的魚和蔬菜？ B：主廚每天早上五點，趁還沒太擁擠前就去當地【市場】，這樣他可以挑選最好的產品，並直接和農夫及漁夫交談。"},{"w":"station","p":"n.","d":"a place where trains or buses stop for passengers","c":"車站","s":"A: How can our visitors from Japan get to the factory from the airport tomorrow without a car? B: They can take the express train to the central station, and our driver will wait for them at the north exit with a sign showing the company name.","t":"A：我們的日本訪客明天沒有車，要怎麼從機場到工廠？ B：他們可以搭快車到中央【車站】，我們的司機會拿著寫有公司名稱的牌子在北出口等他們。"},{"w":"mall","p":"n.","d":"a large building with many shops and restaurants","c":"購物中心；商場","s":"A: Where is the company planning to open its first clothing store in Kaohsiung next spring? B: We signed a contract for a space on the second floor of a new shopping mall near the harbor, which attracts thousands of families and tourists every weekend.","t":"A：公司明年春天計畫在高雄哪裡開第一家服飾店？ B：我們簽約租下港口附近一間新【購物中心】二樓的店面，那裡每個週末都吸引成千上萬的家庭和觀光客。"},{"w":"venue","p":"n.","d":"the place where an event happens","c":"場地；會場","s":"A: Have you found a place for the company's annual awards dinner in December yet? B: Yes, we booked a venue by the lake that can hold three hundred guests, and it has a large stage, a good sound system and plenty of parking spaces for our staff and partners.","t":"A：你找到公司十二月年度頒獎晚宴的地點了嗎？ B：找到了，我們訂了湖邊一個可容納三百位賓客的【場地】，那裡有大舞台、很好的音響系統，還有很多停車位給我們的員工和合作夥伴。"},{"w":"capacity","p":"n.","d":"the largest number of people a place can hold","c":"容量；可容納人數","s":"A: Why did the organizers stop selling tickets for the technology seminar two weeks early? B: The hall has a capacity of only five hundred people because of fire safety rules, and all the seats were taken within a few days after the famous speaker was announced.","t":"A：主辦單位為什麼提早兩週停止販售科技研討會的門票？ B：因為消防安全規定，那個大廳的【可容納人數】只有五百人，而在宣布知名講者後幾天內所有座位就被訂光了。"},{"w":"density","p":"n.","d":"how many people or things are in an area","c":"密度","s":"A: Why does the company want to open its new branch in that part of the city instead of the suburbs? B: The population density there is very high, with many apartment buildings and office towers close together, so a small shop can reach thousands of potential customers every day.","t":"A：公司為什麼想在市內那個區域而不是郊區開設新分店？ B：那裡的人口【密度】非常高，許多公寓大樓和辦公大樓緊鄰在一起，所以一家小店每天就能接觸到成千上萬的潛在顧客。"},{"w":"public","p":"adj.","d":"open to or used by everyone","c":"公共的；公眾的","s":"A: How do most of your employees travel to the new office in the science park? B: Most of them use public transportation, such as the subway and city buses, because parking near the office is expensive, and the company gives everyone a monthly travel card as a benefit.","t":"A：你們大部分員工怎麼到科學園區的新辦公室？ B：他們大多搭乘【公共】交通工具，像是捷運和市公車，因為辦公室附近停車很貴，而且公司每個月都發給每個人一張交通卡作為福利。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a city or town","c":"都市的；城市的","s":"A: Why is the government giving money to companies that build small parks on top of office buildings? B: Many urban areas have very little green space because of crowded housing and busy roads, and the parks help keep buildings cool and give office workers a quiet place to relax.","t":"A：政府為什麼要補助在辦公大樓頂樓建造小公園的公司？ B：由於住宅擁擠、道路繁忙，許多【都市】地區的綠地很少，這些公園有助於讓建築物保持涼爽，也讓上班族有個安靜的地方放鬆。"},{"w":"downtown","p":"adv.","d":"to or in the center of a city","c":"往市中心；在市中心","s":"A: Are you driving to the client's office for the contract meeting this afternoon? B: No, I'll take the subway downtown because there's almost no parking near their building, and the streets around the financial district are always full of taxis and delivery vans at that time.","t":"A：你今天下午要開車去客戶辦公室開合約會議嗎？ B：不，我會搭捷運【到市中心】，因為他們大樓附近幾乎沒有停車位，而且那個時段金融區周圍的街道總是擠滿計程車和送貨車。"},{"w":"sidewalk","p":"n.","d":"a path for people to walk on next to a road","c":"人行道","s":"A: Why did the city fine the restaurant owner on Garden Road last week? B: He put too many tables and chairs on the sidewalk in front of his shop, so people walking by had to step into the road, which was dangerous because of the heavy traffic.","t":"A：市政府上週為什麼開罰花園路上的那位餐廳老闆？ B：他在店門前的【人行道】上擺了太多桌椅，路過的行人只好走到馬路上，因為車流量大，這樣很危險。"},{"w":"platform","p":"n.","d":"the area next to the tracks where people get on and off trains","c":"月台","s":"A: Where should I meet the new sales representative when she arrives from Taichung tomorrow morning? B: Please wait for her on platform three, where the high-speed train stops, because the station is very crowded at that hour and it will be hard to find each other in the main hall.","t":"A：新的業務代表明天早上從台中抵達時，我應該在哪裡跟她碰面？ B：請在高鐵停靠的第三【月台】等她，因為那個時段車站非常擁擠，在大廳裡很難找到彼此。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"a planned public or social occasion","c":"活動；盛事","s":"A: How many people came to the charity run that our company sponsored along the river on Sunday? B: More than three thousand runners took part in the event, and so many families came to watch that the organizers had to close two streets and add extra toilets near the finish line.","t":"A：我們公司週日在河邊贊助的慈善路跑有多少人參加？ B：超過三千名跑者參加了這場【活動】，而且來觀看的家庭非常多，主辦單位只好封閉兩條街並在終點線附近加設廁所。"},{"w":"parade","p":"n.","d":"a public celebration in which people march or ride through the streets","c":"遊行","s":"A: Why is the bus to the office taking a different route this Saturday morning? B: There's a big parade for the national holiday on the main avenue, with marching bands, dancers and colorful floats, so the city has closed several roads until two o'clock in the afternoon.","t":"A：這個週六早上到公司的公車為什麼要改走別的路線？ B：主要大道上有國慶日的大型【遊行】，有樂隊、舞者和色彩繽紛的花車，所以市政府封閉了幾條道路，直到下午兩點。"},{"w":"rush hour","p":"n.phr.","d":"the busiest time of day when people travel to or from work","c":"尖峰時段","s":"A: Why did you schedule the meeting with the suppliers at ten o'clock instead of eight thirty? B: If we meet any earlier, they'll be driving across the city during rush hour, when the roads are full of commuters, and they might arrive late and feel stressed before we even start.","t":"A：你為什麼把和供應商的會議排在十點，而不是八點半？ B：如果更早開會，他們得在【尖峰時段】開車穿越市區，那時道路上擠滿通勤者，他們可能會遲到，還沒開始開會就覺得很有壓力。"}]},{"unit":92,"theme":"Cultural Place 文化場所","cards":[{"w":"museum","p":"n.","d":"a building where people can see old, valuable or interesting objects","c":"博物館","s":"A: Where should we take the visiting engineers from Germany on Saturday afternoon after the factory tour ends? B: I think the science museum near the river would be perfect, because it has a large section on the history of machines, and the entrance is free for groups of ten or more.","t":"A：工廠參觀結束後，星期六下午我們該帶來訪的德國工程師去哪裡？ B：我覺得河邊的科學【博物館】會很適合，因為那裡有一大區介紹機器的歷史，而且十人以上的團體可以免費入場。"},{"w":"gallery","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where works of art are shown","c":"美術館；畫廊","s":"A: Have you decided where to hold the welcome party for our new clients from Singapore next Friday evening? B: Yes, we booked a modern art gallery downtown, because the guests can walk around and look at paintings by local artists while they enjoy drinks and talk with our sales team.","t":"A：你決定好下週五晚上要在哪裡為新加坡來的新客戶舉辦歡迎派對了嗎？ B：決定了，我們訂了市中心一間現代【美術館】，因為客人可以一邊四處走走欣賞本地藝術家的畫作，一邊享用飲料並和我們的業務團隊聊天。"},{"w":"theater","p":"n.","d":"a building where plays and shows are performed","c":"劇院","s":"A: Why is the marketing team leaving the office so early this Thursday, when we still have a lot of work to finish? B: The company bought tickets for everyone to see a musical at the new theater on Park Avenue, as a reward for reaching our sales goal three months early.","t":"A：我們還有很多工作要完成，為什麼行銷團隊這個星期四這麼早就下班？ B：公司幫大家買了票，去公園大道上新開的【劇院】看一齣音樂劇，作為提早三個月達成銷售目標的獎勵。"},{"w":"cinema","p":"n.","d":"a building where people watch films","c":"電影院","s":"A: The shopping mall next to our office looks much busier than usual, so do you know what is happening there today? B: A large cinema with twelve screens opened on the top floor this week, and many people are lining up to buy tickets for the new action film.","t":"A：我們辦公室旁邊的購物中心看起來比平常熱鬧得多，你知道今天那裡發生什麼事嗎？ B：本週頂樓開了一間有十二個影廳的大型【電影院】，很多人正在排隊買新上映動作片的票。"},{"w":"library","p":"n.","d":"a place where people can borrow or read books","c":"圖書館","s":"A: Where can the new interns study quietly for their certification exam during the lunch break, since the office is so noisy? B: The city library across the street has free study rooms and fast Wi-Fi, and it also keeps many business books that they can borrow with a free card.","t":"A：辦公室這麼吵，新實習生午休時可以去哪裡安靜地準備認證考試？ B：對街的市立【圖書館】有免費的自習室和快速的無線網路，還有很多商業書籍，只要辦一張免費的借書證就能借閱。"},{"w":"monument","p":"n.","d":"a statue or building made to help people remember a person or event","c":"紀念碑；紀念建築","s":"A: What is that tall stone structure in the middle of the park that all the tour groups stop to take photos of? B: It is a monument built in 1920 to honor the workers who built the city's first railway, and a small sign beside it explains their story in four languages.","t":"A：公園中間那座所有旅行團都停下來拍照的高大石造建築是什麼？ B：那是一座建於1920年的【紀念碑】，用來紀念建造這座城市第一條鐵路的工人，旁邊有一塊小牌子用四種語言介紹他們的故事。"},{"w":"heritage","p":"n.","d":"the history, traditions and old buildings that a country or group has had for many years","c":"遺產；文化資產","s":"A: Why did the city council refuse the developer's plan to build a hotel on the old harbor site last month? B: The council said the old warehouses are an important part of the city's heritage, so they must be protected and repaired instead of being knocked down for a modern building.","t":"A：上個月市議會為什麼拒絕開發商在舊港口用地蓋飯店的計畫？ B：議會表示那些舊倉庫是這座城市【文化遺產】的重要部分，所以必須加以保護和修繕，而不是拆掉改建成現代建築。"},{"w":"temple","p":"n.","d":"a building where people go to pray, especially in Asian religions","c":"廟；寺廟","s":"A: Our visitors from Canada want to see something special about local culture before they fly home on Sunday, so where should we take them? B: Let's take them to the old temple near the night market, where they can watch people light incense and learn about the gods that local families pray to.","t":"A：我們的加拿大訪客星期天搭機回國前，想看看一些特別的在地文化，我們該帶他們去哪裡？ B：我們帶他們去夜市附近那間古老的【廟宇】吧，他們可以在那裡看人們點香，並了解當地家庭所祭拜的神明。"},{"w":"church","p":"n.","d":"a building where Christians go to pray","c":"教堂","s":"A: Why are there so many people in formal clothes outside the old stone building on Main Street this morning? B: A couple is getting married in the church at eleven o'clock, so the guests are waiting outside, and our café across the street has been very busy serving them coffee.","t":"A：今天早上主街上那棟古老石造建築外面為什麼有那麼多穿正式服裝的人？ B：有一對新人十一點要在【教堂】結婚，所以賓客在外面等候，我們對街的咖啡店一直忙著為他們送咖啡。"},{"w":"mosque","p":"n.","d":"a building where Muslims go to pray","c":"清真寺","s":"A: Is there anything we should know before we take the visiting delegation from Malaysia around the city tomorrow? B: Yes, some of them would like to stop at the mosque near the train station for Friday prayers, so please plan a one-hour break around noon and choose a halal restaurant for lunch.","t":"A：明天帶馬來西亞來訪的代表團在市區參觀之前，我們有什麼需要知道的嗎？ B：有，他們之中有些人想在火車站附近的【清真寺】停留做星期五的禮拜，所以請在中午前後安排一小時的休息時間，並選一間清真餐廳吃午餐。"},{"w":"shrine","p":"n.","d":"a holy place built to honor a god or a special person","c":"神社；聖祠","s":"A: What did you enjoy most about your business trip to Kyoto, apart from the meetings with the suppliers? B: On the last morning I walked to a quiet shrine in the hills, where hundreds of red gates lined the path, and it was the most peaceful hour of the whole busy week.","t":"A：除了和供應商開會之外，你這次京都出差最喜歡的是什麼？ B：最後一天早上，我走到山上一座寧靜的【神社】，小路兩旁排列著數百座紅色鳥居，那是整個忙碌的一週裡最平靜的一個小時。"},{"w":"palace","p":"n.","d":"a large, grand house where a king, queen or president lives or once lived","c":"宮殿","s":"A: How was the company trip to Bangkok, and did the new staff enjoy the sightseeing on the second day? B: Everyone loved it, especially the visit to the royal palace, where the gold roofs shone in the sun, although we had to wear long trousers and cover our shoulders before going inside.","t":"A：公司的曼谷旅遊怎麼樣？新同事喜歡第二天的觀光行程嗎？ B：大家都很喜歡，尤其是參觀皇家【宮殿】，金色的屋頂在陽光下閃閃發亮，不過進去之前我們必須穿長褲並遮住肩膀。"},{"w":"castle","p":"n.","d":"a large, strong building with thick walls, built in the past to protect people","c":"城堡","s":"A: Where will the annual sales conference be held this year, since the hotel we used last year is closed for repairs? B: The organizers booked a five-hundred-year-old castle in Scotland that is now a hotel, so we will have our meetings in a hall with stone walls and enjoy dinner in its garden.","t":"A：去年用的飯店因整修而關閉，今年的年度業務會議要在哪裡舉辦？ B：主辦單位訂了一座位於蘇格蘭、有五百年歷史且現已改成飯店的【城堡】，所以我們會在石牆大廳裡開會，並在它的花園享用晚餐。"},{"w":"plaza","p":"n.","d":"an open public area in a town, often with shops around it","c":"廣場","s":"A: Where will the company set up its booth for the new coffee drink during the holiday weekend? B: We got permission to use the open plaza in front of the city hall, where thousands of shoppers pass every day, so we expect to give away about two thousand free samples.","t":"A：連假週末期間，公司要在哪裡設置新咖啡飲品的攤位？ B：我們獲准使用市政廳前面的開放【廣場】，那裡每天有數千名購物人潮經過，所以我們預計會發送大約兩千份免費試飲品。"},{"w":"square","p":"n.","d":"an open area in a town with buildings on all four sides","c":"廣場","s":"A: Where should I meet the tour group from Japan tomorrow morning, since I have never been to the old town before? B: Wait for them by the fountain in the main square, which is surrounded by cafés and old buildings, and you will easily see the big clock on the town hall.","t":"A：我從沒去過舊城區，明天早上該在哪裡和日本旅行團碰面？ B：在主【廣場】的噴水池旁邊等他們，廣場四周都是咖啡館和老建築，你會很容易看見市政廳上的大時鐘。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"a famous building or object that is easy to see and helps people know where they are","c":"地標","s":"A: Why does the hotel group want to buy that tall old tower near the harbor, even though it needs so many repairs? B: It is the most famous landmark in the city and appears on almost every postcard, so a hotel there would attract many visitors who want a room with a special view.","t":"A：港口附近那座高大的舊塔需要大量修繕，為什麼飯店集團還想買下它？ B：它是這座城市最有名的【地標】，幾乎每張明信片上都有它，所以在那裡開飯店會吸引許多想要特別景觀房的遊客。"},{"w":"exhibition","p":"n.","d":"a public show of art or other interesting things","c":"展覽","s":"A: Why is the museum staying open until ten o'clock every night this month, when it usually closes at five? B: A special exhibition of ancient Egyptian gold jewelry has arrived from London, and so many people want to see it that the managers decided to add evening hours.","t":"A：博物館平常五點就關門，為什麼這個月每天晚上都開到十點？ B：一場古埃及黃金珠寶的特別【展覽】從倫敦運來了，想看的人實在太多，所以館方決定增加晚間開放時段。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special time when people celebrate something, often with music and food","c":"節慶；藝術節","s":"A: Why are all the hotels in the city fully booked for the second weekend of October this year? B: The annual food and music festival takes place along the river that weekend, and it attracts more than a hundred thousand visitors from other countries, so you should book a room today.","t":"A：為什麼今年十月第二個週末城裡所有的飯店都客滿了？ B：那個週末河岸邊會舉辦年度美食音樂【節】，吸引超過十萬名外國遊客，所以你今天就應該訂房。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of playing music, dancing or acting in front of an audience","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: What is planned for the guests after dinner at the hotel on the last night of the international conference? B: A local group will give a short performance of traditional drum music and dance on the stage, and after that everyone can join a free tour of the hotel's garden.","t":"A：國際會議最後一晚，在飯店晚餐後為賓客安排了什麼節目？ B：一個本地團體會在台上進行一段傳統鼓樂和舞蹈的簡短【表演】，之後大家可以參加飯店花園的免費導覽。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom or belief that people have followed for a long time","c":"傳統","s":"A: Why does everyone in the office bring a dish from home on the last Friday before the New Year holiday? B: It is a tradition that started when the company was founded thirty years ago, and the boss believes that sharing food helps the different departments get to know each other better.","t":"A：為什麼新年假期前的最後一個星期五，辦公室裡每個人都從家裡帶一道菜來？ B：這是公司三十年前創立時開始的【傳統】，老闆認為分享食物能幫助不同部門彼此更加認識。"},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"something that people in a society usually do","c":"習俗；慣例","s":"A: Should I bring a gift when I visit the family of our business partner in Seoul next week? B: Yes, it is a local custom to bring a small present such as fruit or sweets when you visit someone's home, and you should also take off your shoes at the door.","t":"A：下週我去拜訪首爾生意夥伴的家人時，應該帶禮物嗎？ B：應該，到別人家拜訪時帶水果或甜點等小禮物是當地的【習俗】，而且你也應該在門口脫鞋。"},{"w":"folklore","p":"n.","d":"old stories and beliefs of a group of people, passed down over time","c":"民間傳說；民俗","s":"A: Why did the advertising agency choose a white snake for the new tea company's logo and TV commercial? B: In local folklore, the white snake is a symbol of good luck and long life, so older shoppers will feel a warm connection to the brand when they see it.","t":"A：廣告公司為什麼為新茶飲公司的商標和電視廣告選擇白蛇？ B：在當地的【民間傳說】中，白蛇象徵好運與長壽，所以年長的消費者看到時會對這個品牌產生親切感。"},{"w":"artifact","p":"n.","d":"an old object made by people, especially one that is important in history","c":"文物；手工藝品","s":"A: Why did the construction work on the new subway station stop suddenly last week? B: The workers found an ancient clay pot under the street, and the city must check whether the artifact is valuable before the digging can continue, so the project may be two months late.","t":"A：新地鐵站的施工上週為什麼突然停工？ B：工人在街道底下發現了一個古老的陶罐，市政府必須先確認這件【文物】是否有價值，才能繼續開挖，所以工程可能會延誤兩個月。"},{"w":"architecture","p":"n.","d":"the style and design of buildings","c":"建築風格；建築學","s":"A: What do foreign visitors usually say about the old part of the city when they come for business meetings? B: Most of them are surprised by the beautiful architecture, because the streets are full of red-brick shop houses from the 1920s that mix Japanese, Western and Chinese styles.","t":"A：外國訪客來這裡開商務會議時，通常怎麼評價城市的舊城區？ B：大多數人都對美麗的【建築風格】感到驚訝，因為街道上滿是1920年代的紅磚街屋，融合了日式、西式和中式風格。"},{"w":"historic","p":"adj.","d":"important in history","c":"具有歷史意義的","s":"A: Why is the hotel so expensive, even though the rooms are smaller than those at the new hotels near the airport? B: It is a historic building where the first trade agreement between the two countries was signed in 1895, so many guests pay extra to stay in such a famous place.","t":"A：那間飯店的房間比機場附近的新飯店小，為什麼還那麼貴？ B：那是一棟【具有歷史意義的】建築，1895年兩國第一份貿易協定就是在那裡簽署的，所以很多客人願意多付錢住在這麼有名的地方。"},{"w":"cultural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the art, music, traditions and way of life of a group of people","c":"文化的","s":"A: Why does the company send new managers to spend a month in the Tokyo office before they start working with Japanese clients? B: The training helps them understand important cultural differences, such as how people give feedback or exchange business cards, so they avoid mistakes in their first important meetings.","t":"A：為什麼公司在新任經理開始和日本客戶合作之前，先派他們到東京辦公室待一個月？ B：這項訓練能幫助他們了解重要的【文化】差異，例如人們如何給予回饋或交換名片，讓他們在最初的重要會議中避免犯錯。"},{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following ways of doing things that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統的","s":"A: What kind of restaurant should we book for the dinner with our clients from Paris on their first night in Taipei? B: Let's take them to a traditional Taiwanese restaurant in Dadaocheng, where the cooks still make dishes the old way and the guests sit at round wooden tables.","t":"A：巴黎客戶在台北的第一晚，我們應該訂什麼樣的餐廳和他們吃晚餐？ B：帶他們去大稻埕一間【傳統】台菜餐廳吧，那裡的廚師仍用古早方法做菜，客人坐在木製圓桌旁用餐。"},{"w":"ethnic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a group of people who share a culture, language or history","c":"民族的；種族的","s":"A: Why did the supermarket chain decide to open a new section near the entrance of every store this spring? B: Our research showed that more shoppers want to cook ethnic food at home, so the new section sells spices, sauces and noodles from Thailand, India, Mexico and Korea.","t":"A：這家連鎖超市今年春天為什麼決定在每家店的入口附近開設新區？ B：我們的研究顯示，越來越多顧客想在家烹調【異國民族風味的】料理，所以新區販售來自泰國、印度、墨西哥和韓國的香料、醬料和麵條。"},{"w":"sacred","p":"adj.","d":"holy; connected with God or religion and treated with great respect","c":"神聖的","s":"A: Why did the mining company cancel its plan to dig on the mountain after spending two years on research? B: The local people consider the mountain sacred, because their families have prayed there for centuries, and the company decided that keeping a good relationship with them was more important.","t":"A：這家礦業公司花了兩年做研究之後，為什麼取消了在那座山開採的計畫？ B：當地人認為那座山是【神聖的】，因為他們的家族世世代代在那裡祈禱，公司認為維持與他們的良好關係更重要。"},{"w":"tourist","p":"n.","d":"a person who visits a place for pleasure","c":"觀光客；遊客","s":"A: Why does the new hotel near the station offer free maps and bicycles at the front desk? B: Almost every tourist who stays there wants to explore the old town by themselves, and the manager found that guests who enjoy their visit are more likely to leave good reviews online.","t":"A：車站附近那間新飯店為什麼在櫃台提供免費地圖和腳踏車？ B：幾乎每位住在那裡的【觀光客】都想自己探索舊城區，經理發現玩得愉快的客人比較會在網路上留下好評。"},{"w":"guide","p":"v.","d":"to show someone the way, especially around a place","c":"引導；帶領","s":"A: Who will take care of the twenty visitors from our partner bank when they come to see the new head office on Monday? B: Mr. Lee from the front desk will guide them through each floor, explain how the departments work together, and then bring them to the meeting room for lunch.","t":"A：星期一合作銀行的二十位訪客來參觀新總部時，由誰負責接待？ B：櫃台的李先生會【帶領】他們參觀每個樓層，說明各部門如何合作，然後帶他們到會議室用午餐。"},{"w":"tour","p":"n.","d":"a visit to a place in which you walk around and look at it","c":"參觀；遊覽","s":"A: What will the overseas buyers do on the morning after they arrive, before the contract meeting begins? B: Our factory manager will give them a two-hour tour of the production line, so they can see how carefully we test every product before it is packed and shipped.","t":"A：海外買家抵達後的隔天早上，在合約會議開始之前要做什麼？ B：我們的廠長會帶他們進行兩小時的生產線【參觀】，讓他們看到我們在每件產品包裝出貨前測試得多麼仔細。"},{"w":"display","p":"v.","d":"to put something in a place where people can see it easily","c":"展示；陳列","s":"A: Where should we put the old photos and the first product the company ever made, now that the new lobby is finished? B: Let's display them in a glass case near the main entrance, so that visitors can learn about our sixty-year history while they wait for their appointments.","t":"A：新大廳完工了，我們該把那些舊照片和公司做出的第一件產品放在哪裡？ B：我們把它們【展示】在主入口附近的玻璃櫃裡吧，讓訪客在等候會面時可以了解公司六十年的歷史。"},{"w":"preserve","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in its original state and protect it from harm","c":"保存；保護","s":"A: Why is the government giving money to the owners of old wooden houses in the mountain village? B: It wants to preserve these hundred-year-old homes for future generations, so owners who repair the roofs and walls using the original methods can receive up to half of the cost.","t":"A：政府為什麼要撥款給山村裡老木屋的屋主？ B：政府希望為後代【保存】這些百年老屋，所以用原始工法修繕屋頂和牆壁的屋主，最多可以獲得一半費用的補助。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable for a special day or event","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Why is the whole staff going to a restaurant by the river after work this Friday instead of going home? B: We are going to celebrate the company's twentieth anniversary together, and the president will give a short speech and hand out awards to the employees who have worked here the longest.","t":"A：為什麼全體員工這週五下班後不回家，而是要去河邊的一家餐廳？ B：我們要一起【慶祝】公司成立二十週年，總裁會發表簡短致詞，並頒獎給在這裡工作最久的員工。"}]},{"unit":93,"theme":"Culture 文化","cards":[{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom or belief that has existed for a long time","c":"傳統","s":"A: Why is the whole office going out for dinner together next Friday instead of having the usual year-end party at the hotel? B: It has become a tradition in our company to eat a big meal together before the Lunar New Year holiday, and the boss always pays for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼下週五整個辦公室要一起出去吃晚餐，而不是像往常一樣在飯店辦尾牙？ B：在農曆新年假期前一起吃頓大餐已經成為我們公司的【傳統】，而且老闆總是請大家。"},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"a usual way of doing something in a place or group","c":"習俗；風俗","s":"A: I'm flying to Tokyo next week to meet our new business partners for the first time, so is there anything I should know before the meeting? B: Yes, it's a local custom to exchange business cards with both hands and a small bow, so take plenty of cards and read each one carefully.","t":"A：我下週要飛去東京，第一次和我們的新商業夥伴見面，開會前有什麼我該知道的嗎？ B：有，用雙手交換名片並微微鞠躬是當地的【習俗】，所以多帶些名片，並仔細看每一張。"},{"w":"heritage","p":"n.","d":"the history, buildings and traditions of a place that are passed down","c":"遺產；傳統文化","s":"A: Why did the city council reject the plan to build a new shopping mall on the old street near the river last month? B: The buildings there are more than two hundred years old and are part of the city's cultural heritage, so the council wants to protect them for future generations.","t":"A：為什麼市議會上個月否決了在河邊老街上興建新購物中心的計畫？ B：那裡的建築已有兩百多年歷史，是這座城市文化【遺產】的一部分，所以議會想為後代子孫保護它們。"},{"w":"identity","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that make a person, group or brand different from others","c":"身分；認同；特色","s":"A: Why did the coffee chain keep its old logo and shop design when it was bought by the large international company last year? B: The new owners understood that the brand's strong local identity was the main reason why loyal customers kept coming back, so they decided not to change it.","t":"A：去年那家咖啡連鎖店被大型國際公司收購時，為什麼還保留舊標誌和店面設計？ B：新老闆了解，這個品牌強烈的在地【特色】是忠實顧客不斷回流的主要原因，所以決定不改變它。"},{"w":"ethnic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a group of people who share a culture, language or origin","c":"種族的；民族的；異國風味的","s":"A: What kind of restaurants can our visitors from the head office find near the hotel where they are staying this week? B: The area around the hotel has many small ethnic restaurants run by families from Vietnam, India and Thailand, so our guests can try a different kind of food every night.","t":"A：總公司來的訪客這週住的飯店附近，有哪些餐廳可以去？ B：飯店周圍有很多由越南、印度和泰國家庭經營的小型【異國風味】餐廳，所以我們的客人每晚都可以嘗試不同的料理。"},{"w":"diverse","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other; of many kinds","c":"多元的；各式各樣的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team invite people from so many different age groups and countries to test the new mobile app last week? B: Our customers come from very diverse backgrounds, so we wanted to make sure that the app is easy to use for everyone, not just for young people in Taipei.","t":"A：行銷團隊上週為什麼邀請這麼多不同年齡層和國家的人來測試新的手機應用程式？ B：我們的顧客來自非常【多元的】背景，所以我們想確保這個應用程式人人都容易使用，而不只是台北的年輕人。"},{"w":"multicultural","p":"adj.","d":"having people of many different cultures living together","c":"多元文化的","s":"A: Why do so many international companies choose to open their Asian head offices in Singapore rather than in other cities in the region? B: Singapore is a multicultural society where people speak English, Chinese, Malay and Tamil, so foreign staff often feel comfortable living and working there with their families.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多跨國公司選擇把亞洲總部設在新加坡，而不是這個地區的其他城市？ B：新加坡是一個【多元文化的】社會，人們說英語、華語、馬來語和坦米爾語，所以外籍員工和家人在那裡生活和工作常常感到很自在。"},{"w":"intercultural","p":"adj.","d":"happening between people from different cultures","c":"跨文化的（不同文化之間的）","s":"A: Why does the company ask every new manager to join a two-day training course before they start working with our overseas offices? B: The course teaches intercultural communication skills, such as how to give feedback politely to colleagues in Japan or Germany, because small misunderstandings can easily damage important business relationships.","t":"A：為什麼公司要求每位新任經理在開始和海外分公司合作前，參加為期兩天的訓練課程？ B：這門課教的是【跨文化】溝通技巧，例如如何禮貌地給日本或德國同事回饋意見，因為小誤會很容易破壞重要的商業關係。"},{"w":"cross-cultural","p":"adj.","d":"comparing or involving two or more different cultures","c":"跨文化的（比較不同文化的）","s":"A: What did the new sales director learn during her first year working with clients in the Middle East and South America? B: She said that cross-cultural differences in how people treat time and deadlines surprised her most, so she now plans extra days for every project in those regions.","t":"A：新任業務總監在中東和南美與客戶合作的第一年學到了什麼？ B：她說人們看待時間和截止期限的【跨文化】差異最讓她驚訝，所以她現在在那些地區的每個專案都會多預留幾天。"},{"w":"belief","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling that something is true or right","c":"信念；信仰；看法","s":"A: Why does the hotel in Hong Kong not have a fourth floor, and why do the elevator buttons go straight from three to five? B: Many local guests hold a strong belief that the number four brings bad luck because it sounds like the word for death, so the owners decided to skip it.","t":"A：為什麼香港那家飯店沒有四樓，電梯按鈕直接從三跳到五？ B：許多當地客人有個強烈的【信念】，認為數字四會帶來厄運，因為它聽起來像「死」這個字，所以業主決定跳過它。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"an idea or quality that people think is important in life or work","c":"價值觀；價值","s":"A: Why did the company spend so much time choosing new staff for the customer service team this spring? B: The manager says that honesty is the most important value in our company culture, so she only hires people who will tell customers the truth even when the news is bad.","t":"A：公司今年春天為什麼花這麼多時間挑選客服團隊的新員工？ B：經理說誠實是我們公司文化中最重要的【價值觀】，所以她只雇用即使消息不好也會對顧客說實話的人。"},{"w":"norm","p":"n.","d":"what is usual or expected in a group or society","c":"常態；規範","s":"A: Is it okay for me to leave the office at five o'clock sharp, or will my new manager think I am lazy? B: In this company it is the norm for most people to stay until about six, but nobody will complain if you finish all your work and go home on time.","t":"A：我五點整準時下班可以嗎？還是新主管會覺得我很懶？ B：在這家公司，大部分人待到六點左右是【常態】，但如果你完成所有工作並準時回家，沒人會抱怨。"},{"w":"ritual","p":"n.","d":"a set of actions that is always done in the same way","c":"儀式；例行習慣","s":"A: Why does the new team leader always buy coffee for everyone before the Monday morning meeting starts? B: It is a little ritual that she started at her old company, because she believes that sharing a hot drink helps people relax and talk more openly about problems.","t":"A：為什麼新的組長總是在週一早上開會前請大家喝咖啡？ B：這是她在之前的公司開始的一個小【儀式】，因為她相信一起喝杯熱飲能幫助大家放鬆，更坦率地談論問題。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal public event held for a special occasion","c":"典禮；儀式","s":"A: What time should the guests arrive at the new factory on Friday, and will the mayor be there too? B: The opening ceremony begins at ten in the morning, when the mayor and our president will cut the red ribbon together, and then everyone is invited to a short tour and lunch.","t":"A：客人週五應該幾點到新工廠？市長也會出席嗎？ B：開幕【典禮】早上十點開始，市長和我們的總裁會一起剪綵，之後邀請大家參加簡短的參觀和午餐。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special time or event when people celebrate something","c":"節慶；節日；藝術節","s":"A: Why are all the hotels in Tainan fully booked for the second weekend of February this year? B: The city is holding its famous lantern festival that weekend, and thousands of visitors from all over Taiwan and Japan are coming to see the lights and enjoy the street food.","t":"A：為什麼今年二月第二個週末台南的飯店全都客滿了？ B：那個週末這座城市要舉辦著名的燈籠【節】，成千上萬來自全台灣和日本的遊客會來看燈並享受街頭小吃。"},{"w":"folklore","p":"n.","d":"old stories and beliefs of a group of people","c":"民間傳說；民俗","s":"A: Why did the tourism office hire a local storyteller to lead the evening walking tours in the old town this summer? B: Visitors love hearing the folklore of the area, such as old tales about ghosts in the temple and the fisherman who married a sea goddess, so the tours sell out every night.","t":"A：觀光局今年夏天為什麼聘請一位當地說故事的人帶領老城區的夜間徒步導覽？ B：遊客很喜歡聽這個地區的【民間傳說】，例如寺廟裡的鬼故事和娶了海神的漁夫，所以導覽每晚都賣光。"},{"w":"myth","p":"n.","d":"an idea that many people believe but that is not true; an old story","c":"迷思；神話","s":"A: Do you really think working from home makes employees less productive, as some managers say? B: That is a myth, actually, because our study last year showed that people who worked from home finished more tasks, took fewer sick days and were happier with their jobs.","t":"A：你真的認為在家工作會讓員工生產力降低嗎？就像有些經理說的那樣？ B：事實上那是個【迷思】，因為我們去年的研究顯示，在家工作的人完成更多任務、請更少病假，而且對工作更滿意。"},{"w":"art","p":"n.","d":"paintings, drawings and other beautiful things that people create","c":"藝術；美術","s":"A: Why did the bank decide to hang so many paintings in the main hall of its new head office downtown? B: The chairman loves modern art and believes that beautiful pictures make both customers and staff feel calm, so he bought works from young painters in Taipei.","t":"A：銀行為什麼決定在市中心新總部的大廳掛這麼多畫？ B：董事長很喜愛現代【藝術】，相信美麗的畫作能讓顧客和員工都感到平靜，所以他向台北的年輕畫家買了作品。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"sounds arranged in a pleasant way by singing or playing instruments","c":"音樂","s":"A: What can we do to make the waiting room at the clinic feel less stressful for patients in the afternoon? B: We could play some soft music in the background and add a few green plants, because research shows that calm sounds help people feel relaxed while they wait for their appointments.","t":"A：我們可以做什麼讓診所的候診室下午時對病人來說比較不緊張？ B：我們可以播放一些輕柔的背景【音樂】並加幾盆綠色植物，因為研究顯示平靜的聲音能幫助人們在等候看診時感到放鬆。"},{"w":"dance","p":"n.","d":"a set of movements done to music","c":"舞蹈；舞","s":"A: What kind of entertainment are we planning for the guests at the end of the international sales conference? B: A group of young performers will show a traditional Indigenous dance from eastern Taiwan, and afterward they will invite our guests onto the stage to learn a few simple steps.","t":"A：國際業務會議結束時，我們打算為客人安排什麼樣的娛樂表演？ B：一群年輕表演者會表演一支來自台灣東部的傳統原住民【舞蹈】，之後他們會邀請客人上台學幾個簡單的舞步。"},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"books, poems and plays, especially those thought to be of high quality","c":"文學","s":"A: Why did the publishing company hire a new editor who speaks both Korean and Chinese last month? B: We plan to translate more modern Korean literature, especially popular novels and short stories, because readers in Taiwan have become very interested in them after watching so many Korean dramas.","t":"A：出版公司上個月為什麼聘請一位會說韓文和中文的新編輯？ B：我們打算翻譯更多現代韓國【文學】，特別是受歡迎的小說和短篇故事，因為台灣讀者看了這麼多韓劇後，對它們變得很有興趣。"},{"w":"language","p":"n.","d":"the system of words that people of a country use to speak and write","c":"語言","s":"A: What is the biggest challenge for our engineers who moved to the new factory in Vietnam this year? B: The language barrier is the biggest problem at first, because most local workers do not speak English, so the company now pays for Vietnamese lessons twice a week after work.","t":"A：今年調到越南新工廠的工程師們，遇到最大的挑戰是什麼？ B：一開始最大的問題是【語言】障礙，因為大多數當地工人不會說英文，所以公司現在支付每週兩次下班後的越南語課程費用。"},{"w":"dialect","p":"n.","d":"a form of a language spoken in one area","c":"方言","s":"A: Why did the call center in Kaohsiung hire several older staff members who grew up in the countryside? B: Many of our elderly customers in southern Taiwan prefer to speak a local dialect rather than Mandarin on the phone, so we need people who can understand them and answer their questions clearly.","t":"A：高雄的客服中心為什麼聘請了幾位在鄉下長大的年長員工？ B：南台灣許多年長顧客在電話中比較喜歡說當地【方言】而不是華語，所以我們需要能聽懂他們並清楚回答問題的人。"},{"w":"cuisine","p":"n.","d":"a style of cooking from a country or area","c":"料理；菜餚","s":"A: Where should we take the clients from Paris for dinner after the contract signing on Thursday evening? B: Let's book a table at the new restaurant near the station, because it serves excellent Taiwanese cuisine with a modern style, and the chef can explain each dish in French.","t":"A：週四晚上簽約後，我們該帶巴黎來的客戶去哪裡吃晚餐？ B：我們去車站附近那家新餐廳訂位吧，因為它供應風格現代的優質台灣【料理】，而且主廚可以用法文介紹每道菜。"},{"w":"costume","p":"n.","d":"clothes worn for a show, a festival or a special occasion","c":"服裝；戲服","s":"A: Why are the hotel staff wearing such colorful clothes at the front desk this week? B: The hotel is celebrating the Mid-Autumn Festival, so the manager asked everyone to wear a traditional Chinese costume to welcome guests and make the lobby feel more cheerful during the holiday.","t":"A：為什麼這週飯店櫃檯的員工穿著這麼鮮豔的衣服？ B：飯店正在慶祝中秋節，所以經理請大家穿傳統中式【服裝】迎接客人，讓大廳在假期間更有歡樂氣氛。"},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"a picture or object that represents an idea","c":"象徵；符號","s":"A: Why did the company choose a mountain for the new logo instead of the old blue circle? B: The designers wanted a symbol of strength and growth that customers would remember easily, and Jade Mountain is famous all over Taiwan as the highest peak on the island.","t":"A：公司為什麼選擇一座山作為新標誌，而不是原本的藍色圓圈？ B：設計師想要一個代表力量和成長、顧客容易記住的【象徵】，而玉山是台灣最高峰，全台聞名。"},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"the fact of including many different types of people or things","c":"多元化；多樣性","s":"A: Why is the human resources department trying to hire more women and people from other countries this year? B: The board believes that greater diversity in the workplace brings fresh ideas and helps us understand customers in different markets, so they have set clear goals for every team.","t":"A：人資部門今年為什麼努力雇用更多女性和來自其他國家的人？ B：董事會相信職場更加【多元化】能帶來新想法，並幫助我們了解不同市場的顧客，所以他們為每個團隊設定了明確的目標。"},{"w":"global","p":"adj.","d":"involving the whole world","c":"全球的","s":"A: Why did the electronics company move its main office from Hsinchu to Singapore last spring? B: The company wants to become a global brand that sells products in more than fifty countries, and Singapore makes it easier to reach customers and partners in Asia, Europe and Australia.","t":"A：那家電子公司去年春天為什麼把總部從新竹搬到新加坡？ B：公司想成為在五十多個國家銷售產品的【全球】品牌，而新加坡讓它更容易接觸亞洲、歐洲和澳洲的顧客與夥伴。"},{"w":"local","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the area where you live or work","c":"當地的；在地的","s":"A: Why does the new supermarket on Main Street sell so many vegetables from small farms near the city? B: The owner wants to support local farmers and reduce transport costs, and customers are happy to pay a little more for fresh food that was picked only a day before.","t":"A：大街上那家新超市為什麼賣這麼多來自城市附近小農場的蔬菜？ B：老闆想支持【當地的】農民並降低運輸成本，而顧客也很樂意為前一天才採收的新鮮食物多付一點錢。"},{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following old customs or ways of doing things","c":"傳統的","s":"A: What kind of gift should we give the Japanese clients when they visit our office next month? B: I think they would like something traditional from Taiwan, such as a set of fine oolong tea and a handmade teapot, because it shows our culture and is easy to carry home.","t":"A：日本客戶下個月來訪時，我們該送什麼禮物？ B：我想他們會喜歡台灣【傳統的】東西，例如一套上等烏龍茶和手工茶壺，因為它展現我們的文化，而且方便帶回家。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"new and using the latest ideas or designs","c":"現代的；現代化的","s":"A: Why did so many young engineers apply for jobs at the new software company in Taichung this year? B: The company has a very modern office with standing desks, a gym and a quiet room for naps, and it also lets staff choose flexible working hours.","t":"A：今年為什麼這麼多年輕工程師應徵台中那家新軟體公司的工作？ B：那家公司有非常【現代化的】辦公室，有站立式辦公桌、健身房和可以小睡的安靜房間，還讓員工選擇彈性工時。"},{"w":"influence","p":"v.","d":"to change how someone thinks or acts","c":"影響","s":"A: Why is our marketing team paying a famous YouTuber to try our new running shoes and post a video about them? B: Our research shows that popular online stars strongly influence what young people decide to buy, so one good video can bring us thousands of new customers in a week.","t":"A：我們的行銷團隊為什麼付錢給知名YouTuber試穿我們的新跑鞋並發布影片？ B：我們的研究顯示，受歡迎的網路明星會強烈【影響】年輕人決定購買什麼，所以一支好影片在一週內就能為我們帶來數千名新顧客。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change something so that it fits a new situation","c":"使適應；改編","s":"A: How did the fast-food chain manage to become so popular in India, where many people do not eat beef? B: The company had to adapt its menu to local tastes, so it created spicy chicken and vegetable burgers, and now its restaurants there are busier than the ones in America.","t":"A：那家速食連鎖店是怎麼在許多人不吃牛肉的印度變得這麼受歡迎的？ B：公司必須讓菜單【適應】當地口味，所以推出了辣味雞肉和蔬菜漢堡，現在那裡的餐廳比美國的還要忙。"},{"w":"preserve","p":"v.","d":"to keep something safe so that it continues to exist","c":"保存；保護","s":"A: Why is the old tea company in Pinglin still making tea by hand when machines would be much faster? B: The family wants to preserve the skills that their grandparents taught them, and many tourists visit the shop because they want to see how tea was made a hundred years ago.","t":"A：坪林那家老茶行為什麼還用手工製茶，明明機器會快得多？ B：這個家族想【保存】祖父母傳授給他們的技術，而且很多遊客來店裡，是因為想看看一百年前茶是怎麼做的。"}]},{"unit":94,"theme":"Curtain 窗簾","cards":[{"w":"drape","p":"n.","d":"a long, heavy curtain","c":"帷幔；厚窗簾","s":"A: Why does the hotel lobby feel so much warmer and quieter than it did when we stayed here last spring? B: The new owners hung a long, heavy drape across the tall glass wall near the entrance, so it keeps out the cold wind in winter and also reduces the noise from the busy street outside.","t":"A：為什麼飯店大廳感覺比我們去年春天住在這裡時溫暖又安靜許多？ B：新老闆在入口附近的高大玻璃牆前掛了一片又長又厚的【布簾】，所以冬天能擋住冷風，也能減少外面繁忙街道的噪音。"},{"w":"blind","p":"n.","d":"a window cover that you pull down to block light","c":"百葉窗；捲簾","s":"A: Why is it so hard to see the slides during the afternoon meetings in the small conference room on the fifth floor? B: The sun shines straight through the window after two o'clock, so I have asked the facilities team to put up a blind that we can pull down whenever we give presentations.","t":"A：為什麼五樓小會議室在下午開會時很難看清楚投影片？ B：兩點以後陽光直接從窗戶照進來，所以我已經請設施組裝一個【捲簾】，讓我們每次做簡報時都能拉下來。"},{"w":"shade","p":"n.","d":"something that blocks direct sunlight","c":"遮陽物；遮光簾","s":"A: The customers at the café's outdoor tables keep complaining about the heat at lunchtime, so what can we do before the summer season starts? B: We could put up a large umbrella or a cloth shade over the patio, which would keep the tables cool and let people enjoy their meals outside without sitting in the strong sun.","t":"A：咖啡店戶外座位的客人一直抱怨午餐時間太熱，夏季開始前我們能做什麼？ B：我們可以在露台上方架設一把大傘或一片布製【遮陽篷】，讓桌子保持涼爽，客人就能在戶外用餐而不用坐在烈日下。"},{"w":"panel","p":"n.","d":"one flat piece of curtain or other material","c":"一片（窗簾布）；面板","s":"A: The new curtains for the training room arrived this morning, but why are there four separate pieces instead of one big curtain? B: The supplier sent each panel separately so that it is easier to carry and wash, and when we hang all four of them side by side, they will cover the entire glass wall.","t":"A：訓練教室的新窗簾今天早上到了，但為什麼是四塊分開的布，而不是一大片窗簾？ B：供應商把每一片【窗簾布片】分開寄送，這樣比較好搬也好洗，等我們把四片並排掛起來，就能遮住整面玻璃牆。"},{"w":"fabric","p":"n.","d":"cloth used to make clothes, curtains, etc.","c":"布料；織物","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager reject the first set of curtain samples that the designer brought to the meeting yesterday? B: She said the fabric felt too thin and cheap for the luxury suites, so she asked the designer to find a thicker material that looks elegant and does not fade in strong sunlight.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理昨天拒絕了設計師帶來開會的第一批窗簾樣品？ B：她說那種【布料】摸起來太薄又廉價，不適合豪華套房，所以她請設計師找一種看起來高雅、在強烈陽光下也不會褪色的較厚材質。"},{"w":"velvet","p":"n.","d":"a soft, thick cloth with a smooth surface","c":"天鵝絨；絲絨","s":"A: What kind of curtains did the theater choose for the main stage when it was renovated last year? B: They chose deep red velvet, which is soft, thick and expensive, because the director wanted the hall to look rich and classic when the audience walks in before each evening show.","t":"A：劇院去年整修時，主舞台選了什麼樣的布幕？ B：他們選了深紅色的【天鵝絨】，又軟又厚又昂貴，因為導演希望觀眾每晚演出前走進來時，整個大廳看起來華麗又古典。"},{"w":"linen","p":"n.","d":"a cloth made from the flax plant","c":"亞麻布","s":"A: Our restaurant wants a relaxed, natural look for the new seaside branch, so which material do you recommend for the curtains? B: I suggest light linen in a sandy color, because it lets in plenty of soft daylight, feels cool in hot weather, and matches the wooden tables and plants you plan to use.","t":"A：我們餐廳希望新的海邊分店有輕鬆自然的風格，你建議窗簾用什麼材質？ B：我建議用沙色的輕薄【亞麻布】，因為它能透進大量柔和的日光，天熱時摸起來涼爽，也和你們打算使用的木桌及植物很搭。"},{"w":"sheer","p":"adj.","d":"very thin, so you can almost see through it","c":"薄透的；透明的","s":"A: The clients want privacy in the meeting room, but they also want natural light, so what should we put on the windows? B: We can hang sheer curtains that are thin enough to let sunlight come through, but people walking past in the hallway outside will not be able to see clearly into the room.","t":"A：客戶希望會議室有隱私，但也想要自然光，我們窗戶該裝什麼？ B：我們可以掛【薄透的】窗簾，薄到能讓陽光透進來，但在外面走廊經過的人無法清楚看到室內。"},{"w":"opaque","p":"adj.","d":"not clear, so you cannot see through it","c":"不透明的","s":"A: Why did the medical clinic replace the glass doors of its examination rooms during the renovation last month? B: Patients said they felt uncomfortable because people in the waiting area could see inside, so the clinic put in opaque glass that nobody can see through at all, and the doctors also added thick curtains for extra protection.","t":"A：那間診所上個月整修時為什麼換掉了診療室的玻璃門？ B：病人說他們覺得不自在，因為候診區的人看得到裡面，所以診所換成了完全看不透的【不透明】玻璃，醫生們還加裝了厚窗簾以多一層保護。"},{"w":"blackout","p":"adj.","d":"(of curtains) stopping all light from coming in","c":"遮光的","s":"A: The night-shift nurses say they cannot sleep well during the day in the staff dormitory, so how can we help them? B: We should install blackout curtains in every bedroom, because they stop almost all sunlight from coming in, and the rooms will stay dark and quiet even at noon.","t":"A：夜班護理師說她們白天在員工宿舍睡不好，我們能怎麼幫忙？ B：我們應該在每間臥室裝【遮光】窗簾，因為它們幾乎能擋住所有陽光，即使中午房間也會保持昏暗安靜。"},{"w":"pleat","p":"n.","d":"a fold that is sewn into cloth","c":"褶；褶襉","s":"A: The customer says the curtains we made for her living room look flat and plain, so what can we change to make them look more stylish? B: We can sew a neat pleat at the top every ten centimeters, so the fabric falls in soft, even folds and looks fuller and more expensive when it hangs from the rail.","t":"A：客人說我們幫她客廳做的窗簾看起來平平的很單調，我們可以改什麼讓它更有型？ B：我們可以在頂端每隔十公分縫一道整齊的【褶】，讓布料垂成柔和均勻的皺褶，掛在軌道上時看起來更飽滿、更高級。"},{"w":"rod","p":"n.","d":"a long, thin pole for hanging curtains","c":"桿；窗簾桿","s":"A: Why are the new curtains in the reception area hanging so low that they touch the dirty floor? B: The workers fixed the metal rod about twenty centimeters too low on the wall, so I have asked them to move it higher tomorrow morning before the guests arrive for the opening ceremony.","t":"A：接待區的新窗簾為什麼掛得那麼低，都碰到髒地板了？ B：工人把金屬【窗簾桿】裝在牆上時低了大約二十公分，所以我已經請他們明天早上在賓客抵達參加開幕典禮之前把它往上移。"},{"w":"rail","p":"n.","d":"a bar or track that curtains hang from","c":"軌道；橫桿","s":"A: Why does it take so long to open and close the curtains in the big ballroom before each wedding banquet? B: The old plastic rail is bent in several places, so the curtains keep getting stuck, and the hotel has decided to replace it with a smooth aluminum track next week.","t":"A：為什麼每次婚宴前，大宴會廳的窗簾都要花很久才能拉開和拉上？ B：舊的塑膠【窗簾軌道】有好幾處彎掉了，所以窗簾一直卡住，飯店決定下週換成滑順的鋁製軌道。"},{"w":"hook","p":"n.","d":"a curved piece of metal or plastic for hanging things","c":"鉤子；掛鉤","s":"A: The curtain in Room 512 fell down again this morning, so do we need to call a repair company? B: No, it is a small problem, because one plastic hook broke and the curtain slipped off the rail, so housekeeping can replace it in a few minutes with a spare part from the storeroom.","t":"A：512號房的窗簾今天早上又掉下來了，我們需要叫維修公司嗎？ B：不用，這是小問題，只是有一個塑膠【掛鉤】斷了，窗簾才從軌道上滑落，房務部用倉庫裡的備用零件幾分鐘就能換好。"},{"w":"ring","p":"n.","d":"a small circle used to hang a curtain on a pole","c":"環；圈","s":"A: Our café curtains make a loud scraping noise every time the staff pull them, and the customers have noticed, so what is the cause? B: Each metal ring rubs against the iron pole, so we should replace them with wooden ones, which slide more quietly and also look warmer with our furniture.","t":"A：我們咖啡店的窗簾每次員工拉的時候都會發出很大的刮擦聲，客人都注意到了，原因是什麼？ B：每個金屬【圓環】都會摩擦鐵桿，所以我們應該換成木製的，它們滑動起來比較安靜，和我們的家具搭配也更溫馨。"},{"w":"tieback","p":"n.","d":"a band that holds a curtain to one side","c":"窗簾綁帶；窗簾扣","s":"A: The curtains in the hotel restaurant keep falling across the windows, and guests at the corner tables cannot see the harbor view, so what should we do? B: Let's attach a cloth tieback to the wall beside each window, so the staff can hold the curtains to the side neatly during breakfast and lunch.","t":"A：飯店餐廳的窗簾一直垂落遮住窗戶，角落座位的客人看不到港口景色，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們在每扇窗戶旁的牆上裝一條布製【窗簾綁帶】，讓員工在早餐和午餐時段能把窗簾整齊地束在一邊。"},{"w":"valance","p":"n.","d":"a short piece of cloth across the top of a window","c":"窗簾頂帷；帷幔","s":"A: The curtain rails in the new boutique look ugly and industrial, so how can we hide them without spending too much money? B: We can put a short decorative valance across the top of each window, which covers the metal tracks and also adds a little color that matches the shop's logo.","t":"A：新精品店的窗簾軌道看起來很醜又很工業風，我們怎麼樣才能不花太多錢把它們遮起來？ B：我們可以在每扇窗戶頂端加一條短的裝飾【窗簾頂帷】，既能遮住金屬軌道，也能增添一點和店家標誌相配的色彩。"},{"w":"hem","p":"n.","d":"the folded and sewn edge of a piece of cloth","c":"褶邊；底邊","s":"A: The new curtains for the hotel lobby are about five centimeters too long, so should we send all of the curtains back to the factory? B: No, our tailor can simply fold up the hem at the bottom and sew it again, which is much faster and cheaper than ordering a whole new set from overseas.","t":"A：飯店大廳的新窗簾長了大約五公分，我們應該把所有窗簾都退回工廠嗎？ B：不用，我們的裁縫只要把底部的【褶邊】往上折再重新縫好就行了，這比從海外訂一整套新的快得多也便宜得多。"},{"w":"lining","p":"n.","d":"a layer of cloth on the back or inside of something","c":"襯裡；內襯","s":"A: Why are the curtains in our east-facing guest rooms fading so quickly when the ones on the west side still look new? B: The curtains on the east side were made without a lining, so the morning sun hits the colored fabric directly, while the others have an extra layer of white cloth behind them that protects them.","t":"A：為什麼我們朝東的客房窗簾褪色得那麼快，而西側的看起來還像新的？ B：東側的窗簾做的時候沒有【襯裡】，所以早晨的陽光直接照在有顏色的布料上，而其他窗簾後面多了一層白布保護。"},{"w":"hang","p":"v.","d":"to put something up so that it is held from above","c":"懸掛","s":"A: The art gallery is opening a new exhibition on Friday evening, so what still needs to be done in the main hall? B: The workers still need to hang the long white curtains along the back wall and then set up the lights, so I asked them to come in early on Thursday.","t":"A：美術館星期五晚上要開新展覽，主展廳還有什麼事要做？ B：工人還需要沿著後牆【掛】上長長的白色窗簾，然後架設燈光，所以我請他們星期四早點來。"},{"w":"draw","p":"v.","d":"to pull curtains open or closed","c":"拉（窗簾）","s":"A: The marketing director is about to show the new commercial on the big screen, but the room is far too bright, so what should I do? B: Please draw the curtains on both sides of the room before she starts, so the sunlight stays outside and everyone can see the colors in the video clearly.","t":"A：行銷總監馬上要在大螢幕上播放新廣告，但房間太亮了，我該怎麼辦？ B：請在她開始之前把房間兩側的窗簾【拉上】，這樣陽光就被擋在外面，大家都能清楚看到影片中的色彩。"},{"w":"open","p":"v.","d":"to move something so that it is no longer shut","c":"打開；拉開","s":"A: The conference room smells a bit stale after this morning's long workshop, so what can we do before the clients arrive at two? B: Let's open the curtains and the windows for about half an hour, so fresh air and bright sunlight can come in and the room will feel much more welcoming.","t":"A：今天早上的長時間工作坊結束後，會議室有點悶，客戶兩點到之前我們能做什麼？ B：我們把窗簾和窗戶【打開】大約半小時，讓新鮮空氣和明亮的陽光進來，房間會感覺親切許多。"},{"w":"close","p":"v.","d":"to shut something","c":"關上；拉上","s":"A: The hotel guests in Room 808 have complained that the street lights shine into their room all night, so what did you tell them? B: I explained that they can press the button beside the bed to close the electric curtains automatically, and I also offered them a free eye mask.","t":"A：808號房的房客抱怨路燈整晚照進房間，你怎麼跟他們說？ B：我向他們說明可以按床邊的按鈕，自動【關上】電動窗簾，我還送了他們一個免費的眼罩。"},{"w":"slide","p":"v.","d":"to move smoothly along a surface","c":"滑動","s":"A: Why did the restaurant spend so much money on new glass doors for the terrace? B: The old doors were heavy and difficult to move, but the new ones slide smoothly along a metal track, so the waiters can open the whole terrace to the garden in seconds on warm evenings.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳花那麼多錢為露台換新的玻璃門？ B：舊門又重又難推，而新門能沿著金屬軌道順暢地【滑動】，所以在溫暖的夜晚，服務生幾秒鐘就能把整個露台向花園打開。"},{"w":"block","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from passing through","c":"阻擋；擋住","s":"A: Our designers say the afternoon sunlight makes it hard for them to see their computer screens, so what is the best solution for the studio? B: We should install thick curtains on the west windows, because they will block most of the strong light while still letting a little daylight in from the north side.","t":"A：我們的設計師說午後的陽光讓他們很難看清電腦螢幕，工作室最好的解決辦法是什麼？ B：我們應該在西側窗戶裝上厚窗簾，因為它們能【阻擋】大部分強光，同時仍讓北側透進一些日光。"},{"w":"cover","p":"v.","d":"to put something over something else to protect or hide it","c":"覆蓋；遮蓋","s":"A: The painters are coming to repaint the boardroom ceiling this weekend, so how will we protect the expensive furniture and the new carpet? B: We will move the chairs into the hallway and cover the long table and the floor with plastic sheets, so no paint will drip onto anything valuable.","t":"A：油漆工這個週末要來重新粉刷董事會議室的天花板，我們要怎麼保護昂貴的家具和新地毯？ B：我們會把椅子搬到走廊，再用塑膠布【蓋住】長桌和地板，這樣油漆就不會滴到任何貴重物品上。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look nicer by adding things to it","c":"裝飾","s":"A: The company's twentieth anniversary party is next Saturday, so how are you planning to make the plain office hall look special? B: We will decorate the walls with gold curtains, colorful balloons and photos from the last twenty years, so every guest can see how much the company has grown.","t":"A：公司二十週年派對在下週六，你打算怎麼讓樸素的辦公大廳看起來特別？ B：我們會用金色布幔、彩色氣球和過去二十年的照片【裝飾】牆面，讓每位來賓都能看到公司成長了多少。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being seen or heard by other people","c":"隱私","s":"A: Why did the bank add thick curtains around the desks in the loan department last month? B: Customers often talk about their salaries and debts there, so the bank wanted to give them more privacy and make sure other people in the waiting area cannot hear or see their personal information.","t":"A：銀行上個月為什麼在貸款部的辦公桌周圍加裝了厚窗簾？ B：顧客常在那裡談論他們的薪水和債務，所以銀行想給他們更多【隱私】，確保候位區的其他人無法聽到或看到他們的個人資料。"},{"w":"shadow","p":"n.","d":"a dark shape made when something blocks light","c":"影子；陰影","s":"A: Why does the photographer want us to move the meeting table away from the window before the team photo? B: The sunlight is coming in at a low angle, so it throws a dark shadow across half of everyone's faces, and he says the picture will look much better with soft, even light.","t":"A：為什麼攝影師要我們在拍團隊照之前把會議桌移離窗戶？ B：陽光以很低的角度照進來，在每個人半張臉上投下一道深色的【陰影】，他說用柔和均勻的光線拍出來的照片會好看很多。"},{"w":"glare","p":"n.","d":"strong, bright light that hurts your eyes","c":"刺眼的強光；反光","s":"A: The receptionists say they get headaches by the end of every afternoon shift, so have you found out what is causing the problem? B: The glare from the sun reflecting off the white floor is very strong after three o'clock, so we have ordered tinted blinds and a darker rug for the front desk area.","t":"A：櫃檯人員說每次下午班快結束時都會頭痛，你找出是什麼原因了嗎？ B：三點以後，陽光從白色地板反射的【刺眼強光】非常強烈，所以我們已經為前台區域訂了有色百葉窗和一塊深色地毯。"},{"w":"interior","p":"adj.","d":"inside a building or object","c":"內部的；室內的","s":"A: The architect's plan for the new office has lots of glass, so how will the staff in the middle of the building get any privacy? B: She designed interior walls made of frosted glass with thin curtains, so the meeting rooms in the center stay private but still receive light from the outside windows.","t":"A：建築師的新辦公室設計用了很多玻璃，那大樓中間的員工要怎麼保有隱私？ B：她設計了用霧面玻璃加上薄窗簾做成的【室內】隔間牆，讓中央的會議室保有隱私，但仍能從外側窗戶得到光線。"},{"w":"window","p":"n.","d":"an opening in a wall, with glass, that lets in light","c":"窗戶","s":"A: Which seat would you like for the client lunch at the new Italian restaurant downtown on Friday? B: I would like a table by the window, because the restaurant is on the twentieth floor, and our clients from overseas will enjoy the view of the river and the mountains while we discuss the contract.","t":"A：星期五在市中心新開的義大利餐廳和客戶吃午餐，你想坐哪個位子？ B：我想要靠【窗】的桌子，因為餐廳在二十樓，我們的海外客戶可以在我們討論合約時欣賞河流和山景。"},{"w":"stage","p":"n.","d":"the raised area where people perform or give speeches","c":"舞台","s":"A: How are the preparations going for the annual awards ceremony in the hotel ballroom tonight? B: The technicians have already set up the microphones and lights on the stage, and now they are testing the red curtain to make sure it opens smoothly when the host walks out at seven.","t":"A：今晚在飯店宴會廳舉行的年度頒獎典禮準備得如何？ B：技術人員已經在【舞台】上裝好麥克風和燈光，現在正在測試紅色布幕，確保主持人七點走出來時它能順利拉開。"},{"w":"backdrop","p":"n.","d":"a painted or printed cloth at the back of a stage or event","c":"背景幕；背景","s":"A: What do we need for the photo area at the product launch event next Wednesday afternoon? B: We need a large printed backdrop with our company logo behind the speakers, so every photo that journalists take will clearly show our brand name and the new phone.","t":"A：下週三下午的產品發表會拍照區需要什麼？ B：我們需要在講者後方放一大片印有公司標誌的【背景布幕】，這樣記者拍的每張照片都能清楚顯示我們的品牌名稱和新手機。"}]},{"unit":95,"theme":"Daily Routine 日常作息","cards":[{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual order of things you do every day","c":"例行公事；日常作息","s":"A: Why does the new receptionist arrive at the office thirty minutes before everyone else, even though her shift starts at nine? B: She says that a calm morning routine helps her a lot, so she checks the calendar, waters the plants, and answers her emails before the phones start ringing.","t":"A：新來的接待員為什麼比其他人早三十分鐘到辦公室，即使她的班九點才開始？ B：她說平靜的早晨【例行作息】對她幫助很大，所以她會在電話開始響之前查看行事曆、幫植物澆水，並回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something you do often, almost without thinking","c":"習慣","s":"A: How did you manage to finish your online marketing course while you were working full-time at the bank last year? B: I made a habit of studying for forty minutes on the train every morning, and after a few weeks it felt completely natural, so I never had to force myself.","t":"A：你去年在銀行全職工作時，是怎麼完成線上行銷課程的？ B：我養成了每天早上在火車上讀書四十分鐘的【習慣】，幾週後感覺就很自然了，所以我從來不必勉強自己。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists the times when things will happen","c":"時間表；行程","s":"A: Can we move the meeting with the designers from Thursday afternoon to Friday morning, since the technician is coming to fix the printer on Thursday? B: Let me check my schedule first, because I already promised to visit a client in the morning, but I think I can be back at the office by eleven.","t":"A：既然週四技術人員要來修印表機，我們可以把跟設計師的會議從週四下午改到週五早上嗎？ B：讓我先查看一下我的【行程】，因為我已經答應早上要去拜訪客戶，但我想我十一點前能回到辦公室。"},{"w":"timetable","p":"n.","d":"a list that shows when buses, trains or classes leave or happen","c":"時刻表","s":"A: How will the visitors from Tokyo get from the airport to our factory in Taichung if nobody can pick them up on Sunday? B: I've printed the high-speed rail timetable for them, so they can see when each train leaves, and our driver will meet them at the station when they arrive.","t":"A：如果週日沒有人能去接機，來自東京的訪客要怎麼從機場到我們在台中的工廠？ B：我已經幫他們印好了高鐵【時刻表】，讓他們知道每班車什麼時候發車，他們抵達時我們的司機會在車站接他們。"},{"w":"wake","p":"v.","d":"to stop sleeping","c":"醒來；叫醒","s":"A: Why did you miss the conference call with the London office last night, when you promised the manager you would join? B: I set my alarm for two in the morning, but I was so tired that I didn't wake up until six, so I sent an apology email to everyone right away.","t":"A：你昨晚為什麼錯過了和倫敦辦公室的電話會議？你明明答應經理會參加。 B：我把鬧鐘設在凌晨兩點，但我太累了，直到六點才【醒來】，所以我立刻寄了一封道歉信給大家。"},{"w":"rise","p":"v.","d":"to get out of bed in the morning; to go up","c":"起床；上升","s":"A: How does the owner of the bakery near our office manage to have fresh bread on the shelves by six every morning? B: He and his two assistants rise at three o'clock, start the ovens by four, and bake several hundred rolls before the first office workers stop by on their way to the station.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家麵包店的老闆是怎麼做到每天早上六點前架上就有新鮮麵包的？ B：他和兩位助手凌晨三點就【起床】，四點前開好烤箱，在第一批上班族前往車站途中順道光顧之前，烤好好幾百個麵包捲。"},{"w":"stretch","p":"v.","d":"to make your arms, legs or body long and straight","c":"伸展","s":"A: Do you have any advice for me, because my back always hurts after I sit at my desk and type reports for eight hours? B: Try to stand up every hour and stretch your arms and shoulders for a minute or two, and you might also ask the office manager for a better chair.","t":"A：你有什麼建議嗎？因為我坐在辦公桌前打八小時報告後，背總是很痛。 B：試著每小時站起來【伸展】一下手臂和肩膀一兩分鐘，你也可以請辦公室經理換一張比較好的椅子。"},{"w":"shower","p":"v.","d":"to wash your body while standing under running water","c":"淋浴；沖澡","s":"A: Is there anywhere in the building where employees can get ready after they cycle to the office in the hot summer weather? B: Yes, there's a small changing room on the basement level, so you can shower and change your clothes there before you go up to your desk on the fifth floor.","t":"A：大樓裡有沒有地方可以讓員工在炎熱夏天騎腳踏車上班後整理一下？ B：有，地下室有一間小更衣室，你可以在那裡【沖澡】、換衣服，然後再上五樓的座位。"},{"w":"brush","p":"v.","d":"to clean or make something tidy with a brush","c":"刷；梳","s":"A: Why does the dentist's office send a text message to all its patients a day before their appointments? B: The message reminds them to brush their teeth carefully before they come in, and it also tells them to arrive ten minutes early so that the receptionist can update their insurance information.","t":"A：牙醫診所為什麼要在看診前一天傳簡訊給所有病人？ B：簡訊會提醒他們來之前要仔細【刷】牙，也會告訴他們提早十分鐘到，讓櫃檯人員更新保險資料。"},{"w":"dress","p":"v.","d":"to put on clothes; to wear a certain kind of clothes","c":"穿衣；打扮","s":"A: Should I wear a suit to the interview at the law firm tomorrow, or is a shirt and trousers good enough? B: Law firms are usually quite formal, so I would dress in a dark suit and a plain tie, because it's better to look too professional than too casual on your first visit.","t":"A：明天去律師事務所面試應該穿西裝，還是穿襯衫和長褲就夠了？ B：律師事務所通常相當正式，所以我會【穿】深色西裝搭配素色領帶，因為第一次拜訪時看起來太專業總比太隨便好。"},{"w":"breakfast","p":"n.","d":"the first meal of the day","c":"早餐","s":"A: What time should the guests come down to the hotel restaurant tomorrow, since the bus to the trade fair leaves at eight? B: breakfast is served from six-thirty until nine-thirty, but I'd recommend going down by seven, because the restaurant gets very crowded when the tour groups arrive.","t":"A：既然明天往商展的巴士八點出發，客人們應該幾點下樓到飯店餐廳？ B：【早餐】供應時間從六點半到九點半，但我建議七點前下去，因為旅行團到了以後餐廳會非常擁擠。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between your home and your workplace","c":"通勤","s":"A: Why did Sarah decide to rent an apartment near the office instead of staying with her parents in the suburbs? B: She had to commute for almost two hours each way by bus and train, so she was always exhausted, and now she can walk to work in ten minutes.","t":"A：莎拉為什麼決定在辦公室附近租公寓，而不繼續和父母住在郊區？ B：她以前單程要搭公車和火車【通勤】將近兩小時，所以總是筋疲力盡，現在她走路十分鐘就能到公司。"},{"w":"work","p":"v.","d":"to do a job, usually to earn money","c":"工作","s":"A: Are you going to the company barbecue on Saturday afternoon, or do you have other plans for the long weekend? B: Unfortunately, I have to work at the airport counter until five, because two of my colleagues are sick, but I'll try to join you all for dinner later.","t":"A：你週六下午會參加公司烤肉嗎？還是長週末有其他計畫？ B：很可惜，我得在機場櫃台【工作】到五點，因為我有兩位同事生病了，但我晚點會試著和你們一起吃晚餐。"},{"w":"study","p":"v.","d":"to spend time learning about a subject","c":"讀書；學習","s":"A: How are you preparing for the accounting certificate exam next month while you're also training the new interns? B: I study for an hour every evening after dinner, and on Saturdays I go to the library because it's much quieter than my apartment, where the neighbors play loud music.","t":"A：你一邊訓練新實習生，一邊要怎麼準備下個月的會計證照考試？ B：我每天晚餐後【讀書】一小時，週六則去圖書館，因為那裡比我的公寓安靜多了，我的鄰居會大聲放音樂。"},{"w":"task","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work that must be done","c":"任務；工作","s":"A: You look really busy today, so is there anything I can do to help you before the sales report is due at five? B: Thanks, that would be great, because the most boring task is checking all the numbers in the spreadsheet, so could you compare them with last month's figures?","t":"A：你今天看起來真的很忙，在業績報告五點截止前，有什麼我能幫忙的嗎？ B：謝謝，那太好了，因為最無聊的【工作】是核對試算表中的所有數字，你可以幫我和上個月的數據做比較嗎？"},{"w":"meeting","p":"n.","d":"an event where people come together to discuss something","c":"會議","s":"A: Why are so many people waiting outside the conference room on the third floor this morning? B: The weekly team meeting is running late, because the director wanted to discuss the new budget in detail, so the marketing staff can't start their presentation until the room is free.","t":"A：今天早上三樓會議室外面為什麼有那麼多人在等？ B：每週的團隊【會議】延誤了，因為主管想詳細討論新預算，所以行銷人員要等會議室空出來才能開始簡報。"},{"w":"lunch","p":"n.","d":"the meal you eat in the middle of the day","c":"午餐","s":"A: Would you like to try the new Thai restaurant across the street today, or are you too busy with the client project? B: I'd love to, but I only have thirty minutes for lunch because the client is calling at one, so let's order takeout and eat in the staff room instead.","t":"A：你今天想試試對街新開的泰式餐廳嗎？還是你忙著客戶的專案？ B：我很想去，但我只有三十分鐘吃【午餐】，因為客戶一點會打電話來，所以我們改成叫外帶，在員工休息室吃吧。"},{"w":"break","p":"n.","d":"a short time when you stop working to rest","c":"休息時間","s":"A: How long have the factory workers been on the production line this morning without stopping? B: They started at seven, so it's almost three hours now, and I think we should give everyone a fifteen-minute break to drink some water and sit down before the next shipment arrives.","t":"A：工廠工人今天早上在生產線上連續工作多久了？ B：他們七點開始，所以現在快三個小時了，我想我們應該讓大家有十五分鐘的【休息時間】喝點水、坐一下，再迎接下一批貨。"},{"w":"exercise","p":"v.","d":"to move your body to stay healthy and strong","c":"運動","s":"A: How do you stay so energetic during the busy tax season, when everyone else in the office looks tired? B: I exercise at the gym near the station for half an hour before I come in each morning, and I also try to go to bed before eleven, even when there's a lot to do.","t":"A：在忙碌的報稅季，辦公室其他人都看起來很累，你怎麼還能保持那麼有活力？ B：我每天早上進公司前會在車站附近的健身房【運動】半小時，而且即使事情很多，我也盡量十一點前上床睡覺。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and become calm","c":"放鬆","s":"A: What are you planning to do after you finish the big product launch next Friday? B: I've booked two nights at a quiet hot spring hotel in the mountains, so I can turn off my phone and relax for a while, because I've been working late every night this month.","t":"A：下週五完成大型產品發表會後，你打算做什麼？ B：我在山上一間安靜的溫泉旅館訂了兩晚，這樣我可以關掉手機好好【放鬆】一下，因為這個月我每天晚上都工作到很晚。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"嗜好","s":"A: What do you usually do on weekends to forget about the pressure of your job at the bank? B: My favorite hobby is gardening, so I spend most Saturday mornings growing tomatoes and herbs on my balcony, and sometimes I bring the extra vegetables to the office for my colleagues.","t":"A：你週末通常做什麼來忘掉銀行工作的壓力？ B：我最喜歡的【嗜好】是園藝，所以大多數週六早上我都在陽台種番茄和香草，有時候會把多的蔬菜帶到辦公室給同事。"},{"w":"dinner","p":"n.","d":"the main meal of the evening","c":"晚餐；晚宴","s":"A: Has anyone booked a restaurant for the visitors from our partner company in Singapore yet? B: Yes, I reserved a private room at the seafood restaurant by the harbor, and the general manager will host the dinner at seven, right after the factory tour finishes.","t":"A：有人已經幫新加坡合作公司的訪客訂好餐廳了嗎？ B：有，我在港邊的海鮮餐廳訂了包廂，工廠參觀結束後，總經理七點會主持【晚宴】。"},{"w":"family","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who are related, such as parents and children","c":"家人；家庭","s":"A: Why did Mr. Chen turn down the promotion to the Shanghai office, even though the salary was much higher? B: He said he wanted to spend more time with his family, because his children are still in elementary school and his wife has just started a new job in Taipei.","t":"A：陳先生為什麼拒絕調到上海辦公室的升遷機會，即使薪水高很多？ B：他說他想多花時間陪【家人】，因為他的孩子還在讀小學，而他太太剛在台北開始新工作。"},{"w":"read","p":"v.","d":"to look at and understand written words","c":"閱讀","s":"A: What do you usually do on the long train ride to the head office in Kaohsiung every Monday morning? B: I like to read business magazines and industry news on my tablet, because it helps me learn about our competitors, and I sometimes find useful ideas for the weekly sales meeting.","t":"A：每週一早上搭長途火車到高雄總公司，你通常都做什麼？ B：我喜歡在平板上【閱讀】商業雜誌和產業新聞，因為這能幫助我了解競爭對手，有時候也能找到每週業務會議用得上的好點子。"},{"w":"watch","p":"v.","d":"to look at something for a period of time","c":"觀看","s":"A: How did the new employees learn to use the online ordering system so quickly last week? B: The trainer asked them to watch a short video that shows every step, and then they practiced with sample orders for an hour before they started taking real calls from customers.","t":"A：新員工上週怎麼這麼快就學會使用線上訂購系統？ B：訓練員請他們【觀看】一段示範每個步驟的短片，然後他們用範例訂單練習了一小時，才開始接聽客戶的真實來電。"},{"w":"plan","p":"v.","d":"to decide in detail what you will do","c":"計劃；規劃","s":"A: How do you manage to finish so many projects every week without ever staying late at the office? B: Every Monday morning, I plan my whole week in a notebook, putting the most important jobs first, so I always know exactly what to do next and rarely waste any time.","t":"A：你怎麼能每週完成那麼多專案，卻從來不用在辦公室待到很晚？ B：每週一早上，我會在筆記本上【規劃】一整週，把最重要的工作排在最前面，所以我總是清楚知道下一步要做什麼，很少浪費時間。"},{"w":"prepare","p":"v.","d":"to make something ready","c":"準備","s":"A: What does the restaurant staff need to do before the doors open for the busy Sunday lunch crowd? B: The cooks prepare the vegetables and sauces by ten, while the servers set the tables and check the reservation list, so that everything runs smoothly when the first guests arrive.","t":"A：在週日繁忙的午餐人潮開門前，餐廳員工需要做哪些事？ B：廚師們十點前要【準備】好蔬菜和醬汁，服務生則擺設餐桌並核對訂位名單，好讓第一批客人到達時一切順利。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in a clear order","c":"整理；安排","s":"A: Why is the shared drive so hard to use, when I need to find last year's contracts quickly? B: Nobody has had time to organize the files properly, so documents are saved in random folders, but the IT team promised to sort them by year and client next week.","t":"A：當我需要快速找到去年的合約時，共用硬碟為什麼這麼難用？ B：沒有人有時間好好【整理】檔案，所以文件被存在隨便的資料夾裡，不過資訊部門答應下週會按年份和客戶分類。"},{"w":"clean","p":"v.","d":"to remove dirt from something","c":"打掃；清潔","s":"A: Who is responsible for the kitchen on our floor, because the sink is full of dirty cups again this afternoon? B: Each department takes turns, and this week it's the design team's job to clean it, so I'll send them a friendly reminder before they leave tonight.","t":"A：我們這層樓的茶水間由誰負責？今天下午水槽裡又堆滿了髒杯子。 B：各部門輪流負責，這週輪到設計團隊【打掃】，所以我會在他們今晚下班前友善地提醒一下。"},{"w":"cook","p":"v.","d":"to make food by heating it","c":"烹煮；做飯","s":"A: Do you usually eat out after work, or do you make your own meals during the week to save money? B: I cook a big pot of soup and some rice on Sunday evenings, and then I bring a box to the office every day, which is healthier and much cheaper than buying lunch.","t":"A：你下班後通常外食，還是平日自己煮飯省錢？ B：我每週日晚上會【煮】一大鍋湯和一些飯，然後每天帶一盒到辦公室，這比買午餐健康又便宜多了。"},{"w":"rest","p":"v.","d":"to stop working and relax or sleep","c":"休息","s":"A: The doctor said you should stay home for a few days, so why are you answering emails from your bed? B: I know I should rest, but the client needs the price list by tomorrow, so I'll send it this morning and then turn off my laptop until Thursday.","t":"A：醫生說你應該在家待幾天，你為什麼還躺在床上回電子郵件？ B：我知道我應該【休息】，但客戶明天前需要價目表，所以我今天早上寄出後，就會把筆電關掉直到週四。"},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something","c":"反思；回顧","s":"A: Why do you write in a notebook for ten minutes at the end of every working day? B: It helps me reflect on what went well and what didn't, so I can learn from my mistakes and make a better plan for the next morning before I go home.","t":"A：你為什麼每個工作日結束時都要在筆記本上寫十分鐘？ B：這能幫助我【反思】哪些事情做得好、哪些沒做好，讓我從錯誤中學習，並在回家前為隔天早上擬定更好的計畫。"},{"w":"sleep","p":"v.","d":"to rest with your eyes closed and your mind not awake","c":"睡覺","s":"A: You look much more awake than last week, so did you finally fix the noise problem in your apartment? B: Yes, my neighbors moved out, so now I can sleep for seven or eight hours without waking up, and I can concentrate much better during long meetings at work.","t":"A：你看起來比上週精神多了，你終於解決公寓的噪音問題了嗎？ B：是的，我的鄰居搬走了，所以現在我可以【睡】七、八個小時都不會醒來，在公司開長時間的會議時也能更專心。"},{"w":"bedtime","p":"n.","d":"the time when you usually go to bed","c":"就寢時間","s":"A: How do you stop yourself from checking work emails late at night, since your boss often sends messages after ten? B: I put my phone in the living room an hour before bedtime, and I read a novel instead, so I fall asleep more easily and feel fresh the next morning.","t":"A：既然你老闆常在十點後傳訊息，你怎麼克制自己深夜不查看工作郵件？ B：我在【就寢時間】前一小時把手機放在客廳，改讀一本小說，這樣我比較容易入睡，隔天早上也覺得精神飽滿。"},{"w":"balance","p":"v.","d":"to give the right amount of time or attention to different things","c":"平衡；兼顧","s":"A: How does your manager manage to raise three young children while she leads such a large sales team? B: She works from home on Wednesdays and never takes calls after seven, so she can balance her job and her home life, and she encourages all of us to do the same.","t":"A：你的經理帶領這麼大的業務團隊，怎麼還能養育三個年幼的孩子？ B：她每週三在家工作，七點後從不接電話，所以能【兼顧】工作和家庭生活，她也鼓勵我們所有人這樣做。"}]},{"unit":96,"theme":"Damage 損壞","cards":[{"w":"harm","p":"n.","d":"damage or hurt caused to someone or something","c":"傷害；損害","s":"A: Why did the factory stop using the cheaper cleaning chemical that the new supplier sent us last spring? B: The safety team found that it could cause serious harm to workers' skin and eyes, so the manager decided to return all the bottles and go back to the old product.","t":"A：為什麼工廠停止使用新供應商去年春天送來的那款較便宜的清潔化學品？ B：安全小組發現它可能對工人的皮膚和眼睛造成嚴重的【傷害】，所以經理決定退回所有瓶子，改回使用舊產品。"},{"w":"destruction","p":"n.","d":"the act of damaging something so badly that it no longer exists or works","c":"破壞；毀滅","s":"A: Why is the insurance company sending three more inspectors to the coast this week instead of just one? B: The storm last weekend caused the destruction of more than two hundred homes and several hotels along the beach, so they need extra staff to check every claim quickly.","t":"A：為什麼保險公司這週要再派三名檢查員到海岸，而不是只派一名？ B：上週末的暴風雨造成海灘沿線兩百多棟房屋和數間飯店【毀壞】，所以他們需要額外人手快速審核每一件理賠。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to spoil or damage something completely","c":"毀掉；破壞","s":"A: Should we hold the company picnic in the park on Saturday, or would it be safer to book the hotel ballroom instead? B: Let's book the ballroom, because the weather report says heavy rain is coming, and I don't want a storm to ruin the whole day for our staff and their families.","t":"A：我們週六要在公園舉辦公司野餐，還是改訂飯店宴會廳比較保險？ B：訂宴會廳吧，因為氣象報告說會下大雨，我不希望一場暴風雨【毀掉】員工和他們家人的一整天。"},{"w":"loss","p":"n.","d":"the fact of losing something, or the money or value you lose","c":"損失；喪失","s":"A: How much did the fire in the storage room last month cost the bookstore, and was everything covered by insurance? B: The owner said the total loss was about fifty thousand dollars, mostly because of burned books and smoke, but the insurance company will pay for nearly all of it.","t":"A：上個月儲藏室的火災讓書店損失多少？所有東西都有保險理賠嗎？ B：老闆說總【損失】大約五萬美元，主要是燒毀的書和煙害，但保險公司幾乎會全額賠償。"},{"w":"break","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so that it separates into pieces or stops working","c":"打破；弄壞","s":"A: Why are the movers wrapping every glass and plate in so much paper before they put them into the boxes? B: The road to our new office is very bumpy, and they don't want anything to break during the trip, because the company would have to pay for any damage.","t":"A：搬家工人為什麼在把每個玻璃杯和盤子放進箱子前都用這麼多紙包起來？ B：通往我們新辦公室的路很顛簸，他們不希望任何東西在途中【破掉】，因為任何損壞公司都得賠償。"},{"w":"crack","p":"n.","d":"a thin line on the surface of something where it has started to break","c":"裂縫；裂痕","s":"A: Why did the building manager close the north stairway this morning without telling any of the tenants first? B: A cleaner noticed a long crack in the wall next to the third-floor landing, so the manager wants an engineer to check that the stairs are still safe to use.","t":"A：大樓經理今天早上為什麼沒先通知任何住戶就封閉了北側樓梯？ B：一位清潔人員發現三樓平台旁的牆上有一道長長的【裂縫】，所以經理想請工程師檢查樓梯是否仍能安全使用。"},{"w":"shatter","p":"v.","d":"to break suddenly into many small pieces","c":"粉碎；碎裂","s":"A: Why does the new display case in the jewelry store cost so much more than the old one we had before? B: It is made of special safety glass that will not shatter even if someone hits it with a hammer, so our expensive rings and watches are much better protected at night.","t":"A：珠寶店新的展示櫃為什麼比我們以前那個貴這麼多？ B：它是用特殊的安全玻璃做的，即使有人用鐵鎚敲也不會【碎裂】，所以我們昂貴的戒指和手錶在夜間能受到更好的保護。"},{"w":"scratch","p":"n.","d":"a thin mark or cut on a surface","c":"刮痕；擦痕","s":"A: Why did the customer return the laptop she bought from our online shop only two days after it arrived? B: She said there was a deep scratch across the screen when she opened the box, so we apologized, sent her a new one, and asked the warehouse to pack more carefully.","t":"A：那位顧客為什麼在筆電送達後才兩天就把在我們網路商店買的電腦退回？ B：她說打開箱子時螢幕上有一道很深的【刮痕】，所以我們向她道歉、寄了一台新的給她，並請倉庫包裝時更小心。"},{"w":"dent","p":"n.","d":"a hollow place in a hard surface where something has hit it","c":"凹痕","s":"A: Why is the sales manager so angry about the company car that came back from the repair shop yesterday afternoon? B: Someone hit it in the parking lot while it was there, and now there is a large dent in the back door that the shop refuses to fix for free.","t":"A：業務經理為什麼對昨天下午從修車廠回來的公司車那麼生氣？ B：車子停在那裡的時候有人在停車場撞到它，現在後車門上有一個很大的【凹痕】，而修車廠拒絕免費修理。"},{"w":"tear","p":"v.","d":"to pull something apart so that it splits, or to become split","c":"撕破；扯破","s":"A: Why are we switching to a new company for the shopping bags we give customers at the checkout counter? B: The old paper bags are so thin that they often tear when people put heavy bottles inside, and many shoppers have complained about dropping their groceries in the parking lot.","t":"A：我們為什麼要換一家公司來提供結帳櫃檯給顧客的購物袋？ B：舊的紙袋太薄了，人們放重的瓶子進去時常常會【破掉】，很多購物者抱怨在停車場把買的東西掉了一地。"},{"w":"rip","p":"v.","d":"to tear something quickly and roughly","c":"撕裂；扯開","s":"A: Why do the warehouse workers have to wear thick gloves when they open the boxes from the new supplier? B: The boxes are sealed with very strong plastic straps, and if you try to rip them open with your bare hands, you can easily cut your fingers on the sharp edges.","t":"A：倉庫工人打開新供應商送來的箱子時為什麼要戴厚手套？ B：箱子是用很堅固的塑膠帶封起來的，如果你想徒手把它們【撕開】，很容易被銳利的邊緣割傷手指。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"to fall down suddenly because of weakness or damage","c":"倒塌；崩塌","s":"A: Why has the city council decided to close the old wooden bridge near the train station to all traffic? B: Engineers found that its main supports are badly damaged by water, and they warned that the bridge could collapse if heavy trucks keep driving across it every day.","t":"A：市議會為什麼決定將火車站附近的舊木橋全面禁止通行？ B：工程師發現它的主要支柱被水嚴重損壞，並警告如果重型卡車每天繼續通過，這座橋可能會【倒塌】。"},{"w":"burn","p":"v.","d":"to damage or destroy something with fire or heat","c":"燒毀；燒傷","s":"A: Why did the hotel kitchen staff have to attend an extra safety training session this afternoon? B: Last week a cook left a pan of oil on the stove for too long, and the manager wants everyone to know how to stop a small fire before it can burn down the whole kitchen.","t":"A：飯店廚房員工今天下午為什麼得參加額外的安全訓練課程？ B：上週有位廚師把一鍋油放在爐子上太久，經理希望大家都知道如何在小火【燒毀】整個廚房之前把它撲滅。"},{"w":"flood","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of water that covers an area that is usually dry","c":"水災；洪水","s":"A: Why are all the computers and printers in the basement office being moved up to the second floor today? B: Heavy rain is expected all weekend, and the last time there was a flood in this part of the city, the basement filled with water and we lost a lot of equipment.","t":"A：地下室辦公室所有的電腦和印表機今天為什麼都要搬到二樓？ B：預計整個週末都會下大雨，上次這一區發生【水災】時，地下室整個淹水，我們損失了很多設備。"},{"w":"corrode","p":"v.","d":"to slowly damage metal by a chemical action, such as rust","c":"腐蝕；侵蝕","s":"A: Why does the maintenance team check the metal pipes on the roof of the seaside hotel every single month? B: The salty air from the ocean can corrode the steel much faster than in the city, so they look for rust early and replace any weak pipes before they start leaking.","t":"A：維修團隊為什麼每個月都要檢查海邊飯店屋頂上的金屬管線？ B：來自海洋的鹹空氣【腐蝕】鋼材的速度比在城市裡快得多，所以他們會及早檢查有沒有生鏽，並在管線開始漏水前更換脆弱的部分。"},{"w":"wear","p":"v.","d":"to become thinner or damaged because of long use","c":"磨損；耗損","s":"A: Why did the office manager choose such an expensive carpet for the main hallway instead of a cheaper one? B: Hundreds of employees and visitors walk through that hallway every day, and a cheap carpet would quickly wear out and look old, so this one will save money in the long run.","t":"A：辦公室經理為什麼為主要走廊選了這麼貴的地毯，而不是便宜一點的？ B：每天有數百名員工和訪客走過那條走廊，便宜的地毯很快就會【磨損】變舊，所以長期來看這款反而比較省錢。"},{"w":"erode","p":"v.","d":"to slowly damage or remove something, especially land, by water or wind","c":"侵蝕；逐漸削弱","s":"A: Why is the beach resort spending so much money on a new stone wall along the shore this year? B: Every winter, strong waves erode more of the sand in front of the hotel, and the owners worry that the swimming pool and the restaurant will be in danger within a few years.","t":"A：海灘度假村今年為什麼花這麼多錢在海岸沿線蓋新的石牆？ B：每年冬天，強浪都會【侵蝕】飯店前更多的沙灘，業主擔心幾年內游泳池和餐廳就會有危險。"},{"w":"decay","p":"v.","d":"to become rotten or slowly break down over time","c":"腐爛；衰敗","s":"A: Why did the restaurant throw away so many boxes of fruit and vegetables after the long holiday weekend? B: The refrigerator stopped working on Saturday while the kitchen was closed, and by Tuesday morning much of the fresh food had started to decay, so the chef said it was not safe to serve.","t":"A：餐廳在連假週末過後為什麼丟掉了那麼多箱蔬果？ B：週六廚房休息時冰箱故障了，到了週二早上很多新鮮食物已經開始【腐爛】，所以主廚說不能安全地端給客人。"},{"w":"injure","p":"v.","d":"to hurt a person or animal","c":"使受傷；傷害","s":"A: Why does the warehouse supervisor insist that everyone wear a hard hat, even when they are only walking through? B: Boxes sometimes fall from the high shelves without warning, and a heavy one could seriously injure someone's head, so the rule protects both the workers and the company.","t":"A：倉庫主管為什麼堅持每個人都要戴安全帽，即使只是路過也一樣？ B：箱子有時會毫無預警地從高架上掉下來，重的箱子可能會嚴重【傷到】人的頭部，所以這條規定同時保護了員工和公司。"},{"w":"destroy","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it cannot be used or repaired","c":"摧毀；毀壞","s":"A: Why does the law firm keep paper copies of all its important contracts in a bank safe across town? B: If a fire or an earthquake ever hit our office building, it could destroy every document we have here, so the partners want a second copy stored somewhere completely safe.","t":"A：律師事務所為什麼把所有重要合約的紙本存放在城另一頭的銀行保險箱裡？ B：如果我們的辦公大樓遇到火災或地震，可能會【毀掉】我們這裡所有的文件，所以合夥人希望在完全安全的地方保存第二份副本。"},{"w":"impair","p":"v.","d":"to make something weaker or less good than before","c":"損害；削弱","s":"A: Why did the airline change its rules so that pilots must rest for at least twelve hours between long flights? B: Studies showed that a lack of sleep can impair a pilot's judgment and reaction time, and the company does not want to take any risks with passenger safety.","t":"A：航空公司為什麼改變規定，要求機師在長途航班之間至少休息十二小時？ B：研究顯示睡眠不足會【損害】機師的判斷力和反應時間，公司不想在乘客安全上冒任何風險。"},{"w":"defect","p":"n.","d":"a fault or problem in something that makes it not work correctly","c":"缺陷；瑕疵","s":"A: Why did the car company ask thousands of customers to bring their new cars back to the dealers this month? B: Engineers discovered a defect in the brake system of one model, so the company decided to fix every car for free before anyone could get hurt on the road.","t":"A：汽車公司這個月為什麼要求數千名顧客把新車開回經銷商？ B：工程師發現某款車型的煞車系統有【缺陷】，所以公司決定在有人在路上受傷之前免費修理每一輛車。"},{"w":"fault","p":"n.","d":"a problem in a machine or system that stops it working correctly","c":"故障；毛病","s":"A: Why were all the elevators in the shopping mall out of service for most of yesterday afternoon? B: The technicians found an electrical fault in the main control panel, so they had to turn off the power to every elevator until they could replace the broken part safely.","t":"A：購物中心所有的電梯為什麼昨天下午大部分時間都停止運作？ B：技術人員在主控制面板發現電路【故障】，所以他們必須關掉每部電梯的電源，直到能安全更換損壞的零件。"},{"w":"leak","p":"n.","d":"a small hole or crack that lets liquid or gas escape","c":"漏水；洩漏","s":"A: Why is there a large plastic bucket in the corner of the meeting room on the fifth floor this week? B: There is a leak in the ceiling above that corner, and whenever it rains, water drips onto the carpet, so the building manager has called a roofer to come on Friday.","t":"A：五樓會議室角落這週為什麼放了一個大塑膠桶？ B：那個角落上方的天花板有【漏水】處，每次下雨水都會滴到地毯上，所以大樓經理已經找了屋頂工人週五來修。"},{"w":"spill","p":"v.","d":"to accidentally let liquid flow out of its container","c":"灑出；濺出","s":"A: Why aren't employees allowed to bring coffee or tea into the new computer training room anymore? B: Last month a trainee was careless enough to spill a whole cup of hot coffee onto one of the keyboards, and the repair cost was so high that the manager decided to ban all drinks.","t":"A：員工為什麼不能再把咖啡或茶帶進新的電腦訓練教室？ B：上個月有位受訓人員不小心把一整杯熱咖啡【灑】在其中一個鍵盤上，維修費用非常高，所以經理決定禁止所有飲料。"},{"w":"stain","p":"n.","d":"a dirty mark that is difficult to remove","c":"污漬；污點","s":"A: Why did the hotel guest in room 512 ask the front desk for a discount when she checked out this morning? B: She found a large brown stain on the bed sheet when she arrived late last night, and the housekeeping staff did not come to change it until almost midnight.","t":"A：512號房的房客今天早上退房時為什麼要求櫃檯打折？ B：她昨晚很晚抵達時發現床單上有一大塊褐色【污漬】，而房務人員直到快半夜才來更換。"},{"w":"fragile","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged","c":"易碎的；脆弱的","s":"A: Why did the shipping company charge us extra for the boxes we sent to the museum in Paris last week? B: We were sending old glass vases that are very fragile, so the boxes needed special foam packing and careful handling all the way from our warehouse to the museum.","t":"A：貨運公司為什麼對我們上週寄到巴黎博物館的箱子額外收費？ B：我們寄的是非常【易碎】的古老玻璃花瓶，所以從倉庫到博物館一路上箱子都需要特殊的泡棉包裝和小心搬運。"},{"w":"severe","p":"adj.","d":"very serious or bad","c":"嚴重的；劇烈的","s":"A: Why did the factory in the south have to stop production for almost three weeks last summer? B: A typhoon caused severe damage to the roof and the machines on the ground floor, and the owners had to wait for new equipment to arrive from Japan before they could reopen.","t":"A：南部的工廠去年夏天為什麼得停產將近三週？ B：一場颱風對屋頂和一樓的機器造成【嚴重的】損壞，業主必須等新設備從日本運來才能重新開工。"},{"w":"minor","p":"adj.","d":"small and not very serious","c":"輕微的；次要的","s":"A: Was anyone hurt when the delivery van hit the post outside the bakery early this morning? B: No, the driver was fine, and there was only minor damage to the front light of the van, so he was able to finish the rest of his deliveries before lunch.","t":"A：今天一早送貨車撞到麵包店外的柱子時，有人受傷嗎？ B：沒有，司機沒事，貨車只有前燈有【輕微的】損壞，所以他還能在午餐前送完剩下的貨。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a very long time or forever","c":"永久的；長期的","s":"A: Why does the electronics company give free earplugs to every worker who operates the loud machines in the factory? B: Working near that kind of noise for years can cause permanent hearing loss, and the company wants to protect its staff before any damage happens that cannot be fixed.","t":"A：電子公司為什麼要發免費耳塞給每位在工廠操作吵雜機器的員工？ B：長年在那種噪音附近工作可能導致【永久性】聽力受損，公司希望在造成無法修復的傷害之前保護員工。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for only a short time","c":"暫時的；臨時的","s":"A: Where will the accounting team work while the workers repair the water damage in their office next month? B: The company has rented a temporary space on the third floor of the building across the street, and the team will stay there for about six weeks until the repairs are finished.","t":"A：下個月工人修理會計團隊辦公室的水損時，他們要在哪裡辦公？ B：公司已經在對街大樓的三樓租了一個【臨時】空間，團隊會在那裡待大約六週，直到修繕完成。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken or damaged","c":"修理；修補","s":"A: How long will it take to get the photocopier on the second floor working again after it jammed this morning? B: The technician said he can repair it by Thursday, but he must order a new roller from the supplier first, so we should use the machine downstairs until then.","t":"A：二樓的影印機今天早上卡紙後，要多久才能恢復運作？ B：技術人員說他週四前可以【修好】，但他得先向供應商訂購新的滾輪，所以在那之前我們應該用樓下的機器。"},{"w":"restore","p":"v.","d":"to bring something back to its good condition","c":"修復；恢復","s":"A: Why did the hotel close its famous old ballroom for the whole of last year? B: The owners hired a team of experts to restore the painted ceiling and the wooden floor, which had been damaged by water and time, and now the room looks exactly as it did a hundred years ago.","t":"A：飯店去年為什麼整年關閉了那間著名的老宴會廳？ B：業主請了一組專家來【修復】被水和歲月損壞的彩繪天花板和木地板，現在那個廳看起來和一百年前一模一樣。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to get back something lost, or to return to a normal condition","c":"恢復；取回","s":"A: Did the IT department manage to save any of the sales files after the main server crashed on Monday night? B: Yes, they were able to recover almost all of the data from the backup system, but the reports we wrote on Monday afternoon were lost, so we have to do them again.","t":"A：週一晚上主伺服器當機後，資訊部有沒有救回任何業務檔案？ B：有，他們從備份系統【復原】了幾乎所有資料，但我們週一下午寫的報告不見了，所以得重做。"}]},{"unit":97,"theme":"Data Table 數據表格","cards":[{"w":"data table","p":"n.phr.","d":"a set of information arranged in rows and columns","c":"數據表格；資料表","s":"A: How should I show the monthly sales figures from our five branch offices in the report for tomorrow's board meeting? B: Put them in a simple data table with one line for each branch and one for each month, so the directors can compare the numbers quickly without reading long paragraphs.","t":"A：明天董事會會議的報告中，我應該如何呈現五間分公司的每月銷售數字？ B：把它們放進一個簡單的【數據表格】，每間分公司一行、每個月一欄，這樣董事們不用讀長篇段落就能快速比較數字。"},{"w":"row","p":"n.","d":"a line of things going across from left to right","c":"列；橫排","s":"A: I added the new customer's name to the spreadsheet, but where should I type her address and phone number? B: Keep all of her details in the same row as her name, and then move across to the right, filling in each box until her contact information is complete.","t":"A：我把新客戶的名字加進試算表了，但她的地址和電話號碼要打在哪裡？ B：把她所有的資料都放在跟她名字同一【列】，然後往右移，逐格填寫，直到她的聯絡資訊完整為止。"},{"w":"column","p":"n.","d":"a line of things going from top to bottom","c":"欄；直行","s":"A: The finance manager says the expense sheet is hard to read, so what change do you think we should make first? B: Let's add a separate column on the far right for the total cost of each trip, so she can look down that side and see every amount at once.","t":"A：財務經理說費用表很難閱讀，你認為我們應該先做什麼修改？ B：我們在最右邊另外加一個【欄】來放每趟出差的總費用，這樣她往下看那一側就能一次看到所有金額。"},{"w":"cell","p":"n.","d":"one small box in a table or spreadsheet","c":"儲存格","s":"A: Why is the total at the bottom of the budget sheet showing an error message instead of a number this morning? B: Someone typed the word 'ten' into one cell instead of the number 10, so the formula can't add it up until we correct that box.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上預算表底部的總計顯示錯誤訊息而不是數字？ B：有人在一個【儲存格】裡打了英文字「ten」而不是數字10，所以在我們修正那一格之前，公式無法把它加總。"},{"w":"header","p":"n.","d":"the title at the top of a column or page","c":"表頭；標題列","s":"A: The new interns keep putting phone numbers in the email column of the client list, so how can we stop this mistake? B: Let's write a clear header in bold at the top of every column, such as 'Phone' or 'Email', so nobody has to guess what goes where.","t":"A：新來的實習生一直把電話號碼填到客戶名單的電子郵件欄，我們要怎麼避免這種錯誤？ B：我們在每一欄最上方用粗體寫一個清楚的【表頭】，例如「電話」或「電子郵件」，這樣就沒人需要猜什麼該填在哪裡。"},{"w":"field","p":"n.","d":"a space in a form or database for one kind of information","c":"欄位","s":"A: Why did the online booking system refuse my order when I tried to reserve a meeting room for next Tuesday? B: You probably left one required field empty, such as your department code, and the system won't accept the form until every box with a star is filled in.","t":"A：我想預訂下週二的會議室時，為什麼線上預訂系統拒絕了我的訂單？ B：你可能把一個必填【欄位】留白了，例如部門代碼，在每個標有星號的格子都填好之前，系統不會接受表單。"},{"w":"record","p":"n.","d":"a set of information about one person or thing stored together","c":"紀錄；一筆資料","s":"A: A customer called to say she moved to a new apartment last month, so what should I do? B: Open her record in the customer database, change the old address to the new one, and save it, so our next delivery goes to the right place.","t":"A：一位顧客打電話來說她上個月搬到新公寓了，我該怎麼做？ B：在客戶資料庫裡打開她的【資料紀錄】，把舊地址改成新地址並儲存，這樣我們下一次的送貨就會送到正確的地方。"},{"w":"dataset","p":"n.","d":"a collection of related data used for study or work","c":"資料集","s":"A: How did the marketing team find out which age group buys the most of our new sports drink? B: They studied a large dataset from last year's online orders, which included the age, city, and purchase history of over twenty thousand customers, and found that buyers under thirty led sales.","t":"A：行銷團隊是怎麼發現哪個年齡層最常買我們的新運動飲料？ B：他們研究了去年網路訂單的一個大型【資料集】，裡面包含超過兩萬名顧客的年齡、城市和購買紀錄，發現三十歲以下的買家是銷售主力。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"a number or amount in a box or calculation","c":"數值","s":"A: The chart in my presentation shows that our Tokyo office sold almost nothing in March, but is that really correct? B: No, the value in that box should be 4,500, not 45, so someone left out two zeros when they copied the numbers from the regional report.","t":"A：我簡報裡的圖表顯示東京辦公室三月幾乎沒賣出東西，但這真的正確嗎？ B：不，那一格的【數值】應該是4,500而不是45，有人從區域報告複製數字時漏掉了兩個零。"},{"w":"entry","p":"n.","d":"one item of information written in a list or record","c":"項目；一筆登錄資料","s":"A: Why does the visitor log show the same delivery driver coming in twice at exactly 9:15 this morning? B: The guard at the front desk accidentally saved the same entry two times, so please delete the extra line before the security manager checks the list this afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼訪客登記表顯示同一位送貨司機今天早上9:15整進來兩次？ B：前台警衛不小心把同一筆【登錄資料】存了兩次，所以請在保全經理今天下午檢查名單之前刪掉多餘的那一行。"},{"w":"format","p":"n.","d":"the way information is arranged or shown","c":"格式","s":"A: The dates in the report from our London office look strange, so why does it say 03/04 for the April meeting? B: They use a different format that puts the day before the month, so we should change all the dates to one style before we combine the two reports.","t":"A：倫敦辦公室報告裡的日期看起來很奇怪，為什麼四月的會議寫成03/04？ B：他們使用不同的【格式】，把日放在月之前，所以在合併兩份報告之前，我們應該把所有日期改成同一種樣式。"},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of something are organized","c":"結構","s":"A: Our new inventory spreadsheet has become very confusing since three different departments started adding their own data to it. B: I agree, so let's plan a clear structure before next week, with one sheet for each warehouse and the same columns in the same order on every page.","t":"A：自從三個不同部門開始在新的庫存試算表加入自己的資料後，它就變得非常混亂。 B：我同意，所以我們在下週之前規劃一個清楚的【結構】，每個倉庫一張工作表，而且每一頁的欄位都相同、順序也一樣。"},{"w":"sort","p":"v.","d":"to put things in a particular order","c":"排序；分類","s":"A: The sales director wants to know which of our two hundred products made the most money this quarter, so how can I find that fast? B: Just sort the list by total sales from highest to lowest, and the top ten products will appear at the top of the screen.","t":"A：業務總監想知道我們兩百種產品中哪一種這一季最賺錢，我要怎麼快速找到？ B：只要依照總銷售額從高到低把清單【排序】，前十名產品就會出現在螢幕最上方。"},{"w":"filter","p":"v.","d":"to show only the items that match certain conditions","c":"篩選","s":"A: I need a list of only the customers who live in Taichung for our new store opening, but the file has thousands of names. B: You can filter the city column so that it shows Taichung only, and then copy those rows into a new sheet for the invitation letters.","t":"A：為了新店開幕，我需要一份只有住在台中的顧客名單，但檔案裡有好幾千個名字。 B：你可以【篩選】城市那一欄，讓它只顯示台中，然後把那些列複製到新的工作表上寄邀請函。"},{"w":"index","p":"n.","d":"a list that helps you find information quickly","c":"索引","s":"A: The new staff handbook has more than two hundred pages, so how will employees find the rules about vacation days? B: We added an index at the back with key topics in alphabetical order and page numbers, so anyone can find the holiday policy in seconds.","t":"A：新的員工手冊有超過兩百頁，員工要怎麼找到休假天數的規定？ B：我們在後面加了一份【索引】，依字母順序列出重要主題和頁碼，所以任何人都能在幾秒內找到休假規定。"},{"w":"lookup","p":"n.","d":"the act of searching a table to find matching information","c":"查找；查詢","s":"A: How does the new price sheet show the correct cost when I type a product code into the order form? B: It does an automatic lookup in the main product table, finds the matching code, and then brings back the latest price so you don't have to search by hand.","t":"A：當我在訂單表單輸入產品代碼時，新的價格表是怎麼顯示正確價格的？ B：它會在主產品表中自動進行【查找】，找到相符的代碼，然後帶回最新價格，所以你不必手動搜尋。"},{"w":"alignment","p":"n.","d":"the way text or numbers are lined up on a page","c":"對齊；對齊方式","s":"A: The numbers in the price column look messy on the printed copy, so what should I fix before the client meeting at two? B: Change the alignment so all the numbers line up on the right side of each box, which makes the prices much easier to compare.","t":"A：價格欄裡的數字在列印版上看起來很亂，兩點的客戶會議前我該修正什麼？ B：把【對齊方式】改成所有數字都靠每一格的右側排列，這樣價格比較起來會容易得多。"},{"w":"summary","p":"n.","d":"a short statement of the main points","c":"摘要；總結","s":"A: The CEO doesn't have time to read all twelve pages of the customer survey results before her flight tonight. B: Then let's write a one-page summary with the five most important findings and a small chart, so she can understand the main points while she waits at the airport.","t":"A：執行長今晚搭機前沒有時間看完十二頁的顧客調查結果。 B：那我們寫一份一頁的【摘要】，列出五個最重要的發現和一張小圖表，讓她在機場等候時就能了解重點。"},{"w":"aggregate","p":"v.","d":"to put separate numbers together into one total","c":"匯總；合計","s":"A: Each of our six stores sends its daily sales numbers in a separate file, so how can head office see the whole picture? B: The new software will aggregate the figures from all six files every evening and create one total report that managers can read the next morning.","t":"A：我們六家店各自用不同的檔案傳每日銷售數字，總公司要怎麼看到整體情況？ B：新軟體每天晚上會【匯總】六個檔案的數字，並產生一份總報告，讓經理們隔天早上就能閱讀。"},{"w":"accuracy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being correct and without mistakes","c":"準確性","s":"A: Why is the accounting team checking every number in the annual report again when they already finished it last Friday? B: The bank will use these figures to decide on our loan, so the manager wants to be sure of their accuracy before we send the report on Monday.","t":"A：會計團隊上週五已經完成年度報告了，為什麼還要再檢查每一個數字？ B：銀行會用這些數字來決定我們的貸款，所以經理想在週一寄出報告前確認它們的【準確性】。"},{"w":"consistency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of always being the same in style or method","c":"一致性","s":"A: Why did the manager return our quarterly report and ask us to change so many small details in the tables? B: She wants consistency across all the pages, so every table must use the same font, the same date style, and the same currency symbol from beginning to end.","t":"A：為什麼經理退回我們的季報，要我們修改表格中這麼多小細節？ B：她希望所有頁面保持【一致性】，所以每個表格從頭到尾都必須使用相同的字型、相同的日期樣式和相同的貨幣符號。"},{"w":"update","p":"v.","d":"to add the newest information to something","c":"更新","s":"A: The price list on our website still shows last year's prices, and three customers have already called to complain about it today. B: I'll update the table with the new prices right after lunch and ask the IT team to check that the website shows the correct numbers by this evening.","t":"A：我們網站上的價目表還顯示著去年的價格，今天已經有三位顧客打電話來抱怨了。 B：我午餐後馬上用新價格【更新】表格，並請資訊團隊確認網站在今晚前顯示正確的數字。"},{"w":"validation","p":"n.","d":"the process of checking that information is correct or acceptable","c":"驗證；確認","s":"A: How can we stop people from typing letters instead of numbers in the phone column of the sign-up sheet? B: We can add data validation to that column, so the sheet shows a warning message and refuses any entry that contains anything other than numbers.","t":"A：我們要怎麼防止大家在報名表的電話欄打字母而不是數字？ B：我們可以在那一欄加入資料【驗證】，這樣試算表就會顯示警告訊息，並拒絕任何包含數字以外內容的輸入。"},{"w":"numeric","p":"adj.","d":"made up of numbers","c":"數字的","s":"A: The new employee ID cards are ready, but why did the system reject the codes that Human Resources sent this morning? B: The system only accepts numeric codes with eight digits, and some of the codes from Human Resources included letters, so they need to be changed before printing.","t":"A：新的員工識別證準備好了，但為什麼系統拒絕了人資部今天早上傳來的代碼？ B：系統只接受八位數的【數字】代碼，而人資部有些代碼包含字母，所以在列印前需要修改。"},{"w":"text","p":"n.","d":"written words","c":"文字","s":"A: Why can't the spreadsheet add up the prices in column D, even though they all look like normal numbers? B: Someone saved them as text instead of numbers when they copied them from an email, so the program treats them like words and cannot calculate them.","t":"A：為什麼試算表無法加總D欄的價格，即使它們看起來都是正常的數字？ B：有人從電子郵件複製時把它們存成【文字】而不是數字，所以程式把它們當成字詞，無法計算。"},{"w":"missing","p":"adj.","d":"not there; lost or not included","c":"缺少的；遺漏的","s":"A: Why can't we send the shipping report to the customer yet, when the deadline is at five o'clock today? B: There are still some missing delivery dates in the table, so I'm calling the warehouse to get those details before we send anything to the client.","t":"A：今天的截止時間是五點，為什麼我們還不能把出貨報告寄給客戶？ B：表格中還有一些【缺少的】送貨日期，所以我正在打電話給倉庫索取那些細節，然後才會寄任何東西給客戶。"},{"w":"normalize","p":"v.","d":"to change data so that it all follows the same standard","c":"標準化；正規化","s":"A: Our offices in Japan, Korea, and the United States report sales in different currencies, so how can we compare them fairly? B: Before we build the chart, we should normalize all the figures by changing them into US dollars, so every office is measured in the same way.","t":"A：我們在日本、韓國和美國的辦公室用不同的貨幣回報銷售額，我們要怎麼公平比較？ B：在製作圖表之前，我們應該把所有數字換算成美元，將它們【標準化】，讓每個辦公室都用同樣的方式衡量。"},{"w":"export","p":"v.","d":"to move data from one program into a file another program can use","c":"匯出","s":"A: The accountant from the outside firm doesn't use our company's sales program, so how can we send her the figures? B: We can export the monthly sales table as an Excel file and email it to her, so she can open it easily on her own computer.","t":"A：外部事務所的會計師不使用我們公司的銷售程式，我們要怎麼把數字寄給她？ B：我們可以把每月銷售表【匯出】成Excel檔，再用電子郵件寄給她，這樣她就能在自己的電腦上輕鬆打開。"},{"w":"import","p":"v.","d":"to bring data from another file or program into the one you are using","c":"匯入","s":"A: The supplier sent us a list of five hundred new products, so do I need to type every item into our system by hand? B: No, you can import the whole file directly into the inventory program, which will take only a few minutes and avoid typing mistakes.","t":"A：供應商寄給我們一份五百項新產品的清單，我需要把每個品項都手動輸入系統嗎？ B：不用，你可以把整個檔案直接【匯入】庫存程式，只要幾分鐘，還能避免打字錯誤。"},{"w":"readability","p":"n.","d":"how easy something is to read","c":"可讀性；易讀性","s":"A: Several board members complained that last month's financial tables were too crowded and hard to follow during the meeting. B: This time, I'll improve the readability by using a larger font, adding more space between lines, and shading every other row in light gray.","t":"A：幾位董事抱怨上個月的財務表格太擁擠，開會時很難看懂。 B：這次我會使用較大的字型、增加行距，並把每隔一列塗上淺灰色，來提升表格的【可讀性】。"},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"something you look at to get information","c":"參考；參考資料","s":"A: Should I print the list of product codes for the new sales assistants who start working at the store on Monday? B: Yes, print a copy for each of them to keep near the cash register as a quick reference, because they won't remember all the codes during their first week.","t":"A：我應該為週一開始在店裡上班的新銷售助理列印產品代碼清單嗎？ B：是的，每人印一份放在收銀機旁當作快速【參考資料】，因為他們在第一週不會記得所有代碼。"}]},{"unit":98,"theme":"Day Off 休假日","cards":[{"w":"holiday","p":"n.","d":"a day when people do not go to work or school","c":"假日；節日","s":"A: Is the office going to be open next Monday, or should I tell my clients to call back on Tuesday instead? B: Monday is a national holiday, so the whole building will be closed, but our customer service team will still answer emails from home in the afternoon.","t":"A：辦公室下週一會開嗎？還是我應該請客戶改在週二再打來？ B：週一是國定【假日】，所以整棟大樓都會關閉，不過我們的客服團隊下午仍會在家回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"vacation","p":"n.","d":"a period of time spent away from work, often traveling","c":"假期；休假","s":"A: Why has Mr. Lee asked the receptionist to forward all of his urgent calls to his assistant for the next two weeks? B: He is taking a long vacation with his family in Japan, and he wants to enjoy the trip without worrying about work or checking his phone every hour.","t":"A：李先生為什麼要請接待員在接下來兩週把他所有的緊急電話轉給他的助理？ B：他要和家人去日本度一個長【假】，他想好好享受旅程，不用擔心工作，也不必每小時查看手機。"},{"w":"break","p":"n.","d":"a short time when you stop working to rest","c":"休息時間","s":"A: You have been sitting at your desk and typing that sales report since eight o'clock this morning, so aren't you tired? B: Yes, my eyes really hurt, so I'm going to take a short break and walk to the café downstairs for a coffee before I finish the last section.","t":"A：你從今天早上八點就坐在桌前打那份銷售報告，不累嗎？ B：累啊，我的眼睛真的很痛，所以我要稍微【休息】一下，走到樓下的咖啡廳買杯咖啡，再完成最後一部分。"},{"w":"leave","p":"n.","d":"time that you are allowed to be away from your job","c":"休假；假期","s":"A: Will Jessica be able to lead the training session for the new staff members at the end of this month? B: No, she has asked for two weeks of paid leave to look after her father after his operation, so Tom from the human resources team will run it instead.","t":"A：潔西卡這個月底能帶領新進員工的訓練課程嗎？ B：不行，她父親手術後她要照顧他，所以申請了兩週的帶薪【休假】，因此改由人資部門的湯姆來主持。"},{"w":"rest","p":"v.","d":"to stop working or moving so that your body can get better","c":"休息","s":"A: You look very pale after flying back from the trade fair in Berlin last night, so why did you come to the office today? B: I wanted to finish the report, but you are right, so I will go home early this afternoon and rest until tomorrow morning.","t":"A：你昨晚從柏林的貿易展飛回來後看起來臉色很蒼白，今天為什麼還來辦公室？ B：我想把報告完成，不過你說得對，所以我今天下午會早點回家，【休息】到明天早上。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to become calm and stop worrying","c":"放鬆","s":"A: What do you usually do after a long week of meetings with difficult customers and late nights at the office? B: On Friday evenings I like to sit on my balcony, listen to soft music, and relax with a cup of tea, because it helps me forget about work for a while.","t":"A：在和難搞的客戶開了一整週的會、又在辦公室待到很晚之後，你通常會做什麼？ B：週五晚上我喜歡坐在陽台上聽輕柔的音樂，喝杯茶【放鬆】一下，因為這能讓我暫時忘掉工作。"},{"w":"sleep in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to sleep later than usual in the morning","c":"睡懶覺；睡晚一點","s":"A: Are you going to join us for the early morning bike ride along the river this Saturday? B: I'm afraid not, because I've worked overtime every night this week, so I really want to sleep in until ten o'clock and then have a slow breakfast at home with my family.","t":"A：你這週六要跟我們一起去河邊騎清晨的腳踏車嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為我這週每天晚上都在加班，所以我真的很想【睡懶覺】到十點，然後在家跟家人悠閒地吃早餐。"},{"w":"nap","p":"n.","d":"a short sleep during the day","c":"小睡；午睡","s":"A: How do you stay so energetic during the afternoon when everyone else in the department looks tired after lunch? B: I usually take a twenty-minute nap in the quiet room on the fifth floor, and when I wake up, I can focus on my work again until six.","t":"A：午餐過後部門裡其他人都看起來很累，你下午怎麼還能那麼有精神？ B：我通常會在五樓的安靜室【小睡】二十分鐘，醒來後就能再專心工作到六點。"},{"w":"unwind","p":"v.","d":"to relax after a period of work or stress","c":"放鬆身心","s":"A: Why did the company decide to build a small garden with benches on the roof of the office building last year? B: The managers wanted to give employees a pleasant place where they could unwind during their lunch hour, because many people were feeling stressed by the heavy workload.","t":"A：公司去年為什麼決定在辦公大樓頂樓蓋一座有長椅的小花園？ B：主管們想給員工一個舒適的地方，讓他們可以在午休時間【放鬆身心】，因為很多人被繁重的工作量壓得很有壓力。"},{"w":"recharge","p":"v.","d":"to get back your energy by resting","c":"恢復精力；充電","s":"A: Why are you taking three days off right after the busy product launch, when there are still so many emails to answer? B: I've been working twelve hours a day for a month, so I need time to recharge at the beach before I start planning the next big project with the team.","t":"A：產品發表會忙完後還有那麼多郵件要回，你為什麼馬上要請三天假？ B：我已經連續一個月每天工作十二小時了，所以在和團隊開始規劃下一個大案子之前，我需要時間在海邊【充電】一下。"},{"w":"refresh","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less tired or hot","c":"使恢復精神；使清爽","s":"A: The workshop has been going on for three hours, so should we continue with the next topic or stop for a while? B: Let's stop for fifteen minutes so everyone can get some fresh air and refresh themselves with cold drinks, and then we'll start the discussion about the new budget.","t":"A：工作坊已經進行三個小時了，我們要繼續下一個主題還是先停一下？ B：我們休息十五分鐘，讓大家呼吸新鮮空氣、喝杯冷飲【提神】一下，然後再開始討論新預算。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"time when you are not working and can do what you enjoy","c":"休閒；空閒","s":"A: Why do so many young engineers want to work for that software company even though the salary is not very high? B: The company gives its staff a four-day work week, so they have more leisure time to spend with friends, play sports, or learn new skills outside the office.","t":"A：那家軟體公司薪水不算高，為什麼這麼多年輕工程師想去那裡工作？ B：公司讓員工一週只上四天班，所以他們有更多【休閒】時間可以和朋友相處、運動，或在辦公室以外學習新技能。"},{"w":"free time","p":"n.phr.","d":"time when you do not have to work or study","c":"空閒時間","s":"A: Do you have any plans for the long weekend, or are you going to stay in the city and catch up on work? B: I'm going to spend most of my free time at the community center, where I teach English to children, because I really enjoy helping them learn.","t":"A：連假你有什麼計畫嗎？還是要待在城裡把工作補完？ B：我打算把大部分的【空閒時間】花在社區中心，在那裡教小朋友英文，因為我真的很喜歡幫助他們學習。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"嗜好；興趣","s":"A: I noticed the beautiful photos of mountains on the wall of your office, so did a professional photographer take them? B: No, I took them myself, because photography has been my favorite hobby since college, and I usually go hiking with my camera at least twice a month.","t":"A：我注意到你辦公室牆上那些漂亮的山景照片，是專業攝影師拍的嗎？ B：不是，是我自己拍的，因為攝影從大學起就是我最喜歡的【嗜好】，我通常每個月至少帶著相機去爬山兩次。"},{"w":"outing","p":"n.","d":"a short trip that a group takes for fun","c":"出遊；遠足","s":"A: What did the human resources department organize for the staff after the company reached its sales target this year? B: They planned a one-day outing to a farm in the mountains, where we picked strawberries, had a barbecue lunch, and played team games until the bus took us home.","t":"A：公司今年達成銷售目標後，人資部門為員工安排了什麼活動？ B：他們規劃了到山上農場的一日【出遊】，我們在那裡採草莓、吃烤肉午餐，還玩團隊遊戲，直到巴士載我們回家。"},{"w":"trip","p":"n.","d":"a journey to a place and back again","c":"旅行；行程","s":"A: Where did you go during the holiday last week, and why do you have so many photos of old temples on your phone? B: My wife and I took a short trip to Kyoto, where we visited several famous temples, tried local food, and stayed in a traditional guesthouse near the river.","t":"A：上週放假你去了哪裡？為什麼你手機裡有那麼多古廟的照片？ B：我和太太去京都做了一趟短期【旅行】，我們參觀了幾座有名的寺廟，品嚐當地美食，還住在河邊一間傳統民宿。"},{"w":"travel","p":"v.","d":"to go from one place to another, often far away","c":"旅行；行進","s":"A: Why did you decide to take all of your annual leave at once instead of using a few days each month? B: I want to travel around South America for three weeks, and I need enough time to visit several countries without rushing from one airport to another.","t":"A：你為什麼決定一次把年假全部休完，而不是每個月用幾天？ B：我想在南美洲【旅行】三週，我需要足夠的時間去好幾個國家，才不用匆匆忙忙從一個機場趕到另一個機場。"},{"w":"picnic","p":"n.","d":"a meal that you eat outdoors, often in a park","c":"野餐","s":"A: The weather forecast says it will be sunny and warm on Sunday, so do you have any plans with your family? B: We're going to have a picnic in the park near the lake, so my husband is making sandwiches and I'm going to bring fruit, drinks, and a big blanket to sit on.","t":"A：氣象預報說星期天會晴朗溫暖，你跟家人有什麼計畫嗎？ B：我們要在湖邊的公園【野餐】，所以我先生在做三明治，我會帶水果、飲料和一條可以坐的大毯子。"},{"w":"movie","p":"n.","d":"a story shown in moving pictures at a cinema or on TV","c":"電影","s":"A: What did you and your coworkers do after you finished the big project on Friday evening? B: We went to see a new movie at the cinema near the station, and after that we had dinner together at an Italian restaurant and talked about our plans for next year.","t":"A：週五晚上大案子結束後，你和同事們做了什麼？ B：我們去車站附近的電影院看了一部新【電影】，之後一起在一家義大利餐廳吃晚餐，聊了明年的計畫。"},{"w":"read","p":"v.","d":"to look at and understand written words","c":"閱讀；讀","s":"A: How do you usually spend your Sunday mornings when you don't have to go into the office? B: I like to sit in a quiet café near my apartment and read a good novel for a few hours, because it helps me forget about my busy job and feel calm.","t":"A：不用進辦公室的星期天早上，你通常怎麼度過？ B：我喜歡坐在我公寓附近一間安靜的咖啡館，【閱讀】一本好小說幾個小時，因為這能讓我忘掉忙碌的工作，感到平靜。"},{"w":"watch","p":"v.","d":"to look at something for a period of time","c":"觀看","s":"A: Are you coming to the team dinner on Saturday night, or do you have other plans with your friends? B: Sorry, I can't come, because my friends and I are going to watch the final game of the basketball season at a sports bar downtown, and we booked a table weeks ago.","t":"A：你週六晚上會來團隊聚餐嗎？還是你跟朋友有別的計畫？ B：抱歉，我不能去，因為我和朋友要去市中心的運動酒吧【看】籃球季的總決賽，我們幾週前就訂好位子了。"},{"w":"cook","p":"v.","d":"to make food ready to eat by heating it","c":"烹煮；做飯","s":"A: Why do you bring your own lunch to the office every day instead of eating at the restaurant downstairs with us? B: I enjoy spending Sunday afternoons in my kitchen, where I cook healthy meals for the whole week, and it also saves me a lot of money each month.","t":"A：你為什麼每天都自己帶午餐到公司，而不跟我們在樓下的餐廳吃？ B：我喜歡星期天下午待在廚房，【煮】好一整週的健康餐點，而且這樣每個月也能幫我省下不少錢。"},{"w":"clean","p":"v.","d":"to remove dirt from something","c":"打掃；清潔","s":"A: You told me you were too busy to go out on Saturday, so what did you have to do all day? B: My parents are coming to stay with me next week, so I had to clean the whole apartment, wash the curtains, and buy new towels for the guest room.","t":"A：你說你週六忙到不能出門，那你一整天要做什麼？ B：我爸媽下週要來住我家，所以我得把整間公寓【打掃】乾淨、洗窗簾，還要幫客房買新毛巾。"},{"w":"exercise","p":"v.","d":"to move your body to stay healthy and strong","c":"運動","s":"A: How do you manage to stay so healthy when you work such long hours at the bank every day? B: I try to exercise for at least an hour on my days off, usually by swimming at the sports center or jogging in the park, and I also walk to work when the weather is nice.","t":"A：你每天在銀行工作那麼長的時間，怎麼還能保持這麼健康？ B：我休假時盡量至少【運動】一小時，通常是去運動中心游泳或在公園慢跑，天氣好的時候我也會走路上班。"},{"w":"walk","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere on foot; to take an animal out on foot","c":"走路；遛（狗）","s":"A: Your dog looks very happy and healthy, but how do you find time to take care of it with your busy work schedule? B: I always walk him along the river early in the morning before work, and on weekends we spend a few hours in the big park near my home.","t":"A：你的狗看起來很開心又健康，但工作那麼忙，你怎麼有時間照顧牠？ B：我總是在上班前一大早沿著河邊【遛】牠，週末我們則會在我家附近的大公園待上幾個小時。"},{"w":"shop","p":"v.","d":"to go to stores to buy things","c":"購物；買東西","s":"A: Why are you leaving the office so early on a Friday afternoon when the manager is still in a meeting? B: I took a half day off because I need to shop for a new suit before my sister's wedding next week, and the stores in the mall get very crowded in the evening.","t":"A：經理還在開會，你為什麼週五下午這麼早就離開辦公室？ B：我請了半天假，因為下週我姊姊結婚前我得去【買】一套新西裝，而購物中心的店晚上會非常擁擠。"},{"w":"visit","p":"v.","d":"to go to see a person or place","c":"探望；參觀","s":"A: Do you have any plans for the Lunar New Year holiday, or will you stay in Taipei and relax at home? B: I'm going to take the high-speed train to Tainan to visit my grandparents, who I haven't seen since last summer because I've been so busy with my new job.","t":"A：農曆新年假期你有什麼計畫嗎？還是會待在台北在家休息？ B：我要搭高鐵去台南【探望】我的祖父母，因為新工作太忙，我從去年夏天就沒見過他們了。"},{"w":"gather","p":"v.","d":"to come together in one place as a group","c":"聚集；團聚","s":"A: What does your family usually do on the national holiday in October, when everyone has the day off? B: All of my relatives gather at my uncle's house in the countryside, where we cook a big lunch together, play cards, and share news about our jobs and children.","t":"A：十月國定假日大家都放假時，你們家通常做什麼？ B：我所有的親戚都會【聚集】在我叔叔鄉下的房子，我們一起煮一頓豐盛的午餐、打牌，並分享彼此工作和孩子的近況。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable for a special day or event","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Why is the restaurant on the top floor of the hotel fully booked for this Friday evening? B: Our company has reserved the whole place to celebrate its twentieth anniversary, and the president has invited all employees, their families, and some of our most important clients.","t":"A：飯店頂樓的餐廳這週五晚上為什麼全部被訂滿了？ B：我們公司包下整間餐廳來【慶祝】成立二十週年，總裁邀請了全體員工、他們的家人，以及一些我們最重要的客戶。"},{"w":"lazy","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to work or do anything active","c":"懶散的；慵懶的","s":"A: Did you do anything special on your day off yesterday, like going to the beach or visiting the new museum? B: No, it was a lazy day, because I stayed in my pajamas until noon, ordered pizza for lunch, and watched television on the sofa for most of the afternoon.","t":"A：你昨天休假有做什麼特別的事嗎？像是去海邊或參觀新的博物館？ B：沒有，那是【懶散】的一天，因為我穿著睡衣待到中午，午餐叫了披薩，下午大部分時間都在沙發上看電視。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and calm, without noise or trouble","c":"寧靜的；和平的","s":"A: Why did you choose that small hotel in the mountains for your vacation instead of a big resort by the sea? B: I wanted a peaceful place far away from traffic and crowds, where I could wake up to the sound of birds and walk in the forest without hearing any phones ring.","t":"A：你為什麼選擇山上那間小旅館度假，而不是海邊的大型度假村？ B：我想要一個遠離車流和人潮的【寧靜】地方，可以在鳥叫聲中醒來，在森林裡散步時也聽不到任何電話響。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making very little noise","c":"安靜的","s":"A: Where do you go when you want to read or think about a problem without any noise or interruptions? B: I usually go to the public library near my apartment, because the reading room on the third floor is always quiet, even on busy Saturday afternoons when many students are studying there.","t":"A：當你想看書或思考問題、不想被噪音或打擾時，你會去哪裡？ B：我通常去我公寓附近的公立圖書館，因為三樓的閱覽室總是很【安靜】，即使在很多學生念書的忙碌週六下午也是。"},{"w":"restful","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel calm and rested","c":"悠閒的；使人放鬆的","s":"A: How was your long weekend at the hot spring hotel that the company gave you as a reward for your hard work? B: It was very restful, because I slept well, enjoyed the warm water every evening, and didn't check my work email once, so I feel full of energy today.","t":"A：公司為了獎勵你的辛勞送你去溫泉飯店過的那個連假怎麼樣？ B：非常【悠閒放鬆】，因為我睡得很好，每天晚上都享受溫泉，而且一次都沒查看工作郵件，所以我今天覺得精力充沛。"},{"w":"refreshing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel less tired, hot or bored","c":"提神的；清爽的","s":"A: Why do you go swimming in the outdoor pool every Saturday morning, even in the cold winter months? B: The cold water feels really refreshing after a long week in the office, and it wakes up my body and mind, so I feel ready for the weekend afterwards.","t":"A：你為什麼每週六早上都去戶外泳池游泳，連寒冷的冬天也一樣？ B：在辦公室忙了一整週後，冷水讓人覺得非常【清爽提神】，它能喚醒我的身體和頭腦，讓我之後覺得準備好迎接週末。"}]},{"unit":99,"theme":"Decision 決定","cards":[{"w":"choice","p":"n.","d":"the act of picking one thing from several","c":"選擇","s":"A: Why did the marketing team pick the small hotel by the lake for next month's training retreat instead of the big resort downtown? B: It was an easy choice, because the hotel offered a quiet meeting room, free parking and lower prices, and most staff wanted to get away from the busy city for a few days.","t":"A：行銷團隊為什麼選擇湖邊的小旅館作為下個月培訓營的地點，而不是市中心的大型度假村？ B：這是個很容易的【選擇】，因為那家旅館提供安靜的會議室、免費停車和較低的價格，而且大多數員工都想離開繁忙的城市幾天。"},{"w":"option","p":"n.","d":"one of the things you can choose","c":"選項；可選擇的事物","s":"A: The client in Osaka still hasn't received the replacement parts, so what can we do before their factory line stops on Friday? B: The fastest option is to send the parts by air freight today; it costs more than shipping by sea, but they will arrive by Wednesday morning.","t":"A：大阪的客戶還沒收到替換零件，在他們的工廠生產線週五停工之前我們能做什麼？ B：最快的【選項】是今天用空運寄出零件；雖然比海運貴，但週三早上就能送達。"},{"w":"selection","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that you can choose from","c":"可供挑選的品項；選擇","s":"A: Have you decided where to take the visiting buyers from Germany for dinner after the trade show on Thursday evening? B: Yes, I booked the seafood restaurant near the harbor, because it has a wide selection of local dishes and a private room where we can talk about the contract quietly.","t":"A：你決定好週四晚上商展結束後，要帶來訪的德國買家去哪裡吃晚餐了嗎？ B：決定了，我訂了港口附近的海鮮餐廳，因為那裡的在地菜餚【選擇】很多，還有一間包廂讓我們可以安靜地討論合約。"},{"w":"judgment","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make good decisions; an opinion","c":"判斷；判斷力","s":"A: Should we accept the supplier's offer of a lower price if we sign a five-year contract with them today? B: I trust your judgment on this, since you have worked with them for many years, but please check their delivery record carefully before you make the final call.","t":"A：如果我們今天和供應商簽五年合約，他們願意降價，我們應該接受嗎？ B：這件事我相信你的【判斷】，因為你和他們合作很多年了，但在做最後決定前，請仔細檢查他們的交貨紀錄。"},{"w":"conclusion","p":"n.","d":"a decision you make after thinking about the facts","c":"結論","s":"A: What did the research team say after they studied the customer survey results for almost three weeks? B: They came to the conclusion that young customers care more about fast delivery than low prices, so they suggest that we open a second warehouse in the north next year.","t":"A：研究團隊花了將近三週研究顧客調查結果後，他們怎麼說？ B：他們得出的【結論】是年輕顧客比起低價更在乎快速到貨，所以他們建議我們明年在北部開設第二座倉庫。"},{"w":"resolution","p":"n.","d":"a solution to a problem or an argument","c":"解決；解決方案","s":"A: Did the two department heads finally agree on how to share the meeting rooms on the third floor? B: Yes, after a long and tense discussion yesterday afternoon, they reached a resolution: sales will use the rooms in the morning and the design team will use them after lunch.","t":"A：兩位部門主管對於如何共用三樓會議室，最後達成共識了嗎？ B：有，昨天下午經過漫長又緊張的討論後，他們達成了【解決方案】：業務部早上使用會議室，設計團隊則在午餐後使用。"},{"w":"plan","p":"n.","d":"an idea of what you will do and how you will do it","c":"計畫","s":"A: The office is moving to the new building next month, so how will we keep serving customers during the move? B: Our manager has a clear plan: half of the team will work from home each week, while the others pack boxes and answer phone calls at the old office.","t":"A：辦公室下個月要搬到新大樓，搬家期間我們要怎麼繼續服務客戶？ B：我們經理有一個清楚的【計畫】：每週一半的團隊在家工作，另一半則在舊辦公室打包箱子並接聽電話。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a careful plan for reaching a goal","c":"策略","s":"A: Sales of our sports drinks dropped by twenty percent last year, so what is the new marketing director going to change? B: Her strategy is to stop paying for TV ads and spend the money on online videos with young athletes, because most of our customers are under thirty.","t":"A：我們的運動飲料去年銷量下滑了百分之二十，新的行銷總監打算改變什麼？ B：她的【策略】是停止投放電視廣告，把錢花在與年輕運動員合作的網路影片上，因為我們大部分的顧客都不到三十歲。"},{"w":"policy","p":"n.","d":"a set of official rules of a company or government","c":"政策；規定","s":"A: Can I bring my dog to the office on Fridays, like the employees do at the design company next door? B: I'm afraid not, because our company policy does not allow pets in the building, since some workers have allergies and we often have important clients visiting.","t":"A：我可以像隔壁設計公司的員工那樣，週五帶我的狗來辦公室嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為我們公司的【政策】不允許寵物進入大樓，有些員工會過敏，而且我們常有重要客戶來訪。"},{"w":"decide","p":"v.","d":"to make a choice after thinking","c":"決定","s":"A: Why is the hiring manager still interviewing people for the accountant position after three weeks of meetings? B: She needs to decide between two excellent candidates, one with more experience and one who speaks Japanese, and the director wants her answer by Monday at the latest.","t":"A：面試了三週，為什麼招聘經理還在面試會計職位的應徵者？ B：她必須在兩位優秀的候選人之間做【決定】，一位經驗比較豐富，另一位會說日文，而總監最晚週一就要她的答覆。"},{"w":"choose","p":"v.","d":"to pick one thing or person from a group","c":"選擇；挑選","s":"A: The company is giving each employee a free gift for the tenth anniversary, so what are the options this year? B: You can choose a pair of wireless headphones, a coffee machine or a shopping voucher, but you must fill out the online form before the end of this month.","t":"A：公司在十週年時要送每位員工一份免費禮物，今年有哪些選項？ B：你可以【選擇】一副無線耳機、一台咖啡機或一張購物禮券，但必須在這個月底前填好線上表格。"},{"w":"select","p":"v.","d":"to choose carefully from a group","c":"挑選；選出","s":"A: How will the committee decide which staff members get to attend the leadership course in Singapore next spring? B: They will select five people based on their sales results and their managers' reports, and the company will pay for their flights, hotel rooms and meals.","t":"A：委員會要如何決定哪些員工可以參加明年春天在新加坡的領導力課程？ B：他們會根據業績和主管的報告【挑選】五個人，公司會支付他們的機票、飯店房間和餐費。"},{"w":"determine","p":"v.","d":"to find out the facts about something","c":"確定；查明","s":"A: Why did the airline cancel the flight to Taipei this afternoon even though the weather looks fine now? B: The engineers found a problem with one engine, and they need a few hours to determine what caused it before the plane can safely carry passengers again.","t":"A：現在天氣看起來還不錯，航空公司為什麼取消今天下午飛往台北的班機？ B：工程師發現其中一具引擎有問題，他們需要幾個小時來【查明】原因，飛機才能再次安全載客。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to find a way to end a problem","c":"解決","s":"A: Why has the IT team been working so late every night this week while the rest of us go home at six? B: They are trying to resolve a serious problem with the online payment system, because many customers cannot finish their orders and the company is losing money every hour.","t":"A：為什麼這週我們其他人六點就下班，資訊團隊卻每晚都工作到很晚？ B：他們正在努力【解決】線上付款系統的一個嚴重問題，因為很多顧客無法完成訂單，公司每小時都在虧錢。"},{"w":"weigh","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about the good and bad points","c":"權衡；考慮","s":"A: Are you going to accept the job offer from the bank in Hong Kong, or will you stay with our company? B: I haven't answered yet, because I need to weigh the higher salary against the long working hours and the cost of moving my whole family to another city.","t":"A：你要接受香港那家銀行的工作邀約，還是會留在我們公司？ B：我還沒回覆，因為我需要【權衡】較高的薪水和長時間工作，以及全家搬到另一個城市的費用。"},{"w":"consider","p":"v.","d":"to think about something before deciding","c":"考慮","s":"A: The printer in the sales office breaks down almost every week, so should we just call the repair company again? B: I think we should consider buying a new one instead, because the repairs have already cost us more than a new machine, and the staff waste a lot of time waiting.","t":"A：業務辦公室的印表機幾乎每週都故障，我們應該再打電話給維修公司嗎？ B：我覺得我們應該【考慮】改買一台新的，因為維修費已經比一台新機器還貴，而且員工浪費很多時間在等待。"},{"w":"evaluate","p":"v.","d":"to judge how good or useful something is","c":"評估；評價","s":"A: How does the hotel know whether the new front desk staff are doing a good job with guests? B: Every three months, the manager will evaluate their work by reading online reviews, watching how they handle check-ins and asking guests to fill out a short survey at checkout.","t":"A：飯店怎麼知道新的櫃台人員對待客人是否表現良好？ B：每三個月，經理會透過閱讀網路評論、觀察他們如何處理入住手續，以及請客人在退房時填寫簡短問卷，來【評估】他們的工作。"},{"w":"assess","p":"v.","d":"to study something to judge its amount or value","c":"評估；估算","s":"A: The storm last night broke several windows at our warehouse, so when can we start moving the goods back inside? B: The insurance company is sending an expert this morning to assess the damage, and we can start cleaning only after she takes photos and writes her report.","t":"A：昨晚的暴風雨打破了倉庫好幾扇窗戶，我們什麼時候可以開始把貨物搬回裡面？ B：保險公司今天早上會派一位專家來【評估】損害，等她拍照並寫好報告後，我們才能開始清理。"},{"w":"deliberate","p":"v.","d":"to think about or discuss something carefully before deciding","c":"仔細考慮；商議","s":"A: Why haven't we heard anything from the city council about our plan to build a parking lot behind the store? B: The council members will deliberate for at least two more weeks, because many local residents are worried about traffic and noise, and they want to hear every opinion first.","t":"A：關於我們打算在店後方蓋停車場的計畫，為什麼市議會到現在都還沒有任何消息？ B：議員們至少還要再【商議】兩週，因為很多當地居民擔心交通和噪音問題，他們想先聽取每一種意見。"},{"w":"hesitate","p":"v.","d":"to wait a moment before doing something because you are not sure","c":"猶豫；遲疑","s":"A: I'm new here and I still don't understand how to use the booking system for the meeting rooms on this floor. B: Please don't hesitate to ask me or anyone on the team for help, because we all had the same trouble during our first week, and we're happy to show you.","t":"A：我是新來的，還不太懂怎麼使用這層樓會議室的預約系統。 B：請不要【猶豫】，儘管向我或團隊任何人求助，因為我們第一週都遇過同樣的困難，很樂意教你。"},{"w":"doubt","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of not being sure about something","c":"懷疑；疑慮","s":"A: Do you think the new shopping mall will really open on time in December, as the developer promised in the newspaper? B: I have some doubt about it, because when I drove past yesterday, the workers were still building the roof, and the parking area wasn't finished at all.","t":"A：你覺得新的購物中心真的會像開發商在報紙上承諾的那樣，在十二月準時開幕嗎？ B：我對此有些【懷疑】，因為我昨天開車經過時，工人還在蓋屋頂，停車場也完全還沒完工。"},{"w":"uncertain","p":"adj.","d":"not sure; not yet decided","c":"不確定的","s":"A: Has the director said whether the company will open the new branch in Vietnam next year? B: Not yet; the future of the project is still uncertain, because the cost of land has gone up quickly and the board wants to see the new sales numbers before it agrees.","t":"A：總監有說公司明年是否會在越南開新分公司嗎？ B：還沒有，這個專案的未來仍然【不確定】，因為土地成本上漲得很快，董事會想先看新的銷售數字再同意。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure that something will happen or that you can do it","c":"有信心的","s":"A: How do you feel about giving the presentation to the investors from London tomorrow morning? B: I feel quite confident now, because I practiced it three times with my team this week, and our sales results for the last quarter are the best in the company's history.","t":"A：明天早上要向倫敦來的投資人做簡報，你感覺如何？ B：我現在覺得相當【有信心】，因為我這週和團隊練習了三次，而且我們上一季的業績是公司史上最好的。"},{"w":"firm","p":"adj.","d":"strong and not likely to change","c":"堅定的；堅決的","s":"A: The customer keeps asking for a bigger discount, so should we lower the price again to keep his business? B: No, we need to be firm this time, because we already gave him fifteen percent off, and other buyers will expect the same deal if we agree again.","t":"A：那位客戶一直要求更大的折扣，我們應該再降價來留住他的生意嗎？ B：不，這次我們必須【堅定】，因為我們已經給他打了八五折，如果再答應，其他買家也會期待同樣的優惠。"},{"w":"final","p":"adj.","d":"last; not able to be changed","c":"最後的；最終的","s":"A: Can I still change the colors on the new product packaging, or is it too late now? B: I'm sorry, but the design you sent on Tuesday was the final version, and the factory has already started printing fifty thousand boxes for the summer sales season.","t":"A：我還可以修改新產品包裝的顏色嗎？還是現在已經太遲了？ B：很抱歉，你週二寄來的設計就是【最終】版本，工廠已經開始為夏季銷售旺季印製五萬個盒子了。"},{"w":"careful","p":"adj.","d":"giving a lot of attention to avoid mistakes","c":"小心的；謹慎的","s":"A: The new contract with the shipping company is almost forty pages long, so can I just sign it this afternoon? B: Please be careful and read every page first, because last year we signed a contract too quickly and later found out that we had to pay extra fees for weekend deliveries.","t":"A：和貨運公司的新合約將近四十頁，我可以今天下午直接簽嗎？ B：請【小心】，先把每一頁都看過，因為去年我們太快簽約，後來才發現週末送貨必須額外付費。"},{"w":"wise","p":"adj.","d":"showing good sense and good judgment","c":"明智的","s":"A: Do you think I should ask my manager for a raise this week, right after the company announced that profits fell? B: It might not be wise to ask now; it would be better to wait until the end of the year, when everyone's performance is reviewed and the budget is clearer.","t":"A：公司才剛宣布獲利下滑，你覺得我這週應該向經理要求加薪嗎？ B：現在提出可能不太【明智】；最好等到年底大家的績效評估完、預算也比較明確的時候再說。"},{"w":"logical","p":"adj.","d":"sensible and based on clear reasons","c":"合理的；合乎邏輯的","s":"A: Why did the company move its call center from the city center to the small town near the airport? B: It was a logical step, because the rent there is much cheaper, many young people in the town need jobs, and our managers can easily fly in from head office.","t":"A：公司為什麼把客服中心從市中心搬到機場附近的小鎮？ B：這是很【合理】的一步，因為那裡的租金便宜得多，鎮上很多年輕人需要工作，而且我們的主管可以很方便地從總公司搭機過來。"},{"w":"practical","p":"adj.","d":"useful and suitable for real situations","c":"實用的；實際的","s":"A: The architect wants to put glass walls in every meeting room of our new office, so what do you think of her design? B: It looks beautiful, but it isn't very practical, because the rooms will get too hot in summer, and people won't have any privacy during interviews or salary talks.","t":"A：建築師想在新辦公室的每間會議室都裝玻璃牆，你覺得她的設計怎麼樣？ B：看起來很漂亮，但不太【實用】，因為夏天會議室會太熱，而且面試或談薪水時大家都沒有隱私。"},{"w":"consequence","p":"n.","d":"a result of something, often a bad one","c":"後果；結果","s":"A: What happened after the restaurant forgot to check the temperature of its fridges during the long holiday weekend? B: As a consequence, it had to throw away almost all of its fresh meat and fish, and it stayed closed for two days until new food arrived from the supplier.","t":"A：那家餐廳在連假期間忘了檢查冰箱溫度，後來發生了什麼事？ B：【結果】它幾乎得把所有生鮮肉類和魚都丟掉，而且關店兩天，直到供應商送來新的食材。"},{"w":"outcome","p":"n.","d":"the final result of an event or process","c":"結果；成果","s":"A: How did the negotiations with the Korean electronics company go after three long days of meetings in Seoul? B: The outcome was better than we expected, because they agreed to buy our software for all of their factories and to sign a contract for at least four years.","t":"A：在首爾開了漫長的三天會議後，與那家韓國電子公司的談判結果如何？ B：【結果】比我們預期的好，因為他們同意為旗下所有工廠購買我們的軟體，並簽下至少四年的合約。"},{"w":"factor","p":"n.","d":"one of the things that affects a result or decision","c":"因素","s":"A: Why did you choose the apartment near the train station, even though it is smaller and older than the one by the river? B: The most important factor for me was the short commute, because I start work at seven every morning and I don't want to spend two hours in traffic.","t":"A：靠河邊那間公寓比較新也比較大，你為什麼還是選擇車站附近的那間？ B：對我來說最重要的【因素】是通勤時間短，因為我每天早上七點就要上班，不想在路上塞兩個小時。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"something that is more important than other things","c":"優先事項；首要之務","s":"A: There are so many tasks on my list this week, so which one should I work on first? B: Your top priority is the price report for the client meeting on Thursday; the training slides and the team schedule can wait until next week if you don't have enough time.","t":"A：我這週清單上的工作好多，我應該先做哪一項？ B：你的首要【優先事項】是週四客戶會議要用的價格報告；如果時間不夠，培訓投影片和團隊排班表可以等到下週再做。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which each side gives up part of what it wants","c":"妥協；折衷辦法","s":"A: The sales team wanted a bigger budget for travel, and the finance team wanted to cut costs, so what did the director decide? B: She found a compromise: the sales staff can travel to meet important clients, but they must take economy flights and stay in cheaper hotels.","t":"A：業務團隊想要更多差旅預算，財務團隊卻想削減成本，總監最後怎麼決定？ B：她找到了一個【折衷辦法】：業務人員可以出差拜訪重要客戶，但必須搭經濟艙並住比較便宜的飯店。"}]},{"unit":100,"theme":"Decoration 裝潢佈置","cards":[{"w":"redesign","p":"v.","d":"to plan and change the look or layout of something again","c":"重新設計","s":"A: Our customers keep saying the waiting area in the bank looks old and dark, so what is the manager planning to do about it this year? B: She has hired an architect to redesign the whole space, adding bright lights, softer chairs and a small coffee corner so that people feel more relaxed while they wait.","t":"A：客戶一直說銀行的等候區看起來又舊又暗，經理今年打算怎麼處理？ B：她請了一位建築師來【重新設計】整個空間，加入明亮的燈光、更柔軟的椅子和一個小咖啡角，讓人們等候時感覺更放鬆。"},{"w":"utilitarian","p":"adj.","d":"made to be useful and practical, not beautiful","c":"實用的；講求實效的","s":"A: Why does the new staff kitchen look so plain, with only metal shelves, white walls and simple plastic chairs instead of nice decorations? B: The building manager wanted a utilitarian room that is easy to clean and cheap to repair, because hundreds of workers use it every day and things break quickly.","t":"A：新的員工廚房為什麼看起來這麼簡陋，只有金屬架、白牆和簡單的塑膠椅，而沒有漂亮的裝飾？ B：大樓經理想要一個好清潔、修理又便宜的【實用】空間，因為每天有數百名員工使用，東西很快就會壞。"},{"w":"style","p":"n.","d":"a particular way something is designed or looks","c":"風格；樣式","s":"A: The new hotel owner asked us to choose furniture for the lobby, but I'm not sure whether we should buy modern pieces or classic ones. B: Let's look at the building first, because the outside has old stone walls and tall windows, so a classic style would probably match the guests' expectations better than bright plastic chairs.","t":"A：新飯店老闆請我們為大廳挑選家具，但我不確定該買現代款還是經典款。 B：我們先看看建築本身吧，外觀有古老的石牆和高窗，所以經典的【風格】可能比鮮豔的塑膠椅更符合客人的期待。"},{"w":"taste","p":"n.","d":"the ability to choose things that look good","c":"品味；鑑賞力","s":"A: Do you think the client will like the dark green walls and gold lamps that our team chose for her new restaurant downtown? B: I'm a little worried, because she told us during the first meeting that she has simple taste and prefers light colors, so we should prepare a second plan just in case.","t":"A：你覺得客戶會喜歡我們團隊為她市中心新餐廳挑選的深綠色牆面和金色燈具嗎？ B：我有點擔心，因為她在第一次開會時告訴我們，她的【品味】簡約、偏好淺色，所以我們應該準備第二套方案以防萬一。"},{"w":"measurement","p":"n.","d":"the size or length of something that you find by measuring","c":"測量；尺寸","s":"A: Can we order the new carpet for the conference room today, or do we need to wait until the designer visits again next week? B: We should wait, because the designer needs to take an exact measurement of the floor first, and if the numbers are wrong, the store won't let us return the carpet.","t":"A：我們今天可以訂會議室的新地毯嗎，還是要等設計師下週再來？ B：我們應該等，因為設計師得先做精確的地板【測量】，如果數字錯了，店家不會讓我們退貨。"},{"w":"impetus","p":"n.","d":"a reason or force that makes something happen","c":"動力；推動力","s":"A: Why did the company finally decide to renovate the old office after talking about it for almost five years without doing anything? B: The impetus came from a staff survey last spring, which showed that many employees felt tired and unhappy in the dark rooms, so the directors knew they had to act quickly.","t":"A：公司談了將近五年都沒有行動，為什麼最後決定翻修舊辦公室？ B：【動力】來自去年春天的員工調查，調查顯示許多員工在昏暗的房間裡感到疲倦和不快樂，所以董事們知道必須迅速採取行動。"},{"w":"comfort","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant, relaxed feeling with no pain or worry","c":"舒適；舒服","s":"A: Why are we spending so much money on new sofas and soft lights for the waiting room at the dental clinic this year? B: Many patients feel nervous before their treatment, so the clinic manager believes that their comfort is very important, and a warm, relaxing room helps them feel calmer while they wait.","t":"A：今年我們為什麼要花這麼多錢為牙科診所的候診室添購新沙發和柔和燈光？ B：許多病患在治療前會感到緊張，所以診所經理認為他們的【舒適】非常重要，溫暖放鬆的空間能幫助他們在等候時比較冷靜。"},{"w":"slipcover","p":"n.","d":"a cloth cover that fits over a sofa or chair and can be removed","c":"（家具的）活動布套；沙發套","s":"A: The sofas in the hotel lounge have coffee stains all over them, but we don't have the budget to buy new ones this year, do we? B: No, but we can order a washable slipcover for each sofa, which costs much less, protects the old material and can be cleaned easily in the hotel laundry.","t":"A：飯店交誼廳的沙發上到處都是咖啡漬，但我們今年沒有預算買新的，對吧？ B：沒錯，不過我們可以為每張沙發訂一個可水洗的【沙發套】，便宜很多，又能保護舊布料，還能在飯店洗衣房輕鬆清洗。"},{"w":"capture","p":"v.","d":"to show or express a feeling or quality well","c":"捕捉；表現出","s":"A: What do you want the new lobby design to show visitors when they walk into our office building for the first time? B: We want it to capture the spirit of our company, so the designer is using bright colors, local art and plenty of plants to show that we are creative and friendly.","t":"A：訪客第一次走進我們的辦公大樓時，你希望新大廳的設計向他們展現什麼？ B：我們希望它能【捕捉】公司的精神，所以設計師使用鮮豔的色彩、在地藝術和大量植物，來展現我們有創意又友善。"},{"w":"variation","p":"n.","d":"a slightly different form or version of something","c":"變化；變化版本","s":"A: The client said she likes the blue design for the reception area, but she is worried it will feel too cold in winter. B: Then let's show her a variation of the same plan, with warmer wood colors and softer lighting, so she can compare both versions before she makes her final decision on Friday.","t":"A：客戶說她喜歡接待區的藍色設計，但擔心冬天會感覺太冷。 B：那我們就給她看同一方案的另一個【變化版本】，用比較溫暖的木頭色和更柔和的燈光，讓她在星期五做最後決定前可以比較兩個版本。"},{"w":"freshen","p":"v.","d":"to make something look newer, cleaner or more attractive","c":"使煥然一新；使清新","s":"A: The meeting room looks old and boring, but we only have a small budget and two days before the investors arrive, right? B: That's right, so we can freshen up the room with a few green plants, new cushions and a coat of light paint instead of buying expensive new furniture.","t":"A：會議室看起來又舊又無聊，但我們預算不多，而且投資人兩天後就要來了，對吧？ B：對，所以我們可以用幾盆綠色植物、新靠墊和一層淺色油漆讓房間【煥然一新】，而不是買昂貴的新家具。"},{"w":"vibe","p":"n.","d":"the feeling or mood that a place gives you","c":"氛圍；感覺","s":"A: What kind of feeling should the new café near the university have, since most of the customers will be students and young office workers? B: The owner wants a relaxed and friendly vibe, so the designer is adding soft music, wooden tables and big windows that let in lots of natural light during the day.","t":"A：大學附近的新咖啡廳應該營造什麼樣的感覺？因為大部分客人會是學生和年輕上班族。 B：老闆想要輕鬆友善的【氛圍】，所以設計師加入了輕柔的音樂、木頭桌子，以及白天能讓大量自然光進來的大窗戶。"},{"w":"impression","p":"n.","d":"the opinion or feeling you get about someone or something","c":"印象","s":"A: Why is the manager so worried about the old carpet and broken lamps in the reception area before Monday's meeting? B: Important clients are visiting us for the first time, and the reception area is the first thing they see, so she wants them to get a good impression of our company right away.","t":"A：經理為什麼在星期一的會議前這麼擔心接待區的舊地毯和壞掉的燈？ B：重要客戶第一次來拜訪，接待區是他們最先看到的地方，所以她希望他們馬上對我們公司留下好【印象】。"},{"w":"minimalism","p":"n.","d":"a way of designing that uses very few, simple things","c":"極簡主義","s":"A: Why does the new office have so few decorations, with only white walls, one long table and a single plant in the corner? B: The founder is a big fan of minimalism, and she believes that a simple space with fewer objects helps employees focus better and keeps the office easy to clean and organize.","t":"A：新辦公室為什麼只有白牆、一張長桌和角落一盆植物，裝飾這麼少？ B：創辦人非常喜歡【極簡主義】，她相信物品較少的簡單空間能幫助員工更專心，也讓辦公室容易清潔和整理。"},{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following old ways or styles that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統的","s":"A: The hotel in Kyoto wants to update its guest rooms, but do they plan to make everything look modern like a city hotel? B: No, they want to keep the traditional wooden doors and paper screens, because many foreign tourists choose the hotel because it shows the local culture and history.","t":"A：京都的那家飯店想翻新客房，他們打算把一切都改得像城市飯店一樣現代嗎？ B：不，他們想保留【傳統的】木門和紙屏風，因為很多外國遊客選擇這家飯店，正是因為它展現了當地的文化和歷史。"},{"w":"elaborate","p":"adj.","d":"having many small parts or details; carefully planned","c":"精心製作的；複雜精緻的","s":"A: Did you see the plans for the new ballroom at the hotel, with gold lamps, painted walls and carved columns everywhere? B: Yes, the design is very elaborate, and it will take the workers at least six months to finish, but the owner believes it will attract many rich couples who want luxury weddings.","t":"A：你看過飯店新宴會廳的設計圖嗎？到處都是金色燈具、彩繪牆面和雕刻柱子。 B：看過，設計非常【精緻複雜】，工人至少要六個月才能完成，但老闆相信它會吸引許多想辦豪華婚禮的有錢新人。"},{"w":"fancy","p":"adj.","d":"expensive, decorated, or not simple","c":"花俏的；高級的","s":"A: Should we buy expensive crystal lights and velvet chairs for the new staff break room on the third floor? B: I don't think we need anything fancy, because employees just want a clean, quiet place to eat lunch and rest, so simple tables and soft chairs will be more than enough.","t":"A：我們應該為三樓新的員工休息室買昂貴的水晶燈和天鵝絨椅子嗎？ B：我覺得不需要任何【花俏的】東西，因為員工只想要一個乾淨安靜、能吃午餐和休息的地方，所以簡單的桌子和柔軟的椅子就綽綽有餘了。"},{"w":"molding","p":"n.","d":"a decorative strip of wood or plaster along the edge of a wall or ceiling","c":"（牆面或天花板的）裝飾線條；飾條","s":"A: The walls in the old meeting room look a little plain, but the manager doesn't want to change the paint color, does she? B: No, she likes the cream color, so we suggested adding white wooden molding along the top of the walls, which will make the room look more stylish without much cost.","t":"A：舊會議室的牆看起來有點單調，但經理不想換油漆顏色，對嗎？ B：對，她喜歡奶油色，所以我們建議沿著牆的上緣加裝白色木製【飾條】，不用花太多錢就能讓房間看起來更有格調。"},{"w":"flaw","p":"n.","d":"a small mark or fault that makes something not perfect","c":"瑕疵；缺陷","s":"A: Why did the store manager refuse to accept the new marble tables that arrived at the shop this morning? B: She checked each table carefully and found a small flaw on the surface of almost every one, so she sent them back and asked the supplier to deliver perfect ones before the opening.","t":"A：店長今天早上為什麼拒收送到店裡的新大理石桌？ B：她仔細檢查了每張桌子，發現幾乎每張表面都有小【瑕疵】，所以她退貨並要求供應商在開幕前送來完美的桌子。"},{"w":"weary","p":"adj.","d":"tired, or bored with something after a long time","c":"厭倦的；疲倦的","s":"A: Why does the director want to change the colors and furniture in the main office after only three years? B: She said many employees feel weary of the gray walls and dark desks, and she hopes brighter colors and more plants will give everyone more energy during long working days.","t":"A：主管為什麼才過三年就想更換主辦公室的顏色和家具？ B：她說許多員工對灰色牆面和深色辦公桌感到【厭倦】，她希望更明亮的顏色和更多植物能讓大家在漫長的工作日裡更有活力。"},{"w":"illumination","p":"n.","d":"light, or the way a place is lit","c":"照明；光線","s":"A: The art gallery wants to show its new paintings next month, but the visitors complained that the rooms were too dark last time. B: Then we should improve the illumination in every room by adding soft spotlights above each painting, so people can see the colors clearly without hurting their eyes.","t":"A：美術館下個月要展出新畫作，但上次參觀者抱怨展間太暗。 B：那我們應該在每個展間的每幅畫上方加裝柔和的聚光燈來改善【照明】，讓人們能清楚看到色彩，又不會傷眼睛。"},{"w":"contemporary","p":"adj.","d":"modern; belonging to the present time","c":"當代的；現代的","s":"A: The bank wants its new branch to attract young customers, so what kind of design did the architect suggest at yesterday's meeting? B: She suggested a contemporary look with glass walls, simple furniture and digital screens, because younger people usually prefer spaces that feel up-to-date rather than old-fashioned.","t":"A：銀行希望新分行能吸引年輕客戶，那建築師在昨天的會議上建議了什麼樣的設計？ B：她建議採用【當代的】風貌，有玻璃牆、簡約家具和數位螢幕，因為年輕人通常喜歡感覺新穎而非老派的空間。"},{"w":"futuristic","p":"adj.","d":"looking very modern, as if from the future","c":"未來感的；未來派的","s":"A: Have you seen the new showroom that the electric car company opened downtown last week? B: Yes, it has a very futuristic design, with silver walls, blue lights and robots that greet visitors at the door, so it really feels like walking into a science fiction movie set in the next century.","t":"A：你看過那家電動車公司上週在市中心開的新展示廳嗎？ B：看過，設計非常【有未來感】，有銀色牆面、藍色燈光，還有在門口迎接訪客的機器人，真的感覺像走進一部以下個世紀為背景的科幻電影。"},{"w":"redecoration","p":"n.","d":"the work of painting and decorating a place again","c":"重新裝潢；重新佈置","s":"A: Why is the hotel restaurant closed for the whole month of March, even though it is usually very busy in spring? B: The restaurant is closed for redecoration, because the owners are painting the walls, replacing the old curtains and buying new tables, and they want everything to look fresh before the summer season.","t":"A：飯店餐廳為什麼整個三月都不營業，明明春天通常很忙？ B：餐廳因【重新裝潢】而暫停營業，因為業主正在粉刷牆面、更換舊窗簾、購買新桌子，他們希望在夏季旺季前讓一切煥然一新。"},{"w":"drapes","p":"n.","d":"long, heavy curtains","c":"（厚重的）窗簾；簾幕","s":"A: The sunlight in the meeting room is so strong in the afternoon that nobody can see the slides on the screen clearly. B: I'll ask the office manager to order some heavy drapes for the windows, so we can close them during presentations and open them again when we want natural light.","t":"A：會議室下午的陽光太強，沒人能看清楚螢幕上的投影片。 B：我會請辦公室經理為窗戶訂一些厚重的【窗簾】，這樣我們簡報時可以拉上，想要自然光時再拉開。"},{"w":"fabric","p":"n.","d":"cloth used for making clothes, curtains, or furniture covers","c":"布料；織物","s":"A: Which material should we choose for the new chairs in the hotel lobby, leather or something softer? B: I'd choose a strong fabric that is easy to clean, because hundreds of guests sit in the lobby every day, and leather can get scratched quickly by bags and suitcases.","t":"A：飯店大廳的新椅子該選哪種材質，皮革還是更柔軟的東西？ B：我會選容易清潔的耐用【布料】，因為每天有數百位客人坐在大廳，皮革很容易被包包和行李箱刮傷。"},{"w":"elongated","p":"adj.","d":"longer and thinner than usual","c":"加長的；狹長的","s":"A: The meeting room is very long and narrow, so what kind of table do you think will fit best for our weekly team meetings? B: An elongated oval table would be perfect, because it follows the shape of the room, leaves space to walk around, and lets twelve people sit together and see the screen.","t":"A：會議室又長又窄，你覺得什麼樣的桌子最適合我們每週的團隊會議？ B：【加長形的】橢圓桌會很完美，因為它順著房間的形狀，留有走動的空間，還能讓十二個人坐在一起看螢幕。"},{"w":"ceiling","p":"n.","d":"the top inside surface of a room","c":"天花板","s":"A: The new office feels a little dark and crowded, even though it has large windows and white walls, so what else can we do? B: We could paint the ceiling a very light color and hang a few simple lamps from it, because that will make the room look taller and much brighter.","t":"A：新辦公室雖然有大窗戶和白牆，還是感覺有點暗又擁擠，我們還能做什麼？ B：我們可以把【天花板】漆成很淺的顏色，再從上面吊幾盞簡單的燈，這樣房間會看起來更高也更明亮。"},{"w":"refreshing","p":"adj.","d":"pleasantly new and different","c":"令人耳目一新的；清新的","s":"A: What did the staff say about the new green walls and plants in the break room after the renovation was finished? B: Most of them said it was a refreshing change from the old gray room, and many people now enjoy spending their lunch break there instead of eating at their desks.","t":"A：翻修完成後，員工對休息室新的綠色牆面和植物有什麼看法？ B：大部分人說，和以前灰暗的房間相比，這是個【令人耳目一新的】改變，現在很多人喜歡在那裡度過午休，而不是在座位上吃飯。"},{"w":"exterior","p":"n.","d":"the outside part of a building or object","c":"外部；外觀","s":"A: The inside of our store looks great after the renovation, but why are customers still walking past without coming in? B: I think the exterior of the building still looks old and dirty, so we should paint the front, clean the windows and add a bright new sign above the door.","t":"A：我們店內翻修後看起來很棒，但為什麼客人還是走過不進來？ B：我想是建築物的【外部】還是看起來又舊又髒，所以我們應該粉刷店面、清洗窗戶，並在門上方加一塊明亮的新招牌。"},{"w":"interior","p":"n.","d":"the inside part of a building or room","c":"內部；室內","s":"A: The new hotel looks very plain from the street, so why are so many travel magazines writing about it this month? B: The interior is what makes it special, because every guest room and hallway is decorated with local art, colorful tiles and handmade furniture from nearby villages.","t":"A：新飯店從街上看起來很平凡，為什麼這個月有這麼多旅遊雜誌報導它？ B：它的【內部】才是特別之處，因為每間客房和走廊都用在地藝術、彩色磁磚和附近村莊的手工家具裝飾。"},{"w":"appearance","p":"n.","d":"the way someone or something looks","c":"外觀；外表","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner spend so much money changing the tables, lights and wall colors when the food was already popular? B: She knew that the appearance of a restaurant matters as much as the menu, because customers often decide whether to come inside after a quick look through the front window.","t":"A：餐廳的餐點已經很受歡迎了，老闆為什麼還要花這麼多錢更換桌子、燈具和牆面顏色？ B：她知道餐廳的【外觀】和菜單一樣重要，因為客人常常從前窗快速看一眼後，就決定要不要進來。"},{"w":"preference","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that you like one thing more than another","c":"偏好；喜好","s":"A: Before we start choosing colors and furniture for the new manager's office, should we ask her what she likes? B: Yes, we should send her a short survey first, because she will work in that room every day, and her preference for light or dark colors will affect all our other choices.","t":"A：在我們開始為新經理的辦公室挑選顏色和家具之前，是否應該問問她喜歡什麼？ B：是的，我們應該先寄一份簡短的問卷給她，因為她每天都會在那個房間工作，她對淺色或深色的【偏好】會影響我們其他所有的選擇。"},{"w":"elegant","p":"adj.","d":"beautiful in a simple and graceful way","c":"優雅的；高雅的","s":"A: What did the guests say about the hotel's new wedding hall when they visited it for the first time last weekend? B: They loved it, and many of them said it looked simple but very elegant, with soft white lights, tall windows, and beautiful flowers on every table near the stage.","t":"A：客人上週末第一次參觀飯店新的婚宴廳時，他們怎麼說？ B：他們很喜歡，很多人說它看起來簡約卻非常【優雅】，有柔和的白光、高大的窗戶，舞台附近每張桌上都有美麗的花。"}]},{"unit":101,"theme":"Dependent 依賴","cards":[{"w":"reliance","p":"n.","d":"the state of needing someone or something","c":"依賴；信賴","s":"A: Why is the board so worried about the new supplier in Vietnam, even though their prices are lower than everyone else's? B: Our reliance on a single factory for all our parts is risky, because if they close for a week, our whole production line in Taichung will stop.","t":"A：為什麼董事會這麼擔心越南的新供應商，即使他們的價格比其他人都低？ B：我們所有零件都【依賴】單一工廠，風險很高，因為如果他們停工一週，我們在台中的整條生產線就會停擺。"},{"w":"rely","p":"v.","d":"to trust or need someone or something","c":"依靠；信賴","s":"A: Who should I ask to check the sales figures before I send the quarterly report to the head office tomorrow morning? B: You can rely on Kevin in accounting, because he always finds small mistakes that other people miss, and he never complains about extra work.","t":"A：明天早上把季報寄給總公司之前，我該請誰檢查銷售數字？ B：你可以【依靠】會計部的凱文，因為他總能找出別人漏掉的小錯誤，而且他從不抱怨額外的工作。"},{"w":"dependency","p":"n.","d":"a need for something in order to work or exist","c":"依賴（性）；依存關係","s":"A: Why did the IT manager say that the new booking system might cause problems for the hotel next month? B: It has a dependency on an old payment program that will stop receiving updates soon, so we must replace that program before the busy holiday season begins.","t":"A：為什麼資訊經理說新的訂房系統下個月可能會給飯店帶來問題？ B：它對一套很快就不再更新的舊付款程式有【依存關係】，所以我們必須在忙碌的假期旺季開始之前替換掉那套程式。"},{"w":"depend","p":"v.","d":"to be decided by something; to need someone or something","c":"取決於；依賴","s":"A: Will the company picnic still take place at the riverside park on Saturday, or should I cancel the bus I booked for the staff? B: It will depend on the weather, so let's check the forecast on Friday afternoon and make a final decision before everyone leaves the office.","t":"A：公司野餐週六還會在河濱公園舉行嗎？還是我應該取消為員工預訂的巴士？ B：那要【取決於】天氣，所以我們週五下午查一下天氣預報，在大家下班前做最後決定。"},{"w":"reliant","p":"adj.","d":"needing someone or something in order to succeed","c":"依賴的","s":"A: Why is the restaurant owner trying so hard to attract more local customers this year? B: The business has been too reliant on foreign tourists, and when fewer visitors came last winter, sales dropped by half, so she wants a more stable group of regular diners.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳老闆今年這麼努力想吸引更多本地顧客？ B：這家店過去太【依賴】外國觀光客，去年冬天遊客變少時，營業額掉了一半，所以她想要一群更穩定的常客。"},{"w":"interdependent","p":"adj.","d":"needing each other in order to work well","c":"相互依存的","s":"A: Why can't the marketing team simply launch the campaign without waiting for the product designers to finish? B: The two departments are completely interdependent, because the ads need the final package design, and the designers need our customer research to choose the right colors.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊不能直接推出活動，而不用等產品設計師完成？ B：這兩個部門是完全【相互依存】的，因為廣告需要最終的包裝設計，而設計師需要我們的顧客研究來選擇合適的顏色。"},{"w":"codependent","p":"adj.","d":"needing each other too much in an unhealthy way","c":"過度互相依賴的","s":"A: Why did the consultant suggest that the two sales managers should stop working as a pair next quarter? B: She said their working relationship had become codependent, because neither of them would make any decision alone, and the rest of the team was waiting days for simple answers.","t":"A：為什麼顧問建議那兩位業務經理下一季不要再搭檔工作？ B：她說他們的工作關係已經變得【過度互相依賴】，因為兩人都不肯獨自做任何決定，團隊其他人要等好幾天才能得到簡單的答覆。"},{"w":"contingent","p":"adj.","d":"depending on something else happening first","c":"視…而定的；取決於…的","s":"A: Has the bank finally approved the loan for our new warehouse near the port, or are we still waiting for their answer? B: The loan is contingent on a successful safety inspection of the building, so we cannot sign the contract until the inspector visits next Thursday.","t":"A：銀行終於核准我們港口附近新倉庫的貸款了嗎？還是我們還在等他們的答覆？ B：這筆貸款【取決於】大樓能否通過安全檢查，所以在檢查員下週四來之前，我們不能簽約。"},{"w":"conditional","p":"adj.","d":"happening only if certain things are done first","c":"有條件的","s":"A: Did the candidate from Singapore accept our job offer for the new project manager position last Friday? B: Her acceptance is conditional, because she will only join us if we let her work from home two days a week and pay for her moving costs.","t":"A：那位來自新加坡的應徵者上週五接受我們新專案經理職位的錄取了嗎？ B：她的接受是【有條件的】，因為只有我們讓她每週在家工作兩天並支付她的搬家費用，她才會加入。"},{"w":"needy","p":"adj.","d":"poor and needing help","c":"貧困的；需要幫助的","s":"A: What is the company going to do with all the office furniture and laptops left over after the move? B: We plan to give them to a charity that helps needy families in the neighborhood, so children can use the laptops for their schoolwork at home.","t":"A：搬遷後剩下的辦公家具和筆電，公司打算怎麼處理？ B：我們計畫把它們捐給一家幫助附近【貧困】家庭的慈善機構，讓孩子們可以在家用筆電做功課。"},{"w":"vulnerable","p":"adj.","d":"easily hurt or attacked","c":"易受傷害的；脆弱的","s":"A: Why does the IT department want every employee to change their passwords again this month? B: Some of our older computers are vulnerable to a new type of online attack, and if hackers get in, they could steal customer data and damage our reputation.","t":"A：為什麼資訊部這個月又要每位員工更改密碼？ B：我們有些較舊的電腦很【容易受到】一種新型網路攻擊，如果駭客入侵，他們可能會竊取顧客資料並損害我們的聲譽。"},{"w":"supported","p":"adj.","d":"helped or kept working by someone or something","c":"受支援的；有支持的","s":"A: Can I still use my old tablet to open the new sales app that the company introduced last week? B: Unfortunately, that model is no longer supported, so the app will not install on it, and you should ask the IT desk for a newer device.","t":"A：我還能用舊平板開啟公司上週推出的新銷售應用程式嗎？ B：很遺憾，那個型號已經不再【受支援】，所以應用程式無法安裝，你應該向資訊服務台申請一台較新的裝置。"},{"w":"subsidy","p":"n.","d":"money from the government to help pay for something","c":"補助金","s":"A: How can a small bakery like ours afford those expensive new energy-saving ovens this year? B: The city government offers a subsidy to small businesses that reduce their electricity use, so it will pay about forty percent of the cost if we apply before June.","t":"A：像我們這樣的小麵包店，今年怎麼負擔得起那些昂貴的新節能烤箱？ B：市政府提供【補助金】給減少用電的小型企業，所以如果我們在六月前申請，它會支付約百分之四十的費用。"},{"w":"assistance","p":"n.","d":"help","c":"協助；幫助","s":"A: What should I do if a passenger at the gate needs a wheelchair but our ground staff are all busy with boarding? B: Call the airport service desk and request assistance, and they will send someone within ten minutes to help the passenger reach the plane safely.","t":"A：如果登機門有旅客需要輪椅，但我們的地勤人員都在忙登機，我該怎麼辦？ B：打電話給機場服務台請求【協助】，他們會在十分鐘內派人來幫助旅客安全登機。"},{"w":"maintenance","p":"n.","d":"work done to keep something in good condition","c":"維修；保養","s":"A: Why are the elevators in the east wing closed all day, and when will they be working again? B: The building manager scheduled regular maintenance for this morning, and the technicians said they need to replace some parts, so the elevators should reopen by five o'clock.","t":"A：為什麼東側大樓的電梯整天關閉？什麼時候會恢復運作？ B：大樓管理員安排今天早上進行定期【維修保養】，技術人員說需要更換一些零件，所以電梯應該在五點前重新開放。"},{"w":"sustenance","p":"n.","d":"food and drink needed to stay alive","c":"食物；糧食；營養","s":"A: Why did the volunteers bring so many boxes of rice, canned food, and bottled water to the village after the flood? B: Many families lost their crops and kitchens in the storm, so they needed basic sustenance until the roads opened and the local markets could start selling food again.","t":"A：為什麼志工在水災後帶了這麼多箱米、罐頭和瓶裝水到村子裡？ B：許多家庭在暴風雨中失去了農作物和廚房，所以在道路通車、當地市場重新開始賣食物之前，他們需要基本的【糧食】。"},{"w":"caretaker","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks after a building or another person","c":"管理員；照顧者","s":"A: Who should I contact if the heating in the community center stops working during the weekend workshop? B: Call the caretaker, Mr. Lin, because he lives in the small house next to the building, and he has keys to every room and the boiler.","t":"A：如果週末工作坊期間社區中心的暖氣壞了，我該聯絡誰？ B：打給【管理員】林先生，因為他住在大樓旁的小房子裡，而且他有每個房間和鍋爐的鑰匙。"},{"w":"guardian","p":"n.","d":"a person who is legally responsible for a child","c":"監護人；守護者","s":"A: Can the high school student who applied for our summer internship sign the contract by himself? B: No, because he is only seventeen, a parent or legal guardian must also sign the form before he can start working in our office in July.","t":"A：申請我們暑期實習的那位高中生可以自己簽合約嗎？ B：不行，因為他只有十七歲，他的父母或法定【監護人】也必須在表格上簽名，他才能七月開始在我們辦公室工作。"},{"w":"beneficiary","p":"n.","d":"a person who receives money or help from something","c":"受益人","s":"A: Why does the insurance company need me to fill out this extra page before my new policy starts? B: You must name a beneficiary, the person who will receive the money if something happens to you, and most people choose their husband, wife, or children.","t":"A：為什麼保險公司要我在新保單生效前填寫這額外的一頁？ B：你必須指定一位【受益人】，也就是萬一你發生什麼事時會收到這筆錢的人，大多數人會選擇丈夫、妻子或子女。"},{"w":"client","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays for a service","c":"客戶；委託人","s":"A: Why do you have to leave the office so early this afternoon when we still have a lot of work to finish? B: I'm meeting an important client from Tokyo at the airport, and then I'll take her to dinner to discuss next year's advertising contract.","t":"A：我們還有很多工作要完成，你今天下午為什麼要這麼早離開辦公室？ B：我要去機場接一位來自東京的重要【客戶】，然後帶她去吃晚餐，討論明年的廣告合約。"},{"w":"attachment","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of love for someone or something","c":"依戀；附件","s":"A: Why doesn't the manager want to move the team to the bright new building across the street? B: He has a strong attachment to the old office, because he started the company there twenty years ago, and every room reminds him of the early days.","t":"A：為什麼經理不想把團隊搬到對街明亮的新大樓？ B：他對舊辦公室有很深的【依戀】，因為二十年前他在那裡創立公司，每個房間都讓他想起創業初期的日子。"},{"w":"autonomy","p":"n.","d":"the freedom to make your own decisions","c":"自主權；自治","s":"A: Why do so many young engineers want to join the small design studio instead of the big electronics company? B: The studio gives its staff more autonomy, so they can choose their own projects and working hours, while the big company makes every decision at the top.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多年輕工程師想加入那家小型設計工作室，而不是大型電子公司？ B：工作室給員工更多【自主權】，他們可以選擇自己的專案和工作時間，而大公司的每個決定都由高層做出。"},{"w":"independence","p":"n.","d":"the freedom to live or act without help from others","c":"獨立；自主","s":"A: Why did your sister decide to rent her own apartment downtown even though the rent is so expensive? B: After she got her first full-time job at the bank, she wanted more independence, so she could cook, travel, and plan her life without asking our parents first.","t":"A：你姊姊為什麼決定在市中心自己租公寓，即使房租那麼貴？ B：她在銀行找到第一份全職工作後，想要更多【獨立】，這樣她就可以不必先問爸媽，自己做飯、旅行和規劃生活。"},{"w":"obligation","p":"n.","d":"something you must do because of a law, rule, or promise","c":"義務；責任","s":"A: Do I really have to stay at the company for two more years after it paid for my master's degree? B: Yes, you signed an agreement, so you have an obligation to work here until 2028, or you must pay back the full cost of the course.","t":"A：公司幫我付了碩士學費之後，我真的必須再留在公司兩年嗎？ B：是的，你簽了協議，所以你有【義務】在這裡工作到2028年，否則你必須償還全部課程費用。"},{"w":"responsibility","p":"n.","d":"a duty to deal with or take care of something","c":"責任；職責","s":"A: Who will handle customer complaints while the service manager is on vacation in Europe next month? B: Linda will take responsibility for answering all complaints, and she will report any serious problems directly to the general manager every Friday afternoon by email.","t":"A：服務經理下個月去歐洲度假期間，誰會處理顧客投訴？ B：琳達會負起回覆所有投訴的【責任】，並在每週五下午用電子郵件直接向總經理報告任何嚴重問題。"},{"w":"backing","p":"n.","d":"support, especially money or approval","c":"支持；資助","s":"A: How did such a small start-up manage to open three new shops in Taipei in only one year? B: They got strong financial backing from a large investment company, which gave them enough money to rent good locations and hire experienced staff.","t":"A：這麼小的新創公司怎麼能在短短一年內在台北開三家新店？ B：他們得到一家大型投資公司強力的資金【支持】，給了他們足夠的錢租下好地點並雇用有經驗的員工。"},{"w":"provision","p":"n.","d":"the act of supplying something; a rule in a contract or law","c":"提供；條款","s":"A: Does our new office lease say anything about who pays if the air conditioning breaks down in summer? B: Yes, there is a provision in section six which says that the landlord must repair all major equipment within three working days at his own cost.","t":"A：我們新的辦公室租約有提到夏天冷氣壞了由誰付錢嗎？ B：有，第六節有一項【條款】寫明房東必須在三個工作天內自費修理所有主要設備。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"protection from danger or loss; a feeling of being safe","c":"保障；安全","s":"A: Why did you leave a well-paid job at the start-up to work for the government tax office? B: The start-up paid more, but I wanted job security, because my wife and I just bought a house and we cannot risk losing my income next year.","t":"A：你為什麼離開新創公司的高薪工作，去政府稅務局上班？ B：新創公司薪水比較高，但我想要工作【保障】，因為我和太太剛買了房子，我們不能冒明年失去收入的風險。"},{"w":"fallback","p":"n.","d":"a plan or choice you can use if the first one fails","c":"備案；退路","s":"A: What will we do if the hotel cancels our conference room booking at the last minute again? B: We have a fallback, because the university near the station agreed to rent us a lecture hall, so the event can still go ahead on the same day.","t":"A：如果飯店又在最後一刻取消我們的會議室預訂，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們有【備案】，因為車站附近的大學同意租給我們一間演講廳，所以活動仍然可以在同一天舉行。"},{"w":"dependence","p":"n.","d":"the state of needing something or someone","c":"依賴","s":"A: Why is the government spending so much money on solar and wind farms along the west coast? B: It wants to reduce the country's dependence on imported oil and gas, because prices change so quickly, and a sudden increase can hurt factories and families.","t":"A：為什麼政府在西海岸的太陽能和風力發電場上花這麼多錢？ B：政府想減少國家對進口石油和天然氣的【依賴】，因為價格變動太快，突然上漲會傷害工廠和家庭。"}]},{"unit":102,"theme":"Description Letter 描述信","cards":[{"w":"detail","p":"n.","d":"a small fact or piece of information","c":"細節","s":"A: Did the hotel send us any information about the meeting rooms before we sign the contract for next month's sales conference? B: Yes, the manager wrote a long letter that describes every detail of the main hall, including the number of seats, the lighting and the sound system, so we can plan everything easily.","t":"A：在我們簽下下個月業務會議的合約之前，飯店有寄來任何關於會議室的資料嗎？ B：有，經理寫了一封長信，描述主廳的每一個【細節】，包括座位數、燈光和音響系統，所以我們可以輕鬆規劃一切。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear or easy to understand","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Why did the customer write to us again this week after we had already replaced her broken coffee machine? B: She wanted to explain that the new machine makes a loud noise every morning, and she asked us to send a technician to her café before the weekend rush begins.","t":"A：我們已經更換了她壞掉的咖啡機，為什麼那位顧客這週又寫信給我們？ B：她想【說明】新機器每天早上都會發出很大的噪音，並要求我們在週末人潮開始前派一位技師到她的咖啡店。"},{"w":"mention","p":"v.","d":"to speak or write about something briefly","c":"提到；提及","s":"A: Did the new employee's letter of introduction say anything about her previous work in Japan? B: Yes, she was careful to mention that she worked for a travel agency in Tokyo for three years, which is very useful because we are planning to open a branch office there next spring.","t":"A：新員工的自我介紹信有提到她以前在日本的工作嗎？ B：有，她特別【提到】她曾在東京一家旅行社工作三年，這非常有用，因為我們計畫明年春天在那裡開設分公司。"},{"w":"introduce","p":"v.","d":"to tell people someone's name or present something new","c":"介紹；引進","s":"A: How should I start the letter to the new supplier in Vietnam, since we have never worked with them before? B: To begin with, you should introduce yourself and our company in a few short sentences, and after that describe the products we need and the date when we hope to receive them.","t":"A：因為我們以前從未和越南的新供應商合作過，我該如何開始寫給他們的信？ B：一開始，你應該用幾句簡短的話【介紹】你自己和我們公司，之後再描述我們需要的產品以及希望收到貨的日期。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to let others have or know something you have","c":"分享","s":"A: Why is the marketing manager asking all the staff to write about their trip to the trade fair in Singapore last month? B: She wants everyone to share their ideas and photos in a short letter, so she can put the best parts in the company newsletter that goes out in December.","t":"A：行銷經理為什麼要求所有員工寫下上個月去新加坡參加貿易展的經過？ B：她希望每個人都能在一封簡短的信中【分享】他們的想法和照片，這樣她就能把最精彩的部分放進十二月發行的公司電子報。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"something that happens to you and affects how you feel","c":"經驗；經歷","s":"A: What did the guest write in the letter she sent to the hotel manager after her stay last weekend? B: She described her experience at the hotel in a very positive way, saying the staff were friendly, the room was spotless, and breakfast was the best she had ever had on a business trip.","t":"A：那位客人上週末住宿後寄給飯店經理的信裡寫了什麼？ B：她以非常正面的方式描述了她在飯店的【經驗】，說員工很友善、房間一塵不染，而且早餐是她出差以來吃過最好的。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"a planned public or social occasion","c":"活動；事件","s":"A: Why does the director want a letter describing last Friday's charity dinner for the company website? B: The event raised more than ten thousand dollars for the local children's hospital, and she believes that a clear description with photos will encourage more employees to join us next year.","t":"A：為什麼主任想要一封描述上週五慈善晚宴的信放在公司網站上？ B：這場【活動】為當地兒童醫院募得超過一萬美元，她相信附上照片的清楚描述會鼓勵更多員工明年加入我們。"},{"w":"situation","p":"n.","d":"the things that are happening at a certain time and place","c":"情況；處境","s":"A: Why did the store manager send such a long letter to the head office in Taipei yesterday afternoon? B: She needed to describe the situation at her branch after the heavy rain, because water came into the storage room and damaged boxes of shoes worth several thousand dollars.","t":"A：店長昨天下午為什麼寄了一封這麼長的信給台北總公司？ B：她需要描述大雨過後她分店的【情況】，因為水流進了倉庫，損壞了價值數千美元的好幾箱鞋子。"},{"w":"story","p":"n.","d":"a description of events that happened","c":"故事；經過","s":"A: What will the company newsletter include this month, now that the new factory in Kaohsiung is open at last? B: It will tell the story of how the building team completed the project two months early, with interviews and photos showing how hard everyone worked during the hot summer.","t":"A：既然高雄的新工廠終於開幕了，這個月的公司電子報會包含什麼內容？ B：它會講述建廠團隊如何提早兩個月完成工程的【故事】，並附上訪談和照片，呈現大家在炎熱夏天裡有多努力工作。"},{"w":"background","p":"n.","d":"a person's education, family and past experience","c":"背景","s":"A: What should I write in the first part of my cover letter for the accountant position at the bank? B: You should describe your educational background, including your degree in finance, and after that talk about the jobs you have had and the skills you learned in each one.","t":"A：應徵銀行會計職位的求職信第一段我應該寫什麼？ B：你應該描述你的學歷【背景】，包括你的財務學位，之後再談談你做過的工作以及在每份工作中學到的技能。"},{"w":"appearance","p":"n.","d":"the way someone or something looks","c":"外觀；外表","s":"A: Why did the landlord send us a letter with so many photos of the office before we signed the lease? B: He wanted to show the appearance of the rooms after the repairs, because the old carpet was replaced, the walls were painted white and new lights were put in every room.","t":"A：為什麼房東在我們簽租約前寄給我們一封附有這麼多辦公室照片的信？ B：他想展示房間修繕後的【外觀】，因為舊地毯換掉了，牆壁漆成白色，而且每個房間都裝了新的燈。"},{"w":"feature","p":"n.","d":"an important or interesting part of something","c":"特色；特點","s":"A: What did the sales team say in the letter they sent to customers about the new laptop model? B: They described the most important feature, which is a battery that lasts up to twenty hours, so people who travel often can work all day without looking for a place to charge it.","t":"A：業務團隊寄給顧客的那封關於新款筆電的信裡說了什麼？ B：他們描述了最重要的【特色】，也就是電池可以持續長達二十小時，所以常出差的人可以工作一整天而不用找地方充電。"},{"w":"characteristic","p":"n.","d":"a typical quality of a person or thing","c":"特質；特徵","s":"A: Why does the human resources manager want a letter describing each candidate before the last interviews next week? B: She wants to know the main characteristic of each person, like whether they are patient, organized or creative, so she can decide who would work best with the current team.","t":"A：為什麼人資經理希望在下週最後一輪面試前，收到一封描述每位應徵者的信？ B：她想知道每個人的主要【特質】，像是他們是否有耐心、有條理或有創意，這樣她才能決定誰最適合與現有團隊合作。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the feeling or mood of a place","c":"氣氛；氛圍","s":"A: How did the restaurant owner describe her new café in the letter she sent to the local newspaper? B: She said the atmosphere is warm and relaxing, with soft music, comfortable chairs and big windows, so it is a good place for people to meet friends or work quietly on weekday afternoons.","t":"A：餐廳老闆在寄給當地報紙的信中如何描述她的新咖啡店？ B：她說店裡的【氣氛】溫暖又放鬆，有輕柔的音樂、舒適的椅子和大片窗戶，所以是人們平日下午和朋友見面或安靜工作的好地方。"},{"w":"environment","p":"n.","d":"the conditions around you where you live or work","c":"環境","s":"A: Why did so many employees write positive letters about the company's new head office this year? B: They like the working environment much better now, because the office has fresh plants, quiet meeting rooms and a kitchen where everyone can have lunch together instead of eating at their desks.","t":"A：為什麼今年有這麼多員工寫信讚美公司的新總部？ B：他們現在更喜歡這個工作【環境】，因為辦公室有新鮮的植物、安靜的會議室，還有一間大家可以一起吃午餐的廚房，而不用在座位上吃。"},{"w":"location","p":"n.","d":"the place where something is","c":"地點；位置","s":"A: Why did the conference organizer choose the hotel near the train station for next month's meeting? B: She said in her letter that the location is very convenient, because guests can walk there in five minutes from the station, and there are many shops and restaurants nearby.","t":"A：會議主辦人為什麼選擇火車站附近的飯店舉辦下個月的會議？ B：她在信中說那個【地點】非常方便，因為客人從車站步行五分鐘就能到，而且附近有很多商店和餐廳。"},{"w":"view","p":"n.","d":"what you can see from a place","c":"景色；視野","s":"A: Why are the hotel rooms on the twentieth floor so much more expensive than the rooms on the lower floors? B: The letter from the hotel says those rooms have a lovely view of the harbor and the mountains, and guests can watch the sunset from their balconies every evening.","t":"A：為什麼二十樓的飯店房間比低樓層的房間貴這麼多？ B：飯店的信上說那些房間有港口和山的美麗【景色】，客人每天傍晚都可以在陽台上看夕陽。"},{"w":"scenery","p":"n.","d":"the natural features of an area, such as mountains and rivers","c":"風景；景色","s":"A: What did the travel agency write in its letter to the company about the staff trip to Hualien in October? B: It said the scenery along the coast is wonderful, with high cliffs and blue ocean, so employees should bring cameras and plan to stop often during the bus ride.","t":"A：旅行社在給公司關於十月花蓮員工旅遊的信中寫了什麼？ B：信中說沿海的【風景】非常美妙，有高聳的懸崖和藍色的海洋，所以員工應該帶相機，並計畫在搭巴士途中多次停下來。"},{"w":"beautiful","p":"adj.","d":"very nice to look at","c":"美麗的；漂亮的","s":"A: What did the bride's mother write in her thank-you letter to the hotel after the wedding party last Saturday? B: She said the hall looked beautiful, with white flowers on every table and soft lights on the ceiling, and all the guests praised the staff for their excellent service.","t":"A：新娘的母親在上週六婚宴後寫給飯店的感謝信裡說了什麼？ B：她說宴會廳看起來很【漂亮】，每張桌子上都有白色的花，天花板上有柔和的燈光，所有賓客都稱讚員工的服務很出色。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"making you admire it because it is very good or big","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"A: Why did the investors decide to put more money into our company after they visited the factory last month? B: In their letter, they said the new production line was very impressive, because it can make twice as many products as before while using much less electricity and fewer workers.","t":"A：為什麼投資人上個月參觀工廠後，決定對我們公司投入更多資金？ B：他們在信中說新的生產線非常【令人印象深刻】，因為它能生產兩倍於以往的產品，同時使用更少的電力和人力。"},{"w":"interesting","p":"adj.","d":"making you want to know more","c":"有趣的","s":"A: Did you read the letter from the new intern describing her first week in the design department? B: Yes, it was very interesting, because she described how the team creates a new package from the early sketches to the finished product, and she included some funny stories about the meetings.","t":"A：你讀了新實習生描述她在設計部第一週的信嗎？ B：讀了，內容很【有趣】，因為她描述了團隊如何從早期草圖到完成品製作新包裝，還寫了一些關於開會的好笑故事。"},{"w":"amazing","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising and wonderful","c":"驚人的；令人驚嘆的","s":"A: How did the customers describe the new theme park in the letters they sent to the tourism office? B: Most of them said the light show at night was amazing, and many families wrote that it was the best part of their holiday, even better than the rides.","t":"A：顧客在寄給觀光局的信中如何描述新的主題樂園？ B：他們大多數說夜間的燈光秀很【令人驚嘆】，許多家庭寫道那是他們假期中最棒的部分，甚至比遊樂設施還好。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and calm","c":"寧靜的；平靜的","s":"A: Why did the manager book a small hotel in the mountains for the team's planning meeting next week? B: The hotel's letter describes it as a peaceful place far from the noisy city, so she thinks we can focus on our plans without phone calls or other interruptions.","t":"A：經理為什麼為下週的團隊規劃會議預訂了山上的一間小飯店？ B：飯店的信把它描述成一個遠離吵雜城市的【寧靜】地方，所以她認為我們可以專心討論計畫，不受電話或其他干擾。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of too many people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: Why did the customer write a letter to complain about the shopping mall's holiday sale last weekend? B: She said the stores were so crowded that she waited more than forty minutes to pay, and there were not enough staff to help people find the right sizes.","t":"A：那位顧客為什麼寫信抱怨購物中心上週末的假日特賣？ B：她說店裡太【擁擠】了，她等了四十多分鐘才結帳，而且沒有足夠的店員幫大家找到合適的尺寸。"},{"w":"busy","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot to do; full of activity","c":"忙碌的；繁忙的","s":"A: Why didn't the restaurant answer our letter about booking a table for the year-end party until today? B: The owner wrote back that December is always very busy for them, with big groups almost every night, so she needed time to check which evenings were still available.","t":"A：為什麼那家餐廳直到今天才回覆我們預約尾牙桌位的信？ B：老闆回信說十二月對他們來說總是非常【忙碌】，幾乎每晚都有大型團體，所以她需要時間確認哪些晚上還有空位。"},{"w":"large","p":"adj.","d":"big in size or amount","c":"大的；大量的","s":"A: What did the real estate agent describe in her letter about the new office space on Main Street? B: She said the meeting room is large enough for forty people, and it also has a kitchen and a storage area, which would be perfect for our growing sales team.","t":"A：房仲在她關於大街新辦公空間的信中描述了什麼？ B：她說會議室【大】到足以容納四十人，而且還有廚房和儲藏區，對我們不斷成長的業務團隊來說非常理想。"},{"w":"small","p":"adj.","d":"little in size or amount","c":"小的","s":"A: Why did the guest ask to change rooms in the letter she sent to the hotel manager on Tuesday? B: She wrote that her room was too small for her and her two children, because there was only one bed and no space for their suitcases, so she wanted a family room instead.","t":"A：那位客人為什麼在週二寄給飯店經理的信中要求換房？ B：她寫道她的房間對她和兩個孩子來說太【小】了，因為只有一張床，也沒有地方放行李箱，所以她想改住家庭房。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"new and using the latest ideas or technology","c":"現代的；現代化的","s":"A: How does the brochure describe the new training center that the company opened in Taichung last month? B: It describes the building as very modern, with smart screens in every classroom, fast wireless internet and a system that controls the lights and air conditioning automatically.","t":"A：公司上個月在台中開設的新訓練中心，在簡介手冊中是如何描述的？ B：手冊把這棟建築描述得非常【現代化】，每間教室都有智慧螢幕、快速的無線網路，還有一套自動控制燈光和空調的系統。"},{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following old ways that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統的","s":"A: What kind of restaurant did you describe in the letter to our Japanese clients who are visiting next week? B: I described a traditional Taiwanese restaurant in an old house, where they serve dishes that have been cooked the same way for over a hundred years by the same family.","t":"A：你在給下週來訪的日本客戶的信中描述了哪種餐廳？ B：我描述了一家位於老房子裡的【傳統】台灣餐廳，那裡供應同一個家族用相同方法烹調了一百多年的菜餚。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的","s":"A: Why did the bakery owner write to the newspaper about her shop's new pineapple cake? B: She wanted to describe how popular the cake has become, since tourists from Japan and Korea now wait in long lines every morning, and she has hired five more workers to keep up with orders.","t":"A：麵包店老闆為什麼寫信給報社介紹她店裡的新款鳳梨酥？ B：她想描述這款鳳梨酥變得有多【受歡迎】，因為現在每天早上都有日本和韓國觀光客大排長龍，她還多雇了五名員工來應付訂單。"},{"w":"famous","p":"adj.","d":"known by many people","c":"有名的；著名的","s":"A: Why does the hotel's letter say that guests should book a table at its restaurant early? B: The restaurant is famous for its fresh seafood and its chef, who has won several international cooking awards, so tables are often fully booked weeks before the weekend.","t":"A：為什麼飯店的信說客人應該提早預訂餐廳的位子？ B：這家餐廳以新鮮海鮮和主廚【聞名】，主廚贏得過好幾個國際廚藝獎，所以週末前好幾週位子常常就被訂滿了。"},{"w":"mainly","p":"adv.","d":"mostly; more than anything else","c":"主要地","s":"A: What did the customers write about in the survey letters we received after the summer sale? B: They mainly described problems with delivery, because many packages arrived a week late, but a few people also said that our website was difficult to use on their phones.","t":"A：我們在夏季特賣後收到的問卷信中，顧客寫了些什麼？ B：他們【主要】描述了送貨的問題，因為很多包裹晚了一週才到，但也有少數人說我們的網站用手機很難操作。"},{"w":"especially","p":"adv.","d":"more than usual; above all","c":"尤其；特別","s":"A: Did the visitors from the Tokyo office enjoy their tour of our factory and offices yesterday? B: Yes, in their thank-you letter they said they liked everything, especially the new packing machines, which they want to buy for their own factory in Osaka next year.","t":"A：東京辦公室的訪客昨天參觀我們的工廠和辦公室時玩得愉快嗎？ B：是的，他們在感謝信中說他們什麼都喜歡，【尤其】是新的包裝機，他們明年想為大阪自己的工廠購買。"},{"w":"particularly","p":"adv.","d":"more than usual; very","c":"特別地；尤其","s":"A: Why did the director write a letter to thank the customer service team at the end of the year? B: She was particularly pleased with the way they handled hundreds of calls during the system problem in November, and she wanted to describe their hard work to the whole company.","t":"A：主任為什麼在年底寫信感謝客服團隊？ B：她【特別】滿意他們在十一月系統出問題時處理數百通電話的方式，並想向全公司描述他們的辛勞。"},{"w":"clearly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easy to see or understand","c":"清楚地","s":"A: Why did the manager return my letter to the client and ask me to write it again before sending it? B: She said I should describe the delivery problem more clearly, with the exact dates and order numbers, so the client can understand what happened without calling us.","t":"A：經理為什麼把我給客戶的信退回，要我在寄出前重寫？ B：她說我應該更【清楚地】描述送貨問題，附上確切的日期和訂單編號，這樣客戶不用打電話給我們就能了解發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"briefly","p":"adv.","d":"in a few words; for a short time","c":"簡短地；短暫地","s":"A: How long should my letter to the hotel be when I describe the room problems from my business trip? B: You only need to briefly describe what went wrong in two or three sentences, and then ask them politely for a partial refund or a free night on your next visit.","t":"A：我寫信給飯店描述出差時遇到的房間問題，信要寫多長？ B：你只需要用兩三句話【簡短地】描述出了什麼問題，然後禮貌地要求部分退款或下次入住免費一晚。"},{"w":"in detail","p":"phr.","d":"including all the small facts","c":"詳細地","s":"A: Why did the insurance company ask you to write another letter about the car accident outside the warehouse? B: They want me to describe the accident in detail, including the exact time, the weather, the speed of each truck and the names of everyone who saw it happen.","t":"A：保險公司為什麼要你再寫一封關於倉庫外車禍的信？ B：他們要我【詳細地】描述這起事故，包括確切時間、天氣、每輛卡車的速度，以及所有目擊者的姓名。"},{"w":"for example","p":"phr.","d":"used to give a case that shows what you mean","c":"例如；舉例來說","s":"A: How can I make my letter describing our new cleaning service more useful for hotel managers? B: Give them real cases; for example, you could describe how we cleaned all two hundred rooms at a big hotel in one day after a major conference ended.","t":"A：我要如何讓描述我們新清潔服務的信對飯店經理更有用？ B：給他們真實的案例；【例如】，你可以描述我們如何在一場大型會議結束後，一天內清潔完一家大飯店的全部兩百間客房。"},{"w":"such as","p":"phr.","d":"used before giving examples","c":"例如；像是","s":"A: What information should we include in the letter describing the new office building to employees? B: We should list the useful services, such as the gym on the third floor, the free parking area and the coffee shop in the lobby, so people feel excited about the move next month.","t":"A：在向員工描述新辦公大樓的信中，我們應該放入哪些資訊？ B：我們應該列出實用的設施，【例如】三樓的健身房、免費停車區和大廳的咖啡店，讓大家對下個月的搬遷感到興奮。"},{"w":"overall","p":"adv.","d":"when you think about everything together","c":"整體來說；大致上","s":"A: What did the guests think of the company's annual dinner, based on the letters and emails we received? B: A few people said the food was cold, but overall, most guests described the evening as fun and well organized, and they hope we hold it at the same hotel next year.","t":"A：根據我們收到的信件和電子郵件，賓客們覺得公司年度晚宴如何？ B：有少數人說食物冷掉了，但【整體來說】，大多數賓客形容那個晚上很有趣而且安排得很好，希望明年在同一家飯店舉辦。"},{"w":"in general","p":"phr.","d":"usually; in most cases","c":"一般來說；大體上","s":"A: How do customers usually describe our online store when they write reviews or send us letters? B: Customers in general seem happy with us, because they say the website is easy to use and the prices are fair, but some want more payment choices and faster delivery to small towns.","t":"A：顧客寫評論或寄信給我們時，通常如何描述我們的網路商店？ B：顧客【一般來說】似乎對我們很滿意，因為他們說網站很容易使用、價格也公道，但有些人希望有更多付款方式，並加快寄到小鎮的速度。"},{"w":"first","p":"adv.","d":"before anything else","c":"首先；第一","s":"A: How should I organize my letter describing the problems with the new printers in our office? B: You should first describe what the printers are doing wrong, then say how long the problem has lasted, and finally ask the supplier to send someone to repair them this week.","t":"A：我該如何組織那封描述辦公室新印表機問題的信？ B：你應該【首先】描述印表機出了什麼問題，接著說明問題持續了多久，最後請供應商這週派人來修理。"},{"w":"then","p":"adv.","d":"after that; next","c":"然後；接著","s":"A: What did the tour guide write in her letter about our team's schedule for the trip to Kyoto? B: We will visit an old temple in the morning and then have lunch at a famous noodle shop before taking the train to Osaka in the afternoon.","t":"A：導遊在信中如何寫我們團隊京都之旅的行程？ B：我們早上會參觀一座古老的寺廟，【然後】在一家有名的麵店吃午餐，下午再搭火車去大阪。"},{"w":"finally","p":"adv.","d":"after a long time; at the end","c":"終於；最後","s":"A: Did the client ever reply to the long letter describing our new design for their office lobby? B: Yes, after three weeks of waiting, she finally wrote back yesterday to say that her board liked the design and wants us to start work in January.","t":"A：客戶有回覆那封描述我們為她辦公室大廳所做新設計的長信嗎？ B：有，等了三個星期後，她昨天【終於】回信說她的董事會喜歡這個設計，希望我們一月開始動工。"}]},{"unit":103,"theme":"Dessert 甜點","cards":[{"w":"store","p":"v.","d":"to keep something somewhere until you need it","c":"存放；儲存","s":"A: We have three chocolate cakes left over from the staff party this afternoon, so what should we do with them before we lock the office tonight? B: Let's cut them into small pieces and store them in the kitchen fridge, and then everyone can enjoy a slice with their coffee tomorrow morning.","t":"A：今天下午員工派對剩下三個巧克力蛋糕，我們今晚鎖辦公室之前該怎麼處理？ B：我們把它們切成小塊，【存放】在茶水間的冰箱裡，這樣明天早上大家就能配咖啡享用一片。"},{"w":"consumption","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something that people eat, drink or use","c":"消耗量；攝取量","s":"A: Why did the café owner decide to offer smaller cups of ice cream and more fresh fruit on the new summer menu? B: She read a report showing that sugar consumption among young office workers has risen sharply, so she wants to give her customers healthier choices without losing any of her regular guests.","t":"A：咖啡店老闆為什麼決定在新的夏季菜單上提供較小杯的冰淇淋和更多新鮮水果？ B：她讀到一份報告，顯示年輕上班族的糖分【攝取量】大幅上升，所以她想給顧客更健康的選擇，同時不流失任何常客。"},{"w":"pastry","p":"n.","d":"a baked sweet food made with flour, butter and often fruit","c":"酥皮點心；糕點","s":"A: What should we order for the breakfast meeting with the new clients on Friday, since some of them are coming straight from the airport? B: Let's get hot coffee, orange juice and a large apple pastry that we can cut into slices, because the French bakery downstairs makes them light and buttery, and visitors always love them.","t":"A：週五和新客戶的早餐會議我們該訂什麼？有些人會直接從機場過來。 B：我們訂熱咖啡、柳橙汁，再加一個可以切片的大蘋果【酥皮點心】，因為樓下的法式麵包店做得又輕又有奶油香，訪客總是很喜歡。"},{"w":"avoid","p":"v.","d":"to stay away from something or not do it","c":"避免；避開","s":"A: Do you know why Mark never takes any of the cookies or doughnuts that people bring into the office on Friday afternoons? B: His doctor told him to avoid sweet snacks for a few months after his last health check, so he brings his own nuts and fruit and drinks plenty of water instead.","t":"A：你知道為什麼馬克從不拿大家週五下午帶來辦公室的餅乾或甜甜圈嗎？ B：上次健康檢查後，醫生要他幾個月內【避免】吃甜食，所以他改帶自己的堅果和水果，並且多喝水。"},{"w":"conscious","p":"adj.","d":"knowing about something and paying attention to it","c":"意識到的；注意的；在意的","s":"A: Why has the bakery near the train station started printing the number of calories next to every cake in the display window? B: Many customers have become more conscious of what they eat these days, and the manager noticed that people often asked about sugar and fat, so clear labels help them choose quickly and feel better about buying something sweet.","t":"A：火車站附近的麵包店為什麼開始在櫥窗裡每個蛋糕旁邊標示熱量？ B：最近很多顧客對自己吃的東西變得更加【在意】，經理注意到大家常詢問糖分和脂肪，所以清楚的標示能幫助他們快速選擇，買甜食時也比較安心。"},{"w":"splurge","p":"v.","d":"to spend a lot of money on something special","c":"揮霍；花大錢買","s":"A: You have been bringing a simple sandwich for lunch every day this month, so why did you buy that expensive cake from the hotel café today? B: I finally finished the big sales report that my manager needed, so I decided to splurge on a special treat to celebrate before I start the next project.","t":"A：你這個月每天都帶簡單的三明治當午餐，今天為什麼在飯店咖啡廳買了那個昂貴的蛋糕？ B：我終於完成經理需要的大型業績報告了，所以決定【揮霍】一下買個特別的點心慶祝，然後再開始下一個專案。"},{"w":"weight","p":"n.","d":"how heavy a person or thing is","c":"體重；重量","s":"A: How is your new plan to walk to work and skip dessert after dinner going, and do you feel any different after the first month? B: It is going well, because I have already lost some weight, I sleep better at night, and I have more energy during long meetings in the afternoon.","t":"A：你走路上班、晚餐後不吃甜點的新計畫進行得如何？第一個月後有覺得哪裡不一樣嗎？ B：進行得很順利，因為我已經減了一些【體重】，晚上睡得比較好，下午開長會時也更有精神。"},{"w":"diet","p":"n.","d":"the food a person eats, or a plan to eat less or eat healthier food","c":"飲食；節食","s":"A: Why didn't Sarah eat any of the birthday cake at the office party yesterday, even though chocolate is her favorite flavor? B: She is on a strict diet because she is training for a marathon next month, so she only eats lean meat, vegetables and rice until the race is over.","t":"A：莎拉昨天在辦公室派對上為什麼一口生日蛋糕都沒吃？巧克力明明是她最喜歡的口味。 B：她正在進行嚴格的【飲食控制】，因為她在為下個月的馬拉松訓練，所以比賽結束前她只吃瘦肉、蔬菜和米飯。"},{"w":"random","p":"adj.","d":"chosen by chance, without any plan","c":"隨機的；任意的","s":"A: How does the coffee shop decide which customers get a free slice of cheesecake every Friday afternoon? B: The computer at the counter picks a random receipt number each hour, so any customer who has bought a drink can win, and the staff announce the lucky number loudly to everyone in the shop.","t":"A：那家咖啡店每週五下午是怎麼決定哪些顧客可以免費獲得一片起司蛋糕的？ B：櫃檯的電腦每小時會挑選一個【隨機的】收據號碼，所以任何買過飲料的顧客都可能中獎，店員會大聲向店裡的每個人宣布幸運號碼。"},{"w":"culprit","p":"n.","d":"the person or thing that causes a problem","c":"罪魁禍首；元兇","s":"A: Do you know why so many people in our department have felt tired and sleepy after lunch this week? B: I think the culprit is the large box of sugary doughnuts that the sales team leaves in the break room every morning, because everyone eats two or three before noon.","t":"A：你知道為什麼我們部門這週有那麼多人午餐後覺得又累又想睡嗎？ B：我想【罪魁禍首】是業務團隊每天早上放在休息室的那一大盒含糖甜甜圈，因為大家中午前都會吃兩三個。"},{"w":"obese","p":"adj.","d":"very fat in a way that is unhealthy","c":"肥胖的","s":"A: Why is the company offering free gym memberships and healthy cooking classes to all employees starting next month? B: The latest health survey showed that many staff members are overweight and some are even obese, so the managers want to help everyone eat better and exercise more before serious health problems begin.","t":"A：公司為什麼從下個月開始提供所有員工免費健身房會員和健康烹飪課？ B：最新的健康調查顯示，許多員工體重過重，有些甚至已經【肥胖】，所以主管們想在嚴重的健康問題出現之前，幫助大家吃得更好、多運動。"},{"w":"obesity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being very fat in an unhealthy way","c":"肥胖（症）","s":"A: What was the main topic of the speech that the doctor gave at the parents' meeting at the local school yesterday evening? B: She talked about childhood obesity and explained that too many sweet drinks and desserts can cause serious health problems, so she asked parents to pack fruit instead of candy in lunch boxes.","t":"A：昨晚那位醫生在當地學校家長會上的演講主題是什麼？ B：她談到了兒童【肥胖】問題，並解釋太多含糖飲料和甜點會造成嚴重的健康問題，所以她請家長在午餐盒裡放水果而不是糖果。"},{"w":"sweet tooth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a strong love of sweet food","c":"愛吃甜食；嗜甜","s":"A: Why does our manager always keep a jar of chocolates on her desk, and why does she visit the bakery across the street every afternoon? B: She has a real sweet tooth, so she can't get through a busy day without something sugary, but she always shares her treats with anyone who stops by her office.","t":"A：為什麼我們經理總是在桌上放一罐巧克力，而且每天下午都去對街的麵包店？ B：她真的很【愛吃甜食】，所以忙碌的一天裡沒有甜的東西就撐不下去，不過她總是會把點心分給來她辦公室的人。"},{"w":"fluffy","p":"adj.","d":"soft and light, full of air","c":"蓬鬆的；鬆軟的","s":"A: What makes the pancakes at the new breakfast café near our office so popular with customers, even though they are quite expensive? B: The cooks beat the eggs for a long time and add a little sparkling water, so every pancake comes out soft, light and fluffy, almost like a cloud on your plate.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家新早餐店的鬆餅為什麼那麼受顧客歡迎，雖然價格相當貴？ B：廚師會把蛋打很久，再加一點氣泡水，所以每一片鬆餅都又軟又輕又【蓬鬆】，盤子裡的鬆餅幾乎像一朵雲。"},{"w":"fundamental","p":"adj.","d":"basic and most important","c":"基本的；根本的","s":"A: What did the head baker teach the new kitchen staff on their first morning, before they started making any cakes for customers? B: She explained the fundamental rules of baking, such as measuring every ingredient carefully and keeping the kitchen clean, because even small mistakes can ruin a whole batch of desserts.","t":"A：新的廚房員工在第一天早上、開始為顧客做蛋糕之前，烘焙主廚教了他們什麼？ B：她講解了烘焙的【基本】規則，例如仔細測量每一種食材以及保持廚房乾淨，因為即使是小錯誤也可能毀掉整批甜點。"},{"w":"approach","p":"n.","d":"a way of dealing with something","c":"方法；處理方式","s":"A: How is the new café manager trying to sell more desserts without making customers feel that they are eating too much sugar? B: She is trying a fresh approach, offering smaller portions at lower prices and adding fruit to every plate, and so far both sales and customer reviews have improved.","t":"A：新的咖啡廳經理要怎麼在不讓顧客覺得吃太多糖的情況下賣出更多甜點？ B：她正在嘗試一種新的【方法】，以較低的價格供應較小的份量，並在每盤加上水果，到目前為止，銷售量和顧客評價都提升了。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"doing a job that needs special training; done with skill","c":"專業的；職業的","s":"A: Should we bake the cake for the company's tenth anniversary party ourselves, or should we order one from a shop? B: I think we should hire a professional baker, because more than two hundred guests are coming, and the cake needs to look perfect in the photos for our website and the local newspaper.","t":"A：公司十週年派對的蛋糕我們要自己烤，還是向店家訂？ B：我認為我們應該請一位【專業的】烘焙師，因為會有兩百多位賓客來參加，而且蛋糕在我們網站和地方報紙的照片中必須看起來完美無缺。"},{"w":"preheat","p":"v.","d":"to heat an oven before you put food in it","c":"預熱","s":"A: I followed the recipe exactly, so why did my chocolate cake come out of the oven flat and heavy instead of tall and soft? B: You probably forgot to preheat the oven before you put the cake in, because the batter needs high heat from the very first minute to rise properly.","t":"A：我完全照食譜做，為什麼我的巧克力蛋糕出爐時又扁又硬，而不是又高又鬆軟？ B：你可能忘了在放蛋糕進去之前先【預熱】烤箱，因為麵糊從第一分鐘起就需要高溫才能好好膨脹。"},{"w":"grease","p":"v.","d":"to put butter or oil on something","c":"塗油；抹油","s":"A: Why do the cakes at our café sometimes break into pieces when the kitchen staff take them out of the pans in the morning? B: Some of the new workers forget to grease the pans with butter before they pour in the batter, so the cakes stick to the metal and tear when they are removed.","t":"A：為什麼我們咖啡廳的蛋糕早上有時候在廚房員工脫模時會碎掉？ B：有些新員工在倒入麵糊之前忘了用奶油在烤模上【抹油】，所以蛋糕會黏在金屬上，取出時就裂開了。"},{"w":"pastry chef","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cook whose job is making cakes and desserts","c":"甜點師傅；糕點主廚","s":"A: Who designed the amazing chocolate sculpture that was standing in the hotel lobby during the international conference last weekend? B: The hotel's pastry chef spent three days making it by hand, and many guests took photos with it, so the marketing team has asked her to create another one for the holiday season.","t":"A：上週末國際會議期間擺在飯店大廳那座很棒的巧克力雕塑是誰設計的？ B：飯店的【甜點師傅】花了三天親手製作，許多賓客都和它合照，所以行銷團隊已經請她在節慶期間再做一座。"},{"w":"tedious","p":"adj.","d":"boring because it takes a long time and does not change","c":"單調乏味的；冗長的","s":"A: You look really tired this afternoon, so what have you been doing in the bakery kitchen since early this morning? B: I have been decorating four hundred small cookies with colored icing for a wedding, and the work is so tedious that my hands and eyes feel sore after doing the same pattern again and again.","t":"A：你今天下午看起來很累，從一大早開始你在麵包店廚房裡做了什麼？ B：我一直在為一場婚禮用彩色糖霜裝飾四百塊小餅乾，這工作非常【單調乏味】，同樣的圖案重複做了一次又一次，我的手和眼睛都痠了。"},{"w":"reliant","p":"adj.","d":"needing someone or something in order to work or succeed","c":"依賴的；依靠的","s":"A: Why did the bakery have to close early yesterday, even though there were still many customers waiting in line outside? B: The shop is completely reliant on one supplier for flour and butter, and when that delivery truck broke down, the bakers simply had nothing left to make bread or cakes with.","t":"A：為什麼那家麵包店昨天必須提早打烊，雖然外面還有很多顧客在排隊？ B：這家店的麵粉和奶油完全【依賴】一家供應商，當那輛送貨卡車拋錨時，麵包師傅就再也沒有材料可以做麵包或蛋糕了。"},{"w":"constant","p":"adj.","d":"staying the same; happening all the time","c":"恆定的；持續不斷的","s":"A: Why did the café owner decide to buy a new freezer for the ice cream, even though the old one still works? B: The old freezer couldn't keep a constant temperature, so the ice cream sometimes melted and froze again, and customers complained that it tasted icy and hard.","t":"A：為什麼咖啡店老闆決定為冰淇淋買一台新的冷凍櫃，雖然舊的還能用？ B：舊冷凍櫃無法維持【恆定的】溫度，所以冰淇淋有時會融化後再結凍，顧客抱怨吃起來有冰渣又很硬。"},{"w":"indulge","p":"v.","d":"to let yourself enjoy something special, such as rich food","c":"縱情享受；放縱一下","s":"A: Are you going to try the famous chocolate lava cake at the restaurant tonight, or are you still trying to eat healthily? B: I usually choose fruit for dessert, but since we are celebrating the end of this busy project, I think I will indulge just this once and enjoy every bite.","t":"A：你今晚要試試那家餐廳有名的巧克力熔岩蛋糕嗎？還是你還在努力吃得健康？ B：我通常選水果當甜點，不過既然我們在慶祝這個忙碌的專案結束，我想就這一次【放縱一下】，好好享受每一口。"},{"w":"picky","p":"adj.","d":"liking only a few things and hard to please","c":"挑剔的；挑食的","s":"A: What kind of cake should we order for Mr. Lee's retirement party, since he has worked here for over thirty years? B: We should ask his secretary first, because he is very picky about food and only likes plain vanilla cake without cream, nuts or any kind of fruit on top.","t":"A：李先生在這裡工作超過三十年了，他的退休派對我們該訂哪種蛋糕？ B：我們應該先問他的秘書，因為他對食物非常【挑剔】，只喜歡不加鮮奶油、堅果或任何水果的原味香草蛋糕。"}]},{"unit":104,"theme":"Diagram & Chart 圖表","cards":[{"w":"illustration","p":"n.","d":"a picture or drawing that helps explain something","c":"插圖；圖解","s":"A: Why did the marketing team decide to add a picture to the first page of the new product brochure, even though the printing cost will go up a little? B: They found that customers often skip long paragraphs, so a clear illustration of the machine helps readers understand how it works before they read the details.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊決定在新產品手冊的第一頁加上一張圖，即使印刷成本會稍微增加？ B：他們發現顧客常常跳過長段落，所以一張清楚的機器【插圖】能幫助讀者在閱讀細節之前先了解它如何運作。"},{"w":"visual","p":"adj.","d":"related to seeing or pictures","c":"視覺的","s":"A: Do you think I should send the sales figures as a long spreadsheet, or is there a better way to share them with the managers before Friday's meeting? B: Most of our managers are very busy and prefer visual information, so I'd turn the numbers into a few simple charts that they can understand in just a few seconds.","t":"A：你覺得我應該把銷售數字用一份很長的試算表寄出去，還是有更好的方式在星期五開會前分享給經理們？ B：我們大部分的經理都很忙，比較喜歡【視覺的】資訊，所以我會把數字轉換成幾張簡單的圖表，讓他們幾秒鐘就能看懂。"},{"w":"example","p":"n.","d":"something that shows what others of the same kind are like","c":"例子；範例","s":"A: The new employees still seem confused about how to fill out the monthly expense report, so what can we do to help them during tomorrow's training session? B: Let's show them a completed form as an example, and then we can walk through each section together so they can see exactly what information goes where.","t":"A：新員工對於如何填寫每月費用報告似乎還是很困惑，我們在明天的訓練課程中可以怎麼幫助他們？ B：我們拿一份填好的表格給他們當作【範例】，然後一起逐一說明每個部分，讓他們清楚知道哪些資訊該填在哪裡。"},{"w":"concept","p":"n.","d":"a general idea about something","c":"概念","s":"A: How did the designer present her idea for the new office layout when she met the board of directors last week? B: She started with a simple drawing that showed the basic concept of an open workspace, and then she explained how shared tables and quiet rooms would help different teams work together more easily.","t":"A：上週設計師和董事會開會時，她是如何呈現新辦公室格局的構想？ B：她先用一張簡單的圖畫說明開放式工作空間的基本【概念】，接著解釋共用桌和安靜室如何讓不同團隊更容易合作。"},{"w":"explanation","p":"n.","d":"words that make something clear or give a reason","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Why did the finance director ask Mark to stay after the meeting, even though his budget report was finished on time? B: Some of the numbers in his chart were much higher than last year, so she wanted a clear explanation of why the travel costs had increased before she sends the report to head office.","t":"A：為什麼財務總監要馬克在會後留下來，即使他的預算報告準時完成了？ B：他圖表中的一些數字比去年高出很多，所以她在把報告送到總公司之前，想要一個清楚的【說明】，了解差旅費為什麼增加。"},{"w":"representation","p":"n.","d":"a picture or sign that shows or stands for something","c":"表示；呈現","s":"A: Why does the map in the annual report show our branch offices as small colored circles instead of photos of each building? B: The circles are a simple representation of each office, and their size shows how many employees work there, so readers can compare the locations quickly without reading a long list.","t":"A：為什麼年度報告中的地圖用彩色小圓圈來標示我們的分公司，而不是放每棟建築的照片？ B：圓圈是每間辦公室的簡單【呈現方式】，圓圈大小顯示那裡有多少員工，讓讀者不必看一長串名單就能快速比較各地點。"},{"w":"clarity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand","c":"清晰；明確","s":"A: What did the trainer say about the slides you prepared for the safety workshop, and do you need to change many of them before next Monday? B: She liked the content, but she said some slides had too much text and too many colors, so I need to improve the clarity of each page by keeping only the most important points.","t":"A：訓練師對你為安全研習準備的投影片有什麼意見？你下週一之前需要修改很多張嗎？ B：她喜歡內容，但她說有些投影片文字太多、顏色太雜，所以我需要只保留最重要的重點，來提升每一頁的【清晰度】。"},{"w":"diagram","p":"n.","d":"a simple drawing that shows how something works or is arranged","c":"圖表；示意圖","s":"A: The new technicians keep asking me where each cable should go when they set up the meeting room equipment, so is there anything that could help them? B: Why don't you draw a simple diagram that shows how the projector, speakers, and computer connect, and then put a copy on the wall next to the equipment cabinet?","t":"A：新來的技術人員在架設會議室設備時一直問我每條線該接到哪裡，有什麼東西可以幫助他們嗎？ B：你何不畫一張簡單的【示意圖】，顯示投影機、喇叭和電腦如何連接，然後在設備櫃旁的牆上貼一份？"},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"a sign or picture that stands for an idea","c":"符號；象徵","s":"A: Why is there a small green leaf next to some of the products in our online catalog, and do customers really understand what it means? B: That symbol shows which items are made from recycled materials, and our survey found that many shoppers look for it because they want to buy products that are better for the environment.","t":"A：為什麼我們線上型錄裡有些產品旁邊有一片綠色小葉子？顧客真的懂它的意思嗎？ B：那個【符號】表示哪些商品是用回收材料製成的，我們的調查發現很多購物者會特別找它，因為他們想買對環境比較好的產品。"},{"w":"icon","p":"n.","d":"a small picture on a screen that you click to do something","c":"圖示","s":"A: I can't find the button to share the monthly report with the rest of the team in this new software, so could you show me where it is? B: Sure, just look at the top right corner of the screen and click the small icon that looks like an arrow, and then you can type the names of the people who need the file.","t":"A：我在這個新軟體裡找不到把月報分享給團隊其他人的按鈕，你可以告訴我在哪裡嗎？ B：當然，看螢幕右上角，點那個像箭頭的小【圖示】，然後就可以輸入需要這個檔案的人的名字。"},{"w":"annotation","p":"n.","d":"a short note added to explain a picture or text","c":"註解；註釋","s":"A: The client said our chart about online sales was hard to understand, so how should we change it before we send the final version tomorrow morning? B: We could add a short annotation next to each sudden rise or drop in the line, explaining what happened that month, such as a holiday sale or a problem with the website.","t":"A：客戶說我們的線上銷售圖表很難懂，在明天早上寄出最終版本之前，我們該怎麼修改？ B：我們可以在線條每次突然上升或下降的地方加上簡短的【註解】，說明那個月發生了什麼事，例如假期特賣或網站出問題。"},{"w":"label","p":"n.","d":"a word or short text that names a part of something","c":"標籤；標示","s":"A: Why did the manager ask us to redo the pie chart for the quarterly report when the colors and numbers were already correct? B: Each slice of the chart needs a clear label with the name of the region, because without one, readers couldn't tell which color stood for Asia and which stood for Europe.","t":"A：顏色和數字都已經正確了，為什麼經理還要我們重做季報裡的圓餅圖？ B：圖表的每一塊都需要一個寫著區域名稱的清楚【標示】，因為沒有標示的話，讀者分不出哪個顏色代表亞洲、哪個代表歐洲。"},{"w":"highlight","p":"v.","d":"to make something easy to notice; to show it is important","c":"強調；突顯；標亮","s":"A: The board members will only have ten minutes to look at our long report before they vote, so how can we make sure they notice the main results? B: Let's use a bright yellow color to highlight the three most important numbers in the summary table, so the members can see them immediately even if they don't read every page.","t":"A：董事們在投票前只有十分鐘看我們這份很長的報告，我們要怎麼確保他們注意到主要結果？ B：我們用亮黃色來【標亮】摘要表中最重要的三個數字，這樣即使他們沒有讀每一頁，也能馬上看到。"},{"w":"simplify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to understand or do","c":"簡化","s":"A: Our customers keep calling the help desk because they find the setup guide for the new printer too confusing, so what should we do about it? B: I think we should simplify the instructions by using fewer technical words and adding a picture for each step, so that people can set up the machine by themselves.","t":"A：我們的顧客一直打電話到客服中心，因為他們覺得新印表機的安裝指南太難懂了，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我認為我們應該【簡化】說明，少用專業術語，並為每個步驟加上一張圖，讓大家可以自己安裝機器。"},{"w":"demonstrate","p":"v.","d":"to show how something works by doing it","c":"示範；展示","s":"A: Will the sales representative bring the new coffee machine to the office, or will she only show us a video about it during the meeting? B: She is bringing a sample machine, because she wants to demonstrate how quickly it can make different drinks and how easy it is to clean after a busy morning in the break room.","t":"A：業務代表會把新咖啡機帶到辦公室嗎？還是她在會議中只會給我們看影片？ B：她會帶一台樣品機來，因為她想【示範】它能多快做出不同的飲品，以及在休息室忙碌的早上過後清潔起來有多容易。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear by giving details or reasons","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Several team members were confused by the new chart about overtime hours that you sent around yesterday afternoon, so what are you planning to do? B: I've booked the small meeting room for tomorrow morning, and I'll explain what each color and line means, and then I'll answer any questions they still have about their working hours.","t":"A：好幾位團隊成員對你昨天下午發出的加班時數新圖表感到困惑，你打算怎麼做？ B：我已經預約了明天早上的小會議室，我會【解釋】每個顏色和線條代表什麼，然後回答他們對工作時數還有的任何問題。"},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of something are organized","c":"結構；架構","s":"A: The new staff seem to have trouble knowing who they should report to, so how can we make this clearer for them during their first week? B: We could show them a chart of the company's structure, with each department in a box and lines that connect every team leader to the manager above them.","t":"A：新員工似乎搞不清楚自己該向誰報告，我們在他們第一週要怎麼讓這件事更清楚？ B：我們可以給他們看一張公司【組織架構】圖，每個部門用一個方框表示，並用線條把每位組長連到他們上面的經理。"},{"w":"layout","p":"n.","d":"the way things are arranged on a page or in a space","c":"版面配置；格局","s":"A: Did the printing company send us the first draft of the new event poster, and are you happy with the way it looks? B: Yes, they sent it this morning, but I'd like to change the layout a little, because the photo takes up too much space and the date and location are too small to read from far away.","t":"A：印刷公司寄來新活動海報的初稿了嗎？你滿意它的樣子嗎？ B：有，今天早上寄來了，但我想稍微調整一下【版面配置】，因為照片佔太多空間，而日期和地點太小，遠遠地看不清楚。"},{"w":"context","p":"n.","d":"the facts or situation around something that help you understand it","c":"背景；來龍去脈","s":"A: Why did you start your presentation with a short story about the company's history before you showed the new sales chart to the investors? B: I wanted to give them some context, because the numbers only make sense when people know that we moved into a new market three years ago and needed time to grow.","t":"A：你在給投資人看新的銷售圖表之前，為什麼先用一段公司歷史的小故事開場？ B：我想先給他們一些【背景】，因為只有當大家知道我們三年前進入新市場、需要時間成長時，這些數字才說得通。"},{"w":"flow","p":"n.","d":"the steady movement of something from one place or step to the next","c":"流程；流動","s":"A: Why is the new chart on the factory wall covered with arrows that go from one box to the next? B: It shows the flow of materials through the factory, from the moment they arrive at the loading area until the finished products are packed, so workers can see where delays usually happen and how to avoid them.","t":"A：為什麼工廠牆上的新圖表佈滿了從一個方框指向下一個方框的箭頭？ B：它顯示原料在工廠內的【流動】過程，從抵達裝卸區那一刻起到成品包裝完成，讓工人看出延誤通常發生在哪裡以及如何避免。"},{"w":"sequence","p":"n.","d":"the order in which things happen or are done","c":"順序","s":"A: The new assistants keep making mistakes when they prepare the meeting room for video calls, so what would help them remember the right steps? B: Let's put up a simple chart with numbered pictures that shows the correct sequence, starting with turning on the screen and ending with testing the microphone and camera before the guests arrive.","t":"A：新助理在為視訊會議準備會議室時一直出錯，有什麼能幫助他們記住正確步驟？ B：我們貼一張有編號圖片的簡單圖表，顯示正確的【順序】，從打開螢幕開始，到客人抵達前測試麥克風和攝影機為止。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking at two or more things to see how they are alike or different","c":"比較","s":"A: Why did you put last year's sales figures next to this year's figures on the same slide instead of on two separate pages? B: A side-by-side comparison makes it much easier for the managers to see how much each product has grown, and they won't need to keep going back and forth between the slides.","t":"A：你為什麼把去年和今年的銷售數字放在同一張投影片上，而不是分成兩頁？ B：並排【比較】讓經理們更容易看出每項產品成長了多少，他們也不需要在投影片之間來回切換。"},{"w":"emphasis","p":"n.","d":"special importance given to something","c":"強調；重點","s":"A: The new manager's report on customer service is very long, so what is the main message that she wants all the staff to remember? B: She puts special emphasis on answering emails within one working day, because the survey showed that slow replies were the biggest reason why customers felt unhappy with our company last year.","t":"A：新經理的客服報告非常長，她希望全體員工記住的主要訊息是什麼？ B：她特別【強調】要在一個工作天內回覆電子郵件，因為調查顯示，回覆太慢是去年顧客對我們公司不滿的最大原因。"},{"w":"design","p":"n.","d":"the way something is planned and made to look","c":"設計","s":"A: Are the customers happy with the new version of our company website, or have we received many complaints since we launched it last month? B: Most people like the clean, modern design with bigger buttons and fewer menus, but a few older customers said the text is still too small to read on their phones.","t":"A：顧客對我們公司網站的新版本滿意嗎？還是自從上個月上線以來我們收到了很多抱怨？ B：大部分人喜歡這個簡潔、現代、按鈕更大、選單更少的【設計】，但有幾位年長的顧客說，文字在手機上還是太小看不清楚。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch or listen to a talk or show","c":"觀眾；聽眾","s":"A: Should I use the same slides for the investors' meeting on Tuesday that I used for the training session with our new employees last week? B: No, you should change them, because the audience is very different; investors care about profits and future plans, while the new staff mainly needed to learn about daily tasks and company rules.","t":"A：星期二的投資人會議，我應該用上週新員工訓練時用的同一份投影片嗎？ B：不，你應該修改，因為【聽眾】很不一樣；投資人在意的是獲利和未來計畫，而新員工主要需要了解日常工作和公司規定。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the sharing of information between people","c":"溝通；交流","s":"A: Why did the head office decide to send a short chart every Monday instead of long emails about the progress of each project? B: The managers felt that good communication between departments was getting harder, so a simple weekly chart helps everyone see the status of every project quickly and reduces misunderstandings between the teams.","t":"A：為什麼總公司決定每週一寄一張簡短的圖表，而不是寄長篇電子郵件說明每個專案的進度？ B：經理們覺得部門之間要有良好的【溝通】越來越難，所以一張簡單的每週圖表能讓大家快速看到每個專案的狀態，並減少團隊之間的誤會。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to decide what something means","c":"解讀；詮釋","s":"A: The research team sent us a lot of charts about customer behavior, but I'm not sure what most of them actually mean for our sales plan. B: Don't worry, the team leader is coming to our meeting on Thursday to help us interpret the data, and she will explain which trends are the most important for next year.","t":"A：研究團隊寄給我們很多關於顧客行為的圖表，但我不確定大部分對我們的銷售計畫實際上代表什麼。 B：別擔心，組長星期四會來參加我們的會議，幫我們【解讀】這些數據，她會說明哪些趨勢對明年最重要。"},{"w":"visualization","p":"n.","d":"the act of showing information as pictures, charts or maps","c":"視覺化","s":"A: Why did our department buy new software for the analysts when the old spreadsheet program still works fine for most tasks? B: The new program is great for data visualization, because it can quickly turn thousands of numbers into colorful maps and charts that managers can understand without reading every row.","t":"A：舊的試算表程式在大部分工作上都還很好用，為什麼我們部門要幫分析師買新軟體？ B：新程式很適合做資料【視覺化】，因為它能快速把數千個數字轉換成彩色地圖和圖表，經理們不用看每一列就能看懂。"},{"w":"overview","p":"n.","d":"a short description of the main facts about something","c":"概要；概觀","s":"A: The new regional manager starts on Monday and has never worked in our industry before, so how should we help her during her first meeting with the team? B: Let's begin with a short overview of our main products, customers, and sales results for the past year, and then we can talk about each project in more detail later in the week.","t":"A：新的區域經理星期一上任，她以前從沒在我們這個產業工作過，在她和團隊的第一次會議中我們該怎麼幫她？ B：我們先簡短【概述】我們的主要產品、客戶和過去一年的銷售成果，然後這週稍晚再更詳細地討論每個專案。"},{"w":"instructional","p":"adj.","d":"used for teaching people how to do something","c":"教學的；說明用的","s":"A: The new factory workers are having trouble using the packing machine correctly, and the paper manual is too long for them to read during their shifts. B: We're making a short instructional video with clear pictures and simple steps, so they can watch it on their phones whenever they forget how to start or clean the machine.","t":"A：新來的工廠工人在正確操作包裝機上有困難，而紙本手冊太長，他們輪班時沒時間看。 B：我們正在製作一支簡短的【教學】影片，有清楚的畫面和簡單的步驟，讓他們忘記如何啟動或清潔機器時，隨時可以用手機觀看。"}]},{"unit":105,"theme":"Difficult 困難","cards":[{"w":"hard","p":"adj.","d":"not easy to do or understand","c":"困難的；艱難的","s":"A: Why did so many of the new interns stay late at the office last night instead of going home at six o'clock as usual? B: The manager gave them a very hard test on the new accounting software, and most of them needed extra time to finish all the questions correctly.","t":"A：為什麼很多新來的實習生昨晚留在辦公室加班，而不是像平常一樣六點回家？ B：經理給了他們一份關於新會計軟體、非常【困難】的測驗，大部分人都需要額外的時間才能把所有題目答對。"},{"w":"challenging","p":"adj.","d":"difficult in a way that tests your skills","c":"具挑戰性的","s":"A: Are you enjoying your new position in the marketing department, or do you miss working with the sales team on the second floor? B: I really like it, because the work is challenging and I have to learn new skills every week, but I sometimes miss chatting with my old teammates at lunch.","t":"A：你喜歡行銷部的新職位嗎？還是你會想念和二樓業務團隊一起工作的日子？ B：我真的很喜歡，因為這份工作很【具挑戰性】，我每週都得學新技能，不過我有時候會想念午餐時和老同事聊天。"},{"w":"tough","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to deal with; needing a lot of effort","c":"棘手的；艱難的","s":"A: Has the board of directors decided whether to close the small branch in the north of the city, which has been losing money for years? B: Not yet, because it is a tough decision for them, since forty loyal employees work there and many local customers still depend on that branch.","t":"A：董事會決定是否要關閉市區北邊那家虧損多年的小分店了嗎？ B：還沒有，因為這對他們來說是個【艱難的】決定，那裡有四十名忠誠的員工，而且許多當地顧客仍然依賴那家分店。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, energy or attention","c":"要求高的；費力的","s":"A: Why does Rachel look so tired these days, and is she still working on the big hotel project for our client in Singapore? B: Yes, she is, and the client is very demanding, so she has to answer emails late at night and change the designs again and again until they are satisfied.","t":"A：瑞秋最近為什麼看起來這麼累？她還在負責新加坡客戶的那個大型飯店案子嗎？ B：是的，而且那位客戶非常【要求高】，所以她得在深夜回覆電子郵件，還要一再修改設計直到他們滿意為止。"},{"w":"complicated","p":"adj.","d":"having many parts, so it is hard to understand","c":"複雜的","s":"A: Could you help me fill out this travel expense form, because I have tried three times and the finance office keeps sending it back to me? B: Of course, the form is quite complicated with all those boxes and codes, so let's sit down together after lunch and check each section one by one.","t":"A：你可以幫我填這張差旅費報銷單嗎？我已經填了三次，財務室一直退回給我。 B：當然可以，這張表格有那麼多欄位和代碼，相當【複雜】，我們午餐後一起坐下來，一個部分一個部分檢查吧。"},{"w":"complex","p":"adj.","d":"made of many connected parts","c":"複雜的；錯綜的","s":"A: Why is the new computer system taking so long to install in our head office, when the technicians promised it would be ready last Friday? B: The system is very complex, because it connects our sales, payroll and warehouse records, so the technicians must test every link carefully before we can use it.","t":"A：新的電腦系統為什麼在總部安裝這麼久？技術人員明明保證上週五就會好。 B：這套系統非常【複雜】，因為它串連了我們的銷售、薪資和倉庫紀錄，所以技術人員必須仔細測試每一個連結，我們才能使用。"},{"w":"tricky","p":"adj.","d":"difficult and needing care or skill","c":"棘手的；需要技巧的","s":"A: Do you think I should tell our biggest customer about the delay in person, or would it be better to send a short email this afternoon? B: It's a tricky situation, so I think you should call her first and explain the reason politely, and then send an email with the new delivery date.","t":"A：你覺得我該親自告訴我們最大的客戶延誤的事，還是今天下午寄一封簡短的電子郵件比較好？ B：這是個【棘手的】情況，所以我認為你應該先打電話給她，禮貌地說明原因，然後再寄一封寫明新交貨日期的電子郵件。"},{"w":"problematic","p":"adj.","d":"causing problems; hard to deal with","c":"有問題的；難處理的","s":"A: Why did the company stop using the cheap printers that the purchasing team bought from the new supplier last spring? B: They turned out to be problematic, because the paper got stuck almost every day, and the repair costs were much higher than the money we saved when we first bought them.","t":"A：公司為什麼不再使用採購部去年春天向新供應商買的那些便宜印表機？ B：結果那些印表機很【有問題】，幾乎每天都卡紙，而且維修費比我們當初購買時省下的錢高得多。"},{"w":"burdensome","p":"adj.","d":"causing worry or hard work, like a heavy load","c":"繁重的；累贅的","s":"A: Why do small shop owners in this area want the city government to make the new tax forms simpler and shorter? B: They say the paperwork is too burdensome, because it takes them several hours every month, and they would rather spend that time serving customers and running their businesses.","t":"A：為什麼這一區的小商家希望市政府把新的稅務表格改得更簡單、更簡短？ B：他們說這些文書工作太【繁重】了，每個月要花好幾個小時，他們寧願把那些時間拿來服務顧客、經營生意。"},{"w":"arduous","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of effort and energy over a long time","c":"艱鉅的；費力的","s":"A: How was the trip to the new factory in the mountains, and did the engineers manage to check all the machines before the weekend? B: It was an arduous journey, because the road was narrow and muddy after the heavy rain, but the engineers finally arrived and finished their inspection on Saturday morning.","t":"A：去山區新工廠的行程如何？工程師們有在週末前檢查完所有機器嗎？ B：那是一段【艱辛的】旅程，因為大雨過後道路又窄又泥濘，不過工程師們最後還是抵達了，並在星期六早上完成了檢查。"},{"w":"laborious","p":"adj.","d":"taking a lot of time and slow, careful work","c":"費力的；費時的","s":"A: Why are we buying a scanner for the archive room when the old files have been kept in boxes for more than twenty years? B: Typing every old contract into the computer by hand is a laborious task, so the scanner will save the staff many hours and reduce the number of mistakes.","t":"A：舊檔案已經放在箱子裡二十多年了，為什麼我們還要為檔案室買一台掃描器？ B：把每一份舊合約用手打進電腦是件很【費時費力的】工作，所以掃描器能幫員工省下許多時間，也能減少錯誤。"},{"w":"strenuous","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of physical effort","c":"費力的；激烈的（體力）","s":"A: Will Mr. Lee join the team-building hike up the mountain next Saturday, or is he still recovering from his knee operation? B: His doctor told him to avoid strenuous exercise for at least two more months, so he will meet us at the restaurant for dinner after the hike instead.","t":"A：李先生下週六會參加登山的團隊建立活動嗎？還是他的膝蓋手術還在恢復中？ B：他的醫生要他至少再兩個月避免【激烈的】運動，所以他會改在健行結束後到餐廳和我們一起吃晚餐。"},{"w":"formidable","p":"adj.","d":"powerful and difficult to defeat or deal with","c":"強大的；令人敬畏的","s":"A: Why is our sales director so worried about the new electronics store that will open across the street next month? B: That company is a formidable competitor, because it has lower prices, a famous brand and a huge advertising budget, so we need a strong plan to keep our regular customers.","t":"A：為什麼我們的業務總監這麼擔心下個月要在對街開幕的那家新電子商店？ B：那家公司是個【強大的】競爭對手，價格比較低、品牌有名，而且廣告預算龐大，所以我們需要一個有力的計畫來留住老顧客。"},{"w":"daunting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel nervous or less confident","c":"令人卻步的；令人畏懼的","s":"A: How do you feel about leading the training session for two hundred new employees at the annual conference next month? B: To be honest, it seems a bit daunting, because I have never spoken in front of such a large crowd, but my manager will help me practice my presentation every afternoon this week.","t":"A：下個月要在年度大會上帶領兩百名新進員工的訓練課程，你感覺如何？ B：老實說，這看起來有點【令人卻步】，因為我從來沒有在這麼多人面前說過話，不過我的經理這週每天下午都會幫我練習簡報。"},{"w":"gruelling","p":"adj.","d":"very tiring and difficult for a long time","c":"累垮人的；極度辛苦的","s":"A: Why are the nurses at the city hospital asking the managers to hire more staff and change the work schedule this winter? B: They often work gruelling twelve-hour shifts without a proper break, and many of them feel too exhausted to take good care of their patients by the end of the night.","t":"A：今年冬天，市立醫院的護理師為什麼要求主管多聘人手並調整班表？ B：她們常常得上【累垮人的】十二小時班，中間沒有像樣的休息，很多人到了深夜都累到無法好好照顧病人。"},{"w":"cumbersome","p":"adj.","d":"large, heavy and difficult to carry or use","c":"笨重的；麻煩的","s":"A: Why did the sales team ask for lighter laptops when the old ones still work perfectly well for writing reports? B: The old laptops are big and cumbersome, so carrying them to meetings with clients all over the city every day makes everyone's shoulders sore and tired.","t":"A：舊筆電寫報告明明還很好用，業務團隊為什麼要求換比較輕的筆電？ B：舊筆電又大又【笨重】，每天帶著它們到城市各處和客戶開會，大家的肩膀都又痠又累。"},{"w":"awkward","p":"adj.","d":"making people feel uncomfortable or embarrassed","c":"尷尬的；令人不自在的","s":"A: What happened at the meeting this morning, and why did everyone leave the room so quietly when it was over? B: The manager accidentally showed a slide with the wrong sales figures in front of the client, and there was an awkward silence for a few seconds before he apologized and corrected it.","t":"A：今天早上的會議發生了什麼事？為什麼會議結束時大家都那麼安靜地離開房間？ B：經理不小心在客戶面前放了一張銷售數字錯誤的投影片，在他道歉並更正之前，現場出現了幾秒鐘【尷尬的】沉默。"},{"w":"thorny","p":"adj.","d":"difficult and likely to cause arguments","c":"棘手的；麻煩的","s":"A: Are the managers going to talk about pay raises at the staff meeting on Friday, or will they discuss it later in private? B: Salary is a thorny issue in this company, so they plan to meet each employee in private next month, because they don't want an argument during the general meeting.","t":"A：經理們會在星期五的員工會議上談加薪的事嗎？還是之後私下再討論？ B：薪資在這家公司是個【棘手的】問題，所以他們打算下個月私下和每位員工面談，因為他們不希望在全體會議上起爭執。"},{"w":"onerous","p":"adj.","d":"involving a lot of work or responsibility that is hard to bear","c":"繁重的；費力的","s":"A: Why did the assistant manager decide to step down from the safety committee after only three months in the role? B: The extra duties became too onerous for her, because she had to write weekly reports and inspect every floor while still managing her own team of fifteen people.","t":"A：副理為什麼才在安全委員會待了三個月就決定卸下職務？ B：額外的職責對她來說變得太【繁重】了，因為她得寫每週報告、檢查每一層樓，同時還要管理自己十五個人的團隊。"},{"w":"inconvenient","p":"adj.","d":"causing problems or extra effort, especially about time or place","c":"不方便的","s":"A: Could we move the video call with the suppliers in Germany to eight o'clock tomorrow morning, since I have a dentist appointment at nine? B: I'm afraid that would be an inconvenient time for them, because it would be one o'clock in the morning there, so let's ask about the afternoon instead.","t":"A：因為我九點要看牙醫，可以把和德國供應商的視訊會議改到明天早上八點嗎？ B：恐怕那對他們來說是個【不方便的】時間，因為那邊是凌晨一點，所以我們改問看看下午可不可以吧。"},{"w":"exacting","p":"adj.","d":"expecting a very high level of care and accuracy","c":"嚴格的；要求極高的","s":"A: Why does every watch from this factory pass through five separate checks before it is packed and sent to the stores? B: The company has very exacting standards, so even a tiny scratch on the glass means the watch must be repaired before any customer can buy it.","t":"A：為什麼這家工廠的每支手錶在包裝送到店面前，都要經過五道不同的檢查？ B：這家公司的標準非常【嚴格】，所以即使玻璃上只有一道小刮痕，那支手錶也必須先修好，才能賣給任何顧客。"},{"w":"intimidating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel nervous or a little afraid","c":"令人膽怯的；嚇人的","s":"A: How was your job interview at the law firm downtown, and do you think you will get a second interview next week? B: The three partners asked very serious questions and hardly smiled, so the atmosphere was quite intimidating, but I stayed calm and answered everything as clearly as I could.","t":"A：你在市中心那家律師事務所的面試如何？你覺得下週會有第二次面試嗎？ B：三位合夥人問的問題都很嚴肅，幾乎沒有笑容，所以氣氛相當【令人緊張害怕】，不過我保持冷靜，盡可能清楚地回答了每一個問題。"},{"w":"obstacle","p":"n.","d":"something that stops you or makes progress difficult","c":"障礙；阻礙","s":"A: Why hasn't the company opened its new branch in Tokyo yet, when the plan was announced at the shareholders' meeting two years ago? B: The biggest obstacle has been finding enough staff who speak both English and Japanese, so the human resources team is now running language classes for current employees.","t":"A：公司兩年前就在股東大會上宣布了計畫，為什麼到現在還沒在東京開設新分公司？ B：最大的【障礙】一直是找不到足夠會說英語和日語的員工，所以人資團隊現在正為現有員工開設語言課程。"},{"w":"barrier","p":"n.","d":"a problem that stops people from doing something or communicating","c":"障礙；隔閡","s":"A: Why did the hotel hire two new receptionists who can speak Korean and Thai, even though most of our guests understand some English? B: The manager noticed that the language barrier was causing many problems at the front desk, so guests were often confused about check-out times and room charges.","t":"A：雖然大部分客人都懂一點英文，為什麼飯店還是聘了兩位會說韓語和泰語的新櫃檯人員？ B：經理注意到語言【隔閡】在櫃檯造成了很多問題，客人常常搞不清楚退房時間和房間費用。"},{"w":"hurdle","p":"n.","d":"a problem you must deal with before you can make progress","c":"難關；障礙","s":"A: Has the government approved the plan for our new shopping mall near the train station, or are we still waiting for more documents? B: We passed the safety inspection last week, which was the final hurdle, so the builders can start working on the site as soon as the weather improves next month.","t":"A：政府核准我們在火車站附近蓋新購物中心的計畫了嗎？還是我們還在等更多文件？ B：我們上週通過了安全檢查，那是最後一道【難關】，所以下個月天氣一好轉，營造商就能開始在工地施工。"},{"w":"complication","p":"n.","d":"a new problem that makes a situation more difficult","c":"併發症；使情況更複雜的因素","s":"A: How is your father doing after his heart operation, and when do you think you can come back to the office full-time? B: The doctors say the operation went well, but they want to keep him in the hospital for a few more days in case there is any complication, so I will return next Monday.","t":"A：你父親心臟手術後還好嗎？你覺得你什麼時候能回辦公室全職上班？ B：醫生說手術很順利，不過他們想讓他再住院幾天，以防出現任何【併發症】，所以我下星期一會回去上班。"},{"w":"predicament","p":"n.","d":"a difficult or unpleasant situation that is hard to get out of","c":"困境；窘境","s":"A: Why was Mark so late for the sales conference in Osaka, and did he miss his own presentation in the afternoon? B: He was in a real predicament after he lost his passport at the airport, but the embassy helped him quickly, and he arrived just ten minutes before his presentation started.","t":"A：馬克為什麼參加大阪的業務研討會遲到這麼久？他有錯過自己下午的簡報嗎？ B：他在機場弄丟護照後陷入了真正的【困境】，不過大使館很快就幫了他，他在簡報開始前十分鐘才趕到。"},{"w":"dilemma","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which you must choose between two difficult options","c":"兩難；進退兩難","s":"A: Has the owner of the restaurant decided what to do now that the price of meat and vegetables has gone up so much? B: She faces a dilemma, because she can either raise the menu prices and lose some customers, or keep the prices the same and earn almost no profit this year.","t":"A：肉類和蔬菜價格漲了這麼多，餐廳老闆決定好該怎麼做了嗎？ B：她面臨【兩難】，因為她可以調高菜單價格但會流失一些顧客，或者維持原價但今年幾乎賺不到利潤。"},{"w":"adversity","p":"n.","d":"a very difficult or unlucky situation","c":"逆境；困境","s":"A: Why do so many employees respect the founder of our company, even though she is very strict about deadlines? B: She kept the business running during the economic crisis without firing anyone, and she always stayed calm and positive in the face of adversity, which encouraged everyone to work harder.","t":"A：雖然我們公司的創辦人對截止期限非常嚴格，為什麼還是有這麼多員工尊敬她？ B：她在經濟危機期間沒有解雇任何人，讓公司持續運作，而且面對【逆境】時她總是保持冷靜和積極，這鼓勵了大家更努力工作。"},{"w":"hardship","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which life is very difficult, often because of a lack of money","c":"艱難；困苦","s":"A: Why did the factory owners decide to give every worker a small bonus this month, even though sales have been slow all year? B: They knew that many families were suffering financial hardship after the typhoon damaged their homes, so they wanted to help them pay for repairs and food.","t":"A：雖然今年整年銷售都很慢，為什麼工廠老闆還是決定這個月給每位工人一小筆獎金？ B：他們知道很多家庭在颱風損壞房屋後面臨經濟上的【困苦】，所以想幫他們支付修繕和食物的費用。"},{"w":"trial","p":"n.","d":"a difficult experience that tests your patience or strength","c":"考驗；磨難","s":"A: How was your first year running the small coffee shop near the university, and are you planning to open a second one soon? B: It was a real trial of my patience, because I had money problems and staff kept quitting, but now business is steady and I'm thinking about a second shop.","t":"A：你在大學附近經營小咖啡店的第一年過得如何？你打算很快開第二家店嗎？ B：那真的是對我耐心的一大【考驗】，因為我遇到資金問題，員工又一直離職，不過現在生意穩定了，我正在考慮開第二家店。"},{"w":"ordeal","p":"n.","d":"a very unpleasant and painful experience","c":"痛苦的經歷；折磨","s":"A: Did the passengers on the flight from London finally arrive, after the plane was stuck on the runway in the snowstorm? B: Yes, they landed this morning after a twelve-hour ordeal without proper food or sleep, so the airline gave each of them a free hotel room and a meal voucher.","t":"A：從倫敦起飛的那班飛機在暴風雪中困在跑道上之後，乘客們終於抵達了嗎？ B：是的，他們今天早上降落，經歷了沒有像樣食物和睡眠的十二小時【折磨】，所以航空公司給每個人一間免費飯店房間和一張餐券。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed because you cannot do what you want","c":"令人沮喪的；令人氣惱的","s":"A: Why are you still at your desk at seven o'clock, when you told me you would leave early to watch the baseball game tonight? B: My computer froze three times while I was saving the monthly report, and I had to type everything again, which was really frustrating, so now I'm hurrying to finish it.","t":"A：你不是跟我說今晚要提早走去看棒球比賽嗎？為什麼七點了還坐在位子上？ B：我在存月報時電腦當機了三次，我得全部重打，真的很【令人沮喪】，所以我現在正趕著把它完成。"},{"w":"taxing","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of mental or physical effort","c":"費力的；累人的","s":"A: Why do you look so tired today, when you usually have so much energy after a normal day of work in the office? B: I spent the whole day checking a long contract word by word with our lawyers, and it was mentally taxing, so I just want to go home and rest.","t":"A：你平常在辦公室工作一整天後還很有精神，為什麼今天看起來這麼累？ B：我整天都和律師們逐字檢查一份很長的合約，在腦力上非常【累人】，所以我只想回家休息。"},{"w":"impossible","p":"adj.","d":"not able to happen or be done","c":"不可能的","s":"A: Can your team finish translating all two hundred pages of the product manual by tomorrow morning, before the client's meeting? B: I'm sorry, but that is impossible with only three translators, so could you ask the client to accept the first fifty pages tomorrow and the rest by Friday?","t":"A：你的團隊能在明天早上客戶開會前，把整本兩百頁的產品手冊翻譯完嗎？ B：很抱歉，只有三位譯者的話那是【不可能的】，所以你能不能請客戶接受明天先交前五十頁，其餘的星期五前交？"}]},{"unit":106,"theme":"Dinner 晚餐","cards":[{"w":"supper","p":"n.","d":"a light meal eaten in the evening","c":"晚餐；宵夜","s":"A: The workshop with our partners in Osaka finishes very late on Friday, so where should the team eat after the final session ends? B: The hotel restaurant stays open until eleven, so I booked a simple supper there for everyone, and we can relax and talk about the results before we go back to our rooms.","t":"A：我們和大阪合作夥伴的研習會星期五很晚才結束，最後一場結束後團隊要去哪裡吃東西？ B：飯店餐廳營業到十一點，所以我幫大家在那裡訂了簡單的【晚餐】，我們可以在回房間之前放鬆一下，聊聊這次的成果。"},{"w":"meal","p":"n.","d":"food eaten at one time, such as breakfast, lunch or dinner","c":"一餐；餐點","s":"A: Our new clients from Germany are arriving at the airport at six this evening, and they will probably be tired and hungry after such a long flight. B: Then let's take them straight to the Italian restaurant near their hotel, so they can enjoy a good meal and get some rest before tomorrow's long meeting.","t":"A：我們德國的新客戶今晚六點抵達機場，經過這麼長的飛行，他們大概會又累又餓。 B：那我們就直接帶他們去飯店附近的義大利餐廳，讓他們好好享用一【餐】，在明天冗長的會議前休息一下。"},{"w":"feast","p":"n.","d":"a large special meal for many people, often to celebrate","c":"盛宴；大餐","s":"A: How did the company celebrate after the sales team broke its record for the whole year, and did the CEO attend the party? B: Yes, she came and gave a short speech, and then the hotel prepared a huge feast with roast meat, fresh seafood and many kinds of cakes, so everyone ate until midnight.","t":"A：業務團隊打破全年紀錄後，公司是怎麼慶祝的？執行長有出席派對嗎？ B：有，她來了並做了簡短致詞，然後飯店準備了一場豐盛的【盛宴】，有烤肉、新鮮海鮮和各式各樣的蛋糕，所以大家一直吃到半夜。"},{"w":"banquet","p":"n.","d":"a large formal dinner for many people, often with speeches","c":"宴會；正式宴席","s":"A: What should I wear to the annual awards dinner at the Grand Hotel next Saturday, since this is my first year at the company? B: It is a formal banquet for over three hundred employees and their partners, so men usually wear dark suits and women wear evening dresses, and the president gives the awards after the main dishes.","t":"A：下週六在大飯店舉行的年度頒獎晚宴我該穿什麼？這是我在公司的第一年。 B：那是一場有三百多位員工及其伴侶參加的正式【宴會】，所以男士通常穿深色西裝，女士穿晚禮服，總裁會在主菜之後頒獎。"},{"w":"buffet","p":"n.","d":"a meal where people take food themselves from a long table","c":"自助餐","s":"A: There will be about eighty people at the training seminar on Monday, so how are we going to give everyone lunch without making them wait too long? B: I asked the hotel to set up a buffet in the hall next to the meeting room, so people can choose their own food quickly and return to their seats before the afternoon session.","t":"A：星期一的訓練研討會大約有八十人參加，我們要怎麼讓每個人吃到午餐，又不讓他們等太久？ B：我請飯店在會議室旁邊的大廳擺設【自助餐】，這樣大家可以很快自己選餐，並在下午的課程開始前回到座位。"},{"w":"entrée","p":"n.","d":"the main dish of a meal","c":"主菜","s":"A: The menu for the client dinner lists soup, salad and three choices for the main dish, so what do you suggest for our visitors from Japan? B: I would recommend the salmon as the entrée, because it is the chef's most popular dish, and it is lighter than the beef, which many visitors find too heavy at night.","t":"A：客戶晚宴的菜單上列了湯、沙拉和三種主菜選擇，你建議我們的日本訪客點什麼？ B：我會推薦鮭魚當【主菜】，因為那是主廚最受歡迎的料理，而且比牛肉清淡，很多訪客覺得牛肉晚上吃太膩。"},{"w":"main course","p":"n.phr.","d":"the largest and most important dish of a meal","c":"主菜；主餐","s":"A: The waiter just asked whether we are ready to order, but Mr. Lee is still outside on the phone with the head office in Seoul. B: Let's order the soup and salad first, and we can wait for him to come back before choosing the main course, since he wants to try either the steak or the roast chicken tonight.","t":"A：服務生剛問我們是否準備好點餐，但李先生還在外面和首爾總公司講電話。 B：我們先點湯和沙拉，等他回來再選【主菜】，因為他今晚想吃牛排或烤雞。"},{"w":"appetizer","p":"n.","d":"a small dish eaten before the main part of a meal","c":"開胃菜","s":"A: Our visitors from the bank will arrive at the restaurant around seven, but the manager is stuck in traffic and may be thirty minutes late. B: In that case, let's order an appetizer like spring rolls or a cheese plate for the table, so the visitors have something to eat while we wait for her.","t":"A：銀行的訪客大約七點會到餐廳，但經理塞在車陣中，可能會晚三十分鐘。 B：既然這樣，我們先幫這桌點個【開胃菜】，像是春捲或起司拼盤，讓訪客在等她的時候有東西吃。"},{"w":"starter","p":"n.","d":"the first small dish of a meal","c":"前菜；開胃菜","s":"A: I'm planning the menu for the London office's farewell dinner, and I'm not sure what to put before the main dishes, since some people are vegetarian. B: Tomato soup would be a good starter, because almost everyone likes it, it is easy for the kitchen to make, and it is safe for people who don't eat meat.","t":"A：我正在規劃倫敦辦公室的歡送晚宴菜單，不確定主菜前要放什麼，因為有些人吃素。 B：番茄湯會是很好的【前菜】，因為幾乎每個人都喜歡，廚房也容易做，而且不吃肉的人也可以吃。"},{"w":"side dish","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small amount of food served with the main dish","c":"配菜","s":"A: The steak at this restaurant looks really good, but does it come with anything else, or do we have to pay extra for vegetables and potatoes? B: Each main plate comes with one free side dish, so you can choose mashed potatoes, a green salad or fried rice, and the waiter will bring it at the same time.","t":"A：這家餐廳的牛排看起來真不錯，但有附其他東西嗎？還是蔬菜和馬鈴薯要另外付費？ B：每份主餐都附一道免費的【配菜】，你可以選馬鈴薯泥、蔬菜沙拉或炒飯，服務生會同時送上。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: Everyone has finished the main dishes, and the clients seem very happy, but should we ask for the bill now or wait a little longer? B: Let's not rush, because the chef here is famous for his chocolate cake, so we should order some dessert and coffee for the table before we finish the evening.","t":"A：大家都吃完主菜了，客戶看起來很開心，我們現在要結帳還是再等一下？ B：別急，這裡的主廚以巧克力蛋糕聞名，所以我們應該在結束今晚之前，幫這桌點些【甜點】和咖啡。"},{"w":"beverage","p":"n.","d":"a drink of any kind","c":"飲料","s":"A: The catering company sent the price list for Friday's product launch, but I'm not sure whether drinks are included in the price per person. B: Food is included, but every beverage such as juice, soda and coffee costs extra, so please check how many people are coming before we place the order.","t":"A：外燴公司寄來了星期五產品發表會的價目表，但我不確定每人的價格有沒有包含飲料。 B：餐點有包含，但果汁、汽水和咖啡等每一種【飲料】都要另外收費，所以下訂單前請先確認有多少人會來。"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"instructions for making a dish","c":"食譜","s":"A: The soup at the staff party was so good that several people asked who made it, and they want to try making it at home this weekend. B: Our receptionist made it, and she is happy to share her grandmother's recipe, so she will email the list of steps and the cooking time to everyone tomorrow.","t":"A：員工派對上的湯好喝到好幾個人問是誰做的，他們這個週末想在家試做。 B：是我們的櫃檯人員做的，她很樂意分享她祖母的【食譜】，所以她明天會把步驟和烹煮時間寄給大家。"},{"w":"ingredient","p":"n.","d":"one of the foods used to make a dish","c":"材料；食材","s":"A: Why did the new restaurant downtown suddenly raise the prices of all its pasta dishes by almost twenty percent this month? B: The owner said the cost of every important ingredient, especially cheese, tomatoes and olive oil, went up sharply after the bad weather in Europe last summer, so he had no other choice.","t":"A：市中心那家新餐廳為什麼這個月突然把所有義大利麵的價格調漲將近百分之二十？ B：老闆說每一樣重要【食材】的成本都大幅上漲，尤其是起司、番茄和橄欖油，因為去年夏天歐洲天氣不好，所以他別無選擇。"},{"w":"cook","p":"v.","d":"to make food ready to eat by heating it","c":"烹調；煮","s":"A: Are we ordering food from a restaurant for the team's end-of-year party, or is someone in the office going to make the dinner? B: Our manager wants to cook the dinner himself at his house, so he is buying fish, vegetables and rice on Saturday morning, and we only need to bring drinks and some fruit.","t":"A：團隊的年終派對我們要跟餐廳訂餐，還是辦公室有人要負責做晚餐？ B：我們經理想在他家親自【煮】晚餐，所以他星期六早上會去買魚、蔬菜和米，我們只需要帶飲料和一些水果。"},{"w":"prepare","p":"v.","d":"to make food ready to be eaten","c":"準備；製作（餐點）","s":"A: The kitchen staff look very busy this afternoon, so is there a special event at the hotel tonight that I don't know about? B: Yes, a technology company booked the main hall for a dinner, so the chefs must prepare food for two hundred people before seven, and they started washing vegetables at noon.","t":"A：廚房員工今天下午看起來非常忙，今晚飯店有我不知道的特別活動嗎？ B：有，一家科技公司預訂了主廳辦晚宴，所以廚師們必須在七點前【準備】兩百人份的餐點，他們中午就開始洗菜了。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drinks to people at a meal","c":"供應；上（菜）","s":"A: The conference ends at five thirty, so what time should the hotel staff bring the food into the dining room for our international visitors? B: Please ask them to serve dinner at six thirty, because people will need about an hour to check in, change their clothes and make phone calls to their families.","t":"A：會議五點半結束，飯店員工應該幾點把餐點送進餐廳給我們的國際訪客？ B：請他們六點半【上】晚餐，因為大家需要大約一小時辦理入住、換衣服，並打電話給家人。"},{"w":"guest","p":"n.","d":"a person you invite to a meal or event","c":"客人；賓客","s":"A: How many chairs should I put in the private dining room for Mr. Chen's retirement dinner on Friday evening? B: Each department may bring one guest, such as a former coworker or a family member, so please prepare forty seats and tell the restaurant about any special food needs before Thursday.","t":"A：星期五晚上陳先生的退休晚宴，我應該在包廂放幾張椅子？ B：每個部門可以帶一位【客人】，例如前同事或家人，所以請準備四十個座位，並在星期四之前告知餐廳任何特殊的飲食需求。"},{"w":"homemade","p":"adj.","d":"made at home, not bought from a store or factory","c":"自製的；家常的","s":"A: Why is the small café across from our office always so crowded at lunchtime, even though it only has six tables? B: The owner bakes all the bread and pies herself every morning, so the food is fresh and homemade, and many office workers are happy to wait in line for it.","t":"A：我們辦公室對面那家小咖啡館只有六張桌子，為什麼午餐時間總是那麼擠？ B：老闆每天早上親自烤所有的麵包和派，所以食物新鮮又是【自製的】，很多上班族都樂意排隊購買。"},{"w":"hearty","p":"adj.","d":"large and filling","c":"豐盛的；分量足的","s":"A: The volunteers will be cleaning the park from early morning until late afternoon on Saturday, so what kind of food should we give them? B: They will work hard outside in the cold, so we should give them a hearty lunch with beef stew, bread and potatoes, which will keep them full and warm all afternoon.","t":"A：志工們星期六會從一大早清掃公園到傍晚，我們應該給他們準備什麼樣的食物？ B：他們會在寒冷的戶外辛苦工作，所以應該給他們一份【豐盛的】午餐，有燉牛肉、麵包和馬鈴薯，讓他們整個下午都吃得飽又暖和。"},{"w":"light","p":"adj.","d":"small in amount and easy to digest","c":"清淡的；分量少的","s":"A: I have a big presentation to the board of directors right after lunch, and I don't want to feel sleepy while I'm speaking. B: Then you should just have a light lunch, like a salad or a small sandwich, because a big plate of rice or noodles will make you tired in the afternoon.","t":"A：午餐後我馬上要向董事會做一場重要簡報，我不想在講話時覺得想睡。 B：那你午餐應該吃得【清淡】一點，像沙拉或小三明治，因為一大盤飯或麵會讓你下午很累。"},{"w":"delicious","p":"adj.","d":"having a very good taste","c":"美味的","s":"A: Did the clients enjoy the seafood restaurant you chose last night, or should we try a different place when they visit again next month? B: They loved it, and the director said the crab was the most delicious thing he had eaten in Taipei, so let's book the same restaurant for their next visit.","t":"A：客戶喜歡你昨晚選的海鮮餐廳嗎？還是他們下個月再來時我們該換個地方？ B：他們很喜歡，處長說那道螃蟹是他在台北吃過最【美味的】東西，所以他們下次來我們就訂同一家餐廳吧。"},{"w":"savory","p":"adj.","d":"salty or spicy, not sweet","c":"鹹的；鹹香的","s":"A: The afternoon tea for the visiting managers will have lots of cakes and cookies, but is there anything for people who don't like sweet food? B: Yes, the bakery will also bring some savory snacks, such as cheese pastries, ham sandwiches and small meat pies, so everyone will find something they like.","t":"A：給來訪經理們的下午茶會有很多蛋糕和餅乾，但有沒有給不喜歡甜食的人吃的東西？ B：有，麵包店也會帶一些【鹹的】點心，像是起司酥皮、火腿三明治和小肉派，所以每個人都能找到喜歡的。"},{"w":"flavorful","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, pleasant taste","c":"味道濃郁的；有風味的","s":"A: Why do so many of our foreign visitors ask to eat at that small Thai restaurant on the corner instead of the hotel restaurant? B: The chef uses fresh herbs, garlic and chili in every dish, so the food is much more flavorful than the plain hotel menu, and the prices are lower too.","t":"A：為什麼我們很多外國訪客要求去轉角那家小泰國餐廳吃，而不是飯店餐廳？ B：主廚在每道菜都用新鮮香草、大蒜和辣椒，所以食物比飯店平淡的菜單【味道濃郁】得多，而且價格也比較低。"},{"w":"grilled","p":"adj.","d":"cooked over direct heat on metal bars","c":"炙烤的；烤的","s":"A: The doctor told my manager to eat healthier food, so what should we order for him at the steakhouse during tonight's business dinner? B: He could have the grilled chicken with vegetables, because it is cooked over a fire without much oil, and it is still very tasty and filling.","t":"A：醫生要我經理吃得健康一點，今晚商務晚餐在牛排館我們該幫他點什麼？ B：他可以點【炙烤】雞肉配蔬菜，因為那是用火烤的，不太用油，而且還是很好吃又有飽足感。"},{"w":"roasted","p":"adj.","d":"cooked in an oven or over a fire","c":"烘烤的；烤的","s":"A: What are the kitchen staff making for the Thanksgiving lunch for our American coworkers, since many of them miss their families at this time of year? B: They are making a big roasted turkey in the oven with potatoes and carrots, so our American friends will feel a little more at home during the holiday.","t":"A：廚房員工要為美國同事的感恩節午餐做什麼？很多人每年這個時候都很想念家人。 B：他們正在用烤箱做一隻大【烤】火雞，配上馬鈴薯和紅蘿蔔，讓我們的美國朋友在節日期間更有家的感覺。"},{"w":"fried","p":"adj.","d":"cooked in hot oil","c":"油炸的；炒的","s":"A: The night market near our hotel has so many food stands, but I'm worried that some of the snacks might be too oily for me. B: Many of the fried snacks, like chicken and sweet potato balls, are cooked in a lot of hot oil, so you could try the soup or grilled corn instead.","t":"A：我們飯店附近的夜市有好多小吃攤，但我擔心有些小吃對我來說太油了。 B：很多【油炸的】小吃，像雞排和地瓜球，都是用大量熱油做的，所以你可以改試湯或烤玉米。"},{"w":"steamed","p":"adj.","d":"cooked with hot water vapor","c":"蒸的","s":"A: Our Hong Kong partners want to try a traditional Chinese breakfast before their factory tour, so where should we take them? B: There is a famous dim sum restaurant on the second floor of the mall, and they offer fresh steamed dumplings and buns in small bamboo baskets, which visitors always love.","t":"A：我們的香港合作夥伴想在參觀工廠前嚐嚐傳統的中式早餐，我們該帶他們去哪裡？ B：商場二樓有一家很有名的港式點心餐廳，他們用小竹籠供應新鮮的【蒸】餃和包子，訪客總是很喜歡。"},{"w":"boiled","p":"adj.","d":"cooked in very hot water","c":"水煮的","s":"A: The hotel breakfast has many choices, but which dish would you recommend for someone who wants something simple and healthy before a long day of meetings? B: I usually take two boiled eggs with some fruit and toast, because they are full of protein, they don't contain any oil, and they keep me full until lunch.","t":"A：飯店早餐有很多選擇，對想在一整天會議前吃點簡單健康東西的人，你會推薦哪道菜？ B：我通常拿兩顆【水煮】蛋配一些水果和吐司，因為蛋白質豐富、不含油，而且能讓我撐到午餐。"},{"w":"leftovers","p":"n.","d":"food that remains after a meal","c":"剩菜；吃剩的食物","s":"A: We ordered far too much food for the sales meeting today, and there are still three trays of sandwiches and pasta on the table. B: Let's put the leftovers in the office refrigerator, and anyone who works late tonight or comes in early tomorrow can take some for a free lunch.","t":"A：我們今天的業務會議訂太多食物了，桌上還有三盤三明治和義大利麵。 B：我們把【剩菜】放進辦公室冰箱，今晚加班或明天早到的人都可以拿一些當免費的午餐。"},{"w":"takeout","p":"n.","d":"food bought from a restaurant to eat somewhere else","c":"外帶食物","s":"A: We have to finish the budget report for the head office by nine o'clock tonight, so we probably won't have time to go out for dinner. B: Don't worry, I'll order Chinese takeout from the restaurant downstairs, and we can eat at our desks while we check the last few pages.","t":"A：今晚九點前我們必須完成給總公司的預算報告，所以大概沒時間出去吃晚餐了。 B：別擔心，我會跟樓下的餐廳訂中式【外帶餐點】，我們可以邊在座位上吃邊檢查最後幾頁。"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to keep a table for you at a restaurant","c":"預訂；訂位","s":"A: The French restaurant near the train station is very popular on Friday nights, so do you think we can get a table for our clients without calling first? B: No, it's almost always full on weekends, so I'll call this afternoon and make a reservation for six people at seven thirty, near the window if possible.","t":"A：火車站附近那家法國餐廳週五晚上很熱門，你覺得我們不先打電話也能幫客戶找到位子嗎？ B：不行，週末幾乎都客滿，所以我今天下午會打電話【訂位】，七點半六個人，可以的話靠窗。"},{"w":"tableware","p":"n.","d":"plates, bowls, cups, knives and forks used at meals","c":"餐具","s":"A: The caterer will bring the food for the garden party, but who is going to provide the plates, cups, knives and forks for two hundred people? B: The hotel will lend us all the tableware, and their staff will collect and wash everything after the party, so we only need to pay a small cleaning fee.","t":"A：外燴業者會帶花園派對的食物，但兩百人用的盤子、杯子、刀叉由誰提供？ B：飯店會借我們所有的【餐具】，派對結束後他們的員工會收回並清洗，所以我們只需支付一小筆清潔費。"},{"w":"napkin","p":"n.","d":"a piece of cloth or paper used to clean your mouth and hands while eating","c":"餐巾；餐巾紙","s":"A: The chicken at the team picnic was great, but my hands are really oily now, and I don't want to touch my phone or my laptop. B: Here, take a napkin from the box on the table next to the drinks, and there is also a sink with soap behind the tent if you want to wash your hands.","t":"A：團隊野餐的雞肉很好吃，但現在我的手好油，不想碰手機或筆電。 B：來，從飲料旁邊桌上的盒子拿一張【餐巾紙】，帳篷後面也有附肥皂的洗手台，如果你想洗手的話。"},{"w":"tablecloth","p":"n.","d":"a cloth that covers a table during a meal","c":"桌布","s":"A: The dining tables in the meeting hall look old and scratched, so how can we make the room look nicer for the welcome dinner tonight? B: We can put a clean white tablecloth on each table and add some flowers and candles, so the visitors won't notice the scratches at all.","t":"A：會議廳的餐桌看起來又舊又有刮痕，今晚的歡迎晚宴我們要怎麼讓房間看起來好一點？ B：我們可以在每張桌子鋪上乾淨的白色【桌布】，再擺些花和蠟燭，這樣訪客就完全不會注意到刮痕了。"},{"w":"portion","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food served to one person","c":"一份（食物）；分量","s":"A: The new staff restaurant gets a lot of complaints, so what is the main reason that so many employees prefer to eat lunch somewhere else? B: Many people say each portion is too small for the price, especially the rice and meat, so they still feel hungry in the afternoon and buy snacks later.","t":"A：新員工餐廳收到很多抱怨，為什麼這麼多員工寧可去別的地方吃午餐？ B：很多人說以這個價格來說每一【份】都太少了，尤其是飯和肉，所以他們下午還是會餓，之後又去買零食。"}]},{"unit":107,"theme":"Disagreement 意見分歧","cards":[{"w":"argument","p":"n.","d":"a disagreement in which people speak angrily or give different opinions","c":"爭論；爭吵","s":"A: Why did the two supervisors leave the planning meeting so early this morning, and is everything all right between them now? B: They had a loud argument about who should manage the new budget, so the director asked them to calm down and discuss the problem privately after lunch.","t":"A：為什麼那兩位主管今天早上這麼早就離開企劃會議？他們之間現在還好嗎？ B：他們為了誰該管理新預算而大聲【爭論】，所以處長請他們冷靜下來，午餐後再私下討論這個問題。"},{"w":"conflict","p":"n.","d":"a serious disagreement between people or groups","c":"衝突","s":"A: Our project keeps falling behind schedule because the design team and the engineering team never seem to agree on anything important. B: I think we should hire a professional trainer to help them solve this conflict, because the longer it continues, the more money and time the company will lose.","t":"A：我們的專案一直落後進度，因為設計團隊和工程團隊似乎在任何重要的事情上都無法達成共識。 B：我認為我們應該請一位專業講師幫他們解決這個【衝突】，因為它持續越久，公司損失的金錢和時間就越多。"},{"w":"controversy","p":"n.","d":"public disagreement about something that many people have strong opinions on","c":"爭議；爭論","s":"A: Have you read the news about the supermarket chain that suddenly decided to charge customers for every plastic bag at the checkout? B: Yes, the decision caused a lot of controversy online, because some shoppers support the plan to protect the environment, while others think it is simply a way to make more profit.","t":"A：你看過那則關於連鎖超市突然決定在結帳時對每個塑膠袋收費的新聞嗎？ B：看過，這個決定在網路上引起很大的【爭議】，因為有些購物者支持這個保護環境的計畫，而其他人則認為這只是賺更多錢的方法。"},{"w":"discord","p":"n.","d":"a lack of agreement, so people do not get along or work well together","c":"不和；紛爭","s":"A: The new manager seems very friendly, so why are so many people in the accounting office unhappy since she arrived last spring? B: She often gives the best tasks to her old friends, and this has created discord among the staff, so several experienced workers are now looking for other jobs.","t":"A：新經理看起來很友善，為什麼她去年春天到任後，會計辦公室有這麼多人不開心？ B：她常把最好的工作交給她的老朋友，這在員工之間造成了【不和】，所以好幾位有經驗的員工現在正在找其他工作。"},{"w":"friction","p":"n.","d":"disagreement and unfriendly feelings between people who work or live together","c":"摩擦；不和","s":"A: Is it true that the sales staff and the warehouse workers often complain about each other during the busy holiday season? B: Yes, there is some friction between them, because salespeople promise fast delivery to customers while the warehouse simply does not have enough workers to pack all the orders on time.","t":"A：業務人員和倉庫員工在忙碌的假期旺季常常互相抱怨，這是真的嗎？ B：是的，他們之間有些【摩擦】，因為業務員向顧客承諾快速出貨，但倉庫根本沒有足夠的人手準時包裝所有訂單。"},{"w":"tension","p":"n.","d":"a nervous, unfriendly feeling between people who may soon argue","c":"緊張關係；緊繃氣氛","s":"A: You looked uncomfortable at the board meeting yesterday afternoon, so what exactly happened while I was visiting the factory? B: There was a lot of tension in the room, because two directors disagreed about closing the old branch, and nobody wanted to speak until the chairman finally changed the topic.","t":"A：你昨天下午在董事會上看起來很不自在，我去參觀工廠的時候到底發生了什麼事？ B：會議室裡充滿【緊繃氣氛】，因為兩位董事對於關閉舊分店意見不同，沒有人想發言，直到董事長終於轉移了話題。"},{"w":"opposition","p":"n.","d":"strong disagreement with a plan or idea","c":"反對","s":"A: The city wants to build a large shopping mall next to the park, so do you think the plan will be approved soon? B: I doubt it, because there is strong opposition from local residents, who worry about heavy traffic and noise, and they have already collected over five thousand signatures against it.","t":"A：市政府想在公園旁邊蓋一座大型購物中心，你覺得這個計畫很快就會通過嗎？ B：我很懷疑，因為當地居民強烈【反對】，他們擔心交通擁擠和噪音，而且已經收集了超過五千份反對連署。"},{"w":"objection","p":"n.","d":"a reason you give for not agreeing with something","c":"異議；反對理由","s":"A: Before we sign the contract with the new cleaning company next week, does anyone in the department have concerns about the terms? B: My only objection is the price, because their service costs almost twice as much as our current supplier, and I am not sure the quality is really that much better.","t":"A：下週我們和新的清潔公司簽約之前，部門裡有人對條款有疑慮嗎？ B：我唯一的【異議】是價格，因為他們的服務費用幾乎是我們現在廠商的兩倍，而我不確定品質是否真的好那麼多。"},{"w":"row","p":"n.","d":"a noisy, angry argument between people","c":"吵架；爭吵","s":"A: Why did the restaurant manager have to call security last night when the dining room was so busy with customers? B: Two guests started a loud row over a table they had both reserved, and they kept shouting at each other until the staff finally found them separate seats near the window.","t":"A：昨晚用餐區客人這麼多的時候，餐廳經理為什麼必須叫保全？ B：兩位客人為了一張他們都有預約的桌子大聲【吵架】，而且一直對彼此大吼，直到員工終於幫他們在窗邊找到不同的座位。"},{"w":"feud","p":"n.","d":"a long and bitter argument between two people, families or groups","c":"長期不和；宿怨","s":"A: I heard that the two coffee shops on Main Street refuse to join the local business association together, so what is the story behind that? B: The owners are brothers who have had a feud for over ten years since their father left the family business to only one of them, and they still do not speak.","t":"A：我聽說主街上那兩家咖啡店拒絕一起加入當地商業協會，這背後有什麼故事？ B：兩位老闆是兄弟，自從他們的父親把家族事業只留給其中一人後，他們已經【長期不和】超過十年，到現在還是不說話。"},{"w":"rift","p":"n.","d":"a break in a friendly relationship caused by a disagreement","c":"裂痕；嫌隙","s":"A: The two partners started the company together as close friends, so why are they now planning to go their separate ways? B: A serious rift developed between them last year when one partner wanted to expand overseas quickly, while the other believed the business should stay small and safe.","t":"A：兩位合夥人當初是以好朋友的身分一起創立公司的，為什麼他們現在打算分道揚鑣？ B：去年他們之間出現了嚴重的【裂痕】，當時一位合夥人想快速擴展到海外，而另一位則認為公司應該維持小規模、穩健經營。"},{"w":"division","p":"n.","d":"a disagreement that separates people into groups with different opinions","c":"分歧；分裂","s":"A: The staff vote on the new four-day work week was very close, wasn't it, and how do employees feel about the result now? B: Yes, it was, and there is still a clear division in the company, because younger workers love the idea, but many parents worry about the longer working hours each day.","t":"A：員工對新的每週工作四天制度的投票結果非常接近，對吧？員工現在對結果有什麼感受？ B：對，而且公司內部仍有明顯的【分歧】，因為年輕員工很喜歡這個主意，但許多為人父母者擔心每天的工時變長。"},{"w":"differ","p":"v.","d":"to have a different opinion from someone else","c":"意見不同；有分歧","s":"A: You and the marketing director usually agree on most plans, so why didn't you support her idea about the new television advertisement? B: We sometimes differ on how to spend the budget, and this time I believe online videos will reach more young customers for much less money than a TV commercial.","t":"A：你和行銷總監通常在大部分計畫上都意見一致，為什麼你不支持她的新電視廣告構想？ B：我們有時在如何使用預算上會【意見不同】，而這次我認為網路影片能以比電視廣告少得多的錢接觸到更多年輕顧客。"},{"w":"disagree","p":"v.","d":"to have a different opinion; to not agree","c":"不同意","s":"A: The consultant suggested that we should close our store on Sundays to save money on staff costs, so what do you think about that? B: I strongly disagree with that idea, because Sunday is actually our busiest day, and many families come in to shop together after lunch.","t":"A：顧問建議我們週日關店以節省人事成本，你覺得呢？ B：我強烈【不同意】那個想法，因為週日其實是我們最忙的一天，很多家庭會在午餐後一起來購物。"},{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"to disagree with a plan and try to stop it","c":"反對","s":"A: The head office wants to move our entire customer service team to another city next year, so how will the union respond to this plan? B: The union leaders will definitely oppose it, because many workers have children in local schools and cannot easily move their families so far away.","t":"A：總公司想在明年把我們整個客服團隊搬到另一個城市，工會會怎麼回應這個計畫？ B：工會領袖一定會【反對】，因為許多員工的孩子在當地上學，沒辦法輕易舉家搬到那麼遠的地方。"},{"w":"contradict","p":"v.","d":"to say the opposite of what someone else has said","c":"反駁；與…矛盾","s":"A: During the presentation, why did you look so embarrassed when the client asked about our delivery times? B: My assistant started to contradict me in front of everyone, saying that orders actually take two weeks, not five days, and unfortunately the client believed her instead of me.","t":"A：簡報時，客戶問到我們的交貨時間，你為什麼看起來那麼尷尬？ B：我的助理開始當著大家的面【反駁】我，說訂單其實要兩週而不是五天，不幸的是客戶相信她而不是我。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"v.","d":"to question whether something is right, fair or true","c":"質疑；挑戰","s":"A: The new rule says all staff must work in the office five days a week, but many people were much more productive working from home. B: Several team leaders plan to challenge the rule at the next meeting, and they will show data proving that remote work has improved sales and reduced costs.","t":"A：新規定說所有員工每週都必須進辦公室五天，但很多人在家工作時效率高得多。 B：幾位組長打算在下次會議中【質疑】這項規定，他們會提出數據證明遠距工作提升了業績並降低了成本。"},{"w":"object","p":"v.","d":"to say that you do not like or agree with something","c":"反對；不贊成","s":"A: The landlord wants to raise the rent for our office by twenty percent from next month, and he says it is because of higher costs. B: We should object to such a large increase, because our contract clearly says the rent can only go up by five percent each year.","t":"A：房東想從下個月起把我們辦公室的租金調漲百分之二十，他說是因為成本提高。 B：我們應該【反對】這麼大的漲幅，因為我們的合約清楚寫明租金每年只能調漲百分之五。"},{"w":"counter","p":"v.","d":"to answer an argument or attack with an opposite idea or action","c":"反駁；反擊","s":"A: Our biggest competitor just told the media that its products are cheaper and better than ours, so how should we respond? B: We can counter their claims by publishing honest customer reviews and a clear price comparison, which will show that our products last much longer and offer better value.","t":"A：我們最大的競爭對手剛對媒體說他們的產品比我們的更便宜、更好，我們該怎麼回應？ B：我們可以發布真實的顧客評價和清楚的價格比較來【反駁】他們的說法，這會顯示我們的產品耐用得多、更划算。"},{"w":"contest","p":"v.","d":"to say formally that a decision or result is wrong and try to change it","c":"對…提出異議；爭奪","s":"A: The tax office says our company owes a large amount of money from three years ago, but our accountant thinks the numbers are wrong. B: In that case, we should contest the decision formally, and our lawyer can help us prepare all the receipts and documents before the deadline at the end of the month.","t":"A：稅務局說我們公司欠了三年前的一大筆錢，但我們的會計師認為數字有錯。 B：既然如此，我們應該正式對這項決定【提出異議】，我們的律師可以幫我們在月底期限前準備好所有收據和文件。"},{"w":"argumentative","p":"adj.","d":"often arguing or liking to argue","c":"愛爭論的；好爭辯的","s":"A: The new intern is clever and works hard, so why do some of the senior staff prefer not to work with him on projects? B: He can be quite argumentative in meetings, because he questions every small decision and refuses to accept other people's ideas, which makes simple discussions last much longer than necessary.","t":"A：新來的實習生很聰明又努力，為什麼有些資深員工不想和他一起做專案？ B：他在會議上相當【愛爭論】，因為他質疑每個小決定，又拒絕接受別人的想法，讓簡單的討論拖得比需要的久得多。"},{"w":"hostile","p":"adj.","d":"unfriendly and angry toward someone or something","c":"有敵意的；不友善的","s":"A: How did the shareholders react when the CEO announced that there would be no bonus this year after such a successful season? B: The crowd became very hostile, and some people even shouted at him, so he promised to review the decision and explain the company's financial situation more clearly next week.","t":"A：在這麼成功的一季之後，執行長宣布今年不發紅利時，股東們有什麼反應？ B：現場變得非常有【敵意】，有些人甚至對他大吼，所以他答應會重新檢討這個決定，並在下週更清楚說明公司的財務狀況。"},{"w":"antagonistic","p":"adj.","d":"showing strong dislike or opposition toward someone","c":"敵對的；對立的","s":"A: The meeting between the factory owners and the workers' representatives went badly again yesterday, didn't it? B: Yes, both sides were very antagonistic from the start, so instead of discussing the safety problems calmly, they spent most of the afternoon blaming each other for the recent accidents in the factory.","t":"A：工廠老闆和員工代表之間的會議昨天又談得很糟，對吧？ B：對，雙方一開始就非常【敵對】，所以他們沒有冷靜討論安全問題，反而花了大半個下午互相指責工廠最近發生的意外。"},{"w":"divided","p":"adj.","d":"having different opinions, so people are split into groups","c":"意見分歧的；分裂的","s":"A: Has the board finally decided whether to open a new branch in Tokyo or to invest more money in our online store instead? B: Not yet, because the members are still divided on the issue, and half of them think Japan is too risky while the others believe it is a great opportunity.","t":"A：董事會終於決定要在東京開新分公司，還是要把更多錢投資在我們的網路商店了嗎？ B：還沒，因為成員們在這個問題上仍然【意見分歧】，一半的人認為日本風險太高，而其他人則相信這是個大好機會。"},{"w":"irreconcilable","p":"adj.","d":"so different that agreement is impossible","c":"無法調和的；不可和解的","s":"A: Why did the two companies cancel their merger at the last minute after spending so many months on negotiations? B: They had irreconcilable differences about who would control the new company, and neither side was willing to give up power, so in the end they decided to walk away.","t":"A：兩家公司花了好幾個月談判，為什麼在最後一刻取消合併？ B：他們對於誰來掌控新公司有【無法調和的】歧見，雙方都不願意放棄權力，所以最後決定放棄。"},{"w":"opposed","p":"adj.","d":"disagreeing strongly with something","c":"反對的","s":"A: The government plans to build a new airport runway close to several villages, so what do the local farmers think about it? B: Most of them are firmly opposed to the project, because the noise will disturb their animals, and they are afraid that they will lose part of their land without fair payment.","t":"A：政府打算在幾個村莊附近興建新的機場跑道，當地農民對此有什麼看法？ B：他們大多數人堅決【反對】這項計畫，因為噪音會干擾他們的動物，而且他們擔心會在沒有合理補償的情況下失去部分土地。"},{"w":"disputably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that can be questioned or argued about","c":"有爭議地；可質疑地","s":"A: The magazine called our new smartphone the best on the market this year, so should we print that on all our advertisements? B: That ranking is disputably correct at best, because several other phones scored higher in battery tests, so let's use a safer message to avoid complaints from customers.","t":"A：雜誌稱我們的新智慧型手機是今年市場上最好的，我們應該把這句話印在所有廣告上嗎？ B：這個排名充其量只是【有爭議地】正確，因為其他幾款手機在電池測試中得分更高，所以我們用比較保險的訊息，以免顧客抱怨。"},{"w":"controversially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes public disagreement","c":"有爭議地；引起爭議地","s":"A: Did the bank really decide to close all of its small branches in the countryside, even though many older customers still depend on them? B: Yes, and quite controversially, it also announced that customers must now pay a fee to speak with a staff member, which has made many people extremely angry.","t":"A：那家銀行真的決定關閉所有鄉下的小分行嗎？即使許多年長顧客仍仰賴它們。 B：是的，而且相當【引起爭議】的是，它還宣布顧客現在必須付費才能和行員交談，這讓許多人非常憤怒。"}]},{"unit":108,"theme":"Discussion 討論","cards":[{"w":"talkative","p":"adj.","d":"liking to talk a lot","c":"健談的；愛說話的","s":"A: Who should we ask to lead the small-group discussion at the client workshop next week, since we need someone who can keep the conversation going? B: I think Kevin would be perfect, because he is very talkative and friendly, and he never lets an awkward silence last long when people are too shy to share their ideas.","t":"A：下週客戶研習會的小組討論該請誰來帶領？我們需要一個能讓對話持續下去的人。 B：我覺得凱文是最佳人選，因為他非常【健談】又友善，當大家太害羞不敢分享想法時，他從不讓尷尬的沉默持續太久。"},{"w":"mature","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in a sensible way, like a responsible adult","c":"成熟的；穩重的","s":"A: Why did the manager choose Linda to handle the angry customer's complaint during yesterday's meeting, even though she is the youngest person on the team? B: Although she is only twenty-four, she is very mature for her age, and she always stays calm and listens carefully before she offers a solution to any problem.","t":"A：為什麼經理在昨天的會議上選琳達來處理那位生氣客戶的投訴？她明明是團隊裡最年輕的人。 B：雖然她才二十四歲，但以她的年紀來說非常【成熟】，而且她在提出任何問題的解決方法之前，總是保持冷靜並仔細聆聽。"},{"w":"paranormal","p":"adj.","d":"strange and impossible to explain by science, such as ghosts","c":"超自然的；靈異的","s":"A: The marketing team is discussing ideas for the new mobile game, so what kind of story do you think young players would enjoy most this year? B: Many of them love mysterious stories about ghosts and strange powers, so I suggest a paranormal adventure in which players explore an old hotel and solve puzzles that science cannot explain.","t":"A：行銷團隊正在討論新手機遊戲的點子，你覺得今年年輕玩家最喜歡哪種故事？ B：他們很多人喜歡關於鬼魂和奇異力量的神祕故事，所以我建議做一個【超自然】冒險，讓玩家探索一間老飯店，並解開科學無法解釋的謎題。"},{"w":"cartoon","p":"n.","d":"a funny drawing or a short film made of drawings","c":"卡通；漫畫","s":"A: Our new safety video for factory workers is long and rather boring, so how can we make the important rules easier to remember during the training session? B: Why don't we ask the design team to create a short cartoon with funny characters, since people usually pay more attention to colorful drawings than to long lists of rules?","t":"A：我們給工廠員工看的新安全影片又長又無聊，在訓練課程中要怎樣讓重要規定更容易記住？ B：我們何不請設計團隊製作一部有趣角色的短篇【卡通】？因為大家通常對彩色圖畫比對一長串規定更專心。"},{"w":"fashion","p":"n.","d":"the popular style of clothes, hair, etc. at a particular time","c":"時尚；流行","s":"A: The clothing company wants to open a new store downtown, so what did the managers decide at this morning's planning meeting? B: They agreed to hold a fashion show on opening day, because young customers love seeing the latest styles on real models, and it will also attract reporters from local newspapers and websites.","t":"A：這家服飾公司想在市中心開一家新店，經理們在今天早上的規劃會議上決定了什麼？ B：他們同意在開幕當天舉辦一場【時裝】秀，因為年輕顧客喜歡看真人模特兒展示最新款式，而且這也會吸引當地報紙和網站的記者。"},{"w":"extroverted","p":"adj.","d":"outgoing and enjoying being with other people","c":"外向的","s":"A: We are hiring a new event coordinator who must greet guests and speak to large groups, so what kind of person are we looking for? B: We need someone extroverted who feels comfortable meeting strangers and enjoys being the center of attention, because a quiet person might find the busy conference days very tiring.","t":"A：我們要招募一位新的活動協調人，他必須接待賓客並對大批群眾說話，我們要找什麼樣的人？ B：我們需要一個【外向】的人，能自在地與陌生人見面並喜歡成為眾人注目的焦點，因為安靜的人可能會覺得忙碌的會議日子非常累人。"},{"w":"affair","p":"n.","d":"an event or matter, especially one of a particular kind","c":"事情；事務；（某種）活動","s":"A: How much did the company spend on last month's product launch, and why does the finance director want to discuss it at Friday's meeting? B: The launch turned out to be an expensive affair, because we rented a large hall and hired famous speakers, so the director wants to talk about cheaper options before we plan the next event.","t":"A：公司上個月的產品發表會花了多少錢？為什麼財務長想在星期五的會議上討論這件事？ B：那場發表會結果是一件花費高昂的【事】，因為我們租了大型會場又請了知名講者，所以財務長想在規劃下一場活動前討論更便宜的方案。"},{"w":"horror","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of fear and shock; stories or films meant to scare people","c":"恐怖；驚恐","s":"A: The team-building night is on Friday, and someone suggested watching a movie together after dinner, so what kind of film should we choose? B: Let's avoid a horror movie, because several colleagues said they hate scary scenes and blood, and a light comedy would help everyone relax and laugh together after such a stressful month.","t":"A：團隊建立之夜在星期五，有人建議晚餐後一起看電影，我們該選哪種片？ B：我們避開【恐怖】片吧，因為好幾位同事說他們討厭嚇人的場面和血腥畫面，而輕鬆的喜劇能讓大家在壓力這麼大的一個月後放鬆、一起開懷大笑。"},{"w":"captivating","p":"adj.","d":"so interesting or attractive that it holds your attention","c":"迷人的；引人入勝的","s":"A: How was the guest speaker at this morning's sales conference, and did people stay until the end of her presentation? B: Her talk was so captivating that nobody looked at their phones for an hour, because she told real stories about her mistakes and showed how she turned a small shop into a national business.","t":"A：今天早上業務會議的客座講者表現如何？大家有待到她簡報結束嗎？ B：她的演講非常【引人入勝】，整整一小時都沒人看手機，因為她講了自己犯錯的真實故事，並說明她如何把一家小店發展成全國性企業。"},{"w":"conscious","p":"adj.","d":"noticing or knowing about something","c":"意識到的；察覺的","s":"A: Why did the new manager change the way we run our weekly team meetings, and why does everyone now get two minutes to speak? B: She is very conscious of the fact that quieter employees rarely share their opinions, so she wants to make sure that every person has a fair chance to be heard.","t":"A：新經理為什麼改變我們每週團隊會議的進行方式？為什麼現在每個人都有兩分鐘的發言時間？ B：她非常【意識到】比較安靜的員工很少分享意見，所以她想確保每個人都有公平的機會被聽見。"},{"w":"convincing","p":"adj.","d":"making you believe that something is true or right","c":"有說服力的；令人信服的","s":"A: Did the finance department accept your proposal to buy new laptops for the whole sales team during this afternoon's budget meeting? B: Yes, they agreed in the end, because I gave them a convincing reason with clear numbers that showed how much time and money the new machines would save us over the next three years.","t":"A：財務部門在今天下午的預算會議上接受你為整個業務團隊購買新筆電的提案了嗎？ B：有，他們最後同意了，因為我給了他們一個【有說服力的】理由，並用清楚的數字顯示新電腦在未來三年能幫我們省下多少時間和金錢。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at two or more things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"A: We have received three different offers for the new office printers, so how should we decide which company to choose at Thursday's meeting? B: Let's make a simple chart to compare the prices, the speed and the repair services of each machine, so everyone can see the differences clearly before we vote.","t":"A：我們收到了三份新辦公室印表機的不同報價，星期四開會時該怎麼決定選哪家公司？ B：我們做一張簡單的圖表來【比較】每台機器的價格、速度和維修服務，這樣大家在投票前就能清楚看出差異。"},{"w":"brutally","p":"adv.","d":"in a very direct and harsh way that may hurt feelings","c":"殘酷地；毫不留情地","s":"A: I asked Mark to give me feedback on my presentation before the client meeting, but why did he say so many negative things about it? B: He can be brutally honest sometimes, but he only wants to help you, and if you fix the weak points he mentioned, your talk will be much stronger tomorrow.","t":"A：我在客戶會議前請馬克給我的簡報一些意見，但他為什麼說了那麼多負面的話？ B：他有時候會坦白得【毫不留情】，但他只是想幫你，如果你修正他提到的弱點，你明天的報告會好很多。"},{"w":"embarrassed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling shy, ashamed or uncomfortable in front of others","c":"尷尬的；難為情的","s":"A: Why did Tom leave the conference room so quickly after the meeting ended, and is he upset about something that happened? B: He felt very embarrassed because he called the new client by the wrong name twice during the discussion, but I told him that everyone makes small mistakes like that sometimes.","t":"A：湯姆為什麼會議一結束就那麼快離開會議室？他是對發生的事情感到不高興嗎？ B：他覺得非常【尷尬】，因為他在討論中兩次叫錯新客戶的名字，但我告訴他每個人有時候都會犯這種小錯。"},{"w":"hesitate","p":"v.","d":"to stop or wait before doing something because you are unsure","c":"猶豫；遲疑","s":"A: I have some ideas about how to reduce our shipping costs, but I am new here, so is it all right to share them at tomorrow's team meeting? B: Of course, please don't hesitate to speak up, because our manager always welcomes fresh opinions, and new employees often notice problems that the rest of us have stopped seeing.","t":"A：我對如何降低運費有些想法，但我是新來的，可以在明天的團隊會議上分享嗎？ B：當然可以，請不要【猶豫】，儘管發言，因為我們經理總是歡迎新的意見，而新員工常會注意到我們其他人已經視而不見的問題。"},{"w":"habitually","p":"adv.","d":"as a usual habit; regularly","c":"習慣性地；慣常地","s":"A: Why does the director always start our Monday meetings ten minutes late, and should we say something to her about it? B: She habitually checks her email and answers urgent questions from overseas customers first thing every Monday, so I think we should simply move the meeting to nine-fifteen instead of complaining.","t":"A：為什麼主管總是讓星期一的會議晚十分鐘開始？我們應該跟她說些什麼嗎？ B：她每週一早上一來都【習慣性地】先查看電子郵件並回覆海外客戶的緊急問題，所以我覺得我們乾脆把會議改到九點十五分，而不是抱怨。"},{"w":"stick","p":"v.","d":"to keep following a plan, decision or rule without changing it","c":"堅持；遵守（stick to）","s":"A: The discussion about the new advertising plan took almost three hours yesterday, so has the team finally made a decision about the budget? B: Yes, after looking at several other ideas, we decided to stick to the original plan, because it is cheaper and the managers believe it will still reach enough young customers.","t":"A：昨天關於新廣告計畫的討論花了將近三個小時，團隊終於對預算做出決定了嗎？ B：有，在看過其他幾個點子之後，我們決定【堅持】原本的計畫，因為它比較便宜，而且經理們相信它仍然能接觸到足夠多的年輕顧客。"},{"w":"seldomly","p":"adv.","d":"not often; rarely (a less common form of seldom)","c":"很少；不常","s":"A: How often does the regional manager join our weekly sales discussions, and should we prepare a special report in case she comes? B: She seldomly attends our meetings because she travels to other branches most of the month, but it is still a good idea to have the latest numbers ready just in case.","t":"A：區域經理多久參加一次我們每週的業務討論？我們要準備一份特別報告以防她出席嗎？ B：她【很少】參加我們的會議，因為她一個月大部分時間都在其他分店出差，不過還是把最新數字準備好以防萬一比較好。"},{"w":"randomly","p":"adv.","d":"by chance, without any plan or order","c":"隨機地；任意地","s":"A: Our weekly brainstorming meetings always have the same three people talking, so how can we get the others to join the discussion? B: Next time, let's randomly choose names from a box and ask each person to share one idea, so everyone has to prepare and nobody can stay silent for the whole hour.","t":"A：我們每週的腦力激盪會議總是同樣三個人在講話，要怎麼讓其他人加入討論？ B：下次我們從箱子裡【隨機】抽名字，請每個人分享一個想法，這樣大家都得事先準備，也沒有人能整整一小時都不說話。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make something better","c":"改善；改進","s":"A: Customers have complained that our online ordering system is slow and confusing, so what did the IT team suggest at the meeting? B: They plan to improve the website by making the menu simpler and adding a faster payment page, and they hope to finish the changes before the busy holiday season starts in December.","t":"A：顧客抱怨我們的線上訂購系統又慢又難用，資訊團隊在會議上提出了什麼建議？ B：他們計畫透過簡化選單和新增更快速的付款頁面來【改善】網站，並希望在十二月忙碌的假期旺季開始前完成這些修改。"},{"w":"critically","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful way that looks for faults and judges whether something is good","c":"批判性地；嚴格審視地","s":"A: The new marketing report is ready, but before we present it to the board on Monday, what should our team do with it? B: Each of us should read it critically and look for weak points, missing data or unclear charts, because the board members will ask difficult questions and we need to have good answers ready.","t":"A：新的行銷報告已經完成了，但在星期一向董事會報告之前，我們團隊應該怎麼處理它？ B：我們每個人都應該【批判性地】閱讀它，找出弱點、遺漏的數據或不清楚的圖表，因為董事們會問困難的問題，我們需要準備好完善的答案。"},{"w":"diligently","p":"adv.","d":"in a hard-working and careful way","c":"勤奮地；認真地","s":"A: How did the new assistant manage to finish the entire customer survey report in only one week, when it usually takes us almost a month? B: She worked very diligently every day, checked each answer carefully and asked questions at our team discussions whenever something was unclear, so the director was really impressed with her effort.","t":"A：新來的助理是怎麼只用一週就完成整份顧客問卷報告的？我們通常要花將近一個月。 B：她每天都非常【勤奮地】工作，仔細檢查每份回答，並在團隊討論中遇到不清楚的地方就提問，所以主管對她的努力印象深刻。"}]},{"unit":109,"theme":"Doing Something Well 做得好","cards":[{"w":"excel","p":"v.","d":"to be very good at something","c":"擅長；表現優異","s":"A: We need someone to lead the presentation for the new client next week, but most of our team feels nervous about speaking in front of large groups. B: Why don't we ask Jenny from marketing, because she tends to excel at public speaking and always explains complex ideas in a clear and friendly way?","t":"A：下週我們需要有人帶領對新客戶的簡報，但團隊大多數人在一大群人面前講話都會緊張。 B：何不請行銷部的珍妮來呢？因為她向來【擅長】公開演講，總能用清楚又親切的方式解釋複雜的想法。"},{"w":"succeed","p":"v.","d":"to get the result that you wanted","c":"成功","s":"A: I heard the small coffee shop on the corner was almost forced to close last year because of high rent and fewer customers. B: That's true, but the owner started selling coffee beans online and offering delivery, so she managed to succeed in turning the business around within just six months.","t":"A：我聽說轉角那家小咖啡店去年因為房租高、客人變少，差點被迫歇業。 B：沒錯，但老闆開始在網路上賣咖啡豆並提供外送，所以她在短短六個月內就【成功】讓生意起死回生。"},{"w":"accomplish","p":"v.","d":"to finish something successfully","c":"完成；達成","s":"A: The warehouse team had to pack and ship more than two thousand orders before the holiday weekend, which seemed impossible with only eight workers. B: I know, but they divided the work carefully and took short breaks, so they were able to accomplish the whole task a day earlier than expected.","t":"A：倉庫團隊必須在連假週末前包裝並寄出兩千多張訂單，只有八名員工看起來根本不可能。 B：我知道，但他們仔細分工又適時短暫休息，所以比預期提早一天就【完成】了全部任務。"},{"w":"achieve","p":"v.","d":"to reach a goal or result by working hard","c":"達到；實現","s":"A: Our department has set a goal of cutting paper use by thirty percent this year, but some people still print every single email they receive. B: If we want to achieve that target, we should store all documents online and remind everyone at the weekly meeting about the cost of printing.","t":"A：我們部門今年設定了減少百分之三十用紙量的目標，但有些人還是會把收到的每一封電子郵件都印出來。 B：如果我們想【達成】那個目標，就應該把所有文件存在線上，並在每週會議上提醒大家列印的成本。"},{"w":"master","p":"v.","d":"to learn something completely so you can do it very well","c":"精通；掌握","s":"A: The company is switching to a new accounting program next month, and I'm worried because I'm not very good with computers. B: Don't worry, because the IT department is offering free training sessions every Tuesday, and most people are able to master the basic functions after a few weeks of practice.","t":"A：公司下個月要換新的會計軟體，我很擔心，因為我不太會用電腦。 B：別擔心，資訊部門每週二都有免費的訓練課程，大部分人練習幾週後就能【掌握】基本功能。"},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to do a job or activity, well or badly","c":"表現；執行","s":"A: How did the new sales staff do during their first month, and should we keep all of them after the trial period ends? B: Most of them did a great job, but two of them didn't perform as well as we expected, so their manager will give them extra training before making a final decision.","t":"A：新進業務人員第一個月的表現如何？試用期結束後我們應該全部留下嗎？ B：大部分人都做得很好，但其中兩位的【表現】不如我們預期，所以他們的經理在做最後決定前會再給他們額外訓練。"},{"w":"thrive","p":"v.","d":"to grow, develop or succeed very well","c":"茁壯成長；蓬勃發展","s":"A: Do you think our new branch in the city center will do well, even though there are already many restaurants in that area? B: I believe it will thrive, because office workers there are always looking for healthy lunch options, and our prices are lower than most of the places nearby.","t":"A：你覺得我們在市中心的新分店會經營得好嗎？那一區已經有很多餐廳了。 B：我相信它會【蓬勃發展】，因為那裡的上班族一直在找健康的午餐選擇，而且我們的價格比附近大多數店家都便宜。"},{"w":"shine","p":"v.","d":"to do something very well and be noticed","c":"表現出色；發光","s":"A: Tom is usually very quiet in team meetings, so I was surprised when the director chose him to give the speech at the product launch. B: He spent weeks preparing, and when he finally stood on the stage, he really began to shine, and the audience loved his funny stories about our customers.","t":"A：湯姆在團隊會議中通常很安靜，所以主管選他在產品發表會上致詞時我很驚訝。 B：他花了好幾週準備，當他終於站上台時，真的【大放異彩】，觀眾都很喜歡他講的那些關於我們顧客的有趣故事。"},{"w":"flourish","p":"v.","d":"to grow or develop successfully","c":"繁榮；興盛","s":"A: Ten years ago this street had only a few old shops, but now it is full of cafés, bookstores and small design studios. B: Yes, after the city built a new subway station nearby, local businesses began to flourish, and rents have gone up because so many people want to open stores here.","t":"A：十年前這條街只有幾家老店，但現在到處都是咖啡廳、書店和小型設計工作室。 B：對，自從市政府在附近蓋了新的捷運站後，當地商家開始【繁榮興盛】，而且因為很多人想在這裡開店，租金也上漲了。"},{"w":"impress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone admire or respect you","c":"使印象深刻；使欽佩","s":"A: I have a final interview with the bank's regional manager tomorrow morning, and I really want this job more than anything. B: To impress her, you should research the bank's recent projects, prepare a few smart questions, and arrive at least fifteen minutes early wearing a neat business suit.","t":"A：我明天早上要和銀行的區域經理進行最後一輪面試，我真的非常想要這份工作。 B：要讓她【留下深刻印象】，你應該研究一下銀行最近的專案、準備幾個聰明的問題，並穿著整齊的套裝至少提早十五分鐘到。"},{"w":"competence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something well enough","c":"能力；勝任","s":"A: Why does the hospital ask all of its nurses to take a practical test every year, even the ones who have worked there for a long time? B: Medical equipment and rules change quickly, so the hospital needs to check each nurse's competence regularly to make sure patients always receive safe and correct care.","t":"A：為什麼醫院要求所有護理師每年都要參加實作測驗，連工作很久的人也要？ B：醫療設備和規定變化很快，所以醫院需要定期檢查每位護理師的【能力】，以確保病人總是得到安全又正確的照護。"},{"w":"proficiency","p":"n.","d":"a high level of ability or skill in something","c":"精通；熟練程度","s":"A: The job advertisement for the hotel front desk says that applicants need to speak English, but how will the manager know how good my English is? B: You will probably need to show a recent test score or certificate that proves your proficiency, and the manager may also ask you some questions in English during the interview.","t":"A：飯店櫃檯的徵人廣告說應徵者需要會說英文，但經理要怎麼知道我的英文程度有多好？ B：你可能需要出示近期的考試成績或證書來證明你的【熟練程度】，而且經理在面試時也可能會用英文問你一些問題。"},{"w":"expertise","p":"n.","d":"special knowledge or skill in a particular area","c":"專業知識；專門技能","s":"A: Our company wants to start selling products in Southeast Asia, but none of us know much about the laws and customs in those countries. B: In that case, we should hire a consultant who has real expertise in that market, because one costly mistake could damage our reputation before we even open our first store.","t":"A：我們公司想開始在東南亞銷售產品，但我們沒有人很了解那些國家的法律和習俗。 B：既然這樣，我們應該聘請一位在那個市場具有真正【專業知識】的顧問，因為一個代價高昂的錯誤可能在我們開第一家店之前就損害我們的聲譽。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"an ability to do something well that comes from training or practice","c":"技能；技巧","s":"A: I have been working as a cashier for two years, and now I would like to apply for a position as an assistant manager at the store. B: That's a good plan, and the most useful skill you can build right now is leadership, so offer to train new staff members and handle customer complaints whenever your supervisor is busy.","t":"A：我當收銀員已經兩年了，現在想應徵店裡副理的職位。 B：這是個好計畫，而你現在最值得培養的【技能】就是領導力，所以要主動訓練新進員工，並在主管忙碌時處理顧客的抱怨。"},{"w":"talent","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability to do something well","c":"天賦；才能","s":"A: Did you know that Kevin from the accounting department designed the poster for our charity concert, even though he has never studied art? B: Yes, I saw it, and everyone was amazed, so I think the marketing team should invite him to help them because he clearly has a natural talent for design.","t":"A：你知道會計部的凱文設計了我們慈善音樂會的海報嗎？他從來沒學過美術。 B：知道，我看到了，大家都很驚豔，所以我覺得行銷團隊應該邀請他幫忙，因為他顯然在設計方面有與生俱來的【天賦】。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"a good quality or ability that makes someone effective","c":"優點；長處","s":"A: During my job interview yesterday, the manager asked me about my greatest strength, and I didn't know what to say, so I just talked about being hardworking. B: Next time, give a specific example, such as how you organized a busy event or solved a difficult problem, because examples are much more convincing than general words.","t":"A：我昨天面試時，經理問我最大的【優點】是什麼，我不知道該說什麼，所以只說了自己很勤奮。 B：下次要舉具體的例子，像是你如何籌辦一場忙碌的活動或解決一個困難的問題，因為例子比空泛的話更有說服力。"},{"w":"excellence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being extremely good","c":"卓越；優秀","s":"A: Why is there a long line of people waiting outside that small noodle shop every day, even though there are cheaper restaurants on the same street? B: The owner has won several awards for excellence in cooking, and she still makes fresh noodles by hand every morning, so customers know they will get great food.","t":"A：為什麼那家小麵店外面每天都大排長龍，即使同一條街上有更便宜的餐廳？ B：老闆曾多次獲得烹飪【卓越】獎，而且她每天早上仍然親手做新鮮的麵條，所以顧客知道一定能吃到很棒的食物。"},{"w":"perfection","p":"n.","d":"the state of being perfect, with no mistakes","c":"完美","s":"A: Our designer has changed the company logo eleven times this month, and the printing company is still waiting for the final version. B: I understand that she wants perfection, but we have a deadline on Friday, so please tell her that a very good design is enough and we must send the file today.","t":"A：我們的設計師這個月已經改了公司標誌十一次，印刷公司還在等最終版本。 B：我了解她追求【完美】，但我們星期五就要截止了，所以請告訴她一個很好的設計就夠了，我們今天必須把檔案送出去。"},{"w":"successfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that gets the result you wanted","c":"成功地","s":"A: Was the IT team able to move all of our customer data to the new system over the weekend, or will there be problems on Monday morning? B: Good news, the data was successfully transferred on Sunday night, and the team checked every file twice, so all the sales staff can log in normally today.","t":"A：資訊團隊週末有辦法把我們所有的客戶資料轉移到新系統嗎？還是星期一早上會出問題？ B：好消息，資料在星期天晚上已經【成功地】轉移完成，團隊也把每個檔案檢查了兩次，所以所有業務人員今天都可以正常登入。"},{"w":"skillfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows great ability","c":"熟練地；巧妙地","s":"A: The customer at table five was shouting about his cold soup, and I was afraid he would leave a terrible review online. B: Luckily, our manager skillfully handled the situation by apologizing calmly, bringing him a fresh bowl and offering a free dessert, and in the end he left with a smile.","t":"A：五號桌的客人在大聲抱怨他的湯是冷的，我很怕他會在網路上留下很差的評論。 B：幸好我們的經理【巧妙地】處理了這個狀況，冷靜地道歉、送上一碗新的湯並招待免費甜點，最後他是笑著離開的。"},{"w":"efficiently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that does not waste time, money or energy","c":"有效率地","s":"A: Our office electricity bill has almost doubled since last summer, and the finance manager wants to know why we are spending so much money. B: The old air conditioners don't run efficiently anymore, so I suggest we replace them with modern models that use less power and still keep the rooms cool.","t":"A：我們辦公室的電費從去年夏天以來幾乎翻倍，財務經理想知道為什麼我們花這麼多錢。 B：舊的冷氣機已經無法【有效率地】運轉了，所以我建議換成更省電、又能讓房間保持涼爽的新型機種。"},{"w":"effectively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that produces the result you want","c":"有效地","s":"A: Many customers have told us that our online instructions are confusing, and they keep calling the help line with the same simple questions. B: We need to explain the steps more effectively, so let's add short videos and clear pictures to the website, which should reduce the number of phone calls.","t":"A：很多顧客跟我們說線上說明令人困惑，他們一直打客服專線問同樣簡單的問題。 B：我們需要更【有效地】說明步驟，所以在網站上加入簡短的影片和清楚的圖片吧，這樣應該能減少來電數量。"},{"w":"competently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows enough ability to do something well","c":"稱職地；能幹地","s":"A: How did the new receptionist manage on her first day when the phones were ringing nonstop and three visitors arrived at the same time? B: She stayed calm and dealt with everything competently, so I think she will become a valuable member of the front office team very quickly.","t":"A：新來的櫃檯接待員第一天上班時電話響個不停，又同時來了三位訪客，她應付得怎麼樣？ B：她保持冷靜，把所有事情都處理得很【稱職】，所以我覺得她很快就會成為櫃檯團隊中重要的一員。"},{"w":"brilliant","p":"adj.","d":"extremely clever or very good","c":"傑出的；絕妙的","s":"A: Our sales were very low last winter, so does anyone have an idea for bringing more customers into the store during the cold months? B: Mia suggested offering free hot chocolate to anyone who buys a coat, and I think it's a brilliant idea because it's cheap and makes people feel welcome.","t":"A：我們去年冬天的業績很差，有沒有人有在寒冷月份吸引更多顧客上門的點子？ B：米亞建議買外套就送免費熱可可，我覺得這是個【絕妙的】點子，因為成本低又能讓人覺得受歡迎。"},{"w":"excellent","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good","c":"極好的；優秀的","s":"A: I'm planning a dinner for twelve clients from Korea next Thursday, so could you recommend a restaurant that is quiet enough for business conversation? B: The Garden Room near the train station has excellent service and private dining areas, and the chef can also prepare dishes for guests who don't eat meat.","t":"A：下週四我要為十二位韓國客戶安排晚餐，你能推薦一家夠安靜、適合談生意的餐廳嗎？ B：火車站附近的花園廳有【極好的】服務和包廂，主廚也能為不吃肉的客人準備菜色。"},{"w":"outstanding","p":"adj.","d":"much better than others","c":"傑出的；出色的","s":"A: Who do you think will receive the employee of the year award at the company party, since so many people worked hard this year? B: My guess is Daniel, because his outstanding performance helped us win four new contracts, and he also trained all the new staff in the sales department.","t":"A：你覺得誰會在公司派對上獲得年度最佳員工獎？今年有這麼多人都很努力。 B：我猜是丹尼爾，因為他【傑出的】表現幫我們拿下四份新合約，他還訓練了業務部所有的新進人員。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good; much better than normal","c":"優異的；非凡的","s":"A: The hotel received hundreds of positive reviews last month, and many guests mentioned one particular staff member by name. B: That must be Lisa at the front desk, because she provides exceptional service, remembers every regular guest's name and often solves problems before customers even notice them.","t":"A：飯店上個月收到幾百則好評，很多房客都指名提到某一位員工。 B：那一定是櫃檯的莉莎，因為她提供【非常優異的】服務，記得每位常客的名字，而且常常在顧客發現之前就把問題解決了。"},{"w":"superb","p":"adj.","d":"of very high quality; excellent","c":"極好的；一流的","s":"A: How was the company retreat at the mountain resort last weekend, and would you recommend the place for next year's training camp? B: Absolutely, the food was superb, the meeting rooms had modern equipment, and we could enjoy a beautiful view of the lake during every coffee break.","t":"A：上週末在山區度假村的公司員工旅遊怎麼樣？你會推薦那裡作為明年訓練營的地點嗎？ B：當然會，那裡的食物【一流】，會議室有現代化設備，而且每次休息喝咖啡時都能欣賞美麗的湖景。"},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adj.","d":"unusual or special in a way that makes people notice","c":"非凡的；驚人的","s":"A: I heard that the new manager at our Taichung branch has completely changed the way the office works in just a few months. B: Yes, the results are remarkable, because sales have gone up by forty percent, staff turnover has dropped, and customers say the service is much faster now.","t":"A：我聽說我們台中分公司的新經理在短短幾個月內就徹底改變了辦公室的運作方式。 B：是的，成果相當【驚人】，業績成長了百分之四十，員工流動率下降，顧客也說現在的服務快多了。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"making people admire it because it is very good","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"A: Did you see the presentation that the design team gave to the investors this morning about our new electric scooter? B: Yes, it was very impressive, because they showed a working model, explained the costs clearly, and answered every difficult question without looking at their notes.","t":"A：你有看到設計團隊今天早上向投資人介紹我們新款電動機車的簡報嗎？ B：有，非常【令人印象深刻】，因為他們展示了可運作的模型、清楚說明了成本，而且不看筆記就回答了每個困難的問題。"},{"w":"capable","p":"adj.","d":"having the ability to do something","c":"有能力的；能幹的","s":"A: The director will be away on a business trip for three weeks, so who is going to make important decisions about the budget while she is gone? B: She has asked Mr. Chen to take charge, and I think he is fully capable of running the department because he has managed large projects before.","t":"A：主任要出差三週，她不在的期間誰來做預算方面的重要決定？ B：她請陳先生負責，我認為他完全【有能力】管理這個部門，因為他以前就管理過大型專案。"},{"w":"adept","p":"adj.","d":"very good at doing something that needs skill","c":"熟練的；擅長的","s":"A: Our online store gets a lot of angry messages when deliveries are late, and some of the new staff don't know how to reply politely. B: Ask Grace to train them, because she is very adept at calming upset customers and always finds a fair solution that keeps them shopping with us.","t":"A：每當送貨延遲，我們的網路商店就會收到很多憤怒的訊息，有些新進員工不知道該如何禮貌地回覆。 B：請葛蕾絲來訓練他們，因為她非常【擅長】安撫生氣的顧客，總能找到公平的解決辦法，讓他們繼續在我們這裡購物。"},{"w":"proficient","p":"adj.","d":"able to do something well because of training and practice","c":"精通的；熟練的","s":"A: The new position in our Tokyo office involves talking with Japanese suppliers every day, so what kind of person are we looking for? B: The ideal candidate should be proficient in both Japanese and English, and should also have some experience with shipping schedules and international contracts.","t":"A：我們東京辦公室的新職缺每天都要和日本供應商溝通，那我們要找什麼樣的人？ B：理想的人選應該【精通】日文和英文，並且也要有一些處理船運時程和國際合約的經驗。"},{"w":"gifted","p":"adj.","d":"having a natural ability to do something very well","c":"有天賦的；有才華的","s":"A: I heard that the young pianist who played at our company's anniversary dinner is only fourteen years old and has already won several international competitions. B: Yes, she is a truly gifted musician, and our CEO was so moved by her performance that he offered to sponsor her studies at a music school in Vienna.","t":"A：我聽說在我們公司週年晚宴上演奏的年輕鋼琴家只有十四歲，卻已經贏過好幾場國際比賽。 B：是的，她是一位真正【有天賦的】音樂家，我們的執行長被她的演出深深感動，主動提出要贊助她到維也納的音樂學校念書。"},{"w":"successful","p":"adj.","d":"achieving the result that you wanted","c":"成功的","s":"A: How did the charity sale go last Saturday, and did we raise enough money to buy new computers for the local library? B: It was very successful, because more than three hundred people came, we sold almost everything, and we collected twice as much money as we had planned.","t":"A：上週六的義賣進行得怎麼樣？我們有籌到足夠的錢為當地圖書館買新電腦嗎？ B：非常【成功】，有三百多人到場，我們幾乎把東西都賣光了，募到的錢是原本計畫的兩倍。"},{"w":"well","p":"adv.","d":"in a good, skillful or satisfactory way","c":"好地；順利地","s":"A: How did the meeting with the hospital's purchasing manager go this afternoon, and do you think they will order our new medical beds? B: It went really well, because she liked our product demonstration, asked about bulk discounts, and wants to visit our factory next week before signing the contract.","t":"A：今天下午和醫院採購經理的會議進行得怎麼樣？你覺得他們會訂購我們的新款病床嗎？ B：進行得非常【順利】，因為她很喜歡我們的產品示範、詢問了大量購買的折扣，還想在簽約前於下週參觀我們的工廠。"}]},{"unit":110,"theme":"Drama 戲劇","cards":[{"w":"theatre","p":"n.","d":"a building where plays and shows are performed","c":"劇院；戲院","s":"A: Our sales team reached its yearly target last month, so how should we celebrate with them before the holiday break begins? B: I suggest we buy group tickets for the new musical at the theatre downtown, because the show starts at seven, and we can have dinner at the Italian restaurant across the street first.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊上個月達成了年度目標，在假期開始前我們該怎麼和他們一起慶祝？ B：我建議我們買市中心那家【劇院】新音樂劇的團體票，因為表演七點開始，我們可以先在對街的義大利餐廳吃晚餐。"},{"w":"play","p":"n.","d":"a story that actors perform on a stage","c":"戲劇；劇本","s":"A: The company is sponsoring a local arts festival this year, so what kind of event will our logo appear on in the program? B: Our logo will be printed on the posters for a play about a small family business, which a group of college students wrote themselves and will perform three times next weekend at the community center.","t":"A：公司今年贊助一個地方藝術節，我們的標誌會出現在節目單上的哪種活動？ B：我們的標誌會印在一齣關於小型家族企業的【戲劇】海報上，那是一群大學生自己寫的，下週末將在社區中心演出三場。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of singing, dancing or acting for an audience","c":"演出；表演","s":"A: Did you enjoy the show that the marketing department organized for our overseas guests last night, or did you leave early? B: I stayed until the very end, because the performance was excellent, and the clients told me the singers and dancers were the best part of their whole business trip to Taipei.","t":"A：你喜歡行銷部昨晚為海外貴賓安排的表演嗎？還是你提早離開了？ B：我一直待到最後，因為那場【演出】非常精彩，客戶告訴我，那些歌手和舞者是他們這次台北商務之旅中最棒的部分。"},{"w":"stage","p":"n.","d":"the raised area in a theatre or hall where people perform or speak","c":"舞台","s":"A: The awards ceremony starts in two hours, so is everything ready in the main hall for our chairman's speech? B: Almost, but the workers are still setting up the lights and the microphone on the stage, and I asked them to place a small table there for the trophies before the guests arrive.","t":"A：頒獎典禮兩小時後開始，主廳裡為董事長演講準備的一切都就緒了嗎？ B：差不多了，但工人還在【舞台】上架設燈光和麥克風，我也請他們在賓客抵達前在那裡放一張小桌子擺獎盃。"},{"w":"actor","p":"n.","d":"a person, usually a man, who acts in plays, films or TV shows","c":"演員；男演員","s":"A: Who is going to host the opening night of our new hotel, since the general manager is too nervous to speak in front of a large crowd? B: We hired a famous local actor who has appeared in several popular TV series, and he will welcome the guests and introduce the chef before dinner is served.","t":"A：我們新飯店的開幕之夜要由誰來主持？因為總經理太緊張，不敢在一大群人面前說話。 B：我們請了一位知名的本地【男演員】，他演過好幾部熱門電視劇，他會在晚餐上桌前歡迎賓客並介紹主廚。"},{"w":"actress","p":"n.","d":"a woman who acts in plays, films or TV shows","c":"女演員","s":"A: Why is there such a long line outside the bookstore at the shopping mall this afternoon, and should we change our meeting place? B: A well-known actress is signing copies of her new book about her life in films, so it will be crowded for hours, and we had better meet at the coffee shop on the second floor instead.","t":"A：今天下午購物中心書店外面為什麼排了這麼長的隊伍？我們要不要換個碰面地點？ B：一位知名的【女演員】正在為她講述自己電影生涯的新書簽名，所以接下來幾個小時都會很擁擠，我們最好改在二樓的咖啡店碰面。"},{"w":"cast","p":"n.","d":"all the actors in a play, film or show","c":"演員陣容；全體演員","s":"A: I heard the staff musical for the company's anniversary is going well, but how many employees finally agreed to take part? B: The cast now includes eighteen people from five different departments, and even the finance manager agreed to sing a short song, so everyone is practicing during lunch breaks twice a week.","t":"A：我聽說公司週年慶的員工音樂劇進行得很順利，最後有多少員工同意參加？ B：現在的【演員陣容】包括來自五個不同部門的十八個人，連財務經理都答應唱一首短歌，所以大家每週兩次利用午休時間練習。"},{"w":"script","p":"n.","d":"the written words of a play, film, speech or broadcast","c":"劇本；腳本；講稿","s":"A: The video team wants to film our new training program next Monday, but have the trainers prepared what they are going to say on camera? B: Yes, the human resources department wrote a clear script for each trainer, and they will read it carefully over the weekend so that the filming can finish in one day.","t":"A：影片團隊想在下週一拍攝我們的新訓練課程，但講師們準備好要在鏡頭前說什麼了嗎？ B：準備好了，人資部門為每位講師寫了一份清楚的【腳本】，他們週末會仔細閱讀，好讓拍攝能在一天內完成。"},{"w":"scene","p":"n.","d":"one part of a play or film that happens in one place","c":"（戲劇、電影的）一場；場景","s":"A: The new television commercial for our sports drink looks great, but why did the shooting take two extra days? B: The final scene, where the runner crosses the finish line at sunrise, had to be filmed three more times because heavy clouds kept covering the sky, and the director wanted the light to be perfect.","t":"A：我們運動飲料的新電視廣告看起來很棒，但拍攝為什麼多花了兩天？ B：最後一【場戲】，也就是跑者在日出時衝過終點線的那一段，必須再多拍三次，因為厚厚的雲層一直遮住天空，而導演希望光線完美無缺。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"the words that people say to each other in a play, film or book","c":"對話；對白","s":"A: Our English training course for front desk staff starts next month, so how will the teacher help them practice talking with hotel guests? B: Each lesson includes a short dialogue between a receptionist and a traveler, and the staff will act it out in pairs so they feel more confident when they answer real questions.","t":"A：我們櫃檯員工的英語訓練課程下個月開始，老師會怎麼幫助他們練習和飯店客人交談？ B：每堂課都包含一段櫃檯接待員和旅客之間的簡短【對話】，員工會兩人一組演練，這樣他們回答真正的問題時會更有自信。"},{"w":"monologue","p":"n.","d":"a long speech by one actor alone in a play or film","c":"獨白","s":"A: The drama club is performing at our company's year-end party, so how long will the main actor be alone in front of the audience? B: He has a five-minute monologue near the end of the show, when he talks about his dreams for the future, and many people say it is the most moving part of the whole story.","t":"A：戲劇社要在我們公司的尾牙演出，主角會獨自面對觀眾多久？ B：他在戲快結束時有一段五分鐘的【獨白】，訴說他對未來的夢想，很多人說那是整個故事中最感人的部分。"},{"w":"tragedy","p":"n.","d":"a serious play or story with a sad ending","c":"悲劇","s":"A: Several clients asked whether they could bring their children to the show we booked for Saturday evening, so what should I tell them? B: Please explain that it is a serious tragedy about a family that loses everything in a war, so it may be too sad for young children, and we can offer them tickets to the musical instead.","t":"A：有好幾位客戶問能不能帶孩子去看我們訂的星期六晚上的演出，我該怎麼回覆他們？ B：請向他們說明這是一齣嚴肅的【悲劇】，講述一個家庭在戰爭中失去一切的故事，對年幼的孩子來說可能太悲傷了，我們可以改提供音樂劇的票給他們。"},{"w":"comedy","p":"n.","d":"a funny play, film or show that makes people laugh","c":"喜劇","s":"A: Everyone has been working very hard on the annual report, so what kind of entertainment should we choose for the team night out on Friday? B: Let's book seats for the new comedy at the arts center, because it is full of funny jokes and silly characters, and a good laugh is exactly what the team needs after such a stressful month.","t":"A：大家都非常努力在做年度報告，星期五的團隊聚會我們該選哪種娛樂活動？ B：我們去訂藝術中心那齣新【喜劇】的位子吧，因為裡面充滿好笑的笑話和滑稽的角色，在這麼有壓力的一個月之後，好好笑一場正是團隊需要的。"},{"w":"melodrama","p":"n.","d":"a story or play with too much strong emotion and exciting events","c":"通俗劇；灑狗血的戲","s":"A: Did you like the television series that the advertising agency recommended for our product placement, or do you think it is a bad match for our brand? B: Honestly, it is a melodrama with too many tears, shouting and surprising love stories, so I worry that our older banking customers will not take our message seriously if we appear in it.","t":"A：你喜歡廣告代理商推薦我們做置入性行銷的那部電視劇嗎？還是你覺得它和我們的品牌不搭？ B：老實說，那是一部充滿太多眼淚、爭吵和意外愛情故事的【通俗劇】，所以我擔心如果我們出現在劇中，我們年長的銀行客戶不會認真看待我們的訊息。"},{"w":"plot","p":"n.","d":"the main events of a story, film or play","c":"情節；劇情","s":"A: The publisher wants to turn the best-selling novel into a stage musical, but what did the producers think about the story when they read it? B: They loved the plot, in which a young chef secretly saves a failing restaurant, but they said several parts are too long and must be shortened before rehearsals begin in March.","t":"A：出版社想把那本暢銷小說改編成舞台音樂劇，製作人讀過後覺得這個故事怎麼樣？ B：他們很喜歡那個【情節】，講的是一位年輕廚師暗中拯救一家快倒閉的餐廳，但他們說有好幾個部分太長，必須在三月開始排練前刪短。"},{"w":"climax","p":"n.","d":"the most exciting or important part of a story","c":"高潮；頂點","s":"A: The audience at last night's show seemed quiet for most of the evening, so were the sponsors disappointed with the performance? B: Not at all, because at the climax of the story, when the hero finally discovers the truth about his father, everyone stood up and clapped, and the sponsors said they would support the next season as well.","t":"A：昨晚演出的觀眾大部分時間似乎都很安靜，贊助商對演出感到失望嗎？ B：一點也不，因為在故事的【高潮】，當主角終於發現關於他父親的真相時，所有人都站起來鼓掌，贊助商還說他們下一季也會繼續支持。"},{"w":"conflict","p":"n.","d":"a serious disagreement or fight between people","c":"衝突；矛盾","s":"A: The new drama that our company is sponsoring has received great reviews, so why do critics say it feels so real? B: The main conflict is between two brothers who disagree about whether to sell their late father's factory, and many people in the audience recognize the same arguments from their own family businesses.","t":"A：我們公司贊助的新戲獲得很好的評價，為什麼評論家說它感覺這麼真實？ B：主要的【衝突】發生在兩兄弟之間，他們對是否要賣掉亡父的工廠意見不合，許多觀眾在其中看到了自己家族企業中同樣的爭執。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"a person in a story, play or film","c":"角色；人物","s":"A: The children's theatre group asked our toy company to design a doll for their new show, so what information do we need from them first? B: We need a clear description of the main character, including her age, clothes and personality, so that our designers can create a doll that looks exactly like the girl on stage.","t":"A：兒童劇團請我們玩具公司為他們的新戲設計一個娃娃，我們首先需要他們提供什麼資訊？ B：我們需要主要【角色】的清楚描述，包括她的年齡、服裝和個性，這樣我們的設計師才能做出和舞台上那個女孩一模一樣的娃娃。"},{"w":"role","p":"n.","d":"the part that an actor plays in a play or film","c":"角色；（演員扮演的）角","s":"A: Our receptionist Anna told me she was chosen for the community musical next month, so will she need to take any days off? B: Yes, she got the leading role as a young nurse, so she asked for two afternoons off for rehearsals, and I have already found someone to cover the front desk while she is away.","t":"A：我們的櫃檯人員安娜告訴我，她被選上參加下個月的社區音樂劇，她需要請假嗎？ B：需要，她拿到了一位年輕護士的主要【角色】，所以她請了兩個下午的假去排練，我已經找好人在她不在時代班櫃檯。"},{"w":"rehearsal","p":"n.","d":"a practice of a play, show or speech before the real one","c":"排練；彩排","s":"A: The marketing team is presenting the new product at the trade show on Thursday, but are they ready to speak in front of hundreds of buyers? B: They will hold a full rehearsal in the large meeting room tomorrow afternoon, with the lights, slides and microphones, so they can fix any problems before the real event begins.","t":"A：行銷團隊星期四要在商展上發表新產品，他們準備好在數百位買家面前演講了嗎？ B：他們明天下午會在大會議室進行一次完整的【彩排】，包括燈光、投影片和麥克風，這樣就能在正式活動開始前修正任何問題。"},{"w":"direct","p":"v.","d":"to be in charge of the actors and the making of a play or film","c":"導演；執導","s":"A: The college drama club is planning a show to raise money for the local hospital, so who will guide the actors during practice? B: A retired film teacher has kindly agreed to direct the show for free, and he will meet the students every Saturday to help them with their acting and movement on stage.","t":"A：大學戲劇社正在籌劃一場演出，為當地醫院募款，練習時由誰來指導演員？ B：一位退休的電影老師好心答應免費【執導】這場演出，他每個星期六都會和學生見面，幫助他們練習演技和舞台走位。"},{"w":"director","p":"n.","d":"the person in charge of making a film or play","c":"導演","s":"A: The bank wants to make a short video about its history for its fiftieth anniversary, so who is in charge of the filming? B: We hired an experienced director who has made many award-winning documentaries, and she will decide which employees to interview and how each part of the video should look.","t":"A：銀行想為五十週年拍一支關於其歷史的短片，拍攝由誰負責？ B：我們聘請了一位經驗豐富的【導演】，她拍過許多得獎的紀錄片，她會決定要採訪哪些員工以及影片每個部分該呈現什麼樣子。"},{"w":"production","p":"n.","d":"a play, film or show that is made for the public","c":"（戲劇、電影的）製作；作品","s":"A: Our company has agreed to sponsor a musical at the city arts center, so how much money will we need to give them this year? B: The new production needs about two million dollars for costumes, lights and actors' salaries, and in return, our logo will appear on every poster and ticket for the whole season.","t":"A：我們公司同意贊助市立藝術中心的一齣音樂劇，今年我們需要給他們多少錢？ B：這部新【製作】大約需要兩百萬元來支付服裝、燈光和演員的薪水，作為回報，我們的標誌會出現在整季的每一張海報和門票上。"},{"w":"dramatic","p":"adj.","d":"sudden and very big; also related to plays and acting","c":"戲劇性的；巨大的；突然的","s":"A: Did the sales figures change much after we launched the new online advertising campaign in September, or did the results disappoint the managers? B: Yes, there was a dramatic increase in orders during the first two weeks, so the warehouse had to hire extra workers, and the manager is now asking for a bigger budget for next year.","t":"A：我們九月推出新的網路廣告活動後，銷售數字有很大的變化嗎？還是結果讓經理們失望了？ B：有變化，頭兩週的訂單出現【大幅的】增加，所以倉庫必須加聘人手，經理現在正在爭取明年更多的預算。"},{"w":"theatrical","p":"adj.","d":"related to the theatre or acting","c":"劇場的；戲劇的","s":"A: Why did the hotel ask the event company to decorate the ballroom for the charity dinner instead of doing it themselves? B: The event company has special theatrical lighting and colorful curtains, so they can make the room look like a real stage, and the guests will feel as if they are attending a show on Broadway.","t":"A：為什麼飯店請活動公司來布置慈善晚宴的宴會廳，而不是自己布置？ B：活動公司有專業的【劇場】燈光和色彩繽紛的布幕，可以讓宴會廳看起來像真正的舞台，賓客會覺得彷彿在百老匯看表演一樣。"},{"w":"emotional","p":"adj.","d":"making people feel strong feelings, such as sadness or love","c":"情緒的；感人的；激動的","s":"A: How did the staff react at the farewell party when our general manager announced that she was finally retiring after thirty years? B: It was a very emotional evening, because many people cried during her speech, and several employees said that she had been like a mother to them since they first joined the company.","t":"A：在歡送會上，當我們的總經理宣布她在三十年後終於要退休時，員工有什麼反應？ B：那是一個非常【感人】的夜晚，因為很多人在她致詞時都哭了，好幾位員工說，從他們剛進公司起，她就像母親一樣照顧他們。"},{"w":"intense","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or extreme","c":"強烈的；激烈的；極大的","s":"A: The new manager seems very tired these days, so is something wrong at the branch office she is in charge of? B: She has been under intense pressure to finish the merger with the Japanese company by the end of the month, so she works late every night and rarely has time for lunch.","t":"A：新經理最近看起來很疲倦，她負責的分公司出了什麼問題嗎？ B：她承受著【極大的】壓力，必須在月底前完成與日本公司的合併案，所以她每天晚上都工作到很晚，幾乎沒有時間吃午餐。"},{"w":"captivating","p":"adj.","d":"so interesting or beautiful that it holds your attention","c":"迷人的；引人入勝的","s":"A: Why did so many people stay at our booth at the travel fair, even though other companies were giving away free gifts? B: Our new video about the islands was truly captivating, with beautiful music and amazing pictures of the ocean, so visitors stopped to watch it and then asked many questions about our holiday packages.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多人停留在我們旅展的攤位上，即使其他公司都在發送免費贈品？ B：我們關於那些島嶼的新影片真的很【引人入勝】，有優美的音樂和令人驚豔的海洋畫面，所以參觀者停下來觀看，接著問了很多關於我們度假套裝行程的問題。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"showing feelings and thoughts clearly","c":"富有表現力的；富有表情的","s":"A: Which of the two singers do you think we should invite to perform at the hotel's grand opening next month? B: I prefer the younger one, because she has a very expressive face and voice, so even guests who don't understand Chinese can feel the happiness and sadness in her songs.","t":"A：你覺得下個月飯店盛大開幕時，我們應該邀請兩位歌手中的哪一位來表演？ B：我比較喜歡年輕的那位，因為她的表情和嗓音都非常【富有表現力】，所以即使是聽不懂中文的賓客，也能感受到她歌曲中的喜悅與悲傷。"},{"w":"dramatically","p":"adv.","d":"in a sudden and very big way","c":"大幅地；戲劇性地","s":"A: Has the number of visitors to our online ticket store changed since we started offering student discounts for weekend shows? B: Yes, it has risen dramatically over the past three months, so we now sell almost twice as many tickets, and we may need to add extra performances on Sunday afternoons.","t":"A：自從我們開始提供週末演出的學生折扣後，我們網路售票商店的訪客人數有改變嗎？ B：有，過去三個月人數【大幅地】上升，所以我們現在賣出的票幾乎是原來的兩倍，我們可能需要在星期日下午加場演出。"},{"w":"passionately","p":"adv.","d":"with very strong feelings or interest","c":"熱情地；熱烈地","s":"A: Why did the board finally agree to give money to the city's new youth theatre, when they had refused the same request last year? B: The young director spoke so passionately about helping teenagers build confidence through acting that every board member was moved, and they voted to support the project for three years.","t":"A：董事會去年拒絕了同樣的請求，為什麼最後同意捐款給市裡的新青少年劇院？ B：那位年輕導演【熱情地】談到如何透過表演幫助青少年建立自信，讓每一位董事都很感動，於是他們投票決定支持這個計畫三年。"},{"w":"portray","p":"v.","d":"to show or describe someone in a certain way, or to act as a character","c":"描繪；飾演","s":"A: The film company wants to make a movie about our company's founder, but are we happy with the way they plan to show him? B: Yes, they promised to portray him as a hard-working and honest man who started with nothing, and our public relations team will check the script before filming begins.","t":"A：電影公司想拍一部關於我們公司創辦人的電影，我們對他們打算呈現他的方式滿意嗎？ B：滿意，他們承諾會把他【描繪】成一個白手起家、勤奮又誠實的人，而我們的公關團隊會在開拍前審核劇本。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to understand or perform something in a particular way","c":"詮釋；解讀","s":"A: The actors in our training video for new employees seem confused about the customer complaint scene, so what should we do? B: Let's ask the trainer to explain the situation again, because each actor may interpret the angry customer's feelings differently, and we want everyone to show the same calm and polite response.","t":"A：我們新進員工訓練影片中的演員對客訴那一場戲似乎感到困惑，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們請講師再解釋一次情況吧，因為每個演員對憤怒客戶的情緒可能有不同的【詮釋】，而我們希望每個人都表現出同樣冷靜又有禮貌的回應。"},{"w":"improvise","p":"v.","d":"to speak or act without planning or preparing first","c":"即興發揮；即興表演","s":"A: What happened at the product launch yesterday when the projector suddenly stopped working in the middle of the presentation? B: Our sales manager had to improvise, so he told a funny story about the first time he used the product, and the audience laughed and didn't even notice the problem with the screen.","t":"A：昨天產品發表會進行到一半投影機突然故障時，發生了什麼事？ B：我們的業務經理只好【即興發揮】，他講了一個自己第一次使用這項產品的有趣故事，觀眾都笑了，甚至沒注意到螢幕出了問題。"},{"w":"spotlight","p":"n.","d":"a strong light that shines on one person or place on a stage","c":"聚光燈；（眾人的）焦點","s":"A: How will our new chief executive be introduced to the investors at the annual meeting next week? B: The lights in the hall will go down, and then a bright spotlight will shine on her as she walks to the front, so everyone will know immediately who she is before she begins her speech.","t":"A：下週年度大會上，我們的新執行長要怎麼介紹給投資人？ B：大廳的燈光會暗下來，接著當她走到前面時，一道明亮的【聚光燈】會照在她身上，這樣在她開始演講前，大家馬上就會知道她是誰。"}]},{"unit":111,"theme":"Drawing 繪畫","cards":[{"w":"illustration","p":"n.","d":"a picture drawn for a book, magazine or advertisement","c":"插圖；圖解","s":"A: The publisher wants the cover of the new children's cookbook finished by the end of the month, but our designer is still on vacation. B: Don't worry, I have already contacted a freelance artist who can draw a colorful illustration of a family cooking together, and she promised to send us the first sketch by Friday.","t":"A：出版社希望新的兒童食譜封面在月底前完成，但我們的設計師還在休假。 B：別擔心，我已經聯絡了一位自由接案的畫家，她可以畫一幅一家人一起做飯的彩色【插圖】，而且她答應星期五前把第一版草圖寄給我們。"},{"w":"portrait","p":"n.","d":"a painting, drawing or photo of a person, especially the face","c":"肖像；畫像","s":"A: The bank is celebrating its fiftieth anniversary next month, and the board would like to give the retiring chairman a special gift. B: How about hiring a local artist to draw a portrait of him in his office? We could hang it in the main lobby so that customers and staff can remember everything he did for the company.","t":"A：銀行下個月要慶祝成立五十週年，董事會想送即將退休的董事長一份特別的禮物。 B：請一位當地畫家畫一幅他在辦公室裡的【肖像】如何？我們可以把它掛在大廳，讓顧客和員工記得他為公司所做的一切。"},{"w":"cartoon","p":"n.","d":"a funny drawing, often in a newspaper or magazine","c":"漫畫；卡通","s":"A: Our monthly newsletter is full of long reports about sales figures, and I'm afraid most employees stop reading after the first page. B: Why don't we add a small cartoon on the back page each month? If it shows a funny moment from office life, people will look forward to the next issue and may read the other articles too.","t":"A：我們的月刊裡全是關於銷售數字的冗長報告，我擔心大部分員工讀完第一頁就不看了。 B：我們何不每個月在封底加一則小【漫畫】？如果它呈現辦公室生活中的有趣時刻，大家就會期待下一期，或許也會讀其他文章。"},{"w":"shade","p":"n.","d":"a particular darkness or lightness of a color","c":"色調；（顏色的）深淺","s":"A: The client said the blue in our new logo looks too bright on the website, and she wants something that feels calmer and more professional. B: I understand, so I'll try a darker shade of blue this afternoon and send her three different versions, because it is easier for clients to choose when they can compare them side by side.","t":"A：客戶說我們新標誌的藍色在網站上看起來太亮了，她想要感覺更沉穩、更專業的顏色。 B：我明白，所以我今天下午會試一種較深的藍色【色調】，並寄給她三個不同的版本，因為客戶能並排比較時比較容易做選擇。"},{"w":"shading","p":"n.","d":"the use of darker marks in a drawing to show shadow or depth","c":"（繪畫的）明暗處理；陰影","s":"A: I drew this coffee cup for the café's new menu, but my manager says it still looks flat and a little boring. B: You should add some shading on the right side, where the light doesn't reach, because darker areas will make the cup look round and give the whole picture a more realistic feeling.","t":"A：我為咖啡館的新菜單畫了這個咖啡杯，但我的經理說它看起來還是很平面，有點無趣。 B：你應該在光線照不到的右側加一些【明暗陰影】，因為較暗的區域會讓杯子看起來是圓的，讓整張圖更有真實感。"},{"w":"line","p":"n.","d":"a long thin mark made with a pen or pencil","c":"線；線條","s":"A: The new trainees in our design department keep asking how they can improve their sketches of buildings and furniture quickly. B: Tell them to practice drawing a straight line without a ruler for ten minutes every morning, since steady hands are the base of every good sketch, and they will notice a big difference after a few weeks.","t":"A：我們設計部門的新進受訓人員一直問要怎麼快速改善他們的建築和家具素描。 B：叫他們每天早上花十分鐘練習不用尺畫直【線】，因為穩定的手是每張好素描的基礎，幾週後他們就會發現很大的差別。"},{"w":"stroke","p":"n.","d":"a single movement of a pen or brush, or the mark it makes","c":"一筆；筆畫","s":"A: The calligraphy teacher at the community center said my characters look messy, but I'm not sure what I'm doing wrong. B: She probably means you are moving the brush too quickly, so try to finish each stroke slowly and with the same pressure, and remember to let the ink dry before you start the next character.","t":"A：社區中心的書法老師說我的字看起來很亂，但我不確定自己哪裡做錯了。 B：她大概是指你運筆太快了，所以試著慢慢地用相同的力道完成每一【筆】，而且記得在寫下一個字之前讓墨水乾掉。"},{"w":"contour","p":"n.","d":"the outer edge or shape of something","c":"輪廓；外形","s":"A: The architecture firm asked us to make a simple map for the new hiking trail, but they don't need every small feature of the area. B: Then we should only draw the contour of the hills and the river, because visitors mainly want to see the shape of the land and the easiest path to the top.","t":"A：建築事務所請我們為新的健行步道製作一張簡單的地圖，但他們不需要該區域的每個小地物。 B：那我們就只畫山丘和河流的【輪廓】，因為遊客主要是想看地形的樣子以及通往山頂最容易的路線。"},{"w":"composition","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of a picture are arranged","c":"構圖；（畫面的）布局","s":"A: The photo of our new office building for the annual report looks nice, but something about it feels unbalanced to me. B: I agree, because the building is right in the corner while the empty sky takes up most of the space, so let's improve the composition by moving the building closer to the center of the picture.","t":"A：年報裡我們新辦公大樓的照片看起來不錯，但我覺得有點不平衡。 B：我同意，因為大樓擠在角落，而空蕩蕩的天空卻佔了大部分空間，所以我們把大樓移到靠近畫面中央的地方來改善【構圖】吧。"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n.","d":"a way of drawing that makes things look near or far, as in real life","c":"透視法","s":"A: The drawings of the new shopping mall look strange, because the people in the back are as large as the people in the front. B: That's because the junior designer hasn't learned to use perspective correctly yet, so I'll show him how objects should become smaller as they get farther away, which will make the space look much deeper.","t":"A：新購物中心的圖看起來很奇怪，因為後面的人和前面的人一樣大。 B：那是因為那位初級設計師還沒學會正確運用【透視法】，所以我會教他物體離得越遠應該畫得越小，這樣空間看起來就會更有深度。"},{"w":"proportion","p":"n.","d":"the correct size of one part compared with another","c":"比例","s":"A: Our art teacher says the hands in my portrait drawing are too big, but I measured everything carefully before I started. B: Maybe you measured each part on its own, so try comparing the size of the hand with the face, because getting the proportion right is more important than drawing every small wrinkle or fingernail.","t":"A：我們的美術老師說我畫的人像裡手太大了，但我開始畫之前每個地方都仔細量過了。 B：也許你是把每個部位分開量的，試著把手的大小和臉做比較，因為把【比例】畫對比畫出每一條小皺紋或指甲更重要。"},{"w":"detail","p":"n.","d":"a small part or fact of something","c":"細節","s":"A: The marketing team loved the first draft of the poster, but they asked whether we could make the product look more attractive. B: Sure, I'll add more detail to the watch in the center, such as the tiny numbers and the silver buttons on the side, so customers can see how carefully it was made.","t":"A：行銷團隊很喜歡海報的初稿，但他們問我們能不能讓產品看起來更吸引人。 B：當然，我會為中間的手錶加上更多【細節】，像是細小的數字和側面的銀色按鈕，讓顧客能看出它做工有多精細。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way a surface feels or looks, such as rough or smooth","c":"質地；紋理","s":"A: The furniture company wants our drawings of their new wooden tables to look as real as possible in the online catalog. B: In that case, I'll use soft pencils to show the texture of the wood, including the natural patterns and small marks, so that customers can almost feel the surface just by looking at the picture.","t":"A：家具公司希望我們為他們新木桌畫的圖在線上型錄裡看起來越真實越好。 B：這樣的話，我會用軟鉛筆表現木頭的【紋理】，包括天然的花紋和細小的痕跡，讓顧客光看圖片就幾乎能感覺到桌面的觸感。"},{"w":"medium","p":"n.","d":"the material an artist uses, such as paint or pencil","c":"（藝術創作的）媒材","s":"A: I'm signing up for the evening art class at the community college, but I can't decide between the painting course and the drawing course. B: If you are a beginner, I suggest you start with pencil, because it is a cheap and simple medium, and you can easily fix your mistakes while you are still learning the basics.","t":"A：我要報名社區大學的晚間美術課，但我無法決定要選繪畫課還是素描課。 B：如果你是初學者，我建議你從鉛筆開始，因為它是便宜又簡單的【媒材】，而且你在學基礎時可以輕易修正錯誤。"},{"w":"pencil","p":"n.","d":"a thin tool with a gray or colored center, used for writing or drawing","c":"鉛筆","s":"A: Our office supplies order is due tomorrow, and the architects on the third floor have asked for something new for their early sketches. B: Then please order a good mechanical pencil for each of them, along with extra leads and erasers, because they like to sketch their ideas quickly by hand before they move to the computer.","t":"A：我們的辦公用品訂單明天截止，三樓的建築師們要求為他們的初步草圖準備一些新東西。 B：那就請幫他們每人訂一支好的自動【鉛筆】，再加上額外的筆芯和橡皮擦，因為他們喜歡在用電腦之前先快速手繪構想。"},{"w":"charcoal","p":"n.","d":"a black stick of burned wood used for drawing","c":"炭筆；木炭","s":"A: The art class tomorrow is about drawing faces, and the teacher told us to bring something that makes very dark, soft marks. B: Then you should buy a stick of charcoal at the art shop near the station, but remember to bring some wet tissues too, because it will easily make your hands and clothes black.","t":"A：明天的美術課是畫臉部，老師叫我們帶可以畫出很深、很柔和痕跡的東西。 B：那你應該去車站附近的美術用品店買一根【炭筆】，但記得也要帶些濕紙巾，因為它很容易把你的手和衣服弄黑。"},{"w":"ink","p":"n.","d":"a colored liquid used for writing, drawing or printing","c":"墨水；油墨","s":"A: The printer in the design studio keeps producing pale, gray pages, and we have to send the final brochure to the client this afternoon. B: It's probably running out of black ink, so I'll replace the cartridge right away, and if that doesn't work, we can print the brochure at the copy shop across the street.","t":"A：設計工作室的印表機一直印出淡淡的灰色頁面，而我們今天下午必須把最終版手冊寄給客戶。 B：它大概是黑色【墨水】快用完了，所以我馬上換匣，如果那樣還不行，我們可以到對街的影印店印手冊。"},{"w":"marker","p":"n.","d":"a pen with a thick tip, used for writing on boards or drawing","c":"麥克筆；記號筆","s":"A: During tomorrow's brainstorming meeting, I want everyone to write their ideas on the whiteboard so the whole team can see them. B: Good idea, but most of the pens in the meeting room have dried up, so I'll bring a new marker in each color from the supply cabinet before the meeting starts at nine.","t":"A：明天的腦力激盪會議上，我希望每個人都把點子寫在白板上，讓整個團隊都看得到。 B：好主意，但會議室裡大部分的筆都乾掉了，所以我會在九點開會前從用品櫃拿每種顏色各一支新的【麥克筆】過來。"},{"w":"brush","p":"n.","d":"a tool with hairs on a handle, used for painting","c":"畫筆；刷子","s":"A: My watercolor paintings always look messy at the edges, even though I buy expensive paints from the art store. B: The paint may not be the problem, so try using a smaller brush with soft hair for the edges, because a thin tip gives you much better control when you are painting small areas.","t":"A：我的水彩畫邊緣看起來總是很亂，雖然我都在美術用品店買昂貴的顏料。 B：問題可能不在顏料，所以畫邊緣時試著用一支軟毛的小【畫筆】，因為細的筆尖在畫小區域時能讓你控制得好得多。"},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"strong cloth that artists paint on","c":"畫布","s":"A: The hotel manager wants a large painting of the harbor for the wall behind the reception desk, about two meters wide. B: Then I'll need to order a special canvas from the art supplier, because the ones they keep in the store are too small, and it may take a week to arrive.","t":"A：飯店經理想在櫃台後面的牆上掛一幅大約兩公尺寬的港口大畫。 B：那我需要向美術用品供應商訂購一塊特製的【畫布】，因為他們店裡的太小了，而且可能要一週才會到貨。"},{"w":"paper","p":"n.","d":"thin material made from wood, used for writing, drawing or printing","c":"紙；紙張","s":"A: The students in the Saturday drawing class complained that their pencil sketches look gray and dirty after only a few minutes. B: That's because the cheap paper we bought is too smooth and thin, so next month I'll order a thicker kind that is made for drawing and can hold the pencil marks better.","t":"A：星期六素描班的學生抱怨他們的鉛筆素描才幾分鐘就看起來灰灰髒髒的。 B：那是因為我們買的便宜【紙張】太光滑又太薄，所以下個月我會訂一種專門用來畫圖、較厚而且更能留住鉛筆痕跡的款式。"},{"w":"precise","p":"adj.","d":"exact and correct in every small part","c":"精確的；準確的","s":"A: The engineers need the drawings of the new machine part by Monday, and they said even a small mistake could cause problems in the factory. B: In that case, we must use a computer program instead of drawing by hand, because the measurements have to be precise down to the last millimeter, and the software can check them for us.","t":"A：工程師們星期一前需要新機械零件的圖，他們說即使是小錯誤也可能在工廠造成問題。 B：這樣的話，我們必須用電腦程式而不是手繪，因為尺寸必須【精確】到最後一毫米，而且軟體可以幫我們檢查。"},{"w":"rough","p":"adj.","d":"not finished or exact; done quickly as a first try","c":"粗略的；草擬的","s":"A: The client wants to see our ideas for the new restaurant sign tomorrow morning, but we haven't finished any of the final designs yet. B: That's fine, because at this stage we only need to show her a few rough sketches, and once she chooses the one she likes, we can spend next week adding color and other finishing touches.","t":"A：客戶明天早上想看我們對新餐廳招牌的構想，但我們還沒完成任何最終設計。 B：沒關係，因為這個階段我們只需要給她看幾張【粗略的】草圖，等她選出喜歡的那一張，我們下週再花時間上色並做其他最後的修飾。"},{"w":"realistic","p":"adj.","d":"showing things as they really are","c":"寫實的；逼真的","s":"A: The real estate agency wants pictures of the apartments before they are built, so buyers can imagine living there. B: Then we'll create very realistic drawings with sunlight coming through the windows and furniture in every room, because buyers are more likely to sign a contract when the home looks like a real place.","t":"A：房地產仲介希望在公寓蓋好之前就有圖片，讓買家能想像住在那裡的樣子。 B：那我們就畫非常【寫實的】圖，畫出陽光從窗戶照進來、每個房間都擺好家具，因為當房子看起來像真實的地方時，買家比較可能簽約。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"using shapes and colors instead of showing real people or things","c":"抽象的","s":"A: The new lobby looks a bit empty, and the CEO asked me to find some art that won't distract visitors or feel too old-fashioned. B: How about a few abstract paintings with simple shapes and soft colors? They feel modern and calm, and since they don't show any particular people or places, they suit almost any business.","t":"A：新大廳看起來有點空，執行長要我找一些不會讓訪客分心、也不會顯得太老派的藝術品。 B：幾幅有簡單形狀和柔和色彩的【抽象】畫如何？它們感覺現代又沉穩，而且因為沒有描繪特定的人或地方，幾乎適合任何企業。"},{"w":"artistic","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing skill in art","c":"有藝術天分的；藝術的","s":"A: We're looking for someone to design the store's window displays for the holiday season, but nobody on the sales team has any experience. B: Actually, Mia in accounting is very artistic, and she spends her weekends painting and taking photos, so why don't we ask her to share a few ideas at Thursday's meeting?","t":"A：我們在找人設計店裡節慶季節的櫥窗陳列，但業務團隊裡沒有人有經驗。 B：其實會計部的米亞很有【藝術天分】，她週末都在畫畫和拍照，我們何不請她在星期四的會議上分享一些想法？"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new and original ideas","c":"有創意的；有創造力的","s":"A: Our advertisements for the new juice brand look almost the same as our competitors', and sales have been slow since the launch. B: We need a more creative approach, so let's invite a few young designers to a workshop next week and let them try some unusual ideas, such as drawing the fruit as cartoon characters.","t":"A：我們新果汁品牌的廣告看起來和競爭對手的幾乎一樣，而且上市以來銷售一直很慢。 B：我們需要更【有創意的】做法，所以下週邀請幾位年輕設計師來參加工作坊，讓他們嘗試一些不尋常的點子，例如把水果畫成卡通人物。"},{"w":"render","p":"v.","d":"to draw or show something in a particular way, often using a computer","c":"描繪；（用電腦）繪製呈現","s":"A: The architects need images of the new library for the city council meeting, and they want people to see how it will look at night. B: Our team can render the building with its lights on and a dark blue sky behind it, but the computer will need several hours to finish each image, so please give us until Thursday.","t":"A：建築師們需要新圖書館的圖像給市議會開會用，他們想讓大家看到它晚上的樣子。 B：我們團隊可以把建築【繪製呈現】成燈火通明、背景是深藍夜空的樣子，但電腦完成每張圖需要好幾個小時，所以請給我們到星期四的時間。"},{"w":"trace","p":"v.","d":"to copy a picture by drawing over its lines through thin paper","c":"描摹；描繪","s":"A: The children at our summer art camp find it very hard to draw animals, and some of them get upset and want to give up. B: Let them trace simple pictures from a book first by placing thin sheets over the page, because copying the outlines helps them learn the shapes, and later they can try drawing on their own.","t":"A：我們暑期美術營的孩子們覺得畫動物很難，有些人會沮喪想放棄。 B：先讓他們把薄紙放在書頁上【描摹】簡單的圖，因為描出輪廓能幫助他們學會形狀，之後他們就能試著自己畫。"},{"w":"erase","p":"v.","d":"to remove marks, especially pencil marks","c":"擦掉；抹去","s":"A: I made a mistake on the floor plan I drew for the client, and the meeting starts in less than twenty minutes. B: Don't panic, because you drew it in pencil, so you can simply erase the wrong wall with a soft rubber and draw it again in the right place before she arrives.","t":"A：我為客戶畫的平面圖出錯了，而會議不到二十分鐘就要開始。 B：別慌，因為你是用鉛筆畫的，所以你只要用軟橡皮擦把畫錯的牆【擦掉】，在她到之前重新畫在正確的位置就好。"}]},{"unit":112,"theme":"Dream 夢想","cards":[{"w":"aspiration","p":"n.","d":"a strong hope to achieve something important","c":"抱負；志向","s":"A: During your performance review yesterday, what did you tell the department manager about your plans for the next five years at our company? B: I explained that my main aspiration is to lead an international sales team, so I asked whether the company could pay for a management course next spring.","t":"A：昨天你的績效考核時，你跟部門經理說了你未來五年在公司有什麼計畫？ B：我說明我主要的【志向】是帶領一個國際業務團隊，所以我問公司是否能支付明年春天的管理課程費用。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to be successful or achieve something","c":"雄心；抱負","s":"A: Why did Daniel leave his comfortable position at the bank after working there for nearly ten years with a good salary and friendly coworkers? B: He has always had a strong ambition to open his own coffee shop downtown, so he finally saved enough money and rented a small space near the train station.","t":"A：Daniel 在銀行工作了將近十年，薪水不錯、同事也友善，為什麼他要離開那份舒適的職位？ B：他一直懷有在市中心開自己咖啡店的強烈【雄心】，所以他終於存夠了錢，在火車站附近租了一個小店面。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"an idea or picture of what the future should be like","c":"願景；遠見","s":"A: At the opening of the new branch office, what did the CEO say about the company's plans for the future and the role of our employees? B: She shared her vision of becoming the most trusted online bookstore in Asia, and she said every staff member would play an important part in reaching it.","t":"A：在新分公司開幕時，執行長對公司的未來計畫和員工的角色說了什麼？ B：她分享了她要成為亞洲最受信賴網路書店的【願景】，並說每位員工都會在實現它的過程中扮演重要角色。"},{"w":"goal","p":"n.","d":"something you are trying to achieve","c":"目標","s":"A: How many new customers does the marketing department need to find this quarter, and do you think the team can manage it with the current budget? B: Our goal is to sign up five hundred new members by the end of March, and I believe we can do it if the online advertising campaign starts next week.","t":"A：行銷部門這一季需要找到多少新客戶？你認為團隊用目前的預算做得到嗎？ B：我們的【目標】是在三月底前招募五百位新會員，如果線上廣告活動下週開始，我相信我們做得到。"},{"w":"fantasy","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant idea that is very unlikely to happen","c":"幻想","s":"A: Have you heard that Kevin from accounting wants to quit his job, buy a sailboat, and travel around the world with his family next year? B: Yes, but I think it's just a fantasy, because he still has a large house loan to pay and his children are only starting elementary school this fall.","t":"A：你有聽說會計部的 Kevin 想辭職、買一艘帆船，明年帶著家人環遊世界嗎？ B：有啊，但我覺得那只是一個【幻想】，因為他還有一大筆房貸要付，而且他的孩子今年秋天才剛要上小學。"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to create new ideas or pictures in your mind","c":"想像力","s":"A: The new advertisement for our sports drinks looks really different from the old ones, so who came up with the idea of using cartoon animals? B: Our youngest designer did, and her imagination really impressed the clients, who said the colorful characters would attract both children and their parents in supermarkets.","t":"A：我們運動飲料的新廣告看起來跟舊的很不一樣，是誰想出用卡通動物的點子？ B：是我們最年輕的設計師，她的【想像力】讓客戶非常驚艷，他們說這些色彩繽紛的角色在超市裡會同時吸引孩子和家長。"},{"w":"nightmare","p":"n.","d":"a very bad dream; a very unpleasant experience","c":"惡夢；可怕的經歷","s":"A: How was your business trip to Singapore last week, and did you manage to meet all the clients you had planned to see? B: It was a complete nightmare, because my flight was canceled, my luggage was lost at the airport, and two important meetings had to be moved to video calls instead.","t":"A：你上週去新加坡出差怎麼樣？你有見到所有原本計畫要見的客戶嗎？ B：簡直是一場【惡夢】，因為我的班機被取消，行李在機場遺失，兩個重要會議也只好改成視訊會議。"},{"w":"lucid","p":"adj.","d":"clear and easy to understand","c":"清楚易懂的；清醒的","s":"A: Did the new manager explain the changes to the company's travel policy clearly enough during the meeting this morning, or were people still confused? B: Her explanation was very lucid, so everyone understood the new rules for booking hotels and flights, and nobody had to ask any questions afterwards.","t":"A：新經理今天早上開會時，有把公司差旅政策的改變解釋得夠清楚嗎？還是大家還是很困惑？ B：她的說明非常【清楚易懂】，所以大家都了解訂飯店和機票的新規定，事後沒有人需要再發問。"},{"w":"vivid","p":"adj.","d":"very clear and bright in your mind","c":"鮮明的；生動的","s":"A: Do you still remember your first day working at the hotel reception desk when that famous movie star suddenly checked in without any notice? B: Yes, I have a very vivid memory of that day, because dozens of reporters rushed into the lobby and the manager asked me to call the security team immediately.","t":"A：你還記得你在飯店櫃檯上班的第一天，那位知名電影明星突然在沒有通知的情況下入住嗎？ B：記得，我對那天有非常【鮮明】的記憶，因為幾十位記者衝進大廳，經理要我立刻打電話給保全團隊。"},{"w":"surreal","p":"adj.","d":"very strange, like something in a dream","c":"超現實的；如夢似幻的","s":"A: How did it feel to stand on the stage and receive the Employee of the Year award in front of the whole company at the annual dinner? B: It was a little surreal, because only two years ago I was a part-time cashier, and now the president was shaking my hand while hundreds of people clapped.","t":"A：在年度晚宴上當著全公司的面站上舞台領取年度最佳員工獎，感覺如何？ B：感覺有點【如夢似幻】，因為兩年前我還是兼職收銀員，而現在總裁在數百人鼓掌下跟我握手。"},{"w":"unreal","p":"adj.","d":"so strange or extreme that it is hard to believe","c":"不真實的；難以置信的","s":"A: Have you seen the price the developer is asking for the small office space next to the train station, and is it worth checking out? B: The rent is completely unreal, almost three times what we pay now, so I suggest we keep looking for a cheaper place in the suburbs instead.","t":"A：你有看到開發商對火車站旁那間小辦公室開的價格嗎？值得去看看嗎？ B：那租金完全【令人難以置信】，幾乎是我們現在付的三倍，所以我建議我們改去郊區找便宜一點的地方。"},{"w":"doze","p":"v.","d":"to sleep lightly for a short time","c":"打瞌睡；打盹","s":"A: Why did the director look so annoyed at the end of the training session that was held in the conference room after lunch today? B: Two new employees started to doze during the boring safety video, so she stopped the presentation and asked everyone to stand up and stretch for a few minutes.","t":"A：為什麼今天午餐後在會議室舉行的訓練課程結束時，主任看起來那麼不高興？ B：有兩位新員工在無聊的安全影片播放時開始【打瞌睡】，所以她暫停了簡報，請大家站起來伸展幾分鐘。"},{"w":"drift","p":"v.","d":"to move slowly without a clear direction","c":"飄移；（思緒）飄走","s":"A: Why do you always turn off your phone notifications when you are writing the monthly sales report in the afternoon? B: If I see too many messages, my thoughts start to drift away from the numbers, and then I make careless mistakes that my supervisor has to correct before the report goes to headquarters.","t":"A：為什麼你下午寫每月銷售報告時總是關掉手機通知？ B：如果我看到太多訊息，我的思緒就會開始從數字上【飄走】，然後我就會犯一些粗心的錯，主管必須在報告送到總部之前幫我修正。"},{"w":"envision","p":"v.","d":"to imagine something that may happen in the future","c":"設想；展望","s":"A: When you started this small online clothing business in your apartment five years ago, did you expect it to grow so quickly? B: Not at all, I didn't envision having three stores and forty employees, because at first I only wanted to sell a few handmade shirts to my friends and neighbors.","t":"A：五年前你在公寓裡開始經營這個小小的網路服飾生意時，你有預料到它會成長得這麼快嗎？ B：完全沒有，我從沒【設想過】會擁有三家店和四十名員工，因為一開始我只想賣幾件手工襯衫給朋友和鄰居。"},{"w":"visualize","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture of something in your mind","c":"想像；使形象化","s":"A: Before you give an important presentation to a big client, what do you do to stay calm and feel confident in the meeting room? B: I close my eyes and try to visualize the whole meeting from beginning to end, including the client's questions, so I feel prepared and less nervous when it actually happens.","t":"A：在向大客戶做重要簡報之前，你會做什麼來保持冷靜並在會議室裡感到有自信？ B：我會閉上眼睛，試著在腦中【想像】整場會議從頭到尾的情況，包括客戶的提問，這樣真正上場時我會覺得準備充分、比較不緊張。"},{"w":"long","p":"v.","d":"to want something very much","c":"渴望","s":"A: Your team has been working overtime every weekend since the new factory opened, so how are people feeling about the schedule now? B: Everyone is tired and many of them long for a proper holiday, so the manager promised to give each worker three extra days off once the big order is finished.","t":"A：自從新工廠開幕後，你的團隊每個週末都在加班，大家現在對這個排班感覺如何？ B：每個人都很累，很多人都【渴望】好好放個假，所以經理承諾等這筆大訂單完成後，每位員工都多放三天假。"},{"w":"yearn","p":"v.","d":"to want something very much, often something hard to get","c":"渴望；嚮往","s":"A: Why did Maria apply for the job in the Paris office even though the salary there is lower than what she earns here in Taipei? B: She has always seemed to yearn for a life abroad, and she believes that working in Europe will help her learn French and meet designers from many different countries.","t":"A：為什麼 Maria 要申請巴黎辦公室的職位，即使那裡的薪水比她在台北賺的還低？ B：她似乎一直【嚮往】在國外生活，而且她相信在歐洲工作能幫助她學法文，並認識來自許多不同國家的設計師。"},{"w":"destiny","p":"n.","d":"what will happen to someone in the future","c":"命運；天命","s":"A: After failing the bank's entrance exam twice, why did Jason decide to become a chef instead of trying a third time? B: He said cooking was his destiny, because his grandmother taught him family recipes when he was young, and now his small restaurant is fully booked every weekend.","t":"A：Jason 兩次沒通過銀行的入職考試後，為什麼決定改當廚師而不是再試第三次？ B：他說烹飪是他的【天命】，因為他小時候奶奶教了他家傳食譜，而現在他的小餐廳每個週末都客滿。"},{"w":"target","p":"n.","d":"a result or level you try to reach","c":"目標；指標","s":"A: The regional manager looks very pleased today, so did our branch sell enough insurance policies this month to receive the bonus? B: Yes, we reached our sales target three days early, so every member of the team will get an extra payment and a free dinner at the hotel restaurant on Friday.","t":"A：區域經理今天看起來非常高興，我們分行這個月賣出的保單夠多，可以拿到獎金嗎？ B：是的，我們提前三天達成了銷售【目標】，所以每位團隊成員都會拿到額外獎金，並在週五享用飯店餐廳的免費晚餐。"},{"w":"illusion","p":"n.","d":"something that seems true or real but is not","c":"錯覺；假象","s":"A: Our online store has a lot of visitors every day, so why are the sales numbers still so low compared with last year? B: The high number of visitors creates an illusion of success, but most people leave the website without buying anything because our shipping fees are much higher than our competitors'.","t":"A：我們的網路商店每天有很多訪客，為什麼銷售數字跟去年相比還是那麼低？ B：大量的訪客製造了一種成功的【假象】，但大多數人沒買任何東西就離開網站，因為我們的運費比競爭對手高得多。"},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"a picture or thing that represents an idea","c":"象徵；符號","s":"A: Why did the design team choose a green tree for the new company logo instead of keeping the old blue letters we used for years? B: The tree is a symbol of growth and protecting nature, and the marketing director wants customers to know that we now use recycled materials in all our products.","t":"A：為什麼設計團隊為新的公司標誌選了一棵綠色的樹，而不是保留我們用了好幾年的舊藍色字母？ B：這棵樹是成長與保護自然的【象徵】，行銷總監希望顧客知道我們現在所有產品都使用回收材料。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to explain or understand the meaning of something","c":"解讀；詮釋","s":"A: The survey results show that many customers visited our shop only once last year, so what do you think these numbers really mean? B: It's hard to interpret the data without more information, so I suggest we call some of those customers and ask them directly why they didn't come back.","t":"A：調查結果顯示去年很多顧客只來過我們店一次，你認為這些數字真正代表什麼？ B：沒有更多資訊很難【解讀】這些數據，所以我建議我們打電話給其中一些顧客，直接問他們為什麼沒有再回來。"},{"w":"reflective","p":"adj.","d":"thinking quietly and carefully","c":"沉思的；反省的","s":"A: You seemed very quiet after the team meeting where the project results were announced, so is everything all right with you? B: I'm fine, I was just in a reflective mood, thinking about what we did wrong and how we can plan the next project better so we don't miss the deadline again.","t":"A：在宣布專案結果的團隊會議之後，你似乎很安靜，你還好嗎？ B：我沒事，我只是處於一種【沉思】的心情，在想我們哪裡做錯了，以及下一個專案要如何規劃得更好，才不會再錯過截止日期。"},{"w":"restful","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel calm and relaxed","c":"寧靜的；令人放鬆的","s":"A: Where are you planning to stay during the company retreat in the mountains next month, and is the hotel close to the meeting center? B: We booked a small guesthouse by the lake, which is quiet and restful, and it's only a ten-minute walk from the center where the workshops will be held every morning.","t":"A：下個月在山上的公司員工旅遊，你打算住哪裡？那間飯店離會議中心近嗎？ B：我們訂了湖邊的一間小民宿，那裡安靜又【令人放鬆】，而且走路到每天早上舉辦工作坊的中心只要十分鐘。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something good","c":"激勵；啟發","s":"A: Why did the company invite a famous mountain climber to speak at the annual sales conference instead of an expert in marketing? B: The president hoped his amazing story would inspire the sales staff to work harder and never give up, even when customers say no to them many times.","t":"A：為什麼公司在年度業務會議上邀請一位知名登山家演講，而不是行銷專家？ B：總裁希望他精彩的故事能【激勵】業務人員更努力工作、永不放棄，即使客戶拒絕他們很多次。"},{"w":"motivating","p":"adj.","d":"making you want to work hard or do something","c":"有激勵作用的","s":"A: Do you think offering a free trip to Japan to the top salesperson of the year is a good idea for our small company? B: Yes, I think a prize like that is very motivating, because last year, when we only gave out gift cards, most of the sales staff didn't seem excited at all.","t":"A：你覺得為我們這家小公司的年度最佳業務員提供免費日本旅遊是個好主意嗎？ B：是的，我覺得那樣的獎品非常【有激勵作用】，因為去年我們只發禮券時，大部分業務人員似乎一點都不興奮。"}]},{"unit":113,"theme":"E-books 電子書","cards":[{"w":"e-book","p":"n.","d":"an electronic version of a book that you read on a screen","c":"電子書","s":"A: Our training team wants every new employee to read the customer service handbook before their first week, but printing two hundred copies seems expensive and slow. B: Why don't we turn the handbook into an e-book and email it to everyone, so they can read it on their phones during the commute?","t":"A：我們的訓練團隊希望每位新進員工在第一週前讀完客服手冊，但印兩百本似乎又貴又慢。 B：我們何不把手冊做成【電子書】，再用電子郵件寄給大家，讓他們能在通勤時用手機閱讀？"},{"w":"e-reader","p":"n.","d":"a small device used for reading e-books","c":"電子閱讀器","s":"A: I'm flying to Singapore for the trade fair next week, and I'd like to bring some novels, but my suitcase is already full of product samples and brochures. B: You should take an e-reader instead, because it's light, the battery lasts for weeks, and it can hold hundreds of books in one small device.","t":"A：我下週要飛新加坡參加商展，想帶幾本小說，但我的行李箱已經塞滿了產品樣品和型錄。 B：你應該改帶一台【電子閱讀器】，因為它很輕，電池可以撐好幾週，而且一台小小的裝置就能裝下好幾百本書。"},{"w":"digital","p":"adj.","d":"stored or sent as computer data","c":"數位的","s":"A: The accounting department keeps losing paper receipts, and the auditors are coming next month to check every expense from last year. B: Let's ask everyone to scan their receipts and keep digital copies in the shared folder, so nothing gets lost and the auditors can find each file quickly.","t":"A：會計部門一直弄丟紙本收據，而稽核人員下個月就要來檢查去年的每一筆開支。 B：我們請大家把收據掃描起來，並把【數位】副本存在共用資料夾裡，這樣就不會遺失，稽核人員也能很快找到每個檔案。"},{"w":"electronic","p":"adj.","d":"using electricity and computer technology","c":"電子的","s":"A: Do customers still need to sign the paper order form at the front desk, or has the process changed since the new system was installed last month? B: They can now sign an electronic form on the tablet at the counter, which saves paper and lets our sales staff process orders much faster.","t":"A：客人還需要在櫃台簽紙本訂購單嗎？還是自從上個月裝了新系統後流程就改了？ B：他們現在可以在櫃台的平板上簽【電子】表單，這樣既省紙，也讓我們的銷售人員處理訂單快得多。"},{"w":"format","p":"n.","d":"the way a file is arranged or saved","c":"格式","s":"A: The client says she can't open the sales report we sent this morning, and she needs it for her board meeting at three o'clock. B: I probably saved it in the wrong format, so I'll convert it right away and send her a version that works on any computer or phone.","t":"A：客戶說她打不開我們今天早上寄的銷售報告，而她三點的董事會議需要用到。 B：我大概存成了錯誤的【格式】，所以我會馬上轉檔，寄給她一個任何電腦或手機都能開的版本。"},{"w":"EPUB","p":"n.","d":"a common e-book file type that fits its text to any screen size","c":"EPUB電子書格式","s":"A: The marketing team finished writing our travel guide, but which file type should we choose so readers can enjoy it on both tablets and small phone screens? B: I'd recommend EPUB, because the text adjusts automatically to any screen size, and most online bookstores and reading apps accept it.","t":"A：行銷團隊寫完了我們的旅遊指南，但我們該選哪種檔案類型，讓讀者在平板和小小的手機螢幕上都能閱讀？ B：我建議用【EPUB格式】，因為文字會自動配合任何螢幕大小調整，而且大部分線上書店和閱讀應用程式都接受。"},{"w":"PDF","p":"n.","d":"a file type that keeps a document's layout the same on any device","c":"PDF檔","s":"A: Should I send the signed contract to the supplier as a Word file, or is there a better way to make sure nobody can change the layout? B: Please save it as a PDF before you attach it, because the pages will look exactly the same on every computer and it's harder to edit.","t":"A：我該把簽好的合約用Word檔寄給供應商嗎？還是有更好的方法能確保沒人能改動版面？ B：請在附加之前先存成【PDF檔】，因為頁面在每台電腦上看起來都會一模一樣，而且比較難被修改。"},{"w":"MOBI","p":"n.","d":"an older e-book file type used mainly on Kindle devices","c":"MOBI電子書格式（Kindle舊格式）","s":"A: Some of our older customers say the cookbook they bought from our website won't open on their Kindle devices, so what should we do? B: Let's offer a MOBI version as well, since many older Kindles were designed for that file type, and we can email it to them free of charge.","t":"A：一些老顧客說，他們從我們網站買的食譜在他們的Kindle裝置上打不開，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們也提供【MOBI格式】的版本吧，因為很多舊型Kindle就是為那種檔案類型設計的，而且我們可以免費用電子郵件寄給他們。"},{"w":"download","p":"v.","d":"to copy a file from the internet to your device","c":"下載","s":"A: The sales conference starts tomorrow morning, and I'm worried the hotel Wi-Fi will be too slow to open the presentation slides. B: You should download all the files to your laptop tonight, so you can show them without an internet connection, even if the hotel network goes down.","t":"A：業務研討會明天早上開始，我擔心飯店的無線網路太慢，打不開簡報投影片。 B：你應該今晚就把所有檔案【下載】到筆電裡，這樣即使飯店網路斷線，你不用連網也能展示。"},{"w":"upload","p":"v.","d":"to send a file from your device to a website or server","c":"上傳","s":"A: The photographer finished taking pictures of our new product line yesterday, but how will the design team in Tokyo get the files in time? B: She'll upload them to the company cloud folder this afternoon, and the designers can start working on the catalog as soon as they arrive tomorrow.","t":"A：攝影師昨天拍完了我們新產品系列的照片，但東京的設計團隊要怎麼及時拿到檔案？ B：她今天下午會把照片【上傳】到公司的雲端資料夾，設計師們明天一到就能開始製作型錄。"},{"w":"library","p":"n.","d":"a collection of books that people can borrow or read","c":"圖書館；（數位）書庫","s":"A: Is it true that employees can borrow business books for free, or do we have to buy them ourselves for the leadership course? B: The company has an online library with over five hundred titles, so you just log in with your staff number and borrow whatever you need for two weeks.","t":"A：員工真的可以免費借商業書籍嗎？還是領導力課程用的書得自己買？ B：公司有一個超過五百本書的線上【圖書館】，你只要用員工編號登入，就可以借任何需要的書兩週。"},{"w":"annotation","p":"n.","d":"a short note added to a text to explain or comment on it","c":"註解；批註","s":"A: Did the lawyer have any comments on the new rental agreement before we send it back to the landlord on Friday? B: Yes, she added an annotation next to the paragraph about repairs, explaining that we should ask the landlord to pay for any damage caused by old pipes.","t":"A：在我們星期五把新租約寄回給房東之前，律師有什麼意見嗎？ B：有，她在關於維修的那一段旁邊加了一則【註解】，說明我們應該要求房東負擔老舊水管造成的任何損壞。"},{"w":"font","p":"n.","d":"the style and size of printed letters","c":"字型","s":"A: Several older readers have complained that our monthly newsletter is hard to read, especially the small print at the bottom of each page. B: Let's choose a larger and clearer font for the next issue, and we can also add more space between the lines so everything looks less crowded.","t":"A：好幾位年長讀者抱怨我們的月刊電子報很難閱讀，尤其是每頁底部的小字。 B：下一期我們就選一個更大、更清楚的【字型】，也可以加大行距，讓整體看起來不那麼擁擠。"},{"w":"screen","p":"n.","d":"the flat surface of a device that shows pictures or words","c":"螢幕","s":"A: Why are you holding your phone so close to your face while you read the meeting agenda that the manager sent this morning? B: I dropped it on the train yesterday, so the screen is cracked, and I can hardly see the words until I get it repaired at the store.","t":"A：你看經理今天早上寄來的會議議程時，為什麼把手機拿得離臉那麼近？ B：我昨天在火車上把它摔了，所以【螢幕】裂了，在拿去店裡修好之前我幾乎看不清楚字。"},{"w":"brightness","p":"n.","d":"how much light something gives off","c":"亮度","s":"A: My eyes feel tired after reading reports on my tablet for three hours, and I still have two more files to review before tomorrow's meeting. B: Try lowering the brightness of the display and taking a short break every half hour, because a very strong light can make your eyes hurt.","t":"A：我在平板上看了三個小時的報告，眼睛好累，而明天開會前我還有兩個檔案要審閱。 B：試著調低顯示器的【亮度】，並且每半小時休息一下，因為太強的光線會讓眼睛不舒服。"},{"w":"battery","p":"n.","d":"the part that stores power for a device","c":"電池","s":"A: Can I borrow your charger before the client meeting starts, because my laptop has only five percent power left and the presentation is on it? B: Sure, but the battery takes almost an hour to fill completely, so plug it in now and start with the printed handouts first.","t":"A：客戶會議開始前可以借一下你的充電器嗎？我的筆電只剩百分之五的電，而簡報就存在裡面。 B：當然可以，但【電池】要將近一小時才能充滿，所以現在就插上電，先從紙本講義開始講。"},{"w":"storage","p":"n.","d":"space for keeping files on a device or computer","c":"儲存空間","s":"A: The new tablets we ordered for the sales team can't save all the product videos, and the staff keep getting warning messages. B: They only have thirty-two gigabytes of storage, so we should either buy memory cards or keep the large videos in the company's online folder instead.","t":"A：我們幫業務團隊訂的新平板存不下所有產品影片，員工一直收到警告訊息。 B：它們只有32GB的【儲存空間】，所以我們要嘛買記憶卡，要嘛把大型影片改存在公司的線上資料夾。"},{"w":"cloud","p":"n.","d":"online servers where you can keep and share files","c":"雲端","s":"A: What happens to all my work files if my laptop is stolen during the business trip, because I haven't made a copy of anything yet? B: Don't worry, the IT team set up automatic backups last month, so every document is saved in the cloud and you can open it from any device.","t":"A：如果我的筆電在出差時被偷了，我所有的工作檔案會怎麼樣？我還沒有備份任何東西。 B：別擔心，資訊團隊上個月設定了自動備份，所以每份文件都存在【雲端】，你從任何裝置都能打開。"},{"w":"sync","p":"v.","d":"to make the same data appear on two or more devices","c":"同步","s":"A: I added the client's new phone number on my office computer this morning, but it's not showing on my phone, and I need to call her now. B: You probably need to sync your devices first, so tap the update button in the contacts app and wait a few seconds for the information to appear.","t":"A：我今天早上在辦公室電腦上加了客戶的新電話號碼，但手機上沒有顯示，而我現在就需要打給她。 B：你可能得先把裝置【同步】，所以在聯絡人應用程式裡點一下更新按鈕，等幾秒鐘資料就會出現。"},{"w":"reader","p":"n.","d":"a person who reads","c":"讀者","s":"A: Why did the publishing company decide to print a second edition of the travel guide so soon after the first one came out? B: Almost every reader who bought the first edition left a positive review online, so the store ran out of copies in just three weeks.","t":"A：為什麼出版公司在旅遊指南第一版出版後這麼快就決定印第二版？ B：幾乎每位買了第一版的【讀者】都在網路上留下好評，所以書店短短三週就賣光了。"},{"w":"interface","p":"n.","d":"the screen design that lets a person use a program","c":"介面","s":"A: Our customers keep calling the help desk because they can't find the payment button in the new shopping app we launched last week. B: The design team is already making the interface simpler, with bigger buttons and clearer menus, so users should find everything easily after next week's update.","t":"A：我們的顧客一直打電話到服務台，因為他們在我們上週推出的新購物應用程式裡找不到付款按鈕。 B：設計團隊已經在簡化【介面】，加大按鈕並讓選單更清楚，所以下週更新後使用者應該就能輕鬆找到所有功能。"},{"w":"portable","p":"adj.","d":"light and easy to carry","c":"輕便的；可攜帶的","s":"A: I need a projector for my sales presentations at different client offices next month, but the one in our meeting room is far too heavy. B: The supply office has a small portable model that fits in a laptop bag, so you can easily carry it on the train and set it up anywhere.","t":"A：我下個月要到不同的客戶辦公室做業務簡報，需要一台投影機，但我們會議室那台太重了。 B：庫房有一台小型【可攜式】機種，放得進筆電包，所以你可以輕鬆帶上火車，到哪裡都能架設。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy to reach, get, or use","c":"可取得的；容易使用的","s":"A: How can we make sure that staff in our overseas branches can read the safety training materials, even when they work night shifts? B: We'll put everything online so the materials are accessible twenty-four hours a day, and employees can study whenever it's convenient for them.","t":"A：我們要怎麼確保海外分公司的員工，即使上夜班也能閱讀安全訓練教材？ B：我們會把所有內容放上網，讓教材一天二十四小時都【可以取得】，員工可以在自己方便的時候學習。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing users to take part and get a response","c":"互動式的","s":"A: Last year's training videos were boring, and many new employees stopped watching them after just ten minutes, so what should we change this time? B: Let's make the course more interactive, with short quizzes, clickable charts, and small games, so trainees stay involved and remember the information better.","t":"A：去年的訓練影片很無聊，許多新進員工看了十分鐘就不看了，這次我們該做什麼改變？ B：我們讓課程更【互動】一點，加入簡短小測驗、可點選的圖表和小遊戲，讓受訓者保持參與並記得更牢。"},{"w":"searchable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be searched by a computer","c":"可搜尋的","s":"A: The old customer contracts are stored as photos, so I spend hours looking through them whenever a client asks about a specific payment term. B: The new software will turn every page into searchable text, so you can type a keyword and find the right paragraph in seconds.","t":"A：舊的客戶合約都是以照片存檔，所以每當客戶詢問某個付款條件時，我都要花好幾個小時翻找。 B：新軟體會把每一頁轉成【可搜尋的】文字，你只要輸入關鍵字，幾秒鐘就能找到正確的段落。"},{"w":"subscription","p":"n.","d":"a regular payment to receive a product or service","c":"訂閱","s":"A: Do we really need to buy each business magazine separately for the staff lounge, or is there a cheaper option that our budget can cover? B: We could pay for a yearly subscription to a digital reading service, which gives everyone unlimited access to hundreds of magazines for a fixed monthly cost.","t":"A：我們真的需要為員工休息室分別購買每一本商業雜誌嗎？還是有我們預算負擔得起的更便宜選擇？ B：我們可以付費【訂閱】一年的數位閱讀服務，以固定的月費讓大家無限閱讀數百種雜誌。"},{"w":"copyright","p":"n.","d":"the legal right to control copies of a book, song, or other work","c":"版權；著作權","s":"A: Can we copy a few chapters from that popular management book and share them with all the trainees in next week's workshop? B: Not without permission, because the publisher owns the copyright, so I'll contact them today and ask how much it would cost to use those chapters legally.","t":"A：我們可以影印那本熱門管理書籍的幾個章節，在下週的工作坊分給所有受訓者嗎？ B：沒有許可是不行的，因為出版社擁有【版權】，所以我今天會聯絡他們，詢問合法使用那些章節要花多少錢。"},{"w":"publisher","p":"n.","d":"a company that prepares, prints, and sells books","c":"出版商；出版社","s":"A: Our sales manager wrote a guide about negotiating with international clients, and she wants to sell it in bookstores across Asia next year. B: She should contact a publisher that specializes in business titles, because they can edit, print, and market the book much more effectively than she can alone.","t":"A：我們的業務經理寫了一本與國際客戶談判的指南，她想明年在亞洲各地的書店販售。 B：她應該聯絡一家專門出版商業書籍的【出版社】，因為他們編輯、印刷和行銷這本書的效果會比她自己一個人好得多。"},{"w":"self-publish","p":"v.","d":"to publish your own book without a publishing company","c":"自行出版；自費出版","s":"A: My colleague finished writing a cookbook, but several publishing companies have rejected it, and she's starting to feel disappointed and wants to give up. B: She could self-publish it online instead, since many writers now sell their books directly on digital platforms and keep a larger share of the profits.","t":"A：我同事寫完了一本食譜，但好幾家出版公司都拒絕了，她開始感到失望，想要放棄。 B：她可以改在網路上【自行出版】，因為現在很多作家直接在數位平台上賣書，還能保留較多的利潤。"},{"w":"platform","p":"n.","d":"a website or system where services or products are offered","c":"平台","s":"A: Where should we sell our new language-learning e-books, because our own website doesn't get many visitors yet and the budget for advertising is small? B: Let's use a popular online platform that already has millions of users, so readers around the world can find and buy our books easily.","t":"A：我們新的語言學習電子書應該在哪裡賣？因為我們自己的網站訪客還不多，廣告預算也很少。 B：我們就用一個已經有數百萬使用者的熱門線上【平台】，讓世界各地的讀者都能輕鬆找到並購買我們的書。"},{"w":"reader-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"easy for readers to read and understand","c":"易於閱讀的","s":"A: The annual report is full of long paragraphs and technical terms, and the shareholders say they can't understand the main points before the meeting. B: Let's make it more reader-friendly by adding clear headings, simple charts, and short summaries at the start of each section.","t":"A：年度報告充滿了冗長的段落和專業術語，股東們說他們在會議前看不懂重點。 B：我們加上清楚的標題、簡單的圖表和每一節開頭的簡短摘要，讓它更【易於閱讀】。"},{"w":"convenient","p":"adj.","d":"easy and useful, not causing problems","c":"方便的","s":"A: Is it better for our team to meet in the downtown office or at the airport hotel when the visitors from Germany arrive next Tuesday? B: The airport hotel is more convenient for them, because they land at nine o'clock and can walk to the meeting room without taking a taxi.","t":"A：下週二德國訪客抵達時，我們團隊在市區辦公室還是機場飯店開會比較好？ B：機場飯店對他們比較【方便】，因為他們九點落地，不用搭計程車就能走到會議室。"},{"w":"paperless","p":"adj.","d":"using electronic files instead of paper","c":"無紙化的","s":"A: Our office spends a lot of money on printing every month, and the cabinets are completely full of old invoices and reports. B: Management plans to create a paperless office by next year, so all invoices and reports will be stored and signed electronically instead.","t":"A：我們辦公室每個月花很多錢在列印上，而且櫃子都塞滿了舊發票和報告。 B：管理階層計劃在明年前打造【無紙化】辦公室，所以所有發票和報告都會改成電子方式儲存和簽核。"},{"w":"instant","p":"adj.","d":"happening immediately","c":"即時的；立即的","s":"A: How long does it take for customers to receive the e-book after they pay on our website, because some say they waited a whole day? B: With the new system, delivery is instant, so the download link appears on the screen right after payment, and a copy is also sent by email.","t":"A：顧客在我們網站付款後要多久才能收到電子書？有些人說他們等了一整天。 B：有了新系統，交件是【即時的】，付款後下載連結會立刻出現在螢幕上，同時也會用電子郵件寄一份過去。"}]},{"unit":114,"theme":"E-mail 電子郵件","cards":[{"w":"inbox","p":"n.","d":"the folder where new e-mails arrive","c":"收件匣","s":"A: Did you see the message from the hotel about our booking for the sales conference next month in Kaohsiung? B: Not yet, because my inbox is full of over two hundred unread e-mails after the holiday, so I will search for it after lunch and forward it to you.","t":"A：你有看到飯店寄來關於我們下個月在高雄業務研討會訂房的訊息嗎？ B：還沒，因為假期過後我的【收件匣】裡塞滿了兩百多封未讀郵件，所以我午餐後會找找看，再轉寄給你。"},{"w":"outbox","p":"n.","d":"the folder that holds e-mails waiting to be sent","c":"寄件匣","s":"A: Why hasn't the client received the price list I e-mailed him this morning, even though I clicked the button twice before the meeting? B: I think your laptop lost its internet connection, so the message is probably still stuck in your outbox, waiting until you connect to the office network again.","t":"A：為什麼客戶還沒收到我今天早上寄給他的價目表？我開會前明明按了兩次按鈕。 B：我想你的筆電斷線了，所以那封信大概還卡在你的【寄件匣】裡，要等你重新連上公司網路才會寄出。"},{"w":"sent","p":"adj.","d":"already mailed out (used for e-mails you have mailed)","c":"已寄出的；寄件備份的","s":"A: The customer says she never got our refund confirmation, but I am sure our team e-mailed it to her last Friday afternoon. B: Please check the sent folder on the shared account, and if you find the message there, forward a copy to her with the original date clearly shown.","t":"A：那位顧客說她從沒收到我們的退款確認信，但我確定我們團隊上週五下午寄給她了。 B：請查看共用帳號裡的【寄件備份】資料夾，如果找到那封信，就把副本轉寄給她，並清楚顯示原本的日期。"},{"w":"draft","p":"n.","d":"an e-mail that is written but not mailed yet","c":"草稿","s":"A: Could you look at my e-mail to the new supplier before I send it, because I am worried that the tone sounds too strong? B: Sure, save it as a draft and share it with me, and I will read it carefully and suggest a few polite changes before the meeting at three.","t":"A：在我寄出給新供應商的電子郵件之前，你可以幫我看一下嗎？我擔心語氣聽起來太強硬。 B：沒問題，把它存成【草稿】並分享給我，我會在三點開會前仔細閱讀，並建議幾處比較禮貌的修改。"},{"w":"attachment","p":"n.","d":"a file that is mailed together with an e-mail","c":"附件","s":"A: I received your e-mail about the new training schedule, but I can't find the timetable you mentioned anywhere in the message. B: Sorry, I forgot to add the attachment because I was in a hurry to catch my train, so I will send the PDF file again as soon as I get to the office.","t":"A：我收到你關於新訓練時程的電子郵件了，但我在信裡找不到你提到的時間表。 B：抱歉，我急著趕火車，忘了加上【附件】，所以我一到辦公室就會重新寄出那份PDF檔。"},{"w":"cc","p":"v.","d":"to send a copy of an e-mail to another person","c":"以副本寄送","s":"A: Should I tell my manager that I am changing the delivery date for the Lin Trading order, or is that not necessary? B: Yes, please cc her on your e-mail to the customer, so she can see the new date and won't be surprised if the client calls her about it.","t":"A：我要更改林氏貿易訂單的交貨日期，需要告訴經理嗎？還是不必？ B：要，請在寄給客戶的郵件中【以副本寄送】給她，這樣她就能看到新日期，如果客戶打電話問她，她也不會感到意外。"},{"w":"bcc","p":"v.","d":"to send a copy of an e-mail secretly, so others cannot see the address","c":"以密件副本寄送","s":"A: I need to e-mail the event details to all two hundred guests, but I don't want them to see each other's addresses for privacy reasons. B: Then put your own address in the To line and bcc all the guests, so each person receives the message without seeing the full list.","t":"A：我需要把活動細節寄給全部兩百位賓客，但基於隱私考量，我不想讓他們看到彼此的地址。 B：那就把你自己的地址放在收件人欄，並用【密件副本】寄給所有賓客，這樣每個人都能收到信件，卻看不到完整名單。"},{"w":"subject","p":"n.","d":"the short title of an e-mail that tells what it is about","c":"主旨","s":"A: Why didn't the finance team answer my request for the travel budget, even though I sent it to them two days ago? B: They get hundreds of messages every day, so you should write a clear subject line like 'Urgent: Travel Budget for May' to help them notice it quickly.","t":"A：為什麼財務部沒有回覆我的差旅預算申請？我兩天前就寄給他們了。 B：他們每天收到上百封信，所以你應該寫一個清楚的【主旨】，例如「緊急：五月差旅預算」，幫助他們快速注意到。"},{"w":"signature","p":"n.","d":"the name and contact details added at the end of every e-mail","c":"簽名檔","s":"A: Our marketing department moved to the fifth floor last week, so what should I do about the old office address that customers still see? B: Update the signature at the bottom of your e-mails with the new address and phone number, so customers can contact you without any confusion.","t":"A：我們行銷部上週搬到五樓了，客戶還看到舊的辦公室地址，我該怎麼辦？ B：更新你郵件底部的【簽名檔】，換上新地址和電話號碼，這樣客戶就能順利聯絡你而不會混淆。"},{"w":"reply","p":"v.","d":"to answer an e-mail or message","c":"回覆","s":"A: The hotel in Tainan asked whether we need a projector and extra chairs for our training workshop next Tuesday morning. B: Please reply to them before five o'clock today and say we need both, because they have to prepare the meeting room the day before.","t":"A：台南的飯店問我們下週二上午的培訓研習是否需要投影機和額外椅子。 B：請在今天五點前【回覆】他們，說兩樣都需要，因為他們必須在前一天準備好會議室。"},{"w":"forward","p":"v.","d":"to send an e-mail you received to another person","c":"轉寄","s":"A: I just got a message from a customer who wants a discount on fifty office chairs, but I am not sure I can approve that. B: You should forward it to Mr. Chen in the sales department, since he handles large orders and can decide on special prices for regular clients.","t":"A：我剛收到一位顧客的信，他想買五十張辦公椅並要求折扣，但我不確定能不能核准。 B：你應該把它【轉寄】給業務部的陳先生，因為他負責大宗訂單，能決定給老客戶的特別價格。"},{"w":"compose","p":"v.","d":"to write an e-mail or message","c":"撰寫","s":"A: How long did it take you to finish the message to the investors about the delay in opening our new store downtown? B: It took me almost an hour to compose it, because I wanted to explain the problem honestly while still sounding positive about the opening next month.","t":"A：你寫那封給投資人、說明市中心新店延後開幕的信，花了多久時間？ B：我花了將近一小時來【撰寫】它，因為我想誠實說明問題，同時對下個月的開幕仍保持正面的語氣。"},{"w":"send","p":"v.","d":"to make a message or letter go to someone","c":"寄送；發送","s":"A: When do you think the customers will get the invitation to our product launch party at the convention center next month? B: I will send it this afternoon after my manager checks the date and the map, so they should have it in their inboxes by tonight.","t":"A：你覺得客戶什麼時候會收到我們下個月在會展中心舉辦的產品發表派對邀請函？ B：等經理確認日期和地圖後，我今天下午就會【寄出】，所以他們今晚前應該就會在收件匣裡看到。"},{"w":"receive","p":"v.","d":"to get something that someone mails or gives you","c":"收到","s":"A: Has the accounting team said anything about the invoice from the printing company for the brochures we ordered last month? B: Yes, they told me they didn't receive it until this morning, so the payment will be a few days late, and they have already apologized to the printer.","t":"A：會計部有提到印刷公司寄來的、我們上個月訂購的手冊發票嗎？ B：有，他們說直到今天早上才【收到】，所以付款會晚幾天，他們已經向印刷廠道歉了。"},{"w":"delete","p":"v.","d":"to remove something from a computer","c":"刪除","s":"A: My computer keeps telling me that my e-mail storage is almost full, and now I can't get any new messages from clients. B: You should delete old messages with large files, like photos and videos, and then empty the trash folder so you have enough space again.","t":"A：我的電腦一直提醒我電子郵件儲存空間快滿了，現在我收不到客戶的任何新郵件。 B：你應該【刪除】附有大檔案的舊郵件，像是照片和影片，然後清空垃圾桶資料夾，這樣就會再有足夠的空間。"},{"w":"archive","p":"v.","d":"to store old e-mails in a safe place so you can find them later","c":"封存；歸檔","s":"A: Should I keep all the e-mails about last year's contract with the shipping company, even though the project is already finished? B: Yes, please archive them in a separate folder instead of deleting them, because the lawyers may need to check the details if there is a problem later.","t":"A：去年和貨運公司的合約相關郵件，雖然專案已經結束了，我還要全部保留嗎？ B：要，請把它們【封存】到另一個資料夾而不是刪除，因為如果日後出了問題，律師可能需要查看細節。"},{"w":"spam","p":"n.","d":"unwanted e-mails, usually advertisements, mailed to many people","c":"垃圾郵件","s":"A: I applied for the marketing job at a big hotel two weeks ago, but I still haven't heard anything from their human resources office. B: Check your spam folder, because messages from new companies sometimes end up there by mistake, and you might have missed an interview invitation.","t":"A：我兩週前應徵了一家大飯店的行銷職缺，但到現在還沒收到人資部門的任何消息。 B：查看一下你的【垃圾郵件】資料夾，因為新公司寄來的信有時會被誤放在那裡，你可能錯過了面試邀請。"},{"w":"filter","p":"v.","d":"to sort or block messages automatically","c":"過濾","s":"A: I get so many advertisements every day that I often miss important messages from my team members and our customers. B: You can set up rules to filter your e-mail, so messages from the office go into one folder and the advertisements are moved away automatically.","t":"A：我每天收到太多廣告，常常錯過組員和客戶寄來的重要郵件。 B：你可以設定規則來【過濾】電子郵件，讓辦公室寄來的信進入同一個資料夾，廣告則自動被移走。"},{"w":"thread","p":"n.","d":"a series of e-mails that answer each other on one topic","c":"郵件串；討論串","s":"A: I just joined the project team, so how can I find out what everyone has already decided about the new website design? B: Read the whole e-mail thread about the website from the beginning, because it shows every message and decision in order since the first meeting in March.","t":"A：我剛加入專案小組，要怎麼知道大家對新網站設計已經做了哪些決定？ B：從頭閱讀整個關於網站的【郵件串】，因為它依序列出從三月第一次會議以來的每封信和每個決定。"},{"w":"newsletter","p":"n.","d":"a regular report with news mailed to members or customers","c":"電子報；通訊","s":"A: How do you usually tell our customers about new products, special discounts, and changes to the store opening hours? B: We send a monthly newsletter by e-mail to everyone who signs up on our website, and it usually brings many visitors to the store the following weekend.","t":"A：你們通常怎麼告訴顧客新產品、特別折扣和營業時間的變動？ B：我們每月會用電子郵件寄送【電子報】給所有在網站上註冊的人，而且通常在接下來的週末帶來許多來店顧客。"},{"w":"notification","p":"n.","d":"a message that tells you something has happened","c":"通知","s":"A: How did you know so quickly that the client had changed the meeting time, when you were driving to the airport? B: My phone showed a notification as soon as her e-mail arrived, so my coworker in the passenger seat read it to me and called our assistant to update the schedule.","t":"A：你開車去機場的路上，怎麼那麼快就知道客戶改了開會時間？ B：她的信一到，我的手機就跳出【通知】，所以坐在副駕駛座的同事唸給我聽，並打電話請助理更新行程。"},{"w":"account","p":"n.","d":"a personal record that lets you use an e-mail or online service","c":"帳號；帳戶","s":"A: I am starting my new job at the bank on Monday, so how will I get messages from my manager and the team? B: The IT department will create an e-mail account for you on your first morning, and they will give you a temporary password to sign in.","t":"A：我週一要開始在銀行的新工作，我要怎麼收到經理和團隊的訊息？ B：資訊部門會在你第一天早上幫你建立一個電子郵件【帳號】，並給你一組臨時密碼登入。"},{"w":"password","p":"n.","d":"a secret word you type to enter a computer system","c":"密碼","s":"A: I tried to sign in to my work e-mail this morning, but the system keeps saying that my information is wrong. B: You probably need to change your password, because the company asks every employee to choose a new one every ninety days for security reasons.","t":"A：我今天早上試著登入工作信箱，但系統一直說我的資料錯誤。 B：你大概需要更改【密碼】，因為公司基於安全考量，要求每位員工每九十天換一個新的。"},{"w":"login","p":"n.","d":"the name and details you use to enter a computer system","c":"登入帳號；登入資訊","s":"A: The new intern can't open the company e-mail system, and she needs to send the meeting notes to the director before noon. B: Ask the IT office to give her a login today, and in the meantime she can save the notes on a USB drive and bring them to me.","t":"A：新來的實習生打不開公司的電子郵件系統，而她必須在中午前把會議記錄寄給主管。 B：請資訊室今天給她一組【登入帳號】，在那之前她可以先把記錄存在隨身碟裡拿給我。"},{"w":"logout","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a computer system","c":"登出","s":"A: Why does the e-mail system keep closing while I am in the middle of writing a long report to the head office? B: There is an automatic logout after fifteen minutes without any activity, so save your work often and type something every few minutes to stay connected.","t":"A：為什麼我寫給總公司的長篇報告寫到一半，電子郵件系統就一直關閉？ B：系統在十五分鐘沒有任何動作後會自動【登出】，所以要經常存檔，並每隔幾分鐘輸入點東西以保持連線。"},{"w":"server","p":"n.","d":"a main computer that stores and sends e-mails for many users","c":"伺服器","s":"A: Why can't anyone in the office send or receive e-mails this morning, even though the internet seems to be working fine? B: The company's e-mail server is being repaired by the technicians, and they said everything should be back to normal before our meeting with the clients at eleven.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上辦公室裡沒人能收發電子郵件？網路明明看起來正常。 B：公司的電子郵件【伺服器】正由技術人員維修中，他們說在我們十一點和客戶開會前應該就會恢復正常。"},{"w":"provider","p":"n.","d":"a company that offers a service such as e-mail or internet","c":"供應商；服務業者","s":"A: Our small company keeps having problems with lost messages and slow service, so what do you think we should do about it? B: I think we should switch to a bigger e-mail provider that offers more storage, better security, and customer support twenty-four hours a day, even if it costs more.","t":"A：我們小公司一直有郵件遺失和服務緩慢的問題，你覺得該怎麼辦？ B：我認為我們應該換一家較大的電子郵件服務【供應商】，提供更多儲存空間、更好的安全性和全天候客服，即使費用較高也值得。"},{"w":"client","p":"n.","d":"a computer program used to read and write e-mails","c":"用戶端程式","s":"A: Which program should I install on my new laptop so I can read my work messages even when I am not connected to the internet? B: The company recommends a desktop e-mail client because it saves copies of your messages, so you can read them on the plane during business trips.","t":"A：我的新筆電該安裝哪個程式，才能在沒連網時也能讀工作郵件？ B：公司推薦使用桌面版電子郵件【用戶端程式】，因為它會儲存郵件副本，讓你出差時在飛機上也能閱讀。"},{"w":"mailbox","p":"n.","d":"the storage space where your e-mails are kept","c":"信箱","s":"A: Why did my message to the human resources manager come back with an error, even though I typed her address correctly? B: Her mailbox is full because she has been on vacation for two weeks, so she can't get any new e-mails until she clears some space.","t":"A：為什麼我寄給人資經理的信被退回並顯示錯誤？我明明把她的地址打對了。 B：她的【信箱】滿了，因為她已經休假兩週，在她清出空間之前收不到任何新郵件。"},{"w":"delivery","p":"n.","d":"the act of a message reaching the person it was meant for","c":"送達；投遞","s":"A: How can I be sure that the manager in Tokyo actually got the contract I e-mailed to him late last night? B: You can ask for a delivery receipt when you send important messages, so the system tells you the exact time the e-mail reached his mailbox.","t":"A：我要怎麼確定東京的經理真的收到我昨晚寄給他的合約？ B：寄重要郵件時你可以要求【送達】回條，系統就會告訴你那封信抵達他信箱的確切時間。"},{"w":"bounce","p":"v.","d":"(of an e-mail) to come back because it cannot be delivered","c":"（郵件）被退回","s":"A: I sent the price list to the new customer three times, but each time I got an error message a few minutes later. B: Your e-mails will bounce if the address has a spelling mistake, so call the customer and check the exact address before you try again.","t":"A：我把價目表寄給新客戶三次，但每次幾分鐘後都收到錯誤訊息。 B：如果地址拼錯，你的郵件就會被【退回】，所以打電話給客戶確認正確地址後再試一次。"},{"w":"encrypt","p":"v.","d":"to change information into a secret code so others cannot read it","c":"加密","s":"A: I need to send the employees' salary information to the accountant, but I'm worried that someone else could read it. B: You should encrypt the message before sending it, so only the accountant can open it with a special code, and the information stays safe from hackers.","t":"A：我需要把員工的薪資資料寄給會計師，但我擔心別人可能會看到。 B：你應該在寄出前將郵件【加密】，這樣只有會計師能用特殊密碼打開，資料就不會被駭客竊取。"},{"w":"unsubscribe","p":"v.","d":"to stop getting e-mails from a company or list","c":"取消訂閱","s":"A: I keep getting advertising e-mails from an online clothing store that I bought a jacket from once, two years ago. B: Scroll to the bottom of one of their messages and click the link to unsubscribe, and then you should stop receiving their advertisements within a few days.","t":"A：我兩年前在一家網路服飾店買過一件夾克，之後就一直收到他們的廣告信。 B：捲動到他們其中一封信的最下方，點擊連結來【取消訂閱】，幾天內你應該就不會再收到他們的廣告了。"},{"w":"auto-reply","p":"n.","d":"an answer that is mailed automatically when you are away","c":"自動回覆","s":"A: I'm going on a business trip to Singapore next week, and I won't be able to check my e-mails very often. B: Then set up an auto-reply before you leave, so people know you are away and can contact your assistant for urgent matters while you are traveling.","t":"A：我下週要去新加坡出差，沒辦法常常查看電子郵件。 B：那出發前先設定【自動回覆】，讓大家知道你不在，緊急事情可以在你出差期間聯絡你的助理。"}]},{"unit":115,"theme":"Eating 飲食","cards":[{"w":"eat","p":"v.","d":"to put food in your mouth and swallow it","c":"吃","s":"A: Do you know where the new interns usually go at lunchtime, because I want to invite them to join our team for a welcome event this week? B: Most of them eat at the small Italian café across the street, since it is cheap, fast, and only two minutes from the office.","t":"A：你知道新來的實習生午餐時間通常去哪裡嗎？因為我想邀請他們本週參加我們團隊的歡迎活動。 B：他們大多數人在對街那家小義大利咖啡館【吃飯】，因為那裡便宜、快速，而且離辦公室只要兩分鐘。"},{"w":"consume","p":"v.","d":"to eat or drink something; to use something up","c":"食用；消耗","s":"A: Why did the cafeteria manager put up a new sign next to the drink machines in the staff lounge yesterday afternoon? B: She wants to remind employees that they should consume food and drinks only in the break room, not at their desks, because crumbs are attracting insects to the office.","t":"A：餐廳經理昨天下午為什麼在員工休息室的飲料機旁邊貼了一張新告示？ B：她想提醒員工，只能在休息室裡【食用】食物和飲料，不要在座位上吃，因為碎屑正把蟲子引進辦公室。"},{"w":"devour","p":"v.","d":"to eat something very quickly because you are very hungry","c":"狼吞虎嚥；吞食","s":"A: How did the warehouse staff react when you brought those boxes of pizza after the long inventory check on Saturday? B: They were so hungry after working for nine hours without a proper break that they managed to devour all six pizzas in less than ten minutes and then thanked me many times.","t":"A：週六那場漫長的盤點結束後，你帶那幾盒披薩過去，倉庫員工有什麼反應？ B：他們連續工作九個小時都沒有好好休息，餓壞了，不到十分鐘就把六個披薩全部【狼吞虎嚥地吃光】，然後向我道謝了好多次。"},{"w":"nibble","p":"v.","d":"to eat something in small bites, slowly","c":"小口地吃；啃","s":"A: Will there be a full lunch at the product training session, or should I bring something to eat during the afternoon? B: There will only be light snacks, so most trainees just nibble on crackers and fruit while they listen, and then they go out for a real dinner after the session ends at six.","t":"A：產品培訓課程會提供完整的午餐嗎？還是我下午應該自己帶點東西吃？ B：只會有輕食點心，所以大多數學員一邊聽課一邊【小口吃】餅乾和水果，等六點課程結束後再出去好好吃頓晚餐。"},{"w":"chew","p":"v.","d":"to bite food many times with your teeth before swallowing it","c":"咀嚼；嚼","s":"A: Why did the dentist at the company health fair tell everyone to slow down at lunch and avoid eating at their desks? B: He explained that people who chew their food slowly and carefully usually feel better in the afternoon, because their stomachs do not have to work so hard after a big meal.","t":"A：公司健康博覽會上的牙醫為什麼要大家午餐吃慢一點，並避免在座位上吃飯？ B：他解釋說，慢慢且仔細【咀嚼】食物的人下午通常感覺比較好，因為飽餐後胃不必那麼辛苦地工作。"},{"w":"swallow","p":"v.","d":"to make food or drink go down your throat","c":"吞下；嚥下","s":"A: Did the pharmacist give you any special instructions when you picked up the medicine for your business trip to Singapore? B: Yes, she told me to swallow one tablet with a full glass of water after breakfast every morning, and she warned me not to take it on an empty stomach.","t":"A：你去領新加坡出差要用的藥時，藥劑師有沒有給你什麼特別的指示？ B：有，她叫我每天早上早餐後配一整杯水【吞服】一顆藥錠，並提醒我不要空腹服用。"},{"w":"savor","p":"v.","d":"to eat or drink something slowly so you can enjoy it fully","c":"細細品嚐；品味","s":"A: Why did you choose such an expensive French restaurant for the dinner with our new partners from Tokyo next Friday night? B: The chef serves seven small courses over three hours, so our guests can relax, savor every dish, and talk about the contract in a calm and friendly atmosphere.","t":"A：下週五晚上和東京新合作夥伴的晚餐，你為什麼選了這麼昂貴的法國餐廳？ B：主廚會在三小時內上七道小份料理，讓我們的客人可以放鬆、【細細品嚐】每道菜，並在平靜友好的氣氛中討論合約。"},{"w":"dine","p":"v.","d":"to eat dinner, especially a formal one","c":"用餐；進餐","s":"A: Where are the conference speakers going after the awards ceremony on Thursday evening, and do they need a bus from the hotel? B: They will dine at the rooftop restaurant on the twentieth floor of the same hotel, so they can simply take the elevator upstairs after the ceremony ends.","t":"A：週四晚上頒獎典禮結束後，研討會講者要去哪裡？他們需要從飯店搭巴士嗎？ B：他們會在同一家飯店二十樓的屋頂餐廳【用餐】，所以典禮結束後只要搭電梯上樓就可以了。"},{"w":"gorge","p":"v.","d":"to eat far too much food","c":"大吃特吃；吃撐","s":"A: Why do you always feel so sleepy during the Monday afternoon sales meeting, even when you go to bed early on Sunday night? B: I think it is because I gorge on fried chicken and noodles at the company buffet every Monday, and that heavy food makes it very hard to concentrate afterward.","t":"A：為什麼你在週一下午的業務會議上總是很想睡，即使週日晚上很早就上床睡覺？ B：我想是因為我每週一都在公司自助餐【大吃特吃】炸雞和麵，那些油膩的食物讓我之後很難專心。"},{"w":"overeat","p":"v.","d":"to eat more food than your body needs","c":"吃太多；暴食","s":"A: Do you have any advice for the new staff who are attending the three-day sales conference with a free buffet at every meal? B: Yes, I always tell them not to overeat at lunch, because they need to stay alert for the afternoon workshops and the long networking events in the evening.","t":"A：對於要參加三天業務研討會、每餐都有免費自助餐的新員工，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：有，我總是告訴他們午餐不要【吃太多】，因為他們需要保持清醒，參加下午的工作坊和晚上漫長的交流活動。"},{"w":"undereat","p":"v.","d":"to eat less food than your body needs","c":"吃得不夠；進食不足","s":"A: Why did the coach of our company running team ask everyone to write down their meals before the city marathon next month? B: He worries that some busy runners undereat during long work weeks, and without enough food they will not have the energy to finish the race safely.","t":"A：我們公司跑步隊的教練為什麼要大家在下個月的城市馬拉松之前記錄自己的餐點？ B：他擔心有些忙碌的跑者在漫長的工作週裡【吃得不夠】，沒有足夠的食物，他們就沒有體力安全地跑完比賽。"},{"w":"appetite","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you want to eat","c":"食慾；胃口","s":"A: Is the new manager feeling better now, or is he still tired after flying back from the trade show in Berlin last week? B: He is much better, and his appetite has finally returned, so he ordered a big lunch today and even asked the team where to find good local food.","t":"A：新經理現在好點了嗎？還是上週從柏林商展飛回來後還是很累？ B：他好多了，【胃口】也終於恢復了，所以他今天點了一份豐盛的午餐，甚至還問團隊哪裡有好吃的在地美食。"},{"w":"hunger","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you need food","c":"飢餓","s":"A: Why did the factory decide to provide free breakfast for workers on the early morning shift starting next month? B: Many workers said that hunger made it hard for them to focus before lunch, and the safety manager believes a warm breakfast will reduce mistakes on the production line.","t":"A：工廠為什麼決定從下個月開始為清晨班的工人提供免費早餐？ B：很多工人說【飢餓】讓他們在午餐前很難專心，而安全主管認為一份熱騰騰的早餐能減少生產線上的錯誤。"},{"w":"full","p":"adj.","d":"having eaten so much that you do not want more","c":"飽的","s":"A: Would you like to try a piece of the chocolate cake that the marketing team brought to celebrate our successful product launch? B: Thank you, but I am completely full after the large business lunch with our clients, so could you please save me a small piece for tomorrow morning?","t":"A：你要不要嚐一塊行銷團隊為慶祝產品成功上市帶來的巧克力蛋糕？ B：謝謝，不過和客戶吃完那頓豐盛的商務午餐後，我已經完全【吃飽】了，可以幫我留一小塊明天早上吃嗎？"},{"w":"satisfied","p":"adj.","d":"pleased because you got what you wanted or needed","c":"滿足的；滿意的","s":"A: Did the guests at the hotel conference center like the new lunch menu that the kitchen staff prepared for the medical seminar yesterday? B: Yes, most of them said they were very satisfied with the fresh salads and grilled fish, and several people even asked the chef for his recipes.","t":"A：飯店會議中心的賓客喜歡廚房人員昨天為醫學研討會準備的新午餐菜單嗎？ B：喜歡，大多數人說他們對新鮮沙拉和烤魚非常【滿意】，還有幾個人甚至向主廚要了食譜。"},{"w":"hungry","p":"adj.","d":"wanting or needing food","c":"餓的","s":"A: Should we order some sandwiches for the board meeting, or do you think it will finish before lunchtime today? B: Let's order them now, because the meeting may run until two o'clock, and people make poor decisions when they are tired and hungry after a long morning.","t":"A：我們要為董事會會議訂一些三明治嗎？還是你覺得今天會議會在午餐前結束？ B：現在就訂吧，因為會議可能會開到兩點，而人在經過漫長的早上又累又【餓】的時候，會做出不好的決定。"},{"w":"starving","p":"adj.","d":"very hungry","c":"餓壞了的","s":"A: You look tired, so did you have time for breakfast before your early flight back from the client meeting in Seoul? B: No, the flight was delayed for three hours and the airport shops were closed, so I am absolutely starving and need to find a restaurant before I return to the office.","t":"A：你看起來很累，從首爾客戶會議搭早班機回來之前，你有時間吃早餐嗎？ B：沒有，班機延誤了三個小時，機場的商店又都關門了，所以我真的【餓壞了】，回辦公室前得先找間餐廳。"},{"w":"nutritious","p":"adj.","d":"full of things your body needs to stay healthy","c":"有營養的","s":"A: Why is the company cafeteria changing its menu next month, and will the prices for lunch go up as a result? B: The prices will stay the same, but the new supplier will offer more nutritious dishes, such as vegetable soups and brown rice, because employees asked for better options.","t":"A：公司餐廳下個月為什麼要更換菜單？午餐價格會因此上漲嗎？ B：價格會維持不變，但新的供應商會提供更多【有營養的】菜色，例如蔬菜湯和糙米飯，因為員工要求更好的選擇。"},{"w":"healthy","p":"adj.","d":"good for your body","c":"健康的","s":"A: Have you noticed that the vending machines on the third floor now sell fruit and yogurt instead of chips and candy? B: Yes, the human resources team replaced the snacks because they want to encourage healthy eating habits, and so far most employees seem quite happy with the change.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到三樓的自動販賣機現在賣的是水果和優格，而不是洋芋片和糖果？ B：有，人資團隊換掉了那些零食，因為他們想鼓勵【健康的】飲食習慣，到目前為止大多數員工似乎都很滿意這個改變。"},{"w":"balanced","p":"adj.","d":"having the right amounts of different kinds of food","c":"均衡的","s":"A: What did the nutrition expert talk about at the employee wellness workshop that you attended last Wednesday afternoon? B: She explained that a balanced diet with vegetables, protein, and whole grains helps office workers stay focused, and she gave us some simple lunch ideas that we can prepare at home.","t":"A：你上週三下午參加的員工健康工作坊上，營養專家講了什麼？ B：她解釋說，包含蔬菜、蛋白質和全穀物的【均衡】飲食能幫助上班族保持專注，她還給了我們一些可以在家準備的簡單午餐點子。"},{"w":"flavorful","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of strong, pleasant taste","c":"味道濃郁的；美味的","s":"A: How did the customers respond to the new chicken curry that our restaurant added to the lunch menu last month? B: Many regular customers said it was the most flavorful dish on the menu because of the fresh herbs and spices, so we plan to offer it every day from now on.","t":"A：顧客對我們餐廳上個月新增到午餐菜單的雞肉咖哩反應如何？ B：很多常客說因為用了新鮮香草和香料，它是菜單上【味道最濃郁】的一道菜，所以我們打算從現在起每天供應。"},{"w":"savory","p":"adj.","d":"salty or spicy rather than sweet","c":"鹹的；鹹香的","s":"A: What kind of snacks should we prepare for the afternoon break at the client workshop, since many guests do not like sugar? B: Let's order some savory items like cheese crackers, mini sausage rolls, and vegetable chips, and we can also offer a small plate of fruit for anyone who prefers it.","t":"A：客戶工作坊下午休息時間我們該準備什麼點心？因為很多客人不喜歡甜食。 B：我們訂一些【鹹的】點心吧，像是起司餅乾、迷你香腸捲和蔬菜脆片，也可以為喜歡水果的人準備一小盤水果。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"tasting like sugar","c":"甜的","s":"A: Why did the bakery near our office lose so many customers after it changed its recipes at the beginning of the year? B: People complained that the new cakes were far too sweet, and many office workers who wanted a light treat with their afternoon coffee started buying from the shop across the street instead.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家麵包店年初改了食譜之後，為什麼流失了那麼多顧客？ B：大家抱怨新的蛋糕太【甜】了，很多想在下午喝咖啡時配點清爽點心的上班族就改去對街那家店買了。"},{"w":"spicy","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, hot taste from spices","c":"辣的","s":"A: Do you think our visitors from London will enjoy the Sichuan restaurant that you booked for dinner tomorrow night? B: I called the restaurant this morning and asked the chef to make some dishes less spicy, because our guests told me they cannot handle very hot food at all.","t":"A：你覺得我們來自倫敦的訪客會喜歡你為明晚晚餐訂的那家川菜餐廳嗎？ B：我今天早上打電話給餐廳，請主廚把一些菜做得沒那麼【辣】，因為我們的客人跟我說他們完全吃不了太辣的食物。"},{"w":"bland","p":"adj.","d":"having very little taste","c":"清淡無味的","s":"A: Why are so many patients leaving negative comments about the meals at the hospital where your sister works as a manager? B: They say the food is too bland because the kitchen uses very little salt or seasoning, so the hospital is now hiring a new chef to improve the menu.","t":"A：為什麼有那麼多病人對你姊姊擔任主管的那家醫院的餐點留下負評？ B：他們說食物太【淡而無味】，因為廚房幾乎不用鹽或調味料，所以醫院現在正在聘請新主廚來改善菜單。"},{"w":"delicious","p":"adj.","d":"tasting very good","c":"美味的","s":"A: How was the catering company that we hired for the retirement party of our finance director last Friday evening? B: Everyone said the food was absolutely delicious, especially the roast beef and the lemon tart, so I think we should use the same company for the holiday party in December.","t":"A：上週五晚上我們為財務總監的退休派對請的外燴公司表現如何？ B：大家都說食物非常【美味】，尤其是烤牛肉和檸檬塔，所以我覺得十二月的節慶派對也該找同一家公司。"},{"w":"tasty","p":"adj.","d":"having a good flavor","c":"好吃的","s":"A: Is there anywhere near the convention center where we can buy a quick lunch between the morning and afternoon sessions? B: There is a small food truck in the parking lot that sells cheap but very tasty noodles, and the line usually moves quickly, so we can get back before the next session.","t":"A：會展中心附近有沒有地方可以在上午和下午場次之間快速買個午餐？ B：停車場有一輛小餐車，賣便宜但非常【好吃】的麵，排隊通常很快，所以我們可以在下一場開始前回來。"},{"w":"digest","p":"v.","d":"to break down food in the stomach so the body can use it","c":"消化","s":"A: Why did the doctor suggest that you take a short walk after lunch instead of going straight back to your desk? B: She said a fifteen-minute walk helps the body digest food more easily, and it also gives me more energy for the long meetings that I usually have in the afternoon.","t":"A：醫生為什麼建議你午餐後去散個步，而不是直接回到座位上？ B：她說散步十五分鐘可以幫助身體更容易【消化】食物，也能讓我在下午通常要開的長時間會議中更有精神。"},{"w":"digestion","p":"n.","d":"the process of breaking down food in the body","c":"消化","s":"A: Why does the new health drink that our company is launching next month contain so much fiber and ginger? B: Our research team found that both ingredients support good digestion, so we will market the drink to busy office workers who often eat heavy lunches very quickly.","t":"A：我們公司下個月要推出的新健康飲品為什麼含有那麼多纖維和薑？ B：我們的研究團隊發現這兩種成分都有助於良好的【消化】，所以我們會把這款飲品推銷給常常很快吃完油膩午餐的忙碌上班族。"},{"w":"portion","p":"n.","d":"an amount of food for one person","c":"一份（食物）","s":"A: Why are some customers complaining about our restaurant on the review website, even though they say the food tastes great? B: They think each portion is too small for the price, so the owner has decided to serve larger plates of pasta and add a free salad at lunchtime.","t":"A：為什麼有些顧客在評論網站上抱怨我們餐廳，即使他們說食物很好吃？ B：他們覺得以這個價格來說每【份】太少了，所以老闆決定提供更大盤的義大利麵，並在午餐時段加送免費沙拉。"},{"w":"leftovers","p":"n.","d":"food that is not eaten at the end of a meal","c":"剩菜；剩飯","s":"A: What should we do with all the extra sandwiches and salads from the staff training session that ended early this afternoon? B: Let's put the leftovers in the office refrigerator and send an email to everyone, so people working late tonight can have a free dinner instead of ordering takeout.","t":"A：今天下午提早結束的員工培訓課程剩下那麼多三明治和沙拉，我們該怎麼處理？ B：我們把【剩菜】放進辦公室冰箱，再寄電子郵件通知大家，這樣今晚加班的人就可以吃免費晚餐，不必叫外賣。"},{"w":"meal","p":"n.","d":"the food you eat at one time, such as breakfast, lunch, or dinner","c":"一餐；餐點","s":"A: Does the company pay for food when we travel overseas for the trade show in Frankfurt next month? B: Yes, you can claim up to fifty dollars for each meal, but remember to keep every receipt and submit them to the finance department within one week after you return.","t":"A：下個月我們出國參加法蘭克福商展時，公司會支付餐費嗎？ B：會，你每【餐】最多可以申報五十美元，但記得保留每張收據，並在回國後一週內交給財務部。"}]},{"unit":116,"theme":"Economy 經濟","cards":[{"w":"inflation","p":"n.","d":"a general rise in prices over time","c":"通貨膨脹","s":"A: Why did the company cafeteria raise the price of lunch boxes again this month, even though the portions look exactly the same as before? B: Rising inflation has pushed up the cost of rice, meat, and cooking oil, so the supplier increased its prices and the cafeteria had no choice but to follow.","t":"A：為什麼公司餐廳這個月又調漲了便當的價格，即使份量看起來和以前完全一樣？ B：不斷上升的【通貨膨脹】推高了米、肉和食用油的成本，所以供應商調漲了價格，餐廳也只好跟著調整。"},{"w":"deflation","p":"n.","d":"a general fall in prices over time","c":"通貨緊縮","s":"A: Prices at the shopping mall have been falling for months, so why does the economist on the news seem so worried about it instead of happy? B: She explained that long periods of deflation make people delay their purchases, which lowers company sales, cuts wages, and can slowly weaken the whole economy.","t":"A：購物中心的價格已經下跌好幾個月了，為什麼新聞上的經濟學家看起來那麼擔心，而不是高興？ B：她解釋說，長期的【通貨緊縮】會讓人們延後購買，這會降低公司的銷售額、減少薪資，並可能慢慢削弱整體經濟。"},{"w":"recession","p":"n.","d":"a period when the economy shrinks and business slows down","c":"經濟衰退","s":"A: Do you think the company will still open the new branch office in Kaohsiung next spring as the director promised at the annual meeting? B: Probably not, because many of our clients have cut their spending during the recession, so management wants to wait until sales recover before taking such a big risk.","t":"A：你覺得公司明年春天還會像董事在年會上承諾的那樣，在高雄開設新的分公司嗎？ B：大概不會，因為在【經濟衰退】期間我們許多客戶都削減了開支，所以管理階層想等到銷售回升後再冒這麼大的風險。"},{"w":"boom","p":"n.","d":"a period of fast economic growth","c":"繁榮；景氣大好","s":"A: Why is it suddenly so hard to find an apartment near the science park, and why have the rents gone up so quickly this year? B: The local technology boom has brought thousands of new engineers to the area, so landlords know they can easily find tenants even at higher prices.","t":"A：為什麼突然很難在科學園區附近找到公寓，而且今年租金漲得這麼快？ B：當地的科技業【繁榮】為這個地區帶來了數千名新工程師，所以房東知道即使價格較高也很容易找到房客。"},{"w":"GDP","p":"n.","d":"gross domestic product; the total value of goods and services a country produces in a year","c":"國內生產毛額","s":"A: Why is everyone in the finance department talking about the new government report that came out this morning before the market opened? B: It shows that the country's GDP grew by almost four percent last year, which means consumers are spending more and our sales targets for next year may be raised.","t":"A：為什麼財務部的每個人都在討論今天早上開盤前公布的新政府報告？ B：報告顯示，國家的【國內生產毛額】去年成長了將近百分之四，這表示消費者花費更多，我們明年的銷售目標可能會被調高。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"an area or group of people where a product is bought and sold","c":"市場","s":"A: Why did the marketing team decide to translate all of our product brochures and website pages into Japanese and Korean this quarter? B: The board wants to enter the Asian market next year, and our research shows there is strong demand for affordable smart home devices in those countries.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊決定這一季把我們所有的產品手冊和網頁都翻譯成日文和韓文？ B：董事會想在明年進入亞洲【市場】，而我們的研究顯示這些國家對平價智慧家庭裝置有強烈的需求。"},{"w":"trade","p":"n.","d":"the buying and selling of goods between countries","c":"貿易","s":"A: Why are the shipping costs for our imported coffee beans so much higher than they were at the beginning of the year? B: New rules on trade between the two countries have added extra taxes and paperwork, so our supplier now needs more time and money to send every container to Taiwan.","t":"A：為什麼我們進口咖啡豆的運費比年初高出這麼多？ B：兩國之間新的【貿易】規定增加了額外的稅和文件作業，所以我們的供應商現在需要更多時間和金錢才能把每個貨櫃運到台灣。"},{"w":"export","p":"v.","d":"to sell and send goods to another country","c":"出口","s":"A: How is the small tea farm in Nantou able to grow so quickly when most farms in the area are struggling to survive? B: The owner started to export high-quality oolong tea to Japan and Canada three years ago, and those overseas buyers pay much better prices than local shops do.","t":"A：南投那座小茶園為什麼能成長得這麼快，而該地區大多數農場都在努力求生存？ B：老闆三年前開始把高品質的烏龍茶【出口】到日本和加拿大，而那些海外買家付的價格比當地商店好得多。"},{"w":"import","p":"v.","d":"to buy and bring in goods from another country","c":"進口","s":"A: Why does the new restaurant downtown charge so much more for steak than the other places on the same street? B: The chef insists that they import all their beef directly from Australia, and the shipping, storage, and customs fees make every dish quite costly, although customers say the quality is excellent.","t":"A：為什麼市中心那家新餐廳的牛排比同一條街上其他餐廳貴這麼多？ B：主廚堅持所有牛肉都直接從澳洲【進口】，而運費、倉儲費和關稅讓每道菜都相當昂貴，不過顧客說品質非常好。"},{"w":"investment","p":"n.","d":"money put into something in order to earn more later","c":"投資","s":"A: Why did the factory manager buy those expensive robots when the old machines were still working well enough for the production line? B: He sees it as a long-term investment, because the robots work faster, make fewer mistakes, and should save the company a lot of money within about five years.","t":"A：為什麼舊機器還能應付生產線，工廠經理卻買了那些昂貴的機器人？ B：他把這視為一項長期【投資】，因為機器人工作更快、錯誤更少，大約五年內應該能替公司省下很多錢。"},{"w":"capital","p":"n.","d":"money used to start or grow a business","c":"資本；資金","s":"A: Your bakery has been so popular since it opened, so why haven't you opened a second shop in the busy train station yet? B: I don't have enough capital right now, because renting a space there and buying new ovens would cost about three million dollars, so I'm still talking with the bank about a loan.","t":"A：你的麵包店開幕以來一直很受歡迎，為什麼還沒在熱鬧的火車站開第二家店呢？ B：我現在沒有足夠的【資金】，因為在那裡租店面和購買新烤箱大約要花三百萬元，所以我還在和銀行商量貸款的事。"},{"w":"revenue","p":"n.","d":"the money a company receives from selling goods or services","c":"營收；收入","s":"A: Why does the sales director look so pleased this morning after the quarterly meeting with the board of directors? B: Our online store's revenue rose by thirty percent compared with last year, mainly because the new mobile app made shopping easier, and the board has agreed to give the team a bonus.","t":"A：為什麼業務總監今天早上和董事會開完季度會議後看起來那麼高興？ B：我們網路商店的【營收】比去年成長了百分之三十，主要是因為新的手機應用程式讓購物更方便，而董事會也同意發獎金給團隊。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"money earned after all costs are paid","c":"利潤","s":"A: The shop sold thousands of umbrellas during the rainy season, so why is the owner still complaining about money? B: Rent, staff wages, and shipping costs went up so much that he made only a small profit on each umbrella, even though sales were the best they have ever been.","t":"A：這家店在雨季賣出了數千把雨傘，為什麼老闆還在抱怨錢的問題？ B：房租、員工薪資和運費漲了很多，所以即使銷售量是有史以來最好的，他每把雨傘也只賺到一點點【利潤】。"},{"w":"loss","p":"n.","d":"money lost when costs are higher than income","c":"虧損","s":"A: Why did the company suddenly decide to close three of its convenience stores in the suburbs last month? B: Those stores had been running at a loss for over two years, because fewer people shopped there after the new supermarket opened, and the rent kept going up every year.","t":"A：為什麼公司上個月突然決定關閉郊區的三家便利商店？ B：那些店已經【虧損】經營超過兩年了，因為新超市開幕後去那裡購物的人變少，而房租每年還一直上漲。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"a plan of how much money can be spent","c":"預算","s":"A: Can we hire a famous singer to perform at the company's year-end party, since everyone worked so hard this year? B: I'm afraid not, because the budget for the party is only two hundred thousand dollars, and most of that money is already being used for the food, the hotel ballroom, and the prizes.","t":"A：既然今年大家都這麼努力，我們可以請一位知名歌手在公司尾牙表演嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為尾牙的【預算】只有二十萬元，而且大部分的錢已經用在餐點、飯店宴會廳和獎品上了。"},{"w":"tax","p":"n.","d":"money that people and companies must pay to the government","c":"稅；稅金","s":"A: Why are so many people waiting in line at the accounting office this week, and why does everyone look so stressed? B: The deadline for paying income tax is this Friday, so many small business owners have come to get help filling out the forms before they have to pay a fine.","t":"A：為什麼這週有這麼多人在會計事務所排隊，而且大家看起來都壓力很大？ B：繳納所得【稅】的截止日期是這個星期五，所以很多小企業老闆都來請人幫忙填表，以免被罰款。"},{"w":"subsidy","p":"n.","d":"money the government gives to help a group or lower costs","c":"補助金；補貼","s":"A: How did the small farm near the river afford to install so many solar panels on the roofs of its storage buildings? B: The government offered a subsidy that covered half of the cost, because officials want more farms to produce clean energy and reduce their electricity bills.","t":"A：河邊那座小農場怎麼負擔得起在倉庫屋頂上安裝這麼多太陽能板？ B：政府提供了一筆【補助金】，負擔了一半的費用，因為官員希望更多農場生產乾淨能源並降低電費。"},{"w":"unemployment","p":"n.","d":"the state of not having a job; the number of people without jobs","c":"失業","s":"A: Why is the city government holding so many free job fairs and computer training classes at the community center this year? B: Local unemployment rose sharply after two large factories closed, so officials want to help those workers learn new skills and find positions in other companies quickly.","t":"A：為什麼市政府今年在社區中心舉辦這麼多免費的就業博覽會和電腦訓練課程？ B：兩家大工廠關閉後，當地的【失業】人數急劇上升，所以官員想幫助那些工人學習新技能，並盡快在其他公司找到職位。"},{"w":"employment","p":"n.","d":"paid work; jobs for people","c":"就業；僱用","s":"A: Why is the mayor so excited about the new electric car factory that will be built just outside the city next year? B: The factory will create employment for nearly two thousand local people, which means many young graduates won't have to move to Taipei to find good jobs.","t":"A：為什麼市長對明年將在市郊興建的新電動車工廠這麼興奮？ B：這座工廠將為近兩千名當地居民創造【就業】機會，這表示許多年輕畢業生不必搬到台北找好工作。"},{"w":"productivity","p":"n.","d":"how much work is done in a certain amount of time","c":"生產力","s":"A: Why did the office manager give everyone two new computer screens and replace the old chairs in the design department? B: She noticed that the team's productivity was dropping because staff wasted time switching between windows and felt tired from sitting badly, so she hoped the changes would help them work faster.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理給每個人兩台新螢幕，還更換了設計部門的舊椅子？ B：她注意到團隊的【生產力】在下降，因為員工浪費時間切換視窗，又因坐姿不良而感到疲累，所以她希望這些改變能幫助他們工作得更快。"},{"w":"consumption","p":"n.","d":"the amount of goods or energy that people use","c":"消費；消耗量","s":"A: Why has the building manager asked every department to turn off the lights and computers before leaving the office each evening? B: Our electricity consumption rose by twenty percent last summer, and the company wants to lower its bills and show customers that it cares about protecting the environment.","t":"A：為什麼大樓經理要求每個部門每天傍晚離開辦公室前都要關燈和關電腦？ B：我們的用電【消耗量】去年夏天增加了百分之二十，公司想降低電費，並向客戶表明我們重視環境保護。"},{"w":"supply","p":"n.","d":"an amount of something that is available to use or sell","c":"供給；供應","s":"A: Why can't we get the new laptops for the sales team until the end of next month, even though we ordered them weeks ago? B: The manufacturer has a limited supply of computer chips because of problems at a factory overseas, so all orders are being delayed until production returns to normal.","t":"A：為什麼我們幾週前就訂了業務團隊的新筆電，卻要到下個月底才能拿到？ B：因為海外一家工廠出了問題，製造商的電腦晶片【供應】有限，所以所有訂單都被延後，直到生產恢復正常為止。"},{"w":"demand","p":"n.","d":"the need or wish of customers to buy something","c":"需求","s":"A: Why is the factory asking workers to stay late and work on Saturdays for the next two months? B: There is huge demand for our electric fans because of the record heat wave this summer, and the stores keep calling us to send more boxes as soon as possible.","t":"A：為什麼工廠要求工人在接下來兩個月加班並在星期六上班？ B：因為今年夏天創紀錄的熱浪，我們的電風扇【需求】非常大，商店一直打電話要我們盡快送更多貨過去。"},{"w":"finance","p":"n.","d":"the management of money, especially by a company or government","c":"財務；金融","s":"A: Who should I talk to about getting paid back for the hotel and taxi costs from my business trip to Singapore last week? B: You need to send your receipts to the finance department on the third floor, and they usually transfer the money to your bank account within ten working days.","t":"A：上週我去新加坡出差的飯店和計程車費用，應該找誰申請報銷？ B：你需要把收據交給三樓的【財務】部門，他們通常會在十個工作天內把錢轉入你的銀行帳戶。"},{"w":"bankruptcy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being unable to pay your debts","c":"破產","s":"A: Why did the popular furniture store on Main Street suddenly close its doors and stop answering phone calls from customers? B: The owner declared bankruptcy last week because the business owed the bank millions of dollars and could no longer pay its suppliers or employees.","t":"A：為什麼大街上那家受歡迎的家具店突然關門，也不再接聽顧客的電話？ B：老闆上週宣告【破產】，因為公司欠銀行數百萬元，再也付不出供應商和員工的錢了。"},{"w":"interest","p":"n.","d":"extra money paid for borrowing money","c":"利息","s":"A: Why did you decide to pay off your car loan early instead of keeping that money in your savings account for emergencies? B: The bank was charging me a high rate of interest on the loan every month, so paying it all back now will save me a lot of money over the next three years.","t":"A：你為什麼決定提早還清車貸，而不是把那筆錢留在儲蓄帳戶裡應急？ B：銀行每個月對這筆貸款收取很高的【利息】，所以現在全部還清能在接下來三年替我省下很多錢。"},{"w":"debt","p":"n.","d":"money that is owed to someone","c":"債務","s":"A: Why has the new manager cancelled all the business trips and stopped buying new office furniture this year? B: The company is trying to reduce its debt, because it borrowed a lot from the bank to build the new warehouse, and the monthly payments are now very heavy.","t":"A：為什麼新經理今年取消了所有出差，也不再購買新的辦公家具？ B：公司正在努力減少【債務】，因為為了建造新倉庫向銀行借了很多錢，現在每月的還款負擔非常沉重。"},{"w":"currency","p":"n.","d":"the money used in a country","c":"貨幣","s":"A: Should I change my Taiwan dollars at the airport before my business trip to Tokyo, or wait until I arrive in Japan? B: It's usually better to buy the local currency at your own bank before you leave, because the airport counters often give a worse rate and charge an extra service fee.","t":"A：我去東京出差前應該在機場換台幣，還是等到了日本再換？ B：通常最好出發前在你自己的銀行購買當地【貨幣】，因為機場櫃檯的匯率往往比較差，還會多收手續費。"},{"w":"exchange","p":"n.","d":"the act of changing one country's money into another's","c":"兌換；匯兌","s":"A: Why did our Japanese supplier suddenly raise the price of the machine parts we have been buying from them for years? B: The exchange rate between the yen and the US dollar changed a lot this spring, so their costs went up and they had to adjust the prices in our new contract.","t":"A：為什麼我們的日本供應商突然調漲了我們多年來一直向他們購買的機械零件價格？ B：今年春天日圓和美元之間的【匯兌】比率變動很大，所以他們的成本上升，只好在新合約中調整價格。"},{"w":"industry","p":"n.","d":"a type of business or trade","c":"產業；工業","s":"A: Why did you leave your job at the bank to work for a small company that makes video games for mobile phones? B: I believe the gaming industry will keep growing quickly over the next ten years, and I wanted to build my career in a creative field with many chances for promotion.","t":"A：你為什麼辭去銀行的工作，去一家製作手機遊戲的小公司上班？ B：我相信遊戲【產業】在未來十年會持續快速成長，而我想在一個充滿升遷機會的創意領域發展事業。"},{"w":"manufacturing","p":"n.","d":"the business of making goods in factories","c":"製造業；製造","s":"A: Why did the company move most of its production from Taoyuan to a new plant in Vietnam last year? B: Costs for manufacturing are much lower there, because land and labor are cheaper, so the company can make shoes at a lower price and stay competitive with other brands.","t":"A：為什麼公司去年把大部分生產從桃園移到越南的新工廠？ B：那裡的【製造】成本低得多，因為土地和勞工比較便宜，所以公司能以較低的價格生產鞋子，並和其他品牌保持競爭力。"},{"w":"service","p":"n.","d":"work done to help customers rather than goods made","c":"服務","s":"A: Why do so many guests leave five-star reviews for that small hotel near the train station, even though the rooms are quite old? B: The staff provide excellent customer service, such as carrying bags, recommending local restaurants, and arranging taxis at any time, so visitors feel very welcome during their stay.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多房客給火車站附近那家小飯店五星評價，即使房間相當老舊？ B：員工提供極佳的顧客【服務】，例如幫忙提行李、推薦當地餐廳，以及隨時安排計程車，讓旅客在住宿期間感到非常受歡迎。"},{"w":"enterprise","p":"n.","d":"a business or company","c":"企業","s":"A: Why does the government offer free business classes and cheap loans to young people who want to start their own companies? B: Officials believe every new small enterprise can create jobs for local people, so they want to help more young owners open shops, cafés, and online businesses across the country.","t":"A：為什麼政府要提供免費的商業課程和低利貸款給想自己創業的年輕人？ B：官員相信每一家新的小型【企業】都能為當地居民創造工作機會，所以他們想幫助更多年輕老闆在全國各地開設商店、咖啡館和網路商店。"},{"w":"entrepreneur","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts and runs a business","c":"企業家；創業家","s":"A: Who is the woman giving the speech at the business conference this afternoon, and why is everyone so excited to hear her? B: She is a young entrepreneur who started an online clothing company in her apartment five years ago, and now her business has more than two hundred employees around Asia.","t":"A：今天下午在商業研討會上演講的女士是誰？為什麼大家都那麼期待聽她演講？ B：她是一位年輕的【創業家】，五年前在自己的公寓裡創立了一家網路服飾公司，現在她的事業在亞洲有超過兩百名員工。"},{"w":"globalization","p":"n.","d":"the process by which businesses and economies around the world become connected","c":"全球化","s":"A: Why can we buy fresh fruit from Chile, phones from Korea, and clothes from Vietnam in the same shopping mall in Taipei? B: Because of globalization, companies now sell their products all over the world, and faster shipping and the internet make it easy for goods to travel between countries.","t":"A：為什麼我們能在台北的同一間購物中心買到智利的新鮮水果、韓國的手機和越南的衣服？ B：由於【全球化】，現在公司把產品銷售到世界各地，而更快速的運輸和網路讓商品很容易在國家之間流通。"}]},{"unit":117,"theme":"Education 教育","cards":[{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an official record showing you finished training or passed an exam","c":"資格；學歷證明","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager reject so many applicants for the front desk job last week, even though they seemed friendly and polite? B: Most of them did not have a qualification in hospitality, and the company now requires an official certificate before it lets new staff deal with guests.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理上週拒絕了這麼多應徵櫃檯工作的人，即使他們看起來友善又有禮貌？ B：他們大多數沒有餐旅業的【資格證明】，而公司現在規定新員工在接待客人之前必須有正式證書。"},{"w":"enroll","p":"v.","d":"to officially join a course or school","c":"註冊；登記入學","s":"A: Are you still planning to take that evening business course at the community college, or is your schedule at the office too busy this year? B: I am going to enroll in the spring program next week, because my manager agreed to pay half the fee and let me leave early on Thursdays.","t":"A：你還打算去社區大學上那門晚間商業課程嗎？還是你今年辦公室的行程太忙了？ B：我下週要【報名註冊】春季課程，因為我的經理同意支付一半的費用，並讓我每週四提早下班。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control yourself and follow rules","c":"紀律；自制力","s":"A: How did your daughter manage to study for the bank's entrance exam while working full-time at the café downtown? B: She showed great discipline by waking up at five every morning, reviewing her notes for two hours, and turning off her phone so nothing could distract her.","t":"A：你女兒在市中心咖啡館全職工作的同時，是怎麼準備銀行入行考試的？ B：她展現了極大的【自律】，每天早上五點起床，複習筆記兩個小時，並且關掉手機，讓任何事都無法使她分心。"},{"w":"distance learning","p":"n.phr.","d":"studying from home through the internet instead of going to a school","c":"遠距學習","s":"A: How can our sales staff in the southern branch get the new marketing training if they cannot travel to the head office this month? B: The training department has set up a distance learning program, so they can watch the lessons online, join live chats, and submit their tasks from their own desks.","t":"A：如果南部分公司的業務人員這個月無法到總公司，他們要如何接受新的行銷培訓？ B：培訓部門已經設立了一個【遠距學習】課程，所以他們可以在線上觀看課程、參加即時討論，並在自己的座位上繳交作業。"},{"w":"boarding school","p":"n.phr.","d":"a school where students live during the term","c":"寄宿學校","s":"A: Since you and your husband will both be working overseas for the next three years, where will your son continue his studies? B: We have found an excellent boarding school in the countryside, where he can live in the dormitory, eat with his classmates, and come home to his grandparents during the holidays.","t":"A：既然你和你先生接下來三年都要在海外工作，你兒子要在哪裡繼續學業？ B：我們在鄉間找到一所很棒的【寄宿學校】，他可以住在宿舍、和同學一起吃飯，假期時則回祖父母家。"},{"w":"bachelor's degree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a first university degree, usually after four years of study","c":"學士學位","s":"A: What are the basic requirements for the junior accountant position that the finance department posted on its website yesterday? B: Applicants need a bachelor's degree in accounting or business, at least one year of office experience, and good computer skills, because they will prepare monthly reports for the managers.","t":"A：財務部昨天在網站上公布的初級會計職位，基本條件是什麼？ B：應徵者需要具備會計或商業的【學士學位】、至少一年的辦公室經驗以及良好的電腦能力，因為他們要替經理們準備每月報告。"},{"w":"master's degree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a higher university degree taken after a first degree","c":"碩士學位","s":"A: Why has Linda been leaving the office so early every Tuesday and Thursday since the beginning of September? B: She is studying for a master's degree in project management at night, and the company agreed to change her hours because the new skills will help her lead bigger projects next year.","t":"A：為什麼從九月初開始，琳達每週二和週四都那麼早離開辦公室？ B：她晚上在攻讀專案管理的【碩士學位】，公司同意調整她的上班時間，因為這些新技能將幫助她明年帶領更大的專案。"},{"w":"higher education","p":"n.phr.","d":"study at a college or university after high school","c":"高等教育","s":"A: Why is the bank offering such low interest rates on student loans to young customers this autumn? B: The government wants more people to continue into higher education after high school, so it is giving banks money to help families pay for university fees and living costs.","t":"A：為什麼銀行今年秋天對年輕客戶提供這麼低利率的學生貸款？ B：政府希望更多人在高中畢業後繼續接受【高等教育】，所以提供資金給銀行，幫助家庭支付大學學費和生活費。"},{"w":"intensive course","p":"n.phr.","d":"a course that teaches a lot in a short time","c":"密集課程","s":"A: How did the new sales assistant learn to speak Japanese so well before the trade fair in Osaka last month? B: She took a two-week intensive course at a language school, studying six hours every day, so she could talk with customers and explain our products clearly at the booth.","t":"A：新來的業務助理是怎麼在上個月大阪商展之前把日語學得這麼好的？ B：她在語言學校上了為期兩週的【密集課程】，每天學習六個小時，所以她能在攤位上和客戶交談並清楚說明我們的產品。"},{"w":"internship","p":"n.","d":"a short period of work to gain experience, often for students","c":"實習","s":"A: Do you know why that university student has been sitting at the empty desk next to the printer since Monday morning? B: He is doing a three-month internship with our design team, so he will help with simple projects, attend meetings, and learn how a real office works before he graduates.","t":"A：你知道為什麼那位大學生從週一早上就坐在印表機旁邊的空位上嗎？ B：他正在我們設計團隊進行為期三個月的【實習】，所以他會協助簡單的專案、參加會議，並在畢業前了解真實的辦公室如何運作。"},{"w":"humanity","p":"n.","d":"a subject about people and culture, such as history or literature","c":"人文學科","s":"A: Why did the publishing company hire someone who studied philosophy instead of business for the new editor position? B: The manager believes that a graduate in a humanity like history or literature reads carefully, writes well, and understands people, which are exactly the skills an editor needs every day.","t":"A：為什麼出版公司在新的編輯職位上僱用了一位念哲學而不是商業的人？ B：經理認為，主修歷史或文學等【人文學科】的畢業生閱讀仔細、文筆好又了解人，而這些正是編輯每天需要的技能。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"v.","d":"to organize and carry out something","c":"進行；實施","s":"A: Why are so many students walking around the shopping mall with clipboards and asking customers questions this afternoon? B: They are university business students who need to conduct a survey about shopping habits, and the results will be used in their final report for the marketing class.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午有這麼多學生拿著寫字板在購物中心裡走動並向顧客提問？ B：他們是大學商學系的學生，需要【進行】一項關於購物習慣的調查，結果將用在他們行銷課的期末報告中。"},{"w":"acquire","p":"v.","d":"to get or learn something, such as a skill","c":"獲得；習得","s":"A: Why does the company send every new engineer to work in the factory for six months before they join the design office? B: Management wants them to acquire practical skills by watching the machines and talking to workers, so their later designs will be easier and cheaper to produce.","t":"A：為什麼公司在每位新工程師進入設計部門之前，都先派他們到工廠工作六個月？ B：管理階層希望他們透過觀察機器和與工人交談來【獲得】實務技能，這樣他們日後的設計會更容易生產，成本也更低。"},{"w":"compulsory","p":"adj.","d":"required by a rule; you must do it","c":"強制的；必修的","s":"A: Do all of the new employees really have to join the safety workshop on Friday, even the ones who work only in the office? B: Yes, it is compulsory for every staff member this year, because the government changed the fire rules and the company could be fined if anyone misses it.","t":"A：所有新員工真的都必須參加週五的安全研習嗎？連只在辦公室工作的人也一樣？ B：是的，今年這對每位員工都是【強制的】，因為政府修改了消防規定，如果有人缺席，公司可能會被罰款。"},{"w":"semester","p":"n.","d":"one of the two main parts of a school year","c":"學期","s":"A: When will the university students from the business program start working part-time at our customer service center? B: They will join us at the beginning of the next semester in February, because their classes are lighter then and they can work three afternoons a week without hurting their grades.","t":"A：商學系的大學生什麼時候會開始在我們的客服中心兼職工作？ B：他們會在二月下個【學期】開始時加入我們，因為那時他們的課比較少，每週可以工作三個下午而不會影響成績。"},{"w":"major","p":"n.","d":"the main subject a student studies at university","c":"主修科目","s":"A: What did the new marketing assistant study at university, and does she have any experience with social media campaigns? B: Her major was communications, and during her studies she ran the online pages for a local bakery, so she already knows how to attract customers and write short posts.","t":"A：新的行銷助理在大學念什麼？她有任何社群媒體行銷活動的經驗嗎？ B：她的【主修】是傳播，求學期間她還幫一家當地麵包店經營網路粉絲頁，所以她已經知道如何吸引顧客和撰寫簡短貼文。"},{"w":"faculty","p":"n.","d":"all the teachers in a school or university department","c":"全體教職員；學院","s":"A: Who will be giving the talks at the business conference that the university is hosting in the main hall next weekend? B: Several members of the faculty will speak about their research, and two local company owners will also share how they work with students on real projects.","t":"A：大學下週末在大禮堂舉辦的商業研討會將由誰來演講？ B：幾位【教職員】會談他們的研究，另外兩位當地企業主也會分享他們如何與學生合作進行實際專案。"},{"w":"intriguing","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting because it is unusual","c":"引人入勝的；有趣的","s":"A: Why did so many employees stay after work yesterday to listen to the guest speaker in the training room? B: She gave an intriguing talk about how small shops use online games to teach customers about their products, and everyone wanted to ask questions when it was finished.","t":"A：為什麼昨天有這麼多員工下班後留在訓練室聽客座講者演講？ B：她做了一場【引人入勝的】演講，內容是小商店如何利用線上遊戲讓顧客認識產品，結束時大家都想發問。"},{"w":"intrinsic","p":"adj.","d":"coming naturally from inside a person or thing","c":"內在的；固有的","s":"A: Why does Professor Chen not give students extra points for finishing optional reading at home each week? B: She believes that real learning comes from intrinsic motivation, so she wants students to read because they enjoy it and want to grow, not because they are hoping for a reward.","t":"A：為什麼陳教授不給每週在家完成選讀的學生加分？ B：她相信真正的學習來自【內在的】動機，所以她希望學生閱讀是因為喜歡並想成長，而不是因為期待獎勵。"},{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"all the subjects taught in a school or course","c":"課程（全部科目）","s":"A: Why are the teachers at the training center staying late every evening this month instead of going home on time? B: They are updating the curriculum for next year, adding new classes on digital marketing and data skills because local companies keep asking for employees with these abilities.","t":"A：為什麼訓練中心的老師們這個月每天晚上都留到很晚，而不是準時回家？ B：他們正在更新明年的【課程】，增加數位行銷和資料技能的新課，因為當地企業一直在找具備這些能力的員工。"},{"w":"syllabus","p":"n.","d":"a list of the topics a course will cover","c":"課程大綱","s":"A: How can I find out which chapters will be on the accounting exam before I register for the evening class next month? B: You can download the syllabus from the college website, because it lists every topic, the reading for each week, and the dates of all the quizzes and tests.","t":"A：在我下個月報名夜間課程之前，要怎麼知道會計考試會考哪些章節？ B：你可以從學院網站下載【課程大綱】，因為上面列出了每個主題、每週的閱讀內容，以及所有小考和考試的日期。"},{"w":"multinational","p":"adj.","d":"having offices or business in many countries","c":"跨國的","s":"A: Why are so many graduates from the business school applying for jobs at that large electronics company this spring? B: It is a multinational company with offices in more than thirty countries, so new employees have the chance to travel, work with people from different cultures, and get promoted quickly.","t":"A：為什麼今年春天有這麼多商學院畢業生應徵那家大型電子公司的工作？ B：那是一家在三十多個國家設有辦公室的【跨國】公司，所以新進員工有機會出差、與不同文化的人合作，並且很快就能升遷。"},{"w":"dropout","p":"n.","d":"a person who leaves school before finishing","c":"輟學生","s":"A: Is it true that the owner of that famous coffee chain never finished his studies at the university in Taipei? B: Yes, he was a college dropout who left after one year to open a small coffee stand, and now he gives talks to students about taking risks and working hard.","t":"A：那家知名咖啡連鎖店的老闆真的沒有完成在台北的大學學業嗎？ B：是的，他是大學【輟學生】，念了一年就離開去開一個小咖啡攤，現在他會向學生演講，談冒險和努力工作。"},{"w":"coursework","p":"n.","d":"work students do during a course that counts toward the final grade","c":"課業；課程作業","s":"A: How is your part-time MBA program going now that you are also managing the new team at the office? B: It is difficult because the coursework includes weekly reports and group projects, so I spend most of my weekends at the library to make sure everything is finished on time.","t":"A：既然你在辦公室還要管理新團隊，你的在職企管碩士課程進行得如何？ B：很辛苦，因為【課程作業】包含每週報告和小組專題，所以我週末大多待在圖書館，確保所有東西都能準時完成。"},{"w":"bookworm","p":"n.","d":"a person who loves reading very much","c":"書蟲；愛讀書的人","s":"A: Who do you think should help choose the new books for the reading corner in our staff lounge this year? B: Ask Mary in accounting, because she is a real bookworm who reads two or three novels every week on the train and always recommends great titles to her coworkers.","t":"A：你覺得今年該由誰來幫忙挑選員工休息室閱讀角落的新書？ B：去問會計部的瑪莉，她是個十足的【書蟲】，每週在火車上讀兩三本小說，而且總是推薦很棒的書給同事。"},{"w":"eager beaver","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is very keen and works very hard","c":"做事非常積極的人","s":"A: Why is the new intern already in the office at seven every morning when work does not start until nine? B: He is a real eager beaver who wants to impress the manager, so he arrives early to prepare the meeting rooms, check the reports, and ask what extra tasks he can do.","t":"A：為什麼新來的實習生每天早上七點就到辦公室，而上班時間是九點？ B：他是個非常【積極賣力的人】，想讓經理留下好印象，所以他提早到來準備會議室、檢查報告，並詢問還能做哪些額外的工作。"},{"w":"face-to-face classes","p":"n.phr.","d":"lessons where students and teachers are in the same room","c":"面對面授課；實體課程","s":"A: Will the language school continue to teach all of its business English lessons online after the holidays are over? B: No, it will offer face-to-face classes again in January, because many students said they learn better when they can practice speaking with the teacher and classmates in the same room.","t":"A：假期結束後，語言學校會繼續在線上教所有的商用英語課程嗎？ B：不會，一月起它會再次提供【實體面對面課程】，因為很多學生說，能在同一個教室和老師及同學練習口說，他們學得比較好。"},{"w":"hit the books","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start studying hard","c":"用功讀書","s":"A: Are you coming to the team dinner at the new Italian restaurant on Friday night after the sales meeting? B: I am sorry, but I really need to hit the books this weekend, because my accounting certificate exam is on Monday morning and I have not finished reviewing the last three chapters.","t":"A：你週五晚上業務會議結束後，要來新的義大利餐廳參加團隊聚餐嗎？ B：很抱歉，我這個週末真的得【用功讀書】，因為我的會計證照考試在週一早上，而最後三章我還沒複習完。"},{"w":"schoolboy error","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very simple, silly mistake","c":"低級錯誤","s":"A: Why did the client send back our price list this morning and ask us to check all the numbers again? B: Someone made a schoolboy error and typed the prices in the wrong currency, so the totals looked far too high, and the manager was quite embarrassed when she found out.","t":"A：為什麼客戶今天早上把我們的價目表退回，並要求我們重新檢查所有數字？ B：有人犯了【低級錯誤】，把價格打成錯的幣別，所以總額看起來高得離譜，經理發現時相當尷尬。"},{"w":"teacher's pet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a student whom the teacher likes best","c":"老師的寵兒","s":"A: Why do the other trainees seem a little annoyed with Tom during the computer training sessions this week? B: They think he is the teacher's pet because the instructor always asks him to help and praises his work, even though everyone else is also working hard and finishing their tasks.","t":"A：為什麼這週電腦訓練課時，其他受訓學員似乎對湯姆有點不滿？ B：他們認為他是【老師的寵兒】，因為講師總是請他幫忙並稱讚他的作品，即使其他人也同樣努力並完成了任務。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event, class, or meeting","c":"參加；出席","s":"A: Can you cover my shift at the front desk on Wednesday afternoon, since I will be out of the office for a few hours? B: Sure, I know you need to attend the customer service workshop at the head office, and the manager already told me to answer your phone and greet any visitors.","t":"A：週三下午我會離開辦公室幾個小時，你可以幫我代櫃檯的班嗎？ B：當然，我知道你要去總公司【參加】客服研習，經理已經告訴我要幫你接電話並接待訪客。"},{"w":"goof around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to waste time doing silly things","c":"胡鬧；鬼混","s":"A: Why did the supervisor move the two new warehouse workers to different shifts after only one week? B: She saw them goof around with the boxes and the delivery cart instead of packing orders, and she was worried that someone could get hurt or that customers would get their packages late.","t":"A：為什麼主管才過一週就把兩名新的倉庫員工調到不同班別？ B：她看到他們拿著箱子和送貨推車【胡鬧】，而不是在包裝訂單，她擔心有人會受傷，或是顧客會晚收到包裹。"},{"w":"meet a deadline","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish work by the required time","c":"趕上截止期限","s":"A: Why is the design team ordering pizza and staying at the office so late tonight instead of going home? B: They have to meet a deadline for the new advertising campaign, because the client wants the final posters by eight o'clock tomorrow morning and there are still several changes to make.","t":"A：為什麼設計團隊今晚叫披薩並留在辦公室到這麼晚，而不是回家？ B：他們必須【趕上截止期限】完成新的廣告活動，因為客戶要在明天早上八點前拿到最終海報，而且還有好幾處要修改。"},{"w":"pass with flying colours","p":"v.phr.","d":"to pass an exam or test very successfully","c":"以優異成績通過","s":"A: Are you worried about the new staff member who is taking the professional banking exam this Saturday morning? B: Not at all, she has studied every evening for three months and got top scores on all the practice tests, so I am sure she will pass with flying colours and get her certificate.","t":"A：你擔心這週六早上要參加銀行專業考試的新同事嗎？ B：一點也不，她三個月來每晚都在讀書，所有模擬考都拿最高分，所以我確信她會【以優異成績通過】並拿到證照。"},{"w":"play truant","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay away from school without permission","c":"逃學；曠課","s":"A: Why did the school call Mrs. Wang at the office in the middle of the afternoon meeting yesterday? B: Her son decided to play truant and spent the whole day at a game center downtown, so the teacher wanted her to know he had missed three important classes.","t":"A：為什麼學校昨天在下午會議中途打電話到辦公室找王太太？ B：她兒子決定【逃學】，整天待在市中心的電玩中心，所以老師想讓她知道他缺了三堂重要的課。"},{"w":"tuition","p":"n.","d":"money paid for teaching at a school or college","c":"學費","s":"A: Does our company offer any help for employees who want to study part-time for a business degree at a local university? B: Yes, the company will pay half of your tuition if your manager approves the course and you finish each class with at least a B grade.","t":"A：公司對想在當地大學兼讀商學學位的員工有提供任何協助嗎？ B：有，如果你的主管核准該課程，而且每門課至少拿到B，公司會支付你一半的【學費】。"}]},{"unit":118,"theme":"Employment 就業","cards":[{"w":"job","p":"n.","d":"work that you do regularly to earn money","c":"工作；職業","s":"A: Why does your brother look so happy this morning, and why did he bring a box of cakes to the office for everyone? B: He finally got a new job at a large bank downtown, so he will start next Monday and earn more money than he does here.","t":"A：你哥哥今天早上為什麼看起來這麼開心，還帶了一盒蛋糕來辦公室給大家？ B：他終於在市中心一家大銀行找到一份新【工作】，所以他下週一開始上班，而且賺的錢會比在這裡多。"},{"w":"occupation","p":"n.","d":"a person's job or type of work","c":"職業","s":"A: When I filled out the visa form at the travel agency yesterday, I wasn't sure what to write in one of the boxes. B: That box asks for your occupation, so you should simply write sales manager and then add the name of the company where you work now.","t":"A：我昨天在旅行社填簽證表格時，不確定其中一個欄位要寫什麼。 B：那一欄是問你的【職業】，所以你只要寫業務經理，然後再加上你目前任職公司的名稱就好。"},{"w":"career","p":"n.","d":"the series of jobs a person has over a long time","c":"職業生涯；事業","s":"A: Why did Linda decide to leave her well-paid position at the bank after working there for almost ten years? B: She wanted to start a new career in graphic design, so she took evening classes for two years and finally opened her own small studio last month.","t":"A：琳達為什麼在銀行工作將近十年後，決定離開那份高薪的職位？ B：她想在平面設計領域展開新的【職業生涯】，所以她上了兩年的夜間課程，終於在上個月開了自己的小工作室。"},{"w":"profession","p":"n.","d":"a job that needs special training, like doctor or lawyer","c":"專業；（需專業訓練的）職業","s":"A: Your cousin always seems so busy, and I heard she rarely has time to join the family for dinner on weekends. B: That's true, because she works as a nurse, and the medical profession often requires long hours, night duty, and a lot of patience with patients and their families.","t":"A：你表姊似乎總是很忙，我聽說她週末很少有空和家人一起吃晚餐。 B：沒錯，因為她是護理師，而醫療【專業】常常需要長時間工作、值夜班，並且對病人和家屬要很有耐心。"},{"w":"employer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays people to work","c":"雇主","s":"A: Did you hear why the factory workers were so pleased when the manager spoke to them in the cafeteria this afternoon? B: Yes, their employer announced that every worker will receive a bonus at the end of the year because the company sold far more products than it expected.","t":"A：你有聽說今天下午經理在餐廳跟工廠工人講話時，他們為什麼那麼高興嗎？ B：有，他們的【雇主】宣布每位工人年底都會拿到獎金，因為公司賣出的產品遠遠超出預期。"},{"w":"employee","p":"n.","d":"a person who is paid to work for a company or person","c":"員工；受雇者","s":"A: Who is the young man sitting at the front desk, and why is he reading the company handbook so carefully? B: He is a new employee in the accounting department, and he needs to learn our rules about holidays, sick leave, and expense reports before he starts working on real accounts.","t":"A：坐在前台的那位年輕人是誰？他為什麼這麼仔細地讀公司手冊？ B：他是會計部的新【員工】，在開始處理真正的帳目之前，他需要先了解我們關於假期、病假和費用報告的規定。"},{"w":"hire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job and pay them","c":"雇用；聘請","s":"A: The customer service team has been answering phone calls until late every night since the holiday sale began last week. B: I know, so the manager plans to hire three more assistants this month, and they will help us answer questions and handle orders until the busy season ends.","t":"A：自從上週假期特賣開始以來，客服團隊每天晚上都接電話接到很晚。 B：我知道，所以經理打算這個月再【雇用】三名助理，他們會幫我們回答問題、處理訂單，直到旺季結束。"},{"w":"recruit","p":"v.","d":"to find new people to join a company or group","c":"招募；招聘","s":"A: Why is our human resources manager traveling to so many universities around the country this spring? B: She wants to recruit talented graduates for our new research center, so she is giving short talks to students and collecting their contact details at job fairs.","t":"A：我們的人資經理今年春天為什麼要跑全國這麼多所大學？ B：她想為我們新的研發中心【招募】有才華的畢業生，所以她在就業博覽會上對學生做簡短演講，並收集他們的聯絡資料。"},{"w":"apply","p":"v.","d":"to ask formally for a job, usually in writing","c":"申請；應徵","s":"A: I saw an advertisement for a marketing assistant position at the hotel near the station, but I'm not sure I have enough experience. B: You should still apply before the end of this week, because they said they will train the right person and the pay is quite good.","t":"A：我看到車站附近那家飯店在徵行銷助理，但我不確定自己的經驗夠不夠。 B：你還是應該在這週結束前去【應徵】，因為他們說會訓練合適的人選，而且薪水相當不錯。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a formal written request for a job","c":"申請書；申請","s":"A: Have you finished all the paperwork for the designer position at that advertising agency in Taipei? B: Almost, I just need to attach a copy of my diploma to my application and send it by email before the deadline at five o'clock this afternoon.","t":"A：你應徵台北那家廣告公司設計師職位的文件都準備好了嗎？ B：差不多了，我只需要把畢業證書影本附在我的【申請書】上，然後在今天下午五點截止前用電子郵件寄出。"},{"w":"resume","p":"n.","d":"a document listing your education and work history","c":"履歷","s":"A: The hiring manager said she would contact me if she wanted to meet, but what should I send her first? B: You should send her your resume, which clearly lists your education, your previous positions, and your computer abilities, along with a short cover letter about why you want the position.","t":"A：招聘經理說如果她想見面會跟我聯絡，但我應該先寄什麼給她？ B：你應該寄給她你的【履歷】，上面清楚列出你的學歷、過去的職位和電腦能力，再附上一封簡短的求職信，說明你為什麼想要這個職位。"},{"w":"interview","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where an employer asks a job seeker questions","c":"面試","s":"A: You look very nervous this morning, and why are you wearing your best suit on a Tuesday? B: I have a job interview with a large shipping company at ten o'clock, and I want to make a good impression on the three managers who will ask me questions.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來很緊張，而且為什麼星期二就穿上你最好的西裝？ B：我十點要去一家大型航運公司求職【面試】，我想讓那三位要問我問題的經理留下好印象。"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an exam passed or a skill that makes you suitable for a job","c":"資格；學歷證書","s":"A: Do you think Ken can get the position of head accountant at the new branch office? B: I'm not sure, because the most important qualification for that role is a professional accounting certificate, and he is still studying for the final exam this year.","t":"A：你覺得肯能拿到新分公司首席會計師的職位嗎？ B：我不確定，因為那個職位最重要的【資格】是專業會計證照，而他今年還在準備最後一場考試。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"an ability to do something well because of practice","c":"技能；技巧","s":"A: Why did the manager choose Kevin to deal with the angry customers who called about the late deliveries? B: Kevin has a special skill for calming people down, so even when customers are upset, he can listen patiently and find a solution quickly.","t":"A：經理為什麼選凱文去處理那些因為延遲送貨而打電話來的生氣客戶？ B：凱文有讓人冷靜下來的特殊【技能】，所以即使客戶很不高興，他也能耐心傾聽並迅速找到解決辦法。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge you get from doing a job for some time","c":"經驗","s":"A: The new sales assistant seems to know exactly what to say when customers ask difficult questions about our products. B: That's because she has five years of experience working in a large electronics store, where she dealt with hundreds of shoppers and learned how to explain technical details simply.","t":"A：新來的銷售助理在客人問到產品的難題時，似乎總是知道該說什麼。 B：那是因為她有在大型電器行工作五年的【經驗】，在那裡她接待過數百位顧客，學會如何簡單地解釋技術細節。"},{"w":"salary","p":"n.","d":"fixed money paid to a worker every month or year","c":"薪水；薪資","s":"A: Why is Tom thinking about leaving our company when he seems to enjoy working with everyone on the team? B: Another firm offered him a higher salary, so he would earn about twenty percent more each month and could finally save enough money to buy an apartment.","t":"A：湯姆似乎很喜歡和團隊的每個人一起工作，為什麼他在考慮離開公司？ B：另一家公司給他更高的【薪水】，所以他每個月大約可以多賺兩成，終於能存夠錢買一間公寓。"},{"w":"wage","p":"n.","d":"money paid for work, usually by the hour or week","c":"工資","s":"A: Why are so many students applying to work at the new coffee shop on the corner of our street? B: The owner pays a good hourly wage, and he also lets workers choose their own hours, so students can earn money without missing their classes.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多學生去應徵我們街角那家新咖啡店的工作？ B：老闆付的時薪【工資】不錯，而且還讓員工自己選上班時段，所以學生可以賺錢又不會錯過上課。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"n.","d":"something extra a worker gets besides pay, such as insurance","c":"福利","s":"A: Besides the monthly pay, why do you think so many people want to work for that large technology company? B: Free health insurance is a major benefit, and staff members also get extra holidays, free lunches, and money to take training courses that help them improve.","t":"A：除了月薪之外，你覺得為什麼這麼多人想在那家大型科技公司上班？ B：免費健康保險是一項重要的【福利】，而且員工還有額外假期、免費午餐，以及參加進修課程的補助。"},{"w":"contract","p":"n.","d":"a legal written agreement between people or companies","c":"合約；契約","s":"A: Have you officially accepted the new position with the design firm, or are you still discussing the details? B: I'm meeting the manager tomorrow morning to sign the contract, which explains my working hours, my pay, and the length of time I agree to stay with the company.","t":"A：你正式接受那家設計公司的新職位了嗎？還是還在討論細節？ B：我明天早上要跟經理見面簽【合約】，上面說明了我的工作時數、薪資，以及我同意在公司待多久。"},{"w":"full-time","p":"adj.","d":"working the whole of a normal working week","c":"全職的","s":"A: Are you still working only three mornings a week at the bookstore, or has your schedule changed recently? B: The manager offered me a full-time position last month, so now I work from nine to six, Monday to Friday, and I also get paid holidays and insurance.","t":"A：你還是一週只在書店上三個早上的班嗎？還是你的班表最近有改變？ B：經理上個月給了我一個【全職的】職位，所以我現在週一到週五從九點上到六點，還有帶薪假和保險。"},{"w":"part-time","p":"adj.","d":"working only some hours or days of the week","c":"兼職的","s":"A: How do you manage to study at the university and still pay for your rent and living costs every month? B: I have a part-time job at a supermarket near my apartment, where I work about fifteen hours a week, mostly on weekends and some evenings.","t":"A：你是怎麼一邊在大學讀書，一邊每個月還能付房租和生活費的？ B：我在公寓附近的超市有一份【兼職的】工作，每週大約工作十五個小時，大多是週末和一些晚上。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only for a short time","c":"臨時的；暫時的","s":"A: Is the receptionist at the front desk new, because I haven't seen her before this week? B: She is only a temporary worker from an agency, and she will help us for two months while our regular receptionist is away on maternity leave.","t":"A：前台的接待員是新來的嗎？我這週之前沒見過她。 B：她只是派遣公司派來的【臨時】員工，在我們的正職接待員休產假的這兩個月幫忙。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time or without an end date","c":"長期的；永久的","s":"A: You've been working at the hotel as a trainee for six months now, so what happens after the training ends? B: If my manager is satisfied with my performance, the hotel will give me a permanent position, which means I can stay as long as I want and receive full benefits.","t":"A：你在飯店當實習生已經六個月了，那訓練結束後會怎樣？ B：如果經理滿意我的表現，飯店就會給我一個【長期的】職位，這表示我可以想待多久就待多久，而且享有完整福利。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"a move to a higher position at work","c":"升遷；晉升","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department congratulating Sarah and bringing her flowers this morning? B: She got a promotion to team leader because her advertising campaign doubled our online sales, so she will now manage six people and earn a higher salary.","t":"A：今天早上行銷部的大家為什麼都在恭喜莎拉，還送她花？ B：她【升遷】為組長了，因為她的廣告活動讓我們的網路銷售翻倍，所以她現在要管理六個人，薪水也更高。"},{"w":"transfer","p":"v.","d":"to move someone to a different place or department for work","c":"調職；調動","s":"A: Why is David packing up all the files on his desk and saying goodbye to everyone in the office? B: The company decided to transfer him to the new branch in Kaohsiung, where he will help train the local staff and manage the opening of the store next month.","t":"A：大衛為什麼在整理桌上所有的檔案，還跟辦公室的每個人道別？ B：公司決定把他【調】到高雄的新分店，他會在那裡協助訓練當地員工，並負責下個月的開幕事宜。"},{"w":"resign","p":"v.","d":"to leave your job by choice","c":"辭職","s":"A: Why did the sales director suddenly decide to leave the company after working here for fifteen years? B: He decided to resign because he wanted to spend more time with his family, so he gave the board a letter last week and will leave at the end of the month.","t":"A：業務總監在這裡工作了十五年，為什麼突然決定離開公司？ B：他決定【辭職】是因為想多陪陪家人，所以他上週向董事會遞了信，月底就會離開。"},{"w":"retire","p":"v.","d":"to stop working because you have reached a certain age","c":"退休","s":"A: Our factory supervisor has worked here for nearly forty years, so when is he planning to stop working? B: He will retire next spring when he turns sixty-five, and after that he wants to travel around Europe with his wife and spend more time in his garden.","t":"A：我們的工廠主管已經在這裡工作快四十年了，他打算什麼時候不做了？ B：他明年春天滿六十五歲時就會【退休】，之後他想和太太去歐洲旅行，並多花點時間在花園裡。"},{"w":"dismiss","p":"v.","d":"to officially remove someone from their job","c":"解僱；開除","s":"A: Why isn't the new cashier working at the supermarket anymore, when she only started two months ago? B: The manager had to dismiss her because she was often late, and she also made several serious mistakes with the money in the cash register.","t":"A：那位新收銀員才來兩個月，為什麼已經不在超市工作了？ B：經理不得不【解僱】她，因為她常常遲到，而且收銀機裡的錢她也出了好幾次嚴重的錯。"},{"w":"layoff","p":"n.","d":"the act of ending workers' jobs because there is not enough work","c":"裁員；資遣","s":"A: Why does everyone at the car factory look so worried, and why are there so many meetings this week? B: Sales have fallen sharply, so the company announced a layoff of two hundred workers, and nobody knows yet which departments will lose people first.","t":"A：汽車工廠的大家為什麼看起來這麼擔心？這週為什麼開這麼多會議？ B：銷售量大幅下滑，所以公司宣布【裁員】兩百名工人，而且還沒有人知道哪些部門會先減少人手。"},{"w":"unemployment","p":"n.","d":"the state of not having a job","c":"失業","s":"A: Why are so many young people in this small town moving to big cities after they finish school? B: The unemployment rate here is very high because two factories closed last year, so it is difficult for graduates to find work, and many of them look for positions elsewhere.","t":"A：為什麼這個小鎮有這麼多年輕人畢業後搬到大城市？ B：這裡的【失業】率很高，因為去年有兩家工廠關閉了，所以畢業生很難找到工作，很多人只好到別處找職缺。"},{"w":"workforce","p":"n.","d":"all the people who work for a company or in a country","c":"勞動力；全體員工","s":"A: How many people does the new electronics factory near the airport employ now that it is fully open? B: Its workforce has grown to about two thousand people, and most of them are local residents who work in production, quality control, and shipping.","t":"A：機場附近那家新的電子工廠全面開工後，現在雇用多少人？ B：它的【員工總數】已經增加到大約兩千人，其中大多數是在生產、品管和出貨部門工作的當地居民。"},{"w":"workplace","p":"n.","d":"the office, factory, or other place where people work","c":"工作場所；職場","s":"A: Why did the company add plants, comfortable chairs, and a small kitchen to the office last month? B: The managers want to create a friendlier workplace, because they believe staff who feel relaxed and comfortable at work are more productive and less likely to leave.","t":"A：公司上個月為什麼在辦公室增加了植物、舒適的椅子和一間小廚房？ B：主管們想打造更友善的【工作環境】，因為他們相信在工作時感到放鬆舒適的員工更有效率，也比較不會離職。"},{"w":"shift","p":"n.","d":"a set period of work time, such as day or night","c":"班；輪班","s":"A: Can you cover for me at the restaurant on Saturday, because my sister is getting married that day? B: Sure, I can take your evening shift, which starts at five and finishes at midnight, if you agree to work my morning hours next Wednesday.","t":"A：星期六你可以幫我在餐廳代班嗎？因為我姊姊那天結婚。 B：當然，我可以幫你上晚【班】，從五點到半夜十二點，只要你同意下週三幫我上早上的時段。"},{"w":"overtime","p":"n.","d":"extra time worked after normal working hours","c":"加班；加班時間","s":"A: Why have you been coming home so late every night for the past two weeks? B: Our team has to finish a big order for an overseas client, so the manager asked us to put in a lot of overtime, but at least the company pays us extra for every additional hour.","t":"A：過去兩週你為什麼每天晚上都這麼晚回家？ B：我們團隊必須完成一位海外客戶的大訂單，所以經理要我們大量【加班】，不過至少公司每多一小時都會付我們額外的錢。"},{"w":"probation","p":"n.","d":"a trial period at the start of a new job","c":"試用期","s":"A: Has the new office assistant become a regular employee yet, or is he still being evaluated by the manager? B: He is still on probation for the first three months, so his supervisor will check his work carefully before deciding whether to offer him a long-term position.","t":"A：新來的辦公室助理已經成為正式員工了嗎？還是經理還在評估他？ B：他前三個月還在【試用期】，所以他的主管會仔細檢查他的工作，再決定是否給他長期職位。"}]},{"unit":119,"theme":"Encourage 鼓勵","cards":[{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help someone by giving them encouragement or practical help","c":"支持；支援","s":"A: Our team has to finish the new product launch plan by Friday, but two designers are on vacation this week, so what should we do? B: Don't worry, the manager in the marketing department promised to support us by lending two of her staff until the project is completed next month.","t":"A：我們團隊必須在週五前完成新產品上市計畫，但這週有兩位設計師在休假，我們該怎麼辦？ B：別擔心，行銷部門的經理答應會借調兩名員工來【支援】我們，直到下個月專案完成為止。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something or work harder","c":"激勵；使有動力","s":"A: Sales in our downtown store have been low for three months, and many of the staff seem tired and bored at work, so do you have any ideas? B: We could offer a small bonus to the top seller each month, which should motivate everyone to talk with more customers and work harder.","t":"A：我們市中心門市的業績已經低迷了三個月，很多員工上班時看起來又累又無聊，你有什麼想法嗎？ B：我們可以每個月發一筆小獎金給業績最好的銷售員，這應該能【激勵】大家和更多顧客交談、更努力工作。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the idea or the wish to do something good","c":"啟發；激發","s":"A: Why did you decide to start your own small bakery after working at a large bank for almost ten years? B: My grandmother ran a popular café in our hometown for forty years, and I want my shop to inspire young people in the neighborhood to follow their own dreams just as she did.","t":"A：你在大銀行工作了將近十年，為什麼決定開一家自己的小麵包店？ B：我祖母在我們家鄉經營一家很受歡迎的咖啡館長達四十年，我希望我的店也能像她一樣【啟發】附近的年輕人去追求自己的夢想。"},{"w":"boost","p":"v.","d":"to increase or improve something","c":"提升；促進","s":"A: The new coffee shop on the corner has very few customers on weekday mornings, even though the coffee is excellent and the prices are fair, so what is the owner going to do about it? B: She plans to hand out free samples at the train station next week, which she hopes will boost sales and bring in more office workers.","t":"A：轉角那家新咖啡店平日早上客人很少，雖然咖啡很棒、價格也合理，老闆打算怎麼處理？ B：她打算下週在火車站發放免費試喝品，她希望這能【提升】銷量並吸引更多上班族。"},{"w":"promote","p":"v.","d":"to help something grow, develop or become more popular","c":"促進；推廣","s":"A: Why is the city giving free bus passes to all students and older people starting next month? B: The local government wants to promote the use of public transportation, because the roads downtown are always crowded and the air quality has become worse over the past few years.","t":"A：為什麼市政府從下個月開始要提供所有學生和長者免費公車票？ B：地方政府想要【推廣】大眾運輸的使用，因為市中心的道路總是很擁擠，而且過去幾年空氣品質也變得更差了。"},{"w":"reinforce","p":"v.","d":"to make an idea, feeling or habit stronger","c":"加強；強化","s":"A: The new staff learned the safety rules during their first week, but some of them still forget to wear gloves in the warehouse, so what should we do? B: Let's put large posters near every door and hold a short meeting each Monday to reinforce the rules until everyone follows them naturally.","t":"A：新進員工在第一週就學過安全規定了，但有些人在倉庫裡還是忘記戴手套，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們在每扇門旁邊貼上大海報，並且每週一開個簡短的會議來【加強】這些規定，直到每個人都自然而然地遵守為止。"},{"w":"uplift","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel happier or more hopeful","c":"振奮；使精神振奮","s":"A: Why are there so many bright paintings and green plants in the hospital waiting area now? B: The hospital director believes that a cheerful space can uplift patients and their families while they wait, so she asked local artists and a garden company to redesign the whole floor last spring.","t":"A：為什麼醫院候診區現在有這麼多色彩明亮的畫作和綠色植物？ B：院長認為一個令人愉快的空間能在病患和家屬等候時【振奮】他們的心情，所以她去年春天請了當地藝術家和一家園藝公司重新設計整層樓。"},{"w":"cheer","p":"v.","d":"to shout to show support or praise","c":"歡呼；為…加油","s":"A: Are you going to the company's charity run in the park on Saturday morning, or do you have other plans this weekend? B: I hurt my knee last month, so I can't run, but I'll stand near the finish line with my kids and cheer for our sales team as they cross it.","t":"A：你週六早上會去參加公司在公園舉辦的慈善路跑嗎？還是你這週末有其他計畫？ B：我上個月膝蓋受傷了，所以不能跑步，但我會帶孩子站在終點線附近，在我們業務團隊衝過終點時為他們【歡呼加油】。"},{"w":"urge","p":"v.","d":"to strongly advise or ask someone to do something","c":"力勸；敦促","s":"A: I heard that the airport will be very busy this Friday because of the national holiday, so how early should our team leave the office? B: The travel agent sent an email this morning to urge all passengers to arrive at least three hours before their flights, so we should leave by noon.","t":"A：我聽說因為國定假日，這週五機場會非常擁擠，那我們團隊應該多早離開辦公室？ B：旅行社今天早上寄了一封電子郵件，【敦促】所有旅客至少在班機起飛前三小時抵達，所以我們應該在中午前出發。"},{"w":"stimulate","p":"v.","d":"to cause something to become more active or to grow","c":"刺激；促進","s":"A: Why did the government decide to lower taxes for small businesses this year, even though it needs money for new roads and schools? B: Many shops closed during the last economic slowdown, so officials hope lower taxes will stimulate local business activity and help companies hire more workers in the coming months.","t":"A：政府今年為什麼決定為小型企業減稅，即使它需要經費來興建新道路和學校？ B：上一次經濟衰退期間有許多商店倒閉，所以官員希望降低稅負能【刺激】地方商業活動，並幫助公司在接下來幾個月僱用更多員工。"},{"w":"empower","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the power, confidence or right to do something","c":"授權；使有能力","s":"A: Why do the front desk staff at your hotel solve guest problems so quickly without calling a manager first? B: Our general manager believes we should empower employees to make their own decisions, so every receptionist can offer a free breakfast or a room upgrade when a guest has a bad experience.","t":"A：為什麼你們飯店的櫃檯人員不用先打電話給經理，就能這麼快解決房客的問題？ B：我們的總經理認為應該【授權】員工自己做決定，所以當房客有不好的體驗時，每位櫃檯人員都可以提供免費早餐或客房升等。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something by giving good reasons","c":"說服","s":"A: Did you manage to change the client's mind about canceling their order after the shipping delay last week? B: Yes, I offered them a ten percent discount and free express delivery on their next order, and that was enough to persuade them to stay with our company for another year.","t":"A：上週出貨延誤後，你有成功讓客戶改變取消訂單的想法嗎？ B：有，我給他們打九折，並在下一筆訂單提供免費快遞，這樣就足以【說服】他們繼續跟我們公司合作一年。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe that something is true","c":"使確信；說服","s":"A: The board members still think the new software is too expensive, so how can we get them to approve the purchase at Thursday's meeting? B: Let's show them the report from our test in the Taipei office, because clear numbers about time and money saved will convince them that it is worth the cost.","t":"A：董事會成員還是覺得新軟體太貴了，我們要怎麼讓他們在週四的會議上批准這筆採購？ B：我們給他們看台北辦公室的試用報告吧，因為關於節省時間和金錢的明確數據能讓他們【確信】這筆花費是值得的。"},{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone what you think they should do","c":"建議；勸告","s":"A: I'm thinking about moving my savings into a new online investment company that a friend told me about, but I'm not sure it's safe, so what do you think? B: Before you do anything, talk to a financial expert at your bank, because they can advise you on the risks and help you compare other options.","t":"A：我在考慮把存款轉到一個朋友介紹的新網路投資公司，但我不確定是否安全，你覺得呢？ B：在採取任何行動之前，先跟你銀行的理財專員談談，因為他們可以就風險給你【建議】，並幫你比較其他選擇。"},{"w":"guide","p":"v.","d":"to show someone the way or help them understand what to do","c":"引導；指導","s":"A: Our new interns start on Monday, and none of them have worked in an office before, so who will show them how everything works here? B: Ms. Chen from human resources will guide them through the building on the first morning and then explain how to use the computer system after lunch.","t":"A：我們的新實習生週一開始上班，他們都沒在辦公室工作過，誰會帶他們了解這裡的一切運作？ B：人資部的陳小姐第一天早上會【引導】他們參觀整棟大樓，午餐後再說明如何使用電腦系統。"},{"w":"mentor","p":"v.","d":"to give a less experienced person advice and help over a period of time","c":"指導；當…的導師","s":"A: How is the new accountant doing in her first month, and does she need any extra training before the busy tax season begins? B: She is doing well, and our senior accountant has offered to mentor her for the next six months, meeting with her every Friday to answer questions and review her work.","t":"A：新來的會計第一個月表現如何？在忙碌的報稅季開始前她需要額外的訓練嗎？ B：她表現得很好，我們的資深會計已經主動提出在接下來六個月【指導】她，每週五和她見面回答問題並檢查她的工作。"},{"w":"praise","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is very good","c":"稱讚；讚揚","s":"A: How did the customers react to the new menu that our chef introduced at the restaurant last weekend? B: Most of them loved it, and several food bloggers wrote online reviews to praise the fresh local ingredients and the friendly service, so we have been fully booked every night since then.","t":"A：顧客對我們主廚上週末在餐廳推出的新菜單反應如何？ B：大部分顧客都很喜歡，還有好幾位美食部落客在網路上寫評論【稱讚】新鮮的在地食材和親切的服務，所以從那之後我們每晚都客滿。"},{"w":"compliment","p":"v.","d":"to say something nice to someone about their work, looks or actions","c":"稱讚；恭維","s":"A: You look very happy this afternoon, so did something good happen during your presentation to the clients from Japan? B: Yes, after the meeting their director came over to compliment me on my clear slides and helpful answers, and she even said they would like to work with us again next year.","t":"A：你今天下午看起來很開心，你向日本客戶做簡報時發生了什麼好事嗎？ B：是啊，會議結束後他們的主管走過來【稱讚】我的投影片很清楚、回答也很有幫助，她甚至說明年還想再跟我們合作。"},{"w":"reassure","p":"v.","d":"to say or do something to make someone feel less worried","c":"使安心；安慰","s":"A: Many passengers are getting upset because our flight to Singapore has been delayed for two hours without any explanation, so what should we do? B: I'll ask the gate agent to make an announcement right away, because clear information about the new departure time will reassure them and stop people from crowding around the counter.","t":"A：我們飛往新加坡的班機已經延誤兩小時卻沒有任何說明，很多乘客越來越不高興了，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我會請登機門地勤人員馬上廣播，因為關於新起飛時間的清楚資訊能讓他們【安心】，也能避免大家擠在櫃檯周圍。"},{"w":"comfort","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less sad or worried","c":"安慰","s":"A: Did you hear that Kevin's father is in the hospital, and he has to fly to his hometown tonight? B: Yes, so a few of us are going to stop by his desk this afternoon to comfort him, and we'll also offer to handle his clients until he returns next week.","t":"A：你有聽說凱文的父親住院了，他今晚必須飛回家鄉嗎？ B：有，所以我們幾個人今天下午要去他的座位【安慰】他，我們也會主動幫他處理客戶，直到他下週回來。"},{"w":"back","p":"v.","d":"to give support or money to a person, plan or idea","c":"支持；資助","s":"A: Do you think the directors will approve Lisa's idea of opening a second branch in Kaohsiung next year? B: I think so, because the sales manager and the finance director have both agreed to back her plan at the meeting, and their support usually carries a lot of weight with the board.","t":"A：你覺得董事們會批准麗莎明年在高雄開第二家分店的構想嗎？ B：我想會，因為業務經理和財務長都同意在會議上【支持】她的計畫，而他們的意見通常對董事會很有份量。"},{"w":"endorse","p":"v.","d":"to publicly say that you approve of or support someone or something","c":"公開支持；代言","s":"A: Why have sales of that new sports drink increased so quickly over the past two months in convenience stores? B: A famous basketball player agreed to endorse the product in a series of TV commercials, so many young fans started buying it after school and before their own games.","t":"A：為什麼那款新運動飲料過去兩個月在便利商店的銷量成長得這麼快？ B：一位知名籃球員同意在一系列電視廣告中為這項產品【代言】，所以許多年輕球迷開始在放學後和自己比賽前購買。"},{"w":"champion","p":"v.","d":"to strongly support and fight for a cause or idea","c":"擁護；倡導","s":"A: Who started the program that lets employees work from home two days a week at our company? B: Our human resources director decided to champion the idea after a survey showed that many staff spent over two hours a day commuting, and she presented the plan to the CEO herself.","t":"A：是誰發起讓我們公司員工每週可以在家工作兩天的計畫？ B：一項調查顯示許多員工每天通勤超過兩小時後，我們的人資長決定【大力倡導】這個構想，並親自向執行長提出這項計畫。"},{"w":"foster","p":"v.","d":"to help something develop over time","c":"培養；促進","s":"A: Why does your company organize a team lunch and a sports day every month, even when everyone is busy with projects? B: Our managers believe these events foster good relationships between departments, so people feel more comfortable sharing ideas and asking each other for help when problems come up.","t":"A：為什麼你們公司每個月都舉辦團隊午餐和運動日，即使大家都忙於專案？ B：我們的主管認為這些活動能【促進】部門之間的良好關係，讓大家在遇到問題時更自在地分享想法、互相幫忙。"},{"w":"cultivate","p":"v.","d":"to develop a skill, quality or relationship through effort","c":"培養；建立","s":"A: How did you get so many large companies to become regular customers of your small printing business? B: For years I have tried to cultivate strong relationships with clients by calling them personally, delivering orders early, and remembering small details about each company's needs and style.","t":"A：你是怎麼讓這麼多大公司成為你小型印刷公司的常客？ B：多年來我一直努力和客戶【建立】穩固的關係，像是親自打電話給他們、提早交貨，以及記住每家公司在需求和風格上的小細節。"},{"w":"nurture","p":"v.","d":"to help someone or something grow and develop by caring for them","c":"培育；栽培","s":"A: Your company has won the best young designer award three years in a row, so what is your secret? B: We hire talented graduates every summer and try to nurture their creativity by giving them real projects, friendly feedback, and the chance to attend design fairs in Tokyo and Milan.","t":"A：你們公司已經連續三年贏得最佳新銳設計師獎，你們的秘訣是什麼？ B：我們每年夏天都會招募有才華的畢業生，並藉由給他們真實的專案、友善的回饋，以及參加東京和米蘭設計展的機會來【培育】他們的創造力。"},{"w":"spur","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen faster or make someone try harder","c":"激勵；刺激","s":"A: Why did the electronics store suddenly become so crowded last weekend when it is usually quiet? B: They advertised a one-day sale with half-price laptops and free headphones, and the special offer helped spur demand so much that the shelves were nearly empty by late afternoon.","t":"A：那家電子產品店平常很冷清，為什麼上週末突然這麼擁擠？ B：他們打廣告推出一日特賣，筆電半價還送免費耳機，這項優惠大大【刺激】了需求，到傍晚貨架幾乎都空了。"},{"w":"drive","p":"v.","d":"to cause something to happen or make something go up","c":"驅使；推動","s":"A: Why has the price of fresh fruit at the supermarket gone up so much since the beginning of the summer? B: The heavy rain and typhoons damaged many farms in the south, and the smaller harvest will drive prices even higher over the next few weeks, so buy what you need now.","t":"A：超市的新鮮水果價格為什麼從夏天開始漲了這麼多？ B：大雨和颱風損壞了南部許多農場，收成減少會在接下來幾週把價格【推升】得更高，所以你需要什麼就現在買吧。"},{"w":"energize","p":"v.","d":"to give someone more energy or enthusiasm","c":"使充滿活力；激勵","s":"A: Everyone looked tired and quiet during this morning's planning meeting, so how can we make the afternoon workshop more lively? B: Let's start with a short team game and some fresh fruit and coffee, because a fun activity at the beginning will energize the group before we discuss next year's budget.","t":"A：今天早上的規劃會議大家看起來都又累又安靜，我們要怎麼讓下午的研習會更有活力？ B：我們先玩一個簡短的團隊遊戲，再準備一些新鮮水果和咖啡，因為一開始的有趣活動能在討論明年預算之前讓大家【充滿活力】。"},{"w":"embolden","p":"v.","d":"to give someone more courage or confidence to do something","c":"使有膽量；壯膽","s":"A: Why did the quiet new engineer suddenly share so many ideas at the product meeting yesterday afternoon? B: Her manager praised her design in front of the whole team last week, and that positive feedback seemed to embolden her to speak up and suggest changes to the project plan.","t":"A：那位安靜的新工程師昨天下午的產品會議上為什麼突然分享了這麼多想法？ B：她的主管上週在整個團隊面前稱讚她的設計，那些正面回饋似乎讓她【更有勇氣】發言，並提出對專案計畫的修改建議。"},{"w":"incentivize","p":"v.","d":"to encourage someone to do something by offering a reward","c":"以獎勵激勵","s":"A: Fewer customers are using our mobile app this year, even though we spent a lot of money to improve its design, so what should we try next? B: We could incentivize people to download it by offering a fifteen percent discount on their first online order and free delivery for the first month.","t":"A：今年使用我們手機應用程式的顧客變少了，即使我們花了很多錢改善它的設計，接下來我們該試試什麼？ B：我們可以提供首筆網路訂單八五折以及第一個月免運費，用獎勵【鼓勵】大家下載。"},{"w":"encouraging","p":"adj.","d":"giving hope or confidence","c":"令人鼓舞的","s":"A: How were the results of the customer survey for the new frozen dumplings that we launched in supermarkets last month? B: The results were very encouraging, because almost eighty percent of shoppers said they would buy them again, so the sales director wants to add two new flavors before the winter holidays.","t":"A：我們上個月在超市推出的新款冷凍水餃，顧客問卷調查結果如何？ B：結果非常【令人鼓舞】，因為將近百分之八十的購物者說他們會再買，所以業務總監想在寒假前再推出兩種新口味。"},{"w":"motivational","p":"adj.","d":"making people want to work hard or achieve something","c":"激勵人心的","s":"A: Who is giving the opening talk at our annual sales conference in Taichung next month, and what will it be about? B: We invited a former Olympic swimmer to give a motivational speech about setting goals and never giving up, because the team needs some fresh energy after a difficult year.","t":"A：下個月我們在台中舉辦的年度業務大會由誰做開場演講？內容是什麼？ B：我們邀請了一位前奧運游泳選手來做一場關於設定目標、永不放棄的【激勵人心的】演講，因為團隊在艱難的一年後需要一些新的活力。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help, kindness and encouragement","c":"支持的；給予幫助的","s":"A: How do you like your new job at the design company after your first three months, and are you still nervous about the long hours? B: I really enjoy it, because my manager and coworkers are very supportive, and they always explain things patiently when I make a mistake or need help with a project.","t":"A：在設計公司做了三個月，你喜歡新工作嗎？還會對長工時感到緊張嗎？ B：我真的很喜歡，因為我的主管和同事都非常【支持我】，每當我犯錯或專案需要幫忙時，他們總是很有耐心地解釋。"},{"w":"positively","p":"adv.","d":"in a good or helpful way","c":"正面地；積極地","s":"A: How did the staff react when the company announced the new flexible working hours at yesterday's meeting? B: Most people responded very positively, because parents can now pick up their children from school, and many workers said they would feel less stressed and be able to work more efficiently.","t":"A：公司在昨天的會議上宣布新的彈性工時，員工的反應如何？ B：大多數人的反應都非常【正面】，因為家長現在可以去學校接孩子，而且許多員工說他們會覺得壓力較小，工作也能更有效率。"}]},{"unit":120,"theme":"Energetic Person 精力充沛的人","cards":[{"w":"energetic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and ready to be active","c":"精力充沛的","s":"A: Who do you think should lead the morning tour for the new interns, since it involves walking around the whole factory for three hours? B: I would choose Daniel from the marketing team, because he is always energetic early in the day and he never complains about long walks or busy schedules.","t":"A：你覺得誰應該帶新實習生進行早上的參觀？因為要在整個工廠走三個小時。 B：我會選行銷部的丹尼爾，因為他一大早總是【精力充沛】，而且從不抱怨走很多路或行程很忙。"},{"w":"lively","p":"adj.","d":"full of life, fun and activity","c":"活潑的；熱鬧的","s":"A: How was the welcome dinner for the visiting clients from Japan last night, and did everyone get along well? B: It was a really lively evening, because the restaurant had live music, the staff told funny stories, and the clients stayed chatting with us until almost midnight.","t":"A：昨晚為日本來訪客戶舉辦的歡迎晚宴怎麼樣？大家相處得好嗎？ B：那真是一個非常【熱鬧】的晚上，因為餐廳有現場音樂，員工講了很多有趣的故事，客戶跟我們聊到快半夜才走。"},{"w":"active","p":"adj.","d":"busy doing things and taking part in them","c":"積極的；活躍的","s":"A: Do you know whether our new branch manager has any experience working with local community groups in this area? B: Yes, she has been very active in the city's business association for years, so she already knows many shop owners and often helps organize charity events on weekends.","t":"A：你知道我們新的分行經理有沒有和這一帶在地社區團體合作的經驗嗎？ B：有，她多年來一直在市內的商業協會非常【活躍】，所以她已經認識很多店家老闆，而且週末常幫忙籌辦慈善活動。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy, new ideas and change","c":"有活力的；變化快速的","s":"A: What kind of company culture should we describe in the job advertisement to attract younger designers and engineers? B: We should say that we offer a dynamic work environment where new ideas are welcomed, projects change quickly, and employees can grow their skills by working with different departments.","t":"A：我們應該在徵才廣告中描述什麼樣的公司文化，才能吸引較年輕的設計師和工程師？ B：我們應該說我們提供一個【充滿活力】的工作環境，歡迎新想法、專案變化快速，而且員工可以透過與不同部門合作來提升技能。"},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"bright, exciting and full of life","c":"充滿活力的；鮮豔的","s":"A: Why did the company decide to open its new office downtown instead of in the quiet business park near the airport? B: The downtown area has a vibrant atmosphere with cafés, shops, and cultural events, so the managers believed it would help attract talented young employees and impress visiting clients.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定把新辦公室開在市中心，而不是機場附近安靜的商業園區？ B：市中心有咖啡館、商店和文化活動，氣氛【充滿活力】，所以經理們認為這有助於吸引有才華的年輕員工，也能讓來訪的客戶留下好印象。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing strong interest and excitement","c":"熱情的；熱衷的","s":"A: How did the sales staff react when the director announced the new bonus plan at Monday's meeting? B: Most of them were very enthusiastic about it, because the plan rewards good teamwork, and several people immediately started talking about how they could reach their targets before the end of the quarter.","t":"A：週一會議上主任宣布新的獎金方案時，業務人員有什麼反應？ B：他們大多數人對此都非常【熱衷】，因為這個方案會獎勵良好的團隊合作，有好幾個人立刻開始討論要怎麼在這一季結束前達成目標。"},{"w":"passionate","p":"adj.","d":"having very strong feelings about something you love","c":"熱愛的；充滿熱情的","s":"A: Why did the hiring committee choose Ms. Lin for the position at the environmental research center over the other candidates? B: She has less experience than some of them, but she is truly passionate about protecting the ocean, and she spoke about her volunteer work so clearly that everyone was impressed.","t":"A：為什麼招聘委員會在眾多應徵者中選了林小姐擔任環境研究中心的職位？ B：她的經驗比其中幾個人少，但她真的非常【熱愛】保護海洋，而且她把自己的志工經驗講得很清楚，讓每個人都印象深刻。"},{"w":"spirited","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and strong feeling","c":"熱烈的；激烈的；生氣勃勃的","s":"A: Did the board members agree quickly on the plan to move the factory overseas, or was there a long argument? B: There was a spirited debate that lasted almost two hours, because several members strongly disagreed about the costs, but in the end they voted to study the idea for another month.","t":"A：董事會成員是很快就同意把工廠遷往海外的計畫，還是經過了長時間的爭論？ B：有一場將近兩小時的【激烈】辯論，因為好幾位成員對成本強烈反對，但最後他們投票決定再研究這個構想一個月。"},{"w":"vigorous","p":"adj.","d":"strong, active and full of energy","c":"強而有力的；劇烈的","s":"A: What did the doctor at the company health check tell you about your back pain and your long hours at the computer? B: She told me to avoid vigorous exercise for two weeks, take short breaks every hour, and walk slowly after lunch until the pain in my lower back gets better.","t":"A：公司健康檢查的醫生針對你的背痛和長時間使用電腦說了什麼？ B：她叫我兩週內避免【劇烈】運動，每小時短暫休息一下，午餐後慢慢散步，直到下背的疼痛好轉。"},{"w":"robust","p":"adj.","d":"strong and healthy; not easily weakened","c":"強健的；穩健的","s":"A: Are you worried that the new coffee chain across the street will take away many of our regular customers this year? B: Not really, because our sales have been robust for three years in a row, our customers love the loyalty program, and we are planning to add a breakfast menu next month.","t":"A：你擔心對街新開的連鎖咖啡店今年會搶走我們很多常客嗎？ B：不太擔心，因為我們的銷售已經連續三年都很【穩健】，客人很喜歡我們的集點方案，而且我們打算下個月推出早餐菜單。"},{"w":"peppy","p":"adj.","d":"lively, cheerful and full of energy","c":"活潑的；輕快的；精神十足的","s":"A: What kind of music should we play in the background of the new advertisement for our sports drink? B: I think we need something short and peppy with a fast beat, because the video shows young people running and dancing, and slow music would make the whole thing feel boring.","t":"A：我們新的運動飲料廣告背景應該放什麼樣的音樂？ B：我覺得我們需要一段簡短又【輕快活潑】、節奏很快的音樂，因為影片中是年輕人在跑步和跳舞，慢歌會讓整支廣告感覺很無聊。"},{"w":"bubbly","p":"adj.","d":"very cheerful, friendly and full of energy","c":"活潑開朗的","s":"A: Why do so many hotel guests mention the young woman at the front desk in their online reviews? B: She has such a bubbly personality, always smiling and chatting with people from different countries, that guests feel welcome as soon as they arrive, even after a long and tiring flight.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多飯店住客在網路評論中提到櫃檯那位年輕女生？ B：她的個性非常【活潑開朗】，總是面帶微笑，和來自不同國家的人聊天，所以即使旅客搭了又長又累的班機，一抵達就會感到受歡迎。"},{"w":"animated","p":"adj.","d":"full of interest and energy, especially when talking","c":"熱烈的；生動的","s":"A: Was the training session on the new software as boring as everyone expected it to be this afternoon? B: Not at all, because the trainer asked so many interesting questions that we had an animated conversation about our daily problems, and the time passed much faster than I thought.","t":"A：今天下午的新軟體訓練課程有大家預期的那麼無聊嗎？ B：一點也不，因為講師問了很多有趣的問題，我們針對日常遇到的問題進行了【熱烈】的對話，時間過得比我想的快很多。"},{"w":"zestful","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and enjoyment","c":"充滿熱情的；興致勃勃的","s":"A: How would you describe the new tour guide that the travel agency hired for the summer mountain trips? B: He has a zestful attitude toward every trip, telling stories, singing songs on the bus, and cheering up tired travelers, so customers say the long hours on the road feel short and fun.","t":"A：你會怎麼形容旅行社為夏季山區行程新聘的導遊？ B：他對每一趟行程都抱持【充滿熱情】的態度，會講故事、在巴士上唱歌，並為疲累的旅客打氣，所以客人都說長時間的車程感覺又短又有趣。"},{"w":"zealous","p":"adj.","d":"very eager and determined, sometimes too much","c":"熱心的；狂熱的","s":"A: Why did several customers complain about the new security guard at the shopping mall entrance last weekend? B: He was a little too zealous about following the rules, so he checked every bag very slowly, and a long line of shoppers formed outside the doors during the busy Saturday sale.","t":"A：為什麼上週末有好幾位顧客投訴購物中心入口的新警衛？ B：他對遵守規定有點過於【熱衷】，所以每個包包都檢查得很慢，結果在忙碌的週六特賣期間，門外排起了一長串購物人潮。"},{"w":"driven","p":"adj.","d":"very determined to succeed","c":"有幹勁的；有強烈企圖心的","s":"A: Do you think Kevin will really finish his MBA while working full-time as an assistant manager at the bank? B: I'm sure he will, because he is extremely driven and organized, studying every night after work and on weekends, and he has already told everyone he wants to become a branch director.","t":"A：你覺得凱文真的能一邊在銀行全職擔任副理，一邊完成他的企管碩士嗎？ B：我確定他可以，因為他非常【有企圖心】又很有條理，每天下班後和週末都在念書，而且他已經告訴大家他想成為分行主管。"},{"w":"motivated","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to do something and willing to work hard for it","c":"有動力的；積極的","s":"A: What qualities are you looking for in the new sales assistant, since you said experience is not the most important thing? B: I want someone who is highly motivated and willing to learn, because we can teach product knowledge in a few weeks, but a positive attitude toward work is much harder to train.","t":"A：你說經驗不是最重要的，那你希望新的業務助理具備什麼特質？ B：我希望找一個非常【積極主動】又願意學習的人，因為產品知識幾週內就能教會，但對工作的正面態度要難訓練得多。"},{"w":"go-getter","p":"n.","d":"a person who works hard and is determined to succeed","c":"積極進取的人；有魄力的人","s":"A: Why did the regional manager promote Sarah so quickly after she joined the company only a year ago? B: She is a real go-getter who finds new customers on her own, solves problems without waiting for instructions, and she brought in three large contracts during her first six months.","t":"A：為什麼莎拉才進公司一年，區域經理就這麼快升她的職？ B：她是一個真正【積極進取的人】，會自己開發新客戶、不等指示就主動解決問題，而且在頭六個月就談成了三份大合約。"},{"w":"self-starter","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts work without needing to be told","c":"主動自發的人；能自我激勵的人","s":"A: Our new team members will work from home most days, so what kind of people should we look for during the interviews? B: Each person should be a self-starter who can plan the day alone, finish tasks without close supervision, and contact the manager only when something is really unclear.","t":"A：我們的新團隊成員大部分時間都會在家工作，那面試時我們應該找什麼樣的人？ B：每個人都應該是能【主動自發的人】，能獨自規劃一天的工作，在沒有密切監督的情況下完成任務，只有在真的不清楚時才聯絡主管。"},{"w":"hardworking","p":"adj.","d":"working with a lot of effort","c":"勤奮的","s":"A: What did the restaurant owner say about the kitchen staff when the food critic praised the meal in the newspaper? B: He thanked his hardworking cooks and dishwashers, who start preparing ingredients at six every morning, and he gave everyone an extra day off to celebrate the excellent review.","t":"A：美食評論家在報紙上稱讚那頓餐點時，餐廳老闆怎麼評論廚房員工？ B：他感謝他那些【勤奮】的廚師和洗碗工，他們每天早上六點就開始準備食材，他還多給每個人一天假來慶祝這篇好評。"},{"w":"industrious","p":"adj.","d":"always working hard","c":"勤勉的；勤奮的","s":"A: How did the small family business manage to grow into a company with five factories in just twenty years? B: The founder was an industrious man who worked long hours, saved every dollar, and trained his children carefully, so the business kept expanding even during difficult economic times.","t":"A：那家小型家族企業怎麼能在短短二十年內成長為擁有五座工廠的公司？ B：創辦人是一位【勤勉】的人，他工作時間很長、省下每一塊錢，並用心培訓他的孩子，所以即使經濟困難時，事業也持續擴張。"},{"w":"tireless","p":"adj.","d":"working hard for a long time without stopping","c":"不知疲倦的；孜孜不倦的","s":"A: Why is the hospital naming its new children's wing after a nurse instead of a doctor or a donor? B: Ms. Wong spent forty years caring for sick children, and the hospital wanted to honor her tireless efforts, especially her work raising money for families who could not afford treatment.","t":"A：為什麼醫院要以一位護理師的名字，而不是醫生或捐款人的名字，來命名新的兒童大樓？ B：黃小姐花了四十年照顧生病的孩子，醫院想表揚她【不辭辛勞】的付出，特別是她為付不起醫療費的家庭募款的貢獻。"},{"w":"relentless","p":"adj.","d":"never stopping or becoming weaker","c":"不懈的；持續不斷的","s":"A: How did your small online shop become so successful, even with large companies selling similar products at lower prices? B: We had a relentless focus on customer service, answering every message within an hour, and that careful attention helped us build a loyal group of buyers who recommended us to friends.","t":"A：即使大公司以更低的價格販售類似商品，你們的小網店是怎麼變得這麼成功的？ B：我們【持續不懈】地專注於客戶服務，每則訊息都在一小時內回覆，這種用心幫我們建立了一群忠實顧客，他們還會把我們推薦給朋友。"},{"w":"eager","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to do or have something","c":"渴望的；熱切的","s":"A: How are the new interns doing in their first week at the accounting firm, and do they need more help? B: They are all eager to learn, asking good questions in every meeting, but I think they need more practice with our software before they handle real client accounts next month.","t":"A：新實習生在會計事務所的第一週表現如何？他們需要更多協助嗎？ B：他們都很【渴望】學習，每次開會都會提出好問題，但我想在下個月處理真正的客戶帳目之前，他們需要多練習我們的軟體。"},{"w":"keen","p":"adj.","d":"very interested in something and wanting to do it","c":"熱衷的；渴望的","s":"A: Has the marketing director decided whether our department will attend the trade fair in Singapore this spring? B: She is very keen on the idea, because many of our Asian buyers will be there, but she still needs approval from finance before she books the booth and the flights.","t":"A：行銷總監決定我們部門今年春天是否要參加新加坡的商展了嗎？ B：她非常【熱衷】這個想法，因為我們很多亞洲買家都會到場，但她在預訂攤位和機票之前，仍需要財務部門的核准。"},{"w":"brisk","p":"adj.","d":"quick and full of energy; busy (business)","c":"輕快的；（生意）興隆的","s":"A: How were sales at the new bakery near the train station during its first week of business? B: Trade was brisk, especially in the early morning when commuters stopped for coffee and sandwiches, so the owner is already planning to hire two more workers for the morning shift.","t":"A：火車站附近新開的麵包店開幕第一週的銷售情況如何？ B：生意很【興隆】，特別是清晨通勤族會停下來買咖啡和三明治的時候，所以老闆已經打算為早班再多雇兩名員工。"},{"w":"sprightly","p":"adj.","d":"lively and active, especially for an older person","c":"（老人）精神矍鑠的；輕快的","s":"A: Is the retired engineer who leads our factory tours really over eighty years old, as the visitors were saying? B: Yes, he is eighty-two, but he is so sprightly that he climbs the stairs faster than most of us and still walks around the whole plant twice a week.","t":"A：帶我們工廠導覽的那位退休工程師真的像參觀者說的已經八十多歲了嗎？ B：是的，他八十二歲了，但他【精神矍鑠】，爬樓梯比我們大多數人都快，而且每週仍會繞整個廠區走兩次。"},{"w":"vivacious","p":"adj.","d":"attractive because lively and full of energy","c":"活潑迷人的","s":"A: Who are we inviting to host the company's annual awards dinner, since last year's host was so quiet? B: We've invited a vivacious TV presenter who is famous for her bright smile and quick jokes, so we hope she will keep the audience laughing and make the long evening more fun.","t":"A：既然去年的主持人那麼安靜，今年公司年度頒獎晚宴我們要邀請誰來主持？ B：我們邀請了一位【活潑迷人】的電視節目主持人，她以燦爛的笑容和機智的笑話聞名，希望她能讓觀眾一直笑，讓漫長的晚上更有趣。"},{"w":"high-spirited","p":"adj.","d":"lively, cheerful and full of energy","c":"興高采烈的；活潑的","s":"A: Why was the school group on the museum tour so noisy this morning, and did they disturb the other visitors? B: The children were a bit high-spirited after the long bus ride, laughing and running around, but their teachers calmed them down quickly, and nobody complained at the front desk.","t":"A：今天早上參加博物館導覽的學生團為什麼那麼吵？他們有打擾到其他參觀者嗎？ B：孩子們在長途巴士車程後有點【興高采烈】，又笑又跑，但老師們很快就讓他們安靜下來，沒有人到服務台抱怨。"},{"w":"adventurous","p":"adj.","d":"willing to try new or exciting things","c":"愛冒險的；勇於嘗試的","s":"A: Which of our travel packages would you recommend for a young couple who want something different for their honeymoon? B: If they are adventurous, I'd suggest the ten-day trip to Iceland, which includes glacier hiking, cave tours, and a night in a small cabin to watch the northern lights.","t":"A：有一對年輕夫妻想要不一樣的蜜月旅行，你會推薦我們哪個旅遊方案？ B：如果他們【喜歡冒險】，我會建議十天的冰島行程，其中包括冰河健行、洞穴導覽，以及在小木屋住一晚觀賞北極光。"},{"w":"enterprising","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new ways to make money or solve problems","c":"有進取心的；有創業精神的","s":"A: How did that small noodle shop near our office become famous across the whole city so quickly? B: An enterprising young owner started selling cooking videos online, showing customers how she makes the noodles by hand, and soon thousands of people were visiting the shop to try them.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家小麵店怎麼這麼快就紅遍全市？ B：一位【有進取心】的年輕老闆開始在網路上販售烹飪影片，向顧客展示她如何手工製作麵條，很快就有成千上萬的人來店裡品嚐。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"producing a lot; getting a lot done","c":"有成效的；多產的","s":"A: How was the meeting with the suppliers this afternoon, and did you settle the delivery problems from last month? B: It was very productive, because we agreed on a new schedule, solved the packaging issue, and even got a small discount on our next order of raw materials.","t":"A：今天下午和供應商的會議如何？你們解決上個月的交貨問題了嗎？ B：會議非常【有成效】，因為我們談定了新的時程，解決了包裝問題，甚至在下一批原料訂單上還拿到了小折扣。"},{"w":"fast-paced","p":"adj.","d":"happening or moving very quickly","c":"快節奏的","s":"A: Why did Tom leave his job at the small bookstore to work at the busy advertising agency downtown? B: He said he wanted a more fast-paced job with tight deadlines and new projects every week, because selling books all day had started to feel too slow and quiet for him.","t":"A：湯姆為什麼辭掉小書店的工作，去市中心忙碌的廣告公司上班？ B：他說他想要一份更【快節奏】的工作，有緊迫的截止期限，每週都有新專案，因為整天賣書開始讓他覺得太慢又太安靜了。"},{"w":"energetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows a lot of energy","c":"精力充沛地；積極地","s":"A: How did the new sales team respond when the company lost its biggest customer in the middle of the year? B: They worked energetically to find new clients, making dozens of calls every day and visiting stores across the region, and by December they had replaced almost all the lost business.","t":"A：公司在年中失去最大客戶時，新的業務團隊如何因應？ B：他們【積極地】努力開發新客戶，每天打幾十通電話並拜訪全區的商店，到了十二月，他們幾乎已經補回了所有流失的業務。"},{"w":"enthusiastically","p":"adv.","d":"in a very interested and excited way","c":"熱情地；熱烈地","s":"A: How did the audience respond after the CEO introduced the new electric car at the product launch yesterday? B: They clapped enthusiastically for almost a minute, and many reporters rushed to the stage to take photos, so the marketing team believes the car will sell very well this year.","t":"A：昨天產品發表會上執行長介紹新款電動車後，觀眾反應如何？ B：他們【熱烈地】鼓掌將近一分鐘，許多記者衝到台前拍照，所以行銷團隊相信這款車今年會賣得很好。"}]},{"unit":121,"theme":"Energy 能源","cards":[{"w":"power","p":"n.","d":"the energy, especially electricity, used to make machines work","c":"電力；動力","s":"A: Why did everyone in the accounting department stop working at around two o'clock yesterday afternoon, just before the monthly reports were due? B: A strong storm knocked out the power in the whole building for nearly three hours, so the computers, printers, and even the elevators stopped working until the repair crew arrived.","t":"A：為什麼昨天下午大約兩點，就在月報要交之前，會計部的每個人都停止工作了？ B：一場強烈的暴風雨讓整棟大樓的【電力】中斷了將近三個小時，所以電腦、印表機，甚至電梯都停止運作，直到維修人員抵達。"},{"w":"electricity","p":"n.","d":"energy that is carried by wires and used for lights and machines","c":"電；電力","s":"A: Our office bills have gone up a lot this winter, and the finance manager wants to know why we are spending so much more than last year. B: I think the new heaters in the meeting rooms use a lot of electricity, so we should turn them off at night and on weekends when nobody is working there.","t":"A：今年冬天我們辦公室的帳單漲了很多，財務經理想知道為什麼我們比去年多花這麼多錢。 B：我想會議室裡的新暖氣用了很多【電】，所以我們應該在晚上和週末沒人在那裡工作時把它們關掉。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"n.","d":"something such as gas, oil, or coal that is burned to make heat or power","c":"燃料","s":"A: Why has the delivery company raised its prices again this month, even though the number of packages we send has stayed about the same? B: The manager explained that the cost of fuel for their trucks has risen sharply since the summer, so they need to charge customers a little more to cover their expenses.","t":"A：為什麼這個月快遞公司又漲價了，儘管我們寄送的包裹數量大致相同？ B：經理解釋說，自從夏天以來他們卡車的【燃料】成本大幅上漲，所以他們需要向客戶多收一點費用來支付開銷。"},{"w":"battery","p":"n.","d":"an object that stores electricity and gives power to a device","c":"電池","s":"A: Can you lend me your laptop charger before the client meeting starts, because I forgot mine at home this morning? B: Sure, but you may not need it, since the battery in my laptop usually lasts about eight hours, and the meeting room also has several outlets near the long table.","t":"A：客戶會議開始前你可以借我筆電充電器嗎？因為我今天早上把我的忘在家裡了。 B：當然可以，不過你可能用不到，因為我筆電的【電池】通常可以用大約八個小時，而且會議室長桌附近也有好幾個插座。"},{"w":"charge","p":"v.","d":"to put electricity into a battery or device","c":"充電","s":"A: Is there anywhere in the airport lounge where I can charge my phone before my flight to Tokyo, because it is almost dead and I need to call my client? B: Yes, there are free outlets next to the coffee bar, and you can also borrow a power bank from the front desk if all the seats are taken.","t":"A：機場貴賓室裡有地方可以讓我在飛往東京前幫手機【充電】嗎？因為它快沒電了，我還需要打電話給客戶。 B：有的，咖啡吧旁邊有免費插座，如果座位都滿了，你也可以向櫃台借行動電源。"},{"w":"generator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that produces electricity","c":"發電機","s":"A: What will happen to the hospital's computer system and medical machines if the city loses electricity during the typhoon this weekend? B: Don't worry, the hospital has a large backup generator in the basement that starts automatically within seconds, so the important equipment will keep running until the main supply returns.","t":"A：如果這個週末颱風期間全市停電，醫院的電腦系統和醫療機器會怎麼樣？ B：別擔心，醫院地下室有一台大型備用【發電機】，幾秒內就會自動啟動，所以重要設備在主要電源恢復前都會持續運作。"},{"w":"renewable","p":"adj.","d":"coming from a natural source that does not run out, like sun or wind","c":"可再生的","s":"A: Why is the company planning to put solar panels on the roof of the new warehouse instead of just buying electricity from the city? B: The board wants us to use more renewable energy over the next five years, because it lowers our long-term costs and also improves our image with customers who care about the environment.","t":"A：為什麼公司打算在新倉庫的屋頂裝太陽能板，而不是直接向市政府買電？ B：董事會希望我們在未來五年使用更多【可再生】能源，因為它可以降低我們的長期成本，也能提升我們在關心環境的客戶心中的形象。"},{"w":"nonrenewable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be replaced after it is used up, like coal or oil","c":"不可再生的","s":"A: Why does our sustainability report say we must reduce our use of coal and natural gas at the factory as soon as possible? B: Because they are nonrenewable resources that will eventually run out, and their prices keep going up, so depending on them could seriously hurt our profits in the future.","t":"A：為什麼我們的永續報告說工廠必須盡快減少使用煤和天然氣？ B：因為它們是終將用完的【不可再生】資源，而且價格一直上漲，所以依賴它們未來可能會嚴重損害我們的利潤。"},{"w":"solar","p":"adj.","d":"using or coming from the energy of the sun","c":"太陽能的；太陽的","s":"A: How has the hotel managed to cut its monthly energy bill so much since last spring, even though it has more guests now? B: The owner installed solar panels on the roof and over the parking lot, so most of the hot water and lighting now comes from sunlight instead of the city's electricity.","t":"A：自從去年春天以來，雖然現在客人更多了，飯店是怎麼把每月的能源帳單降低這麼多的？ B：老闆在屋頂和停車場上方裝了【太陽能】板，所以現在大部分的熱水和照明都來自陽光，而不是市電。"},{"w":"wind","p":"n.","d":"air that moves outside, which can be used to make power","c":"風","s":"A: Why are there so many tall white towers along the coast near the new industrial park, and who owns them? B: They belong to an energy company that uses the strong wind from the sea to produce electricity, and several factories in the park have signed contracts to buy power from them.","t":"A：為什麼新工業區附近的海岸邊有那麼多高大的白色塔，它們是誰的？ B：它們屬於一家能源公司，利用海上的強【風】來發電，園區裡有好幾家工廠已經簽約向他們購買電力。"},{"w":"hydropower","p":"n.","d":"electricity made from the force of moving water","c":"水力發電","s":"A: Why did the government decide to build a large dam on the river in the mountains, even though the project is very expensive? B: The dam will produce hydropower for nearly half a million homes, and it will also help control flooding during the rainy season, so officials believe the cost is worth it.","t":"A：為什麼政府決定在山區的河流上興建大型水壩，儘管這項工程非常昂貴？ B：這座水壩將為將近五十萬戶家庭提供【水力發電】，而且在雨季也有助於控制洪水，所以官員認為這筆花費是值得的。"},{"w":"geothermal","p":"adj.","d":"using the natural heat from deep inside the earth","c":"地熱的","s":"A: I heard that the resort we are visiting for the company retreat in Iceland heats all its buildings without burning any oil or gas. Is that true? B: Yes, it uses geothermal energy from the hot water deep underground, which also supplies the warm outdoor pools that guests enjoy in the evening.","t":"A：我聽說我們公司員工旅遊要去的冰島度假村，所有建築物的暖氣都不用燒任何油或天然氣，是真的嗎？ B：是的，它使用來自地底深處熱水的【地熱】能源，這些熱水也供應客人晚上喜歡泡的戶外溫水池。"},{"w":"biomass","p":"n.","d":"plant or animal material, such as wood, used as fuel","c":"生質物；生物質","s":"A: What does the paper factory do with all the wood chips and tree bark left over after production every day? B: They burn the biomass in a special boiler to make steam and electricity for the factory, which reduces waste and saves the company thousands of dollars on energy bills every month.","t":"A：造紙廠每天生產後剩下的木屑和樹皮都怎麼處理？ B：他們把這些【生質物】放在特殊鍋爐裡燃燒，為工廠產生蒸氣和電力，這減少了廢棄物，也讓公司每個月省下數千美元的能源費用。"},{"w":"nuclear","p":"adj.","d":"using the energy made when atoms are split","c":"核能的；核子的","s":"A: Why are so many people in the town attending tonight's public meeting at the community center? B: The government is planning to build a nuclear power plant near the coast, and many residents want to ask questions about safety, waste storage, and how the project will affect local jobs and property prices.","t":"A：為什麼鎮上有這麼多人要參加今晚在社區中心舉辦的公聽會？ B：政府計畫在海岸附近興建一座【核能】發電廠，許多居民想詢問有關安全、廢料儲存，以及這項計畫會如何影響當地工作和房價的問題。"},{"w":"efficiency","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do a job well without wasting energy, time, or money","c":"效率","s":"A: Why did the operations manager decide to replace all the old lights and air conditioners in the factory this year instead of next year? B: The new models have much higher energy efficiency, so they use less electricity to do the same work, and the savings will pay for the upgrade in about two years.","t":"A：為什麼營運經理決定今年就更換工廠所有舊的燈和冷氣，而不是明年？ B：新機型的能源【效率】高很多，所以做同樣的工作用電更少，省下的錢大約兩年就能付清這次升級的費用。"},{"w":"conservation","p":"n.","d":"the careful use of something so that it is not wasted","c":"節約；保護","s":"A: What was the main topic of the email that the building manager sent to all the tenants this morning? B: She asked everyone to support energy conservation during the hot summer months by turning off unused lights, closing windows when the air conditioning is on, and shutting down computers before leaving work.","t":"A：大樓管理員今天早上寄給所有租戶的電子郵件主要在講什麼？ B：她請大家在炎熱的夏季月份支持能源【節約】，像是關掉沒用的燈、開冷氣時關窗，以及下班前將電腦關機。"},{"w":"consumption","p":"n.","d":"the amount of energy, fuel, or food that is used","c":"消耗量；消費","s":"A: Why did the facilities team put new meters in every department last month, and what are they planning to do with the information? B: They want to measure the energy consumption of each floor, so they can find out which areas use the most electricity and then suggest ways to reduce waste.","t":"A：為什麼設施團隊上個月在每個部門都裝了新電表？他們打算怎麼使用這些資訊？ B：他們想測量每個樓層的能源【消耗量】，這樣就能找出哪些區域用電最多，然後建議減少浪費的方法。"},{"w":"output","p":"n.","d":"the amount of power or goods that something produces","c":"輸出量；產量","s":"A: How much electricity can the new solar farm outside the city produce, and will it be enough for the nearby factories? B: According to the engineer, its maximum output is about fifty megawatts on a sunny day, which is enough for the three largest factories in the area during working hours.","t":"A：城外新的太陽能電廠可以生產多少電力？足夠附近的工廠使用嗎？ B：根據工程師的說法，它在晴天的最大【輸出量】大約是五十百萬瓦，足夠這個地區最大的三間工廠在上班時間使用。"},{"w":"input","p":"n.","d":"the energy or material that is put into a machine or system","c":"輸入；投入","s":"A: Why does the report say that the old furnace in the factory is wasting so much money every month? B: The furnace needs a very large energy input of gas and electricity, but much of the heat escapes through the walls, so only a small part of what we pay for is actually used.","t":"A：為什麼報告說工廠裡的舊熔爐每個月浪費這麼多錢？ B：這座熔爐需要非常大量的瓦斯和電力能源【輸入】，但很多熱量從牆壁散失，所以我們付錢買的只有一小部分真正被使用到。"},{"w":"supply","p":"n.","d":"an amount of something that is provided for people to use","c":"供應；供給","s":"A: Is the factory going to stop production during the repairs to the city's power station next week? B: No, the manager arranged a temporary supply of electricity from a nearby company, so our machines can keep running, although we may have to cut back on lighting and air conditioning for a few days.","t":"A：下週市電廠維修期間工廠會停工嗎？ B：不會，經理已經安排從附近一家公司取得臨時的電力【供應】，所以我們的機器可以繼續運轉，不過幾天內我們可能得減少照明和冷氣的使用。"},{"w":"demand","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something that people want or need to use","c":"需求","s":"A: Why does the power company ask businesses to reduce their electricity use between two and five o'clock on summer afternoons? B: During those hours, demand for electricity is at its highest because offices, shops, and homes are all running air conditioners, so the system can become overloaded if everyone uses too much.","t":"A：為什麼電力公司要求企業在夏天下午兩點到五點之間減少用電？ B：在那段時間，電力的【需求】最高，因為辦公室、商店和住家都在開冷氣，所以如果每個人用太多，系統可能會超載。"},{"w":"grid","p":"n.","d":"the network of wires that carries electricity to a large area","c":"電網","s":"A: Can our company sell the extra electricity from the solar panels on our roof when we don't need it on weekends? B: Yes, we can send the extra power back to the national grid, and the electricity company will pay us for every unit we provide, which helps us recover the installation cost faster.","t":"A：週末我們用不到時，公司可以賣掉屋頂太陽能板多出來的電嗎？ B：可以，我們可以把多餘的電送回國家【電網】，電力公司會為我們提供的每一度電付錢，這有助於我們更快回收安裝成本。"},{"w":"turbine","p":"n.","d":"a machine with turning blades that makes power from wind, water, or steam","c":"渦輪機","s":"A: Why is the wind farm near the harbor not producing any electricity today, even though it is very windy outside? B: The engineers stopped every turbine this morning for safety checks, because one of the large blades was damaged during last week's storm and they need to inspect the others carefully.","t":"A：為什麼今天外面風很大，港口附近的風場卻沒有發電？ B：工程師今天早上為了安全檢查把每一座【渦輪機】都停了，因為上週暴風雨期間其中一片大型葉片受損，他們需要仔細檢查其他的。"},{"w":"emission","p":"n.","d":"gas or other material sent out into the air","c":"排放；排放物","s":"A: Why is the logistics company replacing so many of its old diesel trucks with electric ones this year? B: The government has introduced strict new rules on the emission of carbon dioxide from delivery vehicles, and companies that fail to meet the limits will have to pay heavy fines, so the managers decided to act early.","t":"A：為什麼物流公司今年要把這麼多舊柴油卡車換成電動卡車？ B：政府對送貨車輛的二氧化碳【排放】實施了嚴格的新規定，未達標準的公司必須支付高額罰款，所以經理們決定提早行動。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to continue for a long time without harming the environment","c":"永續的；可持續的","s":"A: Why did our biggest customer ask so many questions about our factory's energy use during the meeting yesterday? B: They only want to work with suppliers that follow sustainable practices, such as using clean energy and reducing waste, because their own investors are paying close attention to environmental issues.","t":"A：為什麼我們最大的客戶昨天開會時問了那麼多關於我們工廠能源使用的問題？ B：他們只想和採取【永續】做法的供應商合作，例如使用乾淨能源和減少浪費，因為他們自己的投資人非常關注環境議題。"},{"w":"clean","p":"adj.","d":"not making the air, water, or land dirty","c":"乾淨的；無污染的","s":"A: Why is the city giving money to companies that install solar panels or buy electric delivery vans this year? B: The mayor wants to encourage businesses to use more clean energy that does not pollute the air, because the smog in the city center has become a serious problem for workers and residents.","t":"A：為什麼市政府今年要補助安裝太陽能板或購買電動送貨車的公司？ B：市長想鼓勵企業使用更多不會污染空氣的【乾淨】能源，因為市中心的霧霾已經成為上班族和居民的嚴重問題。"},{"w":"green","p":"adj.","d":"good for the environment","c":"環保的；綠色的","s":"A: Why does the new office tower downtown ask for higher rent than the older buildings on the same street? B: It is a green building with solar panels, rainwater collection, and smart lighting, so tenants pay a little more rent but save a lot on utility bills and enjoy a healthier workplace.","t":"A：為什麼市中心新的辦公大樓租金比同一條街上的舊大樓高？ B：它是一棟有太陽能板、雨水回收和智慧照明的【環保】建築，所以租戶付的租金雖然稍高，卻能省下很多水電費，並享有更健康的工作環境。"},{"w":"intensity","p":"n.","d":"the amount of energy used to produce something","c":"密集度；強度","s":"A: Why did the consultant say our steel factory needs to change its production methods within the next three years? B: She found that the energy intensity of our process is much higher than that of our competitors, which means we use far more electricity to make each ton of steel and lose money.","t":"A：為什麼顧問說我們的鋼鐵廠必須在未來三年內改變生產方式？ B：她發現我們製程的能源【密集度】遠高於競爭對手，這表示我們每生產一噸鋼要用更多電，因而虧錢。"},{"w":"storage","p":"n.","d":"the keeping of something, such as energy, until it is needed","c":"儲存","s":"A: What will the factory do with all the extra electricity that the solar panels produce at noon when the machines are not using it? B: The company bought a large battery storage system that keeps the extra power, so we can use it in the evening when electricity prices from the grid are much higher.","t":"A：中午機器沒在用時，工廠要怎麼處理太陽能板產生的多餘電力？ B：公司買了一套大型電池【儲存】系統來保存多餘的電力，這樣我們就能在晚上電網電價高很多的時候使用。"},{"w":"transmit","p":"v.","d":"to send electricity or signals from one place to another","c":"輸送；傳送","s":"A: Why does the power company need to build so many new tall towers and cables across the farmland outside the town? B: They need to transmit electricity from the new wind farm on the coast to the large cities in the north, which are about two hundred kilometers away from the sea.","t":"A：為什麼電力公司需要在鎮外的農田上蓋那麼多新的高塔和電纜？ B：他們需要把電力從海岸新的風場【輸送】到北方的大城市，那些城市距離海邊大約兩百公里。"},{"w":"convert","p":"v.","d":"to change something into a different form","c":"轉換；轉變","s":"A: How do the panels on the roof of the shopping mall actually help reduce the monthly electricity bill for the store owners? B: The panels convert sunlight into electricity during the day, which powers the lights and escalators, so the mall buys much less power from the city and passes the savings to tenants.","t":"A：購物中心屋頂上的板子實際上是怎麼幫店家降低每月電費的？ B：這些板子白天把陽光【轉換】成電力，供應照明和手扶梯使用，所以購物中心向市電購買的電少很多，並把省下的錢回饋給租戶。"},{"w":"generate","p":"v.","d":"to produce energy such as electricity or heat","c":"產生；發（電）","s":"A: Is it true that the new sports stadium can produce its own electricity, even during big evening games with thousands of fans? B: Yes, the solar roof and small wind turbines generate enough power for the lights and screens on most days, and the stadium only buys extra electricity during the winter months.","t":"A：新體育館真的能自己發電嗎？即使是晚上有數千名球迷的大型比賽也可以？ B：是的，太陽能屋頂和小型風力渦輪機大多數日子都能【產生】足夠電力供應照明和螢幕，體育館只有在冬季幾個月才需要額外買電。"},{"w":"distribute","p":"v.","d":"to give or send something out to different people or places","c":"分配；配送","s":"A: After the earthquake, how did the city government make sure that the hospitals and schools still had electricity? B: Officials set up a plan to distribute power from the remaining stations to the most important buildings first, and then slowly restored it to homes and shops over the next few days.","t":"A：地震過後，市政府是怎麼確保醫院和學校仍然有電的？ B：官員擬定計畫，先把剩餘電廠的電力【分配】給最重要的建築物，接著在之後幾天慢慢恢復住家和商店的供電。"},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"working well without wasting energy, time, or money","c":"有效率的；節能的","s":"A: Should we buy the cheaper refrigerators for the staff kitchens, or spend a little more on the newer models from the other supplier? B: I think we should choose the newer models, because they are much more energy efficient and will save us a lot of money on electricity over the next ten years.","t":"A：我們該為員工廚房買比較便宜的冰箱，還是多花一點錢買另一家供應商的新機型？ B：我認為我們應該選新機型，因為它們在能源上【有效率】得多，未來十年能幫我們省下很多電費。"},{"w":"energetic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and very active","c":"精力充沛的","s":"A: Who is going to lead the tour of the new solar power plant for the visiting investors next Friday morning? B: The manager chose Kevin, because he is very energetic and friendly, knows the equipment well, and can keep a large group interested even during a long walk around the site in hot weather.","t":"A：下週五早上誰要帶來訪的投資人參觀新的太陽能發電廠？ B：經理選了凱文，因為他非常【精力充沛】又友善，熟悉設備，即使在炎熱天氣中繞場長時間走動，也能讓一大群人保持興趣。"}]},{"unit":122,"theme":"English Lesson 英語課","cards":[{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"a period of time in which someone is taught something","c":"課；一堂課","s":"A: Are you coming to the English lesson that the company offers every Thursday afternoon, or do you have to meet the clients from Osaka again? B: I will be there, because my manager wants me to improve my speaking before I lead the sales meeting with our overseas partners next month.","t":"A：你會來參加公司每週四下午開設的英語【課】嗎？還是你又要和大阪來的客戶開會？ B：我會去，因為我的經理希望我在下個月主持和海外合作夥伴的業務會議之前，先加強我的口說能力。"},{"w":"teacher","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to teach","c":"老師；教師","s":"A: Who is going to run the new business English class for the staff in the customer service department, and when will it start? B: The training office has hired an experienced teacher from a language school downtown, and she will start next Monday morning in the large meeting room on the third floor.","t":"A：誰要負責為客服部門員工開設新的商用英語課，什麼時候開始？ B：訓練處已經從市中心一家語言學校聘請了一位經驗豐富的【老師】，她下週一早上會在三樓的大會議室開始上課。"},{"w":"student","p":"n.","d":"a person who is studying at a school or university","c":"學生","s":"A: Why is the new intern so quiet during our team meetings, even though everyone says he is very smart and hardworking? B: He is still a university student who studies marketing part-time, so he feels nervous about speaking in front of senior staff, but he writes excellent reports and learns very quickly.","t":"A：為什麼新來的實習生在我們團隊會議中這麼安靜，明明大家都說他很聰明又勤奮？ B：他還是一名兼職修讀行銷的大學【學生】，所以在資深員工面前發言會緊張，但他寫的報告很出色，學得也很快。"},{"w":"classroom","p":"n.","d":"a room where classes are taught","c":"教室","s":"A: Where will the English training session for the new sales staff take place this week, since the main conference hall is being painted? B: The human resources team has booked a small classroom at the community center across the street, and they will provide a projector, a whiteboard, and free coffee for everyone.","t":"A：既然主會議廳正在油漆，這週新進業務人員的英語培訓課要在哪裡上？ B：人資團隊已經預訂了對街社區中心的一間小【教室】，他們會提供投影機、白板，還有免費咖啡給大家。"},{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"all the subjects and topics taught in a course","c":"課程（內容）","s":"A: Has the training department decided what topics the new English course for our engineers will cover this year? B: Yes, they designed a curriculum that focuses on writing clear e-mails, giving short presentations, and handling phone calls with international suppliers, because those are the skills our engineers use most often.","t":"A：訓練部門決定今年為工程師開設的新英語課程要涵蓋哪些主題了嗎？ B：決定了，他們設計了一套【課程】，著重於撰寫清楚的電子郵件、做簡短的簡報，以及和國際供應商通電話，因為這些是我們的工程師最常用到的技能。"},{"w":"textbook","p":"n.","d":"a book used for studying a subject","c":"課本；教科書","s":"A: Do I need to buy anything before the business English class starts on Monday, or will the company provide all the materials? B: The company will give each participant a free textbook with useful dialogues for meetings and phone calls, but you should bring a notebook and a pen to take notes during class.","t":"A：週一商用英語課開始前，我需要買什麼東西嗎？還是公司會提供所有的教材？ B：公司會發給每位學員一本免費的【課本】，裡面有會議和電話中實用的對話，不過你上課時應該帶筆記本和筆來做筆記。"},{"w":"worksheet","p":"n.","d":"a sheet of paper with questions or tasks for learners","c":"學習單；練習卷","s":"A: What should we do while the trainer is busy helping the new employees in the back of the room? B: She asked us to complete the worksheet on our desks, which has twenty short questions about polite phrases for meetings, and then compare our answers with a partner before the break.","t":"A：訓練師在教室後面忙著協助新員工時，我們該做什麼？ B：她要我們完成桌上的【學習單】，上面有二十個關於會議禮貌用語的簡短問題，然後在休息前和夥伴對答案。"},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work given to someone as part of a course or job","c":"作業；指派的任務","s":"A: Why are you staying late at the office tonight when the project report is not due until next week? B: My English trainer gave us a writing assignment about our company's products, and I want to finish it carefully tonight because I will be traveling to visit clients for the rest of the week.","t":"A：專案報告下週才要交，你為什麼今晚還留在辦公室加班？ B：我的英語訓練師給了我們一份介紹公司產品的寫作【作業】，我想今晚好好把它完成，因為這週剩下的時間我都要出差拜訪客戶。"},{"w":"homework","p":"n.","d":"work that a learner is given to do at home","c":"回家作業；功課","s":"A: Do you think the evening English course is too difficult for people who work full-time and have families to take care of? B: Not really, because the trainer only gives a little homework each week, usually a short e-mail to write, so most of us can finish it during our lunch break.","t":"A：你覺得晚間英語課程對全職工作又要照顧家庭的人來說會不會太難？ B：其實還好，因為訓練師每週只出一點點【回家作業】，通常是寫一封簡短的電子郵件，所以我們大多數人都能在午休時完成。"},{"w":"exercise","p":"n.","d":"an activity or set of questions done to practice a skill","c":"練習；練習題","s":"A: How did the trainer help you prepare for the difficult phone calls with angry customers in yesterday's workshop? B: She gave us a role-play exercise in which one person acted as an upset customer and the other had to stay calm, listen carefully, and offer a polite solution within three minutes.","t":"A：昨天的研習中，訓練師是怎麼幫你們準備應對憤怒客戶的困難電話的？ B：她讓我們做了一個角色扮演【練習】，其中一個人扮演不高興的客戶，另一個人必須保持冷靜、仔細聆聽，並在三分鐘內提出有禮貌的解決方法。"},{"w":"vocabulary","p":"n.","d":"all the words a person knows or uses","c":"字彙；詞彙","s":"A: Why do you always carry that small notebook to the weekly meetings with our partners from London? B: I write down every new business word I hear, because I want to build my vocabulary before the big contract negotiation next spring, and I review the list on the train every morning.","t":"A：你為什麼每週和倫敦合作夥伴開會時都帶著那本小筆記本？ B：我會把聽到的每個新商業用字都記下來，因為我想在明年春天的大型合約談判之前增加我的【字彙】量，而且我每天早上都會在火車上複習這份清單。"},{"w":"grammar","p":"n.","d":"the rules for putting words together in a language","c":"文法","s":"A: Could you check this e-mail to our new supplier in Canada before I send it this afternoon? B: Sure, the message is clear and polite, but there are a few grammar mistakes with past tenses in the second paragraph, so let me fix them quickly before you click the send button.","t":"A：你可以在我今天下午寄出之前，幫我檢查這封給加拿大新供應商的電子郵件嗎？ B：當然，內容清楚又有禮貌，但第二段有幾個過去式的【文法】錯誤，我先快速幫你改好，你再按下寄出。"},{"w":"pronunciation","p":"n.","d":"the way a word is said","c":"發音","s":"A: Why did the clients from Texas look confused when our new manager introduced the product during the video call? B: His ideas were excellent, but his pronunciation of some technical words was unclear, so the trainer is helping him practice slowly with recordings every afternoon before the next meeting.","t":"A：我們的新經理在視訊會議中介紹產品時，德州來的客戶為什麼看起來很困惑？ B：他的想法很棒，但一些技術用字的【發音】不清楚，所以訓練師每天下午都用錄音幫他慢慢練習，為下次會議做準備。"},{"w":"spelling","p":"n.","d":"the way letters are put together to form a word","c":"拼字；拼法","s":"A: Did the marketing team find any problems in the new brochure before they sent it to the printing company? B: Yes, they found a spelling mistake in the name of our main product on the front cover, so they corrected it right away and asked the printer to wait one more day.","t":"A：行銷團隊在把新手冊送去印刷公司之前，有發現任何問題嗎？ B：有，他們發現封面上我們主要產品名稱有一個【拼字】錯誤，所以馬上更正，並請印刷廠多等一天。"},{"w":"listening","p":"n.","d":"the skill of understanding spoken language","c":"聽力","s":"A: What part of the English test do most of our new employees find the hardest when they apply for overseas positions? B: Most of them say the listening section is the most difficult, because the speakers in the recordings talk quickly and use different accents from Britain, Australia, and the United States.","t":"A：我們的新員工申請海外職位時，大多認為英語測驗的哪一部分最難？ B：他們大多說【聽力】部分最難，因為錄音中的說話者講得很快，而且使用英國、澳洲和美國等不同的口音。"},{"w":"speaking","p":"n.","d":"the skill of talking in a language","c":"口說；說話","s":"A: Why did the human resources manager ask every applicant to have a short conversation in English during the interview? B: The job involves meeting foreign visitors every day, so she wants to check each person's speaking ability and see whether they can answer questions clearly and confidently without notes.","t":"A：人資經理為什麼在面試時要求每位應徵者用英語簡短對話？ B：這份工作每天都要接待外國訪客，所以她想確認每個人的【口說】能力，看看他們能不能不看筆記就清楚又有自信地回答問題。"},{"w":"reading","p":"n.","d":"the activity or skill of looking at and understanding written words","c":"閱讀","s":"A: How can I get better at understanding the long contracts and technical reports that our overseas partners send us? B: I suggest doing some extra reading every evening, such as business news articles online, because it will help you learn common phrases and understand long documents much faster at work.","t":"A：我要怎麼樣才能更容易看懂海外合作夥伴寄來的長篇合約和技術報告？ B：我建議你每天晚上做一些額外的【閱讀】，例如網路上的商業新聞文章，因為這能幫你學會常用片語，在工作上更快理解長篇文件。"},{"w":"writing","p":"n.","d":"the skill or activity of putting ideas into written words","c":"寫作","s":"A: Why did the manager ask Kevin to take the business English course even though he speaks well in meetings? B: Kevin is very good at talking with clients, but his writing is weak, and several of his e-mails and reports last month were confusing, so the course will help him organize his ideas.","t":"A：Kevin在會議中英語講得很好，為什麼經理還要他去上商用英語課？ B：Kevin很擅長和客戶交談，但他的【寫作】能力較弱，上個月他寫的幾封電子郵件和報告都讓人看不懂，所以這門課能幫助他整理想法。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a conversation in which people share ideas about a topic","c":"討論","s":"A: What did you do in the second half of the English workshop after the trainer finished explaining the new expressions? B: We formed small groups and had a discussion about how to reduce delivery delays, and each group had to use at least five of the new expressions before sharing its ideas.","t":"A：訓練師講解完新的用語後，英語研習的後半段你們做了什麼？ B：我們分成小組，針對如何減少送貨延誤進行【討論】，每一組在分享想法之前都必須用到至少五個新用語。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk that gives information to a group of people","c":"簡報；報告","s":"A: Are you ready for the meeting with the investors from Singapore tomorrow morning, or do you need more time to prepare? B: I have finished the slides, but I still want to practice my presentation with the English trainer this afternoon, because I need to explain our sales plan clearly in only fifteen minutes.","t":"A：明天早上和新加坡投資人的會議你準備好了嗎？還是需要更多時間準備？ B：投影片我已經做好了，但我今天下午還想和英語訓練師演練我的【簡報】，因為我必須在短短十五分鐘內把我們的銷售計畫說明清楚。"},{"w":"quiz","p":"n.","d":"a short test","c":"小考；測驗","s":"A: Why is everyone in the training room studying their notes so carefully during the coffee break this morning? B: The trainer announced that there will be a short quiz on the new customer service phrases after the break, and the three people with the highest scores will win free movie tickets.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上休息時間訓練室裡每個人都那麼認真看筆記？ B：訓練師宣布休息後會有一個關於新客服用語的簡短【小考】，分數最高的三個人可以贏得免費電影票。"},{"w":"test","p":"n.","d":"a set of questions to measure someone's skill or knowledge","c":"測驗；考試","s":"A: Do I need any special qualifications before I can apply for the new position at our office in Sydney? B: Yes, every applicant must pass an English test with a high score, and the company will pay the fee if you take it before the end of this month.","t":"A：申請雪梨辦公室的新職位前，我需要具備什麼特別的資格嗎？ B：需要，每位應徵者都必須以高分通過一項英語【測驗】，如果你在這個月底前參加，公司會支付報名費。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"comments about how well someone has done something","c":"意見回饋；反饋","s":"A: How did the trainer respond after you gave your sales presentation in English at the end of yesterday's workshop? B: She gave me some useful feedback, saying my slides were clear and well organized, but I should speak more slowly and look at the audience more often instead of reading from my notes.","t":"A：昨天研習結束時你用英語做了業務簡報之後，訓練師怎麼回應？ B：她給了我一些很有用的【意見回饋】，說我的投影片清楚又有條理，但我應該講慢一點，並且多看觀眾，而不是一直看著筆記唸。"},{"w":"correction","p":"n.","d":"a change that makes something right","c":"更正；訂正","s":"A: Did you notice that the price of the new printer was wrong in the e-mail we sent to all of our customers this morning? B: Yes, the sales manager noticed it at lunch, so we will send a correction this afternoon with the right price and a short apology for the confusion.","t":"A：你有注意到我們今天早上寄給所有客戶的電子郵件中，新印表機的價格寫錯了嗎？ B：有，業務經理午餐時發現了，所以我們今天下午會寄出一封【更正】信，附上正確價格並為造成的困擾簡短道歉。"},{"w":"practice","p":"n.","d":"doing something again and again to get better at it","c":"練習","s":"A: How did you become so confident at answering the phone in English when you joined the company only six months ago? B: It took a lot of practice, because I recorded myself every evening, listened to my mistakes, and asked friendly coworkers to call me with difficult questions during quiet afternoons.","t":"A：你六個月前才進公司，怎麼能這麼有自信地用英語接電話？ B：那需要大量的【練習】，因為我每天晚上都錄下自己的聲音，聽自己的錯誤，還請友善的同事在不忙的下午打電話問我一些困難的問題。"},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity","c":"參與；參加","s":"A: Is the weekly English workshop only for people in the marketing department, or can someone from accounting join too? B: Everyone in the company is welcome to participate, but you need to sign up with the human resources office by Friday, because each group is limited to twelve people.","t":"A：每週的英語研習只開放給行銷部門的人嗎？還是會計部的人也可以加入？ B：公司裡的每個人都歡迎【參加】，但你必須在週五前向人資辦公室報名，因為每組限額十二人。"},{"w":"review","p":"v.","d":"to look at or study something again","c":"複習；檢閱","s":"A: What are you planning to do before the English interview for the team leader position next Wednesday morning? B: I am going to review my notes from the business English course and prepare short answers about my experience, because I want to sound calm and professional in front of the managers.","t":"A：下週三早上團隊主管職位的英語面試之前，你打算做什麼準備？ B：我打算【複習】商用英語課的筆記，並準備一些關於我工作經驗的簡短回答，因為我想在主管們面前表現得冷靜又專業。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear and easy to understand","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Why did the new staff members look so confused after the meeting about the updated travel expense rules this morning? B: The finance manager spoke too fast, so I asked her to explain the new rules again in simple English and send everyone a short summary with examples by e-mail.","t":"A：今天早上關於新版差旅費規定的會議結束後，新進員工為什麼看起來那麼困惑？ B：財務經理講得太快了，所以我請她用簡單的英語再【解釋】一次新規定，並用電子郵件寄給大家一份附有例子的簡短摘要。"},{"w":"translate","p":"v.","d":"to change words from one language into another","c":"翻譯","s":"A: Our new customers in Mexico cannot read Chinese, so what should we do with the product manual before the shipment leaves next week? B: We should hire a professional company to translate the manual into English and Spanish, so customers can understand the safety instructions and set up the machine correctly.","t":"A：我們在墨西哥的新客戶看不懂中文，下週出貨前，產品手冊該怎麼處理？ B：我們應該請專業公司把手冊【翻譯】成英文和西班牙文，讓客戶能看懂安全說明並正確安裝機器。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information or ideas with others","c":"溝通；傳達","s":"A: Why does the company want all the warehouse supervisors to take a basic English course this year? B: We now work with drivers and suppliers from several countries, so supervisors must be able to communicate clearly with them about delivery times, safety rules, and problems that happen during busy seasons.","t":"A：公司為什麼希望今年所有倉庫主管都去上基礎英語課？ B：我們現在和來自好幾個國家的司機及供應商合作，所以主管必須能夠清楚地和他們【溝通】送貨時間、安全規定，以及旺季時發生的問題。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"involving people doing things together, not just listening","c":"互動的","s":"A: Why do the employees enjoy the new English training program so much more than the old one with long lectures? B: The new program is very interactive, because people play language games, answer questions on their phones, and work in pairs instead of just sitting and listening to the trainer for two hours.","t":"A：為什麼員工比起以前那種長篇講課，更喜歡新的英語培訓課程？ B：新課程非常【互動】，因為大家會玩語言遊戲、用手機回答問題，並兩人一組練習，而不是只坐著聽訓練師講兩個小時。"},{"w":"educational","p":"adj.","d":"helping people learn","c":"教育性的；有教育意義的","s":"A: Do you think the children of our employees will enjoy the company's family day at the science museum next Saturday? B: Yes, the museum has many educational activities about energy and space, and the staff there give short talks in simple English, so both parents and children can learn something new together.","t":"A：你覺得員工的孩子會喜歡下週六公司在科學博物館舉辦的家庭日嗎？ B：會的，博物館有很多關於能源和太空的【教育性】活動，那裡的工作人員還會用簡單的英語做簡短解說，讓家長和孩子都能一起學到新東西。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"serious and polite, used in official situations","c":"正式的","s":"A: Should I start my e-mail to the new director of our partner company in Germany with \"Hi\" and his first name? B: No, it is better to use a more formal greeting, such as \"Dear Mr. Weber,\" because this is your first message to him and he is a senior manager whom you have never met.","t":"A：我寫給德國合作公司新任董事的電子郵件，開頭可以用「Hi」加上他的名字嗎？ B：不行，最好用比較【正式】的問候語，例如「Dear Mr. Weber,」，因為這是你第一次寫信給他，而且他是你從未見過的資深經理。"},{"w":"informal","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and friendly, not official","c":"非正式的；輕鬆的","s":"A: What should I wear and how should I behave at the welcome party for the new team members on Friday evening? B: The party is quite informal, so jeans and a nice shirt are fine, and you can chat with your coworkers about hobbies and weekend plans instead of talking about work.","t":"A：週五晚上新成員的歡迎派對，我該穿什麼、該怎麼表現？ B：那個派對相當【非正式】，所以穿牛仔褲配一件好看的襯衫就可以了，你也可以和同事聊聊嗜好和週末計畫，而不用談工作。"},{"w":"fluently","p":"adv.","d":"in a smooth and easy way, without stopping","c":"流利地","s":"A: Why did the hotel decide to hire Maria as the new front desk manager instead of the other three applicants? B: She has eight years of experience in hospitality, and she speaks English, Japanese, and Spanish fluently, so she can help guests from many countries check in quickly and answer their questions.","t":"A：飯店為什麼決定聘請Maria擔任新的櫃檯經理，而不是另外三位應徵者？ B：她有八年的餐旅業經驗，而且能【流利地】說英語、日語和西班牙語，所以能協助來自許多國家的旅客快速辦理入住並回答他們的問題。"}]},{"unit":123,"theme":"Entertainment 娛樂","cards":[{"w":"amusement","p":"n.","d":"enjoyment from something fun; fun activities","c":"娛樂；樂趣；消遣","s":"A: Why did the company choose a seaside hotel for the annual staff trip instead of the mountain resort we visited last year? B: The seaside hotel has a large amusement park right next door, so employees can bring their children, enjoy the rides together, and still attend the training sessions in the afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼公司這次員工旅遊選擇海邊的飯店，而不是我們去年去過的山上度假村？ B：海邊飯店旁邊就有一座大型【遊樂】園，所以員工可以帶孩子一起玩遊樂設施，下午還能參加培訓課程。"},{"w":"fun","p":"n.","d":"enjoyment; a good time","c":"樂趣；好玩的事","s":"A: How was the team-building day that the human resources department organized at the riverside park last Saturday? B: It was a lot of fun, because we played outdoor games in small groups, shared a barbecue lunch, and got to know colleagues from other departments whom we rarely meet at the office.","t":"A：人資部門上週六在河濱公園舉辦的團隊建立活動怎麼樣？ B：非常【好玩】，因為我們分成小組玩戶外遊戲、一起吃烤肉午餐，還認識了平常在辦公室很少碰到的其他部門同事。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"free time when you are not working","c":"閒暇；休閒","s":"A: Now that the new office building is finished, what will the empty space on the top floor be used for? B: Management plans to turn it into a leisure area with sofas, board games, and a coffee machine, so staff can relax during their breaks and feel less stressed after long meetings.","t":"A：既然新辦公大樓已經完工，頂樓那塊空間要做什麼用？ B：管理階層打算把它改成【休閒】區，擺上沙發、桌遊和咖啡機，讓員工在休息時間放鬆，開完冗長的會議後也比較不會有壓力。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities people do for enjoyment in their free time","c":"休閒娛樂；消遣","s":"A: I heard the city council approved a large budget for the old factory site near the river, but what exactly will they build there? B: They are going to build a public recreation center with a swimming pool, tennis courts, and a jogging path, which should attract families and create jobs for local residents.","t":"A：我聽說市議會為河邊那塊舊工廠用地通過了一大筆預算，他們到底要在那裡蓋什麼？ B：他們要蓋一座公共【休閒娛樂】中心，有游泳池、網球場和慢跑步道，應該能吸引家庭前來，也能為當地居民創造工作機會。"},{"w":"show","p":"n.","d":"a performance on stage, TV, or radio","c":"表演；節目","s":"A: Are you free on Friday evening, or do you have to stay late to finish the sales report for the regional manager? B: I should be finished by six, so I'd love to join you, especially if we can grab a quick dinner before the show starts at the theater downtown.","t":"A：你週五晚上有空嗎？還是你得留下來加班完成給區域經理的銷售報告？ B：我應該六點前就能做完，所以很樂意跟你去，尤其如果我們能在市中心劇院的【表演】開始前先快速吃個晚餐的話。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"an act of playing music, dancing, or acting for an audience","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: Did the client from Tokyo enjoy the evening we planned for him after the contract was signed yesterday? B: Yes, he loved it, and he said the traditional dance performance at the cultural center was the highlight of his trip, so he even asked our assistant to buy tickets for his wife.","t":"A：昨天簽完合約後，我們為那位東京來的客戶安排的晚上行程，他喜歡嗎？ B：是的，他非常喜歡，還說文化中心的傳統舞蹈【表演】是他這趟旅程的亮點，他甚至請我們的助理幫他太太也買票。"},{"w":"concert","p":"n.","d":"a public event where people play music","c":"音樂會；演唱會","s":"A: Why is the hotel lobby so crowded tonight, and why are there so many young people waiting at the front desk? B: A famous rock band is holding a concert at the stadium across the street, so most of the rooms are fully booked and the staff are working extra hours to check everyone in.","t":"A：今晚飯店大廳怎麼這麼擁擠？為什麼有這麼多年輕人在櫃檯排隊？ B：一個知名搖滾樂團在對街的體育館舉辦【演唱會】，所以大部分房間都被訂滿了，員工也正在加班幫大家辦理入住。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special event or celebration, often with music, food, or films","c":"節慶；藝術節；慶典","s":"A: Our sales at the downtown café doubled last weekend, but do you know what caused such a sudden increase in customers? B: The city held its annual three-day lantern festival in the square right outside our shop, so thousands of visitors stopped by for coffee between the stage shows and parades.","t":"A：我們市中心咖啡店上週末的營業額翻倍了，你知道是什麼造成顧客突然增加嗎？ B：市政府在我們店外的廣場舉辦一年一度、為期三天的燈籠【節】，所以成千上萬的遊客在舞台表演和遊行之間進來買咖啡。"},{"w":"theater","p":"n.","d":"a building where plays and shows are performed","c":"劇院；戲院","s":"A: Where should we take the overseas partners after the dinner on Thursday, since they said they want to experience some local culture? B: Let's take them to the new theater near the train station, because it offers plays with English subtitles and the seats are comfortable enough for a two-hour evening program.","t":"A：週四晚餐後我們要帶海外合作夥伴去哪裡？他們說想體驗一些在地文化。 B：我們帶他們去火車站附近新開的【劇院】吧，那裡的戲劇有英文字幕，座位也很舒服，適合兩小時的晚間節目。"},{"w":"cinema","p":"n.","d":"a building where people watch films","c":"電影院","s":"A: The shopping mall's visitor numbers dropped sharply last year, so what is the management team planning to do about it? B: They are going to open a modern cinema with ten screens on the top floor, hoping that people who come to watch films will also eat and shop there.","t":"A：購物中心去年的來客數大幅下滑，管理團隊打算怎麼處理？ B：他們準備在頂樓開一家有十個影廳的現代化【電影院】，希望來看電影的人也會順便在那裡用餐購物。"},{"w":"movie","p":"n.","d":"a film","c":"電影","s":"A: Have you decided what we should do for the department's monthly social night, since the budget is quite small this time? B: I suggest borrowing the conference room projector and showing a well-known movie with free popcorn, because it is cheap, easy to organize, and most colleagues can stay after work.","t":"A：這次預算很少，部門每月的聯誼之夜你決定要做什麼了嗎？ B：我建議借會議室的投影機，放一部知名【電影】並提供免費爆米花，因為便宜、好安排，而且大多數同事下班後都能留下來。"},{"w":"television","p":"n.","d":"a system or machine for watching programs at home","c":"電視","s":"A: Why does the marketing department want to spend so much of this year's budget on a single advertisement? B: The ad will appear on national television during the baseball finals, when millions of families are watching at home, so the manager believes it will greatly increase sales of our new sports drink.","t":"A：為什麼行銷部門要把今年這麼多預算花在單一支廣告上？ B：這支廣告會在棒球總決賽期間於全國【電視】播出，那時有數百萬個家庭在家收看，所以經理相信它會大幅提升我們新運動飲料的銷量。"},{"w":"series","p":"n.","d":"a set of TV programs with the same characters or subject","c":"系列節目；影集","s":"A: You look really tired this morning, so did you stay up late working on the budget proposal again? B: Actually, no, I started watching a new crime series online last night and couldn't stop until I finished six episodes, so I only slept for about four hours before my alarm rang.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來很累，昨晚又熬夜做預算提案了嗎？ B：其實沒有，我昨晚在網路上開始看一部新的犯罪【影集】，一口氣看完六集停不下來，所以鬧鐘響之前只睡了大約四個小時。"},{"w":"comedy","p":"n.","d":"a funny play, film, or show that makes people laugh","c":"喜劇","s":"A: The atmosphere in the office has been very tense since the restructuring, so do you have any ideas for the year-end party? B: How about inviting a local comedy group to perform for thirty minutes, since a lot of laughter could help everyone relax and feel more connected to each other again?","t":"A：自從組織重整後，辦公室氣氛一直很緊繃，你對尾牙有什麼點子嗎？ B：邀請一個本地【喜劇】團體來表演三十分鐘怎麼樣？大量的笑聲可能幫助大家放鬆，彼此也能再次感覺更親近。"},{"w":"drama","p":"n.","d":"a play or show with actors, often serious","c":"戲劇；劇","s":"A: Why did the training department hire actors for next week's customer service workshop instead of using the usual videos? B: The trainers believe that a short drama about an angry customer will be more realistic and memorable, so new employees can practice calm responses after watching the actors on stage.","t":"A：為什麼訓練部門下週的客服工作坊要請演員，而不是用平常的影片？ B：培訓師認為一齣關於憤怒顧客的短【劇】會更真實、更令人印象深刻，新進員工看完台上演員的演出後，就能練習冷靜地回應。"},{"w":"musical","p":"n.","d":"a play or film with a lot of singing and dancing","c":"音樂劇","s":"A: Is it true that the travel agency is offering a special package for tourists who visit London this spring? B: Yes, the package includes three nights at a central hotel, breakfast every morning, and two tickets to a famous musical with plenty of singing and dancing in the West End.","t":"A：旅行社今年春天真的有為去倫敦的遊客推出特別套裝行程嗎？ B：是的，套裝包含市中心飯店三晚住宿、每天早餐，以及兩張西區一齣充滿歌舞的知名【音樂劇】門票。"},{"w":"game","p":"n.","d":"a sports match or an activity played with rules","c":"比賽；遊戲","s":"A: Why were so many staff members late to work this morning, even though the trains were running on time? B: The national team played an important baseball game that ended after midnight, so many people stayed up to watch it on television and then overslept because they were too tired.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有這麼多員工遲到？火車明明都準時啊。 B：國家隊打了一場重要的棒球【比賽】，過了午夜才結束，所以很多人熬夜看電視轉播，結果太累而睡過頭。"},{"w":"sport","p":"n.","d":"a physical activity or game with rules","c":"運動；體育活動","s":"A: The new employee wellness program looks great, but which activities is the company paying for this year? B: The company will cover the cost of one team sport, such as basketball or volleyball, because the HR manager believes playing together improves both health and communication between departments.","t":"A：新的員工健康計畫看起來很棒，今年公司會補助哪些活動？ B：公司會負擔一項團隊【運動】的費用，例如籃球或排球，因為人資經理認為一起運動能同時改善健康以及部門之間的溝通。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"嗜好；業餘愛好","s":"A: You always seem so calm, even when the deadlines at the office are extremely tight, so what is your secret? B: Gardening is my favorite hobby, so every weekend I spend a few hours planting vegetables on my balcony, and it helps me forget about work and feel ready for Monday.","t":"A：即使辦公室的截止期限非常緊迫，你似乎總是很冷靜，你的祕訣是什麼？ B：園藝是我最喜歡的【嗜好】，所以每個週末我都會花幾個小時在陽台種菜，這讓我忘掉工作，為週一做好準備。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"sounds arranged in a pleasant way, played or sung","c":"音樂","s":"A: Customers have complained that our restaurant feels too quiet and uncomfortable during dinner, so what should we change first? B: Let's play some soft jazz music in the background and dim the lights a little, because a warmer atmosphere will encourage guests to stay longer and order dessert.","t":"A：顧客抱怨我們餐廳在晚餐時段太安靜、讓人不自在，我們應該先改變什麼？ B：我們在背景播放一些輕柔的爵士【音樂】，再把燈光調暗一點，因為更溫馨的氣氛會讓客人待久一點並點甜點。"},{"w":"dance","p":"n.","d":"a set of steps and movements done to music","c":"舞蹈；舞","s":"A: The hotel ballroom is booked for the company's anniversary dinner, but what kind of entertainment have you arranged for the guests? B: After the speeches, a professional band will play, and we have hired an instructor to teach everyone a simple group dance, so even shy employees can join in comfortably.","t":"A：飯店宴會廳已經訂好要辦公司週年晚宴，你為賓客安排了什麼樣的娛樂？ B：致詞結束後會有專業樂團演奏，我們還請了一位老師教大家一支簡單的團體【舞】，讓就算是害羞的員工也能自在地參與。"},{"w":"art","p":"n.","d":"paintings, photos, sculptures, and other creative works","c":"藝術；藝術品","s":"A: The new head office looks rather plain, so has the design team decided how to decorate the long hallway near the entrance? B: They are going to display modern art by local painters and photographers, which will make the space more attractive and also support young creative people in our city.","t":"A：新總部看起來有點單調，設計團隊決定好要怎麼裝飾入口附近的長走廊了嗎？ B：他們打算展示本地畫家和攝影師的現代【藝術】作品，這會讓空間更有吸引力，也能支持我們城市裡年輕的創作者。"},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"books, poems, and plays, especially ones of high quality","c":"文學；文學作品","s":"A: Why is the bookstore chain hosting reading events every Saturday afternoon this month? B: Sales of classic literature have been falling for years, so the company invited well-known authors to discuss famous novels with readers, hoping to attract more young customers and build a loyal community of book lovers.","t":"A：為什麼那家連鎖書店這個月每週六下午都舉辦閱讀活動？ B：經典【文學】作品的銷量多年來持續下滑，所以公司邀請知名作家和讀者討論著名小說，希望吸引更多年輕顧客，並建立忠實的愛書人社群。"},{"w":"broadcast","p":"v.","d":"to send out a program on TV, radio, or the internet","c":"播送；廣播；轉播","s":"A: Will the CEO's speech at the annual conference be available for employees working at our overseas branches? B: Yes, the IT team will broadcast it on our internal network at nine o'clock, and a recording will be posted later for staff in different time zones who cannot watch it at that time.","t":"A：執行長在年會上的演講，海外分公司的員工也看得到嗎？ B：可以，資訊團隊會在九點透過公司內部網路【播送】，之後也會上傳錄影，給那些因為時區不同而無法在當時觀看的員工。"},{"w":"stream","p":"v.","d":"to play video or music directly from the internet","c":"串流播放；線上直播","s":"A: The training seminar room only holds fifty people, so how can all two hundred sales representatives attend next week? B: We will stream the seminar online so that representatives in other cities can watch it on their laptops, and they can type questions to the speaker in the chat box.","t":"A：培訓研討室只能容納五十人，下週兩百位業務代表要怎麼全部參加？ B：我們會在線上【串流直播】這場研討會，讓其他城市的業務代表可以用筆電觀看，也能在聊天框裡打字向講者提問。"},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to sing, dance, act, or play music for an audience","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: The opening ceremony for our new factory is next Friday, but have we found any entertainers for the guests yet? B: Yes, a group of students from the local high school will perform traditional drum music for about fifteen minutes, which should create a lively and festive atmosphere for the visitors.","t":"A：新工廠的開幕典禮在下週五，我們找到為賓客表演的人了嗎？ B：找到了，一群本地高中的學生會【表演】大約十五分鐘的傳統鼓樂，應該能為來賓營造熱鬧又歡樂的氣氛。"},{"w":"entertain","p":"v.","d":"to give people a good time; to host guests","c":"招待；使娛樂","s":"A: The overseas buyers will arrive two days before the trade fair begins, so what should we do with them during that time? B: We could entertain them with a boat tour around the harbor and a seafood dinner, which would help us build a friendly relationship before the price negotiations start.","t":"A：海外買家會在商展開始前兩天抵達，那段時間我們該怎麼安排他們？ B：我們可以安排港口遊船和海鮮晚餐來【招待】他們，這有助於在價格談判開始前建立友好的關係。"},{"w":"enjoyable","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant and fun","c":"令人愉快的","s":"A: How did the guests feel about the cooking class we organized for the sales team's reward trip to Bangkok? B: Almost everyone said it was the most enjoyable part of the trip, because they learned to make local dishes, laughed a lot together, and ate the delicious meal they had prepared.","t":"A：我們為業務團隊的曼谷獎勵旅遊安排的烹飪課，參加的人覺得怎麼樣？ B：幾乎每個人都說那是整趟旅程中最【令人愉快】的部分，因為他們學會做當地料理、一起開懷大笑，還吃到了自己做的美味餐點。"},{"w":"exciting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel very happy and interested","c":"令人興奮的","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department talking so loudly and smiling this morning? B: The manager just announced some exciting news, because our company has been chosen as the official sponsor of the international film festival, which means our brand will be seen by millions of people.","t":"A：為什麼行銷部門的大家今天早上都講話這麼大聲、笑容滿面？ B：經理剛宣布了一個【令人興奮】的消息，我們公司被選為國際影展的官方贊助商，這代表我們的品牌將被數百萬人看見。"},{"w":"engaging","p":"adj.","d":"interesting and able to hold your attention","c":"吸引人的；引人入勝的","s":"A: The last training video was so boring that half the staff fell asleep, so how will the new one be different? B: The new video uses real stories, short quizzes, and funny characters to make the lessons more engaging, so employees will pay attention and remember the safety rules much better.","t":"A：上一支培訓影片太無聊，一半的員工都睡著了，新的這支會有什麼不同？ B：新影片用真實故事、小測驗和有趣的角色讓課程更【吸引人】，員工就會專心觀看，也更能記住安全規則。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的；流行的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant on the corner decide to stay open until midnight on weekends? B: Its new late-night dessert menu has become very popular with young office workers who go there after movies or concerts, so the owner hired extra staff to serve the crowds.","t":"A：為什麼轉角那家餐廳決定週末營業到午夜？ B：它新推出的深夜甜點菜單在年輕上班族之間非常【受歡迎】，他們看完電影或演唱會後會去那裡，所以老闆多請了員工來應付人潮。"},{"w":"live","p":"adj.","d":"performed or shown while it is actually happening, not recorded","c":"現場的；直播的","s":"A: Do you think the hotel restaurant is a good place to take the new clients on Friday night? B: Yes, I think so, because they have live jazz every Friday from seven to ten, the food is excellent, and the room is quiet enough for us to talk about the contract details.","t":"A：你覺得飯店餐廳適合週五晚上帶新客戶去嗎？ B：適合，因為他們每週五晚上七點到十點都有【現場】爵士樂演奏，食物也很棒，而且環境安靜，足以讓我們討論合約細節。"},{"w":"digital","p":"adj.","d":"using computers or electronic technology","c":"數位的","s":"A: Why are fewer customers buying DVDs and CDs at our electronics store these days? B: Most people now prefer digital entertainment, such as streaming films and downloading songs to their phones, so we should reduce our disc stock and give more shelf space to tablets and wireless headphones.","t":"A：為什麼最近在我們電子用品店買DVD和CD的顧客越來越少？ B：現在大多數人比較喜歡【數位】娛樂，例如串流看電影、把歌曲下載到手機裡，所以我們應該減少光碟庫存，把更多貨架空間留給平板和無線耳機。"},{"w":"entertainingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a fun and interesting way","c":"有趣地；令人愉快地","s":"A: Why do so many employees sign up for the finance director's workshops, even though the topic is usually boring numbers? B: She explains complex budgets so entertainingly with funny stories and real examples that everyone stays interested, and people actually leave the room understanding how the company spends its money.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多員工報名財務長的工作坊，即使主題通常是無聊的數字？ B：她用有趣的故事和真實例子把複雜的預算講解得非常【生動有趣】，讓每個人都保持興趣，大家離開時也真的了解公司是怎麼花錢的。"}]},{"unit":124,"theme":"Environment 環境","cards":[{"w":"air pollution","p":"n.phr.","d":"dirty or harmful things in the air","c":"空氣污染","s":"A: Why did the city government ask all the factories near the river to reduce their working hours during the coming holiday week? B: Because air pollution has reached a dangerous level this month, and doctors say that children and older people may have trouble breathing if they stay outside too long.","t":"A：為什麼市政府要求河邊附近所有的工廠在即將到來的假期週減少工作時數？ B：因為這個月的【空氣污染】已經達到危險的程度，醫生說如果兒童和老人在戶外待太久，可能會呼吸困難。"},{"w":"noise pollution","p":"n.phr.","d":"loud, unpleasant sounds that disturb people","c":"噪音污染","s":"A: Have the employees on the third floor been complaining again about the construction work going on next to our office building? B: Yes, the noise pollution from the drills and trucks starts at seven every morning, so several people have asked if they can work from home until the project is finished next month.","t":"A：三樓的員工又在抱怨我們辦公大樓旁邊正在進行的施工嗎？ B：是的，鑽孔機和卡車造成的【噪音污染】每天早上七點就開始了，所以有好幾個人詢問能否在下個月工程結束前在家工作。"},{"w":"marine pollution","p":"n.phr.","d":"harmful waste and chemicals in the sea","c":"海洋污染","s":"A: Why is our seafood restaurant changing its main supplier after working with the same fishing company for more than ten years? B: The manager read a report saying that marine pollution near their fishing area has become serious, and she does not want to take any risks with the quality and safety of our dishes.","t":"A：我們的海鮮餐廳為什麼在跟同一家漁業公司合作十多年後要更換主要供應商？ B：經理看到一份報告說他們捕魚區附近的【海洋污染】變得很嚴重，她不想在我們菜餚的品質和安全上冒任何風險。"},{"w":"overpopulation","p":"n.","d":"too many people living in one place","c":"人口過剩","s":"A: Why are housing prices and rents in the capital rising so quickly, even though the government has built many new apartment buildings this year? B: Many experts believe that overpopulation is the main reason, because more and more young people move there for jobs, and the city simply does not have enough space for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼首都的房價和房租漲得這麼快，即使政府今年已經蓋了很多新的公寓大樓？ B：許多專家認為【人口過剩】是主要原因，因為越來越多年輕人為了工作搬到那裡，而這座城市根本沒有足夠的空間容納所有人。"},{"w":"result","p":"n.","d":"something that happens because of something else","c":"結果","s":"A: Did the marketing team share the findings of the customer survey about our new recycling program at this morning's meeting? B: Yes, and the main result was very encouraging, since almost eighty percent of the people who answered said they would be happy to return used bottles to our stores every week.","t":"A：行銷團隊在今天早上的會議中有分享關於我們新回收計畫的顧客調查發現嗎？ B：有，主要的【結果】非常令人鼓舞，因為幾乎百分之八十的受訪者表示他們很樂意每週把用過的瓶子拿回我們的門市。"},{"w":"drain","p":"v.","d":"to flow away, or to make liquid flow away","c":"排水；流掉","s":"A: Why is the maintenance crew working in the parking lot so late this evening, and when will we be allowed to use it again? B: After yesterday's heavy storm, the water could not drain away properly because the pipes were blocked with leaves, so they need to clear them before the morning shift arrives.","t":"A：為什麼維修人員今晚這麼晚還在停車場工作？我們什麼時候才能再使用停車場？ B：昨天的暴風雨過後，因為管子被落葉堵住，水無法正常【排】走，所以他們必須在早班人員抵達之前把管子清通。"},{"w":"oxygen","p":"n.","d":"the gas in the air that people need to breathe","c":"氧氣","s":"A: Why does the new office design include so many large plants in the hallways and meeting rooms on every floor of the building? B: The designer explained that plants add oxygen to the air and remove some harmful chemicals, so the staff should feel fresher and more focused during long working days.","t":"A：為什麼新的辦公室設計在大樓每層樓的走廊和會議室都放了這麼多大型植物？ B：設計師解釋說植物會為空氣增加【氧氣】並去除一些有害化學物質，所以員工在漫長的工作日裡應該會覺得更有精神、更專注。"},{"w":"carbon dioxide","p":"n.phr.","d":"a gas that people and animals breathe out and that burning produces","c":"二氧化碳","s":"A: What exactly does the new sensor on the meeting room wall measure, and why did the facilities team decide to install it last week? B: It measures the level of carbon dioxide in the room, so when too many people breathe in a small space for hours, it reminds us to open the windows for fresh air.","t":"A：會議室牆上的新感測器到底在測量什麼？設施團隊為什麼上週決定安裝它？ B：它測量室內【二氧化碳】的濃度，所以當太多人在狹小的空間裡呼吸好幾個小時，它就會提醒我們打開窗戶讓新鮮空氣進來。"},{"w":"carbon emissions","p":"n.phr.","d":"carbon gases sent into the air by cars, factories, etc.","c":"碳排放","s":"A: Why has the company decided to replace all of its old delivery vans with electric vehicles over the next two years, even though they cost more? B: The board wants to cut our carbon emissions by half before 2030, and many of our biggest customers now prefer to work with suppliers that protect the environment.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定在未來兩年內把所有舊的送貨廂型車換成電動車，即使電動車比較貴？ B：董事會希望在2030年前把我們的【碳排放】減半，而且我們許多最大的客戶現在比較喜歡與保護環境的供應商合作。"},{"w":"climate change","p":"n.phr.","d":"long-term changes in the Earth's weather and temperature","c":"氣候變遷","s":"A: Why did the insurance company raise the price of our flood protection policy so much when we renewed the contract this spring? B: Their agent said that climate change is causing stronger storms and heavier rain in our area every year, so the risk of serious damage to our warehouse is much higher now.","t":"A：今年春天續約時，保險公司為什麼把我們的防洪保單價格調漲這麼多？ B：他們的業務員說【氣候變遷】讓我們地區每年的暴風雨更強、雨量更大，所以我們倉庫遭受嚴重損害的風險現在高很多。"},{"w":"environmentally friendly","p":"adj.phr.","d":"not harmful to the environment","c":"環保的；對環境友善的","s":"A: Have you decided which cleaning company we should hire for the new office, since the two price offers we received are almost the same? B: I prefer the second one because all of their products are environmentally friendly, and our staff have complained about the strong chemical smell left by the previous cleaners.","t":"A：既然我們收到的兩份報價幾乎一樣，你決定好新辦公室要雇用哪一家清潔公司了嗎？ B：我比較喜歡第二家，因為他們所有的產品都是【環保的】，而且我們的員工曾抱怨之前的清潔人員留下很重的化學味道。"},{"w":"waste disposal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the process of getting rid of garbage","c":"廢棄物處理","s":"A: Why is the restaurant's monthly operating cost so much higher than last year, even though our food and staff costs have stayed the same? B: The city introduced new rules for waste disposal, so we now pay a private company to collect our kitchen garbage and used oil three times a week.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳每月的營運成本比去年高出這麼多，即使我們的食材和人事成本都沒變？ B：市政府推出了新的【廢棄物處理】規定，所以我們現在要付錢請一家民營公司每週三次來收廚餘和廢油。"},{"w":"combustion","p":"n.","d":"the process of burning","c":"燃燒","s":"A: Why did the factory safety officer ask everyone to move the boxes of paper away from the heating equipment in the storage room yesterday? B: He explained that the high temperature could cause combustion if anything burnable stays too close to the machines, and a fire there would destroy most of our stock.","t":"A：工廠安全官昨天為什麼要求大家把紙箱搬離儲藏室的加熱設備？ B：他解釋說如果任何可燃物離機器太近，高溫可能引起【燃燒】，而那裡一旦發生火災會燒毀我們大部分的庫存。"},{"w":"automobiles","p":"n.","d":"cars","c":"汽車","s":"A: Why is the city planning to close the downtown shopping street to traffic every weekend starting next month? B: The mayor wants to reduce the number of automobiles in the busy center, so shoppers can walk safely, breathe cleaner air, and spend more time visiting the small local stores.","t":"A：為什麼市政府計畫從下個月開始每個週末封閉市中心購物街禁止車輛通行？ B：市長想減少繁忙市中心的【汽車】數量，讓購物者能安全地步行、呼吸更乾淨的空氣，並花更多時間逛當地的小商店。"},{"w":"potential","p":"adj.","d":"possible in the future","c":"潛在的；可能的","s":"A: Why did our team spend the whole afternoon visiting that small village outside the city instead of preparing the sales report? B: The director thinks it is a potential location for our new solar farm, because it gets lots of sunshine all year and the land there is quite cheap.","t":"A：為什麼我們團隊花了整個下午去參觀城外的那個小村莊，而不是準備銷售報告？ B：主管認為那裡是我們新太陽能發電廠的【潛在】地點，因為那裡全年日照充足，土地也相當便宜。"},{"w":"endanger","p":"v.","d":"to put someone or something in danger","c":"危及；使瀕臨危險","s":"A: Why did the local residents protest outside the city hall about the plan to build a new shopping mall near the lake last weekend? B: They believe the construction will endanger the rare birds that live there, and they also worry that the extra traffic will make the quiet neighborhood much noisier.","t":"A：上週末當地居民為什麼在市政府外抗議在湖邊興建新購物中心的計畫？ B：他們認為施工會【危及】住在那裡的稀有鳥類，而且他們也擔心額外的車流會讓這個安靜的社區變得吵雜許多。"},{"w":"ecosystem","p":"n.","d":"all the plants and animals in an area and how they live together","c":"生態系統","s":"A: Why does the tour company ask visitors to stay on the wooden paths when they walk through the wetland park during the guided tour? B: The guide says the ecosystem there is very delicate, and stepping on the plants can harm the insects, frogs, and birds that all depend on one another to survive.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社要求遊客在導覽行程中穿越濕地公園時要待在木棧道上？ B：導遊說那裡的【生態系統】非常脆弱，踩到植物可能會傷害昆蟲、青蛙和鳥類，而牠們都彼此依賴才能生存。"},{"w":"smog","p":"n.","d":"dirty air that looks like fog, found in cities","c":"霧霾；煙霧","s":"A: Why was this morning's outdoor sales event at the city park canceled at the last minute, after we had already set up all the tables? B: The government warned that thick smog would cover the city until the evening, so the organizers decided it was not safe for people to stand outside for hours.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上在市立公園的戶外促銷活動在我們已經擺好所有桌子之後臨時取消？ B：政府警告濃厚的【霧霾】會籠罩城市直到傍晚，所以主辦單位認為讓民眾在戶外站好幾個小時並不安全。"},{"w":"smoke","p":"n.","d":"the gray or black gas that comes from something burning","c":"煙","s":"A: Why did the fire alarm go off on the fifth floor during our training session this afternoon, and was anyone hurt? B: Nobody was hurt, but someone left toast in the machine in the staff kitchen, and the smoke quickly filled the hallway, so everyone had to leave the building for twenty minutes.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午我們培訓課程期間五樓的火災警報響了？有人受傷嗎？ B：沒有人受傷，但有人把吐司留在員工廚房的機器裡，【煙】很快就充滿了走廊，所以大家必須離開大樓二十分鐘。"},{"w":"hazardous","p":"adj.","d":"dangerous, especially to health or safety","c":"有害的；危險的","s":"A: Why do the workers in the laboratory have to attend a special safety class before they can start their first day on the job? B: They will handle hazardous chemicals that can burn the skin or cause serious illness, so they must learn how to store, use, and throw them away correctly.","t":"A：為什麼實驗室的工作人員在開始第一天上班前必須參加特別的安全課程？ B：他們會處理可能灼傷皮膚或導致嚴重疾病的【有害的】化學物質，所以他們必須學會如何正確地存放、使用和丟棄這些物質。"},{"w":"chronic","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time","c":"慢性的；長期的","s":"A: Why has the health insurance company started a new program that sends nurses to visit our older customers at home every month? B: Many of those customers suffer from chronic health problems, such as heart disease or breathing trouble, and regular visits help them manage their conditions before they become serious.","t":"A：為什麼健康保險公司開始了一項新計畫，每個月派護士到我們年長客戶的家中拜訪？ B：那些客戶當中有許多人患有【慢性的】健康問題，例如心臟病或呼吸困難，定期拜訪可以幫助他們在病情變嚴重前控制病況。"},{"w":"estimate","p":"v.","d":"to guess a number or amount carefully","c":"估計","s":"A: How much money do you think the company will save after we install solar panels on the roof of the main factory next year? B: The engineers estimate that we will cut our electricity bill by about thirty percent, but the exact amount will depend on the weather and how much we produce.","t":"A：你認為明年我們在主要工廠的屋頂上安裝太陽能板後，公司可以省下多少錢？ B：工程師【估計】我們的電費會減少大約百分之三十，但確切的金額將取決於天氣和我們的產量。"},{"w":"premature","p":"adj.","d":"happening too early","c":"過早的；提早的","s":"A: Why did the health department publish a new report about the air quality in our city's industrial areas this week? B: The report shows that dirty air causes thousands of premature deaths every year, so officials want factories to install better filters and use cleaner fuels as soon as possible.","t":"A：衛生部門這週為什麼發表一份關於我們城市工業區空氣品質的新報告？ B：報告顯示，骯髒的空氣每年造成數千人【過早的】死亡，所以官員希望工廠盡快安裝更好的過濾器並使用更乾淨的燃料。"},{"w":"deforestation","p":"n.","d":"the cutting down of large areas of forest","c":"森林砍伐","s":"A: Why did our furniture company stop buying wood from that supplier in South America, even though their prices were the lowest? B: We discovered that they were causing serious deforestation by clearing huge areas of rainforest, and our customers would be very upset if they knew we supported that.","t":"A：為什麼我們家具公司停止向那家南美洲的供應商購買木材，即使他們的價格最低？ B：我們發現他們砍伐大片雨林，造成嚴重的【森林砍伐】，如果顧客知道我們支持這種做法會非常不高興。"},{"w":"destroy","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it cannot be used","c":"摧毀；破壞","s":"A: Why is the farm owner so worried about the weather forecast for the coming weekend, when the harvest is almost finished? B: A strong typhoon is expected to hit the area on Saturday, and the heavy wind and rain could destroy the remaining crops before the workers can pick them.","t":"A：既然收成快結束了，農場主人為什麼還那麼擔心這個週末的天氣預報？ B：預計週六會有強烈颱風侵襲這個地區，強風豪雨可能會在工人採收之前【摧毀】剩下的農作物。"},{"w":"destruction","p":"n.","d":"very serious damage","c":"破壞；毀滅","s":"A: Why did the environmental group send a letter to our company about the new hotel we are planning to build on the coast? B: They are worried about the destruction of the beach and the coral reef nearby, so they want us to change the design and keep the building farther from the sea.","t":"A：為什麼環保團體寫信給我們公司，談我們計畫在海岸興建的新飯店？ B：他們擔心附近海灘和珊瑚礁遭到【破壞】，所以希望我們修改設計，讓建築物離海遠一點。"},{"w":"cutting down","p":"n.phr.","d":"the act of cutting trees so that they fall","c":"砍伐；砍倒","s":"A: Why are so many people in the neighborhood signing that petition at the community center this week? B: They want to stop the cutting down of the old trees along Park Avenue, because the city plans to widen the road there for more traffic and parking spaces.","t":"A：為什麼這週有這麼多社區居民在社區中心簽署那份請願書？ B：他們想阻止公園大道沿路老樹的【砍伐】，因為市政府計畫在那裡拓寬道路，以容納更多車流和停車位。"},{"w":"large scale","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very big size or level","c":"大規模","s":"A: Is the company still testing the new recycling machines in only one store, or are they planning to put them in every branch soon? B: After the successful trial, the managers decided to introduce them on a large scale next year, so all our branches across the country will get two machines by June.","t":"A：公司還在只有一家門市測試新的回收機嗎？還是他們打算很快就在每家分店都放置？ B：試驗成功後，經理們決定明年【大規模】引進這些機器，所以全國所有分店在六月前都會有兩台機器。"},{"w":"affect","p":"v.","d":"to cause a change in someone or something","c":"影響","s":"A: Why did the airline send all of us an email about our flight to Tokyo this evening, and do we need to change our plans? B: The volcanic ash in the sky may affect several flights in the region tonight, so we should check the website before leaving for the airport after work.","t":"A：航空公司為什麼寄電子郵件給我們所有人，說明今晚飛往東京的班機？我們需要改變計畫嗎？ B：天空中的火山灰今晚可能會【影響】該地區的幾個航班，所以我們下班後出發去機場前應該先查看網站。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the layer of gases around the Earth","c":"大氣層","s":"A: Why did the science museum add a new section about space and the air around our planet to its main exhibition this year? B: The curator wants visitors to understand how the atmosphere protects the Earth from the sun's strong rays and keeps the temperature comfortable enough for life.","t":"A：為什麼科學博物館今年在主要展覽中新增了一個關於太空和地球周圍空氣的展區？ B：策展人希望參觀者了解【大氣層】如何保護地球免受太陽強烈光線的傷害，並讓溫度保持在適合生命生存的範圍。"},{"w":"water cycle","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way water moves from the sea to the sky and back again","c":"水循環","s":"A: What topic will the science teachers cover during the summer camp that our company is sponsoring for the employees' children next month? B: They will explain the water cycle, showing the kids how rain falls, flows into rivers, rises into the sky again as vapor, and finally forms new clouds.","t":"A：下個月我們公司為員工子女贊助的夏令營中，科學老師會講什麼主題？ B：他們會講解【水循環】，讓孩子們了解雨如何落下、流入河川、再以水蒸氣的形式升上天空，最後形成新的雲。"},{"w":"biodiversity","p":"n.","d":"the variety of plants and animals in a place","c":"生物多樣性","s":"A: Why is the government giving money to farmers who leave small areas of their land wild instead of planting crops there? B: Officials want to increase biodiversity in the countryside, because many kinds of bees, birds, and wild plants have disappeared in recent years, and farms need them to stay healthy.","t":"A：政府為什麼要補助那些保留一小塊土地讓它野生、而不種植作物的農民？ B：官員希望增加鄉村地區的【生物多樣性】，因為近年來許多種類的蜜蜂、鳥類和野生植物已經消失，而農場需要牠們才能保持健康。"},{"w":"species","p":"n.","d":"a group of animals or plants of the same kind","c":"物種","s":"A: Why are so many reporters and photographers waiting outside the zoo's main entrance so early this morning? B: The zoo is announcing the birth of a baby panda, which is great news because the species is still rare in the wild, and the staff have worked hard for years to protect it.","t":"A：為什麼今天一大早有這麼多記者和攝影師在動物園正門外等候？ B：動物園要宣布一隻熊貓寶寶誕生了，這是個好消息，因為這個【物種】在野外仍然很稀少，工作人員多年來一直努力保護牠們。"},{"w":"remain","p":"v.","d":"to stay in the same place or condition","c":"維持；保持；留下","s":"A: Has the government finally decided when the beach near our hotel will reopen to tourists after the oil spill last month? B: Not yet, the beach will remain closed until the cleanup team removes all the oil from the sand, which could take at least three more weeks.","t":"A：上個月漏油事件後，政府終於決定我們飯店附近的海灘何時重新對遊客開放了嗎？ B：還沒有，在清理團隊把沙灘上的油全部清除之前，海灘將【維持】關閉，這可能至少還需要三個星期。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural home of an animal or plant","c":"棲息地","s":"A: Why did the developers change the location of the new golf course after the first plans were shown to the public last year? B: Scientists found that the original site was the natural habitat of a rare kind of frog, so building there would have forced the animals to lose their home.","t":"A：為什麼開發商在去年公開首批計畫後更換了新高爾夫球場的地點？ B：科學家發現原本的地點是一種稀有青蛙的天然【棲息地】，所以在那裡興建會讓這些動物失去牠們的家。"},{"w":"absorb","p":"v.","d":"to take in liquid, gas, or heat","c":"吸收","s":"A: Why did the city plant thousands of new trees along the highways and around the industrial park this spring? B: Trees can absorb harmful gases from the air and reduce noise from the traffic, so the people living nearby should enjoy cleaner air and quieter evenings.","t":"A：為什麼市政府今年春天在高速公路沿線和工業園區周圍種了好幾千棵新樹？ B：樹木可以【吸收】空氣中的有害氣體並減少交通噪音，所以住在附近的人應該能享受更乾淨的空氣和更安靜的夜晚。"},{"w":"give sth off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to send out a smell, gas, heat, or light","c":"散發出；放出","s":"A: Why did the office manager ask the cleaning staff to stop using that new floor polish in the meeting rooms after only one week? B: Like many cheap cleaning products, it can give sth off — in this case, a strong chemical smell — which causes headaches for some employees, so she wants them to return to the old product.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理在一週後就要求清潔人員停止在會議室使用那款新的地板蠟？ B：它容易【散發出】一股強烈的化學氣味，讓一些員工頭痛，所以她希望他們改回原本的產品。"},{"w":"soil erosion","p":"n.phr.","d":"the loss of the top layer of earth because of wind or rain","c":"土壤侵蝕","s":"A: Why are the workers placing large stones and planting grass along the hillside next to the new highway this month? B: The engineers want to prevent soil erosion, because heavy summer rain could wash the earth down onto the road and cause dangerous accidents for drivers.","t":"A：為什麼工人這個月在新高速公路旁的山坡上放置大石頭並種草？ B：工程師想防止【土壤侵蝕】，因為夏季大雨可能會把泥土沖到路上，對駕駛人造成危險的意外。"},{"w":"expose","p":"v.","d":"to put someone in a situation where something can harm them","c":"使暴露於","s":"A: Why does the factory require every worker in the paint section to wear a mask and gloves, even for very short tasks? B: The managers do not want to expose anyone to the strong chemicals in the paint, since breathing them in or touching them can cause serious health problems later.","t":"A：為什麼工廠要求油漆部門的每位工人都要戴口罩和手套，即使是非常短的工作也一樣？ B：經理們不想讓任何人【暴露】在油漆中的強烈化學物質之下，因為吸入或接觸這些物質之後可能會導致嚴重的健康問題。"},{"w":"evaporate","p":"v.","d":"to change from a liquid into a gas","c":"蒸發","s":"A: Why does the water level in the hotel's outdoor swimming pool drop so quickly during the summer months, even when nobody is swimming? B: The hot sun makes a lot of the water evaporate every afternoon, so the maintenance staff have to refill the pool almost every other day.","t":"A：為什麼飯店戶外游泳池的水位在夏季月份下降得那麼快，即使沒有人在游泳？ B：炎熱的陽光每天下午都讓大量的池水【蒸發】，所以維修人員幾乎每隔一天就得把泳池補滿。"},{"w":"nutrients","p":"n.","d":"substances that plants and animals need to grow","c":"養分；營養素","s":"A: Why did the farm manager decide to buy that new organic fertilizer, even though it costs more than the one we used before? B: She tested the land and found that the soil had lost many of its nutrients, so the vegetables were growing smaller and the harvest was getting worse every year.","t":"A：為什麼農場經理決定購買那款新的有機肥料，即使它比我們以前用的貴？ B：她檢測了土地，發現土壤已經失去了許多【養分】，所以蔬菜長得越來越小，收成也一年比一年差。"},{"w":"reverse","p":"v.","d":"to change something back to how it was before","c":"扭轉；使逆轉","s":"A: Do you think the new rules on plastic bags will really help the sea, since so much damage has already been done over many years? B: Experts say we can still reverse some of the damage if companies and shoppers work together, but it will take time, money, and a lot of patience.","t":"A：你認為新的塑膠袋規定真的能幫助海洋嗎？畢竟多年來已經造成了這麼多的破壞。 B：專家說如果企業和購物者共同努力，我們仍然可以【扭轉】部分的損害，但這需要時間、金錢和很大的耐心。"},{"w":"acid rain","p":"n.phr.","d":"rain that contains harmful chemicals from factories and cars","c":"酸雨","s":"A: Why does the old stone statue in front of the city library look so damaged, with parts of its face almost gone? B: For many years, acid rain caused by the smoke from nearby factories slowly ate away at the stone, so the city now plans to repair it and move it indoors.","t":"A：為什麼市立圖書館前那座古老的石雕像看起來損壞得這麼嚴重，臉的部分幾乎不見了？ B：多年來，附近工廠的煙所造成的【酸雨】慢慢地侵蝕了石頭，所以市政府現在計畫修復它並移到室內。"},{"w":"contain","p":"v.","d":"to have something inside","c":"含有；包含","s":"A: Why did the supermarket remove that brand of children's juice from all its shelves so suddenly this morning? B: A government test showed that the drinks contain too much sugar and a chemical that is not allowed, so the store wants to protect its customers until the problem is solved.","t":"A：為什麼超市今天早上突然把那個品牌的兒童果汁從所有貨架上撤下？ B：政府檢測顯示這些飲料【含有】過多的糖和一種不被允許的化學物質，所以在問題解決之前，商店想保護顧客。"},{"w":"particle","p":"n.","d":"a very small piece of something","c":"微粒；顆粒","s":"A: Why did the company buy expensive air cleaners for every office, even though the windows are usually kept closed? B: Even a very small particle of dust from the busy road outside can get through gaps in the windows, and the cleaners catch these before employees breathe them in during the long workday.","t":"A：為什麼公司幫每間辦公室都買了昂貴的空氣清淨機，即使窗戶通常都是關著的？ B：即使是外面繁忙道路上非常微小的一顆灰塵【微粒】也能從窗戶縫隙進來，而清淨機能在員工漫長的工作日中吸入之前把這些捕捉起來。"},{"w":"lung","p":"n.","d":"one of the two organs in the chest used for breathing","c":"肺","s":"A: Why did the doctor tell our sales director to stop jogging along the main road every morning before coming to the office? B: Her tests showed that one lung was not working as well as it should, and the dirty air from the traffic was making her breathing problems even worse.","t":"A：為什麼醫生要我們的業務總監停止每天早上進辦公室前沿著大馬路慢跑？ B：她的檢查顯示一邊的【肺】功能不如應有的好，而交通造成的骯髒空氣讓她的呼吸問題更加惡化。"},{"w":"seep","p":"v.","d":"to flow slowly through small holes or spaces","c":"滲出；滲入","s":"A: Why did the residents near the old gas station complain to the city about the water from their kitchen taps last month? B: Tests showed that oil from a broken underground tank had started to seep into the ground, and some of it had reached the pipes that carry drinking water to their homes.","t":"A：上個月為什麼舊加油站附近的居民向市政府投訴他們廚房水龍頭的水？ B：檢測顯示，一個破損的地下儲油槽裡的油已經開始【滲】入地下，有些已經流到輸送飲用水到他們家中的水管。"},{"w":"exhaust fumes","p":"n.phr.","d":"the gases that come out of a car or engine","c":"廢氣","s":"A: Why did the company decide to move the staff break area from the side of the building to the rooftop garden? B: The old break area was right next to the loading dock, and the exhaust fumes from the delivery trucks made it unpleasant and unhealthy for people to sit there.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定把員工休息區從大樓側邊移到屋頂花園？ B：舊的休息區就在卸貨區旁邊，送貨卡車排放的【廢氣】讓人坐在那裡既不舒服又不健康。"},{"w":"fossil fuel","p":"n.phr.","d":"fuel such as coal, oil, or gas formed from old plants and animals","c":"化石燃料","s":"A: Why is the power company building so many wind turbines along the coast, and will it change our electricity bills? B: The company wants to depend less on coal, oil, and other kinds of fossil fuel, and prices may actually go down once the new turbines start producing power next year.","t":"A：為什麼電力公司沿著海岸興建這麼多風力發電機？這會改變我們的電費嗎？ B：公司希望減少對煤、石油和其他種類【化石燃料】的依賴，而且等新的發電機明年開始發電後，價格實際上可能會下降。"},{"w":"global warming","p":"n.phr.","d":"the slow rise in the Earth's temperature","c":"全球暖化","s":"A: Why did the ski resort decide to spend so much money on machines that make artificial snow this winter? B: Because of global warming, the temperature in the mountains has risen over the past ten years, and there is not enough natural snow to keep the slopes open all season.","t":"A：為什麼滑雪度假村今年冬天決定花這麼多錢購買人工造雪機？ B：由於【全球暖化】，山區的氣溫在過去十年來上升了，自然降雪已經不足以讓雪道整季開放。"},{"w":"greenhouse effect","p":"n.phr.","d":"the warming of the Earth when gases trap the sun's heat","c":"溫室效應","s":"A: What did the speaker at this morning's environmental conference say about the rising temperatures around the world? B: She explained that the greenhouse effect happens when certain gases trap the sun's heat near the Earth, and this process is getting stronger because we burn too much coal and oil.","t":"A：今天早上環境研討會的講者對全球氣溫上升說了什麼？ B：她解釋說，當某些氣體把太陽的熱困在地球附近時就會產生【溫室效應】，而這個過程正在加劇，因為我們燃燒了太多煤和石油。"},{"w":"natural disaster","p":"n.phr.","d":"a flood, earthquake, storm, etc. that causes great damage","c":"天然災害","s":"A: Why is the head office asking every branch to update its emergency plan and check its supplies of water and flashlights this month? B: After last year's earthquake, the managers want to make sure every office is ready if another natural disaster like a flood or a typhoon hits suddenly.","t":"A：為什麼總公司這個月要求每家分公司更新緊急應變計畫，並檢查水和手電筒的庫存？ B：去年地震之後，主管們想確保萬一又有像水災或颱風這樣的【天然災害】突然來襲時，每間辦公室都已經做好準備。"},{"w":"recycle","p":"v.","d":"to treat used things so they can be used again","c":"回收；再利用","s":"A: What should we do with all the old printers and computer screens that are sitting in the storage room on the second floor? B: Please do not throw them in the garbage, because the city has a special center where we can recycle electronic products for free, and they will reuse the metal parts.","t":"A：我們該怎麼處理二樓儲藏室裡所有的舊印表機和電腦螢幕？ B：請不要把它們丟進垃圾桶，因為市政府有一個特別的中心，我們可以在那裡免費【回收】電子產品，他們會再利用金屬零件。"},{"w":"poacher","p":"n.","d":"a person who illegally hunts animals","c":"盜獵者","s":"A: Why did the safari company hire extra guards for the national park, even though the number of tourists has dropped this year? B: Last month, a poacher was caught trying to kill an elephant for its tusks, so the company wants to protect the animals and keep its guests safe.","t":"A：為什麼野生動物旅遊公司為國家公園增聘了額外的警衛，即使今年遊客人數已經減少？ B：上個月有一名【盜獵者】被抓到企圖為了象牙而殺害一頭大象，所以公司想保護動物並確保遊客的安全。"},{"w":"dry up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become completely dry","c":"乾涸；枯竭","s":"A: Why are the farmers in the southern region asking the government for help with water supplies this summer? B: It has not rained for almost three months, and the farmers are afraid the river will dry up completely before the rice is ready to harvest in August.","t":"A：為什麼南部地區的農民今年夏天要請求政府協助供水？ B：已經將近三個月沒下雨了，農民擔心河流會在八月稻米可以收割之前完全【乾涸】。"}]},{"unit":125,"theme":"Equipment 設備","cards":[{"w":"device","p":"n.","d":"a small machine or tool made for a special job","c":"裝置；設備","s":"A: Why is the security guard asking every visitor to leave their phones at the front desk before entering the research lab this afternoon? B: The lab director worries that any electronic device with a camera could record the new product designs, so nobody may bring one inside until the testing is finished next week.","t":"A：為什麼保全今天下午要求每位訪客進入研究實驗室前把手機留在前台？ B：實驗室主任擔心任何有相機的電子【裝置】可能會拍下新產品設計，所以在下週測試結束前，任何人都不得帶進去。"},{"w":"machine","p":"n.","d":"a piece of equipment with moving parts that does work","c":"機器","s":"A: Why are there so many people waiting in line outside the break room on the third floor this morning? B: The coffee machine broke down yesterday afternoon, and the technician only fixed it an hour ago, so everyone is rushing to get a hot drink before the weekly sales meeting starts.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上三樓茶水間外面有這麼多人在排隊？ B：咖啡【機】昨天下午故障了，技術人員一小時前才修好，所以大家都趕在每週業務會議開始前去拿杯熱飲。"},{"w":"tool","p":"n.","d":"something you hold and use to do a job","c":"工具","s":"A: Do you know who borrowed the small screwdriver from the storeroom, because I need it to fix the broken shelf in the storage area? B: I think Kevin took it last Friday, but if you can't find it, the shop across the street sells every basic tool you might need at a fair price.","t":"A：你知道誰從儲藏室借走了小螺絲起子嗎？我需要用它來修理倉庫區那個壞掉的架子。 B：我想是凱文上週五拿走的，但如果你找不到，對街的店以合理價格販售你可能需要的各種基本【工具】。"},{"w":"apparatus","p":"n.","d":"a set of equipment used for a special purpose","c":"器具；裝置","s":"A: Why did the safety inspector stop the training session at the fire station so suddenly yesterday afternoon? B: He noticed that the breathing apparatus one trainee was wearing had a cracked mask, so he asked the team to check every set carefully before any firefighter used them during the exercise.","t":"A：為什麼安全檢查員昨天下午突然中止了消防局的訓練課程？ B：他注意到一名學員配戴的呼吸【器具】面罩有裂痕，所以要求團隊在任何消防員於演練中使用前仔細檢查每一套。"},{"w":"instrument","p":"n.","d":"a tool for exact work, such as measuring or medical work","c":"儀器；器械","s":"A: Why does the hospital need to buy so many new things for the operating rooms before the end of this year? B: Almost every surgical instrument in the main room is more than ten years old, and the doctors say that modern ones are sharper, easier to clean, and much safer for patients during long operations.","t":"A：為什麼醫院要在今年年底前為手術室購買這麼多新東西？ B：主手術室裡幾乎每一件手術【器械】都超過十年了，醫生們說新式的器械更鋒利、更容易清潔，在長時間手術中對病人也安全得多。"},{"w":"gear","p":"n.","d":"the equipment and clothes you need for an activity","c":"裝備；用具","s":"A: Is there anything special I should bring for the company hiking trip to the mountains this weekend? B: Yes, the weather may turn cold and rainy in the afternoon, so please pack warm clothes, a waterproof jacket, and good walking boots, and the organizer will provide all the camping gear we need for the night.","t":"A：這個週末公司去山上健行，我需要帶什麼特別的東西嗎？ B：需要，下午天氣可能會變冷又下雨，所以請準備保暖衣物、防水外套和好走的登山靴，主辦人會提供我們過夜所需的所有露營【裝備】。"},{"w":"kit","p":"n.","d":"a set of tools or things kept together for one purpose","c":"成套用品；工具組","s":"A: What should I do if one of the workers on the production line cuts his finger while the nurse is out to lunch? B: There is a first-aid kit hanging on the wall next to the emergency exit, so clean the wound, cover it with a bandage, and then report the accident to your supervisor.","t":"A：如果護士外出吃午餐時，生產線上有工人割傷手指，我該怎麼辦？ B：緊急出口旁邊的牆上掛著一個急救【箱】，所以先清潔傷口、用繃帶包好，然後向你的主管報告這起意外。"},{"w":"hardware","p":"n.","d":"the physical parts of a computer system","c":"硬體","s":"A: Why is the IT department replacing all the old computers in the accounting office this month instead of next year? B: The programs are fine, but the hardware is too old to run the new accounting system quickly, so the staff keep losing time waiting for their reports to load.","t":"A：為什麼資訊部門這個月就要汰換會計辦公室所有的舊電腦，而不是明年？ B：程式沒問題，但【硬體】太舊，無法快速執行新的會計系統，所以員工一直浪費時間等報表載入。"},{"w":"software","p":"n.","d":"programs that run on a computer","c":"軟體","s":"A: How long will it take for the new staff to learn the booking system that our travel agency started using last month? B: The software is quite simple to use, so after a two-hour training session on Monday morning, most of them should be able to make reservations for customers on their own.","t":"A：新進員工要多久才能學會我們旅行社上個月開始使用的訂位系統？ B：這套【軟體】相當容易使用，所以週一上午兩小時的培訓課程後，他們大多數應該就能獨立幫客戶訂位了。"},{"w":"material","p":"n.","d":"a substance used for making or building things","c":"材料；原料","s":"A: Why did the builders stop working on the new office building for almost two weeks last month? B: The supplier delivered the wrong building material for the walls, and the project manager refused to accept it, so everyone had to wait until the correct order arrived from the factory.","t":"A：為什麼上個月建商停工新辦公大樓將近兩週？ B：供應商送錯了牆面用的建築【材料】，專案經理拒收，所以大家只好等工廠送來正確的訂貨。"},{"w":"component","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that make up a machine or system","c":"零件；組成部分","s":"A: Why are the new laptops arriving three weeks later than the supplier promised in the contract? B: The factory in Malaysia ran out of one important electronic component that goes inside the screen, so production stopped until a new shipment arrived from another company last Thursday.","t":"A：為什麼新筆電比供應商在合約中承諾的晚了三週到貨？ B：馬來西亞的工廠缺少一個裝在螢幕裡的重要電子【零件】，所以生產停擺，直到上週四另一家公司的新貨送到為止。"},{"w":"accessory","p":"n.","d":"an extra item that you add to a main product","c":"配件","s":"A: Did the customer who bought the expensive camera yesterday also buy anything else from our store? B: Yes, she asked for advice about which accessory would help her take better photos at night, so I sold her a strong tripod and an extra battery as well.","t":"A：昨天買那台昂貴相機的顧客還有在我們店裡買其他東西嗎？ B：有，她詢問哪種【配件】能幫助她在晚上拍出更好的照片，所以我還賣給她一個堅固的三腳架和一顆備用電池。"},{"w":"attachment","p":"n.","d":"an extra part you fix onto a machine for a special job","c":"附件；附加裝置","s":"A: Can we use the same vacuum cleaner for both the carpets in the offices and the narrow corners behind the desks? B: Yes, but you need to change the attachment first, because the long thin one reaches into small spaces much better than the wide brush that comes on the machine.","t":"A：我們可以用同一台吸塵器清潔辦公室的地毯和辦公桌後面的狹窄角落嗎？ B：可以，但你得先換【附件】，因為細長的那個比機器原本附的寬刷頭更容易伸進小空間。"},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"a building or place used for a particular activity","c":"設施；場所","s":"A: Why did the company decide to build its new warehouse outside the city instead of near the main office downtown? B: Land is much cheaper there, and the new facility will be close to the highway, so our trucks can deliver products to customers in the south more quickly and save money on fuel.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定把新倉庫蓋在市郊，而不是市中心總公司附近？ B：那裡的土地便宜很多，而且新【設施】靠近高速公路，所以我們的卡車能更快把產品送到南部客戶手中，也能省下油錢。"},{"w":"installation","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting equipment in place so it is ready to use","c":"安裝","s":"A: When will we be able to use the new air conditioners in the meeting rooms on the fifth floor? B: The workers will start the installation early on Saturday morning while the office is empty, and the manager expects everything to be working properly before the staff return on Monday.","t":"A：我們什麼時候可以使用五樓會議室裡的新冷氣機？ B：工人會在週六一早趁辦公室沒人時開始【安裝】，經理預計員工週一回來之前一切都能正常運作。"},{"w":"maintenance","p":"n.","d":"regular work to keep something in good condition","c":"保養；維修","s":"A: Why is the elevator in our building closed every first Monday of the month from nine to eleven in the morning? B: The building manager arranges regular maintenance with a service company, so technicians can check the cables and doors and prevent serious problems before they happen.","t":"A：為什麼我們大樓的電梯每個月第一個星期一上午九點到十一點都會停用？ B：大樓管理員和一家服務公司安排了定期【保養】，讓技術人員檢查纜線和門，在嚴重問題發生前加以預防。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken","c":"修理","s":"A: The printer in the sales department is making strange noises again, so should we just order a new one? B: Let's ask the technician to repair it first, because a new printer costs a lot of money, and he said last time that changing one small part would solve the problem.","t":"A：業務部的印表機又發出奇怪的聲音了，我們乾脆訂一台新的吧？ B：我們先請技術人員【修理】看看，因為新印表機很貴，而且他上次說換一個小零件就能解決問題。"},{"w":"upgrade","p":"v.","d":"to make something newer, better, or more powerful","c":"升級","s":"A: Our online store keeps crashing when many customers visit at the same time during the holiday sale, so what can we do? B: We should upgrade our server to a faster plan before next month's promotion, even though it will cost more, because losing customers is much more expensive.","t":"A：假日特賣期間大量顧客同時造訪時，我們的網路商店一直當機，我們能怎麼辦？ B：我們應該在下個月的促銷前把伺服器【升級】到更快的方案，雖然會多花錢，但流失顧客的代價大得多。"},{"w":"replace","p":"v.","d":"to put a new thing in the place of an old one","c":"更換；取代","s":"A: The light bulbs in the hallway near the reception area keep flickering, and visitors have started to complain about it. B: I'll call the maintenance team and ask them to replace all of them with new energy-saving bulbs this afternoon, which should also lower our monthly electricity bill.","t":"A：接待區附近走廊的燈泡一直閃爍，訪客已經開始抱怨了。 B：我會打電話給維修團隊，請他們今天下午把燈泡全部【更換】成新的節能燈泡，這應該也能降低我們每月的電費。"},{"w":"operate","p":"v.","d":"to use and control a machine","c":"操作","s":"A: Can the new part-time workers start using the forklift in the warehouse on their first day? B: No, they are not allowed to operate it until they finish a safety course and pass a short test, because driving it carelessly could injure someone or damage the products on the shelves.","t":"A：新來的兼職員工上班第一天就可以使用倉庫裡的堆高機嗎？ B：不行，他們必須完成安全課程並通過簡短測驗後才能【操作】，因為駕駛時不小心可能會傷到人或損壞架上的產品。"},{"w":"handle","p":"v.","d":"to touch, hold, or move something with your hands","c":"搬運；處理","s":"A: Should I ask the delivery company to bring the glass display cases directly to the showroom tomorrow? B: Yes, but please remind them to handle the boxes with great care, because the cases are very fragile, and we cannot open the new store next week if any of them arrive broken.","t":"A：我應該請貨運公司明天把玻璃展示櫃直接送到展示廳嗎？ B：是的，但請提醒他們【搬運】箱子時要非常小心，因為展示櫃非常易碎，若有任何一個送到時破了，我們下週就無法開新店。"},{"w":"assemble","p":"v.","d":"to put the parts of something together","c":"組裝","s":"A: The new desks for the marketing team arrived this morning in large flat boxes, so who is going to put them together? B: The furniture store will send two workers to assemble them tomorrow morning, so please clear the space near the windows and move the old chairs into the storage room before they come.","t":"A：行銷團隊的新辦公桌今天早上用大型扁平箱送到了，誰要來把它們組合起來？ B：家具行明天早上會派兩名工人來【組裝】，所以請在他們來之前清出窗邊的空間，並把舊椅子搬到儲藏室。"},{"w":"dismantle","p":"v.","d":"to take a machine or structure apart into pieces","c":"拆解；拆卸","s":"A: How are we going to move the huge printing press from the old factory to the new one across town? B: The engineers will dismantle it into smaller pieces next week, put each piece on a separate truck, and then rebuild it carefully at the new site before production starts again.","t":"A：我們要怎麼把那台巨大的印刷機從舊工廠搬到城另一頭的新工廠？ B：工程師們下週會把它【拆解】成較小的部分，每一部分分別放上一輛卡車，然後在生產重新開始前，於新廠址仔細重新組裝。"},{"w":"calibrate","p":"v.","d":"to adjust a measuring tool so it gives correct results","c":"校準","s":"A: Why are the scales in the shipping department showing different weights for the same package this morning? B: Nobody has checked them for months, so I've asked the technician to calibrate them today, because wrong weights mean we charge our customers the wrong shipping fees every day.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上出貨部門的磅秤對同一個包裹顯示不同的重量？ B：好幾個月都沒人檢查過了，所以我已經請技術人員今天【校準】，因為重量錯誤代表我們每天向顧客收取的運費也會出錯。"},{"w":"portable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to carry or move","c":"可攜式的；便於攜帶的","s":"A: I need to give a presentation to a client at their office tomorrow, but they told me their meeting room has no screen. B: You can borrow the small portable projector from the IT department, since it fits easily in your bag and only needs a laptop and a white wall to work well.","t":"A：我明天要到客戶的辦公室做簡報，但他們說會議室沒有螢幕。 B：你可以向資訊部借那台小型的【可攜式】投影機，它很容易放進你的包包，只需要一台筆電和一面白牆就能正常使用。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"strong and able to last a long time","c":"耐用的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner choose these plastic chairs for the outdoor area instead of the wooden ones we saw? B: She said plastic is more durable in rain and strong sunshine, so the chairs will last for many years without breaking, and they are also easier to clean after busy weekends.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳老闆為戶外區選了這些塑膠椅，而不是我們看到的木椅？ B：她說塑膠在雨天和強烈陽光下更【耐用】，所以椅子可以用很多年都不會壞，而且忙碌的週末過後也更容易清潔。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted to work well every time","c":"可靠的","s":"A: Which delivery company should we choose for sending important documents to our branch office in Kaohsiung every week? B: I recommend the one we used last year, because they were very reliable and never lost a package, even during the typhoon season when many other companies had serious delays.","t":"A：每週寄重要文件到高雄分公司，我們應該選哪家快遞公司？ B：我推薦我們去年用的那家，因為他們非常【可靠】，從來沒有遺失過包裹，即使在颱風季許多其他公司嚴重延誤時也一樣。"},{"w":"advanced","p":"adj.","d":"modern and using the newest ideas or technology","c":"先進的","s":"A: Why are so many hospitals from other countries sending their doctors to visit our medical center this month? B: We recently bought very advanced scanning equipment that can find small health problems much earlier, so doctors want to see how it works and learn how to use it in their own hospitals.","t":"A：為什麼這個月有這麼多其他國家的醫院派醫生來參訪我們的醫學中心？ B：我們最近購買了非常【先進】的掃描設備，可以更早發現小的健康問題，所以醫生們想來看看它如何運作，並學習在自己的醫院使用。"},{"w":"automatic","p":"adj.","d":"working by itself without a person controlling it","c":"自動的","s":"A: Do I have to remember to turn off all the lights in the office when I leave late in the evening? B: No, the building has an automatic system that switches off the lights when nobody has moved in a room for fifteen minutes, which helps the company save quite a lot of electricity.","t":"A：我晚上很晚離開時，必須記得關掉辦公室所有的燈嗎？ B：不用，大樓有一套【自動】系統，當房間內十五分鐘沒有人走動時就會關燈，這幫公司省下不少電。"},{"w":"manual","p":"n.","d":"a book that explains how to use a machine","c":"使用手冊；說明書","s":"A: I just set up the new coffee machine in the staff kitchen, but I can't figure out how to change the cup size. B: Check the user manual that came in the box, because it explains every button step by step, and there are also pictures showing how to clean the machine every week.","t":"A：我剛在員工廚房裝好新咖啡機，但我搞不清楚怎麼改變杯量。 B：看看盒子裡附的使用【手冊】，它一步一步說明每個按鈕，還有圖片示範每週如何清潔機器。"},{"w":"heavy-duty","p":"adj.","d":"very strong and made for hard work or heavy use","c":"重型的；耐用的","s":"A: The cleaning company keeps complaining that their normal bags break when they collect rubbish from our factory floor. B: Then we should order heavy-duty bags that can carry sharp metal pieces and wet waste without tearing, even if they cost a little more than the ones we usually buy from the supermarket.","t":"A：清潔公司一直抱怨，他們從我們工廠地面收垃圾時，一般的垃圾袋都會破。 B：那我們應該訂購【重型耐用】的垃圾袋，可以裝尖銳的金屬碎片和濕垃圾而不破，即使比我們平常在超市買的貴一點也值得。"},{"w":"lightweight","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy; easy to lift and carry","c":"輕量的；輕便的","s":"A: Our sales staff travel to visit customers almost every week, so which laptop should the company buy for them? B: We should choose a lightweight model that weighs about one kilogram, because they carry their bags all day through airports and train stations, and a heavy computer would make their trips much more tiring.","t":"A：我們的業務人員幾乎每週都要出差拜訪客戶，公司應該幫他們買哪款筆電？ B：我們應該選一台約一公斤重的【輕量】機型，因為他們整天背著包包穿梭在機場和車站，笨重的電腦會讓出差更累。"},{"w":"safely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that does not cause danger or harm","c":"安全地","s":"A: What is the most important thing the new factory workers must learn during their first week of training here? B: They must learn how to use the cutting machines safely, which means always wearing gloves and glasses, keeping their hands away from the blades, and turning the power off before cleaning.","t":"A：新進工廠員工在第一週培訓中最重要要學的是什麼？ B：他們必須學會如何【安全地】使用切割機，也就是一定要戴手套和護目鏡、雙手遠離刀片，並在清潔前關掉電源。"},{"w":"efficiently","p":"adv.","d":"in a quick and well-organized way without wasting time","c":"有效率地","s":"A: How did the warehouse team manage to pack and send so many more orders this month than last month? B: The manager bought new scanners and changed the layout of the shelves, so the workers can now find products and finish their tasks much more efficiently without walking back and forth.","t":"A：倉庫團隊這個月怎麼能比上個月多包裝並寄出這麼多訂單？ B：經理買了新的掃描器並改變了貨架的配置，所以工人現在能更【有效率地】找到商品並完成工作，不用來回走動。"}]},{"unit":126,"theme":"Evening 傍晚","cards":[{"w":"dusk","p":"n.","d":"the time in the evening when it is starting to get dark","c":"黃昏；薄暮","s":"A: Should we start the outdoor cleanup in the park after work today, or will it be too dark for the volunteers to see clearly? B: We should begin right after five o'clock and finish before dusk, because the park has no streetlights and the manager wants everyone safely home before it gets dark.","t":"A：我們今天下班後應該在公園開始戶外清潔活動嗎？還是會太暗，志工們看不清楚？ B：我們應該在五點一過就開始，並在【黃昏】之前結束，因為公園沒有路燈，而且經理希望大家在天黑前安全回家。"},{"w":"twilight","p":"n.","d":"the soft, weak light just after the sun goes down","c":"暮光；黃昏時分","s":"A: Why did the photographer ask to move the outdoor product shoot for the new watches from noon to the end of the day? B: She said the soft blue light of twilight, just after the sun goes down, makes the metal look elegant, and it removes the strong shadows that appear at midday.","t":"A：為什麼攝影師要求把新款手錶的戶外產品拍攝從中午改到傍晚？ B：她說太陽剛下山後【暮光】中柔和的藍色光線會讓金屬看起來很優雅，而且能消除正午時出現的強烈陰影。"},{"w":"sunset","p":"n.","d":"the time when the sun goes down and the sky changes color","c":"日落；夕陽","s":"A: Our clients from Tokyo arrive on Friday afternoon, so what kind of welcome event do you think we should plan for them that evening? B: Let's book a table on the hotel's rooftop terrace, where they can enjoy the beautiful sunset over the harbor while we talk about the project in a relaxed setting.","t":"A：我們東京的客戶星期五下午抵達，你覺得那天晚上我們應該為他們安排什麼樣的歡迎活動？ B：我們在飯店的屋頂露台訂位吧，他們可以在那裡欣賞港口上美麗的【夕陽】，同時我們在輕鬆的環境下討論專案。"},{"w":"nightfall","p":"n.","d":"the time in the evening when it becomes dark","c":"入夜；黃昏","s":"A: The hiking trip for the new employees starts at two in the afternoon, so do you think the group can get back to the parking lot safely? B: Yes, the guide says the trail takes about three hours, so we should return before nightfall, but everyone should still bring a flashlight just in case.","t":"A：新進員工的健行活動下午兩點開始，你覺得這群人能安全回到停車場嗎？ B：可以，嚮導說這條步道大約需要三個小時，所以我們應該能在【入夜】前回來，不過以防萬一，每個人還是應該帶一支手電筒。"},{"w":"sundown","p":"n.","d":"the time when the sun goes down; sunset","c":"日落時分","s":"A: The farmers' market downtown is very popular, but do you know how long the food stalls stay open on Saturdays during the summer? B: Most of the vendors keep selling fruit, bread, and snacks until sundown, and then the city cleaning crew arrives to clear the street before the night traffic begins.","t":"A：市中心的農夫市集很受歡迎，你知道夏天週六那些食物攤位營業到幾點嗎？ B：大部分攤販會一直賣水果、麵包和點心到【日落】，然後市政清潔人員會在夜間車流開始前來清理街道。"},{"w":"early evening","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first part of the evening, around 5 to 7 p.m.","c":"傍晚；晚間初時","s":"A: When is the best time to call our sales partners in London, since they are eight hours behind us here in Taipei? B: Try calling them in the early evening, around six or seven o'clock our time, because that is late morning for them and they usually have just finished their first meetings.","t":"A：我們倫敦的業務夥伴比台北這裡晚八個小時，什麼時候打電話給他們最好？ B：試著在【傍晚】打給他們，大約是我們這邊的六、七點，因為那是他們的上午稍晚，他們通常剛開完第一批會議。"},{"w":"late evening","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last part of the evening, before midnight","c":"深夜；晚間較晚時分","s":"A: Why are the cleaning staff in our office building working such strange hours this month instead of during the afternoon? B: The building manager moved their shift to the late evening, after ten o'clock, so the noisy vacuum cleaners will not disturb employees who are still in meetings or talking with customers on the phone.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公大樓的清潔人員這個月不在下午工作，而是在這麼奇怪的時間上班？ B：大樓經理把他們的班次調到【深夜】，也就是十點以後，這樣吵雜的吸塵器就不會打擾仍在開會或正在和客戶講電話的員工。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and feel calm","c":"放鬆；休息","s":"A: You have been working on the annual budget report for three weeks without a break, so what are you going to do this weekend? B: I plan to turn off my work phone, sit in the garden with a good book, and just relax for two days so I can feel fresh when the new quarter starts.","t":"A：你已經連續三週不停地做年度預算報告了，這個週末你打算做什麼？ B：我打算關掉工作手機，帶本好書坐在花園裡，好好【放鬆】兩天，這樣新的一季開始時我才能精神飽滿。"},{"w":"unwind","p":"v.","d":"to stop worrying and become calm after work or stress","c":"放鬆；解除緊張","s":"A: The sales team looks really tired after finishing that difficult contract negotiation, so is there anything special planned for them tonight? B: The director booked a private room at a quiet jazz bar near the station, where everyone can unwind with some music and snacks after such a long and stressful week.","t":"A：業務團隊結束了那場艱難的合約談判後看起來真的很累，今晚有為他們安排什麼特別的活動嗎？ B：主管在車站附近一間安靜的爵士酒吧訂了包廂，大家可以在漫長又充滿壓力的一週後，聽聽音樂、吃點小點心【放鬆一下】。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"free time when you are not working","c":"空閒；休閒","s":"A: The new apartment complex across from our office is advertising itself to young professionals, so what makes it so attractive to them? B: Besides being close to the train station, it offers a gym, a pool, and a rooftop garden, so residents have plenty of places to enjoy their leisure time after work.","t":"A：我們辦公室對面的新公寓大樓正在向年輕上班族打廣告，它為什麼對他們這麼有吸引力？ B：除了靠近火車站，它還提供健身房、游泳池和屋頂花園，所以住戶下班後有很多地方可以享受【休閒】時光。"},{"w":"dinner","p":"n.","d":"the main meal of the day, usually eaten in the evening","c":"晚餐；正餐","s":"A: The CEO of our biggest supplier is visiting Taipei next Thursday, so how should we welcome him after the factory tour? B: I think we should invite him to a formal dinner at a famous Taiwanese restaurant at seven o'clock, so he can try local dishes and meet our senior managers in a friendly setting.","t":"A：我們最大供應商的執行長下週四要來台北，參觀工廠後我們應該如何招待他？ B：我認為我們應該在七點邀請他到一家知名的台菜餐廳享用正式【晚餐】，讓他可以品嚐在地菜餚，並在友善的氣氛中認識我們的高階主管。"},{"w":"supper","p":"n.","d":"a light meal eaten in the evening","c":"（簡單的）晚餐；宵夜","s":"A: The conference program says the sessions end at nine at night, but will the guests get anything to eat after such a long day? B: Yes, the hotel will serve a light supper of soup, sandwiches, and fruit in the lobby lounge, so people can have a simple meal before going up to their rooms.","t":"A：會議議程說場次到晚上九點才結束，經過這麼漫長的一天，來賓們會有東西吃嗎？ B：有的，飯店會在大廳酒吧提供有湯、三明治和水果的清淡【晚餐】，讓大家回房前可以簡單吃一點。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people for a social purpose","c":"聚會；集會","s":"A: Our department hit its sales target this quarter, so is the manager planning anything to celebrate the team's hard work? B: She is organizing a small gathering at her house on Friday evening, where we can share food, play some games, and finally get to know the new staff members better.","t":"A：我們部門這一季達成了銷售目標，經理有打算辦什麼活動來慶祝團隊的努力嗎？ B：她正在籌辦星期五晚上在她家的一場小型【聚會】，我們可以在那裡分享食物、玩些遊戲，終於可以更認識新同事。"},{"w":"stroll","p":"n.","d":"a slow, relaxed walk","c":"散步；漫步","s":"A: The hotel restaurant was excellent, but I ate far too much, so what would you like to do before we go back to our rooms? B: Let's take a short stroll along the riverside path behind the hotel, because the weather is cool tonight and a gentle walk will help us feel more comfortable.","t":"A：飯店餐廳很棒，但我吃太多了，回房間前你想做什麼？ B：我們沿著飯店後面的河濱步道【散散步】吧，因為今晚天氣涼爽，悠閒地走一走會讓我們覺得舒服些。"},{"w":"dim","p":"adj.","d":"not bright; with little light","c":"昏暗的；暗淡的","s":"A: The restaurant we chose for the client dinner looks very romantic, but will it be a good place to show them the product samples? B: Probably not, because the lights there are quite dim in the evening, so it would be hard for the clients to see the colors and details of our new designs.","t":"A：我們為客戶晚餐選的餐廳看起來很浪漫，但那裡適合給他們看產品樣品嗎？ B：可能不適合，因為那裡晚上的燈光相當【昏暗】，客戶很難看清楚我們新設計的顏色和細節。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"calm and without noise or trouble","c":"寧靜的；平靜的","s":"A: Why did the company choose a hotel so far outside the city for the annual planning meeting this year? B: The managers wanted a peaceful place in the mountains, away from traffic noise and phone calls, so everyone could focus on long-term goals and think clearly about next year's strategy.","t":"A：今年公司為什麼選了一間離市區這麼遠的飯店來開年度規劃會議？ B：經理們想要一個在山上的【寧靜】地方，遠離車流噪音和電話，讓大家能專注於長期目標，清楚思考明年的策略。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making very little noise","c":"安靜的","s":"A: I need to finish the contract review before the meeting tomorrow morning, but the open office is so noisy that I can't concentrate. B: Why don't you stay a little later tonight, because after six o'clock most people go home and the office becomes very quiet, so you can work without any interruptions.","t":"A：我必須在明天早上開會前完成合約審查，但開放式辦公室太吵了，我無法專心。 B：你今晚何不稍微晚一點走，因為六點以後大部分人都回家了，辦公室會變得很【安靜】，你就可以不受打擾地工作。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and pleasant","c":"溫暖舒適的；溫馨的","s":"A: We're looking for a small café where the book club from our company can meet on Wednesday evenings, so do you know a good one? B: There's a cozy little café on Fifth Street with soft sofas, warm lights, and a fireplace, so it feels comfortable and friendly, especially on cold winter nights.","t":"A：我們在找一間小咖啡館，讓公司的讀書會可以在星期三晚上聚會，你知道哪間不錯嗎？ B：第五街有一間【溫馨舒適】的小咖啡館，有柔軟的沙發、溫暖的燈光和壁爐，感覺舒服又友善，尤其是在寒冷的冬夜。"},{"w":"calmly","p":"adv.","d":"in a relaxed way, without getting upset","c":"冷靜地；平靜地","s":"A: How did the hotel staff handle the situation when the power suddenly went out during the wedding banquet last night? B: The manager calmly explained the problem to the guests, asked the waiters to bring candles to every table, and kept everyone seated until the electricity came back about fifteen minutes later.","t":"A：昨晚婚宴中突然停電時，飯店員工是怎麼處理的？ B：經理【冷靜地】向賓客說明狀況，請服務生為每一桌送上蠟燭，並讓大家保持就座，直到大約十五分鐘後電力恢復。"},{"w":"softly","p":"adv.","d":"in a quiet and gentle way","c":"輕柔地；輕聲地","s":"A: Is it all right if we play some background music in the hotel lobby during the evening reception for our international guests? B: Yes, but please make sure the piano plays softly, because guests will be talking about business and they should be able to hear each other without raising their voices.","t":"A：在為國際來賓舉辦的晚間招待會期間，我們可以在飯店大廳播放一些背景音樂嗎？ B：可以，但請確保鋼琴【輕柔地】演奏，因為來賓會談論生意，他們應該不必提高音量就能聽見彼此說話。"},{"w":"glow","p":"n.","d":"a soft, steady light","c":"光輝；柔和的光芒","s":"A: The designers want the outside of our new store to look attractive at night, so what kind of lighting have they chosen for the front? B: They picked warm yellow lights under the windows, which give the whole entrance a soft glow after dark and make people walking past feel welcome to come inside.","t":"A：設計師希望我們新店的外觀在晚上看起來很吸引人，他們為店面選了什麼樣的照明？ B：他們在窗戶下方挑選了溫暖的黃色燈光，天黑後會讓整個入口散發柔和的【光芒】，讓路過的人覺得受到歡迎而想進來。"},{"w":"fade","p":"v.","d":"to slowly become less bright or strong","c":"逐漸消失；變暗","s":"A: The outdoor concert for our customers starts at seven, so when should the stage crew turn on the spotlights and decorations? B: They should wait until the daylight starts to fade, around six-thirty, because the colored lights will look much brighter and more impressive against the darkening sky.","t":"A：為客戶舉辦的戶外音樂會七點開始，舞台工作人員應該什麼時候打開聚光燈和裝飾燈？ B：他們應該等到天光開始【漸漸消失】，大約六點半，因為在漸暗的天空襯托下，彩色燈光會看起來更明亮、更令人印象深刻。"},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something","c":"反思；仔細思考","s":"A: You always seem so organized at work, so do you have any special habit that helps you plan your tasks each day? B: Every evening after dinner, I spend ten minutes writing in a notebook to reflect on what went well and what went wrong, and then I make a short list for tomorrow.","t":"A：你工作時總是很有條理，你有什麼特別的習慣能幫你規劃每天的工作嗎？ B：每天晚餐後，我會花十分鐘在筆記本上寫字，【反思】哪些事做得好、哪些事出了錯，然後為明天列一張簡短的清單。"},{"w":"nap","p":"n.","d":"a short sleep during the day","c":"小睡；打盹","s":"A: You look much more energetic than you did at lunch, so did you drink a lot of coffee this afternoon? B: No, I took a twenty-minute nap in the staff lounge during my break, and now I feel ready to prepare the slides for the evening presentation to the board.","t":"A：你看起來比午餐時有精神多了，你今天下午喝了很多咖啡嗎？ B：沒有，我休息時在員工休息室【小睡】了二十分鐘，現在我覺得已經準備好為晚上向董事會的簡報準備投影片了。"},{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual order in which you do things every day","c":"例行公事；日常作息","s":"A: Now that you work from home three days a week, how do you separate your job from your personal life in the evenings? B: I follow the same routine every day: I shut down my laptop at six, go for a short walk, cook something simple, and never check work e-mails after eight.","t":"A：既然你現在每週有三天在家工作，你晚上如何把工作和個人生活分開？ B：我每天都遵循同樣的【例行作息】：六點關掉筆電、去散步一下、煮點簡單的東西，而且八點以後絕不查看工作郵件。"},{"w":"entertainment","p":"n.","d":"shows, games, or activities that people enjoy","c":"娛樂；娛樂活動","s":"A: The trade fair ends at five each day, but what will the overseas visitors do in the evening while they are staying in the city? B: The organizers have arranged evening entertainment for them, including a night market tour, a traditional music show, and a boat ride on the river, so nobody will feel bored.","t":"A：商展每天五點結束，但海外訪客住在城裡期間晚上要做什麼呢？ B：主辦單位已經為他們安排了晚間【娛樂活動】，包括夜市導覽、傳統音樂表演和河上遊船，所以沒有人會感到無聊。"},{"w":"outing","p":"n.","d":"a short trip for fun, often with a group","c":"出遊；遠足","s":"A: Our team has been under a lot of pressure lately, so what is human resources doing to help improve morale this month? B: They have planned an evening outing to the harbor on Friday, with a seafood buffet and fireworks, and the company will pay for the bus and the meal for everyone.","t":"A：我們團隊最近壓力很大，人資部這個月有做什麼來幫忙提升士氣嗎？ B：他們安排了星期五晚上到港口的【出遊】，有海鮮自助餐和煙火，公司會為每個人支付巴士和餐費。"},{"w":"refreshment","p":"n.","d":"food and drinks served at a meeting or event","c":"茶點；點心飲料","s":"A: The evening seminar for new investors will last about three hours, so should we provide anything for the guests during the break? B: Yes, please set up a table outside the hall with coffee, tea, and cookies, because people will appreciate a little refreshment after listening to presentations for such a long time.","t":"A：新投資人的晚間研討會將持續大約三個小時，休息時間我們應該為來賓準備些什麼嗎？ B：要，請在會議廳外擺一張桌子，放上咖啡、茶和餅乾，因為聽了這麼久的簡報，大家會很感謝有些【茶點】可以享用。"},{"w":"lamplight","p":"n.","d":"the light that comes from a lamp","c":"燈光","s":"A: The bookstore owner wants to attract more customers in the evening, so what changes has she made to the reading area? B: She replaced the bright ceiling lights with small table lamps, so people can now read by warm lamplight in comfortable chairs, and many customers stay longer and buy more books.","t":"A：書店老闆想在晚上吸引更多顧客，她對閱讀區做了什麼改變？ B：她把明亮的天花板燈換成小檯燈，所以現在大家可以坐在舒適的椅子上，在溫暖的【燈光】下閱讀，許多顧客待得更久、買更多書。"},{"w":"fireplace","p":"n.","d":"an open place in the wall of a room where a fire is made","c":"壁爐","s":"A: The mountain lodge we booked for the winter team-building weekend looks great online, but will it be warm enough at night? B: Don't worry, the main living room has a large stone fireplace, and the staff will light a fire every evening so we can sit together, drink hot tea, and chat.","t":"A：我們為冬季團隊建立週末預訂的山中小屋在網路上看起來很棒，但晚上會夠暖和嗎？ B：別擔心，主客廳有一座大型石砌【壁爐】，工作人員每天晚上都會生火，讓我們可以坐在一起喝熱茶聊天。"},{"w":"moonrise","p":"n.","d":"the time when the moon first appears in the sky","c":"月出；月亮升起","s":"A: The resort is offering a special evening boat tour on Saturday, so what makes it different from the regular sightseeing trips? B: The boat leaves the harbor just before moonrise, so guests can watch the full moon slowly appear over the sea while they enjoy a light meal and live music.","t":"A：度假村星期六推出特別的夜間遊船行程，它和一般的觀光行程有什麼不同？ B：船會在【月出】前離開港口，讓旅客在享用簡餐和現場音樂的同時，欣賞滿月緩緩從海面上升起。"},{"w":"starry","p":"adj.","d":"full of stars","c":"佈滿星星的；星光燦爛的","s":"A: Why did the tour company choose a campsite so far from the city for the overnight trip with our overseas clients? B: The area has almost no light pollution, so on clear nights guests can lie on the grass and look up at a starry sky, which is something they can never see at home.","t":"A：旅行社為什麼要為我們海外客戶的過夜行程選一個離城市這麼遠的營地？ B：那個地區幾乎沒有光害，所以在晴朗的夜晚，客人可以躺在草地上仰望【繁星點點的】天空，這是他們在家鄉永遠看不到的。"},{"w":"pleasant","p":"adj.","d":"nice and enjoyable","c":"令人愉快的；宜人的","s":"A: How was the welcome reception for the new branch manager last night, and did she get a chance to meet everyone? B: It was a very pleasant evening, because the food was delicious, the speeches were short, and she spent time talking with almost every staff member in a friendly way.","t":"A：昨晚新分行經理的歡迎會怎麼樣？她有機會見到每個人嗎？ B：那是一個非常【愉快的】夜晚，因為食物很美味、致詞很簡短，而且她親切地跟幾乎每一位員工都聊了天。"},{"w":"wind-down","p":"n.","d":"a period of slowly becoming less active before stopping","c":"逐步減緩；收尾","s":"A: The factory runs three shifts a day, so how do the night supervisors prepare the machines before the morning team arrives? B: During the last hour there is a slow wind-down of production, when workers turn off the machines one by one, clean the equipment, and write notes for the next shift.","t":"A：工廠一天三班運作，夜班主管們在早班人員到達前如何準備機器？ B：在最後一個小時會有一段生產逐步【收尾減緩】的時間，工人們會逐一關閉機器、清潔設備，並為下一班寫下交接紀錄。"}]},{"unit":127,"theme":"Exercise 運動","cards":[{"w":"workout","p":"n.","d":"a session of physical exercise","c":"健身鍛鍊；運動","s":"A: You look really tired today, so did you stay late at the office again to finish the quarterly sales report for the director? B: No, I finished it yesterday, but I joined a new class at the gym after work and the workout was much harder than I expected, so my legs still hurt this morning.","t":"A：你今天看起來很累，是不是又在辦公室待到很晚，把要給主管的季度銷售報告做完？ B：不是，我昨天就做完了，但我下班後在健身房參加了一個新課程，那次【健身鍛鍊】比我預期的難得多，所以我的腿到今天早上還在痛。"},{"w":"train","p":"v.","d":"to practice a sport or skill to get ready for something","c":"訓練；鍛鍊","s":"A: I heard that several people from the marketing department are going to run in the city marathon next month, and are you one of them? B: Yes, I am, and I train three evenings a week with a coach near my apartment because I want to finish the race in under four hours.","t":"A：我聽說行銷部有好幾個人下個月要參加城市馬拉松，你是其中之一嗎？ B：是的，我有參加，而且我每週有三個晚上在我公寓附近跟著教練【訓練】，因為我想在四小時內跑完全程。"},{"w":"fitness","p":"n.","d":"the condition of being physically strong and healthy","c":"健康；體能","s":"A: Why did the company decide to open a small gym on the third floor instead of using the space for another meeting room? B: The managers believe that better fitness will help employees feel less stressed, take fewer sick days, and stay focused during long afternoons at their desks.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定在三樓開一間小型健身房，而不是把那個空間拿來當另一間會議室？ B：主管們相信更好的【體能】能幫助員工減輕壓力、減少請病假的天數，並在辦公桌前漫長的下午保持專注。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"the physical power to lift or move heavy things","c":"力氣；體力","s":"A: Do you think the new warehouse staff will be able to move all of these heavy boxes onto the delivery truck before the driver leaves at noon? B: I hope so, because they have a lot of strength, but we should still use the machine for the largest boxes so nobody gets hurt.","t":"A：你覺得新來的倉庫員工能在司機中午出發前，把這些很重的箱子全部搬上送貨卡車嗎？ B：希望可以，因為他們很有【力氣】，不過最大的箱子我們還是應該用機器搬，這樣才不會有人受傷。"},{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to keep doing something hard for a long time","c":"耐力","s":"A: How did you manage to hike all the way to the top of the mountain during the company retreat while most of us stopped halfway to rest? B: I have been swimming every morning for a year, so my endurance is much better now, and I did not feel tired until we reached the top.","t":"A：公司員工旅遊時，我們大多數人爬到一半就停下來休息，你是怎麼一路爬到山頂的？ B：我已經每天早上游泳游了一年，所以我的【耐力】現在好多了，一直到我們抵達山頂我都沒覺得累。"},{"w":"flexibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to bend your body easily","c":"柔軟度","s":"A: Why does the physical therapist at the clinic want you to do yoga twice a week after you finish work at the office? B: She says sitting at my desk for nine hours a day has reduced my flexibility, so my back and shoulders feel stiff and I often get pain when I bend down.","t":"A：為什麼診所的物理治療師要你在辦公室下班後每週做兩次瑜伽？ B：她說我每天坐在辦公桌前九個小時，降低了我的【柔軟度】，所以我的背和肩膀感覺很僵硬，彎腰時也常常會痛。"},{"w":"stretch","p":"v.","d":"to make your arms, legs or body longer to relax your muscles","c":"伸展","s":"A: My neck and shoulders always feel tight by the end of the day, and I am not sure what I should do about it at work. B: Every hour, you should stand up, stretch your arms above your head for a minute, and take a short break from your computer screen to rest your eyes.","t":"A：我的脖子和肩膀到下班時總是很緊繃，我不確定上班時該怎麼辦。 B：你應該每小時站起來一次，把手臂舉過頭頂【伸展】一分鐘，並暫時離開電腦螢幕休息一下，讓眼睛放鬆。"},{"w":"warm-up","p":"n.","d":"gentle exercise you do before harder exercise","c":"暖身運動","s":"A: Should we start the company soccer game right away, since everyone is already here and the field is only booked until six o'clock? B: Let's do a short warm-up first, because several players came straight from the office and could easily pull a muscle if they start running too fast.","t":"A：既然大家都到了，而且球場只預約到六點，我們要不要馬上開始公司的足球比賽？ B：我們先做個簡短的【暖身運動】吧，因為有幾位球員是直接從辦公室過來的，如果一開始就跑太快，很容易拉傷肌肉。"},{"w":"cool-down","p":"n.","d":"slow, easy exercise you do after hard exercise to help your body relax","c":"緩和運動","s":"A: After the spinning class at the fitness center last night, my legs felt so heavy that I could hardly walk up the stairs to my apartment. B: Did you skip the cool-down at the end of the class? The instructor says ten minutes of slow pedaling and stretching really helps your muscles recover.","t":"A：昨晚在健身中心上完飛輪課後，我的腿重到幾乎爬不上樓梯回公寓。 B：你是不是跳過了課程最後的【緩和運動】？教練說十分鐘的慢速踩踏和伸展真的很有助於肌肉恢復。"},{"w":"jog","p":"v.","d":"to run slowly and steadily for exercise","c":"慢跑","s":"A: Since our hotel is right next to the river, do you want to do something active before the sales conference starts tomorrow morning? B: Sure, let's meet in the lobby at six and jog along the river path for about thirty minutes, then we can have breakfast together before the first session.","t":"A：既然我們的飯店就在河邊，明天早上業務會議開始前，你想不想做點運動？ B：好啊，我們六點在大廳碰面，然後沿著河邊步道【慢跑】大約三十分鐘，接著可以在第一場會議前一起吃早餐。"},{"w":"run","p":"v.","d":"to move very quickly on your feet","c":"跑步","s":"A: How do you stay so fit when you work such long hours at the bank and also have two young children at home? B: I run to the office three days a week instead of taking the bus, so I get my exercise and save money on transportation at the same time.","t":"A：你在銀行工作時間那麼長，家裡又有兩個小孩，你是怎麼保持這麼好的身材？ B：我每週有三天【跑步】去辦公室，而不是搭公車，這樣既能運動，又能同時省下交通費。"},{"w":"walk","p":"v.","d":"to move on foot at a normal speed","c":"走路；步行","s":"A: The doctor at my annual health check said I need to move more, but I really don't have time to go to the gym after work. B: Why not walk to the train station every morning instead of driving? It only takes twenty minutes, and you can listen to podcasts on the way.","t":"A：年度健康檢查的醫生說我需要多活動，但我下班後真的沒時間去健身房。 B：何不每天早上【走路】去火車站，而不是開車呢？只要二十分鐘，而且你還可以在路上聽播客。"},{"w":"cycle","p":"v.","d":"to ride a bicycle","c":"騎自行車","s":"A: The parking fees near our new office building are really expensive, so how are you planning to get to work every day? B: I've decided to cycle to work along the new bike lane, which is cheaper than driving, good for my health, and only takes about twenty-five minutes.","t":"A：我們新辦公大樓附近的停車費真的很貴，你打算每天怎麼去上班？ B：我決定沿著新的自行車道【騎自行車】上班，這比開車便宜，對健康也有好處，而且只要大約二十五分鐘。"},{"w":"swim","p":"v.","d":"to move through water using your arms and legs","c":"游泳","s":"A: The hotel we booked for the sales training has a large indoor pool on the top floor, but are you going to use it? B: Yes, I plan to swim for half an hour every morning before the workshop begins, because it helps me wake up and feel relaxed before a long day.","t":"A：我們為業務訓練預訂的飯店頂樓有一座大型室內游泳池，你會去用嗎？ B：會啊，我打算每天早上在研習開始前【游泳】半小時，因為這能幫助我清醒，並在漫長的一天之前感到放鬆。"},{"w":"lift","p":"v.","d":"to raise something heavy, such as weights or boxes","c":"舉起；抬起","s":"A: Why did your manager tell you to ask for help when the new printers arrive at the office later this afternoon? B: She knows I hurt my back last month, and the doctor told me not to lift anything heavier than ten kilograms until my next appointment in two weeks.","t":"A：為什麼你的主管叫你今天下午新印表機送到辦公室時要找人幫忙？ B：她知道我上個月傷到背，而醫生告訴我，在兩週後的下次回診之前，不要【舉起】任何超過十公斤的東西。"},{"w":"aerobic","p":"adj.","d":"describing exercise that makes your heart and lungs work harder, like running or dancing","c":"有氧的","s":"A: The fitness center near our office offers many different classes, so which one would you recommend for a beginner like me? B: I would start with a simple aerobic dance class on Tuesday evenings, because it raises your heart rate, burns calories, and the music makes the hour go by quickly.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近的健身中心有很多不同的課程，你會推薦哪一種給像我這樣的初學者？ B：我會從週二晚上簡單的【有氧】舞蹈課開始，因為它能提高心率、燃燒卡路里，而且音樂讓那一小時過得很快。"},{"w":"vigorous","p":"adj.","d":"very active, strong and full of energy","c":"劇烈的；激烈的","s":"A: My doctor said I should get more exercise, but should I start with long runs every day to lose weight more quickly? B: Not yet, because vigorous exercise can be dangerous if your body isn't ready, so begin with gentle walks and slowly increase the time and speed over several weeks.","t":"A：醫生說我應該多運動，但我要不要一開始就每天長跑，好讓體重減得更快？ B：先不要，因為如果你的身體還沒準備好，【劇烈的】運動可能會很危險，所以先從輕鬆的散步開始，然後在幾週內慢慢增加時間和速度。"},{"w":"moderate","p":"adj.","d":"not too much and not too little; medium","c":"適度的；中等的","s":"A: How much exercise do you think our older employees should do each week if they want to join the new company health program? B: The program's nurse suggests about thirty minutes of moderate activity five days a week, such as brisk walking or light cycling, which is safe for most people.","t":"A：如果年紀較大的員工想參加公司新的健康計畫，你覺得他們每週應該做多少運動？ B：計畫的護理師建議每週五天、每次大約三十分鐘的【適度】活動，例如快走或輕鬆騎腳踏車，這對大多數人來說都很安全。"},{"w":"active","p":"adj.","d":"moving around and doing things a lot","c":"活躍的；好動的","s":"A: Since you started working from home last year, do you find it harder to stay healthy without the daily trip to the office? B: Yes, so I try to stay active by taking the stairs, playing tennis with my neighbors on weekends, and walking my dog twice a day around the park.","t":"A：自從你去年開始在家工作後，少了每天通勤去辦公室，你會覺得比較難保持健康嗎？ B：會，所以我盡量保持【活躍】，像是走樓梯、週末跟鄰居打網球，還有每天帶狗繞公園散步兩次。"},{"w":"sedentary","p":"adj.","d":"involving a lot of sitting and little movement","c":"久坐的","s":"A: Why is the human resources department buying standing desks for everyone in the accounting team this month? B: Accountants have a very sedentary job, sitting in front of computers for most of the day, and the company hopes the new desks will reduce back pain and help people move more.","t":"A：人資部門為什麼這個月要幫會計團隊每個人購買站立式辦公桌？ B：會計師的工作非常【久坐】，一天大部分時間都坐在電腦前，公司希望新的辦公桌能減少背痛，並幫助大家多活動。"},{"w":"trainer","p":"n.","d":"a person who teaches people how to exercise","c":"教練","s":"A: You've lost a lot of weight since the summer, so did you follow a special diet or join a sports team after work? B: Neither, actually; I hired a personal trainer at the gym near my office, and she designed a program that fits my busy schedule and keeps me motivated.","t":"A：你從夏天以來瘦了很多，你是有遵循特別的飲食，還是下班後參加了運動隊？ B：其實都不是；我在辦公室附近的健身房請了一位私人【教練】，她設計了一套符合我忙碌行程的計畫，讓我保持動力。"},{"w":"gym","p":"n.","d":"a room or building with equipment for exercise","c":"健身房","s":"A: Is it true that the company is offering a discount on memberships for employees who want to exercise after work? B: Yes, the gym across the street from our building gives us thirty percent off, and it stays open until eleven at night, so even people who work late can go.","t":"A：公司真的有提供會員優惠給想在下班後運動的員工嗎？ B：是的，我們大樓對面的【健身房】給我們打七折，而且營業到晚上十一點，所以就算是加班的人也可以去。"},{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual set of things you do regularly","c":"例行公事；固定習慣","s":"A: How do you find time to exercise when you travel so often for business meetings in different cities? B: I keep a simple routine of push-ups, sit-ups, and stretching that I can do in any hotel room in twenty minutes, so I never have to skip a day.","t":"A：你經常到不同城市出差開會，是怎麼找出時間運動的？ B：我維持一套簡單的伏地挺身、仰臥起坐和伸展的【固定習慣】，在任何飯店房間二十分鐘就能做完，所以我從不需要停一天。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to stay steady without falling","c":"平衡","s":"A: Why does the yoga teacher at the community center ask everyone to stand on one leg at the start of every class? B: She says it improves your balance and helps prevent falls as you get older, which is why many retired people from our company now attend her lessons.","t":"A：社區中心的瑜伽老師為什麼每堂課一開始都要大家單腳站立？ B：她說這能改善你的【平衡】，並幫助你在年紀漸長時預防跌倒，這也是為什麼我們公司許多退休人員現在都去上她的課。"},{"w":"posture","p":"n.","d":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand","c":"姿勢","s":"A: I have had terrible back pain since I started working on the new design project, and I don't understand why. B: You often lean forward toward your laptop for hours, so your posture is poor; try raising the screen and sitting up straight with both feet on the floor.","t":"A：自從我開始做新的設計專案後，背就痛得很厲害，我不明白為什麼。 B：你常常好幾個小時身體前傾靠向筆電，所以你的【姿勢】很差；試著把螢幕架高，坐直並讓雙腳平放在地上。"},{"w":"heartbeat","p":"n.","d":"the regular movement or sound of your heart","c":"心跳","s":"A: Why are so many people in our department wearing those new smart watches that the company gave out last week? B: The watches check your heartbeat while you exercise and send a warning if it gets too fast, so people feel safer when they jog or play sports after work.","t":"A：為什麼我們部門這麼多人都戴著公司上週發的新智慧手錶？ B：這些手錶會在你運動時監測你的【心跳】，太快時還會發出警告，所以大家下班後慢跑或運動時會覺得比較安全。"},{"w":"sweat","p":"v.","d":"to produce liquid through your skin when you are hot or working hard","c":"流汗","s":"A: Why do you always bring an extra shirt to the office on the days when you ride your bike to work? B: The road from my apartment has two steep hills, and I sweat a lot on the way, so I change clothes before my first meeting with clients.","t":"A：為什麼你騎腳踏車上班的那幾天總是多帶一件襯衫到辦公室？ B：我公寓出來的路上有兩個陡坡，我在路上會【流汗】流很多，所以在跟客戶第一場會議之前我會換衣服。"},{"w":"breathe","p":"v.","d":"to take air into your body and let it out","c":"呼吸","s":"A: I always feel so nervous before I give a presentation to the board of directors, and my voice starts to shake. B: Before you walk into the meeting room, stand still, breathe slowly and deeply for one minute, and you will feel much calmer and more confident when you begin.","t":"A：每次要向董事會做簡報前我都非常緊張，聲音還會開始發抖。 B：在你走進會議室之前，先站好，緩慢而深沉地【呼吸】一分鐘，你開始報告時就會覺得冷靜許多，也更有自信。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to become healthy or strong again after an illness, injury or hard exercise","c":"恢復；康復","s":"A: Is Daniel coming back to work on Monday, or will he need more time off after hurting his knee in the company soccer game? B: The doctor said it will take about three weeks for him to recover fully, so he will work from home until he can walk without pain.","t":"A：Daniel星期一會回來上班嗎？還是他在公司足球賽傷到膝蓋後需要更多休假？ B：醫生說他大約需要三週才能完全【康復】，所以在他能不痛地走路之前，他會在家工作。"},{"w":"muscle","p":"n.","d":"a part of the body that tightens and relaxes to make you move","c":"肌肉","s":"A: You were walking strangely when you came into the office this morning, so did something happen on your way to work? B: I pulled a muscle in my leg while I was playing basketball with my coworkers last night, so the nurse told me to rest and put ice on it.","t":"A：你今天早上進辦公室時走路怪怪的，上班途中發生了什麼事嗎？ B：我昨晚跟同事打籃球時拉傷了腿部的【肌肉】，所以護理師叫我休息並冰敷。"},{"w":"calorie","p":"n.","d":"a unit that measures the energy in food","c":"卡路里；熱量","s":"A: The new cafeteria menu shows a number next to every meal, but what does that number actually mean for the staff? B: It shows the total amount of energy in each dish, so if you want to lose weight, you can count every calorie you eat at lunch and choose lighter meals more easily.","t":"A：新的員工餐廳菜單在每道餐點旁邊都標了一個數字，那個數字對員工來說到底代表什麼？ B：它顯示每道菜的總熱量，所以如果你想減重，就可以計算午餐吃下的每一【卡路里】，更輕鬆地選擇比較清淡的餐點。"},{"w":"healthy","p":"adj.","d":"physically strong and not sick","c":"健康的","s":"A: Why does the company give every employee free fruit in the break room and pay for a yearly medical check-up? B: The managers know that healthy workers take fewer sick days and have more energy, so these small costs actually save the company money over time.","t":"A：為什麼公司在休息室提供每位員工免費水果，還支付每年的健康檢查費用？ B：主管們知道【健康的】員工請病假的天數比較少，精力也比較充沛，所以這些小小的花費長期下來其實能幫公司省錢。"},{"w":"energetic","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of energy and being very active","c":"精力充沛的","s":"A: How do you feel since you started going swimming before work three times a week with your neighbor? B: I feel much more energetic during the day, and I no longer need two cups of coffee after lunch to stay awake in long afternoon meetings with clients.","t":"A：自從你開始每週三次在上班前跟鄰居去游泳後，感覺怎麼樣？ B：我白天覺得【精力充沛】多了，在下午跟客戶的長時間會議裡，也不再需要午餐後喝兩杯咖啡來保持清醒。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often, at the same times each day or week","c":"規律地；定期地","s":"A: My new doctor told me that short exercise once a month is not enough, but I don't understand why that matters. B: Your body only gets stronger if you exercise regularly, so it is better to walk for thirty minutes every day than to run for three hours once a month.","t":"A：我的新醫生說一個月運動一次短時間是不夠的，但我不懂為什麼那很重要。 B：你的身體只有在你【規律地】運動時才會變得更強壯，所以每天走路三十分鐘，比一個月跑一次三小時還要好。"},{"w":"physically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to the body","c":"身體上；體力上","s":"A: Why does the delivery company give new drivers a health check before they start working on the trucks next month? B: The job is very physically demanding, because drivers carry heavy packages up and down stairs all day, so the company wants to be sure they are strong enough.","t":"A：為什麼這家快遞公司要在新司機下個月開始上卡車工作之前，先幫他們做健康檢查？ B：這份工作在【體力上】要求非常高，因為司機整天都要搬著重包裹上下樓梯，所以公司想確定他們夠強壯。"}]},{"unit":128,"theme":"Exhibition 展覽","cards":[{"w":"display","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement of things for people to look at","c":"展示；陳列","s":"A: Why did the marketing team ask the store staff to stay late on Friday evening after all the customers had gone home? B: They wanted to set up a new window display of our winter jackets and boots, so shoppers walking past the mall entrance would notice the products on Saturday morning.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊要求店員在週五晚上所有顧客離開後留下來加班？ B：他們想布置一個新的冬季外套和靴子櫥窗【展示】，讓週六早上經過購物中心入口的購物者能注意到這些商品。"},{"w":"gallery","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where art is shown or sold","c":"畫廊；美術館","s":"A: Where should we take the visiting clients from Japan after our long meeting ends on Thursday afternoon? B: There is a small art gallery next to the hotel that shows paintings by local artists, and it stays open until eight, so we could walk there before having dinner together.","t":"A：週四下午漫長的會議結束後，我們應該帶來訪的日本客戶去哪裡？ B：飯店旁邊有一間小型藝術【畫廊】展出本地藝術家的畫作，而且開到八點，所以我們可以在一起吃晚餐前走過去看看。"},{"w":"museum","p":"n.","d":"a building where old, important, or interesting objects are kept and shown","c":"博物館","s":"A: What are the new employees from the overseas branch going to do on their free day during the training week? B: The HR department has booked a group tour of the city's history museum, where they can learn about the local culture, and then they will have lunch at a traditional restaurant nearby.","t":"A：海外分公司的新進員工在訓練週的空閒日要做什麼？ B：人資部門已經預約了市立歷史【博物館】的團體導覽，讓他們可以認識當地文化，之後他們會在附近一家傳統餐廳吃午餐。"},{"w":"showcase","p":"n.","d":"an event or place that shows the best qualities of something","c":"展示會；展示平台","s":"A: Why is the design department working so hard on those product samples even though the launch is still two months away? B: The annual technology showcase in Taipei is next week, and our manager hopes that presenting our new smart lamps there will attract buyers from several large international companies.","t":"A：為什麼設計部門這麼努力準備那些產品樣品，明明上市還有兩個月？ B：台北的年度科技【展示會】就在下週，我們經理希望在那裡展示新的智慧檯燈能吸引幾家大型國際公司的買家。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of similar things that someone has gathered","c":"收藏品；館藏","s":"A: Do you know why there are so many security guards standing near the entrance of our office building this morning? B: Our company chairman is lending his private collection of rare old coins to the city museum for a special show, so the guards are protecting the boxes until the delivery trucks arrive.","t":"A：你知道為什麼今天早上我們辦公大樓入口附近站了這麼多保全嗎？ B：我們公司董事長要把他私人的稀有古錢幣【收藏】借給市立博物館辦特展，所以保全在保護那些箱子，直到運送的卡車抵達。"},{"w":"artifact","p":"n.","d":"an object made by people long ago that is historically interesting","c":"文物；古器物","s":"A: Why has the construction work on the new shopping center across from our office stopped for the past two weeks? B: The workers dug up an ancient artifact while they were preparing the ground, so the city sent experts to study the area carefully before the building project can continue.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室對面新購物中心的工程已經停了兩個星期？ B：工人在整地時挖出了一件古代【文物】，所以市政府派了專家來仔細研究那個區域，之後建案才能繼續進行。"},{"w":"painting","p":"n.","d":"a picture made with paint","c":"畫作；繪畫","s":"A: Have you decided what we should buy as a retirement gift for Mr. Lin, who has worked in our accounting department for thirty years? B: Since he loves the mountains, I suggest a large painting of Yushan by a local artist, which he can hang in his living room at home.","t":"A：你決定好我們要買什麼退休禮物送給在會計部工作了三十年的林先生了嗎？ B：既然他熱愛山，我建議買一幅本地藝術家畫的玉山大型【畫作】，他可以掛在家裡的客廳。"},{"w":"sculpture","p":"n.","d":"a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, metal, or clay","c":"雕塑；雕像","s":"A: What is that huge metal object that the workers are putting in front of the main entrance of our headquarters? B: It is a modern sculpture designed by a famous artist from Spain, and the board of directors hopes it will make our building look more welcoming to clients and visitors.","t":"A：工人們放在我們總部大門前面的那個巨大金屬物體是什麼？ B：那是一位西班牙知名藝術家設計的現代【雕塑】，董事會希望它能讓我們的大樓對客戶和訪客看起來更親切。"},{"w":"installation","p":"n.","d":"a large artwork made for a particular space, often with light, sound, or objects","c":"裝置藝術","s":"A: Why are so many young people taking photos on the second floor of the shopping mall this weekend? B: An artist created a light installation there with thousands of tiny colored lamps hanging from the ceiling, and it has become very popular on social media since it opened on Friday.","t":"A：為什麼這個週末有這麼多年輕人在購物中心二樓拍照？ B：一位藝術家在那裡創作了一件燈光【裝置藝術】，有上千盞彩色小燈從天花板垂下來，自從週五開放以來就在社群媒體上非常受歡迎。"},{"w":"photography","p":"n.","d":"the art or job of taking photos","c":"攝影","s":"A: Why did you sign up for that evening class at the community center when you are already so busy at the office? B: Our company website needs better pictures of our products, so I want to improve my photography skills, and the class teaches lighting and camera settings every Tuesday night.","t":"A：你在辦公室已經這麼忙了，為什麼還報名社區中心的夜間課程？ B：我們公司網站需要更好的產品照片，所以我想提升我的【攝影】技巧，而那門課每週二晚上教打光和相機設定。"},{"w":"artist","p":"n.","d":"a person who paints, draws, or makes art","c":"藝術家；畫家","s":"A: Who designed the colorful wall pictures in the new staff lounge that everyone has been talking about this week? B: The office manager hired a young local artist who spent three days painting flowers and city scenes on the walls, and she even asked employees for ideas before she started.","t":"A：這週大家都在討論的新員工休息室裡那些色彩繽紛的牆面圖畫是誰設計的？ B：辦公室經理請了一位年輕的本地【藝術家】，她花了三天在牆上畫花朵和城市風景，而且開始之前還詢問了員工的想法。"},{"w":"curator","p":"n.","d":"a person in charge of the objects in a museum or gallery","c":"策展人；館長","s":"A: Who should I contact about borrowing some old photographs of our factory for the company's fiftieth anniversary event next month? B: You should email the curator at the city history museum, because she is responsible for the items they keep and decides whether they can be lent to other organizations.","t":"A：為了下個月公司五十週年活動，我想借一些工廠的老照片，應該聯絡誰？ B：你應該寫電子郵件給市立歷史博物館的【策展人】，因為她負責館內保存的物品，並決定是否能借給其他機構。"},{"w":"theme","p":"n.","d":"the main subject or idea of an event or work","c":"主題","s":"A: Has the planning committee decided on the decorations for the company's year-end party at the hotel ballroom? B: Yes, they chose \"Travel Around the World\" as the theme, so each department will decorate a table with food and pictures from a different country, and guests can wear costumes.","t":"A：籌備委員會決定好公司在飯店宴會廳舉辦的尾牙裝飾了嗎？ B：決定了，他們選了「環遊世界」作為【主題】，所以每個部門會用不同國家的食物和圖片布置一張桌子，賓客也可以穿戲服。"},{"w":"venue","p":"n.","d":"the place where an event happens","c":"場地；會場","s":"A: Why did the event organizers move the product launch from the downtown hotel to the convention center at the last minute? B: More than five hundred guests registered, so the hotel ballroom was too small, and they needed a larger venue with enough seats, parking spaces, and a big stage.","t":"A：為什麼活動主辦單位在最後一刻把產品發表會從市中心飯店改到會展中心？ B：報名的賓客超過五百人，飯店宴會廳太小了，他們需要一個有足夠座位、停車位和大舞台的更大【場地】。"},{"w":"opening","p":"n.","d":"the first day or ceremony when something starts or opens to the public","c":"開幕；開幕式","s":"A: Are you going to the new art center downtown on Saturday evening, or do you have to work overtime again? B: I'm definitely going, because our company sponsored the grand opening, and my manager asked me to welcome the guests and give out free drinks at the front door.","t":"A：你週六晚上會去市中心新的藝術中心嗎？還是你又得加班？ B：我一定會去，因為我們公司贊助了盛大的【開幕式】，經理要我在門口迎接賓客並發送免費飲料。"},{"w":"visitor","p":"n.","d":"a person who comes to see a place or person","c":"訪客；參觀者","s":"A: Why does the security guard at the front desk ask everyone to sign a book when they enter our building? B: Every visitor must write down their name, the company they work for, and the time they arrive, so that the office knows exactly who is inside in case of an emergency.","t":"A：為什麼前台的保全要每個進入我們大樓的人在本子上簽名？ B：每位【訪客】都必須寫下姓名、任職的公司和抵達時間，這樣萬一發生緊急狀況，辦公室才能確切知道誰在裡面。"},{"w":"ticket","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper or digital code that lets you enter an event","c":"門票；票","s":"A: How much did it cost the company to take our whole sales team to the science fair in Kaohsiung last weekend? B: Each ticket was only two hundred dollars because we bought them online a month early, but the train fares and hotel rooms made the total cost much higher.","t":"A：上週末公司帶整個業務團隊去高雄的科學展花了多少錢？ B：每張【門票】只要兩百元，因為我們提早一個月在網路上買，但火車票和飯店房間讓總花費高了很多。"},{"w":"brochure","p":"n.","d":"a thin booklet with pictures and information about a product, service, or event","c":"小冊子；簡介手冊","s":"A: What should we hand to the guests who stop at our booth at the trade show next Wednesday? B: The design team printed a colorful brochure that explains our products, prices, and contact information, so visitors can take it home and read it later when they have more time.","t":"A：下週三商展時，我們應該發什麼給停在我們攤位的來賓？ B：設計團隊印了一份彩色的【簡介手冊】，說明我們的產品、價格和聯絡資訊，讓訪客可以帶回家，等有空時再讀。"},{"w":"catalog","p":"n.","d":"a list or book of all the items for sale or on show","c":"目錄；型錄","s":"A: How can our customers in other countries find out about all the furniture we sell if they cannot visit the showroom? B: We send them our online catalog, which has photos, sizes, and prices of every sofa and table, and they can place orders directly on the website.","t":"A：如果其他國家的客戶無法參觀展示間，他們要怎麼了解我們販售的所有家具？ B：我們會寄給他們線上【型錄】，裡面有每張沙發和桌子的照片、尺寸和價格，他們可以直接在網站上下單。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"letting people take part by touching, using, or responding","c":"互動的","s":"A: Why do children enjoy the new science center so much more than the old one that closed last year? B: The new building has many interactive screens and machines that let kids press buttons, play games, and do simple experiments themselves instead of just reading signs on the walls.","t":"A：為什麼孩子們比較喜歡新的科學中心，而不是去年關閉的舊館？ B：新館有許多【互動式】螢幕和機器，讓孩子可以自己按按鈕、玩遊戲、做簡單的實驗，而不只是讀牆上的說明牌。"},{"w":"educational","p":"adj.","d":"teaching people something useful","c":"有教育意義的","s":"A: Why did the school choose the ocean exhibit for the students' field trip instead of the amusement park this year? B: The teachers wanted something more educational, so the students can learn about sea animals and pollution, and they will also write short reports about what they saw afterward.","t":"A：為什麼學校今年的校外教學選擇海洋特展而不是遊樂園？ B：老師們想要更有【教育意義】的活動，讓學生可以認識海洋動物和污染問題，之後他們也要針對所見寫簡短的報告。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for only a short time","c":"暫時的；臨時的","s":"A: Is the dinosaur show at the natural history museum going to stay there for the rest of the year? B: No, it is only a temporary exhibit that will close at the end of March, so if you want to take your kids, you should buy tickets online soon before they sell out.","t":"A：自然史博物館的恐龍展會一直展到年底嗎？ B：不會，那只是一個【短期的】特展，三月底就會結束，所以如果你想帶孩子去，應該盡快在網路上買票，以免賣完。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a very long time or forever","c":"永久的；常設的","s":"A: Will the famous painting that was shown here last month return to the gallery in Paris after the show ends? B: No, our museum bought it from the owner, so it is now part of the permanent collection, and visitors will be able to see it in the main hall every day.","t":"A：上個月在這裡展出的那幅名畫，展覽結束後會回到巴黎的美術館嗎？ B：不會，我們博物館向收藏者買下了它，所以它現在是【永久】館藏的一部分，訪客每天都能在主廳看到它。"},{"w":"visual","p":"adj.","d":"relating to seeing or things you can see","c":"視覺的","s":"A: Do you think our sales presentation for the hotel group next Monday needs any changes before we send it out? B: The information is good, but it has too much text, so I suggest adding more visual elements like charts, photos, and short videos to keep the audience interested.","t":"A：你覺得我們下週一要給飯店集團的業務簡報在寄出前需要修改嗎？ B：內容很好，但文字太多，所以我建議加入更多像圖表、照片和短片這類【視覺】元素，讓聽眾保持興趣。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"having or using new and original ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: Why did the advertising agency hire that young designer even though she has only one year of work experience? B: Her ideas are very creative and fresh, and during the interview she showed a poster campaign that helped a small café double its customers in just three months.","t":"A：為什麼廣告公司會錄用那位年輕設計師，明明她只有一年工作經驗？ B：她的想法非常【有創意】又新穎，而且面試時她展示了一個海報宣傳活動，幫助一家小咖啡館在短短三個月內客人翻倍。"},{"w":"informative","p":"adj.","d":"giving useful information","c":"提供有用資訊的；內容豐富的","s":"A: How was the safety training session that the factory manager organized for all the new workers yesterday afternoon? B: It was very informative, because the trainer explained how to use each machine correctly, showed real examples of accidents, and answered every question we asked clearly.","t":"A：昨天下午廠長為所有新進員工安排的安全訓練課程怎麼樣？ B：內容非常【豐富實用】，因為講師說明了如何正確使用每台機器、展示了真實的事故案例，並清楚回答了我們提出的每個問題。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around or look at a place to learn about it","c":"探索；探究","s":"A: What are you planning to do during your free afternoon after the conference in Tokyo ends on Friday? B: I want to explore the old neighborhoods near the river, visit a few small shops and temples, and try some local street food before I fly back to Taipei on Saturday.","t":"A：週五東京的會議結束後，你空閒的下午打算做什麼？ B：我想去【探索】河邊的老街區，逛幾家小店和寺廟，再嚐嚐當地的街頭小吃，然後週六飛回台北。"},{"w":"observe","p":"v.","d":"to watch someone or something carefully","c":"觀察","s":"A: Why is the new assistant sitting in the back of the meeting room without saying anything during the client meetings? B: The manager asked her to observe how the senior staff talk with customers and handle difficult questions, so she can learn before she starts leading meetings herself next month.","t":"A：為什麼新助理在客戶會議時都坐在會議室後面一句話也不說？ B：經理要她【觀察】資深員工如何與客戶交談及處理困難的問題，這樣她下個月開始自己主持會議前就能先學習。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to understand and enjoy the good qualities of something","c":"欣賞；重視","s":"A: Why did the museum guide ask everyone to put away their phones before entering the main hall this afternoon? B: She said visitors can appreciate the details of the paintings much better when they look carefully with their own eyes instead of taking photos the whole time.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午博物館導覽員要大家在進入主廳前把手機收起來？ B：她說訪客用自己的眼睛仔細看，而不是一直拍照，才更能【欣賞】畫作的細節。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the idea or desire to do something","c":"啟發；激勵","s":"A: Why does the company invite successful business owners to speak to the young employees every month? B: The managers hope their stories will inspire the staff to work harder, share new ideas, and maybe even start their own projects within the company in the future.","t":"A：為什麼公司每個月都邀請成功的企業主來對年輕員工演講？ B：主管們希望他們的故事能【激勵】員工更努力工作、分享新點子，甚至未來在公司內部發起自己的專案。"},{"w":"highlight","p":"v.","d":"to show that something is important; to make something stand out","c":"強調；突顯","s":"A: What should I focus on in my report about the trade fair for the board meeting tomorrow morning? B: You should highlight the three new contracts we signed with buyers from Europe, because the directors care most about results and will want to know how much income they will bring.","t":"A：明天早上董事會的商展報告，我應該著重在哪裡？ B：你應該【強調】我們和歐洲買家簽下的三份新合約，因為董事們最在意成果，也會想知道這些合約能帶來多少收入。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk that gives information about something","c":"簡報；發表","s":"A: Why are you staying so late at the office tonight when everyone else has already gone home? B: I have to give a presentation about our new product line to the sales directors at nine tomorrow morning, and I still need to finish the slides and practice what I want to say.","t":"A：大家都回家了，為什麼你今晚還在辦公室待這麼晚？ B：明天早上九點我要向業務總監們做一場關於新產品線的【簡報】，我還得完成投影片並練習要說的內容。"},{"w":"guided","p":"adj.","d":"led by a guide who shows and explains things","c":"有導覽的","s":"A: How will the overseas partners see our factory when they visit Hsinchu next Tuesday afternoon? B: The production manager will lead a guided tour of the whole building, explaining each step of the process, and afterwards the partners will have tea and cake in the meeting room.","t":"A：下週二下午海外合作夥伴來新竹時，要怎麼參觀我們的工廠？ B：生產經理會帶領一場整棟廠房的【導覽】參觀，說明製程的每個步驟，之後夥伴們會在會議室享用茶點和蛋糕。"},{"w":"cultural","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the customs, arts, and beliefs of a group of people","c":"文化的","s":"A: Why do we give new foreign employees a short training course before they start working with our local customers? B: There are many cultural differences in how people greet each other, give gifts, and talk about business, so the course helps them avoid embarrassing mistakes with clients.","t":"A：為什麼我們要在外籍新進員工開始接觸本地客戶前，先讓他們上一個短期訓練課程？ B：人們打招呼、送禮和談生意的方式有許多【文化】差異，所以這個課程幫助他們避免在客戶面前犯下尷尬的錯誤。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that everyone can see or know about","c":"公開地","s":"A: When will the company tell everyone about the plan to open three new stores in southern Taiwan next year? B: The CEO will announce the plan publicly at a press conference on Monday, but until then, managers have asked staff not to discuss it with customers or post anything online.","t":"A：公司什麼時候會讓大家知道明年要在南台灣開三家新店的計畫？ B：執行長會在週一的記者會上【公開】宣布這項計畫，但在那之前，主管要求員工不要和客戶討論，也不要在網路上發布任何消息。"}]},{"unit":129,"theme":"Expensive 昂貴","cards":[{"w":"costly","p":"adj.","d":"costing a lot of money; causing loss or damage","c":"昂貴的；代價高的","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to cancel the plan to move our main office downtown next spring? B: She found that the move would be too costly for us this year, because the rent is much higher there and we would also need new furniture and computers for every department.","t":"A：經理為什麼決定取消明年春天把總公司搬到市中心的計畫？ B：她發現今年搬遷對我們來說太【昂貴】了，因為那裡的租金高得多，而且我們還需要為每個部門添購新家具和電腦。"},{"w":"pricey","p":"adj.","d":"(informal) expensive","c":"昂貴的（口語）","s":"A: Have you tried the new Italian restaurant across the street from our office, and would it be good for the team lunch on Friday? B: The food is excellent and the service is friendly, but it is a little pricey, so we should probably ask the manager whether the company will pay for it.","t":"A：你試過我們辦公室對面那家新開的義大利餐廳嗎？它適合星期五的團隊午餐嗎？ B：那裡的食物很棒，服務也很親切，但有點【貴】，所以我們大概應該問問經理公司會不會出錢。"},{"w":"luxurious","p":"adj.","d":"very comfortable and expensive","c":"豪華的；奢侈的","s":"A: How was the hotel that the travel agency booked for you during the sales conference in Singapore last week? B: It was very luxurious, with a huge bed, a marble bathroom, and a swimming pool on the roof, so I felt completely relaxed after the long meetings every day.","t":"A：上週你在新加坡參加業務會議期間，旅行社幫你訂的飯店怎麼樣？ B：那裡非常【豪華】，有超大的床、大理石浴室，屋頂還有游泳池，所以每天開完冗長的會議後我都覺得非常放鬆。"},{"w":"premium","p":"adj.","d":"of very high quality and more expensive than others","c":"高級的；優質的","s":"A: Why are we paying more for this coffee than the brand we used to buy for the office kitchen? B: The supplier only sells premium beans that are grown in the mountains and roasted carefully, and most of our staff said in the survey that they prefer the richer taste.","t":"A：為什麼我們買這種咖啡要比以前買給辦公室茶水間的牌子付更多錢？ B：這家供應商只賣在山區種植、經過細心烘焙的【高級】咖啡豆，而且大部分員工在問卷調查中都說他們比較喜歡這種更濃郁的味道。"},{"w":"high-priced","p":"adj.","d":"having a high price","c":"高價的；昂貴的","s":"A: Is the company planning to hire an outside consultant to help us with the new marketing strategy this year? B: The board thought about hiring a high-priced consultant from a famous firm in New York, but they decided our own team has enough experience to do the job well.","t":"A：公司今年打算聘請外部顧問來協助我們制定新的行銷策略嗎？ B：董事會曾考慮聘請紐約一家知名公司的【高價】顧問，但他們認為我們自己的團隊有足夠的經驗把工作做好。"},{"w":"overpriced","p":"adj.","d":"costing more than it is really worth","c":"定價過高的；太貴的","s":"A: Did you buy the new printer from the electronics store near the train station that you mentioned at the meeting? B: No, I compared prices online and found that the store's model was seriously overpriced, so I ordered the same printer from another website and saved almost a hundred dollars.","t":"A：你有在開會時提到的火車站附近那家電器行買新的印表機嗎？ B：沒有，我在網路上比價後發現那家店的機型【定價過高】得離譜，所以我在另一個網站訂了同一台印表機，省了將近一百美元。"},{"w":"exorbitant","p":"adj.","d":"much too high in price","c":"（價格）過高的；離譜的","s":"A: Why did the new tenants decide not to renew their lease for the shop on the ground floor of our building? B: The landlord asked for an exorbitant increase in rent, almost double the old amount, so they found a cheaper space in another part of the city instead.","t":"A：為什麼新房客決定不續租我們大樓一樓的店面？ B：房東要求【過高的】漲租幅度，幾乎是原本金額的兩倍，所以他們改在城裡其他地方找到了更便宜的店面。"},{"w":"valuable","p":"adj.","d":"worth a lot of money or very useful","c":"貴重的；寶貴的","s":"A: Should we keep these old customer records in the storage room, or can we throw them away before we move to the new office? B: Please keep them, because they contain valuable information about our long-term clients, and the sales team often uses it to plan special offers and follow-up calls.","t":"A：我們應該把這些舊的客戶資料留在儲藏室，還是可以在搬到新辦公室前把它們丟掉？ B：請保留下來，因為它們含有關於長期客戶的【寶貴】資訊，業務團隊經常用它來規劃特別優惠和後續追蹤電話。"},{"w":"exclusive","p":"adj.","d":"only for a few special people; expensive and not open to everyone","c":"獨有的；專屬的；高級的","s":"A: Why can't everyone attend the product launch party at the hotel next Thursday evening? B: It is an exclusive event for our top fifty customers and a few reporters, so only staff from the sales department will be invited to welcome the guests and answer their questions.","t":"A：為什麼不是每個人都可以參加下週四晚上在飯店舉行的產品發表派對？ B：那是只為我們前五十名大客戶和幾位記者舉辦的【專屬】活動，所以只有業務部的員工會受邀去接待賓客並回答他們的問題。"},{"w":"fancy","p":"adj.","d":"expensive and stylish, often with lots of decoration","c":"高檔的；花俏的","s":"A: Where should we take the visiting clients from Japan for dinner after the factory tour tomorrow? B: Let's not choose anywhere too fancy, because they told me they would prefer a simple local restaurant where they can try traditional dishes and talk comfortably about the new contract.","t":"A：明天參觀工廠後，我們該帶來訪的日本客戶去哪裡吃晚餐？ B：我們別選太【高檔】的地方，因為他們告訴我比較喜歡簡單的在地餐廳，可以品嚐傳統菜餚，也能輕鬆地談新合約。"},{"w":"deluxe","p":"adj.","d":"of very high quality and more comfortable than usual","c":"豪華的；高級的","s":"A: Which room did you book for the CEO when she visits our branch office in Tokyo next month? B: I reserved a deluxe room on the top floor with a city view and a private desk, because she will need a quiet space to prepare for several important meetings.","t":"A：執行長下個月來東京分公司時，你幫她訂了哪種房間？ B：我訂了頂樓一間可看市景、附私人書桌的【豪華】客房，因為她需要一個安靜的空間來準備幾場重要的會議。"},{"w":"upscale","p":"adj.","d":"designed for rich people; expensive and high-class","c":"高檔的；高級的","s":"A: Why did the company choose such an expensive area for our new clothing store instead of the shopping mall near the station? B: Our target customers are wealthy professionals, so the marketing director believes an upscale neighborhood with fine restaurants and art galleries will attract more of the right buyers.","t":"A：為什麼公司為新服飾店選了那麼貴的地段，而不是車站附近的購物中心？ B：我們的目標客群是富裕的專業人士，所以行銷總監認為一個有高級餐廳和藝廊的【高檔】社區能吸引更多合適的買家。"},{"w":"lavish","p":"adj.","d":"very large, expensive, or generous","c":"奢華的；鋪張的","s":"A: Did the company spend a lot of money on the annual dinner party for employees this year? B: Not really, the managers decided against a lavish party at a five-star hotel and used the money for staff bonuses instead, which most people in the office were very happy about.","t":"A：公司今年在員工年度晚宴上花了很多錢嗎？ B：其實沒有，主管們決定不在五星級飯店辦【奢華的】派對，而是把錢拿來發員工獎金，辦公室大部分的人對此都很開心。"},{"w":"splurge","p":"v.","d":"to spend a lot of money on something you enjoy","c":"揮霍；大手筆花錢","s":"A: What are you going to do with the bonus you received after the team finished the big project early? B: I usually save most of my money, but this time I'm going to splurge on a new laptop and a weekend trip to the beach with my family.","t":"A：團隊提早完成大型專案後，你打算怎麼運用拿到的獎金？ B：我通常會把大部分的錢存起來，但這次我要【揮霍一下】，買一台新筆電，並和家人去海邊度個週末。"},{"w":"afford","p":"v.","d":"to have enough money to pay for something","c":"負擔得起；買得起","s":"A: Is our department going to buy the new design software that the graphic team asked for last month? B: Unfortunately, we can't afford it this quarter because sales were lower than expected, but the manager promised to look at the budget again in January.","t":"A：我們部門會買平面設計團隊上個月要求的新設計軟體嗎？ B：很遺憾，因為銷售額低於預期，我們這一季【負擔】不起，但經理承諾會在一月重新檢視預算。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you have to spend on something","c":"預算","s":"A: How much money can we spend on decorations and food for the grand opening of the new branch next month? B: The finance department has given us a budget of five thousand dollars, so we need to compare prices from several suppliers before we place any orders.","t":"A：下個月新分店盛大開幕時，我們可以花多少錢在裝飾和食物上？ B：財務部給了我們五千美元的【預算】，所以在下任何訂單之前，我們需要先比較幾家供應商的價格。"},{"w":"expense","p":"n.","d":"money spent on something","c":"費用；開銷","s":"A: Can I get my money back for the taxi I took to the airport when I went to the trade show in Taipei? B: Yes, just fill out the expense report on the company website, attach the receipt, and send it to the accounting team before the end of the month.","t":"A：我去台北參加貿易展時搭計程車去機場的錢可以報銷嗎？ B：可以，只要在公司網站上填寫【費用】報告，附上收據，並在月底前寄給會計團隊就好。"},{"w":"investment","p":"n.","d":"money or time spent to get a future benefit","c":"投資","s":"A: Why did the company spend so much money on training courses for new employees this year? B: The president sees it as a long-term investment, because well-trained workers make fewer mistakes, serve customers better, and usually stay with the company for many more years.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年在新進員工的訓練課程上花了這麼多錢？ B：總裁把它視為一項長期【投資】，因為受過良好訓練的員工犯錯較少、更能服務顧客，而且通常會在公司待得更久。"},{"w":"fee","p":"n.","d":"money you pay for a service or to join something","c":"費用；（服務）費","s":"A: How much does it cost to join the business networking club that meets downtown every Wednesday morning? B: There is a yearly membership fee of two hundred dollars, which includes breakfast at every meeting and free entry to their large conference in the autumn.","t":"A：參加每週三早上在市中心聚會的商務交流俱樂部要花多少錢？ B：每年的會員【費】是兩百美元，包括每次聚會的早餐，以及免費參加他們秋季的大型研討會。"},{"w":"charge","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you must pay for something","c":"收費；費用","s":"A: Why is the total on this hotel bill higher than the room price we agreed on when we booked online? B: There is an extra charge for the late checkout and the room service you ordered last night, but I can ask the front desk to explain each item.","t":"A：為什麼這張飯店帳單的總額比我們上網預訂時談好的房價還高？ B：因為晚退房和你昨晚點的客房服務有額外【費用】，不過我可以請櫃檯說明每一個項目。"},{"w":"rate","p":"n.","d":"a fixed amount of money charged for something","c":"費率；價格","s":"A: Which hotel should we recommend to the guests coming to our sales conference in December? B: The Grand Plaza has offered a special group rate of ninety dollars a night for our guests, which is much lower than the normal price, and it is only five minutes from the venue.","t":"A：我們應該推薦哪家飯店給十二月來參加業務研討會的客人？ B：Grand Plaza 為我們的客人提供每晚九十美元的團體優惠【費率】，比平常的價格低很多，而且距離會場只要五分鐘。"},{"w":"price","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you must pay to buy something","c":"價格","s":"A: Have you decided which supplier we should use for the new office chairs that the staff have been asking for? B: I chose the company in Taichung, because their price is lower than the others and they offer free delivery and a five-year guarantee on every chair.","t":"A：你決定好員工一直要求的新辦公椅要用哪家供應商了嗎？ B：我選了台中那家公司，因為他們的【價格】比其他家低，而且每張椅子都提供免費運送和五年保固。"},{"w":"dearly","p":"adv.","d":"at a high cost; in a way that causes great loss","c":"代價高昂地；慘重地","s":"A: Why is the manager so careful about checking every contract before anyone signs it these days? B: Last year the company paid dearly for a small mistake in a contract with a supplier, losing thousands of dollars, so now she reads every page herself before signing.","t":"A：為什麼經理最近在任何人簽約前都這麼仔細地檢查每一份合約？ B：去年公司因為和供應商合約中的一個小錯誤付出了【慘痛的】代價，損失了好幾千美元，所以現在她簽名前都會親自看過每一頁。"},{"w":"economically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that uses little money","c":"經濟地；節約地","s":"A: How can our small team run the new online advertising campaign without spending too much money? B: We can do it more economically by using social media instead of television, sharing videos made by our own staff, and checking the results every week to avoid wasting money.","t":"A：我們的小團隊要怎麼在不花太多錢的情況下推動新的線上廣告活動？ B：我們可以改用社群媒體而不是電視、分享員工自己拍的影片，並每週檢查成效以避免浪費，這樣就能更【經濟地】進行。"},{"w":"reasonable","p":"adj.","d":"fair and not too expensive","c":"（價格）合理的；公道的","s":"A: Do you think the price the printing company quoted for our new brochures is fair? B: Yes, it seems quite reasonable, because they will print five thousand color copies on good paper and deliver them to our office by Friday, which is faster than most other companies.","t":"A：你覺得印刷公司為我們新的宣傳手冊開的報價公道嗎？ B：是的，看起來相當【合理】，因為他們會用好紙印五千份彩色本，而且星期五前送到我們辦公室，比大多數其他公司都快。"},{"w":"affordable","p":"adj.","d":"cheap enough for most people to buy","c":"負擔得起的；平價的","s":"A: Why are so many young employees moving to the small town outside the city these days? B: Housing there is much more affordable than downtown, and the new train line makes it easy to travel to work in about forty minutes, so they can save money every month.","t":"A：為什麼最近有這麼多年輕員工搬到城外的小鎮？ B：那裡的房子比市中心【便宜實惠】得多，而且新的鐵路線讓通勤上班只要大約四十分鐘，所以他們每個月都能省錢。"},{"w":"cheap","p":"adj.","d":"low in price; costing little money","c":"便宜的；廉價的","s":"A: Should we order the paper for the office printers from the new online shop that our neighbor recommended? B: Their paper is very cheap, but last time it was so thin that it kept getting stuck in the machines, so I think we should stay with our usual supplier.","t":"A：我們該向鄰居推薦的那家新網路商店訂辦公室印表機用的紙嗎？ B：他們的紙非常【便宜】，但上次紙太薄，一直卡在機器裡，所以我覺得我們應該繼續用平常的供應商。"},{"w":"discount","p":"n.","d":"an amount taken off the usual price","c":"折扣","s":"A: Is there any way we can lower the cost of the new laptops for the sales team this year? B: If we order more than fifty computers at once, the supplier will give us a fifteen percent discount, and they will also set up the software for free.","t":"A：今年有什麼辦法能降低業務團隊新筆電的成本嗎？ B：如果我們一次訂購五十台以上的電腦，供應商會給我們百分之十五的【折扣】，而且還會免費幫我們安裝軟體。"},{"w":"bargain","p":"n.","d":"something bought for less than its usual price","c":"便宜貨；划算的交易","s":"A: Where did you find such a nice leather bag for your business trips, and how much did it cost? B: I bought it at the department store last weekend for only forty dollars instead of the usual hundred and twenty, so it was a real bargain, and the quality is excellent.","t":"A：你在哪裡找到這麼好看、適合出差用的皮包？花了多少錢？ B：我上週末在百貨公司只花了四十美元買到，原價是一百二十美元，所以真的很【划算】，而且品質非常好。"},{"w":"sale","p":"n.","d":"a time when a shop sells things at lower prices","c":"特賣；拍賣","s":"A: When is the best time to buy new furniture for the reception area of our office? B: The furniture store on Main Street is having a big sale next weekend, with up to forty percent off sofas and tables, so we should visit on Saturday morning before everything is gone.","t":"A：什麼時候是為辦公室接待區添購新家具的最佳時機？ B：大街上那家家具店下週末有大型【特賣】，沙發和桌子最多打六折，所以我們應該在星期六早上東西被搶光前過去。"},{"w":"worthwhile","p":"adj.","d":"useful or important enough to spend time or money on","c":"值得的；有價值的","s":"A: Do you think the two-day leadership workshop that you attended in Kaohsiung was useful for your job? B: Yes, it was very worthwhile, because I learned practical ways to manage meetings and give feedback, and I have already used some of the ideas with my own team this week.","t":"A：你覺得你在高雄參加的兩天領導力工作坊對你的工作有幫助嗎？ B：是的，非常【值得】，因為我學到了主持會議和給予回饋的實用方法，而且這週已經在自己的團隊用上了一些點子。"},{"w":"extravagant","p":"adj.","d":"spending or costing much more money than is sensible","c":"奢侈的；鋪張浪費的","s":"A: Why did the board of directors criticize the marketing manager at the meeting yesterday afternoon? B: They felt his plan to rent a private island for the product launch was too extravagant, especially when the company is trying to cut costs and many departments have smaller budgets this year.","t":"A：為什麼董事會昨天下午在會議上批評行銷經理？ B：他們覺得他租私人島嶼來辦產品發表會的計畫太【鋪張浪費】了，尤其公司正努力削減成本，而且今年許多部門的預算都變少了。"},{"w":"frugal","p":"adj.","d":"careful to spend only a little money","c":"節儉的；節約的","s":"A: How did your small company manage to survive during the difficult years when sales were so low? B: We were very frugal, so we rented a smaller office, bought used equipment, and asked everyone to save electricity, which helped us keep all of our employees until business improved.","t":"A：在銷售額很低的那幾年艱困時期，你們這家小公司是怎麼撐下來的？ B：我們非常【節儉】，租了較小的辦公室、買二手設備，並請大家節約用電，這幫助我們在生意好轉前留住了所有員工。"},{"w":"financially","p":"adv.","d":"relating to money","c":"財務上；經濟上","s":"A: Is the small bakery that opened next to our office last year doing well? B: The owner told me the business is now financially stable, because many office workers buy breakfast there every morning and several companies order cakes for their meetings and parties.","t":"A：去年在我們辦公室隔壁開的那家小麵包店經營得好嗎？ B：老闆告訴我生意現在【財務上】很穩定，因為許多上班族每天早上都在那裡買早餐，還有好幾家公司訂蛋糕來開會和辦派對。"}]},{"unit":130,"theme":"Express 表達","cards":[{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"a look on someone's face, or a way of showing a feeling","c":"表情；表達","s":"A: Did the new marketing assistant enjoy the welcome lunch that the team organized for her on Friday afternoon at the Italian restaurant downtown? B: I think so, because she had a happy expression on her face the whole time, and she thanked everyone for the kind cards and flowers before she left.","t":"A：新來的行銷助理喜歡團隊週五下午在市中心義大利餐廳為她辦的歡迎午餐嗎？ B：我想是的，因為她整段時間臉上都帶著開心的【表情】，而且離開前還感謝大家送的卡片和花。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"showing feelings or meaning clearly","c":"富有表現力的；表達情感的","s":"A: Why did the director choose Emma to give the product presentation at the trade show instead of one of the senior sales staff? B: She has a very expressive way of speaking, and her hand movements and warm smile keep the audience interested, so customers always remember the products she introduces.","t":"A：為什麼主管選了艾瑪在商展上做產品簡報，而不是選資深業務人員之一？ B：她說話的方式非常【富有表現力】，她的手勢和溫暖的笑容能讓觀眾保持興趣，所以客戶總是記得她介紹的產品。"},{"w":"expressively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows feelings clearly","c":"富有表情地；生動地","s":"A: How did the new tour guide manage to keep the large group of tired tourists interested during the long museum visit yesterday afternoon? B: She told the old stories very expressively, changing her voice for each character and using her hands, so even the children were listening carefully until the end.","t":"A：新導遊昨天下午在漫長的博物館參觀中，是怎麼讓那一大群疲累的遊客保持興趣的？ B：她非常【生動地】講述那些古老的故事，為每個角色變換聲音並搭配手勢，所以連孩子們都專心聽到最後。"},{"w":"convey","p":"v.","d":"to make feelings, ideas or information known to someone","c":"傳達；表達","s":"A: Could you help me write the email to our overseas suppliers about the delayed shipment, since I'm worried my English sounds too rude? B: Sure, we should convey our concerns politely but clearly, explain how the delay affects our customers, and ask them to confirm a new delivery date by Friday.","t":"A：你能幫我寫那封寄給海外供應商、關於延誤出貨的電子郵件嗎？我擔心我的英文聽起來太不禮貌。 B：當然，我們應該禮貌但清楚地【傳達】我們的擔憂，說明延誤如何影響我們的客戶，並請他們在週五前確認新的交貨日期。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information or ideas with others","c":"溝通；傳達","s":"A: The engineers in Taipei and the designers in Berlin keep making mistakes on the new phone project, so what do you think the main problem is? B: I think they don't communicate often enough, so we should set up a weekly video meeting and a shared online folder for all the drawings and updates.","t":"A：台北的工程師和柏林的設計師在新手機專案上一直出錯，你認為主要問題是什麼？ B：我認為他們【溝通】得不夠頻繁，所以我們應該安排每週一次的視訊會議，並建立一個共用的線上資料夾來放所有的圖面和最新資訊。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the act of sharing information with others","c":"溝通；通訊","s":"A: Why did the hotel guests complain so much about the renovation work on the third floor last week, even though it finished on time? B: There was poor communication between the front desk and the building team, so nobody told the guests about the noise before they checked in, and many of them felt upset.","t":"A：為什麼上週飯店客人對三樓的整修工程抱怨這麼多，即使工程準時完工？ B：櫃檯和施工團隊之間的【溝通】不良，所以沒有人在客人入住前告知他們會有噪音，很多人因此感到不滿。"},{"w":"declare","p":"v.","d":"to state something officially; to tell customs about goods you are carrying","c":"宣布；申報","s":"A: I'm flying back from the electronics fair in Tokyo tomorrow with some expensive camera samples, so do I need to do anything special at the airport? B: Yes, you must declare the samples at customs when you land, and keep the invoices from the company in your bag in case the officers want to check them.","t":"A：我明天要從東京電子展搭機回來，帶著一些昂貴的相機樣品，我在機場需要做什麼特別的事嗎？ B：需要，你降落後必須在海關【申報】這些樣品，並把公司的發票放在包包裡，以防海關人員要查看。"},{"w":"announcement","p":"n.","d":"a public statement that gives information","c":"公告；宣布","s":"A: Why is everyone gathering in the main hall of the office building at ten o'clock this morning instead of starting their usual work? B: The CEO is going to make an important announcement about the merger with our biggest competitor, and all departments were asked to attend so nobody hears rumors first.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上十點大家都聚集在辦公大樓的大廳，而不是像平常一樣開始工作？ B：執行長要發布一項關於與我們最大競爭對手合併的重要【公告】，所有部門都被要求出席，這樣就沒有人會先聽到謠言。"},{"w":"proclaim","p":"v.","d":"to announce something officially and publicly","c":"宣布；宣告","s":"A: Why are there so many colorful posters and banners hanging along the main street near the city hall this week? B: The mayor is going to proclaim the first Sunday of next month as City Recycling Day, so local shops and schools are preparing special events to celebrate it together.","t":"A：為什麼這週市政府附近的主要街道上掛了那麼多色彩繽紛的海報和布條？ B：市長將【正式宣布】下個月的第一個星期日為城市回收日，所以當地商店和學校正在準備特別活動一起慶祝。"},{"w":"utter","p":"v.","d":"to say something or make a sound with your voice","c":"說出；發出（聲音）","s":"A: How did the new intern behave during her first meeting with the important clients from Singapore yesterday afternoon? B: She was so nervous that she didn't utter a single word for the whole hour, but she took careful notes, and later she wrote an excellent summary for the manager.","t":"A：新來的實習生昨天下午第一次和新加坡的重要客戶開會時表現如何？ B：她緊張到整整一個小時都沒【說出】一個字，但她做了仔細的筆記，之後還幫經理寫了一份很棒的摘要。"},{"w":"voice","p":"v.","d":"to tell people your opinion or feeling","c":"表達；說出（意見）","s":"A: The staff seem unhappy about the new rule that everyone must work on Saturdays during the busy season, so what should we do about it? B: We should hold a meeting where employees can voice their concerns openly, and then the managers can discuss possible changes, such as extra pay or days off later.","t":"A：員工似乎對旺季期間每個人都必須週六上班的新規定感到不滿，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該召開一場會議，讓員工能公開【表達】他們的擔憂，然後經理們可以討論可能的調整，例如加班費或之後補休。"},{"w":"statement","p":"n.","d":"something that is said or written officially","c":"聲明；陳述","s":"A: Have the reporters received any official information yet about the fire at our factory in Taichung last night? B: Not yet, but the public relations team is preparing a short statement for the press, which will explain what happened, confirm that no workers were hurt, and describe our next steps.","t":"A：記者們收到任何有關昨晚我們台中工廠火災的官方資訊了嗎？ B：還沒有，但公關團隊正在準備一份給媒體的簡短【聲明】，內容會說明事發經過、確認沒有工人受傷，並描述我們接下來的步驟。"},{"w":"remark","p":"n.","d":"something you say that gives an opinion","c":"評論；話語","s":"A: Why does Jason look so upset after the team lunch, when he was in such a good mood this morning? B: The manager made a rude remark about his sales report in front of everyone, and although she apologized later, Jason still feels embarrassed and doesn't want to talk about it.","t":"A：為什麼傑森在團隊午餐後看起來那麼難過？他今天早上心情還很好。 B：經理當著大家的面對他的業績報告說了一句無禮的【話】，雖然她後來道歉了，傑森還是覺得很難堪，不想談這件事。"},{"w":"comment","p":"n.","d":"an opinion that you say or write","c":"評論；意見；留言","s":"A: The new website for our bakery went online last Monday, so have any customers said anything about the design or the ordering system? B: Yes, one customer left a helpful comment saying the menu was hard to find on her phone, so our designer is going to move it to the top of the page this week.","t":"A：我們麵包店的新網站上週一上線了，有顧客對設計或訂購系統說了什麼嗎？ B：有，一位顧客留下了一則很有幫助的【留言】，說在她的手機上很難找到菜單，所以我們的設計師這週會把它移到頁面頂端。"},{"w":"articulate","p":"v.","d":"to express ideas clearly in words","c":"清楚表達；闡明","s":"A: The investors want to know exactly why we need more money for the new delivery app, so how should we prepare for the meeting? B: We need to articulate our goals clearly in the first five minutes, show them simple charts about our growth, and answer their questions about the costs honestly.","t":"A：投資人想確切知道為什麼我們的新外送應用程式需要更多資金，我們該如何準備這場會議？ B：我們需要在前五分鐘清楚地【闡明】我們的目標，給他們看關於成長的簡單圖表，並誠實回答他們關於成本的問題。"},{"w":"gesture","p":"n.","d":"an action that shows your feelings; a movement of the hands","c":"表示；姿態；手勢","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager send flowers and a free dinner voucher to the guests in room 512 this afternoon? B: Their air conditioner broke during the hot night, so he wanted to make a kind gesture to show that the hotel cares and to apologize for all the trouble they had.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理今天下午送花和免費晚餐券給512號房的客人？ B：他們的冷氣在炎熱的夜裡壞了，所以他想做個貼心的【表示】，表達飯店的關心並為他們遇到的所有麻煩道歉。"},{"w":"indicate","p":"v.","d":"to show or point out that something is true","c":"顯示；表明","s":"A: Should we open a second coffee shop near the train station next year, or is it still too risky for our small company? B: Our latest survey results indicate that many commuters want a quick breakfast there, so I think it is a good chance, but we should check the rent first.","t":"A：我們明年該在火車站附近開第二家咖啡店嗎？還是對我們這種小公司來說風險仍然太高？ B：我們最新的調查結果【顯示】許多通勤族想在那裡買快速的早餐，所以我認為這是個好機會，但我們應該先確認租金。"},{"w":"demonstrate","p":"v.","d":"to show how something works; to prove something","c":"示範；證明","s":"A: Our customers keep calling the help desk because they don't understand how to use the new coffee machine, so what can we do? B: Let's make a short video to demonstrate each step, from adding water to cleaning the parts, and put a link to it on the box and our website.","t":"A：我們的顧客一直打電話到服務台，因為他們不懂如何使用新的咖啡機，我們能怎麼做？ B：我們來拍一支短片【示範】每個步驟，從加水到清潔零件，並把連結放在包裝盒和我們的網站上。"},{"w":"portray","p":"v.","d":"to show or describe someone or something in a certain way","c":"描繪；描寫","s":"A: Are you happy with the new television advertisement that the agency made for our family hotel by the lake? B: Mostly, because it tries to portray the hotel as a quiet, friendly place for parents and children, but I think the music is too loud and we should change it.","t":"A：你滿意廣告公司為我們湖邊家庭旅館製作的新電視廣告嗎？ B：大致滿意，因為它試圖把旅館【描繪】成一個安靜、友善、適合父母和孩子的地方，但我覺得音樂太大聲了，我們應該換掉。"},{"w":"reveal","p":"v.","d":"to show or tell something that was secret or hidden","c":"揭露；透露；揭曉","s":"A: When will the company tell the public about the new electric scooter that the design team has been working on for two years? B: The marketing director plans to reveal the final design at the technology show in March, and she hopes the media will share photos of it all over the internet.","t":"A：公司什麼時候會向大眾公布設計團隊研發了兩年的新電動機車？ B：行銷總監計劃在三月的科技展上【揭曉】最終設計，她希望媒體能在網路上到處分享它的照片。"},{"w":"emphasize","p":"v.","d":"to show that something is very important","c":"強調","s":"A: What should I say first when I train the new cashiers at the supermarket branch tomorrow morning? B: You should emphasize the importance of checking every customer's change carefully, because last month we lost a lot of money from small mistakes at the busy registers during weekends.","t":"A：我明天早上在超市分店訓練新收銀員時，應該先說什麼？ B：你應該【強調】仔細核對每位顧客找零的重要性，因為上個月週末忙碌時，我們在收銀台因為小錯誤損失了很多錢。"},{"w":"highlight","p":"v.","d":"to make something easy to notice","c":"突顯；強調；用螢光筆標示","s":"A: The annual report is almost fifty pages long, so how can we make sure the board members notice our best results this year? B: Let's highlight the main achievements on the first page, such as the twenty percent rise in online sales, and add a few clear charts to support them.","t":"A：年度報告將近五十頁，我們要怎麼確保董事會成員注意到我們今年最好的成果？ B：我們在第一頁【突顯】主要成就，例如網路銷售成長百分之二十，並加上幾張清楚的圖表來佐證。"},{"w":"imply","p":"v.","d":"to suggest something without saying it directly","c":"暗示；意味著","s":"A: The client said our price was 'interesting' during the phone call, so do you think he is happy with our offer? B: I'm not sure, because that word might imply that he thinks it is too high, so we should send him a polite email and ask what he really means.","t":"A：客戶在電話中說我們的價格「很有意思」，你覺得他對我們的報價滿意嗎？ B：我不確定，因為那個字可能【暗示】他覺得價格太高，所以我們應該寄給他一封禮貌的電子郵件，問他真正的意思是什麼。"},{"w":"hint","p":"n.","d":"a small or indirect suggestion","c":"暗示；提示","s":"A: Do you know what kind of birthday present our manager would like, since the whole team wants to buy her something nice? B: She gave us a small hint last week when she said her old coffee mug was broken, so maybe we could buy her a beautiful new one with a card.","t":"A：你知道我們經理會喜歡什麼樣的生日禮物嗎？整個團隊都想買個好東西給她。 B：她上週給了我們一點小【暗示】，說她的舊咖啡杯破了，所以也許我們可以買一個漂亮的新杯子再附上一張卡片。"},{"w":"clarify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to understand","c":"澄清；闡明","s":"A: Several employees are confused about the new travel expense policy and keep asking me about taxi receipts and hotel costs, so what should we do? B: Let's ask the finance manager to clarify the rules at Monday's staff meeting and send a simple one-page guide to everyone afterward, so the questions stop.","t":"A：好幾位員工對新的差旅費政策感到困惑，一直問我有關計程車收據和飯店費用的問題，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們請財務經理在週一的員工會議上【釐清】這些規定，之後再寄一份簡單的一頁指南給大家，這樣問題就會停止了。"},{"w":"illustrate","p":"v.","d":"to explain something by using examples or pictures","c":"說明；舉例闡明；配插圖","s":"A: How can I make my sales presentation more interesting for the new clients, since last time some people almost fell asleep? B: Try to illustrate your main points with real stories from happy customers and a few colorful pictures, because people remember examples much better than long lists of numbers.","t":"A：我要怎麼讓我的銷售簡報對新客戶來說更有趣？上次有些人差點睡著。 B：試著用滿意顧客的真實故事和幾張色彩鮮明的圖片來【說明】你的重點，因為人們記住例子的能力比記住一長串數字好得多。"},{"w":"communicative","p":"adj.","d":"willing and able to talk and share information","c":"善於溝通的；健談的","s":"A: What kind of person are we looking for to lead the new customer service team at the call center in Kaohsiung? B: We need someone who is friendly, patient and very communicative, because the leader must talk with angry callers, train new staff, and report problems to managers every day.","t":"A：我們要找什麼樣的人來帶領高雄客服中心的新客服團隊？ B：我們需要一個友善、有耐心且非常【善於溝通】的人，因為這位主管每天都必須和生氣的來電者交談、訓練新進員工，並向經理回報問題。"},{"w":"outspoken","p":"adj.","d":"saying what you think openly, even if others disagree","c":"直言不諱的；坦率的","s":"A: Why did the board invite Ms. Lin to the planning meeting, when they know she often disagrees with their ideas? B: She is very outspoken and always tells the truth about problems, so the board believes her honest opinions will help them avoid expensive mistakes on the new project.","t":"A：既然董事會知道林女士常常不同意他們的想法，為什麼還邀請她參加規劃會議？ B：她非常【直言不諱】，總是如實說出問題，所以董事會相信她誠實的意見能幫助他們在新專案上避免昂貴的錯誤。"},{"w":"confess","p":"v.","d":"to admit that you did something wrong","c":"坦承；承認","s":"A: Why did Daniel suddenly go to the manager's office this morning before the weekly meeting had even started? B: He wanted to confess that he forgot to send the important contract to the client last Friday, and he hoped to fix the problem before the client called to complain.","t":"A：為什麼丹尼爾今天早上在每週會議開始前就突然去了經理辦公室？ B：他想【坦承】他上週五忘了把重要合約寄給客戶，並希望在客戶打電話來抱怨之前解決這個問題。"},{"w":"exclaim","p":"v.","d":"to say something suddenly and loudly because of strong feeling","c":"驚叫；大聲說出","s":"A: How did the staff react when the CEO said at the party that everyone would get a bonus and an extra week of holiday? B: Many people began to exclaim with joy, some of them clapped loudly, and a few even hugged their coworkers because it had been such a difficult year.","t":"A：當執行長在派對上說每個人都會拿到獎金和額外一週假期時，員工有什麼反應？ B：很多人開始高興地【大聲歡呼】，有些人大聲鼓掌，甚至有幾個人擁抱同事，因為這一年實在太辛苦了。"},{"w":"affirm","p":"v.","d":"to state firmly that something is true","c":"斷言；肯定；重申","s":"A: Have you heard that many customers are worried after reading the news that our company might close some of its stores in the south? B: Yes, so the president will affirm in tomorrow's press conference that all stores will stay open, and she will also share our plans to hire more staff next year.","t":"A：你有聽說很多顧客在看到我們公司可能關閉南部部分門市的新聞後很擔心嗎？ B：有，所以總裁會在明天的記者會上【明確表示】所有門市都會繼續營業，她也會分享我們明年要招募更多員工的計畫。"},{"w":"assert","p":"v.","d":"to say firmly that something is true","c":"堅稱；主張；維護","s":"A: Our competitor says its new phone has the longest battery life on the market, but is that really true? B: They assert it in every advertisement, but our own tests show that our phone lasts two hours longer, so we should share those results with customers clearly.","t":"A：我們的競爭對手說它的新手機擁有市面上最長的電池續航力，但那是真的嗎？ B：他們在每則廣告中都這麼【宣稱】，但我們自己的測試顯示我們的手機多撐兩小時，所以我們應該清楚地把這些結果分享給顧客。"}]},{"unit":131,"theme":"Extreme Sports 極限運動","cards":[{"w":"adrenaline","p":"n.","d":"a chemical your body makes when you feel excited or afraid","c":"腎上腺素","s":"A: Why did the marketing team look so excited when they came back from the company outing on Saturday afternoon? B: They spent the whole morning on the giant zip line over the valley, and the rush of adrenaline kept them laughing and talking about it all the way home on the bus.","t":"A：行銷團隊星期六下午從公司出遊回來時，為什麼看起來那麼興奮？ B：他們整個早上都在山谷上方的巨型滑索上，那股【腎上腺素】帶來的快感讓他們在回程的巴士上一路笑著談論這件事。"},{"w":"thrill","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of excitement and pleasure","c":"興奮；刺激感","s":"A: Our travel agency wants to add a new tour package for younger customers next summer, but what kind of activity should we offer them? B: Many young travelers are looking for the thrill of trying something new, so a guided river trip or a hot-air balloon ride would probably sell very well.","t":"A：我們旅行社明年夏天想為年輕客戶增加一個新的旅遊套裝行程，但我們應該提供什麼樣的活動呢？ B：許多年輕旅客都在尋找嘗試新事物的【刺激感】，所以有導遊帶領的河上之旅或熱氣球之旅應該會賣得很好。"},{"w":"adventure","p":"n.","d":"an exciting and unusual experience","c":"冒險；冒險經歷","s":"A: Have you finished the new brochure for the mountain resort, and did the manager approve the main photo on the front cover? B: Yes, she loved the picture of the hikers on the cliff, and she wants the headline to promise a real adventure for families who are tired of ordinary beach holidays.","t":"A：你完成山區度假村的新宣傳手冊了嗎？經理有核准封面的主要照片嗎？ B：有，她很喜歡登山客站在懸崖上的那張照片，她希望標題能向厭倦了一般海灘假期的家庭保證一場真正的【冒險】。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something bad will happen","c":"風險；危險","s":"A: Why did the insurance company raise the price of our group policy for the employees who joined the outdoor sports club this year? B: The agent explained that activities like cliff jumping carry a higher risk of serious accidents, so the company has to charge more to cover possible hospital costs.","t":"A：保險公司為什麼調高了我們今年加入戶外運動社團員工的團體保單價格？ B：業務員解釋說，像懸崖跳水這樣的活動發生嚴重意外的【風險】較高，所以公司必須收取更多費用來支付可能的醫療費用。"},{"w":"dangerous","p":"adj.","d":"likely to hurt or harm someone","c":"危險的","s":"A: Should we still hold the team-building hike on Friday, even though the weather report says there will be heavy rain all afternoon? B: I think we should cancel it, because the trail along the river becomes very dangerous when the rocks are wet, and nobody wants to see a colleague get hurt.","t":"A：即使氣象報告說整個下午都會下大雨，我們星期五還要舉辦團隊健行嗎？ B：我覺得應該取消，因為岩石濕滑時沿河的步道會變得非常【危險】，沒有人想看到同事受傷。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"n.","d":"something difficult that tests your ability","c":"挑戰","s":"A: Are you really going to join the twenty-kilometer mountain race that the sports company is sponsoring next month? B: Yes, I know it will be a huge challenge for someone who only started running in the spring, but my coach believes I can finish it if I prepare carefully.","t":"A：你真的要參加運動用品公司下個月贊助的二十公里山地賽跑嗎？ B：是的，我知道這對一個春天才開始跑步的人來說是很大的【挑戰】，但我的教練相信只要我仔細準備就能跑完。"},{"w":"daring","p":"adj.","d":"brave enough to do risky or surprising things","c":"大膽的；勇敢的","s":"A: Did you see the video that our new sales director posted on the company website about her weekend activities? B: Yes, it showed her jumping from a small plane over the coast, and everyone in the office agrees that it was a very daring thing to do for someone who is afraid of flying.","t":"A：你有看到我們新任業務總監在公司網站上發布的週末活動影片嗎？ B：有，影片中她從一架小飛機上跳下飛越海岸，辦公室裡每個人都同意，對一個怕坐飛機的人來說，那是一件非常【大膽的】事。"},{"w":"fearless","p":"adj.","d":"not afraid of anything","c":"無所畏懼的","s":"A: Why did the film company choose that young actor for the lead role in their new action movie about mountain rescue teams? B: The director said he looked completely fearless during the screen test on the high bridge, and he did most of the difficult scenes himself without asking for help.","t":"A：電影公司為什麼選那位年輕演員擔任他們新的山難救援隊動作片主角？ B：導演說他在高橋上試鏡時看起來完全【無所畏懼】，而且大部分困難的場景都是他自己完成，沒有要求協助。"},{"w":"helmet","p":"n.","d":"a hard hat that protects your head","c":"安全帽；頭盔","s":"A: Excuse me, can I rent one of these mountain bikes for the afternoon, or do I need to make a reservation in advance? B: You can take one now, but for safety reasons you must wear a helmet at all times on the trail, and you need to sign this form before you leave the shop.","t":"A：不好意思，我可以租一台登山車用一個下午嗎？還是需要事先預約？ B：您現在就可以租，但為了安全起見，在步道上必須全程戴著【安全帽】，而且離開店前需要簽這份表格。"},{"w":"protective gear","p":"n.phr.","d":"special clothes and equipment that keep your body safe","c":"防護裝備","s":"A: What should I bring to the motorcycle training course that the delivery company is organizing for new drivers next week? B: You only need comfortable clothes and a valid license, because the school will provide all the protective gear, including gloves, knee pads, and a strong jacket for every student.","t":"A：外送公司下週為新進司機舉辦的機車訓練課程，我應該帶什麼？ B：你只需要穿舒適的衣服並帶有效的駕照，因為學校會提供所有的【防護裝備】，包括每位學員的手套、護膝和堅固的外套。"},{"w":"skydiving","p":"n.","d":"the sport of jumping from a plane and falling before opening a parachute","c":"高空跳傘","s":"A: What did the employees choose as the special reward activity after the team reached its sales target last quarter? B: Most of them voted for skydiving at the airfield outside the city, so next Saturday they will jump from a plane with experienced instructors and then celebrate together at dinner.","t":"A：團隊上一季達成業績目標後，員工選了什麼作為特別的獎勵活動？ B：他們大多數人投票選擇在市郊的機場玩【高空跳傘】，所以下週六他們會跟著經驗豐富的教練從飛機上跳下來，然後一起吃晚餐慶祝。"},{"w":"parachute","p":"n.","d":"a large piece of cloth that helps a person or object fall slowly from the sky","c":"降落傘","s":"A: How does the new delivery company send medical supplies to the small villages in the mountains when the roads are closed by snow? B: They fly over the villages in a light plane and drop the boxes with a parachute, so the packages land safely and the local clinics receive them within a few hours.","t":"A：當道路因下雪而封閉時，那家新的物流公司要如何把醫療用品送到山區的小村莊？ B：他們用輕型飛機飛越村莊上空，用【降落傘】投下箱子，讓包裹安全著陸，當地診所在幾小時內就能收到。"},{"w":"bungee jumping","p":"n.phr.","d":"jumping from a high place while tied to a long elastic rope","c":"高空彈跳","s":"A: What is the most popular activity for tourists who visit the bridge near the waterfall during the summer holiday season? B: It is definitely bungee jumping, because visitors can fall more than fifty meters toward the river before the rope pulls them back, and the tour company is fully booked every weekend.","t":"A：暑假期間造訪瀑布附近那座橋的遊客最喜歡的活動是什麼？ B：絕對是【高空彈跳】，因為遊客可以朝河面下墜超過五十公尺，然後繩索才把他們拉回來，而且旅行社每個週末都被訂滿了。"},{"w":"snowboarding","p":"n.","d":"the sport of moving down snowy hills on one wide board","c":"單板滑雪","s":"A: Are you taking any time off work in January, or will you stay in the office to finish the annual report? B: I am going to Hokkaido for a week with my cousins, and we have already signed up for snowboarding lessons because none of us knows how to stand on the board yet.","t":"A：你一月會請假嗎？還是會留在辦公室完成年度報告？ B：我要和表兄弟姊妹去北海道一個星期，我們已經報名了【單板滑雪】課程，因為我們都還不知道怎麼站在滑雪板上。"},{"w":"skateboarding","p":"n.","d":"the sport of riding and doing tricks on a board with small wheels","c":"滑板運動","s":"A: Why is the city government building a new concrete park next to the shopping mall instead of more parking spaces? B: Many teenagers were practicing skateboarding on the sidewalks and stairs, which was unsafe for shoppers, so the city decided to give them a proper place with ramps and rails.","t":"A：市政府為什麼要在購物中心旁邊蓋一座新的水泥公園，而不是增加停車位？ B：許多青少年在人行道和樓梯上練習【滑板】，這對購物的民眾來說很不安全，所以市政府決定給他們一個有斜坡和欄杆的合適場地。"},{"w":"rock climbing","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sport of climbing steep rock walls","c":"攀岩","s":"A: Do you know why the human resources department booked the indoor sports center for our training day next Thursday? B: They want us to try rock climbing on the big wall there, because reaching the top together teaches teams to trust each other and communicate clearly under pressure.","t":"A：你知道人資部門為什麼預訂了室內運動中心作為我們下週四的訓練日嗎？ B：他們想讓我們在那裡的大型岩壁上嘗試【攀岩】，因為一起爬到頂端能教會團隊彼此信任，並在壓力下清楚溝通。"},{"w":"mountaineering","p":"n.","d":"the sport of climbing high mountains","c":"登山運動","s":"A: How did the new CEO become such a calm and patient leader when the company faces difficult problems? B: She spent ten years doing mountaineering in the Himalayas before she joined the business world, and she says that climbing high peaks taught her to plan carefully and never panic.","t":"A：新任執行長是如何成為一位在公司面臨難題時如此冷靜又有耐心的領導者？ B：她在進入商界之前，花了十年在喜馬拉雅山從事【登山運動】，她說攀登高峰教會她仔細規劃、永不驚慌。"},{"w":"surfing","p":"n.","d":"the sport of riding ocean waves on a board","c":"衝浪","s":"A: Why is the beach hotel offering such large discounts for guests who stay during the autumn months this year? B: The waves are much bigger in October, so the manager wants to attract young travelers who enjoy surfing, and the hotel has even hired two instructors to teach beginners.","t":"A：海灘飯店今年為什麼要給秋季入住的客人這麼大的折扣？ B：十月的海浪大得多，所以經理想吸引喜歡【衝浪】的年輕旅客，飯店甚至請了兩位教練來教初學者。"},{"w":"windsurfing","p":"n.","d":"the sport of moving across water on a board with a sail","c":"風帆衝浪","s":"A: What equipment does the water sports shop by the lake need to order before the summer season starts next month? B: They need at least ten new boards with sails for windsurfing, because the strong afternoon wind on the lake attracts many visitors who want to rent them by the hour.","t":"A：湖邊的水上運動用品店在下個月夏季開始前需要訂購什麼設備？ B：他們至少需要十塊新的附帆板子來玩【風帆衝浪】，因為湖上下午的強風吸引了許多想按小時租用的遊客。"},{"w":"rafting","p":"n.","d":"traveling down a river in a rubber boat","c":"泛舟","s":"A: How was the company trip to Hualien last weekend, and did everyone enjoy the activities that the organizers planned? B: It was great, especially the river rafting on Saturday morning, when twelve of us paddled a rubber boat through fast water and got completely wet but laughed the whole time.","t":"A：上週末公司去花蓮的旅遊怎麼樣？大家都喜歡主辦人規劃的活動嗎？ B：很棒，尤其是星期六早上的河上【泛舟】，我們十二個人划著橡皮艇穿過湍急的水流，全身都濕透了，但一路笑個不停。"},{"w":"kayaking","p":"n.","d":"moving through water in a small narrow boat with a paddle","c":"划獨木舟","s":"A: Could you recommend a relaxing activity for the visiting clients who will have a free afternoon after the meeting on Friday? B: I suggest kayaking around the quiet bay near the hotel, because each person paddles a small boat slowly along the coast and can enjoy the beautiful view of the islands.","t":"A：星期五會議結束後，來訪的客戶有一個空閒的下午，你能推薦一個放鬆的活動嗎？ B：我建議在飯店附近寧靜的海灣【划獨木舟】，因為每個人可以划著小船沿著海岸慢慢前進，欣賞島嶼的美麗景色。"},{"w":"motocross","p":"n.","d":"motorcycle racing on rough, muddy tracks","c":"越野機車賽","s":"A: Why does the motorcycle company want to sponsor that dirt-track event in the countryside instead of a normal road race? B: Young riders love watching motocross, and when they see racers jump over muddy hills on our bikes, they are much more likely to visit our stores and buy one.","t":"A：那家機車公司為什麼想贊助鄉下的泥地賽道活動，而不是一般的公路賽？ B：年輕騎士很喜歡觀看【越野機車賽】，當他們看到賽車手騎著我們的機車飛越泥濘的山丘時，就更有可能到我們的門市購買。"},{"w":"speed","p":"n.","d":"how fast something moves","c":"速度","s":"A: Why did the delivery company install new cameras and tracking systems in all of its trucks last month? B: Several drivers were caught going too fast on the highway, so the managers now check the speed of every vehicle and send a warning when someone drives over the limit.","t":"A：物流公司上個月為什麼在所有貨車上安裝了新的攝影機和追蹤系統？ B：有幾位司機被發現在高速公路上開太快，所以主管們現在會檢查每輛車的【速度】，有人超速時就會發出警告。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to stay steady without falling","c":"平衡；平衡感","s":"A: How are your yoga classes going, and do you think they are helping you with the back pain from sitting at your desk all day? B: Yes, my back feels much better, and the teacher says my balance has improved a lot, because I can now stand on one leg for a full minute without falling.","t":"A：你的瑜伽課上得怎麼樣？你覺得對你整天坐在辦公桌前造成的背痛有幫助嗎？ B：有，我的背感覺好多了，老師說我的【平衡感】進步很多，因為我現在可以單腳站立整整一分鐘而不會跌倒。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"an ability to do something well, learned through practice","c":"技能；技巧","s":"A: Why did the outdoor tour company ask all of its new guides to take a two-week course before the busy season begins? B: Leading groups in the mountains requires a lot of skill, such as reading maps, giving first aid, and making quick decisions when the weather suddenly changes.","t":"A：戶外旅遊公司為什麼要求所有新導遊在旺季開始前上兩週的課程？ B：在山區帶團需要很多【技能】，例如看地圖、急救，以及在天氣突然變化時迅速做出決定。"},{"w":"training","p":"n.","d":"the process of learning and practicing skills for a job or sport","c":"訓練；培訓","s":"A: Is it true that the new diving instructors at the resort will not start working with guests until next month? B: Yes, they must complete three weeks of safety training first, which includes rescue practice in the pool and several long swims in the open sea with a senior instructor.","t":"A：度假村新來的潛水教練真的要到下個月才會開始帶客人嗎？ B：是的，他們必須先完成三週的安全【訓練】，包括在泳池裡練習救援，以及跟著資深教練在開放海域長距離游泳數次。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"having the training and qualifications for a job; doing something as a paid job","c":"專業的；職業的","s":"A: Do you think the hotel should hire a local guide for the climbing tours, or can our own staff lead the guests? B: We should definitely hire a professional guide with official certificates, because our insurance will not cover any accidents if the person in charge has no proper qualifications.","t":"A：你覺得飯店應該為攀岩行程聘請當地嚮導，還是我們自己的員工就可以帶客人？ B：我們絕對應該聘請一位持有正式證照的【專業】嚮導，因為如果負責人沒有適當的資格，我們的保險將不會理賠任何意外。"},{"w":"amateur","p":"adj.","d":"doing something for fun, not as a paid job","c":"業餘的","s":"A: Is the cycling race this weekend only for famous athletes, or can ordinary people from our office sign up too? B: Anyone can join, because it is an amateur event for people who ride as a hobby, and the organizers just want everyone to have fun and raise money for charity.","t":"A：這個週末的自行車賽只限知名運動員參加嗎？還是我們辦公室的一般人也可以報名？ B：任何人都可以參加，因為那是一場為把騎車當作嗜好的人舉辦的【業餘】活動，主辦單位只是希望大家玩得開心並為慈善機構募款。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"involving strong competition; wanting very much to win","c":"競爭激烈的；好勝的","s":"A: Why did the sporting goods store lower the prices of its helmets and gloves so much this month? B: The market has become very competitive since two large online shops opened last year, so the store must offer better deals and faster service to keep its regular customers.","t":"A：體育用品店這個月為什麼把安全帽和手套的價格降這麼多？ B：自從去年兩家大型網路商店開業以來，市場變得非常【競爭激烈】，所以這家店必須提供更好的優惠和更快的服務來留住老顧客。"},{"w":"intense","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or extreme","c":"強烈的；激烈的","s":"A: How did you feel after the first day of the survival course that the company sent you to in the mountains? B: It was really intense, because we hiked for nine hours with heavy bags, built our own shelter before dark, and only had a few hours of sleep in the cold.","t":"A：公司派你去參加的山區求生課程，第一天結束後你感覺如何？ B：真的很【激烈】，因為我們背著沉重的背包健行了九個小時，在天黑前自己搭好避難所，而且只在寒冷中睡了幾個小時。"},{"w":"physically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to the body","c":"身體上地","s":"A: Why does the adventure travel agency ask every customer to fill out a health form before booking the glacier hiking tour? B: The tour lasts six hours on ice and steep paths, so guests must be physically fit and able to walk long distances without needing to stop and rest very often.","t":"A：探險旅行社為什麼要求每位顧客在預訂冰河健行行程前填寫健康表格？ B：這趟行程要在冰上和陡峭的小路上走六個小時，所以客人必須【身體上】健康，能夠走長距離而不需要經常停下來休息。"},{"w":"mentally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to the mind","c":"心理上地；精神上地","s":"A: What advice did the coach give the young climbers before the final stage of the competition yesterday afternoon? B: He told them that staying mentally strong is just as important as having powerful arms, because fear and panic can cause mistakes even when the body still has plenty of energy.","t":"A：昨天下午比賽最後階段前，教練給了年輕攀岩選手什麼建議？ B：他告訴他們，保持【心理上】的堅強和擁有強壯的手臂一樣重要，因為即使身體還有充足的體力，恐懼和驚慌也可能導致失誤。"},{"w":"courage","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something that frightens you","c":"勇氣","s":"A: Did our manager really give the opening speech at the international conference even though she is usually so shy? B: Yes, it took a lot of courage for her to stand in front of five hundred people, but she practiced every evening for a month and the audience loved her talk.","t":"A：我們經理平常那麼害羞，她真的在國際研討會上發表了開幕演說嗎？ B：是的，要站在五百人面前需要很大的【勇氣】，但她整整一個月每天晚上都在練習，觀眾都很喜歡她的演講。"},{"w":"stamina","p":"n.","d":"the energy to keep doing something for a long time","c":"耐力；體力","s":"A: Why are the new warehouse workers taking a fitness class every morning before their shifts start this month? B: The job requires carrying heavy boxes for eight hours a day, so the manager wants them to build enough stamina to work long hours without getting tired or hurting themselves.","t":"A：新的倉庫員工這個月為什麼每天早上上班前都要上體能課？ B：這份工作需要每天搬重箱子八個小時，所以經理希望他們培養足夠的【耐力】，能長時間工作而不會疲累或受傷。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"physical harm to the body","c":"傷害；受傷","s":"A: Why wasn't Kevin at the sales meeting this morning, and who is going to meet his clients from Japan this afternoon? B: He hurt his knee while skiing last weekend, and the doctor said the injury needs two weeks of rest, so Lisa will take care of his clients until he returns.","t":"A：凱文今天早上為什麼沒來參加業務會議？今天下午誰要去見他的日本客戶？ B：他上週末滑雪時傷了膝蓋，醫生說這個【傷勢】需要休息兩週，所以麗莎會負責照顧他的客戶直到他回來。"}]},{"unit":132,"theme":"Failed 失敗","cards":[{"w":"fail","p":"v.","d":"to not succeed in doing something","c":"失敗；未能","s":"A: Why does the marketing team look so worried this afternoon, and why did the director cancel the lunch meeting with the new clients? B: They think the online advertising campaign may fail because sales have not gone up at all in the last three weeks, so they are working hard on a new plan before Friday.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊今天下午看起來這麼擔心，而且主任為什麼取消了和新客戶的午餐會議？ B：他們認為網路廣告活動可能會【失敗】，因為過去三週銷售量完全沒有增加，所以他們正在努力在星期五之前想出新的計畫。"},{"w":"failure","p":"n.","d":"a lack of success; a machine or system stopping working","c":"失敗；故障","s":"A: Did the factory finish the large order for the hotel chain last night, or are the workers still waiting for the missing parts from the supplier? B: Unfortunately, a power failure stopped all the machines for six hours, so the night shift could not finish, and we have asked the hotel to give us two more days.","t":"A：工廠昨晚有完成連鎖飯店的大訂單嗎？還是工人們還在等供應商缺少的零件？ B：很不幸，一次電力【故障】讓所有機器停擺了六個小時，所以夜班無法完成，我們已經請飯店再給我們兩天。"},{"w":"unsuccessful","p":"adj.","d":"not getting the result you wanted","c":"不成功的；失敗的","s":"A: How did your interview for the manager position at the bank go last week, and have you heard anything from the human resources department yet? B: Sadly, my application was unsuccessful because they chose someone with more experience, but the interviewer said I should apply again next year when another position opens.","t":"A：你上週在銀行應徵經理職位的面試結果如何？你有收到人資部門的任何消息嗎？ B：很遺憾，我的申請【沒有成功】，因為他們選了一位經驗更豐富的人，不過面試官說明年有其他職缺時我應該再申請一次。"},{"w":"defeat","p":"n.","d":"the fact of losing a game, fight or competition","c":"失敗；挫敗","s":"A: Why is everyone in the sales department so quiet today, and why has the big celebration dinner on Friday night been canceled? B: Our company lost the city contract to a smaller competitor, and the manager took the defeat very hard because the whole team spent four months preparing the proposal.","t":"A：為什麼今天業務部的每個人都這麼安靜，而且星期五晚上的盛大慶功晚宴為什麼取消了？ B：我們公司把市政府的合約輸給了一家規模較小的競爭對手，經理對這次【挫敗】非常難過，因為整個團隊花了四個月準備企劃書。"},{"w":"defeated","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that you have lost and cannot succeed","c":"被擊敗的；感到挫敗的","s":"A: How did the young engineers react when the board of directors rejected their design for the new shopping center downtown? B: They felt completely defeated at first because they had worked late every night for weeks, but after a short break they started improving the plan with fresh ideas.","t":"A：董事會否決年輕工程師們為市中心新購物中心設計的方案時，他們有什麼反應？ B：一開始他們覺得完全【被擊垮】了，因為他們連續好幾週每晚都工作到很晚，但短暫休息後，他們就帶著新點子開始改善計畫。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"to fall down suddenly; to fail suddenly","c":"倒塌；崩潰；突然失敗","s":"A: Why did the city close the old shopping mall near the train station, and where will all the small shop owners move their businesses? B: Engineers warned that the roof might collapse after the heavy snow last winter, so the city is helping the owners find new spaces in the office building across the street.","t":"A：為什麼市政府關閉了火車站附近的舊購物中心？那些小店老闆會把生意搬到哪裡？ B：工程師警告說，經過去年冬天的大雪後，屋頂可能會【倒塌】，所以市政府正在協助店主們在對街的辦公大樓找新的空間。"},{"w":"flop","p":"n.","d":"a product, film or plan that is not successful","c":"失敗之作；徹底失敗","s":"A: Is the new energy drink that our company launched in September selling well in the supermarkets, or should we change the advertising plan? B: To be honest, it has been a complete flop because customers think it is too sweet and too expensive, so the product team wants to stop making it next month.","t":"A：我們公司九月推出的新能量飲料在超市賣得好嗎？還是我們應該改變廣告計畫？ B：老實說，它完全是個【失敗之作】，因為顧客覺得它太甜又太貴，所以產品團隊想從下個月起停產。"},{"w":"setback","p":"n.","d":"a problem that slows down progress","c":"挫折；阻礙","s":"A: Will the new branch office in Kaohsiung still open in March as planned, or do we need to tell our customers about a change? B: We had a small setback when the building company found problems with the electrical system, so the opening will probably be delayed by about three weeks.","t":"A：高雄的新分公司還會照計畫在三月開幕嗎？還是我們需要通知客戶有變動？ B：建築公司發現電力系統有問題，我們因此遇到了一點小【挫折】，所以開幕可能會延後大約三週。"},{"w":"breakdown","p":"n.","d":"a time when a machine or vehicle stops working","c":"故障；拋錨；(關係等)破裂","s":"A: Why did the delivery driver arrive at the restaurant two hours late with the fresh vegetables and meat for tonight's big dinner party? B: His truck had a breakdown on the highway, and he had to wait a long time for a mechanic, so the chef is now rushing to prepare everything before the guests arrive.","t":"A：為什麼送貨司機晚了兩個小時才把今晚大型晚宴要用的新鮮蔬菜和肉送到餐廳？ B：他的卡車在高速公路上【拋錨】了，他等了很久才等到技師，所以主廚現在正趕著在客人到達前準備好一切。"},{"w":"misstep","p":"n.","d":"a wrong action or bad decision","c":"失誤；失策","s":"A: Why did the new manager apologize to the whole team during the meeting this morning, and what exactly did he do wrong last week? B: He made a misstep by sending the confidential salary report to all employees by accident, but he quickly explained the situation and promised to be more careful.","t":"A：為什麼新經理今天早上在會議中向整個團隊道歉？他上週到底做錯了什麼？ B：他不小心把機密的薪資報告寄給了全體員工，犯了一個【失誤】，但他很快解釋了情況，並承諾以後會更小心。"},{"w":"mistake","p":"n.","d":"something that is wrong or not correct","c":"錯誤","s":"A: Why did the customer call the front desk three times this morning, and is she still angry about her hotel bill? B: The receptionist made a mistake and charged her for two nights instead of one, but we have already fixed the bill and offered her a free breakfast for the trouble.","t":"A：為什麼那位顧客今天早上打了三次電話到櫃台？她還在為飯店帳單生氣嗎？ B：接待員犯了一個【錯誤】，向她收了兩晚而不是一晚的費用，不過我們已經更正了帳單，並提供免費早餐作為補償。"},{"w":"error","p":"n.","d":"a mistake, especially in a system, number or calculation","c":"錯誤；差錯","s":"A: Why can't the staff in the accounting department log in to the new computer system this morning, and when will it be working again? B: The technician says a software error happened during last night's update, so he is fixing it now and expects everything to be ready before lunch.","t":"A：為什麼會計部門的員工今天早上無法登入新的電腦系統？什麼時候才能恢復正常？ B：技術人員說昨晚更新時發生了軟體【錯誤】，所以他現在正在修理，預計午餐前一切都會恢復。"},{"w":"fault","p":"n.","d":"a problem in a machine or system that stops it working well","c":"故障；缺陷；過錯","s":"A: Why are the passengers at gate twelve still waiting, and has the airline said when the flight to Tokyo will finally leave? B: The pilots found an electrical fault in the plane during the final safety check, so the engineers are repairing it, and the airline is giving everyone free meal coupons.","t":"A：為什麼十二號登機門的乘客還在等？航空公司有說飛往東京的班機什麼時候才會起飛嗎？ B：機師在最後的安全檢查時發現飛機有電力【故障】，所以工程師正在修理，航空公司也發給每個人免費餐券。"},{"w":"abort","p":"v.","d":"to stop something before it is finished, usually because of a problem","c":"中止；放棄(計畫等)","s":"A: Why did the technology company stop the launch of its new satellite yesterday afternoon when thousands of people were watching online? B: The engineers decided to abort the launch only ten seconds before takeoff because a sensor showed a problem with the fuel system, and they will try again next week.","t":"A：為什麼那家科技公司昨天下午在數千人線上觀看時停止了新衛星的發射？ B：工程師在起飛前僅十秒決定【中止】發射，因為一個感應器顯示燃料系統有問題，他們下週會再試一次。"},{"w":"fall apart","p":"v.phr.","d":"to break into pieces; to stop working or existing","c":"瓦解；崩潰；散架","s":"A: What happened to the business partnership between the two restaurant owners who opened that popular café downtown last year? B: Their partnership started to fall apart when they argued about money and the menu, so one of them sold his share and moved to another city to start a bakery.","t":"A：去年在市中心開了那家熱門咖啡館的兩位餐廳老闆，他們的合夥關係後來怎麼了？ B：他們為了錢和菜單爭吵後，合夥關係就開始【瓦解】，所以其中一人賣掉了股份，搬到另一個城市開麵包店。"},{"w":"give up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop trying to do something","c":"放棄","s":"A: Is your sister still studying for the accounting exam while working full-time at the bank, or has she decided to wait until next year? B: She was very tired and almost wanted to give up, but her manager offered her a flexible schedule, so now she studies every morning before work.","t":"A：你姊姊還一邊在銀行全職工作、一邊準備會計考試嗎？還是她決定等到明年？ B：她非常累，差點想【放棄】，但她的經理給了她彈性的上班時間，所以現在她每天上班前早上念書。"},{"w":"lose","p":"v.","d":"to stop having something; to not win","c":"失去；輸掉","s":"A: Why does the sales director want to meet with the customer service team immediately after lunch today? B: She is worried that we will lose our biggest customer because their orders have arrived late three times this month, so she wants a better delivery plan before she calls them.","t":"A：為什麼業務總監今天想在午餐後馬上和客服團隊開會？ B：她擔心我們會【失去】最大的客戶，因為他們的訂單這個月已經遲到三次了，所以她想在打電話給他們之前先擬好更好的送貨計畫。"},{"w":"miss","p":"v.","d":"to be too late for something, or to not hit or catch it","c":"錯過；未趕上","s":"A: Why are you leaving the office so early today when we still have so many reports to finish before the end of the month? B: I have to catch the five o'clock train to Taichung for a client meeting tomorrow morning, and if I miss it, the next one does not leave until nine tonight.","t":"A：我們在月底前還有這麼多報告要完成，你今天為什麼這麼早離開辦公室？ B：我必須趕上五點往台中的火車，明天早上要和客戶開會，如果我【錯過】這班，下一班要到今晚九點才開。"},{"w":"botched","p":"adj.","d":"done badly or carelessly","c":"搞砸的；拙劣的","s":"A: Why is the restaurant on the corner closed this week, and when will customers be able to eat there again? B: The owner hired a cheap company for the kitchen repairs, but it was a botched job with leaking pipes everywhere, so another team is fixing everything and they hope to reopen next Monday.","t":"A：轉角那家餐廳為什麼這週停業？顧客什麼時候才能再去用餐？ B：老闆請了一家便宜的公司來修廚房，結果是個【搞砸的】工程，到處都是漏水的管線，所以另一組人正在修理一切，他們希望下週一重新開幕。"},{"w":"fruitless","p":"adj.","d":"producing no useful result","c":"毫無成果的；徒勞的","s":"A: Did the purchasing manager find a cheaper supplier for our office paper and printer ink during her business trip to Singapore? B: No, her search was fruitless because every company she visited asked for higher prices than our current supplier, so we will keep our old contract for another year.","t":"A：採購經理到新加坡出差時，有找到更便宜的辦公用紙和印表機墨水供應商嗎？ B：沒有，她的尋找【毫無成果】，因為她拜訪的每家公司開價都比我們現在的供應商高，所以我們會再續約舊合約一年。"},{"w":"ineffective","p":"adj.","d":"not working well or not producing the result you want","c":"無效的；效果不佳的","s":"A: Why did the city government decide to change the parking rules downtown again after only two months? B: The old rules were ineffective because many drivers still parked on the sidewalks, and shop owners complained that customers could not walk easily, so officials will now add more parking officers and higher fines.","t":"A：為什麼市政府才過兩個月就決定再次修改市中心的停車規定？ B：舊規定【沒有效果】，因為很多駕駛還是把車停在人行道上，店家也抱怨顧客無法順利行走，所以官員們現在會增加更多停車稽查員並提高罰款。"},{"w":"futile","p":"adj.","d":"having no chance of success; useless","c":"徒勞的；無用的","s":"A: Should we keep calling the airline to ask about our missing luggage, or should we just go to the hotel and wait for news? B: I think more calls are futile because the agent said the bags are still in Hong Kong, so let's check in, rest, and buy a few things we need for tomorrow's meeting.","t":"A：我們應該繼續打電話給航空公司詢問遺失的行李，還是直接去飯店等消息？ B：我覺得再打電話也是【徒勞無功】，因為客服人員說行李還在香港，所以我們先入住、休息，再買一些明天開會需要的東西吧。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it is spoiled","c":"毀壞；毀掉","s":"A: Why does the event manager look so nervous about the outdoor wedding party at the garden hotel this Saturday afternoon? B: The weather report says heavy rain may ruin the whole celebration, so she is calling the hotel to ask if they can move the dinner and music into the big ballroom.","t":"A：為什麼活動經理對這週六下午在花園飯店舉行的戶外婚宴看起來這麼緊張？ B：氣象報告說大雨可能會【毀了】整個慶祝活動，所以她正打電話問飯店能不能把晚宴和音樂移到大宴會廳。"},{"w":"derail","p":"v.","d":"to stop a plan or process from continuing as planned","c":"使脫軌；使(計畫)受挫","s":"A: Why is the project manager so worried about the new factory, and does she think it will still be finished by the end of the year? B: She fears that the shortage of steel could derail the whole project, so she is looking for another supplier and asking the workers to focus on other tasks for now.","t":"A：為什麼專案經理對新工廠這麼擔心？她覺得年底前還能完工嗎？ B：她擔心鋼材短缺可能會讓整個專案【脫軌】，所以她正在找其他供應商，並請工人們暫時專注於其他工作。"},{"w":"disaster","p":"n.","d":"something very bad that causes great damage or a complete failure","c":"災難；徹底的失敗","s":"A: How was the company's first outdoor sales event at the city park last Saturday, and did many new customers sign up? B: It was a total disaster because a storm knocked down our tents and the sound system stopped working, so we have decided to hold the next event inside the convention center.","t":"A：公司上週六在市立公園舉辦的第一場戶外促銷活動如何？有很多新客戶登記嗎？ B：那完全是一場【災難】，因為暴風雨吹倒了我們的帳篷，音響系統也壞了，所以我們決定下次活動改在會議中心室內舉行。"},{"w":"downfall","p":"n.","d":"the loss of power, money or success","c":"垮台；沒落","s":"A: Why did the famous electronics company close all of its stores last year after being so successful for many decades? B: Many experts say its downfall came from ignoring smartphones, because the managers kept selling old products while younger customers moved to newer brands with better technology.","t":"A：為什麼那家著名的電子公司在成功了幾十年之後，去年關閉了所有門市？ B：許多專家說它的【沒落】是因為忽視了智慧型手機，經理們一直在賣舊產品，而年輕顧客則轉向擁有更好技術的新品牌。"},{"w":"letdown","p":"n.","d":"something that is not as good as you hoped","c":"令人失望的事","s":"A: Did you enjoy the expensive dinner at the new French restaurant that the marketing director recommended to everyone in the office? B: To be honest, it was a big letdown because the food was cold and the service was very slow, so I don't think I will take any of our clients there.","t":"A：你喜歡行銷總監推薦給辦公室所有人的那家新法式餐廳的昂貴晚餐嗎？ B：老實說，那真是一大【令人失望的事】，因為食物是冷的，服務又非常慢，所以我想我不會帶任何客戶去那裡。"},{"w":"washout","p":"n.","d":"an event that fails, often because of rain","c":"(因雨)泡湯的活動；徹底失敗","s":"A: How was the company's summer barbecue at the beach last Friday, and did the new employees have a chance to meet everyone? B: Unfortunately, it was a complete washout because it rained all afternoon, so most people went home early, and the manager plans to hold another party next month.","t":"A：公司上週五在海灘舉辦的夏季烤肉活動如何？新員工有機會認識大家嗎？ B：很遺憾，那完全是一場【泡湯的活動】，因為整個下午都在下雨，大部分人提早回家，所以經理打算下個月再辦一次派對。"}]},{"unit":133,"theme":"Family 家庭","cards":[{"w":"parent","p":"n.","d":"a mother or a father","c":"父親或母親；家長","s":"A: Why is the new receptionist leaving the office at four o'clock every day this month, even when the lobby is still busy with visitors? B: She is a single parent of two young kids, so the manager agreed she could pick them up from school and finish her reports online at night.","t":"A：為什麼新來的接待員這個月每天四點就離開辦公室，即使大廳還有很多訪客？ B：她是兩個小孩的單親【家長】，所以經理同意她去學校接孩子，晚上再在線上完成報告。"},{"w":"father","p":"n.","d":"a male parent","c":"父親；爸爸","s":"A: Is Mr. Chen taking a few days off next week, because I need him to sign the new supplier contract before Friday? B: Yes, he just became a father for the first time last night, so he is on paternity leave, but his assistant can send the contract to his email.","t":"A：陳先生下週要請幾天假嗎？因為我需要他在星期五前簽新的供應商合約。 B：是的，他昨晚第一次當【父親】，所以正在請陪產假，不過他的助理可以把合約寄到他的電子信箱。"},{"w":"mother","p":"n.","d":"a female parent","c":"母親；媽媽","s":"A: Why did the marketing team change the date of the company picnic from Saturday to the following weekend? B: Our team leader's mother is coming from Kaohsiung to visit her for a few days, and she didn't want to miss the picnic, so everyone agreed to move it.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊把公司野餐的日期從星期六改到下個週末？ B：我們組長的【母親】要從高雄來看她幾天，她不想錯過野餐，所以大家都同意延期。"},{"w":"child","p":"n.","d":"a young boy or girl; a son or daughter","c":"孩子；兒童","s":"A: Does the hotel offer any discounts for families who are traveling with young kids during the summer holiday season? B: Yes, each child under twelve can stay for free in the same room as the parents, and breakfast at the buffet restaurant is also half price for them.","t":"A：飯店在暑假旺季有提供帶小孩旅行的家庭任何折扣嗎？ B：有的，每位十二歲以下的【孩子】和父母同房可免費入住，自助餐廳的早餐也半價。"},{"w":"son","p":"n.","d":"a male child of a parent","c":"兒子","s":"A: Why is the owner of the bakery not working behind the counter this morning like he usually does? B: He has finally handed the daily business over to his son, who studied baking in Japan for three years, so now he only comes in on weekends to check the quality.","t":"A：為什麼麵包店老闆今天早上不像平常一樣在櫃檯後面工作？ B：他終於把日常生意交給了他的【兒子】，他兒子在日本學了三年烘焙，所以現在他只有週末才來檢查品質。"},{"w":"daughter","p":"n.","d":"a female child of a parent","c":"女兒","s":"A: Who is the young woman sitting at the front desk today, and why is she answering the phones for the clinic? B: She is the dentist's daughter, and since she is home from university for the summer, she offered to help while our regular receptionist is on vacation.","t":"A：今天坐在櫃檯的年輕女子是誰？為什麼她在幫診所接電話？ B：她是牙醫的【女兒】，因為她暑假從大學回家，所以在我們的固定接待員休假時主動來幫忙。"},{"w":"sibling","p":"n.","d":"a brother or a sister","c":"兄弟姊妹","s":"A: The application form for the company scholarship asks if any brothers or sisters also work here, so what should I write? B: If you have a sibling in any department of the company, just write down their name and position, because the rules say family members cannot review each other's applications.","t":"A：公司獎學金的申請表問有沒有兄弟姊妹也在這裡工作，我該怎麼寫？ B：如果你有【兄弟姊妹】在公司任何部門，就寫下他們的姓名和職位，因為規定家人不能審核彼此的申請。"},{"w":"brother","p":"n.","d":"a boy or man who has the same parents as you","c":"兄弟；哥哥；弟弟","s":"A: Who will take care of your flower shop while you are attending the trade show in Singapore next month? B: My younger brother has worked there with me for years, so he knows all our regular customers and suppliers, and he will open the shop every morning while I'm away.","t":"A：你下個月去新加坡參加貿易展時，誰會照顧你的花店？ B：我【弟弟】已經和我一起在那裡工作好幾年了，他認識所有的老客戶和供應商，我不在時他每天早上都會開店。"},{"w":"sister","p":"n.","d":"a girl or woman who has the same parents as you","c":"姊妹；姊姊；妹妹","s":"A: How did you find such a good accountant for your small business after your last one moved to another city? B: My older sister recommended her, since the accountant has handled the tax returns for her restaurant for over ten years and never made a single mistake.","t":"A：你上一位會計搬到別的城市後，你是怎麼為你的小公司找到這麼好的會計的？ B：我【姊姊】推薦她的，因為這位會計替她的餐廳處理報稅已經超過十年，從沒出過任何差錯。"},{"w":"grandparent","p":"n.","d":"the father or mother of your parent","c":"祖父母；外祖父母","s":"A: Why did you ask the travel agent for a hotel room with two beds and an elevator close to the room? B: I'm taking my kids on a trip, and one grandparent is coming with us too, so we need a room that is easy to reach because walking up stairs is difficult for him.","t":"A：你為什麼要求旅行社安排有兩張床、而且離電梯近的房間？ B：我要帶孩子去旅行，還有一位【祖父母】也跟我們一起去，所以需要一間容易到達的房間，因為爬樓梯對他來說很困難。"},{"w":"grandfather","p":"n.","d":"the father of your father or mother","c":"祖父；外祖父","s":"A: That old wooden desk in your office looks really beautiful, so where did you buy it? B: I didn't buy it, because my grandfather made it by hand more than fifty years ago when he was a carpenter, and he gave it to me when I opened my own law firm.","t":"A：你辦公室那張舊木桌看起來真漂亮，你在哪裡買的？ B：不是買的，是我【祖父】五十多年前當木匠時親手做的，我開了自己的律師事務所時他送給了我。"},{"w":"grandmother","p":"n.","d":"the mother of your father or mother","c":"祖母；外祖母","s":"A: Your new restaurant's beef noodle soup is so popular that customers are waiting in line outside every evening, so what's the secret? B: The recipe came from my grandmother, who cooked it for our family every winter, and I only changed a few ingredients to make it suitable for a restaurant kitchen.","t":"A：你新餐廳的牛肉麵好受歡迎，每天晚上客人都在外面排隊，秘訣是什麼？ B：食譜來自我的【祖母】，她每年冬天都為我們家煮這道湯，我只改了幾樣食材，讓它適合餐廳廚房。"},{"w":"relative","p":"n.","d":"a person in your family","c":"親戚；親屬","s":"A: Why did you request three days of personal leave at the end of this month, since that is our busiest week? B: A close relative is getting married in Tainan that weekend, and my whole family is expected to attend the wedding banquet, so I really cannot miss it.","t":"A：你為什麼申請在月底請三天事假？那是我們最忙的一週。 B：一位近【親戚】那個週末要在台南結婚，我們全家都要參加喜宴，所以我真的不能缺席。"},{"w":"cousin","p":"n.","d":"a child of your aunt or uncle","c":"堂／表兄弟姊妹","s":"A: How did you get an interview at that famous design company when they almost never advertise open positions? B: My cousin works in their human resources department, and she told me about the opening before it was announced, but I still had to pass three difficult interviews.","t":"A：那家知名設計公司幾乎從不公開徵才，你是怎麼得到面試機會的？ B：我的【表姊】在他們的人資部門工作，她在職缺公布前就告訴我，但我還是得通過三次很難的面試。"},{"w":"uncle","p":"n.","d":"the brother of your mother or father, or your aunt's husband","c":"叔叔；伯伯；舅舅；姑丈；姨丈","s":"A: Are you going to work at the bank after you graduate, or have you decided to try something different? B: My uncle runs a small trading company in Taichung, and he offered me a job as his assistant, so I will learn about importing and exporting from him for a couple of years.","t":"A：你畢業後要去銀行工作，還是決定嘗試不同的工作？ B：我【叔叔】在台中經營一家小貿易公司，他給了我一份助理的工作，所以我會跟他學幾年進出口。"},{"w":"aunt","p":"n.","d":"the sister of your mother or father, or your uncle's wife","c":"阿姨；姑姑；嬸嬸；舅媽","s":"A: Where are you staying during your business trip to Vancouver, since the hotels near the convention center are fully booked? B: My aunt lives about twenty minutes from the center, so she invited me to stay in her guest room, which will save the company a lot of money on hotel costs.","t":"A：你去溫哥華出差住哪裡？會議中心附近的飯店都客滿了。 B：我【阿姨】住在離中心大約二十分鐘的地方，她邀請我住她的客房，這樣能幫公司省下很多住宿費。"},{"w":"nephew","p":"n.","d":"a son of your brother or sister","c":"姪子；外甥","s":"A: Who is the teenager helping you carry boxes into the storage room this afternoon? He works really hard. B: He's my sister's son, so he's my nephew, and he wanted some work experience during his summer vacation, so I asked the manager if he could help us for a week.","t":"A：今天下午幫你把箱子搬進儲藏室的青少年是誰？他工作很認真。 B：他是我姊姊的兒子，所以是我的【外甥】，他想在暑假累積一些工作經驗，所以我問經理他能不能幫我們一週。"},{"w":"niece","p":"n.","d":"a daughter of your brother or sister","c":"姪女；外甥女","s":"A: Why are you buying so many children's books at the bookstore today when you don't have any kids? B: My niece, my brother's little girl, is turning six this weekend, and she loves stories about animals, so I'm getting her a few as a birthday present.","t":"A：你沒有小孩，為什麼今天在書店買這麼多童書？ B：我的【姪女】，也就是我哥哥的小女兒，這個週末滿六歲，她喜歡動物故事，所以我要買幾本當生日禮物。"},{"w":"marriage","p":"n.","d":"the legal relationship between a husband and wife","c":"婚姻","s":"A: Why does the HR department need a copy of my wedding certificate before the end of this month? B: Because your marriage changes your health insurance plan, they need official proof so that your wife can be added to the company insurance and receive the same benefits as you.","t":"A：為什麼人資部門需要我在月底前交結婚證書影本？ B：因為你的【婚姻】會改變你的健康保險方案，他們需要正式證明，才能把你太太加入公司保險，並享有和你一樣的福利。"},{"w":"couple","p":"n.","d":"two people who are married or in a relationship","c":"夫妻；情侶","s":"A: Who is renting the empty apartment on the third floor of our building, and when will they move in? B: A young couple from Hsinchu signed the lease yesterday, and they plan to move in next Saturday, because the husband just started a new job at the hospital near here.","t":"A：誰要租我們大樓三樓那間空公寓？他們什麼時候搬進來？ B：一對來自新竹的年輕【夫妻】昨天簽了租約，打算下星期六搬進來，因為先生剛在附近的醫院開始新工作。"},{"w":"spouse","p":"n.","d":"a husband or wife","c":"配偶","s":"A: Can I bring someone with me to the company's year-end party at the hotel, or is it only for employees? B: Every employee may bring a spouse or partner, but please add their name to the online form by Friday so that the event planner can arrange enough seats and meals.","t":"A：我可以帶人參加公司在飯店舉辦的尾牙嗎？還是只限員工？ B：每位員工可以攜帶【配偶】或伴侶，但請在星期五前把他們的名字填進線上表單，讓活動企劃安排足夠的座位和餐點。"},{"w":"husband","p":"n.","d":"the man a woman is married to","c":"丈夫；先生","s":"A: You usually drive to work, so why did you take the bus this morning and arrive so late? B: My husband needed the car to take our daughter to the hospital for a check-up, so I took the bus, but it was stuck in heavy traffic near the train station.","t":"A：你平常開車上班，為什麼今天早上搭公車而且這麼晚到？ B：我【先生】需要開車帶女兒去醫院檢查，所以我搭了公車，但它在火車站附近塞車了。"},{"w":"wife","p":"n.","d":"the woman a man is married to","c":"妻子；太太","s":"A: Why is Mr. Lin moving to the Tokyo branch next spring when he has worked in this office for fifteen years? B: His wife got a great job offer from a Japanese university, so they decided to move together, and the company agreed to transfer him to our Tokyo branch.","t":"A：林先生在這間辦公室工作了十五年，為什麼明年春天要調到東京分公司？ B：他【太太】得到日本一所大學很好的工作機會，所以他們決定一起搬過去，公司也同意把他調到東京分公司。"},{"w":"home","p":"n.","d":"the place where you live","c":"家；住所","s":"A: Will you be in the office tomorrow, because I'd like to show you the new design for the client's website? B: I'll be working from home tomorrow because a technician is coming to fix my washing machine, but we can have a video call at ten and share the screen.","t":"A：你明天會進辦公室嗎？我想給你看客戶網站的新設計。 B：我明天會在【家】工作，因為有技師要來修洗衣機，不過我們可以十點視訊通話並分享螢幕。"},{"w":"household","p":"n.","d":"all the people who live together in one house","c":"一戶人家；家庭","s":"A: Why did the electric company send us this survey about how much power we use every month? B: They are collecting information from every household in the city, because they want to understand how families use electricity so they can plan a cheaper price plan for next year.","t":"A：電力公司為什麼寄這份每月用電量的問卷給我們？ B：他們正在向市內每一【戶人家】收集資料，因為想了解家庭如何用電，以便規劃明年更便宜的電價方案。"},{"w":"relationship","p":"n.","d":"the way two people or groups feel and act toward each other","c":"關係","s":"A: How did you keep such a big client for over ten years, even when other companies offered them lower prices? B: We built a strong relationship with their managers by visiting them often, answering problems quickly, and always being honest about delivery times, so they trust us more than cheaper suppliers.","t":"A：即使其他公司開價更低，你是怎麼留住這麼大的客戶超過十年的？ B：我們經常拜訪他們、快速處理問題，並且對交貨時間總是誠實，和他們的經理建立了穩固的【關係】，所以他們比起較便宜的供應商更信任我們。"},{"w":"support","p":"n.","d":"help and encouragement","c":"支持；幫助","s":"A: How did you manage to finish your MBA at night while working full-time at the bank and raising two kids? B: Well, I couldn't have done it without the support of my family, because my parents cooked dinner for the kids and my husband helped them with their homework every evening.","t":"A：你是怎麼一邊在銀行全職工作、養兩個孩子，一邊晚上完成MBA的？ B：嗯，沒有家人的【支持】我做不到，因為我父母幫孩子煮晚餐，我先生每天晚上幫他們寫功課。"},{"w":"care","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking after someone","c":"照顧；照料","s":"A: Who looks after your father during the day now that he can no longer live by himself? B: A nurse comes to his apartment every morning to provide daily care, such as helping him take his medicine and cook lunch, and my brother visits him after work every evening.","t":"A：既然你父親無法再獨自生活，白天誰照顧他？ B：每天早上有護理師到他的公寓提供日常【照顧】，例如幫他吃藥和煮午餐，我哥哥每天下班後也會去看他。"},{"w":"bond","p":"n.","d":"a close feeling that connects people","c":"情感連結；聯繫","s":"A: Why does the company organize a family day at the amusement park every year when it costs so much money? B: The managers believe it helps create a strong bond between employees and their families, and staff who feel connected to the company usually stay longer and work harder.","t":"A：公司每年都在遊樂園舉辦家庭日，花費很多，為什麼還要辦？ B：經理們認為這有助於在員工和家人之間建立緊密的【情感連結】，而對公司有歸屬感的員工通常待得更久、工作更努力。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom that people have followed for a long time","c":"傳統；慣例","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office bringing homemade dumplings to share for lunch today? B: It's a tradition in our department that started about twenty years ago, because every winter before the holidays, each person brings a dish from their hometown so that we can celebrate together like one big family.","t":"A：為什麼今天辦公室每個人都帶自己包的水餃來分享當午餐？ B：這是我們部門大約二十年前開始的【傳統】，每年冬天放假前，每個人都會帶一道家鄉菜，讓我們像一個大家庭一樣一起慶祝。"},{"w":"generation","p":"n.","d":"all the people born at about the same time; one step in a family line","c":"世代；一代","s":"A: How long has this tea shop been open on this street, because the building looks really old? B: The same family has run it for more than a hundred years, and the owner you met today is the fourth generation to manage the shop, after his father, grandfather, and great-grandfather.","t":"A：這家茶行在這條街上開多久了？建築看起來很老。 B：同一個家族經營它超過一百年了，你今天見到的老闆是經營這家店的第四【代】，前面是他的父親、祖父和曾祖父。"},{"w":"close-knit","p":"adj.","d":"having close, caring relationships","c":"緊密團結的；關係親密的","s":"A: Why do so many employees at that small accounting firm stay for so long instead of moving to bigger companies? B: The firm has a very close-knit team of about fifteen people who eat lunch together, celebrate birthdays, and help each other during the busy tax season, so it feels like a family.","t":"A：為什麼那家小會計事務所的員工待那麼久，而不跳槽到大公司？ B：那家事務所有一支大約十五人、非常【緊密團結的】團隊，他們一起吃午餐、慶祝生日，並在忙碌的報稅季互相幫忙，所以感覺像一家人。"},{"w":"loving","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of love and care","c":"充滿愛的；慈愛的","s":"A: What did the parents in the survey say they want most from the new day care center near the office? B: Most of them said they want a safe and loving place where the teachers are kind and patient, because they worry about leaving their babies with strangers for eight hours a day.","t":"A：調查中的家長說他們最希望辦公室附近新的托兒中心提供什麼？ B：大部分人說想要一個安全又【充滿愛的】地方，老師親切有耐心，因為他們擔心每天把寶寶交給陌生人八小時。"},{"w":"responsible","p":"adj.","d":"having the duty to take care of something","c":"負責的；有責任的","s":"A: Who should I talk to about the broken air conditioner in the meeting room on the fifth floor? B: Please contact Mr. Wu in the facilities department, because he is responsible for all repairs in the building, and he can usually send a technician within one or two working days.","t":"A：五樓會議室冷氣壞了，我該找誰？ B：請聯絡設施部門的吳先生，因為他【負責】大樓所有的維修，通常一兩個工作天內就能派技師過來。"},{"w":"together","p":"adv.","d":"with each other; as a group","c":"一起；共同","s":"A: Are you and your sister planning to open the new coffee shop by yourselves, or will you hire a manager? B: We will run it together for the first year, because she is good at baking and I'm good at accounting, and then we may hire a manager when the business grows.","t":"A：你和你姊姊打算自己開這家新咖啡店，還是會請一位經理？ B：第一年我們會【一起】經營，因為她擅長烘焙，我擅長會計，等生意變大後可能再請經理。"}]},{"unit":134,"theme":"Family Member 家庭成員","cards":[{"w":"parent","p":"n.","d":"a mother or a father","c":"父親或母親；家長","s":"A: Why is the school's open house starting at seven in the evening instead of during the afternoon this year? B: The principal moved it because almost every working parent told her that leaving the office early was too difficult, and she wants more families to meet the new teachers.","t":"A：今年學校的開放日為什麼從晚上七點開始，而不是在下午？ B：校長把它改了時間，因為幾乎每位上班的【家長】都告訴她提早下班太困難，而她希望有更多家庭能認識新老師。"},{"w":"father","p":"n.","d":"a male parent","c":"父親","s":"A: Is it true that Mr. Lin is taking two weeks off right after the big product launch next month? B: Yes, his wife is expecting their first baby in March, and the company gives every new father paid leave so he can help at home during those busy first weeks.","t":"A：林先生下個月大型產品發表會一結束就要休假兩週，是真的嗎？ B：是的，他太太三月要生第一胎，而公司給每位新手【爸爸】有薪假，讓他能在最忙碌的頭幾週在家幫忙。"},{"w":"mother","p":"n.","d":"a female parent","c":"母親","s":"A: Why did Karen ask to work from home on Tuesdays and Thursdays starting next semester? B: She is a mother of three young kids, and since their school ends at noon on those days, she needs to pick them up and make lunch before her afternoon meetings.","t":"A：凱倫為什麼要求從下學期開始每週二和週四在家工作？ B：她是三個年幼孩子的【母親】，而因為孩子們的學校那兩天中午就放學，她需要在下午開會之前去接他們並準備午餐。"},{"w":"child","p":"n.","d":"a young boy or girl; a son or daughter","c":"小孩；子女","s":"A: Do we need to buy a full-price ticket for my nephew when we visit the science museum downtown this weekend? B: No, the museum lets each child under twelve enter for half price on weekends, so you can save some money and spend it on lunch instead.","t":"A：這個週末我們去市中心的科學博物館時，需要幫我外甥買全票嗎？ B：不用，博物館週末讓每位十二歲以下的【兒童】半價入場，所以你可以省點錢，拿去吃午餐。"},{"w":"son","p":"n.","d":"a male child of a parent","c":"兒子","s":"A: Who is the young man helping the owner carry boxes into the bakery every morning before it opens? B: That is her son, who just finished university, and he plans to take over the family business someday, so he is learning how to bake and manage the store.","t":"A：每天早上開店前幫老闆把箱子搬進麵包店的那位年輕人是誰？ B：那是她的【兒子】，他剛從大學畢業，打算有一天接手家族事業，所以正在學習烘焙和經營這家店。"},{"w":"daughter","p":"n.","d":"a female child of a parent","c":"女兒","s":"A: Why is the manager leaving the office so early this Friday when we still have the monthly report to finish? B: Her daughter is graduating from high school this afternoon, and she promised the girl months ago that she would be in the front row for the ceremony.","t":"A：這個週五我們還有月報要完成，經理為什麼這麼早就離開辦公室？ B：她的【女兒】今天下午高中畢業，而她好幾個月前就答應那個女孩會坐在第一排參加典禮。"},{"w":"sibling","p":"n.","d":"a brother or a sister","c":"兄弟姊妹","s":"A: Does the new employee form ask about family members other than a spouse and children for the health insurance plan? B: Yes, you can list one sibling as an emergency contact, so if you have a brother or sister living nearby, please write down their name and phone number.","t":"A：新進員工表格的健康保險部分，除了配偶和子女之外還會詢問其他家人嗎？ B：會，你可以填寫一位【兄弟姊妹】作為緊急聯絡人，所以如果你有住在附近的兄弟或姊妹，請寫下他們的姓名和電話。"},{"w":"brother","p":"n.","d":"a boy or man who has the same parents as you","c":"兄弟","s":"A: How did you find such a reliable mechanic so quickly after your car broke down on the way to the client meeting? B: My older brother owns a small garage near the station, so I called him, and he sent his best worker to tow my car right away.","t":"A：你的車在去見客戶的路上拋錨後，你怎麼這麼快就找到可靠的修車師傅？ B：我【哥哥】在車站附近開了一家小修車廠，所以我打電話給他，他立刻派最好的員工來把我的車拖走。"},{"w":"sister","p":"n.","d":"a girl or woman who has the same parents as you","c":"姊妹","s":"A: Are you going to stay in a hotel when you travel to Tokyo for the trade show next month? B: No, my younger sister works for a design company there and has a spare room, so she invited me to stay with her and save the company some money.","t":"A：下個月你去東京參加商展時會住飯店嗎？ B：不會，我【妹妹】在那裡的一家設計公司上班，有一間空房，所以她邀我和她一起住，也替公司省點錢。"},{"w":"grandparent","p":"n.","d":"the father or mother of your parent","c":"祖父母；外祖父母","s":"A: Why are there so many older people with small children at the amusement park on a Wednesday morning? B: Many parents are at work during the week, so a grandparent often takes the kids out on school holidays, and the park offers cheaper tickets for seniors on weekdays.","t":"A：為什麼週三早上的遊樂園有這麼多老人帶著小孩？ B：許多父母平日都在上班，所以學校放假時常由【祖父母】帶孩子出門，而且遊樂園平日提供較便宜的敬老票。"},{"w":"grandfather","p":"n.","d":"the father of your father or mother","c":"祖父；外祖父","s":"A: How did you learn so much about fixing old clocks and watches before you started working at this repair shop? B: My grandfather was a watchmaker for forty years, and when I was a boy, I spent every summer vacation in his small store watching him repair them.","t":"A：你來這家修理店工作之前，怎麼會懂得這麼多修理舊時鐘和手錶的知識？ B：我【爺爺】當了四十年的鐘錶師傅，我小時候每個暑假都待在他的小店裡看他修理鐘錶。"},{"w":"grandmother","p":"n.","d":"the mother of your father or mother","c":"祖母；外祖母","s":"A: Your new restaurant's beef noodle soup is amazing, so where did you get such a special recipe? B: It came from my grandmother, who cooked it for the whole family every Lunar New Year, and before she passed away, she taught me every step and secret ingredient.","t":"A：你新餐廳的牛肉麵太棒了，你是從哪裡得到這麼特別的食譜的？ B：它來自我的【奶奶】，她每年農曆新年都會煮給全家人吃，在她過世之前，她教了我每個步驟和秘密食材。"},{"w":"relative","p":"n.","d":"a person in your family","c":"親戚","s":"A: Why are you taking a whole week of vacation in the middle of the busy season this year? B: A close relative of mine is getting married in Canada, and since my whole family is flying over for the wedding, I don't want to miss this rare chance to see everyone.","t":"A：今年你為什麼在旺季中間請了一整個星期的假？ B：我的一位近【親】要在加拿大結婚，既然我全家都要飛過去參加婚禮，我不想錯過這個難得能見到大家的機會。"},{"w":"cousin","p":"n.","d":"the child of your aunt or uncle","c":"堂／表兄弟姊妹","s":"A: Do you know anyone who could help us translate these product brochures into Japanese before the trade fair next week? B: My cousin grew up in Osaka because her father, my uncle, worked there, so she speaks perfect Japanese and might do it for a reasonable price.","t":"A：你認識誰能在下週商展前幫我們把這些產品手冊翻譯成日文嗎？ B：我的【表姊】在大阪長大，因為她父親，也就是我舅舅，在那裡工作，所以她的日文非常好，也許能以合理的價格幫忙。"},{"w":"uncle","p":"n.","d":"the brother of your father or mother, or your aunt's husband","c":"叔叔；伯伯；舅舅；姑丈；姨丈","s":"A: How did you get such a good summer job at the shipping company when you were still a university student? B: My uncle, who is my mother's older brother, worked there as a manager, so he told me about the opening and helped me prepare for the interview.","t":"A：你還是大學生的時候，怎麼能在那家貨運公司找到這麼好的暑期工作？ B：我的【舅舅】，也就是我母親的哥哥，在那裡當經理，所以他告訴我有職缺，還幫我準備面試。"},{"w":"aunt","p":"n.","d":"the sister of your father or mother, or your uncle's wife","c":"阿姨；姑姑；嬸嬸；舅媽","s":"A: Who will take care of your children while you attend the three-day training course in Kaohsiung next week? B: My aunt, who is my mother's younger sister, has just retired, so she offered to stay at our apartment and drive the kids to school every day.","t":"A：下週你去高雄參加三天的訓練課程時，誰來照顧你的孩子？ B：我的【阿姨】，也就是我母親的妹妹，剛退休，所以她主動提出要住在我們公寓，每天開車送孩子上學。"},{"w":"nephew","p":"n.","d":"the son of your brother or sister","c":"姪子；外甥","s":"A: Why did you buy so many toy cars at the department store during your lunch break today? B: My sister's little boy turns five on Saturday, and since he loves anything with wheels, I want to give my nephew a big box of cars at his birthday party.","t":"A：你今天午休時為什麼在百貨公司買了那麼多玩具車？ B：我姊姊的小兒子週六滿五歲，而且他喜歡任何有輪子的東西，所以我想在他的生日派對上送我的【外甥】一大盒車子。"},{"w":"niece","p":"n.","d":"the daughter of your brother or sister","c":"姪女；外甥女","s":"A: Do you know anyone who might be interested in the summer internship we are offering in the marketing department? B: My brother's daughter is studying business at university, so I will tell my niece about the position tonight and ask her to send you her résumé.","t":"A：你知道有誰可能對我們行銷部提供的暑期實習有興趣嗎？ B：我哥哥的女兒正在大學念商科，所以我今晚會告訴我的【姪女】這個職缺，並請她把履歷寄給你。"},{"w":"spouse","p":"n.","d":"a husband or wife","c":"配偶","s":"A: Can employees bring a guest to the company's annual dinner at the hotel next month, or is it only for staff? B: Each employee may bring a spouse to the dinner, so if you are married, please write your husband's or wife's name on the form by Friday.","t":"A：員工可以帶一位客人參加下個月在飯店舉行的公司年度晚宴嗎？還是只限員工？ B：每位員工可以帶【配偶】出席晚宴，所以如果你已婚，請在週五前把你先生或太太的名字寫在表格上。"},{"w":"husband","p":"n.","d":"the man that a woman is married to","c":"丈夫","s":"A: Why does Ms. Chen leave the office at exactly five o'clock every day, even when we are very busy? B: Her husband works night shifts at the hospital, so she has to get home before he leaves for work and their two young children are alone.","t":"A：為什麼陳小姐每天都準時五點離開辦公室，即使我們非常忙碌也一樣？ B：她的【先生】在醫院上夜班，所以她必須在他出門上班、留下兩個年幼的孩子獨自在家之前趕回家。"},{"w":"wife","p":"n.","d":"the woman that a man is married to","c":"妻子","s":"A: Is Mr. Huang going to move to the Singapore branch when his promotion begins next spring? B: He is still thinking about it, because his wife has a good job as a nurse here, and she would have to quit if the whole family moved abroad.","t":"A：黃先生明年春天升職後會調到新加坡分公司嗎？ B：他還在考慮，因為他的【太太】在這裡有一份很好的護理師工作，如果全家搬到國外，她就必須辭職。"},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"the person you live with or are in a romantic relationship with","c":"伴侶","s":"A: Do I have to be married to add someone to my company health insurance plan, or are there other options? B: No, the new policy covers a partner who has lived with you for at least one year, so you just need to show a shared rental contract.","t":"A：我一定要結婚才能把某人加入公司的健康保險嗎？還是有其他選擇？ B：不用，新政策涵蓋與你同住至少一年的【伴侶】，所以你只需出示一份共同的租屋契約。"},{"w":"stepfather","p":"n.","d":"the man who is married to your mother but is not your father","c":"繼父","s":"A: Who taught you how to run a small business before you opened this coffee shop across from the train station? B: My mother married again when I was ten, and my stepfather owned a restaurant, so I grew up helping him with orders, staff schedules, and money.","t":"A：在你開這間火車站對面的咖啡店之前，是誰教你如何經營小生意的？ B：我十歲時母親再婚，而我的【繼父】經營一家餐廳，所以我從小就幫他處理訂單、員工排班和帳務。"},{"w":"stepmother","p":"n.","d":"the woman who is married to your father but is not your mother","c":"繼母","s":"A: Your father remarried a few years ago, right, so how do you get along with his new wife these days? B: Very well, actually, because my stepmother is kind and patient, and she even helped me choose the right university and apply for my first job.","t":"A：你父親幾年前再婚了，對吧？那你最近和他的新太太相處得怎麼樣？ B：其實非常好，因為我的【繼母】既親切又有耐心，她甚至幫我選對了大學，還協助我申請第一份工作。"},{"w":"stepson","p":"n.","d":"the son of your husband or wife from an earlier relationship","c":"繼子","s":"A: Is the teenager working at the front desk this summer related to the hotel owner in some way? B: Yes, he is her stepson, because she married his father last year, and the boy wanted some work experience before starting college in the fall.","t":"A：今年夏天在櫃檯工作的那位青少年跟飯店老闆有什麼關係嗎？ B：有，他是她的【繼子】，因為她去年嫁給了他的父親，而那個男孩想在秋天上大學前累積一些工作經驗。"},{"w":"stepdaughter","p":"n.","d":"the daughter of your husband or wife from an earlier relationship","c":"繼女","s":"A: Why did Mr. Wu take a day off in the middle of the week when we have so many orders to ship? B: His stepdaughter, the girl his wife had before they married, was performing in her first piano concert, and he did not want to disappoint her.","t":"A：我們有這麼多訂單要出貨，吳先生為什麼在週間請了一天假？ B：他的【繼女】，也就是他太太婚前所生的女孩，要舉行她的第一場鋼琴演奏會，他不想讓她失望。"},{"w":"in-law","p":"n.","d":"a relative of your husband or wife","c":"姻親","s":"A: Why are you so nervous about the dinner party at your house this Saturday evening? B: My wife's whole family is coming, and it is the first time I will cook for every in-law at once, so I want the food and the house to be perfect.","t":"A：你為什麼對這週六晚上在你家舉辦的晚餐聚會這麼緊張？ B：我太太全家都要來，這是我第一次同時為所有【姻親】下廚，所以我希望食物和家裡都很完美。"},{"w":"father-in-law","p":"n.","d":"the father of your husband or wife","c":"岳父；公公","s":"A: How did you get such useful advice about buying your first apartment in the city? B: My wife's dad worked as a real estate agent for thirty years, so my father-in-law looked at every contract with me and helped me avoid some very expensive mistakes.","t":"A：你買第一間市區公寓時，怎麼得到這麼有用的建議？ B：我太太的爸爸當了三十年房地產仲介，所以我的【岳父】陪我看過每份合約，幫我避免了一些非常昂貴的錯誤。"},{"w":"mother-in-law","p":"n.","d":"the mother of your husband or wife","c":"岳母；婆婆","s":"A: Who looks after your baby now that you have come back to the office after your maternity leave? B: My husband's mother lives just two blocks from us, so my mother-in-law takes care of the baby during the day, and we pick him up after work.","t":"A：你產假結束回到辦公室後，現在是誰在照顧你的寶寶？ B：我先生的母親就住在離我們兩條街的地方，所以白天由我【婆婆】照顧寶寶，我們下班後再去接他。"},{"w":"brother-in-law","p":"n.","d":"the brother of your husband or wife, or your sister's husband","c":"姊夫；妹夫；大伯；小叔；內兄；內弟","s":"A: Who designed the new website for your bakery, because it looks so professional and modern? B: My sister's husband is a web designer, so my brother-in-law built it for us during his free weekends and only asked for a few boxes of cakes in return.","t":"A：誰幫你的麵包店設計新網站的？它看起來好專業又好現代。 B：我姊姊的先生是網頁設計師，所以我的【姊夫】利用空閒的週末幫我們做的，而且只要了幾盒蛋糕作為回報。"},{"w":"sister-in-law","p":"n.","d":"the sister of your husband or wife, or your brother's wife","c":"嫂嫂；弟媳；大姑；小姑；姨子","s":"A: Who is the woman helping your brother serve customers at his noodle shop on weekends? B: That is his wife, my sister-in-law, and she used to work at a big hotel, so she knows how to keep customers happy even when the line is very long.","t":"A：週末在你哥哥麵店幫忙招呼客人的那位女士是誰？ B：那是他太太，也就是我的【嫂嫂】，她以前在大飯店工作，所以即使隊伍排得很長，她也知道怎麼讓客人保持愉快。"},{"w":"guardian","p":"n.","d":"a person who is legally responsible for a child","c":"監護人","s":"A: Can my fifteen-year-old nephew join the summer coding camp at the community center without his parents? B: Yes, but because he is under eighteen, a parent or legal guardian must sign the permission form and give an emergency phone number before the first class.","t":"A：我十五歲的外甥可以在沒有父母陪同的情況下參加社區中心的暑期程式營嗎？ B：可以，但因為他未滿十八歲，必須在第一堂課前由父母或法定【監護人】簽署同意書並提供緊急聯絡電話。"},{"w":"ancestor","p":"n.","d":"a family member who lived a long time ago","c":"祖先","s":"A: Why are you flying to a small village in southern Italy for your vacation instead of going to Rome? B: I found out that my great-great-grandfather was born there, so I want to see the place where my ancestor lived and maybe find some old family records.","t":"A：你度假為什麼要飛去義大利南部的一個小村莊，而不是去羅馬？ B：我發現我的高祖父是在那裡出生的，所以我想看看我【祖先】住過的地方，也許還能找到一些舊的家族紀錄。"},{"w":"descendant","p":"n.","d":"a person who comes from a family member who lived long ago","c":"後代；子孫","s":"A: Why is the owner of this old tea company so famous in town, even though the shop is quite small? B: She is a direct descendant of the man who started the company in 1890, and her family has run the same shop on this street for five generations.","t":"A：這家老茶行的老闆為什麼在鎮上這麼有名，即使店面很小？ B：她是1890年創立這家公司那位男士的直系【後代】，她的家族已經在這條街上經營同一家店五代了。"},{"w":"newlywed","p":"n.","d":"a person who has just married","c":"新婚者","s":"A: Why did the travel agency create a special package with ocean-view rooms and a private dinner on the beach? B: Many couples book trips right after their wedding, so the agency wants every newlywed to choose our island resort for a romantic honeymoon this year.","t":"A：旅行社為什麼推出包含海景房和海灘私人晚餐的特別套裝行程？ B：許多夫妻在婚禮後立刻預訂旅遊，所以旅行社希望今年每位【新婚者】都選擇我們的海島度假村度過浪漫的蜜月。"}]},{"unit":135,"theme":"Famous 有名的","cards":[{"w":"well-known","p":"adj.","d":"known by many people","c":"眾所周知的；有名的","s":"A: Why did our marketing team choose that small bakery on Main Street to provide the snacks for next week's product launch event? B: It is a well-known shop in this neighborhood, and many of our regular customers already love its bread, so serving its food should make guests feel comfortable and welcome.","t":"A：為什麼我們的行銷團隊選擇主街上那家小麵包店，為下週的產品發表活動提供點心？ B：它是這個社區裡一家【眾所周知的】店，我們許多老顧客已經很喜歡它的麵包，所以提供它的食物應該能讓來賓感到自在又受歡迎。"},{"w":"renowned","p":"adj.","d":"famous and admired for a special skill or quality","c":"著名的；享有盛譽的","s":"A: Have you heard who will lead the cooking workshop that the hotel is organizing for its kitchen staff next month? B: Yes, a renowned chef from Paris is coming, and since he has won several international awards, the manager expects every cook to attend and take careful notes.","t":"A：你聽說飯店下個月為廚房員工舉辦的烹飪工作坊將由誰主持嗎？ B：聽說了，一位來自巴黎的【著名的】主廚會來，因為他贏過好幾個國際獎項，經理希望每位廚師都參加並仔細做筆記。"},{"w":"celebrated","p":"adj.","d":"praised and admired by many people","c":"著名的；備受讚揚的","s":"A: Why are so many visitors lining up outside the art gallery downtown even though it is raining heavily this afternoon? B: The gallery is showing paintings by a celebrated local artist for only three days, so people want to see her work before the exhibition closes on Sunday evening.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午雨下得這麼大，市中心的美術館外面還有這麼多遊客在排隊？ B：美術館只展出三天一位【備受讚揚的】本地藝術家的畫作，所以大家想在週日晚上展覽結束前去看她的作品。"},{"w":"notable","p":"adj.","d":"important or interesting enough to be noticed","c":"值得注意的；顯著的","s":"A: Did anything special happen at the annual sales conference in Tokyo, or was it the same as last year's boring meeting? B: There was one notable change, because the company invited customers to share their opinions on stage, and many managers said it was the most useful session of the whole week.","t":"A：在東京舉行的年度業務大會上有發生什麼特別的事嗎？還是跟去年一樣是無聊的會議？ B：有一個【值得注意的】改變，因為公司邀請客戶上台分享意見，許多經理說那是整週最有用的一場。"},{"w":"prominent","p":"adj.","d":"important and well known","c":"重要的；著名的；顯眼的","s":"A: Who is going to cut the ribbon at the opening ceremony of our new factory in the industrial park next Friday morning? B: A prominent business leader from the local chamber of commerce agreed to come, and her presence will help us attract attention from reporters and possible investors.","t":"A：下週五早上我們在工業區新工廠的開幕典禮上，由誰來剪綵？ B：本地商會一位【重要的】企業領袖答應要來，她的出席將幫助我們吸引記者和潛在投資人的注意。"},{"w":"distinguished","p":"adj.","d":"very successful and respected","c":"傑出的；卓越的","s":"A: Why did the university ask our CEO to give the main speech at its graduation ceremony this summer instead of a professor? B: He has had a long and distinguished career in international trade, and the students hope to learn how he built the company from a tiny office into a global business.","t":"A：為什麼大學請我們的執行長在今年夏天的畢業典禮上致主要演說，而不是請一位教授？ B：他在國際貿易領域有一段漫長而【傑出的】職業生涯，學生們希望了解他如何把公司從一間小辦公室發展成全球企業。"},{"w":"legendary","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and talked about for a long time","c":"傳奇的；極其有名的","s":"A: Why is everyone in the sales department so excited about the training session scheduled for tomorrow morning in the large meeting room? B: A legendary salesperson who once sold more cars in one year than anyone else in the country will share his secrets and answer our questions after lunch.","t":"A：為什麼業務部的每個人都對明天早上在大會議室舉行的訓練課程這麼興奮？ B：一位曾在一年內賣出比全國任何人都多汽車的【傳奇的】業務員，會分享他的秘訣，並在午餐後回答我們的問題。"},{"w":"iconic","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and seen as a symbol of something","c":"代表性的；標誌性的","s":"A: Where should we take the overseas clients for photos on Saturday afternoon before their flight back to London leaves in the evening? B: Let's take them to the iconic tower near the river, because it appears on almost every postcard of the city, and visitors always enjoy the amazing view from the top.","t":"A：週六下午在海外客戶晚上飛回倫敦之前，我們應該帶他們去哪裡拍照？ B：帶他們去河邊那座【標誌性的】塔吧，因為它幾乎出現在這座城市的每一張明信片上，而且遊客總是很喜歡從頂樓看到的壯觀景色。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked or enjoyed by many people","c":"受歡迎的；流行的","s":"A: Which item on the new lunch menu should we advertise first on the café's social media account this week? B: The chicken salad has been very popular with office workers since we started selling it on Monday, so let's post a photo of it with a short discount offer for weekday customers.","t":"A：這週我們應該先在咖啡廳的社群帳號上宣傳新午餐菜單中的哪一道？ B：雞肉沙拉從週一開賣以來就很【受歡迎】，深受上班族喜愛，所以我們貼一張它的照片，再加上給平日顧客的短期折扣優惠吧。"},{"w":"influential","p":"adj.","d":"having the power to change what people think or do","c":"有影響力的","s":"A: Why did the publishing company send free copies of our new business book to that blogger who writes about personal finance? B: She is very influential among young professionals, and if she writes a positive review, thousands of readers will probably order the book from online stores within a few days.","t":"A：為什麼出版公司要把我們的新商業書免費寄給那位寫個人理財的部落客？ B：她在年輕上班族之間非常【有影響力】，如果她寫了正面的書評，幾天內可能會有數千名讀者從網路書店訂購這本書。"},{"w":"respected","p":"adj.","d":"admired by others because of good work or character","c":"受尊敬的","s":"A: Why does the board want Ms. Chen to lead the new project team instead of hiring an experienced manager from outside the company? B: She is a respected engineer who has worked here for fifteen years, and her colleagues trust her because she always listens carefully and makes fair decisions.","t":"A：為什麼董事會想讓陳女士領導新的專案團隊，而不是從公司外部聘請一位有經驗的經理？ B：她是一位在這裡工作了十五年、【受尊敬的】工程師，同事們都信任她，因為她總是仔細傾聽並做出公平的決定。"},{"w":"recognized","p":"adj.","d":"accepted or known as good or official","c":"公認的；被認可的","s":"A: Should we hire the cheaper training company, or is it worth paying extra for the one that the human resources director suggested? B: I think we should pay more, because the other company offers a recognized certificate that employers across the country accept, and that will help our staff get promoted later.","t":"A：我們應該聘請比較便宜的培訓公司，還是值得多付錢給人資主管推薦的那一家？ B：我認為應該多付一點，因為那家公司提供全國雇主都接受的【公認的】證書，這會幫助我們的員工以後升職。"},{"w":"acclaimed","p":"adj.","d":"praised publicly by many people, especially critics","c":"廣受好評的","s":"A: Why are tickets for the theater show on Friday night so expensive compared with the other performances in town this month? B: It is a highly acclaimed musical that won several awards in New York last year, so the theater knows many people are willing to pay more to see it.","t":"A：為什麼週五晚上那場戲劇表演的票，跟這個月城裡其他的表演比起來這麼貴？ B：那是一齣去年在紐約贏得好幾個獎項、非常【廣受好評的】音樂劇，所以劇院知道很多人願意多付錢去看。"},{"w":"esteemed","p":"adj.","d":"greatly respected and admired","c":"受敬重的；尊敬的","s":"A: How should I begin the welcome speech for the international guests at tonight's company dinner in the hotel ballroom? B: Start by thanking our esteemed partners from Germany and Japan for traveling so far, and then briefly explain how our cooperation has helped both sides grow over the past ten years.","t":"A：今晚在飯店宴會廳的公司晚宴上，我該如何開始給國際來賓的歡迎致詞？ B：先感謝我們來自德國和日本、【受敬重的】合作夥伴遠道而來，然後簡短說明過去十年來我們的合作如何幫助雙方成長。"},{"w":"eminent","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected in a particular profession","c":"傑出的；著名的（指專業領域）","s":"A: Who will speak at the medical conference that our pharmaceutical company is sponsoring at the convention center next month? B: An eminent doctor who has studied heart disease for thirty years will give the opening talk, and the organizers expect more than five hundred people to attend her session.","t":"A：下個月我們製藥公司在會議中心贊助的醫學研討會上，誰會演講？ B：一位研究心臟疾病三十年的【傑出的】醫生將發表開幕演說，主辦單位預計會有超過五百人參加她的場次。"},{"w":"star","p":"n.","d":"a very famous performer, such as an actor or athlete","c":"明星；巨星","s":"A: Why are there so many reporters and photographers waiting outside the shopping mall entrance this morning? B: A famous movie star is opening a new clothing store on the second floor, and the manager expects a huge crowd, so extra security guards have been hired for the whole weekend.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上購物中心入口外有這麼多記者和攝影師在等候？ B：一位知名電影【明星】要在二樓開一家新的服裝店，經理預期會有大批人潮，所以整個週末都加聘了保全人員。"},{"w":"celebrity","p":"n.","d":"a famous person, especially in entertainment","c":"名人","s":"A: Do you think hiring a famous singer for our new shampoo advertisement is really worth the high cost? B: Yes, because research shows that customers often trust products when a celebrity uses them, and our sales team believes the campaign could double our market share within a year.","t":"A：你認為為我們的新洗髮精廣告請一位知名歌手，真的值得這麼高的費用嗎？ B：值得，因為研究顯示當【名人】使用某產品時，顧客往往會信任它，而且我們的業務團隊相信這次宣傳活動可以在一年內讓市占率翻倍。"},{"w":"figure","p":"n.","d":"an important or well-known person","c":"人物","s":"A: Who was the man giving interviews to the reporters in the hotel lobby after the economic forum ended yesterday? B: He is a leading figure in the electric car industry, and many people believe his company will soon build a large factory in our city, creating thousands of new jobs.","t":"A：昨天經濟論壇結束後，在飯店大廳接受記者採訪的那位男士是誰？ B：他是電動車產業的一位重要【人物】，很多人相信他的公司很快就會在我們的城市蓋一座大型工廠，創造數千個新工作機會。"},{"w":"hero","p":"n.","d":"a person admired for being brave or doing something great","c":"英雄","s":"A: Why did the staff give the security guard a big round of applause at the morning meeting today? B: He became a hero last night when he noticed smoke in the storage room, called the fire department quickly, and helped everyone leave the building safely before the fire spread.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上的會議上員工們給那位保全熱烈的掌聲？ B：他昨晚成了【英雄】，因為他發現儲藏室冒煙，迅速打電話給消防隊，並在火勢蔓延前幫助大家安全離開大樓。"},{"w":"idol","p":"n.","d":"a famous person that many people love and admire","c":"偶像","s":"A: Why is your teenage son so excited about the concert at the stadium next Saturday evening? B: His idol is a young pop singer from Korea, and he has saved his allowance for months to buy a ticket, so he can finally see her perform live with his friends.","t":"A：為什麼你十幾歲的兒子對下週六晚上在體育館舉行的演唱會這麼興奮？ B：他的【偶像】是一位來自韓國的年輕流行歌手，他存了好幾個月的零用錢買票，終於可以和朋友們一起看她的現場表演了。"},{"w":"household name","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person or product that almost everyone knows","c":"家喻戶曉的名字","s":"A: Was the coffee company always this successful, or did it start as a small business like ours? B: It started with one tiny shop twenty years ago, but after years of hard work and clever advertising, it became a household name that almost every family in the country knows today.","t":"A：那家咖啡公司一直都這麼成功嗎？還是也像我們一樣從小生意開始？ B：它二十年前從一家小店開始，但經過多年努力和巧妙的廣告，它成了一個【家喻戶曉的名字】，如今全國幾乎每個家庭都知道。"},{"w":"spotlight","p":"n.","d":"public attention","c":"公眾注意；聚光燈","s":"A: Why did the new manager decline the invitation to appear on the television business program next week? B: She prefers to work quietly and avoid the spotlight, so she asked the company's founder to answer the reporters' questions about the merger instead of doing the interview herself.","t":"A：為什麼新經理拒絕了下週上電視商業節目的邀請？ B：她比較喜歡低調工作、避開【公眾注意】，所以她請公司創辦人代替她回答記者有關合併的問題，而不是自己接受採訪。"},{"w":"publicity","p":"n.","d":"attention given to someone or something by newspapers, TV, and the internet","c":"宣傳；公眾的注意","s":"A: Is the charity run that our company is organizing in the park next month going to help our brand at all? B: Yes, it should bring us a lot of positive publicity, because several local newspapers and radio stations have already promised to report on the event and interview our volunteers.","t":"A：我們公司下個月在公園舉辦的慈善路跑，對我們的品牌會有幫助嗎？ B：會，它應該能帶給我們很多正面的【宣傳】，因為好幾家地方報紙和電台已經答應要報導這個活動並採訪我們的志工。"},{"w":"reputation","p":"n.","d":"the opinion that people have about someone or something","c":"名聲；聲譽","s":"A: Why do you want to choose that printing company even though its prices are a little higher than the others? B: It has an excellent reputation for finishing large orders on time, and last year it printed all our catalogs without a single mistake, so I think it is worth the extra cost.","t":"A：為什麼即使那家印刷公司的價格比別家高一點，你還是想選它？ B：它以準時完成大訂單而享有極好的【聲譽】，去年它印我們所有的型錄都沒有出過任何錯，所以我認為多付的費用很值得。"},{"w":"prestige","p":"n.","d":"respect and admiration because of success or high quality","c":"聲望；威望","s":"A: Why did you decide to accept the job offer from the international bank instead of the local company that offered a higher salary? B: Working for such a large bank brings a lot of prestige, and I believe the experience will open many doors for my career in finance later on.","t":"A：為什麼你決定接受那家國際銀行的工作，而不是薪水比較高的本地公司？ B：在這麼大的銀行工作會帶來很高的【聲望】，而且我相信這段經驗以後會為我在金融業的職涯打開很多扇門。"},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"praise and thanks for someone's work","c":"表揚；認可","s":"A: Why did the director give Mr. Lee a special award at the year-end party in the hotel last night? B: It was in recognition of his hard work on the new customer service system, which reduced complaints by half and saved the company a lot of money this year.","t":"A：為什麼主管在昨晚飯店的尾牙上頒給李先生一個特別獎？ B：那是為了【表揚】他在新客服系統上的努力，那套系統讓客訴減少了一半，今年也為公司省下很多錢。"},{"w":"fame","p":"n.","d":"the state of being known by many people","c":"名聲；名氣","s":"A: How did that small noodle restaurant near the train station suddenly become so busy every night? B: It rose to fame after a popular food blogger posted a video about its spicy beef soup, and now people wait in long lines even on cold and rainy evenings.","t":"A：火車站附近那家小麵館怎麼突然每天晚上都這麼忙？ B：在一位受歡迎的美食部落客貼出它的辣牛肉湯影片之後，它就打響了【名氣】，現在連寒冷下雨的晚上大家都要排長長的隊。"},{"w":"stardom","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a very famous performer","c":"明星地位；星運","s":"A: Did the young actress in our coffee commercial become famous right after the advertisement appeared on television? B: Not immediately, but her road to stardom began with that commercial, because a film director saw it, invited her to an audition, and later gave her the main role in a successful movie.","t":"A：我們咖啡廣告裡的那位年輕女演員，是在廣告上電視之後就馬上出名了嗎？ B：沒有馬上，但她通往【明星地位】之路是從那支廣告開始的，因為一位電影導演看到了它，邀請她去試鏡，後來讓她在一部賣座電影中擔任主角。"},{"w":"notoriety","p":"n.","d":"the state of being famous for something bad","c":"惡名；臭名","s":"A: Why did the hotel change its name and repaint the whole building last spring? B: It gained notoriety after several guests posted angry reviews online about dirty rooms and rude staff, so the new owners wanted a fresh start and a completely different image for travelers.","t":"A：為什麼那家飯店去年春天改名並重新粉刷整棟建築？ B：在幾位客人上網發表關於房間骯髒和員工無禮的憤怒評論後，它就有了【惡名】，所以新老闆想要重新開始，給旅客一個完全不同的形象。"},{"w":"viral","p":"adj.","d":"spreading quickly to many people on the internet","c":"（網路上）爆紅的；迅速傳播的","s":"A: How did the small toy company receive so many online orders over the weekend without spending money on advertising? B: A funny video of a cat playing with one of its toys went viral, and within two days millions of people watched it and shared it with their friends.","t":"A：那家小玩具公司怎麼能在週末沒花錢打廣告就收到這麼多網路訂單？ B：一支貓咪玩它家玩具的有趣影片在網路上【爆紅】，兩天之內就有數百萬人觀看並分享給朋友。"},{"w":"globally","p":"adv.","d":"in or around the whole world","c":"全球地；在全世界","s":"A: Why is the company hiring so many translators and customer service staff who can speak different languages this year? B: The management plans to sell our phones globally instead of only in Asia, so we need people who can support customers in Europe, Africa, and South America.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年要聘請這麼多會說不同語言的翻譯和客服人員？ B：管理階層計畫將我們的手機銷售到【全球】，而不只在亞洲，所以我們需要能支援歐洲、非洲和南美洲客戶的人員。"},{"w":"widely","p":"adv.","d":"by many people or in many places","c":"廣泛地","s":"A: Why don't we use the new accounting software that the sales representative showed us at the trade fair? B: It is not widely used yet, and our accountants say it might be difficult to find training courses or technical support if something goes wrong during the busy tax season.","t":"A：為什麼我們不用那位業務代表在商展上展示給我們看的新會計軟體？ B：它還沒有被【廣泛地】使用，而我們的會計師說，如果在忙碌的報稅季出問題，可能很難找到訓練課程或技術支援。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is open for everyone to see or hear","c":"公開地","s":"A: Has the company told the employees about the plan to move the main office to another city next year? B: Not yet, because the president wants to announce it publicly at the press conference on Monday, and he asked the managers to keep the information secret until then.","t":"A：公司已經告訴員工明年要把總部搬到另一個城市的計畫了嗎？ B：還沒，因為總裁想在週一的記者會上【公開地】宣布，他要求經理們在那之前對這個消息保密。"},{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to respect and like someone or something very much","c":"欽佩；讚賞","s":"A: Why do you always ask Mrs. Wang for advice when you have problems with difficult customers at the store? B: I really admire the way she stays calm and polite even when people shout at her, and I hope I can handle complaints as well as she does someday.","t":"A：為什麼你在店裡遇到難搞的顧客時，總是向王太太請教？ B：我真的很【欽佩】她即使在別人對她大吼時也能保持冷靜和禮貌，我希望有一天也能像她一樣處理客訴。"},{"w":"honor","p":"v.","d":"to show public respect for someone","c":"表揚；向……致敬","s":"A: What is the purpose of the special dinner that the company is holding at the restaurant on Friday evening? B: We want to honor three employees who have worked here for more than thirty years, so the president will give each of them a gold watch and a short speech.","t":"A：公司週五晚上在餐廳舉辦的特別晚宴目的是什麼？ B：我們想【表揚】三位在這裡工作超過三十年的員工，所以總裁會送給他們每人一支金錶並發表簡短演說。"}]},{"unit":136,"theme":"Farewell Letter 告別信","cards":[{"w":"goodbye","p":"n.","d":"words or actions when someone leaves","c":"再見；告別","s":"A: Is everyone in the accounting department planning to stop by the lounge at four o'clock this afternoon, since Linda is moving to our Tokyo office next week? B: Yes, we bought a cake and a card that all of us signed, because we want to say a proper goodbye to her before she flies to Japan on Monday.","t":"A：會計部的每個人都打算今天下午四點到休息室去嗎？因為琳達下週就要調到我們的東京辦公室了。 B：是的，我們買了蛋糕和一張大家都簽了名的卡片，因為我們想在她星期一飛往日本之前，好好地跟她【道別】。"},{"w":"departure","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a job or a place","c":"離開；離職","s":"A: Why did the director send an email to all of the staff this morning, and why does everyone in the sales department look so surprised? B: She announced the departure of our marketing manager, who has accepted a position at a bank in Singapore, and she said his last day here will be the end of this month.","t":"A：主管今天早上為什麼寄電子郵件給全體員工？為什麼業務部的每個人看起來都那麼驚訝？ B：她宣布了我們行銷經理的【離職】，他已經接受了新加坡一家銀行的職位，她說他在這裡的最後一天是這個月底。"},{"w":"leave","p":"v.","d":"to stop working at a company or go away from a place","c":"離開；辭去","s":"A: Have you heard why Tom has been cleaning out his desk and packing all of his files into boxes since early this morning? B: He decided to leave the company after twelve years because he wants to start his own small coffee shop near the train station with his wife and brother.","t":"A：你知道湯姆為什麼從今天一大早就開始清理他的桌子，把所有的檔案都裝進箱子裡嗎？ B：他在公司工作十二年之後，決定【離開】公司，因為他想和太太及弟弟在火車站附近開一家自己的小咖啡店。"},{"w":"resign","p":"v.","d":"to officially say that you are leaving your job","c":"辭職","s":"A: Why is the human resources manager meeting with the head of the design department behind closed doors, and why does she look so serious? B: He told her that he plans to resign next month, because his family is moving to Canada and he needs time to find a home and a school for his children.","t":"A：人資經理為什麼關起門來和設計部門的主管開會？她為什麼看起來那麼嚴肅？ B：他告訴她，他打算下個月【辭職】，因為他們全家要搬去加拿大，他需要時間找房子，也要幫孩子找學校。"},{"w":"retirement","p":"n.","d":"the time when you stop working, usually because of age","c":"退休","s":"A: What should we buy for Helen, who has worked at the front desk for almost thirty years and knows nearly every regular customer by name? B: Since she loves gardening, we are giving her a set of tools and some flower seeds at her retirement party, which will be held in the hotel restaurant on Friday evening.","t":"A：我們該買什麼給海倫？她在櫃檯工作了將近三十年，幾乎叫得出每位老顧客的名字。 B：因為她很喜歡園藝，我們要在她的【退休】派對上送她一組園藝工具和一些花的種子，派對星期五晚上在飯店餐廳舉行。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to feel thankful for something","c":"感激；感謝","s":"A: Did you read the card that the new interns left on your desk before they finished their summer program and went back to university? B: Yes, they wrote that they really appreciate all the time I spent showing them how to use the database and answering their questions, even when I was busy with my own reports.","t":"A：你看了那些新實習生在結束暑期計畫、回大學之前留在你桌上的卡片嗎？ B：看了，他們寫說非常【感謝】我花了那麼多時間教他們使用資料庫、回答他們的問題，即使在我忙著寫自己的報告時也一樣。"},{"w":"gratitude","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being thankful","c":"感激；感謝之情","s":"A: What did the factory manager say in his speech at the farewell lunch, since I had to go early to meet a supplier? B: He expressed his deep gratitude to the workers who stayed late during the busy season last winter, and he said the company could not have finished the big order without their hard work.","t":"A：廠長在歡送午宴上的致詞說了什麼？因為我得提早離開去見一位供應商。 B：他向去年冬天旺季時留下來加班的工人表達了深深的【感激】，他說如果沒有他們的努力，公司不可能完成那筆大訂單。"},{"w":"thankful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling glad and grateful","c":"感謝的；感激的","s":"A: How do you feel now that your final day at the hospital is almost here and you are moving to a new job at a clinic closer to home? B: I am very thankful for the patient nurses who trained me when I first arrived, because they taught me how to stay calm and kind even during the busiest night shifts.","t":"A：既然你在醫院的最後一天快到了，而且要到離家比較近的診所上班，你現在感覺如何？ B：我非常【感謝】當初我剛來時訓練我的那些有耐心的護理師，因為她們教會我即使在最忙的夜班也要保持冷靜和親切。"},{"w":"memories","p":"n.","d":"things you remember from the past","c":"回憶","s":"A: What did you write in the farewell card for Daniel, who is moving from our hotel to manage a new resort in Thailand next month? B: I wrote that I have many happy memories of working with him at the front desk, especially the night when we helped fifty tired guests after their tour bus broke down in the rain.","t":"A：丹尼爾下個月要離開我們飯店，去管理泰國的一間新度假村，你在給他的歡送卡上寫了什麼？ B：我寫說和他一起在櫃檯工作留下了許多快樂的【回憶】，特別是那天晚上旅行團的遊覽車在雨中拋錨後，我們一起幫助了五十位疲累的客人。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or skill you get from doing something","c":"經驗","s":"A: Why did you decide to stay at this small advertising agency for five years instead of joining a bigger company with a higher salary? B: I gained so much valuable experience here, because the managers let me work directly with important clients and lead several projects even when I was still quite young.","t":"A：你為什麼決定在這家小型廣告公司待五年，而不是去薪水較高的大公司？ B：我在這裡得到了非常寶貴的【經驗】，因為即使我當時還很年輕，主管們就讓我直接和重要客戶合作，還讓我主導好幾個專案。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something good","c":"機會","s":"A: What is the most important thing you want to say in your goodbye email to the whole department before you move to the London branch? B: I want to thank our manager for giving me the opportunity to travel to trade shows in Europe, because those trips helped me improve my English and meet many useful business contacts.","t":"A：在你調到倫敦分公司之前，你想在寄給全部門的告別郵件裡說的最重要的事是什麼？ B：我想感謝我們經理給了我去歐洲參加商展的【機會】，因為那些出差幫助我提升英文，也認識了很多有用的商業人脈。"},{"w":"support","p":"n.","d":"help and kindness that someone gives you","c":"支持；幫助","s":"A: How did you manage to finish your night classes in accounting while working full-time in the busy shipping department last year? B: I could not have done it without the support of my coworkers, who often covered my evening shifts and lent me their notes when I was too tired to study after work.","t":"A：去年你一邊在忙碌的出貨部門全職工作，一邊是怎麼完成會計夜間課程的？ B：如果沒有同事們的【支持】，我不可能做到，他們常常幫我代晚班，在我下班後累得沒辦法讀書時還借我筆記。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give someone confidence","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: Were you nervous when you gave your first presentation to the board of directors three years ago, right after you joined the company? B: I was very nervous, but my supervisor's encouragement helped me a lot, because she practiced with me the night before and told me that my ideas were clear and useful.","t":"A：你三年前剛進公司，第一次向董事會做簡報時會緊張嗎？ B：我非常緊張，但我主管的【鼓勵】幫了我很大的忙，因為她前一晚陪我練習，還告訴我我的想法既清楚又實用。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about what to do","c":"指導；指引","s":"A: Why are you sending flowers and a long thank-you letter to your former mentor in the finance department before you move to the new office? B: Her patient guidance during my first year helped me understand the budget system, and without her advice I would never have been promoted to team leader so quickly.","t":"A：你為什麼在搬到新辦公室之前，送花和一封長長的感謝信給你在財務部的前導師？ B：她在我第一年時耐心的【指導】幫助我了解預算系統，如果沒有她的建議，我絕不可能這麼快就升為組長。"},{"w":"leadership","p":"n.","d":"the way someone leads and manages a group","c":"領導（能力）","s":"A: Why are so many employees coming to the farewell dinner for the general manager, even the workers from the warehouse across town? B: Because his strong leadership helped the company survive a very difficult year, and he always listened to every worker's ideas, no matter which department they came from.","t":"A：為什麼有那麼多員工來參加總經理的歡送晚宴，連城市另一頭倉庫的工人都來了？ B：因為他強而有力的【領導】幫助公司度過非常艱難的一年，而且不管員工來自哪個部門，他總是聆聽每個人的想法。"},{"w":"colleague","p":"n.","d":"a person you work with","c":"同事","s":"A: Who is that woman giving a speech near the window, and why is everyone in the meeting room clapping so loudly for her? B: She is a colleague of mine from the research department who is retiring today, and she is thanking all of us for working with her on so many projects over the past twenty years.","t":"A：在窗邊致詞的那位女士是誰？為什麼會議室裡的每個人都為她那麼熱烈地鼓掌？ B：她是我研究部門的【同事】，今天要退休了，她正在感謝我們所有人在過去二十年裡和她一起合作了那麼多專案。"},{"w":"team","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together","c":"團隊","s":"A: What are you going to miss most about this company when you start your new job at the airline in Hong Kong next week? B: I will miss my team the most, because the five of us have worked so closely together on the customer service project that we feel more like a family than coworkers.","t":"A：你下週要去香港的航空公司開始新工作了，你最會想念這家公司的什麼？ B：我最會想念我的【團隊】，因為我們五個人在客服專案上合作得非常密切，感覺比較像一家人，而不只是同事。"},{"w":"miss","p":"v.","d":"to feel sad because someone is not with you any more","c":"想念","s":"A: How does everyone in the office feel now that Susan has gone to her new job at the bank, since she sat at the front desk for so long? B: We really miss her cheerful voice in the morning, because she always greeted every visitor with a big smile and remembered the names of all our regular clients.","t":"A：既然蘇珊已經去銀行上新工作了，辦公室裡的大家感覺如何？畢竟她在櫃檯坐了那麼久。 B：我們真的很【想念】她早上開朗的聲音，因為她總是帶著大大的笑容迎接每位訪客，還記得所有老客戶的名字。"},{"w":"cherish","p":"v.","d":"to love and value something very much","c":"珍惜；珍愛","s":"A: Why do you keep that old photo of the sales department on your desk, even though most of those people work for other companies now? B: I will always cherish the years we spent together building this business from a tiny office, because those coworkers taught me how to work hard and never give up.","t":"A：你為什麼還把那張業務部的舊照片放在桌上？那些人現在大多在別的公司工作了。 B：我會永遠【珍惜】我們從一間小辦公室開始一起打拚這份事業的那些年，因為那些同事教會了我如何努力工作、永不放棄。"},{"w":"remember","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in your mind","c":"記得","s":"A: What do you want the new staff to learn from your farewell speech before you go, after fifteen years as head chef of this restaurant? B: I want them to remember that good service starts in the kitchen, so every dish should be prepared carefully and served on time, even when the dining room is completely full.","t":"A：你擔任這家餐廳主廚十五年後要離開了，你希望新員工從你的告別致詞中學到什麼？ B：我希望他們【記得】好的服務是從廚房開始的，所以即使用餐區完全客滿，每道菜都應該用心準備並準時上菜。"},{"w":"wish","p":"v.","d":"to say that you hope something good happens to someone","c":"祝福；祝願","s":"A: What did the manager write on the cake that the staff ordered for Kevin, who is moving to Australia to study for a master's degree? B: She wrote a short message to wish him good luck with his studies, and she also asked him to send us photos from Sydney when he settles into his new apartment.","t":"A：員工們為凱文訂的蛋糕上，經理寫了什麼？他要去澳洲攻讀碩士學位。 B：她寫了一段簡短的話【祝】他學業順利，還請他在雪梨的新公寓安頓好之後寄照片給我們。"},{"w":"career","p":"n.","d":"the series of jobs a person has in their working life","c":"職業生涯","s":"A: Why did the company invite reporters from the local newspaper to the chief engineer's farewell party at the hotel last night? B: Because she had a long and successful career of almost forty years, during which she designed several famous bridges and trained many young engineers who now work all over the country.","t":"A：公司為什麼邀請地方報紙的記者參加昨晚在飯店舉行的總工程師歡送會？ B：因為她擁有將近四十年漫長而成功的【職業生涯】，期間設計了好幾座著名的橋梁，也培訓了許多現在在全國各地工作的年輕工程師。"},{"w":"achievement","p":"n.","d":"something good that you succeed in doing","c":"成就","s":"A: What will the CEO talk about when she presents the award to the retiring sales director at the annual dinner on Saturday? B: She will talk about his greatest achievement, which was opening five new branches in Southeast Asia, and she will thank him for bringing in so many loyal customers over the years.","t":"A：執行長星期六在年度晚宴上頒獎給即將退休的業務總監時會談些什麼？ B：她會談到他最大的【成就】，也就是在東南亞開設了五家新分公司，她也會感謝他這些年來帶來了那麼多忠實的客戶。"},{"w":"contribution","p":"n.","d":"something you give or do to help a group succeed","c":"貢獻","s":"A: Why is the company naming the new training room after Grace, who is retiring from the IT department this Friday after twenty-five years? B: The board wants to honor her important contribution to the company, since she built our first computer network and trained hundreds of employees to use the new software.","t":"A：公司為什麼要用葛瑞絲的名字來命名新的訓練室？她在資訊部工作二十五年後，這個星期五就要退休了。 B：董事會想表揚她對公司的重要【貢獻】，因為她建立了我們第一套電腦網路，還訓練了數百名員工使用新軟體。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something good","c":"激勵；啟發","s":"A: Why did so many young employees cry during the farewell speech that the head of customer service gave in the cafeteria this afternoon? B: She has always tried to inspire new workers to keep learning, and many of them decided to take night classes and apply for higher positions because of her advice.","t":"A：今天下午客服主管在員工餐廳發表告別演說時，為什麼那麼多年輕員工都哭了？ B：她一直努力【激勵】新進員工持續學習，許多人因為她的建議而決定去上夜間課程，並申請更高的職位。"},{"w":"friendship","p":"n.","d":"a relationship between friends","c":"友誼","s":"A: Are you going to stay in touch with Mark after he moves back to Germany, since you two have shared an office for so many years? B: Of course, our friendship is much more than a work relationship, so we already plan to video chat every month and visit each other during our summer vacations.","t":"A：既然你和馬克共用一間辦公室這麼多年，他搬回德國之後你還會和他保持聯絡嗎？ B：當然，我們的【友誼】遠不只是工作上的關係，所以我們已經計畫每個月視訊聊天，並在暑假時互相拜訪。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable for a special event","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Why has the manager booked the whole second floor of the Italian restaurant next Friday, and should I bring anything to the event? B: We are going to celebrate Jenny's thirty years of service before she retires, so you only need to bring a short message for the memory book that we are making for her.","t":"A：經理為什麼包下了下週五那間義大利餐廳的整個二樓？我需要帶什麼東西去嗎？ B：我們要在珍妮退休前【慶祝】她三十年的服務，所以你只需要帶一段簡短的留言，放進我們為她製作的紀念冊裡。"},{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to respect and like someone for what they do","c":"欽佩；欣賞","s":"A: Why did you ask the retiring factory director to write a few words in your notebook at the farewell party last night? B: I really admire the way he treated every worker fairly and calmly, even during difficult times, and I want to keep his advice with me when I become a manager someday.","t":"A：昨晚在歡送會上，你為什麼請即將退休的廠長在你的筆記本上寫幾句話？ B：我真的很【欽佩】他即使在困難時期，仍公平又冷靜地對待每位工人的作風，我希望將來有一天當上經理時，能把他的建議帶在身邊。"},{"w":"respect","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that someone is good and important","c":"尊敬；尊重","s":"A: Why did all the drivers at the delivery company stand up and clap when the old operations manager walked into the meeting on his last day? B: He earned the respect of every driver by working long hours beside them, fixing problems quickly, and always being honest about the company's plans and difficulties.","t":"A：老營運經理在最後一天走進會議時，為什麼送貨公司的所有司機都站起來鼓掌？ B：他贏得了每位司機的【尊敬】，因為他和他們一起長時間工作、迅速解決問題，而且對公司的計畫和困難總是很坦誠。"},{"w":"kindness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being friendly, helpful, and caring","c":"仁慈；善意","s":"A: Why are you writing such a long thank-you note to the office manager before you finish your contract and go back to Brazil next week? B: When I first arrived in this city, she showed me great kindness by helping me find an apartment and inviting me to her family dinners during the holidays.","t":"A：你下週合約結束要回巴西了，為什麼要寫一張這麼長的感謝卡給辦公室經理？ B：我剛到這個城市時，她對我展現了極大的【善意】，幫我找公寓，還在假日邀請我去參加她的家庭聚餐。"},{"w":"generous","p":"adj.","d":"happy to give money, time, or help to others","c":"慷慨的；大方的","s":"A: Did the company give anything special to the staff who worked at the old factory before it closed down and moved to another city? B: Yes, the owner was very generous, because he gave every worker an extra month's salary and wrote personal letters to help them find new jobs nearby.","t":"A：舊工廠關閉並遷到別的城市之前，公司有給在那裡工作的員工什麼特別的東西嗎？ B：有，老闆非常【慷慨】，他給每位工人多發一個月的薪水，還親自寫推薦信幫他們在附近找新工作。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"working very hard because you care a lot about something","c":"盡心盡力的；專注的","s":"A: Why is the hospital holding a special ceremony for Nurse Lin, who is retiring after more than thirty years in the children's ward? B: She was a truly dedicated nurse who often stayed after her shift to comfort sick children and their worried parents, so the doctors wanted to thank her in front of everyone.","t":"A：林護理師在兒童病房服務三十多年後即將退休，醫院為什麼要為她舉辦特別的典禮？ B：她是一位非常【盡心盡力】的護理師，常常在下班後留下來安慰生病的孩子和憂心的父母，所以醫生們想在大家面前感謝她。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"showing the skills and good behavior expected at work","c":"專業的","s":"A: What did the client from Japan say about Amy when he heard that she was moving from our travel agency to an airline? B: He said she was always very professional, because she answered his emails quickly, planned every business trip carefully, and stayed calm even when flights were cancelled at the last minute.","t":"A：那位日本客戶聽說艾咪要從我們旅行社轉到航空公司工作時，他對她說了什麼？ B：他說她一直都非常【專業】，因為她總是很快回覆他的郵件、仔細規劃每趟商務旅行，即使班機在最後一刻被取消也能保持冷靜。"},{"w":"unforgettable","p":"adj.","d":"so good or special that you cannot forget it","c":"難忘的","s":"A: How was the farewell trip that the department organized for the retiring engineers at the mountain resort last weekend? B: It was unforgettable, because we watched the sunrise together, shared funny stories from the past twenty years, and gave each of them a photo album filled with pictures from old company events.","t":"A：上週末部門在山區度假村為即將退休的工程師們舉辦的歡送旅行怎麼樣？ B：真是【難忘】，因為我們一起看日出、分享過去二十年的趣事，還送給他們每人一本裝滿以前公司活動照片的相簿。"},{"w":"all the best","p":"phr.","d":"a friendly way to wish someone success and happiness","c":"祝一切順利","s":"A: How should I finish my goodbye card to Peter, who is leaving our law firm to open his own small office in his hometown next month? B: You could thank him for helping you with your first cases and then write \"all the best with your new business,\" because that sounds warm, friendly, and suitable for a coworker.","t":"A：彼得下個月要離開我們的律師事務所，回家鄉開自己的小事務所，我該怎麼結束給他的告別卡？ B：你可以先謝謝他幫你處理最初的幾個案子，然後寫「祝你的新事業【一切順利】」，因為那聽起來溫暖友善，也很適合寫給同事。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"in an honest and true way","c":"真誠地；誠摯地","s":"A: How did the department head end the formal letter she sent to the staff when she announced that she was retiring at the end of the year? B: She wrote that she sincerely hoped everyone would continue to work together closely, and she thanked each person for making her twenty years at the company so meaningful.","t":"A：部門主管宣布年底退休時，寄給員工的正式信件是怎麼結尾的？ B：她寫說她【真誠地】希望大家能繼續緊密合作，並感謝每個人讓她在公司的二十年如此有意義。"}]},{"unit":137,"theme":"Farming 農耕","cards":[{"w":"orchard","p":"n.","d":"an area of land where fruit trees are grown","c":"果園","s":"A: Where are we taking the new interns for the team-building trip on Saturday, and do they need to bring anything special with them? B: We're visiting a family-owned apple orchard outside the city, so they should wear comfortable shoes, bring a hat, and be ready to pick fruit for most of the afternoon.","t":"A：星期六的團隊建立活動我們要帶新來的實習生去哪裡？他們需要帶什麼特別的東西嗎？ B：我們要去市郊一座家族經營的蘋果【果園】，所以他們應該穿舒適的鞋子、帶頂帽子，並準備好整個下午大部分時間都要採水果。"},{"w":"vineyard","p":"n.","d":"a farm where grapes are grown, usually to make wine","c":"葡萄園","s":"A: Why did the restaurant manager change the wine list again this month, and are the customers happy with the new choices so far? B: She signed a contract with a small vineyard in the hills nearby, so the wines are cheaper and fresher, and most guests say they really enjoy trying local flavors.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳經理這個月又更換了酒單？到目前為止顧客對新的選擇滿意嗎？ B：她和附近山上一座小型【葡萄園】簽了合約，所以酒更便宜也更新鮮，大部分客人都說他們很喜歡品嚐在地的風味。"},{"w":"refreshing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel cool, rested, or full of energy again","c":"令人提神的；清爽的","s":"A: How was the company picnic at the farm last weekend, and did anyone complain about the hot weather or the long bus ride there? B: It was hot, but the farmer served cold fruit juice straight from the field, which was really refreshing, so everyone felt relaxed and happy during the whole afternoon.","t":"A：上週末在農場舉辦的公司野餐怎麼樣？有人抱怨天氣太熱或到那裡的巴士車程太長嗎？ B：天氣是很熱，但農夫端出了用田裡現採水果做的冰果汁，真的很【清爽提神】，所以大家整個下午都覺得很放鬆、很開心。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"special or enjoyable enough to be remembered for a long time","c":"難忘的；值得紀念的","s":"A: What did the visitors from our Japanese partner company think about the farm tour you organized for them on Friday afternoon? B: They said it was the most memorable part of their business trip, because they planted rice with local farmers and took lots of photos to show their colleagues back home.","t":"A：日本合作公司的訪客覺得你星期五下午幫他們安排的農場參訪怎麼樣？ B：他們說那是這趟出差最【難忘】的部分，因為他們和當地農夫一起插秧，還拍了很多照片要給國內的同事看。"},{"w":"hay","p":"n.","d":"grass that has been cut and dried to feed animals","c":"乾草","s":"A: Why is the delivery truck from the farm supply store parked behind the barn, and when will the driver finish unloading everything? B: He is unloading a large order of hay for the horses and cows, so it will take about an hour, but he promised to move the truck before the visitors arrive.","t":"A：農業用品店的送貨卡車為什麼停在穀倉後面？司機什麼時候會卸完所有東西？ B：他正在卸一大批給馬和牛吃的【乾草】，所以大約要花一個小時，不過他保證會在訪客抵達前把卡車移走。"},{"w":"poultry","p":"n.","d":"birds such as chickens and ducks kept for meat or eggs","c":"家禽","s":"A: Has the supermarket chain decided which local farm will supply its chicken and duck products starting next quarter? B: Yes, the purchasing manager chose a poultry farm in the south because its prices are fair, its birds are raised outdoors, and it can deliver fresh products to every store twice a week.","t":"A：連鎖超市決定好下一季開始要由哪一家在地農場供應雞肉和鴨肉產品了嗎？ B：決定了，採購經理選了南部一家【家禽】養殖場，因為它價格公道、禽鳥在戶外飼養，而且每週能送兩次新鮮產品到每家分店。"},{"w":"bear","p":"v.","d":"to produce fruit or crops; to accept something difficult","c":"結（果實）；忍受","s":"A: Why did the farm manager order so many new trees for the north field when the old ones still look healthy? B: The old trees are too old to bear much fruit anymore, so he wants to replace them now, and the young trees should start producing apples in about three years.","t":"A：北邊田地的老樹看起來還很健康，為什麼農場經理要訂那麼多新樹苗？ B：那些老樹已經太老，【結】不了多少果實了，所以他想現在就換掉，而新樹大約三年後就會開始長出蘋果。"},{"w":"puke","p":"v.","d":"(informal) to bring food up from your stomach through your mouth; to vomit","c":"嘔吐（口語）","s":"A: Why did Tom leave the farm tour so early yesterday afternoon, and is he feeling better now? B: The bus ride on the mountain road was so bumpy that he felt sick and almost had to puke, so his manager drove him back to the hotel to rest, and he feels fine this morning.","t":"A：湯姆昨天下午為什麼那麼早就離開農場參訪？他現在感覺好一點了嗎？ B：山路上的巴士車程太顛簸，他覺得很不舒服，差點就要【吐】了，所以他的經理開車送他回飯店休息，他今天早上已經沒事了。"},{"w":"unbearable","p":"adj.","d":"too bad, painful, or unpleasant to accept","c":"無法忍受的","s":"A: Why did the farm workers start their shifts at five in the morning this week instead of at eight like usual? B: The afternoon heat has been almost unbearable lately, so the supervisor changed the schedule, and now the workers finish picking the vegetables before the hottest part of the day begins.","t":"A：為什麼農場工人這週早上五點就開始上班，而不是像平常一樣八點？ B：最近下午的高溫幾乎讓人【無法忍受】，所以主管調整了班表，現在工人們會在一天最熱的時段開始前就採收完蔬菜。"},{"w":"crucial","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important","c":"極重要的；關鍵的","s":"A: Why does the farm owner check the weather report so carefully every morning before he plans the day's work? B: Rain at the wrong time can destroy the whole crop, so the weather is crucial for his business, and he needs to know when to plant, water, and harvest the vegetables.","t":"A：為什麼農場主人每天早上安排工作前都要那麼仔細地查看天氣預報？ B：在錯誤的時間下雨可能會毀掉整片作物，所以天氣對他的生意【至關重要】，他需要知道什麼時候該播種、澆水和採收蔬菜。"},{"w":"despise","p":"v.","d":"to dislike someone or something very much","c":"鄙視；厭惡","s":"A: Why did Mark decide to leave his office job in the city and move to his parents' farm in the countryside? B: He told me he had come to despise long meetings and crowded trains, so he chose to work outdoors with his family, even though the pay is lower and the hours are much longer.","t":"A：馬克為什麼決定辭掉城市裡的辦公室工作，搬到鄉下他父母的農場？ B：他跟我說他已經變得非常【厭惡】冗長的會議和擁擠的電車，所以選擇和家人一起在戶外工作，即使薪水比較低、工時也長得多。"},{"w":"backbreaking","p":"adj.","d":"(of work) very hard and tiring for the body","c":"極累人的；繁重的","s":"A: Why is the farm hiring so many extra workers this month, and how long will the new staff stay on the job? B: Picking strawberries by hand is backbreaking work that takes many hours each day, so the owner needs more people until the harvest ends, which should be in about six weeks.","t":"A：農場這個月為什麼要多雇那麼多工人？新員工會做多久？ B：用手採草莓是每天要花好幾個小時的【繁重累人】工作，所以農場主人在採收結束前需要更多人手，大約還要六個星期。"},{"w":"enjoyable","p":"adj.","d":"giving pleasure; fun","c":"令人愉快的；有趣的","s":"A: Should we book the farm-stay package for our department's weekend trip, or would a hotel near the beach be a better choice? B: I think the farm would be more enjoyable, because the staff can feed the animals, cook with fresh vegetables, and relax together away from the noise and stress of the office.","t":"A：我們部門的週末旅遊應該訂農場住宿方案，還是住海邊附近的飯店比較好？ B：我覺得農場會更【有趣愉快】，因為員工可以餵動物、用新鮮蔬菜煮飯，還能遠離辦公室的噪音和壓力，一起放鬆。"},{"w":"regional","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a particular area of a country","c":"地區的；區域性的","s":"A: Why is the grocery store putting signs that say \"local\" on so many of the fruit and vegetable boxes this month? B: The company started a program to support regional farmers, so now most of the produce comes from farms within one hundred kilometers, and customers seem to like buying fresh local food.","t":"A：雜貨店這個月為什麼在那麼多蔬果箱上貼「在地」的標示？ B：公司推出了一個支持【地區】農民的計畫，所以現在大部分農產品都來自一百公里內的農場，而顧客似乎很喜歡買新鮮的在地食物。"},{"w":"farmland","p":"n.","d":"land that is used for farming","c":"農田；耕地","s":"A: Why are so many people in the town upset about the new shopping mall that the city council approved last week? B: The developers plan to build it on good farmland that has grown rice for generations, so local farmers are worried about losing their jobs and the town's traditional way of life.","t":"A：為什麼鎮上這麼多人對市議會上週通過的新購物中心感到不滿？ B：開發商打算把它蓋在世世代代種稻的良好【農地】上，所以當地農民擔心會失去工作，也擔心小鎮傳統的生活方式消失。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to continue for a long time without harming the environment","c":"永續的；可持續的","s":"A: Why did the food company decide to pay more for the vegetables it buys from farms in the eastern region? B: Those farms use sustainable methods that protect the soil and save water, and the company believes customers will pay a little more for products that are better for the environment.","t":"A：為什麼食品公司決定用更高的價格向東部地區的農場購買蔬菜？ B：那些農場採用保護土壤又節水的【永續】耕作方法，公司相信顧客會願意為對環境更好的產品多付一點錢。"},{"w":"restore","p":"v.","d":"to bring something back to its earlier good condition","c":"恢復；修復","s":"A: What is the government planning to do with the old farm fields that were damaged by the flood last summer? B: It will give farmers money and advice to help restore the soil, so the land can grow healthy crops again, and officials hope most fields will be ready by next spring.","t":"A：政府打算如何處理去年夏天被洪水破壞的舊農田？ B：政府會提供農民資金和建議，幫助他們【恢復】土壤，讓土地能再次種出健康的作物，官員希望大部分田地能在明年春天前準備好。"},{"w":"spray","p":"v.","d":"to cover something with small drops of liquid","c":"噴灑","s":"A: Why are the workers wearing masks and gloves in the apple field this morning, and is it safe for the visitors to walk there? B: They need to spray the trees with a natural liquid that keeps insects away, so please ask the visitors to wait in the shop until the workers have finished, which should take an hour.","t":"A：今天早上工人們為什麼在蘋果園裡戴著口罩和手套？訪客在那裡走動安全嗎？ B：他們要用一種能驅蟲的天然液體【噴灑】果樹，所以請讓訪客先在商店裡等到工人完成，大約需要一個小時。"},{"w":"steady","p":"adj.","d":"developing or happening at a regular, even rate","c":"穩定的；平穩的","s":"A: How are sales of the farm's organic eggs doing this year, and does the owner plan to raise more chickens soon? B: Sales have shown steady growth every month since January, so she is building a larger chicken house, and she expects to double production by the end of next year.","t":"A：農場的有機雞蛋今年銷售得怎麼樣？老闆打算很快多養一些雞嗎？ B：從一月起每個月的銷售都呈現【穩定】成長，所以她正在蓋一座更大的雞舍，預計明年底前產量會加倍。"},{"w":"hardworking","p":"adj.","d":"putting a lot of effort into work","c":"勤奮的；努力工作的","s":"A: Why did the farm owner give every worker a bonus at the end of the harvest season this year? B: He said the team was very hardworking during the busy months, often staying late to finish picking the crops before the storms came, so he wanted to thank them for their effort.","t":"A：農場主人今年為什麼在採收季結束時發給每位工人一筆獎金？ B：他說團隊在忙碌的那幾個月非常【勤奮】，常常留到很晚，好在暴風雨來之前採收完作物，所以他想感謝大家的努力。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a city or town","c":"都市的；城市的","s":"A: What is the green area on the roof of the new office building, and who takes care of all those plants? B: It's an urban farm where employees grow vegetables for the staff cafeteria, and a small team of volunteers waters the plants every morning before work starts.","t":"A：新辦公大樓屋頂上那片綠色區域是什麼？那些植物是誰在照顧的？ B：那是一座【都市】農場，員工在那裡種植供員工餐廳使用的蔬菜，還有一小群志工每天早上上班前會去澆水。"},{"w":"jungle","p":"n.","d":"a thick tropical forest with many trees and plants","c":"叢林；熱帶雨林","s":"A: Where does the coffee company get the beans for the new premium blend that it started selling last month? B: The beans come from small farms at the edge of a jungle in South America, where the hot, wet weather and rich soil give the coffee a very strong and special flavor.","t":"A：咖啡公司上個月開始販售的新款頂級綜合咖啡，豆子是從哪裡來的？ B：豆子來自南美洲一片【叢林】邊緣的小農場，那裡炎熱潮濕的氣候和肥沃的土壤讓咖啡有非常濃郁又特別的風味。"},{"w":"pillar","p":"n.","d":"a very important part of something; a tall column that supports a building","c":"支柱；柱子","s":"A: Why does the mayor talk so much about farming in his speeches when most people in the city work in offices now? B: He says agriculture is still a pillar of the local economy, because many factories, shops, and restaurants in the area depend on the food that nearby farms produce every year.","t":"A：現在市內大多數人都在辦公室工作，為什麼市長在演講中還那麼常談到農業？ B：他說農業仍然是地方經濟的【支柱】，因為這一帶許多工廠、商店和餐廳都仰賴附近農場每年生產的糧食。"},{"w":"purify","p":"v.","d":"to make something clean by removing dirty or harmful things","c":"淨化；使純淨","s":"A: Why did the farm buy that expensive new machine next to the well, and what does it actually do? B: It is used to purify the water before the workers wash the vegetables, so the produce stays clean and safe, and the farm can pass the health inspection next month without any problems.","t":"A：農場為什麼在水井旁邊買了那台昂貴的新機器？它到底是做什麼用的？ B：它是用來在工人清洗蔬菜前【淨化】用水的，這樣農產品就能保持乾淨安全，農場下個月也能順利通過衛生檢查。"},{"w":"organic","p":"adj.","d":"grown or made without artificial chemicals","c":"有機的","s":"A: Why are the vegetables in this section of the supermarket so much more expensive than the ones near the entrance? B: These are organic vegetables grown without chemicals, so they cost more to produce, but many customers are happy to pay extra because they believe the food is healthier.","t":"A：超市這一區的蔬菜為什麼比入口附近的貴那麼多？ B：這些是不使用化學藥劑種植的【有機】蔬菜，所以生產成本比較高，但很多顧客樂意多付錢，因為他們相信這些食物比較健康。"},{"w":"equivalent","p":"n.","d":"something that has the same amount, value, or size as something else","c":"相等物；等量","s":"A: How large is the new farm that the agricultural company bought in the countryside last month? B: It covers the equivalent of about fifty soccer fields, so the manager plans to hire twenty more workers and buy several new tractors before the planting season begins in March.","t":"A：那家農業公司上個月在鄉下買的新農場有多大？ B：面積【相當於】大約五十個足球場，所以經理打算在三月播種季開始前再雇二十名工人，並添購幾台新拖拉機。"},{"w":"opt","p":"v.","d":"to choose one thing instead of another","c":"選擇；挑選","s":"A: Did the farmers in the village agree to sell their crops to the big supermarket chain, or are they still discussing the offer? B: Most of them decided to opt for the local market instead, because they can set their own prices there and they don't want to depend on one large buyer.","t":"A：村裡的農民同意把作物賣給那家大型連鎖超市了嗎？還是他們還在討論這個提議？ B：他們大多數決定改【選擇】在地市場，因為在那裡可以自己定價，而且他們不想依賴單一的大買家。"},{"w":"indulge","p":"v.","d":"to allow yourself to enjoy something special","c":"沉溺；盡情享受","s":"A: What do the visitors usually do at the end of the farm tour, after they have picked fruit and fed the animals? B: Most of them indulge in fresh strawberry ice cream at the farm café, and many also buy jam and honey to take home as gifts for their friends and coworkers.","t":"A：農場參訪結束時，訪客採完水果、餵完動物之後通常會做什麼？ B：他們大多會在農場咖啡廳【盡情享用】新鮮草莓冰淇淋，很多人還會買果醬和蜂蜜帶回家，當作送給朋友和同事的禮物。"},{"w":"abundance","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount of something","c":"大量；豐富","s":"A: Why are fruit prices at the market so much lower this month than they were in the spring? B: The good weather this summer produced an abundance of peaches and plums, so farmers have more fruit than they can sell, and they are lowering prices to sell everything before it goes bad.","t":"A：為什麼市場上這個月的水果價格比春天時低那麼多？ B：今年夏天天氣好，桃子和李子【大豐收】，所以農民的水果多到賣不完，他們正在降價，好在水果壞掉前全部賣出去。"},{"w":"stimulate","p":"v.","d":"to encourage something to grow, develop, or become more active","c":"刺激；促進","s":"A: Why did the government announce new loans for young people who want to start farms in rural areas? B: Officials hope the loans will stimulate growth in the countryside, because many villages have lost workers to the cities, and new farms could create jobs and bring families back.","t":"A：政府為什麼宣布要提供新貸款給想在鄉村地區開農場的年輕人？ B：官員希望這些貸款能【刺激】鄉村的發展，因為許多村莊的勞動力都流失到城市，而新農場可以創造工作機會並把家庭帶回來。"},{"w":"appetite","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you want to eat food","c":"食慾；胃口","s":"A: Did the guests enjoy lunch at the farm restaurant after the long morning of picking apples in the orchard? B: Yes, all that fresh air and hard work gave everyone a big appetite, so they ate almost everything on the table and even asked the chef for the recipe for her vegetable soup.","t":"A：在果園採了一整個早上的蘋果後，客人們喜歡農場餐廳的午餐嗎？ B：喜歡，新鮮空氣加上辛苦工作讓大家【胃口】大開，所以他們幾乎吃光了桌上所有的菜，甚至還向主廚要了她的蔬菜湯食譜。"},{"w":"migrate","p":"v.","d":"to move from one place to another to live or work","c":"遷移；移居","s":"A: Why are there fewer young workers in the farming villages than there were ten or twenty years ago? B: Many young people migrate to big cities to look for better-paid jobs, so farm owners now find it hard to hire staff, and some are starting to use machines instead.","t":"A：為什麼現在農村裡的年輕工人比十年或二十年前少？ B：許多年輕人【移居】到大城市尋找薪水更好的工作，所以農場主人現在很難雇到人手，有些人開始改用機器。"}]},{"unit":138,"theme":"Fashion 時尚","cards":[{"w":"style","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of dressing or doing something","c":"風格；款式","s":"A: I'm going to a job interview at a large advertising agency next Tuesday, so do you think I should wear my gray suit or something more relaxed? B: Creative companies usually like people who show their personal style, so wear the suit but add a bright tie or an interesting scarf to look confident.","t":"A：我下週二要去一家大型廣告公司面試，你覺得我應該穿灰色西裝，還是穿得輕鬆一點？ B：有創意的公司通常喜歡能展現個人【風格】的人，所以穿西裝，但搭配一條亮色領帶或有趣的圍巾，看起來會更有自信。"},{"w":"trend","p":"n.","d":"a new fashion or a general change in what people do or like","c":"潮流；趨勢","s":"A: Why did the store manager ask us to move all the wide-leg pants to the front window this morning before the customers arrived? B: Wide-leg pants are the biggest trend this season, and our sales report shows that young office workers have been buying them much faster than any other item.","t":"A：為什麼店經理今天早上要我們在客人到之前，把所有寬褲移到前面的櫥窗？ B：寬褲是這一季最大的【潮流】，而且我們的銷售報告顯示，年輕上班族購買寬褲的速度比其他任何商品都快。"},{"w":"outfit","p":"n.","d":"a set of clothes worn together","c":"一套服裝","s":"A: Do you know what I should wear to the company's annual dinner at the hotel on Friday night, since it's my first time attending? B: Most people choose a simple but smart outfit, like a dark dress or a jacket with nice trousers, because the managers and some important clients will be there.","t":"A：你知道星期五晚上在飯店舉辦的公司年度晚宴我該穿什麼嗎？這是我第一次參加。 B：大多數人會選一套簡單但得體的【服裝】，像是深色洋裝或西裝外套配好看的長褲，因為經理們和一些重要客戶都會出席。"},{"w":"clothing","p":"n.","d":"clothes in general","c":"衣物；服裝","s":"A: Our team is helping at the community center this weekend, so what kind of things should we collect from the employees in the office? B: The center mainly needs warm clothing such as coats, sweaters and gloves, because many families in the area cannot afford them when the cold weather arrives in December.","t":"A：我們的團隊這個週末要去社區中心幫忙，我們該向辦公室員工收集哪些東西？ B：中心主要需要保暖的【衣物】，像是外套、毛衣和手套，因為這地區很多家庭在十二月寒冷天氣來臨時買不起這些東西。"},{"w":"apparel","p":"n.","d":"clothes, especially ones that are sold in stores","c":"服飾；服裝","s":"A: Which department will be responsible for the new line of sportswear that the company plans to sell online next spring? B: The apparel team will handle it, since they already design the running shirts and yoga pants, and they have good relationships with the factories that produce our products overseas.","t":"A：公司計畫明年春天在網路上販售的新運動服系列，會由哪個部門負責？ B：會由【服飾】團隊負責，因為他們已經在設計跑步上衣和瑜珈褲，而且他們和海外生產我們產品的工廠關係良好。"},{"w":"garment","p":"n.","d":"one piece of clothing","c":"衣服；一件衣物","s":"A: Why are the workers in the factory checking every shirt so carefully before they put them into boxes for shipping? B: Last month a customer returned a large order because some buttons were missing, so now each garment must pass a quality check before it leaves the building.","t":"A：為什麼工廠的工人在把每件襯衫裝箱出貨前都檢查得這麼仔細？ B：上個月有位客戶因為有些鈕扣不見而退回一大筆訂單，所以現在每件【衣服】離開工廠前都必須通過品質檢查。"},{"w":"designer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to plan how clothes or products will look","c":"設計師","s":"A: Who created the beautiful uniforms that the hotel staff started wearing at the front desk last week? B: The hotel hired a young local designer who studied in Paris, and she chose soft colors and comfortable materials so that the staff could look professional and still move easily during long shifts.","t":"A：上週飯店櫃檯人員開始穿的那套漂亮制服是誰設計的？ B：飯店聘請了一位曾在巴黎求學的年輕本地【設計師】，她選了柔和的顏色和舒適的材質，讓員工看起來專業，在長時間輪班時也能活動自如。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a product name that a company uses for its goods","c":"品牌","s":"A: Why are so many customers lining up outside the shopping mall so early on a Saturday morning? B: A famous sports brand is opening its first store in our city today, and it is giving free T-shirts to the first one hundred people who buy something before noon.","t":"A：為什麼星期六一大早就有這麼多顧客在購物中心外面排隊？ B：一個知名運動【品牌】今天在我們城市開第一家店，而且會送免費T恤給中午前購物的前一百位顧客。"},{"w":"runway","p":"n.","d":"the long, narrow stage that models walk on at a fashion show","c":"伸展台","s":"A: Were you able to see the new collection at the fashion show downtown last night, or was it too crowded to get in? B: I got a seat near the runway, so I could watch the models walking very closely, and I took lots of photos of the jackets for our marketing team.","t":"A：你昨晚有看到市中心時裝秀的新系列嗎？還是人太多進不去？ B：我坐在【伸展台】附近，所以能很近地看模特兒走秀，我還幫我們的行銷團隊拍了很多外套的照片。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a person who wears clothes to show them in photos or shows","c":"模特兒","s":"A: Who is going to wear our new summer dresses in the photos for the online catalog next week? B: We hired a professional model from an agency in Taipei, and the photographer plans to take the pictures at the beach in the early morning when the light is soft.","t":"A：下週網路型錄照片裡，誰要穿我們的新款夏季洋裝？ B：我們從台北一家經紀公司聘請了一位專業【模特兒】，攝影師打算在清晨光線柔和時到海邊拍照。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of new clothes that a designer shows at one time","c":"（服裝）系列","s":"A: When will customers be able to buy the new winter coats and boots that we showed to the store buyers last month? B: The whole collection will arrive in our shops in early November, and we will advertise it on social media and in fashion magazines a few weeks before that.","t":"A：顧客什麼時候能買到我們上個月展示給採購人員看的新款冬季外套和靴子？ B：整個【系列】會在十一月初到店，而我們會在那之前幾週在社群媒體和時尚雜誌上宣傳。"},{"w":"fabric","p":"n.","d":"cloth used for making clothes","c":"布料；織物","s":"A: Why did the customer return the expensive shirt she bought from us only two weeks ago? B: She said the fabric became very thin and lost its color after she washed it only twice, so we gave her a full refund and reported the problem to the supplier.","t":"A：為什麼那位顧客把兩週前才向我們買的昂貴襯衫退回？ B：她說只洗了兩次，【布料】就變得很薄又褪色了，所以我們全額退款給她，並把問題回報給供應商。"},{"w":"pattern","p":"n.","d":"a design of lines, shapes or colors repeated on cloth","c":"圖案；花樣","s":"A: Have you decided which tablecloths we should order for the new restaurant before it opens next month? B: I like the blue ones with a simple flower pattern, because they look bright and friendly, and they will not show small stains as easily as the plain white ones.","t":"A：你決定好新餐廳下個月開幕前我們要訂哪一款桌布了嗎？ B：我喜歡藍色帶有簡單花朵【圖案】的那款，因為看起來明亮又親切，而且不像純白的那款那麼容易看出小污漬。"},{"w":"design","p":"n.","d":"the way something is planned and made to look","c":"設計","s":"A: What do the customers think of the new handbags that we started selling in the department store last month? B: Most people love the simple design and the light leather, but some say the bag is too small to carry a laptop, so we may make a bigger version next year.","t":"A：顧客覺得我們上個月開始在百貨公司販售的新款手提包怎麼樣？ B：大多數人很喜歡它簡單的【設計】和輕巧的皮革，但有些人說包包太小放不下筆電，所以我們明年可能會推出較大的版本。"},{"w":"tailor","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is making or changing clothes to fit people","c":"裁縫師","s":"A: My new suit is a little too long in the sleeves, and I need it for an important presentation to the board next Thursday. B: There is a skilled tailor on the second floor of our office building, and he can usually shorten the sleeves in two or three days for a fair price.","t":"A：我的新西裝袖子有點太長，而我下週四要穿它向董事會做重要簡報。 B：我們辦公大樓二樓有一位手藝很好的【裁縫師】，他通常兩三天就能把袖子改短，價格也很合理。"},{"w":"fit","p":"v.","d":"to be the right size and shape for someone","c":"合身；適合","s":"A: Should I order the company T-shirts for the volunteers in medium size, or do we need different sizes for everyone? B: Please ask each person for their size first, because one size will not fit everyone, and last year many shirts were too tight or too loose to wear.","t":"A：志工的公司T恤我應該全部訂中號，還是每個人需要不同的尺寸？ B：請先問每個人的尺寸，因為單一尺寸不可能讓每個人都【合身】，而且去年很多T恤太緊或太鬆根本不能穿。"},{"w":"accessory","p":"n.","d":"an extra item such as a bag, belt or scarf worn with clothes","c":"配件；飾品","s":"A: Do you think this plain black dress is good enough for the awards dinner, or does it look too simple? B: It looks nice, but you could add one bright accessory, such as a red handbag or a silver necklace, to make it more special for the evening.","t":"A：你覺得這件素面黑洋裝穿去頒獎晚宴夠好嗎？還是看起來太簡單了？ B：很好看，不過你可以加一件亮眼的【配件】，像是紅色手提包或銀項鍊，讓它在晚上看起來更特別。"},{"w":"jewelry","p":"n.","d":"rings, necklaces, earrings and similar things worn for decoration","c":"珠寶；首飾","s":"A: Why does the department store have extra security guards near the main entrance this week? B: They moved the expensive jewelry counter next to the door for the holiday sale, so the guards are watching the gold rings and diamond earrings while large crowds of shoppers walk past.","t":"A：為什麼百貨公司這週在正門附近加派了保全？ B：他們為了節慶特賣把昂貴的【珠寶】櫃移到門邊，所以在大批購物人潮經過時，保全要看守那些金戒指和鑽石耳環。"},{"w":"footwear","p":"n.","d":"things you wear on your feet, such as shoes and boots","c":"鞋類","s":"A: What kind of shoes should the new kitchen staff wear when they start working at the restaurant on Monday? B: Everyone must wear safe footwear that doesn't slip, because the floor often gets wet and oily during busy hours, and we don't want anyone to fall and get hurt.","t":"A：新的廚房員工星期一開始在餐廳上班時應該穿什麼鞋？ B：每個人都必須穿防滑的安全【鞋類】，因為忙碌時段地板常常又濕又油，我們不希望有人跌倒受傷。"},{"w":"casual","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not formal","c":"休閒的；便服的","s":"A: Is it true that we don't have to wear suits and ties to the office on Fridays anymore? B: Yes, the manager announced that Friday is now a casual day, so you can wear jeans and a polo shirt, but you should still dress neatly if you have a meeting with clients.","t":"A：我們星期五真的不用再穿西裝打領帶進辦公室了嗎？ B：對，經理宣布星期五現在是【便服】日，所以你可以穿牛仔褲和polo衫，但如果要跟客戶開會，還是要穿得整齊。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"suitable for serious or important occasions","c":"正式的","s":"A: The invitation for the charity dinner at the Grand Hotel says black tie, so what exactly does that mean for me? B: It means you should wear very formal clothes, such as a dark suit with a bow tie, because many important business leaders and government officials will be attending the event.","t":"A：君悅飯店慈善晚宴的邀請函上寫著黑領結，那對我來說到底是什麼意思？ B：意思是你應該穿非常【正式】的服裝，像是深色西裝配領結，因為很多重要的企業領袖和政府官員都會出席這場活動。"},{"w":"elegant","p":"adj.","d":"beautiful in a graceful and simple way","c":"優雅的；高雅的","s":"A: What did the guests say about the hotel's new lobby after the renovation was finally finished last month? B: Many guests said it looks very elegant now, with soft lights, fresh flowers and marble floors, and several couples have already asked to hold their wedding photos there.","t":"A：飯店大廳上個月終於整修完後，客人怎麼評價？ B：很多客人說現在看起來非常【優雅】，有柔和的燈光、鮮花和大理石地板，已經有好幾對新人詢問能否在那裡拍婚紗照。"},{"w":"trendy","p":"adj.","d":"very popular and new at the moment","c":"時髦的；流行的","s":"A: Why did the company decide to open its new coffee shop in that small neighborhood near the university? B: The area has become very trendy with young people, and there are many popular clothing stores and art galleries there, so the managers believe the shop will attract lots of customers.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定在大學附近那個小社區開新咖啡店？ B：那一區在年輕人當中變得非常【時髦】，那裡有很多受歡迎的服飾店和藝廊，所以經理們相信這家店會吸引很多顧客。"},{"w":"stylish","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and fashionable","c":"時髦的；有型的","s":"A: Our sales team needs new bags for carrying laptops to client meetings, so do you have any suggestions? B: I saw some stylish leather bags at the mall that look smart and professional, and they also have soft pockets that protect computers, so they are both good-looking and useful.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊需要新包包帶筆電去見客戶，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：我在購物中心看到一些【有型】的皮包，看起來俐落又專業，而且有柔軟的夾層保護電腦，所以既好看又實用。"},{"w":"classic","p":"adj.","d":"simple and traditional, and always in fashion","c":"經典的","s":"A: Should we change the restaurant's waiter uniforms to something more colorful to attract younger customers? B: I think we should keep the classic white shirts and black vests, because they never go out of fashion, and many of our regular guests love the traditional feeling of our restaurant.","t":"A：我們要不要把餐廳服務生的制服換成更多彩的款式來吸引年輕顧客？ B：我覺得應該保留【經典】的白襯衫和黑背心，因為它們永遠不會過時，而且很多常客都很喜歡我們餐廳的傳統氛圍。"},{"w":"vintage","p":"adj.","d":"old but of good quality and style","c":"古著的；復古的","s":"A: Where did you find that unusual leather jacket that everyone in the office was talking about this morning? B: I bought it at a vintage shop downtown that sells clothes from the 1970s and 1980s, and it was much cheaper than a new jacket from a department store.","t":"A：今天早上辦公室大家都在討論的那件特別皮夾克，你在哪裡找到的？ B：我在市中心一家賣1970和1980年代衣服的【古著】店買的，比百貨公司的新夾克便宜多了。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"new and using the latest ideas or style","c":"現代的；新式的","s":"A: What does the new office building that the company moved into last week look like inside? B: It has a very modern design with glass walls, bright open spaces and smart lights that turn off automatically, so it feels much more comfortable than our old building from the 1980s.","t":"A：公司上週搬進去的新辦公大樓裡面看起來怎麼樣？ B：它有非常【現代】的設計，有玻璃牆、明亮開放的空間，還有會自動關閉的智慧燈，所以感覺比我們1980年代的舊大樓舒適多了。"},{"w":"fashionable","p":"adj.","d":"popular at a particular time","c":"流行的；時尚的","s":"A: Why are so many office workers wearing white sneakers with their suits these days? B: It became fashionable a few years ago after several famous business leaders started doing it, and now many people think it looks both smart and relaxed for work in the city.","t":"A：為什麼現在這麼多上班族穿西裝配白色運動鞋？ B：幾年前幾位知名企業領袖開始這樣穿之後就變得【流行】了，現在很多人覺得在城市上班這樣穿既得體又輕鬆。"},{"w":"colorful","p":"adj.","d":"having many bright colors","c":"色彩繽紛的","s":"A: How should we decorate the children's clothing section before the store's grand opening next weekend? B: Let's use colorful balloons, bright posters and cartoon pictures on the walls, because parents and kids will notice the area quickly and feel happy while they shop for school clothes.","t":"A：在下週末商店盛大開幕前，我們該怎麼布置童裝區？ B：我們用【色彩繽紛】的氣球、亮眼的海報和牆上的卡通圖片，因為這樣父母和孩子會很快注意到這一區，在買上學衣服時也會很開心。"},{"w":"comfortably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that feels relaxed and pleasant","c":"舒適地","s":"A: The training workshop will last all day on Saturday, so what should the new employees wear? B: Tell them to dress comfortably in soft trousers and flat shoes, because they will be sitting on the floor for some team activities and walking around the factory in the afternoon.","t":"A：週六的培訓工作坊會持續一整天，新員工應該穿什麼？ B：告訴他們穿得【舒適】一點，穿柔軟的長褲和平底鞋，因為有些團隊活動要坐在地上，下午還要在工廠裡走動。"},{"w":"boldly","p":"adv.","d":"in a brave way that is easy to notice","c":"大膽地；醒目地","s":"A: Why did the young sales assistant get so much attention at the company's fashion event last night? B: She dressed very boldly in a bright orange suit with big gold earrings, and many guests, including the president, stopped to ask her where she had bought her clothes.","t":"A：為什麼那位年輕的銷售助理在昨晚公司的時尚活動上那麼引人注目？ B：她穿得非常【大膽】，一身亮橘色套裝配大金耳環，很多賓客，包括總裁，都停下來問她衣服是在哪裡買的。"},{"w":"dress up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put on nice or special clothes","c":"盛裝打扮","s":"A: Do I need to wear something special for the office party on Friday, or can I come in my normal work clothes? B: Most people like to dress up a little for the party, so you might wear a nice shirt or skirt, but you don't need to rent an expensive suit.","t":"A：星期五的辦公室派對我需要穿特別的衣服嗎？還是穿平常的上班服就可以？ B：大部分人參加派對時喜歡稍微【盛裝打扮】一下，所以你可以穿件好看的襯衫或裙子，但不需要去租昂貴的西裝。"},{"w":"coordinate","p":"v.","d":"to make clothes or colors look good together","c":"搭配；協調","s":"A: The new uniforms for the hotel staff have arrived, but some of the colors look strange together, don't they? B: Yes, the designer wanted the scarves to coordinate with the blue jackets, but the factory used the wrong shade of green, so we have asked them to send replacements next week.","t":"A：飯店員工的新制服到了，但有些顏色搭在一起看起來很怪，不是嗎？ B：對，設計師原本想讓圍巾和藍色外套【搭配】，但工廠用錯了綠色的色調，所以我們已經請他們下週寄替換品過來。"},{"w":"experiment","p":"v.","d":"to try new ideas or ways of doing something","c":"嘗試；實驗","s":"A: Why does Lisa from the marketing department wear such different clothes and hairstyles every week? B: She likes to experiment with new colors and styles, and she says it helps her come up with fresh ideas for our advertising campaigns and keeps her work life more interesting.","t":"A：為什麼行銷部的Lisa每週都穿著不同的衣服、換不同的髮型？ B：她喜歡【嘗試】新的顏色和風格，她說這能幫助她為我們的廣告活動想出新點子，也讓她的工作生活更有趣。"}]},{"unit":139,"theme":"Fashionable Person 時髦的人","cards":[{"w":"fashionista","p":"n.","d":"a person who loves fashion and always wears the newest styles","c":"時尚達人；熱愛時尚的人","s":"A: Who should we ask to help choose the new uniforms for the hotel staff, since none of us really follows the latest clothing styles? B: Let's ask Grace from the marketing department, because she is a real fashionista who reads every fashion magazine and always knows which colors will be popular next season.","t":"A：既然我們沒有人真的在追最新的服裝款式，我們該請誰幫忙挑選飯店員工的新制服？ B：我們去問行銷部的葛瑞絲吧，因為她是真正的【時尚達人】，每本時尚雜誌都讀，而且總是知道下一季會流行哪些顏色。"},{"w":"trendsetter","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts a new style that other people copy","c":"引領潮流的人；潮流先驅","s":"A: Why did so many employees suddenly start wearing white sneakers with their business suits after the company holiday party last December? B: Our new sales director wore that look at the party, and because she is such a trendsetter, half the office copied her style within a few weeks.","t":"A：為什麼去年十二月公司節慶派對之後，那麼多員工突然開始穿白色運動鞋搭配西裝？ B：我們的新業務總監在派對上穿了那樣的造型，而且因為她是如此【引領潮流的人】，幾週內辦公室有一半的人都模仿了她的風格。"},{"w":"stylist","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to choose clothes, hair or makeup for people","c":"造型師","s":"A: The magazine photo shoot for our new watch collection starts at nine tomorrow morning, so who will decide what the models should wear? B: The agency is sending an experienced stylist who will bring several outfits, choose the right shoes, and make sure everything matches the colors of our brand.","t":"A：我們新手錶系列的雜誌拍攝明天早上九點開始，那麼誰來決定模特兒該穿什麼？ B：經紀公司會派一位經驗豐富的【造型師】，她會帶來好幾套服裝、挑選合適的鞋子，並確保一切都和我們品牌的顏色相配。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a person who wears clothes in shows or photos to show them to buyers","c":"模特兒","s":"A: How did the fashion show for our autumn jackets go last night, and did the buyers from the department stores seem interested in the designs? B: It went very well, and every model walked down the runway confidently, so several buyers asked for price lists before the event even ended.","t":"A：昨晚我們秋季夾克的時裝秀進行得如何？百貨公司的採購人員看起來對這些設計有興趣嗎？ B：非常順利，每位【模特兒】都很有自信地走過伸展台，所以好幾位採購在活動還沒結束前就索取了價目表。"},{"w":"influencer","p":"n.","d":"a person who affects what many people buy through social media","c":"網紅；有影響力的人","s":"A: Our new skin cream has been in stores for two months, but sales are still low, so what do you think we should try next? B: We could pay a popular online influencer with millions of followers to post a video about it, because young customers often trust these people more than traditional advertisements.","t":"A：我們的新款護膚霜已經上市兩個月了，但銷量仍然很低，你覺得我們接下來該嘗試什麼？ B：我們可以付費請一位擁有數百萬粉絲的熱門線上【網紅】發一支相關影片，因為年輕顧客往往比較信任這些人，而不是傳統廣告。"},{"w":"icon","p":"n.","d":"a famous person who many people admire as a symbol of something","c":"代表人物；偶像","s":"A: Why does the museum's new exhibition about clothing focus so much on one actress from the 1950s instead of including many different designers? B: Because she became a style icon whose simple black dresses and pearl necklaces are still copied by designers and shoppers all over the world today.","t":"A：為什麼博物館關於服裝的新展覽如此聚焦在一位1950年代的女演員身上，而不是納入許多不同的設計師？ B：因為她成為了時尚【代表人物】，她簡約的黑色洋裝和珍珠項鍊至今仍被世界各地的設計師和消費者模仿。"},{"w":"celebrity","p":"n.","d":"a famous person, especially in movies, music or sports","c":"名人；明星","s":"A: Why is there such a big crowd with cameras standing outside the entrance of the shopping mall this afternoon, blocking the sidewalk? B: A famous celebrity from a popular TV drama is opening a new clothing store there today, so hundreds of fans have been waiting since early morning to take pictures.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午購物中心入口外面站著一大群拿著相機的人，把人行道都擋住了？ B：一位熱門電視劇的知名【明星】今天要在那裡開一家新服飾店，所以數百名粉絲從一大早就在等著拍照。"},{"w":"designer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to plan how clothes or products will look","c":"設計師","s":"A: The new winter coats look amazing, so who came up with the idea of using recycled fabric and such bright colors for the collection? B: Our young fashion designer spent three months drawing sketches and testing materials, and she wanted to show that warm clothing can also be friendly to the environment.","t":"A：新的冬季大衣看起來很棒，是誰想到在這個系列使用回收布料和如此鮮豔的顏色？ B：我們年輕的服裝【設計師】花了三個月畫草圖和測試材料，她想證明保暖的衣物也可以對環境友善。"},{"w":"well-dressed","p":"adj.","d":"wearing nice, suitable and attractive clothes","c":"衣著得體的；穿著講究的","s":"A: What kind of impression do you think the bank wants its employees to give when they meet important customers at the front counter? B: The managers want every employee to look well-dressed and professional, so they provide clean suits and ask the staff to check their appearance before the branch opens.","t":"A：你認為銀行希望員工在櫃檯接待重要客戶時給人什麼樣的印象？ B：經理們希望每位員工看起來都【衣著得體】且專業，所以他們提供乾淨的西裝，並要求員工在分行開門前檢查自己的儀容。"},{"w":"stylish","p":"adj.","d":"fashionable and attractive in appearance","c":"時髦的；有型的","s":"A: Have you seen the new uniforms that the airline introduced for its flight attendants this spring, and do passengers like them? B: Yes, they are much more stylish than the old ones, with modern cuts and soft colors, and many passengers have even posted photos of them online.","t":"A：你看過航空公司今年春天為空服員推出的新制服嗎？乘客喜歡嗎？ B：看過，它們比舊制服【時髦】得多，有現代感的剪裁和柔和的顏色，許多乘客甚至還把照片貼到網路上。"},{"w":"trendy","p":"adj.","d":"very fashionable and popular at the moment","c":"流行的；時髦的","s":"A: Why did the owners decide to move their café from the quiet suburbs to the busy downtown area near the university last year? B: They wanted to attract young customers, so they chose a trendy neighborhood full of art galleries and small boutiques where students and office workers like to spend their weekends.","t":"A：為什麼老闆們去年決定把咖啡館從安靜的郊區搬到大學附近熱鬧的市中心？ B：他們想吸引年輕顧客，所以選了一個【時髦】的街區，那裡有很多藝廊和小型精品店，是學生和上班族喜歡度過週末的地方。"},{"w":"chic","p":"adj.","d":"stylish and fashionable in a simple, attractive way","c":"時髦雅緻的；別緻的","s":"A: Where should we hold the dinner for our French business partners next week, since they are used to very nice restaurants in Paris? B: I suggest the chic little bistro on the top floor of the hotel, because it has simple but beautiful decorations, excellent wine, and a wonderful view of the city.","t":"A：下週我們該在哪裡宴請法國商業夥伴？畢竟他們習慣了巴黎非常好的餐廳。 B：我建議飯店頂樓那家【別緻】的小酒館，因為它的裝潢簡單卻美麗，有很棒的葡萄酒，還能欣賞城市的美景。"},{"w":"elegant","p":"adj.","d":"graceful and attractive in a simple, high-quality way","c":"優雅的；高雅的","s":"A: What should the guests wear to the company's fiftieth anniversary dinner at the grand hotel next Saturday evening? B: The invitation asks everyone to wear elegant evening clothes, such as long dresses or dark suits, because the event will include a formal dinner, live music, and speeches from the founders.","t":"A：下週六晚上在大飯店舉辦的公司五十週年晚宴，賓客應該穿什麼？ B：邀請函要求大家穿著【高雅】的晚禮服，例如長禮服或深色西裝，因為活動將有正式晚宴、現場音樂和創辦人的致詞。"},{"w":"sophisticated","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of knowledge and good taste about fashion, culture or the world","c":"有品味的；世故老練的","s":"A: Who is the main target customer for the expensive perfume we are launching in department stores across Asia next month? B: We are aiming at sophisticated professionals in their thirties and forties who travel often, enjoy fine art and good restaurants, and are willing to pay more for quality.","t":"A：我們下個月要在亞洲各地百貨公司推出的昂貴香水，主要目標客群是誰？ B：我們鎖定三、四十歲【有品味的】專業人士，他們經常旅行、喜愛精緻藝術和好餐廳，而且願意為品質多花錢。"},{"w":"classy","p":"adj.","d":"stylish and of high quality in a way that shows good taste","c":"有格調的；高級的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the opening party for the new jewelry store on Main Street last Friday night, or was it too crowded? B: It was a very classy event with soft piano music, fresh flowers on every table, and guests in beautiful outfits, so I stayed much longer than I planned.","t":"A：你喜歡上週五晚上主街新珠寶店的開幕派對嗎？還是人太多了？ B：那是一場非常【有格調】的活動，有輕柔的鋼琴音樂、每張桌上都有鮮花，賓客們也都穿著漂亮的服裝，所以我待得比原本計畫的久很多。"},{"w":"fashion-conscious","p":"adj.","d":"caring a lot about wearing fashionable clothes","c":"注重時尚的","s":"A: Why did our clothing company decide to spend most of its advertising budget on social media this year instead of on television? B: Our research showed that fashion-conscious young shoppers spend hours looking at outfits on their phones every day, so online ads are the best way to reach them.","t":"A：為什麼我們服飾公司今年決定把大部分廣告預算花在社群媒體上，而不是電視？ B：我們的研究顯示，【注重時尚的】年輕消費者每天花好幾個小時在手機上看穿搭，所以網路廣告是接觸他們的最佳方式。"},{"w":"tasteful","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and showing good judgment about what is suitable","c":"有品味的；雅緻的","s":"A: The hotel lobby looks so calm and expensive now, so what exactly did the interior decorators change during the renovation last month? B: They removed the bright posters and plastic plants and added tasteful decorations in soft gray and cream colors, including a few paintings and some fresh flowers.","t":"A：飯店大廳現在看起來好平靜又高級，室內設計師上個月整修時到底改了什麼？ B：他們拿掉了鮮豔的海報和塑膠植物，換上了柔和灰色和米色系的【雅緻】裝飾，包括幾幅畫和一些鮮花。"},{"w":"impeccable","p":"adj.","d":"perfect, with no mistakes or problems at all","c":"完美無缺的；無可挑剔的","s":"A: Why do so many international guests ask for the same waiter whenever they come back to eat at our restaurant? B: His manners and appearance are impeccable, because he always wears a perfectly pressed uniform, remembers every guest's name, and never makes a mistake with an order.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多國際賓客每次回到我們餐廳用餐時都指名同一位服務生？ B：他的禮儀和外表都【無可挑剔】，因為他總是穿著燙得筆挺的制服、記得每位客人的名字，而且點餐從不出錯。"},{"w":"polished","p":"adj.","d":"neat, smart and professional in appearance or manner","c":"優雅得體的；精緻的","s":"A: How did the new account manager manage to win the contract with the luxury hotel chain after only one meeting last week? B: She gave a polished presentation in a smart navy suit, answered every difficult question calmly, and showed the clients that our company pays close attention to details.","t":"A：新任客戶經理上週怎麼只開了一次會就拿下了那家豪華連鎖飯店的合約？ B：她穿著俐落的海軍藍套裝做了一場【精緻得體】的簡報，冷靜地回答每個困難的問題，並讓客戶看到我們公司非常注重細節。"},{"w":"glamorous","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and exciting in a rich, special way","c":"迷人的；光鮮亮麗的","s":"A: Is working for a famous fashion magazine as exciting as people think, with parties, travel, and celebrities every week? B: It looks glamorous from the outside, but most days we are actually sitting in the office until late at night, checking photos, writing articles, and meeting tight deadlines.","t":"A：在知名時尚雜誌工作真的像大家想的那麼刺激嗎？每週都有派對、旅行和名人？ B：從外面看起來很【光鮮亮麗】，但其實大部分的日子我們都坐在辦公室待到深夜，檢查照片、寫文章，趕緊迫的截稿期限。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sure about your own abilities or appearance","c":"有自信的","s":"A: You seemed very relaxed during the job interview at the design company yesterday, so how did you prepare for it? B: I practiced my answers with a friend for a week and bought a new suit that fits well, so I felt confident when I walked into the room.","t":"A：你昨天在設計公司面試時看起來很放鬆，你是怎麼準備的？ B：我跟朋友練習回答問題練了一個星期，還買了一套合身的新西裝，所以走進房間時我覺得很【有自信】。"},{"w":"distinctive","p":"adj.","d":"easy to recognize because it is special or different","c":"與眾不同的；有特色的","s":"A: How can customers recognize our handbags in a busy department store when so many brands sell similar products these days? B: Every bag has a distinctive gold buckle shaped like a small leaf, so shoppers can spot our brand from across the room, even without reading the label.","t":"A：現在那麼多品牌都賣類似的商品，顧客在熱鬧的百貨公司裡要怎麼認出我們的手提包？ B：每個包包都有一個【與眾不同】、形狀像小葉子的金色扣環，所以購物者即使不看標籤，從房間另一頭也能認出我們的品牌。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"new and different from anything else; not copied","c":"原創的；新穎的","s":"A: Why did the judges choose the student from the small art school as the winner of the national clothing design contest this year? B: Her collection was truly original, because she made jackets from old maps and newspapers, and nobody on the panel had ever seen anything like that before.","t":"A：為什麼今年全國服裝設計比賽的評審選了那位來自小型藝術學校的學生為優勝者？ B：她的作品系列非常【原創】，因為她用舊地圖和報紙做成夾克，評審團裡沒有人以前看過類似的東西。"},{"w":"bold","p":"adj.","d":"brave and not afraid to look different; strong and bright","c":"大膽的；醒目的","s":"A: Do you think it was a good idea for the new manager to wear a bright orange suit at her first meeting with the board of directors? B: It was a bold choice in such a conservative bank, but people remembered her immediately, and her confident speech made a very good impression.","t":"A：你覺得新經理在第一次和董事會開會時穿一套鮮橘色西裝是個好主意嗎？ B：在這麼保守的銀行裡那是個【大膽】的選擇，但大家立刻記住了她，而且她充滿自信的演講留下了非常好的印象。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"able to make new and interesting ideas or things","c":"有創意的","s":"A: Our sales of sports shoes have dropped for three months in a row, so what does the marketing director want us to do? B: She wants the team to come up with creative ideas for a new campaign, such as a dance video challenge or a contest where customers design their own shoes.","t":"A：我們運動鞋的銷量已經連續三個月下滑，行銷總監要我們怎麼做？ B：她希望團隊想出【有創意的】新活動點子，例如舞蹈影片挑戰，或是讓顧客自己設計鞋子的比賽。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"using new styles, ideas or technology; not old-fashioned","c":"現代的；新式的","s":"A: Why does the company want to completely redesign its old shop in the city center when the building is still in good condition? B: The owners feel it looks old-fashioned, so they plan a modern interior with glass walls, bright lighting, and digital screens to attract younger shoppers.","t":"A：為什麼公司在市中心的老店建築狀況還很好時，就想要全面重新設計？ B：老闆們覺得它看起來很過時，所以他們計畫打造【現代】風格的室內空間，有玻璃牆、明亮的燈光和數位螢幕，以吸引較年輕的消費者。"},{"w":"vintage","p":"adj.","d":"old but of high quality and still attractive and fashionable","c":"復古的；古著的","s":"A: Where did you find that beautiful leather jacket you wore to the office party, because I have never seen one like it in the stores? B: I bought it at a vintage clothing shop downtown that sells high-quality secondhand items from the 1970s, and it cost much less than a new one.","t":"A：你在辦公室派對上穿的那件漂亮皮夾克是在哪裡找到的？我從沒在店裡看過那樣的。 B：我是在市中心一家【古著】服飾店買的，那家店販售1970年代的高品質二手商品，而且比新的便宜很多。"},{"w":"coordinated","p":"adj.","d":"matching well together in color or style","c":"搭配協調的","s":"A: Why does everyone in the office ask Linda for advice whenever they need to buy clothes for an important event or meeting? B: Her outfits are always perfectly coordinated, with her shoes, scarf, and handbag matching in color, so people trust her taste and her honest opinions.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室裡大家每當需要為重要活動或會議買衣服時，都會向琳達請教？ B：她的穿著總是搭配得非常【協調】，鞋子、圍巾和手提包的顏色都相互呼應，所以大家信任她的品味和誠實的意見。"},{"w":"neatly","p":"adv.","d":"in a tidy, careful and organized way","c":"整齊地；整潔地","s":"A: The manager of the clothing store seemed unhappy this morning, so did something go wrong with the window display or the shelves? B: Some new staff members had left piles of sweaters on the tables, so she asked everyone to fold all the clothes neatly before the store opened at ten.","t":"A：服飾店的經理今天早上看起來不太高興，是櫥窗陳列或貨架出了什麼問題嗎？ B：有些新員工把一堆毛衣留在桌上，所以她要求大家在十點開店前把所有衣服【整齊地】折好。"},{"w":"smartly","p":"adv.","d":"in a neat, stylish and fashionable way","c":"俐落地；體面地","s":"A: What should the new interns wear when they visit the client's headquarters with the senior team next Thursday afternoon? B: They should be smartly dressed in dark suits and polished shoes, because this client is very traditional and first impressions will matter a lot for the contract.","t":"A：下週四下午新實習生和資深團隊一起拜訪客戶總部時應該穿什麼？ B：他們應該穿著深色西裝和擦亮的皮鞋，【體面地】打扮，因為這位客戶非常傳統，第一印象對合約會有很大的影響。"},{"w":"elegantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a graceful and attractive way","c":"優雅地；高雅地","s":"A: How did the hotel staff prepare the ballroom for the wedding reception that took place there last Saturday evening? B: They decorated the room elegantly with white roses, silver candles, and soft lights, and the bride's family said it looked even better than the photos in the brochure.","t":"A：飯店員工是怎麼為上週六晚上在宴會廳舉行的婚宴做準備的？ B：他們用白玫瑰、銀色蠟燭和柔和的燈光把會場佈置得很【高雅】，新娘的家人說看起來甚至比宣傳冊上的照片還要好。"},{"w":"stylishly","p":"adv.","d":"in a fashionable and attractive way","c":"時髦地；有型地","s":"A: Did the customers like the new uniforms that our restaurant staff started wearing at the beginning of this month? B: Yes, many customers said our waiters now look stylishly dressed in black shirts and gray aprons, and some even asked where they could buy the same aprons.","t":"A：顧客喜歡我們餐廳員工這個月初開始穿的新制服嗎？ B：喜歡，很多顧客說我們的服務生現在穿著黑襯衫和灰色圍裙，打扮得很【有型】，有些人甚至問哪裡可以買到同款圍裙。"},{"w":"dress well","p":"v.phr.","d":"to wear nice, suitable and attractive clothes","c":"穿著得體；穿得好看","s":"A: Do you have any advice for my brother, who has his first job interview at a large accounting firm in Taipei next Monday? B: He should dress well, arrive fifteen minutes early, and bring extra copies of his résumé, because the interviewers will notice his appearance as soon as he enters the room.","t":"A：我弟弟下週一要去台北一家大型會計師事務所參加他的第一次面試，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：他應該【穿著得體】、提早十五分鐘到，並多帶幾份履歷，因為面試官在他一進房間就會注意到他的外表。"},{"w":"coordinate","p":"v.","d":"to choose clothes or colors that match well together","c":"搭配（服裝、顏色）","s":"A: I bought a new green jacket for the company photo next week, but I am not sure what to wear with it. B: Try to coordinate it with a cream shirt and brown shoes, because those colors look natural together and will look good in the group picture outside the office.","t":"A：我為了下週的公司合照買了一件新的綠色夾克，但我不確定該搭配什麼。 B：試著用米色襯衫和棕色鞋子來【搭配】它，因為這些顏色放在一起看起來很自然，在辦公室外拍團體照時也會很好看。"},{"w":"accessorize","p":"v.","d":"to add things like jewelry, belts or scarves to make clothes look better","c":"用配件搭配；佩戴飾品","s":"A: I only packed one black dress for the three-day business trip to Singapore, so how can I make it look different every evening? B: You can accessorize it with a bright scarf one night, gold earrings the next, and a colorful belt on the last evening, and nobody will notice.","t":"A：去新加坡三天的出差我只帶了一件黑色洋裝，我要怎麼讓它每天晚上看起來都不一樣？ B：你可以第一晚用鮮豔的圍巾、第二晚用金耳環、最後一晚用彩色腰帶來【搭配】它，沒有人會發現的。"}]},{"unit":140,"theme":"Festival 節慶","cards":[{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a special event or party held because something good has happened","c":"慶祝；慶祝活動","s":"A: Why is the office kitchen full of balloons and boxes of cake this afternoon, and why did the manager ask everyone to stop work at four? B: The company won its biggest contract of the year last week, so the boss is holding a small celebration for the whole sales team before the long weekend begins.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室的茶水間今天下午擺滿了氣球和一盒盒蛋糕，而且經理為什麼要大家四點停止工作？ B：公司上週贏得了今年最大的一份合約，所以老闆要在長週末開始前為整個業務團隊舉辦一場小型【慶祝會】。"},{"w":"parade","p":"n.","d":"a public event in which people walk or ride through the streets to celebrate something","c":"遊行","s":"A: Why are the buses taking a different route through the city center this Saturday morning, and will the shops on Main Street still be open? B: The city is holding a big parade with marching bands and decorated trucks along Main Street from nine to noon, so the road will be closed, but most shops will open as usual.","t":"A：為什麼這週六早上公車要改道穿過市中心，而且主街上的商店還會營業嗎？ B：市政府從九點到中午要在主街上舉辦一場盛大的【遊行】，有樂隊和裝飾過的卡車，所以道路會封閉，不過大部分商店還是會照常營業。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal event held to mark an important occasion","c":"典禮；儀式","s":"A: Will the new factory start production on Monday, or do we still need to wait for the final safety check from the government inspectors? B: Production starts on Monday, but first there will be a short opening ceremony at eight o'clock, where the mayor will cut a red ribbon and the CEO will thank all the workers.","t":"A：新工廠星期一會開始生產嗎？還是我們仍然要等政府檢查員做最後的安全檢查？ B：星期一會開始生產，不過八點會先舉行一場簡短的開幕【典禮】，市長會剪綵，執行長也會感謝所有員工。"},{"w":"carnival","p":"n.","d":"a large public festival with music, dancing and parades in the streets","c":"嘉年華會；狂歡節","s":"A: Why did the hotel ask us to book our rooms for the sales trip to Brazil so early, even though the meeting isn't until late February? B: That week the whole city holds a famous carnival with street parties, music and huge numbers of visitors, so hotel rooms get very expensive and sell out months before.","t":"A：為什麼飯店要我們這麼早就預訂巴西業務出差的房間，明明會議要到二月底才舉行？ B：那一週整座城市會舉辦著名的【嘉年華會】，有街頭派對、音樂和大批遊客，所以飯店房間會變得非常貴，而且好幾個月前就會被訂光。"},{"w":"fair","p":"n.","d":"a large event where companies show and sell their products, or an outdoor event with games and food","c":"展覽會；市集；園遊會","s":"A: Where did you find so many new suppliers for our gift shop this year, and how did you manage to meet them all in only two days? B: I went to the big trade fair at the convention center last month, where hundreds of companies showed their products, so I could compare prices and talk to everyone in one place.","t":"A：你今年是在哪裡為我們的禮品店找到這麼多新供應商的？你又是怎麼在短短兩天內見到他們所有人的？ B：我上個月去了會展中心的大型貿易【展覽會】，那裡有數百家公司展示他們的產品，所以我能在同一個地方比較價格並和每個人洽談。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom or belief that has been passed down for a long time","c":"傳統；慣例","s":"A: Why does everyone in the office bring a small gift to the meeting room on the last Friday before the New Year holiday? B: It's a tradition that started when the company first opened twenty years ago, so each person draws a name from a box and gives a present to that coworker to say thank you.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室裡每個人在新年假期前的最後一個星期五都會帶一份小禮物到會議室？ B：這是公司二十年前剛成立時就開始的【傳統】，所以每個人會從箱子裡抽一個名字，然後送禮物給那位同事表示感謝。"},{"w":"cultural","p":"adj.","d":"related to the customs, art and ideas of a group of people","c":"文化的","s":"A: What kind of activities have you planned for the visiting managers from our Japan office during their free afternoon next week? B: Since they're interested in local history, I've booked a cultural tour of the old temple district, where a guide will explain the customs, art and festivals of the area in simple English.","t":"A：下週日本分公司的經理們來訪時，你為他們的空閒下午安排了哪些活動？ B：因為他們對當地歷史很感興趣，我預訂了老廟區的【文化】導覽，導遊會用簡單的英文解說這個地區的習俗、藝術和節慶。"},{"w":"religious","p":"adj.","d":"connected with religion or faith","c":"宗教的；虔誠的","s":"A: Why is the restaurant near our office closed for three days this week, even though it is usually open every day of the year? B: The owner and his family are taking part in an important religious festival at their temple, so they will pray, prepare special food and welcome guests until Thursday evening.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近的餐廳這週要休息三天，明明它平常一年到頭每天都營業？ B：老闆和他的家人要在他們的廟裡參加一場重要的【宗教】節慶，所以他們會祈禱、準備特別的食物並招待客人，直到星期四晚上。"},{"w":"holiday","p":"n.","d":"a day when most people do not work, often to celebrate something","c":"假日；節日","s":"A: Is the warehouse open next Monday, or should I tell our customers that their orders will arrive later than usual? B: Next Monday is a national holiday, so the warehouse will be closed and no trucks will run, which means you should tell customers that their packages will arrive on Tuesday or Wednesday instead.","t":"A：倉庫下週一有開嗎？還是我應該告訴客戶他們的訂單會比平常晚到？ B：下週一是國定【假日】，所以倉庫會關閉，也沒有卡車出車，這表示你應該告訴客戶他們的包裹會改在星期二或星期三送達。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people for a social or special reason","c":"聚會；集會","s":"A: Why did you reserve the large room at the back of the restaurant for Friday night, and how many people are you expecting to come? B: It's a small gathering for our department to welcome the three new engineers, so about twenty people will come for dinner, and the restaurant has agreed to give us a group discount.","t":"A：你為什麼預訂了餐廳後面的大包廂在星期五晚上使用？你預計會有多少人來？ B：這是我們部門為了歡迎三位新工程師而辦的小型【聚會】，所以大約會有二十個人來吃晚餐，而餐廳也同意給我們團體折扣。"},{"w":"crowd","p":"n.","d":"a large number of people in one place","c":"人群；群眾","s":"A: Why are you leaving the office so early to go to the night market festival when it doesn't start until seven o'clock? B: Last year a huge crowd filled the streets by six thirty, and we couldn't even get near the best snack shops, so this time I want to arrive early and find a good spot.","t":"A：夜市節慶七點才開始，你為什麼這麼早就要離開辦公室過去？ B：去年六點半街上就擠滿了一大群【人潮】，我們連最好的小吃店都靠近不了，所以這次我想早點到，找個好位置。"},{"w":"fireworks","p":"n.","d":"small objects that explode in the sky with bright colors and loud noises","c":"煙火","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager say that rooms facing the river cost more on New Year's Eve than on any other night of the year? B: At midnight the city sets off amazing fireworks over the river for fifteen minutes, so guests in those rooms can watch the bright lights from their windows without standing in the cold.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理說面向河邊的房間在跨年夜比一年中任何一晚都貴？ B：午夜時分市政府會在河的上空施放十五分鐘壯觀的【煙火】，所以住在那些房間的客人可以從窗戶欣賞燦爛的光芒，不必站在寒冷的戶外。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"sounds made by voices or instruments in a way that is pleasant to hear","c":"音樂","s":"A: What do you think made the company picnic so much more fun this year than the one we had last spring? B: The planning team hired a local band to play live music all afternoon, so people sang and danced together, and even the shy new staff members joined in and started talking to everyone.","t":"A：你覺得今年公司野餐比去年春天那次有趣這麼多的原因是什麼？ B：籌備小組請了一個當地樂團整個下午現場演奏【音樂】，所以大家一起唱歌跳舞，就連害羞的新同事也加入了，並開始和每個人聊天。"},{"w":"dance","p":"n.","d":"a set of movements done to music","c":"舞蹈；跳舞","s":"A: Why have the young workers in the marketing team been staying in the meeting room after work every evening this month? B: They are practicing a short dance for the company's year-end party, and they want to surprise the managers with their moves, so they meet for an hour each night to rehearse.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊的年輕員工這個月每天晚上下班後都留在會議室裡？ B：他們正在為公司尾牙練習一段簡短的【舞蹈】，想用他們的舞步給主管們一個驚喜，所以他們每晚聚在一起排練一個小時。"},{"w":"costume","p":"n.","d":"special clothes worn to look like someone or something else, often at a festival or show","c":"（表演或節慶的）服裝；戲服","s":"A: Why is Jenny wearing a long red dress and a gold crown at the reception desk this morning instead of her normal uniform? B: The shopping mall is holding a special event for children today, so all the staff were asked to wear a costume from a famous story to make the young visitors smile.","t":"A：為什麼珍妮今天早上在接待櫃台穿著紅色長裙、戴著金色皇冠，而不是她平常的制服？ B：購物中心今天為孩子們舉辦一場特別活動，所以所有員工都被要求穿上著名故事中的【服裝】，讓小朋友們開心。"},{"w":"float","p":"n.","d":"a large decorated vehicle that moves slowly in a parade","c":"（遊行的）花車","s":"A: Why did our company spend so much money on flowers, lights and a large wooden boat this month? B: We are building a float for the city's spring parade, and it will be pulled by a truck along the main road, so thousands of people will see our company's name and logo on it.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司這個月花了這麼多錢在花卉、燈飾和一艘大型木船上？ B：我們正在為市政府的春季遊行製作一輛【花車】，它會由卡車拉著沿主要道路前進，所以會有成千上萬的人看到上面我們公司的名稱和標誌。"},{"w":"food stall","p":"n.","d":"a small table or shop where food is sold, usually outdoors","c":"小吃攤；食物攤位","s":"A: How are you going to sell our new rice crackers to more people before they appear in supermarkets next spring? B: I've rented a small food stall at the weekend night festival near the train station, so thousands of visitors can taste the crackers for free, and we can collect their opinions at the same time.","t":"A：在明年春天我們的新米餅上架超市之前，你打算怎麼把它賣給更多人？ B：我在火車站附近的週末夜間節慶租了一個小型【小吃攤】，讓成千上萬的遊客可以免費試吃米餅，同時我們也能收集他們的意見。"},{"w":"vendor","p":"n.","d":"a person who sells things, often in the street","c":"小販；攤販；賣方","s":"A: Who sold you those delicious grilled corn and sweet potatoes that you shared with the team after the festival last night? B: A friendly street vendor was cooking them beside the temple gate, and since he only charged fifty dollars each, I bought enough for everyone who stayed late to finish the report.","t":"A：昨晚節慶結束後你和團隊分享的那些美味烤玉米和地瓜是跟誰買的？ B：一位親切的街頭【小販】在廟門旁邊烤，而且因為每個只賣五十元，我就買了足夠的份量給每個留下來加班完成報告的人。"},{"w":"feast","p":"n.","d":"a large special meal for many people","c":"盛宴；宴席","s":"A: Why did the hotel kitchen order so much fish, pork, chicken and fruit for tomorrow night's event in the main hall? B: The owner is holding a big feast for two hundred guests to celebrate the hotel's fiftieth birthday, so the chefs will cook twelve dishes and serve them on long tables.","t":"A：為什麼飯店廚房為明晚在大廳的活動訂了這麼多魚、豬肉、雞肉和水果？ B：老闆要為兩百位賓客舉辦一場盛大的【宴席】來慶祝飯店五十週年，所以廚師們會煮十二道菜，擺在長桌上供應。"},{"w":"lantern","p":"n.","d":"a light inside a container made of paper, glass or metal","c":"燈籠；提燈","s":"A: Why is the hotel lobby full of round paper lights in red and yellow, and will they stay up until the end of the month? B: No, they will come down on Sunday night, because they are only for the festival this week, and each guest can write a wish on a paper lantern and hang it near the front desk.","t":"A：為什麼飯店大廳掛滿了紅色和黃色的圓形紙燈，而且會一直掛到月底嗎？ B：不會，它們星期天晚上就會拆下來，因為只是為了這週的節慶，每位客人都可以在紙【燈籠】上寫下願望，然後掛在櫃台附近。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look more attractive by adding things to it","c":"裝飾；佈置","s":"A: What should the new staff do on Friday afternoon to get the office ready for the holiday party with our biggest clients? B: Please ask them to decorate the reception area and the meeting room with flowers, small lights and colored ribbons, so everything looks bright and welcoming when the guests arrive at six.","t":"A：新進員工星期五下午應該做些什麼，讓辦公室為和大客戶的節日派對做好準備？ B：請他們用花、小燈和彩色緞帶【裝飾】接待區和會議室，讓客人六點到達時，一切看起來都明亮又溫馨。"},{"w":"exhibit","p":"v.","d":"to show something to the public, for example in a museum or show","c":"展出；展示","s":"A: Why is the local art museum so busy this week, and why are so many tour buses parked outside the front gate? B: For the city's arts festival, the museum will exhibit more than one hundred paintings by young local artists until Sunday, so schools and travel agencies are bringing large groups to see them.","t":"A：為什麼當地美術館這週這麼忙，而且為什麼有這麼多遊覽車停在大門外？ B：為了配合城市藝術節，美術館到星期天為止會【展出】一百多幅當地年輕藝術家的畫作，所以學校和旅行社都帶大批團體來參觀。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of singing, dancing, playing music or acting in front of people","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: Did you enjoy the opening night of the music festival, or was it too busy to see the stage from your seats? B: We had great seats near the front, and the singers gave a wonderful performance that lasted almost two hours, so everyone in our group stood up and clapped at the end.","t":"A：你喜歡音樂節的開幕夜嗎？還是人太多，從你們的座位看不到舞台？ B：我們的座位很好，靠近前面，歌手們帶來了一場將近兩小時的精彩【演出】，所以結束時我們團裡的每個人都站起來鼓掌。"},{"w":"outdoor","p":"adj.","d":"happening or used outside, not in a building","c":"戶外的；露天的","s":"A: Where are we having the company's summer festival this year, and should I bring an umbrella in case it rains? B: We're having it in the big park by the river because it's an outdoor event with games and food, so you should bring an umbrella and some sunscreen, just in case the weather changes.","t":"A：今年公司的夏日慶典在哪裡舉辦？我要不要帶把傘以防下雨？ B：我們會在河邊的大公園舉辦，因為這是有遊戲和食物的【戶外】活動，所以你應該帶把傘和一些防曬乳，以防天氣變化。"},{"w":"annual","p":"adj.","d":"happening once every year","c":"一年一度的；每年的","s":"A: Why is the hotel fully booked for the second weekend of October, even though it is not a holiday period? B: The town holds its annual wine festival that weekend, and it has become very famous over the past thirty years, so visitors from all over the country book rooms several months in advance.","t":"A：為什麼飯店十月的第二個週末全部客滿，明明那不是假期？ B：小鎮那個週末會舉辦【一年一度的】葡萄酒節，而且過去三十年來這個節慶變得非常有名，所以全國各地的遊客都會提前好幾個月訂房。"},{"w":"seasonal","p":"adj.","d":"happening or needed only during a particular time of year","c":"季節性的；季節的","s":"A: Why is the café near the station hiring five extra workers this month when it usually has only three staff members? B: The town's winter festival brings thousands of tourists every December, so the owner needs some seasonal workers to help serve hot drinks and snacks until the busy period ends in January.","t":"A：為什麼車站附近的咖啡廳這個月要多雇五名員工，明明平常只有三名員工？ B：小鎮的冬季節慶每年十二月都會吸引數千名遊客，所以老闆需要一些【季節性】員工幫忙供應熱飲和點心，直到一月忙碌期結束。"},{"w":"lively","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy, activity and excitement","c":"熱鬧的；活潑的","s":"A: How was the street festival in the old part of town last Saturday night, and would you recommend it to our visiting clients? B: Yes, it was very lively, with bands playing on every corner, children laughing and people chatting at busy tables, so our clients would really enjoy the friendly and exciting atmosphere.","t":"A：上週六晚上老城區的街頭節慶怎麼樣？你會推薦給來訪的客戶嗎？ B：會，那裡非常【熱鬧】，每個街角都有樂團演奏，孩子們笑著，人們在擠滿人的桌邊聊天，所以我們的客戶一定會很喜歡那種友善又令人興奮的氣氛。"},{"w":"colorful","p":"adj.","d":"having many bright colors","c":"色彩繽紛的；豐富多彩的","s":"A: Why did the designer choose bright red, yellow and blue for the new poster, when our company usually uses only gray and white? B: The poster is for the spring festival, and she wanted a happy, colorful design that people would notice from far away, so the event would attract more families and young visitors.","t":"A：為什麼設計師在新海報上選用鮮紅、黃和藍色，明明我們公司平常只用灰色和白色？ B：這張海報是為了春季節慶，她想要一個快樂又【色彩繽紛】的設計，讓人從遠處就能注意到，好讓活動吸引更多家庭和年輕遊客。"},{"w":"joyful","p":"adj.","d":"very happy, or making people feel very happy","c":"歡欣的；令人高興的","s":"A: How did the staff feel when the manager announced that everyone would get an extra week of holiday after the busy festival season? B: The whole office became very joyful, and people started clapping, laughing and hugging each other, because they had worked long hours for months and really needed a rest.","t":"A：經理宣布忙碌的節慶旺季過後每個人都能多放一週假時，員工們感覺如何？ B：整個辦公室變得非常【歡欣】，大家開始鼓掌、大笑並互相擁抱，因為他們好幾個月都工作很長時間，真的很需要休息。"},{"w":"commemorate","p":"v.","d":"to do something special to remember an important person or event","c":"紀念；慶祝","s":"A: Why is the bank putting up a large stone sign in front of its main office downtown next month? B: The bank wants to commemorate its one hundredth year in business, so the sign will show the date it first opened, and there will also be a short speech and a free concert for customers.","t":"A：為什麼銀行下個月要在市中心總行前面立一塊大石碑？ B：銀行想要【紀念】營業一百週年，所以石碑上會刻上它首次開業的日期，而且還會有簡短的致詞和為顧客舉辦的免費音樂會。"},{"w":"ritual","p":"n.","d":"a set of actions always done in the same way, often for religious or special reasons","c":"儀式；例行公事","s":"A: Why does the team leader always ring a small bell and offer fruit at the front door before a new shop opens? B: It's an old ritual in this area that people believe brings good luck and many customers, so he follows the same steps every time, even though he knows some younger staff find it unusual.","t":"A：為什麼組長在新店開幕前總是在門口搖小鈴並供奉水果？ B：這是這個地區的一種古老【儀式】，人們相信它能帶來好運和許多顧客，所以他每次都按照同樣的步驟進行，即使他知道有些年輕員工覺得這很不尋常。"},{"w":"ticket","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper or a code that lets you enter an event or travel","c":"票；門票","s":"A: How can our clients from Singapore get into the jazz festival on Saturday night, since it's their first time in the city? B: I've already bought a ticket for each of them online, so they only need to show the code on their phones at the front gate, and a staff member will take them to their seats.","t":"A：我們來自新加坡的客戶星期六晚上要怎麼進入爵士音樂節？這是他們第一次來這座城市。 B：我已經在網路上幫他們每人買了一張【門票】，所以他們只要在大門口出示手機上的條碼，工作人員就會帶他們到座位。"},{"w":"host","p":"v.","d":"to organize an event and welcome the guests or people who take part","c":"主辦；主持；招待","s":"A: Why is the city building a new stage and hundreds of extra parking spaces near the harbor this year? B: The city will host an international music festival next summer, and organizers expect more than fifty thousand visitors over three days, so it needs much more space for performers, cars and buses.","t":"A：為什麼市政府今年要在港口附近興建新舞台和數百個額外的停車位？ B：市政府明年夏天將【主辦】一場國際音樂節，主辦單位預計三天內會有超過五萬名遊客，所以需要更多空間給表演者、汽車和巴士。"},{"w":"tourist","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels to a place for fun","c":"觀光客；遊客","s":"A: Why does the information center near the train station stay open until ten o'clock at night during the lantern festival? B: Every tourist who arrives late needs maps, bus times and hotel information, so the city keeps the center open longer to help visitors from other countries find their way around safely.","t":"A：為什麼火車站附近的旅客服務中心在燈會期間營業到晚上十點？ B：每位晚到的【觀光客】都需要地圖、公車時刻和飯店資訊，所以市政府延長服務中心的營業時間，幫助來自其他國家的訪客安全地找到路。"}]},{"unit":141,"theme":"Fish 魚","cards":[{"w":"essential","p":"adj.","d":"very important and necessary","c":"必要的；不可或缺的","s":"A: Why does the new seafood restaurant downtown send its kitchen staff to a two-day training course before they start working with the fresh fish? B: Knowing how to clean and cut fish safely is essential for the job, so the owner wants every new cook to learn the right skills before the restaurant opens next month.","t":"A：為什麼市中心那家新的海鮮餐廳要讓廚房員工在開始處理新鮮魚貨前，先去上兩天的訓練課程？ B：懂得如何安全地清理和切魚是這份工作【不可或缺的】，所以老闆希望每位新廚師在下個月餐廳開幕前學會正確的技巧。"},{"w":"lauded","p":"adj.","d":"highly praised by many people","c":"備受讚揚的；廣受好評的","s":"A: Why is it so hard to get a table at the little fish restaurant near the harbor, even on a rainy Tuesday night in the middle of winter? B: Its head chef is widely lauded for his grilled salmon, and since a famous food magazine wrote about him last month, people have been booking tables weeks in advance.","t":"A：為什麼港口附近那家小魚料理餐廳這麼難訂到位子，連冬天下雨的星期二晚上都一樣？ B：它的主廚以烤鮭魚廣受【讚揚】，而且自從上個月一本知名美食雜誌報導他之後，大家都提前好幾週訂位。"},{"w":"nutrient","p":"n.","d":"a substance in food that helps living things grow and stay healthy","c":"營養素；養分","s":"A: Why did the company nurse put a poster about eating more fish next to the coffee machine in the staff kitchen last week? B: She says fish contains an important nutrient called omega-3 that helps the heart and brain, and many of our office workers eat too much fast food during busy weeks.","t":"A：為什麼公司護理師上週在員工茶水間的咖啡機旁邊貼了一張多吃魚的海報？ B：她說魚含有一種叫做 Omega-3 的重要【營養素】，有助於心臟和大腦，而我們很多上班族在忙碌的時候都吃太多速食了。"},{"w":"protein","p":"n.","d":"a substance in food such as meat, fish and eggs that helps your body grow and repair itself","c":"蛋白質","s":"A: Why did the fitness center near our office start selling grilled tuna salads at the front desk instead of the sweet snacks it used to offer? B: Many members asked for healthier meals after their workouts, and fish is a great source of protein that helps their muscles recover without adding much fat.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近的健身中心開始在櫃檯賣烤鮪魚沙拉，而不是以前賣的甜食？ B：很多會員要求在運動後吃更健康的餐點，而魚是很好的【蛋白質】來源，能幫助肌肉恢復，又不會增加太多脂肪。"},{"w":"mineral","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance such as iron or calcium that the body needs","c":"礦物質","s":"A: Why does the dietitian at the hospital cafeteria recommend the small fried fish that are served with their bones still in them? B: When you eat the soft bones, you get calcium, which is a mineral that keeps your bones and teeth strong, so it is especially good for older patients.","t":"A：為什麼醫院餐廳的營養師推薦那種連骨頭一起上桌的炸小魚？ B：吃下柔軟的魚骨時，你會攝取到鈣，那是一種能讓骨骼和牙齒保持強壯的【礦物質】，所以對年長的病人特別好。"},{"w":"component","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that something is made of","c":"組成部分；成分","s":"A: Why has the frozen food company asked the factory to stop production of its new fish burger until the end of the month? B: The laboratory found that one component of the sauce, a type of imported oil, did not meet the safety standard, so they need to find another supplier first.","t":"A：為什麼冷凍食品公司要求工廠在月底之前暫停生產新的魚堡？ B：實驗室發現醬料的其中一種【成分】，也就是一種進口油，不符合安全標準，所以他們必須先找到另一家供應商。"},{"w":"situate","p":"v.","d":"to build or put something in a particular place","c":"使位於；把……設置在","s":"A: Where is the restaurant group planning to open its new seafood restaurant, and why did the managers spend so long looking at different locations? B: They decided to situate it right next to the fishing port, so the chefs can buy fish directly from the boats every morning and customers can enjoy a view of the sea.","t":"A：餐飲集團打算在哪裡開新的海鮮餐廳？為什麼經理們花了那麼久時間看不同的地點？ B：他們決定把它【設在】漁港旁邊，這樣廚師每天早上就能直接向漁船買魚，顧客也能欣賞海景。"},{"w":"tiny","p":"adj.","d":"very small","c":"極小的；微小的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the cooking class at the community center last Saturday, or was it too difficult for beginners like us? B: It was fun, but removing the tiny bones from the fish took me almost twenty minutes, because they were so thin that I could hardly see them without my glasses.","t":"A：你喜歡上週六在社區中心上的烹飪課嗎？還是對我們這種初學者來說太難了？ B：很好玩，但把魚身上那些【細小的】刺挑出來花了我將近二十分鐘，因為它們細到我不戴眼鏡幾乎看不見。"},{"w":"plenty of","p":"phr.","d":"a lot of; more than enough","c":"很多的；充足的","s":"A: Should we order more food for the department's year-end party, or do you think the seafood buffet will be enough for forty people? B: I think we'll be fine, because the hotel will prepare plenty of grilled fish, shrimp and vegetables, and they can bring out extra dishes quickly if we start running low.","t":"A：我們應該為部門的尾牙多訂一些食物嗎？還是你覺得海鮮自助餐夠四十個人吃？ B：我想應該沒問題，因為飯店會準備【大量的】烤魚、蝦子和蔬菜，而且如果快不夠了，他們也能很快端出更多菜。"},{"w":"in spite of","p":"prep.","d":"without being stopped by something; although something happened","c":"儘管；不顧","s":"A: Did the fishing boat tour that our company booked for the overseas clients still go ahead on Sunday morning? B: Yes, in spite of the strong wind and light rain, the captain said the sea was safe enough, and our clients enjoyed catching their own fish and taking photos of the coast.","t":"A：我們公司幫海外客戶預訂的釣魚船之旅，星期天早上還有照常出發嗎？ B：有，【儘管】風很大又下著小雨，船長說海況夠安全，客戶們都很享受自己釣魚和拍攝海岸的照片。"},{"w":"hectic","p":"adj.","d":"very busy and full of activity","c":"忙亂的；繁忙的","s":"A: How was your first week working at the fish market, and are you getting used to starting work so early in the morning? B: It has been really hectic, because restaurant owners arrive at four o'clock and everyone wants the freshest fish at the same time, but I'm learning to work faster.","t":"A：你在魚市場工作的第一週怎麼樣？習慣那麼早開始上班了嗎？ B：真的很【忙亂】，因為餐廳老闆們四點就到了，每個人都想同時買到最新鮮的魚，不過我正在學著加快速度。"},{"w":"enjoyable","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant and fun","c":"愉快的；令人愉悅的","s":"A: How did the team-building day at the lake go, and did the new employees from the Tokyo office join in the activities? B: It was very enjoyable, because everyone tried fishing for the first time, and later we cooked what we caught together, so people from both offices got to know each other well.","t":"A：在湖邊舉辦的團隊建立日進行得如何？東京辦公室來的新員工有參加活動嗎？ B：非常【愉快】，因為大家都第一次嘗試釣魚，之後我們一起把釣到的魚煮來吃，所以兩個辦公室的人都彼此熟悉了。"},{"w":"vegan","p":"adj.","d":"not using or eating any food that comes from animals","c":"純素的","s":"A: What should we serve at the lunch meeting with our new partners, since the restaurant we chose is famous mostly for its fish dishes? B: Let's ask the chef to prepare a few vegan dishes as well, because two of the partners don't eat meat, fish, eggs or milk, and we want everyone to feel welcome.","t":"A：我們和新合作夥伴的午餐會議要點什麼？我們選的那家餐廳主要以魚料理出名。 B：我們也請主廚準備幾道【純素】料理吧，因為有兩位合作夥伴不吃肉、魚、蛋或奶製品，我們希望每個人都覺得受到歡迎。"},{"w":"find time","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make time for something although you are busy","c":"抽出時間","s":"A: You have been working late every night this month, so how do you still manage to go fishing with your father on weekends? B: I always try to find time for it, even during busy seasons, because sitting by the river with him helps me relax and forget about my work for a few hours.","t":"A：你這個月每天晚上都加班，那你週末怎麼還能陪你爸爸去釣魚？ B：即使在忙碌的旺季，我也總是盡量【抽出時間】去，因為和他一起坐在河邊能幫助我放鬆，暫時忘掉工作幾個小時。"},{"w":"cup of tea","p":"n.phr.","d":"(not my cup of tea) something you like or enjoy","c":"喜歡的事物；（某人的）菜","s":"A: Are you coming on the deep-sea fishing trip that the sales department has planned for next Saturday, or do you have other plans? B: Actually, spending eight hours on a small boat isn't really my cup of tea, because I get seasick easily, so I'll join everyone for the seafood dinner afterwards instead.","t":"A：你會參加業務部安排在下週六的深海釣魚之旅嗎？還是你有其他計畫？ B：其實在小船上待八個小時真的不是我【喜歡的事】，因為我很容易暈船，所以我會改成之後跟大家一起去吃海鮮晚餐。"},{"w":"delectably","p":"adv.","d":"in a very tasty or delicious way","c":"美味地；可口地","s":"A: Why did the food critic give the new seafood restaurant on Harbor Street five stars in this morning's newspaper? B: She wrote that the chef's sea bass was delectably tender and juicy, and that the service was friendly, so she recommended it to anyone looking for a special dinner with clients or family.","t":"A：為什麼那位美食評論家在今天早上的報紙上給港口街那家新海鮮餐廳五顆星？ B：她寫說主廚的鱸魚軟嫩多汁、【美味可口】，服務也很親切，所以推薦給任何想和客戶或家人吃一頓特別晚餐的人。"},{"w":"inexplicable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to explain or understand","c":"無法解釋的；費解的","s":"A: Why did the aquarium close its large fish tank to visitors for the whole weekend, right in the middle of the school holiday? B: Several fish became sick for some inexplicable reason, and the staff couldn't find the cause, so they called in an expert to test the water and check every animal carefully.","t":"A：為什麼水族館在學校放假期間，整個週末都不讓遊客參觀大型魚缸？ B：有幾條魚因為某種【無法解釋的】原因生病了，工作人員找不到原因，所以請了一位專家來檢測水質並仔細檢查每隻動物。"},{"w":"bay","p":"n.","d":"a part of the sea that is partly surrounded by land","c":"海灣","s":"A: Where are we taking the visitors from the Singapore office for dinner on Friday evening after the factory tour? B: I've booked a table at a restaurant beside the bay, where the water is calm and the boats come in at sunset, so they can enjoy fresh seafood and a beautiful view.","t":"A：星期五傍晚參觀完工廠後，我們要帶新加坡辦公室的訪客去哪裡吃晚餐？ B：我在【海灣】旁邊的一家餐廳訂了位，那裡水面平靜，夕陽時分漁船會進港，所以他們可以享用新鮮海鮮和美麗的景色。"},{"w":"suitable","p":"adj.","d":"right or good for a particular person, purpose or situation","c":"適合的；適當的","s":"A: Why did the event planner reject the riverside park as the place for our company's family fishing day in May? B: She said it wasn't suitable for young children, because the river bank is steep and slippery, so she found a quiet lake with a wooden platform and safety fences instead.","t":"A：為什麼活動企劃人員否決了把河濱公園當作我們公司五月家庭釣魚日的場地？ B：她說那裡不【適合】小孩子，因為河岸又陡又滑，所以她改找了一個有木製平台和安全圍欄的安靜湖泊。"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to make pain, stress or a problem less bad","c":"減輕；緩解","s":"A: Why do you keep a small fish tank on your desk when the office is already so crowded with files and computers? B: Watching the fish swim slowly helps to relieve my stress during long, busy afternoons, and several colleagues say it calms them down too when they stop by to chat.","t":"A：辦公室已經堆滿了文件和電腦，為什麼你還在桌上放一個小魚缸？ B：在漫長忙碌的下午看著魚慢慢游，可以幫助【減輕】我的壓力，而且好幾位同事順道過來聊天時也說這讓他們平靜下來。"},{"w":"netting","p":"n.","d":"material made of strings or wires tied together with spaces between them","c":"網子；網狀物","s":"A: Why did the fish farm by the coast have to close for three days last week, and did it lose a lot of money? B: A storm tore the netting around the fish pens, so hundreds of fish escaped into the sea, and the workers needed time to repair everything before they could restart operations.","t":"A：為什麼海邊那座養魚場上週必須關閉三天？他們損失很多錢嗎？ B：一場暴風雨扯破了魚欄周圍的【網子】，數百條魚逃到海裡，工人們需要時間把一切修好才能恢復營運。"},{"w":"hatch","p":"v.","d":"(of a baby animal) to come out of an egg","c":"孵化","s":"A: Why are the scientists at the river research center working such long hours this month, even on weekends and public holidays? B: They are waiting for thousands of salmon eggs to hatch, and they must check the water temperature every few hours so that the baby fish survive and can be released into the river.","t":"A：為什麼河川研究中心的科學家這個月工作時間這麼長，連週末和國定假日都在上班？ B：他們正在等待數千顆鮭魚卵【孵化】，而且必須每隔幾小時檢查一次水溫，這樣小魚才能存活並被放流到河裡。"},{"w":"angling","p":"n.","d":"the sport or activity of catching fish with a rod and line","c":"垂釣；釣魚","s":"A: Why is the small hotel by the lake suddenly so popular with business travelers, even though it is far from the city? B: It offers angling lessons on the lake every evening, so guests can relax with a fishing rod after their meetings, and the hotel kitchen will even cook whatever they catch.","t":"A：湖邊那家小旅館雖然離市區很遠，為什麼突然在商務旅客之間這麼受歡迎？ B：它每天傍晚在湖上提供【垂釣】課程，所以客人開完會後可以拿著釣竿放鬆一下，飯店廚房甚至會把他們釣到的魚煮來吃。"},{"w":"angler","p":"n.","d":"a person who catches fish as a hobby","c":"釣客；垂釣者","s":"A: Why did the city council put new signs and rubbish bins along the river path near our office building last month? B: The river has become very popular, and on weekends you can see an angler at almost every corner of the path from early morning, but some of them left plastic bags and old fishing lines behind.","t":"A：為什麼市議會上個月在我們辦公大樓附近的河濱步道設置了新的告示牌和垃圾桶？ B：這條河變得很熱門，週末從一大早開始，步道幾乎每個角落都能看到【釣客】，但有些人留下了塑膠袋和舊釣線。"},{"w":"fanatic","p":"n.","d":"a person who is extremely interested in an activity","c":"狂熱者；迷","s":"A: Why does Mr. Lin from the accounting department always take his vacation in early October, even when the office is busy? B: He is a real fishing fanatic, and October is the best month to catch tuna off the east coast, so he plans his whole year around that trip and never misses it.","t":"A：為什麼會計部的林先生總是在十月初休假，即使辦公室很忙也一樣？ B：他是個不折不扣的釣魚【狂熱者】，而十月是在東海岸外海釣鮪魚最好的月份，所以他整年都圍繞著那趟旅程做計畫，從來不錯過。"},{"w":"thrill","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of excitement and pleasure","c":"興奮；刺激；快感","s":"A: Why do so many of our customers book the early-morning sea fishing tour, even though it starts at five o'clock and costs quite a lot? B: They love the thrill of feeling a big fish pull hard on the line, and many of them say it is the most exciting part of their whole holiday.","t":"A：為什麼我們有這麼多顧客預訂清晨的海釣行程，即使它五點就開始而且價格不便宜？ B：他們喜歡感覺到大魚用力拉扯釣線時的那種【刺激感】，很多人說那是整個假期中最令人興奮的部分。"},{"w":"pastime","p":"n.","d":"something you do for fun in your free time","c":"消遣；休閒活動","s":"A: What did the retired sales director say he would do with all his free time when he left the company last month? B: He said fishing has always been his favorite pastime, so he bought a small boat and plans to spend his mornings on the lake and his afternoons with his grandchildren.","t":"A：上個月離開公司的退休業務總監說他要怎麼運用所有的空閒時間？ B：他說釣魚一直是他最喜歡的【消遣】，所以他買了一艘小船，打算早上待在湖上，下午陪孫子孫女。"},{"w":"impatient","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to wait calmly","c":"不耐煩的；沒耐心的","s":"A: Why did the customers at table six complain to the manager before their main course had even arrived last night? B: They became impatient after waiting almost an hour for their grilled fish, because the kitchen was short of staff, so the manager apologized and gave them free dessert.","t":"A：為什麼昨晚六號桌的客人在主菜還沒上之前就向經理抱怨？ B：他們等烤魚等了將近一個小時，變得很【不耐煩】，因為廚房人手不足，所以經理道了歉並招待他們免費甜點。"},{"w":"bucket list","p":"n.phr.","d":"a list of things you want to do before you die","c":"人生願望清單","s":"A: Why did your manager take two weeks off to go to Alaska, when she usually only takes short holidays near home? B: Catching a wild salmon in Alaska has been on her bucket list for years, and she finally saved enough money and vacation days to make the dream come true this summer.","t":"A：為什麼你的經理請兩週假去阿拉斯加？她通常只在家附近短暫度假。 B：在阿拉斯加釣到一條野生鮭魚多年來一直在她的【人生願望清單】上，她終於存夠了錢和假期，今年夏天要實現這個夢想。"},{"w":"crucial","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important","c":"至關重要的","s":"A: Why does the seafood company check the temperature of its delivery trucks so often during the hot summer months? B: Keeping the fish cold from the port to the supermarket is crucial, because even a short time in the heat can make it unsafe to eat and damage the company's good reputation.","t":"A：為什麼海鮮公司在炎熱的夏季月份那麼頻繁地檢查送貨卡車的溫度？ B：從港口到超市一路讓魚保持低溫是【至關重要的】，因為即使只在高溫下放一小段時間，也可能讓魚變得不安全，並損害公司的好名聲。"},{"w":"optimal","p":"adj.","d":"the best or most suitable","c":"最佳的；最理想的","s":"A: Why does the fish farm manager check the water in the tanks three times a day, even on Sundays and holidays? B: The fish grow fastest when the water is at the optimal temperature of about twenty degrees, so he adjusts the heaters carefully to keep conditions perfect all year round.","t":"A：為什麼養魚場經理一天檢查三次魚池的水，連星期天和假日也不例外？ B：魚在水溫約二十度這個【最佳】溫度下長得最快，所以他會小心調整加熱器，讓環境全年都保持完美。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way food or a surface feels when you eat or touch it","c":"口感；質地","s":"A: Why did the chef change the cooking method for the cod on the new lunch menu after the staff tasting last Friday? B: Several staff members said the fish was dry and hard, so he now steams it gently to give it a softer texture that melts in your mouth.","t":"A：為什麼主廚在上週五員工試吃後，改變了新午餐菜單上鱈魚的烹調方式？ B：有幾位員工說魚又乾又硬，所以他現在用小火慢蒸，讓它有入口即化、更柔軟的【口感】。"},{"w":"fussy","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to please, especially about food","c":"挑剔的；難取悅的","s":"A: Why did you choose a simple grilled fish restaurant for the dinner with our Japanese clients instead of the fancy French one downtown? B: Their director is quite fussy about food and only eats fresh, plainly cooked dishes, so I thought a place famous for simple seafood would make him happy.","t":"A：為什麼你為了和日本客戶的晚餐選了一家簡單的烤魚餐廳，而不是市中心那家高級法式餐廳？ B：他們的總監對食物相當【挑剔】，只吃新鮮、簡單烹調的料理，所以我想一家以簡單海鮮出名的餐廳會讓他開心。"},{"w":"elusive","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to find, catch or achieve","c":"難以捉摸的；難找到的","s":"A: Why did the TV crew stay at the remote fishing village for almost a month to film the new nature documentary? B: They were trying to film a rare, elusive fish that only comes near the surface a few times a year, so they had to wait patiently until the conditions were right.","t":"A：為什麼電視團隊在偏遠的漁村待了將近一個月拍攝新的自然紀錄片？ B：他們想拍一種稀有又【難以捉摸的】魚，牠一年只會浮到水面附近幾次，所以他們必須耐心等到條件合適。"},{"w":"stalk","p":"v.","d":"to follow an animal quietly in order to catch it","c":"悄悄跟蹤；潛近（獵物）","s":"A: What was the most interesting part of the nature documentary that the marketing team watched during the lunch break yesterday? B: It showed a large bird that can stalk fish in shallow water for several minutes, moving so slowly and quietly that the fish never notice it until it is too late.","t":"A：行銷團隊昨天午休時看的自然紀錄片，最有趣的部分是什麼？ B：它介紹了一種大型鳥類，能在淺水中【悄悄跟蹤】魚好幾分鐘，動作又慢又安靜，魚直到為時已晚才察覺牠。"},{"w":"marvelous","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; wonderful","c":"極好的；令人驚嘆的","s":"A: How was the welcome dinner that the hotel prepared for the conference speakers on the first evening of the event? B: It was marvelous, because the chef served fresh lobster, grilled fish and local vegetables, and all the speakers said it was the best meal they had eaten during their trip.","t":"A：飯店在活動第一天晚上為會議講者準備的歡迎晚宴怎麼樣？ B：非常【棒】，因為主廚上了新鮮龍蝦、烤魚和在地蔬菜，所有講者都說那是他們這趟旅程中吃過最好的一餐。"},{"w":"dismay","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry, disappointment and shock","c":"沮喪；驚愕；失望","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner look so upset when she came back from the fish market early this morning? B: To her dismay, the price of fresh tuna had almost doubled because of the storm last week, so she now has to decide whether to raise menu prices or remove some dishes.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳老闆今天一大早從魚市場回來時看起來那麼難過？ B：令她【沮喪】的是，因為上週的暴風雨，新鮮鮪魚的價格幾乎漲了一倍，所以她現在必須決定要調漲菜單價格還是撤掉一些菜色。"}]},{"unit":142,"theme":"Fishing 釣魚","cards":[{"w":"fish","p":"v.","d":"to try to catch fish","c":"釣魚；捕魚","s":"A: What are you and the other managers planning to do during the company retreat at the lake resort next weekend? B: Most of us want to rent a small boat early on Saturday morning and fish for trout for a few hours, and then we will cook lunch together near the water.","t":"A：你和其他經理們打算在下週末湖邊度假村的公司旅遊期間做什麼？ B：我們大多數人想在星期六一大早租一艘小船，【釣】幾個小時的鱒魚，然後一起在水邊煮午餐。"},{"w":"angler","p":"n.","d":"a person who catches fish with a rod as a hobby","c":"釣客；垂釣者","s":"A: Why is the small hotel near the river always fully booked in early spring, even though it is not a famous tourist area? B: Every March, almost every serious angler in the region comes to try the clear water there, so the owner has to take reservations several months in advance.","t":"A：為什麼河邊那家小旅館每年早春總是客滿，即使那裡並不是有名的觀光區？ B：每年三月，這個地區幾乎每位認真的【釣客】都會來那裡試試清澈的河水，所以老闆必須提前好幾個月接受訂房。"},{"w":"rod","p":"n.","d":"a long thin stick with a line, used for catching fish","c":"釣竿","s":"A: Have you decided what to buy for Mr. Chen's retirement gift, since he told everyone he plans to spend more time at the lake? B: Yes, the team agreed to buy him a light carbon fishing rod from the sports shop downtown, and we will also include a card signed by everyone in the office.","t":"A：你們決定好要買什麼送陳先生當退休禮物了嗎？他跟大家說他打算花更多時間待在湖邊。 B：決定了，團隊同意從市中心的運動用品店買一支輕量碳纖維【釣竿】給他，我們也會附上一張辦公室每個人都簽了名的卡片。"},{"w":"reel","p":"n.","d":"a round device on a fishing rod that winds the line","c":"捲線器","s":"A: Why did the customer bring his fishing equipment back to the store only two days after he bought it from us? B: He said the reel made a strange noise and would not wind the line in smoothly, so I checked it, found a broken part, and gave him a new one right away.","t":"A：為什麼那位顧客在跟我們買了釣具才兩天就拿回店裡？ B：他說【捲線器】發出奇怪的聲音，而且無法順暢地收線，所以我檢查了一下，發現有個零件壞了，就立刻換了一個新的給他。"},{"w":"line","p":"n.","d":"a thin, strong string used for fishing","c":"釣線","s":"A: Why didn't you bring home any fish yesterday when you said the river was full of big ones at this time of year? B: I had one large carp on my hook for nearly ten minutes, but the line was too thin and it suddenly broke just before I could pull the fish onto the bank.","t":"A：你不是說每年這個時候河裡都是大魚嗎？為什麼你昨天一條魚都沒帶回家？ B：我的魚鉤上鉤住一條大鯉魚將近十分鐘，但是【釣線】太細了，就在我快把魚拉上岸之前突然斷了。"},{"w":"hook","p":"n.","d":"a small curved piece of metal that catches the fish","c":"魚鉤","s":"A: What should the new staff at our outdoor shop tell children who want to try fishing at the pond for the first time? B: They should explain that the sharp metal hook can easily hurt small fingers, so an adult must always help put the bait on and take the fish off safely.","t":"A：我們戶外用品店的新員工應該如何告訴第一次想在池塘釣魚的孩子們？ B：他們應該說明尖銳的金屬【魚鉤】很容易刺傷小手指，所以一定要由大人幫忙裝上魚餌並安全地取下魚。"},{"w":"bait","p":"n.","d":"food put on a hook to attract fish","c":"魚餌；誘餌","s":"A: Why did the tour guide stop at the small shop beside the harbor before taking our group out on the fishing boat? B: He needed to buy fresh shrimp and worms for bait, because he said the fish in this bay only bite when the food on the hook smells natural and fresh.","t":"A：為什麼導遊在帶我們這團搭釣魚船出海之前，先在港邊的小店停了一下？ B：他需要買新鮮的蝦子和蟲來當【魚餌】，因為他說這個海灣的魚只有在鉤上的食物聞起來自然又新鮮時才會咬餌。"},{"w":"lure","p":"n.","d":"an artificial object that looks like food, used to attract fish","c":"假餌；擬餌","s":"A: Our customers keep asking about the bright plastic fish in the display case near the front door, so what exactly are they used for? B: Each one is a lure that moves like a small injured fish in the water, so bigger fish attack it, and anglers like them because they never need live worms.","t":"A：我們的顧客一直問起前門附近展示櫃裡那些鮮豔的塑膠魚，它們到底是做什麼用的？ B：每一個都是【假餌】，在水裡會像一條受傷的小魚一樣游動，所以大魚會攻擊它，釣客喜歡它們是因為完全不需要用活的蟲。"},{"w":"net","p":"n.","d":"a material with holes, used to catch or lift fish","c":"網；漁網","s":"A: How do the workers at the fish farm move hundreds of fish from one pond to another without hurting them? B: Two workers hold a large soft net at each end and slowly walk through the shallow water, and then they lift the fish into a tank on the truck very gently.","t":"A：養魚場的工人如何在不傷害魚的情況下，把數百條魚從一個池塘移到另一個池塘？ B：兩位工人各拿著一張柔軟大【網】的一端，慢慢走過淺水，然後非常輕柔地把魚撈進卡車上的水箱裡。"},{"w":"tackle","p":"n.","d":"all the equipment used for fishing","c":"釣具","s":"A: Where should I put all the rods, boxes of hooks, and other equipment after our team-building fishing trip ends this afternoon? B: Please store the tackle in the gray cabinet in the warehouse, and make sure everything is dry first, because the metal parts can rust quickly if they stay wet.","t":"A：今天下午團隊建立釣魚活動結束後，我應該把所有的釣竿、魚鉤盒和其他裝備放在哪裡？ B：請把【釣具】收進倉庫的灰色櫃子裡，並先確定所有東西都是乾的，因為金屬零件如果一直潮濕的話很快就會生鏽。"},{"w":"boat","p":"n.","d":"a small vehicle that travels on water","c":"船；小船","s":"A: How are the visitors from our Japanese office getting to the island for tomorrow's fishing tour, since there is no bridge? B: The travel agency has booked a small boat with a captain who knows the area well, and it will leave the harbor at seven o'clock and return before dinner.","t":"A：既然沒有橋，我們日本分公司的訪客明天要怎麼去島上參加釣魚行程？ B：旅行社已經預訂了一艘小【船】，船長很熟悉這一帶，船會在七點離港，並在晚餐前回來。"},{"w":"dock","p":"n.","d":"a structure where boats stop so people can get on and off","c":"碼頭","s":"A: Where should the delivery driver leave the boxes of ice and drinks for the fishing tournament this Saturday morning? B: Tell him to bring everything to the wooden dock at the end of Harbor Road, where the boats will be tied up, so the crew can load them directly.","t":"A：送貨司機這個星期六早上應該把釣魚比賽要用的冰塊和飲料箱放在哪裡？ B：告訴他把所有東西送到港口路盡頭的木造【碼頭】，船會停靠在那裡，這樣船員就可以直接搬上船。"},{"w":"river","p":"n.","d":"a long natural flow of water across the land","c":"河；河流","s":"A: Why did the city government close the popular walking path near the old bridge for the whole month? B: Heavy rain last week made the river rise quickly and flood part of the path, so workers need time to repair the damage before families and anglers can safely return.","t":"A：為什麼市政府把舊橋附近那條熱門步道封閉一整個月？ B：上週的大雨讓【河】水迅速上漲並淹沒了部分步道，所以工人需要時間修復損壞，家庭和釣客才能安全地回來。"},{"w":"lake","p":"n.","d":"a large area of water surrounded by land","c":"湖","s":"A: Which location did the HR team finally choose for this year's company picnic, after looking at so many parks? B: They picked the park beside the lake in the mountains, because there is a quiet area for fishing, a big lawn for games, and enough parking for all the employees.","t":"A：人資團隊看了那麼多公園之後，最後選了哪裡作為今年公司野餐的地點？ B：他們選了山中【湖】旁邊的公園，因為那裡有安靜的釣魚區、可以玩遊戲的大草坪，還有足夠讓所有員工停車的位置。"},{"w":"sea","p":"n.","d":"the salt water that covers much of the earth","c":"海；海洋","s":"A: Why was this morning's fishing trip for the visiting clients canceled only an hour before departure? B: The captain checked the latest report and said the sea was too rough because of strong winds, so he decided it was not safe to take the boat out until tomorrow.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上為來訪客戶安排的釣魚行程在出發前一小時被取消？ B：船長查看了最新的報告，說因為強風【海】面太過洶湧，所以他決定明天之前開船出去都不安全。"},{"w":"shore","p":"n.","d":"the land along the edge of a sea or lake","c":"岸邊；海岸","s":"A: Do I need to rent a boat if I want to catch some fish during my business trip to the coast next month? B: Not really, because many people stand on the rocks along the shore near the hotel in the evening, and they often catch plenty of fish without going out on the water.","t":"A：如果我下個月去海邊出差時想釣一些魚，需要租船嗎？ B：其實不用，因為傍晚時有很多人站在飯店附近【岸邊】的岩石上，他們常常不用出海就釣到很多魚。"},{"w":"catch","p":"v.","d":"to take hold of a fish or animal","c":"捕捉；釣到","s":"A: What is the main goal of the fishing competition that our sales department is sponsoring next weekend? B: Each team has four hours to catch as many fish as possible, but they must put most of them back in the lake, and the winners will receive gift cards and a trophy.","t":"A：我們業務部下週末贊助的釣魚比賽主要目標是什麼？ B：每一隊有四個小時盡可能【釣到】越多魚越好，但大部分的魚必須放回湖裡，優勝者將獲得禮物卡和一座獎盃。"},{"w":"cast","p":"v.","d":"to throw a fishing line into the water","c":"拋（竿）；甩出（釣線）","s":"A: How did the instructor at the fishing class help the beginners who kept getting their lines stuck in the trees? B: He showed them how to cast the line with a smooth movement of the wrist instead of swinging the whole arm, and after some practice most of them could reach the middle of the pond.","t":"A：釣魚課的教練是如何幫助那些釣線一直卡在樹上的初學者？ B：他示範如何用手腕平順的動作來【拋】出釣線，而不是揮動整隻手臂，經過一些練習後，大部分的人都能拋到池塘中央。"},{"w":"float","p":"v.","d":"to stay on the surface of water","c":"漂浮","s":"A: Why does the safety officer want every passenger on the fishing tour to wear a life jacket, even good swimmers? B: The jacket helps you float on the surface if you fall into the cold water, so you can stay calm and wait for the crew to pull you back onto the boat.","t":"A：為什麼安全官要求釣魚行程上的每位乘客都穿救生衣，即使是很會游泳的人也一樣？ B：如果你掉進冰冷的水裡，救生衣能幫助你【漂浮】在水面上，這樣你就可以保持冷靜，等待船員把你拉回船上。"},{"w":"sink","p":"v.","d":"to go down below the surface of water","c":"下沉；沉沒","s":"A: Why did you add those small metal weights to the line before you started fishing in the deep part of the lake? B: The weights make the bait sink quickly to the bottom, where the big fish usually feed during the hot afternoon, instead of staying near the surface.","t":"A：為什麼你在湖的深水區開始釣魚前，要在釣線上加那些小金屬重物？ B：這些重物能讓魚餌迅速【沉】到底部，大魚在炎熱的下午通常在那裡覓食，而不是讓魚餌停留在水面附近。"},{"w":"patience","p":"n.","d":"the ability to wait calmly without getting upset","c":"耐心","s":"A: Why does our manager say that fishing is good training for people who want to work in sales? B: She believes that both activities need a lot of patience, because you often wait for hours without any results, and you must stay positive until a customer or a fish finally responds.","t":"A：為什麼我們經理說釣魚對想從事業務工作的人來說是很好的訓練？ B：她認為這兩種活動都需要很大的【耐心】，因為你常常等了好幾個小時都沒有任何結果，而且必須保持正面態度，直到客戶或魚終於有了回應。"},{"w":"calm","p":"adj.","d":"still, without big waves or strong wind","c":"平靜的；風平浪靜的","s":"A: What time do you think we should leave the hotel tomorrow if we want to go fishing before the client meeting? B: We should leave around five thirty, because the water in the bay is usually calm early in the morning, and the wind gets much stronger after nine o'clock.","t":"A：如果我們想在客戶會議前去釣魚，你覺得明天應該幾點離開飯店？ B：我們應該五點半左右出發，因為海灣的水面在清晨通常很【平靜】，九點以後風會變得強很多。"},{"w":"deep","p":"adj.","d":"going a long way down from the top","c":"深的","s":"A: Why did the fishing guide tell the children to stay in the shallow area near the shore this afternoon? B: The water becomes very deep only a few meters from the beach, and the current there is strong, so he did not want any of the young visitors to get into trouble.","t":"A：為什麼釣魚嚮導今天下午叫孩子們待在靠近岸邊的淺水區？ B：離海灘才幾公尺遠，水就變得非常【深】，而且那裡的水流很強，所以他不希望任何年輕的訪客遇到危險。"},{"w":"freshwater","p":"adj.","d":"living in or relating to water that is not salty","c":"淡水的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant change its menu after the new chef arrived from the mountain region last month? B: He prefers cooking freshwater fish like trout and carp from local rivers and lakes, so he replaced several ocean dishes with recipes from his hometown, and customers seem to love them.","t":"A：為什麼上個月那位來自山區的新主廚到任後，餐廳就更換了菜單？ B：他偏好烹調當地河川和湖泊的鱒魚和鯉魚等【淡水】魚，所以他把幾道海鮮料理換成了家鄉的食譜，而顧客似乎都很喜歡。"},{"w":"saltwater","p":"adj.","d":"living in or relating to sea water","c":"海水的；鹹水的","s":"A: Why does the shop owner tell customers to wash their equipment carefully after a fishing trip at the beach? B: Fishing in saltwater areas is hard on rods and reels, because the sea air and water make metal parts rust, so a quick rinse with clean water keeps the equipment working for years.","t":"A：為什麼店老闆告訴顧客在海邊釣魚後要仔細清洗裝備？ B：在【海水】區域釣魚對釣竿和捲線器的損耗很大，因為海風和海水會讓金屬零件生鏽，所以快速用清水沖洗一下，就能讓裝備使用好幾年。"},{"w":"species","p":"n.","d":"a group of animals or plants of the same type","c":"物種；種類","s":"A: What did the scientists from the university find when they studied the lake behind our factory last summer? B: They counted more than twenty different species of fish living there, which shows the water is still healthy, and our company plans to share the report with the local community.","t":"A：大學的科學家們去年夏天研究我們工廠後面的湖時發現了什麼？ B：他們算出有超過二十種不同【種類】的魚生活在那裡，這顯示湖水仍然很健康，我們公司打算和當地社區分享這份報告。"},{"w":"tide","p":"n.","d":"the regular rise and fall of the sea","c":"潮汐；潮水","s":"A: Why do the fishermen in this town go out at different times every day instead of keeping a regular schedule? B: They plan their trips around the tide, because when the water comes in, many fish swim closer to the coast to feed, so the catch is usually much better.","t":"A：為什麼這個小鎮的漁夫每天出海的時間都不同，而不是維持固定的時間表？ B：他們依照【潮汐】安排出海時間，因為漲潮時許多魚會游到靠近海岸的地方覓食，所以漁獲量通常會好很多。"},{"w":"weather","p":"n.","d":"the conditions of sun, rain, and wind at a certain time","c":"天氣","s":"A: Should we still hold the fishing event for our customers on Sunday, or should we move it to another date? B: Let's check the weather forecast again on Friday afternoon, and if there is a chance of thunderstorms, we will send everyone an email and move the event to the following weekend.","t":"A：我們星期天還要為客戶舉辦釣魚活動嗎？還是應該改到別的日期？ B：我們星期五下午再查一次【天氣】預報，如果有雷雨的可能，我們會寄電子郵件給大家，並把活動延到下個週末。"},{"w":"license","p":"n.","d":"an official document that gives permission to do something","c":"執照；許可證","s":"A: Can our foreign guests go fishing in the national park during their stay, or is there a special rule for visitors? B: They must buy a short-term fishing license at the visitor center first, because park rangers check documents regularly, and anyone fishing without one may have to pay a large fine.","t":"A：我們的外國賓客在停留期間可以去國家公園釣魚嗎？還是對遊客有特別的規定？ B：他們必須先在遊客中心購買短期釣魚【許可證】，因為公園管理員會定期檢查證件，沒有許可證就釣魚的人可能要支付高額罰款。"},{"w":"harvest","p":"n.","d":"the amount of fish or crops that is collected","c":"收穫量；漁獲量","s":"A: Why are fish prices at the market so much higher than usual this month, according to the restaurant suppliers? B: The fishing companies reported a much smaller harvest this season because of warmer ocean water, so there is less supply, and restaurants have to pay more for the same amount.","t":"A：根據餐廳供應商的說法，為什麼這個月市場上的魚價比平常高這麼多？ B：漁業公司回報說，由於海水變暖，這一季的【漁獲量】少了很多，所以供應減少，餐廳必須花更多錢買同樣的分量。"},{"w":"release","p":"v.","d":"to let a fish go back into the water","c":"放生；釋放","s":"A: What happens to all the fish that people catch at the river during the charity competition next month? B: After the judges measure and photograph each one, the anglers release them back into the water right away, because the event organizers want to protect the river and its wildlife.","t":"A：下個月慈善比賽期間大家在河裡釣到的魚會怎麼處理？ B：評審測量並拍下每一條魚之後，釣客會立刻把牠們【放】回水裡，因為活動主辦單位希望保護這條河和河中的野生動物。"},{"w":"fillet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of fish or meat with the bones removed","c":"魚排；魚片","s":"A: What would you recommend from today's lunch menu for a client who does not like eating fish with small bones? B: I would suggest the grilled salmon fillet, because the chef removes all the bones in the kitchen, and it comes with fresh vegetables and a light lemon sauce.","t":"A：今天的午餐菜單中，你會推薦什麼給不喜歡吃有小刺的魚的客戶？ B：我會推薦烤鮭魚【魚排】，因為主廚在廚房裡把所有的刺都去掉了，而且還搭配新鮮蔬菜和清爽的檸檬醬。"},{"w":"scale","p":"n.","d":"one of the small hard plates that cover a fish's skin","c":"魚鱗","s":"A: Why does the cook at the seafood restaurant use that special metal tool before he cuts the fish open? B: He uses it to remove every scale from the skin quickly, because customers complain if they find small hard pieces in their food, and the tool also saves a lot of time.","t":"A：為什麼海鮮餐廳的廚師在剖開魚之前要使用那個特殊的金屬工具？ B：他用它快速去除魚皮上的每一片【魚鱗】，因為顧客如果在食物裡吃到小硬片就會抱怨，而且這個工具也能節省很多時間。"},{"w":"clean","p":"v.","d":"to remove the inside parts of a fish before cooking it","c":"清理（魚的內臟）","s":"A: What should we do with the fish we caught this morning before we give them to the hotel kitchen for dinner? B: We should clean them at the washing station on the dock by removing the insides and rinsing them well, so the chef can start cooking as soon as we arrive.","t":"A：我們把今天早上釣到的魚交給飯店廚房做晚餐之前，應該先怎麼處理？ B：我們應該在碼頭上的清洗區把牠們【清理】乾淨，去除內臟並好好沖洗，這樣我們一到，主廚就可以馬上開始烹煮。"},{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to cook food over direct heat","c":"燒烤；炙烤","s":"A: What is the plan for dinner after the fishing trip, since the restaurant near the lake is closed on Mondays? B: The campsite has several barbecue areas, so we will grill the fish we catch over charcoal with some salt and lemon, and everyone can bring a side dish to share.","t":"A：既然湖邊的餐廳星期一公休，釣魚之後的晚餐有什麼計畫？ B：營地有好幾個烤肉區，所以我們會用木炭加點鹽和檸檬【烤】我們釣到的魚，每個人也可以帶一道配菜來分享。"}]},{"unit":143,"theme":"Flowchart 流程圖","cards":[{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of something are arranged or organized","c":"結構；架構","s":"A: Why does the new manager want us to redraw the flowchart for the ordering system before Friday's meeting with the finance team? B: She thinks the current structure is too confusing, because the steps jump from one department to another, so she wants a clearer design that new staff can follow easily.","t":"A：為什麼新經理要我們在週五和財務團隊開會前重新畫訂購系統的流程圖？ B：她認為目前的【結構】太混亂了，因為步驟在不同部門之間跳來跳去，所以她想要一個新進員工能輕鬆遵循的更清楚的設計。"},{"w":"flow","p":"n.","d":"the smooth movement of something from one step to the next","c":"流動；流程","s":"A: How can we make sure that customer complaints don't get lost between the call center and the repair department anymore? B: Let's draw a chart that shows the flow of each complaint from the first phone call to the final repair, so everyone can see exactly where the delays happen.","t":"A：我們要怎麼確保客戶的投訴不會再在客服中心和維修部門之間遺失？ B：我們來畫一張圖，顯示每件投訴從第一通電話到最後維修的【流程】，這樣每個人都能清楚看到延誤發生在哪裡。"},{"w":"process","p":"n.","d":"a series of steps that you follow to get a result","c":"過程；程序","s":"A: Why do new employees always take so long to get their laptops and email accounts set up during their first week here? B: The whole process has twelve steps and needs three different signatures, so the IT manager is making a simple flowchart to show which steps we can remove.","t":"A：為什麼新進員工在第一週總是要花那麼久才能設定好筆電和電子郵件帳號？ B：整個【程序】有十二個步驟，還需要三個不同的簽名，所以資訊經理正在做一張簡單的流程圖，標出哪些步驟可以刪掉。"},{"w":"relationship","p":"n.","d":"the way two or more things are connected","c":"關係","s":"A: What did the consultant mean when she said our sales chart was missing something important during yesterday's meeting? B: She meant that the chart doesn't show the relationship between the marketing team and the sales team, so readers can't see how one department's work affects the other's results.","t":"A：昨天開會時顧問說我們的銷售圖表少了重要的東西，她是什麼意思？ B：她的意思是圖表沒有呈現行銷團隊和業務團隊之間的【關係】，所以讀者看不出一個部門的工作如何影響另一個部門的成果。"},{"w":"component","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that together make a machine or system","c":"組成部分；零件","s":"A: Why is the engineer putting so many small boxes on the diagram of the new coffee machine that we are going to sell next spring? B: Each box stands for one component of the machine, such as the water tank or the heater, so the repair staff can find problems quickly.","t":"A：為什麼工程師要在我們明年春天要賣的新咖啡機示意圖上畫那麼多小方框？ B：每個方框代表機器的一個【零件】，例如水箱或加熱器，這樣維修人員就能很快找到問題。"},{"w":"layout","p":"n.","d":"the way things are arranged on a page or in a space","c":"版面配置；布局","s":"A: Did the printing company say anything about the poster that shows our new safety steps for the factory workers? B: Yes, they said the layout is too crowded, because the arrows cross each other and the text is very small, so we should move some boxes and leave more white space.","t":"A：印刷公司對那張顯示工廠工人新安全步驟的海報有說什麼嗎？ B：有，他們說【版面配置】太擁擠了，因為箭頭互相交叉，文字也很小，所以我們應該移動一些方框，留更多空白。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"something that joins two things or shows that they are related","c":"連結；關聯","s":"A: Why did the new trainee draw a long arrow from the warehouse box to the customer service box on the flowchart this morning? B: He wanted to show the connection between the two teams, because late shipments from the warehouse usually cause angry calls to customer service the next day.","t":"A：為什麼新來的實習生今天早上在流程圖上從倉庫方框畫了一條長箭頭到客服方框？ B：他想呈現這兩個團隊之間的【關聯】，因為倉庫延遲出貨通常會在隔天引來打給客服的憤怒電話。"},{"w":"sequence","p":"n.","d":"the order in which things happen or are arranged","c":"順序；次序","s":"A: Why did several new workers make mistakes when they packed the online orders in the warehouse last week? B: The instructions on the wall listed the steps in the wrong sequence, so people sealed the boxes before checking the items, and now the supervisor is fixing the chart.","t":"A：為什麼上週有好幾個新員工在倉庫包裝網路訂單時出錯？ B：牆上的說明把步驟列成錯誤的【順序】，所以大家在檢查商品之前就把箱子封起來了，現在主管正在修正那張圖表。"},{"w":"hierarchy","p":"n.","d":"a system in which people or things are ranked from highest to lowest","c":"階層；層級制度","s":"A: How will the new staff in our Taipei branch know who they should report to when there is a problem with a client? B: The human resources team made a chart that shows the company hierarchy, from the general manager at the top down to the junior assistants at the bottom.","t":"A：我們台北分公司的新員工和客戶出問題時，要怎麼知道該向誰報告？ B：人資團隊做了一張圖，顯示公司的【層級制度】，從最上面的總經理一直到最下面的初級助理。"},{"w":"node","p":"n.","d":"a point in a diagram where lines meet or connect","c":"節點","s":"A: What should I do with this small circle in the middle of the network diagram that the engineers sent us yesterday afternoon? B: That circle is a node, which is the point where two lines meet, so please write the office name inside it before you print the final copy.","t":"A：工程師昨天下午寄給我們的網路圖中間這個小圓圈，我該怎麼處理？ B：那個圓圈是一個【節點】，也就是兩條線交會的地方，所以在印出最終版本前，請把辦公室名稱寫在裡面。"},{"w":"path","p":"n.","d":"the way or route from one point to another","c":"路徑；路線","s":"A: Why does the flowchart for refund requests have two different arrows coming out of the diamond in the middle? B: Each arrow shows a different path, so if the customer has a receipt, the request goes left to the cashier, and if not, it goes right to the store manager.","t":"A：為什麼退款申請的流程圖中間的菱形會延伸出兩個不同的箭頭？ B：每個箭頭顯示不同的【路徑】，所以如果客人有收據，申請就往左交給收銀員；如果沒有，就往右交給店長。"},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"a sign or shape that stands for an idea or action","c":"符號","s":"A: Why did the trainer ask everyone to learn the shapes on the first page of the handbook before the workshop started this morning? B: Each symbol has a special meaning in a flowchart, for example, an oval means start or end and a diamond means a decision.","t":"A：為什麼培訓師在今天早上工作坊開始前要大家先學會手冊第一頁上的圖形？ B：每個【符號】在流程圖中都有特別的意思，例如橢圓形代表開始或結束，菱形代表做決定。"},{"w":"label","p":"n.","d":"a short word or name that tells what something is","c":"標籤；標示","s":"A: The boxes on this chart all look the same, so how will the new cashiers know which step is which during their training next Monday? B: I'll add a clear label to each box, such as Scan Item or Take Payment, so they can understand every step at a glance.","t":"A：這張圖上的方框看起來都一樣，新收銀員在下週一的訓練中要怎麼知道哪個是哪個步驟？ B：我會在每個方框加上清楚的【標示】，例如「掃描商品」或「收款」，讓他們一眼就能看懂每個步驟。"},{"w":"annotation","p":"n.","d":"a short note added to a text or diagram to explain something","c":"註解；註釋","s":"A: The new process chart looks fine, but how will the night shift workers know what to do when the computer system suddenly stops working? B: I wrote a short annotation next to that step in red, which explains that they should call the IT hotline and record the orders by hand.","t":"A：新的流程圖看起來沒問題，但夜班員工在電腦系統突然當機時要怎麼知道該做什麼？ B：我在那個步驟旁邊用紅字寫了一則簡短的【註解】，說明他們應該打資訊部的熱線，並用手寫記錄訂單。"},{"w":"overview","p":"n.","d":"a short description that gives the main ideas but not the details","c":"概要；概觀","s":"A: The directors only have ten minutes for our project at the board meeting tomorrow, so should I explain every step of the new system? B: No, just give them a quick overview with one simple chart, and then email the detailed report to anyone who wants more information afterward.","t":"A：明天董事會上董事們只有十分鐘聽我們的專案，我應該解釋新系統的每一個步驟嗎？ B：不用，只要用一張簡單的圖表給他們一個快速的【概要】，之後再把詳細報告寄給想知道更多的人。"},{"w":"visual","p":"n.","d":"a picture, chart, or video used to help explain something","c":"視覺輔助（圖表、圖片等）","s":"A: My presentation about the new delivery system is full of long sentences, and I'm afraid the clients will get bored halfway through it. B: You should add a visual, such as a colorful chart or a short video, because people remember pictures much better than words on a slide.","t":"A：我關於新配送系統的簡報充滿了長句子，我怕客戶聽到一半就會覺得無聊。 B：你應該加入【視覺輔助】，例如彩色圖表或短片，因為人們記得圖片的效果遠比投影片上的文字好。"},{"w":"clarity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand","c":"清晰；明確","s":"A: Why did the manager ask us to remove half of the arrows and colors from the customer service flowchart last week? B: She said the chart needed more clarity, because the staff were confused by too many details and could not quickly see what to do next.","t":"A：為什麼經理上週要我們刪掉客服流程圖上一半的箭頭和顏色？ B：她說這張圖需要更【清晰】，因為員工被太多細節搞混了，沒辦法快速看出下一步該做什麼。"},{"w":"mapping","p":"n.","d":"the act of drawing or planning how the parts or steps of something are arranged","c":"繪製（流程）圖；對應規劃","s":"A: How did the hospital reduce the waiting time for patients at the front desk by almost half this year? B: They started with careful process mapping, drawing every step from check-in to payment, and then they removed the steps that were slow or unnecessary.","t":"A：醫院今年是怎麼把病患在櫃台的等候時間減少將近一半的？ B：他們從仔細的流程【繪製】開始，畫出從報到到付款的每一個步驟，然後刪掉那些緩慢或不必要的步驟。"},{"w":"illustrate","p":"v.","d":"to explain or show something with pictures or examples","c":"圖解；說明；畫插圖","s":"A: The new interns still don't understand how an order moves from our website to the warehouse, even after reading the manual twice. B: Then let's use a simple flowchart to illustrate each step, because pictures and arrows usually make complicated ideas much easier for beginners to follow.","t":"A：新來的實習生即使讀了兩次手冊，還是不懂訂單是怎麼從我們的網站傳到倉庫的。 B：那我們就用一張簡單的流程圖來【圖解】每個步驟，因為圖片和箭頭通常能讓初學者更容易理解複雜的概念。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in a clear order or system","c":"組織；整理；籌辦","s":"A: I have so many notes from the planning meeting that I don't know where to begin with the project report for the director. B: Try to organize your ideas into a flowchart first, putting the main tasks in boxes and linking them with arrows, and then writing will be much easier.","t":"A：我從規劃會議記下的筆記太多了，不知道要從哪裡開始寫給主任的專案報告。 B：先試著把你的想法【整理】成一張流程圖，把主要任務放進方框並用箭頭連接起來，這樣寫起來就會容易得多。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear and easy to understand","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Our new customers keep calling the help line because they don't know how to return a broken product they bought online. B: We should put a short chart on our website to explain the return steps, and that will probably reduce the number of calls we get every day.","t":"A：我們的新客戶一直打客服專線，因為他們不知道怎麼退回在網路上買到的壞掉商品。 B：我們應該在網站上放一張簡短的圖表來【說明】退貨步驟，這樣大概能減少我們每天接到的電話數量。"},{"w":"simplify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to do or understand","c":"簡化","s":"A: Why are customers complaining that it takes over twenty minutes to open a new account at our bank branch? B: The form has too many steps and repeated questions, so the operations team is drawing a flowchart to simplify the whole procedure and cut the waiting time.","t":"A：為什麼客戶抱怨在我們分行開新帳戶要花超過二十分鐘？ B：表格的步驟太多、問題又重複，所以營運團隊正在畫一張流程圖，要【簡化】整個程序並縮短等候時間。"},{"w":"framework","p":"n.","d":"a basic structure of ideas used to plan or decide something","c":"架構；框架","s":"A: How should we start planning the training program for the new sales staff who are joining us in January? B: Let's first build a simple framework with the main topics and goals for each week, and then we can add the details, activities, and trainers' names later.","t":"A：我們要怎麼開始規劃一月加入的新業務人員的訓練課程？ B：我們先建立一個簡單的【架構】，列出每週的主要主題和目標，之後再加上細節、活動和講師的名字。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a simple copy or description of a system, used to explain or test it","c":"模型；模式","s":"A: Before we spend money on the new delivery system, how can we know whether it will really save time for our drivers? B: The planning team built a computer model of the delivery routes, so we can test different ideas and compare the results before making a final decision.","t":"A：在我們花錢買新的配送系統之前，要怎麼知道它真的能幫司機節省時間？ B：規劃團隊建立了一個配送路線的電腦【模型】，所以我們可以在做最後決定之前測試不同的想法並比較結果。"},{"w":"alignment","p":"n.","d":"the state of being arranged in a straight or correct line","c":"對齊；排列整齊","s":"A: I've checked every step and arrow carefully, so why does the flowchart still look a little messy on the slide? B: The alignment of the boxes is not right, because some are a bit higher than others, so please line them up neatly before the client meeting this afternoon.","t":"A：我已經仔細檢查過每個步驟和箭頭了，為什麼投影片上的流程圖看起來還是有點亂？ B：方框的【對齊】不對，因為有些比其他的高一點，所以請在今天下午和客戶開會前把它們排整齊。"},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"the way people or things communicate or work together","c":"互動；相互作用","s":"A: Why does the new customer service chart include the sales team, the warehouse, and the delivery drivers all on one page? B: It shows the interaction between all three groups, so managers can see how each team's actions affect the others when a customer places an urgent order.","t":"A：為什麼新的客服流程圖把業務團隊、倉庫和送貨司機都放在同一頁？ B：它呈現這三個群體之間的【互動】，讓經理能看到當客戶下緊急訂單時，每個團隊的行動如何影響其他團隊。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking at two or more things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"A: Why did the operations manager put the old ordering steps and the new ordering steps side by side on the same slide? B: She wanted to make a clear comparison, so the directors could easily see that the new system has fewer steps and takes less time.","t":"A：為什麼營運經理把舊的訂購步驟和新的訂購步驟並排放在同一張投影片上？ B：她想做一個清楚的【比較】，讓董事們能輕易看出新系統的步驟比較少，也比較省時間。"},{"w":"visualization","p":"n.","d":"a picture or chart that shows information so that it is easy to see and understand","c":"視覺化（呈現）","s":"A: The sales report has hundreds of numbers from twelve different stores, so how can the regional manager understand it quickly before the meeting? B: The data team created a visualization with colorful charts and a simple flow diagram, so she can see the strongest and weakest stores in seconds.","t":"A：銷售報告裡有來自十二家分店的幾百個數字，區域經理要怎麼在開會前快速看懂？ B：數據團隊製作了一份有彩色圖表和簡單流程圖的【視覺化呈現】，讓她幾秒鐘內就能看出表現最好和最差的分店。"}]},{"unit":144,"theme":"Flowers 花卉","cards":[{"w":"blossom","p":"n.","d":"a flower on a tree or bush, especially in spring","c":"（果樹的）花；花朵","s":"A: Why is the hotel's garden café so busy this week, and why are so many guests taking photos near the entrance? B: The cherry trees by the front gate are covered in pink blossom right now, so visitors come early in the morning to enjoy the view before the petals start falling next week.","t":"A：為什麼飯店的花園咖啡廳這週這麼忙，而且為什麼這麼多客人在入口附近拍照？ B：前門旁的櫻花樹現在開滿了粉紅色的【花朵】，所以遊客一大早就來欣賞美景，趕在下週花瓣開始飄落之前。"},{"w":"petal","p":"n.","d":"one of the soft colored parts of a flower","c":"花瓣","s":"A: Did the wedding planner finally decide how to make the dinner tables look special for Saturday's reception at the hotel? B: Yes, she will place one red rose petal on every guest's napkin, so she has ordered three large boxes from the flower market and will keep them cool in the fridge until Saturday morning.","t":"A：婚禮策劃師最後決定好要怎麼讓週六飯店喜宴的餐桌看起來特別了嗎？ B：決定了，她會在每位賓客的餐巾上放一片紅玫瑰【花瓣】，所以她從花市訂了三大箱，並會放在冰箱裡保持冰涼直到週六早上。"},{"w":"stem","p":"n.","d":"the long thin part of a plant that holds the flower","c":"莖；花梗","s":"A: Why do the flowers in the lobby always stay fresh for more than a week, while the ones in our office die after only two days? B: The hotel staff cut the end of each stem at an angle every morning and change the water, so the flowers can drink more easily and last much longer than ours do.","t":"A：為什麼大廳裡的花總是能保持新鮮超過一週，而我們辦公室的花只撐兩天就凋謝了？ B：飯店員工每天早上都會把每根【花莖】的末端斜切，並且換水，所以花能更容易吸水，也比我們的花持久得多。"},{"w":"leaf","p":"n.","d":"one of the flat green parts of a plant","c":"葉子","s":"A: Is something wrong with the large plant next to the reception desk, or does it just need to be moved closer to the window? B: I noticed that almost every leaf has turned yellow and dry at the edges, so I've asked the cleaning company to send someone from their plant care team to check it on Friday.","t":"A：櫃台旁那盆大型植物是出了什麼問題，還是只需要把它移到靠近窗戶的地方？ B：我注意到幾乎每一片【葉子】的邊緣都變黃變乾了，所以我已經請清潔公司派植物照護團隊的人週五來檢查。"},{"w":"bud","p":"n.","d":"a small part of a plant that will open into a flower","c":"花苞；芽","s":"A: Why did you buy roses that are still closed for the opening party, when the event is only three days away? B: The florist told me that if each bud is still tight when you buy it, the flowers will open slowly and look their best on the day of the event instead of dying early.","t":"A：開幕派對只剩三天了，為什麼你買的玫瑰還都是閉合的？ B：花店老闆告訴我，如果買的時候每個【花苞】都還很緊實，花就會慢慢綻放，在活動當天呈現最美的樣子，而不會太早凋謝。"},{"w":"bloom","p":"v.","d":"to produce flowers; to open","c":"開花","s":"A: When is the best time to bring our overseas clients to visit the famous plum farm in the mountains of Nantou? B: Most of the plum trees there bloom in late January, so if we plan the trip for the last weekend of the month, the clients will see the whole hillside covered in white flowers.","t":"A：什麼時候帶海外客戶去參觀南投山區那座知名的梅園最好？ B：那裡大部分的梅樹在一月下旬【開花】，所以如果我們把行程安排在這個月的最後一個週末，客戶就能看到整片山坡覆蓋著白色的花朵。"},{"w":"fragrant","p":"adj.","d":"having a pleasant smell","c":"芳香的；香的","s":"A: Which flowers should we put in the hotel guest rooms, since several guests last month said the rooms smelled a little like cleaning products? B: Let's choose lilies or jasmine, because they are very fragrant and a small vase on each desk will make the whole room smell sweet and relaxing for our guests.","t":"A：既然上個月有幾位房客說房間聞起來有點像清潔用品，我們應該在飯店客房裡放什麼花？ B：我們選百合或茉莉吧，因為它們非常【芳香】，每張書桌上放一個小花瓶，就能讓整個房間對客人來說聞起來香甜又放鬆。"},{"w":"scent","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant smell","c":"香味；氣味","s":"A: Why does the new shopping mall smell so nice near the main entrance, even though there isn't any flower shop on the first floor? B: The marketing team installed machines that spread a light rose scent through the air, because they believe a pleasant smell makes customers relax and stay in the mall longer.","t":"A：為什麼新購物中心的主入口附近聞起來這麼香，即使一樓並沒有花店？ B：行銷團隊安裝了機器，在空氣中散發淡淡的玫瑰【香味】，因為他們相信宜人的氣味能讓顧客放鬆，並在商場待得更久。"},{"w":"bouquet","p":"n.","d":"a bunch of flowers arranged nicely","c":"花束","s":"A: What should we give Ms. Chen on her last day at the office after working with our company for more than twenty years? B: Everyone in the department has signed a card, and I have also ordered a large bouquet of her favorite yellow roses, which the shop will deliver to the meeting room at four o'clock.","t":"A：陳女士在我們公司服務了二十多年，她最後一天上班時我們應該送她什麼？ B：部門裡每個人都在卡片上簽了名，我也訂了一個用她最喜歡的黃玫瑰做成的大【花束】，花店會在四點鐘送到會議室。"},{"w":"arrangement","p":"n.","d":"flowers placed together in an attractive way","c":"插花；花藝擺設","s":"A: Why does the front desk look so different this morning, and who changed the decorations near the entrance over the weekend? B: The hotel hired a local artist to create a tall flower arrangement with orchids and green branches, and it will be replaced with a new design every Monday for the rest of the year.","t":"A：為什麼櫃台今天早上看起來這麼不一樣，週末是誰換了入口附近的裝飾？ B：飯店聘請了一位當地藝術家，用蘭花和綠色枝葉打造了一座高大的【插花作品】，而且今年剩下的時間每週一都會換上新的設計。"},{"w":"garden","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land where flowers or plants are grown","c":"花園","s":"A: Where are we having the company's summer party this year, since the hotel ballroom is fully booked in July? B: The manager found a restaurant with a large garden full of roses and tall trees behind the building, so we can eat outside in the evening when the weather is cooler.","t":"A：既然飯店宴會廳七月都被訂滿了，今年公司的夏季派對要在哪裡舉辦？ B：經理找到一家餐廳，建築後方有一座種滿玫瑰和高大樹木的大【花園】，所以我們可以在天氣比較涼爽的傍晚在戶外用餐。"},{"w":"vase","p":"n.","d":"a container for holding cut flowers","c":"花瓶","s":"A: Where should I put the flowers that our clients sent us this morning to thank us for finishing their project early? B: There is a tall glass vase in the cupboard next to the kitchen sink, so fill it with cool water and place it on the reception desk where every visitor can see them.","t":"A：客戶今天早上送來感謝我們提早完成專案的花，我應該放在哪裡？ B：廚房水槽旁的櫥櫃裡有一個高的玻璃【花瓶】，裝滿冷水後把它放在接待櫃台上，讓每位訪客都能看到。"},{"w":"rose","p":"n.","d":"a flower with a sweet smell and thorns on its stem","c":"玫瑰","s":"A: What kind of flowers are customers buying most this week, and do we have enough stock for the holiday weekend? B: Since Valentine's Day is on Saturday, almost every customer wants a red rose, so I have asked our supplier to send two hundred more by Thursday afternoon at the latest.","t":"A：這週顧客最常買哪種花？我們有足夠的存貨應付節日週末嗎？ B：因為情人節在週六，幾乎每位顧客都想要一朵紅【玫瑰】，所以我已經請供應商最晚在週四下午前再送兩百朵過來。"},{"w":"tulip","p":"n.","d":"a bright cup-shaped spring flower, famous in the Netherlands","c":"鬱金香","s":"A: What did you enjoy most about your business trip to Amsterdam last April, apart from meeting the new suppliers? B: On my free afternoon, I visited a huge park where thousands of red and yellow tulip flowers grew in long lines, and it was the most colorful place I have ever seen.","t":"A：除了和新供應商見面之外，去年四月去阿姆斯特丹出差，你最喜歡的是什麼？ B：在我空閒的那個下午，我參觀了一座大公園，那裡成千上萬朵紅色和黃色的【鬱金香】排成長長的一列列，那是我看過最繽紛的地方。"},{"w":"daisy","p":"n.","d":"a small flower with white petals and a yellow center","c":"雛菊","s":"A: Why did the café owner choose such simple flowers for the tables instead of expensive roses or orchids? B: She says a small white daisy in a glass bottle matches the café's natural, relaxing style, and it is much cheaper, so she can replace the flowers every two days without spending too much.","t":"A：為什麼咖啡廳老闆選擇這麼簡單的花放在桌上，而不是昂貴的玫瑰或蘭花？ B：她說玻璃瓶裡的一朵小白【雛菊】和咖啡廳自然放鬆的風格很搭，而且便宜得多，所以她每兩天就能換一次花，又不必花太多錢。"},{"w":"lily","p":"n.","d":"a large trumpet-shaped flower, often white","c":"百合","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager ask us to remove all the white flowers from the dining room before the cat show guests arrive? B: She read that the lily is very dangerous for cats, even if they only touch the pollen, so she wants to make sure none of the animals get sick during the event.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理要我們在貓展來賓抵達前，把餐廳裡所有白色的花都撤掉？ B：她讀到【百合】對貓非常危險，就算只碰到花粉也一樣，所以她想確保活動期間沒有任何動物生病。"},{"w":"orchid","p":"n.","d":"an elegant flower with unusual shapes, often given as a gift","c":"蘭花","s":"A: What gift should we send to our business partner who is opening a new office in Hsinchu next Monday? B: In Taiwan, a large potted orchid is a popular gift for a new business because it looks elegant and lasts for months, so let's order one with a card from our CEO.","t":"A：我們的合作夥伴下週一要在新竹開新辦公室，我們應該送什麼禮物？ B：在台灣，大型盆栽【蘭花】是祝賀開業的熱門禮物，因為它看起來高雅又能維持好幾個月，所以我們訂一盆並附上執行長的卡片吧。"},{"w":"sunflower","p":"n.","d":"a very tall plant with a large yellow flower","c":"向日葵","s":"A: Why are so many families driving out to that farm near the coast this weekend, and is it worth taking our team there? B: The farm has a huge field where every tall yellow sunflower turns to face the sun, so it is a great place for group photos, and they also sell fresh ice cream and snacks.","t":"A：為什麼這週末這麼多家庭開車去海岸附近那座農場？值得帶我們團隊去嗎？ B：那座農場有一大片田地，每一株高大的黃色【向日葵】都會轉向太陽，所以很適合拍團體照，而且他們也賣新鮮的冰淇淋和點心。"},{"w":"wildflower","p":"n.","d":"a flower that grows naturally, not planted by people","c":"野花","s":"A: What did you see on the company hiking trip in the mountains last Saturday, since I had to stay home with a cold? B: The trail was lined with every kind of wildflower you can imagine, from tiny purple ones to bright orange ones, and our guide told us we must not pick any of them.","t":"A：上週六公司去山上健行你們看到了什麼？我因為感冒只好待在家。 B：步道兩旁開滿了各式各樣你想像得到的【野花】，從小小的紫色花到鮮豔的橘色花都有，而且導遊告訴我們一朵都不能摘。"},{"w":"colorful","p":"adj.","d":"having many bright colors","c":"色彩繽紛的","s":"A: How did the design team make the new lobby feel so welcoming after so many guests complained that it was dark and boring? B: They added large windows and filled the space with colorful flowers in red, yellow, and purple, so now the area looks bright and cheerful even on rainy days.","t":"A：之前很多客人抱怨大廳又暗又無聊，設計團隊是怎麼讓新大廳變得這麼溫馨的？ B：他們加了大片窗戶，並在空間裡擺滿紅、黃、紫色的【色彩繽紛的】花朵，所以現在即使下雨天，這一區看起來也明亮又愉快。"},{"w":"delicate","p":"adj.","d":"easily damaged; needing careful handling","c":"嬌嫩的；易損的","s":"A: Why did the delivery driver ask us to sign a special form before he unloaded the boxes of flowers for the wedding? B: The orchids inside are very delicate and can break if someone drops the boxes, so the company wants proof that they arrived in perfect condition before we carry them upstairs.","t":"A：為什麼送貨司機在卸下婚禮用的花箱之前，要我們簽一張特別的表格？ B：裡面的蘭花非常【嬌嫩】，如果有人把箱子摔落就可能折斷，所以公司希望在我們搬上樓之前，有證據證明花送達時狀況完好。"},{"w":"fresh","p":"adj.","d":"recently picked; not old or dying","c":"新鮮的","s":"A: Why does the restaurant buy flowers from the market every Monday morning instead of ordering them once a month online? B: The owner believes that only fresh flowers that were cut the same day can make the dining room look elegant, and old ones that start to droop give customers a bad impression.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳每週一早上都去市場買花，而不是一個月在網路上訂一次？ B：老闆認為只有當天剪下的【新鮮】花朵才能讓用餐區看起來高雅，而開始垂頭的舊花會給顧客不好的印象。"},{"w":"artificial","p":"adj.","d":"made by people, not real","c":"人造的；假的","s":"A: Why did the office manager replace the real plants in the meeting rooms with ones that look almost the same? B: Nobody had time to look after the real ones, so she bought artificial flowers made of silk, which never need water and still look beautiful after many months.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理把會議室裡的真植物換成幾乎一模一樣的植物？ B：沒有人有時間照顧真的植物，所以她買了絲綢做的【人造】花，它們永遠不需要澆水，而且幾個月後看起來還是很漂亮。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look nicer by adding things to it","c":"裝飾；布置","s":"A: What are the plans for the company's twentieth anniversary dinner, and do you need any help from our department? B: We are going to decorate the ballroom with white roses and small candles on every table, so it would be great if some of your staff could come early on Friday to help us.","t":"A：公司二十週年紀念晚宴的計畫是什麼？需要我們部門幫忙嗎？ B：我們打算用白玫瑰和每張桌上的小蠟燭來【裝飾】宴會廳，所以如果你們部門有些同事週五能早點來幫忙就太好了。"},{"w":"plant","p":"v.","d":"to put seeds or young plants in the ground to grow","c":"種植","s":"A: What is the new volunteer project that the human resources department announced in this morning's email to all staff? B: Next Saturday, employees can join a team to plant trees and flowers in the small park across the street, and the company will provide gloves, tools, lunch, and free T-shirts for everyone.","t":"A：人資部門今天早上寄給全體員工的信中宣布的新志工專案是什麼？ B：下週六，員工可以加入團隊，到對街的小公園【種植】樹木和花卉，公司會提供手套、工具、午餐，還有每人一件免費T恤。"},{"w":"water","p":"v.","d":"to give water to plants","c":"澆水","s":"A: Who will take care of the plants in the office while most of the team is away at the trade show in Tokyo next week? B: Ken is staying in Taipei, so he promised to water them every other morning and move the small ones away from the window if the afternoon sun becomes too strong.","t":"A：下週大部分團隊成員去東京參加展覽時，誰會照顧辦公室的植物？ B：Ken會留在台北，所以他答應每隔一天早上幫它們【澆水】，如果下午陽光太強，也會把小盆栽從窗邊移開。"},{"w":"fertilize","p":"v.","d":"to add food to soil to help plants grow","c":"施肥","s":"A: Why are the flowers in the front garden of our building growing so slowly this year, even though we water them every day? B: The gardener said the soil has lost most of its nutrients, so he is going to fertilize it once a month, and the flowers should become stronger and healthier by early summer.","t":"A：為什麼我們大樓前花園的花今年長得這麼慢，即使我們每天都澆水？ B：園丁說土壤已經失去大部分的養分，所以他打算每個月【施肥】一次，到初夏時花應該會長得更強壯、更健康。"},{"w":"prune","p":"v.","d":"to cut off unwanted branches to help a plant grow","c":"修剪（枝葉）","s":"A: Why are the rose bushes in front of the hotel entrance so short now, when they were tall and full of flowers last month? B: The gardener had to prune them after the flowering season ended, because removing the old branches helps the plants grow stronger and produce even more flowers next spring.","t":"A：為什麼飯店入口前的玫瑰叢現在這麼矮，上個月明明還很高而且開滿了花？ B：花季結束後，園丁必須【修剪】它們，因為剪掉老枝能幫助植物長得更強壯，明年春天開出更多花。"},{"w":"wither","p":"v.","d":"to become dry and weak and start to die","c":"枯萎；凋謝","s":"A: Why do the flowers on the conference tables look so tired, when they were delivered fresh only this morning? B: The air conditioner broke down during lunch and the room became very hot, so the flowers began to wither quickly, and we need to replace them before the afternoon session starts.","t":"A：為什麼會議桌上的花看起來這麼沒精神，明明今天早上才剛送來很新鮮？ B：冷氣在午餐時間壞了，房間變得非常熱，所以花很快就開始【枯萎】，我們必須在下午的會議開始前把它們換掉。"},{"w":"perennial","p":"n.","d":"a plant that lives for more than two years","c":"多年生植物","s":"A: Why did the building manager choose different plants for the rooftop garden instead of the colorful flowers we had last year? B: She wants each perennial to grow back every spring without being replanted, which will save the company money and time, because the old flowers died after only one season.","t":"A：為什麼大樓經理為屋頂花園選了不同的植物，而不是去年那些色彩繽紛的花？ B：她希望每一株【多年生植物】每年春天都能重新長出來而不必重新種植，這能幫公司省錢又省時間，因為舊的花只活一季就死了。"},{"w":"annual","p":"n.","d":"a plant that lives for only one year or season","c":"一年生植物","s":"A: Why do the gardeners at the city park replace all the flowers in the main flower beds at the beginning of every spring? B: Each plant there is an annual, which grows, flowers, and dies within one season, so the staff must buy new ones every year to keep the park looking bright.","t":"A：為什麼市立公園的園丁每年春天一開始都要把主花圃裡的花全部換掉？ B：那裡的每株植物都是【一年生植物】，在一季之內就發芽、開花、凋謝，所以工作人員每年都必須買新的，讓公園看起來明亮繽紛。"},{"w":"pollen","p":"n.","d":"a yellow powder in flowers that helps make seeds","c":"花粉","s":"A: Why does Linda always close the office windows and take medicine in March, even when the weather is warm and sunny? B: She has a strong allergy to the pollen from the trees outside our building, so on sunny spring days she sneezes all morning unless she keeps the windows closed.","t":"A：為什麼Linda每年三月總是關上辦公室的窗戶並吃藥，即使天氣溫暖晴朗？ B：她對我們大樓外樹木的【花粉】嚴重過敏，所以在晴朗的春天，除非把窗戶關上，否則她整個早上都會打噴嚏。"},{"w":"nectar","p":"n.","d":"the sweet liquid in flowers that bees collect","c":"花蜜","s":"A: Why did the farm owner plant so many purple flowers around the edge of his fields, when he only sells honey and fruit? B: The bees collect sweet nectar from those flowers to make honey, and while they fly from flower to flower, they also help his fruit trees produce a bigger harvest.","t":"A：為什麼農場主人在田地四周種了這麼多紫色的花，而他只賣蜂蜜和水果？ B：蜜蜂從那些花採集香甜的【花蜜】來釀蜂蜜，而牠們在花朵之間飛來飛去時，也幫助他的果樹結出更多果實。"},{"w":"florist","p":"n.","d":"a person or shop that sells and arranges flowers","c":"花商；花藝師；花店","s":"A: Who prepared the beautiful flowers for the grand opening of our new branch, and can we use the same company again next month? B: A local florist on Zhongshan Road made them, and she offers a ten percent discount to business customers who order flowers every month, so I'll call her this afternoon.","t":"A：我們新分店盛大開幕的漂亮花是誰準備的？下個月我們能再找同一家嗎？ B：是中山路上一位當地的【花藝師】做的，她給每月訂花的企業客戶九折優惠，所以我今天下午會打電話給她。"},{"w":"greenhouse","p":"n.","d":"a glass building where plants are grown","c":"溫室","s":"A: How can the farm sell fresh strawberries and roses in the middle of winter, when it is so cold outside? B: They grow everything inside a large glass greenhouse that stays warm all year, and a computer controls the temperature and the light so the plants grow quickly even in January.","t":"A：外面這麼冷，為什麼那座農場在隆冬時節還能賣新鮮的草莓和玫瑰？ B：他們把所有作物都種在一座全年保持溫暖的大型玻璃【溫室】裡，並由電腦控制溫度和光線，所以即使在一月植物也長得很快。"}]},{"unit":145,"theme":"Food 食物","cards":[{"w":"flavor","p":"n.","d":"the special taste of a food or drink","c":"味道；風味","s":"A: The customers at our new café keep asking for something different, so what kind of muffin should we add to the menu next month? B: Let's try a lemon and ginger flavor, because it is light and unusual, and we can offer free samples at the counter to see if people like it.","t":"A：我們新咖啡館的顧客一直要求點不一樣的東西，那下個月我們應該在菜單上加什麼樣的瑪芬？ B：我們試試檸檬薑的【口味】吧，因為它清爽又特別，而且我們可以在櫃檯提供免費試吃，看看大家喜不喜歡。"},{"w":"delicious","p":"adj.","d":"having a very good taste","c":"美味的；可口的","s":"A: How was the welcome dinner for the new clients last night, and did the restaurant near the station handle such a large group well? B: The service was fast and friendly, and everyone said the grilled salmon was delicious, so I think we should book the same place for the year-end party.","t":"A：昨晚為新客戶舉辦的歡迎晚宴怎麼樣？車站附近那家餐廳能好好招待這麼大一群人嗎？ B：服務又快又親切，而且大家都說烤鮭魚很【美味】，所以我覺得年終派對我們應該訂同一家餐廳。"},{"w":"tasty","p":"adj.","d":"having a pleasant, strong taste","c":"好吃的；有滋味的","s":"A: I need to order lunch for the training session on Friday, but our budget is small this quarter, so do you know any good places nearby? B: The noodle shop across the street makes cheap but very tasty lunch boxes, and they deliver to the office for free if we order more than twenty.","t":"A：我需要為星期五的培訓課程訂午餐，但這一季的預算很少，你知道附近有什麼好店家嗎？ B：對街那家麵店做的便當便宜又非常【好吃】，而且如果我們訂超過二十個，他們會免費送到辦公室。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"tasting like sugar or honey","c":"甜的","s":"A: Our manager is trying to eat more healthily these days, so should we still buy a big chocolate cake for her birthday celebration this afternoon? B: Maybe we should choose a fruit tart instead, because it is less sweet than chocolate cake, and everyone in the office can still enjoy a small piece.","t":"A：我們經理最近努力想吃得更健康，那今天下午為她慶生，我們還要買一個大巧克力蛋糕嗎？ B：也許我們應該改選水果塔，因為它沒有巧克力蛋糕那麼【甜】，而且辦公室的每個人仍然可以享用一小塊。"},{"w":"sour","p":"adj.","d":"having a sharp taste like lemon or vinegar","c":"酸的","s":"A: Why did several guests leave their drinks on the tables after the opening ceremony at the hotel yesterday afternoon? B: The kitchen staff added too much lemon juice to the punch, so it tasted very sour, and most people only drank a little before they switched to water or coffee.","t":"A：為什麼昨天下午飯店開幕典禮結束後，好幾位賓客把飲料留在桌上？ B：廚房員工在水果酒裡加了太多檸檬汁，所以喝起來非常【酸】，大部分的人只喝了一點，就改喝水或咖啡了。"},{"w":"bitter","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, sharp, unpleasant taste, like strong coffee","c":"苦的","s":"A: The coffee from the new machine in the break room tastes terrible, so should we call the supplier and ask them to check it? B: Yes, please call them today, because the coffee is so bitter that many staff members now walk to the café downstairs and waste time during their short breaks.","t":"A：休息室新機器煮的咖啡很難喝，我們應該打電話給供應商請他們來檢查嗎？ B：好，請今天就打給他們，因為咖啡【苦】到很多員工現在都走到樓下的咖啡店，在短暫的休息時間裡浪費了不少時間。"},{"w":"spicy","p":"adj.","d":"having a hot, strong taste from chili or pepper","c":"辣的","s":"A: We are taking the visitors from Germany out for dinner on Thursday, so is the Sichuan restaurant on Fifth Avenue a good choice? B: It might be risky, because many of their dishes are very spicy, so let's ask our guests first whether they enjoy hot food or prefer something milder.","t":"A：我們星期四要帶德國來的訪客出去吃晚餐，第五大道上那家川菜館是個好選擇嗎？ B：可能有點冒險，因為他們很多菜都非常【辣】，所以我們先問問客人是喜歡吃辣，還是比較喜歡溫和一點的食物。"},{"w":"savory","p":"adj.","d":"salty or spicy rather than sweet","c":"鹹香的；可口的（非甜的）","s":"A: Most of the snacks at our afternoon meetings are cookies and cakes, but some people say they want something different, so what should I order? B: Why don't you get some savory pastries with cheese and ham, because not everyone likes sugar, and they will keep people full until dinner.","t":"A：我們下午會議的點心大多是餅乾和蛋糕，但有些人說想吃點不一樣的，我該訂什麼？ B：你何不訂一些夾起司和火腿的【鹹】酥皮點心，因為不是每個人都喜歡甜的，而且這些能讓大家撐到晚餐。"},{"w":"fresh","p":"adj.","d":"recently made, picked, or caught; not old","c":"新鮮的","s":"A: Why are the salads at the new restaurant downtown so much more expensive than the ones at the shopping mall food court? B: The owner buys fresh vegetables from local farms every morning, so the quality is much better, and many office workers are happy to pay a little more for a healthy lunch.","t":"A：為什麼市中心那家新餐廳的沙拉比購物中心美食街的貴那麼多？ B：老闆每天早上都向當地農場購買【新鮮】蔬菜，所以品質好很多，許多上班族也很樂意多付一點錢吃一頓健康的午餐。"},{"w":"ripe","p":"adj.","d":"fully grown and ready to eat","c":"成熟的","s":"A: The bananas we bought for the staff kitchen on Monday are still hard and green, so can people eat them yet? B: Not yet, they won't be ripe for another two or three days, so please put them in a paper bag on the counter and tell everyone to wait until Thursday.","t":"A：我們星期一為員工廚房買的香蕉還是硬的、綠的，大家現在可以吃了嗎？ B：還不行，它們還要再兩三天才會【成熟】，所以請把它們放進紙袋擺在流理台上，並告訴大家等到星期四再吃。"},{"w":"raw","p":"adj.","d":"not cooked","c":"生的；未煮過的","s":"A: Several employees felt sick after the company picnic on Saturday, so has anyone found out what caused the problem? B: The health inspector thinks the chicken was still raw in the middle because the grill was not hot enough, so next time we will hire a professional caterer to cook everything.","t":"A：星期六公司野餐後有好幾位員工身體不舒服，有人查出問題的原因了嗎？ B：衛生稽查員認為雞肉中間還是【生的】，因為烤架不夠熱，所以下次我們會請專業的外燴業者來烹煮所有食物。"},{"w":"cooked","p":"adj.","d":"heated and prepared so it is ready to eat","c":"煮熟的","s":"A: Is it safe to leave the leftover rice and chicken from the lunch meeting on the table until the afternoon cleaning staff arrive? B: No, cooked food should go into the refrigerator within two hours, so please pack it in boxes now, and anyone can take some home after work.","t":"A：午餐會議剩下的飯和雞肉，放在桌上等下午清潔人員來可以嗎？ B：不行，【煮熟的】食物應該在兩小時內放進冰箱，所以請現在就把它們裝進盒子裡，下班後任何人都可以帶一些回家。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤","s":"A: The bakery on the corner always has a long line in the morning, so how do they manage to sell so many fresh rolls before nine o'clock? B: The owner told me that his staff start at four a.m. and bake about five hundred rolls every day, so the shelves are always full when the commuters arrive.","t":"A：轉角那家麵包店早上總是大排長龍，他們是怎麼在九點前賣出那麼多新鮮麵包捲的？ B：老闆告訴我，他的員工凌晨四點就開工，每天【烘烤】大約五百個麵包捲，所以通勤族到的時候，架上總是滿滿的。"},{"w":"boil","p":"v.","d":"to cook something in very hot water","c":"煮沸；水煮","s":"A: I'm preparing pasta for twenty people at the team-building event tomorrow, but I've never cooked for such a large group, so do you have any advice? B: Use the biggest pots in the kitchen and boil the pasta in two batches, because if you put too much in one pot, it will stick together.","t":"A：我明天要在團隊建立活動上為二十個人準備義大利麵，但我從沒為這麼多人煮過飯，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：用廚房裡最大的鍋子，分兩批【煮】義大利麵，因為如果你一次在一個鍋子裡放太多，麵會黏在一起。"},{"w":"fry","p":"v.","d":"to cook food in hot oil","c":"油炸；煎","s":"A: Our restaurant's kitchen gets very smoky during the lunch rush, so is there anything we can do before the health inspection next week? B: We should clean the fans over the stoves and fry smaller amounts of chicken at a time, because too much food in the oil makes a lot of smoke.","t":"A：我們餐廳的廚房在午餐尖峰時段煙很大，在下週衛生檢查前我們能做些什麼嗎？ B：我們應該清洗爐子上方的抽風機，並且每次少量【炸】雞肉，因為油裡放太多食物會產生大量油煙。"},{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to cook food over or under direct strong heat","c":"燒烤；烤","s":"A: What are we serving at the outdoor party for our customers next Saturday, and do we need to hire extra staff to help? B: We plan to grill burgers and vegetables in the garden behind the shop, so we only need two more people to help with the cooking and cleaning.","t":"A：下週六為顧客舉辦的戶外派對我們要提供什麼？我們需要多請工作人員幫忙嗎？ B：我們打算在店後面的花園【烤】漢堡和蔬菜，所以只需要再多兩個人來幫忙料理和清潔就好。"},{"w":"roast","p":"v.","d":"to cook meat or vegetables in an oven or over a fire","c":"烘烤（肉類或蔬菜）","s":"A: The hotel wants a special main course for the holiday dinner in December, so what is the chef planning to serve this year? B: He wants to roast a whole turkey for each table with potatoes and carrots, because guests loved it last year, and it looks very impressive in photos.","t":"A：飯店希望十二月的節日晚宴有一道特別的主菜，主廚今年打算端出什麼？ B：他想為每一桌【烤】一整隻火雞，搭配馬鈴薯和紅蘿蔔，因為去年客人很喜歡，而且在照片裡看起來非常令人印象深刻。"},{"w":"steam","p":"v.","d":"to cook food using the hot air from boiling water","c":"蒸","s":"A: Many of our lunch customers are asking for healthier choices, so how can we change our vegetable side dishes without making them boring? B: We could steam the broccoli and carrots instead of frying them, and then add a little garlic and lemon, so they stay bright, crunchy and full of vitamins.","t":"A：很多午餐客人要求更健康的選擇，我們要怎麼改變蔬菜配菜，又不會讓它們變得無聊？ B：我們可以把花椰菜和紅蘿蔔改用【蒸】的而不是用炸的，然後加一點大蒜和檸檬，這樣它們就能保持顏色鮮亮、口感爽脆又充滿維生素。"},{"w":"ingredient","p":"n.","d":"one of the foods used to make a dish","c":"食材；原料","s":"A: Why did the factory stop producing our best-selling cookies for a whole week last month, even though customers wanted to buy them? B: One important ingredient, a special butter from New Zealand, was delayed at the port, so the production line had to wait until the next shipment arrived.","t":"A：為什麼上個月工廠停產我們最暢銷的餅乾整整一週，即使顧客想買？ B：有一樣重要的【原料】，一種來自紐西蘭的特殊奶油，在港口延誤了，所以生產線必須等到下一批貨送到。"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"a set of instructions for cooking a dish","c":"食譜；配方","s":"A: The soup at your café tastes exactly the same every day, even when different cooks are working, so how do you manage that? B: Every cook must follow the same recipe, which lists the exact amounts and cooking times, and the head chef checks the taste before we serve it.","t":"A：你們咖啡館的湯每天喝起來都一模一樣，即使是不同的廚師在上班，你們是怎麼辦到的？ B：每位廚師都必須遵照同一份【食譜】，上面列出確切的份量和烹煮時間，而且主廚會在上菜前試味道。"},{"w":"dish","p":"n.","d":"food prepared in a particular way as part of a meal","c":"一道菜；菜餚","s":"A: Our restaurant's sales have been slow since the new place opened next door, so what can we do to bring customers back? B: We could create a new dish every month using seasonal vegetables, and then promote it online with photos, because people like to try something special.","t":"A：自從隔壁開了新餐廳後，我們餐廳的生意一直很冷清，我們能做些什麼把客人吸引回來？ B：我們可以每個月用當季蔬菜推出一道新【菜】，然後在網路上用照片宣傳，因為大家喜歡嘗試特別的東西。"},{"w":"meal","p":"n.","d":"the food eaten at one time, such as breakfast, lunch or dinner","c":"一餐；餐點","s":"A: The training day will last from eight in the morning until six in the evening, so will the company provide any food for the trainees? B: Yes, each trainee will get a free meal at lunchtime in the staff cafeteria, and there will be coffee and cookies during the afternoon break.","t":"A：培訓日從早上八點持續到晚上六點，公司會為受訓人員提供食物嗎？ B：會的，每位受訓人員午餐時間都可以在員工餐廳享用一份免費【餐點】，下午休息時間也會有咖啡和餅乾。"},{"w":"snack","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of food eaten between meals","c":"點心；零食","s":"A: Our team often works late during the busy season, and people get tired and hungry around four o'clock, so do you have any ideas? B: Let's keep a basket of fruit and nuts in the meeting room, so everyone can grab a quick snack and keep working without leaving the office.","t":"A：旺季時我們團隊常常加班，大家到了四點左右就又累又餓，你有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們在會議室放一籃水果和堅果，這樣每個人都可以很快拿個【點心】，不用離開辦公室就能繼續工作。"},{"w":"portion","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food served to one person","c":"（食物的）一份","s":"A: Some customers complained that our lunch set is too small for the price, so should we raise the amount of food or lower the price? B: I think we should offer a larger portion for an extra two dollars, so hungry customers can choose it while others keep the regular size.","t":"A：有些客人抱怨我們的午間套餐以這個價格來說份量太少，我們應該增加食物量還是降低價格？ B：我認為我們應該提供加兩塊錢的大【份】選項，這樣餓的客人可以選它，其他人則維持一般份量。"},{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the healthy substances in food that the body needs","c":"營養","s":"A: The school cafeteria wants to improve its lunches for students next year, so who is helping them plan the new menu? B: They have hired an expert in nutrition who will make sure every lunch has enough vegetables, protein and vitamins, while keeping the cost under three dollars per student.","t":"A：學校餐廳明年想改善學生的午餐，誰在幫他們規劃新菜單？ B：他們聘請了一位【營養】專家，她會確保每份午餐都有足夠的蔬菜、蛋白質和維生素，同時把每位學生的費用控制在三美元以下。"},{"w":"calorie","p":"n.","d":"a unit that measures how much energy food gives you","c":"卡路里；熱量","s":"A: A lot of our gym members ask how healthy the smoothies in our juice bar are, so what information should we give them? B: Let's print the calorie count and the amount of sugar for each drink on the menu board, so members can choose the right one for their fitness goals.","t":"A：很多健身房會員詢問我們果汁吧的冰沙有多健康，我們應該提供什麼資訊給他們？ B：我們把每杯飲料的【卡路里】數和含糖量印在菜單板上，這樣會員就能依照自己的健身目標選擇適合的飲品。"},{"w":"organic","p":"adj.","d":"grown without chemicals","c":"有機的","s":"A: Why are the tomatoes at the farmers' market twice as expensive as the ones at the supermarket near our office? B: They are organic, which means the farmers don't use any chemicals, so it takes more work to grow them, but many customers think the better taste is worth the higher price.","t":"A：為什麼農夫市集的番茄比我們辦公室附近超市的貴兩倍？ B：它們是【有機的】，意思是農夫不使用任何化學藥劑，所以種植起來更費工，但很多顧客覺得更好的味道值得更高的價格。"},{"w":"processed","p":"adj.","d":"changed in a factory with added chemicals or preservatives","c":"加工的","s":"A: The doctor at our company health check told me that I need to change my diet, so what did she recommend? B: She said I should eat less processed food like sausages and instant noodles, and cook more meals at home with fresh vegetables and fish, especially on busy weekdays.","t":"A：公司健康檢查的醫生告訴我需要改變飲食，她建議了什麼？ B：她說我應該少吃香腸和泡麵這類【加工】食品，多在家用新鮮蔬菜和魚做飯，尤其是在忙碌的平日。"},{"w":"appetizing","p":"adj.","d":"looking or smelling good, so you want to eat it","c":"令人有食慾的；誘人的","s":"A: Our online food orders dropped last month, and the marketing team thinks the problem is our website, so what should we change first? B: We should take new photos of every item with better lighting, because the old pictures look dark and not very appetizing, so customers don't feel like ordering.","t":"A：我們上個月的網路訂餐量下滑，行銷團隊認為問題出在網站上，我們應該先改什麼？ B：我們應該用更好的燈光為每樣餐點重新拍照，因為舊照片看起來很暗、不太【誘人】，所以顧客沒有想點餐的衝動。"},{"w":"hungry","p":"adj.","d":"wanting or needing food","c":"飢餓的","s":"A: The client meeting went on for almost four hours without a break, so how did everyone feel when it finally ended? B: Everyone was tired and very hungry, so we ordered pizza right away, and we agreed that next time we will plan a lunch break in the middle of long meetings.","t":"A：客戶會議幾乎連續開了四個小時都沒休息，終於結束時大家感覺怎麼樣？ B：每個人都很累而且非常【餓】，所以我們馬上訂了披薩，並且同意下次開長會時要在中間安排午餐休息。"},{"w":"full","p":"adj.","d":"having eaten so much that you do not want more","c":"吃飽的","s":"A: Would you like some dessert after the business lunch, because the chocolate cake at this restaurant is famous in the area? B: Thank you, but I'm already full after that big plate of pasta, so I'll just have a cup of tea before we go back to the office for the afternoon meeting.","t":"A：商務午餐後你想來點甜點嗎？這家餐廳的巧克力蛋糕在這一帶很有名。 B：謝謝，但吃完那一大盤義大利麵我已經【飽了】，所以我們回辦公室開下午的會之前，我喝杯茶就好。"},{"w":"taste","p":"n.","d":"the flavor that food has in your mouth","c":"味道；口味","s":"A: We changed our coffee supplier last month to save money, but have any customers said anything about the new beans? B: A few regular customers said the taste is weaker than before, so we should compare the two kinds of beans carefully before we sign a long contract.","t":"A：我們上個月為了省錢換了咖啡供應商，有顧客對新的咖啡豆說了什麼嗎？ B：幾位常客說【味道】比以前淡，所以在簽長期合約前，我們應該仔細比較這兩種咖啡豆。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drinks to people at a meal","c":"供應；上（菜）","s":"A: The conference starts at nine, and about two hundred guests will arrive early, so what time should the hotel start the breakfast? B: Let's ask them to serve breakfast from seven thirty in the main hall, so guests have plenty of time to eat and register before the opening speech.","t":"A：研討會九點開始，大約兩百位來賓會提早到，飯店應該幾點開始提供早餐？ B：我們請他們七點半起在主廳【供應】早餐，這樣來賓在開幕致詞前就有充裕的時間用餐和報到。"},{"w":"garnish","p":"v.","d":"to decorate food with a small amount of another food","c":"裝飾（菜餚）；點綴","s":"A: The plates at our restaurant look a little plain when the waiters bring them out, so how can we make them more attractive without spending much? B: The cooks can garnish each plate with some fresh herbs or a slice of lemon, which costs very little but makes the food look much more colorful.","t":"A：服務生端出來的餐盤看起來有點單調，我們要怎麼在不花太多錢的情況下讓它們更吸引人？ B：廚師可以用一些新鮮香草或一片檸檬來【點綴】每個盤子，這花費很少，卻能讓食物看起來更加繽紛。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant smell, especially of food or coffee","c":"香味；芳香","s":"A: Why do so many people walk into the bakery near the subway station every morning, even when they are in a hurry to get to work? B: The aroma of fresh bread and coffee fills the whole street, so people can't resist stopping for a quick breakfast on their way to the office.","t":"A：為什麼每天早上有那麼多人走進地鐵站附近的麵包店，即使他們趕著上班？ B：新鮮麵包和咖啡的【香味】瀰漫整條街，所以大家在去辦公室的路上都忍不住停下來買份快速早餐。"}]},{"unit":146,"theme":"Forest 森林","cards":[{"w":"woods","p":"n.","d":"an area of land with many trees, smaller than a forest","c":"樹林","s":"A: Where are we holding the team-building picnic next Friday, and should I tell everyone to bring comfortable shoes and warm jackets? B: We booked a quiet spot in the woods behind the conference center, so yes, people should wear good shoes because the paths are still muddy after the recent rain.","t":"A：我們下週五的團隊建立野餐在哪裡舉行？我應該提醒大家帶舒適的鞋子和保暖外套嗎？ B：我們在會議中心後面的【樹林】裡訂了一個安靜的地點，所以是的，大家應該穿好走的鞋，因為最近下過雨，小路還是很泥濘。"},{"w":"jungle","p":"n.","d":"a thick tropical forest with many plants","c":"叢林","s":"A: Why did the documentary crew ask for an extra week before they deliver the final video to our marketing department? B: Heavy rain in the jungle washed away several roads, so the team could not reach the filming location on time and had to wait for local guides to find a safer route.","t":"A：為什麼紀錄片團隊要求多一週才把最終影片交給我們行銷部？ B：【叢林】裡的大雨沖毀了好幾條道路，所以團隊無法準時抵達拍攝地點，只好等當地嚮導找到一條比較安全的路線。"},{"w":"rainforest","p":"n.","d":"a thick forest in a warm place that gets a lot of rain","c":"雨林","s":"A: What is the main message of the new advertising campaign for our organic coffee, and who is the target customer? B: We want to show that our farmers help protect the rainforest in Brazil, because younger shoppers really care about where their coffee comes from and how it affects the planet.","t":"A：我們有機咖啡的新廣告活動主要想傳達什麼？目標客群是誰？ B：我們想呈現我們的農民協助保護巴西的【雨林】，因為年輕的消費者非常在意咖啡的產地以及它對地球的影響。"},{"w":"tree","p":"n.","d":"a tall plant with a wooden trunk and branches","c":"樹","s":"A: Why is the parking lot behind our office closed this morning, and where should visitors leave their cars until it opens again? B: A large tree fell during last night's storm and damaged two cars, so visitors should use the public garage across the street until the workers remove it this afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室後面的停車場今天早上關閉了？在重新開放之前，訪客應該把車停在哪裡？ B：一棵大【樹】在昨晚的暴風雨中倒下，壓壞了兩輛車，所以在工人今天下午把它移走之前，訪客應該使用對街的公共停車場。"},{"w":"canopy","p":"n.","d":"the top layer of branches and leaves in a forest","c":"林冠；樹冠層","s":"A: Did the tour company finally finish building the new walkway for visitors at the nature park outside the city? B: Yes, and guests can now walk high above the ground through the forest canopy, where they can see colorful birds and monkeys that usually stay hidden from people on the paths below.","t":"A：旅遊公司終於完成城外自然公園的新遊客步道了嗎？ B：是的，現在遊客可以在離地很高的森林【樹冠層】中漫步，在那裡可以看到平常躲著下方步道遊客的五彩鳥類和猴子。"},{"w":"underbrush","p":"n.","d":"small bushes and plants growing under the trees in a forest","c":"林下灌木叢","s":"A: Why did the park managers close the hiking area near the lake for the whole weekend, even though the weather was perfect? B: The dry underbrush along the paths could catch fire very easily in this hot weather, so workers needed two full days to cut it back and make the area safe for visitors.","t":"A：為什麼公園管理員整個週末都關閉湖邊的健行區，即使天氣很完美？ B：步道旁乾燥的【林下灌木叢】在這種炎熱天氣下很容易起火，所以工人需要整整兩天把它修剪掉，讓這個區域對遊客來說是安全的。"},{"w":"foliage","p":"n.","d":"the leaves of trees and plants","c":"枝葉；葉子","s":"A: Why are so many hotel rooms in the mountain town already fully booked for the second week of October? B: That is when the autumn foliage turns bright red and gold, so thousands of tourists travel there to take photos, and many companies also plan weekend trips for their staff at that time.","t":"A：為什麼山城的旅館房間在十月第二週就已經全部訂滿了？ B：那正是秋天的【枝葉】轉為鮮紅和金黃的時候，所以成千上萬的遊客會去那裡拍照，許多公司也會在那時為員工安排週末旅遊。"},{"w":"evergreen","p":"adj.","d":"having green leaves all year round","c":"常綠的","s":"A: Which plants should we put along the front entrance of the new office building so that it looks nice all year? B: The designer suggested evergreen bushes, because they stay green even in winter, and they also need very little water and care, which will save our maintenance team a lot of time.","t":"A：我們應該在新辦公大樓的正門沿線種什麼植物，讓它一年四季都好看？ B：設計師建議種【常綠的】灌木，因為它們即使在冬天也保持綠色，而且只需要很少的水和照顧，可以替我們的維修團隊省下很多時間。"},{"w":"deciduous","p":"adj.","d":"losing its leaves every autumn","c":"落葉的","s":"A: Why does the courtyard outside the cafeteria get so much sunlight in winter but stay nice and cool during the summer months? B: The architect planted deciduous trees there on purpose, so their leaves block the hot sun in summer, but they drop in autumn and let warm light come through the windows.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳外的中庭冬天陽光充足，夏天卻很涼爽？ B：建築師特意在那裡種了【落葉的】樹，所以夏天它們的葉子能擋住炎熱的陽光，而秋天葉子掉落後，溫暖的光線就能透過窗戶照進來。"},{"w":"conifer","p":"n.","d":"a tree that has thin needles and produces cones","c":"針葉樹","s":"A: What kind of trees is the paper company planting on the land it bought near the river last spring? B: They are mainly planting a fast-growing conifer that has thin needles and cones, because its wood is soft and easy to process, and it can be harvested in about twenty-five years.","t":"A：造紙公司在去年春天買下的河邊土地上種的是哪一種樹？ B：他們主要種一種生長快速、有細針葉和毬果的【針葉樹】，因為它的木材柔軟又容易加工，而且大約二十五年就可以採伐。"},{"w":"pine","p":"n.","d":"a tall tree with long thin needles that stays green all year","c":"松樹","s":"A: What makes the new line of cleaning products different from the ones our competitors sell in supermarkets? B: They have a fresh pine smell that customers say reminds them of a walk in the mountains, and they are also made with plant-based ingredients that are safe for children and pets.","t":"A：我們新系列的清潔用品和競爭對手在超市賣的有什麼不同？ B：它們有清新的【松樹】香味，顧客說讓他們想起在山裡散步，而且它們是用對孩童和寵物都安全的植物性成分製成的。"},{"w":"oak","p":"n.","d":"a large tree with very hard wood","c":"橡樹；橡木","s":"A: Why is the new conference table for the boardroom so expensive compared with the one we bought for the training room? B: It is made of solid oak wood, which is very strong and heavy, and a local craftsman built it by hand, so it should last for many decades without any problems.","t":"A：為什麼董事會議室的新會議桌比我們為訓練室買的那張貴這麼多？ B：它是用實心【橡】木做的，非常堅固又沉重，而且是當地工匠手工打造的，所以應該可以用好幾十年都沒問題。"},{"w":"birch","p":"n.","d":"a tree with thin white bark and light-colored wood","c":"樺樹；樺木","s":"A: Have you decided what to use for the walls of the new reception area, because the contractor needs an answer today? B: I chose light-colored birch panels, because their pale wood with fine lines makes the room look bright and modern, and they cost less than the dark wood we saw last week.","t":"A：你決定新接待區的牆面要用什麼材料了嗎？因為承包商今天就需要答覆。 B：我選了淺色的【樺木】板，因為它那帶有細紋的淺色木材讓房間看起來明亮又現代，而且比我們上週看的深色木材便宜。"},{"w":"moss","p":"n.","d":"a small soft green plant that grows on wet ground, rocks or trees","c":"苔蘚","s":"A: Why did the building manager ask the cleaning company to come back and wash the stone steps outside the main entrance again? B: Green moss has been growing on them because of all the rain this month, and it makes the steps very slippery, so he is worried that an employee might fall and get hurt.","t":"A：為什麼大樓經理要清潔公司再回來清洗正門外的石階？ B：因為這個月一直下雨，石階上長了綠色的【苔蘚】，讓階梯變得很滑，所以他擔心員工可能會跌倒受傷。"},{"w":"fern","p":"n.","d":"a green plant with feathery leaves and no flowers","c":"蕨類植物","s":"A: What kind of plants would work well in the hotel lobby, since it doesn't get much direct sunlight during the day? B: I would recommend a large fern with soft, feathery leaves, because it grows well in the shade, likes the humid air from the fountain, and makes the space feel calm and relaxing.","t":"A：既然飯店大廳白天沒有太多直射陽光，什麼樣的植物適合放在那裡？ B：我會推薦一株有柔軟羽狀葉子的大型【蕨類植物】，因為它在陰涼處長得很好，喜歡噴泉帶來的潮濕空氣，還能讓空間感覺平靜放鬆。"},{"w":"wildlife","p":"n.","d":"wild animals and birds living in nature","c":"野生動物","s":"A: Why did the city council reject the plan to build a new shopping mall on the edge of the national park? B: Many residents complained that the construction noise and extra traffic would harm the local wildlife, especially the deer and rare birds that live in the area all year round.","t":"A：為什麼市議會否決了在國家公園邊緣興建新購物中心的計畫？ B：許多居民抱怨施工噪音和增加的車流會傷害當地的【野生動物】，尤其是全年住在那個地區的鹿和稀有鳥類。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural home of an animal or plant","c":"棲息地","s":"A: Why did the developer agree to keep that large green area next to the new apartment buildings instead of using it for parking? B: Scientists found that the wetland is an important habitat for several kinds of frogs and birds, so the city required the company to protect it before giving final approval.","t":"A：為什麼開發商同意保留新公寓大樓旁那一大片綠地，而不是拿來當停車場？ B：科學家發現那片濕地是好幾種青蛙和鳥類的重要【棲息地】，所以市政府要求該公司先保護它，才會給予最終核准。"},{"w":"trail","p":"n.","d":"a path through the countryside or a forest","c":"小徑；步道","s":"A: Are you planning to do anything relaxing this weekend after such a long and stressful week of meetings with clients? B: I'm going to walk the new trail that goes along the river to the waterfall, because it only takes about three hours, and the views are supposed to be beautiful this time of year.","t":"A：在這麼漫長又充滿壓力、一直和客戶開會的一週之後，你這週末打算做些放鬆的事嗎？ B：我要去走那條沿著河邊通往瀑布的新【步道】，因為只要大約三個小時，而且聽說每年這個時候的景色都很美。"},{"w":"hike","p":"v.","d":"to take a long walk in the countryside or mountains","c":"健行；徒步旅行","s":"A: How do you usually spend your vacation, since you always come back to the office looking so rested and full of energy? B: My wife and I like to hike in the mountains for several days, carrying our own food and tents, because being away from phones and email helps us forget about work completely.","t":"A：你通常怎麼度假？因為你每次回到辦公室都看起來精神飽滿、充滿活力。 B：我太太和我喜歡在山裡【健行】好幾天，自己背著食物和帳篷，因為遠離手機和電子郵件能讓我們完全忘掉工作。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it","c":"探索；探查","s":"A: What are the new employees going to do on their first afternoon after the orientation meeting ends? B: They will explore the whole campus with a guide, visiting the research labs, the gym, and the cafeteria, so they can learn where everything is before they start working on Monday.","t":"A：新進員工在新人說明會結束後的第一個下午要做什麼？ B：他們會跟著導覽員【探索】整個園區，參觀研究實驗室、健身房和員工餐廳，這樣他們在星期一開始上班前就能知道每個地方在哪裡。"},{"w":"dense","p":"adj.","d":"with many things growing or standing close together; thick","c":"茂密的；濃密的","s":"A: Why didn't the delivery drone reach the cabin resort in the mountains yesterday afternoon as we had planned? B: The forest around the resort is so dense that the drone couldn't find a safe place to land between the trees, so we will have to send the package by truck instead.","t":"A：為什麼送貨無人機昨天下午沒有照計畫抵達山上的小木屋度假村？ B：度假村周圍的森林太【茂密】了，無人機在樹林間找不到安全的降落地點，所以我們只好改用卡車送包裹。"},{"w":"shady","p":"adj.","d":"protected from direct sunlight","c":"陰涼的；遮蔭的","s":"A: Where should we set up the food tables for the company picnic, because the weather report says it will be very hot on Saturday? B: Let's put them in the shady area under the big trees near the lake, so the food stays fresh and guests can sit comfortably without getting sunburned.","t":"A：公司野餐的餐桌應該擺在哪裡？因為氣象報告說星期六會非常熱。 B：我們把它們放在湖邊大樹下的【陰涼】區域吧，這樣食物能保持新鮮，賓客也能舒服地坐著而不會被曬傷。"},{"w":"lush","p":"adj.","d":"having lots of healthy green plants","c":"青翠繁茂的","s":"A: What did the clients say about the resort that we chose for next month's sales conference in the south? B: They loved the photos of the lush gardens around the pool and said the hotel looked like a peaceful place to relax after long meetings, so they have already confirmed their rooms.","t":"A：客戶對我們為下個月南部業務會議選的度假村有什麼看法？ B：他們很喜歡泳池周圍【青翠繁茂的】花園照片，說那間飯店看起來是長時間開會後放鬆的寧靜地方，所以他們已經確認訂房了。"},{"w":"ancient","p":"adj.","d":"very old; from a long time ago","c":"古老的","s":"A: Why is the tour company charging more for the new day trip to the national park than for its other tours? B: The trip includes a special guide who leads visitors to an ancient forest where some of the trees are more than two thousand years old, and the group size is limited to ten people.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社新推出的國家公園一日遊比其他行程貴？ B：這個行程包含一位特別導遊，會帶遊客前往一片【古老的】森林，那裡有些樹已超過兩千年，而且每團人數限制在十人。"},{"w":"natural","p":"adj.","d":"existing in nature, not made by people","c":"天然的；自然的","s":"A: Why does our new office furniture cost more than the cheaper plastic sets the purchasing team showed us last month? B: It is made from natural materials like bamboo and wood instead of plastic, so it is better for the environment, and it also matches the company's green image very well.","t":"A：為什麼我們新的辦公家具比採購團隊上個月給我們看的便宜塑膠組合貴？ B：它是用竹子和木頭這類【天然的】材料做的，而不是塑膠，所以對環境比較好，也非常符合公司的環保形象。"},{"w":"woodland","p":"n.","d":"land that is covered with trees","c":"林地","s":"A: Is the company still planning to build its new distribution center on the land beside the highway? B: No, the plan changed because most of that property is protected woodland, so the managers are now looking at an empty factory site in the next town, which is closer to the port anyway.","t":"A：公司還打算在高速公路旁的那塊地上蓋新的物流中心嗎？ B：沒有，計畫改了，因為那塊地大部分是受保護的【林地】，所以經理們現在在看隔壁鎮的一個閒置工廠用地，而且那裡反正離港口也比較近。"},{"w":"timber","p":"n.","d":"wood that is used for building or making things","c":"木材；木料","s":"A: Why has the price of building the new warehouse gone up so much since the contractor gave us the first estimate in March? B: The cost of timber rose sharply after the floods closed several sawmills, and since the roof and walls need a lot of wood, the total budget increased by almost fifteen percent.","t":"A：為什麼自從承包商三月給我們第一份估價後，興建新倉庫的價格漲了這麼多？ B：洪水讓好幾家鋸木廠關閉後，【木材】成本大幅上漲，而屋頂和牆壁需要大量木頭，所以總預算增加了將近百分之十五。"},{"w":"logging","p":"n.","d":"the work of cutting down trees for wood","c":"伐木（業）","s":"A: Why are so many people in that small mountain town looking for new jobs at the moment? B: The government banned logging in the nearby forest last year to protect rare animals, so the local sawmill closed, and many workers who used to cut trees now need training for different careers.","t":"A：為什麼那個山區小鎮現在有這麼多人在找新工作？ B：政府去年為了保護稀有動物，禁止在附近的森林【伐木】，所以當地的鋸木廠關門了，許多以前砍樹的工人現在需要接受其他職業的訓練。"},{"w":"conservation","p":"n.","d":"the protection of nature, plants and animals","c":"保育；保護","s":"A: Why did our company decide to donate part of this year's profits to an environmental group instead of holding a big party for staff? B: The board wanted to support forest conservation projects in the region, because protecting trees and wildlife fits our green image, and most employees voted for the idea in the survey.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定把今年部分利潤捐給環保團體，而不是為員工辦一場大派對？ B：董事會想支持本地區的森林【保育】計畫，因為保護樹木和野生動物符合我們的環保形象，而且大多數員工在問卷中也投票支持這個想法。"},{"w":"ecosystem","p":"n.","d":"all the plants and animals in an area and how they live together","c":"生態系統","s":"A: Why are the scientists so worried about the new chemical factory that will open beside the river next year? B: They think the waste water could damage the whole ecosystem, because if the fish and insects die, the birds and other animals that depend on them will also have trouble surviving.","t":"A：為什麼科學家這麼擔心明年將在河邊開設的新化工廠？ B：他們認為廢水可能會破壞整個【生態系統】，因為如果魚和昆蟲死了，依賴牠們的鳥類和其他動物也將難以生存。"},{"w":"clearing","p":"n.","d":"an open area in a forest with no trees","c":"林中空地","s":"A: Where exactly will the outdoor wedding ceremony take place, since the invitation only says it will be at the mountain lodge? B: It will be held in a small grassy clearing about ten minutes' walk from the lodge, where the trees open up and guests can enjoy a beautiful view of the valley below.","t":"A：戶外婚禮究竟會在哪裡舉行？因為邀請函上只寫說在山間小屋。 B：會在離小屋步行約十分鐘的一小片草地【林中空地】舉行，那裡樹木散開，賓客可以欣賞下方山谷的美麗景色。"},{"w":"bark","p":"n.","d":"the hard outer covering of a tree","c":"樹皮","s":"A: Why is the new herbal tea from our supplier so popular with customers who have trouble sleeping at night? B: It contains a special kind of tree bark that has been used for hundreds of years to help people relax, and it also has a pleasant, slightly sweet taste that customers enjoy.","t":"A：為什麼供應商的新花草茶這麼受晚上睡不好的顧客歡迎？ B：它含有一種特殊的【樹皮】，幾百年來一直被用來幫助人放鬆，而且它還有顧客喜歡的宜人、微甜的味道。"},{"w":"branch","p":"n.","d":"a part of a tree that grows out from the trunk","c":"樹枝","s":"A: Why is there no electricity in the east wing of the office building this morning, and when will it come back on? B: During the strong winds last night, a heavy branch broke off and landed on the power line, so the electric company is repairing it now and expects to finish by noon.","t":"A：為什麼辦公大樓東翼今天早上沒有電？什麼時候會恢復？ B：昨晚強風時，一根粗重的【樹枝】斷裂並落在電線上，所以電力公司現在正在修理，預計中午前完成。"},{"w":"root","p":"n.","d":"the part of a plant that grows under the ground","c":"根","s":"A: Why is the gardening company digging up the sidewalk in front of our office building this week? B: The root of the old tree near the entrance has grown under the path and pushed the stones up, so several people have tripped, and the city wants it fixed before someone gets seriously hurt.","t":"A：為什麼園藝公司這週要挖開我們辦公大樓前的人行道？ B：入口附近那棵老樹的【根】長到步道下面，把石板頂了起來，已經有好幾個人絆倒，市政府希望在有人嚴重受傷前把它修好。"},{"w":"leaf","p":"n.","d":"a flat green part of a plant that grows from a stem","c":"葉子","s":"A: How did the design team come up with the new logo for our environmentally friendly product line? B: They used a simple green leaf as the main image, because it clearly shows that the products are made from plants, and customers in our survey said it looked fresh, clean, and easy to remember.","t":"A：設計團隊是怎麼想出我們環保產品線的新標誌的？ B：他們用一片簡單的綠色【葉子】作為主要圖像，因為它清楚表達產品是用植物製成的，而問卷中的顧客也說它看起來清新、乾淨又好記。"}]},{"unit":147,"theme":"Free 自由；免費","cards":[{"w":"freedom","p":"n.","d":"the right or ability to act, speak, or choose as you want","c":"自由","s":"A: Why did you decide to leave the large bank and join a small startup company downtown, even though the salary is a little lower? B: I wanted more freedom to choose my own projects and working hours, and my new manager trusts the team to make important decisions without asking her every time.","t":"A：你為什麼決定離開那家大銀行，加入市中心的一間小型新創公司，即使薪水低了一點？ B：我想要有更多【自由】來選擇自己的專案和工作時間，而且我的新主管信任團隊，讓我們不必每次都問她就能做重要決定。"},{"w":"liberate","p":"v.","d":"to set someone or something free from control or a limit","c":"解放；使擺脫","s":"A: How has the new accounting software changed the way your department handles all the monthly reports and customer invoices? B: It has helped liberate our staff from hours of boring paperwork every week, so now they can spend more time talking with clients and planning next year's budget.","t":"A：新的會計軟體如何改變你們部門處理每月報告和客戶發票的方式？ B：它幫助我們的員工【擺脫】每週好幾個小時無聊的文書工作，所以現在他們能花更多時間和客戶溝通，並規劃明年的預算。"},{"w":"liberty","p":"n.","d":"the freedom to live and act as you choose, often protected by law","c":"自由；自由權","s":"A: Can I post photos of the new product design on my personal social media account before the official launch next month? B: No, I'm afraid you are not at liberty to share any details about the design yet, because the contract with our partner company says everything must stay secret until the press conference.","t":"A：我可以在下個月正式上市之前，把新產品設計的照片貼到我的個人社群帳號上嗎？ B：不行，恐怕你目前還沒有【自由】分享任何設計細節，因為我們和合作公司簽的合約規定，在記者會之前一切都必須保密。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"not controlled by or needing help from other people or groups","c":"獨立的","s":"A: Why did the board of directors hire an outside company to check the factory's safety records instead of asking our own managers to do it? B: They wanted an independent review from experts who have no connection to our company, so that customers and investors would trust the results completely.","t":"A：董事會為什麼聘請外部公司來檢查工廠的安全紀錄，而不是請我們自己的主管來做？ B：他們想要一份由與公司毫無關係的專家所做的【獨立】審查，這樣客戶和投資人才會完全信任結果。"},{"w":"autonomous","p":"adj.","d":"able to make decisions and act without being controlled by others","c":"自主的；自治的","s":"A: How does the regional office in Kaohsiung work with headquarters when it needs to make quick decisions about local marketing campaigns? B: The office is fairly autonomous, so the branch manager can approve small advertising budgets on her own, but she still sends a short report to headquarters at the end of each month.","t":"A：高雄的區域辦公室需要快速決定在地行銷活動時，是如何與總部配合的？ B：那間辦公室相當【自主】，所以分公司經理可以自行核准小額廣告預算，但她每個月底仍會寄一份簡短報告給總部。"},{"w":"unrestricted","p":"adj.","d":"not limited or controlled by rules","c":"不受限制的","s":"A: Do new employees have to ask the IT department for permission every time they want to use the online research database at work? B: No, everyone on the staff gets unrestricted access to the database from the first day, so you can search for articles and market reports whenever you need them for a project.","t":"A：新進員工每次想在公司使用線上研究資料庫時，都必須向資訊部門申請許可嗎？ B：不用，所有員工從第一天起就享有【不受限制的】資料庫使用權，所以你在專案需要時，隨時都可以搜尋文章和市場報告。"},{"w":"unconstrained","p":"adj.","d":"not held back or limited by anything","c":"不受約束的；無拘束的","s":"A: What was different about the brainstorming session that the design team held at the mountain resort last weekend? B: The director told everyone to share completely unconstrained ideas without worrying about cost or time limits, so people felt relaxed and came up with several creative plans for the new product line.","t":"A：設計團隊上週末在山區度假村舉辦的腦力激盪會議有什麼不同？ B：主管要大家分享完全【不受約束的】想法，不用擔心成本或時間限制，所以大家都很放鬆，為新產品線想出了好幾個有創意的計畫。"},{"w":"voluntary","p":"adj.","d":"done because you choose to, not because you must","c":"自願的","s":"A: Do all the employees have to join the beach cleanup activity that the company is organizing next Saturday morning? B: No, it's completely voluntary, but the human resources team hopes many people will come because it's a good chance to help the community and meet coworkers from other departments.","t":"A：所有員工都必須參加公司下週六早上舉辦的淨灘活動嗎？ B：不用，那完全是【自願的】，但人資團隊希望很多人會來，因為這是幫助社區、認識其他部門同事的好機會。"},{"w":"gratis","p":"adv.","d":"without having to pay; free of charge","c":"免費地","s":"A: Will the hotel charge us extra if we use the meeting room for a short planning session before the conference starts tomorrow? B: Since your company booked twenty rooms for three nights, the manager said we can use the small meeting room gratis, and they'll even bring us coffee and water.","t":"A：如果我們明天在研討會開始前使用會議室開個簡短的規劃會議，飯店會額外收費嗎？ B：因為你們公司訂了二十間房住三晚，經理說我們可以【免費】使用那間小會議室，他們甚至還會送咖啡和水過來。"},{"w":"complimentary","p":"adj.","d":"given free, especially by a business","c":"免費贈送的","s":"A: Is breakfast included in the price of the room, or do I need to pay for it separately at the restaurant downstairs? B: All guests receive a complimentary breakfast between six and ten every morning, and business travelers can also pick up a free newspaper at the front desk.","t":"A：早餐有包含在房價裡嗎？還是我需要在樓下餐廳另外付費？ B：所有房客每天早上六點到十點都可享用【免費】早餐，商務旅客還可以在櫃檯領取一份免費報紙。"},{"w":"costless","p":"adj.","d":"not costing any money","c":"不花錢的；免費的","s":"A: Our department has almost no budget left this quarter, so how can we improve teamwork among the new staff members? B: There are several costless ways to do it, such as holding a weekly lunch where people bring their own food, or asking senior employees to mentor newcomers during regular office hours.","t":"A：我們部門這一季幾乎沒有預算了，要怎麼增進新進員工之間的團隊合作？ B：有幾種【不花錢的】方法，例如每週舉辦一次大家自備食物的午餐會，或是請資深員工在上班時間指導新人。"},{"w":"exempt","p":"adj.","d":"not required to do or pay something that others must","c":"被免除的；豁免的","s":"A: Do I have to pay import tax on the product samples that our supplier in Japan is sending to the office next week? B: Small samples under a certain value are usually exempt from import tax, but you should still check with the shipping company and keep the invoice in case customs asks for it.","t":"A：我們日本供應商下週要寄到辦公室的產品樣品，我需要付進口稅嗎？ B：低於一定價值的小型樣品通常【免】徵進口稅，但你還是應該向貨運公司確認，並保留發票以防海關要求查看。"},{"w":"exemption","p":"n.","d":"permission not to do or pay something that others must","c":"免除；豁免","s":"A: Why didn't Mr. Chen attend the required safety training session for all warehouse workers on Monday afternoon? B: He received an exemption because he already finished the same course at his previous company last month, and he showed the manager his certificate to prove it.","t":"A：陳先生為什麼沒有參加週一下午所有倉庫員工都必須參加的安全訓練課程？ B：他獲得了【免除】，因為他上個月已經在前一家公司完成了同樣的課程，而且他也向經理出示了證書作為證明。"},{"w":"spare","p":"adj.","d":"extra; not being used and ready when needed","c":"備用的；空閒的","s":"A: The printer in the meeting room just stopped working, and the clients will arrive in ten minutes for the presentation. What should we do? B: Don't worry, there's a spare printer in the storage room next to the kitchen, so I'll bring it here and connect it to your laptop right away.","t":"A：會議室的印表機剛剛壞了，客戶再十分鐘就要來聽簡報了，我們該怎麼辦？ B：別擔心，茶水間旁邊的儲藏室裡有一台【備用的】印表機，我馬上把它搬過來接上你的筆電。"},{"w":"available","p":"adj.","d":"free to be used or to meet someone","c":"有空的；可用的","s":"A: I'd like to schedule a short meeting with the marketing director to discuss the new advertising plan before Friday. B: Let me check her calendar. She's busy all day Wednesday with clients, but she'll be available on Thursday morning from nine to eleven if that time works for you.","t":"A：我想在週五前和行銷總監安排一個簡短的會議，討論新的廣告計畫。 B：我查一下她的行程。她週三整天都要見客戶，但如果你方便的話，她週四早上九點到十一點【有空】。"},{"w":"idle","p":"adj.","d":"not working or being used","c":"閒置的；無所事事的","s":"A: Why did the factory manager decide to sell two of the old packaging machines at the back of the building? B: They have been sitting idle for almost a year since we moved production to the new line, so selling them will free up space and bring in some extra money.","t":"A：工廠經理為什麼決定賣掉大樓後方兩台舊的包裝機？ B：自從我們把生產移到新產線後，它們已經【閒置】將近一年了，所以賣掉它們可以騰出空間，還能帶來一些額外收入。"},{"w":"release","p":"v.","d":"to let someone or something go free; to make something available to the public","c":"釋放；發布","s":"A: When is the company going to tell customers about the new smartphone that the engineers have been developing all year? B: The marketing team plans to release the official details at a press conference next Tuesday, and the phone will go on sale in stores two weeks after that.","t":"A：公司什麼時候要向客戶公布工程師們研發了一整年的新智慧型手機？ B：行銷團隊計畫在下週二的記者會上【發布】正式細節，而手機會在那之後兩週於門市開賣。"},{"w":"escape","p":"v.","d":"to get away from a place or situation","c":"逃離；逃脫","s":"A: Where are you going for the long holiday weekend, and are you taking your work laptop with you? B: I'm going to a quiet hot spring hotel in the mountains to escape the noise of the city for a few days, and I'm leaving my laptop at home so I can really rest.","t":"A：連假你要去哪裡？會帶工作用的筆電去嗎？ B：我要去山上一間安靜的溫泉旅館，【逃離】城市的喧囂幾天，而且我要把筆電留在家，這樣才能真正休息。"},{"w":"loosen","p":"v.","d":"to make something less tight or less strict","c":"鬆開；放寬","s":"A: Has the company changed its dress code for the summer, since it's been so hot and humid in Taipei lately? B: Yes, management decided to loosen the rules a little, so from June to September men don't have to wear ties unless they are meeting important clients.","t":"A：最近台北這麼濕熱，公司夏天的服裝規定有改變嗎？ B：有，管理階層決定稍微【放寬】規定，所以從六月到九月，男士除非要見重要客戶，否則不必打領帶。"},{"w":"detach","p":"v.","d":"to separate one thing from another","c":"拆下；分離","s":"A: How do I return the registration form for the training workshop, and do I need to send the whole brochure back to you? B: Just detach the form at the bottom of the last page along the dotted line, fill in your name and department, and drop it in the box at the front desk.","t":"A：訓練工作坊的報名表要怎麼交回？我需要把整本手冊寄回給你嗎？ B：只要沿著虛線把最後一頁下方的表格【撕下來】，填上你的姓名和部門，然後投進櫃檯的箱子裡就好。"},{"w":"unbind","p":"v.","d":"to untie or free something that is tied or bound","c":"解開；鬆綁","s":"A: The old company reports in the archive room are tied together with string, so how can we scan each page for the new digital system? B: First, carefully unbind each stack of documents, then put the pages in order on the table, and the scanner will process about fifty pages a minute.","t":"A：檔案室裡的舊公司報告都用繩子綁在一起，我們要怎麼把每一頁掃描進新的數位系統？ B：首先，小心地【解開】每一疊文件，接著把頁面依序放在桌上，掃描機每分鐘大約可以處理五十頁。"},{"w":"unlocked","p":"adj.","d":"not locked, so it can be opened easily","c":"未上鎖的","s":"A: The security guard said someone forgot to secure a door last night after the office party. Do you know which one it was? B: It was the back door near the parking lot, which stayed unlocked until morning, so the manager has asked the last person leaving to check every exit.","t":"A：警衛說昨晚辦公室派對結束後有人忘了鎖門，你知道是哪一扇嗎？ B：是停車場旁邊的後門，它一直到早上都【沒上鎖】，所以經理要求最後離開的人檢查每一個出口。"},{"w":"vacant","p":"adj.","d":"empty; not being used or filled by anyone","c":"空著的；空缺的","s":"A: Has the company found someone to replace the sales manager who moved to the Singapore branch last month? B: Not yet, the position is still vacant, so the director is interviewing three candidates this week and hopes to make a final decision before the end of the month.","t":"A：公司找到人接替上個月調到新加坡分公司的業務經理了嗎？ B：還沒，那個職位仍然【空缺】，所以總監這週要面試三位應徵者，希望在月底前做出最後決定。"},{"w":"open","p":"adj.","d":"not closed; ready for people to use or join","c":"開放的；營業的","s":"A: Can visitors from other companies join the technology seminar that our research team is holding at the convention center next month? B: Yes, the seminar is open to the public, but everyone needs to register online by the end of this week because there are only two hundred seats.","t":"A：其他公司的訪客可以參加我們研究團隊下個月在會展中心舉辦的科技研討會嗎？ B：可以，研討會【開放】給一般大眾，但因為只有兩百個座位，大家都必須在這週結束前上網報名。"},{"w":"clear","p":"adj.","d":"free from things that block or cover; not busy","c":"暢通的；空出的","s":"A: Is it a good time to drive to the airport now, or should we wait until after the morning rush hour is over? B: I just checked the traffic app, and the highway is clear all the way to the airport right now, so if we leave in five minutes, we'll arrive with plenty of time.","t":"A：現在開車去機場是好時機嗎？還是我們該等早上尖峰時段過了再出發？ B：我剛查了交通應用程式，現在高速公路一路到機場都很【暢通】，如果我們五分鐘內出發，就會有充裕的時間抵達。"},{"w":"relaxed","p":"adj.","d":"calm and not worried or strict","c":"放鬆的；輕鬆的","s":"A: What is the working atmosphere like at your new office, compared to the bank where you worked for five years? B: It's much more relaxed here, because people wear casual clothes, managers welcome questions, and we often have coffee together in the afternoon while we discuss our projects.","t":"A：和你工作了五年的那家銀行相比，你新辦公室的工作氣氛如何？ B：這裡【輕鬆】多了，因為大家穿便服，主管歡迎提問，而且我們下午常常一起喝咖啡、討論專案。"},{"w":"carefree","p":"adj.","d":"having no worries or problems","c":"無憂無慮的","s":"A: You look very happy and rested today. Did you finally take the vacation you were planning after the busy end of the year? B: Yes, I spent a carefree week at the beach with my family, and I didn't check my work email even once, so I feel ready for the new project.","t":"A：你今天看起來很開心又很有精神，你終於在忙碌的年底之後去了計畫好的假期嗎？ B：是啊，我和家人在海邊度過了【無憂無慮的】一週，而且一次工作郵件都沒看，所以我覺得已經準備好迎接新專案了。"},{"w":"unhindered","p":"adj.","d":"not stopped or slowed down by anything","c":"不受阻礙的","s":"A: Why did the building manager ask everyone to move their boxes out of the hallway outside the conference room this morning? B: The fire inspector is visiting this afternoon, and the emergency exits must allow unhindered movement, so nothing can block the path between the offices and the stairs.","t":"A：大樓管理員今天早上為什麼要求大家把箱子搬離會議室外的走廊？ B：消防檢查員今天下午要來，緊急出口必須讓人【不受阻礙地】通行，所以辦公室和樓梯之間的通道不能有任何東西擋住。"},{"w":"unlimited","p":"adj.","d":"without any limit on amount or number","c":"無限的；不受限制的","s":"A: Which mobile phone plan did the company choose for the sales staff who travel around the country every week? B: We chose a plan with unlimited data, so the team can join video calls and send large files from anywhere without worrying about extra charges at the end of the month.","t":"A：公司為每週跑遍全國的業務人員選了哪一種手機方案？ B：我們選了【無限】流量的方案，這樣團隊在任何地方都能參加視訊會議、傳送大型檔案，月底也不用擔心額外費用。"},{"w":"boundless","p":"adj.","d":"seeming to have no end or limit","c":"無窮的；無限的","s":"A: How does the new intern manage to finish so many tasks every day and still help other people on the team? B: She has boundless energy and a real interest in learning everything about the business, so the managers are already thinking about offering her a full-time job after graduation.","t":"A：新來的實習生是怎麼做到每天完成這麼多工作，還能幫助團隊其他人的？ B：她有【無窮的】精力，也真心想學習公司業務的一切，所以主管們已經在考慮她畢業後提供她全職工作。"},{"w":"unburdened","p":"adj.","d":"free from a heavy load, worry, or duty","c":"卸下負擔的；無負擔的","s":"A: How did you feel after you finally handed the big hotel project over to the new team leader last Friday? B: I felt completely unburdened for the first time in months, because I no longer had to answer calls late at night or worry about every small problem on the construction site.","t":"A：上週五你終於把大型飯店專案交給新的團隊負責人後，感覺如何？ B：這是幾個月來我第一次覺得完全【卸下了重擔】，因為我不用再深夜接電話，也不必擔心工地的每一個小問題。"},{"w":"emancipate","p":"v.","d":"to free people from legal, social, or other control","c":"解放；使不受束縛","s":"A: Why is the government giving small businesses money to buy new digital tools and attend online training courses this year? B: Officials hope the program will emancipate local shop owners from old, slow ways of working, so they can compete with large companies and reach customers around the world.","t":"A：政府今年為什麼要補助小型企業購買新的數位工具並參加線上訓練課程？ B：官員希望這個計畫能讓在地店家【擺脫】老舊緩慢的工作方式，使他們能與大公司競爭，並接觸到全世界的顧客。"},{"w":"emancipation","p":"n.","d":"the act of freeing people from control or limits","c":"解放","s":"A: What is the main topic of the history exhibition that the city museum is opening near our office next week? B: It tells the story of the emancipation of factory workers in the nineteenth century, showing how they won fair wages and shorter working hours after many years of struggle.","t":"A：市立博物館下週要在我們辦公室附近開幕的歷史展覽，主題是什麼？ B：它講述十九世紀工廠工人獲得【解放】的故事，展示他們如何在多年的奮鬥後，爭取到合理的薪資和較短的工時。"},{"w":"discharge","p":"v.","d":"to officially allow someone to leave a hospital, job, or duty","c":"讓…出院；解除","s":"A: Is your manager still in the hospital after the minor car accident she had on the way to work last Tuesday? B: The doctors plan to discharge her tomorrow morning, but she will work from home for another week before she comes back to the office.","t":"A：你的經理上週二上班途中發生小車禍後，還在住院嗎？ B：醫生計畫明天早上讓她【出院】，但她回辦公室之前，還會在家工作一個星期。"},{"w":"redeem","p":"v.","d":"to exchange a coupon or points for goods or money","c":"兌換；贖回","s":"A: I have collected a lot of points on the company's business travel card. How can I use them before they expire at the end of the year? B: You can redeem them for free hotel nights or airline tickets on the card's website, and the process only takes a few minutes.","t":"A：我在公司的商務差旅卡上累積了很多點數，要怎麼在年底到期前使用它們？ B：你可以在信用卡網站上用點數【兌換】免費住宿或機票，整個流程只需要幾分鐘。"}]},{"unit":148,"theme":"Friend 朋友","cards":[{"w":"close friend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a friend you know very well and trust","c":"好朋友；密友","s":"A: Who is the woman sitting next to our new marketing director at the welcome lunch, and why are they laughing together like they have known each other for years? B: She is his close friend from university, and she now works for one of our biggest suppliers, so he invited her to meet the rest of the team.","t":"A：在歡迎午宴上坐在我們新任行銷總監旁邊的那位女士是誰？為什麼他們一起笑得好像已經認識很多年了？ B：她是他大學時的【好朋友】，現在在我們最大的供應商之一工作，所以他邀請她來認識團隊其他成員。"},{"w":"fair-weather friend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a friend who leaves you when you have problems","c":"只能共享樂不能共患難的朋友；酒肉朋友","s":"A: Why did Tom stop asking Kevin to join the weekend hiking trips that the whole department usually goes on together? B: When Tom lost his job last year, Kevin never called or offered help even once, so Tom realized he was just a fair-weather friend who only stays around when everything is going well.","t":"A：為什麼湯姆不再邀請凱文參加整個部門通常一起去的週末健行活動了？ B：去年湯姆失業時，凱文一次也沒打電話或提供幫助，所以湯姆發現他只是個【只能共享樂、不能共患難的朋友】，只有在一切順利時才會待在身邊。"},{"w":"break up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end a romantic relationship","c":"分手","s":"A: Why has Julia been so quiet in meetings this week, and why did she ask her manager for a few days off next month? B: She and her boyfriend decided to break up after five years together, so she needs some time to move out of their apartment and find a new place near the office.","t":"A：茱莉亞這週開會為什麼這麼安靜？她為什麼向經理請了下個月幾天假？ B：她和男友交往五年後決定【分手】，所以她需要一些時間搬出他們的公寓，並在公司附近找新的住處。"},{"w":"drift apart","p":"v.phr.","d":"to slowly become less close to someone","c":"漸行漸遠；逐漸疏遠","s":"A: Do you still keep in contact with the colleagues you worked with at the bank in Kaohsiung before you moved to Taipei? B: Not really, because we were all busy with new jobs and families, so we started to drift apart slowly, and now we only send each other messages on birthdays.","t":"A：你搬到台北之前在高雄銀行一起工作的同事，你們還有保持聯絡嗎？ B：其實沒有，因為大家都忙於新工作和家庭，所以我們慢慢地【漸行漸遠】，現在只在生日時互傳訊息。"},{"w":"strike up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to begin a conversation or friendship with someone","c":"開始（交談、友誼）","s":"A: How did you meet the sales manager from that Japanese company who offered us the big contract last month? B: We were both waiting for a delayed flight at the airport, so I decided to strike up a conversation about the weather, and we ended up talking about business for two hours.","t":"A：你是怎麼認識那家日本公司的業務經理的？他上個月給了我們那份大合約。 B：我們當時都在機場等一班延誤的班機，所以我決定和他【開始】聊聊天氣，結果我們談了兩個小時的生意。"},{"w":"come across","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find or meet someone or something by chance","c":"偶然發現；偶然遇到","s":"A: Where did you find that great Italian restaurant where we had the team dinner to celebrate the end of the project? B: I happened to come across it while I was walking home from the train station one evening, and the owner was so friendly that I booked a table right away.","t":"A：你是在哪裡找到那家很棒的義大利餐廳的？我們在那裡吃了慶祝專案結束的團隊晚餐。 B：有天晚上我從火車站走路回家時碰巧【偶然發現】它，老闆非常友善，所以我馬上就訂了位。"},{"w":"walk up to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to walk toward someone until you are near them","c":"走向；走到……面前","s":"A: How did the new intern make friends so quickly when she doesn't know anyone in the company yet? B: On her first morning, she decided to walk up to a group of designers in the break room, introduce herself with a big smile, and ask them for advice about the best places to eat lunch nearby.","t":"A：那位新實習生在公司還不認識任何人，她怎麼能這麼快就交到朋友？ B：她第一天早上決定【走向】休息室裡的一群設計師，帶著大大的笑容自我介紹，並請他們推薦附近最好的午餐地點。"},{"w":"suspicious","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that something is wrong or someone is not honest","c":"可疑的；懷疑的","s":"A: Why did the receptionist call the security guard when that man came into the lobby without an appointment this afternoon? B: She felt suspicious because he kept asking questions about the manager's schedule and refused to give his name, so she wanted someone to check who he was before letting him upstairs.","t":"A：今天下午那個男子沒有預約就進入大廳時，接待員為什麼打電話給警衛？ B：她覺得【可疑】，因為他一直問經理的行程卻拒絕說出自己的名字，所以她想在讓他上樓前先請人確認他的身分。"},{"w":"jealous","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy because someone has something you want","c":"嫉妒的","s":"A: Why does Ben seem upset whenever the manager praises Lisa during our weekly team meetings? B: I think he is a little jealous because she got the promotion he wanted, even though they started at the company on the same day and have always been good friends.","t":"A：為什麼每次經理在每週團隊會議上稱讚麗莎時，班看起來都不高興？ B：我想他有點【嫉妒】，因為她得到了他想要的升遷，雖然他們同一天進公司，而且一直都是好朋友。"},{"w":"understandable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to accept or forgive because of the situation","c":"可以理解的","s":"A: I'm sorry I forgot to reply to your email about the dinner plans, but I was busy preparing for the client visit all week. B: Don't worry, it's completely understandable, because everyone in the office was working late, so let's just choose another night next week when we are both free.","t":"A：很抱歉我忘了回覆你關於晚餐計畫的電子郵件，因為我整週都在忙著準備客戶來訪。 B：別擔心，這完全【可以理解】，因為辦公室裡每個人都在加班，所以我們就改選下週兩人都有空的另一個晚上吧。"},{"w":"lonely","p":"adj.","d":"sad because you are alone or have no friends","c":"孤單的；寂寞的","s":"A: How is your brother doing since he moved to London to work at the new branch office last spring? B: He felt quite lonely during the first few months because he didn't know anyone there, but now he plays football with his coworkers every Saturday and has made several good friends.","t":"A：你哥哥去年春天搬到倫敦的新分公司工作後過得怎麼樣？ B：最初幾個月他覺得很【孤單】，因為在那裡誰也不認識，但現在他每週六都和同事踢足球，也交了幾個好朋友。"},{"w":"embarrassed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling shy or silly because of something you did","c":"尷尬的；難為情的","s":"A: Why did Mark leave the company party so early on Friday night when everyone else stayed until midnight? B: He felt really embarrassed after he called the new director by the wrong name twice during his speech, and some people in the room started laughing, so he wanted to go home quietly.","t":"A：週五晚上其他人都待到午夜，為什麼馬克那麼早就離開公司派對？ B：他在致詞時兩次叫錯新任總監的名字，有些人開始笑，他覺得非常【尷尬】，所以想悄悄回家。"},{"w":"a shoulder to cry on","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who listens and comforts you when you are sad","c":"可以依靠傾訴的人","s":"A: Why do so many people in the office go to Grace's desk when they have problems at work or at home? B: She always listens patiently and never judges anyone, so when a colleague is having a hard week, she offers a shoulder to cry on and some good advice over a cup of tea.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室裡這麼多人在工作上或家裡遇到問題時都會去找葛瑞絲？ B：她總是耐心傾聽且從不批評任何人，所以當同事度過辛苦的一週時，她會提供【可以依靠傾訴的肩膀】，並邊喝茶邊給些好建議。"},{"w":"see eye to eye","p":"v.phr.","d":"to agree with someone","c":"意見一致；看法相同","s":"A: Are the two project managers going to agree on the new budget before the deadline on Friday? B: I doubt it, because they rarely see eye to eye on spending, and last week they argued for an hour about whether we should hire more staff or buy new software.","t":"A：這兩位專案經理會在週五截止日前就新預算達成共識嗎？ B：我很懷疑，因為他們在花費上很少【意見一致】，上週他們還為了該多雇員工還是買新軟體爭論了一個小時。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to grow or make something grow over time","c":"發展；培養","s":"A: How did you and your business partner start the café together when you came from completely different backgrounds? B: We met in a cooking class five years ago, and over time we began to develop a strong friendship, so when she suggested opening a café, I trusted her completely.","t":"A：你和你的事業夥伴背景完全不同，你們是怎麼一起開咖啡館的？ B：我們五年前在烹飪課上認識，隨著時間我們開始【發展】出深厚的友誼，所以當她提議開咖啡館時，我完全信任她。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it is spoiled","c":"毀掉；破壞","s":"A: Why aren't Sam and Peter talking to each other anymore after working side by side for ten years? B: Sam borrowed a large amount of money from Peter and never paid it back, and that one bad decision helped to ruin a friendship that had lasted since high school.","t":"A：山姆和彼得並肩工作了十年，為什麼現在不再跟對方說話了？ B：山姆向彼得借了一大筆錢卻一直沒還，那一個糟糕的決定【毀了】一段從高中就持續至今的友誼。"},{"w":"renew","p":"v.","d":"to start something again or make it valid for longer","c":"重拾；更新；續約","s":"A: Did you meet anyone interesting at the industry conference in Singapore last weekend? B: Yes, I ran into a classmate I hadn't seen in ten years, and we decided to renew our friendship by meeting for coffee every month, since our offices are now on the same street.","t":"A：你上週末在新加坡的產業研討會上有遇到什麼有趣的人嗎？ B：有，我碰到一位十年沒見的同學，我們決定每個月見面喝咖啡來【重拾】我們的友誼，因為我們的辦公室現在就在同一條街上。"},{"w":"rekindle","p":"v.","d":"to make an old feeling or relationship strong again","c":"重燃；重新點燃","s":"A: Why did you join the alumni dinner last night when you usually say you are too tired after work? B: I wanted to rekindle my old friendship with Anna, because we were very close at university, but we stopped talking after she moved abroad for her first job.","t":"A：你平常總說下班後太累了，為什麼昨晚參加了校友晚宴？ B：我想【重燃】和安娜的舊友誼，因為我們大學時非常要好，但她出國工作後我們就不再聯絡了。"},{"w":"fall for someone","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start to love someone","c":"愛上某人","s":"A: Why is Daniel suddenly so interested in joining the volunteer group that cleans the beach every Saturday morning? B: I think it's because it's easy to fall for someone who shares your interests, and he has been spending a lot of time with the friendly woman who organizes the group.","t":"A：為什麼丹尼爾突然對參加每週六早上淨灘的志工團這麼有興趣？ B：我想是因為人很容易【愛上】和自己興趣相投的人，而他最近和負責籌辦這個團體的那位友善女士相處了很多時間。"},{"w":"fall head over heels","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fall deeply and suddenly in love","c":"深深愛上；神魂顛倒","s":"A: Why did Kevin request a transfer to the Tokyo office after he came back from the training program there? B: He met a lovely interpreter during the program and seemed to fall head over heels for her within a week, so now he wants to live in the same city and spend more time with her.","t":"A：凱文從東京的培訓課程回來後，為什麼申請調職到東京辦公室？ B：他在課程中認識了一位可愛的口譯員，似乎在一週內就【深深愛上】她，所以現在他想住在同一個城市，和她多相處。"},{"w":"fall out with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have an argument and stop being friendly with someone","c":"與……鬧翻；與……吵架","s":"A: Why is Rachel eating lunch alone these days instead of joining her usual group in the cafeteria? B: She didn't want to fall out with her teammates, but they had a big argument about who should get credit for the successful advertising campaign, and now they are hardly speaking.","t":"A：瑞秋最近為什麼都獨自吃午餐，而不是和平常那群人在餐廳一起吃？ B：她並不想和隊友【鬧翻】，但他們為了成功的廣告活動功勞該歸誰大吵一架，現在幾乎不說話了。"},{"w":"hit it off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to like each other as soon as you meet","c":"一見如故；一拍即合","s":"A: How was the dinner with the new client from Canada that you organized at the hotel restaurant last night? B: It went really well, because the client and our sales director seemed to hit it off immediately, talking about golf and travel all evening, and they have already scheduled another meeting.","t":"A：你昨晚在飯店餐廳為加拿大新客戶安排的晚餐怎麼樣？ B：非常順利，因為客戶和我們的業務總監似乎馬上就【一見如故】，整晚都在聊高爾夫和旅行，而且他們已經安排了另一次會議。"},{"w":"ups and downs","p":"n.phr.","d":"the good times and bad times in life or work","c":"起起伏伏；盛衰","s":"A: How have you and your business partner stayed friends for twenty years while running a small company together? B: Of course we have had many ups and downs, including two difficult years when sales dropped, but we always talk honestly about problems and celebrate every success together.","t":"A：你和事業夥伴一起經營小公司，是怎麼維持二十年友誼的？ B：我們當然經歷過許多【起起伏伏】，包括兩年銷售下滑的艱難時期，但我們總是坦誠討論問題，並一起慶祝每一次成功。"},{"w":"lose touch with someone","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop communicating with someone","c":"和某人失去聯絡","s":"A: Why are you working so hard to organize a reunion for everyone from our first job at the hotel? B: When you change jobs and move to a new city, it's easy to lose touch with someone you really care about, so I want to bring everyone together again before more years pass.","t":"A：你為什麼這麼努力為我們當年第一份飯店工作的所有同事籌辦聚會？ B：當你換工作又搬到新城市時，很容易就和真正在乎的人【失去聯絡】，所以我想在更多年過去之前再把大家聚在一起。"},{"w":"love at first sight","p":"n.phr.","d":"loving someone or something the first time you see it","c":"一見鍾情","s":"A: Is it true that the owner of the bakery downstairs met his wife when she came in to buy bread? B: Yes, he says it was love at first sight, because the moment she walked through the door on a rainy morning, he knew he wanted to marry her, and they opened a second shop together.","t":"A：樓下麵包店的老闆是在他太太進來買麵包時認識她的，這是真的嗎？ B：是的，他說那是【一見鍾情】，因為在一個下雨的早晨她走進門的那一刻，他就知道想娶她，後來他們還一起開了第二家店。"},{"w":"tie the knot","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get married","c":"結婚","s":"A: Why are Peter and Amy both taking two weeks of vacation in October, right in the middle of our busiest season? B: They have finally decided to tie the knot at a small beach resort in Bali, and they invited everyone in the accounting department to celebrate with them.","t":"A：為什麼彼得和艾美都在十月、我們最忙的季節中間請兩週假？ B：他們終於決定在峇里島一家小型海灘度假村【結婚】，而且他們邀請了會計部的每個人一起慶祝。"},{"w":"settle down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start living a quiet, stable life in one place","c":"安頓下來；定居","s":"A: Are you still planning to apply for the overseas sales position that requires traveling to a different country every month? B: Not anymore, because my partner and I want to settle down in Taichung, buy a small apartment near my parents, and start a family in the next few years.","t":"A：你還打算申請那個每個月都要去不同國家出差的海外業務職位嗎？ B：不了，因為我和伴侶想在台中【安頓下來】，在我爸媽家附近買間小公寓，並在接下來幾年組成家庭。"},{"w":"well matched","p":"adj.phr.","d":"suitable for each other or equal in ability","c":"非常相配的；旗鼓相當的","s":"A: Why did the manager put Helen and Jason on the same team for the new product launch? B: She believes they are well matched, because Helen is great with numbers and planning, while Jason is creative and friendly with customers, so together they should make the project a success.","t":"A：經理為什麼把海倫和傑森分到同一組負責新產品上市？ B：她認為他們【非常相配】，因為海倫擅長數字和規劃，而傑森有創意又對客戶友善，所以他們合作應該能讓專案成功。"},{"w":"get to know somebody","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spend time with someone and learn about them","c":"認識、了解某人","s":"A: Why does our company organize a weekend trip to the mountains for all new employees every September? B: The managers think it is much easier to get to know somebody when you share fun activities outside the office, so hiking and cooking dinner together help new staff build trust with their coworkers quickly.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司每年九月都為所有新進員工舉辦週末山區旅行？ B：經理們認為在辦公室外一起參加有趣的活動，會更容易【認識、了解一個人】，所以一起健行和煮晚餐能幫助新員工很快和同事建立信任。"},{"w":"roughly","p":"adv.","d":"about; not exactly","c":"大約；大致","s":"A: How many people do you expect at the farewell party for our retiring sales manager next Friday evening? B: I think roughly eighty people will come, including many former colleagues and longtime customers, so we booked the largest room at the hotel and ordered extra food just in case.","t":"A：你預計下週五晚上為我們即將退休的業務經理舉辦的歡送會會有多少人參加？ B：我想【大約】會有八十人，包括許多前同事和老客戶，所以我們預訂了飯店最大的廳，並多訂了一些食物以防萬一。"},{"w":"amiable","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and pleasant","c":"和藹可親的；友善的","s":"A: What do customers usually say about the new receptionist who started working at the front desk last month? B: They say she is very amiable and always greets visitors with a warm smile, and several clients have even written emails to thank her for helping them find the right meeting room.","t":"A：顧客通常怎麼評價上個月開始在櫃台工作的新接待員？ B：他們說她非常【和藹可親】，總是用溫暖的笑容迎接訪客，甚至有幾位客戶寫電子郵件感謝她幫忙找到正確的會議室。"},{"w":"mutual friends","p":"n.phr.","d":"friends that two people both have","c":"共同的朋友","s":"A: How did you find out that the new finance director used to work with your cousin in Hong Kong? B: We discovered that we had several mutual friends when we connected on a business networking website, so we talked about them during lunch and quickly felt comfortable with each other.","t":"A：你是怎麼發現新任財務總監以前在香港和你表哥共事過的？ B：我們在商務社群網站上互相加為聯絡人時，發現我們有好幾位【共同的朋友】，所以午餐時聊起他們，很快就和彼此相處得很自在。"},{"w":"console","p":"v.","d":"to make someone who is sad feel better","c":"安慰","s":"A: Why was Linda sitting with Mike in the meeting room for so long after the department meeting ended? B: Mike had just heard that his project proposal was rejected, so Linda stayed to console him, telling him that the managers liked many of his ideas and would consider them next year.","t":"A：部門會議結束後，為什麼琳達和麥克在會議室裡坐了那麼久？ B：麥克剛聽說他的專案提案被否決了，所以琳達留下來【安慰】他，告訴他經理們很喜歡他的許多想法，明年會再考慮。"}]},{"unit":149,"theme":"Fruit 水果","cards":[{"w":"apple","p":"n.","d":"a round fruit with red, green or yellow skin and white flesh","c":"蘋果","s":"A: What healthy snacks should we put in the break room for the staff, since many people complained that the cookies and chips are too unhealthy? B: Let's order a box of fruit every Monday, and I think a crisp red apple is easy to eat at your desk without making a mess.","t":"A：既然很多人抱怨餅乾和洋芋片太不健康，我們應該在休息室為員工準備哪些健康的點心？ B：我們每週一訂一箱水果吧，我覺得清脆的紅【蘋果】很容易在辦公桌上吃，而且不會弄得一團亂。"},{"w":"banana","p":"n.","d":"a long curved fruit with yellow skin and soft sweet flesh","c":"香蕉","s":"A: Do you have time to eat a proper breakfast before the early sales meeting, or are you going straight to the conference room from the train station? B: I usually just grab a banana from the convenience store near the station because it gives me energy and I can finish it while I walk.","t":"A：你在早上的業務會議前有時間好好吃頓早餐嗎？還是你會從火車站直接去會議室？ B：我通常就在車站附近的便利商店買一根【香蕉】，因為它能給我能量，而且我可以邊走邊吃完。"},{"w":"orange","p":"n.","d":"a round fruit with thick reddish-yellow skin and juicy flesh","c":"柳橙；橘子","s":"A: Why did the café near our office suddenly raise the price of its morning juice, even though customers have been buying it every day for years? B: The manager told me that a cold winter damaged many farms, so every orange they buy from the supplier now costs almost twice as much as before.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近的咖啡店突然調漲早晨果汁的價格？明明顧客已經每天買了好幾年了。 B：經理告訴我，寒冷的冬天損害了許多農場，所以現在他們向供應商買的每一顆【柳橙】價格幾乎是以前的兩倍。"},{"w":"grape","p":"n.","d":"a small round green or purple fruit that grows in bunches","c":"葡萄","s":"A: What kind of fruit plate should we prepare for the wine company's visitors, who are coming to discuss a new distribution contract next Thursday afternoon? B: Since their products are made from the fruit, a plate with green and purple grape varieties and some cheese would be a thoughtful choice for the meeting.","t":"A：下週四下午酒商的訪客要來討論新的經銷合約，我們應該準備什麼樣的水果盤？ B：既然他們的產品是用這種水果做的，在會議上準備一盤綠色和紫色的各種【葡萄】品種再搭配一些起司，會是很貼心的選擇。"},{"w":"pear","p":"n.","d":"a sweet juicy fruit that is narrow at the top and wide at the bottom","c":"梨子；西洋梨","s":"A: Our client from Japan is visiting during the autumn holiday, so what kind of local gift could we give him that is not too expensive? B: A box of large Taiwanese pear fruit would be perfect, because they are juicy and in season now, and many visitors from Japan really enjoy them.","t":"A：我們的日本客戶會在秋季假期來訪，我們可以送他什麼不會太貴的在地禮物呢？ B：一盒台灣的大【梨子】會很完美，因為它們多汁而且現在正當季，很多日本訪客都非常喜歡。"},{"w":"peach","p":"n.","d":"a round fruit with soft fuzzy skin, sweet yellow flesh and a large stone","c":"桃子","s":"A: Which flavor of yogurt sold the most at our stores last summer, and should we produce more of it for the coming season? B: The peach flavor was the clear winner because customers love its soft, sweet taste in hot weather, so I suggest we increase production by about twenty percent.","t":"A：去年夏天我們店裡哪一種口味的優格賣得最好？我們應該為接下來的季節多生產一些嗎？ B：【桃子】口味明顯勝出，因為顧客在炎熱的天氣裡很喜歡它柔軟香甜的味道，所以我建議我們增加大約百分之二十的產量。"},{"w":"plum","p":"n.","d":"a small round fruit with smooth purple, red or yellow skin and a stone","c":"李子；梅子","s":"A: Have you decided what to serve as dessert at the department's end-of-year dinner, since several people asked for something lighter than chocolate cake? B: Yes, the restaurant offered a plum tart made with purple fruit from a local farm, and it is less sweet, so I think everyone will enjoy it.","t":"A：你決定好部門尾牙要上什麼甜點了嗎？因為有好幾個人要求比巧克力蛋糕清爽一點的東西。 B：決定了，餐廳提供一種用當地農場紫色果實做的【李子】塔，它比較不甜，所以我想大家都會喜歡。"},{"w":"mango","p":"n.","d":"a large tropical fruit with smooth skin and sweet orange flesh","c":"芒果","s":"A: The tour group from Europe arrives in Tainan this afternoon, so what famous local dessert should we take them to try after the factory visit? B: Let's bring them to the shaved ice shop near the station, because its mango ice with fresh yellow fruit and sweet syrup is very popular with tourists in summer.","t":"A：歐洲的旅行團今天下午抵達台南，參觀完工廠後我們應該帶他們去嚐什麼有名的在地甜點？ B：我們帶他們去車站附近的剉冰店吧，因為那裡加了新鮮黃色果肉和甜糖漿的【芒果】冰在夏天很受觀光客歡迎。"},{"w":"pineapple","p":"n.","d":"a large tropical fruit with rough brown skin, stiff leaves and sweet yellow flesh","c":"鳳梨","s":"A: Which Taiwanese snack should we include in the gift bags for the overseas guests attending our trade show next month in Taipei? B: I recommend traditional pineapple cakes from a well-known bakery, because they are a famous local specialty, they travel well, and most visitors are happy to receive them.","t":"A：下個月在台北參加我們商展的海外來賓，禮物袋裡應該放哪一種台灣點心？ B：我推薦知名麵包店的傳統【鳳梨】酥，因為它們是有名的在地特產，方便攜帶，而且大部分的訪客收到都很開心。"},{"w":"watermelon","p":"n.","d":"a very large round fruit with green skin, red juicy flesh and black seeds","c":"西瓜","s":"A: The outdoor company picnic is on Saturday and the weather forecast says it will be extremely hot, so what should we bring to keep everyone cool? B: Let's buy two huge watermelon fruits, cut them into pieces, and keep them in a cooler with ice, because they are full of water and very refreshing.","t":"A：公司戶外野餐在星期六，氣象預報說會非常熱，我們應該帶什麼讓大家保持涼爽？ B：我們買兩顆大【西瓜】，切成塊，然後放在加了冰塊的保冷箱裡，因為它們水分很多又非常清爽。"},{"w":"strawberry","p":"n.","d":"a small soft red fruit with tiny seeds on its skin","c":"草莓","s":"A: Why is the farm tour to Dahu so popular with our office workers every winter, even though it takes more than two hours by bus? B: Visitors can pick their own strawberry fruits in the fields, and the bright red berries are especially sweet during the cool months, so families love the trip.","t":"A：為什麼大湖的農場之旅每年冬天都這麼受我們上班族歡迎，即使搭巴士要兩個多小時？ B：遊客可以在田裡自己採【草莓】，而且這些鮮紅的莓果在涼爽的月份特別甜，所以家庭都很喜歡這趟旅程。"},{"w":"blueberry","p":"n.","d":"a small round dark blue berry that is sweet and healthy","c":"藍莓","s":"A: What new item is the bakery planning to add to its breakfast menu, since sales of plain bread have been falling for several months? B: The owner wants to sell blueberry muffins filled with small dark blue berries, because customers think they are both healthy and delicious, especially with a cup of coffee.","t":"A：既然原味麵包的銷量已經下滑好幾個月了，那家麵包店打算在早餐菜單上加什麼新品項？ B：老闆想賣裡面有深藍色小莓果的【藍莓】瑪芬，因為顧客覺得它們既健康又好吃，尤其是配上一杯咖啡。"},{"w":"raspberry","p":"n.","d":"a small soft red berry made of many tiny round parts","c":"覆盆子","s":"A: Which flavor of jam did the hotel guests ask for most often at the breakfast buffet, according to the survey we did last month? B: Most guests chose the raspberry jam because it is bright red, a little sour, and goes well with the warm toast and butter we serve every morning.","t":"A：根據我們上個月做的調查，飯店房客在早餐自助餐最常要求哪一種口味的果醬？ B：大部分房客選擇【覆盆子】果醬，因為它顏色鮮紅、帶點酸味，而且很適合搭配我們每天早上提供的熱吐司和奶油。"},{"w":"cherry","p":"n.","d":"a small round red or black fruit with a long stem and a stone inside","c":"櫻桃","s":"A: Why are the imported fruits at the supermarket so expensive this week, especially the small dark red ones from the United States? B: The cherry season there is very short, and they must be flown here quickly by air so they don't go bad, which makes the shipping costs very high.","t":"A：為什麼超市這週的進口水果這麼貴，尤其是從美國來的深紅色小果子？ B：那裡的【櫻桃】產季非常短，而且必須很快用空運送過來才不會壞掉，這使得運費非常高。"},{"w":"kiwi","p":"n.","d":"a small fruit with brown hairy skin and bright green flesh","c":"奇異果","s":"A: My doctor told me to eat more vitamin C because I keep catching colds at the office, so which fruit would you suggest? B: You could try a kiwi every morning, because the small brown fruit with green flesh has lots of vitamin C, and you can simply cut it in half and use a spoon.","t":"A：醫生叫我多攝取維他命C，因為我在辦公室一直感冒，你會建議吃什麼水果？ B：你可以每天早上吃一顆【奇異果】，因為這種綠色果肉的棕色小水果富含維他命C，而且你只要切成兩半用湯匙挖就可以了。"},{"w":"papaya","p":"n.","d":"a large tropical fruit with orange flesh and many small black seeds","c":"木瓜","s":"A: What drink does that famous stand at the night market sell, and why is there always a long line of tourists in front of it? B: It sells papaya milk, a smooth drink made with soft orange tropical fruit and fresh milk, and many travel blogs recommend it as a must-try local treat.","t":"A：夜市那家有名的攤子在賣什麼飲料？為什麼攤位前面總是有一長排觀光客？ B：它賣【木瓜】牛奶，是一種用柔軟的橘色熱帶水果和鮮奶做成的滑順飲料，很多旅遊部落格都推薦它是必喝的在地美食。"},{"w":"coconut","p":"n.","d":"a large hard brown nut with white flesh and clear juice inside","c":"椰子","s":"A: What did the resort serve the guests when they arrived after their long flight, since the reviews say the welcome was very special? B: Each guest received a fresh green coconut with a straw so they could drink the cool, sweet water inside while they waited at the front desk.","t":"A：客人長途飛行抵達後，度假村提供了什麼給他們？因為評論都說迎賓很特別。 B：每位客人都拿到一顆插著吸管的新鮮青【椰子】，讓他們在櫃台等候時可以喝裡面清涼香甜的水。"},{"w":"avocado","p":"n.","d":"a pear-shaped fruit with dark green skin, a large stone and soft creamy flesh","c":"酪梨","s":"A: Why did the salad shop downstairs become so popular with the young office workers in our building over the last few months? B: It offers a healthy lunch box with avocado slices, eggs and vegetables, and the creamy green fruit makes people feel full for the whole afternoon without feeling heavy.","t":"A：為什麼樓下的沙拉店在過去幾個月變得這麼受我們大樓年輕上班族的歡迎？ B：它提供有【酪梨】片、雞蛋和蔬菜的健康便當，而這種綿密的綠色果實讓人一整個下午都有飽足感，卻不會覺得負擔太重。"},{"w":"fig","p":"n.","d":"a soft sweet fruit with many small seeds, often eaten dried","c":"無花果","s":"A: Which new product from the Turkish supplier do you think we should introduce first in our health food stores in Taichung? B: I'd start with the dried fig snacks, because the soft, sweet fruit is full of fiber, and customers who want healthy desserts are always looking for something new to try.","t":"A：你認為我們應該先在台中的健康食品店引進土耳其供應商的哪一項新產品？ B：我會先從【無花果】乾點心開始，因為這種柔軟香甜的水果富含纖維，而想吃健康甜點的顧客總是在找新東西嘗試。"},{"w":"ripe","p":"adj.","d":"fully grown and ready to eat","c":"成熟的","s":"A: The bananas we bought for the staff kitchen on Monday are still green and hard, so should we throw them away and order new ones? B: No, just leave them in a warm place for two or three days, and they will become ripe and sweet enough for everyone to eat.","t":"A：我們星期一為員工廚房買的香蕉還是綠綠硬硬的，我們應該丟掉再訂新的嗎？ B：不用，把它們放在溫暖的地方兩三天，它們就會變得【成熟】，甜到大家都可以吃了。"},{"w":"juicy","p":"adj.","d":"containing a lot of juice","c":"多汁的","s":"A: Why do customers keep buying the pears from that farm even though they cost more than the ones from other suppliers at the market? B: Their pears are big, crisp and very juicy, so when you bite into one, sweet liquid runs down your hand, and people think the higher price is worth it.","t":"A：為什麼顧客一直買那家農場的梨子，即使它們比市場上其他供應商的還貴？ B：他們的梨子又大又脆而且非常【多汁】，咬一口甜甜的汁液就會流到手上，所以大家覺得較高的價格很值得。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"having a taste like sugar","c":"甜的","s":"A: Should we use less sugar in the new mango cake, since several customers wrote in their reviews that it is too heavy for them? B: Yes, the mangoes we buy in summer are already naturally sweet, so we can cut the sugar by half and still keep a rich, delicious flavor.","t":"A：既然好幾位顧客在評論中寫說新的芒果蛋糕對他們來說太膩，我們應該少放點糖嗎？ B：對，我們夏天買的芒果本來就很【甜】，所以我們可以把糖減半，還是能保有濃郁美味的口感。"},{"w":"sour","p":"adj.","d":"having a sharp acid taste like a lemon","c":"酸的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant add honey to the lemon drink on the new menu, when the old recipe was so popular with the lunch crowd? B: Many customers complained that the old drink was too sour and hurt their teeth, so the chef added a little honey to make it smoother and easier to enjoy.","t":"A：既然舊配方很受午餐人潮歡迎，為什麼餐廳在新菜單的檸檬飲品裡加了蜂蜜？ B：很多顧客抱怨舊的飲料太【酸】，讓他們牙齒不舒服，所以主廚加了一點蜂蜜，讓它更順口、更好入口。"},{"w":"tropical","p":"adj.","d":"coming from or relating to the hot, wet parts of the world","c":"熱帶的","s":"A: What kind of drinks are we serving at the summer welcome party for the new employees, which will be held on the hotel's rooftop next Friday? B: The hotel will prepare cold tropical fruit punch with mango, pineapple and passion fruit, which fits the hot weather and the relaxed holiday atmosphere perfectly.","t":"A：下週五在飯店屋頂舉辦的新進員工夏季歡迎派對，我們要提供什麼飲料？ B：飯店會準備加了芒果、鳳梨和百香果的冰涼【熱帶】水果潘趣酒，非常適合炎熱的天氣和輕鬆的度假氣氛。"},{"w":"citrus","p":"adj.","d":"relating to fruits such as oranges, lemons and limes","c":"柑橘類的","s":"A: Which scent did the cleaning company finally choose for its new line of kitchen products, after testing several options with customers last month? B: They chose a fresh citrus scent made from lemon and orange oils, because customers said it smells clean and bright without being too strong in a small room.","t":"A：清潔公司上個月讓顧客測試了幾種選項後，最後為新的廚房產品系列選了哪一種香味？ B：他們選了用檸檬和柳橙精油做成的清新【柑橘】香味，因為顧客說它聞起來乾淨明亮，在小房間裡也不會太濃。"},{"w":"peel","p":"v.","d":"to remove the skin from fruit or vegetables","c":"剝皮；削皮","s":"A: Why does it take the kitchen staff so long to prepare the fruit plates for the hotel's breakfast buffet every morning? B: They have to wash and peel hundreds of oranges and mangoes by hand before cutting them, so the hotel is now thinking about buying a machine to save time.","t":"A：為什麼廚房員工每天早上準備飯店早餐自助餐的水果盤要花這麼久的時間？ B：他們必須在切之前用手清洗並【剝皮】數百顆柳橙和芒果，所以飯店現在正考慮購買一台機器來節省時間。"},{"w":"slice","p":"v.","d":"to cut something into thin flat pieces","c":"切成薄片","s":"A: How should I prepare the apples for the cake we are baking for the manager's birthday party this afternoon in the meeting room? B: Please wash them first, then slice them into thin pieces with the sharp knife, and put them on top of the cake in neat circles before it goes into the oven.","t":"A：今天下午在會議室的經理生日派對要烤的蛋糕，我應該怎麼處理那些蘋果？ B：請先把它們洗乾淨，然後用利刀【切成薄片】，在放進烤箱前把它們整齊地排成圓圈放在蛋糕上。"},{"w":"seed","p":"n.","d":"the small hard part of a plant or fruit from which a new plant can grow","c":"種子；籽","s":"A: Why do our customers prefer this new type of watermelon, even though it is smaller than the ones we usually sell? B: Because it has almost no seed inside, people can eat it quickly without spitting anything out, which makes it perfect for children and for busy office lunches.","t":"A：為什麼我們的顧客比較喜歡這種新品種的西瓜，即使它比我們平常賣的小？ B：因為它裡面幾乎沒有【籽】，大家可以很快吃完而不用吐出任何東西，這讓它非常適合小孩和忙碌的上班族午餐。"},{"w":"pulp","p":"n.","d":"the soft inside part of a fruit, or the bits of fruit in juice","c":"果肉；果漿","s":"A: Why did the juice company start selling two different versions of its orange drink at the supermarket this month? B: Some customers like juice with lots of pulp because the soft bits of fruit make it feel fresher, while others want a smooth drink, so the company decided to offer both.","t":"A：為什麼果汁公司這個月開始在超市販售兩種不同版本的柳橙飲料？ B：有些顧客喜歡含有很多【果肉】的果汁，因為柔軟的果粒讓它感覺更新鮮，而其他人則想要滑順的飲料，所以公司決定兩種都提供。"},{"w":"orchard","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land where fruit trees are grown","c":"果園","s":"A: Where are we taking the visiting buyers on Saturday, since they said they want to see how our apples are grown before signing the contract? B: We will drive them to the orchard in the mountains, where they can walk among the fruit trees, talk with the farmers, and taste the apples right from the branches.","t":"A：既然那些來訪的買家說簽約前想看看我們的蘋果是怎麼種的，星期六我們要帶他們去哪裡？ B：我們會開車帶他們去山上的【果園】，他們可以在果樹間散步、和農夫聊天，還能直接從樹枝上摘蘋果來嚐。"},{"w":"harvest","p":"n.","d":"the time when crops or fruit are gathered, or the amount gathered","c":"收成；收穫","s":"A: Why are the prices of mangoes so low at the market this year, compared with last summer when they were very expensive? B: The weather was warm and dry during the spring, so farmers had a very large harvest, and now there is more fruit than the shops can sell.","t":"A：為什麼今年市場上的芒果價格這麼低？去年夏天明明非常貴。 B：今年春天的天氣溫暖又乾燥，所以農夫有非常大的【收成】，現在水果多到商店都賣不完。"},{"w":"fresh","p":"adj.","d":"recently picked or made, not old, frozen or canned","c":"新鮮的","s":"A: Why does the hotel restaurant buy fruit from a local farmer instead of a large supplier, even though the large supplier is cheaper? B: The farmer delivers fresh fruit picked that same morning, so the strawberries and peaches taste much better, and guests often mention it in their online reviews.","t":"A：為什麼飯店餐廳向當地農夫買水果，而不是向大型供應商買，即使大型供應商比較便宜？ B：農夫送來的是當天早上才採的【新鮮】水果，所以草莓和桃子的味道好很多，房客也常在網路評論中提到這點。"},{"w":"preserve","p":"v.","d":"to keep food from going bad, for example by cooking it with sugar","c":"保存；醃漬","s":"A: What does the small family company do with all the plums that are too soft to sell at the market in summer? B: They preserve them by cooking the fruit with sugar and putting it into glass jars, so the jam can be sold all year and nothing goes to waste.","t":"A：那家小家族企業夏天時怎麼處理那些太軟、不能拿到市場賣的李子？ B：他們把水果加糖熬煮並裝進玻璃罐來【保存】它們，這樣果醬一整年都可以賣，也不會浪費任何東西。"},{"w":"dried","p":"adj.","d":"with the water removed so that it lasts a long time","c":"乾燥的；曬乾的","s":"A: What kind of healthy snack can I keep in my desk drawer for long work days, since fresh fruit goes bad too quickly in the hot office? B: You could buy a bag of dried mango or apricots, because they last for months without a refrigerator and still taste sweet and chewy.","t":"A：既然新鮮水果在炎熱的辦公室裡壞得太快，我可以在抽屜放什麼健康點心應付漫長的工作日？ B：你可以買一包芒果【乾】或杏桃乾，因為它們不用冰箱也能放好幾個月，而且吃起來還是甜甜有嚼勁。"},{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the healthy substances in food that the body needs to grow and stay well","c":"營養","s":"A: Why did the school cafeteria decide to serve fruit every day at lunch instead of cakes and sweet drinks? B: The new manager read several reports about student health, and she believes better nutrition will help children concentrate in class, so she asked the supplier for more fruit and vegetables.","t":"A：為什麼學校餐廳決定每天午餐提供水果，而不是蛋糕和含糖飲料？ B：新的經理讀了好幾份關於學生健康的報告，她相信更好的【營養】能幫助孩子在課堂上專心，所以她要求供應商提供更多水果和蔬菜。"}]},{"unit":150,"theme":"Furniture 家具","cards":[{"w":"chair","p":"n.","d":"a seat for one person with a back and usually four legs","c":"椅子","s":"A: The new intern will start working in our accounting department on Monday, so is there anything we still need to prepare for her desk? B: Yes, we should order a comfortable office chair with good back support, because she will be sitting in front of the computer for most of the day.","t":"A：新實習生星期一要開始在我們的會計部門工作，她的座位還有什麼需要準備的嗎？ B：有，我們應該訂一張有良好背部支撐、坐起來舒服的辦公【椅子】，因為她一天大部分時間都會坐在電腦前面。"},{"w":"table","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture with a flat top and legs, used for eating or working","c":"桌子","s":"A: How many people have confirmed that they are coming to the client dinner at the Italian restaurant on Friday evening, and have you booked a place yet? B: Twelve guests have replied so far, so I reserved a long table near the window where everyone can sit together and talk easily.","t":"A：有多少人已確認會來參加星期五晚上在義大利餐廳舉行的客戶晚宴？你訂位了嗎？ B：目前有十二位客人回覆了，所以我在窗邊訂了一張長【桌子】，讓大家可以坐在一起輕鬆聊天。"},{"w":"desk","p":"n.","d":"a table for working or studying, often with drawers","c":"書桌；辦公桌","s":"A: I heard that the marketing team is moving to the third floor next week, but do you know where the new graphic designer is going to sit? B: The office manager said she will have the corner desk next to the big window, because she needs plenty of natural light for her design work.","t":"A：我聽說行銷團隊下週要搬到三樓，你知道新來的平面設計師要坐哪裡嗎？ B：辦公室經理說她會坐在大窗戶旁邊那張角落的【辦公桌】，因為她的設計工作需要充足的自然光。"},{"w":"sofa","p":"n.","d":"a long, soft seat with a back and arms for two or more people","c":"沙發","s":"A: The hotel lobby looks much more welcoming since the renovation last month, but what did the manager change to make guests feel more relaxed while waiting? B: She replaced the old hard benches with a large leather sofa and several soft cushions, so tired travelers can sit comfortably while they wait to check in.","t":"A：自從上個月整修後，飯店大廳看起來親切多了，經理改了什麼讓等候的客人感覺更放鬆？ B：她把舊的硬長椅換成一張大型皮【沙發】和幾個軟墊，讓疲累的旅客在等候辦理入住時可以舒服地坐著。"},{"w":"couch","p":"n.","d":"a long comfortable seat for more than one person; a sofa","c":"長沙發；睡椅","s":"A: Our cousin is visiting from Kaohsiung this weekend for a job interview, but we don't have a guest room, so where do you think he can sleep? B: He can sleep on the couch in the living room, because it is long and soft enough, and I will put some clean sheets and a pillow on it tonight.","t":"A：我們的表哥這個週末要從高雄來參加工作面試，但我們沒有客房，你覺得他可以睡哪裡？ B：他可以睡客廳的【長沙發】，因為它夠長也夠軟，我今晚會在上面放乾淨的床單和枕頭。"},{"w":"armchair","p":"n.","d":"a comfortable chair with side supports for your arms","c":"扶手椅","s":"A: The library wants to create a quiet reading corner for older visitors who come every morning to read the newspapers, so what kind of seating should we buy? B: I suggest buying a few soft armchair pieces with high backs and wide arms, because older readers can rest their elbows and stand up from them more easily.","t":"A：圖書館想為每天早上來看報紙的年長訪客打造一個安靜的閱讀角落，我們該買什麼樣的座椅？ B：我建議買幾張高椅背、寬扶手的軟【扶手椅】，因為年長讀者可以把手肘靠在上面，起身時也比較容易。"},{"w":"stool","p":"n.","d":"a seat without a back or arms, usually for one person","c":"凳子；高腳椅","s":"A: The new coffee shop near the train station is very small, so how did the owner manage to fit in enough seats for all the morning commuters? B: He installed a narrow counter along the window and put a tall stool in front of it every half meter, so customers can sit quickly and drink their coffee.","t":"A：火車站附近那家新咖啡店很小，老闆是怎麼塞進足夠的座位給所有早上通勤的人？ B：他沿著窗戶裝了一張窄長的吧檯，每隔半公尺就在前面放一張高【凳子】，讓客人可以很快坐下來喝咖啡。"},{"w":"bench","p":"n.","d":"a long seat for several people, often made of wood and found outdoors","c":"長椅；長凳","s":"A: The city government is improving the park next to our office building, but what changes will they make for the workers who eat lunch outside every day? B: They plan to put a wooden bench under each big tree along the path, so office workers can sit in the shade and enjoy their lunch.","t":"A：市政府正在改善我們辦公大樓旁邊的公園，他們會為每天在戶外吃午餐的上班族做哪些改變？ B：他們打算在步道旁每棵大樹下放一張木製【長椅】，讓上班族可以坐在樹蔭下享用午餐。"},{"w":"cabinet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture with shelves or drawers and doors, used for storing things","c":"櫥櫃；檔案櫃","s":"A: The auditors are coming next Tuesday to check our financial records from last year, so where should I keep all the important documents until then? B: Please put them in the metal filing cabinet in the manager's office and lock it every evening, because those papers contain private information about our clients.","t":"A：審計人員下週二要來檢查我們去年的財務紀錄，在那之前我該把所有重要文件放在哪裡？ B：請把它們放進經理辦公室裡的金屬檔案【櫃】，並且每天晚上上鎖，因為那些文件含有客戶的私人資料。"},{"w":"cupboard","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture or a small space with a door and shelves, used for keeping dishes, food, etc.","c":"碗櫥；櫥櫃","s":"A: I want to make some tea for the visitors from the Japanese company who are waiting in the meeting room, but where are the clean cups kept? B: They are in the kitchen cupboard above the sink, on the second shelf, and you can also find the tea bags and sugar next to them.","t":"A：我想為在會議室等候的日本公司訪客泡些茶，乾淨的杯子放在哪裡？ B：在水槽上方的廚房【碗櫥】裡第二層，你也可以在旁邊找到茶包和糖。"},{"w":"wardrobe","p":"n.","d":"a tall cupboard in which you hang your clothes","c":"衣櫥；衣櫃","s":"A: The guests at our hotel often complain that there is not enough space for their suits and dresses during long business trips, so what can we do about it? B: We could replace the small closets with a bigger wardrobe in every room, so guests can hang all their clothes neatly and keep them free of wrinkles.","t":"A：我們飯店的客人常抱怨長途出差時沒有足夠空間放西裝和洋裝，我們能怎麼做？ B：我們可以把每間房的小衣櫥換成更大的【衣櫃】，讓客人能把所有衣服整齊掛好，不會起皺。"},{"w":"dresser","p":"n.","d":"a piece of bedroom furniture with drawers for clothes, often with a mirror on top","c":"梳妝台；五斗櫃","s":"A: My sister is moving into her first apartment near the hospital where she works, but the bedroom has no closet, so where will she keep her folded clothes? B: She bought a white wooden dresser with six deep drawers and a mirror on top, so she can store her clothes and get ready for work every morning.","t":"A：我妹妹要搬進她工作的醫院附近的第一間公寓，但臥室沒有衣櫥，她要把摺好的衣服放哪裡？ B：她買了一個有六個深抽屜、上面附鏡子的白色木製【五斗櫃】，這樣她既能收納衣服，每天早上也能在那裡準備上班。"},{"w":"bookshelf","p":"n.","d":"a shelf or set of shelves for holding books","c":"書架","s":"A: Our training center has received over two hundred new business books from a generous donor, but where are we going to display them for the staff? B: We will put a tall bookshelf against the wall in the break room, so employees can borrow a book easily and read during their lunch break.","t":"A：我們的訓練中心從一位慷慨的捐贈者那裡收到兩百多本新的商業書籍，我們要把它們陳列在哪裡給員工看？ B：我們會在休息室靠牆放一個高【書架】，讓員工可以輕鬆借書並在午休時閱讀。"},{"w":"bed","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture for sleeping on","c":"床","s":"A: I'm booking a hotel room for the two engineers who are going to Singapore for the installation project, so what kind of room should I reserve? B: Please ask for a room with a separate bed for each person, because they will work long hours and both need a good night's sleep.","t":"A：我在為要去新加坡執行安裝專案的兩位工程師訂飯店房間，我該訂哪種房型？ B：請要一間每人各有一張獨立【床】的房間，因為他們要長時間工作，兩人都需要好好睡一覺。"},{"w":"mattress","p":"n.","d":"the large soft part of a bed that you lie on","c":"床墊","s":"A: Several guests have written online reviews saying they woke up with back pain after staying at our hotel, so what should we do first to solve the problem? B: We should replace the old mattress in every room with a firmer one, because the current ones are over ten years old and too soft.","t":"A：好幾位客人在網路評論中說住了我們飯店後醒來背痛，我們應該先做什麼來解決這個問題？ B：我們應該把每間房的舊【床墊】換成較硬的，因為現有的已經用了十多年，太軟了。"},{"w":"headboard","p":"n.","d":"the upright board at the head end of a bed","c":"床頭板","s":"A: The designer wants the guest rooms to look more luxurious after the renovation, but our budget is limited, so what is a cheap way to improve the beds? B: We could add a tall padded headboard behind each bed, because it makes the room look elegant and gives guests something soft to lean against while reading.","t":"A：設計師希望客房整修後看起來更豪華，但我們預算有限，有什麼便宜的方法可以改善床的樣子？ B：我們可以在每張床後面加一片高的軟墊【床頭板】，因為它讓房間看起來優雅，也讓客人看書時有柔軟的地方可以靠。"},{"w":"nightstand","p":"n.","d":"a small table beside a bed","c":"床頭櫃；床頭桌","s":"A: Many business travelers have asked for a place to charge their phones near the bed, so how can we solve this without doing a lot of construction work? B: We can buy a new nightstand for each room with a built-in USB charger and a small lamp, so guests can charge their phones beside them overnight.","t":"A：很多商務旅客要求床邊要有地方可以幫手機充電，我們怎麼在不大興土木的情況下解決這個問題？ B：我們可以為每個房間買一個內建USB充電器和小檯燈的新【床頭櫃】，讓客人整晚都能在身邊幫手機充電。"},{"w":"drawer","p":"n.","d":"a box-shaped part of a desk or cabinet that slides in and out for storing things","c":"抽屜","s":"A: I need to sign the delivery form for the package that just arrived at the front desk, but I can't find a pen anywhere on my desk, so do you have one? B: There are plenty of pens in the top drawer of my desk, so please take one, and you can also borrow my stapler if you need it.","t":"A：我需要在剛送到櫃台的包裹的簽收單上簽名，但我桌上到處都找不到筆，你有嗎？ B：我桌子最上面的【抽屜】裡有很多筆，請拿一支，如果需要的話你也可以借我的釘書機。"},{"w":"shelf","p":"n.","d":"a flat board fixed to a wall or in a cupboard for putting things on","c":"架子；擱板","s":"A: The new printer paper arrived this morning, but the storage room is already very crowded, so where should I put the twenty boxes? B: Please put them on the empty shelf at the back of the storage room, but make sure the heavy boxes go at the bottom so nothing falls on anyone.","t":"A：新的影印紙今天早上到了，但儲藏室已經很擠了，這二十箱我該放哪裡？ B：請放在儲藏室後面那個空的【架子】上，但一定要把重的箱子放在最下面，這樣才不會有東西掉下來砸到人。"},{"w":"rack","p":"n.","d":"a frame with bars or hooks for holding or hanging things","c":"架子（衣架、置物架）","s":"A: It's raining heavily today, and many visitors are coming to the trade fair with wet umbrellas and coats, so how can we keep the entrance hall dry and safe? B: Let's put a coat rack and an umbrella stand right next to the entrance, so guests can hang their wet things before they walk in.","t":"A：今天雨下得很大，很多訪客帶著濕雨傘和外套來參加商展，我們要怎麼保持入口大廳乾燥又安全？ B：我們在入口旁邊放一個外套【架】和傘架，讓客人進來之前先把濕的東西掛好。"},{"w":"counter","p":"n.","d":"a long flat surface in a shop, bank or kitchen where customers are served or food is prepared","c":"櫃台；流理台","s":"A: The bank branch downtown is always crowded at lunchtime, and customers often wait more than thirty minutes, so what is the manager planning to do about it? B: She plans to open a second service counter during busy hours and add two more tellers, so customers can deposit money and leave more quickly.","t":"A：市中心的銀行分行午餐時間總是很擁擠，客戶常常要等超過三十分鐘，經理打算怎麼處理？ B：她打算在尖峰時段開設第二個服務【櫃台】並增加兩名櫃員，讓客戶能更快存完錢離開。"},{"w":"folding","p":"adj.","d":"able to be bent or closed so that it becomes smaller and easier to carry or store","c":"可摺疊的","s":"A: We are holding the company's outdoor training day on the lawn next month, but we don't have enough seats for all two hundred employees, so what should we do? B: We can rent some folding chairs from an event company, because they are light, easy to carry outside, and simple to store away after the event.","t":"A：我們下個月要在草坪上舉辦公司的戶外訓練日，但座位不夠兩百名員工坐，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們可以向活動公司租一些【可摺疊的】椅子，因為它們很輕、容易搬到外面，活動結束後也很容易收起來。"},{"w":"wooden","p":"adj.","d":"made of wood","c":"木製的","s":"A: The owner of the new bakery wants customers to feel warm and comfortable when they come in, so what kind of furniture did the designer choose for the shop? B: The designer chose simple wooden tables and chairs in a light brown color, because natural materials make the small shop feel cozy and friendly.","t":"A：新麵包店的老闆希望顧客進門時感到溫暖舒適，設計師為店裡選了什麼樣的家具？ B：設計師選了淺棕色的簡單【木製的】桌椅，因為天然材質讓這家小店感覺溫馨又親切。"},{"w":"metal","p":"adj.","d":"made of metal","c":"金屬（製）的","s":"A: The factory needs new storage units for its heavy tools and machine parts, and the old plastic ones keep breaking, so what should the purchasing manager order? B: He should order strong metal shelves that can hold a lot of weight, because they will last much longer and won't break under heavy equipment.","t":"A：工廠需要新的收納設備來放重型工具和機器零件，舊的塑膠架一直壞掉，採購經理應該訂什麼？ B：他應該訂可以承重很多的堅固【金屬】架，因為它們會用得更久，放了重型設備也不會壞。"},{"w":"upholstered","p":"adj.","d":"covered with soft material and cloth, as on chairs and sofas","c":"有軟墊布套的；包覆布料的","s":"A: The waiting room at the dental clinic feels cold and uncomfortable, and patients are already nervous, so how can we make them feel more relaxed? B: We could replace the hard plastic seats with upholstered chairs covered in soft blue fabric, so patients feel more comfortable while they wait for their appointments.","t":"A：牙醫診所的候診室感覺冰冷又不舒服，病人本來就很緊張了，我們要怎麼讓他們感覺更放鬆？ B：我們可以把硬塑膠椅換成包著柔軟藍色布料的【軟墊】椅，讓病人在等候看診時感覺更舒服。"},{"w":"adjustable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed in height, size or position","c":"可調整的","s":"A: Several employees in the design department have complained about neck and back pain after sitting at their computers all day, so what does the health and safety officer suggest? B: She suggests buying adjustable desks that can move up and down, so workers can stand for part of the day and change their position often.","t":"A：設計部門有好幾位員工抱怨整天坐在電腦前後脖子和背部疼痛，職業安全衛生人員有什麼建議？ B：她建議買可以升降的【可調整的】桌子，讓員工一天中有部分時間站著工作，並經常變換姿勢。"},{"w":"compact","p":"adj.","d":"small and using little space","c":"小巧的；緊湊的","s":"A: Our company is opening a small branch office in a busy part of Taipei where rent is very expensive, so how can we make the space work for six people? B: We should choose compact furniture, such as narrow desks and stackable chairs, because it takes up less room and still gives everyone a place to work.","t":"A：我們公司要在台北租金很貴的熱鬧地區開設一間小分公司，我們要怎麼讓空間容納六個人？ B：我們應該選擇【小巧的】家具，例如窄書桌和可疊放的椅子，因為它們佔用空間較少，又能讓每個人都有地方工作。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"of the present time; using new styles and ideas","c":"現代的；新式的","s":"A: The architecture firm wants to impress international clients when they visit the new headquarters, so what style did they choose for the reception area? B: They chose a modern style with clean lines, glass tables, and white leather chairs, because it shows clients that the company is creative and up to date.","t":"A：建築事務所希望國際客戶參觀新總部時留下深刻印象，他們為接待區選了什麼風格？ B：他們選了線條簡潔、搭配玻璃桌和白色皮椅的【現代】風格，因為這讓客戶看到公司富有創意又跟得上潮流。"},{"w":"antique","p":"adj.","d":"old and often valuable because of its age and quality","c":"古董的；古老的","s":"A: The manager of the historic hotel downtown wants guests to feel the history of the building as soon as they walk in, so what did she put in the lobby? B: She placed an antique desk from the 1920s near the entrance, and guests often take photos of it because the wood carvings are so beautiful.","t":"A：市中心那家歷史悠久飯店的經理希望客人一進門就感受到建築的歷史，她在大廳放了什麼？ B：她在入口附近放了一張1920年代的【古董】書桌，客人常常拍照，因為上面的木雕非常漂亮。"},{"w":"assemble","p":"v.","d":"to put the parts of something together","c":"組裝","s":"A: The new office desks were delivered this morning in flat boxes, but the furniture company says installation costs extra, so who is going to put them together? B: Two people from our maintenance team will assemble them this afternoon using the instructions in the boxes, so the new staff can use them tomorrow.","t":"A：新辦公桌今天早上以扁平紙箱送達，但家具公司說安裝要另外收費，誰要把它們組起來？ B：我們維修組的兩個人今天下午會照著箱子裡的說明書【組裝】，讓新同事明天就能使用。"},{"w":"arrange","p":"v.","d":"to put things in a particular order or position","c":"排列；布置","s":"A: We are expecting about fifty people for the product training session tomorrow morning, so how should we set up the chairs in the main conference room? B: Please arrange the chairs in rows facing the screen, and leave a wide path in the middle so people can walk to their seats easily.","t":"A：明天早上的產品訓練課程預計大約有五十人參加，我們應該怎麼在主會議室擺放椅子？ B：請把椅子面向螢幕【排列】成一排排，中間留一條寬走道，讓大家能輕鬆走到座位。"},{"w":"polish","p":"v.","d":"to rub a surface to make it smooth and shiny","c":"擦亮；磨光","s":"A: The company president is coming to visit our branch office on Friday, and the meeting room furniture looks dull and dusty, so what should the cleaning staff do? B: They should polish the long wooden table and the cabinets on Thursday evening, so everything looks clean and shiny when the president arrives.","t":"A：公司總裁星期五要來視察我們分公司，會議室的家具看起來黯淡又有灰塵，清潔人員該做什麼？ B：他們應該在星期四晚上把長木桌和櫃子【擦亮】，這樣總裁到的時候一切看起來乾淨又閃亮。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look more attractive by adding things to it","c":"裝飾；布置","s":"A: The company's twentieth anniversary party will be held in the staff cafeteria next Friday evening, but it looks very plain, so how can we make it feel special? B: We can decorate the room with balloons, flowers, and colorful lights, and put photos from the company's history on the walls for everyone to enjoy.","t":"A：公司二十週年派對下週五晚上要在員工餐廳舉行，但那裡看起來很單調，我們要怎麼讓它感覺特別？ B：我們可以用氣球、鮮花和彩燈【裝飾】這個空間，再把公司歷年照片貼在牆上給大家欣賞。"},{"w":"rearrange","p":"v.","d":"to change the position or order of things","c":"重新排列；重新布置","s":"A: Our sales team has grown from five to nine people this year, and the office now feels crowded and difficult to move around in, so what can we do without moving? B: We could rearrange the desks into two long rows by the windows, which would create more open space in the middle of the room.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊今年從五人增加到九人，辦公室現在感覺很擠，走動也不方便，不搬家的話我們能怎麼做？ B：我們可以把桌子【重新排列】成靠窗的兩長排，這樣房間中間就會空出更多空間。"}]},{"unit":151,"theme":"Game 遊戲；比賽","cards":[{"w":"game","p":"n.","d":"an activity or sport with rules that people play for fun or to win","c":"遊戲；比賽","s":"A: Why did half of the sales department leave the office so early on Friday afternoon, even though the quarterly report was still unfinished? B: The company bought tickets for the whole team to watch the baseball game downtown, so the manager let everyone go at three and promised to finish the report on Monday.","t":"A：為什麼業務部有一半的人星期五下午這麼早就離開辦公室，即使季報都還沒完成？ B：公司幫整個團隊買了票去市中心看棒球【比賽】，所以經理讓大家三點就走，並保證星期一會把報告完成。"},{"w":"play","p":"v.","d":"to take part in a game or sport","c":"玩；打（球）；參加（比賽）","s":"A: What do the new interns usually do during their lunch break, since most of them don't know anyone in the building yet? B: Many of them go up to the staff lounge on the fifth floor to play table tennis together, which helps them relax and get to know people from other departments.","t":"A：新來的實習生午休時間通常都做些什麼？因為他們大部分在這棟大樓裡都還不認識任何人。 B：他們很多人會到五樓的員工休息室一起【打】桌球，這能幫助他們放鬆，也能認識其他部門的人。"},{"w":"player","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a game or sport","c":"選手；玩家","s":"A: Why is the sports company paying so much money to put a basketball star in its new advertising campaign this year? B: The marketing director believes that a famous player will attract younger customers, and sales of the running shoes increased by thirty percent after the last commercial with an athlete.","t":"A：為什麼這家運動用品公司今年要花這麼多錢，請一位籃球明星拍新的廣告活動？ B：行銷總監相信一位知名的【選手】能吸引年輕顧客，而且上次找運動員拍廣告之後，跑鞋的銷售量增加了百分之三十。"},{"w":"team","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who play or work together","c":"隊；團隊","s":"A: Is it true that our company is going to join the charity soccer tournament against the bank next door this summer? B: Yes, the human resources department is putting together a team of eleven employees, and they will practice every Wednesday evening in the park near the train station.","t":"A：我們公司今年夏天真的要參加和隔壁銀行對抗的慈善足球錦標賽嗎？ B：是的，人資部門正在組一支由十一名員工組成的【隊伍】，他們每週三晚上會在火車站附近的公園練習。"},{"w":"opponent","p":"n.","d":"a person or team you compete against","c":"對手","s":"A: How do you feel about the chess competition for staff members next week, now that you have seen the list of players? B: I'm a little nervous because my first opponent is the finance director, who has won the company prize three years in a row and plays online every night.","t":"A：既然你已經看過參賽名單了，你對下週的員工西洋棋比賽感覺如何？ B：我有點緊張，因為我的第一位【對手】是財務長，他已經連續三年贏得公司的獎項，而且每天晚上都在網路上下棋。"},{"w":"score","p":"n.","d":"the number of points each side has in a game","c":"比分；得分","s":"A: Did you see the end of the football final last night, or did you have to leave the sports bar before the second half started? B: I stayed until the end, and the score was tied at two goals each until the very last minute, when the home team finally got another one and the whole bar cheered loudly.","t":"A：你昨晚有看完足球決賽嗎？還是下半場開始前就得離開運動酒吧？ B：我待到最後，【比分】一直是二比二平手，直到最後一分鐘地主隊終於又進了一球，整間酒吧都大聲歡呼起來。"},{"w":"goal","p":"n.","d":"a point won by putting the ball into the net","c":"進球；得分","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing office talking about Kevin this morning instead of preparing for the client meeting? B: He scored the winning goal in the company soccer match against our biggest competitor on Saturday, so people keep asking him to describe how he kicked the ball past their goalkeeper.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上行銷辦公室裡的每個人都在談論凱文，而不是在準備客戶會議？ B：他星期六在公司對抗我們最大競爭對手的足球比賽中踢進了致勝的【一球】，所以大家一直請他描述他是怎麼把球踢過對方守門員的。"},{"w":"win","p":"v.","d":"to be first or best in a game or competition","c":"贏；贏得","s":"A: Why is the sales team working so late every night this month, even though their targets for the quarter have already been reached? B: The company is giving a free trip to Japan to the branch that sells the most, and they really want to win the prize before the contest ends on Friday.","t":"A：為什麼業務團隊這個月每天晚上都工作到這麼晚，即使他們這一季的目標已經達成了？ B：公司要招待銷售量最高的分店免費去日本旅遊，他們非常想在比賽於星期五結束前【贏得】這個獎。"},{"w":"lose","p":"v.","d":"to not win a game or competition","c":"輸；輸掉","s":"A: Why does the manager look so disappointed this morning, and why did she cancel the celebration lunch she planned for the staff? B: Our company basketball team didn't expect to lose the final against the hotel staff yesterday evening, so she decided to save the lunch for a happier day next month.","t":"A：為什麼經理今天早上看起來這麼失望，而且還取消了她為員工安排的慶功午餐？ B：我們公司籃球隊昨天傍晚沒想到會在決賽中【輸】給飯店員工隊，所以她決定把午餐留到下個月比較開心的日子。"},{"w":"draw","p":"n.","d":"a game that ends with both sides having the same score","c":"平手；和局","s":"A: Who won the friendly soccer match between the factory workers and the office staff at the company picnic on Saturday? B: Nobody won, actually, because it ended in a draw of one to one, and since it was getting dark, the organizers decided to give both teams a small trophy and some free drinks.","t":"A：星期六公司野餐時，工廠員工和辦公室職員之間的足球友誼賽是誰贏了？ B：其實沒有人贏，因為比賽以一比一【平手】結束，而且因為天色漸暗，主辦人決定頒給兩隊各一座小獎盃和一些免費飲料。"},{"w":"match","p":"n.","d":"a sports game between two people or teams","c":"比賽","s":"A: Why are so many hotel rooms in the city fully booked this weekend, even though it is not a holiday? B: The national tennis match between the two top players is taking place at the new stadium on Saturday, so thousands of fans are traveling here from other cities to watch it.","t":"A：為什麼這個週末市區有這麼多飯店客滿，即使不是假日？ B：兩位頂尖選手之間的全國網球【比賽】星期六將在新體育館舉行，所以有成千上萬的球迷從其他城市來這裡觀賽。"},{"w":"tournament","p":"n.","d":"a competition with many games in which the winners keep playing until one is left","c":"錦標賽；聯賽","s":"A: Why has the conference center hired so many extra security guards and cleaners for the whole of next week? B: It is hosting an international badminton tournament with more than two hundred players from thirty countries, and the organizers expect large crowds every day until the final on Sunday.","t":"A：為什麼會議中心下週一整週雇用了這麼多額外的保全和清潔人員？ B：它要主辦一場國際羽球【錦標賽】，有來自三十個國家的兩百多名選手參加，主辦單位預期在星期日決賽前每天都會湧入大批人潮。"},{"w":"champion","p":"n.","d":"the winner of a competition","c":"冠軍","s":"A: Who is the speaker at the sales conference tomorrow morning, and why did the organizers choose someone from outside our industry? B: She is a former Olympic swimming champion, and they invited her because she gives excellent talks about setting goals, working hard, and staying calm under pressure.","t":"A：明天早上業務研討會的講者是誰？為什麼主辦單位選了一位我們產業以外的人？ B：她是前奧運游泳【冠軍】，他們邀請她是因為她很擅長演講，談論設定目標、努力工作以及在壓力下保持冷靜。"},{"w":"competition","p":"n.","d":"an event in which people try to win something","c":"比賽；競賽","s":"A: How did the design department get so many fresh ideas for the new company logo in such a short time? B: The director held a competition for all employees, offering a weekend at a mountain resort to the winner, and more than eighty people sent in their drawings before the deadline last Friday.","t":"A：設計部門怎麼能在這麼短的時間內為公司新標誌想出這麼多新點子？ B：主管為全體員工舉辦了一場【比賽】，提供優勝者一個在山區度假村度週末的獎勵，結果上週五截止前就有八十多人交出了他們的作品。"},{"w":"practice","p":"n.","d":"regular training to get better at something","c":"練習","s":"A: Why does Mr. Chen leave the office at exactly six o'clock every Tuesday and Thursday, even when there is a lot of work? B: He is the coach of his daughter's volleyball team, and he has to be at the school gym by six-thirty to lead the practice before their big competition next month.","t":"A：為什麼陳先生每週二和週四都在六點整離開辦公室，即使工作很多也一樣？ B：他是他女兒排球隊的教練，他必須在六點半前到學校體育館帶領【練習】，為下個月的大型比賽做準備。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a careful plan for reaching a goal","c":"策略；戰略","s":"A: Why did the coach call a meeting with all the players during the break, even though the team was already winning? B: She wanted to explain a new strategy for the second half, because the other team had started to defend much better and she was worried they would come back and catch up.","t":"A：為什麼教練在中場休息時召集所有球員開會，即使球隊已經領先了？ B：她想說明下半場的新【策略】，因為對方隊伍的防守開始變得好很多，她擔心他們會反攻追上比分。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something well","c":"技巧；技能","s":"A: Why did the restaurant manager hire the young man with no experience instead of the older cook who applied last week? B: During the interview, he showed amazing skill with a knife and cut the vegetables faster than anyone, and the manager felt he could learn the rest of the job quickly.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳經理雇用了那位沒有經驗的年輕人，而不是上週來應徵的那位年紀較大的廚師？ B：面試時他展現了驚人的刀工【技巧】，切菜比任何人都快，經理覺得他能很快學會其餘的工作。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"n.","d":"something difficult that tests your ability","c":"挑戰","s":"A: Why are so many people in the accounting department walking up and down the stairs during their breaks this month? B: The company started a fitness challenge in which every team counts its steps for thirty days, and the group that walks the most will receive gift cards and a free dinner.","t":"A：為什麼會計部門有這麼多人這個月在休息時間爬上爬下樓梯？ B：公司發起了一項健身【挑戰】，每個小組要計算三十天的步數，走最多步的小組可以得到禮物卡和一頓免費晚餐。"},{"w":"level","p":"n.","d":"one stage of a video game; how high or advanced something is","c":"關卡；等級","s":"A: Why does your son look so tired at breakfast, and why was the light in his bedroom still on so late last night? B: He stayed up until midnight trying to finish the last level of his new video game, and I told him he can't use the computer on school nights anymore.","t":"A：你兒子為什麼早餐時看起來這麼累，而且昨晚他房間的燈為什麼那麼晚還亮著？ B：他熬夜到半夜，想破他新電玩遊戲的最後一個【關卡】，我已經告訴他上學日的晚上不能再用電腦了。"},{"w":"controller","p":"n.","d":"a device you hold in your hands to play video games","c":"遊戲控制器；手把","s":"A: Why did the customer bring the new game system back to the electronics store only two days after he bought it? B: The controller stopped working whenever he pressed the left button, so the sales clerk checked the receipt and gave him a new one without asking him to pay anything extra.","t":"A：為什麼那位顧客買了新遊戲主機才兩天就拿回電器行？ B：只要他按左邊的按鈕，【遊戲手把】就停止運作，所以店員查看了收據後就直接換了一個新的給他，沒有要他多付任何費用。"},{"w":"console","p":"n.","d":"a machine connected to a TV for playing video games","c":"遊戲主機","s":"A: Why is there such a long line outside the electronics store at the shopping mall this morning, even before it opens? B: The store is starting to sell the newest video game console today, and only a few hundred are available, so people have been waiting since last night to buy one.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上購物中心的電器行外面排了這麼長的隊伍，甚至還沒開門就這樣？ B：這家店今天開始賣最新的電玩【遊戲主機】，而且只有幾百台，所以大家從昨晚就開始排隊要買。"},{"w":"board","p":"n.","d":"a flat piece of wood or cardboard with marks, used for games like chess","c":"遊戲盤；棋盤","s":"A: What are we going to do with the children at the company family day if it rains and we can't use the garden? B: We set up a large chess board on every table in the cafeteria, and there are plenty of cards and puzzles, so the kids can play indoors while their parents enjoy lunch and talk with coworkers.","t":"A：如果公司家庭日下雨不能用花園，我們要怎麼安排孩子們？ B：我們在餐廳每張桌子上都擺了一個大【棋盤】，還有很多紙牌和拼圖，讓孩子們可以在室內玩，同時父母可以享用午餐並和同事聊天。"},{"w":"dice","p":"n.","d":"small cubes with dots on each side, used in games","c":"骰子","s":"A: Why did the toy company have to delay the release of its new family game until after the holiday season? B: The factory made a mistake and the dice in the boxes had two sixes and no ones, so the company had to collect all the sets from the stores and fix the problem.","t":"A：為什麼這家玩具公司必須把新的家庭遊戲延到節慶季過後才上市？ B：工廠出了差錯，盒子裡的【骰子】有兩個六點卻沒有一點，所以公司必須從各家店回收所有的組合並修正問題。"},{"w":"card","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of stiff paper used for playing games","c":"紙牌；卡片","s":"A: How do the flight attendants pass the time when their flight is delayed for several hours at the airport? B: They usually sit together in the crew lounge and play a card game or two, and sometimes they invite the pilots to join them while they wait for the weather to improve.","t":"A：班機在機場延誤好幾個小時時，空服員都怎麼打發時間？ B：他們通常一起坐在機組人員休息室玩一兩局【紙牌】遊戲，有時候還會邀請機師加入，一起等待天氣好轉。"},{"w":"puzzle","p":"n.","d":"a game or problem that you solve by thinking or by putting pieces together","c":"拼圖；謎題","s":"A: What is that large picture of a mountain lake on the table in the staff lounge, and why is nobody allowed to move it? B: It's a thousand-piece puzzle that the receptionists have been putting together during their breaks for two weeks, and they hope to finish it before the holiday party next Friday.","t":"A：員工休息室桌上那幅大大的山中湖泊圖是什麼？為什麼都不准人移動它？ B：那是一幅一千片的【拼圖】，櫃檯人員兩個星期以來都利用休息時間在拼，她們希望在下週五的節慶派對前完成。"},{"w":"fun","p":"adj.","d":"enjoyable and pleasant","c":"有趣的；好玩的","s":"A: Did the new employees enjoy the training day at the beach resort, or did they think it was too long and boring? B: They said it was really fun, because the trainers mixed short lessons with team games on the sand, and everyone got to know each other while learning about the company.","t":"A：新進員工喜歡在海灘度假村舉辦的訓練日嗎？還是他們覺得太長又無聊？ B：他們說真的很【好玩】，因為講師把短短的課程和沙灘上的團隊遊戲混在一起，大家在認識公司的同時也彼此熟識了。"},{"w":"exciting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel very happy and interested","c":"令人興奮的；刺激的","s":"A: Why are so many people from the office going to the stadium on Sunday, even though it is supposed to rain all afternoon? B: It's the most exciting race of the year, since the two fastest drivers in the country will compete for the title, and our company is one of the main sponsors of the event.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室有這麼多人星期天要去體育場，即使整個下午據說都會下雨？ B：那是今年最【刺激】的一場賽事，因為全國最快的兩位車手將爭奪冠軍頭銜，而且我們公司是這場活動的主要贊助商之一。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to win; with many people trying to win","c":"好勝的；競爭激烈的","s":"A: Why did the manager ask Tom not to join the friendly bowling night with the new clients next week? B: Tom is so competitive that he gets angry when he loses even a simple game, and the manager worried that he might upset the clients and hurt the business relationship.","t":"A：為什麼經理叫湯姆下週不要參加和新客戶的保齡球友誼之夜？ B：湯姆非常【好勝】，即使只是輸了一場簡單的比賽也會生氣，經理擔心他會讓客戶不高興，進而影響生意上的關係。"},{"w":"cooperative","p":"adj.","d":"involving people working together to reach the same goal","c":"合作的","s":"A: Why did the human resources team choose that strange board game for the training workshop instead of a normal quiz? B: It's a cooperative game in which all the players must work together to escape from a burning island, so it teaches communication and teamwork better than a contest where people compete.","t":"A：為什麼人資團隊在訓練工作坊上選了那款奇怪的桌遊，而不是一般的問答測驗？ B：那是一款【合作型】遊戲，所有玩家必須同心協力從一座失火的島上逃脫，所以它比讓大家互相競爭的比賽更能教導溝通和團隊合作。"},{"w":"casual","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not very serious","c":"休閒的；輕鬆的","s":"A: Do you think the new mobile game will make money, even though it is very simple and has only a few levels? B: Yes, because it is designed for casual players who only want to relax for ten minutes on the train, and those people are the largest group of customers in the market today.","t":"A：你覺得這款新的手機遊戲會賺錢嗎？即使它非常簡單，只有幾個關卡？ B：會的，因為它是為只想在火車上放鬆十分鐘的【休閒】玩家設計的，而這些人是當今市場上最大的顧客群。"},{"w":"serious","p":"adj.","d":"caring a lot about something and doing it with effort","c":"認真的","s":"A: Why does Linda spend so much money on new running shoes and a personal trainer, when she used to jog only on weekends? B: She has become a serious runner since she joined the company marathon club last year, and now she trains five mornings a week before work and enters races in other cities.","t":"A：為什麼琳達花這麼多錢買新跑鞋和請私人教練？她以前只在週末慢跑。 B：自從她去年加入公司的馬拉松社團後，她就成了一位【認真】的跑者，現在她每週有五天早上在上班前訓練，還會去其他城市參加比賽。"},{"w":"spectator","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches a sports event","c":"觀眾","s":"A: Why did the city council decide to build a new parking garage next to the sports stadium this year? B: Every spectator who drove to the football matches last season complained about the lack of parking spaces, and the traffic jams after each match caused problems for local shops and residents.","t":"A：為什麼市議會今年決定在體育場旁邊蓋一座新的停車場？ B：上一季每位開車去看足球比賽的【觀眾】都抱怨停車位不足，而且每場比賽後的塞車也對當地商店和居民造成困擾。"},{"w":"referee","p":"n.","d":"an official who makes sure players follow the rules","c":"裁判","s":"A: Why were the fans so angry at the end of the basketball game last night, and why did some of them throw cups onto the court? B: The referee called a foul in the last second that gave the visiting team two free shots, and most people in the stadium thought it was a terrible decision.","t":"A：為什麼昨晚籃球比賽結束時球迷這麼生氣，有些人甚至把杯子丟到球場上？ B：【裁判】在最後一秒判了一個犯規，讓客隊得到兩次罰球，而體育館裡大部分的人都覺得那是個很糟的判決。"},{"w":"rule","p":"n.","d":"an instruction that says what is allowed in a game","c":"規則","s":"A: Why did the new board game take so long to finish at the staff party, even though the box said it lasts only thirty minutes? B: Nobody understood the main rule about how to move the pieces, so we spent almost an hour reading the instructions and arguing about what was allowed.","t":"A：為什麼那款新桌遊在員工派對上花了這麼久才玩完？盒子上明明寫只要三十分鐘。 B：沒有人搞懂移動棋子的主要【規則】，所以我們花了將近一個小時讀說明書，並爭論哪些動作是被允許的。"},{"w":"turn","p":"n.","d":"the time when it is your chance to play or do something","c":"輪到的機會；（輪流的）一次","s":"A: Why are those two colleagues sitting quietly in the break room and staring at the chess board for so long? B: It's Peter's turn, and he has been thinking about his next move for almost ten minutes because one mistake could cost him the game and the free lunch they bet on.","t":"A：為什麼那兩位同事在休息室裡安靜地坐著，盯著棋盤看了這麼久？ B：現在【輪到】彼得了，他已經思考他的下一步將近十分鐘，因為一個失誤就可能讓他輸掉這局棋和他們打賭的那頓免費午餐。"},{"w":"victory","p":"n.","d":"a win in a game, fight or competition","c":"勝利","s":"A: Why did the company president take the whole soccer team out for an expensive dinner at the hotel last night? B: He wanted to celebrate their victory in the city business league, because it was the first time in ten years that our company beat all the other firms and brought home the trophy.","t":"A：為什麼公司總裁昨晚帶整支足球隊去飯店吃昂貴的晚餐？ B：他想慶祝他們在全市企業聯賽中的【勝利】，因為這是十年來我們公司第一次擊敗所有其他公司並把獎盃帶回家。"}]},{"unit":152,"theme":"Gathering 聚會","cards":[{"w":"meeting","p":"n.","d":"an event where people come together to talk about work","c":"會議","s":"A: Why did the marketing team cancel lunch with the new clients from Osaka this afternoon? B: The director called an urgent meeting at noon to talk about the falling sales numbers, so everyone had to stay in the conference room until almost three o'clock.","t":"A：行銷團隊為什麼取消了今天下午和大阪新客戶的午餐？ B：主管中午召開了一場緊急【會議】討論下滑的銷售數字，所以每個人都得待在會議室裡直到將近三點。"},{"w":"party","p":"n.","d":"a social event where people eat, drink, talk and have fun","c":"派對；聚會","s":"A: Are you going to the restaurant downtown on Friday night to say goodbye to Mr. Lin before he retires next month? B: Yes, the whole accounting department is going to the farewell party, and I've already bought him a nice pen as a small present from all of us.","t":"A：你星期五晚上會去市中心那家餐廳，在林先生下個月退休前跟他道別嗎？ B：會啊，整個會計部門都會去參加歡送【派對】，我已經買了一支好筆，當作我們大家送他的小禮物。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a special event to enjoy an important day or success","c":"慶祝活動；慶典","s":"A: Why are there balloons and a huge chocolate cake in the staff lounge this morning? B: Our company just reached its sales goal for the whole year three weeks early, so the manager planned a small celebration for everyone during the lunch break to thank us for our hard work.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上員工休息室裡有氣球和一個超大的巧克力蛋糕？ B：我們公司提早三週達成了全年的銷售目標，所以經理在午休時間為大家安排了一個小型【慶祝活動】，感謝我們的辛勞。"},{"w":"reunion","p":"n.","d":"a gathering of people who have not seen each other for a long time","c":"團聚；重聚會","s":"A: You look really excited today, so are you doing anything special after work this weekend? B: Yes, I'm flying back to Kaohsiung for my high school class reunion, and I'm going to see many classmates I haven't talked to since we graduated twenty years ago.","t":"A：你今天看起來好興奮，這個週末下班後有什麼特別的安排嗎？ B：有啊，我要飛回高雄參加高中同學【聚會】，會見到很多二十年前畢業後就沒再聯絡的同學。"},{"w":"assembly","p":"n.","d":"a large meeting of a group of people, often for a formal reason","c":"集會；大會","s":"A: Why is everyone walking toward the main hall instead of going back to their desks after lunch? B: The CEO asked all employees to attend a general assembly at one-thirty because she wants to explain the new company policies and answer questions about the upcoming merger.","t":"A：為什麼大家午餐後都往大禮堂走，而不是回到座位上？ B：執行長要求全體員工一點半參加全體【大會】，因為她想說明公司的新政策，並回答有關即將合併的問題。"},{"w":"conference","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting where people discuss a subject for one or more days","c":"研討會；會議","s":"A: Will you be in the office next week to help me finish the budget report for the board? B: Unfortunately not, because I'm traveling to Singapore for a three-day technology conference, where I'm giving a short presentation and meeting several possible business partners.","t":"A：你下週會在辦公室幫我完成要給董事會的預算報告嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為我要去新加坡參加為期三天的科技【研討會】，我會在那裡做一個簡短的報告，並和幾位潛在的商業夥伴見面。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"something important or special that is planned for people to go to","c":"活動；盛事","s":"A: How many people do you think will come to the product launch at the hotel on Saturday? B: We've sent out about three hundred invitations, so the hotel staff are preparing the ballroom for a large event with plenty of seats, drinks, and a big screen for the demonstration.","t":"A：你覺得星期六在飯店舉辦的產品發表會會有多少人來？ B：我們寄出了大約三百張邀請函，所以飯店員工正在把宴會廳布置成一場大型【活動】的場地，有充足的座位、飲料和一個用來示範的大螢幕。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special time of celebration, often with music, food or performances","c":"節慶；藝術節","s":"A: Why are so many hotels in the city fully booked in the second week of October? B: The city holds a famous food and music festival in the park every autumn, so thousands of tourists come from all over the country to enjoy the concerts and try local dishes.","t":"A：為什麼市區很多飯店在十月第二週都客滿了？ B：這座城市每年秋天都會在公園舉辦著名的美食音樂【節】，所以成千上萬的遊客從全國各地前來欣賞演唱會並品嚐當地料理。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal event held for an important occasion","c":"典禮；儀式","s":"A: Do you know why the security guards are setting up a red carpet and rows of chairs in front of the new building? B: The mayor is coming tomorrow morning for the opening ceremony, and our president will cut the ribbon and give a short speech to the reporters and guests.","t":"A：你知道為什麼警衛在新大樓前面鋪紅地毯、擺好一排排椅子嗎？ B：市長明天早上會來參加開幕【典禮】，我們的董事長會剪綵，並向記者和來賓發表簡短的致詞。"},{"w":"get-together","p":"n.","d":"an informal social meeting of friends or co-workers","c":"（非正式的）聚會","s":"A: Are you free on Thursday evening after work, or do you have to finish the sales report? B: I should be free, so why don't we invite a few people from the design team for a casual get-together at the café across the street to relax and talk about something other than work?","t":"A：你星期四晚上下班後有空嗎？還是得完成銷售報告？ B：應該有空，我們何不邀請設計團隊的幾個人，到對街的咖啡館來個輕鬆的【聚會】，放鬆一下，聊聊工作以外的事？"},{"w":"social","p":"adj.","d":"relating to meeting and spending time with other people for fun","c":"社交的；聯誼的","s":"A: Why does the human resources department organize a dinner for new employees every three months? B: It's an important social activity because it helps people from different departments get to know each other, and new staff feel more comfortable asking for help later.","t":"A：為什麼人資部每三個月就為新進員工辦一次晚餐？ B：這是一個重要的【社交】活動，因為它能幫助不同部門的人互相認識，新員工之後也比較敢開口求助。"},{"w":"crowd","p":"n.","d":"a large number of people together in one place","c":"人群","s":"A: Why did it take you almost an hour to get through the entrance of the trade show this morning? B: A huge crowd of visitors was waiting outside when the doors opened at nine, and the security staff had to check everyone's badge before letting them into the exhibition hall.","t":"A：為什麼你今天早上花了將近一小時才通過商展入口？ B：九點開門時外面有一大群【人潮】在等，保全人員必須在讓大家進入展覽館前檢查每個人的識別證。"},{"w":"group","p":"n.","d":"a number of people who are together or do something together","c":"團體；群組","s":"A: How should we organize the forty visitors from our partner company during tomorrow's factory tour? B: Let's put ten visitors in each group and give each one an experienced guide from the production line, so everyone can see the machines clearly and ask questions easily during the two-hour visit.","t":"A：明天參觀工廠時，我們該怎麼安排合作公司來的四十位訪客？ B：我們把每十位訪客分成一【組】，每組配一位來自生產線、經驗豐富的導覽員，這樣在兩小時的參觀中大家都能清楚看到機器，也方便發問。"},{"w":"guest","p":"n.","d":"a person who is invited to an event or someone's home","c":"客人；來賓","s":"A: Who is the woman sitting next to the CEO at the front table of the awards dinner? B: She's a special guest from our biggest customer in Japan, and the CEO invited her because her company helped us increase our overseas sales so much this year.","t":"A：坐在頒獎晚宴主桌、執行長旁邊的那位女士是誰？ B：她是我們在日本最大客戶派來的特別【來賓】，執行長邀請她是因為她的公司今年幫我們大幅提升了海外業績。"},{"w":"host","p":"v.","d":"to organize an event and welcome the people who come","c":"主辦；主持","s":"A: Has the company decided where the annual sales conference will take place next spring? B: Yes, our Taipei office will host it for the first time, so we need to book hotel rooms, plan the meals, and arrange transportation for about two hundred visitors from overseas.","t":"A：公司決定明年春天的年度業務大會要在哪裡舉行了嗎？ B：決定了，我們台北辦公室將首次【主辦】，所以我們得為大約兩百位海外訪客預訂飯店房間、規劃餐點並安排交通。"},{"w":"invite","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone to come to an event","c":"邀請","s":"A: The new restaurant on the corner looks great, so should we take our clients there after the contract signing? B: That's a good idea, and we should also invite the sales manager to join us because she worked very hard on this deal for the last six months.","t":"A：轉角那家新餐廳看起來很棒，我們簽約後要不要帶客戶去那裡？ B：好主意，我們也應該【邀請】業務經理一起來，因為她過去六個月為這筆交易非常努力。"},{"w":"invitation","p":"n.","d":"a written or spoken request asking someone to come to an event","c":"邀請；邀請函","s":"A: Did you get any information about the holiday dinner that the company is holding next month? B: Yes, I received an invitation by email this morning, and it says we need to reply by Friday and tell them if we are bringing a family member.","t":"A：你有收到公司下個月舉辦的節日晚宴的相關資訊嗎？ B：有，我今天早上透過電子郵件收到了【邀請函】，上面說我們必須在星期五前回覆，並告知是否會攜帶家人。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event such as a meeting or class","c":"出席；參加","s":"A: Is it necessary for the whole sales team to come to the training session on Wednesday afternoon? B: Yes, everyone must attend because the trainer will explain the new customer system, and we can't use it next week if we haven't learned how it works.","t":"A：整個業務團隊都必須參加星期三下午的訓練課程嗎？ B：是的，每個人都必須【出席】，因為講師會說明新的客戶系統，如果沒學會怎麼用，我們下週就沒辦法使用。"},{"w":"arrive","p":"v.","d":"to reach a place","c":"抵達；到達","s":"A: What time should the catering staff come to set up the food for tomorrow's lunch reception? B: They should arrive at the hotel by ten-thirty at the latest, because the guests will start coming in at noon and we need enough time to prepare the tables.","t":"A：外燴人員明天應該幾點來布置午宴的餐點？ B：他們最晚要在十點半【抵達】飯店，因為賓客中午就會陸續進場，我們需要足夠的時間準備餐桌。"},{"w":"welcome","p":"v.","d":"to greet someone in a friendly way when they come","c":"歡迎；迎接","s":"A: Who will stand at the front door when the visitors from the German company come in tomorrow morning? B: The general manager and I will welcome them in the lobby, and then we'll take them upstairs to the conference room for coffee and a short introduction.","t":"A：明天早上德國公司的訪客到來時，誰會站在大門口？ B：總經理和我會在大廳【迎接】他們，然後帶他們上樓到會議室喝咖啡，並做個簡短的介紹。"},{"w":"introduce","p":"v.","d":"to tell people each other's names when they meet for the first time","c":"介紹","s":"A: I don't know anyone at this networking dinner except you, so could you help me meet some people? B: Of course, let me introduce you to Mr. Chen first, since he works in the same industry as you and he's always looking for new suppliers.","t":"A：在這場交流晚宴上除了你我誰都不認識，你可以幫我認識一些人嗎？ B：當然，我先把你【介紹】給陳先生，因為他和你在同一個產業，而且他一直在找新的供應商。"},{"w":"chat","p":"v.","d":"to talk in a friendly and informal way","c":"聊天；閒談","s":"A: What did you do during the coffee break at the seminar this morning? B: I had a chance to chat with a few engineers from other companies about their projects, and one of them gave me some useful tips for our new software design.","t":"A：你今天早上研討會的茶歇時間做了什麼？ B：我有機會和幾位其他公司的工程師【聊天】，談他們的專案，其中一位還給了我一些對我們新軟體設計很有用的建議。"},{"w":"discuss","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something with other people to share ideas","c":"討論","s":"A: Why are the department heads meeting in the director's office so late on a Friday evening? B: They need to discuss the budget for next year's company trip, because the hotel prices went up and they must decide whether to change the location.","t":"A：為什麼各部門主管星期五這麼晚還在主管辦公室開會？ B：他們需要【討論】明年員工旅遊的預算，因為飯店價格上漲，他們必須決定是否要換地點。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to tell other people about your ideas or experiences","c":"分享","s":"A: What happens at the monthly lunch meeting that the new manager started in March? B: Every team member gets five minutes to share their ideas and experiences from the past month, so we learn from each other and solve problems together more quickly.","t":"A：新經理三月開始舉辦的每月午餐會都在做什麼？ B：每位成員有五分鐘可以【分享】過去一個月的想法和經驗，所以我們能互相學習，也能更快一起解決問題。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable because of a special day or success","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Our team finally won the large contract with the airline after months of hard work, didn't we? B: Yes, and the manager is taking all of us out to a nice Italian restaurant tonight to celebrate, so please don't make any other plans after work.","t":"A：經過幾個月的努力，我們團隊終於拿下航空公司的大合約了，對吧？ B：對，經理今晚要帶我們大家去一家不錯的義大利餐廳【慶祝】，所以下班後請不要安排其他事。"},{"w":"mingle","p":"v.","d":"to move around and talk to many different people at a social event","c":"（在社交場合）交際；與人打成一片","s":"A: I'm a little nervous about going to the reception for new clients tonight, because I'm not good at talking to strangers. B: Just relax and mingle with the guests for a while, because most people there are friendly and happy to talk about their businesses.","t":"A：我對今晚的新客戶招待會有點緊張，因為我不擅長和陌生人說話。 B：放輕鬆，和賓客們【交際】一下就好，因為那裡大部分的人都很友善，也樂意聊聊自己的生意。"},{"w":"network","p":"v.","d":"to meet and talk with people who may help you in your work","c":"建立人脈；交流","s":"A: Why do you go to so many business breakfasts and industry events every month? B: They give me a chance to network with managers from other companies, and several of the clients I have now came from people I first met at those events.","t":"A：你為什麼每個月要參加那麼多商務早餐會和產業活動？ B：它們讓我有機會和其他公司的主管【建立人脈】，我現在有好幾位客戶就是來自我在那些活動中初次認識的人。"},{"w":"buffet","p":"n.","d":"a meal where people serve themselves from many dishes on a table","c":"自助餐","s":"A: What kind of food will the hotel serve at the company's year-end dinner this Friday? B: They're preparing a large buffet with Chinese, Japanese, and Western dishes, so the guests can walk around the tables and choose whatever they want to eat.","t":"A：這週五公司尾牙飯店會提供什麼樣的餐點？ B：他們正在準備一場大型【自助餐】，有中式、日式和西式料理，賓客可以在餐桌間走動，想吃什麼就拿什麼。"},{"w":"refreshments","p":"n.","d":"small amounts of food and drinks served at an event","c":"茶點；點心飲料","s":"A: Will there be anything to eat during the three-hour training workshop on Saturday morning? B: Yes, light refreshments such as coffee, tea, cookies, and fresh fruit will be served in the hallway outside the training room during the short break at ten-thirty.","t":"A：星期六早上三小時的訓練研習會期間會有東西吃嗎？ B：會，十點半短暫休息時會在訓練教室外的走廊提供咖啡、茶、餅乾和新鮮水果等簡單的【茶點】。"},{"w":"entertainment","p":"n.","d":"performances or activities that people enjoy watching or doing","c":"娛樂；餘興節目","s":"A: Besides dinner and the awards, what else has the planning team prepared for the year-end party? B: They hired a band and a magician for entertainment, and there will also be a lucky draw with prizes like a new phone and a weekend hotel stay.","t":"A：除了晚餐和頒獎，籌備小組還為尾牙準備了什麼？ B：他們請了一個樂團和一位魔術師當作【餘興節目】，還會有摸彩，獎品包括新手機和週末飯店住宿。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"sounds arranged in a pleasant way by singing or playing instruments","c":"音樂","s":"A: What did you think of the welcome dinner for the visiting clients at the hotel last night? B: The food was excellent, and the soft piano music in the background made the atmosphere relaxing, so our guests seemed to enjoy the evening very much.","t":"A：你覺得昨晚在飯店為來訪客戶辦的歡迎晚宴如何？ B：食物非常棒，背景輕柔的鋼琴【音樂】讓氣氛很放鬆，所以我們的客人似乎非常享受那個晚上。"},{"w":"speech","p":"n.","d":"a formal talk given to a group of people","c":"演講；致詞","s":"A: Why does the president look so nervous while he's waiting near the stage at the anniversary dinner? B: He has to give a speech in front of five hundred employees and guests, and he wants to thank everyone properly for the company's thirty years of success.","t":"A：為什麼董事長在週年晚宴的舞台旁等待時看起來那麼緊張？ B：他必須在五百位員工和來賓面前發表【演講】，而且他想好好感謝大家為公司三十年來的成功所做的一切。"},{"w":"informal","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and friendly, not official","c":"非正式的；輕鬆的","s":"A: Do I need to wear a suit and tie to the team lunch with the new manager on Friday? B: No, it's a very informal lunch at a small noodle shop near the office, so jeans and a simple shirt are perfectly fine, and everyone will just be chatting.","t":"A：星期五和新經理的團隊午餐，我需要穿西裝打領帶嗎？ B：不用，那是在公司附近一家小麵店的【非正式】午餐，穿牛仔褲和簡單的襯衫就完全沒問題，大家只是聊聊天而已。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"following official rules or customs; serious and proper","c":"正式的","s":"A: What should I wear to the dinner with the bank's board members next Thursday evening? B: It's a formal dinner at a five-star hotel, so you should wear a dark suit, and remember that the guests will be seated according to a name card on each table.","t":"A：下週四晚上和銀行董事們的晚宴我該穿什麼？ B：那是在五星級飯店舉辦的【正式】晚宴，所以你應該穿深色西裝，還有記得賓客會依照每桌上的名牌入座。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"special or enjoyable enough to be remembered easily","c":"難忘的；值得紀念的","s":"A: How was the company trip to Hualien that the whole office went on last weekend? B: It was really memorable, because we hiked through a beautiful gorge, ate fresh seafood by the ocean, and got to know colleagues from other departments much better.","t":"A：上週末全辦公室一起去的花蓮員工旅遊怎麼樣？ B：真的很【難忘】，因為我們健行穿越美麗的峽谷、在海邊吃新鮮海鮮，還和其他部門的同事變得更熟。"}]},{"unit":153,"theme":"Gender 性別","cards":[{"w":"sex","p":"n.","d":"the group, male or female, that a person or animal belongs to by body","c":"性別（生理上）","s":"A: Why does the new hiring form for the hotel in Kaohsiung no longer ask job applicants to fill in so many personal details about themselves? B: The HR director decided that a person's sex has nothing to do with skills, so she removed that box to keep the process fair for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼高雄那家飯店的新求職表格不再要求應徵者填寫那麼多個人資料？ B：人資總監認為一個人的【性別】和能力無關，所以她刪掉了那一欄，讓流程對每個人都公平。"},{"w":"male","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the sex that cannot have babies","c":"男性的；雄性的","s":"A: Our nursing department has always hired mostly women, so why is the hospital running a new recruitment campaign at local universities this spring? B: The managers want more male nurses on the night shift, because many patients feel more comfortable when the team includes both men and women.","t":"A：我們護理部門一向主要聘用女性，那為什麼醫院今年春天要在當地大學舉辦新的招募活動？ B：主管們希望夜班有更多【男性】護理師，因為當團隊裡男女都有時，許多病患會感到比較自在。"},{"w":"female","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the sex that can have babies","c":"女性的；雌性的","s":"A: I read in the company newsletter that the engineering team has changed a lot over the past five years. What exactly happened there? B: The number of female engineers has doubled since the company started offering flexible hours and a mentoring program for young graduates from technical colleges.","t":"A：我在公司電子報上看到工程團隊過去五年改變很大，那裡到底發生了什麼事？ B：自從公司開始提供彈性工時並為技術學院的年輕畢業生開辦導師計畫以來，【女性】工程師的人數已經增加了一倍。"},{"w":"identity","p":"n.","d":"who or what a person is; the qualities that make a person or group different","c":"身分；認同","s":"A: Why did the marketing agency spend so much time interviewing the owners of the small bakery before designing their new logo and website? B: They wanted to understand the bakery's identity, including its history and values, so customers would immediately recognize what makes the shop special.","t":"A：為什麼行銷公司在設計小麵包店的新標誌和網站之前，要花那麼多時間訪談店主？ B：他們想了解這家麵包店的【身分特色】，包括它的歷史和價值觀，讓顧客能立刻認出這家店的特別之處。"},{"w":"role","p":"n.","d":"the job or position someone has in a group or activity","c":"角色；職責","s":"A: Now that Maria has been promoted to team leader, who is going to handle the weekly reports that she used to prepare for the regional office? B: Kevin will take over that role next month, and Maria will train him for two weeks so the change goes smoothly for everyone.","t":"A：既然瑪麗亞已經升任組長，那以前她為區域辦公室準備的每週報告要由誰負責？ B：凱文下個月會接下那個【職責】，而瑪麗亞會訓練他兩週，讓交接對大家來說都很順利。"},{"w":"equality","p":"n.","d":"the state of everyone having the same rights and chances","c":"平等","s":"A: Why are so many employees talking about the new salary policy that the board of directors announced at the end of last quarter? B: It promises equality in pay, which means men and women doing the same job at the same level will finally earn exactly the same amount.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多員工都在談論董事會上一季末宣布的新薪資政策？ B：它承諾薪資【平等】，也就是說，在相同職級做相同工作的男性和女性終於會領到完全一樣的薪水。"},{"w":"equity","p":"n.","d":"fairness, especially giving people what they need so they have equal chances","c":"公平；公正","s":"A: Why did the school decide to give extra laptops and free tutoring only to some students instead of giving every student exactly the same support? B: The principal believes equity means helping students based on their needs, so children from low-income families can finally compete on a fair level.","t":"A：為什麼學校決定只給部分學生額外的筆電和免費家教，而不是給每個學生完全一樣的支援？ B：校長認為【公平】的意思是依照學生的需求來幫助他們，這樣低收入家庭的孩子才終於能在公平的基礎上競爭。"},{"w":"stereotype","p":"n.","d":"a fixed and often unfair idea about what a type of person is like","c":"刻板印象","s":"A: Why did the advertising team reject the first draft of the commercial for our new kitchen appliances after the client meeting on Monday? B: It showed only women cooking and cleaning, and the client felt that this old stereotype would upset many younger customers who share housework equally.","t":"A：為什麼廣告團隊在星期一的客戶會議後否決了我們新廚房家電廣告的初稿？ B：那支廣告只呈現女性在煮飯和打掃，客戶覺得這種老舊的【刻板印象】會讓許多平均分擔家務的年輕顧客不高興。"},{"w":"bias","p":"n.","d":"an unfair preference for or against someone or something","c":"偏見；偏袒","s":"A: Why does the company now remove names and photos from all résumés before the hiring managers are allowed to read them? B: The HR team wants to reduce bias, because studies show that managers sometimes judge applicants unfairly based on their names, ages, or appearance.","t":"A：為什麼公司現在要在招募主管閱讀履歷之前，先把所有履歷上的姓名和照片移除？ B：人資團隊想減少【偏見】，因為研究顯示主管有時會根據應徵者的姓名、年齡或外表做出不公平的判斷。"},{"w":"discrimination","p":"n.","d":"treating a person or group unfairly because of who they are","c":"歧視","s":"A: What should I do if I believe a manager treated me unfairly during the promotion process because I'm a woman with young children? B: You should report the discrimination to the HR office in writing, and they must investigate it carefully and keep all the details private.","t":"A：如果我認為主管在升遷過程中因為我是有年幼孩子的女性而不公平地對待我，我該怎麼辦？ B：你應該以書面方式向人資辦公室舉報這起【歧視】事件，他們必須仔細調查，並將所有細節保密。"},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"the state of including many different types of people or things","c":"多元性；多樣性","s":"A: Why does the new design team come from so many different countries, age groups, and professional backgrounds this year? B: The director believes diversity brings fresh ideas, so she hired people with various experiences to help the company reach customers all over the world.","t":"A：為什麼今年新的設計團隊成員來自這麼多不同的國家、年齡層和專業背景？ B：總監認為【多元性】能帶來新的想法，所以她聘用了經歷各異的人，幫助公司接觸世界各地的顧客。"},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"including everyone and making all people feel welcome","c":"包容的；包含一切的","s":"A: Why did the organizers change the company picnic from a Saturday afternoon to a weekday lunchtime this year? B: They wanted the event to be more inclusive, because many staff members with children or weekend jobs could never join the fun before.","t":"A：為什麼今年主辦人把公司野餐從星期六下午改到平日午餐時間？ B：他們希望活動更【具包容性】，因為許多有孩子或週末要工作的員工以前從來沒辦法參加。"},{"w":"nonbinary","p":"adj.","d":"describing a person who does not think of themselves as only male or only female","c":"非二元性別的","s":"A: Why did the HR department add a third choice to the gender question on the online employee registration form last week? B: Some staff members are nonbinary, and the company wanted every worker to feel comfortable when they enter their information into the system.","t":"A：為什麼人資部門上週在線上員工登記表的性別問題中新增了第三個選項？ B：有些員工是【非二元性別】者，公司希望每位員工在系統中填寫資料時都能感到自在。"},{"w":"transgender","p":"adj.","d":"describing a person whose gender is different from the sex they were given at birth","c":"跨性別的","s":"A: Why is the hotel group updating its staff handbook and training all of its front desk workers again this month? B: The managers want employees to welcome transgender guests politely and use the names on their reservations, so every customer feels respected during their stay.","t":"A：為什麼這個飯店集團這個月要更新員工手冊，並再次培訓所有櫃台人員？ B：主管們希望員工能有禮貌地接待【跨性別】客人，並使用訂房資料上的名字，讓每位顧客在住宿期間都感到受尊重。"},{"w":"cisgender","p":"adj.","d":"describing a person whose gender is the same as the sex they were given at birth","c":"順性別的","s":"A: In yesterday's diversity workshop, the trainer used a word I had never heard before. Could you explain what it means? B: She said cisgender describes people whose gender matches the sex they were given at birth, and it is simply the opposite of the word transgender.","t":"A：在昨天的多元工作坊中，講師用了一個我從沒聽過的詞，你能解釋那是什麼意思嗎？ B：她說【順性別】是用來描述性別認同與出生時被指定的生理性別一致的人，它就是「跨性別」這個詞的相反。"},{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"the way a person shows feelings, ideas, or who they are","c":"表達；表現","s":"A: Why did the company finally relax its strict dress code for the office staff who don't usually meet clients? B: Management decided that personal expression through clothing and hairstyles makes employees happier, as long as everyone still looks neat and professional at work.","t":"A：為什麼公司終於放寬了對不常接觸客戶的辦公室員工的嚴格服裝規定？ B：管理階層認為透過服裝和髮型來展現個人【表達】能讓員工更快樂，只要大家在工作時仍然看起來整潔又專業就好。"},{"w":"masculine","p":"adj.","d":"having qualities thought to be typical of men","c":"男性化的；陽剛的","s":"A: Why did the cosmetics company hire a new design agency for its skincare products that are made especially for men? B: Sales were low, so they wanted packaging that looks more masculine, with dark colors and simple shapes that appeal to male shoppers in department stores.","t":"A：為什麼這家化妝品公司要為專為男性設計的保養品聘請新的設計公司？ B：銷售量很低，所以他們想要看起來更【陽剛】的包裝，用深色和簡單的造型來吸引百貨公司裡的男性顧客。"},{"w":"feminine","p":"adj.","d":"having qualities thought to be typical of women","c":"女性化的；陰柔的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team decide to change the pink packaging of our new running shoes before the product launch next month? B: Customers said the design looked too feminine, and the team wants the shoes to appeal to all runners, not just women who like soft colors.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊決定在下個月產品上市前更換我們新跑鞋的粉紅色包裝？ B：顧客說那個設計看起來太【女性化】，而團隊希望這款鞋能吸引所有跑者，而不只是喜歡柔和色系的女性。"},{"w":"neutral","p":"adj.","d":"not supporting either side; not showing features of one particular type","c":"中性的；中立的","s":"A: Why did the job advertisement for the warehouse position change the title from \"foreman\" to \"shift supervisor\" this year? B: The company now uses neutral job titles, so the ads don't suggest that only men or only women should apply for certain positions.","t":"A：為什麼今年倉庫職缺的徵才廣告把職稱從「工頭」改成「班組主管」？ B：公司現在使用【中性】的職稱，讓廣告不會暗示某些職位只適合男性或只適合女性應徵。"},{"w":"pronoun","p":"n.","d":"a word like he, she, they, or it that is used instead of a noun","c":"代名詞","s":"A: Why do some of our new colleagues add words like \"she/her\" or \"they/them\" under their names in their email signatures? B: They are telling people which pronoun to use when talking about them, so others can avoid mistakes and show respect in conversations.","t":"A：為什麼我們有些新同事會在電子郵件簽名的名字下方加上「she/her」或「they/them」這類字？ B：他們是在告訴大家談到他們時要用哪個【代名詞】，這樣別人就能避免出錯，並在對話中表現尊重。"},{"w":"respect","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that someone is important and should be treated well","c":"尊重；敬重","s":"A: What is the most important rule in the customer service training that all new staff must complete during their first week? B: The trainer says we must treat every caller with respect, even when they are angry or rude, because calm and polite answers usually solve problems faster.","t":"A：所有新進員工在第一週必須完成的客服訓練中，最重要的規則是什麼？ B：講師說我們必須以【尊重】的態度對待每一位來電者，即使他們生氣或無禮也一樣，因為冷靜有禮的回答通常能更快解決問題。"},{"w":"rights","p":"n.","d":"things that people are allowed to have or do by law or by fairness","c":"權利","s":"A: Why is the labor union holding a meeting in the factory cafeteria after work on Friday evening? B: They want to explain workers' rights under the new law, such as paid parental leave, safe working conditions, and fair overtime pay for every employee.","t":"A：為什麼工會星期五下班後要在工廠餐廳開會？ B：他們想說明新法律下勞工的【權利】，例如帶薪育嬰假、安全的工作環境，以及每位員工都能領到的合理加班費。"},{"w":"representation","p":"n.","d":"the fact of having people from a group present or included","c":"代表性；代表","s":"A: Why did the company decide to change the way it chooses members for the board of directors starting next year? B: Shareholders complained about poor representation, because the board had no women, so the company promised to include more female leaders soon.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定從明年起改變選任董事會成員的方式？ B：股東們抱怨【代表性】不足，因為董事會裡沒有任何女性，所以公司承諾很快會納入更多女性領導者。"},{"w":"advocate","p":"n.","d":"a person who publicly supports an idea or group","c":"倡議者；擁護者","s":"A: Who is the guest speaker that the HR team invited to talk to all the department managers at Thursday's leadership meeting? B: She is a well-known advocate for working mothers, and she will share practical ideas about flexible schedules and childcare support at work.","t":"A：人資團隊邀請在星期四領導會議上對所有部門主管演講的嘉賓是誰？ B：她是一位知名的職業母親【倡議者】，她會分享有關彈性工時和職場托育支援的實用想法。"},{"w":"awareness","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or understanding of a situation or problem","c":"意識；認識","s":"A: Why are all employees required to watch a short online video about fair treatment before the end of this month? B: The company wants to raise awareness of unfair behavior at work, so everyone understands what counts as harassment and how to report it safely.","t":"A：為什麼所有員工都必須在本月底前觀看一段關於公平對待的線上短片？ B：公司想提高大家對職場不公平行為的【意識】，讓每個人都了解什麼算是騷擾，以及如何安全地舉報。"},{"w":"acceptance","p":"n.","d":"the act of agreeing that something is normal, right, or welcome","c":"接納；接受","s":"A: How did the older staff members react when the company started hiring many young employees with very different working styles? B: At first there was some tension, but after several team-building activities, there was growing acceptance, and now both groups cooperate well on projects.","t":"A：當公司開始聘用許多工作風格非常不同的年輕員工時，資深員工的反應如何？ B：一開始有些緊張，但經過幾次團隊建立活動之後，彼此的【接納】逐漸增加，現在兩群人在專案上合作得很好。"},{"w":"tolerance","p":"n.","d":"the willingness to accept opinions or behavior different from your own","c":"容忍；寬容","s":"A: Why does our office now have such a strict policy against rude jokes and comments in the staff break room? B: Management has zero tolerance for harassment, so anyone who makes others feel uncomfortable will receive a formal warning from the HR department.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室現在對員工休息室裡的粗魯玩笑和言論有這麼嚴格的規定？ B：管理階層對騷擾行為採取零【容忍】，所以任何讓別人感到不舒服的人都會收到人資部門的正式警告。"},{"w":"culture","p":"n.","d":"the shared beliefs, values, and habits of a group or organization","c":"文化","s":"A: Why do so many talented young workers want to join that small software company even though the salaries there are not very high? B: It has a friendly culture, where managers listen to new ideas and everyone gets equal chances to lead important projects.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多有才華的年輕人都想加入那家小軟體公司，即使那裡的薪水不算很高？ B：它有友善的企業【文化】，主管會傾聽新想法，而且每個人都有平等的機會帶領重要專案。"},{"w":"norm","p":"n.","d":"a usual or accepted way of behaving in a group","c":"規範；常態","s":"A: Do you think many fathers at our company will actually take the new paternity leave that HR announced last month? B: Yes, because it's becoming the norm for young dads to stay home with their babies, and several team leaders have already used it themselves.","t":"A：你覺得我們公司會有很多爸爸真的請人資上個月宣布的新陪產假嗎？ B：會的，因為年輕爸爸在家陪伴寶寶正逐漸成為【常態】，而且已經有好幾位組長自己請過了。"},{"w":"social","p":"adj.","d":"relating to society and the way people live together","c":"社會的","s":"A: Why did the company start supporting a local program that teaches computer skills to women returning to work after raising children? B: The CEO believes businesses have a social responsibility to help their communities, and the program also helps us find skilled new employees.","t":"A：為什麼公司開始贊助一個教導育兒後重返職場女性電腦技能的地方計畫？ B：執行長認為企業有協助社區的【社會】責任，而且這個計畫也幫助我們找到有技能的新員工。"},{"w":"biological","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the body and natural processes of living things","c":"生物的；生理的","s":"A: Why did the insurance company change its health plan to include more checkups for both men and women this year? B: Doctors explained that some biological differences between the sexes affect which diseases people get, so they recommend different tests for different patients.","t":"A：為什麼保險公司今年修改健康方案，為男性和女性都加入更多健康檢查？ B：醫生解釋說兩性之間的某些【生理】差異會影響人們罹患哪些疾病，所以他們建議不同的病人做不同的檢查。"},{"w":"psychological","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the mind and feelings","c":"心理的","s":"A: Why did the company hire a counselor to visit the office twice a week after the difficult reorganization last spring? B: Many employees were under great stress, and the managers wanted to offer psychological support so people could talk about their worries in private.","t":"A：為什麼公司在去年春天艱難的組織重整後，聘請了一位諮商師每週到辦公室兩次？ B：許多員工承受很大的壓力，主管們想提供【心理】支持，讓大家可以私下談談自己的煩惱。"},{"w":"personal","p":"adj.","d":"relating to one particular person and their private life","c":"個人的；私人的","s":"A: Why did my manager ask me not to share details about my coworker's family situation during yesterday's team meeting? B: Those matters are personal, and the company policy says we should only discuss work topics unless the coworker chooses to tell everyone herself.","t":"A：為什麼我的主管要我不要在昨天的團隊會議上分享同事家庭狀況的細節？ B：那些事情是【私人的】，而公司政策規定我們只應討論工作話題，除非那位同事自己選擇告訴大家。"},{"w":"legal","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the law or allowed by law","c":"法律的；合法的","s":"A: Why did the company hire an outside lawyer before updating its parental leave rules for all of the factory workers? B: The managers wanted legal advice, because they needed to make sure the new rules fully follow the latest labor laws and protect every employee fairly.","t":"A：為什麼公司在為所有工廠員工更新育嬰假規定之前，要聘請外部律師？ B：主管們需要【法律】建議，因為他們必須確保新規定完全符合最新的勞動法，並公平地保障每位員工。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a conversation in which people talk about a subject","c":"討論","s":"A: What will happen at the diversity training session that the HR department has scheduled for next Wednesday afternoon? B: After a short video, there will be a group discussion where employees share their experiences and suggest ways to make our workplace fairer for everyone.","t":"A：人資部門安排在下週三下午的多元訓練課程會進行什麼活動？ B：在一段短片之後，會有小組【討論】，讓員工分享自己的經驗，並提出讓職場對每個人更公平的方法。"}]},{"unit":154,"theme":"Geography 地理","cards":[{"w":"map","p":"n.","d":"a drawing that shows where places, roads and rivers are","c":"地圖","s":"A: I have never visited the new branch office in the business park, so how will I find the right building when I arrive there tomorrow morning? B: Don't worry, I will email you a map that shows the parking area, the main entrance and the closest bus stop before you leave tonight.","t":"A：我從來沒去過商業園區裡的新分公司，明天早上到那裡時我要怎麼找到正確的大樓？ B：別擔心，今晚你出發前我會寄給你一張【地圖】，上面標示了停車區、正門和最近的公車站。"},{"w":"globe","p":"n.","d":"a round model of the Earth; also the whole world","c":"地球儀；全世界","s":"A: What should we put on the reception desk to show visitors that our shipping company works with customers in many different places? B: Let's buy a large globe with small flags on it, so guests can see every city where we deliver goods while they wait for their meetings.","t":"A：我們該在接待櫃台放什麼，讓訪客知道我們的貨運公司和許多不同地方的客戶合作？ B：我們買一個插著小旗子的大【地球儀】吧，這樣客人在等候開會時就能看到我們送貨的每一個城市。"},{"w":"continent","p":"n.","d":"one of the very large land areas of the world, such as Asia or Africa","c":"洲；大陸","s":"A: Our sales team has already opened offices in Japan, Korea and Thailand, so where does the director want to expand the business next year? B: She wants to move into Africa, because it is a huge continent with many growing cities and young customers who are starting to buy smartphones online.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊已經在日本、韓國和泰國開了辦公室，那總監明年想把生意擴展到哪裡？ B：她想進軍非洲，因為那是一個巨大的【大陸】，有許多正在成長的城市，以及開始在網路上買智慧型手機的年輕顧客。"},{"w":"country","p":"n.","d":"an area of land with its own government; a nation","c":"國家","s":"A: Do you know why the new manager from the head office speaks Spanish, French and English so well during our video meetings? B: She grew up in a small country in South America, and later she studied in Europe for six years before she joined our company in Taipei.","t":"A：你知道為什麼總公司來的新經理在我們視訊會議時西班牙文、法文和英文都說得那麼好嗎？ B：她在南美洲的一個小【國家】長大，後來在歐洲讀了六年書，才加入我們在台北的公司。"},{"w":"region","p":"n.","d":"a large area of a country or the world with its own features","c":"地區；區域","s":"A: Why are our coffee shops in the north selling so much more iced tea than the shops in the south this summer? B: The northern region has been much hotter and drier than usual since June, so many customers want cold drinks when they come in after work.","t":"A：為什麼今年夏天我們北部的咖啡店比南部的店賣出更多冰茶？ B：從六月以來，北部【地區】比往常更熱也更乾燥，所以很多顧客下班後進來都想喝冷飲。"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"everything you can see when you look across an area of land","c":"風景；景觀","s":"A: Why did the marketing team choose this small mountain village for the photos in our new travel brochure for next spring? B: The landscape there is beautiful, with green tea fields, old stone houses and a quiet lake, so the pictures will attract many tourists from the city.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊選擇這個小山村來拍我們明年春天新旅遊手冊的照片？ B：那裡的【風景】很美，有綠色的茶園、古老的石屋和寧靜的湖泊，所以照片會吸引很多城市來的遊客。"},{"w":"terrain","p":"n.","d":"land, especially when talking about its shape or how easy it is to cross","c":"地形；地勢","s":"A: Why does the delivery to the farm near the mountains always take two more hours than the delivery to the city stores? B: The terrain in that area is rocky and steep, so our drivers must go slowly and sometimes use a smaller truck to get up the narrow roads safely.","t":"A：為什麼送貨到山區附近那座農場總是比送到市區商店多花兩小時？ B：那個區域的【地形】崎嶇又陡峭，所以我們的司機必須慢慢開，有時還得改用較小的卡車才能安全地開上狹窄的道路。"},{"w":"climate","p":"n.","d":"the usual weather conditions in a place over a long time","c":"氣候","s":"A: Our company is thinking about moving its main factory to the south, but will the hot weather cause problems for our workers and machines? B: The climate there is warm and wet most of the year, so we will need good air conditioning and must plan regular checks on the equipment.","t":"A：我們公司正考慮把主要工廠搬到南部，但炎熱的天氣會不會對我們的員工和機器造成問題？ B：那裡的【氣候】一年中大部分時間都溫暖潮濕，所以我們需要良好的空調，並且必須安排定期檢查設備。"},{"w":"weather","p":"n.","d":"the condition of the air, such as sun, rain, wind or temperature, on a particular day","c":"天氣","s":"A: Are we still going to hold the company picnic in the riverside park on Saturday, or should we tell everyone to stay home? B: The weather report says it will rain heavily all afternoon, so I think we should move the event indoors to the hotel ballroom instead.","t":"A：我們星期六還要在河濱公園舉辦公司野餐嗎？還是應該通知大家待在家？ B：【天氣】預報說整個下午都會下大雨，所以我認為我們應該把活動改到飯店宴會廳的室內舉行。"},{"w":"latitude","p":"n.","d":"the distance of a place north or south of the equator, measured in degrees","c":"緯度","s":"A: The solar panel company says our new warehouse roof can produce a lot of power, but how did they calculate the amount? B: They looked at the latitude of our location, which shows how far north we are, and then they estimated how much sunlight we get each month.","t":"A：太陽能板公司說我們新倉庫的屋頂可以產生很多電力，但他們是怎麼計算出這個數量的？ B：他們查看了我們所在位置的【緯度】，也就是我們在多北邊的位置，然後估算出我們每個月能得到多少日照。"},{"w":"longitude","p":"n.","d":"the distance of a place east or west of a fixed line, measured in degrees","c":"經度","s":"A: How does the captain of our cargo ship know exactly where the ship is when it is in the middle of the ocean at night? B: The navigation system shows both the latitude and the longitude of the ship every minute, so the crew can always check their exact position on the screen.","t":"A：我們貨船的船長晚上在大洋中央時，怎麼知道船的確切位置？ B：導航系統每分鐘都會顯示船的緯度和【經度】，所以船員隨時都能在螢幕上確認他們的確切位置。"},{"w":"equator","p":"n.","d":"an imaginary line around the middle of the Earth","c":"赤道","s":"A: Why is it hot all year in Singapore, even in December, when our office in Taipei is getting cold and people wear jackets? B: Singapore is very close to the equator, so the sun is strong every month, and the temperature hardly changes between summer and winter there.","t":"A：為什麼新加坡一整年都很熱，甚至在十二月，當我們台北的辦公室變冷、大家都穿外套時也是一樣？ B：新加坡非常靠近【赤道】，所以每個月陽光都很強，那裡的氣溫在夏天和冬天之間幾乎沒有變化。"},{"w":"hemisphere","p":"n.","d":"one half of the Earth, such as the northern or southern half","c":"半球","s":"A: Why does our Australian office plan its big summer sale in January when we are selling winter coats here in Taiwan? B: Australia is in the southern hemisphere, so their seasons are the opposite of ours, and January is the hottest time of the year for them.","t":"A：為什麼我們澳洲辦公室把夏季大特賣安排在一月，而我們台灣這邊正在賣冬季外套？ B：澳洲位於南【半球】，所以他們的季節和我們相反，一月對他們來說是一年中最熱的時候。"},{"w":"ocean","p":"n.","d":"the very large area of salt water that covers most of the Earth","c":"海洋；大洋","s":"A: How long will it take for our furniture order from the factory in California to reach the store in Kaohsiung? B: The goods will travel by ship across the Pacific ocean, so it usually takes about three weeks, and then one more day by truck to the store.","t":"A：我們從加州工廠訂的家具要多久才能送到高雄的店？ B：貨物會用船橫越太平【洋】運送，所以通常需要大約三週，然後再用卡車多花一天送到店裡。"},{"w":"sea","p":"n.","d":"a large area of salt water that is smaller than an ocean","c":"海","s":"A: Where would you suggest we hold the team-building trip this summer so that everyone can relax after the busy sales season? B: Let's book a hotel by the sea in Kenting, where people can swim, enjoy fresh seafood for dinner and watch the sunset from the beach.","t":"A：你建議今年夏天的團隊建立旅行辦在哪裡，好讓大家在忙碌的銷售季後放鬆一下？ B：我們訂墾丁【海】邊的飯店吧，大家可以去游泳、晚餐享用新鮮海鮮，還能在海灘上看夕陽。"},{"w":"river","p":"n.","d":"a long natural flow of water that goes into the sea or a lake","c":"河；江","s":"A: Why did the city government decide to build the new office tower so far from the main train station and shopping area? B: The land next to the river was cheaper and larger, and the planners want workers to enjoy the water view and the bike path along the bank.","t":"A：為什麼市政府決定把新辦公大樓蓋在離主要火車站和購物區那麼遠的地方？ B：【河】旁邊的土地比較便宜也比較大，而且規劃人員希望上班族能享受水景和沿著河岸的自行車道。"},{"w":"lake","p":"n.","d":"a large area of fresh water with land all around it","c":"湖","s":"A: Have you decided where the company will hold the weekend retreat for the managers after the end of the financial year? B: Yes, we booked a quiet resort beside a large lake in the mountains, where people can go boating in the morning and have meetings in the afternoon.","t":"A：你決定好財務年度結束後公司要在哪裡為經理們舉辦週末靜修活動了嗎？ B：決定了，我們訂了山中一座大【湖】旁邊的安靜度假村，大家早上可以划船，下午再開會。"},{"w":"mountain","p":"n.","d":"a very high hill","c":"山","s":"A: Why are the tea leaves from that farm so much more expensive than the ones we usually buy for the office kitchen? B: They are grown high on a mountain where the air is cool and clean, and the workers have to pick every leaf by hand on steep slopes.","t":"A：為什麼那座農場的茶葉比我們平常買來放辦公室茶水間的貴那麼多？ B：它們種在高【山】上，那裡空氣涼爽又乾淨，而且工人必須在陡坡上用手摘下每一片葉子。"},{"w":"hill","p":"n.","d":"an area of land that is higher than the land around it but lower than a mountain","c":"小山；丘陵","s":"A: Is the new hotel close enough to the conference center for our guests to walk there each morning, or should we rent a bus? B: It is only ten minutes away, but the road goes up a steep hill, so older guests with heavy bags might prefer to take the shuttle.","t":"A：新飯店離會議中心近到我們的客人每天早上可以走路過去嗎？還是我們應該租一輛巴士？ B：只要十分鐘，但路要爬上一個陡峭的【小山坡】，所以帶著重行李的年長客人可能會比較想搭接駁車。"},{"w":"valley","p":"n.","d":"a low area of land between hills or mountains, often with a river","c":"山谷；谷地","s":"A: Why does the winery in that area produce such good grapes every year, even when the weather in other places is bad? B: The farm sits in a sheltered valley between two mountains, so strong winds cannot reach the vines, and a small river gives them enough water.","t":"A：為什麼那一帶的酒莊每年都能種出那麼好的葡萄，即使其他地方天氣很差也一樣？ B：那座農場位於兩座山之間一個受保護的【山谷】，所以強風吹不到葡萄藤，而且一條小河提供它們足夠的水。"},{"w":"plain","p":"n.","d":"a large area of flat land with few trees","c":"平原","s":"A: Why did the logistics company choose that area for its new distribution center instead of the cheaper land near the hills? B: It is on a wide, flat plain with good highways, so large trucks can drive in and out easily and the building is simple to expand later.","t":"A：為什麼物流公司選那個地區蓋新的配送中心，而不是選山丘附近比較便宜的土地？ B：它位於一片寬廣平坦的【平原】上，有良好的公路，所以大卡車可以輕鬆進出，而且建築物以後也很容易擴建。"},{"w":"plateau","p":"n.","d":"a large area of high, flat land","c":"高原","s":"A: Why did several of our engineers feel tired and short of breath during the first days of the project in the west of China? B: The work site is on a high plateau about four thousand meters above sea level, so the air is thin and people need time to get used to it.","t":"A：為什麼我們有幾位工程師在中國西部的專案頭幾天覺得很累又喘不過氣？ B：工地位於海拔約四千公尺的【高原】上，所以空氣稀薄，大家需要時間來適應。"},{"w":"desert","p":"n.","d":"a large, dry area of land with very little rain and few plants","c":"沙漠","s":"A: Why does the solar energy company want to build its largest power station so far away from the cities in the north? B: The land is a huge desert where it almost never rains, so there is strong sunshine every day and nobody needs the empty ground for farming or houses.","t":"A：為什麼那家太陽能公司想把最大的發電廠蓋在離北部城市那麼遠的地方？ B：那片土地是一大片幾乎從不下雨的【沙漠】，所以每天都有強烈的陽光，而且沒有人需要那塊空地來耕種或蓋房子。"},{"w":"forest","p":"n.","d":"a large area of land covered with trees","c":"森林","s":"A: Where are we taking the new employees for the outdoor training day next Friday, and what should they wear for the activities? B: We are going to a national forest park an hour away, so they should wear comfortable shoes because the walking paths go through thick trees and wet ground.","t":"A：下週五的戶外訓練日我們要帶新進員工去哪裡？他們活動時該穿什麼？ B：我們要去一小時車程外的國家【森林】公園，所以他們應該穿舒適的鞋子，因為步道會穿過茂密的樹林和潮濕的地面。"},{"w":"island","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land with water all around it","c":"島","s":"A: Why do the prices of fruit and vegetables at the hotel restaurant seem much higher than in the city where our head office is? B: The hotel is on a small island, so almost all food must come by boat from the mainland, and the shipping costs are added to every dish.","t":"A：為什麼飯店餐廳的水果和蔬菜價格看起來比我們總公司所在的城市高很多？ B：飯店位於一座小【島】上，所以幾乎所有食物都必須從本島用船運來，運費都被加進了每道菜裡。"},{"w":"peninsula","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of land that is mostly surrounded by water but joined to a larger area","c":"半島","s":"A: The client wants to visit three cities in Korea next month, but how will the travel agent plan such a busy trip in only five days? B: Korea is a peninsula, so the cities are not very far apart, and the fast trains can take them from one coast to another in a few hours.","t":"A：客戶下個月想去韓國的三個城市，但旅行社要怎麼在只有五天內安排這麼緊湊的行程？ B：韓國是一個【半島】，所以城市之間不會太遠，而且高速列車幾個小時內就能帶他們從一邊的海岸到另一邊。"},{"w":"coast","p":"n.","d":"the land next to the sea","c":"海岸；沿海地區","s":"A: Why are so many of the hotel's guests from overseas booking rooms with a balcony on the east side of the building this year? B: The east side faces the coast, so guests can watch the sunrise over the water and hear the waves while they eat breakfast outside.","t":"A：為什麼今年飯店有那麼多外國客人都訂大樓東側附陽台的房間？ B：東側面向【海岸】，所以客人可以看到海上的日出，在外面吃早餐時還能聽到海浪聲。"},{"w":"shore","p":"n.","d":"the land along the edge of a sea, lake or wide river","c":"岸；岸邊","s":"A: The tour group wants to go fishing at the lake during their visit, but do they need to rent a boat from the resort? B: No, they can fish from the shore near the hotel garden, because there is a wooden deck there with chairs, lights and enough space for ten people.","t":"A：旅行團在參觀期間想去湖邊釣魚，他們需要向度假村租船嗎？ B：不用，他們可以在飯店花園附近的【岸邊】釣魚，因為那裡有一座木製平台，有椅子、燈，空間也夠十個人使用。"},{"w":"harbor","p":"n.","d":"an area of water near the land where ships can stay safely","c":"港口；港灣","s":"A: Why did the shipping manager say our container of electronics will arrive two days later than the date on the original schedule? B: A storm closed the harbor in Keelung for two days, so all the cargo ships had to wait outside until it was safe to enter and unload.","t":"A：為什麼航運經理說我們那個貨櫃的電子產品會比原本行程表上的日期晚兩天到？ B：一場暴風雨讓基隆【港】關閉了兩天，所以所有貨船都必須在外面等，直到可以安全進港卸貨。"},{"w":"border","p":"n.","d":"the official line that separates two countries or areas","c":"邊界；國界","s":"A: How long will it take for the truck carrying our machine parts to get from the factory in Germany to our customer in France? B: It is only a short drive, but the truck must stop at the border for a quick check of the documents, so I expect delivery tomorrow afternoon.","t":"A：載著我們機器零件的卡車從德國工廠到法國客戶那裡要多久？ B：其實車程很短，但卡車必須在【邊界】停下來快速檢查文件，所以我預計明天下午會送達。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a city or town","c":"都市的；城市的","s":"A: Why does our bicycle company sell so many folding bikes in Taipei but very few in the farming villages in the south? B: People in urban areas live in small apartments and take the metro to work, so they need a light bike that they can carry easily and store inside.","t":"A：為什麼我們的自行車公司在台北賣出很多摺疊車，但在南部的農村卻賣得很少？ B：【都市】地區的人住在小公寓裡，搭捷運上班，所以他們需要一台可以輕鬆攜帶並放在室內的輕便自行車。"},{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the countryside, not the city","c":"鄉村的；農村的","s":"A: The bank wants to open more branches next year, but why is the manager planning to send mobile service vans instead of building offices? B: Many customers in rural villages live far from town, so a van that visits each village once a week is cheaper and more convenient for them.","t":"A：銀行明年想開更多分行，但為什麼經理打算派行動服務車，而不是蓋辦公室？ B：很多住在【鄉村】的客戶離市區很遠，所以每週到每個村莊一次的服務車對他們來說更便宜也更方便。"},{"w":"natural","p":"adj.","d":"existing in nature and not made or caused by people","c":"自然的；天然的","s":"A: Why did the resort decide to keep the old rocks and trees around the swimming pool instead of building a modern garden? B: The owner believes guests prefer natural beauty, so the designers kept the waterfall, the big stones and the local plants exactly as they were.","t":"A：為什麼度假村決定保留游泳池周圍的老岩石和樹木，而不是蓋一座現代化花園？ B：老闆相信客人比較喜歡【自然】之美，所以設計師把瀑布、大石頭和當地植物都保持原狀。"},{"w":"physical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the real shape and features of land, or to the body","c":"自然地理的；身體的；實體的","s":"A: The new staff member keeps getting lost when she drives to our customers' farms, so what kind of map should we give her? B: Give her a physical map that shows the hills, rivers and valleys, because the small roads out there are not on most phone apps.","t":"A：新同事開車去客戶的農場時一直迷路，我們應該給她哪一種地圖？ B：給她一張標示山丘、河流和山谷的【地形】圖，因為那邊的小路在大部分手機應用程式上都找不到。"},{"w":"human","p":"adj.","d":"relating to people, not to nature or machines","c":"人類的；人文的","s":"A: Why did the city planners invite a university professor to the meeting about the new highway through the old town? B: She studies human geography, so she can explain how the road will change the way people live, shop and travel in that neighborhood.","t":"A：為什麼都市規劃人員邀請一位大學教授來參加關於穿越舊城區新公路的會議？ B：她研究【人文】地理，所以她可以解釋這條路會如何改變那個社區居民的生活、購物和交通方式。"}]},{"unit":155,"theme":"Get Up Early 早起","cards":[{"w":"early","p":"adj.","d":"happening near the beginning of the day or a period","c":"早的；初期的","s":"A: Why did you book the six-thirty train to the head office when the meeting doesn't start until ten o'clock? B: I prefer an early start on meeting days, because the trains are less crowded and I can review the sales figures quietly in the café before everyone arrives.","t":"A：會議十點才開始，你為什麼訂了六點半往總公司的火車？ B：開會的日子我喜歡【早一點】出發，因為火車比較不擁擠，我還能在大家到達之前，先在咖啡館安靜地檢查銷售數字。"},{"w":"dawn","p":"n.","d":"the time when daylight first appears in the morning","c":"黎明；拂曉","s":"A: The photographer wants to take pictures of the new hotel building for our brochure, but when is the best time to do it? B: She plans to arrive at dawn, because the soft light at that time makes the glass walls look warm and the streets are still empty of cars.","t":"A：攝影師想替我們的手冊拍新飯店大樓的照片，什麼時候拍最好？ B：她打算在【黎明】時抵達，因為那時柔和的光線會讓玻璃牆看起來很溫暖，而且街上還沒有車子。"},{"w":"sunrise","p":"n.","d":"the time when the sun first appears in the sky","c":"日出","s":"A: Our company is planning a team-building trip to the mountains next month, so what activity do you think the staff would enjoy most? B: I think a short walk up to the lookout point to watch the sunrise together would be great, and then we could all share a hot breakfast at the lodge.","t":"A：公司下個月要辦一趟到山上的團隊建立旅行，你覺得員工最喜歡什麼活動？ B：我覺得一起短程步行到觀景台看【日出】會很棒，之後大家可以在山屋一起吃熱騰騰的早餐。"},{"w":"morning","p":"n.","d":"the early part of the day, from when the sun rises until noon","c":"早上；上午","s":"A: When would be a good time to call the supplier in Singapore about the late shipment of printer paper and ink? B: Try calling them first thing tomorrow morning, because their office opens at eight and the manager usually answers phone calls before her daily meetings begin.","t":"A：什麼時候打電話給新加坡的供應商詢問印表機紙和墨水延遲出貨的事比較好？ B：明天【早上】一上班就打給他們吧，因為他們的辦公室八點開門，而經理通常會在每日會議開始前接電話。"},{"w":"wake","p":"v.","d":"to stop sleeping","c":"醒來；叫醒","s":"A: How do you manage to get to the gym before work when you live so far away from the city center? B: I wake up at five without an alarm clock now, because after a few weeks my body got used to the new schedule and I actually feel more relaxed all day.","t":"A：你住得離市中心那麼遠，怎麼還能在上班前去健身房？ B：我現在不用鬧鐘五點就會【醒來】，因為幾個星期後我的身體就習慣了新的作息，而且我整天其實都覺得比較放鬆。"},{"w":"awaken","p":"v.","d":"to wake up, or to make someone stop sleeping (formal)","c":"喚醒；醒來","s":"A: Is the hotel near the airport a good choice for our visitors, or will the noise from the planes keep them up all night? B: The rooms have thick windows, so guests are not likely to awaken because of the planes, and the hotel also offers a free shuttle bus to the terminal.","t":"A：機場附近的那家飯店適合我們的訪客嗎？還是飛機的噪音會讓他們整晚睡不著？ B：房間有很厚的窗戶，所以客人不太可能因為飛機而被【吵醒】，而且飯店還提供到航廈的免費接駁車。"},{"w":"rise","p":"v.","d":"to get out of bed after sleeping","c":"起床；升起","s":"A: How has your life changed since you started working at the bakery downtown last spring? B: The biggest change is that I have to rise at four o'clock every day, because the bread must be baked and placed in the window before the first customers come in at seven.","t":"A：自從你去年春天開始在市區麵包店工作，你的生活有什麼改變？ B：最大的改變是我每天必須四點就【起床】，因為麵包必須在七點第一批客人進來之前烤好並擺上櫥窗。"},{"w":"alarm","p":"n.","d":"a clock or sound that wakes you up at a set time","c":"鬧鐘；警報","s":"A: Why were you almost late for the important client presentation this morning, when you are usually the first person in the office? B: My phone battery died during the night, so the alarm didn't go off, and luckily my neighbor knocked on my door when he was leaving for work.","t":"A：你平常總是第一個到辦公室，為什麼今天早上重要的客戶簡報差點遲到？ B：我的手機電池半夜沒電了，所以【鬧鐘】沒響，幸好我的鄰居出門上班時來敲了我的門。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists the times when things will happen","c":"時間表；行程","s":"A: Do you think we can fit a training session for the new staff into next week, since everyone seems so busy? B: Let me check the schedule first, but I believe Tuesday morning is open, because the monthly sales meeting was moved to Thursday afternoon.","t":"A：大家好像都很忙，你覺得下週能排進一場新進員工訓練嗎？ B：我先查一下【行程表】，不過我相信星期二早上有空，因為每月的業務會議已經改到星期四下午了。"},{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual things you do and the order you do them in","c":"例行公事；慣例","s":"A: How do you always stay so calm and organized, even on days when there are many problems in the warehouse? B: I follow the same routine every day: I arrive early, read my emails, check the stock list, and then talk to the team before any trucks arrive.","t":"A：即使倉庫問題很多的日子，你怎麼總能保持冷靜又有條理？ B：我每天都遵循相同的【例行程序】：提早到、讀電子郵件、檢查庫存清單，然後在卡車到達前先和團隊談話。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something you do often and regularly, often without thinking","c":"習慣","s":"A: Your sales reports are always finished before the deadline, so what is your secret for staying ahead of your work? B: I made it a habit to write for thirty minutes before anyone else comes in, because the office is quiet then and I can think clearly without phone calls.","t":"A：你的業務報告總是在截止日前完成，你保持工作超前的秘訣是什麼？ B：我養成了在別人進來之前先寫三十分鐘的【習慣】，因為那時辦公室很安靜，沒有電話打擾，我可以清楚地思考。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control yourself and do what you should do","c":"自律；紀律","s":"A: Our new marketing assistant studies for an MBA at night and still arrives at work early every day, so how does she do it? B: She has a lot of discipline, because she goes to bed at ten, never skips her study hours, and turns off her phone when she needs to focus.","t":"A：我們新來的行銷助理晚上在讀企管碩士，每天還是很早到公司，她是怎麼做到的？ B：她非常【自律】，因為她十點就上床、從不跳過讀書時間，而且需要專心時就會關掉手機。"},{"w":"refresh","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less tired and more full of energy","c":"使恢復精神；使清新","s":"A: You look much happier than you did yesterday, so did something good happen at the meeting with the new client? B: Not really, but I took a short walk in the park before work today, and the cool air helped refresh my mind after a long week of late nights.","t":"A：你看起來比昨天開心多了，和新客戶的會議有什麼好消息嗎？ B：其實沒有，不過我今天上班前在公園短暫散步了一下，涼爽的空氣幫助我在熬夜了一整週之後【恢復】精神。"},{"w":"energetic","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of energy and being very active","c":"精力充沛的","s":"A: Why do you think the morning shift workers at the factory are so much faster than the night shift workers? B: Most of them have had a good night's sleep and a healthy breakfast, so they feel energetic and can work carefully on the production line for many hours.","t":"A：你覺得為什麼工廠早班的工人比夜班的工人快那麼多？ B：他們大多睡了一夜好覺，也吃了健康的早餐，所以感覺【精力充沛】，可以在生產線上仔細工作好幾個小時。"},{"w":"alert","p":"adj.","d":"able to think quickly and notice things","c":"警覺的；機敏的","s":"A: The safety manager says all forklift drivers must sleep at least seven hours before a shift, but why is that rule so important? B: Drivers who are tired can easily make mistakes, so staying alert helps them notice people walking nearby and prevents serious accidents in the busy warehouse.","t":"A：安全經理說所有堆高機司機在上班前至少要睡七小時，為什麼這條規定這麼重要？ B：疲倦的司機很容易出錯，所以保持【警覺】能幫助他們注意到附近走動的人，避免在繁忙的倉庫裡發生嚴重的意外。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"doing or achieving a lot of useful work","c":"有生產力的；有成效的","s":"A: Why did the design team decide to start work at seven o'clock instead of nine o'clock last month? B: They found that they were most productive in the first hours of the day, because there were fewer emails and meetings, so they finished their projects much faster.","t":"A：設計團隊上個月為什麼決定從九點改成七點開始工作？ B：他們發現自己在一天中的最初幾個小時最【有效率】，因為電子郵件和會議比較少，所以他們完成專案的速度快多了。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making very little noise","c":"安靜的","s":"A: Where can I prepare for my job interview tomorrow, since my apartment is next to a noisy construction site? B: The public library on Main Street opens at seven, and the study rooms on the third floor are very quiet, so you can practice your answers without anyone disturbing you.","t":"A：我的公寓旁邊是吵鬧的工地，明天的工作面試我可以去哪裡準備？ B：大街上的公立圖書館七點開門，三樓的自習室非常【安靜】，所以你可以練習回答而不會有人打擾。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"calm and quiet, without worry or trouble","c":"平靜的；寧靜的","s":"A: Why do you always arrive at the office an hour before your team, even though you don't need to? B: The building feels so peaceful before everyone comes in, with no ringing phones or loud talking, so I can drink my tea and plan my day calmly.","t":"A：你明明不需要，為什麼總是比團隊早一小時到辦公室？ B：在大家進來之前，大樓感覺非常【寧靜】，沒有電話鈴聲也沒有大聲交談，所以我可以喝杯茶，冷靜地規劃一天。"},{"w":"fresh","p":"adj.","d":"feeling rested and full of energy; clean and cool","c":"清新的；精神飽滿的","s":"A: Should we hold the budget meeting at the end of the day, after everyone has finished their regular tasks? B: I'd rather hold it at nine, because people come in feeling fresh after a night's rest, and they make better decisions about difficult money matters when they aren't tired.","t":"A：我們要不要在一天結束、大家都做完日常工作後再開預算會議？ B：我寧願九點開，因為大家休息了一晚後進來時都【精神飽滿】，不累的時候對困難的財務問題會做出更好的決定。"},{"w":"exercise","p":"n.","d":"physical activity that you do to stay healthy","c":"運動","s":"A: The company is offering a free membership at the gym across the street, but do you think many employees will use it? B: I think so, because many people want to get some exercise before work, and the gym opens at six with showers and lockers for office workers.","t":"A：公司提供對街健身房的免費會員，但你覺得會有很多員工使用嗎？ B：我想會，因為很多人想在上班前做點【運動】，而且健身房六點就開門，還有給上班族用的淋浴間和置物櫃。"},{"w":"jog","p":"v.","d":"to run slowly and steadily for exercise","c":"慢跑","s":"A: You look very fit these days, so have you joined a sports club or hired a personal trainer? B: No, I just jog along the river for twenty minutes every morning before I take the bus to the office, and it costs nothing at all.","t":"A：你最近看起來身材很好，是加入了運動俱樂部還是請了私人教練？ B：沒有，我只是每天早上搭公車上班前沿著河邊【慢跑】二十分鐘，而且完全不用花錢。"},{"w":"stretch","p":"v.","d":"to make your arms, legs or body as long as possible to loosen muscles","c":"伸展","s":"A: My back always hurts after sitting at my desk for eight hours, so do you have any advice for me? B: Try to stretch for five minutes as soon as you get out of bed, and also stand up and walk around the office once every hour during the day.","t":"A：我在辦公桌前坐八小時後背總是會痛，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：試著一起床就【伸展】五分鐘，白天也每隔一小時站起來在辦公室裡走一走。"},{"w":"meditate","p":"v.","d":"to sit quietly and calm your mind for a period of time","c":"冥想；靜坐","s":"A: How do you stay so calm when customers complain to you on the phone all day long? B: I meditate for ten minutes every morning before I leave home, sitting quietly and breathing slowly, so I start the day calm and don't get upset easily.","t":"A：客人整天在電話裡向你抱怨，你怎麼還能保持那麼冷靜？ B：我每天早上出門前會【冥想】十分鐘，安靜地坐著、慢慢呼吸，所以我一天的開始很平靜，不容易生氣。"},{"w":"breakfast","p":"n.","d":"the first meal of the day","c":"早餐","s":"A: The hotel says the conference guests can eat in the restaurant before the first session, but what time will it open? B: breakfast is served from six-thirty to nine-thirty in the main dining room, so the guests will have enough time to eat before the speeches start at ten.","t":"A：飯店說會議賓客可以在第一場會議前在餐廳用餐，但是幾點開始？ B：【早餐】在主餐廳從六點半供應到九點半，所以賓客在十點演講開始前有足夠的時間吃東西。"},{"w":"coffee","p":"n.","d":"a hot drink made from roasted beans","c":"咖啡","s":"A: The office kitchen is always crowded at eight-thirty, so should we buy a second machine for the staff? B: That's a good idea, because almost everyone wants a cup of coffee as soon as they arrive, and the line often makes people late for the morning meeting.","t":"A：辦公室的茶水間八點半總是很擁擠，我們要不要替員工再買一台機器？ B：好主意，因為幾乎每個人一到公司就想喝杯【咖啡】，而排隊常常讓大家晨會遲到。"},{"w":"focus","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to one thing","c":"專注；集中","s":"A: Why does the editor always come to the office at six-thirty, two hours before the rest of the team? B: She says she can focus on long reports much better when the office is empty, because nobody stops by her desk to ask questions or chat about the weekend.","t":"A：為什麼編輯總是六點半就到辦公室，比團隊其他人早兩小時？ B：她說辦公室沒人時，她比較能【專心】處理冗長的報告，因為沒有人會來她桌邊問問題或聊週末的事。"},{"w":"plan","p":"v.","d":"to decide what you will do and how you will do it","c":"計畫；規劃","s":"A: You always seem to know exactly what to do when you arrive at work, so how do you organize everything? B: I plan my whole day on the train, writing down my meetings, phone calls and tasks in my notebook, so I never waste time wondering what comes next.","t":"A：你到公司時似乎總是很清楚要做什麼，你是怎麼安排一切的？ B：我在火車上【規劃】一整天，把會議、電話和任務寫在筆記本裡，所以我從不浪費時間去想接下來要做什麼。"},{"w":"prepare","p":"v.","d":"to make something or someone ready","c":"準備","s":"A: How do you get your two children to school and still arrive at the office by eight-thirty every morning? B: I prepare their lunches and lay out their clothes the night before, so in the morning we only need to eat breakfast quickly and walk to the bus stop.","t":"A：你每天早上怎麼能送兩個孩子上學，還在八點半前到辦公室？ B：我前一晚就【準備】好他們的午餐並把衣服擺好，所以早上我們只需要快速吃早餐，然後走到公車站。"},{"w":"commute","p":"n.","d":"the trip you make to work and back every day","c":"通勤","s":"A: Why did you decide to leave home at six o'clock instead of seven-thirty, even though your office opens at nine? B: My commute takes only forty minutes if I leave early, but when I leave later, the heavy traffic on the highway makes it take nearly two hours.","t":"A：你的辦公室九點才開，為什麼你決定六點而不是七點半出門？ B：如果早點出門，我的【通勤】只要四十分鐘，但晚一點出門的話，高速公路上的車潮會讓它花上將近兩小時。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the time or date by which something must be finished","c":"截止期限","s":"A: Why did the whole accounting team come in at six this morning, when they usually start work at nine? B: The deadline for the annual tax report is noon today, and they still had to check hundreds of receipts before the manager could sign and send it.","t":"A：整個會計團隊平常九點才上班，為什麼今天早上六點就來了？ B：年度稅務報告的【截止期限】是今天中午，而他們在經理簽名寄出之前還得核對好幾百張收據。"},{"w":"sleepy","p":"adj.","d":"tired and wanting to sleep","c":"想睡的；睏的","s":"A: Why do you never drink coffee after lunch, when most people in our department drink three cups a day? B: Coffee in the afternoon keeps me awake at night, and then I feel sleepy and slow during the next morning's meetings, so I only have one cup at breakfast.","t":"A：我們部門大部分的人一天喝三杯咖啡，為什麼你午餐後從不喝？ B：下午喝咖啡會讓我晚上睡不著，然後隔天早上開會時我就會覺得【昏昏欲睡】又遲鈍，所以我只在早餐時喝一杯。"},{"w":"rested","p":"adj.","d":"not tired because you have slept or relaxed","c":"休息充足的","s":"A: You were so tired last week, but today you look completely different, so what changed? B: I went to bed at ten every night this week instead of watching movies until midnight, so I feel well rested and can finally concentrate on my work again.","t":"A：你上週那麼累，今天卻看起來完全不一樣，發生了什麼改變？ B：這週我每晚十點就上床，而不是看電影到半夜，所以我覺得【休息】得很充足，終於又能專心工作了。"},{"w":"consistent","p":"adj.","d":"always behaving or happening in the same way","c":"一致的；始終如一的","s":"A: I've tried to get up at six many times, but I always give up after a few days, so what am I doing wrong? B: You need to be consistent, which means going to bed and getting up at the same time every day, even on weekends and holidays.","t":"A：我試過很多次六點起床，但總是幾天後就放棄了，我哪裡做錯了？ B：你需要【持之以恆】，也就是每天在同一時間上床和起床，即使週末和假日也一樣。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the reason or desire that makes you want to do something","c":"動機；動力","s":"A: What gave you the motivation to start getting up an hour earlier, since you used to hate mornings so much? B: I wanted to finish my online course in project management before my performance review, and the only free time I had was before work.","t":"A：你以前那麼討厭早上，是什麼給了你【動力】開始提早一小時起床？ B：我想在績效考核前完成線上的專案管理課程，而我唯一的空閒時間就是在上班之前。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"a healthy situation in which different parts of your life get the right amount of time","c":"平衡","s":"A: Why does our company let staff start at seven and leave at four, instead of keeping the usual nine-to-six hours? B: Management wants employees to have a better balance between work and family, so people can spend more evening time with their children and still finish their tasks.","t":"A：為什麼公司讓員工七點上班四點下班，而不是維持一般的九點到六點？ B：管理層希望員工在工作和家庭之間有更好的【平衡】，這樣大家晚上可以花更多時間陪孩子，還能完成工作。"},{"w":"lifestyle","p":"n.","d":"the way a person lives, including habits and activities","c":"生活方式","s":"A: Our health insurance company is offering lower prices to employees who sleep well and exercise, so are you going to join the program? B: Definitely, because I've already changed my lifestyle this year by going to bed earlier, eating healthier food, and walking to work every day.","t":"A：我們的健康保險公司對睡眠充足又運動的員工提供較低的保費，你要參加這個方案嗎？ B：當然，因為我今年已經改變了【生活方式】，更早上床、吃更健康的食物，並且每天走路上班。"}]},{"unit":156,"theme":"Gift 禮物","cards":[{"w":"affection","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of liking and caring for someone","c":"喜愛；感情；關愛","s":"A: Why did the staff decide to buy flowers and a card for the cleaning lady who is retiring next Friday after twenty years at our company? B: Everyone wanted to show their affection for her, because she always greeted us with a smile and often helped new employees find their way around the building.","t":"A：為什麼員工決定買花和卡片送給下週五即將退休、在我們公司服務了二十年的清潔阿姨？ B：大家都想表達對她的【喜愛】，因為她總是面帶微笑跟我們打招呼，也常常幫新進員工熟悉大樓環境。"},{"w":"souvenir","p":"n.","d":"a thing you buy or keep to remember a place or trip","c":"紀念品","s":"A: What did you bring back for the team from your business trip to Kyoto last week, since everyone was asking about it at the morning meeting? B: I bought a small box of green tea cookies as a souvenir for each person, and I put them on the table in the break room this morning.","t":"A：你上週去京都出差帶了什麼回來給團隊？早上開會時大家都在問這件事。 B：我買了一小盒抹茶餅乾給每個人當作【紀念品】，今天早上已經放在休息室的桌上了。"},{"w":"precious","p":"adj.","d":"very valuable or important; not to be wasted","c":"珍貴的；寶貴的","s":"A: Why does the manager keep that old pen on her desk instead of using one of the new ones from the supply room down the hall? B: It was a gift from the founder of the company when she was first promoted, so it is very precious to her and she never lets anyone borrow it.","t":"A：為什麼經理一直把那支舊筆放在桌上，而不用走廊那頭用品室裡的新筆？ B：那是她第一次升職時公司創辦人送給她的禮物，所以對她來說非常【珍貴】，她從不讓任何人借用。"},{"w":"cherish","p":"v.","d":"to love and care about something very much","c":"珍惜；珍愛","s":"A: Did your grandmother like the photo album that you and your sisters made for her birthday party at the restaurant last Sunday evening? B: She loved it, and she told us that she will cherish it for the rest of her life, because it holds pictures of every family trip we took together.","t":"A：你奶奶喜歡你和你姊妹們上週日晚上在餐廳為她慶生時做的相簿嗎？ B：她非常喜歡，還告訴我們她這輩子都會【珍惜】它，因為裡面有我們全家一起旅行的每一張照片。"},{"w":"widely","p":"adv.","d":"by many people or in many places","c":"廣泛地；普遍地","s":"A: Why are so many companies giving gift cards to their employees at the end of the year instead of buying cakes or holiday baskets? B: Gift cards are now widely accepted at shops, restaurants, and online stores, so workers can choose exactly what they want, and the office does not have to store anything.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多公司在年底送員工禮物卡，而不是買蛋糕或節日禮籃？ B：禮物卡現在在商店、餐廳和網路商店都被【廣泛地】接受，所以員工可以挑選自己真正想要的東西，辦公室也不需要存放任何物品。"},{"w":"farewell","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying goodbye, often at a special event","c":"告別；送別","s":"A: Are we still planning to have lunch together on Thursday for Daniel, who is moving to our branch office in Singapore next month? B: Yes, I booked a private room at the Italian restaurant for his farewell, and we collected money from the whole department to buy him a nice leather briefcase.","t":"A：我們還打算週四一起吃午餐，為下個月要調到新加坡分公司的丹尼爾辦活動嗎？ B：是的，我已經在義大利餐廳訂了包廂為他【送別】，而且我們向整個部門收了錢，要買一個不錯的皮革公事包送他。"},{"w":"suitable","p":"adj.","d":"right or good for a particular person, purpose, or situation","c":"合適的；適當的","s":"A: Do you think a bottle of wine would be a good gift for our new client from the Middle East when he visits our office next week? B: I don't think it would be suitable, because many people from his region don't drink alcohol, so a box of dates or a nice pen might be better.","t":"A：你覺得下週我們來自中東的新客戶來訪辦公室時，送他一瓶葡萄酒當禮物好嗎？ B：我覺得不太【合適】，因為他那個地區很多人不喝酒，所以送一盒椰棗或一支好筆可能比較好。"},{"w":"handmade","p":"adj.","d":"made by a person using their hands, not by a machine","c":"手工製作的","s":"A: Where did you get that beautiful wooden box on your desk, and was it very expensive to buy at one of the shops downtown? B: My neighbor made it for me as a thank-you gift, and because it is handmade, every corner is a little different, which makes it even more special to me.","t":"A：你桌上那個漂亮的木盒是在哪裡買的？在市區的店裡買很貴嗎？ B：那是我鄰居做給我的謝禮，因為是【手工製作的】，每個角落都有點不一樣，這讓它對我來說更特別。"},{"w":"bracelet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of jewelry worn around the wrist","c":"手鍊；手環","s":"A: What are you going to buy your wife for your wedding anniversary next month, since you said she doesn't like perfume or flowers very much? B: I'm thinking of getting her a silver bracelet from the jewelry store near our office, because she often wears one on her wrist when we go out for dinner.","t":"A：下個月結婚週年你打算買什麼給你太太？你說過她不太喜歡香水或花。 B：我想在我們辦公室附近的珠寶店買一條銀【手鍊】給她，因為我們出去吃晚餐時她常常在手腕上戴一條。"},{"w":"pricey","p":"adj.","d":"costing a lot of money; expensive","c":"昂貴的；價格高的","s":"A: Should we order the customer gift baskets from the new shop on Main Street, since their products look so fresh and beautiful in the photos? B: Their baskets are a bit pricey for our budget this year, so let's compare prices with two other stores before we make a final decision with the manager.","t":"A：我們要向大街上那家新店訂客戶禮籃嗎？他們的產品在照片裡看起來很新鮮又漂亮。 B：他們的禮籃以我們今年的預算來說有點【貴】，所以我們先跟另外兩家店比價，再和經理做最後決定吧。"},{"w":"accessory","p":"n.","d":"an extra item such as a bag, belt, or case that goes with something","c":"配件；飾品","s":"A: My brother just bought a new smartphone, and I want to give him something useful for his birthday, but I don't have much money left this month. B: Why don't you buy him a phone accessory like a strong case or a wireless charger, because those are cheap but very practical for daily use?","t":"A：我哥哥剛買了一支新智慧型手機，我想送他實用的生日禮物，但我這個月沒剩多少錢了。 B：你何不買個手機【配件】給他，像是堅固的手機殼或無線充電器？這些很便宜，但日常使用非常實用。"},{"w":"diverse","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other; of many kinds","c":"多樣的；各式各樣的","s":"A: How did you choose the holiday gifts for the international team, since the members come from so many countries and have different tastes? B: Because the team is so diverse, we asked each person to pick an item from an online gift list, so everyone received something they really liked and could use.","t":"A：國際團隊的成員來自這麼多國家、喜好也不同，你們是怎麼挑選節日禮物的？ B：因為團隊組成非常【多元】，我們請每個人從線上禮品清單中挑選一樣東西，所以每個人都收到了自己真正喜歡又用得上的禮物。"},{"w":"spiritual","p":"adj.","d":"related to deep feelings, beliefs, or the soul rather than physical things","c":"心靈的；精神上的","s":"A: Why did you give your teacher a small stone statue from the temple instead of something more practical like a scarf or a pen? B: She told us she visits the temple every month for spiritual reasons, so I thought the statue would have a deeper meaning for her than an ordinary gift.","t":"A：你為什麼送老師廟裡的小石像，而不是送圍巾或筆這類比較實用的東西？ B：她告訴過我們她每個月都會因為【心靈上的】原因去廟裡，所以我覺得這尊石像對她來說會比一般禮物更有深刻的意義。"},{"w":"obstacle","p":"n.","d":"something that makes it difficult to do or achieve something","c":"障礙；阻礙","s":"A: Was it difficult to send the gift packages to our customers overseas before the holidays, since the post office was so busy this year? B: The biggest obstacle was the new customs rules in some countries, so we had to fill out extra forms, but most packages still arrived on time.","t":"A：今年郵局這麼忙，在節日前把禮物包裹寄給海外客戶困難嗎？ B：最大的【障礙】是某些國家的新海關規定，所以我們必須填寫額外的表格，不過大部分包裹還是準時送達了。"},{"w":"convey","p":"v.","d":"to express or communicate a feeling or idea to someone","c":"表達；傳達","s":"A: What should I write in the card that goes with the flowers for the client whose father passed away last week? B: Keep it short and simple, and try to convey that the whole company is thinking of her family, because a long message might feel too formal at such a sad time.","t":"A：上週父親過世的那位客戶，我要在隨花附上的卡片裡寫些什麼？ B：寫得簡短一點，試著【傳達】全公司都掛念著她的家人，因為在這麼悲傷的時刻，太長的訊息可能會顯得太正式。"},{"w":"forgiveness","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping being angry with someone who did something wrong","c":"原諒；寬恕","s":"A: Why did the restaurant send us a free dessert and a gift voucher after our team dinner last night, even though we didn't complain much? B: The waiter spilled soup on your jacket, so the manager wanted to ask for our forgiveness and make sure we would come back again for another event.","t":"A：為什麼昨晚我們團隊聚餐後，餐廳送了免費甜點和禮券給我們，我們其實沒有怎麼抱怨啊？ B：服務生把湯灑在你的外套上，所以經理想請求我們的【原諒】，並確保我們下次辦活動還會再光顧。"},{"w":"monetary","p":"adj.","d":"related to money","c":"金錢的；貨幣的","s":"A: Is the company giving us a gift basket again this year, or will they do something different for the staff at the end of December? B: This year they are offering a monetary bonus instead, so each employee will receive extra money in their January paycheck, which most people seem to prefer.","t":"A：今年公司還是送我們禮籃嗎？還是十二月底會為員工做些不一樣的安排？ B：今年改發【現金的】獎金，所以每位員工一月的薪水裡會多一筆錢，大部分人似乎比較喜歡這樣。"},{"w":"reasonable","p":"adj.","d":"fair and not too expensive; sensible","c":"合理的；價格公道的","s":"A: Where do you usually buy the small gifts for visitors who come to our factory tour, since we need about fifty of them every month? B: There is a shop near the train station that sells nice local snacks at very reasonable prices, and they even give us a discount for large orders.","t":"A：你通常在哪裡買給參觀工廠的訪客的小禮物？我們每個月大約需要五十份。 B：火車站附近有一家店，以非常【合理的】價格販售不錯的在地點心，大量訂購時還會給我們折扣。"},{"w":"decent","p":"adj.","d":"good enough; of acceptable quality","c":"像樣的；不錯的","s":"A: I only have about twenty dollars to spend on a gift for the office party exchange next Friday, so do you think that is enough money? B: Sure, you can find a decent coffee mug or a nice notebook for that price at the department store, and nobody will expect anything very expensive.","t":"A：下週五辦公室派對交換禮物，我只有大約二十美元可以花，你覺得這樣的錢夠嗎？ B：當然夠，你可以在百貨公司用這個價錢買到一個【像樣的】咖啡杯或一本不錯的筆記本，而且沒有人會期待很貴的東西。"},{"w":"construe","p":"v.","d":"to understand the meaning of something in a particular way","c":"理解；解讀","s":"A: Is it a good idea to send an expensive watch to the government officer who is reviewing our building permit next month? B: No, he might construe it as a bribe, and that could cause serious legal problems for the company, so it is better to send a simple thank-you letter instead.","t":"A：送一支昂貴的手錶給下個月要審查我們建築許可的政府官員，是個好主意嗎？ B：不好，他可能會把它【解讀】為賄賂，這會給公司帶來嚴重的法律問題，所以最好改寄一封簡單的感謝信。"},{"w":"stingy","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to spend or give money","c":"吝嗇的；小氣的","s":"A: Why did people complain about the gifts that the new manager gave the team at the end of the year, since he usually seems so friendly? B: He gave everyone a single pencil after a very busy year, so many workers thought he was being stingy, even though the company had made a big profit.","t":"A：新經理平常看起來很友善，為什麼大家會抱怨他年底送給團隊的禮物？ B：在非常忙碌的一年之後，他只送每個人一支鉛筆，所以很多員工覺得他很【小氣】，即使公司賺了大筆利潤。"},{"w":"connote","p":"v.","d":"to suggest a feeling or idea in addition to the main meaning","c":"暗示；意味著","s":"A: Why shouldn't we give clocks as gifts to our business partners in Taiwan when we visit their headquarters in Taipei next month? B: In Chinese culture, giving a clock can connote death or the end of a relationship, so it is better to choose tea, fruit, or another gift with a positive meaning.","t":"A：下個月我們去台北拜訪台灣商業夥伴的總部時，為什麼不應該送時鐘當禮物？ B：在華人文化中，送時鐘會【暗示】死亡或關係的結束，所以最好選擇茶葉、水果或其他寓意正面的禮物。"},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adj.","d":"unusual or surprising in a way that people notice","c":"非凡的；值得注意的","s":"A: Did you hear that the sales team raised enough money to buy gifts for every child at the local hospital before the holidays this year? B: Yes, it was a remarkable effort, because they collected over five thousand dollars in just two weeks while still finishing all their regular work on time.","t":"A：你有聽說今年節日前業務團隊募到足夠的錢，為本地醫院的每個孩子買禮物嗎？ B：有啊，那真是【非凡的】努力，因為他們在短短兩週內募到超過五千美元，同時還準時完成所有日常工作。"},{"w":"luxurious","p":"adj.","d":"very comfortable and expensive","c":"奢華的；豪華的","s":"A: How did the company thank the top salespeople this year, since they broke every record in the last quarter? B: They gave them a weekend at a luxurious hotel by the beach, with a private pool, free massages, and dinner at the best restaurant in town for each winner and a guest.","t":"A：公司今年怎麼感謝頂尖業務員？他們在上一季打破了所有紀錄。 B：公司招待他們到海邊一間【豪華的】飯店度週末，有私人泳池、免費按摩，還有每位得獎者和一位同行者在鎮上最好的餐廳享用晚餐。"},{"w":"catalog","p":"n.","d":"a book or list of products with pictures and prices","c":"目錄；型錄","s":"A: How can I choose the corporate gifts for our clients this year if the supplier's showroom is closed for repairs until next month? B: You can look through their online catalog, which shows photos, prices, and sizes of every item, and then call the sales representative to place the order.","t":"A：如果供應商的展示間在整修、要到下個月才開放，我今年要怎麼挑選送客戶的企業禮品？ B：你可以瀏覽他們的線上【型錄】，裡面有每件商品的照片、價格和尺寸，然後再打電話給業務代表下訂單。"}]},{"unit":157,"theme":"Globalization 全球化","cards":[{"w":"integration","p":"n.","d":"the process of joining different parts or groups so they work together as one","c":"整合；融合","s":"A: Why has the head office asked every branch manager to attend a two-day workshop in Singapore next month instead of the usual online meeting? B: The company bought two smaller firms in Asia last year, and the directors believe that the integration of their sales teams will be much smoother if everyone meets face to face.","t":"A：為什麼總公司要求每位分店經理下個月到新加坡參加為期兩天的研習，而不是平常的線上會議？ B：公司去年在亞洲收購了兩家較小的公司，董事們認為如果大家面對面見面，雙方銷售團隊的【整合】會順利得多。"},{"w":"multinational","p":"adj.","d":"working in or involving many different countries","c":"跨國的；多國的","s":"A: Are you still thinking about leaving the small design studio downtown, or have you decided to stay there for a few more years? B: I actually accepted an offer from a large multinational company with offices in twelve countries, so I hope to work abroad for a while and improve my language skills.","t":"A：你還在考慮離開市中心那間小型設計工作室嗎，還是已經決定再待幾年？ B：其實我接受了一家在十二個國家設有辦公室的大型【跨國】公司的工作邀約，所以我希望能到國外工作一段時間，順便提升語言能力。"},{"w":"trade","p":"n.","d":"the activity of buying and selling goods between people, companies or countries","c":"貿易；買賣","s":"A: Why are so many local fruit farmers suddenly sending their mangoes to Japan and Korea instead of selling them at the night markets as they did before? B: The government signed a new agreement last spring that makes trade with those countries cheaper and easier, so farmers can now earn much higher prices overseas.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多本地果農突然把芒果賣到日本和韓國，而不像以前一樣在夜市販售？ B：政府去年春天簽署了一項新協議，讓與這些國家的【貿易】變得更便宜、更容易，所以農民現在在海外能賣到高得多的價格。"},{"w":"tariff","p":"n.","d":"a tax that a government puts on goods coming into or going out of a country","c":"關稅","s":"A: Have you noticed that the price of the imported cheese in the staff cafeteria went up by almost thirty percent this month? B: Yes, the manager explained that a new tariff on European dairy products started in October, so the supplier had to pay more at the border and passed the cost on to us.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到員工餐廳裡進口起司的價格這個月漲了將近三成？ B：有啊，經理解釋說十月起對歐洲乳製品開始課徵一項新的【關稅】，所以供應商在通關時得付更多錢，就把成本轉嫁給我們了。"},{"w":"export","p":"v.","d":"to send goods to another country to sell them","c":"出口；輸出","s":"A: Our tea sales in Taiwan have been flat for two years, so what does the marketing director suggest we do to grow the business? B: She wants us to export our premium oolong to Canada and Australia, because many health-conscious customers there are willing to pay more for high-quality products from Asia.","t":"A：我們在台灣的茶葉銷售兩年來都沒有成長，行銷總監建議我們怎麼擴展業務？ B：她希望我們把高級烏龍茶【出口】到加拿大和澳洲，因為那裡很多注重健康的顧客願意花更多錢購買來自亞洲的優質產品。"},{"w":"import","p":"v.","d":"to bring goods into a country from another country to sell them","c":"進口；輸入","s":"A: Why does the new furniture shop near the station have so many beautiful wooden tables that you cannot find anywhere else in the city? B: The owner travels to Indonesia twice a year, chooses the pieces herself, and then has them shipped here, because she prefers to import handmade items rather than buy from local factories.","t":"A：為什麼車站附近那家新開的家具店有那麼多在城裡其他地方都找不到的漂亮木桌？ B：老闆每年去印尼兩次，親自挑選家具再運回來，因為她比較喜歡【進口】手工製品，而不是向本地工廠購買。"},{"w":"outsourcing","p":"n.","d":"paying another company, often in another country, to do work that your company used to do itself","c":"外包","s":"A: How did our accounting department manage to cut its costs so much this year without hiring fewer people or asking anyone to work overtime? B: The finance team started outsourcing the monthly payroll to a specialist firm in Manila, which allowed our own staff to focus on budgeting and other more important tasks.","t":"A：今年我們會計部門是如何在不減少人手、也不要求任何人加班的情況下大幅降低成本的？ B：財務團隊開始把每月的薪資作業【外包】給馬尼拉一家專業公司，讓我們自己的員工能專注在預算編列和其他更重要的工作上。"},{"w":"supply chain","p":"n.phr.","d":"the whole series of companies and steps involved in making a product and getting it to customers","c":"供應鏈","s":"A: Why were the new laptops for the sales team delivered six weeks late, even though we placed the order back in January? B: The computer maker said a factory fire in one country and a shipping delay in another caused serious problems across its whole supply chain, so many customers around the world had to wait.","t":"A：為什麼業務團隊的新筆電晚了六週才送到，我們明明一月就下單了？ B：電腦製造商說，一個國家的工廠火災加上另一個國家的運輸延誤，讓他們整個【供應鏈】出現嚴重問題，所以全球很多客戶都得等待。"},{"w":"cultural exchange","p":"n.phr.","d":"an activity in which people from different countries share and learn about each other's customs and way of life","c":"文化交流","s":"A: What is the purpose of the program that brings twenty young engineers from Vietnam to work in our Taichung office for six months? B: Besides training them in new skills, the company sees it as a cultural exchange, since our local staff can learn about Vietnamese customs while the visitors experience daily life in Taiwan.","t":"A：讓二十位越南年輕工程師到我們台中辦公室工作六個月的這個計畫目的是什麼？ B：除了訓練他們新技能，公司也把它視為一種【文化交流】，因為我們的本地員工可以認識越南的習俗，而來訪者也能體驗台灣的日常生活。"},{"w":"migration","p":"n.","d":"the movement of people from one place or country to another to live or work","c":"遷移；移民","s":"A: Why is the city planning to build three new schools and a large hospital in the northern district over the next five years? B: The report showed that the migration of young families from the countryside into that area has grown quickly, because many new factories there are offering stable jobs and good salaries.","t":"A：為什麼市政府計畫在未來五年內於北區興建三所新學校和一間大型醫院？ B：報告顯示從鄉村【遷移】到該地區的年輕家庭快速增加，因為那裡很多新工廠提供穩定的工作和不錯的薪水。"},{"w":"urbanization","p":"n.","d":"the process by which more and more people leave the countryside to live in towns and cities","c":"都市化","s":"A: Our sales of small apartment furniture have doubled in Southeast Asia, but do you know what is driving this sudden demand? B: Rapid urbanization is the main reason, since millions of people are moving from farms into crowded cities, where they live in smaller homes and need furniture that saves space.","t":"A：我們的小坪數公寓家具在東南亞的銷量翻倍了，你知道是什麼帶動這股突然的需求嗎？ B：快速的【都市化】是主要原因，因為數百萬人從農村搬到擁擠的城市，住在較小的房子裡，需要節省空間的家具。"},{"w":"digitalization","p":"n.","d":"the change to using computers and digital technology to do work that was done on paper or by hand","c":"數位化","s":"A: Why did the bank close two of its branches downtown and move several tellers to the customer service center last year? B: Because of the digitalization of its services, most customers now open accounts, pay bills and transfer money on their phones, so far fewer people visit the branches in person.","t":"A：為什麼這家銀行去年關閉了市中心的兩間分行，還把幾位櫃員調到客服中心？ B：由於服務的【數位化】，現在大部分客戶都用手機開戶、繳費和轉帳，所以親自到分行的人少了很多。"},{"w":"connectivity","p":"n.","d":"the ability of computers, phones or places to connect with each other or with the internet","c":"連結性；連線能力","s":"A: Why did the conference organizers choose that new hotel by the river instead of the older one we used for the event last year? B: The new hotel offers much better internet connectivity, so speakers can show videos smoothly and guests from overseas can join the sessions online without any problems.","t":"A：為什麼會議主辦單位選了河邊那家新飯店，而不是我們去年辦活動用的那家舊飯店？ B：新飯店提供好得多的網路【連線能力】，講者可以順暢播放影片，海外來賓也能毫無問題地在線上參加議程。"},{"w":"free trade","p":"n.phr.","d":"trade between countries without taxes or limits on the goods that are bought and sold","c":"自由貿易","s":"A: Why are the car parts we buy from Thailand so much cheaper this year than they were when we first ordered them three years ago? B: The two governments signed a free trade agreement last summer, which removed the extra taxes on many products, so our supplier can now offer us much lower prices.","t":"A：為什麼我們向泰國購買的汽車零件今年比三年前第一次訂購時便宜這麼多？ B：兩國政府去年夏天簽署了【自由貿易】協定，取消了許多產品的額外稅金，所以我們的供應商現在能提供低很多的價格。"},{"w":"liberalization","p":"n.","d":"the act of making laws or rules less strict, especially so that business can grow","c":"自由化；開放","s":"A: How were foreign banks able to open so many branches in that country over the last ten years when it used to be nearly impossible? B: After the financial liberalization in 2015, the government removed many strict rules on overseas firms, so international companies could finally enter the market and compete with local banks.","t":"A：過去十年外國銀行是怎麼在那個國家開設這麼多分行的？以前幾乎不可能啊。 B：在2015年金融【自由化】之後，政府取消了許多針對海外公司的嚴格規定，所以國際企業終於能進入市場，和本地銀行競爭。"},{"w":"investment","p":"n.","d":"money that is put into a business or project in order to make a profit later","c":"投資","s":"A: Why is the company suddenly hiring so many engineers and building a second factory outside Kaohsiung this year? B: A large Japanese firm made a major investment in our business last spring, giving us enough money to expand production and develop new products for customers in Asia and Europe.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年突然招募這麼多工程師，還在高雄郊區蓋第二座工廠？ B：一家日本大企業去年春天對我們公司做了一筆重大的【投資】，讓我們有足夠的資金擴大生產，並為亞洲和歐洲的客戶開發新產品。"},{"w":"deregulation","p":"n.","d":"the removal of government rules and controls from an industry","c":"解除管制；放寬管制","s":"A: Why are there so many cheap airlines offering flights between Taipei and other Asian cities these days compared with twenty years ago? B: The deregulation of the airline industry allowed new companies to set their own prices and routes, so competition increased and travelers can now find much lower fares.","t":"A：為什麼現在和二十年前相比，有這麼多廉價航空提供台北往返亞洲其他城市的航班？ B：航空業的【解除管制】讓新公司可以自訂票價和航線，於是競爭增加，旅客現在能找到便宜很多的機票。"},{"w":"cooperation","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together with others to achieve a shared goal","c":"合作","s":"A: How did the two rival electronics companies manage to finish the new charging station for electric scooters ahead of schedule? B: Thanks to close cooperation between their engineering teams, who shared ideas and test results every week, the project avoided many delays and was completed a full month early.","t":"A：那兩家互相競爭的電子公司是怎麼提前完成新的電動機車充電站的？ B：多虧兩家工程團隊的密切【合作】，他們每週分享想法和測試結果，這個專案避開了許多延誤，整整提早了一個月完成。"},{"w":"inequality","p":"n.","d":"an unfair situation in which some people have more money, chances or rights than others","c":"不平等","s":"A: What was the main topic of the speech that the economist gave at the business forum in Taipei yesterday afternoon? B: She talked about growing inequality between rich and poor workers, explaining that while some people benefit from global markets, many factory workers have seen their wages stay the same for years.","t":"A：那位經濟學家昨天下午在台北商業論壇上的演講主題是什麼？ B：她談到富裕和貧窮勞工之間日益擴大的【不平等】，解釋說雖然有些人從全球市場中獲益，但許多工廠工人的薪水多年來都沒有增加。"},{"w":"homogenization","p":"n.","d":"the process of things becoming the same or very similar to each other","c":"同質化","s":"A: Why did the travel writer say in her latest article that many city centers around the world now feel almost exactly alike? B: She was worried about the homogenization of shopping streets, because the same coffee chains, fashion stores and fast-food restaurants have replaced many small local shops with their own special character.","t":"A：為什麼那位旅遊作家在最新文章中說世界各地許多市中心現在感覺幾乎一模一樣？ B：她擔心購物街的【同質化】，因為同樣的連鎖咖啡店、服飾店和速食餐廳已經取代了許多各具特色的在地小店。"},{"w":"localization","p":"n.","d":"the process of changing a product or service so that it suits the language and culture of a particular country","c":"在地化","s":"A: Our mobile game is very popular in Taiwan, so why can't we just launch the same version in Brazil next month? B: The game needs careful localization first, which means translating all the text into Portuguese, changing some holiday events and adjusting prices so that players there feel it was made for them.","t":"A：我們的手機遊戲在台灣很受歡迎，為什麼不能下個月直接在巴西推出同樣的版本？ B：遊戲需要先仔細做【在地化】，也就是把所有文字翻成葡萄牙文、修改一些節慶活動並調整價格，讓那裡的玩家覺得遊戲是為他們打造的。"},{"w":"sustainability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to continue for a long time without harming the environment or using up resources","c":"永續性","s":"A: Why did the board decide to switch to recycled packaging even though it costs the company about ten percent more? B: Many of our biggest overseas clients now ask suppliers to prove their sustainability, so reducing plastic waste helps us protect the environment and keep important contracts at the same time.","t":"A：為什麼董事會決定改用回收包裝，即使這會讓公司多花約一成的成本？ B：我們許多海外大客戶現在要求供應商證明自己的【永續性】，所以減少塑膠廢棄物能幫助我們保護環境，同時保住重要合約。"},{"w":"development","p":"n.","d":"the process of growing or improving, especially of a country's economy or a new product","c":"發展；開發","s":"A: Why is the bank lending so much money to build roads and power stations in that small country in Africa this year? B: The project supports the economic development of the region, because better roads and reliable electricity will help local businesses grow and create thousands of new jobs for young people.","t":"A：為什麼這家銀行今年要借那麼多錢給非洲那個小國修建道路和發電廠？ B：這個計畫支持該地區的經濟【發展】，因為更好的道路和穩定的電力能幫助當地企業成長，並為年輕人創造數千個新工作。"},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"n.","d":"the basic systems a country or city needs, such as roads, bridges, power and water supply","c":"基礎建設","s":"A: Why did our company finally choose Vietnam instead of a nearby country for the new factory after visiting both places? B: The main reason was the infrastructure, since the area in Vietnam already has modern highways, a large port and a stable power supply, which will make shipping our products much easier.","t":"A：為什麼公司在考察兩地之後，最後選擇越南而不是鄰近國家來設新工廠？ B：主要原因是【基礎建設】，因為越南那個地區已經有現代化的高速公路、大型港口和穩定的電力供應，運送產品會方便得多。"},{"w":"innovation","p":"n.","d":"a new idea, method or product, or the act of creating one","c":"創新","s":"A: How has that small software company from Hsinchu been able to win contracts against huge competitors from the United States? B: Its success comes from constant innovation, because the team releases creative new features every few months and listens carefully to what customers need instead of copying other products.","t":"A：新竹那家小型軟體公司是怎麼在與美國大型競爭對手的較量中贏得合約的？ B：它的成功來自不斷的【創新】，因為團隊每隔幾個月就推出有創意的新功能，並且仔細傾聽客戶需求，而不是模仿其他產品。"},{"w":"competitiveness","p":"n.","d":"the ability of a company or country to compete successfully with others","c":"競爭力","s":"A: Why is the government offering free English and computer training courses to factory workers in central Taiwan this year? B: Officials hope to improve the competitiveness of local manufacturers, since workers with better skills can help companies produce higher-quality goods and win more orders from foreign buyers.","t":"A：為什麼政府今年提供中台灣工廠工人免費的英文和電腦訓練課程？ B：官員希望提升本地製造商的【競爭力】，因為技能更好的工人能幫助公司生產品質更高的產品，並贏得更多外國買家的訂單。"},{"w":"diplomacy","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping good relations between the governments of different countries","c":"外交；外交手腕","s":"A: Why did the president of our trade association travel to three European capitals last month to meet government officials? B: Her trip was part of an effort in economic diplomacy, because building friendly relationships with those governments may help our members get fewer trade barriers and more business opportunities abroad.","t":"A：為什麼我們貿易協會的理事長上個月走訪三個歐洲首都和政府官員會面？ B：她的出訪是經濟【外交】工作的一部分，因為和那些政府建立友好關係，可能幫助我們的會員減少貿易障礙，並獲得更多海外商機。"},{"w":"interdependence","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which people, companies or countries depend on each other","c":"相互依存","s":"A: Why did a flood in one Southeast Asian country cause car factories in Japan and America to stop production for several weeks? B: It shows the strong interdependence of today's economies, since a single factory making small electronic parts can affect many manufacturers on the other side of the world.","t":"A：為什麼東南亞某個國家的一場水災，會讓日本和美國的汽車工廠停產好幾週？ B：這顯示出現今各經濟體之間高度的【相互依存】，因為一間製造小型電子零件的工廠，就可能影響世界另一端的許多製造商。"},{"w":"capitalism","p":"n.","d":"an economic system in which businesses are owned by private people and run to make a profit","c":"資本主義","s":"A: What did the professor focus on in his lecture about the history of the global economy at the business school last night? B: He explained how modern capitalism spread around the world after the 1990s, as more countries allowed private companies to own factories, compete freely and keep their profits.","t":"A：昨晚教授在商學院關於全球經濟史的講座中重點講了什麼？ B：他解釋了現代【資本主義】在1990年代之後如何擴散到全世界，因為越來越多國家允許私人公司擁有工廠、自由競爭並保留利潤。"},{"w":"market economy","p":"n.phr.","d":"an economic system in which prices and production are decided by supply and demand rather than by the government","c":"市場經濟","s":"A: Why are so many foreign companies now opening offices in that Eastern European country, which had very few businesses from abroad before? B: The country changed to a market economy about twenty years ago, so prices are now set by supply and demand, and private firms can compete without strict government control.","t":"A：為什麼那個東歐國家以前幾乎沒有外國企業，現在卻有這麼多外國公司去設辦公室？ B：那個國家大約二十年前轉型為【市場經濟】，所以現在價格由供需決定，私人公司也能在沒有嚴格政府管控的情況下競爭。"},{"w":"diversification","p":"n.","d":"the act of starting to sell different products or enter different markets to reduce risk","c":"多角化；多樣化","s":"A: Why did the bicycle maker begin selling electric scooters and outdoor clothing when its bikes were already selling so well in Europe? B: The managers believe that diversification reduces risk, because if demand for bicycles falls in one market, sales of the new products can still keep the company profitable.","t":"A：那家自行車製造商的自行車在歐洲已經賣得很好，為什麼還開始賣電動滑板車和戶外服飾？ B：經理們認為【多角化】能降低風險，因為如果某個市場的自行車需求下滑，新產品的銷售仍能讓公司維持獲利。"},{"w":"expansion","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming larger, for example by opening new stores or entering new markets","c":"擴張；擴展","s":"A: Why is the bubble tea chain hiring so many new managers who can speak both English and Spanish this year? B: The company is planning a rapid expansion into Mexico and the United States, where it hopes to open about fifty new stores in shopping malls and busy downtown areas.","t":"A：為什麼那家珍珠奶茶連鎖店今年招募這麼多會說英文和西班牙文的新經理？ B：公司正計畫快速【擴張】到墨西哥和美國，希望在購物中心和熱鬧的市中心開設約五十家新店。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together with another person or group to create or produce something","c":"合作；協作","s":"A: How did the Taiwanese sportswear brand manage to design such a popular running shoe for the international market so quickly? B: It was the result of a collaboration with a famous design studio in Italy, which shared its experience in style while our engineers focused on comfort and quality.","t":"A：那個台灣運動服飾品牌是怎麼這麼快就為國際市場設計出這麼受歡迎的跑鞋？ B：那是和義大利一家知名設計工作室【合作】的成果，對方分享了風格方面的經驗，而我們的工程師則專注在舒適度和品質上。"},{"w":"influence","p":"n.","d":"the power to have an effect on people, things or the way something develops","c":"影響；影響力","s":"A: Why do so many young people in Taipei now wear clothes and use phrases that come from Korean dramas and pop music? B: Korean entertainment has a strong influence on youth culture across Asia, because popular shows and singers are easy to watch online and quickly set new trends in fashion and language.","t":"A：為什麼台北現在有這麼多年輕人穿的衣服和說的用語都來自韓劇和流行音樂？ B：韓國娛樂對全亞洲的青年文化有很強的【影響】，因為熱門節目和歌手在網路上很容易看到，很快就帶起時尚和語言的新潮流。"}]},{"unit":158,"theme":"Goal 目標","cards":[{"w":"objective","p":"n.","d":"something you are trying to achieve","c":"目標；目的","s":"A: What is the main objective of next week's training session for the new customer service staff at our call center? B: We want them to learn how to handle angry callers politely and solve common billing problems quickly, so that fewer customers need to call us back later.","t":"A：我們客服中心下週為新進客服人員舉辦的訓練課程，主要【目標】是什麼？ B：我們希望他們學會如何有禮貌地應對生氣的來電者，並快速解決常見的帳單問題，讓之後需要再打電話來的客戶變少。"},{"w":"target","p":"n.","d":"a result or amount that you try to reach","c":"目標；指標","s":"A: Did our sales team manage to reach this month's target of two hundred new contracts before the end of the quarter? B: Not quite, because two big clients delayed their orders until January, but the manager believes we can make up the difference with the holiday promotion next month.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊在這一季結束前，有達成這個月簽下兩百份新合約的【目標】嗎？ B：還差一點，因為兩個大客戶把訂單延到一月，不過經理相信我們可以靠下個月的節日促銷活動補足差額。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to be successful or to do something","c":"抱負；雄心","s":"A: Why did Sarah leave her stable job at the bank and start working for a small travel company last spring? B: She has always had the ambition to run her own tour business one day, so she wanted to learn how the travel industry works from the inside first.","t":"A：莎拉為什麼去年春天辭掉銀行的穩定工作，跑去一家小旅行社上班？ B：她一直有個【抱負】，希望有一天能經營自己的旅遊公司，所以她想先從內部了解旅遊業是怎麼運作的。"},{"w":"aspiration","p":"n.","d":"a hope or wish to achieve something important","c":"志向；渴望","s":"A: During her job interview, what did the young applicant say about her long-term career plans in our marketing department? B: She explained that her main aspiration is to become a team leader within five years, and she is already taking evening classes in management to prepare for that role.","t":"A：在面試中，那位年輕應徵者對於她在我們行銷部門的長期職涯規劃說了什麼？ B：她說她最主要的【志向】是五年內成為團隊主管，而且她已經在上夜間管理課程，為那個職位做準備。"},{"w":"purpose","p":"n.","d":"the reason why something is done","c":"目的；用途","s":"A: What is the purpose of the online survey that the human resources department sent to all employees this morning? B: They want to find out how satisfied people are with the new flexible working hours, and they will use the results to decide whether to continue the system next year.","t":"A：人資部門今天早上寄給全體員工的線上問卷，【目的】是什麼？ B：他們想了解大家對新的彈性工時有多滿意，並會根據結果決定明年是否繼續實施這個制度。"},{"w":"mission","p":"n.","d":"the main aim of an organization, or an important job someone is given","c":"使命；任務","s":"A: Why does the company print that short sentence about healthy food on every box and on the wall of the reception area? B: It describes our mission, which is to provide fresh and affordable meals to busy families, and the founders want every employee and visitor to remember it.","t":"A：公司為什麼要在每個盒子上和接待區牆上印那句關於健康食品的短句？ B：那句話說明了我們的【使命】，也就是為忙碌的家庭提供新鮮又實惠的餐點，創辦人希望每位員工和訪客都記得。"},{"w":"intention","p":"n.","d":"something you plan or mean to do","c":"意圖；打算","s":"A: Did the landlord say anything about raising the rent for our office when he visited the building yesterday afternoon? B: He told us that he has no intention of increasing it this year, because he is happy that we always pay on time and take good care of the place.","t":"A：房東昨天下午來大樓時，有提到要調漲我們辦公室的租金嗎？ B：他告訴我們他今年沒有調漲的【打算】，因為他很滿意我們總是準時付款，也把地方照顧得很好。"},{"w":"plan","p":"n.","d":"a set of steps you decide on to do something","c":"計畫","s":"A: What should we prepare before we meet the bank manager on Thursday to ask for a loan for our second café? B: We need a clear business plan that shows our expected costs, how many customers we hope to attract, and how we will pay the money back within three years.","t":"A：我們週四要去見銀行經理，為第二家咖啡店申請貸款，之前應該準備什麼？ B：我們需要一份清楚的營運【計畫】書，列出預估成本、希望吸引多少顧客，以及我們如何在三年內還清貸款。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a careful plan for reaching a goal, especially over a long time","c":"策略","s":"A: Why have our online sales increased so much since the beginning of this year, even though we did not lower our prices? B: The marketing team changed its strategy and started working with popular food bloggers, which helped us reach many younger customers who had never heard of our brand before.","t":"A：雖然我們沒有降價，為什麼今年年初以來線上銷售成長這麼多？ B：行銷團隊改變了【策略】，開始和熱門的美食部落客合作，幫助我們接觸到很多以前從沒聽過我們品牌的年輕顧客。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"an idea of what the future should be like","c":"願景","s":"A: What did the new director talk about during her first speech to the staff at the annual company dinner last night? B: She shared her vision for the next ten years, explaining that she hopes to open branches in three more Asian countries and make our products more environmentally friendly.","t":"A：新任總監昨晚在公司年度晚宴上第一次對員工演講，她談了些什麼？ B：她分享了未來十年的【願景】，說明她希望在另外三個亞洲國家開設分公司，並讓我們的產品更環保。"},{"w":"dream","p":"n.","d":"something you have wanted to do or have for a long time","c":"夢想","s":"A: Is it true that the chef from our hotel restaurant is leaving next month to move back to his hometown in the south? B: Yes, he finally saved enough money to open a small noodle shop there, which has been his dream since he was a teenager helping in his grandmother's kitchen.","t":"A：我們飯店餐廳的主廚下個月要離職、搬回南部老家，是真的嗎？ B：是的，他終於存夠錢要在那裡開一家小麵店，那是他從少年時期在祖母廚房幫忙時就有的【夢想】。"},{"w":"milestone","p":"n.","d":"an important event or stage in a process","c":"里程碑","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office wearing party hats and eating cake this afternoon instead of working at their desks? B: Our online shop just reached one million customers, which is an important milestone for a company that started with only three people in a tiny apartment five years ago.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午辦公室裡每個人都戴著派對帽吃蛋糕，而不是坐在位子上工作？ B：我們的網路商店剛達到一百萬名顧客，對一家五年前只有三個人在小公寓裡創業的公司來說，這是個重要的【里程碑】。"},{"w":"achievement","p":"n.","d":"something good you have done through effort","c":"成就","s":"A: Why was the director of our factory invited to give a speech at the industry conference in Singapore next month? B: Cutting energy use by thirty percent in only two years was a great achievement, and other companies want to learn how her team managed to do it without reducing production.","t":"A：為什麼我們工廠的廠長受邀下個月在新加坡的產業研討會上演講？ B：只用兩年就把能源使用量減少百分之三十是很了不起的【成就】，其他公司都想知道她的團隊如何在不減產的情況下做到。"},{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"the result of getting what you wanted or planned","c":"成功","s":"A: How did the new product launch at the shopping mall go last weekend, and did many people come to try the samples? B: It was a huge success, because all the free samples were gone in two hours, and the store received more than five hundred online orders by Sunday evening.","t":"A：上週末在購物中心的新品發表會進行得如何？有很多人來試用樣品嗎？ B：非常【成功】，所有免費樣品兩個小時內就發完了，而且到週日晚上，店家收到超過五百筆網路訂單。"},{"w":"attain","p":"v.","d":"to reach or achieve something after effort","c":"達到；獲得","s":"A: How long does it usually take for a new staff member at our accounting firm to get the highest professional certificate? B: Most people need about four years of hard study and work experience to attain that level, but a few very talented accountants have done it in less than three.","t":"A：我們會計師事務所的新進人員通常需要多久才能拿到最高等級的專業證照？ B：大多數人需要大約四年的努力讀書和工作經驗才能【達到】那個等級，不過有少數非常有天分的會計師不到三年就做到了。"},{"w":"accomplish","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in doing something","c":"完成；達成","s":"A: Do you really think our small team of four people can finish redesigning the whole company website before the product launch in March? B: It will be hard, but if we divide the work carefully and avoid unnecessary meetings, I believe we can accomplish the task on time without working every weekend.","t":"A：你真的認為我們四人小組能在三月產品發表前完成整個公司網站的改版嗎？ B：會很辛苦，但如果我們仔細分工、避免不必要的會議，我相信我們能準時【完成】這項任務，而且不必每個週末都加班。"},{"w":"pursue","p":"v.","d":"to try to achieve or do something over a period of time","c":"追求；從事","s":"A: Why is Kevin from the sales department leaving the company after working here successfully for more than ten years? B: He has decided to pursue a career in teaching, so he will study at a university in Taichung for two years and then look for a job at a high school.","t":"A：業務部的凱文在這裡表現很好、工作了十多年，為什麼要離開公司？ B：他決定【從事】教職，所以他會在台中的大學進修兩年，然後找一份高中的工作。"},{"w":"strive","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to do something","c":"努力；奮鬥","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager read every online review from guests so carefully, even the short ones written late at night? B: All of our staff strive to give each guest a comfortable and pleasant stay, and reviews help us find small problems that we might not notice by ourselves.","t":"A：飯店經理為什麼會這麼仔細地閱讀每一則房客的網路評論，連深夜寫的短評也不放過？ B：我們所有員工都【努力】讓每位客人住得舒適愉快，而評論能幫助我們發現自己可能沒注意到的小問題。"},{"w":"aim","p":"v.","d":"to plan or try to achieve something","c":"力求；打算","s":"A: How quickly will customers receive their orders after the company opens the new warehouse near the airport next month? B: We aim to deliver every package within twenty-four hours in the northern area, and we are hiring thirty more drivers so that we can keep this promise during busy holidays.","t":"A：公司下個月在機場附近的新倉庫啟用後，顧客多快能收到訂單？ B：我們【力求】在北部地區二十四小時內送達每個包裹，而且我們正在多招募三十名司機，以便在忙碌的假期也能履行這個承諾。"},{"w":"focus","p":"v.","d":"to give most of your attention to one thing","c":"專注；集中","s":"A: There are so many complaints about the new website that I don't know where to start at tomorrow's team meeting. What should we do? B: Let's focus on the payment problems first, because customers cannot buy anything when that page fails, and we can fix the design details later.","t":"A：關於新網站的抱怨實在太多了，我不知道明天團隊會議該從哪裡開始。我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們先【專注】在付款問題上，因為那個頁面出錯時顧客什麼都買不了，設計細節之後再修就好。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"a promise or firm decision to do something","c":"承諾；投入","s":"A: Why did the city choose our company to supply the new buses instead of the cheaper company from overseas? B: The officials were impressed by our strong commitment to reducing pollution, since all our buses are electric and we promised to recycle the old batteries at no extra cost.","t":"A：市政府為什麼選擇我們公司供應新公車，而不是那家比較便宜的海外公司？ B：官員們對我們減少污染的堅定【承諾】印象深刻，因為我們所有公車都是電動的，而且我們承諾免費回收舊電池。"},{"w":"determination","p":"n.","d":"the quality of continuing to try even when something is difficult","c":"決心","s":"A: How did the young designer manage to start her own clothing company after so many banks refused to lend her money? B: She showed great determination, selling her designs at weekend markets for three years and saving every dollar until she finally had enough to rent a small shop.","t":"A：在那麼多銀行拒絕借錢給她之後，這位年輕設計師是怎麼成功創立自己的服飾公司的？ B：她展現了極大的【決心】，花了三年在週末市集販售自己的設計，存下每一塊錢，直到終於有足夠的錢租下一間小店面。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the desire or reason to do something","c":"動機；動力","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to give a small bonus to every worker who finishes their training courses this year? B: She noticed that staff motivation was low after the long busy season, and she hopes the extra money will encourage people to learn new skills and feel more valued.","t":"A：經理為什麼決定今年發一小筆獎金給每位完成培訓課程的員工？ B：她注意到在漫長的旺季之後員工的【動力】很低，希望這筆額外的錢能鼓勵大家學習新技能，並覺得自己更受重視。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"something that is more important than other things","c":"優先事項；首要之務","s":"A: Why do the workers at the factory check every machine so carefully before the morning shift begins, even when we are busy? B: Worker safety is our top priority, so we would rather start production twenty minutes late than let anyone use equipment that might be broken or dangerous.","t":"A：為什麼工廠的工人在早班開始前要那麼仔細地檢查每台機器，即使我們很忙也一樣？ B：員工安全是我們的【首要之務】，所以我們寧願晚二十分鐘開工，也不讓任何人使用可能損壞或危險的設備。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the time or date by which something must be done","c":"截止期限","s":"A: Is there any chance we can send the final design for the hotel brochure to the printing company next Monday instead of this Friday? B: I'm afraid not, because the deadline is Friday at five o'clock, and if we are late, the brochures will not be ready for the travel fair in Tokyo.","t":"A：飯店手冊的最終設計，我們有可能下週一再寄給印刷廠，而不是這週五嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為【截止期限】是週五五點，如果我們遲交，手冊就趕不上東京的旅展了。"},{"w":"progress","p":"n.","d":"movement toward finishing or improving something","c":"進展；進步","s":"A: How is the construction of the new shopping mall near the train station going, and will it really open before the summer holidays? B: The builders are making good progress now that the rainy season is over, and the manager says the first three floors should be ready for shops by early June.","t":"A：火車站附近的新購物中心工程進行得如何？真的會在暑假前開幕嗎？ B：雨季結束後，工人們的【進展】很順利，經理說前三層樓應該在六月初就能讓店家進駐。"},{"w":"outcome","p":"n.","d":"the final result of something","c":"結果","s":"A: Has anyone heard what happened at the meeting with the Japanese supplier about the new prices for next year's orders? B: We are still waiting for the outcome, because both sides wanted more time to think, but our manager expects a final decision by the end of this week.","t":"A：有人知道跟日本供應商討論明年訂單新價格的那場會議怎麼樣了嗎？ B：我們還在等【結果】，因為雙方都想要更多時間考慮，不過經理預計這週結束前會有最終決定。"},{"w":"benchmark","p":"n.","d":"a standard used to compare and judge other things","c":"基準；標竿","s":"A: Why do the engineers keep testing our new laptop against the popular model that our biggest competitor released last year? B: That model has become the benchmark for battery life in the industry, so we need to show customers that our product can run even longer on a single charge.","t":"A：為什麼工程師一直拿我們的新筆電和最大競爭對手去年推出的熱門機型做比較測試？ B：那款機型已經成為業界電池續航力的【基準】，所以我們必須向顧客證明我們的產品充一次電能用得更久。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to make a firm decision to do something","c":"下定決心","s":"A: Do you have any special goals for the new year now that the busy season at the office is finally over? B: Every January I resolve to exercise more and eat healthier food, but this year I have also joined a cooking class with two coworkers so that I will not give up after a few weeks.","t":"A：辦公室的旺季終於結束了，你新的一年有什麼特別的目標嗎？ B：每年一月我都會【下定決心】多運動、吃得更健康，不過今年我還和兩位同事一起報名了烹飪課，這樣才不會過幾週就放棄。"},{"w":"perseverance","p":"n.","d":"continuing to try hard for a long time even when things are difficult","c":"毅力；堅持不懈","s":"A: How did your colleague Ken pass the difficult Japanese language test after failing it twice in the past two years? B: It took a lot of patience and perseverance, because he studied for an hour every night after work and practiced speaking with Japanese clients whenever he had the chance.","t":"A：你同事阿健過去兩年考了兩次都沒過，這次是怎麼通過那個很難的日語檢定的？ B：靠的是很大的耐心和【毅力】，因為他每天下班後都讀一個小時，而且一有機會就跟日本客戶練習會話。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control yourself and follow rules or a routine","c":"自律；紀律","s":"A: I started working from home last month, but I keep watching videos and wasting time instead of finishing my reports. Any advice? B: Working at home takes a lot of discipline, so try to start at the same time every morning, turn off your phone, and take short breaks only after finishing each task.","t":"A：我上個月開始在家工作，但一直看影片浪費時間，報告都沒寫完。有什麼建議嗎？ B：在家工作需要很強的【自律】，所以試著每天早上同一時間開始，把手機關掉，每完成一項工作再稍微休息一下。"},{"w":"direction","p":"n.","d":"the way something is developing or moving","c":"方向","s":"A: Why did the design firm stop making printed catalogs after working with the same department stores for over twenty years? B: After losing two major clients, the owners decided to move in a new direction and now mainly create websites and online advertising for small businesses.","t":"A：這家設計公司和同樣幾家百貨公司合作了二十多年，為什麼不再做印刷型錄了？ B：在失去兩個大客戶之後，老闆們決定朝新的【方向】發展，現在主要為小型企業製作網站和線上廣告。"},{"w":"fulfillment","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of happiness because you are doing something useful or satisfying","c":"成就感；滿足感","s":"A: Why did Linda leave her well-paid job at the bank to work for a charity that helps older people in the countryside? B: She said she never felt any real fulfillment counting money all day, but now she feels happy and useful every time she helps someone get the care they need.","t":"A：琳達為什麼辭掉銀行的高薪工作，去一個幫助鄉下老人的慈善機構上班？ B：她說整天數錢從來沒讓她感到真正的【成就感】，但現在每次幫助別人得到所需的照顧，她都覺得快樂又有意義。"},{"w":"self-improvement","p":"n.","d":"the process of making yourself better through your own effort","c":"自我提升","s":"A: Why does our company pay for online courses and give staff one free afternoon a month for studying? B: The managers believe that self-improvement makes workers more confident and skilled, and employees who keep learning new things usually stay with the company longer and help their teams solve problems.","t":"A：為什麼公司要幫員工付線上課程的費用，還每個月給一個下午的讀書時間？ B：主管們相信【自我提升】能讓員工更有自信、更有技能，而持續學習新事物的員工通常會在公司待得更久，也能幫團隊解決問題。"}]},{"unit":159,"theme":"Goodbye 道別","cards":[{"w":"departure","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a place or a job","c":"離開；離職；出發","s":"A: Since our regional manager is moving to the Singapore office next month, should we organize a small lunch to thank her for everything she has done for us? B: Yes, her departure will be a big change for the team, so let's book a nice restaurant near the station and invite everyone from sales.","t":"A：既然我們的區域經理下個月要調到新加坡辦公室，我們要不要辦個小午餐，感謝她為我們所做的一切？ B：好啊，她的【離開】對團隊來說會是很大的改變，所以我們在車站附近訂一間好餐廳，邀請業務部所有人吧。"},{"w":"leave","p":"v.","d":"to go away from a place or a person","c":"離開","s":"A: Do you know what time Mr. Chen plans to leave the office today, because the clients from Osaka still want to discuss the new contract with him before they fly home? B: He told me he has a dentist appointment at five, so you should call them now and ask them to come over before four thirty.","t":"A：你知道陳先生今天打算幾點【離開】辦公室嗎？因為來自大阪的客戶在搭機回國前，還想跟他討論新合約。 B：他跟我說他五點要看牙醫，所以你應該現在打電話給他們，請他們四點半前過來。"},{"w":"part","p":"v.","d":"to leave someone; to go away from each other","c":"分開；分別","s":"A: After working together on the hotel project for almost three years, how did you feel when you and your business partner finally decided to go separate ways last spring? B: It was hard to part from someone I trusted so much, but we agreed to stay friends and still meet for coffee whenever he visits Taipei.","t":"A：你和你的事業夥伴在飯店專案上合作了將近三年，去年春天終於決定分道揚鑣時，你有什麼感受？ B：要和一個我如此信任的人【分開】很難，但我們同意繼續當朋友，每次他來台北時我們仍會一起喝咖啡。"},{"w":"separation","p":"n.","d":"the state of being apart from someone","c":"分離；分開","s":"A: Why did the company give the overseas engineers a longer holiday this year, even though the factory in Vietnam is very busy with new orders? B: Many of them suffered from a long separation from their families, so the managers believed a month at home would improve their health and their work.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年給海外工程師更長的假期，即使越南工廠因新訂單非常忙碌？ B：他們很多人承受與家人長期【分離】之苦，所以經理們認為回家一個月能改善他們的健康和工作表現。"},{"w":"final","p":"adj.","d":"last; coming at the end","c":"最後的","s":"A: Is tomorrow really the final day for Ms. Lin at the front desk, or will she still come in next week to train the new receptionist we hired? B: Tomorrow is her last day, so we have ordered a cake and a card that everyone in the lobby can sign before lunch.","t":"A：明天真的是櫃檯林小姐的【最後】一天嗎？還是她下週還會來訓練我們新聘的接待員？ B：明天是她最後一天上班，所以我們訂了蛋糕和卡片，讓大廳的每個人午餐前都能簽名。"},{"w":"miss","p":"v.","d":"to feel sad because someone or something is not with you","c":"想念","s":"A: Now that you have moved to the new branch in Kaohsiung, what part of working at the head office in Taipei do you think about most often? B: I really miss my old team and our Friday lunches together, although the people here are friendly and the view from my new desk is wonderful.","t":"A：既然你已經調到高雄的新分公司，你最常想起在台北總公司工作的哪一部分？ B：我真的很【想念】我以前的團隊和我們每週五的午餐聚會，雖然這裡的人很友善，而且我新座位的景色也很棒。"},{"w":"memories","p":"n.","d":"things that you remember from the past","c":"回憶","s":"A: What are you going to put in the photo album that we are giving to Mr. Huang at his retirement party next Thursday evening? B: We collected pictures from company trips, award ceremonies, and year-end parties, so the album will be full of happy memories from his thirty years with us.","t":"A：下週四晚上黃先生的退休派對上，我們要送他的相簿裡會放些什麼？ B：我們收集了員工旅遊、頒獎典禮和尾牙的照片，所以這本相簿會充滿他在我們公司三十年的快樂【回憶】。"},{"w":"remember","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in your mind; not to forget","c":"記得","s":"A: Before you move back to Canada next week, is there anything you would like the marketing team to do for you as a farewell gift? B: Just remember to send me photos of the new product launch in December, because I worked on that campaign for months and really want to see the results.","t":"A：你下週搬回加拿大之前，有沒有什麼希望行銷團隊為你做的，當作送別禮物？ B：只要【記得】把十二月新產品發表會的照片寄給我就好，因為我為那個活動努力了好幾個月，真的很想看看成果。"},{"w":"cherish","p":"v.","d":"to love and care about something very much","c":"珍惜","s":"A: How did you feel when the interns gave you that handmade card on their last afternoon at the design studio before they returned to university? B: I will always cherish it, because each of them wrote a kind message about what they had learned and how much they enjoyed working with me.","t":"A：實習生在回大學前、在設計工作室的最後一個下午送你那張手作卡片時，你有什麼感受？ B：我會永遠【珍惜】它，因為他們每個人都寫了貼心的話，說明他們學到了什麼，以及多麼喜歡和我一起工作。"},{"w":"sad","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy","c":"難過的；傷心的","s":"A: Why does everyone in the accounting department look so quiet this morning, even though we finished the annual report two days before the deadline? B: They just heard that their supervisor is leaving the company at the end of the month, and they feel sad because she has been a wonderful leader for many years.","t":"A：為什麼會計部的每個人今天早上看起來都這麼安靜，即使我們比截止日提早兩天完成了年度報告？ B：他們剛聽說主管月底要離職，所以感到很【難過】，因為她這些年來一直是很棒的領導者。"},{"w":"emotional","p":"adj.","d":"showing strong feelings","c":"情緒激動的；感人的","s":"A: Did Mr. Park give a long speech at his farewell dinner last night, or did he just thank everyone quickly and sit down? B: He tried to speak for a few minutes, but he became very emotional when he talked about the first customers he met, and several people at our table started crying too.","t":"A：朴先生昨晚的歡送晚宴上有發表很長的演講嗎？還是他只是很快地謝謝大家就坐下了？ B：他試著講了幾分鐘，但談到他遇到的第一批客戶時變得非常【激動】，我們那桌好幾個人也跟著哭了。"},{"w":"tearful","p":"adj.","d":"crying or almost crying","c":"含淚的；哭泣的","s":"A: How was the scene at the airport when the exchange students from Japan said goodbye to their host families after the six-week business English program? B: It was a tearful farewell, because many of the students and parents could not stop crying even after the boarding announcement was made.","t":"A：為期六週的商用英語課程結束後，日本交換學生在機場和接待家庭道別時，現場情況如何？ B：那是一場【含淚的】告別，因為很多學生和家長即使在登機廣播響起後仍止不住哭泣。"},{"w":"hug","p":"n.","d":"the act of holding someone close in your arms","c":"擁抱","s":"A: Was it appropriate to give our Australian supplier a hug at the end of the trade fair, or should I have offered a handshake instead? B: Since you have worked closely with her for five years and she opened her arms first, it was a warm and natural way to say goodbye after such a successful week.","t":"A：商展結束時給我們的澳洲供應商一個【擁抱】恰當嗎？還是我應該改成握手？ B：既然你和她密切合作了五年，而且是她先張開雙臂的，在如此成功的一週之後，這是很溫暖又自然的道別方式。"},{"w":"handshake","p":"n.","d":"the act of holding and shaking another person's hand","c":"握手","s":"A: What is the most polite way to end a first meeting with a new client from Germany, especially when we do not know each other well yet? B: A firm handshake and a short thank-you for their time are usually enough, and you can follow up with an email the next morning to confirm the details.","t":"A：和來自德國的新客戶第一次會面結束時，最禮貌的方式是什麼，尤其是我們彼此還不太熟的時候？ B：一個有力的【握手】加上簡短感謝他們撥冗通常就夠了，你可以隔天早上再寄電子郵件確認細節。"},{"w":"wave","p":"v.","d":"to move your hand to say hello or goodbye","c":"揮手","s":"A: Did the tour guide come to the hotel lobby to see our group off when the bus left for the airport early on Sunday morning? B: Yes, she stood outside the entrance and continued to wave at us until the bus turned the corner, which made everyone feel very welcome and appreciated.","t":"A：週日一大早巴士出發前往機場時，導遊有到飯店大廳為我們團送行嗎？ B：有，她站在入口外，一直向我們【揮手】直到巴士轉過街角，讓大家都覺得很受歡迎、很受重視。"},{"w":"wish","p":"v.","d":"to hope that someone will have something good","c":"祝福；祝願","s":"A: What should I write in the card for Daniel, who is leaving our team to start his own coffee business downtown next month? B: You could wish him success with his new shop and mention that we will all come to visit on the opening day with our families and friends.","t":"A：Daniel 下個月要離開我們團隊，在市中心開自己的咖啡店，我該在給他的卡片上寫什麼？ B：你可以【祝】他新店生意成功，並提到我們開幕那天都會帶家人和朋友去捧場。"},{"w":"take care","p":"phr.","d":"a friendly way to say goodbye, meaning look after yourself","c":"保重","s":"A: Is there anything special you want to tell your assistant before you leave for your three-month training course at our London headquarters? B: I gave her a list of tasks for each week, and then I said, \"take care, and call me if anything urgent happens with the Johnson account while I am away.\"","t":"A：你出發前往倫敦總部參加三個月的培訓課程之前，有什麼特別的話要對你的助理說嗎？ B：我給了她一份每週的工作清單，然後說：「【保重】，如果我不在時 Johnson 的案子有任何緊急狀況，打電話給我。」"},{"w":"see you again","p":"phr.","d":"said when you hope to meet someone another time","c":"再見；希望再見到你","s":"A: What did the hotel manager say to the conference guests as they checked out on the last day of the international medical forum? B: She thanked them for choosing the hotel, gave each person a small gift, and said, \"We hope to see you again at next year's forum in this ballroom.\"","t":"A：國際醫學論壇最後一天，與會來賓退房時，飯店經理對他們說了什麼？ B：她感謝他們選擇這家飯店，送每個人一份小禮物，並說：「希望明年的論壇能在這個宴會廳【再見到你們】。」"},{"w":"until we meet again","p":"phr.","d":"said as goodbye when you hope to meet later","c":"後會有期","s":"A: How did the CEO end her speech at the closing ceremony for the branch office that is shutting down after twenty years in the city? B: She thanked every employee for their hard work and loyalty, raised her glass of champagne, and said, \"until we meet again, please stay in touch and look after one another.\"","t":"A：在市區營運二十年後即將關閉的分公司結業典禮上，執行長如何結束她的演講？ B：她感謝每位員工的辛勤付出與忠誠，舉起香檳杯說：「【後會有期】，請保持聯絡，互相照顧。」"},{"w":"future","p":"n.","d":"the time that will come","c":"未來；前途","s":"A: What did you tell the young engineer who is leaving us to study for a master's degree in Germany this autumn? B: I told him that he has a bright future ahead of him, and that our company would be happy to hire him again after he finishes his studies.","t":"A：今年秋天要離開我們去德國攻讀碩士的年輕工程師，你對他說了什麼？ B：我告訴他，他前面有光明的【未來】，而且他完成學業後，我們公司很樂意再次聘用他。"},{"w":"journey","p":"n.","d":"a trip from one place to another","c":"旅程","s":"A: How long will it take Ms. Wu to travel from Taipei to her new position at the branch office in Toronto next Monday? B: The journey takes about fifteen hours with one stop in Vancouver, so we packed some snacks and a travel pillow in her farewell gift bag.","t":"A：吳小姐下週一從台北前往多倫多分公司就任新職，要花多久時間？ B：這趟【旅程】大約要十五個小時，中途在溫哥華停一站，所以我們在她的送別禮袋裡放了一些零食和旅行枕。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be thankful for something","c":"感激；感謝","s":"A: Why did the retiring chef stay late after his last shift to shake hands with every kitchen worker and waiter in the restaurant? B: He said, \"I really appreciate all your hard work over the years,\" and he told them that the restaurant's success belonged to all of them, not just to him.","t":"A：為什麼那位即將退休的主廚在最後一班後留到很晚，和餐廳裡每位廚房員工和服務生握手？ B：他說：「我真的很【感激】你們這些年的辛勤工作。」還告訴他們餐廳的成功屬於所有人，不只是他一個人。"},{"w":"gratitude","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being thankful","c":"感激；感謝之意","s":"A: What gift did the sales team decide to give their manager when she announced that she was retiring after twenty-five years with the company? B: They bought her a beautiful watch with a short message on the back to express their gratitude for her patience, advice, and support.","t":"A：經理宣布在公司服務二十五年後要退休時，業務團隊決定送她什麼禮物？ B：他們買了一支漂亮的手錶，背面刻著簡短訊息，表達他們對她的耐心、建議和支持的【感謝】。"},{"w":"friendship","p":"n.","d":"a relationship between friends","c":"友誼","s":"A: Even though you are moving to a competitor in Hong Kong next month, will you still keep in contact with the people in our department? B: Of course, our friendship is more important than any job, and I have already invited everyone to visit me and try the dim sum near my new apartment.","t":"A：雖然你下個月要跳槽到香港的競爭對手公司，你還會和我們部門的人保持聯絡嗎？ B：當然，我們的【友誼】比任何工作都重要，我已經邀請大家來找我，嚐嚐我新公寓附近的港式點心。"},{"w":"support","p":"n.","d":"help and encouragement","c":"支持；支援","s":"A: Why did Kevin thank the IT team so warmly in his goodbye email before he left for his new job in Singapore? B: Their support helped him finish the difficult system upgrade last year, and he said he could never have succeeded without their help late at night.","t":"A：Kevin 離職去新加坡就任新工作前，為什麼在他的告別郵件裡如此熱情地感謝資訊團隊？ B：他們的【支持】幫助他完成了去年那次困難的系統升級，他說如果沒有他們深夜的協助，他絕對不可能成功。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give someone confidence","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: How did the new graduate feel about leaving the internship program at the bank after six busy months in the customer service department? B: She was a little sad, but her mentor's encouragement gave her the confidence to apply for a full-time position at a larger bank in the city.","t":"A：這位新畢業生在銀行客服部忙了六個月後，對於離開實習計畫有什麼感受？ B：她有點難過，但她導師的【鼓勵】給了她信心，去申請市區一家更大銀行的全職職位。"},{"w":"respect","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of admiring someone for their good qualities","c":"尊敬；敬重","s":"A: Why did so many former employees come back to attend the farewell party for the factory director on Saturday afternoon? B: They had great respect for him because he always treated workers fairly, listened to their ideas, and made safety the top priority in every department.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多前員工週六下午回來參加廠長的歡送會？ B：他們非常【尊敬】他，因為他總是公平對待員工、傾聽他們的想法，而且在每個部門都把安全放在第一位。"},{"w":"kindness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being friendly, caring and helpful","c":"親切；好意","s":"A: What did the guest from Brazil write in the hotel's comment book before she checked out and took a taxi to the airport? B: She thanked the staff for their kindness during her stay, especially the receptionist who helped her find a pharmacy late at night when she felt sick.","t":"A：那位巴西房客退房搭計程車去機場前，在飯店的留言簿上寫了什麼？ B：她感謝員工在她住宿期間的【親切友善】，特別是那位在她深夜身體不適時幫她找藥局的接待員。"},{"w":"grateful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling thankful","c":"感激的","s":"A: How did you feel when your coworkers organized a surprise farewell lunch for you on your last day at the travel agency? B: I was really grateful, because I did not expect anything special, and they even prepared a slideshow of all the trips we planned together.","t":"A：你在旅行社上班最後一天，同事為你辦了一場驚喜歡送午餐時，你有什麼感受？ B：我真的很【感激】，因為我沒預期會有什麼特別安排，他們甚至準備了我們一起規劃過的所有旅程的投影片。"},{"w":"hopeful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that something good will happen","c":"抱有希望的","s":"A: Do you think the director will return to our company after she finishes her two-year project with the government in the capital? B: I am hopeful that she will, because she said at her farewell dinner that she would miss us and wanted to work with this team again someday.","t":"A：你認為主任在首都完成她兩年的政府專案後，會回到我們公司嗎？ B：我【抱持希望】她會回來，因為她在歡送晚宴上說她會想念我們，並希望有一天能再和這個團隊合作。"},{"w":"bittersweet","p":"adj.","d":"happy and sad at the same time","c":"苦樂參半的","s":"A: How do you feel about leaving the small company where you started your career, now that you have accepted that excellent job offer from a large bank? B: It is a bittersweet moment for me, because I am excited about the new challenge, but I will be sad to leave such a caring team.","t":"A：既然你已經接受了一家大銀行的優渥職缺，要離開你開始職涯的這家小公司，你有什麼感受？ B：對我來說這是【苦樂參半】的時刻，因為我對新挑戰感到興奮，但要離開這麼有愛心的團隊也會很難過。"},{"w":"all the best","p":"phr.","d":"used to wish someone good luck","c":"祝一切順利","s":"A: What did you write in the farewell card for the receptionist who is leaving next Friday to work at a five-star hotel in Tokyo? B: I wrote, \"all the best in your new job, and thank you for always greeting our visitors with such a warm and friendly smile.\"","t":"A：櫃檯接待員下週五要離職去東京一家五星級飯店工作，你在給她的送別卡上寫了什麼？ B：我寫了：「祝你新工作【一切順利】，也謝謝你總是用溫暖友善的笑容迎接我們的訪客。」"},{"w":"safe travels","p":"phr.","d":"used to wish someone a safe trip","c":"一路平安","s":"A: What did the receptionist say to the sales team as they left the office for the airport on their way to the trade show in Las Vegas? B: She handed them their printed boarding passes, reminded them to check the weather, and said, \"safe travels, and good luck with the new customers!\"","t":"A：業務團隊離開辦公室前往機場、要去拉斯維加斯參加商展時，接待員對他們說了什麼？ B：她把印好的登機證交給他們，提醒他們查看天氣，並說：「【一路平安】，祝你們開發新客戶順利！」"}]},{"unit":160,"theme":"Government 政府","cards":[{"w":"authority","p":"n.","d":"the power or right to make decisions or give orders","c":"權力；權限；當局","s":"A: Can the shop manager approve a refund of more than five hundred dollars for a customer whose laptop stopped working after only two weeks? B: No, she doesn't have the authority to do that, so she will need to call the regional director at the head office and wait for his written approval.","t":"A：店經理能為一位筆電才用兩週就壞掉的顧客核准超過五百美元的退款嗎？ B：不行，她沒有那樣做的【權限】，所以她得打電話給總公司的區域主管，並等他的書面核准。"},{"w":"administration","p":"n.","d":"the people who manage a government or organization; the work of managing","c":"行政；管理；政府（當局）","s":"A: Why did the city's plans for a new subway line suddenly change after last year's election, even though construction companies had already started preparing the site? B: The new administration decided to spend the money on bus routes instead, because the mayor believes buses can serve more neighborhoods at a lower cost.","t":"A：為什麼市府新地鐵線的計畫在去年選舉之後突然改變了，即使營造公司已經開始整地？ B：新的【市府團隊】決定把錢改用在公車路線上，因為市長認為公車能以較低成本服務更多社區。"},{"w":"policy","p":"n.","d":"a plan or set of rules that an organization or government follows","c":"政策；方針","s":"A: Are employees allowed to work from home on Fridays now, or do we still have to come into the office every day of the week? B: Yes, the company changed its policy last month, so staff can work from home on Fridays as long as their manager agrees and they answer emails quickly.","t":"A：員工現在週五可以在家工作了嗎？還是我們仍然得每天進辦公室？ B：可以，公司上個月改了【政策】，所以只要主管同意而且能迅速回覆電子郵件，員工週五就能在家工作。"},{"w":"legislation","p":"n.","d":"laws, or the process of making laws","c":"立法；法規","s":"A: Why is the restaurant suddenly replacing all of its plastic straws and boxes with paper ones, even though the paper ones cost almost twice as much? B: New legislation passed by the government last spring bans single-use plastic in restaurants starting next month, and owners who ignore it will have to pay a large fine.","t":"A：為什麼這家餐廳突然把所有塑膠吸管和餐盒換成紙製的，即使紙製品的成本幾乎是兩倍？ B：政府去年春天通過的新【法規】從下個月起禁止餐廳使用一次性塑膠，忽視規定的業者將被處以高額罰款。"},{"w":"law","p":"n.","d":"a rule made by the government that everyone must follow","c":"法律","s":"A: Do I really need to give my new part-time workers a written contract, or is a simple agreement by phone good enough for a small café like mine? B: You must give them a written contract, because the law requires every employer to explain wages, working hours, and holidays clearly before the staff start working.","t":"A：我真的需要給新的兼職員工書面合約嗎？還是像我這樣的小咖啡店用電話口頭約定就夠了？ B：你一定要給他們書面合約，因為【法律】規定每位雇主在員工開始上班前都必須清楚說明薪資、工時和假期。"},{"w":"regulation","p":"n.","d":"an official rule that controls how something is done","c":"規定；法規；管制","s":"A: Why can't we bring the new cleaning products from the overseas supplier into the factory right away, since they are cheaper and work much better? B: Unfortunately, a new regulation says that every chemical product must be tested by the health department before it is used in a workplace, so we have to wait until the lab results arrive next week.","t":"A：為什麼我們不能馬上把海外供應商的新清潔用品帶進工廠？它們比較便宜，效果也好得多。 B：很可惜，一項新【規定】要求每種化學產品在用於工作場所前都必須經過衛生部門檢驗，所以我們得等到下週檢驗結果出來。"},{"w":"democracy","p":"n.","d":"a system in which people choose their government by voting; equal say for everyone","c":"民主；民主制度","s":"A: Why did your manager let the whole team vote on which city we should visit for this year's company trip instead of simply choosing one himself? B: He believes in democracy at work, so he wants everyone to share their opinions and have an equal chance to decide things that affect the whole department.","t":"A：為什麼你的經理讓全隊投票決定今年員工旅遊要去哪個城市，而不是自己直接選一個？ B：他相信職場上的【民主】，所以希望每個人都能分享意見，並有平等的機會決定影響整個部門的事。"},{"w":"election","p":"n.","d":"an event in which people vote to choose someone for an official position","c":"選舉","s":"A: Why are there so many posters and flags with smiling faces along the main road near our office building this month? B: The city will hold an election for a new mayor on the first Saturday of December, so all the candidates are trying hard to attract voters before the big day.","t":"A：為什麼這個月我們辦公大樓附近的大馬路上有這麼多掛著笑臉的海報和旗子？ B：本市將在十二月的第一個星期六舉行新市長的【選舉】，所以所有候選人都在大日子前努力爭取選民。"},{"w":"parliament","p":"n.","d":"the group of elected people who make the laws of a country","c":"國會；議會","s":"A: When will the new rule that gives fathers four weeks of paid leave after the birth of a baby actually start in this country? B: The parliament still has to vote on it next month, and if most members agree, the new leave rule could begin at the start of next year.","t":"A：讓父親在孩子出生後享有四週帶薪假的新規定，在這個國家什麼時候會真正開始實施？ B：【國會】下個月還必須對它進行表決，如果多數議員同意，新的休假規定可能在明年初開始。"},{"w":"congress","p":"n.","d":"the group of people elected to make laws, especially in the US; a large formal meeting","c":"國會（尤指美國）；代表大會","s":"A: Is our company worried about the new plan to raise taxes on imported electronics, since most of the parts in our phones come from overseas? B: Yes, very worried, but the plan will only become official if congress approves it, so our managers are watching the news from Washington closely every day.","t":"A：我們公司擔心提高進口電子產品稅的新計畫嗎？畢竟我們手機裡大部分零件都來自海外。 B：是的，非常擔心，但這項計畫只有在【國會】通過後才會正式生效，所以我們的經理們每天都密切關注華盛頓的新聞。"},{"w":"constitution","p":"n.","d":"the set of basic laws and principles of a country","c":"憲法","s":"A: Why can't the government simply stop the newspaper from printing articles that criticize the president and his ministers? B: The constitution protects freedom of speech for every citizen, so even powerful leaders cannot close a newspaper just because they don't like what reporters write about them.","t":"A：為什麼政府不能直接阻止報紙刊登批評總統和部長們的文章？ B：【憲法】保障每位公民的言論自由，所以即使是有權勢的領導人，也不能只因為不喜歡記者寫的內容就關閉報社。"},{"w":"bureaucracy","p":"n.","d":"a system with many complicated rules and steps that make things slow","c":"官僚作風；官僚體制","s":"A: Why did it take you almost three months to get the license for your new bakery when the city website says it only takes two weeks? B: There was so much bureaucracy: I had to fill out seven different forms, visit four separate offices, and wait for each department to stamp my papers.","t":"A：為什麼你的新麵包店拿到執照花了將近三個月，市政府網站上說只要兩週？ B：【官僚程序】實在太多了：我得填七份不同的表格、跑四個不同的辦公室，還要等每個部門在我的文件上蓋章。"},{"w":"public sector","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of the economy run by the government, such as public schools and hospitals","c":"公部門","s":"A: Why did your sister leave her well-paid job at the bank to work as an accountant for the city hospital instead? B: She wanted a more stable career in the public sector, because government jobs usually offer better health insurance, a good pension, and fewer late nights at the office.","t":"A：為什麼你姊姊辭掉銀行的高薪工作，改去市立醫院當會計？ B：她想在【公部門】有更穩定的職涯，因為政府的工作通常提供較好的健康保險、不錯的退休金，也比較少在辦公室加班到深夜。"},{"w":"civil service","p":"n.phr.","d":"all the government departments and the people who work in them","c":"公務員體系；文官制度","s":"A: How did your cousin get a job at the tax office right after university, since everyone says those positions are very hard to get? B: She studied for almost a year to pass the national civil service exam, which tests thousands of applicants every summer on law, math, and writing.","t":"A：你表妹大學一畢業怎麼就進了稅務局？大家都說那些職位很難拿到。 B：她準備了將近一年才通過全國【公務員】考試，這項考試每年夏天都會考數千名考生的法律、數學和寫作。"},{"w":"governance","p":"n.","d":"the way a country or organization is controlled and managed","c":"治理；管理","s":"A: Why did the investors insist on adding two outside experts to the company's board of directors before they agreed to put more money into the business? B: They wanted better governance, because the board had made several poor decisions last year without checking the numbers or asking anyone outside the family for advice.","t":"A：為什麼投資人堅持在公司董事會加入兩位外部專家，才同意對公司增資？ B：他們希望有更好的【治理】，因為董事會去年在沒有核對數字、也沒有詢問家族以外任何人意見的情況下，做了幾個糟糕的決定。"},{"w":"sovereignty","p":"n.","d":"a country's complete power to rule itself","c":"主權","s":"A: Why did the island's leaders refuse the offer from a large neighboring country to build and control a new port on their coast? B: They worried about losing sovereignty, because letting a foreign government manage such an important place could give it too much control over their trade and their decisions.","t":"A：為什麼那座島的領導人拒絕了鄰近大國提出在他們海岸興建並掌控新港口的提議？ B：他們擔心喪失【主權】，因為讓外國政府管理這麼重要的地方，可能使對方對他們的貿易和決策有太大的掌控力。"},{"w":"diplomacy","p":"n.","d":"managing relations between countries; skill in dealing with people politely","c":"外交；交際手腕","s":"A: How did our sales manager manage to keep the angry customer from canceling his large order after the shipment arrived three weeks late? B: She used a lot of diplomacy: she apologized calmly, listened to all his complaints, and then offered free delivery on his next order to rebuild his trust.","t":"A：我們的業務經理是怎麼讓那位生氣的客戶在貨晚到三週後沒有取消大訂單的？ B：她運用了很多【交際手腕】：她冷靜地道歉、聽完他所有抱怨，然後提供下一筆訂單免運費來重建他的信任。"},{"w":"minister","p":"n.","d":"a senior member of government who is in charge of a department","c":"部長；大臣","s":"A: Who is going to open the new international trade fair at the convention center on Monday morning? B: The minister of economic affairs will give a short speech at nine o'clock, and then she will visit several booths to meet local companies that export machines to Asia.","t":"A：週一早上誰會在會展中心為新的國際貿易展開幕？ B：經濟部【部長】九點會發表簡短演說，然後她會參觀幾個攤位，與出口機械到亞洲的本地公司見面。"},{"w":"cabinet","p":"n.","d":"the group of senior ministers who make important government decisions","c":"內閣","s":"A: Why did the evening news say that the president had a long meeting with all of her top ministers late last night? B: The cabinet met to discuss how to help families pay their rising electricity bills, and they finally agreed on a plan to give small payments to low-income homes this winter.","t":"A：為什麼晚間新聞說總統昨晚深夜和她所有的高層部長開了很長的會？ B：【內閣】開會討論如何幫助家庭支付不斷上漲的電費，最後他們同意了一項計畫，今年冬天將提供小額補助給低收入家庭。"},{"w":"president","p":"n.","d":"the leader of a country without a king or queen; the head of a company or organization","c":"總統；總裁","s":"A: Why is everyone in the sales department wearing suits today instead of their usual casual clothes? B: The company's president is flying in from Singapore this afternoon to visit our branch, and he wants to meet each team to hear about our results for the last quarter.","t":"A：為什麼業務部今天每個人都穿西裝，而不是平常的休閒服？ B：公司的【總裁】今天下午從新加坡飛過來視察我們分公司，他想和每個團隊見面，聽取我們上一季的業績。"},{"w":"prime minister","p":"n.phr.","d":"the leader of the government in some countries","c":"總理；首相","s":"A: Why are the roads around city hall closed, and why are there so many police officers standing on every corner this morning? B: The British prime minister is visiting today to sign a trade agreement with our leaders, so the police have closed several streets for safety until the ceremony ends at noon.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上市政府周邊的道路都封閉了，而且每個轉角都站著這麼多警察？ B：英國【首相】今天來訪，要和我們的領導人簽署貿易協定，所以警方為了安全封閉了幾條街道，直到中午典禮結束。"},{"w":"taxation","p":"n.","d":"the system of collecting taxes","c":"稅制；課稅","s":"A: Why did the software company decide to open its new regional office in Ireland instead of in one of the bigger European cities? B: The level of taxation there is much lower for technology firms, so the company can save millions of dollars every year and use the money to hire more engineers.","t":"A：為什麼那家軟體公司決定把新的區域辦公室設在愛爾蘭，而不是歐洲其他較大的城市？ B：那裡對科技公司的【課稅】程度低很多，所以公司每年能省下數百萬美元，並用這筆錢聘請更多工程師。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money available for something and a plan for how to spend it","c":"預算","s":"A: Can we hire a famous singer to perform at the company's year-end party, since everyone worked so hard this year? B: I'm afraid not, because our budget for the party is only twenty thousand dollars, and that has to cover the hotel ballroom, the food, the drinks, and the prizes.","t":"A：既然大家今年都這麼努力，我們可以請知名歌手在公司尾牙表演嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為我們尾牙的【預算】只有兩萬美元，而且要支付飯店宴會廳、食物、飲料和獎品。"},{"w":"welfare","p":"n.","d":"the health and happiness of people; help, especially money, given to people in need","c":"福利；福祉","s":"A: Why did the factory owner build a small gym and hire a nurse for the workers, even though business has been slow this year? B: He really cares about the welfare of his employees, and he believes healthy, happy workers make fewer mistakes and are less likely to leave for other jobs.","t":"A：為什麼工廠老闆即使今年生意不好，還為員工蓋了小健身房並聘請護士？ B：他非常關心員工的【福祉】，而且他相信健康快樂的員工比較少犯錯，也比較不會跳槽。"},{"w":"reform","p":"n.","d":"a change made to improve a system, law, or organization","c":"改革","s":"A: Why do students in this country now spend less time memorizing facts and more time working on group projects in their classrooms? B: The education reform that started three years ago changed the national curriculum, because the government wanted young people to learn teamwork, creative thinking, and problem-solving skills.","t":"A：為什麼這個國家的學生現在在課堂上花比較少時間背誦知識，而花更多時間做小組專題？ B：三年前開始的教育【改革】改變了全國課綱，因為政府希望年輕人學會團隊合作、創意思考和解決問題的能力。"},{"w":"transparency","p":"n.","d":"being open and honest so people can see how decisions are made","c":"透明度","s":"A: Why does the new manager post the whole department's spending on the shared online board at the end of each month? B: She believes in transparency, so she wants every staff member to see exactly where the money goes and to ask questions if any of the costs seem too high.","t":"A：為什麼新經理每個月底都把整個部門的支出公布在共用的線上看板上？ B：她重視【透明度】，所以希望每位員工都能清楚看到錢花在哪裡，若有任何費用看起來太高也可以提出疑問。"},{"w":"accountability","p":"n.","d":"being responsible for your actions and ready to explain them","c":"問責；當責","s":"A: Why did the director ask each project leader to send her a short weekly report about their progress, costs, and problems? B: She wants more accountability in the team, because last year several projects went over budget and nobody could explain who had made the costly decisions.","t":"A：為什麼主任要求每位專案負責人每週寄給她一份關於進度、成本和問題的簡短報告？ B：她希望團隊有更多【當責】，因為去年有好幾個專案超出預算，卻沒有人能說明是誰做了那些代價高昂的決定。"},{"w":"corruption","p":"n.","d":"dishonest or illegal behavior by people in power, such as taking secret money","c":"貪汙；腐敗","s":"A: Why were two officials from the city's building department arrested by the police at their homes early yesterday morning? B: They were charged with corruption, because investigators found that they had secretly accepted money from a construction company in exchange for approving unsafe buildings.","t":"A：為什麼市府建管處的兩名官員昨天一大早在家中被警方逮捕？ B：他們被控【貪汙】，因為調查人員發現他們私下收受營造公司的錢，以換取核准不安全的建築。"},{"w":"justice","p":"n.","d":"fair treatment of people; the system of law and courts","c":"正義；公道；司法","s":"A: Why did the workers keep complaining to the labor office after the factory closed suddenly without paying their final month of wages? B: They wanted justice, and after six months the court finally ordered the owner to pay everyone the money they had earned plus extra for the trouble he caused.","t":"A：為什麼工廠突然關閉且沒付最後一個月薪水後，工人們一直向勞工局申訴？ B：他們想要討回【公道】，六個月後法院終於命令老闆付給大家應得的薪水，並額外賠償他造成的麻煩。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"protection from danger, crime, or attack","c":"安全；保全；安全措施","s":"A: Why do we suddenly need to show our staff ID cards at the front gate and sign in every visitor at the reception desk? B: The company has improved security after someone stole three laptops from the meeting room last month, so now every person entering the building must be checked.","t":"A：為什麼我們突然需要在大門出示員工證，而且每位訪客都要在櫃檯登記？ B：上個月有人從會議室偷走三台筆電後，公司加強了【保全措施】，所以現在每個進入大樓的人都必須接受檢查。"},{"w":"foreign policy","p":"n.phr.","d":"a government's plans for dealing with other countries","c":"外交政策","s":"A: Why did the new government suddenly decide to open embassies in five African countries during its first year in power? B: Its foreign policy focuses on building stronger trade ties with developing nations, so leaders hope the new embassies will help local companies find customers and partners there.","t":"A：為什麼新政府執政第一年就突然決定在五個非洲國家設立大使館？ B：它的【外交政策】著重於和開發中國家建立更緊密的貿易關係，所以領導人希望新使館能幫助本國企業在那裡找到客戶和合作夥伴。"},{"w":"public opinion","p":"n.phr.","d":"what most people in a society think about something","c":"輿論；民意","s":"A: Why did the city cancel its plan to cut down the old trees in the park to build a new parking lot near the train station? B: The mayor changed her mind because public opinion was strongly against it: thousands of residents signed a petition and joined protests saying the park was more important than extra parking spaces.","t":"A：為什麼市府取消了砍掉公園老樹、在火車站附近蓋新停車場的計畫？ B：市長改變了主意，因為【輿論】強烈反對：數千名居民連署請願並參加抗議，表示公園比多出的停車位更重要。"},{"w":"censorship","p":"n.","d":"removing or banning parts of books, films, news, etc. that are seen as unacceptable","c":"審查制度；言論審查","s":"A: Why can't people in some countries watch certain foreign movies or read popular news websites from overseas on their phones? B: Their governments use strict censorship to block information they don't like, so many films are cut or banned and some websites cannot be opened at all.","t":"A：為什麼有些國家的人無法用手機觀看某些外國電影或瀏覽熱門的海外新聞網站？ B：他們的政府實施嚴格的【審查制度】來封鎖不喜歡的資訊，所以很多電影被刪剪或禁播，有些網站則完全打不開。"},{"w":"legitimacy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being fair, legal, and accepted by people","c":"合法性；正當性","s":"A: Why did the small online store ask a well-known bank to check its payment system and put the bank's logo on its checkout page? B: The owners wanted to show the legitimacy of their business, because many new customers were afraid the site might be a scam and refused to enter their card details.","t":"A：為什麼那家小型網路商店請一家知名銀行檢查付款系統，並在結帳頁面放上銀行的標誌？ B：店主想證明他們生意的【正當性】，因為很多新客戶擔心這個網站可能是詐騙，不願輸入信用卡資料。"}]},{"unit":161,"theme":"Grandparents 祖父母","cards":[{"w":"grandfather","p":"n.","d":"the father of your father or mother","c":"祖父；外祖父","s":"A: Why did Mr. Lin take three days off work last week when the busy season had just started at the factory? B: His grandfather turned ninety, so the whole family traveled to the countryside to hold a big birthday dinner for the old man and his many friends from the village.","t":"A：為什麼林先生在工廠旺季剛開始的上週請了三天假？ B：他的【祖父】滿九十歲了，所以全家人前往鄉下，為這位老人和他村裡的許多朋友舉辦一場盛大的生日晚宴。"},{"w":"grandmother","p":"n.","d":"the mother of your father or mother","c":"祖母；外祖母","s":"A: Who taught you to make such delicious dumplings that everyone in the office asked for the recipe after the company party? B: My grandmother showed me when I was a child, and she still calls me every Sunday to check whether I am cooking healthy meals for myself in the city.","t":"A：是誰教你包出這麼好吃的水餃，讓辦公室每個人在公司派對後都來要食譜？ B：是我【祖母】在我小時候教我的，而且她到現在每個星期天還會打電話來，確認我在城市裡有沒有為自己煮健康的餐點。"},{"w":"elderly","p":"adj.","d":"old; past middle age","c":"年長的；上了年紀的","s":"A: Why is the bank opening a special service counter on the first floor near the main entrance next month? B: Many elderly customers have trouble using the machines and climbing the stairs, so the manager wants staff to help them with their accounts in a quiet and comfortable area.","t":"A：為什麼銀行下個月要在一樓靠近大門的地方開設特別服務櫃檯？ B：許多【年長的】顧客在使用機器和爬樓梯方面有困難，所以經理希望員工能在一個安靜舒適的區域協助他們處理帳戶。"},{"w":"retired","p":"adj.","d":"no longer working because of age","c":"退休的","s":"A: Who is the gentleman giving advice to our new engineers in the meeting room every Wednesday afternoon this month? B: He is a retired manager who worked here for thirty-five years, and he agreed to come back as a volunteer because he enjoys sharing what he learned with young people.","t":"A：這個月每週三下午在會議室給新進工程師建議的那位先生是誰？ B：他是一位在這裡工作了三十五年的【退休】經理，他答應以志工身分回來，因為他喜歡和年輕人分享他學到的東西。"},{"w":"wisdom","p":"n.","d":"good judgment that comes from knowledge and life experience","c":"智慧","s":"A: Why does the young director often visit her grandparents before she makes important decisions about the company's future plans? B: She believes their wisdom comes from many years of hard work and difficult times, so their simple advice often helps her see problems more clearly and calmly.","t":"A：為什麼那位年輕的總監在對公司未來計畫做重要決定前，常去拜訪她的祖父母？ B：她相信他們的【智慧】來自多年的辛勤工作和艱難時光，所以他們簡單的建議常幫助她更清楚、更冷靜地看待問題。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or skill you get from doing something for a long time","c":"經驗；經歷","s":"A: Why did the hotel hire an older woman to train the new reception staff instead of someone from a big training company? B: She has over forty years of experience in serving guests, and she knows exactly how to handle angry customers, lost bags, and late check-ins without losing her temper.","t":"A：為什麼飯店雇用一位年長女士來訓練新的櫃檯人員，而不是找大型培訓公司的人？ B：她有超過四十年服務客人的【經驗】，而且她非常清楚如何處理生氣的顧客、遺失的行李和晚到的入住，而不發脾氣。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom or belief passed down over many years","c":"傳統；慣例","s":"A: Why does your family always gather at your grandparents' house on the first night of the Lunar New Year, even when the trains are crowded? B: It is a family tradition that started long before I was born, and everyone feels that the holiday would not be complete without that big dinner together.","t":"A：為什麼你們家即使火車很擠，農曆新年第一晚也總是在祖父母家團聚？ B：這是一個在我出生前很久就開始的家族【傳統】，而且大家都覺得少了那頓團圓大餐，這個節日就不完整。"},{"w":"heritage","p":"n.","d":"the history, buildings, and customs passed down from the past","c":"（文化）遺產；傳承","s":"A: Why is the city council spending money to repair the old wooden houses near the river instead of building new apartments there? B: Those houses are part of our local heritage, and many older residents want their grandchildren to see how people lived and worked in this area a century ago.","t":"A：為什麼市議會要花錢修繕河邊的老木屋，而不是在那裡蓋新公寓？ B：那些房子是我們在地【文化遺產】的一部分，而且許多年長居民希望他們的孫子女能看到一百年前人們在這個地區如何生活和工作。"},{"w":"caregiver","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks after someone who is old or sick","c":"照顧者；看護","s":"A: How does Ms. Chen manage to work full-time while her grandmother needs help with meals and medicine every day? B: The family hired a professional caregiver who visits the house each morning, prepares lunch, and makes sure her grandmother takes her pills on time while Ms. Chen is at the office.","t":"A：陳小姐的祖母每天需要有人幫忙用餐和吃藥，她是怎麼同時兼顧全職工作的？ B：家人請了一位專業的【照顧者】，每天早上到家裡準備午餐，並在陳小姐上班時確保她祖母按時吃藥。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help and encouragement","c":"支持的；給予幫助的","s":"A: How did you find the courage to quit your stable job at the bank and open your own small bakery downtown? B: My grandparents were very supportive from the beginning, and they even lent me some of their savings and helped me design the menu during the first difficult months.","t":"A：你是怎麼鼓起勇氣辭掉銀行的穩定工作，在市中心開自己的小麵包店？ B：我的祖父母從一開始就非常【支持】我，他們甚至借我一些積蓄，並在最初艱難的幾個月幫我設計菜單。"},{"w":"affection","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of liking and caring for someone","c":"喜愛；關愛","s":"A: Why do so many children at the community center run to hug the old man who comes to read stories every Saturday morning? B: He treats them with real affection, always remembers their names and birthdays, and brings small snacks for those who come without breakfast.","t":"A：為什麼社區中心有那麼多孩子會跑去擁抱每週六早上來讀故事的那位老先生？ B：他以真誠的【關愛】對待他們，總是記得他們的名字和生日，還會帶小點心給沒吃早餐就來的孩子。"},{"w":"nurture","p":"v.","d":"to help someone or something grow and develop","c":"培育；養育","s":"A: Why does your company encourage older employees to work closely with the new graduates during their first year? B: Management believes experienced staff can nurture young talent by teaching them patience and good habits, just as grandparents help children grow up with confidence and care.","t":"A：為什麼你們公司鼓勵年長員工在新進畢業生第一年時與他們密切合作？ B：管理層相信有經驗的員工能藉由教導耐心和好習慣來【培育】年輕人才，就像祖父母以信心和關懷幫助孩子成長一樣。"},{"w":"bond","p":"n.","d":"a close feeling that connects people","c":"情感連結；聯繫","s":"A: Why did the travel agency create a special tour package for grandparents and grandchildren this summer? B: The marketing team noticed that many families want to build a stronger bond between generations, and a week of fishing, hiking, and cooking together gives them that chance.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社今年夏天推出祖父母和孫子女專屬的旅遊套裝行程？ B：行銷團隊注意到許多家庭希望在世代之間建立更緊密的【情感連結】，而一週一起釣魚、健行和烹飪正好給了他們這個機會。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about what to do","c":"指導；引導","s":"A: How did you decide which university program to apply for when your parents were both busy working overseas? B: I lived with my grandfather during high school, and his calm guidance helped me compare different courses and choose one that matched my interests and future career goals.","t":"A：你父母都忙著在海外工作時，你是怎麼決定要申請哪個大學科系的？ B：我高中時和祖父住在一起，他冷靜的【指導】幫助我比較不同的課程，並選了一個符合我興趣和未來職涯目標的科系。"},{"w":"storytelling","p":"n.","d":"the activity of telling stories","c":"說故事","s":"A: Why is the public library inviting senior citizens from the neighborhood to visit every Sunday afternoon? B: They are hosting a storytelling event where older residents share tales about the town's past with children, and the librarians hope it will make young visitors more interested in local history.","t":"A：為什麼公立圖書館邀請鄰近的長者每週日下午來訪？ B：他們舉辦一場【說故事】活動，讓年長居民和孩子們分享鎮上過往的故事，館員們希望這能讓年輕的訪客對地方歷史更有興趣。"},{"w":"memories","p":"n.","d":"things you remember from the past","c":"回憶；記憶","s":"A: Why did your grandmother keep that old photo album on the shelf even after the family moved to a smaller apartment? B: It is full of happy memories of her wedding, her first job at the post office, and holidays with her children, so she refuses to throw it away.","t":"A：為什麼你祖母在家人搬到較小的公寓後，還把那本舊相簿放在架子上？ B：它充滿了她婚禮、她在郵局的第一份工作，以及和孩子們度假的快樂【回憶】，所以她不肯把它丟掉。"},{"w":"companionship","p":"n.","d":"the pleasant feeling of being with someone","c":"陪伴；友誼","s":"A: Why did the nursing home start a program where office workers visit residents during their lunch breaks? B: Many older people there feel lonely, and the staff found that regular companionship and simple conversation improve their mood more than expensive activities or new equipment.","t":"A：為什麼安養院開始一個讓上班族在午休時間拜訪住民的計畫？ B：那裡許多長者感到孤單，而工作人員發現規律的【陪伴】和簡單的談話比昂貴的活動或新設備更能改善他們的心情。"},{"w":"generation","p":"n.","d":"all the people born and living at about the same time","c":"一代；世代","s":"A: Why does the furniture store use photos of grandparents and young couples in all of its new advertisements? B: The owners want to show that their tables are strong enough to pass from one generation to the next, which is why they offer a fifty-year warranty on every piece.","t":"A：為什麼家具店在所有新廣告中都使用祖父母和年輕夫妻的照片？ B：老闆想展現他們的桌子堅固到能從一【代】傳到下一代，這也是為什麼他們每件家具都提供五十年保固。"},{"w":"ancestor","p":"n.","d":"a family member who lived long ago","c":"祖先","s":"A: Why did your cousin spend so much time at the city archives during her vacation last month? B: She wanted to find out where her ancestor lived before the family moved to Taipei, so she searched old records and maps to learn about the village and the people who once farmed there.","t":"A：為什麼你表姊上個月放假期間花那麼多時間待在市立檔案館？ B：她想查出她的【祖先】在家族搬到台北之前住在哪裡，所以她查閱舊紀錄和地圖，了解那個村莊和曾經在那裡務農的人們。"},{"w":"respect","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that someone is good or important","c":"尊敬；尊重","s":"A: Why do the younger staff members always stand up and greet Mr. Wang when he enters the office in the morning? B: They show him great respect because he founded the company forty years ago and still remembers every employee's name, even though he only comes in twice a week now.","t":"A：為什麼年輕員工在王先生早上進辦公室時總會站起來打招呼？ B：他們對他表現出極大的【尊敬】，因為他在四十年前創立了公司，而且即使他現在每週只來兩次，仍記得每位員工的名字。"},{"w":"patience","p":"n.","d":"the ability to wait or stay calm without getting angry","c":"耐心","s":"A: How did your grandfather manage to teach you how to repair bicycles when you kept making the same mistakes as a child? B: He had endless patience, and he would calmly explain each step again while we sat together in the garage on weekend afternoons, never raising his voice even once.","t":"A：你小時候一直犯同樣的錯，你祖父是怎麼教會你修腳踏車的？ B：他有無比的【耐心】，週末下午我們一起坐在車庫時，他總是冷靜地把每個步驟再解釋一遍，從來沒有提高音量過一次。"},{"w":"gentle","p":"adj.","d":"kind, calm, and careful","c":"溫柔的；輕柔的","s":"A: Why do the nurses at the clinic always ask Mrs. Huang to calm the nervous children before their check-ups? B: She has a very gentle voice and kind manner, and after raising six grandchildren, she knows exactly how to make little patients feel safe and relaxed in a strange place.","t":"A：為什麼診所的護理師總是請黃太太在健康檢查前安撫緊張的孩子？ B：她有非常【溫柔的】聲音和親切的態度，而且養大六個孫子女之後，她很清楚如何讓小病患在陌生的地方感到安全和放鬆。"},{"w":"devoted","p":"adj.","d":"giving a lot of love, time, or effort to someone or something","c":"全心投入的；忠誠的","s":"A: Why did the neighborhood association give an award to the elderly couple who live at the end of our street? B: They are devoted volunteers who have cleaned the local park every morning for fifteen years, and they also cook meals for families who need help during difficult times.","t":"A：為什麼社區協會頒獎給住在我們街尾的那對老夫婦？ B：他們是【全心投入的】志工，十五年來每天早上打掃當地公園，還會在困難時期為需要幫助的家庭煮飯。"},{"w":"protective","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to keep someone safe; giving protection","c":"保護的；愛護的","s":"A: Why does your grandmother always call you when there is a typhoon warning, even though you live in a safe building downtown? B: She is very protective of all her grandchildren, and she worries about us until she hears that we have enough food and water and will not go outside.","t":"A：為什麼即使你住在市中心安全的大樓裡，每次颱風警報時你祖母總會打電話給你？ B：她非常【保護】她所有的孫子女，在聽到我們有足夠的食物和水而且不會出門之前，她都會擔心我們。"},{"w":"role model","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose good behavior others copy","c":"榜樣；模範","s":"A: Why did you choose to become a nurse after finishing your business degree at the university? B: My grandmother worked in a hospital for forty years, and she has always been my role model because she treated every patient with kindness, no matter how tired or busy she was.","t":"A：為什麼你在大學取得商學學位後，選擇成為一名護理師？ B：我的祖母在醫院工作了四十年，她一直是我的【榜樣】，因為不論多累多忙，她都以善意對待每位病人。"},{"w":"caretaking","p":"n.","d":"the work of looking after a person or place","c":"照料；照顧","s":"A: Why did the company add flexible working hours to its employee benefits policy at the start of this year? B: Many staff members share caretaking duties for aging parents at home, and the managers realized that allowing them to start late or leave early reduces stress and keeps good workers.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年初在員工福利政策中加入彈性工時？ B：許多員工在家要分擔照顧年邁父母的【照料】工作，而主管們了解到讓他們晚點上班或早點下班能減輕壓力並留住好員工。"},{"w":"aging","p":"n.","d":"the process of growing old","c":"老化；變老","s":"A: Why is the government building more health centers and parks with walking paths in small towns around the country? B: The population of these areas is getting older, and officials want to help residents deal with aging by giving them easy ways to stay active and meet their neighbors.","t":"A：為什麼政府要在全國各地小鎮興建更多健康中心和有步道的公園？ B：這些地區的人口正在變老，官員們希望藉由提供居民容易保持活躍和認識鄰居的方式，幫助他們面對【老化】。"},{"w":"family values","p":"n.phr.","d":"beliefs about the importance of family life","c":"家庭價值觀","s":"A: Why did the hotel chain decide to offer free rooms for grandparents who travel with their children and grandchildren? B: The new owner wants the brand to stand for strong family values, and he believes that welcoming three generations together will attract loyal guests for many years.","t":"A：為什麼連鎖飯店決定為和子女、孫子女一同旅行的祖父母提供免費房間？ B：新老闆希望這個品牌代表堅定的【家庭價值觀】，他相信歡迎三代同遊能在多年間吸引忠實客人。"},{"w":"reunion","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people who have not seen each other for a long time","c":"團聚；重聚","s":"A: Why did your manager book the large private room at the seafood restaurant for the second Saturday of next month? B: His grandparents are celebrating their sixtieth wedding anniversary, so he is organizing a family reunion for more than fifty relatives who are flying in from three different countries.","t":"A：為什麼你的經理預訂了海鮮餐廳的大包廂，日期是下個月的第二個星期六？ B：他的祖父母要慶祝結婚六十週年，所以他正在為五十多位從三個不同國家飛來的親戚籌辦一場家族【團聚】。"},{"w":"household","p":"n.","d":"all the people who live together in one home","c":"家庭；一家人","s":"A: Why does the electricity bill at your home seem so much higher than your coworkers' bills each month? B: We have a large household with my grandparents, my parents, my sister, and her two kids all living together, so we use the air conditioner and washing machine almost every day.","t":"A：為什麼你家每個月的電費似乎比你同事的高很多？ B：我們是一個大【家庭】，我的祖父母、父母、妹妹和她的兩個孩子都住在一起，所以我們幾乎每天都用冷氣和洗衣機。"},{"w":"legacy","p":"n.","d":"something left behind by a person for those who come later","c":"傳承；遺產","s":"A: Why did the owner's granddaughter decide to keep the old tea shop open instead of selling the building to a developer? B: She wanted to protect her grandfather's legacy, because he had built the business from nothing and served loyal customers in the neighborhood for over half a century.","t":"A：為什麼老闆的孫女決定繼續經營老茶行，而不是把建築賣給建商？ B：她想守護她祖父留下的【傳承】，因為他白手起家建立這門生意，並為附近的忠實顧客服務了半個多世紀。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone confidence to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: Why did you sign up for the weekend painting class at the community center when you have never painted before? B: My grandmother, who started painting at seventy, always says it is never too late to learn, and her kind words did a lot to encourage me to try something new after a stressful year at work.","t":"A：你從來沒畫過畫，為什麼報名社區中心的週末繪畫課？ B：我的祖母七十歲才開始畫畫，她總是說學習永遠不嫌晚，而且在我工作壓力很大的一年後，她親切的話大大【鼓勵】我去嘗試新事物。"},{"w":"comfort","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being calm, relaxed, or less sad","c":"安慰；舒適","s":"A: Why did you visit your grandparents' farm right after the company announced that your department would be closing? B: I needed some comfort after hearing the bad news, and spending a quiet weekend with them, eating home-cooked meals and talking by the fire, helped me feel calm and hopeful again.","t":"A：為什麼公司宣布你的部門要關閉後，你馬上去了祖父母的農場？ B：聽到這個壞消息後我需要一些【安慰】，和他們度過一個安靜的週末，吃家常菜、在爐火旁聊天，讓我再次感到平靜和充滿希望。"},{"w":"influence","p":"n.","d":"the power to change how someone thinks or acts","c":"影響；影響力","s":"A: Why do you think the new marketing manager is so careful with money even though the company has a large budget this year? B: Her grandparents ran a small grocery store for decades, and their influence taught her to check every cost carefully and never waste resources on things customers do not need.","t":"A：為什麼你覺得新的行銷經理即使公司今年預算充足，仍然對花錢這麼謹慎？ B：她的祖父母經營小雜貨店數十年，他們的【影響】教會她仔細檢查每一筆花費，絕不把資源浪費在顧客不需要的東西上。"}]},{"unit":162,"theme":"Group 團體","cards":[{"w":"team","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together","c":"團隊；小組","s":"A: Why did the manager move Lisa from the accounting department to the marketing floor at the beginning of this month? B: She joined the new team that is planning the summer product launch, because the director wanted someone who understands budgets to work closely with the designers every day.","t":"A：為什麼經理在這個月初把Lisa從會計部調到行銷部樓層？ B：她加入了負責規劃夏季產品發表的新【團隊】，因為主管希望有一位了解預算的人每天和設計師密切合作。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"the people who live in the same area","c":"社區；社群","s":"A: Why is our company paying for new benches and trees in the park across the street from the factory this year? B: The owners want to give something back to the local community, since many of our workers live nearby and families often use the park on weekends.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司今年要出錢在工廠對面的公園設置新長椅和種樹？ B：老闆們想要回饋當地【社區】，因為很多員工住在附近，而且週末常有家庭到公園休閒。"},{"w":"organization","p":"n.","d":"an official group with a shared purpose, such as a company or charity","c":"組織；機構","s":"A: Where did you work before you joined our sales department, and what kind of tasks were you responsible for there? B: I worked for a non-profit organization that helped elderly people in rural areas, and I was in charge of raising money and finding volunteers for its yearly events.","t":"A：你加入我們業務部之前在哪裡工作？在那裡負責哪些工作？ B：我在一個幫助偏鄉長者的非營利【組織】工作，負責募款以及為每年的活動招募志工。"},{"w":"association","p":"n.","d":"a group of people or businesses joined together for a shared interest","c":"協會；公會","s":"A: Why are so many restaurant owners meeting at the convention center downtown tomorrow afternoon? B: The local restaurant association has invited all its members to discuss the new food safety rules, and they also plan to share ideas about how to deal with rising rent and labor costs.","t":"A：為什麼明天下午有這麼多餐廳老闆要在市中心的會議中心開會？ B：當地餐飲【協會】邀請所有會員討論新的食品安全規定，他們也打算分享如何因應房租和人事成本上漲的想法。"},{"w":"committee","p":"n.","d":"a small group chosen to make decisions or plans for a larger group","c":"委員會","s":"A: Who decided that the annual company picnic would be held at the lake instead of the city park this year? B: A small committee of five employees from different departments voted on it last week, after they compared prices, transportation options, and the results of the staff survey.","t":"A：今年公司年度野餐改在湖邊而不是市立公園舉辦，是誰決定的？ B：由不同部門五位員工組成的小型【委員會】上週投票決定，他們比較了價格、交通方式和員工問卷結果之後才做出決定。"},{"w":"club","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who meet regularly for an activity they enjoy","c":"社團；俱樂部","s":"A: Why do you always leave the office so quickly on Wednesday evenings, even when there is a lot of work to finish? B: I joined a running club near the river last spring, and we meet at six thirty every Wednesday to train together for a half marathon in October.","t":"A：為什麼你每週三晚上總是那麼快離開辦公室，即使還有很多工作沒做完？ B：我去年春天加入了河邊的一個跑步【社團】，我們每週三六點半見面，一起為十月的半程馬拉松訓練。"},{"w":"crowd","p":"n.","d":"a large number of people together in one place","c":"人群；人潮","s":"A: Why did it take you almost an hour to get through the main entrance of the trade show this morning? B: A huge crowd was waiting outside because a famous tech company was giving away free samples, and the security guards were checking every visitor's ticket and bag very carefully.","t":"A：為什麼你今天早上花了將近一小時才通過商展的大門？ B：外面有大批【人潮】在等候，因為一家知名科技公司在發送免費樣品，而且保全仔細檢查每位訪客的門票和包包。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people, often for a social reason","c":"聚會；集會","s":"A: Are you planning to come to the small gathering at Mark's house on Saturday to celebrate his promotion to sales manager? B: Yes, I'll be there after my daughter's piano lesson, and I'm going to bring some homemade cookies because he said everyone should bring a dish to share.","t":"A：你打算週六去Mark家參加慶祝他升任業務經理的小型【聚會】嗎？ B：會啊，我女兒的鋼琴課結束後就過去，我會帶一些自製餅乾，因為他說每個人都要帶一道菜來分享。"},{"w":"collective","p":"adj.","d":"shared or done by all members of a group","c":"集體的；共同的","s":"A: How did the small design company manage to win the city's biggest building contract against so many larger firms? B: It was really a collective effort, because every employee, from the interns to the owner, worked late for weeks to prepare drawings, cost reports, and a model for the presentation.","t":"A：那家小型設計公司是如何在眾多大公司競爭下贏得市內最大的建案合約？ B：那真的是【集體】努力的成果，因為從實習生到老闆，每位員工都連續加班好幾週，準備圖稿、成本報告和簡報用的模型。"},{"w":"coalition","p":"n.","d":"a group of organizations or people who join together for a shared goal","c":"聯盟；聯合團體","s":"A: Why did the city finally agree to build a new bicycle lane along the main shopping street? B: A coalition of local shop owners, schools, and environmental groups worked together for two years, collecting signatures and meeting with officials until the plan was approved.","t":"A：為什麼市政府終於同意沿著主要購物街興建新的自行車道？ B：由當地店家、學校和環保團體組成的【聯盟】合作了兩年，收集連署並和官員開會，直到計畫獲得批准。"},{"w":"network","p":"n.","d":"a group of people or things that are connected to each other","c":"人脈；網絡","s":"A: How did you find so many new clients in your first year as a freelance designer after leaving the agency? B: I built a strong network of contacts by going to industry events and keeping in touch with former coworkers, and many of them recommended me to their friends and business partners.","t":"A：你離開廣告公司後，在當自由設計師的第一年是怎麼找到這麼多新客戶的？ B：我參加業界活動、和前同事保持聯絡，建立起強大的人脈【網絡】，其中很多人把我推薦給他們的朋友和事業夥伴。"},{"w":"partnership","p":"n.","d":"a relationship in which two or more people or companies work together","c":"合作關係；合夥","s":"A: Why will our coffee be sold in that popular bookstore chain starting next month? B: Our company signed a partnership with them last week, so they will serve our coffee in all forty of their stores, and in return we will promote their new reading app on our cups.","t":"A：為什麼從下個月開始我們的咖啡會在那家熱門連鎖書店販售？ B：我們公司上週和他們簽訂了【合作】協議，所以他們四十家門市都會供應我們的咖啡，而我們則會在杯子上宣傳他們的新閱讀應用程式。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together with others to create or achieve something","c":"合作；協作","s":"A: How was the new kitchen product developed so quickly, when most of our projects usually take more than a year? B: It came from close collaboration between our engineers in Taipei and a design studio in Milan, who held video meetings almost every day to share drawings and test results.","t":"A：為什麼這款新廚房產品開發得這麼快？我們大部分的專案通常都要超過一年。 B：這來自我們台北工程師和米蘭一家設計工作室之間的密切【合作】，他們幾乎每天開視訊會議分享圖稿和測試結果。"},{"w":"alliance","p":"n.","d":"an agreement between groups or countries to work together for shared benefits","c":"聯盟；同盟","s":"A: Why are those three airlines now letting passengers collect points on each other's flights? B: They formed an alliance earlier this year so that travelers can book connecting flights more easily, share airport lounges, and earn rewards no matter which of the airlines they choose.","t":"A：為什麼那三家航空公司現在讓乘客搭乘彼此的航班都能累積點數？ B：他們今年稍早結成【聯盟】，讓旅客更容易預訂轉機航班、共用機場貴賓室，而且不論選擇哪家航空都能累積回饋。"},{"w":"membership","p":"n.","d":"the state of belonging to a group or club","c":"會員資格；會籍","s":"A: How much does it cost to use the gym on the second floor of our office building, and can I bring a friend? B: A yearly membership is about twelve thousand dollars, but employees of companies in this building get a twenty percent discount, and you can bring one guest each month for free.","t":"A：使用我們辦公大樓二樓的健身房要多少錢？我可以帶朋友去嗎？ B：年度【會員】大約一萬二千元，但這棟大樓內公司的員工可以打八折，而且每個月可以免費帶一位來賓。"},{"w":"participant","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in an activity or event","c":"參加者；參與者","s":"A: How many people have signed up for the online customer service training that starts next Monday morning? B: We already have more than eighty, so each participant will be placed in a smaller class of twenty and will receive a workbook and a certificate after finishing all four sessions.","t":"A：下週一早上開始的線上客服訓練有多少人報名了？ B：已經超過八十人了，所以每位【參加者】都會被分到二十人的小班，完成四堂課後會收到一本練習手冊和一張證書。"},{"w":"leader","p":"n.","d":"a person who guides or is in charge of a group","c":"領導者；負責人","s":"A: Why does everyone on the sales floor seem so happy and motivated since Ms. Chen joined the company in March? B: She is a great leader who listens to her staff, explains her plans clearly, and always gives credit to the people who did the work when a big deal is closed.","t":"A：為什麼自從陳小姐三月加入公司以來，業務部的每個人都顯得那麼開心又有幹勁？ B：她是一位很棒的【領導者】，會傾聽員工意見、清楚說明計畫，而且談成大案子時總是把功勞歸給實際做事的人。"},{"w":"follower","p":"n.","d":"a person who supports someone or follows their account on social media","c":"追隨者；粉絲","s":"A: Why did the cosmetics company choose that young blogger to advertise its new skin cream instead of a movie star? B: She has a huge online audience, and almost every follower of her beauty channel trusts her opinions, so the company believes her short videos will sell more products than a costly TV commercial.","t":"A：為什麼那家化妝品公司選擇那位年輕部落客來宣傳新面霜，而不是找電影明星？ B：她在網路上有大量觀眾，而且她美妝頻道的幾乎每位【粉絲】都信任她的意見，所以公司認為她的短片會比昂貴的電視廣告賣出更多產品。"},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"communication or activity between people","c":"互動；交流","s":"A: Why do you prefer working at the office three days a week instead of staying home every day? B: I enjoy the face-to-face interaction with my coworkers, because quick conversations at lunch or in the hallway often help me solve problems faster than long emails or video calls.","t":"A：為什麼你比較喜歡每週進辦公室三天，而不是每天都在家工作？ B：我喜歡和同事面對面【互動】，因為午餐時或走廊上的簡短交談，往往比冗長的電子郵件或視訊通話更快幫我解決問題。"},{"w":"cooperation","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together and helping each other to reach the same goal","c":"合作；配合","s":"A: Why did the building manager send a letter to all the tenants on Friday afternoon? B: The elevators will be repaired next week, so he asked for everyone's cooperation in using the stairs when possible and in avoiding moving large furniture until the work is finished.","t":"A：為什麼大樓管理員週五下午寄信給所有租戶？ B：下週要維修電梯，所以他請大家【配合】盡量走樓梯，並在工程完成前避免搬運大型家具。"},{"w":"unity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being together or in agreement","c":"團結；統一","s":"A: Why did the CEO invite every department to the same dinner after the difficult merger last year? B: She wanted to build a sense of unity between the two companies' staff, who had different working styles and were still worried about losing their jobs or being moved to other cities.","t":"A：為什麼去年艱難的合併之後，執行長邀請所有部門參加同一場晚宴？ B：她想在兩家公司的員工之間建立【團結】感，因為他們的工作風格不同，而且仍擔心會失業或被調到其他城市。"},{"w":"solidarity","p":"n.","d":"support and agreement among people who share the same goals or problems","c":"團結一致；聲援","s":"A: Why are so many employees wearing yellow ribbons on their jackets at the factory today? B: They are showing solidarity with the workers at our sister plant, who lost their homes in last week's flood, and the union is also collecting money and clothes to send to them.","t":"A：為什麼今天工廠裡有這麼多員工在外套上別著黃絲帶？ B：他們在表達對姊妹廠員工的【聲援】，那些員工在上週水災中失去了家園，工會也在募集金錢和衣物寄給他們。"},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"the condition of including many different types of people or things","c":"多元性；多樣性","s":"A: Why does our human resources department now post job advertisements in several languages and on different websites? B: The company wants more diversity in its workforce, because hiring people from different backgrounds, ages, and countries brings fresh ideas and helps us understand customers around the world.","t":"A：為什麼我們人資部現在用好幾種語言、在不同網站上刊登徵才廣告？ B：公司希望員工更具【多元性】，因為聘用不同背景、年齡和國籍的人能帶來新觀點，並幫助我們了解世界各地的顧客。"},{"w":"inclusion","p":"n.","d":"the act of making sure everyone is accepted and allowed to take part","c":"包容；納入","s":"A: Why did the office install a ramp at the entrance and buy desks that can be raised and lowered? B: Our new policy focuses on inclusion, so the company wants every employee, including those who use wheelchairs, to move around easily and work comfortably without asking for special help.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室在入口裝了斜坡，還買了可以升降的桌子？ B：我們的新政策重視【包容】，所以公司希望每位員工，包括坐輪椅的人，都能輕鬆行動、舒適工作，而不必特別請求協助。"},{"w":"coordination","p":"n.","d":"the act of organizing different people or parts so they work well together","c":"協調；配合","s":"A: How did the hotel manage to serve dinner to five hundred conference guests in less than an hour last night? B: It took careful coordination between the kitchen staff, the waiters, and the event planners, who used radios to tell each other exactly when each table was ready for the next dish.","t":"A：飯店昨晚如何在不到一小時內為五百位會議賓客上完晚餐？ B：這需要廚房員工、服務生和活動企劃之間仔細【協調】，他們用無線電準確告知彼此每一桌何時可以上下一道菜。"},{"w":"consensus","p":"n.","d":"agreement among all or most people in a group","c":"共識","s":"A: Did the board of directors finally decide whether to open a new branch in Kaohsiung next year? B: Not yet, because they couldn't reach a consensus during the three-hour meeting, as some members worried about the high rent while others believed the southern market would grow quickly.","t":"A：董事會最後決定明年是否要在高雄開設新分店了嗎？ B：還沒，因為他們在三小時的會議中無法達成【共識】，有些成員擔心租金太高，有些則認為南部市場會快速成長。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a conversation about a subject in which people share ideas","c":"討論","s":"A: What happened at the staff meeting this morning, and why did it run more than an hour late? B: There was a long discussion about the new work-from-home rules, because many parents wanted more flexible hours while some managers worried that teamwork and communication would suffer.","t":"A：今天早上的員工會議發生了什麼事？為什麼拖延了一個多小時？ B：大家針對新的居家工作規定進行了冗長的【討論】，因為很多家長希望工時更彈性，而有些主管擔心團隊合作和溝通會受影響。"},{"w":"brainstorm","p":"v.","d":"to think of many ideas quickly as a group","c":"腦力激盪；集思廣益","s":"A: What are we going to do in the meeting room this afternoon before the client arrives at four o'clock? B: The manager wants us to brainstorm new names for the energy drink, so please bring any ideas you have, even silly ones, and we'll write all of them on the whiteboard first.","t":"A：今天下午客戶四點到之前，我們要在會議室做什麼？ B：經理要我們為這款能量飲料【腦力激盪】想新名稱，所以請帶著你的任何點子來，即使很好笑的也沒關係，我們會先把全部寫在白板上。"},{"w":"bonding","p":"n.","d":"the process of forming a close relationship with others","c":"建立感情；凝聚情誼","s":"A: Why is the company taking all the new employees on a two-day hiking trip in the mountains next month? B: The trip is designed for team bonding, so the new staff can get to know each other outside the office, learn to trust one another, and feel more comfortable asking for help at work.","t":"A：為什麼公司下個月要帶所有新進員工去山上健行兩天？ B：這趟旅行是為了團隊【凝聚情誼】而設計的，讓新同事能在辦公室外彼此認識、學會互相信任，在工作上也更自在地尋求協助。"},{"w":"subgroup","p":"n.","d":"a smaller group that is part of a larger group","c":"小組；子群組","s":"A: How will the fifty volunteers manage to clean the whole beach before the festival starts on Sunday morning? B: The organizer will divide everyone by area, and each subgroup of ten people will be responsible for one part of the beach, collecting plastic, cans, and broken glass into separate bags.","t":"A：五十位志工要怎樣在週日早上節慶開始前把整個海灘清乾淨？ B：主辦人會依區域分配大家，每個十人【小組】負責海灘的一個區段，把塑膠、鐵罐和碎玻璃分別裝進不同的袋子。"},{"w":"peer","p":"n.","d":"a person who is the same age, level, or job as you","c":"同儕；同事","s":"A: How does the company decide who will receive the best employee award at the end of every year? B: Managers look at sales numbers, but each worker can also nominate a peer who has been especially helpful, because coworkers often notice good work that bosses might miss.","t":"A：公司每年年底如何決定誰獲得最佳員工獎？ B：主管會看業績，但每位員工也可以提名一位特別樂於助人的【同儕】，因為同事往往會注意到老闆可能忽略的好表現。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch or listen to a performance, speech, etc.","c":"觀眾；聽眾","s":"A: How did your presentation at the marketing conference in Singapore go yesterday afternoon? B: It went really well, because the audience asked lots of good questions after my talk, and three companies wanted to meet me later to discuss using our new advertising software.","t":"A：你昨天下午在新加坡行銷研討會的簡報進行得怎麼樣？ B：非常順利，因為我演講後【聽眾】問了很多好問題，還有三家公司想之後跟我見面，討論使用我們的新廣告軟體。"},{"w":"delegation","p":"n.","d":"a group of people sent to represent an organization or country","c":"代表團","s":"A: Why is the meeting room on the tenth floor being decorated with flags and flowers today? B: A delegation of business leaders from Japan is visiting our headquarters tomorrow morning, and the chairman wants to give them a warm welcome before they tour our factory and sign the contract.","t":"A：為什麼今天十樓的會議室要用旗子和花來佈置？ B：一個來自日本的企業界【代表團】明天早上要參觀我們的總部，董事長希望在他們參觀工廠和簽約前熱烈歡迎他們。"},{"w":"assemble","p":"v.","d":"to come together or bring people together in one place","c":"集合；聚集","s":"A: What should all employees do if the fire alarm goes off during next Tuesday's safety drill? B: Everyone should leave the building by the nearest stairs and assemble in the parking lot across the street, where the floor managers will count people and check that nobody is missing.","t":"A：下週二安全演習時，如果火警鈴響，全體員工應該怎麼做？ B：大家應該從最近的樓梯離開大樓，到對街的停車場【集合】，樓層主管會在那裡清點人數，確認沒有人失蹤。"}]},{"unit":163,"theme":"Habits 習慣","cards":[{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"a regular way of doing things in a fixed order","c":"例行公事；慣例","s":"A: Since you started working from home last month, how do you keep yourself organized when there is nobody around to remind you about meetings and deadlines? B: I follow a simple morning routine: I make coffee, check my email at eight, write a to-do list, and then start the most difficult task before lunch.","t":"A：自從你上個月開始在家工作，沒有人提醒你開會和截止日期，你怎麼讓自己保持有條理？ B：我遵循一套簡單的早晨【例行程序】：泡咖啡、八點檢查電子郵件、寫待辦清單，然後在午餐前先處理最困難的工作。"},{"w":"practice","p":"n.","d":"something that is usually or regularly done, often as a rule","c":"慣例；習慣做法","s":"A: Why does our manager always ask everyone to save their files to the shared drive before they leave the office on Friday afternoons? B: It is standard practice in our department, because last year a laptop was stolen and we lost two weeks of important client reports that nobody had copied anywhere else.","t":"A：為什麼我們經理總是要求大家週五下午離開辦公室前把檔案存到共用硬碟？ B：這是我們部門的標準【慣例】，因為去年有一台筆電被偷，我們損失了兩週沒有人另外備份的重要客戶報告。"},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"a traditional way of behaving that a group of people accepts","c":"習俗；風俗","s":"A: I am visiting our partner company in Japan next week for the first time, so is there anything special I should know before I meet their managers? B: It is a local custom to exchange business cards with both hands and a small bow, so bring plenty of cards and read each one carefully before putting it away.","t":"A：我下週第一次去拜訪我們在日本的合作公司，在和他們的經理見面前有什麼特別要知道的嗎？ B：用雙手交換名片並微微鞠躬是當地的【習俗】，所以要帶足夠的名片，並在收起來之前仔細看過每一張。"},{"w":"pattern","p":"n.","d":"a regular way in which something happens again and again","c":"模式；規律","s":"A: Have you looked at the sales figures from our online store over the past six months, and did you notice anything interesting about when customers buy the most? B: Yes, there is a clear pattern: orders rise sharply on Sunday evenings, so the marketing team plans to send its weekly discount emails on Sunday afternoons from now on.","t":"A：你看過我們網路商店過去六個月的銷售數字嗎？有沒有注意到顧客什麼時候買最多？ B：有，有一個很明顯的【模式】：訂單在週日晚上大幅增加，所以行銷團隊打算從現在開始在週日下午寄出每週折扣郵件。"},{"w":"behavior","p":"n.","d":"the way a person acts","c":"行為；舉止","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager call a meeting with all the front desk staff this morning before the busy holiday weekend begins? B: A guest complained about rude behavior at check-in last night, so she wanted to remind everyone to stay polite and patient, even when guests are tired and angry after long flights.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理今天早上在忙碌的假日週末開始前，召集所有櫃檯人員開會？ B：昨晚有位客人抱怨入住時遇到無禮的【行為】，所以她想提醒大家，即使客人在長途飛行後又累又生氣，也要保持禮貌和耐心。"},{"w":"tendency","p":"n.","d":"a habit of acting in a certain way","c":"傾向；趨勢","s":"A: Is there anything I should be careful about when I take over the team's weekly reports from Daniel, who is moving to the Singapore office next month? B: He had a tendency to leave everything until Friday night, so I suggest you start collecting the numbers on Wednesday to avoid working late at the end of the week.","t":"A：我從下個月要調到新加坡辦公室的丹尼爾手上接手團隊週報時，有什麼需要注意的嗎？ B：他有把所有事情拖到週五晚上的【傾向】，所以我建議你週三就開始收集數字，以免週末前加班到很晚。"},{"w":"addiction","p":"n.","d":"a strong need to keep doing or using something that is hard to stop","c":"成癮；沉迷","s":"A: Why has the company decided to block social media websites on office computers during working hours starting next Monday? B: A recent survey showed that many employees spent over two hours a day online, and the HR manager believes this addiction to phones and the internet is hurting productivity and team communication.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定從下週一開始，上班時間在辦公室電腦上封鎖社群網站？ B：最近一項調查顯示，許多員工每天上網超過兩小時，人資經理認為這種對手機和網路的【成癮】正在損害生產力和團隊溝通。"},{"w":"ritual","p":"n.","d":"something you always do in the same way, often at a special time","c":"儀式；例行習慣","s":"A: I noticed that the whole sales team meets in the staff lounge every Monday at nine with coffee and pastries, so is that an official meeting? B: Not really, it is more like a weekly ritual: we share our goals, celebrate last week's deals, and enjoy a few minutes together before the phones start ringing.","t":"A：我注意到整個業務團隊每週一九點會帶著咖啡和點心在員工休息室集合，那是正式會議嗎？ B：其實不算，比較像是每週的【儀式】：我們分享目標、慶祝上週談成的生意，並在電話開始響之前一起享受幾分鐘。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control yourself and keep working in an organized way","c":"自律；紀律","s":"A: How did you manage to finish your online accounting course while working full-time and taking care of two young children at home? B: It took a lot of discipline, because I studied for one hour every night after the kids went to bed, even when I was tired or wanted to watch TV instead.","t":"A：你是怎麼一邊全職工作、一邊在家照顧兩個小孩，還完成線上會計課程的？ B：這需要很大的【自律】，因為我每天晚上孩子睡了以後都讀書一小時，即使累了或想看電視也一樣。"},{"w":"consistency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of always doing something in the same good way","c":"一致性；持續性","s":"A: Our coffee shop has three branches now, so why do customers still sometimes complain that the latte tastes different at each location? B: We need more consistency in training, so next month every barista will attend the same workshop and follow the same recipe card to make sure each drink tastes exactly the same.","t":"A：我們的咖啡店現在有三家分店，為什麼顧客有時還會抱怨每家店的拿鐵味道不同？ B：我們的訓練需要更多【一致性】，所以下個月每位咖啡師都會參加同一個工作坊，並按照同一張配方卡，確保每杯飲料的味道完全相同。"},{"w":"repetition","p":"n.","d":"doing or saying the same thing many times","c":"重複；反覆","s":"A: What is the best way for new staff members to remember the long list of product codes we use when we take orders over the phone? B: The key is repetition: they should read the codes aloud, write them down every morning, and use them in role-play calls until they can recall each one without checking the list.","t":"A：新進員工要記住我們電話接單時使用的一長串產品代碼，最好的方法是什麼？ B：關鍵在於【反覆練習】：他們應該大聲唸出代碼、每天早上寫下來，並在角色扮演的通話中使用，直到不看清單也能記起每一個。"},{"w":"lifestyle","p":"n.","d":"the way a person lives","c":"生活方式","s":"A: Why did you decide to sell your car and start riding a bicycle to the office, even on rainy days when the roads are wet and slippery? B: My doctor told me that I needed a healthier lifestyle, so I am trying to exercise more, eat less fast food, and spend less time sitting in traffic every morning.","t":"A：你為什麼決定賣掉車子改騎腳踏車上班，連路面濕滑的雨天也一樣？ B：醫生告訴我需要更健康的【生活方式】，所以我正努力多運動、少吃速食，並減少每天早上塞在車陣中的時間。"},{"w":"adopt","p":"v.","d":"to start using a new method, idea or habit","c":"採用；養成","s":"A: Our team keeps missing deadlines because people forget what tasks they were given at our meetings, so do you have any suggestions? B: I think we should adopt a new system where every task is written in an online planner with a name and due date, so everyone can check their responsibilities at any time.","t":"A：我們團隊一直錯過截止日期，因為大家會忘記開會時被分配了哪些任務，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：我認為我們應該【採用】新的系統，把每項任務連同負責人和截止日期寫在線上規劃表中，讓每個人隨時都能查看自己的職責。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to make something grow or become stronger over time","c":"培養；發展","s":"A: You always seem so calm and prepared at our monthly client presentations, so were you naturally good at public speaking when you joined the firm? B: Not at all, I was very nervous at first, but I managed to develop the habit of rehearsing in front of a mirror three times before every important meeting.","t":"A：你在每月的客戶簡報中總是看起來很冷靜、準備充分，你剛進公司時就天生擅長公開演講嗎？ B：完全不是，我一開始非常緊張，但我設法【養成】了在每次重要會議前對著鏡子排練三次的習慣。"},{"w":"maintain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something at the same level or in good condition","c":"維持；保持","s":"A: Now that the busy holiday season is over and many of our customers have gone back to normal spending, how will we keep our profits up? B: We plan to maintain strong relationships with our loyal customers by sending personal thank-you notes and offering small discounts on their birthdays throughout the coming year.","t":"A：既然忙碌的假期季節已經結束，許多顧客的消費也恢復正常，我們要怎麼維持利潤？ B：我們打算在接下來的一年裡寄送親筆感謝卡並在顧客生日時提供小折扣，以【維持】和忠實顧客的良好關係。"},{"w":"cultivate","p":"v.","d":"to develop a skill, attitude or relationship carefully over time","c":"培養；建立","s":"A: How does your company help young employees become future leaders, since many of them have never managed a team before? B: We cultivate their leadership skills slowly by giving them small projects first, pairing them with experienced mentors, and letting them lead short meetings before they take charge of larger departments.","t":"A：你們公司如何幫助年輕員工成為未來的領導者？因為他們之中許多人從沒管理過團隊。 B：我們會先給他們小型專案、安排資深導師陪伴，並讓他們主持簡短會議，慢慢【培養】他們的領導能力，之後才讓他們負責較大的部門。"},{"w":"break","p":"v.","d":"to stop doing something that you have done for a long time","c":"改掉；打破（習慣）","s":"A: You used to drink four cans of soda every afternoon at your desk, but I haven't seen you with one for weeks, so what changed? B: I wanted to break that bad habit before my health check in March, so I replaced the soda with green tea and now keep a large water bottle next to my computer.","t":"A：你以前每天下午都在座位上喝四罐汽水，但我已經好幾週沒看到你拿汽水了，發生什麼事了？ B：我想在三月健康檢查之前【改掉】那個壞習慣，所以我用綠茶取代汽水，現在還在電腦旁邊放一大瓶水。"},{"w":"reinforce","p":"v.","d":"to make an idea, feeling, habit or structure stronger","c":"強化；加強","s":"A: Why does the safety manager send a short reminder email about wearing helmets in the warehouse every single Monday, even though everyone already knows the rule? B: She says weekly reminders reinforce safe habits, and since the warehouse started doing this, the number of minor accidents has dropped by almost half compared with last year.","t":"A：為什麼安全經理每個星期一都會寄一封關於在倉庫戴安全帽的簡短提醒信，即使大家都已經知道這項規定？ B：她說每週的提醒能【強化】安全習慣，自從倉庫開始這麼做，小事故的數量和去年相比已經減少了將近一半。"},{"w":"automatic","p":"adj.","d":"done without thinking because you have done it many times; working by itself","c":"自動的；不假思索的","s":"A: How long did it take you to remember all the steps for locking up the store, setting the alarm, and checking the back door at closing time? B: About a month, but now the whole process is completely automatic for me, so I can do it quickly without looking at the checklist taped beside the door.","t":"A：你花了多久才記住打烊時鎖店、設定警報和檢查後門的所有步驟？ B：大約一個月，但現在整個過程對我來說完全是【自動的】，所以我不用看貼在門旁的檢查表就能快速完成。"},{"w":"regular","p":"adj.","d":"happening often or at fixed times","c":"規律的；定期的；經常的","s":"A: Our new accountant seems very tired every morning, so do you think the long hours at the end of the quarter are causing problems for her? B: Probably, she told me she hasn't had regular sleep for weeks, so I suggested she ask the manager whether she could finish earlier on some evenings next week.","t":"A：我們的新會計每天早上看起來都很累，你覺得是季末的長時間工作造成她的困擾嗎？ B：大概是，她告訴我她已經好幾週沒有【規律的】睡眠了，所以我建議她問問經理，下週是否有幾個晚上可以早點下班。"},{"w":"daily","p":"adj.","d":"happening or done every day","c":"每日的","s":"A: How do the managers at your hotel keep track of guest complaints and room problems when there are different staff working each shift? B: Every supervisor writes a short daily report before going home, and the general manager reads all of them each morning so nothing important is forgotten or ignored.","t":"A：你們飯店每班的員工都不同，經理們如何追蹤房客的抱怨和客房問題？ B：每位主管下班前都會寫一份簡短的【每日】報告，總經理每天早上都會閱讀全部報告，這樣就不會遺忘或忽略任何重要的事。"},{"w":"habitual","p":"adj.","d":"done often, as a habit","c":"習慣性的","s":"A: Why is the store manager planning to have a serious talk with Kevin this afternoon, since he seems friendly and works hard during his shifts? B: The problem is that he is a habitual latecomer who has arrived after nine almost every day this month, and other cashiers have had to cover the counter for him.","t":"A：店長為什麼打算今天下午和凱文認真談談？他看起來很友善，上班時也很努力。 B：問題是他是個【習慣性】遲到的人，這個月幾乎每天都在九點之後才到，其他收銀員只好替他顧櫃台。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"getting a lot of useful work done","c":"有成效的；有生產力的","s":"A: You seem to finish your reports much faster now than you did last year, so what has changed in the way you plan your working day? B: I do my hardest tasks first thing in the morning because that is when I am most productive, and I leave emails and phone calls until after lunch.","t":"A：你現在完成報告的速度似乎比去年快很多，你安排工作日的方式有什麼改變嗎？ B：我會在一大早先處理最困難的工作，因為那是我最【有生產力】的時候，而電子郵件和電話則留到午餐後再處理。"},{"w":"unhealthy","p":"adj.","d":"not good for your health","c":"不健康的","s":"A: Why did the company replace the snack machine on the third floor with a fridge full of fresh fruit and yogurt last week? B: The HR team noticed that many employees were eating chips and candy every afternoon, and they wanted to reduce these unhealthy eating habits and help people stay healthier at work.","t":"A：為什麼公司上週把三樓的零食販賣機換成裝滿新鮮水果和優格的冰箱？ B：人資團隊注意到許多員工每天下午都在吃洋芋片和糖果，他們想減少這些【不健康的】飲食習慣，幫助大家在上班時保持更健康。"},{"w":"beneficial","p":"adj.","d":"having a good or helpful effect","c":"有益的","s":"A: Do you really think the short walking meetings that our department started last month are worth continuing during the cold winter months? B: Yes, they have been very beneficial for everyone, because people feel more awake, share ideas more freely, and the meetings rarely last longer than twenty minutes now.","t":"A：你真的認為我們部門上個月開始的簡短散步會議，在寒冷的冬季也值得繼續嗎？ B：是的，這對大家都非常【有益】，因為大家覺得更清醒、更自在地分享想法，而且現在會議很少超過二十分鐘。"},{"w":"mindful","p":"adj.","d":"aware of something and careful about it","c":"留意的；注意的","s":"A: How can we keep the office pleasant next month when the new design team moves into the open area right next to our desks? B: We should all be mindful of noise levels, keep phone calls short, and use the meeting rooms for long conversations so that everyone else can concentrate on their work.","t":"A：下個月新的設計團隊搬進我們座位旁的開放區時，我們要怎麼讓辦公室保持舒適？ B：我們都應該【留意】音量、講電話簡短一點，長時間的談話就到會議室進行，讓其他人可以專心工作。"},{"w":"gradually","p":"adv.","d":"slowly over a period of time","c":"逐漸地","s":"A: Will the new rule about using reusable cups instead of paper cups in the staff kitchen start for everyone on the first day of next month? B: No, the company will introduce it gradually: first the managers will try it for two weeks, then each department will join one by one until the whole building is involved.","t":"A：員工茶水間用環保杯取代紙杯的新規定，會從下個月第一天開始對所有人實施嗎？ B：不會，公司會【逐漸地】推行：先由經理們試行兩週，然後各部門依序加入，直到整棟大樓都參與。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often and at fixed times","c":"定期地；經常地","s":"A: The printer on the second floor broke down again this morning, so how can we stop this from happening every few weeks? B: The technician said it needs to be cleaned and checked regularly, so I have booked him to visit on the first Monday of every month starting in December.","t":"A：二樓的印表機今天早上又壞了，我們要怎麼避免每隔幾週就發生一次？ B：技術人員說它需要【定期】清潔和檢查，所以我已經預約他從十二月起每個月第一個週一來一次。"},{"w":"frequently","p":"adv.","d":"often","c":"經常地；頻繁地","s":"A: Why has the customer service team created a new page on the company website with short answers about shipping, returns, and payments? B: Customers frequently call us with the same simple questions, so the page should save time for both our staff and the people who just want quick answers.","t":"A：客服團隊為什麼在公司網站上新增一個頁面，提供關於運送、退貨和付款的簡短解答？ B：顧客【經常】打電話來問同樣簡單的問題，所以這個頁面應該能為我們的員工和只想快速得到答案的人節省時間。"},{"w":"consistently","p":"adv.","d":"always in the same way or at the same good level","c":"一貫地；始終如一地","s":"A: Why did the board choose Ms. Chen as the new regional manager instead of someone with more years of experience at the company? B: Her team has consistently reached its sales targets every quarter for three years, and the directors trust her to bring the same steady results to the whole region.","t":"A：為什麼董事會選陳小姐擔任新的區域經理，而不是在公司資歷更久的人？ B：她的團隊三年來每季都【始終如一地】達成銷售目標，董事們相信她能為整個地區帶來同樣穩定的成果。"},{"w":"consciously","p":"adv.","d":"knowing what you are doing; on purpose","c":"有意識地","s":"A: How did you stop interrupting your coworkers during meetings, since you used to do it so often that people complained to the manager? B: I consciously reminded myself to wait three seconds after others stopped talking, and after a few weeks I found it much easier to listen patiently before giving my opinion.","t":"A：你以前開會時常打斷同事，甚至有人向經理抱怨，你是怎麼改掉的？ B：我【有意識地】提醒自己在別人說完話後等三秒，幾週後我發現在發表意見前耐心傾聽變得容易多了。"},{"w":"intentionally","p":"adv.","d":"on purpose; not by accident","c":"故意地；刻意地","s":"A: I printed the annual report for the board meeting, but page twelve is completely empty, so should I ask the design team to fix it? B: No need, that page was left blank intentionally, because the next section starts on the right-hand page, which is how most printed company reports are arranged.","t":"A：我為董事會會議印了年度報告，但第十二頁完全空白，要請設計團隊修正嗎？ B：不用，那頁是【刻意】留白的，因為下一節從右頁開始，大多數印刷的公司報告都是這樣安排的。"},{"w":"eventually","p":"adv.","d":"in the end, after a long time","c":"最後；終於","s":"A: Was it difficult to get your team to use the new project software, since many of them had used spreadsheets for more than ten years? B: At first they complained a lot, but eventually they saw how much time it saved, and now nobody wants to go back to the old way of tracking tasks.","t":"A：要讓你的團隊使用新的專案軟體很困難嗎？他們之中很多人用試算表已經十多年了。 B：一開始他們抱怨很多，但【最後】他們看到它省了多少時間，現在沒有人想回到以前追蹤任務的舊方法。"}]},{"unit":164,"theme":"Haircut 理髮","cards":[{"w":"hairdresser","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to cut, wash and style hair","c":"美髮師","s":"A: I have an important job interview at the bank next Monday morning, and my hair looks messy after the long summer holiday. Do you know a good salon near our office? B: Yes, my hairdresser works at a small shop across from the train station, and she always listens carefully before she starts cutting.","t":"A：我下週一早上在銀行有個重要的工作面試，經過長長的暑假，我的頭髮看起來很亂。你知道我們辦公室附近有好的髮廊嗎？ B：知道，我的【美髮師】在火車站對面的一家小店工作，她開始剪之前總是會仔細聆聽。"},{"w":"barber","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to cut men's hair and shave beards","c":"理髮師（男士）","s":"A: Where does your grandfather usually go to get his short hair trimmed and his beard shaved before family events? B: He visits the same barber on Main Street every two weeks, because the old man who runs the shop gives a clean, simple cut and tells funny stories while he works.","t":"A：你爺爺在家族聚會前通常去哪裡修剪短髮、刮鬍子？ B：他每兩週都會去中山街上同一位【理髮師】那裡，因為經營那家店的老先生剪得乾淨俐落，工作時還會講好笑的故事。"},{"w":"fringe","p":"n.","d":"hair cut short so that it hangs over the forehead","c":"瀏海","s":"A: Our manager said the new photos for the staff ID cards must clearly show our eyebrows and eyes, but my hair keeps covering my face. What should I do? B: You could ask the stylist to trim your fringe a little shorter, or simply pin it to the side with a small clip on the day the photos are taken.","t":"A：經理說員工證的新照片必須清楚露出眉毛和眼睛，可是我的頭髮一直遮住臉。我該怎麼辦？ B：你可以請設計師把你的【瀏海】修短一點，或者拍照當天用小髮夾把它夾到旁邊就好。"},{"w":"oftentimes","p":"adv.","d":"many times; often","c":"經常；時常","s":"A: Why do so many busy office workers choose to visit the hair salon during their lunch break instead of going on the weekend? B: oftentimes, the salons near business districts offer quick thirty-minute services at lower prices on weekdays, so people can get a neat cut and still return to their desks on time.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多忙碌的上班族選擇在午休時間去髮廊，而不是週末去？ B：商業區附近的髮廊【經常】在平日提供價格較低的三十分鐘快剪服務，所以大家可以剪個整齊的髮型，還能準時回到座位。"},{"w":"hair colouring","p":"n.phr.","d":"changing the color of hair with a chemical product","c":"染髮","s":"A: The salon is offering a special discount this month, but I'm worried that changing my natural black hair to light brown might damage it. What do you think? B: Modern hair colouring products are much gentler than before, but you should ask for a strand test first and use a good conditioner for several weeks afterwards.","t":"A：這家髮廊這個月有特別折扣，但我擔心把天生的黑髮換成淺棕色會傷髮質。你覺得呢？ B：現代的【染髮】產品比以前溫和很多，但你應該先要求做一小撮的測試，之後幾週也要用好的潤髮乳。"},{"w":"dye","p":"v.","d":"to change the color of something, such as hair, using a special liquid","c":"染（色）","s":"A: I noticed that the receptionist at our hotel came to work with bright purple hair yesterday. Is that allowed under the company's dress code? B: Actually, the hotel changed its rules last spring, so staff can now dye their hair any color they like as long as it looks neat and professional.","t":"A：我注意到我們飯店的櫃檯人員昨天頂著一頭亮紫色的頭髮來上班。公司的服裝規定允許這樣嗎？ B：其實飯店去年春天改了規定，所以現在員工可以把頭髮【染】成任何喜歡的顏色，只要看起來整齊又專業就好。"},{"w":"balayage","p":"n.","d":"a hair coloring method where lighter color is painted on by hand for a natural look","c":"手刷漸層挑染","s":"A: My sister wants a natural, sun-kissed look for her wedding in June, but she doesn't want strong lines when her hair grows out. What should she request? B: She should book a balayage with an experienced colorist, because the lighter shades are painted on by hand and blend softly into her darker roots over time.","t":"A：我姊姊想在六月的婚禮上呈現自然、陽光親吻般的造型，但不希望頭髮長出來時有明顯的分界線。她該要求什麼？ B：她應該找經驗豐富的染髮師預約【手刷漸層挑染】，因為較淺的顏色是用手刷上去的，隨著時間會柔和地融入較深的髮根。"},{"w":"hair rebonding","p":"n.phr.","d":"a chemical treatment that makes curly or wavy hair straight and smooth","c":"離子燙；燙直","s":"A: My curly hair becomes very frizzy in Taipei's humid summer weather, and it takes me almost an hour to straighten it every morning before work. Any ideas? B: You might consider hair rebonding, a chemical treatment that makes hair straight and smooth for several months, although it is quite expensive and takes about four hours at the salon.","t":"A：在台北潮濕的夏天，我的捲髮會變得非常毛躁，每天上班前要花將近一個小時把它弄直。有什麼建議嗎？ B：你可以考慮【離子燙】，這是一種能讓頭髮直順好幾個月的化學療程，不過價格相當貴，而且在髮廊要花大約四個小時。"},{"w":"hairstyle","p":"n.","d":"the way in which someone's hair is cut and arranged","c":"髮型","s":"A: The marketing team is preparing a new advertisement for our shampoo, and the director wants the model to look fresh and modern. Do you have any suggestions? B: I think a short, layered hairstyle with soft waves would look great on camera, and it would also show how shiny and healthy her hair is.","t":"A：行銷團隊正在為我們的洗髮精準備新廣告，導演希望模特兒看起來清新又現代。你有什麼建議嗎？ B：我覺得帶有柔和波浪的短層次【髮型】在鏡頭前會很好看，也能展現她的頭髮有多亮麗健康。"},{"w":"pixie cut","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very short women's haircut, short at the back and sides","c":"精靈短髮","s":"A: Have you seen the new receptionist? She cut off her long hair last weekend, and now it is very short around her ears and neck. B: Yes, she told me that a pixie cut is much easier to manage when she jogs every morning, and she only needs about five minutes to get ready.","t":"A：你看到新來的櫃檯人員了嗎？她上週末剪掉了長髮，現在耳朵和脖子周圍都非常短。 B：看到了，她告訴我【精靈短髮】在她每天早上慢跑時好整理多了，而且她只需要大約五分鐘就能準備好。"},{"w":"ponytails","p":"n.","d":"hair tied together at the back of the head so that it hangs down","c":"馬尾","s":"A: Why do the kitchen staff at the new restaurant all wear their long hair tied back behind their heads during working hours? B: Wearing neat ponytails is required by the health inspectors, because it keeps hair away from the food and stops it from getting caught near the hot stoves.","t":"A：為什麼那家新餐廳的廚房員工上班時都把長髮綁在腦後？ B：衛生稽查員規定要綁整齊的【馬尾】，因為這樣可以讓頭髮遠離食物，也能避免頭髮在熱爐子附近被勾到。"},{"w":"crew cut","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very short haircut, usually for men or boys","c":"平頭；短寸頭","s":"A: My son is starting summer camp next week, and he will be swimming and playing football outdoors every day in the hot weather. B: Maybe you should take him to the barber for a crew cut, because very short hair dries quickly after swimming and keeps him cool during long afternoons in the sun.","t":"A：我兒子下週開始參加夏令營，他每天都會在炎熱的天氣裡游泳和在戶外踢足球。 B：也許你應該帶他去理髮店剪個【平頭】，因為很短的頭髮游泳後乾得快，在陽光下漫長的下午也能讓他保持涼爽。"},{"w":"pompadour","p":"n.","d":"a hairstyle in which the hair is brushed up high and back from the forehead","c":"飛機頭；龐畢度髮型","s":"A: The theater company is looking for a hairstylist for its new musical set in the 1950s. What kind of look do the male actors need? B: Most of them will wear a pompadour, with the hair brushed up high and back from the forehead, just like the famous rock singers of that time.","t":"A：劇團正在為以一九五〇年代為背景的新音樂劇找髮型師。男演員需要什麼樣的造型？ B：他們大多會梳【飛機頭】，把頭髮從額頭往上往後梳得高高的，就像那個年代著名的搖滾歌手一樣。"},{"w":"conventional","p":"adj.","d":"following what is traditional or usual; not unusual","c":"傳統的；保守的","s":"A: Our law firm is quite traditional, so I'm not sure whether I should get bright red highlights before I start my new job next month. B: It might be safer to choose a more conventional style at first, and then you can try something bolder once you understand the office culture and your colleagues better.","t":"A：我們的律師事務所相當傳統，所以我不確定下個月開始新工作前該不該挑染亮紅色。 B：一開始選擇比較【保守的】造型可能比較安全，等你更了解辦公室文化和同事之後，再嘗試大膽一點的造型。"},{"w":"undeniably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is clearly true and cannot be doubted","c":"無可否認地；確實","s":"A: Do you think it was worth paying so much money for the famous stylist at that expensive salon downtown? B: It was undeniably expensive, but my hair has never looked this good, and several customers at the shop have already asked me for the name of the salon.","t":"A：你覺得花那麼多錢請市中心那家昂貴髮廊的知名設計師值得嗎？ B：【無可否認地】很貴，但我的頭髮從來沒有這麼好看過，而且店裡已經有好幾位客人問我那家髮廊的名字。"},{"w":"particular","p":"adj.","d":"caring a lot about small details and difficult to please","c":"講究的；挑剔的","s":"A: Why does Mr. Lin always wait for the same stylist, even when other staff members at the salon are free? B: He is very particular about how his hair looks, so he only trusts the stylist who has cut it for ten years and knows exactly what he likes.","t":"A：為什麼林先生總是等同一位設計師，即使髮廊其他員工有空也一樣？ B：他對自己的頭髮外觀非常【講究】，所以只信任幫他剪了十年、完全知道他喜好的那位設計師。"},{"w":"complement","p":"v.","d":"to go well with something and make it look better","c":"襯托；與……相配","s":"A: I have a round face, and I'm not sure which haircut would look best for my wedding photos next spring. B: A good stylist can choose a cut that will complement your face shape, for example longer layers around the cheeks, which make the face look slimmer in photographs.","t":"A：我是圓臉，不確定哪種髮型在明年春天的婚紗照裡最好看。 B：好的設計師能選擇【襯托】你臉型的剪法，例如在臉頰周圍剪較長的層次，在照片中能讓臉看起來更瘦。"},{"w":"dull","p":"adj.","d":"not bright or shiny","c":"暗沉的；無光澤的","s":"A: My hair looks flat and has lost its shine since I started swimming at the company gym three times a week. What can I do? B: Chlorine in the pool can make hair dry and dull, so you should wear a swimming cap and use a deep conditioner after every swim.","t":"A：自從我開始每週三次在公司健身房游泳後，我的頭髮看起來很塌，也失去了光澤。我該怎麼辦？ B：泳池裡的氯會讓頭髮乾燥又【暗沉】，所以你應該戴泳帽，每次游完泳後都用深層護髮乳。"},{"w":"refreshing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel less tired and full of energy again","c":"令人神清氣爽的","s":"A: How was your visit to the new salon near the office? You were away for nearly two hours during the afternoon. B: It was really refreshing, because the assistant gave me a long head massage with cool mint shampoo, and I felt full of energy when I went back to work.","t":"A：你去辦公室附近那家新髮廊感覺如何？你下午離開了將近兩個小時。 B：真的很【令人神清氣爽】，因為助理用清涼的薄荷洗髮精幫我做了很久的頭部按摩，我回去工作時覺得精神飽滿。"},{"w":"liberating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel free from limits or worries","c":"令人感到解放的；使人自由的","s":"A: I heard that you finally cut off your long hair after keeping it for more than ten years. How do you feel about it? B: It feels surprisingly liberating, because I no longer spend an hour drying it every night, and I feel free to try new styles and colors.","t":"A：聽說你留了十多年的長髮終於剪掉了。你感覺如何？ B：感覺出乎意料地【讓人解放】，因為我不用再每晚花一個小時吹乾頭髮，而且可以自由嘗試新造型和新顏色。"},{"w":"content","p":"adj.","d":"happy and satisfied with what you have","c":"滿足的；滿意的","s":"A: Are you going to try a new style when you visit the salon on Saturday, or will you keep the same look as usual? B: I'm quite content with my current haircut, so I'll just ask the stylist to trim the ends and keep everything else the same.","t":"A：你星期六去髮廊時要嘗試新造型，還是維持平常的樣子？ B：我對目前的髮型相當【滿意】，所以只會請設計師修一下髮尾，其他都保持不變。"},{"w":"fitting","p":"adj.","d":"suitable or right for a particular situation","c":"合適的；恰當的","s":"A: For the company's fiftieth anniversary gala, the CEO wants all the hosts to look elegant and formal on stage. What styles should the salon prepare? B: Smart, simple updos would be the most fitting choice for such a formal evening, and they will also look tidy in the photos for the annual report.","t":"A：在公司五十週年晚會上，執行長希望所有主持人在台上看起來優雅又正式。髮廊應該準備什麼造型？ B：俐落簡單的盤髮會是這種正式晚會最【合適的】選擇，而且在年報的照片裡看起來也會很整齊。"},{"w":"invest","p":"v.","d":"to spend money, time or effort on something to get an advantage later","c":"投資","s":"A: Why did your sister spend so much money on professional scissors and a training course last year? B: She decided to invest in her future career as a hairstylist, and now she cuts hair for many clients and plans to open her own salon next year.","t":"A：你姊姊去年為什麼花那麼多錢買專業剪刀和上培訓課程？ B：她決定為自己未來的髮型師職涯【投資】，現在她幫很多客人剪頭髮，並計劃明年開自己的髮廊。"}]},{"unit":165,"theme":"Handwriting 手寫","cards":[{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following old ways that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統的","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager still ask guests to sign a paper guest book at the front desk when we already have an online check-in system? B: She likes the traditional way of welcoming people, and many older visitors enjoy writing a short message by hand before they go up to their rooms.","t":"A：既然我們已經有線上入住系統，為什麼飯店經理還要請客人在櫃台的紙本留言簿上簽名？ B：她喜歡用【傳統的】方式迎接客人，而且很多年長的旅客喜歡在上樓回房前親手寫一段簡短的留言。"},{"w":"oftentimes","p":"adv.","d":"often; many times","c":"時常；常常","s":"A: Do you prefer to type your meeting notes on a laptop, or do you still write them down in a notebook during the weekly sales meeting? B: oftentimes I write them by hand, because it helps me remember the main points, and later I type a short summary for the whole team.","t":"A：每週業務會議時，你比較喜歡用筆電打會議紀錄，還是仍然寫在筆記本上？ B：我【時常】用手寫，因為這能幫助我記住重點，之後我再為整個團隊打一份簡短摘要。"},{"w":"convenient","p":"adj.","d":"easy to use; saving time or trouble","c":"方便的","s":"A: Why did the receptionist leave a small pad of paper and a pen next to every phone in the office instead of asking us to use the computer? B: She thought it would be more convenient for staff to write down quick phone messages by hand while they are still talking to the customer.","t":"A：為什麼接待人員在辦公室每支電話旁都放了一小本便條紙和一支筆，而不是要我們用電腦？ B：她認為員工在跟客戶講電話時，就能用手快速記下電話留言，這樣會比較【方便】。"},{"w":"penmanship","p":"n.","d":"the skill or style of handwriting","c":"書法；書寫技巧；字跡","s":"A: Why did the wedding planning company hire a new staff member who has no experience in event design or customer service? B: Her penmanship is so beautiful that the manager wants her to write all the names on the invitation cards and seating cards for our clients' weddings.","t":"A：為什麼婚禮企劃公司僱用了一位沒有活動設計或客服經驗的新員工？ B：她的【字跡】非常漂亮，所以經理希望她為客戶的婚禮手寫所有邀請卡和座位卡上的名字。"},{"w":"legible","p":"adj.","d":"clear enough to be read easily","c":"字跡清楚的；易讀的","s":"A: The warehouse team keeps sending the wrong items to customers, so what do you think is causing all these mistakes in our orders? B: I think some of the handwritten order forms are not legible, so the workers guess the product numbers and often pick the wrong boxes from the shelves.","t":"A：倉庫團隊一直寄錯商品給客戶，你認為我們訂單出這麼多錯的原因是什麼？ B：我認為有些手寫訂購單的字跡不【清楚】，所以工人只能猜產品編號，常常從貨架上拿錯箱子。"},{"w":"illegible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible or very hard to read","c":"難以辨認的；字跡潦草的","s":"A: Why did the pharmacist call the clinic this morning before she gave the elderly patient his medicine? B: The doctor's note was completely illegible, so she wanted to check the name and amount of the medicine to make sure the patient would not take the wrong pills.","t":"A：為什麼藥師今天早上在把藥交給那位年長病人前，先打電話給診所？ B：醫師的處方字跡完全【難以辨認】，所以她想確認藥名和劑量，以確保病人不會吃錯藥。"},{"w":"compulsory","p":"adj.","d":"required by a rule; must be done","c":"強制的；必修的","s":"A: Do all new employees at the bank have to attend the training session about filling in paper forms for customers who cannot use the online system? B: Yes, it is compulsory for everyone, because mistakes on these forms can delay payments and cause serious problems for both the bank and the customers.","t":"A：銀行所有新進員工都必須參加如何為無法使用線上系統的客戶填寫紙本表格的訓練課程嗎？ B：是的，這對每個人都是【強制的】，因為這些表格上的錯誤可能延誤付款，給銀行和客戶都造成嚴重的問題。"},{"w":"cursive","p":"n.","d":"a style of handwriting with joined letters","c":"草寫體；連筆字","s":"A: Why is the young intern having trouble reading the old letters that the company founder wrote to his business partners in the 1960s? B: The letters are written in cursive, and since she mostly learned to type at school, she finds the joined-up letters very difficult to read quickly.","t":"A：為什麼那位年輕實習生在閱讀公司創辦人1960年代寫給事業夥伴的舊信件時有困難？ B：那些信是用【草寫體】寫的，而她在學校大多學打字，所以覺得那種連筆字很難快速讀懂。"},{"w":"value","p":"v.","d":"to think something is important or useful","c":"重視；珍視","s":"A: Why does our sales director still send a handwritten thank-you card to every new client, even though it takes her a lot of time each month? B: She knows that many clients value a personal message more than an email, and it helps the company build strong and long-lasting business relationships.","t":"A：為什麼我們的業務總監仍會寄手寫感謝卡給每位新客戶，即使每個月都要花她很多時間？ B：她知道很多客戶【重視】個人化的訊息勝過電子郵件，而這能幫助公司建立穩固且長久的商業關係。"},{"w":"absolutely","p":"adv.","d":"completely; totally","c":"絕對地；完全地","s":"A: Is it really necessary for me to sign every page of the rental contract by hand, or can I just sign the last page and send it back by email? B: It is absolutely necessary to sign each page, because the landlord's lawyer will not accept the contract if even one page is missing a signature.","t":"A：我真的需要在租約的每一頁都親筆簽名嗎？還是只簽最後一頁再用電子郵件寄回就好？ B：每一頁都【絕對】必須簽名，因為只要有一頁漏簽，房東的律師就不會接受這份合約。"},{"w":"essential","p":"adj.","d":"very important and necessary","c":"必要的；不可或缺的","s":"A: What skills should we look for when we hire a new assistant for the busy front office at the medical clinic? B: Clear handwriting is essential for this job, because the assistant writes appointment cards and notes for patients, and nobody wants patients to miss their visits because of a mistake.","t":"A：我們為診所忙碌的前台招聘新助理時，應該重視哪些技能？ B：清楚的字跡對這份工作是【必要的】，因為助理要為病人寫預約卡和便條，沒有人希望病人因為寫錯而錯過看診。"},{"w":"signing","p":"n.","d":"the act of writing your name on an official document","c":"簽署；簽字","s":"A: Why are so many reporters and photographers waiting in the hotel lobby this afternoon, and why has the meeting room been decorated with flags? B: The two companies are holding the official signing of their partnership agreement there at three o'clock, and both presidents will put their names on the documents in front of the cameras.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午有這麼多記者和攝影師在飯店大廳等候，而且會議室還用旗子裝飾？ B：兩家公司三點要在那裡舉行合作協議的正式【簽署】儀式，兩位總裁將在鏡頭前於文件上簽名。"},{"w":"overlook","p":"v.","d":"to fail to notice something","c":"忽略；忽視","s":"A: Why did the accounting department send the expense report back to me when I had already attached all the receipts last Friday? B: You forgot to sign the bottom of the form, and the manager said it is easy to overlook that small box, but the report cannot be approved without your signature.","t":"A：我上週五已經附上所有收據了，為什麼會計部門還把費用報告退回給我？ B：你忘了在表格底部簽名，經理說那個小格子很容易被【忽略】，但沒有你的簽名，報告就無法核准。"},{"w":"firmly","p":"adv.","d":"strongly and steadily","c":"用力地；堅定地","s":"A: Why did the bank clerk ask me to sign the form again when I had already written my name at the bottom of the page? B: You need to press firmly with the pen, because the form has three copies underneath, and your signature was too light to appear on the last one.","t":"A：我已經在頁面底部寫了名字，為什麼銀行行員還要我再簽一次？ B：你需要用筆【用力地】按壓，因為那份表格底下有三聯複寫，你的簽名太淡，沒有印到最後一聯。"},{"w":"digital pen","p":"n.phr.","d":"a pen-like tool for writing on a screen or tablet","c":"數位筆；觸控筆","s":"A: How do the delivery drivers collect customers' signatures now that the company has stopped using paper receipts at every door? B: Each driver carries a tablet with a digital pen, so customers can write their names on the screen, and the signature is sent to the main office right away.","t":"A：公司已經不再於每戶門口使用紙本收據，送貨司機現在要怎麼收集客戶的簽名？ B：每位司機都帶著一台附有【數位筆】的平板，客戶可以在螢幕上寫下名字，簽名會立刻傳送到總公司。"},{"w":"graphology","p":"n.","d":"the study of handwriting to learn about a person's character","c":"筆跡學","s":"A: Is it true that some companies in Europe used to study job applicants' handwriting before they decided whom to hire? B: Yes, they used graphology to guess people's personalities from their writing, but most experts now say it is not a reliable way to choose the right employees.","t":"A：聽說歐洲有些公司以前會在決定僱用誰之前，研究求職者的筆跡，是真的嗎？ B：是的，他們用【筆跡學】從字跡推測人的性格，但現在大多數專家認為這不是挑選合適員工的可靠方法。"},{"w":"outgoing","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and enjoying meeting people","c":"外向的；友善的","s":"A: The handwriting expert at the company workshop said that people with large, wide letters often enjoy meeting others, so does that describe you? B: I think so, because I'm quite outgoing, I love talking to new customers at trade fairs, and my handwriting really is big and round.","t":"A：公司工作坊的筆跡專家說，字寫得又大又寬的人通常喜歡認識別人，這符合你的情況嗎？ B：我想是的，因為我相當【外向】，很喜歡在商展上和新客戶聊天，而且我的字真的又大又圓。"},{"w":"reveal","p":"v.","d":"to show or make something known","c":"透露；顯示","s":"A: Why did the manager keep the handwritten comment cards that the guests left at the hotel restaurant last month? B: She believes the cards reveal what guests really think about the food and service, because people often write more honest opinions by hand than in online reviews.","t":"A：為什麼經理要保留上個月客人在飯店餐廳留下的手寫意見卡？ B：她認為這些卡片能【顯示】客人對餐點和服務的真實想法，因為人們手寫時常常比在網路評論中寫得更坦白。"},{"w":"intricate","p":"adj.","d":"having many small parts or details","c":"複雜精細的","s":"A: Why did it take the designer almost three weeks to finish the handwritten logo for the new coffee shop downtown? B: The owner wanted a very intricate design with many small curls and decorations, so the designer had to draw each letter slowly and carefully by hand many times.","t":"A：為什麼設計師花了將近三週，才完成市中心那家新咖啡店的手寫標誌？ B：店主想要一個帶有許多小捲曲和裝飾的【複雜精細】的設計，所以設計師必須一筆一畫慢慢、仔細地手繪每個字母很多次。"},{"w":"introverted","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and preferring to spend time alone","c":"內向的","s":"A: Why does Kevin from the IT department prefer to leave handwritten notes on our desks instead of coming over to talk to us in person? B: He is quite introverted and feels nervous speaking in front of people, so writing short notes is an easier way for him to share his ideas.","t":"A：為什麼資訊部的凱文喜歡在我們桌上留手寫紙條，而不是親自過來跟我們說話？ B：他相當【內向】，在人前說話會緊張，所以寫簡短的紙條對他來說是分享想法比較容易的方式。"},{"w":"timid","p":"adj.","d":"shy and easily frightened","c":"膽怯的；害羞的","s":"A: Why did the new trainee write her questions on a piece of paper and hand it to the supervisor after the meeting had finished? B: She was too timid to raise her hand in front of thirty experienced colleagues, but she still wanted clear answers about the new safety rules.","t":"A：為什麼那位新進受訓人員在會議結束後，把問題寫在紙上交給主管？ B：她太【膽怯】了，不敢在三十位資深同事面前舉手，但她仍然想得到關於新安全規定的明確答案。"},{"w":"emphatic","p":"adj.","d":"saying something strongly and clearly","c":"強調的；斷然的","s":"A: Did the general manager agree with the plan to replace all paper forms with an online system before the end of this year? B: No, she was very emphatic that some older customers still need paper forms, so she said both options must stay available for at least two more years.","t":"A：總經理同意在今年年底前把所有紙本表格換成線上系統的計畫嗎？ B：不，她非常【強調】有些年長客戶仍然需要紙本表格，所以她說兩種選擇都必須至少再保留兩年。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being sure of yourself","c":"自信；信心","s":"A: Why does the handwriting coach tell people to practice writing their signatures slowly before an important business meeting? B: She says a smooth and steady signature shows confidence, and clients may feel more comfortable making a deal with someone who seems calm and sure of themselves.","t":"A：為什麼書寫教練要大家在重要商務會議前慢慢練習簽名？ B：她說流暢穩定的簽名能展現【自信】，而客戶可能會更放心與看起來冷靜又有把握的人達成交易。"},{"w":"judge","p":"v.","d":"to form an opinion about someone or something","c":"評斷；判斷","s":"A: Do you think the hiring manager will look at the handwritten notes I add to my application form when she makes her decision? B: She might, but she usually tries not to judge people by their handwriting, because she cares much more about their work experience and how they perform in the interview.","t":"A：你認為招募經理做決定時，會看我在申請表上加的手寫註記嗎？ B：她可能會看，但她通常盡量不以字跡來【評斷】人，因為她更在意他們的工作經驗以及面試時的表現。"},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"working well without wasting time or energy","c":"有效率的","s":"A: Why did our office decide to use voice-typing software instead of asking the secretary to write the meeting notes by hand? B: The software is much more efficient, because it saves the secretary about two hours every week, and she can spend that time preparing reports for the directors.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室決定使用語音輸入軟體，而不是請秘書手寫會議紀錄？ B：這套軟體【有效率】得多，因為它每週可以替秘書省下大約兩個小時，她能用那些時間為主管們準備報告。"},{"w":"instantaneously","p":"adv.","d":"immediately; in a very short moment","c":"即時地；瞬間地","s":"A: How long does it take for the signed delivery form to reach the customer service team after the driver collects it at the store? B: It is sent instantaneously through the mobile app, so the team can see the customer's signature on their computer screen less than a second after the driver presses the button.","t":"A：司機在店裡收到簽好的送貨單之後，要多久才會傳到客服團隊？ B：它會透過手機應用程式【即時地】傳送，所以司機按下按鈕不到一秒，團隊就能在電腦螢幕上看到客戶的簽名。"},{"w":"obsolete","p":"adj.","d":"no longer used because something newer exists","c":"過時的；淘汰的","s":"A: Why did the office manager remove the old fax machine and the boxes of carbon paper from the storage room last weekend? B: They have become obsolete since we started using email and electronic signatures, and the space is now needed for new computers and printer supplies.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理上週末把舊傳真機和成箱的複寫紙從儲藏室搬走？ B：自從我們開始使用電子郵件和電子簽名，它們就已經【過時】了，而現在需要那個空間來放新電腦和印表機耗材。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy to reach, get or use","c":"可取得的；容易使用的","s":"A: Why did the city library scan all of its old handwritten letters and diaries and put them on its website last spring? B: The librarians wanted to make these documents accessible to students and researchers around the world, since many people could not travel to the library to see them.","t":"A：為什麼市立圖書館去年春天把所有舊的手寫信件和日記掃描並放上網站？ B：圖書館員希望讓全世界的學生和研究人員都能【取得】這些文件，因為很多人無法親自到圖書館去看。"},{"w":"rely on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to depend on someone or something","c":"依賴；依靠","s":"A: Why do you still carry a paper notebook to every client meeting when you already have a smartphone and a laptop with you? B: I don't want to rely on technology alone, because batteries can die and the internet can fail, but my notebook always works when I need to write something down.","t":"A：既然你已經隨身帶著智慧型手機和筆電，為什麼每次客戶會議還要帶紙本筆記本？ B：我不想只【依賴】科技，因為電池可能沒電、網路可能斷線，但我需要寫東西時，筆記本永遠派得上用場。"},{"w":"corner","p":"n.","d":"the place where two sides or edges meet","c":"角落；轉角","s":"A: Where should I put my signature on this delivery form, because I don't see a line marked for the customer's name? B: Please sign in the bottom right corner of the page, next to today's date, and then give the yellow copy back to the driver before he leaves.","t":"A：我應該在這張送貨單的哪裡簽名？我沒看到標示客戶姓名的欄位。 B：請在這頁右下【角】、今天日期旁邊簽名，然後在司機離開前把黃色那聯還給他。"},{"w":"perfect","p":"adj.","d":"without any mistakes; as good as possible","c":"完美的","s":"A: Why did the designer write the restaurant's menu by hand forty times before she finally sent it to the printer? B: She wanted every letter to look perfect, because the owner planned to use the menu for the grand opening, and even a small mistake would be printed on hundreds of copies.","t":"A：為什麼設計師手寫了四十次餐廳菜單，才終於送去印刷？ B：她希望每個字母看起來都很【完美】，因為老闆打算在盛大開幕時使用這份菜單，即使一個小錯誤也會被印在數百份上。"},{"w":"attached","p":"adj.","d":"feeling love or strong liking for something","c":"依戀的；有感情的","s":"A: Why does our boss still use that old fountain pen when the company gives everyone free ballpoint pens every year? B: She is very attached to it, because her father gave it to her on her first day of work, and she has signed every important contract with it since then.","t":"A：公司每年都免費發原子筆給大家，為什麼我們老闆還在用那支舊鋼筆？ B：她對它非常【依戀】，因為那是她父親在她第一天上班時送她的，從那之後她就用它簽下每一份重要的合約。"}]},{"unit":166,"theme":"Happiness 快樂","cards":[{"w":"joy","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great happiness","c":"喜悅；歡樂","s":"A: How did the new manager react when she heard that our small design team had won the national advertising award for the coffee campaign we worked on all spring? B: She jumped up from her desk with joy and immediately invited everyone to a celebration dinner at the Italian restaurant across the street.","t":"A：當新經理聽到我們的小設計團隊以整個春天製作的咖啡廣告贏得全國廣告獎時，她有什麼反應？ B：她【欣喜】地從座位上跳起來，馬上邀請大家到對街的義大利餐廳吃慶功晚餐。"},{"w":"delight","p":"n.","d":"great pleasure or happiness","c":"欣喜；高興","s":"A: Did the visitors from our Tokyo office like the tour of the factory and the local night market that you organized for them yesterday? B: Yes, to my delight, they said it was the best part of their trip, and they even asked for the names of the food stalls so they could visit again next year.","t":"A：東京辦公室的訪客喜歡你昨天為他們安排的工廠參觀和當地夜市行程嗎？ B：是的，令我【高興】的是，他們說那是這趟旅程最棒的部分，甚至還問了那些小吃攤的名字，好讓明年可以再去。"},{"w":"pleasure","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of enjoyment; an honor","c":"愉快；榮幸","s":"A: Ms. Lin, could you say a few words to welcome our new partners from Singapore before the dinner starts at seven o'clock this evening? B: Of course, it would be a pleasure to speak, because I worked with their sales team last year and I know how much effort they put into this agreement.","t":"A：林小姐，今晚七點晚宴開始前，可以請妳說幾句話歡迎我們來自新加坡的新夥伴嗎？ B：當然，能致詞是我的【榮幸】，因為我去年和他們的業務團隊合作過，知道他們為這份協議付出了多少心力。"},{"w":"contentment","p":"n.","d":"a calm feeling of being happy with what you have","c":"滿足；知足","s":"A: Why did your uncle decide to leave his high-paying job at the bank and open a small bookshop in the countryside last year? B: He said that money never gave him real contentment, and now he feels calm and happy every morning when he opens the shop and chats with his regular customers.","t":"A：你叔叔去年為什麼決定辭掉銀行的高薪工作，到鄉下開一家小書店？ B：他說金錢從來沒有帶給他真正的【滿足】，現在他每天早上開店、和常客聊天時，都覺得平靜又快樂。"},{"w":"satisfaction","p":"n.","d":"the good feeling when you get what you wanted","c":"滿意；滿足","s":"A: Why does the hotel ask every guest to fill out a short online survey after they check out at the front desk? B: The general manager wants to measure customer satisfaction, so she reads the comments every week and uses them to improve the rooms, the breakfast menu, and the staff training program.","t":"A：為什麼飯店要請每位房客在櫃檯退房後填寫一份簡短的線上問卷？ B：總經理想要衡量顧客【滿意度】，所以她每週閱讀意見，並用來改善客房、早餐菜單和員工訓練計畫。"},{"w":"bliss","p":"n.","d":"perfect happiness","c":"極樂；無比幸福","s":"A: How was your week off at the beach resort after you finished that stressful project for the marketing department last month? B: It was pure bliss, because I turned off my work phone, read three novels by the pool, and enjoyed fresh seafood every evening while watching the sun go down over the ocean.","t":"A：上個月你完成行銷部那個壓力很大的專案後，在海灘度假村休假一週感覺如何？ B：真是無比【幸福】，因為我關掉了工作手機，在泳池邊讀了三本小說，每天傍晚一邊看海上夕陽一邊享用新鮮海鮮。"},{"w":"cheerfulness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being happy and friendly","c":"愉快；開朗","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner give the young waiter an award at the staff meeting even though he has only worked there for three months? B: The owner said his cheerfulness makes customers feel welcome, and many diners have written online reviews mentioning his friendly greetings and warm attitude during busy lunch hours.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳老闆在員工會議上頒獎給那位年輕服務生，即使他才在那裡工作三個月？ B：老闆說他的【開朗】讓顧客感到賓至如歸，很多用餐客人都在網路評論中提到他在忙碌午餐時段親切的招呼和溫暖的態度。"},{"w":"well-being","p":"n.","d":"the state of being healthy and happy","c":"幸福；身心健康","s":"A: Why has the human resources department started offering free yoga classes and quiet rest areas on the fifth floor of our building? B: The company wants to improve employee well-being, because a recent survey showed that many workers felt tired and stressed after long hours in front of their computers.","t":"A：為什麼人資部開始在我們大樓五樓提供免費瑜伽課和安靜的休息區？ B：公司想提升員工的【身心健康】，因為最近一項調查顯示，許多員工長時間坐在電腦前後感到疲倦和壓力。"},{"w":"optimism","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that good things will happen","c":"樂觀","s":"A: Do the investors still believe in our new electric scooter even though sales were lower than expected in the first quarter of the year? B: Yes, there is a lot of optimism at the head office, because orders from schools and delivery companies have increased steadily since we lowered the price in April.","t":"A：即使今年第一季銷售低於預期，投資人仍然看好我們的新電動機車嗎？ B：是的，總公司充滿【樂觀】的氣氛，因為自從我們四月降價後，來自學校和快遞公司的訂單穩定增加。"},{"w":"gratitude","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being thankful","c":"感激；感謝","s":"A: What did the hospital director say to the volunteers at the end-of-year party held in the main hall last Friday evening? B: She expressed her deep gratitude for their hard work, explaining that their help at the information desk had made waiting much easier for patients and their families.","t":"A：上週五晚上在大廳舉辦的年終派對上，醫院院長對志工們說了什麼？ B：她對他們的辛勞表達深深的【感激】，並說明他們在服務台的協助讓病患和家屬等候時輕鬆許多。"},{"w":"fulfillment","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of satisfaction from doing something important","c":"成就感；滿足感","s":"A: Why did you leave your job in advertising to become a nurse at the children's hospital, even though the hours are much longer? B: I wanted more fulfillment in my career, and now I feel truly useful every day when I help young patients and their worried parents through difficult times.","t":"A：雖然工時長很多，你為什麼還是離開廣告業，到兒童醫院當護理師？ B：我希望在職涯中得到更多【成就感】，現在我每天幫助年幼的病人和擔心的父母度過難關時，都覺得自己真正有用。"},{"w":"enjoy","p":"v.","d":"to get pleasure from something","c":"享受；喜歡","s":"A: Did the clients from Germany like the welcome lunch at the seafood restaurant near the harbor before our meeting started? B: They seemed to enjoy every dish very much, and their manager even asked the chef for the recipe for the grilled fish so that he could try cooking it at home.","t":"A：德國客戶喜歡會議開始前在港口附近海鮮餐廳的歡迎午餐嗎？ B：他們似乎非常【享受】每一道菜，他們的經理甚至向主廚要了烤魚的食譜，想回家試著做做看。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be thankful for something","c":"感激；感謝","s":"A: Should I send a thank-you note to the IT staff who stayed late on Saturday to repair the network before our online product launch? B: Yes, I think they would really appreciate a short message from you, especially because they gave up their weekend plans to make sure everything worked smoothly.","t":"A：我該寄感謝信給週六留到很晚、在我們線上產品發表前修好網路的資訊人員嗎？ B：是的，我想他們會很【感激】收到你的簡短訊息，尤其他們放棄了週末計畫，確保一切順利運作。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable for a special event or success","c":"慶祝","s":"A: What are we planning to do now that our branch has finally reached its sales target for the whole year two months early? B: The regional manager wants to celebrate with a buffet dinner at a nice hotel downtown, and she will also give every team member a small bonus and a gift card.","t":"A：既然我們分公司終於提早兩個月達成全年業績目標，我們打算做什麼？ B：區域經理想在市中心一家不錯的飯店舉辦自助晚餐來【慶祝】，她還會給每位團隊成員一點獎金和一張禮物卡。"},{"w":"smile","p":"v.","d":"to make a happy expression with your mouth","c":"微笑","s":"A: What advice did the trainer give the new receptionists during their first week at the front desk of the hotel? B: She told them to smile and make eye contact when guests arrive, because a friendly face helps tired travelers feel welcome after a long flight or a difficult drive.","t":"A：新接待員在飯店櫃檯的第一週，訓練員給了他們什麼建議？ B：她要他們在客人抵達時【微笑】並保持眼神接觸，因為一張友善的臉能讓長途飛行或辛苦開車後的疲憊旅客感到受歡迎。"},{"w":"laugh","p":"v.","d":"to make sounds that show you think something is funny","c":"笑；大笑","s":"A: How did the audience respond to the sales director's speech at the annual conference in the convention center yesterday afternoon? B: Everyone started to laugh when she told a funny story about losing her luggage in Paris, and after that the room felt much more relaxed during the serious part of the talk.","t":"A：昨天下午在會議中心的年會上，聽眾對業務總監的演講有什麼反應？ B：她講到在巴黎弄丟行李的趣事時，大家都【笑】了起來，之後在演講嚴肅的部分，現場氣氛也輕鬆多了。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and become calm","c":"放鬆","s":"A: What do you usually do on Sunday afternoons after working long hours at the accounting firm during the busy tax season? B: I like to relax at a quiet café near my apartment, where I drink tea, read a magazine, and forget about the numbers and deadlines for a few hours.","t":"A：報稅旺季在會計師事務所長時間工作後，你週日下午通常做什麼？ B：我喜歡在公寓附近一家安靜的咖啡館【放鬆】，喝喝茶、看看雜誌，暫時忘掉數字和截止期限幾個小時。"},{"w":"savor","p":"v.","d":"to enjoy something slowly","c":"細細品味；品嚐","s":"A: Why did the travel agency add a three-hour lunch stop in the small mountain village to the tour schedule for our clients? B: The guide wanted the guests to savor the local dishes slowly, because the village is famous for its fresh mushrooms, homemade noodles, and a special tea that grows nearby.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社在我們客戶的行程中，加了在小山村停留三小時的午餐？ B：導遊希望客人能慢慢【品嚐】當地菜餚，因為這個村莊以新鮮蘑菇、手工麵條和附近種植的特色茶聞名。"},{"w":"positive","p":"adj.","d":"good, hopeful or approving","c":"正面的；積極的","s":"A: How did the customers react to the new mobile app that our company released for ordering food and drinks last week? B: The feedback was mostly positive, because users said the design is simple, payment is fast, and they can easily collect reward points every time they order a coffee.","t":"A：顧客對我們公司上週推出的點餐飲手機應用程式有什麼反應？ B：回饋大多是【正面的】，因為使用者說設計簡單、付款快速，而且每次點咖啡都能輕鬆累積點數。"},{"w":"cheerful","p":"adj.","d":"happy and friendly","c":"愉快的；開朗的","s":"A: Why do so many regular customers prefer to visit the bakery on Main Street even though it is a little more expensive than the supermarket? B: The owner is always cheerful and remembers everyone's name, and she often gives children a free cookie while their parents choose bread for the week.","t":"A：為什麼許多常客寧願去大街上的麵包店，即使它比超市貴一點？ B：老闆總是很【開朗】，記得每個人的名字，而且常在家長挑選一週麵包時送孩子一塊免費餅乾。"},{"w":"joyful","p":"adj.","d":"very happy","c":"喜悅的；歡樂的","s":"A: What was the mood like at the company party after the CEO announced that every employee would receive an extra week of paid vacation? B: It was a very joyful evening, because people were dancing, taking photos together, and already planning trips to the beach or the mountains with their families.","t":"A：執行長宣布每位員工將多一週帶薪假後，公司派對的氣氛如何？ B：那是個非常【歡樂的】夜晚，大家跳舞、一起拍照，而且已經在計畫和家人去海邊或山上旅行。"},{"w":"content","p":"adj.","d":"happy and satisfied with what you have","c":"滿足的；知足的","s":"A: Has your sister applied for the manager position at the department store, since she has worked there for almost ten years now? B: No, she is content with her current role in the shoe department, because the hours are flexible and she can pick up her children from school every afternoon.","t":"A：你姊姊已經在百貨公司工作快十年了，她有應徵經理職位嗎？ B：沒有，她對目前在鞋類部門的職務感到很【滿足】，因為工時彈性，她每天下午都能去學校接孩子。"},{"w":"grateful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling thankful","c":"感激的","s":"A: How did the new interns feel about the training program that the senior engineers prepared for them during their first month? B: They were very grateful for the extra help, because the engineers explained the software step by step and answered every question patiently, even during the busiest weeks.","t":"A：新實習生對資深工程師在他們第一個月準備的訓練課程有什麼感受？ B：他們非常【感激】這些額外的幫助，因為工程師一步步解說軟體，即使在最忙的幾週也耐心回答每個問題。"},{"w":"satisfied","p":"adj.","d":"pleased because you got what you wanted","c":"滿意的","s":"A: Was the client happy with the new website design that our team delivered on Monday after two months of hard work? B: She said she was completely satisfied with the result, and she has already asked us to create a matching online store and a mobile app for her company next year.","t":"A：客戶喜歡我們團隊辛苦兩個月後在週一交出的新網站設計嗎？ B：她說她對成果完全【滿意】，而且已經請我們明年為她的公司製作搭配的網路商店和手機應用程式。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"calm and quiet","c":"寧靜的；平靜的","s":"A: Why did you choose the small guesthouse by the lake instead of the big hotel in the city center for the management retreat? B: The location is very peaceful, so the managers can think clearly without traffic noise, and they can also walk around the lake during breaks between meetings.","t":"A：管理層的靜修活動，你為什麼選湖邊的小民宿，而不是市中心的大飯店？ B：那裡的環境非常【寧靜】，主管們可以在沒有車聲的情況下清楚思考，會議休息時也能繞著湖散步。"},{"w":"excited","p":"adj.","d":"very happy and eager about something","c":"興奮的","s":"A: How does the sales team feel about the trip to the international trade show in Las Vegas next month? B: They are really excited about it, because they will meet hundreds of potential buyers, see the newest products, and stay in a famous hotel with a large swimming pool.","t":"A：業務團隊對下個月去拉斯維加斯參加國際貿易展有什麼感覺？ B：他們真的很【興奮】，因為他們將見到數百位潛在買家、看到最新產品，還會住在一家有大游泳池的知名飯店。"},{"w":"happily","p":"adv.","d":"in a happy way; willingly","c":"快樂地；欣然地","s":"A: Did the children enjoy the company family day at the science museum that the human resources team organized last Saturday? B: Yes, they played happily with the robots and experiments all morning, and many parents said it was the best event the company has held in years.","t":"A：孩子們喜歡人資團隊上週六在科學博物館舉辦的公司家庭日嗎？ B：喜歡，他們整個早上都【快樂地】玩機器人和做實驗，很多家長說這是公司多年來辦過最棒的活動。"},{"w":"cheerfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a happy and friendly way","c":"愉快地；欣然地","s":"A: How did the hotel staff respond when the tour group arrived three hours late because their flight from Bangkok was delayed? B: The receptionists cheerfully welcomed everyone with cold drinks and hot towels, and they quickly handed out room keys so the tired guests could rest before dinner.","t":"A：旅行團因為曼谷航班延誤晚了三小時抵達，飯店員工如何應對？ B：接待員【愉快地】以冷飲和熱毛巾迎接大家，並迅速發放房卡，讓疲憊的客人能在晚餐前休息。"},{"w":"gratefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a thankful way","c":"感激地","s":"A: What happened when the old man dropped his shopping bags at the bus stop outside our office during the heavy rain this morning? B: Two of our security guards ran out to help him pick everything up, and he gratefully accepted an umbrella from them before he got on the bus home.","t":"A：今天早上下大雨時，那位老先生在我們辦公室外的公車站掉了購物袋，後來怎麼了？ B：我們兩位保全跑出去幫他把東西撿起來，他上公車回家前【感激地】收下了他們給的雨傘。"},{"w":"warmly","p":"adv.","d":"in a friendly and kind way","c":"熱情地；親切地","s":"A: How were you treated when you visited the supplier's factory in Vietnam for the first time last month? B: The owner and his staff welcomed me very warmly, showed me every part of the production line, and even invited me to a family dinner with traditional dishes from their region.","t":"A：上個月你第一次參觀越南供應商的工廠時，受到怎樣的接待？ B：老闆和員工非常【熱情地】歡迎我，帶我看了生產線的每個部分，甚至邀請我參加有當地傳統菜餚的家庭晚餐。"},{"w":"enthusiastically","p":"adv.","d":"with great interest and excitement","c":"熱情地；熱烈地","s":"A: How did the staff react when the manager suggested a weekly running club after work in the park next to our office? B: Most of them agreed enthusiastically, and more than twenty people signed up on the first day, including several senior managers who had never joined a sports group before.","t":"A：經理提議下班後在辦公室旁的公園成立每週跑步社時，員工有什麼反應？ B：大多數人都【熱烈地】贊成，第一天就有二十多人報名，其中包括幾位從未參加過運動社團的資深主管。"},{"w":"calmly","p":"adv.","d":"in a quiet way, without worry or anger","c":"冷靜地；平靜地","s":"A: What did the flight attendant do when the plane suddenly shook during the storm over the mountains on our business trip? B: She calmly explained the situation over the speaker, asked everyone to fasten their seat belts, and then walked down the aisle to check on passengers who looked nervous.","t":"A：我們出差時，飛機在山區上空遇到暴風雨突然搖晃，空服員做了什麼？ B：她透過廣播【冷靜地】說明狀況，請大家繫好安全帶，然後走過走道查看看起來緊張的乘客。"},{"w":"positively","p":"adv.","d":"in a good or approving way","c":"正面地；積極地","s":"A: How did the board of directors respond to your proposal to open a second branch in the new shopping mall downtown next year? B: They reacted very positively, because my report showed strong demand in that area, and they asked me to prepare a detailed budget before their next meeting in March.","t":"A：董事會對你明年在市中心新購物中心開設第二家分店的提案有什麼回應？ B：他們的反應非常【正面】，因為我的報告顯示該區需求強勁，他們請我在三月的下次會議前準備詳細預算。"},{"w":"brightly","p":"adv.","d":"in a happy, lively way; with strong light or color","c":"燦爛地；明亮地","s":"A: How did the new receptionist greet the customers who came to the bank on her very first morning at work? B: She smiled brightly at every visitor, asked how she could help them, and quickly guided them to the correct counter, which impressed both her manager and the regular customers.","t":"A：新接待員上班第一天早上，如何招呼來銀行的顧客？ B：她對每位訪客【燦爛地】微笑，詢問能如何協助，並迅速引導他們到正確的櫃檯，讓主管和常客都留下深刻印象。"}]},{"unit":167,"theme":"Hats 帽子","cards":[{"w":"cap","p":"n.","d":"a soft hat with a hard curved part at the front","c":"鴨舌帽；便帽","s":"A: What kind of gift should we give the volunteers who help at the charity run in the park next Saturday morning? B: Let's order a blue baseball cap with our logo on the front, because it is cheap, easy to carry, and will keep the sun out of their eyes while they work.","t":"A：下週六早上在公園舉辦的慈善路跑，我們應該送什麼禮物給幫忙的志工？ B：我們訂一頂前面印有公司標誌的藍色棒球【帽】吧，因為它便宜、方便攜帶，而且在他們工作時可以替眼睛遮擋陽光。"},{"w":"beanie","p":"n.","d":"a small, close-fitting knitted hat without a brim","c":"毛線帽；無邊便帽","s":"A: I'm flying to Sapporo for the trade fair next week, and the weather report says it will snow every day. What should I pack? B: Bring a thick coat, gloves, and a wool beanie to cover your ears, because the wind is very cold when you walk between the hotel and the exhibition hall.","t":"A：我下週要飛去札幌參加商展，氣象報告說每天都會下雪。我應該帶什麼？ B：帶件厚外套、手套和一頂能蓋住耳朵的羊毛【毛線帽】，因為你在飯店和展覽館之間走路時風非常冷。"},{"w":"beret","p":"n.","d":"a round, flat, soft hat, often made of wool","c":"貝雷帽","s":"A: The fashion magazine wants a photo of our new autumn collection that looks French and artistic. Do you have any ideas for the model's outfit? B: Let's give her a striped shirt, a long coat, and a red beret worn slightly to one side, because that simple look reminds most readers of Paris.","t":"A：時尚雜誌想要一張看起來有法式藝術感的秋季新系列照片。你對模特兒的服裝有什麼想法嗎？ B：我們讓她穿條紋襯衫、長大衣，再戴一頂稍微斜戴的紅色【貝雷帽】，因為這種簡單的造型會讓大多數讀者聯想到巴黎。"},{"w":"fedora","p":"n.","d":"a soft felt hat with a brim and a dent in the top","c":"紳士帽；軟呢帽","s":"A: The theater company needs costumes for its new play about a detective in 1940s New York. What should the main actor wear on stage? B: He should have a long gray raincoat and a brown fedora pulled low over his eyes, since that was the classic style for men in that period.","t":"A：劇團需要為新戲準備服裝，故事講的是1940年代紐約的一名偵探。主角在舞台上應該穿什麼？ B：他應該穿一件灰色長風衣，戴一頂壓低到眼睛的咖啡色【紳士帽】，因為那是那個年代男士的經典打扮。"},{"w":"helmet","p":"n.","d":"a hard hat that protects your head","c":"安全帽；頭盔","s":"A: Can visitors walk around the construction site after the meeting with the engineers this afternoon? B: Yes, but everyone must put on a safety helmet and a bright vest at the entrance gate, because tools and heavy building materials sometimes fall from the upper floors without warning.","t":"A：今天下午和工程師開完會後，訪客可以在工地裡走動嗎？ B：可以，但每個人都必須在入口大門戴上安全【頭盔】並穿上亮色背心，因為工具和沉重的建材有時會毫無預警地從樓上掉下來。"},{"w":"visor","p":"n.","d":"a hat with only a curved front part to shade the eyes and no top","c":"遮陽帽（無頂）；帽舌","s":"A: Our tennis club is choosing new uniforms for the summer tournament. Should players use full caps or something lighter? B: I think a white visor is better, because it shades their eyes from the strong sun but leaves the top of the head open, so they won't feel too hot.","t":"A：我們網球俱樂部正在為夏季錦標賽挑選新制服。球員應該用全罩式的帽子，還是更輕便的？ B：我覺得白色【無頂遮陽帽】比較好，因為它能替眼睛擋住強烈的陽光，但頭頂是露出來的，所以他們不會覺得太熱。"},{"w":"brim","p":"n.","d":"the flat edge around the bottom of a hat that sticks out","c":"帽簷；帽緣","s":"A: Which of these summer hats would you recommend for the staff who guide tourists around the outdoor market all day? B: Choose the straw one with the wide brim, because it shades the face, neck, and shoulders much better than a small cap, and the guides spend hours in the sun.","t":"A：這些夏季帽子中，你會推薦哪一種給整天帶遊客逛戶外市場的員工？ B：選那頂有寬【帽簷】的草帽，因為它比小鴨舌帽更能遮住臉、脖子和肩膀，而導遊們要在太陽下待好幾個小時。"},{"w":"crown","p":"n.","d":"the top part of a hat","c":"帽頂","s":"A: A customer returned this hat to the store yesterday and asked for a refund. Do you know what the problem was? B: She said the crown was too high and stiff, so the hat looked strange on her head and didn't fit well inside her car when she was driving.","t":"A：昨天有位顧客把這頂帽子退回店裡並要求退款。你知道問題出在哪裡嗎？ B：她說【帽頂】太高又太硬，所以帽子戴在她頭上看起來很奇怪，開車時在車裡也很不方便。"},{"w":"headgear","p":"n.","d":"things that people wear on their heads, such as hats and helmets","c":"頭部裝備；帽類","s":"A: The factory manager wants to update the safety rules before the new production line opens next month. What should we include? B: We should say that all workers must wear proper headgear, such as hard hats or hair covers, whenever they are near the machines or the packing area.","t":"A：工廠經理想在下個月新生產線啟用前更新安全規定。我們應該納入哪些內容？ B：我們應該規定所有工人只要靠近機器或包裝區，就必須戴上適當的【頭部裝備】，例如安全帽或髮罩。"},{"w":"sunhat","p":"n.","d":"a hat with a wide brim worn to protect you from the sun","c":"遮陽帽","s":"A: I'm planning the company beach day for next month. What should we remind everyone to bring so they don't get sunburned? B: Tell them to pack sunscreen, sunglasses, and a sunhat with a wide edge, because there are very few trees on that beach and the afternoon sun is very strong.","t":"A：我正在規劃下個月的公司海灘日。我們該提醒大家帶什麼才不會曬傷？ B：告訴他們帶防曬乳、太陽眼鏡和一頂寬邊的【遮陽帽】，因為那片海灘幾乎沒有樹，下午的陽光又非常強。"},{"w":"sombrero","p":"n.","d":"a Mexican hat with a very wide brim and a tall top","c":"墨西哥寬邊帽","s":"A: The restaurant is holding a Mexican food festival next weekend. How can we make the dining room look more fun and festive? B: We could hang colorful flags from the ceiling and give each waiter a large straw sombrero to put on, because customers love taking photos with traditional costumes.","t":"A：餐廳下週末要舉辦墨西哥美食節。我們要怎麼讓用餐區看起來更有趣、更有節慶氣氛？ B：我們可以在天花板掛上彩色旗子，並讓每位服務生戴上一頂大大的草編【墨西哥寬邊帽】，因為顧客很喜歡跟傳統服裝拍照。"},{"w":"top hat","p":"n.","d":"a tall, black, formal hat with a flat top, worn by men","c":"高頂禮帽；大禮帽","s":"A: The hotel is hosting a Victorian-themed wedding on Saturday. What will the groom and his friends wear for the photos? B: They have rented black suits with long jackets, and each man will carry a tall top hat, which makes them look like gentlemen from nineteenth-century London.","t":"A：飯店星期六要舉辦一場維多利亞主題的婚禮。新郎和他的朋友拍照時會穿什麼？ B：他們租了附長版外套的黑色西裝，每位男士還會拿著一頂高高的【高頂禮帽】，讓他們看起來像十九世紀倫敦的紳士。"},{"w":"bowler","p":"n.","d":"a hard, round black hat with a narrow brim","c":"圓頂禮帽","s":"A: Why does the old bank on Main Street have a picture of a man in a black suit and round hat in its lobby? B: That is the bank's founder, and he always wore a bowler to work, so the company still uses that hard round hat in its logo today.","t":"A：為什麼大街上那家老銀行的大廳掛著一張穿黑西裝、戴圓帽的男士照片？ B：那是銀行的創辦人，他上班總是戴著一頂【圓頂禮帽】，所以公司到今天仍在標誌中使用那頂硬挺的圓帽。"},{"w":"snapback","p":"n.","d":"a baseball cap with a flat brim and an adjustable strap at the back","c":"平簷可調式棒球帽","s":"A: The sports shop wants to attract more young customers this season. Which new product should we put in the front window? B: Let's display the snapback with the flat brim and the team logo, because teenagers like how the strap at the back can fit any head size.","t":"A：運動用品店這一季想吸引更多年輕顧客。我們應該把哪一項新商品放在前面的櫥窗？ B：我們來展示那頂有平帽簷和球隊標誌的【平簷可調式棒球帽】吧，因為青少年喜歡後面的扣帶能調整成任何頭圍。"},{"w":"hood","p":"n.","d":"a part of a coat or jacket that you can pull up to cover your head","c":"兜帽；連帽","s":"A: It suddenly started raining during our walk to the client's office, and I don't have an umbrella with me. What should I do? B: Just pull up the hood of your jacket to keep your hair dry, and we can buy an umbrella at the convenience store on the next corner.","t":"A：我們走去客戶辦公室的路上突然下起雨，我身上沒帶傘。我該怎麼辦？ B：先把外套的【兜帽】拉起來讓頭髮保持乾燥，我們可以在下個轉角的便利商店買把傘。"},{"w":"band","p":"n.","d":"a strip of material around the bottom of a hat's top part","c":"帽帶","s":"A: Our hat shop wants to offer something special for customers who buy hats as birthday presents. Any suggestions? B: We could let them choose a colored ribbon band to go around the hat and print the person's name on it, which would make every gift feel personal and unique.","t":"A：我們的帽子店想為買帽子當生日禮物的顧客提供特別服務。有什麼建議嗎？ B：我們可以讓他們挑一條彩色緞帶【帽帶】繫在帽子上，並把收禮人的名字印在上面，讓每份禮物都更有個人特色、獨一無二。"},{"w":"lining","p":"n.","d":"a layer of material on the inside of a hat or piece of clothing","c":"內襯；襯裡","s":"A: Why are these winter hats more expensive than the ones on the other shelf, even though they look almost the same? B: These have a soft silk lining inside, so they don't make your head itch, and they keep you warmer when you wait outside for the bus.","t":"A：為什麼這些冬帽比另一個架上的貴，明明看起來幾乎一樣？ B：這些帽子裡面有一層柔軟的絲質【內襯】，所以戴了頭不會癢，而且在外面等公車時也比較保暖。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look more attractive by adding things to it","c":"裝飾","s":"A: The children's hospital has asked our staff to help with its spring party next Friday. What will the volunteers do? B: We will help the young patients decorate paper hats with stickers, feathers, and colored pens, and then everyone will wear them during the party in the main hall.","t":"A：兒童醫院請我們的員工幫忙下週五的春季派對。志工要做什麼？ B：我們會幫小病患用貼紙、羽毛和彩色筆【裝飾】紙帽，然後大家在大廳派對時都會戴上。"},{"w":"wear","p":"v.","d":"to have clothing, a hat, glasses, etc. on your body","c":"穿；戴","s":"A: The weather forecast says it will be extremely hot during the outdoor company sports day this Saturday. How can staff stay safe? B: Everyone should wear a hat, drink plenty of water, and rest in the shade between games, because last year two people felt sick after standing in the sun too long.","t":"A：氣象預報說這週六戶外公司運動會期間會非常熱。員工要怎麼保持安全？ B：每個人都應該【戴】帽子、多喝水，並在比賽之間到陰涼處休息，因為去年有兩個人在太陽下站太久後身體不適。"},{"w":"tilt","p":"v.","d":"to move something so that one side is higher than the other","c":"使傾斜；斜戴","s":"A: The photographer says the model's face looks too dark under her hat in these pictures for the catalog. How can we fix it? B: Ask her to tilt the hat slightly back and to one side, so more light can reach her eyes and the camera can show her smile clearly.","t":"A：攝影師說在這些型錄照片中，模特兒的臉在帽子下看起來太暗。我們要怎麼解決？ B：請她把帽子稍微往後、往一側【傾斜】，這樣更多光線能照到她的眼睛，相機也能清楚拍出她的笑容。"},{"w":"remove","p":"v.","d":"to take something off or away","c":"脫下；移除","s":"A: I'm taking our foreign visitors to the temple and then to a traditional restaurant tomorrow. Is there anything they should know about local manners? B: Please remind them to remove their hats and shoes before entering the main hall, because this is a sign of respect, and staff there will politely ask them to do it.","t":"A：我明天要帶外國訪客去寺廟，然後去一家傳統餐廳。有什麼當地禮儀是他們應該知道的嗎？ B：請提醒他們進入大殿前要【脫下】帽子和鞋子，因為這是尊重的表現，那裡的工作人員也會禮貌地請他們這麼做。"},{"w":"adjust","p":"v.","d":"to change something slightly so that it fits or works better","c":"調整","s":"A: My new bicycle helmet keeps moving around on my head when I ride to the office in the morning. Should I return it to the shop? B: Before you do that, try to adjust the strap under your chin and the small wheel at the back, so the helmet fits more tightly and stays in place.","t":"A：我早上騎車上班時，新的自行車安全帽一直在頭上晃動。我應該把它退回店裡嗎？ B：在那之前，試著【調整】下巴下方的帶子和後面的小轉輪，讓安全帽更貼合、固定在位置上。"},{"w":"stylish","p":"adj.","d":"fashionable and attractive","c":"時髦的；有型的","s":"A: I need a hat for my cousin's garden wedding next month, but I don't want to look too old-fashioned. What do you think of this one? B: That cream hat with the thin black ribbon is very stylish, and it will match both your blue dress and your new shoes perfectly.","t":"A：我下個月表妹的花園婚禮需要一頂帽子，但我不想看起來太老派。你覺得這頂怎麼樣？ B：那頂繫著細黑緞帶的米白色帽子非常【時髦】，而且跟你的藍色洋裝和新鞋都會非常搭。"},{"w":"fashionable","p":"adj.","d":"popular at a particular time; in fashion","c":"流行的；時尚的","s":"A: Our hat sales dropped a lot last winter, even though the prices were lower than our competitors'. What went wrong? B: Many customers told us that our designs were no longer fashionable, because young people now prefer simple knitted styles in neutral colors instead of bright patterns.","t":"A：去年冬天我們的帽子銷量大跌，即使價格比競爭對手低。哪裡出了問題？ B：許多顧客告訴我們，我們的設計已經不【流行】了，因為現在年輕人比較喜歡中性色的簡約針織款，而不是鮮豔的圖案。"},{"w":"casual","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not formal; suitable for everyday use","c":"休閒的；隨意的","s":"A: Is it OK to come to the office in jeans and a baseball cap on Friday, or should I dress like I do on Monday? B: Fridays are casual days here, so jeans and a cap are fine, unless you have a meeting with clients, and then you should put on a jacket.","t":"A：星期五可以穿牛仔褲、戴棒球帽來辦公室嗎，還是應該像星期一那樣穿？ B：這裡星期五是【休閒】日，所以牛仔褲和鴨舌帽都沒問題，除非你要跟客戶開會，那就該穿上外套。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"suitable for serious or official occasions","c":"正式的","s":"A: The invitation to the company's anniversary dinner at the Grand Hotel says 'black tie.' What does that mean for the guests? B: It means the dress code is very formal, so men should wear dark suits with bow ties, and women usually choose long evening dresses.","t":"A：大飯店公司週年晚宴的邀請函上寫著「black tie」。這對賓客來說是什麼意思？ B：意思是服裝規定非常【正式】，所以男士應該穿深色西裝配領結，女士通常會選擇長版晚禮服。"},{"w":"protective","p":"adj.","d":"designed to keep someone safe from harm","c":"防護的；保護的","s":"A: The new warehouse workers will start operating the forklifts next week. What equipment should we order for them? B: Please order protective gear, including hard hats, gloves, and steel-toed boots, because the safety inspector will check everything before the warehouse opens.","t":"A：新的倉庫員工下週要開始操作堆高機。我們應該為他們訂購哪些裝備？ B：請訂購【防護】裝備，包括安全帽、手套和鋼頭靴，因為安全檢查員會在倉庫啟用前檢查所有東西。"},{"w":"warm","p":"adj.","d":"keeping you from feeling cold","c":"保暖的；溫暖的","s":"A: Our team is going to the mountains to visit a tea farm next month, and the temperature at night drops below zero. What should we bring? B: Pack a warm wool hat and thick gloves, because the guesthouse is old and the heating in the rooms doesn't always work well at night.","t":"A：我們團隊下個月要去山上參訪茶園，晚上氣溫會降到零度以下。我們該帶什麼？ B：帶一頂【保暖】的羊毛帽和厚手套，因為民宿很舊，房間裡的暖氣晚上不一定好用。"},{"w":"decorative","p":"adj.","d":"made to look attractive rather than to be useful","c":"裝飾性的","s":"A: Why are these small hats on the shelf so cheap? They are too tiny to fit anyone's head. B: They are only decorative items, so people put them on dolls or hang them on the wall at home, and many tourists buy them as souvenirs of the hat museum.","t":"A：為什麼架上這些小帽子這麼便宜？它們小到沒有人戴得下。 B：它們只是【裝飾性的】物品，所以人們會把它們放在娃娃身上或掛在家裡牆上，很多遊客也會買來當作帽子博物館的紀念品。"},{"w":"comfortably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that feels pleasant and relaxed","c":"舒適地","s":"A: The delivery drivers complain that their old caps feel tight and give them headaches after a long day on the road. Can we help them? B: Let's buy the new caps with soft stretchy bands, which fit comfortably even after eight hours, and the drivers can try them before we order more.","t":"A：送貨司機抱怨舊的鴨舌帽太緊，在路上跑了一整天後會頭痛。我們能幫他們嗎？ B：我們買那種有柔軟彈性帽帶的新帽子，即使戴八小時也很【舒適地】貼合頭部，而且司機可以在我們加訂之前先試戴。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"firmly, so that it will not move or fall","c":"牢固地；穩固地","s":"A: The wind on the boat tour can be very strong, and last week a tourist lost her hat in the sea. How can we prevent this? B: Let's give guests a hat clip and tell them to fasten the chin strap securely before the boat leaves the harbor, so their hats stay on.","t":"A：遊船行程上的風可能很強，上週有位遊客的帽子掉進海裡。我們要怎麼避免這種事？ B：我們發給乘客帽夾，並告訴他們在船離開港口前把下巴帶【牢固地】扣好，這樣帽子就不會被吹走。"},{"w":"fashionably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is stylish and popular","c":"時髦地","s":"A: The new manager always looks so smart when she arrives at the office, even on rainy days. How does she do it? B: She dresses fashionably but simply, usually with a long coat and a neat felt hat, and she says she plans her outfits the night before.","t":"A：新經理每次到辦公室都看起來很體面，即使是下雨天。她是怎麼做到的？ B：她穿著【時髦】但簡單，通常是一件長大衣配一頂整齊的毛氈帽，她說她前一晚就會規劃好服裝。"},{"w":"properly","p":"adv.","d":"correctly; in the right way","c":"正確地；適當地","s":"A: Our safety report shows that several workers were hurt last month even though they had helmets. How is that possible? B: Many of them did not wear the helmets properly, because they left the chin straps open, so the helmets fell off when something hit them.","t":"A：我們的安全報告顯示，上個月有幾名工人雖然戴了安全帽卻還是受傷。這怎麼可能？ B：他們很多人沒有【正確地】配戴安全帽，因為他們沒扣下巴帶，所以東西撞到時安全帽就掉了。"},{"w":"traditionally","p":"adv.","d":"according to old customs that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統上","s":"A: Why do all the graduates at the university ceremony wear those flat square hats with a tassel on top? B: The hats have traditionally been part of the graduation uniform for hundreds of years, and students throw them into the air at the end to celebrate finishing their studies.","t":"A：為什麼大學典禮上的畢業生都戴著頂端有流蘇的方形平頂帽？ B：這種帽子【傳統上】數百年來一直是畢業服的一部分，學生們會在典禮結束時把帽子拋向空中，慶祝完成學業。"}]},{"unit":168,"theme":"Headphones 耳機","cards":[{"w":"earphones","p":"n.","d":"small devices you wear in or over your ears to hear sound from a phone or computer","c":"耳機","s":"A: Could you lend me something to use during the online training session this afternoon, because I left my own set at home and the office is quite noisy? B: Sure, I keep an extra pair of earphones in my desk drawer, so you can plug them into your laptop and hear the trainer clearly.","t":"A：今天下午的線上培訓課程，你可以借我一些東西用嗎？因為我把自己的忘在家裡，而辦公室又很吵。 B：當然，我在抽屜裡放了一副備用【耳機】，你可以插到筆電上，清楚地聽到講師說話。"},{"w":"headset","p":"n.","d":"a set of headphones with a microphone attached","c":"頭戴式耳機（附麥克風）","s":"A: What equipment do the new customer service staff need before they start answering calls from clients on Monday morning? B: Each of them will receive a headset with a built-in microphone, so they can talk to customers while keeping both hands free to type notes into the system.","t":"A：新進的客服人員在週一早上開始接聽客戶電話之前，需要什麼設備？ B：他們每個人都會拿到一副內建麥克風的【頭戴式耳機】，這樣就能一邊跟客戶說話，一邊用雙手把筆記輸入系統。"},{"w":"earbuds","p":"n.","d":"very small headphones that fit inside the ears","c":"入耳式耳機","s":"A: Why do so many passengers on the morning train seem to be in their own world while they travel to work in the city? B: Most of them are wearing tiny earbuds that fit right inside their ears, so they can enjoy podcasts or music without disturbing the people sitting next to them.","t":"A：為什麼早上火車上這麼多乘客在進城上班的路上似乎都沉浸在自己的世界裡？ B：他們大多戴著小小的、剛好塞進耳朵裡的【入耳式耳機】，這樣就能享受播客或音樂，又不會打擾坐在旁邊的人。"},{"w":"microphone","p":"n.","d":"a device that picks up sound so it can be recorded or made louder","c":"麥克風","s":"A: The people joining our video meeting from the Tokyo branch said they could not hear anything I said during the sales report, so what went wrong? B: I think your microphone was muted, so next time please check the small icon at the bottom of the screen before you begin speaking.","t":"A：從東京分公司參加視訊會議的人說，在我做業績報告時他們什麼都聽不到，出了什麼問題？ B：我想你的【麥克風】是靜音的，所以下次開始說話之前，請先檢查螢幕下方的小圖示。"},{"w":"speaker","p":"n.","d":"a device that produces sound, often used to play music or voices loudly","c":"喇叭；揚聲器","s":"A: Why does the music in the hotel lobby sound so loud and unclear when guests are trying to talk at the front desk? B: One speaker is placed right above the reception area, so we plan to move it closer to the entrance and lower the sound a little next week.","t":"A：當客人在櫃檯說話時，飯店大廳的音樂為什麼聽起來又大聲又不清楚？ B：有一個【喇叭】就裝在接待區正上方，所以我們打算下週把它移到靠近入口的地方，並把聲音調小一點。"},{"w":"volume","p":"n.","d":"how loud or quiet a sound is","c":"音量","s":"A: My manager keeps telling me that she can hear my music from across the office even though I am wearing headphones at my desk, so what should I do? B: You should turn down the volume to a lower level, because loud sound can also damage your hearing after many hours.","t":"A：我的主管一直跟我說，即使我在座位上戴著耳機，她在辦公室另一頭也能聽到我的音樂，我該怎麼辦？ B：你應該把【音量】調低一點，因為長時間聽大聲的聲音也會傷害你的聽力。"},{"w":"bass","p":"n.","d":"the low, deep part of music or sound","c":"低音","s":"A: Why did the electronics store recommend this expensive model to the young customer who mainly listens to dance and hip-hop music? B: These headphones produce very strong bass, so the deep, low sounds of drums and beats feel powerful, which is exactly what fans of that kind of music usually want.","t":"A：為什麼電器行要推薦這款昂貴的型號給主要聽舞曲和嘻哈音樂的年輕顧客？ B：這款耳機能發出非常強勁的【低音】，讓鼓聲和節拍的低沉聲音聽起來很有力，這正是那類音樂的愛好者通常想要的。"},{"w":"treble","p":"n.","d":"the high sounds in music","c":"高音","s":"A: The singer's voice sounds sharp and a little painful in my ears whenever I play this recording on my new headphones, so is something broken? B: Probably not; the treble is just set too high, so open the sound settings on your phone and reduce the high notes slightly.","t":"A：每次我用新耳機播放這段錄音時，歌手的聲音聽起來都很刺耳，讓我耳朵有點痛，是有東西壞了嗎？ B：應該沒有，只是【高音】設得太高了，打開手機的音效設定，把高音稍微調低就好。"},{"w":"noise cancellation","p":"n.phr.","d":"technology that blocks out unwanted sound from around you","c":"降噪（功能）","s":"A: How do you manage to sleep on those long overnight flights when you travel to meet clients in Europe every month? B: My headphones have excellent noise cancellation, which blocks out the sound of the engines and crying babies, so I can rest peacefully for most of the journey.","t":"A：你每個月都要出差去歐洲見客戶，在那些長途夜間航班上你怎麼睡得著？ B：我的耳機有很棒的【降噪功能】，可以隔絕引擎聲和嬰兒哭聲，所以大部分航程我都能安穩地休息。"},{"w":"wireless","p":"adj.","d":"without wires; using radio signals instead of cables","c":"無線的","s":"A: Why did you decide to replace your old headphones with a new pair even though they still worked perfectly well? B: I wanted a wireless model, because the cable kept getting caught on my bag and chair while I was walking around the office and making calls.","t":"A：為什麼你的舊耳機明明還很好用，你卻決定換一副新的？ B：我想要一款【無線的】型號，因為我在辦公室走動和打電話時，線老是卡到我的包包和椅子。"},{"w":"wired","p":"adj.","d":"connected by a wire or cable","c":"有線的","s":"A: Why does the recording studio still use old-fashioned headphones with cables instead of the latest Bluetooth models? B: The engineers prefer wired headphones because a cable gives a stable signal with no delay, and they never need to worry about the battery running out during a long session.","t":"A：為什麼錄音室還在用帶線的老式耳機，而不用最新的藍牙型號？ B：工程師比較喜歡【有線的】耳機，因為線材能提供穩定、沒有延遲的訊號，而且在長時間錄音時，他們永遠不必擔心電池沒電。"},{"w":"bluetooth","p":"n.","d":"a technology that lets devices connect to each other without wires over a short distance","c":"藍牙","s":"A: How can I play the presentation video through the meeting room speaker without looking for a cable in the storage cupboard? B: Just turn on bluetooth on your laptop and choose the speaker from the list of nearby devices, and the sound should start coming through within a few seconds.","t":"A：我要怎樣不用去儲藏櫃找線，就能透過會議室的喇叭播放簡報影片？ B：只要打開筆電的【藍牙】，從附近裝置清單中選擇那台喇叭，幾秒鐘內聲音就會傳出來了。"},{"w":"portable","p":"adj.","d":"light and small enough to carry easily","c":"攜帶式的；便於攜帶的","s":"A: What kind of sound system should we bring to the company picnic at the park, since there is no electricity near the lake? B: Let's take the small portable speaker from the marketing department, because it runs on batteries and is easy to carry in one hand.","t":"A：公司要去公園野餐，湖邊沒有電，我們應該帶什麼樣的音響設備？ B：我們帶行銷部那台小小的【攜帶式】喇叭吧，因為它用電池，單手就能輕鬆拿著。"},{"w":"lightweight","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy","c":"輕量的；輕便的","s":"A: Why do you think so many business travelers are buying this headphone model, even though it costs more than similar products? B: It is extremely lightweight, weighing less than two hundred grams, so people can wear it for a whole flight without feeling any pressure on their head or neck.","t":"A：為什麼你覺得這麼多商務旅客都買這款耳機，即使它比同類產品貴？ B：它非常【輕便】，重量不到兩百公克，所以人們可以整趟航程都戴著，頭部和脖子不會感到任何壓力。"},{"w":"comfortable","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant to wear or use and not causing pain","c":"舒適的","s":"A: Our call center staff wear headphones for eight hours a day, so which model should the purchasing team order for them this year? B: We should choose the one with soft, thick ear pads, because it is the most comfortable to wear during long shifts and does not hurt the ears.","t":"A：我們客服中心的員工每天戴耳機八小時，採購團隊今年應該幫他們訂哪一款？ B：我們應該選有柔軟厚耳墊的那款，因為長時間輪班戴起來最【舒適】，也不會讓耳朵痛。"},{"w":"adjustable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed in size or position","c":"可調整的","s":"A: Will these headphones fit both the adults and the children who join our museum audio tour on weekends? B: Yes, the headband is adjustable, so visitors can easily make it bigger or smaller by sliding each side until it fits their head properly.","t":"A：這些耳機適合週末參加我們博物館語音導覽的大人和小孩戴嗎？ B：可以，頭帶是【可調整的】，所以參觀者只要滑動兩側，就能輕鬆把它調大或調小，直到適合自己的頭型。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"able to last a long time without breaking","c":"耐用的","s":"A: Why did the school choose such expensive headphones for its language lab when cheaper ones were also available online? B: These ones are much more durable, so they will not break easily even when hundreds of students drop or pull them every week for several years.","t":"A：網路上明明也有更便宜的，為什麼學校要為語言教室選這麼貴的耳機？ B：這款【耐用】得多，就算幾年來每週有幾百名學生摔到或拉扯，也不容易壞。"},{"w":"foldable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be folded into a smaller shape","c":"可折疊的","s":"A: My suitcase is already full for the business trip to Singapore, so how can I fit my large headphones inside? B: Don't worry, they are foldable, so you can bend both ear cups inward and put them in the small case that came in the box.","t":"A：我去新加坡出差的行李箱已經塞滿了，要怎麼把我的大耳機放進去？ B：別擔心，它們是【可折疊的】，你可以把兩個耳罩往內折，放進盒子裡附的小收納盒。"},{"w":"listen","p":"v.","d":"to pay attention to sounds or to what someone is saying","c":"聽","s":"A: How do you prepare for the TOEIC test while you commute to work by bus for almost an hour every day? B: I usually listen to practice recordings on my phone during the ride, and then I check the answers and read the scripts during my lunch break.","t":"A：你每天搭將近一小時的公車上班，你是怎麼準備多益考試的？ B：我通常在車上用手機【聽】練習錄音，然後在午休時間核對答案和閱讀文本。"},{"w":"connect","p":"v.","d":"to join two things so that they work together","c":"連接","s":"A: The new interns cannot hear anything from the training video playing on the conference room screen this morning, so can you help them? B: Sure, they just need to connect their headphones to the computer with the cable on the table, and then they should be able to hear it.","t":"A：今天早上新來的實習生聽不到會議室螢幕上播放的培訓影片，你能幫幫他們嗎？ B：當然，他們只要用桌上的線把耳機【連接】到電腦，應該就能聽到了。"},{"w":"charge","p":"v.","d":"to put electricity into a battery","c":"充電","s":"A: My wireless headphones stopped working in the middle of an important phone call with a supplier yesterday afternoon, so what happened? B: The battery was probably empty, so remember to charge them every night before you go to bed, especially before busy days with many calls.","t":"A：昨天下午跟供應商通重要電話時，我的無線耳機突然不能用了，發生了什麼事？ B：電池大概沒電了，所以記得每晚睡前幫它【充電】，特別是在電話很多的忙碌日子之前。"},{"w":"adjust","p":"v.","d":"to change something slightly to make it better or more suitable","c":"調整","s":"A: The headphones feel too tight on my head, and after an hour of working at my desk I always get a headache, so what can I do? B: You can adjust the headband by gently pulling each side down a little, so it sits more loosely and feels better.","t":"A：耳機戴在頭上感覺太緊，每次在桌前工作一小時後我就會頭痛，我能怎麼辦？ B：你可以輕輕把兩側往下拉一點來【調整】頭帶，這樣戴起來會比較鬆，也比較舒服。"},{"w":"isolate","p":"v.","d":"to separate someone or something from others; to keep out sound","c":"隔離；隔絕","s":"A: How do the translators in the conference booth manage to focus when the hall is full of people talking and moving around? B: They wear special headphones that isolate them from the noise in the room, so they can hear only the speaker and translate every word accurately.","t":"A：會議廳裡擠滿了講話和走動的人，翻譯人員在口譯室裡是怎麼保持專注的？ B：他們戴著特殊的耳機，能把他們與室內的噪音【隔絕】開來，所以他們只聽得到講者的聲音，能準確翻譯每一個字。"},{"w":"clear","p":"adj.","d":"easy to hear, see, or understand","c":"清楚的；清晰的","s":"A: Why did the sales team choose this headset for all their calls with international clients instead of the cheaper one? B: The sound quality is very clear, so customers in other countries can understand every word without asking the staff to repeat their questions again and again.","t":"A：為什麼業務團隊所有跟國際客戶的通話都選用這款耳機麥克風，而不是比較便宜的那款？ B：它的音質非常【清晰】，所以其他國家的客戶不必一再要求員工重複問題，就能聽懂每一個字。"},{"w":"crisp","p":"adj.","d":"(of sound) clear, sharp, and pleasant","c":"清脆的；清晰俐落的","s":"A: What did the magazine reviewer like most about the new headphones that our company launched at the technology fair last month? B: She praised their crisp sound, saying that every guitar note and voice was sharp and clean, even when she played complicated classical music at high levels.","t":"A：那位雜誌評論者最喜歡我們公司上個月在科技展推出的新耳機哪一點？ B：她稱讚它們【清脆俐落的】音質，說即使在高音量播放複雜的古典音樂時，每一個吉他音符和人聲都很清晰乾淨。"},{"w":"immersive","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel completely surrounded by and part of something","c":"身歷其境的；沉浸式的","s":"A: Why are gaming companies so interested in partnering with our audio department for their new virtual reality products this year? B: Our headphones create a truly immersive experience, so players feel as if they are standing inside the game world, hearing footsteps and voices from every direction.","t":"A：為什麼遊戲公司今年對於跟我們音響部門合作開發新的虛擬實境產品這麼感興趣？ B：我們的耳機能創造真正【身歷其境的】體驗，讓玩家感覺好像站在遊戲世界裡，聽得到四面八方傳來的腳步聲和人聲。"},{"w":"balanced","p":"adj.","d":"having the right amount of each part; even","c":"均衡的；平衡的","s":"A: Why do music producers often recommend these studio headphones to beginners who are learning to mix songs at home? B: They give a balanced sound, with low, middle and high tones at equal levels, so beginners can hear exactly how the song will sound on other devices.","t":"A：為什麼音樂製作人常推薦這款錄音室耳機給在家學混音的新手？ B：它們的聲音很【均衡】，低、中、高音都在相同的程度，所以新手能準確聽出歌曲在其他裝置上的效果。"},{"w":"distorted","p":"adj.","d":"(of sound) changed so that it is unclear or unpleasant","c":"失真的","s":"A: A customer called this morning to complain that the headphones she bought from our online shop last week make strange noises, so what did she say exactly? B: She said the music sounds distorted and crackly whenever she turns it up, so we offered to send her a replacement pair free of charge.","t":"A：今天早上有位顧客打電話來抱怨，她上週在我們網路商店買的耳機會發出怪聲，她具體怎麼說？ B：她說只要把音量調大，音樂聽起來就【失真】又有劈啪聲，所以我們提議免費寄一副新的給她。"},{"w":"privately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that other people cannot see or hear","c":"私下地；不打擾他人地","s":"A: How can the hospital patients who share a room watch television in the evening without disturbing each other or the nurses on duty? B: Each bed has its own pair of headphones, so patients can watch their favorite programs privately while their neighbors sleep or read in peace.","t":"A：同住一間病房的病人晚上要怎麼看電視，才不會打擾彼此或值班護理師？ B：每張床都有自己的一副耳機，所以病人可以【私下】觀看喜歡的節目，而隔壁的人也能安靜地睡覺或閱讀。"},{"w":"comfortably","p":"adv.","d":"in a pleasant way that does not cause pain or difficulty","c":"舒適地","s":"A: Our customers often complain that their ears hurt after wearing our older headphone models for more than an hour, so how is the new model different? B: It has memory foam cushions that shape themselves to your ears, so people can wear it comfortably all day at work or while traveling.","t":"A：我們的顧客常抱怨戴舊款耳機超過一小時後耳朵會痛，新款有什麼不同？ B：它有能貼合耳朵形狀的記憶泡棉耳墊，所以人們上班或旅行時可以整天【舒適地】戴著。"},{"w":"wirelessly","p":"adv.","d":"without using wires or cables","c":"無線地","s":"A: Is it possible to send the documents from my phone to the office printer without plugging in any cable at all? B: Yes, the new printer that the IT team installed last Friday works wirelessly, so you only need to join the office network and press the print button on your screen.","t":"A：有可能完全不插任何線，就把文件從我的手機傳到辦公室的印表機嗎？ B：可以，IT團隊上週五安裝的新印表機可以【無線地】運作，所以你只需要連上辦公室網路，再按螢幕上的列印按鈕就好。"},{"w":"instantly","p":"adv.","d":"immediately; at once","c":"立即地","s":"A: What happens when I take the new earbuds out of their charging case before my morning video call with the design team? B: They connect to your phone instantly, so you can join the call within a second without opening any settings or pressing extra buttons.","t":"A：在早上和設計團隊視訊通話之前，我把新耳機從充電盒拿出來時會怎樣？ B：它們會【立即】連上你的手機，所以你不用打開任何設定或多按按鈕，一秒內就能加入通話。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often, or at the same times each day, week, etc.","c":"定期地；經常","s":"A: The ear pads on the headphones in our shared meeting room look dirty and smell a bit after so many people have used them, so what should we do? B: The office assistant should clean them regularly, for example every Friday afternoon, with special wipes to keep them fresh and hygienic.","t":"A：會議室共用耳機的耳墊在這麼多人用過之後，看起來很髒，還有點味道，我們該怎麼辦？ B：辦公室助理應該【定期】清潔，例如每週五下午用專用濕紙巾擦拭，讓它們保持清新衛生。"}]},{"unit":169,"theme":"Health 健康","cards":[{"w":"fitness","p":"n.","d":"the condition of being physically strong and healthy","c":"體能；健康","s":"A: Why did the human resources team decide to open a small gym on the third floor of our office building this spring? B: They hoped that staff would improve their fitness by working out during lunch breaks, because many people complained that they felt tired after sitting at their desks all day.","t":"A：為什麼人資團隊今年春天決定在我們辦公大樓三樓開設一間小型健身房？ B：他們希望員工能利用午休時間運動來提升【體能】，因為很多人抱怨整天坐在辦公桌前讓他們覺得很疲累。"},{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the food you eat and how it keeps your body healthy","c":"營養","s":"A: The new menu in the staff cafeteria has a lot more vegetables and fewer fried dishes than last year, hasn't it? B: Yes, the company hired an expert on nutrition who explained that balanced meals help workers stay focused, so the chef changed the recipes after several meetings with her.","t":"A：員工餐廳的新菜單比去年多了很多蔬菜、少了油炸菜色，對吧？ B：是的，公司聘請了一位【營養】專家，她說明均衡的餐點能幫助員工保持專注，所以主廚在和她開了幾次會後就修改了食譜。"},{"w":"diet","p":"n.","d":"the kind of food a person usually eats","c":"飲食；日常飲食","s":"A: I noticed that you have stopped ordering fried chicken and bubble tea with the rest of the team at lunch recently. Is everything all right? B: Everything is fine, but my doctor told me to follow a low-sugar diet for three months because my blood test results last week were a little worrying.","t":"A：我注意到你最近午餐不再跟團隊其他人一起點炸雞和珍珠奶茶了。一切都還好嗎？ B：一切都好，但因為我上週的驗血結果有點令人擔心，醫生要我三個月內遵守低糖【飲食】。"},{"w":"exercise","p":"n.","d":"physical activity that you do to stay healthy and strong","c":"運動","s":"A: How do you manage to stay so energetic even though you work long hours and often travel to meetings in other cities? B: I try to get at least thirty minutes of exercise every morning, such as jogging in the park near my apartment, and it really helps me handle a busy schedule.","t":"A：你經常工作很長時間，還常常到其他城市開會，怎麼還能保持這麼有活力？ B：我每天早上盡量做至少三十分鐘的【運動】，例如在我公寓附近的公園慢跑，這真的幫助我應付忙碌的行程。"},{"w":"wellness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being healthy in body and mind","c":"身心健康","s":"A: What exactly does the new employee wellness program that the company announced in yesterday's email include? B: It offers free yoga classes on Tuesday evenings, monthly talks with a nurse about healthy living, and a fruit basket in every department, because management wants staff to feel better both physically and mentally.","t":"A：公司昨天在電子郵件中宣布的新員工【身心健康】計畫到底包含什麼？ B：計畫提供週二晚上的免費瑜伽課、每月一次與護理師談健康生活的講座，以及每個部門一籃水果，因為管理階層希望員工在身體和心理上都感覺更好。"},{"w":"hygiene","p":"n.","d":"the practice of keeping yourself and your surroundings clean to stop disease","c":"衛生","s":"A: Why did the restaurant manager put up new signs in the kitchen and ask everyone to attend a short training session on Monday? B: The city inspectors are visiting next week, and she wants every cook and server to follow strict hygiene rules, such as washing their hands often and wearing clean uniforms.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳經理在廚房貼了新告示，還要求大家週一參加一個簡短的培訓課程？ B：市府稽查員下週要來訪，她希望每位廚師和服務生都遵守嚴格的【衛生】規定，例如勤洗手和穿著乾淨的制服。"},{"w":"immune","p":"adj.","d":"related to the body's ability to fight infection","c":"免疫的","s":"A: Several people in the accounting department caught a cold last month, but you never seemed to get sick at all. What is your secret? B: I make sure to sleep well, eat plenty of fruit, and walk to work, because my doctor says those things keep the immune system strong during flu season.","t":"A：上個月會計部有好幾個人感冒了，但你似乎完全沒生病。你的秘訣是什麼？ B：我一定睡飽、多吃水果，並且走路上班，因為醫生說這些能在流感季節讓【免疫】系統保持強健。"},{"w":"disease","p":"n.","d":"a serious health problem with clear causes and signs","c":"疾病","s":"A: Why is the insurance company offering free blood pressure checks in the lobby of our building this Friday afternoon? B: They want to help employees discover heart disease early, because many people do not notice any warning signs until the problem becomes serious and much more expensive to treat.","t":"A：為什麼保險公司這週五下午要在我們大樓大廳提供免費血壓檢測？ B：他們想幫助員工及早發現心臟【疾病】，因為很多人直到問題變嚴重、治療費用也高很多時，才注意到任何警訊。"},{"w":"illness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being sick, or a particular sickness","c":"疾病；病痛","s":"A: Has anyone heard why Mr. Huang has not been in the office for almost two weeks, even though the big client presentation is coming up? B: His assistant said he is recovering from a serious illness and will probably return next month, so his manager has asked Linda to lead the presentation instead.","t":"A：有人知道為什麼黃先生快兩週沒進辦公室了嗎？重要的客戶簡報快到了。 B：他的助理說他正在從一場嚴重的【疾病】中康復，大概下個月才會回來，所以他的主管已經請琳達改為負責這次簡報。"},{"w":"symptom","p":"n.","d":"a sign of an illness, such as a fever or a cough","c":"症狀","s":"A: The memo says staff should work from home if they feel unwell, but how do I know when I am too sick to come in? B: If you have a fever, a bad cough, or any other symptom of the flu, you should stay home, rest, and let your team leader know as early as possible.","t":"A：備忘錄說員工若身體不適就應該在家工作，但我要怎麼知道自己病到不能進公司？ B：如果你發燒、咳得很厲害，或有任何其他流感的【症狀】，就應該待在家休息，並盡早告訴你的組長。"},{"w":"treatment","p":"n.","d":"medical care given to a sick or injured person","c":"治療","s":"A: How is your father doing now? I heard he had to stay in the hospital last week after his operation. B: He is getting better every day, thanks to the excellent treatment he received from the doctors and nurses there, and he should be able to come home by the end of this week.","t":"A：你父親現在還好嗎？我聽說他上週手術後必須住院。 B：多虧了那裡醫生和護理師提供的優良【治療】，他一天比一天好，這週末前應該就能回家了。"},{"w":"therapy","p":"n.","d":"treatment that helps a person recover from an illness or injury, often over a long time","c":"治療；療法","s":"A: How has the warehouse supervisor been managing since he hurt his shoulder while lifting those heavy boxes in March? B: He has been going to physical therapy twice a week after work, and his doctor says he should be able to return to his normal duties by the end of next month.","t":"A：倉庫主管三月搬那些重箱子時傷了肩膀，從那之後他的狀況如何？ B：他每週下班後去做兩次物理【治療】，醫生說他應該在下個月底前就能恢復正常職務。"},{"w":"prevention","p":"n.","d":"actions taken to stop something bad, such as illness, from happening","c":"預防","s":"A: Why is the company spending so much money on free flu vaccines and hand sanitizer for every department this winter? B: Management believes that prevention is cheaper than losing workers to sickness for weeks, especially during the busy holiday season when every team needs all of its members.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年冬天要花這麼多錢為每個部門提供免費流感疫苗和乾洗手液？ B：管理階層認為【預防】比讓員工生病請假好幾週更划算，尤其是在每個團隊都需要全員到齊的忙碌假期季節。"},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming healthy again after an illness or injury","c":"康復；復原","s":"A: Will Jessica be able to attend the sales conference in Tokyo after her knee operation next week? B: Probably not, because the surgeon expects a full recovery to take about six weeks, so she will join the meetings online from home while another colleague travels in her place.","t":"A：潔西卡下週膝蓋手術後能參加東京的業務會議嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為外科醫師預計完全【康復】需要大約六週，所以她會在家線上參加會議，由另一位同事代替她出差。"},{"w":"stress","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry and pressure caused by difficult situations","c":"壓力","s":"A: Why did the company start offering short meditation classes in the meeting room every Wednesday afternoon? B: A recent survey showed that many employees feel a lot of stress because of long hours and tight deadlines, so management wanted to give them a quiet time to relax and clear their minds.","t":"A：為什麼公司開始在每週三下午於會議室開設短時間的冥想課？ B：最近一項調查顯示，許多員工因為工時長、期限緊而感到很大的【壓力】，所以管理階層想給他們一段安靜的時間放鬆、清空思緒。"},{"w":"anxiety","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of worry or nervousness about what might happen","c":"焦慮","s":"A: You seem much calmer before presentations these days. Last year you used to get very nervous before speaking to clients. B: I joined a public speaking class, and the teacher showed us some breathing exercises that reduce anxiety, so now I can talk to large groups without my hands shaking.","t":"A：你最近在簡報前看起來冷靜多了。去年你在對客戶說話前總是非常緊張。 B：我參加了一個公開演講課，老師教我們一些能減輕【焦慮】的呼吸練習，所以現在我能對著一大群人說話，手也不會發抖。"},{"w":"depression","p":"n.","d":"a mental illness in which a person feels very sad and hopeless for a long time","c":"憂鬱症；沮喪","s":"A: Why did the company add free counseling sessions to the employee benefits package this year? B: Managers learned that some workers were suffering from depression after the long lockdown, and they wanted to make sure everyone could talk to a professional without worrying about the cost or their privacy.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年在員工福利中加入免費諮商服務？ B：主管們得知有些員工在長期封城後罹患了【憂鬱症】，他們希望確保每個人都能找專業人士談談，而不必擔心費用或隱私問題。"},{"w":"sleep","p":"n.","d":"the natural state of rest when your eyes are closed and your mind is not conscious","c":"睡眠","s":"A: You look really tired this morning. Were you working on the budget report again until late last night? B: Yes, I stayed up until two o'clock to finish it, and I only got about four hours of sleep, so I will probably need a second cup of coffee before the client meeting.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來真的很累。昨晚又為了預算報告熬夜到很晚嗎？ B：是啊，我熬到兩點才完成，只有大約四個小時的【睡眠】，所以在客戶會議前我大概需要第二杯咖啡。"},{"w":"rest","p":"n.","d":"a period of relaxing or sleeping to get back your energy","c":"休息","s":"A: The doctor said you only have a mild cold, so are you planning to come back to the office tomorrow morning? B: She told me to get plenty of rest and drink warm water for two more days, so I will work from home on Thursday and return to the office on Friday.","t":"A：醫生說你只是輕微感冒，所以你打算明天早上回辦公室嗎？ B：她要我再多【休息】兩天、多喝溫水，所以我週四會在家工作，週五再回辦公室。"},{"w":"hydration","p":"n.","d":"having enough water in your body","c":"補充水分；水分充足","s":"A: Why are there so many water stations along the route for the company charity run next Saturday? B: The weather is expected to be very hot, and the organizers want to make sure every runner keeps proper hydration, because drinking too little water can cause dizziness and other serious problems.","t":"A：為什麼下週六公司慈善路跑的路線上設了那麼多補水站？ B：預計天氣會非常炎熱，主辦單位想確保每位跑者都維持適當的【水分補充】，因為喝水太少可能導致頭暈和其他嚴重問題。"},{"w":"vitamin","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance in food that your body needs to stay healthy","c":"維生素；維他命","s":"A: Why did the nurse at the company health check suggest that I should spend more time outside during lunch breaks? B: Your blood test showed that you are low in vitamin D, and sunlight helps your body produce it, so a short walk outside each day could make a real difference.","t":"A：為什麼公司健檢的護理師建議我午休時多花點時間到戶外？ B：你的驗血結果顯示你缺乏【維生素】D，而陽光能幫助身體製造它，所以每天到外面散步一下可能會帶來明顯的改善。"},{"w":"mineral","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance such as iron or calcium that your body needs in small amounts","c":"礦物質","s":"A: Why does the new sports drink sold in the vending machine cost so much more than the regular brands? B: The company says it contains an important mineral called magnesium, which helps athletes avoid muscle cramps, but the nutrition expert at our clinic thinks eating bananas and nuts works just as well.","t":"A：為什麼自動販賣機賣的新運動飲料比一般品牌貴那麼多？ B：廠商說它含有一種叫鎂的重要【礦物質】，能幫助運動員避免肌肉抽筋，但我們診所的營養專家認為吃香蕉和堅果效果也一樣好。"},{"w":"calorie","p":"n.","d":"a unit that measures how much energy food gives you","c":"卡路里；熱量","s":"A: Why did the café near our office start printing numbers next to every drink and sandwich on its new menu board? B: Many customers wanted to know the calorie count of each item, because they are trying to lose weight and need to check how much energy they eat at lunch.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近的咖啡廳在新的菜單板上開始於每種飲料和三明治旁標上數字？ B：很多顧客想知道每項餐點的【卡路里】數，因為他們正在減重，需要確認午餐吃進多少熱量。"},{"w":"obesity","p":"n.","d":"the condition of being extremely overweight in a way that is unhealthy","c":"肥胖","s":"A: Why is the city government paying for more sports fields and healthier school lunches this year? B: A recent report showed that childhood obesity has been rising quickly because many children eat fast food and play video games instead of going outside, and officials worry about future health costs.","t":"A：為什麼市政府今年要出資興建更多運動場並提供更健康的學校午餐？ B：最近一份報告顯示兒童【肥胖】的情況迅速增加，因為許多孩子吃速食、玩電玩而不出門活動，官員擔心未來的醫療成本。"},{"w":"chronic","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time and difficult to cure","c":"慢性的；長期的","s":"A: Why did Peter ask the office manager for a special standing desk and a more comfortable chair last week? B: He has suffered from chronic back pain for more than ten years, and his doctor said that sitting in the same position for many hours every day was making the problem worse.","t":"A：為什麼彼得上週向辦公室經理申請一張特殊的站立式辦公桌和一張更舒適的椅子？ B：他受【慢性】背痛所苦已經超過十年，醫生說每天長時間維持同一個坐姿讓問題變得更糟。"},{"w":"acute","p":"adj.","d":"very serious and starting suddenly","c":"急性的；劇烈的","s":"A: Why did the receptionist call an ambulance for one of the visitors in the lobby this morning? B: The man suddenly felt acute pain in his chest while he was waiting for his appointment, so she called for help right away instead of waiting to see if he would feel better.","t":"A：為什麼櫃檯人員今天早上替大廳裡的一位訪客叫了救護車？ B：那位男士在等候約會時突然感到胸口【劇烈】疼痛，所以她立刻求救，而不是等著看他會不會好轉。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"a healthy situation in which different parts of your life get the right amount of time and attention","c":"平衡","s":"A: Why did you decide to leave your high-paying job at the bank and join this smaller company last year? B: I was working until ten every night and rarely saw my children, so I wanted a better work-life balance, even if it meant earning a little less money each month.","t":"A：你去年為什麼決定離開銀行的高薪工作，加入這家規模較小的公司？ B：我以前每晚工作到十點，很少見到孩子，所以我想要更好的工作與生活【平衡】，即使這代表每個月賺的錢少一點。"},{"w":"lifestyle","p":"n.","d":"the way a person lives, including their daily activities and choices","c":"生活方式","s":"A: Your father looks much healthier than he did at the company family day last year. What changed? B: After his heart problem, he gave up smoking, started walking every evening, and cooked more vegetables at home, so his whole lifestyle is different now and his doctor is very pleased.","t":"A：你父親看起來比去年公司家庭日時健康多了。是什麼改變了？ B：他心臟出問題之後就戒菸，開始每晚散步，在家也煮更多蔬菜，所以他現在整個【生活方式】都不一樣了，醫生也非常滿意。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something you do often and regularly, often without thinking about it","c":"習慣","s":"A: How do you always manage to arrive at the office with so much energy, even on Monday mornings? B: Drinking a big glass of water and doing ten minutes of stretching as soon as I get up has become a daily habit for me, and it really helps me feel awake before work.","t":"A：你怎麼總能精力充沛地來到辦公室，即使是週一早上？ B：一起床就喝一大杯水並做十分鐘伸展，已經成為我每天的【習慣】，這真的能幫助我在上班前感到清醒。"},{"w":"screening","p":"n.","d":"a medical test to check whether people have a disease before they notice any signs","c":"篩檢","s":"A: Why did the human resources department send everyone over forty an email about a visit from the mobile clinic next month? B: The clinic is offering free cancer screening in the parking lot, because finding problems early makes them much easier to treat and the company wants to protect its staff.","t":"A：為什麼人資部寄電子郵件給所有四十歲以上的員工，通知下個月行動診所來訪的事？ B：診所將在停車場提供免費癌症【篩檢】，因為及早發現問題會讓治療容易得多，公司也想保護員工。"},{"w":"diagnosis","p":"n.","d":"the act of finding out what illness a person has","c":"診斷","s":"A: Did the doctor tell you what is causing the headaches that you have been having every afternoon at work? B: Not yet, because she could not make a diagnosis until she sees the results of my blood test and eye exam, so I have another appointment at the clinic next Thursday.","t":"A：醫生有告訴你每天下午上班時頭痛的原因嗎？ B：還沒有，因為她要等看到我的驗血和眼睛檢查結果才能做出【診斷】，所以我下週四還要再去診所一趟。"},{"w":"medication","p":"n.","d":"a medicine or drug used to treat an illness","c":"藥物","s":"A: Can you join us for a drink after the product launch party tonight to celebrate the successful year? B: I would love to, but I am taking medication for my allergies at the moment, and the pharmacist warned me not to drink any alcohol until I finish the whole package next week.","t":"A：今晚產品發表派對後，你能跟我們一起喝一杯慶祝這成功的一年嗎？ B：我很想去，但我目前正在服用過敏的【藥物】，藥劑師提醒我在下週吃完整包藥之前不要喝任何酒。"},{"w":"rehabilitation","p":"n.","d":"the process of helping someone return to a normal life after an injury or illness","c":"復健","s":"A: When will the delivery driver who was hurt in the car accident in July be able to start working again? B: He is spending three months at a rehabilitation center, where nurses and trainers are helping him learn to walk without pain, and the company has promised to keep his position open.","t":"A：七月在車禍中受傷的那位送貨司機什麼時候能重新開始工作？ B：他正在一間【復健】中心待三個月，護理師和訓練師在那裡幫助他重新學會不痛地走路，公司也承諾會為他保留職位。"},{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to keep doing something difficult for a long time","c":"耐力","s":"A: How are you preparing for the forty-kilometer charity bike ride that our department is joining in December? B: I am riding a little farther every weekend to build my endurance, because I want to be strong enough to finish the whole route without stopping to rest in front of my colleagues.","t":"A：你如何準備我們部門十二月要參加的四十公里慈善單車騎行？ B：我每個週末都騎得比上次遠一點來培養【耐力】，因為我希望自己夠強壯，能在同事面前不停下休息就騎完全程。"},{"w":"vitality","p":"n.","d":"energy and strength that makes a person seem healthy and lively","c":"活力；生命力","s":"A: Have you noticed how much more cheerful and active our team leader has been since she came back from her holiday? B: Yes, she spent two weeks hiking in the mountains and eating fresh local food, and now she is full of vitality and ready to start the new project with lots of ideas.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到我們組長度假回來後變得多開朗、多積極？ B：有啊，她花了兩週在山裡健行、吃新鮮的在地食物，現在她充滿【活力】，帶著很多點子準備開始新專案。"}]},{"unit":170,"theme":"Help 幫助","cards":[{"w":"assist","p":"v.","d":"to help someone do something","c":"協助；幫助","s":"A: Why is Daniel staying late at the office tonight when he usually leaves at six to pick up his kids from school? B: The finance manager asked him to assist the new accountant with the monthly report, because she joined the company last week and still doesn't understand our software.","t":"A：丹尼爾平常六點就下班去學校接小孩，為什麼今晚還留在辦公室加班？ B：財務經理請他【協助】新來的會計處理月報，因為她上週才進公司，還不太懂我們的軟體。"},{"w":"aid","p":"n.","d":"help such as food, money or medicine given to people in need","c":"援助；救援物資","s":"A: What did the company do after the heavy typhoon damaged so many homes in the small fishing village near our factory last month? B: The managers sent trucks full of food, water, and blankets as emergency aid, and many employees also spent their weekends cleaning the streets with local families.","t":"A：上個月強烈颱風摧毀了我們工廠附近小漁村的許多房屋後，公司做了什麼？ B：經理們派出滿載食物、飲水和毛毯的卡車作為緊急【援助】，許多員工也利用週末和當地家庭一起清理街道。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to agree with and help an idea or person","c":"支持；贊成","s":"A: Do you think the board members will accept Lisa's plan to open a new branch office in Kaohsiung next spring? B: I'm fairly sure they will, because the sales numbers from the south have been growing quickly, and the CEO has already said publicly that he will support her proposal at the meeting.","t":"A：你覺得董事會成員會接受麗莎明年春天在高雄開設新分公司的計畫嗎？ B：我相當確定會，因為南部的業績成長很快，而且執行長已經公開表示會在會議上【支持】她的提案。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the confidence or reason to do something","c":"鼓勵；激勵","s":"A: How did the HR department manage to get so many staff members to join the company's health program this year? B: They decided to encourage everyone to take part by offering free gym passes and small prizes, and the managers also walked together at lunch to set a good example.","t":"A：人資部今年是怎麼讓這麼多員工參加公司的健康計畫的？ B：他們提供免費健身房通行證和小獎品來【鼓勵】大家參加，主管們也在午餐時間一起散步，樹立好榜樣。"},{"w":"guide","p":"v.","d":"to show someone the way or lead them through a place","c":"引導；帶領","s":"A: Who is going to show the visitors from the Japanese partner company around our factory on Thursday morning? B: Mr. Chen from the production team will guide them through each area, since he speaks Japanese well and can explain how our machines work in simple terms.","t":"A：週四早上誰要帶日本合作公司的訪客參觀我們的工廠？ B：生產部的陳先生會【帶領】他們走過每個區域，因為他日文很好，能用簡單的方式說明我們機器的運作。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food, drinks or help to customers","c":"服務；供應（餐點）","s":"A: Why is the hotel restaurant hiring so many part-time workers before the end of the year? B: The manager expects a lot of company parties in December, so they need enough staff to serve hundreds of guests every night without making anyone wait too long for their meals.","t":"A：飯店餐廳為什麼在年底前招募這麼多兼職人員？ B：經理預期十二月會有很多公司聚餐，所以需要足夠的人手每晚【服務】數百位客人，不讓任何人等餐太久。"},{"w":"donate","p":"v.","d":"to give money or things to help people","c":"捐贈；捐款","s":"A: What are you going to do with all the old laptops that the IT department replaced last week? B: We plan to donate them to a local school in the mountains, because the students there don't have enough computers and our machines still work perfectly well for basic lessons.","t":"A：資訊部上週汰換下來的那些舊筆電，你們打算怎麼處理？ B：我們打算把它們【捐贈】給山區的一所學校，因為那裡的學生電腦不夠，而我們的機器用來上基本課程還完全沒問題。"},{"w":"volunteer","p":"v.","d":"to offer to do something without being asked or paid","c":"自願（做）；當志工","s":"A: Are you joining the beach clean-up event that our company is organizing next Saturday morning? B: Yes, I decided to volunteer for it because I care about the ocean, and my manager said that staff who take part will also receive an extra day off later in the year.","t":"A：你會參加公司下週六早上舉辦的淨灘活動嗎？ B：會，我決定【自願】參加，因為我關心海洋，而且主管說參加的員工今年稍後還會多得到一天假。"},{"w":"rescue","p":"v.","d":"to save someone from danger","c":"救援；營救","s":"A: Did you hear what happened at the mountain resort during the storm last weekend? B: Yes, a group of hikers got lost when the road was blocked, but the local fire department sent a team by helicopter to rescue them, and everyone returned safely to the hotel by evening.","t":"A：你有聽說上週末暴風雨期間山上度假村發生的事嗎？ B：有，一群登山客因為道路封閉而迷路，但當地消防局派出直升機小組去【營救】他們，傍晚前大家都平安回到飯店了。"},{"w":"protect","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something safe from harm","c":"保護","s":"A: Why does the company require all workers in the warehouse to wear helmets and special shoes at all times? B: The safety manager says these items protect employees from serious injuries, because heavy boxes sometimes fall from the high shelves, and forklifts move around the building all day.","t":"A：公司為什麼要求倉庫所有工人隨時戴安全帽、穿特殊的鞋子？ B：安全主管說這些裝備能【保護】員工免於重傷，因為重箱子有時會從高架上掉下來，而且堆高機整天在建築物裡來回移動。"},{"w":"care","p":"v.","d":"to feel that someone or something is important","c":"關心；在乎","s":"A: Why did you choose to work for this small hospital instead of the large one downtown that offered a higher salary? B: The nurses and doctors here really care about every patient, and the director always listens to the staff, so I feel much happier coming to work every morning.","t":"A：市中心那家大醫院給的薪水比較高，你為什麼選擇在這家小醫院工作？ B：這裡的護理師和醫生真的很【關心】每一位病人，院長也總是傾聽員工的意見，所以我每天早上來上班都覺得開心多了。"},{"w":"comfort","p":"v.","d":"to make someone who is sad or worried feel better","c":"安慰","s":"A: How did the team react when Amy told them that her father was in the hospital after a car accident? B: Everyone tried to comfort her by sending kind messages and flowers, and her manager told her to take a few days off so she could stay with her family.","t":"A：艾美告訴團隊她父親車禍住院時，大家有什麼反應？ B：每個人都傳了暖心訊息、送了花來【安慰】她，她的主管也讓她請幾天假，好陪在家人身邊。"},{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone what you think they should do","c":"建議；勸告","s":"A: Should I sign the contract with the new supplier today, or should I wait until next week? B: I would advise you to wait until the legal department has checked every page carefully, because last year we lost a lot of money after agreeing to terms we didn't fully understand.","t":"A：我應該今天就和新供應商簽約，還是等到下週？ B：我會【建議】你等法務部仔細檢查完每一頁再說，因為去年我們同意了不完全了解的條款，結果損失了很多錢。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is good and suggest it to others","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: Can you suggest a good place to take our overseas clients for dinner after the meeting on Friday evening? B: I would strongly recommend the Italian restaurant near the train station, because the food is excellent, the service is fast, and they have a quiet private room for business groups.","t":"A：週五傍晚開完會後，你能推薦一個帶海外客戶去吃晚餐的好地方嗎？ B：我強力【推薦】火車站附近那家義大利餐廳，因為餐點很棒、上菜快，而且有適合商務團體的安靜包廂。"},{"w":"facilitate","p":"v.","d":"to make a process or discussion easier or smoother","c":"促進；使順利進行","s":"A: Why did the company hire an outside expert to lead the planning workshop for all the department heads next month? B: She has a lot of experience, and she will facilitate the discussion so that everyone gets a chance to share ideas and the meeting doesn't run longer than planned.","t":"A：公司為什麼請外部專家來主持下個月所有部門主管的規劃工作坊？ B：她經驗豐富，會【引導促進】討論，讓每個人都有機會分享想法，會議也不會超出預定時間。"},{"w":"enable","p":"v.","d":"to make it possible for someone to do something","c":"使能夠","s":"A: Why did the company spend so much money on the new online system for the customer service team this year? B: The new software will enable our staff to answer customer questions much faster, because it shows all the order details and delivery information on one screen.","t":"A：公司今年為什麼花這麼多錢替客服團隊買新的線上系統？ B：新軟體將【使】我們的員工【能夠】更快回答顧客問題，因為它會在同一個畫面上顯示所有訂單細節和配送資訊。"},{"w":"provide","p":"v.","d":"to give someone something they need","c":"提供","s":"A: Do new employees need to bring their own laptops and phones when they start work here next Monday? B: No, the company will provide all the equipment they need, including a laptop, a phone, and a desk, and the IT team will set everything up before they arrive.","t":"A：新員工下週一來上班時需要自備筆電和手機嗎？ B：不用，公司會【提供】他們需要的所有設備，包括筆電、手機和辦公桌，資訊團隊也會在他們到職前把一切設定好。"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to make pain, worry or pressure less","c":"減輕；緩解","s":"A: What did the manager do when the team became so stressed about the big project deadline last week? B: She hired two temporary workers to relieve some of the pressure on the team, and she also ordered pizza for everyone so they could relax for a while during the long evening.","t":"A：上週團隊為了大型專案的截止日壓力很大時，經理做了什麼？ B：她雇用了兩名臨時員工來【減輕】團隊的部分壓力，還幫大家訂了披薩，讓大家在漫長的晚上可以放鬆一下。"},{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others for a shared goal","c":"合作；配合","s":"A: How did the two departments finally finish the product launch on time after so many problems in the spring? B: The managers agreed to cooperate with each other more closely, so they held short meetings every morning and shared all their plans through one online calendar.","t":"A：春天出了那麼多問題後，兩個部門最後是怎麼準時完成產品上市的？ B：兩位經理同意彼此更密切地【合作】，所以他們每天早上開簡短會議，並透過同一個線上行事曆分享所有計畫。"},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work with another person or group to create something","c":"合作；協作","s":"A: Why is our marketing team flying to Singapore next week instead of holding a video meeting? B: We are going to collaborate with a local design company on a new advertising campaign, and the director believes that working face to face for a few days will produce better ideas.","t":"A：我們的行銷團隊下週為什麼要飛去新加坡，而不是開視訊會議？ B：我們要和當地一家設計公司【合作】一個新的廣告活動，主任認為面對面一起工作幾天會產生更好的點子。"},{"w":"mentor","p":"v.","d":"to give a less experienced person advice and help over time","c":"指導；輔導","s":"A: How do new sales staff learn the job so quickly at your company? B: Each new employee is paired with an experienced salesperson who will mentor them for the first six months, answering their questions, joining their client meetings, and giving them honest advice about how to improve.","t":"A：你們公司的新業務人員怎麼能這麼快上手？ B：每位新員工都會和一位資深業務配對，由他在頭六個月【指導】新人，回答問題、陪同拜訪客戶，並誠實給予改進的建議。"},{"w":"counsel","p":"v.","d":"to give professional advice to someone about a problem","c":"諮詢；輔導；提供建議","s":"A: What does the company offer to employees who feel worried about losing their jobs after the merger next year? B: The HR department has hired a professional adviser to counsel staff members about their career options, and anyone can book a free private meeting with her during working hours.","t":"A：對於擔心明年合併後會失業的員工，公司提供了什麼協助？ B：人資部聘請了一位專業顧問，為員工就職涯選擇提供【諮詢輔導】，任何人都可以在上班時間預約和她免費單獨面談。"},{"w":"mediate","p":"v.","d":"to help two sides who disagree reach an agreement","c":"調解；斡旋","s":"A: How was the argument between the warehouse workers and the factory owners about overtime pay finally solved? B: The city government sent an expert to mediate between the two sides, and after three long meetings they agreed on a fair new pay plan that everyone could accept.","t":"A：倉庫工人和工廠老闆之間關於加班費的爭執最後是怎麼解決的？ B：市政府派了一位專家在雙方之間【調解】，經過三次冗長的會議，他們同意了一個大家都能接受的公平新薪資方案。"},{"w":"intervene","p":"v.","d":"to become involved in a situation to stop or change it","c":"介入；干預","s":"A: Why did the department head join the meeting between the two project leaders yesterday afternoon? B: She had to intervene because their disagreement about the budget was getting louder and louder, and she wanted to stop the conflict before it hurt the whole team's work.","t":"A：部門主管昨天下午為什麼加入兩位專案負責人的會議？ B：她不得不【介入】，因為他們對預算的爭論越來越大聲，她想在衝突影響整個團隊的工作前加以制止。"},{"w":"assistive","p":"adj.","d":"designed to help people with disabilities do things","c":"輔助的","s":"A: Why did the library buy new computers with special software and large keyboards this year? B: The city wanted to offer assistive technology for visitors who have trouble seeing or using their hands, so that everyone can search for books and read the news without help.","t":"A：圖書館今年為什麼購買了配有特殊軟體和大鍵盤的新電腦？ B：市政府希望為視力不佳或雙手不便的訪客提供【輔助】科技，讓每個人都能不靠別人幫忙就搜尋書籍和閱讀新聞。"},{"w":"beneficial","p":"adj.","d":"having a good effect; helpful","c":"有益的","s":"A: Why did the company decide to offer free yoga classes in the meeting room every Wednesday at lunch? B: The HR team read several studies showing that regular exercise is beneficial for workers' health and focus, and they hoped that the classes would also reduce stress in the office.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定每週三午餐時間在會議室提供免費瑜珈課？ B：人資團隊讀了幾份研究，顯示規律運動對員工的健康和專注力【有益】，他們也希望這些課程能減輕辦公室的壓力。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"useful, or willing to help others","c":"有幫助的；樂於助人的","s":"A: How was your first week at the new job in the accounting department downtown? B: It was much easier than I expected, because my coworkers were very helpful, showing me how to use the system and inviting me to lunch so I could get to know everyone quickly.","t":"A：你在市中心會計部新工作的第一週過得怎麼樣？ B：比我預期的輕鬆多了，因為同事們都很【樂於助人】，教我怎麼使用系統，還邀我一起吃午餐，讓我很快就認識了大家。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help and encouragement","c":"支持的；給予鼓勵的","s":"A: How did you manage to finish your master's degree while working full time at the bank? B: My manager was really supportive, because she let me leave early on class nights and changed my schedule during exam weeks, so I never had to choose between work and school.","t":"A：你在銀行全職工作的同時，是怎麼完成碩士學位的？ B：我的主管非常【支持】我，她讓我上課的晚上提早下班，考試週也幫我調整班表，所以我從來不必在工作和學業之間二選一。"},{"w":"kindly","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind and friendly way","c":"好心地；親切地","s":"A: Did the hotel staff help you when you lost your passport during the business trip to Seoul? B: Yes, the front desk manager kindly offered to call the embassy for me, and she even arranged a taxi so I could get there before it closed that afternoon.","t":"A：你去首爾出差弄丟護照時，飯店員工有幫你嗎？ B：有，櫃台經理【好心地】主動幫我打電話給大使館，甚至還幫我安排計程車，讓我在那天下午關門前趕到。"},{"w":"willingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are happy to do something","c":"欣然地；自願地","s":"A: Was it difficult to find people to work on the holiday weekend to finish the urgent order? B: Not at all, because several team members willingly agreed to come in on Saturday after the manager promised extra pay and two days off the following week.","t":"A：要找人在連假週末上班完成緊急訂單很困難嗎？ B：一點也不，因為經理承諾加發薪水並在下週補休兩天後，好幾位組員都【欣然】同意週六來上班。"},{"w":"backup","p":"n.","d":"an extra copy of computer data kept in case the original is lost","c":"備份","s":"A: What happens if the main computer system crashes while we are processing customer orders during the busy season? B: Don't worry, because the IT team makes a full backup of all our data every night, so we can restore everything within an hour and continue working without losing any orders.","t":"A：如果在旺季處理顧客訂單時主電腦系統當機了怎麼辦？ B：別擔心，資訊團隊每晚都會把所有資料做完整【備份】，所以我們能在一小時內恢復一切，繼續工作而不會遺失任何訂單。"},{"w":"service","p":"n.","d":"the help that staff give to customers","c":"服務","s":"A: Why do so many customers choose this small electronics shop instead of the big stores in the shopping mall? B: The prices are similar, but the staff offer excellent customer service, explaining every product patiently and repairing broken devices quickly for free during the first year.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多顧客選擇這家小電器行，而不是購物中心裡的大賣場？ B：價格差不多，但這裡的員工提供優質的顧客【服務】，會耐心介紹每項產品，並在第一年內免費快速維修故障的機器。"},{"w":"assistance","p":"n.","d":"help given to someone","c":"協助；援助","s":"A: What should visitors do if they have trouble finding the conference room on the tenth floor? B: They can ask for assistance at the reception desk in the lobby, where a staff member will give them a map or walk with them to the elevator and show them the way.","t":"A：如果訪客找不到十樓的會議室該怎麼辦？ B：他們可以到大廳的接待櫃台請求【協助】，工作人員會給他們一張地圖，或陪他們走到電梯並告訴他們怎麼走。"},{"w":"charity","p":"n.","d":"an organization that gives money or help to people in need","c":"慈善機構；慈善","s":"A: What is the company going to do with the money raised at the annual year-end party this December? B: All the money from the ticket sales will go to a local charity that helps homeless families find safe places to live and provides warm meals during the cold winter months.","t":"A：公司打算怎麼運用今年十二月年終尾牙募得的款項？ B：所有門票收入都會捐給當地一個【慈善機構】，該機構幫助無家可歸的家庭找到安全的住處，並在寒冷的冬季提供熱食。"}]},{"unit":171,"theme":"High School 高中","cards":[{"w":"transition","p":"n.","d":"a change from one situation or stage to another","c":"過渡；轉變","s":"A: Our daughter starts at the new high school next month, and she seems nervous about leaving all her middle school friends behind, so what can we do as parents to help her? B: Many schools hold a welcome day in August, which can make the transition much smoother because students meet teachers and see the classrooms before the first day.","t":"A：我們女兒下個月要進新的高中，她似乎很擔心要離開國中的朋友，身為父母我們能做些什麼來幫她？ B：許多學校會在八月舉辦迎新日，學生能在開學前先認識老師、看看教室，這能讓【過渡期】順利許多。"},{"w":"teenager","p":"n.","d":"a young person between 13 and 19 years old","c":"青少年","s":"A: The marketing team wants to design a new phone plan for students, but who exactly are we trying to reach with the cheaper price and the extra data for social media apps? B: We are mainly targeting a teenager between fifteen and eighteen who uses the phone for homework, music, and chatting with friends after school every day.","t":"A：行銷團隊想為學生設計新的手機方案，但這個比較便宜、又附加社群軟體流量的方案，我們究竟要鎖定誰？ B：我們主要鎖定十五到十八歲之間的【青少年】，他們每天放學後會用手機寫作業、聽音樂和跟朋友聊天。"},{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"all the subjects and courses taught in a school or program","c":"課程","s":"A: Why did the school board invite several local business owners to the meeting at city hall last Wednesday evening? B: They are updating the curriculum for next year and want to add practical courses such as basic accounting and computer coding, so they asked employers which skills young workers really need.","t":"A：為什麼教育委員會上週三晚上邀請幾位當地企業主到市政廳開會？ B：他們正在更新明年的【課程】，想加入基礎會計和程式設計等實用科目，所以詢問雇主年輕員工真正需要哪些技能。"},{"w":"credit","p":"n.","d":"a unit that shows a student has finished a course","c":"學分","s":"A: My son wants to take a summer course in business English at the community college, but will it actually count toward his high school diploma? B: Yes, if he passes the final test, he will receive one credit, and the school office will add it to his record before the new semester begins in September.","t":"A：我兒子想在社區大學上暑期商用英語課，但這真的能算進他的高中畢業文憑嗎？ B：可以，只要他通過期末測驗，就能拿到一個【學分】，學校辦公室會在九月新學期開始前把它加進他的紀錄。"},{"w":"graduation","p":"n.","d":"finishing your studies at a school; the ceremony for this","c":"畢業；畢業典禮","s":"A: Could I take next Friday afternoon off, even though we have the monthly sales report due that day? B: Of course, I know your daughter's graduation ceremony is at the sports center at two o'clock, so just finish the report on Thursday and enjoy watching her receive her diploma with the rest of the family.","t":"A：雖然下週五要交每月銷售報告，我可以請那天下午的假嗎？ B：當然可以，我知道你女兒的【畢業】典禮下午兩點在體育中心舉行，你週四把報告完成，好好和家人一起看她領畢業證書吧。"},{"w":"elective","p":"n.","d":"a course that a student chooses to take","c":"選修課","s":"A: Besides the required math and science classes, what other subjects is your nephew taking at his high school this year? B: He chose photography as an elective because he hopes to work in advertising someday, and the teacher even arranged a visit to a local design company so students could see real projects.","t":"A：除了必修的數學和自然課，你姪子今年在高中還修了哪些科目？ B：他選了攝影當【選修課】，因為他希望將來從事廣告業，老師甚至安排參觀當地一家設計公司，讓學生看看真實的專案。"},{"w":"requirement","p":"n.","d":"something that you must do or have","c":"要求；必要條件","s":"A: Why are so many seniors suddenly signing up to help at the food bank on weekends this spring? B: Our school now has a requirement that every student must complete forty hours of community service before graduating, and many of them waited until their last semester to start.","t":"A：為什麼今年春天有這麼多高三生突然報名週末去食物銀行幫忙？ B：我們學校現在有一項【規定】，每位學生畢業前都必須完成四十小時的社區服務，很多人拖到最後一學期才開始。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists times for activities","c":"時間表；課表","s":"A: Can the bus company change its morning route so that students from the new apartment complex arrive at school on time? B: We will review the schedule with the school next week, and if we add a stop at seven fifteen, the students should reach the main gate before the first bell rings.","t":"A：公車公司能不能調整早上的路線，讓新公寓社區的學生準時到校？ B：我們下週會和學校一起檢討【時刻表】，如果在七點十五分加一個站，學生應該能在第一聲鐘響前抵達校門口。"},{"w":"homework","p":"n.","d":"schoolwork that students do at home","c":"家庭作業；功課","s":"A: Why did the library decide to stay open until nine o'clock on weekday evenings starting this month? B: Many parents work late, so the library wants to give students a quiet and safe place to finish their homework, and volunteer tutors are available to help with math and English questions.","t":"A：為什麼圖書館決定從這個月起平日晚上開到九點？ B：許多家長工作到很晚，所以圖書館想提供學生一個安靜又安全的地方完成【功課】，而且還有志工家教可以幫忙解答數學和英文問題。"},{"w":"exam","p":"n.","d":"a formal test of knowledge or skill","c":"考試","s":"A: Why is the coffee shop near the high school so crowded with students every afternoon this week? B: They are preparing for the final exam next Monday, so groups of classmates meet here after school to review their notes together, and the owner even offers them a small discount on drinks.","t":"A：為什麼這週每天下午高中附近的咖啡店都擠滿了學生？ B：他們在準備下週一的期末【考試】，同學們放學後成群來這裡一起複習筆記，老闆甚至給他們飲料小折扣。"},{"w":"assessment","p":"n.","d":"a test or judgment of someone's ability or work","c":"評量；評估","s":"A: How do teachers decide whether a student is ready for the advanced English class before the semester starts? B: Each student takes a short assessment that includes reading, listening, and a brief interview, and the results help the department place everyone in a class that matches their level.","t":"A：學期開始前，老師如何判斷學生是否能上進階英文班？ B：每位學生都要做一個簡短的【評量】，包含閱讀、聽力和簡短面談，結果能幫助科內把每個人分到符合程度的班級。"},{"w":"grade","p":"n.","d":"a mark or letter that shows how good a student's work is","c":"成績；等級","s":"A: Why was your son so happy when he came home from school yesterday afternoon? B: He finally received an A as his final grade in chemistry after studying with a tutor twice a week, and his teacher wrote a note saying how much his lab reports had improved this term.","t":"A：你兒子昨天下午放學回家為什麼那麼開心？ B：他每週跟家教讀兩次書後，化學的最終【成績】終於拿到A，老師還寫了紙條說他這學期的實驗報告進步很多。"},{"w":"GPA","p":"n.","d":"grade point average; the average of all a student's marks","c":"學業平均成績","s":"A: What do the admissions officers at the university look at first when they review applications from high school seniors? B: They usually check the student's GPA to see the average of all their course results, but they also read the personal essay and letters from teachers before making a final decision.","t":"A：大學招生人員審閱高三生申請時，第一個看的是什麼？ B：他們通常會先看學生的【在校平均成績】，了解所有課程成績的平均，不過做最後決定前也會讀個人自傳和老師的推薦信。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the latest time by which something must be done","c":"截止期限","s":"A: When do students need to hand in their applications for the summer internship program at our company? B: The deadline is March thirty-first, so please remind the high school career office to send us the forms and recommendation letters early enough for our team to review them carefully.","t":"A：學生何時必須交出本公司暑期實習計畫的申請？ B：【截止日期】是三月三十一日，所以請提醒高中的生涯輔導處盡早把表格和推薦信寄來，讓我們團隊能仔細審閱。"},{"w":"responsibility","p":"n.","d":"a duty to take care of something; being reliable","c":"責任；責任感","s":"A: Why did you let your daughter take a part-time job at the bakery on Saturday mornings during her final year? B: We think working there teaches her responsibility, because she has to arrive on time, handle money carefully, and serve customers politely even when the shop is very busy.","t":"A：為什麼你讓女兒在高三時週六早上去麵包店打工？ B：我們認為在那裡工作能教她【責任感】，因為她必須準時到班、小心處理金錢，而且即使店裡很忙也要有禮貌地招呼客人。"},{"w":"independence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do things without help from others","c":"獨立；自主","s":"A: Isn't your son a little young to travel alone by train to visit the university campus in another city? B: He is seventeen now, and we want him to develop more independence before he leaves home, so he planned the whole trip himself, including the tickets, the hotel, and the campus tour.","t":"A：你兒子獨自搭火車去另一個城市參觀大學校園，會不會有點太小？ B：他現在十七歲了，我們希望他離家前能培養更多【獨立性】，所以整趟旅程都由他自己規劃，包括車票、旅館和校園導覽。"},{"w":"stress","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations","c":"壓力；緊張","s":"A: Why has the school started offering free yoga classes in the gym every Wednesday after lunch? B: Teachers noticed that many students feel a lot of stress during the busy test season, so the counselors hope that some gentle exercise and breathing practice will help them relax and sleep better.","t":"A：為什麼學校開始每週三午餐後在體育館提供免費瑜伽課？ B：老師們發現很多學生在忙碌的考試季感到很大的【壓力】，所以輔導老師希望一些溫和的運動和呼吸練習能幫助他們放鬆並睡得更好。"},{"w":"pressure","p":"n.","d":"a strong demand or push from others to do something","c":"壓力","s":"A: Why did your niece decide to study design instead of medicine, even though her parents are both doctors? B: She felt a lot of pressure from her family at first, but after a long talk, they agreed that she should follow her own interests and choose a career she will truly enjoy.","t":"A：雖然你姪女的父母都是醫生，為什麼她決定念設計而不是醫學？ B：她一開始感受到家人很大的【壓力】，但經過一次長談後，他們同意她應該追隨自己的興趣，選擇真正喜歡的職業。"},{"w":"peer","p":"n.","d":"a person of the same age or position as you","c":"同儕；同輩","s":"A: How does the new tutoring program at the high school work, and who pays the tutors for their time? B: Older students help younger ones with math after class, and the company sponsoring the program gives each peer tutor a small gift card every month to thank them for their effort.","t":"A：高中新的課輔計畫是怎麼運作的？誰付家教的費用？ B：高年級學生下課後幫學弟妹補數學，贊助這個計畫的公司每月會送每位【同儕】小老師一張小禮券，感謝他們的付出。"},{"w":"extracurricular","p":"adj.","d":"done outside normal school classes","c":"課外的","s":"A: Besides good test results, what did the scholarship committee like most about the student who won this year's award? B: She took part in many extracurricular activities, such as the debate team and the school newspaper, and she also volunteered at the hospital every weekend, which showed strong leadership and time management.","t":"A：除了優異的考試成績，獎學金委員會最欣賞今年得獎學生的哪一點？ B：她參加了許多【課外】活動，例如辯論隊和校刊，每週末還去醫院當志工，展現了很強的領導力和時間管理能力。"},{"w":"leadership","p":"n.","d":"the ability to guide and organize a group","c":"領導能力；領導力","s":"A: Why did the company choose a high school student to speak at the opening of the new community center? B: She organized a group of classmates to clean the local park every month, and her leadership impressed the mayor so much that he asked her to share her experience with the audience.","t":"A：為什麼公司選一位高中生在新社區中心開幕時致詞？ B：她組織一群同學每個月清掃當地公園，她的【領導能力】讓市長印象深刻，所以請她和觀眾分享經驗。"},{"w":"club","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who meet for a shared interest","c":"社團；俱樂部","s":"A: Is there any way for students who enjoy cooking to practice their skills at school after classes end? B: Yes, the cooking club meets every Thursday in the home economics room, and next month a local restaurant chef will visit to teach the members how to prepare simple and healthy lunches.","t":"A：有沒有辦法讓喜歡烹飪的學生放學後在學校練習技巧？ B：有，烹飪【社團】每週四在家政教室聚會，下個月還有當地餐廳的主廚會來教社員準備簡單又健康的午餐。"},{"w":"athletics","p":"n.","d":"sports such as running, jumping and other team sports","c":"體育運動；田徑","s":"A: Why is the sporting goods store offering a special discount to students from Central High School this month? B: The store sponsors the school's athletics program, which includes track, swimming, and basketball teams, so it wants to help students buy good running shoes and uniforms before the new season begins.","t":"A：為什麼運動用品店這個月提供中央高中學生特別折扣？ B：這家店贊助學校的【體育運動】計畫，包括田徑、游泳和籃球隊，所以想在新賽季開始前幫學生買到好的跑鞋和制服。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control yourself and follow rules","c":"紀律；自律","s":"A: What do you think is the main reason why your daughter's grades improved so much this semester? B: She showed great discipline by turning off her phone every evening and studying for two hours at the same time each day, even when her friends invited her to go out.","t":"A：你覺得你女兒這學期成績進步這麼多的主要原因是什麼？ B：她展現了很強的【自律】，每天晚上關掉手機，在同一時間讀書兩小時，即使朋友約她出去也一樣。"},{"w":"attendance","p":"n.","d":"being present at school, work or an event; the number of people present","c":"出席；出席人數","s":"A: Why did the principal send letters to some families during the second week of the semester? B: The school is worried about poor attendance, because several students have missed many classes without a reason, and the principal wants parents to make sure their children come to school every day.","t":"A：為什麼校長在學期第二週寄信給一些家庭？ B：學校擔心學生【出席率】不佳，因為有幾位學生無故缺了很多課，校長希望家長確保孩子每天都來上學。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the reason or desire to do something","c":"動機；幹勁","s":"A: How did the teacher get her students so interested in learning English this year when many of them disliked the subject before? B: She increased their motivation by inviting staff from an international company to talk about how they use English at work, so the students finally saw why it matters.","t":"A：很多學生以前不喜歡英文，這位老師今年是怎麼讓學生對學英文這麼有興趣的？ B：她邀請一家跨國公司的員工來分享如何在工作上使用英文，提高了學生的【學習動機】，讓他們終於明白英文的重要。"},{"w":"preparation","p":"n.","d":"the work of getting ready for something","c":"準備","s":"A: Why does your son go to the community center every Saturday morning instead of sleeping late like his friends? B: He is attending a free course in preparation for job interviews, where volunteers from local businesses teach students how to write a résumé, dress properly, and answer common questions.","t":"A：為什麼你兒子每週六早上都去社區中心，而不像他朋友那樣睡懶覺？ B：他在上免費的求職面試【準備】課程，當地企業的志工會教學生如何寫履歷、穿著得體以及回答常見問題。"},{"w":"identity","p":"n.","d":"who a person or group is; a feeling of belonging","c":"身分；認同感","s":"A: Why did the student council decide to design new school jackets with a special logo this year? B: They wanted to build a stronger sense of identity among students, so everyone voted on the colors and the design, and now many students proudly wear the jackets to sports events.","t":"A：為什麼學生會今年決定設計印有特別標誌的新校服外套？ B：他們想在學生之間建立更強的【認同感】，所以大家一起投票選顏色和設計，現在很多學生都驕傲地穿著外套去看比賽。"},{"w":"guidance counselor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a school worker who gives students advice about study and careers","c":"輔導老師","s":"A: My daughter cannot decide whether to study business or nursing at university next year, so who at her high school could help her? B: She should make an appointment with the guidance counselor, who can explain different careers, help her compare programs, and give advice on preparing her application forms.","t":"A：我女兒無法決定明年大學要念商科還是護理，她高中裡誰能幫她？ B：她應該和【輔導老師】預約，對方能介紹不同職業、幫她比較科系，並提供準備申請表的建議。"},{"w":"college-ready","p":"adj.","d":"having the skills needed to succeed at college or university","c":"具備上大學能力的","s":"A: Why did the local technology firm donate laptops and offer free writing workshops to the high school last year? B: The firm wants more graduates to be college-ready when they finish school, so it helps students build strong study and computer skills that they will need in university courses.","t":"A：當地科技公司去年為什麼捐筆電給那所高中，並提供免費寫作工作坊？ B：這家公司希望更多畢業生在畢業時就【具備上大學的能力】，所以幫助學生培養將來大學課程所需的扎實讀書與電腦技能。"},{"w":"achievement","p":"n.","d":"something good that you succeed in doing with effort","c":"成就","s":"A: Why is the company newsletter featuring a story about a high school student this month? B: She won first place in a national science competition with a project on recycling plastic, and our manager thought her achievement would inspire employees, since her mother works in our accounting department.","t":"A：為什麼這個月公司內部刊物刊登一篇關於高中生的報導？ B：她以回收塑膠的專題在全國科學競賽中獲得第一名，經理認為她的【成就】能激勵員工，因為她媽媽在我們會計部工作。"}]},{"unit":172,"theme":"Historical Books 歷史書籍","cards":[{"w":"history","p":"n.","d":"the study or story of past events","c":"歷史；歷史學","s":"A: Why is the city library holding a special exhibition on the second floor this month, and who is organizing all the events for local families? B: The library wants to celebrate the history of our town, so volunteers have collected old photos, maps, and letters showing how the area grew over the last two hundred years.","t":"A：為什麼市立圖書館這個月在二樓舉辦特展？是誰為當地家庭籌劃所有活動？ B：圖書館想慶祝我們小鎮的【歷史】，所以志工收集了舊照片、地圖和信件，展示這個地區過去兩百年來的發展。"},{"w":"chronicle","p":"n.","d":"a written record of events in the order they happened","c":"編年史；紀事","s":"A: What kind of book is the publishing team preparing for the company's fiftieth anniversary celebration next spring? B: They are writing a detailed chronicle of the company's growth, describing each important year in order, from the first small office downtown to the opening of our factories in Asia.","t":"A：出版團隊正在為明年春天公司五十週年慶祝活動準備什麼樣的書？ B：他們正在撰寫一部詳細的公司發展【編年史】，依序描述每個重要的年份，從市中心第一間小辦公室到我們在亞洲的工廠開幕。"},{"w":"archive","p":"n.","d":"a place where old records and documents are kept","c":"檔案館；檔案室","s":"A: Where can I find the original contracts we signed with our first overseas supplier back in the 1980s? B: You should check the company archive in the basement, where all the old paper records are stored in labeled boxes, but remember to ask the librarian for a key before you go down there.","t":"A：我在哪裡可以找到我們在1980年代與第一家海外供應商簽訂的原始合約？ B：你應該去查看地下室的公司【檔案室】，所有舊的紙本紀錄都存放在貼有標籤的箱子裡，但記得下去之前要先向管理員拿鑰匙。"},{"w":"manuscript","p":"n.","d":"a book or document written by hand or not yet printed","c":"手稿；原稿","s":"A: Why is the museum keeping that old book behind thick glass in a dark room with such a low temperature? B: It is a rare manuscript written by hand by a monk about eight hundred years ago, and the paper is so fragile that strong light and warm air could easily damage the pages.","t":"A：為什麼博物館要把那本舊書放在溫度很低的暗室裡、隔著厚玻璃保存？ B：那是一份大約八百年前由一位修士親手寫成的珍貴【手稿】，紙張非常脆弱，強光和溫暖的空氣很容易損壞書頁。"},{"w":"biography","p":"n.","d":"the story of a person's life written by someone else","c":"傳記","s":"A: Have you finished reading the book about the founder of that famous electronics company that the manager recommended at the meeting? B: Yes, the biography was written by a journalist who interviewed his family and former coworkers, and it explains how he turned a small repair shop into a global business.","t":"A：你讀完經理在會議上推薦的那本關於知名電子公司創辦人的書了嗎？ B：讀完了，這本【傳記】是由一位記者寫的，他採訪了創辦人的家人和以前的同事，書中說明了他如何把一間小修理店變成全球企業。"},{"w":"memoir","p":"n.","d":"a book a person writes about their own life and experiences","c":"回憶錄","s":"A: What is the retired CEO planning to do now that she has left the company and has more free time at home? B: She is writing a memoir about her own experiences in the business world, including the difficult decisions she made during the financial crisis and the lessons she learned from her mistakes.","t":"A：那位退休的執行長離開公司、在家有更多空閒時間後打算做什麼？ B：她正在寫一本關於自己在商界經歷的【回憶錄】，包括她在金融危機期間做出的艱難決定，以及她從錯誤中學到的教訓。"},{"w":"era","p":"n.","d":"a long period of time with a special character","c":"時代；年代","s":"A: Why does the new hotel lobby have such old-fashioned furniture, black-and-white photos, and jazz music playing all day? B: The designers wanted guests to feel like they had traveled back to the era of the 1920s, when the building first opened as a luxury hotel for wealthy travelers.","t":"A：為什麼新飯店大廳擺著那麼老式的家具、黑白照片，還整天播放爵士樂？ B：設計師希望客人感覺像回到了1920年代的那個【時代】，那時這棟建築剛以豪華飯店之姿開幕，接待富有的旅客。"},{"w":"period","p":"n.","d":"a length of time in history","c":"時期；期間","s":"A: Which part of the past does the professor's new book on clothing and daily life mainly focus on? B: It covers the period between 1850 and 1900, when factories changed how people worked, and it shows how ordinary families dressed, cooked, and spent their weekends during those busy years.","t":"A：教授那本關於服裝與日常生活的新書主要聚焦在過去的哪一段？ B：它涵蓋1850年到1900年之間的【時期】，當時工廠改變了人們的工作方式，書中呈現一般家庭在那些忙碌的年代如何穿著、做飯和度過週末。"},{"w":"civilization","p":"n.","d":"a developed society with its own culture and way of life","c":"文明","s":"A: What did the tour guide say about the stone buildings and water channels we saw near the river this morning? B: She explained that an ancient civilization built them more than three thousand years ago, and that its people already understood farming, mathematics, and trade with neighboring regions.","t":"A：導遊對我們今天早上在河邊看到的石造建築和水道說了什麼？ B：她解釋說，一個古老的【文明】在三千多年前建造了它們，而且當時的人們已經懂得農耕、數學，以及和鄰近地區貿易。"},{"w":"empire","p":"n.","d":"a group of countries ruled by one leader or government; a large group of businesses","c":"帝國；（商業）王國","s":"A: Why does the history book have so many maps showing different parts of Europe, Africa, and Asia in the same color? B: Those areas were all once part of one huge empire that was controlled by a single emperor in Rome, and the maps show how its borders grew and later became smaller.","t":"A：為什麼那本歷史書有這麼多地圖，把歐洲、非洲和亞洲的不同地區塗成同一種顏色？ B：那些地區曾經都屬於一個由羅馬的一位皇帝統治的龐大【帝國】，地圖顯示了它的疆界如何擴張，後來又如何縮小。"},{"w":"dynasty","p":"n.","d":"a series of rulers from the same family","c":"王朝；朝代","s":"A: Why are visitors from abroad so interested in the old palace that our travel agency includes in the city tour? B: Emperors from the same family lived there for nearly three hundred years, so the guides explain how that dynasty ruled the country and why it finally lost power in 1912.","t":"A：為什麼國外遊客對我們旅行社在市區導覽中安排的那座古老宮殿這麼感興趣？ B：同一個家族的皇帝在那裡住了將近三百年，所以導遊會解說那個【王朝】如何統治國家，以及它為什麼在1912年終於失去政權。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n.","d":"a big change in a government or in the way things are done","c":"革命；巨大變革","s":"A: Why did the speaker at the technology conference keep comparing smartphones to the steam engines of the 1800s? B: She believes mobile devices have started a revolution in the way we work and shop, just as steam power completely changed factories, transportation, and daily life two centuries ago.","t":"A：為什麼科技研討會上的講者一直把智慧型手機比作1800年代的蒸汽機？ B：她認為行動裝置在我們工作和購物的方式上掀起了一場【革命】，就像兩個世紀前蒸汽動力徹底改變了工廠、交通和日常生活一樣。"},{"w":"warfare","p":"n.","d":"fighting in a war; the methods used in war","c":"戰爭；作戰方式","s":"A: What is the main topic of the military museum's new exhibit that opens on the third floor next weekend? B: It shows how warfare changed over the centuries, from soldiers fighting with swords and horses to modern armies using tanks, airplanes, and computers to plan their attacks.","t":"A：軍事博物館下週末在三樓開幕的新展覽主題是什麼？ B：它展示了【戰爭方式】幾世紀以來如何演變，從士兵用刀劍和馬匹作戰，到現代軍隊使用坦克、飛機和電腦來規劃攻擊。"},{"w":"treaty","p":"n.","d":"a formal written agreement between countries","c":"條約","s":"A: Why are the two governments sending their trade ministers to Geneva for meetings that will last the whole week? B: They hope to sign a treaty that will reduce taxes on imported goods and protect fishing rights, but both sides still disagree about several important details in the final agreement.","t":"A：為什麼兩國政府要派貿易部長到日內瓦開整整一週的會議？ B：他們希望簽署一項【條約】來降低進口商品的稅並保護捕魚權，但雙方對最終協議中的幾個重要細節仍有分歧。"},{"w":"colonial","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a time when one country ruled another country","c":"殖民的；殖民時期的","s":"A: What makes the old neighborhood near the harbor so popular with tourists who come to take photos on weekends? B: Many of the buildings there were built during the colonial period, when the area was ruled by a European country, so they have tall windows, wide balconies, and red brick walls.","t":"A：港口附近的老街區為什麼這麼受週末來拍照的遊客歡迎？ B：那裡許多建築是在【殖民】時期建造的，當時該地區由一個歐洲國家統治，所以它們有高窗、寬陽台和紅磚牆。"},{"w":"medieval","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the Middle Ages, about 500 to 1500","c":"中世紀的","s":"A: Where are we going on Saturday during the company trip, and do I need to bring anything special? B: We are visiting a medieval castle with high stone walls and towers that were built about seven hundred years ago, so wear comfortable shoes because there are many steep stairs to climb.","t":"A：公司旅遊星期六要去哪裡？我需要帶什麼特別的東西嗎？ B：我們要參觀一座【中世紀的】城堡，它有大約七百年前建造的高大石牆和塔樓，所以要穿舒適的鞋子，因為有很多陡峭的樓梯要爬。"},{"w":"ancient","p":"adj.","d":"very old; from a very long time ago","c":"古代的；古老的","s":"A: Why did the construction company have to stop work on the new shopping center for almost three months? B: Workers found ancient coins and pottery from about two thousand years ago while digging the foundation, so experts from the university came to study the site before building could continue.","t":"A：為什麼建設公司必須停止新購物中心的工程將近三個月？ B：工人在挖地基時發現了大約兩千年前的【古代】錢幣和陶器，所以大學的專家來研究這個地點，之後才能繼續施工。"},{"w":"primary","p":"adj.","d":"first-hand; made at the time of the event; main","c":"第一手的；主要的","s":"A: How should I support the arguments in my report about the factory strike of 1965 for the history department? B: Try to use primary sources, such as letters, diaries, and newspaper articles written by people who were actually there, because they give the most direct evidence of what happened.","t":"A：我要交給歷史系、關於1965年工廠罷工的報告，該如何支持我的論點？ B：試著使用【第一手】資料，例如由實際在場的人寫的信件、日記和報紙文章，因為它們提供了最直接的事件證據。"},{"w":"secondary","p":"adj.","d":"based on other people's work, not first-hand; less important","c":"第二手的；次要的","s":"A: Is it acceptable to include textbooks and online encyclopedias in the list of materials for my research paper? B: Yes, those are secondary sources, which explain and discuss events using other writers' work, and they are useful for background, but you should also include some original documents from the time.","t":"A：我的研究報告參考資料清單中可以放教科書和線上百科全書嗎？ B：可以，那些是【第二手】資料，它們是利用其他作者的研究來解釋和討論事件，對背景知識很有用，但你也應該加入一些當時的原始文件。"},{"w":"narrative","p":"n.","d":"a story or description of events","c":"敘事；故事","s":"A: Why do so many readers say the new book about the 1906 earthquake is hard to put down, even though it is about history? B: The author tells a powerful narrative through the eyes of three ordinary families, so readers follow their struggles and hopes like characters in a novel while still learning real facts.","t":"A：為什麼很多讀者說那本關於1906年地震的新書讓人愛不釋手，即使它講的是歷史？ B：作者透過三個普通家庭的視角講述了一段動人的【敘事】，所以讀者像在讀小說一樣跟著他們的掙扎和希望，同時還能學到真實的史實。"},{"w":"account","p":"n.","d":"a written or spoken description of an event","c":"描述；記述","s":"A: Why is the old soldier's diary so valuable to the researchers who are writing about the famous battle? B: It gives a detailed account of what happened each day, including the weather, the food, and the fear the young men felt, which official military reports from that time never mention.","t":"A：為什麼那位老兵的日記對研究那場著名戰役的學者來說這麼珍貴？ B：它對每天發生的事情提供了詳細的【記述】，包括天氣、食物以及年輕士兵感受到的恐懼，這些都是當時官方軍事報告從未提到的。"},{"w":"interpretation","p":"n.","d":"an explanation of the meaning of something","c":"解讀；詮釋","s":"A: Why did the two historians argue so strongly during the panel discussion at the book festival yesterday afternoon? B: They read the same letters from the king but came to very different conclusions, and each one believed the other's interpretation of the documents was completely wrong.","t":"A：為什麼昨天下午書展的座談會上那兩位歷史學家爭論得那麼激烈？ B：他們讀了國王的同一批信件，卻得出非常不同的結論，而且彼此都認為對方對這些文件的【解讀】完全錯誤。"},{"w":"documentation","p":"n.","d":"written records or papers that prove or support something","c":"文件記錄；證明文件","s":"A: What do I need to bring when I apply for permission to study the old city records at the national library? B: You must provide proper documentation, such as a letter from your university and a copy of your ID, because the staff only allow registered researchers to handle such valuable papers.","t":"A：我去國家圖書館申請研究舊市政紀錄時需要帶什麼？ B：你必須提供適當的【證明文件】，例如大學的信函和身分證影本，因為工作人員只允許已登記的研究人員接觸這麼珍貴的文件。"},{"w":"timeline","p":"n.","d":"a list or line showing events in the order they happened","c":"時間軸；年表；時程表","s":"A: How can we help new employees quickly understand the major changes our company has gone through since it was founded? B: Let's put a large timeline on the wall of the training room that shows every key event in order, from our first product launch to the merger with our biggest competitor.","t":"A：我們要如何幫助新員工快速了解公司創立以來經歷的重大變化？ B：我們在培訓室的牆上放一張大型【時間軸】吧，依序呈現每一個重要事件，從我們第一個產品上市到與最大競爭對手合併。"},{"w":"heritage","p":"n.","d":"the history, traditions, and buildings a country or group has from the past","c":"遺產；傳統文化","s":"A: Why has the city government decided not to tear down the old train station even though developers offered a lot of money? B: Local residents argued that the building is an important part of the town's cultural heritage, so officials plan to repair it and turn it into a museum and café.","t":"A：為什麼市政府決定不拆除舊火車站，即使開發商出了很多錢？ B：當地居民主張這棟建築是小鎮文化【遺產】的重要部分，所以官員計劃修復它，並把它改建成博物館和咖啡館。"},{"w":"artifact","p":"n.","d":"an object made by people long ago that has historical interest","c":"文物；手工藝品","s":"A: What will visitors be able to see at the new exhibition that opens at the city museum next Monday? B: The most famous artifact on display is a golden cup that farmers discovered in a field last year, and it will be shown beside tools, jewelry, and pottery from the same ancient village.","t":"A：市立博物館下週一開幕的新展覽中，參觀者可以看到什麼？ B：展出的最著名【文物】是農夫去年在田裡發現的一個金杯，它將和同一個古村落的工具、珠寶和陶器一起展示。"},{"w":"legacy","p":"n.","d":"something that a person leaves behind for people in the future","c":"遺產；留下的影響","s":"A: Why are so many employees attending the ceremony for the founder who passed away last month? B: People want to honor his legacy, because the hospital, the scholarship fund, and the training programs he started will continue to help thousands of people in this city for many years.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多員工出席上個月過世的創辦人的紀念儀式？ B：大家想要表彰他留下的【遺澤】，因為他創辦的醫院、獎學金基金和培訓計畫，將在未來很多年繼續幫助這座城市的成千上萬人。"},{"w":"context","p":"n.","d":"the situation or background in which something happens","c":"背景；脈絡","s":"A: Why did the professor tell us to read about the economy of the 1930s before discussing the novel in class next week? B: She said we need to understand the historical context, because the characters' money problems and hard choices only make sense when you know how many people were out of work then.","t":"A：為什麼教授叫我們在下週課堂討論那本小說之前，先閱讀關於1930年代經濟的資料？ B：她說我們需要了解歷史【背景】，因為只有知道當時有多少人失業，角色們的金錢問題和艱難選擇才說得通。"},{"w":"scholar","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies a subject deeply, especially at a university","c":"學者","s":"A: Who is giving the opening speech at the history conference that our company is sponsoring at the convention center? B: A well-known scholar from Oxford University will speak first, since she has spent over thirty years studying ancient trade routes and has published several books on the subject.","t":"A：我們公司在會展中心贊助的歷史研討會，開幕演講由誰主講？ B：一位來自牛津大學的知名【學者】將首先演講，因為她花了三十多年研究古代貿易路線，並出版了好幾本相關的書。"},{"w":"research","p":"n.","d":"careful study to discover new facts","c":"研究","s":"A: How long did it take the writer to finish her new book about the railway workers who built the line through the mountains? B: She spent almost six years doing research in libraries and museums, reading old letters, and interviewing the grandchildren of workers before she even started writing the first chapter.","t":"A：那位作家花了多久時間完成她那本關於修建穿山鐵路工人的新書？ B：她花了將近六年在圖書館和博物館做【研究】、閱讀舊信件，還訪問了工人的孫輩，然後才開始寫第一章。"},{"w":"analysis","p":"n.","d":"a careful study of something to understand it","c":"分析","s":"A: What did the experts discover when they examined the ink and paper of the letter that was supposedly written by the famous general? B: Their analysis showed that the paper was made in a factory about fifty years after his death, so the letter must be a fake created by a clever collector.","t":"A：專家檢驗那封據說是名將所寫的信的墨水和紙張時發現了什麼？ B：他們的【分析】顯示，那張紙是在他死後大約五十年才在工廠製造的，所以這封信一定是某位精明收藏家偽造的。"},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking at a book or source for information; a source used this way","c":"參考；參考資料","s":"A: Can I borrow the large dictionary of historical place names from the library desk and take it home over the weekend? B: I'm sorry, but that book is for reference only, which means you can read it in the reading room or make copies of a few pages, but it cannot leave the building.","t":"A：我可以從圖書館櫃檯借那本大部頭的歷史地名辭典，週末帶回家嗎？ B：很抱歉，那本書僅供【參考】，也就是說你可以在閱覽室閱讀或影印幾頁，但不能帶出館外。"},{"w":"illustrated","p":"adj.","d":"having pictures or drawings","c":"有插圖的；圖解的","s":"A: Which book would you recommend as a gift for my nephew, who is ten years old and loves learning about pirates and ships? B: I'd choose the illustrated edition of the history of sailing, because it has colorful drawings and maps on almost every page, which make the stories much easier for children to follow.","t":"A：我十歲的姪子很喜歡學習海盜和船的知識，你會推薦哪本書當禮物？ B：我會選那本航海史的【插圖】版，因為幾乎每一頁都有彩色圖畫和地圖，讓孩子更容易理解書中的故事。"},{"w":"scholarly","p":"adj.","d":"related to serious academic study","c":"學術的；學者的","s":"A: Why did the publisher reject the history professor's book even though the topic was so interesting? B: The editors said the writing was too scholarly for ordinary readers, with long footnotes and difficult academic language, so they suggested she send it to a university press instead.","t":"A：為什麼出版社拒絕了那位歷史教授的書，即使主題這麼有趣？ B：編輯說內容寫得太【學術】，不適合一般讀者，有長長的註腳和艱深的學術用語，所以他們建議她改投大學出版社。"},{"w":"comprehensive","p":"adj.","d":"including everything or almost everything","c":"全面的；詳盡的","s":"A: Is there one book that covers the whole story of our country, from the earliest settlers to the present day? B: Yes, the national library just published a comprehensive guide in five volumes that includes every major event, important person, and economic change, so many teachers already use it in their classes.","t":"A：有沒有一本書涵蓋我們國家的完整歷史，從最早的移民到現今？ B：有，國家圖書館剛出版了一套五冊的【全面】指南，收錄了每一個重大事件、重要人物和經濟變化，所以很多老師已經在課堂上使用。"}]},{"unit":174,"theme":"Hobby 嗜好","cards":[{"w":"pastime","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"消遣；娛樂","s":"A: What does your manager usually do on weekends now that the big project for the Singapore client is finally finished? B: Her favorite pastime is playing chess online with old friends, because it helps her forget about work and keeps her mind sharp for Monday meetings.","t":"A：既然新加坡客戶的大案子終於完成了，你們經理週末通常都做些什麼？ B：她最喜歡的【消遣】是和老朋友在線上下西洋棋，因為這能讓她暫時忘掉工作，也讓她的頭腦在週一開會時保持敏銳。"},{"w":"interest","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of wanting to know about or do something","c":"興趣","s":"A: Why did the HR department add a question about personal activities to the new staff survey that everyone received this morning? B: They want to start a few after-work groups, so they need to know which employees share an interest in music, sports, or cooking before booking any rooms.","t":"A：為什麼人資部在今天早上大家收到的新員工問卷裡，加了一題關於個人活動的問題？ B：他們想成立幾個下班後的小組，所以在預訂場地之前，需要知道哪些員工對音樂、運動或烹飪有共同的【興趣】。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"time when you are not working and can relax","c":"閒暇；空閒","s":"A: Have you noticed that the new office building has a rooftop garden, a small library, and even a table tennis room on the fifth floor? B: Yes, the company believes that staff who enjoy their leisure time during long lunch breaks will come back to their desks feeling calmer and more productive.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到新辦公大樓有屋頂花園、小圖書館，甚至五樓還有一間桌球室？ B：有啊，公司認為員工在較長的午休中好好享受【閒暇】時光，回到座位時會更平靜、更有效率。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities people do for fun and relaxation","c":"娛樂；休閒活動","s":"A: Where is the city planning to spend the extra money it received from the tourism tax this year, according to this morning's newspaper? B: Most of it will go to a new recreation center near the river, which will include a swimming pool, tennis courts, and free classes for local families.","t":"A：根據今天早上的報紙，市政府打算把今年觀光稅多收到的錢花在哪裡？ B：大部分會用在河邊一座新的【休閒娛樂】中心，裡面會有游泳池、網球場，還有給當地家庭的免費課程。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that someone has gathered because they like them","c":"收藏；收藏品","s":"A: Why is there a line of people waiting outside the small shop across from our office every Saturday morning before it even opens? B: The owner is showing his huge collection of old cameras and vintage postcards, and many visitors come from other cities just to see the rare pieces.","t":"A：為什麼每個星期六早上，我們辦公室對面那家小店還沒開門，外面就有人在排隊？ B：老闆正在展示他大量的老相機和復古明信片【收藏】，很多遊客專程從其他城市來看這些稀有的物品。"},{"w":"craft","p":"n.","d":"an activity of making things by hand","c":"手工藝","s":"A: What kind of activity are you planning for the children's corner at the company's family day next month in the park? B: We'll set up a craft table where kids can make paper animals and simple bracelets with their parents, and every child can take home what they made.","t":"A：下個月公司在公園舉辦的家庭日，你們打算在兒童區安排什麼活動？ B：我們會設一張【手工藝】桌，讓孩子和爸媽一起做紙動物和簡單的手環，每個孩子都可以把自己做的作品帶回家。"},{"w":"painting","p":"n.","d":"the activity of making pictures with paint","c":"繪畫；畫畫","s":"A: Did you know that our receptionist sold three of her pictures at the art fair downtown last weekend for quite a good price? B: Yes, she started painting with watercolors two years ago after work, and now she spends almost every Sunday afternoon in the park creating landscapes of the mountains.","t":"A：你知道我們的櫃檯人員上週末在市中心的藝術市集，以相當好的價格賣出了三幅畫嗎？ B：知道啊，她兩年前下班後開始用水彩【畫畫】，現在幾乎每個星期天下午都在公園裡畫山景。"},{"w":"drawing","p":"n.","d":"a picture made with a pencil or pen","c":"素描；繪圖","s":"A: How does the new designer prepare her ideas before she shows them to the client at the weekly meeting with the marketing team? B: She always begins with a quick pencil drawing on paper during her train ride to work, because she says it helps her see the shape of the product more clearly.","t":"A：新來的設計師在每週和行銷團隊開會、把點子拿給客戶看之前，是怎麼準備的？ B：她總是在搭火車上班時先在紙上快速畫一張鉛筆【素描】，她說這能幫她更清楚地看出產品的外形。"},{"w":"photography","p":"n.","d":"the activity or job of taking photographs","c":"攝影","s":"A: Who took those beautiful pictures of the factory and the staff that appear in our new company brochure and on the website? B: Kevin from accounting did, because photography has been his weekend hobby for years, and he even won a local contest last spring with a photo of the harbor at sunset.","t":"A：公司新簡介和網站上那些工廠和員工的漂亮照片是誰拍的？ B：是會計部的凱文拍的，因為【攝影】多年來一直是他的週末嗜好，他去年春天還以一張港口夕陽的照片贏得了地方比賽。"},{"w":"gardening","p":"n.","d":"the activity of growing plants and flowers in a garden","c":"園藝","s":"A: Why does Mrs. Lin from the finance office always bring fresh tomatoes and herbs to share with everyone in the kitchen on Mondays? B: She has been into gardening since she moved to a house with a big backyard, and she grows far more vegetables than her family can possibly eat.","t":"A：為什麼財務部的林太太每週一總是帶新鮮番茄和香草到茶水間跟大家分享？ B：自從她搬到有大後院的房子後就迷上了【園藝】，她種的蔬菜多到家人根本吃不完。"},{"w":"cooking","p":"n.","d":"the activity of preparing food","c":"烹飪；做菜","s":"A: What is the team-building event that the department manager has planned for us before the end of the year? B: We are going to take a cooking class at a restaurant downtown, where a professional chef will teach us how to prepare three Italian dishes and then we'll eat them together.","t":"A：部門經理在年底前幫我們安排的團隊建立活動是什麼？ B：我們要去市中心一家餐廳上【烹飪】課，專業主廚會教我們做三道義大利菜，然後大家再一起吃掉。"},{"w":"baking","p":"n.","d":"the activity of making bread, cakes, or cookies in an oven","c":"烘焙","s":"A: Where did all these delicious cookies and the chocolate cake in the meeting room come from this afternoon? B: Our new intern brought them, because baking is her favorite way to relax on weekends, and she wanted to thank everyone for helping her during her first busy month here.","t":"A：今天下午會議室裡這些好吃的餅乾和巧克力蛋糕是從哪裡來的？ B：是我們新來的實習生帶來的，因為【烘焙】是她週末最喜歡的放鬆方式，她想謝謝大家在她來這裡忙碌的第一個月幫了她。"},{"w":"fishing","p":"n.","d":"the activity of catching fish","c":"釣魚","s":"A: Why is the sales director taking a long weekend off right after the quarterly report is submitted next Thursday? B: He is going on a fishing trip with his brother to a quiet lake in the mountains, where they plan to rent a small boat and stay in a wooden cabin.","t":"A：為什麼業務總監在下週四交出季報後，馬上要請一個長週末的假？ B：他要和他哥哥去山裡一座安靜的湖進行【釣魚】之旅，他們打算租一艘小船，住在木屋裡。"},{"w":"hiking","p":"n.","d":"the activity of taking long walks in the countryside or mountains","c":"健行；登山","s":"A: Do you have any suggestions for something healthy and cheap that our team could do together on a Saturday morning in spring? B: How about hiking on the trail behind the national park, since it only takes about three hours and there's a nice tea house at the top where we can rest.","t":"A：你有沒有什麼建議，是我們團隊春天某個星期六早上可以一起做、既健康又便宜的活動？ B：去國家公園後面的步道【健行】怎麼樣？只要大約三個小時，山頂還有一間不錯的茶館可以休息。"},{"w":"cycling","p":"n.","d":"the activity of riding a bicycle","c":"騎自行車","s":"A: How do you manage to stay so fit even though you sit in front of a computer for nearly ten hours every working day? B: I joined a cycling group last year, and every Sunday we ride about fifty kilometers along the river path before having breakfast together at a café.","t":"A：你每個工作天都要在電腦前坐將近十個小時，是怎麼保持這麼好的身材的？ B：我去年加入了一個【騎自行車】的團體，每個星期天我們沿著河濱道騎大約五十公里，然後一起在咖啡館吃早餐。"},{"w":"collect","p":"v.","d":"to get and keep things of one type because you like them","c":"收集；收藏","s":"A: Why does Mr. Huang keep asking visitors from overseas offices to bring him coins from their home countries? B: He likes to collect money from different places around the world, and he keeps the coins in special albums that he proudly shows to clients who visit his office.","t":"A：為什麼黃先生一直請海外辦公室的訪客幫他帶他們國家的硬幣？ B：他喜歡【收集】世界各地的錢幣，並把硬幣放在特製的收藏冊裡，很自豪地拿給來他辦公室的客戶看。"},{"w":"create","p":"v.","d":"to make something new","c":"創作；創造","s":"A: What made you decide to sign up for the weekend pottery course at the community center near the train station? B: I spend all week typing reports and answering emails, so I really wanted to create something beautiful with my own hands that I could actually use at home.","t":"A：是什麼讓你決定報名火車站附近社區中心的週末陶藝課？ B：我整個星期都在打報告、回電子郵件，所以很想親手【創作】一些漂亮又真的能在家裡用的東西。"},{"w":"practice","p":"v.","d":"to do something again and again to get better at it","c":"練習","s":"A: How did the new account manager become such a good guitar player while working full-time at a busy company like ours? B: She told me she tries to practice for at least thirty minutes every evening after dinner, even when she feels tired, and she takes lessons twice a month.","t":"A：新來的客戶經理在我們這種忙碌的公司全職工作，是怎麼把吉他彈得這麼好的？ B：她告訴我她每天晚餐後都盡量【練習】至少三十分鐘，即使累了也一樣，而且她每個月上兩次課。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it","c":"探索；探險","s":"A: What do you plan to do during your free afternoon in Kyoto after the trade show ends next Wednesday? B: I want to explore the quiet side streets near the old temples with my camera, because I've heard there are many small shops and hidden gardens that most tourists never find.","t":"A：下週三商展結束後，你在京都空出來的那個下午打算做什麼？ B：我想帶著相機去【探索】老寺廟附近安靜的小巷，因為聽說那裡有很多大部分觀光客都找不到的小店和隱藏的庭園。"},{"w":"relaxing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel calm and comfortable","c":"令人放鬆的","s":"A: Why do so many people in our department spend their lunch break doing jigsaw puzzles in the staff lounge these days? B: They say it is very relaxing after a stressful morning of phone calls and meetings, and finishing a big puzzle together also makes everyone feel more like a team.","t":"A：為什麼我們部門最近有那麼多人午休時在員工休息室拼拼圖？ B：他們說在接了一早上電話、開了一早上會之後，拼圖非常【令人放鬆】，而且一起完成一幅大拼圖也讓大家更有團隊的感覺。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"using imagination to make new things or ideas","c":"有創意的；創造性的","s":"A: Why did the company decide to let staff use the empty conference room for painting and music on Friday afternoons? B: The managers believe that people who have a creative outlet outside their regular tasks come up with better ideas when they work on new advertising campaigns.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定讓員工在星期五下午使用空的會議室畫畫和玩音樂？ B：主管們認為，在日常工作以外有【創意】抒發管道的人，在做新的廣告企劃時會想出更好的點子。"},{"w":"enjoyable","p":"adj.","d":"giving pleasure; fun","c":"令人愉快的；有趣的","s":"A: How was the board game night that the HR team organized for new employees at the café last Friday evening? B: It was really enjoyable, because the games were easy to learn, the snacks were free, and I finally got to know people from other departments that I rarely talk to.","t":"A：人資團隊上週五晚上在咖啡館為新員工辦的桌遊之夜怎麼樣？ B：真的很【愉快】，因為遊戲很容易學、點心免費，而且我終於認識了平常很少說話的其他部門同事。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的；流行的","s":"A: Why did the sports center near our office extend its yoga classes to seven days a week starting this month? B: The classes have become so popular among office workers in this area that people were often turned away at the door because there weren't enough mats for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近的運動中心從這個月開始把瑜伽課延長到一週七天？ B：這些課在這一帶的上班族之間變得非常【受歡迎】，常常因為瑜伽墊不夠，有人在門口就被拒絕入場。"},{"w":"indoor","p":"adj.","d":"done or used inside a building","c":"室內的","s":"A: What should we plan for the staff outing if the weather report says it will rain all weekend in the north? B: Let's book an indoor climbing gym downtown instead, since it has instructors, equipment for beginners, and a large café where people can rest and chat afterward.","t":"A：如果氣象報告說北部整個週末都會下雨，員工出遊我們該怎麼安排？ B：那我們改訂市中心的【室內】攀岩館吧，那裡有教練、適合初學者的裝備，還有一間大咖啡廳，大家結束後可以休息聊天。"},{"w":"outdoor","p":"adj.","d":"done or happening outside","c":"戶外的","s":"A: Why are so many young employees asking for Friday afternoons off during the autumn months this year? B: Many of them have taken up outdoor sports like rock climbing and camping, and they want to drive to the mountains early before the weekend traffic becomes terrible.","t":"A：為什麼今年秋天有這麼多年輕員工申請星期五下午請假？ B：他們很多人開始從事攀岩、露營之類的【戶外】運動，想在週末交通變得很糟之前提早開車上山。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often and at the same times","c":"定期地；規律地","s":"A: How has your health changed since you joined the company badminton team at the beginning of this year? B: Because I now play regularly every Tuesday and Thursday after work, I sleep much better, I have more energy in the mornings, and my doctor says my blood pressure has improved.","t":"A：自從你今年初加入公司羽球隊之後，健康有什麼改變？ B：因為我現在每週二和週四下班後都【規律地】打球，我睡得好多了，早上更有精神，醫生也說我的血壓改善了。"},{"w":"occasionally","p":"adv.","d":"sometimes but not often","c":"偶爾；有時","s":"A: Do you still go to the art museum near the central station as often as you did when you were a student? B: Only occasionally now, because my new job keeps me very busy, but I try to visit whenever there's a special exhibition that I really don't want to miss.","t":"A：你現在還像學生時代那樣常去中央車站附近的美術館嗎？ B：現在只是【偶爾】去，因為新工作讓我非常忙，但只要有我真的不想錯過的特展，我都會盡量去看。"},{"w":"actively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that involves doing things with energy","c":"積極地；主動地","s":"A: Why was Ms. Chen chosen to organize this year's charity run for our company and its business partners? B: She has actively taken part in local running events for many years, so she knows how to plan the route, find sponsors, and keep hundreds of volunteers well organized.","t":"A：為什麼選陳小姐來籌辦今年我們公司和合作夥伴的慈善路跑？ B：她多年來一直【積極地】參加當地的路跑活動，所以知道怎麼規劃路線、找贊助商，以及把數百名志工安排得井井有條。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"an ability to do something well because you have practiced it","c":"技能；技巧","s":"A: Why did the interviewer ask you about your hobbies at the end of yesterday's job interview for the design position? B: She said that hobbies often show a useful skill, and when I explained that I build model airplanes, she agreed that I must be patient and pay close attention to details.","t":"A：昨天設計職位的面試最後，面試官為什麼問你嗜好？ B：她說嗜好常常能展現一項有用的【技能】，當我說明我會組裝模型飛機時，她也同意我一定很有耐心、很注重細節。"},{"w":"talent","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability to do something well","c":"天分；才能","s":"A: Did you hear the receptionist sing at the company's year-end party at the hotel last night? B: Yes, she has an amazing talent for music, and several managers asked her whether she would like to perform again at the opening ceremony of our new branch office next spring.","t":"A：你昨晚在飯店的公司尾牙有聽到櫃檯人員唱歌嗎？ B：有，她在音樂方面有驚人的【天分】，好幾位主管問她明年春天新分公司開幕典禮時願不願意再表演一次。"},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of interest and excitement","c":"熱忱；熱情","s":"A: How did the new photography club manage to attract more than forty members in only two weeks after it was announced? B: The organizer's enthusiasm was really contagious, because he gave short talks in every department, showed his best photos, and offered free lessons to complete beginners.","t":"A：新的攝影社是怎麼在宣布後短短兩週內就吸引到四十多名成員的？ B：發起人的【熱忱】很有感染力，他到每個部門做簡短介紹、展示他最好的照片，還提供完全新手免費課程。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"the willingness to give a lot of time and effort to something","c":"投入；奉獻","s":"A: How did the warehouse supervisor finish building a full-size wooden boat in his garage in just three years? B: It took real dedication, since he worked on it every weekend and many evenings after his shift, and he even studied old books to learn traditional building methods.","t":"A：倉庫主管是怎麼在短短三年內，在自家車庫裡造好一艘實際大小的木船？ B：那需要真正的【投入】，因為他每個週末和許多下班後的晚上都在做，甚至還研讀舊書來學習傳統的造船方法。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who share the same interests or live in the same area","c":"社群；社區","s":"A: Why did you start going to the small board game shop near the subway station every Thursday night after work? B: It has a friendly community of players of all ages, and the regular members always welcome newcomers, explain the rules patiently, and invite everyone to stay for dinner afterward.","t":"A：你為什麼開始每週四下班後都去捷運站附近那家小桌遊店？ B：那裡有一個由各年齡層玩家組成的友善【社群】，常客總是歡迎新人、耐心解說規則，還會邀請大家結束後留下來一起吃晚餐。"},{"w":"club","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who meet to do an activity together","c":"社團；俱樂部","s":"A: Is there any way for new employees in this building to meet people from other companies outside of work? B: You could join the running club that meets in the lobby every Wednesday evening, since it has members from almost every office here and they often go for dinner after the run.","t":"A：這棟大樓的新員工有沒有什麼辦法在工作之外認識其他公司的人？ B：你可以加入每週三晚上在大廳集合的跑步【社團】，因為成員幾乎來自這裡的每間辦公室，跑完步後他們常常一起去吃晚餐。"}]},{"unit":175,"theme":"Holiday 假期","cards":[{"w":"all-in package","p":"n.phr.","d":"a holiday deal whose price includes travel, hotel, meals and drinks","c":"全包式套裝行程","s":"A: My parents want a relaxing trip to Bali next spring, but they hate worrying about extra costs for meals, drinks, and activities after they arrive. What would you suggest? B: I would book an all-in package for them, because the price covers flights, the hotel, all meals, and even airport transfers, so they can simply enjoy themselves.","t":"A：我爸媽想在明年春天去峇里島輕鬆旅行，但他們很討厭抵達後還要擔心餐點、飲料和活動的額外費用。你有什麼建議？ B：我會幫他們訂一個【全包式套裝行程】，因為價格包含機票、飯店、所有餐點，甚至機場接送，所以他們只要好好享受就行了。"},{"w":"package holiday","p":"n.phr.","d":"a holiday where flights and hotel are sold together at one price","c":"套裝度假行程","s":"A: Our sales team finally hit its yearly target, and the manager wants to reward everyone with a trip, but nobody has time to plan flights and hotels separately. What should we do? B: Let's contact a travel agency and choose a package holiday to Okinawa, since the agency arranges transport and accommodation together at one reasonable price.","t":"A：我們業務團隊終於達成年度目標，經理想用一趟旅行獎勵大家，但沒有人有時間分別安排機票和飯店。我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們聯絡旅行社，選一個去沖繩的【套裝度假行程】吧，因為旅行社會以一個合理的價格把交通和住宿一起安排好。"},{"w":"brochure","p":"n.","d":"a small printed book with pictures and information about a product or trip","c":"宣傳手冊；小冊子","s":"A: I'm helping a customer at the travel counter who can't decide between a beach trip and a mountain trip for her family this summer. Do we have anything she can take home? B: Yes, give her our new brochure, which has colorful photos, hotel descriptions, and price lists for both trips, so she can compare them with her husband tonight.","t":"A：我正在旅遊櫃檯協助一位客人，她無法決定今年夏天要帶家人去海邊還是山上旅行。我們有什麼東西可以讓她帶回家嗎？ B：有，給她我們新的【宣傳手冊】，裡面有兩種行程的彩色照片、飯店介紹和價目表，這樣她今晚就可以和先生一起比較。"},{"w":"holiday destination","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where people go for a holiday","c":"度假地點；度假勝地","s":"A: The marketing department is preparing an online campaign to attract more visitors from Japan and Korea to our island next year. What should the main message be? B: We should present the island as a perfect holiday destination for families, because it has safe beaches, friendly local people, delicious seafood, and many hotels that welcome children.","t":"A：行銷部正在準備一個線上宣傳活動，希望明年吸引更多日本和韓國遊客來我們的島。主要訊息應該是什麼？ B：我們應該把這座島塑造成適合家庭的完美【度假勝地】，因為這裡有安全的海灘、友善的當地人、美味的海鮮，還有許多歡迎兒童的飯店。"},{"w":"holiday resort","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large place with hotels, pools and activities where people go on holiday","c":"度假村","s":"A: I heard that you stayed somewhere special during your company's reward trip to Phuket last month. Was it a normal hotel in the city center? B: No, it was a large holiday resort by the sea with three swimming pools, several restaurants, a spa, and evening shows, so we hardly needed to leave the property at all.","t":"A：聽說你上個月參加公司去普吉島的獎勵旅遊時住在很特別的地方。是市中心的一般飯店嗎？ B：不是，那是一座海邊的大型【度假村】，有三座游泳池、好幾間餐廳、一間水療中心和晚間表演，所以我們幾乎完全不需要離開園區。"},{"w":"passport control","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place at an airport or border where officers check passports","c":"護照查驗處；證照查驗","s":"A: Our flight lands in London at seven in the morning, and the client meeting starts at ten. Do you think we will have enough time to get to the office? B: It should be fine, but the line at passport control can be very long in the morning, so we should keep our documents ready and fill in the arrival forms on the plane.","t":"A：我們的班機早上七點降落倫敦，客戶會議十點開始。你覺得我們有足夠的時間趕到辦公室嗎？ B：應該沒問題，但早上【護照查驗處】的隊伍可能很長，所以我們應該把證件準備好，並在飛機上先填好入境表格。"},{"w":"package tour","p":"n.phr.","d":"an organized trip with a guide where travel, hotels and meals are arranged","c":"套裝旅遊；跟團旅遊","s":"A: My grandmother wants to visit several famous cities in Europe, but she doesn't speak English and feels nervous about traveling on her own. What do you recommend? B: A package tour would suit her well, because a guide travels with the group, explains the history of each place, and takes care of the bus, the hotels, and the meals.","t":"A：我奶奶想去歐洲幾個有名的城市，但她不會說英文，而且對自己旅行感到緊張。你推薦什麼？ B：【跟團旅遊】會很適合她，因為導遊會跟團一起行動，講解每個地方的歷史，並負責安排遊覽車、飯店和餐點。"},{"w":"low season","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time of year when few people travel and prices are lower","c":"淡季","s":"A: The hotel manager is worried because there are very few guests in November, and many of our rooms stay empty for weeks. How can we bring more people in? B: We could offer special discounts during the low season, such as free breakfast and cheaper room rates, so that budget travelers and retired couples will choose our hotel.","t":"A：飯店經理很擔心，因為十一月客人很少，我們很多房間好幾個星期都空著。我們要怎麼吸引更多人來？ B：我們可以在【淡季】期間提供特別優惠，例如免費早餐和較便宜的房價，這樣精打細算的旅客和退休夫婦就會選擇我們的飯店。"},{"w":"high season","p":"n.phr.","d":"the busiest time of year for travel, when prices are highest","c":"旺季","s":"A: I'm planning to take my family to the beach in July, but my coworker warned me that it might be expensive and very crowded. Is that true? B: Yes, July is the high season, so hotel prices almost double and popular restaurants are full, which means you should book your rooms and tables several months in advance.","t":"A：我打算七月帶家人去海邊，但我同事警告我那時可能很貴又很擁擠。是真的嗎？ B：是的，七月是【旺季】，所以飯店價格幾乎翻倍，熱門餐廳也都客滿，這表示你應該提前幾個月預訂房間和餐桌。"},{"w":"off-season","p":"n.","d":"the quiet period of the year when a place has few visitors","c":"淡季；非旺季","s":"A: Why did you and your husband decide to visit the ski town in late spring instead of during the winter holidays like most people? B: We went in the off-season on purpose, because the streets were quiet, the hotel gave us a large room at half price, and we could enjoy the mountain views without any crowds.","t":"A：為什麼你和你先生決定在晚春去那個滑雪小鎮，而不是像大多數人一樣在冬季假期去？ B：我們是故意在【非旺季】去的，因為街上很安靜，飯店用半價給我們一間大房間，而且我們可以在沒有人潮的情況下欣賞山景。"},{"w":"short break","p":"n.phr.","d":"a holiday of only a few days","c":"短期度假；短暫休假","s":"A: You look really tired after finishing that big project, and you haven't taken any days off this year. Are you going to rest at all? B: I'm planning a short break in Hualien this weekend, just two nights at a small guesthouse near the ocean, so I can relax, sleep well, and come back to work full of energy.","t":"A：你完成那個大專案後看起來真的很累，而且你今年都還沒請過假。你打算休息一下嗎？ B：我計畫這個週末去花蓮【短期度假】，只在海邊一間小民宿住兩晚，這樣我就能放鬆、好好睡一覺，然後精神飽滿地回來上班。"}]},{"unit":176,"theme":"Home 家","cards":[{"w":"currently","p":"adv.","d":"at the present time","c":"目前；現在","s":"A: Are you still renting that small flat near the train station, or did you finally buy the house you showed me online last month? B: I am currently staying with my sister for a few weeks, because the sale of the new house will not be completed until the bank approves my loan.","t":"A：你還在租火車站附近那間小公寓嗎？還是你終於買下上個月在網路上給我看的那棟房子了？ B：我【目前】暫時住在我姊姊家幾個星期，因為新房子要等銀行核准我的貸款後才能完成交易。"},{"w":"afford","p":"v.","d":"to have enough money to pay for something","c":"負擔得起；買得起","s":"A: Why did you and your husband decide to look for a home in a smaller town instead of staying in the city center near your offices? B: Housing prices downtown have risen so quickly that we simply could not afford a three-bedroom apartment there on our two salaries, even with help from our parents.","t":"A：你和你先生為什麼決定在小鎮找房子，而不是留在離公司近的市中心？ B：市中心的房價漲得太快，即使有父母的幫忙，靠我們兩份薪水也根本【負擔不起】那裡的三房公寓。"},{"w":"yard","p":"n.","d":"an area of land next to a house, often with grass","c":"院子；庭院","s":"A: Is there enough space at your new place for the children to play outside safely when the weather is nice on weekends? B: Yes, there is a large yard behind the house with a wooden fence around it, so the kids can run around and the dog cannot escape into the street.","t":"A：你新家有足夠的空間讓孩子們在週末天氣好的時候安全地在戶外玩嗎？ B：有的，房子後面有一個很大的【院子】，四周圍著木頭籬笆，所以孩子們可以到處跑，狗也跑不到街上去。"},{"w":"veranda","p":"n.","d":"a covered area with a floor along the outside of a house","c":"陽台；走廊（有頂的）","s":"A: Where do you usually have breakfast in the summer, since your kitchen gets so hot in the morning sun? B: We carry our coffee and toast out to the veranda at the front of the house, where the roof gives us shade and we can watch our neighbors walking to work.","t":"A：既然你家廚房在早上的陽光下會變得很熱，你們夏天通常在哪裡吃早餐？ B：我們會把咖啡和吐司端到房子前面的【有頂陽台】，那裡的屋頂可以遮陽，我們還可以看鄰居走路去上班。"},{"w":"spot","p":"n.","d":"a particular place","c":"地點；處所","s":"A: Your new apartment has such a wonderful view of the river and the mountains; how did you manage to find it so quickly? B: A coworker told me about it before it was advertised, and I knew right away it was the perfect spot because it is quiet but still close to the subway.","t":"A：你的新公寓可以看到河流和山景，景色真棒；你是怎麼這麼快就找到的？ B：在廣告刊登之前，一位同事就先告訴我了，我馬上知道那是個完美的【地點】，因為那裡很安靜，但又離捷運很近。"},{"w":"outskirts","p":"n.","d":"the outer areas of a town or city","c":"郊區；市郊","s":"A: Doesn't it take you a long time to drive to the office every morning now that you have moved out of the downtown area? B: It takes about forty minutes, but living on the outskirts of the city means we pay much lower rent and have fresh air, trees, and a quiet street.","t":"A：你搬離市中心之後，現在每天早上開車到公司不是要花很久的時間嗎？ B：大約要四十分鐘，但住在城市的【郊區】代表我們付的房租便宜很多，而且有新鮮空氣、樹木和安靜的街道。"},{"w":"uniquely","p":"adv.","d":"in a special way that is not like anything else","c":"獨特地；獨一無二地","s":"A: Why are so many design magazines writing articles about the old house that your architect friend rebuilt last year? B: The house is uniquely designed, with a glass roof over the living room and walls made from recycled wood, so it looks different from every other home in the neighborhood.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多設計雜誌都在報導你那位建築師朋友去年重建的老房子？ B：那棟房子設計得很【獨特】，客廳上方是玻璃屋頂，牆壁是用回收木材做的，所以看起來和附近其他房子都不一樣。"},{"w":"patio","p":"n.","d":"a flat area with a hard floor next to a house, used for sitting outside","c":"露台；天井","s":"A: Where are you planning to hold the dinner for your team after the project is finished next Saturday evening? B: I am going to set up two long tables on the patio behind my house, because the stone floor is flat and there is enough room for twelve people to eat outdoors.","t":"A：下週六晚上專案結束後，你打算在哪裡為你的團隊舉辦晚餐？ B：我打算在我家後面的【露台】上擺兩張長桌，因為石板地面很平坦，而且有足夠的空間讓十二個人在戶外用餐。"},{"w":"port","p":"n.","d":"a town or city with a harbor where ships load and unload","c":"港口；港市","s":"A: What made you choose to buy a home in Keelung rather than in Taipei, where most of your clients are based? B: I grew up near the sea, and I love living in a busy port where I can watch the cargo ships arriving and eat fresh seafood every weekend.","t":"A：你的客戶大多在台北，是什麼原因讓你選擇在基隆而不是台北買房子？ B：我在海邊長大，我很喜歡住在熱鬧的【港口城市】，可以看貨船進港，每個週末還能吃到新鮮的海鮮。"},{"w":"barbeque","p":"n.","d":"a meal or party where food is cooked outdoors over a fire","c":"烤肉；烤肉聚會","s":"A: What are you doing this Sunday afternoon now that the weather has finally become warm and sunny again? B: My family is having a barbeque in the back of our house, so my father will grill chicken and corn while my cousins bring salads and cold drinks for everyone.","t":"A：天氣終於又變得溫暖晴朗了，你這個星期天下午要做什麼？ B：我們家要在屋後舉辦【烤肉聚會】，我爸爸會烤雞肉和玉米，表兄弟姊妹們則會帶沙拉和冷飲給大家。"},{"w":"apartment block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large building divided into many separate flats","c":"公寓大樓","s":"A: How many families live in the new building that was just finished across the road from our office? B: It is a twelve-story apartment block with about ninety units, and I heard that most of the flats were sold to young couples before construction was even completed.","t":"A：我們公司對面剛完工的新大樓裡住了多少戶人家？ B：那是一棟十二層樓的【公寓大樓】，大約有九十戶，我聽說大部分的房子在還沒蓋好之前就賣給了年輕夫妻。"},{"w":"back garden","p":"n.phr.","d":"a garden behind a house","c":"後花園；後院","s":"A: Your tomatoes and peppers look so fresh; did you buy them at the farmers' market near the station this morning? B: No, I grew them myself in the small back garden behind our kitchen, and I water them every evening after I come home from work.","t":"A：你的番茄和甜椒看起來好新鮮；是今天早上在車站附近的農夫市集買的嗎？ B：不是，是我自己種在廚房後面的小【後花園】裡的，我每天下班回家後都會幫它們澆水。"},{"w":"detached house","p":"n.phr.","d":"a house that stands alone and is not joined to another house","c":"獨棟房屋","s":"A: Why did you decide to sell your flat in the city and move your whole family out to the countryside last spring? B: We wanted a detached house with walls that are not shared with neighbors, so the kids can play the piano loudly without anyone knocking on the door to complain.","t":"A：你去年春天為什麼決定賣掉市區的公寓，帶全家搬到鄉下？ B：我們想要一棟不和鄰居共用牆壁的【獨棟房屋】，這樣孩子們大聲彈鋼琴也不會有人來敲門抱怨。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區；近郊住宅區","s":"A: Do you think it is a good idea for our company to open a new branch outside the city center next year? B: Yes, because many young families have moved to the quiet suburb north of the river, and they would prefer a bank close to their homes and schools.","t":"A：你認為我們公司明年在市中心以外開設新分行是個好主意嗎？ B：是的，因為很多年輕家庭已經搬到河北岸那個安靜的【郊區住宅區】，他們會比較喜歡離家和學校近的銀行。"},{"w":"terraced house","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of a row of houses joined together by their side walls","c":"連棟房屋；排屋","s":"A: What kind of home did you live in when you were working at the London office for three years? B: I rented a narrow terraced house on a long street where every home was connected to the next one, so I could sometimes hear my neighbor's television through the wall.","t":"A：你在倫敦辦公室工作那三年住的是什麼樣的房子？ B：我租了一間狹窄的【連棟房屋】，在一條長街上，每一戶都和隔壁相連，所以我有時候隔著牆壁都聽得到鄰居的電視聲。"},{"w":"dream home","p":"n.phr.","d":"the perfect house that someone has always wanted","c":"夢想中的家","s":"A: You have been saving money and looking at houses for nearly ten years; have you finally found something you really like? B: Yes, we just signed the contract for our dream home, a bright wooden house with a big kitchen, a quiet garden, and a lovely view of the lake.","t":"A：你存錢看房子已經快十年了，終於找到真正喜歡的了嗎？ B：是的，我們剛簽約買下我們【夢想中的家】，那是一棟明亮的木屋，有大廚房、安靜的花園，還有美麗的湖景。"},{"w":"layout","p":"n.","d":"the way the rooms and parts of a place are arranged","c":"格局；布局","s":"A: The apartment is not very big, so why did you say it feels much more comfortable than your old one? B: The layout is much better, because the kitchen opens into the living room and both bedrooms are at the quiet end, away from the front door and the elevator.","t":"A：這間公寓不是很大，為什麼你說住起來比以前那間舒服很多？ B：它的【格局】好很多，因為廚房和客廳是相通的，兩間臥室都在安靜的那一頭，遠離大門和電梯。"},{"w":"troublesome","p":"adj.","d":"causing problems or worry again and again","c":"麻煩的；令人頭痛的","s":"A: Have you fixed the problem with the water heater in your bathroom, or are you still taking cold showers in the morning? B: It has been really troublesome, because the repairman came twice last week but it broke down again yesterday, so the landlord has promised to buy a new one.","t":"A：你浴室熱水器的問題修好了嗎？還是你早上還在洗冷水澡？ B：這真的很【麻煩】，因為修理工上週來了兩次，但昨天又壞了，所以房東答應會買一台新的。"},{"w":"fully-furnished","p":"adj.","d":"having all the furniture needed already in it","c":"附全套家具的","s":"A: Will you need to buy beds, sofas, and a dining table when you move to Singapore for your new job next month? B: No, the company has rented a fully-furnished flat for me, so everything from the bed to the washing machine is already there and I only need to bring my clothes.","t":"A：你下個月為了新工作搬到新加坡時，需要買床、沙發和餐桌嗎？ B：不用，公司幫我租了一間【附全套家具的】公寓，所以從床到洗衣機一應俱全，我只要帶衣服過去就好。"},{"w":"hall of residence","p":"n.phr.","d":"a building where university students live","c":"大學學生宿舍","s":"A: Where did you live during your first year of university before you moved into a shared flat with your friends? B: I stayed in a hall of residence on campus, where about two hundred students had their own small rooms and shared a large kitchen on each floor.","t":"A：你大學一年級在和朋友合租公寓之前住在哪裡？ B：我住在校園裡的【學生宿舍】，那裡大約有兩百名學生各自擁有小房間，每層樓共用一間大廚房。"},{"w":"home comforts","p":"n.phr.","d":"the things that make life at home pleasant and easy","c":"家中的舒適享受","s":"A: How did you feel after spending three weeks working on that construction site in the desert with no hot water? B: It was an interesting experience, but I really missed my home comforts, such as a soft bed, a hot shower, and my mother's cooking every evening.","t":"A：你在那個沒有熱水的沙漠工地工作了三個星期，感覺怎麼樣？ B：那是很有趣的經驗，但我真的很想念【家裡的舒適享受】，像是柔軟的床、熱水澡，還有媽媽每天晚上煮的飯菜。"},{"w":"house-warming party","p":"n.phr.","d":"a party for friends after moving into a new home","c":"喬遷派對；暖屋派對","s":"A: Now that you have finally unpacked all the boxes in your new apartment, are you planning to invite anyone over? B: Yes, we are holding a house-warming party next Saturday night, so please come and meet our new neighbors, and feel free to bring your partner too.","t":"A：你終於把新公寓裡的箱子都拆完了，打算邀請誰來家裡坐坐嗎？ B：有，我們下週六晚上要辦一場【喬遷派對】，請你來認識我們的新鄰居，也歡迎帶你的另一半一起來。"},{"w":"exhausting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel extremely tired","c":"令人筋疲力盡的","s":"A: You look very tired this morning; did you finish moving all your furniture to the new place over the weekend? B: Yes, but it was exhausting, because the building has no elevator and we had to carry the heavy sofa and the bookshelves up to the fifth floor by ourselves.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來好累；你週末把所有家具都搬到新家了嗎？ B：搬完了，但真是【累死人了】，因為那棟大樓沒有電梯，我們得自己把很重的沙發和書架搬上五樓。"},{"w":"move into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start living in a new home","c":"搬進；遷入","s":"A: When will the builders finish painting and cleaning your new apartment so that you can stop paying rent at the old place? B: If everything goes according to plan, we will move into the new flat on the first of next month, just before our daughter starts school.","t":"A：工人什麼時候會完成新公寓的油漆和清潔，讓你不用再付舊房子的房租？ B：如果一切按照計畫，我們下個月一號就會【搬進】新公寓，剛好在女兒開學之前。"},{"w":"chill out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to relax completely","c":"放鬆；休息一下","s":"A: What do you usually do when you get home after a long day of meetings and phone calls with difficult customers? B: I like to chill out on the sofa with a cup of tea and some quiet music, and I try not to check my work email until the next morning.","t":"A：在一整天開會和應付難搞的客戶電話之後，你回到家通常會做什麼？ B：我喜歡在沙發上【放鬆一下】，喝杯茶聽點輕音樂，而且我會盡量到隔天早上才去看工作信箱。"},{"w":"permanent address","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place where someone officially lives for a long time","c":"永久地址；戶籍地址","s":"A: You have moved three times this year for different projects, so which address should I write on your insurance form? B: Please use my permanent address, which is my parents' house in Taichung, because all my official letters still go there while I travel for work.","t":"A：你今年因為不同的專案搬了三次家，那我在你的保險表格上應該寫哪個地址？ B：請寫我的【永久地址】，就是我父母在台中的房子，因為我出差期間所有的正式信件都還是寄到那裡。"},{"w":"ideal home","p":"n.phr.","d":"a home that is exactly right for someone","c":"理想的家","s":"A: If money were not a problem, what kind of place would you like to live in after you retire from the company? B: My ideal home would be a small cottage near the beach with a large kitchen, a sunny reading room, and enough space for my grandchildren to visit.","t":"A：如果錢不是問題，你從公司退休後想住在什麼樣的地方？ B：我【理想的家】會是海邊的一間小屋，有個大廚房、一間陽光充足的閱讀室，還有足夠的空間讓孫子孫女來玩。"},{"w":"single room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room for one person","c":"單人房","s":"A: Do you have to share a room with a colleague when the company sends us to the training center in Kaohsiung next week? B: No, this year every staff member will get a single room with its own small desk and bathroom, so everyone can rest well between the training sessions.","t":"A：下週公司派我們去高雄的訓練中心時，你需要和同事同住一間房嗎？ B：不用，今年每位員工都會分到一間【單人房】，有自己的小書桌和浴室，所以大家在課程之間都能好好休息。"},{"w":"spacious room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room that is large and has plenty of space","c":"寬敞的房間","s":"A: Why did your manager recommend that hotel for the visiting clients from Japan instead of the cheaper one near the station? B: Each guest gets a spacious room with a large desk, a sofa, and a big window, so the clients can work comfortably and even hold small meetings there.","t":"A：為什麼你的經理推薦那家飯店給來訪的日本客戶，而不是車站附近比較便宜的那家？ B：每位房客都有一間【寬敞的房間】，有大書桌、沙發和大窗戶，所以客戶可以舒適地工作，甚至在那裡開小型會議。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and pleasant","c":"溫暖舒適的；舒適宜人的","s":"A: Your living room is quite small, but why do all your guests say they enjoy spending time at your place in winter? B: I think it feels cozy because of the soft lights, the thick carpet, and the warm blankets on the sofa, so everyone wants to stay and talk for hours.","t":"A：你的客廳挺小的，但為什麼你的客人都說冬天很喜歡待在你家？ B：我想是因為柔和的燈光、厚厚的地毯和沙發上的暖毯，讓人覺得很【溫暖舒適】，所以大家都想留下來聊上好幾個小時。"}]},{"unit":177,"theme":"Hometown 家鄉","cards":[{"w":"historical sites","p":"n.phr.","d":"old places that are important in history","c":"歷史古蹟","s":"A: Our overseas clients arrive in Tainan on Thursday, and they will have a free afternoon before the factory tour on Friday morning. What should we show them? B: I suggest taking them to the old fort and the temples, because the city's historical sites give visitors a clear picture of four hundred years of local history.","t":"A：我們的海外客戶週四抵達台南，週五早上參觀工廠前有一個下午的空檔，我們該帶他們看什麼？ B：我建議帶他們去古堡和廟宇，因為這座城市的【歷史古蹟】能讓遊客清楚了解四百年的在地歷史。"},{"w":"breathtaking","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or exciting","c":"令人屏息的；壯觀的","s":"A: You grew up in that small town in the mountains of Hualien, right? Is it worth visiting during the long weekend if my family only has two days? B: Absolutely, the view from the cliff road at sunrise is breathtaking, and you can also stop at small farms along the way to buy fresh fruit.","t":"A：你是在花蓮山區那個小鎮長大的，對吧？如果我們家只有兩天，連假時值得去嗎？ B：當然值得，日出時從懸崖公路看出去的景色【令人屏息】，沿途你還可以在小農場停下來買新鮮水果。"},{"w":"picturesque","p":"adj.","d":"pretty, like a picture","c":"風景如畫的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team choose your hometown as the location for the new travel advertisement instead of a big city like Taipei? B: The director felt that its picturesque streets, with old wooden houses and a small river running beside them, would look beautiful on screen and attract younger travelers.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊選擇你的家鄉而不是台北這樣的大城市來拍新的旅遊廣告？ B：導演覺得那裡【風景如畫的】街道，有老木屋和旁邊流過的小河，在螢幕上會很好看，也能吸引年輕旅客。"},{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following customs that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統的","s":"A: Is there anything special we should prepare for the welcome dinner when the visiting managers come to your hometown next month? B: Yes, I have booked a family restaurant that serves traditional dishes like braised pork rice and fish ball soup, which my grandmother used to cook for festivals.","t":"A：下個月來訪的經理們到你家鄉時，歡迎晚宴我們需要準備什麼特別的嗎？ B：有，我訂了一家家庭餐廳，供應滷肉飯和魚丸湯這類【傳統】料理，那是我祖母以前過節時會煮的。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"new and using the latest ideas or technology","c":"現代化的；新式的","s":"A: Has your hometown changed much since you moved to the capital for work about ten years ago? B: Quite a lot, because the old train station was replaced by a modern building with glass walls, digital ticket machines, and a food court that stays open until midnight.","t":"A：自從你大約十年前搬到首都工作以來，你的家鄉改變很多嗎？ B：改變不少，舊火車站被一棟【現代化的】建築取代，有玻璃牆、數位售票機，還有營業到午夜的美食街。"},{"w":"preserve","p":"v.","d":"to keep something safe and in good condition","c":"保存；維護","s":"A: Why is the city council spending so much money on the old market street when it could build a new shopping center instead? B: Many residents asked the council to preserve the historic shops and narrow lanes, because they are an important part of the town's identity and attract tourists.","t":"A：市議會明明可以蓋新的購物中心，為什麼要花那麼多錢在舊市場街上？ B：許多居民請市議會【保存】那些歷史老店和狹窄巷弄，因為它們是小鎮特色的重要部分，也能吸引觀光客。"},{"w":"high-rise","p":"n.","d":"a very tall building with many floors","c":"高樓大廈","s":"A: Where will the new employees from the Tokyo branch stay while they are working at our headquarters for six months? B: The company has rented several apartments in a new high-rise near the station, so they can walk to the office in ten minutes and enjoy a great view of the city.","t":"A：東京分公司的新員工在我們總部工作六個月期間會住在哪裡？ B：公司在車站附近一棟新的【高樓】租了幾間公寓，所以他們走十分鐘就能到辦公室，還能欣賞很棒的城市景色。"},{"w":"hospitality","p":"n.","d":"friendly and generous treatment of guests","c":"熱情好客；款待","s":"A: How did the overseas buyers feel about their trip to your hometown after the trade fair last week? B: They were very impressed by the hospitality of the local people, who invited them into their homes for tea and even drove them back to the hotel after dinner.","t":"A：上週商展後海外買家對你家鄉之旅感覺如何？ B：他們對當地人的【熱情好客】印象非常深刻，當地人請他們到家裡喝茶，晚餐後甚至開車送他們回飯店。"},{"w":"day by day","p":"phr.","d":"slowly, a little more each day","c":"一天天地；逐日","s":"A: Is the new subway line in your hometown going to be finished before the international sports event next summer? B: The workers are making progress day by day, and the project manager told reporters that the stations should be ready for testing by the end of March.","t":"A：你家鄉的新捷運線能在明年夏天的國際運動賽事前完工嗎？ B：工人們的進度【一天天地】推進，專案經理告訴記者，車站應該在三月底前能準備好進行測試。"},{"w":"potential","p":"n.","d":"the possibility to develop or succeed in the future","c":"潛力","s":"A: Why did the hotel group decide to invest in your quiet hometown instead of a more famous tourist city? B: Their research team believed the area had great potential for growth, since a new highway will open soon and more visitors are looking for peaceful places by the sea.","t":"A：為什麼飯店集團決定投資你那安靜的家鄉，而不是更有名的觀光城市？ B：他們的研究團隊認為這個地區有很大的成長【潛力】，因為新的高速公路即將通車，而且越來越多遊客在尋找海邊的寧靜去處。"},{"w":"hotspot","p":"n.","d":"a popular place where many people go","c":"熱門地點；熱點","s":"A: Have you noticed how crowded the old harbor in your hometown has become on weekends lately? B: Yes, since a famous travel blogger posted photos of its colorful boats and seafood stalls, it has turned into a popular hotspot for young tourists from all over the country.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到你家鄉的老港口最近週末變得多擁擠？ B：有，自從一位知名旅遊部落客貼了那裡彩色漁船和海鮮攤的照片後，那裡就變成全國年輕遊客的熱門【景點】。"},{"w":"settle down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start living in one place for a long time","c":"安定下來；定居","s":"A: After working in three different countries for our company, do you plan to keep moving around for your career? B: Not really, I would like to settle down in my hometown in a few years, buy a small house near my parents, and maybe work for our local branch office.","t":"A：在三個不同國家為公司工作後，你打算為了事業繼續到處搬嗎？ B：不太會，我想幾年後在家鄉【安定下來】，在父母附近買間小房子，也許在我們當地的分公司工作。"},{"w":"enormously","p":"adv.","d":"very much; to a very great degree","c":"極大地；非常","s":"A: Has the new airport made a difference to the businesses in your hometown since it opened last year? B: It has helped them enormously, because hotels are almost always full now and many restaurants have hired extra staff to serve the large number of visitors.","t":"A：新機場去年啟用後，對你家鄉的商家有影響嗎？ B：幫助【非常大】，因為現在飯店幾乎都客滿，很多餐廳也多請了員工來服務大量遊客。"},{"w":"barely","p":"adv.","d":"almost not; only just","c":"幾乎沒有；勉強","s":"A: Did you have time to visit your old friends when you went back to your hometown for the business conference? B: I barely had time to eat, because the meetings started at eight every morning and the client dinners usually lasted until almost eleven at night.","t":"A：你回家鄉參加商務會議時，有時間拜訪老朋友嗎？ B：我【幾乎沒】時間吃飯，因為會議每天早上八點開始，客戶晚宴通常持續到將近晚上十一點。"},{"w":"skyscraper","p":"n.","d":"a very tall modern building in a city","c":"摩天大樓","s":"A: Why is everyone talking about the construction project downtown during the morning coffee break? B: A developer is planning to build a sixty-floor skyscraper there, which will be the tallest building in the area and hold offices, a hotel, and a shopping center.","t":"A：為什麼大家早上喝咖啡休息時都在聊市中心的建案？ B：有一家開發商打算在那裡蓋一棟六十層的【摩天大樓】，它將是這一帶最高的建築，裡面有辦公室、飯店和購物中心。"},{"w":"ameliorate","p":"v.","d":"to make a bad situation better","c":"改善；改良","s":"A: What is the new mayor doing about the noise and air pollution near the industrial zone in your hometown? B: She has promised to ameliorate the situation by planting more trees, moving heavy trucks to a new road, and checking factory smoke every month.","t":"A：新市長對你家鄉工業區附近的噪音和空氣污染有什麼作為？ B：她承諾要透過種更多樹、把大卡車改道到新路，以及每月檢查工廠排煙來【改善】情況。"},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"n.","d":"basic systems a place needs, such as roads, power and water","c":"基礎建設","s":"A: Why do so many young people from your hometown move to big cities after they finish university? B: The town's infrastructure is quite old, so the roads, internet service, and public buses are not good enough for the kinds of companies that offer well-paid jobs.","t":"A：為什麼你家鄉這麼多年輕人大學畢業後就搬到大城市？ B：鎮上的【基礎建設】相當老舊，道路、網路服務和公車都不足以吸引提供高薪工作的公司。"},{"w":"decrepit","p":"adj.","d":"old and in very bad condition","c":"破舊的；衰敗的","s":"A: Is the old cinema on Main Street still open, or has it finally closed after all these years? B: It closed a long time ago, and the building is now so decrepit that the city plans to tear it down next year and build a small park for families.","t":"A：主街上那家老電影院還開著嗎，還是這麼多年後終於關了？ B：很久以前就關了，現在那棟建築已經非常【破舊不堪】，市政府打算明年拆掉，蓋一座給家庭使用的小公園。"},{"w":"region","p":"n.","d":"a large area of a country","c":"地區；區域","s":"A: Why is your hometown famous among food lovers in Taiwan, even though it is a fairly small place? B: The whole region is known for its high-quality rice and fresh oranges, and every autumn there is a farmers' festival that attracts thousands of visitors.","t":"A：為什麼你的家鄉雖然很小，卻在台灣美食愛好者之間很有名？ B：整個【地區】以高品質的米和新鮮柳丁聞名，每年秋天還有吸引數千名遊客的農民節。"},{"w":"vicinity","p":"n.","d":"the area near a place","c":"附近；鄰近地區","s":"A: Are there any good places for our team to have lunch near the conference hall where we will hold the product launch? B: There are several cheap noodle shops and a nice Italian restaurant in the vicinity, so everyone can find something they like within a five-minute walk.","t":"A：我們要舉辦產品發表會的會議廳附近有適合團隊吃午餐的地方嗎？ B：【附近】有幾家便宜的麵店和一家不錯的義大利餐廳，所以大家走五分鐘內都能找到喜歡的東西。"},{"w":"frequently","p":"adv.","d":"often","c":"經常地；頻繁地","s":"A: How often do you go back to visit your parents now that you have been promoted to the Taipei office? B: I return home quite frequently, usually twice a month, because the high-speed train takes only ninety minutes and my mother always cooks my favorite meals.","t":"A：你升調台北辦公室後，多久回去看你父母一次？ B：我相當【經常】回家，通常一個月兩次，因為高鐵只要九十分鐘，而且我媽媽總是煮我最愛吃的菜。"},{"w":"increasingly","p":"adv.","d":"more and more","c":"越來越；日益","s":"A: Why are so many coffee shops and design studios opening along the quiet streets of your hometown these days? B: The town is becoming increasingly popular with young people from the city who want lower rent, fresh air, and a slower pace of life after years of stress.","t":"A：為什麼最近你家鄉安靜的街道上開了那麼多咖啡店和設計工作室？ B：這個小鎮在城市年輕人之間變得【越來越】受歡迎，他們在多年壓力之後想要較低的房租、新鮮空氣和較慢的生活步調。"},{"w":"accessibility","p":"n.","d":"how easy a place is to reach or use, especially for disabled people","c":"無障礙程度；可及性","s":"A: What changes has the train station in your hometown made since the city received complaints last year? B: To improve accessibility for elderly passengers and people in wheelchairs, it added two large elevators, wider gates, and ramps at every entrance of the building.","t":"A：自從去年市府接到投訴後，你家鄉的火車站做了哪些改變？ B：為了提升年長乘客和輪椅使用者的【無障礙便利性】，車站增設了兩部大型電梯、更寬的閘門，並在每個入口加設坡道。"},{"w":"consequently","p":"adv.","d":"as a result","c":"因此；結果","s":"A: Why are hotel prices in your hometown so high this month compared with the same time last year? B: A big international music festival is being held there, and consequently, most rooms were booked months ago by fans who traveled from Japan and Korea.","t":"A：為什麼你家鄉這個月的飯店價格比去年同期高那麼多？ B：那裡正在舉辦一場大型國際音樂節，【因此】大部分房間在幾個月前就被從日本和韓國來的樂迷訂走了。"},{"w":"venues","p":"n.","d":"places where events such as meetings or concerts are held","c":"場地；會場","s":"A: Do you think your hometown could host the company's annual sales conference next spring instead of Taipei? B: I think so, because the city now has several modern venues, including a large convention center and two hotels with ballrooms big enough for three hundred guests.","t":"A：你覺得明年春天公司的年度業務會議可以在你家鄉舉辦，而不是台北嗎？ B：我覺得可以，因為那座城市現在有好幾個現代化的【場地】，包括一座大型會議中心，以及兩間宴會廳大到能容納三百位賓客的飯店。"},{"w":"tourist attraction","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place that many visitors go to see","c":"觀光景點","s":"A: Why did the city decide to repair the old lighthouse on the hill instead of building a new parking lot? B: Officials realized that it could become a major tourist attraction, since visitors love taking photos there at sunset and buying snacks from the shops nearby.","t":"A：為什麼市政府決定修復山丘上的老燈塔，而不是蓋新停車場？ B：官員們發現它能成為主要的【觀光景點】，因為遊客喜歡在那裡拍夕陽照片，還會在附近商店買小吃。"},{"w":"majority","p":"n.","d":"more than half of a group","c":"大多數","s":"A: Do most people in your hometown work in farming, or have things changed over the past twenty years? B: Things have changed a lot, and now the majority of residents work in factories, shops, or offices, while only a few older families still grow rice.","t":"A：你家鄉大部分人都務農嗎，還是過去二十年來情況變了？ B：變了很多，現在【大多數】居民在工廠、商店或辦公室工作，只有少數年長的家庭還在種稻。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work","c":"通勤","s":"A: Have you ever thought about living in your hometown again and still keeping your job at our office in Taichung? B: Yes, many of my old classmates commute by train every day, since the trip takes only forty minutes and housing back home is much cheaper.","t":"A：你有沒有想過搬回家鄉住，同時保留在我們台中辦公室的工作？ B：有啊，我很多老同學每天搭火車【通勤】，因為車程只要四十分鐘，而且老家的房子便宜多了。"},{"w":"transportation","p":"n.","d":"a system of buses, trains and other vehicles for moving people","c":"運輸；交通工具","s":"A: Is it easy for tourists without a car to travel around your hometown and visit the beaches and temples? B: Public transportation has improved a lot recently, because the city added new bus routes and a bike-sharing system that connects the station with most popular places.","t":"A：沒有車的遊客在你家鄉到處遊覽、去海灘和廟宇方便嗎？ B：大眾【運輸】最近改善很多，因為市府增加了新的公車路線，以及一套連接車站和大多數熱門地點的共享單車系統。"},{"w":"traffic jam","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long line of cars that cannot move or move very slowly","c":"塞車；交通堵塞","s":"A: Why did the sales manager arrive almost an hour late for the client meeting this morning? B: She got stuck in a terrible traffic jam on the bridge into the city, because two trucks had an accident and the police closed one lane for cleanup.","t":"A：為什麼業務經理今天早上客戶會議遲到將近一小時？ B：她在進城的橋上碰到嚴重的【塞車】，因為兩輛卡車發生事故，警方封閉了一個車道進行清理。"},{"w":"rush hour","p":"n.phr.","d":"the busy time when people travel to or from work","c":"尖峰時段","s":"A: What time should we leave the office tomorrow if we want to reach the airport by six o'clock in the evening? B: Let's leave by three thirty, because the roads around the city center become very crowded during rush hour and the taxi ride could take twice as long.","t":"A：如果我們想在明天傍晚六點前到機場，應該幾點離開辦公室？ B：我們三點半前出發吧，因為市中心周圍的道路在【尖峰時段】會非常擁擠，計程車車程可能要兩倍時間。"},{"w":"comfort","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being relaxed, calm and less worried","c":"安慰；舒適","s":"A: Why do you always go back to your hometown when you feel tired after a long business trip abroad? B: I find great comfort in sitting with my family at the dinner table, eating my mother's soup, and hearing the familiar sounds of the night market outside.","t":"A：為什麼你每次長途出差回來覺得累時，總是回家鄉？ B：和家人坐在餐桌旁、喝媽媽煮的湯、聽著外面夜市熟悉的聲音，讓我得到很大的【慰藉】。"},{"w":"strive","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to do something","c":"努力；奮鬥","s":"A: What is the local government's main goal now that so many young workers have left the town? B: Officials strive to attract new businesses by offering lower taxes, cheap office space, and training programs, hoping that young people will return and raise their families there.","t":"A：既然那麼多年輕工作者離開了小鎮，地方政府現在的主要目標是什麼？ B：官員們【努力】透過提供較低稅金、便宜辦公空間和培訓計畫來吸引新企業，希望年輕人能回來並在那裡養家。"},{"w":"chain store","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of many shops with the same name and owner","c":"連鎖店","s":"A: Why are some residents in your hometown upset about the new shopping street that opened last month? B: Every shop there is a large chain store selling the same products as in other cities, so the small family businesses that made the town special are losing customers.","t":"A：為什麼你家鄉有些居民對上個月開幕的新購物街不滿？ B：那裡每家店都是大型【連鎖店】，賣的東西和其他城市一樣，所以讓小鎮與眾不同的小型家族商店正在流失顧客。"},{"w":"fashion house","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company that designs and sells expensive clothes","c":"時裝公司；時裝品牌","s":"A: Did you know that the famous designer who grew up in your hometown is opening a store downtown? B: Yes, her fashion house in Paris became very successful, and now she wants to show her new collection in the city where she first learned to sew from her aunt.","t":"A：你知道在你家鄉長大的那位知名設計師要在市中心開店嗎？ B：知道，她在巴黎的【時裝公司】非常成功，現在她想在她最初跟阿姨學縫紉的城市展示新系列。"},{"w":"get around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to travel or move from place to place","c":"四處走動；到處去","s":"A: I'm going to your hometown for a three-day sales trip next week, but I won't have a car. Any advice? B: It's easy to get around because the city is small, the buses run every ten minutes, and you can rent an electric scooter from most convenience stores.","t":"A：我下週要去你家鄉出差三天跑業務，但我沒車。有什麼建議嗎？ B：在那裡【四處走動】很容易，因為城市很小，公車每十分鐘一班，而且大多數便利商店都可以租電動機車。"},{"w":"pavement cafe","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cafe with tables outside on the sidewalk","c":"路邊咖啡座；露天咖啡館","s":"A: Where would be a relaxing place to meet the new client on Saturday afternoon before her flight home? B: There is a lovely pavement cafe on the main square, where you can sit outside under an umbrella, drink good coffee, and watch street performers.","t":"A：週六下午客戶搭機回國前，哪裡適合跟這位新客戶輕鬆見面？ B：主廣場上有一家很棒的【露天咖啡座】，你們可以坐在戶外的陽傘下喝好咖啡，看街頭藝人表演。"},{"w":"linger","p":"v.","d":"to stay somewhere longer than usual because you enjoy it","c":"逗留；流連","s":"A: Why did the tour group return to the bus thirty minutes late after visiting the old street in your hometown? B: Many of the visitors wanted to linger at the small craft shops and food stalls, because they had never seen handmade paper umbrellas before.","t":"A：為什麼旅行團參觀完你家鄉的老街後晚了三十分鐘回到遊覽車上？ B：很多遊客想在小手工藝店和小吃攤【逗留】，因為他們從來沒看過手工紙傘。"},{"w":"residential area","p":"n.phr.","d":"a part of a town where people live, not work","c":"住宅區","s":"A: Why did the city refuse the company's plan to build a new factory near the river last spring? B: The land is in a quiet residential area with many homes, schools, and parks, so the council decided that noise and heavy trucks would cause problems for families.","t":"A：為什麼市政府去年春天拒絕了公司在河邊蓋新工廠的計畫？ B：那塊地位於安靜的【住宅區】，有很多住家、學校和公園，所以議會認為噪音和大卡車會對家庭造成困擾。"},{"w":"inner-city","p":"adj.","d":"in the old central part of a city, often with poor people","c":"市中心老舊地區的","s":"A: What kind of volunteer work will our company support this year as part of its community program? B: We will help inner-city schools in the old downtown district, where many students come from low-income families and need computers, books, and after-school tutoring.","t":"A：今年我們公司的社區計畫要支持什麼樣的志工活動？ B：我們會協助舊市中心區那些【市中心老舊地區的】學校，那裡很多學生來自低收入家庭，需要電腦、書籍和課後輔導。"},{"w":"poor housing","p":"n.phr.","d":"homes that are in bad condition","c":"簡陋的住房；居住條件差","s":"A: Why did the charity choose your hometown for its new building project this year? B: Many families in the old fishing village still live in poor housing with leaking roofs and no hot water, so the volunteers plan to repair fifty homes before winter.","t":"A：為什麼這家慈善機構今年選擇你的家鄉進行新的建設計畫？ B：老漁村裡很多家庭仍住在屋頂漏水又沒熱水的【簡陋住房】裡，所以志工們計畫在冬天前修繕五十間房子。"},{"w":"shopping centre","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large building with many shops (British spelling)","c":"購物中心","s":"A: Where can I buy a suit and some gifts for my clients before the business dinner tonight? B: Go to the new shopping centre across from the train station, which has clothing stores, a bookshop, and a gift market on the ground floor, and it stays open until ten.","t":"A：今晚商務晚宴前，我可以在哪裡買西裝和送客戶的禮物？ B：去火車站對面新的【購物中心】，裡面有服飾店、書店，一樓還有禮品市集，而且營業到十點。"},{"w":"shopping mall","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large building or area with many stores and restaurants","c":"購物商場","s":"A: Why are the small shops on the old street in your hometown losing so many customers this year? B: A huge shopping mall with a cinema, free parking, and over two hundred stores opened just outside town, so most families now go there on weekends.","t":"A：為什麼你家鄉老街上的小店今年流失了那麼多顧客？ B：鎮外剛開了一座有電影院、免費停車場和兩百多家店的巨型【購物商場】，所以現在大部分家庭週末都去那裡。"},{"w":"office block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large building with many offices","c":"辦公大樓","s":"A: Where will our company's new branch office be located when it opens in your hometown next year? B: We have rented the top two floors of a modern office block near the city hall, which has a large parking garage and is close to several bus stops.","t":"A：明年我們公司在你家鄉開的新分公司會在哪裡？ B：我們租了市政府附近一棟現代化【辦公大樓】的頂部兩層，那裡有大型停車場，而且離幾個公車站很近。"}]},{"unit":178,"theme":"Hotel 飯店","cards":[{"w":"accommodation","p":"n.","d":"a place to stay or live, such as a hotel room","c":"住宿；住處","s":"A: Our sales team is attending the trade fair in Osaka next month, so could you tell me whether the company will pay for our hotel rooms? B: Yes, the company covers accommodation for up to four nights, but you need to choose a hotel near the exhibition center and keep every receipt for the finance department.","t":"A：我們業務團隊下個月要參加大阪的商展，可以告訴我公司是否會支付我們的飯店房間費用嗎？ B：會的，公司最多補助四晚的【住宿】，但你必須選擇靠近展覽中心的飯店，並把每張收據都留給財務部。"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to keep a table, room or seat for you","c":"預訂；預約","s":"A: I'm calling because I want to have dinner with three important clients at your hotel restaurant on Friday evening; is there still a table available? B: Yes, we have a quiet table by the window at seven o'clock, and I can make a reservation for you right now if you give me your name and phone number.","t":"A：我打電話來是因為星期五晚上想和三位重要客戶在貴飯店的餐廳用餐，請問還有空桌嗎？ B：有的，七點鐘靠窗有一張安靜的桌子，如果您給我姓名和電話號碼，我現在就可以幫您【預訂】。"},{"w":"check-in","p":"n.","d":"the act of arriving at a hotel and getting your room","c":"入住登記","s":"A: Our flight lands at around eleven in the morning, so can we go straight to our rooms when we arrive at the hotel? B: I'm afraid check-in doesn't start until three in the afternoon, but the front desk can keep your luggage safe while you have lunch and walk around the old town.","t":"A：我們的班機大約早上十一點降落，抵達飯店時可以直接進房間嗎？ B：恐怕【入住登記】要到下午三點才開始，不過您吃午餐、逛老城區的時候，櫃台可以幫您保管行李。"},{"w":"check-out","p":"n.","d":"the act of paying and leaving a hotel","c":"退房","s":"A: Our train back to Taipei doesn't leave until six in the evening, so is it possible for us to keep our room a little longer tomorrow? B: Normal check-out is at noon, but if you ask the front desk tonight, they can usually let you leave at two o'clock without any extra charge.","t":"A：我們回台北的火車要到晚上六點才開，明天可以讓我們晚一點交還房間嗎？ B：一般【退房】時間是中午，但如果您今晚向櫃台提出，他們通常可以讓您兩點再離開，而且不另外收費。"},{"w":"reception","p":"n.","d":"the place in a hotel where guests are welcomed and helped","c":"接待處；櫃台","s":"A: I just arrived for the marketing conference, but I'm not sure where I should go to pick up my room key and the welcome package. B: Please go to the reception desk on the ground floor next to the elevators, where the staff will check your passport and give you everything you need.","t":"A：我剛到這裡參加行銷研討會，但不確定該去哪裡領房間鑰匙和歡迎禮包。 B：請到一樓電梯旁的【接待】櫃台，工作人員會核對您的護照，並把您需要的東西都交給您。"},{"w":"lobby","p":"n.","d":"the large hall near the entrance of a hotel","c":"大廳","s":"A: Where should we meet the clients from Singapore before we take them out to dinner tonight, since none of us know the area very well? B: Let's wait for them in the hotel lobby at half past six, because it has comfortable sofas and is easy to find right after you walk through the main entrance.","t":"A：我們今晚帶新加坡客戶去吃晚餐前，要在哪裡和他們碰面？我們都不太熟悉這一帶。 B：我們六點半在飯店【大廳】等他們吧，那裡有舒服的沙發，而且一走進正門就很容易找到。"},{"w":"suite","p":"n.","d":"a set of connected hotel rooms, usually with a living room","c":"套房","s":"A: The CEO is visiting our Tokyo office next week with his wife, and he wants a room where he can also hold small private meetings. B: Then we should book the executive suite on the top floor, which has a separate living room, a large desk, and a beautiful view of the city.","t":"A：執行長下週要和太太一起來東京辦公室，他想要一間也能開小型私人會議的房間。 B：那我們應該訂頂樓的行政【套房】，裡面有獨立的客廳、大書桌，還有美麗的城市景觀。"},{"w":"single","p":"n.","d":"a hotel room with one bed for one person","c":"單人房","s":"A: The new intern is traveling alone to the training workshop in Kaohsiung, so what kind of room should I reserve for her at the hotel? B: Just reserve a single for two nights, since she doesn't need a big room, and it's the cheapest option that still includes free breakfast and fast internet.","t":"A：新來的實習生要獨自去高雄參加培訓工作坊，我該幫她在飯店預訂哪一種房間？ B：訂兩晚的【單人房】就好，因為她不需要大房間，而且這是仍包含免費早餐和高速網路的最便宜選擇。"},{"w":"double","p":"n.","d":"a hotel room with one large bed for two people","c":"雙人房","s":"A: My husband is joining me on this business trip because we plan to remain in the city for the weekend after the conference finishes. B: In that case, I'll change your booking from a single room to a double, which has one large bed for two people and costs only a little more per night.","t":"A：我先生這次會跟我一起出差，因為研討會結束後我們打算在這個城市多待一個週末。 B：這樣的話，我會把您的預訂從單人房改成【雙人房】，裡面有一張可睡兩人的大床，每晚只貴一點點。"},{"w":"amenity","p":"n.","d":"something that makes a place more comfortable or useful","c":"便利設施；備品","s":"A: Our guests often complain that the rooms feel too basic, so what can we add to make them happier during their visit? B: A popular amenity these days is a coffee machine in every room, and many travelers also expect a hair dryer, free bottled water, and good-quality shampoo.","t":"A：我們的客人常抱怨房間太陽春，我們可以增加什麼讓他們住得更開心？ B：現在很受歡迎的一項【便利設施】是每間房都有咖啡機，很多旅客也期待有吹風機、免費瓶裝水和品質好的洗髮精。"},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"a building or room used for a special purpose","c":"設施；場所","s":"A: We need a hotel for our three-day training program, but it must be a place where forty employees can study and practice together. B: The Grand Plaza has an excellent conference facility with projectors and fast internet, and it's only ten minutes from our office by taxi.","t":"A：我們三天的培訓課程需要一間飯店，但必須是能讓四十位員工一起學習和練習的地方。 B：君悅廣場飯店有很棒的會議【設施】，配備投影機和高速網路，而且從我們辦公室搭計程車只要十分鐘。"},{"w":"housekeeping","p":"n.","d":"the hotel department that cleans rooms and provides towels","c":"房務部；客房清潔","s":"A: There's a coffee stain on the carpet in my room, and I also need two more towels before I take a shower tonight. B: I'm sorry about that, sir; I'll call housekeeping right away, and someone will come up to clean the carpet and bring you fresh towels within fifteen minutes.","t":"A：我房間的地毯上有咖啡漬，而且今晚洗澡前我還需要多兩條毛巾。 B：先生，真抱歉；我馬上通知【房務部】，十五分鐘內就會有人上去清理地毯，並給您送乾淨的毛巾。"},{"w":"concierge","p":"n.","d":"a hotel worker who helps guests with tickets, tours and advice","c":"禮賓人員；服務台人員","s":"A: My clients want to see a traditional music show tonight, but I have no idea where to buy tickets in this city. B: You should ask the concierge near the front entrance, because he knows all the local theaters and can usually get good seats even on the same day.","t":"A：我的客戶今晚想看傳統音樂表演，但我完全不知道在這個城市要去哪裡買票。 B：你應該去問正門附近的【禮賓人員】，因為他熟悉當地所有劇院，即使是當天通常也能拿到好位子。"},{"w":"bellhop","p":"n.","d":"a hotel worker who carries guests' bags to their rooms","c":"行李員","s":"A: I have three heavy suitcases and a box of product samples for tomorrow's presentation, so I can't carry everything upstairs by myself. B: Don't worry, the bellhop will put all your bags on a cart and bring them to your room while you finish signing the forms at the front desk.","t":"A：我有三個很重的行李箱，還有一箱明天簡報要用的產品樣品，沒辦法自己全部搬上樓。 B：別擔心，【行李員】會把您所有的行李放上推車送到房間，您可以先在櫃台把表格簽完。"},{"w":"room service","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hotel service that brings food and drinks to your room","c":"客房服務","s":"A: I'm too tired to go out after this long meeting, but I haven't eaten anything since lunch and I'm really hungry. B: Why don't you order room service from the menu on your desk, since they deliver hot meals to your door until midnight and simply add the cost to your bill?","t":"A：開完這場冗長的會議我累得不想出門，但我從午餐後就沒吃東西，真的很餓。 B：何不用你桌上的菜單叫【客房服務】呢？他們到午夜前都會把熱騰騰的餐點送到門口，費用直接加到帳單上。"},{"w":"buffet","p":"n.","d":"a meal where people serve themselves from many dishes","c":"自助餐","s":"A: Does the room price include breakfast, or will I have to find a café near the office every morning before work? B: It includes a full buffet in the restaurant on the second floor, where you can choose from eggs, fresh fruit, noodles, and bread from six-thirty to ten.","t":"A：房價有包含早餐嗎？還是我每天早上上班前都得在辦公室附近找咖啡店？ B：有包含二樓餐廳的豐盛【自助餐】，從六點半到十點都可以選擇蛋、新鮮水果、麵和麵包。"},{"w":"complimentary","p":"adj.","d":"given free of charge","c":"免費贈送的","s":"A: Do I need to pay extra if I want to use the gym or drink something from the minibar during my three-night visit? B: The gym is complimentary for all guests, and so are the two bottles of water in your room, but the snacks and drinks in the minibar are charged separately.","t":"A：我住三晚期間如果想用健身房或喝迷你吧裡的飲料，需要另外付費嗎？ B：健身房對所有房客都是【免費的】，房間裡的兩瓶水也是，但迷你吧的零食和飲料要另外收費。"},{"w":"vacancy","p":"n.","d":"a room in a hotel that is available","c":"空房","s":"A: We're driving along the coast without a booking, and it's getting dark, so I really hope we can find somewhere to sleep soon. B: Look at that small hotel on the right; the sign says there's a vacancy, so let's stop and ask the price before all the rooms are taken by other tourists.","t":"A：我們沿著海岸開車卻沒有訂房，天色也暗了，真希望能快點找到地方睡覺。 B：你看右邊那間小旅館，招牌上寫著有【空房】，我們停下來問問價錢，免得房間都被其他遊客訂走。"},{"w":"occupancy","p":"n.","d":"the number or percentage of hotel rooms being used","c":"住房率；入住","s":"A: How is the hotel doing this year compared with last year, now that more international tourists are visiting the island again? B: Our occupancy has risen to almost ninety percent during the summer months, so the manager is planning to hire more staff and open another wing next spring.","t":"A：現在越來越多國際觀光客又來島上旅遊，飯店今年和去年相比表現如何？ B：我們夏季的【住房率】已經上升到將近九成，所以經理打算明年春天多雇些員工，並開放另一棟側樓。"},{"w":"rate","p":"n.","d":"the price charged for something, such as a room per night","c":"費率；價格","s":"A: I'm planning a three-week business trip to Seoul, so is there any way to pay less than the normal nightly price? B: If you stay more than ten nights, we can offer you a special weekly rate, which will save your company about twenty percent compared with booking each night separately.","t":"A：我計畫到首爾出差三週，有沒有辦法付比一般每晚價格更少的錢？ B：如果您住超過十晚，我們可以提供特別的週【費率】，跟每晚分開訂相比，能幫貴公司省下約兩成費用。"},{"w":"luxury","p":"n.","d":"great comfort and expensive things","c":"奢華；豪華","s":"A: Why did the company choose such an expensive hotel for the awards dinner when we usually look for cheaper places? B: The directors wanted to thank our top sellers with a little luxury, so they booked a five-star hotel with marble bathrooms, silk sheets, and a famous French chef.","t":"A：我們平常都找比較便宜的地方，為什麼公司這次頒獎晚宴要選這麼貴的飯店？ B：董事們想用一點【奢華】來感謝我們的頂尖業務，所以訂了一間有大理石浴室、絲質床單和知名法國主廚的五星級飯店。"},{"w":"budget","p":"adj.","d":"cheap; low in price","c":"平價的；經濟型的","s":"A: The finance team said we have to cut travel costs this year, so where should the junior staff stay during the training course? B: Let's find a budget hotel near the station, since it will be clean and safe but cost much less than the expensive international chains downtown.","t":"A：財務部說今年必須削減差旅費，那培訓課程期間資淺員工該住哪裡？ B：我們找一間車站附近的【平價】旅館吧，既乾淨又安全，但比市中心昂貴的國際連鎖飯店便宜很多。"},{"w":"downtown","p":"adv.","d":"in or to the center of a city","c":"在市中心；往市中心","s":"A: Would you prefer a hotel near the airport, or somewhere closer to the client's head office for your meetings next week? B: I'd rather stay downtown, because the head office is in the city center and I'd like to walk to restaurants and shops in the evenings.","t":"A：你下週開會比較想住機場附近的飯店，還是離客戶總部近一點的地方？ B：我寧願住在【市中心】，因為總部就在市區，而且我晚上想走路去餐廳和商店。"},{"w":"seaside","p":"adj.","d":"near the sea","c":"海邊的；濱海的","s":"A: Where should we hold the company's summer retreat this year, since everyone said the mountain resort felt too cold and quiet last time? B: How about a seaside resort in Kenting, where staff can swim, play beach volleyball, and enjoy fresh seafood after the team-building activities?","t":"A：今年公司夏季員工旅遊要在哪裡辦？大家都說上次的山區度假村太冷又太安靜。 B：辦在墾丁的【海濱】度假村怎麼樣？員工在團隊建立活動後可以游泳、打沙灘排球，還能享用新鮮海鮮。"},{"w":"spacious","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of space; large","c":"寬敞的","s":"A: Is the new family room big enough for my parents and our two kids, or should I reserve two separate rooms instead? B: It's very spacious, with two large beds, a sofa, and a desk, so all six of you will have plenty of room to move around comfortably.","t":"A：新的家庭房夠我爸媽和我們兩個孩子住嗎？還是我應該改訂兩間分開的房間？ B：那間房非常【寬敞】，有兩張大床、一張沙發和一張書桌，所以你們六個人都有足夠空間舒適地活動。"},{"w":"comfortable","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel relaxed and pleasant","c":"舒適的","s":"A: How was your night at the new airport hotel, since you had to get up so early for your flight to Hong Kong? B: The bed was so comfortable and the room was so quiet that I slept deeply for six hours, even though I was worried about missing my alarm.","t":"A：你為了趕飛往香港的班機要很早起床，在新的機場飯店過夜感覺如何？ B：床很【舒適】，房間又很安靜，所以即使我擔心沒聽到鬧鐘，還是熟睡了六個小時。"},{"w":"cleanliness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being clean","c":"清潔；乾淨","s":"A: What do guests mention most often in their online reviews of our hotel, apart from the friendly front desk staff? B: They mostly praise the cleanliness of the rooms and bathrooms, so the manager wants to give the housekeeping team a bonus for their hard work this year.","t":"A：除了友善的櫃台人員之外，客人在網路評論中最常提到我們飯店的什麼？ B：他們大多稱讚房間和浴室的【清潔】，所以經理想發獎金給房務團隊，感謝他們今年的辛勞。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"protection of people and things from danger or crime","c":"保全；安全","s":"A: I'm a little nervous about leaving my laptop and passport in the room while I attend the conference all day. B: There's no need to worry, because security is excellent here; every room has a safe, and guards check the hallways and cameras twenty-four hours a day.","t":"A：我整天都要參加研討會，把筆電和護照留在房間讓我有點緊張。 B：不用擔心，這裡的【保全】很好；每個房間都有保險箱，警衛二十四小時巡查走廊和監視器。"},{"w":"hospitality","p":"n.","d":"friendly and generous treatment of guests","c":"殷勤款待；好客","s":"A: Why do so many business travelers keep coming back to that small family hotel instead of the big international chains? B: The owners are famous for their warm hospitality, always greeting guests by name, serving homemade tea, and helping them plan trips around the area.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多商務旅客不住大型國際連鎖飯店，而一再回到那間家庭式小旅館？ B：老闆以熱情的【款待】聞名，總是叫得出客人的名字、端上自製的茶，還幫他們規劃附近的行程。"},{"w":"book","p":"v.","d":"to arrange to have a room, seat or ticket","c":"預訂","s":"A: The sales conference in Tainan starts next Thursday, and I just realized nobody has arranged rooms for our team yet. B: I'll book five rooms at the hotel near the convention center this afternoon, and then I'll email everyone the confirmation number and directions.","t":"A：台南的業務會議下週四就開始了，我剛發現還沒有人幫我們團隊安排房間。 B：我今天下午會在會議中心附近的飯店【預訂】五間房，然後把確認號碼和交通路線用電子郵件寄給大家。"},{"w":"stay","p":"v.","d":"to live in a place for a short time as a guest","c":"暫住；停留","s":"A: How long are you planning to remain in Singapore after the product launch, since the client wants to meet you again? B: I'll stay at the same hotel for three more nights, which gives me enough time to visit the client's factory and prepare the final contract.","t":"A：產品發表會後你打算在新加坡待多久？客戶想再跟你見一次面。 B：我會在同一間飯店再【住】三晚，這樣就有足夠時間參觀客戶的工廠並準備最終合約。"},{"w":"upgrade","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a better room or seat","c":"升級","s":"A: I'm a gold member of your hotel program, and I wonder whether my standard room could be changed to something better tonight. B: Since you're a loyal member and we're not fully booked, we can upgrade you to a sea-view room on the twelfth floor at no extra cost.","t":"A：我是貴飯店會員計畫的金卡會員，想問今晚我的標準房能不能換成更好的房間？ B：因為您是忠實會員，而且我們還沒客滿，可以免費幫您【升級】到十二樓的海景房。"},{"w":"conveniently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easy and useful","c":"方便地；便利地","s":"A: How far is your hotel from the subway, since I'll be carrying a lot of display materials to the trade show every day? B: It's conveniently located just two minutes from the main subway station, and there's also a free shuttle bus that goes directly to the exhibition hall.","t":"A：你們飯店離地鐵多遠？因為我每天都要帶很多展示材料去商展。 B：飯店位置【便利】，距離地鐵總站只要兩分鐘，還有免費接駁車直達展覽館。"},{"w":"temporarily","p":"adv.","d":"for a short time only","c":"暫時地","s":"A: Why can't I use the swimming pool this week, when the website says it's open to guests every day of the year? B: I'm sorry, but the pool is temporarily closed for repairs until Friday, so we're offering all guests free passes to the fitness center next door instead.","t":"A：網站上說游泳池全年每天都對房客開放，為什麼我這週不能使用？ B：很抱歉，游泳池因為維修【暫時】關閉到星期五，所以我們改為提供所有房客隔壁健身中心的免費通行證。"}]},{"unit":179,"theme":"House 房屋","cards":[{"w":"home","p":"n.","d":"the place where you live","c":"家","s":"A: Why did you leave the office so early yesterday afternoon, and did the client meeting finish without any problems? B: The meeting went well, but my daughter had a fever, so I returned to my home to look after her and finished the sales report on my laptop later that night.","t":"A：你昨天下午為什麼那麼早離開辦公室？客戶會議順利結束了嗎？ B：會議很順利，但我女兒發燒了，所以我回【家】照顧她，那天晚上稍晚才用筆電完成銷售報告。"},{"w":"residence","p":"n.","d":"a house or place where someone lives, often a formal word","c":"住所；住宅","s":"A: Has the new branch manager from Singapore found a place to live yet, or is she still staying at the hotel near the station? B: The company has rented a private residence for her in a quiet area, and she will move in next Monday after the cleaning team finishes.","t":"A：從新加坡來的新分行經理找到住的地方了嗎？還是她仍住在車站附近的飯店？ B：公司已在一個安靜的地區為她租了一間私人【住所】，等清潔團隊完成工作後，她下週一就會搬進去。"},{"w":"dwelling","p":"n.","d":"a house, flat, or other place where people live","c":"住處；寓所","s":"A: What did the city planning department decide about the empty land next to the old train station downtown? B: They approved a project to build a new dwelling for about two hundred families, and construction should start in spring once all the contracts are signed.","t":"A：市府都市計畫部門對市中心舊火車站旁那塊空地做了什麼決定？ B：他們核准了一項為大約兩百戶家庭興建新【住宅】的計畫，等所有合約簽好後，春天就會開工。"},{"w":"apartment","p":"n.","d":"a set of rooms for living in, usually on one floor of a building","c":"公寓","s":"A: Are you still driving more than an hour to the office every morning, or have you found somewhere closer? B: I finally rented a small apartment on the fifth floor of a building near the subway station, so now my commute takes only fifteen minutes.","t":"A：你還是每天早上開車一個多小時來上班嗎？還是已經找到比較近的地方了？ B：我終於在捷運站附近一棟大樓的五樓租了一間小【公寓】，所以現在通勤只要十五分鐘。"},{"w":"cottage","p":"n.","d":"a small, simple house, usually in the countryside","c":"小屋；農舍","s":"A: Where is the marketing team planning to hold its two-day strategy retreat after the busy holiday season is over? B: We have booked a wooden cottage in the mountains with a fireplace and a lake view, because the manager believes a quiet place helps everyone think more creatively.","t":"A：行銷團隊打算在忙碌的假期旺季結束後，到哪裡舉辦兩天的策略營？ B：我們訂了山上一間有壁爐和湖景的木造【小屋】，因為經理認為安靜的地方能幫助大家更有創意地思考。"},{"w":"villa","p":"n.","d":"a large house, often with a garden, used for holidays","c":"別墅","s":"A: How was the company's reward trip to Bali for the top sales staff, and did everyone enjoy the hotel? B: We didn't stay in a hotel; instead, we shared a large villa with a private swimming pool and a garden, and a chef cooked breakfast for us every morning.","t":"A：公司招待頂尖業務員的峇里島獎勵旅遊如何？大家喜歡那間飯店嗎？ B：我們沒有住飯店，而是一起住在一棟有私人游泳池和花園的大【別墅】，每天早上還有廚師為我們做早餐。"},{"w":"mansion","p":"n.","d":"a very large and expensive house","c":"大宅；豪宅","s":"A: Why is the old building on the hill so famous among tourists who visit our town every summer? B: It is a huge mansion that a wealthy factory owner built a hundred years ago, and now it has been turned into a museum with guided tours and a small café.","t":"A：為什麼山丘上那棟老建築在每年夏天來我們鎮上的遊客之間那麼有名？ B：那是一位富有的工廠老闆一百年前蓋的巨大【宅邸】，現在已改建成有導覽和小咖啡館的博物館。"},{"w":"bungalow","p":"n.","d":"a house with only one floor","c":"平房","s":"A: Why did your parents decide to sell their three-story house after your father retired from the bank last year? B: Climbing the stairs became difficult for them, so they bought a bungalow near the beach where all the rooms are on one level and they can walk around easily.","t":"A：你父親去年從銀行退休後，你父母為什麼決定賣掉他們的三層樓房子？ B：爬樓梯對他們來說變得很吃力，所以他們在海邊附近買了一間【平房】，所有房間都在同一層，走動很方便。"},{"w":"roof","p":"n.","d":"the top covering of a building","c":"屋頂","s":"A: Why are the workers putting buckets in the meeting room on the top floor this afternoon? B: Last night's heavy storm damaged the roof of our building, so rainwater is leaking through, and the repair company cannot come until Thursday because they are very busy.","t":"A：為什麼工人今天下午在頂樓的會議室裡放水桶？ B：昨晚的強烈暴風雨損壞了我們大樓的【屋頂】，所以雨水一直漏進來，而修繕公司因為很忙，要到星期四才能來。"},{"w":"wall","p":"n.","d":"one of the sides of a room or building","c":"牆壁","s":"A: Where should we hang the new company calendar and the safety rules that arrived from head office this morning? B: Let's put them on the wall next to the photocopier, because everyone walks past that spot several times a day and will notice any changes quickly.","t":"A：今天早上總公司寄來的新公司月曆和安全規定要掛在哪裡？ B：我們把它們貼在影印機旁邊的【牆】上吧，因為大家每天都會經過那裡好幾次，很快就會注意到任何變動。"},{"w":"ceiling","p":"n.","d":"the top inside surface of a room","c":"天花板","s":"A: Why does the conference room feel so much brighter today than it did during last week's meeting? B: The maintenance team installed new LED lights in the ceiling over the weekend, so now we can see the presentation slides clearly and save electricity at the same time.","t":"A：為什麼今天的會議室感覺比上週開會時明亮許多？ B：維修團隊週末在【天花板】裝了新的LED燈，所以現在我們能清楚看到簡報投影片，同時還能節省電力。"},{"w":"floor","p":"n.","d":"the flat surface you walk on inside a building","c":"地板","s":"A: Why did the cleaner put a yellow warning sign near the elevator in the main lobby this morning? B: Someone spilled coffee on the floor a few minutes ago, and it is still very slippery, so she wants visitors and staff to walk carefully until it dries.","t":"A：清潔人員今天早上為什麼在大廳電梯附近放了黃色警告標誌？ B：幾分鐘前有人把咖啡灑在【地板】上，現在還很滑，所以她希望訪客和員工在地板乾之前小心行走。"},{"w":"window","p":"n.","d":"an opening in a wall, with glass, that lets in light and air","c":"窗戶","s":"A: It is really hot and stuffy in this training room, and the air conditioner doesn't seem to be working properly. B: Could you open the window behind you to let some fresh air in while I call the building manager and ask him to send a technician?","t":"A：這間訓練教室真的又熱又悶，冷氣好像也沒有正常運作。 B：你可以打開你後面的【窗戶】讓新鮮空氣進來嗎？我來打電話給大樓管理員，請他派一位技術人員過來。"},{"w":"door","p":"n.","d":"the thing you open and close to enter or leave a room or building","c":"門","s":"A: Why did the security guard stop me at the entrance when I arrived for my job interview this morning? B: Since last month, every visitor must sign in and show identification before entering, so the guard keeps the front door locked and checks each person carefully.","t":"A：我今天早上來參加面試時，警衛為什麼在入口攔住我？ B：從上個月開始，每位訪客進入前都必須登記並出示證件，所以警衛把前【門】鎖著，並仔細檢查每個人。"},{"w":"kitchen","p":"n.","d":"a room where food is prepared and cooked","c":"廚房","s":"A: Where can I heat up my lunch, and is there a place to store food for the afternoon? B: There is a small staff kitchen at the end of the hallway with a microwave, a fridge, and a coffee machine, but please clean up after you use it.","t":"A：我可以在哪裡加熱午餐？有地方可以放下午要吃的食物嗎？ B：走廊盡頭有一間小小的員工【廚房】，裡面有微波爐、冰箱和咖啡機，但使用後請收拾乾淨。"},{"w":"bedroom","p":"n.","d":"a room used for sleeping","c":"臥室","s":"A: Did you find a suitable place for your family before you transfer to the Tokyo office next month? B: Yes, we rented a flat with a large bedroom for us, a smaller one for the kids, and a study where I can work on Fridays.","t":"A：你下個月調到東京辦公室之前，有替家人找到合適的住處嗎？ B：有，我們租了一間公寓，有一間給我們住的大【臥室】、一間給孩子的小房間，還有一間讓我星期五可以工作的書房。"},{"w":"bathroom","p":"n.","d":"a room with a toilet, a sink, and often a shower or bath","c":"浴室；洗手間","s":"A: Excuse me, I am here for the two o'clock interview, but could you tell me where I can wash my hands first? B: Of course, the bathroom is down the hall on your left, right next to the elevators, and the interview room is just across from it.","t":"A：不好意思，我是來參加兩點鐘面試的，可以先告訴我哪裡可以洗手嗎？ B：當然，【洗手間】就在走廊左手邊，緊鄰電梯，而面試室就在它正對面。"},{"w":"living room","p":"n.phr.","d":"the main room in a home where people sit and relax together","c":"客廳","s":"A: How do you usually spend your evenings now that you work from home three days a week? B: After dinner, my family and I relax together in the living room, watching the news on TV or playing board games, which helps me forget about work stress.","t":"A：既然你現在一週有三天在家工作，你晚上通常怎麼度過？ B：晚餐後，我和家人會一起在【客廳】放鬆，看電視新聞或玩桌遊，這能幫助我忘掉工作壓力。"},{"w":"garage","p":"n.","d":"a building or space where cars are parked","c":"車庫；停車場","s":"A: Is there any parking near your new office, or should I take a taxi to the meeting on Friday? B: You can drive, because the building has an underground garage with plenty of spaces for visitors, and the receptionist will give you a free parking ticket.","t":"A：你們新辦公室附近有停車的地方嗎？還是我星期五應該搭計程車去開會？ B：你可以開車來，因為大樓有一個地下【停車場】，有很多訪客車位，櫃台人員還會給你免費停車券。"},{"w":"garden","p":"n.","d":"an area of land where flowers, plants, or vegetables are grown","c":"花園","s":"A: What did the hotel do to make its outdoor wedding area more attractive for customers this year? B: They planted hundreds of roses and built a small fountain in the garden behind the restaurant, so many couples now choose to take their wedding photos there.","t":"A：飯店今年做了什麼讓戶外婚禮場地對顧客更有吸引力？ B：他們在餐廳後面的【花園】種了數百株玫瑰，還建了一座小噴泉，所以現在很多新人選擇在那裡拍婚紗照。"},{"w":"yard","p":"n.","d":"an open area of ground next to a building","c":"院子","s":"A: Why did the restaurant start serving lunch outside instead of only in the dining room? B: The owner cleaned up the empty yard behind the kitchen and put tables and umbrellas there, so customers can enjoy the sunshine when the weather is nice.","t":"A：那家餐廳為什麼開始在戶外供應午餐，而不是只在用餐區？ B：老闆把廚房後面空著的【院子】整理乾淨，放上桌子和陽傘，讓顧客在天氣好時可以享受陽光。"},{"w":"furniture","p":"n.","d":"things such as chairs, tables, and beds that you put in a room","c":"家具","s":"A: When will the new office be ready for us to move in, and what is still missing? B: The painting is finished, but the furniture has not been delivered yet, so we still have no desks, chairs, or cabinets, and the supplier promised to bring everything on Wednesday.","t":"A：新辦公室什麼時候可以讓我們搬進去？還缺什麼？ B：油漆已經完成了，但【家具】還沒送來，所以我們仍然沒有桌子、椅子或櫃子，供應商答應星期三會把所有東西送來。"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"things used to make a place look more beautiful or festive","c":"裝飾；布置","s":"A: Who is in charge of preparing the hall for the company's year-end party next Friday evening? B: The HR team is ordering food and drinks, while Lisa's group will handle the decoration, including balloons, lights, and flowers on every table to create a festive atmosphere.","t":"A：誰負責為下週五晚上的公司尾牙布置會場？ B：人資團隊負責訂餐點和飲料，而Lisa那組會負責【裝飾】，包括氣球、燈飾和每張桌上的花，營造出歡樂的節慶氣氛。"},{"w":"renovate","p":"v.","d":"to repair and improve an old building or room","c":"翻修；整修","s":"A: Why is the hotel closed for three months even though summer is the busiest season for tourists? B: The owners decided to renovate all the guest rooms and the lobby, replacing the old carpets and bathrooms, because many customers had complained in online reviews that everything looked outdated.","t":"A：為什麼那間飯店要關閉三個月，明明夏天是觀光客最多的季節？ B：業主決定【翻修】所有客房和大廳，更換舊地毯和浴室，因為很多顧客在網路評論中抱怨一切看起來都很過時。"},{"w":"maintain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in good condition by checking and repairing it","c":"維護；保養","s":"A: Why does the building manager want to hire two more technicians before the end of this year? B: Our office tower is getting older, and he needs more people to maintain the elevators, heating system, and lights properly so that tenants do not complain about breakdowns.","t":"A：大樓經理為什麼想在年底前再雇用兩名技術人員？ B：我們的辦公大樓越來越老舊，他需要更多人妥善【維護】電梯、暖氣系統和照明，這樣租戶才不會抱怨設備故障。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make a place look more attractive by adding things to it","c":"裝飾；布置","s":"A: What are you planning to do with the empty reception area before our important clients visit next week? B: We will decorate it with some green plants, modern paintings, and comfortable sofas so that visitors feel welcome and get a good first impression of our company.","t":"A：在重要客戶下週來訪之前，你們打算怎麼處理空蕩蕩的接待區？ B：我們會用一些綠色植物、現代畫作和舒適的沙發來【布置】它，讓訪客感到賓至如歸，並對我們公司留下良好的第一印象。"},{"w":"spacious","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of space inside","c":"寬敞的","s":"A: Why did you choose this restaurant for the team dinner instead of the Italian place we went to last time? B: This one has a spacious private dining room that holds thirty people comfortably, so the whole department can sit together and the waiters can move around easily.","t":"A：你為什麼選這家餐廳辦團隊聚餐，而不是我們上次去的那家義大利餐廳？ B：這家有一間【寬敞的】私人包廂，可以舒適地容納三十人，所以整個部門可以坐在一起，服務生走動也很方便。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and relaxing","c":"舒適溫馨的","s":"A: Do you prefer working in that big open-plan office or in the small café downstairs? B: I like the café better because it is warm and cozy, with soft chairs and quiet music, so I can concentrate on writing reports without people walking past my desk all day.","t":"A：你比較喜歡在那個開放式的大辦公室工作，還是在樓下的小咖啡館？ B：我比較喜歡咖啡館，因為那裡溫暖又【舒適】，有柔軟的椅子和輕柔的音樂，我可以專心寫報告，不會整天有人從我桌邊走過。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"new and using the latest ideas, styles, or technology","c":"現代的；新式的","s":"A: What do customers usually say about the new headquarters when they visit for the first time? B: They are often impressed by its modern design, with glass walls, smart lighting, and digital screens in every meeting room, which shows that our company uses the latest technology.","t":"A：顧客第一次參觀新總部時通常怎麼說？ B：他們常對它的【現代】設計印象深刻，包括玻璃牆、智慧照明和每間會議室的數位螢幕，這顯示我們公司使用最新的科技。"},{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following old customs or styles that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統的","s":"A: What kind of hotel should we book for the overseas guests who are visiting Kyoto next month? B: I suggest a traditional Japanese inn with wooden floors, paper doors, and a hot spring, because our guests told me they want to experience the local culture rather than stay somewhere ordinary.","t":"A：下個月要去京都的海外貴賓，我們該幫他們訂哪種飯店？ B：我建議訂一間有木頭地板、紙拉門和溫泉的【傳統】日式旅館，因為貴賓告訴我，他們想體驗當地文化，而不是住在普通的地方。"},{"w":"secure","p":"adj.","d":"safe and protected from danger or crime","c":"安全的；牢固的","s":"A: Is it safe to leave our laptops in the office overnight, since several companies on this street have had break-ins? B: Yes, the building is very secure now because the owner installed cameras, card readers, and an alarm system, and a guard also checks every floor at midnight.","t":"A：這條街上有好幾家公司遭小偷闖入，把筆電留在辦公室過夜安全嗎？ B：安全，現在這棟大樓非常【安全】，因為業主裝了監視器、刷卡機和警報系統，而且警衛半夜還會巡查每一層樓。"},{"w":"comfortably","p":"adv.","d":"in a comfortable way; with enough space or ease","c":"舒適地；寬裕地","s":"A: Is the new conference room big enough for the training workshop with all the new employees next Monday? B: Yes, it can hold about fifty people comfortably, and each seat has a small desk and a power socket, so trainees can take notes and charge their laptops.","t":"A：新會議室夠大，可以容納下週一所有新進員工的訓練工作坊嗎？ B：夠，它可以【舒適地】容納大約五十人，而且每個座位都有小桌板和插座，受訓者可以做筆記和幫筆電充電。"},{"w":"permanently","p":"adv.","d":"for all time in the future; not temporarily","c":"永久地","s":"A: Is Mr. Chen only visiting the Taipei branch for a few weeks, or is he staying longer this time? B: He is moving here permanently as our new regional director, so he has already sold his house in Hong Kong and enrolled his children in a local school.","t":"A：陳先生只是來台北分公司幾個禮拜，還是這次會待比較久？ B：他要以新任區域總監的身分【永久】搬來這裡，所以他已經賣掉香港的房子，並幫孩子在當地學校註冊了。"},{"w":"indoors","p":"adv.","d":"inside a building","c":"在室內","s":"A: Should we still hold the company sports day at the park on Saturday, even though the weather report says heavy rain is coming? B: I think we should move all the activities indoors to the school gym we rented last year, so nobody gets wet and the games can continue as planned.","t":"A：氣象報告說會下大雨，我們星期六還要在公園舉辦公司運動會嗎？ B：我認為應該把所有活動移到【室內】，改到我們去年租過的學校體育館，這樣就沒人會淋濕，比賽也能照計畫進行。"},{"w":"outdoors","p":"adv.","d":"outside, not in a building","c":"在戶外","s":"A: Why does your team look so much happier and more relaxed after the training weekend in the mountains? B: We spent most of the time outdoors, hiking through the forest and cooking dinner together by the river, which helped us build trust and forget about our deadlines.","t":"A：你們團隊在山上參加完週末訓練後，為什麼看起來快樂又放鬆許多？ B：我們大部分時間都在【戶外】，在森林裡健行，在河邊一起煮晚餐，這幫助我們建立信任，也忘掉了截止期限。"}]},{"unit":180,"theme":"Housework 家務","cards":[{"w":"chore","p":"n.","d":"a regular small job you do at home or work","c":"家務；雜事","s":"A: Now that you and your roommate both work long hours at the bank downtown, how do you decide who takes care of the apartment during the week? B: We made a simple list on the fridge, and each of us chooses one chore every evening, like taking out the trash or washing the dishes after dinner.","t":"A：既然你和室友都在市中心的銀行工作很長的時間，你們平日怎麼決定誰負責整理公寓？ B：我們在冰箱上貼了一張簡單的清單，我們每個人每晚選一項【家務】，像是倒垃圾或晚餐後洗碗。"},{"w":"cleaning","p":"n.","d":"the work of making a place or thing clean","c":"清潔；打掃","s":"A: The office looked amazing when I arrived this morning, but who came in over the weekend while everyone was away at the sales conference in Kaohsiung? B: The building manager hired a professional company to do a deep cleaning of the carpets, desks, and kitchen, so the whole floor smells fresh now.","t":"A：我今天早上到的時候辦公室看起來棒極了，但週末大家都去高雄參加業務會議時，是誰來過？ B：大樓經理請了一家專業公司來對地毯、辦公桌和廚房做徹底的【清潔】，所以整層樓現在聞起來很清新。"},{"w":"tidying","p":"n.","d":"putting things back in their proper places so an area looks neat","c":"整理；收拾","s":"A: Why are you staying late at the store tonight when your shift officially ended at six o'clock and the manager already locked the front door? B: A big group of customers left clothes all over the fitting rooms, so I offered to help with the tidying before the morning staff arrive tomorrow.","t":"A：你的班六點就正式結束了，經理也已經鎖上前門，為什麼你今晚還留在店裡這麼晚？ B：一大群顧客把衣服丟得試衣間到處都是，所以我自願在明天早班員工到之前幫忙【整理】。"},{"w":"laundry","p":"n.","d":"clothes and sheets that need washing, or the job of washing them","c":"洗衣；待洗的衣物","s":"A: Does the new apartment building near the train station have washing machines, or will I need to carry my clothes to a shop every weekend? B: There is a shared laundry room in the basement with six machines and dryers, and residents can use it any time between seven in the morning and ten at night.","t":"A：火車站附近那棟新公寓大樓有洗衣機嗎？還是我每個週末都得把衣服拿到店裡去？ B：地下室有一間共用的【洗衣】間，有六台洗衣機和烘乾機，住戶從早上七點到晚上十點都可以使用。"},{"w":"vacuuming","p":"n.","d":"cleaning floors or carpets with a machine that sucks up dirt","c":"吸塵","s":"A: Should the cleaning staff come into the meeting room during the afternoon, or will the noise bother our clients from Japan during the presentation? B: Please ask them to finish the vacuuming before nine in the morning, because the machine is very loud and our guests need a quiet room to concentrate.","t":"A：清潔人員應該在下午進會議室嗎？還是噪音會在簡報時打擾我們的日本客戶？ B：請他們在早上九點前完成【吸塵】，因為機器很吵，我們的客人需要安靜的房間來專心。"},{"w":"sweeping","p":"n.","d":"cleaning a floor with a brush that has a long handle","c":"掃地","s":"A: What happened to the entrance of the restaurant? There are leaves and sand everywhere, and our first customers will arrive for lunch in about twenty minutes. B: The strong wind last night blew everything in from the street, so I'll grab the broom and start the sweeping right now while you set the tables.","t":"A：餐廳入口怎麼了？到處都是樹葉和沙子，我們的第一批客人大約二十分鐘後就會來吃午餐。 B：昨晚的強風把街上的東西都吹了進來，所以我現在就去拿掃把開始【掃地】，你來擺桌子。"},{"w":"mopping","p":"n.","d":"washing a floor with a wet cloth or sponge on a long stick","c":"拖地","s":"A: Why is there a yellow warning sign in front of the elevator on the second floor, and should I take the stairs to reach the accounting department? B: The janitor is doing the mopping because someone spilled coffee near the doors, so please walk carefully since the tiles are still wet and slippery.","t":"A：二樓電梯前為什麼有黃色警告標誌？我應該走樓梯去會計部嗎？ B：清潔工正在【拖地】，因為有人在門附近打翻了咖啡，所以請小心走，地磚還是濕的而且很滑。"},{"w":"dusting","p":"n.","d":"removing dust from furniture and surfaces with a cloth","c":"撣灰塵；除塵","s":"A: The bookshelves in the hotel library look gray, and a guest complained about sneezing there this afternoon, so what should we do about it? B: I'll ask housekeeping to add dusting to their weekly list, and they can also wipe the lamps and picture frames so the room feels fresh again.","t":"A：飯店圖書室的書架看起來灰灰的，今天下午有位客人抱怨在那裡一直打噴嚏，我們該怎麼處理？ B：我會請房務部把【除塵】加入每週清單，他們也可以擦拭檯燈和相框，讓房間再次感覺清新。"},{"w":"dishwashing","p":"n.","d":"washing plates, cups and cooking tools after a meal","c":"洗碗","s":"A: How did the company picnic go on Saturday, and did anyone stay behind to help the kitchen staff after the food was finished? B: It went very well, and three people from marketing volunteered to do the dishwashing, so all the plates and cups were clean and packed away before sunset.","t":"A：週六的公司野餐進行得如何？食物吃完後有人留下來幫廚房人員嗎？ B：進行得很順利，行銷部有三個人自願負責【洗碗】，所以所有的盤子和杯子在日落前都洗好收起來了。"},{"w":"ironing","p":"n.","d":"making clothes smooth with a hot, flat tool","c":"燙衣服","s":"A: Your shirt looks very sharp today, so did you send it to the dry cleaner before the important interview with the bank this afternoon? B: No, I did the ironing myself last night because the shop was closed, and I wanted to look professional when I meet the hiring manager.","t":"A：你今天的襯衫看起來很筆挺，你是在今天下午跟銀行的重要面試前送去乾洗店的嗎？ B：不，因為店關了，所以我昨晚自己【燙衣服】，我想在跟招聘經理見面時看起來專業一點。"},{"w":"cooking","p":"n.","d":"the activity of preparing food","c":"烹飪；做菜","s":"A: Do you usually eat at the cafeteria near the office, or do you prepare your own lunch to save money during the busy work week? B: I enjoy cooking on Sunday afternoons, so I make large pots of soup and rice, and then I bring a box to work every day.","t":"A：你通常在辦公室附近的自助餐廳吃飯，還是在忙碌的工作週自己準備午餐來省錢？ B：我喜歡在星期天下午【烹飪】，所以我會煮好幾大鍋湯和飯，然後每天帶一盒去上班。"},{"w":"shopping","p":"n.","d":"the activity of buying things in stores","c":"購物；採買","s":"A: Are you free to join us for dinner after work on Friday, or do you already have plans with your family for the long weekend? B: I promised my mother I would do the grocery shopping for our holiday meal, but I can meet you at the restaurant after eight.","t":"A：你週五下班後有空和我們一起吃晚餐嗎？還是你連假已經和家人有計畫了？ B：我答應我媽要為節日大餐去【採買】食品雜貨，不過我可以八點後在餐廳和你們會合。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in a neat and useful order","c":"整理；安排","s":"A: The storage closet next to the copy room is full of old boxes, and nobody can find the printer paper when they need it, can they? B: You're right, so let's spend an hour on Friday afternoon to organize the shelves by type and add clear labels to every box.","t":"A：影印室旁邊的儲藏櫃堆滿了舊箱子，需要的時候沒人找得到印表機紙，對吧？ B：你說得對，所以我們週五下午花一個小時按種類【整理】架子，並在每個箱子上貼清楚的標籤。"},{"w":"wipe","p":"v.","d":"to clean a surface by rubbing it with a cloth","c":"擦拭","s":"A: What should I do before I leave the break room tonight, since the cleaning team won't come back until Monday morning? B: Please wipe the tables with the blue cloth and some spray, because people left coffee rings and crumbs everywhere after the birthday party this afternoon.","t":"A：既然清潔團隊要到週一早上才會回來，我今晚離開茶水間前應該做什麼？ B：請用藍色抹布和一些清潔噴劑【擦拭】桌子，因為今天下午的生日派對後大家留下了到處都是的咖啡杯印和碎屑。"},{"w":"scrub","p":"v.","d":"to clean something by rubbing it hard, usually with a brush","c":"刷洗；擦洗","s":"A: The pots in the restaurant kitchen still have burned sauce on the bottom, so will the dishwasher be able to remove it during the night cycle? B: Probably not, so you'll need to scrub them by hand with hot water and a hard brush before you put them into the machine.","t":"A：餐廳廚房的鍋子底部還有燒焦的醬汁，洗碗機在夜間清洗時能把它去掉嗎？ B：大概不行，所以在放進機器前，你需要用熱水和硬刷子手工【刷洗】它們。"},{"w":"rinse","p":"v.","d":"to wash something quickly with clean water to remove soap or dirt","c":"沖洗；漂洗","s":"A: Why do the glasses from the hotel bar sometimes taste like soap when guests order a drink, and have customers complained to the front desk? B: Yes, two guests did, so I've asked the bar staff to rinse each glass carefully with hot water after washing and then let it dry completely.","t":"A：為什麼飯店酒吧的杯子在客人點飲料時有時會有肥皂味？有客人向櫃台抱怨嗎？ B：有，兩位客人抱怨過，所以我已請酒吧員工在洗完後用熱水仔細【沖洗】每個杯子，然後讓它完全晾乾。"},{"w":"sort","p":"v.","d":"to put things into groups by type","c":"分類；整理","s":"A: There are so many returned items in the warehouse today, and the delivery trucks are coming at three, so where should I begin? B: First sort the products into three piles, damaged, wrong size, and unopened, and then we can decide which ones go back on the shelves.","t":"A：今天倉庫裡退回的商品好多，送貨卡車三點就要來了，我該從哪裡開始？ B：先把產品【分類】成三堆：損壞的、尺寸錯的和沒拆封的，然後我們再決定哪些要放回架上。"},{"w":"fold","p":"v.","d":"to bend cloth or paper so that one part lies on top of another","c":"摺；摺疊","s":"A: The hotel guests on the tenth floor asked for extra towels, so how should I prepare them before bringing them up from the laundry room? B: Please fold each towel neatly into thirds, place them in a clean basket, and add two small bottles of shampoo as a welcome gift.","t":"A：十樓的飯店客人要求額外的毛巾，從洗衣房拿上去之前我該怎麼準備？ B：請把每條毛巾整齊地【摺】成三折，放進乾淨的籃子裡，再加兩小瓶洗髮精當作歡迎禮。"},{"w":"hang","p":"v.","d":"to put something up so that it is held from above","c":"掛；吊","s":"A: The sun is shining this morning after a week of heavy rain, so should we use the dryer for the uniforms from the restaurant? B: Let's save electricity and hang them on the line behind the kitchen, because the weather report says it will stay dry and warm until evening.","t":"A：下了一週大雨後今天早上出太陽了，那我們該用烘乾機烘餐廳的制服嗎？ B：我們省點電，把它們【掛】在廚房後面的曬衣繩上吧，因為氣象報告說到傍晚都會保持乾燥溫暖。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken","c":"修理","s":"A: The washing machine in the staff dormitory is making a loud noise again, and water is leaking onto the floor, so who should I call? B: Contact the maintenance office on the first floor, and they will send a technician to repair it this afternoon before more water damages the carpet.","t":"A：員工宿舍的洗衣機又發出很大的噪音，還有水漏到地板上，我該打給誰？ B：聯絡一樓的維修辦公室，他們今天下午會派技術人員來【修理】，以免更多水損壞地毯。"},{"w":"maintain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in good condition","c":"維護；保養","s":"A: Our new office has a lot of plants and a big glass wall, so how much work will it take to keep everything looking nice? B: We signed a contract with a cleaning company that will maintain the windows and water the plants twice a week, so our staff don't need to worry.","t":"A：我們的新辦公室有很多植物和一大面玻璃牆，要讓一切保持美觀需要多少功夫？ B：我們和一家清潔公司簽了合約，他們每週兩次【維護】窗戶和替植物澆水，所以我們的員工不用擔心。"},{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual order and way in which you regularly do things","c":"例行公事；慣例","s":"A: How do you manage to keep your apartment so clean when you work overtime at the hospital almost every week? B: I follow a simple routine: I wash the dishes right after dinner, I do the laundry on Wednesday nights, and I clean the bathroom every Saturday morning.","t":"A：你幾乎每週都在醫院加班，是怎麼讓公寓保持這麼乾淨的？ B：我遵循一套簡單的【例行程序】：晚餐後馬上洗碗，週三晚上洗衣服，每週六早上打掃浴室。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists the times when things will be done","c":"時間表；行程表","s":"A: The kitchen in our shared office is always dirty by Thursday, and people keep arguing about whose turn it is to clean the fridge, right? B: Exactly, so I made a cleaning schedule with every team member's name and date, and I posted it on the wall next to the coffee machine.","t":"A：我們共用辦公室的廚房每到週四總是很髒，大家一直爭論輪到誰清冰箱，對吧？ B：沒錯，所以我做了一張列出每位組員名字和日期的清潔【時間表】，貼在咖啡機旁邊的牆上。"},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"working well without wasting time, money or energy","c":"有效率的","s":"A: Why did the hotel replace all of its old washing machines last month, since they were still working well enough for the guest rooms? B: The new ones are much more efficient, so they use less water and electricity, and the laundry team can finish twice as many sheets every shift.","t":"A：飯店上個月為什麼要汰換所有舊洗衣機？它們對客房來說還算堪用。 B：新的機器【有效率】得多，用的水和電都更少，洗衣團隊每班能洗完的床單也多了一倍。"},{"w":"thorough","p":"adj.","d":"careful and complete, with nothing missed","c":"徹底的；仔細的","s":"A: The health inspector is visiting our restaurant next Tuesday, so what should the kitchen team do to get ready before she arrives? B: We need a thorough cleaning of every shelf, oven, and fridge, and the manager will check each area herself on Monday afternoon to make sure nothing is missed.","t":"A：衛生稽查員下週二要來我們餐廳，廚房團隊在她來之前應該做什麼準備？ B：我們需要把每個架子、烤箱和冰箱做一次【徹底】的清潔，經理會在週一下午親自檢查每個區域，確保沒有遺漏。"},{"w":"messy","p":"adj.","d":"dirty or not tidy","c":"凌亂的；髒亂的","s":"A: What did the landlord say when he visited the apartment you were renting, after your roommate threw that big party last weekend? B: He said the living room was too messy, with bottles and paper plates everywhere, so we must clean it up before Friday or lose part of our deposit.","t":"A：你室友上週末辦了那場大派對之後，房東來看你租的公寓時說了什麼？ B：他說客廳太【凌亂】了，到處都是瓶子和紙盤，所以我們必須在週五前清理乾淨，否則會被扣部分押金。"},{"w":"neat","p":"adj.","d":"tidy and in good order","c":"整齊的；整潔的","s":"A: What do the customers notice first when they walk into your shop, since you said sales have gone up a lot this year? B: They always tell me the store looks very neat, because we keep every shirt folded and arranged by color and size on clean wooden shelves.","t":"A：既然你說今年業績提升很多，顧客走進你的店時最先注意到什麼？ B：他們總是告訴我店裡看起來很【整齊】，因為我們把每件襯衫都摺好，並按顏色和尺寸排列在乾淨的木架上。"},{"w":"spotless","p":"adj.","d":"completely clean","c":"一塵不染的；非常乾淨的","s":"A: How was your stay at the new business hotel near the airport, and would you recommend it to the sales team for next month's trip? B: Absolutely, the room was spotless, with fresh sheets, shiny floors, and a bathroom that smelled like lemons, and the staff were very friendly as well.","t":"A：你在機場附近那家新商務飯店住得如何？你會推薦給業務團隊下個月出差住嗎？ B：當然會，房間【一塵不染】，床單乾淨、地板光亮、浴室有檸檬香，員工也非常友善。"},{"w":"hygienic","p":"adj.","d":"clean and safe for people's health","c":"衛生的；合乎衛生的","s":"A: Why does the factory cafeteria require all kitchen workers to wear gloves and hair nets, even when they are just serving rice? B: The company wants the food area to be completely hygienic, so it protects workers from getting sick and passes the government health inspection every year.","t":"A：為什麼工廠餐廳要求所有廚房工作人員都戴手套和髮網，即使只是在盛飯？ B：公司希望用餐區完全【合乎衛生】，這樣能保護員工不生病，也能每年通過政府的衛生檢查。"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often and at the same times","c":"定期地；經常地","s":"A: The air conditioners in the conference rooms smell strange whenever we turn them on, so is there anything wrong with them? B: The filters are dirty, so the building staff will now clean them regularly, once every two weeks, to keep the air fresh for everyone working here.","t":"A：會議室的冷氣每次打開都有奇怪的味道，它們出了什麼問題嗎？ B：濾網髒了，所以大樓人員現在會【定期】清理，每兩週一次，讓在這裡工作的每個人都能呼吸新鮮空氣。"},{"w":"carefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that avoids mistakes or damage","c":"小心地；仔細地","s":"A: These wine glasses for the company's anniversary dinner are very expensive, so should I put them in the dishwasher with the other plates? B: No, please wash them carefully by hand in warm water, because they break easily, and we only have exactly enough for the guests tonight.","t":"A：這些公司週年晚宴用的酒杯非常昂貴，我應該把它們和其他盤子一起放進洗碗機嗎？ B：不行，請用溫水【小心地】手洗它們，因為它們很容易破，而且我們的數量剛好只夠今晚的客人用。"},{"w":"quickly","p":"adv.","d":"fast; in a short time","c":"快速地","s":"A: The clients from Singapore will arrive at the office in ten minutes, but the meeting room still has cups and papers from this morning, doesn't it? B: Don't worry, I'll clear the table quickly and open the windows, and you can bring in fresh water and the product samples.","t":"A：新加坡的客戶十分鐘後就會到辦公室，但會議室還留著今天早上的杯子和文件，對吧？ B：別擔心，我會【快速地】清理桌子並打開窗戶，你可以把新的水和產品樣品拿進來。"},{"w":"daily","p":"adv.","d":"every day","c":"每天地","s":"A: How often does the cleaning crew empty the trash cans in the open office, because the one near my desk was full yesterday? B: They are supposed to empty them daily at six in the evening, but one worker was sick this week, so I'll remind the supervisor right away.","t":"A：清潔人員多久清一次開放式辦公室的垃圾桶？我桌旁那個昨天滿了。 B：他們應該【每天】傍晚六點清空，但這週有一位員工生病了，所以我會馬上提醒主管。"},{"w":"occasionally","p":"adv.","d":"sometimes, but not often","c":"偶爾地","s":"A: Do you hire someone to clean your house every week, or do you and your husband share all of the housework yourselves? B: We do most of it ourselves, but we occasionally pay a cleaner to wash the windows and clean the oven, maybe three or four times a year.","t":"A：你們每週請人來打掃房子，還是你和你先生自己分擔所有家務？ B：我們大部分自己做，但【偶爾】會付錢請清潔工來洗窗戶和清烤箱，大概一年三、四次。"}]},{"unit":181,"theme":"Hurry 匆忙","cards":[{"w":"urgent","p":"adj.","d":"needing attention or action right away","c":"緊急的","s":"A: Why did the IT manager call everyone into the meeting room before lunch, even though we already had a team meeting this morning? B: The company website stopped working an hour ago and customers cannot place orders, so it is an urgent problem that we have to fix before the afternoon sales event begins.","t":"A：為什麼資訊部經理在午餐前把大家叫進會議室，即使我們今天早上已經開過團隊會議了？ B：公司網站一小時前停擺，客戶無法下訂單，所以這是個【緊急的】問題，我們必須在下午的促銷活動開始前修好。"},{"w":"rush","p":"v.","d":"to move or do something very quickly","c":"衝；趕緊去","s":"A: Why did Kevin leave the office so suddenly without saying goodbye to anyone after the client meeting ended? B: His daughter's school called to say she felt sick, so he had to rush to the train station and pick her up before the school office closed at four o'clock.","t":"A：客戶會議結束後，Kevin為什麼沒跟任何人道別就突然離開辦公室？ B：他女兒的學校打電話來說她身體不舒服，所以他必須【趕】到火車站，在學校辦公室四點關門前去接她。"},{"w":"terrible","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or unpleasant","c":"糟糕的；可怕的","s":"A: How was your business trip to Singapore last week, and did you manage to meet all of the new suppliers? B: The meetings went well, but the weather was terrible because it rained heavily every afternoon, and my flight home was delayed for six hours, so I arrived back exhausted.","t":"A：你上週去新加坡的出差怎麼樣？有見到所有新的供應商嗎？ B：會議進行得很順利，但天氣【糟透了】，因為每天下午都下大雨，而且我回程的班機延誤了六個小時，所以回到家時已經筋疲力盡。"},{"w":"loss","p":"n.","d":"the fact of losing money, time, or something valuable","c":"損失","s":"A: Why does the finance director look so worried after reading the sales report for the third quarter this year? B: Because the new store downtown opened late and sold far fewer products than expected, the company suffered a large loss of about two million dollars, and the board wants an explanation by Friday.","t":"A：財務總監看完今年第三季的銷售報告後，為什麼看起來這麼擔心？ B：因為市中心的新店開幕延遲，賣出的產品又比預期少很多，公司遭受了大約兩百萬美元的巨大【損失】，董事會要求在週五前提出解釋。"},{"w":"immediately","p":"adv.","d":"at once; without waiting","c":"立刻","s":"A: The printer on the third floor is making a strange noise and smoke is coming out of the back, so what should I do? B: Please turn it off and unplug it immediately, then tell everyone nearby to step away while I call the building manager and the repair company to come and check it.","t":"A：三樓的印表機發出奇怪的聲音，背面還冒出煙，我該怎麼辦？ B：請【立刻】關掉並拔掉插頭，然後叫附近的人都退開，我會打電話請大樓管理員和維修公司來檢查。"},{"w":"guilty","p":"adj.","d":"feeling bad because you did something wrong","c":"內疚的","s":"A: Why did you stay late at the office last night when your shift ended at five o'clock as usual? B: I felt guilty because I had left early on Monday and my teammates had to finish the client presentation without me, so I wanted to help them prepare the slides for tomorrow's meeting.","t":"A：你的班跟平常一樣五點就結束了，為什麼昨晚還留在辦公室到很晚？ B：我覺得很【內疚】，因為我週一提早離開，隊友們只好在沒有我的情況下完成客戶簡報，所以我想幫他們準備明天會議的投影片。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the latest time by which something must be finished","c":"截止期限","s":"A: Do you think we can take a short break this afternoon and go to the café across the street for coffee? B: I'm sorry, but the deadline for the annual budget report is five o'clock today, and our manager needs every department's numbers before she can send the final version to head office.","t":"A：你覺得我們今天下午可以休息一下，去對街的咖啡廳喝杯咖啡嗎？ B：抱歉，年度預算報告的【截止期限】是今天五點，我們經理需要拿到每個部門的數字，才能把最終版本寄給總公司。"},{"w":"put something off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to delay doing something until a later time","c":"拖延（某事）；延後","s":"A: Why are you starting the tax forms now when they are not due until the end of next month? B: Last year I waited until the final week and made many mistakes, so I learned that it is a bad idea to put something off just because it seems boring or difficult at first.","t":"A：稅務表格要到下個月底才到期，你為什麼現在就開始填？ B：去年我等到最後一週才做，犯了很多錯，所以我學到只因為一開始看起來無聊或困難就【把事情往後拖】是個壞主意。"},{"w":"efficiency","p":"n.","d":"the ability to work well without wasting time or money","c":"效率","s":"A: Why did the factory manager decide to buy new packing machines when the old ones still work? B: The new machines can pack twice as many boxes per hour, so they will improve the efficiency of the whole production line and help us deliver orders to customers much faster during the busy season.","t":"A：舊的包裝機還能用，工廠經理為什麼決定買新的？ B：新機器每小時可以包裝兩倍數量的箱子，所以能提升整條生產線的【效率】，幫助我們在旺季更快把訂單送到客戶手中。"},{"w":"prioritize","p":"v.","d":"to decide which tasks are most important and do them first","c":"優先處理","s":"A: I have ten emails to answer, two reports to write, and a meeting at three, so where should I start? B: You should prioritize the report for the Tokyo client because it is due at noon, and then reply to the emails during the afternoon after the meeting has finished.","t":"A：我有十封電子郵件要回、兩份報告要寫，三點還有個會議，我該從哪裡開始？ B：你應該【優先處理】給東京客戶的報告，因為中午就要交，然後在下午會議結束後再回覆郵件。"},{"w":"time limit","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of time allowed to do something","c":"時間限制","s":"A: How long will each candidate have to give the sales presentation during tomorrow's job interviews at the main office? B: There is a strict time limit of fifteen minutes for each person, so the candidates must plan their talks well and leave a few minutes at the end for questions from the managers.","t":"A：明天在總部的工作面試中，每位應徵者做業務簡報的時間有多長？ B：每個人有十五分鐘的嚴格【時間限制】，所以應徵者必須好好規劃講稿，並在最後留幾分鐘回答經理們的提問。"},{"w":"arrange","p":"v.","d":"to plan or organize something","c":"安排","s":"A: The clients from Germany are arriving on Thursday morning, but has anybody booked their transportation from the airport yet? B: Don't worry, I will arrange a car to pick them up at the arrival gate and take them directly to their hotel, so they can rest before the dinner meeting.","t":"A：德國客戶週四早上抵達，但有人幫他們預訂從機場出發的交通了嗎？ B：別擔心，我會【安排】一輛車到入境大門接他們，直接送他們到飯店，好讓他們在晚餐會議前休息一下。"},{"w":"purpose","p":"n.","d":"the reason why something is done","c":"目的","s":"A: Why does the human resources department want every employee to attend the workshop next Wednesday afternoon? B: The main purpose of the workshop is to teach staff how to manage their time better, because many people have been working late and still missing important deadlines this year.","t":"A：人資部門為什麼要每位員工參加下週三下午的工作坊？ B：這個工作坊的主要【目的】是教員工如何更好地管理時間，因為今年很多人都工作到很晚，卻仍然錯過重要的截止期限。"},{"w":"overestimate","p":"v.","d":"to think something is bigger, better, or easier than it really is","c":"高估","s":"A: Why did the marketing team need two extra weeks to finish the new product brochure for the trade show? B: They tend to overestimate how quickly they can work, so they promised it in one week, but the photos and translations took much longer than anyone had expected.","t":"A：行銷團隊為什麼需要多兩週才能完成商展用的新產品手冊？ B：他們往往會【高估】自己工作的速度，所以承諾一週完成，但照片和翻譯花的時間比大家預期的久得多。"},{"w":"unconsciously","p":"adv.","d":"without knowing or noticing","c":"無意識地","s":"A: Have you noticed that our sales director keeps tapping his pen on the table during every long meeting with the board? B: Yes, I think he does it unconsciously when he is nervous or in a hurry, so he probably has no idea that the sound bothers the other people sitting around him.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到我們的業務總監在每次跟董事會開長會時，都一直用筆敲桌子？ B：有啊，我想他在緊張或趕時間時會【無意識地】這麼做，所以他大概不知道這個聲音會打擾坐在他周圍的人。"},{"w":"unforgettable","p":"adj.","d":"so special that you will always remember it","c":"難忘的","s":"A: How was the company trip to Japan that the sales department won as a reward for reaching its goals? B: It was unforgettable because we saw Mount Fuji on a clear day, ate amazing food in Kyoto, and spent our last evening relaxing in a traditional hot spring hotel together.","t":"A：業務部因達成目標而贏得的日本員工旅遊怎麼樣？ B：真是【難忘】，因為我們在晴朗的日子看到富士山，在京都吃到很棒的美食，最後一晚還一起在傳統溫泉旅館放鬆。"},{"w":"rectify","p":"v.","d":"to correct something that is wrong","c":"糾正；修正","s":"A: A customer just called to say that we charged her twice for the same order last week, so what should I tell her? B: Apologize first, and then promise that we will rectify the mistake today by returning the extra payment to her credit card before the end of the business day.","t":"A：有位客戶剛打電話來說，我們上週同一筆訂單向她收了兩次錢，我該怎麼跟她說？ B：先道歉，然後保證我們今天會在下班前把多收的款項退回她的信用卡，【糾正】這個錯誤。"},{"w":"trifling","p":"adj.","d":"small and not important","c":"微不足道的；瑣碎的","s":"A: Should I report the small scratch on the side of the company car to the office manager after I return it? B: It seems like a trifling matter, but you should still mention it, because the rental company might charge us later if nobody writes it down when the car comes back.","t":"A：我還車之後，應該向辦公室經理報告公司車側面的小刮痕嗎？ B：這看起來是件【微不足道的】小事，但你還是應該提一下，因為如果車子還回來時沒人記錄，租車公司之後可能會向我們收費。"},{"w":"stick","p":"v.","d":"to continue with a plan or decision and not change it","c":"堅持；遵守","s":"A: The client wants to add three new features to the website, but can we still finish it by the end of this month? B: Only if we stick to the original plan and save the new features for the second version, because there is simply not enough time or staff to do everything now.","t":"A：客戶想在網站上增加三個新功能，我們還能在這個月底前完成嗎？ B：只有我們【堅持】原本的計畫，把新功能留到第二版才行，因為現在根本沒有足夠的時間或人手做完所有事情。"},{"w":"catch","p":"v.","d":"to get on a bus, train, or plane in time","c":"趕上（車、飛機等）","s":"A: Why are you packing up your things so early when the office doesn't close for another hour? B: I need to catch the six o'clock train to Taichung for a client dinner tonight, and if I leave any later, the traffic to the station will be too heavy.","t":"A：辦公室還要一小時才關，你為什麼這麼早就在收東西？ B：我得【趕上】六點往台中的火車，今晚要和客戶吃晚餐，如果我再晚一點出發，往車站的路上交通會太塞。"},{"w":"miss","p":"v.","d":"to be too late for a bus, train, plane, or event","c":"錯過","s":"A: Why did Ms. Chen join the video conference from the airport instead of from the meeting room this morning? B: Her taxi got stuck in heavy traffic, and if you arrive at the gate even five minutes late, you will miss your flight, which is exactly what happened, so she is waiting for the next one at noon.","t":"A：陳小姐今天早上為什麼是從機場而不是會議室參加視訊會議？ B：她的計程車遇到嚴重塞車，而只要晚五分鐘到登機門，就會【錯過】班機，這正是她遇到的情況，所以她正在等中午的下一班。"},{"w":"take time","p":"v.phr.","d":"to need a long period of time","c":"需要時間；花時間","s":"A: Our new assistant made several mistakes in the sales database this week, so should we look for someone with more experience? B: Learning a new system and all our company rules will take time, so let's give her a few more weeks of training before we make any decisions about her position.","t":"A：我們的新助理這週在銷售資料庫裡犯了好幾個錯，我們該找更有經驗的人嗎？ B：學習新系統和公司所有規定都【需要時間】，所以在決定她的職位之前，我們再給她幾週的訓練吧。"},{"w":"preparations","p":"n.","d":"things you do to get ready for an event","c":"準備工作","s":"A: The international trade fair starts in only three days, so is our booth ready for all the visitors yet? B: Most of the preparations are finished, but we are still waiting for the printed posters and product samples, which the delivery company promised to bring to the exhibition hall tomorrow morning.","t":"A：國際貿易展只剩三天就開始了，我們的攤位準備好迎接所有訪客了嗎？ B：大部分的【準備工作】都完成了，但我們還在等印好的海報和產品樣品，貨運公司答應明天早上送到展覽館。"},{"w":"careful","p":"adj.","d":"giving attention to avoid mistakes or danger","c":"小心的；仔細的","s":"A: I need to send the price list to all of our overseas customers before lunch, so can you give me any advice? B: Be careful when you check the numbers, because even when you are in a hurry, one small mistake in the price could cost the company a lot of money and trust.","t":"A：我需要在午餐前把價目表寄給所有海外客戶，你能給我一些建議嗎？ B：檢查數字時要【小心】，因為就算你在趕時間，價格上一個小錯誤都可能讓公司損失很多錢和信任。"},{"w":"considerate","p":"adj.","d":"thinking about other people's feelings and needs","c":"體貼的","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office so happy to work with the new team leader who joined us last month? B: She is very considerate, because she always asks how we are doing, gives us extra time when our children are sick, and never sends work emails late at night or on weekends.","t":"A：辦公室裡的大家為什麼都這麼喜歡和上個月加入的新組長共事？ B：她非常【體貼】，因為她總是關心我們的近況，在孩子生病時多給我們時間，也從不在深夜或週末寄工作郵件。"},{"w":"logical","p":"adj.","d":"reasonable and sensible, based on clear thinking","c":"合乎邏輯的；合理的","s":"A: Do you think the manager will agree with our plan to move the warehouse closer to the port next year? B: I think so, because it is the most logical choice: shipping costs will fall, deliveries will be faster, and the rent near the port is actually lower than what we pay now.","t":"A：你覺得經理會同意我們明年把倉庫搬到靠近港口的計畫嗎？ B：我想會，因為這是最【合乎邏輯的】選擇：運費會下降、送貨會更快，而且港口附近的租金其實比我們現在付的還低。"},{"w":"preoccupied","p":"adj.","d":"thinking about something so much that you do not notice other things","c":"心事重重的；全神貫注的","s":"A: Why didn't Tom answer when I said good morning to him in the elevator a few minutes ago? B: He is preoccupied with the big presentation to the bank this afternoon, so he probably didn't even hear you, and I'm sure he will apologize once the meeting is over.","t":"A：幾分鐘前我在電梯裡跟Tom說早安，他為什麼沒回應？ B：他正【全神貫注於】今天下午要對銀行做的大型簡報，所以他大概根本沒聽到你，我相信會議一結束他就會道歉。"},{"w":"stressed","p":"adj.","d":"worried and nervous because of too much work or pressure","c":"有壓力的；緊張的","s":"A: You look tired today, so is everything all right with the new project that you are managing for the hospital? B: I feel quite stressed because the client changed the design twice this week, and we still have to finish everything before the hospital opens its new wing next month.","t":"A：你今天看起來很累，你負責的那個醫院新專案一切都還好嗎？ B：我覺得很【有壓力】，因為客戶這週改了兩次設計，而我們還得在醫院下個月新大樓啟用前完成所有工作。"},{"w":"acceptable","p":"adj.","d":"good enough to be allowed or agreed to","c":"可接受的","s":"A: The supplier says it cannot deliver the chairs by Monday, but it can send them by Wednesday, so is that okay? B: Wednesday is acceptable as long as the chairs arrive before noon, because the new office opens on Thursday and the workers need the afternoon to set everything up.","t":"A：供應商說週一前無法交貨椅子，但週三可以送到，這樣可以嗎？ B：只要椅子在中午前送到，週三是【可接受的】，因為新辦公室週四開幕，工人需要整個下午來佈置。"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n.","d":"a way of thinking about something","c":"觀點；看法","s":"A: Why did you invite a customer to speak at our product design meeting this morning instead of only our engineers? B: We wanted to hear a different perspective, because engineers often focus on technical details, while customers can tell us what is actually easy or difficult to use at home.","t":"A：你今天早上為什麼邀請一位顧客到產品設計會議上發言，而不是只找我們的工程師？ B：我們想聽聽不同的【觀點】，因為工程師常常專注在技術細節上，而顧客能告訴我們在家裡實際使用時哪些容易、哪些困難。"},{"w":"insure","p":"v.","d":"to buy insurance so you get money if something is lost or damaged","c":"為…投保","s":"A: We are shipping the new laboratory equipment from Germany next month, so is there anything else we need to do? B: We should insure the whole shipment before it leaves the factory, because the machines are very expensive, and the company would lose a lot of money if anything were damaged at sea.","t":"A：我們下個月要從德國運送新的實驗室設備，還有什麼需要做的嗎？ B：我們應該在整批貨離開工廠前為它【投保】，因為這些機器非常昂貴，如果在海上有任何損壞，公司會損失很多錢。"},{"w":"previously","p":"adv.","d":"before now; earlier","c":"先前；以前","s":"A: Does the new marketing manager have any experience with the Asian market, or will she need extra training? B: She previously worked for a large cosmetics company in Seoul for five years, so she already understands what customers in this region want and how to reach them online.","t":"A：新的行銷經理有亞洲市場的經驗嗎？還是她需要額外訓練？ B：她【先前】在首爾一家大型化妝品公司工作了五年，所以她已經了解這個地區的顧客想要什麼，以及如何在網路上接觸他們。"},{"w":"well-organized","p":"adj.","d":"planned and arranged in a clear, sensible way","c":"井然有序的；組織良好的","s":"A: How was the annual sales conference in Kaohsiung that you attended last weekend with the rest of the team? B: It was very well-organized, because every session started on time, the speakers had clear handouts, and the staff helped us find our rooms quickly when we arrived at the hotel.","t":"A：你上週末和團隊一起參加的高雄年度業務大會怎麼樣？ B：非常【井然有序】，因為每場會議都準時開始，講者都有清楚的講義，而且我們抵達飯店時工作人員很快就幫我們找到房間。"},{"w":"orderly","p":"adj.","d":"arranged or done in a neat, calm way","c":"有秩序的；整齊的","s":"A: There will be more than five hundred guests at the product launch, so how can we stop the entrance from getting crowded? B: We will put up signs and ask staff to guide guests into lines, so that everyone can enter the hall in an orderly way without pushing or waiting too long.","t":"A：產品發表會將有超過五百位來賓，我們要怎麼避免入口擁擠？ B：我們會設置指示牌，並請工作人員引導來賓排隊，讓大家能以【有秩序的】方式進入會場，不會推擠或等太久。"},{"w":"deny","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is not true","c":"否認","s":"A: A local newspaper reported that our company is planning to close the factory in Tainan, so is that true? B: The CEO will deny the report at this afternoon's press conference, because the factory is actually expanding and will hire about one hundred new workers next spring.","t":"A：一家地方報紙報導我們公司打算關閉台南的工廠，這是真的嗎？ B：執行長會在今天下午的記者會上【否認】這則報導，因為工廠其實正在擴廠，明年春天還會招募大約一百名新員工。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"a happy feeling when something bad or worrying ends","c":"寬慰；鬆一口氣","s":"A: How did the team react when the client finally signed the contract after three months of difficult negotiations? B: It was a huge relief for everyone, because we had worked so many late nights on the proposal, and our manager even took the whole team out for dinner to celebrate.","t":"A：經過三個月艱難的談判，客戶終於簽約時，團隊有什麼反應？ B：對大家來說真是大大【鬆了一口氣】，因為我們為了這份提案熬了很多夜，經理甚至帶全隊去吃晚餐慶祝。"}]},{"unit":182,"theme":"Ice Cream 冰淇淋","cards":[{"w":"scoop","p":"n.","d":"a round amount of ice cream taken with a special spoon","c":"一球；一勺","s":"A: Our team finished the sales report early, so the manager wants to buy everyone a treat at the shop across the street; what should I order for you? B: Just get me one scoop of mint ice cream in a small cup, because I still have a client lunch later and do not want to feel too full.","t":"A：我們團隊提早完成了銷售報告，所以經理想請大家去對街的店吃點心；我該幫你點什麼？ B：幫我點一【球】薄荷冰淇淋，裝小杯就好，因為我待會還有跟客戶的午餐，不想吃得太飽。"},{"w":"cone","p":"n.","d":"a crisp, pointed biscuit that holds ice cream","c":"甜筒；錐形餅乾筒","s":"A: The children's party at the office starts at three, and the parents have asked whether the ice cream will be served in bowls or something easier to hold. B: We ordered small portions in a waffle cone for each child, so they can walk around and play games without needing spoons or plates.","t":"A：公司的兒童派對三點開始，家長們問冰淇淋是用碗裝還是用比較好拿的東西裝。 B：我們幫每個孩子訂了小份量的鬆餅【甜筒】，這樣他們可以邊走邊玩遊戲，不需要湯匙或盤子。"},{"w":"cup","p":"n.","d":"a small container used for serving food or drinks","c":"杯；杯子","s":"A: The caterer asked how we want the dessert presented at tomorrow's training session, since some staff will be eating at their desks while they take notes. B: Please ask them to put each serving of ice cream in a paper cup with a lid, so nothing spills on the laptops or the training materials.","t":"A：外燴業者問明天訓練課程的甜點要怎麼呈現，因為有些員工會在座位上邊吃邊做筆記。 B：請他們把每一份冰淇淋裝在有蓋子的紙【杯】裡，這樣就不會灑到筆電或訓練資料上。"},{"w":"flavor","p":"n.","d":"the particular taste of a food","c":"口味；味道","s":"A: Our new shop opens next Monday, and the owner wants to attract young office workers from the nearby business district during their lunch break. B: Then we should advertise a special flavor such as green tea or mango, because those choices are popular with local customers and look great on social media.","t":"A：我們的新店下週一開幕，老闆想在午休時間吸引附近商業區的年輕上班族。 B：那我們應該宣傳一種特別的【口味】，例如抹茶或芒果，因為這些選擇很受當地顧客歡迎，而且在社群媒體上看起來很棒。"},{"w":"vanilla","p":"n.","d":"a sweet flavor made from the seeds of a tropical plant","c":"香草","s":"A: The hotel kitchen is preparing desserts for a wedding of two hundred guests, and the couple has not told us which ice cream they prefer. B: Let's choose classic vanilla as the main choice, because almost everyone enjoys its simple, gentle taste, and it goes well with the chocolate cake they ordered.","t":"A：飯店廚房正在為一場兩百位賓客的婚禮準備甜點，新人還沒告訴我們他們偏好哪種冰淇淋。 B：我們選經典的【香草】當主要選項吧，因為幾乎每個人都喜歡它簡單溫和的味道，而且和他們訂的巧克力蛋糕很搭。"},{"w":"chocolate","p":"n.","d":"a sweet brown food made from cocoa beans","c":"巧克力","s":"A: Our sales of plain ice cream have dropped this quarter, and the marketing director wants a new product that will attract more customers in winter. B: How about a hot chocolate sauce poured over a scoop of vanilla, since people enjoy something warm and sweet when the weather turns cold?","t":"A：我們這一季原味冰淇淋的銷量下降了，行銷總監想要一款能在冬天吸引更多顧客的新產品。 B：在一球香草冰淇淋上淋熱【巧克力】醬如何？因為天氣變冷時，人們喜歡吃溫暖又甜的東西。"},{"w":"strawberry","p":"n.","d":"a small, soft red fruit with tiny seeds on the outside","c":"草莓","s":"A: The farm near our factory has offered to sell us fresh fruit at a low price this spring, and the product team is looking for ideas. B: We could make a limited strawberry ice cream with real pieces of the red fruit, and promote it as a local, seasonal product for families.","t":"A：我們工廠附近的農場今年春天願意以低價賣新鮮水果給我們，產品團隊正在找點子。 B：我們可以推出限量的【草莓】冰淇淋，裡面加入真正的紅色果肉，並把它當作在地的季節性產品向家庭推廣。"},{"w":"topping","p":"n.","d":"food put on top of another food to add flavor or decoration","c":"配料；淋醬","s":"A: Customers keep asking whether they can make their desserts more special, but our menu only offers plain scoops in a few basic flavors. B: Let's add a topping station with nuts, fruit, and sauces, and charge a small extra fee, because it will increase both customer satisfaction and our profits.","t":"A：顧客一直問能不能讓他們的甜點更特別，但我們的菜單只有幾種基本口味的原味冰淇淋球。 B：我們來增設一個【配料】區，提供堅果、水果和醬汁，並收取少許額外費用，因為這樣能提高顧客滿意度和我們的利潤。"},{"w":"sprinkle","p":"v.","d":"to scatter small pieces of something over a surface","c":"撒（上）","s":"A: The children's birthday cake looks a little plain, and the party starts in twenty minutes, so I'm worried the kids will be disappointed. B: Don't worry; just sprinkle some colorful sugar pieces over the ice cream and the frosting, and it will look bright and cheerful in all the photos.","t":"A：孩子的生日蛋糕看起來有點單調，派對二十分鐘後就開始了，我擔心孩子們會失望。 B：別擔心，只要在冰淇淋和糖霜上【撒】一些彩色糖粒，它在所有照片裡看起來就會鮮豔又歡樂。"},{"w":"syrup","p":"n.","d":"a thick, sweet liquid made from sugar","c":"糖漿","s":"A: Several customers complained that our pancakes and ice cream dessert tastes too dry, and the café manager wants to fix the problem before the weekend rush. B: We could pour a little maple syrup over each plate, which will make the dish sweeter and softer without increasing our costs very much.","t":"A：有幾位顧客抱怨我們的鬆餅冰淇淋甜點吃起來太乾，咖啡館經理想在週末客流高峰前解決這個問題。 B：我們可以在每盤淋上一點楓【糖漿】，這樣會讓這道甜點更甜更軟，而且不會增加太多成本。"},{"w":"waffle","p":"n.","d":"a crisp, flat cake with a pattern of square holes","c":"鬆餅；格子鬆餅","s":"A: The breakfast buffet at our conference hotel always runs out of pancakes, and guests have started complaining to the front desk. B: Let's add a waffle machine so guests can make their own crisp cakes and top them with ice cream, fruit, or cream while they wait for their meetings.","t":"A：我們會議飯店的早餐自助吧鬆餅總是不夠，客人已經開始向櫃台抱怨了。 B：我們來加一台【格子鬆餅】機，讓客人在等開會時可以自己做酥脆的鬆餅，再加上冰淇淋、水果或奶油。"},{"w":"gelato","p":"n.","d":"an Italian-style ice cream that is dense and smooth","c":"義式冰淇淋","s":"A: Our partners from Milan are visiting the office next week, and the director wants to take them somewhere special for dessert after the meeting. B: There is a small shop downtown run by an Italian chef that makes fresh gelato every morning, so they might enjoy a taste of home.","t":"A：我們來自米蘭的合作夥伴下週要來參訪公司，總監想在會議後帶他們去個特別的地方吃甜點。 B：市中心有一家由義大利主廚經營的小店，每天早上都會現做【義式冰淇淋】，所以他們或許會喜歡嘗嘗家鄉的味道。"},{"w":"sorbet","p":"n.","d":"a frozen dessert made from fruit juice and sugar, with no milk","c":"雪酪；冰沙","s":"A: Some of the guests at the company dinner cannot eat dairy products, so I'm not sure what dessert we should offer them instead of ice cream. B: The restaurant can serve a lemon sorbet, which is made only from fruit juice, water, and sugar, so it is safe and still feels light and fresh.","t":"A：公司晚宴有些賓客不能吃乳製品，所以我不確定該提供什麼甜點來代替冰淇淋。 B：餐廳可以提供檸檬【雪酪】，它只用果汁、水和糖做成，所以很安全，吃起來也清爽新鮮。"},{"w":"frozen yogurt","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cold dessert like ice cream but made from yogurt","c":"優格冰淇淋；霜凍優格","s":"A: Many of our gym members want a healthy snack after their workout, but the café only sells cakes and sugary drinks right now. B: We should install a self-service frozen yogurt machine with fresh fruit toppings, because it is lower in fat than ice cream and fits our healthy image.","t":"A：我們有很多健身房會員想在運動後吃健康的點心，但咖啡館目前只賣蛋糕和含糖飲料。 B：我們應該安裝一台自助式【優格冰淇淋】機，附上新鮮水果配料，因為它的脂肪比冰淇淋低，也符合我們的健康形象。"},{"w":"creamy","p":"adj.","d":"thick and smooth, like cream","c":"綿密的；奶油般的","s":"A: Customers have said our new low-fat ice cream feels icy and hard, and the sales figures for the last two months are very disappointing. B: The research team is adding more milk to the recipe, so the next version should feel much more creamy and smooth while still keeping the calories low.","t":"A：顧客說我們新的低脂冰淇淋吃起來冰冰硬硬的，過去兩個月的銷售數字非常令人失望。 B：研發團隊正在配方中加入更多牛奶，所以下一個版本吃起來應該會更【綿密】順滑，同時仍保持低熱量。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"having a taste like sugar","c":"甜的","s":"A: The focus group tested our new mango dessert yesterday, and the product manager asked me to summarize their main comments for today's meeting. B: Most people liked the fresh fruit, but they said it was far too sweet, so we should reduce the sugar before we start mass production next month.","t":"A：焦點團體昨天試吃了我們的新芒果甜點，產品經理要我為今天的會議整理他們的主要意見。 B：大部分人喜歡新鮮的水果，但他們說它太【甜】了，所以在下個月開始量產前，我們應該減少糖量。"},{"w":"cold","p":"adj.","d":"having a low temperature","c":"冰冷的；寒冷的","s":"A: Why are the ice cream bars in the delivery van soft today, even though the driver left the warehouse only thirty minutes ago? B: The cooling system broke down on the highway, so the inside of the van was not cold enough, and we will need to return the whole shipment.","t":"A：為什麼送貨車裡的冰棒今天是軟的，司機明明三十分鐘前才離開倉庫？ B：冷卻系統在高速公路上故障了，所以車廂內不夠【冷】，我們得把整批貨退回去。"},{"w":"refreshing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel cooler and less tired","c":"清涼的；提神的","s":"A: It was over thirty-five degrees during the outdoor product launch, and many of the visitors looked tired and hot by the afternoon. B: That's why we handed out free lemon ice pops, which were very refreshing, and several people told me it was the best part of the whole event.","t":"A：戶外產品發表會時氣溫超過三十五度，到了下午很多來賓看起來又累又熱。 B：這就是為什麼我們發送了免費的檸檬冰棒，非常【清涼】，好幾個人跟我說那是整場活動最棒的部分。"},{"w":"rich","p":"adj.","d":"containing a lot of cream, butter, sugar, or flavor","c":"濃郁的；油膩的","s":"A: I had the triple chocolate dessert at the client dinner last night, but I couldn't finish it, even though it looked so wonderful. B: That one is very rich, because the chef uses heavy cream, dark chocolate, and butter, so most guests share one plate between two people.","t":"A：我昨晚在客戶晚宴上點了三重巧克力甜點，雖然看起來很棒，我卻吃不完。 B：那道非常【濃郁】，因為主廚用了濃奶油、黑巧克力和奶油，所以大部分客人都是兩個人分一盤。"},{"w":"smooth","p":"adj.","d":"having an even texture without lumps","c":"滑順的；細滑的","s":"A: The quality control team found small pieces of ice in yesterday's batch, and several stores have already returned the products to our factory. B: We need to check the mixing machine, because when it works correctly, the ice cream is perfectly smooth, with no hard bits that customers can feel on their tongues.","t":"A：品管團隊在昨天那批產品中發現了小冰晶，幾家店已經把產品退回我們工廠了。 B：我們需要檢查攪拌機，因為它正常運作時，冰淇淋會非常【滑順】，顧客舌頭上不會感覺到任何硬顆粒。"},{"w":"melt","p":"v.","d":"to change from solid to liquid because of heat","c":"融化","s":"A: Why did the ice cream cake for the retirement party arrive looking so soft and out of shape this afternoon? B: The delivery driver got stuck in heavy traffic for an hour without a freezer bag, so it started to melt in the hot car before he reached our office building.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午退休派對的冰淇淋蛋糕送來時看起來又軟又變形？ B：送貨司機沒帶保冷袋，在車陣中塞了一個小時，所以蛋糕在抵達我們辦公大樓前，就在悶熱的車裡開始【融化】了。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drinks to customers or guests","c":"供應；端上","s":"A: The restaurant is fully booked tonight for a company celebration, and the head chef is worried that the desserts will be ready too early. B: Keep the ice cream in the freezer and only serve it to the guests right after the main course, so it stays firm and looks perfect on the plate.","t":"A：餐廳今晚被一場公司慶功宴包場了，主廚擔心甜點會太早準備好。 B：把冰淇淋放在冷凍庫，等主菜一結束才【端上】給賓客，這樣它能保持硬度，盤中看起來也很完美。"},{"w":"freeze","p":"v.","d":"to become hard and solid because of cold, or to make something do this","c":"冷凍；結冰","s":"A: The new kitchen assistant asked how long the fruit mixture needs to stay in the cold room before we can sell it to customers. B: You should freeze it for at least six hours, and check it carefully before opening, because if it is still soft, the texture will be wrong.","t":"A：新來的廚房助理問水果混合物要在冷藏室放多久才能賣給顧客。 B：你至少要【冷凍】六個小時，開店前要仔細檢查，因為如果它還是軟的，口感就會不對。"},{"w":"lick","p":"v.","d":"to move your tongue across something","c":"舔","s":"A: The photographer wants a natural picture for our summer advertising campaign, but the child models look nervous in front of the camera. B: Give each child a real ice cream and let them lick it slowly while they play in the park, so they relax and we can take some happy, natural photos.","t":"A：攝影師想為我們的夏季廣告活動拍一張自然的照片，但兒童模特兒在鏡頭前看起來很緊張。 B：給每個孩子一支真的冰淇淋，讓他們在公園玩的時候慢慢【舔】，這樣他們會放鬆，我們就能拍到一些開心又自然的照片。"},{"w":"taste","p":"v.","d":"to try a small amount of food to find out its flavor","c":"品嚐；試吃","s":"A: The supermarket buyer will visit our factory on Thursday to decide whether to stock our new line of desserts in all her stores. B: Let's prepare small samples so she can taste each product before the meeting, because she will trust her own opinion more than our sales figures.","t":"A：超市採購員週四會來我們工廠，決定是否要在她所有的分店上架我們的新系列甜點。 B：我們準備一些小樣品，讓她在會議前【品嚐】每一項產品，因為她會比較相信自己的意見，而不是我們的銷售數字。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: I'm planning the menu for the annual client dinner, and I have already chosen the soup, salad, and main course with the restaurant manager. B: For dessert, let's offer a choice of ice cream or fruit cake, since some guests prefer something light after such a large and heavy meal.","t":"A：我正在規劃年度客戶晚宴的菜單，已經和餐廳經理選好了湯、沙拉和主菜。 B：【甜點】的部分，我們提供冰淇淋或水果蛋糕讓大家選擇吧，因為吃完這麼豐盛的一餐後，有些賓客會想吃清淡一點的東西。"},{"w":"treat","p":"n.","d":"something special and pleasant that you give someone or do for yourself","c":"款待；請客；特別的享受","s":"A: The whole department worked late every night this week to finish the project on time, and everyone looks exhausted this Friday afternoon. B: The manager is buying ice cream for all of us as a treat, so please tell the team to come to the break room at three o'clock.","t":"A：整個部門這週每晚都加班，才準時完成專案，大家在這個週五下午看起來都累壞了。 B：經理要買冰淇淋【請客】慰勞大家，所以請通知團隊三點到休息室集合。"},{"w":"parlor","p":"n.","d":"a shop that sells a particular product or service, such as ice cream","c":"店；專賣店","s":"A: Where should we hold the small farewell party for Linda, since she doesn't like noisy bars or expensive restaurants? B: There's a quiet ice cream parlor around the corner with comfortable sofas and a private room, and it's the perfect place for a relaxed afternoon with the team.","t":"A：我們該在哪裡為琳達辦小型歡送會？因為她不喜歡吵鬧的酒吧或昂貴的餐廳。 B：轉角有一家安靜的冰淇淋【店】，有舒適的沙發和包廂，是和團隊度過輕鬆下午的完美地點。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a product name made by a particular company","c":"品牌","s":"A: Our supermarket has too many kinds of ice cream on the shelves, and the store manager wants to save space in the freezers. B: Let's keep the most popular brand from each price range and stop ordering the ones that sold fewer than fifty boxes last month.","t":"A：我們超市架上的冰淇淋種類太多了，店長想節省冷凍櫃的空間。 B：我們保留每個價位最受歡迎的【品牌】，並停止訂購上個月賣不到五十盒的那些。"},{"w":"portion","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food served to one person","c":"一份；份量","s":"A: Some of our customers say the desserts here are too big, and many of them leave half of their ice cream on the plate. B: We could offer a smaller portion at a lower price, which would reduce food waste and attract people who are trying to eat less sugar.","t":"A：有些顧客說這裡的甜點太大份，很多人把一半的冰淇淋留在盤子上。 B：我們可以用較低的價格提供小一點的【份量】，這樣能減少食物浪費，也能吸引正在努力少吃糖的人。"},{"w":"calorie","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring the energy in food","c":"卡路里；熱量","s":"A: The new government rules require restaurants to show health information on their menus by next month, so what should we add for our desserts? B: We need to print the calorie count next to each item, so customers can see how much energy is in every scoop before they order.","t":"A：新的政府規定要求餐廳在下個月前於菜單上標示健康資訊，那我們的甜點要加上什麼呢？ B：我們需要在每個品項旁印上【卡路里】數，讓顧客在點餐前就能知道每一球含有多少熱量。"},{"w":"occasionally","p":"adv.","d":"sometimes, but not often","c":"偶爾","s":"A: Do you eat ice cream every day now that you work right next to the famous dessert shop on the first floor of our building? B: No, I only buy it occasionally, maybe once or twice a month after a long meeting, because I'm trying to stay healthy and save money.","t":"A：既然你現在就在我們大樓一樓那家知名甜點店旁邊工作，你每天都吃冰淇淋嗎？ B：不，我只是【偶爾】買，大概一個月一兩次，在開完很長的會之後，因為我正努力保持健康和存錢。"},{"w":"quickly","p":"adv.","d":"fast; in a short time","c":"迅速地；很快地","s":"A: Our ice cream truck will be parked at the outdoor music festival all afternoon, and the weather forecast says it will be extremely hot. B: Then the staff must work quickly and close the freezer door after every order, because the products will turn soft in just a few minutes.","t":"A：我們的冰淇淋車整個下午都會停在戶外音樂節，天氣預報說會非常熱。 B：那員工必須【迅速地】工作，每次出餐後都要關上冷凍櫃門，因為產品幾分鐘內就會變軟。"},{"w":"deliciously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that tastes very good","c":"美味地；可口地","s":"A: What did the food critic write about our new dessert in today's newspaper, and should we share the review with our customers? B: She said our coconut ice cream was deliciously creamy and full of real fruit, so we should definitely post her comments on our website and social media pages.","t":"A：美食評論家在今天的報紙上怎麼寫我們的新甜點？我們該把評論分享給顧客嗎？ B：她說我們的椰子冰淇淋【美味地】綿密，充滿真正的果肉，所以我們絕對應該把她的評論貼在網站和社群媒體上。"}]},{"unit":183,"theme":"Ideas 想法","cards":[{"w":"concept","p":"n.","d":"a general idea of what something is or how it should be","c":"概念","s":"A: Our marketing team has been arguing about the new coffee shop design all week, so what exactly did the owner decide at Friday's meeting? B: She chose a simple concept built around local farmers, so every cup, poster, and menu will tell customers where the beans come from and why that matters.","t":"A：我們的行銷團隊整個星期都在為新咖啡店的設計爭論，老闆在週五的會議上到底決定了什麼？ B：她選了一個以在地農民為核心的簡單【概念】，所以每一杯咖啡、每張海報和菜單都會告訴顧客咖啡豆來自哪裡，以及為什麼這很重要。"},{"w":"notion","p":"n.","d":"an idea or belief about something","c":"觀念；想法","s":"A: Why does the new manager keep asking us to take proper lunch breaks and leave the office on time every evening? B: She rejects the old notion that staying late shows hard work, because she believes tired employees make more mistakes and lose the energy they need for creative tasks.","t":"A：為什麼新經理一直要求我們好好休息午餐時間，並且每天晚上準時下班？ B：她不認同「留得晚代表努力工作」這種舊【觀念】，因為她相信疲累的員工會犯更多錯，也會失去做創意工作所需的精力。"},{"w":"thought","p":"n.","d":"an idea or opinion that you have","c":"想法；念頭","s":"A: Before I send this budget to the finance department this afternoon, do you have any comments about the travel costs for the sales trip? B: Just one thought: we could save a lot of money if the team takes the train instead of flying, since the city is only three hours away.","t":"A：我今天下午把這份預算送去財務部之前，你對這趟業務出差的旅費有什麼意見嗎？ B：只有一個【想法】：如果團隊改搭火車而不搭飛機，我們可以省下很多錢，因為那座城市只有三小時車程。"},{"w":"insight","p":"n.","d":"a clear and deep understanding of something","c":"洞察；深刻見解","s":"A: What did you learn from the customer survey that the research company finished for us last week? B: It gave us a valuable insight into why younger shoppers prefer our online store, mainly because they can compare prices quickly and read honest reviews from other buyers before they pay.","t":"A：研究公司上週幫我們完成的顧客調查，你從中學到了什麼？ B：它讓我們對年輕消費者為什麼偏好我們的網路商店有了寶貴的【深入了解】，主要是因為他們可以快速比價，並在付款前閱讀其他買家的真實評論。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"something that gives you new ideas","c":"靈感","s":"A: Where did the designer find the ideas for the colorful new packaging that everyone in the office is talking about? B: She said her inspiration came from the night markets in Taipei, where bright signs, busy crowds, and delicious street food made her want to create something lively and fun.","t":"A：辦公室裡大家都在討論的那款色彩繽紛的新包裝，設計師是從哪裡找到點子的？ B：她說她的【靈感】來自台北的夜市，那裡明亮的招牌、熱鬧的人潮和美味的街頭小吃讓她想創作出活潑有趣的作品。"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make pictures or ideas in your mind","c":"想像力","s":"A: Our children's book publisher wants a new writer for the summer series, so what kind of person should we hire for the job? B: We need someone with a strong imagination who can create magical worlds and funny characters, because young readers quickly lose interest when the stories feel ordinary or predictable.","t":"A：我們的童書出版社想為暑期系列找一位新作家，我們應該雇用什麼樣的人來做這份工作？ B：我們需要一位【想像力】豐富的人，能創造出神奇的世界和有趣的角色，因為故事一旦平淡或可預測，年輕讀者很快就會失去興趣。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"an idea of what the future should be like","c":"願景","s":"A: Why are so many talented engineers applying to work at that small startup even though the salary is lower than at big companies? B: The founder has a clear vision for the future, where clean energy is cheap for every family, and people want to be part of something meaningful.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多優秀的工程師都去應徵那家小型新創公司，即使薪水比大公司低？ B：創辦人對未來有清楚的【願景】，希望讓每個家庭都能用上便宜的乾淨能源，而大家都想參與有意義的事情。"},{"w":"suggestion","p":"n.","d":"an idea that you offer for someone to think about","c":"建議","s":"A: The staff room is always messy after lunch, and nobody wants to clean the fridge, so how can we solve this problem fairly? B: I have a suggestion: let's create a weekly cleaning schedule on the notice board, so each team member takes one turn every month and nobody feels it is unfair.","t":"A：員工休息室午餐後總是很亂，也沒人想清冰箱，我們要怎麼公平地解決這個問題？ B：我有個【建議】：我們在布告欄上排一份每週打掃值日表，讓每位組員每個月輪一次，這樣就沒人會覺得不公平。"},{"w":"proposal","p":"n.","d":"a formal plan or idea that is offered for people to accept","c":"提案；建議書","s":"A: Have you heard whether the directors accepted our idea to open a second branch in Kaohsiung next spring? B: Not yet, but they asked us to send a detailed written proposal by Friday, including the expected costs, the number of new staff, and how long it will take to make a profit.","t":"A：你有聽說董事們是否接受了我們明年春天在高雄開第二家分店的構想嗎？ B：還沒有，不過他們要求我們在週五前送出一份詳細的書面【提案】，內容包括預估成本、新員工人數，以及需要多久才能獲利。"},{"w":"plan","p":"n.","d":"a set of steps you decide on to do something","c":"計畫","s":"A: The office is moving to a new building in March, so how will we make sure that nothing gets lost or damaged during the move? B: The manager has made a careful plan that lists which team packs each room, when the trucks arrive, and who will check every box at the new address.","t":"A：辦公室三月要搬到新大樓，我們要怎麼確保搬遷時沒有東西遺失或損壞？ B：經理已經訂了一份周詳的【計畫】，列出哪個團隊負責打包哪個房間、卡車何時抵達，以及誰會在新地址檢查每一個箱子。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a careful plan to reach a goal","c":"策略","s":"A: Sales of our sports drinks fell sharply last quarter, so what are we going to do to win back customers from our competitors? B: The marketing director introduced a new strategy that focuses on social media videos and free samples at gyms, since young athletes are our most important buyers.","t":"A：我們的運動飲料上一季銷量大幅下滑，我們要怎麼從競爭對手那裡贏回顧客？ B：行銷總監推出了一套新【策略】，重點放在社群媒體影片和在健身房發送免費試用品，因為年輕運動員是我們最重要的買家。"},{"w":"approach","p":"n.","d":"a way of dealing with something","c":"方法；處理方式","s":"A: Training new employees used to take two whole weeks, but this year it only took five days, so what changed in the program? B: We tried a different approach, pairing each new worker with an experienced colleague who explains the tasks while they work together, instead of giving long lectures in a classroom.","t":"A：以前訓練新員工要整整兩週，但今年只花了五天，課程有什麼改變？ B：我們試了一種不同的【方法】，讓每位新員工和一位有經驗的同事搭檔，一邊一起工作一邊解說任務，而不是在教室裡上冗長的課。"},{"w":"solution","p":"n.","d":"a way to solve a problem","c":"解決辦法","s":"A: Customers keep complaining that they wait too long on the phone when they call our service center during busy lunch hours. B: One possible solution is adding an online chat service on our website, so people can ask simple questions without waiting, and our phone staff can handle the difficult cases.","t":"A：顧客一直抱怨在午餐尖峰時段打電話到我們的客服中心時，要在電話上等太久。 B：一個可行的【解決辦法】是在網站上增加線上即時客服，這樣大家問簡單問題就不必等待，電話客服人員也能專心處理困難的案件。"},{"w":"innovation","p":"n.","d":"a new idea, method, or product","c":"創新；新發明","s":"A: Why did the electronics company win so many awards at the technology fair in Berlin this year? B: Judges praised its latest innovation, a folding laptop that charges with sunlight, because it helps travelers and students work anywhere without searching for a power outlet in airports or cafés.","t":"A：為什麼這家電子公司今年在柏林的科技展上贏得這麼多獎項？ B：評審們稱讚它最新的【創新產品】——一台用陽光充電的折疊筆電，因為它讓旅客和學生在任何地方都能工作，不必在機場或咖啡館到處找插座。"},{"w":"theory","p":"n.","d":"an idea that tries to explain why something happens","c":"理論；推測","s":"A: Nobody understands why our online sales always increase on rainy weekends, even when we don't run any special promotions. B: My theory is that people stay indoors when the weather is bad, so they spend more time browsing shopping websites on their phones and end up buying things.","t":"A：沒有人明白為什麼我們的網路銷售在下雨的週末總是增加，即使我們沒有做任何特別促銷。 B：我的【推測】是天氣不好時大家都待在室內，所以會花更多時間用手機瀏覽購物網站，最後就買了東西。"},{"w":"hypothesis","p":"n.","d":"an idea that has not yet been proven and needs testing","c":"假設","s":"A: What is the research team trying to prove in the experiment they started at our three downtown stores last month? B: Their hypothesis is that soft background music makes shoppers stay longer and spend more, so they are comparing sales in stores with and without music for eight weeks.","t":"A：研究團隊上個月在我們市中心三家店開始的實驗，他們想證明什麼？ B：他們的【假設】是輕柔的背景音樂會讓顧客停留更久、花更多錢，所以他們正在比較有音樂和沒音樂的門市八週的銷售額。"},{"w":"belief","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling that something is true or right","c":"信念；信仰","s":"A: Why does the owner of the bakery refuse to sell bread that is more than one day old, even though it wastes money? B: It's her strong belief that customers deserve only the freshest products, and she donates the leftover bread to a local shelter every night instead of throwing it away.","t":"A：為什麼麵包店老闆拒絕販售超過一天的麵包，即使這樣很浪費錢？ B：她堅定的【信念】是顧客只該得到最新鮮的產品，而且她每天晚上都把剩下的麵包捐給當地的收容所，而不是丟掉。"},{"w":"opinion","p":"n.","d":"what you think or feel about something","c":"意見；看法","s":"A: I'm thinking about buying the new laptop for my design work, but it's quite expensive, so do you think it's worth the money? B: In my opinion, it's a good choice, because the screen is bright and accurate, the battery lasts all day, and it will probably save you time on big projects.","t":"A：我在考慮買那台新筆電來做設計工作，但它相當貴，你覺得值得嗎？ B：依我【看】，它是個好選擇，因為螢幕明亮又準確，電池可以撐一整天，而且在大型案子上大概能幫你省下時間。"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of looking at something","c":"觀點；角度","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager ask the cleaning staff to join the meeting about improving guest rooms next year? B: She wanted to hear their perspective, because they visit every room each day and know exactly which beds, lamps, and showers guests complain about most often.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理要請清潔人員參加明年改善客房的會議？ B：她想聽聽他們的【觀點】，因為他們每天進出每個房間，最清楚房客最常抱怨哪些床、檯燈和淋浴設備。"},{"w":"brainstorm","p":"v.","d":"to think of many ideas quickly in a group","c":"腦力激盪；集思廣益","s":"A: We need a fresh name for our new line of healthy snacks before the trade show next month, but nobody has any good ideas yet. B: Let's book the meeting room for an hour tomorrow morning and brainstorm together, writing every possible name on the whiteboard before we choose the best three.","t":"A：下個月商展前，我們需要替新的健康零食系列取個新名字，但目前還沒人有好點子。 B：我們明天早上訂一小時的會議室，一起【腦力激盪】，先把所有可能的名字寫在白板上，再選出最好的三個。"},{"w":"conceive","p":"v.","d":"to think of a new idea or plan","c":"構想出；想出","s":"A: Who first came up with the free shuttle bus that takes employees from the train station to the factory every morning? B: Our human resources manager helped conceive the service three years ago, after noticing that many workers arrived late because the walk from the station took almost forty minutes.","t":"A：每天早上把員工從火車站載到工廠的免費接駁車，最早是誰想出來的？ B：我們的人資經理三年前協助【構想出】這項服務，因為她注意到很多員工遲到，原因是從車站走過來要將近四十分鐘。"},{"w":"propose","p":"v.","d":"to suggest an idea or plan for others to consider","c":"提議；提出","s":"A: The team is tired of the long Monday meetings that often last until lunch, so what are you going to say to the director? B: I'm going to propose a shorter fifteen-minute meeting where everyone stands up and shares only their main tasks, so we can start working much earlier.","t":"A：團隊已經受夠常常開到午餐時間的冗長週一會議了，你打算跟總監說什麼？ B：我打算【提議】改成十五分鐘的短會，大家站著開，只分享自己的主要任務，這樣我們就能早一點開始工作。"},{"w":"imagine","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture of something in your mind","c":"想像","s":"A: The architect showed us drawings of the new office, but it is hard to understand how the space will really look and feel. B: Try to imagine a large bright room with plants everywhere, comfortable sofas near the windows, and quiet booths where you can make phone calls without any noise.","t":"A：建築師給我們看了新辦公室的圖，但很難理解這個空間實際上看起來和感覺起來會是怎樣。 B：試著【想像】一個寬敞明亮、到處都有植物的房間，窗邊有舒服的沙發，還有安靜的小隔間讓你不受噪音干擾地講電話。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to create and build something new over time","c":"開發；發展","s":"A: Our customers keep asking for an easier way to order food from our restaurant without calling during the busy dinner hours. B: That's why we hired a programmer to develop a mobile app, which will let people choose dishes, pay online, and see exactly when their order will be ready for pickup.","t":"A：我們的顧客一直希望有更簡單的方式向餐廳點餐，不必在忙碌的晚餐時段打電話。 B：所以我們請了一位程式設計師來【開發】手機應用程式，讓大家可以選菜、線上付款，並清楚看到餐點何時可以取餐。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and interesting things or ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: What kind of person is the advertising agency looking for to lead its new campaign for the sports shoe company? B: They want a creative designer who can produce surprising videos and posters, because the client believes that ordinary advertisements will not attract the attention of busy teenagers today.","t":"A：廣告公司在找什麼樣的人來帶領運動鞋公司的新宣傳活動？ B：他們想要一位【有創意的】設計師，能做出令人驚喜的影片和海報，因為客戶認為普通的廣告吸引不了現今忙碌的青少年的注意。"},{"w":"innovative","p":"adj.","d":"using new methods or ideas","c":"創新的","s":"A: How did that small local bank manage to attract so many young customers in such a short period of time? B: It introduced an innovative service that lets people open an account in five minutes with their phone, without visiting a branch or filling in long paper forms.","t":"A：那家地方小銀行是怎麼在這麼短時間內吸引這麼多年輕客戶的？ B：它推出了一項【創新的】服務，讓大家用手機五分鐘就能開戶，不必去分行，也不用填冗長的紙本表格。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"new and different from anything else","c":"原創的；獨到的","s":"A: Why didn't the judges choose the poster from the large design company, even though it looked very professional? B: They thought it was too similar to last year's winner, and they preferred a student's original idea that used recycled paper and showed the city in a completely new way.","t":"A：為什麼評審沒有選那家大型設計公司的海報，即使它看起來很專業？ B：他們認為它和去年的得獎作品太像了，他們比較喜歡一位學生的【獨創】點子，用回收紙並以全新的方式呈現這座城市。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"based on general ideas, not real examples","c":"抽象的","s":"A: Why did so many employees look confused after the CEO's speech about the company's new values this morning? B: His ideas were too abstract, with big words like trust and growth but no real examples, so people didn't understand what they should actually do differently at work.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上執行長談公司新價值觀的演講後，這麼多員工看起來一頭霧水？ B：他的想法太【抽象】了，只有「信任」、「成長」這類大字眼卻沒有實際例子，所以大家不明白在工作上實際該做哪些改變。"},{"w":"practical","p":"adj.","d":"useful and sensible in real situations","c":"實用的；務實的","s":"A: The consultant gave us twenty pages of advice about saving energy, but which changes can we actually make this month? B: The most practical step is turning off computers and lights every evening, because it costs nothing, takes only a few minutes, and could reduce our electricity bill noticeably.","t":"A：顧問給了我們二十頁關於節能的建議，但哪些改變是我們這個月真的能做到的？ B：最【實際】的一步是每天晚上關掉電腦和電燈，因為它不花錢、只要幾分鐘，而且能明顯降低我們的電費。"},{"w":"clearly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easy to understand","c":"清楚地","s":"A: The new interns seemed lost during their first week, so what can we do to help the next group understand their tasks better? B: Supervisors should explain each job clearly on the first day, give written instructions with examples, and check in with the interns every afternoon to answer any questions.","t":"A：新來的實習生第一週似乎很迷惘，我們能做些什麼來幫助下一批人更了解他們的工作？ B：主管應該在第一天就【清楚地】說明每項工作，提供附有範例的書面指示，並每天下午關心實習生，回答他們的任何問題。"},{"w":"creatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that uses new and interesting ideas","c":"有創意地","s":"A: Our budget for the company's anniversary party is very small this year, so how can we still make it a fun event for everyone? B: We'll have to think creatively, perhaps by asking staff to perform music, cook their favorite dishes, and decorate the hall with drawings made by their children.","t":"A：今年公司週年派對的預算很少，我們要怎麼還是讓它成為大家都開心的活動？ B：我們得【有創意地】思考，也許請員工表演音樂、煮他們最喜歡的菜，並用他們孩子畫的圖來布置會場。"},{"w":"openly","p":"adv.","d":"in an honest way, without hiding anything","c":"公開地；坦率地","s":"A: How does the new team leader make sure that problems are reported early instead of being hidden until it's too late? B: She encourages everyone to speak openly at the weekly meeting, and she never blames people for mistakes, so staff feel safe sharing bad news quickly.","t":"A：新的組長如何確保問題能及早被回報，而不是被隱瞞到為時已晚？ B：她鼓勵每個人在每週會議上【坦率地】發言，而且她從不因為錯誤責怪別人，所以員工覺得可以放心地盡快分享壞消息。"},{"w":"actively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that involves doing things with energy","c":"積極地；主動地","s":"A: Why was Kevin chosen as employee of the month, when he has only worked in the sales department for six months? B: He actively looks for ways to improve our service, regularly visiting customers, collecting feedback, and sharing useful ideas with the team without waiting for the manager to ask.","t":"A：凱文才在業務部工作六個月，為什麼會被選為本月最佳員工？ B：他【積極地】尋找改善我們服務的方法，經常拜訪客戶、收集意見，而且不等經理要求就主動和團隊分享有用的點子。"},{"w":"widely","p":"adv.","d":"by many people or in many places","c":"廣泛地","s":"A: Is it true that the new recycling program started by our office is now being used by other companies in the city? B: Yes, the idea has been widely accepted, and more than fifty businesses have joined because it saves money and the local newspaper wrote a positive story about it.","t":"A：我們辦公室發起的新回收計畫，現在城裡其他公司也在使用，是真的嗎？ B：是的，這個點子已被【廣泛】接受，超過五十家企業加入了，因為它能省錢，而且當地報紙也寫了一篇正面的報導。"}]},{"unit":184,"theme":"Idol 偶像","cards":[{"w":"celebrity","p":"n.","d":"a famous person, especially in entertainment","c":"名人","s":"A: Why is there such a long line of people with cameras outside the new shopping mall on Main Street this afternoon? B: A famous celebrity from a popular cooking show is opening her own bakery there today, so hundreds of shoppers came early to take photos and get free samples.","t":"A：今天下午為什麼主街新購物中心外面有這麼長一排拿著相機的人？ B：一位來自熱門烹飪節目的知名【名人】今天在那裡開設她自己的烘焙坊，所以數百名購物者提早來拍照並領取免費試吃品。"},{"w":"star","p":"n.","d":"a very famous performer, such as an actor or singer","c":"明星","s":"A: Do you know why the marketing team decided to spend so much of this year's budget on the new television commercial? B: They hired a well-known movie star to appear in it, and they believe her fans will buy our sports drinks after seeing her use them at the gym.","t":"A：你知道為什麼行銷團隊決定把今年這麼多預算花在新的電視廣告上嗎？ B：他們請了一位知名的電影【明星】來拍廣告，他們相信她的粉絲看到她在健身房喝我們的運動飲料後就會購買。"},{"w":"icon","p":"n.","d":"a famous person or thing that represents an idea or style","c":"代表人物；偶像","s":"A: Why did the company choose that older singer for the anniversary campaign instead of someone younger and more modern? B: She is a fashion icon whom people of every age recognize immediately, and the managers think her classic image will remind customers that our brand has been trusted for fifty years.","t":"A：為什麼公司週年活動選了那位資深歌手，而不是更年輕、更現代的人？ B：她是各個年齡層的人都能立刻認出的時尚【代表人物】，主管們認為她經典的形象能提醒顧客，我們的品牌已經受到信賴五十年了。"},{"w":"hero","p":"n.","d":"a person admired for being brave or doing something great","c":"英雄","s":"A: Did you hear what happened at the train station near our office during the fire alarm yesterday evening? B: Yes, a young cleaner helped an elderly passenger out of the building before the firefighters arrived, and now everyone in the neighborhood calls him a local hero and wants to thank him.","t":"A：你有聽說昨天傍晚火警警報響起時，我們辦公室附近的火車站發生了什麼事嗎？ B：有，一位年輕的清潔工在消防員抵達前幫助一位年長的乘客離開建築物，現在整個社區的人都稱他是當地的【英雄】，想要感謝他。"},{"w":"role model","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose good behavior others copy","c":"榜樣；模範","s":"A: Why does the training department want Ms. Lin to speak to all the new employees during their first week at the company? B: She started as a part-time assistant and became a department manager in eight years, so she is a great role model for young workers who want to grow their careers here.","t":"A：為什麼訓練部門希望林小姐在新進員工到職的第一週對他們演講？ B：她從兼職助理做起，八年內成為部門經理，所以對想在這裡發展職涯的年輕員工來說，她是絕佳的【榜樣】。"},{"w":"influence","p":"n.","d":"the power to change what people think or do","c":"影響；影響力","s":"A: Why are so many teenagers suddenly buying that expensive brand of running shoes at our downtown store this month? B: A popular singer wore them in her latest music video, and her influence on young shoppers is so strong that the shoes sold out in just three days.","t":"A：為什麼這個月突然有這麼多青少年在我們市中心的店購買那個昂貴品牌的跑鞋？ B：一位受歡迎的歌手在她最新的音樂影片中穿了那雙鞋，她對年輕消費者的【影響力】非常強大，所以那雙鞋三天內就賣光了。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"someone or something that gives you new ideas or the wish to do something","c":"靈感；啟發","s":"A: Where did the designer get the idea for the colorful new logo that everyone in the meeting liked so much this morning? B: She said her favorite painter was the main inspiration, because she visited his exhibition last weekend and loved how he used bright colors to show happy feelings.","t":"A：設計師是從哪裡得到今天早上會議中大家都很喜歡的那個繽紛新標誌的點子？ B：她說她最喜愛的畫家是主要的【靈感來源】，因為她上週末去看了他的展覽，很喜歡他用明亮色彩表現快樂情緒的方式。"},{"w":"fan","p":"n.","d":"a person who likes a famous person, team, or band very much","c":"粉絲；迷","s":"A: Why are you leaving work early on Friday when we still have so many reports to finish before the end of the month? B: I am a huge fan of that rock band, and I bought tickets to their concert six months ago, but I promise to finish my reports on Thursday night.","t":"A：月底前我們還有這麼多報告要完成，你為什麼星期五要提早下班？ B：我是那個搖滾樂團的超級【粉絲】，六個月前就買了他們演唱會的票，但我保證星期四晚上會把報告完成。"},{"w":"fandom","p":"n.","d":"all the fans of a person, group, or show as a community","c":"粉絲群；粉絲圈","s":"A: Why does our marketing manager spend so much time reading online forums about that Korean pop group? B: The group's fandom is very active on social media, and if those loyal fans like our new phone case design, they will share it with millions of people around the world for free.","t":"A：為什麼我們的行銷經理花這麼多時間看那個韓國流行團體的網路論壇？ B：那個團體的【粉絲群】在社群媒體上非常活躍，如果那些忠實粉絲喜歡我們新的手機殼設計，他們就會免費分享給全世界數百萬人。"},{"w":"supporter","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps or likes a person, group, or idea","c":"支持者","s":"A: How did the small bookstore on Park Road manage to stay open after the rent increased so much last year? B: One loyal supporter who had shopped there for twenty years organized a fundraising event, and many neighbors donated money and bought books to help the owner pay the bills.","t":"A：公園路上那家小書店在去年房租大漲之後，是怎麼繼續營業的？ B：一位在那裡購物二十年的忠實【支持者】籌辦了一場募款活動，許多鄰居捐錢並買書，幫助老闆支付帳單。"},{"w":"follower","p":"n.","d":"a person who follows someone, especially on social media","c":"追蹤者；追隨者","s":"A: Why did the restaurant invite that young food blogger to try the new menu before it opens to the public next week? B: She posts reviews every day, and nearly every follower of her popular account visits the places she recommends, so one good post could bring us hundreds of new customers.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳在下週對外開放前，邀請那位年輕的美食部落客來試吃新菜單？ B：她每天發布評論，幾乎她熱門帳號的每一位【追蹤者】都會去她推薦的地方，所以一篇好評就可能為我們帶來數百位新顧客。"},{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to like and respect someone very much","c":"欽佩；欣賞","s":"A: Why do you always talk about your old manager from the hotel where you worked before joining our company? B: I really admire the way she stayed calm during busy holidays and treated every guest and employee kindly, so I try to follow her example when I lead my own team now.","t":"A：你為什麼總是談到你加入我們公司之前在飯店工作時的前主管？ B：我真的很【欣賞】她在忙碌的假期仍保持冷靜，並且親切對待每位客人和員工，所以現在我帶領自己的團隊時，都努力以她為榜樣。"},{"w":"respect","p":"v.","d":"to have a good opinion of someone because of their qualities","c":"尊敬；尊重","s":"A: Why does everyone in the factory listen so carefully whenever the old engineer gives advice during the morning meetings? B: The workers respect him because he has solved difficult machine problems for over thirty years and always explains things patiently to new staff who make mistakes.","t":"A：為什麼每當那位資深工程師在晨會上給建議時，工廠裡的每個人都聽得那麼仔細？ B：工人們都很【尊敬】他，因為他三十多年來解決過許多困難的機器問題，而且總是耐心地向犯錯的新員工解釋。"},{"w":"praise","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is very good","c":"稱讚；讚揚","s":"A: What did the director say about the charity concert that our team organized at the city park last weekend? B: She plans to praise everyone at Monday's meeting, because the event raised more money than expected and many local newspapers wrote positive stories about our company.","t":"A：主任對我們團隊上週末在市立公園舉辦的慈善音樂會有什麼看法？ B：她打算在星期一的會議上【稱讚】每個人，因為活動募得的款項比預期多，而且許多地方報紙都寫了關於我們公司的正面報導。"},{"w":"idolize","p":"v.","d":"to admire someone so much that you think they are perfect","c":"崇拜；把…當偶像","s":"A: Why does your younger brother practice basketball for four hours every day, even during the cold winter holidays? B: He has started to idolize a famous professional player from Taiwan, so he watches all of her games online and dreams of playing in a big international league one day.","t":"A：為什麼你弟弟每天練習籃球四小時，即使是寒冷的寒假也一樣？ B：他開始【崇拜】一位來自台灣的知名職業球員，所以他在網路上看她所有的比賽，夢想有一天能在大型國際聯賽打球。"},{"w":"promote","p":"v.","d":"to help sell a product or make it well known through advertising","c":"宣傳；推廣","s":"A: Why is that well-known actor visiting our headquarters next Tuesday instead of filming his new movie? B: He signed a contract to promote our new line of electric scooters, so he will record videos in our showroom and talk with reporters about why he enjoys riding them to work.","t":"A：為什麼那位知名演員下週二要來我們總部，而不是去拍他的新電影？ B：他簽了合約要【宣傳】我們新的電動機車系列，所以他會在我們的展示間錄影，並和記者聊聊他為什麼喜歡騎它們上班。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the confidence or support to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: How can we get more employees to join the volunteer program at the children's hospital this year? B: We could invite a popular athlete to visit the office and encourage staff to take part, because many people will listen if someone they admire explains how meaningful the work is.","t":"A：今年我們要怎麼讓更多員工參加兒童醫院的志工計畫？ B：我們可以邀請一位受歡迎的運動員來辦公室【鼓勵】員工參加，因為如果由他們欣賞的人來說明這份工作多有意義，很多人都會聽。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的","s":"A: Why are so many customers asking about the blue jacket in the front window of our clothing store? B: It became very popular after a young singer wore the same style in her latest music video, so we have already ordered three hundred more from the factory.","t":"A：為什麼有這麼多顧客在詢問我們服飾店前面櫥窗裡的那件藍色夾克？ B：在一位年輕歌手於她最新的音樂影片中穿了同款之後，它就變得非常【受歡迎】，所以我們已經向工廠多訂了三百件。"},{"w":"famous","p":"adj.","d":"known by very many people","c":"有名的；著名的","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager ask the staff to clean the lobby twice this afternoon and prepare extra security guards? B: A famous football player is checking in tonight with his family, and the manager expects many reporters and excited fans to wait outside the main entrance.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理要員工今天下午把大廳打掃兩次，並準備額外的保全人員？ B：一位【知名的】足球員今晚要和家人入住，經理預期會有許多記者和興奮的粉絲在正門外等候。"},{"w":"talented","p":"adj.","d":"having a natural ability to do something well","c":"有才華的；有天分的","s":"A: Who will design the posters for the company's music festival this summer, since our usual designer is on vacation? B: We hired a very talented art student from the local university, and her sample drawings were so creative that the whole planning committee agreed to give her the job immediately.","t":"A：既然我們平常合作的設計師在休假，今年夏天公司音樂節的海報要由誰設計？ B：我們請了一位非常【有才華的】當地大學藝術系學生，她的樣稿很有創意，整個籌備委員會都同意立刻把這份工作交給她。"},{"w":"charismatic","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, attractive personality that makes people like and follow you","c":"有魅力的；有領袖氣質的","s":"A: Why did the board choose Mr. Chen as the new spokesperson for our company's environmental campaign? B: He is warm, confident, and charismatic, so when he speaks at press conferences, people pay attention, trust his message, and want to learn more about our recycling program.","t":"A：為什麼董事會選擇陳先生擔任我們公司環保活動的新發言人？ B：他溫暖、自信又【有魅力】，所以當他在記者會上發言時，大家都會專心聽、相信他傳達的訊息，並想進一步了解我們的回收計畫。"},{"w":"influential","p":"adj.","d":"having the power to change what people think or do","c":"有影響力的","s":"A: Why is the publishing company so excited that the TV host mentioned our new cookbook on her morning program? B: She is one of the most influential people in the food industry, and whenever she recommends a book, thousands of viewers order it online on the same day.","t":"A：為什麼出版社對那位電視主持人在她的晨間節目中提到我們的新食譜這麼興奮？ B：她是食品業最【有影響力的】人之一，每當她推薦一本書，就有數千名觀眾當天上網訂購。"},{"w":"stylish","p":"adj.","d":"fashionable and attractive","c":"時髦的；有型的","s":"A: What did the customers say about the new uniforms that our airline introduced for flight attendants last month? B: Most passengers think they look modern and stylish, and several fashion magazines even wrote articles comparing the bright red design to clothes worn by famous models.","t":"A：顧客對我們航空公司上個月為空服員推出的新制服有什麼看法？ B：大部分乘客覺得它們看起來現代又【時髦】，還有幾本時尚雜誌寫文章，把那亮紅色的設計和知名模特兒穿的衣服相比較。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"working very hard because you care about something","c":"投入的；專注的","s":"A: How did that singer stay so successful for more than thirty years while many other artists disappeared quickly? B: She is extremely dedicated to her work, practicing every morning, writing new songs constantly, and always arriving early to rehearsals, so her fans trust her to give an excellent show.","t":"A：在許多其他藝人很快消失的情況下，那位歌手是怎麼成功三十多年的？ B：她對工作極為【投入】，每天早上練習、不斷創作新歌，排練時也總是提早到，所以她的粉絲相信她一定會帶來精彩的演出。"},{"w":"loyally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that keeps supporting someone for a long time","c":"忠誠地；忠實地","s":"A: Why does that small coffee shop still have so many customers even though a big chain store opened across the street? B: Many local people have loyally supported the owner for fifteen years because he remembers everyone's names, and they say his friendly service is worth more than cheaper prices.","t":"A：為什麼那家小咖啡店對面開了大型連鎖店，卻仍然有這麼多顧客？ B：許多當地人十五年來一直【忠實地】支持老闆，因為他記得每個人的名字，他們說他親切的服務比更便宜的價格更有價值。"},{"w":"widely","p":"adv.","d":"by many people or in many places","c":"廣泛地","s":"A: Why do you think the young actress was chosen to be the face of the new tourism campaign for Taiwan? B: She is widely known in Japan and Korea because of her popular TV dramas, so the tourism bureau hopes travelers from those countries will want to visit the places she shows.","t":"A：你覺得為什麼那位年輕女演員被選為台灣新觀光宣傳活動的代言人？ B：因為她受歡迎的電視劇，她在日本和韓國【廣為】人知，所以觀光局希望那些國家的旅客會想去她介紹的地方。"},{"w":"passionately","p":"adv.","d":"with very strong feelings","c":"熱情地；熱烈地","s":"A: Why did so many people stay after the conference to talk with the speaker from the environmental group? B: She spoke so passionately about protecting the ocean, sharing photos and personal stories from her diving trips, that many guests wanted to ask how their companies could help.","t":"A：為什麼會議結束後有這麼多人留下來和那位環保團體的講者交談？ B：她如此【熱情地】談論保護海洋，分享她潛水旅行的照片和親身經歷，讓許多來賓想問他們的公司可以怎麼幫忙。"},{"w":"openly","p":"adv.","d":"honestly, without hiding your feelings or opinions","c":"坦率地；公開地","s":"A: Why has the famous tennis player become so popular with office workers who usually don't watch sports? B: She talks openly in interviews about feeling stressed and tired, so many busy employees feel she understands their daily problems and find her honest words very comforting.","t":"A：為什麼那位知名網球選手會這麼受到平常不看運動比賽的上班族歡迎？ B：她在訪談中【坦率地】談論自己感到壓力和疲累，所以許多忙碌的員工覺得她了解他們每天的煩惱，並覺得她真誠的話語很令人安慰。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that everyone can see or hear","c":"公開地","s":"A: Did the singer ever explain why she canceled her concert at the stadium last weekend at such short notice? B: Yes, she publicly apologized to her fans on her website this morning and promised that everyone who bought a ticket will get a full refund and a free ticket to her next show.","t":"A：那位歌手有解釋為什麼她臨時取消上週末在體育場的演唱會嗎？ B：有，她今天早上在網站上【公開】向粉絲道歉，並承諾每位買票的人都會得到全額退款以及她下一場演出的免費門票。"},{"w":"achievement","p":"n.","d":"something good that you succeed in doing after hard work","c":"成就","s":"A: Why is the team having a special dinner at the Italian restaurant downtown on Friday evening? B: Our manager wants to celebrate a great achievement, because we finished the difficult airport project two weeks early and the client said it was the best work they had ever seen.","t":"A：為什麼團隊星期五晚上要在市中心的義大利餐廳舉辦特別晚餐？ B：我們經理想慶祝一項了不起的【成就】，因為我們提早兩週完成了困難的機場專案，客戶還說那是他們看過最好的作品。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"a show in which someone sings, acts, or plays music","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: How was the concert at the city hall last night that your company sponsored for the local children's charity? B: The band gave an amazing performance that lasted almost three hours, and the audience was so excited that people stood up and sang along to every song until the very end.","t":"A：你們公司昨晚為當地兒童慈善機構贊助的市政廳音樂會怎麼樣？ B：樂團帶來了一場將近三小時的精彩【演出】，觀眾非常興奮，大家站起來跟著唱每一首歌，直到最後。"},{"w":"career","p":"n.","d":"the job or series of jobs a person does during their working life","c":"職業生涯","s":"A: Why did the famous baseball player visit our sports equipment company for a meeting with the marketing director? B: He is retiring next year after a long career, and he wants to start a new business selling gloves and bats designed for children who are just beginning to play.","t":"A：為什麼那位知名棒球選手要來我們運動用品公司和行銷總監開會？ B：他在漫長的【職業生涯】之後明年要退休了，他想創業販售專為剛開始打球的孩子設計的手套和球棒。"},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"public praise and thanks for someone's work","c":"表彰；肯定","s":"A: Why was the old designer invited to the award ceremony at the convention center next month? B: She will receive special recognition for her forty years of work creating beautiful posters for movies, and many young designers who learned from her plan to attend and give speeches.","t":"A：為什麼那位資深設計師受邀參加下個月在會議中心舉行的頒獎典禮？ B：她將因四十年來為電影創作精美海報而獲得特別【表彰】，許多曾向她學習的年輕設計師也打算出席並致詞。"},{"w":"legacy","p":"n.","d":"something good that a person leaves behind for the future","c":"遺產；留下的影響","s":"A: Why is the company building a new music school in the old factory building near the river? B: The founder loved music, and his children want to protect his legacy by giving young people from poor families the chance to learn instruments for free after school.","t":"A：為什麼公司要在河邊的舊工廠建築裡蓋一所新的音樂學校？ B：創辦人熱愛音樂，他的孩子們想藉由讓清寒家庭的年輕人放學後免費學習樂器，來守護他留下的【精神遺產】。"}]},{"unit":185,"theme":"Imagination 想像力","cards":[{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new and unusual ideas","c":"富有想像力的","s":"A: Our new coffee shop opens next month, but the designer's first plan for the walls looked boring and plain. What did you decide? B: We hired a more imaginative artist from a local college, and she painted colorful city scenes that make customers want to stay longer and take photos.","t":"A：我們的新咖啡店下個月開幕，但設計師對牆面的第一個方案看起來既無聊又單調。你們決定怎麼做？ B：我們從當地大學請了一位更【富有想像力的】藝術家，她畫了色彩繽紛的城市景象，讓顧客想待久一點並拍照。"},{"w":"imagine","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture or idea of something in your mind","c":"想像","s":"A: The client wants to see how the new office will look before they sign the contract, but the building is still empty. What should we do? B: Let's show them a 3D model, because it is hard for most people to imagine the final space when they only see bare concrete walls.","t":"A：客戶想在簽約前看看新辦公室的樣子，但大樓還是空的。我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們給他們看3D模型吧，因為大多數人只看到光禿禿的水泥牆時，很難【想像】最後的空間。"},{"w":"imaginary","p":"adj.","d":"not real; existing only in the mind","c":"虛構的；想像中的","s":"A: Why did the sales trainer ask everyone to talk to an empty chair during this afternoon's workshop at the hotel? B: She wanted us to practice with an imaginary customer first, so we could feel more relaxed before calling real clients and answering their difficult questions next week.","t":"A：為什麼銷售講師今天下午在飯店的工作坊上要大家對著一張空椅子說話？ B：她希望我們先和一位【想像中的】顧客練習，這樣下週打電話給真正的客戶並回答他們的難題之前，我們會比較放鬆。"},{"w":"fantasy","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant idea or story that is not real or not likely to happen","c":"幻想；奇幻","s":"A: The publishing company just signed a contract with a young writer from Taichung. What kind of books does she write? B: She writes fantasy novels about dragons and magic kingdoms, and her first series has already sold over fifty thousand copies to teenagers across Asia.","t":"A：出版公司剛和一位來自台中的年輕作家簽約。她寫哪一類的書？ B：她寫關於龍和魔法王國的【奇幻】小說，她的第一個系列已經在亞洲各地賣給青少年超過五萬本。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"able to make new things or think of new ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: Our department has a very small budget for the year-end party, and the manager says we cannot rent a fancy restaurant this time. Any ideas? B: Let's be creative and hold a costume party in the office, with homemade snacks, simple games, and a small prize for the best outfit.","t":"A：我們部門的尾牙預算很少，經理說這次不能租高級餐廳。有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們就【有創意】一點，在辦公室辦一場變裝派對，準備自製點心、簡單遊戲，並為最佳服裝準備一份小獎品。"},{"w":"creativity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to produce new and original ideas","c":"創造力","s":"A: Why did the advertising agency decide to hire the young designer instead of the candidate with ten years of experience? B: The interviewers were really impressed by her creativity, because her portfolio showed fresh ideas for posters, websites, and short videos that no other applicant had suggested.","t":"A：為什麼廣告公司決定聘用那位年輕設計師，而不是有十年經驗的應徵者？ B：面試官對她的【創造力】印象深刻，因為她的作品集展示了海報、網站和短片的新點子，是其他應徵者都沒提出的。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"a clear idea of what you want something to be like in the future","c":"願景；遠見","s":"A: Everyone at the meeting seemed excited after the new CEO's speech this morning. What did she talk about? B: She shared her vision for the company over the next ten years, including opening stores in Japan, cutting plastic waste, and offering more training to young employees.","t":"A：今天早上新執行長演講後，會議上每個人似乎都很興奮。她講了什麼？ B：她分享了她對公司未來十年的【願景】，包括在日本開店、減少塑膠廢棄物，以及為年輕員工提供更多培訓。"},{"w":"visualize","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture of something in your mind","c":"想像；使具體化","s":"A: The architect's drawings are very detailed, but the board members still look confused about the new lobby design. What can we do? B: Let's add some photos of similar hotels, because pictures will help them visualize how guests will move through the space and where the reception desk will be.","t":"A：建築師的圖面很詳細，但董事們對新大廳的設計看起來還是很困惑。我們能怎麼做？ B：我們加一些類似飯店的照片吧，因為圖片能幫助他們【在腦中具體想像】客人會如何在空間中移動，以及接待櫃台會在哪裡。"},{"w":"dream","p":"n.","d":"something you hope very much to have or do","c":"夢想","s":"A: I heard that Mr. Lin finally left the bank after working there for twenty years. What is he doing now? B: He is following his dream of opening a small bakery near the train station, and his bread has become so popular that people line up every morning before seven.","t":"A：我聽說林先生在銀行工作二十年後終於離職了。他現在在做什麼？ B：他正在追求在火車站附近開一家小麵包店的【夢想】，而他的麵包變得非常受歡迎，每天早上七點前就有人排隊。"},{"w":"daydream","p":"v.","d":"to think about pleasant things while you are awake and not paying attention","c":"做白日夢","s":"A: Why did the supervisor speak to the new cashier after lunch today? Did she make a big mistake with the money? B: Not really, but she often stares out of the window and seems to daydream while customers are waiting in line, so the supervisor reminded her to stay focused.","t":"A：今天午餐後主管為什麼找新收銀員談話？她在錢方面犯了大錯嗎？ B：其實沒有，但她常常盯著窗外，似乎在顧客排隊等候時【做白日夢】，所以主管提醒她要保持專注。"},{"w":"innovation","p":"n.","d":"a new idea, method, or product","c":"創新","s":"A: Our competitor's sales grew by thirty percent last year, while ours stayed the same. What do you think they are doing differently? B: They spend much more money on innovation, such as developing new apps and smart products, while we keep selling the same items we offered five years ago.","t":"A：我們的競爭對手去年銷售額成長了百分之三十，而我們的卻持平。你認為他們做了什麼不一樣的事？ B：他們在【創新】上花了更多錢，例如開發新的應用程式和智慧產品，而我們一直在賣五年前就有的同樣商品。"},{"w":"invent","p":"v.","d":"to create something that did not exist before","c":"發明","s":"A: Who is the speaker at the technology conference this Friday, and why is everyone so excited to hear her talk? B: She is the engineer who helped invent a cheap water filter for small villages, and her company now sells the product in more than twenty countries around the world.","t":"A：這週五科技研討會的講者是誰？為什麼大家這麼期待聽她演講？ B：她就是協助【發明】一種給小村莊用的平價濾水器的工程師，她的公司現在在全世界二十多個國家銷售這項產品。"},{"w":"fiction","p":"n.","d":"books and stories about imaginary people and events","c":"小說；虛構","s":"A: The bookstore manager wants to change the layout of the shop before the holiday season begins. What is her main plan? B: She wants to move all the fiction to the front tables, because novels and short story collections sell much better than travel guides and business books during December.","t":"A：書店經理想在假期旺季開始前改變店內的陳設。她主要的計畫是什麼？ B：她想把所有的【小說類書籍】移到前面的桌子，因為在十二月，小說和短篇故事集比旅遊指南和商業書籍賣得好得多。"},{"w":"fanciful","p":"adj.","d":"imaginative but not practical or realistic","c":"異想天開的；不切實際的","s":"A: Did the investors like the startup's plan to build a hotel on the moon within five years? B: Not at all; they said the idea was too fanciful and asked the founders to come back with a more realistic proposal that could actually make money in the near future.","t":"A：投資人喜歡那家新創公司五年內在月球上蓋飯店的計畫嗎？ B：一點也不；他們說這個點子太【異想天開】了，要創辦人帶著一個近期內真的能賺錢、更務實的提案再回來。"},{"w":"originality","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being new and different","c":"獨創性；原創性","s":"A: There were more than three hundred entries in the company's logo design contest. How did the judges choose the winner? B: They gave the highest scores for originality, so designs that looked too similar to famous brands were removed early, and the winner used a fresh shape nobody had seen before.","t":"A：公司標誌設計比賽有三百多件作品參賽。評審是怎麼選出優勝者的？ B：他們對【原創性】給最高分，所以看起來太像知名品牌的設計很早就被淘汰，而優勝者用了一個沒有人見過的新造型。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"someone or something that gives you new ideas","c":"靈感","s":"A: Your new line of summer dresses has such beautiful patterns and colors. Where did the design team get the ideas? B: They traveled to several fishing villages in southern Taiwan, and the bright boats and ocean views became the main inspiration for this year's collection.","t":"A：你們的新款夏季洋裝圖案和顏色好漂亮。設計團隊的點子是從哪裡來的？ B：他們去了台灣南部的幾個漁村，色彩鮮豔的漁船和海景成了今年系列的主要【靈感】。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something or give them new ideas","c":"激勵；啟發","s":"A: Why did the school invite a famous chef to speak to the students at the graduation ceremony next week? B: The principal hopes his life story will inspire young people to work hard, because he started as a dishwasher and later opened restaurants in three different countries.","t":"A：學校為什麼邀請一位知名主廚在下週的畢業典禮上對學生演講？ B：校長希望他的人生故事能【激勵】年輕人努力工作，因為他從洗碗工做起，後來在三個不同的國家開了餐廳。"},{"w":"visionary","p":"adj.","d":"having clear and original ideas about what the future should be like","c":"有遠見的","s":"A: Why do so many business magazines write articles about the founder of that electric car company? B: Many people consider him a visionary leader, because twenty years ago he predicted that clean energy would change transportation, and he built a successful company around that idea.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多商業雜誌寫那家電動車公司創辦人的文章？ B：許多人認為他是一位【有遠見的】領導者，因為二十年前他就預測乾淨能源會改變交通運輸，並圍繞這個想法建立了一家成功的公司。"},{"w":"conception","p":"n.","d":"the forming of an idea or plan; an understanding of something","c":"構想；概念","s":"A: How long did it take your team to finish the new shopping mall, from the first meeting to the opening day? B: From its conception to completion, the project took about six years, because we had to change the design twice and wait for the city government to approve every plan.","t":"A：你們團隊從第一次開會到開幕日，花了多久完成這座新購物中心？ B：從【構想】到完工，這個專案大約花了六年，因為我們必須改兩次設計，並等市政府核准每一份計畫。"},{"w":"brainstorm","p":"v.","d":"to discuss many ideas quickly in a group","c":"腦力激盪","s":"A: The marketing director wants a new slogan for the summer campaign by Friday, but nobody has a good idea yet. What should we do? B: Let's book the small meeting room tomorrow morning and brainstorm together for an hour, writing every suggestion on the whiteboard before we choose the best three.","t":"A：行銷總監要在週五前拿到夏季活動的新標語，但到現在還沒人有好點子。我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們明天早上訂小會議室，一起【腦力激盪】一小時，把每個建議都寫在白板上，再選出最好的三個。"},{"w":"novelty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being new and unusual","c":"新奇；新鮮感","s":"A: The robot waiters at the new restaurant downtown attracted huge crowds when it opened. Are they still that busy now? B: Not really; once the novelty wore off after a few months, fewer customers came, because the food was ordinary and the prices were quite high for such small portions.","t":"A：市中心那家新餐廳開幕時，機器人服務生吸引了大批人潮。他們現在還那麼忙嗎？ B：其實沒有；幾個月後【新鮮感】一過，來的客人就變少了，因為食物很普通，而且份量這麼小價格卻相當高。"},{"w":"illusion","p":"n.","d":"something that seems real or true but is not","c":"錯覺；幻覺","s":"A: This hotel room is quite small, but it feels much bigger than I expected. How did the designers do that? B: They put a large mirror on one wall and used light colors everywhere, which creates the illusion of more space even though the room is only twenty square meters.","t":"A：這間飯店房間蠻小的，但感覺比我預期的大很多。設計師是怎麼做到的？ B：他們在一面牆上裝了大鏡子，而且到處使用淺色，這製造了空間更大的【錯覺】，即使房間只有二十平方公尺。"},{"w":"myth","p":"n.","d":"an idea that many people believe but that is not true; an ancient story","c":"迷思；神話","s":"A: Some of our new employees think they must stay late every night to get promoted. Is that really true at this company? B: No, that is a common myth; the managers here judge people by the quality of their work and their results, not by how many hours they sit at their desks.","t":"A：我們有些新員工認為必須每晚加班才能升遷。在這家公司真的是這樣嗎？ B：不是，那是一個常見的【迷思】；這裡的主管是根據工作品質和成果來評價人，而不是看他們坐在辦公桌前多少小時。"},{"w":"symbolism","p":"n.","d":"the use of symbols to represent ideas","c":"象徵手法；象徵意義","s":"A: The new company logo is just a green leaf and a blue circle. Why did the board choose such a simple design? B: They liked the symbolism behind it, because the leaf represents our care for the environment and the circle shows that we serve customers all around the globe.","t":"A：新的公司標誌只是一片綠葉和一個藍色圓圈。董事會為什麼選了這麼簡單的設計？ B：他們喜歡它背後的【象徵意義】，因為葉子代表我們對環境的關懷，而圓圈表示我們服務全球各地的顧客。"},{"w":"speculate","p":"v.","d":"to guess about something without having all the facts","c":"推測；臆測","s":"A: Everyone in the office is talking about why the general manager suddenly left last Friday. Do you know the real reason? B: No, and I don't want to speculate without facts; the company will send an official announcement on Monday, so we should just wait and focus on our work.","t":"A：辦公室裡每個人都在談論總經理上週五為什麼突然離職。你知道真正的原因嗎？ B：不知道，我也不想在沒有事實的情況下【臆測】；公司週一會發出正式公告，所以我們應該等著，專心做好自己的工作。"},{"w":"conjure","p":"v.","d":"to make a picture or idea appear in someone's mind","c":"使浮現於腦海；變出","s":"A: Why does the travel agency always use photos of white beaches and palm trees in its advertisements for winter tours? B: Those pictures conjure up images of warm sunshine and relaxing holidays, which is exactly what tired office workers want to think about during the cold, rainy months.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社的冬季旅遊廣告總是用白色沙灘和棕櫚樹的照片？ B：那些照片讓人腦中【浮現】溫暖陽光和輕鬆假期的畫面，這正是疲憊的上班族在寒冷多雨的月份裡想要想像的事。"},{"w":"envision","p":"v.","d":"to imagine something that may happen in the future","c":"展望；設想","s":"A: The city plans to turn the old railway station into a public space. What kind of place do the planners have in mind? B: They envision a lively area with cafes, small shops, and a weekend market, where families and tourists can relax after visiting the museums nearby.","t":"A：市政府計畫把舊火車站改造成公共空間。規劃人員心中想的是什麼樣的地方？ B：他們【設想】一個有咖啡館、小商店和週末市集的熱鬧區域，讓家庭和遊客在參觀附近的博物館後可以放鬆。"},{"w":"pretend","p":"v.","d":"to act as if something is true when it is not","c":"假裝","s":"A: During the customer service training, why did the trainer ask Kevin to stand at the front desk and shout at us? B: He asked Kevin to pretend to be an angry guest whose room was not ready, so the rest of us could practice staying calm and offering a polite solution.","t":"A：在客服訓練中，講師為什麼要凱文站在櫃台前對我們大吼？ B：他要凱文【假裝】是一位房間還沒準備好的生氣房客，這樣我們其他人就可以練習保持冷靜並提供有禮貌的解決方法。"},{"w":"hypothetical","p":"adj.","d":"based on a possible situation rather than a real one","c":"假設的","s":"A: During my job interview yesterday, the manager asked what I would do if a supplier suddenly doubled its prices. Was that a real problem? B: No, it was just a hypothetical question to test how you solve problems, so you shouldn't worry that the company is actually facing that situation right now.","t":"A：昨天面試時，經理問我如果供應商突然把價格調高一倍我會怎麼做。那是真實的問題嗎？ B：不是，那只是一個【假設性的】問題，用來測試你如何解決問題，所以你不用擔心公司現在真的面臨那種情況。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"based on ideas rather than real things; not showing objects realistically","c":"抽象的","s":"A: The hotel owner bought several large paintings for the lobby, but I can't tell what they are supposed to show. Can you? B: Not really, because they are abstract art with only shapes and bright colors, but many guests say the paintings make the lobby feel modern and full of energy.","t":"A：飯店老闆為大廳買了幾幅大型畫作，但我看不出它們想表達什麼。你看得出來嗎？ B：其實看不太出來，因為那是只有形狀和鮮豔色彩的【抽象】藝術，但許多房客說這些畫讓大廳感覺很現代又充滿活力。"},{"w":"playful","p":"adj.","d":"full of fun; not serious","c":"好玩的；俏皮的","s":"A: The children's clothing company wants a new advertisement for its spring collection. What style does the client prefer? B: They asked for a playful video with bright music, cartoon animals, and kids jumping in the park, because they want parents to feel happy and relaxed when they watch it.","t":"A：那家童裝公司想為春季系列拍新廣告。客戶偏好什麼風格？ B：他們要求一支【俏皮有趣的】影片，有輕快的音樂、卡通動物和在公園裡跳躍的孩子，因為他們希望父母觀看時感到快樂又放鬆。"},{"w":"surreal","p":"adj.","d":"very strange, like a dream","c":"超現實的；離奇的","s":"A: How did you feel when your small company won the national design award in front of all those famous companies last night? B: It felt completely surreal, like a strange dream, because only three years ago we were working from my tiny apartment with two old computers and no clients.","t":"A：昨晚你們的小公司在那麼多知名企業面前贏得全國設計獎時，你有什麼感覺？ B：感覺完全【不真實】，像一場奇怪的夢，因為三年前我們還在我的小公寓裡用兩台舊電腦工作，而且沒有任何客戶。"},{"w":"whimsical","p":"adj.","d":"unusual and playful in a way that is amusing","c":"異想天開的；古怪有趣的","s":"A: The new children's bookstore near our office has become very popular on social media. What makes it so special? B: It has a whimsical design, with a slide between the two floors, bookshelves shaped like trees, and a reading corner that looks like a cozy little castle.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家新的童書店在社群媒體上變得很受歡迎。它有什麼特別之處？ B：它有一種【奇趣】的設計，兩層樓之間有溜滑梯、書架做成樹的形狀，還有一個看起來像溫馨小城堡的閱讀角落。"}]},{"unit":186,"theme":"Immigration 移民","cards":[{"w":"immigrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who comes to live permanently in a new country","c":"移民（移入者）","s":"A: Who is the new engineer sitting next to Linda in the design department, and how long has he been working with our team? B: He is an immigrant from Brazil who moved here with his family last spring, and he already speaks our language well enough to lead the weekly project meetings.","t":"A：坐在設計部琳達旁邊的新工程師是誰？他和我們團隊合作多久了？ B：他是一位來自巴西的【移民】，去年春天和家人搬到這裡，他的語言已經說得夠好，可以主持每週的專案會議了。"},{"w":"migrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who moves from place to place, often to find work","c":"移工；流動人口","s":"A: Why does the farm hire so many extra workers every autumn, and where do they usually stay during the harvest season? B: Each migrant worker travels from a nearby country for about three months, and the company provides shared housing, meals, and a bus that takes them to the fields every morning.","t":"A：為什麼農場每年秋天都要僱用這麼多額外的工人？收成季節他們通常住在哪裡？ B：每位【移工】都從鄰近國家來工作大約三個月，公司提供共用宿舍、餐點，還有每天早上載他們到田裡的巴士。"},{"w":"migration","p":"n.","d":"the movement of people from one place to another","c":"遷移；移居","s":"A: Why are so many young people leaving the small towns in the north, and how is it affecting the local businesses there? B: The migration of workers to the big cities has been growing for ten years because salaries are higher, so many shops in those towns cannot find enough staff anymore.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多年輕人離開北部的小鎮？這對當地的商家有什麼影響？ B：工作者往大城市的【遷移】已經持續增加了十年，因為那裡薪水比較高，所以那些小鎮的許多商店再也找不到足夠的員工。"},{"w":"emigrate","p":"v.","d":"to leave your own country to live in another one","c":"移居國外","s":"A: I heard that Kevin from the accounting team handed in his resignation letter yesterday, so do you know why he decided to leave? B: He and his wife plan to emigrate to Canada next summer because her parents live there, and he has already received a job offer from a bank in Toronto.","t":"A：我聽說會計部的凱文昨天遞了辭呈，你知道他為什麼決定離職嗎？ B：他和太太打算明年夏天【移居】加拿大，因為她的父母住在那裡，而他已經收到多倫多一家銀行的工作錄取通知了。"},{"w":"emigration","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving your country to live in another one","c":"移出；移居國外","s":"A: Why is the hospital in my hometown having so much trouble finding experienced nurses these days? B: The high rate of emigration among medical workers is a big problem, because many nurses leave the country for better pay abroad, so the government is now offering bonuses to make them stay.","t":"A：為什麼我家鄉的醫院最近很難找到有經驗的護理師？ B：醫療人員的高【移出】率是個大問題，因為許多護理師為了更好的薪水出國工作，所以政府現在提供獎金讓他們留下來。"},{"w":"settle","p":"v.","d":"to start living in a place permanently","c":"定居","s":"A: After working in three different countries for the company, where do you and your family finally want to live? B: We would like to settle in a quiet town near the coast, because our children need a stable school and I can work from home most days of the week.","t":"A：在公司派駐過三個不同的國家之後，你和家人最後想住在哪裡？ B：我們想在海邊附近一個安靜的小鎮【定居】，因為孩子需要穩定的學校，而且我一週大部分的日子都可以在家工作。"},{"w":"residency","p":"n.","d":"the legal right to live in a country","c":"居留權；居留","s":"A: The new manager from Japan has started working here, but why does she still need to visit the government office every week? B: She is applying for permanent residency, so she must submit her work contract, bank records, and health check results before her current status expires next month.","t":"A：從日本來的新經理已經開始在這裡工作了，但她為什麼還需要每週跑政府機關？ B：她正在申請永久【居留權】，所以必須在目前的身分下個月到期前，繳交工作合約、銀行紀錄和健康檢查結果。"},{"w":"citizenship","p":"n.","d":"the legal status of being a member of a country","c":"公民身分；國籍","s":"A: You have lived and worked in this city for over twelve years, so are you planning to become a full member of the country? B: Yes, I finally applied for citizenship last month, and if everything goes well, I will be able to vote in the next election and travel with a new passport.","t":"A：你已經在這個城市生活和工作超過十二年了，你打算成為這個國家的正式一員嗎？ B：是的，我上個月終於申請了【公民身分】，如果一切順利，我就能在下次選舉投票，並且用新護照出國旅行。"},{"w":"visa","p":"n.","d":"an official document that lets you enter or stay in a country","c":"簽證","s":"A: Our sales director wants to attend the trade fair in India next month, so what should she prepare before booking the flight? B: She needs a business visa first, so please ask her to send her passport photo and invitation letter to the travel department by Friday, since processing takes about ten days.","t":"A：我們的業務總監下個月想去參加印度的貿易展，訂機票前她該準備什麼？ B：她得先辦商務【簽證】，所以請她在星期五前把護照照片和邀請函寄給差旅部門，因為辦理大約需要十天。"},{"w":"permit","p":"n.","d":"an official document that allows you to do something","c":"許可證","s":"A: The new chef from Italy is ready to start in our hotel kitchen, so why can't he begin working on Monday as planned? B: His work permit has not been approved yet, and our HR team says it is illegal for him to start until the labor office sends the official paperwork.","t":"A：從義大利來的新主廚已經準備好在我們飯店廚房上工了，為什麼他不能照計畫星期一開始工作？ B：他的工作【許可證】還沒核准，人資團隊說在勞動部門寄來正式文件之前，他開始工作是違法的。"},{"w":"border","p":"n.","d":"the line that separates two countries","c":"邊境；國界","s":"A: Why did the delivery of machine parts from Germany arrive two days later than the supplier promised? B: The trucks had to wait at the border for many hours because customs officers were checking every container carefully, so the driver could not continue the trip until Wednesday afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼從德國來的機械零件比供應商承諾的晚了兩天才送到？ B：卡車必須在【邊境】等好幾個小時，因為海關人員正仔細檢查每個貨櫃，所以司機直到星期三下午才能繼續上路。"},{"w":"refugee","p":"n.","d":"a person forced to leave their country because of war or danger","c":"難民","s":"A: Why is the community center collecting winter coats, blankets, and children's books this month? B: Many refugee families arrived in our city after the war started in their country, and they left home so quickly that most of them could only bring one small bag each.","t":"A：為什麼社區中心這個月在募集冬季外套、毛毯和童書？ B：在他們的國家爆發戰爭後，許多【難民】家庭來到我們的城市，他們離家時非常匆忙，大多數人每人只能帶一個小包包。"},{"w":"asylum","p":"n.","d":"protection given by a country to people escaping danger at home","c":"庇護","s":"A: Why is the young journalist from that country staying in our city, and is it safe for him to go back home? B: He asked for political asylum after writing articles that criticized his government, because he believes he might be arrested if he returns, so a lawyer is helping him with the application.","t":"A：為什麼那位來自那個國家的年輕記者待在我們的城市？他回國安全嗎？ B：他在寫了批評政府的文章之後申請了政治【庇護】，因為他認為如果回去可能會被逮捕，所以有一位律師正在協助他辦理申請。"},{"w":"deport","p":"v.","d":"to force a foreign person to leave a country","c":"驅逐出境","s":"A: Why is our restaurant owner so careful about checking every new worker's documents before hiring them? B: Last year the authorities decided to deport two cooks at a nearby restaurant who had no legal papers, and the owner there also had to pay a very large fine.","t":"A：為什麼我們餐廳老闆在僱用新員工前，對檢查每個人的文件這麼小心？ B：去年當局決定把附近一家餐廳兩名沒有合法文件的廚師【驅逐出境】，那裡的老闆也被罰了一大筆錢。"},{"w":"deportation","p":"n.","d":"the act of forcing someone to leave a country","c":"驅逐出境；遣返","s":"A: What happened to the tourist who stayed in the country for two years after his travel papers expired? B: He was caught working at a factory without permission, and now he is waiting for deportation at a government center, which means he will be sent back home on a flight next week.","t":"A：那個旅遊證件到期後還在這個國家待了兩年的觀光客後來怎麼了？ B：他被發現未經許可在工廠工作，現在正在政府收容中心等待【遣返】，也就是說他下週會被送上飛機回國。"},{"w":"naturalize","p":"v.","d":"to make a foreign person a citizen of a country","c":"使歸化（入籍）","s":"A: My colleague from Vietnam says she will finally receive her new passport next month, so what has she been doing to get it? B: The government agreed to naturalize her after she lived here for eight years, passed the language test, and showed that she had a stable job with our company.","t":"A：我那位來自越南的同事說她下個月終於會拿到新護照了，她這段時間都在做什麼才拿到的？ B：她在這裡住了八年、通過語言測驗，並證明在我們公司有穩定的工作之後，政府同意讓她【歸化入籍】。"},{"w":"naturalization","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming a citizen of a new country","c":"歸化；入籍","s":"A: Why does Mr. Chen look so happy today, and why is he taking the afternoon off from the office? B: His naturalization ceremony is at city hall this afternoon, where he will officially become a citizen after living and working here for more than ten years with his family.","t":"A：陳先生今天為什麼看起來那麼開心？他為什麼下午要請假不進辦公室？ B：他的【入籍】典禮今天下午在市政廳舉行，在這裡和家人生活、工作超過十年後，他將正式成為公民。"},{"w":"integration","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming part of a new group or society","c":"融入；融合","s":"A: How does the company help foreign employees feel comfortable after they move here with their families? B: We offer free language classes, local cooking events, and a buddy program, because successful integration into the community makes new staff happier and more likely to stay with us for many years.","t":"A：公司如何幫助外籍員工和家人搬來這裡後感到自在？ B：我們提供免費語言課程、在地烹飪活動和夥伴計畫，因為成功【融入】社區能讓新員工更快樂，也更可能在我們公司待很多年。"},{"w":"assimilation","p":"n.","d":"the process of fully taking on the culture of a new place","c":"同化","s":"A: Some of our older overseas staff seem to have completely changed their habits, food, and even their accent, haven't they? B: That kind of assimilation often happens after many years abroad, but our training program encourages people to keep their own traditions while they learn the local culture at the same time.","t":"A：我們有些年資較久的外籍員工，好像已經完全改變了他們的習慣、飲食，甚至口音，對吧？ B：在國外生活很多年後，常常會發生那種【同化】，但我們的訓練計畫鼓勵大家在學習當地文化的同時，也保留自己的傳統。"},{"w":"multicultural","p":"adj.","d":"including people of many different cultures","c":"多元文化的","s":"A: What do you like most about working in the Singapore office compared with your last job back home? B: It is a very multicultural workplace, so at lunch I can eat dishes from five different countries, and I have learned a lot from colleagues who celebrate different holidays throughout the year.","t":"A：和你之前在家鄉的工作比起來，你最喜歡在新加坡辦公室工作的哪一點？ B：這是一個非常【多元文化的】工作環境，所以午餐時我可以吃到五個不同國家的料理，也從一年中慶祝不同節日的同事身上學到很多。"},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"a range of different people or things","c":"多樣性；多元","s":"A: Why did the HR department change the way we advertise job openings this year? B: The company wants more diversity in its teams, so we now post jobs in several languages and invite people of different ages, backgrounds, and nationalities to apply for every position.","t":"A：為什麼人資部門今年改變了刊登職缺的方式？ B：公司希望團隊更加【多元】，所以我們現在用好幾種語言刊登職缺，並邀請不同年齡、背景和國籍的人應徵每一個職位。"},{"w":"ethnic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a group of people with a shared culture or origin","c":"種族的；民族的","s":"A: Where should we take the visiting clients for dinner tonight if they want to try something different from hotel food? B: There is a famous street downtown full of ethnic restaurants run by families from Thailand, Lebanon, and Mexico, and the prices are reasonable even for a large group like ours.","t":"A：如果來訪的客戶今晚想吃點和飯店餐點不一樣的東西，我們該帶他們去哪裡吃晚餐？ B：市中心有一條有名的街，滿是來自泰國、黎巴嫩和墨西哥的家庭經營的【異國民族】餐廳，即使像我們這樣的大團體，價格也很合理。"},{"w":"diaspora","p":"n.","d":"people who have spread from their home country to live in other countries","c":"海外僑民（群體）","s":"A: Why is our marketing team translating the new advertisement into Korean for the stores in Los Angeles and New York? B: The Korean diaspora in those cities is very large, and our research shows that many families there still prefer shopping websites and messages written in their first language.","t":"A：為什麼我們的行銷團隊要把新廣告翻譯成韓文，給洛杉磯和紐約的分店使用？ B：那些城市的韓國【海外僑民】人數非常多，我們的研究顯示，那裡有許多家庭仍然比較喜歡用母語寫的購物網站和訊息。"},{"w":"workforce","p":"n.","d":"all the workers in a company, industry, or country","c":"勞動力；全體員工","s":"A: How many of the people working at our factory in Mexico actually come from other countries? B: About a third of our workforce there is from abroad, so we hire interpreters for safety training and print every notice in three languages to make sure that nobody misses important information.","t":"A：在我們墨西哥工廠工作的人當中，實際上有多少來自其他國家？ B：那裡約三分之一的【員工】來自國外，所以我們聘請口譯員進行安全訓練，並把每則公告印成三種語言，確保沒有人錯過重要資訊。"},{"w":"labor","p":"n.","d":"work, especially physical work; workers as a group","c":"勞力；勞工","s":"A: Why are construction companies in the area asking the government to accept more workers from overseas? B: There is a serious shortage of labor on building sites, because young local people prefer office jobs, so many projects are falling behind schedule and costing developers a lot more money.","t":"A：為什麼這一帶的營造公司要求政府接受更多海外工人？ B：工地嚴重缺乏【勞力】，因為當地年輕人比較喜歡辦公室工作，所以許多工程進度落後，讓開發商多花了很多錢。"},{"w":"policy","p":"n.","d":"a set of official rules or plans made by a government or company","c":"政策","s":"A: Has the government changed the rules for hiring nurses and caregivers from other countries this year? B: Yes, the new immigration policy allows hospitals to hire foreign caregivers more quickly, but every worker must now pass a language test before they can start taking care of patients.","t":"A：政府今年有沒有改變僱用其他國家護理師和看護的規定？ B：有，新的移民【政策】讓醫院能更快聘用外籍看護，但現在每位工作者都必須先通過語言測驗，才能開始照顧病人。"},{"w":"quota","p":"n.","d":"a fixed number or amount that is officially allowed","c":"配額；名額","s":"A: Why can't our tech company bring in all ten engineers we interviewed in India last month? B: The government sets a yearly quota for skilled-worker visas, and this year's limit has almost been reached, so we can probably hire only four of them before December.","t":"A：為什麼我們科技公司不能把上個月在印度面試的十位工程師全部請來？ B：政府對技術人員簽證設定了年度【配額】，今年的上限幾乎已經用完，所以在十二月前我們大概只能聘用其中四位。"},{"w":"screening","p":"n.","d":"a careful check of people to find problems or risks","c":"審查；篩檢","s":"A: Why do passengers arriving on international flights have to wait so long at the airport these days? B: Every traveler now goes through a security screening that includes a passport scan, a short interview, and a health check, so the lines are much longer than they were last year.","t":"A：為什麼最近搭國際航班抵達的旅客在機場要等那麼久？ B：現在每位旅客都要經過一道安全【審查】，包括掃描護照、簡短面談和健康檢查，所以排隊人潮比去年長很多。"},{"w":"sponsor","p":"v.","d":"to officially support someone's application, for example for a visa","c":"擔保；資助","s":"A: The young designer we interviewed from Spain is excellent, but she does not have the right to work here yet, does she? B: That's right, so our company has agreed to sponsor her application, which means we will pay the fees and promise the government that she has a real job with us.","t":"A：我們面試的那位西班牙年輕設計師非常優秀，但她還沒有在這裡工作的權利，對吧？ B：沒錯，所以我們公司已經同意為她的申請【擔保】，也就是說我們會支付費用，並向政府保證她在我們這裡有一份真正的工作。"},{"w":"undocumented","p":"adj.","d":"not having official papers that allow you to live or work in a country","c":"無合法證件的","s":"A: Why did the inspectors visit the clothing factory near the harbor yesterday afternoon? B: They received a report that the owner was hiring undocumented workers and paying them very little, so they checked everyone's papers and found that six people had no legal right to work.","t":"A：為什麼檢查人員昨天下午去了港口附近的成衣工廠？ B：他們接獲檢舉，說老闆僱用【無合法證件的】工人而且薪水給得很少，所以他們檢查了每個人的文件，發現有六個人沒有合法工作權。"},{"w":"borderless","p":"adj.","d":"without borders or limits between countries","c":"無國界的","s":"A: How can our small design studio work with clients in Europe, Asia, and South America at the same time? B: The internet has created a borderless market for creative services, so we hold video meetings across time zones and receive payments online without ever leaving our office here in Taipei.","t":"A：我們這間小型設計工作室怎麼能同時和歐洲、亞洲和南美洲的客戶合作？ B：網路為創意服務創造了一個【無國界的】市場，所以我們跨時區開視訊會議、在線上收款，完全不用離開我們台北的辦公室。"},{"w":"relocate","p":"v.","d":"to move to a new place to live or work","c":"搬遷；調派","s":"A: Why is the whole marketing department packing boxes and cleaning their desks this week? B: The company has decided to relocate our regional headquarters to Singapore next month, so most of the team will move there, and HR is helping families find apartments and international schools.","t":"A：為什麼整個行銷部這週都在打包箱子、整理辦公桌？ B：公司決定下個月把我們的區域總部【搬遷】到新加坡，所以大部分的團隊成員都會搬過去，人資部正在幫各個家庭找公寓和國際學校。"},{"w":"resettle","p":"v.","d":"to help people move to a new place to live, especially after leaving their country","c":"重新安置","s":"A: What is the charity in our building doing with all those donated beds, tables, and kitchen supplies? B: They are working with the city to resettle forty families who escaped the floods in their home country, and each family will receive a furnished apartment and help finding a job.","t":"A：我們大樓裡的那個慈善機構拿那些捐贈的床、桌子和廚房用品要做什麼？ B：他們正和市政府合作，【重新安置】四十個逃離母國水災的家庭，每個家庭都會得到一間附家具的公寓，以及找工作的協助。"},{"w":"influx","p":"n.","d":"a large number of people or things arriving at the same time","c":"湧入","s":"A: Why are apartment prices near the new science park rising so quickly this year? B: There has been a huge influx of engineers from overseas since the chip factory opened, so landlords are raising rents, and many local families are now looking for cheaper homes farther away.","t":"A：為什麼新科學園區附近的公寓價格今年漲得這麼快？ B：自從晶片工廠開幕後，大量海外工程師【湧入】，所以房東紛紛調漲租金，許多當地家庭現在都在找更遠、更便宜的房子。"},{"w":"displacement","p":"n.","d":"the situation when people are forced to leave their homes","c":"流離失所；被迫遷移","s":"A: Why did the international aid group ask our company to donate tents, clean water, and emergency food this month? B: The earthquake caused the displacement of thousands of people from their villages, and many of them are now living in temporary camps with very few supplies.","t":"A：為什麼國際援助組織這個月請我們公司捐贈帳篷、乾淨的水和緊急糧食？ B：地震造成數千人從村莊【流離失所】，其中許多人現在住在物資非常缺乏的臨時營地。"}]},{"unit":187,"theme":"Importance 重要性","cards":[{"w":"significance","p":"n.","d":"the importance or meaning of something","c":"重要性；意義","s":"A: Why did the manager ask everyone to attend the meeting about the new client this afternoon, even the interns who only joined our team last week? B: She wanted all of us to understand the significance of this contract, because it could bring in more business than any other deal we have signed this year.","t":"A：為什麼經理要求大家都參加今天下午關於新客戶的會議，連上週才加入團隊的實習生也要去？ B：她希望我們所有人都了解這份合約的【重要性】，因為它可能帶來比今年簽過的任何交易都更多的生意。"},{"w":"significant","p":"adj.","d":"large or important enough to be noticed","c":"重大的；顯著的","s":"A: Have the changes to our online ordering system made any difference since the technical team updated the website at the beginning of last month? B: Yes, we have seen a significant increase in sales, especially from young customers who prefer shopping on their phones during their lunch breaks.","t":"A：自從技術團隊上個月初更新網站後，我們線上訂購系統的改變有帶來任何不同嗎？ B：有，我們看到銷售額【顯著的】成長，特別是來自喜歡在午休時用手機購物的年輕顧客。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how much something is worth or how useful it is","c":"價值","s":"A: Do you think we should still keep the old printer in the storage room, or should we throw it away when the cleaners come on Friday? B: I would sell it online instead, because even though it is old, it still has some value, and a small company might want to buy it.","t":"A：你覺得我們還要留著儲藏室裡的舊印表機，還是星期五清潔人員來的時候把它丟掉？ B：我會改成在網路上賣掉，因為它雖然舊，但仍有一些【價值】，可能會有小公司想買。"},{"w":"valuable","p":"adj.","d":"very useful or worth a lot of money","c":"寶貴的；有價值的","s":"A: How was the training workshop you attended in Kaohsiung last weekend, and would you recommend it to the new sales staff? B: It was really valuable, because the speaker shared practical tips about dealing with difficult customers, and I have already used two of them in my calls this week.","t":"A：你上週末在高雄參加的培訓工作坊怎麼樣？你會推薦給新的業務人員嗎？ B：真的很【寶貴】，因為講者分享了應對難纏顧客的實用技巧，我這週打電話時已經用了其中兩個。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"something that is more important than other things and must be done first","c":"優先事項","s":"A: There are so many tasks on my list today that I don't know where to start, so what should I finish before the director arrives this afternoon? B: Make the sales report your top priority, because the director needs it for her meeting with the investors, and the other jobs can wait until tomorrow.","t":"A：我今天的待辦事項太多，不知道從哪裡開始，主任今天下午到之前我應該先完成什麼？ B：把銷售報告當作你的首要【優先事項】，因為主任和投資人開會時需要它，其他工作可以等到明天。"},{"w":"essential","p":"adj.","d":"completely necessary","c":"必要的；不可或缺的","s":"A: I am packing for the business trip to Singapore next week, but my suitcase is already full, so what should I definitely bring with me? B: Your passport and laptop are essential, but you can leave the extra shoes at home because the hotel is close to the office and you will mostly be indoors.","t":"A：我正在為下週去新加坡出差打包，但行李箱已經滿了，我一定要帶什麼？ B：護照和筆電是【必要的】，但多的鞋子可以留在家，因為飯店離辦公室很近，你大部分時間都會待在室內。"},{"w":"necessity","p":"n.","d":"something that you need","c":"必需品；必要","s":"A: Why did the company decide to give every salesperson a new smartphone this year when the old ones still seem to work fine? B: Because these days a good phone is a necessity for our sales team, since they need to check emails, send quotes, and join video calls while they are visiting customers.","t":"A：舊手機看起來還很好用，為什麼公司今年決定給每位業務員一支新智慧型手機？ B：因為現在好手機對我們業務團隊來說是【必需品】，他們拜訪客戶時需要查看電子郵件、寄報價單和參加視訊會議。"},{"w":"crucial","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important because other things depend on it","c":"關鍵的；至關重要的","s":"A: Should we postpone the product launch, since the designers still haven't finished testing the new battery that has been causing problems? B: Yes, I think the testing stage is crucial, because if the battery fails after customers buy the product, we will lose their trust and our reputation will suffer.","t":"A：既然設計師還沒測試完一直出問題的新電池，我們應該延後產品發表嗎？ B：是的，我認為測試階段是【至關重要的】，因為如果顧客買了產品後電池故障，我們會失去他們的信任，商譽也會受損。"},{"w":"vital","p":"adj.","d":"very important and necessary","c":"極其重要的；不可或缺的","s":"A: Why does the factory manager check the safety equipment every single morning before the workers start operating the heavy machines? B: Because regular checks are vital for preventing accidents, and one broken helmet or loose cable could cause a serious injury that stops production for days.","t":"A：為什麼廠長每天早上在工人開始操作重型機械前都要檢查安全裝備？ B：因為定期檢查對預防意外【極其重要】，一頂破掉的安全帽或一條鬆脫的電線都可能造成嚴重受傷，讓生產停擺好幾天。"},{"w":"key","p":"adj.","d":"most important","c":"關鍵的；主要的","s":"A: What do you think made the new coffee shop near our office so popular with the people who work in this area? B: I believe friendly service was the key factor, because the staff remember everyone's names and favorite drinks, which makes busy office workers feel welcome every morning.","t":"A：你覺得是什麼讓我們辦公室附近的新咖啡店這麼受這一帶上班族歡迎？ B：我相信親切的服務是【關鍵】因素，因為店員記得每個人的名字和愛喝的飲料，讓忙碌的上班族每天早上都覺得受到歡迎。"},{"w":"central","p":"adj.","d":"most important or main","c":"核心的；主要的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team spend so much time talking about customer reviews during yesterday's long planning meeting? B: Because good reviews are central to our new advertising plan, and we want to show real comments from happy customers on our website and social media pages.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊在昨天冗長的企劃會議中花那麼多時間討論顧客評論？ B：因為好評是我們新廣告計畫的【核心】，我們想在網站和社群媒體頁面上展示滿意顧客的真實留言。"},{"w":"primary","p":"adj.","d":"main; most important","c":"主要的；首要的","s":"A: Why are you moving to a new apartment so far from the city center when your current place is close to the office? B: My primary reason is the cost, since the rent downtown went up again this year, and I would rather spend a little more time on the train and save money.","t":"A：你現在住的地方離公司很近，為什麼要搬到離市中心那麼遠的新公寓？ B：我的【主要】原因是費用，因為市中心的房租今年又漲了，我寧願多花一點時間搭火車來省錢。"},{"w":"fundamental","p":"adj.","d":"basic and very important","c":"基本的；根本的","s":"A: Our new employees keep making mistakes with the accounting software, so should we hire an expert to train them again next month? B: I think the problem is more fundamental, because many of them don't understand basic bookkeeping, so we should teach them those simple ideas first before using the software.","t":"A：我們的新員工使用會計軟體一直出錯，我們下個月應該請專家再訓練他們一次嗎？ B：我認為問題更【根本】，因為他們很多人不懂基本的記帳，所以在使用軟體之前應該先教他們這些簡單的概念。"},{"w":"critical","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important; serious","c":"關鍵的；危急的","s":"A: Why is everyone in the IT department working late tonight when they usually leave the office right at six o'clock? B: The next few hours are critical, because they must repair the main server before the online store opens tomorrow morning, or the company will lose thousands of orders.","t":"A：資訊部門的人通常六點準時下班，為什麼今晚大家都在加班？ B：接下來幾個小時很【關鍵】，因為他們必須在明天早上網路商店開張前修好主伺服器，否則公司會損失好幾千筆訂單。"},{"w":"major","p":"adj.","d":"very large or important","c":"主要的；重大的","s":"A: Why has the road in front of our office been closed for almost two weeks, making all of us arrive late every morning? B: The city is doing major repairs to the water pipes under the street, so they had to dig a huge hole, and the work probably won't finish until next month.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室前面的路封了快兩個星期，害我們每天早上都遲到？ B：市政府正在對街道下方的水管進行【重大】維修，所以必須挖一個大洞，工程可能要到下個月才會完成。"},{"w":"minor","p":"adj.","d":"small and not very important","c":"次要的；輕微的","s":"A: Did the delivery truck that hit the parking gate this morning cause a lot of damage to the building or hurt anyone? B: No, it was only a minor accident, so the driver just scratched the paint on the gate, and nobody was hurt, but security still wrote a short report about it.","t":"A：今天早上撞到停車場閘門的送貨卡車有對大樓造成很多損壞或傷到人嗎？ B：沒有，那只是一起【輕微的】事故，司機只刮傷了閘門的油漆，沒有人受傷，但保全還是寫了一份簡短的報告。"},{"w":"weighty","p":"adj.","d":"serious and important","c":"重大的；嚴肅的","s":"A: Why did the board members look so tired when they finally came out of the conference room late last night? B: They had to discuss some weighty issues, such as closing two factories and cutting jobs, so the meeting lasted almost six hours and nobody had time for dinner.","t":"A：為什麼董事會成員昨晚很晚終於走出會議室時看起來那麼疲倦？ B：他們必須討論一些【重大的】議題，例如關閉兩間工廠和裁員，所以會議開了將近六小時，沒有人有時間吃晚餐。"},{"w":"prominent","p":"adj.","d":"important and well known; easy to see","c":"顯眼的；著名的","s":"A: Where should we put the poster for the summer sale so that every customer who walks into the store will notice it? B: Let's hang it in a prominent position near the entrance, right above the shopping baskets, because almost everyone looks there when they first come inside.","t":"A：我們應該把夏季特賣的海報放在哪裡，才能讓每位走進店裡的顧客都注意到？ B：我們把它掛在入口附近【顯眼的】位置，就在購物籃正上方，因為幾乎每個人一進來都會看那裡。"},{"w":"notable","p":"adj.","d":"important or interesting enough to get attention","c":"值得注意的；顯著的","s":"A: Was there anything special about the trade fair in Taipei last week, or was it the same as the one we visited last year? B: The most notable change was the large area for electric cars, which attracted huge crowds, and many visitors stayed there for hours asking the companies questions.","t":"A：上週台北的商展有什麼特別的嗎？還是跟我們去年參觀的一樣？ B：最【值得注意的】改變是電動車的大型展區，吸引了大批人潮，很多參觀者在那裡待了好幾個小時向廠商發問。"},{"w":"meaningful","p":"adj.","d":"serious, useful or important","c":"有意義的","s":"A: Why do you volunteer at the community center every Saturday morning after working such long hours at the bank all week? B: Teaching children to read feels more meaningful to me than anything I do at work, and seeing them improve each week gives me energy for the busy days ahead.","t":"A：你整個星期在銀行工作那麼長的時間，為什麼每週六早上還去社區中心當志工？ B：教孩子閱讀對我來說比工作上做的任何事都更【有意義】，看到他們每週進步讓我有精力面對接下來忙碌的日子。"},{"w":"consequence","p":"n.","d":"a result of an action, often a bad one","c":"後果；結果","s":"A: What happened after the supplier sent the wrong parts to our factory twice in the same month? B: As a consequence, our production line stopped for three days, so the manager decided to find a more reliable supplier and signed a new contract with a company in Taichung.","t":"A：供應商在同一個月內兩次送錯零件到我們工廠之後發生了什麼事？ B：【結果】我們的生產線停了三天，所以經理決定找更可靠的供應商，並和台中的一家公司簽了新合約。"},{"w":"influential","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of power to change what people think or do","c":"有影響力的","s":"A: Why is our company paying so much money to invite that business writer to speak at our annual conference next spring? B: She is very influential in the retail industry, and when she recommends a new idea in her popular blog, thousands of shop owners usually try it within a few weeks.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司要花那麼多錢邀請那位商業作家明年春天在年會上演講？ B：她在零售業非常【有影響力】，當她在熱門部落格推薦一個新點子時，通常幾週內就有數千名店主會嘗試。"},{"w":"impact","p":"n.","d":"a strong effect on something","c":"影響；衝擊","s":"A: Has the new rule about working from home on Fridays changed anything in the office since the company started it in March? B: Yes, it has had a positive impact on staff morale, because people feel less tired, and our managers say the team actually finishes more work during the week.","t":"A：公司從三月開始實施週五在家工作的新規定後，辦公室有什麼改變嗎？ B：有，它對員工士氣產生了正面的【影響】，因為大家覺得比較不累，主管們也說團隊一週內其實完成了更多工作。"},{"w":"impactful","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong effect","c":"有影響力的；效果強大的","s":"A: Which part of the presentation did the clients like most when you met them at their headquarters yesterday afternoon? B: The short video was the most impactful part, because it showed real customers using our product in their homes, and several clients said it made them want to sign the contract right away.","t":"A：你昨天下午在客戶總部和他們見面時，他們最喜歡簡報的哪個部分？ B：那段短片是最【有衝擊力的】部分，因為它呈現真實顧客在家中使用我們產品的樣子，好幾位客戶說看了就想馬上簽約。"},{"w":"relevance","p":"n.","d":"how closely something is connected to the subject","c":"相關性","s":"A: Why did you remove so many slides from my sales presentation before you sent it to the clients this morning? B: Some of them had little relevance to the clients' needs, since they talked about our history instead of the products they want, so I kept only the most useful information.","t":"A：你今天早上把我的銷售簡報寄給客戶之前，為什麼刪掉那麼多張投影片？ B：有些投影片和客戶的需求沒什麼【相關性】，因為它們講的是我們公司的歷史而不是客戶想要的產品，所以我只保留最有用的資訊。"},{"w":"relevant","p":"adj.","d":"connected to what is being discussed","c":"相關的","s":"A: What documents should I bring to the job interview at the trading company on Thursday morning? B: Bring your resume and any relevant certificates, such as your English test results and computer skills, because the manager will want to see proof of the skills listed in the job ad.","t":"A：星期四早上去貿易公司面試，我應該帶哪些文件？ B：帶你的履歷和任何【相關的】證書，例如英文檢定成績和電腦技能證明，因為經理會想看職缺廣告中所列技能的證明。"},{"w":"matter","p":"n.","d":"a subject or situation that you must deal with","c":"事情；問題","s":"A: The customer called again to complain that her refund still hasn't arrived after three weeks, so what should I tell her this time? B: Tell her we are treating it as a matter of urgency, and promise that the finance department will send the money and an email to confirm it before Friday.","t":"A：那位顧客又打電話來抱怨她的退款三週了還沒收到，這次我該怎麼跟她說？ B：告訴她我們把這當作緊急【事情】處理，並承諾財務部會在星期五前把錢匯出並寄電子郵件確認。"},{"w":"urgency","p":"n.","d":"the need to deal with something quickly","c":"緊急；急迫","s":"A: Why did the manager call an emergency meeting at seven o'clock this morning before most of us had even had breakfast? B: She wanted to explain the urgency of the situation, because our biggest customer threatened to cancel their order unless we fix the shipping problem by the end of today.","t":"A：為什麼經理今天早上七點、我們大多數人連早餐都還沒吃就召開緊急會議？ B：她想說明情況的【急迫性】，因為我們最大的客戶威脅說，除非我們今天結束前解決出貨問題，否則就要取消訂單。"},{"w":"urgent","p":"adj.","d":"needing attention immediately","c":"緊急的","s":"A: Can I talk to you about the holiday schedule now, or are you too busy with the report for the accounting department? B: Sorry, I have an urgent call from a client in Tokyo in five minutes, so could we discuss the schedule after lunch when I am less busy?","t":"A：我現在可以跟你談假期排班嗎？還是你忙著做會計部的報告？ B：抱歉，五分鐘後我有一通東京客戶打來的【緊急】電話，我們可以午餐後等我比較不忙時再討論排班嗎？"},{"w":"substantial","p":"adj.","d":"large in amount or value","c":"大量的；可觀的","s":"A: Was it worth moving our warehouse outside the city, even though some workers now have longer journeys every day? B: Yes, we have made substantial savings on rent, and we used part of that money to give the workers a transport allowance, so most of them are happy with the change.","t":"A：把倉庫搬到市區外值得嗎？即使有些工人現在每天通勤時間變長了？ B：值得，我們在租金上省下【可觀的】費用，並用其中一部分錢發給工人交通津貼，所以他們大多數都對這個改變很滿意。"},{"w":"dominant","p":"adj.","d":"more powerful or important than others","c":"佔優勢的；主導的","s":"A: Why is it so hard for small companies to sell their smartphones in this country, even when their prices are lower? B: Two big brands hold a dominant position in the market, so most stores only display their products, and customers rarely notice the cheaper phones from smaller companies.","t":"A：為什麼小公司即使價格比較低，在這個國家也很難賣出他們的智慧型手機？ B：兩個大品牌在市場上佔有【主導】地位，所以大部分店家只陳列他們的產品，顧客很少注意到小公司的便宜手機。"},{"w":"pivotal","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important, affecting how something develops","c":"關鍵的；樞紐的","s":"A: How did your team manage to win the contract with the hotel chain after losing to another company last year? B: Our new sales director played a pivotal role, because she personally met the hotel owners several times and showed them how our system could save them money.","t":"A：你們團隊去年輸給另一家公司後，今年是怎麼拿下連鎖飯店合約的？ B：我們的新業務總監扮演了【關鍵】角色，因為她親自和飯店老闆見了好幾次面，向他們說明我們的系統能如何幫他們省錢。"},{"w":"indispensable","p":"adj.","d":"too important to be without","c":"不可或缺的","s":"A: Why did the manager give Kevin such a big bonus this year when he only joined the company eighteen months ago? B: He has become indispensable to the team, since he is the only person who can fix our computer system quickly, and he also trains the new staff every month.","t":"A：Kevin 十八個月前才進公司，為什麼經理今年給他這麼大筆獎金？ B：他已經成為團隊【不可或缺的】一員，因為他是唯一能快速修好我們電腦系統的人，而且每個月還負責訓練新員工。"},{"w":"paramount","p":"adj.","d":"more important than anything else","c":"至高無上的；最重要的","s":"A: Why do the airline staff check every passenger's bags so carefully, even though it makes the lines at the airport much longer? B: Passenger safety is of paramount importance to the airline, so they would rather make people wait a little than risk allowing something dangerous on the plane.","t":"A：為什麼航空公司人員要那麼仔細地檢查每位乘客的行李，即使這讓機場排隊的隊伍變得更長？ B：乘客安全對航空公司來說是【最為】重要的，所以他們寧願讓大家稍等，也不願冒險讓危險物品上飛機。"}]},{"unit":188,"theme":"Influence 影響","cards":[{"w":"influential","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong effect on people's ideas or decisions","c":"有影響力的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team invite that young blogger to our product launch next Friday instead of a famous actor? B: She is very influential among college students, and her honest reviews often help small companies sell thousands of items within a few days.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊邀請那位年輕部落客來參加我們下週五的產品發表會，而不是找知名演員？ B：她在大學生之間非常【有影響力】，她誠實的評論常常幫助小公司在幾天內賣出數千件商品。"},{"w":"impact","p":"n.","d":"a strong effect that something has on a situation or person","c":"影響；衝擊","s":"A: Have you seen the sales report for the last quarter, and do you know why our numbers in Asia went up so quickly? B: Yes, the new online advertising campaign had a huge impact on sales, especially in Taiwan and Japan, where young customers spend a lot of time on their phones.","t":"A：你看過上一季的銷售報告了嗎？你知道為什麼我們在亞洲的業績成長得這麼快嗎？ B：看過了，新的線上廣告活動對銷售產生了巨大的【影響】，尤其是在台灣和日本，那裡的年輕顧客花很多時間在手機上。"},{"w":"effect","p":"n.","d":"a change or result caused by something","c":"效果；作用；影響","s":"A: The doctor in our company clinic gave me some new medicine for my cold, but should I still drive to the meeting with our clients this afternoon? B: I would take a taxi instead, because one side effect of that medicine is that it can make you feel very sleepy for several hours.","t":"A：公司診所的醫生給了我一些治感冒的新藥，但我今天下午還應該開車去和客戶開會嗎？ B：我會改搭計程車，因為那種藥的一個副【作用】是可能讓你昏昏欲睡好幾個小時。"},{"w":"affect","p":"v.","d":"to cause a change in someone or something","c":"影響","s":"A: Will the heavy snow in the northern region delay the shipment of office chairs that we ordered for the new branch last week? B: Unfortunately, the storm will affect several delivery routes, so the supplier says our order may arrive three or four days later than planned.","t":"A：北部地區的大雪會延誤我們上週為新分公司訂購的辦公椅出貨嗎？ B：很遺憾，這場暴風雪會【影響】好幾條送貨路線，所以供應商說我們的訂單可能會比預定晚三、四天到。"},{"w":"authority","p":"n.","d":"the power or right to make decisions or give orders","c":"權力；權限；職權","s":"A: Can the store manager give this customer a full refund for the broken laptop, even though she lost her receipt last month? B: No, only the regional director has the authority to approve refunds without a receipt, so I will email him and ask him to call the customer today.","t":"A：店經理可以為這位顧客的壞掉筆電全額退款嗎？即使她上個月把收據弄丟了。 B：不行，只有區域總監有【權限】核准沒有收據的退款，所以我會寄電子郵件給他，請他今天打電話給這位顧客。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something by giving good reasons","c":"說服；勸說","s":"A: Our biggest client wants to cancel the contract because our prices went up this year, so what should we do before Friday? B: Let's invite their purchasing manager to lunch and try to persuade her to stay by offering free delivery and a small discount on large orders.","t":"A：我們最大的客戶因為今年價格上漲想要取消合約，我們在星期五之前該怎麼做？ B：我們邀請他們的採購經理吃午餐，試著提供免費送貨和大量訂單的小折扣來【說服】她留下來。"},{"w":"persuasion","p":"n.","d":"the act of making someone agree with you or do something","c":"說服；勸說","s":"A: How did the young sales assistant manage to sell so many expensive coffee machines at the trade show last weekend? B: She is very good at gentle persuasion; she lets customers taste the coffee first, listens to their needs, and then explains clearly how the machine can save them money.","t":"A：那位年輕的銷售助理上週末在商展上是怎麼賣出這麼多台昂貴咖啡機的？ B：她非常擅長溫和的【說服】；她先讓顧客試喝咖啡，聆聽他們的需求，再清楚說明這台機器如何幫他們省錢。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe that something is true","c":"使相信；說服","s":"A: The finance director still thinks that moving our customer service team to a bigger office is too expensive, doesn't he? B: Yes, so we need clear numbers and a simple chart to convince him that the move will actually reduce costs and improve teamwork within two years.","t":"A：財務總監仍然認為把客服團隊搬到更大的辦公室太昂貴了，對吧？ B：對，所以我們需要清楚的數字和簡單的圖表來【說服】他，這次搬遷在兩年內其實會降低成本並改善團隊合作。"},{"w":"pressure","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry caused by too much work or responsibility","c":"壓力","s":"A: You look really tired today; are you still working late every night on the new hotel booking app? B: Yes, the client wants it finished before the holiday season, so the whole team is under a lot of pressure, and nobody has taken a day off for three weeks.","t":"A：你今天看起來真的很累，你還在每晚加班做新的飯店訂房應用程式嗎？ B：是啊，客戶希望在假期旺季前完成，所以整個團隊都承受很大的【壓力】，三個禮拜以來沒有人休過一天假。"},{"w":"manipulate","p":"v.","d":"to control or change something in a dishonest way","c":"操縱；竄改","s":"A: Why did the board of directors decide to fire the chief accountant after the annual audit last month? B: The auditors discovered that he had tried to manipulate the sales figures to make the company look more successful, which is a serious crime and broke the trust of investors.","t":"A：為什麼董事會在上個月年度稽核後決定開除會計長？ B：稽核人員發現他試圖【操縱】銷售數字，讓公司看起來更成功，這是嚴重的犯罪行為，也破壞了投資人的信任。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about how to do something","c":"指導；輔導","s":"A: I've just joined the accounting department, and I'm worried about making mistakes with the new tax software next week. B: Don't worry too much, because Mr. Chen will give you step-by-step guidance during your first month, and you can always ask him questions when you feel confused.","t":"A：我剛加入會計部，我擔心下週用新的報稅軟體時會出錯。 B：別太擔心，陳先生在你第一個月會給你一步一步的【指導】，你感到困惑時隨時可以問他問題。"},{"w":"role model","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose behavior others copy because they admire it","c":"榜樣；模範","s":"A: Why does everyone in the sales department want to work on Ms. Lin's team when the new projects start next month? B: She is a great role model for younger employees, because she stays calm with angry clients, keeps every promise, and always shares her ideas with the team.","t":"A：為什麼下個月新專案開始時，業務部的每個人都想加入林小姐的團隊？ B：她是年輕員工的絕佳【榜樣】，因為她面對生氣的客戶時保持冷靜，信守每個承諾，而且總是與團隊分享她的想法。"},{"w":"trend","p":"n.","d":"a general change in the way people behave or what they like","c":"趨勢；潮流","s":"A: Should our café keep selling the same sandwiches, or should we change the menu before the summer tourists arrive? B: I think we should follow the healthy eating trend and add some salads and plant-based meals, because many young customers have asked for lighter food recently.","t":"A：我們的咖啡館應該繼續賣同樣的三明治，還是在夏季觀光客到來之前更換菜單？ B：我認為我們應該跟上健康飲食的【趨勢】，增加一些沙拉和植物性餐點，因為最近很多年輕顧客要求較清淡的食物。"},{"w":"shaping","p":"n.","d":"the act of forming or influencing how something develops","c":"形塑；塑造","s":"A: How important was the new chief executive in the company's success over the last five years, in your opinion? B: She played a key role in the shaping of our business strategy, especially when she decided to focus on online sales and open small offices in Southeast Asia.","t":"A：依你看，新任執行長在公司過去五年的成功中有多重要？ B：她在【形塑】我們的經營策略上扮演了關鍵角色，尤其是她決定專注於線上銷售並在東南亞開設小型辦事處的時候。"},{"w":"sway","p":"v.","d":"to influence someone so that they change their opinion or choice","c":"左右；影響","s":"A: Do you think the famous chef's positive review in the newspaper will help our new restaurant attract more customers this month? B: Definitely, because reviews from respected experts can sway people's choices, and many diners read the food section before they decide where to eat on weekends.","t":"A：你認為那位知名主廚在報紙上的正面評論會幫我們的新餐廳這個月吸引更多顧客嗎？ B：當然，因為受尊敬專家的評論能【左右】人們的選擇，很多用餐者在決定週末去哪裡吃飯之前都會閱讀美食版。"},{"w":"leverage","p":"v.","d":"to use something you have in order to get the best result","c":"善加利用；發揮","s":"A: We are a small company with a limited budget, so how can we compete with the big electronics stores in the city? B: We should leverage our excellent customer reviews and friendly service, sharing them on social media to attract shoppers who care more about trust than low prices.","t":"A：我們是預算有限的小公司，要怎麼和市區的大型電器行競爭？ B：我們應該【善加利用】我們優秀的顧客評價和親切的服務，把它們分享到社群媒體上，吸引那些比起低價更重視信任的購物者。"},{"w":"dominate","p":"v.","d":"to have the most power or the biggest share of something","c":"主導；支配","s":"A: Why is it so hard for new companies to sell smartphones in this country, even when their phones are cheaper? B: Two large brands dominate the market, and most customers trust them because they have offered good repair services and reliable products for more than ten years.","t":"A：為什麼新公司在這個國家很難賣智慧型手機，即使他們的手機比較便宜？ B：兩個大品牌【主導】了市場，而且大部分顧客信任它們，因為它們十多年來一直提供良好的維修服務和可靠的產品。"},{"w":"dominant","p":"adj.","d":"more powerful, important or common than others","c":"主導的；佔優勢的","s":"A: Which delivery company should we choose for our online shop, since we expect many more orders during the holiday season? B: Let's use FastShip, because it is the dominant company in this area, with the most trucks, the longest opening hours, and very few complaints from customers.","t":"A：既然我們預期假期旺季會有更多訂單，我們的網路商店應該選哪家物流公司？ B：我們用FastShip吧，因為它是這個地區【居主導地位的】公司，擁有最多卡車、最長的營業時間，而且顧客抱怨很少。"},{"w":"control","p":"n.","d":"the power to make something happen the way you want","c":"控制；掌控","s":"A: Why did the factory stop the production line for two hours yesterday afternoon, and did we lose many orders? B: A machine was overheating, so the engineers had to take control of the situation quickly, check every part carefully, and make sure no workers were in danger before restarting.","t":"A：為什麼工廠昨天下午停了生產線兩個小時？我們有損失很多訂單嗎？ B：有一台機器過熱，所以工程師必須迅速【控制】局面，仔細檢查每個零件，並在重新啟動前確保沒有工人處於危險中。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"something that gives you new ideas or makes you want to create","c":"靈感；鼓舞","s":"A: Where did the design team get the idea for the new hotel lobby, with all those plants and wooden furniture? B: They found inspiration during a business trip to Japan, where they visited several traditional gardens and noticed how calm and relaxed the guests seemed in natural spaces.","t":"A：設計團隊是從哪裡得到新飯店大廳的構想，那些植物和木製家具？ B：他們在日本出差時找到了【靈感】，當時他們參觀了幾座傳統庭園，並注意到客人在自然空間中顯得多麼平靜放鬆。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the wish or confidence to do something","c":"激勵；啟發","s":"A: Why did the company invite a famous mountain climber to speak at our annual staff meeting next Thursday? B: The managers hope her story will inspire employees to set bigger goals, work together as a team, and keep trying even when a project becomes difficult.","t":"A：為什麼公司邀請一位知名登山家在下週四的年度員工大會上演講？ B：主管們希望她的故事能【激勵】員工設定更遠大的目標、團隊合作，並且在專案變得困難時也持續努力。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to work hard or do something","c":"激勵；促使","s":"A: Our sales team has seemed tired and unhappy since the busy season ended, so what can we do to help them? B: We could motivate them with a small bonus for every new client, and maybe organize a team dinner at the end of each month to celebrate good results.","t":"A：旺季結束後，我們的業務團隊似乎又累又不開心，我們可以做些什麼來幫助他們？ B：我們可以用每簽一位新客戶就發一小筆獎金來【激勵】他們，也許每個月底再辦一次團隊聚餐慶祝好成績。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the wish or energy to do something well","c":"動力；動機","s":"A: Why did so many of our young engineers quit last year, even though their salaries were quite good? B: According to the survey, they lost motivation because they did the same boring tasks every day and had no chance to learn new skills or get promoted.","t":"A：為什麼去年我們有這麼多年輕工程師離職，即使他們的薪水相當不錯？ B：根據調查，他們失去了【動力】，因為他們每天做同樣無聊的工作，而且沒有機會學習新技能或升遷。"},{"w":"stimulate","p":"v.","d":"to make something become more active or grow","c":"刺激；促進","s":"A: The city government is planning to build a new train station near the old harbor, isn't it? B: Yes, officials believe the station will stimulate the local economy by bringing more tourists, new shops, and hundreds of jobs to an area that has been quiet for years.","t":"A：市政府正計畫在舊港口附近興建一座新火車站，對吧？ B：對，官員們相信這座車站將帶來更多觀光客、新商店和數百個工作機會，【刺激】這個沉寂多年地區的地方經濟。"},{"w":"stimulus","p":"n.","d":"something that helps a process or activity to develop faster","c":"刺激；促進因素","s":"A: Why are so many families buying new refrigerators and washing machines at the electronics store this month? B: The government gave every household a small cash payment as an economic stimulus, and many people are using the money to replace old appliances before prices go up.","t":"A：為什麼這個月有這麼多家庭在電器行買新冰箱和洗衣機？ B：政府發給每戶一小筆現金作為經濟【刺激】方案，很多人正利用這筆錢在漲價前汰換舊家電。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone support or reasons to do something","c":"鼓勵；促進","s":"A: Our office uses so much paper every week, so is there anything simple we can do to reduce waste? B: We could encourage staff to read documents on their screens, put recycling boxes next to every printer, and print only when it is really necessary for meetings.","t":"A：我們辦公室每週用很多紙，有什麼簡單的方法可以減少浪費嗎？ B：我們可以【鼓勵】員工在螢幕上閱讀文件，在每台印表機旁放回收箱，並且只在開會真正需要時才列印。"},{"w":"discourage","p":"v.","d":"to try to stop someone from doing something","c":"勸阻；使打消念頭","s":"A: Why did the shopping mall raise its parking fees so much for cars that stay longer than three hours? B: The managers want to discourage office workers from parking there all day, because shoppers often complain that they cannot find empty spaces on busy weekday afternoons.","t":"A：為什麼購物中心對停超過三小時的車大幅調高停車費？ B：管理階層想要【阻止】上班族整天停在那裡，因為購物者常常抱怨在忙碌的平日下午找不到空車位。"},{"w":"peer","p":"n.","d":"a person of the same age, level or job as you","c":"同儕；同事","s":"A: How do you usually check the quality of the reports before they are sent to our clients in Singapore? B: Each report is first reviewed by a peer in the same department, who checks the numbers and grammar, and then the team leader reads it one more time before it goes out.","t":"A：在報告寄給新加坡客戶之前，你們通常怎麼檢查品質？ B：每份報告先由同部門的一位【同儕】審閱，他會檢查數字和文法，然後組長再讀一遍才寄出。"},{"w":"socialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend time with other people in a friendly way","c":"交際；社交往來","s":"A: Are you coming to the welcome party for the new employees in the hotel garden after work on Friday? B: Yes, I think it's important to socialize with people from other departments, because we often need their help, and it's easier to work together when you know each other.","t":"A：你星期五下班後會來飯店花園參加新員工歡迎派對嗎？ B：會啊，我認為和其他部門的人【交際往來】很重要，因為我們常常需要他們幫忙，而彼此認識後合作起來比較容易。"},{"w":"reinforce","p":"v.","d":"to make an idea, feeling or rule stronger","c":"強化；加強","s":"A: The new safety rules for the warehouse were introduced last month, but some workers still forget to wear their helmets. B: Let's reinforce the message by putting large posters near every entrance and reminding everyone at the short meeting before each morning shift starts.","t":"A：倉庫的新安全規定上個月就實施了，但有些工人還是忘了戴安全帽。 B：我們在每個入口附近張貼大海報，並在每天早班開始前的簡短會議上提醒大家，來【強化】這個訊息吧。"},{"w":"exposure","p":"n.","d":"the chance to be seen or noticed by the public","c":"曝光；接觸","s":"A: Why does our small furniture company want to pay for a booth at the international design fair in Taipei next spring? B: The fair will give us great exposure to thousands of buyers and journalists from many countries, which we could never reach with our small advertising budget alone.","t":"A：為什麼我們這家小家具公司想花錢在明年春天台北的國際設計展租攤位？ B：展覽會讓我們在來自許多國家的數千位買家和記者面前獲得極佳的【曝光】，這是光靠我們少量廣告預算永遠接觸不到的。"},{"w":"impression","p":"n.","d":"the opinion or feeling you get about someone or something","c":"印象","s":"A: I have a job interview at a large bank tomorrow morning, and I'm really nervous about what to wear and say. B: Arrive ten minutes early, wear a simple dark suit, and smile when you shake hands, because making a good first impression is very important in banking.","t":"A：我明天早上在一家大銀行有工作面試，我真的很緊張不知道該穿什麼、說什麼。 B：提早十分鐘到，穿簡單的深色西裝，握手時微笑，因為在銀行業留下良好的第一【印象】非常重要。"}]},{"unit":189,"theme":"Information 資訊","cards":[{"w":"data","p":"n.","d":"facts or numbers collected for study or use","c":"資料；數據","s":"A: Why did the marketing team cancel this afternoon's meeting with the new clients from Osaka? B: The research company sent us the wrong customer data last night, so we need two more days to check the sales numbers carefully before we can present our plan to them.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊取消了今天下午和大阪新客戶的會議？ B：研究公司昨晚寄給我們錯誤的客戶【資料】，所以我們需要再兩天仔細核對銷售數字，才能向他們提出我們的計畫。"},{"w":"detail","p":"n.","d":"a small fact or piece of information","c":"細節","s":"A: The hotel manager called again about the company dinner next Friday, but I'm not sure what she needs from us now. B: She wants to know every detail of the menu, including how many guests don't eat meat, so please send her the final list before lunch today.","t":"A：飯店經理又打電話來問下週五公司晚宴的事，但我不確定她現在需要我們提供什麼。 B：她想知道菜單的每一個【細節】，包括有多少位賓客不吃肉，所以請在今天午餐前把最終名單寄給她。"},{"w":"fact","p":"n.","d":"something that is known to be true","c":"事實","s":"A: Our boss said the new delivery service is cheaper, but are you sure that it will really save the company money this year? B: Yes, it's a fact that their prices are twenty percent lower than our current supplier, and I compared both contracts line by line this morning.","t":"A：老闆說新的快遞服務比較便宜，但你確定今年真的能幫公司省錢嗎？ B：是的，他們的價格比我們現在的供應商低百分之二十，這是【事實】，而且我今天早上已經逐行比較過兩份合約了。"},{"w":"knowledge","p":"n.","d":"information and understanding that you get from learning or experience","c":"知識；了解","s":"A: Do you think Linda is the right person to train the new staff members at our Taichung branch next month? B: Definitely, because she has worked in customer service for ten years, and her knowledge of our products is better than anyone else's in the whole department.","t":"A：你認為琳達適合下個月在我們台中分公司訓練新進員工嗎？ B：當然，因為她在客服部門工作了十年，而且她對我們產品的【了解】比整個部門任何人都好。"},{"w":"evidence","p":"n.","d":"facts or things that show something is true","c":"證據","s":"A: The customer says the package arrived broken, but our warehouse team insists it was packed carefully. What should we do? B: Let's ask her to send photos as evidence of the damage, and then we can decide whether to give her a refund or a replacement.","t":"A：顧客說包裹送到時是壞的，但我們的倉庫團隊堅持包裝得很仔細。我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們請她寄照片作為損壞的【證據】，然後再決定要給她退款還是換貨。"},{"w":"report","p":"n.","d":"a written or spoken description of a situation or results","c":"報告","s":"A: Have you finished checking the sales numbers for the third quarter that the director asked about yesterday? B: Almost, I just need to add two charts and a short conclusion, and then I'll send the complete report to her before the board meeting starts at three.","t":"A：主任昨天問的第三季銷售數字，你核對完了嗎？ B：快好了，我只需要再加兩張圖表和簡短的結論，然後會在三點董事會開始前把完整的【報告】寄給她。"},{"w":"record","p":"n.","d":"written information about past events, kept so it can be checked later","c":"紀錄","s":"A: A customer called to complain that she paid her bill twice last month, but she can't find her receipt. B: Don't worry, our accounting system keeps a record of every payment, so I'll look up her account number and check the dates right away.","t":"A：一位顧客打電話來抱怨她上個月付了兩次帳單，但她找不到收據。 B：別擔心，我們的會計系統保存了每一筆付款的【紀錄】，所以我馬上查她的帳號並核對日期。"},{"w":"file","p":"n.","d":"a set of information stored on a computer under one name","c":"檔案","s":"A: I can't open the presentation you emailed me this morning, and the client meeting starts in less than an hour. B: Sorry about that, the file was probably too large for the email system, so I'll save it to our shared drive and send you the link now.","t":"A：我打不開你今天早上寄給我的簡報，而客戶會議不到一個小時就要開始了。 B：抱歉，那個【檔案】可能太大，電子郵件系統無法處理，所以我現在把它存到共用雲端硬碟，再把連結傳給你。"},{"w":"document","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that gives information or proof","c":"文件","s":"A: What do I need to bring to the bank tomorrow when I open the new business account for our company? B: You should bring your passport, the company registration certificate, and any other official document that shows you are allowed to sign for the business.","t":"A：明天我去銀行為公司開新的企業帳戶時，需要帶什麼？ B：你應該帶護照、公司登記證，以及任何其他能證明你有權代表公司簽名的正式【文件】。"},{"w":"source","p":"n.","d":"a person, book or place that gives you information","c":"來源；消息來源","s":"A: Where did you find the information about our competitor's new product, which you mentioned in this morning's sales meeting? B: A source inside the industry told me about it at last week's trade fair, but we should still wait for an official announcement before we change our plans.","t":"A：你在今天早上業務會議中提到的競爭對手新產品資訊，是從哪裡得知的？ B：一位業界的【消息來源】在上週的貿易展告訴我的，但在改變計畫之前，我們還是應該等正式公告。"},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking at something for information","c":"參考","s":"A: The new sales assistants keep asking me the same questions about prices and discounts every single day. B: Why don't we make a short printed guide for their reference, so they can check the prices quickly by themselves when customers ask questions at the counter?","t":"A：新來的銷售助理每天都一直問我同樣關於價格和折扣的問題。 B：我們何不做一本簡短的印刷手冊供他們【參考】，這樣顧客在櫃檯發問時，他們就能自己快速查價格？"},{"w":"statistics","p":"n.","d":"numbers that show facts about a large group","c":"統計數字","s":"A: How do we know that more young people are shopping at our stores this year than they did last year? B: The latest statistics from our membership program show that customers under thirty now make up forty percent of all sales, compared with only twenty-five percent before.","t":"A：我們怎麼知道今年來我們店購物的年輕人比去年多？ B：會員計畫最新的【統計數字】顯示，三十歲以下的顧客現在占所有銷售額的百分之四十，而以前只有百分之二十五。"},{"w":"figure","p":"n.","d":"a number, especially an official one","c":"數字；數據","s":"A: Did the finance team finally send the numbers for last month's online sales to the manager? B: Yes, and the final figure was much higher than we expected, so the manager wants to give everyone in the online team a small bonus at the end of the year.","t":"A：財務團隊終於把上個月的線上銷售數字寄給經理了嗎？ B：寄了，而且最終【數字】比我們預期的高很多，所以經理想在年底給線上團隊每個人一筆小獎金。"},{"w":"content","p":"n.","d":"the information, words, pictures or videos in something such as a website","c":"內容","s":"A: Our company website gets lots of visitors, but very few of them stay for more than a minute. Why? B: I think the content is too boring and old, so we should add short videos, customer stories, and useful tips that people actually want to read.","t":"A：我們公司的網站有很多訪客，但很少人停留超過一分鐘。為什麼？ B：我覺得【內容】太無聊又太舊了，所以我們應該加入短片、顧客故事以及大家真正想看的實用小技巧。"},{"w":"message","p":"n.","d":"a piece of written or spoken information that you send or leave for someone","c":"訊息；留言","s":"A: Mr. Chen from the shipping company called while you were at lunch, and he sounded quite worried about something. B: Thanks for telling me. Did he leave a message for me, or should I call him back as soon as I finish checking these delivery orders?","t":"A：你去吃午餐時，貨運公司的陳先生打電話來，他聽起來對某件事很擔心。 B：謝謝你告訴我。他有給我【留言】嗎？還是我檢查完這些送貨單後就馬上回電給他？"},{"w":"signal","p":"n.","d":"radio waves that carry sound or pictures to a phone or TV","c":"訊號","s":"A: Why do you keep walking to the window every time you talk on the phone with our clients? B: The mobile phone signal in this meeting room is really weak, so the calls often drop, and I have to stand near the window to hear people clearly.","t":"A：為什麼你每次和客戶講電話時都一直走到窗邊？ B：這間會議室的手機【訊號】真的很弱，所以電話常常斷線，我必須站在窗邊才能聽清楚對方說話。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"opinions about how good or bad something is","c":"意見回饋","s":"A: How did the customers like the new menu that our restaurant started serving last weekend? B: We got a lot of positive feedback on our website, but several people said the portions were too small, so the chef is planning to make a few changes.","t":"A：顧客喜歡我們餐廳上週末開始供應的新菜單嗎？ B：我們在網站上收到很多正面的【意見回饋】，但有幾個人說份量太少，所以主廚打算做一些調整。"},{"w":"update","p":"n.","d":"the newest information about something","c":"最新消息；最新進度","s":"A: The shipment of laptops for our new office was supposed to arrive this morning, but nothing has come yet. B: I called the delivery company an hour ago, and they promised to send us an update on the truck's location by email before the end of the day.","t":"A：要送到新辦公室的那批筆電原本今天早上應該到，但到現在什麼都沒來。 B：我一個小時前打電話給貨運公司，他們答應今天下班前會用電子郵件寄給我們卡車位置的【最新消息】。"},{"w":"briefing","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where people are given information or instructions","c":"簡報會；簡要說明","s":"A: What time do the sales staff need to arrive at the convention center on the first morning of the trade show? B: Please tell them to come by eight, because there is a short briefing with the manager about prices, sample products, and important customers before the doors open at nine.","t":"A：展覽第一天早上，業務人員需要幾點到會議中心？ B：請告訴他們八點前到，因為九點開門前，經理會舉行一場關於價格、樣品和重要客戶的簡短【簡報會】。"},{"w":"announcement","p":"n.","d":"an official public statement about something","c":"公告；宣布","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office talking about the company's plans for next year this morning? B: The president made an announcement at the staff meeting that we will open two new branches in Japan, and some of us may get a chance to work overseas.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上辦公室裡每個人都在談論公司明年的計畫？ B：總裁在員工大會上【宣布】我們將在日本開兩家新分公司，而且我們之中有些人可能有機會到海外工作。"},{"w":"instruction","p":"n.","d":"information that tells you how to do something","c":"指示；說明","s":"A: I tried to set up the new printer in the meeting room by myself, but it still won't connect to my computer. B: Did you follow every instruction in the user's guide carefully, especially the part about installing the software before you plug in the cable?","t":"A：我試著自己安裝會議室的新印表機，但它還是連不上我的電腦。 B：你有仔細遵照使用手冊裡的每一項【說明】嗎？特別是插上電線之前要先安裝軟體的那部分？"},{"w":"guideline","p":"n.","d":"a rule or piece of advice about how to do something","c":"準則；指導原則","s":"A: Can I post photos from our office party on my personal social media account this weekend? B: You should check the company's new guideline about social media first, because it says employees must ask their coworkers before sharing any pictures that show their faces online.","t":"A：我這個週末可以把辦公室派對的照片貼到我的個人社群帳號嗎？ B：你應該先看看公司新的社群媒體【準則】，因為上面說員工在網路上分享任何拍到同事臉的照片之前，必須先徵求他們同意。"},{"w":"description","p":"n.","d":"words that tell what something or someone is like","c":"描述；說明","s":"A: Why are so many customers returning the blue jackets that we started selling on our website last month? B: The product description said they were waterproof, but they actually aren't, so we need to change the wording and offer refunds to the unhappy buyers.","t":"A：為什麼有那麼多顧客退回我們上個月開始在網站上販售的藍色夾克？ B：商品【說明】寫著它們是防水的，但實際上並不是，所以我們需要修改文字，並退款給不滿意的買家。"},{"w":"summary","p":"n.","d":"a short statement of the main points","c":"摘要","s":"A: I missed the planning meeting yesterday because my flight from Singapore was delayed for five hours. B: No problem, I wrote a short summary of the main points and decisions, so I'll email it to you now, and you can call me if you have any questions.","t":"A：我錯過了昨天的企劃會議，因為我從新加坡出發的班機延誤了五個小時。 B：沒問題，我寫了一份重點和決議的簡短【摘要】，現在就用電子郵件寄給你，有任何問題可以打電話給我。"},{"w":"overview","p":"n.","d":"a short general description of something","c":"概要；概述","s":"A: What will happen on the first day of the training program for the new employees next Monday morning? B: The HR manager will give a general overview of the company's history, departments, and main products before the new staff members meet their team leaders after lunch.","t":"A：下週一早上新進員工訓練課程的第一天會進行什麼？ B：人資經理會先介紹公司歷史、各部門和主要產品的整體【概要】，午餐後新進員工再去和他們的組長見面。"},{"w":"clarify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to understand","c":"澄清；說明清楚","s":"A: Some of our customers seem confused about the new return rules that we put on the website last week. B: Then let's send them an email to clarify the main points, especially how many days they have to return items and whether they need the original receipt.","t":"A：我們有些顧客似乎對上週放在網站上的新退貨規定感到困惑。 B：那我們寄封電子郵件給他們，【說明清楚】重點，特別是他們有幾天可以退貨，以及是否需要原始收據。"},{"w":"inform","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone about something officially","c":"通知；告知","s":"A: The training session for the new accounting software has been moved from Tuesday to Thursday afternoon. B: Okay, I'll inform everyone in the finance department by email right away, so nobody comes to the meeting room on the wrong day and wastes their time.","t":"A：新會計軟體的訓練課程已經從星期二改到星期四下午了。 B：好，我馬上用電子郵件【通知】財務部的每個人，這樣就不會有人在錯的日子到會議室浪費時間。"},{"w":"notify","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone about something, usually in a formal way","c":"通知","s":"A: What should I do if a hotel guest leaves a bag or a phone in their room after checking out? B: First, put the item in the lost-and-found box at the front desk, and then notify the guest by phone or email so they can decide how to get it back.","t":"A：如果飯店房客退房後把包包或手機留在房間裡，我該怎麼做？ B：首先，把物品放進櫃檯的失物招領箱，然後用電話或電子郵件【通知】房客，讓他們決定要怎麼取回。"},{"w":"reveal","p":"v.","d":"to show or tell something that was secret or unknown","c":"揭露；公布","s":"A: When will the company tell the public about the new smartphone that the design team has been working on all year? B: The CEO plans to reveal the new model at a big press event in Taipei next month, so we must keep everything secret until then.","t":"A：公司什麼時候會向大眾公開設計團隊忙了一整年的新智慧型手機？ B：執行長計畫下個月在台北的大型記者會上【公布】新機型，所以在那之前我們必須把一切保密。"},{"w":"disclose","p":"v.","d":"to make information known to the public, especially information that was private","c":"公開；透露","s":"A: A reporter called and asked how much money we paid for the new factory in Vietnam last spring. B: Please tell her politely that we cannot disclose the price, because the contract says both companies must keep the details private for at least two years.","t":"A：一位記者打電話來，問我們去年春天在越南買新工廠付了多少錢。 B：請禮貌地告訴她，我們不能【透露】價格，因為合約規定兩家公司必須對細節保密至少兩年。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share ideas, information or feelings with other people","c":"溝通","s":"A: Our team members work in three different countries, so it's really hard to share ideas and solve problems quickly. B: Maybe we should use a group chat app, so everyone can communicate more easily, and we can also hold a short video meeting every Monday morning.","t":"A：我們的團隊成員在三個不同的國家工作，所以要快速分享想法和解決問題真的很困難。 B：也許我們應該使用群組聊天應用程式，讓每個人能更方便地【溝通】，我們也可以每週一早上開個簡短的視訊會議。"},{"w":"informative","p":"adj.","d":"giving a lot of useful information","c":"資訊豐富的；有益的","s":"A: Was the seminar about online marketing worth the money that the company paid for our tickets last Saturday? B: Yes, it was very informative, because the speakers shared many useful tips about social media advertising that we can use for our new product launch next month.","t":"A：上週六那場網路行銷研討會值得公司幫我們付的票錢嗎？ B：值得，內容非常【豐富有益】，因為講者分享了許多社群媒體廣告的實用技巧，我們下個月的新產品發表就能用上。"},{"w":"accurate","p":"adj.","d":"correct and without mistakes","c":"準確的","s":"A: Why does the manager want us to count all the products in the warehouse again this weekend? B: The numbers in our computer system aren't accurate, because some boxes were sent to the wrong store last month, and we need correct numbers before we order more goods.","t":"A：為什麼經理要我們這個週末再把倉庫裡所有的產品清點一次？ B：我們電腦系統裡的數字不【準確】，因為上個月有些箱子被送錯分店，我們在訂購更多貨品之前需要正確的數字。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted to do something well","c":"可靠的","s":"A: We need a new company to deliver our products to stores in southern Taiwan. Do you have any suggestions? B: I recommend Fast Line Logistics, because they are very reliable, their trucks always arrive on time, and their prices are reasonable for small businesses like ours.","t":"A：我們需要一家新公司把產品送到南台灣的門市。你有什麼建議嗎？ B：我推薦快線物流，因為他們非常【可靠】，卡車總是準時抵達，而且價格對我們這種小公司來說很合理。"},{"w":"confidential","p":"adj.","d":"meant to be kept secret","c":"機密的","s":"A: Can I take these salary documents home tonight, so I can finish checking them before tomorrow's meeting? B: I'm afraid not, because that information is strictly confidential, and company rules say it must stay in the office and be locked in the cabinet every evening.","t":"A：我今晚可以把這些薪資文件帶回家，好在明天會議前檢查完嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為那些資訊是嚴格【機密】，公司規定它們必須留在辦公室，而且每天晚上要鎖在櫃子裡。"}]},{"unit":190,"theme":"Insect 昆蟲","cards":[{"w":"adore","p":"v.","d":"to love or like something very much","c":"非常喜愛；熱愛","s":"A: I heard you are organizing the children's science day at the city museum next month, so which activity do you think the young visitors will enjoy most? B: Kids absolutely adore the butterfly garden, so we will give every family a free guided tour there and finish with a short drawing class.","t":"A：我聽說你正在籌劃下個月在市立博物館舉辦的兒童科學日，你認為年輕的參觀者最喜歡哪個活動？ B：孩子們非常【喜愛】蝴蝶花園，所以我們會為每個家庭提供免費的導覽，最後再上一堂簡短的繪畫課。"},{"w":"hair-raising","p":"adj.","d":"very frightening but often exciting","c":"令人毛骨悚然的；驚險的","s":"A: How was the business trip to the research station in the mountains last week, and did your team manage to collect all the samples on time? B: The drive along the narrow cliff road was truly hair-raising because of the heavy rain, but we arrived safely and finished the work a day early.","t":"A：上週去山上研究站的出差怎麼樣？你們團隊有準時採集完所有樣本嗎？ B：因為下大雨，沿著狹窄懸崖道路開車真的很【驚險】，但我們平安抵達，還提早一天完成了工作。"},{"w":"living organism","p":"n.phr.","d":"a living thing, such as a plant, animal or bacterium","c":"生物；有機體","s":"A: Why does the new laboratory manager keep reminding everyone to wear gloves and close the containers when we handle the soil samples from the farm? B: Even a small spoonful of that soil can hide a tiny living organism such as a bacterium or an insect egg, so we must protect both ourselves and the accuracy of our test results.","t":"A：為什麼新的實驗室主管一直提醒大家，在處理農場的土壤樣本時要戴手套並蓋好容器？ B：就算只是一小匙土壤，也可能藏著細菌或昆蟲卵之類的微小【生物】，所以我們必須保護自己，也要確保檢測結果的準確性。"},{"w":"pollinate","p":"v.","d":"to move pollen to a flower so it can make seeds or fruit","c":"給（植物）授粉","s":"A: Why did the fruit company decide to rent dozens of beehives from a local farmer before the apple trees started to bloom this spring? B: Without enough bees to pollinate the flowers, the trees would give us far fewer apples, and we would lose a large part of our yearly income.","t":"A：為什麼這家水果公司決定在今年春天蘋果樹開花前，向當地農夫租用幾十個蜂箱？ B：如果沒有足夠的蜜蜂為花朵【授粉】，果樹結的蘋果會少很多，我們就會損失很大一部分的年收入。"},{"w":"produce","p":"v.","d":"to make or grow something","c":"生產；製造","s":"A: Our marketing team wants to sell local honey in the hotel gift shop, but do you know how much honey one beehive can actually make in a year? B: A healthy hive can produce around twenty kilograms of honey each season, so a small farm nearby could easily supply our shop every month.","t":"A：我們的行銷團隊想在飯店禮品店販售當地蜂蜜，但你知道一個蜂箱一年實際能產出多少蜂蜜嗎？ B：一個健康的蜂巢每季可以【生產】大約二十公斤的蜂蜜，所以附近的小農場就能輕鬆地每個月供貨給我們的店。"},{"w":"loathe","p":"v.","d":"to hate something very much","c":"極度厭惡；痛恨","s":"A: Why does the new receptionist always ask someone else to open the windows in the waiting room during the summer, even when it is really hot? B: She told me she really does loathe mosquitoes and flies, and she is afraid they will fly inside and bother the guests while they are waiting.","t":"A：為什麼新來的接待員夏天總是請別人去開候客室的窗戶，即使天氣真的很熱？ B：她告訴我她非常【痛恨】蚊子和蒼蠅，怕牠們飛進來打擾正在等候的客人。"},{"w":"no-brainer","p":"n.","d":"a decision that is very easy to make","c":"不用多想的事；顯而易見的決定","s":"A: The supplier offered us a free upgrade to the better pest control service if we sign a two-year contract, so should we discuss it with the board first? B: Honestly, it is a no-brainer because the price stays the same and the restaurant passed every health inspection after using their service last year.","t":"A：供應商說如果我們簽兩年合約，就免費升級成更好的除蟲服務，我們要先和董事會討論嗎？ B：說真的，這根本是【不用多想的決定】，因為價格不變，而且餐廳去年使用他們的服務後通過了每一次衛生檢查。"},{"w":"frightened","p":"adj.","d":"feeling afraid","c":"受驚嚇的；害怕的","s":"A: Why did the little girl at table five start crying and run to her parents in the middle of the outdoor company picnic this afternoon? B: She was frightened by a large spider that climbed onto her plate, so one of the waiters gently carried it away and brought her a fresh dessert.","t":"A：今天下午公司戶外野餐進行到一半時，五號桌的小女孩為什麼突然哭著跑向她父母？ B：她被一隻爬上她盤子的大蜘蛛【嚇到】了，所以一位服務生輕輕把蜘蛛帶走，並給她送來一份新的甜點。"},{"w":"hornet","p":"n.","d":"a large wasp that can give a painful sting","c":"大黃蜂；虎頭蜂","s":"A: Why has the park closed the walking path behind the visitor center, and when do you think it will be open again for the tour groups? B: Workers found a huge hornet nest under the wooden bridge, and those large wasps can be dangerous, so experts will remove it safely by Friday.","t":"A：公園為什麼封閉了遊客中心後面的步道？你覺得什麼時候會重新開放給旅行團？ B：工人在木橋下發現了一個巨大的【虎頭蜂】窩，那種大型胡蜂可能很危險，所以專家會在星期五前把它安全移除。"},{"w":"life-threatening","p":"adj.","d":"able to cause death","c":"危及生命的","s":"A: Why must every staff member at the summer camp complete the first-aid course before the children arrive next week? B: Some people have serious allergies, and a single bee sting can become life-threatening within minutes, so we all need to know how to act quickly and call an ambulance.","t":"A：為什麼夏令營的每位工作人員都必須在下週孩子們抵達前完成急救課程？ B：有些人有嚴重過敏，一次蜂螫就可能在幾分鐘內變得【危及生命】，所以我們都必須知道如何迅速處理並叫救護車。"},{"w":"endearing","p":"adj.","d":"making people feel love or affection","c":"惹人喜愛的；討喜的","s":"A: What did the customers say about the new cartoon ladybug that the design team created as the mascot for our organic vegetable brand? B: Most of them found its big eyes and shy smile very endearing, and several parents said their children now ask for our vegetables at the supermarket.","t":"A：顧客對設計團隊為我們有機蔬菜品牌創作的新卡通瓢蟲吉祥物有什麼看法？ B：大部分人覺得牠的大眼睛和害羞的笑容非常【討喜】，還有幾位家長說他們的孩子現在會在超市指名要買我們的蔬菜。"},{"w":"insecticide","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used to kill insects","c":"殺蟲劑","s":"A: The farm manager says the cabbages in the north field have holes in their leaves again, so what should we do before the harvest next month? B: We could spray a natural insecticide that is approved for organic farms, because it kills the caterpillars without harming the soil or our customers' trust in our brand.","t":"A：農場經理說北邊田裡的高麗菜葉子又出現破洞了，下個月收成前我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們可以噴灑經有機農場認證的天然【殺蟲劑】，因為它能殺死毛毛蟲，又不會傷害土壤或顧客對我們品牌的信任。"},{"w":"irritating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed","c":"惱人的；令人煩躁的","s":"A: Why did so many guests leave the outdoor wedding reception at the hotel garden before the dessert was even served last night? B: Clouds of small flies kept landing on the food and buzzing around people's faces, which was very irritating, so the manager has ordered new fans for the terrace.","t":"A：昨晚飯店花園的戶外婚宴，為什麼那麼多賓客在甜點還沒上之前就離開了？ B：成群的小蒼蠅不斷停在食物上，還在大家臉旁嗡嗡飛，非常【惱人】，所以經理已經為露台訂購了新的電風扇。"},{"w":"firefly","p":"n.","d":"a small flying insect whose body gives off light at night","c":"螢火蟲","s":"A: Our travel agency wants a special evening activity for the tour group visiting the countryside in June, so do you have any good ideas? B: They could take a quiet walk by the river after dinner, because that is the season when every firefly lights up the dark fields like tiny stars.","t":"A：我們旅行社想為六月去鄉間的旅行團安排特別的晚間活動，你有什麼好點子嗎？ B：他們可以在晚餐後沿著河邊安靜散步，因為那正是每一隻【螢火蟲】像小星星般照亮黑暗田野的季節。"},{"w":"butterfly","p":"n.","d":"an insect with large, colorful wings","c":"蝴蝶","s":"A: What is the main attraction at the new botanical park that our company is sponsoring, and why do you think families will want to visit? B: There is a large glass house where you can watch a colorful butterfly come out of its cocoon, and children love taking photos of them in the flowers.","t":"A：我們公司贊助的新植物園，主要景點是什麼？你為什麼認為家庭遊客會想去？ B：那裡有一座大型玻璃溫室，你可以看到色彩繽紛的【蝴蝶】破繭而出，孩子們很喜歡在花叢中幫牠們拍照。"},{"w":"bee","p":"n.","d":"a flying insect that makes honey and can sting","c":"蜜蜂","s":"A: Why is the hotel putting small wooden boxes on the roof garden, and will they cause any problems for the guests who relax up there? B: Each box is a home for a bee colony that will make honey for our breakfast buffet, and the boxes are far from the seating area, so guests will be safe.","t":"A：飯店為什麼要在屋頂花園放小木箱？會對在那裡休息的客人造成任何問題嗎？ B：每個木箱都是一個【蜜蜂】群的家，牠們會為我們的早餐自助吧生產蜂蜜，而且木箱離座位區很遠，所以客人會很安全。"},{"w":"beetle","p":"n.","d":"an insect with a hard, shiny shell covering its wings","c":"甲蟲","s":"A: The museum curator said the insect exhibition needs one more interesting display before it opens to the public next Monday, so what can we add? B: We could show a rare beetle with a shiny green shell from South America, since its hard wings look like jewelry and visitors will surely want to take photos.","t":"A：博物館策展人說昆蟲展在下週一對外開放前還需要再一個有趣的展品，我們可以加什麼？ B：我們可以展出一隻來自南美洲、有著閃亮綠色外殼的稀有【甲蟲】，因為牠堅硬的翅膀看起來像珠寶，參觀者一定會想拍照。"},{"w":"stunning","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or impressive","c":"令人驚豔的；極美的","s":"A: Did the photographer we hired for the nature magazine finish the pictures of the butterflies in the national park yesterday? B: Yes, and the close-up shots are absolutely stunning, with bright wings and perfect light, so the editor wants to use one of them on the cover of the next issue.","t":"A：我們為自然雜誌請的攝影師昨天拍完國家公園裡蝴蝶的照片了嗎？ B：拍完了，而且特寫照片絕對【令人驚豔】，翅膀色彩鮮豔、光線完美，所以編輯想用其中一張當下一期的封面。"},{"w":"ecosystem","p":"n.","d":"all the living things in an area and how they depend on each other","c":"生態系統","s":"A: Why is the government asking the construction company to change its plan for the new shopping mall near the wetland area? B: The wetland is part of a fragile ecosystem where birds, frogs, and many insects depend on each other, so building there could cause serious damage to the environment.","t":"A：政府為什麼要求建設公司修改濕地附近新購物中心的計畫？ B：那片濕地屬於一個脆弱的【生態系統】，鳥類、青蛙和許多昆蟲彼此依存，所以在那裡興建可能會對環境造成嚴重破壞。"},{"w":"sketch","p":"v.","d":"to draw something quickly and simply","c":"畫素描；畫草圖","s":"A: How will the design team create the new insect illustrations for the children's science textbook before the printing deadline at the end of the month? B: First, our artist will sketch each insect roughly with a pencil while looking at real specimens, and then she will add color on the computer.","t":"A：設計團隊要如何在月底印刷截止日前，為兒童科學課本完成新的昆蟲插圖？ B：首先，我們的畫家會一邊觀察真正的標本，一邊用鉛筆把每隻昆蟲粗略地【畫成草圖】，然後再用電腦上色。"},{"w":"biodiverse","p":"adj.","d":"having many different kinds of plants and animals","c":"生物多樣性豐富的","s":"A: Why does the travel company want to promote eco-tours to this small island in its new brochure for European customers? B: The island is one of the most biodiverse places in the region, with hundreds of kinds of plants, birds, and insects, so nature lovers will gladly pay extra to explore it.","t":"A：旅遊公司為什麼想在給歐洲客戶的新手冊中推廣這座小島的生態旅遊？ B：這座島是該地區【生物多樣性最豐富】的地方之一，有數百種植物、鳥類和昆蟲，所以大自然愛好者會很樂意多付錢去探索。"},{"w":"jungles","p":"n.","d":"thick tropical forests with many trees and plants","c":"叢林（複數）","s":"A: Where did the research team find the new kinds of insects that the science museum will show in its special exhibition this winter? B: They spent three months exploring the thick jungles of Southeast Asia, where it rains almost every day and many animals have never been studied by scientists before.","t":"A：研究團隊是在哪裡發現科學博物館今年冬天特展要展出的新種昆蟲？ B：他們花了三個月探索東南亞茂密的【叢林】，那裡幾乎天天下雨，而且許多動物從未被科學家研究過。"},{"w":"rainforest","p":"n.","d":"a thick forest in a warm place where it rains a lot","c":"雨林","s":"A: Our coffee company wants to use a new supplier from South America next year, but how can we make sure the farm treats nature responsibly? B: We should choose a farm that grows coffee under the trees instead of cutting down the rainforest, since that protects the many insects and birds living there.","t":"A：我們咖啡公司明年想採用一家南美洲的新供應商，但要怎麼確保農場以負責任的方式對待大自然？ B：我們應該選擇在樹下種植咖啡、而不是砍伐【雨林】的農場，因為這樣能保護住在那裡的許多昆蟲和鳥類。"},{"w":"botanical","p":"adj.","d":"related to plants or the study of plants","c":"植物的；植物學的","s":"A: Where should we take the overseas clients on Saturday afternoon if they want a relaxing activity away from the busy downtown offices? B: The city's botanical garden is a great choice because it has thousands of plants, a beautiful butterfly house, and a quiet café where we can continue talking business.","t":"A：如果海外客戶星期六下午想做些遠離繁忙市中心辦公室的輕鬆活動，我們該帶他們去哪裡？ B：市立【植物】園是很好的選擇，因為那裡有數千種植物、一座漂亮的蝴蝶館，還有一間安靜的咖啡館，我們可以繼續談生意。"},{"w":"shape","p":"n.","d":"the outer form or outline of something","c":"形狀；外形","s":"A: How did the designer come up with the idea for the new company logo that everyone in the meeting seemed to like so much? B: She studied the shape of a dragonfly's wings for several days, then turned those thin, elegant lines into a simple symbol that shows speed and lightness.","t":"A：設計師是怎麼想出那個會議上大家似乎都非常喜歡的新公司標誌？ B：她花了好幾天研究蜻蜓翅膀的【形狀】，然後把那些纖細優雅的線條變成一個代表速度與輕盈的簡單符號。"},{"w":"documentary","p":"n.","d":"a film or TV program that gives facts about a real subject","c":"紀錄片","s":"A: What kind of program is the television station planning for the nature channel next season, and how big is the budget for it? B: They are making a six-part documentary about the secret life of ants, and the producers will spend almost a year filming in forests and deserts around the world.","t":"A：電視台下一季為自然頻道規劃了什麼樣的節目？預算有多少？ B：他們正在製作一部關於螞蟻秘密生活的六集【紀錄片】，製作人將花將近一年的時間在世界各地的森林和沙漠拍攝。"},{"w":"portray","p":"v.","d":"to show or describe someone or something in a certain way","c":"描繪；描寫","s":"A: Why are the entomology experts unhappy with the new animated film about insects that the studio released last month? B: They feel the movie tends to portray spiders and wasps as evil monsters, which could make children afraid of creatures that actually help farmers by eating harmful pests.","t":"A：為什麼昆蟲學專家對製片廠上個月推出的那部昆蟲動畫電影不滿意？ B：他們覺得這部電影常把蜘蛛和胡蜂【描繪】成邪惡的怪物，這可能會讓孩子害怕這些其實會吃掉害蟲、幫助農夫的生物。"},{"w":"sting","p":"v.","d":"(of an insect) to hurt someone by pushing a sharp part into the skin","c":"螫；叮","s":"A: Why is the gardener wearing a thick jacket, gloves, and a net over his face when it is so hot outside this afternoon? B: He has to move the beehives near the parking lot, and the bees may sting him if they feel that their home is in danger, so he is not taking any chances.","t":"A：今天下午外面這麼熱，園丁為什麼還穿著厚外套、戴手套和面網？ B：他必須搬動停車場附近的蜂箱，如果蜜蜂覺得牠們的家有危險，可能會【螫】他，所以他不想冒任何風險。"},{"w":"stinger","p":"n.","d":"the sharp part of an insect that it uses to sting","c":"螫針","s":"A: The hotel nurse said a guest was hurt by a bee near the pool, so what should the lifeguards do if this happens again tomorrow? B: They should first remove the stinger from the skin carefully with a card, wash the area with soap and water, and then put some ice on it to reduce the swelling.","t":"A：飯店護士說有位客人在泳池邊被蜜蜂所傷，如果明天又發生這種事，救生員該怎麼做？ B：他們應該先用卡片小心地把【螫針】從皮膚上刮出，用肥皂和水清洗傷處，然後冰敷以減輕腫脹。"},{"w":"rash","p":"n.","d":"an area of red spots on the skin","c":"疹子；皮疹","s":"A: Why did the employee from the warehouse leave work early today, and will he be able to come back tomorrow morning? B: He developed a red, itchy rash on his arms after moving some boxes full of insects and dust, so the doctor gave him some cream and told him to rest.","t":"A：倉庫那位員工今天為什麼提早下班？他明天早上能回來上班嗎？ B：他搬了一些滿是蟲子和灰塵的箱子後，手臂上長出又紅又癢的【疹子】，所以醫生給了他一些藥膏，要他好好休息。"},{"w":"aesthetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to beauty and how things look","c":"在美學上；在外觀上","s":"A: Why did the architect choose to cover the walls of the new office lobby with hundreds of plants and colorful butterfly paintings? B: She wanted the space to be aesthetically pleasing for visitors while also making the air cleaner, so employees and guests would feel calmer the moment they walked in.","t":"A：建築師為什麼選擇在新辦公大廳的牆上布滿數百株植物和色彩繽紛的蝴蝶畫？ B：她希望這個空間在【外觀上】讓訪客賞心悅目，同時也讓空氣更乾淨，讓員工和客人一走進來就感到更平靜。"},{"w":"textures","p":"n.","d":"the ways surfaces feel when you touch them, such as rough or smooth","c":"質地；觸感（複數）","s":"A: What makes the new insect exhibit at the science museum so popular with schools, and why do teachers keep booking extra visits? B: Children can touch models that copy the different textures of real insects, such as rough beetle shells and soft butterfly wings, which helps them learn through their hands.","t":"A：科學博物館新的昆蟲展為什麼這麼受學校歡迎？老師們為什麼一直加訂參觀？ B：孩子們可以觸摸模仿真實昆蟲各種【質地】的模型，例如粗糙的甲蟲外殼和柔軟的蝴蝶翅膀，這讓他們透過雙手學習。"}]},{"unit":191,"theme":"Inspired 受到啟發","cards":[{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"something that gives you new ideas or the wish to do something","c":"靈感；鼓舞","s":"A: Where did the design team get the inspiration for the new office lobby, because everyone who visits says it looks fresh and welcoming? B: They took a trip to several small cafés in Kyoto last spring, and the warm wood, soft lights, and indoor plants gave them lots of ideas.","t":"A：設計團隊新辦公大廳的【靈感】是從哪裡來的？因為每位來訪的人都說它看起來清新又親切。 B：他們去年春天到京都去參觀了幾間小咖啡館，那裡溫暖的木頭、柔和的燈光和室內植物給了他們很多想法。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to work hard or do something","c":"激勵；促使","s":"A: Sales have been slow for three months, and the team seems tired and bored, so what can we do as managers to help? B: I think a small bonus for every new client and a fun team dinner at the end of the month would really motivate them to try harder.","t":"A：銷售已經低迷三個月了，團隊看起來又累又無聊，身為經理我們能做些什麼來幫忙？ B：我認為每簽一位新客戶就發一小筆獎金，再加上月底一頓有趣的團隊晚餐，真的能【激勵】他們更加努力。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the reason or energy that makes you want to do something","c":"動機；動力","s":"A: You started taking online accounting classes every evening after work even though you are already busy, so why did you decide to do it? B: My main motivation is the promotion that will open next year, because the new position requires a certificate and pays almost twenty percent more.","t":"A：你雖然已經很忙了，卻還是每天下班後去上線上會計課，你為什麼決定這麼做？ B：我主要的【動機】是明年將開放的升遷機會，因為那個新職位需要證照，而且薪水多了將近百分之二十。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone support or confidence to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: The new interns are very quiet during our weekly meetings, and I am worried that they have good ideas but are too shy to speak up. B: Let's ask each of them one easy question at the start, and then encourage them to share their opinions without worrying about making mistakes.","t":"A：新來的實習生在我們每週的會議上都很安靜，我擔心他們其實有好點子，只是太害羞而不敢發言。 B：我們一開始先問他們每人一個簡單的問題，然後【鼓勵】他們分享意見，不必擔心犯錯。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give someone support and confidence","c":"鼓勵；激勵","s":"A: How did you finally manage to finish the marathon last weekend when you told me your legs were hurting badly after the first twenty kilometers? B: My coworkers were waiting along the road with signs and water, and their loud encouragement helped me keep running all the way to the finish line.","t":"A：你告訴過我跑完前二十公里後腿就痛得很厲害，那你上週末到底是怎麼跑完馬拉松的？ B：我的同事們拿著標語和水在路邊等我，他們大聲的【鼓勵】讓我一路跑到了終點線。"},{"w":"influence","p":"n.","d":"the power to change how someone thinks or behaves","c":"影響；影響力","s":"A: Why did our young customers suddenly start buying so many green tea drinks this summer when they used to prefer sweet coffee? B: A popular food blogger posted several videos about healthy drinks, and her influence on teenagers and college students is much stronger than any of our television ads.","t":"A：為什麼我們的年輕顧客以前偏好甜咖啡，今年夏天卻突然開始買那麼多綠茶飲料？ B：一位很紅的美食部落客發了好幾支關於健康飲品的影片，她對青少年和大學生的【影響力】遠比我們任何電視廣告都還要大。"},{"w":"role model","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose behavior others copy because they admire them","c":"榜樣；模範","s":"A: Why do so many new employees in the marketing department ask to join Ms. Chen's projects even though her deadlines are always very tight? B: She is a great role model for young workers because she stays calm under pressure, treats everyone fairly, and always explains clearly how she solves problems.","t":"A：為什麼行銷部有那麼多新員工要求加入陳小姐的專案，即使她的截止期限總是很緊？ B：她是年輕員工很好的【榜樣】，因為她在壓力下保持冷靜、公平對待每個人，而且總是清楚解釋她如何解決問題。"},{"w":"example","p":"n.","d":"a person or action that others can learn from or copy","c":"榜樣；例子","s":"A: Our new branch manager comes to the office before eight every morning and is always the last person to turn off the lights, isn't she? B: Yes, and she sets a good example for the whole team, so now even the salespeople who used to arrive late are coming in early.","t":"A：我們新的分店經理每天早上八點前就到辦公室，而且總是最後一個關燈的人，對吧？ B：對，她為整個團隊樹立了好【榜樣】，所以現在連以前常遲到的業務員也都提早上班了。"},{"w":"idea","p":"n.","d":"a thought or plan about what to do","c":"想法；主意","s":"A: The hotel wants to attract more families during the slow winter months, but the manager says the budget for advertising is very small this year. B: I have an idea that might help: we could offer free breakfast for children and a weekend cooking class that parents and kids can join together.","t":"A：飯店想在淡季的冬季月份吸引更多家庭客，但經理說今年的廣告預算很少。 B：我有一個可能有幫助的【主意】：我們可以提供兒童免費早餐，以及一個讓父母和孩子一起參加的週末烹飪課。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"a clear picture or plan of what the future should be like","c":"願景；遠見","s":"A: Why did the investors agree to put so much money into such a small startup that only has twelve employees and one product? B: The founder shared a clear vision of building affordable solar panels for every home in Asia, and her detailed five-year plan made the investors feel confident.","t":"A：為什麼投資人願意投那麼多錢到一家只有十二名員工和一項產品的小新創公司？ B：創辦人分享了要為亞洲每個家庭打造平價太陽能板的清楚【願景】，而她詳細的五年計畫讓投資人很有信心。"},{"w":"dream","p":"n.","d":"something you hope very much to do or have in the future","c":"夢想","s":"A: You've worked as an accountant for ten years, so why are you suddenly taking baking classes on Saturday mornings at the community center? B: It has always been my dream to open a small bakery near the train station, and I want to learn the skills before I leave my office job.","t":"A：你已經當了十年會計師，為什麼突然在社區中心上週六早上的烘焙課？ B：在火車站附近開一間小麵包店一直是我的【夢想】，我想在辭掉辦公室工作前先學會這些技能。"},{"w":"goal","p":"n.","d":"something you are trying to achieve","c":"目標","s":"A: What did the manager say during the meeting this morning about our plans for the next quarter, since I missed it because of a dentist appointment? B: Our main goal is to increase online sales by fifteen percent, so we will spend more on social media ads and improve the website.","t":"A：經理今天早上開會時對下一季的計畫說了些什麼？因為我去看牙醫所以錯過了。 B：我們的主要【目標】是讓線上銷售成長百分之十五，所以我們會在社群媒體廣告上花更多錢，並改善網站。"},{"w":"create","p":"v.","d":"to make something new","c":"創造；建立","s":"A: Our website looks old-fashioned, and many customers have complained that they cannot find the product information they need on their phones. B: Let's hire a young designer to create a new homepage that is simple, colorful, and easy to use on both smartphones and laptops.","t":"A：我們的網站看起來很老氣，很多顧客抱怨用手機找不到他們需要的產品資訊。 B：我們請一位年輕設計師來【建立】一個簡單、色彩豐富，而且在手機和筆電上都容易使用的新首頁吧。"},{"w":"imagine","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture of something in your mind","c":"想像","s":"A: The new conference room is still empty and full of dust, so it is hard for me to believe it will be ready for the clients next week. B: Just imagine it with a long wooden table, big windows, soft chairs, and a large screen on the wall, and you will see how nice it will be.","t":"A：新的會議室還是空的而且滿是灰塵，我很難相信下週就能準備好迎接客戶。 B：只要【想像】一下裡面擺上一張長木桌、大窗戶、柔軟的椅子，牆上還有一個大螢幕，你就會知道它會有多棒。"},{"w":"discover","p":"v.","d":"to find or learn something for the first time","c":"發現","s":"A: How did you start your career as a professional photographer when you studied engineering at university and worked in a factory for five years? B: During a business trip to Iceland, I happened to discover how much I loved taking pictures of mountains, so I took evening courses and slowly built my portfolio.","t":"A：你大學讀工程，又在工廠工作了五年，你是怎麼開始專業攝影師的職涯的？ B：在一次去冰島的出差中，我碰巧【發現】自己有多喜歡拍山景，所以我去上夜間課程，慢慢建立起我的作品集。"},{"w":"spark","p":"v.","d":"to cause something to start or develop","c":"激發；引發","s":"A: Why did the city library invite a famous astronaut to give a free talk to the high school students on Saturday afternoon? B: The librarians hoped her exciting stories about life in space would spark the teenagers' interest in science and encourage more of them to study engineering later.","t":"A：為什麼市立圖書館邀請一位知名太空人在週六下午為高中生舉辦一場免費演講？ B：圖書館員希望她在太空生活的精彩故事能【激發】青少年對科學的興趣，並讓更多人日後去讀工程。"},{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to respect and like someone because of what they do","c":"欽佩；欣賞","s":"A: Why do you always quote our former CEO in your presentations even though she retired from the company more than five years ago? B: I really admire the way she saved the business during the financial crisis without firing anyone, and her honest leadership still guides how I manage my team.","t":"A：為什麼你在簡報裡總是引用我們前任執行長的話，即使她已經退休超過五年了？ B：我真的很【欽佩】她在金融危機期間沒有裁掉任何人就救了公司，她誠實的領導方式至今仍指引我管理團隊。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new and original ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: We need someone to plan the decorations, games, and music for the company's twentieth anniversary party, but nobody has volunteered yet. B: Why don't we ask Tina from the design department, because she is very creative and always comes up with fun and surprising ideas for our team events?","t":"A：我們需要有人來規劃公司二十週年派對的布置、遊戲和音樂，但目前還沒人自願。 B：我們何不請設計部的蒂娜來負責？她非常【有創意】，總能為我們的團隊活動想出有趣又令人驚喜的點子。"},{"w":"passionate","p":"adj.","d":"having very strong feelings about something you love","c":"熱情的；熱愛的","s":"A: What did you think of the new chef that the restaurant owner hired last week to manage the kitchen during the busy holiday season? B: He is truly passionate about local food, and he visits the farmers' market every morning to choose the freshest vegetables and talk with the growers.","t":"A：你覺得餐廳老闆上週聘請、在繁忙假期負責廚房的新主廚怎麼樣？ B：他真的非常【熱愛】在地食材，每天早上都去農夫市集挑選最新鮮的蔬菜，還會和種植者聊天。"},{"w":"motivated","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to do something and willing to work hard","c":"有幹勁的；積極的","s":"A: Why did the human resources team choose the candidate with less experience instead of the one who had worked in sales for ten years? B: She seemed highly motivated during the interview, she had already studied our products in detail, and she clearly wanted to learn and grow with the company.","t":"A：為什麼人資團隊選了經驗較少的應徵者，而不是在業務領域工作了十年的那位？ B：她在面試時看起來非常【有幹勁】，已經詳細研究過我們的產品，而且顯然很想和公司一起學習成長。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of interest and excitement","c":"熱心的；熱情的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the director announced that the office would move to a new building with a gym and a rooftop garden? B: Everyone was very enthusiastic about the news, and several people immediately started planning lunchtime yoga classes and weekend gardening activities together.","t":"A：當主管宣布辦公室要搬到一棟有健身房和屋頂花園的新大樓時，員工的反應如何？ B：大家對這個消息都非常【熱烈】，好幾個人立刻開始一起規劃午休瑜伽課和週末園藝活動。"},{"w":"determined","p":"adj.","d":"having made a firm decision to do something","c":"下定決心的；堅定的","s":"A: Your team failed the safety inspection twice this year, so are you going to give up on getting the international certificate for the factory? B: No, we are determined to pass next time, so we hired an outside expert, trained every worker again, and replaced all the old machines.","t":"A：你們團隊今年已經兩次沒通過安全檢查，你們要放棄為工廠取得國際認證嗎？ B：不，我們【下定決心】下次一定要通過，所以我們聘請了外部專家、重新訓練每位工人，並更換了所有舊機器。"},{"w":"hopeful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that something good will probably happen","c":"抱有希望的","s":"A: Do you think the company will win the large contract with the Japanese electronics firm after last week's long meeting in Osaka? B: I'm quite hopeful because their managers liked our samples, asked many questions about delivery times, and invited us back for a factory tour next month.","t":"A：上週在大阪那場冗長的會議之後，你覺得公司會拿到那家日本電子公司的大合約嗎？ B：我相當【有希望】，因為他們的經理們很喜歡我們的樣品，問了很多交貨時間的問題，還邀請我們下個月再去參觀工廠。"},{"w":"bright","p":"adj.","d":"full of hope and likely to be successful","c":"光明的；有前途的","s":"A: Our small company only sold coffee in one shop three years ago, so how do you feel about opening five new branches across the country next year? B: The future looks bright because our online orders keep growing every month, and many shopping malls have contacted us about renting space.","t":"A：我們這家小公司三年前只在一家店賣咖啡，你對明年在全國開五家新分店有什麼感覺？ B：未來看起來很【光明】，因為我們的線上訂單每個月都在成長，而且很多購物中心都主動聯絡我們洽談租用空間。"},{"w":"strongly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very firm or powerful way","c":"強烈地；堅決地","s":"A: The board is still deciding whether to move the factory overseas, so what is your opinion as the head of the local workers' team? B: I strongly believe we should stay here, because our skilled workers, good roads, and close relationship with nearby suppliers are worth much more than cheaper rent.","t":"A：董事會仍在決定是否要把工廠移到海外，身為本地工人團隊的負責人，你的意見是什麼？ B：我【堅決】認為我們應該留在這裡，因為我們熟練的工人、良好的道路以及和附近供應商的密切關係，比便宜的租金值得多了。"},{"w":"deeply","p":"adv.","d":"very much; in a strong way","c":"深深地","s":"A: How did the audience react to the short film about the volunteer doctors that our charity showed at the dinner event last Friday evening? B: Many guests were deeply moved by the stories of the children who were treated, and several of them offered to donate money before the dinner even ended.","t":"A：上週五晚上我們的慈善機構在晚宴活動中播放了那部關於志工醫生的短片，觀眾的反應如何？ B：許多來賓都被那些接受治療的孩子們的故事【深深地】感動，有好幾位甚至在晚宴結束前就表示要捐款。"},{"w":"greatly","p":"adv.","d":"very much; to a large degree","c":"大大地；非常","s":"A: Since the company started offering flexible working hours and the option to work from home twice a week, have you noticed any changes? B: Yes, staff morale has greatly improved, fewer people are taking sick days, and our customer service team is answering emails much faster than before.","t":"A：自從公司開始提供彈性工時，並讓員工每週可以在家工作兩天，你有注意到什麼改變嗎？ B：有，員工士氣【大大地】提升了，請病假的人變少了，而且我們的客服團隊回覆電子郵件也比以前快得多。"},{"w":"creatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that uses new and original ideas","c":"有創意地","s":"A: Our budget for the product launch was cut by half last week, so how can we still get attention from customers without expensive television ads? B: We need to think creatively, perhaps by holding a free tasting event in the train station and asking customers to share photos online for a small prize.","t":"A：我們產品發表會的預算上週被砍了一半，沒有昂貴的電視廣告，我們要怎麼還能吸引顧客注意？ B：我們需要【有創意地】思考，也許可以在火車站舉辦免費試吃活動，並請顧客在網路上分享照片來換小獎品。"},{"w":"passionately","p":"adv.","d":"with very strong feelings or great interest","c":"熱情地；熱烈地","s":"A: Why did the city council finally decide to keep the old public library open instead of turning the building into a parking lot? B: Hundreds of residents came to the meeting and spoke passionately about how the library helped their children, so the council members changed their minds.","t":"A：為什麼市議會最後決定保留舊的公立圖書館，而不是把那棟建築改成停車場？ B：數百位居民來參加會議，【熱情地】講述圖書館如何幫助他們的孩子，所以議員們改變了心意。"},{"w":"openly","p":"adv.","d":"in an honest way, without hiding anything","c":"公開地；坦率地","s":"A: The team leader said the project was going well, but I heard there were serious problems with the software during testing last week. B: I think we should talk openly about those problems at the next meeting, so everyone understands the risks and we can solve them together quickly.","t":"A：組長說專案進行得很順利，但我聽說上週測試時軟體出了嚴重的問題。 B：我認為我們應該在下次會議上【坦率地】討論那些問題，讓大家都了解風險，這樣我們才能一起快速解決。"},{"w":"positively","p":"adv.","d":"in a good or hopeful way","c":"正面地；積極地","s":"A: I was nervous about introducing the new online ordering system to our older customers who usually call the store to place their orders. B: Don't worry, because most of them have responded positively so far, and several told us the website is easier than waiting on the phone.","t":"A：我原本很擔心要向通常打電話到店裡訂貨的年長顧客介紹新的線上訂購系統。 B：別擔心，到目前為止他們大多數的反應都很【正面】，好幾位還告訴我們網站比在電話上等候還方便。"}]},{"unit":192,"theme":"Intelligent Person 聰明的人","cards":[{"w":"smart","p":"adj.","d":"able to learn and understand things quickly","c":"聰明的；精明的","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to give the new marketing project to Kevin instead of one of the senior staff members last week? B: She thinks he is a very smart young man, because he solved the customer database problem in two days and also found a way to cut our printing costs.","t":"A：為什麼經理上週決定把新的行銷專案交給凱文，而不是交給資深員工？ B：她認為他是個非常【聰明】的年輕人，因為他兩天內就解決了客戶資料庫的問題，還找到了減少印刷成本的方法。"},{"w":"bright","p":"adj.","d":"intelligent and quick to learn","c":"聰明的；機靈的","s":"A: How are the summer interns doing in the accounting department so far, and are any of them ready to help with the monthly reports? B: Most of them are still learning, but Amy is especially bright, so she understood our software after one training session and is already checking invoices on her own.","t":"A：會計部的暑期實習生目前表現如何？有沒有人已經可以幫忙做月報了？ B：大部分還在學習中，但艾咪特別【聰明】，她上過一次訓練課就懂了我們的軟體，現在已經能自己核對發票了。"},{"w":"clever","p":"adj.","d":"quick at learning and good at finding new ideas","c":"聰明的；巧妙的","s":"A: How did your team manage to finish the trade show booth so cheaply when the budget was cut by almost half this year? B: Our designer came up with a clever idea, so we reused the old display boards, painted them with the new company colors, and borrowed lights from the training room.","t":"A：今年預算被砍了將近一半，你們團隊是怎麼用這麼少的錢完成展覽攤位的？ B：我們的設計師想出了一個【巧妙的】點子，我們重複利用舊的展示板，漆上公司的新顏色，還向訓練教室借了燈。"},{"w":"wise","p":"adj.","d":"able to make good decisions because of experience and knowledge","c":"有智慧的；明智的","s":"A: Should I accept the job offer from the startup right away, or should I wait until my current company announces this year's promotions next month? B: I think it would be wise to wait a few weeks, because you can compare both offers carefully and you won't lose the bonus you have already earned here.","t":"A：我應該馬上接受新創公司的工作邀約，還是等到現在的公司下個月宣布今年的升遷名單？ B：我覺得等幾個星期是【明智的】，因為你可以仔細比較兩邊的條件，也不會失去你在這裡已經賺到的獎金。"},{"w":"knowledgeable","p":"adj.","d":"knowing a lot about a subject","c":"知識豐富的；很懂的","s":"A: Who should we ask to lead the workshop on international shipping rules for the new sales staff next Thursday afternoon? B: Mr. Chen is very knowledgeable about customs and import taxes, since he worked at a logistics company in Singapore for ten years before he joined our firm.","t":"A：下週四下午給新業務人員上的國際運輸規定工作坊，我們應該請誰來帶？ B：陳先生對海關和進口稅非常【了解】，因為他加入我們公司之前，在新加坡的一家物流公司工作了十年。"},{"w":"learned","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of knowledge from many years of study","c":"有學問的；博學的","s":"A: Why is the university library inviting that elderly professor to give the opening speech at the history conference this weekend? B: She is a learned woman who has studied ancient trade routes for over forty years, so many researchers and students are traveling from other cities just to hear her talk.","t":"A：為什麼大學圖書館邀請那位年長的教授在這個週末的歷史研討會上致開幕詞？ B：她是一位【博學的】女士，研究古代貿易路線超過四十年，所以很多研究人員和學生特地從其他城市來聽她演講。"},{"w":"educated","p":"adj.","d":"having received a good education","c":"受過教育的","s":"A: What kind of customers usually buy the expensive business magazines that we sell in the airport bookstore near the departure gates? B: Most of them are highly educated professionals who travel for work often, so they want detailed articles about finance and technology to read during their long flights.","t":"A：通常是哪一類顧客會買我們在登機門附近機場書店賣的那些昂貴商業雜誌？ B：大多是經常出差、受過高等【教育】的專業人士，所以他們想在長途飛行中閱讀關於金融和科技的深入文章。"},{"w":"intellectual","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the ability to think and understand serious ideas","c":"智力的；知性的","s":"A: Why do so many employees enjoy the monthly book club that the human resources department started in the staff lounge last spring? B: It gives them an intellectual challenge outside their daily tasks, because they discuss difficult ideas, share different opinions, and practice explaining their thoughts clearly in English.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多員工喜歡人資部去年春天在員工休息室開辦的每月讀書會？ B：它在日常工作之外給了他們【智力上的】挑戰，因為他們可以討論困難的觀念、分享不同的意見，並練習用英文清楚表達想法。"},{"w":"genius","p":"n.","d":"a person who is extremely intelligent or skilled","c":"天才","s":"A: Have you heard that the young engineer in our design team fixed the factory's broken robot arm in just one afternoon yesterday? B: Yes, everyone is calling him a genius, because the outside repair company said it would take two weeks and cost us thousands of dollars in lost production.","t":"A：你聽說了嗎？我們設計團隊那位年輕工程師昨天只花一個下午就修好了工廠壞掉的機械手臂。 B：聽說了，大家都叫他【天才】，因為外面的維修公司說要花兩個星期，還會讓我們損失好幾千元的產量。"},{"w":"prodigy","p":"n.","d":"a young person who has a very great natural ability","c":"神童；奇才","s":"A: Is it true that the pianist performing at our company's anniversary dinner on Friday night is only twelve years old? B: Yes, she is a real child prodigy who started playing at three, and she has already won several international competitions in Vienna and Tokyo, so the tickets sold out quickly.","t":"A：在我們公司週五晚上週年晚宴表演的鋼琴家真的只有十二歲嗎？ B：是的，她是真正的【神童】，三歲就開始彈琴，已經在維也納和東京贏得好幾項國際比賽，所以票很快就賣完了。"},{"w":"expert","p":"n.","d":"a person with special skill or knowledge in a certain area","c":"專家","s":"A: Our online store was attacked by hackers again last night, so what should we do before the big holiday sale begins next Monday? B: We should hire a security expert to check our whole system, because one more attack could close the website and make customers lose trust in us.","t":"A：我們的網路商店昨晚又被駭客攻擊了，在下週一大型假期特賣開始前我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該請一位資安【專家】檢查整個系統，因為再被攻擊一次，網站可能就得關閉，顧客也會對我們失去信任。"},{"w":"scholar","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies a subject very deeply, often at a university","c":"學者","s":"A: Who wrote the introduction to the new guidebook about the old temples and markets that our travel agency is selling this year? B: A well-known scholar from National Taiwan University wrote it, since she has spent many years researching local history and reading old government records about the city.","t":"A：我們旅行社今年在賣的那本介紹老廟宇和市場的新旅遊書，序言是誰寫的？ B：是一位台灣大學的知名【學者】寫的，因為她花了很多年研究地方歷史，閱讀這座城市的舊政府紀錄。"},{"w":"thinker","p":"n.","d":"a person who thinks deeply or in a special way","c":"思想家；思考者","s":"A: Why did the board invite that famous author to speak at our annual leadership meeting at the hotel conference center next month? B: He is an original thinker whose books about teamwork changed how many companies train managers, so the directors hope he will give us fresh ideas for the future.","t":"A：為什麼董事會邀請那位知名作家在下個月飯店會議中心舉行的年度領導會議上演講？ B：他是一位有原創性的【思想家】，他關於團隊合作的書改變了許多公司培訓主管的方式，所以董事們希望他能為我們的未來帶來新想法。"},{"w":"analytical","p":"adj.","d":"using careful and logical study of information","c":"分析的；善於分析的","s":"A: What skills are you looking for in the person who will replace Linda in the finance department after she retires in December? B: We need someone with strong analytical skills, because the job involves studying sales figures every week, finding problems in the budget, and writing clear reports for the directors.","t":"A：琳達十二月退休後，你們要找什麼樣技能的人來接替她在財務部的工作？ B：我們需要有很強【分析】能力的人，因為這份工作要每週研究銷售數字、找出預算中的問題，並為董事們寫清楚的報告。"},{"w":"logical","p":"adj.","d":"reasonable and based on clear thinking","c":"合邏輯的；合理的","s":"A: Why did the committee choose to move the training center to the building next to the train station instead of the cheaper one outside the city? B: It was the most logical choice, because most of our trainees come by train, and they would waste a lot of time and money traveling to the countryside.","t":"A：為什麼委員會選擇把訓練中心搬到火車站旁邊的大樓，而不是城外比較便宜的那棟？ B：那是最【合理的】選擇，因為大部分學員都搭火車來，如果要去郊區會浪費很多時間和金錢。"},{"w":"perceptive","p":"adj.","d":"good at noticing and understanding things that others miss","c":"有洞察力的；敏銳的","s":"A: How did the new sales manager know that the client was unhappy with our proposal even though he smiled during the whole meeting? B: She is very perceptive, so she noticed that he kept checking his watch and asking about prices, and she quickly offered him a better payment plan.","t":"A：客戶整場會議都在微笑，新業務經理怎麼知道他對我們的提案不滿意？ B：她非常【敏銳】，注意到他一直看手錶又一直問價格，所以她很快就提供他更好的付款方案。"},{"w":"observant","p":"adj.","d":"good at noticing small details","c":"觀察力敏銳的","s":"A: How was the missing package finally found at the warehouse after the delivery company had searched for it for three days? B: One observant worker noticed that a box with the wrong label was sitting behind the loading door, so he checked the tracking number and found that it was ours.","t":"A：貨運公司找了三天，那個遺失的包裹最後是怎麼在倉庫找到的？ B：一位【觀察力敏銳的】員工注意到裝卸門後面有個貼錯標籤的箱子，他查了追蹤號碼，發現就是我們的。"},{"w":"insightful","p":"adj.","d":"showing a clear and deep understanding of something","c":"有深刻見解的","s":"A: Did you find the speaker's presentation about online shopping trends useful for planning our marketing campaign for next year? B: Yes, it was very insightful, because she explained why young customers prefer mobile payments and showed us how small shops can compete with large websites by offering faster delivery.","t":"A：你覺得那位講者關於網購趨勢的簡報，對規劃我們明年的行銷活動有幫助嗎？ B：有，內容非常【有見地】，她解釋了年輕顧客為什麼偏好行動支付，也告訴我們小商店如何靠更快的配送和大型網站競爭。"},{"w":"astute","p":"adj.","d":"clever at understanding situations and using them to get an advantage","c":"精明的；機敏的","s":"A: How did your uncle's small coffee company grow so quickly when so many other cafés in the neighborhood closed during the economic slowdown? B: He is an astute businessman, so he bought coffee beans cheaply before prices went up and started selling packaged drinks to office buildings nearby.","t":"A：經濟不景氣時附近很多咖啡店都倒了，你叔叔的小咖啡公司怎麼還能成長得這麼快？ B：他是個【精明的】生意人，在價格上漲前就便宜買進咖啡豆，還開始賣包裝飲料給附近的辦公大樓。"},{"w":"sharp","p":"adj.","d":"quick to notice and understand things","c":"敏銳的；機靈的","s":"A: Is your grandfather still helping at the family's hardware store even though he is almost eighty years old this year? B: Yes, his mind is still very sharp, so he remembers the price of every item, catches mistakes on the receipts, and gives customers excellent advice about tools.","t":"A：你爺爺今年都快八十歲了，還在家裡的五金行幫忙嗎？ B：是啊，他的頭腦還是很【敏銳】，記得每樣商品的價格，能抓出收據上的錯誤，還會給顧客很棒的工具建議。"},{"w":"brilliant","p":"adj.","d":"extremely clever or skillful","c":"傑出的；絕妙的","s":"A: What did the clients say after they watched the video advertisement that our team made for their new line of sports shoes? B: They said it was brilliant, because the story was exciting, the music fit perfectly, and they believe it will attract many young runners to their stores this summer.","t":"A：客戶看完我們團隊為他們新系列運動鞋製作的影片廣告後怎麼說？ B：他們說拍得【太出色了】，因為故事很精彩、音樂很搭，他們相信今年夏天會吸引很多年輕跑者到店裡。"},{"w":"gifted","p":"adj.","d":"having a natural ability or talent","c":"有天賦的","s":"A: Why does the company always ask Mark to give the speeches when we meet important investors at the annual business conference? B: He is a gifted speaker who can explain complicated numbers in simple words, and his friendly jokes help the audience relax and listen more carefully.","t":"A：為什麼公司在年度商務會議上見重要投資人時，總是請馬克來演講？ B：他是個【有天分的】演講者，能用簡單的話解釋複雜的數字，他親切的笑話也讓聽眾放鬆，更專心聆聽。"},{"w":"talented","p":"adj.","d":"having a special natural skill or ability","c":"有才華的","s":"A: Who designed the beautiful new logo and posters for the coffee shop that just opened on the first floor of our office building? B: A talented graphic designer from our marketing department did them in her free time, and now several other shop owners want to hire her as well.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓一樓剛開的那家咖啡店，漂亮的新標誌和海報是誰設計的？ B：是我們行銷部一位【有才華的】平面設計師利用空閒時間做的，現在還有好幾位店家老闆也想請她設計。"},{"w":"innovative","p":"adj.","d":"using new methods or ideas","c":"創新的","s":"A: Why are so many investors interested in that small technology company that only started three years ago in Hsinchu? B: It has developed an innovative battery that charges phones in five minutes, and several large electronics brands are already discussing contracts to use it in their new products.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多投資人對那家三年前才在新竹成立的小科技公司感興趣？ B：它開發出一種【創新的】電池，五分鐘就能把手機充飽電，好幾個大型電子品牌已經在洽談合約，要用在他們的新產品上。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and original things or ideas","c":"有創造力的；有創意的","s":"A: What kind of person are you hoping to hire for the open position in the advertising department after the interviews next week? B: We want someone creative who can come up with fresh ideas for social media campaigns, design attractive images, and write short messages that customers will remember.","t":"A：下週面試之後，你們希望為廣告部的空缺錄用什麼樣的人？ B：我們想要【有創意的】人，能為社群媒體活動想出新點子、設計吸引人的圖片，並寫出讓顧客記得住的簡短文案。"},{"w":"rational","p":"adj.","d":"based on reason and facts, not on feelings","c":"理性的","s":"A: Why didn't the manager get angry when the client canceled the big order at the last minute on Friday afternoon? B: He always tries to make rational decisions instead of emotional ones, so he calmly checked the contract, calculated our losses, and called other customers to sell the extra goods.","t":"A：週五下午客戶在最後一刻取消大訂單時，經理為什麼沒有生氣？ B：他總是盡量做【理性的】決定而不是情緒化的決定，所以他冷靜地檢查合約、計算損失，並打電話給其他客戶把多出來的貨賣掉。"},{"w":"thoughtful","p":"adj.","d":"thinking carefully, or showing care for other people's needs","c":"深思熟慮的；體貼的","s":"A: Did you read the report that Jenny wrote about improving customer service at our branch offices before the meeting this morning? B: Yes, it was a very thoughtful report, because she clearly considered the problems from both the staff's and the customers' points of view before she offered any suggestions.","t":"A：今天早上開會前，你有讀珍妮寫的那份改善分公司客戶服務的報告嗎？ B：有，那是一份非常【深思熟慮的】報告，因為她在提出任何建議之前，顯然都從員工和顧客兩方的角度考慮過問題。"},{"w":"resourceful","p":"adj.","d":"good at finding quick and clever ways to solve problems","c":"足智多謀的；機智的","s":"A: How did the tour guide handle the situation when the bus broke down on the mountain road during the company trip last weekend? B: She was very resourceful, because she called a local taxi company, arranged lunch at a nearby farm, and kept everyone happy until a new bus arrived.","t":"A：上週末公司旅遊時，巴士在山路上拋錨，導遊是怎麼處理的？ B：她非常【機智】，打電話叫當地的計程車行，安排大家在附近農場吃午餐，讓每個人都開開心心地等到新巴士來。"},{"w":"capable","p":"adj.","d":"having the ability to do something well","c":"有能力的；能夠的","s":"A: Do you think the new assistant can manage the visitor schedule by herself while I am away at the conference in Seoul next week? B: Don't worry, she is fully capable of handling it, because she organized all the meetings for the sales team last month without a single mistake.","t":"A：下週我去首爾開會時，你覺得新助理能自己處理訪客行程嗎？ B：別擔心，她完全【有能力】處理，因為她上個月幫業務團隊安排所有會議，一個錯誤都沒有。"},{"w":"competent","p":"adj.","d":"having enough skill or knowledge to do a job well","c":"能勝任的；稱職的","s":"A: Are you satisfied with the new accountant whom the agency sent to help us during the busy tax season this spring? B: Yes, he is very competent, because he finished checking all the receipts on time, answered our questions clearly, and found two errors that saved us money.","t":"A：今年春天報稅旺季時仲介派來幫忙的新會計，你們滿意嗎？ B：滿意，他非常【稱職】，準時核對完所有收據，清楚回答我們的問題，還找出兩個錯誤幫我們省了錢。"},{"w":"erudite","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing great knowledge from a lot of reading","c":"博學的；學識淵博的","s":"A: Why did the publishing company choose that retired professor to write the introduction for the new collection of classic novels? B: She is an erudite writer who has read thousands of books in several languages, so readers trust her to explain the history and meaning of each story.","t":"A：出版社為什麼選那位退休教授為新的經典小說選集寫導讀？ B：她是一位【學識淵博的】作家，讀過好幾種語言的數千本書，所以讀者相信她能解說每個故事的歷史和意義。"},{"w":"brainy","p":"adj.","d":"very clever (informal)","c":"頭腦好的；聰明的（口語）","s":"A: Who helped you fix the complicated formulas in the sales spreadsheet before the deadline yesterday afternoon? B: My brainy cousin who studies math at the university came over after class, and she found the errors in ten minutes and showed me a faster way to calculate the totals.","t":"A：昨天下午截止前，是誰幫你修好銷售試算表裡那些複雜公式的？ B：我那個在大學讀數學、【頭腦很好的】表妹下課後過來，她十分鐘就找出錯誤，還教我更快算總數的方法。"},{"w":"savvy","p":"adj.","d":"having practical knowledge and good judgment about something","c":"精明的；在行的","s":"A: Why does the company want young employees to manage its new online store and social media pages this year? B: Many of them are very tech-savvy, so they understand how customers shop on their phones and can quickly answer questions and post attractive videos about our products.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年想讓年輕員工管理新的網路商店和社群媒體專頁？ B：他們很多人都很【精通】科技，了解顧客如何用手機購物，也能很快回覆問題並發布吸引人的產品影片。"},{"w":"sensible","p":"adj.","d":"reasonable and showing good judgment","c":"明智的；合理的","s":"A: The weather report says a typhoon may hit the city on Thursday, so should we still hold the outdoor product launch in the park? B: I think the sensible thing is to move the event indoors to the hotel ballroom, because we cannot risk the guests' safety or damage to the expensive equipment.","t":"A：氣象報告說週四颱風可能會侵襲本市，我們還要在公園舉辦戶外產品發表會嗎？ B：我認為【明智的】做法是把活動移到飯店宴會廳室內舉行，因為我們不能拿賓客的安全或昂貴設備的損壞冒險。"}]},{"unit":193,"theme":"Interesting 有趣的","cards":[{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"極有趣的；迷人的","s":"A: Did you go to the factory tour that the marketing team organized for the new interns last Friday afternoon? B: Yes, and it was truly fascinating, because the engineer showed us how the robots pack thousands of boxes every hour without making a single mistake.","t":"A：你有去參加行銷團隊上週五下午為新實習生安排的工廠參觀嗎？ B：有，而且真的非常【引人入勝】，因為工程師讓我們看機器人如何每小時包裝數千個箱子而且一個錯誤都沒有。"},{"w":"engaging","p":"adj.","d":"interesting and able to keep people involved","c":"吸引人參與的；有魅力的","s":"A: How did the new trainer do during the customer service workshop yesterday, since the last one made everyone fall asleep? B: She was very engaging, so she asked us lots of questions, used short role-plays, and kept the whole room talking and laughing until the session ended at five.","t":"A：新的講師昨天在客服工作坊表現得如何？上一位讓大家都睡著了。 B：她非常【吸引人參與】，問了我們很多問題、用了簡短的角色扮演，讓整個教室一直討論和歡笑到五點課程結束。"},{"w":"captivating","p":"adj.","d":"so attractive that you keep watching or listening","c":"迷人的；令人著迷的","s":"A: Why were so many shoppers standing in front of the department store window on Saturday evening instead of going inside? B: The store had set up a captivating light show with moving snowflakes and music, and people stopped to watch it for several minutes before they continued shopping.","t":"A：為什麼週六晚上有那麼多購物者站在百貨公司櫥窗前而不進去？ B：店家布置了一場有飄動雪花和音樂的【迷人】燈光秀，人們停下來看了好幾分鐘才繼續逛街。"},{"w":"intriguing","p":"adj.","d":"strange or unusual in a way that makes you want to know more","c":"耐人尋味的；引起好奇的","s":"A: Have you read the email from the new supplier in Osaka that arrived this morning, because I don't understand their offer? B: Yes, it is quite intriguing, since they say they can cut our shipping costs by half, but they haven't explained how, so I want to call them.","t":"A：你看了今天早上大阪新供應商寄來的電子郵件嗎？我看不懂他們的報價。 B：看了，內容相當【耐人尋味】，因為他們說可以把我們的運費減半，卻沒說明怎麼做，所以我想打電話問他們。"},{"w":"absorbing","p":"adj.","d":"so interesting that it holds all your attention","c":"引人入勝的；令人全神貫注的","s":"A: You missed your train stop yesterday evening, didn't you, and arrived late for the team dinner at the restaurant? B: I did, because the mystery book my manager lent me was so absorbing that I forgot where I was until the train reached the last station.","t":"A：你昨晚坐過站了，對吧？所以團隊聚餐才遲到。 B：對，因為經理借我的推理小說太【引人入勝】了，我忘了自己在哪裡，直到火車開到終點站。"},{"w":"entertaining","p":"adj.","d":"fun to watch or listen to","c":"有娛樂性的；令人愉快的","s":"A: What kind of speaker should we invite to the company's year-end party, since last year's guest was rather boring? B: Let's hire someone entertaining, like a comedian or a magician, because staff want to relax, laugh, and enjoy the evening after working so hard all year.","t":"A：公司尾牙我們該邀請哪種講者？去年的來賓相當無聊。 B：我們請個【有娛樂性】的人吧，像喜劇演員或魔術師，因為員工辛苦工作一整年後想放鬆、大笑、享受這個晚上。"},{"w":"amusing","p":"adj.","d":"funny and making people smile or laugh","c":"好笑的；有趣的","s":"A: Why was everyone in the office laughing so loudly after lunch, and should I be worried about the noise? B: Not at all, the sales manager just shared an amusing story about how his dog ran into the video meeting yesterday and barked at the clients during his presentation.","t":"A：為什麼午餐後辦公室裡大家笑得那麼大聲？我需要擔心這些噪音嗎？ B：完全不用，業務經理剛剛分享了一個【好笑】的故事，說他的狗昨天在他簡報時衝進視訊會議對著客戶叫。"},{"w":"compelling","p":"adj.","d":"very strong and convincing","c":"有說服力的；令人信服的","s":"A: Do you think the board will approve the plan to open a second branch in Kaohsiung next spring? B: I think so, because the finance team prepared a compelling report showing strong demand, low rent, and enough skilled workers, so the directors will find it hard to say no.","t":"A：你認為董事會會核准明年春天在高雄開第二家分店的計畫嗎？ B：我想會，因為財務團隊準備了一份【有說服力的】報告，顯示需求強勁、租金低廉且有足夠的熟練員工，董事們很難拒絕。"},{"w":"stimulating","p":"adj.","d":"full of new ideas that make you think","c":"激發思考的；刺激的","s":"A: How was the two-day leadership course that the company paid for in Taichung last week? B: It was really stimulating, because the discussions made us think about our own problems in new ways, and I came back to the office with many fresh ideas for my team.","t":"A：公司上週在台中出錢讓你參加的兩天領導力課程怎麼樣？ B：真的很【激發思考】，因為討論讓我們用新的方式思考自己的問題，我回到辦公室時帶著許多給團隊的新點子。"},{"w":"thought-provoking","p":"adj.","d":"making people think seriously about something","c":"發人深省的","s":"A: Why did the department manager ask all of us to watch that short documentary before the meeting on Monday morning? B: She said it was a thought-provoking film about how small companies waste energy, and she hopes it will make us question our own habits and suggest real changes.","t":"A：部門經理為什麼要我們在週一早上開會前看那部短紀錄片？ B：她說那是一部關於小公司如何浪費能源的【發人深省】的影片，希望讓我們反思自己的習慣並提出真正的改變。"},{"w":"exciting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel happy and full of energy","c":"令人興奮的","s":"A: Have you heard the news that our company will launch its new electric scooter at the Taipei trade show next month? B: Yes, it's very exciting for everyone in the design team, because we have worked on this product for two years and finally people will see it.","t":"A：你聽說公司下個月要在台北商展推出新款電動機車了嗎？ B：聽說了，這對設計團隊每個人來說都非常【令人興奮】，因為我們做這個產品兩年了，終於能讓大家看到。"},{"w":"appealing","p":"adj.","d":"attractive or interesting to someone","c":"吸引人的；有魅力的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant change its menu design after only three months, since the old one looked fine to me? B: The owner wanted it to be more appealing to young customers, so she added bright photos, shorter descriptions, and cheaper lunch sets that office workers can afford.","t":"A：為什麼那家餐廳才三個月就改了菜單設計？我覺得舊的看起來還不錯。 B：老闆想讓它對年輕顧客更【有吸引力】，所以加了鮮豔的照片、更短的說明，以及上班族負擔得起的平價午餐套餐。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: Why does the new receptionist ask so many questions about every department in the building during her lunch break? B: She is simply curious and wants to understand how the whole company works, so she can direct visitors to the right office quickly and answer phone calls better.","t":"A：為什麼新來的接待員午休時問那麼多關於大樓裡每個部門的問題？ B：她只是很【好奇】，想了解整間公司如何運作，這樣她就能很快把訪客帶到正確的辦公室，也能更好地接聽電話。"},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adj.","d":"unusual or special in a way that people notice","c":"非凡的；值得注意的","s":"A: How did the small online shop manage to double its sales in just six months, even during a slow economy? B: It was a remarkable achievement, because the owner used social media cleverly, offered free delivery, and answered every customer message within one hour, even late at night.","t":"A：那家小網路商店怎麼能在經濟不景氣時只花六個月就讓營業額翻倍？ B：那是個【非凡的】成就，因為老闆巧妙運用社群媒體、提供免運，而且即使深夜也在一小時內回覆每則顧客訊息。"},{"w":"noteworthy","p":"adj.","d":"important or interesting enough to notice","c":"值得注意的","s":"A: Is there anything special in the quarterly report that I should mention when I present it to the director tomorrow? B: The most noteworthy point is that customer complaints dropped by forty percent after we hired more staff, so you should put that on the first slide.","t":"A：季報裡有什麼特別的內容是我明天向主管報告時應該提到的嗎？ B：最【值得注意的】一點是我們增聘人手後客訴下降了百分之四十，所以你應該把它放在第一張投影片。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"making people admire it","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"A: What did the visiting clients from Singapore think of our new headquarters when they came for the tour this morning? B: They found it very impressive, especially the glass meeting rooms, the rooftop garden, and the solar panels that provide almost half of the building's electricity.","t":"A：今天早上來參觀的新加坡客戶覺得我們的新總部怎麼樣？ B：他們覺得非常【令人印象深刻】，尤其是玻璃會議室、屋頂花園，以及提供大樓將近一半電力的太陽能板。"},{"w":"colorful","p":"adj.","d":"having many bright colors","c":"色彩繽紛的","s":"A: Which brochure design should we choose for the summer travel promotion, the plain blue one or the other? B: I prefer the colorful one with bright pictures of beaches, markets, and festivals, because it will catch people's eyes when they walk past our counter at the mall.","t":"A：夏季旅遊促銷我們該選哪個手冊設計，素藍色的還是另一個？ B：我比較喜歡那個有海灘、市集和節慶鮮豔圖片的【色彩繽紛】版本，因為人們經過我們在商場的櫃位時會被吸引目光。"},{"w":"lively","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and activity","c":"熱鬧的；活潑的","s":"A: How was the networking event at the hotel last night, since I couldn't stay after the opening speech? B: It was very lively, with live music, lots of food, and about two hundred guests chatting and exchanging business cards until the staff finally turned off the lights at eleven.","t":"A：昨晚在飯店的交流活動怎麼樣？開幕致詞後我就沒辦法留下來了。 B：非常【熱鬧】，有現場音樂、很多食物，大約兩百位來賓一直聊天、交換名片，直到十一點工作人員終於關燈。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and new ideas","c":"有活力的；充滿幹勁的","s":"A: What kind of person is the company looking for to lead the new marketing team in Hong Kong? B: They want a dynamic leader who is full of energy, can make quick decisions in a fast-changing market, and can encourage young staff to try new ideas without fear.","t":"A：公司在找什麼樣的人來帶領香港的新行銷團隊？ B：他們要一位【有活力的】領導者，精力充沛、能在快速變化的市場中迅速決策，並能鼓勵年輕員工無懼地嘗試新點子。"},{"w":"novel","p":"adj.","d":"new and different from anything before","c":"新穎的；新奇的","s":"A: How is the startup planning to reduce food waste in supermarkets, since many companies have already tried and failed? B: They have a novel idea that nobody has used before, which is an app that tells shoppers when fresh food will be discounted near closing time each day.","t":"A：那家新創公司打算怎麼減少超市的食物浪費？許多公司都試過也失敗了。 B：他們有一個前所未有的【新穎】點子，是一個應用程式，會告訴購物者每天快打烊時哪些生鮮食品會打折。"},{"w":"unique","p":"adj.","d":"being the only one of its kind","c":"獨特的；獨一無二的","s":"A: Why are tourists willing to pay so much more to stay at that small hotel in the mountains? B: The hotel offers a unique experience that you can't find anywhere else, because every room is built inside an old tea factory and guests can pick tea leaves in the morning.","t":"A：為什麼遊客願意花多那麼多錢住那間山上的小旅館？ B：那間旅館提供在別處找不到的【獨特】體驗，因為每間客房都蓋在一座老茶廠裡，房客早上還能採茶。"},{"w":"unusual","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is normal or expected","c":"不尋常的；罕見的","s":"A: Did anything strange happen at the warehouse last night, because the security guard called me very early this morning? B: Yes, he noticed something unusual, since the back door was open and the lights were on, although everyone had left at six, so he checked the cameras right away.","t":"A：昨晚倉庫發生什麼怪事了嗎？保全今天一大早就打電話給我。 B：是的，他注意到一些【不尋常】的情況，雖然大家六點就離開了，但後門開著、燈也亮著，所以他立刻檢查了監視器。"},{"w":"refreshing","p":"adj.","d":"pleasantly new and different","c":"令人耳目一新的","s":"A: What did you think of the new manager's first speech to the staff at the meeting this morning? B: It was refreshing to hear a boss admit his own mistakes and ask for honest feedback, because our last manager never listened to anyone and always blamed the team instead.","t":"A：你覺得新經理今天早上在會議上對員工的第一次談話如何？ B：聽到老闆承認自己的錯誤並請大家給真誠的意見，真是【令人耳目一新】，因為我們前一任經理從不聽任何人說話，總是怪罪團隊。"},{"w":"enjoyable","p":"adj.","d":"giving pleasure","c":"令人愉快的","s":"A: How was your business trip to Tokyo last week, and did you have any free time after the meetings? B: It was very enjoyable, because the clients were friendly, the meetings went smoothly, and on the last evening I visited a famous market and tried some excellent local food.","t":"A：你上週去東京出差怎麼樣？開完會後有空閒時間嗎？ B：非常【愉快】，因為客戶很友善、會議很順利，最後一晚我還去了一個有名的市場，品嚐了一些很棒的當地美食。"},{"w":"fun","p":"adj.","d":"enjoyable and entertaining","c":"好玩的；有趣的","s":"A: Should we plan a team-building activity for the new employees before the busy season starts next month? B: Yes, let's organize a cooking class or a bowling night, because it will be fun for everyone and help people from different departments get to know each other better.","t":"A：我們要不要在下個月旺季開始前為新員工規劃一個團隊建立活動？ B：好，我們來辦烹飪課或保齡球之夜吧，因為大家都會覺得很【好玩】，也能幫助不同部門的人更認識彼此。"},{"w":"riveting","p":"adj.","d":"so interesting that you cannot stop paying attention","c":"極吸引人的；扣人心弦的","s":"A: Why did the conference room stay full after the final session, even though it was already past six o'clock? B: The guest speaker gave a riveting talk about how she rebuilt her failing company, and nobody wanted to leave before she answered the last question from the audience.","t":"A：為什麼最後一場議程結束後會議室還是坐滿人，明明已經過了六點？ B：客座講者發表了一場關於她如何重建瀕臨倒閉公司的【扣人心弦的】演講，在她回答完觀眾最後一個問題前沒有人想離開。"},{"w":"spellbinding","p":"adj.","d":"holding your attention completely, as if by magic","c":"令人著迷的；迷人的","s":"A: Did you see the dance performance at the opening ceremony of the international trade fair yesterday afternoon? B: Yes, it was absolutely spellbinding, because the dancers moved so beautifully with the lights and music that the whole hall became silent and many visitors recorded it on their phones.","t":"A：你昨天下午有看到國際商展開幕典禮上的舞蹈表演嗎？ B：有，真是太【令人著迷】了，舞者隨著燈光和音樂跳得那麼美，整個大廳都安靜下來，很多參觀者用手機錄了下來。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"special and easy to remember","c":"難忘的","s":"A: What would you like to do for the company's tenth anniversary celebration in December, since it's a big event? B: I'd like to make it truly memorable for our staff and clients, so let's rent a boat for a dinner cruise and give everyone a special photo book as a gift.","t":"A：公司十二月的十週年慶祝活動你想怎麼辦？這可是件大事。 B：我想讓它對員工和客戶來說真正【難忘】，所以我們租一艘船辦晚餐遊船，並送每個人一本特別的相簿當禮物。"},{"w":"vivid","p":"adj.","d":"very clear and detailed in your mind","c":"鮮明的；生動的","s":"A: Can you describe the man who came into the shop and left without paying for the camera yesterday? B: I have a vivid picture of him in my mind, because he wore a bright red jacket, a yellow cap, and black sunglasses, so I can tell the police exactly what he looked like.","t":"A：你能描述昨天進店裡拿了相機沒付錢就離開的那個男人嗎？ B：我腦中對他有很【鮮明的】印象，因為他穿著亮紅色外套、戴黃色帽子和黑色太陽眼鏡，所以我可以準確告訴警方他的長相。"},{"w":"charismatic","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong personal charm that attracts people","c":"有魅力的；有領袖氣質的","s":"A: Why do so many young employees want to join the team led by Ms. Lin, even though the work is hard? B: She is a charismatic leader who speaks with warmth and confidence, and people naturally trust her, so they feel excited to follow her ideas and work long hours.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多年輕員工想加入林小姐帶領的團隊，即使工作很辛苦？ B：她是一位【有魅力的】領導者，說話溫暖又有自信，大家自然信任她，所以很樂意跟隨她的想法並長時間工作。"},{"w":"alluring","p":"adj.","d":"very attractive and tempting","c":"誘人的；極具吸引力的","s":"A: Why did the travel agency's new advertisement bring in so many customers during the first week of the campaign? B: It showed an alluring image of a quiet island with clear blue water and white sand, and many tired office workers immediately wanted to book a holiday there.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社的新廣告在活動第一週就吸引了那麼多客人？ B：廣告呈現了一座有清澈藍色海水和白沙的寧靜小島的【誘人】畫面，許多疲憊的上班族立刻想去那裡訂假期。"},{"w":"gripping","p":"adj.","d":"very exciting and holding your attention","c":"扣人心弦的；吸引人的","s":"A: Are you still watching that detective series that everyone in the accounting department keeps talking about at lunch? B: Yes, the story is so gripping that I watched three episodes last night instead of sleeping, and now I'm very tired, but I really want to know the ending.","t":"A：你還在看會計部大家午餐時一直在聊的那部偵探影集嗎？ B：是啊，劇情太【扣人心弦】了，我昨晚沒睡覺連看了三集，現在很累，但我真的很想知道結局。"},{"w":"absorptive","p":"adj.","d":"able to soak up liquid","c":"有吸收力的","s":"A: Which type of floor mat should we order for the entrance of the hotel lobby before the rainy season starts? B: We should buy the thick absorptive mats, because they soak up water from guests' shoes and umbrellas quickly, which keeps the marble floor dry and prevents people from slipping.","t":"A：雨季開始前，我們該為飯店大廳入口訂哪種地墊？ B：我們應該買厚的【吸水】地墊，因為它們能快速吸乾客人鞋子和雨傘上的水，讓大理石地板保持乾燥，避免有人滑倒。"},{"w":"pleasing","p":"adj.","d":"nice to look at, hear, or experience","c":"令人愉悅的；悅目的","s":"A: What did the customers say about the new packaging for our green tea products in the survey last month? B: Most of them said the soft colors and simple design were very pleasing to the eye, and several mentioned that the boxes looked elegant enough to give as gifts.","t":"A：上個月的調查中，顧客對我們綠茶產品的新包裝有什麼看法？ B：大多數人說柔和的色彩和簡單的設計看起來很【賞心悅目】，還有幾位提到盒子看起來高雅，很適合拿來送禮。"}]},{"unit":194,"theme":"Interesting Person 有趣的人","cards":[{"w":"interesting","p":"adj.","d":"able to hold your attention","c":"有趣的","s":"A: How was the guest speaker at yesterday's sales conference, and did the new team members stay awake during the long afternoon session? B: She told an interesting story about how she opened her first shop with almost no money, so everyone listened carefully and asked many questions afterward.","t":"A：昨天銷售會議的客座講者表現如何？新進團隊成員在漫長的下午場有保持清醒嗎？ B：她講了一個【有趣的】故事，說她當初幾乎沒錢就開了第一家店，所以大家都很專心聽，之後也問了很多問題。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"引人入勝的；令人著迷的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the factory tour that the client arranged for our visitors from Japan last Thursday afternoon? B: Yes, it was fascinating to watch the robots pack thousands of boxes every hour, and our guests kept taking photos because they had never seen such a fast production line before.","t":"A：上週四下午客戶為我們日本訪客安排的工廠參觀，你喜歡嗎？ B：喜歡，看機器人每小時包裝數千個箱子真是【令人著迷】，我們的客人一直拍照，因為他們從沒看過這麼快的生產線。"},{"w":"engaging","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant and keeping your interest","c":"吸引人的；迷人的","s":"A: Why do so many customers stay on our new website for such a long time compared with the old one we had last year? B: The designers added short videos and an engaging quiz on the home page, so visitors keep clicking, reading product details, and sharing the links with their friends.","t":"A：為什麼和去年的舊網站相比，這麼多顧客會在我們的新網站停留這麼久？ B：設計師在首頁加了短影片和一個【吸引人的】小測驗，所以訪客一直點擊、閱讀產品細節，還把連結分享給朋友。"},{"w":"captivating","p":"adj.","d":"so attractive that you cannot look away","c":"令人著迷的；迷人的","s":"A: Why was the theater completely full on Saturday night even though the tickets were more expensive than usual? B: The lead actress gave a captivating performance that critics praised in every newspaper, so people from all over the city booked seats as soon as the reviews came out.","t":"A：為什麼週六晚上劇院全滿，即使票價比平常貴？ B：女主角的表演【令人著迷】，各大報的評論家都讚不絕口，所以評論一出來，全市的人都馬上訂了座位。"},{"w":"intriguing","p":"adj.","d":"interesting because it is strange or not fully known","c":"耐人尋味的；引起好奇的","s":"A: Have you read the email from the new supplier in Vietnam about their unusual pricing plan for next year? B: Yes, their offer is quite intriguing because they will lower prices if we order early, but I want to ask the finance team a few questions before we decide anything.","t":"A：你看過越南新供應商寄來、關於明年特殊定價方案的電子郵件了嗎？ B：看過了，他們的提議相當【耐人尋味】，因為如果我們提早訂貨他們就會降價，但在做任何決定之前，我想先問財務團隊幾個問題。"},{"w":"charming","p":"adj.","d":"very pleasant and attractive","c":"迷人的；可愛的","s":"A: What did you think of the small bed-and-breakfast where we stayed during the business trip to the countryside last month? B: It was a charming little place with flowers in every window and a friendly owner who served homemade bread, so I would happily book it again for our next visit.","t":"A：你覺得上個月到鄉下出差時我們住的那間小民宿怎麼樣？ B：那是個【迷人的】小地方，每扇窗戶都有花，還有一位會端出自製麵包的親切老闆，所以下次去我很樂意再訂。"},{"w":"charismatic","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong personal charm that attracts people","c":"有領袖魅力的","s":"A: Why do you think so many employees voted for Mr. Lin to become the new leader of the workers' committee this year? B: He is a charismatic speaker who makes everyone feel important, and when he talks at meetings, even the quiet staff members start sharing their ideas and supporting his plans.","t":"A：你覺得為什麼今年有這麼多員工投票讓林先生成為員工委員會的新領導人？ B：他是一位【有領袖魅力的】演說者，讓每個人都覺得自己很重要，他在會議上說話時，連安靜的員工也會開始分享想法並支持他的計畫。"},{"w":"entertaining","p":"adj.","d":"fun and enjoyable to watch or listen to","c":"有趣的；具娛樂性的","s":"A: How should we keep the children busy while their parents attend the long product training at the hotel on Sunday? B: We could hire a magician to give an entertaining show in the next room, and the staff can also prepare snacks, games, and coloring books for the younger ones.","t":"A：週日家長在飯店參加冗長的產品訓練時，我們該如何讓孩子們有事做？ B：我們可以請一位魔術師在隔壁房間表演一場【有趣的】秀，工作人員也可以為年紀較小的孩子準備點心、遊戲和著色本。"},{"w":"amusing","p":"adj.","d":"funny and making people smile or laugh","c":"好笑的；逗趣的","s":"A: Why was everyone in the break room laughing so loudly when I walked past after lunch today? B: Kevin was telling an amusing story about how he got lost in the airport in Tokyo and accidentally joined a tour group of retired teachers for almost an hour.","t":"A：今天午餐後我經過休息室時，為什麼大家笑得那麼大聲？ B：Kevin在講一個【好笑的】故事，說他在東京機場迷路，還不小心跟著一群退休老師的旅行團走了將近一個小時。"},{"w":"lively","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy, activity, or excitement","c":"熱鬧的；活潑的","s":"A: Which restaurant would you suggest for the team dinner after we finish the big project on Friday evening? B: Try the Italian place near the station, because it has a lively atmosphere with live music and friendly waiters, and the large tables are perfect for a group of twelve people.","t":"A：週五晚上我們完成大專案後，你建議去哪家餐廳辦團隊晚餐？ B：試試車站附近那家義大利餐廳，那裡氣氛【熱鬧】，有現場音樂和親切的服務生，大桌子也很適合十二個人的團體。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and new ideas","c":"有活力的；積極進取的","s":"A: What kind of person is the marketing department looking for to replace Sarah when she moves to the Singapore office? B: They want someone dynamic who has lots of energy, can manage several campaigns at once, and is not afraid to try new ideas when the market changes quickly.","t":"A：Sarah調到新加坡辦公室後，行銷部想找什麼樣的人來接替她？ B：他們想找一個【有活力的】人，精力充沛、能同時管理好幾個宣傳活動，而且在市場快速變化時不怕嘗試新點子。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and original things or ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: How did the small design company win the contract to make the new logo for the city's tourism office? B: Their designers came up with a very creative idea that combined the mountains and the river into one simple picture, and the judges said nobody else had thought of it.","t":"A：那家小設計公司是如何贏得為市觀光局設計新標誌的合約？ B：他們的設計師想出了一個非常【有創意的】點子，把山和河結合成一個簡單的圖案，評審說沒有其他人想到這一點。"},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"showing new and unusual ideas from the mind","c":"富有想像力的","s":"A: Why did the toy company decide to hire that young writer to create stories for their new product line? B: Her books are full of imaginative characters, such as talking clouds and flying trains, and the managers believe children will love buying toys based on those unusual worlds.","t":"A：為什麼玩具公司決定聘請那位年輕作家為他們的新產品線創作故事？ B：她的書裡充滿了【富有想像力的】角色，例如會說話的雲和會飛的火車，經理們相信孩子們會喜歡購買以那些奇特世界為主題的玩具。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making people want to do something good","c":"鼓舞人心的","s":"A: Was the talk by the founder of the recycling company worth attending, or should I watch the recording later at home? B: It was really inspiring, because she explained how she started with only two workers and now employs five hundred people, and many of us left wanting to start our own projects.","t":"A：那家回收公司創辦人的演講值得去聽嗎？還是我晚點在家看錄影就好？ B：真的很【鼓舞人心】，因為她說明了她如何從只有兩名員工開始，到現在僱用了五百人，我們很多人離開時都想開始自己的計畫。"},{"w":"influential","p":"adj.","d":"able to change what people think or do","c":"有影響力的","s":"A: Why is the publishing company paying so much money to invite Professor Chen to write a review of our new book? B: He is one of the most influential critics in the country, and when he recommends a book, sales usually go up quickly in bookstores and online shops.","t":"A：為什麼出版公司要花這麼多錢邀請陳教授為我們的新書寫書評？ B：他是國內最【有影響力的】評論家之一，當他推薦一本書時，書店和網路商店的銷量通常會迅速上升。"},{"w":"thoughtful","p":"adj.","d":"kind and thinking about other people's needs","c":"體貼的；細心的","s":"A: Did anyone remember that today is the receptionist's last day before she leaves for her new job in Kaohsiung? B: Yes, Daniel was very thoughtful and bought her a card and some flowers, and he also asked everyone in the office to write a short message wishing her good luck.","t":"A：有人記得今天是接待員去高雄新工作前的最後一天嗎？ B：有，Daniel非常【體貼】，幫她買了卡片和一些花，還請辦公室每個人寫一段祝她好運的簡短留言。"},{"w":"insightful","p":"adj.","d":"showing a deep and clear understanding","c":"有見地的；有洞察力的","s":"A: Was the report from the outside consultant useful, or was it just a list of things we already knew about our customers? B: It was very insightful, because it explained why young shoppers prefer our competitor's app, and it gave us several clear steps to improve our online service.","t":"A：外部顧問的報告有用嗎？還是只是列出我們早就知道的顧客資訊？ B：非常【有見地】，因為它說明了為什麼年輕購物者偏好競爭對手的應用程式，還給了我們幾個改善線上服務的明確步驟。"},{"w":"perceptive","p":"adj.","d":"quick to notice and understand things","c":"感覺敏銳的；有洞察力的","s":"A: How did the new manager know that the team was unhappy even though nobody had complained to her directly? B: She is very perceptive and noticed that people stopped joining lunch together and spoke less at meetings, so she arranged private talks to find out what was wrong.","t":"A：新經理是怎麼知道團隊不開心的，明明沒有人直接向她抱怨？ B：她非常【有洞察力】，注意到大家不再一起吃午餐、開會時話也變少了，所以她安排了私下談話來了解問題所在。"},{"w":"observant","p":"adj.","d":"good at noticing small details","c":"觀察力敏銳的","s":"A: How did the security guard find the lost laptop so quickly after the busy conference ended last night? B: He is very observant and remembered seeing a black bag under a chair in the third row, so he checked there first and returned it to the owner within ten minutes.","t":"A：昨晚忙碌的會議結束後，保全人員是怎麼這麼快找到遺失的筆電的？ B：他觀察力非常【敏銳】，記得曾看到第三排椅子下有個黑色袋子，所以他先去那裡找，十分鐘內就把它還給了失主。"},{"w":"intelligent","p":"adj.","d":"able to learn and understand things quickly","c":"聰明的；有才智的","s":"A: Why did the bank promote Amy to team leader after she had worked in the loan department for only two years? B: She is extremely intelligent and can solve difficult problems quickly, and her managers were impressed by how fast she learned the new computer system last spring.","t":"A：為什麼銀行在Amy只在貸款部門工作兩年後，就把她升為組長？ B：她非常【聰明】，能迅速解決困難的問題，主管們也對她去年春天很快就學會新電腦系統印象深刻。"},{"w":"brilliant","p":"adj.","d":"extremely clever or excellent","c":"傑出的；絕妙的","s":"A: How did the engineering team manage to cut the factory's electricity costs by almost thirty percent this year? B: One of the young engineers had a brilliant idea to use the heat from the machines to warm the offices, and the plan worked better than anyone expected.","t":"A：工程團隊是如何在今年把工廠的電費削減將近百分之三十的？ B：其中一位年輕工程師想出了一個【絕妙的】點子，利用機器產生的熱來為辦公室供暖，這個計畫的效果比任何人預期的都好。"},{"w":"knowledgeable","p":"adj.","d":"knowing a lot about a subject","c":"知識淵博的；很懂的","s":"A: Who should we ask about the new tax rules before we send the invoices to our customers in Europe next week? B: Talk to Mr. Huang in accounting, because he is very knowledgeable about international tax, and he helped several departments with similar questions last year.","t":"A：下週寄發票給歐洲客戶之前，我們該向誰詢問新的稅務規定？ B：去找會計部的黃先生，因為他對國際稅務非常【在行】，去年他還幫好幾個部門解答過類似的問題。"},{"w":"articulate","p":"adj.","d":"able to express ideas clearly in words","c":"能言善道的；表達清楚的","s":"A: Why did the directors choose Jessica to present our proposal to the investors at next month's meeting? B: She is very articulate and can explain complicated financial information in simple, clear sentences, so investors who are not experts can still understand our plans easily.","t":"A：為什麼董事們選Jessica在下個月的會議上向投資人報告我們的提案？ B：她非常【能言善道】，能用簡單清楚的句子解釋複雜的財務資訊，所以不是專家的投資人也能輕鬆理解我們的計畫。"},{"w":"witty","p":"adj.","d":"clever and funny with words","c":"機智風趣的","s":"A: Why do so many people read the weekly newsletter written by the head of the customer service team? B: She writes witty comments about everyday office problems, like broken printers and long meetings, so readers laugh while they learn about the latest company news and updates.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多人閱讀客服團隊主管寫的每週電子報？ B：她會針對日常辦公室的問題寫一些【風趣機智的】評論，像是故障的印表機和冗長的會議，所以讀者能一邊笑一邊了解公司的最新消息和動態。"},{"w":"humorous","p":"adj.","d":"funny and making people laugh","c":"幽默的","s":"A: Should I start my presentation to the new employees with company history, or is there a better way to begin? B: Start with a short humorous video about a confused new worker on his first day, because it will make people relax before you explain the more serious rules.","t":"A：我向新進員工簡報時，應該從公司歷史開始講嗎？還是有更好的開場方式？ B：先放一段關於一位新員工上班第一天手忙腳亂的【幽默】短片，因為這會讓大家在你說明比較嚴肅的規定之前先放鬆下來。"},{"w":"friendly","p":"adj.","d":"kind and pleasant to other people","c":"友善的","s":"A: How was your first week at the new branch office, and did you have any trouble finding your way around? B: Everyone was very friendly, so my coworkers showed me where the meeting rooms were, invited me to lunch, and helped me set up my computer on the first morning.","t":"A：你在新分公司的第一週過得怎麼樣？有沒有找不到路的困擾？ B：大家都非常【友善】，所以同事們帶我去看會議室在哪裡、邀我一起吃午餐，第一天早上還幫我設定好電腦。"},{"w":"outgoing","p":"adj.","d":"liking to meet and talk with people","c":"外向的；友好的","s":"A: What kind of personality does the hotel want for the new guest relations position at the front desk? B: They are looking for an outgoing person who enjoys talking with strangers, because the job includes welcoming guests, answering questions, and organizing evening events for international visitors.","t":"A：飯店櫃台新的賓客關係職位想要什麼樣個性的人？ B：他們在找一個【外向的】人，喜歡和陌生人聊天，因為這份工作包括迎接客人、回答問題，以及為國際旅客籌辦晚間活動。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure about yourself and your abilities","c":"有自信的","s":"A: Are you nervous about leading the training session for the sales staff from the three new stores tomorrow? B: Not really, I feel confident because I practiced the whole presentation twice with my manager, and I know the products very well after selling them for five years.","t":"A：明天要為三家新門市的銷售人員主持訓練課程，你會緊張嗎？ B：不太會，我覺得很有【自信】，因為我已經和經理把整個簡報練習了兩次，而且賣了五年產品，我對它們非常熟悉。"},{"w":"unique","p":"adj.","d":"the only one of its kind; very special","c":"獨特的；獨一無二的","s":"A: Why are tourists willing to pay so much more to stay at that small hotel instead of the large ones downtown? B: Each room has a unique design painted by a local artist, so no two rooms look the same, and guests often post photos of their room online.","t":"A：為什麼觀光客願意多花那麼多錢住那間小飯店，而不住市中心的大飯店？ B：每個房間都有由當地藝術家彩繪的【獨特】設計，所以沒有兩間房看起來一樣，房客也常把房間的照片貼到網路上。"},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adj.","d":"unusual or surprising in a way that people notice","c":"非凡的；顯著的","s":"A: How did the new store manage to sell so much during its first three months, even with the bad weather? B: The sales team made remarkable progress by calling every old customer and offering free delivery, and the final numbers were almost double what the directors had expected.","t":"A：新門市在頭三個月是如何賣出這麼多的，即使天氣不好？ B：銷售團隊打電話給每位老顧客並提供免費送貨，取得了【顯著的】進展，最後的數字幾乎是董事們預期的兩倍。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to remember because it is special","c":"難忘的","s":"A: How can we make sure our booth stands out at the trade fair, since there will be more than three hundred companies there? B: Let's give visitors a memorable experience, such as a short virtual reality tour of our factory, because people often forget brochures but remember something fun they tried.","t":"A：商展會有超過三百家公司參加，我們要怎麼確保攤位能脫穎而出？ B：我們給參觀者一個【難忘的】體驗吧，例如參觀我們工廠的簡短虛擬實境導覽，因為人們常會忘記宣傳冊，但會記得他們試過的有趣事物。"},{"w":"passionate","p":"adj.","d":"having very strong feelings about something you love","c":"熱情的；熱愛的","s":"A: Why did the café owner spend so much money on special coffee machines and training for all of her staff? B: She is passionate about serving the best coffee in the city, and she believes that well-trained baristas will bring customers back again and again.","t":"A：那位咖啡店老闆為什麼花那麼多錢買特殊咖啡機，還讓所有員工受訓？ B：她對提供全市最好的咖啡充滿【熱情】，而且她相信訓練有素的咖啡師會讓顧客一再回流。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing great interest and excitement","c":"熱衷的；熱烈的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the company announced the new plan to let employees work from home on Fridays? B: Most people were very enthusiastic about the idea, and several workers with long commutes said it would save them hours of travel time every week.","t":"A：公司宣布讓員工週五在家工作的新計畫時，員工的反應如何？ B：大多數人對這個想法都非常【熱衷】，好幾位通勤時間長的員工說，這每週能為他們省下好幾個小時的交通時間。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: Why does the new intern ask so many questions about how each department works during her first week here? B: She is curious about every part of the business, and she wants to understand how sales, shipping, and accounting connect before she chooses which team to join.","t":"A：為什麼新實習生在第一週一直問那麼多關於各部門如何運作的問題？ B：她對公司的每個部分都很【好奇】，想在選擇加入哪個團隊之前，了解銷售、出貨和會計之間是如何連結的。"},{"w":"open-minded","p":"adj.","d":"willing to accept new or different ideas","c":"心胸開放的；開明的","s":"A: Do you think the new director will agree to try our plan to hold meetings outside in the park during summer? B: Probably, because she is quite open-minded and always listens carefully to unusual suggestions, even when they are very different from the way things were done before.","t":"A：你覺得新主管會同意試試我們夏天在公園戶外開會的計畫嗎？ B：應該會，因為她相當【心胸開放】，總是仔細傾聽不尋常的建議，即使那些建議和以往的做法非常不同。"},{"w":"warm","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and kind in a way that makes people feel welcome","c":"熱情的；溫暖的","s":"A: How did the staff at the Tainan branch treat you when you visited them for the quarterly review last week? B: They gave me a very warm welcome at the station, took me to a famous local restaurant for dinner, and showed me around their newly renovated office the next morning.","t":"A：上週你去台南分公司做季度考核時，那裡的員工如何招待你？ B：他們在車站給了我非常【熱情的】歡迎，帶我去一家有名的當地餐廳吃晚餐，隔天早上還帶我參觀他們剛整修好的辦公室。"}]},{"unit":195,"theme":"Interesting Place 有趣的地方","cards":[{"w":"attractive","p":"adj.","d":"pleasing, or interesting enough to make people want it","c":"有吸引力的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team choose this small coastal town for the company's spring retreat instead of a big city hotel? B: The town has clean beaches, friendly local shops, and very reasonable prices, so it was the most attractive option for our budget and for staff who want to relax.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊選擇這個海邊小鎮作為公司春季員工旅遊的地點，而不是大城市的飯店？ B：這個小鎮有乾淨的海灘、友善的在地商店，價格也很合理，所以對我們的預算和想放鬆的員工來說，它是最【有吸引力的】選擇。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"迷人的；極有趣的","s":"A: How was the guided tour of the old silk factory that the sales department visited during the conference last Friday? B: It was really fascinating, because the guide showed us how workers made cloth by hand a hundred years ago, and nobody wanted to leave when the tour ended.","t":"A：上週五開會期間，業務部參觀那座老絲綢工廠的導覽怎麼樣？ B：真的非常【精彩有趣】，因為導覽員讓我們看到一百年前工人如何用手工織布，導覽結束時大家都不想離開。"},{"w":"scenic","p":"adj.","d":"having beautiful natural views","c":"風景優美的","s":"A: Should we take the highway or the mountain road when we drive our clients to the countryside hotel on Saturday morning? B: Let's take the scenic route along the lake, because it only adds about twenty minutes, and our guests will enjoy the green hills and the views of the water.","t":"A：星期六早上我們開車載客戶去鄉間飯店時，應該走高速公路還是山路？ B：我們走沿著湖邊那條【風景優美的】路線吧，因為只多花大約二十分鐘，而且客人會很喜歡綠色的山丘和湖景。"},{"w":"picturesque","p":"adj.","d":"very pretty, like a painting","c":"如畫的；景色優美的","s":"A: Have you found a good place for the photo shoot for our new travel brochure, or are you still searching online? B: Yes, I found a picturesque fishing town with colorful wooden houses and small boats, and the mayor has already given us permission to take pictures there next week.","t":"A：我們新旅遊手冊的拍攝地點找到了嗎，還是你還在網路上搜尋？ B：找到了，我找到一個【如詩如畫的】漁港小鎮，有色彩繽紛的木屋和小船，而且鎮長已經同意我們下週去那裡拍照。"},{"w":"historic","p":"adj.","d":"important in history","c":"有歷史意義的；歷史性的","s":"A: Why is the city council spending so much money to repair that old brick building next to the train station downtown? B: It is a historic building where the first city government met over two hundred years ago, so officials want to protect it and open it to visitors.","t":"A：市議會為什麼花這麼多錢整修市中心火車站旁那棟老磚房？ B：那是一棟【具有歷史意義的】建築，兩百多年前第一屆市政府就在那裡開會，所以官員們想保護它並開放給遊客參觀。"},{"w":"cultural","p":"adj.","d":"related to the arts, customs and traditions of a group","c":"文化的","s":"A: What kinds of activities are planned for the overseas partners who are arriving in Taipei next Monday for the trade fair? B: Besides the business meetings, we've arranged several cultural events, such as a tea ceremony, a temple visit, and a traditional music performance in the evening.","t":"A：下週一為了商展抵達台北的海外合作夥伴，安排了哪些活動？ B：除了商務會議之外，我們還安排了幾場【文化】活動，例如茶道、參觀廟宇，以及晚上的傳統音樂表演。"},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy, color and activity","c":"充滿活力的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant group decide to open its new branch in that area near the university instead of the business center? B: The area has a vibrant night life with street music, colorful shops, and lots of young people, so the owners believe the restaurant will stay busy every evening.","t":"A：為什麼餐飲集團決定把新分店開在大學附近那一區，而不是商業中心？ B：那一區的夜生活【充滿活力】，有街頭音樂、色彩繽紛的商店和許多年輕人，所以老闆們相信餐廳每天晚上都會很忙。"},{"w":"lively","p":"adj.","d":"full of activity and cheerful noise","c":"熱鬧的；活潑的","s":"A: Is the café across from our office a good place to hold a quiet meeting with the new supplier this afternoon? B: Probably not, because it gets very lively after lunch, with students chatting loudly and music playing, so I suggest we book the small meeting room upstairs instead.","t":"A：我們辦公室對面的咖啡廳，適合今天下午和新供應商開個安靜的會議嗎？ B：大概不適合，因為午餐後那裡會變得很【熱鬧】，學生大聲聊天、還放著音樂，所以我建議我們改訂樓上的小會議室。"},{"w":"bustling","p":"adj.","d":"busy and full of people moving around","c":"熙熙攘攘的；繁忙的","s":"A: Why did it take you so long to get back to the hotel after shopping for souvenirs with the clients yesterday? B: The night market was so bustling that we could hardly walk through the crowds, and it took us almost an hour to find a taxi on the main street.","t":"A：昨天你和客戶買完紀念品後，為什麼過了那麼久才回到飯店？ B：夜市實在太【熙熙攘攘】了，我們幾乎擠不過人群，而且在大街上花了將近一個小時才叫到計程車。"},{"w":"unique","p":"adj.","d":"the only one of its kind","c":"獨特的；獨一無二的","s":"A: What makes this small island so special that our travel agency wants to add it to every summer tour package next year? B: It has a unique kind of black sand beach that you cannot find anywhere else in the region, and customers keep asking us to include it.","t":"A：這座小島有什麼特別之處，讓我們旅行社明年想把它加進每個夏季旅遊套裝行程？ B：它有一種【獨特的】黑沙海灘，在這個地區其他地方都找不到，而且客人一直要求我們把它納入行程。"},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adj.","d":"unusual and worth noticing","c":"非凡的；值得注意的","s":"A: Did the new hotel manager really manage to increase the number of guests during the rainy season this year? B: Yes, the results were remarkable, because bookings went up by forty percent after she started offering free cooking classes and guided walks for every guest.","t":"A：新任飯店經理今年真的在雨季增加了住客人數嗎？ B：是的，成果非常【驚人】，因為她開始為每位客人提供免費烹飪課和導覽散步之後，訂房量增加了百分之四十。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"special and easy to remember","c":"難忘的","s":"A: How should we plan the farewell dinner for the retiring director so that everyone will talk about it for years? B: Let's hold it on the rooftop of the riverside hotel at sunset, since a beautiful view and good speeches will make the evening truly memorable for her and her family.","t":"A：我們該如何規劃即將退休的處長的歡送晚宴，讓大家多年後還會談論它？ B：我們在日落時分辦在河畔飯店的頂樓吧，因為美麗的景色加上精彩的致詞，會讓那個晚上對她和她的家人來說真正【難忘】。"},{"w":"charming","p":"adj.","d":"very pleasant and attractive","c":"迷人的；可愛的","s":"A: What did you think of the little guesthouse where the design team stayed during the workshop in the countryside last month? B: It was a charming place with flower boxes on every window and a friendly owner who baked fresh bread for us each morning, so several of us want to go back.","t":"A：上個月設計團隊去鄉下參加工作坊時住的那間小民宿，你覺得怎麼樣？ B：那是個【迷人的】地方，每扇窗戶都有花箱，友善的老闆每天早上都為我們烤新鮮麵包，所以我們好幾個人都想再去一次。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and calm","c":"寧靜的；平和的","s":"A: Where would you recommend I go this weekend after such a stressful month of reports and late meetings at the office? B: Try the small temple garden on the hill behind the city, because it is a peaceful spot where you can sit by the pond, listen to the birds, and forget about work.","t":"A：在辦公室經歷了一個月壓力很大的報告和深夜會議之後，你推薦我這個週末去哪裡？ B：去城市後山上的小寺廟花園吧，那是個【寧靜的】地方，你可以坐在池塘邊聽鳥叫，把工作忘掉。"},{"w":"tranquil","p":"adj.","d":"calm and quiet, without any disturbance","c":"寧靜的；安靜的","s":"A: Why are so many companies booking that lakeside resort for their management training programs this autumn? B: The lake is very tranquil in the early morning, with no traffic noise at all, so managers can concentrate during the sessions and take relaxing walks during their breaks.","t":"A：為什麼今年秋天有這麼多公司預訂那間湖畔度假村來辦主管訓練課程？ B：那座湖在清晨非常【寧靜】，完全沒有車聲，所以主管們上課時能專心，休息時也能輕鬆散步。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"far away from towns and people","c":"偏遠的","s":"A: Is it difficult to deliver office supplies to the new research center that the company built in the mountains? B: Yes, it is in a remote area about three hours from the nearest town, so our trucks can only go there twice a week when the weather is good.","t":"A：把辦公用品送到公司在山裡蓋的新研究中心很困難嗎？ B：是的，它位於【偏遠的】地區，離最近的城鎮大約三小時，所以我們的卡車只能在天氣好的時候每週去兩次。"},{"w":"exotic","p":"adj.","d":"unusual and exciting because it comes from a faraway place","c":"異國情調的；外來的","s":"A: What kind of trip is the travel agency planning to offer as the top prize in this year's customer contest? B: The winner will receive a week on a tropical island with exotic flowers, unusual birds, and food that most of our customers have never tasted before, so we expect many entries.","t":"A：旅行社打算拿什麼樣的旅遊當作今年顧客競賽的頭獎？ B：得獎者將獲得在熱帶島嶼待一週的行程，那裡有【充滿異國風情的】花朵、罕見的鳥類，以及大多數顧客從沒吃過的食物，所以我們預期會有很多人報名。"},{"w":"touristy","p":"adj.","d":"full of tourists and things made for them, often in a bad way","c":"觀光客多的；過度商業化的","s":"A: Do you think we should take the visiting engineers to the famous old street near the harbor for dinner tonight? B: I'd rather not, because it has become too touristy, with crowds, expensive souvenir stands, and average food, so let's take them to a family restaurant that local people prefer.","t":"A：你覺得今晚我們該帶來訪的工程師去港口附近那條有名的老街吃晚餐嗎？ B：我寧可不要，因為那裡已經變得太【觀光化】了，人潮擁擠、紀念品攤很貴、食物也普普通通，我們還是帶他們去在地人比較喜歡的家庭餐廳吧。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的","s":"A: Why do we need to reserve the tickets for the night river cruise more than two weeks before the clients arrive? B: The cruise is extremely popular with both tourists and local families, so it is usually fully booked on weekends, especially during the summer festival season.","t":"A：為什麼我們需要在客戶抵達前兩週以上就預訂夜間遊河的船票？ B：這個遊船行程非常【受】觀光客和本地家庭【歡迎】，所以週末通常都會客滿，尤其是在夏季節慶期間。"},{"w":"hidden","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to find or see","c":"隱藏的；隱密的","s":"A: How did you find that wonderful little noodle shop where we had lunch with the new interns yesterday? B: A taxi driver told me about it, since it is hidden at the end of a narrow lane behind the post office, and most visitors walk right past without seeing it.","t":"A：昨天我們和新實習生吃午餐的那家很棒的小麵店，你是怎麼找到的？ B：是一位計程車司機告訴我的，因為它【隱身】在郵局後面一條窄巷的盡頭，大部分遊客都直接走過而沒看到。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"a famous building or place that is easy to recognize","c":"地標","s":"A: How will the visitors from the Tokyo office find our new headquarters if they do not speak any Chinese? B: Tell them to look for Taipei 101, because that famous landmark is right across the street from our building, and any taxi driver can take them there easily.","t":"A：東京辦公室的訪客如果完全不會說中文，要怎麼找到我們的新總部？ B：告訴他們找台北101，因為那個著名的【地標】就在我們大樓對面，任何計程車司機都能輕鬆載他們過去。"},{"w":"destination","p":"n.","d":"the place someone is traveling to","c":"目的地","s":"A: Which city did the board finally choose for next year's sales incentive trip, and why did it take so long to decide? B: They chose Kyoto as the destination, because it offers temples, good hotels, and short flights, but they needed time to compare costs with Bangkok and Seoul.","t":"A：董事會最後選了哪個城市作為明年業務獎勵旅遊的地點？為什麼花了那麼久才決定？ B：他們選擇京都作為【目的地】，因為那裡有寺廟、好飯店，而且航程短，但他們需要時間和曼谷、首爾比較費用。"},{"w":"attraction","p":"n.","d":"a place people visit for interest or fun","c":"景點；吸引人的事物","s":"A: What should our guests see if they only have one free afternoon after the trade show finishes on Thursday? B: The main attraction in this city is the National Palace Museum, so I suggest booking a guided tour there and having dinner at the night market afterward.","t":"A：如果我們的客人在星期四商展結束後只有一個下午的空閒，他們應該去看什麼？ B：這個城市的主要【景點】是故宮博物院，所以我建議預約那裡的導覽，之後再去夜市吃晚餐。"},{"w":"resort","p":"n.","d":"a place where people go on holiday, with many services","c":"度假村；度假勝地","s":"A: Where will the annual staff trip be held this year, and will employees be able to bring their families along? B: We have booked a beach resort in Kenting with three pools, a spa, and a kids' club, and each employee may bring up to two family members at a discount.","t":"A：今年的年度員工旅遊會在哪裡舉辦？員工可以帶家人一起去嗎？ B：我們訂了墾丁一間有三座泳池、水療中心和兒童俱樂部的海灘【度假村】，每位員工最多可以用優惠價帶兩位家人同行。"},{"w":"neighborhood","p":"n.","d":"an area of a town where people live","c":"街坊；社區；鄰近地區","s":"A: Why are you thinking about moving to a new apartment when your current one is so close to the office? B: My neighborhood has become very noisy since a new bar opened downstairs, and I would like to live somewhere quieter with a park and a good school nearby.","t":"A：你現在的公寓離辦公室那麼近，為什麼還考慮搬到新公寓？ B：自從樓下開了一家新酒吧後，我住的【社區】就變得很吵，我想住在比較安靜、附近有公園和好學校的地方。"},{"w":"harbor","p":"n.","d":"a sheltered area of water where ships and boats stay","c":"港口；港灣","s":"A: Why will the shipment of furniture from Vietnam arrive three days later than the date on the original contract? B: A typhoon closed the harbor in Kaohsiung for two days, so the cargo ship had to wait at sea until the port authorities said it was safe to enter.","t":"A：為什麼從越南運來的家具會比原合約上的日期晚三天抵達？ B：颱風讓高雄的【港口】關閉了兩天，所以貨輪必須在海上等待，直到港務單位宣布可以安全進港。"},{"w":"waterfront","p":"n.","d":"the part of a town next to a river, lake or sea","c":"濱水區；海濱","s":"A: Where is the company holding its end-of-year party, and is it easy to get there by public transportation? B: It will be at a restaurant on the waterfront in Tamsui, so guests can watch the sunset over the river, and the MRT station is only a five-minute walk away.","t":"A：公司的尾牙辦在哪裡？搭大眾運輸容易到嗎？ B：會辦在淡水【河岸邊】的一家餐廳，客人可以欣賞河上的夕陽，而且捷運站走路只要五分鐘。"},{"w":"viewpoint","p":"n.","d":"a place from which you can see a beautiful view","c":"觀景點","s":"A: Is there a good place on the mountain trail where the hiking group can stop to rest and take photos during Saturday's team-building trip? B: Yes, about halfway up there is a viewpoint with benches and a wooden platform, and from there you can see the whole city and the ocean.","t":"A：星期六團隊建立活動時，登山步道上有沒有適合健行隊伍停下來休息和拍照的地方？ B：有，大約在半山腰有一個設有長椅和木平台的【觀景點】，從那裡可以看到整座城市和海洋。"},{"w":"monument","p":"n.","d":"a structure built to help people remember a person or event","c":"紀念碑；紀念建築","s":"A: What is that tall stone structure in the middle of the square in front of the city hall where we are meeting? B: It is a monument built in honor of the workers who built the first railway here, and many tour groups stop there to take photos and read the history.","t":"A：我們要碰面的市政府前廣場中央，那座高高的石造建築是什麼？ B：那是一座為了紀念在這裡興建第一條鐵路的工人而建的【紀念碑】，很多旅行團會停在那裡拍照、閱讀歷史介紹。"},{"w":"gallery","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where art is shown","c":"美術館；畫廊","s":"A: Where are we going to hold the launch event for the new line of designer furniture next month? B: We have rented a modern art gallery downtown, so guests can look at paintings and sculptures while they try the new chairs and enjoy drinks.","t":"A：下個月新系列設計師家具的發表會要在哪裡舉辦？ B：我們租了市中心一間現代藝術【畫廊】，讓客人可以一邊欣賞畫作和雕塑，一邊試坐新椅子、享用飲料。"},{"w":"marketplace","p":"n.","d":"an open area where people buy and sell goods","c":"市集；市場","s":"A: What should I do if I want to buy fresh local fruit and handmade gifts for my colleagues before I fly home tomorrow? B: Go to the old marketplace in the center of town early in the morning, because farmers and craftspeople set up stalls there and sell their goods at fair prices.","t":"A：如果我想在明天搭機回家前，買些新鮮的在地水果和手工禮物給同事，該怎麼做？ B：一大早去鎮中心的老【市集】吧，因為農夫和工匠會在那裡擺攤，用公道的價格販售商品。"},{"w":"district","p":"n.","d":"a particular area of a city or country","c":"區；地區","s":"A: Why are so many technology companies opening offices in that part of the city near the new metro line? B: The government made it a special business district with lower taxes and fast internet, so rents there are attractive for startups and large firms alike.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多科技公司在城市新捷運線附近那一帶開設辦公室？ B：政府把那裡劃為享有較低稅率和高速網路的特別商業【區】，所以那裡的租金對新創公司和大企業都很有吸引力。"},{"w":"village","p":"n.","d":"a very small town in the countryside","c":"村莊","s":"A: Where does the tea we serve in our office lounge actually come from, and why does it taste so fresh? B: It comes from a small mountain village in Nantou where farmers grow it by hand, and our supplier picks it up directly from them every two weeks.","t":"A：我們辦公室休息室提供的茶到底是從哪裡來的？為什麼喝起來這麼新鮮？ B：它來自南投一個小山【村】，那裡的農夫用手工種植，我們的供應商每兩週直接向他們取貨。"},{"w":"heritage","p":"n.","d":"the history, traditions and buildings passed down from the past","c":"遺產；文化資產","s":"A: Why can't the developer simply knock down the old houses on that street and build a new shopping mall there? B: The houses are listed as part of the city's heritage, so they are protected by law, and any changes need approval from the cultural affairs office first.","t":"A：為什麼建商不能直接拆掉那條街上的老房子，在那裡蓋一座新的購物中心？ B：那些房子被列為城市【文化資產】的一部分，所以受到法律保護，任何改變都必須先經過文化局核准。"},{"w":"panorama","p":"n.","d":"a wide view of a large area","c":"全景","s":"A: Why is the hotel charging so much more for the rooms on the top floor than for the ones below? B: From the top floor, guests can enjoy a wide panorama of the mountains, the river, and the city lights at night, so many travelers are happy to pay extra for it.","t":"A：為什麼飯店頂樓的房間比樓下的房間貴那麼多？ B：從頂樓，客人可以欣賞到山巒、河流和夜晚城市燈火的寬廣【全景】，所以很多旅客都很樂意為此多付錢。"},{"w":"hotspot","p":"n.","d":"a popular place where many people like to go","c":"熱門地點","s":"A: Why is the new rooftop café near our office always full, even on weekday afternoons when people should be working? B: It has become a social media hotspot, because influencers post photos of its colorful drinks and city views, so young customers line up there every day.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近那家新開的頂樓咖啡廳總是客滿，連平日下午大家應該在上班的時候也一樣？ B：它已經成為社群媒體上的【熱門地點】，因為網紅會發布它色彩繽紛的飲料和城市景觀的照片，所以年輕顧客每天都去排隊。"}]},{"unit":196,"theme":"International 國際","cards":[{"w":"global","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the whole world","c":"全球的；全世界的","s":"A: Why does our marketing team need to hold so many video meetings late at night these days? B: Since the company launched its new global campaign last month, we have to work closely with partners in Europe, Asia, and South America, so the meeting times are difficult for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼我們的行銷團隊最近需要在深夜開這麼多視訊會議？ B：自從公司上個月推出新的【全球】宣傳活動後，我們必須和歐洲、亞洲及南美洲的夥伴密切合作，所以會議時間對每個人來說都很難安排。"},{"w":"worldwide","p":"adj.","d":"happening or existing in all parts of the world","c":"全世界的；遍及全球的","s":"A: Have you heard any news about the new smartphone that our client is planning to release this spring? B: Yes, the manager told me it will have a worldwide launch on the same day in over fifty countries, so our factory must finish producing two million units by the end of February.","t":"A：你有聽到我們客戶打算今年春天推出的新智慧型手機的消息嗎？ B：有，經理告訴我它將在五十多個國家同一天進行【全球性的】上市，所以我們工廠必須在二月底前生產完兩百萬台。"},{"w":"overseas","p":"adv.","d":"in or to a foreign country across the sea","c":"在海外；到國外","s":"A: Why did Kevin suddenly quit his comfortable job at the bank downtown after working there for almost ten years? B: He received an exciting offer to work overseas at a branch office in Singapore, and his wife thought it would be a great chance for their children to learn new languages.","t":"A：為什麼凱文在市中心的銀行工作了將近十年後，突然辭掉那份安穩的工作？ B：他收到一個令人興奮的機會，到新加坡的分公司【海外】工作，他太太認為這是讓孩子們學習新語言的好機會。"},{"w":"foreign","p":"adj.","d":"from or relating to another country","c":"外國的","s":"A: Why is the hotel front desk so busy this week, and why did the manager hire two extra part-time workers? B: A large group of foreign tourists from Japan and Korea arrived for the music festival, so the staff need more help answering questions and arranging taxis to the city center.","t":"A：為什麼飯店櫃檯這週這麼忙，而且經理還多雇了兩名兼職員工？ B：一大群來自日本和韓國的【外國】觀光客為了音樂節來到這裡，所以員工需要更多人手幫忙回答問題和安排去市中心的計程車。"},{"w":"abroad","p":"adv.","d":"in or to a foreign country","c":"在國外；到國外","s":"A: Do you know why Linda has been taking evening Spanish classes after work for the past few months? B: She plans to study abroad in Madrid next year for a business degree, and she wants to be able to talk with her classmates and teachers without any problems when she arrives.","t":"A：你知道為什麼琳達過去幾個月下班後都在上西班牙語夜間課程嗎？ B：她打算明年到【國外】的馬德里攻讀商業學位，她希望抵達時能和同學及老師順利交談。"},{"w":"multinational","p":"adj.","d":"having offices or factories in many countries","c":"跨國的；多國的","s":"A: Why are so many young graduates applying for jobs at that new office building next to the train station? B: A large multinational company that has factories in twenty countries just opened its Asian headquarters there, and it offers good salaries, training programs, and chances to travel for work.","t":"A：為什麼有這麼多年輕畢業生去應徵火車站旁邊那棟新辦公大樓的工作？ B：一家在二十個國家設有工廠的大型【跨國】公司剛在那裡設立了亞洲總部，而且提供優渥的薪水、培訓課程，以及出差的機會。"},{"w":"transnational","p":"adj.","d":"operating across the borders of several countries","c":"跨國的；超越國界的","s":"A: Why did the police department invite experts from several countries to the meeting room this afternoon? B: They are working together to stop a transnational crime group that steals credit card information online and moves the money through banks in different countries, so no single police force can handle it alone.","t":"A：為什麼警察局今天下午邀請了好幾個國家的專家到會議室？ B：他們正在合作阻止一個【跨國】犯罪集團，該集團在網路上竊取信用卡資料，並透過不同國家的銀行轉移金錢，所以沒有任何單一警力能獨自處理。"},{"w":"cross-border","p":"adj.","d":"happening between two countries or across a border","c":"跨境的","s":"A: Why has our online store started charging customers in Canada a higher shipping fee this month? B: Because cross-border deliveries now need extra customs forms and inspections, the shipping company raised its prices, and we decided to share some of the cost with our customers instead of paying it all ourselves.","t":"A：為什麼我們的網路商店這個月開始向加拿大顧客收取較高的運費？ B：因為【跨境】運送現在需要額外的海關表格和檢查，貨運公司調漲了價格，所以我們決定和顧客分擔一部分成本，而不是全部自己負擔。"},{"w":"diplomatic","p":"adj.","d":"skillful at dealing with people without upsetting them; relating to relations between countries","c":"圓滑的；外交的","s":"A: The two partner companies argued loudly during yesterday's meeting, so how did our manager manage to calm everyone down? B: She gave a very diplomatic answer that respected both sides, suggested a short coffee break, and then helped them find a fair way to share the project costs.","t":"A：兩家合作公司在昨天的會議上吵得很大聲，我們經理最後是怎麼讓大家冷靜下來的？ B：她給了一個非常【圓融得體】的回答，尊重雙方立場，建議先短暫休息喝杯咖啡，然後幫助他們找到公平分攤專案費用的方法。"},{"w":"diplomacy","p":"n.","d":"the work of managing relations between countries; skill in dealing with people","c":"外交；交際手腕","s":"A: How did the two neighboring countries finally solve their long argument over the fishing rights near the islands? B: After months of careful diplomacy, their leaders met in Geneva and agreed to share the fishing area, which pleased local fishermen and helped seafood companies in both countries plan for the future.","t":"A：這兩個鄰國最後是如何解決他們在島嶼附近漁權上的長期爭議？ B：經過數個月謹慎的【外交】斡旋，兩國領袖在日內瓦會面並同意共享漁區，這讓當地漁民很高興，也幫助兩國的海鮮公司規劃未來。"},{"w":"treaty","p":"n.","d":"a formal written agreement between countries","c":"條約；協定","s":"A: Why are the prices of imported cheese and wine at the supermarket so much lower than they were last year? B: Our government signed a free trade treaty with several European countries in January, so import taxes on many food products were removed, and stores can now sell them more cheaply.","t":"A：為什麼超市裡進口起司和葡萄酒的價格比去年便宜這麼多？ B：我們政府在一月和幾個歐洲國家簽署了自由貿易【條約】，所以許多食品的進口稅被取消了，商店現在能以更便宜的價格販售。"},{"w":"alliance","p":"n.","d":"an agreement between groups to work together for shared benefits","c":"聯盟；結盟","s":"A: How will our small airline compete with the big companies now that fuel prices are rising so quickly? B: We are joining an alliance with three other regional airlines, so we can share airport counters, sell each other's tickets, and offer passengers more destinations without buying new planes.","t":"A：既然燃料價格上漲得這麼快，我們這家小航空公司要如何和大公司競爭？ B：我們將和其他三家區域航空公司加入一個【聯盟】，這樣就能共用機場櫃台、互相銷售機票，並在不購買新飛機的情況下為乘客提供更多目的地。"},{"w":"cooperation","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together toward the same goal","c":"合作；協力","s":"A: How did the hospital manage to move all of its patients to the new building in just one weekend? B: It was possible because of the close cooperation between doctors, nurses, drivers, and city police, who planned every step carefully and worked long hours to keep the patients safe and comfortable.","t":"A：醫院是如何在短短一個週末內把所有病人搬到新大樓的？ B：這要歸功於醫生、護理師、司機和市警之間密切的【合作】，他們仔細規劃每一個步驟，並長時間工作以確保病人安全舒適。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"the act of working with another person or group to create something","c":"合作；協作","s":"A: Who designed the beautiful new uniforms that the flight attendants started wearing last week? B: They were created in collaboration with a famous fashion designer from Paris, who visited our office several times to listen to the staff's ideas about comfort, color, and the local culture.","t":"A：空服員上週開始穿的漂亮新制服是誰設計的？ B：那是與一位來自巴黎的知名時尚設計師【合作】創作的，她來我們辦公室好幾次，聆聽員工對舒適度、顏色和在地文化的想法。"},{"w":"exchange","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving and receiving; a program in which people visit each other's countries","c":"交流；交換","s":"A: Why are there so many university students from Germany working in our engineering department this summer? B: They are part of a student exchange program with a university in Berlin, and next year five of our young engineers will go there for three months to learn about German technology.","t":"A：為什麼今年夏天我們工程部有這麼多來自德國的大學生在工作？ B：他們參加的是和柏林一所大學合作的學生【交換】計畫，明年我們有五位年輕工程師也會去那裡三個月，學習德國的技術。"},{"w":"trade","p":"n.","d":"the buying and selling of goods between people or countries","c":"貿易","s":"A: Why is the port so crowded with container ships and trucks compared with this time last year? B: trade between our country and Southeast Asia has grown quickly since the new agreement was signed, so more goods like rice, electronics, and clothing are moving through the harbor every day.","t":"A：跟去年這個時候相比，為什麼港口擠滿了這麼多貨櫃船和卡車？ B：自從簽署新協議以來，我國與東南亞之間的【貿易】成長迅速，所以每天有更多像是稻米、電子產品和衣服的商品經過這個港口。"},{"w":"export","p":"v.","d":"to send goods to another country to sell","c":"出口；輸出","s":"A: Our tea farm has sold its products only in local markets for twenty years, so what is the plan for next year? B: The owner wants to export our high-mountain oolong tea to Japan and Canada, so we are designing new packages with English labels and learning about the safety rules in those countries.","t":"A：我們的茶園二十年來都只在本地市場販售產品，那明年有什麼計畫？ B：老闆想把我們的高山烏龍茶【出口】到日本和加拿大，所以我們正在設計有英文標籤的新包裝，並了解那些國家的安全規定。"},{"w":"import","p":"v.","d":"to bring goods from another country to sell","c":"進口；輸入","s":"A: Why does this furniture store need such a big warehouse near the harbor when its showroom is quite small? B: The company has decided to import most of its wooden tables and chairs from Indonesia and Vietnam, so it needs plenty of space to store the large shipments before delivering them to customers.","t":"A：這家家具店的展示間很小，為什麼還需要港口附近這麼大的倉庫？ B：公司決定從印尼和越南【進口】大部分的木製桌椅，所以需要足夠的空間存放大批貨物，再送到顧客手上。"},{"w":"tariff","p":"n.","d":"a tax on goods coming into or going out of a country","c":"關稅","s":"A: Why did the car company raise the price of its electric vehicles by almost ten percent this month? B: The government added a new tariff on batteries and parts brought in from other countries, so the company's production costs went up, and it had to pass some of them on to buyers.","t":"A：為什麼這家汽車公司這個月把電動車的價格調漲了將近百分之十？ B：政府對從其他國家進口的電池和零件加徵了新的【關稅】，所以公司的生產成本上升，只好將部分成本轉嫁給買家。"},{"w":"visa","p":"n.","d":"an official document that lets you enter or stay in a country","c":"簽證","s":"A: Are you ready for your business trip to the trade show in Chicago at the end of next month? B: Not yet, because I still have to apply for a work visa at the American office downtown, and the travel agent said it can take up to three weeks to get approved.","t":"A：你準備好下個月底去芝加哥參加商展的出差了嗎？ B：還沒，因為我還得去市中心的美國辦事處申請工作【簽證】，旅行社說可能要花三週才會核准。"},{"w":"passport","p":"n.","d":"an official document that shows who you are when you travel to other countries","c":"護照","s":"A: Why are you looking through every drawer in your desk so nervously this morning before the flight? B: I can't find my passport, and without it I won't be allowed to board the plane to Tokyo for the client meeting, so please help me check the meeting room and the copy machine.","t":"A：你今天早上搭飛機前為什麼這麼緊張地翻找辦公桌的每個抽屜？ B：我找不到我的【護照】，沒有它我就不能登上飛往東京參加客戶會議的飛機，所以請幫我檢查會議室和影印機。"},{"w":"embassy","p":"n.","d":"the official office of a country's government in a foreign capital","c":"大使館","s":"A: Our engineer lost all his documents while working in Brazil last week, so what should he do now? B: He should go to our country's embassy in the capital as soon as possible, because the officials there can give him a temporary travel document and help him contact his family.","t":"A：我們的工程師上週在巴西工作時遺失了所有證件，他現在該怎麼辦？ B：他應該盡快去首都的我國【大使館】，因為那裡的官員可以給他一份臨時旅行文件，並幫他聯絡家人。"},{"w":"consulate","p":"n.","d":"a government office in a foreign city that helps its citizens and handles visas","c":"領事館","s":"A: Do I have to fly all the way to the capital to get my documents signed for the job in Osaka? B: No, you can visit the Japanese consulate here in our city instead, which handles visas and other papers for local residents, but remember to book an appointment online first.","t":"A：我必須一路飛到首都才能為大阪的工作把文件簽好嗎？ B：不用，你可以改去我們市區的日本【領事館】，那裡會為當地居民處理簽證和其他文件，但記得先上網預約。"},{"w":"summit","p":"n.","d":"an important meeting between the leaders of governments","c":"高峰會","s":"A: Why are the hotels near the convention center fully booked, and why are there so many police officers on the streets? B: Leaders from twenty countries are meeting at an economic summit there this weekend to discuss climate change and trade, so security is very tight around the whole area.","t":"A：為什麼會議中心附近的飯店都客滿了，街上還有這麼多警察？ B：二十個國家的領袖這個週末要在那裡參加一場經濟【高峰會】，討論氣候變遷和貿易，所以整個區域的保安非常嚴密。"},{"w":"conference","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting where people discuss a subject","c":"會議；研討會","s":"A: Will you be in the office next Tuesday to review the budget report with the finance team? B: No, I'll be in Seoul for three days attending an international conference on green energy, where I will give a short speech and meet possible partners from several Asian companies.","t":"A：下週二你會在辦公室和財務團隊一起檢查預算報告嗎？ B：不會，我會在首爾待三天參加一場關於綠色能源的國際【研討會】，我會在那裡做一個簡短演講，並與幾家亞洲公司的潛在夥伴見面。"},{"w":"organization","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together for a shared purpose","c":"組織；機構","s":"A: Why did you leave your job at the advertising company to work for much less money? B: I joined a non-profit organization that provides clean water to villages in Africa, and although the salary is lower, I feel proud that my work helps thousands of families every year.","t":"A：你為什麼離開廣告公司，去做一份薪水少很多的工作？ B：我加入了一個為非洲村莊提供乾淨用水的非營利【組織】，雖然薪水較低，但我很自豪我的工作每年能幫助數千個家庭。"},{"w":"ngo","p":"n.","d":"a non-governmental organization; a group that works for social causes without being part of a government","c":"非政府組織","s":"A: Who is paying for the free English classes that are held in the community center every Saturday morning? B: A local ngo that receives donations from businesses and private citizens runs them, and our company sends two volunteers each week to help the teachers and prepare the learning materials.","t":"A：每週六早上在社區中心開設的免費英語課是誰出錢的？ B：是一個接受企業和民眾捐款的當地【非政府組織】舉辦的，我們公司每週會派兩名志工去協助老師並準備教材。"},{"w":"peacekeeping","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping peace in an area, usually by international troops","c":"維和；維持和平","s":"A: Why has the city's largest hospital asked for volunteer doctors who can travel for six months? B: The United Nations is sending a peacekeeping team to a country recovering from a long war, and it needs medical staff to treat injured people and train local nurses while the soldiers protect the area.","t":"A：為什麼市內最大的醫院在徵求能出國六個月的志工醫師？ B：聯合國將派遣一支【維和】團隊到一個正從長期戰爭中復原的國家，需要醫護人員治療傷者並訓練當地護理師，同時由士兵保護該地區。"},{"w":"sanction","p":"n.","d":"an official order that limits trade or contact with a country to punish it","c":"制裁","s":"A: Why did our company suddenly stop shipping machine parts to that country last month? B: Several governments placed a strict sanction on trade with it after it broke an international agreement, so we are not allowed to sell any equipment there until the rules change.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司上個月突然停止運送機械零件到那個國家？ B：在那個國家違反了一項國際協議後，好幾個國家政府對它的貿易實施了嚴格的【制裁】，所以在規定改變之前，我們不能在那裡販售任何設備。"},{"w":"negotiation","p":"n.","d":"formal discussion to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"A: Has the purchasing team agreed on a final price with the steel supplier in Korea yet? B: Not yet, because the negotiation has taken longer than expected, but both sides are meeting again on Friday, and our director hopes to sign the contract before the end of the month.","t":"A：採購團隊和韓國的鋼鐵供應商談好最終價格了嗎？ B：還沒，因為【談判】花的時間比預期長，不過雙方週五會再見面，我們主管希望在月底前簽下合約。"},{"w":"integration","p":"n.","d":"the process of combining people or things so they work together as one","c":"融合；整合","s":"A: Why has the company hired so many trainers and translators since it bought the factory in Mexico? B: The managers want a smooth integration of the new workers into our company, so they are offering language lessons, training on our safety rules, and team activities to help everyone work well together.","t":"A：自從公司買下墨西哥的工廠後，為什麼雇用了這麼多培訓師和翻譯？ B：經理們希望新員工能順利【融入】我們公司，所以提供語言課程、安全規範訓練和團隊活動，幫助大家好好合作。"},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"the state of including many different types of people or things","c":"多樣性；多元化","s":"A: What do you like most about working at the new international design office in Singapore? B: I love the diversity of the team, because my coworkers come from eight different countries, and their different cultures, languages, and experiences give us many creative ideas for our clients' products.","t":"A：你最喜歡在新加坡新的國際設計辦公室工作的哪一點？ B：我喜歡團隊的【多元性】，因為我的同事來自八個不同國家，他們不同的文化、語言和經驗為客戶的產品帶來許多創意點子。"},{"w":"mobility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to move easily between places or jobs","c":"流動性；移動能力","s":"A: Why do so many young engineers want to work for this large company even though the starting salary is average? B: The company offers excellent job mobility, which means employees can easily move to its offices in London, Tokyo, or New York after two years and gain valuable international experience.","t":"A：即使起薪普通，為什麼還有這麼多年輕工程師想到這家大公司工作？ B：這家公司提供很好的工作【流動性】，也就是員工兩年後可以輕鬆調到倫敦、東京或紐約的辦公室，獲得寶貴的國際經驗。"},{"w":"connectivity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to connect to networks or other systems","c":"連線能力；連通性","s":"A: Why did the conference organizers choose this hotel instead of the cheaper one near the airport? B: This hotel offers much better internet connectivity in every meeting room, and since many speakers will join by video from other countries, a strong and stable connection is very important.","t":"A：為什麼會議主辦單位選擇這家飯店，而不是機場附近比較便宜的那家？ B：這家飯店每間會議室都有好得多的網路【連線品質】，而且因為許多講者會從其他國家透過視訊參加，穩定強大的連線非常重要。"},{"w":"interdependence","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which people or countries depend on each other","c":"相互依存","s":"A: Why did the factory in our town have to stop production when there was an earthquake in another country? B: It shows the strong interdependence of today's economies, because our factory depends on computer chips made there, and without those small parts we cannot finish building our machines.","t":"A：為什麼另一個國家發生地震時，我們鎮上的工廠必須停止生產？ B：這顯示出當今各經濟體之間強烈的【相互依存】，因為我們的工廠依賴那裡製造的電腦晶片，沒有那些小零件，我們就無法完成機器的組裝。"}]},{"unit":197,"theme":"Internet 網際網路","cards":[{"w":"website","p":"n.","d":"a group of pages on the internet about a company or subject","c":"網站","s":"A: Where can new customers find our price list and the opening hours of the downtown store, since the printed brochures ran out last week? B: They can visit our company website, which the marketing team updated yesterday with the new prices, store hours, and a short map showing how to get there by bus.","t":"A：既然印刷的小冊子上週已經發完了，新客戶要在哪裡找到我們的價目表和市中心門市的營業時間？ B：他們可以瀏覽我們公司的【網站】，行銷團隊昨天已經更新了新價格、營業時間，以及一張說明如何搭公車前往的簡單地圖。"},{"w":"browser","p":"n.","d":"a program used to look at pages on the internet","c":"瀏覽器","s":"A: The online booking form keeps freezing on my laptop every time I try to reserve the meeting room for Friday afternoon, so what should I do? B: Try opening it in a different browser, because the IT department said the old version you are using no longer works well with our new system.","t":"A：每次我想預約週五下午的會議室時，線上預約表單在我的筆電上就一直當機，我該怎麼辦？ B：試著用另一個【瀏覽器】打開，因為資訊部門說你正在用的舊版本跟我們的新系統已經不太相容了。"},{"w":"online","p":"adv.","d":"on or through the internet","c":"在線上；透過網路","s":"A: Do I need to visit the bank in person to pay the invoice from our new supplier before the end of the month? B: No, you can pay it online in about five minutes, and the system will send a receipt to your email so you can show it to the accounting department later.","t":"A：我需要親自去銀行，在月底前支付新供應商的發票嗎？ B：不用，你可以大約五分鐘內【在線上】付款，系統會寄一份收據到你的電子郵件，讓你之後可以拿給會計部門看。"},{"w":"offline","p":"adj.","d":"not connected to the internet","c":"離線的","s":"A: Why can't the sales staff in the branch office check the new orders this morning, even though their computers are turned on? B: The main system has been offline since eight o'clock because the technicians are installing an update, but they promised everything would be working again before lunch.","t":"A：為什麼分公司的業務人員今天早上無法查看新訂單，即使他們的電腦都開著？ B：主系統從八點起就一直處於【離線】狀態，因為技術人員正在安裝更新，不過他們保證午餐前一切就會恢復正常。"},{"w":"download","p":"v.","d":"to copy a file from the internet onto your computer or phone","c":"下載","s":"A: I'm flying to Singapore tomorrow for the trade show, and I'm worried that there won't be any internet on the plane, so how can I review the slides? B: You should download the presentation onto your tablet tonight, so you can practice your speech during the flight without needing a connection.","t":"A：我明天要飛去新加坡參加貿易展，我擔心飛機上沒有網路，那我要怎麼複習投影片？ B：你應該今晚就把簡報【下載】到平板電腦上，這樣你在飛行途中不需要連線也能練習演講。"},{"w":"upload","p":"v.","d":"to send a file from your computer to the internet","c":"上傳","s":"A: The manager in Tokyo needs to see the photos from yesterday's product launch before her meeting this afternoon, but the files are too large to email. B: Then please upload them to the shared folder right now, and send her a short message so she knows where to find them.","t":"A：東京的經理今天下午開會前需要看昨天產品發表會的照片，但檔案太大無法用電子郵件寄送。 B：那請現在就把它們【上傳】到共用資料夾，並傳個簡短訊息給她，讓她知道去哪裡找。"},{"w":"stream","p":"v.","d":"to send or watch video or sound over the internet as it happens","c":"串流播放；直播","s":"A: Many of our overseas employees can't travel to the head office for the CEO's speech next Monday, so how can they still watch it? B: We plan to stream the whole event live on the company website, and anyone who misses it can watch the recording later in the week.","t":"A：我們許多海外員工下週一無法到總公司聽執行長的演講，那他們要怎麼觀看？ B：我們打算在公司網站上【直播】整場活動，錯過的人也可以在這週稍晚觀看錄影。"},{"w":"wifi","p":"n.","d":"a way of connecting to the internet without wires","c":"無線網路","s":"A: Excuse me, I'm waiting for my interview with the hiring manager, and I need to check an important email from my current employer, so is there any internet I can use? B: Yes, our free guest wifi is available in the lobby, and the password is printed on the card next to the reception desk.","t":"A：不好意思，我正在等招聘經理的面試，我需要查看現任雇主寄來的一封重要電子郵件，請問有網路可以用嗎？ B：有的，大廳提供免費的訪客【無線網路】，密碼就印在接待櫃檯旁邊的卡片上。"},{"w":"network","p":"n.","d":"a group of computers that are connected to each other","c":"網路；網絡","s":"A: Why are all the printers on the third floor showing an error message, even though they have plenty of paper and ink? B: The office network went down after the storm last night, so none of the computers can send documents to them until the technician fixes the cables.","t":"A：為什麼三樓所有的印表機都顯示錯誤訊息，即使它們的紙和墨水都很充足？ B：辦公室【網路】在昨晚的暴風雨後就斷線了，所以在技術人員修好線路之前，沒有一台電腦能把文件傳送給它們。"},{"w":"server","p":"n.","d":"a powerful computer that stores information and sends it to other computers","c":"伺服器","s":"A: Our online store was very slow during the holiday sale, and many customers complained that they couldn't finish paying for their orders. B: That's because our server couldn't handle so many visitors at once, so the IT manager has decided to buy a more powerful one before the next big promotion.","t":"A：我們的網路商店在假期特賣期間非常慢，很多顧客抱怨無法完成訂單付款。 B：那是因為我們的【伺服器】無法同時應付這麼多訪客，所以資訊經理決定在下一次大型促銷前買一台更強大的。"},{"w":"client","p":"n.","d":"a computer program that connects to a server to get information, such as an email program","c":"用戶端；客戶端","s":"A: I can read my work emails on the website, but they don't appear in the mail program on my new laptop, so what is wrong? B: You probably haven't set up the email client with the correct server address yet, so let me show you the settings that the IT team sent us last week.","t":"A：我可以在網站上看我的工作郵件，但它們沒有出現在我新筆電的郵件程式裡，是哪裡出問題了？ B：你可能還沒用正確的伺服器位址設定電子郵件【用戶端】，我來給你看資訊團隊上週寄給我們的設定。"},{"w":"cloud","p":"n.","d":"online storage on servers that you can use from anywhere","c":"雲端","s":"A: My laptop was stolen at the airport yesterday, and I'm afraid I've lost all the sales reports I was working on for the regional meeting. B: Don't worry too much, because the company saves all our files in the cloud automatically, so you can open them again from any computer once you log in.","t":"A：我的筆電昨天在機場被偷了，我擔心我為區域會議準備的所有銷售報告都不見了。 B：別太擔心，因為公司會自動把我們所有的檔案儲存在【雲端】，所以你只要登入，就能從任何一台電腦再次打開它們。"},{"w":"cyberspace","p":"n.","d":"the online world of computer networks","c":"網路空間","s":"A: Our new product video was shared thousands of times over the weekend, but some people posted angry comments about the price, so should we reply? B: Yes, but carefully, because once something is said in cyberspace, it can spread around the world in minutes and is almost impossible to remove.","t":"A：我們的新產品影片在週末被分享了好幾千次，但有些人留下對價格不滿的評論，我們應該回覆嗎？ B：應該，但要小心，因為一旦在【網路空間】說了什麼，它就可能在幾分鐘內傳遍全世界，幾乎不可能刪除。"},{"w":"social media","p":"n.phr.","d":"websites and apps where people share messages, photos and videos","c":"社群媒體","s":"A: How did so many young customers hear about the opening of our new coffee shop near the university, since we didn't put any ads in the newspaper? B: Our marketing assistant posted photos of the drinks and the cozy seating area on social media, and students quickly shared them with their friends.","t":"A：既然我們沒有在報紙上登任何廣告，那麼這麼多年輕顧客是怎麼得知我們在大學附近新咖啡店開幕的？ B：我們的行銷助理在【社群媒體】上發布了飲料和舒適座位區的照片，學生們很快就分享給他們的朋友。"},{"w":"platform","p":"n.","d":"a website or service people use to do something online, such as selling goods","c":"平台","s":"A: We want to sell our handmade bags to customers in other countries, but we don't have the money to build our own online shop yet. B: Then we could start on a popular shopping platform that already has millions of users, and it will also handle the payments and shipping labels for us.","t":"A：我們想把手工包賣給其他國家的顧客，但我們還沒有錢架設自己的網路商店。 B：那我們可以先在一個已經擁有數百萬用戶的熱門購物【平台】上開始，它也會幫我們處理付款和運送標籤。"},{"w":"search engine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a website that helps you find information on the internet","c":"搜尋引擎","s":"A: When people look for office furniture in our city, our company appears on the fifth page of results, so very few of them ever find us. B: We should hire an expert to improve how our website appears on the main search engine, so that we show up on the first page instead.","t":"A：當人們在我們城市找辦公家具時，我們公司出現在搜尋結果第五頁，所以很少人找得到我們。 B：我們應該請專家改善我們的網站在主要【搜尋引擎】上的呈現方式，讓我們改為出現在第一頁。"},{"w":"keyword","p":"n.","d":"an important word you type to find information","c":"關鍵字","s":"A: I've been looking through the company's old customer files for an hour, but I still can't find the contract with the supplier from Osaka. B: Try typing the keyword \"Osaka\" into the box at the top of the folder, and the system will show you every document that contains that name.","t":"A：我已經翻公司的舊客戶檔案一個小時了，但還是找不到和大阪供應商簽的合約。 B：試著在資料夾上方的框格輸入【關鍵字】「大阪」，系統就會顯示所有包含那個名稱的文件。"},{"w":"link","p":"n.","d":"a word or picture on a web page that takes you to another page when you click it","c":"連結","s":"A: How will the new employees sign up for the online safety training course that starts next Wednesday morning? B: I'll send everyone an email with a link to the registration page, and they just need to click it, enter their staff number, and choose a time.","t":"A：新員工要怎麼報名下週三早上開始的線上安全訓練課程？ B：我會寄給每個人一封附有報名頁面【連結】的電子郵件，他們只要點擊它、輸入員工編號並選擇時段就好。"},{"w":"homepage","p":"n.","d":"the main page of a website","c":"首頁","s":"A: Our customers keep calling to ask whether the store will be closed during the national holiday next week, and the receptionist is getting very busy. B: Let's put a clear notice about the holiday hours at the top of our homepage, so visitors will see it as soon as they open the website.","t":"A：顧客一直打電話來問店裡下週國定假日是否休息，櫃檯人員變得非常忙碌。 B：我們在【首頁】最上方放一則清楚的假日營業時間公告吧，這樣訪客一打開網站就會看到。"},{"w":"account","p":"n.","d":"a personal record that lets you use a website or service","c":"帳號；帳戶","s":"A: I'd like to track the delivery of the printer paper I ordered from your website last Tuesday, but I can't find the order number anywhere. B: If you log in to your account and click on 'My Orders,' you'll see the order number, the delivery date, and the name of the shipping company.","t":"A：我想追蹤上週二在你們網站訂購的印表機紙張的配送進度，但到處都找不到訂單編號。 B：如果你登入你的【帳號】並點選「我的訂單」，就會看到訂單編號、送達日期和貨運公司的名稱。"},{"w":"password","p":"n.","d":"a secret word you use to enter a computer system or website","c":"密碼","s":"A: I've been away on vacation for two weeks, and now the computer won't let me into the sales system, no matter how many times I try. B: The company asks everyone to change their password every month for safety reasons, so you'll need to call the help desk to get a new one.","t":"A：我休假兩週回來，現在不管試幾次，電腦都不讓我進入銷售系統。 B：公司基於安全考量要求每個人每個月都要更改【密碼】，所以你需要打電話給服務台取得一個新的。"},{"w":"username","p":"n.","d":"the name you use to log in to a computer system or website","c":"使用者名稱","s":"A: I'm trying to sign in to the training website for new staff, but it keeps telling me that my details are wrong even though I typed carefully. B: Your username is probably your employee number, not your email address, so check the welcome letter from Human Resources and try again.","t":"A：我想登入新進員工的訓練網站，但即使我很小心地輸入，它還是一直說我的資料錯誤。 B：你的【使用者名稱】可能是你的員工編號，而不是電子郵件地址，所以看一下人資部的歡迎信再試一次。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the right to keep your personal information secret","c":"隱私","s":"A: Some customers are worried about giving us their phone numbers and home addresses when they join our new membership program at the supermarket. B: We should explain clearly that we protect their privacy and will never sell their personal information to other companies, and we can print this promise on the application form.","t":"A：有些顧客擔心在加入我們超市新的會員計畫時，要給我們他們的電話號碼和住址。 B：我們應該清楚說明我們會保護他們的【隱私】，絕不會把他們的個人資料賣給其他公司，我們也可以把這個承諾印在申請表上。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"protection against danger, crime or attacks","c":"安全；資安","s":"A: Why did the bank ask me to enter a code from my phone after I typed my password into its website this morning? B: It's an extra security step to protect your money, because criminals sometimes steal passwords, and the code proves that the person logging in is really you.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上我在銀行網站輸入密碼後，它還要求我輸入手機上的驗證碼？ B：那是額外的【安全】步驟，用來保護你的錢，因為罪犯有時會偷取密碼，而這個驗證碼能證明登入的人真的是你。"},{"w":"virus","p":"n.","d":"a program that secretly enters a computer and damages files","c":"電腦病毒","s":"A: My computer suddenly became very slow after I opened an attachment from someone I didn't know, and now strange windows keep appearing on the screen. B: It sounds like you've got a virus, so turn off the internet right away and call the IT department before it spreads to other computers in the office.","t":"A：我打開一個陌生人寄來的附件後，電腦突然變得很慢，現在螢幕上一直跳出奇怪的視窗。 B：聽起來你中了【病毒】，所以馬上關掉網路並打電話給資訊部門，以免它擴散到辦公室裡的其他電腦。"},{"w":"spam","p":"n.","d":"unwanted emails sent to many people, usually to sell something","c":"垃圾郵件","s":"A: Every morning my inbox is full of messages about cheap watches and free prizes, and it takes me twenty minutes to find the emails from real customers. B: You can turn on the spam filter in your settings, and it will move those advertising messages into a separate folder automatically.","t":"A：每天早上我的收件匣都塞滿關於便宜手錶和免費獎品的訊息，我要花二十分鐘才能找到真正客戶寄來的郵件。 B：你可以在設定中開啟【垃圾郵件】過濾功能，它會自動把那些廣告訊息移到另一個資料夾。"},{"w":"firewall","p":"n.","d":"a system that stops dangerous or unwanted access to a computer network","c":"防火牆","s":"A: I'm trying to open a website for my research report, but a message says the page is blocked by the company, so what does that mean? B: Our firewall stops staff from visiting websites that might be dangerous, but if you really need that page for work, the IT team can check it and unblock it.","t":"A：我想為我的研究報告打開一個網站，但訊息顯示該網頁被公司封鎖了，這是什麼意思？ B：我們的【防火牆】會阻止員工瀏覽可能有危險的網站，不過如果你工作上真的需要那個網頁，資訊團隊可以檢查後幫你解除封鎖。"},{"w":"bandwidth","p":"n.","d":"the amount of data an internet connection can carry in a certain time","c":"頻寬","s":"A: Every afternoon our video meetings with the factory in Vietnam keep freezing, and sometimes we can't hear what the engineers are saying at all. B: That's when many staff are uploading large files at the same time, so we don't have enough bandwidth, and the manager is planning to upgrade our internet package.","t":"A：每天下午我們和越南工廠的視訊會議都一直卡住，有時候完全聽不到工程師在說什麼。 B：那是因為很多員工在同一時間上傳大型檔案，所以我們的【頻寬】不足，經理正計劃升級我們的網路方案。"},{"w":"latency","p":"n.","d":"the delay between sending data and its arrival","c":"延遲","s":"A: During yesterday's online meeting with our partners in Brazil, there was a short pause every time someone spoke, so people kept interrupting each other. B: The high latency was caused by the long distance and a weak connection, so next time we should use the meeting room with the faster cable line.","t":"A：在昨天和巴西合作夥伴的線上會議中，每次有人說話時都會短暫停頓，所以大家一直打斷彼此。 B：高【延遲】是由遙遠距離和連線不穩所造成的，所以下次我們應該使用有較快有線網路的會議室。"},{"w":"forum","p":"n.","d":"a website where people discuss a subject by posting messages","c":"論壇","s":"A: I'm having trouble using the new accounting software, and the user guide doesn't explain how to create a monthly sales chart. B: Have you tried asking on the company's user forum, where thousands of customers share tips and answer each other's questions about common problems every day?","t":"A：我在使用新的會計軟體時遇到困難，使用手冊也沒有說明如何製作每月銷售圖表。 B：你試過到該公司的用戶【論壇】上發問嗎？那裡每天有成千上萬的顧客分享訣竅，並互相回答常見問題。"},{"w":"blog","p":"n.","d":"a website where someone regularly writes about their experiences or opinions","c":"部落格","s":"A: How can our small travel agency show customers that our staff really know the best places to visit in Japan and Korea? B: We could start a blog where our tour guides write about their favorite restaurants, hotels, and hidden spots, and then we can add a new article every week.","t":"A：我們這間小旅行社要怎麼向顧客展現我們的員工真的很了解日本和韓國最值得去的地方？ B：我們可以開一個【部落格】，讓我們的導遊寫他們最喜歡的餐廳、飯店和私房景點，然後每週新增一篇文章。"},{"w":"podcast","p":"n.","d":"a recorded audio program that you can listen to on the internet","c":"播客；Podcast節目","s":"A: I spend almost an hour on the train every morning, and I'd like to use that time to learn more about marketing and leadership. B: You should listen to a business podcast, because many experts talk about their experiences in short episodes, and you can download them to your phone before you leave home.","t":"A：我每天早上要在火車上花將近一小時，我想利用這段時間多學一些行銷和領導的知識。 B：你應該聽商業【播客節目】，因為很多專家會在短短的單集中分享他們的經驗，你可以在出門前下載到手機上。"},{"w":"ecommerce","p":"n.","d":"buying and selling goods on the internet","c":"電子商務","s":"A: Our sales in the shopping mall have dropped by twenty percent this year, while more and more people seem to buy everything with their phones. B: That's why the board wants to invest in ecommerce, so customers can order our shoes from home and have them delivered to their door within two days.","t":"A：我們今年在購物中心的銷售額下滑了百分之二十，而越來越多人似乎都用手機購買所有東西。 B：這就是為什麼董事會想投資【電子商務】，讓顧客可以在家訂購我們的鞋子，並在兩天內送到家門口。"},{"w":"digital","p":"adj.","d":"using computers or the internet; not on paper","c":"數位的","s":"A: The accounting department still keeps thousands of paper receipts in boxes, and it takes hours to find an old one when the tax office asks for it. B: The new manager plans to scan everything and create digital copies, so staff can find any receipt in seconds by typing the date or the amount.","t":"A：會計部門仍然把成千上萬張紙本收據放在箱子裡，當稅務局要求時，找一張舊收據要花好幾個小時。 B：新經理打算把所有東西都掃描並建立【數位】副本，讓員工只要輸入日期或金額就能在幾秒內找到任何收據。"}]}];
